window.EDMUND_IELTS_LISTENING_PRACTICES_2_20_SEED = {"ielts/listening/Practice 10/task-1":[{"front":"be interested in restaurant work","meaning":"對餐廳工作有興趣","examples":[{"en":"The man is interested in restaurant work.","zh":"那名男子對餐廳工作有興趣。"},{"en":"To be interested in restaurant work means to want to work in a restaurant or learn more about that kind of job.","zh":"對餐廳工作有興趣意思是想在餐廳工作，或想進一步了解這類工作。"},{"en":"A student may be interested in restaurant work because they enjoy cooking and meeting customers.","zh":"學生可能因喜歡烹飪和接觸顧客而對餐廳工作有興趣。"},{"en":"Interest in restaurant work can lead someone to apply for waiter, chef, or kitchen assistant jobs.","zh":"對餐廳工作有興趣，可以令人申請侍應、廚師或廚房助理職位。"},{"en":"This phrase describes curiosity or enthusiasm about working in restaurants.","zh":"這個短語描述對在餐廳工作有好奇或熱情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have a bit of experience","meaning":"有一點經驗","examples":[{"en":"The man has a bit of experience in restaurant work.","zh":"那名男子在餐廳工作方面有一點經驗。"},{"en":"To have a bit of experience means to have some, but not a lot, of practical knowledge or practice.","zh":"有一點經驗意思是有一些實際知識或實踐，但不是很多。"},{"en":"A teenager may have a bit of experience in customer service after helping in a family shop.","zh":"青少年在家庭店舖幫忙後，可能在顧客服務方面有一點經驗。"},{"en":"Having a bit of experience can make an applicant more confident in an interview.","zh":"有一點經驗可以令求職者在面試中更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests basic experience, not expert-level skill.","zh":"這個短語暗示基本經驗，而不是專家級技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"provide references","meaning":"提供推薦人資料","examples":[{"en":"The man can provide references for his previous work.","zh":"那名男子可以為自己以前的工作提供推薦人資料。"},{"en":"To provide references means to give the names or contact details of people who can confirm your work or character.","zh":"提供推薦人資料意思是提供能確認你工作表現或品格的人的姓名或聯絡資料。"},{"en":"A job applicant may provide references from former teachers or managers.","zh":"求職者可能提供前老師或前經理作推薦人。"},{"en":"Employers ask for references because they want to check whether a candidate is reliable.","zh":"僱主要求推薦人資料，因為他們想核實候選人是否可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in job applications and recruitment.","zh":"這個短語常見於求職和招聘。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"check all that later","meaning":"稍後核實所有資料","examples":[{"en":"The woman says she can check all that later.","zh":"那名女子說她可以稍後核實所有資料。"},{"en":"To check all that later means to verify the details at a later time.","zh":"稍後核實所有資料意思是在之後再確認細節。"},{"en":"A teacher may say she will check all that later after collecting students’ forms.","zh":"老師收集學生表格後，可能說會稍後核實所有資料。"},{"en":"Checking details later helps avoid mistakes before a final decision is made.","zh":"稍後核實資料有助在作出最終決定前避免錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the main discussion should continue first.","zh":"當主要討論應先繼續時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have some vacancies","meaning":"有一些職位空缺","examples":[{"en":"Milo’s Restaurants have some vacancies at the moment.","zh":"Milo’s Restaurants 目前有一些職位空缺。"},{"en":"To have some vacancies means to have some job positions available.","zh":"有一些職位空缺意思是有一些工作崗位可供申請。"},{"en":"A school may have some vacancies for teaching assistants after several staff leave.","zh":"幾名職員離職後，學校可能有一些教學助理職位空缺。"},{"en":"Companies advertise vacancies when they need new workers.","zh":"公司需要新員工時，會刊登職位空缺。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when an organisation is hiring.","zh":"這個短語用於機構正在招聘時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"at the moment","meaning":"目前","examples":[{"en":"Milo’s Restaurants have some vacancies at the moment.","zh":"Milo’s Restaurants 目前有一些職位空缺。"},{"en":"At the moment means right now or at the present time.","zh":"目前意思是現在或此刻。"},{"en":"The library is closed at the moment because workers are repairing the roof.","zh":"圖書館目前關閉，因為工人正在維修屋頂。"},{"en":"A situation at the moment may change later, so people should check again if needed.","zh":"目前的情況之後可能會改變，所以有需要時應再次查詢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the present situation.","zh":"這個短語描述現在的情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a good company to work for","meaning":"一間值得任職的公司","examples":[{"en":"Milo’s Restaurants are a good company to work for.","zh":"Milo’s Restaurants 是一間值得任職的公司。"},{"en":"A good company to work for is an employer that treats staff well and offers fair conditions.","zh":"一間值得任職的公司是善待員工並提供公平條件的僱主。"},{"en":"A company with training, fair pay, and supportive managers is a good company to work for.","zh":"有培訓、公平薪酬和支持型經理的公司，是值得任職的公司。"},{"en":"People stay longer in jobs when the company is a good place to work.","zh":"當公司值得任職，員工會更願意長期留下。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the employee’s experience of the company.","zh":"這個短語重點是員工在公司的工作體驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lots of benefits","meaning":"很多福利","examples":[{"en":"The company offers lots of benefits to its staff.","zh":"公司向員工提供很多福利。"},{"en":"Lots of benefits means many extra advantages, usually beyond basic pay.","zh":"很多福利意思是有許多額外好處，通常超出基本薪金。"},{"en":"A job may offer lots of benefits, such as medical insurance, training, and staff discounts.","zh":"一份工作可能提供很多福利，例如醫療保險、培訓和員工折扣。"},{"en":"Benefits can make a job more attractive even if the salary is not the highest.","zh":"即使薪金不是最高，福利也可以令工作更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extra positive features of a job or service.","zh":"這個短語描述工作或服務的額外好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have a good reputation for","meaning":"在……方面有很好的名聲","examples":[{"en":"Milo’s Restaurants have a good reputation for looking after staff.","zh":"Milo’s Restaurants 在照顧職員方面有很好的名聲。"},{"en":"To have a good reputation for something means to be known positively because of that quality or behaviour.","zh":"在某方面有很好的名聲意思是因某種特質或行為而被人正面認識。"},{"en":"A school may have a good reputation for helping weaker students improve.","zh":"學校可能在幫助較弱學生進步方面有很好的名聲。"},{"en":"A good reputation can attract customers, students, or job applicants.","zh":"好名聲可以吸引顧客、學生或求職者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what people generally believe about an organisation or person.","zh":"這個短語描述人們一般如何看待某機構或某人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look after staff","meaning":"照顧職員","examples":[{"en":"The company has a good reputation for looking after staff.","zh":"該公司在照顧職員方面有很好的名聲。"},{"en":"To look after staff means to take care of employees’ needs, safety, and working conditions.","zh":"照顧職員意思是關心員工的需要、安全和工作條件。"},{"en":"A manager looks after staff by giving clear instructions and fair breaks.","zh":"經理透過提供清楚指示和公平休息時間來照顧職員。"},{"en":"Companies that look after staff often have happier and more loyal employees.","zh":"照顧職員的公司通常有更快樂和更忠誠的員工。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests care and responsibility toward workers.","zh":"這個短語暗示對員工的關懷和責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"all employees","meaning":"所有僱員","examples":[{"en":"All employees at Milo’s Restaurants receive training.","zh":"Milo’s Restaurants 的所有僱員都接受培訓。"},{"en":"All employees means every person who works for a company or organisation.","zh":"所有僱員意思是在公司或機構工作的每一個人。"},{"en":"All employees must read the safety rules before starting work in a kitchen.","zh":"所有僱員在廚房開始工作前都必須閱讀安全規則。"},{"en":"When a rule applies to all employees, nobody is excluded from it.","zh":"當規則適用於所有僱員，沒有人被排除在外。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the whole workforce is included.","zh":"這個短語強調整個員工隊伍都包括在內。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get training","meaning":"接受培訓","examples":[{"en":"All employees get training, even temporary staff.","zh":"所有僱員都接受培訓，連臨時職員也一樣。"},{"en":"To get training means to receive instruction or practice for a job or skill.","zh":"接受培訓意思是為工作或技能接受指導或練習。"},{"en":"New cashiers get training before they serve customers alone.","zh":"新收銀員在獨自服務顧客前會接受培訓。"},{"en":"Training helps workers avoid mistakes and feel more confident.","zh":"培訓幫助員工避免錯誤並更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in workplaces and courses.","zh":"這個短語常見於工作場所和課程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"even temporary staff","meaning":"連臨時職員也","examples":[{"en":"Even temporary staff at Milo’s Restaurants get training.","zh":"Milo’s Restaurants 連臨時職員也接受培訓。"},{"en":"Even temporary staff means that short-term workers are included too, which may be unexpected.","zh":"連臨時職員也意思是短期員工也包括在內，這可能有點出乎意料。"},{"en":"Even temporary staff should know emergency exits before working in a shop.","zh":"連臨時職員也應在商店工作前知道緊急出口。"},{"en":"Including temporary staff in training can improve safety and service quality.","zh":"讓臨時職員接受培訓可以改善安全和服務質素。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the rule applies beyond permanent employees.","zh":"這個短語強調規則不只適用於長期員工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"quite unusual","meaning":"頗少見","examples":[{"en":"The man thinks training temporary staff is quite unusual.","zh":"那名男子認為培訓臨時職員頗少見。"},{"en":"Quite unusual means rather uncommon or not what people normally expect.","zh":"頗少見意思是相當不常見，或不是人們通常預期的。"},{"en":"It is quite unusual for a small shop to offer paid training to weekend staff.","zh":"小店向週末員工提供有薪培訓是頗少見的。"},{"en":"Unusual benefits can make a company stand out from other employers.","zh":"不尋常福利可以令公司在其他僱主中突圍而出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that is noticeable because it is not common.","zh":"這個短語描述某事因不常見而令人注意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"free uniforms","meaning":"免費制服","examples":[{"en":"The man asks whether staff get free uniforms.","zh":"那名男子問員工是否有免費制服。"},{"en":"Free uniforms are work clothes provided without staff having to pay for them.","zh":"免費制服是由僱主提供、員工不用付款的工作服。"},{"en":"A hotel may give free uniforms to receptionists so everyone looks professional.","zh":"酒店可能向接待員提供免費制服，令所有人看起來專業。"},{"en":"Free uniforms can reduce costs for employees and help a company create a consistent image.","zh":"免費制服可以減少員工開支，並幫助公司建立一致形象。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing job benefits.","zh":"這個短語常見於討論工作福利時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"it says here","meaning":"這裏寫着","examples":[{"en":"The woman says it states here that staff wear a white T-shirt and black trousers.","zh":"那名女子說，這裏寫着員工穿白色 T 恤和黑色長褲。"},{"en":"It says here means the written information in front of the speaker gives that detail.","zh":"這裏寫着意思是說話者面前的書面資料提供了該細節。"},{"en":"It says here that the interview starts at 10 a.m. in Room 3.","zh":"這裏寫着面試上午十時在 3 號房開始。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when reading from a form, notice, website, or document.","zh":"人們在讀表格、通告、網站或文件時會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the speaker is relying on written information.","zh":"這個短語顯示說話者依據書面資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"wear a white T-shirt","meaning":"穿白色T恤","examples":[{"en":"Staff need to wear a white T-shirt and black trousers.","zh":"員工需要穿白色 T 恤和黑色長褲。"},{"en":"To wear a white T-shirt means to put on a plain white short-sleeved top as clothing.","zh":"穿白色 T 恤意思是穿上一件白色短袖上衣。"},{"en":"A restaurant may ask staff to wear a white T-shirt so the team looks neat and simple.","zh":"餐廳可能要求員工穿白色 T 恤，讓團隊看起來整齊簡潔。"},{"en":"Clothing rules help customers recognise staff more easily.","zh":"服裝規定幫助顧客更容易認出員工。"},{"en":"This phrase describes part of a uniform or dress code.","zh":"這個短語描述制服或服裝規定的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"black trousers","meaning":"黑色長褲","examples":[{"en":"Staff need to wear black trousers at work.","zh":"員工上班時需要穿黑色長褲。"},{"en":"Black trousers are long black pants worn as part of clothing or a uniform.","zh":"黑色長褲是作為衣着或制服一部分的黑色長褲。"},{"en":"Many restaurants require black trousers because they look tidy and professional.","zh":"許多餐廳要求穿黑色長褲，因為它們看起來整齊專業。"},{"en":"Dark trousers can hide small stains better than light-coloured trousers.","zh":"深色長褲比淺色長褲更能遮住小污漬。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in workplace dress codes.","zh":"這個短語常出現在工作場所服裝規定中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I guess not","meaning":"我想不是","examples":[{"en":"The woman guesses that staff do not get free uniforms.","zh":"那名女子猜想員工應該沒有免費制服。"},{"en":"I guess not means I think the answer is probably no, although I am not completely certain.","zh":"我想不是意思是我認為答案大概是否定的，但不是完全肯定。"},{"en":"If the shop closes at six and it is already seven, I guess not many staff are still inside.","zh":"如果商店六點關門而現在已經七點，我想裏面應該沒有多少職員。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they are making a careful guess.","zh":"人們在作出謹慎猜測時會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds informal and slightly uncertain.","zh":"這個短語較口語，而且帶一點不確定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"another benefit of","meaning":"……的另一個好處","examples":[{"en":"Another benefit of working for a big company is the staff discount.","zh":"在大公司工作的另一個好處是員工折扣。"},{"en":"Another benefit of something means one more advantage in addition to the others already mentioned.","zh":"某事的另一個好處意思是在已提及的好處之外，再多一個優點。"},{"en":"Another benefit of walking to school is that students get daily exercise.","zh":"步行上學的另一個好處是學生能每天運動。"},{"en":"Listing another benefit helps explain why an option is attractive.","zh":"列出另一個好處有助解釋某選項為何吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when adding a positive point.","zh":"這個短語適合用於加入正面重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"working for a big company","meaning":"在大公司工作","examples":[{"en":"Working for a big company like Milo’s has several benefits.","zh":"在 Milo’s 這樣的大公司工作有幾個好處。"},{"en":"Working for a big company means being employed by a large organisation with many staff or branches.","zh":"在大公司工作意思是受僱於有很多員工或分店的大型機構。"},{"en":"Working for a big company can offer training, promotion chances, and stable rules.","zh":"在大公司工作可以提供培訓、晉升機會和穩定制度。"},{"en":"Some people prefer big companies because benefits and procedures are clearer.","zh":"有些人較喜歡大公司，因為福利和程序較清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes employment in a large organisation.","zh":"這個短語描述在大型機構受僱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"get a discount at","meaning":"在……享有折扣","examples":[{"en":"Staff can get a discount at any of the company’s restaurants.","zh":"員工可以在公司旗下任何餐廳享有折扣。"},{"en":"To get a discount at a place means to pay less than the normal price there.","zh":"在某處享有折扣意思是在那裏支付低於正常價格的金額。"},{"en":"Students may get a discount at the cinema by showing a student card.","zh":"學生出示學生證可能可在戲院享有折扣。"},{"en":"Staff discounts can encourage employees to use the company’s own services.","zh":"員工折扣可以鼓勵員工使用公司自己的服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about reduced prices.","zh":"這個短語適合用於談論減價優惠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"any of their restaurants","meaning":"他們旗下任何一間餐廳","examples":[{"en":"Staff can use the discount at any of their restaurants.","zh":"員工可以在他們旗下任何一間餐廳使用折扣。"},{"en":"Any of their restaurants means every restaurant in that company’s group is included.","zh":"他們旗下任何一間餐廳意思是該公司集團的每間餐廳都包括在內。"},{"en":"A gift voucher may be used at any of the chain’s branches.","zh":"禮券可能可在連鎖店旗下任何分店使用。"},{"en":"Allowing discounts at any restaurant makes the benefit more useful for staff.","zh":"允許在任何餐廳使用折扣，會令這項福利對員工更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the choice is not limited to one location.","zh":"這個短語強調選擇不限於一個地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"even at weekends","meaning":"即使在週末","examples":[{"en":"The man asks whether the discount is available even at weekends.","zh":"那名男子問折扣是否即使在週末也適用。"},{"en":"Even at weekends means including Saturdays and Sundays, which may be unexpected.","zh":"即使在週末意思是包括星期六和星期日，這可能有點出乎意料。"},{"en":"Some buses run late even at weekends because many people go out at night.","zh":"有些巴士即使在週末也會開到很晚，因為很多人晚上外出。"},{"en":"A benefit is more valuable if staff can use it even at weekends.","zh":"如果員工即使在週末也能使用福利，該福利會更有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that weekends are included too.","zh":"這個短語強調週末也包括在內。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be working then anyway","meaning":"反正那時也會上班","examples":[{"en":"The woman says he will be working then anyway.","zh":"那名女子說他反正那時也會上班。"},{"en":"To be working then anyway means to be at work at that time regardless of other plans.","zh":"反正那時也會上班意思是無論其他安排如何，那個時間本來就在工作。"},{"en":"If you are working then anyway, you might as well join the staff meeting after your shift.","zh":"如果你反正那時也會上班，不妨下班後參加員工會議。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the situation is already expected, so it does not change much.","zh":"這個短語暗示情況本已預期，所以影響不大。"},{"en":"It is often used to make a point sound practical.","zh":"它常用來令說法聽起來實際。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"I suppose so","meaning":"我想也是","examples":[{"en":"The man says, “I suppose so,” when he realises he will work at weekends.","zh":"當那名男子意識到自己會在週末上班時，他說：「我想也是。」"},{"en":"I suppose so means I think that is probably true, although I am not very enthusiastic.","zh":"我想也是意思是我認為那大概是真的，雖然不算很熱切。"},{"en":"If the bus is cheaper but slower, a student may say, “I suppose so,” before agreeing to take it.","zh":"如果巴士較便宜但較慢，學生在同意乘搭前可能會說：「我想也是。」"},{"en":"This phrase can show reluctant agreement.","zh":"這個短語可以表示勉強同意。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken English.","zh":"它常見於口語英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"most of their restaurants","meaning":"他們大部分餐廳","examples":[{"en":"Most of their restaurants are in the city centre.","zh":"他們大部分餐廳都在市中心。"},{"en":"Most of their restaurants means the majority of the restaurants owned by that company.","zh":"他們大部分餐廳意思是該公司擁有的餐廳中的多數。"},{"en":"Most of the school’s sports facilities are near the main building.","zh":"學校大部分運動設施都在主樓附近。"},{"en":"When most branches are central, customers and staff may find them easier to reach.","zh":"當大部分分店位於市中心，顧客和員工可能較容易到達。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the majority within a group.","zh":"這個短語描述某群體中的大多數。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the city centre","meaning":"在市中心","examples":[{"en":"Most of Milo’s restaurants are in the city centre.","zh":"Milo’s 大部分餐廳都在市中心。"},{"en":"In the city centre means in the main central area of a city.","zh":"在市中心意思是在城市的主要中心地帶。"},{"en":"Shops in the city centre are often close to offices, buses, and train stations.","zh":"市中心的商店通常接近辦公室、巴士站和火車站。"},{"en":"A city-centre location can attract more customers because it is easy to reach.","zh":"市中心位置可以吸引更多顧客，因為容易到達。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a central urban location.","zh":"這個短語描述城市中心位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"easy to get to","meaning":"容易到達","examples":[{"en":"The restaurants are easy to get to by bus.","zh":"這些餐廳乘巴士容易到達。"},{"en":"Easy to get to means simple or convenient to reach.","zh":"容易到達意思是前往簡單或方便。"},{"en":"A school near a train station is easy to get to for students from different districts.","zh":"靠近火車站的學校，對來自不同地區的學生來說容易到達。"},{"en":"Places that are easy to get to can attract more visitors and workers.","zh":"容易到達的地方可以吸引更多訪客和員工。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on transport convenience.","zh":"這個短語重點是交通便利。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"by bus","meaning":"乘巴士","examples":[{"en":"The restaurants are easy to get to by bus.","zh":"這些餐廳乘巴士容易到達。"},{"en":"By bus means using a bus as the method of transport.","zh":"乘巴士意思是使用巴士作為交通方式。"},{"en":"Many students go to school by bus when they live far away.","zh":"許多學生住得遠時會乘巴士上學。"},{"en":"Travelling by bus may be cheaper than taking a taxi.","zh":"乘巴士可能比乘的士便宜。"},{"en":"This phrase tells how someone travels to a place.","zh":"這個短語說明某人如何前往某地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"do a late shift","meaning":"上夜班","examples":[{"en":"Staff may have to do a late shift at Milo’s.","zh":"員工可能需要在 Milo’s 上夜班。"},{"en":"To do a late shift means to work during the late evening or night.","zh":"上夜班意思是在晚上較遲或夜間工作。"},{"en":"A nurse may do a late shift and finish work after most people have gone home.","zh":"護士可能上夜班，在大多數人已回家後才下班。"},{"en":"Late shifts can affect transport, sleep, and family time.","zh":"夜班可以影響交通、睡眠和家庭時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a work schedule, not the type of work itself.","zh":"這個短語描述工作時間表，而不是工作種類本身。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"finish work after midnight","meaning":"午夜後下班","examples":[{"en":"Staff may finish work after midnight after a late shift.","zh":"員工上夜班後可能在午夜後下班。"},{"en":"To finish work after midnight means to end a shift later than 12 a.m.","zh":"午夜後下班意思是在凌晨 12 時之後結束班次。"},{"en":"Restaurant staff may finish work after midnight when dinner service ends late.","zh":"當晚餐服務很晚才結束，餐廳員工可能午夜後下班。"},{"en":"Finishing after midnight can make safe transport home especially important.","zh":"午夜後下班會令安全回家交通特別重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very late end time for work.","zh":"這個短語描述非常晚的下班時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pay for someone to","meaning":"付款讓某人……","examples":[{"en":"The company will pay for staff to get a taxi home.","zh":"公司會付款讓員工乘的士回家。"},{"en":"To pay for someone to do something means to cover the cost so that person can do it.","zh":"付款讓某人做某事意思是承擔費用，使那人可以做該事。"},{"en":"A school may pay for students to take a bus to a museum.","zh":"學校可能付款讓學生乘巴士去博物館。"},{"en":"Companies sometimes pay for staff to attend training because the skills help the workplace.","zh":"公司有時會付款讓員工參加培訓，因為技能對工作場所有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase connects payment with another person’s action.","zh":"這個短語把付款與另一人的行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get a taxi home","meaning":"乘的士回家","examples":[{"en":"The company pays for staff to get a taxi home after midnight.","zh":"員工午夜後下班時，公司會付款讓他們乘的士回家。"},{"en":"To get a taxi home means to travel home by taxi.","zh":"乘的士回家意思是乘坐的士返回家中。"},{"en":"A worker may get a taxi home after a late shift if buses have stopped running.","zh":"如果巴士已停駛，員工下夜班後可能乘的士回家。"},{"en":"Paying for taxis can help staff get home safely at night.","zh":"支付的士費可以幫助員工晚上安全回家。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the journey home after work or an event.","zh":"這個短語重點是下班或活動後回家的旅程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"probably won’t need one","meaning":"大概不需要","examples":[{"en":"The man says he probably will not need a taxi.","zh":"那名男子說他大概不需要的士。"},{"en":"Probably won’t need one means it is likely that the person will not require that thing.","zh":"大概不需要某物意思是那人很可能不需要該東西。"},{"en":"If the school is only five minutes away, I probably won’t need a bus.","zh":"如果學校只距離五分鐘路程，我大概不需要乘巴士。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they are making a reasonable prediction.","zh":"人們在作出合理預測時會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It sounds less certain than saying “I definitely will not need one”.","zh":"它聽起來不如「我一定不需要」那麼肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"use my bike","meaning":"踩單車","examples":[{"en":"The man thinks he would use his bike instead of taking a taxi.","zh":"那名男子認為自己會踩單車，而不是乘的士。"},{"en":"To use my bike means to travel by bicycle or ride it for transport.","zh":"踩單車意思是以單車作為交通方式。"},{"en":"A student may use their bike to get to school when the weather is good.","zh":"天氣好時，學生可能踩單車上學。"},{"en":"Using a bike can save money and avoid waiting for public transport.","zh":"踩單車可以節省金錢，也避免等公共交通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing cycling as the way to travel.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇單車作為出行方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"specific requirements","meaning":"具體要求","examples":[{"en":"Milo’s has some specific requirements for the people they hire.","zh":"Milo’s 對聘請的人有一些具體要求。"},{"en":"Specific requirements are clear conditions or qualities that must be met.","zh":"具體要求是必須符合的清楚條件或特質。"},{"en":"A school trip may have specific requirements, such as parental consent and suitable shoes.","zh":"學校旅行可能有具體要求，例如家長同意書和合適鞋履。"},{"en":"Employers list specific requirements so applicants know whether they are suitable.","zh":"僱主列出具體要求，讓申請人知道自己是否合適。"},{"en":"This phrase describes detailed expectations, not general preferences.","zh":"這個短語描述詳細期望，而不是一般喜好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the kind of person","meaning":"某類人","examples":[{"en":"The company has specific requirements for the kind of person it is looking for.","zh":"公司對自己正在尋找的某類人有具體要求。"},{"en":"The kind of person means the type of person with particular qualities or habits.","zh":"某類人意思是具有特定特質或習慣的人。"},{"en":"A school may look for the kind of person who is patient and enjoys helping younger students.","zh":"學校可能尋找有耐性並喜歡幫助低年級學生的那類人。"},{"en":"Employers describe the kind of person they want so applicants understand the role better.","zh":"僱主描述想要的某類人，讓申請者更理解職位。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on personal qualities, not only qualifications.","zh":"這個短語重點是個人特質，而不只是資格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be looking for","meaning":"正在尋找","examples":[{"en":"Milo’s is looking for people who can fit into the team.","zh":"Milo’s 正在尋找能融入團隊的人。"},{"en":"To be looking for someone means to be trying to find or hire that person.","zh":"正在尋找某人意思是嘗試找到或聘請那個人。"},{"en":"A company may be looking for a receptionist who can speak clearly and handle customers politely.","zh":"公司可能正在尋找一位能清楚說話並有禮處理顧客的接待員。"},{"en":"When employers are looking for staff, they usually consider skills, attitude, and availability.","zh":"僱主尋找員工時，通常會考慮技能、態度和可上班時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in recruitment.","zh":"這個短語常見於招聘。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a young, dynamic company","meaning":"年輕而有活力的公司","examples":[{"en":"Milo’s is described as a young, dynamic company.","zh":"Milo’s 被形容為一間年輕而有活力的公司。"},{"en":"A young, dynamic company is a newer business that feels energetic, active, and ready to grow.","zh":"年輕而有活力的公司是較新的企業，感覺充滿能量、行動力和成長準備。"},{"en":"A young, dynamic company may attract workers who enjoy change and fast teamwork.","zh":"年輕而有活力的公司可能吸引喜歡變化和快速團隊合作的員工。"},{"en":"Dynamic companies often expect staff to learn quickly and adapt to new ideas.","zh":"有活力的公司通常期望員工快速學習並適應新想法。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a positive image of energy and development.","zh":"這個短語帶出充滿能量和發展的正面形象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be keen on","meaning":"熱衷於……；很重視……","examples":[{"en":"The company is keen on creating a strong team.","zh":"公司很重視建立強大的團隊。"},{"en":"To be keen on something means to be very interested in it or consider it important.","zh":"熱衷於或很重視某事意思是對它很有興趣，或認為它重要。"},{"en":"A school may be keen on improving students’ speaking confidence.","zh":"學校可能很重視提升學生的說話信心。"},{"en":"When a company is keen on teamwork, it may hire people who communicate well.","zh":"當公司重視團隊合作，可能會聘請溝通良好的人。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong interest or emphasis.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈興趣或重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"create a strong team","meaning":"建立強大的團隊","examples":[{"en":"Milo’s is keen on creating a strong team.","zh":"Milo’s 很重視建立強大的團隊。"},{"en":"To create a strong team means to build a group of people who work well together.","zh":"建立強大的團隊意思是組成一群能良好合作的人。"},{"en":"A manager creates a strong team by hiring carefully and helping staff trust one another.","zh":"經理可以透過謹慎招聘和幫助員工互相信任來建立強大的團隊。"},{"en":"Strong teams can improve service because workers support each other under pressure.","zh":"強大團隊可以改善服務，因為員工在壓力下互相支持。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in workplace and leadership contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於工作場所和領導語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"it’s really important that","meaning":"……非常重要","examples":[{"en":"It is really important that new staff can fit in.","zh":"新員工能夠融入非常重要。"},{"en":"It’s really important that means the following point matters a lot.","zh":"……非常重要意思是接下來的重點很重要。"},{"en":"It is really important that students understand the rules before using laboratory equipment.","zh":"學生在使用實驗室設備前明白規則非常重要。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase when they want listeners to pay special attention.","zh":"說話者想聽眾特別留意時會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a key requirement or warning.","zh":"這個短語引入關鍵要求或提醒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fit in","meaning":"融入","examples":[{"en":"New staff need to fit in with the team.","zh":"新員工需要融入團隊。"},{"en":"To fit in means to become comfortable in a group and work well with others.","zh":"融入意思是在群體中感到自在並能與他人良好合作。"},{"en":"A new student may fit in more easily when classmates invite them to lunch.","zh":"當同學邀請新生一起吃午飯，新生可能更容易融入。"},{"en":"Staff who fit in can communicate better and avoid unnecessary conflict.","zh":"能融入的員工可以更好溝通並避免不必要衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on social and team adjustment.","zh":"這個短語重點是社交和團隊適應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get on well with","meaning":"與……相處融洽","examples":[{"en":"Staff need to get on well with everyone.","zh":"員工需要與所有人相處融洽。"},{"en":"To get on well with someone means to have a friendly and smooth relationship with them.","zh":"與某人相處融洽意思是與他有友善而順暢的關係。"},{"en":"A student who gets on well with classmates may enjoy group projects more.","zh":"與同學相處融洽的學生可能更享受小組項目。"},{"en":"Getting on well with colleagues can make busy shifts less stressful.","zh":"與同事相處融洽可以令繁忙班次較不緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase describes good personal relationships.","zh":"這個短語描述良好人際關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have no problem with","meaning":"對……沒有問題","examples":[{"en":"The man says he has no problem with fitting in.","zh":"那名男子說他對融入團隊沒有問題。"},{"en":"To have no problem with something means to feel comfortable about it and not find it difficult.","zh":"對某事沒有問題意思是對它感到自在，並不覺得困難。"},{"en":"A student may have no problem with speaking in pairs but feel nervous in front of the whole class.","zh":"學生可能對二人對話沒有問題，但在全班面前會緊張。"},{"en":"If someone has no problem with teamwork, they may suit a customer-service job.","zh":"如果某人對團隊合作沒有問題，他可能適合顧客服務工作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows acceptance or confidence.","zh":"這個短語顯示接受或信心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sound good","meaning":"聽起來不錯","examples":[{"en":"The job requirements sound good to the man.","zh":"這些工作要求對那名男子來說聽起來不錯。"},{"en":"Sound good means seem attractive, suitable, or acceptable when described.","zh":"聽起來不錯意思是被描述時看似吸引、合適或可接受。"},{"en":"A weekend class may sound good if the timetable fits a student’s schedule.","zh":"如果時間表配合學生日程，週末課程可能聽起來不錯。"},{"en":"Something can sound good at first, but people should still check the details.","zh":"某事一開始可以聽起來不錯，但人們仍應核實細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive first impression.","zh":"這個短語描述正面的第一印象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the last place I worked for","meaning":"我上一間任職的地方","examples":[{"en":"The last place the man worked for was quite demanding.","zh":"那名男子上一間任職的地方要求頗高。"},{"en":"The last place I worked for means the most recent company, shop, or organisation where I had a job.","zh":"我上一間任職的地方意思是我最近工作的公司、店舖或機構。"},{"en":"The last place I worked for gave staff very clear rules about customer service.","zh":"我上一間任職的地方對顧客服務有非常清楚的規則。"},{"en":"Talking about the last place you worked for helps interviewers understand your experience.","zh":"談及上一間任職的地方，有助面試官了解你的經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a previous employer.","zh":"這個短語指前僱主。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"quite demanding","meaning":"要求頗高","examples":[{"en":"The man’s previous workplace was quite demanding.","zh":"那名男子以前的工作場所要求頗高。"},{"en":"Quite demanding means needing a lot of effort, skill, or attention.","zh":"要求頗高意思是需要大量努力、技能或注意力。"},{"en":"A restaurant job can be quite demanding when many customers arrive at the same time.","zh":"當很多顧客同時到來，餐廳工作可以要求頗高。"},{"en":"Demanding work can build skills, but it may also make staff tired.","zh":"要求高的工作可以建立技能，但也可能令員工疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a task, job, or environment that is not easy.","zh":"這個短語描述不容易的任務、工作或環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Staff had to make sure they gave a high level of service.","zh":"員工必須確保自己提供高水平服務。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check carefully or do what is needed so something happens correctly.","zh":"確保意思是仔細檢查或採取所需行動，使某事正確發生。"},{"en":"A waiter should make sure every order is written down clearly.","zh":"侍應應確保每張訂單都清楚寫下。"},{"en":"Making sure details are correct can prevent complaints and mistakes.","zh":"確保細節正確可以防止投訴和錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when accuracy or responsibility matters.","zh":"當準確性或責任重要時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a high level of service","meaning":"高水平服務","examples":[{"en":"The man had to provide a high level of service in his previous job.","zh":"那名男子在上一份工作中必須提供高水平服務。"},{"en":"A high level of service means polite, efficient, and careful help for customers.","zh":"高水平服務意思是為顧客提供有禮、有效率和細心的協助。"},{"en":"Hotels need a high level of service because guests expect comfort and quick responses.","zh":"酒店需要高水平服務，因為住客期待舒適和快速回應。"},{"en":"Good service can make customers return even when prices are not the lowest.","zh":"良好服務可以令顧客再次光顧，即使價格不是最低。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in restaurants, hotels, shops, and customer care.","zh":"這個短語常見於餐廳、酒店、商店和顧客服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"good to hear","meaning":"很高興聽到","examples":[{"en":"The woman says it is good to hear that the man values service.","zh":"那名女子說很高興聽到那名男子重視服務。"},{"en":"Good to hear means I am pleased to learn that information.","zh":"很高興聽到意思是知道該資料令人感到高興。"},{"en":"A teacher may say it is good to hear that a student has started revising early.","zh":"老師可能會說很高興聽到學生已開始提早溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when someone’s answer gives a positive impression.","zh":"當某人的回答給人正面印象時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It sounds friendly and encouraging.","zh":"它聽起來友善而鼓勵人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"equally important","meaning":"同樣重要","examples":[{"en":"A high level of service will be equally important at Milo’s.","zh":"高水平服務在 Milo’s 也同樣重要。"},{"en":"Equally important means just as important as something else already mentioned.","zh":"同樣重要意思是與已提及的另一事物一樣重要。"},{"en":"In a restaurant, food quality is important, but hygiene is equally important.","zh":"在餐廳中，食物質素很重要，但衛生同樣重要。"},{"en":"When two qualities are equally important, neither should be ignored.","zh":"當兩項特質同樣重要，兩者都不應被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when balancing two important points.","zh":"這個短語適合用於平衡兩個重要重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have an eye for detail","meaning":"注重細節","examples":[{"en":"Milo’s wants people who have an eye for detail.","zh":"Milo’s 想聘請注重細節的人。"},{"en":"To have an eye for detail means to notice small things that others may miss.","zh":"注重細節意思是能注意到別人可能錯過的小地方。"},{"en":"A receptionist with an eye for detail may spot a wrong booking date before it causes trouble.","zh":"注重細節的接待員可能在造成麻煩前發現錯誤訂房日期。"},{"en":"Attention to detail can prevent errors in orders, bills, and customer requests.","zh":"注重細節可以防止訂單、帳單和顧客要求出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful observation and accuracy.","zh":"這個短語描述細心觀察和準確性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be used to working in","meaning":"習慣在……工作","examples":[{"en":"The man is used to working in a demanding environment.","zh":"那名男子習慣在要求高的環境中工作。"},{"en":"To be used to working in a place or situation means to be familiar with it because of experience.","zh":"習慣在某地或某情況中工作意思是因經驗而熟悉它。"},{"en":"A nurse is used to working in a busy hospital where decisions must be made quickly.","zh":"護士習慣在繁忙醫院工作，因為那裏必須快速作決定。"},{"en":"People who are used to pressure may stay calmer in difficult workplaces.","zh":"習慣壓力的人在困難工作場所可能更冷靜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes comfort gained through repeated experience.","zh":"這個短語描述透過重複經驗而獲得的適應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"that kind of environment","meaning":"那種環境","examples":[{"en":"The man is used to working in that kind of environment.","zh":"那名男子習慣在那種環境中工作。"},{"en":"That kind of environment means that type of workplace, situation, or atmosphere.","zh":"那種環境意思是那類工作場所、情況或氣氛。"},{"en":"A quiet student may struggle in a noisy classroom if they are not used to that kind of environment.","zh":"如果安靜學生不習慣那種環境，他可能在嘈雜課室中感到吃力。"},{"en":"People perform better when the environment matches their experience and personality.","zh":"當環境配合人的經驗和個性，人們會表現得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a situation already described.","zh":"這個短語指回已描述的情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the only other thing required","meaning":"唯一另一項要求","examples":[{"en":"The only other thing required is good communication skills.","zh":"唯一另一項要求是良好的溝通技巧。"},{"en":"The only other thing required means the last additional requirement that is needed.","zh":"唯一另一項要求意思是最後一項還需要的額外條件。"},{"en":"For this school trip, the only other thing required is a signed parent consent form.","zh":"對這次學校旅行來說，唯一另一項要求是已簽署的家長同意書。"},{"en":"This phrase helps make a list of requirements sound complete.","zh":"這個短語有助令要求清單聽起來完整。"},{"en":"It suggests there are no many extra conditions left.","zh":"它暗示沒有很多額外條件剩下。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"good communication skills","meaning":"良好的溝通技巧","examples":[{"en":"The job requires good communication skills.","zh":"這份工作需要良好的溝通技巧。"},{"en":"Good communication skills mean the ability to speak, listen, and share information clearly.","zh":"良好的溝通技巧意思是能清楚說話、聆聽和分享資訊的能力。"},{"en":"Waiters need good communication skills to understand orders and answer customers politely.","zh":"侍應需要良好的溝通技巧，以理解訂單並有禮貌地回答顧客。"},{"en":"Poor communication can lead to mistakes, complaints, and confusion at work.","zh":"溝通差可以導致錯誤、投訴和工作上的混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in job advertisements.","zh":"這個短語常見於招聘廣告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have a certificate in English","meaning":"持有英文證書","examples":[{"en":"The man needs to have a certificate in English.","zh":"那名男子需要持有英文證書。"},{"en":"To have a certificate in English means to possess an official qualification showing English ability.","zh":"持有英文證書意思是擁有顯示英語能力的正式資格。"},{"en":"Some reception jobs require applicants to have a certificate in English.","zh":"有些接待職位要求申請人持有英文證書。"},{"en":"A certificate can help employers judge whether a candidate has enough language skills.","zh":"證書可以幫助僱主判斷候選人是否有足夠語言能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal proof of English competence.","zh":"這個短語描述英語能力的正式證明。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"current job vacancies","meaning":"目前的職位空缺","examples":[{"en":"The woman checks the current job vacancies at Milo’s.","zh":"那名女子查看 Milo’s 目前的職位空缺。"},{"en":"Current job vacancies are job openings available now.","zh":"目前的職位空缺是現在可申請的工作崗位。"},{"en":"A careers website lists current job vacancies for teachers, assistants, and office staff.","zh":"求職網站列出教師、助理和辦公室職員目前的職位空缺。"},{"en":"Checking current vacancies helps applicants choose roles that are actually open.","zh":"查看目前職位空缺有助申請人選擇真正正在招聘的職位。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in recruitment and job searching.","zh":"這個短語用於招聘和求職。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Wivenhoe Street","meaning":"Wivenhoe Street","examples":[{"en":"The first vacancy is in Wivenhoe Street.","zh":"第一個職位空缺在 Wivenhoe Street。"},{"en":"Wivenhoe Street is the name of the street where the first job is located.","zh":"Wivenhoe Street 是第一份工作所在地的街道名稱。"},{"en":"An applicant should check how to travel to Wivenhoe Street before accepting an interview.","zh":"申請人在接受面試前應查清如何前往 Wivenhoe Street。"},{"en":"Knowing the street helps candidates judge commuting time and convenience.","zh":"知道街道位置有助候選人判斷通勤時間和便利程度。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific job location.","zh":"這個短語命名一個具體工作地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"quite central","meaning":"位置頗近市中心","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant in Wivenhoe Street is quite central.","zh":"Wivenhoe Street 的餐廳位置頗近市中心。"},{"en":"Quite central means fairly close to the main part of a town or city.","zh":"位置頗近市中心意思是相當接近城鎮或城市的主要中心地帶。"},{"en":"A flat that is quite central may be convenient but more expensive.","zh":"位置頗近市中心的單位可能方便但較貴。"},{"en":"Central locations are easier to reach but can also be busier.","zh":"市中心位置較容易到達，但也可能較繁忙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a location that is reasonably near the centre.","zh":"這個短語描述相當接近中心的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"just off Cork Street","meaning":"就在 Cork Street 附近","examples":[{"en":"Wivenhoe Street is just off Cork Street.","zh":"Wivenhoe Street 就在 Cork Street 附近。"},{"en":"Just off a street means very close to it, usually connected by a small side street.","zh":"就在某街附近意思是非常接近該街，通常由小街連接。"},{"en":"The café is just off the main road, so it is easy to find.","zh":"咖啡店就在大路附近，所以容易找到。"},{"en":"Saying a place is just off a familiar street helps people locate it quickly.","zh":"說某地就在熟悉街道附近，有助人們快速定位。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a nearby location.","zh":"這個短語描述附近位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"breakfast supervisor","meaning":"早餐主管","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant is looking for a breakfast supervisor.","zh":"該餐廳正在招聘早餐主管。"},{"en":"A breakfast supervisor is a person who manages staff and service during breakfast hours.","zh":"早餐主管是在早餐時段管理員工和服務的人。"},{"en":"A hotel breakfast supervisor checks that food is ready and tables are clean before guests arrive.","zh":"酒店早餐主管會在住客到達前檢查食物是否準備好、餐桌是否乾淨。"},{"en":"Supervisors help maintain quality by checking staff, food, and procedures.","zh":"主管透過檢查員工、食物和程序來維持質素。"},{"en":"This phrase names a management role for morning food service.","zh":"這個短語命名早上餐飲服務的管理職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be familiar with","meaning":"熟悉……","examples":[{"en":"The man is probably familiar with the responsibilities involved.","zh":"那名男子大概熟悉當中涉及的職責。"},{"en":"To be familiar with something means to know it well because of experience or learning.","zh":"熟悉某事意思是因經驗或學習而很了解它。"},{"en":"A teacher is familiar with common spelling mistakes after marking many essays.","zh":"老師批改很多文章後，會熟悉常見串字錯誤。"},{"en":"Being familiar with a task helps workers do it more quickly and confidently.","zh":"熟悉一項任務有助員工更快和更有信心地完成它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes knowledge gained through experience.","zh":"這個短語描述透過經驗獲得的知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the responsibilities involved","meaning":"當中涉及的職責","examples":[{"en":"The woman explains the responsibilities involved in the supervisor role.","zh":"那名女子解釋主管職位當中涉及的職責。"},{"en":"The responsibilities involved are the duties and tasks connected with a job or situation.","zh":"當中涉及的職責是與工作或情況相關的責任和任務。"},{"en":"Before joining a club committee, students should understand the responsibilities involved.","zh":"學生加入學會委員會前，應了解當中涉及的職責。"},{"en":"Knowing the responsibilities involved helps people decide whether they can manage the role.","zh":"知道當中涉及的職責，有助人們決定自己能否應付該角色。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what someone must do.","zh":"這個短語重點是某人必須做甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"check that","meaning":"檢查……是否","examples":[{"en":"The supervisor checks that all the portions are correct.","zh":"主管檢查所有食物分量是否正確。"},{"en":"To check that something is true means to make sure it is correct.","zh":"檢查某事是否真實意思是確保它正確。"},{"en":"A teacher checks that every student has written their name on the answer sheet.","zh":"老師檢查每位學生是否已在答題紙上寫名字。"},{"en":"Checking details can prevent errors before customers or users are affected.","zh":"檢查細節可以在顧客或使用者受影響前防止錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when someone verifies a condition.","zh":"這個短語用於某人核實某情況時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"portions","meaning":"食物分量","examples":[{"en":"The supervisor checks that all the portions are correct.","zh":"主管檢查所有食物分量是否正確。"},{"en":"Portions are the amounts of food served to each person.","zh":"食物分量是給每個人的食物份量。"},{"en":"A restaurant must control portions so customers receive fair and consistent meals.","zh":"餐廳必須控制食物分量，讓顧客得到公平和一致的餐點。"},{"en":"If portions are too small, customers may complain; if they are too large, food may be wasted.","zh":"如果食物分量太少，顧客可能投訴；如果太多，食物可能被浪費。"},{"en":"This word is common in restaurants, diets, and food service.","zh":"這個詞常見於餐廳、飲食和餐飲服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"procedures for cleaning","meaning":"清潔……的程序","examples":[{"en":"The supervisor checks the procedures for cleaning the equipment.","zh":"主管檢查清潔設備的程序。"},{"en":"Procedures for cleaning are the steps workers must follow to clean something properly.","zh":"清潔程序是員工必須跟從以妥善清潔某物的步驟。"},{"en":"A kitchen may have procedures for cleaning knives, chopping boards, and ovens.","zh":"廚房可能有清潔刀具、砧板和焗爐的程序。"},{"en":"Clear cleaning procedures reduce health risks and keep workplaces safe.","zh":"清楚清潔程序可以減少健康風險並保持工作場所安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised instructions for hygiene.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的衛生指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cleaning the equipment","meaning":"清潔設備","examples":[{"en":"Staff must follow the procedures for cleaning the equipment.","zh":"員工必須遵守清潔設備的程序。"},{"en":"Cleaning the equipment means washing or sanitising tools and machines used at work.","zh":"清潔設備意思是清洗或消毒工作中使用的工具和機器。"},{"en":"Restaurant staff clean the equipment after service so it is ready for the next shift.","zh":"餐廳員工在服務後清潔設備，讓它準備好供下一班使用。"},{"en":"Cleaning equipment properly prevents germs, smells, and food contamination.","zh":"妥善清潔設備可以防止細菌、異味和食物污染。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in kitchens, hospitals, and workplaces with tools.","zh":"這個短語常見於廚房、醫院和有工具的工作場所。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be followed","meaning":"被遵守","examples":[{"en":"The supervisor checks that the cleaning procedures are being followed.","zh":"主管檢查清潔程序是否正被遵守。"},{"en":"To be followed means to be obeyed or carried out as instructed.","zh":"被遵守意思是按照指示被服從或執行。"},{"en":"School safety rules must be followed during science experiments.","zh":"科學實驗期間，學校安全規則必須被遵守。"},{"en":"If procedures are not followed, mistakes and accidents become more likely.","zh":"如果程序沒有被遵守，錯誤和意外會更容易發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for rules, instructions, and procedures.","zh":"這個短語常用於規則、指示和程序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"what about the salary?","meaning":"薪金方面怎樣？","examples":[{"en":"The man asks, “What about the salary?”","zh":"那名男子問：「薪金方面怎樣？」"},{"en":"“What about the salary?” means asking for information about how much the job pays.","zh":"「薪金方面怎樣？」意思是詢問該工作支付多少薪酬。"},{"en":"A job applicant may ask, “What about the salary?” after hearing about the duties.","zh":"求職者聽完職責後，可能會問：「薪金方面怎樣？」"},{"en":"Salary matters because it affects whether a person can accept the job.","zh":"薪金很重要，因為它影響一個人能否接受工作。"},{"en":"This question is common in job discussions.","zh":"這個問題常見於工作討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in my last job","meaning":"在我上一份工作","examples":[{"en":"In his last job, the man was getting £9.50 per hour.","zh":"在他上一份工作中，那名男子每小時賺 £9.50。"},{"en":"In my last job means during the previous job I had.","zh":"在我上一份工作意思是在我以前最近一份工作期間。"},{"en":"In my last job, I learned how to deal with difficult customers.","zh":"在我上一份工作中，我學會如何處理難應付的顧客。"},{"en":"People mention their last job to compare pay, duties, or experience.","zh":"人們提及上一份工作，是為了比較薪金、職責或經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to someone’s most recent previous employment.","zh":"這個短語指某人最近的前一份工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"per hour","meaning":"每小時","examples":[{"en":"The man was earning £9.50 per hour in his last job.","zh":"那名男子上一份工作每小時賺 £9.50。"},{"en":"Per hour means for each hour of work or time.","zh":"每小時意思是每工作或經過一小時。"},{"en":"A tutor may charge £30 per hour for private lessons.","zh":"補習老師可能每小時收 £30 私人課費。"},{"en":"Hourly pay helps workers calculate how much they will earn for each shift.","zh":"時薪幫助員工計算每班可以賺多少。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when money or rates are measured by the hour.","zh":"這個短語用於金錢或比率按小時計算時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hope to get a bit more than","meaning":"希望比……多一點","examples":[{"en":"The man hopes to get a bit more than £9.50 per hour.","zh":"那名男子希望每小時薪金比 £9.50 多一點。"},{"en":"To hope to get a bit more than an amount means to want slightly higher pay or value than that amount.","zh":"希望比某金額多一點意思是想得到略高於該金額的薪酬或價值。"},{"en":"A worker may hope to get a bit more than their old salary after gaining experience.","zh":"員工累積經驗後，可能希望比舊薪金多一點。"},{"en":"People ask about pay because they want to know whether the new job improves their situation.","zh":"人們詢問薪金，因為他們想知道新工作是否改善自己的情況。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a modest expectation, not a huge demand.","zh":"這個短語表達溫和期望，而不是巨大要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"to begin with","meaning":"起初；一開始","examples":[{"en":"To begin with, the pay is £9.75 per hour.","zh":"起初，薪金是每小時 £9.75。"},{"en":"To begin with means at the start or in the first stage.","zh":"起初或一開始意思是在開始或第一階段。"},{"en":"To begin with, new staff may only handle simple customer orders.","zh":"一開始，新員工可能只處理簡單顧客訂單。"},{"en":"Starting conditions may change later as workers gain experience.","zh":"初始條件可能在員工累積經驗後改變。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the initial situation.","zh":"這個短語引入最初情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go up to","meaning":"升至……","examples":[{"en":"The pay goes up to £11.25 after three months.","zh":"薪金三個月後升至 £11.25。"},{"en":"To go up to an amount means to increase until it reaches that amount.","zh":"升至某數額意思是增加直到達到該數額。"},{"en":"A bus fare may go up to £3 next month.","zh":"巴士車費下個月可能升至 £3。"},{"en":"Pay increases can encourage workers to stay after the first training period.","zh":"加薪可以鼓勵員工在最初培訓期後留下。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase to a new level.","zh":"這個短語描述增加到新水平。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"after three months","meaning":"三個月後","examples":[{"en":"The salary increases after three months.","zh":"薪金三個月後增加。"},{"en":"After three months means when three months have passed.","zh":"三個月後意思是三個月過去之後。"},{"en":"A probation period may end after three months if the worker performs well.","zh":"如果員工表現良好，試用期可能三個月後結束。"},{"en":"Waiting three months for a pay rise gives employers time to assess performance.","zh":"等三個月才加薪，讓僱主有時間評估表現。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear time point after starting.","zh":"這個短語提供開始後的清楚時間點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not too bad","meaning":"還不錯","examples":[{"en":"The man thinks the starting salary is not too bad.","zh":"那名男子認為起薪還不錯。"},{"en":"Not too bad means acceptable or fairly good, though not excellent.","zh":"還不錯意思是可以接受或頗好，但不是極好。"},{"en":"A student may say a test result is not too bad if it is better than expected.","zh":"如果測驗成績比預期好，學生可能說還不錯。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows mild approval rather than strong excitement.","zh":"這個短語通常表示輕微認同，而不是非常興奮。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken English.","zh":"它常見於口語英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an early start","meaning":"很早開始工作","examples":[{"en":"The breakfast supervisor job involves an early start.","zh":"早餐主管職位需要很早開始工作。"},{"en":"An early start means beginning work or an activity early in the morning.","zh":"很早開始工作意思是在早上很早開始工作或活動。"},{"en":"A baker’s job usually involves an early start because bread must be ready before customers arrive.","zh":"麵包師工作通常需要很早開始，因為麵包必須在顧客到達前準備好。"},{"en":"Early starts can be tiring, but they may leave more free time later in the day.","zh":"很早開始工作可能令人疲倦，但也可能在一天較後時間留下更多空閒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the starting time of a day’s work.","zh":"這個短語描述一天工作的開始時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the only unattractive thing about","meaning":"……唯一不太吸引的地方","examples":[{"en":"The early start is the only unattractive thing about the job.","zh":"很早開始工作是這份工作唯一不太吸引的地方。"},{"en":"The only unattractive thing about something means the one feature that is not appealing.","zh":"某事唯一不太吸引的地方意思是唯一不吸引人的特點。"},{"en":"The only unattractive thing about the flat is that it is far from the station.","zh":"這個單位唯一不太吸引的地方是距離車站很遠。"},{"en":"A job may still be worth taking if the only unattractive thing is manageable.","zh":"如果唯一缺點可以應付，一份工作仍可能值得接受。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts one disadvantage with other positive features.","zh":"這個短語把一個缺點與其他正面特點作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have the afternoons and evenings free","meaning":"下午和晚上有空","examples":[{"en":"The job leaves the afternoons and evenings free.","zh":"這份工作讓下午和晚上有空。"},{"en":"To have the afternoons and evenings free means not to have work or fixed duties during those times.","zh":"下午和晚上有空意思是在那些時段沒有工作或固定職責。"},{"en":"A morning job lets a student have the afternoons and evenings free for study.","zh":"早上工作可以讓學生下午和晚上有空溫習。"},{"en":"Free afternoons and evenings can make an early start feel more acceptable.","zh":"下午和晚上有空可以令早起工作變得較可接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes available personal time later in the day.","zh":"這個短語描述一天較後時間可供個人使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"start serving breakfast","meaning":"開始供應早餐","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant starts serving breakfast at 7 a.m.","zh":"餐廳早上 7 時開始供應早餐。"},{"en":"To start serving breakfast means to begin offering breakfast food to customers.","zh":"開始供應早餐意思是開始向顧客提供早餐食物。"},{"en":"A hotel may start serving breakfast before guests leave for work or sightseeing.","zh":"酒店可能在住客上班或觀光前開始供應早餐。"},{"en":"Staff must prepare food and tables before breakfast service begins.","zh":"早餐服務開始前，員工必須準備食物和餐桌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of a meal service.","zh":"這個短語描述餐飲服務的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have to be there at","meaning":"必須在……到達","examples":[{"en":"The breakfast supervisor has to be there at 5.30 a.m.","zh":"早餐主管必須在早上 5 時 30 分到達。"},{"en":"To have to be there at a time means to be required to arrive at that time.","zh":"必須在某時間到達意思是被要求於該時間抵達。"},{"en":"Students have to be at the exam hall at 8.30 a.m.","zh":"學生必須在上午 8 時 30 分到達試場。"},{"en":"Early arrival may be needed when preparation must happen before customers or visitors arrive.","zh":"當準備工作必須在顧客或訪客到達前完成，可能需要早到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a required arrival time.","zh":"這個短語描述必須抵達的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"set everything up","meaning":"準備好一切","examples":[{"en":"The supervisor has to set everything up before breakfast.","zh":"主管必須在早餐前準備好一切。"},{"en":"To set everything up means to prepare all the things needed before an event or service begins.","zh":"準備好一切意思是在活動或服務開始前準備所有需要的東西。"},{"en":"Students may arrive early to set everything up for a school fair.","zh":"學生可能提早到達，為學校嘉年華準備好一切。"},{"en":"Setting everything up properly prevents delays and confusion later.","zh":"妥善準備好一切可以防止之後延誤和混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparation before an activity starts.","zh":"這個短語描述活動開始前的準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be finished at","meaning":"在……下班；在……完成工作","examples":[{"en":"The breakfast supervisor is finished at 12.30 p.m.","zh":"早餐主管在下午 12 時 30 分下班。"},{"en":"To be finished at a time means to complete work or duty at that time.","zh":"在某時間下班意思是在該時間完成工作或職責。"},{"en":"A part-time worker may be finished at 6 p.m. and go home after closing the shop.","zh":"兼職員工可能下午 6 時下班，關店後回家。"},{"en":"Knowing when work is finished helps people plan transport and personal time.","zh":"知道何時下班有助人們安排交通和私人時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an end time for work.","zh":"這個短語描述工作結束時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as you say","meaning":"正如你所說","examples":[{"en":"The man agrees by saying, “As you say, there are advantages to that.”","zh":"那名男子說：「正如你所說，那是有好處的。」以表示同意。"},{"en":"As you say means I agree with or accept the point you just made.","zh":"正如你所說意思是我同意或接受你剛才提出的觀點。"},{"en":"As you say, the early bus is less comfortable, but it is cheaper.","zh":"正如你所說，早班巴士較不舒服，但較便宜。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite because it recognises the other person’s point.","zh":"這個短語很有禮，因為它承認對方的觀點。"},{"en":"It is common in conversations when agreeing and continuing the discussion.","zh":"在對話中同意並繼續討論時，它很常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"advantages to","meaning":"……的好處","examples":[{"en":"There are advantages to finishing work early.","zh":"早下班有好處。"},{"en":"Advantages to something are the good points or benefits connected with it.","zh":"某事的好處是與它相關的優點或益處。"},{"en":"There are advantages to studying in the morning if you feel fresh then.","zh":"如果你早上精神好，早上溫習是有好處的。"},{"en":"Noticing advantages helps people decide whether a choice is worthwhile.","zh":"注意到好處有助人們決定某選擇是否值得。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing positive sides of a situation.","zh":"這個短語用於討論某情況的正面部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be interested in","meaning":"對……有興趣","examples":[{"en":"The man might also be interested in the City Road branch job.","zh":"那名男子也可能對 City Road 分店的工作有興趣。"},{"en":"To be interested in something means to want to know more about it or consider choosing it.","zh":"對某事有興趣意思是想了解更多，或考慮選擇它。"},{"en":"A student may be interested in a summer course after reading its description.","zh":"學生閱讀課程簡介後，可能對暑期課程有興趣。"},{"en":"Interest often leads people to ask more questions before making a decision.","zh":"興趣通常會令人作決定前提出更多問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes curiosity or possible preference.","zh":"這個短語描述好奇或可能的偏好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the City Road branch","meaning":"City Road 分店","examples":[{"en":"There is also a vacancy at the City Road branch.","zh":"City Road 分店也有一個職位空缺。"},{"en":"The City Road branch means the company’s location or restaurant on City Road.","zh":"City Road 分店意思是該公司位於 City Road 的地點或餐廳。"},{"en":"A bank may have different services at its central branch and its neighbourhood branch.","zh":"銀行的中環分行和社區分行可能有不同服務。"},{"en":"Mentioning the branch helps applicants know where they would work.","zh":"提及分店有助申請人知道自己會在哪裏工作。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific branch location.","zh":"這個短語指出具體分店位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"junior chef","meaning":"初級廚師","examples":[{"en":"The City Road branch is looking for a junior chef.","zh":"City Road 分店正在招聘初級廚師。"},{"en":"A junior chef is a lower-level chef who assists more senior kitchen staff and learns through work.","zh":"初級廚師是較低級別的廚師，負責協助較資深廚房員工並透過工作學習。"},{"en":"A junior chef may prepare ingredients, check stock, and support the sous chef.","zh":"初級廚師可能準備食材、檢查存貨和協助副主廚。"},{"en":"Junior roles help people gain experience before moving into more responsible positions.","zh":"初級職位幫助人們在晉升至更有責任的職位前累積經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an early-career kitchen role.","zh":"這個短語描述早期職涯的廚房職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a position of responsibility","meaning":"一個有責任的職位","examples":[{"en":"The junior chef role is also a position of responsibility.","zh":"初級廚師角色也是一個有責任的職位。"},{"en":"A position of responsibility is a job that requires careful decisions and dependable behaviour.","zh":"有責任的職位是需要謹慎決定和可靠行為的工作。"},{"en":"A class monitor has a position of responsibility because they help teachers and classmates.","zh":"班長是一個有責任的職位，因為他協助老師和同學。"},{"en":"Responsible positions can be stressful because mistakes may affect other people.","zh":"有責任的職位可能有壓力，因為錯誤可能影響其他人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a role where trust and duty are important.","zh":"這個短語描述信任和職責很重要的角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"I might prefer","meaning":"我可能比較喜歡","examples":[{"en":"The man says he might prefer the junior chef role.","zh":"那名男子說他可能比較喜歡初級廚師職位。"},{"en":"I might prefer means I may like one option more than another, but I am not completely certain yet.","zh":"我可能比較喜歡意思是我也許較喜歡其中一個選項，但仍未完全確定。"},{"en":"A student may say, “I might prefer the morning class,” after comparing the timetable.","zh":"學生比較時間表後，可能說：「我可能比較喜歡早上課。」"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone is considering choices politely.","zh":"當某人有禮貌地考慮選擇時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It sounds less definite than “I definitely prefer”.","zh":"它比「我一定比較喜歡」語氣較不肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"this role would involve","meaning":"這個職位會涉及……","examples":[{"en":"This role would involve supporting the sous chef and senior staff.","zh":"這個職位會涉及協助副主廚和資深職員。"},{"en":"This role would involve means this job would include certain duties or activities.","zh":"這個職位會涉及某事，意思是這份工作會包括某些職責或活動。"},{"en":"A school secretary role would involve answering calls and organising documents.","zh":"學校秘書職位會涉及接聽電話和整理文件。"},{"en":"Understanding what a role involves helps applicants decide whether it suits them.","zh":"了解一個職位涉及甚麼，有助申請人決定它是否適合自己。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces job responsibilities.","zh":"這個短語引入工作職責。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"support the sous chef","meaning":"協助副主廚","examples":[{"en":"The junior chef would support the sous chef.","zh":"初級廚師會協助副主廚。"},{"en":"To support the sous chef means to assist the second-in-command chef in kitchen tasks.","zh":"協助副主廚意思是幫助廚房中第二把手廚師完成任務。"},{"en":"A junior chef may support the sous chef by preparing ingredients and checking deliveries.","zh":"初級廚師可能透過準備食材和檢查送貨來協助副主廚。"},{"en":"Supporting senior staff helps the kitchen run smoothly during busy service.","zh":"協助資深員工有助廚房在繁忙服務時段順利運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes helping a higher-ranking chef.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助較高級廚師。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"senior staff","meaning":"資深職員","examples":[{"en":"The junior chef would work with the sous chef and other senior staff.","zh":"初級廚師會與副主廚和其他資深職員一起工作。"},{"en":"Senior staff are experienced or higher-ranking employees in an organisation.","zh":"資深職員是機構中有經驗或職級較高的員工。"},{"en":"New workers often learn workplace routines from senior staff.","zh":"新員工通常向資深職員學習工作常規。"},{"en":"Senior staff may make decisions, train juniors, and check work quality.","zh":"資深職員可能作決定、培訓新人和檢查工作質素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes staff with more responsibility or experience.","zh":"這個短語描述有更多責任或經驗的員工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be responsible for","meaning":"負責……","examples":[{"en":"The junior chef would be responsible for checking stock and deliveries.","zh":"初級廚師會負責檢查存貨和送貨。"},{"en":"To be responsible for something means to have the duty to manage or complete it.","zh":"負責某事意思是有職責管理或完成它。"},{"en":"A class monitor may be responsible for collecting homework every morning.","zh":"班長可能負責每天早上收功課。"},{"en":"When someone is responsible for a task, others expect them to do it carefully.","zh":"當某人負責一項任務，別人會期望他仔細完成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes duty and accountability.","zh":"這個短語描述職責和問責。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"enough stock","meaning":"足夠存貨","examples":[{"en":"The junior chef must make sure there is enough stock each week.","zh":"初級廚師必須確保每星期有足夠存貨。"},{"en":"Enough stock means sufficient supplies or goods for the expected work or sales.","zh":"足夠存貨意思是有足夠供應品或貨品應付預期工作或銷售。"},{"en":"A shop needs enough stock of bottled water before a hot weekend.","zh":"炎熱週末前，商店需要有足夠樽裝水存貨。"},{"en":"If there is not enough stock, customers may be disappointed and sales may be lost.","zh":"如果沒有足夠存貨，顧客可能失望，銷售也可能流失。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in shops, restaurants, and warehouses.","zh":"這個短語常見於商店、餐廳和貨倉。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"each week","meaning":"每星期","examples":[{"en":"The junior chef checks the stock each week.","zh":"初級廚師每星期檢查存貨。"},{"en":"Each week means every week.","zh":"每星期意思是每一週。"},{"en":"A teacher may check students’ reading records each week.","zh":"老師可能每星期檢查學生的閱讀紀錄。"},{"en":"Tasks done each week become part of a regular routine.","zh":"每星期完成的任務會成為定期常規的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weekly frequency.","zh":"這個短語描述每週頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sort out deliveries","meaning":"處理送貨安排","examples":[{"en":"The junior chef must sort out all the deliveries.","zh":"初級廚師必須處理所有送貨安排。"},{"en":"To sort out deliveries means to organise, check, and deal with goods that arrive.","zh":"處理送貨安排意思是整理、核對和處理送到的貨物。"},{"en":"A shop assistant may sort out deliveries by checking invoices and putting products on shelves.","zh":"店員可能透過核對發票和把產品放上貨架來處理送貨安排。"},{"en":"Sorting out deliveries properly prevents missing items and stock confusion.","zh":"妥善處理送貨安排可以防止物品遺漏和存貨混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical organisation of arriving goods.","zh":"這個短語描述對到貨物品的實際整理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"I’ve never done that before","meaning":"我以前未做過那件事","examples":[{"en":"The man says he has never sorted out deliveries before.","zh":"那名男子說他以前從未處理過送貨安排。"},{"en":"I’ve never done that before means I have no previous experience of that task.","zh":"我以前未做過那件事意思是我沒有該任務的過往經驗。"},{"en":"A student may say, “I’ve never done that before,” before trying a science experiment.","zh":"學生在嘗試科學實驗前可能說：「我以前未做過那件事。」"},{"en":"People may need training or support when they have never done a task before.","zh":"當人們以前未做過一項任務，可能需要培訓或支援。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses lack of experience, not refusal.","zh":"這個短語表達缺乏經驗，而不是拒絕。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fairly straightforward","meaning":"頗簡單直接","examples":[{"en":"The man imagines that the task is fairly straightforward.","zh":"那名男子想像該任務頗簡單直接。"},{"en":"Fairly straightforward means quite simple and not too difficult to understand.","zh":"頗簡單直接意思是相當簡單，而且不太難理解。"},{"en":"Filling in a basic application form is usually fairly straightforward.","zh":"填寫基本申請表通常頗簡單直接。"},{"en":"A task may become straightforward once the steps are explained clearly.","zh":"當步驟被清楚解釋，一項任務可能變得簡單直接。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something manageable rather than complicated.","zh":"這個短語描述可應付而不是複雜的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"once you get the hang of it","meaning":"一旦掌握竅門","examples":[{"en":"The task should be straightforward once he gets the hang of it.","zh":"一旦他掌握竅門，這項任務應該頗簡單直接。"},{"en":"Once you get the hang of it means after you understand how to do it through practice.","zh":"一旦掌握竅門意思是透過練習明白如何做之後。"},{"en":"Cycling feels difficult at first, but it becomes easier once you get the hang of it.","zh":"踩單車起初感覺困難，但一旦掌握竅門就會較容易。"},{"en":"Practice helps people get the hang of new routines and stop feeling nervous.","zh":"練習幫助人掌握新常規的竅門，並不再緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning a skill until it feels natural.","zh":"這個短語描述學會一項技能，直到它感覺自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"work alongside","meaning":"與……一起工作","examples":[{"en":"The man would work alongside more experienced staff at first.","zh":"那名男子起初會與較有經驗的職員一起工作。"},{"en":"To work alongside someone means to work with them in the same place or on the same task.","zh":"與某人一起工作意思是在同一地方或同一任務上與他合作。"},{"en":"A new nurse may work alongside senior nurses during the first week.","zh":"新護士第一星期可能與資深護士一起工作。"},{"en":"Working alongside experienced people helps beginners learn by watching and asking questions.","zh":"與有經驗的人一起工作，有助新手透過觀察和發問來學習。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests cooperation and guidance.","zh":"這個短語暗示合作和指導。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"experienced staff","meaning":"有經驗的職員","examples":[{"en":"The man would begin by working with more experienced staff.","zh":"那名男子會先與較有經驗的職員一起工作。"},{"en":"Experienced staff are workers who have done the job for some time and know it well.","zh":"有經驗的職員是已做該工作一段時間並很熟悉它的員工。"},{"en":"Experienced staff can show new employees how to handle busy periods.","zh":"有經驗的職員可以向新員工示範如何處理繁忙時段。"},{"en":"Learning from experienced staff can reduce mistakes and build confidence.","zh":"向有經驗的職員學習可以減少錯誤並建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes workers with practical knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述有實際知識的員工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"to begin with","meaning":"起初；一開始","examples":[{"en":"To begin with, he would work alongside more experienced staff.","zh":"起初，他會與較有經驗的職員一起工作。"},{"en":"To begin with means at the start or during the first stage.","zh":"起初或一開始意思是在開始或第一階段。"},{"en":"To begin with, new chefs may only prepare simple ingredients.","zh":"起初，新廚師可能只準備簡單食材。"},{"en":"Starting with support helps beginners learn safely before working alone.","zh":"一開始有人支援，有助新手在獨自工作前安全學習。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the first stage of a process.","zh":"這個短語引入過程的第一階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"it wouldn’t be a problem","meaning":"這不會成問題","examples":[{"en":"The woman is sure the stock duties would not be a problem.","zh":"那名女子肯定存貨職責不會成問題。"},{"en":"It wouldn’t be a problem means the situation or task would be manageable and not difficult.","zh":"這不會成問題意思是該情況或任務可以應付，而且不困難。"},{"en":"If the school provides clear instructions, filling in the form would not be a problem.","zh":"如果學校提供清楚指示，填寫表格不會成問題。"},{"en":"People say this to reassure someone who is worried about a task.","zh":"人們用這句話安慰擔心某任務的人。"},{"en":"This phrase shows confidence that something can be handled.","zh":"這個短語顯示有信心某事可以處理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"slightly higher","meaning":"稍高","examples":[{"en":"The salary for the junior chef role is slightly higher.","zh":"初級廚師職位的薪金稍高。"},{"en":"Slightly higher means a little more than another amount or level.","zh":"稍高意思是比另一數額或水平多一點。"},{"en":"A shop may charge a slightly higher price for fresh fruit than for canned fruit.","zh":"商店可能對新鮮水果收取比罐頭水果稍高的價格。"},{"en":"A slightly higher salary can make one job more attractive than another.","zh":"稍高薪金可以令一份工作比另一份更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small increase or difference.","zh":"這個短語描述小幅增加或差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an annual salary of","meaning":"年薪為……","examples":[{"en":"The junior chef role has an annual salary of £23,000.","zh":"初級廚師職位年薪為 £23,000。"},{"en":"An annual salary of an amount means that total pay is earned over one year.","zh":"年薪為某金額意思是一年內賺取該總薪酬。"},{"en":"A job advertisement may offer an annual salary of £30,000 plus benefits.","zh":"招聘廣告可能提供年薪 £30,000 加福利。"},{"en":"Annual salary helps applicants compare full-time jobs more easily than hourly pay alone.","zh":"年薪比單看時薪更有助申請人比較全職工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes yearly income from a job.","zh":"這個短語描述一份工作的每年收入。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"if they like you","meaning":"如果他們欣賞你","examples":[{"en":"If they like the man, he may be promoted quickly.","zh":"如果他們欣賞那名男子，他可能很快獲晉升。"},{"en":"If they like you means if the employer or managers are impressed by you and your work.","zh":"如果他們欣賞你意思是如果僱主或經理對你和你的工作印象良好。"},{"en":"If they like you during the interview, they may invite you for a trial shift.","zh":"如果他們在面試中欣賞你，可能會邀請你試工。"},{"en":"Managers are more likely to promote workers they trust and value.","zh":"經理較可能晉升他們信任和重視的員工。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and refers to positive approval from decision-makers.","zh":"這個短語較口語，指決策者的正面認可。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be promoted quite quickly","meaning":"很快獲晉升","examples":[{"en":"The man is likely to be promoted quite quickly if the company likes him.","zh":"如果公司欣賞他，那名男子很可能很快獲晉升。"},{"en":"To be promoted quite quickly means to move to a higher job position after a short time.","zh":"很快獲晉升意思是在短時間後升到更高職位。"},{"en":"A hardworking assistant may be promoted quickly if they show leadership and reliability.","zh":"勤奮助理如果展現領導力和可靠性，可能很快獲晉升。"},{"en":"Quick promotion can motivate employees because they see a future in the company.","zh":"快速晉升可以激勵員工，因為他們看見在公司的前途。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fast career progress.","zh":"這個短語描述快速職涯進展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be worth thinking about","meaning":"值得考慮","examples":[{"en":"The possibility of promotion is worth thinking about.","zh":"晉升可能性值得考慮。"},{"en":"To be worth thinking about means to deserve careful consideration.","zh":"值得考慮意思是值得仔細思考。"},{"en":"A lower-paid job with excellent training may still be worth thinking about.","zh":"薪金較低但培訓很好的工作仍可能值得考慮。"},{"en":"People consider future opportunities before deciding whether a job suits them.","zh":"人們在決定工作是否適合自己前，會考慮未來機會。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an option should not be dismissed quickly.","zh":"這個短語暗示不應太快排除某選項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sound interesting","meaning":"聽起來有意思","examples":[{"en":"The junior chef role sounds interesting to the man.","zh":"初級廚師職位對那名男子來說聽起來有意思。"},{"en":"Sound interesting means seem attractive or worth learning more about.","zh":"聽起來有意思意思是看似吸引或值得進一步了解。"},{"en":"A science club may sound interesting if students can do real experiments.","zh":"如果學生可以做真正實驗，科學學會可能聽起來有意思。"},{"en":"Something that sounds interesting may encourage people to ask for more details.","zh":"聽起來有意思的事情可能鼓勵人們詢問更多細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive reaction to an idea or offer.","zh":"這個短語描述對想法或提議的正面反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"what are the hours like?","meaning":"工作時間是怎樣的？","examples":[{"en":"The man asks what the working hours are like.","zh":"那名男子問工作時間是怎樣的。"},{"en":"“What are the hours like?” means asking about the work schedule and when shifts begin or end.","zh":"「工作時間是怎樣的？」意思是詢問工作時間表，以及班次何時開始或結束。"},{"en":"A job applicant may ask what the hours are like before deciding whether the role fits their life.","zh":"求職者可能在決定職位是否配合生活前，詢問工作時間是怎樣的。"},{"en":"Working hours affect transport, rest, family time, and study plans.","zh":"工作時間影響交通、休息、家庭時間和學習安排。"},{"en":"This question is common in job interviews and job enquiries.","zh":"這個問題常見於求職面試和職位查詢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the usual","meaning":"一般情況；通常那樣","examples":[{"en":"The hours are the usual for restaurant work.","zh":"工作時間是餐廳工作的一般情況。"},{"en":"The usual means what normally happens or what people generally expect.","zh":"一般情況或通常那樣意思是平常發生或人們一般預期的情況。"},{"en":"The shop opens at the usual time even during the school holiday.","zh":"商店即使在學校假期也按通常時間開門。"},{"en":"In restaurant work, the usual hours may include evenings and weekends.","zh":"在餐廳工作中，一般工時可能包括晚上和週末。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a normal pattern.","zh":"這個短語指正常模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"evening and weekend work","meaning":"晚上及週末工作","examples":[{"en":"The junior chef role involves a lot of evening and weekend work.","zh":"初級廚師職位涉及大量晚上及週末工作。"},{"en":"Evening and weekend work means working outside normal weekday daytime hours.","zh":"晚上及週末工作意思是在平日白天正常工作時間以外工作。"},{"en":"Restaurant jobs often include evening and weekend work because customers eat out then.","zh":"餐廳工作常包括晚上及週末工作，因為顧客那時會外出用餐。"},{"en":"Evening and weekend work can be difficult for people with family or study commitments.","zh":"對有家庭或學習責任的人來說，晚上及週末工作可能困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a work schedule that includes nights and weekends.","zh":"這個短語描述包括晚上和週末的工作時間表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be closed on Mondays","meaning":"逢星期一休息","examples":[{"en":"The City Road branch is closed on Mondays.","zh":"City Road 分店逢星期一休息。"},{"en":"To be closed on Mondays means not to open for business every Monday.","zh":"逢星期一休息意思是每個星期一不營業。"},{"en":"Some restaurants are closed on Mondays because staff need a regular rest day.","zh":"有些餐廳逢星期一休息，因為員工需要固定休息日。"},{"en":"If a shop is closed on Mondays, customers must visit on another day.","zh":"如果商店逢星期一休息，顧客必須改天到訪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a regular weekly closing day.","zh":"這個短語描述每週固定休息日。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"get one Sunday off","meaning":"有一個星期日休息","examples":[{"en":"Staff get one Sunday off every four weeks.","zh":"員工每四星期有一個星期日休息。"},{"en":"To get one Sunday off means to have one Sunday when you do not need to work.","zh":"有一個星期日休息意思是有一個星期日不用上班。"},{"en":"A nurse may get one weekend off each month if the hospital schedule allows it.","zh":"如果醫院更表允許，護士可能每月有一個週末休息。"},{"en":"Having a Sunday off can help workers rest or spend time with family.","zh":"有星期日休息可以幫助員工休息或陪伴家人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific day of leave from work.","zh":"這個短語描述特定一天不用上班。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"every four weeks","meaning":"每四星期","examples":[{"en":"Staff get one Sunday off every four weeks.","zh":"員工每四星期有一個星期日休息。"},{"en":"Every four weeks means once in each four-week period.","zh":"每四星期意思是在每一個四星期期間一次。"},{"en":"A club may hold a members’ meeting every four weeks.","zh":"俱樂部可能每四星期舉行一次會員會議。"},{"en":"A regular four-week cycle helps workers know when their rest day will come.","zh":"固定四星期循環有助員工知道自己的休息日何時到來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeating schedule.","zh":"這個短語描述重複時間表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 10/task-2":[{"front":"members of the public","meaning":"市民；公眾人士","examples":[{"en":"Many members of the public have shown up for the presentation.","zh":"許多市民出席了介紹會。"},{"en":"Members of the public are ordinary people in society, not officials or invited specialists.","zh":"members of the public 指社會上的普通人，而不是官員或受邀專家。"},{"en":"Members of the public can use the library, attend council meetings, and ask questions about local plans.","zh":"市民可以使用圖書館、出席區議會會議，並詢問本地計劃。"},{"en":"When many members of the public attend a meeting, it shows that the issue affects the community.","zh":"當許多公眾人士出席會議，顯示該議題影響社區。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in formal notices, public services, and government discussions.","zh":"這個片語常見於正式告示、公共服務和政府討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"show up for","meaning":"出席；現身參加","examples":[{"en":"Many people have shown up for the presentation on the new housing development.","zh":"許多人出席了關於新住宅發展項目的介紹會。"},{"en":"To show up for an event means to arrive and attend it.","zh":"show up for an event 指到達並參加某活動。"},{"en":"Students should show up for the school meeting if they want to vote.","zh":"如果學生想投票，就應出席學校會議。"},{"en":"If few residents show up for a consultation, planners may not hear enough local opinions.","zh":"如果很少居民出席諮詢會，規劃者可能聽不到足夠本地意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is more casual than “attend” but has a similar meaning.","zh":"這個片語比 “attend” 較口語，但意思相近。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"presentation on","meaning":"關於……的介紹會","examples":[{"en":"The presentation is on the new housing development planned near Nunston.","zh":"這場介紹會是關於計劃在 Nunston 附近興建的新住宅發展項目。"},{"en":"A presentation on something is a talk that explains information about that topic.","zh":"presentation on something 指解釋某主題資料的講解或匯報。"},{"en":"A student may give a presentation on climate change in geography class.","zh":"學生可能在地理課做關於氣候變化的匯報。"},{"en":"Presentations help audiences understand plans before they ask questions or make decisions.","zh":"介紹會幫助聽眾在提問或作決定前理解計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the subject of a talk or briefing.","zh":"這個片語引出講座或簡報的主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"housing development","meaning":"住宅發展項目","examples":[{"en":"The presentation is about a new housing development on the outskirts of Nunston.","zh":"介紹會是關於 Nunston 市郊一個新住宅發展項目。"},{"en":"A housing development is a planned area of new homes, often with roads and facilities.","zh":"housing development 指一個規劃好的新住宅區，通常包括道路和設施。"},{"en":"A housing development may include houses, apartment blocks, shops, and public spaces.","zh":"住宅發展項目可能包括獨立屋、住宅大廈、商店和公共空間。"},{"en":"New housing developments can reduce housing shortages, but they may also affect traffic and farmland.","zh":"新住宅發展項目可以減少住房短缺，但也可能影響交通和農地。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a planned residential project, not one single house.","zh":"這個片語指規劃中的住宅項目，而不是單一房屋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"planned on the outskirts of","meaning":"計劃設於……市郊","examples":[{"en":"The new housing development is planned on the outskirts of Nunston.","zh":"新住宅發展項目計劃設於 Nunston 市郊。"},{"en":"Planned on the outskirts of a place means intended to be built near the edge of that town or city.","zh":"planned on the outskirts of a place 指計劃在某城鎮或城市邊緣興建。"},{"en":"A new sports centre may be planned on the outskirts of a town where land is cheaper.","zh":"新體育中心可能計劃設於市郊，因為土地較便宜。"},{"en":"Building on the outskirts can provide space, but it may require better roads and transport.","zh":"在市郊興建可提供空間，但可能需要更好的道路和交通。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a future project with a location outside the main centre.","zh":"這個片語把未來項目與主要中心外的位置連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"outskirts of","meaning":"……的市郊","examples":[{"en":"The development will be built on the outskirts of Nunston.","zh":"該發展項目將建於 Nunston 的市郊。"},{"en":"The outskirts of a place are the outer areas near the edge of a town or city.","zh":"outskirts of a place 指城鎮或城市邊緣附近的外圍地區。"},{"en":"Some families live on the outskirts of the city because homes are larger there.","zh":"有些家庭住在城市市郊，因為那裡的房屋較大。"},{"en":"Outskirts often have more open land, but shops and schools may be farther away.","zh":"市郊通常有更多空地，但商店和學校可能較遠。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the edge of a place with its town centre.","zh":"這個片語把地方邊緣與市中心作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Communications Manager","meaning":"傳訊經理","examples":[{"en":"Mark Reynolds is Communications Manager at the development.","zh":"Mark Reynolds 是該發展項目的傳訊經理。"},{"en":"A Communications Manager is a person responsible for sharing information clearly with the public, staff, or media.","zh":"Communications Manager 指負責向公眾、員工或傳媒清楚傳達資訊的人。"},{"en":"A school’s Communications Manager may write notices and answer parents’ questions.","zh":"學校的傳訊經理可能撰寫通告並回答家長問題。"},{"en":"Good communication can reduce confusion when a large project affects many residents.","zh":"當大型項目影響許多居民，良好傳訊可以減少混亂。"},{"en":"This job title focuses on public information, not building work itself.","zh":"這個職銜着重公共資訊，而不是建築工程本身。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"start by","meaning":"首先做……","examples":[{"en":"Mark will start by giving a brief overview of the plans.","zh":"Mark 會首先簡要概述計劃。"},{"en":"To start by doing something means to do that action first before moving on to other points.","zh":"start by doing something 指先做某行動，然後再進入其他重點。"},{"en":"A teacher may start by explaining the task before students begin group work.","zh":"老師可能首先解釋任務，然後學生才開始小組活動。"},{"en":"Starting with an overview helps listeners understand the whole topic before details appear.","zh":"先作概述有助聽眾在聽細節前理解整個主題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when organising speeches, meetings, and lessons.","zh":"這個片語適合用於組織演講、會議和課堂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"give a brief overview of","meaning":"簡要概述……","examples":[{"en":"Mark gives a brief overview of the plans for the development.","zh":"Mark 簡要概述該發展項目的計劃。"},{"en":"To give a brief overview of something means to explain the main points shortly.","zh":"give a brief overview of something 指簡短解釋主要重點。"},{"en":"A student may give a brief overview of a book before discussing its characters.","zh":"學生可能先簡要概述一本書，然後討論人物。"},{"en":"A brief overview helps people understand the topic without too much detail at the start.","zh":"簡要概述幫助人們在一開始不用面對太多細節也能理解主題。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in presentations, reports, and meetings.","zh":"這個片語常見於簡報、報告和會議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"plans for the development","meaning":"發展項目的計劃","examples":[{"en":"Mark explains the plans for the development.","zh":"Mark 解釋發展項目的計劃。"},{"en":"Plans for the development are the proposed designs, facilities, buildings, and arrangements for the project.","zh":"plans for the development 指該項目的擬議設計、設施、建築物和安排。"},{"en":"Residents may ask to see the plans for the development before construction begins.","zh":"居民可能在工程開始前要求查看發展項目的計劃。"},{"en":"Clear plans help people understand what will be built and how the area may change.","zh":"清晰計劃幫助人們理解將會興建甚麼，以及該區可能如何改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the project’s intended future layout and features.","zh":"這個片語指項目未來的佈局和特色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one thing I’m sure","meaning":"我肯定的一件事","examples":[{"en":"One thing Mark is sure people want to know is why the site was selected.","zh":"Mark 肯定大家想知道的一件事，是為甚麼選擇這個地點。"},{"en":"One thing I’m sure means one point the speaker feels confident about.","zh":"one thing I’m sure 指說話者很有信心的一點。"},{"en":"One thing I’m sure students want is clearer exam instructions.","zh":"我肯定學生想要的一件事，是更清楚的考試指示。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase when they predict what the audience is most concerned about.","zh":"說話者預測聽眾最關心甚麼時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a confident observation before giving an explanation.","zh":"這個片語在解釋前引入一個有信心的觀察。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"want to know","meaning":"想知道","examples":[{"en":"Residents want to know why this site was selected.","zh":"居民想知道為甚麼選擇這個地點。"},{"en":"To want to know means to wish to get information or an explanation.","zh":"want to know 指希望得到資料或解釋。"},{"en":"Parents want to know whether the school trip will be safe.","zh":"家長想知道學校旅行是否安全。"},{"en":"When people are affected by a decision, they naturally want to know the reasons behind it.","zh":"當人們受某決定影響，他們自然想知道背後原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for introducing public questions or concerns.","zh":"這個片語適合用來引入公眾問題或憂慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"select this particular site","meaning":"選擇這個特定地點","examples":[{"en":"The company selected this particular site for a housing development.","zh":"該公司選擇這個特定地點作住宅發展項目。"},{"en":"To select this particular site means to choose this exact location rather than another one.","zh":"select this particular site 指選擇這個確切位置，而不是其他地方。"},{"en":"A school may select a particular site for a new sports hall because it is near the playground.","zh":"學校可能選擇某個特定地點興建新體育館，因為它接近操場。"},{"en":"Choosing a site affects transport, cost, noise, and nearby residents.","zh":"選址會影響交通、成本、噪音和附近居民。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the exact location was chosen for reasons.","zh":"這個片語強調確切地點是有原因地被選中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at present","meaning":"目前；現時","examples":[{"en":"At present, the site is being used for farming.","zh":"目前，該地點被用作農業用途。"},{"en":"At present means now or at the current time.","zh":"at present 指現在或目前。"},{"en":"At present, the library is closed for repairs.","zh":"目前，圖書館因維修而關閉。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the situation may change later.","zh":"這個片語顯示情況之後可能會改變。"},{"en":"It is more formal than “now” and is common in reports or presentations.","zh":"它比 “now” 較正式，常見於報告或介紹會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be used for farming","meaning":"被用作農業用途","examples":[{"en":"The land is being used for farming at present.","zh":"該土地目前被用作農業用途。"},{"en":"To be used for farming means the land is used to grow crops or raise animals.","zh":"be used for farming 指土地被用來種植農作物或飼養動物。"},{"en":"Fields outside a town may be used for farming before new buildings are planned.","zh":"城鎮外的田地在規劃新建築前，可能被用作農業用途。"},{"en":"If farming land becomes housing, local food production and landscape may change.","zh":"如果農地變成住宅，本地食物生產和景觀可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the current purpose of land.","zh":"這個片語描述土地目前的用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"much of the land around","meaning":"……周邊大部分土地","examples":[{"en":"Much of the land around Nunston is used for farming.","zh":"Nunston 周邊大部分土地被用作農業用途。"},{"en":"Much of the land around a place means a large part of the nearby area.","zh":"much of the land around a place 指某地附近一大部分土地。"},{"en":"Much of the land around the school is used for sports fields and gardens.","zh":"學校周邊大部分土地用作運動場和花園。"},{"en":"If much of the nearby land is farmland, new development may attract public concern.","zh":"如果附近大部分土地是農地，新發展項目可能引起公眾關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large surrounding area, not one small plot.","zh":"這個片語描述大範圍周邊地區，而不是一小塊土地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"industrial centre","meaning":"工業中心","examples":[{"en":"There is a new industrial centre in Nunston.","zh":"Nunston 有一個新的工業中心。"},{"en":"An industrial centre is an area with factories, warehouses, offices, or businesses related to production.","zh":"industrial centre 指有工廠、倉庫、辦公室或與生產相關企業的區域。"},{"en":"A town with an industrial centre may need more housing for workers.","zh":"有工業中心的城鎮可能需要更多住房給工人。"},{"en":"Industrial centres can create jobs, but they can also increase traffic and demand for services.","zh":"工業中心可以創造職位，但也會增加交通和服務需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place focused on work and industry.","zh":"這個片語描述以工作和工業為重點的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"demand for housing","meaning":"對住房的需求","examples":[{"en":"There is a lot of demand for housing in the region.","zh":"該區對住房有很大需求。"},{"en":"Demand for housing means many people need or want places to live.","zh":"demand for housing 指許多人需要或想要住處。"},{"en":"A new university can create demand for housing when many students move nearby.","zh":"新大學會在許多學生搬到附近時創造對住房的需求。"},{"en":"High demand for housing can push up rents and make homes harder to find.","zh":"對住房的高需求會推高租金，並令住屋更難尋找。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in planning, property, and community discussions.","zh":"這個片語常見於規劃、地產和社區討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"employees in the region","meaning":"區內僱員","examples":[{"en":"The new homes are needed for employees in the region.","zh":"新住宅是為區內僱員所需。"},{"en":"Employees in the region are people who work in that local area.","zh":"employees in the region 指在該本地區域工作的人。"},{"en":"Employees in the region may include factory workers, teachers, hospital staff, and shop assistants.","zh":"區內僱員可能包括工廠工人、教師、醫院職員和店員。"},{"en":"If employees cannot live near work, they may spend more time and money commuting.","zh":"如果僱員不能住在工作地附近，他們可能花更多時間和金錢通勤。"},{"en":"This phrase links workers with the area where they are employed.","zh":"這個片語把工作者與其受僱地區連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have to commute","meaning":"需要通勤","examples":[{"en":"Many employees have to commute long distances.","zh":"許多僱員需要長距離通勤。"},{"en":"To have to commute means to need to travel regularly between home and work or school.","zh":"have to commute 指需要定期往返住所與工作地或學校。"},{"en":"Some teachers have to commute by train for over an hour every morning.","zh":"有些老師每天早上需要乘火車通勤超過一小時。"},{"en":"Long commutes can make workers tired before the day even begins.","zh":"長時間通勤會令工人在一天開始前已感疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests regular travel is necessary, not optional.","zh":"這個片語暗示定期出行是必要的，而不是可選的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"commute long distances","meaning":"長距離通勤","examples":[{"en":"Many employees are having to commute long distances at present.","zh":"目前，許多僱員需要長距離通勤。"},{"en":"To commute long distances means to travel far between home and work regularly.","zh":"commute long distances 指定期在住所和工作地之間遠距離出行。"},{"en":"A nurse may commute long distances if there is no affordable housing near the hospital.","zh":"如果醫院附近沒有可負擔住房，護士可能需要長距離通勤。"},{"en":"Long-distance commuting can increase stress, fuel use, and time away from family.","zh":"長距離通勤會增加壓力、燃油使用和離開家庭的時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical problem caused by living far from work.","zh":"這個片語描述住得離工作地遠造成的實際問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"international airport","meaning":"國際機場","examples":[{"en":"There is an international airport just 20 minutes’ drive away.","zh":"附近有一個國際機場，只有 20 分鐘車程。"},{"en":"An international airport is an airport with flights to and from other countries.","zh":"international airport 指有往返其他國家航班的機場。"},{"en":"A city near an international airport may attract hotels, offices, and visitors.","zh":"靠近國際機場的城市可能吸引酒店、辦公室和訪客。"},{"en":"Airport access can help businesses, but it may also bring noise and traffic.","zh":"機場交通可以幫助企業，但也可能帶來噪音和交通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transport infrastructure connecting a region to the world.","zh":"這個片語描述把地區與世界連接起來的交通基建。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"20 minutes’ drive away","meaning":"20分鐘車程以外","examples":[{"en":"The airport is just 20 minutes’ drive away.","zh":"機場只有 20 分鐘車程。"},{"en":"Twenty minutes’ drive away means it takes about twenty minutes to reach by car.","zh":"20 minutes’ drive away 指駕車大約二十分鐘可到達。"},{"en":"The hospital is ten minutes’ drive away from the school.","zh":"醫院距離學校十分鐘車程。"},{"en":"Saying a place is a short drive away helps people understand practical distance.","zh":"說某地方只是短車程，可以幫助人理解實際距離。"},{"en":"This phrase measures distance by travel time rather than kilometres.","zh":"這個片語用行車時間而不是公里數量度距離。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"major criteria","meaning":"主要準則","examples":[{"en":"The airport was not one of the major criteria for choosing the site.","zh":"機場並不是選址的主要準則之一。"},{"en":"Major criteria are the most important standards used for making a decision.","zh":"major criteria 指作決定時使用的最重要標準。"},{"en":"Safety and cost may be major criteria when a school chooses a bus company.","zh":"學校選擇巴士公司時，安全和成本可能是主要準則。"},{"en":"Clear criteria help decision-makers explain why one option was chosen over another.","zh":"清晰準則幫助決策者解釋為何選擇某個選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in planning or evaluation.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常見於規劃或評估。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"choosing the site","meaning":"選址","examples":[{"en":"The hospital was important when choosing the site.","zh":"選址時，醫院是一個重要因素。"},{"en":"Choosing the site means selecting the location where something will be built or placed.","zh":"choosing the site 指選擇某物將要興建或放置的位置。"},{"en":"When choosing the site for a school, planners consider safety, transport, and nearby families.","zh":"選擇學校地點時，規劃者會考慮安全、交通和附近家庭。"},{"en":"Poor site choice can create traffic problems or make services hard to reach.","zh":"選址不佳可能造成交通問題，或令服務難以到達。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on location decisions.","zh":"這個片語着重地點決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be more interested in","meaning":"對……更感興趣","examples":[{"en":"The planners were more interested in the nearby hospital.","zh":"規劃者對附近醫院更感興趣。"},{"en":"To be more interested in something means to care about it more than another factor.","zh":"be more interested in something 指比另一因素更重視某事。"},{"en":"Parents may be more interested in school safety than in the colour of the uniform.","zh":"家長可能比校服顏色更重視學校安全。"},{"en":"Planners may focus on hospitals and schools because residents need services close to home.","zh":"規劃者可能重視醫院和學校，因為居民需要接近住所的服務。"},{"en":"This phrase compares priorities.","zh":"這個片語比較優先次序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"excellent hospital","meaning":"非常好的醫院","examples":[{"en":"There is an excellent hospital just 15 kilometres away.","zh":"距離 15 公里處有一間非常好的醫院。"},{"en":"An excellent hospital is a very good hospital with reliable care, staff, and facilities.","zh":"excellent hospital 指有可靠醫療、職員和設施的優質醫院。"},{"en":"Families may feel safer living near an excellent hospital.","zh":"住在非常好的醫院附近，家庭可能感到更安全。"},{"en":"Good medical services can make a housing development more attractive to residents.","zh":"良好醫療服務可以令住宅發展項目對居民更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase praises the quality of healthcare nearby.","zh":"這個片語讚賞附近醫療質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"even closer than that","meaning":"比那個更近","examples":[{"en":"A large secondary school is even closer than the hospital.","zh":"一間大型中學比醫院更近。"},{"en":"Even closer than that means nearer than the place or distance just mentioned.","zh":"even closer than that 指比剛才提及的地方或距離更近。"},{"en":"The library is five minutes away, and the bus stop is even closer than that.","zh":"圖書館距離五分鐘，而巴士站比那個更近。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare nearby facilities in a clear way.","zh":"這個片語有助清楚比較附近設施。"},{"en":"It emphasises that one place is not only close, but closer than another.","zh":"它強調某地方不只是近，而且比另一地方更近。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"one drawback to","meaning":"……的一個缺點","examples":[{"en":"One drawback to the site is that it is on a steep slope.","zh":"該地點的一個缺點是它位於陡斜坡上。"},{"en":"One drawback to something means one disadvantage or problem connected with it.","zh":"one drawback to something 指與某事相關的一個缺點或問題。"},{"en":"One drawback to living far from school is the long journey every morning.","zh":"住得離學校遠的一個缺點是每天早上路程很長。"},{"en":"Identifying drawbacks helps planners prepare solutions before problems become serious.","zh":"找出缺點有助規劃者在問題變嚴重前準備解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a negative point in a balanced discussion.","zh":"這個片語在平衡討論中引入負面重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"steep slope","meaning":"陡斜坡","examples":[{"en":"The site is on quite a steep slope.","zh":"該地點位於相當陡的斜坡上。"},{"en":"A steep slope is land that rises or falls sharply.","zh":"steep slope 指急劇上升或下降的土地。"},{"en":"Walking up a steep slope can be difficult for elderly residents or people with pushchairs.","zh":"對長者或推嬰兒車的人來說，走上陡斜坡可能很困難。"},{"en":"Building on a steep slope may require careful engineering and drainage.","zh":"在陡斜坡上建設可能需要仔細工程和排水安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes land shape and possible construction difficulty.","zh":"這個片語描述土地形狀和可能的建築困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take account of","meaning":"考慮到","examples":[{"en":"The planners have taken account of the steep slope.","zh":"規劃者已考慮到陡斜坡。"},{"en":"To take account of something means to consider it when making plans or decisions.","zh":"take account of something 指在規劃或決策時考慮某事。"},{"en":"Schools must take account of students’ different needs when planning lessons.","zh":"學校規劃課堂時必須考慮到學生的不同需要。"},{"en":"If planners take account of risks early, they can design safer solutions.","zh":"如果規劃者及早考慮風險，就能設計更安全的解決方案。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and useful in planning or reports.","zh":"這個片語較正式，適合用於規劃或報告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in our planning","meaning":"在我們的規劃中","examples":[{"en":"The company has taken account of the slope in its planning.","zh":"公司已在規劃中考慮到斜坡。"},{"en":"In our planning means during the process of designing or organising a future project.","zh":"in our planning 指在設計或組織未來項目的過程中。"},{"en":"In our planning, we considered traffic, safety, and cost.","zh":"在我們的規劃中，我們考慮了交通、安全和成本。"},{"en":"Careful planning can prevent avoidable problems after construction begins.","zh":"仔細規劃可以避免工程開始後出現可避免的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a decision with the planning process.","zh":"這個片語把某決定與規劃過程連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"major problem","meaning":"主要問題","examples":[{"en":"The steep slope should not be a major problem.","zh":"陡斜坡應該不會是主要問題。"},{"en":"A major problem is a serious difficulty that can strongly affect a plan.","zh":"major problem 指會嚴重影響計劃的重大困難。"},{"en":"Lack of buses can be a major problem for students living far from school.","zh":"對住得離學校遠的學生來說，缺乏巴士可能是主要問題。"},{"en":"If a problem is not major, it can usually be managed with planning.","zh":"如果問題不是主要問題，通常可以透過規劃處理。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate serious issues from smaller concerns.","zh":"這個片語有助區分嚴重問題和較小憂慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"positive feedback","meaning":"正面回饋","examples":[{"en":"The company has received a lot of positive feedback about the plans.","zh":"公司收到很多關於計劃的正面回饋。"},{"en":"Positive feedback means comments showing approval, support, or satisfaction.","zh":"positive feedback 指表示認同、支持或滿意的意見。"},{"en":"A teacher may receive positive feedback after making lessons clearer.","zh":"老師令課堂更清楚後，可能收到正面回饋。"},{"en":"Positive feedback can encourage planners to keep parts of a design that people like.","zh":"正面回饋可以鼓勵規劃者保留人們喜歡的設計部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes favourable responses, not criticism.","zh":"這個片語描述有利回應，而不是批評。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"wide variety of","meaning":"種類繁多的……","examples":[{"en":"People like the wide variety of accommodation types and prices.","zh":"人們喜歡種類繁多的住屋類型和價格。"},{"en":"A wide variety of something means many different kinds are available.","zh":"wide variety of something 指有許多不同種類可供選擇。"},{"en":"A library with a wide variety of books can serve readers of different ages.","zh":"有種類繁多書籍的圖書館可以服務不同年齡讀者。"},{"en":"Variety helps people choose something that matches their needs and budget.","zh":"多樣性幫助人們選擇符合需要和預算的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises choice and diversity.","zh":"這個片語強調選擇和多元性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"accommodation types","meaning":"住宿類型；住屋類型","examples":[{"en":"The development offers a wide variety of accommodation types.","zh":"該發展項目提供種類繁多的住屋類型。"},{"en":"Accommodation types are different kinds of homes or places where people can live.","zh":"accommodation types 指不同類型的住所或可居住地方。"},{"en":"Accommodation types may include houses, flats, studios, and homes for older residents.","zh":"住屋類型可能包括獨立屋、公寓、開放式單位和長者住宅。"},{"en":"Different accommodation types allow singles, families, and elderly people to live in the same area.","zh":"不同住屋類型讓單身人士、家庭和長者能住在同一區。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in housing and travel contexts.","zh":"這個片語適合用於住房和旅遊語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"only a short drive to","meaning":"開車很快便可到……","examples":[{"en":"It is only a short drive to get out into the countryside.","zh":"開車很快便可到郊外去。"},{"en":"Only a short drive to a place means it takes little time to reach by car.","zh":"only a short drive to a place 指駕車只需短時間便可到達某地。"},{"en":"The beach is only a short drive from our flat.","zh":"海灘距離我們的單位只有短短車程。"},{"en":"If countryside is a short drive away, residents can enjoy nature without living far from town.","zh":"如果郊外很快便可開車到達，居民不用住得離市鎮很遠也能享受自然。"},{"en":"This phrase presents a place as conveniently close by car.","zh":"這個片語把某地方描述為駕車方便到達。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get out into the countryside","meaning":"到郊外去","examples":[{"en":"Residents can quickly get out into the countryside.","zh":"居民可以很快到郊外去。"},{"en":"To get out into the countryside means to leave town and go to rural or natural areas.","zh":"get out into the countryside 指離開市鎮，前往鄉郊或自然地區。"},{"en":"Families may get out into the countryside at weekends for walking and fresh air.","zh":"家庭可能在週末到郊外散步和呼吸新鮮空氣。"},{"en":"Access to countryside can improve quality of life by offering space and relaxation.","zh":"接近郊外可以透過提供空間和放鬆來改善生活質素。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests escaping urban life for nature.","zh":"這個片語暗示離開城市生活、走進自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"particularly pleased that","meaning":"特別高興……","examples":[{"en":"The company was particularly pleased that many people liked the layout.","zh":"公司特別高興很多人喜歡佈局。"},{"en":"Particularly pleased that means especially happy because of a specific result or comment.","zh":"particularly pleased that 指因某個具體結果或意見而特別開心。"},{"en":"A teacher was particularly pleased that quiet students joined the discussion.","zh":"老師特別高興安靜的學生參與了討論。"},{"en":"Positive public reaction can make a company feel more confident about its plan.","zh":"公眾正面反應可以令公司對計劃更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the reason for strong satisfaction.","zh":"這個片語突出強烈滿意的原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"designs for the layout","meaning":"佈局設計","examples":[{"en":"Many people liked the designs for the layout of the development.","zh":"許多人喜歡該發展項目的佈局設計。"},{"en":"Designs for the layout are plans showing how buildings, roads, open spaces, and facilities are arranged.","zh":"designs for the layout 指顯示建築物、道路、空地和設施如何安排的設計圖。"},{"en":"A school may show designs for the layout of a new playground before building it.","zh":"學校可能在興建新操場前展示其佈局設計。"},{"en":"Good layout design can make an area easier to move around and more pleasant to live in.","zh":"良好佈局設計可以令地區更易通行，也更宜居。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on arrangement, not only appearance.","zh":"這個片語着重安排，而不只是外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the layout of the development","meaning":"發展項目的佈局","examples":[{"en":"The layout of the development made a good impression.","zh":"發展項目的佈局留下良好印象。"},{"en":"The layout of the development means how the homes, roads, facilities, and open spaces are arranged.","zh":"the layout of the development 指住宅、道路、設施和空地如何安排。"},{"en":"A clear layout can help residents find schools, shops, and parks easily.","zh":"清晰佈局可以幫助居民容易找到學校、商店和公園。"},{"en":"Poor layout can create long walks, traffic confusion, or isolated spaces.","zh":"差劣佈局可能造成長距離步行、交通混亂或孤立空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the overall arrangement of a planned area.","zh":"這個片語描述規劃區域的整體安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the majority of people","meaning":"大多數人","examples":[{"en":"The majority of people said the design made a good impression.","zh":"大多數人說設計留下良好印象。"},{"en":"The majority of people means more than half of the people.","zh":"the majority of people 指超過一半的人。"},{"en":"The majority of students chose the earlier lunch time.","zh":"大多數學生選擇較早的午餐時間。"},{"en":"If the majority support a plan, decision-makers may feel more confident moving forward.","zh":"如果大多數人支持計劃，決策者可能更有信心推進。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the larger part of a group.","zh":"這個片語描述群體中的較大部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"generally made a good impression","meaning":"整體留下良好印象","examples":[{"en":"The layout generally made a good impression.","zh":"佈局整體留下良好印象。"},{"en":"Generally made a good impression means most people had a positive first reaction.","zh":"generally made a good impression 指大部分人有正面的第一反應。"},{"en":"The new library design generally made a good impression because it looked bright and spacious.","zh":"新圖書館設計因明亮寬敞而整體留下良好印象。"},{"en":"A good first impression can help reduce public anxiety about a project.","zh":"良好第一印象可以幫助減少公眾對項目的焦慮。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests overall approval, even if some concerns remain.","zh":"這個片語暗示整體認同，即使仍有一些憂慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"blend in well with","meaning":"與……融和得很好","examples":[{"en":"The design blends in well with the natural features of the landscape.","zh":"該設計與景觀的自然特色融和得很好。"},{"en":"To blend in well with something means to fit naturally and not look out of place.","zh":"blend in well with something 指自然配合某物，看起來不突兀。"},{"en":"A small wooden café may blend in well with a country park.","zh":"一間小木咖啡店可能與郊野公園融和得很好。"},{"en":"Designs that blend in with the landscape can reduce visual damage to an area.","zh":"與景觀融和的設計可以減少對地區的視覺破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for buildings, colours, and styles.","zh":"這個片語常用於建築物、顏色和風格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"natural features of the landscape","meaning":"景觀的自然特色","examples":[{"en":"The design protects the natural features of the landscape.","zh":"該設計保護景觀的自然特色。"},{"en":"Natural features of the landscape are parts of the land such as trees, slopes, streams, rocks, or views.","zh":"natural features of the landscape 指土地中的樹木、斜坡、溪流、岩石或景色等部分。"},{"en":"A park design may keep natural features like old trees and ponds.","zh":"公園設計可能保留古樹和池塘等自然特色。"},{"en":"Protecting natural features can make development feel less artificial and more attractive.","zh":"保護自然特色可以令發展項目感覺沒那麼人工，並更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what already exists in nature at the site.","zh":"這個片語着重地盤上原本存在的自然事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"provision made for","meaning":"已作出……安排","examples":[{"en":"Provision has been made for protecting trees and wildlife.","zh":"已作出保護樹木及野生動物的安排。"},{"en":"Provision made for something means arrangements have been included to deal with that need.","zh":"provision made for something 指已包括處理某需要的安排。"},{"en":"A school trip plan should include provision for students with allergies.","zh":"學校旅行計劃應為有敏感症的學生作出安排。"},{"en":"Making provision early helps avoid problems when the project begins.","zh":"及早作出安排有助避免項目開始後出現問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in planning documents.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常見於規劃文件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"protecting trees and wildlife","meaning":"保護樹木及野生動物","examples":[{"en":"The plan includes provision for protecting trees and wildlife.","zh":"該計劃包括保護樹木及野生動物的安排。"},{"en":"Protecting trees and wildlife means taking steps to keep plants and animals safe from harm.","zh":"protecting trees and wildlife 指採取措施保護植物和動物免受傷害。"},{"en":"A school garden project can protect wildlife by keeping nesting areas undisturbed.","zh":"學校花園項目可以透過不打擾築巢區來保護野生動物。"},{"en":"If trees and wildlife are protected, development can be less damaging to nature.","zh":"如果樹木和野生動物受到保護，發展項目對自然的破壞可以較小。"},{"en":"This phrase connects environmental care with practical planning.","zh":"這個片語把環境照顧與實際規劃連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on the site","meaning":"在該地盤上","examples":[{"en":"Trees and wildlife on the site will be protected.","zh":"該地盤上的樹木和野生動物將受到保護。"},{"en":"On the site means at the exact place where work, construction, or an event is happening.","zh":"on the site 指在工程、建設或活動發生的確切地方。"},{"en":"Workers on the site must wear safety helmets.","zh":"地盤上的工人必須戴安全帽。"},{"en":"Conditions on the site affect how planners design roads, homes, and open spaces.","zh":"地盤上的情況會影響規劃者如何設計道路、住宅和空地。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the project location itself.","zh":"這個片語指項目所在地本身。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"facilities for cyclists","meaning":"單車人士設施","examples":[{"en":"Some people would like to see more facilities for cyclists.","zh":"有些人希望看到更多單車人士設施。"},{"en":"Facilities for cyclists are things such as cycle lanes, bike parking, signs, or repair points.","zh":"facilities for cyclists 指單車徑、單車泊位、標誌或維修點等設施。"},{"en":"A school may provide facilities for cyclists so students can ride safely.","zh":"學校可能提供單車人士設施，讓學生安全騎車。"},{"en":"Good cycling facilities can reduce car use and make roads safer.","zh":"良好單車設施可以減少汽車使用，並令道路更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on services or structures that support people riding bicycles.","zh":"這個片語着重支援騎單車人士的服務或結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"look at that","meaning":"研究一下；考慮一下","examples":[{"en":"The company will look at the request for more cycling facilities.","zh":"公司會研究一下增加單車設施的要求。"},{"en":"To look at that means to consider, examine, or study that issue.","zh":"look at that 指考慮、檢視或研究該議題。"},{"en":"The school will look at parents’ request for longer library hours.","zh":"學校會考慮家長要求延長圖書館開放時間的建議。"},{"en":"Looking at a request does not always mean accepting it, but it shows it will be considered.","zh":"研究一項要求不一定代表接受，但顯示它會被考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used politely when responding to suggestions.","zh":"這個片語常用於有禮回應建議時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"overall feedback","meaning":"整體回饋","examples":[{"en":"The overall feedback about the design has been positive.","zh":"關於設計的整體回饋是正面的。"},{"en":"Overall feedback means the general response or opinion after considering all comments together.","zh":"overall feedback 指把所有意見合起來考慮後的整體反應或看法。"},{"en":"The overall feedback from students about the new timetable was mixed.","zh":"學生對新時間表的整體回饋好壞參半。"},{"en":"Overall feedback helps decision-makers see the main public reaction, not just one complaint.","zh":"整體回饋幫助決策者看見主要公眾反應，而不只是單一投訴。"},{"en":"This phrase summarises many views into a broad impression.","zh":"這個片語把許多意見概括為整體印象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"design and facilities","meaning":"設計及設施","examples":[{"en":"The design and facilities make the development seem suitable for all ages.","zh":"設計及設施令該發展項目看似適合各年齡層。"},{"en":"Design and facilities mean both the layout or appearance and the services or spaces provided.","zh":"design and facilities 指佈局或外觀，以及所提供的服務或空間。"},{"en":"A school’s design and facilities affect how students move, learn, and rest.","zh":"學校的設計及設施會影響學生如何行走、學習和休息。"},{"en":"Good facilities can make a place more useful, while good design can make it easier to enjoy.","zh":"良好設施可以令地方更有用，而良好設計可以令它更容易享受。"},{"en":"This phrase combines planning style with practical features.","zh":"這個片語結合規劃風格和實用特色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"people of all ages","meaning":"各年齡層人士","examples":[{"en":"People of all ages can live together happily in the development.","zh":"各年齡層人士都可以在該發展項目中愉快地共住。"},{"en":"People of all ages means children, adults, elderly people, and everyone in between.","zh":"people of all ages 指兒童、成年人、長者，以及介乎其中的所有人。"},{"en":"A community centre should offer activities for people of all ages.","zh":"社區中心應為各年齡層人士提供活動。"},{"en":"If a neighbourhood serves all ages, families can stay there through different life stages.","zh":"如果社區服務所有年齡層，家庭就能在不同人生階段繼續住在那裡。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises inclusiveness across age groups.","zh":"這個片語強調跨年齡群體的包容性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"live together happily","meaning":"愉快地共住","examples":[{"en":"The development is designed so that people of all ages can live together happily.","zh":"該發展項目經設計，讓各年齡層人士可以愉快地共住。"},{"en":"To live together happily means to share a community peacefully and comfortably.","zh":"live together happily 指在同一社區中和平而舒適地共同生活。"},{"en":"Families, students, and elderly residents can live together happily if facilities suit everyone.","zh":"如果設施適合所有人，家庭、學生和長者可以愉快地共住。"},{"en":"Good planning can reduce conflict by providing quiet areas, play spaces, and safe paths.","zh":"良好規劃可以透過提供安靜區、遊樂空間和安全通道來減少衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests social harmony in a shared living area.","zh":"這個片語暗示共享居住區中的社會和諧。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"proposed development","meaning":"擬議發展項目","examples":[{"en":"Mark puts a map of the proposed development on the screen.","zh":"Mark 把擬議發展項目的地圖放到螢幕上。"},{"en":"A proposed development is a building project that has been suggested or planned but may not yet be finished.","zh":"proposed development 指已被提出或規劃、但可能尚未完成的建築項目。"},{"en":"Residents may study maps of a proposed development before giving opinions.","zh":"居民可能在提供意見前研究擬議發展項目的地圖。"},{"en":"Proposed developments can change after public feedback, planning rules, or budget decisions.","zh":"擬議發展項目可能因公眾回饋、規劃規則或預算決定而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a plan under consideration, not a completed project.","zh":"這個片語指正在考慮中的計劃，而不是已完成項目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"up on the screen","meaning":"放到螢幕上","examples":[{"en":"Mark puts a map up on the screen.","zh":"Mark 把地圖放到螢幕上。"},{"en":"Up on the screen means displayed on a screen for people to see.","zh":"up on the screen 指顯示在螢幕上讓人看見。"},{"en":"The teacher put the exam instructions up on the screen.","zh":"老師把考試指示放到螢幕上。"},{"en":"Showing information on the screen helps a large audience follow the explanation.","zh":"把資料顯示在螢幕上，有助大量聽眾跟上解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in presentations and classrooms.","zh":"這個片語常見於簡報和課室。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be bounded by","meaning":"以……為界","examples":[{"en":"The development is bounded on the south side by the main road.","zh":"該發展項目南面以大路為界。"},{"en":"To be bounded by something means to have that thing forming the edge or border.","zh":"be bounded by something 指以某物形成邊緣或界線。"},{"en":"The school playground is bounded by trees on two sides.","zh":"學校操場兩邊以樹木為界。"},{"en":"Boundaries help people understand where a site begins and ends.","zh":"邊界幫助人們理解地盤從哪裡開始和結束。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used when describing maps or land.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常用於描述地圖或土地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on the south side","meaning":"在南面","examples":[{"en":"The development is bounded on the south side by the main road.","zh":"該發展項目在南面以大路為界。"},{"en":"On the south side means on the part facing or located toward the south.","zh":"on the south side 指在面向或位於南方的部分。"},{"en":"The school garden is on the south side of the building, so it gets more sunlight.","zh":"學校花園在建築物南面，所以得到更多陽光。"},{"en":"Direction words help people understand locations on a map clearly.","zh":"方向詞幫助人們清楚理解地圖上的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing boundaries, buildings, and maps.","zh":"這個片語適合用於描述邊界、建築物和地圖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"main road","meaning":"大路；主要道路","examples":[{"en":"The main road goes on to Nunston.","zh":"主要道路繼續通往 Nunston。"},{"en":"A main road is an important road that carries a lot of traffic and connects places.","zh":"main road 指承載大量交通並連接不同地方的重要道路。"},{"en":"Shops near a main road may attract more customers because many people pass by.","zh":"靠近大路的商店可能吸引更多顧客，因為很多人經過。"},{"en":"Living beside a main road can be convenient, but it may also be noisy.","zh":"住在主要道路旁邊可以很方便，但也可能很嘈吵。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a major route, not a small side street.","zh":"這個片語指主要路線，而不是小支路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"go on to","meaning":"繼續通往","examples":[{"en":"The main road then goes on to Nunston.","zh":"這條主要道路之後繼續通往 Nunston。"},{"en":"To go on to a place means to continue in that direction until reaching it.","zh":"go on to a place 指繼續朝某方向前進直到到達該地。"},{"en":"This bus goes on to the city centre after stopping at the hospital.","zh":"這輛巴士停靠醫院後，繼續通往市中心。"},{"en":"Roads that go on to nearby towns can make commuting easier.","zh":"繼續通往附近城鎮的道路可以令通勤更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continued movement or route direction.","zh":"這個片語描述持續移動或路線方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"another boundary is formed by","meaning":"另一條邊界由……構成","examples":[{"en":"Another boundary is formed by London Road.","zh":"另一條邊界由 London Road 構成。"},{"en":"Another boundary is formed by something means a different edge of the area is marked by that feature.","zh":"another boundary is formed by something 指該區另一邊緣由某特色標示。"},{"en":"Another boundary of the park is formed by a river.","zh":"公園另一條邊界由河流構成。"},{"en":"Roads, rivers, walls, and fields can all form boundaries on a map.","zh":"道路、河流、牆和田地都可以在地圖上構成邊界。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and helps describe the shape of an area.","zh":"這個片語較正式，有助描述一個區域的形狀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"western side of","meaning":"……的西面","examples":[{"en":"London Road is on the western side of the development.","zh":"London Road 位於該發展項目的西面。"},{"en":"The western side of a place is the part located toward the west.","zh":"western side of a place 指位於某地西方的部分。"},{"en":"The car park is on the western side of the school.","zh":"停車場在學校西面。"},{"en":"Knowing the western side helps people follow map directions more accurately.","zh":"知道西面位置有助人們更準確跟隨地圖方向。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in formal location descriptions.","zh":"這個片語適合用於正式位置描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"inside the development","meaning":"在發展項目內","examples":[{"en":"Inside the development, there will be houses and apartment blocks.","zh":"在發展項目內，將會有房屋和住宅大廈。"},{"en":"Inside the development means within the planned housing area.","zh":"inside the development 指在規劃住宅區之內。"},{"en":"Inside the development, residents may find shops, parks, and community facilities.","zh":"在發展項目內，居民可能找到商店、公園和社區設施。"},{"en":"Facilities inside the development are easier for residents to reach without travelling far.","zh":"發展項目內的設施較容易讓居民到達，不用走很遠。"},{"en":"This phrase separates what is within the project from what is outside it.","zh":"這個片語把項目內部與外部區分開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"apartment blocks","meaning":"住宅大廈","examples":[{"en":"The development will include about 400 houses and three apartment blocks.","zh":"該發展項目將包括約 400 間房屋和三座住宅大廈。"},{"en":"Apartment blocks are buildings divided into many separate flats.","zh":"apartment blocks 指分成許多獨立單位的住宅建築物。"},{"en":"A city may build apartment blocks near a station to house more people in less land.","zh":"城市可能在車站附近興建住宅大廈，以用較少土地容納更多人。"},{"en":"Apartment blocks can increase housing supply, but they need good lifts, safety systems, and shared spaces.","zh":"住宅大廈可以增加房屋供應，但需要良好升降機、安全系統和共享空間。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to residential buildings with multiple units.","zh":"這個片語指有多個單位的住宅建築物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"children up to 11 years old","meaning":"11歲或以下兒童","examples":[{"en":"There will be a school for children up to 11 years old.","zh":"那裡將有一間供 11 歲或以下兒童就讀的學校。"},{"en":"Children up to 11 years old means children aged 11 or younger.","zh":"children up to 11 years old 指 11 歲或以下的兒童。"},{"en":"A playground for children up to 11 years old should be safe for younger users.","zh":"供 11 歲或以下兒童使用的遊樂場，應對年幼使用者安全。"},{"en":"If a school serves children up to 11, older students will need another school nearby.","zh":"如果學校服務 11 歲或以下兒童，較年長學生便需要附近另一間學校。"},{"en":"This phrase defines an age limit.","zh":"這個片語界定年齡上限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"South Entrance","meaning":"南入口","examples":[{"en":"A road from the South Entrance goes up through the development.","zh":"一條從南入口開始的道路向上貫穿發展項目。"},{"en":"The South Entrance is the entrance located at the southern part of a site or building.","zh":"South Entrance 指位於地盤或建築物南面的入口。"},{"en":"Visitors may use the South Entrance if they arrive from the main road.","zh":"如果訪客從大路到達，可能會使用南入口。"},{"en":"Naming entrances helps people follow directions in large developments.","zh":"為入口命名有助人們在大型發展項目中跟隨方向。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific access point.","zh":"這個片語識別一個特定出入口。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at the bottom of the map","meaning":"在地圖底部","examples":[{"en":"The South Entrance is at the bottom of the map.","zh":"南入口在地圖底部。"},{"en":"At the bottom of the map means located near the lower edge of the map image.","zh":"at the bottom of the map 指位於地圖圖像的下方邊緣附近。"},{"en":"The river is shown at the bottom of the map, below the school.","zh":"河流顯示在地圖底部，在學校下方。"},{"en":"Map directions help listeners understand locations even if they have not visited the place.","zh":"地圖方向幫助聽眾理解位置，即使他們未曾到訪該地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position on a map, not necessarily downhill in real life.","zh":"這個片語描述地圖上的位置，不一定代表現實中較低處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go right up through","meaning":"一路向上貫穿……","examples":[{"en":"A road goes right up through the development.","zh":"一條道路一路向上貫穿該發展項目。"},{"en":"To go right up through a place means to continue directly through it from lower to higher or from one end to another.","zh":"go right up through a place 指從較低處到較高處，或從一端到另一端直接穿過某地。"},{"en":"A path goes right up through the park to the hilltop.","zh":"一條小徑一路向上貫穿公園，通往山頂。"},{"en":"A road through a development can connect entrances, homes, and facilities.","zh":"貫穿發展項目的道路可以連接入口、住宅和設施。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a clear route running through the whole area.","zh":"這個片語暗示一條清晰路線穿過整個區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at the corner of","meaning":"在……的角落","examples":[{"en":"The school will be at the corner of the second turning to the left.","zh":"學校將位於第二個左轉路口的角落。"},{"en":"At the corner of a place means at the point where two roads or sides meet.","zh":"at the corner of a place 指在兩條路或兩邊相接的地方。"},{"en":"The café is at the corner of the main street and the lane.","zh":"咖啡店在大街和小巷交界的角落。"},{"en":"Corners are useful landmarks because they are easy to recognise when giving directions.","zh":"角落是有用地標，因為指路時容易辨認。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a precise location.","zh":"這個片語描述準確位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"second turning to the left","meaning":"第二個左轉路口","examples":[{"en":"The school is located at the second turning to the left.","zh":"學校位於第二個左轉路口。"},{"en":"The second turning to the left means the second road or path on the left after you start moving.","zh":"second turning to the left 指開始前行後左邊第二條路或小徑。"},{"en":"To reach the library, take the second turning to the left after the traffic lights.","zh":"要到圖書館，經過交通燈後在第二個左轉路口轉入。"},{"en":"Counting turnings helps people follow directions step by step.","zh":"數路口有助人們一步一步跟隨方向。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in spoken directions.","zh":"這個片語常見於口頭指路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sports centre","meaning":"體育中心","examples":[{"en":"A large sports centre is planned for the development.","zh":"該發展項目計劃興建一個大型體育中心。"},{"en":"A sports centre is a building or area with facilities for exercise and sports.","zh":"sports centre 指有運動和健身設施的建築物或區域。"},{"en":"A sports centre may include courts, a gym, changing rooms, and outdoor pitches.","zh":"體育中心可能包括球場、健身室、更衣室和戶外球場。"},{"en":"Sports centres can improve community health by giving residents places to exercise.","zh":"體育中心可以透過提供運動場所改善社區健康。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to shared sports facilities, not one single playground.","zh":"這個片語指共享體育設施，而不是單一遊樂場。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"facilities for indoor and outdoor activities","meaning":"室內及戶外活動設施","examples":[{"en":"The sports centre will have facilities for indoor and outdoor activities.","zh":"體育中心將有室內及戶外活動設施。"},{"en":"Facilities for indoor and outdoor activities are spaces and equipment for activities inside buildings and outside in the open air.","zh":"facilities for indoor and outdoor activities 指供室內和戶外活動使用的空間和設備。"},{"en":"A school sports centre may have a gym indoors and football pitches outdoors.","zh":"學校體育中心可能有室內健身室和戶外足球場。"},{"en":"Offering both indoor and outdoor facilities lets people exercise in different weather.","zh":"同時提供室內及戶外設施，讓人們在不同天氣下運動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the centre supports many types of activities.","zh":"這個片語顯示中心支援多種類型活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"western side of the development","meaning":"發展項目的西面","examples":[{"en":"The sports centre will be on the western side of the development.","zh":"體育中心將位於發展項目的西面。"},{"en":"The western side of the development means the part of the project area facing west.","zh":"western side of the development 指項目範圍面向西方的部分。"},{"en":"The car park may be placed on the western side of a school campus.","zh":"停車場可能設於學校校園西面。"},{"en":"Locating a facility on one side affects how far residents must walk to reach it.","zh":"把設施放在某一邊會影響居民需要走多遠才能到達。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for explaining positions on a map.","zh":"這個片語適合用於解釋地圖上的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"branch off from","meaning":"從……分岔出來","examples":[{"en":"The road branches off from London Road.","zh":"這條路從 London Road 分岔出來。"},{"en":"To branch off from a road means to separate from it and go in another direction.","zh":"branch off from a road 指從某道路分離並朝另一方向延伸。"},{"en":"A small path branches off from the main road and leads to the park.","zh":"一條小路從大路分岔出來，通往公園。"},{"en":"Roads that branch off can connect main routes with homes and facilities.","zh":"分岔道路可以把主要路線與住宅和設施連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a route splitting away from another route.","zh":"這個片語描述路線從另一條路分出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"health problems","meaning":"健康問題","examples":[{"en":"Residents can go to the clinic if they have health problems.","zh":"如果居民有健康問題，可以去診所。"},{"en":"Health problems are illnesses, injuries, or medical concerns that affect a person’s body or mind.","zh":"health problems 指影響身體或心理的疾病、受傷或醫療憂慮。"},{"en":"A child with breathing problems may need to visit a clinic quickly.","zh":"有呼吸問題的孩子可能需要快速到診所求醫。"},{"en":"Nearby healthcare services help residents deal with health problems before they become serious.","zh":"附近醫療服務幫助居民在問題變嚴重前處理健康問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is broad and can refer to minor or serious medical issues.","zh":"這個片語範圍很廣，可指輕微或嚴重醫療問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"towards the top of the map","meaning":"靠近地圖上方","examples":[{"en":"The lake is towards the top of the map.","zh":"湖泊靠近地圖上方。"},{"en":"Towards the top of the map means near the upper part of the map, though not necessarily at the very top.","zh":"towards the top of the map 指靠近地圖上部，但不一定在最頂端。"},{"en":"The school is towards the top of the map, just below the park.","zh":"學校靠近地圖上方，就在公園下方。"},{"en":"This phrase helps listeners locate something approximately before giving more detail.","zh":"這個片語幫助聽眾先大約定位，再聽更詳細資料。"},{"en":"It describes map position, not always real-world height.","zh":"它描述地圖位置，不一定代表現實高度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"just below this","meaning":"就在這個下方","examples":[{"en":"The clinic will be just below the lake.","zh":"診所將就在湖泊下方。"},{"en":"Just below this means directly or very near underneath the place just mentioned on a map or picture.","zh":"just below this 指在地圖或圖像上剛才提及地方的正下方或非常接近下方。"},{"en":"The toilets are just below the café on the floor plan.","zh":"洗手間就在平面圖上咖啡店下方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining locations in relation to a visible feature.","zh":"這個片語適合用來以可見特色作參照解釋位置。"},{"en":"It gives a close position rather than a distant general area.","zh":"它提供接近位置，而不是遙遠大概區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"to the right of","meaning":"在……右方","examples":[{"en":"The clinic will be to the right of a street of houses.","zh":"診所將位於一排住宅街道右方。"},{"en":"To the right of something means on its right-hand side.","zh":"to the right of something 指在某物右手邊。"},{"en":"The library is to the right of the school office.","zh":"圖書館在校務處右方。"},{"en":"Left-right directions help people locate places quickly on maps.","zh":"左右方向有助人們在地圖上快速定位。"},{"en":"This phrase depends on the direction from which the map or person is viewed.","zh":"這個片語取決於看地圖或人的方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a street of houses","meaning":"一排住宅街道","examples":[{"en":"The clinic will be to the right of a street of houses.","zh":"診所將位於一排住宅街道右方。"},{"en":"A street of houses is a road with homes built along it.","zh":"a street of houses 指沿道路興建住宅的一條街。"},{"en":"A quiet street of houses may be suitable for families with young children.","zh":"安靜的一排住宅街道可能適合有年幼孩子的家庭。"},{"en":"A clinic beside a street of houses gives residents nearby access to medical help.","zh":"診所位於住宅街道旁邊，能讓附近居民方便獲得醫療協助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a residential street.","zh":"這個片語描述住宅街道。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"community centre","meaning":"社區中心","examples":[{"en":"There will be a community centre for people of all ages.","zh":"那裡將有一個供各年齡層人士使用的社區中心。"},{"en":"A community centre is a shared building where residents can meet, take classes, and join activities.","zh":"community centre 指居民可見面、上課和參加活動的共享建築物。"},{"en":"A community centre may offer exercise classes, youth clubs, and elderly services.","zh":"社區中心可能提供健身班、青年活動和長者服務。"},{"en":"Community centres help residents build relationships and reduce loneliness.","zh":"社區中心幫助居民建立關係並減少孤獨感。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a public or shared local facility.","zh":"這個片語指公共或共享本地設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on the northeast side of","meaning":"在……東北面","examples":[{"en":"The specially designed houses will be on the northeast side of the development.","zh":"特別設計的住宅將位於發展項目的東北面。"},{"en":"On the northeast side of a place means in the part between north and east.","zh":"on the northeast side of a place 指在介乎北方和東方之間的部分。"},{"en":"The playground is on the northeast side of the park.","zh":"遊樂場在公園東北面。"},{"en":"Directional phrases help people understand map positions precisely.","zh":"方向片語幫助人們準確理解地圖位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in site descriptions.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常用於地盤描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a row of","meaning":"一排……","examples":[{"en":"There will be a row of specially designed houses.","zh":"那裡將有一排特別設計的住宅。"},{"en":"A row of something means several things placed in a straight or ordered line.","zh":"a row of something 指幾樣東西以直線或有序方式排列。"},{"en":"A row of trees can provide shade along a school path.","zh":"一排樹可以為學校小路提供陰影。"},{"en":"Houses in a row can make planning roads and entrances easier.","zh":"一排住宅可以令道路和入口規劃更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arrangement and order.","zh":"這個片語描述排列和秩序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"specially designed houses","meaning":"特別設計的住宅","examples":[{"en":"There will be specially designed houses for residents over 65.","zh":"那裡將有專為 65 歲以上居民而設的特別設計住宅。"},{"en":"Specially designed houses are homes planned for particular needs or groups of people.","zh":"specially designed houses 指為特定需要或人群規劃的住宅。"},{"en":"Houses for elderly residents may include ramps, wider doors, and safer bathrooms.","zh":"長者住宅可能包括斜道、較闊門口和更安全浴室。"},{"en":"Special design can help residents live independently for longer.","zh":"特別設計可以幫助居民更長時間獨立生活。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the homes are not ordinary standard houses.","zh":"這個片語暗示這些住宅不是普通標準房屋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"specifically for","meaning":"專為……而設","examples":[{"en":"The houses are specifically for residents over 65.","zh":"這些住宅專為 65 歲以上居民而設。"},{"en":"Specifically for means designed or intended for one particular group or purpose.","zh":"specifically for 指為某一特定群體或目的而設計或準備。"},{"en":"A reading room may be specifically for quiet study.","zh":"閱讀室可能專為安靜自修而設。"},{"en":"If facilities are specifically for older residents, they should match older people’s needs.","zh":"如果設施專為長者而設，就應符合長者需要。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the purpose clearly.","zh":"這個片語清楚收窄用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"residents over 65","meaning":"65歲以上居民","examples":[{"en":"The houses are designed for residents over 65.","zh":"這些住宅是為 65 歲以上居民設計的。"},{"en":"Residents over 65 are people living in an area who are older than 65 years old.","zh":"residents over 65 指居住在某區、年齡超過 65 歲的人。"},{"en":"Residents over 65 may need homes near clinics, shops, and public transport.","zh":"65 歲以上居民可能需要接近診所、商店和公共交通的住宅。"},{"en":"Planning for older residents can help them stay safe and independent.","zh":"為長者規劃可以幫助他們保持安全和獨立。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies an age group within a community.","zh":"這個片語識別社區中的一個年齡群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"adjoining this","meaning":"與此相連；毗鄰","examples":[{"en":"The community centre will be adjoining the row of houses.","zh":"社區中心將與那排住宅相連。"},{"en":"Adjoining this means next to and connected with the place just mentioned.","zh":"adjoining this 指毗鄰並連接剛才提及的地方。"},{"en":"The reading room is adjoining the children’s library.","zh":"閱讀室與兒童圖書館相連。"},{"en":"If a community centre adjoins elderly housing, residents can reach activities easily.","zh":"如果社區中心毗鄰長者住宅，居民可以容易到達活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes close physical connection.","zh":"這個片語描述緊密實體連接。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"haven’t forgotten about","meaning":"沒有忘記……","examples":[{"en":"The planners have not forgotten about shopping.","zh":"規劃者沒有忘記購物需要。"},{"en":"Haven’t forgotten about something means someone has remembered to include or consider it.","zh":"haven’t forgotten about something 指某人記得包括或考慮某事。"},{"en":"The school has not forgotten about students who need lunch assistance.","zh":"學校沒有忘記需要午餐支援的學生。"},{"en":"Saying this reassures people that an important need has not been ignored.","zh":"這樣說可以安撫人們，表示重要需要沒有被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when responding to possible public concerns.","zh":"這個片語常用於回應可能的公眾關注。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"between the two entrances","meaning":"在兩個入口之間","examples":[{"en":"The supermarket will be between the two entrances to the development.","zh":"超市將位於發展項目兩個入口之間。"},{"en":"Between the two entrances means in the space separating one entrance from the other.","zh":"between the two entrances 指位於兩個入口之間的空間。"},{"en":"A reception desk may be placed between the two entrances of a school hall.","zh":"接待處可能設在學校禮堂兩個入口之間。"},{"en":"A central location between entrances makes a facility easy to reach from both sides.","zh":"位於兩個入口之間的中心位置，令設施從兩邊都容易到達。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a position in the middle of two access points.","zh":"這個片語描述兩個出入口中間的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"leave the three large trees","meaning":"保留三棵大樹","examples":[{"en":"The company plans to leave the three large trees near London Road.","zh":"公司計劃保留 London Road 附近的三棵大樹。"},{"en":"To leave the three large trees means to keep them in place instead of cutting them down.","zh":"leave the three large trees 指把三棵大樹留在原地，而不是砍掉。"},{"en":"A school may leave old trees in the playground because they give shade.","zh":"學校可能保留操場上的老樹，因為它們提供陰影。"},{"en":"Keeping mature trees can protect wildlife and make a new area look more natural.","zh":"保留成熟樹木可以保護野生動物，並令新區看起來更自然。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests preservation during development.","zh":"這個片語暗示在發展期間進行保育。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"near London Road","meaning":"在London Road附近","examples":[{"en":"The three large trees are near London Road.","zh":"三棵大樹在 London Road 附近。"},{"en":"Near London Road means close to that road.","zh":"near London Road 指接近 London Road。"},{"en":"A bus stop near the main road is easier for residents to find.","zh":"靠近大路的巴士站較容易讓居民找到。"},{"en":"Describing something as near a known road helps people locate it on a map.","zh":"把某物描述為在已知道路附近，有助人們在地圖上定位。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a practical location reference.","zh":"這個片語提供實用位置參照。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"to the south of","meaning":"在……以南","examples":[{"en":"The supermarket will be just to the south of the trees.","zh":"超市將就在樹木以南。"},{"en":"To the south of something means located below or southward from it on a map.","zh":"to the south of something 指在某物的南方，或在地圖上其下方。"},{"en":"The car park is to the south of the school building.","zh":"停車場在校舍以南。"},{"en":"Directional phrases help planners describe exact positions without long explanations.","zh":"方向片語幫助規劃者不用長篇解釋也能描述準確位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in map descriptions.","zh":"這個片語常見於地圖描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"playground for younger children","meaning":"供年幼兒童使用的遊樂場","examples":[{"en":"The development will have a playground for younger children.","zh":"該發展項目將有一個供年幼兒童使用的遊樂場。"},{"en":"A playground for younger children is a safe play area designed for small children.","zh":"playground for younger children 指為小朋友設計的安全遊樂區。"},{"en":"Such a playground may include low slides, soft surfaces, and simple climbing equipment.","zh":"這類遊樂場可能包括較低滑梯、軟墊地面和簡單攀爬設備。"},{"en":"Age-appropriate playgrounds reduce injury risk because the equipment matches children’s abilities.","zh":"適合年齡的遊樂場能降低受傷風險，因為設備配合兒童能力。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both the facility and its intended users.","zh":"這個片語同時指出設施及其目標使用者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"goes up from","meaning":"從……向上延伸","examples":[{"en":"The road goes up from the South Entrance.","zh":"道路從南入口向上延伸。"},{"en":"Goes up from a place means moves upward or northward from that starting point on a map.","zh":"goes up from a place 指從某起點向上坡或在地圖上向上方延伸。"},{"en":"The path goes up from the car park to the school hall.","zh":"小徑從停車場向上延伸至學校禮堂。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people follow a route from a clear starting point.","zh":"這個片語幫助人們從清晰起點跟隨路線。"},{"en":"It can refer to real uphill movement or upward direction on a map.","zh":"它可以指真實上坡，也可以指地圖上的向上方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"curve round to the left","meaning":"向左彎曲","examples":[{"en":"The road curves round to the left at the top.","zh":"道路在上方向左彎曲。"},{"en":"To curve round to the left means to bend gradually toward the left side.","zh":"curve round to the left 指逐漸向左邊彎曲。"},{"en":"The path curves round to the left before reaching the lake.","zh":"小徑到達湖泊前向左彎曲。"},{"en":"Curved roads can slow traffic and shape where facilities are placed.","zh":"彎曲道路可以減慢車速，並影響設施放在哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the shape and direction of a route.","zh":"這個片語描述路線的形狀和方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at the top","meaning":"在上方","examples":[{"en":"The road curves round to the left at the top.","zh":"道路在上方向左彎曲。"},{"en":"At the top means at the upper part of a map, hill, road, or area.","zh":"at the top 指在地圖、山丘、道路或區域的上方部分。"},{"en":"The school is at the top of the hill.","zh":"學校在山頂。"},{"en":"When reading a map, “at the top” usually means near the upper edge of the map.","zh":"看地圖時，“at the top” 通常指靠近地圖上邊緣。"},{"en":"This phrase needs context because it can describe height or map position.","zh":"這個片語需要語境，因為它可以描述高度或地圖位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in that curve","meaning":"在那個彎位內","examples":[{"en":"The playground will be in that curve.","zh":"遊樂場將位於那個彎位內。"},{"en":"In that curve means located inside or within the bend of a road or path just mentioned.","zh":"in that curve 指位於剛提及道路或小徑彎曲部分之內。"},{"en":"A small garden may be placed in the curve of a quiet road.","zh":"小花園可能設於一條安靜道路的彎位內。"},{"en":"Curved spaces can create sheltered areas for playgrounds or seating.","zh":"彎位空間可以形成較受保護的遊樂場或座位區。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a road shape as a location marker.","zh":"這個片語以道路形狀作位置標記。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"with nice views of","meaning":"可欣賞……美景","examples":[{"en":"The playground will have nice views of the lake.","zh":"遊樂場可欣賞湖泊美景。"},{"en":"With nice views of something means having a pleasant sight of that place or feature.","zh":"with nice views of something 指可以看見某地方或特色的美好景色。"},{"en":"A classroom with nice views of the garden can feel calmer.","zh":"可欣賞花園景色的課室可以感覺更平靜。"},{"en":"Good views can make public spaces more enjoyable and attractive.","zh":"良好景觀可以令公共空間更令人享受和吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what people can see from a place.","zh":"這個片語描述人們從某地可以看見甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"anyone","meaning":"有沒有人","examples":[{"en":"Mark asks if anyone has any questions.","zh":"Mark 問有沒有人有問題。"},{"en":"Anyone means any person in the group, without choosing a specific individual.","zh":"anyone 指群體中的任何人，沒有指定某一個人。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask if anyone needs help before starting the test.","zh":"老師可能在測驗開始前問有沒有人需要幫忙。"},{"en":"Asking “anyone” gives everyone a chance to speak or respond.","zh":"問 “anyone” 給每個人發言或回應的機會。"},{"en":"This word is useful when addressing a whole audience.","zh":"這個字適合用於向整個聽眾發問。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9}],"ielts/listening/Practice 10/task-3":[{"front":"make a start on","meaning":"開始着手做……","examples":[{"en":"Adam asks Michelle whether they should make a start on their presentation.","zh":"Adam 問 Michelle 他們是否應該開始着手做簡報。"},{"en":"To make a start on something means to begin doing a task, especially one that may take time.","zh":"make a start on something 的意思是開始做一項任務，尤其是需要時間完成的任務。"},{"en":"Students should make a start on revision before the exam week becomes too busy.","zh":"學生應在考試週變得太忙之前開始着手溫習。"},{"en":"Making a start early can reduce stress because the task no longer feels completely untouched.","zh":"早點開始着手做可以減少壓力，因為任務不再感覺完全未開始。"},{"en":"Even writing a title and a few ideas can help you make a start on an essay.","zh":"即使只是寫下標題和幾個想法，也可以幫助你開始着手寫文章。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"haven’t got that much time left","meaning":"剩下的時間不多","examples":[{"en":"They have not got that much time left to prepare.","zh":"他們剩下的準備時間不多。"},{"en":"Haven’t got that much time left means there is not much time remaining before something must be done.","zh":"haven’t got that much time left 的意思是在某事必須完成前，剩下的時間不多。"},{"en":"If the bus leaves in ten minutes, we haven’t got that much time left to buy snacks.","zh":"如果巴士十分鐘後開出，我們剩下的時間不多，不能慢慢買零食。"},{"en":"When people realise they have not got much time left, they usually work faster and cut unnecessary details.","zh":"當人們意識到剩下時間不多，他們通常會加快工作並刪去不必要細節。"},{"en":"This phrase often creates a sense of urgency.","zh":"這個短語常營造迫切感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"at least","meaning":"至少","examples":[{"en":"At least they have done all the background reading.","zh":"至少他們已經完成所有背景閱讀。"},{"en":"At least is used to point out one positive fact in a difficult or imperfect situation.","zh":"at least 用來指出困難或不完美情況中的一個正面事實。"},{"en":"We did not finish the whole project, but at least the introduction is ready.","zh":"我們沒有完成整個項目，但至少引言已經準備好。"},{"en":"Saying “at least” can make a problem feel slightly less worrying because something has been achieved.","zh":"說 at least 可以令問題感覺稍微沒那麼令人擔心，因為已有某些成果。"},{"en":"At least you arrived safely, even though the journey was delayed.","zh":"即使旅程延誤，至少你安全到達了。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"background reading","meaning":"背景閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Michelle and Adam have done all the background reading for the presentation.","zh":"Michelle 和 Adam 已經為簡報完成所有背景閱讀。"},{"en":"Background reading is reading done before a task so you understand the topic better.","zh":"background reading 是在做任務前進行的閱讀，幫助你更好理解題目。"},{"en":"Before writing a history essay, students may do background reading about the period and key events.","zh":"寫歷史文章前，學生可能會做關於該時期和重要事件的背景閱讀。"},{"en":"Good background reading helps speakers explain a topic more confidently and accurately.","zh":"良好的背景閱讀能幫助講者更有信心、更準確地解釋題目。"},{"en":"Without background reading, a presentation may sound shallow or confused.","zh":"沒有背景閱讀，簡報可能聽起來膚淺或混亂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"find something really interesting","meaning":"覺得某事很有趣","examples":[{"en":"Michelle found the research on the Laki eruption really interesting.","zh":"Michelle 覺得關於 Laki 火山噴發的研究很有趣。"},{"en":"To find something really interesting means to feel strongly curious about it or enjoy learning about it.","zh":"find something really interesting 的意思是對某事感到很有好奇心，或享受學習它。"},{"en":"A student may find space science really interesting after watching a documentary about planets.","zh":"學生觀看關於行星的紀錄片後，可能覺得太空科學很有趣。"},{"en":"When learners find a topic interesting, they often remember facts more easily.","zh":"當學習者覺得某題目有趣，他們通常更容易記住資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal interest, not just objective importance.","zh":"這個短語描述個人興趣，而不只是客觀重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"never even heard of","meaning":"甚至從未聽過","examples":[{"en":"Michelle had never even heard of the Laki eruption before the project.","zh":"Michelle 在這個項目前甚至從未聽過 Laki 火山噴發。"},{"en":"Never even heard of something means not knowing that it existed at all.","zh":"never even heard of something 的意思是完全不知道某事物存在。"},{"en":"Before visiting the museum, I had never even heard of that ancient city.","zh":"參觀博物館前，我甚至從未聽過那座古城。"},{"en":"People may ignore important historical events simply because they have never even heard of them.","zh":"人們可能忽略重要歷史事件，只因他們甚至從未聽過。"},{"en":"The word “even” makes the lack of knowledge sound stronger.","zh":"even 這個詞令不知道的程度聽起來更強。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Laki eruption","meaning":"Laki 火山噴發","examples":[{"en":"The students are preparing a presentation on the Laki eruption.","zh":"學生正在準備關於 Laki 火山噴發的簡報。"},{"en":"The Laki eruption was a major volcanic eruption in Iceland in the eighteenth century.","zh":"Laki eruption 是十八世紀冰島一次重大火山噴發。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may use the Laki eruption to show how volcanoes can affect weather and society.","zh":"地理課可能用 Laki 火山噴發來展示火山如何影響天氣和社會。"},{"en":"The Laki eruption matters because its effects reached far beyond Iceland.","zh":"Laki 火山噴發重要，是因為其影響遠遠超出冰島。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific historical volcanic event.","zh":"這個短語指一個特定的歷史火山事件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"before this","meaning":"在此之前","examples":[{"en":"Michelle had not heard of the Laki eruption before this.","zh":"Michelle 在此之前沒有聽過 Laki 火山噴發。"},{"en":"Before this means before the present situation, event, or discussion.","zh":"before this 的意思是在目前情況、事件或討論之前。"},{"en":"I had never tried online learning before this course.","zh":"在這個課程之前，我從未嘗試過網上學習。"},{"en":"People often realise how little they knew before this when a project introduces a new topic.","zh":"當一個項目介紹新題目，人們常會意識到自己在此之前知道得很少。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to an earlier time.","zh":"這個短語指回較早的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"me neither","meaning":"我也沒有","examples":[{"en":"Adam says “Me neither” because he had not heard of it before either.","zh":"Adam 說「我也沒有」，因為他之前也沒有聽過。"},{"en":"Me neither means I have not done, felt, or experienced that thing either.","zh":"me neither 的意思是我也沒有做過、感受過或經歷過那件事。"},{"en":"If one student says, “I haven’t finished the reading,” another may reply, “Me neither.”","zh":"如果一名學生說：「我還沒有完成閱讀。」另一人可能回答：「我也沒有。」"},{"en":"This phrase is used to agree with a negative statement about yourself.","zh":"這個短語用來同意一句關於自己的否定句。"},{"en":"It is a short and natural phrase in casual conversation.","zh":"這是日常對話中簡短而自然的說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"I suppose","meaning":"我想；我估計","examples":[{"en":"Adam supposes that 1783 was a long time ago.","zh":"Adam 估計1783年已經是很久以前。"},{"en":"I suppose is used when someone thinks something is probably true but is not speaking very strongly.","zh":"I suppose 用於某人認為某事大概是真的，但語氣不是十分肯定。"},{"en":"I suppose we should leave early if the traffic is usually heavy.","zh":"我想如果交通通常繁忙，我們應該早點出發。"},{"en":"Speakers use I suppose when they are guessing, softening an opinion, or thinking aloud.","zh":"說話者在猜測、軟化意見或邊想邊說時會使用 I suppose。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds less certain than “I know”.","zh":"這個短語聽起來沒有 I know 那麼肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a huge eruption","meaning":"大規模火山噴發","examples":[{"en":"The Laki eruption was a huge eruption with devastating consequences.","zh":"Laki 火山噴發是一次帶來毀滅性後果的大規模火山噴發。"},{"en":"A huge eruption is a very large volcanic event that releases great amounts of ash, gas, or lava.","zh":"huge eruption 是非常大型的火山事件，會釋放大量火山灰、氣體或熔岩。"},{"en":"A huge eruption can force nearby villages to evacuate quickly.","zh":"大規模火山噴發可以迫使附近村莊迅速疏散。"},{"en":"Large eruptions may change weather, damage crops, and affect health far away.","zh":"大型噴發可能改變天氣、破壞農作物，並影響遠方人們的健康。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the size and seriousness of a volcanic event.","zh":"這個短語強調火山事件的規模和嚴重性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"devastating consequences","meaning":"毀滅性後果","examples":[{"en":"The eruption had devastating consequences across several countries.","zh":"這次火山噴發在多個國家造成毀滅性後果。"},{"en":"Devastating consequences are extremely harmful results that cause serious damage, suffering, or loss.","zh":"devastating consequences 是極其有害的結果，造成嚴重破壞、痛苦或損失。"},{"en":"A major flood can have devastating consequences for homes, farms, and roads.","zh":"大型洪水可以對房屋、農場和道路造成毀滅性後果。"},{"en":"When warnings are ignored, a disaster may lead to more devastating consequences.","zh":"當警告被忽視，災難可能導致更毀滅性的後果。"},{"en":"This phrase is much stronger than “bad results”.","zh":"這個短語比 bad results 強烈得多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"primary sources","meaning":"原始資料","examples":[{"en":"There were many primary sources for the students to look at.","zh":"有許多原始資料供學生查看。"},{"en":"Primary sources are original materials from the time being studied, such as diaries, letters, records, or reports.","zh":"primary sources 是來自被研究時期的原始材料，例如日記、信件、紀錄或報告。"},{"en":"In history class, students may use primary sources to understand how people felt during a war.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生可能使用原始資料來理解戰爭期間人們的感受。"},{"en":"Primary sources are useful because they show direct evidence rather than later summaries.","zh":"原始資料有用，因為它們展示直接證據，而不是後來的摘要。"},{"en":"However, primary sources still need careful interpretation because writers may be biased or mistaken.","zh":"不過，原始資料仍需要仔細解讀，因為作者可能有偏見或出錯。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"look at","meaning":"查看；研究","examples":[{"en":"The students had many primary sources to look at.","zh":"學生有許多原始資料可以查看。"},{"en":"To look at something means to examine, read, study, or consider it carefully.","zh":"look at something 的意思是仔細檢查、閱讀、研究或考慮某事。"},{"en":"A doctor may look at test results before giving advice.","zh":"醫生可能在給建議前查看測試結果。"},{"en":"Students should look at the question carefully before writing an answer.","zh":"學生在寫答案前應仔細查看題目。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean more than simply seeing something with your eyes.","zh":"這個短語不只是用眼睛看見某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"give someone a sense of","meaning":"令某人感受到……","examples":[{"en":"The sources give readers a sense of how catastrophic the volcano was.","zh":"這些資料令讀者感受到這次火山噴發有多災難性。"},{"en":"To give someone a sense of something means to help them understand or feel what it was like.","zh":"give someone a sense of something 的意思是幫助某人理解或感受某事是怎樣的。"},{"en":"Old photographs can give students a sense of how crowded the city used to be.","zh":"舊照片可以令學生感受到這座城市以前有多擁擠。"},{"en":"Personal stories give readers a sense of a disaster because they show real human experience.","zh":"個人故事令讀者感受到災難，因為它們展示真實的人類經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase often connects facts with feeling or imagination.","zh":"這個短語常把事實與感受或想像連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"catastrophic","meaning":"災難性的","examples":[{"en":"The primary sources show how catastrophic the volcano was.","zh":"原始資料顯示這次火山噴發有多災難性。"},{"en":"Catastrophic means causing sudden, severe, and widespread damage.","zh":"catastrophic 的意思是造成突然、嚴重而廣泛的破壞。"},{"en":"A catastrophic storm can destroy homes, roads, and power supplies in one night.","zh":"災難性風暴可以在一夜之間摧毀房屋、道路和電力供應。"},{"en":"If a hospital loses electricity during an emergency, the results could be catastrophic.","zh":"如果醫院在緊急情況中失去電力，結果可能是災難性的。"},{"en":"This word is much stronger than “serious”.","zh":"這個詞比 serious 強烈得多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"make sense of","meaning":"理解；弄明白","examples":[{"en":"People at the time were trying to make sense of the science.","zh":"當時的人正試圖弄明白相關科學。"},{"en":"To make sense of something means to understand it, especially when it is confusing or unfamiliar.","zh":"make sense of something 的意思是理解某事，尤其是它令人困惑或陌生時。"},{"en":"Students may need a diagram to make sense of a difficult science process.","zh":"學生可能需要圖表來理解困難的科學過程。"},{"en":"People ask questions when they are trying to make sense of surprising events.","zh":"當人們試圖理解令人意外的事件時，他們會提出問題。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes the effort to understand something complicated.","zh":"這個短語常描述努力理解複雜事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"for the first time","meaning":"第一次","examples":[{"en":"People were trying to make sense of volcanic science for the first time.","zh":"人們第一次試圖理解火山科學。"},{"en":"For the first time means something has never happened before that moment.","zh":"for the first time 的意思是某事在那一刻之前從未發生過。"},{"en":"A child may feel nervous when speaking on stage for the first time.","zh":"小孩第一次上台說話時可能感到緊張。"},{"en":"Doing something for the first time can be difficult because there is no past experience to rely on.","zh":"第一次做某事可能困難，因為沒有過往經驗可以依靠。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a new experience or beginning.","zh":"這個短語標示新的經驗或開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what I found more significant was","meaning":"我覺得更重要的是……","examples":[{"en":"Michelle says what she found more significant was the political impact.","zh":"Michelle 說她覺得更重要的是政治影響。"},{"en":"What I found more significant was introduces the thing the speaker considers more important than other points.","zh":"what I found more significant was 用來引出說話者認為比其他要點更重要的事情。"},{"en":"In the report, what I found more significant was the rise in student stress, not the small drop in grades.","zh":"在報告中，我覺得更重要的是學生壓力上升，而不是成績小幅下降。"},{"en":"This phrase helps shift attention from one detail to a more important one.","zh":"這個短語幫助把注意力從一個細節轉向更重要的一點。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing levels of importance.","zh":"它適合用於比較重要性高低。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"impact directly and indirectly on","meaning":"直接及間接影響……","examples":[{"en":"The eruption impacted directly and indirectly on political events.","zh":"這次火山噴發直接及間接影響政治事件。"},{"en":"To impact directly and indirectly on something means to affect it in obvious ways and also through less obvious chains of results.","zh":"impact directly and indirectly on something 的意思是以明顯方式以及較不明顯的連鎖結果影響某事。"},{"en":"A transport strike can impact directly and indirectly on schools by delaying students and disrupting parents’ work.","zh":"交通罷工可以直接及間接影響學校，例如令學生遲到並打亂父母工作。"},{"en":"Climate events may indirectly affect food prices even when farms are far away.","zh":"氣候事件即使發生在遠方農場，也可能間接影響食物價格。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that effects can be immediate and hidden.","zh":"這個短語顯示影響可以是即時的，也可以是隱藏的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"political events","meaning":"政治事件","examples":[{"en":"The students want to discuss how the eruption affected political events.","zh":"學生想討論這次火山噴發如何影響政治事件。"},{"en":"Political events are important happenings connected with governments, laws, leaders, protests, or public power.","zh":"political events 是與政府、法律、領袖、抗議或公共權力有關的重要事件。"},{"en":"Elections, revolutions, government reforms, and wars are political events.","zh":"選舉、革命、政府改革和戰爭都是政治事件。"},{"en":"Economic hardship can influence political events because people may demand change.","zh":"經濟困難可以影響政治事件，因為人們可能要求改變。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on public affairs rather than private life.","zh":"這個短語集中於公共事務，而不是私人生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"以及","examples":[{"en":"The eruption affected political events as well as society and the economy.","zh":"這次火山噴發影響政治事件，以及社會和經濟。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to something else.","zh":"as well as 的意思是除了某事之外，也包括另一事。"},{"en":"A good school supports mental health as well as academic results.","zh":"好學校支援精神健康以及學業成績。"},{"en":"A storm can damage roads as well as homes and farms.","zh":"風暴可以破壞道路以及房屋和農場。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another area, benefit, or effect.","zh":"這個短語加入另一個範疇、好處或影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"massive social and economic consequences","meaning":"巨大的社會和經濟後果","examples":[{"en":"The eruption had massive social and economic consequences.","zh":"這次火山噴發帶來巨大的社會和經濟後果。"},{"en":"Massive social and economic consequences are very large effects on people’s lives, communities, jobs, prices, and money.","zh":"massive social and economic consequences 是對人們生活、社區、工作、價格和金錢造成的巨大影響。"},{"en":"A long lockdown can have massive social and economic consequences for families and small businesses.","zh":"長期封城可以對家庭和小企業造成巨大的社會和經濟後果。"},{"en":"Disasters affect society when people lose homes, and they affect the economy when work and trade stop.","zh":"當人們失去家園，災難會影響社會；當工作和貿易停止，災難會影響經濟。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an event changes both daily life and financial systems.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個事件同時改變日常生活和金融系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"main focus","meaning":"主要焦點","examples":[{"en":"The political, social and economic impact should be the main focus of the presentation.","zh":"政治、社會和經濟影響應該是簡報的主要焦點。"},{"en":"The main focus is the most important topic or point that receives the most attention.","zh":"main focus 是獲得最多注意的最重要題目或觀點。"},{"en":"In a health talk, the main focus may be how to prevent illness, not how to treat it.","zh":"在健康講座中，主要焦點可能是如何預防疾病，而不是如何治療疾病。"},{"en":"Choosing a clear main focus helps a presentation stay organised and easy to follow.","zh":"選擇清晰主要焦點有助簡報保持有組織並容易跟上。"},{"en":"Without a main focus, listeners may not know what the speaker is trying to prove.","zh":"沒有主要焦點，聽眾可能不知道講者想證明甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"observations made by","meaning":"由……作出的觀察","examples":[{"en":"The observations made by people at the time were interesting.","zh":"由當時的人作出的觀察很有趣。"},{"en":"Observations made by someone are things that person noticed, recorded, or described.","zh":"observations made by someone 是某人注意到、記錄或描述的事情。"},{"en":"Observations made by nurses can help doctors understand a patient’s condition.","zh":"由護士作出的觀察可以幫助醫生了解病人情況。"},{"en":"Careful observations can become valuable evidence when many people report similar details.","zh":"當許多人報告相似細節，仔細觀察可以成為有價值證據。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what people saw or noticed.","zh":"這個短語集中於人們看見或注意到甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at the time","meaning":"當時","examples":[{"en":"People at the time recorded what they saw after the eruption.","zh":"當時的人記錄了火山噴發後他們看見的事情。"},{"en":"At the time means during the period when something was happening.","zh":"at the time 的意思是在某事發生的那段時期。"},{"en":"People at the time did not have smartphones to record every event immediately.","zh":"當時的人沒有智能電話可以立即記錄每件事。"},{"en":"Understanding what people knew at the time helps us judge their decisions more fairly.","zh":"理解人們當時知道甚麼，有助我們更公平地判斷他們的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the historical moment being discussed.","zh":"這個短語指向正在討論的歷史時刻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give a consistent account of","meaning":"對……作出一致描述","examples":[{"en":"The sources gave a pretty consistent account of what happened.","zh":"這些資料對發生的事情作出相當一致的描述。"},{"en":"To give a consistent account of something means to describe it in a way that matches other descriptions and does not keep changing.","zh":"give a consistent account of something 的意思是以與其他描述吻合、而且沒有不斷改變的方式描述某事。"},{"en":"Witnesses gave a consistent account of the accident, so the police trusted their evidence more.","zh":"目擊者對意外作出一致描述，所以警方更信任他們的證供。"},{"en":"Consistent accounts make an event easier to reconstruct because the details support one another.","zh":"一致描述令事件更容易重建，因為細節互相支持。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing reports from different people.","zh":"這個短語適合用於比較不同人的報告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what happened","meaning":"發生的事情","examples":[{"en":"The writers gave similar accounts of what happened.","zh":"這些作者對發生的事情作出相似描述。"},{"en":"What happened means the events or facts of a situation.","zh":"what happened 的意思是某情況中的事件或事實。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to explain what happened during a playground argument.","zh":"老師可能要求學生解釋操場爭執中發生的事情。"},{"en":"Knowing what happened is the first step before deciding who is responsible.","zh":"知道發生了甚麼，是決定誰有責任前的第一步。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for the actual events, not rumours or guesses.","zh":"這個短語要求實際事件，而不是謠言或猜測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"even if","meaning":"即使","examples":[{"en":"The accounts were consistent even if writers used different terminology.","zh":"即使作者使用不同術語，描述仍然一致。"},{"en":"Even if means although a particular condition is true or possible.","zh":"even if 的意思是即使某條件是真實或可能的。"},{"en":"You should check the timetable even if you think you know the bus time.","zh":"即使你以為知道巴士時間，也應該查看時間表。"},{"en":"Even if two people use different words, they may still describe the same event.","zh":"即使兩個人使用不同字眼，他們仍可能描述同一事件。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one fact does not change the main point.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個事實不會改變主要觀點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"use the same terminology","meaning":"使用相同術語","examples":[{"en":"The writers did not always use the same terminology.","zh":"這些作者並不總是使用相同術語。"},{"en":"To use the same terminology means to use the same technical words or labels.","zh":"use the same terminology 的意思是使用相同的專門詞語或標籤。"},{"en":"Doctors and patients may not use the same terminology when describing pain.","zh":"醫生和病人在描述疼痛時可能不使用相同術語。"},{"en":"If team members use different terminology, they may misunderstand each other even when they mean the same thing.","zh":"如果團隊成員使用不同術語，即使意思相同也可能誤解彼此。"},{"en":"Shared terminology helps a group discuss a complex topic more clearly.","zh":"共同術語有助團隊更清楚討論複雜題目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"weather stations","meaning":"氣象站","examples":[{"en":"There were already many weather stations established by that time.","zh":"到那時已經有許多氣象站建立了。"},{"en":"Weather stations are places or instruments used to measure weather conditions such as temperature, pressure, wind, and rainfall.","zh":"weather stations 是用來量度氣溫、氣壓、風和降雨等天氣情況的地方或儀器。"},{"en":"A school weather station can help students record daily temperature and rainfall.","zh":"學校氣象站可以幫助學生記錄每日氣溫和降雨量。"},{"en":"Weather stations provide data that helps people compare changes across places and times.","zh":"氣象站提供數據，幫助人們比較不同地點和時間的變化。"},{"en":"Without weather stations, unusual weather patterns would be harder to prove.","zh":"沒有氣象站，異常天氣模式會更難被證明。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be established by that time","meaning":"到那時已經建立","examples":[{"en":"Many weather stations had been established by that time.","zh":"到那時已經有許多氣象站建立了。"},{"en":"To be established by that time means to have already been created or set up before that point.","zh":"be established by that time 的意思是在該時間點之前已經被創立或設立。"},{"en":"By the time the new students arrived, clear school rules had already been established.","zh":"到新學生到達時，清晰校規已經建立。"},{"en":"If a support system is established early, people can respond faster during a crisis.","zh":"如果支援系統早早建立，人們在危機中就能更快回應。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an existing arrangement with a specific moment in the past.","zh":"這個短語把已有安排與過去某個特定時刻連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"by the hour","meaning":"按小時","examples":[{"en":"The records show how the weather changed, often by the hour.","zh":"這些紀錄顯示天氣如何變化，往往按小時記錄。"},{"en":"By the hour means hour by hour, with changes recorded or happening every hour.","zh":"by the hour 的意思是一小時一小時地記錄或發生。"},{"en":"During a storm, weather conditions can change by the hour.","zh":"風暴期間，天氣情況可以按小時變化。"},{"en":"Tracking something by the hour gives more detail than checking it once a day.","zh":"按小時追蹤某事，比每天檢查一次提供更多細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when changes happen quickly.","zh":"當變化發生得很快時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"writers at the time","meaning":"當時的作家","examples":[{"en":"Writers at the time used the term “Laki haze”.","zh":"當時的作家使用「Laki 霧霾」這個詞。"},{"en":"Writers at the time are people who wrote during the period being discussed.","zh":"writers at the time 是在所討論時期寫作的人。"},{"en":"Writers at the time described factory smoke before modern pollution science existed.","zh":"當時的作家在現代污染科學出現前描述工廠煙霧。"},{"en":"Their words can show how people understood events before later explanations became available.","zh":"他們的文字可以顯示在後來解釋出現前，人們如何理解事件。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate historical voices from modern writers.","zh":"這個短語幫助區分歷史聲音與現代作者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Laki haze","meaning":"Laki 霧霾","examples":[{"en":"Writers used “Laki haze” to describe the volcanic fog.","zh":"作家使用「Laki 霧霾」來描述火山霧。"},{"en":"Laki haze refers to the strange haze or fog linked to the Laki eruption.","zh":"Laki haze 指與 Laki 火山噴發有關的奇怪霧霾或霧。"},{"en":"Historical reports used Laki haze to explain unusual skies, poor air, and health complaints.","zh":"歷史報告使用 Laki 霧霾來解釋異常天空、空氣差和健康投訴。"},{"en":"Naming the Laki haze helped people describe a phenomenon they did not fully understand.","zh":"命名 Laki 霧霾幫助人們描述一個他們未完全理解的現象。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a visible atmospheric effect with a volcanic event.","zh":"這個短語把可見的大氣影響與火山事件連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"volcanic fog","meaning":"火山霧","examples":[{"en":"The Laki haze was a volcanic fog that spread across Europe.","zh":"Laki 霧霾是蔓延至歐洲各地的火山霧。"},{"en":"Volcanic fog is fog or haze formed from gases and particles released by a volcano.","zh":"volcanic fog 是由火山釋放的氣體和微粒形成的霧或霧霾。"},{"en":"Volcanic fog can irritate the eyes, throat, and lungs.","zh":"火山霧可以刺激眼睛、喉嚨和肺部。"},{"en":"If volcanic fog spreads widely, people far from the volcano may still feel its effects.","zh":"如果火山霧廣泛擴散，遠離火山的人仍可能感受到其影響。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a weather-like effect caused by volcanic activity.","zh":"這個短語解釋由火山活動造成、類似天氣的現象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"spread across","meaning":"蔓延至……各地","examples":[{"en":"The volcanic fog spread across Europe.","zh":"火山霧蔓延至歐洲各地。"},{"en":"To spread across an area means to move or extend over that area.","zh":"spread across an area 的意思是移動或延伸到該地區各處。"},{"en":"News of the school closure spread across the town within an hour.","zh":"學校停課的消息在一小時內傳遍全鎮。"},{"en":"Smoke can spread across a city when wind carries it from a fire.","zh":"當風把火災煙霧吹走，煙可以蔓延至城市各處。"},{"en":"This phrase shows movement from one place to many places.","zh":"這個短語顯示由一地移動到多地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be used to","meaning":"習慣於……","examples":[{"en":"People realised that this was not the sort of fog they were used to.","zh":"人們意識到這不是他們習慣的那種霧。"},{"en":"To be used to something means to be familiar with it because you have experienced it before.","zh":"be used to something 的意思是因以前經歷過而對某事熟悉。"},{"en":"A student who is used to quiet study rooms may find a busy café distracting.","zh":"習慣於安靜自修室的學生，可能覺得繁忙咖啡店令人分心。"},{"en":"When something is unlike what people are used to, they may feel confused or worried.","zh":"當某事不同於人們習慣的情況，他們可能感到困惑或擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes familiarity, not past habit only.","zh":"這個短語描述熟悉感，而不只是過去習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pre-industrial times","meaning":"前工業時代","examples":[{"en":"The Laki eruption happened in pre-industrial times.","zh":"Laki 火山噴發發生在前工業時代。"},{"en":"Pre-industrial times are the period before large-scale industry, factories, and modern industrial pollution became common.","zh":"pre-industrial times 是大型工業、工廠和現代工業污染普遍出現之前的時期。"},{"en":"In pre-industrial times, most people lived closer to farming and manual work.","zh":"在前工業時代，大多數人的生活更接近農業和體力勞動。"},{"en":"Events from pre-industrial times may be harder to study because records were less complete.","zh":"前工業時代的事件可能較難研究，因為紀錄不太完整。"},{"en":"This phrase gives historical context before modern industry changed society.","zh":"這個短語提供現代工業改變社會前的歷史背景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"experience sulphur-smelling fog","meaning":"經歷帶硫磺味的霧","examples":[{"en":"People had not experienced sulphur-smelling fog before.","zh":"人們以前沒有經歷過帶硫磺味的霧。"},{"en":"To experience sulphur-smelling fog means to live through or encounter fog that smells like sulphur.","zh":"experience sulphur-smelling fog 的意思是經歷或遇到有硫磺氣味的霧。"},{"en":"Residents may become alarmed if they experience sulphur-smelling fog near a volcano.","zh":"如果居民在火山附近經歷帶硫磺味的霧，他們可能會感到驚慌。"},{"en":"An unfamiliar smell in fog can make people suspect pollution, fire, or chemical danger.","zh":"霧中有陌生氣味，可以令人懷疑有污染、火災或化學危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both a physical event and the human experience of it.","zh":"這個短語同時描述身體事件和人對它的經歷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sulphur-smelling","meaning":"帶硫磺味的","examples":[{"en":"The fog was unusual because it was sulphur-smelling.","zh":"這霧很不尋常，因為它帶硫磺味。"},{"en":"Sulphur-smelling means having a strong smell like sulphur, often like rotten eggs.","zh":"sulphur-smelling 的意思是有強烈硫磺氣味，常像臭雞蛋。"},{"en":"A sulphur-smelling gas leak would make people leave the area quickly.","zh":"帶硫磺味的氣體洩漏會令人迅速離開該區。"},{"en":"Sulphur-smelling air can be frightening because it suggests chemical or volcanic activity.","zh":"帶硫磺味的空氣可能令人害怕，因為它暗示有化學或火山活動。"},{"en":"This adjective describes smell, not colour or thickness.","zh":"這個形容詞描述氣味，而不是顏色或濃度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reports from the period","meaning":"當時的報告","examples":[{"en":"Reports from the period described health problems caused by the haze.","zh":"當時的報告描述了霧霾造成的健康問題。"},{"en":"Reports from the period are written accounts produced during the historical time being studied.","zh":"reports from the period 是在被研究歷史時期中產生的書面記錄。"},{"en":"Reports from the period may show what people noticed before modern science explained it.","zh":"當時的報告可能顯示在現代科學解釋之前，人們注意到甚麼。"},{"en":"Historians compare reports from the period to see which details appear repeatedly.","zh":"歷史學家比較當時的報告，看看哪些細節反覆出現。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies historical evidence from the same time as the event.","zh":"這個短語指出與事件同時期的歷史證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"blame something for","meaning":"把……歸咎於……","examples":[{"en":"Reports from the period blamed the haze for health problems.","zh":"當時的報告把健康問題歸咎於霧霾。"},{"en":"To blame something for a problem means to say it caused the problem.","zh":"blame something for a problem 的意思是說某事造成該問題。"},{"en":"Residents blamed the noisy roadworks for their poor sleep.","zh":"居民把睡眠差歸咎於嘈雜道路工程。"},{"en":"People may blame the wrong cause when they do not have enough evidence.","zh":"當人們沒有足夠證據，可能把問題歸咎於錯誤原因。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a problem with its supposed cause.","zh":"這個短語把問題與其被認為的成因連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an increase in","meaning":"……的增加","examples":[{"en":"The reports blamed the haze for an increase in headaches.","zh":"這些報告把頭痛增加歸咎於霧霾。"},{"en":"An increase in something means a rise in its number, amount, or level.","zh":"an increase in something 的意思是某事物的數量、程度或水平上升。"},{"en":"A school may notice an increase in absences during flu season.","zh":"學校可能在流感季節注意到缺席人數增加。"},{"en":"An increase in prices can make daily life harder for low-income families.","zh":"物價增加可以令低收入家庭日常生活更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upward change.","zh":"這個短語描述向上的變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"respiratory issues","meaning":"呼吸系統問題","examples":[{"en":"The haze was linked to respiratory issues.","zh":"霧霾與呼吸系統問題有關。"},{"en":"Respiratory issues are health problems related to breathing, the lungs, or the airways.","zh":"respiratory issues 是與呼吸、肺部或氣道有關的健康問題。"},{"en":"Dusty classrooms can cause respiratory issues for students with asthma.","zh":"塵多的課室可以令患哮喘的學生出現呼吸系統問題。"},{"en":"Air pollution may increase respiratory issues because people breathe in harmful particles.","zh":"空氣污染可能增加呼吸系統問題，因為人們吸入有害微粒。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than simply saying “breathing problems”.","zh":"這個短語比單純說 breathing problems 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"asthma attacks","meaning":"哮喘發作","examples":[{"en":"Reports mentioned an increase in asthma attacks.","zh":"報告提到哮喘發作增加。"},{"en":"Asthma attacks are sudden episodes when a person with asthma struggles to breathe.","zh":"asthma attacks 是哮喘患者突然呼吸困難的情況。"},{"en":"Smoke, dust, cold air, or stress can trigger asthma attacks.","zh":"煙、灰塵、冷空氣或壓力都可以引發哮喘發作。"},{"en":"During an asthma attack, a person may need medicine quickly to open the airways.","zh":"哮喘發作時，患者可能需要迅速用藥打開氣道。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a serious breathing event, not ordinary coughing.","zh":"這個短語指嚴重呼吸事件，而不是普通咳嗽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cover the sun","meaning":"遮住太陽","examples":[{"en":"The haze covered the sun and changed its colour.","zh":"霧霾遮住太陽，並改變了它的顏色。"},{"en":"To cover the sun means to block sunlight so the sun is partly or fully hidden.","zh":"cover the sun 的意思是阻擋陽光，使太陽部分或完全被遮蔽。"},{"en":"Thick clouds can cover the sun and make the afternoon feel dark.","zh":"厚雲可以遮住太陽，令下午感覺昏暗。"},{"en":"Smoke covering the sun can lower visibility and make people worried about air quality.","zh":"煙霧遮住太陽可以降低能見度，並令人擔心空氣質素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something coming between the sun and observers.","zh":"這個短語描述某物位於太陽與觀察者之間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make it look","meaning":"令它看起來……","examples":[{"en":"The haze made the sun look a strange red colour.","zh":"霧霾令太陽看起來呈奇怪的紅色。"},{"en":"To make something look a certain way means to cause it to appear that way.","zh":"make something look a certain way 的意思是令某物看起來呈某種樣子。"},{"en":"Bright classroom lights can make a whiteboard look too shiny.","zh":"明亮課室燈光可以令白板看起來太反光。"},{"en":"Smoke in the air can make buildings look grey and distant.","zh":"空氣中的煙可以令建築物看起來灰暗而遙遠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes appearance, not necessarily reality.","zh":"這個短語描述外觀，而不一定是現實本身。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a strange red colour","meaning":"奇怪的紅色","examples":[{"en":"The sun appeared a strange red colour through the haze.","zh":"透過霧霾，太陽呈現奇怪的紅色。"},{"en":"A strange red colour means an unusual red shade that looks surprising or unnatural.","zh":"a strange red colour 是一種不尋常、令人驚訝或不自然的紅色。"},{"en":"During a sandstorm, the sky may turn a strange red colour.","zh":"沙塵暴期間，天空可能變成奇怪的紅色。"},{"en":"An unusual colour in the sky can make people suspect smoke, dust, or pollution.","zh":"天空出現異常顏色，可能令人懷疑有煙、塵或污染。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights how visually unusual something appears.","zh":"這個短語突出某物在視覺上有多不尋常。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"must have been","meaning":"一定是……","examples":[{"en":"Adam says the red sun must have been very weird.","zh":"Adam 說紅色太陽一定是非常奇怪。"},{"en":"Must have been is used to make a strong guess about the past.","zh":"must have been 用來對過去作出強烈推測。"},{"en":"The roads are wet, so it must have been raining earlier.","zh":"道路濕了，所以之前一定下過雨。"},{"en":"If everyone was silent after the announcement, the news must have been shocking.","zh":"如果公告後人人沉默，消息一定很震驚。"},{"en":"This phrase shows high certainty, but it is still an inference.","zh":"這個短語顯示高度肯定，但仍是推論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"write about","meaning":"寫及；記述","examples":[{"en":"Benjamin Franklin wrote about the Laki haze.","zh":"Benjamin Franklin 寫及 Laki 霧霾。"},{"en":"To write about something means to describe, discuss, or explain it in writing.","zh":"write about something 的意思是以文字描述、討論或解釋某事。"},{"en":"Students may write about a natural disaster after reading eyewitness reports.","zh":"學生閱讀目擊者報告後，可能寫及一場自然災害。"},{"en":"Writing about an event helps preserve details for later readers.","zh":"記述一個事件能為後來讀者保存細節。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the topic of written work.","zh":"這個短語集中於文字作品的題目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"American ambassador","meaning":"美國大使","examples":[{"en":"Benjamin Franklin was the American ambassador in Paris at the time.","zh":"Benjamin Franklin 當時是駐巴黎的美國大使。"},{"en":"An American ambassador is an official representative of the United States in another country.","zh":"American ambassador 是美國在另一個國家的官方代表。"},{"en":"An ambassador may meet government leaders, protect citizens, and explain their country’s views.","zh":"大使可能會見政府領袖、保護公民，並解釋本國立場。"},{"en":"Ambassadors can record important observations because they often communicate across countries.","zh":"大使可以記錄重要觀察，因為他們常在國家之間溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a diplomatic role.","zh":"這個短語描述外交角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at first","meaning":"起初","examples":[{"en":"At first, no one realised that the haze was caused by the eruption.","zh":"起初，沒有人意識到霧霾是由火山噴發造成的。"},{"en":"At first means in the beginning, before people understood more or before things changed.","zh":"at first 的意思是一開始，在人們理解更多或事情改變之前。"},{"en":"At first, the new student felt nervous, but later she made friends.","zh":"起初，新學生感到緊張，但後來她交到朋友。"},{"en":"People often misunderstand a problem at first because they do not yet have enough evidence.","zh":"人們起初常誤解問題，因為他們還沒有足夠證據。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the beginning with what happened later.","zh":"這個短語把開始時與後來發展作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be caused by","meaning":"由……造成","examples":[{"en":"The haze was caused by the volcanic eruption in Iceland.","zh":"霧霾是由冰島火山噴發造成的。"},{"en":"To be caused by something means to happen because of that thing.","zh":"be caused by something 的意思是因某事而發生。"},{"en":"The delay was caused by heavy traffic near the tunnel.","zh":"延誤是由隧道附近交通繁忙造成的。"},{"en":"A rash may be caused by an allergy, so doctors ask about food and medicine.","zh":"皮疹可能由過敏造成，所以醫生會詢問食物和藥物。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an effect with its cause.","zh":"這個短語把結果與原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"volcanic eruption","meaning":"火山噴發","examples":[{"en":"The volcanic eruption in Iceland caused the haze.","zh":"冰島的火山噴發造成霧霾。"},{"en":"A volcanic eruption happens when lava, ash, gas, or rocks are forced out of a volcano.","zh":"volcanic eruption 是熔岩、火山灰、氣體或岩石從火山中被噴出的事件。"},{"en":"People living near a volcano may evacuate before a volcanic eruption.","zh":"住在火山附近的人可能在火山噴發前疏散。"},{"en":"A volcanic eruption can affect air travel if ash rises high into the atmosphere.","zh":"如果火山灰升到高空，火山噴發可以影響航空交通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a powerful geological event.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的地質事件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"before anyone else","meaning":"比任何人都早","examples":[{"en":"Michelle says Benjamin Franklin realised the cause before anyone else.","zh":"Michelle 說 Benjamin Franklin 比任何人都早意識到原因。"},{"en":"Before anyone else means earlier than all other people.","zh":"before anyone else 的意思是比所有其他人都更早。"},{"en":"A good doctor may notice a patient’s symptoms before anyone else does.","zh":"好醫生可能比任何人都早注意到病人的症狀。"},{"en":"Discovering something before anyone else can bring credit, but evidence is still needed.","zh":"比任何人都早發現某事可以帶來功勞，但仍需要證據。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises being first.","zh":"這個短語強調最先做到。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be credited with","meaning":"被認為有……的功勞","examples":[{"en":"Benjamin Franklin is often credited with identifying the cause of the haze.","zh":"Benjamin Franklin 常被認為有識別霧霾成因的功勞。"},{"en":"To be credited with something means to be recognised as having done it or contributed to it.","zh":"be credited with something 的意思是被認可曾做成某事或對某事有貢獻。"},{"en":"A scientist may be credited with discovering a new treatment.","zh":"科學家可能被認為有發現新療法的功勞。"},{"en":"People can be credited with an idea even if others reached a similar conclusion separately.","zh":"即使其他人也獨立得出相似結論，一個人仍可能被認為有某想法的功勞。"},{"en":"This phrase is about public recognition or historical credit.","zh":"這個短語關乎公開認可或歷史功勞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"apparently","meaning":"顯然；據說","examples":[{"en":"Adam says Franklin is often credited with that, apparently.","zh":"Adam 說 Franklin 據說常被認為有那個功勞。"},{"en":"Apparently means according to what people say or according to the information available.","zh":"apparently 的意思是根據人們所說或現有資料看來。"},{"en":"Apparently, the library will close early tomorrow because of maintenance.","zh":"據說圖書館明天會因維修提早關門。"},{"en":"Speakers use apparently when they are reporting information but may not be completely certain.","zh":"說話者在轉述資料但未必完全確定時，會使用 apparently。"},{"en":"This word can signal that the information comes from another source.","zh":"這個詞可以表示資訊來自另一來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"naturalist","meaning":"博物學家","examples":[{"en":"A French naturalist may have identified the cause before Franklin.","zh":"一位法國博物學家可能比 Franklin 更早識別成因。"},{"en":"A naturalist is a person who studies plants, animals, rocks, weather, or other parts of the natural world.","zh":"naturalist 是研究植物、動物、岩石、天氣或自然世界其他部分的人。"},{"en":"A naturalist may keep careful notes about birds, insects, and seasonal changes.","zh":"博物學家可能仔細記錄鳥類、昆蟲和季節變化。"},{"en":"Naturalists were important before modern science became highly specialised.","zh":"在現代科學高度專門化之前，博物學家很重要。"},{"en":"This word describes someone who observes and studies nature.","zh":"這個詞描述觀察和研究自然的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"beat someone to it","meaning":"搶先某人一步做到","examples":[{"en":"A French naturalist beat Franklin to it.","zh":"一位法國博物學家搶先 Franklin 一步做到。"},{"en":"To beat someone to it means to do something before another person gets the chance.","zh":"beat someone to it 的意思是在另一人有機會前先做到某事。"},{"en":"I wanted to book the last ticket, but my friend beat me to it.","zh":"我想預訂最後一張票，但朋友搶先我一步訂了。"},{"en":"In research, one scientist may beat another to a discovery by publishing first.","zh":"在研究中，一名科學家可能透過先發表而搶先另一人一步發現。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often means someone acted faster.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，常表示某人行動更快。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"look it up","meaning":"查一下","examples":[{"en":"Adam would have to look up the naturalist’s name.","zh":"Adam 需要查一下那位博物學家的名字。"},{"en":"To look something up means to search for information in a book, online, or another source.","zh":"look something up 的意思是在書本、網上或其他來源搜尋資料。"},{"en":"If you do not know a word, you can look it up in a dictionary.","zh":"如果你不認識一個字，可以在字典中查一下。"},{"en":"Looking up facts helps prevent mistakes when preparing a presentation.","zh":"查證資料有助準備簡報時避免錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is practical and common in study and work.","zh":"這個短語很實用，常見於學習和工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have the same idea","meaning":"有相同想法","examples":[{"en":"Other naturalists had the same idea independently.","zh":"其他博物學家也獨立地有相同想法。"},{"en":"To have the same idea means two or more people think of a similar explanation, plan, or solution.","zh":"have the same idea 的意思是兩個或以上的人想到相似解釋、計劃或解決方法。"},{"en":"Two students may have the same idea for a science project without copying each other.","zh":"兩名學生可能在沒有抄襲下，對科學項目有相同想法。"},{"en":"People can have the same idea when they examine the same evidence carefully.","zh":"當人們仔細查看相同證據，可能會有相同想法。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights similarity in thought.","zh":"這個短語突出思想上的相似。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"independently of each other","meaning":"彼此獨立地","examples":[{"en":"The naturalists reached the same conclusion independently of each other.","zh":"這些博物學家彼此獨立地得出相同結論。"},{"en":"Independently of each other means separately, without working together or copying one another.","zh":"independently of each other 的意思是分開地、沒有一起工作或互相抄襲。"},{"en":"Two teams may solve the same problem independently of each other.","zh":"兩個團隊可能彼此獨立地解決同一問題。"},{"en":"If people reach the same result independently, the idea may seem more convincing.","zh":"如果人們彼此獨立地得出相同結果，該想法可能顯得更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing that agreement did not come from collaboration.","zh":"這個短語適合用於顯示一致並非來自合作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"immediate impact","meaning":"直接影響；即時影響","examples":[{"en":"The students discuss the immediate impact of the eruption.","zh":"學生討論火山噴發的即時影響。"},{"en":"Immediate impact means the effect that happens quickly after an event.","zh":"immediate impact 是事件發生後很快出現的影響。"},{"en":"The immediate impact of a power cut may be darkness, stopped lifts, and delayed work.","zh":"停電的即時影響可能是黑暗、電梯停用和工作延誤。"},{"en":"Immediate impacts are often easier to see than long-term consequences.","zh":"即時影響通常比長期後果更容易看見。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on early effects.","zh":"這個短語集中於早期影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"especially in","meaning":"尤其在……","examples":[{"en":"The immediate impact was enormous, especially in Iceland.","zh":"即時影響非常巨大，尤其在冰島。"},{"en":"Especially in means particularly in one place, group, or situation more than others.","zh":"especially in 的意思是特別在某地方、群體或情況中，比其他地方更明顯。"},{"en":"Heat can be dangerous, especially in crowded city areas with little shade.","zh":"炎熱可以很危險，尤其在缺少樹蔭的擁擠城市地區。"},{"en":"A problem may affect many people but be worse especially in poorer communities.","zh":"一個問題可能影響許多人，但尤其在較貧困社區更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights where something is most true or most serious.","zh":"這個短語突出某事最真實或最嚴重的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"volcanic ash","meaning":"火山灰","examples":[{"en":"The volcanic ash drifted swiftly after the eruption.","zh":"火山噴發後，火山灰迅速飄散。"},{"en":"Volcanic ash is tiny rock, mineral, and glass particles thrown into the air by a volcano.","zh":"volcanic ash 是火山噴到空中的微小岩石、礦物和玻璃顆粒。"},{"en":"Volcanic ash can cover roads, damage engines, and make breathing difficult.","zh":"火山灰可以覆蓋道路、損壞引擎，並令人呼吸困難。"},{"en":"If volcanic ash enters the atmosphere, flights may be cancelled for safety.","zh":"如果火山灰進入大氣，航班可能因安全原因取消。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to fine particles, not soft ash from paper or wood.","zh":"這個短語指細小顆粒，而不是紙或木頭燃燒後的柔軟灰燼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"drift swiftly","meaning":"迅速飄散","examples":[{"en":"The volcanic ash drifted swiftly across large areas.","zh":"火山灰迅速飄散至大片地區。"},{"en":"To drift swiftly means to be carried quickly by air or water without much control.","zh":"drift swiftly 的意思是被空氣或水快速帶走，幾乎不能控制。"},{"en":"Smoke can drift swiftly through a building if doors are left open.","zh":"如果門打開，煙可以迅速飄散到整棟建築物。"},{"en":"When ash drifts swiftly, warnings must reach people before conditions worsen.","zh":"當火山灰迅速飄散，警告必須在情況惡化前傳到人們手上。"},{"en":"This phrase combines smooth movement with speed.","zh":"這個短語結合平滑移動和速度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go on for so long","meaning":"持續那麼久","examples":[{"en":"Adam did not expect the effects to go on for so long.","zh":"Adam 沒有預料影響會持續那麼久。"},{"en":"To go on for so long means to continue for a much longer time than expected.","zh":"go on for so long 的意思是比預期持續久得多。"},{"en":"The meeting went on for so long that everyone missed lunch.","zh":"會議持續那麼久，以致人人都錯過午飯。"},{"en":"When a problem goes on for too long, people may become tired or frustrated.","zh":"當問題持續太久，人們可能變得疲倦或沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises surprising duration.","zh":"這個短語強調令人意外的持續時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"two years after","meaning":"在……兩年後","examples":[{"en":"Strange weather events were still being reported two years after the eruption.","zh":"在火山噴發兩年後，仍有人報告異常天氣事件。"},{"en":"Two years after means two years later than a particular event.","zh":"two years after 的意思是在某特定事件之後兩年。"},{"en":"Two years after moving school, she still remembered her first teacher.","zh":"轉校兩年後，她仍記得第一位老師。"},{"en":"If effects continue two years after a disaster, the event was probably very serious.","zh":"如果災難兩年後影響仍持續，該事件很可能非常嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a later time with an earlier event.","zh":"這個短語把較後時間與較早事件連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"strange weather events","meaning":"異常天氣事件","examples":[{"en":"Strange weather events were reported long after the eruption.","zh":"火山噴發很久後仍有人報告異常天氣事件。"},{"en":"Strange weather events are unusual weather conditions that surprise people or do not match normal patterns.","zh":"strange weather events 是令人驚訝或不符合正常模式的異常天氣情況。"},{"en":"Snow in a normally warm city would be a strange weather event.","zh":"在通常溫暖的城市下雪，就是異常天氣事件。"},{"en":"Strange weather events may lead people to ask whether climate or atmospheric conditions have changed.","zh":"異常天氣事件可能令人詢問氣候或大氣情況是否已改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unusual weather, not ordinary seasonal changes.","zh":"這個短語描述不尋常天氣，而不是普通季節變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as far away as","meaning":"遠至……","examples":[{"en":"Reports came from places as far away as North America and North Africa.","zh":"報告來自遠至北美和北非的地方。"},{"en":"As far away as means even from a very distant place.","zh":"as far away as 的意思是甚至來自非常遙遠的地方。"},{"en":"Visitors came from places as far away as Japan to attend the exhibition.","zh":"訪客從遠至日本的地方前來參加展覽。"},{"en":"If reports arrive from places far away, the event’s effects may have spread widely.","zh":"如果報告來自遙遠地方，事件影響可能已廣泛傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises surprising distance.","zh":"這個短語強調令人驚訝的距離。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hard to believe","meaning":"難以相信","examples":[{"en":"Michelle found the long-term effects hard to believe.","zh":"Michelle 覺得這些長期影響難以相信。"},{"en":"Hard to believe means difficult to accept as true because it seems surprising or extreme.","zh":"hard to believe 的意思是因某事令人驚訝或極端而難以接受為真。"},{"en":"It is hard to believe that a small leak could flood the whole classroom.","zh":"一個小漏洞可以浸滿整間課室，這很難相信。"},{"en":"Facts can be hard to believe when they are far beyond everyday experience.","zh":"當事實遠超日常經驗，它可能難以相信。"},{"en":"This phrase shows surprise, not necessarily disbelief after evidence is given.","zh":"這個短語表示驚訝，而不一定是在有證據後仍不相信。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"there was nothing anyone could do","meaning":"無人能做甚麼","examples":[{"en":"There was nothing anyone could do about the ash cloud.","zh":"對於火山灰雲，無人能做甚麼。"},{"en":"There was nothing anyone could do means people had no practical way to stop or change the situation.","zh":"there was nothing anyone could do 的意思是人們沒有實際方法阻止或改變情況。"},{"en":"When the last train had already left, there was nothing anyone could do except call a taxi.","zh":"當最後一班火車已開出，除了叫的士外，無人能做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase shows helplessness in the face of a problem.","zh":"這個短語顯示面對問題時的無力感。"},{"en":"It is often used when a situation is beyond human control.","zh":"它常用於情況超出人類控制時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ash cloud","meaning":"火山灰雲","examples":[{"en":"People could do nothing even if the ash cloud was coming towards them.","zh":"即使火山灰雲朝人們方向而來，他們也甚麼都做不了。"},{"en":"An ash cloud is a large mass of volcanic ash floating in the air after an eruption.","zh":"ash cloud 是火山噴發後漂浮在空中的大量火山灰。"},{"en":"An ash cloud can make skies dark and damage aircraft engines.","zh":"火山灰雲可以令天空變暗，並損壞飛機引擎。"},{"en":"If an ash cloud moves toward a town, people may need masks and indoor shelter.","zh":"如果火山灰雲移向城鎮，人們可能需要口罩和室內庇護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes airborne volcanic material.","zh":"這個短語描述空中的火山物質。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"come in one’s direction","meaning":"朝某人的方向而來","examples":[{"en":"The ash cloud was coming in people’s direction.","zh":"火山灰雲正朝人們的方向而來。"},{"en":"To come in one’s direction means to move toward someone or the place where they are.","zh":"come in one’s direction 的意思是朝某人或其所在地方移動。"},{"en":"If a storm is coming in your direction, you should close the windows and stay indoors.","zh":"如果風暴正朝你的方向而來，你應關窗並留在室內。"},{"en":"People feel anxious when danger is moving in their direction because they may soon be affected.","zh":"當危險朝自己方向而來，人們會感到焦慮，因為可能很快受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement toward a person or group.","zh":"這個短語描述朝某人或某群體移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"run through","meaning":"快速梳理；逐一講解","examples":[{"en":"The students should run through the consequences in different countries.","zh":"學生應快速梳理不同國家的後果。"},{"en":"To run through something means to review or explain it quickly and in order.","zh":"run through something 的意思是快速而有次序地重溫或解釋某事。"},{"en":"Before a performance, actors may run through the whole scene once more.","zh":"表演前，演員可能再次快速排練整個場景。"},{"en":"Running through key points helps speakers check that nothing important is missing.","zh":"快速梳理重點幫助講者檢查沒有漏掉重要內容。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a quick but organised review.","zh":"這個短語表示快速但有組織的重溫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"terrible consequences","meaning":"可怕後果","examples":[{"en":"The presentation will cover the terrible consequences of the eruption.","zh":"簡報將涵蓋火山噴發的可怕後果。"},{"en":"Terrible consequences are very bad results that cause suffering, damage, or loss.","zh":"terrible consequences 是造成痛苦、損害或損失的非常壞結果。"},{"en":"A serious road accident can have terrible consequences for families and communities.","zh":"嚴重交通意外可以為家庭和社區帶來可怕後果。"},{"en":"Poor preparation before a disaster can make the consequences even worse.","zh":"災難前準備不足可以令後果更加嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase is strong but less formal than “devastating consequences”.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈，但比 devastating consequences 較口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be experienced in","meaning":"在……經歷","examples":[{"en":"Terrible consequences were experienced in different countries.","zh":"不同國家都經歷了可怕後果。"},{"en":"To be experienced in a place means to be felt or lived through by people there.","zh":"be experienced in a place 的意思是某地的人感受到或經歷某事。"},{"en":"Water shortages were experienced in several villages during the drought.","zh":"乾旱期間，幾條村都經歷食水短缺。"},{"en":"If a problem is experienced in many areas, it may need national action.","zh":"如果多個地區都經歷一個問題，它可能需要全國性行動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on where people felt the effects.","zh":"這個短語集中於人們在哪裡感受到影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a varied range","meaning":"多樣化的範圍","examples":[{"en":"There was a varied range of consequences in different countries.","zh":"不同國家出現多樣化的後果。"},{"en":"A varied range means many different types or examples of something.","zh":"a varied range 的意思是某事物有許多不同類型或例子。"},{"en":"A library should offer a varied range of books for children with different interests.","zh":"圖書館應為興趣不同的兒童提供多樣化的書籍範圍。"},{"en":"A varied range of effects can make an event difficult to summarise simply.","zh":"多樣化的影響範圍可以令事件難以簡單概括。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises diversity and difference.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣性和差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"start with","meaning":"由……開始","examples":[{"en":"The students plan to start with Iceland.","zh":"學生計劃由冰島開始。"},{"en":"To start with something means to begin a discussion, task, or list with that item.","zh":"start with something 的意思是以某項內容開始討論、任務或清單。"},{"en":"When cleaning a room, you might start with the desk because it is the messiest part.","zh":"打掃房間時，你可能由書桌開始，因為它最凌亂。"},{"en":"Starting with the clearest example helps listeners understand the topic more easily.","zh":"由最清晰的例子開始，有助聽眾更容易理解題目。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the first step or first point.","zh":"這個短語顯示第一步或第一點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"impact on farming","meaning":"對農業的影響","examples":[{"en":"The impact on farming in Iceland was devastating.","zh":"對冰島農業的影響是毀滅性的。"},{"en":"Impact on farming means the effect on crops, animals, soil, food production, or farmers’ income.","zh":"impact on farming 指對農作物、牲畜、土壤、糧食生產或農民收入的影響。"},{"en":"A long drought can have a serious impact on farming by killing crops and reducing harvests.","zh":"長期乾旱可以透過令農作物死亡和收成下降，對農業造成嚴重影響。"},{"en":"If farming is badly affected, food prices may rise and rural families may lose income.","zh":"如果農業受到嚴重影響，食物價格可能上升，農村家庭可能失去收入。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an event with agricultural life.","zh":"這個短語把事件與農業生活連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dramatic things","meaning":"最劇烈的事情之一","examples":[{"en":"One of the most dramatic things was the effect on livestock.","zh":"最劇烈的事情之一是對牲畜的影響。"},{"en":"Dramatic things are events or changes that are striking, serious, or emotionally powerful.","zh":"dramatic things 是引人注目、嚴重或情感上強烈的事件或變化。"},{"en":"One dramatic thing after the storm was the sudden collapse of the bridge.","zh":"風暴後其中一件劇烈的事情是橋樑突然倒塌。"},{"en":"A dramatic change gets attention because it is hard to ignore.","zh":"劇烈變化會引起注意，因為它很難被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a particularly noticeable or powerful detail.","zh":"這個短語突出特別明顯或有力的細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"effect on livestock","meaning":"對牲畜的影響","examples":[{"en":"The eruption had a severe effect on livestock.","zh":"這次火山噴發對牲畜造成嚴重影響。"},{"en":"Effect on livestock means the impact on farm animals such as cows, sheep, goats, or horses.","zh":"effect on livestock 指對牛、羊、山羊或馬等農場動物的影響。"},{"en":"Contaminated grass can have an effect on livestock if animals eat it every day.","zh":"如果動物每天吃受污染的草，受污染草地可以對牲畜造成影響。"},{"en":"When livestock become sick, farmers may lose food, income, and transport animals.","zh":"當牲畜生病，農民可能失去食物、收入和運輸動物。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on farm animals rather than wild animals.","zh":"這個短語集中於農場動物，而不是野生動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"graze in the fields","meaning":"在田野中吃草","examples":[{"en":"The livestock were poisoned as they grazed in the fields.","zh":"牲畜在田野中吃草時中毒了。"},{"en":"To graze in the fields means animals eat grass or plants while moving around open farmland.","zh":"graze in the fields 的意思是動物在開闊農田中一邊移動一邊吃草或植物。"},{"en":"Cows graze in the fields during the day and return to shelter at night.","zh":"牛白天在田野中吃草，晚上回到棚舍。"},{"en":"If fields are contaminated, animals that graze there may become sick.","zh":"如果田野受污染，在那裡吃草的動物可能生病。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a normal feeding habit of farm animals.","zh":"這個短語描述農場動物正常的進食習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be poisoned","meaning":"中毒","examples":[{"en":"The animals were poisoned by contaminated vegetation.","zh":"這些動物因受污染植被而中毒。"},{"en":"To be poisoned means to become sick or die after taking in a harmful substance.","zh":"be poisoned 的意思是因攝入有害物質而生病或死亡。"},{"en":"A dog may be poisoned if it eats food containing dangerous chemicals.","zh":"如果狗吃了含危險化學物的食物，可能會中毒。"},{"en":"Poisoning can happen through food, water, air, or skin contact.","zh":"中毒可以透過食物、水、空氣或皮膚接觸發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harm caused by a toxic substance.","zh":"這個短語描述有毒物質造成的傷害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"vegetation","meaning":"植被；植物","examples":[{"en":"The livestock ate vegetation contaminated with fluorine.","zh":"牲畜吃了被氟污染的植被。"},{"en":"Vegetation means plants growing in an area, such as grass, bushes, leaves, and trees.","zh":"vegetation 指某地生長的植物，例如草、灌木、葉子和樹木。"},{"en":"Thick vegetation can make a hiking path difficult to see.","zh":"茂密植被可以令人難以看見行山徑。"},{"en":"Animals depend on vegetation for food, shelter, and nesting places.","zh":"動物依賴植被獲得食物、庇護和築巢地點。"},{"en":"This word refers to plant life in general, not one single plant.","zh":"這個詞泛指植物生命，而不是單一植物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be contaminated with","meaning":"被……污染","examples":[{"en":"The vegetation had been contaminated with fluorine.","zh":"植被已被氟污染。"},{"en":"To be contaminated with something means to be made dirty, unsafe, or harmful by that substance.","zh":"be contaminated with something 的意思是被某物弄髒、變得不安全或有害。"},{"en":"Drinking water can be contaminated with bacteria after a flood.","zh":"洪水後，飲用水可能被細菌污染。"},{"en":"If food is contaminated with chemicals, people should not eat it.","zh":"如果食物被化學品污染，人們不應進食。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something harmful has entered or covered another thing.","zh":"這個短語顯示有害物質進入或覆蓋另一事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fluorine","meaning":"氟","examples":[{"en":"The volcanic fallout contaminated vegetation with fluorine.","zh":"火山沉降物以氟污染了植被。"},{"en":"Fluorine is a chemical element that can be harmful in high amounts or certain forms.","zh":"fluorine 是一種化學元素，在高濃度或某些形式下可能有害。"},{"en":"Scientists may test soil for fluorine if animals become sick after eating local plants.","zh":"如果動物吃本地植物後生病，科學家可能檢測土壤中的氟。"},{"en":"Too much fluorine in vegetation can poison grazing animals.","zh":"植被中過多氟可以毒害吃草動物。"},{"en":"This word is scientific and usually appears in chemistry or environmental reports.","zh":"這個詞是科學用語，通常出現在化學或環境報告中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"由於……","examples":[{"en":"The vegetation was contaminated as a result of the volcanic fallout.","zh":"植被由於火山沉降物而受到污染。"},{"en":"As a result of means because of something that happened earlier.","zh":"as a result of 的意思是由於之前發生的某事。"},{"en":"The match was cancelled as a result of heavy rain.","zh":"比賽由於大雨而取消。"},{"en":"As a result of poor planning, the event ran out of chairs and water.","zh":"由於規劃不周，活動沒有足夠椅子和水。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly introduces a cause.","zh":"這個短語清楚引出原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"volcanic fallout","meaning":"火山沉降物","examples":[{"en":"The volcanic fallout contaminated plants in Iceland.","zh":"火山沉降物污染了冰島的植物。"},{"en":"Volcanic fallout is ash, dust, or chemical material that falls from the air after a volcanic eruption.","zh":"volcanic fallout 是火山噴發後從空中落下的火山灰、塵埃或化學物質。"},{"en":"Volcanic fallout can land on fields, roofs, rivers, and roads.","zh":"火山沉降物可以落在田野、屋頂、河流和道路上。"},{"en":"If volcanic fallout contains harmful chemicals, crops and animals may be affected.","zh":"如果火山沉降物含有有害化學物，農作物和動物可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes material that falls back to the ground after an eruption.","zh":"這個短語描述火山噴發後落回地面的物質。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bizarre weather patterns","meaning":"異常天氣模式","examples":[{"en":"Bizarre weather patterns led to severe drought in Egypt.","zh":"異常天氣模式導致埃及嚴重乾旱。"},{"en":"Bizarre weather patterns are very unusual or strange changes in weather.","zh":"bizarre weather patterns 是非常不尋常或奇怪的天氣變化。"},{"en":"A winter with sudden heatwaves and snow in the same week would show bizarre weather patterns.","zh":"同一星期內突然熱浪又下雪的冬天，會顯示異常天氣模式。"},{"en":"Bizarre weather patterns can confuse farmers because planting seasons become less predictable.","zh":"異常天氣模式可以令農民困惑，因為種植季節變得較難預測。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests weather that is far from normal.","zh":"這個短語表示天氣遠離正常情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"The bizarre weather patterns led to a severe drought.","zh":"異常天氣模式導致嚴重乾旱。"},{"en":"To lead to something means to cause it or make it happen.","zh":"lead to something 的意思是造成或促成某事發生。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can lead to weak concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致課堂專注力差。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can lead to flooding if drains are blocked.","zh":"如果排水渠堵塞，大雨可以導致水浸。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with a result.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"severe drought","meaning":"嚴重乾旱","examples":[{"en":"Egypt experienced a severe drought after the eruption.","zh":"火山噴發後，埃及經歷嚴重乾旱。"},{"en":"A severe drought is a long period with dangerously little rain or water.","zh":"severe drought 是長時間降雨或水源少到危險的情況。"},{"en":"A severe drought can dry up rivers, kill crops, and reduce drinking water supplies.","zh":"嚴重乾旱可以令河流乾涸、農作物死亡，並減少飲用水供應。"},{"en":"Farmers suffer during severe drought because plants and animals may not survive.","zh":"農民在嚴重乾旱期間受苦，因為植物和動物可能無法存活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious water shortage, not just a dry week.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重缺水，而不只是乾燥一星期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the Nile","meaning":"尼羅河","examples":[{"en":"The Nile did not flood because of the drought.","zh":"尼羅河因乾旱而沒有泛濫。"},{"en":"The Nile is a major river in northeastern Africa, historically central to farming in Egypt.","zh":"the Nile 是非洲東北部一條主要河流，歷史上對埃及農業十分重要。"},{"en":"Ancient Egyptian agriculture depended on the Nile’s water and fertile silt.","zh":"古埃及農業依賴尼羅河的水和肥沃淤泥。"},{"en":"If the Nile did not flood in the past, crops could fail and food shortages could follow.","zh":"如果過去尼羅河沒有泛濫，農作物可能歉收，並接着出現糧食短缺。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific river, not rivers in general.","zh":"這個短語指特定河流，而不是一般河流。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"crops failed","meaning":"農作物歉收","examples":[{"en":"The crops failed because the Nile did not flood.","zh":"由於尼羅河沒有泛濫，農作物歉收。"},{"en":"Crops failed means plants grown for food did not grow properly or did not produce enough harvest.","zh":"crops failed 的意思是用作糧食的植物沒有正常生長或沒有足夠收成。"},{"en":"Crops may fail if there is drought, disease, flooding, or poor soil.","zh":"如果出現乾旱、疾病、洪水或貧瘠土壤，農作物可能歉收。"},{"en":"When crops fail, food prices rise and farming families lose income.","zh":"當農作物歉收，食物價格會上升，農民家庭會失去收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes agricultural failure, not exam failure.","zh":"這個短語描述農業失敗，而不是考試失敗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"far from","meaning":"遠離……","examples":[{"en":"Egypt is far from where the eruption happened.","zh":"埃及遠離火山噴發發生的地方。"},{"en":"Far from means a long distance away from a place, idea, or condition.","zh":"far from 的意思是距離某地方、想法或狀態很遠。"},{"en":"The village is far from the nearest hospital, so emergencies are harder to manage.","zh":"這條村遠離最近的醫院，所以緊急情況較難處理。"},{"en":"A place far from a disaster can still be affected if weather or trade systems are connected.","zh":"遠離災難的地方仍可能受影響，如果天氣或貿易系統互相連接。"},{"en":"This phrase often highlights distance or difference.","zh":"這個短語常突出距離或差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"where the eruption happened","meaning":"火山噴發發生的地方","examples":[{"en":"Egypt was far from where the eruption happened.","zh":"埃及遠離火山噴發發生的地方。"},{"en":"Where the eruption happened means the place where the volcanic event took place.","zh":"where the eruption happened 的意思是火山事件發生的地點。"},{"en":"Scientists compare weather records with where the eruption happened to trace possible effects.","zh":"科學家把天氣紀錄與火山噴發發生的地方比較，以追蹤可能影響。"},{"en":"A place far from where a disaster happened can still feel indirect consequences.","zh":"遠離災難發生地的地方仍可能感受到間接後果。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the original location of the event.","zh":"這個短語指出事件的原始地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"famine","meaning":"饑荒","examples":[{"en":"The famine in Egypt caused many deaths.","zh":"埃及的饑荒造成許多人死亡。"},{"en":"A famine is an extreme shortage of food that causes hunger, illness, and death.","zh":"famine 是極端食物短缺，造成飢餓、疾病和死亡。"},{"en":"A long drought can lead to famine if crops fail and food supplies run out.","zh":"如果農作物歉收而食物供應耗盡，長期乾旱可以導致饑荒。"},{"en":"During a famine, families may sell possessions or leave home to search for food.","zh":"饑荒期間，家庭可能出售財物或離家尋找食物。"},{"en":"This word describes a severe food crisis, not ordinary hunger.","zh":"這個詞描述嚴重糧食危機，而不是普通飢餓。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lead to more people dying","meaning":"導致更多人死亡","examples":[{"en":"The famine led to more people dying than in any other country.","zh":"這場饑荒導致比任何其他國家更多人死亡。"},{"en":"To lead to more people dying means to cause a higher number of deaths.","zh":"lead to more people dying 的意思是造成死亡人數增加。"},{"en":"Delayed medical help can lead to more people dying after a disaster.","zh":"災難後醫療援助延誤可以導致更多人死亡。"},{"en":"Food shortages may lead to more people dying if aid does not arrive quickly.","zh":"如果援助沒有快速到達，食物短缺可能導致更多人死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly connects a cause with loss of life.","zh":"這個短語清楚把原因與生命損失連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"any other country","meaning":"任何其他國家","examples":[{"en":"More people died in Egypt than in any other country affected by the eruption.","zh":"在受火山噴發影響的國家中，埃及死亡人數比任何其他國家都多。"},{"en":"Any other country means every country except the one being discussed.","zh":"any other country 的意思是除了正在討論的國家以外的每一個國家。"},{"en":"This city had more visitors than any other city in the region last year.","zh":"這座城市去年遊客比該地區任何其他城市都多。"},{"en":"Comparing one place with any other country can show how unusually serious its situation was.","zh":"把一個地方與任何其他國家比較，可以顯示其情況有多異常嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to make a strong comparison.","zh":"這個短語用於作出強烈比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"worse than","meaning":"比……更糟","examples":[{"en":"The famine was worse than the plague.","zh":"這場饑荒比瘟疫更糟。"},{"en":"Worse than means more serious, harmful, unpleasant, or difficult than something else.","zh":"worse than 的意思是比另一事更嚴重、有害、令人不快或困難。"},{"en":"Missing the bus is annoying, but losing your wallet is worse than that.","zh":"錯過巴士令人煩惱，但丟失銀包比那更糟。"},{"en":"A problem may be worse than expected if it affects more people than first thought.","zh":"如果一個問題影響的人比最初想像更多，它可能比預期更糟。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to compare negative situations.","zh":"這個短語用於比較負面情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"plague","meaning":"瘟疫","examples":[{"en":"The famine in Egypt was worse than the plague.","zh":"埃及的饑荒比瘟疫更糟。"},{"en":"Plague is a serious infectious disease that has caused deadly outbreaks in history.","zh":"plague 是一種嚴重傳染病，歷史上曾造成致命爆發。"},{"en":"In historical writing, plague often represents fear, mass illness, and high death rates.","zh":"在歷史寫作中，瘟疫常代表恐懼、大規模疾病和高死亡率。"},{"en":"A community facing plague needs medical care, isolation measures, and public information.","zh":"面對瘟疫的社區需要醫療、隔離措施和公共資訊。"},{"en":"This word may refer to a specific disease or, more broadly, a devastating outbreak.","zh":"這個詞可以指特定疾病，也可以較廣泛地指毀滅性疫情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mortality rate","meaning":"死亡率","examples":[{"en":"The mortality rate in the UK went up a lot.","zh":"英國的死亡率大幅上升。"},{"en":"Mortality rate means the number or percentage of people who die in a particular group or period.","zh":"mortality rate 是特定群體或時期中死亡人數或比例。"},{"en":"Doctors track the mortality rate during a disease outbreak to understand its severity.","zh":"醫生在疾病爆發期間追蹤死亡率，以了解其嚴重程度。"},{"en":"A rising mortality rate may show that health conditions or environmental conditions have worsened.","zh":"死亡率上升可能顯示健康情況或環境情況惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in statistics, medicine, and history.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於統計、醫學和歷史。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"go up a lot","meaning":"大幅上升","examples":[{"en":"The mortality rate went up a lot after the eruption.","zh":"火山噴發後，死亡率大幅上升。"},{"en":"To go up a lot means to increase greatly.","zh":"go up a lot 的意思是大幅增加。"},{"en":"Food prices went up a lot after the storm damaged farms.","zh":"風暴破壞農場後，食物價格大幅上升。"},{"en":"If hospital visits go up a lot, officials may investigate the cause.","zh":"如果求診人數大幅上升，官員可能調查原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and describes a large rise.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，描述大幅增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"presumably from","meaning":"推測是因為……","examples":[{"en":"The increase was presumably from respiratory illnesses.","zh":"這種增加推測是因為呼吸系統疾病。"},{"en":"Presumably from means probably caused by something, based on available evidence but without complete certainty.","zh":"presumably from 的意思是根據現有證據，大概由某事造成，但未完全肯定。"},{"en":"The noise was presumably from the roadworks outside.","zh":"那噪音推測是因為外面的道路工程。"},{"en":"Historians use presumably when the evidence points to a cause but does not prove it fully.","zh":"當證據指向某成因但未完全證明，歷史學家會使用 presumably。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a careful guess.","zh":"這個短語表示審慎推測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"respiratory illnesses","meaning":"呼吸系統疾病","examples":[{"en":"The rise in deaths was presumably caused by respiratory illnesses.","zh":"死亡人數上升推測是由呼吸系統疾病造成。"},{"en":"Respiratory illnesses are diseases that affect breathing, the lungs, or the airways.","zh":"respiratory illnesses 是影響呼吸、肺部或氣道的疾病。"},{"en":"Flu, pneumonia, and severe asthma problems can be respiratory illnesses.","zh":"流感、肺炎和嚴重哮喘問題都可以是呼吸系統疾病。"},{"en":"Air pollution can increase respiratory illnesses because harmful particles enter the lungs.","zh":"空氣污染可以增加呼吸系統疾病，因為有害微粒進入肺部。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in health and environmental discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於健康和環境討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"According to one report, the death toll was about double the usual number.","zh":"根據一份報告，死亡人數約為平常數目的兩倍。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a person, document, or source says.","zh":"according to 的意思是根據某人、文件或來源所說。"},{"en":"According to the timetable, the last train leaves at midnight.","zh":"根據時間表，最後一班火車午夜開出。"},{"en":"Writers use according to when they want to show where information comes from.","zh":"作者在想顯示資訊來源時會使用 according to。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a source of evidence.","zh":"這個短語引出證據來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"double the usual number","meaning":"平常數目的兩倍","examples":[{"en":"The number of deaths was about double the usual number.","zh":"死亡人數約為平常數目的兩倍。"},{"en":"Double the usual number means twice as many as normally expected.","zh":"double the usual number 的意思是正常預期數量的兩倍。"},{"en":"The clinic had double the usual number of patients during flu season.","zh":"流感季節期間，診所病人數量是平常數目的兩倍。"},{"en":"If absences are double the usual number, the school may investigate whether illness is spreading.","zh":"如果缺席人數是平常數目的兩倍，學校可能調查疾病是否正在傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a large increase compared with normal levels.","zh":"這個短語顯示與正常水平相比大幅增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"an unusually high percentage of","meaning":"異常高比例的……","examples":[{"en":"The deaths included an unusually high percentage of young people.","zh":"死亡者中包括異常高比例的年輕人。"},{"en":"An unusually high percentage of something means a share that is much higher than normal or expected.","zh":"an unusually high percentage of something 的意思是某比例遠高於正常或預期。"},{"en":"The class had an unusually high percentage of students who joined the debate team.","zh":"這班有異常高比例的學生加入辯論隊。"},{"en":"If an illness affects an unusually high percentage of children, doctors may look for a specific cause.","zh":"如果一種疾病影響異常高比例的兒童，醫生可能尋找特定原因。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a surprising proportion.","zh":"這個短語突出令人意外的比例。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"under the age of","meaning":"……歲以下","examples":[{"en":"Many of those who died were under the age of 25.","zh":"許多死者都在25歲以下。"},{"en":"Under the age of a number means younger than that age.","zh":"under the age of 某數字的意思是比該年齡年輕。"},{"en":"Children under the age of six may need an adult to enter the pool with them.","zh":"六歲以下兒童可能需要成人陪同進入泳池。"},{"en":"Rules often use “under the age of” to define who needs permission or protection.","zh":"規則常使用 under the age of 來界定誰需要許可或保護。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an age limit.","zh":"這個短語提供年齡限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be badly affected","meaning":"受到嚴重影響","examples":[{"en":"The weather in the USA was badly affected too.","zh":"美國的天氣也受到嚴重影響。"},{"en":"To be badly affected means to be seriously harmed or strongly influenced in a negative way.","zh":"be badly affected 的意思是受到嚴重損害或強烈負面影響。"},{"en":"Shops were badly affected when the road was closed for repairs.","zh":"道路關閉維修時，商店受到嚴重影響。"},{"en":"Students can be badly affected by poor sleep because concentration and mood suffer.","zh":"學生可能受到睡眠不足嚴重影響，因為專注力和心情會受損。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the effect is serious, not minor.","zh":"這個短語顯示影響嚴重，而不是輕微。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make a note in","meaning":"在……中記下","examples":[{"en":"George Washington made a note in his diary about the weather.","zh":"George Washington 在日記中記下關於天氣的事。"},{"en":"To make a note in something means to write down a short record in a notebook, diary, or document.","zh":"make a note in something 的意思是在筆記簿、日記或文件中簡短記錄。"},{"en":"A teacher may make a note in her planner about a student who needs extra help.","zh":"老師可能在計劃簿中記下一名需要額外幫助的學生。"},{"en":"Making notes helps people remember details that might later become important.","zh":"記筆記幫助人們記住之後可能變得重要的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on recording information briefly.","zh":"這個短語集中於簡短記錄資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be snowbound until","meaning":"被大雪困住直到……","examples":[{"en":"People in Virginia were snowbound until March.","zh":"維珍尼亞州的人被大雪困住直到三月。"},{"en":"To be snowbound until a time means to be trapped or unable to travel because of snow until that time.","zh":"be snowbound until 某時間的意思是因大雪被困或無法出行直到那時。"},{"en":"Villagers were snowbound until the road was cleared by rescue workers.","zh":"村民被大雪困住，直到救援人員清理道路。"},{"en":"Being snowbound can stop work, school, transport, and food deliveries.","zh":"被大雪困住可以令工作、學校、交通和食物運送停止。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how snow can isolate people for a period.","zh":"這個短語顯示大雪如何在一段時間內隔離人們。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"become president","meaning":"成為總統","examples":[{"en":"The diary entry was written before George Washington became president.","zh":"這篇日記是在 George Washington 成為總統之前寫的。"},{"en":"To become president means to take on the role of president of a country, organisation, or group.","zh":"become president 的意思是擔任一個國家、組織或團體的主席或總統角色。"},{"en":"A student may become president of the student council after winning an election.","zh":"學生可能在選舉勝出後成為學生會主席。"},{"en":"Becoming president usually brings greater responsibility and public attention.","zh":"成為總統或主席通常帶來更大責任和公眾關注。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a change in position or status.","zh":"這個短語標示職位或身份的改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ice floating down","meaning":"冰沿着……漂流","examples":[{"en":"There was ice floating down the Mississippi.","zh":"有冰沿着密西西比河漂流。"},{"en":"Ice floating down a river means pieces of ice are being carried along by the river’s current.","zh":"ice floating down a river 的意思是冰塊被河流水流帶着向下游移動。"},{"en":"After a very cold winter, people may see ice floating down a river toward the sea.","zh":"在非常寒冷的冬天後，人們可能看見冰沿着河流漂向大海。"},{"en":"Ice floating down a major river can show that the weather has been unusually cold.","zh":"冰沿着主要河流漂流，可以顯示天氣異常寒冷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible movement on water.","zh":"這個短語描述水面上可見的移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Mississippi River","meaning":"密西西比河","examples":[{"en":"Ice was seen floating down the Mississippi River.","zh":"有人看見冰沿着密西西比河漂流。"},{"en":"The Mississippi River is a major river in the United States.","zh":"Mississippi River 是美國一條主要河流。"},{"en":"Towns along the Mississippi River have historically depended on it for transport, trade, and water.","zh":"密西西比河沿岸城鎮歷史上依賴它進行運輸、貿易和用水。"},{"en":"Unusual ice on the Mississippi River can show how extreme winter weather has become.","zh":"密西西比河上出現異常冰塊，可以顯示冬季天氣有多極端。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific river, not rivers in general.","zh":"這個短語指特定河流，而不是一般河流。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"unprecedented","meaning":"前所未有的","examples":[{"en":"Ice floating down the Mississippi River was unprecedented.","zh":"冰沿着密西西比河漂流是前所未有的。"},{"en":"Unprecedented means never known, seen, or experienced before.","zh":"unprecedented 的意思是以前從未知道、看見或經歷過。"},{"en":"An unprecedented number of students joined the science club this year.","zh":"今年有前所未有數量的學生加入科學學會。"},{"en":"When something is unprecedented, people may not know how to respond because there is no earlier example.","zh":"當某事前所未有，人們可能不知道如何回應，因為沒有過往例子。"},{"en":"This word emphasises that the event is historically unusual.","zh":"這個詞強調事件在歷史上不尋常。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"astonishing","meaning":"令人驚訝的","examples":[{"en":"Michelle describes the weather effects as astonishing.","zh":"Michelle 形容這些天氣影響令人驚訝。"},{"en":"Astonishing means extremely surprising or difficult to believe.","zh":"astonishing 的意思是極其令人驚訝或難以相信。"},{"en":"The speed of the city’s recovery after the flood was astonishing.","zh":"這座城市在洪水後的恢復速度令人驚訝。"},{"en":"Astonishing facts catch people’s attention because they go beyond normal expectations.","zh":"令人驚訝的事實會吸引注意，因為它們超出正常預期。"},{"en":"This word expresses strong surprise.","zh":"這個詞表達強烈驚訝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"anyway","meaning":"不管怎樣；話說回來","examples":[{"en":"Michelle uses “Anyway” to move on to the next point.","zh":"Michelle 使用 “Anyway” 來轉到下一點。"},{"en":"Anyway is used to return to the main topic, change direction, or move on after a side comment.","zh":"anyway 用來回到主要話題、轉換方向，或在旁枝話題後繼續說下去。"},{"en":"Anyway, let’s finish the worksheet before the lesson ends.","zh":"話說回來，我們先在下課前完成工作紙吧。"},{"en":"Speakers use anyway when they want to stop discussing one detail and continue with the main point.","zh":"說話者想停止討論一個細節並繼續主要觀點時，會使用 anyway。"},{"en":"This word helps organise conversation naturally.","zh":"這個詞幫助自然地組織對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 10/task-4":[{"front":"be asked to","meaning":"被要求……","examples":[{"en":"The students have been asked to choose an aspect of European clothing.","zh":"學生被要求選擇歐洲服裝的一個方面。"},{"en":"To be asked to do something means someone has requested or instructed you to do it.","zh":"be asked to do something 是指有人要求或指示你做某事。"},{"en":"Students may be asked to hand in their homework before Friday.","zh":"學生可能被要求在星期五前交功課。"},{"en":"If workers are asked to stay late, they may need clear reasons and extra pay.","zh":"如果員工被要求加班，他們可能需要清楚原因和額外薪酬。"},{"en":"This phrase is passive, so it focuses on the request rather than the person making it.","zh":"這個短語是被動語態，所以焦點在要求本身，而不是提出要求的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"choose an aspect of","meaning":"選擇……的一個方面","examples":[{"en":"The students need to choose an aspect of European clothing or fashion.","zh":"學生需要選擇歐洲服裝或時裝的一個方面。"},{"en":"To choose an aspect of something means to select one part, feature, or angle of a larger topic.","zh":"choose an aspect of something 是指從較大的主題中選擇一個部分、特徵或角度。"},{"en":"A student may choose an aspect of school life, such as homework pressure or friendships.","zh":"學生可能選擇校園生活的一個方面，例如功課壓力或友誼。"},{"en":"Choosing one aspect makes a presentation clearer because the topic is not too broad.","zh":"選擇一個方面會令匯報更清晰，因為題目不會太廣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a large subject must be narrowed down.","zh":"當大題目需要收窄時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"European clothing","meaning":"歐洲服裝","examples":[{"en":"The presentation focuses on an aspect of European clothing.","zh":"這個匯報集中於歐洲服裝的一個方面。"},{"en":"European clothing means clothing styles, garments, and fashion traditions from Europe.","zh":"European clothing 是指來自歐洲的服裝款式、衣物和時裝傳統。"},{"en":"A museum display on European clothing may show dresses, suits, hats, and shoes from different centuries.","zh":"關於歐洲服裝的博物館展覽可能展示不同世紀的連身裙、西裝、帽和鞋。"},{"en":"Studying European clothing can reveal changes in class, work, gender, and daily life.","zh":"研究歐洲服裝可以揭示階級、工作、性別和日常生活的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to clothes from Europe, not simply clothes worn in modern shops.","zh":"這個短語指歐洲的服裝，而不只是現代商店裏售賣的衣服。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fashion","meaning":"時裝；時尚","examples":[{"en":"The speaker talks about the development of pockets in fashion.","zh":"講者談論衣袋在時裝中的發展。"},{"en":"Fashion means popular styles of clothing, appearance, or design at a particular time.","zh":"fashion 是指某個時期流行的服裝、外觀或設計風格。"},{"en":"Teenagers may follow fashion by wearing colours or shoes that are currently popular.","zh":"青少年可能透過穿着當下流行的顏色或鞋款來跟隨時尚。"},{"en":"Fashion changes when people’s tastes, technology, work, or social ideas change.","zh":"當人們的品味、科技、工作或社會觀念改變，時裝也會改變。"},{"en":"This word can refer to clothing trends, not just expensive designer clothes.","zh":"這個詞可以指服裝潮流，不只是昂貴設計師品牌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"talk about","meaning":"談論……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker is going to talk about the development of pockets.","zh":"講者將會談論衣袋的發展。"},{"en":"To talk about something means to discuss or explain that topic.","zh":"talk about something 是指討論或解釋該主題。"},{"en":"In class, students may talk about how transport affects city life.","zh":"課堂上，學生可能談論交通如何影響城市生活。"},{"en":"Talking about a topic helps listeners understand what happened and why it matters.","zh":"談論一個主題有助聽者理解發生了甚麼，以及為何重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple and common when introducing the subject of a speech or conversation.","zh":"這個短語簡單常見，常用來引入演講或對話的主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"development over time","meaning":"隨時間的發展","examples":[{"en":"The task is to talk about the development of an aspect of fashion over time.","zh":"這項任務是談論時裝某一方面隨時間的發展。"},{"en":"Development over time means the way something changes gradually across different periods.","zh":"development over time 是指某事在不同時期中逐漸改變的方式。"},{"en":"A history project may examine the development of public transport over time.","zh":"歷史專題可能研究公共交通隨時間的發展。"},{"en":"Looking at development over time helps people see causes, patterns, and turning points.","zh":"觀察隨時間的發展，有助人們看見原因、模式和轉折點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing the past with the present.","zh":"這個短語適合用於比較過去與現在。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"decide to focus on","meaning":"決定集中講……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker decided to focus on pockets.","zh":"講者決定集中講衣袋。"},{"en":"To decide to focus on something means to choose it as the main topic or centre of attention.","zh":"decide to focus on something 是指選擇某事作為主要主題或注意中心。"},{"en":"A student may decide to focus on pollution rather than all environmental problems.","zh":"學生可能決定集中講污染，而不是所有環境問題。"},{"en":"Focusing on one topic makes research easier because the material becomes more manageable.","zh":"集中於一個主題會令研究較容易，因為資料變得更易處理。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears when someone narrows a broad subject.","zh":"當某人把廣泛題目收窄時，常會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a rather small area of","meaning":"……中一個相當細小的範疇","examples":[{"en":"The speaker focuses on a rather small area of clothing.","zh":"講者集中於服裝中一個相當細小的範疇。"},{"en":"A rather small area of something means a fairly narrow part of a larger subject.","zh":"a rather small area of something 是指一個較大主題中的相當狹窄部分。"},{"en":"A presentation on school uniforms is a rather small area of education policy.","zh":"關於校服的匯報，是教育政策中一個相當細小的範疇。"},{"en":"Studying a small area can still be useful if it reveals larger social changes.","zh":"研究細小範疇仍然有用，因為它可以揭示較大的社會變化。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the topic is limited, but not unimportant.","zh":"這個短語表示題目範圍有限，但並非不重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pockets","meaning":"衣袋；口袋","examples":[{"en":"The speaker chose pockets as the topic of the presentation.","zh":"講者選擇衣袋作為匯報題目。"},{"en":"Pockets are small spaces sewn into clothing or attached to clothing for carrying things.","zh":"pockets 是縫在衣服裏或附在衣服上、用來攜帶物品的小空間。"},{"en":"People use pockets to carry keys, coins, phones, tissues, or travel cards.","zh":"人們用衣袋攜帶鑰匙、硬幣、電話、紙巾或交通卡。"},{"en":"Pockets are useful because they let people keep small objects close without holding a bag.","zh":"衣袋很有用，因為它讓人不用拿袋也能把小物件放在身邊。"},{"en":"In fashion history, pockets can show how clothing was designed for different needs.","zh":"在時裝史中，衣袋可以顯示服裝如何為不同需要而設計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for two reasons","meaning":"基於兩個原因","examples":[{"en":"The speaker chose pockets for two reasons.","zh":"講者基於兩個原因選擇衣袋。"},{"en":"For two reasons means there are exactly two main explanations for a choice or opinion.","zh":"for two reasons 是指某個選擇或意見正好有兩個主要解釋。"},{"en":"I chose this school for two reasons: the teachers are supportive and the location is convenient.","zh":"我選擇這間學校基於兩個原因：老師支持學生，而且地點方便。"},{"en":"Giving two reasons helps listeners follow the argument clearly.","zh":"提供兩個原因有助聽者清楚跟上論點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when organising a short explanation or presentation.","zh":"這個短語適合用來組織簡短解釋或匯報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"even though","meaning":"即使","examples":[{"en":"Even though people often carry bags, pockets are still convenient.","zh":"即使人們常攜帶袋子，衣袋仍然方便。"},{"en":"Even though introduces a contrast between an expected situation and the actual result.","zh":"even though 用來引入預期情況與實際結果之間的對比。"},{"en":"Even though it was raining, many students still came to the school fair.","zh":"即使下雨，許多學生仍然來到學校市集。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that one fact does not stop another fact from being true.","zh":"這個短語有助顯示一個事實不會阻止另一個事實成立。"},{"en":"It is stronger and clearer than simply saying “but”.","zh":"它比單純說 but 更強、更清楚。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"carry bags or briefcases","meaning":"攜帶袋或公事包","examples":[{"en":"People often carry bags or briefcases as well.","zh":"人們也常攜帶袋或公事包。"},{"en":"To carry bags or briefcases means to bring personal or work items in handheld containers.","zh":"carry bags or briefcases 是指用手提容器攜帶個人或工作物品。"},{"en":"Office workers may carry bags or briefcases to hold laptops, documents, and lunch boxes.","zh":"辦公室員工可能攜帶袋或公事包來放手提電腦、文件和飯盒。"},{"en":"Carrying bags can be useful, but it may become inconvenient on crowded trains.","zh":"攜帶袋子可以有用，但在擁擠火車上可能變得不方便。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common way of transporting belongings outside pockets.","zh":"這個短語描述在衣袋以外攜帶物品的常見方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"nothing is quite as convenient as","meaning":"沒有甚麼比……更方便","examples":[{"en":"Nothing is quite as convenient as putting a phone into a pocket.","zh":"沒有甚麼比把電話放進衣袋更方便。"},{"en":"Nothing is quite as convenient as means no other option is as easy or useful.","zh":"nothing is quite as convenient as 是指沒有其他選項同樣容易或實用。"},{"en":"Nothing is quite as convenient as paying by contactless card when the queue is long.","zh":"排長隊時，沒有甚麼比用感應卡付款更方便。"},{"en":"People choose convenient options because they save time and effort.","zh":"人們選擇方便的選項，因為它們節省時間和力氣。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly praises one option by comparing it with all others.","zh":"這個短語透過與所有其他選項比較，強烈稱讚其中一個選項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be able to","meaning":"能夠……","examples":[{"en":"It is convenient to be able to put your phone into your pocket.","zh":"能夠把電話放進衣袋是很方便的。"},{"en":"To be able to do something means to have the ability, chance, or permission to do it.","zh":"be able to do something 是指有能力、機會或許可去做某事。"},{"en":"Students need to be able to explain their answers, not just choose the right option.","zh":"學生需要能夠解釋自己的答案，而不只是選對選項。"},{"en":"If people are able to pay online, they may not need to visit the office in person.","zh":"如果人們能夠網上付款，就可能不需要親身到辦公室。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on possibility or ability.","zh":"這個短語著重可能性或能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pop something into","meaning":"把某物隨手放入……","examples":[{"en":"You can pop your phone or credit card into your pocket.","zh":"你可以把電話或信用卡隨手放進衣袋。"},{"en":"To pop something into a place means to put it there quickly and casually.","zh":"pop something into a place 是指快速而隨意地把某物放進某處。"},{"en":"A student may pop a pen into her bag before leaving the classroom.","zh":"學生離開課室前，可能把筆隨手放進書包。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the action is easy, quick, and not very formal.","zh":"這個短語表示動作容易、快速，而且不太正式。"},{"en":"People use it when putting a small item somewhere for convenience.","zh":"當人們為方便而把小物件放到某處時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"credit card","meaning":"信用卡","examples":[{"en":"You can pop your phone or credit card into your pocket.","zh":"你可以把電話或信用卡隨手放進衣袋。"},{"en":"A credit card is a plastic or digital payment card that lets you buy things and pay later.","zh":"credit card 是一種塑膠或數碼付款卡，讓你先購物後付款。"},{"en":"Many people use a credit card to pay for hotel bookings or online shopping.","zh":"許多人用信用卡支付酒店預訂或網上購物。"},{"en":"Credit cards are convenient, but careless use can lead to debt.","zh":"信用卡很方便，但若不小心使用，可能導致債務。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a payment method, not ordinary cash.","zh":"這個短語指一種付款方式，而不是普通現金。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I suspect that","meaning":"我猜想……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker suspects that people do not think about pockets very much.","zh":"講者猜想人們不太會思考衣袋。"},{"en":"I suspect that means I think something is probably true, although I am not completely certain.","zh":"I suspect that 是指我認為某事很可能是真的，但並非完全肯定。"},{"en":"I suspect that many students are tired because the test is near.","zh":"我猜想很多學生很疲累，因為測驗快到了。"},{"en":"This phrase lets a speaker give an opinion carefully rather than as a proven fact.","zh":"這個短語讓說話者謹慎地表達意見，而不是當作已證實事實。"},{"en":"It is useful when making a reasonable guess based on experience.","zh":"當根據經驗作出合理推測時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"other than that","meaning":"除此之外","examples":[{"en":"Other than that, people do not think about pockets too much.","zh":"除此之外，人們不會太多思考衣袋。"},{"en":"Other than that means apart from the thing just mentioned.","zh":"other than that 是指除了剛才提到的事情以外。"},{"en":"I was late once last week, but other than that, my attendance has been good.","zh":"我上星期遲到過一次，但除此之外，我的出席情況很好。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate one exception from the general situation.","zh":"這個短語有助把一個例外與整體情況分開。"},{"en":"It is often used to continue after mentioning a small point or exception.","zh":"它常用於提到小點或例外後繼續說明。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"think about something too much","meaning":"太多思考某事","examples":[{"en":"People do not really think about pockets too much.","zh":"人們其實不會太多思考衣袋。"},{"en":"To think about something too much means to give it more attention than usual or necessary.","zh":"think about something too much 是指給某事比平常或必要更多的注意。"},{"en":"A student may think about one mistake too much and forget the rest of the exam went well.","zh":"學生可能太多思考一個錯誤，而忘記整場考試其他部分其實不錯。"},{"en":"People often do not think about everyday objects until those objects stop working.","zh":"人們通常到日常物件不能使用時，才會開始留意它們。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest either overthinking or simply paying little attention, depending on the sentence.","zh":"這個短語可表示想太多，也可表示平時少想，視乎句子而定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be overlooked as","meaning":"作為……被忽略","examples":[{"en":"Pockets are rather overlooked as a fashion item.","zh":"衣袋作為時裝元素相當被忽略。"},{"en":"To be overlooked as something means to be ignored or not properly recognised in that role.","zh":"be overlooked as something 是指在某個角色上被忽視或未被充分重視。"},{"en":"School cleaners are often overlooked as important members of the school community.","zh":"學校清潔工常作為校園社群的重要成員而被忽略。"},{"en":"When something is overlooked, people may fail to see its value or influence.","zh":"當某物被忽略，人們可能看不到它的價值或影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something ordinary deserves more attention.","zh":"當普通事物其實值得更多注意時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fashion item","meaning":"時裝元素","examples":[{"en":"Pockets are often overlooked as a fashion item.","zh":"衣袋作為時裝元素常被忽略。"},{"en":"A fashion item is a piece of clothing or accessory considered part of style or appearance.","zh":"fashion item 是被視為風格或外觀一部分的衣物或配飾。"},{"en":"A scarf can be both warm clothing and a fashion item.","zh":"圍巾既可以是保暖衣物，也可以是時裝元素。"},{"en":"Fashion items may show taste, status, culture, or practical needs.","zh":"時裝元素可能顯示品味、地位、文化或實際需要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an object’s role in style, not just its basic function.","zh":"這個短語指物件在風格上的角色，而不只是基本功能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go back in time","meaning":"回到過去","examples":[{"en":"It is interesting to go back in time and see how pockets developed.","zh":"回到過去看看衣袋如何發展，是很有趣的。"},{"en":"To go back in time means to look at or imagine an earlier period in history.","zh":"go back in time 是指回顧或想像歷史上的較早時期。"},{"en":"A museum allows visitors to go back in time by showing old homes, tools, and clothes.","zh":"博物館透過展示舊家居、工具和衣服，讓訪客回到過去。"},{"en":"Going back in time helps people understand why modern objects look the way they do.","zh":"回到過去有助人們理解現代物件為何是現在的樣子。"},{"en":"This phrase does not usually mean real time travel; it means studying the past.","zh":"這個短語通常不指真正時光旅行，而是指研究過去。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"develop for men and women","meaning":"為男女而發展","examples":[{"en":"Pockets developed differently for men and women.","zh":"衣袋為男女而有不同發展。"},{"en":"To develop for men and women means to change in different ways according to gendered clothing needs or social rules.","zh":"develop for men and women 是指因男女服裝需要或社會規範不同而以不同方式改變。"},{"en":"Shoes developed differently for men and women because work, fashion, and movement were viewed differently.","zh":"鞋履為男女而有不同發展，因為工作、時裝和活動方式被不同看待。"},{"en":"When an item develops differently for different groups, it can reveal social expectations.","zh":"當一件物品為不同群體而有不同發展，它可以揭示社會期望。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing how design changes for separate groups.","zh":"這個短語適合用於比較設計如何為不同群體而改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"quite different from","meaning":"與……相當不同","examples":[{"en":"Fashions in the 18th century were quite different from today’s fashions.","zh":"18世紀的時裝與今天的時裝相當不同。"},{"en":"Quite different from means noticeably unlike something else.","zh":"quite different from 是指與某物有明顯不同。"},{"en":"Online learning is quite different from sitting in a traditional classroom.","zh":"網上學習與坐在傳統課室中相當不同。"},{"en":"When two things are quite different, examples are often needed to show the contrast clearly.","zh":"當兩件事相當不同時，通常需要例子清楚展示對比。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for comparing periods, places, styles, or habits.","zh":"這個短語適合比較時期、地方、風格或習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the way they are now","meaning":"現在的樣子","examples":[{"en":"Fashions were quite different from the way they are now.","zh":"時裝與它們現在的樣子相當不同。"},{"en":"The way they are now means their present form, style, or condition.","zh":"the way they are now 是指它們現在的形式、風格或狀態。"},{"en":"Schools today are different from the way they were before online learning became common.","zh":"今天的學校與網上學習普及前的樣子不同。"},{"en":"Comparing the past with the way things are now helps people notice change.","zh":"把過去與現在的樣子比較，有助人們注意到變化。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the current state of something.","zh":"這個短語指某事目前的狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"think about male fashion first","meaning":"先談男性時裝","examples":[{"en":"The speaker thinks about male fashion first.","zh":"講者先談男性時裝。"},{"en":"To think about male fashion first means to begin the discussion with men’s clothing styles.","zh":"think about male fashion first 是指先從男性服裝風格開始討論。"},{"en":"A historian may think about children’s clothing first before discussing adult fashion.","zh":"歷史學者可能先談兒童服裝，然後才討論成人時裝。"},{"en":"Starting with one group helps organise a comparison more clearly.","zh":"從一個群體開始，有助更清楚組織比較。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the order in which topics are discussed.","zh":"這個短語顯示討論主題的次序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"male fashion","meaning":"男性時裝","examples":[{"en":"Male fashion changed significantly in the 18th century.","zh":"男性時裝在18世紀有重大改變。"},{"en":"Male fashion means clothing styles and appearance associated with men.","zh":"male fashion 是指與男性相關的服裝風格和外觀。"},{"en":"Male fashion in an office may include suits, shirts, ties, or smart shoes.","zh":"辦公室中的男性時裝可能包括西裝、恤衫、領帶或端莊皮鞋。"},{"en":"Male fashion changes when work, class, comfort, and public image change.","zh":"當工作、階級、舒適度和公眾形象改變，男性時裝也會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to men’s style, not simply clothes worn by any person.","zh":"這個短語指男性風格，而不只是任何人穿的衣服。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"that was the time when","meaning":"那正是……的時候","examples":[{"en":"That was the time when suits became popular.","zh":"那正是西裝變得流行的時候。"},{"en":"That was the time when means that period was when a particular change or event happened.","zh":"that was the time when 是指某個時期正是某種變化或事件發生的時候。"},{"en":"The 1990s was the time when many families first started using home computers.","zh":"1990年代正是許多家庭開始使用家用電腦的時候。"},{"en":"This phrase links a historical period with an important development.","zh":"這個短語把歷史時期與重要發展連繫起來。"},{"en":"It helps listeners understand when something began or became important.","zh":"它幫助聽者理解某事何時開始或變得重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"become popular","meaning":"變得流行","examples":[{"en":"Suits became popular in the 18th century.","zh":"西裝在18世紀變得流行。"},{"en":"To become popular means to start being liked, used, or accepted by many people.","zh":"become popular 是指開始被很多人喜歡、使用或接受。"},{"en":"Online shopping became popular because it is convenient and often cheaper.","zh":"網上購物因方便且通常較便宜而變得流行。"},{"en":"A style becomes popular when people see others using it and want to copy it.","zh":"當人們看見其他人使用某種風格並想模仿，它便會變得流行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change from less common to widely accepted.","zh":"這個短語描述從較少見變成廣泛接受的轉變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"knee-length","meaning":"及膝長度的","examples":[{"en":"Trousers were knee-length only.","zh":"褲子只有及膝長度。"},{"en":"Knee-length means reaching down to around the knees.","zh":"knee-length 是指長度到膝蓋附近。"},{"en":"A knee-length skirt is longer than a mini skirt but shorter than an ankle-length skirt.","zh":"及膝裙比迷你裙長，但比及踝裙短。"},{"en":"Clothing length affects movement, warmth, and how formal an outfit looks.","zh":"衣物長度會影響活動、保暖和造型的正式程度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical length of a garment.","zh":"這個短語描述衣物的實際長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be referred to as","meaning":"被稱為……","examples":[{"en":"Knee-length trousers were referred to as breeches.","zh":"及膝長褲被稱為 breeches。"},{"en":"To be referred to as something means to be called or described by that name.","zh":"be referred to as something 是指被叫作或被描述為某個名稱。"},{"en":"A school principal may be referred to as the head teacher in British English.","zh":"在英式英語中，校長可能被稱為 head teacher。"},{"en":"When an object is referred to by a special term, readers may need an explanation.","zh":"當物件被用專門術語稱呼，讀者可能需要解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing formal, historical, or technical names.","zh":"這個短語適合用於引入正式、歷史或技術名稱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"breeches","meaning":"馬褲；及膝短褲","examples":[{"en":"Knee-length trousers were referred to as breeches.","zh":"及膝長褲被稱為馬褲。"},{"en":"Breeches were short trousers that usually reached the knee and were worn by men in the past.","zh":"breeches 是過去男性常穿、通常長至膝蓋的短褲。"},{"en":"Historical costumes may include breeches, stockings, waistcoats, and jackets.","zh":"歷史服裝可能包括馬褲、長襪、馬甲和外套。"},{"en":"Breeches show that men’s trousers in the past were not always full-length.","zh":"馬褲顯示過去男性長褲不一定是全長的。"},{"en":"This word is mainly used when discussing older clothing styles.","zh":"這個詞主要用於討論較舊的服裝款式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"waistcoats","meaning":"背心；馬甲","examples":[{"en":"The waistcoats were short in 18th-century male fashion.","zh":"在18世紀男性時裝中，馬甲較短。"},{"en":"Waistcoats are sleeveless garments worn over shirts and under jackets.","zh":"waistcoats 是穿在恤衫外、外套內的無袖衣物。"},{"en":"A man may wear a waistcoat with a suit at a formal wedding.","zh":"男士可能在正式婚禮中穿西裝配馬甲。"},{"en":"Waistcoats can add warmth, style, or a more formal appearance.","zh":"馬甲可以增加保暖、風格或更正式的外觀。"},{"en":"This word is common in British English; American English often uses “vest”.","zh":"這個詞常見於英式英語；美式英語常用 vest。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"garments","meaning":"衣物","examples":[{"en":"The trousers, waistcoats and jackets were all lined with material.","zh":"褲子、馬甲和外套全都內裏襯有布料。"},{"en":"Garments are pieces of clothing, especially when discussed formally or technically.","zh":"garments 是指一件件衣物，尤其用於較正式或技術性的討論。"},{"en":"A clothing factory may check each garment before it is packed and sold.","zh":"製衣廠可能在包裝出售前檢查每件衣物。"},{"en":"Garments can be designed for warmth, movement, protection, or fashion.","zh":"衣物可以為保暖、活動、防護或時裝而設計。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than simply saying “clothes”.","zh":"這個詞比單純說 clothes 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be lined with","meaning":"內裏襯有……","examples":[{"en":"The garments were lined with material.","zh":"這些衣物內裏襯有布料。"},{"en":"To be lined with something means to have an inner layer of that material.","zh":"be lined with something 是指內部有一層該材料作襯裏。"},{"en":"A winter coat may be lined with soft wool to keep the wearer warm.","zh":"冬天外套可能內裏襯有柔軟羊毛，以保持穿着者溫暖。"},{"en":"Lining can make clothing more comfortable, stronger, or neater inside.","zh":"襯裏可以令衣物更舒適、更耐用或內部更整齊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what is attached to the inside surface.","zh":"這個短語描述附在內側表面的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"material","meaning":"布料","examples":[{"en":"The garments were lined with material.","zh":"這些衣物內裏襯有布料。"},{"en":"Material means cloth or fabric used to make or line clothing.","zh":"material 是指用來製作或作衣物襯裏的布料。"},{"en":"A tailor may choose thicker material for a winter jacket.","zh":"裁縫可能為冬季外套選擇較厚布料。"},{"en":"The material affects how clothing feels, moves, and lasts.","zh":"布料會影響衣物的觸感、活動性和耐用程度。"},{"en":"In this context, material means fabric, not information or study content.","zh":"在這個語境中，material 指布料，而不是資料或學習內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be sewn into","meaning":"被縫進……","examples":[{"en":"Pockets were sewn into the lining by the tailor.","zh":"衣袋由裁縫縫進襯裏。"},{"en":"To be sewn into something means to be attached inside it using stitches.","zh":"be sewn into something 是指用針線把某物縫入其中。"},{"en":"A name label may be sewn into a child’s school jacket.","zh":"姓名標籤可能被縫進孩子的校褸。"},{"en":"When something is sewn into clothing, it becomes part of the garment rather than a separate item.","zh":"當某物被縫進衣物，它便成為衣物的一部分，而不是分開的物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how fabric pieces are fixed together.","zh":"這個短語描述布料部件如何被固定在一起。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"whichever tailor","meaning":"顧客所選的任何裁縫","examples":[{"en":"Pockets were sewn in by whichever tailor the customer used.","zh":"衣袋由顧客所選的任何裁縫縫進去。"},{"en":"Whichever tailor means any tailor chosen by the customer, without naming one specific person.","zh":"whichever tailor 是指顧客選擇的任何裁縫，而不是指定某一人。"},{"en":"Whichever teacher checks the homework should use the same marking rules.","zh":"無論哪位老師批改功課，都應使用相同評分規則。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the result does not depend on which person is chosen.","zh":"這個短語顯示結果不取決於選擇了哪個人。"},{"en":"It is useful when the exact person may vary.","zh":"當確切人物可能不同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the customer used","meaning":"顧客所用的","examples":[{"en":"The tailor the customer used would sew pockets into the clothing.","zh":"顧客所用的裁縫會把衣袋縫進衣服。"},{"en":"The customer used means the customer chose or hired that service or person.","zh":"the customer used 是指顧客選擇或聘用了某項服務或某個人。"},{"en":"The moving company the family used arrived early and packed everything carefully.","zh":"那個家庭所用的搬屋公司很早到達，並小心包裝所有東西。"},{"en":"This phrase often identifies which provider someone selected for a job.","zh":"這個短語常用來指出某人選用了哪個服務提供者。"},{"en":"It is common when comparing services, workers, shops, or professionals.","zh":"它常見於比較服務、工人、商店或專業人士時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the wearer","meaning":"穿着者","examples":[{"en":"The wearer could carry small objects on their person.","zh":"穿着者可以把小物件隨身攜帶。"},{"en":"The wearer is the person who is wearing a piece of clothing or accessory.","zh":"the wearer 是指穿着某件衣物或配飾的人。"},{"en":"A raincoat keeps the wearer dry during heavy rain.","zh":"雨衣在大雨中讓穿着者保持乾爽。"},{"en":"Clothing design matters because it affects the wearer’s comfort and movement.","zh":"服裝設計很重要，因為它影響穿着者的舒適度和活動。"},{"en":"This word is useful when focusing on the person using the garment.","zh":"當焦點在使用衣物的人身上時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"small objects","meaning":"小物件","examples":[{"en":"The wearer could carry small objects such as pencils or coins.","zh":"穿着者可以攜帶鉛筆或硬幣等小物件。"},{"en":"Small objects are little items that can be held, carried, or stored easily.","zh":"small objects 是指容易拿着、攜帶或存放的小件物品。"},{"en":"Keys, coins, buttons, and paper clips are small objects people often lose.","zh":"鑰匙、硬幣、鈕扣和萬字夾是人們常遺失的小物件。"},{"en":"Pockets are useful because they keep small objects close and easy to find.","zh":"衣袋很有用，因為它能把小物件放在身邊並容易找到。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to physical things, not ideas or large belongings.","zh":"這個短語指實體物品，而不是想法或大型物件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"such as","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"The wearer could carry small objects such as pencils or coins.","zh":"穿着者可以攜帶小物件，例如鉛筆或硬幣。"},{"en":"Such as introduces examples of the thing just mentioned.","zh":"such as 用來引入剛提及事物的例子。"},{"en":"Students need stationery such as pens, rulers, and notebooks.","zh":"學生需要文具，例如筆、尺和筆記簿。"},{"en":"Examples after “such as” help readers understand a general category more clearly.","zh":"such as 後面的例子有助讀者更清楚理解一般類別。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving specific items within a larger group.","zh":"當在較大群組中列出具體項目時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on their person","meaning":"隨身","examples":[{"en":"The wearer could carry small objects on their person.","zh":"穿着者可以隨身攜帶小物件。"},{"en":"On their person means carried on the body or in the clothing someone is wearing.","zh":"on their person 是指放在身上或穿着中的衣物裏。"},{"en":"A traveller should keep important documents on their person rather than in checked luggage.","zh":"旅客應把重要文件隨身攜帶，而不是放在寄艙行李中。"},{"en":"Carrying money on your person can be useful, but it may also attract pickpockets.","zh":"隨身帶錢可能有用，但也可能吸引扒手。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often refers to things kept close to the body.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常指貼身保管的物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reach them through","meaning":"透過……拿到它們","examples":[{"en":"The wearer could reach the objects through a gap in the lining.","zh":"穿着者可以透過內襯中的開口拿到那些物件。"},{"en":"To reach them through something means to get to those things by putting your hand through an opening or space.","zh":"reach them through something 是指把手伸過某個開口或空間來拿到那些東西。"},{"en":"A child may reach toys through a gap under the bed.","zh":"孩子可能透過床底空隙拿到玩具。"},{"en":"If objects are hidden under clothing, an opening is needed to reach them easily.","zh":"如果物件藏在衣服下面，就需要開口才能容易拿到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the route or opening used to get something.","zh":"這個短語描述拿取某物所經過的路徑或開口。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a gap in the lining","meaning":"內襯中的開口","examples":[{"en":"The wearer could reach objects through a gap in the lining.","zh":"穿着者可以透過內襯中的開口拿到物件。"},{"en":"A gap in the lining is an opening or space in the inner layer of a garment.","zh":"a gap in the lining 是衣物內層中的開口或空隙。"},{"en":"A small gap in the lining of a coat may allow someone to repair the inside pocket.","zh":"外套內襯中的小開口可能讓人修補內袋。"},{"en":"Without a gap, the wearer might not be able to reach the hidden pocket.","zh":"如果沒有開口，穿着者可能無法拿到隱藏衣袋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical opening inside clothing.","zh":"這個短語描述衣物內部的實體開口。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"coat pockets","meaning":"外套衣袋","examples":[{"en":"Coat pockets became increasingly decorative for stylish men.","zh":"對時髦男性來說，外套衣袋變得越來越具裝飾性。"},{"en":"Coat pockets are pockets found on or inside coats.","zh":"coat pockets 是外套上或外套裏面的衣袋。"},{"en":"A winter coat pocket can hold gloves, keys, or a travel card.","zh":"冬季外套衣袋可以放手套、鑰匙或交通卡。"},{"en":"Coat pockets may be designed for function, decoration, or both.","zh":"外套衣袋可以為功能、裝飾或兩者而設計。"},{"en":"This phrase refers specifically to pockets connected with coats, not trousers or bags.","zh":"這個短語專指與外套相關的衣袋，而不是褲袋或手袋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"increasingly decorative","meaning":"越來越具裝飾性","examples":[{"en":"Coat pockets became increasingly decorative on the outside.","zh":"外套衣袋在外面變得越來越具裝飾性。"},{"en":"Increasingly decorative means becoming more and more designed for beauty or style.","zh":"increasingly decorative 是指越來越為美觀或風格而設計。"},{"en":"Shop windows become increasingly decorative before major festivals.","zh":"大型節日前，商店櫥窗會變得越來越具裝飾性。"},{"en":"When something becomes decorative, appearance may become as important as function.","zh":"當某物變得具裝飾性，外觀可能變得與功能同樣重要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a gradual move towards ornament and visual style.","zh":"這個短語顯示逐漸走向裝飾和視覺風格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on the outside","meaning":"在外面","examples":[{"en":"Men’s coat pockets became decorative on the outside.","zh":"男性外套衣袋在外面變得具裝飾性。"},{"en":"On the outside means on the outer surface or visible part of something.","zh":"on the outside 是指在某物的外層表面或可見部分。"},{"en":"A schoolbag may look plain on the outside but have many compartments inside.","zh":"書包外面可能看起來樸素，但裏面有很多間隔。"},{"en":"Details on the outside of clothing are visible and can affect style.","zh":"衣物外面的細節可被看見，並會影響風格。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with what is hidden inside.","zh":"這個短語與隱藏在裏面的東西相對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"look stylish","meaning":"看起來時髦","examples":[{"en":"Some men wanted to look stylish.","zh":"有些男性想看起來時髦。"},{"en":"To look stylish means to appear fashionable, attractive, and well dressed.","zh":"look stylish 是指看起來時尚、吸引和穿着得體。"},{"en":"A person may wear a simple black jacket to look stylish at a dinner.","zh":"一個人可能穿簡單黑色外套，讓自己在晚餐中看起來時髦。"},{"en":"People may choose decorative details because they want to look stylish.","zh":"人們可能選擇裝飾細節，因為他們想看起來時髦。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on appearance and fashion impression.","zh":"這個短語著重外觀和時尚印象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"larger but plainer","meaning":"較大但較樸素","examples":[{"en":"Professional men’s pockets were often larger but plainer.","zh":"專業男性的衣袋通常較大但較樸素。"},{"en":"Larger but plainer means bigger in size but simpler in decoration.","zh":"larger but plainer 是指尺寸較大，但裝飾較簡單。"},{"en":"A school bag for exams may be larger but plainer than a fashionable weekend bag.","zh":"考試用書包可能比時尚週末袋較大但較樸素。"},{"en":"Practical needs often make items larger but plainer because function becomes more important than style.","zh":"實際需要常令物件較大但較樸素，因為功能比風格更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a contrast between usefulness and decoration.","zh":"這個短語顯示實用性與裝飾之間的對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"with a profession","meaning":"有專業職業的","examples":[{"en":"The pockets were larger if the wearer was someone with a profession.","zh":"如果穿着者是有專業職業的人，衣袋會較大。"},{"en":"Someone with a profession is a person who has a skilled or formal job.","zh":"someone with a profession 是指擁有技能或正式職業的人。"},{"en":"A person with a profession, such as a lawyer or doctor, may need tools or documents for work.","zh":"有專業職業的人，例如律師或醫生，可能需要工作用工具或文件。"},{"en":"Clothing for people with professions may change because their work requires practical features.","zh":"有專業職業人士的服裝可能會改變，因為工作需要實用特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase often refers to trained, respected, or specialised work.","zh":"這個短語常指受過訓練、受尊重或專門的工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"carry medical instruments","meaning":"攜帶醫療器具","examples":[{"en":"Doctors needed pockets to carry medical instruments.","zh":"醫生需要衣袋來攜帶醫療器具。"},{"en":"To carry medical instruments means to bring tools used for medical examination or treatment.","zh":"carry medical instruments 是指攜帶用於醫療檢查或治療的工具。"},{"en":"A nurse may carry medical instruments such as a thermometer or small scissors.","zh":"護士可能攜帶體溫計或小剪刀等醫療器具。"},{"en":"Large pockets helped doctors work because they could keep tools close at hand.","zh":"大衣袋幫助醫生工作，因為他們可以把工具放在身邊。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a practical reason for clothing design.","zh":"這個短語顯示服裝設計的實際原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"medical instruments","meaning":"醫療器具","examples":[{"en":"A physician might need to carry medical instruments.","zh":"內科醫生可能需要攜帶醫療器具。"},{"en":"Medical instruments are tools used by doctors or nurses to examine, treat, or care for patients.","zh":"medical instruments 是醫生或護士用來檢查、治療或照顧病人的工具。"},{"en":"A stethoscope, thermometer, and forceps are examples of medical instruments.","zh":"聽診器、體溫計和鉗子都是醫療器具的例子。"},{"en":"Medical instruments must be clean because they may touch patients directly.","zh":"醫療器具必須清潔，因為它們可能直接接觸病人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to professional medical tools, not ordinary household items.","zh":"這個短語指專業醫療工具，而不是普通家居物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"physician","meaning":"內科醫生","examples":[{"en":"A doctor or physician might need larger pockets.","zh":"醫生或內科醫生可能需要較大的衣袋。"},{"en":"A physician is a medical doctor, especially one who diagnoses and treats illness.","zh":"physician 是醫生，尤其指診斷和治療疾病的內科醫生。"},{"en":"A patient may see a physician if they have chest pain or a long fever.","zh":"如果病人胸口痛或長時間發燒，可能會見內科醫生。"},{"en":"Physicians may need tools, notes, or small instruments while seeing patients.","zh":"內科醫生看病人時可能需要工具、筆記或小型器具。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “doctor” in everyday conversation.","zh":"這個詞比日常對話中的 doctor 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a little different","meaning":"有點不同","examples":[{"en":"The development of women’s pockets was a little different.","zh":"女性衣袋的發展有點不同。"},{"en":"A little different means slightly different, not completely unlike something else.","zh":"a little different 是指稍有不同，而不是完全不一樣。"},{"en":"The new timetable is a little different from last year’s, but most lessons stay the same.","zh":"新時間表與去年的有點不同，但大部分課堂保持不變。"},{"en":"Small differences can still matter if they affect how people use an object.","zh":"如果小差異影響人們如何使用物件，它們仍然重要。"},{"en":"This phrase gently introduces contrast without making it sound extreme.","zh":"這個短語溫和地引入對比，而不令差異聽起來很極端。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"for one thing","meaning":"首先；其中一點是","examples":[{"en":"For one thing, women’s pockets were not as visible as men’s.","zh":"首先，女性衣袋不如男性衣袋明顯。"},{"en":"For one thing is used to introduce one reason or point among others.","zh":"for one thing 用來引入眾多理由或觀點中的其中一點。"},{"en":"I prefer the bus; for one thing, it is cheaper than driving.","zh":"我較喜歡巴士；其中一點是它比駕車便宜。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise reasons without listing everything at once.","zh":"這個短語有助組織理由，而不用一次列出所有內容。"},{"en":"It often suggests that more reasons may follow.","zh":"它常暗示之後可能還有更多理由。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not nearly as visible as","meaning":"遠不如……明顯","examples":[{"en":"Women’s pockets were not nearly as visible as men’s.","zh":"女性衣袋遠不如男性衣袋明顯。"},{"en":"Not nearly as visible as means much less easy to see than something else.","zh":"not nearly as visible as 是指遠比另一物難看見。"},{"en":"A small sign behind a tree is not nearly as visible as a large sign at the entrance.","zh":"樹後的小標誌遠不如入口處的大標誌明顯。"},{"en":"If a detail is not visible, people may overlook its importance.","zh":"如果某個細節不明顯，人們可能忽略它的重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly compares how easy two things are to notice.","zh":"這個短語強烈比較兩件事有多容易被注意到。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"easy to reach","meaning":"容易拿取","examples":[{"en":"Women’s pockets were not as easy to reach as men’s.","zh":"女性衣袋不如男性衣袋容易拿取。"},{"en":"Easy to reach means simple to get to or access with your hand.","zh":"easy to reach 是指容易用手拿到或接觸到。"},{"en":"A phone in a front pocket is easy to reach when it rings.","zh":"電話放在前袋，響起時便容易拿取。"},{"en":"If something is hard to reach, people may avoid using it often.","zh":"如果某物難以拿取，人們可能不常使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase is often about physical access and convenience.","zh":"這個短語常關於實體接觸和便利性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"numerous possessions","meaning":"許多隨身物品","examples":[{"en":"Women carried numerous possessions on their person.","zh":"女性隨身攜帶許多物品。"},{"en":"Numerous possessions means many personal belongings or items.","zh":"numerous possessions 是指很多個人物品或東西。"},{"en":"A traveller may carry numerous possessions, including tickets, medicine, chargers, and cash.","zh":"旅客可能攜帶許多隨身物品，包括車票、藥物、充電器和現金。"},{"en":"Carrying numerous possessions requires safe storage so items do not get lost.","zh":"攜帶許多物品需要安全存放，這樣物品才不會遺失。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds more formal than “lots of things”.","zh":"這個短語比 lots of things 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be worth a lot of money","meaning":"值很多錢","examples":[{"en":"Some of the possessions could be worth a lot of money.","zh":"有些物品可能值很多錢。"},{"en":"To be worth a lot of money means to have high financial value.","zh":"be worth a lot of money 是指有很高金錢價值。"},{"en":"A watch may be worth a lot of money if it is rare or made by a famous brand.","zh":"如果手錶罕有或由著名品牌製造，它可能值很多錢。"},{"en":"Valuable objects attract thieves because they can be sold for profit.","zh":"貴重物品會吸引小偷，因為可以賣出圖利。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why people need to protect certain belongings carefully.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何人們需要小心保護某些物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"vulnerable to theft","meaning":"較容易成為盜竊目標","examples":[{"en":"Women were more vulnerable to theft.","zh":"女性較容易成為盜竊目標。"},{"en":"To be vulnerable to theft means to be more likely to have belongings stolen.","zh":"be vulnerable to theft 是指較容易被人偷走財物。"},{"en":"Tourists carrying open bags in crowded markets are vulnerable to theft.","zh":"在擁擠市集攜帶開口袋的遊客較容易成為盜竊目標。"},{"en":"If valuables are visible and easy to reach, the owner becomes more vulnerable to theft.","zh":"如果貴重物品明顯又容易拿到，物主便更容易成為盜竊目標。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights risk and the need for protection.","zh":"這個短語突出風險和保護需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"wealthy women","meaning":"富有女性","examples":[{"en":"Wealthy women worried constantly about pickpockets.","zh":"富有女性經常擔心扒手。"},{"en":"Wealthy women are women who have a lot of money or valuable possessions.","zh":"wealthy women 是指擁有很多金錢或貴重物品的女性。"},{"en":"In the past, wealthy women might wear expensive fabrics, jewellery, and decorated accessories.","zh":"在過去，富有女性可能穿昂貴布料、佩戴珠寶和裝飾配飾。"},{"en":"Wealth can increase the risk of theft because valuable objects attract attention.","zh":"財富可能增加被盜風險，因為貴重物品會吸引注意。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to social and financial status.","zh":"這個短語指社會和財政地位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in particular","meaning":"尤其是","examples":[{"en":"Wealthy women, in particular, worried about pickpockets.","zh":"尤其是富有女性，會擔心扒手。"},{"en":"In particular means especially or more than others.","zh":"in particular 是指尤其是，或比其他人事物更特別。"},{"en":"Students, in particular, need affordable transport because many do not earn money.","zh":"尤其是學生需要負擔得起的交通，因為很多學生沒有收入。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights one group or detail within a larger situation.","zh":"這個短語在較大情況中突出一個群體或細節。"},{"en":"It is useful when one example deserves special attention.","zh":"當某個例子值得特別注意時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"worry constantly about","meaning":"經常擔心……","examples":[{"en":"Wealthy women worried constantly about pickpockets.","zh":"富有女性經常擔心扒手。"},{"en":"To worry constantly about something means to keep feeling anxious about it again and again.","zh":"worry constantly about something 是指不斷反覆為某事感到焦慮。"},{"en":"Parents may worry constantly about a child who travels home late every night.","zh":"如果孩子每天很晚回家，父母可能會經常擔心。"},{"en":"Constant worry can change behaviour because people try to avoid danger.","zh":"持續擔心會改變行為，因為人們會嘗試避開危險。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repeated anxiety, not just one short moment of concern.","zh":"這個短語表示反覆焦慮，而不只是短暫擔心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pickpockets","meaning":"扒手","examples":[{"en":"Wealthy women worried constantly about pickpockets.","zh":"富有女性經常擔心扒手。"},{"en":"Pickpockets are thieves who steal things from people’s pockets or bags in public places.","zh":"pickpockets 是在公共地方從別人的衣袋或袋中偷東西的小偷。"},{"en":"Pickpockets often work in crowded areas such as markets, stations, and tourist sites.","zh":"扒手常在市集、車站和旅遊景點等擁擠地方活動。"},{"en":"People protect themselves from pickpockets by keeping valuables hidden and close to the body.","zh":"人們把貴重物品藏好並貼身保管，以防扒手。"},{"en":"This word refers to a specific kind of thief who steals secretly.","zh":"這個詞指一種秘密偷竊的特定小偷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"what they did was to","meaning":"她們的做法是……","examples":[{"en":"What they did was to have a pair of pockets made.","zh":"她們的做法是請人製作一對衣袋。"},{"en":"What they did was to is used to emphasise the action someone chose as a solution.","zh":"what they did was to 用來強調某人選擇作為解決方法的行動。"},{"en":"The room was too noisy, so what the teacher did was to move the discussion outside.","zh":"房間太嘈，所以老師的做法是把討論移到外面。"},{"en":"This structure makes the action sound like a deliberate response to a problem.","zh":"這個結構令行動聽起來像是對問題的有意識回應。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining how people dealt with a situation.","zh":"當解釋人們如何處理情況時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have something made","meaning":"請人製作某物","examples":[{"en":"Women had a pair of pockets made.","zh":"女性請人製作一對衣袋。"},{"en":"To have something made means to ask or pay someone else to make it for you.","zh":"have something made 是指請人或付錢給別人為你製作某物。"},{"en":"A family may have curtains made if the windows are an unusual size.","zh":"如果窗戶尺寸不常見，一個家庭可能會請人製作窗簾。"},{"en":"People have items made when ordinary shop products do not fit their needs.","zh":"當普通商店產品不符合需要，人們會請人製作物品。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on arranging the work, not making the item yourself.","zh":"這個短語著重安排別人做工，而不是自己製作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a pair of pockets","meaning":"一對衣袋","examples":[{"en":"Women had a pair of pockets made and tied together.","zh":"女性請人製作一對衣袋並把它們綁在一起。"},{"en":"A pair of pockets means two pockets designed to be used together.","zh":"a pair of pockets 是指設計成一起使用的兩個衣袋。"},{"en":"A pair of pockets on a jacket can help balance weight on both sides.","zh":"外套上的一對衣袋可以幫助平衡兩邊重量。"},{"en":"Having two pockets gives the wearer more space and better organisation.","zh":"有兩個衣袋給穿着者更多空間和更好分類。"},{"en":"This phrase uses “pair” because the pockets come as two matching parts.","zh":"這個短語使用 pair，因為衣袋是一組兩個相配部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be tied together with","meaning":"用……綁在一起","examples":[{"en":"The pockets were tied together with string.","zh":"這些衣袋用繩綁在一起。"},{"en":"To be tied together with something means to be joined using that material.","zh":"be tied together with something 是指用某種材料把物件連接起來。"},{"en":"Old newspapers may be tied together with rope before recycling.","zh":"舊報紙回收前可能會用繩綁在一起。"},{"en":"Tying two items together helps keep them from separating or getting lost.","zh":"把兩件物品綁在一起有助防止它們分開或遺失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the action and the material used.","zh":"這個短語同時描述動作和所使用的材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"string","meaning":"繩","examples":[{"en":"The pockets were tied together with string.","zh":"這些衣袋用繩綁在一起。"},{"en":"String is thin cord used for tying, fastening, or hanging things.","zh":"string 是用來綁、固定或懸掛物品的幼繩。"},{"en":"A child may use string to tie a label onto a school bag.","zh":"孩子可能用繩把標籤綁在書包上。"},{"en":"String is useful because it is light, flexible, and easy to knot.","zh":"繩很有用，因為它輕、柔軟，而且容易打結。"},{"en":"This word refers to a simple tying material, not a musical instrument string here.","zh":"這裏的 string 指簡單綁物材料，而不是樂器的弦。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be made of","meaning":"由……製成","examples":[{"en":"The pockets were made of fabric.","zh":"這些衣袋由布料製成。"},{"en":"To be made of something means to consist of that material.","zh":"be made of something 是指由某種材料組成。"},{"en":"A desk may be made of wood, metal, or plastic.","zh":"書桌可能由木、金屬或塑膠製成。"},{"en":"The material something is made of affects its strength, weight, and appearance.","zh":"某物由甚麼材料製成，會影響其強度、重量和外觀。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when describing what an object physically consists of.","zh":"當描述物件實際由甚麼組成時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fabric","meaning":"布料","examples":[{"en":"The pockets were made of fabric.","zh":"這些衣袋由布料製成。"},{"en":"Fabric is cloth used for making clothing, bags, curtains, and other soft items.","zh":"fabric 是用來製作衣服、袋、窗簾和其他柔軟物品的布料。"},{"en":"A tailor may choose strong fabric for pockets because they hold objects.","zh":"裁縫可能為衣袋選擇結實布料，因為衣袋要承載物件。"},{"en":"Fabric can be cheap, expensive, plain, colourful, thin, or thick.","zh":"布料可以便宜、昂貴、樸素、彩色、薄或厚。"},{"en":"This word focuses on cloth as a material.","zh":"這個詞著重作為材料的布。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"recycled cloth","meaning":"再用布料","examples":[{"en":"Poorer wearers might use recycled cloth for their pockets.","zh":"較貧窮的穿着者可能用再用布料製作衣袋。"},{"en":"Recycled cloth is fabric reused from old clothing or other textiles.","zh":"recycled cloth 是從舊衣物或其他紡織品再利用的布料。"},{"en":"A family may use recycled cloth to make cleaning rags or simple bags.","zh":"家庭可能用再用布料製作清潔布或簡單袋子。"},{"en":"Using recycled cloth saves money and reduces waste.","zh":"使用再用布料可以省錢並減少浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests practical reuse rather than buying new fabric.","zh":"這個短語表示實際重用，而不是購買新布料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"if the wearer had little money","meaning":"如果穿着者錢不多","examples":[{"en":"The pockets might be made of recycled cloth if the wearer had little money.","zh":"如果穿着者錢不多，衣袋可能由再用布料製成。"},{"en":"If the wearer had little money means if the person wearing the item was poor or had limited income.","zh":"if the wearer had little money 是指如果穿着該物的人貧窮或收入有限。"},{"en":"If a student has little money, she may buy second-hand books instead of new ones.","zh":"如果學生錢不多，她可能買二手書而不是新書。"},{"en":"Limited money often affects what materials people can choose.","zh":"金錢有限常會影響人們可以選擇甚麼材料。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how financial situation influences clothing choices.","zh":"這個短語解釋財政狀況如何影響服裝選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"something more expensive","meaning":"較昂貴的東西","examples":[{"en":"Richer women might use something more expensive such as linen.","zh":"較富有的女性可能使用較昂貴的東西，例如亞麻布。"},{"en":"Something more expensive means an item or material that costs more money than another option.","zh":"something more expensive 是指比另一選項花費更多金錢的物品或材料。"},{"en":"A restaurant may use something more expensive, such as fresh seafood, for a special menu.","zh":"餐廳可能為特別餐牌使用較昂貴的東西，例如新鮮海鮮。"},{"en":"People choose more expensive materials when they want better quality, status, or appearance.","zh":"人們想要更好質素、地位或外觀時，會選擇較昂貴的材料。"},{"en":"This phrase compares cheaper and dearer choices without naming all options.","zh":"這個短語比較較便宜和較昂貴的選擇，而不列出所有選項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"linen","meaning":"亞麻布","examples":[{"en":"Some pockets were made of linen.","zh":"有些衣袋由亞麻布製成。"},{"en":"Linen is a strong cloth made from the flax plant.","zh":"linen 是由亞麻植物製成的結實布料。"},{"en":"Linen shirts are popular in hot weather because the fabric feels light and breathable.","zh":"亞麻恤衫在炎熱天氣中受歡迎，因為布料感覺輕盈透氣。"},{"en":"Linen was often valued because it could look clean, fine, and expensive.","zh":"亞麻布常被重視，因為它看起來乾淨、精細和昂貴。"},{"en":"This word refers to a specific type of fabric.","zh":"這個詞指一種特定布料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"feature delicate embroidery","meaning":"有精緻刺繡","examples":[{"en":"Some pockets featured very delicate embroidery.","zh":"有些衣袋有非常精緻的刺繡。"},{"en":"To feature delicate embroidery means to include fine stitched decoration as an important detail.","zh":"feature delicate embroidery 是指包含精細針線裝飾作為重要細節。"},{"en":"A wedding dress may feature delicate embroidery around the sleeves.","zh":"婚紗可能在袖口周圍有精緻刺繡。"},{"en":"Delicate embroidery can make a simple item look more expensive and personal.","zh":"精緻刺繡可以令簡單物件看起來更昂貴和個人化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes decoration that is carefully made and visually important.","zh":"這個短語描述細心製作且視覺上重要的裝飾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"delicate embroidery","meaning":"精緻刺繡","examples":[{"en":"Some women’s pockets had delicate embroidery.","zh":"有些女性衣袋有精緻刺繡。"},{"en":"Delicate embroidery is fine, careful decorative stitching on fabric.","zh":"delicate embroidery 是布料上精細而細心的裝飾刺繡。"},{"en":"A handkerchief with delicate embroidery may be kept as a special gift.","zh":"有精緻刺繡的手帕可能被保存為特別禮物。"},{"en":"Delicate embroidery takes time and skill because the stitches are small and detailed.","zh":"精緻刺繡需要時間和技巧，因為針腳細小而仔細。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests beauty, care, and fine craftsmanship.","zh":"這個短語表示美感、用心和精細工藝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tie something around","meaning":"把某物綁在……周圍","examples":[{"en":"Women tied the pockets around their waist.","zh":"女性把衣袋綁在腰間。"},{"en":"To tie something around a body part means to fasten it so it goes around that part.","zh":"tie something around a body part 是指把某物固定，使它圍着身體某部位。"},{"en":"A runner may tie a jacket around her waist when she gets too warm.","zh":"跑步者覺得太熱時，可能把外套綁在腰間。"},{"en":"Tying something around the waist keeps it close while leaving the hands free.","zh":"把某物綁在腰間，可以讓它貼身，又可空出雙手。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fastening by wrapping and knotting.","zh":"這個短語描述透過圍繞和打結來固定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"around their waist","meaning":"在腰間","examples":[{"en":"Women wore the pockets around their waist.","zh":"女性把衣袋穿戴在腰間。"},{"en":"Around their waist means encircling the middle part of the body.","zh":"around their waist 是指圍繞身體中間部分。"},{"en":"A belt is worn around the waist to hold trousers in place.","zh":"皮帶戴在腰間，用來固定褲子。"},{"en":"Items worn around the waist are usually easy to carry without using the hands.","zh":"戴在腰間的物件通常容易攜帶，又不用雙手拿着。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position on the body.","zh":"這個短語描述身體上的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hang beneath","meaning":"垂在……下面","examples":[{"en":"The pockets hung beneath women’s clothes.","zh":"衣袋垂在女性衣服下面。"},{"en":"To hang beneath something means to hang or rest below it.","zh":"hang beneath something 是指垂掛或位於某物下方。"},{"en":"A name tag may hang beneath a visitor’s jacket if the cord is too long.","zh":"如果繩太長，名牌可能垂在訪客外套下面。"},{"en":"If something hangs beneath clothing, it may be hidden from view.","zh":"如果某物垂在衣服下面，它可能被隱藏起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position below another object.","zh":"這個短語描述位於另一物下方的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"beneath their clothes","meaning":"在她們衣服下面","examples":[{"en":"Women’s pockets were hidden beneath their clothes.","zh":"女性衣袋藏在她們衣服下面。"},{"en":"Beneath their clothes means under the garments they were wearing.","zh":"beneath their clothes 是指在她們穿着的衣物下面。"},{"en":"A money belt may be worn beneath clothes when travelling.","zh":"旅行時，貼身錢包可能戴在衣服下面。"},{"en":"Keeping valuables beneath clothing can reduce the risk of theft.","zh":"把貴重物品放在衣服下面可以減少被盜風險。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that something is covered and not easily seen.","zh":"這個短語強調某物被遮蓋，不容易看見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"plenty of room","meaning":"足夠空間","examples":[{"en":"There was plenty of room to hide small possessions.","zh":"有足夠空間藏起小型物品。"},{"en":"Plenty of room means enough space, or more than enough space.","zh":"plenty of room 是指有足夠或綽綽有餘的空間。"},{"en":"A large school bag has plenty of room for books, lunch, and sports clothes.","zh":"大書包有足夠空間放書、午餐和運動服。"},{"en":"When there is plenty of room, people can store things without squeezing them in.","zh":"當有足夠空間，人們可以存放物品而不用硬塞。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests comfort and sufficient space.","zh":"這個短語表示舒適和空間充足。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a whole range of","meaning":"各式各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"Women could hide a whole range of small possessions.","zh":"女性可以藏起各式各樣的小型物品。"},{"en":"A whole range of something means many different kinds of it.","zh":"a whole range of something 是指許多不同種類的某物。"},{"en":"A supermarket sells a whole range of snacks, drinks, and household items.","zh":"超級市場售賣各式各樣的零食、飲品和家居用品。"},{"en":"Having a range of choices helps people find what suits their needs.","zh":"有多種選擇可以幫助人們找到適合自己需要的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises variety, not just quantity.","zh":"這個短語強調種類多，而不只是數量多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"layers of petticoats","meaning":"多層襯裙","examples":[{"en":"Women hid possessions between the layers of petticoats.","zh":"女性把物品藏在多層襯裙之間。"},{"en":"Layers of petticoats means several underskirts worn one over another under a skirt or dress.","zh":"layers of petticoats 是指穿在裙或連身裙下面、一層疊一層的多條襯裙。"},{"en":"Historical costumes may include layers of petticoats to make a skirt look fuller.","zh":"歷史服裝可能包括多層襯裙，使裙子看起來更蓬鬆。"},{"en":"Multiple layers created space where hidden pockets could be worn.","zh":"多層衣物創造了可穿戴隱藏衣袋的空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clothing built up in several fabric levels.","zh":"這個短語描述由幾層布料組成的服裝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"petticoats","meaning":"襯裙","examples":[{"en":"Petticoats were commonly worn under skirts.","zh":"襯裙過去常穿在裙子下面。"},{"en":"Petticoats are underskirts worn beneath outer skirts or dresses.","zh":"petticoats 是穿在外層裙或連身裙下面的襯裙。"},{"en":"In the past, petticoats helped shape the skirt and add warmth.","zh":"在過去，襯裙幫助塑造裙形並增加保暖。"},{"en":"Petticoats could also hide pockets or other small items under the outer clothing.","zh":"襯裙也可以把衣袋或其他小物件藏在外衣下面。"},{"en":"This word is mainly used when discussing traditional or historical women’s clothing.","zh":"這個詞主要用於討論傳統或歷史女性服裝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"commonly worn","meaning":"常穿的","examples":[{"en":"Petticoats were commonly worn in the past.","zh":"襯裙在過去是常穿的。"},{"en":"Commonly worn means often worn by many people or in many situations.","zh":"commonly worn 是指很多人或在很多情況下經常穿着。"},{"en":"School uniforms are commonly worn by students in many countries.","zh":"校服在許多國家是學生常穿的衣物。"},{"en":"Clothing becomes commonly worn when it is practical, accepted, or fashionable.","zh":"當衣物實用、被接受或流行時，它便會變得常穿。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequency and social normality.","zh":"這個短語描述頻率和社會上的普遍性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an opening in","meaning":"……中的開口","examples":[{"en":"Women had an opening in the folds of their skirts.","zh":"女性在裙子的褶位中有一個開口。"},{"en":"An opening in something is a hole, gap, or space that lets someone reach or pass through.","zh":"an opening in something 是某物中的洞、縫隙或空間，讓人伸手或通過。"},{"en":"A jacket may have an opening in the sleeve where the lining has torn.","zh":"外套袖子裏襯破了時，可能會有一個開口。"},{"en":"An opening makes hidden parts easier to reach.","zh":"開口令隱藏部分更容易拿到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical gap within a larger surface or structure.","zh":"這個短語描述較大表面或結構中的實體縫隙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"folds of their skirts","meaning":"裙子的褶位","examples":[{"en":"Women reached their pockets through the folds of their skirts.","zh":"女性透過裙子的褶位拿到衣袋。"},{"en":"The folds of their skirts are the pleats or overlapping parts of fabric in the skirt.","zh":"folds of their skirts 是裙子上的褶位或重疊布料部分。"},{"en":"A long skirt may have folds that move when the wearer walks.","zh":"長裙可能有走路時會擺動的褶位。"},{"en":"Folds can hide openings, pockets, or small repairs in clothing.","zh":"褶位可以隱藏開口、衣袋或小修補痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the gathered or layered parts of a skirt.","zh":"這個短語描述裙子收摺或重疊的部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"through which","meaning":"透過它","examples":[{"en":"They had an opening through which they could reach their pockets.","zh":"她們有一個開口，透過它可以拿到衣袋。"},{"en":"Through which means by means of that opening, place, or thing.","zh":"through which 是指透過那個開口、地方或東西。"},{"en":"The door had a small window through which visitors could see inside.","zh":"那扇門有一個小窗，訪客可以透過它看見裏面。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a noun with the action made possible by it.","zh":"這個短語把名詞與它所促成的動作連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is often used in more formal or careful writing.","zh":"它常用於較正式或仔細的寫作中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"whatever they needed","meaning":"她們需要的任何東西","examples":[{"en":"Women could reach whatever they needed through the opening.","zh":"女性可以透過開口拿到她們需要的任何東西。"},{"en":"Whatever they needed means anything that was necessary at that moment.","zh":"whatever they needed 是指當時所需的任何東西。"},{"en":"A teacher keeps pens, notes, and stickers nearby so she can get whatever she needs during class.","zh":"老師把筆、筆記和貼紙放在附近，這樣上課時可拿到需要的任何東西。"},{"en":"Having easy access to items helps people act quickly when they need them.","zh":"容易拿到物品有助人們在需要時迅速行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is broad and does not name each item individually.","zh":"這個短語範圍廣，不逐一列出每件物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"working women","meaning":"職業女性；勞動女性","examples":[{"en":"Working women also needed to carry useful items.","zh":"職業女性也需要攜帶有用物品。"},{"en":"Working women are women who do paid work or labour, either at home or outside it.","zh":"working women 是指從事有薪工作或勞動的女性，不論在家中或外面。"},{"en":"Working women in markets may need to carry money, tools, lists, or small goods.","zh":"市場中的勞動女性可能需要攜帶金錢、工具、清單或小貨品。"},{"en":"Work needs can influence clothing because people must carry items while moving around.","zh":"工作需要可以影響服裝，因為人們活動時必須攜帶物品。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on women’s role as workers, not only their social appearance.","zh":"這個短語著重女性作為工作者的角色，而不只是社交外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"carry around","meaning":"隨身攜帶","examples":[{"en":"Working women needed to carry around items for their work.","zh":"勞動女性需要隨身攜帶工作用品。"},{"en":"To carry around something means to take it with you from place to place.","zh":"carry around something 是指把某物從一個地方帶到另一個地方。"},{"en":"A student may carry around a water bottle all day at school.","zh":"學生可能整天在學校隨身攜帶水樽。"},{"en":"People carry things around when they need them often or cannot leave them safely elsewhere.","zh":"當人們經常需要某些東西，或不能安全地把它們放在別處時，便會隨身攜帶。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests regular movement with items on the body or in a bag.","zh":"這個短語表示帶着物品到處移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"job or trade","meaning":"工作或行業","examples":[{"en":"Working women carried items for whatever job or trade they were involved in.","zh":"勞動女性會攜帶她們所從事工作或行業所需的物品。"},{"en":"Job or trade means a person’s work, especially skilled or practical work.","zh":"job or trade 是指一個人的工作，尤其是有技能或實用性的工作。"},{"en":"A carpenter’s trade requires tools, while a teacher’s job requires books and lesson plans.","zh":"木匠的行業需要工具，而老師的工作需要書本和教案。"},{"en":"The items people carry often depend on their job or trade.","zh":"人們攜帶的物品常取決於其工作或行業。"},{"en":"This phrase covers different kinds of work, from professions to manual skills.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋不同類型工作，從專業到手工技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be involved in","meaning":"從事；參與","examples":[{"en":"Working women carried items for the trade they were involved in.","zh":"勞動女性會攜帶她們所從事行業需要的物品。"},{"en":"To be involved in something means to take part in it or have a role in it.","zh":"be involved in something 是指參與某事或在其中有角色。"},{"en":"A parent may be involved in a school event by helping with tickets or food.","zh":"家長可能透過幫忙賣票或準備食物參與學校活動。"},{"en":"If someone is involved in a trade, their daily tasks and tools may shape what they wear.","zh":"如果某人從事某個行業，日常任務和工具可能會影響其衣着。"},{"en":"This phrase shows participation or connection.","zh":"這個短語顯示參與或連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"remain on the inside of","meaning":"留在……內側","examples":[{"en":"Women’s pockets remained on the inside of their clothing.","zh":"女性衣袋仍然留在衣服內側。"},{"en":"To remain on the inside of something means to stay within or beneath the inner part.","zh":"remain on the inside of something 是指保持在某物內部或內側下方。"},{"en":"A label may remain on the inside of a jacket so it does not affect the outside appearance.","zh":"標籤可能留在外套內側，這樣不會影響外觀。"},{"en":"Keeping pockets inside clothing made them less visible but harder to reach.","zh":"把衣袋放在衣服內側令它們較不明顯，但較難拿取。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the position did not move to the outside.","zh":"這個短語強調位置沒有移到外面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get bigger or longer","meaning":"變得更大或更長","examples":[{"en":"The pockets just got bigger or longer.","zh":"衣袋只是變得更大或更長。"},{"en":"To get bigger or longer means to increase in size or length.","zh":"get bigger or longer 是指尺寸或長度增加。"},{"en":"A child’s school trousers may get longer as sizes increase.","zh":"隨着尺碼增加，孩子的校褲可能會變得更長。"},{"en":"Objects get bigger or longer when people need more space or coverage.","zh":"當人們需要更多空間或覆蓋範圍，物件會變得更大或更長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple physical change.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單的實體變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"reach down to","meaning":"垂到……","examples":[{"en":"Some pockets reached down to women’s knees.","zh":"有些衣袋垂到女性膝蓋。"},{"en":"To reach down to a place means to extend downward as far as that point.","zh":"reach down to a place 是指向下延伸到某個位置。"},{"en":"A long coat may reach down to a person’s ankles.","zh":"長外套可能垂到一個人的腳踝。"},{"en":"If pockets reach down to the knees, they must be very long and spacious.","zh":"如果衣袋垂到膝蓋，它們一定非常長和寬敞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the lowest point something extends to.","zh":"這個短語描述某物向下延伸到的最低位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tie-on pockets","meaning":"綁帶式衣袋","examples":[{"en":"Tie-on pockets continued well into the 19th century.","zh":"綁帶式衣袋一直延續到19世紀很長一段時間。"},{"en":"Tie-on pockets are separate pockets attached to the body by tying them on, rather than sewn into clothing.","zh":"tie-on pockets 是用綁帶繫在身上的分離式衣袋，而不是縫進衣服的衣袋。"},{"en":"A costume designer may use tie-on pockets to recreate historical women’s clothing.","zh":"服裝設計師可能使用綁帶式衣袋重現歷史女性服裝。"},{"en":"Tie-on pockets were practical because they could be worn under different skirts.","zh":"綁帶式衣袋很實用，因為它們可以穿在不同裙子下面。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to removable pockets fastened with ties or string.","zh":"這個短語指用帶子或繩固定的可拆式衣袋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"go well into","meaning":"一直延續到……","examples":[{"en":"Tie-on pockets went well into the 19th century.","zh":"綁帶式衣袋一直延續到19世紀很長一段時間。"},{"en":"To go well into a period means to continue far into that period, not just reach its beginning.","zh":"go well into a period 是指持續到某時期的較後部分，而不只是到其開始。"},{"en":"Some old school rules continued well into the 20th century.","zh":"有些舊校規一直延續到20世紀很長一段時間。"},{"en":"When a practice goes well into a later period, it remains common longer than expected.","zh":"當一種做法一直延續到較後時期，它比預期更長時間保持常見。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises duration and continuation.","zh":"這個短語強調持續時間和延續性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"altered towards the end of","meaning":"在……末期改變","examples":[{"en":"Fashion altered towards the end of the 19th century.","zh":"時裝在19世紀末期改變。"},{"en":"To alter towards the end of a period means to change near the final part of that period.","zh":"alter towards the end of a period 是指在某段時期接近結尾時改變。"},{"en":"School rules altered towards the end of the year after parents complained.","zh":"家長投訴後，校規在學年末期改變。"},{"en":"Changes near the end of a period can lead to a new style or system.","zh":"時期末段的改變可以帶來新風格或新制度。"},{"en":"This phrase links timing with gradual change.","zh":"這個短語把時間與逐漸變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"towards the end of","meaning":"到……末期","examples":[{"en":"Pocket fashion changed towards the end of the period.","zh":"衣袋時裝到該時期末期改變。"},{"en":"Towards the end of means near the final part of a time, event, or process.","zh":"towards the end of 是指接近某段時間、活動或過程的最後部分。"},{"en":"Towards the end of the lesson, the teacher gave a short quiz.","zh":"到課堂末段，老師給了一個小測。"},{"en":"Important changes sometimes happen towards the end because people are preparing for the next stage.","zh":"重要改變有時發生在末期，因為人們正準備進入下一階段。"},{"en":"This phrase helps locate an event in time.","zh":"這個短語幫助指出事件發生的時間位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"dresses became tighter","meaning":"連身裙變得更貼身","examples":[{"en":"Dresses became tighter towards the end of the 19th century.","zh":"連身裙在19世紀末變得更貼身。"},{"en":"Dresses became tighter means dresses fitted more closely to the body.","zh":"dresses became tighter 是指連身裙更貼近身體。"},{"en":"Sports clothing became tighter when designers wanted to reduce extra fabric and improve movement.","zh":"當設計師想減少多餘布料並改善活動時，運動服變得更貼身。"},{"en":"When dresses became tighter, hidden bulky pockets became easier to see.","zh":"當連身裙變得更貼身，隱藏而厚重的衣袋便更容易被看見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change in clothing shape and fit.","zh":"這個短語描述衣物形狀和剪裁的改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"less bulky","meaning":"較不厚重","examples":[{"en":"Dresses became tighter and less bulky.","zh":"連身裙變得更貼身和較不厚重。"},{"en":"Less bulky means less thick, heavy, or large in shape.","zh":"less bulky 是指形狀上不那麼厚、不那麼重或不那麼大。"},{"en":"A thin laptop is less bulky than an old heavy computer.","zh":"薄身手提電腦比舊式笨重電腦較不厚重。"},{"en":"Clothing becomes less bulky when designers remove extra layers or loose fabric.","zh":"當設計師移除額外層次或寬鬆布料，衣物會變得較不厚重。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests a slimmer, lighter, or more convenient design.","zh":"這個短語常暗示較修身、較輕或較方便的設計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"become very noticeable","meaning":"變得非常顯眼","examples":[{"en":"The pairs of pockets became very noticeable.","zh":"一對對衣袋變得非常顯眼。"},{"en":"To become very noticeable means to become easy to see or attract attention.","zh":"become very noticeable 是指變得很容易看見或吸引注意。"},{"en":"A stain on a white shirt becomes very noticeable under bright light.","zh":"白恤衫上的污漬在強光下會變得非常顯眼。"},{"en":"When hidden pockets stood out under tight dresses, they became a fashion problem.","zh":"當隱藏衣袋在貼身裙下突出，它們便成為時裝問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change from hidden or subtle to obvious.","zh":"這個短語描述從隱藏或不明顯變成明顯。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stand out too much","meaning":"太突出","examples":[{"en":"The pockets stood out too much under tighter dresses.","zh":"衣袋在較貼身的連身裙下太突出。"},{"en":"To stand out too much means to be too noticeable in a way that looks awkward or unwanted.","zh":"stand out too much 是指過於明顯，以致看起來尷尬或不合意。"},{"en":"Bright red shoes may stand out too much at a very formal black-tie event.","zh":"在非常正式的黑領結活動中，鮮紅色鞋可能太突出。"},{"en":"If something stands out too much, it can distract from the overall appearance.","zh":"如果某物太突出，它可能分散人們對整體外觀的注意。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows that visibility has become a problem.","zh":"這個短語常表示可見程度已成為問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"detract from","meaning":"有損……","examples":[{"en":"The visible pockets detracted from the woman’s image.","zh":"顯眼的衣袋有損女性形象。"},{"en":"To detract from something means to make it less attractive, effective, or impressive.","zh":"detract from something 是指令某事較不吸引、較不有效或較不令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"Spelling mistakes can detract from an otherwise strong essay.","zh":"串字錯誤可能有損一篇本來很強的文章。"},{"en":"Bulky pockets could detract from a smooth fashionable outline.","zh":"厚重衣袋可能有損平滑的時尚輪廓。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one detail weakens the overall effect.","zh":"當某個細節削弱整體效果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"women who had been used to","meaning":"已經習慣……的女性","examples":[{"en":"Women who had been used to carrying possessions needed another solution.","zh":"已經習慣攜帶物品的女性需要另一個解決方法。"},{"en":"Women who had been used to doing something means women who had become familiar with that habit.","zh":"women who had been used to doing something 是指已熟悉某種習慣的女性。"},{"en":"Students who had been used to online classes needed time to return to face-to-face lessons.","zh":"已經習慣網課的學生需要時間回到面授課堂。"},{"en":"When people are used to a habit, sudden change can create inconvenience.","zh":"當人們習慣某種做法，突然改變可能造成不便。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a new solution was necessary.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何需要新的解決方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"personal possessions","meaning":"私人物品","examples":[{"en":"Women wanted to keep carrying personal possessions.","zh":"女性想繼續攜帶私人物品。"},{"en":"Personal possessions are items that belong to someone and are used or valued by that person.","zh":"personal possessions 是屬於某人並由其使用或重視的物品。"},{"en":"A student’s personal possessions may include a wallet, phone, keys, and notebook.","zh":"學生的私人物品可能包括銀包、電話、鑰匙和筆記簿。"},{"en":"People need safe places for personal possessions because losing them can cause trouble.","zh":"人們需要安全地方放私人物品，因為遺失它們可能造成麻煩。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to belongings, especially those carried or owned individually.","zh":"這個短語指個人擁有的物品，尤其是隨身攜帶或個人所有的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"somewhere to carry","meaning":"用來攜帶……的地方","examples":[{"en":"Women needed somewhere to carry these items.","zh":"女性需要一個用來攜帶這些物品的地方。"},{"en":"Somewhere to carry something means a place or container for transporting it.","zh":"somewhere to carry something 是指用來運送某物的地方或容器。"},{"en":"A commuter needs somewhere to carry a laptop safely on the train.","zh":"通勤者需要一個地方在火車上安全攜帶手提電腦。"},{"en":"If clothing has no pockets, people may need a bag as somewhere to carry small items.","zh":"如果衣服沒有衣袋，人們可能需要袋子作為攜帶小物品的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on storage during movement.","zh":"這個短語著重移動時的存放空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"about their person","meaning":"在身上","examples":[{"en":"Women needed somewhere to carry items about their person.","zh":"女性需要一個地方把物品帶在身上。"},{"en":"About their person means on or close to their body.","zh":"about their person 是指在她們身上或貼近身體。"},{"en":"A traveller may keep cash about their person instead of leaving it in a suitcase.","zh":"旅客可能把現金放在身上，而不是留在行李箱裏。"},{"en":"Keeping valuables about the person can be safer in crowded places.","zh":"在擁擠地方，把貴重物品放在身上可能較安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and similar to “on their person”.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思接近 on their person。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"that was when","meaning":"那就是……的時候","examples":[{"en":"That was when small bags came into fashion.","zh":"那就是小袋開始流行的時候。"},{"en":"That was when means that was the time at which something happened or began.","zh":"that was when 是指那正是某事發生或開始的時間。"},{"en":"The bus routes changed in 2018; that was when more people started cycling.","zh":"巴士路線在2018年改變；那就是更多人開始踩單車的時候。"},{"en":"This phrase links a change to the moment or period that caused it.","zh":"這個短語把一項改變與造成它的時刻或時期連繫起來。"},{"en":"It helps explain sequence in a story or historical account.","zh":"它有助在故事或歷史敘述中解釋次序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"small bags","meaning":"小袋","examples":[{"en":"Small bags became fashionable when dresses became tighter.","zh":"當連身裙變得更貼身，小袋開始流行。"},{"en":"Small bags are little containers carried by hand or worn to hold personal items.","zh":"small bags 是手拿或穿戴、用來放私人物品的小型容器。"},{"en":"A small bag can hold a phone, wallet, keys, and lipstick.","zh":"小袋可以放電話、銀包、鑰匙和唇膏。"},{"en":"When clothing has fewer useful pockets, small bags become more necessary.","zh":"當衣物較少實用衣袋，小袋便變得更有需要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to portable personal storage.","zh":"這個短語指可攜帶的個人儲物物件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pouches","meaning":"小囊袋","examples":[{"en":"Small bags were known as pouches.","zh":"小袋當時被稱為小囊袋。"},{"en":"Pouches are small soft bags used to hold or carry items.","zh":"pouches 是用來放置或攜帶物品的小型軟袋。"},{"en":"A traveller may keep coins in a small pouch inside a larger bag.","zh":"旅客可能把硬幣放在大袋內的小囊袋裏。"},{"en":"Pouches are useful because they group small things together and stop them from getting lost.","zh":"小囊袋很有用，因為它們把小物件集中起來，防止遺失。"},{"en":"This word often suggests a small, simple, soft container.","zh":"這個詞常表示小型、簡單、柔軟的容器。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as they were known","meaning":"正如當時所稱","examples":[{"en":"Small bags, or pouches as they were known, came into fashion.","zh":"小袋，正如當時所稱的小囊袋，開始流行。"},{"en":"As they were known means by the name people used for them at that time.","zh":"as they were known 是指按當時人們使用的名稱來說。"},{"en":"The early computers, as they were known then, filled whole rooms.","zh":"早期電腦，正如當時所稱，佔滿整個房間。"},{"en":"This phrase explains an older or alternative name for something.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物較舊或另一個名稱。"},{"en":"It is useful in historical writing when names have changed.","zh":"當名稱已經改變時，它在歷史寫作中很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"come into fashion","meaning":"開始流行","examples":[{"en":"Pouches came into fashion when dresses became tighter.","zh":"當連身裙變得更貼身，小囊袋開始流行。"},{"en":"To come into fashion means to become stylish, popular, or widely accepted.","zh":"come into fashion 是指變得時尚、流行或被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"Trainers came into fashion as everyday shoes when comfort became more important.","zh":"當舒適變得更重要，運動鞋開始作為日常鞋履流行。"},{"en":"An item comes into fashion when social habits and tastes make people want it.","zh":"當社會習慣和品味令人們想要某物，它便會開始流行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of popularity.","zh":"這個短語描述流行的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"inevitably","meaning":"無可避免地","examples":[{"en":"Pouches inevitably led on to the modern handbag.","zh":"小囊袋無可避免地進一步發展成現代手袋。"},{"en":"Inevitably means in a way that is almost certain to happen and difficult to avoid.","zh":"inevitably 是指幾乎一定會發生，而且難以避免。"},{"en":"If a class does not revise, mistakes will inevitably appear in the test.","zh":"如果一班學生不溫習，測驗中無可避免地會出現錯誤。"},{"en":"When a useful object becomes popular, it may inevitably develop into newer forms.","zh":"當一件有用物件變得流行，它可能無可避免地發展成更新形式。"},{"en":"This word suggests the result follows naturally from the situation.","zh":"這個詞表示結果自然地由情況引出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lead on to","meaning":"進一步發展成……","examples":[{"en":"Pouches led on to the handbag of more modern times.","zh":"小囊袋進一步發展成較現代時期的手袋。"},{"en":"To lead on to something means to develop into it or cause the next stage.","zh":"lead on to something 是指發展成某事，或引出下一階段。"},{"en":"Basic reading practice can lead on to more confident essay writing.","zh":"基本閱讀練習可以進一步發展成更有信心的文章寫作。"},{"en":"One design change may lead on to a completely new product later.","zh":"一項設計改變之後可能進一步發展成全新產品。"},{"en":"This phrase shows progression from one stage to another.","zh":"這個短語顯示從一個階段進展到另一階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"handbag","meaning":"手袋","examples":[{"en":"Pouches led on to the modern handbag.","zh":"小囊袋進一步發展成現代手袋。"},{"en":"A handbag is a bag, often carried by hand or over the shoulder, used for personal belongings.","zh":"handbag 是一種常用手提或肩背、用來放私人物品的袋。"},{"en":"A handbag may hold a purse, phone, keys, make-up, and travel card.","zh":"手袋可能放錢包、電話、鑰匙、化妝品和交通卡。"},{"en":"Handbags became important when clothing no longer provided enough hidden storage.","zh":"當衣物不再提供足夠隱藏儲物空間，手袋便變得重要。"},{"en":"This word usually refers to a personal bag, often associated with women’s fashion.","zh":"這個詞通常指個人用袋，常與女性時裝相關。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"more modern times","meaning":"較現代的時期","examples":[{"en":"Pouches developed into the handbag of more modern times.","zh":"小囊袋發展成較現代時期的手袋。"},{"en":"More modern times means later periods closer to the present.","zh":"more modern times 是指較接近現在的後來時期。"},{"en":"In more modern times, many people store tickets and money on their phones.","zh":"在較現代的時期，許多人把車票和金錢存放在手機上。"},{"en":"Objects often change in more modern times because technology and habits change.","zh":"物件在較現代的時期常會改變，因為科技和習慣會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts later history with earlier periods.","zh":"這個短語把後來歷史與較早時期作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"remove pockets altogether","meaning":"完全取消衣袋","examples":[{"en":"Fashion eventually removed pockets altogether.","zh":"時裝最終完全取消衣袋。"},{"en":"To remove pockets altogether means to take away pockets completely so none remain.","zh":"remove pockets altogether 是指完全拿走衣袋，令衣物沒有衣袋。"},{"en":"Some formal dresses remove pockets altogether to keep a smooth shape.","zh":"有些正式連身裙會完全取消衣袋，以保持平滑輪廓。"},{"en":"Removing pockets altogether can make clothing look neater but less practical.","zh":"完全取消衣袋可以令衣物看起來更整潔，但較不實用。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises total removal, not just making pockets smaller.","zh":"這個短語強調完全移除，而不只是把衣袋縮小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 10 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 11/task-1":[{"front":"camera club","meaning":"攝影會","examples":[{"en":"Dan wants to join the Wayside Camera Club.","zh":"Dan 想加入 Wayside 攝影會。"},{"en":"A camera club is a group where people meet to learn about photography, share photos, and join activities.","zh":"camera club 指一個人們聚在一起學習攝影、分享照片和參加活動的小組。"},{"en":"A student may join a camera club to learn how to take better pictures for school events.","zh":"學生可能加入攝影會，學習如何為學校活動拍更好的照片。"},{"en":"Camera clubs can help beginners improve because members give advice and feedback.","zh":"攝影會可以幫助初學者進步，因為會員會給建議和意見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a social group built around photography.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞攝影而建立的社交團體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"speaking","meaning":"我是……；……接聽","examples":[{"en":"Breda answers the phone by saying, “Wayside Camera Club, Breda speaking.”","zh":"Breda 接電話時說：「Wayside 攝影會，我是 Breda。」"},{"en":"“Speaking” is used on the phone to say who is answering or who is on the line.","zh":"“speaking” 用於電話中，表示誰正在接聽或誰在線上。"},{"en":"A receptionist may say, “Green Dental Clinic, Amy speaking,” when answering a call.","zh":"接待員接電話時可能說：「Green Dental Clinic，我是 Amy。」"},{"en":"This phrase helps callers know they have reached the right person or organisation.","zh":"這個短語幫助來電者知道自己是否打到正確的人或機構。"},{"en":"It is polite and common in telephone conversations.","zh":"它有禮，常見於電話對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"would like to join","meaning":"想加入","examples":[{"en":"Dan says he would like to join the club.","zh":"Dan 說他想加入這個會。"},{"en":"Would like to join means want to become a member in a polite way.","zh":"would like to join 指有禮地表示想成為成員。"},{"en":"A student may say, “I would like to join the chess club,” when speaking to the teacher in charge.","zh":"學生與負責老師說話時，可能說：「我想加入棋藝學會。」"},{"en":"Using “would like to” sounds more polite than simply saying “I want to”.","zh":"使用 “would like to” 比直接說 “I want to” 更有禮。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when applying for clubs, classes, or organisations.","zh":"申請加入學會、課程或組織時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"application form","meaning":"申請表","examples":[{"en":"The club has an application form for new members.","zh":"這個會有一份給新會員填寫的申請表。"},{"en":"An application form is a document that asks for details from someone who wants to join or apply.","zh":"application form 指要求申請者提供資料的文件。"},{"en":"A school may ask students to complete an application form before joining a study tour.","zh":"學校可能要求學生參加遊學團前填寫申請表。"},{"en":"Application forms help organisations collect names, addresses, contact details, and preferences.","zh":"申請表幫助組織收集姓名、地址、聯絡資料和偏好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal way to request membership or a place.","zh":"這個短語描述申請會員資格或名額的正式方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"complete it over the phone","meaning":"透過電話填寫","examples":[{"en":"Dan can complete the application form over the phone.","zh":"Dan 可以透過電話填寫申請表。"},{"en":"To complete it over the phone means to give the required information during a phone call instead of writing it yourself.","zh":"complete it over the phone 指在電話中提供所需資料，而不是自己書面填寫。"},{"en":"A receptionist may help an elderly customer complete a booking form over the phone.","zh":"接待員可能幫助年長顧客透過電話填寫預約表。"},{"en":"Completing a form by phone is useful when the applicant cannot visit in person.","zh":"當申請人不能親身到場時，透過電話填表很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes filling in information through a phone conversation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過電話對話填寫資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ask any questions","meaning":"提出任何問題","examples":[{"en":"Dan can ask any questions he might have while completing the form.","zh":"Dan 填寫表格時，可以提出任何問題。"},{"en":"To ask any questions means to raise anything unclear or uncertain.","zh":"ask any questions 指提出任何不清楚或不確定的地方。"},{"en":"A student should ask any questions before submitting a complicated homework task.","zh":"學生提交複雜功課前，應提出任何問題。"},{"en":"Asking questions prevents mistakes when instructions are new or confusing.","zh":"當指示新或令人困惑時，提問可以避免錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase gives permission for the listener to check details freely.","zh":"這個短語表示聽者可以自由確認細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"family name","meaning":"姓氏","examples":[{"en":"Breda asks Dan for his family name.","zh":"Breda 問 Dan 的姓氏。"},{"en":"A family name is the surname shared by members of a family.","zh":"family name 指家庭成員共同使用的姓。"},{"en":"On many forms, people write their family name after their first name or in a separate box.","zh":"在許多表格上，人們會在名字後或另一欄寫上姓氏。"},{"en":"Asking for a family name helps organisations identify members correctly.","zh":"詢問姓氏有助組織正確識別會員。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in forms, registration, and official records.","zh":"這個短語常見於表格、登記和正式紀錄。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"take your email address","meaning":"記下你的電郵地址","examples":[{"en":"Breda asks whether she can take Dan’s email address.","zh":"Breda 問是否可以記下 Dan 的電郵地址。"},{"en":"To take your email address means to write down or record your email for future contact.","zh":"take your email address 指寫下或記錄你的電郵，以便日後聯絡。"},{"en":"A school office may take a parent’s email address to send notices.","zh":"學校辦公室可能記下家長的電郵地址，以發送通告。"},{"en":"Taking an email address helps an organisation send updates, forms, or reminders.","zh":"記下電郵地址有助組織發送更新、表格或提醒。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when collecting contact details.","zh":"收集聯絡資料時會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"email address","meaning":"電郵地址","examples":[{"en":"Dan gives Breda his email address.","zh":"Dan 把他的電郵地址告訴 Breda。"},{"en":"An email address is the electronic address people use to send and receive emails.","zh":"email address 指人們用來收發電子郵件的電子地址。"},{"en":"A student needs an email address to receive online class notices.","zh":"學生需要電郵地址來接收網上課堂通知。"},{"en":"If an email address is typed wrongly, important messages may not arrive.","zh":"如果電郵地址輸入錯誤，重要訊息可能收不到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a basic digital contact detail.","zh":"這個短語描述基本數碼聯絡資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"home address","meaning":"住址","examples":[{"en":"Breda asks Dan for his home address.","zh":"Breda 問 Dan 的住址。"},{"en":"A home address is the place where someone lives, including street, number, town, and sometimes postcode.","zh":"home address 指某人居住的地方，包括街道、門牌、市鎮，有時還有郵政編碼。"},{"en":"A club may need a home address to send membership cards or official letters.","zh":"會社可能需要住址來寄會員證或正式信件。"},{"en":"Giving a correct home address prevents mail from being sent to the wrong place.","zh":"提供正確住址可以避免郵件寄錯地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a person’s residential contact detail.","zh":"這個短語描述一個人的住宅聯絡資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ten miles away from","meaning":"距離……十英里","examples":[{"en":"Dan lives about ten miles away from the club.","zh":"Dan 住在距離攝影會大約十英里的地方。"},{"en":"Ten miles away from means the distance between two places is about ten miles.","zh":"ten miles away from 指兩個地方之間相距大約十英里。"},{"en":"A student who lives ten miles away from school may need to take a bus every morning.","zh":"住在距離學校十英里的學生，可能每天早上需要乘巴士。"},{"en":"Distance affects how easy it is to attend meetings regularly.","zh":"距離會影響定期出席會議是否方便。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how far one place is from another.","zh":"解釋兩地相距多遠時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"house number and street","meaning":"門牌號碼及街道","examples":[{"en":"Breda asks for Dan’s house number and street.","zh":"Breda 詢問 Dan 的門牌號碼及街道。"},{"en":"House number and street means the number of the building and the name of the road where someone lives.","zh":"house number and street 指某人住所的樓宇號碼和道路名稱。"},{"en":"A delivery company needs your house number and street to bring a parcel to the right door.","zh":"速遞公司需要你的門牌號碼及街道，才能把包裹送到正確門口。"},{"en":"Missing either the number or street can make an address unclear.","zh":"如果缺少門牌號碼或街道，地址會變得不清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase names the basic parts of a home address.","zh":"這個短語指出住址的基本部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"that’s right","meaning":"沒錯","examples":[{"en":"Dan says, “That’s right,” when Breda checks the spelling.","zh":"Breda 檢查拼寫時，Dan 說：「沒錯。」"},{"en":"That’s right means the information just said is correct.","zh":"that’s right 指剛才說出的資料是正確的。"},{"en":"A student may say “That’s right” when a teacher checks the spelling of her name.","zh":"老師檢查學生姓名拼寫時，學生可能說「沒錯」。"},{"en":"This phrase confirms that the listener has understood or written something accurately.","zh":"這個短語確認聽者已準確理解或記下某事。"},{"en":"It is a simple way to correct or approve information.","zh":"它是確認或認可資料的簡單說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"how did you hear about","meaning":"你是怎樣得知……的","examples":[{"en":"Breda asks how Dan heard about the club.","zh":"Breda 問 Dan 是怎樣得知這個會的。"},{"en":"How did you hear about something? asks where or from whom someone first learned about it.","zh":"How did you hear about something? 用來問某人最初從哪裏或誰那裏知道某事。"},{"en":"A shop may ask customers how they heard about a sale.","zh":"商店可能問顧客是怎樣得知減價活動的。"},{"en":"This question helps organisations know which advertisements or recommendations work.","zh":"這個問題幫助組織知道哪些廣告或推薦有效。"},{"en":"It is common in applications, surveys, and customer forms.","zh":"它常見於申請、問卷和顧客表格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"look on the internet","meaning":"在網上查找","examples":[{"en":"Breda asks whether Dan looked on the internet.","zh":"Breda 問 Dan 是否在網上查找。"},{"en":"To look on the internet means to search online for information.","zh":"look on the internet 指在網上搜尋資料。"},{"en":"A student may look on the internet for opening hours before visiting a museum.","zh":"學生參觀博物館前，可能在網上查找開放時間。"},{"en":"Looking online can quickly provide addresses, reviews, prices, and contact details.","zh":"網上查找可以快速提供地址、評價、價格和聯絡資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using the web to find information.","zh":"這個短語描述使用網絡尋找資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the other day","meaning":"前幾天","examples":[{"en":"Dan was talking to a relative the other day.","zh":"Dan 前幾天與一名親戚談話。"},{"en":"The other day means a few days ago, though the exact date is not important.","zh":"the other day 指幾天前，但確切日期不重要。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “I saw your brother at the library the other day.”","zh":"老師可能說：「我前幾天在圖書館見到你哥哥。」"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when casually mentioning a recent past event.","zh":"輕鬆提到最近過去事件時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It gives a rough time without needing a specific date.","zh":"它給出大約時間，而不需要具體日期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"suggest something","meaning":"建議；推薦某事","examples":[{"en":"A relative suggested the camera club to Dan.","zh":"一名親戚向 Dan 推薦了這個攝影會。"},{"en":"To suggest something means to recommend it as an idea or possible choice.","zh":"suggest something 指把某事作為想法或可能選擇推薦出來。"},{"en":"A friend may suggest a quiet café for studying after school.","zh":"朋友可能建議一間安靜咖啡店，供放學後溫習。"},{"en":"Suggestions can help people discover options they had not considered.","zh":"建議可以幫助人發現自己未曾考慮的選項。"},{"en":"This verb is used when someone offers an idea, not an order.","zh":"這個動詞用於某人提出想法，而不是下命令。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be a member","meaning":"是會員","examples":[{"en":"Breda asks whether Dan’s relative is a member too.","zh":"Breda 問 Dan 的親戚是否也是會員。"},{"en":"Be a member means belong officially to a club, group, or organisation.","zh":"be a member 指正式屬於某學會、團體或組織。"},{"en":"A student may be a member of the school music society.","zh":"學生可能是學校音樂學會的會員。"},{"en":"Members usually receive certain rights, news, or chances to join activities.","zh":"會員通常會得到某些權利、消息或參加活動的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal belonging.","zh":"這個短語描述正式歸屬。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"belong to","meaning":"屬於；是……的成員","examples":[{"en":"Dan’s relative belongs to another club.","zh":"Dan 的親戚屬於另一個會。"},{"en":"Belong to a club means be a member of that club.","zh":"belong to a club 指是該會的會員。"},{"en":"A photographer may belong to a local art group as well as a camera club.","zh":"攝影師除了加入攝影會，也可能是本地藝術小組的成員。"},{"en":"Belonging to a group can give people community, support, and shared interests.","zh":"屬於某團體可以給人社群、支援和共同興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes membership or connection.","zh":"這個短語描述會員身份或連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hear good things about","meaning":"聽聞……很不錯","examples":[{"en":"Dan’s relative had heard good things about Wayside Camera Club.","zh":"Dan 的親戚聽聞 Wayside 攝影會很不錯。"},{"en":"To hear good things about something means to receive positive comments or reports about it.","zh":"hear good things about something 指聽到關於某事的正面評價或消息。"},{"en":"A parent may hear good things about a school from other families.","zh":"家長可能從其他家庭聽聞某學校很不錯。"},{"en":"Positive recommendations can make people more willing to try a club or service.","zh":"正面推薦可以令人更願意嘗試某個會或服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reputation passed through word of mouth.","zh":"這個短語描述透過口碑傳出的聲譽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hope to get from","meaning":"希望從……得到","examples":[{"en":"Breda asks what Dan hopes to get from joining.","zh":"Breda 問 Dan 希望從加入中得到甚麼。"},{"en":"Hope to get from something means want to gain a benefit, experience, or result from it.","zh":"hope to get from something 指希望從某事中獲得好處、經驗或結果。"},{"en":"A student may hope to get confidence from joining a speaking club.","zh":"學生可能希望從加入演講學會中得到信心。"},{"en":"Knowing what someone hopes to get helps a club support that person better.","zh":"知道某人希望得到甚麼，有助學會更好支援那人。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about a person’s goal or expectation.","zh":"這個短語詢問一個人的目標或期望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"one thing that really interests me","meaning":"真正令我感興趣的一件事","examples":[{"en":"One thing that really interests Dan is the competitions.","zh":"真正令 Dan 感興趣的一件事是比賽。"},{"en":"One thing that really interests me means one particular part strongly attracts my attention.","zh":"one thing that really interests me 指某一個部分特別吸引我的注意。"},{"en":"A student may say, “One thing that really interests me about science is experiments.”","zh":"學生可能說：「科學真正令我感興趣的一件事是實驗。」"},{"en":"This phrase helps a speaker identify their main area of interest.","zh":"這個短語幫助說話者指出自己的主要興趣範疇。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why you want to join something.","zh":"解釋為何想加入某事時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"competitions","meaning":"比賽","examples":[{"en":"Dan is interested in the club’s competitions.","zh":"Dan 對攝影會的比賽感興趣。"},{"en":"Competitions are events where people enter and try to win by showing skill or quality.","zh":"competitions 指人們參加並透過展示技能或質素爭取勝出的活動。"},{"en":"A school may hold photography competitions for students during arts week.","zh":"學校可能在藝術週為學生舉辦攝影比賽。"},{"en":"Competitions can motivate people to practise and improve.","zh":"比賽可以激勵人練習和進步。"},{"en":"This word describes organised contests with winners or judging.","zh":"這個字描述有勝出者或評審的有組織競賽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"enjoy entering","meaning":"喜歡參加","examples":[{"en":"Dan enjoys entering photography competitions.","zh":"Dan 喜歡參加攝影比賽。"},{"en":"Enjoy entering means like taking part in competitions or events.","zh":"enjoy entering 指喜歡參加比賽或活動。"},{"en":"A student may enjoy entering writing contests because they provide a clear goal.","zh":"學生可能喜歡參加寫作比賽，因為它們提供清楚目標。"},{"en":"If someone enjoys entering competitions, they may practise more regularly.","zh":"如果某人喜歡參加比賽，他可能更定期練習。"},{"en":"This phrase connects enjoyment with participation.","zh":"這個短語把享受與參與連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"socialise with","meaning":"與……交誼；交流","examples":[{"en":"Dan likes to socialise with other photographers.","zh":"Dan 喜歡與其他攝影師交流。"},{"en":"To socialise with people means to spend time with them in a friendly way.","zh":"socialise with people 指以友善方式與人相處和交流。"},{"en":"New students may socialise with classmates during lunch to make friends.","zh":"新學生可能在午飯時與同學交流，以結交朋友。"},{"en":"Socialising with people who share your interest can make learning more enjoyable.","zh":"與有共同興趣的人交流，可以令學習更愉快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes friendly interaction, not formal work only.","zh":"這個短語描述友善互動，而不只是正式工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"other photographers","meaning":"其他攝影師","examples":[{"en":"Dan wants to socialise with other photographers.","zh":"Dan 想與其他攝影師交流。"},{"en":"Other photographers are people besides Dan who also take photographs, either as a hobby or professionally.","zh":"other photographers 指 Dan 以外也拍攝照片的人，可以是興趣或專業。"},{"en":"A beginner can learn camera settings by talking to other photographers.","zh":"初學者可以透過與其他攝影師交談來學習相機設定。"},{"en":"Meeting other photographers can lead to advice, friendship, and new ideas.","zh":"認識其他攝影師可以帶來建議、友誼和新想法。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people who share the same activity.","zh":"這個短語指共享同一活動的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"type of membership","meaning":"會員類別","examples":[{"en":"Breda asks what type of membership Dan would like.","zh":"Breda 問 Dan 想要哪種會員類別。"},{"en":"Type of membership means the category of membership a person can choose.","zh":"type of membership 指一個人可以選擇的會員分類。"},{"en":"A gym may offer different types of membership, such as student, full, or family plans.","zh":"健身室可能提供不同會員類別，例如學生、正式或家庭計劃。"},{"en":"Different membership types may have different fees, rights, and benefits.","zh":"不同會員類別可能有不同費用、權利和福利。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a club has more than one joining option.","zh":"當會所有多於一種加入選項時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what are the options","meaning":"有甚麼選擇","examples":[{"en":"Dan asks Breda what the membership options are.","zh":"Dan 問 Breda 會員選項有甚麼。"},{"en":"What are the options? asks what choices are available.","zh":"What are the options? 用來詢問有哪些可用選擇。"},{"en":"A student may ask, “What are the options?” before choosing after-school activities.","zh":"學生選擇課外活動前，可能問：「有甚麼選擇？」"},{"en":"Knowing the options helps people compare price, time, and benefits.","zh":"知道選項有助人比較價格、時間和好處。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when making a decision.","zh":"作決定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"full membership","meaning":"正式會員","examples":[{"en":"Full membership costs £30 a year.","zh":"正式會員每年費用為30英鎊。"},{"en":"Full membership is the complete membership level, usually with all main rights and benefits.","zh":"full membership 指完整會員級別，通常包括所有主要權利和福利。"},{"en":"A full member of a club may attend events, enter competitions, and vote in meetings.","zh":"會所正式會員可以參加活動、參加比賽，並在會議中投票。"},{"en":"Full membership often costs more because it gives wider access.","zh":"正式會員通常較貴，因為它提供更廣泛使用權。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with cheaper or limited membership types.","zh":"這個短語與較便宜或有限制的會員類別形成對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"associate membership","meaning":"準會員","examples":[{"en":"Associate membership costs £20 a year.","zh":"準會員每年費用為20英鎊。"},{"en":"Associate membership is a limited membership level with fewer rights than full membership.","zh":"associate membership 指有限會員級別，權利比正式會員少。"},{"en":"An associate member may join activities but may not be able to vote.","zh":"準會員可以參加活動，但可能不能投票。"},{"en":"This type can be cheaper because it offers fewer benefits.","zh":"這類會員可能較便宜，因為福利較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a partial or lower-level membership.","zh":"這個短語描述部分或較低級別的會員資格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"go for","meaning":"選擇","examples":[{"en":"Dan decides to go for the full membership.","zh":"Dan 決定選擇正式會員。"},{"en":"To go for something means to choose it from the available options.","zh":"go for something 指從可用選項中選擇某物。"},{"en":"A student may go for the cheaper lunch set if she wants to save money.","zh":"如果學生想省錢，可能選擇較便宜的午餐套餐。"},{"en":"People often go for the option that best matches their needs and budget.","zh":"人們通常會選擇最符合需要和預算的選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and common in everyday decisions.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常見於日常決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"vote in meetings","meaning":"在會議中投票","examples":[{"en":"Associate members cannot vote in meetings.","zh":"準會員不能在會議中投票。"},{"en":"To vote in meetings means to formally choose or decide something during a meeting.","zh":"vote in meetings 指在會議中正式選擇或決定某事。"},{"en":"Club members may vote in meetings to choose the next chairperson.","zh":"會所會員可能在會議中投票選出下一任主席。"},{"en":"Voting gives members a say in how the organisation is run.","zh":"投票讓會員對組織如何運作有發言權。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal decision-making right.","zh":"這個短語描述正式決策權利。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"find out a bit more about","meaning":"多了解……一點","examples":[{"en":"Breda wants to find out a bit more about Dan.","zh":"Breda 想多了解 Dan 一點。"},{"en":"To find out a bit more about someone means to learn some additional information about them.","zh":"find out a bit more about someone 指多知道一些關於某人的資料。"},{"en":"A teacher may find out a bit more about a new student before choosing a suitable reading book.","zh":"老師可能先多了解新學生一點，再選合適閱讀書。"},{"en":"Extra information helps people give better advice or support.","zh":"額外資料有助人給出更好建議或支援。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds friendly and not too formal.","zh":"這個短語聽起來友善而不太正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"compete","meaning":"參賽","examples":[{"en":"Dan wants to compete in photography competitions.","zh":"Dan 想參加攝影比賽。"},{"en":"To compete means to take part in a contest and try to do better than others.","zh":"compete 指參加比賽並嘗試比別人表現更好。"},{"en":"A student may compete in a spelling contest after months of practice.","zh":"學生經過數月練習後，可能參加串字比賽。"},{"en":"Competing can motivate people to improve their skills.","zh":"參賽可以激勵人提升技能。"},{"en":"This verb describes entering a contest with the aim of doing well.","zh":"這個動詞描述以表現良好為目標參加競賽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"win a photography competition","meaning":"贏得攝影比賽","examples":[{"en":"Dan has not yet won any photography competitions.","zh":"Dan 還未贏得任何攝影比賽。"},{"en":"To win a photography competition means to have your photo judged as the best or one of the best.","zh":"win a photography competition 指你的照片被評為最佳或其中最佳。"},{"en":"A student may win a photography competition with a clear and emotional picture of school life.","zh":"學生可能憑一張清晰而有情感的校園生活照片贏得攝影比賽。"},{"en":"Winning can give photographers confidence and recognition.","zh":"勝出可以給攝影師信心和認可。"},{"en":"This phrase describes success in a judged photo contest.","zh":"這個短語描述在評審攝影比賽中的成功。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not yet","meaning":"還未","examples":[{"en":"Dan has not won any competitions yet.","zh":"Dan 還未贏得任何比賽。"},{"en":"Not yet means something has not happened up to now, but it may happen later.","zh":"not yet 指某事到目前為止尚未發生，但之後可能會發生。"},{"en":"A student may say, “I haven’t finished the essay yet,” because she is still working on it.","zh":"學生可能說：「我還未完成文章」，因為她仍在寫。"},{"en":"This phrase keeps the possibility open for the future.","zh":"這個短語保留未來可能性。"},{"en":"It is different from “never”, which sounds more final.","zh":"它與 “never” 不同，因為 “never” 聽起來更像永不發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"enter competitions","meaning":"參加比賽","examples":[{"en":"Dan has entered three photography competitions in the past.","zh":"Dan 過去參加過三個攝影比賽。"},{"en":"To enter competitions means to officially take part in them.","zh":"enter competitions 指正式參與比賽。"},{"en":"A school athlete may enter competitions to test her speed against other runners.","zh":"學校運動員可能參加比賽，測試自己與其他跑手相比的速度。"},{"en":"Entering competitions gives people experience even if they do not win.","zh":"參加比賽即使沒有勝出，也能給人經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes participation in contests.","zh":"這個短語描述參與競賽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"過去","examples":[{"en":"Dan has entered three competitions in the past.","zh":"Dan 過去參加過三個比賽。"},{"en":"In the past means before now or in earlier times.","zh":"in the past 指在現在之前或較早時期。"},{"en":"A student may say she has joined debate competitions in the past.","zh":"學生可能說她過去參加過辯論比賽。"},{"en":"Past experience can help explain someone’s current interests or skills.","zh":"過去經驗可以解釋某人現在的興趣或技能。"},{"en":"This phrase places events before the present.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在現在之前。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tell me something about","meaning":"告訴我一些關於……的事","examples":[{"en":"Breda asks Dan to tell her something about the competitions.","zh":"Breda 請 Dan 告訴她一些關於比賽的事。"},{"en":"Tell me something about means give me some information or details about a topic.","zh":"tell me something about 指給我一些關於某題目的資料或細節。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask, “Tell me something about the book you read.”","zh":"老師可能問：「告訴我一些關於你讀過那本書的事。」"},{"en":"This phrase invites the speaker to explain without needing every detail.","zh":"這個短語邀請說話者解釋，但不需要每個細節。"},{"en":"It is useful in interviews and friendly conversations.","zh":"它適合用於面試和友善對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"start with","meaning":"由……開始","examples":[{"en":"Breda suggests starting with the first competition.","zh":"Breda 建議由第一個比賽開始。"},{"en":"To start with something means to begin a discussion or process using that item first.","zh":"start with something 指用某項目作為討論或過程的第一步。"},{"en":"A teacher may start with easy questions before moving to harder ones.","zh":"老師可能由簡單問題開始，再轉到較難問題。"},{"en":"Starting with the first event helps keep the story in order.","zh":"由第一件事開始有助故事保持次序。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for organising information step by step.","zh":"這個短語適合逐步組織資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the theme was entitled","meaning":"主題名為","examples":[{"en":"The theme of the first competition was entitled “Domestic Life”.","zh":"第一個比賽的主題名為「家庭生活」。"},{"en":"The theme was entitled means the topic was given a particular title or name.","zh":"the theme was entitled 指主題被賦予某個特定標題或名稱。"},{"en":"A writing contest may have a theme entitled “A Better Future”.","zh":"寫作比賽的主題可能名為「更美好的未來」。"},{"en":"A clear theme title tells participants what their work should focus on.","zh":"清楚的主題標題告訴參賽者作品應聚焦於甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in competitions or exhibitions.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常見於比賽或展覽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"domestic life","meaning":"家庭生活","examples":[{"en":"The first photography competition was about domestic life.","zh":"第一個攝影比賽是關於家庭生活。"},{"en":"Domestic life means everyday life at home, including family routines, meals, chores, and relationships.","zh":"domestic life 指家中的日常生活，包括家庭習慣、用餐、家務和關係。"},{"en":"A photo of children doing homework at the kitchen table can show domestic life.","zh":"孩子在廚房餐桌做功課的照片可以展示家庭生活。"},{"en":"Domestic life can look ordinary, but it often reveals emotion and family habits.","zh":"家庭生活可能看似平凡，但常揭示情感和家庭習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on home and family settings.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於家居和家庭場景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The photograph had to be related to the home.","zh":"照片必須與家居有關。"},{"en":"Be related to something means have a clear connection with it.","zh":"be related to something 指與某事有清楚連繫。"},{"en":"A school poster competition may require pictures related to environmental protection.","zh":"學校海報比賽可能要求圖片與環境保護有關。"},{"en":"If a photo is not related to the theme, judges may mark it lower.","zh":"如果照片與主題無關，評判可能給較低分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes connection between an idea and a topic.","zh":"這個短語描述想法與題目之間的連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"choose to","meaning":"選擇去……","examples":[{"en":"Dan chose to take a photo of a family having a meal.","zh":"Dan 選擇去拍攝一家人吃飯的照片。"},{"en":"Choose to do something means decide to do it instead of other possible actions.","zh":"choose to do something 指決定做某事，而不是做其他可能行動。"},{"en":"A student may choose to write about friendship rather than family in an essay.","zh":"學生可能選擇在文章中寫友誼，而不是家庭。"},{"en":"Choosing one option means leaving other options behind.","zh":"選擇一個選項意味著放棄其他選項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a deliberate decision.","zh":"這個短語描述有意識的決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take a photo of","meaning":"拍攝……的照片","examples":[{"en":"Dan took a photo of a family round the dinner table.","zh":"Dan 拍攝了一家人圍坐餐桌的照片。"},{"en":"To take a photo of something means to use a camera to capture its image.","zh":"take a photo of something 指用相機捕捉某物的影像。"},{"en":"A student may take a photo of a science project before taking it apart.","zh":"學生可能在拆除科學項目前，先拍攝它的照片。"},{"en":"Taking a photo preserves a moment that may quickly pass.","zh":"拍照可以保存一個很快會過去的時刻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the basic action of photography.","zh":"這個短語描述攝影的基本動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sitting round","meaning":"圍坐在……旁","examples":[{"en":"Dan photographed a family sitting round the dinner table.","zh":"Dan 拍攝了一家人圍坐在餐桌旁。"},{"en":"Sitting round something means sitting around it in a circle or group.","zh":"sitting round something 指圍着某物坐成一圈或一組。"},{"en":"Children may sit round a teacher during story time.","zh":"故事時間時，小朋友可能圍坐在老師旁。"},{"en":"People sitting round a table often look connected because they share the same space.","zh":"圍坐在桌旁的人常看起來有連繫，因為他們共享同一空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arrangement and closeness.","zh":"這個短語描述座位安排和親近感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dinner table","meaning":"餐桌","examples":[{"en":"The family were sitting round the dinner table.","zh":"那家人圍坐在餐桌旁。"},{"en":"A dinner table is the table where people usually eat their main meal.","zh":"dinner table 指人們通常吃正餐的桌子。"},{"en":"A family may talk about their day around the dinner table.","zh":"一家人可能圍着餐桌談論自己的一天。"},{"en":"The dinner table can show family habits, relationships, and daily routines.","zh":"餐桌可以展示家庭習慣、關係和日常規律。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to both a piece of furniture and a family setting.","zh":"這個短語既指一件家具，也指家庭場景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have a meal","meaning":"吃飯","examples":[{"en":"The family were having a meal in Dan’s photo.","zh":"在 Dan 的照片中，那家人正在吃飯。"},{"en":"To have a meal means to eat breakfast, lunch, dinner, or another main eating occasion.","zh":"have a meal 指吃早餐、午餐、晚餐或其他主要餐點。"},{"en":"Students may have a meal together after a school competition.","zh":"學生可能在學校比賽後一起吃飯。"},{"en":"Having a meal together can show friendship, family life, or celebration.","zh":"一起吃飯可以展示友誼、家庭生活或慶祝。"},{"en":"This phrase describes eating as a shared activity.","zh":"這個短語描述作為共同活動的進食。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get some feedback","meaning":"得到一些意見","examples":[{"en":"Dan did not win, but he got some feedback.","zh":"Dan 沒有勝出，但得到了一些意見。"},{"en":"To get some feedback means to receive comments that explain what was good and what could improve.","zh":"get some feedback 指收到解釋甚麼做得好、甚麼可改善的評語。"},{"en":"A student may get feedback from a teacher after giving a presentation.","zh":"學生做完簡報後，可能從老師得到一些意見。"},{"en":"Feedback helps people learn from mistakes even when they do not win.","zh":"意見可以幫助人從錯誤中學習，即使沒有勝出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving advice for improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述收到改善建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"judges","meaning":"評判","examples":[{"en":"The judges said Dan’s picture was too busy.","zh":"評判說 Dan 的照片畫面太雜亂。"},{"en":"Judges are people who decide the winners or give marks in a competition.","zh":"judges 指在比賽中決定勝出者或給分的人。"},{"en":"In a school art contest, judges may look at creativity, skill, and message.","zh":"在學校藝術比賽中，評判可能看創意、技巧和訊息。"},{"en":"Judges’ comments can help participants understand how their work was evaluated.","zh":"評判的評語可以幫助參賽者了解作品如何被評估。"},{"en":"This word describes people with decision-making authority in a contest.","zh":"這個字描述在比賽中有決策權的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"too busy as a picture","meaning":"作為照片來說畫面太雜亂","examples":[{"en":"The judges said Dan’s photograph was too busy as a picture.","zh":"評判說 Dan 的照片作為照片來說畫面太雜亂。"},{"en":"Too busy as a picture means there are too many things in the image, making it hard to focus.","zh":"too busy as a picture 指影像中有太多東西，令人難以集中焦點。"},{"en":"A photo of a desk covered with books, cups, wires, and toys may look too busy.","zh":"一張滿是書、杯、電線和玩具的書桌照片，可能看起來太雜亂。"},{"en":"A busy image can confuse viewers because they do not know where to look first.","zh":"畫面太雜亂會令觀眾困惑，因為不知道先看哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing visual composition.","zh":"這個短語常見於討論視覺構圖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"composition of the picture","meaning":"照片構圖","examples":[{"en":"The judges criticised the composition of the picture.","zh":"評判批評照片構圖。"},{"en":"The composition of a picture is the way people, objects, light, and space are arranged in it.","zh":"composition of a picture 指照片中人物、物件、光線和空間的安排方式。"},{"en":"A photo has good composition if the main subject is clear and the background is not distracting.","zh":"如果照片主體清晰，背景不令人分心，構圖就好。"},{"en":"Poor composition can make even an interesting subject look weak.","zh":"差劣構圖會令即使有趣的題材也顯得薄弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the visual structure of an image.","zh":"這個短語描述影像的視覺結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"criticise","meaning":"批評","examples":[{"en":"The judges criticised the composition of Dan’s photograph.","zh":"評判批評 Dan 的照片構圖。"},{"en":"To criticise means to point out problems or weaknesses in something.","zh":"criticise 指指出某事的問題或弱點。"},{"en":"A teacher may criticise an essay if the argument is unclear.","zh":"如果文章論點不清，老師可能會批評它。"},{"en":"Criticism can feel uncomfortable, but it can also help people improve.","zh":"批評可能令人不舒服，但也能幫助人進步。"},{"en":"This verb does not always mean being cruel; it can mean giving serious judgement.","zh":"這個動詞不一定代表刻薄；它可以指給出認真評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"see my mistake","meaning":"看出自己的錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Once the judges told him, Dan could see his mistake.","zh":"評判告訴他後，Dan 就能看出自己的錯誤。"},{"en":"To see my mistake means to understand what I did wrong after it is explained or noticed.","zh":"see my mistake 指在被解釋或注意後，明白自己做錯了甚麼。"},{"en":"A student may see her mistake after a teacher shows why the answer is wrong.","zh":"老師指出答案為何錯後，學生可能看出自己的錯誤。"},{"en":"Seeing a mistake clearly is the first step to improving.","zh":"清楚看出錯誤是改進的第一步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes understanding an error, not literally seeing it with the eyes.","zh":"這個短語描述理解錯誤，而不是字面用眼睛看見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the theme of","meaning":"……的主題","examples":[{"en":"Breda asks about the theme of the second competition.","zh":"Breda 問第二個比賽的主題。"},{"en":"The theme of something is the main topic, idea, or subject it focuses on.","zh":"theme of something 指某事聚焦的主要題目、想法或主題。"},{"en":"The theme of a school poster competition may be road safety.","zh":"學校海報比賽的主題可能是道路安全。"},{"en":"Knowing the theme helps participants decide what kind of work to create.","zh":"知道主題有助參賽者決定創作哪類作品。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in competitions, essays, exhibitions, and stories.","zh":"這個短語常見於比賽、文章、展覽和故事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on the coast","meaning":"在海邊","examples":[{"en":"Dan’s university was on the coast.","zh":"Dan 的大學在海邊。"},{"en":"On the coast means located near the sea or along the edge of the land beside the sea.","zh":"on the coast 指位於海附近，或沿着海邊陸地邊緣。"},{"en":"A town on the coast may have beaches, boats, and sea views.","zh":"海邊城鎮可能有沙灘、船隻和海景。"},{"en":"Coastal places often provide good chances to photograph sunsets and waves.","zh":"海岸地方常提供拍攝日落和海浪的好機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a seaside location.","zh":"這個短語描述海邊位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"beautiful sunsets","meaning":"美麗日落","examples":[{"en":"The coastal area gets a lot of beautiful sunsets.","zh":"這個海岸地區有很多美麗日落。"},{"en":"Beautiful sunsets are colourful evening views when the sun goes down.","zh":"beautiful sunsets 指太陽下山時色彩漂亮的黃昏景色。"},{"en":"A photographer may wait by the beach to capture beautiful sunsets.","zh":"攝影師可能在海灘等待拍攝美麗日落。"},{"en":"Clouds, sea, and changing light can make sunsets more dramatic.","zh":"雲、海和變化中的光線可以令日落更有戲劇感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an attractive natural scene.","zh":"這個短語描述吸引人的自然景象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"instructions were to","meaning":"指示是要……","examples":[{"en":"The instructions were to capture the clouds as well.","zh":"指示是也要拍下雲朵。"},{"en":"The instructions were to means the rules or directions told participants what they had to do.","zh":"instructions were to 指規則或指引告訴參與者必須做甚麼。"},{"en":"In an exam, the instructions may be to answer only two questions.","zh":"在考試中，指示可能是只回答兩條問題。"},{"en":"Following instructions is important because judges or teachers check whether the task was done properly.","zh":"跟從指示很重要，因為評判或老師會檢查任務是否正確完成。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces required actions.","zh":"這個短語引出必要行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"capture the clouds","meaning":"拍下雲朵","examples":[{"en":"Dan had to capture the clouds in his sunset photograph.","zh":"Dan 必須在日落照片中拍下雲朵。"},{"en":"To capture the clouds means to photograph the clouds clearly as part of the image.","zh":"capture the clouds 指把雲朵清楚地拍攝成影像的一部分。"},{"en":"A photographer may capture the clouds to show movement, colour, and depth in the sky.","zh":"攝影師可能拍下雲朵，以展示天空中的動感、色彩和深度。"},{"en":"Including clouds can make a sunset photo more interesting than just a plain sky.","zh":"加入雲朵可以令日落照片比單純天空更有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase uses “capture” to mean record with a camera.","zh":"這個短語中的 “capture” 指用相機記錄。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"blue sky","meaning":"藍天","examples":[{"en":"The photograph could not just show blue sky and a setting sun.","zh":"照片不能只顯示藍天和夕陽。"},{"en":"Blue sky means a clear sky with little or no cloud.","zh":"blue sky 指清澈、很少或沒有雲的天空。"},{"en":"A photo with only blue sky may look empty if there is no subject or pattern.","zh":"如果沒有主體或圖案，只有藍天的照片可能看起來空洞。"},{"en":"In photography, too much plain blue sky can make the picture less interesting.","zh":"在攝影中，太多單調藍天會令照片較不有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple weather and visual condition.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單天氣和視覺狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"setting sun","meaning":"夕陽","examples":[{"en":"The photograph had to include more than a setting sun.","zh":"照片必須包括比夕陽更多的元素。"},{"en":"The setting sun is the sun as it goes down in the evening.","zh":"setting sun 指傍晚正在落下的太陽。"},{"en":"A setting sun can create warm orange light over buildings or the sea.","zh":"夕陽可以在建築物或海面上製造溫暖橙光。"},{"en":"A photo of only the setting sun may need clouds, people, or landscape to add interest.","zh":"只有夕陽的照片可能需要雲、人或風景來增加趣味。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the sun during sunset.","zh":"這個短語描述日落時的太陽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"give you all those","meaning":"帶來那些……","examples":[{"en":"The clouds give you all those amazing pinks and purples.","zh":"雲朵會帶來那些迷人的粉紅色和紫色。"},{"en":"Give you all those means produce or provide many of the things just mentioned.","zh":"give you all those 指產生或提供剛才提到的許多東西。"},{"en":"A good market gives you all those fresh smells, bright colours, and lively sounds.","zh":"好街市會帶來那些新鮮氣味、鮮艷色彩和熱鬧聲音。"},{"en":"In a sunset, clouds can create many colours that a clear sky cannot provide.","zh":"在日落中，雲朵可以創造清澈天空不能提供的多種色彩。"},{"en":"This phrase is conversational and points to a rich visual effect.","zh":"這個短語較口語，指向豐富視覺效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"amazing pinks and purples","meaning":"迷人的粉紅色和紫色","examples":[{"en":"The clouds created amazing pinks and purples in the sky.","zh":"雲朵在天空中創造出迷人的粉紅色和紫色。"},{"en":"Amazing pinks and purples are striking shades of pink and purple that look beautiful or surprising.","zh":"amazing pinks and purples 指看起來美麗或令人驚喜的粉紅和紫色色調。"},{"en":"A sunset after rain may produce amazing pinks and purples above the city.","zh":"雨後日落可能在城市上空產生迷人的粉紅色和紫色。"},{"en":"Strong colours can make a photo more dramatic and memorable.","zh":"強烈色彩可以令照片更有戲劇感和記憶點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes vivid colour in a visual scene.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺場景中的鮮明色彩。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"feedback was that","meaning":"意見是……","examples":[{"en":"The feedback was that Dan should have waited longer.","zh":"意見是 Dan 應該等久一點。"},{"en":"Feedback was that means the advice or comment given was a particular point.","zh":"feedback was that 指得到的建議或評語是某個特定重點。"},{"en":"The feedback was that the essay needed clearer examples.","zh":"意見是文章需要更清楚例子。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the main message from judges, teachers, or reviewers.","zh":"這個短語引出評判、老師或評論者的主要訊息。"},{"en":"It is useful when reporting someone else’s comments.","zh":"報告別人的評語時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"wait a bit longer","meaning":"再等久一點","examples":[{"en":"Dan should have waited a bit longer before taking the photo.","zh":"Dan 拍照前應該再等久一點。"},{"en":"To wait a bit longer means to delay for a little more time.","zh":"wait a bit longer 指多等一小段時間。"},{"en":"A photographer may wait a bit longer for the street to become less crowded.","zh":"攝影師可能再等久一點，讓街道沒那麼擠迫。"},{"en":"Waiting can improve a photo if the light, action, or expression changes.","zh":"如果光線、動作或表情會改變，等待可以改善照片。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests patience can lead to a better result.","zh":"這個短語暗示耐性可以帶來更好結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get the shot","meaning":"拍到那張照片","examples":[{"en":"Dan should have waited longer to get the shot.","zh":"Dan 應該等久一點，才拍到那張照片。"},{"en":"To get the shot means to successfully take the photograph you wanted.","zh":"get the shot 指成功拍到自己想要的照片。"},{"en":"A sports photographer may wait near the goal to get the shot of a winning moment.","zh":"體育攝影師可能在球門附近等待，拍到勝利一刻的照片。"},{"en":"Good timing often helps photographers get the shot they need.","zh":"好時機常幫助攝影師拍到需要的照片。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in photography and filming.","zh":"這個短語常見於攝影和拍片。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the timing was not right","meaning":"時機不對","examples":[{"en":"Breda says the timing was not right.","zh":"Breda 說時機不對。"},{"en":"The timing was not right means the action happened too early, too late, or at the wrong moment.","zh":"timing was not right 指行動太早、太遲或在錯誤時刻發生。"},{"en":"A student may answer too soon in a debate if the timing is not right.","zh":"如果時機不對，學生在辯論中可能太早回答。"},{"en":"In photography, poor timing can make someone miss the best light or expression.","zh":"在攝影中，時機差會令人錯過最佳光線或表情。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a good idea did not work well.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何好想法沒有做好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take it too soon","meaning":"太早拍攝","examples":[{"en":"Dan took the sunset photograph too soon.","zh":"Dan 太早拍攝那張日落照片。"},{"en":"To take it too soon means to take the photo before the best moment has arrived.","zh":"take it too soon 指在最佳時刻到來前拍照。"},{"en":"A photographer may take a group photo too soon before everyone is smiling.","zh":"攝影師可能在大家還未笑時太早拍攝大合照。"},{"en":"Taking a photo too soon can miss better light, colour, or movement.","zh":"太早拍照可能錯過更好的光線、色彩或動作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a timing mistake.","zh":"這個短語描述時間掌握錯誤。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the third competition I entered","meaning":"我參加的第三個比賽","examples":[{"en":"The third competition Dan entered was called “Animal Magic”.","zh":"Dan 參加的第三個比賽名為「Animal Magic」。"},{"en":"The third competition I entered means the third contest I took part in.","zh":"the third competition I entered 指我參與的第三個競賽。"},{"en":"A student may say, “The third competition I entered was a poetry contest.”","zh":"學生可能說：「我參加的第三個比賽是一個詩歌比賽。」"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise past events in order.","zh":"這個短語幫助按次序組織過去事件。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing experience step by step.","zh":"逐步描述經驗時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"difficult subject","meaning":"困難的題材","examples":[{"en":"Breda says animals are a difficult subject for photography.","zh":"Breda 說動物是攝影中困難的題材。"},{"en":"A difficult subject is something hard to photograph, study, draw, or discuss well.","zh":"difficult subject 指難以拍攝、研究、繪畫或討論得好的題材。"},{"en":"Small children can be a difficult subject because they move and change expression quickly.","zh":"小朋友可能是困難的題材，因為他們很快移動和改變表情。"},{"en":"A difficult subject requires patience, planning, and many attempts.","zh":"困難題材需要耐性、計劃和多次嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a topic or object that is challenging to handle.","zh":"這個短語描述難以處理的題目或對象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take hundreds of shots","meaning":"拍數百張照片","examples":[{"en":"Dan had to take hundreds of shots for the animal competition.","zh":"Dan 為動物比賽不得不拍數百張照片。"},{"en":"To take hundreds of shots means to take a very large number of photos.","zh":"take hundreds of shots 指拍攝非常大量照片。"},{"en":"A wildlife photographer may take hundreds of shots to get one sharp picture of a bird.","zh":"野生動物攝影師可能拍數百張照片，才得到一張清晰鳥類照片。"},{"en":"Taking many shots increases the chance of capturing the right moment.","zh":"拍很多張照片會增加捕捉正確時刻的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase shows repeated effort in photography.","zh":"這個短語顯示攝影中的反覆努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"move all the time","meaning":"一直移動","examples":[{"en":"Animals move all the time, so they are difficult to photograph.","zh":"動物一直移動，所以很難拍攝。"},{"en":"Move all the time means keep changing position or direction without staying still.","zh":"move all the time 指不停改變位置或方向，不會靜止不動。"},{"en":"Toddlers move all the time, so parents often struggle to take clear photos of them.","zh":"幼兒一直移動，所以家長常難以拍到清晰照片。"},{"en":"Constant movement can make photos blurred or badly framed.","zh":"持續移動會令照片模糊或構圖不佳。"},{"en":"This phrase describes why a subject is hard to capture.","zh":"這個短語描述為何拍攝對象難以捕捉。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"show movement","meaning":"展現動作","examples":[{"en":"The photograph had to show movement in the scene.","zh":"照片必須在畫面中展現動作。"},{"en":"To show movement means to make viewers feel that something is moving in the image.","zh":"show movement 指令觀眾感覺影像中有東西正在移動。"},{"en":"A photo of a runner with blurred legs can show movement.","zh":"一張跑手雙腿模糊的照片可以展現動作。"},{"en":"Showing movement can make a still photo feel energetic and alive.","zh":"展現動作可以令靜態照片感覺有活力和生命力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visual effect in photography.","zh":"這個短語描述攝影中的視覺效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the scene","meaning":"在畫面中","examples":[{"en":"There had to be some movement in the scene.","zh":"畫面中必須有一些動作。"},{"en":"In the scene means within the picture, setting, or moment being shown.","zh":"in the scene 指在被展示的照片、場景或時刻之內。"},{"en":"In a street photo, movement in the scene may come from people walking or cars passing.","zh":"在街頭照片中，畫面中的動作可能來自行人走路或車輛駛過。"},{"en":"What appears in the scene affects the mood and story of the photograph.","zh":"畫面中出現的東西會影響照片的氣氛和故事。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the visual space inside an image.","zh":"這個短語指影像內的視覺空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get a great shot of","meaning":"拍到一張很好的……照片","examples":[{"en":"Dan got a great shot of a fox in the end.","zh":"Dan 最後拍到一張很好的狐狸照片。"},{"en":"To get a great shot of something means to take a very good photograph of it.","zh":"get a great shot of something 指為某物拍到一張非常好的照片。"},{"en":"A student may get a great shot of the school team celebrating after a win.","zh":"學生可能拍到一張很好的校隊勝利後慶祝照片。"},{"en":"A great shot often depends on timing, light, focus, and composition.","zh":"好照片通常取決於時機、光線、焦點和構圖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes successful photography.","zh":"這個短語描述成功攝影。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the end","meaning":"最後","examples":[{"en":"Dan got a good photo of a fox in the end.","zh":"Dan 最後拍到一張好的狐狸照片。"},{"en":"In the end means finally, after some time, effort, or difficulty.","zh":"in the end 指經過一些時間、努力或困難後，最後。"},{"en":"A student may struggle with a maths problem but solve it in the end.","zh":"學生可能一開始解不到數學題，但最後解決了。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests that the result came after attempts or delays.","zh":"這個短語常暗示結果是在多次嘗試或延誤後出現。"},{"en":"It is useful when telling how something finally turned out.","zh":"說明某事最終如何發展時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take it at night","meaning":"在晚上拍攝","examples":[{"en":"Dan took the photograph of the fox at night.","zh":"Dan 在晚上拍攝那張狐狸照片。"},{"en":"To take it at night means to take the photo during the night-time.","zh":"take it at night 指在夜間拍攝照片。"},{"en":"A photographer may take city photos at night to capture bright lights.","zh":"攝影師可能在晚上拍攝城市照片，以捕捉明亮燈光。"},{"en":"Night photography can be difficult because there is less natural light.","zh":"夜間攝影可能很難，因為自然光較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes when the photo was taken.","zh":"這個短語描述照片拍攝的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"suspect that","meaning":"懷疑；覺得","examples":[{"en":"Dan suspected that the photograph was a bit dark.","zh":"Dan 懷疑那張照片有點暗。"},{"en":"Suspect that means think something is probably true, though you are not completely sure.","zh":"suspect that 指認為某事很可能是真的，但不完全肯定。"},{"en":"A teacher may suspect that a student is tired if he keeps yawning.","zh":"如果學生不停打呵欠，老師可能覺得他很累。"},{"en":"People suspect something when they notice clues but do not have full proof.","zh":"當人們注意到線索但沒有完整證據，就會懷疑某事。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a careful guess.","zh":"這個短語表達謹慎猜測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a bit dark","meaning":"有點暗","examples":[{"en":"The photograph of the fox was a bit dark.","zh":"那張狐狸照片有點暗。"},{"en":"A bit dark means slightly too low in light or brightness.","zh":"a bit dark 指光線或亮度稍微不足。"},{"en":"A classroom photo may be a bit dark if the curtains are closed.","zh":"如果窗簾關上，課室照片可能有點暗。"},{"en":"If a photo is too dark, viewers may not see the subject clearly.","zh":"如果照片太暗，觀眾可能看不清主體。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a mild criticism of lighting.","zh":"這個短語對光線作出溫和批評。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"which is what I was told","meaning":"而這正是我被告知的","examples":[{"en":"Dan thought the photo was dark, which is what he was told.","zh":"Dan 覺得照片很暗，而這正是他被告知的。"},{"en":"Which is what I was told means that this matched the feedback or information someone gave me.","zh":"which is what I was told 指這與別人給我的意見或資料相符。"},{"en":"A student may say, “My essay was too short, which is what I was told by the teacher.”","zh":"學生可能說：「我的文章太短，而這正是老師告訴我的。」"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the speaker’s own opinion agrees with another person’s comment.","zh":"這個短語顯示說話者自己的看法與別人的評語一致。"},{"en":"It is useful when confirming feedback.","zh":"確認回饋時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"seem to be really keen","meaning":"看起來真的很熱衷","examples":[{"en":"Breda says Dan seems to be really keen.","zh":"Breda 說 Dan 看起來真的很熱衷。"},{"en":"Seem to be really keen means appear very interested, enthusiastic, or eager.","zh":"seem to be really keen 指看起來非常感興趣、熱情或渴望參與。"},{"en":"A student who asks many questions about a club seems to be really keen.","zh":"一名學生如果問很多關於學會的問題，就看起來真的很熱衷。"},{"en":"Enthusiasm can make teachers or organisers more confident about accepting someone.","zh":"熱情可以令老師或組織者更有信心接納某人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how someone’s interest appears to others.","zh":"這個短語描述某人的興趣在別人眼中如何呈現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be delighted to have you","meaning":"很高興有你加入","examples":[{"en":"Breda says the club would be delighted to have Dan.","zh":"Breda 說攝影會很高興有 Dan 加入。"},{"en":"Be delighted to have you means be very pleased that you can join or take part.","zh":"be delighted to have you 指非常高興你能加入或參與。"},{"en":"A school team may say, “We’d be delighted to have you with us next season.”","zh":"學校隊伍可能說：「我們很高興下季有你加入。」"},{"en":"This phrase makes the listener feel welcome and valued.","zh":"這個短語令聽者感到受歡迎和被重視。"},{"en":"It is warm, polite, and common when accepting someone into a group.","zh":"它溫暖有禮，常用於接納某人加入小組。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"help with","meaning":"幫助改善……","examples":[{"en":"The club can help Dan with the areas he has outlined.","zh":"攝影會可以幫助 Dan 改善他提到的那些方面。"},{"en":"To help with something means to give support, advice, or practical assistance in that area.","zh":"help with something 指在某方面提供支援、建議或實際協助。"},{"en":"A teacher may help a student with essay structure before an exam.","zh":"老師可能在考試前幫助學生改善文章結構。"},{"en":"Help with a specific weakness can make improvement faster.","zh":"針對特定弱點提供幫助，可以令進步更快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes targeted support.","zh":"這個短語描述有針對性的支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"those areas","meaning":"那些方面","examples":[{"en":"The club can help Dan with those areas of photography.","zh":"攝影會可以幫助 Dan 改善攝影中的那些方面。"},{"en":"Those areas means the particular parts or skills already mentioned.","zh":"those areas 指已經提到的特定部分或技能。"},{"en":"If a student struggles with grammar and pronunciation, a tutor can help with those areas.","zh":"如果學生在文法和發音方面吃力，補習老師可以幫助改善那些方面。"},{"en":"Referring to “those areas” avoids repeating a long list.","zh":"使用 “those areas” 可以避免重複一長串內容。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to topics already discussed.","zh":"這個短語指回已討論的題目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"outline","meaning":"概述；提出","examples":[{"en":"Dan has outlined several areas where he needs help.","zh":"Dan 已概述幾個他需要幫助的方面。"},{"en":"To outline something means to describe the main points without giving every detail.","zh":"outline something 指描述主要重點，而不提供每個細節。"},{"en":"A student may outline her essay plan before writing the full answer.","zh":"學生可能在寫完整答案前先概述文章計劃。"},{"en":"Outlining problems helps others understand what kind of support is needed.","zh":"概述問題有助別人明白需要哪類支援。"},{"en":"This verb is useful when giving a clear but brief summary.","zh":"這個動詞適合用於提供清楚但簡短的總結。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8}],"ielts/listening/Practice 11/task-2":[{"front":"be delighted to welcome","meaning":"很高興歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The presenter is delighted to welcome Dan Beagle.","zh":"主持人很高興歡迎Dan Beagle。"},{"en":"To be delighted to welcome someone means to be very happy to introduce or receive that person.","zh":"be delighted to welcome某人，意思是非常高興介紹或接待該人。"},{"en":"A principal may be delighted to welcome parents to the school open day.","zh":"校長可能很高興歡迎家長來到學校開放日。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase to sound warm, polite and enthusiastic at the start of an event.","zh":"講者在活動開始時使用這個短語，令語氣溫暖、有禮而熱情。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal and cheerful than simply saying “welcome”.","zh":"這個短語比單純說welcome更正式和愉快。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"write a book on","meaning":"寫了一本關於……的書","examples":[{"en":"Dan Beagle has written a book on finding food in the wild.","zh":"Dan Beagle寫了一本關於在野外尋找食物的書。"},{"en":"To write a book on something means to write a book about that subject.","zh":"write a book on某事，意思是寫一本關於該主題的書。"},{"en":"A doctor may write a book on healthy eating for busy families.","zh":"醫生可能寫一本關於忙碌家庭健康飲食的書。"},{"en":"Writing a book on a topic usually suggests the writer has knowledge or experience in it.","zh":"寫一本關於某主題的書，通常暗示作者在該方面有知識或經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing an author’s area of expertise.","zh":"這個短語適合用於介紹作者的專業範疇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look for and find food","meaning":"尋找並找到食物","examples":[{"en":"Dan’s book is about looking for and finding food in the wild.","zh":"Dan的書是關於在野外尋找並找到食物。"},{"en":"To look for and find food means to search for food and successfully discover it.","zh":"look for and find food意思是搜尋食物並成功發現它。"},{"en":"Campers may learn how to look for and find food safely if they are far from shops.","zh":"露營者如果遠離商店，可能要學習如何安全地尋找並找到食物。"},{"en":"Looking for food is not enough; people must also know which foods are safe to eat.","zh":"尋找食物並不足夠；人們也必須知道哪些食物可以安全食用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the search and the successful result.","zh":"這個短語同時描述搜尋和成功結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the wild","meaning":"在野外","examples":[{"en":"Dan writes about finding food in the wild.","zh":"Dan寫的是在野外尋找食物。"},{"en":"In the wild means in natural places where plants and animals live without human control.","zh":"in the wild意思是在植物和動物不受人類控制地生活的自然地方。"},{"en":"Children may see birds in the wild during a countryside walk.","zh":"孩子在郊外散步時，可能在野外看見鳥類。"},{"en":"Food found in the wild can be useful, but it may also be dangerous if wrongly identified.","zh":"在野外找到的食物可以有用，但如果辨認錯誤也可能危險。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts nature with farms, shops or homes.","zh":"這個短語把自然環境與農場、商店或家居作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tell someone everything they need to know about","meaning":"告訴某人關於……需要知道的一切","examples":[{"en":"Dan will tell the audience everything they need to know about picking wild mushrooms.","zh":"Dan會告訴觀眾關於採摘野生蘑菇需要知道的一切。"},{"en":"To tell someone everything they need to know about something means to give the essential information they require.","zh":"tell someone everything they need to know about某事，意思是提供對方所需的基本資訊。"},{"en":"A nurse may tell new parents everything they need to know about caring for a newborn.","zh":"護士可能告訴新手父母關於照顧初生嬰兒需要知道的一切。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the speaker will cover safety, steps, warnings and useful advice.","zh":"這個短語暗示講者會涵蓋安全、步驟、警告和實用建議。"},{"en":"It is often used when introducing a practical guide or talk.","zh":"它常用於介紹實用指南或講座。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pick wild mushrooms","meaning":"採摘野生蘑菇","examples":[{"en":"Dan gives advice on picking wild mushrooms safely.","zh":"Dan就安全採摘野生蘑菇提供建議。"},{"en":"To pick wild mushrooms means to collect mushrooms growing naturally outdoors.","zh":"pick wild mushrooms意思是收集在戶外自然生長的蘑菇。"},{"en":"A beginner should not pick wild mushrooms without someone experienced nearby.","zh":"初學者不應在沒有有經驗人士陪同下採摘野生蘑菇。"},{"en":"Picking the wrong mushroom can be dangerous because some species are poisonous.","zh":"採錯蘑菇可以很危險，因為有些品種有毒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a food-gathering activity that requires careful knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述一項需要仔細知識的採集食物活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"start by talking about","meaning":"先從……談起","examples":[{"en":"Dan needs to start by talking about safety.","zh":"Dan需要先從安全談起。"},{"en":"To start by talking about something means to discuss that topic first.","zh":"start by talking about某事，意思是先討論該主題。"},{"en":"A swimming coach may start by talking about safety before teaching any techniques.","zh":"游泳教練可能先從安全談起，然後才教授技巧。"},{"en":"Speakers often start with the most important warning so listeners do not miss it.","zh":"講者常先講最重要警告，讓聽眾不會錯過。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the first topic in a talk or explanation.","zh":"這個短語顯示講座或解釋中的第一個主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"know what you’re doing","meaning":"知道自己在做甚麼","examples":[{"en":"You really need to know what you’re doing when picking mushrooms.","zh":"採摘蘑菇時，你真的需要知道自己在做甚麼。"},{"en":"To know what you’re doing means to understand the task well enough to do it safely and correctly.","zh":"know what you’re doing意思是足夠了解任務，能安全和正確地完成它。"},{"en":"A person fixing electrical wires must know what they are doing, or they may get hurt.","zh":"修理電線的人必須知道自己在做甚麼，否則可能受傷。"},{"en":"If you do not know what you are doing, a simple outdoor activity can become risky.","zh":"如果你不知道自己在做甚麼，簡單戶外活動也可以變得有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that confidence alone is not enough; skill and knowledge matter.","zh":"這個短語提醒人單靠信心不足夠；技能和知識很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"extremely poisonous","meaning":"有劇毒","examples":[{"en":"Some wild mushrooms are extremely poisonous.","zh":"有些野生蘑菇有劇毒。"},{"en":"Extremely poisonous means very toxic and able to cause serious illness or death.","zh":"extremely poisonous意思是毒性非常強，能造成嚴重疾病或死亡。"},{"en":"A plant can be extremely poisonous even if its berries look bright and attractive.","zh":"植物即使果實鮮艷吸引，也可能有劇毒。"},{"en":"Extremely poisonous substances must be avoided because a small amount may be dangerous.","zh":"有劇毒的物質必須避免，因為少量也可能危險。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strong warning about serious harm.","zh":"這個短語對嚴重傷害作出強烈警告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"having said that","meaning":"話雖如此","examples":[{"en":"Having said that, mushroom picking is worth doing if you know what to look for.","zh":"話雖如此，如果你知道要找甚麼，採摘蘑菇仍值得做。"},{"en":"Having said that means despite what I have just said, I will now add a balancing point.","zh":"having said that意思是儘管我剛才那樣說，現在要補充一個平衡觀點。"},{"en":"The course is difficult; having said that, it teaches skills employers really value.","zh":"課程很困難；話雖如此，它教授僱主真正重視的技能。"},{"en":"This phrase helps speakers acknowledge a warning before giving a positive side.","zh":"這個短語幫助講者先承認警告，再提出正面一面。"},{"en":"It is useful when an idea needs balance rather than only criticism.","zh":"當一個想法需要平衡，而不只是批評時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"once you know what to look for","meaning":"一旦知道要找甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Once you know what to look for, mushroom picking is worth doing.","zh":"一旦知道要找甚麼，採摘蘑菇就值得做。"},{"en":"Once you know what to look for means after you understand which signs, features or details matter.","zh":"once you know what to look for意思是在你明白哪些標誌、特徵或細節重要之後。"},{"en":"Once you know what to look for in a job advert, you can avoid unsuitable roles faster.","zh":"一旦知道求職廣告中要看甚麼，你就能更快避開不合適職位。"},{"en":"Knowing what to look for reduces mistakes because you recognise useful clues.","zh":"知道要找甚麼可以減少錯誤，因為你能辨認有用線索。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that knowledge makes a task easier and safer.","zh":"這個短語顯示知識能令任務更容易和更安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be worth doing","meaning":"值得做","examples":[{"en":"Picking wild mushrooms is worth doing for the variety available.","zh":"因為可找到的種類繁多，採摘野生蘑菇值得做。"},{"en":"If something is worth doing, it gives enough benefit, pleasure or value to justify the effort.","zh":"如果某事be worth doing，意思是它帶來足夠好處、樂趣或價值，值得付出努力。"},{"en":"Learning basic first aid is worth doing because it may help someone in an emergency.","zh":"學習基本急救值得做，因為它可能在緊急情況中幫到人。"},{"en":"A task is worth doing when the result is more valuable than the time and energy spent.","zh":"當結果比所花時間和精力更有價值，任務就值得做。"},{"en":"This phrase judges whether an activity is worthwhile.","zh":"這個短語判斷某活動是否值得。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"amazing variety of","meaning":"種類繁多而令人驚喜","examples":[{"en":"There is an amazing variety of wild mushrooms available.","zh":"野生蘑菇種類繁多而令人驚喜。"},{"en":"An amazing variety of something means many different kinds, often more than expected.","zh":"amazing variety of某物，意思是有許多不同種類，通常比預期更多。"},{"en":"A large library may offer an amazing variety of books, from comics to history.","zh":"大型圖書館可能提供種類繁多而令人驚喜的書，由漫畫到歷史都有。"},{"en":"Variety can make an activity more enjoyable because people keep discovering new examples.","zh":"多樣性可以令活動更有趣，因為人們不斷發現新例子。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses surprise at how many types there are.","zh":"這個短語表達對種類數量之多感到驚喜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"available","meaning":"可取得；可找到","examples":[{"en":"There is an amazing variety of wild mushrooms available.","zh":"有種類繁多而令人驚喜的野生蘑菇可找到。"},{"en":"Available means able to be found, used, bought or chosen.","zh":"available意思是可以被找到、使用、購買或選擇。"},{"en":"A student may choose a course only if places are still available.","zh":"只有在仍有名額時，學生才可以選擇某課程。"},{"en":"If something is available locally, people do not need to travel far to get it.","zh":"如果某物在本地可取得，人們就不需要走很遠去得到它。"},{"en":"This word describes access or possibility.","zh":"這個詞描述取得機會或可能性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"get in the shops","meaning":"在店舖買到","examples":[{"en":"Some wild mushrooms cannot be found in the shops.","zh":"有些野生蘑菇不能在店舖買到。"},{"en":"To get something in the shops means to buy or find it in ordinary stores.","zh":"get something in the shops意思是在普通商店購買或找到某物。"},{"en":"Some local snacks are easy to get in the shops near schools.","zh":"有些本地小食很容易在學校附近店舖買到。"},{"en":"If a food cannot be found in shops, people may value it more when they find it themselves.","zh":"如果食物不能在店舖買到，人們自己找到時可能更珍惜。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts buying something with finding or collecting it elsewhere.","zh":"這個短語把購買某物與在其他地方尋找或採集作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"of course","meaning":"當然","examples":[{"en":"Of course, you have to be very careful when picking mushrooms.","zh":"當然，採摘蘑菇時你必須非常小心。"},{"en":"Of course is used to introduce something obvious, expected or already understood.","zh":"of course用來引入明顯、預期中或已被理解的事情。"},{"en":"Of course, students should check the question carefully before writing an answer.","zh":"當然，學生在寫答案前應仔細看清楚題目。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase when they want to remind listeners of an important basic point.","zh":"講者想提醒聽眾重要基本點時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It can make advice sound natural rather than surprising.","zh":"它可以令建議聽起來自然，而不是令人驚訝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"consume mushrooms","meaning":"食用蘑菇","examples":[{"en":"You should never consume mushrooms picked by friends or neighbours.","zh":"你絕不應食用由朋友或鄰居採摘的蘑菇。"},{"en":"To consume mushrooms means to eat them.","zh":"consume mushrooms意思是食用蘑菇。"},{"en":"People should not consume wild mushrooms unless they are certain they are safe.","zh":"除非確定安全，否則人們不應食用野生蘑菇。"},{"en":"Consuming the wrong mushroom can lead to serious illness.","zh":"食用錯誤蘑菇可以導致嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than simply saying “eat mushrooms”.","zh":"這個短語比單純說eat mushrooms更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"picked by","meaning":"由……採摘","examples":[{"en":"Never consume mushrooms picked by friends or neighbours.","zh":"絕不要食用由朋友或鄰居採摘的蘑菇。"},{"en":"Picked by someone means collected or gathered by that person.","zh":"picked by某人，意思是由該人收集或採摘。"},{"en":"Fruit picked by children on a school farm should be washed before eating.","zh":"由孩子在學校農場採摘的水果，食用前應先清洗。"},{"en":"If food is picked by someone inexperienced, there may be safety concerns.","zh":"如果食物由沒有經驗的人採摘，可能有安全疑慮。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who collected the item.","zh":"這個短語指出物品由誰收集。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"friends or neighbours","meaning":"朋友或鄰居","examples":[{"en":"Dan warns people not to eat mushrooms picked by friends or neighbours.","zh":"Dan警告人們不要吃由朋友或鄰居採摘的蘑菇。"},{"en":"Friends or neighbours are people you know socially or people who live near you.","zh":"friends or neighbours是你在社交上認識的人或住在你附近的人。"},{"en":"Friends or neighbours may mean well, but they may not have expert knowledge.","zh":"朋友或鄰居可能出於好意，但未必有專業知識。"},{"en":"Advice from friends or neighbours can be useful, but safety decisions may require specialists.","zh":"朋友或鄰居的建議可以有用，但安全決定可能需要專家。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to familiar people, not trained professionals.","zh":"這個短語指熟悉的人，而不是受訓專業人士。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"poisonous mushrooms","meaning":"有毒蘑菇","examples":[{"en":"Some poisonous mushrooms look similar to edible ones.","zh":"有些有毒蘑菇看起來與可食用蘑菇相似。"},{"en":"Poisonous mushrooms are mushrooms that contain toxins and can make people sick or even kill them.","zh":"poisonous mushrooms是含有毒素、可令人患病甚至死亡的蘑菇。"},{"en":"A poisonous mushroom may look harmless to someone without training.","zh":"對沒有訓練的人來說，有毒蘑菇可能看似無害。"},{"en":"Because poisonous mushrooms can be mistaken for safe ones, identification is extremely important.","zh":"因為有毒蘑菇可能被誤認為安全蘑菇，辨認非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strong safety warning.","zh":"這個短語帶有強烈安全警告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"look very similar to","meaning":"看起來與……非常相似","examples":[{"en":"Some poisonous mushrooms look very similar to edible ones.","zh":"有些有毒蘑菇看起來與可食用蘑菇非常相似。"},{"en":"To look very similar to something means to have almost the same appearance.","zh":"look very similar to某物，意思是外觀幾乎一樣。"},{"en":"Two school uniforms may look very similar to each other if the colours and badges are alike.","zh":"如果顏色和校章相似，兩套校服可能看起來非常相似。"},{"en":"When dangerous things look similar to safe things, people can easily make mistakes.","zh":"當危險東西看起來與安全東西相似，人們很容易犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual resemblance that may cause confusion.","zh":"這個短語描述可能造成混淆的外觀相似。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"edible ones","meaning":"可食用的那些","examples":[{"en":"Some poisonous mushrooms look like edible ones.","zh":"有些有毒蘑菇看起來像可食用的那些。"},{"en":"Edible ones means the ones that are safe or suitable to eat.","zh":"edible ones意思是那些安全或適合食用的。"},{"en":"Some berries look attractive, but only the edible ones should be eaten.","zh":"有些漿果看起來吸引，但只有可食用的那些才應被吃。"},{"en":"Confusing poisonous plants with edible ones can be dangerous.","zh":"把有毒植物與可食用的那些混淆可以很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to food items already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回前文已提及的食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"get confused","meaning":"感到混淆","examples":[{"en":"It is easy for people to get confused when identifying mushrooms.","zh":"人們辨認蘑菇時很容易感到混淆。"},{"en":"To get confused means to become unsure because things are difficult to tell apart or understand.","zh":"get confused意思是因事物難以區分或理解而變得不確定。"},{"en":"Students may get confused if two grammar rules look almost the same.","zh":"如果兩條文法規則看起來幾乎一樣，學生可能感到混淆。"},{"en":"Confusion can lead to mistakes, especially when safety depends on correct identification.","zh":"混淆可以導致錯誤，尤其當安全取決於正確辨認時。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a state of uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語描述不確定的狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the other thing to avoid","meaning":"另一件要避免的事","examples":[{"en":"The other thing to avoid is mushrooms growing beside busy roads.","zh":"另一件要避免的事，是生長在繁忙道路旁邊的蘑菇。"},{"en":"The other thing to avoid means another action, item or situation that people should stay away from.","zh":"the other thing to avoid意思是人們應避開的另一行動、物品或情況。"},{"en":"When cycling, the other thing to avoid is wearing dark clothes at night.","zh":"踩單車時，另一件要避免的事是晚上穿深色衣服。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another warning after one has already been given.","zh":"這個短語在已給出一項警告後，再加入另一項警告。"},{"en":"It helps organise safety advice into separate points.","zh":"它幫助把安全建議整理成不同重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"grow beside","meaning":"生長在……旁邊","examples":[{"en":"Avoid mushrooms growing beside busy roads.","zh":"避免生長在繁忙道路旁邊的蘑菇。"},{"en":"To grow beside something means to grow next to or near it.","zh":"grow beside某物，意思是生長在它旁邊或附近。"},{"en":"Flowers may grow beside a path where people walk every day.","zh":"花可能生長在人們每天步行的小路旁邊。"},{"en":"Plants growing beside roads may absorb pollution from traffic and dust.","zh":"生長在道路旁邊的植物可能吸收交通和塵土帶來的污染。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location in relation to another object or place.","zh":"這個短語描述相對於另一物或地方的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"busy roads","meaning":"繁忙道路","examples":[{"en":"Mushrooms growing beside busy roads should be avoided.","zh":"應避免生長在繁忙道路旁邊的蘑菇。"},{"en":"Busy roads are roads with a lot of traffic.","zh":"busy roads是有大量交通的道路。"},{"en":"Children should be careful near busy roads because cars may move quickly.","zh":"孩子在繁忙道路附近應小心，因為車輛可能行駛得很快。"},{"en":"Pollution from busy roads can affect nearby air, soil and plants.","zh":"繁忙道路帶來的污染可以影響附近空氣、土壤和植物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes roads where traffic is heavy and conditions may be unsafe.","zh":"這個短語描述交通繁重、情況可能不安全的道路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for obvious reasons","meaning":"原因很明顯","examples":[{"en":"You should avoid mushrooms beside busy roads for obvious reasons.","zh":"你應避免繁忙道路旁邊的蘑菇，原因很明顯。"},{"en":"For obvious reasons means the reason is clear and does not need much explanation.","zh":"for obvious reasons意思是原因很清楚，不需要太多解釋。"},{"en":"People should not swim during a thunderstorm, for obvious reasons.","zh":"人們不應在雷暴期間游泳，原因很明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when the danger or problem is easy to understand.","zh":"當危險或問題容易理解時，常會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It can make a warning sound direct and common-sense.","zh":"它可以令警告聽起來直接而合乎常識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"nothing beats","meaning":"沒有甚麼比得上","examples":[{"en":"Nothing beats the taste of freshly picked mushrooms.","zh":"沒有甚麼比得上新鮮採摘蘑菇的味道。"},{"en":"Nothing beats something means nothing is better than it.","zh":"nothing beats某事，意思是沒有東西比它更好。"},{"en":"After a long school day, nothing beats a hot meal at home.","zh":"漫長上學日後，沒有甚麼比得上家中的熱飯。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to express strong preference or enjoyment.","zh":"人們使用這個短語來表達強烈偏好或享受。"},{"en":"It is a friendly, conversational way to praise something highly.","zh":"它是一種友善而口語化的高度讚賞方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"freshly picked mushrooms","meaning":"新鮮採摘的蘑菇","examples":[{"en":"Freshly picked mushrooms taste better than shop-bought ones.","zh":"新鮮採摘的蘑菇比店舖買到的味道更好。"},{"en":"Freshly picked mushrooms are mushrooms collected recently, before they lose freshness.","zh":"freshly picked mushrooms是最近採集、尚未失去新鮮感的蘑菇。"},{"en":"Freshly picked fruit often smells stronger than fruit that has travelled for days.","zh":"新鮮採摘的水果通常比運輸了幾天的水果氣味更濃。"},{"en":"Freshness can improve taste because food has not dried out or aged too much.","zh":"新鮮度可以改善味道，因為食物未乾掉或放得太久。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses recent collection and better quality.","zh":"這個短語強調近期採集和較好質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"don’t forget that","meaning":"別忘記","examples":[{"en":"Don’t forget that shop mushrooms are often several days old.","zh":"別忘記店舖裏的蘑菇通常已放了好幾天。"},{"en":"Don’t forget that means remember this important point.","zh":"don’t forget that意思是記得這個重要重點。"},{"en":"Don’t forget that the library closes early on Fridays.","zh":"別忘記圖書館星期五會提早關門。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase to remind listeners of information that may affect their decision.","zh":"講者使用這個短語提醒聽眾可能影響決定的資訊。"},{"en":"It often introduces a practical warning or useful reminder.","zh":"它常引入實用警告或有用提醒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"several days old","meaning":"已放了好幾天","examples":[{"en":"The mushrooms in the shops are often several days old.","zh":"店舖裏的蘑菇通常已放了好幾天。"},{"en":"Several days old means something has existed or been kept for a few days.","zh":"several days old意思是某物已存在或存放了幾天。"},{"en":"Bread that is several days old may become dry and hard.","zh":"已放了好幾天的麵包可能變乾變硬。"},{"en":"Food that is several days old may still be safe, but it may no longer taste fresh.","zh":"已放了好幾天的食物可能仍然安全，但未必再有新鮮味道。"},{"en":"This phrase describes age and possible loss of freshness.","zh":"這個短語描述存放時間和可能失去新鮮度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"past their best","meaning":"已過最佳狀態","examples":[{"en":"Shop mushrooms are often past their best.","zh":"店舖蘑菇通常已過最佳狀態。"},{"en":"Past their best means no longer at the freshest, strongest or most attractive stage.","zh":"past their best意思是不再處於最新鮮、最強或最吸引的階段。"},{"en":"Flowers are past their best when their petals start to turn brown.","zh":"當花瓣開始變啡，花就已過最佳狀態。"},{"en":"Food past its best may still be edible but may have poorer taste or texture.","zh":"已過最佳狀態的食物可能仍可食用，但味道或口感較差。"},{"en":"This phrase describes decline after the best condition has passed.","zh":"這個短語描述最佳狀態過後的下降。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"certain ideas about","meaning":"關於……的某些觀念","examples":[{"en":"There are certain ideas about wild mushrooms that people should know.","zh":"有一些關於野生蘑菇的觀念是人們應該知道的。"},{"en":"Certain ideas about something are particular beliefs or opinions connected with that topic.","zh":"certain ideas about某事，是與該主題有關的特定信念或意見。"},{"en":"Students may have certain ideas about university life before they actually experience it.","zh":"學生在真正經歷大學生活前，可能對它有某些觀念。"},{"en":"Some ideas can be useful, while others may be wrong or dangerous.","zh":"有些觀念可以有用，而另一些可能錯誤或危險。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces beliefs that need to be explained or checked.","zh":"這個短語引入需要解釋或檢查的信念。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be aware of","meaning":"了解；意識到","examples":[{"en":"It is important to be aware of common ideas about wild mushrooms.","zh":"了解關於野生蘑菇的常見觀念很重要。"},{"en":"To be aware of something means to know about it and understand that it matters.","zh":"be aware of某事，意思是知道它並理解它重要。"},{"en":"Students should be aware of deadlines before starting a large project.","zh":"學生在開始大型專題前，應意識到截止日期。"},{"en":"Awareness helps people avoid mistakes because they notice risks early.","zh":"意識到問題能幫助人避免錯誤，因為他們及早注意到風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes informed attention.","zh":"這個短語描述有資訊支持的注意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"listen to people who","meaning":"聽信那些……的人","examples":[{"en":"Do not listen to people who say only pale mushrooms are safe.","zh":"不要聽信那些說只有淡色蘑菇才安全的人。"},{"en":"To listen to people who say something means to accept or follow their advice or claims.","zh":"listen to people who說某事，意思是接受或跟從他們的建議或聲稱。"},{"en":"Students should not listen to people who say revision is useless without checking the evidence.","zh":"學生不應聽信那些說溫習沒有用的人，而不查證證據。"},{"en":"Listening to the wrong people can lead to poor decisions.","zh":"聽信錯誤的人可以導致差劣決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in warnings about unreliable advice.","zh":"這個短語常用於警告不可靠建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"it is only OK to","meaning":"只有……才可以","examples":[{"en":"It is untrue that it is only OK to eat pale mushrooms.","zh":"說只有淡色蘑菇才可以吃是不正確的。"},{"en":"It is only OK to do something means it is acceptable only under that condition.","zh":"it is only OK to do something意思是只有在該條件下做某事才可接受。"},{"en":"It is only OK to enter the laboratory if a teacher is present.","zh":"只有老師在場時，才可以進入實驗室。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a strict condition, but the condition may be false or unnecessary.","zh":"這個短語設定嚴格條件，但該條件可能是錯誤或不必要的。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining or challenging a rule.","zh":"它適合用於解釋或挑戰規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pale or dull","meaning":"顏色淡或暗沉","examples":[{"en":"Some people wrongly believe only pale or dull mushrooms are safe.","zh":"有些人錯誤地相信只有顏色淡或暗沉的蘑菇才安全。"},{"en":"Pale or dull means light-coloured or not bright.","zh":"pale or dull意思是顏色淺或不鮮艷。"},{"en":"A pale or dull wall colour may make a classroom feel calm but less lively.","zh":"顏色淡或暗沉的牆色可能令課室感覺平靜但較不活潑。"},{"en":"Colour alone does not prove whether food, plants or mushrooms are safe.","zh":"單靠顏色不能證明食物、植物或蘑菇是否安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes appearance, not safety.","zh":"這個短語描述外觀，而不是安全性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"completely untrue","meaning":"完全不正確","examples":[{"en":"The idea that only dull mushrooms are edible is completely untrue.","zh":"只有暗沉蘑菇才可食用這個想法完全不正確。"},{"en":"Completely untrue means totally false.","zh":"completely untrue意思是完全錯誤。"},{"en":"The claim that all homework is useless is completely untrue because practice can build skill.","zh":"所有功課都沒用這個說法完全不正確，因為練習能建立技能。"},{"en":"A completely untrue belief can be dangerous if people act on it.","zh":"如果人們按完全不正確的信念行事，它可能很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly rejects a false idea.","zh":"這個短語強烈否定錯誤想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"edible mushrooms","meaning":"可食用蘑菇","examples":[{"en":"Some edible mushrooms are bright red.","zh":"有些可食用蘑菇是鮮紅色的。"},{"en":"Edible mushrooms are mushrooms that are safe to eat.","zh":"edible mushrooms是可以安全食用的蘑菇。"},{"en":"Shops sell edible mushrooms such as button mushrooms and shiitake mushrooms.","zh":"商店售賣可食用蘑菇，例如白蘑菇和冬菇。"},{"en":"Even edible mushrooms should be cleaned and cooked properly if a recipe requires it.","zh":"即使是可食用蘑菇，如果食譜要求，也應正確清洗和烹煮。"},{"en":"This phrase separates safe mushrooms from poisonous ones.","zh":"這個短語把安全蘑菇與有毒蘑菇分開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"personally","meaning":"就個人而言","examples":[{"en":"Personally, Dan prefers mushrooms cooked.","zh":"就個人而言，Dan比較喜歡蘑菇煮熟。"},{"en":"Personally means from my own opinion or preference.","zh":"personally意思是從我個人的意見或偏好來看。"},{"en":"Personally, I find handwritten notes easier to remember than typed notes.","zh":"就個人而言，我覺得手寫筆記比打字筆記更容易記住。"},{"en":"Speakers use this word to show they are giving a personal view, not a general rule.","zh":"講者使用這個詞來顯示自己是在表達個人看法，而不是一般規則。"},{"en":"This word makes an opinion sound more clearly personal.","zh":"這個詞令意見更清楚地帶有個人性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"prefer something cooked","meaning":"比較喜歡……煮熟","examples":[{"en":"Dan prefers mushrooms cooked.","zh":"Dan比較喜歡蘑菇煮熟。"},{"en":"To prefer something cooked means to like it better after it has been heated or prepared by cooking.","zh":"prefer something cooked意思是較喜歡某食物經加熱或烹調後的狀態。"},{"en":"Some people prefer carrots cooked because they become softer and sweeter.","zh":"有些人比較喜歡紅蘿蔔煮熟，因為它會變得較軟和較甜。"},{"en":"Cooking can change the taste, texture and safety of food.","zh":"烹調可以改變食物的味道、口感和安全性。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a preference about food preparation.","zh":"這個短語表達對食物處理方式的偏好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"do someone any harm","meaning":"對某人有害","examples":[{"en":"Eating some mushrooms uncooked in salads will not do you any harm.","zh":"在沙律中生吃某些蘑菇不會對你有害。"},{"en":"To do someone any harm means to hurt or damage them in some way.","zh":"do someone any harm意思是以某種方式傷害或損害某人。"},{"en":"Drinking a glass of water before bed will not do most people any harm.","zh":"睡前喝一杯水通常不會對大多數人有害。"},{"en":"A harmless action does not create injury, illness or serious trouble.","zh":"無害的行動不會造成受傷、生病或嚴重麻煩。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to reassure someone about safety.","zh":"這個短語常用於讓人放心安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"uncooked","meaning":"未煮熟的；生的","examples":[{"en":"Some mushrooms can be eaten uncooked in salads.","zh":"有些蘑菇可以在沙律中生吃。"},{"en":"Uncooked means not cooked or heated.","zh":"uncooked意思是未經烹煮或加熱。"},{"en":"Uncooked vegetables are often used in salads because they stay crisp.","zh":"未煮熟的蔬菜常用於沙律，因為它們保持爽脆。"},{"en":"Some foods are safe uncooked, while others must be cooked to kill germs or toxins.","zh":"有些食物生吃是安全的，而另一些必須煮熟以殺死細菌或毒素。"},{"en":"This word describes the state of food before cooking.","zh":"這個詞描述食物烹調前的狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in salads","meaning":"在沙律中","examples":[{"en":"Some mushrooms can be eaten uncooked in salads.","zh":"有些蘑菇可以在沙律中生吃。"},{"en":"In salads means as part of a cold dish usually made with vegetables or other fresh ingredients.","zh":"in salads意思是作為通常由蔬菜或其他新鮮材料製成的冷盤一部分。"},{"en":"Tomatoes, cucumbers and lettuce are often used in salads.","zh":"番茄、青瓜和生菜常用於沙律中。"},{"en":"Foods used in salads should be washed carefully because they may be eaten raw.","zh":"用於沙律中的食物應仔細清洗，因為它們可能會生吃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how an ingredient is served.","zh":"這個短語描述食材如何被上菜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"peel them","meaning":"把它們去皮","examples":[{"en":"It is not necessary to peel mushrooms.","zh":"沒有必要把蘑菇去皮。"},{"en":"To peel them means to remove the outer skin or surface from them.","zh":"peel them意思是去除它們的外皮或表層。"},{"en":"You may peel apples if the skin is tough or dirty.","zh":"如果蘋果皮很硬或骯髒，你可能會把它們去皮。"},{"en":"Some foods need peeling, but mushrooms usually only need cleaning.","zh":"有些食物需要去皮，但蘑菇通常只需要清潔。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a preparation step before eating or cooking.","zh":"這個短語描述食用或烹調前的準備步驟。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tell if","meaning":"判斷是否……","examples":[{"en":"You cannot tell if a mushroom is safe to eat by its smell.","zh":"你不能靠氣味判斷蘑菇是否可以安全食用。"},{"en":"To tell if something is true means to judge or know whether it is true.","zh":"tell if某事屬實，意思是判斷或知道某事是否真實。"},{"en":"You cannot always tell if a student understands by looking at their face.","zh":"你不能總是靠看學生表情判斷他是否明白。"},{"en":"Some things require testing or expert knowledge before you can tell if they are safe.","zh":"有些東西需要測試或專家知識，才可判斷是否安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when judging between two possibilities.","zh":"這個短語用於在兩種可能之間作判斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"safe to eat","meaning":"可以安全食用","examples":[{"en":"You cannot tell if a mushroom is safe to eat by smelling it.","zh":"你不能靠嗅聞蘑菇來判斷它是否可以安全食用。"},{"en":"Safe to eat means not dangerous to consume.","zh":"safe to eat意思是食用時沒有危險。"},{"en":"Food left outside overnight may not be safe to eat the next day.","zh":"放在外面過夜的食物第二天可能不可以安全食用。"},{"en":"Safety depends on what the food is, how it was stored and whether it contains toxins.","zh":"安全性取決於食物是甚麼、如何儲存，以及是否含有毒素。"},{"en":"This phrase is especially important when discussing wild food.","zh":"這個短語在討論野外食物時尤其重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"by its smell","meaning":"靠氣味","examples":[{"en":"You cannot judge a mushroom’s safety by its smell.","zh":"你不能靠氣味判斷蘑菇的安全性。"},{"en":"By its smell means using its smell as the way to judge it.","zh":"by its smell意思是用它的氣味作為判斷方法。"},{"en":"You may recognise fresh bread by its smell when you pass a bakery.","zh":"你經過麵包店時，可能靠氣味認出新鮮麵包。"},{"en":"Smell can give clues about some foods, but it is not reliable for mushroom safety.","zh":"氣味可以為某些食物提供線索，但對蘑菇安全性並不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the method used for judgement.","zh":"這個短語指出所使用的判斷方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"deadly mushrooms","meaning":"致命蘑菇","examples":[{"en":"Some deadly mushrooms have no smell.","zh":"有些致命蘑菇沒有氣味。"},{"en":"Deadly mushrooms are mushrooms that can cause death if eaten.","zh":"deadly mushrooms是食用後可以導致死亡的蘑菇。"},{"en":"A deadly mushroom may look ordinary, so appearance alone is not enough for identification.","zh":"致命蘑菇可能看起來很普通，所以單靠外觀不足以辨認。"},{"en":"The danger of deadly mushrooms is why beginners should learn from experts.","zh":"致命蘑菇的危險正是初學者應向專家學習的原因。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the strongest kind of safety warning.","zh":"這個短語給出最強烈的安全警告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have no smell","meaning":"沒有氣味","examples":[{"en":"Some deadly mushrooms have no smell.","zh":"有些致命蘑菇沒有氣味。"},{"en":"To have no smell means to produce no noticeable odour.","zh":"have no smell意思是沒有可察覺的氣味。"},{"en":"A gas can be dangerous if it has no smell and people cannot notice a leak.","zh":"如果氣體沒有氣味，而人們無法察覺洩漏，它可以很危險。"},{"en":"If something dangerous has no smell, people cannot rely on their nose for warning.","zh":"如果危險東西沒有氣味，人們就不能靠鼻子作警告。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the absence of a sensory clue.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏感官線索。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"taste quite nice","meaning":"味道相當不錯","examples":[{"en":"Some deadly mushrooms apparently taste quite nice.","zh":"有些致命蘑菇據說味道相當不錯。"},{"en":"To taste quite nice means to have a fairly pleasant flavour.","zh":"taste quite nice意思是味道頗令人愉快。"},{"en":"A medicine may taste quite nice even though it still needs to be taken carefully.","zh":"藥物可能味道相當不錯，但仍需要小心服用。"},{"en":"Pleasant taste does not always mean food is safe.","zh":"味道好並不總代表食物安全。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that flavour can be misleading.","zh":"這個短語提醒人味道可能具誤導性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"apparently","meaning":"據說；顯然","examples":[{"en":"Some deadly mushrooms apparently taste quite nice.","zh":"有些致命蘑菇據說味道相當不錯。"},{"en":"Apparently means according to what people say or according to available information.","zh":"apparently意思是根據人們所說或現有資訊。"},{"en":"Apparently, the bus route will change next month, but we should check the official notice.","zh":"據說巴士路線下個月會改，但我們應查看官方通知。"},{"en":"This word can show that the speaker is not claiming direct personal knowledge.","zh":"這個詞可以顯示說話者並非聲稱有直接親身知識。"},{"en":"It is useful when reporting information carefully.","zh":"它適合用於謹慎轉述資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"just because...doesn’t mean","meaning":"只因……並不代表","examples":[{"en":"Just because deer eat a mushroom does not mean humans can eat it.","zh":"只因鹿吃某種蘑菇，並不代表人類可以吃它。"},{"en":"Just because one thing is true doesn’t mean another thing must also be true.","zh":"just because一件事屬實，doesn’t mean另一件事也必然屬實。"},{"en":"Just because a friend likes a course does not mean it is right for you.","zh":"只因朋友喜歡某課程，並不代表它適合你。"},{"en":"This pattern warns people not to make a weak assumption.","zh":"這個句式提醒人不要作出薄弱假設。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting a false connection between two ideas.","zh":"當要糾正兩個想法之間的錯誤連結時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a particular mushroom","meaning":"某一種蘑菇","examples":[{"en":"Animals may be able to eat a particular mushroom safely.","zh":"動物可能能夠安全食用某一種蘑菇。"},{"en":"A particular mushroom means one specific kind or example of mushroom.","zh":"a particular mushroom意思是某一個特定種類或例子的蘑菇。"},{"en":"A guidebook may warn that a particular mushroom is safe only after careful cooking.","zh":"指南書可能警告某一種蘑菇只有在仔細煮熟後才安全。"},{"en":"Different species react differently, so information about one mushroom may not apply to another.","zh":"不同物種反應不同，所以關於某一種蘑菇的資訊未必適用於另一種。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on one exact type, not mushrooms in general.","zh":"這個短語著重某個確切種類，而不是泛指蘑菇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關聯","examples":[{"en":"Mushroom picking is associated with the countryside.","zh":"採摘蘑菇常與鄉郊有關聯。"},{"en":"To be associated with something means to be connected with it in people’s minds.","zh":"be associated with某事，意思是在人的想法中與它有連繫。"},{"en":"Red lanterns are often associated with Lunar New Year celebrations.","zh":"紅燈籠常與農曆新年慶祝活動有關聯。"},{"en":"An activity can be associated with a place because people often do it there.","zh":"一項活動可以因人們常在某地方做它，而與該地方有關聯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mental or cultural connection.","zh":"這個短語描述思想上或文化上的連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the countryside","meaning":"鄉郊","examples":[{"en":"Mushroom picking is often associated with the countryside.","zh":"採摘蘑菇常與鄉郊有關。"},{"en":"The countryside is land outside towns and cities, often with fields, woods and villages.","zh":"the countryside是城鎮和城市以外的土地，通常有田地、樹林和村莊。"},{"en":"Families may visit the countryside for fresh air and quiet walks.","zh":"家庭可能到鄉郊呼吸新鮮空氣和安靜散步。"},{"en":"The countryside can offer natural habitats that are less common in cities.","zh":"鄉郊可以提供城市較少見的自然棲地。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts rural places with urban areas.","zh":"這個短語把鄉村地方與城市地區作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"your local park","meaning":"你本區的公園","examples":[{"en":"Your local park can be a great place to start mushroom picking.","zh":"你本區的公園可以是開始採摘蘑菇的好地方。"},{"en":"Your local park is a public green space near where you live.","zh":"your local park是你居住地附近的公共綠地。"},{"en":"Families may use their local park for walking, jogging and weekend picnics.","zh":"家庭可能使用本區公園散步、跑步和週末野餐。"},{"en":"Local parks can be good learning places because they are easy to reach.","zh":"本區公園可以是良好學習地方，因為它們容易到達。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the advice feel close and practical.","zh":"這個短語令建議感覺貼近而實用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a great place to start","meaning":"很好的起點","examples":[{"en":"A local park can be a great place to start.","zh":"本地公園可以是很好的起點。"},{"en":"A great place to start means a good first place or first step for beginners.","zh":"a great place to start意思是對初學者而言很好的第一個地方或第一步。"},{"en":"A school library is a great place to start if you want to read more.","zh":"如果你想多閱讀，學校圖書館是很好的起點。"},{"en":"Starting in an easy, familiar place can build confidence before trying harder tasks.","zh":"在容易而熟悉的地方開始，可以在嘗試更難任務前建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving beginner-friendly advice.","zh":"這個短語適合用於提供初學者友善建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a range of habitats","meaning":"一系列不同棲地","examples":[{"en":"There is usually a range of habitats where mushrooms grow.","zh":"通常有一系列不同棲地供蘑菇生長。"},{"en":"A range of habitats means several different natural places where living things can live.","zh":"a range of habitats意思是幾種不同、可供生物生活的自然地方。"},{"en":"A park may have a range of habitats, including grass, trees, ponds and flower beds.","zh":"公園可能有一系列不同棲地，包括草地、樹木、池塘和花圃。"},{"en":"Different habitats support different plants, insects and fungi.","zh":"不同棲地支援不同植物、昆蟲和真菌。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety in natural environments.","zh":"這個短語強調自然環境中的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"playing fields","meaning":"運動場","examples":[{"en":"Mushrooms may grow in playing fields.","zh":"蘑菇可能在運動場生長。"},{"en":"Playing fields are open grassy areas used for sports and games.","zh":"playing fields是用於運動和遊戲的開放草地。"},{"en":"Students may practise football on the school playing fields after lessons.","zh":"學生可能放學後在學校運動場練習足球。"},{"en":"Mushrooms can appear in playing fields when grass is damp and conditions are suitable.","zh":"當草地潮濕而條件合適，蘑菇可以在運動場出現。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to sports areas, not indoor playgrounds.","zh":"這個短語指運動用草地，而不是室內遊樂場。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"wooded areas","meaning":"林地","examples":[{"en":"Mushrooms often grow in wooded areas.","zh":"蘑菇常在林地生長。"},{"en":"Wooded areas are places with many trees.","zh":"wooded areas是有許多樹木的地方。"},{"en":"A country park may have wooded areas where birds, insects and fungi live.","zh":"郊野公園可能有林地，讓鳥類、昆蟲和真菌生活。"},{"en":"Wooded areas are good for mushrooms because shade and fallen leaves create damp conditions.","zh":"林地適合蘑菇，因為陰影和落葉創造潮濕環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tree-covered natural spaces.","zh":"這個短語描述被樹木覆蓋的自然空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"first thing in the morning","meaning":"一大清早","examples":[{"en":"You need to go mushroom picking first thing in the morning.","zh":"你需要一大清早去採摘蘑菇。"},{"en":"First thing in the morning means very early, before doing other activities.","zh":"first thing in the morning意思是很早，在做其他活動之前。"},{"en":"A student may check exam results first thing in the morning.","zh":"學生可能一大清早查看考試結果。"},{"en":"Going early can help people avoid crowds and get the best choice.","zh":"早去可以幫助人避開人群並得到最好選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses doing something at the start of the day.","zh":"這個短語強調在一天開始時做某事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"there is likely to be","meaning":"很可能會有","examples":[{"en":"There is likely to be a lot of competition for mushrooms.","zh":"很可能會有很多人爭奪蘑菇。"},{"en":"There is likely to be means something will probably exist or happen.","zh":"there is likely to be意思是某事很可能存在或發生。"},{"en":"There is likely to be heavy traffic near the stadium after the match.","zh":"比賽後體育館附近很可能會有嚴重交通擠塞。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they are making a careful prediction.","zh":"人們在作謹慎預測時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It suggests probability, not complete certainty.","zh":"它表示可能性，而不是完全確定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a lot of competition","meaning":"激烈競爭","examples":[{"en":"There is likely to be a lot of competition for the best mushrooms.","zh":"最好的蘑菇很可能會有激烈競爭。"},{"en":"A lot of competition means many people or groups are trying to get the same thing.","zh":"a lot of competition意思是許多人或群體嘗試得到同一東西。"},{"en":"There is a lot of competition for places in popular university programmes.","zh":"熱門大學課程名額有激烈競爭。"},{"en":"Competition can make people act earlier, work harder or accept less convenient options.","zh":"競爭可以令人更早行動、更努力或接受較不方便的選項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pressure caused by many people wanting the same opportunity.","zh":"這個短語描述很多人想要同一機會所造成的壓力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not just from…but…","meaning":"不只是來自……也來自……","examples":[{"en":"There is competition not just from people but from wildlife too.","zh":"競爭不只是來自人類，也來自野生動物。"},{"en":"Not just from A but from B too means one source exists, and another source also matters.","zh":"not just from A but from B too意思是不只有A這個來源，B這個來源也重要。"},{"en":"A school may face pressure not just from exams but from parents’ expectations too.","zh":"學校面對的壓力不只是來自考試，也來自家長期望。"},{"en":"This structure expands the cause or source beyond the first obvious one.","zh":"這個結構把原因或來源擴展到第一個明顯來源以外。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing that a situation is more complicated than expected.","zh":"當要顯示情況比預期複雜時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"wildlife","meaning":"野生動物","examples":[{"en":"Wildlife may compete with people for wild mushrooms.","zh":"野生動物可能與人類爭奪野生蘑菇。"},{"en":"Wildlife means animals and plants living naturally in the wild.","zh":"wildlife意思是在野外自然生活的動物和植物。"},{"en":"Birds, foxes, insects and wildflowers are all examples of wildlife in a country park.","zh":"鳥、狐狸、昆蟲和野花都是郊野公園中的野生生物例子。"},{"en":"Human activities can affect wildlife by changing habitats or removing food sources.","zh":"人類活動可以透過改變棲地或移除食物來源來影響野生動物。"},{"en":"This word refers to living things that are not domesticated or farmed.","zh":"這個詞指非馴養或非農場飼養的生物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"complete beginner","meaning":"完全新手","examples":[{"en":"A complete beginner should not go mushroom picking alone.","zh":"完全新手不應獨自去採摘蘑菇。"},{"en":"A complete beginner is someone with no experience or knowledge in an activity.","zh":"complete beginner是對某活動沒有經驗或知識的人。"},{"en":"A complete beginner in swimming should learn in shallow water with an instructor.","zh":"游泳完全新手應在教練陪同下於淺水學習。"},{"en":"Beginners need guidance because they may not recognise common risks.","zh":"新手需要指導，因為他們可能認不出常見風險。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a total lack of experience.","zh":"這個短語強調完全缺乏經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"recommend going alone","meaning":"建議獨自前往","examples":[{"en":"Dan does not recommend going alone if you are a beginner.","zh":"如果你是初學者，Dan不建議獨自前往。"},{"en":"To recommend going alone means to advise someone to go by themselves.","zh":"recommend going alone意思是建議某人自己一個人去。"},{"en":"A teacher would not recommend going alone on a difficult hike for a first outdoor trip.","zh":"對第一次戶外活動的人，老師不會建議獨自前往困難遠足路線。"},{"en":"If a task is risky, experts may recommend going with someone experienced instead.","zh":"如果任務有風險，專家可能會建議與有經驗人士同行。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when giving safety advice.","zh":"這個短語常用於提供安全建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rely on","meaning":"依賴","examples":[{"en":"Beginners should not rely on photos in a book.","zh":"初學者不應依賴書中的照片。"},{"en":"To rely on something means to depend on it for help, information or support.","zh":"rely on某物，意思是依靠它提供幫助、資訊或支援。"},{"en":"Students should not rely on memory alone when exam dates are written in the timetable.","zh":"當考試日期已寫在時間表上，學生不應只依賴記憶。"},{"en":"Relying on one weak source can lead to mistakes.","zh":"依賴單一薄弱來源可以導致錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dependence on someone or something.","zh":"這個短語描述對某人或某物的依靠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"phone apps","meaning":"手機應用程式","examples":[{"en":"Some phone apps are useful for identifying mushrooms.","zh":"有些手機應用程式有助辨認蘑菇。"},{"en":"Phone apps are software programmes used on mobile phones.","zh":"phone apps是在手機上使用的軟件程式。"},{"en":"Students may use phone apps to learn vocabulary, check transport or track exercise.","zh":"學生可能使用手機應用程式學詞彙、查交通或記錄運動。"},{"en":"Apps can be helpful, but they may fail without internet access or accurate data.","zh":"應用程式可以有幫助，但若沒有網絡或準確資料，可能會失效。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to mobile digital tools.","zh":"這個短語指手機數碼工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"identify mushrooms","meaning":"辨認蘑菇","examples":[{"en":"Phone apps can help people identify mushrooms.","zh":"手機應用程式可以幫助人辨認蘑菇。"},{"en":"To identify mushrooms means to recognise which type of mushroom they are.","zh":"identify mushrooms意思是認出蘑菇屬於哪一種類。"},{"en":"Experts identify mushrooms by checking shape, colour, gills, smell and habitat.","zh":"專家透過檢查形狀、顏色、菌褶、氣味和棲地來辨認蘑菇。"},{"en":"Correct identification is important because some safe and poisonous mushrooms look similar.","zh":"正確辨認很重要，因為有些安全和有毒蘑菇看起來相似。"},{"en":"This phrase describes naming or recognising a mushroom accurately.","zh":"這個短語描述準確命名或認出蘑菇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rely on getting","meaning":"指望能夠得到","examples":[{"en":"You cannot always rely on getting a good signal in a wood.","zh":"你不能總是指望能夠在樹林中得到良好訊號。"},{"en":"To rely on getting something means to depend on being able to receive or obtain it.","zh":"rely on getting某物，意思是依賴自己能夠收到或取得它。"},{"en":"Students should not rely on getting a printer at school five minutes before the deadline.","zh":"學生不應在截止前五分鐘才指望能夠在學校找到打印機。"},{"en":"If you rely on getting something uncertain, your plan may fail.","zh":"如果你指望能得到不確定的東西，計劃可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against depending on something that may not happen.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要依賴未必會發生的事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a good signal","meaning":"良好訊號","examples":[{"en":"You may not get a good signal in the middle of a wood.","zh":"你在樹林深處可能得不到良好訊號。"},{"en":"A good signal is a strong mobile or internet connection.","zh":"a good signal是強而穩定的手機或網絡連接。"},{"en":"People need a good signal to make calls, use maps or send messages.","zh":"人們需要良好訊號來打電話、使用地圖或發訊息。"},{"en":"In remote areas, a weak signal can make phone apps unreliable.","zh":"在偏遠地區，訊號弱可以令手機應用程式不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to communication strength on a device.","zh":"這個短語指裝置上的通訊強度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the middle of","meaning":"在……深處","examples":[{"en":"You cannot always get a phone signal in the middle of a wood.","zh":"你不能總是在樹林深處收到手機訊號。"},{"en":"In the middle of something means deep inside or at the central part of it.","zh":"in the middle of某處，意思是在其深處或中央部分。"},{"en":"A student may feel nervous if the bus breaks down in the middle of nowhere.","zh":"如果巴士在荒郊野外中途拋錨，學生可能感到緊張。"},{"en":"When people are in the middle of a forest, help and communication may be farther away.","zh":"當人在森林深處，協助和通訊可能更遠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position inside a place or situation.","zh":"這個短語描述在某地方或情況中的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"if possible","meaning":"如果可能","examples":[{"en":"If possible, beginners should go with a group led by an expert.","zh":"如果可能，初學者應跟隨由專家帶領的小組。"},{"en":"If possible means if it can be done or arranged.","zh":"if possible意思是如果能做到或安排得到。"},{"en":"If possible, students should visit the campus before choosing a university.","zh":"如果可能，學生在選擇大學前應參觀校園。"},{"en":"This phrase gives advice while recognising that circumstances may not always allow it.","zh":"這個短語提供建議，同時承認情況未必總是容許。"},{"en":"It makes a recommendation sound practical and flexible.","zh":"它令建議聽起來實際而有彈性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go with a group","meaning":"跟小組同行","examples":[{"en":"Beginners should go with a group when picking mushrooms.","zh":"初學者採摘蘑菇時應跟小組同行。"},{"en":"To go with a group means to travel or take part together with other people.","zh":"go with a group意思是與其他人一起前往或參與。"},{"en":"Students should go with a group on their first night hike for safety.","zh":"學生第一次夜行遠足時應跟小組同行，以確保安全。"},{"en":"Going with a group can provide support, shared knowledge and quicker help.","zh":"跟小組同行可以提供支援、共享知識和更快協助。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts group participation with going alone.","zh":"這個短語把小組參與與獨自行動作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"led by an expert","meaning":"由專家帶領","examples":[{"en":"A beginner should join a group led by an expert.","zh":"初學者應加入由專家帶領的小組。"},{"en":"Led by an expert means guided by someone with strong knowledge and experience.","zh":"led by an expert意思是由有豐富知識和經驗的人指導。"},{"en":"A mountain walk led by an expert is safer for people who do not know the route.","zh":"對不熟悉路線的人來說，由專家帶領的山路步行較安全。"},{"en":"Expert leadership helps beginners avoid dangerous mistakes.","zh":"專家帶領能幫助初學者避免危險錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who is responsible for guiding the group.","zh":"這個短語指出誰負責引導小組。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"stay safe","meaning":"保持安全","examples":[{"en":"Going with an expert helps beginners stay safe.","zh":"跟專家同行有助初學者保持安全。"},{"en":"To stay safe means to avoid danger, injury or serious mistakes.","zh":"stay safe意思是避免危險、受傷或嚴重錯誤。"},{"en":"Students should stay safe online by not sharing personal passwords.","zh":"學生不分享個人密碼，就能在網上保持安全。"},{"en":"Safety advice helps people enjoy an activity without unnecessary risk.","zh":"安全建議幫助人們享受活動，而不承受不必要風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in warnings and practical guidance.","zh":"這個短語常用於警告和實用指引。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"learn a lot that way","meaning":"那樣能學到很多","examples":[{"en":"You will stay safe and learn a lot that way.","zh":"你會保持安全，而且那樣能學到很多。"},{"en":"To learn a lot that way means to gain much knowledge by using that method.","zh":"learn a lot that way意思是透過那種方法得到很多知識。"},{"en":"A student who practises speaking with classmates can learn a lot that way.","zh":"與同學練習口語的學生可以那樣學到很多。"},{"en":"Learning with experienced people is useful because they can correct mistakes immediately.","zh":"與有經驗人士學習很有用，因為他們可以即時糾正錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase praises a particular method of learning.","zh":"這個短語讚賞某種學習方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"conservation","meaning":"保育","examples":[{"en":"Conservation is a really important consideration when picking mushrooms.","zh":"採摘蘑菇時，保育是一個非常重要的考慮因素。"},{"en":"Conservation means protecting nature, wildlife or natural resources from damage or loss.","zh":"conservation意思是保護自然、野生生物或自然資源免受破壞或流失。"},{"en":"A country park uses conservation rules to protect rare plants and animals.","zh":"郊野公園使用保育規則保護稀有植物和動物。"},{"en":"Without conservation, people may collect too much and damage habitats.","zh":"沒有保育，人們可能採集過量並破壞棲地。"},{"en":"This word is important when human enjoyment must be balanced with nature’s survival.","zh":"當人類享受需要與自然生存平衡時，這個詞很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"important consideration","meaning":"重要考慮因素","examples":[{"en":"Conservation is an important consideration.","zh":"保育是一個重要考慮因素。"},{"en":"An important consideration is a factor that must be thought about before making a decision.","zh":"important consideration是在作決定前必須思考的因素。"},{"en":"Cost is an important consideration when a family chooses a course.","zh":"家庭選擇課程時，費用是一個重要考慮因素。"},{"en":"If people ignore important considerations, their decisions may cause problems later.","zh":"如果人們忽略重要考慮因素，他們的決定日後可能造成問題。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a factor that should not be forgotten.","zh":"這個短語突顯不應忘記的因素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"follow basic rules","meaning":"遵守基本規則","examples":[{"en":"Mushroom pickers must follow a few basic rules.","zh":"採蘑菇的人必須遵守幾條基本規則。"},{"en":"To follow basic rules means to obey simple important instructions.","zh":"follow basic rules意思是遵守簡單而重要的指示。"},{"en":"Students must follow basic rules in the laboratory, such as wearing goggles.","zh":"學生在實驗室必須遵守基本規則，例如戴護目鏡。"},{"en":"Basic rules reduce risk because everyone knows what not to do.","zh":"基本規則能減少風險，因為每個人都知道甚麼不應做。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in safety advice and organised activities.","zh":"這個短語常見於安全建議和有組織活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in one area","meaning":"在同一區域內","examples":[{"en":"You should never pick all the mushrooms in one area.","zh":"你絕不應在同一區域內採摘所有蘑菇。"},{"en":"In one area means in a single place or section.","zh":"in one area意思是在單一地方或範圍內。"},{"en":"A gardener should not remove all flowers in one area if insects depend on them.","zh":"如果昆蟲依賴花朵，園丁不應移走同一區域內所有花。"},{"en":"Taking everything from one area can damage local growth and reduce future supply.","zh":"從同一區域拿走所有東西，可以破壞本地生長並減少未來供應。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on limiting impact in a specific place.","zh":"這個短語著重限制對特定地方的影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"collect only enough for","meaning":"只採集足夠……的量","examples":[{"en":"You should collect only enough mushrooms for your own needs.","zh":"你應只採集足夠自己所需的蘑菇。"},{"en":"To collect only enough for something means to take no more than the amount required.","zh":"collect only enough for某用途，意思是只取所需數量，不多取。"},{"en":"Campers should collect only enough water for the day if supplies are limited.","zh":"如果供應有限，露營者應只收集足夠當天使用的水。"},{"en":"Taking only enough leaves resources for others and protects the environment.","zh":"只取足夠分量能把資源留給他人並保護環境。"},{"en":"This phrase teaches restraint and responsible use.","zh":"這個短語教人節制和負責任使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"your own needs","meaning":"自己所需","examples":[{"en":"Pick only enough mushrooms for your own needs.","zh":"只採摘足夠自己所需的蘑菇。"},{"en":"Your own needs are the amount or support you personally require.","zh":"your own needs是你個人所需要的數量或支援。"},{"en":"A student should borrow only the books needed for their own needs so others can use the library too.","zh":"學生應只借自己所需的書，讓其他人也能使用圖書館。"},{"en":"Thinking about your own needs prevents waste when resources are limited.","zh":"考慮自己所需可以在資源有限時防止浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on personal necessity rather than greed.","zh":"這個短語著重個人需要，而不是貪心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be careful that","meaning":"小心不要……","examples":[{"en":"Be careful that you do not trample on young mushrooms.","zh":"小心不要踩踏幼小蘑菇。"},{"en":"Be careful that means pay attention so that a problem does not happen.","zh":"be careful that意思是留意，以免問題發生。"},{"en":"Be careful that you save your essay before closing the computer.","zh":"小心在關電腦前先儲存文章。"},{"en":"Careful attention prevents accidental damage or mistakes.","zh":"小心注意能防止意外破壞或錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a warning about what to avoid.","zh":"這個短語引入關於避免甚麼的警告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"trample on","meaning":"踩踏","examples":[{"en":"Pickers must not trample on young mushrooms or other plants.","zh":"採摘者不得踩踏幼小蘑菇或其他植物。"},{"en":"To trample on something means to step heavily on it and damage it.","zh":"trample on某物，意思是重重踩在它上面並造成破壞。"},{"en":"Students should not trample on flower beds when crossing the school garden.","zh":"學生穿過學校花園時，不應踩踏花圃。"},{"en":"Trampling can kill young plants before they have a chance to grow.","zh":"踩踏可以在幼苗有機會生長前殺死它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage caused by walking carelessly.","zh":"這個短語描述因走路不小心造成的破壞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"young mushrooms","meaning":"幼小蘑菇","examples":[{"en":"Pickers should avoid damaging young mushrooms.","zh":"採摘者應避免破壞幼小蘑菇。"},{"en":"Young mushrooms are mushrooms that are still small and not fully grown.","zh":"young mushrooms是仍然細小、未完全長成的蘑菇。"},{"en":"Young plants and fungi need time to develop before they can reproduce.","zh":"幼小植物和真菌需要時間發展，才可以繁殖。"},{"en":"Damaging young mushrooms can reduce the number of mushrooms in the area later.","zh":"破壞幼小蘑菇可以減少該區日後的蘑菇數量。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on early growth and future supply.","zh":"這個短語著重早期生長和未來供應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"protected by law","meaning":"受法律保護","examples":[{"en":"Some endangered mushrooms are protected by law.","zh":"有些瀕危蘑菇受法律保護。"},{"en":"Protected by law means guarded by legal rules that forbid harm, collection or destruction.","zh":"protected by law意思是受法律規則保護，禁止傷害、採集或破壞。"},{"en":"Historic buildings may be protected by law so owners cannot demolish them freely.","zh":"歷史建築可能受法律保護，所以業主不能隨意拆卸。"},{"en":"If a species is protected by law, breaking the rules may lead to punishment.","zh":"如果某物種受法律保護，違反規則可能導致懲罰。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that protection is official, not just a suggestion.","zh":"這個短語顯示保護是官方的，而不只是建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a decline in","meaning":"……的下降","examples":[{"en":"There has been a decline in some varieties of wild mushrooms.","zh":"有些野生蘑菇品種數量有所下降。"},{"en":"A decline in something means a decrease in its number, amount or strength.","zh":"a decline in某事，意思是其數量、程度或力量下降。"},{"en":"A decline in school attendance may worry teachers and parents.","zh":"學校出席率下降可能令老師和家長擔心。"},{"en":"Declines can happen when habitats are damaged or conditions change.","zh":"當棲地受損或條件改變，下降可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a downward trend.","zh":"這個短語描述向下趨勢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"varieties of","meaning":"……的品種","examples":[{"en":"There has been a decline in some varieties of wild mushrooms.","zh":"有些野生蘑菇品種數量有所下降。"},{"en":"Varieties of something are different types within the same general group.","zh":"varieties of某物，是同一大類中的不同種類。"},{"en":"A market may sell many varieties of apples, each with a different taste.","zh":"市場可能售賣多個蘋果品種，每種味道不同。"},{"en":"Protecting varieties matters because losing one type reduces natural diversity.","zh":"保護不同品種很重要，因為失去一種會減少自然多樣性。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on different types, not total quantity only.","zh":"這個短語著重不同類型，而不只是總數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"wild mushrooms","meaning":"野生蘑菇","examples":[{"en":"Some varieties of wild mushrooms have declined.","zh":"有些野生蘑菇品種數量已下降。"},{"en":"Wild mushrooms are mushrooms that grow naturally outdoors without being farmed.","zh":"wild mushrooms是在戶外自然生長、並非人工栽培的蘑菇。"},{"en":"Wild mushrooms may appear after rain in woods, fields or parks.","zh":"雨後，野生蘑菇可能在樹林、田野或公園出現。"},{"en":"Because wild mushrooms are not grown under controlled conditions, identification is important.","zh":"因為野生蘑菇不是在受控條件下栽培，辨認很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts naturally growing mushrooms with farmed or shop-bought ones.","zh":"這個短語把自然生長的蘑菇與人工栽培或店舖購買的蘑菇作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in this part of the country","meaning":"在這個國家的這一地區","examples":[{"en":"Some wild mushrooms have declined in this part of the country.","zh":"有些野生蘑菇在這個國家的這一地區數量已下降。"},{"en":"In this part of the country means in this particular region or area of the nation.","zh":"in this part of the country意思是在該國家的這個特定地區。"},{"en":"In this part of the country, winters are wetter than summers.","zh":"在這個國家的這一地區，冬天比夏天更潮濕。"},{"en":"Local conditions can make one region very different from another.","zh":"本地條件可以令一個地區與另一地區非常不同。"},{"en":"This phrase limits a statement to a specific area.","zh":"這個短語把說法限制在特定地區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"become more interested in","meaning":"對……越來越感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Restaurants are becoming more interested in locally sourced food.","zh":"餐廳對本地採購食材越來越感興趣。"},{"en":"To become more interested in something means to care about it or want it more than before.","zh":"become more interested in某事，意思是比以前更關心或更想要它。"},{"en":"Students may become more interested in science after doing a real experiment.","zh":"學生做過真實實驗後，可能對科學越來越感興趣。"},{"en":"Interest can increase when people see practical value or new demand.","zh":"當人們看見實用價值或新需求，興趣可以增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a growing attraction or concern.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸增加的吸引或關注。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"locally sourced food","meaning":"本地採購的食材","examples":[{"en":"Restaurants are interested in locally sourced food like wild mushrooms.","zh":"餐廳對野生蘑菇等本地採購食材感興趣。"},{"en":"Locally sourced food is food obtained from nearby farms, producers or natural areas.","zh":"locally sourced food是從附近農場、生產者或自然地區取得的食物。"},{"en":"A café may buy locally sourced vegetables to support farmers in the area.","zh":"咖啡店可能購買本地採購蔬菜，以支持區內農民。"},{"en":"Local sourcing can reduce transport and make food feel fresher and more connected to place.","zh":"本地採購可以減少運輸，並令食物感覺更新鮮和更有地方連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in restaurant and sustainability contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於餐廳和可持續發展語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the biggest problem","meaning":"最大問題","examples":[{"en":"The biggest problem is the construction of many new houses.","zh":"最大問題是興建許多新房屋。"},{"en":"The biggest problem means the most serious or important difficulty.","zh":"the biggest problem意思是最嚴重或最重要的困難。"},{"en":"For many students, the biggest problem in writing is organising ideas clearly.","zh":"對許多學生來說，寫作最大問題是清楚組織想法。"},{"en":"Identifying the biggest problem helps people decide what to solve first.","zh":"找出最大問題幫助人們決定先解決甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase ranks one difficulty above the others.","zh":"這個短語把一個困難排在其他困難之上。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the last ten years","meaning":"在過去十年","examples":[{"en":"Many new houses have been built in the area in the last ten years.","zh":"在過去十年，該區興建了許多新房屋。"},{"en":"In the last ten years means during the most recent ten-year period.","zh":"in the last ten years意思是在最近十年期間。"},{"en":"In the last ten years, many schools have started using online learning platforms.","zh":"在過去十年，許多學校開始使用網上學習平台。"},{"en":"This phrase connects present conditions with recent changes.","zh":"這個短語把當前情況與近期變化連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining how a situation has developed over time.","zh":"當解釋情況如何隨時間發展時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"because of this","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"More water is being taken from rivers and reservoirs because of this.","zh":"因此，更多水正從河流和水塘被取走。"},{"en":"Because of this means as a result of the thing just mentioned.","zh":"because of this意思是由於剛才提到的事情。"},{"en":"The school hall is being repaired; because of this, the concert will be held outside.","zh":"學校禮堂正在維修；因此，音樂會將在戶外舉行。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with its consequence.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"},{"en":"It helps readers follow the logic from one event to the next.","zh":"它幫助讀者跟隨事件之間的邏輯。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be taken from","meaning":"從……取走","examples":[{"en":"More water is being taken from rivers and reservoirs.","zh":"更多水正從河流和水塘被取走。"},{"en":"To be taken from somewhere means to be removed or collected from that place.","zh":"be taken from某處，意思是從該地方被移走或收集。"},{"en":"Books may be taken from the library only after they are borrowed properly.","zh":"書本必須正式借出後，才可從圖書館取走。"},{"en":"If too much water is taken from natural sources, habitats may dry out.","zh":"如果太多水從自然來源被取走，棲地可能乾涸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes removal from a source.","zh":"這個短語描述從來源移除某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rivers and reservoirs","meaning":"河流和水塘","examples":[{"en":"Water is being taken from rivers and reservoirs.","zh":"水正從河流和水塘被取走。"},{"en":"Rivers and reservoirs are natural or man-made water sources used for ecosystems and human needs.","zh":"rivers and reservoirs是用於生態系統和人類需要的天然或人工水源。"},{"en":"Cities may store drinking water in reservoirs and receive fresh water from rivers.","zh":"城市可能把飲用水儲存在水塘，並從河流取得淡水。"},{"en":"Taking too much water from rivers and reservoirs can affect wildlife and farming.","zh":"從河流和水塘取走太多水，可以影響野生動物和農業。"},{"en":"This phrase names important freshwater sources.","zh":"這個短語命名重要淡水來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"mushroom habitats","meaning":"蘑菇棲息地","examples":[{"en":"Mushroom habitats have been destroyed.","zh":"蘑菇棲息地已被破壞。"},{"en":"Mushroom habitats are natural places where mushrooms can grow and reproduce.","zh":"mushroom habitats是蘑菇可以生長和繁殖的自然地方。"},{"en":"Damp woodland and old grassland can be important mushroom habitats.","zh":"潮濕林地和老草地可以是重要蘑菇棲息地。"},{"en":"If habitats are damaged, mushroom varieties may decline or disappear.","zh":"如果棲地受損，蘑菇品種可能減少或消失。"},{"en":"This phrase links mushrooms with the environments they need.","zh":"這個短語把蘑菇與它們需要的環境連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be destroyed","meaning":"被破壞","examples":[{"en":"Some mushroom habitats have been destroyed.","zh":"有些蘑菇棲息地已被破壞。"},{"en":"To be destroyed means to be damaged so badly that something no longer exists or works properly.","zh":"be destroyed意思是被嚴重損壞，以致某物不再存在或無法正常運作。"},{"en":"A playground may be destroyed by a severe storm.","zh":"遊樂場可能被嚴重風暴破壞。"},{"en":"Once a habitat is destroyed, the plants and animals that depend on it may disappear.","zh":"棲地一旦被破壞，依賴它的植物和動物可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious damage, not a small change.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重破壞，而不是小變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a word of advice on","meaning":"關於……的一點建議","examples":[{"en":"Dan gives a word of advice on storing mushrooms.","zh":"Dan給出關於保存蘑菇的一點建議。"},{"en":"A word of advice on something means a short piece of useful guidance about that topic.","zh":"a word of advice on某事，意思是關於該主題的一小段有用指引。"},{"en":"A teacher may give a word of advice on preparing for oral exams.","zh":"老師可能給出關於準備口試的一點建議。"},{"en":"This phrase is used before giving a practical tip or warning.","zh":"這個短語用於給出實用提示或警告之前。"},{"en":"It sounds friendly and helpful rather than formal.","zh":"它聽起來友善而有幫助，不太正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"store mushrooms","meaning":"保存蘑菇","examples":[{"en":"Dan gives advice on how to store mushrooms.","zh":"Dan就如何保存蘑菇給出建議。"},{"en":"To store mushrooms means to keep them properly until they are eaten or cooked.","zh":"store mushrooms意思是妥善保存蘑菇，直到食用或烹調。"},{"en":"Fresh vegetables must be stored carefully so they do not spoil quickly.","zh":"新鮮蔬菜必須小心保存，才不會很快變壞。"},{"en":"Good storage keeps food fresh and reduces waste.","zh":"良好保存方法能保持食物新鮮並減少浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what to do after collecting or buying mushrooms.","zh":"這個短語描述採集或購買蘑菇後要做的事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"brown paper bag","meaning":"啡色紙袋","examples":[{"en":"Mushrooms should be collected in a brown paper bag.","zh":"蘑菇應放入啡色紙袋中採集。"},{"en":"A brown paper bag is a simple paper bag, often used for carrying food or small goods.","zh":"brown paper bag是簡單紙袋，常用於盛載食物或小件貨品。"},{"en":"A bakery may put fresh bread into a brown paper bag.","zh":"麵包店可能把新鮮麵包放進啡色紙袋。"},{"en":"Paper bags allow air to move better than plastic bags, which can trap moisture.","zh":"紙袋比膠袋更能讓空氣流通，而膠袋可能困住濕氣。"},{"en":"This phrase names a practical container for collecting mushrooms.","zh":"這個短語命名採集蘑菇的實用容器。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as soon as","meaning":"一……就……","examples":[{"en":"Put the mushrooms in the fridge as soon as you get home.","zh":"你一回到家，就把蘑菇放入雪櫃。"},{"en":"As soon as means immediately after something happens.","zh":"as soon as意思是在某事發生後立即。"},{"en":"Students should wash their hands as soon as they return from a field trip.","zh":"學生一從實地考察回來，就應洗手。"},{"en":"Acting as soon as possible can prevent food from spoiling or problems from growing.","zh":"盡快行動可以防止食物變壞或問題擴大。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses quick action after a specific event.","zh":"這個短語強調在特定事件後迅速行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"put something in the fridge","meaning":"把……放入雪櫃","examples":[{"en":"Put the mushrooms in the fridge when you get home.","zh":"你回家時，把蘑菇放入雪櫃。"},{"en":"To put something in the fridge means to place it in a cold storage space to keep it fresh.","zh":"put something in the fridge意思是把某物放進冷藏空間以保持新鮮。"},{"en":"After buying milk, you should put it in the fridge quickly.","zh":"買牛奶後，你應盡快把它放入雪櫃。"},{"en":"Cold storage slows down spoilage and helps food last longer.","zh":"冷藏可以減慢變壞速度，幫助食物保存更久。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for everyday food storage.","zh":"這個短語用於日常食物保存。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be fine for","meaning":"可以保存……","examples":[{"en":"The mushrooms will be fine for a couple of days.","zh":"這些蘑菇可以保存幾日。"},{"en":"To be fine for a period means to remain acceptable, safe or usable for that length of time.","zh":"be fine for某段時間，意思是在該段時間內仍可接受、安全或可用。"},{"en":"Cooked rice may be fine for a short time if stored properly in the fridge.","zh":"如果妥善放入雪櫃，熟飯可能可以保存短時間。"},{"en":"Food is not fine forever, so people should still check smell, texture and storage time.","zh":"食物不是永遠都可以保存，所以人們仍應檢查氣味、質感和保存時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how long something remains usable.","zh":"這個短語描述某物能維持可用多久。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a couple of days","meaning":"幾日","examples":[{"en":"The mushrooms will be fine for a couple of days.","zh":"這些蘑菇可以保存幾日。"},{"en":"A couple of days means about two days or a few days.","zh":"a couple of days意思是大約兩天或幾天。"},{"en":"A student may need a couple of days to finish a short project properly.","zh":"學生可能需要幾日才能好好完成短專題。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate short period rather than an exact number.","zh":"這個短語給出大概短時間，而不是精確數字。"},{"en":"It is common in everyday conversation.","zh":"它常見於日常對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"it’s best to","meaning":"最好……","examples":[{"en":"It is best to cook the mushrooms as soon as possible.","zh":"最好盡快烹煮蘑菇。"},{"en":"It’s best to do something means it is the wisest or safest choice.","zh":"it’s best to do something意思是做某事是最明智或最安全的選擇。"},{"en":"It’s best to check the weather before going hiking.","zh":"去遠足前最好查看天氣。"},{"en":"This phrase gives advice without sounding too forceful.","zh":"這個短語提供建議而不會聽起來太強硬。"},{"en":"It often introduces the recommended action.","zh":"它常引入建議採取的行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as soon as possible","meaning":"盡快","examples":[{"en":"Cook the mushrooms as soon as possible.","zh":"盡快烹煮蘑菇。"},{"en":"As soon as possible means with no unnecessary delay.","zh":"as soon as possible意思是不作不必要延誤。"},{"en":"Students should report a lost ID card as soon as possible.","zh":"學生遺失學生證後應盡快報告。"},{"en":"Quick action can reduce risk, waste or inconvenience.","zh":"迅速行動可以減少風險、浪費或不便。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses urgency but does not give an exact time.","zh":"這個短語強調迫切性，但不給出確切時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"after washing them","meaning":"清洗它們之後","examples":[{"en":"Cook the mushrooms after washing them carefully.","zh":"小心清洗蘑菇之後再烹煮。"},{"en":"After washing them means once they have been cleaned with water.","zh":"after washing them意思是在它們已用水清潔之後。"},{"en":"Eat fruit only after washing it, especially if it was bought from an outdoor market.","zh":"水果應在清洗之後才食用，尤其是從露天市場買來的水果。"},{"en":"Washing removes dirt, insects or other unwanted material before cooking or eating.","zh":"清洗能在烹煮或食用前去除泥土、昆蟲或其他不想要的物質。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the order of preparation steps.","zh":"這個短語描述準備步驟的先後次序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"what something tastes like","meaning":"……是甚麼味道","examples":[{"en":"Most people know what a mushroom tastes like.","zh":"大多數人知道蘑菇是甚麼味道。"},{"en":"What something tastes like means the flavour or eating experience it has.","zh":"what something tastes like意思是某物有甚麼味道或食用感受。"},{"en":"A child may ask what durian tastes like before deciding whether to try it.","zh":"孩子在決定是否嘗試榴槤前，可能會問它是甚麼味道。"},{"en":"Describing taste helps people imagine food before eating it.","zh":"描述味道能幫助人在食用前想像食物。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when talking about flavour.","zh":"這個短語用於談論味道。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be surprised by","meaning":"對……感到驚訝","examples":[{"en":"You will be surprised by the huge variety of wild mushrooms.","zh":"你會對野生蘑菇種類之多感到驚訝。"},{"en":"To be surprised by something means to feel unexpected interest, shock or amazement because of it.","zh":"be surprised by某事，意思是因它而感到意外、震驚或驚奇。"},{"en":"A student may be surprised by how many careers use design skills.","zh":"學生可能對有多少職業會用到設計技能感到驚訝。"},{"en":"Surprise happens when reality is different from what people expected.","zh":"當現實與人們預期不同，驚訝就會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces something that may change a person’s expectations.","zh":"這個短語引入可能改變人預期的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"huge variety of","meaning":"種類繁多的……","examples":[{"en":"There is a huge variety of wild mushrooms.","zh":"野生蘑菇種類繁多。"},{"en":"A huge variety of something means a very large number of different types.","zh":"huge variety of某物，意思是有非常多不同種類。"},{"en":"A supermarket may sell a huge variety of snacks from different countries.","zh":"超級市場可能售賣種類繁多、來自不同國家的小食。"},{"en":"Variety gives people more choices, but it can also make identification harder.","zh":"多樣性給人更多選擇，但也可能令辨認更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that there are many kinds.","zh":"這個短語強調種類很多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be adventurous","meaning":"大膽嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Dan encourages people to be adventurous with wild mushrooms.","zh":"Dan鼓勵人們對野生蘑菇大膽嘗試。"},{"en":"To be adventurous means to be willing to try new or unfamiliar things.","zh":"be adventurous意思是願意嘗試新事物或不熟悉的事情。"},{"en":"A student can be adventurous by trying a new sport instead of choosing the same activity every year.","zh":"學生可以透過嘗試新運動，而不是每年選同一活動，來大膽嘗試。"},{"en":"Being adventurous can lead to discovery, but it should still be balanced with safety.","zh":"大膽嘗試可以帶來發現，但仍應與安全平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase praises curiosity and willingness to experiment.","zh":"這個短語讚賞好奇心和實驗意願。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be great in","meaning":"很適合用於……","examples":[{"en":"Wild mushrooms are great in many dishes.","zh":"野生蘑菇很適合用於許多菜式。"},{"en":"To be great in something means to work very well as part of that dish or situation.","zh":"be great in某物，意思是在該菜式或情況中非常合適。"},{"en":"Fresh herbs are great in soup because they add smell and flavour.","zh":"新鮮香草很適合用於湯，因為它們增加香氣和味道。"},{"en":"An ingredient is great in a dish when it improves taste, texture or appearance.","zh":"當食材改善味道、口感或外觀，它就很適合用於某道菜。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when recommending food uses.","zh":"這個短語常用於推薦食物用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"so many dishes","meaning":"很多菜式","examples":[{"en":"Wild mushrooms are great in so many dishes.","zh":"野生蘑菇很適合用於很多菜式。"},{"en":"So many dishes means a large number of different meals or recipes.","zh":"so many dishes意思是大量不同餐點或食譜。"},{"en":"Eggs can be used in so many dishes, from breakfast food to desserts.","zh":"雞蛋可以用於很多菜式，由早餐食物到甜品都有。"},{"en":"When one ingredient works in many dishes, it becomes useful in the kitchen.","zh":"當一種食材適合很多菜式，它在廚房中就變得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses wide cooking possibilities.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛烹調可能性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"stir fries","meaning":"炒菜","examples":[{"en":"Wild mushrooms can be used in stir fries.","zh":"野生蘑菇可以用於炒菜。"},{"en":"Stir fries are dishes cooked quickly in a hot pan while ingredients are stirred.","zh":"stir fries是在熱鍋中快速翻炒食材而成的菜式。"},{"en":"A simple stir fry may include vegetables, noodles and small pieces of meat.","zh":"簡單炒菜可能包括蔬菜、麵條和小塊肉。"},{"en":"Mushrooms work well in stir fries because they cook quickly and absorb flavour.","zh":"蘑菇適合炒菜，因為它們熟得快並能吸收味道。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common cooking style.","zh":"這個短語命名一種常見烹調方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"risottos","meaning":"意式燉飯","examples":[{"en":"Wild mushrooms are great in risottos.","zh":"野生蘑菇很適合用於意式燉飯。"},{"en":"Risottos are creamy Italian rice dishes cooked slowly with liquid.","zh":"risottos是用液體慢慢煮成、口感幼滑的意大利米飯菜式。"},{"en":"A mushroom risotto can be rich and filling because the rice absorbs stock and flavour.","zh":"蘑菇意式燉飯可以濃郁又飽肚，因為米飯吸收高湯和味道。"},{"en":"Ingredients added to risottos should match the soft texture of the rice.","zh":"加入意式燉飯的食材應配合米飯的柔軟口感。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific Italian dish.","zh":"這個短語命名一道特定意大利菜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pasta","meaning":"意粉","examples":[{"en":"Wild mushrooms can be added to pasta dishes.","zh":"野生蘑菇可以加入意粉菜式。"},{"en":"Pasta is an Italian-style food made from dough, often served with sauce.","zh":"pasta是由麵糰製成的意大利式食物，常配醬汁食用。"},{"en":"Students may cook pasta quickly after school because it is simple and filling.","zh":"學生放學後可能快速煮意粉，因為它簡單又飽肚。"},{"en":"Mushrooms can add flavour and texture to pasta sauces.","zh":"蘑菇可以為意粉醬汁增加味道和口感。"},{"en":"This word is common in food and recipe discussions.","zh":"這個詞常見於食物和食譜討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be aware that","meaning":"留意到；知道","examples":[{"en":"Be aware that some people can react badly to certain mushrooms.","zh":"要留意有些人會對某些蘑菇有不良反應。"},{"en":"Be aware that means know this important fact before acting.","zh":"be aware that意思是在行動前知道這個重要事實。"},{"en":"Be aware that the path becomes slippery after rain.","zh":"要留意雨後小路會變得濕滑。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a warning or important reminder.","zh":"這個短語引入警告或重要提醒。"},{"en":"It helps people make safer and more informed decisions.","zh":"它幫助人作出更安全和更有資訊支持的決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"react badly to","meaning":"對……有不良反應","examples":[{"en":"Some people can react badly to certain varieties of mushroom.","zh":"有些人會對某些蘑菇品種有不良反應。"},{"en":"To react badly to something means to have an unpleasant physical or emotional response to it.","zh":"react badly to某物，意思是對它有不愉快的身體或情緒反應。"},{"en":"Some children react badly to dairy products and get stomach pain.","zh":"有些孩子對乳製品有不良反應，會肚痛。"},{"en":"Bad reactions can happen even when a food is safe for most people.","zh":"即使食物對大多數人安全，也可能有人出現不良反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for allergies, sensitivities or strong negative responses.","zh":"這個短語常用於過敏、敏感或強烈負面反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"certain varieties","meaning":"某些品種","examples":[{"en":"Some people react badly to certain varieties of mushroom.","zh":"有些人會對某些蘑菇品種有不良反應。"},{"en":"Certain varieties means particular types within a larger group.","zh":"certain varieties意思是較大類別中的特定種類。"},{"en":"Some people can eat most fruit but react badly to certain varieties of melon.","zh":"有些人可以吃大多數水果，但會對某些蜜瓜品種有不良反應。"},{"en":"Knowing which varieties cause problems helps people avoid only the risky ones.","zh":"知道哪些品種造成問題，可以幫助人只避開有風險的那些。"},{"en":"This phrase is more specific than saying all types.","zh":"這個短語比說所有種類更具體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"it’s a good idea to","meaning":"……是個好主意","examples":[{"en":"It is a good idea not to eat huge quantities at first.","zh":"一開始不要吃大量蘑菇是個好主意。"},{"en":"It’s a good idea to do something means it is sensible or helpful to do it.","zh":"it’s a good idea to do something意思是做某事是明智或有幫助的。"},{"en":"It’s a good idea to save your work before updating your computer.","zh":"更新電腦前先儲存工作是個好主意。"},{"en":"This phrase gives gentle advice rather than a strict order.","zh":"這個短語提供溫和建議，而不是嚴格命令。"},{"en":"It is useful when suggesting a safe or practical action.","zh":"當建議安全或實用行動時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"huge quantities","meaning":"大量","examples":[{"en":"Do not eat huge quantities of wild mushrooms to begin with.","zh":"一開始不要吃大量野生蘑菇。"},{"en":"Huge quantities means very large amounts.","zh":"huge quantities意思是非常大的數量。"},{"en":"Eating huge quantities of sweets can make a child feel sick.","zh":"吃大量糖果可以令孩子感到不適。"},{"en":"Large amounts of unfamiliar food may cause discomfort even if the food is normally safe.","zh":"大量陌生食物即使通常安全，也可能造成不適。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against taking too much.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要攝取過多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"to begin with","meaning":"一開始","examples":[{"en":"Do not eat huge quantities to begin with.","zh":"一開始不要吃大量。"},{"en":"To begin with means at first or in the early stage.","zh":"to begin with意思是起初或在早期階段。"},{"en":"To begin with, new runners should exercise slowly rather than run long distances.","zh":"一開始，新跑手應慢慢運動，而不是跑長距離。"},{"en":"Starting carefully helps people test how their body or situation responds.","zh":"小心開始可以幫助人測試身體或情況如何反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving beginner advice or step-by-step guidance.","zh":"這個短語適合用於給初學者建議或逐步指引。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 11/task-3":[{"front":"a seminar on","meaning":"關於……的研討會","examples":[{"en":"The students attended a seminar on automation and the future of work.","zh":"學生參加了一個關於自動化和工作未來的研討會。"},{"en":"A seminar on a topic is a meeting or lesson where people discuss and learn about that subject.","zh":"seminar on a topic 指人們討論並學習某主題的會議或課堂。"},{"en":"Students may attend a seminar on mental health before exam season.","zh":"學生可能在考試季前參加關於心理健康的研討會。"},{"en":"If a seminar on careers is useful, students can ask questions and plan their next steps.","zh":"如果關於職業的研討會有用，學生可以提問並規劃下一步。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the main subject of a formal discussion.","zh":"這個短語引出正式討論的主要主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"automation","meaning":"自動化","examples":[{"en":"The seminar was about automation and the future of work.","zh":"研討會是關於自動化和工作的未來。"},{"en":"Automation is the use of machines, computers, or technology to do tasks that people used to do.","zh":"automation 指使用機器、電腦或科技完成以往由人做的工作。"},{"en":"A supermarket uses automation when customers scan and pay for goods by themselves.","zh":"當顧客自行掃描和付款時，超級市場就是在使用自動化。"},{"en":"Automation can save time, but it may also change what workers are needed for.","zh":"自動化可以節省時間，但也可能改變哪些工作需要人手。"},{"en":"This word is often used when discussing technology and jobs.","zh":"這個字常用於討論科技和工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the future of work","meaning":"工作的未來","examples":[{"en":"The seminar discussed automation and the future of work.","zh":"研討會討論自動化和工作的未來。"},{"en":"The future of work means how jobs, workplaces, skills, and working lives may change in the years ahead.","zh":"the future of work 指工作、工作場所、技能和職業生活在未來可能如何改變。"},{"en":"A careers teacher may discuss the future of work with students choosing university subjects.","zh":"職業老師可能與選大學科目的學生討論工作的未來。"},{"en":"If technology changes the future of work, young people may need different skills.","zh":"如果科技改變工作的未來，年輕人可能需要不同技能。"},{"en":"This phrase looks ahead at how employment may develop.","zh":"這個短語展望就業如何發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the first industrial revolution","meaning":"第一次工業革命","examples":[{"en":"The seminar looked at the first industrial revolution in Britain.","zh":"研討會探討英國的第一次工業革命。"},{"en":"The first industrial revolution was the period when machines, factories, and new power sources changed production deeply.","zh":"the first industrial revolution 指機器、工廠和新能源深刻改變生產方式的時期。"},{"en":"In history lessons, students learn how the first industrial revolution changed towns, work, and transport.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生學習第一次工業革命如何改變城鎮、工作和交通。"},{"en":"Because machines replaced some hand labour, many workers felt uncertain during this period.","zh":"因為機器取代部分手工勞動，許多工人在這段時期感到不安。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a major historical shift in industry and society.","zh":"這個短語指工業和社會的重大歷史轉變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"react to massive change","meaning":"對巨大變化作出反應","examples":[{"en":"The students learned how people reacted to massive change.","zh":"學生學習人們如何對巨大變化作出反應。"},{"en":"To react to massive change means to respond when life, work, or society changes in a very big way.","zh":"react to massive change 指當生活、工作或社會出現重大改變時作出回應。"},{"en":"Workers may react to massive change by learning new skills or protesting against new rules.","zh":"工人可能透過學習新技能或抗議新規則，對巨大變化作出反應。"},{"en":"If people are not prepared for massive change, fear and anger may grow.","zh":"如果人們沒有準備好面對巨大變化，恐懼和憤怒可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on human response to major disruption.","zh":"這個短語重點在人們對重大衝擊的反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a real eye-opener","meaning":"令人眼界大開的事","examples":[{"en":"The seminar on the first industrial revolution was a real eye-opener.","zh":"關於第一次工業革命的研討會令人眼界大開。"},{"en":"A real eye-opener is something that makes you understand a situation in a new or surprising way.","zh":"a real eye-opener 指令人以新的或令人驚訝的方式理解情況的事情。"},{"en":"Visiting a care home can be a real eye-opener for students who know little about elderly care.","zh":"對不太了解長者照顧的學生來說，參觀安老院可以令人眼界大開。"},{"en":"If a talk reveals facts you had never considered, it can be a real eye-opener.","zh":"如果講座揭示你從未考慮過的事實，它可以令人眼界大開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an experience that changes your understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述改變理解的經歷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"feel about","meaning":"對……有甚麼感受","examples":[{"en":"It was interesting to hear how people felt about automation then.","zh":"聽到當時人們對自動化有甚麼感受很有趣。"},{"en":"To feel about something means to have an opinion or emotion about it.","zh":"feel about something 指對某事有某種看法或情緒。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students how they feel about online learning after a term.","zh":"老師可能在一個學期後問學生對網上學習有甚麼感受。"},{"en":"If people feel worried about technology, they may resist using it.","zh":"如果人們對科技感到擔心，他們可能抗拒使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about attitudes, not physical feelings.","zh":"這個短語詢問態度，而不是身體感覺。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"face challenges","meaning":"面對挑戰","examples":[{"en":"The workers faced many challenges during the industrial revolution.","zh":"工人在工業革命期間面對許多挑戰。"},{"en":"To face challenges means to deal with difficult situations or problems.","zh":"face challenges 指處理困難情況或問題。"},{"en":"New students may face challenges when they move to a larger school.","zh":"新生轉到較大的學校時可能面對挑戰。"},{"en":"If workers face challenges without support, stress and mistakes may increase.","zh":"如果工人在沒有支援下面對挑戰，壓力和錯誤可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes having to handle difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述必須處理困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"start with","meaning":"由……開始","examples":[{"en":"The protests first started with workers in the textile industry.","zh":"抗議最初由紡織業工人開始。"},{"en":"To start with someone or something means to begin from that person, group, or point.","zh":"start with someone or something 指由某人、某群體或某一點開始。"},{"en":"A teacher may start with simple examples before explaining a difficult grammar rule.","zh":"老師可能先由簡單例子開始，再解釋困難文法規則。"},{"en":"If a campaign starts with a small group, it may later spread to others.","zh":"如果運動由一小群人開始，之後可能擴散到其他人。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the beginning point of an action or discussion.","zh":"這個短語顯示行動或討論的起點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"workers in the textile industry","meaning":"紡織業工人","examples":[{"en":"The first protests started with workers in the textile industry.","zh":"最早的抗議由紡織業工人開始。"},{"en":"Workers in the textile industry are people who make cloth, clothing, or fabric products.","zh":"workers in the textile industry 指製造布料、衣服或紡織品的人。"},{"en":"Workers in the textile industry may operate sewing machines, dye cloth, or check fabric quality.","zh":"紡織業工人可能操作縫紉機、染布或檢查布料質素。"},{"en":"If new machines reduce the need for hand labour, textile workers may fear job loss.","zh":"如果新機器減少對手工勞動的需要，紡織工人可能害怕失業。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a group of workers in cloth production.","zh":"這個短語指出布料生產行業中的工人群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"protesting workers","meaning":"抗議工人","examples":[{"en":"The protesting workers were called the Luddites.","zh":"這些抗議工人被稱為 Luddites。"},{"en":"Protesting workers are workers who publicly object to something they think is unfair or harmful.","zh":"protesting workers 指公開反對他們認為不公平或有害事情的工人。"},{"en":"Protesting workers may gather outside a factory to demand safer conditions.","zh":"抗議工人可能聚集在工廠外，要求更安全的工作條件。"},{"en":"If protesting workers feel ignored, their actions may become louder or more disruptive.","zh":"如果抗議工人覺得被忽視，他們的行動可能變得更大聲或更具干擾性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes workers taking action to express opposition.","zh":"這個短語描述工人採取行動表達反對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be called the Luddites","meaning":"被稱為 Luddites","examples":[{"en":"The workers who destroyed machines were called the Luddites.","zh":"破壞機器的工人被稱為 Luddites。"},{"en":"To be called the Luddites means to be given the name used for workers who opposed certain machines in early industrial Britain.","zh":"be called the Luddites 指被冠以早期英國工業時代反對某些機器的工人名稱。"},{"en":"In history class, students learn that the Luddites feared machines would damage their livelihoods.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生學到 Luddites 擔心機器會損害他們的生計。"},{"en":"If someone today is called a Luddite, it may mean they resist new technology.","zh":"如果今天有人被稱為 Luddite，可能表示他抗拒新科技。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a historical group with fear of technological change.","zh":"這個短語把歷史群體與對科技變化的恐懼連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"knitting machines","meaning":"針織機","examples":[{"en":"The Luddites destroyed their knitting machines.","zh":"Luddites 破壞了他們的針織機。"},{"en":"Knitting machines are machines used to make knitted cloth or clothing more quickly than hand knitting.","zh":"knitting machines 指比手工編織更快製作針織布料或衣物的機器。"},{"en":"A clothing factory may use knitting machines to produce jumpers in large numbers.","zh":"服裝工廠可能使用針織機大量生產冷衫。"},{"en":"If knitting machines replace skilled hand workers, those workers may fear losing income.","zh":"如果針織機取代熟練手工工人，這些工人可能害怕失去收入。"},{"en":"This phrase names machines used in textile production.","zh":"這個短語指出紡織生產中使用的機器。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be worried about losing one’s job","meaning":"擔心失去工作","examples":[{"en":"The Luddites were worried about losing their jobs.","zh":"Luddites 擔心失去工作。"},{"en":"To be worried about losing one’s job means to fear becoming unemployed.","zh":"be worried about losing one’s job 指害怕變成失業。"},{"en":"A cashier may be worried about losing her job when a shop installs self-service machines.","zh":"當店舖安裝自助機時，收銀員可能擔心失去工作。"},{"en":"If workers are worried about losing their jobs, they may ask for retraining or protection.","zh":"如果工人擔心失去工作，他們可能要求再培訓或保障。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fear about employment security.","zh":"這個短語描述對就業安全的恐懼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ultimately","meaning":"最終","examples":[{"en":"Ultimately, the Luddites did not achieve anything.","zh":"最終，Luddites 沒有達成任何成果。"},{"en":"Ultimately means in the end, after everything has been considered or after events have finished.","zh":"ultimately 指最終，在所有事情被考慮後或事件結束後。"},{"en":"The debate was long, but ultimately the school decided to keep the old timetable.","zh":"辯論很長，但最終學校決定保留舊時間表。"},{"en":"If a plan fails ultimately, early effort may still teach useful lessons.","zh":"如果計劃最終失敗，早期努力仍可能帶來有用教訓。"},{"en":"This word introduces the final result.","zh":"這個字引出最後結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"achieve anything","meaning":"達成任何成果","examples":[{"en":"The Luddites did not achieve anything through their protests.","zh":"Luddites 沒有透過抗議達成任何成果。"},{"en":"To achieve anything means to succeed in getting a result, goal, or change.","zh":"achieve anything 指成功取得結果、目標或改變。"},{"en":"A student may feel he did not achieve anything if he studies without a clear plan.","zh":"如果學生沒有清晰計劃地溫習，他可能覺得自己沒有達成任何成果。"},{"en":"If a protest achieves nothing, people may need a different strategy.","zh":"如果抗議沒有達成任何成果，人們可能需要不同策略。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether effort leads to a real result.","zh":"這個短語重點在努力是否帶來實際結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"industrialisation","meaning":"工業化","examples":[{"en":"Industrialisation created more jobs than it destroyed.","zh":"工業化創造的工作比它摧毀的更多。"},{"en":"Industrialisation is the process in which factories, machines, and large-scale production become central to an economy.","zh":"industrialisation 指工廠、機器和大規模生產成為經濟核心的過程。"},{"en":"Industrialisation changed many villages because people moved to cities for factory work.","zh":"工業化改變了許多村莊，因為人們搬到城市做工廠工作。"},{"en":"If industrialisation grows quickly, societies may gain jobs but also face pollution and inequality.","zh":"如果工業化快速發展，社會可能獲得工作，但也面對污染和不平等。"},{"en":"This word describes a major shift from hand production to machine-based industry.","zh":"這個字描述由手工生產轉向機器工業的重大轉變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"create more jobs than it destroyed","meaning":"創造的工作比摧毀的更多","examples":[{"en":"Industrialisation created more jobs than it destroyed.","zh":"工業化創造的工作比摧毀的更多。"},{"en":"To create more jobs than it destroyed means to produce a net increase in employment despite removing some old jobs.","zh":"create more jobs than it destroyed 指雖然消除了一些舊工作，但整體就業增加。"},{"en":"Online shopping destroyed some shop jobs but created more delivery and warehouse jobs in some cities.","zh":"網上購物在一些城市消除了部分店舖工作，但創造更多送貨和倉庫工作。"},{"en":"If new technology creates more jobs than it destroys, workers may still need retraining.","zh":"如果新科技創造的工作比摧毀的更多，工人仍可能需要再培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase compares jobs gained with jobs lost.","zh":"這個短語比較新增職位與流失職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"seem a positive thing","meaning":"看起來是正面的事情","examples":[{"en":"Industrialisation probably did not seem a positive thing at the time.","zh":"工業化在當時可能並不看起來是正面的事情。"},{"en":"To seem a positive thing means to appear good or beneficial.","zh":"seem a positive thing 指看起來是好的或有益的。"},{"en":"A new school rule may not seem a positive thing until students see fewer arguments.","zh":"新校規在學生看到爭吵減少前，可能不覺得是正面的事情。"},{"en":"If change brings fear first, it may not seem positive even if benefits come later.","zh":"如果改變先帶來恐懼，即使好處後來出現，它也可能看起來不正面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how something appears to people.","zh":"這個短語描述某事在人們眼中如何呈現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at the time","meaning":"當時","examples":[{"en":"Industrialisation probably felt frightening at the time.","zh":"工業化在當時可能令人感到害怕。"},{"en":"At the time means during that particular period in the past or situation being discussed.","zh":"at the time 指在過去或正在討論的特定時期。"},{"en":"At the time, many students thought online lessons were strange and difficult.","zh":"當時，許多學生覺得網課奇怪又困難。"},{"en":"If we judge a decision at the time, we should remember what people knew then.","zh":"如果我們按當時情況判斷決定，就應記得人們那時知道甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase places feelings or events in their original context.","zh":"這個短語把感受或事件放回原本背景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I can see why","meaning":"我能理解為甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The young man can see why the Luddites felt threatened.","zh":"這名年輕男子能理解為甚麼 Luddites 感到受威脅。"},{"en":"I can see why means I understand the reason for someone’s feeling or action.","zh":"I can see why 指我明白某人感受或行動背後的原因。"},{"en":"I can see why students worry when an exam format suddenly changes.","zh":"我能理解為甚麼學生在考試形式突然改變時會擔心。"},{"en":"If you can see why someone is upset, you may respond with more empathy.","zh":"如果你能理解某人為何不安，你可能會更有同理心地回應。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses understanding even if you may not fully agree.","zh":"這個短語表示理解，即使你未必完全同意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"feel threatened","meaning":"感到受威脅","examples":[{"en":"The Luddites felt threatened by automation.","zh":"Luddites 因自動化而感到受威脅。"},{"en":"To feel threatened means to feel that something may harm your safety, job, status, or way of life.","zh":"feel threatened 指感到某事可能傷害自己的安全、工作、地位或生活方式。"},{"en":"A small shop may feel threatened when a large chain opens nearby.","zh":"當大型連鎖店在附近開業，小店可能感到受威脅。"},{"en":"If workers feel threatened by new machines, training can reduce fear.","zh":"如果工人因新機器感到受威脅，培訓可以減少恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sense of danger or insecurity.","zh":"這個短語描述危險感或不安全感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"feel the same","meaning":"有同樣感受","examples":[{"en":"The young woman thinks she would have felt the same.","zh":"這名年輕女子認為自己也會有同樣感受。"},{"en":"To feel the same means to have the same emotion or opinion as someone else.","zh":"feel the same 指與其他人有相同情緒或看法。"},{"en":"If my job were replaced by a machine, I might feel the same as those workers.","zh":"如果我的工作被機器取代，我可能會和那些工人有同樣感受。"},{"en":"When people feel the same, they may find it easier to support each other.","zh":"當人們有同樣感受，他們可能更容易互相支持。"},{"en":"This phrase shows shared feeling or agreement.","zh":"這個短語顯示共同感受或同意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the discussion about","meaning":"關於……的討論","examples":[{"en":"The discussion about the future of work was optimistic.","zh":"關於工作未來的討論是樂觀的。"},{"en":"The discussion about a topic is the part of a conversation focused on that subject.","zh":"discussion about a topic 指對話中集中於某主題的部分。"},{"en":"The discussion about school lunches became lively when students shared their experiences.","zh":"當學生分享經歷時，關於學校午餐的討論變得熱烈。"},{"en":"If a discussion about a problem includes solutions, people may feel more hopeful.","zh":"如果關於問題的討論包括解決方法，人們可能更有希望。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what people are talking about.","zh":"這個短語指出人們正在談論甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"optimistic for a change","meaning":"難得樂觀","examples":[{"en":"The discussion about the future of work was optimistic for a change.","zh":"關於工作未來的討論難得樂觀。"},{"en":"Optimistic for a change means unusually hopeful compared with what normally happens.","zh":"optimistic for a change 指與平常相比，少有地帶有希望。"},{"en":"The news about the environment was optimistic for a change after weeks of bad reports.","zh":"經過幾星期壞消息後，關於環境的新聞難得樂觀。"},{"en":"If a topic is usually negative, an optimistic view can feel refreshing.","zh":"如果一個題目平時很負面，樂觀看法會令人耳目一新。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests pleasant surprise at a hopeful tone.","zh":"這個短語暗示對有希望語氣的愉快驚喜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the idea that","meaning":"……這個想法","examples":[{"en":"The young woman likes the idea that work will involve fewer boring tasks.","zh":"這名年輕女子喜歡工作會包含較少沉悶任務這個想法。"},{"en":"The idea that introduces a belief, possibility, or proposal.","zh":"the idea that 用來引出一個信念、可能性或建議。"},{"en":"Many students like the idea that lessons can include more real-life projects.","zh":"許多學生喜歡課堂可以包括更多真實生活專題這個想法。"},{"en":"If people like the idea that machines can remove boring tasks, they may support automation.","zh":"如果人們喜歡機器可以消除沉悶工作這個想法，他們可能支持自動化。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a thought for discussion.","zh":"這個短語引出可供討論的想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"involve doing","meaning":"涉及做……","examples":[{"en":"Future work may not involve doing boring, repetitive tasks.","zh":"未來工作可能不涉及做沉悶而重複的任務。"},{"en":"To involve doing something means to include that action as part of a job or activity.","zh":"involve doing something 指包括某動作作為工作或活動的一部分。"},{"en":"A nurse’s work may involve helping patients wash, eat, and take medicine.","zh":"護士工作可能涉及幫助病人洗澡、進食和服藥。"},{"en":"If a job involves doing the same task all day, workers may become tired or bored.","zh":"如果一份工作涉及整天做同一任務，工人可能感到疲倦或沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what an activity includes.","zh":"這個短語解釋某活動包括甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"boring, repetitive tasks","meaning":"沉悶而重複的工作","examples":[{"en":"Robots may take over boring, repetitive tasks.","zh":"機械人可能接管沉悶而重複的工作。"},{"en":"Boring, repetitive tasks are dull jobs that require the same action again and again.","zh":"boring, repetitive tasks 指沉悶、需要一再重複同一動作的工作。"},{"en":"Entering hundreds of identical numbers into a spreadsheet can be a boring, repetitive task.","zh":"把數百個相同類型的數字輸入試算表，可以是沉悶而重複的工作。"},{"en":"If machines do boring, repetitive tasks, people may have more time for creative or caring work.","zh":"如果機器處理沉悶重複工作，人們可能有更多時間做創意或照顧工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work that is monotonous and repeated.","zh":"這個短語描述單調而反覆的工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"negative stuff about","meaning":"關於……的負面東西","examples":[{"en":"People usually hear negative stuff about the future.","zh":"人們通常聽到關於未來的負面東西。"},{"en":"Negative stuff about a topic means bad, worrying, or pessimistic information about it.","zh":"negative stuff about a topic 指關於某主題的壞消息、憂慮或悲觀看法。"},{"en":"Students often hear negative stuff about exams, such as stress and competition.","zh":"學生常聽到關於考試的負面東西，例如壓力和競爭。"},{"en":"If people hear only negative stuff about technology, they may ignore its benefits.","zh":"如果人們只聽到關於科技的負面東西，可能會忽略其好處。"},{"en":"This informal phrase refers to unpleasant information or opinions.","zh":"這個非正式短語指令人不快的資料或意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a bit too optimistic","meaning":"有點過分樂觀","examples":[{"en":"The young man thinks the seminar was a bit too optimistic.","zh":"這名年輕男子認為研討會有點過分樂觀。"},{"en":"A bit too optimistic means slightly more hopeful than seems realistic.","zh":"a bit too optimistic 指比現實情況稍微更抱希望。"},{"en":"A student may be a bit too optimistic if he expects to finish a long essay in ten minutes.","zh":"如果學生期望十分鐘內完成長文，他可能有點過分樂觀。"},{"en":"If a plan ignores possible problems, it may sound a bit too optimistic.","zh":"如果計劃忽略可能問題，它可能聽起來有點過分樂觀。"},{"en":"This phrase gently criticises excessive hopefulness.","zh":"這個短語溫和批評過度樂觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"I can’t see how","meaning":"我看不出怎樣……","examples":[{"en":"The young man cannot see how people will have more leisure time.","zh":"這名年輕男子看不出人們怎樣會有更多閒暇時間。"},{"en":"I can’t see how means I do not understand how something is possible.","zh":"I can’t see how 指我不明白某事如何可能發生。"},{"en":"I can’t see how we can finish the project today if half the team is absent.","zh":"如果一半組員缺席，我看不出我們今天怎樣完成項目。"},{"en":"If someone says this, they are usually questioning the logic of an idea.","zh":"如果某人這樣說，他通常是在質疑某想法的邏輯。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses doubt about possibility.","zh":"這個短語表達對可能性的懷疑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be about to","meaning":"即將……","examples":[{"en":"He cannot see how people are about to have more leisure time.","zh":"他看不出人們怎樣即將有更多閒暇時間。"},{"en":"To be about to do something means to be going to do it very soon.","zh":"be about to do something 指很快就會做某事。"},{"en":"The lesson is about to begin, so students should sit down.","zh":"課堂即將開始，所以學生應坐下。"},{"en":"If a company is about to change its system, staff need clear instructions.","zh":"如果公司即將更改系統，員工需要清楚指示。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that is expected to happen soon.","zh":"這個短語描述預期很快發生的事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"leisure time","meaning":"閒暇時間","examples":[{"en":"Automation may not necessarily give people more leisure time.","zh":"自動化未必一定會給人更多閒暇時間。"},{"en":"Leisure time is free time when people are not working or doing necessary duties.","zh":"leisure time 指人們不用工作或處理必要職責的自由時間。"},{"en":"Students may use leisure time to play sports, read, or meet friends.","zh":"學生可能用閒暇時間做運動、閱讀或見朋友。"},{"en":"If working hours become longer, people have less leisure time for rest and family.","zh":"如果工作時間變長，人們用於休息和家庭的閒暇時間就會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes time for relaxation and personal activities.","zh":"這個短語描述放鬆和個人活動的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"all the evidence shows","meaning":"所有證據顯示","examples":[{"en":"All the evidence shows that people are spending longer at work.","zh":"所有證據顯示人們工作時間更長。"},{"en":"All the evidence shows means the available facts strongly point to the same conclusion.","zh":"all the evidence shows 指現有事實強烈指向同一結論。"},{"en":"All the evidence shows that students sleep better when they stop using phones late at night.","zh":"所有證據顯示，學生深夜停止使用手機後睡得更好。"},{"en":"If all the evidence shows a problem, decision-makers should not ignore it.","zh":"如果所有證據顯示有問題，決策者不應忽視它。"},{"en":"This phrase gives strong support to a claim.","zh":"這個短語為主張提供強力支持。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"spend longer than ever at work","meaning":"工作時間比以往更長","examples":[{"en":"People are spending longer than ever at work.","zh":"人們工作時間比以往更長。"},{"en":"To spend longer than ever at work means to work more hours than in the past.","zh":"spend longer than ever at work 指工作時數比過去更多。"},{"en":"Some office workers spend longer than ever at work because emails follow them home.","zh":"有些辦公室員工工作時間比以往更長，因為電郵會跟着他們回家。"},{"en":"If people spend longer at work, stress and family conflict may increase.","zh":"如果人們工作時間更長，壓力和家庭衝突可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rise in working time.","zh":"這個短語描述工作時間上升。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lower unemployment","meaning":"較低失業率","examples":[{"en":"The students are unsure whether automation will lead to lower unemployment.","zh":"學生不肯定自動化是否會帶來較低失業率。"},{"en":"Lower unemployment means fewer people are without jobs.","zh":"lower unemployment 指沒有工作的人較少。"},{"en":"A new factory may lead to lower unemployment if it hires many local workers.","zh":"如果新工廠聘請很多本地工人，可能帶來較低失業率。"},{"en":"If technology creates new jobs faster than it removes old ones, unemployment may fall.","zh":"如果科技創造新工作比淘汰舊工作更快，失業率可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement in the job market.","zh":"這個短語描述就業市場改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"I’m not so sure about that","meaning":"我對此不太肯定","examples":[{"en":"The young woman is not so sure about lower unemployment.","zh":"這名年輕女子對較低失業率不太肯定。"},{"en":"I’m not so sure about that means I doubt that point or do not fully agree.","zh":"I’m not so sure about that 指我懷疑那一點，或不完全同意。"},{"en":"If someone says online learning is always better, I’m not so sure about that.","zh":"如果有人說網上學習永遠更好，我對此不太肯定。"},{"en":"This phrase is a polite way to express uncertainty or disagreement.","zh":"這個短語是表達不確定或不同意的禮貌方式。"},{"en":"It softens criticism by avoiding a direct “you are wrong.”","zh":"它避免直接說「你錯了」，令批評較溫和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the long term","meaning":"長遠而言","examples":[{"en":"Lower unemployment may happen in the long term.","zh":"長遠而言，較低失業率可能會出現。"},{"en":"In the long term means over a long future period, not immediately.","zh":"in the long term 指在較長的未來時期內，而不是立即。"},{"en":"In the long term, regular reading can improve writing more than last-minute memorisation.","zh":"長遠而言，定期閱讀比臨急背誦更能改善寫作。"},{"en":"If a policy is painful now but useful in the long term, people may still support it.","zh":"如果政策現在痛苦但長遠有用，人們仍可能支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts future results with short-term effects.","zh":"這個短語把未來結果與短期影響作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the foreseeable future","meaning":"在可見將來","examples":[{"en":"Lower unemployment is unlikely in the foreseeable future.","zh":"在可見將來，較低失業率不太可能出現。"},{"en":"In the foreseeable future means in the period ahead that people can reasonably predict.","zh":"in the foreseeable future 指人們合理地能預測的未來一段時間。"},{"en":"The school has no plan to build a swimming pool in the foreseeable future.","zh":"學校在可見將來沒有興建泳池的計劃。"},{"en":"If change is unlikely in the foreseeable future, people should prepare for current conditions to continue.","zh":"如果變化在可見將來不太可能，人們應準備現況會持續。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the near or predictable future.","zh":"這個短語指較近或可預見的未來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be expected to","meaning":"被期望；被要求","examples":[{"en":"Most people will be expected to work until they are older.","zh":"大多數人會被期望工作到年紀較大。"},{"en":"To be expected to do something means people think or require that you should do it.","zh":"be expected to do something 指人們認為或要求你應該做某事。"},{"en":"Students are expected to arrive on time for exams.","zh":"學生被要求準時到達考場。"},{"en":"If workers are expected to learn new software, companies should provide training.","zh":"如果員工被期望學習新軟件，公司應提供培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social, school, or workplace expectation.","zh":"這個短語描述社會、學校或工作場所期望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"work until they are much older","meaning":"工作到年紀更大","examples":[{"en":"Many people may have to work until they are much older.","zh":"許多人可能要工作到年紀更大。"},{"en":"To work until people are much older means to continue employment later into old age.","zh":"work until people are much older 指繼續工作到較年老階段。"},{"en":"Some people work until they are much older because retirement savings are not enough.","zh":"有些人因退休儲蓄不足而工作到年紀更大。"},{"en":"If people live longer, governments may expect them to work for more years.","zh":"如果人們壽命更長，政府可能期望他們工作更多年。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a longer working life.","zh":"這個短語描述更長的職業生涯。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"live much longer","meaning":"壽命長得多","examples":[{"en":"People are living much longer than before.","zh":"人們比以前壽命長得多。"},{"en":"To live much longer means to have a much longer lifespan than people had in the past.","zh":"live much longer 指壽命比過去的人長很多。"},{"en":"Better healthcare can help people live much longer.","zh":"更好的醫療可以幫助人們壽命長得多。"},{"en":"If people live much longer, pensions and care services need more planning.","zh":"如果人們壽命長得多，退休金和護理服務就需要更多規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increased life expectancy.","zh":"這個短語描述預期壽命增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"that’s already happening","meaning":"這已經在發生","examples":[{"en":"The young man says that longer working lives are already happening.","zh":"這名年輕男子說更長的工作人生已經在發生。"},{"en":"That’s already happening means the change has started and is not just a future possibility.","zh":"that’s already happening 指變化已開始，而不只是未來可能性。"},{"en":"Some people think online shopping will grow, but that is already happening.","zh":"有些人認為網上購物將會增長，但這已經在發生。"},{"en":"If a trend is already happening, people should respond now rather than wait.","zh":"如果趨勢已經在發生，人們應現在回應，而不是等待。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a current reality.","zh":"這個短語指出當前現實。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"technology has changed","meaning":"科技已經改變……","examples":[{"en":"The students discussed how technology has changed some jobs.","zh":"學生討論科技如何已經改變一些工作。"},{"en":"Technology has changed something means new tools or systems have altered how it works.","zh":"technology has changed something 指新工具或系統已改變某事的運作方式。"},{"en":"Technology has changed schoolwork because students now submit assignments online.","zh":"科技已經改變學校功課，因為學生現在網上提交作業。"},{"en":"If technology changes a job, workers may need new skills or responsibilities.","zh":"如果科技改變一份工作，員工可能需要新技能或新責任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the effect of modern tools on life or work.","zh":"這個短語描述現代工具對生活或工作的影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be likely to change","meaning":"很可能改變","examples":[{"en":"Some jobs are likely to change in the near future.","zh":"一些工作在不久將來很可能改變。"},{"en":"To be likely to change means there is a strong chance that something will become different.","zh":"be likely to change 指某事很有可能變得不同。"},{"en":"School rules are likely to change if many parents complain.","zh":"如果許多家長投訴，校規很可能改變。"},{"en":"If a job uses computers heavily, it is likely to change when software improves.","zh":"如果一份工作大量使用電腦，軟件改善時它很可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses probable change.","zh":"這個短語表達可能性很高的變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the near future","meaning":"在不久將來","examples":[{"en":"Technology will change many jobs in the near future.","zh":"科技將在不久將來改變許多工作。"},{"en":"In the near future means soon or within the next short period of time.","zh":"in the near future 指很快或在接下來較短時間內。"},{"en":"The school plans to open a new library in the near future.","zh":"學校計劃在不久將來開設新圖書館。"},{"en":"If a change is coming in the near future, workers should prepare early.","zh":"如果變化在不久將來到來，員工應及早準備。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a time not far ahead.","zh":"這個短語指不遠的未來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"technological innovations","meaning":"科技創新","examples":[{"en":"Technological innovations have changed the work of accountants.","zh":"科技創新已改變會計師的工作。"},{"en":"Technological innovations are new tools, systems, or methods created through technology.","zh":"technological innovations 指透過科技創造的新工具、系統或方法。"},{"en":"Mobile payment is a technological innovation that changed how people shop.","zh":"流動支付是一項改變人們購物方式的科技創新。"},{"en":"If technological innovations spread quickly, old work habits may disappear.","zh":"如果科技創新快速普及，舊工作習慣可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes new technology that changes how people live or work.","zh":"這個短語描述改變人們生活或工作的科技新事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"put someone out of a job","meaning":"令某人失業","examples":[{"en":"Technological innovations have not put accountants out of a job.","zh":"科技創新並沒有令會計師失業。"},{"en":"To put someone out of a job means to cause that person to lose employment.","zh":"put someone out of a job 指導致某人失去工作。"},{"en":"A factory machine may put some workers out of a job if no retraining is offered.","zh":"如果沒有提供再培訓，工廠機器可能令一些工人失業。"},{"en":"If technology changes tasks instead of removing workers, it may not put people out of a job.","zh":"如果科技只是改變任務而不是淘汰工人，它未必會令人失業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes job loss caused by change.","zh":"這個短語描述由變化造成的失業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, there are more accountants than ever.","zh":"事實上，會計師比以往更多。"},{"en":"In fact introduces information that strengthens, corrects, or contrasts with what was just said.","zh":"in fact 用來引出加強、修正或對比前文的資料。"},{"en":"The shop looks small; in fact, it has a large storage room upstairs.","zh":"那間店看起來很小；事實上，樓上有很大的儲物室。"},{"en":"If a fact is surprising, “in fact” helps signal the correction.","zh":"如果某事實令人意外，in fact 可以提示這是修正。"},{"en":"This phrase often reveals the real situation.","zh":"這個短語常揭示真實情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"more than ever","meaning":"比以往更多","examples":[{"en":"There are more accountants than ever.","zh":"會計師比以往更多。"},{"en":"More than ever means more than at any previous time.","zh":"more than ever 指比過去任何時候都多。"},{"en":"Students need digital skills more than ever because schoolwork often happens online.","zh":"學生比以往更需要數碼技能，因為學校功課常在網上進行。"},{"en":"If a service is needed more than ever, demand for workers in that area may rise.","zh":"如果某服務比以往更被需要，該領域的工人需求可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a record or unusually high level.","zh":"這個短語強調創紀錄或異常高的水平。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in demand","meaning":"需求很高","examples":[{"en":"Accountants are still really in demand.","zh":"會計師仍然需求很高。"},{"en":"To be in demand means many people or organisations want or need something or someone.","zh":"be in demand 指許多人或機構想要或需要某物或某人。"},{"en":"Nurses are in demand when hospitals need more staff.","zh":"當醫院需要更多人手時，護士需求很高。"},{"en":"If a skill is in demand, people who have it may find jobs more easily.","zh":"如果某項技能需求很高，擁有它的人可能較容易找到工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong market need.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈市場需求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"become far more efficient","meaning":"變得有效率得多","examples":[{"en":"Accountants have become far more efficient because of technology.","zh":"會計師因科技而變得有效率得多。"},{"en":"To become far more efficient means to do work much faster or with less waste than before.","zh":"become far more efficient 指工作比以前快得多，或浪費少得多。"},{"en":"A school office became far more efficient after forms moved online.","zh":"表格轉到網上後，學校辦公室變得有效率得多。"},{"en":"If workers become more efficient, they can complete more tasks in less time.","zh":"如果員工變得更有效率，就能用較少時間完成更多任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major improvement in productivity.","zh":"這個短語描述生產力大幅改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"compared to","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"There are twenty times more accountants compared to the 19th century.","zh":"與十九世紀相比，現在會計師數量多二十倍。"},{"en":"Compared to means measured or considered against another time, number, or situation.","zh":"compared to 指與另一時間、數字或情況作比較。"},{"en":"This year’s school fair had more visitors compared to last year.","zh":"與去年相比，今年學校嘉年華有更多訪客。"},{"en":"If data is compared to the past, changes become clearer.","zh":"如果數據與過去相比，變化會更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a comparison.","zh":"這個短語引出比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the 19th century","meaning":"十九世紀","examples":[{"en":"There are far more accountants now than in the 19th century.","zh":"現在的會計師遠多於十九世紀。"},{"en":"The 19th century means the years from 1801 to 1900.","zh":"the 19th century 指1801年至1900年。"},{"en":"Students study the 19th century to understand industrialisation and empire.","zh":"學生研究十九世紀，以理解工業化和帝國發展。"},{"en":"If we compare today with the 19th century, changes in work and technology look huge.","zh":"如果我們把今天與十九世紀相比，工作和科技變化會顯得巨大。"},{"en":"This phrase names a historical period.","zh":"這個短語指出一個歷史時期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"I’d never have thought that","meaning":"我從未想過","examples":[{"en":"The young man had never thought that demand for hairdressing would rise so much.","zh":"這名年輕男子從未想過美髮服務需求會上升這麼多。"},{"en":"I’d never have thought that means I find the information surprising because I had not expected it.","zh":"I’d never have thought that 指我覺得資料令人驚訝，因為我原本沒有預期。"},{"en":"I’d never have thought that a small habit like sleeping earlier could improve my marks.","zh":"我從未想過早睡這樣的小習慣可以改善成績。"},{"en":"If a fact changes your assumptions, you might say you had never thought that before.","zh":"如果某事實改變你的假設，你可能說自己從未想過。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses surprise at new information.","zh":"這個短語表達對新資料的驚訝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"demand for","meaning":"對……的需求","examples":[{"en":"Demand for hairdressing has gone up sharply.","zh":"對美髮服務的需求大幅上升。"},{"en":"Demand for something is how much people want or need that product or service.","zh":"demand for something 指人們對某產品或服務有多想要或需要。"},{"en":"Demand for tutors often rises before major exams.","zh":"大型考試前，對補習老師的需求常會上升。"},{"en":"If demand for a service grows, more workers may enter that field.","zh":"如果對某服務的需求增加，更多工人可能進入該行業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes market need.","zh":"這個短語描述市場需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hairdressing","meaning":"美髮服務","examples":[{"en":"Demand for hairdressing has increased over the last hundred years.","zh":"在過去一百年，對美髮服務的需求增加了。"},{"en":"Hairdressing is the work of cutting, styling, colouring, or caring for people’s hair.","zh":"hairdressing 指剪髮、造型、染髮或護理頭髮的工作。"},{"en":"A hairdressing salon may offer haircuts, washing, colouring, and styling.","zh":"美髮店可能提供剪髮、洗髮、染髮和造型服務。"},{"en":"If people have more money for personal services, demand for hairdressing may rise.","zh":"如果人們有更多錢花在個人服務上，美髮服務需求可能上升。"},{"en":"This word describes a skilled personal service.","zh":"這個字描述一種熟練的個人服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"go up","meaning":"上升；增加","examples":[{"en":"Demand for hairdressing has gone up a lot.","zh":"對美髮服務的需求增加了很多。"},{"en":"To go up means to increase or rise.","zh":"go up 指增加或上升。"},{"en":"Bus fares may go up when fuel prices increase.","zh":"當燃油價格上升時，巴士票價可能上升。"},{"en":"If demand goes up, businesses may hire more staff or raise prices.","zh":"如果需求增加，企業可能聘請更多員工或提高價格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upward change.","zh":"這個短語描述向上的變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the last hundred years","meaning":"在過去一百年","examples":[{"en":"Demand for hairdressing has risen in the last hundred years.","zh":"在過去一百年，對美髮服務的需求上升了。"},{"en":"In the last hundred years means during the most recent period of one hundred years.","zh":"in the last hundred years 指在最近一百年的時期內。"},{"en":"In the last hundred years, transport has changed from horse carts to high-speed trains.","zh":"在過去一百年，交通由馬車變成高速列車。"},{"en":"If a trend continues for a hundred years, it shows a deep social change.","zh":"如果趨勢持續一百年，它顯示深層社會變化。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a long historical time frame.","zh":"這個短語提供長期歷史時間框架。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"one hairdresser for every","meaning":"每……人有一名髮型師","examples":[{"en":"There is now one hairdresser for every 287 people.","zh":"現在每287人有一名髮型師。"},{"en":"One hairdresser for every number of people means that each hairdresser serves about that many people.","zh":"one hairdresser for every number of people 指每名髮型師大約服務該數量的人。"},{"en":"A town may have one doctor for every 1,000 residents.","zh":"一個城鎮可能每1,000名居民有一名醫生。"},{"en":"If there is one teacher for every thirty students, class sizes may be manageable.","zh":"如果每三十名學生有一名老師，班級人數可能較容易管理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a ratio between workers and people served.","zh":"這個短語描述工作者與服務人口之間的比例。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"earning power","meaning":"賺錢能力；收入能力","examples":[{"en":"People’s earning power has gone up.","zh":"人們的收入能力提高了。"},{"en":"Earning power is a person’s ability to earn money through work or skills.","zh":"earning power 指一個人透過工作或技能賺錢的能力。"},{"en":"Learning a useful trade can improve a young worker’s earning power.","zh":"學習有用手藝可以改善年輕工人的賺錢能力。"},{"en":"If people’s earning power rises, they may spend more on services and leisure.","zh":"如果人們收入能力提高，他們可能在服務和休閒上花更多錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes income potential.","zh":"這個短語描述收入潛力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"afford to spend more on","meaning":"負擔得起在……花更多錢","examples":[{"en":"People can afford to spend more on personal services.","zh":"人們負擔得起在個人服務上花更多錢。"},{"en":"To afford to spend more on something means to have enough money to pay more for it.","zh":"afford to spend more on something 指有足夠金錢為某事支付更多。"},{"en":"Families may afford to spend more on tutoring when their income rises.","zh":"當收入上升時，家庭可能負擔得起在補習上花更多錢。"},{"en":"If people can afford more services, industries such as hairdressing may grow.","zh":"如果人們負擔得起更多服務，美髮等行業可能增長。"},{"en":"This phrase links income with spending ability.","zh":"這個短語把收入與消費能力連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"personal services","meaning":"個人服務","examples":[{"en":"Hairdressing is an example of a personal service.","zh":"美髮服務是個人服務的一個例子。"},{"en":"Personal services are services provided directly to individuals, often for appearance, health, care, or convenience.","zh":"personal services 指直接提供給個人的服務，常與外觀、健康、照顧或便利有關。"},{"en":"Haircuts, childcare, massage, and home cleaning are personal services.","zh":"剪髮、托兒、按摩和家居清潔都是個人服務。"},{"en":"If incomes rise, demand for personal services may increase.","zh":"如果收入上升，對個人服務的需求可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes services focused on individual needs.","zh":"這個短語描述以個人需要為中心的服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the actual job","meaning":"實際工作內容","examples":[{"en":"Technology has not changed the actual job of hairdressers very much.","zh":"科技並沒有很大程度改變髮型師的實際工作內容。"},{"en":"The actual job means the real work someone does, not the title or image of the job.","zh":"the actual job 指某人真正做的工作，而不是職銜或外在形象。"},{"en":"The actual job of a teacher includes planning, marking, and helping students, not only speaking in class.","zh":"老師的實際工作包括備課、批改和幫助學生，不只是上課說話。"},{"en":"If technology changes the tools but not the actual job, workers still need the same core skills.","zh":"如果科技改變工具但沒有改變實際工作，員工仍需要相同核心技能。"},{"en":"This phrase points to what the work really involves.","zh":"這個短語指出工作真正包括甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"depend on a computer","meaning":"依賴電腦","examples":[{"en":"Hairdressing is one job where people do not depend on a computer.","zh":"美髮服務是一種人們不依賴電腦的工作。"},{"en":"To depend on a computer means to need a computer to complete the work.","zh":"depend on a computer 指需要電腦才能完成工作。"},{"en":"Accountants depend on computers to organise records and calculate figures.","zh":"會計師依賴電腦整理紀錄和計算數字。"},{"en":"If a job depends less on computers, human skill and direct service may matter more.","zh":"如果一份工作較少依賴電腦，人類技巧和直接服務可能更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reliance on digital tools.","zh":"這個短語描述對數碼工具的依賴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"administrative staff","meaning":"行政職員","examples":[{"en":"The work done by administrative staff has changed enormously.","zh":"行政職員所做的工作發生了巨大變化。"},{"en":"Administrative staff are workers who organise records, appointments, communication, and office processes.","zh":"administrative staff 指負責整理紀錄、預約、溝通和辦公室流程的員工。"},{"en":"School administrative staff help handle student records, notices, and parent enquiries.","zh":"學校行政職員協助處理學生紀錄、通告和家長查詢。"},{"en":"If administrative staff use better software, office work can become faster and more accurate.","zh":"如果行政職員使用更好的軟件，辦公室工作可以更快、更準確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes office support workers.","zh":"這個短語描述辦公室支援人員。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"change enormously","meaning":"發生巨大變化","examples":[{"en":"The kind of work that administrative staff do has changed enormously.","zh":"行政職員所做的工作種類發生了巨大變化。"},{"en":"To change enormously means to become very different in a major way.","zh":"change enormously 指以重大方式變得非常不同。"},{"en":"Communication has changed enormously since people started using smartphones.","zh":"自從人們開始使用智能手機，溝通方式發生了巨大變化。"},{"en":"If a job changes enormously, workers may need new skills and training.","zh":"如果一份工作發生巨大變化，員工可能需要新技能和培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very large change.","zh":"這個短語描述非常大的改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"thanks to","meaning":"由於；多虧","examples":[{"en":"Administrative work has changed enormously thanks to technology.","zh":"由於科技，行政工作發生了巨大變化。"},{"en":"Thanks to means because of, usually when the result is positive or important.","zh":"thanks to 指由於某事，通常結果是正面或重要的。"},{"en":"Thanks to a new bus route, students can get to school more easily.","zh":"多虧新的巴士路線，學生可以更容易到校。"},{"en":"If work becomes faster thanks to software, staff may handle more complex tasks.","zh":"如果工作因軟件而變快，員工可能處理更複雜任務。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the cause of a helpful result.","zh":"這個短語顯示有幫助結果的原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"secretaries doing dictation and typing","meaning":"負責聽寫和打字的秘書","examples":[{"en":"Twenty years ago, there were still secretaries doing dictation and typing.","zh":"二十年前，仍有負責聽寫和打字的秘書。"},{"en":"Secretaries doing dictation and typing are office workers who write down spoken words and prepare typed documents.","zh":"secretaries doing dictation and typing 指負責記下口述內容並準備打字文件的辦公室人員。"},{"en":"Before email became common, secretaries often typed letters for managers.","zh":"電郵普及前，秘書常為經理打信。"},{"en":"If software records speech automatically, fewer secretaries may spend all day on dictation.","zh":"如果軟件能自動記錄語音，較少秘書會整天處理聽寫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an older form of clerical work.","zh":"這個短語描述較舊式的文書工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"compared to these days","meaning":"與現在相比","examples":[{"en":"Secretarial work was more repetitive compared to these days.","zh":"與現在相比，秘書工作較重複。"},{"en":"Compared to these days means when judged against the situation now.","zh":"compared to these days 指與現今情況相比。"},{"en":"Travelling was slower compared to these days because online booking did not exist.","zh":"與現在相比，以前旅遊較慢，因為沒有網上預訂。"},{"en":"If we compare old office work to these days, technology has removed many manual tasks.","zh":"如果把舊式辦公室工作與現在相比，科技已消除許多手動任務。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the past with the present.","zh":"這個短語把過去與現在作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be given much more responsibility","meaning":"被賦予更多責任","examples":[{"en":"Administrative staff are now given much more responsibility.","zh":"行政職員現在被賦予更多責任。"},{"en":"To be given much more responsibility means to be trusted with more important duties or decisions.","zh":"be given much more responsibility 指被信任去承擔更多重要職責或決定。"},{"en":"A senior student may be given more responsibility during a school open day.","zh":"高年級學生可能在學校開放日被賦予更多責任。"},{"en":"If workers are given more responsibility, they may need better training and higher pay.","zh":"如果員工被賦予更多責任，他們可能需要更好培訓和更高薪酬。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase in duties and trust.","zh":"這個短語描述職責和信任增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"higher status","meaning":"較高地位","examples":[{"en":"Administrative staff now often have higher status.","zh":"行政職員現在通常有較高地位。"},{"en":"Higher status means a more respected or important position in a group or workplace.","zh":"higher status 指在群體或工作場所中更受尊重或更重要的位置。"},{"en":"A nurse with specialist training may have higher status in a hospital team.","zh":"有專科訓練的護士在醫院團隊中可能有較高地位。"},{"en":"If a job requires more skill and responsibility, its status may rise.","zh":"如果一份工作需要更多技能和責任，其地位可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes greater respect or importance.","zh":"這個短語描述更高尊重或重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"graduates","meaning":"大學畢業生","examples":[{"en":"A lot of graduates go into administrative work now.","zh":"現在很多大學畢業生從事行政工作。"},{"en":"Graduates are people who have completed a degree or course at a university or college.","zh":"graduates 指完成大學或學院學位或課程的人。"},{"en":"Many graduates look for work that uses communication, organisation, and problem-solving skills.","zh":"許多大學畢業生尋找能運用溝通、組織和解難技能的工作。"},{"en":"If more graduates enter a field, employers may expect higher qualifications.","zh":"如果更多大學畢業生進入某行業，僱主可能期望更高學歷。"},{"en":"This word describes people after completing higher education.","zh":"這個字描述完成高等教育的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go in for","meaning":"從事；投身於","examples":[{"en":"Many graduates go in for this kind of work now.","zh":"現在許多大學畢業生投身於這類工作。"},{"en":"To go in for a kind of work means to choose it or enter that field.","zh":"go in for a kind of work 指選擇某種工作或進入某個領域。"},{"en":"Some students go in for nursing because they want practical work that helps people.","zh":"有些學生投身護理，因為他們想做實用又助人的工作。"},{"en":"If many people go in for the same career, competition may increase.","zh":"如果許多人投身同一職業，競爭可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase is a British way to talk about choosing an activity or career.","zh":"這個短語是英式說法，用來談論選擇活動或職業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"this kind of work","meaning":"這類工作","examples":[{"en":"Many graduates now choose this kind of work.","zh":"現在許多大學畢業生選擇這類工作。"},{"en":"This kind of work means this type or category of job.","zh":"this kind of work 指這種類型或類別的工作。"},{"en":"This kind of work may suit people who enjoy organising information and solving office problems.","zh":"這類工作可能適合喜歡整理資料和解決辦公室問題的人。"},{"en":"If this kind of work becomes more skilled, salaries and status may rise.","zh":"如果這類工作變得更需要技能，薪金和地位可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to the work already being discussed.","zh":"這個短語指回正在討論的工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"I’d expected there to be","meaning":"我原本以為會有","examples":[{"en":"The young woman had expected there to be a bigger change in agricultural employment.","zh":"這名年輕女子原本以為農業就業會有更大變化。"},{"en":"I’d expected there to be means I thought something would exist or happen, but reality may be different.","zh":"I’d expected there to be 指我原本以為某事會存在或發生，但現實可能不同。"},{"en":"I’d expected there to be more seats at the seminar, but the room was small.","zh":"我原本以為研討會會有更多座位，但房間很小。"},{"en":"If people expect a big change and find a smaller one, they may ask why.","zh":"如果人們預期有巨大改變卻發現變化較小，他們可能會問原因。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses an earlier expectation.","zh":"這個短語表達較早的預期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a much bigger change","meaning":"大得多的變化","examples":[{"en":"She expected a much bigger change in the number of agricultural workers.","zh":"她原本預期農業工人數量會有大得多的變化。"},{"en":"A much bigger change means a far greater difference than the one observed.","zh":"a much bigger change 指比所觀察到的差異大很多的變化。"},{"en":"A student may expect a much bigger change in marks after studying every day.","zh":"學生每天溫習後，可能預期成績有大得多的變化。"},{"en":"If the real change is smaller than expected, the data may surprise people.","zh":"如果實際變化比預期小，數據可能令人意外。"},{"en":"This phrase compares expected and actual size of change.","zh":"這個短語比較預期和實際變化幅度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"agricultural workers","meaning":"農業工人","examples":[{"en":"The number of agricultural workers has fallen dramatically.","zh":"農業工人的數量已大幅下降。"},{"en":"Agricultural workers are people who work in farming, growing crops, or caring for farm animals.","zh":"agricultural workers 指從事農耕、種植作物或照顧農場動物的人。"},{"en":"Agricultural workers may plant seeds, harvest fruit, or feed cattle.","zh":"農業工人可能播種、收割水果或餵牛。"},{"en":"If machines replace manual farm work, the number of agricultural workers may fall.","zh":"如果機器取代手工農務，農業工人數量可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes workers in farming and food production.","zh":"這個短語描述農業和食物生產中的工人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the 1871 census","meaning":"1871年人口普查","examples":[{"en":"The 1871 census showed that roughly 25% of the population worked on the land.","zh":"1871年人口普查顯示，大約25%人口從事農業工作。"},{"en":"The 1871 census was an official count of the population carried out in 1871.","zh":"the 1871 census 指1871年進行的官方人口統計。"},{"en":"A census records information such as age, work, family size, and where people live.","zh":"人口普查記錄年齡、工作、家庭人數和居住地等資料。"},{"en":"If a census shows many people worked on the land, agriculture was important at that time.","zh":"如果人口普查顯示很多人務農，農業在當時很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to historical population data.","zh":"這個短語指歷史人口數據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"roughly","meaning":"大約","examples":[{"en":"Roughly 25% of the population worked on the land in 1871.","zh":"1871年，大約25%人口務農。"},{"en":"Roughly means approximately or not exactly.","zh":"roughly 指大約或不完全精確。"},{"en":"Roughly thirty students joined the after-school revision class.","zh":"大約三十名學生參加放學後溫習班。"},{"en":"If a number is rough, it gives a useful estimate but not a precise count.","zh":"如果數字是大約數，它提供有用估算，但不是精確點算。"},{"en":"This word is used when exact accuracy is not necessary.","zh":"這個字用於不需要完全準確時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"work on the land","meaning":"務農；從事農業工作","examples":[{"en":"Roughly 25% of the population worked on the land in 1871.","zh":"1871年，大約25%人口務農。"},{"en":"To work on the land means to farm, grow crops, or look after animals on farms.","zh":"work on the land 指務農、種植作物或在農場照顧動物。"},{"en":"Some families still work on the land by planting vegetables and raising chickens.","zh":"有些家庭仍透過種菜和養雞務農。"},{"en":"If fewer people work on the land, machines may be doing more farm labour.","zh":"如果較少人務農，機器可能正在做更多農務。"},{"en":"This phrase is an older or broader way to describe agricultural work.","zh":"這個短語是較舊或較廣泛地描述農業工作的說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"I’d have assumed","meaning":"我原本以為","examples":[{"en":"The young man had assumed that the figure would be more than 50%.","zh":"這名年輕男子原本以為該數字會超過50%。"},{"en":"I’d have assumed means I would have guessed or believed something without checking.","zh":"I’d have assumed 指我原本會在沒有查證下猜想或相信某事。"},{"en":"I’d have assumed the train was faster, but the bus actually took less time.","zh":"我原本以為火車較快，但巴士實際上用時更少。"},{"en":"If your assumption is wrong, new data can surprise you.","zh":"如果你的假設錯了，新數據可能令你驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an expectation based on guesswork.","zh":"這個短語引出基於猜測的預期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"less than","meaning":"少於","examples":[{"en":"Now less than 0.2% of the population works on the land.","zh":"現在少於0.2%人口務農。"},{"en":"Less than means a smaller amount or number than the one stated.","zh":"less than 指少於所說的數量或數字。"},{"en":"The walk to school takes less than ten minutes.","zh":"步行上學需時少於十分鐘。"},{"en":"If less than one percent of people work in a sector, it is a very small share.","zh":"如果少於百分之一人口在某行業工作，比例就非常小。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a number with an upper limit.","zh":"這個短語把數字與上限作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"care workers","meaning":"護理人員；照顧服務人員","examples":[{"en":"The students also discuss the future of care workers.","zh":"學生也討論護理人員的未來。"},{"en":"Care workers are people who help elderly, disabled, sick, or vulnerable people with daily needs.","zh":"care workers 指幫助長者、殘疾人士、病人或弱勢人士處理日常需要的人。"},{"en":"Care workers may help residents wash, eat, move, and take medicine.","zh":"護理人員可能幫助院友洗澡、進食、移動和服藥。"},{"en":"If a society has more elderly people, demand for care workers usually rises.","zh":"如果社會有更多長者，對護理人員的需求通常會上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes workers who provide personal support and care.","zh":"這個短語描述提供個人支援和照顧的工作者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"barely exist","meaning":"幾乎不存在","examples":[{"en":"Care workers barely existed in the 19th century.","zh":"護理人員在十九世紀幾乎不存在。"},{"en":"To barely exist means to exist only in a very small amount or almost not at all.","zh":"barely exist 指只以很少量存在，或幾乎完全不存在。"},{"en":"Online shopping barely existed when most families first used the internet.","zh":"當大多數家庭剛開始使用互聯網時，網上購物幾乎不存在。"},{"en":"If a job barely exists in one period, it may become common later when society changes.","zh":"如果一份工作在某時期幾乎不存在，社會改變後它可能變得常見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that is almost absent.","zh":"這個短語描述某事幾乎不存在。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lifespan","meaning":"壽命","examples":[{"en":"Care workers barely existed because people’s lifespan was much shorter.","zh":"護理人員幾乎不存在，因為人們壽命短得多。"},{"en":"Lifespan means the length of time a person, animal, or thing lives or lasts.","zh":"lifespan 指人、動物或物件生存或使用的時間長度。"},{"en":"Better medicine and cleaner water can increase human lifespan.","zh":"更好的醫療和更清潔食水可以延長人類壽命。"},{"en":"If people’s lifespan becomes longer, more elderly care may be needed.","zh":"如果人們壽命變長，就可能需要更多長者護理。"},{"en":"This word describes length of life or use.","zh":"這個字描述生命或使用年期的長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"this sector","meaning":"這個行業","examples":[{"en":"This sector will see huge growth in the future.","zh":"這個行業未來會出現巨大增長。"},{"en":"This sector means this part of the economy or field of work being discussed.","zh":"this sector 指正在討論的經濟或工作領域的一部分。"},{"en":"The education sector includes schools, tutors, publishers, and training companies.","zh":"教育行業包括學校、補習老師、出版社和培訓公司。"},{"en":"If a sector grows, more jobs and businesses may appear there.","zh":"如果某行業增長，該領域可能出現更多工作和企業。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to an industry or area already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回已提及的產業或範疇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"see huge growth","meaning":"出現巨大增長","examples":[{"en":"The care sector will see huge growth.","zh":"護理行業將出現巨大增長。"},{"en":"To see huge growth means to experience a very large increase.","zh":"see huge growth 指經歷非常大的增加。"},{"en":"A school club may see huge growth after winning a public competition.","zh":"學校學會在贏得公開比賽後可能出現巨大增長。"},{"en":"If an industry sees huge growth, it may need many more trained workers.","zh":"如果一個行業出現巨大增長，可能需要更多受訓工人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rapid and large expansion.","zh":"這個短語描述快速而大幅的擴張。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hard enough to","meaning":"已經很難……","examples":[{"en":"It is hard enough to meet current demand for care workers.","zh":"要滿足目前對護理人員的需求已經很難。"},{"en":"Hard enough to do something means already difficult to do that thing.","zh":"hard enough to do something 指做某事本身已經困難。"},{"en":"It is hard enough to finish homework on time without extra meetings after school.","zh":"沒有放學後額外會議，準時完成功課已經很難。"},{"en":"If a task is already hard enough, extra pressure can make it almost impossible.","zh":"如果一項任務已經很難，額外壓力可能令它幾乎不可能完成。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses existing difficulty.","zh":"這個短語強調現有困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"meet current demand","meaning":"滿足目前需求","examples":[{"en":"It is already difficult to meet current demand for care workers.","zh":"要滿足目前對護理人員的需求已經很困難。"},{"en":"To meet current demand means to provide enough supply for what people need now.","zh":"meet current demand 指提供足夠供應，以滿足人們現在的需要。"},{"en":"A canteen may fail to meet current demand if too many students buy lunch at once.","zh":"如果太多學生同時買午餐，飯堂可能無法滿足目前需求。"},{"en":"If hospitals cannot meet current demand for nurses, patients may wait longer.","zh":"如果醫院不能滿足目前對護士的需求，病人可能要等更久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes satisfying present needs.","zh":"這個短語描述滿足現時需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"look quite bleak","meaning":"看起來相當黯淡","examples":[{"en":"The future looks quite bleak for bank clerks.","zh":"銀行文員的未來看起來相當黯淡。"},{"en":"To look quite bleak means to seem rather hopeless, difficult, or lacking in good prospects.","zh":"look quite bleak 指看起來相當沒有希望、困難或缺乏好前景。"},{"en":"A small shop’s future may look quite bleak if rent rises and customers disappear.","zh":"如果租金上升而顧客消失，小店的未來可能看起來相當黯淡。"},{"en":"If an occupation is being replaced by technology, its future may look bleak.","zh":"如果某職業正被科技取代，其前景可能黯淡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a pessimistic outlook.","zh":"這個短語描述悲觀前景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bank clerks","meaning":"銀行文員；銀行櫃員","examples":[{"en":"The future looks bleak for bank clerks.","zh":"銀行文員的未來看起來黯淡。"},{"en":"Bank clerks are workers who handle customer transactions, records, and basic services in banks.","zh":"bank clerks 指在銀行處理顧客交易、紀錄和基本服務的員工。"},{"en":"A bank clerk may help customers deposit money or update account details.","zh":"銀行櫃員可能幫助顧客存款或更新戶口資料。"},{"en":"If online banking grows, fewer bank clerks may be needed at counters.","zh":"如果網上銀行發展，櫃位可能需要較少銀行文員。"},{"en":"This phrase describes traditional front-line banking workers.","zh":"這個短語描述傳統前線銀行員工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be in decline","meaning":"正在減少；走下坡","examples":[{"en":"Bank clerks have been in decline since ATMs were introduced.","zh":"自從自動櫃員機推出以來，銀行文員一直在減少。"},{"en":"To be in decline means to be becoming fewer, weaker, or less important over time.","zh":"be in decline 指隨時間變少、變弱或變得較不重要。"},{"en":"Handwritten letters have been in decline since messaging apps became common.","zh":"自從即時通訊應用程式普及後，手寫信一直在減少。"},{"en":"If a job is in decline, young people may avoid training for it.","zh":"如果某工作正在走下坡，年輕人可能避免接受相關培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual reduction.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步減少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"since ATMs were introduced","meaning":"自從自動櫃員機推出以來","examples":[{"en":"Bank clerks have been in decline since ATMs were introduced in the eighties.","zh":"自從八十年代自動櫃員機推出以來，銀行文員一直在減少。"},{"en":"Since ATMs were introduced means from the time cash machines began to be used.","zh":"since ATMs were introduced 指自動櫃員機開始被使用以來。"},{"en":"Since online booking was introduced, fewer people have queued at travel agencies.","zh":"自從網上預訂推出以來，較少人到旅行社排隊。"},{"en":"If a technology has changed behaviour since it was introduced, older jobs may shrink.","zh":"如果某科技推出後改變了行為，舊工作可能萎縮。"},{"en":"This phrase links a change to the start of a new technology.","zh":"這個短語把變化與新科技開始使用連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the eighties","meaning":"八十年代","examples":[{"en":"ATMs were introduced in the eighties.","zh":"自動櫃員機在八十年代推出。"},{"en":"The eighties means the years from 1980 to 1989.","zh":"the eighties 指1980年至1989年。"},{"en":"Many people remember the eighties for music, fashion, and early home computers.","zh":"許多人記得八十年代的音樂、時裝和早期家用電腦。"},{"en":"If a machine was introduced in the eighties, it may now feel ordinary and old.","zh":"如果一種機器在八十年代推出，它現在可能顯得普通又舊。"},{"en":"This phrase names a decade.","zh":"這個短語指出一個十年期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make jobs redundant","meaning":"令職位變得多餘","examples":[{"en":"Technology will make many bank-clerk jobs redundant.","zh":"科技會令許多銀行文員職位變得多餘。"},{"en":"To make jobs redundant means to remove the need for those jobs, often because machines or systems can do the work.","zh":"make jobs redundant 指令某些工作不再需要，常因機器或系統能完成相關工作。"},{"en":"Self-checkout machines may make some cashier jobs redundant.","zh":"自助付款機可能令部分收銀員職位變得多餘。"},{"en":"If jobs are made redundant, workers may need retraining or support.","zh":"如果職位變得多餘，工人可能需要再培訓或支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work becoming unnecessary.","zh":"這個短語描述工作變得不再必要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"most of the jobs they do now","meaning":"他們現時所做的大部分工作","examples":[{"en":"Technology will replace most of the jobs that bank clerks do now.","zh":"科技將取代銀行文員現時所做的大部分工作。"},{"en":"Most of the jobs they do now means the majority of their current tasks or duties.","zh":"most of the jobs they do now 指他們目前大多數任務或職責。"},{"en":"A school office system may handle most of the tasks clerks do now, such as filing and searching records.","zh":"學校辦公室系統可能處理文員現時所做的大部分工作，例如歸檔和搜尋紀錄。"},{"en":"If technology replaces most current tasks, the job role must change or disappear.","zh":"如果科技取代大部分現有任務，工作角色就必須改變或消失。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on present duties being affected.","zh":"這個短語重點在目前職責受到影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"although the situation may change","meaning":"雖然情況可能會改變","examples":[{"en":"The young woman agrees, although the situation may change.","zh":"這名年輕女子同意，雖然情況可能會改變。"},{"en":"Although the situation may change means the statement is true now, but future conditions could be different.","zh":"although the situation may change 指現在陳述成立，但未來情況可能不同。"},{"en":"The library is quiet today, although the situation may change during exam week.","zh":"圖書館今天很安靜，雖然情況可能會在考試週改變。"},{"en":"If the situation may change, people should avoid making overly certain predictions.","zh":"如果情況可能改變，人們應避免作出過於肯定的預測。"},{"en":"This phrase adds caution to an opinion.","zh":"這個短語為意見加入謹慎語氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"predict what will happen","meaning":"預測將會發生甚麼","examples":[{"en":"It is very hard to predict what will happen.","zh":"要預測將會發生甚麼非常困難。"},{"en":"To predict what will happen means to say what you think the future result will be.","zh":"predict what will happen 指說出你認為未來結果會是甚麼。"},{"en":"It is hard to predict what will happen to exam results when the format changes.","zh":"當考試形式改變時，很難預測成績會發生甚麼變化。"},{"en":"If many factors are uncertain, predictions may easily be wrong.","zh":"如果許多因素不確定，預測很容易出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes guessing or forecasting future events.","zh":"這個短語描述推測或預測未來事件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9}],"ielts/listening/Practice 11/task-4":[{"front":"astronomy lecture","meaning":"天文學講座","examples":[{"en":"In today’s astronomy lecture, the speaker talks about satellites in orbit around the Earth.","zh":"在今天的天文學講座中，講者談及在地球軌道上的衛星。"},{"en":"An astronomy lecture is a talk or lesson about space, stars, planets, or other objects beyond Earth.","zh":"天文學講座是關於太空、恆星、行星或地球以外其他物體的講座或課堂。"},{"en":"A school may invite a scientist to give an astronomy lecture about the Moon and Mars.","zh":"學校可能邀請科學家舉辦關於月球和火星的天文學講座。"},{"en":"Astronomy lectures help students understand space by explaining difficult ideas clearly.","zh":"天文學講座透過清楚解釋困難概念，幫助學生理解太空。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for an educational talk about space science.","zh":"這個短語用於關於太空科學的教育講座。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"talk about the need for","meaning":"談論……的需要","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer talks about the need for a system to manage satellites.","zh":"講師談論需要一個系統來管理衛星。"},{"en":"To talk about the need for something means to explain why that thing is necessary.","zh":"談論某事的需要意思是解釋為何該事物是必要的。"},{"en":"A teacher may talk about the need for better study habits before exams.","zh":"老師可能在考試前談論改善學習習慣的需要。"},{"en":"People discuss the need for a system when a problem cannot be solved casually.","zh":"當問題不能隨便解決時，人們會討論建立系統的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason why a solution is required.","zh":"這個短語引入為何需要某解決方案的原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"manage the movement of","meaning":"管理……的運行","examples":[{"en":"A Space Traffic Management system would manage the movement of satellites.","zh":"太空交通管理系統會管理衛星的運行。"},{"en":"To manage the movement of something means to control or organise how it moves.","zh":"管理某物的運行意思是控制或組織它如何移動。"},{"en":"Traffic lights manage the movement of cars at busy junctions.","zh":"交通燈管理繁忙路口車輛的運行。"},{"en":"Managing movement helps prevent accidents when many objects use the same space.","zh":"當許多物體使用同一空間時，管理運行有助防止意外。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing traffic, transport, or objects in motion.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論交通、運輸或移動中的物體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"satellites and other objects","meaning":"衛星和其他物體","examples":[{"en":"The system would manage satellites and other objects in orbit.","zh":"該系統會管理軌道上的衛星和其他物體。"},{"en":"Satellites and other objects means working satellites as well as other items moving in space.","zh":"衛星和其他物體意思是正在運作的衛星，以及在太空中移動的其他物件。"},{"en":"Space agencies track satellites and other objects so they can avoid dangerous paths.","zh":"太空機構追蹤衛星和其他物體，以避免危險路徑。"},{"en":"Other objects may include old rocket parts, broken equipment, and space debris.","zh":"其他物體可能包括舊火箭部件、損壞設備和太空碎片。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the issue is wider than active satellites alone.","zh":"這個短語顯示問題不只涉及運作中的衛星。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in orbit around the Earth","meaning":"在地球軌道上","examples":[{"en":"Many satellites and other objects are in orbit around the Earth.","zh":"許多衛星和其他物體在地球軌道上。"},{"en":"In orbit around the Earth means moving around Earth in a curved path because of gravity.","zh":"在地球軌道上意思是因重力而沿彎曲路徑圍繞地球移動。"},{"en":"A weather satellite in orbit around the Earth can collect data about storms.","zh":"在地球軌道上的天氣衛星可以收集風暴資料。"},{"en":"Objects in orbit can remain there for a long time if their path is stable.","zh":"如果軌道路徑穩定，物體可以在軌道上停留很長時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a position and movement in space near Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述近地太空中的位置和運動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in other words","meaning":"換句話說","examples":[{"en":"In other words, the lecturer is talking about a Space Traffic Management system.","zh":"換句話說，講師正在談論太空交通管理系統。"},{"en":"In other words means saying the same idea again in a clearer or simpler way.","zh":"換句話說意思是用更清楚或更簡單的方式重述同一想法。"},{"en":"The shop is understaffed; in other words, there are not enough workers.","zh":"這間店人手不足；換句話說，員工不夠。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase when they want to restate an idea for easier understanding.","zh":"說話者想令想法更容易理解時，會使用這個短語重述。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain technical or difficult information.","zh":"這個短語有助解釋技術性或困難資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Space Traffic Management system","meaning":"太空交通管理系統","examples":[{"en":"A Space Traffic Management system would help control satellites.","zh":"太空交通管理系統會幫助管制衛星。"},{"en":"A Space Traffic Management system is a system for organising and monitoring objects moving in space.","zh":"太空交通管理系統是用來組織和監察太空中移動物體的系統。"},{"en":"Such a system would be similar to air traffic control, but for satellites and space debris.","zh":"這樣的系統會類似空中交通管制，但對象是衛星和太空碎片。"},{"en":"Space traffic management can reduce the risk of collisions in orbit.","zh":"太空交通管理可以降低軌道碰撞風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a proposed way to make space activity safer.","zh":"這個短語描述一種使太空活動更安全的擬議方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"effective Air Traffic Control systems","meaning":"有效的空中交通管制系統","examples":[{"en":"We already have effective Air Traffic Control systems for planes.","zh":"我們已經有用於飛機的有效空中交通管制系統。"},{"en":"Effective Air Traffic Control systems are systems that successfully guide aircraft and prevent unsafe situations.","zh":"有效的空中交通管制系統是能成功引導飛機並防止不安全情況的系統。"},{"en":"Airports use Air Traffic Control systems to tell pilots when to take off or land.","zh":"機場使用空中交通管制系統告訴機師何時起飛或降落。"},{"en":"Effective control systems reduce confusion when many planes are using the same airspace.","zh":"當許多飛機使用同一空域時，有效管制系統可以減少混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised safety systems for air travel.","zh":"這個短語指航空旅程中的有組織安全系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"used internationally","meaning":"在國際上使用","examples":[{"en":"Air Traffic Control systems are used internationally.","zh":"空中交通管制系統在國際上使用。"},{"en":"Used internationally means used in many countries or across national borders.","zh":"在國際上使用意思是在許多國家或跨越國界使用。"},{"en":"English is used internationally in aviation because pilots and controllers need a shared language.","zh":"英語在航空中被國際上使用，因為機師和管制員需要共同語言。"},{"en":"Systems used internationally need common rules so different countries can cooperate.","zh":"在國際上使用的系統需要共同規則，讓不同國家能合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something accepted or applied beyond one country.","zh":"這個短語描述超越單一國家的應用或接受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ensure that","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Air Traffic Control systems ensure that planes navigate our skies safely.","zh":"空中交通管制系統確保飛機在天空中安全航行。"},{"en":"To ensure that something happens means to make certain it happens.","zh":"確保某事發生意思是使某事必定發生。"},{"en":"Teachers check attendance to ensure that all students are safe during a school trip.","zh":"老師核對出席名單，以確保學校旅行期間所有學生安全。"},{"en":"Clear rules ensure that people understand what they should do in an emergency.","zh":"清楚規則確保人們明白緊急情況下應做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining purpose and safety.","zh":"這個短語適合用於解釋目的和安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"navigate our skies safely","meaning":"在天空中安全航行","examples":[{"en":"Air Traffic Control helps planes navigate our skies safely.","zh":"空中交通管制幫助飛機在天空中安全航行。"},{"en":"To navigate our skies safely means to travel through the air without causing danger or confusion.","zh":"在天空中安全航行意思是在空中移動而不造成危險或混亂。"},{"en":"Pilots need clear instructions to navigate busy skies safely near airports.","zh":"機師在機場附近繁忙空域中需要清楚指示，才能安全航行。"},{"en":"Safe navigation prevents aircraft from getting too close to one another.","zh":"安全航行防止飛機彼此過於接近。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled and safe movement in the air.","zh":"這個短語描述在空中的受控安全移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a similar concept","meaning":"類似概念","examples":[{"en":"Space Traffic Management is a similar concept.","zh":"太空交通管理是一個類似概念。"},{"en":"A similar concept is an idea that works in a comparable way to another idea.","zh":"類似概念是以可比較方式運作的想法。"},{"en":"A school timetable is a similar concept to a work schedule because both organise time.","zh":"學校時間表與工作更表是類似概念，因為兩者都組織時間。"},{"en":"Comparing a new idea with a similar concept helps listeners understand it more quickly.","zh":"把新想法與類似概念比較，有助聽眾更快理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining something unfamiliar through something familiar.","zh":"當透過熟悉事物解釋陌生事物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"集中於","examples":[{"en":"Space Traffic Management focuses on the control of satellites.","zh":"太空交通管理集中於衛星管制。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give main attention to it.","zh":"集中於某事意思是把主要注意力放在它上面。"},{"en":"A science lesson may focus on climate change for one week.","zh":"科學課可能有一星期集中於氣候變化。"},{"en":"Focusing on one issue helps people study it more clearly and deeply.","zh":"集中於一個議題有助人們更清楚和深入地研究它。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main topic or target.","zh":"這個短語指出主要主題或目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"control of satellites","meaning":"衛星管制","examples":[{"en":"Space Traffic Management focuses on the control of satellites.","zh":"太空交通管理集中於衛星管制。"},{"en":"Control of satellites means managing where satellites move and how they operate.","zh":"衛星管制意思是管理衛星移動到哪裏以及如何運作。"},{"en":"Control of satellites is important when many satellites share nearby orbits.","zh":"當許多衛星共用附近軌道時，衛星管制很重要。"},{"en":"Poor control can increase the chance of collisions or communication problems.","zh":"管制不佳會增加碰撞或通訊問題的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised management of satellite movement and activity.","zh":"這個短語描述對衛星運行和活動的有組織管理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the aim of","meaning":"……的目標","examples":[{"en":"The aim of such a system is to prevent collisions in space.","zh":"這樣的系統的目標是防止太空碰撞。"},{"en":"The aim of something is its purpose or goal.","zh":"某事的目標是它的目的或想達成的結果。"},{"en":"The aim of a fire drill is to teach people how to leave safely.","zh":"火警演習的目標是教人如何安全離開。"},{"en":"Knowing the aim of a system helps people understand why it is needed.","zh":"知道一個系統的目標，有助人們理解為何需要它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the main purpose of a plan or action.","zh":"這個短語引入計劃或行動的主要目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"such a system","meaning":"這樣的系統","examples":[{"en":"Such a system would help prevent accidents in space.","zh":"這樣的系統會幫助防止太空事故。"},{"en":"Such a system means a system like the one just described.","zh":"這樣的系統意思是像剛才描述那樣的系統。"},{"en":"A school may use such a system to track attendance and contact parents quickly.","zh":"學校可能使用這樣的系統來追蹤出席並快速聯絡家長。"},{"en":"Referring to such a system avoids repeating a long technical name.","zh":"使用「這樣的系統」可以避免重複很長的技術名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to an idea already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回已提及的想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"prevent the danger of","meaning":"防止……的危險","examples":[{"en":"The system would prevent the danger of collisions in space.","zh":"該系統會防止太空碰撞的危險。"},{"en":"To prevent the danger of something means to stop a risky situation from happening.","zh":"防止某事的危險意思是阻止有風險的情況發生。"},{"en":"Seatbelts help prevent the danger of passengers being thrown forward in a crash.","zh":"安全帶有助防止乘客在撞車中向前拋出的危險。"},{"en":"A warning system can prevent danger by giving people time to react.","zh":"警報系統可以透過給人反應時間來防止危險。"},{"en":"This phrase connects prevention with a specific risk.","zh":"這個短語把預防與特定風險連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"collisions in space","meaning":"太空碰撞","examples":[{"en":"Space Traffic Management aims to prevent collisions in space.","zh":"太空交通管理旨在防止太空碰撞。"},{"en":"Collisions in space are crashes between satellites, spacecraft, or debris in orbit.","zh":"太空碰撞是在軌道上的衛星、太空器或碎片之間的撞擊。"},{"en":"A small piece of debris can cause serious damage if it creates a collision in space.","zh":"如果一小塊碎片造成太空碰撞，也可能引起嚴重損害。"},{"en":"Preventing space collisions is important because broken objects can create even more debris.","zh":"防止太空碰撞很重要，因為破碎物體可以產生更多碎片。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accidents between fast-moving objects beyond Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述地球以外高速移動物體之間的事故。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"objects in orbit","meaning":"軌道上的物體","examples":[{"en":"The system would control objects in orbit around the Earth.","zh":"該系統會控制地球軌道上的物體。"},{"en":"Objects in orbit are things moving around a planet or moon in a path controlled by gravity.","zh":"軌道上的物體是受重力控制、圍繞行星或月球移動的東西。"},{"en":"Objects in orbit can include satellites, rocket parts, and pieces of debris.","zh":"軌道上的物體可以包括衛星、火箭部件和碎片。"},{"en":"If objects in orbit are not tracked, they may move dangerously close to one another.","zh":"如果軌道上的物體沒有被追蹤，它們可能危險地彼此接近。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to items circling Earth or another body in space.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞地球或其他天體運行的物件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了","examples":[{"en":"In order to prevent collisions, legal and technical systems are needed.","zh":"為了防止碰撞，需要法律和技術系統。"},{"en":"In order to means for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"為了意思是以做某事為目的。"},{"en":"Students practise past papers in order to understand the exam format.","zh":"學生練習歷屆試題，為了理解考試格式。"},{"en":"People create rules in order to make shared spaces safer and more organised.","zh":"人們制定規則，為了令共享空間更安全和更有組織。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly introduces purpose.","zh":"這個短語清楚引入目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a set of legal measures","meaning":"一套法律措施","examples":[{"en":"We need a set of legal measures to manage space traffic.","zh":"我們需要一套法律措施來管理太空交通。"},{"en":"A set of legal measures means a group of laws, rules, or official actions.","zh":"一套法律措施意思是一組法律、規則或官方行動。"},{"en":"A city may introduce a set of legal measures to reduce dangerous driving.","zh":"城市可能引入一套法律措施，以減少危險駕駛。"},{"en":"Legal measures give people clear responsibilities and consequences.","zh":"法律措施給人清楚責任和後果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised rules created to manage a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述為管理問題而建立的有組織規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"develop the technical systems","meaning":"發展技術系統","examples":[{"en":"Scientists also need to develop the technical systems for space traffic control.","zh":"科學家也需要發展太空交通管制的技術系統。"},{"en":"To develop the technical systems means to design and build the technology needed for a task.","zh":"發展技術系統意思是設計並建立完成任務所需的科技。"},{"en":"Engineers develop technical systems to monitor trains and prevent delays.","zh":"工程師發展技術系統來監察列車並防止延誤。"},{"en":"Technical systems are needed when human observation alone is not enough.","zh":"當單靠人手觀察不足夠時，就需要技術系統。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on creating practical technological tools.","zh":"這個短語重點是創造實用科技工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"enable us to","meaning":"使我們能夠","examples":[{"en":"Technical systems would enable us to prevent such accidents.","zh":"技術系統會使我們能夠防止這類事故。"},{"en":"To enable us to do something means to make it possible for us to do it.","zh":"使我們能夠做某事意思是令我們可以做到該事。"},{"en":"Online maps enable us to find unfamiliar places more easily.","zh":"網上地圖使我們能夠更容易找到陌生地方。"},{"en":"Good technology can enable people to solve problems that are too complex to manage manually.","zh":"良好科技可以使人們能夠解決太複雜而不能靠人手管理的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase links a tool or condition with the action it makes possible.","zh":"這個短語把工具或條件與其促成的行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prevent such accidents","meaning":"防止這類事故","examples":[{"en":"The system would enable us to prevent such accidents in space.","zh":"該系統會使我們能夠防止太空中的這類事故。"},{"en":"To prevent such accidents means to stop accidents like the ones just described from happening.","zh":"防止這類事故意思是阻止剛才描述的那類意外發生。"},{"en":"Better road signs can prevent such accidents at dangerous junctions.","zh":"更好的路牌可以防止危險路口的這類事故。"},{"en":"Preventing accidents often requires planning before the danger becomes immediate.","zh":"防止事故通常需要在危險變得迫切前作好計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a specific type of accident already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回已提及的特定類型事故。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"unfortunately","meaning":"不幸的是","examples":[{"en":"Unfortunately, we do not yet have a Space Traffic Management system that works.","zh":"不幸的是，我們尚未有一個有效運作的太空交通管理系統。"},{"en":"Unfortunately is used to introduce bad, disappointing, or regrettable information.","zh":"不幸的是用來引入壞消息、令人失望或令人遺憾的資訊。"},{"en":"Unfortunately, the train has been delayed because of signal problems.","zh":"不幸的是，列車因訊號問題延誤。"},{"en":"Speakers use this word to show that the information is negative but important.","zh":"說話者使用這個詞表示資訊負面但重要。"},{"en":"This word prepares listeners for a problem or limitation.","zh":"這個詞讓聽眾準備接收問題或限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at present","meaning":"目前","examples":[{"en":"At present, we do not have a Space Traffic Management system that works.","zh":"目前，我們沒有有效運作的太空交通管理系統。"},{"en":"At present means at the current time.","zh":"目前意思是在現在這個時間。"},{"en":"At present, the school library is closed for repairs.","zh":"目前，學校圖書館因維修而關閉。"},{"en":"A situation at present may change when new systems or rules are introduced.","zh":"目前的情況可能在新系統或規則引入後改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the current state of affairs.","zh":"這個短語描述當前情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a system that works","meaning":"有效運作的系統","examples":[{"en":"We do not yet have a Space Traffic Management system that works.","zh":"我們尚未有有效運作的太空交通管理系統。"},{"en":"A system that works is a system that functions properly and solves the problem it was designed for.","zh":"有效運作的系統是能正常運作並解決其設計目的的系統。"},{"en":"A school needs a system that works for recording attendance quickly and accurately.","zh":"學校需要一個有效運作的系統來快速準確記錄出席。"},{"en":"If a system does not work, people may still face confusion and danger.","zh":"如果系統不能有效運作，人們仍可能面對混亂和危險。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語重點是實際成效。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for one thing","meaning":"首先；其中一個原因是","examples":[{"en":"For one thing, satellites are relatively cheap these days.","zh":"其中一個原因是，現今衛星相對便宜。"},{"en":"For one thing means one reason or one point is being introduced.","zh":"For one thing 意思是正在引入其中一個原因或重點。"},{"en":"I prefer studying in the library; for one thing, it is quieter than home.","zh":"我較喜歡在圖書館溫習；其中一個原因是那裏比家中安靜。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase when giving the first reason in an explanation.","zh":"說話者在解釋中給出第一個理由時會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise reasons clearly.","zh":"這個短語有助清楚組織原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"relatively cheap","meaning":"相對便宜","examples":[{"en":"Satellites are relatively cheap these days.","zh":"現今衛星相對便宜。"},{"en":"Relatively cheap means inexpensive compared with something else or compared with the past.","zh":"相對便宜意思是與其他東西或過去相比不算昂貴。"},{"en":"Online courses can be relatively cheap compared with private lessons.","zh":"網上課程與私人課堂相比可以相對便宜。"},{"en":"When technology becomes cheaper, more people and companies can use it.","zh":"當科技變得較便宜，更多人和公司可以使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes price in comparison, not absolute cheapness.","zh":"這個短語描述比較下的價格，而不是絕對便宜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"these days","meaning":"現今","examples":[{"en":"Satellites are cheaper these days than they were in the past.","zh":"現今衛星比過去便宜。"},{"en":"These days means nowadays or in the present period.","zh":"現今意思是現在或目前這個時期。"},{"en":"Many people use mobile payment these days instead of carrying cash.","zh":"現今許多人使用手機付款，而不是攜帶現金。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing the present with the past.","zh":"當比較現在與過去時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It often suggests that habits, prices, or technology have changed.","zh":"它常暗示習慣、價格或科技已有改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Satellites are cheap compared with how they were in the past.","zh":"與過去相比，衛星很便宜。"},{"en":"Compared with something means judged beside it or measured against it.","zh":"與某物相比意思是與它並列判斷或衡量。"},{"en":"Cycling is cheap compared with taking a taxi every day.","zh":"與每天乘的士相比，踩單車很便宜。"},{"en":"Comparisons help people understand whether something is high, low, easy, or difficult.","zh":"比較幫助人們理解某事是高、低、容易還是困難。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the thing used as the basis for comparison.","zh":"這個短語引入用作比較基準的事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"過去","examples":[{"en":"Satellites used to be more expensive in the past.","zh":"過去衛星曾經更昂貴。"},{"en":"In the past means at an earlier time, before now.","zh":"過去意思是在現在之前的較早時間。"},{"en":"In the past, students often used paper dictionaries more than phone apps.","zh":"過去，學生使用紙本字典的次數通常多於手機應用程式。"},{"en":"Changes in technology can make tasks cheaper and faster than in the past.","zh":"科技變化可以令任務比過去更便宜和更快捷。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when comparing earlier times with the present.","zh":"當比較較早時期與現在時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"can afford to","meaning":"有能力負擔去","examples":[{"en":"More people can afford to put satellites into space.","zh":"更多人有能力負擔把衛星送上太空。"},{"en":"To be able to afford to do something means to have enough money or resources to do it.","zh":"有能力負擔做某事意思是有足夠金錢或資源去做它。"},{"en":"Some families cannot afford to buy a new computer every year.","zh":"有些家庭不能負擔每年買一部新電腦。"},{"en":"When costs fall, more organisations can afford to use advanced technology.","zh":"當成本下降，更多機構便有能力負擔使用先進科技。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on financial ability.","zh":"這個短語重點是財政能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"put them into space","meaning":"把它們送上太空","examples":[{"en":"More people can afford to put satellites into space.","zh":"更多人有能力負擔把衛星送上太空。"},{"en":"To put satellites into space means to launch them beyond Earth’s atmosphere.","zh":"把衛星送上太空意思是把它們發射到地球大氣層外。"},{"en":"A company may pay a rocket provider to put its satellite into space.","zh":"公司可能付費給火箭供應商，把自己的衛星送上太空。"},{"en":"Putting more objects into space increases the need for tracking and management.","zh":"把更多物體送上太空會增加追蹤和管理的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sending objects from Earth into orbit or beyond.","zh":"這個短語描述把物體從地球送到軌道或更遠地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"out there","meaning":"在外面；在太空中","examples":[{"en":"There are a lot more satellites out there now.","zh":"現在太空中有更多衛星。"},{"en":"Out there can mean in space or in a place away from where we are.","zh":"Out there 可以指在太空中，或在離我們較遠的地方。"},{"en":"Scientists know there are many small pieces of debris out there in orbit.","zh":"科學家知道軌道上有很多小碎片在外面。"},{"en":"In space discussions, “out there” often refers to objects beyond Earth.","zh":"在太空討論中，“out there” 常指地球以外的物體。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and points to a distant place.","zh":"這個短語較口語，指向遠處地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"launch single satellites","meaning":"發射單顆衛星","examples":[{"en":"People are not just launching single satellites.","zh":"人們不只是發射單顆衛星。"},{"en":"To launch single satellites means to send one satellite at a time into space.","zh":"發射單顆衛星意思是一次把一顆衛星送上太空。"},{"en":"In the past, a company might launch a single satellite for communication services.","zh":"過去，公司可能發射單顆衛星來提供通訊服務。"},{"en":"Launching one satellite is different from sending a whole group into orbit.","zh":"發射一顆衛星與把整個群組送上軌道不同。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts individual satellites with large satellite constellations.","zh":"這個短語把單獨衛星與大型衛星星座作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"whole constellations","meaning":"整個衛星星座","examples":[{"en":"Some operators are launching whole constellations of satellites.","zh":"有些營運者正在發射整個衛星星座。"},{"en":"Whole constellations of satellites are large groups of satellites designed to work as a network.","zh":"整個衛星星座是設計成作為網絡運作的大型衛星群。"},{"en":"A communications company may launch a whole constellation to provide internet coverage.","zh":"通訊公司可能發射整個衛星星座，以提供互聯網覆蓋。"},{"en":"Large constellations can improve services but also make orbit more crowded.","zh":"大型衛星星座可以改善服務，但也會令軌道更擁擠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes many satellites launched as a connected system.","zh":"這個短語描述作為連接系統發射的許多衛星。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"consisting of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"Some constellations consist of thousands of satellites.","zh":"有些衛星星座由數以千計的衛星組成。"},{"en":"Consisting of means being made up of particular parts or members.","zh":"由某些部分組成意思是由特定部分或成員構成。"},{"en":"A school committee consisting of teachers, parents, and students can discuss new rules.","zh":"由老師、家長和學生組成的學校委員會可以討論新規則。"},{"en":"Knowing what a system consists of helps people understand its size and complexity.","zh":"知道一個系統由甚麼組成，有助人們理解其規模和複雜性。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the parts that form a whole.","zh":"這個短語引入形成整體的部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"thousands of","meaning":"數以千計的","examples":[{"en":"Some satellite constellations consist of thousands of satellites.","zh":"有些衛星星座由數以千計的衛星組成。"},{"en":"Thousands of means a very large number, usually more than one thousand.","zh":"數以千計的意思是非常大的數量，通常多於一千。"},{"en":"Thousands of people use public transport during the morning rush hour.","zh":"早上繁忙時間有數以千計的人使用公共交通。"},{"en":"When thousands of objects are involved, a system becomes harder to manage.","zh":"當涉及數以千計的物體，系統會更難管理。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises large quantity.","zh":"這個短語強調數量龐大。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"designed to work together","meaning":"設計成共同運作","examples":[{"en":"The satellites are designed to work together.","zh":"這些衛星設計成共同運作。"},{"en":"Designed to work together means planned so that separate parts cooperate as one system.","zh":"設計成共同運作意思是計劃讓分開部分像一個系統般合作。"},{"en":"A team project is designed to work together when each student has a clear role.","zh":"當每位學生都有清楚角色，小組項目就是設計成共同運作。"},{"en":"Satellites working together can provide wider coverage than one satellite alone.","zh":"共同運作的衛星可以比單顆衛星提供更廣覆蓋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes coordination built into the design.","zh":"這個短語描述設計中包含的協調。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"space is getting more crowded","meaning":"太空正變得越來越擁擠","examples":[{"en":"Space is getting more crowded every day.","zh":"太空每天都正變得越來越擁擠。"},{"en":"Space is getting more crowded means more objects are being placed in orbit over time.","zh":"太空正變得越來越擁擠意思是隨時間有更多物體被放進軌道。"},{"en":"Roads get more crowded when more cars use them without better traffic control.","zh":"如果更多汽車使用道路而沒有更好交通管制，道路會變得更擁擠。"},{"en":"Crowded space increases the need for tracking, rules, and collision prevention.","zh":"擁擠的太空增加了追蹤、規則和防止碰撞的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rising congestion in orbit.","zh":"這個短語描述軌道擠塞日益增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in spite of this","meaning":"儘管如此","examples":[{"en":"In spite of this, satellites do not have to send back identification information.","zh":"儘管如此，衛星不需要傳回識別資料。"},{"en":"In spite of this means although this situation exists.","zh":"儘管如此意思是雖然這種情況存在。"},{"en":"The road is dangerous; in spite of this, some drivers still speed.","zh":"這條路很危險；儘管如此，有些司機仍然超速。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between what we might expect and what actually happens.","zh":"這個短語引入預期情況與實際情況之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when a fact seems surprising after the previous point.","zh":"當某事在前一點之後顯得令人意外時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be surprised to learn","meaning":"可能會驚訝地得知","examples":[{"en":"You may be surprised to learn that satellites do not need to send back identification information.","zh":"你可能會驚訝地得知，衛星不需要傳回識別資料。"},{"en":"To be surprised to learn something means to feel unexpectedness when you find out a fact.","zh":"驚訝地得知某事意思是在知道某事實時感到意外。"},{"en":"Students may be surprised to learn that some animals can survive without oxygen for short periods.","zh":"學生可能會驚訝地得知，有些動物能在短時間內不用氧氣仍存活。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase before presenting a fact that listeners may not expect.","zh":"說話者在提出聽眾可能沒有預期的事實前，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase creates interest and prepares the audience for new information.","zh":"這個短語製造興趣，並讓聽眾準備接收新資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"launch a satellite into space","meaning":"把衛星發射到太空","examples":[{"en":"You can launch a satellite into space without sending back identification information.","zh":"你可以在不傳回識別資料的情況下把衛星發射到太空。"},{"en":"To launch a satellite into space means to send it from Earth into orbit or beyond.","zh":"把衛星發射到太空意思是把它從地球送入軌道或更遠地方。"},{"en":"A company may launch a satellite into space to provide internet or weather data.","zh":"公司可能把衛星發射到太空，以提供互聯網或天氣資料。"},{"en":"Launching satellites creates responsibility because they may affect other objects in orbit.","zh":"發射衛星會帶來責任，因為它們可能影響軌道上的其他物體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the act of sending a satellite beyond Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述把衛星送離地球的行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"once it is out there","meaning":"一旦它進入太空","examples":[{"en":"Once it is out there, the satellite does not have to identify itself.","zh":"一旦它進入太空，該衛星不必表明身份。"},{"en":"Once it is out there means after it has reached space or the distant place being discussed.","zh":"一旦它進入太空意思是它到達太空或正在討論的遠處地方之後。"},{"en":"Once a message is out there online, it can be difficult to remove completely.","zh":"一旦訊息被放到網上，就可能很難完全移除。"},{"en":"After a satellite is in space, tracking and identification become more important.","zh":"衛星進入太空後，追蹤和識別變得更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase marks what happens after something has been sent away.","zh":"這個短語標示某物被送出後會發生甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"send back information","meaning":"傳回資料","examples":[{"en":"The satellite does not have to send back information to Earth.","zh":"該衛星不必向地球傳回資料。"},{"en":"To send back information means to transmit data from one place to another, often back to a control centre.","zh":"傳回資料意思是把數據從一處傳送到另一處，通常是傳回控制中心。"},{"en":"A weather satellite can send back information about clouds and storms.","zh":"天氣衛星可以傳回關於雲層和風暴的資料。"},{"en":"Without information being sent back, it is harder to know what an object is doing.","zh":"如果沒有資料傳回，便更難知道物體正在做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing data from machines, spacecraft, or sensors.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論來自機器、太空器或感應器的數據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"allow its identification","meaning":"使其身份可被識別","examples":[{"en":"The satellite does not have to send back information to allow its identification.","zh":"該衛星不必傳回資料以使其身份可被識別。"},{"en":"To allow its identification means to make it possible to recognise what the object is.","zh":"使其身份可被識別意思是令辨認該物體是甚麼變得可能。"},{"en":"A student card allows identification when students enter the library.","zh":"學生證使學生進入圖書館時身份可被識別。"},{"en":"Identification information helps controllers know which satellite belongs to which operator.","zh":"識別資料幫助管制員知道哪顆衛星屬於哪個營運者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information that makes recognition possible.","zh":"這個短語描述使辨認成為可能的資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"international systems for ensuring","meaning":"用以確保……的國際系統","examples":[{"en":"We have international systems for ensuring that planes can be tracked.","zh":"我們有用以確保飛機可被追蹤的國際系統。"},{"en":"International systems for ensuring something are shared systems used across countries to make sure it happens.","zh":"用以確保某事的國際系統，是跨國使用以保證某事發生的共同系統。"},{"en":"Aviation uses international systems for ensuring that pilots follow common safety rules.","zh":"航空業使用國際系統來確保機師遵守共同安全規則。"},{"en":"Shared systems are important when transport crosses national borders.","zh":"當交通跨越國界，共同系統很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised global cooperation for safety or control.","zh":"這個短語描述為安全或管制而建立的全球合作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prevent them from colliding with","meaning":"防止它們與……碰撞","examples":[{"en":"Air Traffic Control systems prevent planes from colliding with one another.","zh":"空中交通管制系統防止飛機彼此碰撞。"},{"en":"To prevent something from colliding with something else means to stop two objects from crashing into each other.","zh":"防止某物與另一物碰撞，意思是阻止兩個物體互相撞上。"},{"en":"Traffic lights prevent cars from colliding with pedestrians at busy crossings.","zh":"交通燈防止汽車在繁忙過路處與行人碰撞。"},{"en":"Preventing collisions requires accurate information about where moving objects are.","zh":"防止碰撞需要準確知道移動物體的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stopping physical crashes.","zh":"這個短語描述阻止實體撞擊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"one another","meaning":"彼此","examples":[{"en":"Air Traffic Control prevents planes from colliding with one another.","zh":"空中交通管制防止飛機彼此碰撞。"},{"en":"One another means each other, especially when two or more people or things interact.","zh":"彼此意思是互相，尤其是兩個或更多人或物互動時。"},{"en":"Students should help one another during group projects.","zh":"學生在小組項目中應彼此幫助。"},{"en":"Objects moving too close to one another can create danger.","zh":"移動物體彼此太接近可能造成危險。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a relationship between members of the same group.","zh":"這個短語顯示同一群體成員之間的關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"when it comes to","meaning":"說到……","examples":[{"en":"When it comes to the safety of satellites, tracking is still inadequate.","zh":"說到衛星安全，追蹤仍然不足。"},{"en":"When it comes to something means when discussing or considering that topic.","zh":"說到某事意思是在討論或考慮該主題時。"},{"en":"When it comes to exam preparation, regular practice is more useful than last-minute revision.","zh":"說到考試準備，定期練習比最後一刻溫習更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase helps shift attention to a specific issue.","zh":"這個短語有助把注意力轉到特定議題。"},{"en":"It is common in explanations and comparisons.","zh":"它常見於解釋和比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the safety of satellites","meaning":"衛星安全","examples":[{"en":"Tracking systems are important for the safety of satellites.","zh":"追蹤系統對衛星安全很重要。"},{"en":"The safety of satellites means protecting satellites from damage, collision, or loss of control.","zh":"衛星安全意思是保護衛星免受損壞、碰撞或失控。"},{"en":"Satellite safety matters because modern communication, navigation, and weather services depend on them.","zh":"衛星安全很重要，因為現代通訊、導航和天氣服務依賴衛星。"},{"en":"Poor tracking can put satellite safety at risk.","zh":"追蹤不足可能危及衛星安全。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to keeping satellites functioning and protected in orbit.","zh":"這個短語指保持衛星在軌道上運作並受保護。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"anything like enough","meaning":"遠遠不足夠","examples":[{"en":"At present, we do not have anything like enough proper ways of tracking satellites.","zh":"目前，我們遠遠沒有足夠適當方法追蹤衛星。"},{"en":"Anything like enough means nearly enough; in a negative sentence, it means far from enough.","zh":"Anything like enough 意思是接近足夠；用於否定句時，意思是遠遠不足夠。"},{"en":"The school does not have anything like enough computers for every student to use one.","zh":"學校電腦遠遠不足夠讓每位學生各用一部。"},{"en":"If resources are not anything like enough, the system cannot work properly.","zh":"如果資源遠遠不足夠，系統便不能正常運作。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises shortage.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調短缺。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"proper ways of tracking","meaning":"適當的追蹤方法","examples":[{"en":"We need proper ways of tracking satellites.","zh":"我們需要適當的追蹤衛星方法。"},{"en":"Proper ways of tracking are suitable and reliable methods for following the location of something.","zh":"適當的追蹤方法是用來跟蹤某物位置的合適而可靠方法。"},{"en":"Hospitals need proper ways of tracking medicine so expired drugs are not used.","zh":"醫院需要適當的藥物追蹤方法，以免使用過期藥物。"},{"en":"Without proper tracking methods, fast-moving objects can become dangerous.","zh":"沒有適當追蹤方法，高速移動物體可能變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on accurate and organised monitoring.","zh":"這個短語重點是準確而有組織的監察。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"entire satellites","meaning":"完整衛星","examples":[{"en":"We need to consider more than just entire satellites.","zh":"我們需要考慮的不只是完整衛星。"},{"en":"Entire satellites means complete satellites, not broken pieces or debris.","zh":"完整衛星意思是整顆衛星，而不是破碎部分或碎片。"},{"en":"Tracking entire satellites is easier than tracking tiny fragments from old spacecraft.","zh":"追蹤完整衛星比追蹤舊太空器留下的微小碎片容易。"},{"en":"Focusing only on whole satellites may ignore smaller objects that still cause damage.","zh":"只集中於完整衛星可能忽略仍能造成損害的小物體。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts complete objects with fragments.","zh":"這個短語把完整物體與碎片作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a greater threat","meaning":"更大的威脅","examples":[{"en":"A greater threat is the huge amount of space debris.","zh":"更大的威脅是大量太空碎片。"},{"en":"A greater threat means a more serious danger than something else mentioned.","zh":"更大的威脅意思是比已提及事物更嚴重的危險。"},{"en":"For cyclists, careless drivers may be a greater threat than bad weather.","zh":"對踩單車的人來說，粗心司機可能比壞天氣是更大的威脅。"},{"en":"Identifying the greater threat helps people decide where to focus safety efforts.","zh":"找出更大的威脅有助人們決定安全工作應集中在哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase compares levels of danger.","zh":"這個短語比較危險程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"huge amount of","meaning":"大量","examples":[{"en":"There is a huge amount of space debris in orbit.","zh":"軌道上有大量太空碎片。"},{"en":"A huge amount of something means a very large quantity of it.","zh":"大量某物意思是非常多的某物。"},{"en":"A restaurant may waste a huge amount of food if portions are not planned carefully.","zh":"如果食物分量沒有仔細計劃，餐廳可能浪費大量食物。"},{"en":"When there is a huge amount of material to manage, a clear system becomes necessary.","zh":"當有大量材料需要管理，清楚系統便變得必要。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises very large quantity.","zh":"這個短語強調數量非常多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"space debris","meaning":"太空碎片","examples":[{"en":"Space debris is a major threat to satellites.","zh":"太空碎片是衛星的主要威脅。"},{"en":"Space debris means broken or unused objects left in space, such as old satellite parts.","zh":"太空碎片意思是留在太空中的破損或不用物體，例如舊衛星部件。"},{"en":"Even a small piece of space debris can damage a satellite because it moves very fast.","zh":"即使一小塊太空碎片也可以損壞衛星，因為它移動得非常快。"},{"en":"More launches can create more debris if old objects are not removed or controlled.","zh":"如果舊物體沒有被移除或管制，更多發射可以產生更多碎片。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to dangerous waste material in orbit.","zh":"這個短語指軌道上的危險廢棄物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"broken bits of satellite","meaning":"衛星碎片","examples":[{"en":"Space debris includes broken bits of satellite.","zh":"太空碎片包括衛星碎片。"},{"en":"Broken bits of satellite are small pieces that have separated from damaged or old satellites.","zh":"衛星碎片是從受損或舊衛星分離出來的小塊物件。"},{"en":"A collision can create broken bits of satellite that continue moving around Earth.","zh":"碰撞可以產生繼續圍繞地球移動的衛星碎片。"},{"en":"These fragments are dangerous because they may be too small to track easily.","zh":"這些碎片很危險，因為它們可能太小而難以追蹤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one type of space debris.","zh":"這個短語描述一種太空碎片。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"junk from space stations","meaning":"太空站垃圾","examples":[{"en":"Space debris includes junk from space stations.","zh":"太空碎片包括太空站垃圾。"},{"en":"Junk from space stations means unwanted or broken material that comes from stations in space.","zh":"太空站垃圾意思是來自太空站的不需要或損壞材料。"},{"en":"Old tools, panels, or equipment can become junk from space stations if they are lost or discarded.","zh":"如果舊工具、面板或設備遺失或被丟棄，它們可能成為太空站垃圾。"},{"en":"Space junk matters because it can keep orbiting and threaten other spacecraft.","zh":"太空垃圾很重要，因為它可以繼續繞行並威脅其他太空器。"},{"en":"This phrase describes waste connected with human activity in space.","zh":"這個短語描述與人類太空活動有關的廢物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"and so on","meaning":"等等","examples":[{"en":"Space debris includes broken satellites, junk from space stations and so on.","zh":"太空碎片包括破損衛星、太空站垃圾等等。"},{"en":"And so on means and other similar things.","zh":"等等意思是以及其他類似事物。"},{"en":"A school bag may contain books, pens, notebooks, and so on.","zh":"書包可能有書、筆、筆記簿等等。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when the list could continue but the examples are enough.","zh":"當清單可以繼續但例子已足夠時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It helps avoid making a long list too repetitive.","zh":"它有助避免很長清單變得重複。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"so small that","meaning":"如此……以致","examples":[{"en":"Some pieces of space debris are so small that they are hard to identify.","zh":"有些太空碎片如此細小，以致難以辨識。"},{"en":"So small that means small to such a degree that a result happens.","zh":"如此細小以致某結果發生，意思是小到導致該結果。"},{"en":"Some insects are so small that they can hide inside tiny cracks.","zh":"有些昆蟲如此細小，以致能藏在微小裂縫中。"},{"en":"Very small objects can be difficult to see, measure, or track.","zh":"非常細小的物體可能難以看見、量度或追蹤。"},{"en":"This structure links a high degree with a consequence.","zh":"這個結構把高程度與後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hard to identify","meaning":"難以辨識","examples":[{"en":"Small pieces of space debris can be very hard to identify.","zh":"小塊太空碎片可能非常難以辨識。"},{"en":"Hard to identify means difficult to recognise or name accurately.","zh":"難以辨識意思是難以準確認出或命名。"},{"en":"A student’s handwriting may be hard to identify if the letters are unclear.","zh":"如果字母不清楚，學生的筆跡可能難以辨識。"},{"en":"Objects are harder to identify when they are small, far away, or badly damaged.","zh":"當物體細小、遙遠或嚴重損壞時，會更難以辨識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulty in recognition.","zh":"這個短語描述識別上的困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in addition","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"In addition, some operators may be unwilling to share information.","zh":"此外，有些營運者可能不願意分享資料。"},{"en":"In addition means also or as another point.","zh":"此外意思是另外或作為另一點。"},{"en":"The course teaches grammar; in addition, it gives students speaking practice.","zh":"課程教授文法；此外，它給學生口語練習。"},{"en":"This phrase helps add another idea to an explanation.","zh":"這個短語有助在解釋中加入另一個想法。"},{"en":"It is common in formal writing and presentations.","zh":"它常見於正式寫作和匯報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"operators","meaning":"營運者","examples":[{"en":"Some operators may be unwilling to share information about their satellites.","zh":"有些營運者可能不願意分享關於其衛星的資料。"},{"en":"Operators are people or organisations that run, control, or manage a service or machine.","zh":"營運者是營運、控制或管理服務或機器的人或機構。"},{"en":"Bus operators must make sure their vehicles follow safety rules.","zh":"巴士營運者必須確保車輛遵守安全規則。"},{"en":"Satellite operators control satellites and decide what information to share.","zh":"衛星營運者控制衛星並決定分享甚麼資料。"},{"en":"This word describes those responsible for running a system.","zh":"這個詞描述負責營運系統的人或機構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"unwilling to","meaning":"不願意","examples":[{"en":"Some operators may be unwilling to share information.","zh":"有些營運者可能不願意分享資料。"},{"en":"To be unwilling to do something means to not want to do it.","zh":"不願意做某事意思是不想做該事。"},{"en":"A student may be unwilling to speak in class because they fear making mistakes.","zh":"學生可能因害怕犯錯而不願意在課堂發言。"},{"en":"People may be unwilling to share information if they think it gives others an advantage.","zh":"如果人們認為資料會給別人優勢，可能不願意分享。"},{"en":"This phrase shows reluctance or refusal.","zh":"這個短語顯示不情願或拒絕。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"share information about","meaning":"分享關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"Operators may not want to share information about their satellites.","zh":"營運者可能不想分享關於其衛星的資料。"},{"en":"To share information about something means to give others details concerning it.","zh":"分享關於某事的資料意思是把有關它的細節提供給他人。"},{"en":"Doctors share information about patients only when privacy rules allow it.","zh":"醫生只有在私隱規則容許時，才會分享關於病人的資料。"},{"en":"Sharing accurate information helps different groups cooperate and avoid mistakes.","zh":"分享準確資料有助不同群體合作並避免錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making details available to others.","zh":"這個短語描述把細節提供給他人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be designed for","meaning":"被設計作……用途","examples":[{"en":"A satellite may be designed for military purposes.","zh":"衛星可能被設計作軍事用途。"},{"en":"To be designed for something means to be made with that purpose in mind.","zh":"被設計作某用途意思是製造時以該目的為考慮。"},{"en":"A waterproof jacket is designed for rainy weather.","zh":"防水外套是為雨天而設計的。"},{"en":"Objects designed for special purposes may contain information that owners do not want to share.","zh":"被設計作特殊用途的物體，可能包含擁有人不想分享的資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase explains intended use.","zh":"這個短語解釋預定用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"military purposes","meaning":"軍事目的","examples":[{"en":"Some satellites are designed for military purposes.","zh":"有些衛星被設計作軍事目的。"},{"en":"Military purposes are uses connected with defence, armed forces, or national security.","zh":"軍事目的是與防衛、武裝部隊或國家安全有關的用途。"},{"en":"Some technology is kept secret because it is used for military purposes.","zh":"有些科技因用於軍事目的而被保密。"},{"en":"Satellites for military purposes may collect sensitive information.","zh":"軍事用途衛星可能收集敏感資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes defence-related uses.","zh":"這個短語描述與防衛相關的用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"commercial reasons","meaning":"商業原因","examples":[{"en":"Some satellites are launched for commercial reasons.","zh":"有些衛星因商業原因而被發射。"},{"en":"Commercial reasons are business reasons connected with making money or providing paid services.","zh":"商業原因是與賺錢或提供付費服務有關的業務原因。"},{"en":"A company may open a new branch for commercial reasons, such as reaching more customers.","zh":"公司可能因商業原因開設新分店，例如接觸更多顧客。"},{"en":"Satellites launched for commercial reasons may support internet, television, or navigation services.","zh":"因商業原因發射的衛星可能支援互聯網、電視或導航服務。"},{"en":"This phrase explains business motivation.","zh":"這個短語解釋商業動機。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"competitors","meaning":"競爭對手","examples":[{"en":"Operators may not want competitors to have information about their satellites.","zh":"營運者可能不想競爭對手擁有關於其衛星的資料。"},{"en":"Competitors are businesses or people trying to succeed in the same market or activity.","zh":"競爭對手是在同一市場或活動中爭取成功的企業或人士。"},{"en":"Two restaurants on the same street may be competitors.","zh":"同一街上的兩間餐廳可能是競爭對手。"},{"en":"Companies may keep information private because competitors could use it to gain an advantage.","zh":"公司可能把資訊保密，因為競爭對手可以用它取得優勢。"},{"en":"This word describes rivals in business, sport, or other fields.","zh":"這個詞描述商業、運動或其他領域中的對手。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"even if","meaning":"即使","examples":[{"en":"Even if operators are willing to provide information, it is not easy to collect.","zh":"即使營運者願意提供資料，資料也不容易收集。"},{"en":"Even if means although a possible condition is true.","zh":"即使意思是雖然某個可能條件是真的。"},{"en":"Even if a student studies hard, they still need enough sleep before an exam.","zh":"即使學生努力溫習，考試前仍需要足夠睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a condition that does not remove the main problem.","zh":"這個短語引入一個不能消除主要問題的條件。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining that an obstacle remains.","zh":"當解釋障礙仍然存在時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be willing to","meaning":"願意","examples":[{"en":"Some operators may be willing to provide information.","zh":"有些營運者可能願意提供資料。"},{"en":"To be willing to do something means to be ready or happy to do it.","zh":"願意做某事意思是準備好或樂意做該事。"},{"en":"A student may be willing to help classmates revise before a test.","zh":"學生可能願意在測驗前幫同學溫習。"},{"en":"Cooperation becomes easier when people are willing to share useful information.","zh":"當人們願意分享有用資料，合作會變得較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase shows readiness, not force.","zh":"這個短語顯示準備或樂意，而不是被迫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"provide it","meaning":"提供該資料","examples":[{"en":"Even if operators provide it, the information is not easy to collect.","zh":"即使營運者提供該資料，資料也不容易收集。"},{"en":"To provide it means to give the information or item already mentioned.","zh":"提供該資料意思是給出剛才已提及的資訊或物件。"},{"en":"If the school asks for a parent’s signature, students must provide it before the trip.","zh":"如果學校要求家長簽名，學生必須在旅行前提供該簽名。"},{"en":"Providing information does not always mean it will be easy to organise or use.","zh":"提供資料不一定代表它容易整理或使用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to something previously discussed.","zh":"這個短語指回之前討論的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"easy to collect","meaning":"容易收集","examples":[{"en":"Satellite information is not easy to collect.","zh":"衛星資料不容易收集。"},{"en":"Easy to collect means simple to gather from different sources.","zh":"容易收集意思是能簡單地從不同來源取得。"},{"en":"Survey answers are easy to collect online if the form is short and clear.","zh":"如果表格短而清楚，網上調查答案就容易收集。"},{"en":"Information becomes hard to collect when many owners use different formats or refuse to cooperate.","zh":"當許多擁有人使用不同格式或拒絕合作，資料便難以收集。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the difficulty of gathering data.","zh":"這個短語描述收集數據的難度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"details are needed about","meaning":"需要關於……的細節","examples":[{"en":"Details are needed about the object itself.","zh":"需要關於物體本身的細節。"},{"en":"Details are needed about something means more specific information is required.","zh":"需要關於某事的細節意思是需要更具體資料。"},{"en":"Before a school trip, details are needed about transport, lunch, and emergency contacts.","zh":"學校旅行前，需要關於交通、午餐和緊急聯絡人的細節。"},{"en":"Without enough details, people cannot make safe or accurate decisions.","zh":"沒有足夠細節，人們不能作出安全或準確決定。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the information required for proper understanding.","zh":"這個短語引入正確理解所需的資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the object itself","meaning":"物體本身","examples":[{"en":"Scientists need details about the object itself.","zh":"科學家需要關於物體本身的細節。"},{"en":"The object itself means the actual object, not only its surroundings or location.","zh":"物體本身意思是實際的物體，而不只是其周圍環境或位置。"},{"en":"A mechanic needs information about the car itself, not just where it broke down.","zh":"技工需要知道車輛本身的資料，而不只是它在哪裏壞了。"},{"en":"Knowing the object itself helps experts judge its size, shape, purpose, and risk.","zh":"了解物體本身有助專家判斷其大小、形狀、用途和風險。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses attention on the thing being discussed.","zh":"這個短語把注意力集中在正在討論的東西上。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"以及","examples":[{"en":"Scientists need details about the object itself, as well as its location.","zh":"科學家需要物體本身的細節，以及其位置。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to.","zh":"以及意思是此外還有。"},{"en":"A job applicant should mention experience as well as qualifications.","zh":"求職者應提及經驗以及資格。"},{"en":"Good decisions often require facts about the object as well as the situation around it.","zh":"好決定通常需要關於物體的事實，以及其周圍情況。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another important item to the first one.","zh":"這個短語在第一項之外加入另一項重要內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at a particular time","meaning":"在特定時間","examples":[{"en":"Scientists need to know a satellite’s location at a particular time.","zh":"科學家需要知道衛星在特定時間的位置。"},{"en":"At a particular time means at one specific moment or point in time.","zh":"在特定時間意思是在某一個具體時刻或時間點。"},{"en":"A school bus timetable tells students where the bus will be at a particular time.","zh":"校巴時間表告訴學生巴士在特定時間會在哪裏。"},{"en":"For moving objects, location changes quickly, so time must be stated clearly.","zh":"對移動物體而言，位置很快改變，所以必須清楚說明時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when exact timing matters.","zh":"當精確時間重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"it is likely to be","meaning":"很可能會","examples":[{"en":"A satellite is likely to be moving at thousands of kilometres an hour.","zh":"衛星很可能會以每小時數千公里移動。"},{"en":"It is likely to be means it will probably be in that state or situation.","zh":"很可能會意思是大概會處於該狀態或情況。"},{"en":"The road is likely to be busy after school because many parents pick up children.","zh":"放學後道路很可能會繁忙，因為很多家長接孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses probability rather than certainty.","zh":"這個短語表達可能性，而不是確定性。"},{"en":"It is useful when making careful predictions.","zh":"當作出謹慎預測時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"thousands of kilometres an hour","meaning":"每小時數千公里","examples":[{"en":"A satellite may move at thousands of kilometres an hour.","zh":"衛星可能以每小時數千公里移動。"},{"en":"Thousands of kilometres an hour means a speed of many thousands of kilometres in one hour.","zh":"每小時數千公里意思是一小時內移動許多千公里的速度。"},{"en":"Aircraft travel fast, but satellites can move at thousands of kilometres an hour.","zh":"飛機飛得很快，但衛星可以每小時移動數千公里。"},{"en":"Very high speeds make tracking and collision prediction much harder.","zh":"極高速度令追蹤和碰撞預測困難得多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extremely fast movement.","zh":"這個短語描述極高速移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"constantly follow","meaning":"持續追蹤","examples":[{"en":"We do not have sensors that can constantly follow such fast objects.","zh":"我們沒有能持續追蹤這類高速物體的感應器。"},{"en":"To constantly follow something means to track it continuously without stopping.","zh":"持續追蹤某物意思是不停地連續跟蹤它。"},{"en":"A fitness watch can constantly follow a runner’s heart rate during exercise.","zh":"健身手錶可以在運動期間持續追蹤跑手的心率。"},{"en":"Constant tracking is difficult when an object moves quickly and is far away.","zh":"當物體移動快速且距離遙遠時，持續追蹤很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continuous monitoring.","zh":"這個短語描述連續監察。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"moving so fast","meaning":"移動得如此快","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to track something moving so fast.","zh":"追蹤移動得如此快的東西很困難。"},{"en":"Moving so fast means travelling at a very high speed.","zh":"移動得如此快意思是以非常高速度行進。"},{"en":"A small bird moving so fast may be hard to photograph clearly.","zh":"移動得很快的小鳥可能很難被清楚拍攝。"},{"en":"When an object is moving very fast, even a small error in tracking can matter.","zh":"當物體移動得很快，即使追蹤中有小錯誤也可能很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why observation becomes difficult.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何觀察變得困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"put forward a prediction","meaning":"提出預測","examples":[{"en":"Scientists can only put forward a prediction about where the satellite is heading.","zh":"科學家只能提出關於衛星前進方向的預測。"},{"en":"To put forward a prediction means to present an informed guess about what will happen.","zh":"提出預測意思是提供一個基於資料的未來推測。"},{"en":"Economists may put forward a prediction about next year’s prices.","zh":"經濟學家可能提出關於明年價格的預測。"},{"en":"Predictions are useful, but they can be wrong if the data is incomplete.","zh":"預測很有用，但如果數據不完整，也可能出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes offering a forecast for consideration.","zh":"這個短語描述提出預測供人考慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"concerning","meaning":"關於","examples":[{"en":"Scientists make predictions concerning where a satellite is heading next.","zh":"科學家作出關於衛星接下來會往哪裏去的預測。"},{"en":"Concerning means about or related to.","zh":"關於意思是有關或與某事相關。"},{"en":"The school sent parents a notice concerning the new uniform rules.","zh":"學校向家長發出關於新校服規定的通告。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “about”.","zh":"這個詞比 “about” 更正式。"},{"en":"It is often used in reports, notices, and official explanations.","zh":"它常用於報告、通告和官方解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"where the satellite is heading next","meaning":"衛星接下來會往哪裡去","examples":[{"en":"Scientists predict where the satellite is heading next.","zh":"科學家預測衛星接下來會往哪裏去。"},{"en":"Where the satellite is heading next means the direction or future path the satellite will take.","zh":"衛星接下來會往哪裏去，意思是衛星將採取的方向或未來路徑。"},{"en":"A bus tracker shows passengers where the bus is heading next.","zh":"巴士追蹤器顯示乘客巴士接下來會往哪裏去。"},{"en":"Predicting an object’s next path helps people avoid collisions and plan responses.","zh":"預測物體接下來的路徑有助人們避免碰撞並計劃應對。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on future movement.","zh":"這個短語重點是未來移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"some of the problems","meaning":"其中一些問題","examples":[{"en":"These are some of the problems that scientists are facing.","zh":"這些是科學家正面對的其中一些問題。"},{"en":"Some of the problems means several issues from a larger group of difficulties.","zh":"其中一些問題意思是較大困難群中的幾個議題。"},{"en":"Lack of time and limited equipment are some of the problems students face during projects.","zh":"時間不足和設備有限是學生做專題時面對的其中一些問題。"},{"en":"Mentioning some problems helps introduce the main challenges without listing everything.","zh":"提及部分問題有助引入主要挑戰，而不用列出所有內容。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the list may not be complete.","zh":"這個短語顯示清單未必完整。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"we are facing","meaning":"我們正面對","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer explains the problems we are facing in space traffic control.","zh":"講師解釋我們在太空交通管制中正面對的問題。"},{"en":"We are facing means we are dealing with or experiencing a difficulty now.","zh":"我們正面對意思是我們現在正在處理或經歷某困難。"},{"en":"The city is facing traffic problems because more people are driving.","zh":"城市正面對交通問題，因為更多人駕車。"},{"en":"When people understand what they are facing, they can plan better solutions.","zh":"當人們理解自己正面對甚麼，就能更好規劃解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes current challenges.","zh":"這個短語描述當前挑戰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"suggested solutions","meaning":"已提出的解決方案","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer considers some suggested solutions.","zh":"講師考慮一些已提出的解決方案。"},{"en":"Suggested solutions are ideas proposed to solve a problem.","zh":"已提出的解決方案是為解決問題而提出的想法。"},{"en":"A class may discuss suggested solutions for reducing lunch waste at school.","zh":"班級可能討論減少學校午餐浪費的已提出解決方案。"},{"en":"Suggested solutions need to be tested because not every idea will work.","zh":"已提出的解決方案需要測試，因為不是每個想法都有效。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to possible answers, not final decisions.","zh":"這個短語指可能答案，而不是最終決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one key issue","meaning":"一個關鍵問題","examples":[{"en":"One key issue is the way in which information is dealt with.","zh":"一個關鍵問題是資料被處理的方式。"},{"en":"One key issue means one very important problem or point.","zh":"一個關鍵問題意思是一個非常重要的問題或重點。"},{"en":"In online learning, one key issue is whether students have stable internet access.","zh":"在網上學習中，一個關鍵問題是學生是否有穩定網絡。"},{"en":"Identifying a key issue helps people focus on what matters most.","zh":"找出關鍵問題有助人們集中於最重要的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an especially important part of a problem.","zh":"這個短語引入問題中特別重要的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the way in which","meaning":"……的方式","examples":[{"en":"The key issue is the way in which information is dealt with.","zh":"關鍵問題是資料被處理的方式。"},{"en":"The way in which something happens means how it happens or is done.","zh":"某事發生的方式意思是它如何發生或被完成。"},{"en":"Teachers may study the way in which students learn new vocabulary.","zh":"老師可能研究學生學習新詞彙的方式。"},{"en":"Understanding how something is done can reveal why a problem continues.","zh":"理解某事如何被完成，可以揭示問題為何持續。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and useful in explanations.","zh":"這個短語較正式，適合用於解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be dealt with","meaning":"被處理","examples":[{"en":"Information needs to be dealt with properly.","zh":"資料需要被妥善處理。"},{"en":"To be dealt with means to be handled, managed, or processed.","zh":"被處理意思是被處理、管理或加工。"},{"en":"Customer complaints should be dealt with quickly and politely.","zh":"顧客投訴應快速而有禮地被處理。"},{"en":"If information is not dealt with properly, mistakes and confusion may follow.","zh":"如果資料沒有被妥善處理，之後可能出現錯誤和混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a problem, task, or material is handled.","zh":"這個短語描述問題、任務或材料如何被處理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"accessible at a global level","meaning":"可在全球層面取得","examples":[{"en":"Satellite information needs to be accessible at a global level.","zh":"衛星資料需要可在全球層面取得。"},{"en":"Accessible at a global level means available to people or organisations around the world.","zh":"可在全球層面取得意思是世界各地的人或組織都能取得。"},{"en":"Weather data is more useful when it is accessible at a global level.","zh":"天氣數據如果可在全球層面取得，會更有用。"},{"en":"Global access helps different countries respond to shared risks.","zh":"全球存取有助不同國家應對共同風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information that can be reached internationally.","zh":"這個短語描述能在國際上取得的資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at a global level","meaning":"在全球層面","examples":[{"en":"Information should be shared at a global level.","zh":"資料應在全球層面分享。"},{"en":"At a global level means across the world or involving many countries.","zh":"在全球層面意思是跨越世界或涉及許多國家。"},{"en":"Climate change must be discussed at a global level because it affects many nations.","zh":"氣候變化必須在全球層面討論，因為它影響許多國家。"},{"en":"Problems that cross borders need cooperation at a global level.","zh":"跨越國界的問題需要在全球層面合作。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises worldwide scale.","zh":"這個短語強調世界性規模。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"establish shared standards","meaning":"建立共同標準","examples":[{"en":"We need to establish shared standards for presenting information.","zh":"我們需要建立呈現資料的共同標準。"},{"en":"To establish shared standards means to create common rules that many groups agree to use.","zh":"建立共同標準意思是創造許多群體同意使用的共同規則。"},{"en":"Schools establish shared standards so teachers mark essays more fairly.","zh":"學校建立共同標準，讓老師更公平地批改文章。"},{"en":"Shared standards make cooperation easier because everyone follows the same format.","zh":"共同標準令合作更容易，因為每個人都跟從同一格式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating agreed rules for consistency.","zh":"這個短語描述為一致性而建立共同規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"agree on","meaning":"就……達成共識","examples":[{"en":"Countries need shared standards that they can all agree on.","zh":"各國需要大家都能就其達成共識的共同標準。"},{"en":"To agree on something means to reach a common decision about it.","zh":"就某事達成共識意思是對它作出共同決定。"},{"en":"A group project works better when students agree on deadlines and roles.","zh":"當學生就期限和角色達成共識，小組項目會運作得更好。"},{"en":"Agreement is important when several groups must use the same system.","zh":"當幾個群體必須使用同一系統，共識很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching shared understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述達成共同理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the way in which information is presented","meaning":"資料呈現的方式","examples":[{"en":"Standards are needed for the way in which information is presented.","zh":"資料呈現的方式需要標準。"},{"en":"The way in which information is presented means the format, order, or method used to show data.","zh":"資料呈現的方式意思是展示數據時使用的格式、次序或方法。"},{"en":"A clear table can improve the way in which information is presented to students.","zh":"清楚表格可以改善向學生呈現資料的方式。"},{"en":"Poor presentation of information can make even accurate data hard to use.","zh":"資料呈現方式差，即使數據準確也可能難以使用。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the form in which information is shown.","zh":"這個短語重點是資料被展示出來的形式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in other areas of science","meaning":"在其他科學領域","examples":[{"en":"Shared standards already exist in other areas of science.","zh":"共同標準已經存在於其他科學領域。"},{"en":"In other areas of science means in different scientific fields or subjects.","zh":"在其他科學領域意思是在不同科學範疇或學科中。"},{"en":"Standard units are used in other areas of science, such as chemistry and physics.","zh":"標準單位用於其他科學領域，例如化學和物理。"},{"en":"Looking at other scientific fields can show that shared systems are possible.","zh":"觀察其他科學領域可以顯示共同系統是可能的。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one field with other scientific disciplines.","zh":"這個短語把一個領域與其他科學學科作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not an impossible task","meaning":"並非不可能完成的任務","examples":[{"en":"Creating shared standards is challenging but not an impossible task.","zh":"建立共同標準具挑戰性，但並非不可能完成的任務。"},{"en":"Not an impossible task means difficult but still possible to complete.","zh":"並非不可能完成的任務意思是困難但仍可以完成。"},{"en":"Learning a new language as an adult is not an impossible task if practice is regular.","zh":"成年後學新語言如果規律練習，並非不可能完成的任務。"},{"en":"Calling something not impossible can encourage people to keep trying.","zh":"說某事並非不可能，可以鼓勵人們繼續嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase balances difficulty with hope.","zh":"這個短語平衡困難與希望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be put together","meaning":"被整合起來","examples":[{"en":"The collected information needs to be put together.","zh":"收集到的資料需要被整合起來。"},{"en":"To be put together means to be combined into one organised whole.","zh":"被整合起來意思是被合併成一個有組織的整體。"},{"en":"Students’ survey answers can be put together in a single spreadsheet.","zh":"學生的調查答案可以被整合到一張試算表中。"},{"en":"Information is easier to use when it is put together instead of scattered in many places.","zh":"資料被整合起來，而不是分散在多處時，會更容易使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes combining separate parts.","zh":"這個短語描述把分開部分合併。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"so it can be used","meaning":"以便能夠使用","examples":[{"en":"The information needs to be put together so it can be used.","zh":"資料需要被整合起來，以便能夠使用。"},{"en":"So it can be used means for the purpose of making it practical or useful.","zh":"以便能夠使用意思是為了令它變得實用或可用。"},{"en":"Notes should be organised clearly so they can be used for revision.","zh":"筆記應清楚整理，以便能夠用於溫習。"},{"en":"Data that is collected but not organised may be difficult to use.","zh":"已收集但未整理的數據可能難以使用。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose of organising something.","zh":"這個短語解釋整理某物的目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"involve creating","meaning":"涉及建立","examples":[{"en":"Collecting the information will involve creating a single database.","zh":"收集資料會涉及建立單一資料庫。"},{"en":"To involve creating something means to include the task of making it.","zh":"涉及建立某物意思是包括製作它這項任務。"},{"en":"Planning a school website may involve creating pages for news, forms, and events.","zh":"規劃學校網站可能涉及建立新聞、表格和活動頁面。"},{"en":"Large projects often involve creating systems before the main work can succeed.","zh":"大型項目通常涉及建立系統，主要工作才可成功。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an important part of a process.","zh":"這個短語引入過程中的重要部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a single database","meaning":"單一資料庫","examples":[{"en":"The information should be entered into a single database.","zh":"資料應被輸入單一資料庫。"},{"en":"A single database is one organised digital place where related information is stored.","zh":"單一資料庫是一個有組織的數碼位置，用來儲存相關資料。"},{"en":"A hospital may use a single database to store patient appointment records.","zh":"醫院可能使用單一資料庫儲存病人預約紀錄。"},{"en":"A single database reduces confusion because everyone checks the same source.","zh":"單一資料庫可以減少混亂，因為每個人都查閱同一來源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes centralised information storage.","zh":"這個短語描述集中式資訊儲存。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be entered","meaning":"被輸入","examples":[{"en":"The information can be entered into a single database.","zh":"資料可以被輸入單一資料庫。"},{"en":"To be entered means to be typed, recorded, or put into a system.","zh":"被輸入意思是被打字、記錄或放入系統。"},{"en":"Students’ marks are entered into the school system after exams.","zh":"考試後，學生分數會被輸入學校系統。"},{"en":"If data is entered incorrectly, later decisions may be wrong.","zh":"如果數據被錯誤輸入，之後的決定可能出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing forms, records, and databases.","zh":"這個短語常見於討論表格、紀錄和資料庫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"push forward new developments","meaning":"推動新發展","examples":[{"en":"Humans continue to push forward new developments in space.","zh":"人類繼續推動太空中的新發展。"},{"en":"To push forward new developments means to actively make new progress happen.","zh":"推動新發展意思是主動令新的進步發生。"},{"en":"Scientists push forward medical developments by testing new treatments carefully.","zh":"科學家透過仔細測試新療法來推動醫學新發展。"},{"en":"New developments can create benefits, but they may also create new risks to manage.","zh":"新發展可以帶來好處，但也可能產生需要管理的新風險。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active progress and innovation.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動進步和創新。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"congestion of the space environment","meaning":"太空環境擠塞","examples":[{"en":"Congestion of the space environment is only going to increase.","zh":"太空環境擠塞只會增加。"},{"en":"Congestion of the space environment means overcrowding in orbit caused by many satellites and objects.","zh":"太空環境擠塞意思是因許多衛星和物體而造成軌道過度擁擠。"},{"en":"Traffic congestion on roads helps us imagine congestion in space, where too many objects share limited paths.","zh":"道路交通擠塞可以幫助我們想像太空擠塞，即太多物體共用有限路徑。"},{"en":"More satellites can increase congestion and make collision avoidance harder.","zh":"更多衛星可以增加擠塞，並令避免碰撞更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes crowding in the orbital environment.","zh":"這個短語描述軌道環境中的擁擠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"is only going to increase","meaning":"只會增加","examples":[{"en":"Space congestion is only going to increase.","zh":"太空擠塞只會增加。"},{"en":"Is only going to increase means will continue to grow and is unlikely to decrease.","zh":"只會增加意思是會繼續增長，而且不太可能下降。"},{"en":"If no new buses are added, waiting time is only going to increase.","zh":"如果沒有新增巴士，等候時間只會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a problem will become worse without action.","zh":"這個短語提醒人，如果不採取行動，問題會惡化。"},{"en":"It is useful when predicting a rising trend.","zh":"當預測上升趨勢時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cope with","meaning":"應對","examples":[{"en":"We need a new system to cope with space congestion.","zh":"我們需要新系統來應對太空擠塞。"},{"en":"To cope with something means to manage or deal with a difficult situation.","zh":"應對某事意思是管理或處理困難情況。"},{"en":"Students need good planning to cope with exam pressure.","zh":"學生需要良好規劃來應對考試壓力。"},{"en":"A system that cannot cope with too much demand may break down or become unsafe.","zh":"不能應對過多需求的系統可能崩潰或變得不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes handling difficulty effectively.","zh":"這個短語描述有效處理困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a system like the one described","meaning":"像所描述那樣的系統","examples":[{"en":"We need to develop a system like the one described in the lecture.","zh":"我們需要發展一個像講座中所描述那樣的系統。"},{"en":"A system like the one described means a system similar to the one just explained.","zh":"像所描述那樣的系統意思是與剛才解釋的系統相似的系統。"},{"en":"A hospital may need a system like the one described to track medicine safely.","zh":"醫院可能需要像所描述那樣的系統來安全追蹤藥物。"},{"en":"Referring to a described system helps avoid repeating all its details.","zh":"提及所描述的系統，有助避免重複所有細節。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to an earlier explanation.","zh":"這個短語指回較早的解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"coordinate the work of","meaning":"協調……的工作","examples":[{"en":"The system should coordinate the work of spacecraft operators.","zh":"該系統應協調太空器營運者的工作。"},{"en":"To coordinate the work of people means to organise their actions so they work together smoothly.","zh":"協調人們的工作意思是組織他們的行動，使他們順暢合作。"},{"en":"A project manager coordinates the work of designers, writers, and technicians.","zh":"項目經理協調設計師、作者和技術人員的工作。"},{"en":"Coordination prevents different teams from repeating work or creating conflicts.","zh":"協調可以防止不同團隊重複工作或產生衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised cooperation.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織合作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"numerous spacecraft operators","meaning":"眾多太空器營運者","examples":[{"en":"The system would coordinate numerous spacecraft operators.","zh":"該系統會協調眾多太空器營運者。"},{"en":"Numerous spacecraft operators means many organisations or people who control spacecraft.","zh":"眾多太空器營運者意思是許多控制太空器的組織或人士。"},{"en":"Managing numerous bus operators in one city requires shared timetables and rules.","zh":"在一個城市管理眾多巴士營運者，需要共同時間表和規則。"},{"en":"When numerous operators work in the same environment, coordination becomes essential.","zh":"當眾多營運者在同一環境中工作，協調變得必要。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a large number of space-activity managers.","zh":"這個短語強調大量太空活動管理者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"it is essential that","meaning":"……是必要的","examples":[{"en":"It is essential that the system establishes trust.","zh":"該系統建立信任是必要的。"},{"en":"It is essential that means it is absolutely necessary that something happens.","zh":"某事是必要的意思是某事絕對需要發生。"},{"en":"It is essential that students know the fire exits before a laboratory lesson.","zh":"學生在實驗課前知道走火通道是必要的。"},{"en":"When safety depends on cooperation, trust is essential.","zh":"當安全取決於合作，信任就是必要的。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a very important requirement.","zh":"這個短語引入非常重要的要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"establish trust","meaning":"建立信任","examples":[{"en":"The system must establish trust among the people who use it.","zh":"該系統必須在使用它的人之間建立信任。"},{"en":"To establish trust means to build confidence that people or systems are reliable and fair.","zh":"建立信任意思是建立對人或系統可靠和公平的信心。"},{"en":"A teacher establishes trust by treating students consistently and listening to concerns.","zh":"老師透過一致地對待學生並聆聽關注來建立信任。"},{"en":"Trust encourages people to share information and follow shared rules.","zh":"信任鼓勵人們分享資料並遵守共同規則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a reliable relationship over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間建立可靠關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the people that use it","meaning":"使用它的人","examples":[{"en":"The system needs to establish trust among the people that use it.","zh":"該系統需要在使用它的人之間建立信任。"},{"en":"The people that use it means the users of the system.","zh":"使用它的人意思是該系統的使用者。"},{"en":"A school app must be easy for the people that use it, including teachers, parents, and students.","zh":"學校應用程式必須方便使用它的人，包括老師、家長和學生。"},{"en":"Systems work better when users trust them and understand their purpose.","zh":"當使用者信任系統並理解其目的，系統會運作得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the users affected by a system.","zh":"這個短語指出受系統影響的使用者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"both nationally and at a global level","meaning":"在國內及全球層面","examples":[{"en":"The system must build trust both nationally and at a global level.","zh":"該系統必須在國內及全球層面建立信任。"},{"en":"Both nationally and at a global level means within individual countries and across the world.","zh":"在國內及全球層面意思是在個別國家內部以及世界各地之間。"},{"en":"Disease control requires cooperation both nationally and at a global level.","zh":"疾病控制需要在國內及全球層面合作。"},{"en":"A space traffic system must work inside countries and between countries.","zh":"太空交通系統必須在國家內部以及國家之間運作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that action is needed on two scales.","zh":"這個短語顯示行動需要在兩個層面進行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"one interesting development","meaning":"一項有趣的發展","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer begins to introduce one interesting development.","zh":"講師開始介紹一項有趣的發展。"},{"en":"One interesting development means one new change or event that is worth attention.","zh":"一項有趣的發展意思是一個值得注意的新變化或事件。"},{"en":"One interesting development in education is the wider use of online lessons.","zh":"教育上的一項有趣發展是網上課堂更廣泛使用。"},{"en":"Interesting developments can show how a field is changing over time.","zh":"有趣的發展可以顯示一個領域如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used before introducing a new example, trend, or discovery.","zh":"這個短語常用於引入新例子、趨勢或發現之前。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 11 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 12/task-1":[{"front":"the right person to talk to about","meaning":"可以查詢……的合適人選","examples":[{"en":"Jan asks whether Peter is the right person to talk to about the Buckworth Conservation Group.","zh":"Jan 問 Peter 是否可以查詢 Buckworth Conservation Group 的合適人選。"},{"en":"The right person to talk to about something is the person who has the information, role, or experience needed to answer questions.","zh":"the right person to talk to about something 指有相關資料、職責或經驗，可以回答問題的人。"},{"en":"If you want to join the school choir, the music teacher is the right person to talk to about rehearsals.","zh":"如果你想加入學校合唱團，音樂老師就是可以查詢綵排安排的合適人選。"},{"en":"Speaking to the right person saves time because you do not have to repeat your questions to several people.","zh":"找對人查詢可以節省時間，因為你不用向幾個人重複問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when politely checking whether someone can help with a specific topic.","zh":"這個片語適合用於禮貌地確認某人能否幫忙處理特定主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"conservation group","meaning":"保育團體","examples":[{"en":"Jan wants to know more about the Buckworth Conservation Group.","zh":"Jan 想多了解 Buckworth Conservation Group。"},{"en":"A conservation group is an organisation that protects nature, wildlife, buildings, or local environments.","zh":"conservation group 指保護自然、野生動物、建築物或本地環境的組織。"},{"en":"A conservation group may organise beach cleaning, tree planting, or wildlife surveys.","zh":"保育團體可能組織清潔海灘、植樹或野生動物調查。"},{"en":"Conservation groups help communities care for places that could be damaged by neglect or development.","zh":"保育團體幫助社區照顧可能因忽視或發展而受損的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to people working together to protect something valuable.","zh":"這個片語通常指一群人共同保護有價值的事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"secretary","meaning":"秘書","examples":[{"en":"Peter is the secretary of the Buckworth Conservation Group.","zh":"Peter 是 Buckworth Conservation Group 的秘書。"},{"en":"A secretary is a person who organises records, meetings, messages, and administrative work for a group.","zh":"secretary 指為團體整理紀錄、會議、訊息和行政工作的人。"},{"en":"The club secretary may send emails to members before each meeting.","zh":"學會秘書可能在每次會議前向會員發電郵。"},{"en":"A good secretary helps a group run smoothly because information is recorded and shared clearly.","zh":"好秘書能幫助團體順利運作，因為資訊會被清楚記錄和分享。"},{"en":"This word can describe an office job or a role within a society or committee.","zh":"這個字可以描述辦公室工作，也可以指社團或委員會中的職務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"move to this area","meaning":"搬到這個地區","examples":[{"en":"Jan has just moved to this area.","zh":"Jan 剛搬到這個地區。"},{"en":"To move to this area means to start living in this neighbourhood, town, or region.","zh":"move to this area 指開始住在這個社區、城鎮或地區。"},{"en":"A family may move to this area because it is closer to school and work.","zh":"一個家庭可能因為這裡較接近學校和工作地點而搬到這個地區。"},{"en":"After moving to a new area, people often look for local shops, clubs, and transport.","zh":"搬到新地區後，人們常會尋找本地商店、社團和交通。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why someone may need information about community groups.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何某人可能需要社區團體的資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be interested in getting involved","meaning":"有興趣參與","examples":[{"en":"Jan is interested in getting involved in the conservation group.","zh":"Jan 有興趣參與這個保育團體。"},{"en":"To be interested in getting involved means to want to take part actively, not just watch from outside.","zh":"be interested in getting involved 指想積極參與，而不是只在旁邊觀看。"},{"en":"A student may be interested in getting involved in the drama club after seeing a performance.","zh":"學生看完演出後，可能有興趣參與戲劇學會。"},{"en":"People get involved when they care about an issue and want to help in a practical way.","zh":"當人們關心某議題並想實際幫忙，就會參與其中。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for volunteering, clubs, campaigns, and community work.","zh":"這個片語適合用於義工服務、學會、運動和社區工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"similar group","meaning":"類似團體","examples":[{"en":"Jan was in a similar group where she used to live.","zh":"Jan 以前住的地方有參加過一個類似團體。"},{"en":"A similar group is another organisation with the same kind of purpose, activities, or members.","zh":"similar group 指另一個有相近目的、活動或成員的組織。"},{"en":"If you joined an environmental club before, a local conservation group may feel like a similar group.","zh":"如果你以前參加過環保學會，本地保育團體可能感覺像類似團體。"},{"en":"Experience in a similar group can make it easier to join a new one.","zh":"在類似團體的經驗可以令加入新團體更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two groups without saying they are exactly the same.","zh":"這個片語比較兩個團體，但不表示它們完全一樣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"where I used to live","meaning":"我以前住的地方","examples":[{"en":"Jan joined a similar group where she used to live.","zh":"Jan 在以前住的地方參加過一個類似團體。"},{"en":"Where I used to live means the place where I lived in the past but do not live now.","zh":"where I used to live 指我過去住過、但現在不住的地方。"},{"en":"Where I used to live, there was a small library beside the market.","zh":"我以前住的地方，市場旁邊有一間小圖書館。"},{"en":"People mention where they used to live when comparing old and new communities.","zh":"人們比較舊社區和新社區時，會提到以前住的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase connects past experience with the present situation.","zh":"這個片語把過去經驗與目前情況連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tell me something about","meaning":"告訴我一些關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"Jan asks Peter to tell her something about the group’s activities.","zh":"Jan 請 Peter 告訴她一些關於該團體活動的資料。"},{"en":"Tell me something about means give me some basic information about a topic.","zh":"tell me something about 指給我一些關於某主題的基本資料。"},{"en":"A new student may ask, “Can you tell me something about the school library?”","zh":"新學生可能會問：「你可以告訴我一些關於學校圖書館的資料嗎？」"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when you want an introduction before asking detailed questions.","zh":"當你想先得到簡介，再問詳細問題時，這個片語很有用。"},{"en":"It sounds friendly and open-ended.","zh":"它聽起來友善，而且問題較開放。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a mixture of","meaning":"……的混合","examples":[{"en":"The group has a mixture of regular activities and special events.","zh":"該團體有定期活動和特別活動的混合。"},{"en":"A mixture of things means a combination of different types.","zh":"a mixture of things 指不同類型事物的組合。"},{"en":"A good school programme may include a mixture of lessons, games, and outdoor activities.","zh":"好的學校計劃可能包括課堂、遊戲和戶外活動的混合。"},{"en":"Having a mixture of activities helps members with different interests take part.","zh":"有多種活動組合，可以幫助有不同興趣的成員參與。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests variety rather than one single type.","zh":"這個片語暗示多樣性，而不是單一類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"regular activities","meaning":"定期活動","examples":[{"en":"Keeping the beach free of litter is one of the group’s regular activities.","zh":"保持海灘沒有垃圾是該團體的定期活動之一。"},{"en":"Regular activities are activities that happen repeatedly, such as weekly, monthly, or every season.","zh":"regular activities 指重複進行的活動，例如每週、每月或每季一次。"},{"en":"A school club may have regular activities every Friday after lessons.","zh":"學校學會可能每星期五放學後有定期活動。"},{"en":"Regular activities help members build habits and stay connected to the group.","zh":"定期活動幫助成員建立習慣，並與團體保持聯繫。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts repeated work with one-off special events.","zh":"這個片語把重複工作與一次性特別活動作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"special events","meaning":"特別活動","examples":[{"en":"The group organises both regular activities and special events.","zh":"該團體舉辦定期活動和特別活動。"},{"en":"Special events are activities arranged for a particular occasion, purpose, or date.","zh":"special events 指為特定場合、目的或日期安排的活動。"},{"en":"A library may hold special events during Reading Week.","zh":"圖書館可能在閱讀週舉辦特別活動。"},{"en":"Special events can attract new people because they feel different from normal meetings.","zh":"特別活動可以吸引新人，因為它們感覺不同於平常會議。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to less frequent activities with a clear focus.","zh":"這個片語通常指不太頻繁、而且有清楚重點的活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"keep the beach free of litter","meaning":"保持海灘沒有垃圾","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers try to keep the beach free of litter.","zh":"義工嘗試保持海灘沒有垃圾。"},{"en":"To keep a beach free of litter means to make sure rubbish is removed and does not build up there.","zh":"keep a beach free of litter 指確保垃圾被清走，並不在海灘累積。"},{"en":"Students can keep the school playground free of litter by using bins properly.","zh":"學生可以透過正確使用垃圾桶，保持學校操場沒有垃圾。"},{"en":"A clean beach protects wildlife and makes the area safer for visitors.","zh":"乾淨海灘能保護野生動物，也令該區對遊客更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase connects cleaning with prevention.","zh":"這個片語把清潔與預防連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"litter","meaning":"垃圾","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers spend time clearing litter from the beach.","zh":"義工花時間清理海灘上的垃圾。"},{"en":"Litter is rubbish left in public places instead of being put in bins.","zh":"litter 指被留在公共地方、而沒有放進垃圾桶的垃圾。"},{"en":"Plastic bottles, snack wrappers, and cigarette ends can all become litter.","zh":"膠樽、小食包裝和煙頭都可以成為垃圾。"},{"en":"Litter can harm animals, block drains, and make public spaces unpleasant.","zh":"垃圾會傷害動物、堵塞渠口，並令公共空間令人不快。"},{"en":"This word usually refers to rubbish in the wrong place.","zh":"這個字通常指放錯地方的垃圾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a few of us","meaning":"我們當中幾個人","examples":[{"en":"A few of the volunteers spend a couple of hours a month on beach cleaning.","zh":"義工當中幾個人每月花幾小時清潔海灘。"},{"en":"A few of us means a small number of people from our group.","zh":"a few of us 指我們團體中的少數幾個人。"},{"en":"A few of us stayed after class to help the teacher put away the chairs.","zh":"我們當中幾個人放學後留下來幫老師收拾椅子。"},{"en":"Even if only a few people help regularly, their work can make a visible difference over time.","zh":"即使只有幾個人定期幫忙，他們的工作長遠也可以帶來明顯分別。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds personal and conversational.","zh":"這個片語聽起來個人化而口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"spend a couple of hours a month on","meaning":"每月花幾小時在……上","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers spend a couple of hours a month on clearing the beach.","zh":"義工每月花幾小時清理海灘。"},{"en":"To spend a couple of hours a month on something means to use a few hours each month for that activity.","zh":"spend a couple of hours a month on something 指每月用幾小時做某活動。"},{"en":"A student may spend a couple of hours a month on volunteering at an animal shelter.","zh":"學生可能每月花幾小時在動物收容所做義工。"},{"en":"Small regular time commitments can still help a community project continue.","zh":"小量但定期的時間投入，仍可幫助社區項目持續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a manageable amount of monthly effort.","zh":"這個片語描述可負擔的每月努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"it’s awful how much","meaning":"……的數量很糟糕","examples":[{"en":"Peter says it is awful how much litter there is to clear.","zh":"Peter 說要清理的垃圾數量很糟糕。"},{"en":"It’s awful how much means the amount is surprisingly large in a bad or upsetting way.","zh":"it’s awful how much 指某數量大得令人驚訝，而且情況很差或令人不快。"},{"en":"It is awful how much food is wasted in the canteen every day.","zh":"飯堂每天浪費的食物數量很糟糕。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when a quantity shows a serious problem.","zh":"當某個數量顯示嚴重問題時，人們會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses shock or disappointment about the scale of something.","zh":"這個片語表達對某事規模的震驚或失望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"clear litter","meaning":"清理垃圾","examples":[{"en":"The group has a lot of litter to clear from the beach.","zh":"該團體有很多海灘垃圾要清理。"},{"en":"To clear litter means to remove rubbish from a place.","zh":"clear litter 指從某地方移走垃圾。"},{"en":"Students helped clear litter from the playground after sports day.","zh":"運動會後，學生幫忙清理操場垃圾。"},{"en":"Clearing litter makes public spaces safer, cleaner, and more pleasant to use.","zh":"清理垃圾可以令公共空間更安全、更乾淨，也更令人愉快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical cleaning work.","zh":"這個片語描述實際清潔工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I wish people would","meaning":"我希望人們會……","examples":[{"en":"Peter wishes people would be more responsible with their litter.","zh":"Peter 希望人們會更負責任地處理自己的垃圾。"},{"en":"I wish people would is used when someone wants others to change their behaviour.","zh":"I wish people would 用於某人希望其他人改變行為時。"},{"en":"I wish people would speak more quietly in the library.","zh":"我希望人們會在圖書館說話小聲一點。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows frustration because the speaker cannot control other people’s actions.","zh":"這個片語常顯示無奈，因為說話者不能控制別人的行動。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing habits that affect the community.","zh":"它適合用於討論影響社區的習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be more responsible","meaning":"更負責任","examples":[{"en":"Peter wishes people would be more responsible and take their rubbish home.","zh":"Peter 希望人們會更負責任，並把垃圾帶回家。"},{"en":"To be more responsible means to behave more carefully and accept duty for one’s actions.","zh":"be more responsible 指行為更小心，並承擔自己行動的責任。"},{"en":"Students should be more responsible by returning library books on time.","zh":"學生應更負責任，準時歸還圖書館書籍。"},{"en":"Responsible behaviour prevents extra work for others and protects shared places.","zh":"負責任行為可以避免為他人製造額外工作，並保護共享地方。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests that current behaviour is careless.","zh":"這個片語常暗示目前行為有點粗心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"take it home with them","meaning":"把它帶回家","examples":[{"en":"Visitors should take their litter home with them.","zh":"遊客應把自己的垃圾帶回家。"},{"en":"To take it home with them means to carry something away and bring it back home.","zh":"take it home with them 指把某物帶走並帶回家。"},{"en":"Hikers should take their rubbish home with them if there are no bins on the trail.","zh":"如果山徑上沒有垃圾桶，行山人士應把垃圾帶回家。"},{"en":"Taking litter home prevents animals from eating plastic or being trapped by waste.","zh":"把垃圾帶回家可以防止動物吃下塑膠或被廢物困住。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in countryside and beach notices.","zh":"這個片語常見於郊野和海灘告示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I totally agree","meaning":"我完全同意","examples":[{"en":"Jan totally agrees that people should be more responsible.","zh":"Jan 完全同意人們應該更負責任。"},{"en":"I totally agree means I strongly share the same opinion.","zh":"I totally agree 指我強烈持有相同意見。"},{"en":"I totally agree that students should not leave rubbish in the classroom.","zh":"我完全同意學生不應把垃圾留在課室。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to show strong support in a conversation.","zh":"人們在對話中用這個片語表達強烈支持。"},{"en":"It is more emphatic than simply saying “I agree”.","zh":"它比單純說 “I agree” 更有強調意味。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be happy to help with","meaning":"很樂意幫忙……","examples":[{"en":"Jan would be happy to help with beach cleaning.","zh":"Jan 很樂意幫忙清潔海灘。"},{"en":"To be happy to help with something means to be willing and pleased to assist.","zh":"be happy to help with something 指願意並樂於協助某事。"},{"en":"A student may be happy to help with setting up chairs before a school event.","zh":"學生可能很樂意幫忙在學校活動前擺放椅子。"},{"en":"When people are happy to help, volunteer work becomes easier to organise.","zh":"當人們樂意幫忙，義工工作會更容易組織。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds polite and enthusiastic.","zh":"這個片語聽起來有禮而熱心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"take dogs","meaning":"帶狗","examples":[{"en":"Jan asks whether it is OK to take dogs to the beach activity.","zh":"Jan 問是否可以帶狗參加海灘活動。"},{"en":"To take dogs means to bring dogs along to a place or event.","zh":"take dogs 指把狗一同帶到某地方或活動。"},{"en":"Families may ask whether they can take dogs on a countryside walk.","zh":"家庭可能會問可否帶狗參加郊野步行活動。"},{"en":"Events may ban dogs if wildlife, safety, or hygiene could be affected.","zh":"如果野生動物、安全或衛生可能受影響，活動可能禁止帶狗。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on bringing pets with you.","zh":"這個片語着重把寵物帶在身邊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"I’m afraid not","meaning":"恐怕不行","examples":[{"en":"Peter says, “I’m afraid not,” because dogs are banned from the beach.","zh":"Peter 說「恐怕不行」，因為狗被禁止進入海灘。"},{"en":"I’m afraid not is a polite way to say no or to give disappointing information.","zh":"I’m afraid not 是有禮貌地說不或給出令人失望資料的方法。"},{"en":"“Can I hand in the form tomorrow?” “I’m afraid not; the deadline is today.”","zh":"「我可以明天交表嗎？」「恐怕不行；截止日期是今天。」"},{"en":"People use this phrase to soften refusal.","zh":"人們用這個片語柔化拒絕。"},{"en":"It is more polite than saying only “No”.","zh":"它比只說 “No” 更有禮貌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be banned from","meaning":"被禁止進入……","examples":[{"en":"Dogs are banned from the beach itself.","zh":"狗被禁止進入海灘本身。"},{"en":"To be banned from a place means to be officially not allowed to enter or use it.","zh":"be banned from a place 指被正式禁止進入或使用某地方。"},{"en":"Smoking is banned from many public buildings.","zh":"許多公共建築物禁止吸煙。"},{"en":"Bans are often used to protect safety, cleanliness, or wildlife.","zh":"禁令常用來保護安全、清潔或野生動物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rule, not merely personal dislike.","zh":"這個片語描述規則，而不只是個人不喜歡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the beach itself","meaning":"海灘本身","examples":[{"en":"Dogs are banned from the beach itself.","zh":"狗被禁止進入海灘本身。"},{"en":"The beach itself means the actual sandy or seaside area, not nearby paths or cliffs.","zh":"the beach itself 指真正的沙灘或海邊區域，而不是附近小徑或懸崖。"},{"en":"Dogs may be allowed near the café but not on the beach itself.","zh":"狗可能可在咖啡店附近活動，但不可到海灘本身。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a distinction between the main place and surrounding areas.","zh":"這個片語區分主要地方和周邊地區。"},{"en":"It helps avoid misunderstanding when rules apply only to a specific part.","zh":"當規則只適用於特定部分時，它有助避免誤解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take them along","meaning":"帶牠們沿着……走","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can take dogs along the cliffs.","zh":"遊客可以帶狗沿着懸崖走。"},{"en":"To take them along means to bring them with you while you go somewhere.","zh":"take them along 指去某地方時把牠們或他們一起帶去。"},{"en":"Parents may take children along to a community fair.","zh":"家長可能帶孩子一起去社區嘉年華。"},{"en":"If dogs are allowed along the cliffs, owners can still enjoy a walk without entering the beach.","zh":"如果狗可沿着懸崖行走，主人仍可享受散步而不進入海灘。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and often used for bringing people or pets.","zh":"這個片語較口語，常用於帶人或寵物同行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the cliffs","meaning":"懸崖","examples":[{"en":"Dogs can be taken along the cliffs.","zh":"狗可以被帶到懸崖一帶。"},{"en":"Cliffs are high, steep rock faces, often beside the sea.","zh":"cliffs 指高而陡的岩石面，常位於海邊。"},{"en":"Walkers should be careful near cliffs because strong wind or loose ground can be dangerous.","zh":"行人接近懸崖時應小心，因為強風或鬆散地面可能危險。"},{"en":"Cliffs can offer beautiful views, but paths there need clear safety signs.","zh":"懸崖可以提供美麗景觀，但附近小徑需要清楚安全標誌。"},{"en":"This word describes a natural landform with a steep drop.","zh":"這個字描述有陡峭落差的自然地貌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"children are welcome","meaning":"歡迎小朋友參加","examples":[{"en":"Children are welcome to join the beach-cleaning activity.","zh":"歡迎小朋友參加海灘清潔活動。"},{"en":"Children are welcome means children are allowed and encouraged to take part.","zh":"children are welcome 指兒童獲准並受鼓勵參與。"},{"en":"Children are welcome at the library storytelling session.","zh":"歡迎小朋友參加圖書館講故事環節。"},{"en":"Saying children are welcome helps families know the activity is suitable for young people.","zh":"說歡迎小朋友參加，有助家庭知道活動適合年輕人。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds friendly and inclusive.","zh":"這個片語聽起來友善而包容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"manage a nature reserve","meaning":"管理自然保護區","examples":[{"en":"The conservation group also manages a nature reserve.","zh":"該保育團體也管理一個自然保護區。"},{"en":"To manage a nature reserve means to look after and organise a protected natural area.","zh":"manage a nature reserve 指照顧並組織一個受保護的自然區域。"},{"en":"Staff may manage a nature reserve by maintaining paths, signs, habitats, and visitor rules.","zh":"職員可能透過維護小徑、標誌、棲地和遊客規則來管理自然保護區。"},{"en":"Good management protects wildlife while allowing people to visit safely.","zh":"良好管理可以保護野生動物，同時讓人們安全到訪。"},{"en":"This phrase involves both environmental care and practical organisation.","zh":"這個片語涉及環境照顧和實際組織。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"nature reserve","meaning":"自然保護區","examples":[{"en":"There is a lot to do at the nature reserve all year round.","zh":"自然保護區全年都有很多工作要做。"},{"en":"A nature reserve is an area protected because of its wildlife, plants, habitats, or landscape.","zh":"nature reserve 指因野生動物、植物、棲地或景觀而受到保護的區域。"},{"en":"Schools may take students to a nature reserve to learn about birds and plants.","zh":"學校可能帶學生到自然保護區學習鳥類和植物。"},{"en":"Nature reserves need careful rules because too many visitors can damage habitats.","zh":"自然保護區需要仔細規則，因為太多遊客可能破壞棲地。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a protected natural area, not just any park.","zh":"這個片語指受保護的自然區域，而不只是任何公園。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"all year round","meaning":"全年","examples":[{"en":"The group has work to do at the nature reserve all year round.","zh":"該團體全年都要在自然保護區工作。"},{"en":"All year round means during every season of the year.","zh":"all year round 指一年四季都如此。"},{"en":"The swimming pool is open all year round because it is indoors.","zh":"游泳池因為是室內，所以全年開放。"},{"en":"Conservation work continues all year round because different tasks are needed in different seasons.","zh":"保育工作全年持續，因為不同季節需要不同任務。"},{"en":"This phrase means not only in summer or during holidays.","zh":"這個片語指不只是夏天或假期才有。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a popular place to visit","meaning":"受歡迎的遊覽地點","examples":[{"en":"The nature reserve is a popular place to visit.","zh":"自然保護區是一個受歡迎的遊覽地點。"},{"en":"A popular place to visit is a location many people like going to.","zh":"a popular place to visit 指許多人喜歡前往的地方。"},{"en":"The old harbour is a popular place to visit at weekends.","zh":"舊海港在週末是受歡迎的遊覽地點。"},{"en":"Popular places need good paths, signs, and rules because many visitors use them.","zh":"受歡迎的地方需要良好小徑、標誌和規則，因為有很多遊客使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place that attracts visitors.","zh":"這個片語描述吸引遊客的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"spend a lot of time doing","meaning":"花很多時間做……","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers spend a lot of time looking after the paths.","zh":"義工花很多時間維護小路。"},{"en":"To spend a lot of time doing something means to use many hours on that activity.","zh":"spend a lot of time doing something 指用很多小時做某活動。"},{"en":"Students spend a lot of time preparing for exams in the final month.","zh":"學生在最後一個月花很多時間準備考試。"},{"en":"If a task is important or difficult, volunteers may need to spend a lot of time on it.","zh":"如果任務重要或困難，義工可能需要花很多時間處理。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights effort and time commitment.","zh":"這個片語突出努力和時間投入。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"look after the paths","meaning":"維護小路","examples":[{"en":"The group looks after the paths in the nature reserve.","zh":"該團體維護自然保護區內的小路。"},{"en":"To look after the paths means to maintain them so they stay safe and usable.","zh":"look after the paths 指維護小路，使其保持安全和可使用。"},{"en":"Park staff look after paths by clearing leaves, repairing holes, and cutting back plants.","zh":"公園職員透過清理落葉、修補坑洞和修剪植物來維護小路。"},{"en":"If paths are not looked after, visitors may slip, get lost, or damage nearby habitats.","zh":"如果小路沒有被維護，遊客可能滑倒、迷路或破壞附近棲地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical maintenance work.","zh":"這個片語描述實際維修保養工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in good condition","meaning":"狀況良好","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers make sure the paths are in good condition for walking.","zh":"義工確保小路狀況良好，適合步行。"},{"en":"In good condition means not damaged and suitable for use.","zh":"in good condition 指沒有損壞，而且適合使用。"},{"en":"A second-hand bike is worth buying if it is still in good condition.","zh":"如果二手單車仍然狀況良好，就值得購買。"},{"en":"Keeping facilities in good condition prevents accidents and reduces repair costs later.","zh":"保持設施狀況良好可以防止意外，並減少日後維修成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the quality or state of something.","zh":"這個片語描述某物的質素或狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in good condition for walking","meaning":"適合步行","examples":[{"en":"The paths must be kept in good condition for walking.","zh":"小路必須保持狀況良好，適合步行。"},{"en":"In good condition for walking means safe, clear, and suitable for people to walk on.","zh":"in good condition for walking 指安全、清晰並適合人行走。"},{"en":"A path is in good condition for walking if it is not muddy, broken, or blocked.","zh":"如果小路不泥濘、不破爛、不被阻塞，就是適合步行。"},{"en":"Well-maintained walking paths help visitors enjoy nature without damaging plants.","zh":"維護良好的步行小路幫助遊客享受自然，同時不破壞植物。"},{"en":"This phrase connects physical condition with a specific use.","zh":"這個片語把實體狀態與特定用途連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"I could certainly help with that","meaning":"這方面我肯定可以幫忙","examples":[{"en":"Jan says she could certainly help with looking after the paths.","zh":"Jan 說維護小路這方面她肯定可以幫忙。"},{"en":"I could certainly help with that means I am definitely able and willing to assist with that task.","zh":"I could certainly help with that 指我肯定有能力並願意協助那項任務。"},{"en":"If the class needs someone to design posters, I could certainly help with that.","zh":"如果班上需要有人設計海報，這方面我肯定可以幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase shows confidence and willingness at the same time.","zh":"這個片語同時顯示信心和意願。"},{"en":"It is a polite way to volunteer for a specific job.","zh":"這是主動提出協助特定工作的一種有禮說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a programme of","meaning":"一系列……計劃","examples":[{"en":"The group has a programme of creating new habitats.","zh":"該團體有一系列創造新棲地的計劃。"},{"en":"A programme of something is an organised set of activities or projects over time.","zh":"a programme of something 指一套有組織、隨時間進行的活動或項目。"},{"en":"A school may run a programme of talks to help students plan their careers.","zh":"學校可能舉辦一系列講座，幫助學生規劃事業。"},{"en":"A programme gives structure, so work happens in stages rather than randomly.","zh":"計劃提供結構，讓工作分階段進行，而不是隨意進行。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests organised and repeated effort.","zh":"這個片語暗示有組織和持續的努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"create new habitats","meaning":"創造新棲地","examples":[{"en":"The group is creating new habitats in the nature reserve.","zh":"該團體正在自然保護區創造新棲地。"},{"en":"To create new habitats means to make new places where plants or animals can live.","zh":"create new habitats 指製造新的地方，讓植物或動物可以生活。"},{"en":"A school garden can create new habitats for butterflies and bees.","zh":"學校花園可以為蝴蝶和蜜蜂創造新棲地。"},{"en":"New habitats help wildlife survive when old habitats are damaged or disappearing.","zh":"當舊棲地受損或消失，新棲地可以幫助野生動物生存。"},{"en":"This phrase connects practical work with nature protection.","zh":"這個片語把實際工作與自然保護連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"habitats","meaning":"棲地","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers are creating habitats for wildlife.","zh":"義工正在為野生動物創造棲地。"},{"en":"Habitats are natural homes where plants and animals live, feed, and reproduce.","zh":"habitats 指植物和動物生活、覓食和繁殖的自然家園。"},{"en":"Ponds, forests, grassland, and hedges can all be habitats.","zh":"池塘、森林、草地和樹籬都可以是棲地。"},{"en":"If habitats are destroyed, wildlife may lose food, shelter, and breeding places.","zh":"如果棲地被破壞，野生動物可能失去食物、藏身處和繁殖地。"},{"en":"This word is central to conservation and ecology.","zh":"這個字是保育和生態學中的核心詞彙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make and install","meaning":"製作並安裝","examples":[{"en":"The group has finished making and installing nesting boxes.","zh":"該團體已完成製作並安裝鳥巢箱。"},{"en":"To make and install something means to build it and then put it in the correct place for use.","zh":"make and install something 指先製作某物，然後把它放到正確位置供使用。"},{"en":"Students may make and install bird feeders in the school garden.","zh":"學生可能在學校花園製作並安裝餵鳥器。"},{"en":"Installation matters because a well-made box will not help birds if it is placed badly.","zh":"安裝位置很重要，因為做得好的箱子如果放錯地方，也幫不到鳥類。"},{"en":"This phrase combines construction with practical placement.","zh":"這個片語結合製作和實際放置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"nesting boxes","meaning":"鳥巢箱","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers have installed nesting boxes for birds to use.","zh":"義工已安裝鳥巢箱供鳥類使用。"},{"en":"Nesting boxes are small boxes where birds can build nests and raise young.","zh":"nesting boxes 指讓鳥類築巢和育雛的小箱子。"},{"en":"A garden with nesting boxes may attract birds during breeding season.","zh":"有鳥巢箱的花園可能在繁殖季節吸引鳥類。"},{"en":"Nesting boxes help birds when natural tree holes are limited.","zh":"當天然樹洞有限，鳥巢箱可以幫助鳥類。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to artificial homes provided for wildlife.","zh":"這個片語指提供給野生動物的人造居所。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"work on","meaning":"致力於；處理","examples":[{"en":"The group is going to work on encouraging insects.","zh":"該團體將致力於吸引昆蟲。"},{"en":"To work on something means to spend time and effort improving, developing, or dealing with it.","zh":"work on something 指花時間和努力改善、發展或處理某事。"},{"en":"A student may work on pronunciation before a speaking exam.","zh":"學生可能在口試前練習發音。"},{"en":"Conservation groups work on habitats because wildlife needs food and shelter to survive.","zh":"保育團體致力處理棲地問題，因為野生動物需要食物和藏身處生存。"},{"en":"This phrase is very common for projects, skills, and problems.","zh":"這個片語很常用於項目、技能和問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"encourage insects","meaning":"吸引昆蟲","examples":[{"en":"The next project is to encourage insects in the reserve.","zh":"下一個項目是在保護區吸引昆蟲。"},{"en":"To encourage insects means to create conditions that attract and support insect life.","zh":"encourage insects 指創造吸引和支援昆蟲生活的條件。"},{"en":"Planting wildflowers can encourage insects such as bees and butterflies.","zh":"種植野花可以吸引蜜蜂和蝴蝶等昆蟲。"},{"en":"More insects can support birds, plants, and the wider food chain.","zh":"更多昆蟲可以支援鳥類、植物和更廣泛的食物鏈。"},{"en":"This phrase means helping insects live there, not persuading them like people.","zh":"這個片語意思是幫助昆蟲在那裡生活，而不是像說服人一樣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be important for","meaning":"對……很重要","examples":[{"en":"Insects are important for the biodiversity of the reserve.","zh":"昆蟲對保護區的生物多樣性很重要。"},{"en":"To be important for something means to play a necessary or valuable role in it.","zh":"be important for something 指在某事中扮演必要或有價值的角色。"},{"en":"Sleep is important for students’ memory and concentration.","zh":"睡眠對學生記憶和專注力很重要。"},{"en":"Insects are important for plants because many of them help with pollination.","zh":"昆蟲對植物很重要，因為許多昆蟲幫助授粉。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why something matters.","zh":"這個片語解釋某事為何重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"biodiversity","meaning":"生物多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Insects are important for the biodiversity of the reserve.","zh":"昆蟲對保護區的生物多樣性很重要。"},{"en":"Biodiversity is the variety of living things in an area, including plants, animals, fungi, and microorganisms.","zh":"biodiversity 指一個地區內生物的多樣性，包括植物、動物、真菌和微生物。"},{"en":"A pond with fish, insects, plants, and frogs has more biodiversity than an empty concrete pool.","zh":"有魚、昆蟲、植物和青蛙的池塘，比空水泥池有更多生物多樣性。"},{"en":"High biodiversity makes ecosystems healthier and more able to survive changes.","zh":"高生物多樣性令生態系統更健康，也更能承受變化。"},{"en":"This word is often used in environmental science and conservation.","zh":"這個字常用於環境科學和保育。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the reserve","meaning":"保護區","examples":[{"en":"The insects support the biodiversity of the reserve.","zh":"昆蟲支援保護區的生物多樣性。"},{"en":"The reserve means the nature reserve or protected area already mentioned.","zh":"the reserve 指前面提及的自然保護區或受保護地區。"},{"en":"Visitors must follow the rules of the reserve to protect wildlife.","zh":"遊客必須遵守保護區規則，以保護野生動物。"},{"en":"Work in the reserve may include maintaining paths, planting flowers, and monitoring animals.","zh":"保護區內的工作可能包括維護小路、種植花卉和監察動物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a protected natural area.","zh":"這個片語指回一個受保護的自然區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"run a project","meaning":"進行一個項目","examples":[{"en":"The group is running a project to identify butterfly species.","zh":"該團體正在進行一個辨認蝴蝶種類的項目。"},{"en":"To run a project means to organise and manage a planned piece of work.","zh":"run a project 指組織和管理一項有計劃的工作。"},{"en":"A school may run a project to reduce plastic waste in the canteen.","zh":"學校可能進行一個項目，以減少飯堂塑膠廢物。"},{"en":"Running a project requires planning tasks, people, time, and resources.","zh":"進行項目需要規劃任務、人手、時間和資源。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on managing an organised activity.","zh":"這個片語着重管理有組織的活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"identify the different species of","meaning":"辨認不同種類的……","examples":[{"en":"The project identifies the different species of butterflies that visit the reserve.","zh":"該項目辨認到訪保護區的不同蝴蝶種類。"},{"en":"To identify the different species of something means to recognise and name the different types.","zh":"identify the different species of something 指辨認並命名不同種類。"},{"en":"Science students may identify different species of plants during a field trip.","zh":"科學學生可能在實地考察中辨認不同植物種類。"},{"en":"Identifying species helps researchers understand which animals live in an area.","zh":"辨認物種幫助研究人員了解哪些動物生活在某地區。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in biology, conservation, and surveys.","zh":"這個片語常見於生物學、保育和調查。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"species of butterflies","meaning":"蝴蝶種類","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers identify species of butterflies in the reserve.","zh":"義工在保護區辨認蝴蝶種類。"},{"en":"Species of butterflies are different biological types of butterflies.","zh":"species of butterflies 指不同生物分類的蝴蝶種類。"},{"en":"A nature guide may teach children how to recognise common species of butterflies by wing colour.","zh":"自然導賞員可能教孩子透過翅膀顏色辨認常見蝴蝶種類。"},{"en":"Counting butterfly species can show whether a habitat is healthy.","zh":"統計蝴蝶種類可以顯示棲地是否健康。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to types of butterflies, not individual butterflies.","zh":"這個片語指蝴蝶類型，而不是個別蝴蝶。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take part in","meaning":"參加","examples":[{"en":"Peter thinks Jan might be interested in taking part in the butterfly project.","zh":"Peter 認為 Jan 可能有興趣參加蝴蝶項目。"},{"en":"To take part in something means to join and participate in an activity.","zh":"take part in something 指加入並參與某活動。"},{"en":"Students can take part in the beach clean-up after school.","zh":"學生可以放學後參加海灘清潔活動。"},{"en":"Taking part in community projects helps people meet others and learn useful skills.","zh":"參加社區項目可以幫助人認識他人並學習實用技能。"},{"en":"This phrase is more active than simply watching.","zh":"這個片語比單純觀看更主動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be involved in","meaning":"參與","examples":[{"en":"Jan was involved in a similar project where she used to live.","zh":"Jan 在以前住的地方參與過一個類似項目。"},{"en":"To be involved in something means to take part in it or have a role in it.","zh":"be involved in something 指參加某事或在其中有角色。"},{"en":"A parent may be involved in organising the school fair.","zh":"家長可能參與籌辦學校嘉年華。"},{"en":"Being involved in a project gives people experience and a sense of responsibility.","zh":"參與項目給人經驗和責任感。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe active participation, not just interest.","zh":"這個片語可以描述積極參與，而不只是有興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"something similar","meaning":"類似的事情","examples":[{"en":"Jan was involved in something similar before she moved.","zh":"Jan 搬家前參與過類似的事情。"},{"en":"Something similar means an activity, situation, or object that is like the one being discussed.","zh":"something similar 指與正在討論的事相似的活動、情況或物件。"},{"en":"If you have organised a school clean-up, you have done something similar to a beach clean-up.","zh":"如果你曾組織學校清潔活動，你就做過與海灘清潔類似的事情。"},{"en":"Previous experience with something similar can make a new task easier.","zh":"有類似事情的過往經驗，可以令新任務更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase compares things without saying they are exactly the same.","zh":"這個片語比較事物，但不表示它們完全一樣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"count species of","meaning":"統計……的種類","examples":[{"en":"Jan previously helped count species of moths.","zh":"Jan 以前幫忙統計蛾的種類。"},{"en":"To count species of something means to record how many different types are found.","zh":"count species of something 指記錄找到多少不同種類。"},{"en":"Students may count species of birds in a park for a science project.","zh":"學生可能為科學項目在公園統計鳥類種類。"},{"en":"Counting species helps conservationists measure biodiversity and notice changes over time.","zh":"統計物種種類幫助保育人士量度生物多樣性，並注意隨時間出現的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on variety, not only the total number of animals.","zh":"這個片語着重種類多樣性，而不只是動物總數。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"moths","meaning":"蛾","examples":[{"en":"Jan used to count different species of moths.","zh":"Jan 以前統計不同種類的蛾。"},{"en":"Moths are insects similar to butterflies, often active at night.","zh":"moths 指類似蝴蝶、常在夜間活動的昆蟲。"},{"en":"Some moths are attracted to light outside houses and shops.","zh":"有些蛾會被屋外和商店外的燈光吸引。"},{"en":"Moths can be important for ecosystems because they pollinate plants and provide food for birds and bats.","zh":"蛾對生態系統很重要，因為牠們為植物授粉，並成為鳥類和蝙蝠的食物。"},{"en":"This word names a group of insects, not a kind of bird.","zh":"這個字命名一類昆蟲，而不是鳥類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"I’d enjoy that","meaning":"我會很喜歡","examples":[{"en":"Jan says she would enjoy taking part in the butterfly project.","zh":"Jan 說她會很喜歡參加蝴蝶項目。"},{"en":"I’d enjoy that means I think I would find that activity pleasant or interesting.","zh":"I’d enjoy that 指我認為自己會覺得那活動愉快或有趣。"},{"en":"If the class visits the nature reserve, I’d enjoy that.","zh":"如果班上參觀自然保護區，我會很喜歡。"},{"en":"People say this when an activity sounds suitable for their interests.","zh":"當某活動聽起來符合興趣時，人們會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase politely shows enthusiasm.","zh":"這個片語有禮地表示熱情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"another job we’re doing","meaning":"我們正在做的另一項工作","examples":[{"en":"Another job the group is doing is replacing a wall.","zh":"該團體正在做的另一項工作是更換一堵牆。"},{"en":"Another job we’re doing means one more task or piece of work currently being carried out.","zh":"another job we’re doing 指目前正在進行的另一項任務或工作。"},{"en":"Another job we’re doing is repainting the classroom noticeboards.","zh":"我們正在做的另一項工作是重新油漆課室告示板。"},{"en":"Listing another job helps show the range of work a group is responsible for.","zh":"列出另一項工作有助顯示團體負責的工作範圍。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an additional task.","zh":"這個片語引入額外任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"replace the wall","meaning":"更換牆壁","examples":[{"en":"The group is replacing the wall on the southern side of the reserve.","zh":"該團體正在更換保護區南側的牆壁。"},{"en":"To replace the wall means to remove the old or damaged wall and build a new one.","zh":"replace the wall 指拆除舊牆或損壞牆壁，並建造新牆。"},{"en":"A school may replace a wall if cracks make it unsafe.","zh":"如果裂縫令牆壁不安全，學校可能更換牆壁。"},{"en":"Replacing a damaged wall can protect people, animals, and nearby property.","zh":"更換受損牆壁可以保護人、動物和附近物業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repair by putting in a new structure.","zh":"這個片語描述以新結構進行修復。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on the southern side","meaning":"在南側","examples":[{"en":"The damaged wall is on the southern side of the reserve.","zh":"受損牆壁在保護區南側。"},{"en":"On the southern side means on the part facing or located toward the south.","zh":"on the southern side 指在面向或位於南方的部分。"},{"en":"The main gate is on the southern side of the school.","zh":"正門在學校南側。"},{"en":"Directional phrases help people identify exact locations in a large area.","zh":"方向片語幫助人們在大型區域中識別準確位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when describing maps, buildings, and land.","zh":"這個片語常用於描述地圖、建築物和土地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"parking area","meaning":"停車區","examples":[{"en":"The wall is between the parking area and the woodshed.","zh":"那堵牆位於停車區和木棚之間。"},{"en":"A parking area is a place where vehicles can be parked.","zh":"parking area 指可停泊車輛的地方。"},{"en":"Visitors should leave their cars in the parking area before entering the reserve.","zh":"遊客進入保護區前應把車停在停車區。"},{"en":"Clear parking areas keep roads safer and stop cars from damaging grassland.","zh":"清楚的停車區令道路更安全，並防止汽車損壞草地。"},{"en":"This phrase is similar to “car park” but can sound more general.","zh":"這個片語與 “car park” 相近，但語氣較泛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"woodshed","meaning":"木棚","examples":[{"en":"The damaged wall is near the group’s woodshed.","zh":"受損牆壁在該團體的木棚附近。"},{"en":"A woodshed is a small building used for storing wood, tools, or outdoor materials.","zh":"woodshed 指用來存放木材、工具或戶外材料的小型建築物。"},{"en":"A nature reserve may keep path-repair tools in a woodshed.","zh":"自然保護區可能把修路工具存放在木棚。"},{"en":"A woodshed should be kept dry so wood and tools do not rot or rust.","zh":"木棚應保持乾爽，這樣木材和工具才不會腐爛或生鏽。"},{"en":"This word refers to a practical storage structure.","zh":"這個字指實用儲物建築。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be badly damaged","meaning":"嚴重損壞","examples":[{"en":"The wall was badly damaged in a storm last month.","zh":"那堵牆在上月的暴風雨中嚴重損壞。"},{"en":"To be badly damaged means to be seriously harmed or broken.","zh":"be badly damaged 指嚴重受損或破壞。"},{"en":"The playground fence was badly damaged after a fallen tree hit it.","zh":"一棵倒下的樹撞到遊樂場圍欄後，圍欄嚴重損壞。"},{"en":"Badly damaged structures may need full replacement rather than small repairs.","zh":"嚴重損壞的結構可能需要完全更換，而不只是小修。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe damage.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重損害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in a storm","meaning":"在暴風雨中","examples":[{"en":"The wall was damaged in a storm.","zh":"那堵牆在暴風雨中受損。"},{"en":"In a storm means during strong bad weather with wind, rain, thunder, or lightning.","zh":"in a storm 指在有強風、大雨、雷聲或閃電的惡劣天氣期間。"},{"en":"Several trees fell in a storm near the school.","zh":"學校附近有幾棵樹在暴風雨中倒下。"},{"en":"Storm damage can be dangerous because broken branches, walls, or roofs may fall later.","zh":"暴風雨造成的損壞可能危險，因為斷枝、牆壁或屋頂之後可能倒下。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the weather event that caused damage.","zh":"這個片語解釋造成損壞的天氣事件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a programme of events","meaning":"一系列活動","examples":[{"en":"The group has a programme of events at weekends and during the week.","zh":"該團體在週末和平日都有一系列活動。"},{"en":"A programme of events is an organised list or schedule of activities.","zh":"programme of events 指有組織的活動清單或時間表。"},{"en":"A museum may publish a programme of events for the summer holiday.","zh":"博物館可能發布暑假一系列活動。"},{"en":"A clear programme helps members choose activities that fit their interests and timetable.","zh":"清楚的活動安排幫助成員選擇符合興趣和時間表的活動。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests planned activities over a period of time.","zh":"這個片語暗示一段時間內有計劃的活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at the weekend","meaning":"在週末","examples":[{"en":"The group organises events at the weekend.","zh":"該團體在週末舉辦活動。"},{"en":"At the weekend means on Saturday, Sunday, or during the weekend period.","zh":"at the weekend 指在星期六、星期日或週末期間。"},{"en":"Families often visit nature reserves at the weekend.","zh":"家庭常在週末到訪自然保護區。"},{"en":"Weekend events are useful because many volunteers are free from work or school.","zh":"週末活動很有用，因為許多義工不用上班或上學。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English; American English often uses “on the weekend”.","zh":"這個片語常見於英式英語；美式英語常用 “on the weekend”。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"during the week","meaning":"在平日","examples":[{"en":"The group also organises events during the week.","zh":"該團體也在平日舉辦活動。"},{"en":"During the week means from Monday to Friday, rather than at the weekend.","zh":"during the week 指星期一至星期五，而不是週末。"},{"en":"Some libraries are quieter during the week than on Saturdays.","zh":"有些圖書館平日比星期六安靜。"},{"en":"Weekday events can help retired people, part-time workers, or flexible volunteers join in.","zh":"平日活動可以幫助退休人士、兼職人士或時間彈性的義工參與。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts weekdays with weekends.","zh":"這個片語把平日與週末作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"I presume","meaning":"我想；我估計","examples":[{"en":"Jan presumes that the group has guided walks.","zh":"Jan 估計該團體有導覽步行活動。"},{"en":"I presume means I suppose or I think something is probably true.","zh":"I presume 指我想或我估計某事大概是真的。"},{"en":"I presume the meeting is in the library because that is where we met last time.","zh":"我估計會議在圖書館，因為我們上次在那裡見面。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when making a reasonable guess.","zh":"人們作合理推測時會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It sounds more formal than “I guess”.","zh":"它比 “I guess” 較正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"guided walks","meaning":"導覽步行活動","examples":[{"en":"The group organises guided walks in the local countryside.","zh":"該團體在本地郊野舉辦導覽步行活動。"},{"en":"Guided walks are walks led by someone who explains the route, history, nature, or safety points.","zh":"guided walks 指由某人帶領並解釋路線、歷史、自然或安全重點的步行活動。"},{"en":"A school may join a guided walk to learn about plants in a country park.","zh":"學校可能參加導覽步行活動，學習郊野公園中的植物。"},{"en":"Guided walks help visitors explore safely while learning more than they would alone.","zh":"導覽步行活動幫助遊客安全探索，同時學到比獨自行走更多的知識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an organised walking activity with a leader.","zh":"這個片語描述有領隊的有組織步行活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get to know","meaning":"了解；熟悉","examples":[{"en":"Jan wants to get to know the local countryside.","zh":"Jan 想了解本地郊野。"},{"en":"To get to know a place means to become familiar with it through experience.","zh":"get to know a place 指透過經驗逐漸熟悉某地方。"},{"en":"A new student needs time to get to know the school building.","zh":"新學生需要時間熟悉校舍。"},{"en":"Walking, joining activities, and talking to locals can help people get to know an area.","zh":"步行、參加活動和與本地人交談，可以幫助人熟悉一個地區。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests gradual familiarity, not instant knowledge.","zh":"這個片語暗示逐漸熟悉，而不是立即知道。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"local countryside","meaning":"本地郊野","examples":[{"en":"Jan wants to get to know the local countryside.","zh":"Jan 想熟悉本地郊野。"},{"en":"Local countryside means the rural or natural areas near where someone lives.","zh":"local countryside 指某人居住地附近的鄉郊或自然地區。"},{"en":"Families may explore the local countryside by walking along rivers and fields.","zh":"家庭可能沿河流和田野散步，探索本地郊野。"},{"en":"Knowing the local countryside can help residents appreciate wildlife and protect paths.","zh":"熟悉本地郊野可以幫助居民欣賞野生動物並保護小徑。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts nearby rural areas with towns and cities.","zh":"這個片語把附近鄉郊地區與城鎮和城市作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be new to the area","meaning":"剛到這個地區","examples":[{"en":"Jan is new to the area.","zh":"Jan 剛到這個地區。"},{"en":"To be new to the area means to have recently moved there or not know the place well yet.","zh":"be new to the area 指最近搬到那裡，或尚未熟悉該地方。"},{"en":"A neighbour who is new to the area may ask where the nearest supermarket is.","zh":"剛到這個地區的鄰居可能會問最近的超市在哪裡。"},{"en":"People who are new to an area often join clubs to meet others and learn local places.","zh":"剛到一個地區的人常會加入社團，以認識他人並了解本地地方。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why someone may need help or information.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何某人可能需要幫助或資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a week on Saturday","meaning":"下星期六","examples":[{"en":"The next walk is to Ruston Island a week on Saturday.","zh":"下一次步行活動是下星期六前往 Ruston Island。"},{"en":"A week on Saturday means the Saturday after the coming Saturday, or one week from this Saturday in British English.","zh":"a week on Saturday 在英式英語中指即將到來的星期六之後的那個星期六，或由這個星期六起一星期後。"},{"en":"The school fair is a week on Saturday, so we still have time to prepare.","zh":"學校嘉年華在下星期六，所以我們仍有時間準備。"},{"en":"This phrase helps give a future date without naming the exact calendar day.","zh":"這個片語不用說出確切日期，也能表達未來時間。"},{"en":"It can be confusing, so people may confirm the date if timing matters.","zh":"它可能令人混淆，所以如果時間重要，人們可能會確認日期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"meet in the car park","meaning":"在停車場集合","examples":[{"en":"The group will meet in the car park at Dunsmore Beach.","zh":"該團體將在 Dunsmore Beach 的停車場集合。"},{"en":"To meet in the car park means to gather in the parking area before starting an activity.","zh":"meet in the car park 指活動開始前在停車區集合。"},{"en":"Students may meet in the car park before leaving for a school trip.","zh":"學生可能在學校旅行出發前於停車場集合。"},{"en":"Meeting in one clear place helps organisers check attendance and give instructions.","zh":"在一個清楚地點集合，有助主辦方點名並給出指示。"},{"en":"This phrase is common for outdoor trips and group travel.","zh":"這個片語常用於戶外活動和團體出行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"low tide","meaning":"退潮","examples":[{"en":"The group will walk to the island at low tide.","zh":"該團體將在退潮時步行到島上。"},{"en":"Low tide is the time when the sea level is lower and more sand or rocks are exposed.","zh":"low tide 指海平面較低、更多沙地或岩石露出的時候。"},{"en":"People can sometimes walk across a beach safely at low tide.","zh":"人們有時可以在退潮時安全橫過海灘。"},{"en":"Tide times matter because a safe path can disappear when the sea comes back in.","zh":"潮汐時間很重要，因為安全路線在潮水回來時可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase is important for coastal walks and sea safety.","zh":"這個片語對海岸步行和海邊安全很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dry enough for","meaning":"乾得足以……","examples":[{"en":"At low tide, the sands are dry enough for the group to walk to the island.","zh":"退潮時，沙地乾得足以讓團體步行到島上。"},{"en":"Dry enough for something means sufficiently dry to allow that activity.","zh":"dry enough for something 指乾燥程度足以進行某活動。"},{"en":"The grass is dry enough for students to sit on after lunch.","zh":"午飯後，草地乾得足以讓學生坐下。"},{"en":"If the sand is not dry enough, walkers may get wet or stuck.","zh":"如果沙地不夠乾，行人可能會弄濕或陷住。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a condition with what people can safely do.","zh":"這個片語把某條件與人們可安全做到的事連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"without getting wet","meaning":"不會弄濕","examples":[{"en":"The group can walk to the island without getting wet.","zh":"團體可以步行到島上而不會弄濕。"},{"en":"Without getting wet means without water touching your clothes, shoes, or body.","zh":"without getting wet 指衣服、鞋或身體不會碰到水。"},{"en":"Children can cross the playground without getting wet if they use the covered path.","zh":"如果孩子使用有蓋通道，就可以穿過操場而不會弄濕。"},{"en":"Coastal walkers need tide information if they want to cross safely without getting wet.","zh":"海岸步行者如果想安全橫過而不弄濕，就需要潮汐資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes avoiding contact with water.","zh":"這個片語描述避免接觸水。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a great place to explore","meaning":"適合探索的好地方","examples":[{"en":"Ruston Island is a great place to explore.","zh":"Ruston Island 是適合探索的好地方。"},{"en":"A great place to explore is somewhere interesting to walk around, observe, and discover.","zh":"a great place to explore 指一個很有趣、適合四處走動、觀察和發現的地方。"},{"en":"A museum with many small rooms can be a great place to explore on a rainy day.","zh":"有許多小房間的博物館，在雨天可以是適合探索的好地方。"},{"en":"Places with varied habitats give visitors more to see and learn.","zh":"有多樣棲地的地方給遊客更多可看和可學的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests curiosity, discovery, and enjoyment.","zh":"這個片語暗示好奇、發現和享受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a range of habitats","meaning":"多種棲地","examples":[{"en":"The island has a range of habitats.","zh":"該島有多種棲地。"},{"en":"A range of habitats means several different natural environments for plants and animals.","zh":"a range of habitats 指幾種不同的自然環境，供植物和動物生活。"},{"en":"A nature reserve may have a range of habitats, such as woodland, ponds, grassland, and marshes.","zh":"自然保護區可能有多種棲地，例如樹林、池塘、草地和沼澤。"},{"en":"Different habitats support different species, so variety can increase biodiversity.","zh":"不同棲地支援不同物種，因此多樣性可以增加生物多樣性。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises ecological diversity.","zh":"這個片語強調生態多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an ideal location for","meaning":"觀察……的理想地點","examples":[{"en":"Ruston Island is an ideal location for seeing seals.","zh":"Ruston Island 是觀察海豹的理想地點。"},{"en":"An ideal location for something is a very suitable place for that activity or purpose.","zh":"an ideal location for something 指非常適合某活動或目的的地方。"},{"en":"A quiet library corner is an ideal location for reading before exams.","zh":"安靜的圖書館角落是考試前閱讀的理想地點。"},{"en":"A place becomes ideal when its natural conditions match what visitors want to do.","zh":"當一個地方的自然條件符合遊客想做的事，它就成為理想地點。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly suggests suitability.","zh":"這個片語強烈暗示合適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"see seals","meaning":"觀察海豹","examples":[{"en":"The island is an ideal location for seeing seals.","zh":"該島是觀察海豹的理想地點。"},{"en":"To see seals means to observe these sea mammals in their natural environment.","zh":"see seals 指在自然環境中觀察這些海洋哺乳動物。"},{"en":"Visitors may see seals resting on rocks near the coast.","zh":"遊客可能看見海豹在海岸附近的岩石上休息。"},{"en":"People should keep their distance when they see seals so the animals are not disturbed.","zh":"人們觀察海豹時應保持距離，避免打擾動物。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to wildlife watching, not touching or feeding animals.","zh":"這個片語通常指觀察野生動物，而不是觸摸或餵飼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"just off the coast","meaning":"就在近岸處","examples":[{"en":"Visitors may see seals just off the coast.","zh":"遊客可能就在近岸處看見海豹。"},{"en":"Just off the coast means in the sea very near the shore.","zh":"just off the coast 指在非常接近海岸的海上。"},{"en":"Small fishing boats were floating just off the coast.","zh":"小漁船就在近岸處漂浮。"},{"en":"Animals seen just off the coast can often be watched from the beach or cliffs.","zh":"在近岸處看見的動物，通常可以從海灘或懸崖觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a location close to land but still in the water.","zh":"這個片語描述接近陸地但仍在水中的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on the beach","meaning":"在海灘上","examples":[{"en":"Visitors may even see seals on the beach.","zh":"遊客甚至可能在海灘上看見海豹。"},{"en":"On the beach means on the sand or shore beside the sea.","zh":"on the beach 指在海邊的沙灘或岸邊。"},{"en":"Families often sit on the beach to eat lunch and watch the waves.","zh":"家庭常坐在海灘上吃午餐和看海浪。"},{"en":"If seals are on the beach, visitors should avoid getting too close.","zh":"如果海豹在海灘上，遊客應避免太接近。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a location at the seaside.","zh":"這個片語描述海邊位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"Jan asks whether they should bring something, like a picnic, for instance.","zh":"Jan 問他們是否應帶些東西，例如野餐食物。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance 指例如。"},{"en":"Volunteers should bring practical items, water bottles, for instance.","zh":"義工應帶實用物品，例如水樽。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to give one example from a larger group of possibilities.","zh":"人們用這個片語從較大可能性中提出一個例子。"},{"en":"It is slightly more formal than “for example” in casual speech.","zh":"在口語中，它比 “for example” 略正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bring a picnic","meaning":"帶野餐食物","examples":[{"en":"Participants should bring a picnic for the full-day walk.","zh":"參加者應為全日步行活動帶野餐食物。"},{"en":"To bring a picnic means to carry food and drinks to eat outdoors during an outing.","zh":"bring a picnic 指帶食物和飲品，在戶外活動期間食用。"},{"en":"Families may bring a picnic to the park instead of buying lunch there.","zh":"家庭可能帶野餐食物到公園，而不是在那裡買午餐。"},{"en":"Bringing a picnic is useful on long walks because there may be no shops nearby.","zh":"長途步行時帶野餐食物很有用，因為附近可能沒有商店。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to prepared food for an outdoor meal.","zh":"這個片語指為戶外餐準備食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"full-day walk","meaning":"全日步行活動","examples":[{"en":"The walk to Ruston Island is a full-day walk.","zh":"前往 Ruston Island 的步行是全日步行活動。"},{"en":"A full-day walk is a walking activity that takes most or all of the day.","zh":"full-day walk 指需時大部分或整天的步行活動。"},{"en":"A full-day walk requires food, water, suitable shoes, and enough energy.","zh":"全日步行活動需要食物、水、合適鞋履和足夠體力。"},{"en":"Participants should check the weather before a full-day walk because conditions may change.","zh":"參加者在全日步行活動前應查看天氣，因為情況可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the length and seriousness of a walking event.","zh":"這個片語描述步行活動的長度和認真程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"walking across and back","meaning":"來回步行橫過","examples":[{"en":"Participants will be wet walking across and back.","zh":"參加者來回步行橫過時會弄濕。"},{"en":"Walking across and back means going from one side to the other and then returning.","zh":"walking across and back 指從一邊走到另一邊，然後再走回來。"},{"en":"Students walked across the field and back during the sports test.","zh":"學生在體育測驗中來回步行橫過操場。"},{"en":"If the path is wet, walking across and back can leave shoes soaked.","zh":"如果路面濕，來回步行橫過會令鞋子濕透。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a return journey on foot.","zh":"這個片語描述步行來回路程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Peter tells Jan to make sure her boots are waterproof.","zh":"Peter 告訴 Jan 要確保她的靴子是防水的。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check carefully so that something is true or done.","zh":"make sure 指仔細檢查，確保某事是真的或已完成。"},{"en":"Make sure your phone is charged before a long walk.","zh":"長途步行前，確保你的電話已充電。"},{"en":"Checking equipment before an outdoor activity can prevent problems later.","zh":"戶外活動前檢查裝備可以防止之後出問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when something is important enough to confirm.","zh":"當某事重要得需要確認時，會使用這個片語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"waterproof","meaning":"防水的","examples":[{"en":"Participants should wear waterproof boots.","zh":"參加者應穿防水靴。"},{"en":"Waterproof means designed to stop water from passing through.","zh":"waterproof 指設計成能阻止水穿透。"},{"en":"A waterproof jacket keeps students dry during a rainy school trip.","zh":"防水外套可以在下雨的學校旅行中令學生保持乾爽。"},{"en":"Waterproof boots are important on wet paths because ordinary shoes may fill with water.","zh":"在濕滑小徑上，防水靴很重要，因為普通鞋可能進水。"},{"en":"This word describes protection against water.","zh":"這個字描述對水的保護。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"buy a new pair","meaning":"買一雙新的","examples":[{"en":"Jan needs to buy a new pair of boots.","zh":"Jan 需要買一雙新的靴子。"},{"en":"To buy a new pair means to purchase two matching items, such as shoes, socks, or gloves.","zh":"buy a new pair 指購買兩件成對物品，例如鞋、襪或手套。"},{"en":"A student may buy a new pair of trainers before sports day.","zh":"學生可能在運動會前買一雙新的運動鞋。"},{"en":"Buying a new pair is necessary when the old pair is damaged or no longer fits.","zh":"當舊的一雙已損壞或不再合穿，就有需要買一雙新的。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for items that normally come in twos.","zh":"這個片語用於通常成雙出現的物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"current ones","meaning":"現時那雙","examples":[{"en":"There is a hole in one of Jan’s current boots.","zh":"Jan 現時那雙靴子其中一隻有一個洞。"},{"en":"Current ones means the ones someone has or uses now.","zh":"current ones 指某人現在擁有或使用的那些。"},{"en":"My current glasses are scratched, so I need a new pair.","zh":"我現時那副眼鏡刮花了，所以需要一副新的。"},{"en":"Comparing current items with new ones helps people decide whether replacement is necessary.","zh":"把現有物品與新物品比較，有助人們決定是否需要更換。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the noun already mentioned.","zh":"這個片語避免重複已提及的名詞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"there’s a hole in","meaning":"……有一個洞","examples":[{"en":"There is a hole in one of Jan’s current boots.","zh":"Jan 現時那雙靴子其中一隻有一個洞。"},{"en":"There’s a hole in something means there is an opening or tear where there should not be one.","zh":"there’s a hole in something 指某物有不應存在的開口或破洞。"},{"en":"There is a hole in my schoolbag, so my pens keep falling out.","zh":"我的書包有一個洞，所以筆一直掉出來。"},{"en":"A hole in a boot can let in water and make a walk uncomfortable.","zh":"靴子有洞會令水滲入，令步行不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies damage in an object.","zh":"這個片語指出物件上的損壞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"I’d definitely like to","meaning":"我肯定想……","examples":[{"en":"Jan says she would definitely like to come on the walk.","zh":"Jan 說她肯定想參加步行活動。"},{"en":"I’d definitely like to means I am very sure I want to do something.","zh":"I’d definitely like to 指我非常肯定自己想做某事。"},{"en":"I’d definitely like to join the clean-up if it is on Saturday morning.","zh":"如果清潔活動在星期六早上，我肯定想參加。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they want to show clear interest and enthusiasm.","zh":"人們想清楚表示興趣和熱情時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It is stronger than simply saying “I’d like to”.","zh":"它比單純說 “I’d like to” 更強烈。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"come on the walk","meaning":"參加步行活動","examples":[{"en":"Jan would like to come on the guided walk.","zh":"Jan 想參加導覽步行活動。"},{"en":"To come on the walk means to join the organised walking activity.","zh":"come on the walk 指參加有組織的步行活動。"},{"en":"Friends may come on the walk if they enjoy nature and do not mind early starts.","zh":"如果朋友喜歡自然，而且不介意早起，他們可能參加步行活動。"},{"en":"Joining a walk helps new residents learn the area and meet local people.","zh":"參加步行活動幫助新居民了解地區並認識本地人。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for taking part in a planned walk with others.","zh":"這個片語用於與他人一起參與計劃好的步行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"later this month","meaning":"本月稍後","examples":[{"en":"Later this month, the group is holding a woodwork session.","zh":"本月稍後，該團體將舉辦木工課。"},{"en":"Later this month means at some time after now but before the current month ends.","zh":"later this month 指在現在之後、但在本月結束之前的某個時間。"},{"en":"The school will hold a parents’ meeting later this month.","zh":"學校本月稍後會舉行家長會。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a general future time without naming the exact date.","zh":"這個片語提供大概未來時間，而不說明確日期。"},{"en":"It is useful when the exact date is not the main point.","zh":"當確切日期不是重點時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one-day woodwork session","meaning":"一日木工課","examples":[{"en":"The group is holding a one-day woodwork session in Hopton Wood.","zh":"該團體將在 Hopton Wood 舉辦一日木工課。"},{"en":"A one-day woodwork session is a short course or workshop about making things from wood, lasting one day.","zh":"one-day woodwork session 指一個為期一天、學習用木材製作物品的短課程或工作坊。"},{"en":"A community centre may hold a one-day woodwork session for beginners.","zh":"社區中心可能為初學者舉辦一日木工課。"},{"en":"One-day sessions are useful because people can try a new skill without a long commitment.","zh":"一日課程很有用，因為人們可以嘗試新技能，而不用作長期承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase combines the activity, length, and workshop style.","zh":"這個片語結合活動、長度和工作坊形式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"woodwork session","meaning":"木工課","examples":[{"en":"The woodwork session will be led by experts.","zh":"木工課將由專家帶領。"},{"en":"A woodwork session is a class or workshop where people learn to make or repair things using wood.","zh":"woodwork session 指人們學習用木材製作或修理物品的課堂或工作坊。"},{"en":"Students may join a woodwork session to make a small shelf or spoon.","zh":"學生可能參加木工課，製作小架或木匙。"},{"en":"Woodwork sessions need safety guidance because tools can be sharp or heavy.","zh":"木工課需要安全指導，因為工具可能鋒利或沉重。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a practical hands-on activity.","zh":"這個片語指實用的動手活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"I’ve never tried that before","meaning":"我以前從未試過","examples":[{"en":"Jan says she has never tried woodwork before.","zh":"Jan 說她以前從未試過木工。"},{"en":"I’ve never tried that before means I have no previous experience of doing that activity.","zh":"I’ve never tried that before 指我以前沒有做過那項活動。"},{"en":"I’ve never tried kayaking before, so I need clear instructions.","zh":"我以前從未試過獨木舟，所以需要清楚指示。"},{"en":"People say this when they are interested but may need beginner support.","zh":"人們有興趣但可能需要初學者支援時，會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain why someone asks whether beginners can join.","zh":"這個片語有助解釋為何某人詢問初學者能否參加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"beginners","meaning":"初學者","examples":[{"en":"Jan asks whether beginners can take part in the woodwork session.","zh":"Jan 問初學者是否可以參加木工課。"},{"en":"Beginners are people who are new to an activity and have little or no experience.","zh":"beginners 指剛開始某活動、幾乎沒有經驗的人。"},{"en":"A yoga class for beginners should explain basic movements slowly.","zh":"初學者瑜伽班應慢慢解釋基本動作。"},{"en":"Beginners need clear instructions so they can learn safely and confidently.","zh":"初學者需要清楚指示，才能安全而有信心地學習。"},{"en":"This word identifies the starting level of learners.","zh":"這個字識別學習者的起點水平。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take part","meaning":"參加","examples":[{"en":"Beginners can take part in the woodwork session.","zh":"初學者可以參加木工課。"},{"en":"To take part means to join and participate in an activity.","zh":"take part 指加入並參與某活動。"},{"en":"Students can take part in the school clean-up even if they have no experience.","zh":"即使沒有經驗，學生也可以參加學校清潔活動。"},{"en":"Allowing beginners to take part can help more people learn new skills.","zh":"讓初學者參加可以幫助更多人學習新技能。"},{"en":"This phrase is active and means more than just watching.","zh":"這個片語較主動，意思不只是觀看。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a couple of experts","meaning":"幾位專家","examples":[{"en":"A couple of experts will lead the woodwork session.","zh":"幾位專家將帶領木工課。"},{"en":"A couple of experts means two or a few people with special knowledge or skill.","zh":"a couple of experts 指兩位或幾位有專門知識或技能的人。"},{"en":"A couple of experts may visit a school to teach students about recycling.","zh":"幾位專家可能到學校教學生有關回收的知識。"},{"en":"Expert support makes a new activity safer and easier for beginners.","zh":"專家支援令新活動對初學者更安全和更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a small number of skilled people.","zh":"這個片語暗示少數有技能的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lead the session","meaning":"帶領課堂","examples":[{"en":"Experts will lead the woodwork session.","zh":"專家將帶領木工課。"},{"en":"To lead the session means to guide the activity, explain tasks, and help participants.","zh":"lead the session 指引導活動、解釋任務並協助參加者。"},{"en":"A coach may lead the training session before an important match.","zh":"教練可能在重要比賽前帶領訓練課。"},{"en":"Good leaders keep a session organised and make sure everyone knows what to do.","zh":"好領導者會令課堂有組織，並確保每個人知道要做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes responsibility for running a class or activity.","zh":"這個片語描述負責主持課堂或活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"keep the number of participants down","meaning":"限制參加人數","examples":[{"en":"The group keeps the number of participants down so everyone can get help.","zh":"該團體限制參加人數，讓每個人都能得到協助。"},{"en":"To keep the number of participants down means to limit how many people can join.","zh":"keep the number of participants down 指限制可參加的人數。"},{"en":"A cooking class may keep the number of participants down for safety reasons.","zh":"烹飪課可能因安全原因限制參加人數。"},{"en":"Smaller groups allow teachers or experts to give more individual help.","zh":"較小組別讓老師或專家能提供更多個別協助。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why an activity may have limited places.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何活動可能名額有限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"participants","meaning":"參加者","examples":[{"en":"The number of participants in the woodwork session is limited.","zh":"木工課的參加者人數有限。"},{"en":"Participants are people who take part in an activity, event, or project.","zh":"participants 指參加活動、事件或項目的人。"},{"en":"Participants in a guided walk should arrive on time and bring suitable shoes.","zh":"導覽步行活動的參加者應準時到達並帶合適鞋履。"},{"en":"Organisers need to know the number of participants so they can prepare enough materials.","zh":"主辦方需要知道參加者人數，以便準備足夠材料。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “people who join”.","zh":"這個字比 “people who join” 較正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as much help as you need","meaning":"所需的足夠協助","examples":[{"en":"Participants will get as much help as they need.","zh":"參加者將得到所需的足夠協助。"},{"en":"As much help as you need means enough support for your own level or difficulty.","zh":"as much help as you need 指按自己的水平或困難程度得到足夠支援。"},{"en":"Beginners in a language class should receive as much help as they need with pronunciation.","zh":"語言班初學者應在發音方面得到所需的足夠協助。"},{"en":"When learners get enough help, they are more likely to try new tasks confidently.","zh":"當學習者得到足夠協助，他們更可能有信心嘗試新任務。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures people that they will not be left alone.","zh":"這個片語安撫人們，表示他們不會被獨自留下。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be able to make","meaning":"能夠製作","examples":[{"en":"Jan would love to be able to make chairs.","zh":"Jan 很想能夠製作椅子。"},{"en":"To be able to make something means to have the skill or ability to create it.","zh":"be able to make something 指有技能或能力創造某物。"},{"en":"A student may want to be able to make a simple website after a coding course.","zh":"學生可能希望在編程課後能夠製作簡單網站。"},{"en":"Learning to make something by hand can give people a strong sense of achievement.","zh":"學會親手製作東西可以給人強烈成就感。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on gaining a practical skill.","zh":"這個片語着重獲得實用技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"too ambitious for","meaning":"對……而言太有野心","examples":[{"en":"Making a chair is probably too ambitious for one day.","zh":"製作椅子對一天而言可能太有野心。"},{"en":"Too ambitious for something means too difficult or large for the time, ability, or situation available.","zh":"too ambitious for something 指對可用時間、能力或情況而言太困難或太大。"},{"en":"Writing a full novel is too ambitious for a one-week school project.","zh":"在一星期學校專題中寫完整小說太有野心。"},{"en":"If a task is too ambitious, beginners may become frustrated instead of learning well.","zh":"如果任務太有野心，初學者可能變得沮喪，而不是好好學習。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a goal may be unrealistic.","zh":"這個片語提醒某目標可能不切實際。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"start with","meaning":"由……開始","examples":[{"en":"Beginners will start with wooden spoons.","zh":"初學者會由木匙開始。"},{"en":"To start with something means to begin by doing or learning that first.","zh":"start with something 指先做或先學某事。"},{"en":"New English learners often start with simple greetings.","zh":"英語初學者常由簡單問候語開始。"},{"en":"Starting with an easier task helps learners build confidence before harder work.","zh":"由較容易任務開始，有助學習者在面對較困難工作前建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the first step in a process.","zh":"這個片語引入過程中的第一步。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"wooden spoons","meaning":"木匙","examples":[{"en":"Participants will start by making wooden spoons.","zh":"參加者會先製作木匙。"},{"en":"Wooden spoons are spoons made of wood, often used for cooking or serving food.","zh":"wooden spoons 指用木材製成、常用於烹調或盛載食物的匙。"},{"en":"A beginner woodwork class may make wooden spoons because they are small and useful.","zh":"初學者木工課可能製作木匙，因為它們小巧而實用。"},{"en":"Making a wooden spoon teaches basic shaping, smoothing, and tool control.","zh":"製作木匙可以教授基本塑形、打磨和工具控制。"},{"en":"This phrase names a simple handmade object.","zh":"這個片語命名一種簡單手製物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"use the tools","meaning":"使用工具","examples":[{"en":"Participants will learn how to use the tools.","zh":"參加者將學習如何使用工具。"},{"en":"To use the tools means to handle equipment properly to complete a task.","zh":"use the tools 指正確操作設備以完成任務。"},{"en":"Students must learn how to use the tools safely before starting a science experiment.","zh":"學生開始科學實驗前，必須學會安全使用工具。"},{"en":"Knowing how to use tools reduces accidents and improves the quality of the finished work.","zh":"知道如何使用工具可以減少意外，並提高完成品質素。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical skill and safety.","zh":"這個片語着重實用技能和安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"anything you make","meaning":"你製作的任何東西","examples":[{"en":"Anything participants make is theirs to take home.","zh":"參加者製作的任何東西都屬於他們，可以帶回家。"},{"en":"Anything you make means every object you create during the activity.","zh":"anything you make 指你在活動中創造的每一件物品。"},{"en":"In an art workshop, anything you make can be displayed at home.","zh":"在藝術工作坊中，你製作的任何東西都可以在家展示。"},{"en":"Letting people keep what they make gives them a sense of ownership and pride.","zh":"讓人保留自己製作的東西，會給他們擁有感和自豪感。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in craft, art, and cooking classes.","zh":"這個片語常用於手工藝、藝術和烹飪課。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be yours to take home","meaning":"屬於你並可帶回家","examples":[{"en":"Anything you make is yours to take home.","zh":"你製作的任何東西都屬於你並可帶回家。"},{"en":"To be yours to take home means you are allowed to keep it and bring it home after the activity.","zh":"be yours to take home 指活動後你獲准保留並帶回家。"},{"en":"In the pottery class, the cup you make is yours to take home.","zh":"在陶藝課中，你製作的杯子屬於你並可帶回家。"},{"en":"This promise can make workshops more attractive because participants leave with something personal.","zh":"這個承諾可以令工作坊更吸引，因為參加者會帶着個人物品離開。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly tells people what happens to the finished item.","zh":"這個片語清楚告訴人們完成品之後如何處理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"that sounds like fun","meaning":"那聽起來很有趣","examples":[{"en":"Jan thinks the woodwork session sounds like fun.","zh":"Jan 覺得木工課聽起來很有趣。"},{"en":"That sounds like fun means the activity seems enjoyable from the description.","zh":"that sounds like fun 指根據描述，該活動似乎令人愉快。"},{"en":"A beach clean-up followed by a picnic sounds like fun.","zh":"海灘清潔後再野餐聽起來很有趣。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they are interested in trying an activity.","zh":"人們對嘗試某活動感興趣時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It is casual, positive, and common in conversation.","zh":"它口語、正面，並常見於對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a charge of","meaning":"收費為……","examples":[{"en":"There is a charge of £35 for the woodwork session.","zh":"木工課收費為 35 英鎊。"},{"en":"A charge of a certain amount means a fee or cost that must be paid.","zh":"a charge of a certain amount 指必須支付的費用或成本。"},{"en":"There is a charge of ten dollars for replacing a lost library card.","zh":"補領遺失圖書館借書證收費為十元。"},{"en":"Clear charges help participants decide whether an activity fits their budget.","zh":"清楚收費有助參加者決定活動是否符合預算。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when explaining prices for services or events.","zh":"這個片語常用於解釋服務或活動價格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"including lunch","meaning":"包括午餐","examples":[{"en":"The charge is £35, including lunch.","zh":"收費為 35 英鎊，包括午餐。"},{"en":"Including lunch means lunch is part of the price or arrangement.","zh":"including lunch 指午餐已包含在價格或安排內。"},{"en":"The school trip costs $200, including lunch and transport.","zh":"學校旅行費用為 200 元，包括午餐和交通。"},{"en":"If lunch is included, participants do not need to bring or buy their own meal.","zh":"如果包括午餐，參加者就不用自己帶或購買餐點。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what is covered by a fee.","zh":"這個片語解釋費用包含甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"camp in the wood","meaning":"在樹林中露營","examples":[{"en":"Participants can pay extra if they want to camp in the wood.","zh":"如果參加者想在樹林中露營，可以額外付款。"},{"en":"To camp in the wood means to stay overnight outdoors in a wooded area, usually in a tent.","zh":"camp in the wood 指通常在帳篷中於樹林地區戶外過夜。"},{"en":"Scouts may camp in the wood during a weekend training activity.","zh":"童軍可能在週末訓練活動中於樹林中露營。"},{"en":"Camping in woodland requires warm clothes, safe cooking, and respect for wildlife.","zh":"在樹林中露營需要保暖衣物、安全煮食和尊重野生動物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an outdoor overnight activity.","zh":"這個片語描述戶外過夜活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"come home the same day","meaning":"當天回家","examples":[{"en":"Jan thinks she will come home the same day.","zh":"Jan 覺得她會當天回家。"},{"en":"To come home the same day means to return home before the day ends, without staying overnight.","zh":"come home the same day 指在當天結束前回家，不留宿。"},{"en":"Students can visit the museum and come home the same day if the journey is short.","zh":"如果路程短，學生可以參觀博物館並當天回家。"},{"en":"Coming home the same day is easier for people who do not want to camp or book accommodation.","zh":"對不想露營或訂住宿的人來說，當天回家較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts a day trip with an overnight stay.","zh":"這個片語把一日行程與過夜逗留作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"join the group","meaning":"加入團體","examples":[{"en":"Jan would certainly like to join the conservation group.","zh":"Jan 肯定想加入這個保育團體。"},{"en":"To join the group means to become a member or start taking part in its activities.","zh":"join the group 指成為成員，或開始參與該團體的活動。"},{"en":"A student may join the gardening group to learn about plants and meet friends.","zh":"學生可能加入園藝小組，以學習植物知識和認識朋友。"},{"en":"Joining a group can help new residents feel connected to the community.","zh":"加入團體可以幫助新居民感到與社區有連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming part of an organisation or team.","zh":"這個片語描述成為組織或團隊的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 12/task-2":[{"front":"tour guide","meaning":"導遊","examples":[{"en":"Lou Miller is going to be the tour guide for the boat trip.","zh":"Lou Miller 將會是這次乘船遊覽的導遊。"},{"en":"A tour guide is a person who leads visitors, explains places, and gives useful information during a trip.","zh":"tour guide 是帶領遊客、介紹地方並在旅程中提供有用資訊的人。"},{"en":"A tour guide may tell tourists where to stand, what to look at, and when to return to the bus.","zh":"導遊可能告訴遊客站在哪裡、看甚麼，以及何時回到巴士。"},{"en":"A good tour guide helps visitors enjoy a place safely and understand its history.","zh":"好導遊幫助遊客安全地享受一個地方，並理解其歷史。"},{"en":"Without a tour guide, tourists may miss important details or get confused about the route.","zh":"沒有導遊，遊客可能會錯過重要細節或對路線感到困惑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as we take","meaning":"當我們進行……時","examples":[{"en":"Lou will guide the visitors as they take a boat trip around the coast.","zh":"當遊客沿海岸乘船遊覽時，Lou 會帶領他們。"},{"en":"As we take a trip means while we are making or experiencing that trip.","zh":"as we take a trip 的意思是當我們進行或經歷該旅程時。"},{"en":"As we take the train into the city, the teacher will explain the buildings we pass.","zh":"當我們乘火車進城時，老師會講解我們經過的建築物。"},{"en":"A guide often gives information as visitors travel, so they can connect words with what they see.","zh":"導遊常在遊客旅途中提供資訊，讓他們把說明與眼前所見連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase links an action with something happening at the same time.","zh":"這個短語把一個行動與同時發生的事連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"boat trip","meaning":"乘船遊覽","examples":[{"en":"The visitors are taking a boat trip around the Tasmanian coast.","zh":"遊客正沿塔斯曼尼亞海岸乘船遊覽。"},{"en":"A boat trip is a journey or short tour made by boat.","zh":"boat trip 是乘船進行的旅程或短途遊覽。"},{"en":"Families may take a boat trip to see islands, cliffs, or wildlife from the water.","zh":"家庭可能乘船遊覽，從水上觀看小島、懸崖或野生動物。"},{"en":"A boat trip can be relaxing, but passengers must follow safety instructions.","zh":"乘船遊覽可以很放鬆，但乘客必須遵守安全指示。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on travel by boat, usually for enjoyment or sightseeing.","zh":"這個短語集中於乘船旅行，通常是為了享受或觀光。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"around the Tasmanian coast","meaning":"沿塔斯曼尼亞海岸一帶","examples":[{"en":"The boat trip goes around the Tasmanian coast.","zh":"這次乘船遊覽沿塔斯曼尼亞海岸一帶進行。"},{"en":"Around the Tasmanian coast means along or near the coastline of Tasmania.","zh":"around the Tasmanian coast 的意思是沿着或接近塔斯曼尼亞的海岸線。"},{"en":"Tourists may travel around the Tasmanian coast to see beaches, cliffs, and marine animals.","zh":"遊客可能沿塔斯曼尼亞海岸一帶旅行，觀看海灘、懸崖和海洋動物。"},{"en":"A journey around a coast often includes changing views because the boat passes different parts of the shoreline.","zh":"沿海岸的旅程通常有不斷變化的景色，因為船會經過海岸線不同部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the route of the trip.","zh":"這個短語描述旅程路線。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"before we set off","meaning":"在我們出發前","examples":[{"en":"Before they set off, Lou explains a few things about the journey.","zh":"在他們出發前，Lou 解釋關於旅程的幾件事。"},{"en":"Before we set off means before we begin a journey.","zh":"before we set off 的意思是在我們開始旅程之前。"},{"en":"Before we set off for the hike, the leader checks everyone has water.","zh":"在我們出發行山前，領隊會檢查人人都有水。"},{"en":"Giving instructions before people set off can prevent accidents and confusion later.","zh":"在人們出發前給指示，可以避免之後發生意外和混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used before trips, walks, drives, or tours.","zh":"這個短語常用於旅行、步行、駕車或導賞前。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"set off","meaning":"出發","examples":[{"en":"The boat will set off after the guide gives some instructions.","zh":"導遊給出一些指示後，船就會出發。"},{"en":"To set off means to begin a journey.","zh":"set off 的意思是開始一段旅程。"},{"en":"We should set off early if we want to avoid traffic.","zh":"如果我們想避開交通，我們應該早點出發。"},{"en":"If a group sets off late, the whole schedule may be delayed.","zh":"如果團隊出發遲了，整個行程可能會延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when people leave for a trip.","zh":"這個短語常用於人們出發旅行時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a few things about","meaning":"關於……的幾件事","examples":[{"en":"The guide wants to tell the visitors a few things about the journey.","zh":"導遊想告訴遊客關於旅程的幾件事。"},{"en":"A few things about something means several useful points or details related to it.","zh":"a few things about something 的意思是與某事有關的幾個有用要點或細節。"},{"en":"Before the exam, the teacher explained a few things about the format.","zh":"考試前，老師解釋了關於格式的幾件事。"},{"en":"Knowing a few things about a trip helps people feel more prepared.","zh":"知道關於旅程的幾件事，能令人感到更有準備。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces short, practical information rather than a long lecture.","zh":"這個短語引出簡短實用資訊，而不是長篇演講。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as you can see","meaning":"正如你們所見","examples":[{"en":"As the visitors can see, the boats are not huge.","zh":"正如遊客所見，這些船並不巨大。"},{"en":"As you can see is used to point to something visible or obvious in front of people.","zh":"as you can see 用來指出人們眼前可見或明顯的事物。"},{"en":"As you can see, the classroom has been rearranged for group work.","zh":"正如你們所見，課室已重新排列成小組工作模式。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase when the audience can confirm the point with their own eyes.","zh":"當聽眾可以親眼確認某點，講者會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase often makes an explanation feel direct and clear.","zh":"這個短語常令解釋感覺直接而清楚。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"staff members on board","meaning":"船上的職員","examples":[{"en":"There are three staff members on board the boat.","zh":"船上有三名職員。"},{"en":"Staff members on board are workers who are present on the boat during the journey.","zh":"staff members on board 是旅程期間在船上的工作人員。"},{"en":"Staff members on board may help passengers, give safety instructions, and handle emergencies.","zh":"船上的職員可能協助乘客、給予安全指示和處理緊急情況。"},{"en":"Having enough staff on board makes a trip safer and more organised.","zh":"船上有足夠職員會令旅程更安全和更有組織。"},{"en":"This phrase tells passengers who is available to help during the trip.","zh":"這個短語告訴乘客旅程中誰可以提供協助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on board","meaning":"在船上","examples":[{"en":"Three staff members are already on board.","zh":"三名職員已經在船上。"},{"en":"On board means on or inside a boat, plane, train, or other vehicle.","zh":"on board 的意思是在船、飛機、火車或其他交通工具上。"},{"en":"Passengers must be on board ten minutes before the ferry leaves.","zh":"乘客必須在渡輪開出前十分鐘上船。"},{"en":"Once everyone is on board, the driver can begin the journey safely.","zh":"當所有人都在車上，司機就可以安全開始旅程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being physically inside a vehicle.","zh":"這個短語描述人在交通工具內。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on top of that","meaning":"除此之外","examples":[{"en":"On top of that, the boat can carry fifteen passengers.","zh":"除此之外，這艘船可以載十五名乘客。"},{"en":"On top of that means in addition to what has already been mentioned.","zh":"on top of that 的意思是除了已經提到的事之外。"},{"en":"The hotel is close to the station; on top of that, breakfast is included.","zh":"這間酒店靠近車站；除此之外，早餐也包括在內。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase to add another useful or important point.","zh":"說話者使用這個短語來加入另一個有用或重要的要點。"},{"en":"It often strengthens the previous information.","zh":"它常用來加強前面的資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"transport a further fifteen people","meaning":"再運載十五人","examples":[{"en":"The boat can transport a further fifteen people.","zh":"這艘船可以再運載十五人。"},{"en":"To transport a further fifteen people means to carry fifteen more people from one place to another.","zh":"transport a further fifteen people 的意思是再把十五人從一個地方載到另一個地方。"},{"en":"A shuttle bus may transport a further twenty students if another group joins the trip.","zh":"如果另一組學生加入旅程，穿梭巴士可能再運載二十名學生。"},{"en":"Transporting more people safely requires enough space, balance, and staff.","zh":"安全運載更多人需要足夠空間、平衡和職員。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and focuses on carrying passengers.","zh":"這個短語較正式，集中於運載乘客。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"around the coastline","meaning":"沿海岸線","examples":[{"en":"The boat transports passengers around the coastline.","zh":"這艘船沿海岸線運載乘客。"},{"en":"Around the coastline means along the edge of the land beside the sea.","zh":"around the coastline 的意思是沿着陸地與海洋相接的邊緣。"},{"en":"Tour buses may drive visitors around the coastline to see beaches and fishing villages.","zh":"旅遊巴可能沿海岸線載遊客觀看海灘和漁村。"},{"en":"Travelling around the coastline gives people changing views of cliffs, bays, and islands.","zh":"沿海岸線旅行會讓人看見不斷變化的懸崖、海灣和小島景色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement near the sea’s edge.","zh":"這個短語描述在海邊附近移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"please note","meaning":"請注意","examples":[{"en":"Please note that passengers must stay balanced on both sides of the boat.","zh":"請注意，乘客必須在船的兩邊保持平衡。"},{"en":"Please note is a polite way to ask people to pay attention to important information.","zh":"please note 是禮貌地要求人注意重要資訊的說法。"},{"en":"Please note that the library will close early on Friday.","zh":"請注意，圖書館星期五會提早關門。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used before rules, warnings, or practical details.","zh":"這個短語常用於規則、警告或實用細節之前。"},{"en":"It sounds formal but polite.","zh":"它聽起來正式但有禮貌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on either side of","meaning":"在……任何一邊","examples":[{"en":"There should not be more than nine people on either side of the boat.","zh":"船的任何一邊都不應超過九人。"},{"en":"On either side of something means on each of the two sides.","zh":"on either side of something 的意思是在某物的兩邊各一邊。"},{"en":"Trees were planted on either side of the road to provide shade.","zh":"道路兩旁都種了樹，以提供樹蔭。"},{"en":"If too many people stand on one side of a boat, the balance may become unsafe.","zh":"如果太多人站在船的一邊，平衡可能變得不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about two sides of an object or route.","zh":"這個短語適合用於談論物件或路線的兩邊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"move some of you over","meaning":"請你們一些人移到另一邊","examples":[{"en":"The staff may move some passengers over to the other side.","zh":"職員可能會請部分乘客移到另一邊。"},{"en":"To move some of you over means to ask or help some people shift to another place or side.","zh":"move some of you over 的意思是要求或協助部分人移到另一個地方或另一邊。"},{"en":"A teacher may move some students over so every group has enough space.","zh":"老師可能請一些學生移到另一邊，讓每組都有足夠空間。"},{"en":"Moving people over can improve balance, safety, or organisation.","zh":"移動部分人可以改善平衡、安全或安排。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in practical instructions.","zh":"這個短語常出現在實用指示中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"otherwise","meaning":"否則","examples":[{"en":"Otherwise, everyone might end up in the sea.","zh":"否則，所有人都可能最後掉進海裏。"},{"en":"Otherwise means if not, or if that does not happen.","zh":"otherwise 的意思是如果不這樣，或如果那件事沒有發生。"},{"en":"Put your phone on silent; otherwise, it may disturb the class.","zh":"把電話調成靜音；否則，它可能打擾課堂。"},{"en":"This word introduces a possible bad result if advice is not followed.","zh":"這個詞引出不跟隨建議時可能出現的壞結果。"},{"en":"It is useful for warnings and instructions.","zh":"它適合用於警告和指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"end up in the sea","meaning":"最後掉進海裏","examples":[{"en":"If the boat is unbalanced, everyone could end up in the sea.","zh":"如果船失去平衡，所有人都可能最後掉進海裏。"},{"en":"To end up in the sea means to finally fall or land in the sea, usually by accident.","zh":"end up in the sea 的意思是最後跌入或落入海中，通常是意外地。"},{"en":"If children lean too far over the pier, they could end up in the sea.","zh":"如果小孩在碼頭邊探身太遠，他們可能最後掉進海裏。"},{"en":"Safety rules stop passengers from ending up in the sea during rough weather.","zh":"安全規則防止乘客在惡劣天氣中最後掉進海裏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unwanted final result.","zh":"這個短語描述不想要的最終結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recently upgraded","meaning":"最近升級","examples":[{"en":"The company has recently upgraded all its boats.","zh":"公司最近升級了所有船隻。"},{"en":"Recently upgraded means improved or replaced not long ago.","zh":"recently upgraded 的意思是不久前改良或更換。"},{"en":"The school recently upgraded its computers, so lessons run more smoothly.","zh":"學校最近升級了電腦，所以課堂運作更順暢。"},{"en":"Upgrading equipment can improve safety, comfort, and efficiency.","zh":"升級設備可以改善安全、舒適和效率。"},{"en":"This phrase tells us that improvements are new.","zh":"這個短語告訴我們改良是最近發生的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"jet black","meaning":"烏黑發亮的","examples":[{"en":"The old boats used to be jet black.","zh":"舊船以前是烏黑發亮的。"},{"en":"Jet black means very deep, shiny black.","zh":"jet black 的意思是非常深、帶光澤的黑色。"},{"en":"She wore a jet black coat that stood out against the snow.","zh":"她穿着一件烏黑發亮的外套，在雪地中特別突出。"},{"en":"Jet black colours can look smart and dramatic, but they may absorb heat in the sun.","zh":"烏黑發亮的顏色可以看起來整潔而搶眼，但在陽光下可能吸熱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong shade of black.","zh":"這個短語描述一種強烈的黑色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"dark red seats","meaning":"深紅色座位","examples":[{"en":"The new boats have comfortable dark red seats.","zh":"新船有舒適的深紅色座位。"},{"en":"Dark red seats are seats with a deep red colour.","zh":"dark red seats 是深紅色的座位。"},{"en":"A theatre may use dark red seats to create a warm and classic atmosphere.","zh":"劇院可能使用深紅色座位，營造溫暖而經典的氣氛。"},{"en":"Seat colour can affect how clean, modern, or comfortable a place looks.","zh":"座位顏色可以影響一個地方看起來是否乾淨、現代或舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both furniture and colour.","zh":"這個短語同時描述家具和顏色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"light-green exterior","meaning":"淺綠色外觀","examples":[{"en":"The new boats have a light-green exterior.","zh":"新船有淺綠色外觀。"},{"en":"A light-green exterior means the outside surface is pale green.","zh":"light-green exterior 的意思是外部表面是淺綠色。"},{"en":"A café with a light-green exterior may look fresh and easy to notice.","zh":"有淺綠色外觀的咖啡店可能看起來清新又容易注意到。"},{"en":"Changing the exterior colour can help a business create a new image.","zh":"改變外觀顏色可以幫助企業創造新形象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the outside appearance of something.","zh":"這個短語描述某物的外部外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了……","examples":[{"en":"The boats have a light-green exterior in order to stand out.","zh":"這些船有淺綠色外觀，為了突顯出來。"},{"en":"In order to means for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"in order to 的意思是為了達到某個目的。"},{"en":"Students revise past papers in order to understand exam question styles.","zh":"學生操練歷屆試題，為了理解考試題型。"},{"en":"Companies change packaging in order to attract customers’ attention.","zh":"公司改變包裝，為了吸引顧客注意。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly connects an action with its purpose.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接行動與目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stand out from","meaning":"從……中突顯出來","examples":[{"en":"The new boats stand out from other boats.","zh":"新船從其他船隻中突顯出來。"},{"en":"To stand out from something means to look different from others in a noticeable way.","zh":"stand out from something 的意思是以明顯方式看起來與其他東西不同。"},{"en":"A bright yellow umbrella stands out from a crowd of black umbrellas.","zh":"一把鮮黃色雨傘會從一群黑傘中突顯出來。"},{"en":"A design that stands out can help people remember a brand more easily.","zh":"突顯出來的設計可以幫助人更容易記住品牌。"},{"en":"This phrase usually describes clear difference and visibility.","zh":"這個短語通常描述清楚差異和可見度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"promote our company","meaning":"宣傳我們公司","examples":[{"en":"The new design helps promote the company.","zh":"新設計有助宣傳公司。"},{"en":"To promote our company means to make people notice, remember, or think positively about our business.","zh":"promote our company 的意思是令人注意、記得或對我們的公司有正面印象。"},{"en":"A shop may promote its company by using a clear logo on staff uniforms.","zh":"商店可能透過在員工制服上使用清晰標誌來宣傳公司。"},{"en":"Promotion can bring more customers because people become aware of the service.","zh":"宣傳可以帶來更多顧客，因為人們開始知道該服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is about publicity and business image.","zh":"這個短語關乎宣傳和企業形象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"unique appearance","meaning":"獨特外觀","examples":[{"en":"The new colours give the boats a unique appearance.","zh":"新顏色賦予船隻獨特外觀。"},{"en":"A unique appearance is a look that is special and different from others.","zh":"unique appearance 是特別並與其他東西不同的外觀。"},{"en":"A building with curved windows may have a unique appearance in a street of square offices.","zh":"在一條滿是方形辦公室的街道上，有彎曲窗戶的建築物可能有獨特外觀。"},{"en":"A unique appearance can help people recognise something quickly.","zh":"獨特外觀可以幫助人快速認出某物。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on visual distinctiveness.","zh":"這個短語集中於視覺上的獨特性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"don’t you think","meaning":"你不覺得嗎","examples":[{"en":"The guide says the boats have a unique appearance, don’t you think?","zh":"導遊說這些船有獨特外觀，你不覺得嗎？"},{"en":"Don’t you think? is used to invite agreement or ask for the listener’s opinion.","zh":"don’t you think? 用來邀請對方同意或詢問對方意見。"},{"en":"This classroom looks brighter after the repainting, don’t you think?","zh":"重新油漆後，這間課室看起來更明亮，你不覺得嗎？"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase when they expect the listener may agree.","zh":"說話者在預期聽者可能同意時會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It sounds conversational and friendly.","zh":"它聽起來自然、友善而像對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"offer someone a free lunchbox","meaning":"向某人提供免費午餐盒","examples":[{"en":"The company offers visitors a free lunchbox during the trip.","zh":"公司在旅程期間向遊客提供免費午餐盒。"},{"en":"To offer someone a free lunchbox means to provide a meal box to them without charging money.","zh":"offer someone a free lunchbox 的意思是免費向某人提供一份午餐盒。"},{"en":"A school trip may offer students a free lunchbox if the journey lasts all day.","zh":"如果旅程持續整天，學校旅行可能向學生提供免費午餐盒。"},{"en":"Offering food can make an activity more convenient because people do not need to buy lunch separately.","zh":"提供食物可以令活動更方便，因為人們不用另外買午餐。"},{"en":"This phrase shows both giving and no cost.","zh":"這個短語同時顯示提供和免費。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"during the trip","meaning":"在旅程期間","examples":[{"en":"Visitors receive a free lunchbox during the trip.","zh":"遊客在旅程期間會收到免費午餐盒。"},{"en":"During the trip means while the journey or activity is happening.","zh":"during the trip 的意思是在旅程或活動進行期間。"},{"en":"During the trip, students should stay with their group and listen to the teacher.","zh":"在旅程期間，學生應留在自己小組並聽從老師指示。"},{"en":"Problems during a trip are easier to handle if people know who to ask for help.","zh":"如果人們知道向誰求助，旅程期間的問題會較容易處理。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the time between the start and end of a journey.","zh":"這個短語指旅程開始與結束之間的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"three types","meaning":"三種類型","examples":[{"en":"The company has three types of lunchbox.","zh":"公司有三種類型的午餐盒。"},{"en":"Three types means three different kinds or choices.","zh":"three types 的意思是三種不同種類或選擇。"},{"en":"The café sells three types of sandwich: chicken, cheese, and egg.","zh":"咖啡店售賣三種類型的三文治：雞肉、芝士和雞蛋。"},{"en":"Offering three types gives people choice without making the decision too complicated.","zh":"提供三種類型能給人選擇，而不會令決定太複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when listing options.","zh":"這個短語適合用於列出選項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"contain","meaning":"包含；載有","examples":[{"en":"Lunchbox 1 contains ham and tomato sandwiches.","zh":"一號午餐盒包含火腿番茄三文治。"},{"en":"To contain something means to have it inside.","zh":"contain something 的意思是內裏有某物。"},{"en":"This medicine contains sugar, so diabetic patients should check with a doctor.","zh":"這種藥含糖，所以糖尿病患者應先問醫生。"},{"en":"Food labels tell people what a product contains so they can avoid allergies.","zh":"食物標籤告訴人們產品包含甚麼，讓他們避免過敏。"},{"en":"This word is useful for describing ingredients, contents, and information.","zh":"這個詞適合用於描述材料、內容和資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ham and tomato sandwiches","meaning":"火腿番茄三文治","examples":[{"en":"Lunchbox 1 contains ham and tomato sandwiches.","zh":"一號午餐盒包含火腿番茄三文治。"},{"en":"Ham and tomato sandwiches are sandwiches filled with ham and tomato slices.","zh":"ham and tomato sandwiches 是夾有火腿和番茄片的三文治。"},{"en":"A picnic lunch may include ham and tomato sandwiches because they are simple to carry.","zh":"野餐午餐可能包括火腿番茄三文治，因為它們方便攜帶。"},{"en":"Sandwich fillings matter because some people cannot eat pork or certain vegetables.","zh":"三文治餡料很重要，因為有些人不能吃豬肉或某些蔬菜。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific lunch item.","zh":"這個短語指一種特定午餐食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cheddar cheese roll","meaning":"車打芝士麵包卷","examples":[{"en":"Lunchbox 2 contains a cheddar cheese roll.","zh":"二號午餐盒包含一個車打芝士麵包卷。"},{"en":"A cheddar cheese roll is a bread roll filled with cheddar cheese.","zh":"cheddar cheese roll 是夾有車打芝士的麵包卷。"},{"en":"A vegetarian passenger may choose a cheddar cheese roll instead of a ham sandwich.","zh":"素食乘客可能選擇車打芝士麵包卷，而不是火腿三文治。"},{"en":"Cheese rolls are easy to pack because they can be eaten without cutlery.","zh":"芝士麵包卷容易包裝，因為不用餐具也可以吃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple bread-based lunch item.","zh":"這個短語描述一種簡單的麵包類午餐食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"salad-based","meaning":"以沙律為主的","examples":[{"en":"Lunchbox 3 is salad-based and also contains eggs and tuna.","zh":"三號午餐盒以沙律為主，也包含雞蛋和吞拿魚。"},{"en":"Salad-based means mainly made of salad ingredients such as vegetables, leaves, or cold toppings.","zh":"salad-based 的意思是主要由沙律材料組成，例如蔬菜、葉菜或冷配料。"},{"en":"A salad-based lunch may feel lighter than a meal with fried food.","zh":"以沙律為主的午餐可能比油炸食物較清淡。"},{"en":"People who want a fresher option may choose a salad-based meal.","zh":"想要較清新選擇的人可能會選擇以沙律為主的餐點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main style of the food.","zh":"這個短語描述食物的主要風格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"eggs and tuna","meaning":"雞蛋和吞拿魚","examples":[{"en":"Lunchbox 3 contains eggs and tuna.","zh":"三號午餐盒包含雞蛋和吞拿魚。"},{"en":"Eggs and tuna are common protein foods often used in salads, sandwiches, and lunchboxes.","zh":"eggs and tuna 是常見蛋白質食物，常用於沙律、三文治和午餐盒。"},{"en":"A salad with eggs and tuna can be more filling than vegetables alone.","zh":"有雞蛋和吞拿魚的沙律會比只有蔬菜更飽肚。"},{"en":"People with allergies should check lunchboxes carefully if they contain eggs or fish.","zh":"如果午餐盒含有雞蛋或魚類，過敏人士應仔細檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase names two specific food ingredients.","zh":"這個短語指兩種特定食材。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a packet of crisps","meaning":"一包薯片","examples":[{"en":"All three lunchboxes have a packet of crisps.","zh":"三款午餐盒都有一包薯片。"},{"en":"A packet of crisps is a small bag of thin fried potato snacks.","zh":"a packet of crisps 是一小包薄片油炸薯仔零食。"},{"en":"Children often like a packet of crisps with a sandwich lunch.","zh":"兒童常喜歡三文治午餐配一包薯片。"},{"en":"Crisps add salt and crunch, but they are not the healthiest part of a meal.","zh":"薯片增加鹹味和脆口感，但不是一餐中最健康的部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English; in American English, people often say “chips”.","zh":"這個短語常見於英式英文；美式英文通常說 chips。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"chocolate bar","meaning":"朱古力條","examples":[{"en":"Each lunchbox also contains a chocolate bar.","zh":"每個午餐盒也包含一條朱古力條。"},{"en":"A chocolate bar is a small solid piece of chocolate sold as a snack.","zh":"chocolate bar 是作為零食出售的一小塊固體朱古力。"},{"en":"A chocolate bar can give quick energy during a long trip.","zh":"朱古力條可以在長途旅程中快速提供能量。"},{"en":"Too many chocolate bars can add a lot of sugar to a child’s diet.","zh":"吃太多朱古力條會令孩子飲食中增加大量糖分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a common sweet snack.","zh":"這個短語指一種常見甜食零食。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"let staff know","meaning":"通知職員","examples":[{"en":"Visitors should let staff know which lunchbox they prefer.","zh":"遊客應通知職員自己較喜歡哪款午餐盒。"},{"en":"To let staff know means to tell the workers or organisers something they need to know.","zh":"let staff know 的意思是告訴工作人員或組織者他們需要知道的事情。"},{"en":"Please let staff know if you have a food allergy.","zh":"如果你有食物敏感，請通知職員。"},{"en":"Letting staff know early helps them prepare and avoid mistakes.","zh":"早點通知職員有助他們準備並避免錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and practical in public services and events.","zh":"這個短語在公共服務和活動中禮貌而實用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"which lunchbox you prefer","meaning":"你較喜歡哪款午餐盒","examples":[{"en":"Visitors should say which lunchbox they prefer.","zh":"遊客應說明自己較喜歡哪款午餐盒。"},{"en":"Which lunchbox you prefer means the lunchbox option you like or want most.","zh":"which lunchbox you prefer 的意思是你最喜歡或最想要的午餐盒選項。"},{"en":"The teacher asked students which lunchbox they preferred before ordering food.","zh":"老師在訂餐前問學生較喜歡哪款午餐盒。"},{"en":"Asking preferences prevents waste because people receive food they are more likely to eat.","zh":"詢問喜好可以避免浪費，因為人們會收到更可能吃的食物。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when people must choose between options.","zh":"這個短語用於人們需要在選項之間作選擇時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"I’m sure I don’t have to","meaning":"我相信我不用……","examples":[{"en":"The guide says, “I’m sure I don’t have to ask you not to throw anything into the sea.”","zh":"導遊說：「我相信我不用要求你們不要把任何東西丟進海裏。」"},{"en":"I’m sure I don’t have to means the speaker believes the listener already understands what should be done.","zh":"I’m sure I don’t have to 的意思是說話者相信聽者已明白應該怎樣做。"},{"en":"I’m sure I don’t have to remind you to be quiet in the hospital.","zh":"我相信我不用提醒你在醫院保持安靜。"},{"en":"This phrase can make a warning sound polite but still clear.","zh":"這個短語可以令警告聽起來有禮貌但仍然清楚。"},{"en":"It often appears before a rule that should be obvious.","zh":"它常出現在應該很明顯的規則之前。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"throw anything into the sea","meaning":"把任何東西丟進海裏","examples":[{"en":"Visitors should not throw anything into the sea.","zh":"遊客不應把任何東西丟進海裏。"},{"en":"To throw anything into the sea means to drop or toss objects into the water.","zh":"throw anything into the sea 的意思是把物件丟入或拋進海水中。"},{"en":"People should not throw plastic bottles into the sea because marine animals may eat them.","zh":"人們不應把膠樽丟進海裏，因為海洋動物可能會吃下。"},{"en":"Throwing rubbish into the sea pollutes the water and harms wildlife.","zh":"把垃圾丟進海裏會污染海水並傷害野生動物。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in environmental rules.","zh":"這個短語常用於環保規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bins to put litter in","meaning":"用來放垃圾的垃圾桶","examples":[{"en":"The boat does not have bins to put litter in.","zh":"船上沒有用來放垃圾的垃圾桶。"},{"en":"Bins to put litter in are containers where people can place rubbish.","zh":"bins to put litter in 是讓人放垃圾的容器。"},{"en":"A park needs enough bins to put litter in so visitors do not leave rubbish on the grass.","zh":"公園需要足夠用來放垃圾的垃圾桶，讓遊客不會把垃圾留在草地上。"},{"en":"If there are no bins, people should keep their rubbish until staff collect it.","zh":"如果沒有垃圾桶，人們應保留垃圾，直到職員收取。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical place for waste.","zh":"這個短語描述放置廢物的實用地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"collect it from you","meaning":"向你收取它","examples":[{"en":"The guides will collect litter from the passengers after lunch.","zh":"導遊會在午餐後向乘客收取垃圾。"},{"en":"To collect it from you means to take it from you, usually because staff will deal with it properly.","zh":"collect it from you 的意思是從你手上收走某物，通常因職員會妥善處理它。"},{"en":"The teacher will collect the worksheets from you at the end of the lesson.","zh":"老師會在課堂結束時向你們收取工作紙。"},{"en":"Collecting rubbish from passengers helps keep the boat clean and protects the sea.","zh":"向乘客收取垃圾有助保持船隻清潔並保護海洋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone else takes responsibility for an item.","zh":"這個短語適合用於別人接手負責某物時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"after lunch","meaning":"午餐後","examples":[{"en":"The staff will collect rubbish after lunch.","zh":"職員會在午餐後收集垃圾。"},{"en":"After lunch means following the midday meal.","zh":"after lunch 的意思是在午餐之後。"},{"en":"Students return to class after lunch.","zh":"學生午餐後回到課室。"},{"en":"Cleaning up after lunch keeps shared spaces tidy for the next activity.","zh":"午餐後清理可以保持共用空間整潔，方便下一個活動。"},{"en":"This phrase simply marks time in the day.","zh":"這個短語簡單標示一天中的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"large plastic sack","meaning":"大膠袋","examples":[{"en":"The staff will put all the litter in a large plastic sack.","zh":"職員會把所有垃圾放進一個大膠袋。"},{"en":"A large plastic sack is a big plastic bag used for carrying rubbish or other items.","zh":"large plastic sack 是用來裝垃圾或其他物品的大型膠袋。"},{"en":"Cleaners may use a large plastic sack to collect rubbish after a school event.","zh":"清潔工可能在學校活動後用大膠袋收集垃圾。"},{"en":"Using one large sack makes rubbish easier to carry away safely.","zh":"使用一個大袋可以令垃圾更容易安全帶走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical container.","zh":"這個短語描述實用容器。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"engine on the boat","meaning":"船上的引擎","examples":[{"en":"The engine on the boat makes quite a lot of noise.","zh":"船上的引擎發出頗大的噪音。"},{"en":"The engine on the boat is the machine that powers the boat and makes it move.","zh":"engine on the boat 是推動船隻前進的機器。"},{"en":"The engine on a boat must be checked before passengers board.","zh":"船上的引擎必須在乘客登船前檢查。"},{"en":"A noisy engine can make it harder for passengers to hear the guide.","zh":"嘈雜引擎可以令乘客更難聽到導遊說話。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific part of the boat.","zh":"這個短語指出船上的特定部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make quite a lot of noise","meaning":"發出頗大的噪音","examples":[{"en":"The boat engine makes quite a lot of noise.","zh":"船上的引擎發出頗大的噪音。"},{"en":"To make quite a lot of noise means to produce a fairly loud sound.","zh":"make quite a lot of noise 的意思是產生相當大的聲音。"},{"en":"Roadworks outside a classroom can make quite a lot of noise.","zh":"課室外的道路工程可以發出頗大的噪音。"},{"en":"When a machine makes a lot of noise, people may need to speak more loudly or use microphones.","zh":"當機器發出很大噪音，人們可能需要更大聲說話或使用咪高峰。"},{"en":"This phrase is softer than saying something is extremely noisy.","zh":"這個短語比 extremely noisy 語氣較溫和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"before we head off","meaning":"在我們出發前","examples":[{"en":"Before they head off, Lou explains what the visitors will see.","zh":"在他們出發前，Lou 解釋遊客將會看到甚麼。"},{"en":"Before we head off means before we leave or begin a journey.","zh":"before we head off 的意思是在我們離開或開始旅程前。"},{"en":"Before we head off to the museum, let’s check everyone has their tickets.","zh":"在我們出發去博物館前，先檢查每個人都有門票。"},{"en":"Giving a short explanation before heading off helps people know what to expect.","zh":"出發前作簡短解釋，有助人們知道可以期待甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and similar to “before we set off”.","zh":"這個短語較口語，意思與 before we set off 相近。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"head off","meaning":"出發","examples":[{"en":"The boat will head off after the guide’s introduction.","zh":"導遊介紹後，船就會出發。"},{"en":"To head off means to leave or start going somewhere.","zh":"head off 的意思是離開或開始前往某地。"},{"en":"We should head off now if we want to arrive before dark.","zh":"如果我們想天黑前到達，現在應該出發。"},{"en":"If a group heads off without clear instructions, people may become confused later.","zh":"如果團隊沒有清晰指示就出發，之後可能會混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in casual spoken English.","zh":"這個短語常見於日常口語英文。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"what you’re going to see","meaning":"你們將會看到的東西","examples":[{"en":"The guide explains what the visitors are going to see.","zh":"導遊解釋遊客將會看到的東西。"},{"en":"What you’re going to see means the things you will look at or experience later.","zh":"what you’re going to see 的意思是你稍後會觀看或經歷的事物。"},{"en":"Before a museum tour, the guide may explain what visitors are going to see in each room.","zh":"博物館導賞前，導遊可能解釋遊客在每個展室將會看到的東西。"},{"en":"Knowing what you are going to see can make the trip more meaningful.","zh":"知道將會看到甚麼，可以令旅程更有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase prepares listeners for upcoming sights or events.","zh":"這個短語讓聽眾為即將出現的景物或事件作準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be famous for","meaning":"以……聞名","examples":[{"en":"The area is famous for its ancient lighthouse.","zh":"這個地區以古老燈塔聞名。"},{"en":"To be famous for something means to be well known because of it.","zh":"be famous for something 的意思是因某事而廣為人知。"},{"en":"The town is famous for its seafood and night market.","zh":"這個城鎮以海鮮和夜市聞名。"},{"en":"A place can become famous for one landmark that visitors remember easily.","zh":"一個地方可以因一個容易令人記住的地標而聞名。"},{"en":"This phrase connects reputation with a special feature.","zh":"這個短語把名聲與特色連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ancient lighthouse","meaning":"古老燈塔","examples":[{"en":"The area is famous for its ancient lighthouse.","zh":"這個地區以古老燈塔聞名。"},{"en":"An ancient lighthouse is a very old tower with a light that guides ships.","zh":"ancient lighthouse 是非常古老、用燈光引導船隻的塔。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit an ancient lighthouse to learn about sailors and sea travel.","zh":"遊客可能參觀古老燈塔，了解海員和海上航行。"},{"en":"An ancient lighthouse can become a local landmark because it has history and dramatic views.","zh":"古老燈塔可以因有歷史和壯觀景色而成為本地地標。"},{"en":"This phrase combines age, architecture, and maritime safety.","zh":"這個短語結合年代、建築和海上安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"turn past","meaning":"繞過……","examples":[{"en":"The visitors will see the lighthouse as the boat turns past the first island.","zh":"當船繞過第一個小島時，遊客會看到燈塔。"},{"en":"To turn past something means to change direction and move beyond it.","zh":"turn past something 的意思是改變方向並經過某物。"},{"en":"The bus turns past the school before reaching the sports centre.","zh":"巴士到達體育中心前會繞過學校。"},{"en":"When a boat turns past an island, passengers may suddenly see a new view.","zh":"當船繞過小島，乘客可能突然看見新景色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement around and beyond a point.","zh":"這個短語描述繞着某點並越過它的移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"first little island","meaning":"第一個小島","examples":[{"en":"The boat will pass the first little island before the lighthouse comes into view.","zh":"燈塔出現前，船會經過第一個小島。"},{"en":"The first little island means the first small island on the route.","zh":"first little island 的意思是路線上的第一個小型島嶼。"},{"en":"During the tour, the first little island may help passengers understand where they are on the map.","zh":"在導賞中，第一個小島可能幫助乘客理解自己在地圖上的位置。"},{"en":"Small islands can act as landmarks during a boat trip.","zh":"小島可以在乘船遊覽中作為地標。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific point in the journey.","zh":"這個短語指出旅程中的特定位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be built in","meaning":"建於……","examples":[{"en":"The lighthouse was built in 1838.","zh":"這座燈塔建於1838年。"},{"en":"To be built in a year means construction was completed or created in that year.","zh":"be built in 某年，意思是建築在那一年建成或創建。"},{"en":"The old town hall was built in 1902.","zh":"舊市政廳建於1902年。"},{"en":"Knowing when a building was built helps people understand its historical context.","zh":"知道建築建於何時，有助人們理解其歷史背景。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when describing landmarks and architecture.","zh":"這個短語常用於描述地標和建築。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"protect sailors","meaning":"保護海員","examples":[{"en":"The lighthouse was built to protect sailors.","zh":"這座燈塔是為保護海員而建的。"},{"en":"To protect sailors means to keep people travelling by sea safe from danger.","zh":"protect sailors 的意思是保護在海上航行的人免受危險。"},{"en":"Bright lights and warning signs protect sailors by guiding ships away from rocks.","zh":"明亮燈光和警告標誌透過引導船隻避開岩石來保護海員。"},{"en":"If sailors cannot see dangerous coastlines, shipwrecks become more likely.","zh":"如果海員看不到危險海岸線，船難就更可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase connects safety with people working or travelling at sea.","zh":"這個短語把安全與在海上工作或航行的人連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as a number of","meaning":"因為多宗……","examples":[{"en":"The lighthouse was built because a number of shipwrecks had occurred.","zh":"這座燈塔建成，是因為曾發生多宗船難。"},{"en":"A number of means several or many.","zh":"a number of 的意思是幾個或多個。"},{"en":"The school changed its rules after a number of students arrived late repeatedly.","zh":"在多名學生反覆遲到後，學校改變了規則。"},{"en":"When a number of accidents happen in one place, people may demand safety improvements.","zh":"當同一地點發生多宗意外，人們可能要求改善安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than “some”.","zh":"這個短語比 some 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"shipwrecks","meaning":"船難","examples":[{"en":"A number of shipwrecks led to significant loss of life.","zh":"多宗船難造成重大人命損失。"},{"en":"Shipwrecks are accidents in which ships are badly damaged, sink, or are destroyed at sea.","zh":"shipwrecks 是船隻在海上嚴重受損、沉沒或被摧毀的事故。"},{"en":"Storms, rocks, fog, and poor navigation can cause shipwrecks.","zh":"風暴、岩石、霧和導航不良都可以造成船難。"},{"en":"Shipwrecks can lead to deaths, lost cargo, and changes in safety rules.","zh":"船難可以導致死亡、貨物損失和安全規則改變。"},{"en":"This word is closely connected with sea travel and danger.","zh":"這個詞與海上航行和危險密切相關。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lead to significant loss of life","meaning":"造成重大人命損失","examples":[{"en":"The shipwrecks led to significant loss of life.","zh":"這些船難造成重大人命損失。"},{"en":"To lead to significant loss of life means to cause many people to die.","zh":"lead to significant loss of life 的意思是造成許多人死亡。"},{"en":"A building collapse can lead to significant loss of life if people cannot escape in time.","zh":"如果人們不能及時逃生，建築物倒塌可以造成重大人命損失。"},{"en":"Strong safety measures are needed when an accident could lead to many deaths.","zh":"當意外可能造成大量死亡，就需要強力安全措施。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and serious.","zh":"這個短語正式而嚴肅。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"significant loss of life","meaning":"重大人命損失","examples":[{"en":"The lighthouse was built after significant loss of life.","zh":"這座燈塔是在重大人命損失後建成的。"},{"en":"Significant loss of life means many deaths or a serious number of deaths.","zh":"significant loss of life 的意思是多人死亡或死亡人數嚴重。"},{"en":"A disaster with significant loss of life often leads to public investigations.","zh":"造成重大人命損失的災難常導致公開調查。"},{"en":"Authorities may change safety laws after significant loss of life.","zh":"當出現重大人命損失，當局可能修改安全法例。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and respectful when discussing death.","zh":"這個短語在討論死亡時正式而莊重。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"construction itself","meaning":"建造本身","examples":[{"en":"The construction itself was complicated.","zh":"建造本身很複雜。"},{"en":"Construction itself means the actual process of building something, not the planning or result.","zh":"construction itself 的意思是實際建造某物的過程，而不是規劃或結果。"},{"en":"The design looked simple, but the construction itself took years.","zh":"設計看起來簡單，但建造本身花了多年。"},{"en":"Building in a remote area can make the construction itself more expensive and dangerous.","zh":"在偏遠地區建造可以令建造本身更昂貴和危險。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses attention on the building process.","zh":"這個短語把注意力集中在建造過程上。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"original drawings","meaning":"原始圖則","examples":[{"en":"The local council kept some original drawings of the lighthouse.","zh":"本地議會保存了一些燈塔的原始圖則。"},{"en":"Original drawings are the first design plans or sketches made for a building or object.","zh":"original drawings 是為建築物或物件製作的最初設計圖或草圖。"},{"en":"Architects may study original drawings before repairing an old building.","zh":"建築師在修復舊建築前，可能研究原始圖則。"},{"en":"Original drawings can show how difficult a construction project was.","zh":"原始圖則可以顯示一個建造項目有多困難。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to early design documents, not later copies or photos.","zh":"這個短語指早期設計文件，而不是後來副本或照片。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"local council","meaning":"本地議會","examples":[{"en":"The local council kept the original drawings.","zh":"本地議會保存了原始圖則。"},{"en":"A local council is a local government body that manages services and decisions in an area.","zh":"local council 是管理某地服務和決策的地方政府機構。"},{"en":"A local council may look after roads, parks, libraries, and planning applications.","zh":"本地議會可能負責道路、公園、圖書館和規劃申請。"},{"en":"Local councils keep records because they are responsible for public buildings and community services.","zh":"本地議會保存紀錄，因為它們負責公共建築和社區服務。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to local government, not a private company.","zh":"這個短語指地方政府，而不是私人公司。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as the drawings show","meaning":"正如圖則所顯示","examples":[{"en":"The construction was complicated, as the original drawings show.","zh":"正如原始圖則所顯示，建造很複雜。"},{"en":"As the drawings show means the drawings provide evidence for the point being made.","zh":"as the drawings show 的意思是圖則為正在提出的觀點提供證據。"},{"en":"The bridge was difficult to build, as the old drawings show.","zh":"正如舊圖則所顯示，這座橋很難建造。"},{"en":"Visual records can support an explanation because people can see the details themselves.","zh":"視覺紀錄可以支持解釋，因為人們能親眼看到細節。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a statement with evidence from images or plans.","zh":"這個短語把陳述與圖片或圖則中的證據連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sit right on top of","meaning":"正正位於……頂部","examples":[{"en":"The lighthouse sits right on top of the cliffs.","zh":"燈塔正正位於懸崖頂部。"},{"en":"To sit right on top of something means to be positioned directly above it.","zh":"sit right on top of something 的意思是直接位於某物上方。"},{"en":"The old temple sits right on top of the hill, overlooking the village.","zh":"古老寺廟正正位於山頂，俯瞰村莊。"},{"en":"A building on top of cliffs can be dramatic, but it may face strong wind and difficult access.","zh":"位於懸崖頂部的建築可以很壯觀，但可能面對強風和難以到達的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises exact position.","zh":"這個短語強調準確位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cliffs","meaning":"懸崖","examples":[{"en":"The lighthouse sits on top of the cliffs.","zh":"燈塔位於懸崖頂部。"},{"en":"Cliffs are high, steep rock faces, often beside the sea or a valley.","zh":"cliffs 是高而陡峭的岩石面，常位於海邊或山谷旁。"},{"en":"Visitors should not stand too close to cliffs because the edge may be dangerous.","zh":"遊客不應站得太靠近懸崖，因為邊緣可能危險。"},{"en":"Sea cliffs can provide nesting places for birds and dramatic views for tourists.","zh":"海邊懸崖可以為鳥類提供築巢地點，並為遊客帶來壯觀景色。"},{"en":"This word describes a natural steep landform.","zh":"這個詞描述自然的陡峭地貌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"isolated spot","meaning":"偏僻地點","examples":[{"en":"The lighthouse is in a very isolated spot.","zh":"這座燈塔位於非常偏僻的地點。"},{"en":"An isolated spot is a place far away from other people, buildings, or services.","zh":"isolated spot 是遠離其他人、建築物或服務的地方。"},{"en":"A small house on a mountain path may be in an isolated spot.","zh":"山路上的小屋可能位於偏僻地點。"},{"en":"Living in an isolated spot can be peaceful, but getting help may take longer.","zh":"住在偏僻地點可以很平靜，但求助可能需時更久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes remoteness and separation.","zh":"這個短語描述偏遠和分隔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the nineteenth century","meaning":"在19世紀","examples":[{"en":"In the nineteenth century, lighthouse keepers had many jobs to do.","zh":"在19世紀，燈塔看守人有許多工作要做。"},{"en":"In the nineteenth century means during the years 1801 to 1900.","zh":"in the nineteenth century 的意思是在1801年至1900年期間。"},{"en":"In the nineteenth century, travel was slower because cars and planes were not common.","zh":"在19世紀，交通較慢，因為汽車和飛機並不普遍。"},{"en":"Historical context matters because work and technology were very different in the nineteenth century.","zh":"歷史背景很重要，因為19世紀的工作和科技非常不同。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event in a historical period.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在一個歷史時期中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"such as","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"The lighthouse keepers had jobs such as polishing lamps and chopping firewood.","zh":"燈塔看守人有擦亮燈和劈柴等工作。"},{"en":"Such as means for example.","zh":"such as 的意思是例如。"},{"en":"Students need basic supplies such as pens, notebooks, and folders.","zh":"學生需要基本用品，例如筆、筆記簿和文件夾。"},{"en":"Giving examples such as these makes an explanation clearer.","zh":"給出這類例子能令解釋更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples from a wider group.","zh":"這個短語從較大類別中引出例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"polish the brass lamps","meaning":"擦亮黃銅燈","examples":[{"en":"Lighthouse keepers had to polish the brass lamps.","zh":"燈塔看守人必須擦亮黃銅燈。"},{"en":"To polish brass lamps means to clean and rub them until the metal shines.","zh":"polish brass lamps 的意思是清潔並擦拭黃銅燈，直到金屬發亮。"},{"en":"Museum staff may polish brass lamps before an exhibition opens.","zh":"博物館職員可能在展覽開幕前擦亮黃銅燈。"},{"en":"Polishing lamps was important because dirty lamps could reduce the brightness of the light.","zh":"擦亮燈具很重要，因為骯髒的燈會減低亮度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical maintenance job.","zh":"這個短語描述實際維護工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"brass lamps","meaning":"黃銅燈","examples":[{"en":"The lighthouse keepers polished the brass lamps.","zh":"燈塔看守人擦亮黃銅燈。"},{"en":"Brass lamps are lamps made partly or fully from brass, a yellow metal.","zh":"brass lamps 是部分或全部由黃銅這種黃色金屬製成的燈。"},{"en":"Old brass lamps can look beautiful but need regular cleaning to stay shiny.","zh":"舊黃銅燈可以很漂亮，但需要定期清潔才保持光亮。"},{"en":"In a lighthouse, lamps were important because sailors depended on their light.","zh":"在燈塔中，燈很重要，因為海員依靠它們的光。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific kind of lamp.","zh":"這個短語指一種特定燈具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"chop firewood","meaning":"劈柴","examples":[{"en":"Lighthouse keepers also had to chop firewood.","zh":"燈塔看守人也必須劈柴。"},{"en":"To chop firewood means to cut wood into pieces for burning.","zh":"chop firewood 的意思是把木材劈成可燃燒的小塊。"},{"en":"People living in cold villages may chop firewood before winter arrives.","zh":"住在寒冷村莊的人可能在冬天到來前劈柴。"},{"en":"Chopping firewood takes strength and time, especially without modern machines.","zh":"劈柴需要體力和時間，尤其在沒有現代機器時。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical household or survival task.","zh":"這個短語描述體力家務或生存任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"keep someone busy","meaning":"令某人忙個不停","examples":[{"en":"These jobs kept the lighthouse keepers busy.","zh":"這些工作令燈塔看守人忙個不停。"},{"en":"To keep someone busy means to give someone many things to do.","zh":"keep someone busy 的意思是給某人許多事情做。"},{"en":"Preparing for a school fair can keep teachers busy for weeks.","zh":"準備學校嘉年華可以令老師忙上幾個星期。"},{"en":"When many small tasks keep people busy, they may have little time to rest.","zh":"當許多小任務令人忙個不停，人們可能幾乎沒有時間休息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing activity or workload.","zh":"這個短語描述持續活動或工作量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lighthouse keepers","meaning":"燈塔看守人","examples":[{"en":"Lighthouse keepers worked in the isolated lighthouse.","zh":"燈塔看守人在偏僻的燈塔工作。"},{"en":"Lighthouse keepers were people responsible for operating and maintaining a lighthouse.","zh":"lighthouse keepers 是負責操作和維護燈塔的人。"},{"en":"Lighthouse keepers cleaned lamps, watched the weather, and made sure the light worked.","zh":"燈塔看守人清潔燈具、觀察天氣，並確保燈光正常運作。"},{"en":"Their work protected sailors because a failed light could lead to danger at sea.","zh":"他們的工作保護海員，因為燈光失效可能導致海上危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an old maritime job.","zh":"這個短語描述一種舊式海事工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"prison convicts","meaning":"監獄囚犯","examples":[{"en":"The workers were mainly prison convicts until the middle of the century.","zh":"直到該世紀中期，工人主要是監獄囚犯。"},{"en":"Prison convicts are people who have been found guilty of crimes and sent to prison.","zh":"prison convicts 是被裁定犯下罪行並被送入監獄的人。"},{"en":"In the past, prison convicts were sometimes made to do difficult public work.","zh":"過去，監獄囚犯有時被安排做艱苦公共工程。"},{"en":"Using prison convicts as workers shows how punishment and labour were connected in some periods.","zh":"使用監獄囚犯作工人，顯示某些時期懲罰與勞動如何相連。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a legal and social status.","zh":"這個短語描述法律和社會身份。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"until the middle of","meaning":"直到……中期","examples":[{"en":"Prison convicts worked there until the middle of the nineteenth century.","zh":"監獄囚犯在那裡工作直到19世紀中期。"},{"en":"Until the middle of a period means continuing up to around the halfway point of that period.","zh":"until the middle of 某時期的意思是持續到該時期大約一半的位置。"},{"en":"The road will be closed until the middle of next month.","zh":"這條道路會關閉直到下個月中旬。"},{"en":"If a rule lasts until the middle of the year, people can expect change after that point.","zh":"如果一條規則持續到年中，人們可以預期之後會有改變。"},{"en":"This phrase marks when something stopped or changed.","zh":"這個短語標示某事停止或改變的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ordinary families","meaning":"普通家庭","examples":[{"en":"Ordinary families later took over the work.","zh":"普通家庭後來接手這項工作。"},{"en":"Ordinary families are normal families who are not famous, rich, or officially powerful.","zh":"ordinary families 是不出名、不富有或沒有官方權力的普通家庭。"},{"en":"Ordinary families often make big sacrifices to support children’s education.","zh":"普通家庭常作出重大犧牲來支持子女教育。"},{"en":"When ordinary families take on difficult work, history becomes about everyday people, not only leaders.","zh":"當普通家庭承擔困難工作，歷史就不只關於領袖，也關於日常人物。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on common people.","zh":"這個短語集中於普通人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be willing to","meaning":"願意……","examples":[{"en":"Ordinary families were willing to live in difficult circumstances.","zh":"普通家庭願意在困難環境中生活。"},{"en":"To be willing to do something means to accept or agree to do it.","zh":"be willing to do something 的意思是接受或同意做某事。"},{"en":"Volunteers are willing to help at the shelter even on weekends.","zh":"義工願意在週末到庇護中心幫忙。"},{"en":"People are more willing to do difficult work when they understand its purpose.","zh":"當人們理解工作的目的，他們會更願意做困難工作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows readiness or acceptance.","zh":"這個短語顯示準備好或願意接受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"live in such circumstances","meaning":"在這種環境下生活","examples":[{"en":"Some families were willing to live in such isolated circumstances.","zh":"有些家庭願意在這種偏僻環境下生活。"},{"en":"To live in such circumstances means to live under those particular conditions.","zh":"live in such circumstances 的意思是在那些特定條件下生活。"},{"en":"Some workers live in difficult circumstances because housing near their job is expensive.","zh":"有些工人因工作附近住屋昂貴而在困難環境下生活。"},{"en":"Living in isolated circumstances can be lonely and inconvenient.","zh":"在偏僻環境下生活可能孤單又不方便。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the conditions of daily life.","zh":"這個短語集中於日常生活條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"take over","meaning":"接手","examples":[{"en":"Ordinary families took over from prison convicts.","zh":"普通家庭從監獄囚犯手中接手。"},{"en":"To take over means to begin doing a job or responsibility that someone else did before.","zh":"take over 的意思是開始做之前由其他人負責的工作或責任。"},{"en":"A new manager may take over when the old manager retires.","zh":"舊經理退休時，新經理可能接手。"},{"en":"When someone takes over a task, they need to understand how it was done before.","zh":"當某人接手一項任務，他需要理解之前如何進行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a transfer of responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述責任轉移。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"some of you have asked me","meaning":"你們有些人問過我","examples":[{"en":"Some of the visitors have asked the guide about local creatures.","zh":"有些遊客問過導遊關於本地生物的事。"},{"en":"Some of you have asked me means a few people in the group have already asked the speaker a question.","zh":"some of you have asked me 的意思是群體中有幾個人已經問過說話者一個問題。"},{"en":"Some of you have asked me whether the trip will still happen if it rains.","zh":"你們有些人問過我，如果下雨旅程是否仍會進行。"},{"en":"This phrase lets a speaker answer a question that several listeners may share.","zh":"這個短語讓講者回答幾位聽眾可能都有的問題。"},{"en":"It sounds conversational and inclusive.","zh":"它聽起來像對話，也讓人感到被包括在內。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"what creatures we can expect to see","meaning":"我們預計會看到哪些生物","examples":[{"en":"The visitors asked what creatures they could expect to see.","zh":"遊客問他們預計會看到哪些生物。"},{"en":"What creatures we can expect to see means which animals are likely to appear during the trip.","zh":"what creatures we can expect to see 的意思是旅程中可能會出現哪些動物。"},{"en":"Before a forest walk, children may ask what creatures they can expect to see.","zh":"森林步行前，孩子可能問他們預計會看到哪些生物。"},{"en":"Knowing expected wildlife helps visitors stay alert without expecting guaranteed sightings.","zh":"知道預計可見的野生動物，有助遊客保持留意，但不會以為一定看到。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in nature tours.","zh":"這個短語適用於自然導賞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"penguins","meaning":"企鵝","examples":[{"en":"Visitors may hope to see penguins on the trip.","zh":"遊客可能希望在旅程中看到企鵝。"},{"en":"Penguins are flightless seabirds that usually live in cold or southern coastal regions.","zh":"penguins 是不會飛的海鳥，通常生活在寒冷或南方沿岸地區。"},{"en":"Tourists often watch penguins from a distance to avoid disturbing them.","zh":"遊客常從遠處觀看企鵝，以免打擾牠們。"},{"en":"Penguins may hide or move away if boats or people come too close.","zh":"如果船隻或人太接近，企鵝可能躲起來或離開。"},{"en":"This word names a well-known marine bird.","zh":"這個詞指一種著名海鳥。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tend to hide from","meaning":"通常躲避……","examples":[{"en":"Penguins tend to hide from passing boats.","zh":"企鵝通常躲避經過的船隻。"},{"en":"To tend to hide from something means to usually avoid it by staying out of sight.","zh":"tend to hide from something 的意思是通常避開某物並不讓自己被看見。"},{"en":"Shy children may tend to hide from visitors when guests arrive at home.","zh":"有客人到訪時，害羞孩子可能通常會躲避訪客。"},{"en":"Animals hide from threats because staying unseen can keep them safe.","zh":"動物躲避威脅，因為不被看見可以保障安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a usual behaviour, not something that always happens.","zh":"這個短語描述通常行為，而不是必然發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"passing boats","meaning":"經過的船隻","examples":[{"en":"Penguins often hide from passing boats.","zh":"企鵝常躲避經過的船隻。"},{"en":"Passing boats are boats that move past a place without stopping there for long.","zh":"passing boats 是經過某地但不長時間停留的船隻。"},{"en":"People on the shore may wave to passing boats.","zh":"岸上的人可能向經過的船隻揮手。"},{"en":"Wildlife may be disturbed if passing boats come too close or make too much noise.","zh":"如果經過的船隻太接近或太嘈，野生動物可能受干擾。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on boats moving by.","zh":"這個短語集中於正在經過的船。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the distance","meaning":"在遠處","examples":[{"en":"Visitors might see birds in the distance.","zh":"遊客可能在遠處看到雀鳥。"},{"en":"In the distance means far away from where someone is standing or looking.","zh":"in the distance 的意思是離某人站立或觀看的位置很遠。"},{"en":"We could see a lighthouse in the distance through the fog.","zh":"我們透過霧在遠處看到一座燈塔。"},{"en":"Something in the distance may look small or unclear because it is far away.","zh":"遠處的東西可能看起來很小或不清楚，因為距離很遠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location and perspective.","zh":"這個短語描述位置和視角。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sea eagles","meaning":"海鵰","examples":[{"en":"Visitors may see sea eagles flying around the cliffs.","zh":"遊客可能看到海鵰在懸崖周圍飛翔。"},{"en":"Sea eagles are large birds of prey that live near coasts, rivers, or lakes and hunt fish or other animals.","zh":"sea eagles 是生活在海岸、河流或湖泊附近的大型猛禽，會捕魚或其他動物。"},{"en":"Sea eagles may circle above cliffs while looking for food.","zh":"海鵰可能在懸崖上空盤旋尋找食物。"},{"en":"Seeing sea eagles can excite visitors because the birds are large and powerful.","zh":"看見海鵰可以令遊客興奮，因為牠們巨大而有力量。"},{"en":"This phrase names a coastal bird of prey.","zh":"這個短語指一種沿岸猛禽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fly around","meaning":"在……周圍飛翔","examples":[{"en":"Sea eagles fly around the cliff edges.","zh":"海鵰在懸崖邊周圍飛翔。"},{"en":"To fly around something means to move through the air near or around it.","zh":"fly around something 的意思是在某物附近或周圍於空中移動。"},{"en":"Birds often fly around trees before landing on a branch.","zh":"鳥兒常在樹木周圍飛翔，然後落在樹枝上。"},{"en":"When birds fly around cliffs, they may be hunting, nesting, or riding the wind.","zh":"當鳥兒在懸崖周圍飛翔，牠們可能在捕獵、築巢或乘風而行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated movement in the air.","zh":"這個短語描述空中的反覆移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cliff edges","meaning":"懸崖邊","examples":[{"en":"Sea eagles nest around the cliff edges.","zh":"海鵰在懸崖邊附近築巢。"},{"en":"Cliff edges are the outer borders of steep rock faces.","zh":"cliff edges 是陡峭岩壁的外圍邊緣。"},{"en":"Visitors should stay away from cliff edges because loose rocks can be dangerous.","zh":"遊客應遠離懸崖邊，因為鬆動石頭可能危險。"},{"en":"Birds may nest near cliff edges because predators are less likely to reach them.","zh":"鳥類可能在懸崖邊附近築巢，因為捕食者較難到達。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the risky boundary of a cliff.","zh":"這個短語描述懸崖的危險邊界。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"nest","meaning":"築巢","examples":[{"en":"Sea eagles nest near the cliff edges.","zh":"海鵰在懸崖邊附近築巢。"},{"en":"To nest means to build or use a place where birds lay eggs and raise young.","zh":"nest 的意思是建造或使用一個地方，讓鳥類產卵和養育幼鳥。"},{"en":"Swallows often nest under roofs or bridges.","zh":"燕子常在屋頂下或橋下築巢。"},{"en":"Birds choose nesting places that protect their eggs from weather and predators.","zh":"鳥類會選擇能保護鳥蛋免受天氣和捕食者影響的築巢地點。"},{"en":"This verb describes a key part of bird life.","zh":"這個動詞描述鳥類生活的重要部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rocky area","meaning":"岩石區","examples":[{"en":"The boat will stop near a rocky area inhabited by fur seals.","zh":"船會停在由海狗棲息的岩石區附近。"},{"en":"A rocky area is a place covered with many rocks or stone surfaces.","zh":"rocky area 是覆蓋許多岩石或石面的地方。"},{"en":"Children should wear strong shoes when walking through a rocky area.","zh":"兒童穿過岩石區時應穿結實鞋子。"},{"en":"Rocky coastal areas can provide resting places for seals and nesting places for seabirds.","zh":"沿岸岩石區可以為海豹提供休息地，也為海鳥提供築巢地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical character of a place.","zh":"這個短語描述一個地方的物理特徵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be inhabited by","meaning":"由……棲息","examples":[{"en":"The rocky area is inhabited by fur seals.","zh":"這個岩石區由海狗棲息。"},{"en":"To be inhabited by animals or people means they live there.","zh":"be inhabited by 動物或人，意思是牠們或他們住在那裡。"},{"en":"The island is inhabited by many seabirds during the breeding season.","zh":"繁殖季節期間，這座島由許多海鳥棲息。"},{"en":"If an area is inhabited by wildlife, visitors should avoid disturbing it.","zh":"如果一個地區由野生動物棲息，遊客應避免打擾它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in nature descriptions.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於自然描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fur seals","meaning":"海狗","examples":[{"en":"Fur seals live in the rocky area along the coast.","zh":"海狗住在沿岸的岩石區。"},{"en":"Fur seals are marine mammals with thick fur that often rest on rocky coasts.","zh":"fur seals 是有厚毛的海洋哺乳動物，常在岩石海岸休息。"},{"en":"Tourists may watch fur seals from a boat without going too close.","zh":"遊客可能從船上觀看海狗，而不太接近牠們。"},{"en":"Fur seals need safe resting areas because they spend time both in the sea and on land.","zh":"海狗需要安全休息區，因為牠們會在海中和陸上活動。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific sea animal.","zh":"這個短語指一種特定海洋動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"swim around the coast","meaning":"在海岸附近游泳","examples":[{"en":"The visitors will watch fur seals swimming around the coast.","zh":"遊客會觀看海狗在海岸附近游泳。"},{"en":"To swim around the coast means to move through the water near the shoreline.","zh":"swim around the coast 的意思是在靠近海岸線的水域中游動。"},{"en":"Dolphins may swim around the coast when they are feeding or playing.","zh":"海豚在覓食或玩耍時，可能在海岸附近游泳。"},{"en":"Watching animals swim around the coast can help visitors understand their natural habitat.","zh":"觀看動物在海岸附近游泳，可以幫助遊客理解牠們的自然棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement in coastal waters.","zh":"這個短語描述沿岸水域中的移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"inquisitive creatures","meaning":"好奇心強的生物","examples":[{"en":"Fur seals are inquisitive creatures.","zh":"海狗是好奇心強的生物。"},{"en":"Inquisitive creatures are animals that are curious and often interested in new things.","zh":"inquisitive creatures 是好奇並常對新事物感興趣的動物。"},{"en":"A young dog is often an inquisitive creature, sniffing every new object in a room.","zh":"小狗常是好奇心強的生物，會嗅房間中每件新物件。"},{"en":"Inquisitive animals may approach boats or people because they want to investigate.","zh":"好奇動物可能靠近船或人，因為牠們想探索。"},{"en":"This phrase describes curious behaviour in living things.","zh":"這個短語描述生物的好奇行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"don’t be surprised if","meaning":"如果……不要驚訝","examples":[{"en":"Don’t be surprised if a fur seal pops up in front of you.","zh":"如果一隻海狗突然在你面前冒出來，不要驚訝。"},{"en":"Don’t be surprised if means something may happen, so people should be ready for it.","zh":"don’t be surprised if 的意思是某事可能發生，所以人們應有心理準備。"},{"en":"Don’t be surprised if the bus is late during heavy rain.","zh":"如果大雨期間巴士遲到，不要驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase prepares listeners for something possible or likely.","zh":"這個短語讓聽眾為可能或很可能發生的事作準備。"},{"en":"It often softens a warning or expectation.","zh":"它常用來柔化警告或預期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pop up","meaning":"突然冒出來","examples":[{"en":"A fur seal may pop up right in front of the visitors.","zh":"海狗可能突然在遊客面前冒出來。"},{"en":"To pop up means to appear suddenly and often unexpectedly.","zh":"pop up 的意思是突然且常出乎意料地出現。"},{"en":"A message may pop up on your computer screen during a lesson.","zh":"上課期間，訊息可能突然在你的電腦螢幕上彈出。"},{"en":"When an animal pops up near a boat, passengers may be startled but excited.","zh":"當動物突然在船附近冒出來，乘客可能又驚又喜。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests sudden appearance.","zh":"這個短語表示突然出現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"right in front of","meaning":"就在……前面","examples":[{"en":"A fur seal may appear right in front of the boat.","zh":"海狗可能就在船前面出現。"},{"en":"Right in front of means directly before someone or something, very close to them.","zh":"right in front of 的意思是直接在某人或某物前面，非常接近。"},{"en":"The taxi stopped right in front of the hotel entrance.","zh":"的士停在酒店入口正前方。"},{"en":"When something appears right in front of you, it is hard to miss.","zh":"當某物就在你前面出現，你很難錯過。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises closeness and direct position.","zh":"這個短語強調接近和直接位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"predators","meaning":"捕食者","examples":[{"en":"Orca whales are predators of fur seals.","zh":"虎鯨是海狗的捕食者。"},{"en":"Predators are animals that hunt and eat other animals.","zh":"predators 是獵捕並吃其他動物的動物。"},{"en":"Cats are predators of small birds and mice.","zh":"貓是小鳥和老鼠的捕食者。"},{"en":"Predators help balance ecosystems by controlling the numbers of other animals.","zh":"捕食者透過控制其他動物數量，幫助平衡生態系統。"},{"en":"This word describes the hunter in a food chain.","zh":"這個詞描述食物鏈中的獵食者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"orca whales","meaning":"虎鯨","examples":[{"en":"Orca whales hunt along the coastline.","zh":"虎鯨沿着海岸線捕獵。"},{"en":"Orca whales are large black-and-white marine mammals also known as killer whales.","zh":"orca whales 是大型黑白色海洋哺乳動物，也稱為 killer whales。"},{"en":"Orca whales can hunt fish, seals, and other marine animals.","zh":"虎鯨可以捕食魚、海豹和其他海洋動物。"},{"en":"Seeing orca whales is exciting because they are powerful but not commonly seen on every trip.","zh":"看見虎鯨令人興奮，因為牠們強大，但並非每次旅程都常見。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific ocean predator.","zh":"這個短語指一種特定海洋捕食者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hunt along","meaning":"沿着……捕獵","examples":[{"en":"Orca whales hunt along the coastline.","zh":"虎鯨沿着海岸線捕獵。"},{"en":"To hunt along a place means to search for and catch prey while moving through that area.","zh":"hunt along 某地的意思是在穿過該區域時尋找並捕捉獵物。"},{"en":"Cats may hunt along garden walls at night.","zh":"貓可能在夜晚沿着花園圍牆捕獵。"},{"en":"Animals often hunt along routes where prey is likely to appear.","zh":"動物常沿着獵物可能出現的路線捕獵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hunting movement across a particular area.","zh":"這個短語描述在特定區域中的捕獵移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"spotting one of these is rare","meaning":"看見這些其中之一很罕見","examples":[{"en":"Spotting an orca whale is rare.","zh":"看見虎鯨很罕見。"},{"en":"Spotting one of these is rare means seeing one is unusual and does not happen often.","zh":"spotting one of these is rare 的意思是看見其中之一並不常見。"},{"en":"Spotting a shooting star is rare if the sky is cloudy and city lights are bright.","zh":"如果天空多雲而城市燈光明亮，看見流星會很罕見。"},{"en":"Rare sightings feel special because visitors cannot expect them every time.","zh":"罕見目擊令人感到特別，因為遊客不能每次都期待見到。"},{"en":"This phrase sets realistic expectations.","zh":"這個短語設定現實期望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"Dolphins, on the other hand, may sometimes approach the boat.","zh":"另一方面，海豚有時可能靠近船。"},{"en":"On the other hand is used to introduce a contrast or different point.","zh":"on the other hand 用來引出對比或不同觀點。"},{"en":"The walk is long; on the other hand, the view at the end is beautiful.","zh":"這段路很長；另一方面，終點景色很美。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare two situations fairly.","zh":"這個短語幫助公平比較兩種情況。"},{"en":"It often shows that one point is different from the previous one.","zh":"它常顯示某一點與前一點不同。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"approach on their own","meaning":"獨自靠近","examples":[{"en":"Dolphins can approach the boat on their own.","zh":"海豚可以獨自靠近船。"},{"en":"To approach on their own means to come closer without being forced, called, or chased.","zh":"approach on their own 的意思是在沒有被強迫、呼喚或追趕下自行靠近。"},{"en":"A shy cat may approach on its own when it feels safe.","zh":"害羞的貓在感到安全時，可能會自己靠近。"},{"en":"Wild animals should approach people on their own; people should not chase them.","zh":"野生動物應該自行靠近人；人不應追趕牠們。"},{"en":"This phrase shows voluntary movement.","zh":"這個短語顯示自願移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in groups","meaning":"成群地","examples":[{"en":"Dolphins may approach in groups.","zh":"海豚可能成群地靠近。"},{"en":"In groups means together with several others, not alone.","zh":"in groups 的意思是與幾個其他人或動物一起，而不是單獨。"},{"en":"Students often work in groups during science experiments.","zh":"學生在科學實驗中常成組工作。"},{"en":"Animals moving in groups may be safer because they can watch for danger together.","zh":"動物成群地移動可能更安全，因為牠們可以一起留意危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collective action.","zh":"這個短語描述集體行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ride the waves","meaning":"乘着海浪前進","examples":[{"en":"Dolphins sometimes ride the waves beside the boat.","zh":"海豚有時在船旁乘着海浪前進。"},{"en":"To ride the waves means to move along with the force and shape of waves.","zh":"ride the waves 的意思是順着海浪的力量和形狀移動。"},{"en":"Surfers ride the waves by balancing on a board.","zh":"滑浪者透過在滑浪板上保持平衡來乘着海浪前進。"},{"en":"Dolphins may ride waves because the water movement helps them travel and play.","zh":"海豚可能乘着海浪前進，因為水流能幫助牠們移動和玩耍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement using wave energy.","zh":"這個短語描述利用海浪能量移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"beside us","meaning":"在我們旁邊","examples":[{"en":"Dolphins may ride the waves beside the boat.","zh":"海豚可能在船旁乘着海浪前進。"},{"en":"Beside us means next to us or close at our side.","zh":"beside us 的意思是在我們旁邊或靠近我們側面。"},{"en":"A friend sat beside us during the concert.","zh":"音樂會期間，一位朋友坐在我們旁邊。"},{"en":"When dolphins swim beside a boat, passengers can see them clearly without leaving their seats.","zh":"當海豚在船旁游泳，乘客不用離開座位也能清楚看見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes close side-by-side position.","zh":"這個短語描述近距離並排位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lastly","meaning":"最後","examples":[{"en":"Lastly, the guide mentions the caves.","zh":"最後，導遊提到洞穴。"},{"en":"Lastly means finally, before finishing a list or explanation.","zh":"lastly 的意思是在清單或解釋結束前，最後一點。"},{"en":"Lastly, please remember to bring your student card tomorrow.","zh":"最後，請記得明天帶學生證。"},{"en":"Speakers use lastly to show that they are reaching the final point.","zh":"講者使用 lastly 來顯示自己正說到最後一點。"},{"en":"This word helps organise information clearly.","zh":"這個詞幫助清楚組織資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mention the caves","meaning":"提及洞穴","examples":[{"en":"The guide wants to mention the caves before the boat leaves.","zh":"導遊想在船離開前提及洞穴。"},{"en":"To mention the caves means to talk about the caves briefly or include them in the explanation.","zh":"mention the caves 的意思是簡短談到洞穴或把它們包括在解釋中。"},{"en":"A teacher may mention the museum shop before students leave the exhibition.","zh":"老師可能在學生離開展覽前提及博物館商店。"},{"en":"Mentioning an attraction before arrival helps visitors know what to look for.","zh":"到達前提及景點，有助遊客知道要留意甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a short but useful reference.","zh":"這個短語表示簡短但有用的提及。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the ones we’ll pass by","meaning":"我們將會經過的那些","examples":[{"en":"The caves the boat will pass by are very impressive.","zh":"我們將會經過的那些洞穴非常壯觀。"},{"en":"The ones we’ll pass by means the particular places or things we will go past during the journey.","zh":"the ones we’ll pass by 的意思是旅程中我們將會經過的特定地方或事物。"},{"en":"The buildings we’ll pass by on the bus are some of the oldest in the city.","zh":"我們乘巴士將會經過的那些建築物，是城中一些最古老的建築。"},{"en":"Pointing out the ones we will pass by helps visitors prepare to look in the right direction.","zh":"指出我們將會經過的那些地方，有助遊客準備望向正確方向。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to specific things on the route.","zh":"這個短語指路線上的特定事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be lost for words","meaning":"驚訝得說不出話","examples":[{"en":"People are lost for words when they see the caves.","zh":"人們看見洞穴時驚訝得說不出話。"},{"en":"To be lost for words means to be so surprised, impressed, or emotional that you do not know what to say.","zh":"be lost for words 的意思是因太驚訝、太感動或情緒太強而不知道說甚麼。"},{"en":"She was lost for words when she saw the mountain view at sunrise.","zh":"她看見日出時的山景，驚訝得說不出話。"},{"en":"People may be lost for words when something is more beautiful or shocking than expected.","zh":"當某事比預期更美或更震撼，人們可能驚訝得說不出話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong emotion that stops speech.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈情緒令人無法說話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"can only be approached by sea","meaning":"只能從海上接近","examples":[{"en":"The caves can only be approached by sea.","zh":"這些洞穴只能從海上接近。"},{"en":"If a place can only be approached by sea, people can reach it only by boat or from the water.","zh":"如果一個地方 can only be approached by sea，意思是人們只能乘船或從水上到達。"},{"en":"Some remote beaches can only be approached by sea because cliffs block the land route.","zh":"有些偏遠海灘因懸崖阻隔陸路，只能從海上接近。"},{"en":"Places that can only be approached by sea may feel special but require careful safety planning.","zh":"只能從海上接近的地方可能感覺特別，但需要仔細安全規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited access.","zh":"這個短語描述受限制的進入方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"if you feel that","meaning":"如果你覺得……","examples":[{"en":"If visitors feel that they want to see more, they can return by kayak.","zh":"如果遊客覺得想看更多，他們可以划獨木舟回來。"},{"en":"If you feel that means if you think, believe, or have the desire that something is true or needed.","zh":"if you feel that 的意思是如果你認為、相信或有某種需要或感受。"},{"en":"If you feel that the class is too difficult, speak to the teacher early.","zh":"如果你覺得課堂太難，應及早和老師說。"},{"en":"This phrase invites personal judgement or feeling.","zh":"這個短語邀請人作出個人判斷或表達感受。"},{"en":"It sounds softer than simply saying “if you want”.","zh":"它比單純說 if you want 語氣更柔和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"more than we’re able to show you","meaning":"比我們能展示給你的更多","examples":[{"en":"Visitors may want to see more than the boat trip can show them.","zh":"遊客可能想看比這次乘船遊覽能展示給他們的更多內容。"},{"en":"More than we’re able to show you means beyond what we can include, provide, or display this time.","zh":"more than we’re able to show you 的意思是超出我們這次能包括、提供或展示的範圍。"},{"en":"A museum guide may say there is more than they are able to show visitors in one hour.","zh":"博物館導遊可能說，一小時內能展示給遊客的內容有限，還有更多看不到。"},{"en":"Limited time means a tour can show highlights, not everything.","zh":"時間有限代表導賞只能展示重點，而不是所有東西。"},{"en":"This phrase politely explains a limit.","zh":"這個短語禮貌地解釋限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take a kayak into","meaning":"划獨木舟進入……","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can take a kayak into the area on another day.","zh":"遊客可以在另一天划獨木舟進入該區。"},{"en":"To take a kayak into an area means to travel there in a small narrow boat moved by paddling.","zh":"take a kayak into an area 的意思是乘坐用槳推動的小型狹長船進入某地區。"},{"en":"Adventurous visitors may take a kayak into a quiet bay to see wildlife closely.","zh":"喜歡冒險的遊客可能划獨木舟進入寧靜海灣，近距離觀看野生動物。"},{"en":"Taking a kayak into caves can give better views, but it requires safety knowledge.","zh":"划獨木舟進入洞穴可以看到更好景色，但需要安全知識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes travel by kayak into a place.","zh":"這個短語描述以獨木舟進入某地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on another day","meaning":"在另一天","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can return to the caves by kayak on another day.","zh":"遊客可以在另一天划獨木舟回到洞穴。"},{"en":"On another day means at a different time, not today or not during this trip.","zh":"on another day 的意思是在另一個時間，不是今天或不是這次旅程期間。"},{"en":"If the museum is too crowded, we can visit on another day.","zh":"如果博物館太擠，我們可以在另一天參觀。"},{"en":"Suggesting another day gives people a future option when time is limited.","zh":"建議另一天給人未來選項，尤其在時間有限時。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for rescheduling or extending plans.","zh":"這個短語適合用於重新安排或延伸計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"give you more information on","meaning":"向你提供更多關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"A member of staff will give visitors more information on kayaking.","zh":"一名職員會向遊客提供更多關於划獨木舟的資料。"},{"en":"To give you more information on something means to provide extra details about that topic.","zh":"give you more information on something 的意思是就該主題提供額外細節。"},{"en":"The librarian can give you more information on joining the reading club.","zh":"圖書館員可以向你提供更多關於加入閱讀會的資料。"},{"en":"Extra information helps people decide whether an activity suits their time, ability, and budget.","zh":"額外資料幫助人們決定活動是否適合自己的時間、能力和預算。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and practical in customer service.","zh":"這個短語在客戶服務中禮貌而實用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"what we’ll do is to","meaning":"我們會做的是……","examples":[{"en":"What the boat will do is to go through a narrow channel.","zh":"這艘船會做的是穿過一條狹窄水道。"},{"en":"What we’ll do is to means the speaker is about to explain the plan or next action.","zh":"what we’ll do is to 的意思是說話者即將解釋計劃或下一步行動。"},{"en":"What we’ll do is to finish the easy questions first and then return to the harder ones.","zh":"我們會做的是先完成容易題目，然後再回到較難題目。"},{"en":"This phrase helps listeners follow a plan step by step.","zh":"這個短語幫助聽眾逐步跟上計劃。"},{"en":"It often introduces a clear action after a general explanation.","zh":"它常在一般解釋後引出清晰行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"go through","meaning":"穿過","examples":[{"en":"The boat will go through a narrow channel.","zh":"船會穿過一條狹窄水道。"},{"en":"To go through a place means to pass from one side or end to the other.","zh":"go through a place 的意思是從某地方的一邊或一端穿行到另一邊或另一端。"},{"en":"The train will go through several tunnels before reaching the city.","zh":"火車到達城市前會穿過幾條隧道。"},{"en":"Going through a narrow space requires careful control and attention.","zh":"穿過狹窄空間需要小心控制和注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement through the inside of a route or space.","zh":"這個短語描述穿過路線或空間內部的移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"narrow channel","meaning":"狹窄水道","examples":[{"en":"The boat will go through a narrow channel.","zh":"船會穿過一條狹窄水道。"},{"en":"A narrow channel is a thin passage of water between land, rocks, or islands.","zh":"narrow channel 是位於陸地、岩石或小島之間的狹長水路。"},{"en":"Small boats can pass through a narrow channel that large ships cannot enter.","zh":"小船可以穿過大型船隻不能進入的狹窄水道。"},{"en":"A narrow channel may require slow speed because there is little space to turn.","zh":"狹窄水道可能需要慢速行駛，因為轉向空間很少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a tight water route.","zh":"這個短語描述狹窄的水上路線。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"incredible rock formations","meaning":"令人驚嘆的岩石形態","examples":[{"en":"The boat will pass some incredible rock formations.","zh":"船會經過一些令人驚嘆的岩石形態。"},{"en":"Incredible rock formations are impressive natural rock shapes created by wind, water, time, or geological forces.","zh":"incredible rock formations 是由風、水、時間或地質力量形成的壯觀自然岩石形狀。"},{"en":"Tourists often take photos of incredible rock formations because they look unusual and dramatic.","zh":"遊客常拍攝令人驚嘆的岩石形態，因為它們看起來奇特而壯觀。"},{"en":"Rock formations can help explain how landscapes were shaped over many years.","zh":"岩石形態可以幫助解釋地貌如何經多年塑造。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights both beauty and natural structure.","zh":"這個短語同時突出美感和自然結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"from there","meaning":"從那裏","examples":[{"en":"From there, visitors will be able to see the cave openings.","zh":"從那裏，遊客將能看到洞穴入口。"},{"en":"From there means from that place or position.","zh":"from there 的意思是從那個地方或位置。"},{"en":"Walk to the bridge; from there, you can see the whole harbour.","zh":"走到橋上；從那裏，你可以看到整個海港。"},{"en":"A guide uses “from there” to explain what becomes visible at a certain point.","zh":"導遊使用 from there 來解釋在某個位置可以看到甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a location with the next view or action.","zh":"這個短語把一個位置與下一個景觀或行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"openings to the caves","meaning":"洞穴入口","examples":[{"en":"Visitors will be able to see the openings to the caves.","zh":"遊客將能看到洞穴入口。"},{"en":"Openings to the caves are the entrances or visible gaps leading into the caves.","zh":"openings to the caves 是通往洞穴的入口或可見缺口。"},{"en":"From the beach, children could see dark openings to caves in the cliffs.","zh":"從海灘上，孩子可以看見懸崖上黑暗的洞穴入口。"},{"en":"Cave openings can look mysterious because people cannot always see what is inside.","zh":"洞穴入口可能看起來神秘，因為人們不一定看到裏面有甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where a cave begins.","zh":"這個短語描述洞穴開始的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"at that point","meaning":"到那個時候","examples":[{"en":"At that point, the guides will explain what lies beyond.","zh":"到那個時候，導遊會解釋裏面深處有甚麼。"},{"en":"At that point means at that particular moment, stage, or place in a process.","zh":"at that point 的意思是在過程中的那個特定時刻、階段或位置。"},{"en":"Finish the first draft; at that point, the teacher will give feedback.","zh":"完成初稿；到那個時候，老師會給回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show when the next action will happen.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示下一個行動何時發生。"},{"en":"It is useful for guiding people through a sequence.","zh":"它適合用於引導人們跟隨一個次序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"what lies beyond","meaning":"裏面深處有甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The guides will talk about what lies beyond the cave openings.","zh":"導遊會講解洞穴入口裏面深處有甚麼。"},{"en":"What lies beyond means what exists farther inside, farther away, or past the visible point.","zh":"what lies beyond 的意思是更深處、更遠處或可見位置之後存在甚麼。"},{"en":"A museum guide may explain what lies beyond a locked door if visitors cannot enter.","zh":"如果遊客不能進入，博物館導遊可能解釋鎖門後面深處有甚麼。"},{"en":"People feel curious about what lies beyond when they can see only the entrance or edge of a place.","zh":"當人們只能看到入口或邊緣，他們會對裏面深處有甚麼感到好奇。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a sense of mystery and further discovery.","zh":"這個短語營造神秘感和進一步探索的感覺。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/listening/Practice 12/task-3":[{"front":"short summary of","meaning":"……的簡短總結","examples":[{"en":"Diana and Tim have to do a short summary of their work experience.","zh":"Diana 和 Tim 必須做一個關於他們工作體驗的簡短總結。"},{"en":"A short summary of something is a brief account of its main points.","zh":"short summary of something 是指某事主要內容的簡短說明。"},{"en":"A student may write a short summary of a book after finishing it.","zh":"學生讀完一本書後，可能會寫一個簡短總結。"},{"en":"A short summary helps listeners understand the key ideas without too much detail.","zh":"簡短總結幫助聽者了解重點，而不用聽太多細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when only the most important information is needed.","zh":"當只需要最重要資料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"work experience on a farm","meaning":"農場工作體驗；農場實習","examples":[{"en":"The students are discussing their work experience on a farm.","zh":"學生正在討論他們的農場工作體驗。"},{"en":"Work experience on a farm means spending time working or observing work on a farm to learn practical skills.","zh":"work experience on a farm 是指在農場工作或觀察工作，以學習實用技能。"},{"en":"A student may do work experience on a farm to learn how animals are cared for.","zh":"學生可能進行農場工作體驗，以學習如何照顧動物。"},{"en":"Farm work experience can show students that animal care involves early mornings and physical work.","zh":"農場工作體驗可以讓學生知道動物護理涉及早起和體力勞動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to real workplace learning, not just reading about farming.","zh":"這個短語指真實工作場所學習，而不只是閱讀農業資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"arrange the work experience","meaning":"安排工作體驗","examples":[{"en":"Tim found arranging the work experience hard.","zh":"Tim 覺得安排工作體驗很困難。"},{"en":"To arrange the work experience means to organise where, when, and how the placement will happen.","zh":"arrange the work experience 是指安排實習地點、時間和進行方式。"},{"en":"A student may arrange work experience by emailing companies and checking available dates.","zh":"學生可能透過電郵公司和確認日期來安排工作體驗。"},{"en":"Arranging a placement can be difficult if transport, timing, or accommodation is a problem.","zh":"如果交通、時間或住宿有問題，安排實習可能很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the planning before the experience begins.","zh":"這個短語著重體驗開始前的規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"miles away","meaning":"很遠","examples":[{"en":"Tim’s farm was miles away, and he does not drive.","zh":"Tim 的農場很遠，而他不會駕車。"},{"en":"Miles away means very far from where someone is.","zh":"miles away 是指離某人所在地方非常遠。"},{"en":"The nearest hospital may feel miles away if there is no bus service.","zh":"如果沒有巴士服務，最近的醫院可能感覺很遠。"},{"en":"If a workplace is miles away, travelling there every day can be tiring.","zh":"如果工作地點很遠，每天通勤可能很累。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often expresses inconvenience caused by distance.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常表達距離造成的不便。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"placement for","meaning":"……的實習崗位","examples":[{"en":"Tim wanted a placement for a month.","zh":"Tim 想要一個為期一個月的實習崗位。"},{"en":"A placement for a period of time is a temporary position arranged for training or experience.","zh":"placement for a period of time 是指為訓練或體驗而安排的臨時崗位。"},{"en":"A nursing student may need a hospital placement for six weeks.","zh":"護理學生可能需要一個為期六星期的醫院實習崗位。"},{"en":"The length of a placement affects how much the student can learn.","zh":"實習長度會影響學生能學到多少。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in education, training, and workplace learning.","zh":"這個短語常見於教育、培訓和職場學習中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"could only get one for","meaning":"只能找到一個為期……的","examples":[{"en":"Tim could only get a placement for two weeks.","zh":"Tim 只能找到一個為期兩星期的實習崗位。"},{"en":"Could only get one for means the best available option lasted only that length of time.","zh":"could only get one for 是指可找到的最好選項只維持那段時間。"},{"en":"A student wanted a summer job for two months but could only get one for three weeks.","zh":"學生想找兩個月暑期工，但只能找到一份為期三星期的。"},{"en":"Limited availability can force people to accept a shorter placement than they wanted.","zh":"名額有限可能迫使人接受比期望更短的實習。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the result was less than the person hoped for.","zh":"這個短語顯示結果低於那個人原本希望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"let someone stay","meaning":"讓某人留下；讓某人住宿","examples":[{"en":"The farmer let Diana stay on the farm.","zh":"農夫讓 Diana 住在農場。"},{"en":"To let someone stay means to allow that person to live or sleep somewhere temporarily.","zh":"let someone stay 是指允許某人暫時居住或過夜。"},{"en":"A friend may let you stay at her flat if your train is cancelled.","zh":"如果你的火車取消，朋友可能讓你在她的單位住宿。"},{"en":"Letting someone stay can solve transport problems when the place is far away.","zh":"讓某人住宿可以解決地點很遠時的交通問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on giving permission to remain somewhere.","zh":"這個短語著重給予留在某地的許可。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"did not have to travel","meaning":"不用通勤","examples":[{"en":"Diana stayed on the farm, so she did not have to travel.","zh":"Diana 住在農場，所以不用通勤。"},{"en":"Did not have to travel means there was no need to make a journey each day.","zh":"did not have to travel 是指不需要每天出行。"},{"en":"If a student lives near school, she does not have to travel far in the morning.","zh":"如果學生住在學校附近，早上就不用走很遠。"},{"en":"Not having to travel saves time, money, and energy.","zh":"不用通勤可以節省時間、金錢和精力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when accommodation removes the need for commuting.","zh":"當住宿安排免除了通勤需要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the right sort of","meaning":"合適類型的……","examples":[{"en":"Finding the right sort of farm to apply to was not easy.","zh":"找到合適類型的農場去申請並不容易。"},{"en":"The right sort of something means the type that fits your needs or purpose.","zh":"the right sort of something 是指符合需要或目的的類型。"},{"en":"A student needs the right sort of course if she wants practical training, not just theory.","zh":"如果學生想要實用訓練而不只是理論，她需要合適類型的課程。"},{"en":"Choosing the wrong sort of placement may mean the student cannot learn what they need.","zh":"選錯類型的實習可能令學生學不到需要的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses suitability, not just availability.","zh":"這個短語強調合適，而不只是有名額。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"apply to","meaning":"申請","examples":[{"en":"Diana had difficulty finding the right farm to apply to.","zh":"Diana 很難找到合適的農場去申請。"},{"en":"To apply to a place means to formally ask to join, work, study, or train there.","zh":"apply to a place 是指正式申請加入、工作、學習或受訓。"},{"en":"A student may apply to several companies for summer work experience.","zh":"學生可能向幾間公司申請暑期工作體驗。"},{"en":"Applying to the right organisation increases the chance of a useful placement.","zh":"申請合適機構會增加獲得有用實習的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase usually involves forms, emails, interviews, or official requests.","zh":"這個短語通常涉及表格、電郵、面試或正式請求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"through a friend of","meaning":"透過……的一位朋友","examples":[{"en":"Tim found his farm through a friend of his mother’s.","zh":"Tim 透過他母親的一位朋友找到那個農場。"},{"en":"Through a friend of someone means by using that person’s social connection.","zh":"through a friend of someone 是指透過某人的社交關係。"},{"en":"A graduate may find her first job through a friend of her teacher’s.","zh":"畢業生可能透過老師的一位朋友找到第一份工作。"},{"en":"Personal connections can help people find opportunities that are not advertised.","zh":"人脈可以幫助人找到沒有公開招聘的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how someone obtained information or access through another person.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人如何透過另一個人取得資料或機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mostly livestock","meaning":"主要是牲畜","examples":[{"en":"Tim’s farm was mostly livestock, especially sheep.","zh":"Tim 的農場主要是牲畜，尤其是羊。"},{"en":"Mostly livestock means the farm mainly keeps animals rather than growing crops.","zh":"mostly livestock 是指農場主要飼養動物，而不是種植農作物。"},{"en":"A farm that is mostly livestock may have cows, sheep, goats, or chickens.","zh":"一個主要飼養牲畜的農場可能有牛、羊、山羊或雞。"},{"en":"Livestock farms require daily feeding, cleaning, and health checks.","zh":"牲畜農場需要每天餵飼、清潔和檢查健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main type of farming done there.","zh":"這個短語描述該農場主要從事的農業類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"livestock","meaning":"牲畜","examples":[{"en":"The farm kept livestock, especially sheep.","zh":"這個農場飼養牲畜，尤其是羊。"},{"en":"Livestock are farm animals kept for food, milk, wool, work, or sale.","zh":"livestock 是為了食物、牛奶、羊毛、勞動或出售而飼養的農場動物。"},{"en":"Cows, sheep, pigs, goats, and chickens can all be livestock.","zh":"牛、羊、豬、山羊和雞都可以是牲畜。"},{"en":"Livestock need proper food, shelter, water, and veterinary care.","zh":"牲畜需要適當食物、住所、水和獸醫護理。"},{"en":"This word refers to farm animals, not wild animals or pets.","zh":"這個詞指農場動物，而不是野生動物或寵物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"help out with","meaning":"幫忙處理；幫忙照顧","examples":[{"en":"Tim enjoyed helping out with the sheep.","zh":"Tim 喜歡幫忙照顧羊。"},{"en":"To help out with something means to assist with a task, often in a practical way.","zh":"help out with something 是指協助處理某項任務，通常是實際工作。"},{"en":"A child may help out with dinner by washing vegetables.","zh":"孩子可能透過洗菜幫忙準備晚餐。"},{"en":"Helping out on a farm can include feeding animals, cleaning sheds, or moving equipment.","zh":"在農場幫忙可以包括餵動物、清潔棚舍或搬運設備。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds friendly and often suggests teamwork.","zh":"這個短語聽起來友善，常表示合作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be up most of one night","meaning":"幾乎整晚沒睡","examples":[{"en":"Tim was up most of one night helping a sheep give birth.","zh":"Tim 有一晚幾乎整晚沒睡，幫一隻羊生產。"},{"en":"To be up most of one night means to stay awake for most of the night.","zh":"be up most of one night 是指一晚大部分時間都醒着。"},{"en":"A parent may be up most of one night caring for a sick child.","zh":"父母可能為照顧生病孩子而幾乎整晚沒睡。"},{"en":"Staying up most of the night can leave someone tired the next day.","zh":"幾乎整晚沒睡會令人第二天很疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a long period without normal sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述長時間沒有正常睡眠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"deliver a lamb","meaning":"接生小羊","examples":[{"en":"Tim helped a sheep deliver a lamb.","zh":"Tim 幫一隻羊接生小羊。"},{"en":"To deliver a lamb means to help a sheep give birth to a baby sheep.","zh":"deliver a lamb 是指幫母羊生下一隻小羊。"},{"en":"A farmer may need to deliver a lamb if the mother sheep is having difficulty.","zh":"如果母羊生產有困難，農夫可能需要接生小羊。"},{"en":"Helping deliver a lamb requires calm hands and knowledge of animal birth.","zh":"接生小羊需要冷靜的雙手和動物生產知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in farming or veterinary contexts.","zh":"這個短語用於農場或獸醫語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on your own","meaning":"獨自一人","examples":[{"en":"Diana asks whether Tim helped the sheep on his own.","zh":"Diana 問 Tim 是否獨自一人幫那隻羊。"},{"en":"On your own means alone, without help from other people.","zh":"on your own 是指獨自一人，沒有別人幫助。"},{"en":"A student may find it hard to complete a science project on her own.","zh":"學生可能覺得獨自完成科學專題很困難。"},{"en":"Doing a difficult task on your own can be stressful if you lack experience.","zh":"如果缺乏經驗，獨自做困難任務可能很有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises independence or lack of support.","zh":"這個短語強調獨立或缺乏支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tell someone what to do","meaning":"告訴某人要做甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The farmer told Tim what to do during the birth.","zh":"農夫在生產期間告訴 Tim 要做甚麼。"},{"en":"To tell someone what to do means to give instructions or guidance.","zh":"tell someone what to do 是指給某人指示或指導。"},{"en":"A teacher may tell students what to do before a laboratory experiment.","zh":"老師可能在實驗室實驗前告訴學生要做甚麼。"},{"en":"Clear instructions help beginners avoid mistakes in unfamiliar tasks.","zh":"清楚指示幫助初學者避免在陌生任務中犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase can be neutral, though it may sound bossy in some situations.","zh":"這個短語本身可以是中性，但在某些情況下可能聽起來專橫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"straightforward birth","meaning":"順利的生產","examples":[{"en":"The lamb’s birth was not straightforward.","zh":"那隻小羊的出生並不順利。"},{"en":"A straightforward birth is a birth that happens easily, normally, and without major problems.","zh":"straightforward birth 是指容易、正常而沒有重大問題的生產。"},{"en":"A farmer is relieved when a cow has a straightforward birth without needing extra help.","zh":"如果母牛順利生產而不需要額外幫助，農夫會鬆一口氣。"},{"en":"If a birth is not straightforward, a vet or experienced person may be needed.","zh":"如果生產不順利，可能需要獸醫或有經驗的人協助。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts a simple birth with a difficult or risky one.","zh":"這個短語把簡單生產與困難或有風險的生產作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"manage","meaning":"應付得來","examples":[{"en":"The birth was difficult, but Tim managed.","zh":"生產很困難，但 Tim 應付得來。"},{"en":"To manage means to succeed in doing something difficult.","zh":"manage 是指成功完成困難的事情。"},{"en":"A student may find the homework hard but still manage to finish it before dinner.","zh":"學生可能覺得功課很難，但仍能在晚飯前完成。"},{"en":"People manage difficult tasks better when they have guidance and stay calm.","zh":"有指導並保持冷靜時，人們較能應付困難任務。"},{"en":"This verb shows success despite difficulty.","zh":"這個動詞顯示即使有困難，仍然成功。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a great feeling to","meaning":"做……的感覺很好","examples":[{"en":"It was a great feeling to see the lamb stand up.","zh":"看到小羊站起來感覺很好。"},{"en":"A great feeling to do something means the experience makes you feel happy, proud, or relieved.","zh":"a great feeling to do something 是指做某事令人感到開心、自豪或鬆一口氣。"},{"en":"It is a great feeling to pass an exam after months of practice.","zh":"練習幾個月後通過考試，感覺很好。"},{"en":"Seeing a result after hard work often creates a great feeling.","zh":"努力後看到成果，常會帶來很好的感覺。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the emotion caused by an experience.","zh":"這個短語著重經歷所帶來的情感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stagger to its feet","meaning":"搖搖晃晃地站起來","examples":[{"en":"The lamb staggered to its feet after being born.","zh":"小羊出生後搖搖晃晃地站起來。"},{"en":"To stagger to its feet means to stand up unsteadily and with difficulty.","zh":"stagger to its feet 是指困難而不穩地站起來。"},{"en":"A tired runner may stagger to his feet after falling near the finish line.","zh":"疲累的跑手可能在終點附近跌倒後搖搖晃晃地站起來。"},{"en":"Newborn animals often stagger because their legs are weak at first.","zh":"初生動物常會搖晃，因為牠們的腿一開始很弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shaky movement while trying to stand.","zh":"這個短語描述嘗試站立時不穩的動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"start feeding","meaning":"開始吃奶；開始進食","examples":[{"en":"The lamb started feeding almost straightaway.","zh":"小羊幾乎立刻開始吃奶。"},{"en":"To start feeding means to begin drinking milk or eating food.","zh":"start feeding 是指開始喝奶或吃東西。"},{"en":"A newborn puppy should start feeding soon after birth.","zh":"初生小狗應在出生後不久開始吃奶。"},{"en":"Starting to feed quickly is important because young animals need energy and warmth.","zh":"很快開始吃奶很重要，因為幼小動物需要能量和保暖。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for babies or young animals.","zh":"這個短語常用於嬰兒或幼小動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"almost straightaway","meaning":"幾乎立刻","examples":[{"en":"The lamb started feeding almost straightaway.","zh":"小羊幾乎立刻開始吃奶。"},{"en":"Almost straightaway means very soon after something happens.","zh":"almost straightaway 是指某事發生後很快。"},{"en":"After the fire alarm rang, students left the classroom almost straightaway.","zh":"火警鐘響後，學生幾乎立刻離開課室。"},{"en":"When something happens almost straightaway, there is very little delay.","zh":"當某事幾乎立刻發生，延遲很少。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English and means nearly immediately.","zh":"這個短語常見於英式英語，意思接近 immediately。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get the vet in","meaning":"請獸醫來","examples":[{"en":"The farmer got the vet in to set the lamb’s leg.","zh":"農夫請獸醫來接駁小羊的腿。"},{"en":"To get the vet in means to call or bring a veterinarian to come and help.","zh":"get the vet in 是指召喚或請獸醫前來幫忙。"},{"en":"A farmer may get the vet in if a cow stops eating for several days.","zh":"如果牛幾天不吃東西，農夫可能會請獸醫來。"},{"en":"Getting the vet in can prevent a small health problem from becoming serious.","zh":"請獸醫來可以防止小健康問題變嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and focuses on bringing professional help to the farm.","zh":"這個短語較口語，著重把專業協助帶到農場。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"set a broken leg","meaning":"接駁斷腿","examples":[{"en":"The vet came to set the lamb’s broken leg.","zh":"獸醫來接駁小羊的斷腿。"},{"en":"To set a broken leg means to put the broken bone into the correct position so it can heal.","zh":"set a broken leg 是指把斷骨放回正確位置，讓它可以癒合。"},{"en":"A doctor may set a broken arm before putting it in a cast.","zh":"醫生可能在打石膏前接駁斷手。"},{"en":"Setting a broken bone properly helps prevent long-term pain or poor movement.","zh":"正確接駁斷骨有助防止長期痛楚或活動不良。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in medical and veterinary situations.","zh":"這個短語用於醫療和獸醫情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"talk someone through","meaning":"一邊做一邊向某人解釋","examples":[{"en":"The vet talked Tim through what he was doing.","zh":"獸醫一邊做，一邊向 Tim 解釋自己在做甚麼。"},{"en":"To talk someone through something means to explain each step while it is happening.","zh":"talk someone through something 是指在事情進行時逐步向某人解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may talk students through a maths problem on the board.","zh":"老師可能在黑板上一邊做數學題，一邊向學生解釋。"},{"en":"Talking someone through a process helps beginners understand actions, reasons, and order.","zh":"逐步解釋流程可以幫助初學者理解動作、原因和次序。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone is learning by watching or doing.","zh":"當某人透過觀看或實作學習時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"really useful","meaning":"很有用","examples":[{"en":"Tim found the vet’s explanation really useful.","zh":"Tim 覺得獸醫的解釋很有用。"},{"en":"Really useful means very helpful in a practical way.","zh":"really useful 是指非常有實際幫助。"},{"en":"A clear checklist is really useful before a school trip.","zh":"學校旅行前，一份清楚清單很有用。"},{"en":"Information becomes really useful when it helps someone avoid mistakes or solve a problem.","zh":"當資料能幫助某人避免錯誤或解決問題，它便很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday speech for strong positive feedback.","zh":"這個短語常用於日常口語中表達強烈正面回饋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in a valley","meaning":"在山谷裏","examples":[{"en":"Diana’s farm was in a valley.","zh":"Diana 的農場在山谷裏。"},{"en":"In a valley means located in low land between hills or mountains.","zh":"in a valley 是指位於山丘或山脈之間的低地。"},{"en":"A village in a valley may be surrounded by steep green hills.","zh":"山谷裏的村莊可能被陡峭綠山包圍。"},{"en":"Farms in valleys may have different weather and soil from farms on hills.","zh":"山谷裏的農場可能與山上的農場有不同天氣和土壤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical location of a place.","zh":"這個短語描述一個地方的實際位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lowland breed","meaning":"低地品種","examples":[{"en":"Diana’s farm kept a lowland breed called Suffolks.","zh":"Diana 的農場飼養一種叫 Suffolk 的低地品種。"},{"en":"A lowland breed is a type of animal suited to flatter, lower land rather than hills.","zh":"lowland breed 是適合較平坦、較低土地，而不是山地的動物品種。"},{"en":"Some sheep breeds do better on lowland farms where fields are richer and less steep.","zh":"有些羊品種在田地較肥沃、坡度較小的低地農場表現較好。"},{"en":"The breed chosen affects feeding, health, and farming methods.","zh":"所選品種會影響餵飼、健康和農場管理方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the animal type and the environment it suits.","zh":"這個短語同時描述動物類型和適合的環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"過去","examples":[{"en":"The farmer had kept other sheep breeds in the past.","zh":"那位農夫過去曾飼養其他羊品種。"},{"en":"In the past means during an earlier time before now.","zh":"in the past 是指現在之前的較早時期。"},{"en":"In the past, many students wrote essays by hand rather than on computers.","zh":"過去，許多學生用手寫文章，而不是用電腦。"},{"en":"Looking at the past helps people understand how habits and choices have changed.","zh":"回顧過去有助人們理解習慣和選擇如何改變。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts earlier experience with the present situation.","zh":"這個短語把較早經驗與目前情況作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be bred for","meaning":"為……而飼養","examples":[{"en":"The sheep were mostly bred for their meat.","zh":"這些羊主要為了取肉而飼養。"},{"en":"To be bred for something means to be raised or developed for a particular purpose.","zh":"be bred for something 是指為某個特定目的而飼養或培育。"},{"en":"Some dogs are bred for guiding people, while others are bred for guarding homes.","zh":"有些狗為導盲而培育，另一些則為看守家居而培育。"},{"en":"Animals bred for one purpose may have physical features that suit that use.","zh":"為某用途而培育的動物，可能有適合該用途的身體特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a particular breed is kept.","zh":"這個短語解釋某品種為何被飼養。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for their meat","meaning":"為了取肉","examples":[{"en":"Suffolk sheep are mostly bred for their meat.","zh":"Suffolk 羊主要為了取肉而飼養。"},{"en":"For their meat means for the purpose of producing meat for food.","zh":"for their meat 是指為了生產供人食用的肉。"},{"en":"Some cattle are raised for their meat, while others are kept for milk.","zh":"有些牛為了取肉而飼養，另一些則用來產奶。"},{"en":"Animals bred for meat may be selected for size, growth rate, and body shape.","zh":"為取肉而培育的動物可能按體型、生長速度和身體形狀選育。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the farming purpose clearly.","zh":"這個短語清楚說明農業目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"big and solid","meaning":"又大又壯實","examples":[{"en":"The Suffolk sheep were quite big and solid.","zh":"Suffolk 羊相當又大又壯實。"},{"en":"Big and solid means large, strong, and heavy-looking.","zh":"big and solid 是指體型大、結實，看起來有重量。"},{"en":"A big and solid table is useful in a classroom because it does not move easily.","zh":"又大又穩固的桌子在課室很有用，因為它不易移動。"},{"en":"Animals bred for meat are often big and solid because size affects production.","zh":"為取肉而飼養的動物通常又大又壯實，因為體型影響產量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong physical build.","zh":"這個短語描述強壯的身體結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"up in the hills","meaning":"在山上","examples":[{"en":"Tim’s farm was up in the hills.","zh":"Tim 的農場在山上。"},{"en":"Up in the hills means located in a higher hilly area.","zh":"up in the hills 是指位於較高的丘陵地區。"},{"en":"A cottage up in the hills may be peaceful but hard to reach without a car.","zh":"山上的小屋可能很寧靜，但沒有車就難以到達。"},{"en":"Farms in the hills may need animals that can handle rougher land and colder weather.","zh":"山上的農場可能需要能適應崎嶇土地和較冷天氣的動物。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear sense of height and location.","zh":"這個短語清楚表示高度和位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a different breed of","meaning":"不同品種的……","examples":[{"en":"Tim’s farm had a different breed of sheep.","zh":"Tim 的農場有不同品種的羊。"},{"en":"A different breed of animal means another type within the same species.","zh":"a different breed of animal 是指同一物種中的另一個品種。"},{"en":"A farm may keep a different breed of cow if it wants more milk rather than meat.","zh":"如果農場想要更多牛奶而不是牛肉，可能會飼養不同品種的牛。"},{"en":"Different breeds can vary in size, behaviour, health needs, and products.","zh":"不同品種在體型、行為、健康需要和產品方面可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing types of the same animal.","zh":"這個短語適合用來比較同一動物的不同類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Cheviots","meaning":"切維厄特羊","examples":[{"en":"The sheep on Tim’s farm were Cheviots.","zh":"Tim 農場上的羊是切維厄特羊。"},{"en":"Cheviots are a breed of sheep known for living well in hilly areas.","zh":"Cheviots 是一種以適合山地生活聞名的羊品種。"},{"en":"A hill farm may keep Cheviots because they are hardy and suited to rough land.","zh":"山地農場可能飼養切維厄特羊，因為牠們強健並適合崎嶇土地。"},{"en":"The breed affects what the sheep are useful for, such as wool or meat.","zh":"品種會影響羊的用途，例如羊毛或羊肉。"},{"en":"This word names a specific sheep breed.","zh":"這個詞指一種特定羊品種。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be sought after","meaning":"很受歡迎；需求很高","examples":[{"en":"Cheviot wool is really sought after.","zh":"切維厄特羊毛需求很高。"},{"en":"To be sought after means to be wanted by many people because it is valuable or useful.","zh":"be sought after 是指因有價值或有用而被很多人想要。"},{"en":"Experienced nurses are sought after because hospitals need skilled staff.","zh":"有經驗護士很受歡迎，因為醫院需要熟練職員。"},{"en":"A product becomes sought after when it is high quality, rare, or fashionable.","zh":"當產品質素高、罕有或時尚，它便會很受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong demand.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈需求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hardwearing","meaning":"耐用","examples":[{"en":"Cheviot wool is very hardwearing.","zh":"切維厄特羊毛非常耐用。"},{"en":"Hardwearing means strong and able to last a long time even with heavy use.","zh":"hardwearing 是指堅固，而且即使頻繁使用也能用很久。"},{"en":"School shoes need to be hardwearing because children wear them every day.","zh":"校鞋需要耐用，因為孩子每天都穿。"},{"en":"Hardwearing materials are useful for items that face rubbing, pressure, or dirt.","zh":"耐用材料適合用於會承受摩擦、壓力或污垢的物品。"},{"en":"This word is often used for cloth, shoes, bags, and furniture.","zh":"這個詞常用於布料、鞋、袋和家具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be used for","meaning":"被用於……","examples":[{"en":"Cheviot wool is used for carpets.","zh":"切維厄特羊毛被用於製作地氈。"},{"en":"To be used for something means to serve a particular purpose.","zh":"be used for something 是指被用作某個特定目的。"},{"en":"A calculator is used for solving maths problems quickly.","zh":"計算機被用於快速解數學題。"},{"en":"Materials are chosen because they are suitable for the purpose they are used for.","zh":"材料會因適合其用途而被選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase explains function or purpose.","zh":"這個短語解釋功能或目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"carpets","meaning":"地氈","examples":[{"en":"Cheviot wool is used for carpets.","zh":"切維厄特羊毛被用於製作地氈。"},{"en":"Carpets are thick floor coverings made from materials such as wool or synthetic fibres.","zh":"carpets 是由羊毛或合成纖維等材料製成的厚地面覆蓋物。"},{"en":"A hotel may choose hardwearing carpets because many people walk on them every day.","zh":"酒店可能選擇耐用地氈，因為每天很多人踩在上面。"},{"en":"Carpets can make a room warmer, quieter, and more comfortable.","zh":"地氈可以令房間更溫暖、更安靜和更舒適。"},{"en":"This word refers to flooring, not clothing.","zh":"這個詞指地面用品，而不是衣物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the amount of","meaning":"……的數量","examples":[{"en":"Tim was interested in the amount of supplements added to feed.","zh":"Tim 對加入飼料中的補充劑數量感興趣。"},{"en":"The amount of something means how much of it there is.","zh":"the amount of something 是指某物有多少。"},{"en":"A doctor may ask about the amount of sugar a patient drinks each day.","zh":"醫生可能詢問病人每天飲用的糖分數量。"},{"en":"The amount of a substance matters because too little or too much can cause problems.","zh":"某物的數量很重要，因為太少或太多都可能造成問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when quantity is important.","zh":"當數量重要時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"supplements","meaning":"補充劑","examples":[{"en":"Farmers add supplements to animals’ feed.","zh":"農夫把補充劑加入動物飼料。"},{"en":"Supplements are extra nutrients added to a diet to improve health or performance.","zh":"supplements 是加入飲食中以改善健康或表現的額外營養。"},{"en":"Some people take vitamin supplements when their diet lacks certain nutrients.","zh":"有些人在飲食缺乏某些營養時服用維他命補充劑。"},{"en":"Supplements can help, but they should be used only when needed and in the right amount.","zh":"補充劑可以有幫助，但應只在需要時按正確分量使用。"},{"en":"This word refers to additions, not ordinary food itself.","zh":"這個詞指額外添加物，而不是普通食物本身。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"add something to","meaning":"將某物加入……","examples":[{"en":"Farmers add supplements to animals’ feed nowadays.","zh":"現今農夫會將補充劑加入動物飼料。"},{"en":"To add something to something else means to put it into or combine it with another thing.","zh":"add something to something else 是指把某物放入或混入另一物。"},{"en":"A cook may add salt to soup to improve the flavour.","zh":"廚師可能把鹽加入湯中以改善味道。"},{"en":"Adding supplements to feed can change the nutrients animals receive.","zh":"將補充劑加入飼料可以改變動物攝取的營養。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly shows both the added item and the place it is added.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示被加入的東西和加入的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"animals’ feed","meaning":"動物飼料","examples":[{"en":"Supplements are added to animals’ feed.","zh":"補充劑被加入動物飼料。"},{"en":"Animals’ feed is the food given to farm animals or kept animals.","zh":"animals’ feed 是給農場動物或飼養動物吃的食物。"},{"en":"Chickens’ feed may include grain, vitamins, and minerals.","zh":"雞飼料可能包括穀物、維他命和礦物質。"},{"en":"Good feed helps animals grow, stay healthy, and produce milk, eggs, meat, or wool.","zh":"良好飼料幫助動物成長、保持健康，並生產牛奶、蛋、肉或羊毛。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to food for animals, not food for humans.","zh":"這個短語指動物食物，而不是人類食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"nowadays","meaning":"現今","examples":[{"en":"Tim noticed how many supplements are added to feed nowadays.","zh":"Tim 注意到現今有很多補充劑被加入飼料。"},{"en":"Nowadays means at the present time, compared with the past.","zh":"nowadays 是指現今，與過去相比。"},{"en":"Nowadays, many students use tablets instead of paper notebooks.","zh":"現今，許多學生使用平板電腦，而不是紙本筆記簿。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing modern habits or changes.","zh":"這個詞適合用來描述現代習慣或變化。"},{"en":"It often suggests that things were different before.","zh":"它常暗示以前情況不同。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"extra vitamins","meaning":"額外維他命","examples":[{"en":"Even the chickens got extra vitamins in their feed.","zh":"連雞的飼料中也有額外維他命。"},{"en":"Extra vitamins are additional vitamins added beyond what is naturally in the normal diet.","zh":"extra vitamins 是指在正常飲食天然含量之外額外加入的維他命。"},{"en":"A child may need extra vitamins if a doctor finds a deficiency.","zh":"如果醫生發現孩子缺乏某種營養，他可能需要額外維他命。"},{"en":"Extra vitamins can support health, but too much may be unnecessary or harmful.","zh":"額外維他命可以支持健康，但太多可能沒有必要或有害。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to added nutrients, not ordinary food.","zh":"這個短語指額外添加的營養，而不是普通食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"electrolytes","meaning":"電解質","examples":[{"en":"The chickens received extra vitamins and electrolytes.","zh":"雞得到額外維他命和電解質。"},{"en":"Electrolytes are minerals in the body that help with fluid balance, muscles, and nerves.","zh":"electrolytes 是體內幫助水分平衡、肌肉和神經運作的礦物質。"},{"en":"Sports drinks may contain electrolytes to replace minerals lost through sweating.","zh":"運動飲品可能含有電解質，以補充流汗流失的礦物質。"},{"en":"Animals may need electrolytes when they are stressed, hot, or unwell.","zh":"動物在受壓、炎熱或不適時可能需要電解質。"},{"en":"This word is common in health, sport, and animal care contexts.","zh":"這個詞常見於健康、運動和動物護理語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not cheap","meaning":"不便宜","examples":[{"en":"The supplements are useful, but they are not cheap.","zh":"這些補充劑有用，但不便宜。"},{"en":"Not cheap means fairly expensive or costing more than expected.","zh":"not cheap 是指相當昂貴或比預期花費更多。"},{"en":"A good winter coat is not cheap, but it may last for years.","zh":"一件好的冬天外套不便宜，但可能可以穿很多年。"},{"en":"When something is not cheap, people may think carefully before buying it.","zh":"當某物不便宜，人們購買前可能會仔細考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase is softer than saying “very expensive”.","zh":"這個短語比說 very expensive 較柔和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"overpriced for what they are","meaning":"以實際價值來說定價過高","examples":[{"en":"Diana’s farmer said some supplements are overpriced for what they are.","zh":"Diana 的農夫說有些補充劑以實際價值來說定價過高。"},{"en":"Overpriced for what they are means costing more than their real value or quality justifies.","zh":"overpriced for what they are 是指價格高於其實際價值或質素所能合理支持的水平。"},{"en":"A plain sandwich may be overpriced for what it is if it costs as much as a full meal.","zh":"如果一個普通三文治價錢像一頓完整飯那麼高，它就是定價過高。"},{"en":"People feel cheated when basic products are overpriced for what they are.","zh":"當基本產品以實際價值來說定價過高，人們會覺得被騙。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises price by comparing cost with actual value.","zh":"這個短語透過比較價錢與實際價值來批評價格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as a matter of routine","meaning":"作為例行做法","examples":[{"en":"The farmer did not give supplements as a matter of routine.","zh":"農夫不會把給補充劑作為例行做法。"},{"en":"As a matter of routine means as a regular, automatic habit rather than because of a special need.","zh":"as a matter of routine 是指作為定期、自動的習慣，而不是因特殊需要。"},{"en":"A doctor may not give antibiotics as a matter of routine for every cough.","zh":"醫生未必會把抗生素作為每次咳嗽的例行處理。"},{"en":"Avoiding routine use can prevent waste and unnecessary treatment.","zh":"避免例行使用可以防止浪費和不必要治療。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts regular automatic action with careful case-by-case choice.","zh":"這個短語把自動例行行動與逐個情況判斷作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at times when","meaning":"在……的時候","examples":[{"en":"The farmer only gave supplements at times when the chickens needed them.","zh":"農夫只在雞需要補充劑的時候才給牠們。"},{"en":"At times when means during particular occasions or periods when a condition is true.","zh":"at times when 是指在某條件成立的特定時刻或時期。"},{"en":"Students need extra support at times when exams are near.","zh":"學生在考試臨近的時候需要額外支援。"},{"en":"Giving help only at the right times can be more effective than doing it constantly.","zh":"只在合適時候提供幫助，可能比一直提供更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase links an action to a specific situation.","zh":"這個短語把行動與特定情況連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"particularly require","meaning":"特別需要","examples":[{"en":"The chickens received supplements when they seemed to particularly require them.","zh":"當雞似乎特別需要補充劑時，牠們才會得到補充劑。"},{"en":"To particularly require something means to need it especially strongly in a certain situation.","zh":"particularly require something 是指在某情況下尤其需要某物。"},{"en":"A sick child may particularly require rest and clean water.","zh":"生病孩子可能特別需要休息和乾淨食水。"},{"en":"Animals may particularly require supplements during stress, illness, or rapid growth.","zh":"動物在受壓、生病或快速成長時可能特別需要補充劑。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests special need, not ordinary daily use.","zh":"這個短語表示特殊需要，而不是普通日常使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"certain breeds of","meaning":"某些品種的……","examples":[{"en":"Certain breeds of chickens may need more supplements than others.","zh":"某些品種的雞可能比其他品種需要更多補充劑。"},{"en":"Certain breeds of animals means particular types within one species.","zh":"certain breeds of animals 是指同一物種中的某些特定品種。"},{"en":"Certain breeds of dogs need more exercise than small indoor breeds.","zh":"某些品種的狗比小型室內犬需要更多運動。"},{"en":"Different breeds may have different health needs, growth rates, or behaviour.","zh":"不同品種可能有不同健康需要、生長速度或行為。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows a statement to specific types, not all animals.","zh":"這個短語把說法收窄到特定品種，而不是所有動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"need more supplements than","meaning":"比……需要更多補充劑","examples":[{"en":"Some chicken breeds may need more supplements than others.","zh":"有些雞品種可能比其他品種需要更多補充劑。"},{"en":"Need more supplements than means require a larger amount of added nutrients compared with another group.","zh":"need more supplements than 是指與另一組相比，需要較多額外營養。"},{"en":"A growing teenager may need more calcium than an adult who already has a balanced diet.","zh":"成長中的青少年可能比飲食已均衡的成年人需要更多鈣。"},{"en":"Different needs can depend on age, health, breed, or activity level.","zh":"不同需要可能取決於年齡、健康、品種或活動量。"},{"en":"This phrase compares nutritional requirements.","zh":"這個短語比較營養需求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"basically the same","meaning":"基本上相同","examples":[{"en":"The cheap and expensive supplements are basically the same.","zh":"便宜和昂貴的補充劑基本上相同。"},{"en":"Basically the same means almost the same, with no important difference.","zh":"basically the same 是指幾乎一樣，沒有重要差異。"},{"en":"Two notebooks may be basically the same even if one has a prettier cover.","zh":"兩本筆記簿即使其中一本封面較漂亮，也可能基本上相同。"},{"en":"If two products are basically the same, the cheaper one may be better value.","zh":"如果兩件產品基本上相同，較便宜的可能更划算。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when differences look large but matter little.","zh":"當差異看似很大但其實不重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"any other livestock","meaning":"其他牲畜","examples":[{"en":"Tim asks whether Diana’s farm had any other livestock.","zh":"Tim 問 Diana 的農場是否有其他牲畜。"},{"en":"Any other livestock means any additional farm animals besides the ones already mentioned.","zh":"any other livestock 是指除了已提到的動物以外，是否還有其他農場動物。"},{"en":"A visitor may ask if a farm has any other livestock after seeing cows and sheep.","zh":"訪客看到牛和羊後，可能會問農場是否有其他牲畜。"},{"en":"Knowing other livestock helps people understand how varied the farm is.","zh":"知道有沒有其他牲畜，有助人了解農場有多多元。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about extra animal types.","zh":"這個短語詢問額外的動物種類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dairy cows","meaning":"乳牛","examples":[{"en":"Diana’s farm also had dairy cows.","zh":"Diana 的農場也有乳牛。"},{"en":"Dairy cows are cows kept mainly for producing milk.","zh":"dairy cows 是主要用來生產牛奶的牛。"},{"en":"A dairy farm needs equipment for milking, cooling, and storing milk safely.","zh":"乳牛場需要擠奶、冷藏和安全儲存牛奶的設備。"},{"en":"Dairy cows require regular milking and careful health checks.","zh":"乳牛需要定期擠奶和仔細健康檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to cows used for milk production, not meat production.","zh":"這個短語指用於產奶的牛，而不是用於產肉的牛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"embarrassing mistake","meaning":"尷尬錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Diana made an embarrassing mistake in the milk shed.","zh":"Diana 在擠奶棚犯了一個尷尬錯誤。"},{"en":"An embarrassing mistake is an error that makes someone feel ashamed, awkward, or foolish.","zh":"embarrassing mistake 是令人感到羞愧、不自在或愚蠢的錯誤。"},{"en":"A student may make an embarrassing mistake by calling a teacher by the wrong name.","zh":"學生叫錯老師名字，可能會犯一個尷尬錯誤。"},{"en":"Embarrassing mistakes can happen when people are new, nervous, or confused.","zh":"當人們新手、緊張或混亂時，尷尬錯誤可能會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the mistake and the uncomfortable feeling it creates.","zh":"這個短語同時描述錯誤和它造成的不舒服感覺。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"milk shed","meaning":"擠奶棚","examples":[{"en":"Diana was working in the milk shed.","zh":"Diana 當時在擠奶棚工作。"},{"en":"A milk shed is a farm building or area where cows are milked and milk is handled.","zh":"milk shed 是農場中擠奶和處理牛奶的建築或區域。"},{"en":"Workers in a milk shed must keep equipment clean to protect food safety.","zh":"擠奶棚工人必須保持設備清潔，以保障食品安全。"},{"en":"Mistakes in the milk shed can affect a whole batch of milk.","zh":"擠奶棚中的錯誤可能影響整批牛奶。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a practical farming workspace.","zh":"這個短語指實際農場工作空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be treated with antibiotics","meaning":"接受抗生素治療","examples":[{"en":"Some cows had been treated with antibiotics.","zh":"有些牛接受過抗生素治療。"},{"en":"To be treated with antibiotics means to receive medicine that fights bacterial infection.","zh":"be treated with antibiotics 是指接受對抗細菌感染的藥物治療。"},{"en":"A cow may be treated with antibiotics if it has a serious infection.","zh":"如果牛有嚴重感染，可能會接受抗生素治療。"},{"en":"Milk from treated animals may need to be kept separate for safety reasons.","zh":"來自接受治療動物的牛奶可能基於安全原因需要分開處理。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in medical and veterinary care.","zh":"這個短語用於醫療和獸醫護理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"antibiotics","meaning":"抗生素","examples":[{"en":"Milk from cows treated with antibiotics was not suitable for human consumption.","zh":"來自接受抗生素治療的牛的牛奶不適合人類飲用。"},{"en":"Antibiotics are medicines used to treat bacterial infections.","zh":"antibiotics 是用來治療細菌感染的藥物。"},{"en":"A doctor may prescribe antibiotics for some infections, but not for ordinary colds.","zh":"醫生可能為某些感染處方抗生素，但不會用於普通感冒。"},{"en":"Food from animals treated with antibiotics may need safety checks before humans consume it.","zh":"來自接受抗生素治療動物的食品，可能需要安全檢查才可供人食用。"},{"en":"This word refers to a type of medicine, not a vitamin or painkiller.","zh":"這個詞指一類藥物，而不是維他命或止痛藥。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be suitable for","meaning":"適合……","examples":[{"en":"The milk was not suitable for human consumption.","zh":"這些牛奶不適合人類飲用。"},{"en":"To be suitable for something means to be safe, appropriate, or right for that purpose.","zh":"be suitable for something 是指對某目的而言安全、合適或正確。"},{"en":"A film may not be suitable for young children if it contains frightening scenes.","zh":"如果電影有驚嚇場面，可能不適合年幼兒童觀看。"},{"en":"If food is not suitable for eating, it must not be served.","zh":"如果食物不適合食用，就不應供應。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether something fits a use or group.","zh":"這個短語著重某物是否適合某用途或群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"human consumption","meaning":"人類食用；人類飲用","examples":[{"en":"The milk was not suitable for human consumption.","zh":"這些牛奶不適合人類飲用。"},{"en":"Human consumption means eating or drinking by people.","zh":"human consumption 是指由人類食用或飲用。"},{"en":"Food sold in supermarkets must be safe for human consumption.","zh":"超級市場出售的食品必須適合人類食用。"},{"en":"Products not intended for human consumption may still be safe for animals or other uses.","zh":"不供人類食用的產品，仍可能適合動物或其他用途。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in food safety contexts.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常見於食品安全語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"separate container","meaning":"單獨容器","examples":[{"en":"The milk had to be put in a separate container.","zh":"這些牛奶必須放進單獨容器。"},{"en":"A separate container is a different box, bottle, or tank used to keep something apart.","zh":"separate container 是用來把某物分開存放的另一個盒、瓶或桶。"},{"en":"In a kitchen, raw meat should be kept in a separate container from cooked food.","zh":"在廚房中，生肉應與熟食分別放在單獨容器中。"},{"en":"Separate containers prevent mixing and reduce safety risks.","zh":"單獨容器可防止混合並減少安全風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when different items must not be combined.","zh":"當不同物品不能混在一起時，這個短語很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get mixed up","meaning":"弄混","examples":[{"en":"Diana got mixed up and poured the wrong milk into the container.","zh":"Diana 弄混了，把錯誤的牛奶倒進容器。"},{"en":"To get mixed up means to become confused and mistake one thing for another.","zh":"get mixed up 是指變得混亂，把一物誤認為另一物。"},{"en":"A student may get mixed up and bring the wrong textbook to class.","zh":"學生可能弄混，帶錯課本上課。"},{"en":"Getting mixed up can cause bigger problems when similar items must be kept separate.","zh":"當相似物品必須分開時，弄混可能造成更大問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes confusion that leads to an error.","zh":"這個短語描述導致錯誤的混亂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pour something in with","meaning":"將某物倒進……混在一起","examples":[{"en":"Diana poured some milk from the wrong cow in with the milk for humans.","zh":"Diana 把來自錯誤牛隻的牛奶倒進供人飲用的牛奶中。"},{"en":"To pour something in with something else means to add liquid to another liquid or mixture.","zh":"pour something in with something else 是指把液體倒入另一液體或混合物中。"},{"en":"A child may pour orange juice in with milk by mistake.","zh":"孩子可能誤把橙汁倒進牛奶裏。"},{"en":"Pouring the wrong liquid in with another can contaminate the whole container.","zh":"把錯誤液體倒進另一物中，可能污染整個容器。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two things become mixed together.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩種東西被混在一起。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the wrong cow","meaning":"錯誤的牛","examples":[{"en":"Diana used milk from the wrong cow.","zh":"Diana 使用了來自錯誤牛隻的牛奶。"},{"en":"The wrong cow means not the correct cow for that particular purpose.","zh":"the wrong cow 是指對該目的而言不是正確的那隻牛。"},{"en":"A farmer may milk the wrong cow if the animals are not clearly marked.","zh":"如果動物沒有清楚標記，農夫可能擠錯牛的奶。"},{"en":"Using milk from the wrong cow can be serious if that cow has been treated with medicine.","zh":"如果那隻牛接受過藥物治療，用錯牛奶可能很嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a selection mistake was made.","zh":"這個短語顯示選擇上出了錯。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the whole lot","meaning":"整批；全部","examples":[{"en":"The whole lot of milk had to be thrown away.","zh":"整批牛奶都必須丟掉。"},{"en":"The whole lot means all of it, without leaving any part.","zh":"the whole lot 是指全部，一點也不剩。"},{"en":"If one egg breaks in a bag and ruins everything, the whole lot may need cleaning.","zh":"如果袋中一隻蛋破了並弄髒所有東西，整批都可能需要清潔。"},{"en":"One mistake can sometimes affect the whole lot, not just a small part.","zh":"一個錯誤有時會影響全部，而不只是小部分。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the complete quantity.","zh":"這個短語強調完整數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be thrown away","meaning":"被丟掉","examples":[{"en":"The contaminated milk had to be thrown away.","zh":"受污染的牛奶必須被丟掉。"},{"en":"To be thrown away means to be discarded because it is unwanted, unsafe, or unusable.","zh":"be thrown away 是指因不需要、不安全或不能使用而被棄掉。"},{"en":"Food past its expiry date may have to be thrown away.","zh":"過了食用日期的食物可能必須被丟掉。"},{"en":"Throwing away contaminated products protects people from illness.","zh":"丟掉受污染產品可以保護人們免於生病。"},{"en":"This passive phrase focuses on what happens to the item, not who discards it.","zh":"這個被動短語著重物品發生甚麼事，而不是誰丟掉它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not too happy with","meaning":"對……不太高興","examples":[{"en":"The farmer was not too happy with Diana.","zh":"農夫對 Diana 不太高興。"},{"en":"Not too happy with someone means displeased or annoyed with that person, but said mildly.","zh":"not too happy with someone 是指對某人不滿或生氣，但語氣較溫和。"},{"en":"A teacher may be not too happy with a student who forgets homework again.","zh":"如果學生又忘記交功課，老師可能對他不太高興。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to show disapproval without sounding extremely angry.","zh":"人們用這個短語表達不滿，但不想聽起來非常憤怒。"},{"en":"It is softer than saying “furious with”.","zh":"它比 furious with 更柔和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"依賴","examples":[{"en":"Tim asked how much the farmer depended on the vet.","zh":"Tim 問農夫有多依賴獸醫。"},{"en":"To depend on someone means to need their help, support, or skill.","zh":"depend on someone 是指需要某人的幫助、支持或技術。"},{"en":"A small business may depend on regular customers to survive.","zh":"小企業可能依賴固定顧客來生存。"},{"en":"Farmers depend on vets when animal health problems are too serious to handle alone.","zh":"當動物健康問題太嚴重，農夫會依賴獸醫。"},{"en":"This phrase shows reliance.","zh":"這個短語表示倚賴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"deal with health problems","meaning":"處理健康問題","examples":[{"en":"The vet helps deal with animal health problems.","zh":"獸醫幫忙處理動物健康問題。"},{"en":"To deal with health problems means to handle, treat, or manage illness or injury.","zh":"deal with health problems 是指處理、治療或管理疾病或受傷。"},{"en":"A school nurse helps deal with minor health problems during the school day.","zh":"校護在上課日幫忙處理輕微健康問題。"},{"en":"Dealing with health problems early can prevent them from becoming more serious.","zh":"及早處理健康問題可以防止它們變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical action to manage health issues.","zh":"這個短語著重管理健康問題的實際行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"livestock’s health","meaning":"牲畜健康","examples":[{"en":"Reports say livestock’s health is being affected by pressure to increase production.","zh":"報告指牲畜健康正受增加產量的壓力影響。"},{"en":"Livestock’s health means the physical condition and wellbeing of farm animals.","zh":"livestock’s health 是指農場動物的身體狀況和福祉。"},{"en":"A farmer checks livestock’s health by watching appetite, movement, and behaviour.","zh":"農夫透過觀察食慾、活動和行為來檢查牲畜健康。"},{"en":"Poor housing or overwork can damage livestock’s health.","zh":"惡劣住所或過度勞動可以損害牲畜健康。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the welfare of farm animals.","zh":"這個短語著重農場動物的福祉。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be affected","meaning":"受到影響","examples":[{"en":"Livestock’s health may be affected by farming pressure.","zh":"牲畜健康可能受到農業壓力影響。"},{"en":"To be affected means to be changed or influenced by something.","zh":"be affected 是指被某事改變或影響。"},{"en":"Students’ concentration can be affected by lack of sleep.","zh":"學生專注力可能受到睡眠不足影響。"},{"en":"When health is affected, performance, mood, or safety may also change.","zh":"當健康受到影響，表現、情緒或安全也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase does not always say whether the effect is small or large.","zh":"這個短語不一定說明影響是大還是小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"under pressure to","meaning":"承受壓力去……","examples":[{"en":"Farmers are under pressure to increase production.","zh":"農夫承受增加產量的壓力。"},{"en":"To be under pressure to do something means to feel forced or strongly expected to do it.","zh":"be under pressure to do something 是指感到被迫或被強烈期望做某事。"},{"en":"Students may be under pressure to get high exam marks.","zh":"學生可能承受取得高分的壓力。"},{"en":"Pressure can lead people to make decisions that are efficient but not always healthy.","zh":"壓力可能令人在效率與健康之間作出不理想決定。"},{"en":"This phrase links stress with an expected action.","zh":"這個短語把壓力與被期望的行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"increase production","meaning":"增加產量","examples":[{"en":"Farmers are under pressure to increase production.","zh":"農夫承受增加產量的壓力。"},{"en":"To increase production means to make or produce more of something.","zh":"increase production 是指製造或生產更多某物。"},{"en":"A factory may increase production before a major holiday season.","zh":"工廠可能在大型節日前增加產量。"},{"en":"Increasing production can raise income, but it may also create pressure on workers or animals.","zh":"增加產量可以提高收入，但也可能為工人或動物帶來壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in farming, business, and manufacturing.","zh":"這個短語常見於農業、商業和製造業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"agree with","meaning":"同意","examples":[{"en":"Tim’s farmer did not agree with the reports.","zh":"Tim 的農夫不同意那些報告。"},{"en":"To agree with something means to think it is correct or true.","zh":"agree with something 是指認為某事正確或真實。"},{"en":"A student may agree with a teacher’s advice after seeing her exam results improve.","zh":"學生成績進步後，可能會同意老師的建議。"},{"en":"People may not agree with a report if their own experience is different.","zh":"如果自己的經驗不同，人們可能不同意某份報告。"},{"en":"This phrase shows acceptance of an idea, opinion, or statement.","zh":"這個短語表示接受某個想法、意見或說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"some of the stuff","meaning":"其中一些事情","examples":[{"en":"The farmer said he could do some of the stuff vets do.","zh":"農夫說他可以做獸醫做的其中一些事情。"},{"en":"Some of the stuff means some of the tasks, things, or work, said informally.","zh":"some of the stuff 是指部分任務、事情或工作，語氣較口語。"},{"en":"A receptionist may do some of the stuff a manager usually handles when the office is busy.","zh":"辦公室忙碌時，接待員可能會做經理平常處理的其中一些事情。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds casual and is not suitable for very formal writing.","zh":"這個短語較口語，不適合很正式的寫作。"},{"en":"It is useful in conversation when the exact list is not important.","zh":"當確切清單不重要時，它在對話中很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"minor operations","meaning":"小型手術","examples":[{"en":"The farmer felt capable of doing minor operations himself.","zh":"農夫覺得自己有能力做小型手術。"},{"en":"Minor operations are small medical or surgical procedures that are not very complex.","zh":"minor operations 是不太複雜的小型醫療或外科程序。"},{"en":"A vet may perform minor operations to clean a wound or remove a small object.","zh":"獸醫可能進行小型手術來清潔傷口或移除小物件。"},{"en":"Even minor operations need skill because mistakes can cause pain or infection.","zh":"即使是小型手術也需要技術，因為錯誤可能造成痛楚或感染。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts small procedures with major surgery.","zh":"這個短語把小程序與大型手術作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be capable of doing","meaning":"有能力做……","examples":[{"en":"The farmer said he was capable of doing some minor operations himself.","zh":"農夫說他有能力自己做一些小型手術。"},{"en":"To be capable of doing something means to have the ability or skill to do it.","zh":"be capable of doing something 是指有能力或技能做某事。"},{"en":"A trained student may be capable of repairing a simple computer problem.","zh":"受過訓練的學生可能有能力修理簡單電腦問題。"},{"en":"Being capable does not always mean it is safe or wise to do the task alone.","zh":"有能力做某事不一定代表獨自去做是安全或明智的。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on ability.","zh":"這個短語著重能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reckon","meaning":"認為","examples":[{"en":"Diana’s farmer reckons vets’ skills are still needed.","zh":"Diana 的農夫認為獸醫的技術仍然需要。"},{"en":"To reckon means to think or believe something, especially in informal speech.","zh":"reckon 是指認為或相信某事，尤其用於非正式說話。"},{"en":"I reckon the bus will be late because the road is very busy.","zh":"我認為巴士會遲到，因為道路很繁忙。"},{"en":"People use reckon when giving a personal opinion rather than a proven fact.","zh":"人們給出個人意見而不是已證實事實時，會用 reckon。"},{"en":"This word is common in British conversational English.","zh":"這個詞常見於英式口語英文。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"vets’ skills","meaning":"獸醫的技術","examples":[{"en":"Vets’ skills are still needed on farms.","zh":"農場仍然需要獸醫的技術。"},{"en":"Vets’ skills are the professional abilities veterinarians use to diagnose and treat animals.","zh":"vets’ skills 是獸醫用來診斷和治療動物的專業能力。"},{"en":"Vets’ skills include examining animals, giving medicine, and performing operations.","zh":"獸醫的技術包括檢查動物、用藥和做手術。"},{"en":"Farmers may know their animals well, but vets’ skills are needed for serious conditions.","zh":"農夫可能很了解自己的動物，但嚴重情況仍需要獸醫技術。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises professional animal health expertise.","zh":"這個短語強調專業動物健康知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be still needed","meaning":"仍然需要","examples":[{"en":"Diana’s farmer says vets’ skills are still needed.","zh":"Diana 的農夫說獸醫的技術仍然需要。"},{"en":"To be still needed means to continue being necessary.","zh":"be still needed 是指繼續有必要。"},{"en":"Even with online maps, local guides are still needed in remote mountain areas.","zh":"即使有網上地圖，偏遠山區仍然需要本地嚮導。"},{"en":"Something may still be needed when technology or experience cannot replace it completely.","zh":"當科技或經驗不能完全取代某物，它可能仍然需要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a need has not disappeared.","zh":"這個短語顯示某種需要並未消失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"give feedback about","meaning":"就……給予意見","examples":[{"en":"The students have to give feedback about last term’s modules.","zh":"學生必須就上學期的課程單元給予意見。"},{"en":"To give feedback about something means to share comments on what was good, bad, or useful.","zh":"give feedback about something 是指分享某事好、不好或有用之處的意見。"},{"en":"Students may give feedback about a new lunch menu after trying it for a week.","zh":"學生試用新午餐餐牌一星期後，可能會給予意見。"},{"en":"Feedback helps teachers or organisers improve future lessons or services.","zh":"回饋幫助老師或組織者改善未來課堂或服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in education, training, and workplaces.","zh":"這個短語常見於教育、培訓和職場。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"last term’s modules","meaning":"上學期的課程單元","examples":[{"en":"Diana and Tim discuss last term’s modules.","zh":"Diana 和 Tim 討論上學期的課程單元。"},{"en":"Last term’s modules are the course units studied during the previous school or university term.","zh":"last term’s modules 是指上一個學期修讀的課程單元。"},{"en":"A student may review last term’s modules before choosing new ones.","zh":"學生選新單元前，可能會回顧上學期的課程單元。"},{"en":"Discussing earlier modules helps teachers know what students found useful or difficult.","zh":"討論較早的單元有助老師了解學生覺得甚麼有用或困難。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to parts of a course from the previous term.","zh":"這個短語指上一學期課程中的部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"short comments","meaning":"簡短評語","examples":[{"en":"The feedback only requires short comments.","zh":"回饋只需要簡短評語。"},{"en":"Short comments are brief opinions or remarks, usually only one or two sentences.","zh":"short comments 是簡短意見或評論，通常只有一兩句。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask for short comments after a school trip.","zh":"學校旅行後，老師可能要求學生寫簡短評語。"},{"en":"Short comments save time but still show what people think.","zh":"簡短評語節省時間，但仍能顯示人們的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with long reports or detailed essays.","zh":"這個短語與長篇報告或詳細文章作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"apparently","meaning":"看來；顯然","examples":[{"en":"Apparently, the feedback only needs short comments.","zh":"看來，回饋只需要簡短評語。"},{"en":"Apparently means according to what someone has heard, read, or been told.","zh":"apparently 是指根據某人聽到、讀到或被告知的資料。"},{"en":"Apparently, the library will close early today because of maintenance.","zh":"看來，圖書館今天會因維修提早關門。"},{"en":"People use apparently when they believe information is true but did not see it directly.","zh":"當人們相信資料真實，但並非親眼看見時，會用 apparently。"},{"en":"This word can make a statement sound slightly uncertain or based on reported information.","zh":"這個詞可以令說法聽起來略帶不確定，或基於轉述資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"medical terminology","meaning":"醫學術語","examples":[{"en":"The students discuss the medical terminology module.","zh":"學生討論醫學術語課程單元。"},{"en":"Medical terminology means the special words and phrases used in medicine and healthcare.","zh":"medical terminology 是醫學和醫療保健中使用的專門詞語和短語。"},{"en":"Nurses need medical terminology to understand patient notes and doctor instructions.","zh":"護士需要醫學術語來理解病人紀錄和醫生指示。"},{"en":"Learning medical terminology can be difficult because many terms come from Latin or Greek.","zh":"學習醫學術語可能困難，因為許多詞來自拉丁語或希臘語。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to professional medical vocabulary.","zh":"這個短語指專業醫學詞彙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"my heart sank","meaning":"我的心沉了下去","examples":[{"en":"Diana’s heart sank when she saw medical terminology on the course.","zh":"Diana 看到課程中有醫學術語時，心沉了下去。"},{"en":"My heart sank means I suddenly felt disappointed, worried, or discouraged.","zh":"my heart sank 是指我突然感到失望、擔心或灰心。"},{"en":"A student’s heart may sink when she sees a difficult question on the exam paper.","zh":"學生看到試卷上有難題時，心可能會沉下去。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when hope or confidence drops suddenly.","zh":"當希望或信心突然下降時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It describes an emotional reaction, not a physical heart problem.","zh":"它描述情緒反應，而不是心臟實際問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"right at the beginning of","meaning":"就在……一開始","examples":[{"en":"The medical terminology module came right at the beginning of the course.","zh":"醫學術語單元就在課程一開始出現。"},{"en":"Right at the beginning of means exactly at the start of something.","zh":"right at the beginning of 是指正正在某事開始時。"},{"en":"The teacher explained the rules right at the beginning of the lesson.","zh":"老師就在課堂一開始解釋規則。"},{"en":"Something placed at the beginning can strongly affect first impressions.","zh":"放在開頭的東西可以強烈影響第一印象。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises early timing.","zh":"這個短語強調很早的時間點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"struggle with","meaning":"對……感到吃力","examples":[{"en":"Diana struggled with medical terminology.","zh":"Diana 對醫學術語感到吃力。"},{"en":"To struggle with something means to find it difficult to understand, do, or manage.","zh":"struggle with something 是指覺得某事難以理解、完成或處理。"},{"en":"A student may struggle with grammar if the rules feel confusing.","zh":"如果文法規則令人混亂，學生可能會對文法感到吃力。"},{"en":"People often struggle with new topics before they build enough practice and confidence.","zh":"人們在有足夠練習和信心前，常會對新題目感到吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows difficulty, not complete failure.","zh":"這個短語表示困難，而不是完全失敗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"find something straightforward","meaning":"覺得某事頗簡單","examples":[{"en":"Tim found medical terminology quite straightforward.","zh":"Tim 覺得醫學術語頗簡單。"},{"en":"To find something straightforward means to think it is clear and not difficult.","zh":"find something straightforward 是指覺得某事清楚而不難。"},{"en":"A student may find fractions straightforward after a teacher explains them with pizzas.","zh":"老師用薄餅解釋分數後，學生可能覺得分數頗簡單。"},{"en":"Something feels straightforward when the steps or meanings are easy to follow.","zh":"當步驟或意思容易跟上，某事會感覺簡單直接。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the learner’s opinion of difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述學習者對難度的看法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"diet and nutrition","meaning":"飲食與營養","examples":[{"en":"The students discuss the diet and nutrition module.","zh":"學生討論飲食與營養課程單元。"},{"en":"Diet and nutrition means what people or animals eat and how that food affects health.","zh":"diet and nutrition 是指人或動物吃甚麼，以及食物如何影響健康。"},{"en":"A school lesson on diet and nutrition may compare fresh food with sugary snacks.","zh":"關於飲食與營養的學校課堂可能比較新鮮食物和含糖零食。"},{"en":"Understanding diet and nutrition helps people make healthier choices.","zh":"了解飲食與營養幫助人作出更健康選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase connects eating habits with body needs.","zh":"這個短語把飲食習慣與身體需要連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pet food","meaning":"寵物食品","examples":[{"en":"The module included information about pet food.","zh":"這個單元包括關於寵物食品的資料。"},{"en":"Pet food is food made for animals kept as pets, such as dogs, cats, or rabbits.","zh":"pet food 是為狗、貓或兔等寵物製造的食物。"},{"en":"Pet food labels may show ingredients, nutrients, and feeding amounts.","zh":"寵物食品標籤可能顯示成分、營養和餵飼分量。"},{"en":"Good pet food supports growth, energy, and long-term animal health.","zh":"良好寵物食品支持成長、能量和動物長遠健康。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to food for companion animals, not farm animals.","zh":"這個短語指伴侶動物的食物，而不是農場動物飼料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"limited checking into","meaning":"對……的檢查有限","examples":[{"en":"There is limited checking into whether pet food is contaminated.","zh":"對寵物食品是否受污染的檢查有限。"},{"en":"Limited checking into something means only a small amount of investigation or testing is done.","zh":"limited checking into something 是指對某事只進行少量調查或測試。"},{"en":"A school may have limited checking into food waste if it has no staff to collect data.","zh":"如果學校沒有人手收集數據，對廚餘的檢查可能有限。"},{"en":"Limited checking can allow problems to go unnoticed.","zh":"檢查有限可能令問題未被發現。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that more careful inspection may be needed.","zh":"這個短語暗示可能需要更仔細檢查。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"whether or not","meaning":"是否","examples":[{"en":"The module discussed whether or not pet food is contaminated.","zh":"這個單元討論寵物食品是否受污染。"},{"en":"Whether or not means if something is true or not true.","zh":"whether or not 是指某事是否真實。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask whether or not students understood the instructions.","zh":"老師可能詢問學生是否明白指示。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when there are two possible answers: yes or no.","zh":"當有兩種可能答案：是或否時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It often introduces a question that needs checking or evidence.","zh":"它常引入需要檢查或證據的問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be contaminated","meaning":"受到污染","examples":[{"en":"Pet food may be contaminated.","zh":"寵物食品可能受到污染。"},{"en":"To be contaminated means to contain harmful or unwanted substances.","zh":"be contaminated 是指含有有害或不應有的物質。"},{"en":"Drinking water can be contaminated if chemicals leak into the supply.","zh":"如果化學物質滲入供水，飲用水可能受到污染。"},{"en":"Contaminated food can make people or animals ill.","zh":"受污染食物可以令人或動物生病。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in health, food safety, and environmental topics.","zh":"這個短語常見於健康、食品安全和環境議題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in comparison with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Checking on pet food is limited in comparison with food for humans.","zh":"與人類食品相比，對寵物食品的檢查有限。"},{"en":"In comparison with means when compared with another thing.","zh":"in comparison with 是指與另一事物比較時。"},{"en":"Public transport may be cheap in comparison with driving and parking every day.","zh":"與每天駕車和泊車相比，公共交通可能很便宜。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show differences in amount, quality, or level.","zh":"這個短語有助顯示數量、質素或程度上的差異。"},{"en":"It is often used in formal explanations and reports.","zh":"它常用於正式解釋和報告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"checks on","meaning":"對……的檢查","examples":[{"en":"The checks on food for humans are stricter than those on pet food.","zh":"對人類食品的檢查比對寵物食品的檢查更嚴格。"},{"en":"Checks on something are inspections or tests used to make sure it is safe or correct.","zh":"checks on something 是用來確保某物安全或正確的檢查或測試。"},{"en":"Airports carry out checks on luggage before passengers board planes.","zh":"機場在乘客登機前對行李進行檢查。"},{"en":"Checks on food protect consumers from contamination and poor quality.","zh":"對食品的檢查保護消費者免受污染和劣質產品影響。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on inspection and control.","zh":"這個短語著重檢驗和控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"food for humans","meaning":"人類食品","examples":[{"en":"Food for humans is checked more strictly than pet food.","zh":"人類食品比寵物食品受到更嚴格檢查。"},{"en":"Food for humans means food intended to be eaten by people.","zh":"food for humans 是指供人食用的食物。"},{"en":"Food for humans must meet safety rules before it can be sold in shops.","zh":"人類食品在商店出售前必須符合安全規則。"},{"en":"Stronger checks are needed because unsafe food for humans can affect public health.","zh":"需要更嚴格檢查，因為不安全的人類食品會影響公共健康。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts human food with animal feed or pet food.","zh":"這個短語把人類食品與動物飼料或寵物食品作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"impress someone","meaning":"令某人留下深刻印象","examples":[{"en":"The animal disease module really impressed Diana.","zh":"動物疾病單元令 Diana 留下深刻印象。"},{"en":"To impress someone means to make them admire or remember something strongly.","zh":"impress someone 是指令某人佩服或深深記住某事。"},{"en":"A clear science demonstration can impress students by making a difficult idea easy to see.","zh":"清楚的科學示範可以令學生留下深刻印象，因為它令難懂概念變得可見。"},{"en":"People are impressed when something is interesting, useful, or better than expected.","zh":"當某事有趣、有用或比預期更好，人們會留下深刻印象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong positive effect on someone.","zh":"這個短語描述對某人的強烈正面影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"animal disease","meaning":"動物疾病","examples":[{"en":"Diana was impressed by the animal disease module.","zh":"Diana 對動物疾病單元印象深刻。"},{"en":"Animal disease means illness that affects animals.","zh":"animal disease 是指影響動物的疾病。"},{"en":"Farmers must watch for animal disease because it can spread quickly in herds.","zh":"農夫必須留意動物疾病，因為它可以在畜群中迅速傳播。"},{"en":"Animal disease can affect food supply, farm income, and animal welfare.","zh":"動物疾病可以影響食物供應、農場收入和動物福祉。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in veterinary science and farming.","zh":"這個短語常見於獸醫科學和農業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"domesticated animals","meaning":"家養動物","examples":[{"en":"The students studied domesticated animals in different parts of the world.","zh":"學生研究世界各地的家養動物。"},{"en":"Domesticated animals are animals kept and bred by humans for work, food, transport, or companionship.","zh":"domesticated animals 是由人類飼養和培育，用於工作、食物、交通或陪伴的動物。"},{"en":"Dogs, cows, horses, camels, and chickens are examples of domesticated animals.","zh":"狗、牛、馬、駱駝和雞都是家養動物的例子。"},{"en":"Domesticated animals often depend on humans for food, shelter, and care.","zh":"家養動物常依賴人類提供食物、住所和照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with wild animals.","zh":"這個短語與野生動物相對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"different parts of the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"The module covered animals in different parts of the world.","zh":"這個單元涵蓋世界各地的動物。"},{"en":"Different parts of the world means various countries, regions, or continents.","zh":"different parts of the world 是指不同國家、地區或大洲。"},{"en":"Students may study festivals in different parts of the world to compare cultures.","zh":"學生可能研究世界各地的節日，以比較文化。"},{"en":"Animals in different regions may face different climates, diseases, and farming needs.","zh":"不同地區的動物可能面對不同氣候、疾病和農業需要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows wide geographical variety.","zh":"這個短語顯示廣泛的地理多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"camels","meaning":"駱駝","examples":[{"en":"The module included domesticated animals such as camels.","zh":"這個單元包括駱駝等家養動物。"},{"en":"Camels are large animals often used for transport, milk, and meat in dry regions.","zh":"camels 是大型動物，在乾旱地區常用於交通、產奶和取肉。"},{"en":"People in desert areas may depend on camels because they can travel long distances with little water.","zh":"沙漠地區的人可能依賴駱駝，因為牠們可以少水長途行走。"},{"en":"Camels are important where other livestock struggle with heat and dryness.","zh":"在其他牲畜難以應付炎熱和乾旱的地方，駱駝很重要。"},{"en":"This word refers to a domesticated animal strongly linked with desert environments.","zh":"這個詞指一種與沙漠環境密切相關的家養動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"water buffalo","meaning":"水牛","examples":[{"en":"The module included water buffalo.","zh":"這個單元包括水牛。"},{"en":"Water buffalo are large domesticated animals often used for farming work, milk, and meat.","zh":"water buffalo 是大型家養動物，常用於農務、產奶和取肉。"},{"en":"In some countries, water buffalo help farmers plough wet rice fields.","zh":"在一些國家，水牛幫助農夫犁水稻田。"},{"en":"Water buffalo are valuable because they can work in muddy, wet conditions.","zh":"水牛很有價值，因為牠們能在泥濘濕地中工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a farm animal important in many Asian regions.","zh":"這個短語指在許多亞洲地區很重要的農場動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"alpaca","meaning":"羊駝","examples":[{"en":"The module included alpacas.","zh":"這個單元包括羊駝。"},{"en":"An alpaca is a domesticated South American animal kept mainly for its soft wool-like fibre.","zh":"alpaca 是南美洲家養動物，主要為其柔軟、像羊毛的纖維而飼養。"},{"en":"Farmers may keep alpacas for fibre, breeding, or farm tourism.","zh":"農夫可能為纖維、繁殖或農場旅遊而飼養羊駝。"},{"en":"Alpaca fibre is valued because it can be soft, warm, and light.","zh":"羊駝纖維受重視，因為它可以柔軟、保暖和輕身。"},{"en":"This word refers to an animal related to llamas.","zh":"這個詞指與美洲駝有親緣關係的動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"depend on these","meaning":"依賴這些","examples":[{"en":"The economies of many countries depend on these animals.","zh":"許多國家的經濟依賴這些動物。"},{"en":"Depend on these means rely on these things for support, income, or survival.","zh":"depend on these 是指依靠這些東西來獲得支持、收入或生存。"},{"en":"Some villages depend on these animals for transport, milk, wool, and farm work.","zh":"有些村莊依賴這些動物提供交通、牛奶、羊毛和農務勞動。"},{"en":"If communities depend on certain animals, disease can damage both livelihoods and food supply.","zh":"如果社區依賴某些動物，疾病可以損害生計和食物供應。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong reliance on the things just mentioned.","zh":"這個短語顯示對剛提到事物的強烈依賴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"affect them","meaning":"影響牠們","examples":[{"en":"Scientists know little about the diseases that affect these animals.","zh":"科學家對影響這些動物的疾病了解不多。"},{"en":"To affect them means to influence, harm, or change those animals.","zh":"affect them 是指影響、傷害或改變那些動物。"},{"en":"Heat can affect animals by reducing appetite and energy.","zh":"炎熱可以影響動物，令牠們食慾和精力下降。"},{"en":"Diseases that affect farm animals can also affect farmers’ income.","zh":"影響農場動物的疾病也可以影響農夫收入。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with its impact on the animals mentioned.","zh":"這個短語把原因與對所提動物的影響連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ways of controlling","meaning":"控制……的方法","examples":[{"en":"Tim expected scientists to know ways of controlling animal diseases.","zh":"Tim 以為科學家會知道控制動物疾病的方法。"},{"en":"Ways of controlling something are methods used to limit, manage, or stop it.","zh":"ways of controlling something 是指限制、管理或阻止某事的方法。"},{"en":"Schools use ways of controlling infection, such as handwashing and staying home when ill.","zh":"學校使用控制感染的方法，例如洗手和生病時留在家中。"},{"en":"Finding ways of controlling disease can protect animals and the people who depend on them.","zh":"找到控制疾病的方法可以保護動物，以及依賴牠們的人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical methods for managing a problem.","zh":"這個短語著重管理問題的實際方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"eradicating diseases","meaning":"根除疾病","examples":[{"en":"Scientists know less than expected about eradicating these diseases.","zh":"科學家對根除這些疾病的了解比預期少。"},{"en":"Eradicating diseases means removing diseases completely so they no longer exist in a population.","zh":"eradicating diseases 是指完全消除疾病，使它們不再存在於某群體中。"},{"en":"Vaccination programmes can help eradicate a disease if enough people are protected.","zh":"如果足夠多人受到保護，疫苗計劃可以幫助根除疾病。"},{"en":"Eradicating disease is difficult because infection can spread, return, or hide in animals.","zh":"根除疾病很困難，因為感染可以傳播、回來或藏在動物中。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply controlling a disease.","zh":"這個短語比單純控制疾病更強。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"that is not the case","meaning":"事實並非如此","examples":[{"en":"Tim realised that his assumption was not the case at all.","zh":"Tim 意識到他的假設完全並非如此。"},{"en":"That is not the case means that what someone believed or expected is not true.","zh":"that is not the case 是指某人相信或預期的事情並不是真的。"},{"en":"Many people think all farms use the same methods, but that is not the case.","zh":"許多人以為所有農場都使用相同方法，但事實並非如此。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects a wrong idea or assumption.","zh":"這個短語用來修正錯誤想法或假設。"},{"en":"It is useful when reality is different from what people imagine.","zh":"當現實與人們想像不同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at all","meaning":"完全","examples":[{"en":"Scientists do not know as much as Tim expected at all.","zh":"科學家完全沒有 Tim 預期中知道得那麼多。"},{"en":"At all is used for emphasis, often in negative sentences.","zh":"at all 用於強調，常見於否定句。"},{"en":"The instructions were not clear at all, so many students made mistakes.","zh":"指示完全不清楚，所以很多學生犯錯。"},{"en":"Adding “at all” makes the negative meaning stronger.","zh":"加上 at all 會令否定意思更強。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows surprise, disappointment, or strong disagreement.","zh":"這個短語常表示驚訝、失望或強烈不同意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"wildlife medication unit","meaning":"野生動物醫療單元","examples":[{"en":"Tim loved the wildlife medication unit.","zh":"Tim 很喜歡野生動物醫療單元。"},{"en":"A wildlife medication unit is a course section about treating or caring for wild animals medically.","zh":"wildlife medication unit 是關於用醫療方式治療或照顧野生動物的課程部分。"},{"en":"Students may learn in a wildlife medication unit how to help injured birds or mammals.","zh":"學生可能在野生動物醫療單元學習如何幫助受傷雀鳥或哺乳動物。"},{"en":"This unit matters because wild animals often need different care from pets or livestock.","zh":"這個單元重要，因為野生動物常需要與寵物或牲畜不同的護理。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a learning module, not a hospital department here.","zh":"這裏的短語指學習單元，而不是醫院部門。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be caught in oil spills","meaning":"被困於漏油事故中","examples":[{"en":"The unit discussed birds that had been caught in oil spills.","zh":"這個單元討論被困於漏油事故中的雀鳥。"},{"en":"To be caught in oil spills means to become trapped, covered, or affected by leaked oil.","zh":"be caught in oil spills 是指被洩漏的石油困住、覆蓋或影響。"},{"en":"Seabirds can be caught in oil spills when oil spreads across the surface of the sea.","zh":"當石油在海面擴散，海鳥可能被困於漏油事故中。"},{"en":"Birds caught in oil may lose waterproofing and struggle to fly or stay warm.","zh":"沾上石油的鳥可能失去防水能力，難以飛行或保持溫暖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wildlife being harmed by environmental accidents.","zh":"這個短語描述野生動物被環境事故傷害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"oil spills","meaning":"漏油事故","examples":[{"en":"Wildlife medication may involve helping birds affected by oil spills.","zh":"野生動物醫療可能包括幫助受漏油事故影響的雀鳥。"},{"en":"Oil spills are accidents where oil leaks into the sea, rivers, or land.","zh":"oil spills 是石油洩漏到海洋、河流或土地上的事故。"},{"en":"An oil spill near the coast can harm fish, birds, beaches, and local businesses.","zh":"海岸附近的漏油事故可以傷害魚類、雀鳥、海灘和本地商業。"},{"en":"Cleaning oil spills is difficult because oil spreads and sticks to animals and surfaces.","zh":"清理漏油事故很困難，因為石油會擴散並黏在動物和表面上。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in environmental and wildlife protection topics.","zh":"這個短語常見於環境和野生動物保護議題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"something I had not thought about before","meaning":"我以前沒有想過的事","examples":[{"en":"Helping birds after oil spills was something Tim had not thought about before.","zh":"漏油事故後幫助雀鳥，是 Tim 以前沒有想過的事。"},{"en":"Something I had not thought about before means an idea or issue that had never entered my mind earlier.","zh":"something I had not thought about before 是指以前從未想到過的想法或議題。"},{"en":"Food waste in school kitchens may be something students had not thought about before.","zh":"學校廚房的廚餘可能是學生以前沒有想過的事。"},{"en":"Learning new topics can reveal problems people never noticed.","zh":"學習新主題可以揭示人們從未注意到的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows surprise and new awareness.","zh":"這個短語顯示驚訝和新的意識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"write my dissertation on","meaning":"以……作為論文題目","examples":[{"en":"Diana might write her dissertation on wildlife medication.","zh":"Diana 可能以野生動物醫療作為論文題目。"},{"en":"To write my dissertation on something means to choose that topic for a long university research project.","zh":"write my dissertation on something 是指選擇某主題作為大學長篇研究論文的題目。"},{"en":"A student may write her dissertation on how diet affects animal health.","zh":"學生可能以飲食如何影響動物健康作為論文題目。"},{"en":"Choosing a dissertation topic matters because it requires months of reading and research.","zh":"選擇論文題目很重要，因為它需要數月閱讀和研究。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in university study.","zh":"這個短語用於大學學習中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"something connected with","meaning":"與……有關的事情","examples":[{"en":"Diana may write her dissertation on something connected with wildlife medication.","zh":"Diana 可能以與野生動物醫療有關的事情作為論文題目。"},{"en":"Something connected with a topic means something related to that topic.","zh":"something connected with a topic 是指與該主題相關的事情。"},{"en":"A student interested in transport may study something connected with bus delays or cycling safety.","zh":"對交通感興趣的學生可能研究與巴士延誤或單車安全有關的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the exact topic is not yet decided.","zh":"當確切題目尚未決定時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It gives a general area while leaving room to choose a more specific focus later.","zh":"它提供一個大方向，同時保留之後選擇更具體焦點的空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 12/task-4":[{"front":"labyrinths","meaning":"單一路徑迷宮；螺旋迷宮","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths have existed for well over 4,000 years.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮已存在遠超過4,000年。"},{"en":"Labyrinths are single-path designs that lead walkers slowly towards a centre.","zh":"labyrinths 指只有一條路徑、引導行走者慢慢走向中心的設計。"},{"en":"A school garden may have a small labyrinth for students to walk through quietly.","zh":"學校花園可能有一個小型單一路徑迷宮，讓學生安靜地行走。"},{"en":"Unlike mazes, traditional labyrinths do not have many wrong paths.","zh":"與多路徑迷宮不同，傳統 labyrinths 沒有許多錯誤路徑。"},{"en":"This word describes an ancient walking pattern, not simply any confusing place.","zh":"這個字描述古老的步行圖案，而不只是任何令人困惑的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"well over","meaning":"遠超過","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths have existed for well over 4,000 years.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮已存在遠超過4,000年。"},{"en":"Well over means much more than a stated number or amount.","zh":"well over 指比某個數字或數量多很多。"},{"en":"The school fair raised well over $10,000 for charity.","zh":"學校賣物會為慈善籌得遠超過10,000元。"},{"en":"If a journey takes well over two hours, it is much longer than expected.","zh":"如果車程需時遠超過兩小時，它就比預期長很多。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the number is clearly above the figure mentioned.","zh":"這個短語強調數字明顯高於所提到的數目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"labyrinthine symbols","meaning":"迷宮式符號","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinthine symbols have been found in many different regions.","zh":"許多不同地區都發現過迷宮式符號。"},{"en":"Labyrinthine symbols are signs or patterns that look like labyrinths, with winding paths or spirals.","zh":"labyrinthine symbols 指看起來像單一路徑迷宮、有蜿蜒路徑或螺旋的符號或圖案。"},{"en":"Ancient carvings may contain labyrinthine symbols on stones or walls.","zh":"古代雕刻可能在石頭或牆上包含迷宮式符號。"},{"en":"These symbols can show that the labyrinth shape had cultural or spiritual meaning.","zh":"這些符號可以顯示迷宮形狀曾有文化或精神意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes maze-like patterns used as signs or designs.","zh":"這個短語描述被用作符號或設計的迷宮狀圖案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be found in","meaning":"在……被發現","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths and labyrinthine symbols have been found in regions across the world.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮和迷宮式符號在世界各地不同地區被發現。"},{"en":"Be found in means exist or be discovered in a particular place.","zh":"be found in 指存在於或被發現在某個特定地方。"},{"en":"Fossils can be found in rocks that were once under the sea.","zh":"化石可以在曾經位於海底的岩石中被發現。"},{"en":"If the same design is found in many places, it may have been important to different cultures.","zh":"如果同一設計在許多地方被發現，它可能對不同文化都很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when describing discoveries and locations.","zh":"這個短語常用於描述發現和位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"regions as diverse as","meaning":"多樣如……的地區","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths have been found in regions as diverse as Turkey, Ireland, Greece, and India.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮在多樣如土耳其、愛爾蘭、希臘和印度的地區被發現。"},{"en":"Regions as diverse as means places that are very different from one another.","zh":"regions as diverse as 指彼此非常不同的地方。"},{"en":"Similar stories appear in regions as diverse as Africa, Europe, and East Asia.","zh":"類似故事出現在多樣如非洲、歐洲和東亞的地區。"},{"en":"If something appears in very diverse regions, it may have wide human appeal.","zh":"如果某物出現在非常多樣的地區，它可能具有廣泛的人類吸引力。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses geographical or cultural variety.","zh":"這個短語強調地理或文化上的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"modern-day","meaning":"現今的……","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths have been found in modern-day Turkey.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮曾在現今的土耳其被發現。"},{"en":"Modern-day means existing now or referring to the present name of a place.","zh":"modern-day 指現今存在的，或指一個地方現在的名稱。"},{"en":"Ancient Troy was located in what is now modern-day Turkey.","zh":"古代特洛伊位於現今的土耳其。"},{"en":"Writers use modern-day names to help readers connect ancient places with current maps.","zh":"作者使用現今地名，幫助讀者把古代地方與現代地圖連起來。"},{"en":"This phrase links history with the present.","zh":"這個短語把歷史與現在連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"various designs of","meaning":"各種……設計","examples":[{"en":"There are various designs of labyrinth.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮有各種設計。"},{"en":"Various designs of something means several different forms or patterns of it.","zh":"various designs of something 指某物的幾種不同形式或圖案。"},{"en":"A museum may show various designs of traditional baskets from different villages.","zh":"博物館可能展示來自不同村莊的各種傳統籃子設計。"},{"en":"Different designs can share one basic idea while looking very different.","zh":"不同設計可以共享同一基本概念，但外觀非常不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one object has several styles.","zh":"當一種物件有幾種風格時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have in common","meaning":"有共同點","examples":[{"en":"All labyrinths have a winding spiral path in common.","zh":"所有單一路徑迷宮都有蜿蜒螺旋路徑這個共同點。"},{"en":"Have something in common means share the same feature or quality.","zh":"have something in common 指共享同一特徵或品質。"},{"en":"Good teachers often have patience and clear communication in common.","zh":"好老師通常有耐性和清晰溝通這些共同點。"},{"en":"When objects have a feature in common, we can group them together.","zh":"當物件有共同特徵，我們就可以把它們歸為一類。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare different things by showing similarity.","zh":"這個短語透過指出相似處來幫助比較不同事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"winding spiral path","meaning":"蜿蜒的螺旋路徑","examples":[{"en":"A labyrinth has a winding spiral path that leads to a central area.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮有一條通向中央區域的蜿蜒螺旋路徑。"},{"en":"A winding spiral path is a curved route that turns around gradually towards a centre.","zh":"winding spiral path 指逐漸繞向中心的彎曲路線。"},{"en":"A garden may use a winding spiral path to make a short walk feel longer and calmer.","zh":"花園可以使用蜿蜒螺旋路徑，令短短步行感覺更長、更平靜。"},{"en":"Because the path winds, walkers move slowly rather than straight ahead.","zh":"因為路徑蜿蜒，行走者會慢慢前進，而不是直走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main shape of a traditional labyrinth.","zh":"這個短語描述傳統單一路徑迷宮的主要形狀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"通向……","examples":[{"en":"The spiral path leads to a central area.","zh":"螺旋路徑通向中央區域。"},{"en":"Lead to means take someone or something towards a place, result, or situation.","zh":"lead to 指把某人或某物帶向某地方、結果或情況。"},{"en":"A narrow corridor may lead to the school library.","zh":"一條狹窄走廊可能通向學校圖書館。"},{"en":"Poor planning can lead to confusion during a group project.","zh":"計劃不足會導致小組項目混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe both physical direction and cause-and-effect.","zh":"這個短語既可描述實際方向，也可描述因果關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"central area","meaning":"中央區域","examples":[{"en":"The goal of a labyrinth is to reach the central area.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮的目標是到達中央區域。"},{"en":"The central area is the middle part of a place or design.","zh":"central area 指地方或設計的中間部分。"},{"en":"A park may have a fountain in its central area.","zh":"公園的中央區域可能有噴水池。"},{"en":"In a labyrinth, the central area often feels like the end point of a journey.","zh":"在單一路徑迷宮中，中央區域常感覺像旅程的終點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the space at or near the centre.","zh":"這個短語描述位於或接近中心的空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"starting point","meaning":"起點","examples":[{"en":"There is one starting point at the entrance.","zh":"入口處有一個起點。"},{"en":"A starting point is the place where a journey, process, or activity begins.","zh":"starting point 指旅程、過程或活動開始的地方。"},{"en":"In a race, the starting point is where runners line up before the signal.","zh":"在賽跑中，起點是跑手在信號前排隊的位置。"},{"en":"A clear starting point helps people know where to begin.","zh":"清楚的起點幫助人知道從哪裏開始。"},{"en":"This phrase can be used for physical routes and ideas.","zh":"這個短語可用於實際路線和想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at the entrance","meaning":"在入口處","examples":[{"en":"The starting point is at the entrance of the labyrinth.","zh":"起點在單一路徑迷宮的入口處。"},{"en":"At the entrance means located where people enter a place.","zh":"at the entrance 指位於人們進入某地方的位置。"},{"en":"A ticket desk may be at the entrance of a museum.","zh":"售票處可能位於博物館入口處。"},{"en":"Placing information at the entrance helps visitors understand what to do first.","zh":"把資訊放在入口處，有助訪客明白第一步要做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a position near the way in.","zh":"這個短語描述接近進入點的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the goal is to","meaning":"目標是……","examples":[{"en":"The goal is to reach the central area.","zh":"目標是到達中央區域。"},{"en":"The goal is to means the purpose or aim is to do something.","zh":"the goal is to 指目的或目標是做某事。"},{"en":"In a reading lesson, the goal is to understand the main idea.","zh":"在閱讀課中，目標是理解主旨。"},{"en":"A clear goal helps people know what they are trying to achieve.","zh":"清楚目標幫助人知道自己想達成甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the main purpose of an activity.","zh":"這個短語引出活動的主要目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reach the central area","meaning":"到達中央區域","examples":[{"en":"Visitors follow the path to reach the central area.","zh":"訪客沿着路徑走，以到達中央區域。"},{"en":"To reach the central area means to arrive at the middle part of a place or design.","zh":"reach the central area 指到達某地方或設計的中間部分。"},{"en":"Tourists may follow signs to reach the central area of an old town.","zh":"遊客可能跟隨指示牌到達古城的中央區域。"},{"en":"In a labyrinth, reaching the centre can feel like completing a quiet journey.","zh":"在單一路徑迷宮中，到達中心會感覺像完成了一段安靜旅程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arrival at the centre.","zh":"這個短語描述到達中心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"find your way through","meaning":"找到穿過……的路","examples":[{"en":"Finding your way through a labyrinth involves many twists and turns.","zh":"找到穿過單一路徑迷宮的路涉及許多曲折轉彎。"},{"en":"To find your way through something means to move through it successfully by following the route.","zh":"find your way through something 指成功沿路穿過某地方。"},{"en":"A new student may need help to find her way through a large school building.","zh":"新學生可能需要幫助，才能找到穿過大型校舍的路。"},{"en":"Clear signs help people find their way through unfamiliar places.","zh":"清楚標示能幫助人找到穿過陌生地方的路。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe both physical movement and dealing with a difficult process.","zh":"這個短語既可描述實際移動，也可描述處理困難過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"involve","meaning":"涉及；包含","examples":[{"en":"Finding your way through a labyrinth involves many twists and turns.","zh":"找到穿過單一路徑迷宮的路涉及許多曲折轉彎。"},{"en":"Involve means include or require something as part of an activity or situation.","zh":"involve 指在某活動或情況中包括或需要某事。"},{"en":"Preparing a school play involves rehearsals, costumes, lighting, and teamwork.","zh":"準備校劇涉及排練、服裝、燈光和團隊合作。"},{"en":"If a task involves many steps, people need careful planning.","zh":"如果任務涉及很多步驟，人們就需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"This verb shows what is included in a process.","zh":"這個動詞顯示某過程包含甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"twists and turns","meaning":"彎彎曲曲；曲折轉彎","examples":[{"en":"A labyrinth involves many twists and turns.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮包含許多曲折轉彎。"},{"en":"Twists and turns are bends and changes in direction along a path.","zh":"twists and turns 指路徑上的彎位和方向變化。"},{"en":"A mountain road with many twists and turns may make drivers slow down.","zh":"有很多彎彎曲曲的山路會令司機減速。"},{"en":"In writing, twists and turns can also mean unexpected changes in a story.","zh":"在寫作中，twists and turns 也可指故事中的意外變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a route or process that is not straight.","zh":"這個短語描述不筆直的路線或過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"get lost","meaning":"迷路","examples":[{"en":"It is not possible to get lost in a traditional labyrinth.","zh":"在傳統單一路徑迷宮中不可能迷路。"},{"en":"To get lost means to be unable to find the correct way or know where you are.","zh":"get lost 指找不到正確方向，或不知道自己在哪裏。"},{"en":"A tourist may get lost in a city if street signs are unclear.","zh":"如果街道指示不清，遊客可能在城市中迷路。"},{"en":"In a traditional labyrinth, there is only one path, so visitors cannot choose a wrong route.","zh":"在傳統單一路徑迷宮中，只有一條路，所以訪客不能選錯路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes losing direction.","zh":"這個短語描述失去方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"one single path","meaning":"一條單一路徑","examples":[{"en":"A labyrinth has only one single path.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮只有一條單一路徑。"},{"en":"One single path means there is only one route to follow, with no alternative branches.","zh":"one single path 指只有一條可跟隨的路線，沒有其他分岔。"},{"en":"A walking trail with one single path is easier for children to follow.","zh":"只有一條單一路徑的步行徑較容易讓小朋友跟着走。"},{"en":"If there is one single path, the challenge is the journey, not choosing directions.","zh":"如果只有一條路，挑戰在於旅程，而不是選方向。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with many possible paths in a maze.","zh":"這個短語與多路徑迷宮中的許多可能路線形成對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in modern times","meaning":"在現代","examples":[{"en":"In modern times, the word labyrinth has taken on a different meaning.","zh":"在現代，labyrinth 這個字帶有不同意思。"},{"en":"In modern times means in the present period or recent history.","zh":"in modern times 指在現今時期或近代歷史中。"},{"en":"In modern times, many students use phones as dictionaries.","zh":"在現代，許多學生把手機當作字典使用。"},{"en":"Words can change meaning in modern times as people use them differently.","zh":"在現代，由於人們用法不同，詞語意思可以改變。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the present with the past.","zh":"這個短語把現在與過去作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"take on a different meaning","meaning":"帶有不同意思","examples":[{"en":"The word labyrinth has taken on a different meaning.","zh":"labyrinth 這個字已帶有不同意思。"},{"en":"To take on a different meaning means to begin to mean something new or different from before.","zh":"take on a different meaning 指開始帶有與以前不同的新意思。"},{"en":"The word “cloud” has taken on a different meaning in computer technology.","zh":"“cloud” 這個字在電腦科技中已帶有不同意思。"},{"en":"When society changes, old words may take on new meanings.","zh":"當社會改變，舊詞可能帶有新意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in meaning over time.","zh":"這個短語描述意思隨時間轉變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be used as","meaning":"被用作……","examples":[{"en":"The word labyrinth is often used as a synonym for a maze.","zh":"labyrinth 這個字常被用作 maze 的同義詞。"},{"en":"Be used as means serve the purpose or function of something.","zh":"be used as 指被用來發揮某物的用途或功能。"},{"en":"A classroom can be used as a meeting room after school.","zh":"課室放學後可以被用作會議室。"},{"en":"If a word is used as another word, people treat the two meanings as similar.","zh":"如果一個字被用作另一個字，人們會把兩個意思視為相近。"},{"en":"This phrase describes function or role.","zh":"這個短語描述功能或角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a synonym for","meaning":"……的同義詞","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinth is often used as a synonym for maze.","zh":"labyrinth 常被用作 maze 的同義詞。"},{"en":"A synonym for a word is another word with the same or very similar meaning.","zh":"synonym for a word 指另一個意思相同或非常相近的詞。"},{"en":"“Big” is a synonym for “large” in many simple sentences.","zh":"在許多簡單句子中，“big” 是 “large” 的同義詞。"},{"en":"Synonyms can be useful, but they do not always have exactly the same meaning.","zh":"同義詞很有用，但意思不一定完全相同。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when explaining vocabulary.","zh":"解釋詞彙時，這個短語很常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"maze","meaning":"迷宮；多路徑迷宮","examples":[{"en":"A maze is quite different from a labyrinth.","zh":"多路徑迷宮與單一路徑迷宮相當不同。"},{"en":"A maze is a puzzle made of many paths, choices, and dead ends.","zh":"maze 指由許多路徑、選擇和死路組成的謎題。"},{"en":"Children may enter a garden maze and try to find the exit.","zh":"小朋友可能進入花園迷宮，嘗試找到出口。"},{"en":"In a maze, people can get lost because some paths lead nowhere.","zh":"在 maze 中，人們可能迷路，因為有些路無法通行。"},{"en":"This word describes a multi-path puzzle, not a single-path labyrinth.","zh":"這個字描述多路徑謎題，而不是單一路徑迷宮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"quite different","meaning":"相當不同","examples":[{"en":"A maze is quite different from a labyrinth.","zh":"多路徑迷宮與單一路徑迷宮相當不同。"},{"en":"Quite different means clearly or noticeably not the same.","zh":"quite different 指清楚或明顯不一樣。"},{"en":"Online learning is quite different from sitting in a classroom.","zh":"網上學習與坐在課室中相當不同。"},{"en":"When two things are quite different, using the same word for both may cause confusion.","zh":"當兩件事相當不同，對兩者使用同一字可能造成混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong contrast.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a kind of puzzle","meaning":"一種謎題","examples":[{"en":"A maze is a kind of puzzle with many possible paths.","zh":"多路徑迷宮是一種有許多可能路徑的謎題。"},{"en":"A kind of puzzle means a type of problem or game that people must solve.","zh":"a kind of puzzle 指某類需要人解決的問題或遊戲。"},{"en":"A crossword is a kind of puzzle that tests vocabulary.","zh":"填字遊戲是一種測試詞彙的謎題。"},{"en":"A maze becomes a puzzle because visitors must choose the correct route.","zh":"多路徑迷宮成為謎題，因為訪客必須選擇正確路線。"},{"en":"This phrase classifies something as a problem-solving activity.","zh":"這個短語把某事分類為解難活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"intricate network of paths","meaning":"複雜的路徑網絡","examples":[{"en":"A maze contains an intricate network of paths.","zh":"多路徑迷宮包含複雜的路徑網絡。"},{"en":"An intricate network of paths is a complicated system of many connected routes.","zh":"intricate network of paths 指由許多相連路線組成的複雜系統。"},{"en":"An old market may have an intricate network of narrow lanes.","zh":"舊街市可能有複雜的狹窄小巷網絡。"},{"en":"If paths form an intricate network, people need signs or memory to find the way.","zh":"如果路徑形成複雜網絡，人們需要指示牌或記憶才能找到路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a complex arrangement of routes.","zh":"這個短語描述路線的複雜安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"become fashionable","meaning":"變得流行","examples":[{"en":"Mazes became fashionable in Europe in the 15th and 16th centuries.","zh":"多路徑迷宮在15和16世紀的歐洲變得流行。"},{"en":"Become fashionable means become popular or admired during a period of time.","zh":"become fashionable 指在某時期變得受歡迎或受欣賞。"},{"en":"Cycling became fashionable in some cities after new bike lanes were built.","zh":"一些城市建成新單車徑後，踩單車變得流行。"},{"en":"When something becomes fashionable, more people want to copy or display it.","zh":"當某物變得流行，更多人想模仿或展示它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a trend becoming popular.","zh":"這個短語描述趨勢變得受歡迎。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"great houses and palaces","meaning":"大宅和宮殿","examples":[{"en":"Mazes can still be found in the gardens of great houses and palaces.","zh":"多路徑迷宮至今仍可在大宅和宮殿的花園中找到。"},{"en":"Great houses and palaces are large, important homes or royal buildings.","zh":"great houses and palaces 指大型重要住宅或皇家建築。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit great houses and palaces to see old gardens and furniture.","zh":"遊客可能參觀大宅和宮殿，欣賞古老花園和家具。"},{"en":"Wealthy owners used garden mazes to display taste, status, and entertainment.","zh":"富有主人利用花園迷宮展示品味、地位和娛樂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes grand historic buildings.","zh":"這個短語描述宏偉歷史建築。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be surrounded by","meaning":"被……包圍","examples":[{"en":"The paths are usually surrounded by thick, high hedges.","zh":"路徑通常被又厚又高的樹籬包圍。"},{"en":"Be surrounded by means have something all around it.","zh":"be surrounded by 指四周都有某物。"},{"en":"A playground may be surrounded by trees to give children shade.","zh":"遊樂場可能被樹木包圍，為孩子提供樹蔭。"},{"en":"If paths are surrounded by high hedges, visitors cannot easily see outside them.","zh":"如果路徑被高樹籬包圍，訪客就不容易看見外面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what is around a place or object.","zh":"這個短語描述某地方或物件周圍有甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"thick, high hedges","meaning":"又厚又高的樹籬","examples":[{"en":"The paths are surrounded by thick, high hedges.","zh":"路徑被又厚又高的樹籬包圍。"},{"en":"Thick, high hedges are dense rows of tall bushes used as barriers or walls.","zh":"thick, high hedges 指由高大密集灌木形成的屏障或牆。"},{"en":"A garden may use thick, high hedges to create privacy from neighbours.","zh":"花園可能使用又厚又高的樹籬來隔開鄰居視線。"},{"en":"In a maze, high hedges stop visitors from seeing the correct route from above.","zh":"在迷宮中，高樹籬阻止訪客從高處看見正確路線。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural walls made of plants.","zh":"這個短語描述由植物形成的天然牆。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"see over","meaning":"越過……看","examples":[{"en":"The hedges are so high that it is not possible to see over them.","zh":"樹籬太高，以致不可能越過它們看。"},{"en":"To see over something means to look above it and see what is on the other side.","zh":"see over something 指從某物上方看過去，看見另一邊。"},{"en":"A child may not be able to see over a tall fence.","zh":"小朋友可能無法越過高圍欄看。"},{"en":"If visitors cannot see over the hedges, the maze becomes more difficult.","zh":"如果訪客不能越過樹籬看，迷宮就變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes seeing beyond a barrier.","zh":"這個短語描述越過障礙物觀看。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"entering a maze","meaning":"進入迷宮","examples":[{"en":"Entering a maze usually involves getting lost a few times.","zh":"進入多路徑迷宮通常涉及迷路幾次。"},{"en":"Entering a maze means going into a puzzle-like network of paths.","zh":"entering a maze 指走進一個像謎題般的路徑網絡。"},{"en":"Children entering a maze at a theme park may feel excited and nervous.","zh":"小朋友進入主題公園迷宮時，可能感到興奮又緊張。"},{"en":"Once people enter a maze, they must make choices about which path to follow.","zh":"一旦人們進入迷宮，就必須選擇跟隨哪條路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of the maze experience.","zh":"這個短語描述迷宮體驗的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"use logic to","meaning":"運用邏輯去……","examples":[{"en":"Visitors use logic to work out the pattern.","zh":"訪客運用邏輯去推算出模式。"},{"en":"Use logic to do something means use reason and careful thinking to solve a problem.","zh":"use logic to do something 指用理性和仔細思考去解決問題。"},{"en":"Students use logic to solve a maths puzzle instead of guessing randomly.","zh":"學生運用邏輯去解數學謎題，而不是隨便猜。"},{"en":"In a maze, logic helps people remember which paths have already failed.","zh":"在迷宮中，邏輯幫助人記住哪些路已經走不通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes solving something through reasoning.","zh":"這個短語描述透過推理解決問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"work out the pattern","meaning":"推算出模式","examples":[{"en":"Visitors use logic to work out the pattern of the maze.","zh":"訪客運用邏輯推算出迷宮的模式。"},{"en":"To work out the pattern means to understand how something is organised.","zh":"work out the pattern 指理解某事如何被組織。"},{"en":"A student may work out the pattern in a number sequence by comparing the differences.","zh":"學生可以透過比較差異，推算出數列模式。"},{"en":"When people work out a maze pattern, they can avoid repeating the same mistake.","zh":"當人們推算出迷宮模式，就能避免重複同一錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discovering the hidden order in something.","zh":"這個短語描述發現某事背後的隱藏規律。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"find your way to","meaning":"找到通往……的路","examples":[{"en":"Visitors try to find their way to the centre and then out again.","zh":"訪客嘗試找到通往中心的路，然後再走出來。"},{"en":"To find your way to a place means to discover how to reach it.","zh":"find your way to a place 指找出如何到達某地方。"},{"en":"New students may need a map to find their way to the science laboratory.","zh":"新學生可能需要地圖，才能找到通往科學實驗室的路。"},{"en":"Finding your way requires signs, memory, directions, or careful observation.","zh":"找路需要標示、記憶、方向指示或仔細觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching a destination.","zh":"這個短語描述到達目的地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dead ends","meaning":"死路","examples":[{"en":"There are lots of dead ends in a maze.","zh":"多路徑迷宮中有很多死路。"},{"en":"Dead ends are paths that stop and do not lead anywhere useful.","zh":"dead ends 指停住而不能通向有用地方的路。"},{"en":"A driver may reach a dead end in a narrow village road and need to turn back.","zh":"司機可能在狹窄村路遇到死路，需要掉頭。"},{"en":"In a maze, dead ends force visitors to try another route.","zh":"在迷宮中，死路迫使訪客嘗試另一條路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes routes that cannot continue.","zh":"這個短語描述不能繼續前進的路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lead you back to","meaning":"把你帶回……","examples":[{"en":"Some paths lead you back to where you started.","zh":"有些路會把你帶回開始的地方。"},{"en":"Lead you back to means take you again to an earlier place or position.","zh":"lead you back to 指再次把你帶到較早的位置或地方。"},{"en":"A wrong corridor in a shopping centre may lead you back to the main entrance.","zh":"商場中的錯誤走廊可能把你帶回正門。"},{"en":"In a maze, some routes waste time by returning you to the beginning.","zh":"在迷宮中，有些路會把你帶回起點，浪費時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a path that brings you back rather than forward.","zh":"這個短語描述把你帶回去而不是向前的路徑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"where you started","meaning":"你開始的地方","examples":[{"en":"Some paths lead you back to where you started.","zh":"有些路會把你帶回你開始的地方。"},{"en":"Where you started means the place or point where you began.","zh":"where you started 指你開始的地點或位置。"},{"en":"If a bus route forms a circle, it may bring you back to where you started.","zh":"如果巴士路線形成一個圓圈，它可能把你帶回開始的地方。"},{"en":"Returning to where you started can feel frustrating if you expected progress.","zh":"如果你原本期待有進展，回到起點會令人沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the original starting place.","zh":"這個短語指原本開始的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be believed to","meaning":"據信……","examples":[{"en":"The word “maze” is believed to come from a Scandinavian word.","zh":"“maze” 這個字據信來自一個斯堪的納維亞語詞。"},{"en":"Be believed to means people generally think something is true, although it may not be certain.","zh":"be believed to 指人們普遍認為某事是真的，雖然未必完全確定。"},{"en":"This old building is believed to be over 300 years old.","zh":"這座舊建築據信已有超過300年歷史。"},{"en":"Scholars use this phrase when evidence suggests something but is not completely final.","zh":"當證據顯示某事但未完全定論時，學者會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a widely accepted belief.","zh":"這個短語表達被廣泛接受的看法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"come from","meaning":"來自……","examples":[{"en":"The word “maze” comes from a Scandinavian word.","zh":"“maze” 這個字來自一個斯堪的納維亞語詞。"},{"en":"Come from means originate in a place, source, or earlier form.","zh":"come from 指源自某地方、來源或早期形式。"},{"en":"Many English words come from Latin, French, or Greek.","zh":"許多英文字來自拉丁語、法語或希臘語。"},{"en":"Knowing where a word comes from can explain its meaning today.","zh":"知道一個字來自哪裏，可以解釋它今天的意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes origin.","zh":"這個短語描述起源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Scandinavian word","meaning":"斯堪的納維亞語詞","examples":[{"en":"The word “maze” is believed to come from a Scandinavian word.","zh":"“maze” 這個字據信來自一個斯堪的納維亞語詞。"},{"en":"A Scandinavian word is a word from the languages of countries such as Norway, Sweden, or Denmark.","zh":"Scandinavian word 指來自挪威、瑞典或丹麥等國語言的詞。"},{"en":"Some English words come from Scandinavian words brought by earlier settlers.","zh":"有些英文字來自早期定居者帶來的斯堪的納維亞語詞。"},{"en":"Word origins can show historical contact between different peoples.","zh":"詞源可以顯示不同民族之間的歷史接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a linguistic source from Northern Europe.","zh":"這個短語指出來自北歐的語言來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a state of confusion","meaning":"混亂狀態","examples":[{"en":"The original word referred to a state of confusion.","zh":"原本的詞指一種混亂狀態。"},{"en":"A state of confusion is a situation in which people feel lost, unclear, or unable to understand what is happening.","zh":"state of confusion 指人們感到迷失、不清楚或無法理解正在發生甚麼的情況。"},{"en":"A new student may be in a state of confusion on the first day at a large school.","zh":"新學生第一天到大型學校時，可能處於混亂狀態。"},{"en":"Confusing instructions can create a state of confusion for everyone in a class.","zh":"混亂的指示會令全班陷入混亂狀態。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental disorder or uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語描述精神上的混亂或不確定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"this is where","meaning":"這就是……的來源","examples":[{"en":"This is where the word “amazing” comes from.","zh":"這就是 “amazing” 這個字的來源。"},{"en":"This is where means this is the point, place, or source from which something begins or develops.","zh":"this is where 指這就是某事開始或發展的點、地方或來源。"},{"en":"This is where the problem started: nobody checked the timetable.","zh":"這就是問題開始的地方：沒有人檢查時間表。"},{"en":"The phrase helps explain origin or cause.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋起源或原因。"},{"en":"It points to the source of something being discussed.","zh":"它指向正在討論的事物來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths, on the other hand, have a very different function.","zh":"另一方面，單一路徑迷宮有非常不同的功能。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrast with what was just said.","zh":"on the other hand 用來引出與剛才所說內容的對比。"},{"en":"A car is fast; on the other hand, a bicycle is cheaper and healthier.","zh":"汽車很快；另一方面，單車較便宜也較健康。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare two different ideas fairly.","zh":"這個短語幫助公平比較兩個不同想法。"},{"en":"It is useful in explanations and essays.","zh":"它適合用於解釋和文章。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have a very different function","meaning":"有非常不同的功能","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths have a very different function from mazes.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮與多路徑迷宮有非常不同的功能。"},{"en":"Have a very different function means serve a completely different purpose.","zh":"have a very different function 指發揮完全不同的用途。"},{"en":"A library and a cinema may both be public places, but they have very different functions.","zh":"圖書館和戲院都可以是公共地方，但功能非常不同。"},{"en":"Understanding function helps people avoid confusing similar-looking things.","zh":"理解功能有助人避免混淆外觀相似的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difference in purpose, not only appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述用途上的差異，而不只是外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"稱……為……","examples":[{"en":"People now often refer to complicated things as labyrinths.","zh":"現在人們常把複雜的東西稱為 labyrinths。"},{"en":"To refer to something as something else means to call or describe it using that term.","zh":"refer to something as something else 指用某個詞稱呼或描述某事。"},{"en":"People may refer to a difficult form as a nightmare if it is too confusing.","zh":"如果表格太混亂，人們可能把它稱為噩夢。"},{"en":"The words people use can show how they understand an object or situation.","zh":"人們使用的詞語可以顯示他們如何理解某物或情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes naming or describing.","zh":"這個短語描述命名或形容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"complicated","meaning":"複雜的","examples":[{"en":"People often describe complicated things as labyrinths.","zh":"人們常把複雜的東西形容為 labyrinths。"},{"en":"Complicated means having many parts or details, making something difficult to understand or deal with.","zh":"complicated 指有許多部分或細節，使某事難以理解或處理。"},{"en":"A school timetable can become complicated if every class has a different room.","zh":"如果每堂課都在不同課室，學校時間表可能變得複雜。"},{"en":"Complicated systems may need clear instructions to avoid confusion.","zh":"複雜系統可能需要清晰指示，以避免混亂。"},{"en":"This word describes something not simple.","zh":"這個字描述不簡單的事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not how they were seen","meaning":"過去並非這樣被看待","examples":[{"en":"This is not how labyrinths were seen in the past.","zh":"過去單一路徑迷宮並非這樣被看待。"},{"en":"Not how they were seen means not the way people understood or regarded them before.","zh":"not how they were seen 指不是人們以前理解或看待它們的方式。"},{"en":"Mobile phones were not how they were seen twenty years ago; now they are everyday tools.","zh":"手機已不是二十年前被看待的樣子；現在它們是日常工具。"},{"en":"Views can change when culture, technology, or language changes.","zh":"當文化、科技或語言改變，觀點也會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts past understanding with present understanding.","zh":"這個短語把過去理解與現代理解作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"在過去","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths were seen differently in the past.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮在過去被不同地看待。"},{"en":"In the past means at an earlier time before now.","zh":"in the past 指在現在之前的較早時間。"},{"en":"In the past, students wrote letters more often than emails.","zh":"在過去，學生較常寫信，而不是電郵。"},{"en":"Looking at the past helps explain why meanings and customs change.","zh":"回看過去有助解釋意思和習俗為何改變。"},{"en":"This phrase places a situation in earlier history.","zh":"這個短語把情況放在較早歷史中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the winding spiral","meaning":"蜿蜒的螺旋路徑","examples":[{"en":"The winding spiral of the labyrinth has been used as a metaphor.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮的蜿蜒螺旋路徑曾被用作隱喻。"},{"en":"The winding spiral is the curved path that turns inward or outward in a labyrinth.","zh":"winding spiral 指單一路徑迷宮中向內或向外旋轉的彎曲路徑。"},{"en":"A winding spiral can make a walker feel that the journey is slow and reflective.","zh":"蜿蜒的螺旋路徑可以令行走者感到旅程緩慢而具反思性。"},{"en":"Because it does not go straight, it can represent life’s indirect progress.","zh":"因為它不是直路，所以可以代表人生間接而曲折的進展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both a shape and a symbolic path.","zh":"這個短語同時描述形狀和象徵性道路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"for centuries","meaning":"幾個世紀以來","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths have been used for centuries as a metaphor for life’s journey.","zh":"幾個世紀以來，單一路徑迷宮一直被用作人生旅程的隱喻。"},{"en":"For centuries means for hundreds of years.","zh":"for centuries 指持續數百年。"},{"en":"People have used herbal medicines for centuries in many cultures.","zh":"許多文化幾個世紀以來一直使用草藥。"},{"en":"If a symbol lasts for centuries, it likely continues to feel meaningful.","zh":"如果一個符號延續幾個世紀，它很可能仍然有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a very long period of time.","zh":"這個短語強調非常長的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"metaphor for","meaning":"……的隱喻","examples":[{"en":"The labyrinth has been used as a metaphor for life’s journey.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮一直被用作人生旅程的隱喻。"},{"en":"A metaphor for something is an image or idea used to represent it.","zh":"metaphor for something 指用來代表某事的形象或想法。"},{"en":"A long road can be a metaphor for growing up because both involve progress and difficulty.","zh":"長路可以是成長的隱喻，因為兩者都涉及進展和困難。"},{"en":"Metaphors help people understand abstract experiences through concrete images.","zh":"隱喻幫助人透過具體形象理解抽象經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes symbolic comparison.","zh":"這個短語描述象徵性比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"life’s journey","meaning":"人生旅程","examples":[{"en":"The labyrinth is a metaphor for life’s journey.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮是人生旅程的隱喻。"},{"en":"Life’s journey means the path of a person’s life, including choices, difficulties, growth, and change.","zh":"life’s journey 指一個人的人生道路，包括選擇、困難、成長和改變。"},{"en":"Graduation is one step in a young person’s life journey.","zh":"畢業是年輕人人生旅程中的一步。"},{"en":"A winding path can represent life’s journey because progress is rarely straight.","zh":"蜿蜒路徑可以代表人生旅程，因為進展很少是筆直的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes life as a long process.","zh":"這個短語把人生描述為一個長過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"serve as","meaning":"作為……","examples":[{"en":"The labyrinth served as a spiritual reminder.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮作為一種精神上的提醒。"},{"en":"Serve as means function as or be used as something.","zh":"serve as 指發揮某種功能或被用作某物。"},{"en":"A school library can serve as a quiet study space after lessons.","zh":"學校圖書館可以在放學後作為安靜自修空間。"},{"en":"An object can serve as a reminder when it helps people remember an idea or duty.","zh":"當一件物品幫助人記住某個想法或責任，它就可以作為提醒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the role something plays.","zh":"這個短語描述某物扮演的角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spiritual reminder","meaning":"精神上的提醒","examples":[{"en":"The labyrinth served as a spiritual reminder of purpose and meaning.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮作為關於目的和意義的精神提醒。"},{"en":"A spiritual reminder is something that helps people remember deeper values, beliefs, or meaning.","zh":"spiritual reminder 指幫助人記起更深層價值、信念或意義的事物。"},{"en":"A quiet church bell may serve as a spiritual reminder to pause and reflect.","zh":"安靜的教堂鐘聲可以作為精神上的提醒，叫人停下來反思。"},{"en":"Walking a labyrinth can remind people to slow down and think beyond daily worries.","zh":"行走單一路徑迷宮可以提醒人放慢腳步，思考日常憂慮以外的事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an object or practice with inner meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述帶有內在意義的物件或做法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"purpose and meaning","meaning":"目的和意義","examples":[{"en":"The labyrinth reminded people that life has purpose and meaning.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮提醒人們生命有目的和意義。"},{"en":"Purpose and meaning are the reasons and values that make life feel worthwhile.","zh":"purpose and meaning 指令人覺得人生值得的原因和價值。"},{"en":"A student may find purpose and meaning in helping younger classmates learn.","zh":"學生可能在幫助低年級同學學習中找到目的和意義。"},{"en":"When people lose a sense of purpose and meaning, they may feel directionless.","zh":"當人失去目的和意義感，可能會感到沒有方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deeper reasons for living or acting.","zh":"這個短語描述生活或行動背後較深層原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"give people a sense of direction","meaning":"給人方向感","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths helped to give people a sense of direction.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮幫助給人方向感。"},{"en":"To give people a sense of direction means help them feel they know where they are going or what matters.","zh":"give people a sense of direction 指幫助人感到自己知道要往哪裏去或甚麼重要。"},{"en":"A clear study plan can give students a sense of direction before exams.","zh":"清晰溫習計劃可以在考試前給學生方向感。"},{"en":"Without direction, people may feel confused even if they are busy.","zh":"沒有方向時，即使忙碌，人們也可能感到混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe emotional guidance as well as physical direction.","zh":"這個短語既可描述情感指引，也可描述實際方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be thought to","meaning":"被認為……","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths are thought to encourage a feeling of calm.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮被認為能帶來平靜感。"},{"en":"Be thought to means people believe or consider that something is true.","zh":"be thought to 指人們相信或認為某事是真的。"},{"en":"Green spaces are thought to reduce stress for many city residents.","zh":"綠化空間被認為能為許多城市居民減壓。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting a belief without claiming complete certainty.","zh":"當報告某種信念而不作完全肯定時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It often appears in careful explanations.","zh":"它常出現在謹慎解釋中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"encourage a feeling of calm","meaning":"帶來平靜感","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths are thought to encourage a feeling of calm.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮被認為能帶來平靜感。"},{"en":"To encourage a feeling of calm means to help people become quieter, less anxious, and more peaceful.","zh":"encourage a feeling of calm 指幫助人變得更安靜、較不焦慮和更平和。"},{"en":"Soft music may encourage a feeling of calm before a stressful exam.","zh":"柔和音樂可能在壓力大的考試前帶來平靜感。"},{"en":"Slow walking can reduce rushing thoughts and help calmness grow.","zh":"慢步行可以減少急促思緒，幫助平靜感增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating emotional quietness.","zh":"這個短語描述創造情緒上的安靜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"meditation and prayer tool","meaning":"冥想和祈禱工具","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths have been used as a meditation and prayer tool.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮一直被用作冥想和祈禱工具。"},{"en":"A meditation and prayer tool is something used to help people focus quietly or spiritually.","zh":"meditation and prayer tool 指用來幫助人安靜或精神上集中注意力的東西。"},{"en":"Some people use candles, beads, or quiet music as meditation tools.","zh":"有些人使用蠟燭、念珠或安靜音樂作為冥想工具。"},{"en":"Walking a labyrinth can give the body a simple rhythm while the mind reflects.","zh":"行走單一路徑迷宮可以給身體簡單節奏，同時讓心靈反思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical aid for inner focus.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助內心專注的實用工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in many cultures","meaning":"在許多文化中","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths have been used in many cultures over many centuries.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮在許多文化中使用了許多世紀。"},{"en":"In many cultures means among many different societies and traditions.","zh":"in many cultures 指在許多不同社會和傳統之中。"},{"en":"Stories about heroes appear in many cultures around the world.","zh":"關於英雄的故事出現在世界許多文化中。"},{"en":"If a symbol appears in many cultures, it may speak to a shared human experience.","zh":"如果一個符號出現在許多文化中，它可能觸及共同的人類經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses wide cultural spread.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛的文化分布。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"earliest examples of","meaning":"最早的例子","examples":[{"en":"The earliest examples of the spiral pattern have been found carved into stone.","zh":"螺旋圖案最早的例子被發現刻在石頭上。"},{"en":"The earliest examples of something are the oldest known cases or forms of it.","zh":"earliest examples of something 指目前已知最古老的案例或形式。"},{"en":"The earliest examples of writing were often scratched onto clay or stone.","zh":"文字最早的例子常被刻在泥板或石頭上。"},{"en":"Early examples help historians understand when an idea first appeared.","zh":"早期例子幫助歷史學家理解某想法何時首次出現。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the oldest evidence available.","zh":"這個短語指向可得的最古老證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spiral pattern","meaning":"螺旋圖案","examples":[{"en":"The labyrinth spiral pattern appears in many ancient carvings.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮的螺旋圖案出現在許多古代雕刻中。"},{"en":"A spiral pattern is a shape that curves around a centre while moving inward or outward.","zh":"spiral pattern 指圍繞中心向內或向外彎曲的形狀。"},{"en":"Shells, storms, and some staircases can have spiral patterns.","zh":"貝殼、風暴和一些樓梯都可以有螺旋圖案。"},{"en":"Spiral patterns often suggest movement, growth, or a journey towards a centre.","zh":"螺旋圖案常暗示移動、成長或走向中心的旅程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated curved design.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆彎曲的設計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"carved into stone","meaning":"刻在石頭上","examples":[{"en":"The earliest labyrinth patterns were carved into stone.","zh":"最早的單一路徑迷宮圖案被刻在石頭上。"},{"en":"Carved into stone means cut or shaped into stone using tools.","zh":"carved into stone 指用工具在石頭上切刻或塑形。"},{"en":"Ancient names were sometimes carved into stone so they would last for centuries.","zh":"古代名字有時被刻在石頭上，以便保存數百年。"},{"en":"Carving into stone preserves designs better than drawing on paper.","zh":"刻在石頭上比畫在紙上更能保存設計。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a permanent way of making marks.","zh":"這個短語描述製造永久痕跡的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"date from","meaning":"可追溯至……","examples":[{"en":"In Europe, these spiral carvings date from the late Bronze Age.","zh":"在歐洲，這些螺旋雕刻可追溯至青銅時代晚期。"},{"en":"Date from means come from or belong to a particular time in history.","zh":"date from 指源自或屬於歷史上某個特定時期。"},{"en":"Some old city walls date from the medieval period.","zh":"有些舊城牆可追溯至中世紀。"},{"en":"If an object dates from an ancient period, it can help historians study that time.","zh":"如果一件物件可追溯至古代時期，它可以幫助歷史學家研究那段時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes historical origin by time.","zh":"這個短語按時間描述歷史起源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"late Bronze Age","meaning":"青銅時代晚期","examples":[{"en":"The spiral carvings date from the late Bronze Age.","zh":"這些螺旋雕刻可追溯至青銅時代晚期。"},{"en":"The late Bronze Age is the later part of the historical period when bronze tools and objects were widely used.","zh":"late Bronze Age 指青銅工具和物件被廣泛使用的歷史時期後段。"},{"en":"Archaeologists study late Bronze Age objects to understand ancient technology and beliefs.","zh":"考古學家研究青銅時代晚期物件，以了解古代科技和信仰。"},{"en":"If a carving dates from this period, it is thousands of years old.","zh":"如果雕刻來自這一時期，它已有數千年歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific ancient historical period.","zh":"這個短語指出特定古代歷史時期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Native American","meaning":"美洲原住民的","examples":[{"en":"The Native American Pima tribe used a circular labyrinth design.","zh":"美洲原住民的 Pima 部落使用圓形迷宮圖案。"},{"en":"Native American means relating to the Indigenous peoples of North America.","zh":"Native American 指與北美原住民族有關。"},{"en":"Native American art often uses patterns, materials, and stories connected to tribal traditions.","zh":"美洲原住民藝術常使用與部落傳統相關的圖案、材料和故事。"},{"en":"This term should be used respectfully because it refers to real peoples and cultures.","zh":"這個詞應尊重地使用，因為它指真實民族和文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes Indigenous American identity or culture.","zh":"這個短語描述美洲原住民身份或文化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Pima tribe","meaning":"Pima 部落","examples":[{"en":"The Pima tribe wove baskets with a labyrinth design.","zh":"Pima 部落編織帶有迷宮圖案的籃子。"},{"en":"The Pima tribe is a Native American group known for cultural traditions including basket-making.","zh":"Pima tribe 指一個美洲原住民群體，以包括編籃在內的文化傳統聞名。"},{"en":"A museum may display baskets made by the Pima tribe to show their craft and symbols.","zh":"博物館可能展示 Pima 部落製作的籃子，以呈現其工藝和符號。"},{"en":"Tribal designs can express beliefs about life, land, and the universe.","zh":"部落圖案可以表達關於生命、土地和宇宙的信念。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific Indigenous group.","zh":"這個短語指出一個特定原住民族群。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"weave baskets","meaning":"編織籃子","examples":[{"en":"The Pima tribe wove baskets with circular labyrinth designs.","zh":"Pima 部落編織帶有圓形迷宮圖案的籃子。"},{"en":"To weave baskets means to make baskets by crossing strips of material over and under each other.","zh":"weave baskets 指把材料條交錯穿插來製作籃子。"},{"en":"A craft class may teach students how to weave baskets from reeds or paper.","zh":"手工藝班可能教學生用蘆葦或紙編織籃子。"},{"en":"Basket weaving can preserve traditional patterns and skills.","zh":"編籃可以保存傳統圖案和技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a handcraft process.","zh":"這個短語描述手工藝過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"circular labyrinth design","meaning":"圓形迷宮圖案","examples":[{"en":"The baskets had a circular labyrinth design.","zh":"這些籃子有圓形迷宮圖案。"},{"en":"A circular labyrinth design is a round pattern with a path that winds towards a centre.","zh":"circular labyrinth design 指有一條路徑蜿蜒通向中心的圓形圖案。"},{"en":"A plate or carpet may use a circular labyrinth design as decoration.","zh":"碟子或地氈可能使用圓形迷宮圖案作裝飾。"},{"en":"The circular shape can suggest movement, cycle, and return.","zh":"圓形可以暗示移動、循環和回歸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a round labyrinth pattern used in art or objects.","zh":"這個短語描述用於藝術或物件上的圓形迷宮圖案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"depict","meaning":"描繪","examples":[{"en":"The design depicted the tribe’s own cosmology.","zh":"這個設計描繪了該部落自己的宇宙觀。"},{"en":"To depict means to show or represent something in art, writing, or design.","zh":"depict 指在藝術、寫作或設計中展示或代表某事物。"},{"en":"A painting may depict a busy market on a festival day.","zh":"一幅畫可能描繪節日當天繁忙的街市。"},{"en":"Designs can depict beliefs without using words.","zh":"設計可以不用文字也描繪信念。"},{"en":"This verb describes visual or artistic representation.","zh":"這個動詞描述視覺或藝術呈現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cosmology","meaning":"宇宙觀","examples":[{"en":"The labyrinth design depicted the Pima tribe’s cosmology.","zh":"迷宮圖案描繪了 Pima 部落的宇宙觀。"},{"en":"Cosmology is a culture’s or belief system’s understanding of the universe and human place within it.","zh":"cosmology 指一種文化或信仰體系對宇宙以及人在其中位置的理解。"},{"en":"Ancient stories often reveal a people’s cosmology through ideas about sky, earth, gods, and creation.","zh":"古代故事常透過天空、大地、神明和創世觀念揭示一個民族的宇宙觀。"},{"en":"A design can express cosmology by showing how life, nature, and spirit are connected.","zh":"設計可以透過展示生命、自然和精神如何相連來表達宇宙觀。"},{"en":"This word describes a worldview about the universe.","zh":"這個字描述關於宇宙的世界觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Ancient Greece","meaning":"古希臘","examples":[{"en":"In Ancient Greece, the labyrinth spiral was used on coins.","zh":"在古希臘，迷宮螺旋被用在硬幣上。"},{"en":"Ancient Greece refers to the Greek civilisation of the ancient world.","zh":"Ancient Greece 指古代世界中的希臘文明。"},{"en":"Ancient Greece is often studied for its art, philosophy, theatre, and mythology.","zh":"古希臘常因藝術、哲學、戲劇和神話而被研究。"},{"en":"Objects from Ancient Greece can show what symbols mattered to people at the time.","zh":"古希臘物件可以顯示當時人們重視甚麼符號。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a major historical civilisation.","zh":"這個短語指出一個重要歷史文明。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be used on","meaning":"被用在……上","examples":[{"en":"The labyrinth spiral was used on coins around 4,000 years ago.","zh":"迷宮螺旋約4,000年前被用在硬幣上。"},{"en":"Be used on means be placed, printed, carved, or shown on a surface or object.","zh":"be used on 指被放置、印刷、雕刻或顯示在某表面或物件上。"},{"en":"A school logo may be used on uniforms, letters, and posters.","zh":"學校標誌可能被用在校服、信件和海報上。"},{"en":"If a symbol is used on coins, it may have public or cultural importance.","zh":"如果符號被用在硬幣上，它可能具有公共或文化重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where a design appears.","zh":"這個短語描述設計出現在哪裏。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"made of mosaics","meaning":"由馬賽克製成","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths made of mosaics were common in the Roman Empire.","zh":"由馬賽克製成的迷宮在羅馬帝國很常見。"},{"en":"Made of mosaics means created from many small coloured pieces of stone, glass, or tile.","zh":"made of mosaics 指由許多小塊彩色石、玻璃或瓷磚製成。"},{"en":"A church floor may be made of mosaics showing animals or patterns.","zh":"教堂地板可能由馬賽克製成，展示動物或圖案。"},{"en":"Mosaic designs can last for a long time because the pieces are hard and durable.","zh":"馬賽克設計可以保存很久，因為材料堅硬耐用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the material and method of decoration.","zh":"這個短語描述裝飾的材料和方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be commonly found in","meaning":"常見於……","examples":[{"en":"Mosaic labyrinths were commonly found in bathhouses, villas and tombs.","zh":"馬賽克迷宮常見於浴場、別墅和陵墓。"},{"en":"Be commonly found in means often appear or exist in particular places.","zh":"be commonly found in 指經常出現或存在於某些地方。"},{"en":"Noticeboards are commonly found in schools, offices, and community centres.","zh":"告示板常見於學校、辦公室和社區中心。"},{"en":"If a design is commonly found in certain buildings, it may have been part of everyday culture.","zh":"如果某設計常見於某些建築，它可能曾是日常文化的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequent location.","zh":"這個短語描述常見位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bathhouses","meaning":"浴場","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths were commonly found in Roman bathhouses.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮常見於羅馬浴場。"},{"en":"Bathhouses were public or private buildings where people went to wash, bathe, and relax.","zh":"bathhouses 指人們前往清洗、沐浴和放鬆的公共或私人建築。"},{"en":"Roman bathhouses often included pools, heated rooms, and decorated floors.","zh":"羅馬浴場常包括水池、加熱房間和裝飾地板。"},{"en":"Decorations in bathhouses show that bathing could be social and cultural, not only practical.","zh":"浴場中的裝飾顯示沐浴可以是社交和文化活動，而不只是實用需要。"},{"en":"This word describes bathing buildings, especially in historical contexts.","zh":"這個字描述沐浴建築，尤其用於歷史語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"villas","meaning":"別墅","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths were also found in Roman villas.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮也在羅馬別墅中被發現。"},{"en":"Villas are large country houses or comfortable private homes, often owned by wealthy people.","zh":"villas 指大型鄉郊住宅或舒適私人住宅，常由富有人士擁有。"},{"en":"A Roman villa might have gardens, courtyards, and decorated floors.","zh":"羅馬別墅可能有花園、庭院和裝飾地板。"},{"en":"Finding labyrinths in villas suggests the design was used in private living spaces.","zh":"在別墅中發現迷宮，顯示這種設計曾用於私人生活空間。"},{"en":"This word describes large elegant homes, especially in historical settings.","zh":"這個字描述大型優雅住宅，尤其在歷史語境中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tombs","meaning":"陵墓","examples":[{"en":"Mosaic labyrinths were found in tombs throughout the Roman Empire.","zh":"馬賽克迷宮在遍及羅馬帝國的陵墓中被發現。"},{"en":"Tombs are places where dead people are buried or remembered.","zh":"tombs 指埋葬或紀念死者的地方。"},{"en":"Ancient tombs often contain objects, symbols, or art connected to beliefs about death.","zh":"古代陵墓常包含與死亡信仰有關的物件、符號或藝術。"},{"en":"A labyrinth in a tomb may suggest a symbolic journey or spiritual idea.","zh":"陵墓中的迷宮可能暗示象徵性旅程或精神想法。"},{"en":"This word describes burial places.","zh":"這個字描述埋葬場所。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"throughout the Roman Empire","meaning":"遍及羅馬帝國","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths were found throughout the Roman Empire.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮遍及羅馬帝國被發現。"},{"en":"Throughout the Roman Empire means across many parts of the lands ruled by Rome.","zh":"throughout the Roman Empire 指遍及羅馬統治的許多地區。"},{"en":"Roman roads were built throughout the Roman Empire to connect cities and armies.","zh":"羅馬道路遍及羅馬帝國修建，用來連接城市和軍隊。"},{"en":"If a design appeared throughout the empire, it was widely spread.","zh":"如果某設計遍及帝國出現，它就是廣泛流傳的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad distribution across Roman territory.","zh":"這個短語描述在羅馬領土上的廣泛分布。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"actual physical labyrinths","meaning":"真正的實體迷宮","examples":[{"en":"In Northern Europe, there were actual physical labyrinths for walking on.","zh":"在北歐，有真正可供行走的實體單一路徑迷宮。"},{"en":"Actual physical labyrinths are real structures or patterns people can walk on, not just drawings or symbols.","zh":"actual physical labyrinths 指人們可以行走其上的真實結構或圖案，而不只是圖畫或符號。"},{"en":"A park may build an actual physical labyrinth out of stones or plants.","zh":"公園可能用石頭或植物建造真正的實體迷宮。"},{"en":"Physical labyrinths let people experience the pattern with their whole body.","zh":"實體迷宮讓人用整個身體體驗圖案。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real walkable structures with pictures.","zh":"這個短語把可行走的真實結構與圖片作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"designed for","meaning":"設計作……用途","examples":[{"en":"Some labyrinths were designed for walking on.","zh":"有些單一路徑迷宮設計作行走用途。"},{"en":"Designed for something means created with a particular purpose or use in mind.","zh":"designed for something 指創造時以某特定目的或用途為考慮。"},{"en":"A quiet study room is designed for reading and concentration.","zh":"安靜自修室設計作閱讀和集中精神用途。"},{"en":"If a space is designed for walking, its paths and surfaces must be safe.","zh":"如果空間設計作行走用途，路徑和地面必須安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intended purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述預定目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"walking on","meaning":"在上面行走","examples":[{"en":"Physical labyrinths were designed for walking on.","zh":"實體迷宮設計作讓人在上面行走。"},{"en":"Walking on something means moving across its surface on foot.","zh":"walking on something 指用腳在某物表面上移動。"},{"en":"A beach path made of wood is designed for walking on without sinking into sand.","zh":"木製海灘小路設計作讓人在上面行走，而不會陷入沙中。"},{"en":"If a pattern is for walking on, people experience it by moving through it.","zh":"如果圖案是供人行走，人們就透過穿行來體驗它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes use by foot movement.","zh":"這個短語描述以步行方式使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be cut into","meaning":"被切割在……上","examples":[{"en":"These labyrinths were cut into the turf or grass.","zh":"這些迷宮被切割在草皮或草地上。"},{"en":"Be cut into means be made by cutting a shape or pattern into a surface.","zh":"be cut into 指透過在表面切出形狀或圖案而製成。"},{"en":"A child may cut a simple shape into paper during an art lesson.","zh":"小朋友在美術課中可能在紙上剪出簡單形狀。"},{"en":"Cutting a design into grass or turf creates a visible path.","zh":"在草或草皮上切出設計會形成可見路徑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a pattern by removing or shaping material.","zh":"這個短語描述透過移除或塑形材料來製作圖案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"turf","meaning":"草皮","examples":[{"en":"Walking labyrinths were cut into the turf.","zh":"可行走迷宮被切割在草皮上。"},{"en":"Turf is the surface layer of grass and soil.","zh":"turf 指草和泥土的表層。"},{"en":"A football field needs healthy turf so players can run safely.","zh":"足球場需要健康草皮，讓球員安全奔跑。"},{"en":"Cutting paths into turf can create patterns that people can walk along.","zh":"在草皮上切出路徑可以形成讓人沿着走的圖案。"},{"en":"This word describes grass-covered ground.","zh":"這個字描述長有草的地面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"circular pattern","meaning":"圓形圖案","examples":[{"en":"The labyrinths were usually made in a circular pattern.","zh":"這些迷宮通常以圓形圖案製成。"},{"en":"A circular pattern is a design based on circles or round shapes.","zh":"circular pattern 指以圓或圓形形狀為基礎的設計。"},{"en":"A garden bed may be planted in a circular pattern around a tree.","zh":"花圃可以圍着一棵樹以圓形圖案種植。"},{"en":"Circular patterns can make movement feel continuous and balanced.","zh":"圓形圖案可以令移動感覺連續和平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a round arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述圓形排列。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"origin","meaning":"起源","examples":[{"en":"The origin of these walking labyrinths remains unclear.","zh":"這些步行迷宮的起源仍不清楚。"},{"en":"Origin means where something began or first came from.","zh":"origin 指某事開始或最初來自哪裏。"},{"en":"Historians may study the origin of a festival by reading old records.","zh":"歷史學家可能透過閱讀舊紀錄研究節日的起源。"},{"en":"If the origin of a tradition is unclear, people may offer different explanations.","zh":"如果某傳統的起源不清楚，人們可能提出不同解釋。"},{"en":"This word describes the beginning or source of something.","zh":"這個字描述某事的開始或來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"remain unclear","meaning":"仍不清楚","examples":[{"en":"The origin of the walking labyrinths remains unclear.","zh":"步行迷宮的起源仍不清楚。"},{"en":"Remain unclear means still not be known or understood clearly.","zh":"remain unclear 指仍然未能被清楚知道或理解。"},{"en":"The reason for the power cut may remain unclear until engineers check the system.","zh":"停電原因可能要到工程師檢查系統後仍不清楚。"},{"en":"When evidence is limited, historical questions can remain unclear for a long time.","zh":"當證據有限，歷史問題可以長期仍不清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continuing uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語描述持續不確定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fertility rites","meaning":"生育儀式","examples":[{"en":"The walking labyrinths were probably used for fertility rites.","zh":"步行迷宮很可能用於生育儀式。"},{"en":"Fertility rites are ceremonies connected with birth, growth, crops, or the ability to have children.","zh":"fertility rites 指與出生、成長、農作物或生育能力有關的儀式。"},{"en":"Ancient farming communities sometimes held fertility rites before planting season.","zh":"古代農耕社區有時在播種季節前舉行生育儀式。"},{"en":"Such rites often show hopes for life, renewal, and abundance.","zh":"這類儀式常顯示對生命、更新和豐盛的盼望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ritual practices linked to fertility and growth.","zh":"這個短語描述與生育和成長有關的儀式做法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"date back","meaning":"追溯至……","examples":[{"en":"These rites may date back thousands of years.","zh":"這些儀式可能追溯至數千年前。"},{"en":"Date back means have existed since a time in the distant past.","zh":"date back 指自遙遠過去某時期已存在。"},{"en":"Some village customs date back to times before written records.","zh":"有些村落習俗可追溯至文字紀錄以前。"},{"en":"If a practice dates back thousands of years, it has a very long history.","zh":"如果某做法追溯至數千年前，它就有非常悠久歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase describes historical age and continuity.","zh":"這個短語描述歷史年代和延續性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"thousands of years","meaning":"數千年","examples":[{"en":"The fertility rites may date back thousands of years.","zh":"生育儀式可能追溯至數千年前。"},{"en":"Thousands of years means a very long period of many thousand years.","zh":"thousands of years 指長達許多千年的非常漫長時期。"},{"en":"Some cave paintings have survived for thousands of years.","zh":"有些洞穴壁畫保存了數千年。"},{"en":"When something lasts thousands of years, it can connect modern people with ancient lives.","zh":"當某物延續數千年，它可以把現代人與古代生活連起來。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses deep historical time.","zh":"這個短語強調深遠歷史時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"turf labyrinths","meaning":"草皮迷宮","examples":[{"en":"Eleven examples of turf labyrinths survive today.","zh":"十一個草皮迷宮的例子保留至今。"},{"en":"Turf labyrinths are labyrinth patterns cut into grass-covered ground.","zh":"turf labyrinths 指切割在長草地面上的迷宮圖案。"},{"en":"Visitors may walk turf labyrinths in historic villages or church fields.","zh":"訪客可能在歷史村莊或教堂草地上行走草皮迷宮。"},{"en":"Because turf can grow over, these labyrinths need care to remain visible.","zh":"因為草皮會重新生長，這些迷宮需要保養才能保持可見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes grass-based walking labyrinths.","zh":"這個短語描述以草地為基礎的步行迷宮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"survive today","meaning":"保留至今","examples":[{"en":"Eleven examples of turf labyrinths survive today.","zh":"十一個草皮迷宮例子保留至今。"},{"en":"Survive today means still exist in the present despite age, damage, or change.","zh":"survive today 指儘管經歷年代、損壞或改變，仍存在於現在。"},{"en":"Some ancient temples survive today because people repaired them for centuries.","zh":"有些古代寺廟因人們數百年來修復而保留至今。"},{"en":"If only a few examples survive today, they are historically valuable.","zh":"如果只有少數例子保留至今，它們就具有歷史價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something lasting into the present.","zh":"這個短語描述某物延續到現在。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"used to have","meaning":"以前曾有","examples":[{"en":"The largest turf labyrinth used to have a large tree in the middle.","zh":"最大的草皮迷宮以前曾有一棵大樹在中央。"},{"en":"Used to have means had something in the past but does not necessarily have it now.","zh":"used to have 指過去曾有某物，但現在未必仍有。"},{"en":"This park used to have a fountain, but it was removed years ago.","zh":"這個公園以前曾有一個噴水池，但多年前被移走了。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a place or object has changed over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示地方或物件隨時間改變。"},{"en":"It describes a past feature.","zh":"它描述過去的特徵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the middle of","meaning":"在……中央","examples":[{"en":"There used to be a large tree in the middle of the labyrinth.","zh":"迷宮中央以前曾有一棵大樹。"},{"en":"In the middle of means at the centre of a place or thing.","zh":"in the middle of 指在某地方或物件的中心。"},{"en":"A statue may stand in the middle of a town square.","zh":"雕像可能矗立在廣場中央。"},{"en":"Something placed in the middle can become the focus of the whole space.","zh":"放在中央的東西可以成為整個空間的焦點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes central position.","zh":"這個短語描述中心位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"more recently","meaning":"近年來","examples":[{"en":"More recently, labyrinths have experienced a revival.","zh":"近年來，單一路徑迷宮出現了復興。"},{"en":"More recently means in the nearer past, closer to the present time.","zh":"more recently 指在較接近現在的過去。"},{"en":"This town was once industrial; more recently, it has become a tourist area.","zh":"這個城鎮曾經是工業區；近年來，它變成旅遊區。"},{"en":"The phrase helps move from older history to newer developments.","zh":"這個短語幫助從較舊歷史轉向較新發展。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing change over time.","zh":"描述隨時間變化時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"experience something of a revival","meaning":"出現某程度上的復興","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths have experienced something of a revival.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮出現了某程度上的復興。"},{"en":"Experience something of a revival means become popular or used again to some degree.","zh":"experience something of a revival 指某事在某程度上再次變得受歡迎或被使用。"},{"en":"Vinyl records have experienced something of a revival among young music fans.","zh":"黑膠唱片在年輕樂迷之間出現某程度上的復興。"},{"en":"A revival can happen when people find new value in an old practice.","zh":"當人們在舊做法中發現新價值，復興就可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a partial return of interest.","zh":"這個短語描述興趣的部分回歸。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"promote healing","meaning":"促進療癒","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe that walking a labyrinth promotes healing.","zh":"有些人相信行走單一路徑迷宮能促進療癒。"},{"en":"To promote healing means to help recovery, comfort, or improvement in body or mind.","zh":"promote healing 指幫助身體或心靈恢復、得到安慰或改善。"},{"en":"Rest, sleep, and gentle exercise can promote healing after illness.","zh":"休息、睡眠和溫和運動可以在病後促進療癒。"},{"en":"If an activity reduces stress, people may feel that it promotes emotional healing.","zh":"如果一項活動減輕壓力，人們可能覺得它促進情緒療癒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes helping someone become better or calmer.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助某人變好或平靜下來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"mindfulness","meaning":"正念","examples":[{"en":"Walking a labyrinth is thought to promote mindfulness.","zh":"行走單一路徑迷宮被認為能促進正念。"},{"en":"Mindfulness is the practice of paying calm attention to the present moment.","zh":"mindfulness 指平靜地注意當下時刻的練習。"},{"en":"A student may practise mindfulness by breathing slowly before an exam.","zh":"學生可能在考試前透過慢慢呼吸練習正念。"},{"en":"Mindfulness can help people notice thoughts without immediately reacting to them.","zh":"正念可以幫助人注意自己的思緒，而不是立即作出反應。"},{"en":"This word describes calm awareness of the present.","zh":"這個字描述對當下的平靜覺察。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"there are those who believe","meaning":"有些人相信","examples":[{"en":"There are those who believe in the emotional and physical benefits of labyrinths.","zh":"有些人相信單一路徑迷宮有情緒和身體上的好處。"},{"en":"There are those who believe means some people hold this belief.","zh":"there are those who believe 指有些人持有這種看法。"},{"en":"There are those who believe that school should start later for teenagers.","zh":"有些人相信青少年上學時間應該較遲。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a view without saying everyone agrees.","zh":"這個短語引出一種觀點，但沒有說人人同意。"},{"en":"It is useful when presenting one side of a discussion.","zh":"呈現討論中的其中一方時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"emotional and physical benefits","meaning":"情緒和身體上的好處","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe in the emotional and physical benefits of labyrinths.","zh":"有些人相信單一路徑迷宮有情緒和身體上的好處。"},{"en":"Emotional and physical benefits are improvements to feelings, stress levels, body, or health.","zh":"emotional and physical benefits 指對感受、壓力水平、身體或健康的改善。"},{"en":"Regular walking can bring emotional and physical benefits by lifting mood and improving fitness.","zh":"定期步行可以透過改善心情和體能帶來情緒和身體上的好處。"},{"en":"If an activity calms the mind and relaxes the body, it may have both kinds of benefit.","zh":"如果一項活動能平靜心靈並放鬆身體，它可能同時有兩種好處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes effects on both mind and body.","zh":"這個短語描述對心靈和身體的影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"slower breathing","meaning":"放慢呼吸","examples":[{"en":"The benefits may include slower breathing.","zh":"這些好處可能包括放慢呼吸。"},{"en":"Slower breathing means breathing more gently and less quickly.","zh":"slower breathing 指呼吸更慢、更柔和。"},{"en":"A person may practise slower breathing before giving a speech.","zh":"一個人在演講前可能練習放慢呼吸。"},{"en":"Slower breathing can make the body feel less tense during stress.","zh":"放慢呼吸可以在壓力中令身體沒那麼緊繃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a calming physical response.","zh":"這個短語描述令人平靜的身體反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"restored sense of balance","meaning":"恢復平衡感","examples":[{"en":"Walking a labyrinth may bring a restored sense of balance.","zh":"行走單一路徑迷宮可能帶來恢復了的平衡感。"},{"en":"A restored sense of balance means feeling calm, steady, and emotionally centred again.","zh":"restored sense of balance 指再次感到平靜、穩定和情緒上回到中心。"},{"en":"After a stressful week, a quiet walk may restore a person’s sense of balance.","zh":"經過壓力大的一星期後，安靜散步可能恢復一個人的平衡感。"},{"en":"People may feel balanced when their thoughts and emotions no longer feel scattered.","zh":"當思緒和情緒不再分散，人們可能感到平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recovering inner steadiness.","zh":"這個短語描述恢復內在穩定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"perspective","meaning":"看待事物的角度","examples":[{"en":"Walking a labyrinth may help restore perspective.","zh":"行走單一路徑迷宮可能有助恢復看待事物的角度。"},{"en":"Perspective is the way someone sees, understands, or judges a situation.","zh":"perspective 指某人看待、理解或判斷情況的方式。"},{"en":"Talking to a trusted friend can give a student perspective after a disappointing grade.","zh":"成績令人失望後，與信任的朋友交談可以給學生新的角度。"},{"en":"When people regain perspective, problems may feel smaller and more manageable.","zh":"當人重新得到角度，問題可能感覺較小、較可處理。"},{"en":"This word describes a mental viewpoint.","zh":"這個字描述思想上的視角。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"become so popular that","meaning":"變得非常流行，以致……","examples":[{"en":"The idea has become so popular that labyrinths have been placed in wellness centres.","zh":"這個想法變得非常流行，以致單一路徑迷宮被放置在健康中心。"},{"en":"Become so popular that means become popular enough to cause a particular result.","zh":"become so popular that 指流行到造成某個特定結果。"},{"en":"The game became so popular that the school started a club for it.","zh":"這個遊戲變得非常流行，以致學校為它成立學會。"},{"en":"When an idea becomes very popular, organisations may begin to adopt it.","zh":"當一個想法變得很流行，組織可能開始採用它。"},{"en":"This structure links popularity with a consequence.","zh":"這個結構把流行程度與後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be laid into","meaning":"被鋪設在……之中","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths have been laid into the floors of spas and wellness centres.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮已被鋪設在水療中心和健康中心的地板中。"},{"en":"Be laid into means be built, placed, or set into a surface.","zh":"be laid into 指被建造、放置或嵌入某表面。"},{"en":"Decorative tiles may be laid into a hotel lobby floor.","zh":"裝飾瓷磚可能被鋪設在酒店大堂地板中。"},{"en":"When a pattern is laid into a floor, people can walk over it as part of the space.","zh":"當圖案被鋪設在地板中，人們可以在空間中走過它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes installing a design into a surface.","zh":"這個短語描述把設計安裝進表面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"spas","meaning":"水療中心","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths have been laid into the floors of spas.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮已被鋪設在水療中心的地板中。"},{"en":"Spas are places where people go for relaxation, beauty treatments, or wellness services.","zh":"spas 指人們前往放鬆、美容護理或健康服務的地方。"},{"en":"A spa may offer massage, warm baths, quiet rooms, and calming music.","zh":"水療中心可能提供按摩、暖浴、安靜房間和舒緩音樂。"},{"en":"Adding a labyrinth to a spa fits the idea of relaxation and reflection.","zh":"在水療中心加入迷宮符合放鬆和反思的概念。"},{"en":"This word describes wellness and relaxation centres.","zh":"這個字描述健康和放鬆中心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"wellness centres","meaning":"健康中心","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths can now be found in wellness centres.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮現在可以在健康中心找到。"},{"en":"Wellness centres are places that offer services for physical and mental wellbeing.","zh":"wellness centres 指提供身體和心理健康服務的地方。"},{"en":"A wellness centre may provide yoga, counselling, massage, or relaxation spaces.","zh":"健康中心可能提供瑜伽、輔導、按摩或放鬆空間。"},{"en":"Labyrinths in wellness centres are meant to support calm and mindfulness.","zh":"健康中心中的迷宮旨在支持平靜和正念。"},{"en":"This phrase describes places focused on health and wellbeing.","zh":"這個短語描述聚焦健康和身心安好的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in recent years","meaning":"近年來","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths have appeared in spas and prisons in recent years.","zh":"近年來，單一路徑迷宮出現在水療中心和監獄中。"},{"en":"In recent years means during the last few years or the near past.","zh":"in recent years 指在最近幾年或近一段過去時間中。"},{"en":"In recent years, more schools have used tablets in lessons.","zh":"近年來，更多學校在課堂中使用平板電腦。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that a development is modern or current.","zh":"這個短語有助顯示某發展是現代或近期的。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing new trends.","zh":"描述新趨勢時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pamphlet","meaning":"小冊子","examples":[{"en":"A pamphlet at Colorado Children’s Hospital explains the benefits of labyrinths.","zh":"Colorado Children’s Hospital 的一本小冊子解釋單一路徑迷宮的好處。"},{"en":"A pamphlet is a small booklet or folded paper that gives information.","zh":"pamphlet 指提供資料的小冊子或摺頁。"},{"en":"A clinic may give patients a pamphlet about healthy eating.","zh":"診所可能給病人一本關於健康飲食的小冊子。"},{"en":"Pamphlets help people understand services, instructions, or advice quickly.","zh":"小冊子幫助人快速理解服務、指示或建議。"},{"en":"This word describes a short printed information guide.","zh":"這個字描述簡短印刷資料指南。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"inform patients that","meaning":"告訴病人……","examples":[{"en":"The pamphlet informs patients that walking a labyrinth can calm people.","zh":"小冊子告訴病人，行走單一路徑迷宮可以令人平靜。"},{"en":"To inform patients that means to tell patients a fact, advice, or explanation.","zh":"inform patients that 指告訴病人某個事實、建議或解釋。"},{"en":"A nurse may inform patients that they should not eat before surgery.","zh":"護士可能告訴病人手術前不應進食。"},{"en":"Clear information helps patients understand what to expect and what choices they have.","zh":"清楚資訊幫助病人理解會發生甚麼，以及自己有甚麼選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving medical or practical information to patients.","zh":"這個短語描述向病人提供醫療或實用資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in the midst of","meaning":"在……之中","examples":[{"en":"Walking a labyrinth can calm people in the midst of a crisis.","zh":"行走單一路徑迷宮可以在危機之中令人平靜。"},{"en":"In the midst of means in the middle of a difficult situation or event.","zh":"in the midst of 指在困難情況或事件的中間。"},{"en":"A teacher may stay calm in the midst of a classroom emergency.","zh":"老師可能在課室緊急情況之中保持冷靜。"},{"en":"When people are in the midst of stress, simple routines can help them feel steadier.","zh":"當人們處於壓力之中，簡單規律可以幫助他們更穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being surrounded by an ongoing situation.","zh":"這個短語描述置身於正在發生的情況中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"crisis","meaning":"危機","examples":[{"en":"Walking a labyrinth may calm people during a crisis.","zh":"行走單一路徑迷宮可能在危機期間令人平靜。"},{"en":"A crisis is a serious and difficult situation that needs urgent attention.","zh":"crisis 指需要緊急處理的嚴重困難情況。"},{"en":"A family may face a crisis if a child suddenly becomes very ill.","zh":"如果孩子突然重病，家庭可能面對危機。"},{"en":"During a crisis, people often need calm, support, and clear decisions.","zh":"在危機期間，人們通常需要冷靜、支援和清晰決定。"},{"en":"This word describes an urgent moment of danger or serious trouble.","zh":"這個字描述危險或嚴重麻煩的緊急時刻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"apparently","meaning":"顯然","examples":[{"en":"Apparently, it is not only patients who benefit.","zh":"顯然，受益的不只是病人。"},{"en":"Apparently means according to what seems true or what has been reported.","zh":"apparently 指根據看起來是真的情況或所聽聞資料。"},{"en":"Apparently, the school trip was cancelled because the bus broke down.","zh":"顯然，學校旅行取消是因為巴士壞了。"},{"en":"This word often shows that the speaker is reporting information, not personally proving it.","zh":"這個字常顯示說話者是在報告資料，而不是親自證明。"},{"en":"It is useful when presenting something that seems to be the case.","zh":"當呈現似乎成立的事情時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"benefit","meaning":"受益","examples":[{"en":"Patients and visitors can benefit from walking a labyrinth.","zh":"病人和訪客可以從行走單一路徑迷宮中受益。"},{"en":"To benefit from something means to gain help, advantage, or improvement from it.","zh":"benefit from something 指從某事中得到幫助、好處或改善。"},{"en":"Students can benefit from regular feedback because they learn what to improve.","zh":"學生可以從定期回饋中受益，因為他們知道要改善甚麼。"},{"en":"If an activity reduces stress, many people may benefit from it.","zh":"如果一項活動能減壓，許多人可能從中受益。"},{"en":"This verb describes receiving a positive effect.","zh":"這個動詞描述得到正面效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"less stressful than","meaning":"壓力比……小","examples":[{"en":"Walking a labyrinth can be less stressful than sitting in a waiting room.","zh":"行走單一路徑迷宮的壓力可能比坐在候診室小。"},{"en":"Less stressful than means causing less pressure or anxiety compared with something else.","zh":"less stressful than 指與另一事相比，造成較少壓力或焦慮。"},{"en":"Walking home slowly may be less stressful than waiting in a crowded bus queue.","zh":"慢慢走回家可能比在擠迫巴士隊伍中等待壓力小。"},{"en":"If one activity is less stressful, people may choose it to feel calmer.","zh":"如果一項活動壓力較小，人們可能選擇它來讓自己更平靜。"},{"en":"This phrase compares levels of stress.","zh":"這個短語比較壓力程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"corridor","meaning":"走廊","examples":[{"en":"Some visitors find walking less stressful than sitting in a corridor.","zh":"有些訪客覺得步行比坐在走廊壓力小。"},{"en":"A corridor is a long passage inside a building that connects rooms.","zh":"corridor 指建築物內連接房間的長通道。"},{"en":"Students may wait in a corridor before entering an exam room.","zh":"學生可能在進入考試室前在走廊等待。"},{"en":"Sitting in a hospital corridor can feel uncomfortable because people keep passing by.","zh":"坐在醫院走廊可能令人不舒服，因為人們不斷經過。"},{"en":"This word describes an indoor passageway.","zh":"這個字描述室內通道。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"waiting room","meaning":"候診室","examples":[{"en":"A labyrinth may be less stressful than a waiting room.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮可能比候診室壓力小。"},{"en":"A waiting room is a place where people sit until they are called or seen.","zh":"waiting room 指人們坐着等待被叫到或接見的地方。"},{"en":"Patients often wait in a waiting room before seeing a doctor.","zh":"病人在見醫生前通常在候診室等待。"},{"en":"Waiting rooms can feel stressful when people are worried about news or treatment.","zh":"當人們擔心消息或治療時，候診室可能令人有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a waiting area in clinics, hospitals, or offices.","zh":"這個短語描述診所、醫院或辦公室中的等候區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"during their breaks","meaning":"在休息時間","examples":[{"en":"Some doctors walk the labyrinth during their breaks.","zh":"有些醫生在休息時間行走迷宮。"},{"en":"During their breaks means while they are taking short periods of rest from work.","zh":"during their breaks 指在他們短暫停止工作休息期間。"},{"en":"Teachers may drink tea during their breaks between lessons.","zh":"老師可能在課堂之間的休息時間喝茶。"},{"en":"Breaks give workers a chance to recover before returning to duties.","zh":"休息時間給員工機會恢復精神，再回到職責中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what people do in rest periods.","zh":"這個短語描述人們在休息時段做甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"patients who can’t walk","meaning":"不能行走的病人","examples":[{"en":"Patients who can’t walk can use a paper finger labyrinth.","zh":"不能行走的病人可以使用紙製手指迷宮。"},{"en":"Patients who can’t walk are patients who are unable to move on foot because of illness, injury, or disability.","zh":"patients who can’t walk 指因疾病、受傷或殘疾而無法步行的病人。"},{"en":"A hospital may bring activities to patients who can’t walk to the activity room.","zh":"醫院可能把活動帶給不能走到活動室的病人。"},{"en":"If patients cannot walk, tools used by hand can offer an alternative experience.","zh":"如果病人不能行走，用手操作的工具可以提供替代體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies people with limited mobility.","zh":"這個短語指出行動能力受限的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"finger labyrinth","meaning":"手指迷宮","examples":[{"en":"A finger labyrinth can be brought to a patient’s bed.","zh":"手指迷宮可以被帶到病床旁。"},{"en":"A finger labyrinth is a small labyrinth pattern that people trace with a finger instead of walking.","zh":"finger labyrinth 指人們用手指描走，而不是用腳行走的小型迷宮圖案。"},{"en":"A child may use a finger labyrinth on paper to calm down after a stressful moment.","zh":"小朋友在壓力大的時刻後，可能用紙上手指迷宮冷靜下來。"},{"en":"Finger labyrinths let people experience the pattern even when they cannot walk.","zh":"手指迷宮讓不能行走的人也能體驗迷宮圖案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a hand-based version of a labyrinth.","zh":"這個短語描述用手操作的迷宮版本。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be brought to","meaning":"被帶到……","examples":[{"en":"A paper finger labyrinth can be brought to a patient’s bed.","zh":"紙製手指迷宮可以被帶到病床旁。"},{"en":"Be brought to means be carried or taken to a particular place or person.","zh":"be brought to 指被帶到某特定地方或某人身邊。"},{"en":"A nurse may bring medicine to a patient’s room.","zh":"護士可能把藥帶到病人房間。"},{"en":"Bringing an activity to someone helps when they cannot move easily.","zh":"當某人行動不便，把活動帶到他身邊會有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving something towards someone.","zh":"這個短語描述把某物移向某人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the science behind","meaning":"……背後的科學依據","examples":[{"en":"The science behind the theory is a little sketchy.","zh":"這個理論背後的科學依據有點不足。"},{"en":"The science behind something means the research or evidence that explains whether it works.","zh":"science behind something 指解釋某事是否有效的研究或證據。"},{"en":"Students should ask about the science behind a health claim before believing it.","zh":"學生相信健康聲稱前，應先問其背後的科學依據。"},{"en":"If the science behind an idea is weak, people should treat the claim carefully.","zh":"如果某想法背後的科學依據薄弱，人們應謹慎看待該聲稱。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on evidence and explanation.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於證據和解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a little sketchy","meaning":"有點不足；不太充分","examples":[{"en":"The science behind the theory is a little sketchy.","zh":"這個理論背後的科學依據有點不足。"},{"en":"A little sketchy means not fully clear, complete, or reliable.","zh":"a little sketchy 指不完全清楚、完整或可靠。"},{"en":"A student’s essay plan may be a little sketchy if it has ideas but no examples.","zh":"如果學生的文章計劃有想法但沒有例子，就可能有點不充分。"},{"en":"If evidence is sketchy, people should avoid making strong claims.","zh":"如果證據不足，人們應避免作出強烈聲稱。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a mild criticism of quality or certainty.","zh":"這個短語對質素或確定性作出溫和批評。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"small-scale studies","meaning":"小規模研究","examples":[{"en":"There are dozens of small-scale studies on labyrinths.","zh":"關於單一路徑迷宮有數十項小規模研究。"},{"en":"Small-scale studies are research projects involving a limited number of people, places, or cases.","zh":"small-scale studies 指涉及有限人數、地點或案例的研究項目。"},{"en":"A school may run a small-scale study with one class before changing the whole timetable.","zh":"學校更改整個時間表前，可能先用一班學生做小規模研究。"},{"en":"Small studies can suggest useful ideas, but larger studies may be needed for strong proof.","zh":"小型研究可以提出有用想法，但強有力證明可能需要更大型研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited research.","zh":"這個短語描述有限規模的研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"support claims about","meaning":"支持關於……的說法","examples":[{"en":"Small-scale studies support claims about the benefits of labyrinths.","zh":"小規模研究支持關於單一路徑迷宮好處的說法。"},{"en":"To support claims about something means to provide evidence that makes those statements seem more believable.","zh":"support claims about something 指提供證據，使那些說法更可信。"},{"en":"Test results may support claims about a new teaching method.","zh":"測驗結果可能支持關於新教學方法的說法。"},{"en":"Evidence can support a claim without proving it completely.","zh":"證據可以支持某個聲稱，但不一定完全證明它。"},{"en":"This phrase links research with statements people make.","zh":"這個短語把研究與人們作出的說法連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"provide short-term calming","meaning":"提供短期平靜作用","examples":[{"en":"Walking a labyrinth provided short-term calming for Alzheimer’s patients.","zh":"行走單一路徑迷宮為阿茲海默症患者提供短期平靜作用。"},{"en":"Provide short-term calming means help people feel calmer for a limited period.","zh":"provide short-term calming 指幫助人在有限時間內感到較平靜。"},{"en":"Slow breathing may provide short-term calming before a stressful interview.","zh":"慢呼吸可能在壓力大的面試前提供短期平靜作用。"},{"en":"Short-term calming can be useful even if it does not solve the deeper problem.","zh":"即使不能解決深層問題，短期平靜作用仍然有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes temporary relief from stress or agitation.","zh":"這個短語描述暫時紓緩壓力或躁動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"relaxation","meaning":"放鬆","examples":[{"en":"Walking a labyrinth may provide relaxation.","zh":"行走單一路徑迷宮可能帶來放鬆。"},{"en":"Relaxation is a state of feeling calm, rested, and less tense.","zh":"relaxation 指感到平靜、休息好和較不緊張的狀態。"},{"en":"Listening to quiet music can help students find relaxation after exams.","zh":"考試後聽安靜音樂可以幫助學生放鬆。"},{"en":"Relaxation can improve mood and help the body recover from stress.","zh":"放鬆可以改善心情，並幫助身體從壓力中恢復。"},{"en":"This word describes physical and mental easing.","zh":"這個字描述身心上的舒緩。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"relief from anxiety","meaning":"紓緩焦慮","examples":[{"en":"The study found that labyrinth walking provided relief from anxiety.","zh":"研究發現行走單一路徑迷宮能紓緩焦慮。"},{"en":"Relief from anxiety means a reduction in worry, fear, or nervous tension.","zh":"relief from anxiety 指減少擔憂、恐懼或緊張。"},{"en":"Talking to a counsellor may give a student relief from anxiety before exams.","zh":"與輔導員交談可能在考試前給學生焦慮上的紓緩。"},{"en":"Relief does not always remove the problem completely, but it can make it easier to cope.","zh":"紓緩不一定完全移除問題，但可以令它較容易應付。"},{"en":"This phrase describes easing anxious feelings.","zh":"這個短語描述減輕焦慮感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Alzheimer’s patients","meaning":"阿茲海默症患者","examples":[{"en":"Walking a labyrinth may help Alzheimer’s patients.","zh":"行走單一路徑迷宮可能幫助阿茲海默症患者。"},{"en":"Alzheimer’s patients are people with Alzheimer’s disease, a condition that affects memory and thinking.","zh":"Alzheimer’s patients 指患有阿茲海默症的人，這種疾病會影響記憶和思考。"},{"en":"Alzheimer’s patients may need routines, reminders, and calm surroundings.","zh":"阿茲海默症患者可能需要規律、提醒和安靜環境。"},{"en":"Gentle activities may help some patients feel less anxious or restless.","zh":"溫和活動可能幫助一些患者感到較不焦慮或不安。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a group of patients with memory-related illness.","zh":"這個短語指出患有記憶相關疾病的病人群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"what is it about","meaning":"到底是甚麼特質使……","examples":[{"en":"What is it about labyrinths that makes their appeal so universal?","zh":"到底是單一路徑迷宮的甚麼特質使它們有如此普世的吸引力？"},{"en":"What is it about something that...? asks which quality or feature causes a particular effect.","zh":"What is it about something that...? 用來問某物哪種品質或特徵造成某種效果。"},{"en":"What is it about music that makes people remember old memories?","zh":"到底是音樂的甚麼特質使人記起舊回憶？"},{"en":"This question looks for the special reason behind an attraction or reaction.","zh":"這個問題尋找吸引力或反應背後的特別原因。"},{"en":"It is useful when exploring why something affects people strongly.","zh":"探討某事為何強烈影響人時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"appeal","meaning":"吸引力","examples":[{"en":"Labyrinths have a universal appeal.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮具有普世吸引力。"},{"en":"Appeal is the power to attract interest, attention, or liking.","zh":"appeal 指吸引興趣、注意或喜愛的力量。"},{"en":"A quiet garden may have appeal for people who want to escape noise.","zh":"安靜花園對想逃離噪音的人可能有吸引力。"},{"en":"Something with strong appeal can attract people from different ages and cultures.","zh":"具有強大吸引力的東西可以吸引不同年齡和文化的人。"},{"en":"This word describes attractiveness or interest.","zh":"這個字描述吸引力或興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"universal","meaning":"普遍的；具普世性的","examples":[{"en":"The appeal of labyrinths seems universal.","zh":"單一路徑迷宮的吸引力似乎具普世性。"},{"en":"Universal means existing, understood, or felt by people everywhere or almost everywhere.","zh":"universal 指存在於、被理解於或被感受到於各地或幾乎各地的人。"},{"en":"The need for friendship is often seen as universal.","zh":"對友誼的需要常被視為具普世性。"},{"en":"If an idea is universal, it can speak to people beyond one culture or period.","zh":"如果一個想法是普世的，它可以觸及超越單一文化或時期的人。"},{"en":"This word describes something with very wide human reach.","zh":"這個字描述具有非常廣泛人類觸及面的事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 12 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/listening/Practice 13/task-1":[{"front":"Jane Fairbanks speaking","meaning":"我是 Jane Fairbanks；Jane Fairbanks 在聽","examples":[{"en":"Jane answers the phone by saying, “Jane Fairbanks speaking.”","zh":"Jane接電話時說：「我是Jane Fairbanks。」"},{"en":"“Jane Fairbanks speaking” is a formal way to identify yourself when answering the phone.","zh":"Jane Fairbanks speaking是接電話時正式表明自己身份的說法。"},{"en":"A receptionist may answer, “Central Library, Anna Lee speaking,” so callers know who they are talking to.","zh":"接待員可能接電話說：「中央圖書館，Anna Lee在聽」，讓來電者知道正在與誰通話。"},{"en":"Giving your name clearly at the start of a call helps the conversation begin smoothly.","zh":"在電話開始時清楚說出自己的名字，有助對話順利開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and common in work or official phone calls.","zh":"這個短語有禮，常見於工作或正式電話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"I’ve just retired","meaning":"我剛退休","examples":[{"en":"Frank has just retired and moved to Southoe.","zh":"Frank剛退休並搬到Southoe。"},{"en":"I’ve just retired means I have recently stopped working, usually because I reached retirement age.","zh":"I’ve just retired意思是我最近停止工作，通常因為已到退休年齡。"},{"en":"A teacher who has just retired may want to spend more time travelling or volunteering.","zh":"剛退休的老師可能想花更多時間旅行或做義工。"},{"en":"Retirement can create free time, so people may look for new activities in the community.","zh":"退休可以帶來空閒時間，所以人們可能在社區尋找新活動。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a recent life change.","zh":"這個短語解釋近期的人生變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"move to","meaning":"搬到……","examples":[{"en":"Frank has moved to Southoe after retiring.","zh":"Frank退休後搬到Southoe。"},{"en":"To move to a place means to go and live there.","zh":"move to某地，意思是搬去那裡居住。"},{"en":"A family may move to a quieter town when the parents start working from home.","zh":"父母開始在家工作後，一個家庭可能搬到較安靜的小鎮。"},{"en":"Moving to a new place often means finding new friends, services and routines.","zh":"搬到新地方通常意味着要尋找新朋友、服務和生活規律。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing where one lives.","zh":"這個短語描述居住地的改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"become a volunteer","meaning":"成為義工","examples":[{"en":"Frank would like to become a volunteer in the village.","zh":"Frank想在村內成為義工。"},{"en":"To become a volunteer means to start helping without being paid.","zh":"become a volunteer意思是開始無償幫助別人。"},{"en":"A student may become a volunteer at an animal shelter during the holidays.","zh":"學生可能在假期成為動物收容所義工。"},{"en":"People become volunteers when they want to use their time to support others.","zh":"當人們想用自己的時間支援他人，就會成為義工。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking on an unpaid service role.","zh":"這個短語描述承擔無薪服務角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"I gather","meaning":"我聽說；我了解到","examples":[{"en":"Frank gathers that Jane co-ordinates voluntary work in the village.","zh":"Frank了解到Jane統籌村內義工工作。"},{"en":"I gather means I understand or have heard from the information available.","zh":"I gather意思是我從現有資訊中了解到或聽說。"},{"en":"I gather from the notice that the meeting has been moved to Friday.","zh":"我從通告了解到會議已改到星期五。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they are politely checking whether their understanding is correct.","zh":"人們在有禮地確認自己理解是否正確時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It sounds more careful than saying “I know”.","zh":"它比直接說I know更謹慎。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"co-ordinate voluntary work","meaning":"統籌義工工作","examples":[{"en":"Jane co-ordinates voluntary work in the village.","zh":"Jane統籌村內義工工作。"},{"en":"To co-ordinate voluntary work means to organise volunteer tasks, people and schedules.","zh":"co-ordinate voluntary work意思是組織義工任務、人手和時間表。"},{"en":"A school may need someone to co-ordinate voluntary work for open day helpers.","zh":"學校可能需要有人統籌開放日幫手的義工工作。"},{"en":"Good co-ordination prevents confusion because volunteers know where to go and what to do.","zh":"良好統籌能防止混亂，因為義工知道要去哪裡和做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising unpaid community service.","zh":"這個短語描述組織無薪社區服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"voluntary work","meaning":"義務工作；義工服務","examples":[{"en":"Frank wants to get involved in voluntary work.","zh":"Frank想參與義工服務。"},{"en":"Voluntary work is unpaid work done to help other people or the community.","zh":"voluntary work是為幫助他人或社區而做的無薪工作。"},{"en":"Helping at a charity shop on weekends is a form of voluntary work.","zh":"週末在慈善商店幫忙是一種義工服務。"},{"en":"Voluntary work can give people experience, friendships and a sense of purpose.","zh":"義工服務可以給人經驗、友誼和目標感。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to service done by choice, not for salary.","zh":"這個短語指自願做的服務，而不是為薪金而做。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the village","meaning":"在村內","examples":[{"en":"Jane co-ordinates voluntary work in the village.","zh":"Jane在村內統籌義工工作。"},{"en":"In the village means within the local village community.","zh":"in the village意思是在本地村落社區內。"},{"en":"New residents may join activities in the village to meet neighbours.","zh":"新居民可能參加村內活動來認識鄰居。"},{"en":"Services in the village are often supported by people who know the local area well.","zh":"村內服務通常由熟悉本地的人支援。"},{"en":"This phrase places the activity inside a small local community.","zh":"這個短語把活動放在小型本地社區中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"that’s right","meaning":"沒錯","examples":[{"en":"Jane confirms Frank’s understanding by saying, “That’s right.”","zh":"Jane說「沒錯」，確認Frank的理解。"},{"en":"That’s right means what you said is correct.","zh":"that’s right意思是你所說的是正確的。"},{"en":"If a student says the exam starts at nine, the teacher may reply, “That’s right.”","zh":"如果學生說考試九點開始，老師可能回答：「沒錯。」"},{"en":"This phrase confirms information and keeps the conversation moving.","zh":"這個短語確認資訊，並讓對話繼續。"},{"en":"It is a simple, polite way to agree with someone’s statement.","zh":"它是同意某人陳述的簡單有禮方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what sort of thing","meaning":"哪一類事情","examples":[{"en":"Frank asks what sort of thing he could do as a volunteer.","zh":"Frank問自己作為義工可以做哪一類事情。"},{"en":"What sort of thing means what kind of activity, task or option.","zh":"what sort of thing意思是哪一類活動、任務或選項。"},{"en":"A new student may ask what sort of thing happens at the drama club.","zh":"新學生可能問戲劇學會會做哪一類事情。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone wants examples rather than a general answer.","zh":"當某人想要例子而不是一般答案時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It sounds natural and conversational.","zh":"它聽起來自然且口語化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"need help with","meaning":"需要協助處理……","examples":[{"en":"The village library needs help from volunteers.","zh":"村圖書館需要義工協助。"},{"en":"To need help with something means to require support in doing that task.","zh":"need help with某事，意思是需要支援去完成該任務。"},{"en":"A school fair may need help with setting up tables and serving food.","zh":"學校賣物會可能需要協助擺放桌子和供應食物。"},{"en":"Asking for help allows a task to be completed faster and more smoothly.","zh":"尋求協助能讓任務更快、更順利完成。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the area where assistance is needed.","zh":"這個短語引入需要幫忙的範疇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the village library","meaning":"村圖書館","examples":[{"en":"Frank may be able to help with the village library.","zh":"Frank可能可以協助村圖書館。"},{"en":"The village library is a small local library serving people in the village.","zh":"village library是服務村內居民的小型本地圖書館。"},{"en":"A village library may lend books, organise reading groups and provide a quiet place to study.","zh":"村圖書館可能借出書籍、舉辦閱讀小組並提供安靜溫習地方。"},{"en":"Small libraries often depend on volunteers because budgets and staff are limited.","zh":"小型圖書館通常依靠義工，因為預算和人手有限。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a community book service in a village.","zh":"這個短語指村內的社區書籍服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"borrow books from","meaning":"從……借書","examples":[{"en":"The village library borrows books from the town library.","zh":"村圖書館從鎮圖書館借書。"},{"en":"To borrow books from somewhere means to take books temporarily and return them later.","zh":"borrow books from某處，意思是暫時取用書籍並日後歸還。"},{"en":"Students borrow books from the school library when they need sources for a project.","zh":"學生需要專題資料時，會從學校圖書館借書。"},{"en":"Borrowing helps small libraries offer more choice without buying every book.","zh":"借書能幫助小型圖書館提供更多選擇，而不必購買每本書。"},{"en":"This phrase describes temporary use, not permanent ownership.","zh":"這個短語描述暫時使用，而不是永久擁有。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the town library","meaning":"鎮圖書館","examples":[{"en":"The village library borrows books from the town library.","zh":"村圖書館從鎮圖書館借書。"},{"en":"The town library is a larger public library in the nearby town.","zh":"town library是附近城鎮中較大型的公共圖書館。"},{"en":"A town library may have more books, staff and services than a small village library.","zh":"鎮圖書館可能比小型村圖書館有更多書、人手和服務。"},{"en":"Sharing books with a town library can help smaller communities access more reading materials.","zh":"與鎮圖書館共享書籍，可以幫助較小社區取得更多閱讀材料。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a public library serving a town.","zh":"這個短語指出服務城鎮的公共圖書館。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"donate books","meaning":"捐書","examples":[{"en":"Individuals also donate books to the village library.","zh":"個別人士也會向村圖書館捐書。"},{"en":"To donate books means to give books without asking for payment.","zh":"donate books意思是無償把書送出。"},{"en":"Families may donate books their children have outgrown to a school library.","zh":"家庭可能把孩子已不再閱讀的書捐給學校圖書館。"},{"en":"Book donations can help libraries grow their collections at low cost.","zh":"捐書可以幫助圖書館以低成本增加藏書。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving books for public or charitable use.","zh":"這個短語描述把書捐作公共或慈善用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"get involved in","meaning":"參與……","examples":[{"en":"Frank could get involved in collecting books.","zh":"Frank可以參與收集書籍。"},{"en":"To get involved in something means to take part in it actively.","zh":"get involved in某事，意思是積極參與其中。"},{"en":"A student may get involved in the school newspaper by writing short articles.","zh":"學生可能透過寫短文章參與校報。"},{"en":"Getting involved helps newcomers meet people and learn how a community works.","zh":"參與活動幫助新來者認識人並了解社區如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active participation, not just watching.","zh":"這個短語描述主動參與，而不只是旁觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"collecting books","meaning":"收集書籍","examples":[{"en":"One volunteer task involves collecting books.","zh":"其中一項義工任務涉及收集書籍。"},{"en":"Collecting books means gathering books from different places or people.","zh":"collecting books意思是從不同地方或人士收集書本。"},{"en":"Volunteers may collect books from homes and bring them to the library.","zh":"義工可能從居民家中收集書籍並帶到圖書館。"},{"en":"Collecting donated books helps libraries sort, record and share them with readers.","zh":"收集捐贈書籍能幫助圖書館分類、記錄並與讀者分享。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical task in a library or charity project.","zh":"這個短語描述圖書館或慈善項目中的實際任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"if you’ve got a car","meaning":"如果你有車","examples":[{"en":"Frank can help collect books if he has a car.","zh":"如果Frank有車，他可以幫忙收集書籍。"},{"en":"If you’ve got a car means if you own or have access to a car.","zh":"if you’ve got a car意思是如果你擁有或可以使用汽車。"},{"en":"If you’ve got a car, you can help transport boxes to the community centre.","zh":"如果你有車，你可以幫忙把箱子運到社區中心。"},{"en":"Having a car matters when the task involves carrying heavy items or travelling between places.","zh":"當任務涉及搬運重物或往返不同地方，有車就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a condition for being able to help.","zh":"這個短語提出能否幫忙的條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"that is","meaning":"也就是說；前提是","examples":[{"en":"Jane adds, “if you’ve got a car, that is.”","zh":"Jane補充說：「前提是你有車。」"},{"en":"That is can mean in other words or to be more exact.","zh":"that is可以表示換言之，或更準確地說。"},{"en":"You can join the trip, if you are free on Saturday, that is.","zh":"你可以參加旅行，前提是你星期六有空。"},{"en":"This phrase adds a condition or clarification after a statement.","zh":"這個短語在陳述後加入條件或澄清。"},{"en":"It helps the speaker correct or narrow what they have just said.","zh":"它幫助說話者修正或收窄剛才所說的內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"that’s no problem","meaning":"那沒問題","examples":[{"en":"Frank says that having a car is no problem.","zh":"Frank說有車那沒問題。"},{"en":"That’s no problem means it is easy, acceptable or not an issue.","zh":"that’s no problem意思是那很容易、可以接受或不是問題。"},{"en":"If someone asks whether you can arrive at ten, you may say, “That’s no problem.”","zh":"如果有人問你可否十點到，你可以說：「那沒問題。」"},{"en":"This phrase reassures the other person that their request can be handled.","zh":"這個短語讓對方放心，表示其要求可以處理。"},{"en":"It is common in polite everyday conversation.","zh":"它常見於有禮的日常對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pretty flexible","meaning":"頗有彈性","examples":[{"en":"The times for collecting books are pretty flexible.","zh":"收集書籍的時間頗有彈性。"},{"en":"Pretty flexible means quite able to change according to someone’s needs.","zh":"pretty flexible意思是頗能根據某人的需要作出改變。"},{"en":"A part-time job with pretty flexible hours is useful for students.","zh":"工時頗有彈性的兼職工作對學生很有用。"},{"en":"Flexible arrangements make it easier for volunteers to fit tasks around their lives.","zh":"彈性安排讓義工更容易把任務配合自己的生活。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests there is room for adjustment.","zh":"這個短語暗示有調整空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"arrange it to suit you","meaning":"按你的時間安排","examples":[{"en":"Jane can arrange the volunteer work to suit Frank.","zh":"Jane可以按Frank的時間安排義工工作。"},{"en":"To arrange it to suit you means to organise it in a way that fits your time or needs.","zh":"arrange it to suit you意思是以符合你時間或需要的方式安排。"},{"en":"A tutor may arrange lessons to suit a student’s school timetable.","zh":"補習老師可能按學生的學校時間表安排課堂。"},{"en":"Flexible arrangements make people more willing to take part.","zh":"彈性安排會令人更願意參與。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when someone offers personalised timing or planning.","zh":"這個短語用於有人提供個人化時間或計劃時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the records that we keep","meaning":"我們保存的記錄","examples":[{"en":"Jane explains the records that the library keeps.","zh":"Jane解釋圖書館保存的記錄。"},{"en":"The records that we keep are the written or computerised information we store and update.","zh":"the records that we keep是我們保存和更新的書面或電腦化資料。"},{"en":"A school keeps records of attendance, marks and parent contact details.","zh":"學校保存出席率、分數和家長聯絡資料的記錄。"},{"en":"Keeping records helps an organisation know what it owns, receives or must return.","zh":"保存記錄幫助機構知道自己擁有、收到或必須歸還甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised information used for management.","zh":"這個短語指用於管理的有組織資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be given books","meaning":"收到別人贈送的書","examples":[{"en":"The library keeps records of the books it is given.","zh":"圖書館保存收到別人贈送的書的記錄。"},{"en":"To be given books means to receive books from someone as a donation or gift.","zh":"be given books意思是從某人那裡收到作為捐贈或禮物的書。"},{"en":"A classroom may be given books by parents at the end of the school year.","zh":"學年結束時，課室可能收到家長贈送的書。"},{"en":"If a library is given books, it needs to record who donated them and what condition they are in.","zh":"如果圖書館收到贈書，就需要記錄誰捐贈以及書的狀況。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on receiving books, not buying them.","zh":"這個短語著重收到書，而不是購買書。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"need to return","meaning":"需要歸還","examples":[{"en":"The library keeps records of books it needs to return.","zh":"圖書館保存需要歸還的書的記錄。"},{"en":"To need to return something means to have to give it back to its owner or original place.","zh":"need to return某物，意思是必須把它交還物主或原來地方。"},{"en":"Students need to return borrowed sports equipment after the lesson.","zh":"學生課後需要歸還借用的運動器材。"},{"en":"Records help people remember what must be returned and by when.","zh":"記錄幫助人記得甚麼必須歸還，以及何時歸還。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an obligation to give something back.","zh":"這個短語描述把某物交回去的責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"keep records up to date","meaning":"保持記錄更新","examples":[{"en":"The library needs help keeping its records up to date.","zh":"圖書館需要幫忙保持記錄更新。"},{"en":"To keep records up to date means to make sure stored information is current and accurate.","zh":"keep records up to date意思是確保存檔資料是最新和準確的。"},{"en":"A clinic must keep patient records up to date so doctors have the right information.","zh":"診所必須保持病人記錄更新，讓醫生有正確資訊。"},{"en":"Out-of-date records can cause mistakes, delays or lost items.","zh":"過時記錄可以造成錯誤、延誤或物品遺失。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in administration and office work.","zh":"這個短語常見於行政和辦公室工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be used to working on","meaning":"習慣使用……工作","examples":[{"en":"Frank is used to working on a computer.","zh":"Frank習慣使用電腦工作。"},{"en":"To be used to working on something means to be familiar and comfortable with using it for work.","zh":"be used to working on某物，意思是熟悉並習慣用它工作。"},{"en":"A designer is used to working on digital software for many hours.","zh":"設計師習慣長時間使用數碼軟件工作。"},{"en":"If someone is used to a tool, they usually need less training to use it well.","zh":"如果某人習慣使用某工具，通常較少需要培訓就能好好使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes familiarity gained through experience.","zh":"這個短語描述透過經驗而來的熟悉感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"work on a computer","meaning":"使用電腦工作","examples":[{"en":"Frank is used to working on a computer.","zh":"Frank習慣使用電腦工作。"},{"en":"To work on a computer means to use a computer to complete tasks.","zh":"work on a computer意思是使用電腦完成任務。"},{"en":"Office workers often work on a computer to write emails, update files and prepare reports.","zh":"辦公室員工常使用電腦工作，例如寫電郵、更新檔案和準備報告。"},{"en":"Computer work can make record-keeping faster and easier to search.","zh":"電腦工作可以令記錄保存更快，也更容易搜尋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using digital tools for work.","zh":"這個短語描述使用數碼工具工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"I presume","meaning":"我推測；我想","examples":[{"en":"Frank presumes that the library records are computerised.","zh":"Frank推測圖書館記錄已電腦化。"},{"en":"I presume means I suppose something is true based on what I know.","zh":"I presume意思是根據我所知道的情況，我推測某事屬實。"},{"en":"I presume the meeting is in the hall because the classroom is too small.","zh":"我想會議在禮堂舉行，因為課室太小。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite when checking an assumption.","zh":"這個短語在確認假設時很有禮。"},{"en":"It sounds careful because the speaker is not completely certain.","zh":"它聽起來謹慎，因為說話者不是完全肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be computerised","meaning":"電腦化","examples":[{"en":"The library records are computerised.","zh":"圖書館記錄已電腦化。"},{"en":"To be computerised means to be stored or managed using computers.","zh":"be computerised意思是使用電腦儲存或管理。"},{"en":"A hospital’s appointment system may be computerised so staff can find bookings quickly.","zh":"醫院預約系統可能已電腦化，讓員工快速找到預約。"},{"en":"Computerised records are easier to search, update and share.","zh":"電腦化記錄較容易搜尋、更新和分享。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving from paper systems to digital systems.","zh":"這個短語描述由紙本系統轉向數碼系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"purpose-built","meaning":"專門建造的","examples":[{"en":"Frank asks whether the library is purpose-built.","zh":"Frank問圖書館是否是專門建造的。"},{"en":"Purpose-built means specially designed and built for a particular use.","zh":"purpose-built意思是為某特定用途專門設計和建造的。"},{"en":"A purpose-built sports centre has spaces made specifically for training and competitions.","zh":"專門建造的體育中心有特別為訓練和比賽而設的空間。"},{"en":"Purpose-built buildings often work better because their design matches their function.","zh":"專門建造的建築通常更好用，因為設計配合功能。"},{"en":"This word contrasts with a place that is simply adapted for use.","zh":"這個詞與只是改作某用途的地方形成對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"notice something","meaning":"留意到某物","examples":[{"en":"Frank has not noticed the library when walking round the village.","zh":"Frank在村內四處走時沒有留意到圖書館。"},{"en":"To notice something means to see it or become aware of it.","zh":"notice something意思是看見或意識到某物。"},{"en":"A student may not notice a small spelling mistake until the teacher points it out.","zh":"學生可能直到老師指出，才留意到小串字錯誤。"},{"en":"People fail to notice things when they are hidden, ordinary or not clearly marked.","zh":"當東西被隱藏、很普通或標示不清，人們就可能沒有留意到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming aware through sight or attention.","zh":"這個短語描述透過視覺或注意而意識到某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"walk round","meaning":"四處走走；在……逛","examples":[{"en":"Frank has walked round the village without noticing the library.","zh":"Frank在村內四處走，卻沒有留意到圖書館。"},{"en":"To walk round a place means to walk around it and look at different parts.","zh":"walk round某地，意思是在那裡四處步行並看看不同部分。"},{"en":"New students may walk round the campus to find classrooms before term starts.","zh":"新學生可能在開學前到校園四處走走，尋找課室。"},{"en":"Walking round an area helps people become familiar with local buildings and routes.","zh":"在某區四處走走能幫助人熟悉本地建築和路線。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exploring a place on foot.","zh":"這個短語描述步行探索某地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have the use of","meaning":"可使用……","examples":[{"en":"The library has the use of a room in the village hall.","zh":"圖書館可使用村民會堂內的一個房間。"},{"en":"To have the use of something means to be allowed to use it, even if you do not own it.","zh":"have the use of某物，意思是獲准使用它，即使你不擁有它。"},{"en":"A club may have the use of a classroom every Friday afternoon.","zh":"社團可能每星期五下午可使用一間課室。"},{"en":"Having the use of a shared space helps small groups operate without buying a building.","zh":"可使用共享空間能幫助小團體運作，而不用購買建築物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes permission to use a place or facility.","zh":"這個短語描述使用地方或設施的許可。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a room in the village hall","meaning":"村民會堂內的一個房間","examples":[{"en":"The library uses a room in the village hall.","zh":"圖書館使用村民會堂內的一個房間。"},{"en":"A room in the village hall is one space inside a community building used by villagers.","zh":"a room in the village hall是村民使用的社區建築內的一個空間。"},{"en":"A youth group may meet in a room in the village hall after school.","zh":"青年小組可能放學後在村民會堂內的一個房間聚會。"},{"en":"Shared rooms allow several local services to use the same building.","zh":"共用房間讓多項本地服務使用同一座建築物。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific community space.","zh":"這個短語指出一個特定社區空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the West Room","meaning":"West Room 房間","examples":[{"en":"The library is in the West Room of the village hall.","zh":"圖書館位於村民會堂的West Room房間。"},{"en":"The West Room is the name of a particular room, probably located in the west part of the hall.","zh":"West Room是一個特定房間的名稱，可能位於會堂西面部分。"},{"en":"Visitors may be told to meet in the West Room before the talk begins.","zh":"訪客可能被告知在講座開始前到West Room集合。"},{"en":"Giving a room name helps people find the right place inside a larger building.","zh":"提供房間名稱能幫助人在較大建築物內找到正確地方。"},{"en":"This phrase functions like a location label.","zh":"這個短語像位置標籤一樣使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on the left as you go in","meaning":"進去後在左邊","examples":[{"en":"The West Room is on the left as you go in.","zh":"West Room進去後在左邊。"},{"en":"On the left as you go in means on the left-hand side when you enter.","zh":"on the left as you go in意思是你進入時在左手邊。"},{"en":"The school office is on the left as you go in through the main entrance.","zh":"從正門進去後，校務處在左邊。"},{"en":"Clear directions help newcomers find places without needing to ask again.","zh":"清晰方向能幫助新來者找到地方，而不必再問。"},{"en":"This phrase gives simple indoor directions.","zh":"這個短語提供簡單室內方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"go and have a look","meaning":"去看一看","examples":[{"en":"Frank says he must go and have a look inside the hall.","zh":"Frank說他必須去會堂裏面看一看。"},{"en":"To go and have a look means to visit a place and see it for yourself.","zh":"go and have a look意思是親自去某地方看看。"},{"en":"A student may go and have a look at the noticeboard to check club times.","zh":"學生可能去通告板看一看，以查核社團時間。"},{"en":"Looking in person can help people understand a place better than just hearing about it.","zh":"親身查看可以比只聽別人描述更了解一個地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and practical.","zh":"這個短語較口語而實用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"inside the hall","meaning":"在會堂裏面","examples":[{"en":"Frank wants to look inside the village hall.","zh":"Frank想看看村民會堂裏面。"},{"en":"Inside the hall means within the interior part of the hall building.","zh":"inside the hall意思是在會堂建築物的內部。"},{"en":"The concert audience waited inside the hall because it was raining outside.","zh":"因為外面下雨，音樂會觀眾在會堂裏面等候。"},{"en":"Some rooms or signs cannot be seen until you go inside the hall.","zh":"有些房間或指示牌要進入會堂裏面才看得到。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the inside of a building with the outside.","zh":"這個短語把建築物內部與外部作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"run a lunch club","meaning":"開辦長者午餐會","examples":[{"en":"The village runs a lunch club for elderly people.","zh":"村內為長者開辦午餐會。"},{"en":"To run a lunch club means to organise regular meals and social gatherings for a group.","zh":"run a lunch club意思是為某群體組織定期膳食和社交聚會。"},{"en":"A community centre may run a lunch club for older residents who live alone.","zh":"社區中心可能為獨居長者開辦午餐會。"},{"en":"Lunch clubs can reduce loneliness by giving people food and company.","zh":"午餐會可以透過提供食物和陪伴來減少孤獨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising an ongoing community service.","zh":"這個短語描述組織持續社區服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"elderly people","meaning":"長者","examples":[{"en":"The lunch club is for elderly people.","zh":"午餐會是為長者而設。"},{"en":"Elderly people are older adults, especially those who may need extra care or support.","zh":"elderly people是年紀較大的成年人，尤其是可能需要額外照顧或支援的人。"},{"en":"Elderly people may need help with transport, shopping or medical appointments.","zh":"長者可能需要交通、購物或醫療預約方面的幫助。"},{"en":"Community activities help elderly people stay connected and active.","zh":"社區活動幫助長者保持連繫和活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite but should be used respectfully.","zh":"這個短語有禮，但使用時應保持尊重。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a lot of places do","meaning":"很多地方都有這樣做","examples":[{"en":"Frank knows that a lot of places run lunch clubs.","zh":"Frank知道很多地方都有開辦午餐會。"},{"en":"A lot of places do means many towns, villages or organisations do the same thing.","zh":"a lot of places do意思是許多城鎮、村落或機構都做同一件事。"},{"en":"A lot of places offer recycling points near supermarkets.","zh":"很多地方都在超市附近提供回收點。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an activity is common, not unusual.","zh":"這個短語顯示某活動很常見，而不是罕見。"},{"en":"It is a conversational way to refer to many examples.","zh":"它是以口語方式指很多例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a very successful club","meaning":"很成功的會社；很成功的活動","examples":[{"en":"The village has a very successful lunch club.","zh":"村內有一個很成功的午餐會。"},{"en":"A very successful club is a club that works well and attracts or helps many people.","zh":"a very successful club是運作良好並吸引或幫助很多人的會社或活動。"},{"en":"A reading club may be very successful if students keep attending every week.","zh":"如果學生每星期持續出席，閱讀會可能很成功。"},{"en":"Successful clubs usually meet a real need and are well organised.","zh":"成功的會社通常滿足真實需要，而且組織良好。"},{"en":"This phrase praises how well a group or activity is doing.","zh":"這個短語讚賞一個團體或活動運作得很好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"help with transport","meaning":"協助交通接送","examples":[{"en":"Frank could help with transport for the lunch club.","zh":"Frank可以為午餐會協助交通接送。"},{"en":"To help with transport means to assist by driving people or arranging travel.","zh":"help with transport意思是透過駕車接送或安排交通來協助。"},{"en":"Volunteers may help with transport by taking elderly residents to medical appointments.","zh":"義工可能透過接送長者去覆診來協助交通。"},{"en":"Transport help matters when people cannot drive or public buses are limited.","zh":"當人們不能駕車或公共巴士有限，交通協助很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical travel support.","zh":"這個短語描述實際交通支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"if that’s of any use","meaning":"如果那有用的話","examples":[{"en":"Frank offers to help with transport if that is of any use.","zh":"Frank表示如果那有用的話，他可以協助交通接送。"},{"en":"If that’s of any use means if that would be helpful.","zh":"if that’s of any use意思是如果那會有幫助的話。"},{"en":"I can bring extra chairs, if that’s of any use.","zh":"如果那有用的話，我可以帶額外椅子來。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds modest because the speaker offers help without assuming it is needed.","zh":"這個短語聽起來謙遜，因為說話者提供幫助但不假定一定需要。"},{"en":"It is common when politely offering assistance.","zh":"它常見於有禮地提供協助時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"from neighbouring villages","meaning":"來自鄰近村落","examples":[{"en":"Some people come to the club from neighbouring villages.","zh":"有些人來自鄰近村落參加午餐會。"},{"en":"From neighbouring villages means from nearby villages.","zh":"from neighbouring villages意思是來自附近村落。"},{"en":"Students may travel from neighbouring villages to attend the only secondary school in the area.","zh":"學生可能從鄰近村落前往區內唯一一間中學上課。"},{"en":"People from nearby places may depend on the same community service.","zh":"來自附近地方的人可能依賴同一項社區服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where participants come from.","zh":"這個短語描述參與者來自哪裡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be in need of","meaning":"需要……","examples":[{"en":"The lunch club is always in need of more drivers.","zh":"午餐會一直需要更多司機。"},{"en":"To be in need of something means to require it because there is not enough.","zh":"be in need of某物，意思是因不足夠而需要它。"},{"en":"A school charity sale may be in need of more volunteers before opening day.","zh":"學校慈善義賣在開放日前可能需要更多義工。"},{"en":"When a group is in need of help, extra support can keep the service running.","zh":"當團體需要幫助，額外支援可以令服務繼續運作。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds slightly formal and polite.","zh":"這個短語聽起來略為正式而有禮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"more drivers","meaning":"更多司機","examples":[{"en":"The lunch club needs more drivers to help with transport.","zh":"午餐會需要更多司機協助交通接送。"},{"en":"More drivers means additional people who can drive vehicles for a service or event.","zh":"more drivers意思是額外可以駕車支援服務或活動的人。"},{"en":"A school trip may need more drivers if there are many students and few buses.","zh":"如果學生很多而巴士很少，學校旅行可能需要更多司機。"},{"en":"Extra drivers reduce waiting time and make transport safer and more reliable.","zh":"額外司機可以減少等候時間，令交通更安全和可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a practical staffing need.","zh":"這個短語指出實際人手需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"focus on a particular hobby","meaning":"專注於某項特定興趣","examples":[{"en":"Some groups focus on a particular hobby.","zh":"有些小組專注於某項特定興趣。"},{"en":"To focus on a particular hobby means to centre activities around one specific interest.","zh":"focus on a particular hobby意思是以一項特定興趣為活動中心。"},{"en":"A photography group may focus on a particular hobby by organising photo walks every month.","zh":"攝影小組可能透過每月舉辦攝影散步來專注於某項興趣。"},{"en":"Groups with a clear focus attract people who share the same interest.","zh":"有清晰焦點的小組能吸引有相同興趣的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a club organised around one activity.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞一項活動組織的社團。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get involved in one or two","meaning":"參與一兩個","examples":[{"en":"Frank could get involved in one or two hobby groups.","zh":"Frank可以參與一兩個興趣小組。"},{"en":"To get involved in one or two means to take part in a small number of activities.","zh":"get involved in one or two意思是參與少數幾項活動。"},{"en":"A new student may get involved in one or two clubs before joining more.","zh":"新學生可能先參與一兩個社團，再加入更多。"},{"en":"Starting with one or two activities helps people avoid becoming too busy.","zh":"先從一兩項活動開始，可以幫助人避免太忙。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests limited but active participation.","zh":"這個短語暗示有限但主動的參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"particularly if","meaning":"尤其是如果……","examples":[{"en":"Frank is interested in helping, particularly if there are art groups.","zh":"Frank有興趣幫忙，尤其是如果有藝術小組。"},{"en":"Particularly if means especially if a certain condition is true.","zh":"particularly if意思是尤其在某條件成立時。"},{"en":"A student may join a summer camp, particularly if it includes outdoor activities.","zh":"學生可能參加暑期營，尤其是如果它包括戶外活動。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the condition that makes someone more interested.","zh":"這個短語突顯令某人更感興趣的條件。"},{"en":"It is useful when one possibility is more attractive than others.","zh":"當某個可能性比其他更吸引時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"art groups","meaning":"藝術小組","examples":[{"en":"Frank is particularly interested in art groups.","zh":"Frank尤其對藝術小組感興趣。"},{"en":"Art groups are groups of people who meet to practise, discuss or enjoy art.","zh":"art groups是人們聚在一起練習、討論或欣賞藝術的小組。"},{"en":"An art group may paint landscapes, visit galleries or invite local artists to teach.","zh":"藝術小組可能畫風景、參觀畫廊或邀請本地藝術家教學。"},{"en":"Art groups help people share creativity and learn from one another.","zh":"藝術小組幫助人們分享創意並互相學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes community groups centred on visual or creative art.","zh":"這個短語描述以視覺或創意藝術為中心的社區小組。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"find out where","meaning":"查明哪裏……","examples":[{"en":"Jane will find out where the village needs help.","zh":"Jane會查明村裏哪裏需要幫忙。"},{"en":"To find out where help is needed means to discover which place, group or task requires support.","zh":"find out where help is needed意思是找出哪個地方、團體或任務需要支援。"},{"en":"A teacher may find out where students need help by checking their homework mistakes.","zh":"老師可能透過檢查功課錯誤，查明學生哪裏需要幫忙。"},{"en":"Finding out the exact need prevents people from wasting time on the wrong task.","zh":"查明確切需要能防止人把時間浪費在錯誤任務上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gathering information before arranging help.","zh":"這個短語描述在安排幫忙前收集資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get back to you","meaning":"再回覆你；再聯絡你","examples":[{"en":"Jane will get back to Frank after finding out where help is needed.","zh":"Jane查明哪裏需要幫忙後會再回覆Frank。"},{"en":"To get back to you means to contact you later with an answer or more information.","zh":"get back to you意思是之後再聯絡你，提供答案或更多資料。"},{"en":"A receptionist may say, “I’ll check the booking and get back to you this afternoon.”","zh":"接待員可能說：「我會查核預訂，今天下午再回覆你。」"},{"en":"This phrase is polite when someone cannot answer immediately.","zh":"當某人不能立即回答時，這個短語很有禮。"},{"en":"It shows that a follow-up response will come later.","zh":"它顯示之後會有跟進回覆。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"individual residents","meaning":"個別居民","examples":[{"en":"Frank asks about help for individual residents.","zh":"Frank詢問關於幫助個別居民的事。"},{"en":"Individual residents are separate people living in a community, rather than a whole group.","zh":"individual residents是住在社區中的個別人士，而不是整個群體。"},{"en":"A volunteer scheme may help individual residents with shopping or hospital visits.","zh":"義工計劃可能協助個別居民購物或去醫院覆診。"},{"en":"Helping individuals can solve personal problems that general community services miss.","zh":"幫助個別人士可以解決一般社區服務未能照顧的個人問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on one resident at a time.","zh":"這個短語著重每次一位居民。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"arrange that","meaning":"安排那件事","examples":[{"en":"Frank asks whether Jane arranges help for individual residents.","zh":"Frank問Jane是否為個別居民安排那件事。"},{"en":"To arrange that means to organise that particular thing.","zh":"arrange that意思是組織或安排剛才提到的特定事情。"},{"en":"If a student needs a quiet room for an exam, the school can arrange that in advance.","zh":"如果學生考試需要安靜房間，學校可以事先安排那件事。"},{"en":"Arranging help requires checking the need, finding a volunteer and setting a time.","zh":"安排幫助需要查核需要、尋找義工並設定時間。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to something already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回前文已提到的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as a one-off","meaning":"作為一次性安排","examples":[{"en":"Jane says they arrange help for individual residents as a one-off.","zh":"Jane說他們會為個別居民作一次性安排。"},{"en":"As a one-off means as a single event, not something regular or repeated.","zh":"as a one-off意思是作為單次事件，而不是定期或重複的安排。"},{"en":"A neighbour may help with shopping as a one-off when someone is ill.","zh":"鄰居可能在某人生病時作一次性安排，幫忙買東西。"},{"en":"One-off help is useful for short-term needs that do not require ongoing support.","zh":"一次性幫助適合短期需要，而不需要持續支援。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts a single arrangement with a regular service.","zh":"這個短語把單次安排與定期服務作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"need a lift to","meaning":"需要有人接送到……","examples":[{"en":"Mrs Carroll needs a lift to the hospital next week.","zh":"Carroll太太下星期需要有人接送到醫院。"},{"en":"To need a lift to a place means to need someone to drive you there.","zh":"need a lift to某地，意思是需要有人開車送你到那裡。"},{"en":"An elderly resident may need a lift to the clinic if there is no bus nearby.","zh":"如果附近沒有巴士，長者居民可能需要有人接送到診所。"},{"en":"Getting a lift can be important when someone cannot drive or travel alone easily.","zh":"當某人不能駕車或難以獨自出行，接送就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday British English.","zh":"這個短語常見於日常英式英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"struggle to find someone","meaning":"努力尋找某人；難以找到某人","examples":[{"en":"Jane is struggling to find someone to take Mrs Carroll to hospital.","zh":"Jane正努力尋找某人送Carroll太太去醫院。"},{"en":"To struggle to find someone means to have difficulty finding a suitable person.","zh":"struggle to find someone意思是很難找到合適的人。"},{"en":"A school may struggle to find someone to supervise a trip at short notice.","zh":"學校臨時可能難以找到人監督旅行。"},{"en":"When few people are available, organisers may struggle to find help.","zh":"當可用人手很少，組織者可能難以找到幫忙的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes effort and difficulty in finding a person.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找某人時的努力和困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have an appointment","meaning":"有預約","examples":[{"en":"Mrs Carroll has an appointment at the hospital on Tuesday.","zh":"Carroll太太星期二在醫院有預約。"},{"en":"To have an appointment means to have an arranged time to meet a doctor, official or professional.","zh":"have an appointment意思是有一個已安排時間去見醫生、職員或專業人士。"},{"en":"A student may have an appointment with a careers adviser after school.","zh":"學生可能放學後與職業顧問有預約。"},{"en":"Appointments help busy services manage time and avoid confusion.","zh":"預約能幫助繁忙服務管理時間並避免混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for medical or formal meetings.","zh":"這個短語常用於醫療或正式會面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take the whole morning","meaning":"花整個上午","examples":[{"en":"The hospital trip would take the whole morning.","zh":"去醫院這趟行程會花整個上午。"},{"en":"To take the whole morning means to require all or most of the morning.","zh":"take the whole morning意思是需要整個上午或大部分上午。"},{"en":"A dental appointment may take the whole morning if travel and waiting time are included.","zh":"如果包括交通和等候時間，牙科預約可能花整個上午。"},{"en":"Tasks that take a whole morning must be planned around other responsibilities.","zh":"需要花整個上午的任務，必須配合其他責任作安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a long time commitment.","zh":"這個短語描述長時間投入。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"I could do that","meaning":"我可以做那件事","examples":[{"en":"Frank says he could take Mrs Carroll to hospital.","zh":"Frank說他可以送Carroll太太去醫院。"},{"en":"I could do that means I am able and willing to help with that task.","zh":"I could do that意思是我有能力也願意幫忙做那件事。"},{"en":"If a teacher asks for help carrying books, a student may say, “I could do that.”","zh":"如果老師請人幫忙搬書，學生可能說：「我可以做那件事。」"},{"en":"This phrase offers help in a simple and practical way.","zh":"這個短語以簡單實際方式提供幫忙。"},{"en":"It shows willingness without sounding too dramatic.","zh":"它顯示願意幫忙，而不會聽起來誇張。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"that would be great","meaning":"那就太好了","examples":[{"en":"Jane says it would be great if Frank could help.","zh":"Jane說如果Frank可以幫忙，那就太好了。"},{"en":"That would be great means that would be very helpful or pleasing.","zh":"that would be great意思是那會非常有幫助或令人高興。"},{"en":"If a friend offers to collect your notes, you may reply, “That would be great.”","zh":"如果朋友提出幫你拿筆記，你可能回答：「那就太好了。」"},{"en":"This phrase expresses appreciation before the help has happened.","zh":"這個短語在幫忙發生前先表達感謝。"},{"en":"It is common in polite spoken English.","zh":"它常見於有禮的英語口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"arrange to have work done","meaning":"安排找人做工程；安排找人處理","examples":[{"en":"Jane is arranging to have some work done to Mr Selsbury’s house.","zh":"Jane正在安排找人為Selsbury先生的房子做一些工程。"},{"en":"To arrange to have work done means to organise for someone to repair, decorate or improve something.","zh":"arrange to have work done意思是安排某人維修、裝修或改善某物。"},{"en":"A homeowner may arrange to have work done on the roof before the rainy season.","zh":"屋主可能在雨季前安排找人維修屋頂。"},{"en":"This phrase often means the person arranges the work but does not do it personally.","zh":"這個短語通常表示該人安排工作，但不是親自做。"},{"en":"It is useful when talking about repairs or home improvement.","zh":"它適合用於談論維修或家居改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"before he moves","meaning":"在他搬走之前","examples":[{"en":"The work will be done before Mr Selsbury moves.","zh":"工程會在Selsbury先生搬走之前完成。"},{"en":"Before he moves means before he changes his home to another place.","zh":"before he moves意思是在他搬到另一個地方之前。"},{"en":"A tenant may clean the flat before he moves out.","zh":"租客可能在搬走之前清潔單位。"},{"en":"Doing work before someone moves can help the property be ready on time.","zh":"在某人搬走前完成工程，可以幫助物業準時準備好。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a deadline based on a future move.","zh":"這個短語以未來搬遷作為期限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not healthy enough to","meaning":"身體狀況不足以……","examples":[{"en":"Mr Selsbury is not healthy enough to do the work himself.","zh":"Selsbury先生身體狀況不足以親自做那些工作。"},{"en":"Not healthy enough to do something means lacking the physical condition needed to do it safely.","zh":"not healthy enough to do something意思是身體狀況不足以安全完成某事。"},{"en":"An elderly person may not be healthy enough to carry heavy boxes upstairs.","zh":"長者可能身體狀況不足以把重箱搬上樓。"},{"en":"Health limits can make ordinary housework difficult or risky.","zh":"健康限制可以令普通家務變得困難或有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why someone needs help.","zh":"這個短語解釋某人為何需要幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"do it himself","meaning":"親自做","examples":[{"en":"Mr Selsbury is not healthy enough to do the work himself.","zh":"Selsbury先生身體狀況不足以親自做那些工作。"},{"en":"To do it himself means to complete the task without another person doing it for him.","zh":"do it himself意思是不由別人代勞，而是自己完成任務。"},{"en":"A child may want to tie his shoes himself to show independence.","zh":"孩子可能想親自綁鞋帶，以顯示獨立。"},{"en":"Some tasks are too heavy or dangerous for people to do themselves.","zh":"有些任務太重或太危險，人們不適合親自做。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses personal action rather than help from others.","zh":"這個短語強調個人行動，而不是他人幫忙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get people to","meaning":"找人去……","examples":[{"en":"Jane has got some people to decorate Mr Selsbury’s kitchen.","zh":"Jane已找了一些人去裝修Selsbury先生的廚房。"},{"en":"To get people to do something means to arrange or persuade people to do it.","zh":"get people to do something意思是安排或說服人們去做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may get students to help move chairs before a school concert.","zh":"老師可能找學生在學校音樂會前幫忙搬椅子。"},{"en":"Getting people to help is easier when the task and time are clear.","zh":"當任務和時間清楚，找人幫忙會更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising other people’s action.","zh":"這個短語描述組織他人行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"decorate his kitchen","meaning":"裝修他的廚房","examples":[{"en":"Some volunteers will decorate Mr Selsbury’s kitchen.","zh":"一些義工會裝修Selsbury先生的廚房。"},{"en":"To decorate his kitchen means to improve its appearance, often by painting or putting up new materials.","zh":"decorate his kitchen意思是改善他的廚房外觀，通常透過油漆或安裝新材料。"},{"en":"A family may decorate the kitchen before selling their flat.","zh":"家庭可能在出售單位前裝修廚房。"},{"en":"Decorating can make a room cleaner, brighter and more pleasant to use.","zh":"裝修可以令房間更乾淨、更光亮和更宜使用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to home improvement, not party decoration.","zh":"這個短語指家居改善，而不是派對裝飾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"do some weeding","meaning":"除草","examples":[{"en":"Frank could do some weeding in Mr Selsbury’s garden.","zh":"Frank可以在Selsbury先生的花園除草。"},{"en":"To do some weeding means to remove unwanted plants from a garden or piece of land.","zh":"do some weeding意思是從花園或土地中移除不想要的植物。"},{"en":"Students may do some weeding in the school garden before planting vegetables.","zh":"學生可能在種蔬菜前，在學校花園除草。"},{"en":"Weeding helps useful plants grow because weeds take space, water and nutrients.","zh":"除草幫助有用植物生長，因為雜草會佔空間、水分和養分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical gardening task.","zh":"這個短語描述實際園藝任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"I’d enjoy that","meaning":"我會很樂意做","examples":[{"en":"Frank says he would enjoy doing some weeding.","zh":"Frank說他會很樂意除草。"},{"en":"I’d enjoy that means I would like doing that task.","zh":"I’d enjoy that意思是我會喜歡做那項任務。"},{"en":"If someone asks you to help paint a classroom and you like art, you might say, “I’d enjoy that.”","zh":"如果有人請你幫忙粉刷課室，而你喜歡藝術，你可能說：「我會很樂意做。」"},{"en":"This phrase offers help while showing personal interest.","zh":"這個短語在提供幫忙時，也顯示個人興趣。"},{"en":"It sounds warmer than simply saying “I can do it.”","zh":"它比單純說「我可以做」更溫暖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"presumably","meaning":"想必；大概","examples":[{"en":"Frank says that presumably the day and time are flexible.","zh":"Frank說日期和時間想必有彈性。"},{"en":"Presumably means probably, based on what seems reasonable.","zh":"presumably意思是根據合理推測，大概如此。"},{"en":"Presumably, the library is closed today because the lights are off and the door is locked.","zh":"圖書館燈關了、門也鎖了，想必今天休館。"},{"en":"This word shows that the speaker is making a logical assumption, not stating a confirmed fact.","zh":"這個詞顯示說話者是在作合理假設，而不是說已確認事實。"},{"en":"It is useful when checking what is likely true.","zh":"當查問很可能屬實的事情時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the day and time are flexible","meaning":"日期和時間有彈性","examples":[{"en":"The day and time for weeding are flexible.","zh":"除草的日期和時間有彈性。"},{"en":"The day and time are flexible means the date and hour can be changed to suit someone.","zh":"the day and time are flexible意思是日期和時間可以按某人需要改動。"},{"en":"The day and time for a private lesson may be flexible if the tutor has space.","zh":"如果補習老師有空位，私人課堂的日期和時間可能有彈性。"},{"en":"Flexible timing makes it easier for volunteers to fit help around other duties.","zh":"彈性時間讓義工更容易把幫忙安排在其他責任之間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adjustable scheduling.","zh":"這個短語描述可調整的時間安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"say when","meaning":"說明何時……","examples":[{"en":"Frank only needs to say when would suit him best.","zh":"Frank只需要說明何時最適合他。"},{"en":"To say when means to state what time or date is suitable.","zh":"say when意思是說出甚麼時間或日期合適。"},{"en":"If you want a meeting, just say when you are free.","zh":"如果你想開會，只要說明你何時有空。"},{"en":"Asking someone to say when gives them control over timing.","zh":"請某人說明何時合適，能讓對方掌握時間安排。"},{"en":"This phrase is practical and common in arranging appointments.","zh":"這個短語實用，常見於安排約會或會議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"suit you best","meaning":"最適合你","examples":[{"en":"Frank can choose the time that suits him best.","zh":"Frank可以選擇最適合他的時間。"},{"en":"To suit you best means to fit your needs, schedule or preference most well.","zh":"suit you best意思是最符合你的需要、時間表或偏好。"},{"en":"A student may choose the revision time that suits her best, such as early morning or evening.","zh":"學生可能選擇最適合自己的溫習時間，例如清晨或晚上。"},{"en":"When timing suits someone well, they are more likely to attend or help.","zh":"當時間適合某人，他們更可能出席或幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the most convenient option for a person.","zh":"這個短語描述對某人最方便的選項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"let someone know","meaning":"通知某人","examples":[{"en":"Jane will let Mr Selsbury know when Frank can come.","zh":"Jane會通知Selsbury先生Frank何時可以來。"},{"en":"To let someone know means to inform them.","zh":"let someone know意思是通知某人。"},{"en":"Please let the teacher know if you cannot attend the lesson.","zh":"如果你不能上課，請通知老師。"},{"en":"Letting people know in advance helps them prepare and avoid waiting.","zh":"事先通知人們可以幫助他們準備並避免等候。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in polite arrangements.","zh":"這個短語常見於有禮安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"volunteers group","meaning":"義工小組","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers group organises monthly social events.","zh":"義工小組舉辦每月社交活動。"},{"en":"A volunteers group is a group of people who help in the community without being paid.","zh":"volunteers group是一群在社區無償幫忙的人。"},{"en":"A volunteers group may visit elderly residents, run events and raise money.","zh":"義工小組可能探訪長者、舉辦活動和籌款。"},{"en":"Such groups need organisation because many people may be helping in different ways.","zh":"這類小組需要組織，因為許多人可能以不同方式幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a community service team.","zh":"這個短語描述社區服務團隊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"organise monthly social events","meaning":"舉辦每月社交活動","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers group organises monthly social events.","zh":"義工小組舉辦每月社交活動。"},{"en":"To organise monthly social events means to plan gatherings that happen once every month.","zh":"organise monthly social events意思是策劃每月一次的聚會。"},{"en":"A school club may organise monthly social events so members get to know one another.","zh":"學校社團可能舉辦每月社交活動，讓成員互相認識。"},{"en":"Regular events help people build friendships and feel part of a group.","zh":"定期活動幫助人們建立友誼並感覺自己是團體一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated social planning.","zh":"這個短語描述重複性的社交策劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a great way to","meaning":"……的好方法","examples":[{"en":"The monthly social events are a great way to meet other people.","zh":"每月社交活動是認識其他人的好方法。"},{"en":"A great way to do something means a very good method for doing it.","zh":"a great way to do something意思是做某事的很好方法。"},{"en":"Joining a club is a great way to make friends after moving to a new school.","zh":"搬到新學校後，加入社團是結交朋友的好方法。"},{"en":"Good methods make difficult goals easier and more natural.","zh":"好方法能令困難目標變得更容易和自然。"},{"en":"This phrase recommends a practical method.","zh":"這個短語推薦一種實用方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"meet other people","meaning":"認識其他人","examples":[{"en":"The social events help volunteers meet other people.","zh":"社交活動幫助義工認識其他人。"},{"en":"To meet other people means to get to know new people socially.","zh":"meet other people意思是在社交上認識新的人。"},{"en":"A newcomer may attend a community class to meet other people in the area.","zh":"新來者可能參加社區課程來認識區內其他人。"},{"en":"Meeting people helps reduce loneliness and build support networks.","zh":"認識其他人有助減少孤獨並建立支援網絡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making social connections.","zh":"這個短語描述建立社交連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"next month","meaning":"下個月","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers group is holding a quiz next month.","zh":"義工小組下個月會舉辦問答比賽。"},{"en":"Next month means during the month after the current one.","zh":"next month意思是在本月之後的那個月份。"},{"en":"The school will hold a parents’ evening next month.","zh":"學校下個月會舉辦家長晚會。"},{"en":"Mentioning next month gives people time to plan ahead.","zh":"提到下個月能讓人有時間提前計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a near future time.","zh":"這個短語指向不久後的未來時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hold a quiz","meaning":"舉辦問答比賽","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers group is holding a quiz on 19th October.","zh":"義工小組將於10月19日舉辦問答比賽。"},{"en":"To hold a quiz means to organise a question-and-answer competition or game.","zh":"hold a quiz意思是舉辦問答競賽或遊戲。"},{"en":"A class may hold a quiz to revise vocabulary before a test.","zh":"班級可能在測驗前舉辦問答比賽來溫習詞彙。"},{"en":"Quizzes can be fun because people compete while learning or remembering facts.","zh":"問答比賽可以很有趣，因為人們在競爭中學習或記住事實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising a quiz event.","zh":"這個短語描述組織問答活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be great at","meaning":"擅長……","examples":[{"en":"A couple of residents are great at planning unusual quizzes.","zh":"有幾位居民很擅長設計特別的問答比賽。"},{"en":"To be great at something means to be very good at doing it.","zh":"be great at某事，意思是非常擅長做它。"},{"en":"Some students are great at explaining maths to classmates.","zh":"有些學生很擅長向同學解釋數學。"},{"en":"People who are great at a task often make it look easy.","zh":"擅長某任務的人通常令它看起來很容易。"},{"en":"This phrase praises someone’s ability.","zh":"這個短語讚賞某人的能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"plan unusual ones","meaning":"設計特別的……","examples":[{"en":"Some residents are good at planning unusual quizzes.","zh":"有些居民擅長設計特別的問答比賽。"},{"en":"To plan unusual ones means to design events or activities that are different from normal examples.","zh":"plan unusual ones意思是設計與普通例子不同的活動。"},{"en":"A teacher may plan unusual revision games to keep students interested.","zh":"老師可能設計特別的溫習遊戲來保持學生興趣。"},{"en":"Unusual ideas can make repeated events feel fresh and memorable.","zh":"特別想法可以令重複活動感覺新鮮和令人難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to quizzes and describes creative planning.","zh":"這個短語指回問答比賽，並描述創意策劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fill the village hall","meaning":"坐滿村民會堂","examples":[{"en":"The quiz always fills the village hall.","zh":"問答比賽總是坐滿村民會堂。"},{"en":"To fill the village hall means to attract enough people to occupy the whole hall.","zh":"fill the village hall意思是吸引足夠人數坐滿整個會堂。"},{"en":"A popular concert may fill the school hall with parents and students.","zh":"受歡迎音樂會可能令學校禮堂坐滿家長和學生。"},{"en":"If an event fills a venue, organisers need enough chairs, space and refreshments.","zh":"如果活動坐滿場地，組織者需要足夠椅子、空間和茶點。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an event is very well attended.","zh":"這個短語顯示活動出席人數很多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sound like fun","meaning":"聽起來很有趣","examples":[{"en":"Frank thinks the quiz sounds like fun.","zh":"Frank覺得問答比賽聽起來很有趣。"},{"en":"To sound like fun means to seem enjoyable from the description.","zh":"sound like fun意思是從描述聽來似乎很愉快。"},{"en":"A beach clean-up followed by a picnic sounds like fun to many students.","zh":"海灘清潔後再野餐，對許多學生來說聽起來很有趣。"},{"en":"People may decide to join an event if it sounds interesting and friendly.","zh":"如果活動聽起來有趣又友善，人們可能決定參加。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a positive reaction to a plan.","zh":"這個短語對計劃作出正面反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"do anything to help","meaning":"做些甚麼幫忙","examples":[{"en":"Frank asks whether he can do anything to help.","zh":"Frank問自己是否可以做些甚麼幫忙。"},{"en":"To do anything to help means to offer whatever assistance may be useful.","zh":"do anything to help意思是願意提供任何有用協助。"},{"en":"A student may ask a teacher, “Can I do anything to help before the open day?”","zh":"學生可能問老師：「開放日前我可以做些甚麼幫忙嗎？」"},{"en":"This phrase shows willingness without choosing a specific task yet.","zh":"這個短語顯示願意幫忙，但尚未選定特定任務。"},{"en":"It is a polite way to offer support.","zh":"它是有禮地提供支援的方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"because of the number of people","meaning":"由於人數眾多","examples":[{"en":"The group needs plenty of refreshments because of the number of people.","zh":"由於人數眾多，小組需要大量茶點。"},{"en":"Because of the number of people means due to how many people will attend.","zh":"because of the number of people意思是由於出席人數多少。"},{"en":"A school needs extra chairs because of the number of parents coming to the meeting.","zh":"學校因有很多家長來開會而需要額外椅子。"},{"en":"Large attendance affects food, space, staffing and timing.","zh":"出席人數多會影響食物、空間、人手和時間安排。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a practical need caused by crowd size.","zh":"這個短語解釋由人數造成的實際需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"plenty of refreshments","meaning":"大量茶點","examples":[{"en":"The quiz will require plenty of refreshments.","zh":"問答比賽需要大量茶點。"},{"en":"Plenty of refreshments means a large amount of drinks and light food for people at an event.","zh":"plenty of refreshments意思是為活動參加者準備大量飲品和小食。"},{"en":"A school open day may need plenty of refreshments for visitors and helpers.","zh":"學校開放日可能需要大量茶點供訪客和幫手享用。"},{"en":"Having enough refreshments keeps guests comfortable during a long event.","zh":"有足夠茶點能讓賓客在長活動中感到舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in event planning.","zh":"這個短語常見於活動策劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"halfway through","meaning":"進行到一半時","examples":[{"en":"The refreshments are needed halfway through the quiz.","zh":"茶點在問答比賽進行到一半時需要。"},{"en":"Halfway through means at the middle point of an activity or period.","zh":"halfway through意思是在活動或時段的中間點。"},{"en":"Students may take a short break halfway through a three-hour workshop.","zh":"學生可能在三小時工作坊進行到一半時短暫休息。"},{"en":"A break halfway through helps people rest before continuing.","zh":"中途休息能幫助人們在繼續前稍作休息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes timing at the midpoint.","zh":"這個短語描述中間時間點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"provide refreshments","meaning":"提供茶點","examples":[{"en":"Frank may be able to provide refreshments for the quiz.","zh":"Frank可能可以為問答比賽提供茶點。"},{"en":"To provide refreshments means to prepare or supply drinks and light food.","zh":"provide refreshments意思是準備或供應飲品和小食。"},{"en":"Parents may provide refreshments for students after a school concert.","zh":"家長可能在學校音樂會後為學生提供茶點。"},{"en":"Providing refreshments requires planning quantities, allergies and serving time.","zh":"提供茶點需要計劃數量、過敏問題和供應時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical event-support task.","zh":"這個短語描述實際活動支援任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"we’d be grateful","meaning":"我們會很感激","examples":[{"en":"Jane says they would be grateful if Frank could provide refreshments.","zh":"Jane說如果Frank能提供茶點，他們會很感激。"},{"en":"We’d be grateful means we would appreciate it very much.","zh":"we’d be grateful意思是我們會非常感謝。"},{"en":"We’d be grateful if parents could return the reply slip by Friday.","zh":"如果家長能在星期五前交回回條，我們會很感激。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a request sound polite and appreciative.","zh":"這個短語令請求聽起來有禮且帶感謝。"},{"en":"It is common in emails, notices and formal conversation.","zh":"它常見於電郵、通告和正式對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"think about what to make","meaning":"考慮要做甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Frank will think about what to make for the quiz.","zh":"Frank會考慮為問答比賽做甚麼。"},{"en":"To think about what to make means to consider what food or item to prepare.","zh":"think about what to make意思是考慮要準備甚麼食物或物品。"},{"en":"Before a class party, students may think about what to make for their classmates.","zh":"班會派對前，學生可能考慮要為同學做甚麼食物。"},{"en":"Thinking first helps people choose something suitable for the number of guests and the occasion.","zh":"先思考能幫助人選擇適合賓客人數和場合的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planning before preparing something.","zh":"這個短語描述準備某物前的計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hold a dance","meaning":"舉辦舞會","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers group is holding a dance on 18th November.","zh":"義工小組將於11月18日舉辦舞會。"},{"en":"To hold a dance means to organise a social event where people dance.","zh":"hold a dance意思是舉辦讓人跳舞的社交活動。"},{"en":"A school may hold a dance at the end of term to celebrate students’ hard work.","zh":"學校可能在學期末舉辦舞會，慶祝學生努力。"},{"en":"Dances need music, space, tickets and often refreshments.","zh":"舞會需要音樂、空間、門票，通常也需要茶點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising a dancing event.","zh":"這個短語描述組織跳舞活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"book a band","meaning":"預訂樂隊","examples":[{"en":"The group has booked a band for the dance.","zh":"小組已為舞會預訂樂隊。"},{"en":"To book a band means to arrange and reserve musicians to perform at an event.","zh":"book a band意思是安排並預留音樂人在活動中演出。"},{"en":"A wedding organiser may book a band months before the celebration.","zh":"婚禮策劃人可能在慶祝活動前幾個月預訂樂隊。"},{"en":"Booking performers early helps avoid disappointment if they are popular.","zh":"及早預訂表演者有助避免因他們受歡迎而失望。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in event planning.","zh":"這個短語常見於活動策劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"specialise in","meaning":"專門演奏；專精於……","examples":[{"en":"The band specialises in music of the 1930s.","zh":"該樂隊專門演奏1930年代音樂。"},{"en":"To specialise in something means to focus on one particular area and be especially skilled in it.","zh":"specialise in某事，意思是專注於某特定範疇並尤其熟練。"},{"en":"A doctor may specialise in children’s health.","zh":"醫生可能專精於兒童健康。"},{"en":"Specialising helps people develop deeper knowledge in one area.","zh":"專精能幫助人在某一範疇發展更深入知識。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a person’s or group’s main expertise.","zh":"這個短語指出某人或團體的主要專長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"music of the 1930s","meaning":"1930年代音樂","examples":[{"en":"The band specialises in music of the 1930s.","zh":"該樂隊專門演奏1930年代音樂。"},{"en":"Music of the 1930s means songs and musical styles popular during the 1930s.","zh":"music of the 1930s意思是在1930年代流行的歌曲和音樂風格。"},{"en":"A dance event may use music of the 1930s to create an old-fashioned atmosphere.","zh":"舞會可能使用1930年代音樂來營造懷舊氣氛。"},{"en":"Music from a period can remind older listeners of past styles and memories.","zh":"某個時期的音樂可以令年長聽眾想起過去風格和記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies music by historical period.","zh":"這個短語按歷史時期識別音樂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have been before","meaning":"以前來過","examples":[{"en":"The band has been to the village before.","zh":"該樂隊以前來過村裏。"},{"en":"To have been before means to have visited or performed there previously.","zh":"have been before意思是以前曾經到訪或演出。"},{"en":"A guest speaker who has been before may already know the school hall and equipment.","zh":"以前來過的嘉賓講者可能已熟悉學校禮堂和設備。"},{"en":"Returning visitors often need less explanation because they know the place.","zh":"回訪者通常需要較少解釋，因為他們認識地方。"},{"en":"This phrase shows previous experience of a location.","zh":"這個短語顯示對某地有過往經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have a lot of requests to","meaning":"收到很多要求去……","examples":[{"en":"The group has had a lot of requests to bring the band back.","zh":"小組收到很多要求，希望再請該樂隊回來。"},{"en":"To have a lot of requests to do something means many people have asked for it.","zh":"have a lot of requests to do something意思是有很多人要求做某事。"},{"en":"A school canteen may have a lot of requests to bring back a popular lunch dish.","zh":"學校飯堂可能收到很多要求，希望重新供應受歡迎午餐。"},{"en":"Many requests show strong demand or approval.","zh":"很多要求顯示強烈需求或認可。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why organisers repeat something.","zh":"這個短語適合解釋為何主辦方重複某事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bring them back","meaning":"再請他們回來","examples":[{"en":"Residents have requested that the organisers bring the band back.","zh":"居民要求主辦方再請該樂隊回來。"},{"en":"To bring them back means to invite or arrange for the same people to return.","zh":"bring them back意思是邀請或安排同一批人再次回來。"},{"en":"Students may ask the school to bring back a popular speaker next year.","zh":"學生可能要求學校明年再請受歡迎的講者回來。"},{"en":"Bringing someone back usually means the previous experience was successful.","zh":"再請某人回來通常表示上次經驗很成功。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeating an invitation or arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述重複邀請或安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not really a dancer","meaning":"不太會跳舞的人","examples":[{"en":"Frank says he is not really a dancer.","zh":"Frank說自己不太會跳舞。"},{"en":"Not really a dancer means not especially skilled at or interested in dancing.","zh":"not really a dancer意思是不太擅長或不太熱衷跳舞。"},{"en":"Someone may enjoy music but still say they are not really a dancer.","zh":"有人可能喜歡音樂，但仍說自己不太會跳舞。"},{"en":"This phrase softens the statement and sounds less absolute than “I cannot dance”.","zh":"這個短語柔化說法，比I cannot dance沒那麼絕對。"},{"en":"It explains why someone may prefer to help in another way.","zh":"它解釋為何某人可能較想以另一方式幫忙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"do something to help","meaning":"做點事幫忙","examples":[{"en":"Frank would like to do something to help with the dance.","zh":"Frank想為舞會做點事幫忙。"},{"en":"To do something to help means to contribute in any useful way.","zh":"do something to help意思是以任何有用方式作出貢獻。"},{"en":"A parent may do something to help by setting up chairs before a school event.","zh":"家長可能透過在學校活動前擺放椅子來做點事幫忙。"},{"en":"People can support an event even if they do not take part in the main activity.","zh":"即使不參與主要活動，人們也可以支援活動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows willingness to contribute.","zh":"這個短語顯示願意作出貢獻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sell tickets in advance","meaning":"預先售票","examples":[{"en":"The group sells tickets in advance for the dance.","zh":"小組為舞會預先售票。"},{"en":"To sell tickets in advance means to sell tickets before the event day.","zh":"sell tickets in advance意思是在活動日之前售賣門票。"},{"en":"A theatre may sell tickets in advance so it knows how many seats are needed.","zh":"劇院可能預先售票，以知道需要多少座位。"},{"en":"Advance ticket sales help organisers plan space, staff and refreshments.","zh":"預先售票幫助主辦方規劃空間、人手和茶點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pre-event ticketing.","zh":"這個短語描述活動前售票安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an extra person","meaning":"額外一個人手","examples":[{"en":"Jane says an extra person would be useful at the door.","zh":"Jane說門口有額外一個人手會很有用。"},{"en":"An extra person means one additional helper beyond the people already planned.","zh":"an extra person意思是在原本計劃的人手以外，再多一名幫手。"},{"en":"A school fair may need an extra person at the entrance to guide visitors.","zh":"學校賣物會可能需要門口有額外一個人手指引訪客。"},{"en":"Extra help is useful when many people arrive at the same time.","zh":"當很多人同時到達時，額外幫手很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a small but practical staffing need.","zh":"這個短語指出小但實際的人手需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"check them at the door","meaning":"在門口查票","examples":[{"en":"Frank could check the tickets at the door.","zh":"Frank可以在門口查票。"},{"en":"To check them at the door means to inspect tickets as people enter.","zh":"check them at the door意思是在人們入場時檢查門票。"},{"en":"Volunteers may check tickets at the door before a school concert begins.","zh":"義工可能在學校音樂會開始前在門口查票。"},{"en":"Checking tickets at the entrance prevents confusion about who has paid or booked.","zh":"在入口查票可以防止誰已付款或預訂方面出現混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an entry-control task.","zh":"這個短語描述入口管理任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as people arrive","meaning":"當人們到場時","examples":[{"en":"Tickets need to be checked as people arrive.","zh":"當人們到場時，需要檢查門票。"},{"en":"As people arrive means at the time when people come to the event or place.","zh":"as people arrive意思是在人們來到活動或地方時。"},{"en":"Teachers may mark attendance as students arrive in the classroom.","zh":"老師可能在學生進入課室時點名。"},{"en":"Doing tasks as people arrive prevents queues from growing too long.","zh":"當人們到場時即時處理任務，可以防止隊伍變得太長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes timing linked to people’s arrival.","zh":"這個短語描述與到場時間相關的安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a bottleneck","meaning":"瓶頸；擠塞位置","examples":[{"en":"There can be a bottleneck if everyone arrives at once.","zh":"如果所有人同時到達，可能會出現瓶頸。"},{"en":"A bottleneck is a point where movement or progress slows because too many people or things pass through a limited space.","zh":"bottleneck是因太多人或物通過有限空間而令流動或進度變慢的位置。"},{"en":"The school gate can become a bottleneck when all students leave at the same time.","zh":"當所有學生同時離開，校門可以變成擠塞位置。"},{"en":"Bottlenecks cause delay because the system cannot handle the flow quickly enough.","zh":"瓶頸造成延誤，因為系統不能足夠快速處理流量。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for crowd movement, traffic and work processes.","zh":"這個短語可用於人流、交通和工作流程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"arrive at once","meaning":"同時到達","examples":[{"en":"The entrance can become crowded if everyone arrives at once.","zh":"如果所有人同時到達，入口會變得擁擠。"},{"en":"To arrive at once means to arrive at the same time.","zh":"arrive at once意思是在同一時間到達。"},{"en":"The lift lobby becomes busy when several classes arrive at once.","zh":"當幾個班級同時到達，升降機大堂會變得繁忙。"},{"en":"If many people arrive at once, organisers need more staff to manage them.","zh":"如果很多人同時到達，主辦方需要更多人手管理。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why queues or crowding may happen.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何可能出現排隊或擁擠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"I’m happy with that","meaning":"我很樂意那樣做","examples":[{"en":"Frank says he is happy with checking tickets at the door.","zh":"Frank說他很樂意在門口查票。"},{"en":"I’m happy with that means I agree to that plan or I am comfortable doing it.","zh":"I’m happy with that意思是我同意那個計劃，或覺得那樣做沒問題。"},{"en":"If a teacher asks you to help collect forms, you may say, “I’m happy with that.”","zh":"如果老師請你幫忙收表格，你可以說：「我很樂意那樣做。」"},{"en":"This phrase shows acceptance without complaint.","zh":"這個短語顯示接受安排而沒有抱怨。"},{"en":"It is a friendly way to agree to an arrangement.","zh":"它是友善地同意安排的方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"arrange a New Year’s Eve party","meaning":"籌辦除夕派對","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers group is arranging a New Year’s Eve party.","zh":"義工小組正在籌辦除夕派對。"},{"en":"To arrange a New Year’s Eve party means to plan a party for the evening of 31 December.","zh":"arrange a New Year’s Eve party意思是策劃12月31日晚上舉行的派對。"},{"en":"A community centre may arrange a New Year’s Eve party with music, food and games.","zh":"社區中心可能籌辦有音樂、食物和遊戲的除夕派對。"},{"en":"Such parties require planning for venue, tickets, dinner and entertainment.","zh":"這類派對需要規劃場地、門票、晚餐和娛樂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising a celebration for the end of the year.","zh":"這個短語描述為年末慶祝活動作組織。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"expect something to be","meaning":"預計某事會是……","examples":[{"en":"The group expects the New Year’s Eve party to be a really big event.","zh":"小組預計除夕派對會是一場很大型的活動。"},{"en":"To expect something to be a certain way means to believe it will probably have that quality.","zh":"expect something to be某樣，意思是相信某事很可能具有那種特質。"},{"en":"Teachers expect the school concert to be crowded because many parents have registered.","zh":"因為很多家長已報名，老師預計學校音樂會會很擁擠。"},{"en":"Expectations help organisers prepare for likely needs.","zh":"預期能幫助主辦方準備可能需要的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a prediction about an event or situation.","zh":"這個短語引入對活動或情況的預測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a really big event","meaning":"一場很大型的活動","examples":[{"en":"The New Year’s Eve party is expected to be a really big event.","zh":"除夕派對預計會是一場很大型的活動。"},{"en":"A really big event is an important or large event with many people or much preparation.","zh":"a really big event是有很多人參加或需要大量準備的重要或大型活動。"},{"en":"A town festival can be a really big event if thousands of visitors attend.","zh":"如果有數千名訪客參加，城鎮節日可以是一場很大型的活動。"},{"en":"Big events need careful planning because small problems affect many people.","zh":"大型活動需要仔細規劃，因為小問題會影響很多人。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses size, importance and excitement.","zh":"這個短語強調規模、重要性和熱鬧氣氛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"instead of","meaning":"而不是……","examples":[{"en":"The event will be held in the Mountfort Hotel instead of the village hall.","zh":"活動將在Mountfort Hotel舉行，而不是在村民會堂。"},{"en":"Instead of means in place of one thing, another thing is chosen.","zh":"instead of意思是選擇一件事來取代另一件事。"},{"en":"Students may use an online form instead of a paper reply slip.","zh":"學生可能使用網上表格，而不是紙本回條。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly contrasts the chosen option with the rejected one.","zh":"這個短語清楚對比被選的選項和被放棄的選項。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining a change of plan.","zh":"它適合用於解釋計劃變更。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be held in","meaning":"在……舉行","examples":[{"en":"The New Year’s Eve party will be held in the Mountfort Hotel.","zh":"除夕派對將在Mountfort Hotel舉行。"},{"en":"To be held in a place means to take place there.","zh":"be held in某地，意思是在那裡進行或舉辦。"},{"en":"The debate competition will be held in the school hall.","zh":"辯論比賽將在學校禮堂舉行。"},{"en":"Choosing where an event is held affects space, transport and atmosphere.","zh":"選擇活動在哪裡舉行，會影響空間、交通和氣氛。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in event announcements.","zh":"這個短語常見於活動公告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a couple of miles away","meaning":"幾英里外","examples":[{"en":"The Mountfort Hotel is only a couple of miles away.","zh":"Mountfort Hotel只有幾英里外。"},{"en":"A couple of miles away means about two miles from the place being discussed.","zh":"a couple of miles away意思是距離正在談論的地方大約兩英里。"},{"en":"The sports centre is a couple of miles away, so most people need a lift or a bus.","zh":"體育中心在幾英里外，所以大多數人需要接送或巴士。"},{"en":"Distance affects whether people can walk, drive or arrange transport.","zh":"距離會影響人們能否步行、駕車或安排交通。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate short distance.","zh":"這個短語給出大概的短距離。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"provide dinner","meaning":"提供晚餐","examples":[{"en":"The hotel will provide dinner for the New Year’s Eve party.","zh":"酒店會為除夕派對提供晚餐。"},{"en":"To provide dinner means to supply or serve the evening meal.","zh":"provide dinner意思是供應或提供晚餐。"},{"en":"A school camp may provide dinner for students after the afternoon activities.","zh":"學校宿營可能在下午活動後為學生提供晚餐。"},{"en":"Providing dinner reduces the need for guests to bring their own food.","zh":"提供晚餐可以減少賓客自備食物的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes supplying a meal as part of an event.","zh":"這個短語描述作為活動一部分供應膳食。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the one thing we haven’t got yet","meaning":"我們唯一仍未有的東西","examples":[{"en":"The one thing the organisers have not got yet is a poster.","zh":"主辦方唯一仍未有的東西是一張海報。"},{"en":"The one thing we haven’t got yet means the single item still missing or not prepared.","zh":"the one thing we haven’t got yet意思是唯一仍缺少或未準備好的項目。"},{"en":"For the school fair, the one thing we haven’t got yet is a volunteer schedule.","zh":"對學校賣物會來說，我們唯一仍未有的東西是義工時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the remaining gap after most arrangements are complete.","zh":"這個短語突顯大部分安排完成後仍剩下的缺口。"},{"en":"It is useful when organising events and checking what is still needed.","zh":"它適合用於組織活動和檢查仍需要甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"by any chance","meaning":"不知道是否剛好……","examples":[{"en":"Jane asks whether Frank could make a poster by any chance.","zh":"Jane問Frank不知道是否剛好可以製作海報。"},{"en":"By any chance is a polite phrase used when asking if something is possible.","zh":"by any chance是有禮地詢問某事是否可能的短語。"},{"en":"Do you have a spare pen by any chance?","zh":"不知道你是否剛好有多一支筆？"},{"en":"This phrase makes a request sound less direct and less demanding.","zh":"這個短語令請求聽起來較不直接、較不強求。"},{"en":"It is common when the speaker is unsure whether the answer will be yes.","zh":"當說話者不確定答案是否會是肯定時，常會使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"before I retired","meaning":"在我退休之前","examples":[{"en":"Before he retired, Frank was a graphic designer.","zh":"Frank退休之前是平面設計師。"},{"en":"Before I retired means during the period when I was still working.","zh":"before I retired意思是在我仍然工作期間。"},{"en":"Before I retired, I used to travel to the office every weekday.","zh":"在我退休之前，我以前每個工作日都到辦公室上班。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces someone’s former job, routine or experience.","zh":"這個短語引入某人以前的工作、生活規律或經驗。"},{"en":"It helps explain why a retired person still has useful skills.","zh":"它幫助解釋為何退休人士仍有有用技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"graphic designer","meaning":"平面設計師","examples":[{"en":"Frank used to work as a graphic designer.","zh":"Frank以前擔任平面設計師。"},{"en":"A graphic designer creates visual materials such as posters, logos, leaflets and digital images.","zh":"graphic designer負責創作海報、標誌、傳單和數碼圖像等視覺材料。"},{"en":"A charity may ask a graphic designer to make a clear poster for a fundraising event.","zh":"慈善機構可能請平面設計師為籌款活動製作清晰海報。"},{"en":"Good graphic design helps people notice information quickly and remember it.","zh":"良好平面設計幫助人們快速注意並記住資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a creative visual communication job.","zh":"這個短語描述創意視覺傳達工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"right up my street","meaning":"正是我擅長或感興趣的事","examples":[{"en":"Designing the poster is right up Frank’s street.","zh":"設計海報正是Frank擅長或感興趣的事。"},{"en":"Right up my street means exactly suited to my interests or skills.","zh":"right up my street意思是正正適合我的興趣或技能。"},{"en":"If a student loves cooking, helping with the school bake sale may be right up her street.","zh":"如果學生喜歡烹飪，幫忙學校烘焙義賣可能正是她擅長或感興趣的事。"},{"en":"This phrase shows enthusiasm because the task matches what someone enjoys or does well.","zh":"這個短語顯示熱情，因為任務配合某人喜歡或擅長的事情。"},{"en":"It is informal and common in British English.","zh":"它較口語，常見於英式英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"give you the details","meaning":"把詳情給你","examples":[{"en":"Jane will give Frank the details for the poster.","zh":"Jane會把海報詳情給Frank。"},{"en":"To give you the details means to provide the specific information you need.","zh":"give you the details意思是提供你所需要的具體資訊。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students the details of a trip, including time, place and cost.","zh":"老師可能把旅行詳情給學生，包括時間、地點和費用。"},{"en":"Details help people complete a task accurately instead of guessing.","zh":"詳情幫助人準確完成任務，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when arranging work or events.","zh":"這個短語常見於安排工作或活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"send me a draft","meaning":"寄一份草稿給我","examples":[{"en":"Jane asks Frank to send her a draft of the poster.","zh":"Jane請Frank寄一份海報草稿給她。"},{"en":"To send me a draft means to give me an early version for checking or comments.","zh":"send me a draft意思是把早期版本交給我檢查或給意見。"},{"en":"A student may send a teacher a draft of an essay before writing the final version.","zh":"學生可能在寫最終版本前，寄一份文章草稿給老師。"},{"en":"Drafts allow people to correct mistakes before the finished design is printed or shared.","zh":"草稿讓人們在完成設計被列印或分享前修正錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when work needs review before completion.","zh":"當工作完成前需要審閱時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 13/task-2":[{"front":"welcome to","meaning":"歡迎來到……","examples":[{"en":"Welcome to Oniton Hall, one of the largest estates in the area.","zh":"歡迎來到 Oniton Hall，本區最大的莊園之一。"},{"en":"“Welcome to” is used to greet people when they arrive at a place or event.","zh":"welcome to 用來在人們到達某地方或活動時打招呼。"},{"en":"Welcome to our school library; please keep your voice low inside.","zh":"歡迎來到我們的學校圖書館；請在裡面保持安靜。"},{"en":"If a guide says “welcome to” warmly, visitors may feel comfortable immediately.","zh":"如果導賞員親切地說「歡迎來到」，訪客可能會立即感到自在。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used at the start of tours, talks, and public events.","zh":"這個短語常用於導賞、演講和公開活動的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one of the largest estates","meaning":"最大的莊園之一","examples":[{"en":"Oniton Hall is one of the largest estates in the area.","zh":"Oniton Hall 是本區最大的莊園之一。"},{"en":"One of the largest estates means it is among the biggest pieces of privately owned land and buildings nearby.","zh":"one of the largest estates 指它是附近最大的私人土地和建築群之一。"},{"en":"A country house with gardens, farmland, and woods may be one of the largest estates in a county.","zh":"一座有花園、農地和樹林的鄉村大宅，可能是一個郡內最大的莊園之一。"},{"en":"If an estate is very large, visitors may need a map to explore it.","zh":"如果莊園很大，訪客可能需要地圖才能參觀。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one estate with others in the same area.","zh":"這個短語把一個莊園與同區其他莊園作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the area","meaning":"在本區","examples":[{"en":"Oniton Hall is one of the largest estates in the area.","zh":"Oniton Hall 是本區最大的莊園之一。"},{"en":"In the area means in the local district or nearby region.","zh":"in the area 指在本地區或附近一帶。"},{"en":"This café is popular because it serves some of the best coffee in the area.","zh":"這間咖啡店很受歡迎，因為它供應本區最好的咖啡之一。"},{"en":"If many tourists visit a museum, other shops in the area may benefit.","zh":"如果許多遊客參觀博物館，本區其他商店也可能受惠。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the surrounding place being discussed.","zh":"這個短語指正在討論的周邊地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one of the guides","meaning":"其中一名導賞員","examples":[{"en":"Nick is one of the guides at Oniton Hall.","zh":"Nick 是 Oniton Hall 的其中一名導賞員。"},{"en":"One of the guides means one person in a group of people who show visitors around.","zh":"one of the guides 指帶領訪客參觀的一群人之中的其中一人。"},{"en":"One of the guides at the museum explained the history of the old photographs.","zh":"博物館其中一名導賞員解釋了舊照片的歷史。"},{"en":"If there are several guides, visitors can be divided into smaller groups.","zh":"如果有幾名導賞員，訪客可以分成較小組別。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies someone as part of a guiding team.","zh":"這個短語指出某人是導賞團隊的一員。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"give you a brief introduction to","meaning":"向你簡介……","examples":[{"en":"Nick will give visitors a brief introduction to the estate.","zh":"Nick 會向訪客簡介這個莊園。"},{"en":"To give someone a brief introduction to something means to explain the main points quickly.","zh":"give someone a brief introduction to something 指快速解釋某事的主要重點。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students a brief introduction to a new topic before the lesson begins.","zh":"老師可能在課堂開始前向學生簡介新課題。"},{"en":"If visitors get a brief introduction first, they can understand the tour more easily.","zh":"如果訪客先聽到簡介，他們會更容易理解導賞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a short opening explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述簡短的開場說明。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"brief introduction","meaning":"簡介","examples":[{"en":"The guide gives a brief introduction to the estate.","zh":"導賞員會為這個莊園作簡介。"},{"en":"A brief introduction is a short explanation of the main facts about something.","zh":"brief introduction 指對某事主要資料的簡短說明。"},{"en":"A speaker may begin with a brief introduction before showing detailed slides.","zh":"演講者可能先作簡介，再展示詳細投影片。"},{"en":"If an introduction is too long, listeners may lose interest before the main tour begins.","zh":"如果簡介太長，聽眾可能在正式導賞開始前已失去興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase means a quick overview rather than a full explanation.","zh":"這個短語指快速概覽，而不是完整解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"while you’re sitting down","meaning":"趁大家坐着時","examples":[{"en":"The guide gives an introduction while visitors are sitting down.","zh":"導賞員趁訪客坐着時作簡介。"},{"en":"While you’re sitting down means during the time when you are seated.","zh":"while you’re sitting down 指在你坐着的時候。"},{"en":"The teacher explained the safety rules while the students were sitting down.","zh":"老師趁學生坐着時解釋安全規則。"},{"en":"If visitors hear instructions while sitting down, they may listen more comfortably.","zh":"如果訪客坐着時聽指示，他們可能聽得更舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two actions happen at the same time.","zh":"這個短語表示兩個動作同時發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"walk round","meaning":"四處參觀","examples":[{"en":"After the introduction, the visitors will walk round the estate.","zh":"簡介後，訪客會在莊園四處參觀。"},{"en":"To walk round a place means to walk through different parts of it and look around.","zh":"walk round a place 指步行經過某地方不同部分並到處看看。"},{"en":"Students walked round the museum to see the paintings and old tools.","zh":"學生在博物館四處參觀，看畫作和舊工具。"},{"en":"If visitors walk round slowly, they can notice more details.","zh":"如果訪客慢慢四處參觀，就能注意更多細節。"},{"en":"This British phrase is similar to “walk around.”","zh":"這個英式短語意思接近 walk around。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"consist of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"The estate consists of the house, gardens, parkland and farm.","zh":"這個莊園由大宅、花園、園林綠地和農場組成。"},{"en":"To consist of something means to be made up of those parts.","zh":"consist of something 指由那些部分組成。"},{"en":"A school lunch may consist of rice, vegetables, soup, and fruit.","zh":"學校午餐可能由飯、蔬菜、湯和水果組成。"},{"en":"If a project consists of many sections, each part needs careful planning.","zh":"如果一個項目由許多部分組成，每一部分都需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what something includes.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物包括甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"parkland","meaning":"園林綠地","examples":[{"en":"The estate consists of the house, gardens, parkland and farm.","zh":"這個莊園由大宅、花園、園林綠地和農場組成。"},{"en":"Parkland is open land with grass, trees, and paths, often around a large house.","zh":"parkland 指有草地、樹木和小徑的開放土地，常圍繞大型宅第。"},{"en":"Families may walk across parkland during a weekend visit to a historic estate.","zh":"家庭週末參觀歷史莊園時，可能會走過園林綠地。"},{"en":"If parkland is well maintained, it gives visitors space to relax and enjoy nature.","zh":"如果園林綠地保養良好，它會給訪客放鬆和欣賞自然的空間。"},{"en":"This word describes landscaped open green space.","zh":"這個字描述經規劃的開放綠地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"date back to","meaning":"可追溯至","examples":[{"en":"The estate dates back to the fourteenth century.","zh":"這個莊園可追溯至十四世紀。"},{"en":"To date back to a time means to have existed since that time.","zh":"date back to a time 指自某時期起已經存在。"},{"en":"This village temple dates back to the nineteenth century.","zh":"這座村廟可追溯至十九世紀。"},{"en":"If a building dates back many centuries, it may need careful conservation.","zh":"如果一座建築可追溯至多個世紀前，它可能需要小心保育。"},{"en":"This phrase connects something today with its historical origin.","zh":"這個短語把今天的事物與其歷史源頭連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the fourteenth century","meaning":"十四世紀","examples":[{"en":"Oniton Hall dates back to the fourteenth century.","zh":"Oniton Hall 可追溯至十四世紀。"},{"en":"The fourteenth century means the years from 1301 to 1400.","zh":"the fourteenth century 指1301年至1400年。"},{"en":"Historians study the fourteenth century to understand medieval Europe.","zh":"歷史學家研究十四世紀，以了解中世紀歐洲。"},{"en":"If a house dates from the fourteenth century, it is many hundreds of years old.","zh":"如果一座房子始建於十四世紀，它已有數百年歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase names a historical period.","zh":"這個短語指出一個歷史時期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"original house","meaning":"原來的房子","examples":[{"en":"The original house was replaced in the late seventeenth century.","zh":"原來的房子在十七世紀末被取代。"},{"en":"The original house is the first house that stood on the site before later changes.","zh":"original house 指後來改建前，最早建於該地的房子。"},{"en":"The original house in the village was small, but later owners built a larger one.","zh":"村裡原來的房子很小，但後來的業主建了一座較大的。"},{"en":"If the original house is replaced, only records or old drawings may show what it looked like.","zh":"如果原來的房子被取代，可能只剩紀錄或舊圖畫顯示它的樣貌。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the earliest version of a building.","zh":"這個短語指建築物最早的版本。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be replaced","meaning":"被取代","examples":[{"en":"The original house was replaced in the late seventeenth century.","zh":"原來的房子在十七世紀末被取代。"},{"en":"To be replaced means to be removed and have something else put in its place.","zh":"be replaced 指某物被移走，並由另一物放在其位置。"},{"en":"The old computers were replaced because they were too slow for online lessons.","zh":"舊電腦因為上網課太慢而被取代。"},{"en":"If a building is replaced, the new one may look very different.","zh":"如果一座建築被取代，新建築可能看起來很不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one thing taking the place of another.","zh":"這個短語描述一物取代另一物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in the late seventeenth century","meaning":"在十七世紀末","examples":[{"en":"The original house was replaced in the late seventeenth century.","zh":"原來的房子在十七世紀末被取代。"},{"en":"In the late seventeenth century means near the end of the years from 1601 to 1700.","zh":"in the late seventeenth century 指接近1601年至1700年這段時期的尾聲。"},{"en":"A historian may say a building was redesigned in the late seventeenth century.","zh":"歷史學家可能說一座建築在十七世紀末被重新設計。"},{"en":"If an object comes from the late seventeenth century, it is more than three hundred years old.","zh":"如果一件物品來自十七世紀末，它已有三百多年歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a historical time period near the end of the 1600s.","zh":"這個短語指出十七世紀後期的歷史時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a large number of","meaning":"大量；許多","examples":[{"en":"The estate has had a large number of owners.","zh":"這個莊園曾有許多業主。"},{"en":"A large number of means many.","zh":"a large number of 指很多。"},{"en":"A large number of students joined the history trip after seeing the poster.","zh":"許多學生看到海報後參加歷史考察。"},{"en":"If a place has had a large number of owners, each owner may have changed it.","zh":"如果一個地方曾有許多業主，每位業主都可能改變過它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a high quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述高數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"leave their mark","meaning":"留下痕跡","examples":[{"en":"Almost all the owners have left their mark on the estate.","zh":"幾乎所有業主都在這個莊園留下痕跡。"},{"en":"To leave their mark means to have a lasting effect that can still be seen or felt.","zh":"leave their mark 指留下仍可看見或感受到的長遠影響。"},{"en":"A good teacher can leave her mark on students by changing how they think.","zh":"好老師可以透過改變學生思維，在學生身上留下痕跡。"},{"en":"If many owners leave their mark on a house, the building may show different styles.","zh":"如果許多業主在一座房子留下痕跡，建築可能呈現不同風格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lasting influence.","zh":"這個短語描述持久影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"generally by","meaning":"通常透過","examples":[{"en":"The owners left their mark, generally by adding new rooms.","zh":"業主留下痕跡，通常是透過增建新房間。"},{"en":"Generally by means usually through a particular method or action.","zh":"generally by 指通常透過某種方法或行動。"},{"en":"Students improve their writing generally by reading more and correcting mistakes.","zh":"學生通常透過多閱讀和改正錯誤來改善寫作。"},{"en":"If change happens generally by small steps, people may not notice it immediately.","zh":"如果變化通常透過小步驟發生，人們可能不會立即察覺。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the usual way something is done.","zh":"這個短語引出某事通常如何完成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"add new rooms","meaning":"增建新房間","examples":[{"en":"Many owners changed the house by adding new rooms.","zh":"許多業主透過增建新房間改變這座房子。"},{"en":"To add new rooms means to build extra rooms onto an existing building.","zh":"add new rooms 指在現有建築上建造額外房間。"},{"en":"A school may add new rooms when student numbers increase.","zh":"當學生人數增加時，學校可能增建新課室。"},{"en":"If owners add new rooms, the layout of a house can change greatly.","zh":"如果業主增建新房間，房子的布局可以大大改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes expanding a building.","zh":"這個短語描述擴建建築物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ballroom","meaning":"舞廳","examples":[{"en":"The ballroom was added by one of the owners.","zh":"舞廳是由其中一位業主增建的。"},{"en":"A ballroom is a large room used for dancing, parties, or formal social events.","zh":"ballroom 指用於跳舞、派對或正式社交活動的大房間。"},{"en":"A hotel ballroom may be used for weddings and school graduation dinners.","zh":"酒店舞廳可能用於婚宴和學校畢業晚宴。"},{"en":"If a large house has a ballroom, it suggests the owners hosted important guests.","zh":"如果大型宅第有舞廳，這暗示業主曾招待重要賓客。"},{"en":"This word describes a grand social room.","zh":"這個字描述宏偉的社交房間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"conservatory","meaning":"玻璃溫室","examples":[{"en":"The conservatory was added by one of the owners.","zh":"玻璃溫室是由其中一位業主增建的。"},{"en":"A conservatory is a glass room attached to a house, often used for plants or sitting in sunlight.","zh":"conservatory 指連接房子的玻璃房間，常用於種植物或曬太陽休息。"},{"en":"A family may have breakfast in the conservatory on a bright morning.","zh":"天氣明亮的早上，一家人可能在玻璃溫室吃早餐。"},{"en":"If a house has a conservatory, it can bring more light into the living space.","zh":"如果房子有玻璃溫室，它可以為生活空間帶來更多光線。"},{"en":"This word describes a sunlit glass extension.","zh":"這個字描述陽光充足的玻璃擴建部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"demolish","meaning":"拆卸","examples":[{"en":"Some owners changed the house by demolishing rooms.","zh":"有些業主透過拆卸房間改變這座房子。"},{"en":"To demolish something means to destroy or tear it down completely.","zh":"demolish something 指完全摧毀或拆除某物。"},{"en":"The old classroom block was demolished before the new library was built.","zh":"新圖書館興建前，舊課室大樓被拆卸。"},{"en":"If rooms are demolished, the shape and history of a building may change.","zh":"如果房間被拆卸，建築的形狀和歷史可能改變。"},{"en":"This word describes deliberate destruction of a structure.","zh":"這個字描述有意拆除結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"much as it’s always done","meaning":"大致一如以往","examples":[{"en":"The farm looks much as it’s always done.","zh":"這個農場看起來大致一如以往。"},{"en":"Much as it’s always done means almost the same as it has looked for a long time.","zh":"much as it’s always done 指看起來幾乎和長久以來一樣。"},{"en":"The village shop looks much as it has always done, with wooden shelves and old signs.","zh":"村裡小店有木架和舊招牌，看起來大致一如以往。"},{"en":"If a place looks much as it always has, visitors can imagine the past more easily.","zh":"如果一個地方看起來大致一如以往，訪客就更容易想像過去。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses continuity rather than change.","zh":"這個短語強調延續而不是改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"current owner","meaning":"現任業主","examples":[{"en":"The current owner has done a great deal of work to the flower beds.","zh":"現任業主對花圃做了大量工作。"},{"en":"The current owner is the person who owns something now.","zh":"current owner 指現在擁有某物的人。"},{"en":"The current owner of the café changed the menu but kept the old name.","zh":"這間咖啡店的現任業主更改了餐牌，但保留舊名稱。"},{"en":"If the current owner cares about history, old features may be preserved.","zh":"如果現任業主重視歷史，舊特色可能被保留。"},{"en":"This phrase distinguishes the present owner from past owners.","zh":"這個短語把現時業主與過去業主區分開來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a great deal of work","meaning":"大量工作","examples":[{"en":"The current owner has done a great deal of work to the flower beds.","zh":"現任業主對花圃做了大量工作。"},{"en":"A great deal of work means a large amount of effort or labour.","zh":"a great deal of work 指大量努力或勞動。"},{"en":"Teachers do a great deal of work before a school open day.","zh":"老師在學校開放日前要做大量工作。"},{"en":"If a garden needs a great deal of work, it may take months to restore.","zh":"如果花園需要大量工作，可能要幾個月才能修復。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the effort is substantial.","zh":"這個短語強調努力很多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"flower beds","meaning":"花圃","examples":[{"en":"The current owner has improved the flower beds.","zh":"現任業主改善了花圃。"},{"en":"Flower beds are areas of soil prepared for growing flowers.","zh":"flower beds 指準備用來種花的泥土區域。"},{"en":"Students planted roses and herbs in the flower beds near the school entrance.","zh":"學生在學校入口附近的花圃種玫瑰和香草。"},{"en":"If flower beds are well cared for, a garden looks brighter and more welcoming.","zh":"如果花圃保養良好，花園會看起來更明亮、更吸引人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planted areas in a garden.","zh":"這個短語描述花園中的種植區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be owned by","meaning":"由……擁有","examples":[{"en":"In the seventeenth century, the estate was owned by Sir Edward Downes.","zh":"在十七世紀，這個莊園由 Sir Edward Downes 擁有。"},{"en":"To be owned by someone means to legally belong to that person or organisation.","zh":"be owned by someone 指在法律上屬於某人或某機構。"},{"en":"The old cinema is now owned by a local charity.","zh":"那間舊戲院現在由本地慈善機構擁有。"},{"en":"If a building is owned by a private company, public access may be limited.","zh":"如果建築物由私人公司擁有，公眾進入可能受限制。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the owner of something.","zh":"這個短語指出某物的擁有人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"wealthy man","meaning":"富有的人","examples":[{"en":"The estate was owned by a very wealthy man called Sir Edward Downes.","zh":"這個莊園由一名非常富有的人 Sir Edward Downes 擁有。"},{"en":"A wealthy man is a man who has a lot of money, land, or valuable property.","zh":"wealthy man 指擁有很多金錢、土地或貴重財產的男子。"},{"en":"A wealthy man may donate money to build a hospital or school.","zh":"富有的人可能捐錢興建醫院或學校。"},{"en":"If a wealthy man owns a large estate, he may afford expensive art and servants.","zh":"如果富有的人擁有大型莊園，他可能負擔得起昂貴藝術品和僕人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone with great financial resources.","zh":"這個短語描述擁有大量財力的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"his intention was to","meaning":"他的意圖是","examples":[{"en":"His intention was to escape from the world of politics.","zh":"他的意圖是遠離政治世界。"},{"en":"His intention was to means his purpose or plan was to do something.","zh":"his intention was to 指他的目的或計劃是做某事。"},{"en":"His intention was to study medicine, but he later became a teacher.","zh":"他的意圖原本是讀醫科，但後來成為老師。"},{"en":"If someone’s intention is clear, other people understand why he acts that way.","zh":"如果某人的意圖清楚，其他人就明白他為何那樣行動。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a person’s aim.","zh":"這個短語解釋一個人的目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"escape from","meaning":"逃離；遠離","examples":[{"en":"Sir Edward Downes wanted to escape from the world of politics.","zh":"Sir Edward Downes 想逃離政治世界。"},{"en":"To escape from something means to get away from a place, situation, or pressure.","zh":"escape from something 指離開某地方、情況或壓力。"},{"en":"Some workers go hiking at weekends to escape from office stress.","zh":"有些上班族週末行山，以遠離辦公室壓力。"},{"en":"If a person wants to escape from public life, he may move to a quieter place.","zh":"如果一個人想遠離公眾生活，他可能搬到較安靜的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes leaving something unpleasant or tiring.","zh":"這個短語描述離開令人不快或疲累的事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the world of politics","meaning":"政治世界","examples":[{"en":"Sir Edward Downes wanted to escape from the world of politics.","zh":"Sir Edward Downes 想逃離政治世界。"},{"en":"The world of politics means the people, activities, arguments, and power struggles connected with government.","zh":"the world of politics 指與政府有關的人、活動、爭論和權力鬥爭。"},{"en":"Journalists often report on scandals in the world of politics.","zh":"記者常報道政治世界中的醜聞。"},{"en":"If someone leaves the world of politics, they may want a quieter private life.","zh":"如果某人離開政治世界，他可能想要較安靜的私人生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes politics as a whole social environment.","zh":"這個短語把政治描述成整個社會環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"after years as","meaning":"在多年作為……之後","examples":[{"en":"He wanted to escape from politics after years as an active politician.","zh":"在多年作為活躍政客之後，他想遠離政治。"},{"en":"After years as something means after spending many years in that role or position.","zh":"after years as something 指在某角色或位置多年之後。"},{"en":"After years as a nurse, she became a hospital trainer.","zh":"在多年作為護士之後，她成為醫院培訓員。"},{"en":"If someone changes direction after years as a manager, the decision may feel major.","zh":"如果某人在多年作為經理之後改變方向，這個決定可能很重大。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a long period of previous experience.","zh":"這個短語顯示長時間的過往經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"active politician","meaning":"活躍政客","examples":[{"en":"Sir Edward Downes had spent years as an active politician.","zh":"Sir Edward Downes 曾多年擔任活躍政客。"},{"en":"An active politician is a politician who is regularly involved in public work, debates, and decisions.","zh":"active politician 指經常參與公共工作、辯論和決策的政客。"},{"en":"An active politician may attend meetings, make speeches, and speak to voters.","zh":"活躍政客可能出席會議、發表演說和與選民交談。"},{"en":"If an active politician retires, public life may suddenly feel quieter.","zh":"如果活躍政客退休，公共生活可能突然變得安靜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone deeply involved in politics.","zh":"這個短語描述深度參與政治的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"worthy of","meaning":"配得上……","examples":[{"en":"He wanted to build a new house worthy of his collection.","zh":"他想建一座配得上自己收藏的新房子。"},{"en":"Worthy of something means good enough or suitable enough for it.","zh":"worthy of something 指足夠好或足夠合適，能配得上某事。"},{"en":"A museum display should be worthy of rare historical objects.","zh":"博物館展覽應配得上珍貴歷史物件。"},{"en":"If a prize is worthy of a student’s hard work, it should feel meaningful.","zh":"如果獎項配得上學生的努力，它應該有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one thing deserves or matches another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一物值得或匹配另一物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"big collection of","meaning":"大量收藏","examples":[{"en":"He had a big collection of books, paintings and sculptures.","zh":"他收藏了大量書籍、畫作和雕塑。"},{"en":"A big collection of something means many items gathered together over time.","zh":"big collection of something 指長時間收集起來的許多物品。"},{"en":"My grandfather has a big collection of old coins and postcards.","zh":"我的祖父有大量舊硬幣和明信片收藏。"},{"en":"If a collection is big, it may need a special room for storage and display.","zh":"如果收藏很多，可能需要特別房間存放和展示。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large group of collected items.","zh":"這個短語描述大量被收集的物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sculptures","meaning":"雕塑","examples":[{"en":"Sir Edward Downes had a collection of books, paintings and sculptures.","zh":"Sir Edward Downes 收藏了書籍、畫作和雕塑。"},{"en":"Sculptures are three-dimensional works of art made from materials such as stone, metal, wood, or clay.","zh":"sculptures 指用石、金屬、木或泥等材料製成的立體藝術品。"},{"en":"A public square may display sculptures of famous local figures.","zh":"公共廣場可能展示本地名人的雕塑。"},{"en":"If sculptures are old and valuable, they need careful handling and cleaning.","zh":"如果雕塑古老而珍貴，就需要小心搬運和清潔。"},{"en":"This word refers to art objects with shape and form.","zh":"這個字指具有形狀和立體感的藝術品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"break off contact with","meaning":"與……斷絕聯繫","examples":[{"en":"He broke off contact with his former political allies.","zh":"他與昔日政治盟友斷絕聯繫。"},{"en":"To break off contact with someone means to stop communicating or having a relationship with them.","zh":"break off contact with someone 指停止與某人溝通或維持關係。"},{"en":"A student may break off contact with friends who repeatedly pressure him to cheat.","zh":"如果朋友不斷施壓要他作弊，學生可能與他們斷絕聯繫。"},{"en":"If someone breaks off contact suddenly, others may feel hurt or confused.","zh":"如果某人突然斷絕聯繫，其他人可能感到受傷或困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ending communication or connection.","zh":"這個短語描述結束溝通或連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"former political allies","meaning":"昔日政治盟友","examples":[{"en":"Sir Edward Downes broke off contact with his former political allies.","zh":"Sir Edward Downes 與昔日政治盟友斷絕聯繫。"},{"en":"Former political allies are people who used to support or work with someone in politics.","zh":"former political allies 指以前在政治上支持或合作的人。"},{"en":"Former political allies may become rivals after a disagreement.","zh":"昔日政治盟友可能在分歧後變成對手。"},{"en":"If a leader loses support from former political allies, his influence may weaken.","zh":"如果領袖失去昔日政治盟友的支持，他的影響力可能減弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes past partners in political life.","zh":"這個短語描述政治生涯中的過往夥伴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"host meetings of","meaning":"舉辦……的聚會","examples":[{"en":"He hosted meetings of creative and literary people.","zh":"他舉辦創意及文學界人士的聚會。"},{"en":"To host meetings of a group means to organise or provide a place for that group to gather.","zh":"host meetings of a group 指組織或提供地方讓某群人聚集。"},{"en":"A school may host meetings of parents and teachers before a new term begins.","zh":"學校可能在新學期開始前舉辦家長和老師的聚會。"},{"en":"If a museum hosts meetings of artists, new ideas may develop there.","zh":"如果博物館舉辦藝術家聚會，新想法可能在那裡產生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arranging gatherings for particular people.","zh":"這個短語描述為特定人士安排聚會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"creative and literary people","meaning":"創意及文學界人士","examples":[{"en":"He hosted meetings of creative and literary people.","zh":"他舉辦創意及文學界人士的聚會。"},{"en":"Creative and literary people are people involved in art, writing, poetry, storytelling, or similar cultural work.","zh":"creative and literary people 指參與藝術、寫作、詩歌、故事創作或類似文化工作的人。"},{"en":"A book festival brings creative and literary people together to discuss new writing.","zh":"書展把創意及文學界人士聚在一起討論新作品。"},{"en":"If creative and literary people meet often, they may inspire one another.","zh":"如果創意及文學界人士經常見面，他們可能互相啟發。"},{"en":"This phrase describes artists, writers, and thinkers.","zh":"這個短語描述藝術家、作家和思想者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"painters and poets","meaning":"畫家及詩人","examples":[{"en":"His guests included painters and poets.","zh":"他的賓客包括畫家及詩人。"},{"en":"Painters and poets are artists who create visual art and written verse.","zh":"painters and poets 指創作視覺藝術和詩歌的藝術家。"},{"en":"A cultural evening may invite painters and poets to share their work.","zh":"文化晚會可能邀請畫家及詩人分享作品。"},{"en":"If painters and poets gather, they may exchange ideas about colour, memory, and emotion.","zh":"如果畫家及詩人聚集，他們可能交流關於色彩、記憶和情感的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase names two kinds of creative people.","zh":"這個短語指出兩類創作人士。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"unusually for his time","meaning":"以他那個時代來說很罕見","examples":[{"en":"Unusually for his time, he did not care whether his guests were rich or poor.","zh":"以他那個時代來說很罕見，他不在乎賓客是富有還是貧窮。"},{"en":"Unusually for his time means something was not normal or expected in that historical period.","zh":"unusually for his time 指某事在那個歷史時期並不正常或並非預期。"},{"en":"Unusually for her time, the scientist studied at university when few women could do so.","zh":"以她那個時代來說很罕見，這名科學家在很少女性能上大學時接受大學教育。"},{"en":"If someone acts unusually for his time, his behaviour may seem modern or progressive.","zh":"如果某人的行為以其時代來說很罕見，他的行為可能顯得現代或進步。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a person’s action with the norms of the period.","zh":"這個短語把一個人的行為與當時規範作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"care whether","meaning":"在乎是否","examples":[{"en":"He did not care whether his guests were rich or poor.","zh":"他不在乎賓客是富有還是貧窮。"},{"en":"To care whether something is true means to think that difference matters.","zh":"care whether something is true 指認為某差別是否成立很重要。"},{"en":"A fair teacher does not care whether a student is rich or poor when giving help.","zh":"公平的老師在提供幫助時，不在乎學生是否富有。"},{"en":"If someone does not care whether people have high status, talent may matter more.","zh":"如果某人不在乎人們是否有高地位，才華可能更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows whether a condition is important to someone.","zh":"這個短語顯示某條件對某人是否重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rich or poor","meaning":"貧富","examples":[{"en":"He welcomed talented guests, whether they were rich or poor.","zh":"他歡迎有才華的賓客，不論他們貧富。"},{"en":"Rich or poor means regardless of whether people have a lot of money or very little money.","zh":"rich or poor 指不論人們有很多錢還是很少錢。"},{"en":"A public library should serve everyone, rich or poor.","zh":"公共圖書館應服務所有人，不論貧富。"},{"en":"If an event welcomes people rich or poor, it treats status as unimportant.","zh":"如果活動不論貧富都歡迎人參加，它就是把地位視為不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts wealth and poverty.","zh":"這個短語對比富有與貧窮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"as long as","meaning":"只要","examples":[{"en":"He welcomed guests as long as they had talent.","zh":"只要賓客有才華，他都歡迎。"},{"en":"As long as means provided that or if one condition is satisfied.","zh":"as long as 指只要某條件被滿足。"},{"en":"You can join the trip as long as you return the form on time.","zh":"只要你準時交回表格，就可以參加旅行。"},{"en":"If rules are followed, people can use the room as long as they need it.","zh":"如果規則被遵守，人們可以按需要使用房間。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a condition.","zh":"這個短語引出條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have talent","meaning":"有才華","examples":[{"en":"Sir Edward Downes welcomed people who had talent.","zh":"Sir Edward Downes 歡迎有才華的人。"},{"en":"To have talent means to have a natural or developed ability to do something well.","zh":"have talent 指擁有天生或培養出來的能力，能把某事做好。"},{"en":"A student may have talent for music even before receiving formal training.","zh":"學生即使未接受正式訓練，也可能有音樂才華。"},{"en":"If people have talent and practise hard, they may produce excellent work.","zh":"如果人有才華並努力練習，就可能創作出優秀作品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability or promise.","zh":"這個短語描述能力或潛質。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"big houses like","meaning":"像……這樣的大宅","examples":[{"en":"Big houses like Oniton had dozens of servants.","zh":"像 Oniton 這樣的大宅曾有數十名僕人。"},{"en":"Big houses like something means large homes of the same type or social class as that example.","zh":"big houses like something 指與該例子同類型或同社會階層的大型住宅。"},{"en":"Big houses like this old mansion often had separate rooms for staff.","zh":"像這座舊大宅這樣的大房子，常有給員工使用的獨立房間。"},{"en":"If big houses like these were expensive to run, only wealthy families could maintain them.","zh":"如果像這樣的大宅運作成本高，只有富裕家庭能維持。"},{"en":"This phrase uses one example to describe similar places.","zh":"這個短語用一個例子描述相似地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dozens of servants","meaning":"數十名僕人","examples":[{"en":"Oniton Hall had dozens of servants until the 1920s or 30s.","zh":"Oniton Hall 直到二十世紀二三十年代都有數十名僕人。"},{"en":"Dozens of servants means many household workers, usually at least twenty-four or more.","zh":"dozens of servants 指許多家庭僕役，通常至少二十多名。"},{"en":"A large historic house needed dozens of servants to cook, clean, wash, and care for guests.","zh":"大型歷史宅第需要數十名僕人煮食、清潔、洗衣和照顧賓客。"},{"en":"If a house had dozens of servants, daily life was highly organised and unequal.","zh":"如果一座房子有數十名僕人，日常生活會非常有組織，也很不平等。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the scale of domestic labour in the past.","zh":"這個短語顯示過去家務勞動的規模。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"until the 1920s or 30s","meaning":"直到二十世紀二三十年代","examples":[{"en":"Big houses had servants until the 1920s or 30s.","zh":"大宅直到二十世紀二三十年代都有僕人。"},{"en":"Until the 1920s or 30s means up to the period around the 1920s or 1930s.","zh":"until the 1920s or 30s 指一直到約1920年代或1930年代。"},{"en":"Some families used horse-drawn transport until the 1920s or 30s.","zh":"有些家庭直到二十世紀二三十年代仍使用馬車交通。"},{"en":"If a practice continued until the 1920s or 30s, it lasted into the early twentieth century.","zh":"如果某做法持續到二十世紀二三十年代，它就延續到二十世紀初期。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate historical end point.","zh":"這個短語提供大約的歷史終點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"show what something was like","meaning":"展示……是怎樣的","examples":[{"en":"The estate tries to show what servants’ working lives were like.","zh":"這個莊園嘗試展示僕人的工作生活是怎樣的。"},{"en":"To show what something was like means to help people understand the real experience or appearance of it.","zh":"show what something was like 指幫助人理解某事的真實經歷或樣貌。"},{"en":"A museum room can show what a classroom was like a hundred years ago.","zh":"博物館房間可以展示一百年前的課室是怎樣的。"},{"en":"If an exhibition shows what daily life was like, visitors learn more than from dates alone.","zh":"如果展覽展示日常生活是怎樣的，訪客學到的會不只是日期。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making the past or an experience understandable.","zh":"這個短語描述使過去或經歷變得可理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"working lives","meaning":"工作生活","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition shows what the servants’ working lives were like.","zh":"展覽展示僕人的工作生活是怎樣的。"},{"en":"Working lives are the daily experiences, duties, hours, and conditions people have in their jobs.","zh":"working lives 指人們在工作中的日常經歷、職責、工時和條件。"},{"en":"Interviews with nurses can reveal their working lives during a busy winter.","zh":"與護士的訪問可以揭示她們在繁忙冬季的工作生活。"},{"en":"If workers’ working lives are difficult, they may need better pay or support.","zh":"如果工人的工作生活艱難，他們可能需要更好薪酬或支援。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on life at work, not private life.","zh":"這個短語重點在工作中的生活，而不是私人生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"don’t give much of an idea","meaning":"未能充分令人了解","examples":[{"en":"Photographs do not give much of an idea of servants’ lives.","zh":"照片未能充分令人了解僕人的生活。"},{"en":"To not give much of an idea means to fail to explain or show something clearly enough.","zh":"don’t give much of an idea 指未能足夠清楚地解釋或展示某事。"},{"en":"A menu photo does not give much of an idea of how noisy the restaurant is.","zh":"餐牌照片未能充分令人了解餐廳有多嘈吵。"},{"en":"If old pictures do not give much of an idea of daily work, live demonstrations may help.","zh":"如果舊照片未能令人充分了解日常工作，現場示範可能有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase means the information is too limited to understand properly.","zh":"這個短語指資料太有限，難以真正理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"instead","meaning":"反而；取而代之","examples":[{"en":"Instead, visitors see volunteers dressed as servants.","zh":"取而代之，訪客會看見打扮成僕人的義工。"},{"en":"Instead means as an alternative to what was just mentioned.","zh":"instead 指作為剛提到事情的替代做法。"},{"en":"The class did not watch a video; instead, they visited the museum.","zh":"這班學生沒有觀看影片；反而去了博物館參觀。"},{"en":"If one method does not explain enough, a better method can be used instead.","zh":"如果一種方法解釋不足，可以改用更好的方法。"},{"en":"This word introduces a replacement or different choice.","zh":"這個字引出替代做法或不同選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"go round the house","meaning":"參觀屋內","examples":[{"en":"Visitors see volunteers as they go round the house.","zh":"訪客參觀屋內時會看見義工。"},{"en":"To go round the house means to walk through different rooms and areas of the house.","zh":"go round the house 指步行參觀房子裡不同房間和區域。"},{"en":"During the open day, parents went round the house to see where students lived.","zh":"開放日期間，家長參觀屋內，看看學生居住的地方。"},{"en":"If visitors go round a historic house, they can see how rooms were used.","zh":"如果訪客參觀歷史大宅，就能看到不同房間過去如何使用。"},{"en":"This British phrase means to tour the inside of a house.","zh":"這個英式短語指參觀房子內部。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dressed up as","meaning":"打扮成","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers are dressed up as nineteenth-century servants.","zh":"義工打扮成十九世紀僕人。"},{"en":"To be dressed up as someone means to wear clothes that make you look like that person or type of person.","zh":"dressed up as someone 指穿上衣服，使自己看起來像某人或某類人。"},{"en":"Children were dressed up as doctors during the school career day.","zh":"孩子在學校職業日打扮成醫生。"},{"en":"If guides are dressed up as historical figures, visitors may imagine the past more clearly.","zh":"如果導賞員打扮成歷史人物，訪客可能更清楚想像過去。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wearing costume for a role.","zh":"這個短語描述為扮演角色而穿上服裝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"nineteenth-century servants","meaning":"十九世紀僕人","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers are dressed up as nineteenth-century servants.","zh":"義工打扮成十九世紀僕人。"},{"en":"Nineteenth-century servants were household workers who worked in private homes during the 1800s.","zh":"nineteenth-century servants 指十九世紀在私人住宅工作的家庭僕役。"},{"en":"Nineteenth-century servants often cleaned rooms, cooked meals, washed clothes, and served guests.","zh":"十九世紀僕人常清潔房間、煮飯、洗衣和服侍賓客。"},{"en":"If visitors learn about nineteenth-century servants, they understand class differences better.","zh":"如果訪客了解十九世紀僕人，就能更明白階級差異。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to domestic workers from the 1800s.","zh":"這個短語指十九世紀的家務工作者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"go about their work","meaning":"忙於自己的工作","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers go about their work like servants from the past.","zh":"義工像昔日僕人一樣忙於自己的工作。"},{"en":"To go about one’s work means to do one’s usual tasks.","zh":"go about one’s work 指做自己的日常任務。"},{"en":"Nurses go about their work quietly even when the hospital is busy.","zh":"即使醫院很忙，護士仍安靜地忙於自己的工作。"},{"en":"If visitors watch people go about their work, they can understand routines better.","zh":"如果訪客觀看人們忙於自己的工作，就能更了解日常流程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes carrying out everyday duties.","zh":"這個短語描述執行日常職責。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"explain what they’re doing","meaning":"解釋他們正在做甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers explain what they are doing.","zh":"義工解釋他們正在做甚麼。"},{"en":"To explain what someone is doing means to describe the action and its purpose.","zh":"explain what someone is doing 指描述該動作及其目的。"},{"en":"A science teacher explains what she is doing before mixing chemicals.","zh":"科學老師在混合化學品前解釋她正在做甚麼。"},{"en":"If guides explain what they are doing, visitors learn from watching and listening.","zh":"如果導賞員解釋自己正在做甚麼，訪客就能從觀看和聆聽中學習。"},{"en":"This phrase connects demonstration with explanation.","zh":"這個短語把示範與解釋連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tell you their recipes","meaning":"告訴你他們的食譜","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers tell visitors their recipes.","zh":"義工會告訴訪客他們的食譜。"},{"en":"To tell someone recipes means to explain how particular dishes are made.","zh":"tell someone recipes 指向某人解釋某些菜式如何製作。"},{"en":"A grandmother may tell children her recipes so they can cook family dishes later.","zh":"祖母可能把自己的食譜告訴孩子，讓他們日後能煮家庭菜式。"},{"en":"If visitors hear old recipes, they can understand past eating habits.","zh":"如果訪客聽到舊食譜，就能理解過去的飲食習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sharing cooking instructions.","zh":"這個短語描述分享烹飪方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tools they’re using","meaning":"他們正在使用的工具","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers explain what tools they are using.","zh":"義工解釋他們正在使用的工具。"},{"en":"Tools they’re using means the equipment they are working with at that moment.","zh":"tools they’re using 指他們當時正在用來工作的設備。"},{"en":"A carpenter may show students the tools he is using to make a wooden chair.","zh":"木匠可能向學生展示他正在用來製作木椅的工具。"},{"en":"If people understand the tools being used, they understand the work more clearly.","zh":"如果人們理解正在使用的工具，就會更清楚理解那份工作。"},{"en":"This phrase points to practical equipment in action.","zh":"這個短語指正在使用中的實用設備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"just introduced","meaning":"剛剛推出","examples":[{"en":"The estate has just introduced this feature.","zh":"這個莊園剛剛推出這項特色安排。"},{"en":"Just introduced means something has only recently been started or made available.","zh":"just introduced 指某事最近才開始或提供。"},{"en":"The school has just introduced a new online booking system for parents’ meetings.","zh":"學校剛剛推出家長會網上預約系統。"},{"en":"If a feature has just been introduced, visitors may need clear instructions.","zh":"如果一項特色安排剛剛推出，訪客可能需要清楚指示。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something very new.","zh":"這個短語描述非常新的事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"this feature","meaning":"這項特色安排","examples":[{"en":"This feature replaces the old audio guide.","zh":"這項特色安排取代了舊語音導賞。"},{"en":"This feature means this special part, service, or function of a place or system.","zh":"this feature 指某地方或系統中的這個特別部分、服務或功能。"},{"en":"The app’s best feature is that it reminds students of homework deadlines.","zh":"這個應用程式最好的特色是提醒學生功課期限。"},{"en":"If a feature is useful, people may prefer it to the old system.","zh":"如果一項特色安排有用，人們可能更喜歡它而不是舊系統。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a specific element already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指已提及的特定元素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"replace the audio guide","meaning":"取代語音導賞","examples":[{"en":"The new feature replaces the audio guide.","zh":"新特色安排取代語音導賞。"},{"en":"To replace the audio guide means to take the place of the recorded listening tour.","zh":"replace the audio guide 指取代錄音導覽服務。"},{"en":"A museum may replace the audio guide with live actors and demonstrations.","zh":"博物館可能用現場演員和示範取代語音導賞。"},{"en":"If a new method replaces the audio guide, visitors may get a more interactive experience.","zh":"如果新方法取代語音導賞，訪客可能得到更互動的體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing from recorded guidance to another form.","zh":"這個短語描述由錄音導覽轉為另一種形式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"used to have available","meaning":"以前有提供","examples":[{"en":"The estate used to have an audio guide available.","zh":"這個莊園以前有提供語音導賞。"},{"en":"Used to have available means something was provided in the past but may not be provided now.","zh":"used to have available 指某物過去有提供，但現在可能沒有。"},{"en":"The library used to have printed maps available at the entrance.","zh":"圖書館以前在入口有提供印刷地圖。"},{"en":"If a service used to be available, returning visitors may ask where it has gone.","zh":"如果某服務以前有提供，重訪的訪客可能會問它去了哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a former facility or service.","zh":"這個短語描述過去的設施或服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a number of children","meaning":"一些小朋友","examples":[{"en":"There are a number of children visiting today.","zh":"今天有一些小朋友到訪。"},{"en":"A number of children means several children.","zh":"a number of children 指幾個或一些小朋友。"},{"en":"A number of children waited outside the classroom before the workshop began.","zh":"工作坊開始前，一些小朋友在課室外等候。"},{"en":"If a number of children visit a historic site, staff may prepare simpler activities.","zh":"如果一些小朋友參觀歷史場地，職員可能準備較簡單活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes more than a few children without giving an exact number.","zh":"這個短語描述不止幾名兒童，但沒有給出確實數目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"specially for children","meaning":"專為兒童而設","examples":[{"en":"The estate has several activities specially for children.","zh":"這個莊園有幾項專為兒童而設的活動。"},{"en":"Specially for children means designed especially to suit children’s age, interests, and safety needs.","zh":"specially for children 指特別配合兒童年齡、興趣和安全需要而設計。"},{"en":"The museum created a treasure hunt specially for children.","zh":"博物館設計了一個專為兒童而設的尋寶遊戲。"},{"en":"If an activity is made specially for children, it should be clear, safe, and enjoyable.","zh":"如果活動專為兒童而設，它應該清楚、安全和有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that children are the intended audience.","zh":"這個短語顯示兒童是目標對象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dressing up in","meaning":"穿上……扮演","examples":[{"en":"Children can enjoy dressing up in clothes from the past.","zh":"小朋友可以享受穿上昔日衣服扮演角色。"},{"en":"Dressing up in clothes means wearing special clothes to pretend to be someone or something.","zh":"dressing up in clothes 指穿上特別服裝來扮演某人或某物。"},{"en":"Children enjoy dressing up in doctor’s coats during career day.","zh":"小朋友在職業日喜歡穿上醫生袍扮演醫生。"},{"en":"If children dress up in historical clothes, they may understand the past more vividly.","zh":"如果小朋友穿上歷史服裝，他們可能更生動地理解過去。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wearing costume for play or learning.","zh":"這個短語描述為遊戲或學習而穿上服裝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the sorts of clothes","meaning":"那類衣服","examples":[{"en":"Children can dress up in the sorts of clothes that children wore in the past.","zh":"小朋友可以穿上過去兒童所穿的那類衣服扮演角色。"},{"en":"The sorts of clothes means the kinds or types of clothing.","zh":"the sorts of clothes 指衣服的種類或類型。"},{"en":"A school play may need the sorts of clothes people wore in the 1950s.","zh":"學校話劇可能需要人們在1950年代穿的那類衣服。"},{"en":"If children see the sorts of clothes worn long ago, they can compare old and modern life.","zh":"如果小朋友看到很久以前穿的那類衣服，就能比較昔日和現代生活。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to categories of clothing.","zh":"這個短語指衣服的類別。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"wore in the past","meaning":"過去穿着","examples":[{"en":"Children can wear the sorts of clothes that children wore in the past.","zh":"小朋友可以穿上過去兒童所穿的那類衣服。"},{"en":"Wore in the past means used to wear in an earlier period of history.","zh":"wore in the past 指在較早歷史時期曾經穿着。"},{"en":"Visitors can see the uniforms that nurses wore in the past.","zh":"訪客可以看到護士過去穿着的制服。"},{"en":"If people learn what children wore in the past, they may notice changes in comfort and style.","zh":"如果人們了解兒童過去穿着甚麼，可能注意到舒適度和風格的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase connects clothing with history.","zh":"這個短語把衣着與歷史連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as it’s a fine day","meaning":"由於天氣很好","examples":[{"en":"As it’s a fine day, some children may want to play outside.","zh":"由於天氣很好，有些小朋友可能想在戶外玩。"},{"en":"As it’s a fine day means because the weather is good.","zh":"as it’s a fine day 指因為天氣很好。"},{"en":"As it’s a fine day, the class will have lunch in the garden.","zh":"由於天氣很好，這班學生會在花園吃午餐。"},{"en":"If it is a fine day, outdoor activities become more attractive.","zh":"如果天氣很好，戶外活動就更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase gives good weather as a reason for doing something.","zh":"這個短語以好天氣作為做某事的原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"adventure playground","meaning":"歷奇遊樂場","examples":[{"en":"Some children will probably want to play in the adventure playground.","zh":"有些小朋友大概會想在歷奇遊樂場玩。"},{"en":"An adventure playground is an outdoor play area with climbing frames, slides, ropes, or other active equipment.","zh":"adventure playground 指有攀爬架、滑梯、繩索或其他活動設備的戶外遊樂區。"},{"en":"Children ran to the adventure playground after the picnic.","zh":"野餐後，小朋友跑到歷奇遊樂場。"},{"en":"If an adventure playground is well designed, children can play actively and safely.","zh":"如果歷奇遊樂場設計良好，兒童可以安全而活躍地玩耍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a play area for energetic activities.","zh":"這個短語描述進行活躍遊戲的遊樂區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"latest addition","meaning":"最新增設項目","examples":[{"en":"The latest addition is child-sized tractors.","zh":"最新增設項目是兒童尺寸拖拉機。"},{"en":"The latest addition is the newest thing that has been added to a place, collection, or service.","zh":"latest addition 指最近加入某地方、收藏或服務的新事物。"},{"en":"The latest addition to the library is a quiet study room.","zh":"圖書館最新增設項目是一間安靜自修室。"},{"en":"If the latest addition is popular, more visitors may come.","zh":"如果最新增設項目受歡迎，可能會有更多訪客到來。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces something newly added.","zh":"這個短語引出新加入的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"child-sized tractors","meaning":"兒童尺寸拖拉機","examples":[{"en":"Children can drive child-sized tractors around the grounds.","zh":"小朋友可以駕駛兒童尺寸拖拉機在場地四周行駛。"},{"en":"Child-sized tractors are small toy or practice tractors made for children to use safely.","zh":"child-sized tractors 指為兒童安全使用而製作的小型玩具或練習拖拉機。"},{"en":"A farm attraction may offer child-sized tractors for young visitors to ride.","zh":"農場景點可能提供兒童尺寸拖拉機給小訪客乘坐。"},{"en":"If equipment is child-sized, it is easier and safer for children to handle.","zh":"如果設備是兒童尺寸，兒童就更容易、更安全地操作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes machines made smaller for children.","zh":"這個短語描述為兒童縮小的機器。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"around the grounds","meaning":"在場地四周","examples":[{"en":"Children can drive tractors around the grounds.","zh":"小朋友可以駕駛拖拉機在場地四周行駛。"},{"en":"Around the grounds means throughout the outdoor land belonging to a place.","zh":"around the grounds 指在屬於某地方的戶外土地範圍內四處。"},{"en":"Visitors walked around the grounds before entering the historic house.","zh":"訪客在進入歷史大宅前，在場地四周散步。"},{"en":"If children move around the grounds, staff must keep routes safe.","zh":"如果小朋友在場地四周活動，職員必須確保路線安全。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the outdoor area of an estate, school, or large building.","zh":"這個短語指莊園、學校或大型建築的戶外範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"part of the estate","meaning":"莊園的一部分","examples":[{"en":"The farm is part of the estate.","zh":"農場是莊園的一部分。"},{"en":"Part of the estate means one section or area belonging to the whole estate.","zh":"part of the estate 指屬於整個莊園的一個部分或區域。"},{"en":"The old kitchen garden is part of the estate, although it is behind a wall.","zh":"舊廚房花園雖然在牆後，但也是莊園的一部分。"},{"en":"If the farm is part of the estate, visitors can understand how the house was supplied with food.","zh":"如果農場是莊園的一部分，訪客就能理解大宅過去如何獲得食物供應。"},{"en":"This phrase links one area to a larger property.","zh":"這個短語把一個區域與較大的物業連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"plenty to do","meaning":"有很多活動可做","examples":[{"en":"There is plenty to do on the farm.","zh":"農場有很多活動可做。"},{"en":"Plenty to do means there are many activities or things to see.","zh":"plenty to do 指有許多活動或東西可看。"},{"en":"There is plenty to do at the school fair, including games, food stalls, and performances.","zh":"學校嘉年華有很多活動可做，包括遊戲、食物攤位和表演。"},{"en":"If visitors have plenty to do, they may stay longer and enjoy the visit more.","zh":"如果訪客有很多活動可做，他們可能停留更久並更享受參觀。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a place is active and interesting.","zh":"這個短語暗示一個地方活動豐富而有趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"most of the buildings","meaning":"大部分建築物","examples":[{"en":"Most of the buildings date from the eighteenth century.","zh":"大部分建築物始建於十八世紀。"},{"en":"Most of the buildings means the majority of the buildings in a place.","zh":"most of the buildings 指某地多數建築物。"},{"en":"Most of the buildings on the campus are modern, but the chapel is old.","zh":"校園大部分建築物是現代建築，但小教堂很古老。"},{"en":"If most of the buildings are historical, repairs must be done carefully.","zh":"如果大部分建築物具歷史價值，維修必須小心進行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes more than half of the buildings.","zh":"這個短語描述超過一半的建築物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"date from","meaning":"始建於","examples":[{"en":"Most of the buildings date from the eighteenth century.","zh":"大部分建築物始建於十八世紀。"},{"en":"To date from a period means to have been built or created during that period.","zh":"date from a period 指在某時期建造或創造。"},{"en":"The village bridge dates from the 1800s.","zh":"這條村橋始建於十九世紀。"},{"en":"If a building dates from an old period, historians may study its design.","zh":"如果建築物始建於古老時期，歷史學家可能研究其設計。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies when something began.","zh":"這個短語指出某物開始的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"eighteenth century","meaning":"十八世紀","examples":[{"en":"The farm buildings mostly date from the eighteenth century.","zh":"農場建築物大多始建於十八世紀。"},{"en":"The eighteenth century means the years from 1701 to 1800.","zh":"eighteenth century 指1701年至1800年。"},{"en":"Students studying the eighteenth century may learn about farming, trade, and empire.","zh":"研究十八世紀的學生可能學習農業、貿易和帝國發展。"},{"en":"If a barn comes from the eighteenth century, it has survived for more than two hundred years.","zh":"如果一座穀倉來自十八世紀，它已保存二百多年。"},{"en":"This phrase names a historical century.","zh":"這個短語指出一個歷史世紀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"step back into","meaning":"走回……之中","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can step back into an agricultural past.","zh":"訪客可以走回農業歷史之中。"},{"en":"To step back into the past means to experience something that makes the past feel present again.","zh":"step back into the past 指體驗某事，使過去彷彿再次出現眼前。"},{"en":"A historic classroom lets students step back into school life from a hundred years ago.","zh":"歷史課室讓學生走回一百年前的校園生活之中。"},{"en":"If a place is carefully preserved, visitors can feel as if they step back into history.","zh":"如果一個地方被仔細保存，訪客會感覺像走回歷史之中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an imaginative return to an earlier time.","zh":"這個短語描述想像上回到較早時代。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"agricultural past","meaning":"農業歷史","examples":[{"en":"The farm lets visitors step back into an agricultural past.","zh":"農場讓訪客走回農業歷史之中。"},{"en":"Agricultural past means the earlier history of farming and rural work.","zh":"agricultural past 指農耕和鄉郊工作的早期歷史。"},{"en":"Old tools and barns can help children understand the agricultural past of a village.","zh":"舊工具和穀倉可以幫助孩子理解村莊的農業歷史。"},{"en":"If a society forgets its agricultural past, it may not appreciate how food was produced.","zh":"如果社會忘記自己的農業歷史，就可能不懂珍惜食物如何被生產。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to farming history.","zh":"這個短語指農耕歷史。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"until recently","meaning":"直到最近","examples":[{"en":"Until recently, the dairy was used to make cheese.","zh":"直到最近，乳品房仍用來製作芝士。"},{"en":"Until recently means up to a short time ago.","zh":"until recently 指直到不久以前。"},{"en":"Until recently, the school still used paper forms for every event.","zh":"直到最近，學校仍每個活動都使用紙本表格。"},{"en":"If something changed only recently, older visitors may remember its previous use.","zh":"如果某事只是最近才改變，較早來過的訪客可能記得它以前的用途。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the past situation ended not long ago.","zh":"這個短語顯示過去情況不久前才結束。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dairy","meaning":"乳品房","examples":[{"en":"The dairy was where milk from the cows was turned into cheese.","zh":"乳品房是把牛奶製成芝士的地方。"},{"en":"A dairy is a place where milk is stored, processed, or made into products like cheese and butter.","zh":"dairy 指存放、處理牛奶，或把牛奶製成芝士和牛油等產品的地方。"},{"en":"A farm dairy may show children how fresh milk is cooled and handled.","zh":"農場乳品房可能向孩子展示鮮奶如何冷卻和處理。"},{"en":"If a dairy is no longer used for production, it may become a café or exhibition space.","zh":"如果乳品房不再用於生產，它可能變成咖啡店或展覽空間。"},{"en":"This word describes a place connected with milk products.","zh":"這個字描述與奶製品有關的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be turned into","meaning":"被製成","examples":[{"en":"Milk from the cows was turned into cheese.","zh":"牛奶被製成芝士。"},{"en":"To be turned into something means to be changed into a different form or use.","zh":"be turned into something 指被改變成另一種形式或用途。"},{"en":"An old factory was turned into an art centre.","zh":"一座舊工廠被改建成藝術中心。"},{"en":"If raw materials are turned into useful products, their value increases.","zh":"如果原材料被製成有用產品，它們的價值會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transformation.","zh":"這個短語描述轉化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the place to go for","meaning":"適合去……的地方","examples":[{"en":"The dairy is now the place to go for lunch or afternoon tea.","zh":"乳品房現在是適合去吃午餐或下午茶的地方。"},{"en":"The place to go for something means the best or usual place to get that thing.","zh":"the place to go for something 指取得某物或做某事的最佳或常去地方。"},{"en":"The library is the place to go for quiet study after school.","zh":"圖書館是放學後適合去安靜溫習的地方。"},{"en":"If a café becomes the place to go for lunch, it may get very busy.","zh":"如果一間咖啡店成為適合去吃午餐的地方，它可能非常繁忙。"},{"en":"This phrase recommends a suitable place for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語推薦適合某目的的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"afternoon tea","meaning":"下午茶","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can go to the dairy for afternoon tea.","zh":"訪客可以到乳品房享用下午茶。"},{"en":"Afternoon tea is a light meal or snack with tea, often taken in the afternoon.","zh":"afternoon tea 指下午享用的茶和輕食或小點。"},{"en":"Friends may meet for afternoon tea with sandwiches and cake.","zh":"朋友可能見面吃三文治和蛋糕作下午茶。"},{"en":"If a historic site serves afternoon tea, visitors may stay longer after the tour.","zh":"如果歷史景點供應下午茶，訪客可能在導賞後逗留更久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a British-style afternoon refreshment.","zh":"這個短語描述英式下午茶點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"homemade cake","meaning":"自製蛋糕","examples":[{"en":"The dairy serves coffee and a slice of homemade cake.","zh":"乳品房供應咖啡和一件自製蛋糕。"},{"en":"Homemade cake is cake made at home or in a local kitchen, not mass-produced in a factory.","zh":"homemade cake 指在家中或本地廚房製作，而不是工廠大量生產的蛋糕。"},{"en":"A café may attract customers by selling homemade cake baked that morning.","zh":"咖啡店可能透過售賣當天早上焗好的自製蛋糕吸引顧客。"},{"en":"If food tastes homemade, visitors may feel it is warm and personal.","zh":"如果食物吃起來像自製，訪客可能覺得溫暖和有人情味。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests freshness and a local touch.","zh":"這個短語暗示新鮮和本地特色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"big stone building","meaning":"大型石建築","examples":[{"en":"The big stone building that dominates the farm is the large barn.","zh":"在農場中特別顯眼的大型石建築就是大穀倉。"},{"en":"A big stone building is a large structure made mainly of stone.","zh":"big stone building 指主要由石建成的大型建築物。"},{"en":"A big stone building at the entrance of a village may once have been a school or church.","zh":"村口的大型石建築可能曾是學校或教堂。"},{"en":"If a big stone building stands higher than others, it can become a landmark.","zh":"如果大型石建築比其他建築更高，它可以成為地標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large solid building material and size.","zh":"這個短語描述大型、堅固的建築材料和規模。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dominate the farm","meaning":"在農場中特別顯眼","examples":[{"en":"The large barn dominates the farm.","zh":"大穀倉在農場中特別顯眼。"},{"en":"To dominate the farm means to be the most noticeable or visually powerful building there.","zh":"dominate the farm 指成為農場中最顯眼或視覺上最突出的建築。"},{"en":"A tall clock tower can dominate a school campus.","zh":"高大的鐘樓可以在校園中特別顯眼。"},{"en":"If one building dominates a place, visitors notice it first.","zh":"如果一座建築在某地特別顯眼，訪客會最先注意它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong visual presence.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈的視覺存在感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"large barn","meaning":"大穀倉","examples":[{"en":"The large barn contains a collection of agricultural tools.","zh":"大穀倉收藏了一批農具。"},{"en":"A large barn is a big farm building used for storing crops, tools, animals, or equipment.","zh":"large barn 指用來存放農作物、工具、動物或設備的大型農場建築。"},{"en":"Farmers may keep hay and machines inside a large barn.","zh":"農民可能把乾草和機器存放在大穀倉內。"},{"en":"If a large barn is preserved, it can show visitors how farms worked in the past.","zh":"如果大穀倉被保存，它可以向訪客展示過去農場如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important farm building.","zh":"這個短語描述重要的農場建築。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"collection of","meaning":"……收藏","examples":[{"en":"The barn contains a collection of agricultural tools.","zh":"穀倉收藏了一批農具。"},{"en":"A collection of something is a group of items gathered and kept together.","zh":"collection of something 指被收集並保存在一起的一組物品。"},{"en":"The classroom has a collection of maps from different periods.","zh":"課室有一批不同時期的地圖收藏。"},{"en":"If a collection is well displayed, visitors can compare items easily.","zh":"如果收藏展示得好，訪客就能容易比較物品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gathered objects of a similar kind.","zh":"這個短語描述同類物品的集合。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"agricultural tools","meaning":"農具","examples":[{"en":"The barn displays agricultural tools from the past.","zh":"穀倉展示過去的農具。"},{"en":"Agricultural tools are tools used for farming tasks such as digging, cutting, planting, and harvesting.","zh":"agricultural tools 指用於挖掘、切割、種植和收割等農務的工具。"},{"en":"A hoe, sickle, and plough are examples of agricultural tools.","zh":"鋤頭、鐮刀和犁都是農具的例子。"},{"en":"If visitors see old agricultural tools, they can understand how hard farm work was.","zh":"如果訪客看到舊農具，就能理解農務有多辛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes equipment used in farming.","zh":"這個短語描述農業使用的設備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"在過去","examples":[{"en":"These agricultural tools were used in the past.","zh":"這些農具在過去曾被使用。"},{"en":"In the past means at an earlier time, not now.","zh":"in the past 指在較早時間，而不是現在。"},{"en":"In the past, students wrote essays by hand more often than on computers.","zh":"在過去，學生較常手寫作文，而不是用電腦。"},{"en":"If a tool was used in the past, it may reveal how people worked before modern machines.","zh":"如果工具在過去曾被使用，它可能揭示現代機器出現前人們如何工作。"},{"en":"This phrase places something in earlier times.","zh":"這個短語把某事放在較早時代。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"plough the earth","meaning":"犁地","examples":[{"en":"The tools were used to plough the earth.","zh":"這些工具曾用來犁地。"},{"en":"To plough the earth means to turn over soil so crops can be planted.","zh":"plough the earth 指翻動泥土，以便種植農作物。"},{"en":"Farmers plough the earth before sowing seeds in a field.","zh":"農民在田裡播種前會犁地。"},{"en":"If the earth is not ploughed properly, seeds may not grow well.","zh":"如果土地沒有好好犁過，種子可能長得不好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparing farmland for planting.","zh":"這個短語描述為種植而準備農地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sow seeds","meaning":"播種","examples":[{"en":"The tools were used to sow seeds.","zh":"這些工具曾用來播種。"},{"en":"To sow seeds means to put seeds into soil so plants can grow.","zh":"sow seeds 指把種子放入泥土，讓植物生長。"},{"en":"Children sow seeds in small pots during a school gardening lesson.","zh":"小朋友在學校園藝課中把種子播在小花盆裡。"},{"en":"If farmers sow seeds at the wrong time, the crop may fail.","zh":"如果農民在錯誤時間播種，農作物可能失收。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of growing plants.","zh":"這個短語描述種植植物的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make gates","meaning":"製作閘門","examples":[{"en":"Some tools were used to make gates.","zh":"有些工具曾用來製作閘門。"},{"en":"To make gates means to build or create barriers that can open and close at entrances.","zh":"make gates 指建造或製作可在入口開關的屏障。"},{"en":"A carpenter may make gates for a farm entrance or garden path.","zh":"木匠可能為農場入口或花園小徑製作閘門。"},{"en":"If a farm has strong gates, animals are less likely to escape.","zh":"如果農場有堅固閘門，動物較不容易逃走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing practical entrance barriers.","zh":"這個短語描述製作實用的入口屏障。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"and much more","meaning":"還有很多其他用途","examples":[{"en":"The tools were used to plough, sow seeds, make gates and much more.","zh":"這些工具曾用來犁地、播種、製作閘門，還有很多其他用途。"},{"en":"And much more means there are many additional things not listed.","zh":"and much more 指還有許多沒有列出的其他東西。"},{"en":"The school fair has games, food, performances, and much more.","zh":"學校嘉年華有遊戲、食物、表演，還有很多其他活動。"},{"en":"If a guide says “and much more,” visitors expect more variety than the examples given.","zh":"如果導賞員說 and much more，訪客會預期例子以外還有更多種類。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the list is not complete.","zh":"這個短語暗示清單並不完整。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"small barn","meaning":"小穀倉","examples":[{"en":"There is a small barn where visitors can groom the animals.","zh":"那裡有一座小穀倉，訪客可以為動物梳理毛髮。"},{"en":"A small barn is a smaller farm building used for animals, tools, or activities.","zh":"small barn 指較小型的農場建築，用於動物、工具或活動。"},{"en":"The small barn near the field stores brushes, buckets, and animal feed.","zh":"田邊的小穀倉存放刷子、水桶和動物飼料。"},{"en":"If a small barn is open to visitors, it can provide hands-on farm activities.","zh":"如果小穀倉向訪客開放，它可以提供親身體驗農場活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a modest farm building.","zh":"這個短語描述較小的農場建築。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"made of stone","meaning":"由石建成","examples":[{"en":"The small barn is also made of stone.","zh":"小穀倉也是由石建成。"},{"en":"Made of stone means built or formed using stone as the main material.","zh":"made of stone 指主要用石頭建造或製成。"},{"en":"The old bridge is made of stone and has survived many storms.","zh":"這座舊橋由石建成，經歷過許多風暴仍保存下來。"},{"en":"If a building is made of stone, it may feel strong, cool, and historic.","zh":"如果建築物由石建成，它可能令人感覺堅固、清涼和有歷史感。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the material of an object or building.","zh":"這個短語指出物件或建築的材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"groom the donkeys and horses","meaning":"為驢和馬梳理毛髮","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can groom the donkeys and horses.","zh":"訪客可以為驢和馬梳理毛髮。"},{"en":"To groom the donkeys and horses means to brush and clean their coats.","zh":"groom the donkeys and horses 指為驢和馬刷毛和清潔毛皮。"},{"en":"Children learned how to groom the ponies gently at the farm.","zh":"小朋友在農場學習如何溫柔地為小馬梳理毛髮。"},{"en":"If animals are groomed regularly, their coats stay cleaner and healthier.","zh":"如果動物定期被梳理毛髮，牠們的毛皮會更乾淨、更健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes caring for animals’ hair or coats.","zh":"這個短語描述照顧動物毛髮或毛皮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"keep their coats clean","meaning":"保持牠們的毛皮清潔","examples":[{"en":"Grooming helps keep the animals’ coats clean.","zh":"梳理毛髮有助保持動物的毛皮清潔。"},{"en":"To keep their coats clean means to make sure the animals’ fur or hair stays free from dirt.","zh":"keep their coats clean 指確保動物的毛或皮毛沒有污垢。"},{"en":"Farmers brush horses to keep their coats clean before a show.","zh":"農民在展覽前為馬刷毛，以保持牠們的毛皮清潔。"},{"en":"If animals’ coats are not kept clean, dirt may cause skin problems.","zh":"如果動物毛皮沒有保持清潔，污垢可能引起皮膚問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes maintaining animal hygiene.","zh":"這個短語描述維持動物衞生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"seem to enjoy","meaning":"似乎很享受","examples":[{"en":"The animals really seem to enjoy being groomed.","zh":"動物似乎真的很享受被梳理毛髮。"},{"en":"To seem to enjoy something means to appear happy or relaxed while experiencing it.","zh":"seem to enjoy something 指在經歷某事時看起來開心或放鬆。"},{"en":"The children seem to enjoy the storytelling activity because they keep asking questions.","zh":"孩子似乎很享受講故事活動，因為他們一直提問。"},{"en":"If animals seem to enjoy an activity, handlers may continue it gently.","zh":"如果動物似乎享受某活動，照顧者可能會溫柔地繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an impression based on behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述基於行為而產生的印象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"having it done","meaning":"被人這樣做","examples":[{"en":"The horses and donkeys seem to enjoy having it done.","zh":"馬和驢似乎很享受被人這樣做。"},{"en":"Having it done means receiving an action or service from someone else.","zh":"having it done 指接受別人為自己做某個動作或服務。"},{"en":"Some people enjoy having their hair washed at a salon.","zh":"有些人享受在髮型屋被人洗頭。"},{"en":"If animals enjoy having it done, they may stand still while being groomed.","zh":"如果動物享受被人這樣做，牠們可能在梳理毛髮時站定。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on receiving an action rather than doing it yourself.","zh":"這個短語重點在接受動作，而不是自己做。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"no longer live in","meaning":"不再住在……","examples":[{"en":"The horses no longer live in the stables.","zh":"馬不再住在馬廄裡。"},{"en":"No longer live in means used to live there but do not live there now.","zh":"no longer live in 指以前住在那裡，但現在不再住。"},{"en":"My grandparents no longer live in the old village house.","zh":"我的祖父母不再住在舊村屋裡。"},{"en":"If animals no longer live in a building, that building can be used for another purpose.","zh":"如果動物不再住在某建築裡，該建築可以作其他用途。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a past living arrangement has ended.","zh":"這個短語顯示過去的居住安排已結束。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stables","meaning":"馬廄","examples":[{"en":"The horses no longer live in the stables.","zh":"馬不再住在馬廄裡。"},{"en":"Stables are buildings where horses are kept and cared for.","zh":"stables 指飼養和照顧馬匹的建築物。"},{"en":"The riding school has stables beside the training field.","zh":"騎術學校在訓練場旁邊有馬廄。"},{"en":"If stables are clean and dry, horses stay healthier.","zh":"如果馬廄乾淨乾爽，馬匹會更健康。"},{"en":"This word refers to horse housing.","zh":"這個字指馬匹住所。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"instead","meaning":"反而","examples":[{"en":"The stables instead are used as a shop.","zh":"馬廄反而被用作商店。"},{"en":"Instead means that something different happens or is used in place of the expected thing.","zh":"instead 指發生或使用另一件事，取代原本預期的事。"},{"en":"The old classroom is not used for lessons anymore; instead, it is a music room.","zh":"舊課室不再用來上課；反而成了音樂室。"},{"en":"If a building is no longer needed for animals, it may be used as a shop instead.","zh":"如果建築物不再需要用來養動物，它可能反而被用作商店。"},{"en":"This word signals a different use or choice.","zh":"這個字表示不同用途或選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the place to go to buy","meaning":"購買……的地方","examples":[{"en":"The stables are the place to go to buy gifts and books.","zh":"馬廄是購買禮品和書籍的地方。"},{"en":"The place to go to buy something means the best or usual place for purchasing it.","zh":"the place to go to buy something 指購買某物的最佳或常去地點。"},{"en":"The school bookshop is the place to go to buy exercise books and pens.","zh":"學校書店是購買練習簿和筆的地方。"},{"en":"If visitors know the place to go to buy gifts, they can shop before leaving.","zh":"如果訪客知道購買禮品的地方，就能在離開前購物。"},{"en":"This phrase recommends where to purchase something.","zh":"這個短語推薦在哪裡購買某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"our own jams and pickles","meaning":"我們自製的果醬和醃菜","examples":[{"en":"The shop sells the estate’s own jams and pickles.","zh":"商店售賣莊園自製的果醬和醃菜。"},{"en":"Our own jams and pickles means sweet fruit preserves and preserved vegetables made by the place itself.","zh":"our own jams and pickles 指該地方自己製作的水果果醬和醃製蔬菜。"},{"en":"A farm shop may sell its own jams and pickles made from local fruit and vegetables.","zh":"農場商店可能售賣用本地水果和蔬菜製作的自家果醬和醃菜。"},{"en":"If products are made on the estate, visitors may see them as more special.","zh":"如果產品在莊園內製作，訪客可能覺得它們更特別。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights homemade or local produce.","zh":"這個短語突出自製或本地農產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"made of wool","meaning":"由羊毛製成","examples":[{"en":"The shop sells clothes and blankets made of wool from the estate’s sheep.","zh":"商店售賣由莊園羊隻羊毛製成的衣服和毛氈。"},{"en":"Made of wool means produced from the soft hair of sheep or similar animals.","zh":"made of wool 指由羊或類似動物的柔軟毛製成。"},{"en":"A winter scarf made of wool can keep people warm.","zh":"由羊毛製成的冬天圍巾可以保暖。"},{"en":"If blankets are made of wool, they may feel thick, warm, and natural.","zh":"如果毛氈由羊毛製成，它們可能感覺厚實、溫暖和天然。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the material used to make something.","zh":"這個短語指出製作某物的材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"wool from our sheep","meaning":"來自我們羊隻的羊毛","examples":[{"en":"The clothes are made of wool from the estate’s sheep.","zh":"這些衣服由莊園羊隻的羊毛製成。"},{"en":"Wool from our sheep means wool produced by sheep kept on the farm or estate.","zh":"wool from our sheep 指由農場或莊園飼養的羊產出的羊毛。"},{"en":"A farm may sell hats made from wool from its own sheep.","zh":"農場可能售賣由自家羊隻羊毛製成的帽子。"},{"en":"If wool comes from the estate’s sheep, the product feels closely connected to the place.","zh":"如果羊毛來自莊園羊隻，產品會感覺與該地方關係更密切。"},{"en":"This phrase links a product to local animals.","zh":"這個短語把產品與本地動物連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"outside the shed","meaning":"在棚屋外","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can climb into a carriage outside the shed.","zh":"訪客可以在棚屋外登上一架馬車。"},{"en":"Outside the shed means in the area just beyond or near the shed building.","zh":"outside the shed 指在棚屋建築外面或附近的地方。"},{"en":"The children waited outside the shed before the farm activity began.","zh":"農場活動開始前，小朋友在棚屋外等候。"},{"en":"If an attraction is outside the shed, visitors should follow signs to find it.","zh":"如果景點在棚屋外，訪客應跟隨指示牌尋找。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a location near a small farm building.","zh":"這個短語提供小型農場建築附近的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the only brick building","meaning":"唯一的磚建築","examples":[{"en":"The shed is the only brick building on the farm.","zh":"這座棚屋是農場上唯一的磚建築。"},{"en":"The only brick building means the one building made of brick, while the others are made of different materials.","zh":"the only brick building 指唯一由磚建成的建築，其他建築則用不同材料。"},{"en":"The old office is the only brick building among the wooden huts.","zh":"舊辦公室是木屋之中唯一的磚建築。"},{"en":"If a building is the only brick building, it may stand out visually.","zh":"如果一座建築是唯一的磚建築，它可能在視覺上特別突出。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a unique building material in a group.","zh":"這個短語指出一組建築中獨特的建材。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"climb into","meaning":"登上","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can climb into a horse-drawn carriage.","zh":"訪客可以登上一架馬車。"},{"en":"To climb into something means to get into it, often by stepping up or using effort.","zh":"climb into something 指進入某物，通常需要踏上去或花點力氣。"},{"en":"Children climbed into the bus carefully before the school trip.","zh":"學校旅行前，小朋友小心登上巴士。"},{"en":"If a carriage is high, visitors may need help to climb into it safely.","zh":"如果馬車較高，訪客可能需要協助才能安全登上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes entering something by moving upward or carefully inside.","zh":"這個短語描述向上或小心地進入某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"horse-drawn carriage","meaning":"馬車","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can ride in a horse-drawn carriage.","zh":"訪客可以乘坐馬車。"},{"en":"A horse-drawn carriage is a vehicle pulled by one or more horses.","zh":"horse-drawn carriage 指由一匹或多匹馬拉動的交通工具。"},{"en":"A historic town may offer horse-drawn carriage rides for tourists.","zh":"歷史小鎮可能為遊客提供馬車遊覽。"},{"en":"If people ride in a horse-drawn carriage, they can imagine transport before cars.","zh":"如果人們乘坐馬車，就能想像汽車出現前的交通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an old form of transport.","zh":"這個短語描述舊式交通工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"relaxing tour of","meaning":"輕鬆遊覽……","examples":[{"en":"The carriage offers a relaxing tour of the park and farm.","zh":"馬車提供輕鬆遊覽公園和農場的行程。"},{"en":"A relaxing tour of a place is a calm and pleasant visit around it.","zh":"relaxing tour of a place 指平靜而愉快地參觀某地。"},{"en":"A boat ride can offer a relaxing tour of the harbour.","zh":"乘船可以輕鬆遊覽海港。"},{"en":"If a tour is relaxing, visitors can enjoy the scenery without feeling rushed.","zh":"如果遊覽很輕鬆，訪客可以欣賞景色而不覺得趕急。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a peaceful sightseeing experience.","zh":"這個短語描述平和的觀光體驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"well over","meaning":"遠超過","examples":[{"en":"The carriages are well over a hundred years old.","zh":"這些馬車遠超過一百年歷史。"},{"en":"Well over means much more than a stated number or amount.","zh":"well over 指遠遠超過所說的數字或數量。"},{"en":"The school has well over a thousand students.","zh":"這所學校有遠超過一千名學生。"},{"en":"If an object is well over a century old, it needs careful preservation.","zh":"如果一件物品遠超過一個世紀歷史，就需要小心保存。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the number is clearly higher than the figure given.","zh":"這個短語強調數字明顯高於所給數值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a hundred years old","meaning":"有一百年歷史","examples":[{"en":"The carriages are over a hundred years old.","zh":"這些馬車有超過一百年歷史。"},{"en":"A hundred years old means having existed for one century.","zh":"a hundred years old 指已存在一個世紀。"},{"en":"The village hall is almost a hundred years old.","zh":"村公所差不多有一百年歷史。"},{"en":"If a carriage is a hundred years old, it can show visitors how people travelled long ago.","zh":"如果馬車有一百年歷史，它可以向訪客展示很久以前人們如何出行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes age in years.","zh":"這個短語描述年齡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"and finally","meaning":"最後","examples":[{"en":"And finally, the guide introduces the parkland.","zh":"最後，導賞員介紹園林綠地。"},{"en":"And finally is used to introduce the last point, place, or item in a list.","zh":"and finally 用來引出清單中的最後一點、地方或項目。"},{"en":"And finally, the teacher reminded students to bring their ID cards.","zh":"最後，老師提醒學生帶身份證。"},{"en":"If a guide says “and finally,” visitors know the introduction is near the end.","zh":"如果導賞員說 and finally，訪客就知道介紹接近尾聲。"},{"en":"This phrase signals the final part of a sequence.","zh":"這個短語標示一連串內容的最後部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be laid out","meaning":"被規劃；被設計","examples":[{"en":"The parkland was laid out in the eighteenth century.","zh":"園林綠地在十八世紀被規劃。"},{"en":"To be laid out means to be planned, arranged, or designed in a particular way.","zh":"be laid out 指以某種方式被規劃、安排或設計。"},{"en":"The school garden was laid out with paths, benches, and flower beds.","zh":"學校花園被設計成有小徑、長椅和花圃。"},{"en":"If a park is laid out carefully, visitors can walk through it easily.","zh":"如果公園被仔細規劃，訪客可以容易地走過。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planned design of space.","zh":"這個短語描述空間的規劃設計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"well established","meaning":"已長成；根基穩固","examples":[{"en":"The trees in the parkland are now well established.","zh":"園林綠地中的樹木現在已長成。"},{"en":"Well established means fully grown, settled, or firmly developed.","zh":"well established 指已完全成長、穩定或發展牢固。"},{"en":"A well-established tree has strong roots and can survive normal weather.","zh":"已長成的樹有強壯根部，能承受一般天氣。"},{"en":"If a business is well established, customers already know and trust it.","zh":"如果企業根基穩固，顧客已認識並信任它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something stable and firmly rooted.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定和紮根的狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"types of cattle and sheep","meaning":"牛羊品種","examples":[{"en":"Visitors will see types of cattle and sheep that are now rare.","zh":"訪客會看到現已罕見的牛羊品種。"},{"en":"Types of cattle and sheep means different breeds or varieties of cows and sheep.","zh":"types of cattle and sheep 指不同牛和羊的品種或種類。"},{"en":"A farm show may display old types of cattle and sheep for children to learn about.","zh":"農場展覽可能展示古老牛羊品種，讓孩子學習。"},{"en":"If some types of cattle and sheep become rare, conservation work may be needed.","zh":"如果某些牛羊品種變得罕見，可能需要保育工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes animal varieties in farming.","zh":"這個短語描述農業中的動物品種。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hardly ever found","meaning":"幾乎不再見到","examples":[{"en":"Some types of cattle and sheep are hardly ever found on farms these days.","zh":"有些牛羊品種現今在農場幾乎不再見到。"},{"en":"Hardly ever found means almost never seen or discovered.","zh":"hardly ever found 指幾乎從不被看見或發現。"},{"en":"Old red telephone boxes are hardly ever found in modern city streets.","zh":"舊式紅色電話亭在現代城市街道幾乎不再見到。"},{"en":"If a breed is hardly ever found, it may be close to disappearing.","zh":"如果某品種幾乎不再見到，它可能接近消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme rarity.","zh":"這個短語描述極度罕見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"these days","meaning":"現今","examples":[{"en":"These types of animals are rarely found on farms these days.","zh":"這些類型的動物現今在農場很少見到。"},{"en":"These days means nowadays or in the present period.","zh":"these days 指現今或目前這個時期。"},{"en":"These days, many students use tablets instead of paper dictionaries.","zh":"現今，許多學生使用平板電腦，而不是紙本字典。"},{"en":"If something is rare these days, it used to be more common in the past.","zh":"如果某物現今很罕見，它過去可能較常見。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the present with earlier times.","zh":"這個短語把現在與較早時代作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"help to preserve","meaning":"協助保育","examples":[{"en":"The estate is helping to preserve rare types of cattle and sheep.","zh":"這個莊園正在協助保育罕見牛羊品種。"},{"en":"To help to preserve something means to support efforts to protect it from damage, loss, or extinction.","zh":"help to preserve something 指支持保護某物，使其免受破壞、流失或滅絕。"},{"en":"Schools can help to preserve local history by recording elderly residents’ stories.","zh":"學校可以透過記錄長者故事協助保存本地歷史。"},{"en":"If farms help to preserve rare breeds, future generations may still see them.","zh":"如果農場協助保育罕見品種，後代仍可能看到牠們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes assisting protection and survival.","zh":"這個短語描述協助保護和延續。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"stop their numbers falling further","meaning":"防止牠們數量進一步下降","examples":[{"en":"The estate wants to stop the animals’ numbers falling further.","zh":"這個莊園想防止這些動物的數量進一步下降。"},{"en":"To stop their numbers falling further means to prevent a population from becoming even smaller.","zh":"stop their numbers falling further 指防止某族群數量變得更少。"},{"en":"Conservationists plant trees to stop bird numbers falling further.","zh":"保育人士植樹，以防止鳥類數量進一步下降。"},{"en":"If a rare breed keeps declining, breeding programmes may be needed to stop the fall.","zh":"如果罕見品種持續減少，可能需要繁殖計劃來阻止下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preventing further decline.","zh":"這個短語描述防止進一步減少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"if you’d like to come with me","meaning":"如果大家願意跟我來","examples":[{"en":"The guide says, “If you’d like to come with me, we can begin the tour.”","zh":"導賞員說：「如果大家願意跟我來，我們可以開始導賞。」"},{"en":"If you’d like to come with me is a polite way to invite people to follow you.","zh":"if you’d like to come with me 是禮貌地邀請人跟隨自己的說法。"},{"en":"A receptionist may say, “If you’d like to come with me, I’ll show you the meeting room.”","zh":"接待員可能說：「如果你願意跟我來，我會帶你看會議室。」"},{"en":"If a guide uses this phrase, the tour can begin smoothly and politely.","zh":"如果導賞員使用這個短語，導賞可以自然又禮貌地開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is gentle, formal, and useful for leading visitors.","zh":"這個短語語氣溫和、正式，適合帶領訪客。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 13/task-3":[{"front":"make notes","meaning":"做筆記","examples":[{"en":"Ed asks whether Gemma made notes while watching the performances.","zh":"Ed 問 Gemma 在觀看演出期間是否做了筆記。"},{"en":"To make notes means to write down important points so you can remember them later.","zh":"做筆記意思是寫下重要重點，以便之後記得。"},{"en":"Students often make notes during a lecture so they can revise more easily.","zh":"學生常在講座期間做筆記，方便之後溫習。"},{"en":"Making notes during a play can be difficult because the audience also wants to enjoy the performance.","zh":"在觀看戲劇時做筆記可能很困難，因為觀眾也想享受演出。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for study, meetings, lectures and research.","zh":"這個短語適合用於學習、會議、講座和研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"while watching","meaning":"在觀看……期間","examples":[{"en":"Gemma made notes while watching the performances of Romeo and Juliet.","zh":"Gemma 在觀看《羅密歐與茱麗葉》的演出期間做了筆記。"},{"en":"While watching means during the time someone is looking at or viewing something.","zh":"在觀看……期間意思是在某人觀看某物的時間內。"},{"en":"Students may write down useful phrases while watching an English video.","zh":"學生可能在觀看英文影片期間寫下有用短語。"},{"en":"Doing another task while watching a performance can divide your attention.","zh":"在觀看演出期間做另一件事，可能會分散注意力。"},{"en":"This phrase links an action with something happening at the same time.","zh":"這個短語把一個行動與同時發生的事情連起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"performances of","meaning":"……的演出","examples":[{"en":"The students watched several performances of Romeo and Juliet.","zh":"學生觀看了幾個《羅密歐與茱麗葉》的演出版本。"},{"en":"Performances of a play are staged versions acted in front of an audience or recorded for viewing.","zh":"某劇的演出是由演員在觀眾面前或錄影中呈現的舞台版本。"},{"en":"A drama class may compare different performances of the same Shakespeare play.","zh":"戲劇課可能比較同一齣莎士比亞劇作的不同演出。"},{"en":"Different performances of one play can feel very different because directors make different choices.","zh":"同一齣劇的不同演出可以感覺很不同，因為導演會作出不同選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing theatre, music or dance productions.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論戲劇、音樂或舞蹈製作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"find it quite hard","meaning":"覺得相當困難","examples":[{"en":"Gemma found it quite hard to make notes during the play.","zh":"Gemma 覺得在戲劇期間做筆記相當困難。"},{"en":"To find it quite hard means to feel that something is rather difficult.","zh":"覺得相當困難意思是認為某事頗難做到。"},{"en":"A student may find it quite hard to understand Shakespeare’s language at first.","zh":"學生起初可能覺得理解莎士比亞的語言相當困難。"},{"en":"People often find it hard to take notes and follow fast dialogue at the same time.","zh":"人們常覺得同時做筆記和跟上快速對白很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal difficulty with a task.","zh":"這個短語描述某人對任務的個人困難感受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get too involved in","meaning":"太投入於……","examples":[{"en":"Gemma kept getting too involved in the play.","zh":"Gemma 不斷太投入於那齣戲。"},{"en":"To get too involved in something means to become so emotionally or mentally engaged that it is hard to focus on anything else.","zh":"太投入於某事意思是情感上或思想上太投入，以致難以專注其他事情。"},{"en":"A reader may get too involved in a novel and forget to check the time.","zh":"讀者可能太投入於小說，而忘記查看時間。"},{"en":"Getting too involved in a performance can make note-taking difficult.","zh":"太投入於演出可能令做筆記變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes strong emotional engagement.","zh":"這個短語常描述強烈的情感投入。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"end up doing","meaning":"最後做了……","examples":[{"en":"Ed ended up not taking notes during the performance.","zh":"Ed 最後在演出期間沒有做筆記。"},{"en":"To end up doing something means to finally do it, often although it was not the original plan.","zh":"最後做某事意思是最終做了該事，通常並非原本計劃。"},{"en":"A student may end up rewriting the whole essay after receiving feedback.","zh":"學生收到回饋後，可能最後重寫整篇文章。"},{"en":"If a performance is very engaging, viewers may end up watching instead of analysing.","zh":"如果演出很吸引，觀眾可能最後只是觀看，而不是分析。"},{"en":"This phrase often points to the final result of a situation.","zh":"這個短語常指一個情況的最終結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"write down","meaning":"寫下","examples":[{"en":"Ed wrote down his impressions when he got home.","zh":"Ed 回到家時寫下自己的觀感。"},{"en":"To write down something means to record it in writing.","zh":"寫下某事意思是用文字記錄它。"},{"en":"Students should write down useful vocabulary when they hear it in class.","zh":"學生在課堂聽到有用詞彙時應寫下來。"},{"en":"Writing ideas down quickly can help prevent them from being forgotten.","zh":"快速寫下想法可以防止它們被忘記。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in study, meetings and everyday reminders.","zh":"這個短語常見於學習、會議和日常提醒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"my impressions","meaning":"我的觀感","examples":[{"en":"Ed wrote down his impressions after watching the play.","zh":"Ed 觀看那齣戲後寫下自己的觀感。"},{"en":"My impressions means my first thoughts, feelings or opinions about something.","zh":"我的觀感意思是我對某事的初步想法、感受或意見。"},{"en":"After visiting a university, a student may write down their impressions of the campus.","zh":"參觀大學後，學生可能寫下自己對校園的觀感。"},{"en":"Impressions can include what seemed powerful, weak, beautiful or confusing.","zh":"觀感可以包括甚麼看似有力、薄弱、美麗或令人困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing personal response to an experience.","zh":"當討論對一段經驗的個人反應時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"when I got home","meaning":"當我回到家時","examples":[{"en":"Ed wrote down his impressions when he got home.","zh":"Ed 當他回到家時寫下自己的觀感。"},{"en":"When I got home means at the time I arrived back at my house or flat.","zh":"當我回到家時意思是我回到自己家中或住所的時候。"},{"en":"When I got home, I checked my notes and added more details.","zh":"當我回到家時，我查看筆記並加入更多細節。"},{"en":"People often remember an event better if they write about it soon after getting home.","zh":"如果人們回家後很快寫下經歷，通常會記得更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the time when an action happened.","zh":"這個短語交代行動發生的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"do you mind if","meaning":"你介意我……嗎？","examples":[{"en":"Ed asks Gemma, “Do you mind if I check a few things with you?”","zh":"Ed 問 Gemma：「你介意我和你確認幾件事嗎？」"},{"en":"Do you mind if is a polite way to ask for permission.","zh":"你介意我……嗎是一種有禮貌地請求許可的說法。"},{"en":"Do you mind if I borrow your notes for a few minutes?","zh":"你介意我借你的筆記幾分鐘嗎？"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when you want to make a request without sounding too direct.","zh":"當你想提出要求但不想太直接時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It is common in polite spoken English.","zh":"它常見於有禮貌的口語英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"check a few things with","meaning":"和……確認幾件事","examples":[{"en":"Ed wants to check a few things with Gemma.","zh":"Ed 想和 Gemma 確認幾件事。"},{"en":"To check a few things with someone means to confirm several details by asking that person.","zh":"和某人確認幾件事意思是透過詢問該人來核實幾個細節。"},{"en":"A student may check a few things with a classmate before submitting a group project.","zh":"學生可能在提交小組專題前和同學確認幾件事。"},{"en":"Checking details with someone can help avoid misunderstandings.","zh":"和某人確認細節可以幫助避免誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing notes or confirming information.","zh":"當比較筆記或核實資料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in case","meaning":"以防","examples":[{"en":"Ed wants to check the details in case he has missed anything.","zh":"Ed 想核實細節，以防自己漏掉任何東西。"},{"en":"In case means because something might happen or might have happened.","zh":"以防意思是因為某事可能會發生或可能已發生。"},{"en":"Take an umbrella in case it rains later.","zh":"帶把雨傘，以防稍後下雨。"},{"en":"Students may check their answers again in case they have made careless mistakes.","zh":"學生可能再次檢查答案，以防犯了粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a precaution.","zh":"這個短語引入預防措施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"miss anything","meaning":"漏掉任何東西","examples":[{"en":"Ed wants to make sure he has not missed anything important.","zh":"Ed 想確保自己沒有漏掉任何重要東西。"},{"en":"To miss anything means to fail to notice, hear or include something.","zh":"漏掉任何東西意思是未能注意、聽到或包括某些內容。"},{"en":"A student should read the question carefully so they do not miss anything.","zh":"學生應仔細閱讀題目，以免漏掉任何東西。"},{"en":"In a theatre review, missing an important scene can weaken the analysis.","zh":"在劇評中，如果漏掉重要場景，分析會變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when checking completeness.","zh":"這個短語常用於檢查是否完整。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have questions about","meaning":"對……有問題","examples":[{"en":"Ed has some questions about the assignment.","zh":"Ed 對作業有一些問題。"},{"en":"To have questions about something means to be unsure and want more information about it.","zh":"對某事有問題意思是對它不確定，並想知道更多資料。"},{"en":"A student may have questions about the marking criteria before writing an essay.","zh":"學生在寫文章前可能對評分準則有問題。"},{"en":"Asking questions helps people understand a task more clearly.","zh":"提問有助人們更清楚理解任務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in school, work and discussion settings.","zh":"這個短語適合用於學校、工作和討論場合。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"assignment","meaning":"作業","examples":[{"en":"The students need to write reviews for their assignment.","zh":"學生需要為作業寫評論。"},{"en":"An assignment is a piece of school, college or work task that someone has to complete.","zh":"作業是學生、大學生或員工需要完成的一項任務。"},{"en":"The teacher gave an assignment about comparing two film versions of the same story.","zh":"老師給了一份關於比較同一故事兩個電影版本的作業。"},{"en":"Assignments often require research, planning and clear writing.","zh":"作業通常需要資料搜集、規劃和清楚寫作。"},{"en":"This word is common in education.","zh":"這個詞常見於教育語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"talk things through","meaning":"把事情討論清楚","examples":[{"en":"Gemma says it is good to talk things through.","zh":"Gemma 說把事情討論清楚是好的。"},{"en":"To talk things through means to discuss details carefully until people understand them better.","zh":"把事情討論清楚意思是仔細討論細節，直到大家更明白。"},{"en":"Group members should talk things through before deciding who writes each section.","zh":"小組成員應先把事情討論清楚，再決定誰寫每一部分。"},{"en":"Talking things through can help solve confusion and reveal missing points.","zh":"把事情討論清楚可以幫助解決混亂，並發現遺漏重點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful discussion.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"first of all","meaning":"首先","examples":[{"en":"First of all, Ed asks how much information to include.","zh":"首先，Ed 問應包括多少資料。"},{"en":"First of all is used to introduce the first point or question.","zh":"首先用來引入第一個重點或問題。"},{"en":"First of all, we need to decide the topic of the presentation.","zh":"首先，我們需要決定匯報主題。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise a conversation or essay clearly.","zh":"這個短語有助清楚組織對話或文章。"},{"en":"It is useful when several points will follow.","zh":"當之後會有幾個重點時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not sure how much","meaning":"不確定有多少……","examples":[{"en":"Ed is not sure how much information they should include in their reviews.","zh":"Ed 不確定他們應在評論中包括多少資料。"},{"en":"Not sure how much means uncertain about the correct amount.","zh":"不確定有多少意思是對正確數量不肯定。"},{"en":"A student may be not sure how much detail to include in a short answer.","zh":"學生可能不確定短答題要包括多少細節。"},{"en":"Being unsure about the amount of information can make writing harder.","zh":"不確定資料量會令寫作更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uncertainty about quantity or extent.","zh":"這個短語描述對數量或程度的不確定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"include in","meaning":"包括在……之中","examples":[{"en":"The students need to decide what to include in their reviews.","zh":"學生需要決定評論中要包括甚麼。"},{"en":"To include something in a piece of writing means to put it inside as part of the content.","zh":"把某事包括在文章之中，意思是把它作為內容的一部分放進去。"},{"en":"A review should include comments on acting, design and overall impact.","zh":"評論應包括對演技、設計和整體效果的評語。"},{"en":"Choosing what to include is important when the word limit is short.","zh":"當字數限制很短，選擇包括甚麼很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when planning writing content.","zh":"當規劃寫作內容時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reviews","meaning":"評論","examples":[{"en":"The students are writing reviews of the theatre production.","zh":"學生正在寫這個劇場製作的評論。"},{"en":"Reviews are pieces of writing that evaluate and comment on books, films, plays, restaurants or performances.","zh":"評論是評價並評論書籍、電影、戲劇、餐廳或演出的文章。"},{"en":"A theatre review may discuss acting, staging, lighting and audience response.","zh":"劇評可能討論演技、舞台安排、燈光和觀眾反應。"},{"en":"Good reviews give opinions but also support them with clear examples.","zh":"好評論會提出意見，同時用清楚例子支持。"},{"en":"This word is common in arts, media and consumer writing.","zh":"這個詞常見於藝術、媒體和消費寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"describe what happens","meaning":"描述劇情發生甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Gemma does not think they need to describe what happens in the play.","zh":"Gemma 不認為他們需要描述劇中發生甚麼。"},{"en":"To describe what happens means to explain the events or plot.","zh":"描述劇情發生甚麼意思是解釋事件或情節。"},{"en":"A review should not only describe what happens, but also judge how well it is presented.","zh":"評論不應只描述發生甚麼，也應評價呈現得好不好。"},{"en":"Describing too much plot can waste space in a short review.","zh":"在短評論中描述太多劇情會浪費篇幅。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on retelling events.","zh":"這個短語重點是重述事件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"especially as","meaning":"尤其是因為","examples":[{"en":"They do not need to describe the plot, especially as Romeo and Juliet is well known.","zh":"他們不需要描述劇情，尤其是因為《羅密歐與茱麗葉》很有名。"},{"en":"Especially as means particularly because.","zh":"尤其是因為意思是特別由於某原因。"},{"en":"We should arrive early, especially as the theatre is usually crowded.","zh":"我們應早點到達，尤其是因為劇院通常很擠迫。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strong reason for the previous statement.","zh":"這個短語為前一句提供強而有力的原因。"},{"en":"It is useful when one reason is especially important.","zh":"當某個原因特別重要時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"one of Shakespeare’s most well-known plays","meaning":"莎士比亞最知名劇作之一","examples":[{"en":"Romeo and Juliet is one of Shakespeare’s most well-known plays.","zh":"《羅密歐與茱麗葉》是莎士比亞最知名劇作之一。"},{"en":"One of Shakespeare’s most well-known plays means one play among his most famous works.","zh":"莎士比亞最知名劇作之一意思是他最有名作品中的其中一齣。"},{"en":"Hamlet is also one of Shakespeare’s most well-known plays.","zh":"《哈姆雷特》也是莎士比亞最知名劇作之一。"},{"en":"Well-known plays often need less plot summary because many readers already know the story.","zh":"知名劇作通常需要較少劇情摘要，因為許多讀者已知道故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fame within Shakespeare’s works.","zh":"這個短語描述作品在莎士比亞劇作中的知名度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"everyone knows the story","meaning":"大家都知道故事","examples":[{"en":"Ed says everyone knows the story of Romeo and Juliet.","zh":"Ed 說大家都知道《羅密歐與茱麗葉》的故事。"},{"en":"Everyone knows the story means the plot is very familiar to most people.","zh":"大家都知道故事意思是情節對大多數人來說很熟悉。"},{"en":"Everyone knows the story of Cinderella, so a review may focus on the new interpretation.","zh":"大家都知道灰姑娘的故事，所以評論可以集中於新的詮釋。"},{"en":"When everyone knows the story, writers can spend more time discussing performance choices.","zh":"當大家都知道故事，作者可以花更多時間討論演出選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that detailed explanation may not be necessary.","zh":"這個短語強調詳細解釋可能不必要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in an essay","meaning":"在論文中","examples":[{"en":"In an essay, students would focus on Shakespeare’s language.","zh":"在論文中，學生會聚焦於莎士比亞的語言。"},{"en":"In an essay means in a formal piece of writing that develops an argument or analysis.","zh":"在論文中意思是在一篇發展論點或分析的正式文章中。"},{"en":"In an essay about poetry, students may analyse word choice and imagery.","zh":"在關於詩歌的論文中，學生可能分析用字和意象。"},{"en":"An essay often requires deeper analysis than a short review.","zh":"論文通常比短評論需要更深入分析。"},{"en":"This phrase sets the writing context.","zh":"這個短語設定寫作語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"聚焦於……","examples":[{"en":"In a review, students should focus on this particular production.","zh":"在評論中，學生應聚焦於這個特定製作版本。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give main attention to it.","zh":"聚焦於某事意思是把主要注意力放在它上面。"},{"en":"A film review should focus on how the film works, not only on the plot.","zh":"影評應聚焦於電影如何運作，而不只是劇情。"},{"en":"Focusing on the right topic helps writing stay clear and relevant.","zh":"聚焦於正確主題有助文章保持清楚和相關。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main subject of attention.","zh":"這個短語指出注意力的主要對象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the poetry","meaning":"詩性語言","examples":[{"en":"An essay might focus on the poetry in Shakespeare’s writing.","zh":"論文可能聚焦於莎士比亞寫作中的詩性語言。"},{"en":"The poetry means the poetic qualities of language, such as rhythm, imagery and emotional expression.","zh":"詩性語言意思是語言中的詩意特質，例如節奏、意象和情感表達。"},{"en":"A literature essay may discuss the poetry of Shakespeare’s speeches.","zh":"文學論文可能討論莎士比亞獨白中的詩性語言。"},{"en":"The poetry of a text can create beauty, feeling and deeper meaning.","zh":"文本中的詩性語言可以創造美感、情感和更深層意義。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on literary language rather than stage performance.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於文學語言，而不是舞台演出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"use of imagery","meaning":"意象的運用","examples":[{"en":"An essay might analyse Shakespeare’s use of imagery.","zh":"論文可能分析莎士比亞對意象的運用。"},{"en":"Use of imagery means the way a writer creates pictures in the reader’s mind through language.","zh":"意象的運用意思是作者如何透過語言在讀者腦中創造畫面。"},{"en":"A poet’s use of imagery can make a scene feel vivid and emotional.","zh":"詩人對意象的運用可以令場景感覺鮮明而有情感。"},{"en":"Analysing imagery is common in literature essays.","zh":"分析意象常見於文學論文。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a writer’s method of using descriptive images.","zh":"這個短語指作者使用描述性畫面的方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be relevant in","meaning":"在……中相關","examples":[{"en":"Shakespeare’s use of imagery is not really relevant in a theatre review.","zh":"莎士比亞對意象的運用在劇評中並不太相關。"},{"en":"To be relevant in something means to be directly connected with the purpose or topic of that context.","zh":"在某情境中相關意思是與該情境的目的或主題直接有關。"},{"en":"Detailed grammar analysis may not be relevant in a short film review.","zh":"詳細文法分析在短影評中可能不太相關。"},{"en":"Choosing relevant points helps a writer stay within the task.","zh":"選擇相關重點有助作者符合任務要求。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when deciding what to include or leave out.","zh":"當決定包括或刪去哪些內容時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be supposed to","meaning":"應該；按要求要","examples":[{"en":"The students are supposed to focus on how effective the production is.","zh":"學生按要求應聚焦於這個製作版本有多有效。"},{"en":"To be supposed to do something means to be expected or required to do it.","zh":"應該做某事意思是被期望或被要求做該事。"},{"en":"Students are supposed to answer all questions in complete sentences.","zh":"學生應該用完整句子回答所有問題。"},{"en":"This phrase often refers to instructions, rules or expectations.","zh":"這個短語常指指示、規則或期望。"},{"en":"It helps explain what the task requires.","zh":"它有助解釋任務要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"how effective","meaning":"有多有效","examples":[{"en":"The review should discuss how effective this particular production is.","zh":"評論應討論這個特定製作版本有多有效。"},{"en":"How effective means how well something achieves its purpose.","zh":"有多有效意思是某事達成目的的程度。"},{"en":"A review may ask how effective the lighting is in creating tension.","zh":"評論可能詢問燈光在營造緊張感方面有多有效。"},{"en":"Discussing effectiveness means judging results, not just describing features.","zh":"討論有效程度意思是評價結果，而不只是描述特點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for evaluation.","zh":"這個短語適合用於評估。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"this particular production","meaning":"這個特定製作版本","examples":[{"en":"The review focuses on this particular production of Romeo and Juliet.","zh":"評論聚焦於《羅密歐與茱麗葉》的這個特定製作版本。"},{"en":"This particular production means this specific staged version of the play.","zh":"這個特定製作版本意思是這齣戲的這一個具體舞台版本。"},{"en":"This particular production uses modern costumes and unusual lighting.","zh":"這個特定製作版本使用現代服裝和不尋常燈光。"},{"en":"A theatre review should focus on the production seen, not every possible version of the play.","zh":"劇評應聚焦於看過的製作版本，而不是該劇所有可能版本。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the discussion to one version.","zh":"這個短語把討論收窄到一個版本。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what made it a success or a failure","meaning":"是甚麼令它成功或失敗","examples":[{"en":"The students should say what made the production a success or a failure.","zh":"學生應說明是甚麼令這個製作版本成功或失敗。"},{"en":"What made it a success or a failure means the reasons why it worked well or badly.","zh":"是甚麼令它成功或失敗意思是它表現好或差的原因。"},{"en":"A review should explain what made a performance powerful or disappointing.","zh":"評論應解釋是甚麼令演出有感染力或令人失望。"},{"en":"Strong evaluation identifies causes, such as acting, direction, set design or pacing.","zh":"有力評估會指出原因，例如演技、導演、布景設計或節奏。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when analysing results.","zh":"當分析結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"emotional impact","meaning":"情感影響","examples":[{"en":"The students should discuss the emotional impact of the performance.","zh":"學生應討論演出的情感影響。"},{"en":"Emotional impact means the effect something has on people’s feelings.","zh":"情感影響意思是某事對人們感受造成的效果。"},{"en":"A powerful ending can create a strong emotional impact on the audience.","zh":"有力的結尾可以對觀眾造成強烈情感影響。"},{"en":"Theatre reviews often discuss whether a performance moved, shocked or excited viewers.","zh":"劇評常討論演出是否感動、震撼或令觀眾興奮。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evaluating audience response.","zh":"當評估觀眾反應時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have an impact on","meaning":"對……有影響","examples":[{"en":"The performance had an emotional impact on the audience.","zh":"這場演出對觀眾有情感影響。"},{"en":"To have an impact on someone or something means to affect them in a noticeable way.","zh":"對某人或某事有影響意思是以明顯方式影響他們。"},{"en":"A teacher’s encouragement can have a strong impact on a student’s confidence.","zh":"老師的鼓勵可以對學生信心有強烈影響。"},{"en":"A performance has impact when viewers remember it after leaving the theatre.","zh":"當觀眾離開劇院後仍記得演出，該演出就是有影響力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes influence or effect.","zh":"這個短語描述影響或效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"definitely mention","meaning":"一定要提到","examples":[{"en":"The students should definitely mention the director’s handling of key scenes.","zh":"學生一定要提到導演對關鍵場景的處理。"},{"en":"To definitely mention something means to make sure it is included.","zh":"一定要提到某事意思是確保它被包括在內。"},{"en":"In a restaurant review, you should definitely mention the service if it affected the experience.","zh":"在餐廳評論中，如果服務影響了體驗，你一定要提到。"},{"en":"Important points should be mentioned clearly, especially when they shape your judgement.","zh":"重要重點應清楚提及，尤其是它們影響你的判斷時。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that something should not be left out.","zh":"這個短語強調某事不應被遺漏。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"how well","meaning":"做得有多好","examples":[{"en":"The review should discuss how well the director handled important scenes.","zh":"評論應討論導演處理重要場景做得有多好。"},{"en":"How well means the degree to which something was done successfully.","zh":"做得有多好意思是某事成功完成的程度。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask how well a student supported their argument with examples.","zh":"老師可能問學生用例子支持論點做得有多好。"},{"en":"Reviews often judge how well different production choices worked together.","zh":"評論常評價不同製作選擇配合得有多好。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for evaluating quality.","zh":"這個短語適合用於評估質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"handle important bits of","meaning":"處理……的重要部分","examples":[{"en":"The director handled important bits of the play in different ways.","zh":"導演以不同方式處理這齣戲的重要部分。"},{"en":"To handle important bits of something means to deal with key parts of it.","zh":"處理某事的重要部分意思是應對其中關鍵部分。"},{"en":"A film director must handle important bits of the story carefully so the audience understands them.","zh":"電影導演必須仔細處理故事的重要部分，讓觀眾明白。"},{"en":"Important scenes need careful handling because they affect the whole production.","zh":"重要場景需要小心處理，因為它們影響整個製作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how someone manages key sections.","zh":"當討論某人如何管理關鍵部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the balcony scene","meaning":"陽台一幕","examples":[{"en":"The balcony scene is one of the most famous moments in Romeo and Juliet.","zh":"陽台一幕是《羅密歐與茱麗葉》中最著名的時刻之一。"},{"en":"The balcony scene is the famous scene where Romeo speaks to Juliet near her balcony.","zh":"陽台一幕是 Romeo 在 Juliet 陽台附近與她說話的著名場景。"},{"en":"Directors often make strong choices about staging the balcony scene.","zh":"導演常對陽台一幕的舞台呈現作出強烈選擇。"},{"en":"Because the balcony scene is so well known, audiences may have clear expectations.","zh":"因為陽台一幕非常知名，觀眾可能有清楚期望。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an iconic moment in the play.","zh":"這個短語指該劇中的標誌性時刻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"climb onto","meaning":"爬上","examples":[{"en":"Romeo climbs onto Juliet’s balcony in one important scene.","zh":"Romeo 在一個重要場景中爬上 Juliet 的陽台。"},{"en":"To climb onto something means to move up and get onto its surface.","zh":"爬上某物意思是向上移動並到達其表面。"},{"en":"A child should not climb onto a high wall without adult supervision.","zh":"孩子不應在沒有成年人看管下爬上高牆。"},{"en":"On stage, climbing onto a balcony can create a dramatic visual moment.","zh":"在舞台上，爬上陽台可以創造戲劇性的視覺時刻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upward physical movement onto a place.","zh":"這個短語描述向上移動到某處的動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the fight between","meaning":"……之間的打鬥","examples":[{"en":"The fight between Mercutio and Tybalt is another important scene.","zh":"Mercutio 和 Tybalt 之間的打鬥是另一個重要場景。"},{"en":"The fight between two people means the physical or verbal conflict involving them.","zh":"兩人之間的打鬥意思是涉及他們的身體或言語衝突。"},{"en":"The fight between the two families drives much of the tragedy in the play.","zh":"兩個家族之間的衝突推動了劇中大部分悲劇。"},{"en":"A director’s handling of a fight scene can affect the play’s tension and pace.","zh":"導演處理打鬥場景的方式可以影響戲劇的緊張感和節奏。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the people involved in a conflict.","zh":"這個短語指出衝突中涉及的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"theatre space","meaning":"劇場空間","examples":[{"en":"It would be interesting to mention the theatre space.","zh":"提到劇場空間會很有趣。"},{"en":"Theatre space means the physical area used for the performance, including stage, seating and surroundings.","zh":"劇場空間意思是演出使用的實體區域，包括舞台、座位和周圍環境。"},{"en":"A small theatre space can make the audience feel close to the actors.","zh":"細小劇場空間可以令觀眾感覺接近演員。"},{"en":"The use of theatre space affects how viewers experience movement and atmosphere.","zh":"劇場空間的運用會影響觀眾如何感受動作和氣氛。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in theatre reviews and production analysis.","zh":"這個短語適合用於劇評和製作分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"use the theatre space","meaning":"運用劇場空間","examples":[{"en":"The review could discuss how the director used the theatre space.","zh":"評論可以討論導演如何運用劇場空間。"},{"en":"To use the theatre space means to make creative or practical use of the stage and performance area.","zh":"運用劇場空間意思是創意或實際地使用舞台和演出區域。"},{"en":"A director may use the theatre space by placing actors among the audience.","zh":"導演可能把演員安排在觀眾之間，以運用劇場空間。"},{"en":"Good use of space can make a performance feel more dynamic and immersive.","zh":"良好的空間運用可以令演出更有動感和沉浸感。"},{"en":"This phrase evaluates staging choices.","zh":"這個短語評價舞台安排選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have space in 800 words","meaning":"在800字內有篇幅","examples":[{"en":"The students may not have space in 800 words to discuss everything.","zh":"學生可能在 800 字內沒有篇幅討論所有事情。"},{"en":"To have space in 800 words means to have enough room within an 800-word limit.","zh":"在 800 字內有篇幅意思是在 800 字限制內有足夠空間。"},{"en":"In a short review, writers may not have space to discuss every costume and scene.","zh":"在短評論中，作者可能沒有篇幅討論每套服裝和每個場景。"},{"en":"Word limits force students to choose the most important points.","zh":"字數限制迫使學生選擇最重要的重點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about writing constraints.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論寫作限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sound quite straightforward","meaning":"聽起來相當清楚直接","examples":[{"en":"The assignment sounds quite straightforward to Ed.","zh":"這份作業對 Ed 來說聽起來相當清楚直接。"},{"en":"Sound quite straightforward means seem fairly simple and easy to understand.","zh":"聽起來相當清楚直接意思是看似頗簡單和容易理解。"},{"en":"The task sounds quite straightforward because the teacher gave clear instructions.","zh":"因為老師給了清楚指示，這項任務聽起來相當直接。"},{"en":"Something may sound straightforward at first but still need careful planning.","zh":"某事起初可能聽起來直接，但仍需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a first impression of clarity.","zh":"這個短語描述對清晰程度的第一印象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"production of the play","meaning":"這齣戲的製作版本","examples":[{"en":"The students discuss The Emporium Theatre’s production of the play.","zh":"學生討論 The Emporium Theatre 的這齣戲製作版本。"},{"en":"A production of a play is a particular staged version created by a theatre company or director.","zh":"一齣戲的製作版本是由劇團或導演創作的特定舞台版本。"},{"en":"One production of Romeo and Juliet may use modern costumes while another uses traditional dress.","zh":"一個《羅密歐與茱麗葉》製作版本可能使用現代服裝，另一個則使用傳統服裝。"},{"en":"Reviews focus on the choices made in a specific production.","zh":"評論聚焦於特定製作版本中的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a staged interpretation of a play.","zh":"這個短語指一齣戲的舞台詮釋版本。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"work really well","meaning":"效果非常好","examples":[{"en":"Gemma thought some things worked really well in the production.","zh":"Gemma 認為製作中有些東西效果非常好。"},{"en":"To work really well means to be very effective or successful.","zh":"效果非常好意思是非常有效或成功。"},{"en":"The lighting worked really well because it made the stage feel mysterious.","zh":"燈光效果非常好，因為它令舞台感覺神秘。"},{"en":"In a review, writers should explain why a choice worked well.","zh":"在評論中，作者應解釋為何某個選擇效果好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes successful effect, not just effort.","zh":"這個短語描述成功效果，而不只是努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"there were some problems","meaning":"也有一些問題","examples":[{"en":"There were some problems with the production too.","zh":"這個製作版本也有一些問題。"},{"en":"There were some problems means some aspects did not work well or caused difficulty.","zh":"也有一些問題意思是某些方面效果不好或造成困難。"},{"en":"There were some problems with the sound system during the school concert.","zh":"學校音樂會期間音響系統也有一些問題。"},{"en":"A balanced review should discuss strengths and problems.","zh":"平衡的評論應討論優點和問題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces criticism or limitations.","zh":"這個短語引入批評或限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the set","meaning":"布景","examples":[{"en":"Ed asks Gemma what she thought about the set.","zh":"Ed 問 Gemma 對布景有甚麼看法。"},{"en":"The set is the scenery and physical design on stage for a play or performance.","zh":"布景是戲劇或演出舞台上的景物和實體設計。"},{"en":"A theatre set may include walls, furniture, doors and platforms.","zh":"劇場布景可能包括牆壁、家具、門和平台。"},{"en":"The set can strongly affect the audience’s first impression of a production.","zh":"布景可以強烈影響觀眾對製作的第一印象。"},{"en":"This word is central to theatre design.","zh":"這個詞是劇場設計中的核心用語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"visually stunning","meaning":"視覺上令人驚艷","examples":[{"en":"Gemma thinks the set was visually stunning.","zh":"Gemma 認為布景在視覺上令人驚艷。"},{"en":"Visually stunning means extremely impressive or beautiful to look at.","zh":"視覺上令人驚艷意思是看起來極具震撼力或美感。"},{"en":"The opening scene was visually stunning because of the colours and lighting.","zh":"開場一幕因色彩和燈光而在視覺上令人驚艷。"},{"en":"A visually stunning set can make a production memorable even before the actors speak.","zh":"視覺上令人驚艷的布景可以在演員開口前已令製作難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on appearance and visual impact.","zh":"這個短語重點是外觀和視覺效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the most memorable thing","meaning":"最令人難忘之處","examples":[{"en":"The set was probably the most memorable thing about the production.","zh":"布景大概是這個製作版本最令人難忘之處。"},{"en":"The most memorable thing means the part that people are most likely to remember.","zh":"最令人難忘之處意思是人們最可能記住的部分。"},{"en":"The final song was the most memorable thing about the concert.","zh":"最後一首歌是音樂會最令人難忘之處。"},{"en":"In a review, identifying the most memorable thing helps explain what stood out.","zh":"在評論中，指出最令人難忘之處有助解釋甚麼特別突出。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights lasting impact.","zh":"這個短語突顯持久印象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"set design","meaning":"布景設計","examples":[{"en":"The set design was really impressive.","zh":"布景設計真的令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"Set design means the planning and creation of the scenery and stage environment.","zh":"布景設計意思是規劃和創造舞台景物及環境。"},{"en":"Good set design can show the time, place and mood of a play.","zh":"良好的布景設計可以展示戲劇的時間、地點和氣氛。"},{"en":"Set designers work with directors to create the visual world of a production.","zh":"布景設計師與導演合作，創造製作版本的視覺世界。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the artistic design of the stage setting.","zh":"這個短語指舞台環境的藝術設計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"similar ideas","meaning":"類似意念","examples":[{"en":"Ed has seen similar ideas used in other productions.","zh":"Ed 在其他製作版本中見過類似意念被使用。"},{"en":"Similar ideas are concepts that are alike but not exactly the same.","zh":"類似意念是相近但不完全相同的概念。"},{"en":"A director may use similar ideas in different plays to create a modern style.","zh":"導演可能在不同戲劇中使用類似意念來創造現代風格。"},{"en":"Seeing similar ideas elsewhere may make a design feel less original.","zh":"在其他地方見過類似意念，可能令設計感覺較不原創。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing creative choices.","zh":"當比較創作選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be used in","meaning":"被用於……","examples":[{"en":"Similar design ideas have been used in other productions.","zh":"類似設計意念曾被用於其他製作版本。"},{"en":"To be used in something means to appear or be applied there.","zh":"被用於某事意思是在其中出現或被應用。"},{"en":"Modern costumes are often used in new productions of classic plays.","zh":"現代服裝常被用於經典劇作的新製作版本。"},{"en":"A technique used in one production may inspire another director.","zh":"一個製作版本中使用的技巧可能啟發另一位導演。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where an idea, object or method appears.","zh":"這個短語描述意念、物件或方法出現在哪裏。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"other productions","meaning":"其他製作版本","examples":[{"en":"Ed has seen similar ideas in other theatre productions.","zh":"Ed 在其他劇場製作版本中見過類似意念。"},{"en":"Other productions means different staged versions or performances.","zh":"其他製作版本意思是不同的舞台版本或演出。"},{"en":"Other productions of the same play may choose different costumes, music and staging.","zh":"同一齣戲的其他製作版本可能選擇不同服裝、音樂和舞台安排。"},{"en":"Comparing other productions can help students judge what is original or effective.","zh":"比較其他製作版本可以幫助學生判斷甚麼是原創或有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in theatre comparison.","zh":"這個短語適合用於劇場比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lighting","meaning":"燈光","examples":[{"en":"Gemma comments on the lighting in the production.","zh":"Gemma 評論這個製作版本中的燈光。"},{"en":"Lighting means the use of light in a performance, film or room.","zh":"燈光意思是在演出、電影或房間中使用光線的方式。"},{"en":"Theatre lighting can show mood, time of day and focus on important characters.","zh":"劇場燈光可以顯示氣氛、一天中的時間，並突出重要角色。"},{"en":"Poor lighting may make scenes difficult to see or reduce emotional effect.","zh":"差的燈光可能令場景難以看清，或減弱情感效果。"},{"en":"This word is important in stage and film design.","zh":"這個詞在舞台和電影設計中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dimly lit","meaning":"燈光昏暗的","examples":[{"en":"Some of the scenes were so dimly lit that they were hard to see.","zh":"有些場景燈光如此昏暗，以致很難看清。"},{"en":"Dimly lit means having very little light.","zh":"燈光昏暗的意思是光線很少。"},{"en":"A dimly lit restaurant may feel romantic but make menus hard to read.","zh":"燈光昏暗的餐廳可能感覺浪漫，但會令餐牌難以閱讀。"},{"en":"On stage, dim lighting can create mystery but may hide important action.","zh":"在舞台上，昏暗燈光可以營造神秘感，但也可能遮住重要動作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low lighting conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述低光線情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"quite hard to see","meaning":"相當難看清","examples":[{"en":"The lighting made some scenes quite hard to see.","zh":"燈光令有些場景相當難看清。"},{"en":"Quite hard to see means rather difficult to view clearly.","zh":"相當難看清意思是頗難清楚觀看。"},{"en":"The subtitles were quite hard to see because the screen was too far away.","zh":"因為螢幕太遠，字幕相當難看清。"},{"en":"If an important scene is hard to see, the audience may miss key details.","zh":"如果重要場景難以看清，觀眾可能錯過關鍵細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺上的困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dislike it","meaning":"不喜歡它","examples":[{"en":"Ed did not dislike the dim lighting.","zh":"Ed 並沒有不喜歡昏暗燈光。"},{"en":"To dislike something means to not like it.","zh":"不喜歡某物意思是對它沒有好感。"},{"en":"A viewer may dislike a costume choice if it does not fit the character.","zh":"如果服裝選擇不配合角色，觀眾可能不喜歡它。"},{"en":"Saying someone did not dislike something suggests they may accept it or see some value in it.","zh":"說某人並沒有不喜歡某物，暗示他可能接受它或看見其價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a negative opinion, or the absence of one.","zh":"這個短語描述負面意見，或沒有負面意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"change the mood of","meaning":"改變……的氣氛","examples":[{"en":"The lighting helped to change the mood of the quieter scenes.","zh":"燈光幫助改變較安靜場景的氣氛。"},{"en":"To change the mood of a scene means to alter its emotional atmosphere.","zh":"改變一個場景的氣氛意思是改變其情感氛圍。"},{"en":"Soft music can change the mood of a film scene from tense to peaceful.","zh":"柔和音樂可以把電影場景的氣氛由緊張改為平靜。"},{"en":"Lighting is often used to change mood without changing the dialogue.","zh":"燈光常用來在不改變對白的情況下改變氣氛。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in arts and performance analysis.","zh":"這個短語適合用於藝術和演出分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"quieter scenes","meaning":"較安靜的場景","examples":[{"en":"The lighting suited the quieter scenes.","zh":"燈光適合較安靜的場景。"},{"en":"Quieter scenes are calmer, less dramatic or less noisy parts of a performance.","zh":"較安靜的場景是演出中較平靜、較不戲劇化或較少聲音的部分。"},{"en":"A quiet scene between two characters may need softer lighting and slower pacing.","zh":"兩個角色之間的安靜場景可能需要較柔和燈光和較慢節奏。"},{"en":"Quieter scenes can reveal emotions that action scenes cannot show.","zh":"較安靜的場景可以揭示動作場面不能展示的情感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes scenes with a more restrained mood.","zh":"這個短語描述氣氛較克制的場景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"that’s a good point","meaning":"這是個好觀點","examples":[{"en":"Gemma says Ed’s comment about the lighting is a good point.","zh":"Gemma 說 Ed 關於燈光的評論是個好觀點。"},{"en":"That’s a good point means the speaker thinks the other person has made a useful or valid comment.","zh":"這是個好觀點意思是說話者認為對方提出了有用或合理的評論。"},{"en":"“That’s a good point,” the teacher said when a student noticed the contrast in the scene.","zh":"當學生注意到場景中的對比時，老師說：「這是個好觀點。」"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and helps continue discussion positively.","zh":"這個短語有禮貌，並有助正面延續討論。"},{"en":"It is common in conversations and group work.","zh":"它常見於對話和小組工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"costumes","meaning":"服裝","examples":[{"en":"Ed asks Gemma what she thought of the costumes.","zh":"Ed 問 Gemma 對服裝有甚麼看法。"},{"en":"Costumes are the clothes worn by actors in a play, film or performance.","zh":"服裝是演員在戲劇、電影或演出中穿着的衣服。"},{"en":"Costumes can show a character’s social class, personality or time period.","zh":"服裝可以顯示角色的社會階層、個性或時代背景。"},{"en":"Modern costumes can make an old story feel closer to today’s audience.","zh":"現代服裝可以令古老故事感覺更貼近今天的觀眾。"},{"en":"This word is important in theatre and film reviews.","zh":"這個詞在劇場和電影評論中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be surprised by","meaning":"對……感到驚訝","examples":[{"en":"Gemma was a bit surprised by the contemporary dress.","zh":"Gemma 對現代服裝有點感到驚訝。"},{"en":"To be surprised by something means to feel that it was unexpected.","zh":"對某事感到驚訝意思是覺得它出乎意料。"},{"en":"The audience was surprised by the modern music in a classical play.","zh":"觀眾對古典戲劇中的現代音樂感到驚訝。"},{"en":"Creative choices can surprise viewers when they challenge expectations.","zh":"當創作選擇挑戰期望時，可以令觀眾驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reaction to something unexpected.","zh":"這個短語描述對意外事情的反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"contemporary dress","meaning":"現代服裝","examples":[{"en":"The production used contemporary dress instead of traditional costumes.","zh":"這個製作版本使用現代服裝，而不是傳統服裝。"},{"en":"Contemporary dress means modern clothing from the present time.","zh":"現代服裝意思是現今時代的衣着。"},{"en":"A Shakespeare production in contemporary dress may use jeans, jackets and trainers.","zh":"使用現代服裝的莎士比亞製作版本可能用牛仔褲、外套和波鞋。"},{"en":"Contemporary dress can help audiences see old themes in a modern setting.","zh":"現代服裝可以幫助觀眾在現代背景中看見古老主題。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts modern clothing with historical costume.","zh":"這個短語把現代衣着與歷史服裝作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"I must say","meaning":"我得說","examples":[{"en":"Gemma says she was surprised by the contemporary dress, she must say.","zh":"Gemma 說，我得說，我對現代服裝感到驚訝。"},{"en":"I must say is used to emphasise an honest opinion or reaction.","zh":"我得說用來強調真誠的意見或反應。"},{"en":"I must say, the final scene was more powerful than I expected.","zh":"我得說，最後一幕比我預期更有感染力。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase when they want to sound sincere or reflective.","zh":"說話者想顯得真誠或帶有反思時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken English.","zh":"它常見於口語英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"work well","meaning":"效果不錯","examples":[{"en":"Ed thinks the contemporary dress worked well.","zh":"Ed 認為現代服裝效果不錯。"},{"en":"To work well means to be successful or effective in a situation.","zh":"效果不錯意思是在某情況中成功或有效。"},{"en":"The music worked well because it matched the tension of the scene.","zh":"音樂效果不錯，因為它配合了場景的緊張感。"},{"en":"A creative choice works well when it supports the meaning and mood of the production.","zh":"當創作選擇支持製作的意義和氣氛，它就是效果不錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語描述有效程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"assume it would be","meaning":"原本以為它會是……","examples":[{"en":"Ed had assumed the costumes would be more conventional.","zh":"Ed 原本以為服裝會更傳統。"},{"en":"To assume it would be something means to think it would be that way before checking or seeing it.","zh":"原本以為它會是某樣子，意思是在查證或看見前認為它會如此。"},{"en":"I assumed the play would be serious, but it had many funny moments.","zh":"我原本以為這齣戲會很嚴肅，但它有很多有趣時刻。"},{"en":"Assumptions can be wrong when a production makes unexpected choices.","zh":"當製作作出意外選擇，原本假設可能是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an expectation before experience.","zh":"這個短語描述經驗之前的期望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"conventional","meaning":"傳統的；常規的","examples":[{"en":"Ed expected the costumes to be more conventional.","zh":"Ed 預期服裝會更傳統。"},{"en":"Conventional means traditional, usual or following accepted ways.","zh":"傳統的或常規的意思是遵循一般、傳統或被接受的方式。"},{"en":"A conventional production of Romeo and Juliet might use historical costumes.","zh":"傳統的《羅密歐與茱麗葉》製作版本可能使用歷史服裝。"},{"en":"Conventional choices can feel safe, but they may also seem less original.","zh":"傳統選擇可以感覺穩妥，但也可能顯得較不原創。"},{"en":"This word contrasts with experimental or modern approaches.","zh":"這個詞與實驗性或現代方法形成對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at the beginning","meaning":"在開頭","examples":[{"en":"Gemma liked the music at the beginning of the production.","zh":"Gemma 喜歡製作版本開頭的音樂。"},{"en":"At the beginning means at the start of something.","zh":"在開頭意思是在某事開始的部分。"},{"en":"At the beginning of the play, the music created a sense of excitement.","zh":"在戲劇開頭，音樂營造出興奮感。"},{"en":"The beginning of a performance is important because it shapes first impressions.","zh":"演出的開頭很重要，因為它塑造第一印象。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the time or position of an event.","zh":"這個短語交代事件的時間或位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the musicians were brilliant","meaning":"樂手非常出色","examples":[{"en":"Gemma thought the musicians were brilliant.","zh":"Gemma 認為樂手非常出色。"},{"en":"The musicians were brilliant means the performers playing music were extremely good.","zh":"樂手非常出色意思是演奏音樂的人表現極好。"},{"en":"The musicians were brilliant because they created tension without overpowering the actors.","zh":"樂手非常出色，因為他們營造緊張感而沒有蓋過演員。"},{"en":"Strong musicians can make a production feel more alive and emotional.","zh":"出色樂手可以令製作更有生命力和情感。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a very positive judgement of musical performance.","zh":"這個短語對音樂演出作出非常正面的評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be wasted","meaning":"未被充分利用","examples":[{"en":"Gemma thought the musicians were wasted in the later acts.","zh":"Gemma 認為樂手在後面幾幕未被充分利用。"},{"en":"To be wasted means not to be used fully or effectively.","zh":"未被充分利用意思是沒有被完整或有效地使用。"},{"en":"A talented actor is wasted if given only a tiny role with no important lines.","zh":"如果有才華的演員只被安排一個沒有重要台詞的小角色，就是未被充分利用。"},{"en":"In a production, good music may be wasted if it disappears after the opening.","zh":"在製作中，如果好音樂在開場後消失，就可能是未被充分利用。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises underuse of talent or resources.","zh":"這個短語批評才華或資源使用不足。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have much impact","meaning":"有很大影響","examples":[{"en":"The music did not have much impact in Acts 2 and 3.","zh":"音樂在第二幕和第三幕沒有很大影響。"},{"en":"To have much impact means to have a strong effect on people or on the production.","zh":"有很大影響意思是對人們或製作造成強烈效果。"},{"en":"The lighting did not have much impact because it stayed the same throughout the play.","zh":"燈光沒有很大影響，因為整齣戲都保持不變。"},{"en":"Music has impact when it changes the mood or strengthens emotion.","zh":"當音樂改變氣氛或加強情感，它就有影響力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evaluating effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語適合用於評估有效程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Acts 2 and 3","meaning":"第二幕和第三幕","examples":[{"en":"The music had less impact in Acts 2 and 3.","zh":"音樂在第二幕和第三幕影響較小。"},{"en":"Acts 2 and 3 mean the second and third major sections of a play.","zh":"第二幕和第三幕意思是戲劇的第二和第三個主要部分。"},{"en":"In Acts 2 and 3, the conflict between characters often becomes more serious.","zh":"在第二幕和第三幕中，角色之間的衝突通常變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"Referring to acts helps reviewers locate moments in the structure of the play.","zh":"提及幕數有助評論者指出戲劇結構中的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in theatre analysis.","zh":"這個短語用於戲劇分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"that was a shame","meaning":"那很可惜","examples":[{"en":"Ed says it was a shame that the music had little impact later.","zh":"Ed 說音樂後來影響不大，那很可惜。"},{"en":"That was a shame means that was disappointing or unfortunate.","zh":"那很可惜意思是那令人失望或遺憾。"},{"en":"The set was beautiful, but it was a shame that the actors were hard to hear.","zh":"布景很美，但演員很難聽清，那很可惜。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses mild regret about a missed opportunity.","zh":"這個短語表達對錯失機會的輕微遺憾。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken English.","zh":"它常見於口語英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"one problem with","meaning":"……的一個問題","examples":[{"en":"One problem with the production was the delivery of the lines.","zh":"這個製作版本的一個問題是台詞表達。"},{"en":"One problem with something means one weakness or difficulty connected with it.","zh":"某事的一個問題意思是與它相關的一個弱點或困難。"},{"en":"One problem with the performance was that the ending felt rushed.","zh":"這場演出的一個問題是結尾感覺太倉促。"},{"en":"Identifying one problem clearly helps a review become specific.","zh":"清楚指出一個問題有助評論變得具體。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces criticism.","zh":"這個短語引入批評。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"deliver the lines","meaning":"念台詞；表達台詞","examples":[{"en":"The actors did not deliver the lines that well.","zh":"演員台詞表達得不太好。"},{"en":"To deliver the lines means to speak the words of a script in performance.","zh":"念台詞或表達台詞意思是在演出中說出劇本中的文字。"},{"en":"Actors must deliver the lines clearly so the audience understands the story.","zh":"演員必須清楚念台詞，讓觀眾理解故事。"},{"en":"Good line delivery depends on pace, volume, emotion and clarity.","zh":"良好的台詞表達取決於速度、音量、情感和清晰度。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to acting and theatre reviews.","zh":"這個短語是演技和劇評中的核心用語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"speak too fast","meaning":"說得太快","examples":[{"en":"Gemma thought the actors were speaking too fast.","zh":"Gemma 認為演員說得太快。"},{"en":"To speak too fast means to talk at a speed that makes it hard to follow.","zh":"說得太快意思是說話速度快得令人難以跟上。"},{"en":"A presenter who speaks too fast may lose the audience.","zh":"說得太快的匯報者可能令聽眾跟不上。"},{"en":"In Shakespeare, speaking too fast can make complex language harder to understand.","zh":"在莎士比亞劇作中，說得太快會令複雜語言更難理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a problem with pace.","zh":"這個短語描述速度上的問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"I agree","meaning":"我同意","examples":[{"en":"Ed agrees that the line delivery was a problem.","zh":"Ed 同意台詞表達是一個問題。"},{"en":"I agree means I have the same opinion.","zh":"我同意意思是我有相同意見。"},{"en":"I agree that the lighting was beautiful, but it was sometimes too dark.","zh":"我同意燈光很美，但有時太暗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in discussion because it shows shared understanding.","zh":"這個短語在討論中很有用，因為它顯示共同理解。"},{"en":"It can be followed by a reason or extra point.","zh":"它後面可以接理由或補充重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"speak loudly enough","meaning":"說得夠大聲","examples":[{"en":"Ed thought the actors were not speaking loudly enough.","zh":"Ed 認為演員說得不夠大聲。"},{"en":"To speak loudly enough means to use enough volume for listeners to hear clearly.","zh":"說得夠大聲意思是使用足夠音量讓聽眾清楚聽到。"},{"en":"In a large theatre, actors must speak loudly enough to reach the back row.","zh":"在大型劇院中，演員必須說得夠大聲，讓後排也聽到。"},{"en":"If actors are not loud enough, important lines may be missed.","zh":"如果演員不夠大聲，重要台詞可能會被錯過。"},{"en":"This phrase describes voice volume in communication.","zh":"這個短語描述溝通中的聲量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"especially at","meaning":"尤其在……","examples":[{"en":"The actors were not loud enough, especially at key points in the play.","zh":"演員聲量不夠，尤其在劇中的關鍵時刻。"},{"en":"Especially at means particularly during a certain time, moment or place.","zh":"尤其在某處或某時意思是特別在某個時間、時刻或地方。"},{"en":"Students need to listen carefully, especially at the beginning of the instructions.","zh":"學生需要仔細聆聽，尤其在指示開頭。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a moment where the problem is more serious.","zh":"這個短語突顯問題在某一刻更嚴重。"},{"en":"It is useful when one part deserves special attention.","zh":"當某部分值得特別注意時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"key points","meaning":"關鍵時刻","examples":[{"en":"The actors were too quiet at key points in the play.","zh":"演員在劇中的關鍵時刻太細聲。"},{"en":"Key points are the most important moments, ideas or stages.","zh":"關鍵時刻或重點是最重要的時刻、想法或階段。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to underline the key points in an article.","zh":"老師可能要求學生在文章中劃下重點。"},{"en":"In a play, key points often change the direction of the story.","zh":"在戲劇中，關鍵時刻通常會改變故事方向。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights importance.","zh":"這個短語突顯重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have a problem with","meaning":"對……有問題","examples":[{"en":"Gemma did not have a problem with the actors’ volume.","zh":"Gemma 對演員的音量沒有問題。"},{"en":"To have a problem with something means to find it difficult, unacceptable or unsatisfactory.","zh":"對某事有問題意思是覺得它困難、不可接受或不令人滿意。"},{"en":"Some viewers had a problem with the fast pace of the dialogue.","zh":"有些觀眾對對白節奏太快有問題。"},{"en":"Saying you do not have a problem with something means you accept it or are not bothered by it.","zh":"說你對某事沒有問題，意思是你接受它或不受它困擾。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving opinions.","zh":"這個短語適合用於表達意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an interesting experience","meaning":"一次有趣的經驗","examples":[{"en":"Watching different versions of the play was an interesting experience.","zh":"觀看這齣戲的不同版本是一次有趣的經驗。"},{"en":"An interesting experience is an event or activity that makes someone think, learn or feel curious.","zh":"有趣的經驗是令人思考、學習或感到好奇的事件或活動。"},{"en":"Watching a rehearsal can be an interesting experience for drama students.","zh":"對戲劇學生來說，觀看排練可以是一次有趣的經驗。"},{"en":"Interesting experiences often help students understand a subject more deeply.","zh":"有趣經驗常幫助學生更深入理解一個主題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something worthwhile and thought-provoking.","zh":"這個短語描述值得經歷並引人思考的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"different versions of","meaning":"……的不同版本","examples":[{"en":"The students watched different versions of Romeo and Juliet.","zh":"學生觀看了《羅密歐與茱麗葉》的不同版本。"},{"en":"Different versions of something are different forms, adaptations or interpretations of the same work.","zh":"某事的不同版本是同一作品的不同形式、改編或詮釋。"},{"en":"A class may compare different versions of a fairy tale from different cultures.","zh":"班級可能比較來自不同文化的同一童話不同版本。"},{"en":"Different versions can show how one story changes with time, place and director choices.","zh":"不同版本可以顯示一個故事如何隨時間、地點和導演選擇而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for comparison and adaptation.","zh":"這個短語適合用於比較和改編。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make someone realise","meaning":"令某人意識到","examples":[{"en":"Watching the play made Gemma realise how relevant it still is.","zh":"觀看這齣戲令 Gemma 意識到它仍然多麼貼近現實。"},{"en":"To make someone realise something means to cause them to understand or notice it clearly.","zh":"令某人意識到某事意思是使他們清楚明白或注意到它。"},{"en":"Watching the documentary made students realise how serious food waste is.","zh":"觀看紀錄片令學生意識到食物浪費有多嚴重。"},{"en":"A powerful performance can make viewers realise something they had not thought about before.","zh":"有感染力的演出可以令觀眾意識到之前沒有思考過的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change in awareness.","zh":"這個短語描述意識上的改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"how relevant","meaning":"有多貼近現實；有多相關","examples":[{"en":"Gemma realised how relevant Romeo and Juliet still is.","zh":"Gemma 意識到《羅密歐與茱麗葉》仍然有多貼近現實。"},{"en":"How relevant means the degree to which something is connected to present life or the topic being discussed.","zh":"有多相關意思是某事與當前生活或正在討論的主題有多大聯繫。"},{"en":"Students may realise how relevant old poems are when they discuss love, conflict and ambition.","zh":"當學生討論愛、衝突和野心時，可能會意識到古詩有多貼近現實。"},{"en":"A classic work remains relevant if modern audiences can still connect with its ideas.","zh":"如果現代觀眾仍能與其思想產生連繫，經典作品就仍然相關。"},{"en":"This phrase evaluates connection and importance.","zh":"這個短語評估聯繫和重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"since Shakespeare’s time","meaning":"自莎士比亞時代以來","examples":[{"en":"A lot has changed since Shakespeare’s time.","zh":"自莎士比亞時代以來，很多事情已經改變。"},{"en":"Since Shakespeare’s time means from the period when Shakespeare lived until now.","zh":"自莎士比亞時代以來意思是從莎士比亞生活的時期直到現在。"},{"en":"Theatre technology has changed greatly since Shakespeare’s time.","zh":"自莎士比亞時代以來，劇場科技已大大改變。"},{"en":"Even though society has changed, some human emotions remain familiar.","zh":"即使社會已改變，有些人類情感仍然熟悉。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the modern world with Shakespeare’s era.","zh":"這個短語把現代世界與莎士比亞時代作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in many ways","meaning":"在許多方面","examples":[{"en":"In many ways, the themes of the play have not changed.","zh":"在許多方面，這齣戲的主題並沒有改變。"},{"en":"In many ways means in several different respects or aspects.","zh":"在許多方面意思是在幾個不同層面或方面。"},{"en":"In many ways, school life today is different from school life fifty years ago.","zh":"在許多方面，今天的校園生活與五十年前不同。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a broad comparison without claiming everything is the same.","zh":"這個短語容許廣泛比較，而不是聲稱所有事情都一樣。"},{"en":"It is useful for balanced discussion.","zh":"它適合用於平衡討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"disagreements and tension","meaning":"分歧和緊張關係","examples":[{"en":"There are always disagreements and tension between teenagers and their parents.","zh":"青少年和父母之間總會有分歧和緊張關係。"},{"en":"Disagreements and tension mean arguments, conflict or uncomfortable feelings between people.","zh":"分歧和緊張關係意思是人與人之間的爭論、衝突或不舒服感。"},{"en":"Disagreements and tension may arise when parents and teenagers have different expectations.","zh":"當父母和青少年有不同期望時，可能出現分歧和緊張關係。"},{"en":"Family tension is a theme many young audiences can understand.","zh":"家庭緊張關係是許多年輕觀眾能理解的主題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relationship conflict.","zh":"這個短語描述關係衝突。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"between teenagers and their parents","meaning":"在青少年和父母之間","examples":[{"en":"The play explores tension between teenagers and their parents.","zh":"這齣戲探討青少年和父母之間的緊張關係。"},{"en":"Between teenagers and their parents means involving young people and their mother or father figures.","zh":"在青少年和父母之間意思是涉及年輕人和其母親或父親角色。"},{"en":"Arguments between teenagers and their parents often involve independence and rules.","zh":"青少年和父母之間的爭論常涉及獨立和規則。"},{"en":"This relationship is important in Romeo and Juliet because family pressure shapes the story.","zh":"這種關係在《羅密歐與茱麗葉》中很重要，因為家庭壓力塑造故事。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the two sides of a relationship or conflict.","zh":"這個短語指出關係或衝突的兩方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"relate to","meaning":"對……有共鳴","examples":[{"en":"Young people can relate to the conflict between teenagers and parents.","zh":"年輕人可以對青少年和父母之間的衝突有共鳴。"},{"en":"To relate to something means to understand it because it connects with your own experience.","zh":"對某事有共鳴意思是因為它與自己的經驗有連繫而理解它。"},{"en":"Students may relate to a character who feels pressure from family expectations.","zh":"學生可能對感到家庭期望壓力的角色有共鳴。"},{"en":"When audiences relate to a theme, the story feels more powerful and personal.","zh":"當觀眾對主題有共鳴，故事會感覺更有力量和更個人化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional or personal connection.","zh":"這個短語描述情感或個人連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"more than","meaning":"比……更","examples":[{"en":"The parent-child tension is more relatable than the violence in the play.","zh":"親子緊張關係比劇中的暴力更容易令人有共鳴。"},{"en":"More than is used to compare one thing as greater in degree than another.","zh":"比……更用來比較某事在程度上高於另一事。"},{"en":"The acting affected me more than the set design.","zh":"演技比布景設計更打動我。"},{"en":"Comparisons help reviewers explain which parts mattered most to them.","zh":"比較有助評論者解釋哪些部分對他們最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when ranking or comparing ideas.","zh":"這個短語適合用於排序或比較想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"violence","meaning":"暴力","examples":[{"en":"The play contains violence and extreme emotions.","zh":"這齣戲包含暴力和極端情緒。"},{"en":"Violence means physical force intended to hurt or damage someone or something.","zh":"暴力意思是意圖傷害或破壞人或事物的身體力量。"},{"en":"The fight scenes in Romeo and Juliet show how family conflict can become violence.","zh":"《羅密歐與茱麗葉》中的打鬥場面顯示家族衝突如何變成暴力。"},{"en":"Violence on stage can be powerful, but it must be handled carefully.","zh":"舞台上的暴力可以很有力量，但必須小心處理。"},{"en":"This word is common when discussing conflict and tragedy.","zh":"這個詞常用於討論衝突和悲劇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"extreme emotions","meaning":"極端情緒","examples":[{"en":"Romeo and Juliet contains violence and extreme emotions.","zh":"《羅密歐與茱麗葉》包含暴力和極端情緒。"},{"en":"Extreme emotions are very strong feelings such as intense love, anger, grief or fear.","zh":"極端情緒是非常強烈的感受，例如強烈愛意、憤怒、悲傷或恐懼。"},{"en":"Tragedies often show extreme emotions because characters face serious choices.","zh":"悲劇常展示極端情緒，因為角色面對嚴重選擇。"},{"en":"Extreme emotions can make a performance powerful but also overwhelming.","zh":"極端情緒可以令演出有力量，但也可能令人難以承受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional intensity.","zh":"這個短語描述情感強度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"watch something in translation","meaning":"觀看翻譯版本","examples":[{"en":"The students watched Romeo and Juliet in translation.","zh":"學生觀看了《羅密歐與茱麗葉》的翻譯版本。"},{"en":"To watch something in translation means to watch a version performed or written in another language.","zh":"觀看翻譯版本意思是觀看以另一種語言演出或寫成的版本。"},{"en":"Students may watch a French play in translation if they do not understand French.","zh":"如果學生不懂法文，可能會觀看一齣法國戲劇的翻譯版本。"},{"en":"Watching a play in translation can make the story easier to follow for some audiences.","zh":"對一些觀眾來說，觀看翻譯版本可以令故事更容易跟上。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing language versions of a work.","zh":"當討論作品的語言版本時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"expect to find it more challenging","meaning":"預期它會更具挑戰性","examples":[{"en":"Gemma expected to find the translated version more challenging.","zh":"Gemma 預期翻譯版本會更具挑戰性。"},{"en":"To expect to find something more challenging means to think it will be more difficult before experiencing it.","zh":"預期某事會更具挑戰性意思是在經歷前認為它會更困難。"},{"en":"A student may expect to find Shakespeare difficult before seeing a clear performance.","zh":"學生可能在觀看清楚演出前，預期莎士比亞會很難。"},{"en":"Expectations can change once people actually experience the work.","zh":"一旦人們真正經歷作品，期望可能會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a predicted difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述預想中的困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"follow the story","meaning":"跟得上故事","examples":[{"en":"Gemma could follow the story pretty well.","zh":"Gemma 相當能跟得上故事。"},{"en":"To follow the story means to understand the sequence of events and what is happening.","zh":"跟得上故事意思是理解事件次序和正在發生的事。"},{"en":"Clear acting helped the audience follow the story even without understanding every word.","zh":"清楚演技幫助觀眾即使不明白每個字，也能跟得上故事。"},{"en":"If the plot moves too quickly, viewers may struggle to follow the story.","zh":"如果情節推進太快，觀眾可能難以跟得上故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes understanding a narrative.","zh":"這個短語描述對敘事的理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stop worrying about","meaning":"不再擔心……","examples":[{"en":"Ed stopped worrying about not understanding every word.","zh":"Ed 不再擔心自己不明白每個字。"},{"en":"To stop worrying about something means to no longer feel anxious about it.","zh":"不再擔心某事意思是不再對它感到焦慮。"},{"en":"A student may stop worrying about mistakes after realising communication is more important.","zh":"學生意識到溝通更重要後，可能不再擔心錯誤。"},{"en":"When viewers focus on the overall story, they may stop worrying about individual words.","zh":"當觀眾專注於整體故事，可能不再擔心個別字詞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reduction in anxiety.","zh":"這個短語描述焦慮減少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not being able to","meaning":"無法……","examples":[{"en":"Ed stopped worrying about not being able to understand all the words.","zh":"Ed 不再擔心自己無法理解所有字詞。"},{"en":"Not being able to do something means lacking the ability or opportunity to do it.","zh":"無法做某事意思是缺乏做該事的能力或機會。"},{"en":"A student may worry about not being able to answer questions in a speaking exam.","zh":"學生可能擔心自己無法在口試中回答問題。"},{"en":"Not being able to understand every word does not always prevent understanding the story.","zh":"無法理解每個字詞不一定阻止人理解故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inability or limitation.","zh":"這個短語描述能力不足或限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"focus on the actors’ expressions","meaning":"專注於演員的表情","examples":[{"en":"Ed focused on the actors’ expressions instead.","zh":"Ed 反而專注於演員的表情。"},{"en":"To focus on the actors’ expressions means to pay attention to the emotions shown on their faces.","zh":"專注於演員的表情意思是留意他們臉上顯示的情緒。"},{"en":"When the language is difficult, viewers can focus on the actors’ expressions to understand feeling.","zh":"當語言很難時，觀眾可以專注於演員的表情來理解感受。"},{"en":"Facial expressions can reveal fear, love, anger and grief without words.","zh":"面部表情可以不用文字也顯示恐懼、愛、憤怒和悲傷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes watching non-verbal performance carefully.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細觀看非語言演出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the ending","meaning":"結尾","examples":[{"en":"The ending of the translated version was powerful.","zh":"翻譯版本的結尾很有力量。"},{"en":"The ending is the final part of a story, play or performance.","zh":"結尾是故事、戲劇或演出的最後部分。"},{"en":"A strong ending can change how the audience remembers the whole play.","zh":"強而有力的結尾可以改變觀眾如何記住整齣戲。"},{"en":"Endings are important because they leave the final emotional impression.","zh":"結尾很重要，因為它留下最後的情感印象。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the conclusion of a work.","zh":"這個短語指作品的結論部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pretty powerful","meaning":"相當有感染力","examples":[{"en":"The ending was pretty powerful.","zh":"結尾相當有感染力。"},{"en":"Pretty powerful means quite strong in emotional or dramatic effect.","zh":"相當有感染力意思是在情感或戲劇效果上頗強。"},{"en":"The final speech was pretty powerful because the actor spoke with quiet sadness.","zh":"最後一段獨白相當有感染力，因為演員以安靜的悲傷語氣說出。"},{"en":"A powerful moment can affect the audience even after the performance ends.","zh":"有感染力的時刻可以在演出結束後仍影響觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase is conversational and positive.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並帶正面意思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"intensify the emotion","meaning":"加強情感","examples":[{"en":"The translated performance intensified the emotion for Gemma.","zh":"翻譯演出為 Gemma 加強了情感。"},{"en":"To intensify the emotion means to make the feeling stronger.","zh":"加強情感意思是令感受更強烈。"},{"en":"Soft music can intensify the emotion of a sad scene.","zh":"柔和音樂可以加強悲傷場景的情感。"},{"en":"A director may slow down a scene to intensify the emotion.","zh":"導演可能放慢一幕的節奏來加強情感。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when analysing dramatic effect.","zh":"當分析戲劇效果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"somehow","meaning":"不知怎樣","examples":[{"en":"The ending somehow intensified the emotion for Gemma.","zh":"結尾不知怎樣為 Gemma 加強了情感。"},{"en":"Somehow means in a way that is not completely clear or easy to explain.","zh":"不知怎樣意思是以一種不完全清楚或難以解釋的方式。"},{"en":"Somehow, the simple lighting made the scene more moving.","zh":"不知怎樣，簡單燈光令那一幕更感人。"},{"en":"This word is useful when the speaker feels an effect but cannot fully explain the reason.","zh":"當說話者感受到效果但不能完全解釋原因時，這個詞很有用。"},{"en":"It often adds a reflective or slightly uncertain tone.","zh":"它常加入反思或略帶不確定的語氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be translated into","meaning":"被翻譯成……","examples":[{"en":"Shakespeare’s works have been translated into more languages than any other writer’s.","zh":"莎士比亞的作品被翻譯成比任何其他作家的作品更多的語言。"},{"en":"To be translated into a language means to be changed from one language into another.","zh":"被翻譯成某語言意思是由一種語言轉換成另一種語言。"},{"en":"A novel may be translated into many languages after becoming internationally popular.","zh":"小說在國際上受歡迎後，可能被翻譯成多種語言。"},{"en":"Translation allows audiences from different cultures to access the same work.","zh":"翻譯讓不同文化的觀眾能接觸同一作品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing language versions.","zh":"當討論語言版本時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"international appeal","meaning":"國際吸引力","examples":[{"en":"Gemma asks about the reason for Shakespeare’s international appeal.","zh":"Gemma 問莎士比亞國際吸引力的原因。"},{"en":"International appeal means the ability to attract interest from people in many countries.","zh":"國際吸引力意思是能吸引許多國家的人感興趣的能力。"},{"en":"A film with universal themes may have strong international appeal.","zh":"具有普世主題的電影可能有強大的國際吸引力。"},{"en":"Shakespeare’s international appeal may come from themes that many cultures understand.","zh":"莎士比亞的國際吸引力可能來自許多文化都能理解的主題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes popularity beyond one country.","zh":"這個短語描述超越單一國家的受歡迎程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the reason for","meaning":"……的原因","examples":[{"en":"Gemma asks what the reason for Shakespeare’s international appeal is.","zh":"Gemma 問莎士比亞國際吸引力的原因是甚麼。"},{"en":"The reason for something is the cause or explanation behind it.","zh":"某事的原因是其背後的成因或解釋。"},{"en":"Students may discuss the reason for a character’s tragic decision.","zh":"學生可能討論角色作出悲劇性決定的原因。"},{"en":"Identifying reasons helps analysis move beyond simple opinion.","zh":"找出原因有助分析超越簡單意見。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces cause or explanation.","zh":"這個短語引入成因或解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"I was reading that","meaning":"我讀到過","examples":[{"en":"Ed says he was reading that Shakespeare’s plays deal with basic themes.","zh":"Ed 說他讀到過莎士比亞劇作處理基本主題。"},{"en":"I was reading that means I recently read or came across this information.","zh":"我讀到過意思是我最近讀到或看到這項資料。"},{"en":"I was reading that many theatres use modern settings for classic plays.","zh":"我讀到過許多劇院會為經典劇作使用現代背景。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces information from something the speaker has read.","zh":"這個短語引入說話者讀過的資料。"},{"en":"It sounds conversational and informal.","zh":"它聽起來口語而非正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"basic themes","meaning":"基本主題","examples":[{"en":"Shakespeare’s plays are about basic themes that people everywhere understand.","zh":"莎士比亞劇作關於各地人都明白的基本主題。"},{"en":"Basic themes are simple but important ideas, such as love, jealousy, conflict and ambition.","zh":"基本主題是簡單但重要的想法，例如愛、嫉妒、衝突和野心。"},{"en":"Basic themes can be understood by audiences from different cultures.","zh":"基本主題可以被不同文化的觀眾理解。"},{"en":"A story with basic human themes often remains relevant for a long time.","zh":"具有基本人類主題的故事通常能長期保持相關。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fundamental ideas in literature.","zh":"這個短語描述文學中的根本思想。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be familiar with","meaning":"熟悉……","examples":[{"en":"People everywhere are familiar with the themes in Shakespeare’s plays.","zh":"各地人都熟悉莎士比亞劇作中的主題。"},{"en":"To be familiar with something means to know it or recognise it because of experience.","zh":"熟悉某事意思是因經驗而知道或認出它。"},{"en":"Students are familiar with stories about love and family conflict.","zh":"學生熟悉關於愛和家庭衝突的故事。"},{"en":"Familiar themes make difficult language easier to approach.","zh":"熟悉的主題令困難語言較容易接近。"},{"en":"This phrase describes knowledge or recognition.","zh":"這個短語描述知識或辨認能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be understood on different levels","meaning":"可在不同層次上被理解","examples":[{"en":"Shakespeare’s plays can be understood on different levels.","zh":"莎士比亞劇作可在不同層次上被理解。"},{"en":"To be understood on different levels means to have simple meanings as well as deeper meanings.","zh":"可在不同層次上被理解意思是同時有簡單意思和更深層意思。"},{"en":"Children may understand the story, while older students understand the politics and imagery on different levels.","zh":"孩子可能理解故事，而年長學生則在不同層次上理解政治和意象。"},{"en":"Works with several levels can appeal to both beginners and experts.","zh":"有多重層次的作品可以吸引初學者和專家。"},{"en":"This phrase describes depth and layered meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述深度和層層意義。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have such depth","meaning":"非常有深度","examples":[{"en":"The characters in Shakespeare’s plays have such depth.","zh":"莎士比亞劇作中的角色非常有深度。"},{"en":"To have such depth means to be complex, rich and not simple or flat.","zh":"非常有深度意思是複雜、豐富，而不是簡單或平面。"},{"en":"A character has depth when they show mixed feelings and difficult choices.","zh":"當角色展現複雜感受和困難選擇，他就是有深度。"},{"en":"Deep characters allow audiences to interpret them in many ways.","zh":"有深度的角色讓觀眾能以多種方式詮釋。"},{"en":"This phrase praises complexity and richness.","zh":"這個短語讚賞複雜性和豐富性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"allow someone to","meaning":"讓某人能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The depth of the characters allows directors to experiment.","zh":"角色的深度讓導演能夠嘗試不同做法。"},{"en":"To allow someone to do something means to make it possible for them to do it.","zh":"讓某人能夠做某事意思是令他們可以做該事。"},{"en":"Flexible staging allows directors to create modern interpretations.","zh":"彈性舞台安排讓導演能夠創造現代詮釋。"},{"en":"Rich characters allow actors to show different sides of emotion.","zh":"豐富角色讓演員能夠展示不同情感面向。"},{"en":"This phrase links a quality with the possibility it creates.","zh":"這個短語把某種特質與其創造的可能性連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"experiment","meaning":"嘗試不同做法","examples":[{"en":"Directors can experiment with Shakespeare’s plays.","zh":"導演可以在莎士比亞劇作中嘗試不同做法。"},{"en":"To experiment means to try new methods, styles or ideas to see how they work.","zh":"嘗試不同做法意思是試用新方法、風格或想法，看看效果如何。"},{"en":"A director may experiment with music, costumes or stage space.","zh":"導演可能嘗試不同音樂、服裝或舞台空間運用。"},{"en":"Experimenting can keep classic works fresh for modern audiences.","zh":"嘗試新做法可以令經典作品對現代觀眾保持新鮮感。"},{"en":"This verb suggests creative trial and exploration.","zh":"這個動詞暗示創意試驗和探索。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"find new angles","meaning":"找到新的角度","examples":[{"en":"Directors can find new angles in Shakespeare’s plays.","zh":"導演可以在莎士比亞劇作中找到新的角度。"},{"en":"To find new angles means to discover fresh ways of interpreting or presenting something.","zh":"找到新的角度意思是發現詮釋或呈現某事的新方式。"},{"en":"A director may find a new angle by setting Romeo and Juliet in a modern city.","zh":"導演可以把《羅密歐與茱麗葉》設定在現代城市，找到新的角度。"},{"en":"New angles can help audiences notice ideas they had not seen before.","zh":"新角度可以幫助觀眾注意到以前沒有看見的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing creativity and interpretation.","zh":"當討論創意和詮釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"that’s really important","meaning":"那真的很重要","examples":[{"en":"Gemma says finding new angles is really important.","zh":"Gemma 說找到新的角度真的很重要。"},{"en":"That’s really important means the speaker thinks the point matters a great deal.","zh":"那真的很重要意思是說話者認為該重點非常重要。"},{"en":"Keeping classic plays fresh is really important if young audiences are to connect with them.","zh":"如果要讓年輕觀眾與經典劇作產生連繫，保持作品新鮮感真的很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong agreement or emphasis.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈同意或強調。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken discussion.","zh":"它常見於口語討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 13/task-4":[{"front":"make a start","meaning":"開始","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer says, “Right, everyone, let’s make a start.”","zh":"講師說：「好了，各位，我們開始吧。」"},{"en":"To make a start means to begin doing something.","zh":"make a start 指開始做某事。"},{"en":"The teacher waited for everyone to sit down before making a start.","zh":"老師等所有人坐下後才開始。"},{"en":"In a lesson or meeting, this phrase helps move people from preparation to action.","zh":"在課堂或會議中，這個片語幫助人們從準備轉入正式行動。"},{"en":"It sounds natural and conversational, especially when beginning a group activity.","zh":"它聽起來自然口語，尤其適合開始小組活動時使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over the past few sessions","meaning":"過去幾節課","examples":[{"en":"Over the past few sessions, the class has considered why some languages are in decline.","zh":"過去幾節課，班上探討了為甚麼某些語言正在衰退。"},{"en":"Over the past few sessions means during the last several lessons or meetings.","zh":"over the past few sessions 指在最近幾節課或幾次會議期間。"},{"en":"Over the past few sessions, we have studied how technology changes communication.","zh":"過去幾節課，我們研究了科技如何改變溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect today’s lesson with earlier lessons.","zh":"這個片語有助把今天的課與之前的課連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when a teacher reviews previous work before introducing a new topic.","zh":"當老師在引入新主題前回顧之前內容時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"consider the reasons why","meaning":"探討……的原因","examples":[{"en":"The class has been considering the reasons why some world languages are in decline.","zh":"班上一直在探討為甚麼某些世界語言正在衰退。"},{"en":"To consider the reasons why means to think carefully about the causes of something.","zh":"consider the reasons why 指仔細思考某事發生的原因。"},{"en":"Students considered the reasons why young people spend less time reading.","zh":"學生探討了年輕人為何較少閱讀的原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in academic discussion because it focuses on explanation, not just description.","zh":"這個片語適合學術討論，因為它着重解釋，而不只是描述。"},{"en":"It often leads to analysis of social, historical, or technological factors.","zh":"它常引出對社會、歷史或科技因素的分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"world languages","meaning":"世界語言","examples":[{"en":"The lecture discusses why some world languages are in decline.","zh":"講座討論為甚麼某些世界語言正在衰退。"},{"en":"World languages are languages used by people in different parts of the world.","zh":"world languages 指世界不同地區的人所使用的語言。"},{"en":"English, Spanish, Arabic, and Chinese are often discussed as major world languages.","zh":"英語、西班牙語、阿拉伯語和中文常被視為主要世界語言。"},{"en":"Some world languages are widely used, while others have relatively small speaker communities.","zh":"有些世界語言被廣泛使用，而另一些使用者社群相對較小。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing language use on a global scale.","zh":"這個片語適合討論全球層面的語言使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be in decline","meaning":"正在衰退","examples":[{"en":"Some world languages are in decline.","zh":"某些世界語言正在衰退。"},{"en":"To be in decline means to be becoming weaker, less common, or less widely used.","zh":"be in decline 指變得較弱、較少見或較少被使用。"},{"en":"A traditional craft may be in decline if fewer young people learn it.","zh":"如果較少年輕人學習一種傳統工藝，它可能正在衰退。"},{"en":"A language in decline may lose speakers, social status, or everyday usefulness.","zh":"正在衰退的語言可能失去使用者、社會地位或日常實用性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a downward trend rather than a sudden disappearance.","zh":"這個片語描述下降趨勢，而不是突然消失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"introduce another factor","meaning":"介紹另一個因素","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer introduces another factor that affects languages.","zh":"講師介紹另一個影響語言的因素。"},{"en":"To introduce another factor means to bring in one more cause or influence for discussion.","zh":"introduce another factor 指引入另一個原因或影響因素作討論。"},{"en":"After discussing migration, the teacher introduced another factor: education policy.","zh":"討論移民後，老師介紹另一個因素：教育政策。"},{"en":"This phrase helps structure an explanation with several causes.","zh":"這個片語有助組織包含多個原因的解釋。"},{"en":"It signals that the discussion is moving to a new but related point.","zh":"它表示討論正轉到一個新的相關重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"affect languages","meaning":"影響語言","examples":[{"en":"Digital technology affects languages and their speakers.","zh":"數碼科技影響語言及其使用者。"},{"en":"To affect languages means to influence how languages are used, learned, changed, or preserved.","zh":"affect languages 指影響語言如何被使用、學習、改變或保存。"},{"en":"Social media can affect languages by spreading slang very quickly.","zh":"社交媒體可以透過快速傳播潮語來影響語言。"},{"en":"Technology may support a language, but it can also push speakers towards a more dominant language.","zh":"科技可以支援一種語言，但也可能把使用者推向更強勢的語言。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing language change.","zh":"這個片語適合討論語言變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"speakers of those languages","meaning":"那些語言的使用者","examples":[{"en":"Technology affects languages and the speakers of those languages.","zh":"科技影響語言以及那些語言的使用者。"},{"en":"Speakers of those languages are the people who use those particular languages.","zh":"speakers of those languages 指使用那些特定語言的人。"},{"en":"Speakers of minority languages may need digital tools in their own language.","zh":"少數族群語言的使用者可能需要以自己語言運作的數碼工具。"},{"en":"If technology does not support a language, speakers of that language may switch to another one online.","zh":"如果科技不支援某語言，該語言的使用者可能在線上轉用另一種語言。"},{"en":"This phrase links a language with the people who actually use it.","zh":"這個片語把語言與實際使用它的人連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in particular","meaning":"尤其是","examples":[{"en":"The lecture focuses on technology and, in particular, digital technology.","zh":"講座聚焦於科技，尤其是數碼科技。"},{"en":"In particular means especially or specifically.","zh":"in particular 指尤其是或特別是。"},{"en":"The report discusses transport problems and, in particular, the lack of buses.","zh":"報告討論交通問題，尤其是巴士不足。"},{"en":"This phrase helps narrow a broad topic to one important part.","zh":"這個片語有助把廣泛主題收窄到其中一個重要部分。"},{"en":"It is common in academic and formal speech.","zh":"它常見於學術和正式說話中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"digital technology","meaning":"數碼科技","examples":[{"en":"Digital technology can affect the survival of a language.","zh":"數碼科技可以影響一種語言的存續。"},{"en":"Digital technology includes computers, smartphones, apps, websites, and online systems.","zh":"digital technology 包括電腦、智能電話、應用程式、網站和網上系統。"},{"en":"Digital technology has changed how students read, write, translate, and communicate.","zh":"數碼科技改變了學生閱讀、寫作、翻譯和溝通的方式。"},{"en":"If a language is absent from digital technology, young speakers may use another language online.","zh":"如果某語言缺席於數碼科技，年輕使用者可能在線上使用另一種語言。"},{"en":"This phrase is central when discussing modern communication and language survival.","zh":"討論現代溝通和語言存續時，這個片語很核心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in order to illustrate","meaning":"為了說明……","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer uses Icelandic in order to illustrate the effect of technology.","zh":"講師使用冰島語作例子，為了說明科技的影響。"},{"en":"In order to illustrate means for the purpose of explaining something clearly with an example.","zh":"in order to illustrate 指為了用例子清楚解釋某事。"},{"en":"The teacher used a chart in order to illustrate the rise in internet use.","zh":"老師使用圖表，為了說明互聯網使用量上升。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than simply saying “to show”.","zh":"這個片語比單純說 “to show” 更正式。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving an example that supports a larger argument.","zh":"當例子用來支持較大論點時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"illustrate its effect","meaning":"說明其影響","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic is used to illustrate the effect of digital technology.","zh":"冰島語被用來說明數碼科技的影響。"},{"en":"To illustrate its effect means to show how something influences a situation by using an example.","zh":"illustrate its effect 指用例子顯示某事如何影響一個情況。"},{"en":"The teacher used one student’s timetable to illustrate the effect of too much homework.","zh":"老師用一名學生的時間表來說明過多功課的影響。"},{"en":"Examples can make abstract effects easier to understand.","zh":"例子可以令抽象影響更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in lectures, essays, and reports.","zh":"這個片語適合用於講座、文章和報告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"聚焦於……","examples":[{"en":"The lecture focuses on the Icelandic language.","zh":"講座聚焦於冰島語。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give special attention to it.","zh":"focus on something 指特別注意某事。"},{"en":"Today’s lesson will focus on pronunciation rather than grammar.","zh":"今天的課會聚焦於發音，而不是文法。"},{"en":"Focusing on one case can make a broad issue easier to analyse.","zh":"聚焦於一個案例，可以令廣泛議題更容易分析。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when introducing the main topic.","zh":"這個片語常用於引入主要主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Icelandic language","meaning":"冰島語","examples":[{"en":"The Icelandic language is spoken by around 321,000 people.","zh":"冰島語約有 321,000 人使用。"},{"en":"The Icelandic language is the language traditionally used in Iceland.","zh":"Icelandic language 指冰島傳統上使用的語言。"},{"en":"The Icelandic language has preserved many older features over a long period of time.","zh":"冰島語長時間保存了許多較古老的語言特徵。"},{"en":"Studying Icelandic helps show how small languages face pressure in a digital world.","zh":"研究冰島語有助顯示小語種如何在數碼世界面對壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific national language.","zh":"這個片語命名一種特定民族語言。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be spoken by","meaning":"被……使用","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic is spoken by around 321,000 people.","zh":"冰島語約被 321,000 人使用。"},{"en":"To be spoken by a group means that group uses the language.","zh":"be spoken by a group 指某群體使用該語言。"},{"en":"Cantonese is spoken by many people in Hong Kong.","zh":"粵語被香港許多人使用。"},{"en":"The number of people a language is spoken by can affect its resources and survival.","zh":"一種語言被多少人使用，會影響其資源和存續。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when describing language communities.","zh":"這個片語常用於描述語言社群。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"most of whom","meaning":"其中大部分人","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic is spoken by around 321,000 people, most of whom live in Iceland.","zh":"冰島語約有 321,000 人使用，其中大部分人住在冰島。"},{"en":"Most of whom means most of those people.","zh":"most of whom 指那些人當中的大多數。"},{"en":"The club has fifty members, most of whom are students.","zh":"該學會有五十名成員，其中大部分人是學生。"},{"en":"This phrase links extra information to a group of people already mentioned.","zh":"這個片語把額外資料連繫到前面提及的一群人。"},{"en":"It is formal and often appears in academic writing.","zh":"它較正式，常出現在學術寫作中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"North Atlantic Ocean","meaning":"北大西洋","examples":[{"en":"Iceland is an island in the North Atlantic Ocean.","zh":"冰島是北大西洋中的一個島嶼。"},{"en":"The North Atlantic Ocean is the northern part of the Atlantic Ocean between North America and Europe.","zh":"North Atlantic Ocean 指位於北美洲與歐洲之間的大西洋北部。"},{"en":"Iceland’s position in the North Atlantic Ocean has helped shape its history and culture.","zh":"冰島位於北大西洋的位置塑造了其歷史和文化。"},{"en":"Island communities can preserve languages differently from larger mainland countries.","zh":"島嶼社群保存語言的方式可能與較大的大陸國家不同。"},{"en":"This phrase names a geographical region.","zh":"這個片語命名一個地理區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the problem for this language","meaning":"這種語言面對的問題","examples":[{"en":"The problem for this language is not the number of speakers.","zh":"這種語言面對的問題不是使用者數目。"},{"en":"The problem for this language means the main difficulty or challenge facing that language.","zh":"the problem for this language 指該語言面對的主要困難或挑戰。"},{"en":"The problem for a small language may be lack of digital tools rather than lack of pride.","zh":"一種小語種面對的問題可能是缺乏數碼工具，而不是缺乏自豪感。"},{"en":"Identifying the real problem helps people choose better solutions.","zh":"找出真正問題有助人們選擇更好解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses discussion on the key threat.","zh":"這個片語把討論聚焦於主要威脅。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the number of speakers","meaning":"使用者數目","examples":[{"en":"The number of speakers of Icelandic is small.","zh":"冰島語的使用者數目很少。"},{"en":"The number of speakers means how many people use a language.","zh":"the number of speakers 指有多少人使用一種語言。"},{"en":"A language with a small number of speakers may need special support in schools and media.","zh":"使用者數目少的語言可能需要學校和媒體提供特別支援。"},{"en":"Numbers matter, but they are not the only factor in language survival.","zh":"數目很重要，但並不是語言存續的唯一因素。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in linguistics and language policy.","zh":"這個片語常見於語言學和語言政策。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"even though","meaning":"即使","examples":[{"en":"The problem is not the number of speakers, even though this number is small.","zh":"問題不是使用者數目，即使這個數目很少。"},{"en":"Even though means despite the fact that.","zh":"even though 指即使某事實成立。"},{"en":"The library is popular even though it is small.","zh":"即使圖書館很小，它仍然受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between two ideas.","zh":"這個片語引入兩個想法之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when one fact might seem to weaken the main point but does not.","zh":"當某個事實似乎會削弱主要觀點但其實不會時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"nor is it about","meaning":"也不是關於……","examples":[{"en":"Nor is it about losing words to other languages.","zh":"也不是關於詞彙被其他語言取代。"},{"en":"Nor is it about means and it is also not about.","zh":"nor is it about 指也不是關於某事。"},{"en":"The problem is not cost, nor is it about lack of interest.","zh":"問題不是成本，也不是缺乏興趣。"},{"en":"This structure is formal and helps rule out another possible explanation.","zh":"這個結構較正式，有助排除另一個可能解釋。"},{"en":"It often follows a negative statement.","zh":"它通常跟在否定陳述之後。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lose words to","meaning":"詞彙被……取代","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic is not mainly losing words to other languages.","zh":"冰島語主要並不是詞彙被其他語言取代。"},{"en":"To lose words to another language means to stop using native words because words from another language replace them.","zh":"lose words to another language 指本族語詞彙停止使用，因被另一語言的詞取代。"},{"en":"Some languages lose words to English in areas such as technology and business.","zh":"有些語言在科技和商業等領域中，詞彙被英語取代。"},{"en":"A language can borrow words without disappearing, but heavy replacement may worry speakers.","zh":"一種語言可以借詞而不消失，但大量替換可能令使用者擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes vocabulary pressure from another language.","zh":"這個片語描述來自另一種語言的詞彙壓力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"such as","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"The problem is not losing words to other languages, such as English.","zh":"問題不是詞彙被其他語言取代，例如英語。"},{"en":"Such as means for example.","zh":"such as 指例如。"},{"en":"Many students enjoy creative subjects, such as art, music, and drama.","zh":"許多學生喜歡創意科目，例如藝術、音樂和戲劇。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples from a wider group.","zh":"這個片語從較大類別中引入例子。"},{"en":"It is common in both academic and everyday English.","zh":"它常見於學術和日常英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, the vocabulary of Icelandic is continually increasing.","zh":"事實上，冰島語的詞彙正在持續增加。"},{"en":"In fact introduces information that is true and may correct or strengthen the previous point.","zh":"in fact 引入真實資訊，可能修正或加強前一點。"},{"en":"Many people think the club is small; in fact, it has over two hundred members.","zh":"許多人以為該學會很小；事實上，它有超過二百名成員。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the next statement may surprise the listener.","zh":"當下一句可能令聽者意外時，這個片語很有用。"},{"en":"It often signals contrast with an assumption.","zh":"它常暗示與假設形成對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the vocabulary of","meaning":"……的詞彙","examples":[{"en":"The vocabulary of Icelandic is continually increasing.","zh":"冰島語的詞彙正在持續增加。"},{"en":"The vocabulary of a language means all the words used in that language.","zh":"the vocabulary of a language 指該語言所使用的所有詞語。"},{"en":"The vocabulary of science changes as new discoveries are made.","zh":"科學詞彙會隨新發現而改變。"},{"en":"A language can grow by creating new vocabulary for modern ideas.","zh":"一種語言可以透過為現代概念創造新詞而成長。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on word stock rather than grammar or pronunciation.","zh":"這個片語着重詞庫，而不是文法或發音。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"continually increasing","meaning":"持續增加","examples":[{"en":"The vocabulary of Icelandic is continually increasing.","zh":"冰島語的詞彙正在持續增加。"},{"en":"Continually increasing means growing again and again over time.","zh":"continually increasing 指隨時間不斷增長。"},{"en":"The number of online resources for students is continually increasing.","zh":"給學生使用的網上資源數量正在持續增加。"},{"en":"If vocabulary continually increases, a language can describe new inventions and ideas.","zh":"如果詞彙持續增加，一種語言便能描述新發明和新想法。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests ongoing growth rather than a one-time change.","zh":"這個片語暗示持續增長，而不是一次性改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"need a new word for","meaning":"需要一個表示……的新詞","examples":[{"en":"Speakers create a new word when they need a new word for something.","zh":"當使用者需要一個表示某事的新詞時，他們會創造新詞。"},{"en":"To need a new word for something means to require a term to describe a new idea, object, or activity.","zh":"need a new word for something 指需要一個詞語來描述新概念、物件或活動。"},{"en":"Societies need new words for inventions such as apps and drones.","zh":"社會需要表示應用程式和無人機等發明的新詞。"},{"en":"Without new words, speakers may borrow terms from another language.","zh":"如果沒有新詞，使用者可能會從另一種語言借用詞語。"},{"en":"This phrase connects vocabulary creation with social change.","zh":"這個片語把詞彙創造與社會變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"tend to create","meaning":"傾向於創造","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic speakers tend to create new words.","zh":"冰島語使用者傾向於創造新詞。"},{"en":"To tend to create means to usually or generally make something.","zh":"tend to create 指通常或一般會製造某物。"},{"en":"Young people tend to create new slang when they communicate online.","zh":"年輕人在網上溝通時，傾向於創造新潮語。"},{"en":"A speech community may create new words instead of borrowing foreign ones.","zh":"一個語言社群可能傾向於創造新詞，而不是借用外來詞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a general habit, not something that always happens.","zh":"這個片語描述一般習慣，而不是一定每次都發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"They tend to create new words rather than borrow from another language.","zh":"他們傾向於創造新詞，而不是從另一種語言借用。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of.","zh":"rather than 指而不是。"},{"en":"The school chose to repair old desks rather than buy new ones.","zh":"學校選擇修理舊書桌，而不是購買新書桌。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing two possible choices.","zh":"這個片語適合比較兩個可能選擇。"},{"en":"It often shows a preference for one option over another.","zh":"它常顯示較偏好其中一個選項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"borrow from another language","meaning":"從另一種語言借用","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic speakers often avoid borrowing from another language.","zh":"冰島語使用者常避免從另一種語言借用詞語。"},{"en":"To borrow from another language means to take a word or expression from that language and use it in your own.","zh":"borrow from another language 指從另一種語言取用詞語或表達，並放入自己的語言使用。"},{"en":"Many languages borrow from English when discussing computers and the internet.","zh":"許多語言在討論電腦和互聯網時會從英語借用詞語。"},{"en":"Borrowing can enrich a language, but some communities prefer creating native terms.","zh":"借詞可以豐富語言，但有些社群較喜歡創造本族語詞。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in discussions of vocabulary change.","zh":"這個片語常見於詞彙變化討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make something quite special","meaning":"令某物相當特別","examples":[{"en":"All this makes Icelandic quite a special language.","zh":"這一切令冰島語成為相當特別的語言。"},{"en":"To make something quite special means to give it unusual or valuable qualities.","zh":"make something quite special 指賦予某物不尋常或有價值的特質。"},{"en":"The school’s long history makes it quite special to former students.","zh":"學校悠久歷史令它對舊生相當特別。"},{"en":"Icelandic is special because it has preserved old forms while creating modern words.","zh":"冰島語特別之處在於它保留古老形式，同時創造現代詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why something stands out from others.","zh":"這個片語解釋某物為何與眾不同。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"change very little","meaning":"變化很少","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic has changed very little in the past millennium.","zh":"冰島語在過去一千年變化很少。"},{"en":"To change very little means to remain almost the same over time.","zh":"change very little 指隨時間幾乎保持不變。"},{"en":"The village layout has changed very little since my grandparents were young.","zh":"自我祖父母年輕時起，村莊佈局變化很少。"},{"en":"A language that changes very little can preserve older literature more clearly.","zh":"變化很少的語言可以更清楚保存較古老文學。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stability across time.","zh":"這個片語描述跨時間的穩定性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"past millennium","meaning":"過去一千年","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic has changed very little in the past millennium.","zh":"冰島語在過去一千年變化很少。"},{"en":"The past millennium means the last thousand years.","zh":"past millennium 指過去一千年。"},{"en":"Many cities have changed greatly over the past millennium.","zh":"許多城市在過去一千年變化很大。"},{"en":"Discussing a past millennium gives a very long historical perspective.","zh":"討論過去一千年，可以提供很長的歷史視角。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in history or language study.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常用於歷史或語言研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"handle concepts","meaning":"處理概念","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic can handle twenty-first-century concepts.","zh":"冰島語可以處理 21 世紀概念。"},{"en":"To handle concepts means to express, explain, or deal with ideas effectively.","zh":"handle concepts 指有效表達、解釋或處理想法。"},{"en":"A language needs to handle scientific concepts if it is used in education.","zh":"如果一種語言用於教育，它需要能處理科學概念。"},{"en":"If a language cannot handle modern ideas, speakers may switch to another language for those topics.","zh":"如果一種語言不能處理現代想法，使用者可能在那些主題上轉用另一種語言。"},{"en":"This phrase shows whether a language can serve modern communication needs.","zh":"這個片語顯示一種語言能否滿足現代溝通需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"twenty-first-century concepts","meaning":"21世紀概念","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic can handle twenty-first-century concepts related to technology.","zh":"冰島語可以處理與科技相關的 21 世紀概念。"},{"en":"Twenty-first-century concepts are modern ideas connected with today’s world.","zh":"twenty-first-century concepts 指與當今世界相關的現代想法。"},{"en":"Artificial intelligence, social media, and cloud computing are twenty-first-century concepts.","zh":"人工智能、社交媒體和雲端運算都是 21 世紀概念。"},{"en":"Languages need words for modern concepts if they are to remain useful in daily life.","zh":"如果語言要在日常生活中保持實用，就需要表達現代概念的詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to ideas of the current century.","zh":"這個片語指當前世紀的概念。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"related to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The concepts are related to computers and digital technology.","zh":"這些概念與電腦和數碼科技有關。"},{"en":"Related to means connected with or linked to something.","zh":"related to 指與某事有連繫或關係。"},{"en":"The project is related to climate change and local farming.","zh":"該項目與氣候變化和本地農業有關。"},{"en":"When ideas are related to technology, they may need new vocabulary.","zh":"當概念與科技有關，它們可能需要新詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for showing connection between topics.","zh":"這個片語適合用來顯示主題之間的連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the use of computers","meaning":"電腦的使用","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic can express concepts related to the use of computers.","zh":"冰島語可以表達與電腦使用有關的概念。"},{"en":"The use of computers means how computers are used for work, study, communication, or entertainment.","zh":"the use of computers 指電腦如何用於工作、學習、溝通或娛樂。"},{"en":"The use of computers in schools has changed how students write and research.","zh":"學校中電腦的使用改變了學生寫作和研究的方式。"},{"en":"A language needs computer-related vocabulary if speakers use computers daily.","zh":"如果使用者每天使用電腦，一種語言就需要與電腦相關的詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical computer activity, not only the machines themselves.","zh":"這個片語指實際電腦活動，而不只是機器本身。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take, for example","meaning":"以……為例","examples":[{"en":"Take, for example, the Icelandic word for web browser.","zh":"以冰島語中表示網頁瀏覽器的詞為例。"},{"en":"Take, for example is used to introduce a specific example.","zh":"take, for example 用來引入一個具體例子。"},{"en":"Many languages create new technology terms. Take, for example, the word for smartphone.","zh":"許多語言會創造新的科技詞語。以智能電話一詞為例。"},{"en":"This phrase helps make an abstract point clearer through one case.","zh":"這個片語透過一個案例令抽象觀點更清楚。"},{"en":"It is common in lectures and explanatory writing.","zh":"它常見於講座和說明性寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"web browser","meaning":"網頁瀏覽器","examples":[{"en":"The Icelandic word for web browser is vafri.","zh":"冰島語中表示網頁瀏覽器的詞是 vafri。"},{"en":"A web browser is software used to visit and view websites.","zh":"web browser 指用來到訪和查看網站的軟件。"},{"en":"Chrome, Safari, Firefox, and Edge are examples of web browsers.","zh":"Chrome、Safari、Firefox 和 Edge 都是網頁瀏覽器的例子。"},{"en":"A language needs a word for web browser because people use the internet every day.","zh":"一種語言需要表示網頁瀏覽器的詞，因為人們每天使用互聯網。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common technology term.","zh":"這個片語是常見科技詞語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"come from","meaning":"來自……","examples":[{"en":"The word vafri comes from the verb “to wander”.","zh":"vafri 這個詞來自「漫遊」這個動詞。"},{"en":"To come from something means to originate from it.","zh":"come from something 指源自某事物。"},{"en":"Many English words come from Latin, French, or Greek.","zh":"許多英文字來自拉丁語、法語或希臘語。"},{"en":"Knowing where a word comes from can help learners understand its meaning.","zh":"知道一個詞來自哪裡，可以幫助學習者理解其意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining word origins.","zh":"這個片語適合用於解釋詞源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the verb “to wander”","meaning":"「漫遊」這個動詞","examples":[{"en":"The Icelandic word for web browser comes from the verb “to wander”.","zh":"冰島語中表示網頁瀏覽器的詞來自「漫遊」這個動詞。"},{"en":"The verb “to wander” means to move around without a fixed route or clear destination.","zh":"the verb “to wander” 指沒有固定路線或明確目的地四處走動。"},{"en":"People may wander through a city when they have no strict plan.","zh":"人們沒有嚴格計劃時，可能在城市中漫遊。"},{"en":"The idea of wandering fits web browsing because users move from page to page.","zh":"漫遊的概念很適合網頁瀏覽，因為使用者從一個頁面移到另一個頁面。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the root meaning behind a technology word.","zh":"這個片語解釋科技詞背後的詞根意思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"I can’t think of","meaning":"我想不到","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer cannot think of a more appropriate term.","zh":"講師想不到一個更合適的詞語。"},{"en":"I can’t think of means I cannot imagine or find an example in my mind.","zh":"I can’t think of 指我想像不到或想不起例子。"},{"en":"I can’t think of a better place to study than the library.","zh":"我想不到比圖書館更適合溫習的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to praise something by saying no better example comes to mind.","zh":"這個片語常透過表示想不到更好例子來讚賞某事。"},{"en":"It sounds natural in speech and discussion.","zh":"它在說話和討論中聽起來自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"appropriate term","meaning":"合適的詞語","examples":[{"en":"Vafri is an appropriate term for a web browser.","zh":"vafri 是表示網頁瀏覽器的合適詞語。"},{"en":"An appropriate term is a word or phrase that fits the meaning and context well.","zh":"appropriate term 指意思和語境都很配合的詞或片語。"},{"en":"“Online lesson” is an appropriate term for a class held through the internet.","zh":"“Online lesson” 是表示透過互聯網上課的合適詞語。"},{"en":"A good term should be clear, meaningful, and easy for speakers to accept.","zh":"好詞語應清楚、有意義，而且容易被使用者接受。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evaluating vocabulary.","zh":"這個片語適合用於評價詞彙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"that’s exactly what","meaning":"那正正是……","examples":[{"en":"Browsing the internet is exactly what the word suggests.","zh":"瀏覽互聯網正正是這個詞所暗示的意思。"},{"en":"That’s exactly what means that is precisely the thing being described.","zh":"that’s exactly what 指那正正就是正在描述的事情。"},{"en":"Reading quietly is exactly what a library is for.","zh":"安靜閱讀正正是圖書館的用途。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly confirms that an explanation matches reality.","zh":"這個片語強烈確認解釋與現實相符。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing why a word or idea is suitable.","zh":"當顯示一個詞或想法為何合適時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mentally","meaning":"在心理上","examples":[{"en":"You wander mentally when you browse the internet.","zh":"當你瀏覽互聯網時，你是在心理上漫遊。"},{"en":"Mentally means in the mind or through thought rather than physical movement.","zh":"mentally 指在腦海中或透過思想，而不是身體移動。"},{"en":"A reader may mentally travel to another country while reading a novel.","zh":"讀者閱讀小說時，可能在心理上前往另一個國家。"},{"en":"Online browsing can feel like mental wandering because one idea leads to another.","zh":"網上瀏覽可以像心理漫遊，因為一個想法會引向另一個想法。"},{"en":"This word contrasts thinking activity with physical activity.","zh":"這個字把思考活動與身體活動作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"browse the internet","meaning":"瀏覽互聯網","examples":[{"en":"You wander mentally when you browse the internet.","zh":"當你瀏覽互聯網時，你是在心理上漫遊。"},{"en":"To browse the internet means to look through websites, pages, and information online.","zh":"browse the internet 指在線上瀏覽網站、頁面和資訊。"},{"en":"Students often browse the internet to find articles for homework.","zh":"學生常瀏覽互聯網，尋找功課文章。"},{"en":"Browsing can be useful, but it can also distract people from their original purpose.","zh":"瀏覽可以有用，但也可能令人偏離原本目的。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday technology use.","zh":"這個片語常見於日常科技使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"and so on","meaning":"等等","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer gives examples of Icelandic technology words and so on.","zh":"講師舉出冰島語科技詞語等等的例子。"},{"en":"And so on means and other similar things.","zh":"and so on 指以及其他相似事物。"},{"en":"The course covers grammar, vocabulary, pronunciation, and so on.","zh":"課程涵蓋文法、詞彙、發音等等。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids listing every example when the pattern is already clear.","zh":"當模式已清楚時，這個片語可避免列出每個例子。"},{"en":"It is useful but should not be overused in formal writing.","zh":"它很有用，但正式寫作中不應過度使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"alive and growing","meaning":"仍然有生命力並持續發展","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic is alive and growing.","zh":"冰島語仍然有生命力並持續發展。"},{"en":"Alive and growing means active, used by people, and still developing.","zh":"alive and growing 指活躍、有人使用，而且仍在發展。"},{"en":"A language is alive and growing when speakers create new words and use it in daily life.","zh":"當使用者創造新詞並在日常生活中使用，一種語言便仍然有生命力並持續發展。"},{"en":"Even a small language can remain alive if it is used in homes, schools, and public life.","zh":"即使是小語種，只要在家庭、學校和公共生活中被使用，也能保持生命力。"},{"en":"This phrase presents a language as living rather than frozen in the past.","zh":"這個片語把語言呈現為活的，而不是停留在過去。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a big but","meaning":"一個重大的「但是」","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic is growing, but there is a big but.","zh":"冰島語正在發展，但有一個重大的「但是」。"},{"en":"A big but means an important problem or qualification after a positive statement.","zh":"a big but 指在正面陳述後出現的重要問題或保留。"},{"en":"The plan sounds excellent, but there is a big but: it is too expensive.","zh":"這個計劃聽起來很好，但有一個重大的「但是」：它太昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase prepares listeners for a serious limitation.","zh":"這個片語讓聽者準備面對嚴重限制。"},{"en":"It is conversational and slightly dramatic.","zh":"它語氣口語，並帶點戲劇性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"young Icelanders","meaning":"年輕冰島人","examples":[{"en":"Young Icelanders spend a great deal of time in the digital world.","zh":"年輕冰島人花大量時間在數碼世界中。"},{"en":"Young Icelanders are young people from Iceland or young speakers in Icelandic society.","zh":"young Icelanders 指來自冰島的年輕人，或冰島語社會中的年輕使用者。"},{"en":"Young Icelanders may use English daily when playing games or using social media.","zh":"年輕冰島人在玩遊戲或使用社交媒體時，可能每天使用英語。"},{"en":"Their language habits matter because they shape the future of Icelandic.","zh":"他們的語言習慣很重要，因為會塑造冰島語的未來。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the younger generation in Iceland.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於冰島的年輕一代。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spend a great deal of time","meaning":"花大量時間","examples":[{"en":"Young Icelanders spend a great deal of time in the digital world.","zh":"年輕冰島人花大量時間在數碼世界中。"},{"en":"To spend a great deal of time means to use a very large amount of time.","zh":"spend a great deal of time 指使用非常多時間。"},{"en":"Many teenagers spend a great deal of time watching videos online.","zh":"許多青少年花大量時間在網上看影片。"},{"en":"The more time people spend in one language environment, the more that language may influence them.","zh":"人們在某種語言環境中花越多時間，該語言就可能越影響他們。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a large time investment.","zh":"這個片語強調大量時間投入。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"digital world","meaning":"數碼世界","examples":[{"en":"Young Icelanders spend much of their time in the digital world.","zh":"年輕冰島人大部分時間都在數碼世界中。"},{"en":"The digital world means online spaces, apps, games, websites, and digital communication.","zh":"digital world 指網上空間、應用程式、遊戲、網站和數碼溝通。"},{"en":"Students enter the digital world when they use learning platforms or social media.","zh":"學生使用學習平台或社交媒體時，就進入數碼世界。"},{"en":"The language of the digital world can influence how young people speak offline.","zh":"數碼世界的語言可以影響年輕人在線下如何說話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes modern online life.","zh":"這個片語描述現代網上生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"predominantly English","meaning":"主要以英語為主","examples":[{"en":"The digital world is predominantly English.","zh":"數碼世界主要以英語為主。"},{"en":"Predominantly English means mainly or mostly in English.","zh":"predominantly English 指主要或大部分使用英語。"},{"en":"Many coding resources online are predominantly English.","zh":"許多網上編程資源主要以英語為主。"},{"en":"If digital content is predominantly English, speakers of smaller languages may use English more often.","zh":"如果數碼內容主要以英語為主，小語種使用者可能更常使用英語。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong language dominance.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈語言主導地位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"comparatively recently","meaning":"相對近年","examples":[{"en":"Smartphones did not exist until comparatively recently.","zh":"智能電話直到相對近年才出現。"},{"en":"Comparatively recently means quite recently when compared with a longer period of history.","zh":"comparatively recently 指與較長歷史相比，是相當近期。"},{"en":"Social media became common comparatively recently when compared with books or newspapers.","zh":"與書籍或報紙相比，社交媒體是在相對近年才普及。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds listeners that a major change happened in a short time.","zh":"這個片語提醒聽眾，重大變化在短時間內發生。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing modern developments with long histories.","zh":"當比較現代發展與長歷史時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"use them all the time","meaning":"一直使用它們","examples":[{"en":"Young people use smartphones all the time.","zh":"年輕人一直使用智能電話。"},{"en":"To use them all the time means to use them very frequently, almost constantly.","zh":"use them all the time 指非常頻密地使用它們，幾乎不停使用。"},{"en":"Some students use their phones all the time for messages, videos, and schoolwork.","zh":"有些學生一直用電話傳訊息、看影片和做功課。"},{"en":"Constant use can make a device’s language settings very influential.","zh":"持續使用會令裝置的語言設定很有影響力。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and emphasises frequency.","zh":"這個片語較口語，強調頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in many respects","meaning":"在很多方面","examples":[{"en":"Smartphone use is a good thing in many respects.","zh":"智能電話的使用在很多方面是好事。"},{"en":"In many respects means in many ways or from several points of view.","zh":"in many respects 指在許多方面或從幾個角度來看。"},{"en":"Online learning is useful in many respects, but it cannot replace every classroom experience.","zh":"網上學習在很多方面有用，但不能取代所有課室經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a balanced discussion by admitting advantages before discussing problems.","zh":"這個片語透過先承認優點，再討論問題，讓討論更平衡。"},{"en":"It is slightly formal and often used in essays or lectures.","zh":"它略正式，常用於文章或講座。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"promote bilingual skills","meaning":"促進雙語能力","examples":[{"en":"Digital technology promotes young people’s bilingual skills.","zh":"數碼科技促進年輕人的雙語能力。"},{"en":"To promote bilingual skills means to help people develop ability in two languages.","zh":"promote bilingual skills 指幫助人們發展兩種語言的能力。"},{"en":"Watching videos in English and discussing them in Icelandic may promote bilingual skills.","zh":"看英語影片並用冰島語討論，可能促進雙語能力。"},{"en":"Technology can expose learners to another language every day.","zh":"科技可以讓學習者每天接觸另一種語言。"},{"en":"This phrase presents language influence as a possible benefit.","zh":"這個片語把語言影響呈現為一種可能好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bilingual skills","meaning":"雙語能力","examples":[{"en":"Young Icelanders develop bilingual skills through digital technology.","zh":"年輕冰島人透過數碼科技發展雙語能力。"},{"en":"Bilingual skills are the abilities to understand, speak, read, or write in two languages.","zh":"bilingual skills 指理解、說、讀或寫兩種語言的能力。"},{"en":"A student with bilingual skills may switch between Cantonese and English easily.","zh":"有雙語能力的學生可能輕鬆在粵語和英語之間轉換。"},{"en":"Bilingual skills can help education and work, but they should not weaken a child’s first language.","zh":"雙語能力可以幫助教育和工作，但不應削弱孩子的第一語言。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on ability in two languages.","zh":"這個片語着重兩種語言能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the extent of","meaning":"……的程度","examples":[{"en":"The extent of the influence of English is staggering.","zh":"英語影響的程度令人震驚。"},{"en":"The extent of something means how large, strong, or serious it is.","zh":"the extent of something 指某事的大小、強度或嚴重程度。"},{"en":"The extent of students’ phone use surprised many teachers.","zh":"學生使用電話的程度令許多老師驚訝。"},{"en":"Measuring the extent of a problem helps people decide how urgent it is.","zh":"量度問題的程度有助人們決定它有多緊急。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing scale or degree.","zh":"這個片語適合討論規模或程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"influence of English","meaning":"英語的影響","examples":[{"en":"The influence of English in the virtual world is staggering.","zh":"英語在虛擬世界中的影響令人震驚。"},{"en":"The influence of English means the effect English has on people, languages, or behaviour.","zh":"influence of English 指英語對人、語言或行為產生的影響。"},{"en":"The influence of English can be seen in technology, music, games, and business.","zh":"英語的影響可見於科技、音樂、遊戲和商業。"},{"en":"If English dominates online spaces, smaller languages may become less visible.","zh":"如果英語主導網上空間，小語種可能變得較不顯眼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes language power and impact.","zh":"這個片語描述語言力量和影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"virtual world","meaning":"虛擬世界","examples":[{"en":"English has a strong influence in the virtual world.","zh":"英語在虛擬世界中有強大影響。"},{"en":"The virtual world means online or digital spaces where people communicate, play, learn, or work.","zh":"virtual world 指人們溝通、玩樂、學習或工作的網上或數碼空間。"},{"en":"Teenagers may spend hours in the virtual world through games and social media.","zh":"青少年可能透過遊戲和社交媒體在虛擬世界中花數小時。"},{"en":"The virtual world can shape real-life language habits.","zh":"虛擬世界可以塑造現實生活中的語言習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to digital experience rather than physical places.","zh":"這個片語指數碼經驗，而不是實體地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"staggering","meaning":"令人震驚的","examples":[{"en":"The extent of English influence is staggering.","zh":"英語影響的程度令人震驚。"},{"en":"Staggering means extremely surprising, impressive, or shocking.","zh":"staggering 指極令人驚訝、印象深刻或震撼。"},{"en":"The amount of time teenagers spend online is staggering.","zh":"青少年花在網上的時間令人震驚。"},{"en":"This word often suggests that a number or effect is much bigger than expected.","zh":"這個字常暗示某數字或影響遠大於預期。"},{"en":"It is stronger than “surprising”.","zh":"它比 “surprising” 更強烈。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"happen really fast","meaning":"發生得非常快","examples":[{"en":"The change is happening really fast.","zh":"這個變化發生得非常快。"},{"en":"To happen really fast means to take place very quickly.","zh":"happen really fast 指非常迅速地發生。"},{"en":"The shift from paper homework to online homework happened really fast.","zh":"從紙本功課轉到網上功課的變化發生得非常快。"},{"en":"Rapid change can make it difficult for parents, teachers, and governments to respond in time.","zh":"快速變化會令家長、老師和政府難以及時回應。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and emphasises speed.","zh":"這個片語較口語，強調速度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"less concerning","meaning":"較不令人擔心","examples":[{"en":"The change is less concerning for parents and grandparents.","zh":"對父母和祖父母來說，這個變化較不令人擔心。"},{"en":"Less concerning means causing less worry.","zh":"less concerning 指造成較少憂慮。"},{"en":"Online slang may be less concerning for adults who already have strong writing skills.","zh":"對已有強寫作能力的成年人來說，網上潮語可能較不令人擔心。"},{"en":"A change can be less concerning for one group but more serious for another.","zh":"某變化對一個群體可能較不令人擔心，但對另一群體可能更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase compares levels of worry.","zh":"這個片語比較憂慮程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"native-speaker skills","meaning":"母語者能力","examples":[{"en":"Older generations already have native-speaker skills in Icelandic.","zh":"較年長一代已擁有冰島語的母語者能力。"},{"en":"Native-speaker skills are the natural, fluent abilities of someone who grew up using a language.","zh":"native-speaker skills 指從小使用某語言的人所具備的自然流利能力。"},{"en":"A person with native-speaker skills can usually speak naturally and understand cultural meanings.","zh":"有母語者能力的人通常可以自然說話並理解文化含義。"},{"en":"Adults with strong native-speaker skills may be less affected by English online content.","zh":"有強大母語能力的成年人，可能較少受網上英語內容影響。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on deep fluency in a first language.","zh":"這個片語着重第一語言的深層流利度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the outcome","meaning":"結果","examples":[{"en":"For young speakers, the outcome is troubling.","zh":"對年輕使用者而言，結果令人不安。"},{"en":"The outcome means the result or consequence of a situation.","zh":"the outcome 指某情況的結果或後果。"},{"en":"The outcome of the new policy will depend on how schools apply it.","zh":"新政策的結果將取決於學校如何實施。"},{"en":"Looking at outcomes helps people judge whether a change is helpful or harmful.","zh":"觀察結果有助人們判斷變化是有益還是有害。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in analysis and discussion.","zh":"這個片語常見於分析和討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a little troubling","meaning":"有點令人不安","examples":[{"en":"The outcome for young speakers is a little troubling.","zh":"對年輕使用者而言，結果有點令人不安。"},{"en":"A little troubling means somewhat worrying or disturbing.","zh":"a little troubling 指有點令人擔心或不安。"},{"en":"The drop in students’ reading time is a little troubling.","zh":"學生閱讀時間下降有點令人不安。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds moderate, but it still signals real concern.","zh":"這個片語語氣溫和，但仍表示真正關注。"},{"en":"It is useful when the speaker wants to avoid sounding too extreme.","zh":"當說話者想避免語氣過於極端時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"playground conversations","meaning":"操場上的對話","examples":[{"en":"Playground conversations in Icelandic schools may be conducted in English.","zh":"冰島學校操場上的對話可能以英語進行。"},{"en":"Playground conversations are informal talks children have while playing or spending breaks outside class.","zh":"playground conversations 指兒童玩耍或課外休息時的非正式談話。"},{"en":"Teachers can learn a lot from playground conversations because they show children’s natural language choices.","zh":"老師可以從操場上的對話了解很多，因為它們顯示兒童自然的語言選擇。"},{"en":"If children speak English even during breaks, it may show English is entering everyday life deeply.","zh":"如果兒童連小息也說英語，可能顯示英語正深深進入日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to casual student speech outside lessons.","zh":"這個片語指課堂外的學生 casual speech。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"secondary schools","meaning":"中學","examples":[{"en":"Teachers have noticed English conversations in Icelandic secondary schools.","zh":"老師注意到冰島中學裏有英語對話。"},{"en":"Secondary schools are schools for older children, usually after primary school.","zh":"secondary schools 指小學之後、供較年長兒童就讀的學校。"},{"en":"Students in secondary schools often have more exposure to online games, videos, and social media.","zh":"中學生通常更常接觸網上遊戲、影片和社交媒體。"},{"en":"Language habits in secondary schools can show how teenagers use language with peers.","zh":"中學中的語言習慣可以顯示青少年如何與同輩用語言。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the stage before university or further education.","zh":"這個片語指大學或進一步教育之前的階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be conducted entirely in","meaning":"完全以……進行","examples":[{"en":"Some conversations are conducted entirely in English.","zh":"有些對話完全以英語進行。"},{"en":"To be conducted entirely in a language means to happen completely in that language.","zh":"be conducted entirely in a language 指完全用某語言進行。"},{"en":"The meeting was conducted entirely in English because all guests understood it.","zh":"會議完全以英語進行，因為所有賓客都明白。"},{"en":"If children’s conversations are conducted entirely in another language, their first language may be used less.","zh":"如果兒童對話完全以另一種語言進行，他們的第一語言可能使用較少。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used for meetings, lessons, and discussions.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常用於會議、課堂和討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"much younger children","meaning":"年紀小得多的兒童","examples":[{"en":"Teachers of much younger children have reported similar problems.","zh":"教年紀小得多的兒童的老師也匯報了類似問題。"},{"en":"Much younger children means children who are considerably younger than the group just discussed.","zh":"much younger children 指比剛才討論的群體年幼得多的兒童。"},{"en":"Much younger children may pick up language habits from cartoons and games very quickly.","zh":"年紀小得多的兒童可能很快從卡通和遊戲中學到語言習慣。"},{"en":"If similar language shifts appear among younger children, the change may be spreading early.","zh":"如果類似語言轉變出現在更年幼兒童身上，變化可能很早已開始擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase compares age groups.","zh":"這個片語比較年齡群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"report situations where","meaning":"匯報……的情況","examples":[{"en":"Teachers have reported situations where children prefer English.","zh":"老師匯報了一些兒童較喜歡英語的情況。"},{"en":"To report situations where something happens means to describe cases in which that thing occurs.","zh":"report situations where something happens 指描述某事發生的個案或情況。"},{"en":"Teachers reported situations where students used translation apps instead of writing themselves.","zh":"老師匯報了一些學生使用翻譯程式而不是自己寫作的情況。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving evidence from real observations.","zh":"這個片語適合用於提供來自真實觀察的證據。"},{"en":"It helps move from general claims to specific examples.","zh":"它幫助從一般說法轉向具體例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"find it easier to","meaning":"覺得……較容易","examples":[{"en":"Some children find it easier to describe pictures in English.","zh":"有些兒童覺得用英語描述圖片較容易。"},{"en":"To find it easier to do something means to feel that doing it requires less effort.","zh":"find it easier to do something 指覺得做某事較不費力。"},{"en":"Some students find it easier to speak than to write in a second language.","zh":"有些學生覺得用第二語言說話比寫作較容易。"},{"en":"If children find English easier for certain tasks, they may use Icelandic less in those areas.","zh":"如果兒童覺得某些任務用英語較容易，他們在那些範疇可能較少使用冰島語。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal experience of difficulty.","zh":"這個片語描述個人對難度的感受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"say what is in a picture","meaning":"說出圖片裏有甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Children find it easier to say what is in a picture using English.","zh":"兒童覺得用英語說出圖片裏有甚麼較容易。"},{"en":"To say what is in a picture means to describe the objects, people, actions, or details shown in it.","zh":"say what is in a picture 指描述圖片中顯示的物件、人物、動作或細節。"},{"en":"In a speaking test, students may need to say what is in a picture clearly.","zh":"在口試中，學生可能需要清楚說出圖片裏有甚麼。"},{"en":"Picture description can reveal which language feels more available to a child.","zh":"圖片描述可以顯示哪種語言對孩子來說更容易調動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in language learning and classroom tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於語言學習和課堂任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Some children use English rather than Icelandic to describe pictures.","zh":"有些兒童用英語而不是冰島語描述圖片。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of.","zh":"rather than 指而不是。"},{"en":"Some students type notes rather than write them by hand.","zh":"有些學生打字做筆記，而不是手寫。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one choice is made in place of another.","zh":"這個片語顯示選擇了一項而非另一項。"},{"en":"It is useful when contrasting language choices.","zh":"它適合用於對比語言選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"real and worrying consequence","meaning":"真實而令人擔憂的後果","examples":[{"en":"The real and worrying consequence is that young Icelanders may lose their mother tongue.","zh":"真實而令人擔憂的後果是年輕冰島人可能失去母語。"},{"en":"A real and worrying consequence is an actual result that causes serious concern.","zh":"real and worrying consequence 指真實存在而且令人嚴重關注的結果。"},{"en":"A real and worrying consequence of too much screen time may be weaker sleep habits.","zh":"過多螢幕時間一個真實而令人擔憂的後果，可能是睡眠習慣變差。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the speaker sees the issue as serious, not theoretical.","zh":"這個片語表示說話者認為問題嚴重，而不是純理論。"},{"en":"It often introduces the main danger of a trend.","zh":"它常引入某趨勢的主要危險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"young generation","meaning":"年輕一代","examples":[{"en":"The young generation in Iceland is at risk of losing its mother tongue.","zh":"冰島年輕一代有失去母語的風險。"},{"en":"The young generation means young people in a society, especially compared with older people.","zh":"young generation 指社會中的年輕人，尤其是與較年長人士相比。"},{"en":"The young generation often adopts new technology faster than their parents.","zh":"年輕一代通常比父母更快採用新科技。"},{"en":"If the young generation changes language habits, the future of the language changes too.","zh":"如果年輕一代改變語言習慣，語言的未來也會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on age and future social change.","zh":"這個片語着重年齡和未來社會變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be at risk of","meaning":"有……的風險","examples":[{"en":"Young Icelanders are at risk of losing their mother tongue.","zh":"年輕冰島人有失去母語的風險。"},{"en":"To be at risk of something means to face the possibility of a negative result.","zh":"be at risk of something 指面對某種負面結果的可能性。"},{"en":"Small languages are at risk of disappearing if children stop using them.","zh":"如果兒童停止使用小語種，小語種就有消失的風險。"},{"en":"Recognising risk early helps governments and communities act before damage becomes permanent.","zh":"及早識別風險有助政府和社群在傷害永久化前行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in warnings and problem analysis.","zh":"這個片語常見於警告和問題分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lose one’s mother tongue","meaning":"失去母語","examples":[{"en":"Young Icelanders may lose their mother tongue.","zh":"年輕冰島人可能失去母語。"},{"en":"To lose one’s mother tongue means to stop being able to use one’s first language fluently or naturally.","zh":"lose one’s mother tongue 指不再能流利或自然地使用自己的第一語言。"},{"en":"Children may lose their mother tongue if they rarely hear it at school, online, or with friends.","zh":"如果兒童在學校、網上或朋友之間很少聽到母語，他們可能失去母語。"},{"en":"Losing a mother tongue can affect identity, family communication, and cultural memory.","zh":"失去母語會影響身份認同、家庭溝通和文化記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes more than vocabulary loss; it involves personal and cultural connection.","zh":"這個片語描述的不只是詞彙流失，也涉及個人和文化連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"mother tongue","meaning":"母語","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic is the mother tongue of young Icelanders.","zh":"冰島語是年輕冰島人的母語。"},{"en":"A mother tongue is the first language a person learns naturally as a child.","zh":"mother tongue 指一個人小時候自然學會的第一語言。"},{"en":"A child’s mother tongue often carries family stories, emotions, and cultural habits.","zh":"孩子的母語常承載家庭故事、情感和文化習慣。"},{"en":"Strong mother-tongue skills can support learning other languages more deeply.","zh":"強大的母語能力可以支持更深入學習其他語言。"},{"en":"This phrase is personal and cultural, not only linguistic.","zh":"這個片語不只是語言學上的，也帶有個人和文化意義。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"happen to","meaning":"發生在……身上","examples":[{"en":"This is happening to other European languages too.","zh":"這也發生在其他歐洲語言身上。"},{"en":"To happen to someone or something means to affect that person or thing.","zh":"happen to someone or something 指影響某人或某事物。"},{"en":"Similar pressure is happening to small communities around the world.","zh":"類似壓力正在發生在世界各地小社群身上。"},{"en":"When a problem happens to many languages, it becomes a wider cultural issue.","zh":"當問題發生在許多語言身上，它就成為更廣泛的文化議題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows who or what is experiencing the situation.","zh":"這個片語顯示誰或甚麼正在經歷該情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"European languages","meaning":"歐洲語言","examples":[{"en":"Other European languages face similar pressures.","zh":"其他歐洲語言面對類似壓力。"},{"en":"European languages are languages used in Europe, such as French, German, Icelandic, and Welsh.","zh":"European languages 指歐洲使用的語言，例如法語、德語、冰島語和威爾斯語。"},{"en":"Some European languages have millions of speakers, while others are much smaller.","zh":"有些歐洲語言有數百萬使用者，而另一些則小得多。"},{"en":"Digital English can affect European languages differently depending on size and policy support.","zh":"數碼英語會按語言規模和政策支援，以不同方式影響歐洲語言。"},{"en":"This phrase groups languages by region.","zh":"這個片語按地區把語言歸類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be willing to","meaning":"願意……","examples":[{"en":"Internet companies might be willing to offer French options.","zh":"互聯網公司可能願意提供法語選項。"},{"en":"To be willing to do something means to be prepared or ready to do it.","zh":"be willing to do something 指準備好或願意做某事。"},{"en":"A company may be willing to support a language if many customers request it.","zh":"如果許多顧客要求，公司可能願意支援某種語言。"},{"en":"Willingness often depends on cost, demand, and public pressure.","zh":"願意與否常取決於成本、需求和公眾壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes readiness rather than certainty.","zh":"這個片語描述意願，而不是確定會做。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"offer options","meaning":"提供選項","examples":[{"en":"Internet companies may offer French options in their systems.","zh":"互聯網公司可能在系統中提供法語選項。"},{"en":"To offer options means to provide choices for users or customers.","zh":"offer options 指向使用者或顧客提供選擇。"},{"en":"A website may offer language options such as English, Chinese, and Spanish.","zh":"網站可能提供英語、中文和西班牙語等語言選項。"},{"en":"Language options help users feel included and understand services more easily.","zh":"語言選項幫助使用者感到被包括，並更容易理解服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in technology and customer service.","zh":"這個片語常見於科技和客戶服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"justify the expense of","meaning":"證明……的開支是合理的","examples":[{"en":"It is harder to justify the expense of supporting a small language.","zh":"要證明支援一種小語種的開支是合理的較困難。"},{"en":"To justify the expense of something means to show that the cost is reasonable or worth paying.","zh":"justify the expense of something 指顯示某項成本合理或值得支付。"},{"en":"A school must justify the expense of buying new tablets for every student.","zh":"學校必須證明為每位學生購買新平板電腦的開支是合理的。"},{"en":"Companies may hesitate if the number of users is too small to cover development costs.","zh":"如果使用者數量太少而不能抵消開發成本，公司可能會猶豫。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing money and decision-making.","zh":"這個片語適合討論金錢和決策。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"do the same for","meaning":"為……做同樣的事","examples":[{"en":"Companies may not want to do the same for a smaller language.","zh":"公司可能不想為較小的語言做同樣的事。"},{"en":"To do the same for someone or something means to provide the same action, service, or support.","zh":"do the same for someone or something 指提供相同行動、服務或支援。"},{"en":"A website may support Spanish but refuse to do the same for a smaller language.","zh":"網站可能支援西班牙語，但拒絕為較小語言做同樣的事。"},{"en":"Equal support can be difficult when resources and user numbers differ greatly.","zh":"當資源和使用者數量差異很大時，平等支援可能很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase compares treatment across different groups.","zh":"這個片語比較不同群體所受到的待遇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the size of","meaning":"……的規模","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic has a population the size of a French town.","zh":"冰島語使用人口的規模相當於一個法國城鎮。"},{"en":"The size of something means the amount, number, or scale of it.","zh":"the size of something 指某事物的數量、規模或大小。"},{"en":"A language community the size of a small town may struggle to attract major technology investment.","zh":"規模相當於小城鎮的語言社群，可能難以吸引大型科技投資。"},{"en":"Comparing size helps listeners understand scale quickly.","zh":"比較規模有助聽眾快速理解大小。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in comparisons.","zh":"這個片語適合用於比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"drawback","meaning":"不利因素；缺點","examples":[{"en":"The other drawback of Icelandic is its grammar.","zh":"冰島語另一個不利因素是其文法。"},{"en":"A drawback is a disadvantage or problem.","zh":"drawback 指缺點或問題。"},{"en":"One drawback of online learning is that students may feel isolated.","zh":"網上學習的一個缺點是學生可能感到孤立。"},{"en":"Identifying drawbacks makes an argument more balanced and realistic.","zh":"找出缺點可以令論點更平衡和現實。"},{"en":"This word is common in discussions of advantages and disadvantages.","zh":"這個字常見於優缺點討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"significantly more complex than","meaning":"比……複雜得多","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic grammar is significantly more complex than that of most languages.","zh":"冰島語文法比大多數語言複雜得多。"},{"en":"Significantly more complex than means much more difficult or complicated than something else.","zh":"significantly more complex than 指比另一事物困難或複雜得多。"},{"en":"Academic writing is significantly more complex than casual texting.","zh":"學術寫作比隨意短訊複雜得多。"},{"en":"If grammar is highly complex, building language software becomes more difficult.","zh":"如果文法高度複雜，建立語言軟件會更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a strong comparison.","zh":"這個片語作出強烈比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tech giants","meaning":"科技巨頭","examples":[{"en":"The tech giants are not interested in tackling Icelandic grammar.","zh":"科技巨頭對處理冰島語文法沒有興趣。"},{"en":"Tech giants are very large and powerful technology companies.","zh":"tech giants 指非常大型和有影響力的科技公司。"},{"en":"Tech giants often decide which languages receive strong digital support.","zh":"科技巨頭常決定哪些語言得到強大數碼支援。"},{"en":"Smaller languages may struggle if tech giants see too little profit in supporting them.","zh":"如果科技巨頭認為支援小語種利潤太少，小語種可能會面對困難。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to major global technology firms.","zh":"這個片語通常指大型全球科技企業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be interested in tackling","meaning":"有興趣處理……","examples":[{"en":"Tech giants are not interested in tackling this problem.","zh":"科技巨頭沒有興趣處理這個問題。"},{"en":"To be interested in tackling a problem means to want to deal with it seriously.","zh":"be interested in tackling a problem 指想認真處理某問題。"},{"en":"The council is interested in tackling traffic problems near schools.","zh":"區議會有興趣處理學校附近的交通問題。"},{"en":"Companies may not tackle a problem if it is expensive and benefits only a small group.","zh":"如果問題昂貴而且只惠及小群體，公司可能不會處理。"},{"en":"This phrase links interest with practical action.","zh":"這個片語把興趣與實際行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"do something about","meaning":"就……採取行動","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer asks what the Icelandic government is doing about the problem.","zh":"講師問冰島政府正就這個問題採取甚麼行動。"},{"en":"To do something about a problem means to take action to deal with it.","zh":"do something about a problem 指採取行動處理某問題。"},{"en":"The school must do something about noise in the library.","zh":"學校必須就圖書館噪音問題採取行動。"},{"en":"Asking what is being done about a problem shifts attention from concern to action.","zh":"詢問正就問題做甚麼，會把焦點從憂慮轉到行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is practical and problem-focused.","zh":"這個片語很實用，並以問題為中心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"large sums of money","meaning":"大筆資金","examples":[{"en":"Large sums of money are being allocated to a language technology fund.","zh":"大筆資金正被分配給語言科技基金。"},{"en":"Large sums of money means a lot of money.","zh":"large sums of money 指很多金錢。"},{"en":"Governments may spend large sums of money on education, transport, or healthcare.","zh":"政府可能在教育、交通或醫療上花大筆資金。"},{"en":"Supporting small languages digitally can require large sums because software development is costly.","zh":"以數碼方式支援小語種可能需要大筆資金，因為軟件開發成本高。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises financial scale.","zh":"這個片語強調財務規模。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be allocated to","meaning":"被分配給……","examples":[{"en":"Money is being allocated to a language technology fund.","zh":"資金正被分配給語言科技基金。"},{"en":"To be allocated to something means to be officially set aside or assigned for that purpose.","zh":"be allocated to something 指被正式預留或分配作某用途。"},{"en":"More money was allocated to school libraries this year.","zh":"今年更多資金被分配給學校圖書館。"},{"en":"Allocating funds shows that a government or organisation has chosen a priority.","zh":"分配資金顯示政府或機構選擇了優先事項。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in finance or policy.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常用於財務或政策。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"language technology fund","meaning":"語言科技基金","examples":[{"en":"The government has created a language technology fund.","zh":"政府已成立語言科技基金。"},{"en":"A language technology fund is money set aside to support digital tools and systems for a language.","zh":"language technology fund 指預留資金，用來支援某語言的數碼工具和系統。"},{"en":"Such a fund may help build speech recognition, translation tools, and language apps.","zh":"這類基金可能幫助建立語音識別、翻譯工具和語言應用程式。"},{"en":"A small language may need public funding because private companies may not invest enough.","zh":"小語種可能需要公共資金，因為私人公司未必投資足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase connects language policy with technology development.","zh":"這個片語把語言政策與科技發展連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"it is hoped that","meaning":"人們希望……","examples":[{"en":"It is hoped that the fund will lead to new Icelandic digital systems.","zh":"人們希望該基金會促成新的冰島語數碼系統。"},{"en":"It is hoped that means people hope or expect that something positive will happen.","zh":"it is hoped that 指人們希望或期待某個正面結果會發生。"},{"en":"It is hoped that the new library will encourage more children to read.","zh":"人們希望新圖書館會鼓勵更多兒童閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and avoids naming exactly who hopes so.","zh":"這個片語較正式，避免明確說出是誰希望如此。"},{"en":"It is common in reports, announcements, and lectures.","zh":"它常見於報告、公告和講座。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lead to the development of","meaning":"促成……的發展","examples":[{"en":"The fund may lead to the development of Icelandic-language apps.","zh":"該基金可能促成冰島語應用程式的發展。"},{"en":"To lead to the development of something means to cause or support the creation of it.","zh":"lead to the development of something 指造成或支持某物被創造出來。"},{"en":"Extra funding may lead to the development of better online learning tools.","zh":"額外資金可能促成更好網上學習工具的發展。"},{"en":"Public investment can turn an idea into a usable product or system.","zh":"公共投資可以把想法變成可使用的產品或系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing results of funding or policy.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論資金或政策帶來的結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Icelandic-language apps","meaning":"冰島語應用程式","examples":[{"en":"The government hopes to support the development of Icelandic-language apps.","zh":"政府希望支援冰島語應用程式的發展。"},{"en":"Icelandic-language apps are applications that use or support the Icelandic language.","zh":"Icelandic-language apps 指使用或支援冰島語的應用程式。"},{"en":"Icelandic-language apps could help children chat, learn, search, and play in Icelandic.","zh":"冰島語應用程式可以幫助兒童用冰島語聊天、學習、搜尋和玩遊戲。"},{"en":"Apps in a local language make digital life more accessible to native speakers.","zh":"使用本地語言的應用程式令母語者更容易參與數碼生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes digital tools designed for a specific language.","zh":"這個片語描述為特定語言設計的數碼工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"social media","meaning":"社交媒體","examples":[{"en":"The fund may support Icelandic social media and digital systems.","zh":"該基金可能支援冰島語社交媒體和數碼系統。"},{"en":"Social media are online platforms where people share messages, photos, videos, and opinions.","zh":"social media 指人們分享訊息、照片、影片和意見的網上平台。"},{"en":"Teenagers often use social media to talk with friends and follow trends.","zh":"青少年常使用社交媒體與朋友交談和跟隨潮流。"},{"en":"If social media does not support a language well, young people may switch to another language.","zh":"如果社交媒體不充分支援某語言，年輕人可能轉用另一種語言。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to modern communication.","zh":"這個片語是現代溝通的核心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"digital systems","meaning":"數碼系統","examples":[{"en":"The government wants to develop Icelandic digital systems.","zh":"政府希望發展冰島語數碼系統。"},{"en":"Digital systems are computer-based tools, platforms, or services that process information electronically.","zh":"digital systems 指以電腦為基礎、電子化處理資訊的工具、平台或服務。"},{"en":"Schools use digital systems for attendance, homework, and communication with parents.","zh":"學校使用數碼系統處理出席、功課和與家長溝通。"},{"en":"Language-friendly digital systems can help speakers use their mother tongue online.","zh":"對語言友善的數碼系統可以幫助使用者在線上使用母語。"},{"en":"This phrase covers many kinds of technology infrastructure.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋多種類型的科技基建。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"uphill struggle","meaning":"艱巨任務","examples":[{"en":"Developing Icelandic digital systems will be an uphill struggle.","zh":"發展冰島語數碼系統將是一項艱巨任務。"},{"en":"An uphill struggle is a very difficult task that requires effort over time.","zh":"uphill struggle 指非常困難、需要長時間努力的任務。"},{"en":"Improving students’ reading habits can be an uphill struggle if they dislike books.","zh":"如果學生不喜歡書，改善閱讀習慣可以是一項艱巨任務。"},{"en":"Supporting a small language digitally is hard because it needs money, experts, and long-term maintenance.","zh":"以數碼方式支援小語種很困難，因為需要金錢、專家和長期維護。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests difficulty but not impossibility.","zh":"這個片語暗示困難，但不是不可能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on the positive side","meaning":"從正面來看","examples":[{"en":"On the positive side, Icelandic is still the official language.","zh":"從正面來看，冰島語仍然是官方語言。"},{"en":"On the positive side means looking at the good part of a situation.","zh":"on the positive side 指從情況中較好的一面來看。"},{"en":"The project is expensive; on the positive side, it will create many jobs.","zh":"該項目很昂貴；從正面來看，它會創造很多職位。"},{"en":"This phrase helps balance negative points with encouraging information.","zh":"這個片語有助用鼓舞資訊平衡負面重點。"},{"en":"It is common in discussions that weigh pros and cons.","zh":"它常見於權衡利弊的討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"official language","meaning":"官方語言","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic is still the official language of education and government.","zh":"冰島語仍然是教育和政府的官方語言。"},{"en":"An official language is a language used by the government and public institutions.","zh":"official language 指政府和公共機構使用的語言。"},{"en":"An official language may be used in laws, schools, courts, and public announcements.","zh":"官方語言可能用於法律、學校、法院和公共公告。"},{"en":"Official status can protect a language by keeping it central in public life.","zh":"官方地位可以透過讓語言保持在公共生活中心來保護它。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in language policy.","zh":"這個片語在語言政策中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"education and government","meaning":"教育和政府","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic is used in education and government.","zh":"冰島語用於教育和政府。"},{"en":"Education and government refer to schools, universities, public administration, and official institutions.","zh":"education and government 指學校、大學、公共行政和官方機構。"},{"en":"A language used in education and government has strong public support.","zh":"用於教育和政府的語言有強大的公共支援。"},{"en":"If a language remains important in schools and government, it is less likely to disappear quickly.","zh":"如果一種語言在學校和政府中仍然重要，它較不可能快速消失。"},{"en":"This phrase points to major public domains of language use.","zh":"這個片語指出語言使用的主要公共領域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"survive for well over","meaning":"存續超過……很多","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic has survived for well over a thousand years.","zh":"冰島語已存續超過一千年很多。"},{"en":"To survive for well over a period means to continue existing for much longer than that amount of time.","zh":"survive for well over a period 指持續存在的時間遠超過某段時間。"},{"en":"Some traditions have survived for well over five hundred years.","zh":"有些傳統已存續超過五百年很多。"},{"en":"A language that survives for many centuries often has strong cultural support.","zh":"能存續多個世紀的語言通常有強大文化支援。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises impressive historical endurance.","zh":"這個片語強調令人印象深刻的歷史延續力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"experts predict that","meaning":"專家預測……","examples":[{"en":"Experts predict that Icelandic will remain sound in Iceland.","zh":"專家預測冰島語在冰島將保持穩固。"},{"en":"Experts predict that means specialists believe something is likely to happen in the future.","zh":"experts predict that 指專家相信某事未來很可能發生。"},{"en":"Experts predict that digital learning will become more common.","zh":"專家預測數碼學習會變得更普遍。"},{"en":"Predictions are not guarantees, but they are based on knowledge and evidence.","zh":"預測不是保證，但基於知識和證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic and media reports.","zh":"這個片語常見於學術和媒體報道。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"nation state","meaning":"民族國家","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic has a sound future in this nation state.","zh":"冰島語在這個民族國家中有穩固前景。"},{"en":"A nation state is a country whose people share a strong national identity, often including language and culture.","zh":"nation state 指人民共享強烈民族身份的國家，通常包括語言和文化。"},{"en":"A language may be protected more strongly when it is tied to a nation state.","zh":"當語言與民族國家緊密相連，它可能得到更強保護。"},{"en":"In Iceland, the language is connected to national identity and public institutions.","zh":"在冰島，語言與民族身份和公共機構相連。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and used in politics, history, and sociology.","zh":"這個片語較正式，用於政治、歷史和社會學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be sound","meaning":"穩固的；可靠的","examples":[{"en":"The future of Icelandic in Iceland is sound.","zh":"冰島語在冰島的未來是穩固的。"},{"en":"To be sound means to be strong, reliable, or secure.","zh":"be sound 指強健、可靠或安全穩固。"},{"en":"The school’s plan is sound because it is based on clear evidence.","zh":"學校計劃很可靠，因為它基於清楚證據。"},{"en":"A language future is sound if the language remains used in major parts of society.","zh":"如果一種語言仍在社會主要部分被使用，其未來就是穩固的。"},{"en":"This word expresses confidence in stability.","zh":"這個字表達對穩定性的信心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"continue to be so","meaning":"繼續如此","examples":[{"en":"Experts believe the future of Icelandic will continue to be sound.","zh":"專家相信冰島語的未來會繼續穩固。"},{"en":"Continue to be so means remain in the same state as just described.","zh":"continue to be so 指保持剛才描述的同一狀態。"},{"en":"The library is popular now and will probably continue to be so if it extends its hours.","zh":"圖書館現在很受歡迎，如果延長開放時間，可能會繼續如此。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the adjective or description again.","zh":"這個片語避免再次重複形容詞或描述。"},{"en":"It is useful in formal speech and writing.","zh":"它適合用於正式說話和寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"there’s no doubt that","meaning":"毫無疑問……","examples":[{"en":"There’s no doubt that Icelandic is becoming a second choice for young people.","zh":"毫無疑問，冰島語正成為年輕人的第二選擇。"},{"en":"There’s no doubt that means it is certain or very clear that something is true.","zh":"there’s no doubt that 指某事肯定或非常明顯是真的。"},{"en":"There is no doubt that smartphones have changed how students communicate.","zh":"毫無疑問，智能電話改變了學生溝通方式。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strong, confident claim.","zh":"這個片語提出強而有信心的說法。"},{"en":"It is often used before an important conclusion.","zh":"它常用於重要結論之前。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"inevitable second choice","meaning":"不可避免的第二選擇","examples":[{"en":"Icelandic is becoming an inevitable second choice in young people’s lives.","zh":"冰島語正在成為年輕人生活中不可避免的第二選擇。"},{"en":"An inevitable second choice is something that is likely to be used after another preferred option.","zh":"inevitable second choice 指很可能在另一個首選之後才被使用的選項。"},{"en":"If English dominates online life, a local language may become an inevitable second choice there.","zh":"如果英語主導網上生活，本地語言在那裡可能成為不可避免的第二選擇。"},{"en":"The word “inevitable” suggests the change is difficult to avoid.","zh":"“inevitable” 這個字暗示變化難以避免。"},{"en":"This phrase shows concern about a language losing priority.","zh":"這個片語顯示對語言失去優先地位的憂慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"raise important questions","meaning":"引發重要問題","examples":[{"en":"This change raises important questions.","zh":"這個變化引發重要問題。"},{"en":"To raise important questions means to make people think about serious issues that need discussion.","zh":"raise important questions 指令人思考需要討論的嚴肅議題。"},{"en":"Artificial intelligence raises important questions about learning and originality.","zh":"人工智能引發關於學習和原創性的重要問題。"},{"en":"Language change can raise questions about identity, education, and culture.","zh":"語言變化可以引發關於身份、教育和文化的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when moving from facts to deeper reflection.","zh":"這個片語適合用於從事實轉向更深入反思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"consider how much","meaning":"考慮到……有多少","examples":[{"en":"We should consider how much of the past is tied up in a language.","zh":"我們應考慮到有多少過去與一種語言緊密相連。"},{"en":"To consider how much means to think carefully about the degree or amount of something.","zh":"consider how much 指仔細思考某事的程度或數量。"},{"en":"We should consider how much time students spend online every day.","zh":"我們應考慮學生每天花多少時間在網上。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages deeper evaluation rather than a simple yes-or-no judgement.","zh":"這個片語鼓勵更深入評估，而不是簡單的是非判斷。"},{"en":"It is useful in analytical writing and discussion.","zh":"它適合用於分析性寫作和討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be tied up in","meaning":"與……緊密相連","examples":[{"en":"Much of the past is tied up in a language.","zh":"很多過去都與一種語言緊密相連。"},{"en":"To be tied up in something means to be closely connected with it.","zh":"be tied up in something 指與某事緊密連繫。"},{"en":"Family history can be tied up in old letters and photographs.","zh":"家族歷史可以與舊信件和照片緊密相連。"},{"en":"A language carries stories, names, humour, and memories from the past.","zh":"一種語言承載過去的故事、名字、幽默和記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deep connection rather than a loose link.","zh":"這個片語暗示深層連繫，而不是鬆散關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sense of identity","meaning":"身份認同感","examples":[{"en":"Young Icelanders may lose their sense of identity.","zh":"年輕冰島人可能失去身份認同感。"},{"en":"A sense of identity is a feeling of who you are and where you belong.","zh":"sense of identity 指知道自己是誰、屬於哪裡的感覺。"},{"en":"Language can strengthen a sense of identity because it connects people to family and culture.","zh":"語言可以加強身份認同感，因為它把人與家庭和文化連繫起來。"},{"en":"If young people stop using their mother tongue, their cultural identity may feel weaker.","zh":"如果年輕人停止使用母語，他們的文化身份可能感覺較弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in discussions of language, culture, and belonging.","zh":"這個片語常見於語言、文化和歸屬感討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"another issue that concerns","meaning":"另一個令……關注的問題","examples":[{"en":"Another issue that concerns the government is children’s fluency.","zh":"另一個令政府關注的問題是兒童的流利程度。"},{"en":"Another issue that concerns someone means another problem that worries that person or organisation.","zh":"another issue that concerns someone 指另一個令某人或某機構擔心的問題。"},{"en":"Another issue that concerns teachers is students’ overuse of translation tools.","zh":"另一個令老師關注的問題，是學生過度使用翻譯工具。"},{"en":"This phrase adds one more serious point to the discussion.","zh":"這個片語為討論加入另一個嚴肅重點。"},{"en":"It is formal and useful in reports or lectures.","zh":"它較正式，適合用於報告或講座。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"learn through different routes","meaning":"透過不同途徑學習","examples":[{"en":"Children may learn two languages through different routes.","zh":"兒童可能透過不同途徑學習兩種語言。"},{"en":"To learn through different routes means to acquire knowledge or skills in different ways or environments.","zh":"learn through different routes 指透過不同方式或環境獲得知識或技能。"},{"en":"A child may learn English through games but learn Icelandic mainly through family conversations.","zh":"孩子可能透過遊戲學英語，但主要透過家庭對話學冰島語。"},{"en":"Different learning routes can produce uneven ability in speaking, reading, and writing.","zh":"不同學習途徑可能造成說、讀、寫能力不平均。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how learning method affects fluency.","zh":"這個片語解釋學習方式如何影響流利程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"neither of which","meaning":"兩者都不……","examples":[{"en":"Children may learn two languages, neither of which they are fully fluent in.","zh":"兒童可能學習兩種語言，但兩者都不能完全流利使用。"},{"en":"Neither of which means not one of the two things just mentioned.","zh":"neither of which 指剛才提及的兩樣東西中沒有任何一樣。"},{"en":"He studied two instruments, neither of which he practised regularly.","zh":"他學了兩種樂器，但兩者都沒有定期練習。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and refers back to two previous nouns.","zh":"這個片語較正式，指回前面兩個名詞。"},{"en":"It is useful when both options fail to meet a standard.","zh":"當兩個選項都未達標時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be fully fluent in","meaning":"完全流利使用……","examples":[{"en":"Some children may not be fully fluent in either language.","zh":"有些兒童可能不能完全流利使用任何一種語言。"},{"en":"To be fully fluent in a language means to use it easily, accurately, and naturally in many situations.","zh":"be fully fluent in a language 指能在多種情況中輕鬆、準確和自然地使用該語言。"},{"en":"A student may speak English well but not be fully fluent in academic writing.","zh":"學生可能英語說得好，但未能完全流利地進行學術寫作。"},{"en":"Full fluency includes vocabulary, grammar, confidence, and expressive ability.","zh":"完全流利包括詞彙、文法、信心和表達能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a high level of language command.","zh":"這個片語描述高度語言掌握能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"express themselves properly","meaning":"正確表達自己","examples":[{"en":"Children may struggle to express themselves properly.","zh":"兒童可能難以正確表達自己。"},{"en":"To express themselves properly means to communicate thoughts and feelings clearly, accurately, and appropriately.","zh":"express themselves properly 指清楚、準確和合適地表達思想和感受。"},{"en":"Students need enough vocabulary to express themselves properly in essays and discussions.","zh":"學生需要足夠詞彙，才能在文章和討論中正確表達自己。"},{"en":"If children are not fluent in either language, they may find it hard to explain complex ideas.","zh":"如果兒童不能流利使用任何一種語言，他們可能難以解釋複雜想法。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on meaningful communication, not just knowing individual words.","zh":"這個片語着重有意義的溝通，而不只是知道個別詞語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 13 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 14/task-1":[{"front":"be thinking of","meaning":"正在考慮","examples":[{"en":"The woman is thinking of taking the kids to the seaside.","zh":"這位女士正在考慮帶孩子去海邊。"},{"en":"To be thinking of doing something means to be considering it but not yet fully decided.","zh":"be thinking of doing something 的意思是正在考慮做某事，但尚未完全決定。"},{"en":"I’m thinking of joining a gym, but I want to compare the prices first.","zh":"我正在考慮加入健身室，但我想先比較價錢。"},{"en":"People often say they are thinking of doing something when they want advice before making a plan.","zh":"人們想在制定計劃前聽取意見時，常會說自己正在考慮做某事。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an idea is possible, not certain.","zh":"這個短語表示一個想法有可能發生，但未必確定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"take the kids to","meaning":"帶孩子去……","examples":[{"en":"The woman is thinking of taking the kids to the seaside.","zh":"這位女士正在考慮帶孩子去海邊。"},{"en":"To take the kids to a place means to bring children there, usually for an activity, trip, or visit.","zh":"take the kids to 某地的意思是帶孩子到那裡，通常是為了活動、旅行或探訪。"},{"en":"Parents may take the kids to the park when the weather is good.","zh":"天氣好時，父母可能帶孩子去公園。"},{"en":"Taking kids somewhere requires planning because transport, food, safety, and timing all matter.","zh":"帶孩子去某地需要規劃，因為交通、食物、安全和時間都很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in family conversations.","zh":"這個短語常見於家庭對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the seaside","meaning":"海邊","examples":[{"en":"The family may go to the seaside for a surfing holiday.","zh":"這家人可能去海邊度衝浪假期。"},{"en":"The seaside is the area near the sea, often with beaches, shops, and holiday activities.","zh":"the seaside 是靠近海的地區，通常有沙灘、商店和假期活動。"},{"en":"Families often visit the seaside to swim, walk, eat ice cream, or relax.","zh":"家庭常去海邊游泳、散步、吃雪糕或放鬆。"},{"en":"A trip to the seaside can be enjoyable, but weather and safety conditions should be checked.","zh":"去海邊可以很愉快，但應先查看天氣和安全情況。"},{"en":"This phrase usually suggests a holiday or day out near the coast.","zh":"這個短語通常暗示在海岸附近度假或外出一天。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"surfing holiday","meaning":"衝浪假期","examples":[{"en":"The woman is planning a surfing holiday this summer.","zh":"這位女士正在計劃今年夏天的衝浪假期。"},{"en":"A surfing holiday is a trip where surfing is one of the main activities.","zh":"surfing holiday 是以衝浪作為主要活動之一的旅行。"},{"en":"A family may choose a surfing holiday if the children enjoy beaches and water sports.","zh":"如果孩子喜歡沙灘和水上運動，家庭可能選擇衝浪假期。"},{"en":"Surfing holidays need suitable waves, safe beaches, lessons, and equipment.","zh":"衝浪假期需要合適海浪、安全沙灘、課堂和裝備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a holiday built around learning or enjoying surfing.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞學習或享受衝浪而安排的假期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ask your advice","meaning":"問你的意見","examples":[{"en":"The woman wants to ask Jack’s advice about surfing.","zh":"這位女士想問 Jack 關於衝浪的意見。"},{"en":"To ask someone’s advice means to ask for their opinion or guidance before making a decision.","zh":"ask someone’s advice 的意思是在作決定前詢問某人的看法或指導。"},{"en":"A student may ask a teacher’s advice before choosing exam subjects.","zh":"學生可能在選擇考試科目前問老師的意見。"},{"en":"People ask advice when they think someone has more experience than they do.","zh":"當人們認為某人比自己更有經驗，就會向對方問意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when making polite requests for help.","zh":"這個短語適合用於禮貌地請求幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"such an expert","meaning":"這麼熟悉的專家","examples":[{"en":"The woman thinks Jack is such an expert on surfing.","zh":"這位女士認為 Jack 是這麼熟悉衝浪的專家。"},{"en":"Such an expert means someone is very knowledgeable or skilled in a particular subject.","zh":"such an expert 的意思是某人在特定題目上很有知識或技巧。"},{"en":"My uncle is such an expert on cameras that friends always ask him before buying one.","zh":"我叔叔這麼熟悉相機，朋友買相機前總會問他。"},{"en":"Calling someone an expert can show respect, but it may also make them feel modest or embarrassed.","zh":"稱某人為專家可以表示尊重，但也可能令對方謙虛或不好意思。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly praises someone’s knowledge or ability.","zh":"這個短語強烈稱讚某人的知識或能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"I don’t know about that","meaning":"那倒不敢說","examples":[{"en":"Jack says, “I don’t know about that,” when called an expert.","zh":"當被稱為專家時，Jack 說：「那倒不敢說。」"},{"en":"I don’t know about that is used to politely disagree, sound modest, or show doubt.","zh":"I don’t know about that 用來禮貌地不同意、表示謙虛或表達懷疑。"},{"en":"If someone says you are the best singer in class, you might reply, “I don’t know about that.”","zh":"如果有人說你是班上唱歌最好的人，你可能回答：「那倒不敢說。」"},{"en":"This phrase softens disagreement because it does not directly say “you are wrong”.","zh":"這個短語軟化不同意，因為它沒有直接說「你錯了」。"},{"en":"It is common in casual conversation when people avoid sounding too confident.","zh":"當人們避免顯得太自信時，這句在日常對話中很常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"do a bit of surfing","meaning":"衝過一些浪","examples":[{"en":"Jack has done a bit of surfing over the years.","zh":"Jack 多年來衝過一些浪。"},{"en":"To do a bit of surfing means to surf sometimes or have some experience of surfing.","zh":"do a bit of surfing 的意思是偶爾衝浪，或有一些衝浪經驗。"},{"en":"I did a bit of surfing on holiday, but I am still a beginner.","zh":"我在假期衝過一些浪，但我仍然是初學者。"},{"en":"Saying “a bit of” often makes the experience sound modest rather than expert-level.","zh":"說 a bit of 通常令經驗聽起來較謙虛，而不是專家程度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited but real experience.","zh":"這個短語描述有限但真實的經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over the years","meaning":"多年來","examples":[{"en":"Jack has done some surfing over the years.","zh":"Jack 多年來衝過一些浪。"},{"en":"Over the years means during many years or across a long period of time.","zh":"over the years 的意思是在多年期間或橫跨很長一段時間。"},{"en":"Over the years, the teacher has helped hundreds of students improve their English.","zh":"多年來，這位老師幫助數百名學生改善英文。"},{"en":"Skills often improve over the years because people gain experience little by little.","zh":"技能常會多年來逐漸提升，因為人們一點一點累積經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase shows gradual change or experience over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示隨時間逐漸改變或累積經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"thoroughly recommend","meaning":"極力推薦","examples":[{"en":"Jack would thoroughly recommend a surfing holiday.","zh":"Jack 會極力推薦衝浪假期。"},{"en":"To thoroughly recommend something means to recommend it very strongly because you think it is excellent.","zh":"thoroughly recommend something 的意思是因為你認為某事很好而非常強烈地推薦。"},{"en":"I would thoroughly recommend this restaurant because the food is fresh and the staff are kind.","zh":"我會極力推薦這間餐廳，因為食物新鮮，員工又友善。"},{"en":"People thoroughly recommend things when they have had a very good personal experience.","zh":"人們有非常好的親身經驗時，常會極力推薦某事。"},{"en":"This phrase gives stronger praise than simply saying “recommend”.","zh":"這個短語比單純說 recommend 讚賞更強。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the kind of holiday","meaning":"那種假期","examples":[{"en":"Surfing is the kind of holiday all the family can enjoy.","zh":"衝浪是那種全家都可以享受的假期。"},{"en":"The kind of holiday means the type of holiday or style of trip.","zh":"the kind of holiday 的意思是假期的類型或旅行風格。"},{"en":"A camping trip is the kind of holiday that suits people who enjoy nature and simple living.","zh":"露營旅行是那種適合喜歡自然和簡樸生活的人的假期。"},{"en":"Choosing the right kind of holiday matters because different family members may enjoy different activities.","zh":"選擇合適的假期類型很重要，因為不同家庭成員可能喜歡不同活動。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe what a holiday is like.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述假期是甚麼樣的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"enjoy together","meaning":"一起享受","examples":[{"en":"All the family can enjoy surfing together.","zh":"全家都可以一起享受衝浪。"},{"en":"To enjoy something together means to share a pleasant activity with other people.","zh":"enjoy something together 的意思是與他人共同享受一項愉快活動。"},{"en":"Families can enjoy cooking together on weekends.","zh":"家人可以在週末一起享受烹飪。"},{"en":"Shared activities help people feel closer because they create common memories.","zh":"共同活動能令人感到更親近，因為它們創造共同回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on both enjoyment and togetherness.","zh":"這個短語同時集中於享受和一起參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the thing about","meaning":"……的特點是","examples":[{"en":"The thing about surfing is that it suits all ages and abilities.","zh":"衝浪的特點是它適合各個年齡和不同能力的人。"},{"en":"The thing about something is used to introduce an important feature or point about it.","zh":"the thing about something 用來引出某事的重要特點或要點。"},{"en":"The thing about online learning is that students need self-discipline.","zh":"網上學習的特點是學生需要自律。"},{"en":"This phrase helps speakers explain what makes something special, useful, or difficult.","zh":"這個短語幫助說話者解釋某事有何特別、有用或困難。"},{"en":"It is common in informal explanations.","zh":"它常見於非正式解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"all ages and all abilities","meaning":"各個年齡及不同能力","examples":[{"en":"Surfing is great for all ages and all abilities.","zh":"衝浪很適合各個年齡及不同能力的人。"},{"en":"All ages and all abilities means people who are young or old, beginners or experienced, can take part.","zh":"all ages and all abilities 的意思是年幼或年長、初學或有經驗的人都可以參加。"},{"en":"A community sports day should include activities for all ages and all abilities.","zh":"社區運動日應包括適合各個年齡及不同能力人士的活動。"},{"en":"Activities suitable for all abilities make people feel welcome rather than embarrassed.","zh":"適合不同能力的活動能令人感到受歡迎，而不是尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses inclusion.","zh":"這個短語強調共融。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"youngest","meaning":"最小的孩子","examples":[{"en":"Jack’s youngest started surfing when he was only three.","zh":"Jack 最小的孩子三歲時就開始衝浪。"},{"en":"Someone’s youngest means their youngest child.","zh":"someone’s youngest 的意思是某人最年幼的孩子。"},{"en":"My youngest has just started primary school.","zh":"我最小的孩子剛開始讀小學。"},{"en":"Parents often use “my youngest” when comparing children’s ages or stages.","zh":"父母比較孩子年齡或階段時，常使用 my youngest。"},{"en":"This word is short for “youngest child” in family conversation.","zh":"這個詞在家庭對話中是 youngest child 的簡短說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"physically demanding","meaning":"對體力要求高","examples":[{"en":"Surfing is quite physically demanding.","zh":"衝浪對體力要求相當高。"},{"en":"Physically demanding means needing strength, energy, fitness, or body control.","zh":"physically demanding 的意思是需要力量、精力、體能或身體控制。"},{"en":"Moving heavy boxes all day is physically demanding work.","zh":"整天搬重箱是對體力要求高的工作。"},{"en":"A physically demanding activity can make people tired quickly if they are not fit.","zh":"如果人不夠健壯，對體力要求高的活動可以很快令人疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on effort required from the body.","zh":"這個短語集中於身體需要付出的努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pretty fit","meaning":"身體相當健壯","examples":[{"en":"The woman has heard that surfers need to be pretty fit.","zh":"這位女士聽說衝浪者需要身體相當健壯。"},{"en":"Pretty fit means fairly healthy, strong, and able to do physical activity.","zh":"pretty fit 的意思是相當健康、強壯，並能進行體力活動。"},{"en":"Someone who walks, swims, or cycles regularly is probably pretty fit.","zh":"經常步行、游泳或踩單車的人大概身體相當健壯。"},{"en":"Being pretty fit helps with sports because the body gets tired less quickly.","zh":"身體相當健壯有助運動，因為身體不會那麼快疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and less extreme than “athletic”.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，沒有 athletic 那麼極端。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"learn more quickly","meaning":"學得更快","examples":[{"en":"Fit people will learn surfing more quickly.","zh":"身體健壯的人會更快學會衝浪。"},{"en":"To learn more quickly means to understand or improve faster than before or faster than others.","zh":"learn more quickly 的意思是比以前或比其他人更快理解或進步。"},{"en":"Students often learn more quickly when lessons include clear examples and practice.","zh":"當課堂包括清楚例子和練習，學生常會學得更快。"},{"en":"Good fitness may help beginners learn surfing faster because they can practise for longer.","zh":"良好體能可能幫助初學者更快學會衝浪，因為他們能練習更久。"},{"en":"This phrase compares speed of learning.","zh":"這個短語比較學習速度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tire as easily","meaning":"那麼容易疲倦","examples":[{"en":"Fit people will not tire as easily when surfing.","zh":"身體健壯的人衝浪時不會那麼容易疲倦。"},{"en":"To not tire as easily means not become tired so quickly.","zh":"not tire as easily 的意思是不會那麼快變得疲倦。"},{"en":"A runner who trains regularly will not tire as easily during a long race.","zh":"經常訓練的跑手在長跑比賽中不會那麼容易疲倦。"},{"en":"People with better stamina can enjoy activities longer because they do not tire quickly.","zh":"耐力較好的人可以享受活動更久，因為他們不會那麼快累。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how fast people become tired.","zh":"這個短語比較人們變疲倦的速度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"should be OK for us","meaning":"對我們來說應該沒問題","examples":[{"en":"The woman thinks the physical demands should be OK for her family.","zh":"這位女士認為體力要求對她家人來說應該沒問題。"},{"en":"Should be OK for us means it will probably be suitable, manageable, or not too difficult for us.","zh":"should be OK for us 的意思是對我們來說大概合適、能應付或不太困難。"},{"en":"A short walk should be OK for us, but a mountain hike may be too much.","zh":"短途步行對我們來說應該沒問題，但行山可能太吃力。"},{"en":"People say this when they feel reasonably confident but not completely certain.","zh":"人們在相當有信心但未完全肯定時會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a mild positive judgement.","zh":"這個短語給出溫和的正面判斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a few times","meaning":"幾次","examples":[{"en":"Jack has been surfing in Ireland a few times.","zh":"Jack 去過愛爾蘭衝浪幾次。"},{"en":"A few times means several times, but not many.","zh":"a few times 的意思是數次，但不是很多次。"},{"en":"I have visited that café a few times, so I know the menu quite well.","zh":"我去過那間咖啡店幾次，所以相當熟悉餐牌。"},{"en":"Doing something a few times gives some experience, but not necessarily expert knowledge.","zh":"做某事幾次能帶來一些經驗，但不一定是專家知識。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests limited repeated experience.","zh":"這個短語表示有限但重複的經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"great surfing","meaning":"很好的衝浪地點","examples":[{"en":"There is some great surfing in Ireland.","zh":"愛爾蘭有一些很好的衝浪地點。"},{"en":"Great surfing means good conditions or places for surfing, especially with suitable waves.","zh":"great surfing 指適合衝浪的良好條件或地方，尤其是有合適海浪。"},{"en":"A beach with steady waves and safe water can offer great surfing for beginners.","zh":"有穩定海浪和安全水域的海灘，可以為初學者提供很好的衝浪地點。"},{"en":"Great surfing attracts visitors because people want both excitement and good conditions.","zh":"很好的衝浪地點會吸引遊客，因為人們想要刺激和良好條件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the quality of a surfing location or experience.","zh":"這個短語描述衝浪地點或體驗的質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"do not always realise","meaning":"不一定知道","examples":[{"en":"People do not always realise that Ireland has good surfing.","zh":"人們不一定知道愛爾蘭有好的衝浪地點。"},{"en":"Do not always realise means often fail to notice, understand, or know something.","zh":"do not always realise 的意思是常常沒有注意、理解或知道某事。"},{"en":"Students do not always realise how much sleep affects their memory.","zh":"學生不一定知道睡眠對記憶影響有多大。"},{"en":"People may not realise a place is interesting until someone explains its history.","zh":"人們可能直到有人解釋歷史，才知道一個地方很有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something is true but not widely understood.","zh":"這個短語表示某事是真的，但未被廣泛理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"locations","meaning":"地點","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks which surfing locations Jack would recommend.","zh":"這位女士問 Jack 會推薦哪些衝浪地點。"},{"en":"Locations are places where something happens or can be found.","zh":"locations 是某事發生或可以找到某物的地方。"},{"en":"A travel website lists hotel locations near beaches and train stations.","zh":"旅遊網站列出靠近海灘和火車站的酒店地點。"},{"en":"Choosing the right location can affect cost, safety, and convenience.","zh":"選擇正確地點可以影響費用、安全和便利。"},{"en":"This word is useful when comparing places.","zh":"這個詞適合用於比較地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"there seem to be","meaning":"似乎有","examples":[{"en":"There seem to be quite a few good surfing locations in Ireland.","zh":"愛爾蘭似乎有相當多好的衝浪地點。"},{"en":"There seem to be means it appears that something exists, though the speaker may not be completely certain.","zh":"there seem to be 的意思是看起來有某些東西存在，但說話者未必完全肯定。"},{"en":"There seem to be several empty seats near the front of the classroom.","zh":"課室前排似乎有幾個空位。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they are judging from available information.","zh":"人們根據現有資訊作判斷時會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It sounds less certain than “there are”.","zh":"它聽起來沒有 there are 那麼肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"quite a few","meaning":"相當多","examples":[{"en":"There are quite a few surfing locations in Ireland.","zh":"愛爾蘭有相當多衝浪地點。"},{"en":"Quite a few means a fairly large number, more than just a few.","zh":"quite a few 的意思是數量相當多，比少數幾個多。"},{"en":"Quite a few students stayed after class to ask questions.","zh":"相當多學生課後留下來問問題。"},{"en":"If there are quite a few choices, people may need advice before deciding.","zh":"如果有相當多選擇，人們作決定前可能需要意見。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a noticeable number.","zh":"這個短語表示數量明顯不少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"there are loads","meaning":"有很多","examples":[{"en":"Jack says there are loads of places to surf in Ireland.","zh":"Jack 說愛爾蘭有很多地方可以衝浪。"},{"en":"There are loads means there are many or a lot of something.","zh":"there are loads 的意思是有很多某物。"},{"en":"There are loads of restaurants near the station, so finding dinner is easy.","zh":"車站附近有很多餐廳，所以找晚餐很容易。"},{"en":"When there are loads of options, recommendations help people choose faster.","zh":"當有很多選項，推薦可以幫人更快選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and common in spoken English.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，常見於口語英文。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"County Donegal","meaning":"多尼戈爾郡","examples":[{"en":"Jack went surfing in County Donegal last year.","zh":"Jack 去年在多尼戈爾郡衝浪。"},{"en":"County Donegal is a county in the northwest of Ireland, known for wild coastal scenery.","zh":"County Donegal 是愛爾蘭西北部的一個郡，以壯麗海岸景色聞名。"},{"en":"A family might visit County Donegal for beaches, cliffs, and outdoor activities.","zh":"家庭可能到多尼戈爾郡遊覽海灘、懸崖和戶外活動。"},{"en":"Coastal counties can attract surfers when they have strong waves and open beaches.","zh":"當沿海郡有強浪和開闊海灘，就能吸引衝浪者。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific Irish location.","zh":"這個短語指愛爾蘭的一個特定地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"several great places to surf","meaning":"幾個很好的衝浪地點","examples":[{"en":"There are several great places to surf in County Donegal.","zh":"多尼戈爾郡有幾個很好的衝浪地點。"},{"en":"Several great places to surf means more than two good locations where people can surf.","zh":"several great places to surf 的意思是有多於兩個適合衝浪的好地方。"},{"en":"A coastline with several great places to surf gives families more choice if one beach is too busy.","zh":"有幾個很好的衝浪地點的海岸線，讓家庭在一個海灘太擠時有更多選擇。"},{"en":"Having several good places nearby helps surfers choose according to weather and skill level.","zh":"附近有幾個好地方，有助衝浪者按天氣和能力選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes variety within one area.","zh":"這個短語描述一個地區內的多種選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"County Clare","meaning":"克萊爾郡","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks about surfing in County Clare.","zh":"這位女士問關於在克萊爾郡衝浪的事。"},{"en":"County Clare is a county on the west coast of Ireland, known for coastal scenery and surfing spots.","zh":"County Clare 是愛爾蘭西岸的一個郡，以海岸景色和衝浪地點聞名。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit County Clare to see cliffs, beaches, music towns, and villages.","zh":"遊客可能到克萊爾郡觀看懸崖、海灘、音樂小鎮和村莊。"},{"en":"A place like County Clare can suit a family holiday because it combines nature and activities.","zh":"像克萊爾郡這樣的地方可以適合家庭假期，因為它結合自然和活動。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific Irish county.","zh":"這個短語指愛爾蘭的一個特定郡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be good for surfing","meaning":"適合衝浪","examples":[{"en":"County Clare is really good for surfing.","zh":"克萊爾郡真的很適合衝浪。"},{"en":"To be good for surfing means to have suitable waves, beaches, wind, or facilities for surfing.","zh":"be good for surfing 的意思是有適合衝浪的海浪、沙灘、風或設施。"},{"en":"A beach with gentle waves can be good for beginner surfers.","zh":"有溫和海浪的海灘可以適合初學衝浪者。"},{"en":"A location is better for surfing when it also has lessons, equipment hire, and safe access.","zh":"如果一個地點也有課堂、裝備租借和安全通道，它會更適合衝浪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes suitability for the sport.","zh":"這個短語描述對該運動的適合程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"most people go to","meaning":"大多數人去……","examples":[{"en":"Most people go to Lahinch for surfing.","zh":"大多數人去拉欣奇衝浪。"},{"en":"Most people go to a place means it is the common or popular choice.","zh":"most people go to 某地的意思是該地方是常見或受歡迎的選擇。"},{"en":"Most students go to the library after school when exams are near.","zh":"考試臨近時，大多數學生放學後去圖書館。"},{"en":"A place becomes popular when many people find it convenient, safe, or enjoyable.","zh":"當許多人覺得一個地方方便、安全或愉快，它就會變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase describes common behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述普遍行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Lahinch","meaning":"拉欣奇","examples":[{"en":"Jack’s children love surfing in Lahinch.","zh":"Jack 的孩子很喜歡在拉欣奇衝浪。"},{"en":"Lahinch is a seaside town in County Clare in Ireland, known as a surfing destination.","zh":"Lahinch 是愛爾蘭克萊爾郡的一個海邊小鎮，以衝浪目的地聞名。"},{"en":"Families may choose Lahinch because it offers surfing, accommodation, and a lively town atmosphere.","zh":"家庭可能選擇拉欣奇，因為它提供衝浪、住宿和熱鬧小鎮氣氛。"},{"en":"A named surfing town helps travellers search for lessons, equipment hire, and places to stay.","zh":"一個有名稱的衝浪小鎮，方便旅客搜尋課堂、裝備租借和住宿。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific place.","zh":"這個短語指一個特定地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"waves are not too challenging","meaning":"海浪不算太難應付","examples":[{"en":"The waves in Lahinch are not too challenging.","zh":"拉欣奇的海浪不算太難應付。"},{"en":"If waves are not too challenging, they are not too difficult or dangerous for learners.","zh":"如果 waves are not too challenging，意思是海浪對學習者來說不太困難或危險。"},{"en":"Beginner surfers should choose beaches where the waves are not too challenging.","zh":"初學衝浪者應選擇海浪不算太難應付的海灘。"},{"en":"Easier waves help learners build confidence before trying rougher water.","zh":"較容易的海浪能幫助學習者在嘗試更洶湧水域前建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a manageable level of difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述可應付的難度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"very lively","meaning":"非常熱鬧","examples":[{"en":"The town of Lahinch is very lively.","zh":"拉欣奇這個小鎮非常熱鬧。"},{"en":"Very lively means full of energy, activity, people, and atmosphere.","zh":"very lively 的意思是充滿活力、活動、人群和氣氛。"},{"en":"A market is very lively when stalls, music, and shoppers fill the streets.","zh":"當攤檔、音樂和購物者充滿街道，市場就非常熱鬧。"},{"en":"Lively towns can make holidays more enjoyable because there are things to do after the main activity.","zh":"熱鬧的小鎮可以令假期更愉快，因為主要活動後仍有事情可做。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place that does not feel quiet or dull.","zh":"這個短語描述不安靜、不沉悶的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"good hotels","meaning":"好的酒店","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether there are good hotels in Lahinch.","zh":"這位女士問拉欣奇是否有好的酒店。"},{"en":"Good hotels are places to stay that are clean, comfortable, safe, and well run.","zh":"good hotels 是乾淨、舒適、安全並管理良好的住宿地方。"},{"en":"Families often look for good hotels near beaches so children do not need long journeys.","zh":"家庭常尋找靠近海灘的好酒店，讓孩子不用長途往返。"},{"en":"Good hotels can make a holiday easier because guests can rest properly after activities.","zh":"好的酒店可以令假期更輕鬆，因為客人在活動後能好好休息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accommodation quality.","zh":"這個短語描述住宿質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"basic hostels","meaning":"基本旅舍","examples":[{"en":"There are a few basic hostels in Lahinch.","zh":"拉欣奇有幾間基本旅舍。"},{"en":"Basic hostels are simple, low-cost places to stay, often with shared rooms or facilities.","zh":"basic hostels 是簡單、低成本的住宿地方，通常有共用房間或設施。"},{"en":"Young travellers may choose basic hostels to save money.","zh":"年輕旅客可能選擇基本旅舍來節省金錢。"},{"en":"Basic hostels may not be luxurious, but they can be practical for active holidays.","zh":"基本旅舍未必豪華，但對活動型假期來說可以很實用。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests simple accommodation rather than comfort-focused hotels.","zh":"這個短語表示簡單住宿，而不是重視舒適的酒店。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"campsites","meaning":"露營地點","examples":[{"en":"There are also campsites near the surfing area.","zh":"衝浪區附近也有露營地點。"},{"en":"Campsites are places where people can stay in tents, campervans, or caravans.","zh":"campsites 是讓人住在帳篷、露營車或拖車屋的地方。"},{"en":"Families may choose campsites if they enjoy outdoor living and want a cheaper holiday.","zh":"如果家庭喜歡戶外生活並想要較便宜的假期，可能選擇露營地點。"},{"en":"Campsites near beaches are useful because surfers can reach the water quickly.","zh":"靠近海灘的露營地點很有用，因為衝浪者可以很快到達水邊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes outdoor accommodation.","zh":"這個短語描述戶外住宿。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"need lessons","meaning":"需要上課","examples":[{"en":"Lahinch is good if visitors need surfing lessons.","zh":"如果遊客需要上衝浪課，拉欣奇是不錯的地方。"},{"en":"To need lessons means to require teaching or training before doing an activity well.","zh":"need lessons 的意思是需要教學或訓練，才能把活動做好。"},{"en":"A beginner may need swimming lessons before joining water sports.","zh":"初學者參加水上運動前，可能需要上游泳課。"},{"en":"Lessons help people learn safely because an instructor can correct mistakes early.","zh":"課堂幫助人們安全學習，因為教練可以及早糾正錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a need for guided learning.","zh":"這個短語描述需要有人指導學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"surf schools","meaning":"衝浪學校","examples":[{"en":"The surf schools in Lahinch are excellent.","zh":"拉欣奇的衝浪學校非常出色。"},{"en":"Surf schools are places or organisations that teach people how to surf.","zh":"surf schools 是教人如何衝浪的地方或機構。"},{"en":"A surf school may provide instructors, boards, wetsuits, and safety advice.","zh":"衝浪學校可能提供教練、衝浪板、潛水衣和安全建議。"},{"en":"Good surf schools help beginners learn faster and avoid dangerous mistakes.","zh":"好的衝浪學校幫助初學者更快學習並避免危險錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes training services for surfing.","zh":"這個短語描述衝浪訓練服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lots to see","meaning":"有很多景點","examples":[{"en":"There is lots to see in the area.","zh":"那一帶有很多景點。"},{"en":"Lots to see means many interesting places, sights, or attractions are available.","zh":"lots to see 的意思是有許多有趣地方、景色或景點可看。"},{"en":"A city with museums, parks, markets, and old streets has lots to see.","zh":"有博物館、公園、市集和老街的城市有很多景點。"},{"en":"Having lots to see makes a holiday better when the weather is not suitable for outdoor sports.","zh":"當天氣不適合戶外運動，有很多景點會令假期更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place with many attractions.","zh":"這個短語描述一個地方有許多吸引點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the area","meaning":"在那一帶","examples":[{"en":"There are well-known cliffs in the area.","zh":"那一帶有一些著名懸崖。"},{"en":"In the area means nearby or within the surrounding place being discussed.","zh":"in the area 的意思是在附近或正在討論地方的周邊範圍內。"},{"en":"There are several cafés in the area near the school.","zh":"學校附近那一帶有幾間咖啡店。"},{"en":"Knowing what is in the area helps travellers plan food, transport, and activities.","zh":"知道那一帶有甚麼，有助旅客規劃食物、交通和活動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the local surroundings.","zh":"這個短語指本地周邊地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"well-known cliffs","meaning":"著名懸崖","examples":[{"en":"The area has some well-known cliffs.","zh":"那一帶有一些著名懸崖。"},{"en":"Well-known cliffs are famous steep rock faces, often visited for their views.","zh":"well-known cliffs 是有名的陡峭岩壁，常因景色而吸引遊客。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit well-known cliffs to take photos of the sea below.","zh":"遊客可能參觀著名懸崖，拍攝下方海景。"},{"en":"Famous cliffs can attract many visitors, so safety fences and paths are important.","zh":"著名懸崖可以吸引許多遊客，所以安全圍欄和步道很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase combines natural scenery with public recognition.","zh":"這個短語結合自然景色和公眾知名度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"forget the name of","meaning":"忘記……的名字","examples":[{"en":"Jack has forgotten the name of the cliffs.","zh":"Jack 忘記了那些懸崖的名字。"},{"en":"To forget the name of something means to be unable to remember what it is called.","zh":"forget the name of something 的意思是想不起某物叫甚麼。"},{"en":"I forgot the name of the restaurant, but I remember it was near the station.","zh":"我忘記了那間餐廳的名字，但我記得它在車站附近。"},{"en":"People often forget names even when they remember the place or experience clearly.","zh":"人們即使清楚記得地方或經驗，也常會忘記名字。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common memory problem.","zh":"這個短語描述常見的記憶問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"look them up","meaning":"查找它們","examples":[{"en":"The woman says she can look the cliffs up.","zh":"這位女士說她可以查找那些懸崖。"},{"en":"To look something up means to search for information about it in a book, map, or online.","zh":"look something up 的意思是在書本、地圖或網上搜尋某事的資料。"},{"en":"If you forget a word, you can look it up in a dictionary.","zh":"如果你忘記一個字，可以在字典中查找它。"},{"en":"Looking up a place before travelling helps you check directions and opening times.","zh":"旅行前查找一個地方，有助你查看路線和開放時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is practical and common in study, travel, and work.","zh":"這個短語很實用，常見於學習、旅行和工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"less well-known for","meaning":"較不以……聞名","examples":[{"en":"County Mayo is less well-known for surfing.","zh":"梅奧郡較不以衝浪聞名。"},{"en":"Less well-known for something means not as famous for that activity or feature as other places are.","zh":"less well-known for something 的意思是不如其他地方那樣以某活動或特色聞名。"},{"en":"This town is less well-known for food than for its historic buildings.","zh":"這個城鎮較不以食物聞名，而是以歷史建築聞名。"},{"en":"A less famous place can still be excellent if it has good conditions and fewer crowds.","zh":"較不出名的地方如果有良好條件和較少人群，仍可以很出色。"},{"en":"This phrase compares public reputation.","zh":"這個短語比較公眾名聲。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have a really good time","meaning":"玩得很開心","examples":[{"en":"Jack’s family had a really good time in County Mayo.","zh":"Jack 一家人在梅奧郡玩得很開心。"},{"en":"To have a really good time means to enjoy an experience very much.","zh":"have a really good time 的意思是非常享受一段經歷。"},{"en":"The children had a really good time at the birthday party.","zh":"孩子們在生日派對上玩得很開心。"},{"en":"People remember holidays more warmly when they have a good time together.","zh":"當人們一起玩得開心，他們會更溫暖地記住假期。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong enjoyment.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈享受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a few years ago","meaning":"幾年前","examples":[{"en":"Jack went to County Mayo a few years ago.","zh":"Jack 幾年前去過梅奧郡。"},{"en":"A few years ago means several years before now, but not a very long time ago.","zh":"a few years ago 的意思是現在之前數年，但不是很久以前。"},{"en":"I visited that beach a few years ago, so the hotels may have changed.","zh":"我幾年前去過那個海灘，所以酒店可能已經改變。"},{"en":"Information from a few years ago may still be useful, but it should sometimes be checked.","zh":"幾年前的資料可能仍有用，但有時應該再查證。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a general past time.","zh":"這個短語給出大概的過去時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Carrowniskey Beach","meaning":"Carrowniskey 海灘","examples":[{"en":"There is a good surf school at Carrowniskey Beach.","zh":"Carrowniskey 海灘有一間好的衝浪學校。"},{"en":"Carrowniskey Beach is a specific beach mentioned as a surfing location in County Mayo.","zh":"Carrowniskey Beach 是梅奧郡一個被提及為衝浪地點的特定海灘。"},{"en":"A family may choose Carrowniskey Beach if they want lessons and a quieter surfing place.","zh":"如果家庭想上課並找較安靜的衝浪地點，可能選擇 Carrowniskey 海灘。"},{"en":"Named beaches help travellers search for maps, schools, accommodation, and safety information.","zh":"有名稱的海灘方便旅客搜尋地圖、學校、住宿和安全資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase names a particular beach.","zh":"這個短語指一個特定海灘。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"how do you spell that","meaning":"那怎樣拼寫","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks Jack how to spell Carrowniskey.","zh":"這位女士問 Jack Carrowniskey 怎樣拼寫。"},{"en":"How do you spell that? means what letters are used to write that word or name.","zh":"How do you spell that? 的意思是該詞或名字用哪些字母寫出來。"},{"en":"If a hotel name is unfamiliar, you might ask, “How do you spell that?”","zh":"如果酒店名字不熟悉，你可能問：「那怎樣拼寫？」"},{"en":"Asking for spelling prevents mistakes when writing names, addresses, or bookings.","zh":"詢問拼寫可以避免寫名字、地址或預訂資料時出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in conversations about unfamiliar words.","zh":"這個短語適合用於談到陌生詞語時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"put the kids into","meaning":"讓孩子參加","examples":[{"en":"Jack put the kids into the surf camp.","zh":"Jack 讓孩子參加衝浪營。"},{"en":"To put the kids into an activity means to enrol or place children in that activity.","zh":"put the kids into an activity 的意思是為孩子報名或安排他們參加某活動。"},{"en":"Parents may put the kids into swimming lessons during the summer.","zh":"父母可能在夏天讓孩子參加游泳課。"},{"en":"Putting children into a structured camp can keep them active and supervised.","zh":"讓孩子參加有組織的營隊，可以令他們保持活躍並有人照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and common in family planning.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，常見於家庭計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"surf camp","meaning":"衝浪營","examples":[{"en":"The surf school runs a surf camp during the summer.","zh":"這間衝浪學校在夏季舉辦衝浪營。"},{"en":"A surf camp is a programme where people, often children or teenagers, learn and practise surfing over several days.","zh":"surf camp 是讓人，通常是兒童或青少年，在幾天內學習和練習衝浪的課程。"},{"en":"A surf camp may include lessons, safety training, games, and supervised practice.","zh":"衝浪營可能包括課堂、安全訓練、遊戲和有人監督的練習。"},{"en":"Camps help beginners improve because they practise regularly in a short period.","zh":"營隊幫助初學者進步，因為他們在短時間內規律練習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an organised surfing programme.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的衝浪課程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"run during the summer","meaning":"在夏季舉辦","examples":[{"en":"The surf camp runs during the summer.","zh":"衝浪營在夏季舉辦。"},{"en":"If a programme runs during the summer, it takes place in the summer months.","zh":"如果一個課程 runs during the summer，意思是它在夏季月份進行。"},{"en":"The school library runs during the summer for students who want to read.","zh":"學校圖書館在夏季開放，供想閱讀的學生使用。"},{"en":"Summer programmes are popular because children are not in regular school.","zh":"暑期課程很受歡迎，因為孩子不用上正規學校。"},{"en":"This phrase describes when an activity operates.","zh":"這個短語描述活動何時運作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"10-to-16-year-olds","meaning":"10至16歲人士","examples":[{"en":"The surf camp is for 10-to-16-year-olds.","zh":"這個衝浪營是為10至16歲人士而設。"},{"en":"10-to-16-year-olds are children and teenagers aged from ten to sixteen.","zh":"10-to-16-year-olds 是十至十六歲的兒童和青少年。"},{"en":"A sports camp for 10-to-16-year-olds should offer safe activities at different skill levels.","zh":"為10至16歲人士而設的運動營，應提供不同技能程度的安全活動。"},{"en":"Age groups help organisers design lessons that are not too childish or too difficult.","zh":"年齡組別幫助組織者設計不太幼稚也不太困難的課堂。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the target age range.","zh":"這個短語指出目標年齡範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"every day for a week","meaning":"每天，為期一星期","examples":[{"en":"The surf camp lasted three hours every day for a week.","zh":"衝浪營每天三小時，為期一星期。"},{"en":"Every day for a week means each day across seven days.","zh":"every day for a week 的意思是在七天中每天都做。"},{"en":"Students practised piano every day for a week before the concert.","zh":"音樂會前，學生每天練琴，為期一星期。"},{"en":"Doing something every day for a week can build routine and improve skill quickly.","zh":"每天做某事，為期一星期，可以建立規律並快速提升技能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows both frequency and duration.","zh":"這個短語同時顯示頻率和持續時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tired out","meaning":"累壞了","examples":[{"en":"The children were tired out after the surf camp.","zh":"孩子們參加衝浪營後累壞了。"},{"en":"Tired out means extremely tired after physical or mental effort.","zh":"tired out 的意思是在體力或精神努力後極度疲倦。"},{"en":"The students were tired out after a whole day of hiking.","zh":"學生行山一整天後累壞了。"},{"en":"Physically demanding activities can tire people out, especially if they last several days.","zh":"對體力要求高的活動可以令人累壞，尤其是持續幾天時。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and stronger than just “tired”.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，比 tired 更強。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"I can imagine","meaning":"我可以想像","examples":[{"en":"The woman says, “I can imagine,” when Jack describes the tired children.","zh":"當 Jack 描述孩子們很累時，這位女士說：「我可以想像。」"},{"en":"I can imagine means I understand how that situation probably felt, even though I did not experience it myself.","zh":"I can imagine 的意思是即使我沒有親身經歷，也能理解那情況大概是怎樣。"},{"en":"If someone says the exam was exhausting, you might reply, “I can imagine.”","zh":"如果有人說考試令人筋疲力盡，你可能回答：「我可以想像。」"},{"en":"This phrase shows sympathy, understanding, or agreement.","zh":"這個短語表示同情、理解或同意。"},{"en":"It is common in friendly conversation.","zh":"它常見於友善對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"while the kids were surfing","meaning":"當孩子們在衝浪時","examples":[{"en":"The adults rented kayaks while the kids were surfing.","zh":"當孩子們在衝浪時，成年人租了獨木舟。"},{"en":"While the kids were surfing means during the time when the children were surfing.","zh":"while the kids were surfing 的意思是在孩子們衝浪的那段時間。"},{"en":"Parents may read on the beach while the kids are surfing with instructors.","zh":"當孩子們跟教練衝浪時，父母可能在沙灘上閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase shows two activities happening at the same time.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩項活動同時發生。"},{"en":"It helps explain how adults used the time while children were occupied.","zh":"它幫助解釋成年人如何利用孩子忙着活動的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rent some kayaks","meaning":"租幾隻獨木舟","examples":[{"en":"Jack and his family rented some kayaks near the bay.","zh":"Jack 和家人在海灣附近租了幾隻獨木舟。"},{"en":"To rent some kayaks means to pay to use small boats for a limited time.","zh":"rent some kayaks 的意思是付費在有限時間內使用幾隻小船。"},{"en":"Tourists may rent kayaks for an hour to explore a calm lake.","zh":"遊客可能租幾隻獨木舟一小時，探索平靜湖泊。"},{"en":"Renting equipment is useful when people do not own it or cannot bring it on holiday.","zh":"當人們沒有裝備或不能把它帶去旅行，租用裝備很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes temporary paid use.","zh":"這個短語描述臨時付費使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have a look around","meaning":"四處看看","examples":[{"en":"They rented kayaks to have a look around the bay.","zh":"他們租獨木舟在海灣四處看看。"},{"en":"To have a look around means to explore or examine a place casually.","zh":"have a look around 的意思是輕鬆地探索或看看一個地方。"},{"en":"After arriving at the hotel, we had a look around the nearby streets.","zh":"到達酒店後，我們在附近街道四處看看。"},{"en":"Having a look around helps travellers decide where to eat, shop, or visit next.","zh":"四處看看幫助旅客決定之後去哪裡吃飯、購物或參觀。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and relaxed.","zh":"這個短語是非正式而輕鬆的說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the bay","meaning":"海灣","examples":[{"en":"They looked around the nearby bay by kayak.","zh":"他們乘獨木舟在附近海灣四處看看。"},{"en":"A bay is a part of the sea that curves into the land and is partly surrounded by coastline.","zh":"bay 是海的一部分，向陸地彎入，並部分被海岸包圍。"},{"en":"Boats often stop in a bay because the water may be calmer than the open sea.","zh":"船隻常停在海灣，因為水面可能比外海平靜。"},{"en":"Bays can be good places for kayaking, swimming, and watching wildlife.","zh":"海灣可以是划獨木舟、游泳和觀察野生動物的好地方。"},{"en":"This word describes a coastal water area.","zh":"這個詞描述沿岸水域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"nearby","meaning":"在附近","examples":[{"en":"The bay is nearby.","zh":"海灣就在附近。"},{"en":"Nearby means close to the place being discussed.","zh":"nearby 的意思是靠近正在討論的地方。"},{"en":"There is a supermarket nearby, so we can buy lunch before the trip.","zh":"附近有一間超級市場，所以我們可以在旅程前買午餐。"},{"en":"Nearby facilities make travel easier because people do not need to go far.","zh":"附近設施令旅行更方便，因為人們不用走很遠。"},{"en":"This word describes short distance.","zh":"這個詞描述短距離。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"I’d love to","meaning":"我很想","examples":[{"en":"The woman says she would love to go kayaking.","zh":"這位女士說她很想去划獨木舟。"},{"en":"I’d love to means I would really like to do something.","zh":"I’d love to 的意思是我真的很想做某事。"},{"en":"I’d love to visit Ireland if I have enough time next year.","zh":"如果明年有足夠時間，我很想去愛爾蘭。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong interest or enthusiasm.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈興趣或熱情。"},{"en":"It sounds warmer than simply saying “I want to”.","zh":"它比單純說 I want to 聽起來更溫暖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the only time","meaning":"唯一一次","examples":[{"en":"The only time the woman went to Ireland, it rained almost every day.","zh":"這位女士唯一一次去愛爾蘭時，幾乎每天都下雨。"},{"en":"The only time means the single occasion when something happened.","zh":"the only time 的意思是某事發生的唯一一次。"},{"en":"The only time I tried skiing, I fell over within five minutes.","zh":"我唯一一次嘗試滑雪時，五分鐘內就跌倒了。"},{"en":"One bad experience can shape someone’s opinion if it was the only time they tried something.","zh":"如果某次不好經驗是唯一一次嘗試，它可能塑造一個人的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that there was just one experience.","zh":"這個短語強調只有一次經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"practically every day","meaning":"幾乎每天","examples":[{"en":"It rained practically every day when the woman visited Ireland.","zh":"這位女士去愛爾蘭時幾乎每天都下雨。"},{"en":"Practically every day means almost every day.","zh":"practically every day 的意思是差不多每天。"},{"en":"During exam season, she studied practically every day.","zh":"考試季期間，她幾乎每天都溫習。"},{"en":"If it rains practically every day on holiday, outdoor plans may need to change.","zh":"如果假期幾乎每天下雨，戶外計劃可能需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises very high frequency.","zh":"這個短語強調非常高的頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"that can be a problem","meaning":"那可能是個問題","examples":[{"en":"Jack admits that rain can be a problem in Ireland.","zh":"Jack 承認在愛爾蘭下雨可能是個問題。"},{"en":"That can be a problem means that situation may cause difficulty or inconvenience.","zh":"that can be a problem 的意思是那種情況可能造成困難或不便。"},{"en":"If the train station is far from the hotel, that can be a problem for families with luggage.","zh":"如果火車站離酒店很遠，對帶行李的家庭來說那可能是個問題。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to acknowledge a real disadvantage without making it sound impossible.","zh":"人們使用這個短語來承認真正缺點，但不會說成完全不可行。"},{"en":"It is a balanced way to discuss a concern.","zh":"這是討論憂慮時較平衡的說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"surf in the rain","meaning":"在雨中衝浪","examples":[{"en":"People can surf in the rain.","zh":"人們可以在雨中衝浪。"},{"en":"To surf in the rain means to go surfing while it is raining.","zh":"surf in the rain 的意思是在下雨時去衝浪。"},{"en":"Some surfers do not mind surfing in the rain because they are already wet.","zh":"有些衝浪者不介意在雨中衝浪，因為他們本來已經濕了。"},{"en":"Surfing in the rain may be safe in light rain, but storms and lightning are dangerous.","zh":"小雨中衝浪可能安全，但風暴和閃電很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doing the sport despite wet weather.","zh":"這個短語描述即使天氣潮濕也進行這項運動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have the same appeal","meaning":"有同樣吸引力","examples":[{"en":"Surfing in the rain does not have the same appeal.","zh":"在雨中衝浪沒有同樣吸引力。"},{"en":"To have the same appeal means to be equally attractive or enjoyable.","zh":"have the same appeal 的意思是有同等吸引力或享受程度。"},{"en":"A picnic indoors does not have the same appeal as one in a sunny park.","zh":"室內野餐沒有在陽光明媚公園野餐那麼有吸引力。"},{"en":"Bad weather can reduce an activity’s appeal because the experience feels less comfortable.","zh":"壞天氣可以降低活動吸引力，因為體驗感覺較不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how attractive two situations feel.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種情況的吸引力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"somehow","meaning":"不知怎的","examples":[{"en":"Somehow, surfing in the rain does not sound as appealing.","zh":"不知怎的，在雨中衝浪聽起來沒有那麼吸引。"},{"en":"Somehow means for a reason that is not completely clear or easy to explain.","zh":"somehow 的意思是出於不完全清楚或不容易解釋的原因。"},{"en":"Somehow, the small café feels warmer than the expensive restaurant.","zh":"不知怎的，這間小咖啡店比昂貴餐廳感覺更溫暖。"},{"en":"People use somehow when they sense something but cannot fully explain why.","zh":"當人們感覺到某事但不能完全解釋原因時，會使用 somehow。"},{"en":"This word adds a feeling of uncertainty or instinct.","zh":"這個詞加入不確定或憑感覺的意味。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the last couple of years","meaning":"過去兩年","examples":[{"en":"The weather has been fine for Jack in the last couple of years.","zh":"過去兩年，Jack 遇到的天氣都不錯。"},{"en":"The last couple of years means the most recent two or few years.","zh":"the last couple of years 的意思是最近兩年或幾年。"},{"en":"The school has improved its library in the last couple of years.","zh":"學校在過去兩年改善了圖書館。"},{"en":"Recent experience may feel reliable, but it does not guarantee the future.","zh":"近期經驗可能感覺可靠，但不保證未來也一樣。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a recent time frame.","zh":"這個短語給出近期時間範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tend to rain more","meaning":"通常較多雨","examples":[{"en":"It tends to rain more in August than in spring or autumn.","zh":"八月通常比春季或秋季較多雨。"},{"en":"To tend to rain more means rain usually happens more often or in larger amounts.","zh":"tend to rain more 的意思是降雨通常更頻密或雨量更多。"},{"en":"It tends to rain more in the afternoon during the wet season.","zh":"在雨季，下午通常較多雨。"},{"en":"Knowing when it rains more helps travellers choose better dates.","zh":"知道何時較多雨，有助旅客選擇更好日期。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a general weather pattern, not a fixed rule.","zh":"這個短語描述一般天氣模式，而不是固定規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the spring or autumn","meaning":"在春季或秋季","examples":[{"en":"It rains less in the spring or autumn than in August.","zh":"在春季或秋季，雨量比八月少。"},{"en":"In the spring or autumn means during either of those two seasons.","zh":"in the spring or autumn 的意思是在春天或秋天這兩個季節其中之一期間。"},{"en":"Some families prefer travelling in the spring or autumn because places are less crowded.","zh":"有些家庭較喜歡在春季或秋季旅行，因為地方較少人。"},{"en":"Outdoor activities may feel more comfortable in spring or autumn than in very hot summer weather.","zh":"戶外活動在春季或秋季可能比炎熱夏天更舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase gives seasonal timing.","zh":"這個短語給出季節時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"favourite month","meaning":"最喜歡的月份","examples":[{"en":"September is Jack’s favourite month for surfing.","zh":"九月是 Jack 最喜歡的衝浪月份。"},{"en":"A favourite month is the month someone likes most for a particular activity or reason.","zh":"favourite month 是某人因特定活動或原因最喜歡的月份。"},{"en":"December is my favourite month because I enjoy Christmas lights and family meals.","zh":"十二月是我最喜歡的月份，因為我喜歡聖誕燈飾和家庭飯局。"},{"en":"A favourite month for travel may depend on weather, prices, and crowds.","zh":"最喜歡的旅行月份可能取決於天氣、價錢和人流。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses personal preference about time.","zh":"這個短語表達對時間的個人喜好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the water is warmer then","meaning":"那時水比較暖","examples":[{"en":"Jack likes September because the water is warmer then.","zh":"Jack 喜歡九月，因為那時水比較暖。"},{"en":"The water is warmer then means the sea or pool temperature is higher at that time.","zh":"the water is warmer then 的意思是那個時候海水或泳池水溫較高。"},{"en":"Many swimmers prefer late summer because the water is warmer then.","zh":"許多游泳者較喜歡夏末，因為那時水比較暖。"},{"en":"Warmer water can make water sports more comfortable, especially in cool countries.","zh":"較暖的水可以令水上運動更舒服，尤其是在涼爽國家。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a time with better water temperature.","zh":"這個短語把某個時間與較好水溫連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be back to school","meaning":"回學校上課","examples":[{"en":"The children are back to school in September.","zh":"孩子們九月回學校上課。"},{"en":"To be back to school means to return to school after a holiday or break.","zh":"be back to school 的意思是假期或休息後回到學校上課。"},{"en":"Children are usually back to school after the summer holiday ends.","zh":"暑假結束後，孩子通常回學校上課。"},{"en":"When children are back to school, families may find it harder to travel together.","zh":"當孩子回學校上課，家庭可能較難一起旅行。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing school schedules.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論學校時間表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one good thing about","meaning":"……的一個好處","examples":[{"en":"One good thing about Irish summers is that it does not get too hot.","zh":"愛爾蘭夏天的一個好處是天氣不會太熱。"},{"en":"One good thing about something introduces a positive point about it.","zh":"one good thing about something 用來引出某事的一個正面要點。"},{"en":"One good thing about living near school is that children can walk there.","zh":"住在學校附近的一個好處是孩子可以步行上學。"},{"en":"This phrase helps balance a discussion by adding a benefit after possible problems.","zh":"這個短語可在提到可能問題後加入好處，令討論更平衡。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving advice or opinions.","zh":"它適合用於給建議或表達意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Irish summers","meaning":"愛爾蘭的夏天","examples":[{"en":"Irish summers do not usually get too hot.","zh":"愛爾蘭的夏天通常不會太熱。"},{"en":"Irish summers are the summer seasons in Ireland, often mild compared with hotter countries.","zh":"Irish summers 是愛爾蘭的夏季，與較炎熱國家相比通常較溫和。"},{"en":"Tourists may enjoy Irish summers because outdoor activities can feel comfortable.","zh":"遊客可能喜歡愛爾蘭的夏天，因為戶外活動感覺舒適。"},{"en":"Mild summers can be good for walking and surfing, though rain may still be a problem.","zh":"溫和夏天有利於散步和衝浪，不過下雨仍可能是問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a seasonal climate in Ireland.","zh":"這個短語描述愛爾蘭的季節氣候。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"average temperature","meaning":"平均氣溫","examples":[{"en":"The average temperature is about 19 degrees.","zh":"平均氣溫約為19度。"},{"en":"Average temperature means the usual or mean temperature over a period of time.","zh":"average temperature 是一段時間內通常或平均的氣溫。"},{"en":"The average temperature in a classroom should be comfortable enough for students to concentrate.","zh":"課室平均氣溫應舒適得足以讓學生集中。"},{"en":"Travellers check average temperatures to decide what clothes to pack.","zh":"旅客查看平均氣溫，以決定帶甚麼衣服。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a general weather figure, not the temperature at every moment.","zh":"這個短語提供一般天氣數字，而不是每一刻的氣溫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"go above","meaning":"超過","examples":[{"en":"The temperature usually does not go above 25 degrees.","zh":"氣溫通常不會超過25度。"},{"en":"To go above a number means to become higher than that number.","zh":"go above 某數字的意思是變得高於該數字。"},{"en":"The price should not go above our budget.","zh":"價格不應超過我們的預算。"},{"en":"If the temperature goes above 30 degrees, outdoor sports may feel uncomfortable.","zh":"如果氣溫超過30度，戶外運動可能感覺不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for limits and measurements.","zh":"這個短語適合用於限制和量度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"that sounds alright","meaning":"聽起來還可以","examples":[{"en":"The woman thinks the temperature sounds alright.","zh":"這位女士覺得這個氣溫聽起來還可以。"},{"en":"That sounds alright means the information seems acceptable or suitable.","zh":"that sounds alright 的意思是該資訊看起來可以接受或合適。"},{"en":"If a hotel is close to the beach and not too expensive, that sounds alright.","zh":"如果酒店靠近海灘又不太貴，那聽起來還可以。"},{"en":"People say this when they are mildly satisfied but not extremely excited.","zh":"人們在感到略為滿意但不是非常興奮時會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a relaxed positive reaction.","zh":"這個短語給出輕鬆的正面反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"what about costs","meaning":"費用方面怎樣","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks Jack what about costs.","zh":"這位女士問 Jack 費用方面怎樣。"},{"en":"What about costs? means what should we know about the price or expenses.","zh":"What about costs? 的意思是關於價錢或開支，我們應知道甚麼。"},{"en":"After discussing the location, parents may ask, “What about costs?”","zh":"討論地點後，父母可能問：「費用方面怎樣？」"},{"en":"Asking about costs helps people decide whether a plan is affordable.","zh":"詢問費用有助人們決定計劃是否負擔得起。"},{"en":"This phrase shifts the discussion to money.","zh":"這個短語把討論轉向金錢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pretty cheap holiday","meaning":"相當便宜的假期","examples":[{"en":"Surfing is a pretty cheap holiday.","zh":"衝浪是相當便宜的假期。"},{"en":"A pretty cheap holiday is a holiday that is fairly inexpensive compared with other options.","zh":"pretty cheap holiday 是與其他選擇相比相當便宜的假期。"},{"en":"Camping can be a pretty cheap holiday if families already have tents.","zh":"如果家庭已有帳篷，露營可以是相當便宜的假期。"},{"en":"Cheap holidays are easier to plan when accommodation and activities do not cost too much.","zh":"當住宿和活動費用不太高，便宜假期會較容易規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and positive about cost.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，對費用作出正面評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the hire of equipment","meaning":"租用裝備","examples":[{"en":"The only cost is the hire of equipment.","zh":"唯一費用是租用裝備。"},{"en":"The hire of equipment means paying to use equipment for a limited time.","zh":"the hire of equipment 的意思是在有限時間內付費使用裝備。"},{"en":"The hire of ski equipment can be expensive during peak season.","zh":"滑雪裝備租用在旺季可能很貴。"},{"en":"Equipment hire is useful when travellers do not want to buy or carry heavy items.","zh":"當旅客不想購買或攜帶沉重物品，租用裝備很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on rental cost.","zh":"這個短語集中於租借費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"expect to pay","meaning":"預計要支付","examples":[{"en":"You can expect to pay about 30 euros a day.","zh":"你預計每天要支付約30歐元。"},{"en":"To expect to pay an amount means that amount is the likely or normal cost.","zh":"expect to pay 某金額的意思是該金額大概是可能或正常費用。"},{"en":"In a city centre café, you can expect to pay more than in a small local shop.","zh":"在市中心咖啡店，你預計要支付比小型本地店更多的錢。"},{"en":"Knowing what to expect to pay helps people prepare a realistic budget.","zh":"知道預計要支付多少，有助人們準備現實預算。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an estimated cost.","zh":"這個短語提供估計費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"daily rate","meaning":"每日收費","examples":[{"en":"The daily rate for hiring a wetsuit and board is about 30 euros.","zh":"租潛水衣和衝浪板的每日收費約為30歐元。"},{"en":"Daily rate means the amount charged for one day.","zh":"daily rate 是一天的收費金額。"},{"en":"The daily rate for renting a bicycle is lower if you book online.","zh":"網上預訂單車租借，每日收費可能較低。"},{"en":"Comparing daily rates helps travellers decide whether a weekly price is better.","zh":"比較每日收費有助旅客決定按星期收費是否更划算。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when talking about rentals, hotels, and services.","zh":"這個短語常用於租借、酒店和服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hire a wetsuit and board","meaning":"租潛水衣和衝浪板","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can hire a wetsuit and board for surfing.","zh":"遊客可以租潛水衣和衝浪板來衝浪。"},{"en":"To hire a wetsuit and board means to rent the clothing and surfboard needed for surfing.","zh":"hire a wetsuit and board 的意思是租用衝浪所需的衣物和衝浪板。"},{"en":"Beginners usually hire a wetsuit and board before deciding whether to buy their own.","zh":"初學者通常先租潛水衣和衝浪板，再決定是否購買自己的裝備。"},{"en":"Hiring equipment saves luggage space and reduces the cost of trying a new sport.","zh":"租用裝備可以節省行李空間，並降低嘗試新運動的成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes renting essential surfing gear.","zh":"這個短語描述租用基本衝浪裝備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"save about","meaning":"節省約","examples":[{"en":"You can save about 40 euros if you hire by the week.","zh":"如果按星期租用，你可以節省約40歐元。"},{"en":"To save about an amount means to spend approximately that much less.","zh":"save about 某金額的意思是大約少花該金額。"},{"en":"You can save about ten dollars if you bring lunch instead of eating out.","zh":"如果你帶午餐而不是外出吃飯，可以節省約十美元。"},{"en":"Savings help families choose longer activities without increasing the budget too much.","zh":"節省下來的錢能幫助家庭選擇較長活動，而不大幅增加預算。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate saving, not an exact promise.","zh":"這個短語提供大約節省金額，而不是精確承諾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hire by the week","meaning":"按星期租用","examples":[{"en":"Hiring equipment by the week is cheaper than hiring it daily.","zh":"按星期租用裝備比按日租用便宜。"},{"en":"To hire by the week means to rent something for a whole week instead of paying each day separately.","zh":"hire by the week 的意思是租用整個星期，而不是每天分開付款。"},{"en":"Families may hire a car by the week if they are travelling for several days.","zh":"如果家庭旅行數天，他們可能按星期租車。"},{"en":"Weekly hire can be cheaper because the company gives a longer rental discount.","zh":"按星期租用可能較便宜，因為公司會給予較長租期折扣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rental period and pricing method.","zh":"這個短語描述租借時段和收費方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not too bad","meaning":"不算太差","examples":[{"en":"The woman thinks the equipment cost is not too bad.","zh":"這位女士覺得裝備費用不算太差。"},{"en":"Not too bad means acceptable or better than expected.","zh":"not too bad 的意思是可以接受或比預期好。"},{"en":"The hotel room is small, but the price is not too bad.","zh":"酒店房間很小，但價錢不算太差。"},{"en":"People say this when something is not perfect but still reasonable.","zh":"當某事不完美但仍合理時，人們會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase gives mild approval.","zh":"這個短語表示溫和認可。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Jack says it is important to make sure the wetsuits are good quality.","zh":"Jack 說確保潛水衣質素良好很重要。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check carefully so that something is correct, safe, or certain.","zh":"make sure 的意思是仔細檢查，確定某事正確、安全或肯定。"},{"en":"Make sure you lock the door before leaving home.","zh":"離家前要確保鎖好門。"},{"en":"Checking in advance helps avoid problems later.","zh":"事先檢查有助避免之後出現問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in advice and instructions.","zh":"這個短語常用於建議和指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"good-quality wetsuits","meaning":"優質潛水衣","examples":[{"en":"Surfers need good-quality wetsuits in Ireland.","zh":"在愛爾蘭，衝浪者需要優質潛水衣。"},{"en":"Good-quality wetsuits are well-made suits that keep surfers warm and protected in cold water.","zh":"good-quality wetsuits 是製作良好、能在冷水中保暖和保護衝浪者的潛水衣。"},{"en":"A good-quality wetsuit should fit closely without making movement difficult.","zh":"優質潛水衣應貼身，但不會令動作困難。"},{"en":"Poor wetsuits can make surfing uncomfortable because cold water enters too easily.","zh":"劣質潛水衣會令衝浪不舒服，因為冷水太容易進入。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on equipment quality and safety.","zh":"這個短語集中於裝備質素和安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get too cold","meaning":"變得太冷","examples":[{"en":"Surfers will get too cold if their wetsuits are poor quality.","zh":"如果潛水衣質素差，衝浪者會變得太冷。"},{"en":"To get too cold means to become uncomfortably or dangerously cold.","zh":"get too cold 的意思是變得冷到不舒服或危險。"},{"en":"Children can get too cold if they stay in wet clothes after swimming.","zh":"如果孩子游泳後一直穿着濕衣服，可能會變得太冷。"},{"en":"Getting too cold can reduce energy, concentration, and enjoyment.","zh":"變得太冷可以減少體力、專注力和享受程度。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that temperature can become a problem.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們溫度可能成為問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make sure you also get","meaning":"確保也要準備","examples":[{"en":"Jack tells the woman to make sure she also gets boots.","zh":"Jack 告訴這位女士要確保也準備靴子。"},{"en":"Make sure you also get something means remember to include that extra item as well.","zh":"make sure you also get something 的意思是記得也包括那件額外物品。"},{"en":"When buying school supplies, make sure you also get a calculator.","zh":"買學校用品時，要確保也準備計數機。"},{"en":"Extra items can be important because missing one small thing may make the activity uncomfortable.","zh":"額外物品可能很重要，因為少了一件小東西也可能令活動不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another necessary detail to advice.","zh":"這個短語為建議加入另一個必要細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"boots","meaning":"靴子","examples":[{"en":"Surfing boots help keep the feet warm.","zh":"衝浪靴有助令雙腳保持溫暖。"},{"en":"Boots are strong footwear that cover the feet and often the ankles.","zh":"boots 是覆蓋雙腳並通常覆蓋腳踝的結實鞋類。"},{"en":"Hikers wear boots to protect their feet on rocky paths.","zh":"行山人士穿靴子，以保護雙腳走過岩石路徑。"},{"en":"In cold water sports, boots help protect feet from cold, sharp stones, and slippery surfaces.","zh":"在冷水運動中，靴子有助保護雙腳免受寒冷、尖石和濕滑表面影響。"},{"en":"This word describes protective footwear.","zh":"這個詞描述保護性鞋類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"keep your feet warm","meaning":"令雙腳保持溫暖","examples":[{"en":"Boots keep your feet warm while surfing.","zh":"衝浪時，靴子令雙腳保持溫暖。"},{"en":"To keep your feet warm means to stop your feet from becoming cold.","zh":"keep your feet warm 的意思是防止雙腳變冷。"},{"en":"Thick socks can keep your feet warm during winter walks.","zh":"厚襪可以在冬天散步時令雙腳保持溫暖。"},{"en":"Warm feet help people stay comfortable and active in cold conditions.","zh":"雙腳溫暖有助人們在寒冷環境中保持舒適和活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protection from cold.","zh":"這個短語描述防寒保護。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"with them on","meaning":"穿着它們時","examples":[{"en":"It is easier to surf with boots on.","zh":"穿着靴子時，衝浪會較容易。"},{"en":"With them on means while wearing those items.","zh":"with them on 的意思是穿着或戴着那些物品時。"},{"en":"These gloves feel strange at first, but it is easier to carry hot dishes with them on.","zh":"這些手套起初感覺奇怪，但穿着它們時拿熱盤會較容易。"},{"en":"Wearing the right equipment can make an activity safer and more comfortable.","zh":"穿着合適裝備可以令活動更安全和更舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to items already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回前面已提及的物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10}],"ielts/listening/Practice 14/task-2":[{"front":"run the service","meaning":"負責營運服務","examples":[{"en":"Mrs Carter runs the before and after school extended hours childcare service.","zh":"Carter 太太負責營運上學前及放學後的延時托兒服務。"},{"en":"To run the service means to manage and organise how the service operates.","zh":"run the service 是指管理和安排服務如何運作。"},{"en":"A school may hire a manager to run the lunch service every day.","zh":"學校可能聘請經理每天負責營運午膳服務。"},{"en":"Running a service involves staff, safety, schedules, costs, and communication with users.","zh":"營運服務涉及職員、安全、時間表、成本和與使用者溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on responsibility for daily operation, not just helping occasionally.","zh":"這個短語著重日常營運責任，而不只是偶爾幫忙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"before and after school","meaning":"上學前及放學後","examples":[{"en":"The school offers childcare before and after school.","zh":"學校提供上學前及放學後的托兒服務。"},{"en":"Before and after school means during the time before lessons start and after lessons finish.","zh":"before and after school 是指上課開始前和放學後的時段。"},{"en":"Working parents may need care for children before and after school.","zh":"在職家長可能需要上學前及放學後的兒童照顧。"},{"en":"These times can be difficult for families because parents may already be at work.","zh":"這些時段對家庭可能困難，因為家長可能已經在上班。"},{"en":"This phrase describes childcare around the normal school day.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞正常上課日的托兒安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"extended hours childcare service","meaning":"延時托兒服務","examples":[{"en":"Mrs Carter runs the extended hours childcare service.","zh":"Carter 太太負責營運延時托兒服務。"},{"en":"An extended hours childcare service looks after children outside normal school hours.","zh":"extended hours childcare service 是在正常上課時間以外照顧孩子的服務。"},{"en":"A school may offer an extended hours childcare service for parents who start work early.","zh":"學校可能為很早上班的家長提供延時托兒服務。"},{"en":"Extended childcare helps families when normal school hours do not match working hours.","zh":"當正常上課時間與工作時間不配合時，延時托兒能幫助家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised care before school, after school, or during holidays.","zh":"這個短語指上學前、放學後或假期中的有組織照顧服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have a chance to","meaning":"有機會……","examples":[{"en":"Parents have had a chance to look around the school.","zh":"家長已有機會參觀學校。"},{"en":"To have a chance to do something means to have an opportunity to do it.","zh":"have a chance to do something 是指有機會做某事。"},{"en":"Visitors may have a chance to ask questions after the talk.","zh":"訪客在講座後可能有機會提問。"},{"en":"Having a chance to see a place helps people make a more informed decision.","zh":"有機會參觀一個地方，有助人們作出更有根據的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an opportunity that may not always be available.","zh":"這個短語表示一個不一定經常有的機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have a good look around","meaning":"好好參觀","examples":[{"en":"Parents have had a good look around the school.","zh":"家長已經好好參觀了學校。"},{"en":"To have a good look around means to inspect or explore a place carefully.","zh":"have a good look around 是指仔細查看或參觀一個地方。"},{"en":"Before renting a flat, people should have a good look around every room.","zh":"租單位前，人們應好好看看每個房間。"},{"en":"Looking around carefully helps visitors notice facilities, safety, and atmosphere.","zh":"仔細參觀有助訪客留意設施、安全和氣氛。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests more than a quick glance.","zh":"這個短語表示不只是匆匆看一眼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"talk to staff and pupils","meaning":"與教職員和學生交談","examples":[{"en":"Parents can talk to staff and pupils during the visit.","zh":"家長可以在參觀期間與教職員和學生交談。"},{"en":"To talk to staff and pupils means to speak with school employees and students.","zh":"talk to staff and pupils 是指與學校職員和學生說話。"},{"en":"New parents may talk to staff and pupils to learn what school life is really like.","zh":"新家長可能與教職員和學生交談，以了解真正的校園生活。"},{"en":"Speaking to both adults and children gives visitors a fuller picture of the school.","zh":"同時與成人和孩子交談，可以讓訪客更全面了解學校。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct conversation with people in the school community.","zh":"這個短語描述與校園社群成員直接對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be interested in using","meaning":"有興趣使用……","examples":[{"en":"Many parents are interested in using the childcare service.","zh":"許多家長有興趣使用托兒服務。"},{"en":"To be interested in using something means to want to know more about it or consider using it.","zh":"be interested in using something 是指想了解更多或考慮使用某服務。"},{"en":"Families may be interested in using a school bus if it saves travel time.","zh":"如果校巴能節省交通時間，家庭可能有興趣使用它。"},{"en":"Interest often grows when a service solves a real daily problem.","zh":"當服務能解決真實日常問題，人們的興趣通常會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean the person has already signed up.","zh":"這個短語不代表那個人已經報名。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"when your child joins the school","meaning":"當你的孩子入讀學校時","examples":[{"en":"Parents may use the service when their child joins the school.","zh":"家長可以在孩子入讀學校時使用這項服務。"},{"en":"When your child joins the school means when your child starts studying at that school.","zh":"when your child joins the school 是指當你的孩子開始在該校讀書時。"},{"en":"Parents often have many questions when their child joins a new school.","zh":"當孩子入讀新學校時，家長通常有很多問題。"},{"en":"A child joining a school can change family routines, transport, and childcare needs.","zh":"孩子入讀學校可以改變家庭日程、交通和托兒需要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the beginning of a child’s time at the school.","zh":"這個短語指孩子在學校生活的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"know something about","meaning":"對……有些認識","examples":[{"en":"Some parents already know something about the childcare service.","zh":"有些家長已經對托兒服務有些認識。"},{"en":"To know something about a topic means to have some basic information, but not necessarily full knowledge.","zh":"know something about a topic 是指對某主題有一些基本資料，但不一定完全了解。"},{"en":"A student may know something about a subject before taking the course.","zh":"學生在修讀課程前，可能對該科有些認識。"},{"en":"Knowing something about a service makes it easier to ask specific questions.","zh":"對服務有些認識，會較容易提出具體問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows partial knowledge.","zh":"這個短語表示部分了解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for those who don’t","meaning":"給那些不了解的人","examples":[{"en":"For those who don’t know about the service, Mrs Carter explains the details.","zh":"給那些不了解服務的人，Carter 太太會解釋細節。"},{"en":"For those who don’t means for the people who do not know, understand, or have something.","zh":"for those who don’t 是指給那些不知道、不明白或沒有某物的人。"},{"en":"For those who don’t have a lunch card, the office can issue a temporary one.","zh":"給那些沒有午膳卡的人，辦公室可以發臨時卡。"},{"en":"This phrase helps include people who are less informed or less prepared.","zh":"這個短語有助照顧資料較少或準備不足的人。"},{"en":"It is often used before giving extra explanation.","zh":"它常用於提供額外解釋之前。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"go through","meaning":"講解；逐一說明","examples":[{"en":"Mrs Carter goes through the main details of the childcare service.","zh":"Carter 太太逐一說明托兒服務的主要細節。"},{"en":"To go through something means to explain, check, or discuss it step by step.","zh":"go through something 是指逐步解釋、檢查或討論某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may go through exam instructions before students begin.","zh":"老師可能在學生開始前講解考試指示。"},{"en":"Going through details carefully reduces confusion and mistakes.","zh":"仔細逐一說明細節可以減少混亂和錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when information needs to be covered in order.","zh":"當資料需要按次序涵蓋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"main details","meaning":"主要細節","examples":[{"en":"Mrs Carter explains the main details of the service.","zh":"Carter 太太解釋這項服務的主要細節。"},{"en":"Main details are the most important pieces of information about something.","zh":"main details 是關於某事最重要的資料。"},{"en":"A poster should include the main details of an event, such as time, place, and cost.","zh":"海報應包括活動的主要細節，例如時間、地點和費用。"},{"en":"Giving the main details first helps listeners understand the service quickly.","zh":"先提供主要細節有助聽者快速了解服務。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts key information with smaller extra points.","zh":"這個短語把關鍵資料與較小的附加內容作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"offer childcare for","meaning":"為……提供托兒服務","examples":[{"en":"The school offers childcare for children from the ages of four to eleven.","zh":"學校為4至11歲的孩子提供托兒服務。"},{"en":"To offer childcare for a group means to provide care for those children.","zh":"offer childcare for a group 是指為該群孩子提供照顧服務。"},{"en":"A community centre may offer childcare for parents attending evening classes.","zh":"社區中心可能為參加夜校的家長提供托兒服務。"},{"en":"Offering childcare helps parents work, study, or attend appointments more easily.","zh":"提供托兒服務幫助家長更容易工作、學習或赴約。"},{"en":"This phrase describes who the service is provided for.","zh":"這個短語描述服務提供給誰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"from the ages of four to eleven","meaning":"由4至11歲","examples":[{"en":"The service is for children from the ages of four to eleven.","zh":"這項服務是給4至11歲的孩子。"},{"en":"From the ages of four to eleven means including children aged four, five, and up to eleven.","zh":"from the ages of four to eleven 是指包括4歲、5歲，一直到11歲的孩子。"},{"en":"A sports club may accept children from the ages of six to twelve.","zh":"運動會可能接受6至12歲的孩子。"},{"en":"Age limits help services plan suitable activities and insurance cover.","zh":"年齡限制有助服務規劃合適活動和保險保障。"},{"en":"This phrase defines the age range clearly.","zh":"這個短語清楚界定年齡範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"find something invaluable","meaning":"覺得……非常有價值","examples":[{"en":"Many working parents find this service invaluable.","zh":"許多在職家長覺得這項服務非常有價值。"},{"en":"To find something invaluable means to think it is extremely useful or important.","zh":"find something invaluable 是指認為某物極有用或極重要。"},{"en":"Students may find a clear revision timetable invaluable before exams.","zh":"考試前，學生可能覺得清楚的溫習時間表非常有價值。"},{"en":"A service becomes invaluable when it solves a difficult problem in daily life.","zh":"當服務解決日常生活中的困難問題，它便會變得非常有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase means very valuable, not worthless.","zh":"這個短語解作非常有價值，不是沒有價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"working parents","meaning":"在職家長","examples":[{"en":"Working parents often need before and after school childcare.","zh":"在職家長常需要上學前及放學後托兒服務。"},{"en":"Working parents are parents who have jobs and need to manage both work and family care.","zh":"working parents 是有工作並需要同時處理工作和家庭照顧的家長。"},{"en":"Working parents may struggle if school finishes before their workday ends.","zh":"如果學校放學時間早於下班時間，在職家長可能會感到吃力。"},{"en":"Childcare services support working parents by filling gaps in the day.","zh":"托兒服務透過填補一天中的空隙來支援在職家長。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on parents’ employment and care responsibilities.","zh":"這個短語著重家長的工作和照顧責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"leave your child with us","meaning":"把孩子交給我們照顧","examples":[{"en":"Parents can leave their child with the childcare team.","zh":"家長可以把孩子交給托兒團隊照顧。"},{"en":"To leave your child with someone means to place the child in that person’s care for a period of time.","zh":"leave your child with someone 是指把孩子暫時交由某人照顧。"},{"en":"A parent may leave a child with grandparents while attending a medical appointment.","zh":"家長可能在赴醫療預約時把孩子交給祖父母照顧。"},{"en":"Parents need trust before they feel comfortable leaving their child with others.","zh":"家長需要信任，才會放心把孩子交給別人照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase is about temporary care and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語關於暫時照顧和責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"safe in the knowledge that","meaning":"安心知道……","examples":[{"en":"Parents can leave their child safe in the knowledge that they will be well cared for.","zh":"家長可以把孩子留下，安心知道他們會受到良好照顧。"},{"en":"Safe in the knowledge that means feeling calm and confident because you know something reassuring is true.","zh":"safe in the knowledge that 是指因知道某件令人放心的事是真實的，而感到安心和有信心。"},{"en":"Parents can work late safe in the knowledge that their children are supervised.","zh":"家長可以加班，安心知道孩子有人看管。"},{"en":"Clear information helps people feel safe in the knowledge that risks are managed.","zh":"清楚資料能幫助人安心知道風險已被管理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional reassurance based on certainty.","zh":"這個短語描述基於確定性的情感安心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be extremely well cared for","meaning":"受到非常好的照顧","examples":[{"en":"The children will be extremely well cared for.","zh":"孩子會受到非常好的照顧。"},{"en":"To be extremely well cared for means to receive very good attention, support, and protection.","zh":"be extremely well cared for 是指得到非常好的照料、支援和保護。"},{"en":"Elderly residents in a good care home are extremely well cared for by trained staff.","zh":"好護老院中的長者會由受訓職員給予非常好的照顧。"},{"en":"Good care includes safety, food, kindness, and appropriate activities.","zh":"良好照顧包括安全、食物、善意和合適活動。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures parents that children’s needs will be met carefully.","zh":"這個短語安撫家長，表示孩子的需要會被仔細照顧。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be insured to","meaning":"有保險保障可……","examples":[{"en":"The service is insured to provide care for up to 70 children.","zh":"這項服務有保險保障，可照顧最多70名孩子。"},{"en":"To be insured to do something means insurance covers the service for that permitted activity or number.","zh":"be insured to do something 是指保險涵蓋該服務可進行的活動或人數。"},{"en":"A coach company may be insured to carry up to fifty passengers.","zh":"客車公司可能有保險保障，可載最多50名乘客。"},{"en":"Insurance limits affect how many people a service can safely accept.","zh":"保險限制會影響一項服務能安全接受多少人。"},{"en":"This phrase connects legal or financial protection with what the service is allowed to do.","zh":"這個短語把法律或財務保障與服務可做的事連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"provide care for","meaning":"照顧……","examples":[{"en":"The school can provide care for up to 70 children.","zh":"學校可以照顧最多70名孩子。"},{"en":"To provide care for someone means to look after their needs, safety, and wellbeing.","zh":"provide care for someone 是指照顧某人的需要、安全和福祉。"},{"en":"A nursery provides care for young children while parents work.","zh":"幼兒中心在家長上班時照顧年幼孩子。"},{"en":"Providing care requires trained staff, safe space, food, and activities.","zh":"提供照顧需要受訓職員、安全空間、食物和活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in childcare, healthcare, and elderly services.","zh":"這個短語常見於托兒、醫療和長者服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"up to","meaning":"最多","examples":[{"en":"The service can care for up to 70 children.","zh":"這項服務最多可以照顧70名孩子。"},{"en":"Up to means no more than a stated maximum number or amount.","zh":"up to 是指不超過指定最高數字或數量。"},{"en":"The classroom can hold up to thirty students.","zh":"這間課室最多可容納30名學生。"},{"en":"A limit matters because safety and staffing depend on numbers.","zh":"限額很重要，因為安全和人手取決於人數。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the highest possible amount, not the usual amount.","zh":"這個短語提供最高可能數量，而不是平常數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rarely have this many attending","meaning":"很少有這麼多人出席","examples":[{"en":"The service rarely has this many children attending one session.","zh":"這項服務很少有這麼多孩子出席同一時段。"},{"en":"Rarely have this many attending means it is unusual for so many people to be present.","zh":"rarely have this many attending 是指很少有這麼多人同時在場。"},{"en":"A club may be registered for fifty members but rarely have this many attending meetings.","zh":"學會可能有50名登記會員，但很少有這麼多人出席會議。"},{"en":"Attendance can be lower than registration because people come on different days.","zh":"出席人數可能低於登記人數，因為人們在不同日子參加。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the maximum or registered number with actual attendance.","zh":"這個短語把最高或登記人數與實際出席人數作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at any one session","meaning":"在任何單一時段","examples":[{"en":"There are rarely 70 children attending at any one session.","zh":"在任何單一時段，很少有70名孩子出席。"},{"en":"At any one session means during any single meeting, class, or period of service.","zh":"at any one session 是指在任何一節會議、課堂或服務時段中。"},{"en":"A language centre may limit attendance to twelve students at any one session.","zh":"語言中心可能限制任何單一課堂最多12名學生。"},{"en":"Counting people per session helps staff plan space and safety.","zh":"按時段計算人數有助職員安排空間和安全。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on one time period, not the whole week or month.","zh":"這個短語著重一個時段，而不是整星期或整個月。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"generally expect","meaning":"一般預計","examples":[{"en":"The school generally expects around 50 to 60 children in the afternoon.","zh":"學校一般預計下午會有大約50至60名孩子。"},{"en":"To generally expect something means to usually think it will happen based on normal patterns.","zh":"generally expect something 是指根據平常模式通常預計某事會發生。"},{"en":"A restaurant generally expects more customers on Friday evenings.","zh":"餐廳一般預計星期五晚上會有較多顧客。"},{"en":"Expected numbers help organisations prepare staff, food, and space.","zh":"預計人數幫助機構準備人手、食物和空間。"},{"en":"This phrase allows for normal variation, not an exact promise.","zh":"這個短語容許正常變動，而不是確切承諾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"afternoon sessions","meaning":"下午時段","examples":[{"en":"The afternoon sessions usually have around 50 to 60 children.","zh":"下午時段通常有大約50至60名孩子。"},{"en":"Afternoon sessions are childcare periods that take place after school in the afternoon.","zh":"afternoon sessions 是下午放學後進行的托兒時段。"},{"en":"An afternoon session may include snacks, homework time, games, and activities.","zh":"下午時段可能包括小食、功課時間、遊戲和活動。"},{"en":"Afternoon sessions are often busier because many parents are still at work.","zh":"下午時段通常較繁忙，因為許多家長仍在上班。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific time block in the service.","zh":"這個短語指服務中的特定時間段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"breakfast sessions","meaning":"早餐時段","examples":[{"en":"The breakfast sessions usually have about half that number.","zh":"早餐時段通常大約有一半人數。"},{"en":"Breakfast sessions are morning childcare periods before school, often including breakfast.","zh":"breakfast sessions 是上學前的早上托兒時段，通常包括早餐。"},{"en":"A breakfast session may help parents who need to leave for work early.","zh":"早餐時段可以幫助需要很早上班的家長。"},{"en":"Fewer children may attend breakfast sessions because some parents can bring them later.","zh":"早餐時段參加孩子可能較少，因為有些家長可以較遲帶孩子上學。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the early-morning part of the childcare service.","zh":"這個短語指托兒服務中的清晨部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"currently","meaning":"目前","examples":[{"en":"The service currently has 70 children registered.","zh":"這項服務目前有70名孩子登記。"},{"en":"Currently means at the present time or right now.","zh":"currently 是指目前或現在。"},{"en":"The library is currently closed for repairs.","zh":"圖書館目前因維修而關閉。"},{"en":"This word is useful when a situation may change later.","zh":"當情況之後可能改變時，這個詞很有用。"},{"en":"It focuses on the present condition, not the past or future.","zh":"它著重目前狀況，而不是過去或將來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be registered with","meaning":"在……登記","examples":[{"en":"Seventy children are currently registered with the childcare service.","zh":"目前有70名孩子在托兒服務中登記。"},{"en":"To be registered with a service means to be officially signed up or recorded as a user.","zh":"be registered with a service 是指正式報名或被記錄為服務使用者。"},{"en":"A patient may be registered with a local doctor’s clinic.","zh":"病人可能在本地醫生診所登記。"},{"en":"Registration helps organisations keep records and plan resources.","zh":"登記幫助機構保存紀錄和規劃資源。"},{"en":"This phrase shows official enrolment, not necessarily daily attendance.","zh":"這個短語表示正式登記，不一定代表每天出席。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"attend every day","meaning":"每天參加","examples":[{"en":"Not all registered children attend every day.","zh":"並非所有已登記孩子都每天參加。"},{"en":"To attend every day means to go to a place or service daily.","zh":"attend every day 是指每天到某個地方或使用某項服務。"},{"en":"A child may attend football practice every day during a holiday camp.","zh":"孩子可能在假期營期間每天參加足球訓練。"},{"en":"Attendance can vary when families have different work schedules.","zh":"當家庭有不同工作時間表，出席情況可能會變動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regular daily participation.","zh":"這個短語描述每天定期參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it’s ten years since","meaning":"自從……已有十年","examples":[{"en":"It is ten years since the school began offering the service.","zh":"自從學校開始提供這項服務已有十年。"},{"en":"It’s ten years since means ten years have passed from a past event until now.","zh":"it’s ten years since 是指從過去某事件到現在已過了十年。"},{"en":"It is five years since the library moved to its new building.","zh":"自從圖書館搬到新大樓已有五年。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a past starting point with the present.","zh":"這個短語把過去起點與現在連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing how long a service or situation has existed.","zh":"當描述服務或情況存在了多久時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"begin offering","meaning":"開始提供","examples":[{"en":"The school began offering an extended hours service ten years ago.","zh":"學校十年前開始提供延時服務。"},{"en":"To begin offering something means to start providing it to people.","zh":"begin offering something 是指開始向人們提供某物。"},{"en":"A shop may begin offering online delivery after customers request it.","zh":"顧客提出要求後，商店可能開始提供網上送貨。"},{"en":"Services often begin offering new options when community needs change.","zh":"當社區需要改變，服務通常會開始提供新選項。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the start of providing a service or product.","zh":"這個短語標示開始提供服務或產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"come a long way","meaning":"進步很多；發展很多","examples":[{"en":"The childcare service has come a long way in ten years.","zh":"這項托兒服務十年來發展了很多。"},{"en":"To come a long way means to improve or develop a lot over time.","zh":"come a long way 是指隨時間大大進步或發展。"},{"en":"A shy student has come a long way if she can now speak confidently in class.","zh":"如果害羞學生現在能在課堂上自信發言，她就是進步很多。"},{"en":"Progress over many years can make a small service much stronger.","zh":"多年進步可以令小型服務變得強大得多。"},{"en":"This phrase praises development from an earlier weaker stage.","zh":"這個短語讚賞從較弱早期階段發展至今。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"during that time","meaning":"在那段時間裏","examples":[{"en":"The service has developed a lot during that time.","zh":"這項服務在那段時間裏發展了很多。"},{"en":"During that time means within the period already mentioned.","zh":"during that time 是指在剛才提到的那段時期內。"},{"en":"The club started five years ago, and during that time it has doubled its membership.","zh":"學會五年前成立，在那段時間裏會員人數增加了一倍。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show what happened across a period, not at one single moment.","zh":"這個短語有助顯示某段時間內發生的事，而不是某一刻。"},{"en":"It links development to a stated length of time.","zh":"它把發展與已說明的時間長度連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"first opened","meaning":"剛開始營運時","examples":[{"en":"When the service first opened, only 20 children attended regularly.","zh":"這項服務剛開始營運時，只有20名孩子定期參加。"},{"en":"First opened means began operating for the first time.","zh":"first opened 是指第一次開始營運。"},{"en":"When the new sports centre first opened, local families came to visit it.","zh":"新運動中心剛開幕時，本地家庭都來參觀。"},{"en":"Early attendance can be low when people are still learning about a new service.","zh":"當人們仍在了解新服務時，初期出席人數可能較低。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the beginning of a service, shop, or facility.","zh":"這個短語指服務、商店或設施的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"attend regularly","meaning":"定期參加","examples":[{"en":"About 20 children attended regularly when the service first opened.","zh":"服務剛開始時，約20名孩子定期參加。"},{"en":"To attend regularly means to go often and in a repeated pattern.","zh":"attend regularly 是指經常並按固定模式出席。"},{"en":"Students who attend regularly usually find it easier to keep up with lessons.","zh":"定期上課的學生通常較容易跟上課堂。"},{"en":"Regular attendance helps staff plan numbers and activities.","zh":"定期出席有助職員規劃人數和活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is different from attending once or occasionally.","zh":"這個短語不同於只參加一次或偶爾參加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"keep costs as low as possible","meaning":"盡量降低成本","examples":[{"en":"The school tries to keep its costs as low as possible.","zh":"學校嘗試盡量降低成本。"},{"en":"To keep costs as low as possible means to spend the least amount of money while still running properly.","zh":"keep costs as low as possible 是指在仍能正常運作下花最少金錢。"},{"en":"A family may keep costs low by cooking at home instead of eating out.","zh":"家庭可能透過在家煮飯而不是外出用餐來降低成本。"},{"en":"Lower costs can make a service more affordable for more people.","zh":"較低成本可以令服務對更多人來說更負擔得起。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful budgeting, not poor quality.","zh":"這個短語表示謹慎預算，而不是低質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"provide good value for money","meaning":"物有所值","examples":[{"en":"The school believes the service provides good value for money.","zh":"學校相信這項服務物有所值。"},{"en":"To provide good value for money means to offer quality or usefulness worth the price paid.","zh":"provide good value for money 是指提供與價格相稱的質素或實用價值。"},{"en":"A course provides good value for money if it includes lessons, materials, and feedback.","zh":"如果課程包括課堂、教材和回饋，它就是物有所值。"},{"en":"Parents feel better paying fees when they see clear benefits for their children.","zh":"當家長看見孩子得到明顯好處，他們會更願意付費。"},{"en":"This phrase compares cost with what users receive.","zh":"這個短語比較費用與使用者獲得的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"run from...until...","meaning":"由……至……","examples":[{"en":"The afternoon sessions run from 3:30 until 6 p.m.","zh":"下午時段由3時30分至下午6時。"},{"en":"Run from one time until another means start at the first time and end at the second.","zh":"run from one time until another 是指在第一個時間開始，在第二個時間結束。"},{"en":"The workshop runs from nine until twelve on Saturday morning.","zh":"工作坊星期六早上由九時至十二時。"},{"en":"Clear session times help parents plan pick-up and work schedules.","zh":"清楚時段有助家長安排接送和工作時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for events, services, lessons, and opening hours.","zh":"這個短語可用於活動、服務、課堂和營業時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"if you prefer","meaning":"如果你較喜歡","examples":[{"en":"If you prefer, you can pay for one hour only.","zh":"如果你較喜歡，可以只支付一小時費用。"},{"en":"If you prefer means if that option suits you better or is what you would rather choose.","zh":"if you prefer 是指如果那個選項更適合你，或你較想選擇它。"},{"en":"If you prefer, you can collect the form tomorrow instead of today.","zh":"如果你較喜歡，可以明天才取表格，而不是今天。"},{"en":"This phrase offers flexibility without pressuring the listener.","zh":"這個短語提供彈性，而不向聽者施壓。"},{"en":"It is polite and common when giving choices.","zh":"它有禮貌，常用於提供選擇時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pay for one hour only","meaning":"只支付一小時費用","examples":[{"en":"Parents can pay for one hour only.","zh":"家長可以只支付一小時費用。"},{"en":"To pay for one hour only means to pay just for a single hour of service.","zh":"pay for one hour only 是指只支付一小時服務費。"},{"en":"A parent may pay for one hour only if they can collect the child soon after school.","zh":"如果家長能在放學後不久接孩子，可能只支付一小時費用。"},{"en":"Paying only for the time needed can make childcare more affordable.","zh":"只支付需要的時間可以令托兒更負擔得起。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a shorter and cheaper payment option.","zh":"這個短語突出較短和較便宜的付款選項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the cost of","meaning":"……的費用","examples":[{"en":"The cost of the childcare includes food and snacks.","zh":"托兒服務的費用包括食物和小食。"},{"en":"The cost of something means the amount of money needed to pay for it.","zh":"the cost of something 是指支付某物所需的金額。"},{"en":"The cost of a school trip may include transport, lunch, and entrance tickets.","zh":"學校旅行的費用可能包括交通、午餐和入場票。"},{"en":"Knowing the cost helps families decide whether they can afford a service.","zh":"知道費用有助家庭決定是否負擔得起服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when explaining fees or prices.","zh":"這個短語用於解釋收費或價格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"include food and snacks","meaning":"包括食物和小食","examples":[{"en":"The childcare fee includes food and snacks.","zh":"托兒費用包括食物和小食。"},{"en":"To include food and snacks means meals or light food are part of what is provided.","zh":"include food and snacks 是指膳食或輕食包括在提供內容中。"},{"en":"A holiday camp may include lunch and snacks in the daily fee.","zh":"假期營每日費用可能包括午餐和小食。"},{"en":"Including food helps parents because they do not need to pack extra meals.","zh":"包括食物可以幫助家長，因為他們不用額外準備膳食。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what is covered by the payment.","zh":"這個短語解釋付款涵蓋甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be given breakfast","meaning":"獲提供早餐","examples":[{"en":"Children are given breakfast in the morning.","zh":"孩子早上獲提供早餐。"},{"en":"To be given breakfast means to receive a morning meal from someone.","zh":"be given breakfast 是指由他人提供早餐。"},{"en":"Children at a breakfast club may be given cereal, toast, and fruit.","zh":"早餐會中的孩子可能獲提供麥片、吐司和水果。"},{"en":"Giving breakfast helps children start the school day with energy.","zh":"提供早餐有助孩子有精力開始上課日。"},{"en":"This passive phrase focuses on what children receive.","zh":"這個被動短語著重孩子收到甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"healthy snack","meaning":"健康小食","examples":[{"en":"Children receive a healthy snack after school.","zh":"孩子放學後會獲得健康小食。"},{"en":"A healthy snack is a small amount of food that is good for the body.","zh":"healthy snack 是對身體有益的小份食物。"},{"en":"Fruit, yoghurt, and wholegrain toast can be healthy snacks for children.","zh":"水果、乳酪和全麥多士都可以是孩子的健康小食。"},{"en":"Healthy snacks help children avoid becoming too hungry before dinner.","zh":"健康小食幫助孩子在晚飯前不會太餓。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with sugary or low-nutrition snacks.","zh":"這個短語與高糖或低營養小食相對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as soon as","meaning":"一……就……","examples":[{"en":"Children get a snack as soon as they finish school.","zh":"孩子一放學就會得到小食。"},{"en":"As soon as means immediately after something happens.","zh":"as soon as 是指某事發生後立刻。"},{"en":"Call me as soon as you arrive at the station.","zh":"你一到車站就打電話給我。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that there is very little delay between two actions.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個動作之間幾乎沒有延遲。"},{"en":"It is useful when timing is important.","zh":"當時間安排重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"finish school","meaning":"放學","examples":[{"en":"Children receive a snack when they finish school.","zh":"孩子放學時會得到小食。"},{"en":"To finish school means to complete the school day or, in another context, complete one’s education.","zh":"finish school 可以指結束一天課堂，也可在其他語境中指完成學業。"},{"en":"Primary children may finish school at around three o’clock.","zh":"小學生可能大約三點放學。"},{"en":"After children finish school, they may need care until parents collect them.","zh":"孩子放學後，可能需要有人照顧直到家長接走。"},{"en":"In this context, it means the end of the school day.","zh":"在這個語境中，它指一天課堂結束。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"something more substantial","meaning":"較有份量的食物","examples":[{"en":"At 5 p.m., children are given something more substantial.","zh":"下午5時，孩子會獲提供較有份量的食物。"},{"en":"Something more substantial means food that is more filling or larger than a light snack.","zh":"something more substantial 是指比輕食更飽肚或分量更大的食物。"},{"en":"After sports practice, a child may need something more substantial than a biscuit.","zh":"運動練習後，孩子可能需要比餅乾更有份量的食物。"},{"en":"More substantial food helps children stay comfortable if dinner will be later.","zh":"較有份量的食物能幫助孩子在晚飯較遲時保持舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts a proper light meal with a small snack.","zh":"這個短語把較正式的小餐與小食作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"such as","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"Children are given something more substantial, such as pasta or a casserole.","zh":"孩子會獲提供較有份量的食物，例如意粉或燉菜。"},{"en":"Such as introduces examples of the thing just mentioned.","zh":"such as 用來引入剛提及事物的例子。"},{"en":"Children need stationery such as pencils, rulers, and notebooks.","zh":"孩子需要文具，例如鉛筆、尺和筆記簿。"},{"en":"Examples after “such as” make a general idea easier to understand.","zh":"such as 後面的例子會令籠統概念更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving specific items from a larger group.","zh":"當從較大類別中列出具體項目時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pasta","meaning":"意粉","examples":[{"en":"Pasta is one of the foods served at 5 p.m.","zh":"意粉是下午5時供應的食物之一。"},{"en":"Pasta is food made from flour and water, often served with sauce.","zh":"pasta 是由麵粉和水製成、常配醬汁食用的食物。"},{"en":"Children may eat pasta with tomato sauce after school.","zh":"孩子放學後可能吃番茄醬意粉。"},{"en":"Pasta is filling, so it can work as a more substantial snack or light meal.","zh":"意粉能填飽肚子，所以可作較有份量的小食或輕餐。"},{"en":"This word includes foods such as spaghetti, macaroni, and penne.","zh":"這個詞包括意大利粉、通心粉和長通粉等食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"casserole","meaning":"燉菜；焗燉菜","examples":[{"en":"A casserole may be served as a more substantial snack.","zh":"燉菜可以作為較有份量的小食供應。"},{"en":"A casserole is a dish cooked slowly in one pot or deep dish, often with meat, vegetables, and sauce.","zh":"casserole 是在一個鍋或深盤中慢煮的菜式，常有肉、蔬菜和醬汁。"},{"en":"A school kitchen may serve a vegetable casserole on cold days.","zh":"學校廚房可能在寒冷日子供應蔬菜燉菜。"},{"en":"Casseroles are filling because they often include protein, vegetables, and carbohydrates.","zh":"燉菜通常包括蛋白質、蔬菜和碳水化合物，所以較飽肚。"},{"en":"This word refers to a cooked dish, not just the cooking container.","zh":"這個詞指烹調好的菜式，而不只是烹調容器。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"inform us of","meaning":"通知我們……","examples":[{"en":"Parents should inform the school of any allergies.","zh":"家長應通知學校任何過敏情況。"},{"en":"To inform us of something means to tell us important information formally or clearly.","zh":"inform us of something 是指正式或清楚地告訴我們重要資料。"},{"en":"Please inform the office of any change in your address.","zh":"如地址有任何變更，請通知辦公室。"},{"en":"Informing staff of allergies helps prevent unsafe food being given to a child.","zh":"通知職員過敏情況有助防止孩子獲提供不安全食物。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than “tell us about”.","zh":"這個短語比 tell us about 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"allergies","meaning":"過敏","examples":[{"en":"Parents should tell the school about their child’s allergies.","zh":"家長應告訴學校孩子的過敏情況。"},{"en":"Allergies are strong body reactions to certain foods, substances, or materials.","zh":"allergies 是身體對某些食物、物質或材料的強烈反應。"},{"en":"A child may have allergies to nuts, milk, eggs, or dust.","zh":"孩子可能對堅果、牛奶、雞蛋或塵埃過敏。"},{"en":"Allergies can cause itching, swelling, stomach pain, or breathing problems.","zh":"過敏可能引起痕癢、腫脹、肚痛或呼吸問題。"},{"en":"Schools need allergy information to keep children safe.","zh":"學校需要過敏資料來保障孩子安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"The staff will make sure children are offered suitable food.","zh":"職員會確保孩子獲提供合適食物。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check or act carefully so something happens correctly.","zh":"make sure 是指檢查或小心行動，使某事正確發生。"},{"en":"Parents make sure children bring their homework before leaving home.","zh":"家長離家前會確保孩子帶了功課。"},{"en":"Making sure prevents mistakes, especially when safety is involved.","zh":"確保某事可以防止錯誤，尤其涉及安全時。"},{"en":"This phrase shows care, checking, and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語顯示小心、檢查和責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be offered","meaning":"獲提供","examples":[{"en":"Children with allergies will be offered a suitable alternative.","zh":"有過敏的孩子會獲提供合適的替代選擇。"},{"en":"To be offered something means to be given the chance to receive or choose it.","zh":"be offered something 是指獲得接受或選擇某物的機會。"},{"en":"Visitors may be offered tea or water when they arrive.","zh":"訪客到達時可能獲提供茶或水。"},{"en":"Offering alternatives helps include people with different needs.","zh":"提供替代選擇有助照顧有不同需要的人。"},{"en":"This passive phrase focuses on what is provided to the person.","zh":"這個被動短語著重某人獲提供甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"suitable alternative","meaning":"合適的替代選擇","examples":[{"en":"Children with allergies will be offered a suitable alternative.","zh":"有過敏的孩子會獲提供合適的替代選擇。"},{"en":"A suitable alternative is another option that is safe and appropriate for the situation.","zh":"suitable alternative 是安全並適合情況的另一個選項。"},{"en":"If a child cannot drink milk, oat milk may be a suitable alternative.","zh":"如果孩子不能喝牛奶，燕麥奶可能是合適的替代選擇。"},{"en":"Suitable alternatives allow people to join in without risking their health.","zh":"合適替代選擇讓人可以參與，而不危及健康。"},{"en":"This phrase means a replacement that fits the need, not just any substitute.","zh":"這個短語指符合需要的替代品，而不只是任何替代物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as you may know","meaning":"如你可能知道","examples":[{"en":"As you may know, the childcare service runs through the school holidays.","zh":"如你可能知道，托兒服務會在整段學校假期提供。"},{"en":"As you may know is used before mentioning information some listeners may already know.","zh":"as you may know 用於提及部分聽者可能已經知道的資料之前。"},{"en":"As you may know, the library will move to a new building next month.","zh":"如你可能知道，圖書館下個月會搬到新大樓。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds polite because it recognises that not everyone has the same information.","zh":"這個短語聽起來有禮貌，因為它承認不是每個人都有相同資料。"},{"en":"It is often used in talks, emails, and announcements.","zh":"它常用於演講、電郵和公告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"run through","meaning":"貫穿整段……期間提供","examples":[{"en":"The childcare service runs through the school holidays.","zh":"托兒服務貫穿整段學校假期提供。"},{"en":"To run through a period means to continue operating during that whole period.","zh":"run through a period 是指在整段時期中持續運作。"},{"en":"The summer reading programme runs through July and August.","zh":"暑期閱讀計劃在七月和八月期間持續進行。"},{"en":"Services that run through holidays help families when normal routines change.","zh":"在假期持續提供的服務能在日常規律改變時幫助家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continuous operation over a time period.","zh":"這個短語描述在一段時間內持續運作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"school holidays","meaning":"學校假期","examples":[{"en":"The childcare service is available during the school holidays.","zh":"托兒服務在學校假期期間可供使用。"},{"en":"School holidays are periods when schools are closed and regular lessons stop.","zh":"school holidays 是學校關閉、正常課堂暫停的時期。"},{"en":"Parents may need childcare during school holidays because work continues.","zh":"家長可能在學校假期需要托兒服務，因為工作仍然繼續。"},{"en":"Holiday childcare helps children stay safe and active when school is closed.","zh":"假期托兒幫助孩子在學校關閉時保持安全和活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to breaks from school, not public holidays only.","zh":"這個短語指學校休假，不只是公眾假期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"varied and exciting programme","meaning":"多元而有趣的活動安排","examples":[{"en":"The school offers a varied and exciting holiday programme.","zh":"學校提供多元而有趣的假期活動安排。"},{"en":"A varied and exciting programme includes many different interesting activities.","zh":"varied and exciting programme 是包括許多不同有趣活動的安排。"},{"en":"A holiday programme may include sports, cooking, art, music, and trips.","zh":"假期活動安排可能包括運動、烹飪、美術、音樂和外出參觀。"},{"en":"Variety keeps children interested because they are not doing the same thing every day.","zh":"多樣性令孩子保持興趣，因為他們不是每天做同一件事。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the programme is both diverse and enjoyable.","zh":"這個短語表示活動既多元又有趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"keep the children entertained","meaning":"令孩子保持投入和開心","examples":[{"en":"The programme keeps the children entertained during the holidays.","zh":"這個活動安排在假期中令孩子保持投入和開心。"},{"en":"To keep children entertained means to give them enjoyable activities so they do not become bored.","zh":"keep children entertained 是指提供有趣活動，使孩子不會感到沉悶。"},{"en":"Games, crafts, and stories can keep children entertained on a rainy afternoon.","zh":"遊戲、手工和故事可以在下雨的下午令孩子保持開心。"},{"en":"Keeping children entertained helps them stay happy and engaged.","zh":"令孩子保持投入有助他們快樂並專注參與。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on enjoyment and attention, not only supervision.","zh":"這個短語著重樂趣和注意力，而不只是看管。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"feel as if","meaning":"感覺好像……","examples":[{"en":"The school does not want children to feel as if they are still at school.","zh":"學校不想孩子感覺好像仍然在上學。"},{"en":"To feel as if something is true means to have the impression that it is true.","zh":"feel as if something is true 是指有某事似乎真實的感覺。"},{"en":"After a long meeting, workers may feel as if they have no energy left.","zh":"漫長會議後，員工可能感覺好像已沒有精力。"},{"en":"Holiday programmes should feel different from normal lessons so children can relax.","zh":"假期活動應與正常課堂感覺不同，讓孩子可以放鬆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes perception or feeling, not necessarily fact.","zh":"這個短語描述感覺或印象，不一定是事實。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get the chance to","meaning":"有機會……","examples":[{"en":"Children get the chance to make new friends.","zh":"孩子有機會交新朋友。"},{"en":"To get the chance to do something means to have an opportunity to do it.","zh":"get the chance to do something 是指有機會做某事。"},{"en":"Students may get the chance to perform on stage during the school concert.","zh":"學生可能在學校音樂會中有機會上台表演。"},{"en":"Having chances to try new activities helps children build confidence.","zh":"有機會嘗試新活動可以幫助孩子建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an opportunity that benefits the person.","zh":"這個短語表示對當事人有好處的機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make new friends","meaning":"交新朋友","examples":[{"en":"Children can make new friends with children from other schools.","zh":"孩子可以與來自其他學校的孩子交新朋友。"},{"en":"To make new friends means to form friendships with people you did not know before.","zh":"make new friends 是指與以前不認識的人建立友誼。"},{"en":"A child may make new friends at a sports club or holiday camp.","zh":"孩子可能在運動會或假期營中交新朋友。"},{"en":"Making new friends helps children feel less nervous in unfamiliar places.","zh":"交新朋友幫助孩子在陌生地方感到不那麼緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on building social relationships.","zh":"這個短語著重建立社交關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"children from other schools","meaning":"來自其他學校的孩子","examples":[{"en":"The holiday service includes children from other schools.","zh":"假期服務包括來自其他學校的孩子。"},{"en":"Children from other schools are pupils who normally attend different schools.","zh":"children from other schools 是平時就讀不同學校的學生。"},{"en":"A sports tournament may bring together children from other schools.","zh":"運動比賽可能把來自其他學校的孩子聚在一起。"},{"en":"Mixing with children from other schools helps children widen their social circle.","zh":"與其他學校的孩子相處，有助孩子擴闊社交圈。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the service is not limited to one school’s pupils.","zh":"這個短語顯示服務不限於本校學生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spaces are available","meaning":"有名額","examples":[{"en":"Spaces are available during the school holidays.","zh":"學校假期期間有名額。"},{"en":"Spaces are available means there are places or vacancies that people can book or use.","zh":"spaces are available 是指仍有可預訂或使用的位置或空缺。"},{"en":"A swimming class may still have spaces available for beginners.","zh":"游泳班可能仍有初學者名額。"},{"en":"If spaces are available, more families can join the service.","zh":"如果有名額，更多家庭可以加入服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in bookings, courses, clubs, and childcare.","zh":"這個短語常用於預訂、課程、學會和托兒服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"term-time children","meaning":"學期期間參加托兒服務的孩子","examples":[{"en":"Many term-time children do not attend during the holidays.","zh":"許多學期期間參加托兒服務的孩子在假期不參加。"},{"en":"Term-time children are children who attend a service during the normal school term.","zh":"term-time children 是在正常學期期間使用服務的孩子。"},{"en":"Some term-time children may stay with relatives during school holidays.","zh":"有些學期期間參加服務的孩子可能在學校假期與親戚一起。"},{"en":"If term-time children do not attend holidays, spaces become available for others.","zh":"如果這些孩子假期不參加，其他人便會有名額。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts normal school weeks with holiday periods.","zh":"這個短語把正常上課週與假期作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"over the age of","meaning":"超過……歲","examples":[{"en":"Some parents ask whether children over the age of 11 can attend.","zh":"有些家長詢問超過11歲的孩子是否可以參加。"},{"en":"Over the age of means older than a particular age.","zh":"over the age of 是指年齡大於某個指定歲數。"},{"en":"Children over the age of twelve may need an adult ticket on some buses.","zh":"在某些巴士上，超過12歲的孩子可能需要成人票。"},{"en":"Age rules matter because activities and insurance may be designed for certain ages.","zh":"年齡規則很重要，因為活動和保險可能只為某些年齡設計。"},{"en":"This phrase sets an age boundary.","zh":"這個短語設定年齡界線。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be allowed to","meaning":"被允許……","examples":[{"en":"Children over 11 are not allowed to attend the service.","zh":"超過11歲的孩子不被允許參加這項服務。"},{"en":"To be allowed to do something means to have permission to do it.","zh":"be allowed to do something 是指有許可去做某事。"},{"en":"Students may be allowed to use calculators in some exams.","zh":"學生可能在某些考試中被允許使用計算機。"},{"en":"If someone is not allowed to join, there may be rules or safety reasons behind it.","zh":"如果某人不被允許加入，背後可能有規則或安全原因。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on permission.","zh":"這個短語著重許可。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"younger brothers and sisters","meaning":"弟妹","examples":[{"en":"Older children cannot attend with their younger brothers and sisters.","zh":"年紀較大的孩子不能與弟妹一起參加。"},{"en":"Younger brothers and sisters means younger siblings in the same family.","zh":"younger brothers and sisters 是指同一家庭中年紀較小的兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"A child may walk to school with younger brothers and sisters.","zh":"孩子可能與弟妹一起步行上學。"},{"en":"Older children may want to stay with siblings, but age rules may not allow it.","zh":"年長孩子可能想與弟妹一起留下，但年齡規則可能不容許。"},{"en":"This phrase is family language for younger siblings.","zh":"這個短語是指家庭中的年幼兄弟姊妹。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"I’m afraid","meaning":"很抱歉","examples":[{"en":"I’m afraid the service cannot accept children over 11.","zh":"很抱歉，這項服務不能接受超過11歲的孩子。"},{"en":"I’m afraid is a polite way to introduce disappointing or negative information.","zh":"I’m afraid 是禮貌地引入令人失望或負面的資料。"},{"en":"I’m afraid the class is full, so we cannot take more students.","zh":"很抱歉，這班已滿，所以我們不能收更多學生。"},{"en":"This phrase softens refusal or bad news.","zh":"這個短語令拒絕或壞消息較委婉。"},{"en":"It does not usually mean the speaker is frightened.","zh":"它通常不是指說話者感到害怕。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be unable to","meaning":"不能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The school is unable to accept children over 11.","zh":"學校不能夠接受超過11歲的孩子。"},{"en":"To be unable to do something means to not be able to do it.","zh":"be unable to do something 是指不能做某事。"},{"en":"The clinic is unable to offer appointments today because all doctors are busy.","zh":"診所今天不能提供預約，因為所有醫生都很忙。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and polite when explaining limits.","zh":"這個短語在解釋限制時較正式和有禮貌。"},{"en":"It often suggests the problem is due to rules, capacity, or circumstances.","zh":"它常暗示問題源於規則、容量或情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"because of","meaning":"因為……","examples":[{"en":"The school cannot accept older children because of its insurance.","zh":"學校因為保險而不能接受年紀較大的孩子。"},{"en":"Because of introduces the reason for something.","zh":"because of 用來引入某事的原因。"},{"en":"The picnic was cancelled because of heavy rain.","zh":"野餐因為大雨而取消。"},{"en":"Rules may exist because of safety, cost, or legal reasons.","zh":"規則可能因為安全、成本或法律原因而存在。"},{"en":"This phrase is followed by a noun phrase, not a full sentence.","zh":"這個短語後面接名詞短語，而不是完整句子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"type of insurance","meaning":"保險類型","examples":[{"en":"The type of insurance prevents the service from accepting children over 11.","zh":"這種保險類型令服務不能接受超過11歲的孩子。"},{"en":"Type of insurance means the particular kind of insurance cover a service has.","zh":"type of insurance 是指服務所擁有的特定保險保障類別。"},{"en":"A sports club may need a special type of insurance for high-risk activities.","zh":"運動會可能需要特別保險類型來涵蓋高風險活動。"},{"en":"Insurance type can limit what an organisation is allowed to provide.","zh":"保險類型可以限制機構可提供甚麼服務。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a service may have rules about age or activities.","zh":"這個短語解釋服務為何可能有年齡或活動規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"let me tell you about","meaning":"讓我向你介紹……","examples":[{"en":"Mrs Carter tells parents about the afterschool activities.","zh":"Carter 太太向家長介紹課後活動。"},{"en":"Let me tell you about is used to introduce information the speaker wants to explain.","zh":"let me tell you about 用來引入說話者想解釋的資料。"},{"en":"Let me tell you about the new library rules before you borrow books.","zh":"讓我向你介紹新的圖書館規則，然後你再借書。"},{"en":"This phrase guides listeners to a new topic.","zh":"這個短語引導聽者進入新主題。"},{"en":"It sounds friendly and organised in a talk or presentation.","zh":"它在演講或介紹中聽起來友善而有條理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"afterschool sessions","meaning":"課後時段","examples":[{"en":"Children can join different activities during the afterschool sessions.","zh":"孩子可以在課後時段參加不同活動。"},{"en":"Afterschool sessions are periods after normal lessons when children stay for care or activities.","zh":"afterschool sessions 是正常課堂後孩子留下接受照顧或參加活動的時段。"},{"en":"An afterschool session may include sports, homework help, music, or art.","zh":"課後時段可能包括運動、功課支援、音樂或美術。"},{"en":"These sessions help children use the time before parents collect them.","zh":"這些時段幫助孩子善用家長接走前的時間。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to structured time after the school day.","zh":"這個短語指上課日後的有組織時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"Children can use the playground as well as the computers and library.","zh":"孩子除了可以使用電腦和圖書館外，也可以使用遊樂場。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to something else.","zh":"as well as 是指除了某物之外，還有另一物。"},{"en":"The centre offers dance classes as well as homework support.","zh":"中心除了提供功課支援外，也提供舞蹈課。"},{"en":"This phrase adds extra information and shows there is more than one option.","zh":"這個短語加入額外資料，顯示不止一個選項。"},{"en":"It is useful when listing services, facilities, or activities.","zh":"它適合用於列出服務、設施或活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"playground equipment","meaning":"遊樂場設施","examples":[{"en":"Children can use the playground equipment after school.","zh":"孩子放學後可以使用遊樂場設施。"},{"en":"Playground equipment means structures children play on, such as swings, slides, and climbing frames.","zh":"playground equipment 是孩子用來玩的設施，例如鞦韆、滑梯和攀爬架。"},{"en":"Safe playground equipment gives children space to move, climb, and play.","zh":"安全的遊樂場設施給孩子活動、攀爬和玩耍的空間。"},{"en":"Staff need to supervise playground equipment to reduce accidents.","zh":"職員需要監督遊樂場設施，以減少意外。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to physical play facilities.","zh":"這個短語指實體遊樂設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at least one","meaning":"至少一個","examples":[{"en":"There is usually at least one special activity each day.","zh":"通常每天至少有一個特別活動。"},{"en":"At least one means one or more, but not zero.","zh":"at least one 是指一個或以上，不是零個。"},{"en":"Each group should have at least one adult supervisor.","zh":"每組應至少有一名成人監督。"},{"en":"Saying “at least one” guarantees a minimum number.","zh":"說 at least one 表示保證最低數量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining basic provision or requirements.","zh":"這個短語適合用於解釋基本提供內容或要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"special activity","meaning":"特別活動","examples":[{"en":"Children can usually do one special activity each day.","zh":"孩子通常每天可以做一項特別活動。"},{"en":"A special activity is an organised activity that is different from ordinary free play or routine care.","zh":"special activity 是與普通自由玩耍或日常照顧不同的有組織活動。"},{"en":"Cooking, Spanish, yoga, or painting can be special activities after school.","zh":"烹飪、西班牙語、瑜伽或繪畫都可以是課後特別活動。"},{"en":"Special activities make childcare more interesting and educational.","zh":"特別活動令托兒服務更有趣和有教育意義。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an added feature in the programme.","zh":"這個短語表示活動安排中的額外特色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"specialist teacher","meaning":"專科老師","examples":[{"en":"A specialist teacher comes in every Thursday.","zh":"每逢星期四會有一位專科老師到場。"},{"en":"A specialist teacher is a teacher with particular knowledge or training in one subject or skill.","zh":"specialist teacher 是在某一科目或技能上有特別知識或訓練的老師。"},{"en":"A music specialist teacher may teach instruments better than a general classroom teacher.","zh":"音樂專科老師可能比普通班主任更適合教授樂器。"},{"en":"Specialist teachers help children learn skills that regular staff may not be trained to teach.","zh":"專科老師幫助孩子學習一般職員未必受訓教授的技能。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights professional subject expertise.","zh":"這個短語突出專業科目知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"come in","meaning":"來到；到場","examples":[{"en":"A specialist teacher comes in to teach Spanish.","zh":"一位專科老師會到場教授西班牙語。"},{"en":"To come in means to come to a place, often from outside the organisation, to do a job or activity.","zh":"come in 是指來到某地，通常從機構外部前來做工作或活動。"},{"en":"A dance teacher may come in once a week to teach a class.","zh":"舞蹈老師可能每週到場一次教課。"},{"en":"Bringing in outside teachers can add skills the school does not have every day.","zh":"請外來老師到場可以加入學校日常沒有的技能。"},{"en":"This phrase often means arriving to provide a service.","zh":"這個短語常指前來提供服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"give a basic introduction to","meaning":"對……作基本介紹","examples":[{"en":"The teacher gives a basic introduction to Spanish.","zh":"老師對西班牙語作基本介紹。"},{"en":"To give a basic introduction to a subject means to teach the first simple ideas about it.","zh":"give a basic introduction to a subject 是指教授某主題最初步的簡單概念。"},{"en":"A librarian may give a basic introduction to using the online catalogue.","zh":"圖書館員可能對使用網上目錄作基本介紹。"},{"en":"Basic introductions help beginners feel less nervous before learning more.","zh":"基本介紹幫助初學者在進一步學習前沒那麼緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase means starting with simple foundations, not advanced detail.","zh":"這個短語表示從簡單基礎開始，而不是高階細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"through games and songs","meaning":"透過遊戲和歌曲","examples":[{"en":"The teacher introduces Spanish through games and songs.","zh":"老師透過遊戲和歌曲介紹西班牙語。"},{"en":"Through games and songs means by using games and songs as the method of teaching or learning.","zh":"through games and songs 是指用遊戲和歌曲作為教學或學習方法。"},{"en":"Young children often learn new words through games and songs.","zh":"年幼孩子常透過遊戲和歌曲學新詞。"},{"en":"Games and songs make learning enjoyable and help children remember language.","zh":"遊戲和歌曲令學習有趣，並幫助孩子記住語言。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the method used to teach something.","zh":"這個短語解釋教授某事所用的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"do two sessions","meaning":"開兩節課","examples":[{"en":"The Spanish teacher does two sessions every Thursday.","zh":"西班牙語老師每逢星期四開兩節課。"},{"en":"To do two sessions means to run or teach two separate periods of an activity.","zh":"do two sessions 是指開辦或教授兩個分開的活動時段。"},{"en":"A swimming coach may do two sessions on Saturday morning for different age groups.","zh":"游泳教練可能在星期六早上為不同年齡組開兩節課。"},{"en":"Running two sessions helps organisers separate children by age or ability.","zh":"開兩節課有助組織者按年齡或能力分組。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the number of activity periods.","zh":"這個短語著重活動時段的數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the over 8s","meaning":"8歲以上的孩子","examples":[{"en":"One Spanish session is for the over 8s.","zh":"其中一節西班牙語課是給8歲以上的孩子。"},{"en":"The over 8s means children older than eight years old.","zh":"the over 8s 是指8歲以上的孩子。"},{"en":"A sports club may offer a harder class for the over 8s.","zh":"運動會可能為8歲以上的孩子提供較難的班。"},{"en":"Older children may need different activities because their attention and skills are more developed.","zh":"年紀較大的孩子可能需要不同活動，因為他們的專注力和技能較成熟。"},{"en":"This phrase groups children by age.","zh":"這個短語按年齡把孩子分組。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"younger children","meaning":"年紀較小的孩子","examples":[{"en":"The other Spanish session is for younger children.","zh":"另一節西班牙語課是給年紀較小的孩子。"},{"en":"Younger children are children who are smaller or lower in age than another group.","zh":"younger children 是指比另一組年齡較低或較小的孩子。"},{"en":"Younger children may need shorter activities with more songs and movement.","zh":"年紀較小的孩子可能需要較短活動，並加入更多歌曲和動作。"},{"en":"Activities for younger children should be simple, safe, and easy to follow.","zh":"給年紀較小孩子的活動應簡單、安全、容易跟隨。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one age group with older children.","zh":"這個短語把一個年齡組與較年長孩子作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make an extra charge for","meaning":"就……額外收費","examples":[{"en":"Spanish is the only activity that the school makes an extra charge for.","zh":"西班牙語是學校唯一額外收費的活動。"},{"en":"To make an extra charge for something means to ask people to pay an additional fee for it.","zh":"make an extra charge for something 是指要求人們為某事支付額外費用。"},{"en":"A hotel may make an extra charge for breakfast or parking.","zh":"酒店可能就早餐或泊車額外收費。"},{"en":"Extra charges may be needed when an activity uses outside teachers or special materials.","zh":"當活動使用外來老師或特殊材料時，可能需要額外收費。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a cost beyond the normal fee.","zh":"這個短語突出正常費用以外的成本。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be well worth it","meaning":"非常值得","examples":[{"en":"The Spanish activity costs extra, but it is well worth it.","zh":"西班牙語活動需要額外收費，但非常值得。"},{"en":"To be well worth it means the benefit is good enough to justify the cost or effort.","zh":"be well worth it 是指好處足以令成本或努力合理。"},{"en":"A long journey may be well worth it if the museum is excellent.","zh":"如果博物館非常出色，長途旅程可能非常值得。"},{"en":"People accept extra cost when they feel the experience is well worth it.","zh":"當人們覺得體驗非常值得，便會接受額外成本。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strong positive judgement about value.","zh":"這個短語對價值作出強烈正面評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"once a week","meaning":"每星期一次","examples":[{"en":"The children have the opportunity to do music once a week.","zh":"孩子每星期一次有機會學音樂。"},{"en":"Once a week means one time every week.","zh":"once a week 是指每星期一次。"},{"en":"A student may meet a tutor once a week for extra reading practice.","zh":"學生可能每星期一次與導師進行額外閱讀練習。"},{"en":"Weekly activities create routine without taking up every day.","zh":"每週活動可以建立規律，而不佔用每天時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequency.","zh":"這個短語描述頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have the opportunity to","meaning":"有機會……","examples":[{"en":"Children have the opportunity to do music.","zh":"孩子有機會學音樂。"},{"en":"To have the opportunity to do something means to have the chance to do it.","zh":"have the opportunity to do something 是指有機會做某事。"},{"en":"Students may have the opportunity to visit a science museum during the term.","zh":"學生可能在學期中有機會參觀科學博物館。"},{"en":"Opportunities help children discover interests they might not find at home.","zh":"機會幫助孩子發現他們在家未必會接觸到的興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds slightly more formal than “get the chance to”.","zh":"這個短語比 get the chance to 稍正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be lucky that","meaning":"很幸運……","examples":[{"en":"The school is lucky that one staff member plays in a folk band.","zh":"學校很幸運，因為一名職員在民謠樂隊中演奏。"},{"en":"To be lucky that means to benefit from a fortunate situation.","zh":"be lucky that 是指因有幸遇到某情況而受益。"},{"en":"We are lucky that the library is close to the school.","zh":"我們很幸運，因為圖書館就在學校附近。"},{"en":"A school may offer better activities when staff happen to have useful skills.","zh":"當職員剛好有有用技能，學校可能提供更好的活動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows appreciation for a helpful circumstance.","zh":"這個短語表示對有利情況的感謝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a member of","meaning":"……的一員","examples":[{"en":"One staff member is a member of a folk band.","zh":"一名職員是民謠樂隊的一員。"},{"en":"A member of a group means someone who belongs to that group.","zh":"a member of a group 是指屬於某個群體的人。"},{"en":"A student may be a member of the school choir.","zh":"學生可能是學校合唱團的一員。"},{"en":"Being a member of a group often means taking part regularly.","zh":"作為團體的一員通常意味定期參與。"},{"en":"This phrase shows belonging or participation.","zh":"這個短語表示歸屬或參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"folk band","meaning":"民謠樂隊","examples":[{"en":"One member of staff plays in a folk band.","zh":"一名職員在民謠樂隊中演奏。"},{"en":"A folk band is a music group that plays traditional or folk-style music.","zh":"folk band 是演奏傳統或民謠風格音樂的樂隊。"},{"en":"A folk band may use guitars, fiddles, drums, and simple singing.","zh":"民謠樂隊可能使用結他、小提琴、鼓和簡單歌唱。"},{"en":"Folk music can introduce children to local traditions and storytelling.","zh":"民謠音樂可以向孩子介紹本地傳統和故事。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a group of musicians, not a school class.","zh":"這個短語指一群音樂人，而不是學校課堂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"percussion","meaning":"敲擊樂","examples":[{"en":"Children learn singing and percussion on Mondays.","zh":"孩子星期一學唱歌和敲擊樂。"},{"en":"Percussion means musical instruments played by hitting, shaking, or tapping them.","zh":"percussion 是透過敲打、搖動或拍打來演奏的樂器類別。"},{"en":"Drums, tambourines, and shakers are percussion instruments.","zh":"鼓、鈴鼓和沙槌都是敲擊樂器。"},{"en":"Percussion is useful for children because it teaches rhythm through movement.","zh":"敲擊樂對孩子有用，因為它透過動作教授節奏。"},{"en":"This word refers to a type of music instrument and playing method.","zh":"這個詞指一類樂器和演奏方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rely on","meaning":"依靠……","examples":[{"en":"The school relies on parental support for the music sessions.","zh":"學校在音樂課方面依靠家長支援。"},{"en":"To rely on something means to need or depend on it in order to succeed.","zh":"rely on something 是指需要或依靠某物才能成功。"},{"en":"A small charity may rely on volunteers to run weekend activities.","zh":"小型慈善機構可能依靠義工營運週末活動。"},{"en":"If a service relies on help from parents, it may not work well without them.","zh":"如果服務依靠家長幫忙，沒有他們可能無法順利運作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows dependence.","zh":"這個短語顯示依賴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"parental support","meaning":"家長支援","examples":[{"en":"The music activity relies on parental support.","zh":"音樂活動依靠家長支援。"},{"en":"Parental support means help, encouragement, or involvement from parents.","zh":"parental support 是來自家長的幫助、鼓勵或參與。"},{"en":"Parental support can include attending meetings, helping at events, or practising with children at home.","zh":"家長支援可以包括出席會議、協助活動或在家陪孩子練習。"},{"en":"Activities often improve when parents support them with time or skills.","zh":"當家長以時間或技能支持活動，活動通常會更好。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to parents’ active help, not only paying fees.","zh":"這個短語指家長主動幫忙，而不只是付費。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"play an instrument","meaning":"演奏樂器","examples":[{"en":"Parents who sing or play an instrument can help with music sessions.","zh":"會唱歌或演奏樂器的家長可以幫忙音樂課。"},{"en":"To play an instrument means to make music using a musical instrument.","zh":"play an instrument 是指使用樂器演奏音樂。"},{"en":"A child may learn to play an instrument such as the piano, violin, or drums.","zh":"孩子可能學習演奏鋼琴、小提琴或鼓等樂器。"},{"en":"People who play instruments can support music activities by teaching rhythm or melody.","zh":"會演奏樂器的人可以透過教授節奏或旋律支援音樂活動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to musical skill.","zh":"這個短語指音樂技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be prepared to","meaning":"願意……","examples":[{"en":"Parents may be prepared to help out at the sessions.","zh":"家長可能願意在課堂中幫忙。"},{"en":"To be prepared to do something means to be willing and ready to do it.","zh":"be prepared to do something 是指願意並準備好做某事。"},{"en":"A neighbour may be prepared to feed your cat while you are away.","zh":"你外出時，鄰居可能願意幫你餵貓。"},{"en":"People are more prepared to help when they know what is expected.","zh":"當人們知道期望是甚麼時，他們會更願意幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests willingness, not force.","zh":"這個短語表示意願，而不是被迫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"help out","meaning":"幫忙","examples":[{"en":"Parents can help out at the music sessions.","zh":"家長可以在音樂課中幫忙。"},{"en":"To help out means to give practical assistance.","zh":"help out 是指提供實際協助。"},{"en":"Students may help out at a school fair by selling tickets.","zh":"學生可能透過售票在學校市集中幫忙。"},{"en":"Helping out reduces pressure on staff and makes activities run more smoothly.","zh":"幫忙可以減輕職員壓力，令活動運作更順暢。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds friendly and informal.","zh":"這個短語聽起來友善而較口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at these sessions","meaning":"在這些課堂中","examples":[{"en":"Parents can help out at these music sessions.","zh":"家長可以在這些音樂課中幫忙。"},{"en":"At these sessions means during these particular classes or activity periods.","zh":"at these sessions 是指在這些特定課堂或活動時段中。"},{"en":"Volunteers at these sessions help children set up instruments and tidy the room.","zh":"這些課堂中的義工會幫孩子準備樂器和整理房間。"},{"en":"Help at specific sessions can be easier to organise than general help.","zh":"在指定課堂中幫忙，可能比一般性幫忙更容易安排。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to the sessions already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語回指前面提到的課堂時段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"we’d be delighted","meaning":"我們會非常高興","examples":[{"en":"The school would be delighted if parents helped with music.","zh":"如果家長能幫忙音樂活動，學校會非常高興。"},{"en":"We’d be delighted means we would be very pleased or happy.","zh":"we’d be delighted 是指我們會非常高興。"},{"en":"We’d be delighted if you could join us for the open day.","zh":"如果你能參加開放日，我們會非常高興。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and warm when inviting help or participation.","zh":"這個短語在邀請幫忙或參與時有禮而溫暖。"},{"en":"It expresses stronger happiness than simply saying “that would be fine”.","zh":"它比單純說 that would be fine 表達更強的高興。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"continue to be","meaning":"繼續是……","examples":[{"en":"Painting continues to be one of the most popular activities.","zh":"繪畫繼續是最受歡迎的活動之一。"},{"en":"Continue to be means remain in the same state over time.","zh":"continue to be 是指隨時間仍然保持同一狀態。"},{"en":"Reading continues to be important even when students use more technology.","zh":"即使學生使用更多科技，閱讀仍然繼續重要。"},{"en":"Something continues to be popular when people keep choosing it again and again.","zh":"當人們一次又一次選擇某事，它便繼續受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a situation has not changed.","zh":"這個短語顯示情況沒有改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one of the most popular activities","meaning":"最受歡迎的活動之一","examples":[{"en":"Painting is one of the most popular activities.","zh":"繪畫是最受歡迎的活動之一。"},{"en":"One of the most popular activities means an activity many people choose or enjoy.","zh":"one of the most popular activities 是指許多人選擇或喜歡的活動之一。"},{"en":"Football is one of the most popular activities at many schools.","zh":"足球在許多學校是最受歡迎的活動之一。"},{"en":"Popular activities usually attract more children and need more resources.","zh":"受歡迎的活動通常吸引更多孩子，並需要更多資源。"},{"en":"This phrase puts an activity among the top favourites, not necessarily number one.","zh":"這個短語表示該活動屬於最受喜愛之一，不一定是第一名。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"to begin with","meaning":"起初","examples":[{"en":"To begin with, the school was not keen on offering painting.","zh":"起初，學校不太熱衷於提供繪畫活動。"},{"en":"To begin with means at the start or in the beginning.","zh":"to begin with 是指最初或一開始。"},{"en":"To begin with, the new timetable confused many students.","zh":"起初，新的時間表令許多學生感到混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the early situation with what happened later.","zh":"這個短語把早期情況與後來發展作對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing how opinions or plans changed.","zh":"當描述意見或計劃如何改變時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be keen on","meaning":"熱衷於；喜歡","examples":[{"en":"The school was not keen on offering painting at first.","zh":"學校起初不太熱衷於提供繪畫活動。"},{"en":"To be keen on something means to like it or be enthusiastic about it.","zh":"be keen on something 是指喜歡某事或對它有熱情。"},{"en":"A child who is keen on football may practise every weekend.","zh":"熱衷於足球的孩子可能每週末練習。"},{"en":"If someone is not keen on an idea, they may worry about problems it creates.","zh":"如果某人不太熱衷於一個想法，他可能擔心它帶來的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is softer than saying someone loves or hates something.","zh":"這個短語比說非常愛或非常討厭更柔和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"extra mess involved","meaning":"額外造成的混亂","examples":[{"en":"The school worried about the extra mess involved in painting.","zh":"學校擔心繪畫會額外造成混亂。"},{"en":"Extra mess involved means the additional dirt, disorder, or cleaning caused by an activity.","zh":"extra mess involved 是指某活動帶來額外污糟、混亂或清潔工作。"},{"en":"Cooking with young children can mean extra mess involved in the kitchen.","zh":"與年幼孩子一起烹飪可能會令廚房額外混亂。"},{"en":"Messy activities need planning because staff must clean up afterwards.","zh":"混亂的活動需要規劃，因為職員之後必須清理。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a practical reason for hesitation.","zh":"這個短語解釋猶豫的實際原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"keep asking if","meaning":"不斷詢問是否……","examples":[{"en":"Children kept asking if they could do art.","zh":"孩子不斷詢問是否可以做美術活動。"},{"en":"To keep asking if means to ask the same question repeatedly.","zh":"keep asking if 是指反覆問同一個是否問題。"},{"en":"Children may keep asking if they can go outside when the rain stops.","zh":"雨停後，孩子可能不斷問是否可以出去。"},{"en":"Repeated questions can show strong interest or impatience.","zh":"反覆提問可以顯示強烈興趣或不耐煩。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the request happened many times.","zh":"這個短語表示請求發生了很多次。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"do some art","meaning":"做美術活動","examples":[{"en":"Children kept asking if they could do some art.","zh":"孩子不斷詢問是否可以做美術活動。"},{"en":"To do some art means to take part in creative activities such as drawing, painting, or making things.","zh":"do some art 是指參與繪畫、畫畫或製作物品等創意活動。"},{"en":"Children may do some art after school to relax and express ideas.","zh":"孩子放學後可能做美術活動來放鬆和表達想法。"},{"en":"Art activities help children use imagination and practise hand skills.","zh":"美術活動幫助孩子使用想像力和練習手部技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase is general and can include many kinds of creative work.","zh":"這個短語很籠統，可以包括很多種創作活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"give in","meaning":"讓步","examples":[{"en":"The children kept asking for art, so the school finally gave in.","zh":"孩子不斷要求做美術，所以學校最後讓步。"},{"en":"To give in means to stop resisting and agree to what someone wants.","zh":"give in 是指停止抗拒並同意別人想要的事。"},{"en":"A parent may give in after a child asks many times for a bedtime story.","zh":"孩子多次要求睡前故事後，家長可能會讓步。"},{"en":"People give in when pressure, repeated requests, or persuasion changes their mind.","zh":"當壓力、反覆要求或說服改變人的想法，他們便會讓步。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a reluctant agreement.","zh":"這個短語表示不太情願的同意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be great for","meaning":"很適合用來……","examples":[{"en":"Art is great for helping children relax.","zh":"美術很適合用來幫助孩子放鬆。"},{"en":"To be great for something means to be very useful or suitable for that purpose.","zh":"be great for something 是指對某目的非常有用或合適。"},{"en":"Swimming is great for exercise because it uses the whole body.","zh":"游泳很適合用來運動，因為它會用到全身。"},{"en":"A quiet reading corner is great for children who need calm after a busy day.","zh":"安靜閱讀角很適合忙碌一天後需要平靜的孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a positive practical judgement.","zh":"這個短語給出正面的實用評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"relax after","meaning":"在……之後放鬆","examples":[{"en":"Art helps children relax after working hard at school.","zh":"美術幫助孩子在學校努力學習後放鬆。"},{"en":"To relax after something means to rest and feel calmer following an activity or effort.","zh":"relax after something 是指在某活動或努力之後休息並變得較平靜。"},{"en":"Students may relax after exams by watching a film or playing sport.","zh":"學生可能在考試後透過看電影或做運動放鬆。"},{"en":"Relaxing after hard work helps people recover energy.","zh":"努力後放鬆有助人恢復精力。"},{"en":"This phrase connects rest with what happened before it.","zh":"這個短語把休息與之前發生的事連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"work hard at school","meaning":"在學校努力學習","examples":[{"en":"The children work hard at school all day.","zh":"孩子整天在學校努力學習。"},{"en":"To work hard at school means to put effort into lessons, tasks, and learning.","zh":"work hard at school 是指在課堂、任務和學習上付出努力。"},{"en":"A child who works hard at school may feel tired by the afternoon.","zh":"在學校努力學習的孩子到下午可能會感到疲累。"},{"en":"Working hard helps children learn, but they also need time to rest.","zh":"努力學習幫助孩子進步，但他們也需要休息時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes effort in a school setting.","zh":"這個短語描述在學校環境中的努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"all day","meaning":"一整天","examples":[{"en":"Children need to relax after working hard all day.","zh":"孩子努力一整天後需要放鬆。"},{"en":"All day means for the whole day or for a very long part of the day.","zh":"all day 是指整天或一天中很長一段時間。"},{"en":"A teacher may be tired after standing and teaching all day.","zh":"老師站着教了一整天後可能很疲累。"},{"en":"Doing something all day can make people need rest and variety.","zh":"一整天做同一件事會令人需要休息和變化。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises duration.","zh":"這個短語強調持續時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have been meaning to","meaning":"一直想……","examples":[{"en":"The school has been meaning to introduce yoga for some time.","zh":"學校一段時間以來一直想引入瑜伽。"},{"en":"To have been meaning to do something means to have intended to do it for a while.","zh":"have been meaning to do something 是指一段時間以來一直打算做某事。"},{"en":"I have been meaning to call my grandmother, but I keep getting busy.","zh":"我一直想打電話給祖母，但總是很忙。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they planned something but have not done it yet.","zh":"人們原本計劃某事但尚未完成時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It often suggests delay despite good intention.","zh":"它常暗示雖有好意但一直延遲。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"introduce","meaning":"引入","examples":[{"en":"The school has wanted to introduce yoga for some time.","zh":"學校一段時間以來想引入瑜伽。"},{"en":"To introduce something means to bring it in or start offering it for the first time.","zh":"introduce something 是指首次帶入或開始提供某事。"},{"en":"A school may introduce coding lessons if students need digital skills.","zh":"如果學生需要數碼技能，學校可能引入編程課。"},{"en":"Introducing a new activity takes planning, staff, and resources.","zh":"引入新活動需要規劃、人手和資源。"},{"en":"This verb is common when a new programme or rule begins.","zh":"當新計劃或規則開始時，這個動詞很常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"for some time","meaning":"一段時間以來","examples":[{"en":"The school has been planning to introduce yoga for some time.","zh":"學校一段時間以來一直計劃引入瑜伽。"},{"en":"For some time means for a while or for a fairly long period.","zh":"for some time 是指一段時間或相當長一段時期。"},{"en":"The community has wanted a new playground for some time.","zh":"社區一段時間以來一直想要新遊樂場。"},{"en":"If something has been planned for some time, people may be waiting for the right opportunity.","zh":"如果某事已計劃一段時間，人們可能正在等待合適機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is less exact than giving a specific date.","zh":"這個短語不像給出具體日期那樣精確。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be available to teach","meaning":"有空教授","examples":[{"en":"The school could not find anyone available to teach yoga.","zh":"學校找不到有空教授瑜伽的人。"},{"en":"To be available to teach means to be free and able to teach at the needed time.","zh":"be available to teach 是指在所需時間有空並能夠授課。"},{"en":"A piano teacher may not be available to teach on weekday afternoons.","zh":"鋼琴老師可能星期日下午沒有空教授。"},{"en":"Activities cannot start if no suitable teacher is available.","zh":"如果沒有合適老師有空，活動便無法開始。"},{"en":"This phrase combines time availability with teaching ability.","zh":"這個短語結合了時間上有空和教學能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"until now","meaning":"直到現在","examples":[{"en":"The school could not find a yoga teacher until now.","zh":"學校直到現在才找到瑜伽老師。"},{"en":"Until now means up to the present moment, but the situation has now changed.","zh":"until now 是指直到目前為止，但情況現在已改變。"},{"en":"The club had no coach until now, so training could not begin.","zh":"學會直到現在才有教練，所以之前不能開始訓練。"},{"en":"This phrase often marks the end of a delay or problem.","zh":"這個短語常標示延誤或問題的結束。"},{"en":"It shows that something was not possible before but is possible now.","zh":"它顯示某事以前不可能，但現在可以。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"see how this goes","meaning":"看看效果如何","examples":[{"en":"The school will see how the yoga activity goes.","zh":"學校會看看瑜伽活動效果如何。"},{"en":"To see how this goes means to try something and observe whether it works well.","zh":"see how this goes 是指嘗試某事並觀察它是否運作良好。"},{"en":"A teacher may test a new seating plan for a week and see how it goes.","zh":"老師可能試行新座位安排一星期，看看效果如何。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the final decision depends on results.","zh":"當最終決定取決於結果時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It suggests a flexible trial rather than a fixed long-term promise.","zh":"它表示彈性試行，而不是固定長期承諾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"benefit in all sorts of ways","meaning":"在各方面受益","examples":[{"en":"Children may benefit from yoga in all sorts of ways.","zh":"孩子可能從瑜伽中在各方面受益。"},{"en":"To benefit in all sorts of ways means to gain many different kinds of advantages.","zh":"benefit in all sorts of ways 是指獲得許多不同類型的好處。"},{"en":"Reading regularly can benefit children in all sorts of ways, from vocabulary to imagination.","zh":"定期閱讀可以令孩子在各方面受益，從詞彙到想像力都有幫助。"},{"en":"Yoga may help children with movement, calmness, balance, and concentration.","zh":"瑜伽可能幫助孩子活動、平靜、平衡和專注。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises wide-ranging benefits.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cooking","meaning":"烹飪","examples":[{"en":"Cooking is another popular activity.","zh":"烹飪是另一項受歡迎的活動。"},{"en":"Cooking means preparing food by mixing, heating, baking, or following a recipe.","zh":"cooking 是指透過混合、加熱、烘焗或跟隨食譜來準備食物。"},{"en":"Children may enjoy cooking because they can make something and then eat it.","zh":"孩子可能喜歡烹飪，因為他們可以製作食物然後吃掉。"},{"en":"Cooking activities teach safety, measuring, teamwork, and patience.","zh":"烹飪活動教授安全、量度、合作和耐性。"},{"en":"This word refers to both the skill and the activity of making food.","zh":"這個詞指製作食物的技能和活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a different sort of","meaning":"不同種類的……","examples":[{"en":"Children make a different sort of cake, pizza or bread each week.","zh":"孩子每星期製作不同種類的蛋糕、薄餅或麵包。"},{"en":"A different sort of something means another type or kind of it.","zh":"a different sort of something 是指另一種類型的某物。"},{"en":"A reading club may choose a different sort of book each month.","zh":"閱讀會可能每月選擇不同種類的書。"},{"en":"Changing the sort of activity keeps children interested.","zh":"改變活動種類可以令孩子保持興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights variety within the same general category.","zh":"這個短語突出同一大類中的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"each week","meaning":"每星期","examples":[{"en":"Children cook a different food each week.","zh":"孩子每星期烹調不同食物。"},{"en":"Each week means every week.","zh":"each week 是指每個星期。"},{"en":"Students receive a new spelling list each week.","zh":"學生每星期收到一份新的串字清單。"},{"en":"Weekly change gives children routine and variety at the same time.","zh":"每週改變同時給孩子規律和多樣性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated timing.","zh":"這個短語描述重複的時間安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"love doing it","meaning":"很喜歡做這件事","examples":[{"en":"The younger children love doing cooking.","zh":"年紀較小的孩子很喜歡烹飪。"},{"en":"To love doing something means to enjoy it very much.","zh":"love doing something 是指非常喜歡做某事。"},{"en":"Some children love doing puzzles because they like solving problems.","zh":"有些孩子很喜歡拼圖，因為他們喜歡解決問題。"},{"en":"When children love doing an activity, they usually join in more actively.","zh":"當孩子很喜歡做某活動，他們通常會更積極參與。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong enjoyment.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈喜愛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the mess was just too much","meaning":"場面實在太混亂","examples":[{"en":"The school found that the mess from cooking was just too much.","zh":"學校發現烹飪造成的混亂實在太多。"},{"en":"The mess was just too much means the disorder or cleaning work became more than people could reasonably handle.","zh":"the mess was just too much 是指混亂或清潔工作超出人們合理處理的程度。"},{"en":"After thirty children used paint, the mess was just too much for one teacher to clean alone.","zh":"三十個孩子用完顏料後，場面可能太混亂，一位老師無法獨自清理。"},{"en":"Too much mess can make an activity unsafe or difficult to repeat.","zh":"太多混亂可能令活動不安全或難以重複進行。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why an enjoyable activity may need limits.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何有趣活動也可能需要限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"restrict something to","meaning":"把……限制於……","examples":[{"en":"The school decided to restrict cooking to the over 8s.","zh":"學校決定把烹飪限制於8歲以上的孩子。"},{"en":"To restrict something to a group means to allow only that group to do or use it.","zh":"restrict something to a group 是指只允許該群體做或使用某事。"},{"en":"A library may restrict computer use to members during busy times.","zh":"圖書館在繁忙時間可能把電腦使用限制於會員。"},{"en":"Restrictions can make activities safer and easier to manage.","zh":"限制可以令活動更安全和更容易管理。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a limit on who can take part.","zh":"這個短語顯示誰可以參與的限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"better able to","meaning":"較有能力……","examples":[{"en":"Older children are better able to clean up after themselves.","zh":"年紀較大的孩子較有能力自己收拾善後。"},{"en":"Better able to do something means having more ability or maturity to do it well.","zh":"better able to do something 是指更有能力或更成熟地做好某事。"},{"en":"Older students are better able to organise their homework without reminders.","zh":"年紀較大的學生較有能力不用提醒也能整理功課。"},{"en":"Children become better able to handle tasks as they grow and practise.","zh":"孩子隨着成長和練習，會較有能力處理任務。"},{"en":"This phrase compares ability between groups or stages.","zh":"這個短語比較不同群體或階段的能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"clean up after themselves","meaning":"自己收拾善後","examples":[{"en":"Older children can clean up after themselves.","zh":"年紀較大的孩子可以自己收拾善後。"},{"en":"To clean up after themselves means to tidy the mess they made without leaving it for others.","zh":"clean up after themselves 是指整理自己造成的混亂，而不是留給別人處理。"},{"en":"Children should clean up after themselves after painting or cooking.","zh":"孩子在繪畫或烹飪後應自己收拾善後。"},{"en":"Cleaning up after themselves teaches responsibility and reduces work for staff.","zh":"自己收拾善後能培養責任感，也減少職員工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when people must tidy their own mess.","zh":"當人們必須整理自己造成的混亂時，常用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 14/task-3":[{"front":"talk to someone about","meaning":"跟某人談……","examples":[{"en":"Holly is there to talk to Dr Green about her work placement.","zh":"Holly到來是為了跟Dr Green談她的工作實習。"},{"en":"To talk to someone about something means to discuss that topic with them.","zh":"talk to someone about某事，意思是跟某人討論該主題。"},{"en":"A student may talk to a tutor about choosing the right course.","zh":"學生可能跟導師談選擇合適課程的事。"},{"en":"Talking to an expert can help people make better decisions.","zh":"跟專家交談可以幫助人作出更好決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when arranging advice, meetings or interviews.","zh":"這個短語常見於安排建議、會議或面談時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"work placement","meaning":"工作實習","examples":[{"en":"Holly has chosen a work placement at Orion Stadium.","zh":"Holly選擇了在Orion Stadium的工作實習。"},{"en":"A work placement is a period of practical work experience arranged as part of study or training.","zh":"work placement是作為學習或培訓一部分而安排的實際工作經驗。"},{"en":"A student may complete a work placement in a hotel to learn about customer service.","zh":"學生可能在酒店完成工作實習，以學習客戶服務。"},{"en":"Work placements help students understand real workplaces before choosing a career.","zh":"工作實習幫助學生在選擇職業前了解真實工作場所。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in education and vocational training.","zh":"這個短語常見於教育和職業培訓。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"isn’t it?","meaning":"對吧？","examples":[{"en":"The tutor says, “It’s Holly, isn’t it?”","zh":"導師說：「你是Holly，對吧？」"},{"en":"Isn’t it? is a question tag used to check whether something is correct.","zh":"isn’t it?是附加問句，用來確認某事是否正確。"},{"en":"This is the right classroom, isn’t it?","zh":"這是正確課室，對吧？"},{"en":"Question tags make statements sound more conversational and less direct.","zh":"附加問句令陳述聽起來更像對話，也較不直接。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when the speaker expects agreement.","zh":"當說話者預期對方同意時，常會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"choose a work placement","meaning":"選擇工作實習","examples":[{"en":"The tutor asks Holly which work placement she has chosen.","zh":"導師問Holly選擇了哪個工作實習。"},{"en":"To choose a work placement means to select one practical training opportunity from several options.","zh":"choose a work placement意思是從幾個實習機會中選擇一個。"},{"en":"Students may choose a work placement based on their interests and career plans.","zh":"學生可能根據興趣和職業計劃選擇工作實習。"},{"en":"Choosing a placement carefully can help students gain useful experience.","zh":"仔細選擇實習可以幫助學生獲得有用經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important study-related decision.","zh":"這個短語描述與學業相關的重要決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"decide to go for","meaning":"決定選擇……","examples":[{"en":"Holly decided to go for the Orion Stadium placement.","zh":"Holly決定選擇Orion Stadium實習項目。"},{"en":"To decide to go for something means to choose it after considering the options.","zh":"decide to go for某事，意思是在考慮選項後選擇它。"},{"en":"A student may decide to go for the marketing internship because it matches her skills.","zh":"學生可能因市場推廣實習符合自己的技能而決定選擇它。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often used when talking about choices.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常用於談論選擇。"},{"en":"It suggests the person has made a clear decision.","zh":"它暗示某人已作出清楚決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Orion Stadium placement","meaning":"Orion Stadium 實習項目","examples":[{"en":"Holly chose the Orion Stadium placement for her work experience.","zh":"Holly選擇Orion Stadium實習項目作為工作經驗。"},{"en":"The Orion Stadium placement is the specific work placement based at Orion Stadium.","zh":"the Orion Stadium placement是指位於Orion Stadium的特定工作實習。"},{"en":"A stadium placement may involve event planning, safety checks and working with visitors.","zh":"體育場實習可能涉及活動策劃、安全檢查和接待訪客。"},{"en":"Naming the placement clearly helps the tutor know which opportunity Holly means.","zh":"清楚說出實習項目名稱，有助導師知道Holly指哪個機會。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies one particular placement option.","zh":"這個短語指出一個特定實習選項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the event I’ll be managing","meaning":"我將負責管理的活動","examples":[{"en":"The event Holly will be managing is a sports competition.","zh":"Holly將負責管理的活動是一項體育比賽。"},{"en":"The event I’ll be managing means the event I will be responsible for organising or running.","zh":"the event I’ll be managing意思是我將負責籌辦或運作的活動。"},{"en":"A student may say, “The event I’ll be managing is the school charity fair.”","zh":"學生可能說：「我將負責管理的活動是學校慈善賣物會。」"},{"en":"Managing an event involves planning, safety, staff and timing.","zh":"管理活動涉及策劃、安全、人手和時間安排。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the specific event under someone’s responsibility.","zh":"這個短語介紹某人負責的特定活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"help to set up","meaning":"協助籌辦；協助設立","examples":[{"en":"Holly will help to set up a sports competition for children.","zh":"Holly會協助籌辦一項兒童體育比賽。"},{"en":"To help to set up something means to assist in preparing, organising or arranging it.","zh":"help to set up某事，意思是協助準備、組織或安排它。"},{"en":"Volunteers may help to set up chairs and signs before a school event.","zh":"義工可能在學校活動前協助擺放椅子和指示牌。"},{"en":"Setting up an event properly helps it run smoothly later.","zh":"妥善籌辦活動有助之後順利進行。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on preparation before an activity begins.","zh":"這個短語著重活動開始前的準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sports competition","meaning":"體育比賽","examples":[{"en":"Holly will help to set up a sports competition for primary school children.","zh":"Holly會協助籌辦一項小學生體育比賽。"},{"en":"A sports competition is an event where people compete in physical games or activities.","zh":"sports competition是人們在體能遊戲或活動中競爭的活動。"},{"en":"A school may hold a sports competition with races, ball games and team events.","zh":"學校可能舉辦有賽跑、球類遊戲和團隊項目的體育比賽。"},{"en":"Sports competitions need rules, equipment, safety plans and clear timing.","zh":"體育比賽需要規則、設備、安全計劃和清晰時間安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an organised athletic event.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的運動活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"primary school children","meaning":"小學生","examples":[{"en":"The competition is for primary school children.","zh":"這項比賽是為小學生而設。"},{"en":"Primary school children are young pupils who attend primary school.","zh":"primary school children是在小學就讀的年幼學生。"},{"en":"Primary school children usually need clear instructions and close supervision during events.","zh":"小學生在活動中通常需要清晰指示和密切看管。"},{"en":"Activities for younger children should be safe, simple and well organised.","zh":"為年幼孩子設計的活動應安全、簡單並組織良好。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the age group involved.","zh":"這個短語指出涉及的年齡組別。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a popular placement","meaning":"受歡迎的實習項目","examples":[{"en":"The Orion Stadium placement is always a popular placement.","zh":"Orion Stadium實習項目一直是受歡迎的實習項目。"},{"en":"A popular placement is a work placement that many students want to choose.","zh":"popular placement是許多學生想選擇的工作實習。"},{"en":"A hospital placement may be popular because students can observe real professional practice.","zh":"醫院實習可能很受歡迎，因為學生可以觀察真實專業實務。"},{"en":"Popular placements may fill quickly because demand is high.","zh":"受歡迎的實習項目可能很快滿額，因為需求高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an attractive training opportunity.","zh":"這個短語描述吸引人的培訓機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"even though","meaning":"雖然","examples":[{"en":"The placement is popular even though working with children can be difficult.","zh":"雖然與兒童一起工作可能困難，這個實習項目仍然受歡迎。"},{"en":"Even though means although, and it introduces a contrast.","zh":"even though意思是雖然，用來引入對比。"},{"en":"The course is useful even though the timetable is demanding.","zh":"雖然時間表要求很高，這個課程仍然有用。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one fact does not cancel the other.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個事實不會抵消另一個事實。"},{"en":"It is useful when balancing positive and negative points.","zh":"當平衡正反兩面時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tougher than you think","meaning":"比你想像中困難","examples":[{"en":"Working with children can be tougher than you think.","zh":"與兒童一起工作可能比你想像中困難。"},{"en":"Tougher than you think means more difficult than you expect.","zh":"tougher than you think意思是比你預期更困難。"},{"en":"Organising a simple game for thirty children can be tougher than you think.","zh":"為三十名孩子組織一個簡單遊戲，可能比你想像中困難。"},{"en":"Things seem easy until people try to manage real behaviour, timing and safety.","zh":"事情看似容易，直到人們真正要管理行為、時間和安全。"},{"en":"This phrase warns someone not to underestimate a task.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要低估任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"working with children","meaning":"與兒童一起工作","examples":[{"en":"Working with children can be tougher than people expect.","zh":"與兒童一起工作可能比人們預期困難。"},{"en":"Working with children means teaching, supervising, helping or organising activities for children.","zh":"working with children意思是教導、看管、幫助或為兒童組織活動。"},{"en":"Working with children requires patience, clear instructions and quick reactions.","zh":"與兒童一起工作需要耐性、清晰指示和快速反應。"},{"en":"Children may be energetic and unpredictable, so adults need strong planning.","zh":"兒童可能精力充沛而難以預測，所以成人需要強大規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a people-focused responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述以人為本的責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the fresh air","meaning":"新鮮空氣","examples":[{"en":"The fresh air is what attracts Holly to the placement.","zh":"新鮮空氣正是吸引Holly選擇這個實習的原因。"},{"en":"The fresh air means clean outdoor air, especially away from indoor rooms or pollution.","zh":"the fresh air意思是清新的戶外空氣，尤其是離開室內或污染的空氣。"},{"en":"Many people enjoy outdoor work because the fresh air makes them feel more energetic.","zh":"許多人喜歡戶外工作，因為新鮮空氣令他們更有精神。"},{"en":"Fresh air can make a placement feel healthier and more enjoyable.","zh":"新鮮空氣可以令實習感覺更健康和更愉快。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the appeal of an outdoor activity.","zh":"這個短語解釋戶外活動的吸引力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"attract someone","meaning":"吸引某人","examples":[{"en":"The outdoor nature of the work attracts Holly.","zh":"工作的戶外性質吸引Holly。"},{"en":"To attract someone means to make that person interested in something.","zh":"attract someone意思是令某人對某事感興趣。"},{"en":"A creative project may attract students who enjoy design and teamwork.","zh":"創意項目可能吸引喜歡設計和團隊合作的學生。"},{"en":"People are attracted to opportunities that match their interests and values.","zh":"人們會被符合興趣和價值觀的機會吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what draws someone towards a choice.","zh":"這個短語描述甚麼令某人被某選擇吸引。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"organise something indoors","meaning":"在室內籌辦活動","examples":[{"en":"Organising something indoors does not have the same appeal for Holly.","zh":"在室內籌辦活動對Holly沒有同樣吸引力。"},{"en":"To organise something indoors means to plan and run an activity inside a building.","zh":"organise something indoors意思是在建築物內策劃和運作活動。"},{"en":"Some students prefer organising something indoors because weather will not affect the event.","zh":"有些學生較喜歡在室內籌辦活動，因為天氣不會影響活動。"},{"en":"Indoor organisation may be easier to control, but it may feel less exciting to some people.","zh":"室內籌辦可能較容易控制，但對有些人來說可能較不刺激。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts indoor event planning with outdoor work.","zh":"這個短語把室內活動策劃與戶外工作作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have the same appeal","meaning":"有同樣吸引力","examples":[{"en":"An indoor activity does not have the same appeal for Holly.","zh":"室內活動對Holly沒有同樣吸引力。"},{"en":"To have the same appeal means to be equally attractive or interesting.","zh":"have the same appeal意思是有同等吸引力或趣味。"},{"en":"Online meetings do not have the same appeal for students who enjoy face-to-face discussion.","zh":"對喜歡面對面討論的學生來說，網上會議沒有同樣吸引力。"},{"en":"Two options may be useful, but one may feel more enjoyable than the other.","zh":"兩個選項都可能有用，但其中一個可能感覺更愉快。"},{"en":"This phrase compares attractiveness between choices.","zh":"這個短語比較不同選擇的吸引力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"safety is one of your key concerns","meaning":"安全是你的主要關注之一","examples":[{"en":"Safety will be one of Holly’s key concerns for the event.","zh":"安全會是Holly在活動中的主要關注之一。"},{"en":"Safety is one of your key concerns means safety is one of the main things you must think about.","zh":"safety is one of your key concerns意思是安全是你必須思考的主要事項之一。"},{"en":"For a school trip, safety is one of the teacher’s key concerns.","zh":"對學校旅行而言，安全是老師的主要關注之一。"},{"en":"When children are involved, safety planning becomes especially important.","zh":"當涉及兒童時，安全規劃尤其重要。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a major responsibility.","zh":"這個短語突顯一項重大責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"key concerns","meaning":"主要關注事項","examples":[{"en":"Safety is one of the key concerns for the sports competition.","zh":"安全是體育比賽的主要關注事項之一。"},{"en":"Key concerns are the most important issues that need attention.","zh":"key concerns是需要注意的最重要問題。"},{"en":"For an exam, key concerns include timing, instructions and fairness.","zh":"對考試而言，主要關注事項包括時間、指示和公平性。"},{"en":"Identifying key concerns helps organisers decide what to handle first.","zh":"找出主要關注事項能幫助主辦方決定先處理甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in planning and risk management.","zh":"這個短語常見於策劃和風險管理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"think about","meaning":"考慮；想過","examples":[{"en":"Holly has already thought about safety.","zh":"Holly已經考慮過安全問題。"},{"en":"To think about something means to consider it carefully.","zh":"think about某事，意思是仔細考慮它。"},{"en":"Students should think about transport before choosing a work placement far from home.","zh":"學生選擇離家很遠的工作實習前，應考慮交通。"},{"en":"Thinking about a problem early can prevent trouble later.","zh":"及早考慮問題可以防止日後麻煩。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing planning and preparation.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論策劃和準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Holly needs to make sure the event is safe.","zh":"Holly需要確保活動安全。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check or do what is needed so that something is certain.","zh":"make sure意思是檢查或做所需的事，以確定某事屬實。"},{"en":"A teacher must make sure all students are present before leaving the museum.","zh":"老師離開博物館前必須確保所有學生都在場。"},{"en":"Making sure is important when mistakes could cause danger or confusion.","zh":"當錯誤可能造成危險或混亂，確保事情正確很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a responsibility to confirm something.","zh":"這個短語引入確認某事的責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"damaged equipment","meaning":"損壞的設備","examples":[{"en":"Holly first thinks about checking for damaged equipment.","zh":"Holly首先想到檢查是否有損壞的設備。"},{"en":"Damaged equipment is equipment that is broken, unsafe or not working properly.","zh":"damaged equipment是破損、不安全或不能正常運作的設備。"},{"en":"A football goal with a loose frame is damaged equipment and should not be used.","zh":"框架鬆脫的足球龍門是損壞的設備，不應使用。"},{"en":"Damaged equipment can cause injuries if people do not notice it in time.","zh":"如果人們未能及時發現，損壞的設備可能造成受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in safety checks.","zh":"這個短語在安全檢查中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be someone’s responsibility","meaning":"是某人的責任","examples":[{"en":"The equipment will be the schools’ responsibility.","zh":"設備會是學校的責任。"},{"en":"If something is someone’s responsibility, that person or group must take care of it.","zh":"如果某事是某人的責任，該人或群體必須負責處理。"},{"en":"During a trip, student behaviour is partly the teachers’ responsibility.","zh":"在旅行期間，學生行為部分是老師的責任。"},{"en":"Clear responsibility prevents people from assuming someone else will handle a task.","zh":"清楚責任能防止人們以為別人會處理某任務。"},{"en":"This phrase explains who is accountable.","zh":"這個短語解釋誰需要負責。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"work with schools","meaning":"與學校合作","examples":[{"en":"Holly will be working with schools during the event.","zh":"Holly會在活動中與學校合作。"},{"en":"To work with schools means to cooperate with schools to complete a task or run an activity.","zh":"work with schools意思是與學校合作完成任務或舉辦活動。"},{"en":"A museum may work with schools to organise history workshops.","zh":"博物館可能與學校合作舉辦歷史工作坊。"},{"en":"Working with schools requires clear communication with teachers and pupils.","zh":"與學校合作需要與老師和學生清楚溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cooperation between an organiser and schools.","zh":"這個短語描述主辦方與學校之間的合作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the grounds","meaning":"場地","examples":[{"en":"Holly will be responsible for the grounds.","zh":"Holly會負責場地。"},{"en":"The grounds are the outdoor land or area belonging to a building or venue.","zh":"the grounds是屬於建築物或場館的戶外土地或範圍。"},{"en":"A school’s grounds may include fields, paths, playgrounds and entrances.","zh":"學校場地可能包括球場、小路、操場和入口。"},{"en":"Event organisers must check the grounds for hazards before people arrive.","zh":"活動主辦方必須在人們到達前檢查場地是否有危險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the physical outdoor site.","zh":"這個短語指實體戶外場地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what goes on there","meaning":"那裏發生的事情","examples":[{"en":"Holly will be responsible for what goes on at the grounds.","zh":"Holly會負責場地那裏發生的事情。"},{"en":"What goes on there means what happens in that place.","zh":"what goes on there意思是在那個地方發生的事情。"},{"en":"A teacher supervising the playground is responsible for what goes on there during recess.","zh":"監督操場的老師負責小息期間那裏發生的事情。"},{"en":"Knowing what goes on in an area helps organisers manage safety and behaviour.","zh":"知道某區發生甚麼，有助主辦方管理安全和行為。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to activities, behaviour and incidents in a place.","zh":"這個短語指某地的活動、行為和事件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"include doing something","meaning":"包括做某事","examples":[{"en":"Holly’s responsibilities will include keeping children within the boundary.","zh":"Holly的責任會包括確保孩子留在界線內。"},{"en":"To include doing something means to have that action as part of a larger set of duties.","zh":"include doing something意思是把該行動作為較大職責的一部分。"},{"en":"A volunteer’s tasks may include checking tickets and giving directions.","zh":"義工任務可能包括查票和指示方向。"},{"en":"Listing what duties include helps people understand their role clearly.","zh":"列出職責包括甚麼，有助人清楚理解自己的角色。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces one part of a wider responsibility.","zh":"這個短語引入更廣泛責任中的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"keep everyone within the boundary","meaning":"確保所有人留在界線內","examples":[{"en":"Holly must keep everyone within the boundary during the event.","zh":"Holly必須在活動中確保所有人留在界線內。"},{"en":"To keep everyone within the boundary means to make sure nobody goes outside the marked area.","zh":"keep everyone within the boundary意思是確保沒有人走出標示範圍。"},{"en":"Teachers must keep pupils within the boundary during a sports day.","zh":"老師在運動會期間必須確保學生留在界線內。"},{"en":"Boundaries help prevent children from entering unsafe or uncontrolled areas.","zh":"界線有助防止孩子進入不安全或不受控制的區域。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in safety supervision.","zh":"這個短語在安全監督中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"within the boundary","meaning":"在界線內","examples":[{"en":"The children must stay within the boundary once they are on the field.","zh":"孩子一到場上，就必須留在界線內。"},{"en":"Within the boundary means inside the marked or agreed limit.","zh":"within the boundary意思是在標示或同意的限制範圍內。"},{"en":"Players must stay within the boundary during the game.","zh":"球員在比賽期間必須留在界線內。"},{"en":"Clear boundaries help children know where they may and may not go.","zh":"清晰界線幫助孩子知道哪裏可以去、哪裏不可以去。"},{"en":"This phrase describes staying inside a permitted area.","zh":"這個短語描述留在准許範圍內。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in their kit","meaning":"穿着運動裝備","examples":[{"en":"The children will be in their kit when they go onto the field.","zh":"孩子上場時會穿着運動裝備。"},{"en":"In their kit means wearing the clothes or equipment needed for a sport or activity.","zh":"in their kit意思是穿着某項運動或活動所需的衣服或裝備。"},{"en":"Football players arrive in their kit before the match begins.","zh":"足球員在比賽開始前穿着球衣裝備到場。"},{"en":"Wearing the correct kit helps people play safely and identify teams easily.","zh":"穿着正確裝備有助安全比賽，也方便辨認隊伍。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in sports contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於體育語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on the field","meaning":"在場上","examples":[{"en":"The children must stay within the boundary when they are on the field.","zh":"孩子在場上時必須留在界線內。"},{"en":"On the field means on the sports ground where the game or activity takes place.","zh":"on the field意思是在比賽或活動進行的運動場地上。"},{"en":"Coaches should know how many players are on the field at any time.","zh":"教練應隨時知道場上有多少球員。"},{"en":"Rules on the field may differ from rules in the spectator area.","zh":"場上的規則可能與觀眾區的規則不同。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the active sports area.","zh":"這個短語指出進行體育活動的區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"inspect areas like","meaning":"檢查例如……的地方","examples":[{"en":"Holly needs to inspect areas like changing rooms.","zh":"Holly需要檢查更衣室等地方。"},{"en":"To inspect areas like something means to check places such as those examples carefully.","zh":"inspect areas like某地，意思是仔細檢查那些例子所屬的地方。"},{"en":"Staff should inspect areas like corridors, staircases and toilets before visitors arrive.","zh":"職員應在訪客到達前檢查走廊、樓梯和洗手間等地方。"},{"en":"Inspection helps identify hazards before they cause accidents.","zh":"檢查有助在危險造成意外前找出它們。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples of places that need checking.","zh":"這個短語引入需要檢查的地方例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"changing rooms","meaning":"更衣室","examples":[{"en":"Holly needs to inspect the changing rooms for hazards.","zh":"Holly需要檢查更衣室是否有危險。"},{"en":"Changing rooms are rooms where people change clothes before or after sports.","zh":"changing rooms是人們在運動前後更換衣服的房間。"},{"en":"A swimming pool should keep its changing rooms clean, dry and safe.","zh":"泳池應保持更衣室清潔、乾爽和安全。"},{"en":"Changing rooms may contain wet floors, bags or benches that create trip hazards.","zh":"更衣室可能有濕地板、袋或長椅，造成絆倒危險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an important backstage sports facility.","zh":"這個短語指重要的體育後勤設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"trip over","meaning":"被……絆倒","examples":[{"en":"Holly must look for anything someone can trip over.","zh":"Holly必須尋找任何可能令人絆倒的東西。"},{"en":"To trip over something means to catch your foot on it and almost fall or fall.","zh":"trip over某物，意思是腳被它絆住，差點跌倒或跌倒。"},{"en":"A child may trip over a sports bag left in a corridor.","zh":"孩子可能被放在走廊的運動袋絆倒。"},{"en":"Small objects on the ground can become serious hazards during a busy event.","zh":"地上的小物件在繁忙活動中可以成為嚴重危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in safety checks.","zh":"這個短語在安全檢查中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"main priority","meaning":"首要任務","examples":[{"en":"Holly’s main priority will be not to lose anyone.","zh":"Holly的首要任務會是不要弄失任何人。"},{"en":"A main priority is the most important thing to focus on first.","zh":"main priority是首先要專注的最重要事情。"},{"en":"During a school trip, the main priority is keeping all students safe.","zh":"在學校旅行中，首要任務是確保所有學生安全。"},{"en":"Priorities help organisers decide what matters most when many things happen at once.","zh":"優先次序幫助主辦方在多件事同時發生時決定甚麼最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the top concern.","zh":"這個短語指出最重要的關注。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lose anyone","meaning":"弄失任何人","examples":[{"en":"Holly’s main priority is not to lose anyone during the event.","zh":"Holly的首要任務是在活動中不要弄失任何人。"},{"en":"To lose anyone means to fail to keep track of a person so they cannot be found immediately.","zh":"lose anyone意思是未能掌握某人的位置，以致不能立即找到他。"},{"en":"Teachers count students regularly so they do not lose anyone on a trip.","zh":"老師在旅行中定期點算學生，以免弄失任何人。"},{"en":"Losing a child at a large event can become a serious safety problem.","zh":"在大型活動中弄失孩子可以成為嚴重安全問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is especially important when supervising children.","zh":"這個短語在看管兒童時尤其重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"need staff to help with","meaning":"需要職員協助……","examples":[{"en":"Holly will need staff to help with safety.","zh":"Holly會需要職員協助安全工作。"},{"en":"To need staff to help with something means to require workers or helpers for that task.","zh":"need staff to help with某事，意思是需要工作人員或幫手處理該任務。"},{"en":"A concert organiser may need staff to help with tickets and crowd control.","zh":"音樂會主辦方可能需要職員協助門票和人流控制。"},{"en":"Having enough staff makes an event safer and easier to manage.","zh":"有足夠職員能令活動更安全和更易管理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a staffing requirement.","zh":"這個短語描述人手需求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"don’t forget about","meaning":"不要忘記……","examples":[{"en":"The tutor tells Holly not to forget about the spectators.","zh":"導師提醒Holly不要忘記觀眾。"},{"en":"Don’t forget about something means remember to include or consider it.","zh":"don’t forget about某事，意思是記得包括或考慮它。"},{"en":"When planning a school trip, do not forget about students with food allergies.","zh":"規劃學校旅行時，不要忘記有食物過敏的學生。"},{"en":"This phrase warns someone not to overlook an important group or issue.","zh":"這個短語提醒某人不要忽略重要群體或問題。"},{"en":"It is common in planning conversations.","zh":"它常見於策劃對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"spectators","meaning":"觀眾","examples":[{"en":"Holly must also think about the spectators at the event.","zh":"Holly也必須考慮活動中的觀眾。"},{"en":"Spectators are people who watch an event but do not take part in it.","zh":"spectators是觀看活動但不參與其中的人。"},{"en":"Spectators at a school sports day may include parents, teachers and friends.","zh":"學校運動會的觀眾可能包括家長、老師和朋友。"},{"en":"Spectators need safe viewing areas so they do not interfere with the competition.","zh":"觀眾需要安全觀看區，以免干擾比賽。"},{"en":"This word is common in sports and performance contexts.","zh":"這個詞常見於體育和表演語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"help run the event","meaning":"協助運作活動","examples":[{"en":"Holly thinks some parents could help run the event.","zh":"Holly認為一些家長可以協助運作活動。"},{"en":"To help run the event means to assist in operating or managing it on the day.","zh":"help run the event意思是在活動當日協助操作或管理它。"},{"en":"Volunteers may help run the event by guiding teams and checking equipment.","zh":"義工可能透過指引隊伍和檢查設備來協助運作活動。"},{"en":"Running an event requires people who can solve problems while it is happening.","zh":"運作活動需要能在活動進行時解決問題的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical support during an event.","zh":"這個短語描述活動期間的實際支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rely on","meaning":"依賴……","examples":[{"en":"The tutor warns Holly not to rely on parents as volunteers.","zh":"導師提醒Holly不要依賴家長做義工。"},{"en":"To rely on someone means to depend on them for help or support.","zh":"rely on某人，意思是依靠他們提供幫助或支援。"},{"en":"An organiser should not rely on one person to handle every emergency.","zh":"主辦方不應依賴一個人處理所有緊急情況。"},{"en":"Relying too much on uncertain help can make a plan risky.","zh":"太依賴不確定的幫助會令計劃有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dependence.","zh":"這個短語描述依靠關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be more interested in","meaning":"對……更感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Parents may be more interested in filming their children than volunteering.","zh":"家長可能對拍攝自己的孩子比做義工更感興趣。"},{"en":"To be more interested in something means to care about it more than another thing.","zh":"be more interested in某事，意思是比另一事更關心它。"},{"en":"At a concert, parents may be more interested in taking photos than helping backstage.","zh":"在音樂會上，家長可能對拍照比在後台幫忙更感興趣。"},{"en":"People naturally focus on what matters most to them personally.","zh":"人們自然會專注於對自己最重要的事。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two levels of interest.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種興趣程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"film their children","meaning":"拍攝自己的孩子","examples":[{"en":"Parents may be more interested in filming their children.","zh":"家長可能更感興趣於拍攝自己的孩子。"},{"en":"To film their children means to record video of their children.","zh":"film their children意思是拍攝自己孩子的影片。"},{"en":"Parents often film their children during school plays and sports days.","zh":"家長常在學校話劇和運動會中拍攝自己的孩子。"},{"en":"Filming can become a problem if parents move into unsafe areas to get a better view.","zh":"如果家長為了更好角度而走進不安全區域，拍攝就可能成為問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recording children’s performance or activity.","zh":"這個短語描述記錄孩子的表演或活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"volunteering","meaning":"做義工","examples":[{"en":"Parents may prefer filming their children to volunteering.","zh":"家長可能寧願拍攝自己的孩子，也不想做義工。"},{"en":"Volunteering means giving time and effort to help without being paid.","zh":"volunteering意思是無償付出時間和努力去幫忙。"},{"en":"Volunteering at a school event may involve guiding visitors or serving refreshments.","zh":"在學校活動中做義工可能包括指引訪客或供應茶點。"},{"en":"Volunteering is useful only if helpers understand and follow their role.","zh":"只有當幫手明白並遵守自己的角色時，做義工才有用。"},{"en":"This word describes unpaid service.","zh":"這個詞描述無薪服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"interfere with","meaning":"干擾……","examples":[{"en":"Holly needs to make sure parents do not interfere with the events.","zh":"Holly需要確保家長不會干擾比賽項目。"},{"en":"To interfere with something means to disturb it or prevent it from happening properly.","zh":"interfere with某事，意思是打擾它或阻礙它正常進行。"},{"en":"Loud conversations can interfere with students’ listening exam.","zh":"大聲談話可以干擾學生的聆聽考試。"},{"en":"Spectators may interfere with a race if they stand too close to the track.","zh":"如果觀眾站得太近跑道，可能會干擾比賽。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unwanted disruption.","zh":"這個短語描述不受歡迎的干擾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not always easy","meaning":"並不總是容易","examples":[{"en":"Keeping parents away from the action is not always easy.","zh":"讓家長遠離比賽進行區並不總是容易。"},{"en":"Not always easy means sometimes difficult, even if it may sound simple.","zh":"not always easy意思是有時困難，即使聽起來簡單。"},{"en":"Keeping young children quiet during a long ceremony is not always easy.","zh":"在漫長典禮中讓小孩子保持安靜並不總是容易。"},{"en":"Some tasks are difficult because people’s emotions and behaviour are involved.","zh":"有些任務困難，是因為涉及人的情緒和行為。"},{"en":"This phrase admits that a responsibility can be challenging.","zh":"這個短語承認某責任可能具挑戰性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a proud parent","meaning":"自豪的家長","examples":[{"en":"A proud parent may try to get a photo of their child.","zh":"自豪的家長可能嘗試拍一張孩子的照片。"},{"en":"A proud parent is a parent who feels very pleased about their child’s achievement or performance.","zh":"proud parent是對孩子的成就或表現感到非常高興的家長。"},{"en":"A proud parent may clap loudly when their child wins a race.","zh":"當孩子贏得比賽，自豪的家長可能大聲鼓掌。"},{"en":"Pride is natural, but parents still need to follow event rules.","zh":"自豪感是自然的，但家長仍需要遵守活動規則。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why parents may become overenthusiastic.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何家長可能過分熱心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get a snap of","meaning":"拍一張……的照片","examples":[{"en":"A proud parent may try to get a snap of their child.","zh":"自豪的家長可能嘗試拍一張孩子的照片。"},{"en":"To get a snap of someone means to take a quick photo of them.","zh":"get a snap of某人，意思是快速為某人拍一張照片。"},{"en":"A parent may try to get a snap of her child receiving a medal.","zh":"家長可能嘗試拍一張孩子領獎牌的照片。"},{"en":"The word “snap” is informal and usually means a casual photograph.","zh":"snap這個詞較口語，通常指隨手拍的照片。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday speech about taking photos.","zh":"這個短語常見於日常談論拍照時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"move elsewhere","meaning":"移到其他地方","examples":[{"en":"Holly may need to ask parents to move elsewhere.","zh":"Holly可能需要請家長移到其他地方。"},{"en":"To move elsewhere means to go to another place.","zh":"move elsewhere意思是去另一個地方。"},{"en":"Staff may ask visitors to move elsewhere if they are blocking an emergency exit.","zh":"如果訪客阻塞緊急出口，職員可能請他們移到其他地方。"},{"en":"Moving people to the right area can improve safety and crowd control.","zh":"把人移到正確區域可以改善安全和人流控制。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when managing people at an event.","zh":"這個短語適合用於活動中管理人群。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"what about","meaning":"……方面怎樣？","examples":[{"en":"Holly asks, “What about the scheduling?”","zh":"Holly問：「時間安排方面怎樣？」"},{"en":"What about something? means what should we consider or do regarding that topic?","zh":"what about某事，意思是關於該主題，我們應考慮或怎樣處理？"},{"en":"After discussing safety, a student may ask, “What about transport?”","zh":"討論安全後，學生可能問：「交通方面怎樣？」"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a new but related topic in conversation.","zh":"這個短語在對話中引入新的相關主題。"},{"en":"It is common and conversational.","zh":"它常見而且口語化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the scheduling","meaning":"時間安排","examples":[{"en":"Holly asks the tutor about the scheduling of the sports competition.","zh":"Holly問導師關於體育比賽的時間安排。"},{"en":"The scheduling means the planning of times and order for activities.","zh":"the scheduling意思是活動時間和次序的規劃。"},{"en":"The scheduling of a school concert must allow time for rehearsals and breaks.","zh":"學校音樂會的時間安排必須預留排練和休息時間。"},{"en":"Good scheduling prevents delays and helps everyone know what happens next.","zh":"良好時間安排能防止延誤，並幫助每個人知道下一步。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to event planning.","zh":"這個短語是活動策劃的核心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sporting events","meaning":"體育活動","examples":[{"en":"Sporting events can be affected by weather and injuries.","zh":"體育活動可能受天氣和受傷影響。"},{"en":"Sporting events are organised competitions or activities involving sport.","zh":"sporting events是涉及運動的有組織比賽或活動。"},{"en":"A school sports day and a football tournament are sporting events.","zh":"學校運動會和足球錦標賽都是體育活動。"},{"en":"Sporting events often need flexible plans because players, weather and timing can change.","zh":"體育活動通常需要彈性計劃，因為參賽者、天氣和時間可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in event management and athletics.","zh":"這個短語常見於活動管理和運動語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"all sorts of things","meaning":"各種事情","examples":[{"en":"All sorts of things can alter the timetable.","zh":"各種事情都可以改變時間表。"},{"en":"All sorts of things means many different kinds of things.","zh":"all sorts of things意思是許多不同種類的事情。"},{"en":"All sorts of things can affect a school trip, including traffic, weather and illness.","zh":"各種事情都可以影響學校旅行，包括交通、天氣和疾病。"},{"en":"This phrase is broad because the speaker is not listing every possibility.","zh":"這個短語很廣泛，因為說話者沒有列出每個可能性。"},{"en":"It often suggests that events can be unpredictable.","zh":"它常暗示事情可能難以預測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"alter the timetable","meaning":"改變時間表","examples":[{"en":"Rain or injuries can alter the timetable.","zh":"下雨或受傷可以改變時間表。"},{"en":"To alter the timetable means to change the planned times or order of activities.","zh":"alter the timetable意思是改變原定活動時間或次序。"},{"en":"A late bus may alter the timetable for a school visit.","zh":"巴士遲到可能改變學校參觀的時間表。"},{"en":"Timetable changes can affect staff, participants and spectators.","zh":"時間表改動可以影響職員、參加者和觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change to planned scheduling.","zh":"這個短語描述原定時間安排的改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"Rain, for instance, can alter the timetable.","zh":"例如，下雨可以改變時間表。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance意思是例如。"},{"en":"Many things can delay an event; traffic, for instance, is often hard to control.","zh":"很多事情可以延誤活動；例如，交通通常難以控制。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces one example from a wider group.","zh":"這個短語從較大群組中引入一個例子。"},{"en":"It is useful in explanations and discussions.","zh":"它適合用於解釋和討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"so far","meaning":"到目前為止","examples":[{"en":"So far, the organisers have always been lucky with the weather.","zh":"到目前為止，主辦方在天氣方面一直很走運。"},{"en":"So far means up to the present point in time.","zh":"so far意思是直到目前這一刻。"},{"en":"So far, the project has stayed within budget.","zh":"到目前為止，項目仍然沒有超出預算。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the situation could still change later.","zh":"這個短語暗示情況之後仍可能改變。"},{"en":"It is useful when summarising progress until now.","zh":"它適合用於概括至今的進展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be lucky with","meaning":"在……方面走運","examples":[{"en":"The organisers have always been lucky with the weather.","zh":"主辦方在天氣方面一直很走運。"},{"en":"To be lucky with something means to have good fortune in that area.","zh":"be lucky with某事，意思是在該方面有好運。"},{"en":"The school was lucky with traffic and arrived earlier than expected.","zh":"學校在交通方面很走運，比預期更早到達。"},{"en":"Luck can help an event, but organisers should still prepare for problems.","zh":"運氣可以幫助活動，但主辦方仍應為問題作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes favourable circumstances.","zh":"這個短語描述有利情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get hurt","meaning":"受傷","examples":[{"en":"Holly thinks about what to do if someone gets hurt.","zh":"Holly思考如果有人受傷該怎樣做。"},{"en":"To get hurt means to be injured physically or emotionally.","zh":"get hurt意思是身體或情感上受傷。"},{"en":"A child may get hurt if they run on a wet floor.","zh":"如果孩子在濕地板上奔跑，可能會受傷。"},{"en":"Event organisers must know what to do when someone gets hurt.","zh":"活動主辦方必須知道有人受傷時該怎樣做。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing accidents and safety.","zh":"這個短語常見於討論意外和安全時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cause a terrible delay","meaning":"造成嚴重延誤","examples":[{"en":"An injury caused a terrible delay last year.","zh":"去年一次受傷造成嚴重延誤。"},{"en":"To cause a terrible delay means to make something run very late or stop for a long time.","zh":"cause a terrible delay意思是令某事大幅延遲或長時間停頓。"},{"en":"A broken sound system can cause a terrible delay at a concert.","zh":"音響系統故障可以在音樂會中造成嚴重延誤。"},{"en":"Serious delays can affect the whole timetable and frustrate participants.","zh":"嚴重延誤可以影響整個時間表，並令參與者沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major scheduling problem.","zh":"這個短語描述重大的時間安排問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be prepared for","meaning":"為……作好準備","examples":[{"en":"Holly has to be prepared for injuries and delays.","zh":"Holly必須為受傷和延誤作好準備。"},{"en":"To be prepared for something means to be ready to deal with it if it happens.","zh":"be prepared for某事，意思是準備好在它發生時處理。"},{"en":"Teachers must be prepared for rain during an outdoor school trip.","zh":"老師在戶外學校旅行中必須為下雨作好準備。"},{"en":"Preparation reduces panic because people already have a plan.","zh":"準備能減少恐慌，因為人們已有計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in risk management.","zh":"這個短語常見於風險管理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"such things","meaning":"這類事情","examples":[{"en":"The tutor says Holly must be prepared for such things.","zh":"導師說Holly必須為這類事情作好準備。"},{"en":"Such things means things like the ones just mentioned.","zh":"such things意思是像剛才提到那些事情。"},{"en":"Delays, lost equipment and sudden illness are all such things organisers must consider.","zh":"延誤、設備遺失和突然生病都是主辦方必須考慮的這類事情。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating a list of examples.","zh":"這個短語避免重複列出一串例子。"},{"en":"It refers back to earlier mentioned problems or situations.","zh":"它指回之前提到的問題或情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"end in a draw","meaning":"以平局結束","examples":[{"en":"A match may end in a draw.","zh":"一場比賽可能以平局結束。"},{"en":"To end in a draw means to finish with both sides having the same score.","zh":"end in a draw意思是雙方得分相同而結束。"},{"en":"A football match can end in a draw if both teams score two goals.","zh":"如果兩隊各入兩球，足球比賽可以以平局結束。"},{"en":"Draws may require extra rules if the competition needs a winner.","zh":"如果比賽需要勝方，平局可能需要額外規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in sports.","zh":"這個短語常見於體育語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"keep going","meaning":"繼續進行","examples":[{"en":"The teams might keep going until someone wins.","zh":"隊伍可能會繼續進行，直到有人勝出。"},{"en":"To keep going means to continue doing something.","zh":"keep going意思是繼續做某事。"},{"en":"A game may keep going after normal time if there must be a winner.","zh":"如果必須有勝方，比賽可能在正常時間後繼續進行。"},{"en":"Continuing too long can affect the timetable of later events.","zh":"持續太久可以影響之後活動的時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continuation instead of stopping.","zh":"這個短語描述繼續而不是停止。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be up to you","meaning":"由你決定","examples":[{"en":"Whether a drawn match continues will be up to Holly.","zh":"平局比賽是否繼續將由Holly決定。"},{"en":"If something is up to you, you are responsible for deciding it.","zh":"如果某事be up to you，意思是由你負責決定。"},{"en":"The final design is up to the team leader.","zh":"最終設計由團隊領袖決定。"},{"en":"This phrase gives decision-making power and responsibility to someone.","zh":"這個短語把決策權和責任交給某人。"},{"en":"It is common when discussing choices and authority.","zh":"它常見於討論選擇和權力時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"plan for","meaning":"為……預先計劃","examples":[{"en":"Holly needs to plan for the possibility of a draw.","zh":"Holly需要為平局的可能性預先計劃。"},{"en":"To plan for something means to prepare for it before it happens.","zh":"plan for某事，意思是在它發生前作準備。"},{"en":"Organisers should plan for bad weather during outdoor events.","zh":"主辦方應為戶外活動中的惡劣天氣預先計劃。"},{"en":"Planning for possible problems helps people react quickly.","zh":"為可能問題預先計劃能幫助人迅速反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in event preparation and risk management.","zh":"這個短語適合用於活動準備和風險管理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the aim of","meaning":"……的目的","examples":[{"en":"The aim of the work placement is to develop events-management skills.","zh":"工作實習的目的是培養活動管理技能。"},{"en":"The aim of something is its purpose or goal.","zh":"the aim of某事，是它的目的或目標。"},{"en":"The aim of a training course may be to improve teamwork and confidence.","zh":"培訓課程的目的可能是改善團隊合作和信心。"},{"en":"Knowing the aim helps students understand what they should learn.","zh":"知道目的能幫助學生理解自己應學到甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the purpose behind an activity.","zh":"這個短語引入活動背後的目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"give you the opportunity to","meaning":"給你機會去……","examples":[{"en":"The placement gives Holly the opportunity to develop useful skills.","zh":"實習給Holly機會去培養有用技能。"},{"en":"To give you the opportunity to do something means to allow you the chance to do it.","zh":"give you the opportunity to do something意思是讓你有機會做某事。"},{"en":"A work placement can give students the opportunity to meet professionals.","zh":"工作實習可以給學生機會去認識專業人士。"},{"en":"Opportunities are valuable when they let people practise in real situations.","zh":"當機會讓人們在真實情況中練習，它就很有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a benefit of an experience.","zh":"這個短語突顯某經驗的好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"develop the skills","meaning":"培養技能","examples":[{"en":"The placement helps Holly develop the skills an events manager needs.","zh":"實習幫助Holly培養活動經理所需的技能。"},{"en":"To develop the skills means to improve abilities through practice and experience.","zh":"develop the skills意思是透過練習和經驗提升能力。"},{"en":"Students develop communication skills by giving presentations and receiving feedback.","zh":"學生透過演講和接受回饋培養溝通技巧。"},{"en":"Skills develop over time when people use them in real tasks.","zh":"當人們在真實任務中使用技能，技能就會隨時間發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth in ability.","zh":"這個短語描述能力成長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an events manager","meaning":"活動經理","examples":[{"en":"An events manager needs communication, organisation and leadership skills.","zh":"活動經理需要溝通、組織和領導能力。"},{"en":"An events manager is a person who plans, organises and runs events.","zh":"events manager是策劃、組織和運作活動的人。"},{"en":"An events manager may organise conferences, competitions, concerts or parties.","zh":"活動經理可能籌辦會議、比賽、音樂會或派對。"},{"en":"Events managers must handle people, schedules, venues and unexpected problems.","zh":"活動經理必須處理人員、時間表、場地和突發問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a professional role in event planning.","zh":"這個短語描述活動策劃中的專業角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pretty good","meaning":"頗好","examples":[{"en":"Holly thinks her communication skills are pretty good.","zh":"Holly認為自己的溝通技巧頗好。"},{"en":"Pretty good means quite good, though not necessarily perfect.","zh":"pretty good意思是頗好，但不一定完美。"},{"en":"His presentation was pretty good, but he needs to speak more slowly.","zh":"他的匯報頗好，但需要說慢一點。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and gives moderate praise.","zh":"這個短語較口語，表示中等程度讚賞。"},{"en":"It suggests confidence while leaving room for improvement.","zh":"它暗示有信心，但仍有改善空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"communication skills","meaning":"溝通技巧","examples":[{"en":"Holly thinks her communication skills are good.","zh":"Holly認為自己的溝通技巧很好。"},{"en":"Communication skills are the abilities used to share information clearly with others.","zh":"communication skills是與他人清楚分享資訊所用的能力。"},{"en":"Good communication skills include listening, speaking, writing and reading people’s reactions.","zh":"良好溝通技巧包括聆聽、說話、寫作和觀察別人反應。"},{"en":"Events managers need communication skills because they deal with clients, staff and visitors.","zh":"活動經理需要溝通技巧，因為他們要處理客戶、職員和訪客。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in job and training contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於職業和培訓語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"talk on the phone to","meaning":"打電話跟……交談","examples":[{"en":"Holly can talk on the phone to people when organising events.","zh":"Holly籌辦活動時可以打電話跟人交談。"},{"en":"To talk on the phone to someone means to speak with them by telephone.","zh":"talk on the phone to某人，意思是透過電話與某人交談。"},{"en":"An organiser may talk on the phone to venue staff to confirm booking details.","zh":"主辦方可能打電話跟場地職員確認預訂詳情。"},{"en":"Phone calls are useful when information needs to be checked quickly.","zh":"當資訊需要快速確認時，電話很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one form of professional communication.","zh":"這個短語描述一種專業溝通方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"book venues","meaning":"預訂場地","examples":[{"en":"Holly can talk to people and book venues.","zh":"Holly可以跟人溝通並預訂場地。"},{"en":"To book venues means to reserve places where events can take place.","zh":"book venues意思是預留可舉辦活動的地方。"},{"en":"A student committee may book venues for a charity concert months in advance.","zh":"學生委員會可能提前數月為慈善音樂會預訂場地。"},{"en":"Booking venues early helps organisers secure the right space and date.","zh":"及早預訂場地有助主辦方確保合適空間和日期。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in event planning.","zh":"這個短語常見於活動策劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"that kind of thing","meaning":"那類事情","examples":[{"en":"Holly can book venues and do that kind of thing.","zh":"Holly可以預訂場地和做那類事情。"},{"en":"That kind of thing means similar tasks or activities already suggested.","zh":"that kind of thing意思是與剛提到內容相似的任務或活動。"},{"en":"An assistant may answer emails, update lists and do that kind of thing.","zh":"助理可能回覆電郵、更新名單和做那類事情。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and avoids listing every detail.","zh":"這個短語較口語，避免列出每個細節。"},{"en":"It is useful when the listener already understands the general category.","zh":"當聽者已理解大致類別時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it isn’t only about","meaning":"並不只是關於……","examples":[{"en":"Communication is not only about what Holly says.","zh":"溝通並不只是關於Holly所說的內容。"},{"en":"It isn’t only about something means that one factor is important but not the whole issue.","zh":"it isn’t only about某事，意思是某因素重要，但不是整個問題。"},{"en":"Teaching is not only about explaining rules; it is also about encouraging students.","zh":"教學並不只是關於解釋規則；它也關於鼓勵學生。"},{"en":"This phrase broadens a narrow understanding of a topic.","zh":"這個短語擴闊對某主題的狹窄理解。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting an oversimplified view.","zh":"當糾正過度簡化的看法時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"what you say","meaning":"你所說的內容","examples":[{"en":"Good communication is not only about what you say.","zh":"良好溝通並不只是關於你所說的內容。"},{"en":"What you say means the words or information you express.","zh":"what you say意思是你表達的文字或資訊。"},{"en":"In an interview, what you say matters, but how you say it also matters.","zh":"在面試中，你所說的內容重要，但你如何表達也重要。"},{"en":"Words can be interpreted differently depending on tone and body language.","zh":"語氣和身體語言不同，說話可以被不同方式理解。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on spoken content.","zh":"這個短語著重說話內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"meet someone face-to-face","meaning":"與某人面對面見面","examples":[{"en":"Holly may need to meet someone face-to-face.","zh":"Holly可能需要與某人面對面見面。"},{"en":"To meet someone face-to-face means to meet them in person, not online or by phone.","zh":"meet someone face-to-face意思是親身見某人，而不是網上或電話溝通。"},{"en":"A student may meet a tutor face-to-face to discuss a difficult project.","zh":"學生可能與導師面對面見面，討論困難專題。"},{"en":"Face-to-face meetings can build trust because people see expressions and body language.","zh":"面對面會面可以建立信任，因為人們看見表情和身體語言。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts direct personal meetings with remote communication.","zh":"這個短語把直接親身會面與遙距溝通作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"persuade someone to","meaning":"說服某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Holly may need to persuade someone to be a sponsor.","zh":"Holly可能需要說服某人成為贊助商。"},{"en":"To persuade someone to do something means to convince them to do it.","zh":"persuade someone to do something意思是說服某人去做某事。"},{"en":"A student leader may persuade classmates to join a charity run.","zh":"學生領袖可能說服同學參加慈善跑。"},{"en":"Persuasion requires clear reasons, confidence and understanding the other person’s needs.","zh":"說服需要清晰理由、信心和理解對方需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes influencing someone’s decision.","zh":"這個短語描述影響某人的決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be a sponsor","meaning":"成為贊助商","examples":[{"en":"Holly may need to persuade someone to be a sponsor.","zh":"Holly可能需要說服某人成為贊助商。"},{"en":"To be a sponsor means to support an event, person or organisation with money or resources.","zh":"be a sponsor意思是以金錢或資源支持活動、個人或機構。"},{"en":"A local business may be a sponsor for a school sports day.","zh":"本地企業可能成為學校運動會的贊助商。"},{"en":"Sponsors often help events happen in exchange for publicity or goodwill.","zh":"贊助商通常協助活動舉行，以換取宣傳或好感。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in event management and fundraising.","zh":"這個短語常見於活動管理和籌款。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dress up","meaning":"穿得正式得體","examples":[{"en":"Holly says she will dress up when meeting a potential sponsor.","zh":"Holly說見潛在贊助商時會穿得正式得體。"},{"en":"To dress up means to wear smart, formal or special clothes.","zh":"dress up意思是穿着醒目、正式或特別的衣服。"},{"en":"Students may dress up for an interview to make a good impression.","zh":"學生可能為面試穿得正式得體，以留下好印象。"},{"en":"Dressing up can show respect for the occasion and the person you meet.","zh":"穿得正式可以顯示對場合和對方的尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean dressing formally, not only wearing costumes.","zh":"這個短語可以指穿得正式，不只是穿戲服。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"go on to","meaning":"接着去……","examples":[{"en":"The tutor goes on to talk about organisational skills.","zh":"導師接着去談組織能力。"},{"en":"To go on to do something means to continue by doing the next thing.","zh":"go on to do something意思是繼續做下一件事。"},{"en":"After discussing safety, the teacher went on to explain the timetable.","zh":"討論安全後，老師接着解釋時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show the order of topics in a talk.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示講話中的主題次序。"},{"en":"It is useful when moving from one point to another.","zh":"當由一點轉到另一點時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"organisational skills","meaning":"組織能力","examples":[{"en":"The tutor asks Holly to think about her organisational skills.","zh":"導師請Holly思考自己的組織能力。"},{"en":"Organisational skills are abilities that help people plan, arrange and manage tasks effectively.","zh":"organisational skills是幫助人有效規劃、安排和管理任務的能力。"},{"en":"Keeping lists and setting deadlines can improve organisational skills.","zh":"列清單和設定期限可以改善組織能力。"},{"en":"Events managers need strong organisational skills because many details happen at once.","zh":"活動經理需要強大組織能力，因為許多細節會同時發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in job and study contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於工作和學習語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a people-based industry","meaning":"以人為本的行業","examples":[{"en":"Events management is a very people-based industry.","zh":"活動管理是一個非常以人為本的行業。"},{"en":"A people-based industry is an industry that depends heavily on dealing with people.","zh":"people-based industry是非常依賴與人打交道的行業。"},{"en":"Teaching is a people-based profession because communication with students is central.","zh":"教學是以人為本的專業，因為與學生溝通是核心。"},{"en":"In people-based work, plans may change because people behave unpredictably.","zh":"在以人為本的工作中，計劃可能因人們行為難以預測而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the human side of a job.","zh":"這個短語強調工作的人的一面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"go to plan","meaning":"按計劃進行","examples":[{"en":"In a people-based industry, things will not always go to plan.","zh":"在以人為本的行業中，事情不會總是按計劃進行。"},{"en":"To go to plan means to happen exactly as intended or scheduled.","zh":"go to plan意思是事情完全按原定意圖或時間表發生。"},{"en":"A school trip may not go to plan if the bus breaks down.","zh":"如果巴士拋錨，學校旅行可能不會按計劃進行。"},{"en":"When things do not go to plan, organisers must adapt quickly.","zh":"當事情不按計劃進行，主辦方必須快速適應。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語常見於討論不確定性時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be prepared to","meaning":"準備好去……","examples":[{"en":"Holly needs to be prepared to make changes.","zh":"Holly需要準備好去作出改動。"},{"en":"To be prepared to do something means to be ready and willing to do it if needed.","zh":"be prepared to do something意思是準備好並願意在需要時做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher must be prepared to change the lesson if students are confused.","zh":"如果學生感到困惑，老師必須準備好改變課堂安排。"},{"en":"Being prepared helps people respond calmly when plans change.","zh":"有準備能幫助人在計劃改變時冷靜回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes readiness for action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make changes","meaning":"作出改動","examples":[{"en":"Holly needs to be ready to make changes during an event.","zh":"Holly需要準備好在活動期間作出改動。"},{"en":"To make changes means to alter plans, arrangements or details.","zh":"make changes意思是改變計劃、安排或細節。"},{"en":"Organisers may make changes to the timetable if the weather becomes unsafe.","zh":"如果天氣變得不安全，主辦方可能對時間表作出改動。"},{"en":"Making changes quickly can stop a small problem becoming a big one.","zh":"快速作出改動可以阻止小問題變成大問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in planning and management.","zh":"這個短語常見於策劃和管理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make an on-the-spot change","meaning":"即場作出改動","examples":[{"en":"Holly may have to make an on-the-spot change to a timetable.","zh":"Holly可能要即場對時間表作出改動。"},{"en":"To make an on-the-spot change means to change something immediately during the situation.","zh":"make an on-the-spot change意思是在情況發生時立即改變某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may make an on-the-spot change if the classroom projector stops working.","zh":"如果課室投影機突然故障，老師可能即場作出改動。"},{"en":"Such changes require quick judgement and confidence.","zh":"這類改動需要快速判斷和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes immediate adjustment without much time to plan.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有太多時間規劃的即時調整。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on-the-spot","meaning":"即場的","examples":[{"en":"An events manager may need to make on-the-spot decisions.","zh":"活動經理可能需要作出即場決定。"},{"en":"On-the-spot means immediate and made at the place where something is happening.","zh":"on-the-spot意思是即時並在事情發生現場作出的。"},{"en":"A coach may make an on-the-spot decision to stop a match because of lightning.","zh":"教練可能因閃電而即場決定停止比賽。"},{"en":"On-the-spot decisions are difficult because there is little time to consult others.","zh":"即場決定很困難，因為沒有太多時間諮詢他人。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in emergency or live-event situations.","zh":"這個短語常見於緊急或現場活動情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a problem you hadn’t anticipated","meaning":"你未有預料到的問題","examples":[{"en":"Holly may face a problem she had not anticipated.","zh":"Holly可能面對一個她未有預料到的問題。"},{"en":"A problem you hadn’t anticipated is a difficulty you did not expect beforehand.","zh":"a problem you hadn’t anticipated是你事前沒有預期的困難。"},{"en":"An organiser may face a problem she had not anticipated when the microphone stops working.","zh":"當咪高峰突然失靈，主辦方可能面對未有預料到的問題。"},{"en":"Unexpected problems test how flexible and calm a person is.","zh":"意外問題會考驗一個人有多靈活和冷靜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unplanned challenge.","zh":"這個短語描述計劃以外的挑戰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hadn’t anticipated","meaning":"未有預料到","examples":[{"en":"Holly may need to respond to problems she had not anticipated.","zh":"Holly可能需要回應她未有預料到的問題。"},{"en":"Hadn’t anticipated means had not expected or planned for something.","zh":"hadn’t anticipated意思是沒有預期或沒有為某事作準備。"},{"en":"The team had not anticipated that so many parents would arrive early.","zh":"團隊未有預料到會有這麼多家長提早到達。"},{"en":"When something is not anticipated, people must think quickly.","zh":"當某事未有預料到，人們必須快速思考。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about unexpected situations.","zh":"這個短語適合用於談論意外情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"time management","meaning":"時間管理","examples":[{"en":"The tutor asks Holly about her time management.","zh":"導師問Holly關於她的時間管理。"},{"en":"Time management is the ability to plan and use time effectively.","zh":"time management是有效規劃和使用時間的能力。"},{"en":"Good time management helps students meet deadlines without rushing at the last minute.","zh":"良好時間管理幫助學生準時完成任務，而不用最後一刻趕工。"},{"en":"Events managers need time management because delays can affect many people.","zh":"活動經理需要時間管理，因為延誤可以影響很多人。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in study and workplace skills.","zh":"這個短語常見於學習和職場技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"these days","meaning":"近來；現在","examples":[{"en":"The tutor asks how Holly’s time management is these days.","zh":"導師問Holly近來時間管理如何。"},{"en":"These days means nowadays or at the present time.","zh":"these days意思是現在或近來。"},{"en":"These days, many students use digital calendars to organise homework.","zh":"近來，許多學生使用數碼日曆安排功課。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the present with an earlier time or general past.","zh":"這個短語把現在與較早時間或過去一般情況作比較。"},{"en":"It sounds conversational and natural.","zh":"它聽起來口語而自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"work on it","meaning":"努力改善它","examples":[{"en":"Holly is working on her time management.","zh":"Holly正在努力改善自己的時間管理。"},{"en":"To work on it means to make effort to improve it.","zh":"work on it意思是努力改善它。"},{"en":"A student who often speaks too fast can work on pronunciation and pacing.","zh":"經常說話太快的學生可以努力改善發音和節奏。"},{"en":"Working on a weakness shows self-awareness and willingness to improve.","zh":"努力改善弱點顯示自我認知和進步意願。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing personal development.","zh":"這個短語常見於討論個人發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have a deadline","meaning":"有截止日期","examples":[{"en":"Holly works better when she has a deadline.","zh":"Holly有截止日期時工作得更好。"},{"en":"To have a deadline means to have a final time or date by which something must be finished.","zh":"have a deadline意思是有一個必須完成某事的最後時間或日期。"},{"en":"Students often work harder when they have a clear deadline for an assignment.","zh":"當功課有清晰截止日期，學生通常會更努力。"},{"en":"Deadlines create pressure but can also help people focus.","zh":"截止日期會製造壓力，但也可以幫助人集中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a time limit for completing work.","zh":"這個短語描述完成工作的時間限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"suit me","meaning":"適合我","examples":[{"en":"The work suits Holly because she performs better with deadlines.","zh":"這份工作適合Holly，因為她在有截止日期時表現較好。"},{"en":"Suit me means fit my needs, personality or way of working.","zh":"suit me意思是符合我的需要、性格或工作方式。"},{"en":"A flexible job may suit a student who has many evening classes.","zh":"彈性工作可能適合有很多夜校課的學生。"},{"en":"Work suits someone when its demands match how that person works best.","zh":"當工作的要求配合某人最佳工作方式，它就適合那個人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal fit.","zh":"這個短語描述個人適配度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"respond as the deadline approaches","meaning":"在截止日期接近時作出反應","examples":[{"en":"The tutor asks how Holly responds as a deadline approaches.","zh":"導師問Holly在截止日期接近時如何反應。"},{"en":"To respond as the deadline approaches means to react when the final time gets near.","zh":"respond as the deadline approaches意思是在最後期限接近時作出反應。"},{"en":"Some students become more focused as the deadline approaches.","zh":"有些學生在截止日期接近時會變得更集中。"},{"en":"A calm response near a deadline is important in event management.","zh":"在期限接近時保持冷靜反應，對活動管理很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase connects behaviour with increasing time pressure.","zh":"這個短語把行為與逐漸增加的時間壓力連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as the deadline approaches","meaning":"隨着截止日期接近","examples":[{"en":"Holly needs to stay calm as the deadline approaches.","zh":"隨着截止日期接近，Holly需要保持冷靜。"},{"en":"As the deadline approaches means while the final date or time is getting closer.","zh":"as the deadline approaches意思是當最後日期或時間越來越近。"},{"en":"As the deadline approaches, students may need to prioritise the most important tasks.","zh":"隨着截止日期接近，學生可能需要優先處理最重要任務。"},{"en":"Pressure often increases when there is less time left.","zh":"當剩餘時間變少，壓力通常會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the period before a deadline.","zh":"這個短語描述截止日期前的時段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"look calm","meaning":"看起來冷靜","examples":[{"en":"Holly knows she has to look calm under pressure.","zh":"Holly知道自己在壓力下必須看起來冷靜。"},{"en":"To look calm means to appear relaxed and in control, even if you feel stressed.","zh":"look calm意思是看起來放鬆和受控，即使內心有壓力。"},{"en":"A team leader should look calm during a technical problem so others do not panic.","zh":"團隊領袖在技術問題中應看起來冷靜，讓其他人不會恐慌。"},{"en":"Looking calm can help visitors, staff and clients trust your decisions.","zh":"看起來冷靜可以幫助訪客、職員和客戶信任你的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on outward appearance.","zh":"這個短語著重外在表現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be in a panic","meaning":"感到驚慌","examples":[{"en":"Holly may feel in a panic when a deadline is near.","zh":"截止日期接近時，Holly可能感到驚慌。"},{"en":"To be in a panic means to feel extremely worried and unable to think calmly.","zh":"be in a panic意思是非常擔心，無法冷靜思考。"},{"en":"A student may be in a panic if they lose their notes before an exam.","zh":"如果學生考試前遺失筆記，可能感到驚慌。"},{"en":"Panic can make people rush and make mistakes.","zh":"驚慌可以令人倉促行事並犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong anxious state.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈焦慮狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"think to yourself","meaning":"心裏想着","examples":[{"en":"The tutor tells Holly to think to herself that no one must know she is under pressure.","zh":"導師叫Holly心裏想着，不能讓別人知道她承受壓力。"},{"en":"To think to yourself means to say or realise something silently in your own mind.","zh":"think to yourself意思是在心裏默默說或意識到某事。"},{"en":"Before speaking on stage, a student may think to herself, “I can do this.”","zh":"上台演講前，學生可能心裏想着：「我可以做到。」"},{"en":"Quiet self-talk can help people stay focused under pressure.","zh":"內心自我對話可以幫助人在壓力下保持專注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an inner thought, not spoken words.","zh":"這個短語描述內心想法，而不是說出口的話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be under pressure","meaning":"承受壓力","examples":[{"en":"Holly must not let people know she is under pressure.","zh":"Holly不能讓別人知道她正在承受壓力。"},{"en":"To be under pressure means to feel stress because of demands, deadlines or responsibility.","zh":"be under pressure意思是因要求、期限或責任而感到壓力。"},{"en":"Event organisers are under pressure when the programme is running late.","zh":"當節目延誤，活動主辦方會承受壓力。"},{"en":"People under pressure may need to hide stress so others stay calm.","zh":"承受壓力的人可能需要隱藏壓力，讓其他人保持冷靜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a state of stress.","zh":"這個短語描述壓力狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"multi-task like crazy","meaning":"瘋狂地同時處理多項工作","examples":[{"en":"Holly may be multi-tasking like crazy during an event.","zh":"Holly在活動期間可能要瘋狂地同時處理多項工作。"},{"en":"To multi-task like crazy means to handle many tasks at the same time very intensely.","zh":"multi-task like crazy意思是非常密集地同時處理許多任務。"},{"en":"During a school fair, organisers may be multi-tasking like crazy as visitors arrive.","zh":"在學校賣物會中，當訪客到達時，主辦方可能瘋狂地同時處理多項工作。"},{"en":"Too much multi-tasking can be exhausting, even if it is sometimes necessary.","zh":"過多多工處理可以令人非常疲累，即使有時是必要的。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and emphasises how busy someone is.","zh":"這個短語較口語，強調某人非常忙碌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"creativity","meaning":"創意","examples":[{"en":"Creativity is another skill that events managers need.","zh":"創意是活動經理需要的另一項技能。"},{"en":"Creativity is the ability to produce new, useful or interesting ideas.","zh":"creativity是產生新穎、有用或有趣想法的能力。"},{"en":"Creativity helps organisers turn a simple event into something memorable.","zh":"創意幫助主辦方把簡單活動變成令人難忘的活動。"},{"en":"Creative people can find fresh solutions when plans do not work.","zh":"有創意的人在計劃行不通時，能找到新解決方法。"},{"en":"This word is important in design, events and problem-solving.","zh":"這個詞在設計、活動和解難中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"what we call","meaning":"我們所說的","examples":[{"en":"The tutor refers to what they call the “big picture” idea.","zh":"導師提到我們所說的「大方向」想法。"},{"en":"What we call means the term or name we use for something.","zh":"what we call意思是我們用來稱呼某事的術語或名稱。"},{"en":"Teachers often talk about what we call “active learning”.","zh":"老師常談到我們所說的「主動學習」。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a label or concept.","zh":"這個短語引入一個標籤或概念。"},{"en":"It helps explain terminology before discussing it.","zh":"它幫助在討論之前解釋術語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the big picture idea","meaning":"大方向的想法","examples":[{"en":"The client often has the big picture idea for an event.","zh":"客戶通常有活動的大方向想法。"},{"en":"The big picture idea is the general overall concept rather than the small details.","zh":"big picture idea是整體概念，而不是細小細節。"},{"en":"A client may have the big picture idea of a family-friendly outdoor festival.","zh":"客戶可能有一個家庭友善戶外節日的大方向想法。"},{"en":"The big picture helps guide decisions about style, purpose and audience.","zh":"大方向有助指引風格、目的和受眾方面的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts broad vision with practical details.","zh":"這個短語把廣泛願景與實際細節作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be up to","meaning":"由……負責","examples":[{"en":"It is up to the events manager to think of the details.","zh":"細節由活動經理負責想出。"},{"en":"If something is up to someone, that person is responsible for doing or deciding it.","zh":"如果某事be up to某人，意思是由該人負責做或決定。"},{"en":"It is up to the team leader to decide the final schedule.","zh":"最終時間表由團隊領袖負責決定。"},{"en":"This phrase gives responsibility to a specific person.","zh":"這個短語把責任交給特定人士。"},{"en":"It is common when explaining roles and duties.","zh":"它常見於解釋角色和職責。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"think of","meaning":"想出；考慮到","examples":[{"en":"The events manager must think of all the fine points.","zh":"活動經理必須想出所有細節。"},{"en":"To think of something means to consider or come up with it.","zh":"think of某事，意思是考慮到或想出它。"},{"en":"An organiser must think of where guests will park and where signs should go.","zh":"主辦方必須想到賓客在哪裏泊車，以及指示牌應放在哪裏。"},{"en":"Thinking of details early prevents confusion during the event.","zh":"及早想到細節可以防止活動期間出現混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental planning.","zh":"這個短語描述思考和規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the fine points","meaning":"細節","examples":[{"en":"The events manager must think of the fine points that make the event work.","zh":"活動經理必須想出令活動可行的細節。"},{"en":"The fine points are small but important details.","zh":"the fine points是細小但重要的細節。"},{"en":"In a wedding, the fine points may include lighting, seating cards and music timing.","zh":"在婚禮中，細節可能包括燈光、座位卡和音樂時間。"},{"en":"Small details can affect whether an event feels smooth and professional.","zh":"小細節可以影響活動是否感覺順暢和專業。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises careful attention to detail.","zh":"這個短語強調對細節的仔細注意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make it work","meaning":"令它可行","examples":[{"en":"The fine points help make the client’s idea work.","zh":"細節有助令客戶的想法可行。"},{"en":"To make it work means to make an idea, plan or arrangement successful in practice.","zh":"make it work意思是令一個想法、計劃或安排在實際上成功。"},{"en":"A teacher may adjust group sizes to make a class activity work.","zh":"老師可能調整小組人數，令課堂活動可行。"},{"en":"A good idea still needs practical details before it can work well.","zh":"好想法仍需要實際細節，才可以順利運作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on turning an idea into reality.","zh":"這個短語著重把想法變成現實。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"listen carefully to","meaning":"仔細聆聽……","examples":[{"en":"Holly needs to listen carefully to the client’s idea.","zh":"Holly需要仔細聆聽客戶的想法。"},{"en":"To listen carefully to someone or something means to pay close attention while listening.","zh":"listen carefully to某人或某事，意思是聆聽時非常專注。"},{"en":"Students should listen carefully to exam instructions before writing answers.","zh":"學生在寫答案前應仔細聆聽考試指示。"},{"en":"Careful listening helps people avoid misunderstanding important details.","zh":"仔細聆聽有助避免誤解重要細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes focused attention.","zh":"這個短語描述集中的注意力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fill in the gaps","meaning":"補上不足之處；補齊細節","examples":[{"en":"Holly needs to listen to the idea and fill in the gaps.","zh":"Holly需要聆聽想法並補齊細節。"},{"en":"To fill in the gaps means to add missing details or information.","zh":"fill in the gaps意思是加入缺失的細節或資料。"},{"en":"A project manager may fill in the gaps when a client gives only a rough plan.","zh":"當客戶只提供粗略計劃，項目經理可能需要補齊細節。"},{"en":"Filling in gaps turns a general idea into a workable plan.","zh":"補上不足之處能把一般想法變成可行計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes completing something incomplete.","zh":"這個短語描述完成不完整的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have a team working under you","meaning":"有一個團隊在你手下工作","examples":[{"en":"Holly will have a team working under her.","zh":"Holly會有一個團隊在她手下工作。"},{"en":"To have a team working under you means to supervise or manage people who report to you.","zh":"have a team working under you意思是監督或管理向你匯報的人。"},{"en":"A restaurant manager may have a team working under her during a busy dinner service.","zh":"餐廳經理在繁忙晚餐服務中可能有一個團隊在她手下工作。"},{"en":"Managing a team requires clear instructions and confidence.","zh":"管理團隊需要清晰指示和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes leadership responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述領導責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"key skill","meaning":"關鍵技能","examples":[{"en":"Leadership is another key skill for events managers.","zh":"領導能力是活動經理的另一項關鍵技能。"},{"en":"A key skill is an especially important ability for a task or job.","zh":"key skill是對某任務或工作尤其重要的能力。"},{"en":"Problem-solving is a key skill for anyone working in customer service.","zh":"解難能力是客戶服務工作者的一項關鍵技能。"},{"en":"Key skills affect whether someone can perform a role successfully.","zh":"關鍵技能會影響某人能否成功履行角色。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a skill that matters greatly.","zh":"這個短語指出非常重要的技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"leadership","meaning":"領導能力","examples":[{"en":"Leadership is important because Holly will manage a team.","zh":"領導能力很重要，因為Holly會管理一個團隊。"},{"en":"Leadership is the ability to guide, motivate and make decisions for a group.","zh":"leadership是引導、激勵並為團隊作決定的能力。"},{"en":"Good leadership helps a team stay calm and organised during pressure.","zh":"良好領導能力能幫助團隊在壓力下保持冷靜和有組織。"},{"en":"Leaders must listen to others but still make clear final decisions.","zh":"領袖必須聆聽他人，但仍要作出清晰最終決定。"},{"en":"This word is central to management and teamwork.","zh":"這個詞是管理和團隊合作的核心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have lots of ideas","meaning":"有很多想法","examples":[{"en":"Holly’s team may have lots of ideas too.","zh":"Holly的團隊也可能有很多想法。"},{"en":"To have lots of ideas means to think of many possible suggestions or plans.","zh":"have lots of ideas意思是想到許多可能建議或計劃。"},{"en":"Students may have lots of ideas when planning a charity event.","zh":"學生策劃慈善活動時可能有很多想法。"},{"en":"Many ideas are useful, but someone must choose which ones fit the event.","zh":"許多想法很有用，但必須有人選擇哪些適合活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creativity and participation.","zh":"這個短語描述創意和參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make the ultimate choices","meaning":"作出最終選擇","examples":[{"en":"Holly has to make the ultimate choices for the event.","zh":"Holly必須為活動作出最終選擇。"},{"en":"To make the ultimate choices means to make the final decisions after considering the options.","zh":"make the ultimate choices意思是在考慮選項後作出最終決定。"},{"en":"A director may listen to the team but make the ultimate choices about the performance.","zh":"導演可能聆聽團隊意見，但就表演作出最終選擇。"},{"en":"Final choices require responsibility because others will follow them.","zh":"最終選擇需要責任感，因為其他人會跟從。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights final decision-making authority.","zh":"這個短語突顯最終決策權。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"inside or out","meaning":"在室內還是室外","examples":[{"en":"The team must decide whether to have refreshments inside or out.","zh":"團隊必須決定茶點設在室內還是室外。"},{"en":"Inside or out means indoors or outdoors.","zh":"inside or out意思是在室內還是室外。"},{"en":"Organisers must decide whether to hold the welcome desk inside or out.","zh":"主辦方必須決定接待處設在室內還是室外。"},{"en":"Weather, space and crowd flow can affect whether something should be inside or out.","zh":"天氣、空間和人流可以影響某事應設在室內還是室外。"},{"en":"This phrase presents two location choices.","zh":"這個短語提出兩個地點選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be democratic","meaning":"民主一點","examples":[{"en":"Holly wonders whether it is better to be democratic.","zh":"Holly想知道是否民主一點會較好。"},{"en":"To be democratic means to let people share opinions and take part in decisions.","zh":"be democratic意思是讓人分享意見並參與決定。"},{"en":"A class leader may be democratic by asking classmates to vote on the activity.","zh":"班長可能透過請同學投票選活動來民主一點。"},{"en":"Being democratic can build teamwork, but final responsibility may still belong to one leader.","zh":"民主一點可以建立團隊合作，但最終責任可能仍屬於一位領袖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an inclusive decision-making style.","zh":"這個短語描述包容式決策風格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ultimate responsibility","meaning":"最終責任","examples":[{"en":"Holly has the ultimate responsibility for the event.","zh":"Holly對活動負有最終責任。"},{"en":"Ultimate responsibility is the final duty to make sure something is done properly.","zh":"ultimate responsibility是確保某事妥善完成的最終責任。"},{"en":"A head teacher has ultimate responsibility for safety during a school event.","zh":"校長對學校活動期間的安全負有最終責任。"},{"en":"When someone has ultimate responsibility, they cannot pass every decision to others.","zh":"當某人負有最終責任，就不能把每個決定都交給別人。"},{"en":"This phrase shows final accountability.","zh":"這個短語顯示最終問責。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"believe in","meaning":"相信……","examples":[{"en":"Holly needs to believe in what she thinks best.","zh":"Holly需要相信自己認為最好的做法。"},{"en":"To believe in something means to trust it or feel confident that it is right.","zh":"believe in某事，意思是信任它或相信它是正確的。"},{"en":"A leader must believe in the plan before asking the team to follow it.","zh":"領袖在要求團隊跟從計劃前，必須相信該計劃。"},{"en":"Believing in a decision helps people defend it under pressure.","zh":"相信一個決定能幫助人在壓力下捍衛它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes confidence in an idea or choice.","zh":"這個短語描述對想法或選擇的信心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"what you think best","meaning":"你認為最好的做法","examples":[{"en":"The tutor tells Holly to believe in what she thinks best.","zh":"導師叫Holly相信自己認為最好的做法。"},{"en":"What you think best means the option you judge to be the most suitable.","zh":"what you think best意思是你判斷為最合適的選項。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to choose what they think best after comparing the evidence.","zh":"老師可能要求學生比較證據後，選擇自己認為最好的做法。"},{"en":"Leaders must use judgement when there is no perfect answer.","zh":"當沒有完美答案時，領袖必須運用判斷力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on personal professional judgement.","zh":"這個短語著重個人的專業判斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be prepared to say","meaning":"準備好說……","examples":[{"en":"Holly should be prepared to say when an idea will not work.","zh":"Holly應準備好說明某個想法何時行不通。"},{"en":"To be prepared to say something means to be ready to state it clearly if necessary.","zh":"be prepared to say某事，意思是準備好在需要時清楚說出它。"},{"en":"A manager must be prepared to say when a plan is unsafe.","zh":"經理必須準備好說某計劃不安全。"},{"en":"Honest communication can prevent unrealistic ideas from causing problems.","zh":"誠實溝通可以防止不切實際想法造成問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes readiness to speak firmly.","zh":"這個短語描述準備好堅定發言。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"that’s a good idea but","meaning":"那是個好主意，但……","examples":[{"en":"Holly may need to say, “That’s a good idea, but it won’t work here.”","zh":"Holly可能需要說：「那是個好主意，但在這裏行不通。」"},{"en":"That’s a good idea, but introduces polite disagreement after acknowledging the value of an idea.","zh":"that’s a good idea, but是在承認想法有價值後，引入有禮反對。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “That’s a good idea, but we do not have enough time today.”","zh":"老師可能說：「那是個好主意，但我們今天沒有足夠時間。」"},{"en":"This phrase softens rejection by first recognising the positive side.","zh":"這個短語先承認正面一面，從而柔化拒絕。"},{"en":"It is useful in teamwork and leadership.","zh":"它適合用於團隊合作和領導。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"it won’t work here","meaning":"在這裏行不通","examples":[{"en":"A good idea may not work in a particular event.","zh":"好想法可能在某個特定活動中行不通。"},{"en":"It won’t work here means the idea is not suitable for this situation or place.","zh":"it won’t work here意思是該想法不適合這個情況或地方。"},{"en":"Outdoor games may be fun, but they will not work here if the hall is too small.","zh":"戶外遊戲可能有趣，但如果禮堂太小，在這裏就行不通。"},{"en":"Leaders must explain why an idea will not work in the current context.","zh":"領袖必須解釋為何某想法在當前語境中行不通。"},{"en":"This phrase separates general value from practical suitability.","zh":"這個短語把一般價值與實際適用性分開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"I see what you mean","meaning":"我明白你的意思","examples":[{"en":"Holly says, “I see what you mean.”","zh":"Holly說：「我明白你的意思。」"},{"en":"I see what you mean means I understand your point or explanation.","zh":"I see what you mean意思是我理解你的觀點或解釋。"},{"en":"After the tutor explains the risk, Holly may say, “I see what you mean.”","zh":"導師解釋風險後，Holly可能說：「我明白你的意思。」"},{"en":"This phrase shows understanding without necessarily adding a new opinion.","zh":"這個短語顯示理解，但不一定加入新意見。"},{"en":"It is common in polite conversation.","zh":"它常見於有禮對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the networking side of things","meaning":"人脈建立方面","examples":[{"en":"Holly asks about the networking side of things.","zh":"Holly問關於人脈建立方面的事。"},{"en":"The networking side of things means the part of a situation involving meeting useful professional contacts.","zh":"networking side of things意思是某情況中涉及認識有用專業人脈的部分。"},{"en":"In events management, the networking side of things can include meeting sponsors and venue managers.","zh":"在活動管理中，人脈建立方面可能包括認識贊助商和場地經理。"},{"en":"Networking helps students become known beyond their course.","zh":"人脈建立幫助學生在課程以外被認識。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific aspect of a wider topic.","zh":"這個短語指更大主題中的特定方面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"an area that","meaning":"一個……的範疇","examples":[{"en":"Networking is an area that many students worry about.","zh":"人脈建立是一個許多學生擔心的範疇。"},{"en":"An area that means a part or aspect of a subject that has a particular quality.","zh":"an area that意思是某主題中具有某特質的一部分或方面。"},{"en":"Public speaking is an area that many students find challenging.","zh":"公開演說是一個許多學生覺得具挑戰性的範疇。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a specific part of a broader topic.","zh":"這個短語引入較廣主題中的特定部分。"},{"en":"It is useful when focusing attention on one issue.","zh":"當要把注意力集中於一個問題時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"worry about","meaning":"擔心……","examples":[{"en":"Many students worry about networking.","zh":"許多學生擔心人脈建立。"},{"en":"To worry about something means to feel anxious or concerned about it.","zh":"worry about某事，意思是對它感到焦慮或憂慮。"},{"en":"Students often worry about interviews before they have much practice.","zh":"學生在未有太多練習前常擔心面試。"},{"en":"Worry can be reduced when people receive guidance and experience.","zh":"當人們得到指導和經驗，擔心可以減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes concern about a possible difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述對可能困難的憂慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have much experience to offer","meaning":"有很多經驗可以提供","examples":[{"en":"Students may not have much experience to offer others.","zh":"學生可能沒有很多經驗可以提供給別人。"},{"en":"To have much experience to offer means to possess useful past experience that can benefit others.","zh":"have much experience to offer意思是擁有能令他人受益的有用過往經驗。"},{"en":"New graduates may feel they do not have much experience to offer employers yet.","zh":"新畢業生可能覺得自己暫時沒有很多經驗可以提供給僱主。"},{"en":"Lack of experience does not mean a person has no ideas, energy or potential.","zh":"缺乏經驗不代表一個人沒有想法、活力或潛力。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing confidence and employability.","zh":"這個短語常見於討論信心和受聘能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"even without it","meaning":"即使沒有它","examples":[{"en":"Even without much experience, Holly can still be interesting and useful.","zh":"即使沒有很多經驗，Holly仍可以有趣和有用。"},{"en":"Even without it means despite not having that thing.","zh":"even without it意思是即使沒有那件東西。"},{"en":"Even without a famous degree, a student can impress employers with strong work.","zh":"即使沒有名校學位，學生仍可以用出色作品令僱主留下好印象。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something helpful is not absolutely necessary.","zh":"這個短語顯示某個有用因素並非絕對必要。"},{"en":"It is useful when encouraging someone who lacks one advantage.","zh":"當鼓勵缺少某項優勢的人時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"useful ideas","meaning":"實用的想法","examples":[{"en":"Students can still have useful ideas even without much experience.","zh":"即使沒有很多經驗，學生仍可以有實用的想法。"},{"en":"Useful ideas are suggestions or thoughts that can help solve a problem or improve something.","zh":"useful ideas是能幫助解決問題或改善某事的建議或想法。"},{"en":"A new volunteer may have useful ideas because they see the event with fresh eyes.","zh":"新義工可能有實用的想法，因為他們以新鮮眼光看活動。"},{"en":"Ideas do not have to come only from experienced people.","zh":"想法不一定只來自有經驗的人。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights practical value in thinking.","zh":"這個短語突顯思考中的實際價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the more…, the better","meaning":"越……越好","examples":[{"en":"The more people Holly impresses, the better.","zh":"Holly令越多人留下好印象越好。"},{"en":"The more…, the better means a larger amount will produce a better result.","zh":"the more…, the better意思是數量越多，結果越好。"},{"en":"The more practice students get before the exam, the better.","zh":"學生考試前練習越多越好。"},{"en":"This structure shows that increasing one thing improves the outcome.","zh":"這個結構顯示增加一件事會改善結果。"},{"en":"It is useful for giving general advice.","zh":"它適合用於提供一般建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"impress people","meaning":"令別人留下好印象","examples":[{"en":"Networking helps Holly impress more people.","zh":"人脈建立幫助Holly令更多人留下好印象。"},{"en":"To impress people means to make them admire, remember or respect you.","zh":"impress people意思是令人欣賞、記住或尊重你。"},{"en":"A student may impress people by speaking clearly and showing good preparation.","zh":"學生可以透過說話清晰和準備充分令別人留下好印象。"},{"en":"Impressions matter because people may remember you later when opportunities appear.","zh":"印象很重要，因為機會出現時，人們日後可能記得你。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in careers and networking.","zh":"這個短語在職業和人脈建立中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"apply for a real job","meaning":"申請真正的工作","examples":[{"en":"Networking may help Holly when she applies for a real job.","zh":"當Holly申請真正的工作時，人脈建立可能會幫到她。"},{"en":"To apply for a real job means to formally seek paid employment after training or study.","zh":"apply for a real job意思是在培訓或學習後正式尋找有薪工作。"},{"en":"Students may apply for a real job after completing their work placement.","zh":"學生完成工作實習後，可能申請真正的工作。"},{"en":"Contacts made during training can support future job applications.","zh":"培訓期間建立的人脈可以支援日後求職。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts student experience with actual employment.","zh":"這個短語把學生經驗與實際就業作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"think ahead","meaning":"向前想；為將來打算","examples":[{"en":"The tutor advises Holly to think ahead.","zh":"導師建議Holly為將來打算。"},{"en":"To think ahead means to plan for the future instead of only focusing on the present.","zh":"think ahead意思是為未來作計劃，而不只是專注現在。"},{"en":"Students should think ahead when choosing placements that may lead to jobs.","zh":"學生選擇可能通向工作的實習時，應為將來打算。"},{"en":"Thinking ahead helps people make choices that support long-term goals.","zh":"向前想能幫助人作出支持長遠目標的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages future-focused planning.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵面向未來的規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"remember what your ambitions are","meaning":"記住自己的抱負","examples":[{"en":"Holly should remember what her ambitions are.","zh":"Holly應記住自己的抱負。"},{"en":"To remember what your ambitions are means to keep your long-term goals in mind.","zh":"remember what your ambitions are意思是把自己的長遠目標記在心上。"},{"en":"A student who wants to work in events should remember that ambition when choosing projects.","zh":"想從事活動工作的學生，在選擇項目時應記住這個抱負。"},{"en":"Remembering ambitions helps people choose opportunities that move them closer to their goals.","zh":"記住抱負能幫助人選擇令自己更接近目標的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase connects present choices with future dreams.","zh":"這個短語把現在選擇與未來夢想連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"keep them in mind","meaning":"把它們記在心上","examples":[{"en":"Holly should keep her ambitions in mind.","zh":"Holly應把自己的抱負記在心上。"},{"en":"To keep them in mind means to continue thinking about them when making decisions.","zh":"keep them in mind意思是在作決定時繼續想着它們。"},{"en":"Students should keep their career goals in mind when choosing work placements.","zh":"學生選擇工作實習時，應把職業目標記在心上。"},{"en":"Keeping goals in mind prevents people from being distracted by short-term choices.","zh":"把目標記在心上，可以防止人被短期選擇分散注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes remembering something important as guidance.","zh":"這個短語描述把重要事情記住作為指引。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/listening/Practice 14/task-4":[{"front":"a majority of","meaning":"大部分……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists believe that a majority of the Earth’s bird population migrates in some fashion or other.","zh":"科學家相信，地球上大部分鳥類族群都會以某種方式遷徙。"},{"en":"A majority of means more than half of a group.","zh":"大部分意思是某群體中超過一半。"},{"en":"A majority of students in the class chose the drama project.","zh":"班上大部分學生選擇了戲劇專題。"},{"en":"If a majority of birds migrate, migration is not a rare behaviour.","zh":"如果大部分鳥類都會遷徙，遷徙就不是罕見行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the larger part of a group.","zh":"這個短語適合用於描述一個群體中的較大部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"bird population","meaning":"鳥類族群","examples":[{"en":"Scientists believe that a majority of the Earth’s bird population migrates.","zh":"科學家相信，地球上大部分鳥類族群都會遷徙。"},{"en":"Bird population means the total number or group of birds in a place or on Earth.","zh":"鳥類族群意思是在某地或地球上的鳥類總數或群體。"},{"en":"The bird population in a wetland may rise during migration season.","zh":"濕地的鳥類族群可能在遷徙季節增加。"},{"en":"Studying bird populations helps scientists understand changes in the environment.","zh":"研究鳥類族群有助科學家理解環境變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in ecology and conservation.","zh":"這個短語常見於生態學和保育。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"migrate in some fashion or other","meaning":"以某種方式遷徙","examples":[{"en":"Most birds migrate in some fashion or other.","zh":"大多數鳥類都會以某種方式遷徙。"},{"en":"To migrate in some fashion or other means to move from one place to another in one way or another.","zh":"以某種方式遷徙意思是以某種形式從一地移動到另一地。"},{"en":"Some birds migrate long distances, while others migrate only between nearby habitats.","zh":"有些鳥類長距離遷徙，另一些只在附近棲息地之間遷徙。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that migration can take many different forms.","zh":"這個短語暗示遷徙可以有許多不同形式。"},{"en":"It is useful when the exact method or distance varies.","zh":"當確切方法或距離有所不同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"travel seasonally","meaning":"季節性遷徙","examples":[{"en":"Some birds travel seasonally for relatively short distances.","zh":"有些鳥類會作相對短距離的季節性遷徙。"},{"en":"To travel seasonally means to move at particular times of year.","zh":"季節性遷徙意思是在一年中特定季節移動。"},{"en":"Some animals travel seasonally to find food, warmth or safer breeding places.","zh":"有些動物會季節性遷徙，以尋找食物、溫暖或更安全的繁殖地。"},{"en":"Seasonal travel often follows changes in weather and food supply.","zh":"季節性移動通常跟隨天氣和食物供應變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when movement happens according to the seasons.","zh":"當移動按季節發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"relatively short distances","meaning":"相對較短距離","examples":[{"en":"Some birds travel seasonally for relatively short distances.","zh":"有些鳥類會作相對較短距離的季節性遷徙。"},{"en":"Relatively short distances means distances that are short when compared with others.","zh":"相對較短距離意思是與其他距離相比較短的距離。"},{"en":"Some birds move relatively short distances from valleys to nearby hills.","zh":"有些鳥類會從山谷移到附近山丘，距離相對較短。"},{"en":"A short migration may still be important for survival.","zh":"短距離遷徙仍可能對生存很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distance by comparison, not an exact number.","zh":"這個短語透過比較描述距離，而不是提供精確數字。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"winter habitats","meaning":"冬季棲息地","examples":[{"en":"Some birds move from their winter habitats in lowlands to mountaintops.","zh":"有些鳥類會從低地的冬季棲息地移到山頂。"},{"en":"Winter habitats are places where animals live during the winter.","zh":"冬季棲息地是動物在冬天生活的地方。"},{"en":"A bird’s winter habitat may be warmer and have more available food.","zh":"鳥類的冬季棲息地可能較溫暖，並有更多可取得的食物。"},{"en":"Understanding winter habitats helps scientists protect migration routes.","zh":"了解冬季棲息地有助科學家保護遷徙路線。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing seasonal animal movement.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論動物季節性移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lowlands","meaning":"低地","examples":[{"en":"Some birds spend winter in lowlands.","zh":"有些鳥類在低地過冬。"},{"en":"Lowlands are areas of land that are lower and usually flatter than nearby mountains or hills.","zh":"低地是比附近山脈或山丘較低、通常較平坦的土地。"},{"en":"Lowlands may be warmer than mountain areas in winter.","zh":"低地在冬天可能比山區較溫暖。"},{"en":"Some birds use lowlands as feeding grounds during colder months.","zh":"有些鳥類在較寒冷月份把低地用作覓食地。"},{"en":"This word describes a type of landscape.","zh":"這個詞描述一種地形。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mountain tops","meaning":"山頂","examples":[{"en":"Some birds move from lowlands to mountain tops for the summer.","zh":"有些鳥類夏天會從低地移到山頂。"},{"en":"Mountain tops are the highest parts of mountains.","zh":"山頂是山的最高部分。"},{"en":"Mountain tops can provide cooler temperatures during summer.","zh":"山頂在夏天可以提供較涼的溫度。"},{"en":"Birds may move to mountain tops if food or nesting conditions are better there.","zh":"如果山頂有較好的食物或築巢條件，鳥類可能會移到那裏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a high-altitude habitat.","zh":"這個短語描述高海拔棲息地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Arctic Tern","meaning":"北極燕鷗","examples":[{"en":"The Arctic Tern travels more than 25,000 miles seasonally.","zh":"北極燕鷗每季遷徙超過 25,000 英里。"},{"en":"The Arctic Tern is a seabird famous for very long-distance migration.","zh":"北極燕鷗是一種以長距離遷徙聞名的海鳥。"},{"en":"An Arctic Tern may travel between cold northern and southern regions during the year.","zh":"北極燕鷗一年中可能在寒冷的北方和南方地區之間移動。"},{"en":"Its migration is often used as an example of extreme bird travel.","zh":"牠的遷徙常被用作極端鳥類遷徙的例子。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific bird species.","zh":"這個短語命名一種特定鳥類物種。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"between the northern and southern poles","meaning":"在南北兩極之間","examples":[{"en":"The Arctic Tern travels between the northern and southern poles.","zh":"北極燕鷗在南北兩極之間遷徙。"},{"en":"Between the northern and southern poles means from the Arctic region to the Antarctic region, or vice versa.","zh":"在南北兩極之間意思是從北極地區到南極地區，或相反方向。"},{"en":"A journey between the northern and southern poles covers an enormous part of the planet.","zh":"在南北兩極之間的旅程橫跨地球極大部分。"},{"en":"Very few animals travel such a long distance each year.","zh":"很少動物每年會移動如此漫長的距離。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the extreme range of migration.","zh":"這個短語突顯遷徙範圍極端廣闊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"bird migration","meaning":"鳥類遷徙","examples":[{"en":"Bird migration has been studied over many centuries.","zh":"鳥類遷徙歷經多個世紀被研究。"},{"en":"Bird migration is the seasonal or regular movement of birds from one place to another.","zh":"鳥類遷徙是鳥類從一地到另一地的季節性或定期移動。"},{"en":"Bird migration may happen because of food, temperature or breeding needs.","zh":"鳥類遷徙可能因食物、溫度或繁殖需要而發生。"},{"en":"Scientists study bird migration to understand routes, timing and survival challenges.","zh":"科學家研究鳥類遷徙，以了解路線、時間和生存挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to ornithology and ecology.","zh":"這個短語是鳥類學和生態學的核心概念。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over many centuries","meaning":"歷經多個世紀","examples":[{"en":"Bird migration has been studied over many centuries.","zh":"鳥類遷徙歷經多個世紀被研究。"},{"en":"Over many centuries means during a period of several hundred years.","zh":"歷經多個世紀意思是在幾百年的時間裏。"},{"en":"Human ideas about nature have changed over many centuries.","zh":"人類對自然的想法歷經多個世紀已有改變。"},{"en":"A mystery studied over many centuries may attract many different theories.","zh":"一個被研究多個世紀的謎團可能吸引許多不同理論。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a long historical time frame.","zh":"這個短語提供很長的歷史時間框架。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"through a variety of observations","meaning":"透過各種觀察","examples":[{"en":"Bird migration has been studied through a variety of observations.","zh":"鳥類遷徙一直透過各種觀察被研究。"},{"en":"Through a variety of observations means by using many different kinds of watching, recording or evidence.","zh":"透過各種觀察意思是利用不同類型的觀看、記錄或證據。"},{"en":"Scientists study animal behaviour through a variety of observations in the field and laboratory.","zh":"科學家透過野外和實驗室中的各種觀察研究動物行為。"},{"en":"Different observations can reveal different parts of a mystery.","zh":"不同觀察可以揭示謎團的不同部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a research method based on many sources of evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述基於多種證據來源的研究方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"until relatively recently","meaning":"直到相對近代","examples":[{"en":"Until relatively recently, where birds went in winter was a mystery.","zh":"直到相對近代，鳥類冬天去了哪裏仍是謎團。"},{"en":"Until relatively recently means up to a time not very long ago when compared with the whole history of the topic.","zh":"直到相對近代意思是直到相對於整個主題歷史而言不算很久以前的時期。"},{"en":"Until relatively recently, many people did not understand how diseases spread.","zh":"直到相對近代，許多人仍不了解疾病如何傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when old beliefs changed because of new knowledge.","zh":"當舊信念因新知識而改變時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It compares recent understanding with a much longer past.","zh":"它把近期理解與更漫長的過去作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"something of a mystery","meaning":"某種謎團","examples":[{"en":"Where birds went in winter was considered something of a mystery.","zh":"鳥類冬天去了哪裏曾被視為某種謎團。"},{"en":"Something of a mystery means partly or quite mysterious and not fully understood.","zh":"某種謎團意思是有點或相當神秘，並未被完全理解。"},{"en":"The disappearance of the documents was something of a mystery to the office staff.","zh":"文件消失對辦公室職員來說是某種謎團。"},{"en":"A topic can remain a mystery when there is not enough evidence.","zh":"當證據不足，某個主題可以一直是謎團。"},{"en":"This phrase is softer than saying something is completely mysterious.","zh":"這個短語比說完全神秘語氣較柔和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lack of modern science and technology","meaning":"缺乏現代科學與技術","examples":[{"en":"The lack of modern science and technology led to many strange theories.","zh":"缺乏現代科學與技術導致許多奇怪理論。"},{"en":"A lack of modern science and technology means not having today’s scientific knowledge or tools.","zh":"缺乏現代科學與技術意思是沒有今天的科學知識或工具。"},{"en":"In the past, the lack of modern technology made long-distance tracking almost impossible.","zh":"在過去，缺乏現代科技令長距離追蹤幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"When people lack evidence, they may create imaginative explanations.","zh":"當人們缺乏證據，就可能創造富想像力的解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why earlier theories could be inaccurate.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何早期理論可能不準確。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"led to","meaning":"導致；引致","examples":[{"en":"The lack of modern science and technology led to many theories.","zh":"缺乏現代科學與技術導致許多理論。"},{"en":"Led to means caused or resulted in something.","zh":"導致意思是造成或引起某事。"},{"en":"Heavy rain led to flooding in several villages.","zh":"大雨導致幾條村出現水浸。"},{"en":"In science, limited evidence can lead to mistaken conclusions.","zh":"在科學中，有限證據可能導致錯誤結論。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with its result.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"error-filled","meaning":"充滿錯誤的","examples":[{"en":"Some early theories are now recognised as error-filled.","zh":"有些早期理論現在被認為是充滿錯誤的。"},{"en":"Error-filled means containing many mistakes.","zh":"充滿錯誤的意思是包含許多錯誤。"},{"en":"An error-filled report is hard to trust because the facts may be wrong.","zh":"充滿錯誤的報告難以信任，因為事實可能錯了。"},{"en":"Early scientific ideas can seem error-filled once better tools become available.","zh":"當更好工具出現後，早期科學想法可能顯得充滿錯誤。"},{"en":"This adjective strongly criticises accuracy.","zh":"這個形容詞強烈批評準確性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"somewhat amusing","meaning":"有點好笑","examples":[{"en":"Some early theories now seem somewhat amusing.","zh":"有些早期理論現在看來有點好笑。"},{"en":"Somewhat amusing means a little funny or entertaining.","zh":"有點好笑意思是稍微有趣或令人發笑。"},{"en":"The old idea that birds went to the moon may seem somewhat amusing today.","zh":"鳥類飛到月球這個舊想法今天可能顯得有點好笑。"},{"en":"A theory can be amusing now even if people once took it seriously.","zh":"一個理論現在可以令人覺得好笑，即使人們曾經認真看待它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mild humour rather than strong laughter.","zh":"這個短語描述輕微幽默，而不是大笑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hibernation theory","meaning":"冬眠理論","examples":[{"en":"Hibernation theory claimed that birds spent winter underwater.","zh":"冬眠理論聲稱鳥類在水底過冬。"},{"en":"Hibernation theory is the idea that some birds survived winter by entering a sleep-like state.","zh":"冬眠理論是認為有些鳥類透過進入類似睡眠的狀態度過冬天的想法。"},{"en":"Some people once used hibernation theory to explain why birds disappeared in cold months.","zh":"有些人曾用冬眠理論解釋鳥類為何在寒冷月份消失。"},{"en":"The theory now seems incorrect because birds migrate rather than hibernate underwater.","zh":"這個理論現在看來不正確，因為鳥類是遷徙，而不是在水底冬眠。"},{"en":"This phrase names an old explanation for seasonal bird disappearance.","zh":"這個短語命名一個關於鳥類季節性消失的舊解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"take something for example","meaning":"以……為例","examples":[{"en":"Take hibernation theory for example.","zh":"以冬眠理論為例。"},{"en":"Take something for example means use this thing as an example to explain a point.","zh":"以某事為例意思是用這件事作例子來解釋重點。"},{"en":"Take the Arctic Tern for example: it shows how far some birds can migrate.","zh":"以北極燕鷗為例：牠顯示有些鳥類可以遷徙多遠。"},{"en":"This phrase helps a speaker introduce a specific case.","zh":"這個短語幫助說話者引入具體例子。"},{"en":"It is common in explanations and presentations.","zh":"它常見於解釋和匯報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"commonly believed that","meaning":"人們普遍相信","examples":[{"en":"It was commonly believed that birds went underwater to hibernate.","zh":"人們普遍相信鳥類會潛入水底冬眠。"},{"en":"Commonly believed that means many people thought something was true.","zh":"人們普遍相信某事意思是很多人認為某事是真的。"},{"en":"It was commonly believed that the Earth was the centre of the universe.","zh":"人們曾普遍相信地球是宇宙中心。"},{"en":"Common beliefs can later be disproved by evidence.","zh":"普遍信念之後可以被證據推翻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a widespread idea.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛流傳的想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go underwater","meaning":"潛入水底","examples":[{"en":"People once believed that birds went underwater in winter.","zh":"人們曾相信鳥類冬天會潛入水底。"},{"en":"To go underwater means to move below the surface of water.","zh":"潛入水底意思是移到水面以下。"},{"en":"Ducks can go underwater briefly while feeding.","zh":"鴨子覓食時可以短暫潛入水底。"},{"en":"The idea that birds went underwater for the whole winter now seems unlikely.","zh":"鳥類整個冬天潛入水底這個想法現在看來不太可能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement beneath water.","zh":"這個短語描述在水面以下移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hibernate","meaning":"冬眠","examples":[{"en":"People believed that birds hibernated in the seas and oceans.","zh":"人們相信鳥類在海洋中冬眠。"},{"en":"To hibernate means to spend winter in a state of very low activity.","zh":"冬眠意思是在冬天進入活動量很低的狀態。"},{"en":"Bears and some small mammals may hibernate during cold months.","zh":"熊和一些小型哺乳動物可能在寒冷月份冬眠。"},{"en":"Hibernation helps animals save energy when food is scarce.","zh":"冬眠幫助動物在食物稀少時節省能量。"},{"en":"This verb is used for seasonal dormancy in animals.","zh":"這個動詞用於描述動物的季節性休眠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the seas and oceans","meaning":"在海洋中","examples":[{"en":"Some people believed that birds hibernated in the seas and oceans.","zh":"有些人相信鳥類在海洋中冬眠。"},{"en":"In the seas and oceans means in large bodies of salt water.","zh":"在海洋中意思是在大型鹹水水域裏。"},{"en":"Many marine animals live in the seas and oceans.","zh":"許多海洋動物生活在海洋中。"},{"en":"Early thinkers sometimes imagined strange explanations for what happened in the seas and oceans.","zh":"早期思想家有時會想像關於海洋中發生事情的奇怪解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a marine location.","zh":"這個短語描述海洋位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"regular appearance and disappearance","meaning":"定期出現與消失","examples":[{"en":"Another theory explained the regular appearance and disappearance of birds.","zh":"另一個理論解釋鳥類的定期出現與消失。"},{"en":"Regular appearance and disappearance means something appears and vanishes repeatedly according to a pattern.","zh":"定期出現與消失意思是某物按照模式反覆出現和消失。"},{"en":"The regular appearance and disappearance of certain insects can be linked to seasons.","zh":"某些昆蟲的定期出現與消失可以與季節有關。"},{"en":"Before migration was understood, repeated bird disappearance needed explanation.","zh":"在遷徙被理解之前，鳥類反覆消失需要解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated natural pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述重複的自然模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"spend winter hidden in","meaning":"藏在……過冬","examples":[{"en":"Some people believed that birds spent winter hidden in mud.","zh":"有些人相信鳥類藏在泥中過冬。"},{"en":"To spend winter hidden in a place means to stay concealed there during the winter months.","zh":"藏在某地過冬意思是在冬季月份隱藏並停留在那裏。"},{"en":"Some animals spend winter hidden in burrows to avoid cold weather.","zh":"有些動物藏在洞穴中過冬，以避開寒冷天氣。"},{"en":"People once imagined birds stayed hidden when they could no longer see them.","zh":"人們曾想像當他們看不見鳥時，鳥類就是藏起來了。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a supposed winter hiding place.","zh":"這個短語描述假定的冬季藏身地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"till the weather changed","meaning":"直至天氣轉變","examples":[{"en":"Birds were thought to stay hidden till the weather changed.","zh":"人們認為鳥類會一直藏着，直至天氣轉變。"},{"en":"Till the weather changed means until the weather became different, usually warmer or more suitable.","zh":"直至天氣轉變意思是直到天氣變得不同，通常是更暖或更合適。"},{"en":"Farmers waited till the weather changed before planting the seeds.","zh":"農夫等到天氣轉變才播種。"},{"en":"Seasonal changes often affect animal movement and behaviour.","zh":"季節變化常影響動物移動和行為。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a condition that ends a period of waiting.","zh":"這個短語標示結束等待期的條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"become abundant again","meaning":"再次變得充足","examples":[{"en":"Birds were thought to reappear when food became abundant again.","zh":"人們認為當食物再次變得充足時，鳥類會重新出現。"},{"en":"To become abundant again means to become plentiful again after a period of scarcity.","zh":"再次變得充足意思是在一段缺乏期後重新變得大量。"},{"en":"In spring, insects become abundant again, giving birds more food.","zh":"春天時，昆蟲再次變得充足，為鳥類提供更多食物。"},{"en":"Animals may move when food becomes scarce and return when it becomes abundant again.","zh":"動物可能在食物短缺時移動，並在食物再次充足時返回。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the return of plentiful supply.","zh":"這個短語描述供應重新變多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"persisted until","meaning":"一直持續到","examples":[{"en":"The theory that some birds hibernate persisted until the 1940s.","zh":"有些鳥類會冬眠的理論一直持續到 1940 年代。"},{"en":"Persisted until means continued to exist or be believed up to a certain time.","zh":"一直持續到某時意思是一直存在或被相信直到某個時間。"},{"en":"Some old medical beliefs persisted until modern experiments disproved them.","zh":"有些舊醫學信念一直持續到現代實驗推翻它們。"},{"en":"A theory can persist for a long time if people lack better evidence.","zh":"如果人們缺乏更好證據，一個理論可以持續很久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continuation over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間延續。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"experiments were done on","meaning":"對……進行實驗","examples":[{"en":"Experiments were done on caged birds in the 1940s.","zh":"1940 年代，人們對籠中鳥進行實驗。"},{"en":"Experiments were done on something means tests were carried out using that subject.","zh":"對某物進行實驗意思是用該對象進行測試。"},{"en":"Experiments were done on plants to see how light affected growth.","zh":"人們對植物進行實驗，以觀察光線如何影響生長。"},{"en":"Scientific experiments can challenge long-held beliefs.","zh":"科學實驗可以挑戰長久以來的信念。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research descriptions.","zh":"這個短語常見於研究描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"caged birds","meaning":"籠中鳥","examples":[{"en":"Experiments on caged birds showed that birds have no hibernation instinct.","zh":"對籠中鳥的實驗顯示，鳥類沒有冬眠本能。"},{"en":"Caged birds are birds kept inside cages.","zh":"籠中鳥是被關在籠子裏的鳥。"},{"en":"Researchers can observe caged birds closely, but the setting is not the same as the wild.","zh":"研究人員可以近距離觀察籠中鳥，但該環境與野外不同。"},{"en":"Experiments with caged birds helped test ideas about migration and hibernation.","zh":"對籠中鳥的實驗幫助測試關於遷徙和冬眠的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes birds kept in controlled conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述被置於受控環境中的鳥。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"demonstrated that","meaning":"證明","examples":[{"en":"The experiments demonstrated that birds have no hibernation instinct.","zh":"實驗證明鳥類沒有冬眠本能。"},{"en":"Demonstrated that means showed clearly through evidence or example.","zh":"證明某事意思是透過證據或例子清楚顯示它。"},{"en":"The results demonstrated that regular practice improved students’ pronunciation.","zh":"結果證明定期練習改善了學生發音。"},{"en":"Scientific evidence can demonstrate that an old theory is wrong.","zh":"科學證據可以證明舊理論是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting research findings.","zh":"這個短語適合用於報告研究發現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hibernation instinct","meaning":"冬眠本能","examples":[{"en":"The experiments showed that birds have no hibernation instinct.","zh":"實驗顯示鳥類沒有冬眠本能。"},{"en":"Hibernation instinct would be a natural tendency to enter hibernation during winter.","zh":"冬眠本能是動物在冬天自然進入冬眠的傾向。"},{"en":"Some animals have strong instincts that help them survive seasonal changes.","zh":"有些動物有強烈本能，幫助牠們應對季節變化。"},{"en":"If birds lack a hibernation instinct, migration becomes a more likely explanation for disappearance.","zh":"如果鳥類缺乏冬眠本能，遷徙就更可能解釋牠們的消失。"},{"en":"This phrase combines animal behaviour with seasonal survival.","zh":"這個短語結合動物行為與季節性生存。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"naturalists and philosophers","meaning":"自然學家及哲學家","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle was one of the earliest naturalists and philosophers from ancient Greece.","zh":"Aristotle 是古希臘最早期的自然學家及哲學家之一。"},{"en":"Naturalists and philosophers are people who study nature and think deeply about knowledge, life or the world.","zh":"自然學家及哲學家是研究自然並深入思考知識、生命或世界的人。"},{"en":"Early naturalists and philosophers often observed animals without modern scientific tools.","zh":"早期自然學家及哲學家常在沒有現代科學工具下觀察動物。"},{"en":"Their ideas helped shape later scientific questions, even when some conclusions were wrong.","zh":"他們的想法幫助塑造後來的科學問題，即使有些結論是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes thinkers who studied nature and ideas.","zh":"這個短語描述研究自然和思想的學者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ancient Greece","meaning":"古希臘","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle was a philosopher from ancient Greece.","zh":"Aristotle 是來自古希臘的哲學家。"},{"en":"Ancient Greece was a civilisation in the Mediterranean world many centuries ago.","zh":"古希臘是許多世紀以前地中海世界的一個文明。"},{"en":"Many important ideas in philosophy, politics and science came from ancient Greece.","zh":"許多哲學、政治和科學的重要思想來自古希臘。"},{"en":"Thinkers from ancient Greece often tried to explain nature through observation and reasoning.","zh":"古希臘思想家常透過觀察和推理嘗試解釋自然。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a historical civilisation.","zh":"這個短語指一個歷史文明。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the first writer to discuss","meaning":"第一位討論……的作家","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle was the first writer to discuss the disappearance of some bird species.","zh":"Aristotle 是第一位討論某些鳥類物種消失的作家。"},{"en":"The first writer to discuss something means the earliest known author to write about that topic.","zh":"第一位討論某事的作家意思是已知最早書寫該主題的作者。"},{"en":"A historian may identify the first writer to discuss a particular ancient custom.","zh":"歷史學家可能找出第一位討論某種古代習俗的作家。"},{"en":"Being first to discuss a topic does not mean the explanation was correct.","zh":"第一位討論某主題並不代表解釋一定正確。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights historical priority.","zh":"這個短語突顯歷史上的先後地位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"disappearance and reappearance","meaning":"消失與再次出現","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle discussed the disappearance and reappearance of some bird species.","zh":"Aristotle 討論某些鳥類物種的消失與再次出現。"},{"en":"Disappearance and reappearance means going away from view and later appearing again.","zh":"消失與再次出現意思是從視線中離開，之後再出現。"},{"en":"The disappearance and reappearance of seasonal insects can be linked to life cycles.","zh":"季節性昆蟲的消失與再次出現可以與生命週期有關。"},{"en":"Before migration was understood, bird disappearance and reappearance seemed mysterious.","zh":"在遷徙被理解之前，鳥類消失與再次出現顯得神秘。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated pattern of vanishing and returning.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆消失和回來的模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"bird species","meaning":"鳥類物種","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle discussed the seasonal disappearance of some bird species.","zh":"Aristotle 討論某些鳥類物種的季節性消失。"},{"en":"Bird species are distinct types of birds that can be scientifically identified.","zh":"鳥類物種是可被科學識別的不同鳥類類型。"},{"en":"Robins and redstarts are different bird species.","zh":"知更鳥和紅尾鴝是不同鳥類物種。"},{"en":"Studying different bird species helps scientists compare behaviour and migration patterns.","zh":"研究不同鳥類物種有助科學家比較行為和遷徙模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in biology and bird studies.","zh":"這個短語常見於生物學和鳥類研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at certain times of year","meaning":"在一年中特定時間","examples":[{"en":"Some bird species disappeared at certain times of year.","zh":"有些鳥類物種會在一年中特定時間消失。"},{"en":"At certain times of year means during particular seasons or months.","zh":"在一年中特定時間意思是在特定季節或月份。"},{"en":"Some flowers appear only at certain times of year.","zh":"有些花只會在一年中特定時間出現。"},{"en":"Seasonal patterns often made early observers wonder where animals had gone.","zh":"季節性模式常令早期觀察者想知道動物去了哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes timing linked to the yearly cycle.","zh":"這個短語描述與一年循環相關的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"theory of transmutation","meaning":"物種轉變理論","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle developed the theory of transmutation.","zh":"Aristotle 發展了物種轉變理論。"},{"en":"The theory of transmutation was the idea that one species could change into another.","zh":"物種轉變理論是認為一個物種可以變成另一個物種的想法。"},{"en":"Aristotle used the theory of transmutation to explain seasonal changes in birds.","zh":"Aristotle 用物種轉變理論解釋鳥類的季節性變化。"},{"en":"This theory is now considered incorrect, but it shows how people tried to explain observations.","zh":"這個理論現在被認為不正確，但它顯示人們如何嘗試解釋觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase names an early theory about species change.","zh":"這個短語命名一個關於物種變化的早期理論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"seasonal change","meaning":"季節性轉變","examples":[{"en":"Transmutation was thought to be the seasonal change of one species into another.","zh":"物種轉變被認為是一個物種變成另一個物種的季節性轉變。"},{"en":"Seasonal change means change that happens according to the seasons.","zh":"季節性轉變意思是按照季節發生的變化。"},{"en":"Leaves changing colour in autumn are an example of seasonal change.","zh":"樹葉在秋天變色就是季節性轉變的例子。"},{"en":"Early observers sometimes confused seasonal appearance with actual transformation.","zh":"早期觀察者有時把季節性出現與真正轉變混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changes connected with the yearly cycle.","zh":"這個短語描述與一年循環有關的變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"one species into another","meaning":"一個物種變成另一個物種","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle believed that one species could change into another.","zh":"Aristotle 相信一個物種可以變成另一個物種。"},{"en":"One species into another means one type of organism becoming a different type.","zh":"一個物種變成另一個物種意思是一種生物變成另一種生物。"},{"en":"The idea that a redstart could change into a robin is an example of this belief.","zh":"紅尾鴝可以變成知更鳥這個想法，就是這種信念的例子。"},{"en":"Modern biology does not support the idea of seasonal transformation from one bird species into another.","zh":"現代生物學不支持鳥類物種會季節性變成另一物種的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mistaken form of species change.","zh":"這個短語描述一種錯誤的物種轉變觀念。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"by observing","meaning":"透過觀察","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle developed the theory by observing redstarts and robins.","zh":"Aristotle 透過觀察紅尾鴝和知更鳥發展出這個理論。"},{"en":"By observing means by watching carefully and noticing details.","zh":"透過觀察意思是透過仔細觀看並注意細節。"},{"en":"Scientists learn animal behaviour by observing how animals feed, move and interact.","zh":"科學家透過觀察動物如何覓食、移動和互動來學習動物行為。"},{"en":"Observation is important, but it still needs careful interpretation.","zh":"觀察很重要，但仍需要謹慎詮釋。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the method used to form an idea.","zh":"這個短語引入形成想法的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"redstarts and robins","meaning":"紅尾鴝和知更鳥","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle observed redstarts and robins.","zh":"Aristotle 觀察紅尾鴝和知更鳥。"},{"en":"Redstarts and robins are two types of small birds.","zh":"紅尾鴝和知更鳥是兩種小型鳥類。"},{"en":"Redstarts and robins may look similar in shape, which influenced Aristotle’s idea.","zh":"紅尾鴝和知更鳥外形可能相似，這影響了 Aristotle 的想法。"},{"en":"Comparing similar birds can be difficult without modern classification tools.","zh":"沒有現代分類工具時，比較相似鳥類可以很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase names the two species in Aristotle’s observation.","zh":"這個短語命名 Aristotle 觀察中的兩個物種。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lose their feathers","meaning":"掉羽毛","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle observed that redstarts began to lose their feathers in autumn.","zh":"Aristotle 觀察到紅尾鴝在秋天開始掉羽毛。"},{"en":"To lose their feathers means to shed or drop feathers from the body.","zh":"掉羽毛意思是身體上的羽毛脫落。"},{"en":"Many birds lose feathers during moulting and later grow new ones.","zh":"許多鳥類在換羽期間會掉羽毛，之後長出新羽毛。"},{"en":"Losing feathers can change how a bird looks, which may confuse observers.","zh":"掉羽毛可以改變鳥的外貌，令觀察者混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical change in birds.","zh":"這個短語描述鳥類的身體變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"convinced Aristotle that","meaning":"令Aristotle相信","examples":[{"en":"The observation convinced Aristotle that redstarts changed into robins.","zh":"這項觀察令 Aristotle 相信紅尾鴝變成知更鳥。"},{"en":"Convinced Aristotle that means made Aristotle believe something was true.","zh":"令 Aristotle 相信某事意思是使 Aristotle 認為某事是真的。"},{"en":"The repeated disappearance of birds convinced some early thinkers that they were hiding.","zh":"鳥類反覆消失令一些早期思想家相信牠們藏起來了。"},{"en":"Evidence can convince people, but the conclusion may still be wrong.","zh":"證據可以令人相信某事，但結論仍可能錯。"},{"en":"This phrase connects observation with belief.","zh":"這個短語把觀察與信念連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"change into","meaning":"變成","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle believed that redstarts changed into robins for the winter.","zh":"Aristotle 相信紅尾鴝在冬天會變成知更鳥。"},{"en":"To change into something means to become something different.","zh":"變成某物意思是成為不同的東西。"},{"en":"A caterpillar changes into a butterfly through metamorphosis.","zh":"毛蟲透過變態變成蝴蝶。"},{"en":"Aristotle wrongly thought one bird species could change into another seasonally.","zh":"Aristotle 錯誤地認為一種鳥類可以季節性變成另一種。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transformation.","zh":"這個短語描述轉變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"back into","meaning":"變回","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle believed that robins changed back into redstarts in summer.","zh":"Aristotle 相信知更鳥在夏天會變回紅尾鴝。"},{"en":"Back into means returning to a previous form, state or identity.","zh":"變回意思是回到以前的形式、狀態或身份。"},{"en":"The old theatre was changed back into a community hall after the festival.","zh":"節日後，舊劇院被改回社區禮堂。"},{"en":"In Aristotle’s theory, birds supposedly changed back into their earlier species.","zh":"在 Aristotle 的理論中，鳥類據稱會變回原本物種。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reversal or return.","zh":"這個短語描述逆轉或回復。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"assumptions","meaning":"假設","examples":[{"en":"These assumptions are understandable.","zh":"這些假設是可以理解的。"},{"en":"Assumptions are ideas people accept as true without complete proof.","zh":"假設是人們在沒有完整證據下接受為真的想法。"},{"en":"Early scientists made assumptions based on what they could see.","zh":"早期科學家根據自己能看見的東西作出假設。"},{"en":"Assumptions can be reasonable at first but wrong after more evidence appears.","zh":"假設起初可以合理，但在更多證據出現後可能是錯的。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing reasoning and interpretation.","zh":"這個詞適合用於討論推理和詮釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"understandable given that","meaning":"鑑於……而可以理解","examples":[{"en":"The assumptions are understandable given that the two species are similar.","zh":"鑑於這兩個物種相似，這些假設是可以理解的。"},{"en":"Understandable given that means easy to understand when a particular reason is considered.","zh":"鑑於某原因而可以理解，意思是考慮該原因後容易明白。"},{"en":"Her mistake is understandable given that the instructions were unclear.","zh":"鑑於指示不清楚，她的錯誤是可以理解的。"},{"en":"A wrong conclusion may still be understandable if the available evidence was limited.","zh":"如果可用證據有限，錯誤結論仍可能可以理解。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a belief or action made sense in context.","zh":"這個短語解釋某信念或行動在語境中為何合理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"this pair of species","meaning":"這一對物種","examples":[{"en":"This pair of species is similar in shape.","zh":"這一對物種外形相似。"},{"en":"This pair of species means these two particular species being discussed together.","zh":"這一對物種意思是正在一起討論的這兩個特定物種。"},{"en":"This pair of species confused early observers because they appeared in different seasons.","zh":"這一對物種令早期觀察者混淆，因為牠們在不同季節出現。"},{"en":"Comparing a pair of species can reveal similarities and differences.","zh":"比較一對物種可以揭示相似點和差異。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on two species as a matched comparison.","zh":"這個短語把兩個物種作為一組比較來看。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"similar in shape","meaning":"外形相似","examples":[{"en":"Redstarts and robins are similar in shape.","zh":"紅尾鴝和知更鳥外形相似。"},{"en":"Similar in shape means having a similar outline or body form.","zh":"外形相似意思是輪廓或身體形態相近。"},{"en":"Two different birds may be similar in shape but different in colour and song.","zh":"兩種不同鳥類可能外形相似，但顏色和叫聲不同。"},{"en":"Similar shape can make identification difficult for beginners.","zh":"外形相似會令新手難以辨認。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical resemblance.","zh":"這個短語描述身體外貌上的相似。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a classic example of","meaning":"……的典型例子","examples":[{"en":"This is a classic example of an incorrect interpretation.","zh":"這是錯誤詮釋的典型例子。"},{"en":"A classic example of something means a very typical or well-known example of it.","zh":"某事的典型例子意思是非常典型或知名的例子。"},{"en":"Forgetting to check evidence is a classic example of poor research practice.","zh":"忘記檢查證據是研究方法差的典型例子。"},{"en":"Classic examples help teachers explain abstract ideas clearly.","zh":"典型例子幫助老師清楚解釋抽象概念。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a representative case.","zh":"這個短語引入具代表性的案例。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"incorrect interpretation","meaning":"錯誤詮釋","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle’s theory was an incorrect interpretation based on correct observations.","zh":"Aristotle 的理論是基於正確觀察的錯誤詮釋。"},{"en":"An incorrect interpretation is a wrong explanation of what something means.","zh":"錯誤詮釋是對某事意思作出的錯誤解釋。"},{"en":"A student may make an incorrect interpretation of a poem if they ignore key words.","zh":"如果學生忽略關鍵字，可能會對詩作出錯誤詮釋。"},{"en":"Correct observations can still lead to incorrect interpretations if reasoning is weak.","zh":"如果推理薄弱，正確觀察仍可以導致錯誤詮釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when separating evidence from conclusion.","zh":"這個短語適合用於區分證據與結論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"based on correct observations","meaning":"基於正確觀察","examples":[{"en":"The theory was based on correct observations.","zh":"這個理論基於正確觀察。"},{"en":"Based on correct observations means built from things that were accurately noticed.","zh":"基於正確觀察意思是建立於準確注意到的事情之上。"},{"en":"A conclusion may be based on correct observations but still be wrong.","zh":"一個結論可以基於正確觀察，但仍然錯誤。"},{"en":"Scientific reasoning requires both accurate observation and careful interpretation.","zh":"科學推理需要準確觀察，也需要謹慎詮釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the evidence behind an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述想法背後的證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bizarre theory","meaning":"古怪理論","examples":[{"en":"The most bizarre theory was put forward by Charles Morton.","zh":"最古怪的理論由 Charles Morton 提出。"},{"en":"A bizarre theory is a very strange or unusual explanation.","zh":"古怪理論是非常奇怪或不尋常的解釋。"},{"en":"The idea that birds migrate to the moon is a bizarre theory today.","zh":"鳥類遷徙到月球這個想法今天是古怪理論。"},{"en":"Bizarre theories can appear when people try to explain mysteries without enough evidence.","zh":"當人們在證據不足下嘗試解釋謎團時，古怪理論可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an explanation that seems extremely odd.","zh":"這個短語描述極其古怪的解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put forward by","meaning":"由……提出","examples":[{"en":"The theory was put forward by an English amateur scientist.","zh":"這個理論由一位英國業餘科學家提出。"},{"en":"Put forward by means proposed or suggested by someone.","zh":"由某人提出意思是由某人建議或提出。"},{"en":"The idea was put forward by a student during the discussion.","zh":"這個想法在討論中由一名學生提出。"},{"en":"In science, a theory must be tested after it is put forward.","zh":"在科學中，理論被提出後必須接受測試。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who proposed an idea.","zh":"這個短語指出誰提出某個想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"amateur scientist","meaning":"業餘科學家","examples":[{"en":"Charles Morton was an English amateur scientist.","zh":"Charles Morton 是一位英國業餘科學家。"},{"en":"An amateur scientist is someone who studies science seriously but not as a full professional career.","zh":"業餘科學家是認真研究科學，但不以科學作為全職專業職業的人。"},{"en":"Amateur scientists have sometimes made useful observations of birds, stars or insects.","zh":"業餘科學家有時對鳥類、星星或昆蟲作出有用觀察。"},{"en":"Being amateur does not mean being careless, but it may mean lacking formal training.","zh":"業餘不代表粗心，但可能代表缺乏正式訓練。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a non-professional person engaged in scientific study.","zh":"這個短語描述從事科學研究的非專業人士。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the seventeenth century","meaning":"在十七世紀","examples":[{"en":"Charles Morton put forward his theory in the seventeenth century.","zh":"Charles Morton 在十七世紀提出他的理論。"},{"en":"In the seventeenth century means during the years from 1601 to 1700.","zh":"在十七世紀意思是在 1601 年至 1700 年期間。"},{"en":"Scientific tools were far less advanced in the seventeenth century.","zh":"在十七世紀，科學工具遠不如今天先進。"},{"en":"Ideas from the seventeenth century may seem strange when judged by modern evidence.","zh":"用現代證據判斷時，十七世紀的想法可能顯得奇怪。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a historical period.","zh":"這個短語提供歷史時期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"surprisingly well-regarded paper","meaning":"出乎意料地頗受重視的論文","examples":[{"en":"Morton wrote a surprisingly well-regarded paper about bird migration.","zh":"Morton 寫了一篇關於鳥類遷徙、出乎意料地頗受重視的論文。"},{"en":"A surprisingly well-regarded paper is an academic or serious article respected more than expected.","zh":"出乎意料地頗受重視的論文，是比預期更受尊重的學術或嚴肅文章。"},{"en":"A paper with a strange claim may still be well regarded if it is carefully argued.","zh":"一篇有奇怪主張的論文，如果論證仔細，仍可能頗受重視。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a contrast between the paper’s odd idea and its reputation.","zh":"這個短語暗示論文古怪想法與其聲譽之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when something receives more respect than modern readers might expect.","zh":"當某物比現代讀者預期更受尊重時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"claiming that","meaning":"聲稱","examples":[{"en":"Morton wrote a paper claiming that birds migrated to the moon.","zh":"Morton 寫了一篇論文，聲稱鳥類遷徙到月球。"},{"en":"Claiming that means saying or arguing that something is true.","zh":"聲稱某事意思是說或主張某事是真的。"},{"en":"The article claimed that the old method was more accurate than expected.","zh":"該文章聲稱舊方法比預期更準確。"},{"en":"Claims need evidence before people should accept them.","zh":"主張需要證據，人才應接受。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what someone asserted.","zh":"這個短語引入某人提出的說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"migrate to the moon and back","meaning":"遷徙到月球再返回","examples":[{"en":"Morton claimed that birds migrate to the moon and back every year.","zh":"Morton 聲稱鳥類每年遷徙到月球再返回。"},{"en":"To migrate to the moon and back means to travel from Earth to the Moon and return.","zh":"遷徙到月球再返回意思是從地球移動到月球，然後再回來。"},{"en":"The idea that birds migrate to the moon and back is now seen as impossible.","zh":"鳥類遷徙到月球再返回這個想法現在被視為不可能。"},{"en":"Morton used this claim to explain why some birds seemed to disappear completely.","zh":"Morton 用這個說法解釋為何有些鳥類似乎完全消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extreme and incorrect migration theory.","zh":"這個短語描述一個極端而錯誤的遷徙理論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"came to this conclusion","meaning":"得出這個結論","examples":[{"en":"Morton came to this conclusion as a logical explanation.","zh":"Morton 將這個想法作為合理解釋，並得出這個結論。"},{"en":"To come to this conclusion means to decide that something is true after thinking about it.","zh":"得出這個結論意思是在思考後認定某事為真。"},{"en":"After comparing the evidence, the researcher came to the conclusion that the bird had migrated.","zh":"比較證據後，研究人員得出該鳥已遷徙的結論。"},{"en":"People can come to a conclusion that seems logical but is still wrong.","zh":"人們可以得出看似合理但仍然錯誤的結論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the result of reasoning.","zh":"這個短語描述推理的結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"logical explanation","meaning":"合理解釋","examples":[{"en":"Morton thought the moon theory was the only logical explanation.","zh":"Morton 認為月球理論是唯一合理解釋。"},{"en":"A logical explanation is a reasoned answer that seems to follow sensible thinking.","zh":"合理解釋是似乎符合合理思考的解答。"},{"en":"Migration became a more logical explanation once evidence showed birds travelled long distances.","zh":"當證據顯示鳥類長距離移動後，遷徙成為更合理的解釋。"},{"en":"An explanation may seem logical if people lack better information.","zh":"如果人們缺乏更好資訊，一個解釋可能顯得合理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an answer based on reasoning.","zh":"這個短語描述基於推理的答案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"total disappearance","meaning":"完全消失","examples":[{"en":"The theory tried to explain the total disappearance of some species.","zh":"這個理論嘗試解釋某些物種的完全消失。"},{"en":"Total disappearance means complete absence from view or from a place.","zh":"完全消失意思是從視線或某地完全不見。"},{"en":"The total disappearance of birds in winter puzzled early observers.","zh":"鳥類冬天完全消失令早期觀察者困惑。"},{"en":"If no birds of a species can be seen, people may assume they have vanished completely.","zh":"如果完全看不到某物種的鳥，人們可能以為牠們完全消失了。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises complete disappearance.","zh":"這個短語強調徹底消失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"key moments in","meaning":"……中的關鍵時刻","examples":[{"en":"One of the key moments in migration theory came in 1822.","zh":"遷徙理論中的一個關鍵時刻出現在 1822 年。"},{"en":"Key moments in something are important events that shape its development.","zh":"某事中的關鍵時刻是塑造其發展的重要事件。"},{"en":"The invention of bird ringing was a key moment in the study of migration.","zh":"鳥類繫放技術的發明是遷徙研究中的關鍵時刻。"},{"en":"Key moments help people understand how knowledge changed over time.","zh":"關鍵時刻幫助人們理解知識如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces historically important events.","zh":"這個短語引入歷史上重要事件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"development of migration theory","meaning":"遷徙理論的發展","examples":[{"en":"The white stork was important in the development of migration theory.","zh":"白鸛在遷徙理論的發展中很重要。"},{"en":"The development of migration theory means the gradual growth of ideas explaining bird migration.","zh":"遷徙理論的發展意思是解釋鳥類遷徙的想法逐漸成長。"},{"en":"Evidence from ringed birds helped the development of migration theory.","zh":"來自繫環鳥的證據幫助遷徙理論發展。"},{"en":"Scientific theories develop as new evidence corrects old assumptions.","zh":"科學理論會隨着新證據修正舊假設而發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how understanding of migration improved over time.","zh":"這個短語描述對遷徙的理解如何隨時間改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"white stork","meaning":"白鸛","examples":[{"en":"A white stork was shot in Germany in 1822.","zh":"一隻白鸛於 1822 年在德國被射下。"},{"en":"A white stork is a large migratory bird with long legs, a long neck and mostly white feathers.","zh":"白鸛是一種大型候鳥，有長腿、長頸和主要白色羽毛。"},{"en":"The white stork became important because one bird carried evidence from Africa to Europe.","zh":"白鸛變得重要，是因為其中一隻鳥把來自非洲的證據帶到歐洲。"},{"en":"Storks are often noticed because they are large and distinctive.","zh":"鸛鳥體型大而特徵鮮明，所以常被注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific migratory bird species.","zh":"這個短語命名一種特定候鳥物種。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"made history","meaning":"載入史冊","examples":[{"en":"This particular stork made history.","zh":"這隻特定白鸛載入史冊。"},{"en":"To make history means to become important or famous because of a significant event.","zh":"載入史冊意思是因重大事件而變得重要或著名。"},{"en":"A scientist can make history by proving a long-standing mystery.","zh":"科學家可以透過證明長久謎團而載入史冊。"},{"en":"The stork made history because it provided strong evidence of long-distance migration.","zh":"這隻白鸛載入史冊，因為牠提供了長距離遷徙的有力證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming part of important historical record.","zh":"這個短語描述成為重要歷史記錄的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"long spear in its neck","meaning":"脖子上的長矛","examples":[{"en":"The stork had a long spear in its neck.","zh":"那隻白鸛脖子上有一支長矛。"},{"en":"A long spear in its neck means a long pointed weapon was stuck through or into the bird’s neck.","zh":"脖子上的長矛意思是一支長而尖的武器插在或穿過鳥的脖子。"},{"en":"The spear showed that the bird had travelled from a faraway place.","zh":"那支長矛顯示該鳥曾從遙遠地方飛來。"},{"en":"Such an unusual object provided evidence that could not easily be ignored.","zh":"這樣不尋常的物件提供了難以忽視的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the striking physical evidence found on the stork.","zh":"這個短語描述在白鸛身上發現的驚人實物證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"incredibly","meaning":"令人難以置信地","examples":[{"en":"The spear incredibly had not killed the stork.","zh":"令人難以置信地，那支長矛沒有殺死那隻白鸛。"},{"en":"Incredibly means in a way that is very surprising or hard to believe.","zh":"令人難以置信地意思是以非常令人驚訝或難以相信的方式。"},{"en":"Incredibly, the bird survived a journey with a spear in its neck.","zh":"令人難以置信地，那隻鳥脖子上插着長矛仍完成旅程。"},{"en":"This word is used when a fact seems almost unbelievable.","zh":"當事實幾乎難以相信時，會使用這個詞。"},{"en":"It adds emphasis to the surprising nature of an event.","zh":"它加強事件令人驚訝的程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"immediately realised","meaning":"立即意識到","examples":[{"en":"Everyone immediately realised that the spear was not European.","zh":"所有人立即意識到那支長矛並非歐洲的。"},{"en":"To immediately realise something means to understand it at once.","zh":"立即意識到某事意思是馬上明白它。"},{"en":"Researchers immediately realised the object came from another region.","zh":"研究人員立即意識到該物件來自另一地區。"},{"en":"Immediate realisation can happen when evidence is clear and unusual.","zh":"當證據清楚而不尋常時，人們可以立即意識到事實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quick understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述快速理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"turned out to be","meaning":"結果是","examples":[{"en":"The spear turned out to be from a tribe in Central Africa.","zh":"那支長矛結果是來自中非一個部落。"},{"en":"Turned out to be means was discovered later to be something.","zh":"結果是意思是之後被發現是某事物。"},{"en":"The unusual feather turned out to be from a rare bird species.","zh":"那根不尋常羽毛結果是來自一種稀有鳥類。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces the true explanation after uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語常在不確定之後引入真相。"},{"en":"It is useful when a result is discovered unexpectedly.","zh":"當結果被意外發現時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a tribe in Central Africa","meaning":"中非一個部落","examples":[{"en":"The spear came from a tribe in Central Africa.","zh":"那支長矛來自中非一個部落。"},{"en":"A tribe in Central Africa means a traditional community or people group from the central part of Africa.","zh":"中非一個部落意思是來自非洲中部的傳統社群或族群。"},{"en":"The spear’s origin in Central Africa showed that the bird had travelled a long distance.","zh":"長矛源自中非顯示那隻鳥曾長距離飛行。"},{"en":"Geographic clues can help scientists reconstruct migration routes.","zh":"地理線索可以幫助科學家重建遷徙路線。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the cultural and regional source of the spear.","zh":"這個短語指出長矛的文化和地區來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"truly defining moment","meaning":"真正具決定意義的時刻","examples":[{"en":"This was a truly defining moment in the history of ornithology.","zh":"這是鳥類學史上一個真正具決定意義的時刻。"},{"en":"A truly defining moment is an event that clearly changes the direction of understanding or history.","zh":"真正具決定意義的時刻，是清楚改變理解或歷史方向的事件。"},{"en":"The discovery of bird ringing data was a defining moment in migration research.","zh":"鳥類繫放數據的發現是遷徙研究中的決定性時刻。"},{"en":"Defining moments often replace speculation with stronger evidence.","zh":"具決定意義的時刻常以更強證據取代猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights major historical importance.","zh":"這個短語突顯重大歷史重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"history of ornithology","meaning":"鳥類學史","examples":[{"en":"The stork became important in the history of ornithology.","zh":"那隻白鸛在鳥類學史上變得重要。"},{"en":"The history of ornithology is the history of the scientific study of birds.","zh":"鳥類學史是鳥類科學研究的歷史。"},{"en":"Bird ringing is an important chapter in the history of ornithology.","zh":"鳥類繫放是鳥類學史上的重要篇章。"},{"en":"The history of ornithology shows how observation and technology changed bird research.","zh":"鳥類學史顯示觀察和科技如何改變鳥類研究。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the development of bird science over time.","zh":"這個短語指鳥類科學隨時間的發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"first evidence that","meaning":"……的首個證據","examples":[{"en":"The stork provided the first evidence that storks winter in Africa.","zh":"那隻白鸛提供了鸛鳥在非洲過冬的首個證據。"},{"en":"First evidence that means the earliest proof supporting a claim.","zh":"某事的首個證據意思是支持某主張的最早證明。"},{"en":"A fossil may provide the first evidence that a species lived in a region.","zh":"化石可能提供某物種曾生活在某地區的首個證據。"},{"en":"Evidence can turn a guess into a stronger scientific explanation.","zh":"證據可以把猜測變成更有力的科學解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a breakthrough proof.","zh":"這個短語引入突破性證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"spend their winters in","meaning":"在……過冬","examples":[{"en":"Storks spend their winters in sub-Saharan Africa.","zh":"鸛鳥在撒哈拉以南非洲過冬。"},{"en":"To spend their winters in a place means to live there during the winter season.","zh":"在某地過冬意思是在冬季期間生活在那裏。"},{"en":"Some birds spend their winters in warmer regions where food is easier to find.","zh":"有些鳥類在較溫暖地區過冬，因為食物較容易找到。"},{"en":"Wintering places are important parts of migration routes.","zh":"過冬地是遷徙路線的重要部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes seasonal residence.","zh":"這個短語描述季節性居留。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sub-Saharan Africa","meaning":"撒哈拉以南非洲","examples":[{"en":"The arrow stork proved that storks winter in sub-Saharan Africa.","zh":"箭鸛證明鸛鳥在撒哈拉以南非洲過冬。"},{"en":"Sub-Saharan Africa means the part of Africa south of the Sahara Desert.","zh":"撒哈拉以南非洲意思是撒哈拉沙漠以南的非洲地區。"},{"en":"Many migratory birds from Europe spend winter in sub-Saharan Africa.","zh":"許多來自歐洲的候鳥在撒哈拉以南非洲過冬。"},{"en":"This region can provide warmer conditions and food during European winters.","zh":"這個地區可以在歐洲冬季期間提供較溫暖環境和食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad geographic region.","zh":"這個短語描述一個廣闊地理區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Zoological Collection","meaning":"動物收藏","examples":[{"en":"The arrow stork can still be seen in the Zoological Collection of the University of Rostock.","zh":"箭鸛至今仍可在羅斯托克大學的動物收藏中看到。"},{"en":"A Zoological Collection is a collection of animal specimens kept for study or display.","zh":"動物收藏是為研究或展示而保存的動物標本集合。"},{"en":"Universities may keep zoological collections to support teaching and research.","zh":"大學可能保存動物收藏，以支援教學和研究。"},{"en":"Historical specimens can preserve evidence that shaped scientific understanding.","zh":"歷史標本可以保存塑造科學理解的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an organised animal collection.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的動物標本收藏。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"gradually became aware that","meaning":"逐漸意識到","examples":[{"en":"People gradually became aware that European birds moved south in autumn.","zh":"人們逐漸意識到歐洲鳥類在秋天南飛。"},{"en":"To gradually become aware that something is true means to slowly start to understand it.","zh":"逐漸意識到某事為真意思是慢慢開始理解它。"},{"en":"Scientists gradually became aware that migration routes were much longer than expected.","zh":"科學家逐漸意識到遷徙路線比預期長得多。"},{"en":"Understanding often grows gradually as more evidence is collected.","zh":"理解常隨着更多證據收集而逐漸增長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow development of knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述知識慢慢發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"moved south in autumn","meaning":"秋天南飛","examples":[{"en":"European birds moved south in autumn.","zh":"歐洲鳥類在秋天南飛。"},{"en":"Moved south in autumn means travelled towards warmer southern areas during autumn.","zh":"秋天南飛意思是在秋季朝較溫暖的南方地區移動。"},{"en":"Many birds move south in autumn to escape colder weather.","zh":"許多鳥類在秋天南飛，以避開較寒冷天氣。"},{"en":"Southward movement is a common pattern in bird migration.","zh":"向南移動是鳥類遷徙中的常見模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes seasonal direction of travel.","zh":"這個短語描述季節性移動方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"moved north in summer","meaning":"夏天北返","examples":[{"en":"European birds moved north in summer.","zh":"歐洲鳥類在夏天北返。"},{"en":"Moved north in summer means travelled back towards northern areas during summer.","zh":"夏天北返意思是在夏季返回較北方地區。"},{"en":"Some birds move north in summer to breed in cooler regions.","zh":"有些鳥類夏天北返，到較涼地區繁殖。"},{"en":"Northward movement often follows warmer weather and increased food supply.","zh":"向北返回通常跟隨較暖天氣和增加的食物供應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes seasonal return movement.","zh":"這個短語描述季節性回程移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"didn’t know much about","meaning":"對……了解不多","examples":[{"en":"People did not know much about bird migration until bird ringing became common.","zh":"在鳥類繫放變得常見之前，人們對鳥類遷徙了解不多。"},{"en":"Didn’t know much about means had limited knowledge of something.","zh":"對某事了解不多意思是對它知識有限。"},{"en":"Before modern instruments, people did not know much about deep-sea life.","zh":"在現代儀器出現前，人們對深海生命了解不多。"},{"en":"Limited knowledge can lead to speculation and mistaken theories.","zh":"知識有限可能導致猜測和錯誤理論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lack of understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the practice of","meaning":"……的做法","examples":[{"en":"The practice of putting rings on birds’ legs became established.","zh":"在鳥腳上套環的做法成為既定做法。"},{"en":"The practice of doing something means the regular method or habit of doing it.","zh":"做某事的做法意思是定期做該事的方法或習慣。"},{"en":"The practice of recording rainfall helped scientists study climate patterns.","zh":"記錄降雨量的做法幫助科學家研究氣候模式。"},{"en":"A research practice becomes useful when it produces reliable information.","zh":"當研究做法產生可靠資訊時，它就變得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an established method.","zh":"這個短語引入既定方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"putting rings on their legs","meaning":"在牠們腳上套環","examples":[{"en":"Researchers began putting rings on birds’ legs.","zh":"研究人員開始在鳥類腳上套環。"},{"en":"Putting rings on birds’ legs means attaching small identification bands to birds.","zh":"在鳥類腳上套環意思是把小型識別環套在鳥腳上。"},{"en":"Scientists put rings on birds’ legs so individual birds can be recognised later.","zh":"科學家在鳥腳上套環，以便之後認出個別鳥類。"},{"en":"Ringing birds helps researchers learn where birds travel and how long they live.","zh":"鳥類繫放幫助研究人員了解鳥類去哪裏和壽命有多長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the basic action in bird ringing.","zh":"這個短語描述鳥類繫放的基本動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"became established","meaning":"成為既定做法","examples":[{"en":"Bird ringing became established as a research method.","zh":"鳥類繫放成為既定研究方法。"},{"en":"Became established means became accepted, recognised or regularly used.","zh":"成為既定做法意思是變得被接受、認可或定期使用。"},{"en":"Online learning became established in many schools after repeated use.","zh":"網上學習經過反覆使用後，在許多學校成為既定做法。"},{"en":"A method becomes established when many people trust and use it.","zh":"當許多人信任並使用某方法，它就會成為既定做法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a process of becoming standard.","zh":"這個短語描述變成標準做法的過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"very little information was available","meaning":"可用資料很少","examples":[{"en":"Very little information was available about the destinations of particular species.","zh":"關於特定物種目的地的可用資料很少。"},{"en":"Very little information was available means there was not much information that people could use.","zh":"可用資料很少意思是人們能使用的資料不多。"},{"en":"Before bird ringing, very little information was available about exact migration routes.","zh":"在鳥類繫放之前，關於確切遷徙路線的可用資料很少。"},{"en":"When little information is available, conclusions are often uncertain.","zh":"當可用資料很少，結論通常不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shortage of usable knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述可用知識短缺。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"actual destinations","meaning":"實際目的地","examples":[{"en":"Researchers knew little about the actual destinations of particular species.","zh":"研究人員對特定物種的實際目的地了解很少。"},{"en":"Actual destinations are the real places birds travel to, not guessed places.","zh":"實際目的地是鳥類真正前往的地方，而不是猜測地點。"},{"en":"Bird ringing helped reveal the actual destinations of many migrating birds.","zh":"鳥類繫放幫助揭示許多候鳥的實際目的地。"},{"en":"Knowing actual destinations is important for protecting habitats across migration routes.","zh":"了解實際目的地對保護遷徙路線上的棲息地很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real locations with speculation.","zh":"這個短語把真實地點與猜測作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"particular species","meaning":"特定物種","examples":[{"en":"Researchers wanted to know where particular species travelled.","zh":"研究人員想知道特定物種去了哪裏。"},{"en":"Particular species means specific types of animals or plants.","zh":"特定物種意思是具體某些動物或植物種類。"},{"en":"Scientists may study a particular species to understand its migration route.","zh":"科學家可能研究特定物種，以了解其遷徙路線。"},{"en":"Different species may travel to very different destinations.","zh":"不同物種可能前往非常不同的目的地。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows attention to selected species rather than all birds.","zh":"這個短語把注意力收窄到選定物種，而不是所有鳥類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"how they travelled there","meaning":"牠們如何到達那裏","examples":[{"en":"People did not know how birds travelled to their winter destinations.","zh":"人們不知道鳥類如何到達牠們的冬季目的地。"},{"en":"How they travelled there means the route, method or process by which they reached that place.","zh":"牠們如何到達那裏意思是牠們到達該地方的路線、方法或過程。"},{"en":"Researchers wanted to know whether birds crossed seas, followed coastlines or travelled inland.","zh":"研究人員想知道鳥類是否橫越海洋、沿海岸飛行或經內陸遷徙。"},{"en":"Understanding how birds travel helps explain the risks they face.","zh":"了解鳥類如何旅行有助解釋牠們面對的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the journey rather than the destination alone.","zh":"這個短語重點是旅程，而不只是目的地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"speculated that","meaning":"推測","examples":[{"en":"People speculated that larger birds carried smaller birds.","zh":"人們推測較大型鳥類背着較小型鳥類。"},{"en":"Speculated that means guessed or suggested an idea without firm proof.","zh":"推測某事意思是在沒有確實證據下猜想或提出想法。"},{"en":"Early observers speculated that birds were hiding because they could not see them.","zh":"早期觀察者因看不見鳥類而推測牠們藏起來。"},{"en":"Speculation can be useful at first, but it needs evidence to become reliable.","zh":"猜測起初可以有用，但需要證據才會可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an uncertain explanation.","zh":"這個短語引入不確定的解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"larger birds","meaning":"較大型鳥類","examples":[{"en":"Some people thought larger birds helped smaller birds migrate.","zh":"有些人認為較大型鳥類幫助較小型鳥類遷徙。"},{"en":"Larger birds are birds that are bigger in size than others.","zh":"較大型鳥類是比其他鳥體型更大的鳥。"},{"en":"Cranes and storks are larger birds compared with small songbirds.","zh":"與小型鳴禽相比，鶴和鸛是較大型鳥類。"},{"en":"Early observers imagined larger birds might carry smaller birds across difficult routes.","zh":"早期觀察者想像較大型鳥類可能背着較小型鳥類穿越困難路線。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bird size in comparison.","zh":"這個短語透過比較描述鳥類體型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a kind of taxi service","meaning":"一種類似的士服務","examples":[{"en":"People thought larger birds provided a kind of taxi service.","zh":"人們認為較大型鳥類提供一種類似的士服務。"},{"en":"A kind of taxi service means a way of carrying others from one place to another.","zh":"一種類似的士服務意思是把其他對象從一地載到另一地的方法。"},{"en":"The idea suggested that small birds rode on larger birds like passengers.","zh":"這個想法暗示小鳥像乘客一樣乘在大鳥身上。"},{"en":"This theory now sounds amusing, but it tried to explain a real puzzle.","zh":"這個理論現在聽起來好笑，但它曾嘗試解釋真實謎團。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a familiar modern comparison to describe an old theory.","zh":"這個短語用熟悉的現代比較描述舊理論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"carrying them on their backs","meaning":"把牠們背在背上","examples":[{"en":"People thought larger birds carried smaller birds on their backs.","zh":"人們認為較大型鳥類把較小型鳥類背在背上。"},{"en":"Carrying them on their backs means transporting them while they sit or rest on the larger bird’s back.","zh":"把牠們背在背上意思是讓牠們坐或停在大鳥背上被運送。"},{"en":"The theory imagined small birds being carried across oceans by larger birds.","zh":"這個理論想像小鳥被大鳥背着飛越海洋。"},{"en":"This idea came from trying to explain how very small birds could travel so far.","zh":"這個想法源於嘗試解釋非常小的鳥如何飛得那麼遠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical carrying action.","zh":"這個短語描述實際背負動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"came about because","meaning":"產生的原因是","examples":[{"en":"This idea came about because small birds seemed too light to cross oceans.","zh":"這個想法產生的原因是小鳥似乎太輕，無法橫越海洋。"},{"en":"Came about because means happened or developed as a result of a reason.","zh":"產生的原因是某事意思是某事因一個原因而發生或發展。"},{"en":"The rule came about because too many students were late.","zh":"這條規則產生的原因是太多學生遲到。"},{"en":"Strange theories can come about because people are trying to fill gaps in knowledge.","zh":"古怪理論可能產生於人們嘗試填補知識空白。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the origin of an idea or event.","zh":"這個短語解釋想法或事件的來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"seemed impossible that","meaning":"似乎不可能","examples":[{"en":"It seemed impossible that tiny birds could fly over vast oceans.","zh":"細小鳥類能飛越廣闊海洋似乎不可能。"},{"en":"Seemed impossible that means appeared too unlikely or difficult to believe.","zh":"似乎不可能意思是看起來太不可能或太難相信。"},{"en":"It seemed impossible that such a small bird could travel thousands of kilometres.","zh":"如此細小的鳥能飛行數千公里似乎不可能。"},{"en":"What seems impossible can become believable once evidence is found.","zh":"一旦找到證據，看似不可能的事情可以變得可信。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an impression of impossibility.","zh":"這個短語描述不可能的印象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"weighing only a few grams","meaning":"只有幾克重","examples":[{"en":"Some small birds weigh only a few grams.","zh":"有些小鳥只有幾克重。"},{"en":"Weighing only a few grams means having a very small body weight.","zh":"只有幾克重意思是身體重量非常小。"},{"en":"A bird weighing only a few grams may still be capable of long-distance flight.","zh":"只有幾克重的鳥仍可能有能力長距離飛行。"},{"en":"Small body weight made early observers doubt whether tiny birds could cross oceans.","zh":"很輕的體重令早期觀察者懷疑小鳥能否橫越海洋。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises how light an animal is.","zh":"這個短語強調動物有多輕。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fly over vast oceans","meaning":"飛越廣闊海洋","examples":[{"en":"People doubted that small birds could fly over vast oceans.","zh":"人們懷疑小鳥能否飛越廣闊海洋。"},{"en":"To fly over vast oceans means to travel by air across very large areas of sea.","zh":"飛越廣闊海洋意思是從空中跨越非常大的海域。"},{"en":"Migrating birds may fly over vast oceans without stopping for land.","zh":"候鳥可能不停靠陸地而飛越廣闊海洋。"},{"en":"Long sea crossings require energy, navigation and suitable weather.","zh":"長距離跨海飛行需要能量、導航能力和合適天氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an impressive migration challenge.","zh":"這個短語描述令人驚嘆的遷徙挑戰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"supported by observations of","meaning":"得到……觀察支持","examples":[{"en":"The taxi-service idea was supported by observations of bird behaviour.","zh":"類似的士服務的想法得到鳥類行為觀察支持。"},{"en":"Supported by observations of something means backed up by what people saw or recorded.","zh":"得到某事觀察支持意思是受到人們看到或記錄到的內容支持。"},{"en":"A theory about feeding habits may be supported by observations of birds in the wild.","zh":"關於覓食習慣的理論可能得到野外鳥類觀察支持。"},{"en":"Observations can support an idea, but they must be interpreted carefully.","zh":"觀察可以支持一個想法，但必須謹慎詮釋。"},{"en":"This phrase connects evidence with a theory.","zh":"這個短語把證據與理論連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bird behaviour","meaning":"鳥類行為","examples":[{"en":"Some observations of bird behaviour seemed to support the theory.","zh":"一些鳥類行為觀察似乎支持這個理論。"},{"en":"Bird behaviour means the actions and habits of birds.","zh":"鳥類行為意思是鳥類的動作和習慣。"},{"en":"Singing, nesting, feeding and flying are examples of bird behaviour.","zh":"鳴叫、築巢、覓食和飛行都是鳥類行為例子。"},{"en":"Studying bird behaviour can reveal how birds survive and communicate.","zh":"研究鳥類行為可以揭示鳥類如何生存和溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in animal research.","zh":"這個短語常見於動物研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"harassment of larger birds","meaning":"對較大型鳥類的騷擾","examples":[{"en":"People observed the harassment of larger birds by smaller birds.","zh":"人們觀察到小鳥對較大型鳥類的騷擾。"},{"en":"Harassment of larger birds means smaller birds repeatedly bothering, chasing or attacking bigger birds.","zh":"對較大型鳥類的騷擾意思是小鳥反覆打擾、追逐或攻擊較大的鳥。"},{"en":"Small birds may harass larger birds to protect nests or drive predators away.","zh":"小鳥可能騷擾較大型鳥類，以保護鳥巢或趕走捕食者。"},{"en":"Early observers wrongly connected this behaviour with the idea of riding on larger birds.","zh":"早期觀察者錯誤地把這種行為與乘坐大鳥的想法連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes aggressive or persistent behaviour towards bigger birds.","zh":"這個短語描述針對較大鳥類的攻擊性或持續性行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"development of bird ringing","meaning":"鳥類繫放技術的發展","examples":[{"en":"The development of bird ringing made many discoveries possible.","zh":"鳥類繫放技術的發展令許多發現成為可能。"},{"en":"The development of bird ringing means the creation and improvement of the method of attaching rings to birds.","zh":"鳥類繫放技術的發展意思是在鳥類腳上套環的方法被創造和改善。"},{"en":"The development of bird ringing allowed scientists to follow birds across countries.","zh":"鳥類繫放技術的發展讓科學家能追蹤鳥類跨國移動。"},{"en":"New research methods can open the door to discoveries that were impossible before.","zh":"新研究方法可以打開以前不可能發現的門。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a scientific method becoming useful over time.","zh":"這個短語描述科學方法隨時間變得有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Danish schoolteacher","meaning":"丹麥教師","examples":[{"en":"Hans Christian Cornelius Mortensen was a Danish schoolteacher.","zh":"Hans Christian Cornelius Mortensen 是一位丹麥教師。"},{"en":"A Danish schoolteacher is a teacher from Denmark.","zh":"丹麥教師是來自丹麥的教師。"},{"en":"A Danish schoolteacher helped develop a method that changed bird research.","zh":"一位丹麥教師幫助發展出改變鳥類研究的方法。"},{"en":"Important scientific contributions can come from teachers and amateur observers as well as professional scientists.","zh":"重要科學貢獻可以來自教師和業餘觀察者，也可以來自專業科學家。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a person’s nationality and occupation.","zh":"這個短語指出一個人的國籍和職業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"made many discoveries possible","meaning":"令許多發現成為可能","examples":[{"en":"Bird ringing made many discoveries possible.","zh":"鳥類繫放令許多發現成為可能。"},{"en":"Made many discoveries possible means enabled people to find out many things that they could not know before.","zh":"令許多發現成為可能意思是使人們能知道以前無法知道的許多事情。"},{"en":"Microscopes made many discoveries possible in biology.","zh":"顯微鏡令生物學中的許多發現成為可能。"},{"en":"Bird ringing made discoveries possible by connecting individual birds with specific places.","zh":"鳥類繫放透過把個別鳥類與特定地點連繫起來，令發現成為可能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a tool or method creates new knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述工具或方法如何創造新知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"common practice","meaning":"常見做法","examples":[{"en":"Bird ringing is still common practice today.","zh":"鳥類繫放今天仍是常見做法。"},{"en":"Common practice means a usual or widely accepted way of doing something.","zh":"常見做法意思是通常或廣泛接受的做事方式。"},{"en":"Wearing lab coats is common practice in many science laboratories.","zh":"在許多科學實驗室中，穿實驗袍是常見做法。"},{"en":"A method becomes common practice when many researchers continue to use it.","zh":"當許多研究人員持續使用某方法，它就會成為常見做法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a normal established method.","zh":"這個短語描述正常的既定方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"relies upon","meaning":"依賴","examples":[{"en":"Bird ringing relies upon what is known as recovery.","zh":"鳥類繫放依賴所謂的回收。"},{"en":"Relies upon means depends on something in order to work.","zh":"依賴某事意思是靠它才能運作。"},{"en":"Good research relies upon accurate data.","zh":"良好研究依賴準確數據。"},{"en":"Bird ringing relies on people finding and reporting ringed birds later.","zh":"鳥類繫放依賴人們之後發現並報告繫環鳥。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dependence on a method or condition.","zh":"這個短語描述對方法或條件的依靠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"what is known as","meaning":"所謂的……","examples":[{"en":"The method relies upon what is known as recovery.","zh":"這個方法依賴所謂的回收。"},{"en":"What is known as means what people call by a particular name.","zh":"所謂的某事意思是人們以某個特定名稱稱呼的東西。"},{"en":"The process uses what is known as satellite tracking.","zh":"這個過程使用所謂的衛星追蹤。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a technical or specialised term.","zh":"這個短語引入技術性或專門術語。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining terminology.","zh":"當解釋術語時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"recovery","meaning":"繫放回收","examples":[{"en":"Recovery is when ringed birds are found dead and identified.","zh":"繫放回收是指繫環鳥被發現死亡並被識別。"},{"en":"In bird ringing, recovery means finding a ringed bird later and using its ring to identify it.","zh":"在鳥類繫放中，回收意思是之後找到繫環鳥，並使用腳環識別牠。"},{"en":"Recovery can tell researchers where a bird travelled after it was ringed.","zh":"回收可以告訴研究人員一隻鳥被繫環後去了哪裏。"},{"en":"Although recovery often depends on dead birds, it has provided valuable migration data.","zh":"雖然回收常依賴死鳥，但它提供了有價值的遷徙數據。"},{"en":"This word has a special meaning in bird-ringing research.","zh":"這個詞在鳥類繫放研究中有特殊意思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ringed birds","meaning":"繫上腳環的鳥","examples":[{"en":"Ringed birds can be identified after migration.","zh":"繫上腳環的鳥在遷徙後可以被識別。"},{"en":"Ringed birds are birds with small identification rings attached to their legs.","zh":"繫上腳環的鳥是腳上附有小型識別環的鳥。"},{"en":"A ringed bird found far away can reveal part of its migration route.","zh":"在遠方被發現的繫環鳥可以揭示其部分遷徙路線。"},{"en":"Ringed birds help scientists connect individual animals with specific journeys.","zh":"繫環鳥幫助科學家把個別動物與特定旅程連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes birds marked for research.","zh":"這個短語描述為研究而標記的鳥。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"are found dead","meaning":"被發現死亡","examples":[{"en":"Ringed birds are sometimes found dead in the place they migrated to.","zh":"繫環鳥有時會在牠們遷徙到的地方被發現死亡。"},{"en":"Are found dead means are discovered after they have died.","zh":"被發現死亡意思是在已死亡後被人發現。"},{"en":"A ringed bird found dead in another country can still provide useful information.","zh":"在另一個國家被發現死亡的繫環鳥仍可以提供有用資料。"},{"en":"Finding a dead bird may be sad, but it can help researchers learn about migration.","zh":"發現死鳥可能令人難過，但可以幫助研究人員了解遷徙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the condition in which an animal is discovered.","zh":"這個短語描述動物被發現時的狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"migrated to","meaning":"遷徙到","examples":[{"en":"Birds may be found in the place they have migrated to.","zh":"鳥類可能在牠們遷徙到的地方被發現。"},{"en":"Migrated to means travelled to a new place, usually seasonally.","zh":"遷徙到某地意思是移動到新地方，通常是季節性地。"},{"en":"Some birds migrated to warmer countries before winter arrived.","zh":"有些鳥在冬天來臨前遷徙到較溫暖國家。"},{"en":"Knowing where birds migrated to helps scientists protect their destination habitats.","zh":"知道鳥類遷徙到哪裏有助科學家保護其目的地棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the destination of migration.","zh":"這個短語指出遷徙目的地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be identified","meaning":"被識別","examples":[{"en":"Ringed birds can be identified after they are found.","zh":"繫環鳥被發現後可以被識別。"},{"en":"To be identified means to be recognised or named correctly.","zh":"被識別意思是被正確認出或命名。"},{"en":"A bird can be identified by its ring number, colour pattern or song.","zh":"鳥類可以透過腳環編號、顏色圖案或叫聲被識別。"},{"en":"Identification is important because it links the bird to earlier records.","zh":"識別很重要，因為它把該鳥與早前紀錄連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of recognising something.","zh":"這個短語描述辨認某物的過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"huge amounts of data","meaning":"大量數據","examples":[{"en":"Huge amounts of data were gathered in the early twentieth century.","zh":"二十世紀初期收集了大量數據。"},{"en":"Huge amounts of data means very large quantities of information.","zh":"大量數據意思是非常多的資料。"},{"en":"Bird ringing produced huge amounts of data about where birds travelled.","zh":"鳥類繫放產生了大量關於鳥類去向的數據。"},{"en":"Large data sets can reveal patterns that individual observations cannot show.","zh":"大型數據集可以揭示個別觀察不能顯示的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the scale of collected information.","zh":"這個短語強調收集資訊的規模。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"were gathered","meaning":"被收集","examples":[{"en":"Data about bird migration were gathered through bird ringing.","zh":"關於鳥類遷徙的數據透過鳥類繫放被收集。"},{"en":"Were gathered means were collected from different sources or observations.","zh":"被收集意思是從不同來源或觀察中被取得。"},{"en":"Survey answers were gathered from students in three schools.","zh":"調查答案從三所學校的學生中被收集。"},{"en":"Data must be gathered carefully if researchers want reliable conclusions.","zh":"如果研究人員想得出可靠結論，數據必須被仔細收集。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of collecting information.","zh":"這個短語描述收集資訊的過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"early part of the twentieth century","meaning":"二十世紀初期","examples":[{"en":"Huge amounts of data were gathered in the early part of the twentieth century.","zh":"二十世紀初期收集了大量數據。"},{"en":"The early part of the twentieth century means the first decades of the 1900s.","zh":"二十世紀初期意思是 1900 年代的最初幾十年。"},{"en":"Many scientific methods became more organised in the early part of the twentieth century.","zh":"許多科學方法在二十世紀初期變得更有組織。"},{"en":"This period was important for collecting bird migration evidence.","zh":"這段時期對收集鳥類遷徙證據很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a historical time frame.","zh":"這個短語提供歷史時間框架。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"for the first time in history","meaning":"歷史上第一次","examples":[{"en":"For the first time in history, people understood where birds went in winter.","zh":"歷史上第一次，人們明白鳥類冬天去了哪裏。"},{"en":"For the first time in history means something happened for the first known time ever.","zh":"歷史上第一次意思是某事在已知歷史中首次發生。"},{"en":"For the first time in history, researchers could track some birds across long distances.","zh":"歷史上第一次，研究人員能追蹤一些鳥類跨越長距離。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the importance of a breakthrough.","zh":"這個短語強調突破的重要性。"},{"en":"It is used when a change is historically new.","zh":"當某變化在歷史上是全新的時，會使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"where birds actually went","meaning":"鳥類實際去了哪裏","examples":[{"en":"People began to understand where birds actually went in winter.","zh":"人們開始明白鳥類冬天實際去了哪裏。"},{"en":"Where birds actually went means the real places birds travelled to, not imagined explanations.","zh":"鳥類實際去了哪裏意思是鳥類真正前往的地方，而不是想像出的解釋。"},{"en":"Bird ringing showed where birds actually went after leaving Europe.","zh":"鳥類繫放顯示鳥類離開歐洲後實際去了哪裏。"},{"en":"Knowing actual destinations replaced myths about hibernation and transformation.","zh":"知道實際目的地取代了關於冬眠和轉變的神話。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts reality with earlier guesses.","zh":"這個短語把現實與早期猜測作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in winter","meaning":"在冬天","examples":[{"en":"Researchers discovered where birds went in winter.","zh":"研究人員發現鳥類在冬天去了哪裏。"},{"en":"In winter means during the coldest season of the year.","zh":"在冬天意思是在一年中最寒冷的季節。"},{"en":"Many birds leave cold regions in winter to find food elsewhere.","zh":"許多鳥類在冬天離開寒冷地區，到別處尋找食物。"},{"en":"Winter conditions can affect whether birds stay, migrate or struggle to survive.","zh":"冬季環境會影響鳥類留下、遷徙或努力生存。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the seasonal time of an event.","zh":"這個短語交代事件發生的季節時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"an atlas was published","meaning":"一本地圖集出版","examples":[{"en":"An atlas was published in 1931.","zh":"一本地圖集於 1931 年出版。"},{"en":"An atlas was published means a book or collection of maps was officially produced and made available.","zh":"一本地圖集出版意思是一本地圖書或地圖集合被正式製作並公開。"},{"en":"A migration atlas can show routes and destinations of different bird species.","zh":"遷徙地圖集可以顯示不同鳥類物種的路線和目的地。"},{"en":"Publishing an atlas helped share migration knowledge with more people.","zh":"出版地圖集有助把遷徙知識分享給更多人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the release of a map-based reference work.","zh":"這個短語描述以地圖為基礎的參考作品發行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the most common species","meaning":"最常見物種","examples":[{"en":"The atlas showed where the most common species of European birds migrated.","zh":"該地圖集顯示最常見歐洲鳥類物種遷徙到哪裏。"},{"en":"The most common species means the species seen or found most often.","zh":"最常見物種意思是最常被看見或發現的物種。"},{"en":"Researchers may begin with the most common species because there is more data about them.","zh":"研究人員可能先從最常見物種開始，因為相關數據較多。"},{"en":"Common species can still reveal important migration patterns.","zh":"常見物種仍能揭示重要遷徙模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes species with high frequency or abundance.","zh":"這個短語描述出現頻率或數量高的物種。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"European birds","meaning":"歐洲鳥類","examples":[{"en":"The atlas showed the migration routes of European birds.","zh":"該地圖集顯示歐洲鳥類的遷徙路線。"},{"en":"European birds are birds that live in or migrate through Europe.","zh":"歐洲鳥類是在歐洲生活或經過歐洲遷徙的鳥類。"},{"en":"Many European birds move south when winter approaches.","zh":"許多歐洲鳥類在冬天接近時南飛。"},{"en":"Studying European birds helped early researchers understand long-distance migration.","zh":"研究歐洲鳥類幫助早期研究人員理解長距離遷徙。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies birds by geographic region.","zh":"這個短語以地理區域識別鳥類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"more recent theories about","meaning":"關於……的較新理論","examples":[{"en":"The lecture then moves on to more recent theories about bird migration.","zh":"講座接着轉到關於鳥類遷徙的較新理論。"},{"en":"More recent theories about something are newer explanations or ideas developed closer to the present time.","zh":"關於某事的較新理論，是較接近現代發展出來的新解釋或想法。"},{"en":"More recent theories about migration use data from ringing, radar and satellite tracking.","zh":"關於遷徙的較新理論會使用來自繫放、雷達和衛星追蹤的數據。"},{"en":"Newer theories often improve because they are based on better technology and more evidence.","zh":"較新理論通常會因更好科技和更多證據而改善。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a shift from older ideas to newer scientific explanations.","zh":"這個短語表示從較舊想法轉向較新的科學解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 14 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 15/task-1":[{"front":"cleaning services","meaning":"清潔服務","examples":[{"en":"Easy Life Cleaning Services offers domestic cleaning and maintenance support.","zh":"Easy Life Cleaning Services 提供住家清潔和維修支援。"},{"en":"Cleaning services are professional services that clean homes, offices, shops, or other places.","zh":"cleaning services 指為住宅、辦公室、商店或其他地方提供的專業清潔服務。"},{"en":"Many busy people use cleaning services when they do not have time to clean their flats properly.","zh":"很多忙碌的人沒有時間妥善清潔單位時，會使用清潔服務。"},{"en":"Good cleaning services should be reliable, careful, and clear about what is included.","zh":"良好的清潔服務應該可靠、細心，並清楚說明包括甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to regular cleaning, deep cleaning, or special cleaning tasks.","zh":"這個片語可指定期清潔、深層清潔或特別清潔項目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"speaking","meaning":"我是……；……接聽中","examples":[{"en":"Jacinta answers the phone by saying, “Jacinta speaking.”","zh":"Jacinta 接電話時說：「我是 Jacinta。」"},{"en":"Speaking is used on the phone to say who is answering the call.","zh":"speaking 用於電話中表示是誰正在接聽。"},{"en":"“Reception speaking” means the reception desk is answering the phone.","zh":"“Reception speaking” 的意思是接待處正在接聽電話。"},{"en":"This expression sounds polite and professional in business phone calls.","zh":"這個表達在商務電話中聽起來有禮而專業。"},{"en":"It is similar to saying “This is Jacinta” or “Jacinta here.”","zh":"它類似於說 “This is Jacinta” 或 “Jacinta here”。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look for","meaning":"尋找","examples":[{"en":"The client is looking for a cleaning service for her flat.","zh":"客戶正在尋找一項為她單位提供的清潔服務。"},{"en":"To look for something means to try to find it.","zh":"look for something 指嘗試尋找某物。"},{"en":"A student may look for a quiet place to study before an exam.","zh":"學生可能在考試前尋找安靜的溫習地方。"},{"en":"People look for services by asking friends, searching online, or calling companies.","zh":"人們會透過問朋友、上網搜尋或致電公司來尋找服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is very common in everyday conversation.","zh":"這個片語在日常對話中非常常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cleaning service","meaning":"清潔服務","examples":[{"en":"The client wants a cleaning service for her flat.","zh":"客戶想為她的單位找清潔服務。"},{"en":"A cleaning service is a professional arrangement in which cleaners come to clean a place.","zh":"cleaning service 指清潔員到某地方進行清潔的專業安排。"},{"en":"A cleaning service may visit once a week, once a month, or only when needed.","zh":"清潔服務可以每星期、每月或只在有需要時上門。"},{"en":"Before booking a cleaning service, clients should check the price and what tasks are included.","zh":"預訂清潔服務前，客戶應查看價格和包括哪些工作。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to a paid service, not informal help from a friend.","zh":"這個片語通常指付費服務，而不是朋友的非正式幫忙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"domestic cleaning","meaning":"住家清潔","examples":[{"en":"The client asks whether the company does domestic cleaning.","zh":"客戶詢問該公司是否提供住家清潔。"},{"en":"Domestic cleaning means cleaning inside homes, flats, or private living spaces.","zh":"domestic cleaning 指住宅、單位或私人居住空間內的清潔。"},{"en":"Domestic cleaning may include dusting, floor cleaning, kitchen cleaning, and bathroom cleaning.","zh":"住家清潔可能包括抹塵、清潔地板、清潔廚房和清潔浴室。"},{"en":"People often book domestic cleaning when they are too busy to keep their home tidy.","zh":"人們太忙而無法保持家居整潔時，常會預訂住家清潔。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts home cleaning with office or commercial cleaning.","zh":"這個片語把家居清潔與辦公室或商業清潔作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one-bedroom flat","meaning":"一房單位","examples":[{"en":"The client lives in a one-bedroom flat.","zh":"客戶住在一個一房單位。"},{"en":"A one-bedroom flat is a flat with one separate bedroom.","zh":"one-bedroom flat 指有一間獨立睡房的單位。"},{"en":"A one-bedroom flat may be suitable for one person or a couple.","zh":"一房單位可能適合一個人或一對伴侶居住。"},{"en":"Cleaning a one-bedroom flat usually takes less time than cleaning a larger family home.","zh":"清潔一房單位通常比清潔較大的家庭住宅需時少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the size and layout of a home.","zh":"這個片語描述住所的大小和間隔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"basic cleaning package","meaning":"基本清潔套餐","examples":[{"en":"The client asks whether the company has a basic cleaning package.","zh":"客戶詢問該公司是否有基本清潔套餐。"},{"en":"A basic cleaning package is a standard set of cleaning tasks offered for a fixed service.","zh":"basic cleaning package 指一套標準清潔工作，作為固定服務提供。"},{"en":"A basic cleaning package may include dusting, floor cleaning, and bathroom cleaning.","zh":"基本清潔套餐可能包括抹塵、清潔地板和清潔浴室。"},{"en":"Clients may add extra services if the basic package does not cover everything they need.","zh":"如果基本套餐未涵蓋所有需要，客戶可以增加額外服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing service levels and prices.","zh":"這個片語適合用於比較服務級別和價格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"we’re probably looking at","meaning":"大概需要……","examples":[{"en":"For a one-bedroom flat, they are probably looking at about two hours for a clean.","zh":"對一房單位來說，他們大概需要約兩小時清潔。"},{"en":"We’re probably looking at means we are likely estimating or considering a certain amount.","zh":"we’re probably looking at 指我們大概估計或考慮某個數量。"},{"en":"For this repair, we’re probably looking at about three days of work.","zh":"這項維修大概需要約三天工作。"},{"en":"Companies use this phrase when giving an estimate rather than an exact promise.","zh":"公司在提供估算而不是精確承諾時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It sounds natural in service enquiries and price discussions.","zh":"它在服務查詢和價格討論中聽起來自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"two hours for a clean","meaning":"清潔約兩小時","examples":[{"en":"The company estimates about two hours for a clean.","zh":"公司估計清潔約兩小時。"},{"en":"Two hours for a clean means the cleaning job is expected to take around two hours.","zh":"two hours for a clean 指預計清潔工作需時約兩小時。"},{"en":"A small flat may need two hours for a clean if it is already fairly tidy.","zh":"如果小單位本身相當整潔，清潔可能需要約兩小時。"},{"en":"The time needed for a clean depends on size, dirtiness, and requested tasks.","zh":"清潔所需時間取決於面積、骯髒程度和要求項目。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when estimating service time.","zh":"這個片語適合用於估計服務時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"thorough clean","meaning":"徹底清潔","examples":[{"en":"The cleaners will do a thorough clean of all surfaces.","zh":"清潔員會徹底清潔所有表面。"},{"en":"A thorough clean is a careful and detailed clean, not a quick surface wipe.","zh":"thorough clean 指仔細而詳細的清潔，不只是快速抹一抹表面。"},{"en":"A kitchen needs a thorough clean after heavy cooking.","zh":"大量煮食後，廚房需要徹底清潔。"},{"en":"A thorough clean can remove dust, grease, stains, and hidden dirt.","zh":"徹底清潔可以去除塵埃、油漬、污漬和隱藏污垢。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful attention to detail.","zh":"這個片語暗示細心處理細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"all surfaces","meaning":"所有表面","examples":[{"en":"The cleaners will clean all surfaces in each room.","zh":"清潔員會清潔每個房間的所有表面。"},{"en":"All surfaces means every visible or usable top layer, such as tables, shelves, counters, and cupboards.","zh":"all surfaces 指所有可見或可使用的表層，例如桌面、層架、櫃面和櫥櫃。"},{"en":"Dust can collect on all surfaces if a flat is not cleaned regularly.","zh":"如果單位沒有定期清潔，所有表面都可能積塵。"},{"en":"Cleaning all surfaces helps a room look fresh and reduces allergens.","zh":"清潔所有表面可以令房間看起來清爽，並減少致敏原。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in cleaning instructions.","zh":"這個片語常見於清潔指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in each room","meaning":"在每個房間","examples":[{"en":"The basic package covers surfaces in each room.","zh":"基本套餐涵蓋每個房間的表面。"},{"en":"In each room means in every room separately.","zh":"in each room 指在每個房間分別進行。"},{"en":"The cleaner checked the windows in each room before leaving.","zh":"清潔員離開前檢查了每個房間的窗戶。"},{"en":"Cleaning in each room ensures that no part of the flat is forgotten.","zh":"在每個房間清潔可確保單位沒有部分被遺漏。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the service applies throughout the home.","zh":"這個片語顯示服務適用於整個家居。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"polish where necessary","meaning":"如有需要會拋光","examples":[{"en":"The cleaners will polish surfaces where necessary.","zh":"清潔員會在有需要的地方為表面拋光。"},{"en":"To polish where necessary means to shine or smooth surfaces only when they need it.","zh":"polish where necessary 指只在需要時把表面擦亮或打磨平滑。"},{"en":"Wooden furniture may be polished where necessary to keep it looking new.","zh":"木家具如有需要可以拋光，以保持外觀新淨。"},{"en":"This service is not always needed for every surface.","zh":"並非每個表面都需要這項服務。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the cleaner will judge what is appropriate.","zh":"這個片語顯示清潔員會判斷甚麼做法合適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have carpets","meaning":"有地氈","examples":[{"en":"Jacinta asks whether the flat has carpets.","zh":"Jacinta 問該單位是否有地氈。"},{"en":"To have carpets means to have floors covered with carpet.","zh":"have carpets 指地板鋪有地氈。"},{"en":"Flats with carpets may need vacuuming more often than flats with wooden floors.","zh":"有地氈的單位可能比木地板單位更需要經常吸塵。"},{"en":"Cleaning carpets can take extra time because dust and hair get trapped in the fibres.","zh":"清潔地氈可能需要額外時間，因為塵埃和頭髮會卡在纖維中。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when asking about home cleaning needs.","zh":"這個片語常用於詢問家居清潔需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the floor would need cleaning","meaning":"地板需要清潔","examples":[{"en":"The client says the floor would need cleaning.","zh":"客戶說地板需要清潔。"},{"en":"The floor would need cleaning means the floor should be cleaned as part of the service.","zh":"the floor would need cleaning 指地板應作為服務的一部分被清潔。"},{"en":"After a party, the floor would need cleaning because of spilled drinks and crumbs.","zh":"派對後，地板可能因飲品濺出和食物碎屑而需要清潔。"},{"en":"Clients say this when they want to make sure floor cleaning is included.","zh":"客戶想確保包括地板清潔時，會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase politely states a cleaning requirement.","zh":"這個片語有禮地說明清潔需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"do that in every room","meaning":"在每個房間都做那項工作","examples":[{"en":"The cleaners would clean the floor in every room.","zh":"清潔員會在每個房間清潔地板。"},{"en":"To do that in every room means to carry out the same task throughout all rooms.","zh":"do that in every room 指在所有房間都進行同一項工作。"},{"en":"The cleaner will dust the shelves and do that in every room.","zh":"清潔員會抹層架，並在每個房間都做那項工作。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the full task again.","zh":"這個片語避免再次重複完整工作內容。"},{"en":"It is useful in conversations about service details.","zh":"它適合用於討論服務細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"kitchen and bathroom","meaning":"廚房和浴室","examples":[{"en":"The basic package includes a thorough clean of the kitchen and bathroom.","zh":"基本套餐包括徹底清潔廚房和浴室。"},{"en":"The kitchen and bathroom are often the rooms that need the most cleaning.","zh":"kitchen and bathroom 通常是最需要清潔的房間。"},{"en":"Kitchens may have grease, while bathrooms may have soap marks and water stains.","zh":"廚房可能有油漬，而浴室可能有皂漬和水漬。"},{"en":"A good cleaning service should pay special attention to the kitchen and bathroom.","zh":"好的清潔服務應特別注意廚房和浴室。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in home-cleaning packages.","zh":"這個片語常出現在家居清潔套餐中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"additional services","meaning":"額外服務","examples":[{"en":"The company offers additional services that clients can request.","zh":"該公司提供客戶可要求的額外服務。"},{"en":"Additional services are extra tasks not included in the basic package.","zh":"additional services 指基本套餐以外的額外工作。"},{"en":"Window cleaning and oven cleaning may be additional services.","zh":"清潔窗戶和清潔焗爐可能屬於額外服務。"},{"en":"Clients pay for additional services when they need more than standard cleaning.","zh":"當客戶需要標準清潔以外的工作，便會支付額外服務費用。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate basic work from optional extras.","zh":"這個片語有助區分基本工作和可選額外項目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"request","meaning":"要求；提出要求","examples":[{"en":"Clients can request additional services if they want.","zh":"客戶如果想要，可以要求額外服務。"},{"en":"To request something means to ask for it formally or politely.","zh":"request something 指正式或有禮地要求某事。"},{"en":"A client may request an extra cleaner if the flat is very large.","zh":"如果單位很大，客戶可能要求多一名清潔員。"},{"en":"Service companies often ask clients to request special tasks in advance.","zh":"服務公司常要求客戶提前提出特別工作要求。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “ask for”.","zh":"這個字比 “ask for” 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"for example","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"Jacinta gives oven cleaning as an example of an additional service.","zh":"Jacinta 以清潔焗爐作為額外服務的例子。"},{"en":"For example introduces one case from a larger group.","zh":"for example 從較大類別中引入一個例子。"},{"en":"Some cleaning tasks, for example fridge cleaning, may cost extra.","zh":"有些清潔工作，例如清潔雪櫃，可能需要額外收費。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain a general idea with a concrete example.","zh":"這個片語用具體例子幫助解釋一般想法。"},{"en":"It is common in teaching, service explanations, and everyday conversation.","zh":"它常見於教學、服務說明和日常對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"clean your oven","meaning":"清潔你的焗爐","examples":[{"en":"The company can clean the client’s oven every week.","zh":"公司可以每星期清潔客戶的焗爐。"},{"en":"To clean your oven means to remove grease, burnt food, and stains from inside the oven.","zh":"clean your oven 指清除焗爐內的油污、燒焦食物和污漬。"},{"en":"Some people clean their oven after cooking oily or messy food.","zh":"有些人在煮過油膩或容易弄髒的食物後會清潔焗爐。"},{"en":"Regular oven cleaning can reduce smells and make cooking more hygienic.","zh":"定期清潔焗爐可以減少異味，並令煮食更衛生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific kitchen-cleaning task.","zh":"這個片語描述一項特定廚房清潔工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"every week","meaning":"每星期","examples":[{"en":"The company can clean the fridge every week.","zh":"公司可以每星期清潔雪櫃。"},{"en":"Every week means once each week or weekly.","zh":"every week 指每週一次。"},{"en":"The cleaner visits every week to keep the flat tidy.","zh":"清潔員每星期上門一次，保持單位整潔。"},{"en":"Weekly cleaning is useful for tasks that become dirty quickly.","zh":"每星期清潔適合很快變髒的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regular frequency.","zh":"這個片語描述定期頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hardly ever use","meaning":"幾乎從不使用","examples":[{"en":"The client hardly ever uses the oven.","zh":"客戶幾乎從不使用焗爐。"},{"en":"To hardly ever use something means to use it very rarely.","zh":"hardly ever use something 指非常少使用某物。"},{"en":"I hardly ever use the printer because most documents are digital now.","zh":"我幾乎從不使用打印機，因為現在大部分文件都是數碼的。"},{"en":"If a client hardly ever uses the oven, weekly oven cleaning may not be necessary.","zh":"如果客戶幾乎從不使用焗爐，每星期清潔焗爐可能沒有必要。"},{"en":"This phrase means almost never, but not completely never.","zh":"這個片語指幾乎從不，但不是完全不使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"do the fridge","meaning":"清潔雪櫃","examples":[{"en":"The client asks whether the cleaners can do the fridge.","zh":"客戶問清潔員是否可以清潔雪櫃。"},{"en":"To do the fridge means to clean the fridge, especially inside it.","zh":"do the fridge 指清潔雪櫃，尤其是清潔內部。"},{"en":"A cleaner may do the fridge by removing old food and wiping the shelves.","zh":"清潔員可能透過清走舊食物和抹層架來清潔雪櫃。"},{"en":"Fridge cleaning is useful because spills and smells can build up over time.","zh":"清潔雪櫃很有用，因為溢出的食物和異味會隨時間累積。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and uses “do” to mean “clean”.","zh":"這個片語較口語，當中 “do” 的意思是「清潔」。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have that done","meaning":"讓人做那件事","examples":[{"en":"The client would like the fridge cleaning done every week.","zh":"客戶想每星期讓人清潔雪櫃。"},{"en":"To have that done means to arrange for someone else to do that task.","zh":"have that done 指安排別人完成那項工作。"},{"en":"She has her windows cleaned once a month.","zh":"她每月讓人清潔窗戶一次。"},{"en":"Clients use this structure when they pay or ask another person to do a service.","zh":"客戶付費或請別人提供服務時，會使用這個結構。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on arranging the result, not doing the work yourself.","zh":"這個片語着重安排結果，而不是自己做那項工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ironing clothes","meaning":"熨衣服","examples":[{"en":"The client asks whether ironing clothes is an additional service.","zh":"客戶詢問熨衣服是否屬於額外服務。"},{"en":"Ironing clothes means using a hot iron to remove creases from clothes.","zh":"ironing clothes 指用熱熨斗去除衣服皺褶。"},{"en":"Some people need help ironing clothes because work shirts must look neat.","zh":"有些人需要幫忙熨衣服，因為上班恤衫必須整齊。"},{"en":"Ironing can take time, especially when there are many shirts or formal clothes.","zh":"熨衣服可能需時，尤其是有很多恤衫或正式衣物時。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a household task often offered as an extra service.","zh":"這個片語描述一項常作為額外服務提供的家務工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it wouldn’t be much","meaning":"不會很多","examples":[{"en":"The client says the ironing would not be much.","zh":"客戶說要熨的衣服不會很多。"},{"en":"It wouldn’t be much means the amount of work would be small.","zh":"it wouldn’t be much 指工作量不大。"},{"en":"The washing wouldn’t be much because I only have a few shirts.","zh":"要洗的衣服不會很多，因為我只有幾件恤衫。"},{"en":"Clients may say this to show that an extra task should not take long.","zh":"客戶可能用這句表示額外工作應該不會花很久。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds polite and slightly reassuring.","zh":"這個片語聽起來有禮，並帶一點安撫語氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"shirts for work","meaning":"上班穿的恤衫","examples":[{"en":"The client only needs her shirts for work ironed.","zh":"客戶只需要熨她上班穿的恤衫。"},{"en":"Shirts for work are shirts worn for a job, usually formal or smart-looking.","zh":"shirts for work 指上班穿的恤衫，通常較正式或整齊。"},{"en":"Office workers may need clean shirts for work every weekday.","zh":"辦公室員工可能每個工作日都需要乾淨的上班恤衫。"},{"en":"Work shirts often need ironing because creases can look unprofessional.","zh":"上班恤衫常需要熨，因為皺褶可能顯得不專業。"},{"en":"This phrase connects clothing with workplace appearance.","zh":"這個片語把衣物與職場外觀連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"clean your microwave","meaning":"清潔微波爐","examples":[{"en":"Jacinta says the cleaners could clean the microwave.","zh":"Jacinta 說清潔員可以清潔微波爐。"},{"en":"To clean your microwave means to wipe food stains, smells, and grease from inside and outside it.","zh":"clean your microwave 指擦走微波爐內外的食物污漬、氣味和油污。"},{"en":"A microwave may need cleaning after sauce splashes inside.","zh":"醬汁在微波爐內濺出後，微波爐可能需要清潔。"},{"en":"Regular microwave cleaning keeps food smells from building up.","zh":"定期清潔微波爐可以防止食物氣味累積。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small kitchen appliance-cleaning task.","zh":"這個片語描述一項小型廚房電器清潔工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"wipe something out","meaning":"擦乾淨某物內部","examples":[{"en":"The client wipes the microwave out pretty regularly.","zh":"客戶頗定期地擦乾淨微波爐內部。"},{"en":"To wipe something out means to clean the inside of it with a cloth or tissue.","zh":"wipe something out 指用布或紙巾清潔某物內部。"},{"en":"After heating soup, she wiped the bowl out before washing it properly.","zh":"加熱湯後，她先擦乾淨碗內部，再正式清洗。"},{"en":"Wiping a microwave out regularly prevents stains from becoming hard to remove.","zh":"定期擦乾淨微波爐內部，可以防止污漬變得難以清除。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on cleaning the inside surface.","zh":"這個片語着重清潔內部表面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pretty regularly","meaning":"頗定期地","examples":[{"en":"The client cleans the microwave pretty regularly.","zh":"客戶頗定期地清潔微波爐。"},{"en":"Pretty regularly means fairly often or quite consistently.","zh":"pretty regularly 指相當經常或頗穩定地。"},{"en":"He checks his email pretty regularly during office hours.","zh":"他在辦公時間頗定期地查看電郵。"},{"en":"If something is cleaned pretty regularly, it may not need extra professional cleaning.","zh":"如果某物頗定期地被清潔，它可能不需要額外專業清潔。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and gives an approximate frequency.","zh":"這個片語較口語，表示大約頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"there’s no need for","meaning":"不需要……","examples":[{"en":"The client says there is no need for microwave cleaning.","zh":"客戶說不需要清潔微波爐。"},{"en":"There’s no need for something means it is not necessary.","zh":"there’s no need for something 指某事沒有必要。"},{"en":"There is no need for extra chairs because only five people are coming.","zh":"不需要額外椅子，因為只有五個人會來。"},{"en":"Clients use this phrase when they want to decline an optional service politely.","zh":"客戶想有禮貌地拒絕可選服務時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on necessity, not dislike.","zh":"這個片語着重是否有必要，而不是不喜歡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a bit less often","meaning":"沒那麼頻密","examples":[{"en":"The company offers services that clients may want a bit less often.","zh":"公司提供一些客戶可能沒那麼頻密需要的服務。"},{"en":"A bit less often means not as frequently.","zh":"a bit less often 指沒有那麼經常。"},{"en":"Curtains may need cleaning a bit less often than floors.","zh":"窗簾可能比地板沒那麼頻密需要清潔。"},{"en":"Some tasks do not need weekly attention because they get dirty more slowly.","zh":"有些工作不需要每星期處理，因為它們變髒得較慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lower frequency in a gentle way.","zh":"這個片語以柔和方式描述較低頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"say every month","meaning":"例如每月一次","examples":[{"en":"Some additional services can be done, say, every month.","zh":"有些額外服務可以做，例如每月一次。"},{"en":"Say every month means for example, once a month.","zh":"say every month 指例如每月一次。"},{"en":"You could check the smoke alarm, say, every month.","zh":"你可以檢查煙霧警報器，例如每月一次。"},{"en":"In conversation, “say” is used to suggest an example frequency or amount.","zh":"在對話中，“say” 用來提出一個例子頻率或數量。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds casual and flexible.","zh":"這個片語聽起來口語而有彈性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"inside of your windows","meaning":"窗戶內側","examples":[{"en":"The cleaners can clean the inside of the client’s windows.","zh":"清潔員可以清潔客戶窗戶內側。"},{"en":"The inside of your windows means the interior glass surface facing into your home.","zh":"inside of your windows 指面向家居內部的玻璃表面。"},{"en":"The inside of windows can get dusty from cooking, pets, or fingerprints.","zh":"窗戶內側可能因煮食、寵物或指紋而變得有塵。"},{"en":"Cleaning the inside of windows can make a flat feel brighter.","zh":"清潔窗戶內側可以令單位感覺更光亮。"},{"en":"This phrase distinguishes indoor window cleaning from outside window cleaning.","zh":"這個片語把室內窗戶清潔與外側窗戶清潔區分開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"that’d be good","meaning":"那樣很好","examples":[{"en":"The client says window cleaning would be good.","zh":"客戶說清潔窗戶那樣很好。"},{"en":"That’d be good means that would be useful, suitable, or pleasing.","zh":"that’d be good 指那會有用、合適或令人滿意。"},{"en":"If the cleaner could come on Friday morning, that’d be good.","zh":"如果清潔員可以星期五早上來，那樣很好。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to accept or approve a suggestion casually.","zh":"人們用這個片語輕鬆地接受或認同建議。"},{"en":"It sounds friendly and natural in spoken English.","zh":"它在英語口語中聽起來友善自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on the fifteenth floor","meaning":"在十五樓","examples":[{"en":"The client lives on the fifteenth floor.","zh":"客戶住在十五樓。"},{"en":"On the fifteenth floor means on level fifteen of a building.","zh":"on the fifteenth floor 指在建築物第十五層。"},{"en":"People living on the fifteenth floor may have good views but need lifts every day.","zh":"住在十五樓的人可能有好景觀，但每天需要使用升降機。"},{"en":"Window cleaning on high floors can be more difficult and dangerous outside.","zh":"高層外窗清潔可能更困難和危險。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise building location.","zh":"這個片語提供準確樓層位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the outside gets done regularly","meaning":"外側定期有人清潔","examples":[{"en":"The outside of the windows gets done regularly by specialists.","zh":"窗戶外側定期由專業人員清潔。"},{"en":"The outside gets done regularly means the exterior part is cleaned or maintained on a regular basis.","zh":"the outside gets done regularly 指外部定期被清潔或維護。"},{"en":"In some apartment blocks, the outside windows get done regularly by professional cleaners.","zh":"在有些住宅大廈，外窗會定期由專業清潔員處理。"},{"en":"High-rise residents usually cannot clean outside windows themselves safely.","zh":"高層居民通常不能安全地自行清潔外窗。"},{"en":"This phrase uses “gets done” to mean the work is arranged and completed.","zh":"這個片語用 “gets done” 表示工作已被安排並完成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"specialists","meaning":"專業人員","examples":[{"en":"Specialists regularly clean the outside of the windows.","zh":"專業人員定期清潔窗戶外側。"},{"en":"Specialists are people with special training, skills, or knowledge in a particular job.","zh":"specialists 指在某項工作中有特別訓練、技能或知識的人。"},{"en":"Window-cleaning specialists may use ropes, platforms, and safety equipment.","zh":"清潔窗戶的專業人員可能使用繩索、平台和安全設備。"},{"en":"Some tasks need specialists because they are too risky or technical for ordinary cleaners.","zh":"有些工作需要專業人員，因為對普通清潔員來說太危險或太技術性。"},{"en":"This word emphasises professional expertise.","zh":"這個字強調專業知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get a bit grubby","meaning":"變得有點污糟","examples":[{"en":"The inside of the windows gets a bit grubby.","zh":"窗戶內側會變得有點污糟。"},{"en":"To get a bit grubby means to become slightly dirty.","zh":"get a bit grubby 指變得有點骯髒。"},{"en":"The kitchen wall can get a bit grubby near the cooker.","zh":"廚房牆壁靠近煮食爐的位置可能會變得有點污糟。"},{"en":"Windows get grubby from dust, fingerprints, and moisture.","zh":"窗戶會因塵埃、指紋和濕氣而變污糟。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and less strong than “very dirty”.","zh":"這個片語較口語，比 “very dirty” 語氣輕。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"arrange for","meaning":"安排","examples":[{"en":"The company can arrange for the curtains to get cleaned.","zh":"公司可以安排窗簾清洗。"},{"en":"To arrange for something means to organise it so that it happens.","zh":"arrange for something 指安排某事發生。"},{"en":"The office can arrange for a repairman to visit tomorrow.","zh":"辦公室可以安排維修員明天上門。"},{"en":"Service companies arrange extra work by contacting the right staff or specialists.","zh":"服務公司透過聯絡合適員工或專業人員來安排額外工作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on organising rather than doing the task personally.","zh":"這個片語着重組織安排，而不是親自做該工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"curtains","meaning":"窗簾","examples":[{"en":"Jacinta asks whether the client needs her curtains cleaned.","zh":"Jacinta 問客戶是否需要清洗窗簾。"},{"en":"Curtains are pieces of fabric hung in front of windows for privacy, shade, or decoration.","zh":"curtains 指掛在窗前、用作私隱、遮光或裝飾的布料。"},{"en":"Curtains can collect dust, smells, and moisture over time.","zh":"窗簾會隨時間積聚塵埃、氣味和濕氣。"},{"en":"Cleaning curtains may require special washing or dry-cleaning methods.","zh":"清洗窗簾可能需要特別洗滌或乾洗方法。"},{"en":"This word refers to window fabric, not blinds or glass.","zh":"這個字指窗邊布料，而不是百葉簾或玻璃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get cleaned","meaning":"得到清洗","examples":[{"en":"The curtains can get cleaned if necessary.","zh":"如有需要，窗簾可以得到清洗。"},{"en":"To get cleaned means to be cleaned by someone or through an arranged service.","zh":"get cleaned 指由某人或透過安排服務完成清洗。"},{"en":"The sofa covers can get cleaned before the guests arrive.","zh":"梳化套可以在客人到達前得到清洗。"},{"en":"This structure focuses on the result, not who does the cleaning.","zh":"這個結構着重結果，而不是誰做清潔。"},{"en":"It is common when discussing services arranged for household items.","zh":"它常用於討論為家居物品安排服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"if necessary","meaning":"如有需要","examples":[{"en":"The company can arrange curtain cleaning if necessary.","zh":"如有需要，公司可以安排窗簾清洗。"},{"en":"If necessary means if it is needed.","zh":"if necessary 指如果有需要。"},{"en":"The cleaner can stay longer if necessary.","zh":"如有需要，清潔員可以留久一點。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids promising extra work unless the situation requires it.","zh":"這個片語避免承諾額外工作，除非情況需要。"},{"en":"It is useful in polite and practical service conversations.","zh":"它適合用於有禮而實際的服務對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be able to do something about","meaning":"能夠處理……","examples":[{"en":"The client asks whether the company can do something about the balcony.","zh":"客戶詢問公司能否處理露台。"},{"en":"To be able to do something about a problem means to be able to help deal with it.","zh":"be able to do something about a problem 指能夠幫忙處理某問題。"},{"en":"The landlord may be able to do something about the leaking tap.","zh":"業主可能能夠處理漏水水龍頭。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they are not sure what exact solution is possible.","zh":"當人們不確定有甚麼確切解決方法時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It sounds practical and problem-focused.","zh":"它聽起來實際，並以問題為中心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"balcony","meaning":"露台","examples":[{"en":"The client wants the balcony washed about once a month.","zh":"客戶想大約每月清洗露台一次。"},{"en":"A balcony is an outdoor platform attached to a flat or building, usually above ground level.","zh":"balcony 指連接單位或建築物的戶外平台，通常位於地面以上。"},{"en":"Balconies can collect dust, leaves, and rainwater.","zh":"露台會積聚塵埃、樹葉和雨水。"},{"en":"People may not use a balcony often, but it still needs cleaning from time to time.","zh":"人們可能不常使用露台，但它仍需要不時清潔。"},{"en":"This word refers to an outside part of a home.","zh":"這個字指家居的戶外部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not use it much","meaning":"不太常使用","examples":[{"en":"The client does not use the balcony much.","zh":"客戶不太常使用露台。"},{"en":"To not use it much means to use something only rarely or not very often.","zh":"not use it much 指只是很少或不太頻密地使用某物。"},{"en":"I do not use the oven much because I usually cook on the stove.","zh":"我不太常使用焗爐，因為我通常用爐頭煮食。"},{"en":"Even unused areas can get dirty if they are exposed to dust and weather.","zh":"即使不常使用的地方，如果暴露於塵埃和天氣中，也會變髒。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a service may be needed only occasionally.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何某服務可能只需偶爾做。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"could do with","meaning":"需要；最好有……","examples":[{"en":"The balcony could do with a wash every month or so.","zh":"露台最好大約每月清洗一次。"},{"en":"Could do with something means would benefit from it or really needs it.","zh":"could do with something 指某物會因某事而改善，或確實需要某事。"},{"en":"The kitchen floor could do with a good clean after the party.","zh":"派對後，廚房地板最好徹底清潔一下。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often suggests a gentle recommendation.","zh":"這個片語較口語，常帶有溫和建議意味。"},{"en":"It is softer than saying “must have”.","zh":"它比說 “must have” 更柔和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a wash","meaning":"清洗一次","examples":[{"en":"The balcony could do with a wash every month or so.","zh":"露台大約每月需要清洗一次。"},{"en":"A wash means a cleaning with water.","zh":"a wash 指用水清潔一次。"},{"en":"The car needs a wash after driving through muddy roads.","zh":"汽車駛過泥路後需要清洗一次。"},{"en":"Outdoor areas often need a wash because dust and rain leave marks.","zh":"戶外地方常需要清洗，因為塵埃和雨水會留下痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple and casual.","zh":"這個片語簡單而口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"every month or so","meaning":"大約每月一次","examples":[{"en":"The balcony should be washed every month or so.","zh":"露台應大約每月清洗一次。"},{"en":"Every month or so means approximately once a month.","zh":"every month or so 指大約每月一次。"},{"en":"Curtains may need washing every six months or so.","zh":"窗簾可能大約每六個月清洗一次。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate schedule rather than an exact date.","zh":"這個片語提供大約時間表，而不是確切日期。"},{"en":"It is useful for discussing routine household tasks.","zh":"它適合用於討論日常家務安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pressure washer","meaning":"高壓清洗機","examples":[{"en":"The cleaners can use a pressure washer on the balcony.","zh":"清潔員可以在露台使用高壓清洗機。"},{"en":"A pressure washer is a machine that sprays water with strong force to clean surfaces.","zh":"pressure washer 指以強水壓噴水清潔表面的機器。"},{"en":"A pressure washer can remove dirt from patios, balconies, and outdoor tiles.","zh":"高壓清洗機可以清除庭院、露台和戶外瓷磚上的污垢。"},{"en":"It should be used carefully because strong water pressure can damage delicate surfaces.","zh":"使用時應小心，因為強水壓可能損壞脆弱表面。"},{"en":"This phrase names a cleaning tool for tough outdoor dirt.","zh":"這個片語命名一種用於清理頑固戶外污垢的清潔工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be interested","meaning":"感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Jacinta asks whether the client is interested in general maintenance services.","zh":"Jacinta 問客戶是否對一般維修服務感興趣。"},{"en":"To be interested means to want to know more or possibly use something.","zh":"be interested 指想知道更多，或可能想使用某物。"},{"en":"The client may be interested in a monthly cleaning plan.","zh":"客戶可能對每月清潔計劃感興趣。"},{"en":"Service staff ask this question to see whether they should explain more options.","zh":"服務人員會這樣問，以了解是否應解釋更多選項。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses possible attention or desire.","zh":"這個片語表達可能的注意或意願。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"possibilities to do with","meaning":"與……有關的選項","examples":[{"en":"The company offers other possibilities to do with general maintenance.","zh":"公司提供其他與一般維修有關的選項。"},{"en":"Possibilities to do with something are options connected with that area or topic.","zh":"possibilities to do with something 指與某範疇或主題相關的選項。"},{"en":"The school discussed possibilities to do with improving the library.","zh":"學校討論了與改善圖書館有關的選項。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces related options without listing them all immediately.","zh":"這個片語引入相關選項，而不用立即全部列出。"},{"en":"It is useful when moving to a new service category.","zh":"當轉到新的服務類別時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"general maintenance","meaning":"一般維修","examples":[{"en":"The company can help with general maintenance issues.","zh":"公司可以幫忙處理一般維修問題。"},{"en":"General maintenance means basic repair and upkeep work around a home or building.","zh":"general maintenance 指住宅或建築物內的基本維修和保養工作。"},{"en":"General maintenance may include fixing leaks, checking lights, and repairing small faults.","zh":"一般維修可能包括修理漏水、檢查燈具和修補小故障。"},{"en":"Good maintenance prevents small household problems from becoming serious.","zh":"良好維修可以防止小型家居問題變得嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase covers practical repairs rather than cleaning only.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋實際維修，而不只是清潔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have a problem with","meaning":"在……方面有問題","examples":[{"en":"The client may have a problem with water and need a plumber.","zh":"客戶可能在水喉方面有問題，並需要水喉匠。"},{"en":"To have a problem with something means to experience difficulty or trouble related to it.","zh":"have a problem with something 指在某方面遇到困難或麻煩。"},{"en":"A tenant may have a problem with the electricity after moving in.","zh":"租客搬入後可能在電力方面有問題。"},{"en":"When people have a problem with water, they may need professional repair quickly.","zh":"當人們在水喉方面有問題時，可能需要快速專業維修。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for describing household faults.","zh":"這個片語適合描述家居故障。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"plumber","meaning":"水喉匠","examples":[{"en":"The company can put the client in touch with a plumber.","zh":"公司可以讓客戶聯絡到水喉匠。"},{"en":"A plumber is a worker who repairs water pipes, taps, toilets, and drainage systems.","zh":"plumber 指維修水管、水龍頭、廁所和排水系統的工人。"},{"en":"A plumber may be needed if a sink is leaking or a toilet is blocked.","zh":"如果洗手盆漏水或廁所堵塞，可能需要水喉匠。"},{"en":"Reliable plumbers are important because water problems can damage a home quickly.","zh":"可靠的水喉匠很重要，因為水喉問題可以很快損壞家居。"},{"en":"This word refers to a skilled maintenance worker.","zh":"這個字指熟練維修工人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in a hurry","meaning":"急需地","examples":[{"en":"The client may need a plumber in a hurry.","zh":"客戶可能急需水喉匠。"},{"en":"In a hurry means quickly or urgently.","zh":"in a hurry 指快速地或緊急地。"},{"en":"If water is leaking through the ceiling, you need help in a hurry.","zh":"如果水從天花板漏下來，你就急需幫忙。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when there is little time to wait.","zh":"當沒有太多時間等待時，人們會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It often suggests urgency rather than normal scheduling.","zh":"它常暗示緊急，而不是一般預約安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put someone in touch with","meaning":"讓某人聯絡到……","examples":[{"en":"The company can put the client in touch with a reliable plumber.","zh":"公司可以讓客戶聯絡到一位可靠的水喉匠。"},{"en":"To put someone in touch with another person means to help them contact that person.","zh":"put someone in touch with another person 指幫助某人聯絡到另一人。"},{"en":"The school put parents in touch with a speech therapist.","zh":"學校讓家長聯絡到一位言語治療師。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one person or company recommends a useful contact.","zh":"當某人或公司推薦有用聯絡人時，這個片語很有用。"},{"en":"It focuses on connecting people, not doing the work directly.","zh":"它着重連繫人與人，而不是直接做該工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reliable","meaning":"可靠的","examples":[{"en":"The company can recommend a reliable plumber.","zh":"公司可以推薦一位可靠的水喉匠。"},{"en":"Reliable means trustworthy and likely to do the job properly.","zh":"reliable 指值得信任，而且很可能妥善完成工作。"},{"en":"A reliable cleaner arrives on time and follows instructions carefully.","zh":"可靠的清潔員會準時到達並仔細跟從指示。"},{"en":"People prefer reliable tradespeople because home repairs require trust.","zh":"人們較喜歡可靠的技工，因為家居維修需要信任。"},{"en":"This word is often used for people, services, and machines.","zh":"這個字常用於人、服務和機器。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come out straightaway","meaning":"立即上門","examples":[{"en":"A plumber can come out straightaway in an emergency.","zh":"在緊急情況下，水喉匠可以立即上門。"},{"en":"To come out straightaway means to visit immediately or very soon.","zh":"come out straightaway 指立即或很快上門。"},{"en":"If a pipe bursts, a plumber should come out straightaway.","zh":"如果水管爆裂，水喉匠應立即上門。"},{"en":"Emergency services are valuable because some problems cannot wait.","zh":"緊急服務很有價值，因為有些問題不能等。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in repair and maintenance contexts.","zh":"這個片語常見於維修和保養語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the same thing if","meaning":"如……也一樣","examples":[{"en":"The same thing applies if the client needs an electrician.","zh":"如果客戶需要電工，也是一樣。"},{"en":"The same thing if means the same arrangement or rule also applies in another situation.","zh":"the same thing if 指相同安排或規則也適用於另一情況。"},{"en":"We can call a plumber for leaks, and the same thing applies if you need an electrician.","zh":"漏水時我們可以找水喉匠；如果你需要電工，也是一樣。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating a full explanation.","zh":"這個片語避免重複完整解釋。"},{"en":"It is useful when two services are handled in a similar way.","zh":"當兩項服務處理方式相似時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"electrician","meaning":"電工","examples":[{"en":"The company can also put the client in touch with an electrician.","zh":"公司也可以讓客戶聯絡到電工。"},{"en":"An electrician is a worker who installs, checks, or repairs electrical systems.","zh":"electrician 指安裝、檢查或維修電力系統的工人。"},{"en":"You may need an electrician if lights stop working or sockets become unsafe.","zh":"如果燈不亮或插座變得不安全，你可能需要電工。"},{"en":"Electrical problems should be handled carefully because they can be dangerous.","zh":"電力問題應小心處理，因為可能很危險。"},{"en":"This word refers to a skilled tradesperson.","zh":"這個字指熟練技工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"good to know","meaning":"知道這點很好","examples":[{"en":"The client says that the maintenance support is good to know.","zh":"客戶說知道有維修支援很好。"},{"en":"Good to know means the information is useful or reassuring.","zh":"good to know 指該資訊有用或令人安心。"},{"en":"It is good to know that the cleaner can come on Saturdays.","zh":"知道清潔員可以星期六上門很好。"},{"en":"People say this when new information helps them plan or feel less worried.","zh":"當新資訊幫助人們規劃或減少擔心時，人們會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase is friendly and common in conversation.","zh":"這個片語友善，常見於對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"only just moved here","meaning":"剛剛搬來這裏","examples":[{"en":"The client has only just moved here.","zh":"客戶剛剛搬來這裏。"},{"en":"Only just moved here means moved to this place very recently.","zh":"only just moved here 指非常近期才搬到這個地方。"},{"en":"I have only just moved here, so I do not know any repair services yet.","zh":"我剛剛搬來這裏，所以還不知道任何維修服務。"},{"en":"People who have just moved may need help finding local contacts.","zh":"剛搬來的人可能需要幫忙尋找本地聯絡人。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why someone is still unfamiliar with the area.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何某人仍不熟悉該區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"those sorts of contacts","meaning":"那類聯絡人","examples":[{"en":"The client does not have those sorts of contacts yet.","zh":"客戶還沒有那類聯絡人。"},{"en":"Those sorts of contacts means those kinds of useful people or service providers.","zh":"those sorts of contacts 指那類有用的人或服務提供者。"},{"en":"New residents may not have contacts such as plumbers, electricians, or cleaners.","zh":"新居民可能沒有水喉匠、電工或清潔員等聯絡人。"},{"en":"Having local contacts makes emergencies easier to handle.","zh":"有本地聯絡人會令緊急情況較容易處理。"},{"en":"This phrase is conversational and refers to practical connections.","zh":"這個片語較口語，指實用人脈。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be of interest to","meaning":"對……有興趣","examples":[{"en":"Jacinta asks whether the vacuum cleaning system is of interest to the client.","zh":"Jacinta 問該吸塵系統是否令客戶感興趣。"},{"en":"To be of interest to someone means to be something that person may want to know about or use.","zh":"be of interest to someone 指某事可能令某人想了解或使用。"},{"en":"A discount cleaning plan may be of interest to new tenants.","zh":"折扣清潔計劃可能令新租客感興趣。"},{"en":"Service staff use this phrase politely when offering an optional service.","zh":"服務人員提供可選服務時，會有禮地使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It sounds more formal than “Are you interested in this?”","zh":"它比 “Are you interested in this?” 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"special vacuum cleaning system","meaning":"特別吸塵系統","examples":[{"en":"The company offers a special vacuum cleaning system.","zh":"公司提供一套特別吸塵系統。"},{"en":"A special vacuum cleaning system is an advanced or unusual system for removing dust and dirt.","zh":"special vacuum cleaning system 指用來清除塵埃和污垢的先進或特別系統。"},{"en":"Such a system may be useful for homes with pets, carpets, or allergy sufferers.","zh":"這類系統可能適合有寵物、地氈或過敏人士的家居。"},{"en":"Special cleaning systems often promise better results than ordinary vacuuming.","zh":"特別清潔系統通常承諾比普通吸塵有更好效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a particular cleaning technology.","zh":"這個片語描述一種特定清潔科技。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"indoor air quality","meaning":"室內空氣質素","examples":[{"en":"The vacuum system can improve the indoor air quality of the client’s home.","zh":"該吸塵系統可以改善客戶家中的室內空氣質素。"},{"en":"Indoor air quality means how clean and healthy the air inside a building is.","zh":"indoor air quality 指建築物內空氣有多乾淨和健康。"},{"en":"Dust, smoke, dampness, and poor ventilation can reduce indoor air quality.","zh":"塵埃、煙霧、潮濕和通風差都會降低室內空氣質素。"},{"en":"Better indoor air quality can help people breathe more comfortably at home.","zh":"較好的室內空氣質素可以幫助人在家呼吸得更舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in health, housing, and cleaning contexts.","zh":"這個片語常見於健康、住屋和清潔語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"by capturing up to","meaning":"透過捕捉高達……","examples":[{"en":"The system improves air quality by capturing up to 99% of dust.","zh":"該系統透過捕捉高達 99% 的塵埃來改善空氣質素。"},{"en":"By capturing up to a certain amount means by catching as much as that maximum amount.","zh":"by capturing up to a certain amount 指透過捕捉最高可達某數量來達成效果。"},{"en":"The filter works by capturing up to 95% of tiny particles.","zh":"濾網透過捕捉高達 95% 的微粒來運作。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how a system achieves its result.","zh":"這個片語解釋系統如何達成其效果。"},{"en":"“Up to” gives a maximum figure, not a guarantee in every situation.","zh":"“Up to” 表示最高數字，不保證每種情況都達到。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dust in the air","meaning":"空氣中的塵埃","examples":[{"en":"The system captures dust in the air.","zh":"該系統捕捉空氣中的塵埃。"},{"en":"Dust in the air means tiny particles floating indoors or outdoors.","zh":"dust in the air 指在室內或室外漂浮的微小粒子。"},{"en":"Sunlight can make dust in the air easier to see.","zh":"陽光可以令空氣中的塵埃更容易被看見。"},{"en":"Dust in the air may affect people with allergies or breathing problems.","zh":"空氣中的塵埃可能影響有過敏或呼吸問題的人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to dust before it settles on surfaces.","zh":"這個片語指尚未沉積到表面的塵埃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be troubled by allergies","meaning":"受過敏困擾","examples":[{"en":"The system can help people who are troubled by allergies.","zh":"該系統可以幫助受過敏困擾的人。"},{"en":"To be troubled by allergies means to suffer discomfort because of allergic reactions.","zh":"be troubled by allergies 指因過敏反應而感到不適。"},{"en":"People troubled by allergies may sneeze, cough, or get itchy eyes.","zh":"受過敏困擾的人可能會打噴嚏、咳嗽或眼痕。"},{"en":"Reducing dust can help people troubled by allergies feel better at home.","zh":"減少塵埃可以幫助受過敏困擾的人在家感覺更好。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds more formal than “have allergies”.","zh":"這個片語比 “have allergies” 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make a big difference","meaning":"帶來很大改善","examples":[{"en":"The vacuum system can make a big difference for allergy sufferers.","zh":"該吸塵系統可以為過敏人士帶來很大改善。"},{"en":"To make a big difference means to have a strong positive effect.","zh":"make a big difference 指產生強烈正面影響。"},{"en":"Opening the windows every day can make a big difference to indoor air quality.","zh":"每天開窗可以對室內空氣質素帶來很大改善。"},{"en":"Small changes can make a big difference when they are done regularly.","zh":"小改變如果定期進行，也可以帶來很大改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to emphasise practical improvement.","zh":"這個片語常用來強調實際改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"that sort of problem","meaning":"那類問題","examples":[{"en":"The client does not have that sort of problem.","zh":"客戶沒有那類問題。"},{"en":"That sort of problem means that kind of difficulty or issue.","zh":"that sort of problem 指那一類困難或問題。"},{"en":"People with no pets may not have that sort of problem with fur on carpets.","zh":"沒有寵物的人可能沒有地氈上有毛髮那類問題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a problem already mentioned.","zh":"這個片語指回之前提及的問題。"},{"en":"It is conversational and slightly general.","zh":"它較口語，而且意思略泛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"bear it in mind","meaning":"記住；留意","examples":[{"en":"The client will bear the vacuum system in mind.","zh":"客戶會記住那套吸塵系統。"},{"en":"To bear something in mind means to remember it and consider it later.","zh":"bear something in mind 指記住某事，並在之後考慮。"},{"en":"I will bear your cleaning package in mind when I move into my new flat.","zh":"我搬進新單位時，會記住你的清潔套餐。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they are not choosing something now but may consider it in future.","zh":"人們現在不選擇某事、但日後可能考慮時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It sounds polite and thoughtful.","zh":"它聽起來有禮而周到。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tell me a bit about","meaning":"跟我說一點關於……","examples":[{"en":"The client asks Jacinta to tell her a bit about the cleaning staff.","zh":"客戶請 Jacinta 跟她說一點關於清潔職員的資料。"},{"en":"Tell me a bit about means give me some basic information about something.","zh":"tell me a bit about 指給我一些某事的基本資料。"},{"en":"A new client may ask the company to tell her a bit about its safety checks.","zh":"新客戶可能請公司跟她說一點關於安全審查的資料。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds friendly and not too demanding.","zh":"這個片語聽起來友善，而且不會太強硬。"},{"en":"It is useful when asking for a short explanation.","zh":"它適合用於要求簡短解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cleaning staff","meaning":"清潔職員","examples":[{"en":"The client wants to know about the company’s cleaning staff.","zh":"客戶想了解該公司的清潔職員。"},{"en":"Cleaning staff are workers who do cleaning jobs for a company or organisation.","zh":"cleaning staff 指為公司或機構進行清潔工作的員工。"},{"en":"Reliable cleaning staff should be trained, punctual, and respectful of clients’ homes.","zh":"可靠的清潔職員應受過訓練、準時，並尊重客戶家居。"},{"en":"Clients often want to know who will enter their home before booking a service.","zh":"客戶在預訂服務前，常想知道誰會進入自己家中。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the people providing the cleaning work.","zh":"這個片語指提供清潔工作的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"carefully selected","meaning":"經過謹慎挑選","examples":[{"en":"All the cleaners are very carefully selected.","zh":"所有清潔員都經過非常謹慎挑選。"},{"en":"Carefully selected means chosen with attention, checks, and judgement.","zh":"carefully selected 指經過仔細考慮、審查和判斷後挑選出來。"},{"en":"The company uses carefully selected staff for jobs inside private homes.","zh":"公司會安排經過謹慎挑選的職員處理私人住宅內的工作。"},{"en":"Careful selection helps build trust between clients and the service provider.","zh":"謹慎挑選有助建立客戶與服務提供者之間的信任。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests quality control and caution.","zh":"這個片語暗示質素控制和小心處理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"apply to","meaning":"向……申請","examples":[{"en":"Cleaners have to undergo checks when they apply to the company.","zh":"清潔員向公司申請時，必須接受審查。"},{"en":"To apply to a company means to formally ask for a job there.","zh":"apply to a company 指正式向某公司申請工作。"},{"en":"Applicants usually send a form or CV when they apply to a company.","zh":"申請人向公司申請時，通常會提交表格或履歷。"},{"en":"Companies may check people carefully when the job involves entering clients’ homes.","zh":"當工作涉及進入客戶家中，公司可能會仔細審查申請人。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in job and recruitment contexts.","zh":"這個片語常見於求職和招聘語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"undergo a security check","meaning":"接受保安審查","examples":[{"en":"Applicants have to undergo a security check.","zh":"申請人必須接受保安審查。"},{"en":"To undergo a security check means to be checked for safety, identity, or criminal history.","zh":"undergo a security check 指接受安全、身份或犯罪紀錄審查。"},{"en":"Staff working in schools may need to undergo a security check.","zh":"在學校工作的職員可能需要接受保安審查。"},{"en":"Security checks protect clients by reducing the risk of hiring unsafe workers.","zh":"保安審查透過減低聘用不安全員工的風險來保護客戶。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in recruitment.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常見於招聘。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"with the police","meaning":"向警方；透過警方","examples":[{"en":"The cleaners have to undergo a security check with the police.","zh":"清潔員必須透過警方接受保安審查。"},{"en":"With the police means through or involving the police authority.","zh":"with the police 指透過警方或涉及警方機關。"},{"en":"Some jobs require background checks with the police before applicants are accepted.","zh":"有些工作在接受申請人前，需要向警方作背景審查。"},{"en":"Police checks can confirm whether an applicant has relevant criminal records.","zh":"警方審查可以確認申請人是否有相關犯罪紀錄。"},{"en":"This phrase explains who carries out or supports the checking process.","zh":"這個片語解釋由誰進行或支援審查程序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"The company checks applicants to make sure they have no criminal background.","zh":"公司審查申請人，以確保他們沒有犯罪背景。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check carefully so that something is true.","zh":"make sure 指仔細檢查，以確保某事是真的。"},{"en":"The manager calls clients to make sure they are satisfied with the service.","zh":"經理致電客戶，以確保他們對服務滿意。"},{"en":"Companies make sure important standards are met before hiring staff.","zh":"公司聘用員工前會確保重要標準已達到。"},{"en":"This phrase shows careful checking and control.","zh":"這個片語顯示仔細檢查和控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"criminal background","meaning":"犯罪背景","examples":[{"en":"Applicants must not have any sort of criminal background.","zh":"申請人不得有任何犯罪背景。"},{"en":"A criminal background means a history of criminal behaviour or criminal records.","zh":"criminal background 指有犯罪行為或犯罪紀錄的過往。"},{"en":"Jobs in private homes often require checks for criminal background.","zh":"涉及私人住宅的工作通常需要犯罪背景審查。"},{"en":"Clients feel safer when staff have been checked for criminal history.","zh":"當職員已接受犯罪紀錄審查，客戶會感到更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in security and recruitment contexts.","zh":"這個片語常見於保安和招聘語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"provide references","meaning":"提供推薦人資料","examples":[{"en":"Applicants have to provide references as well.","zh":"申請人也必須提供推薦人資料。"},{"en":"To provide references means to give names or details of people who can confirm your character or work quality.","zh":"provide references 指提供可證明你品格或工作質素的人名或資料。"},{"en":"A cleaner may provide references from previous employers.","zh":"清潔員可能提供前僱主作為推薦人。"},{"en":"References help companies check whether an applicant is reliable and suitable.","zh":"推薦人資料幫助公司確認申請人是否可靠和合適。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in job applications.","zh":"這個片語常見於求職申請。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be suitable for","meaning":"適合……","examples":[{"en":"The company gives training to applicants who may be suitable for the job.","zh":"公司會為可能適合該工作的申請人提供培訓。"},{"en":"To be suitable for something means to have the right qualities or conditions for it.","zh":"be suitable for something 指具有適合某事的特質或條件。"},{"en":"A quiet and careful person may be suitable for home-cleaning work.","zh":"安靜而細心的人可能適合住家清潔工作。"},{"en":"Not every applicant is suitable for a job that requires trust and attention to detail.","zh":"並非每位申請人都適合需要信任和注重細節的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when judging fit.","zh":"這個片語適合用於判斷是否合適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"give someone training","meaning":"給某人培訓","examples":[{"en":"The company gives suitable applicants training for the job.","zh":"公司會給合適申請人工作培訓。"},{"en":"To give someone training means to teach them the skills and knowledge needed for a task.","zh":"give someone training 指教授某人完成任務所需的技能和知識。"},{"en":"New cleaners are given training before they visit clients’ homes.","zh":"新清潔員到客戶家前會接受培訓。"},{"en":"Training helps workers understand standards, safety, and customer service.","zh":"培訓幫助員工了解標準、安全和客戶服務。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on preparing people for work.","zh":"這個片語着重為工作作準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"last for two weeks","meaning":"持續兩星期","examples":[{"en":"The training lasts for two weeks.","zh":"培訓持續兩星期。"},{"en":"To last for two weeks means to continue for a period of fourteen days.","zh":"last for two weeks 指持續十四天。"},{"en":"The course lasts for two weeks and includes both lessons and practice.","zh":"課程持續兩星期，包括課堂和實習。"},{"en":"Longer training can give workers more time to learn procedures properly.","zh":"較長培訓可以給員工更多時間妥善學習程序。"},{"en":"This phrase describes duration.","zh":"這個片語描述持續時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"very thorough","meaning":"非常全面","examples":[{"en":"The two-week training is very thorough.","zh":"兩星期培訓非常全面。"},{"en":"Very thorough means detailed, complete, and careful.","zh":"very thorough 指詳細、完整和仔細。"},{"en":"A very thorough cleaner checks corners, shelves, handles, and hidden dust.","zh":"非常仔細的清潔員會檢查角落、層架、門柄和隱藏塵埃。"},{"en":"Thorough training helps staff avoid mistakes in clients’ homes.","zh":"全面培訓幫助員工避免在客戶家中犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests high standards and careful preparation.","zh":"這個片語暗示高標準和仔細準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at the end of","meaning":"在……結束時","examples":[{"en":"At the end of the training, applicants have a test.","zh":"在培訓結束時，申請人要接受測試。"},{"en":"At the end of something means when it finishes.","zh":"at the end of something 指某事結束時。"},{"en":"At the end of the lesson, the teacher gave a short quiz.","zh":"在課堂結束時，老師安排了一個小測。"},{"en":"Tests at the end of training check whether applicants have learned the required skills.","zh":"培訓結束時的測試可檢查申請人是否學會所需技能。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the final stage of a process.","zh":"這個片語標示過程的最後階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"take someone on","meaning":"錄用某人","examples":[{"en":"The company takes cleaners on if they pass the test.","zh":"如果清潔員通過測試，公司便會錄用他們。"},{"en":"To take someone on means to employ or hire that person.","zh":"take someone on 指聘用或錄用某人。"},{"en":"A restaurant may take on extra staff during the holidays.","zh":"餐廳可能在假期期間錄用額外員工。"},{"en":"Companies only take people on when they believe they are suitable for the job.","zh":"公司只有在相信某人適合工作時才會錄用。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in employment contexts.","zh":"這個片語常見於僱傭語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"monitor someone carefully","meaning":"仔細監察某人","examples":[{"en":"The company monitors its cleaners very carefully.","zh":"公司非常仔細地監察清潔員。"},{"en":"To monitor someone carefully means to watch or check their work closely over time.","zh":"monitor someone carefully 指持續密切觀察或檢查某人的工作。"},{"en":"A manager may monitor new staff carefully during their first month.","zh":"經理可能在新員工第一個月仔細監察他們。"},{"en":"Careful monitoring helps companies find problems before clients lose trust.","zh":"仔細監察幫助公司在客戶失去信任前發現問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests ongoing supervision.","zh":"這個片語暗示持續監督。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"complete a review of","meaning":"填寫對……的評價","examples":[{"en":"Clients complete a review of each cleaner’s performance after every visit.","zh":"客戶每次到訪後都會填寫對每位清潔員表現的評價。"},{"en":"To complete a review of something means to fill in an evaluation about it.","zh":"complete a review of something 指填寫對某事的評估。"},{"en":"Customers may complete a review of the cleaning service online.","zh":"顧客可能在網上填寫對清潔服務的評價。"},{"en":"Reviews help companies understand whether the service met expectations.","zh":"評價幫助公司了解服務是否符合期望。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in customer feedback systems.","zh":"這個片語常見於客戶回饋系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"performance","meaning":"表現","examples":[{"en":"Clients review the cleaner’s performance after every visit.","zh":"客戶每次到訪後評價清潔員的表現。"},{"en":"Performance means how well someone does a job or task.","zh":"performance 指某人完成工作或任務的好壞。"},{"en":"A cleaner’s performance can include punctuality, carefulness, and politeness.","zh":"清潔員的表現可以包括準時、細心和有禮。"},{"en":"Regular feedback on performance helps workers improve.","zh":"對表現作定期回饋，有助員工改善。"},{"en":"This word is common in work, school, and service evaluation.","zh":"這個字常見於工作、學校和服務評估。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"after every visit","meaning":"每次到訪後","examples":[{"en":"Clients send a review after every cleaning visit.","zh":"客戶每次清潔到訪後都會發送評價。"},{"en":"After every visit means each time the cleaner has finished a visit.","zh":"after every visit 指清潔員每次完成上門服務之後。"},{"en":"The company asks for feedback after every visit to check service quality.","zh":"公司每次到訪後都要求回饋，以檢查服務質素。"},{"en":"Frequent reviews help the company notice small problems quickly.","zh":"頻密評價幫助公司快速注意到小問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated action following each appointment.","zh":"這個片語描述每次預約後重複進行的行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"email it to","meaning":"把它電郵給……","examples":[{"en":"Clients email the performance review to the company.","zh":"客戶把表現評價電郵給公司。"},{"en":"To email it to someone means to send it by email to that person or organisation.","zh":"email it to someone 指用電郵把它發送給某人或機構。"},{"en":"Please email the completed form to the office by Friday.","zh":"請在星期五前把填妥的表格電郵給辦公室。"},{"en":"Emailing reviews creates a written record that the company can check later.","zh":"電郵評價可以建立書面紀錄，讓公司之後查閱。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in administrative instructions.","zh":"這個片語常見於行政指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pick up any problems","meaning":"即時發現任何問題","examples":[{"en":"The company can pick up any problems straightaway.","zh":"公司可以即時發現任何問題。"},{"en":"To pick up any problems means to notice or identify problems.","zh":"pick up any problems 指注意到或識別問題。"},{"en":"Regular client reviews help managers pick up problems with service quality.","zh":"定期客戶評價幫助經理發現服務質素問題。"},{"en":"If problems are picked up early, they can be fixed before they become serious.","zh":"如果問題及早被發現，就可以在變嚴重前修正。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in quality control.","zh":"這個片語常見於質素控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"deal with","meaning":"處理","examples":[{"en":"The company can deal with problems as soon as they appear.","zh":"公司可以在問題一出現時便處理。"},{"en":"To deal with something means to handle, solve, or respond to it.","zh":"deal with something 指處理、解決或回應某事。"},{"en":"A good manager deals with customer complaints calmly.","zh":"好經理會冷靜處理客戶投訴。"},{"en":"Companies that deal with problems quickly can keep clients’ trust.","zh":"快速處理問題的公司可以維持客戶信任。"},{"en":"This phrase is practical and widely used.","zh":"這個片語很實用，而且用途廣泛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"that all sounds good","meaning":"那一切聽起來都很好","examples":[{"en":"The client says that all the arrangements sound good.","zh":"客戶說所有安排聽起來都很好。"},{"en":"That all sounds good means everything mentioned seems acceptable or pleasing.","zh":"that all sounds good 指剛才提到的一切都似乎可以接受或令人滿意。"},{"en":"If the cleaner can come every Friday and include the fridge, that all sounds good.","zh":"如果清潔員可以每星期五上門並包括清潔雪櫃，那一切聽起來都很好。"},{"en":"People say this when they are satisfied with the explanation so far.","zh":"人們對目前解釋感到滿意時，會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase is friendly and positive in spoken conversation.","zh":"這個片語在口語對話中友善而正面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have the same cleaner","meaning":"由同一位清潔員服務","examples":[{"en":"The client asks whether she will always have the same cleaner.","zh":"客戶問她是否會一直由同一位清潔員服務。"},{"en":"To have the same cleaner means the same person comes to clean each time.","zh":"have the same cleaner 指每次由同一個人上門清潔。"},{"en":"Some clients prefer to have the same cleaner because trust builds over time.","zh":"有些客戶較喜歡由同一位清潔員服務，因為信任會隨時間建立。"},{"en":"Having the same cleaner can make instructions easier because the cleaner learns the home.","zh":"由同一位清潔員服務可以令指示更容易，因為清潔員會熟悉家居。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on consistency of service.","zh":"這個片語着重服務一致性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"do our best to","meaning":"盡力去……","examples":[{"en":"The company does its best to organise the same cleaner each time.","zh":"公司會盡力安排每次由同一位清潔員服務。"},{"en":"To do our best to do something means to try as hard as possible to achieve it.","zh":"do our best to do something 指盡最大努力達成某事。"},{"en":"We will do our best to arrange a cleaner for Friday morning.","zh":"我們會盡力安排清潔員星期五早上上門。"},{"en":"This phrase promises effort, but not an absolute guarantee.","zh":"這個片語承諾會努力，但不是絕對保證。"},{"en":"It is useful in customer service when schedules depend on staff availability.","zh":"當安排取決於員工時間表時，它在客戶服務中很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"organise it that way","meaning":"以那種方式安排","examples":[{"en":"The company tries to organise the cleaning visits that way.","zh":"公司會嘗試以那種方式安排清潔到訪。"},{"en":"To organise it that way means to arrange things according to that plan or preference.","zh":"organise it that way 指按照那個計劃或偏好安排事情。"},{"en":"If you prefer morning visits, we can try to organise it that way.","zh":"如果你較喜歡上午上門，我們可以嘗試以那種方式安排。"},{"en":"Service companies use this phrase when they try to match a client’s request.","zh":"服務公司嘗試配合客戶要求時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to an arrangement already discussed.","zh":"這個片語指回已討論的安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"usually manage it","meaning":"通常能做到","examples":[{"en":"The company usually manages to arrange the same cleaner.","zh":"公司通常能安排同一位清潔員。"},{"en":"Usually manage it means usually succeed in doing it.","zh":"usually manage it 指通常能成功做到某事。"},{"en":"We usually manage to send the same staff member, but holidays can make it difficult.","zh":"我們通常能派同一位員工，但假期可能會令安排困難。"},{"en":"This phrase gives confidence while leaving room for exceptions.","zh":"這個片語給人信心，同時保留例外情況的空間。"},{"en":"It is common when discussing practical arrangements.","zh":"它常用於討論實際安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"go ahead","meaning":"繼續進行；正式開始","examples":[{"en":"The client says she would like to go ahead with the service.","zh":"客戶說她想正式開始使用服務。"},{"en":"To go ahead with something means to decide to proceed or start it.","zh":"go ahead with something 指決定繼續進行或開始某事。"},{"en":"After hearing the price, the client decided to go ahead with the cleaning package.","zh":"聽完價格後，客戶決定正式開始使用清潔套餐。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they are ready to confirm a plan.","zh":"人們準備確認計劃時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It is common in business, services, and bookings.","zh":"它常見於商務、服務和預訂語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10}],"ielts/listening/Practice 15/task-2":[{"front":"as many of you","meaning":"由於你們許多人……","examples":[{"en":"As many of you have worked in the hotel industry, you know about staff turnover.","zh":"由於你們許多人曾在酒店業工作，你們都知道員工流失的問題。"},{"en":"As many of you means because many people in the audience or group share the same experience.","zh":"as many of you 的意思是由於聽眾或群體中許多人有相同經驗。"},{"en":"As many of you are parents, you understand how difficult it is to balance work and family.","zh":"由於你們許多人是父母，你們明白平衡工作和家庭有多困難。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase to connect their point with the audience’s own experience.","zh":"講者使用這個短語，把自己的觀點與聽眾的經驗連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a talk feel more personal and relevant.","zh":"這個短語令演講感覺更個人化，也更貼近聽眾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hotel industry","meaning":"酒店業","examples":[{"en":"Many people here today have worked in the hotel industry.","zh":"今天在場許多人曾在酒店業工作。"},{"en":"The hotel industry includes businesses that provide accommodation, guest services, food, and hospitality.","zh":"hotel industry 包括提供住宿、顧客服務、餐飲和款待服務的企業。"},{"en":"People in the hotel industry may work at reception, housekeeping, restaurants, or management.","zh":"酒店業人士可能在接待處、房務、餐廳或管理層工作。"},{"en":"The hotel industry depends heavily on good service because guests judge their stay by staff behaviour.","zh":"酒店業非常依賴良好服務，因為住客會按職員表現評價入住體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one part of the wider tourism and hospitality sector.","zh":"這個短語描述旅遊和款待業中其中一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for some time","meaning":"一段時間","examples":[{"en":"Many of the audience have worked in hotels for some time.","zh":"許多聽眾已在酒店工作了一段時間。"},{"en":"For some time means for a fairly long period, though the exact length is not stated.","zh":"for some time 的意思是持續了相當一段時間，但沒有說明確實長度。"},{"en":"She has been learning English for some time, so she understands basic grammar.","zh":"她學英文已有一段時間，所以理解基本文法。"},{"en":"When someone has done a job for some time, they usually notice repeated problems.","zh":"當某人做一份工作已有一段時間，通常會注意到反覆出現的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a general sense of experience over time.","zh":"這個短語概括表示一段時間累積的經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"experience the problem of","meaning":"經歷……的問題","examples":[{"en":"Many hotel managers have experienced the problem of high staff turnover.","zh":"許多酒店經理都經歷過員工流失率高的問題。"},{"en":"To experience the problem of something means to face or suffer from that difficulty in real life.","zh":"experience the problem of something 的意思是在現實中面對或承受某個困難。"},{"en":"Many schools experience the problem of students losing focus during long lessons.","zh":"許多學校都經歷學生在長課中失去專注的問題。"},{"en":"When a business experiences a problem repeatedly, managers need to look for deeper causes.","zh":"當企業反覆經歷一個問題，管理層需要尋找更深層原因。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a general problem with people who actually face it.","zh":"這個短語把一般問題與真正面對它的人連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"high staff turnover","meaning":"員工流失率高","examples":[{"en":"High staff turnover is a common problem in many hotels.","zh":"員工流失率高是許多酒店的常見問題。"},{"en":"High staff turnover means many employees leave an organisation within a short period.","zh":"high staff turnover 的意思是許多員工在短時間內離開機構。"},{"en":"A restaurant with high staff turnover must train new waiters again and again.","zh":"員工流失率高的餐廳必須一再培訓新侍應。"},{"en":"High staff turnover can damage service because experienced workers disappear.","zh":"員工流失率高可以損害服務，因為有經驗員工會流失。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in business and human resources.","zh":"這個短語常用於商業和人力資源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rely on","meaning":"依靠……","examples":[{"en":"Every hotel relies on loyal and experienced staff.","zh":"每間酒店都依靠忠誠而有經驗的職員。"},{"en":"To rely on someone or something means to need them and trust them to help or work properly.","zh":"rely on someone or something 的意思是需要並信任某人或某物能提供幫助或正常運作。"},{"en":"Students rely on clear notes when preparing for exams.","zh":"學生準備考試時依靠清晰筆記。"},{"en":"A business that relies on good service must treat staff seriously.","zh":"依靠良好服務的企業必須認真對待職員。"},{"en":"This phrase shows dependence and trust.","zh":"這個短語顯示依賴和信任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"loyal and experienced members of staff","meaning":"忠誠而有經驗的職員","examples":[{"en":"Hotels need loyal and experienced members of staff.","zh":"酒店需要忠誠而有經驗的職員。"},{"en":"Loyal and experienced members of staff are workers who stay with the company and know the job well.","zh":"loyal and experienced members of staff 是留在公司並熟悉工作的員工。"},{"en":"A school depends on loyal and experienced staff because they understand students and routines.","zh":"學校依靠忠誠而有經驗的職員，因為他們了解學生和日常流程。"},{"en":"Losing experienced staff can make training, service, and teamwork harder.","zh":"失去有經驗職員可以令培訓、服務和團隊合作更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes workers who bring both commitment and knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述同時有承擔和知識的員工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"make sure that","meaning":"確保……","examples":[{"en":"Experienced staff make sure that everything runs smoothly.","zh":"有經驗的職員確保一切順利運作。"},{"en":"To make sure that something happens means to check or act so that it happens properly.","zh":"make sure that something happens 的意思是檢查或採取行動，以確保某事正確發生。"},{"en":"Teachers make sure that students understand the instructions before starting an exam.","zh":"老師在考試開始前確保學生明白指示。"},{"en":"Making sure that details are correct prevents mistakes later.","zh":"確保細節正確可以避免之後出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in advice, management, and safety instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於建議、管理和安全指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"run smoothly","meaning":"順利運作","examples":[{"en":"Hotels need experienced staff to make sure everything runs smoothly.","zh":"酒店需要有經驗的職員來確保一切順利運作。"},{"en":"If something runs smoothly, it works well without delays, confusion, or serious problems.","zh":"如果某事 runs smoothly，意思是它運作良好，沒有延誤、混亂或嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A school trip runs smoothly when transport, food, and timing are well organised.","zh":"當交通、食物和時間安排妥當，學校旅行就會順利運作。"},{"en":"Experienced staff help things run smoothly because they know how to solve small problems quickly.","zh":"有經驗職員能幫助事情順利運作，因為他們知道如何快速解決小問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes efficient and trouble-free operation.","zh":"這個短語描述有效率且少麻煩的運作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"constantly changing","meaning":"不斷變動","examples":[{"en":"If staff are constantly changing, work becomes difficult for everyone.","zh":"如果職員不斷變動，工作對每個人都會變得困難。"},{"en":"Constantly changing means changing again and again, without staying stable.","zh":"constantly changing 的意思是不斷一次又一次改變，沒有保持穩定。"},{"en":"A timetable that is constantly changing makes it hard for students to plan revision.","zh":"不斷變動的時間表會令學生難以規劃溫習。"},{"en":"Constant change can create stress because people must keep learning new routines.","zh":"不斷變動可以製造壓力，因為人們必須一直學習新流程。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests instability.","zh":"這個短語常暗示不穩定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"make life difficult for","meaning":"令……的日子不好過","examples":[{"en":"High staff turnover can make life difficult for everyone.","zh":"員工流失率高可以令每個人的日子不好過。"},{"en":"To make life difficult for someone means to create problems, stress, or inconvenience for them.","zh":"make life difficult for someone 的意思是為某人製造問題、壓力或不便。"},{"en":"Constant noise can make life difficult for students trying to study.","zh":"持續噪音可以令想溫習的學生日子不好過。"},{"en":"When staff leave suddenly, managers and colleagues must work harder to cover the gaps.","zh":"當職員突然離職，經理和同事必須更辛苦地填補空缺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical difficulty in daily life or work.","zh":"這個短語描述日常生活或工作中的實際困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"leave frequently","meaning":"頻繁離職","examples":[{"en":"Staff leave frequently in many hotels.","zh":"許多酒店的職員頻繁離職。"},{"en":"To leave frequently means to leave often or repeatedly.","zh":"leave frequently 的意思是經常或反覆離開工作。"},{"en":"If teachers leave frequently, students may struggle to build stable relationships.","zh":"如果老師頻繁離職，學生可能難以建立穩定關係。"},{"en":"When employees leave frequently, managers spend more time recruiting and training replacements.","zh":"當員工頻繁離職，經理會花更多時間招聘和培訓替代人手。"},{"en":"This phrase shows repeated departure, not just one person leaving.","zh":"這個短語顯示反覆離開，而不只是一次離職。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"low-skilled","meaning":"技術要求低的","examples":[{"en":"Many hotel jobs, such as cleaning, are low-skilled.","zh":"許多酒店工作，例如清潔，都是技術要求低的。"},{"en":"Low-skilled work usually needs less formal training or fewer specialist qualifications.","zh":"low-skilled 工作通常需要較少正式培訓或較少專門資格。"},{"en":"Some low-skilled jobs still require hard work, patience, and reliability.","zh":"有些技術要求低的工作仍需要努力、耐性和可靠性。"},{"en":"Calling a job low-skilled does not mean the workers are unimportant.","zh":"稱一份工作技術要求低，不代表員工不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes job requirements, not personal worth.","zh":"這個短語描述工作要求，而不是個人價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not well-paid","meaning":"薪酬不高","examples":[{"en":"Many low-skilled hotel jobs are not well-paid.","zh":"許多技術要求低的酒店工作薪酬不高。"},{"en":"Not well-paid means the salary or wages are low compared with the work required.","zh":"not well-paid 的意思是薪金或工資相對工作要求而言較低。"},{"en":"Some care jobs are not well-paid even though they involve heavy responsibility.","zh":"有些護理工作雖然責任重大，薪酬仍不高。"},{"en":"If a job is not well-paid, workers may look for better opportunities elsewhere.","zh":"如果一份工作薪酬不高，員工可能到其他地方尋找更好機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low pay in a polite but clear way.","zh":"這個短語以禮貌但清楚的方式描述低薪。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"long hours","meaning":"長工時","examples":[{"en":"Some managers think long hours are a main cause of staff turnover.","zh":"有些經理認為長工時是員工流失的主要原因。"},{"en":"Long hours means working for many hours, often more than is comfortable or healthy.","zh":"long hours 的意思是工作很多小時，常超過舒服或健康的程度。"},{"en":"Nurses may work long hours during busy hospital periods.","zh":"醫院繁忙時期，護士可能要工作長工時。"},{"en":"Long hours can lead to tiredness, mistakes, and lower job satisfaction.","zh":"長工時可以導致疲倦、錯誤和較低工作滿意度。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in discussions of working conditions.","zh":"這個短語常出現在工作條件討論中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"main causes of","meaning":"……的主要原因","examples":[{"en":"Low pay and long hours are often seen as the main causes of staff turnover.","zh":"低薪和長工時常被視為員工流失的主要原因。"},{"en":"Main causes of something are the most important reasons why it happens.","zh":"main causes of something 是某事發生的最重要原因。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep and poor planning are main causes of weak exam performance.","zh":"睡眠不足和規劃差是考試表現差的主要原因。"},{"en":"Identifying the main causes of a problem helps people choose better solutions.","zh":"識別問題的主要原因，有助人們選擇更好解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on root reasons, not minor details.","zh":"這個短語集中於根本原因，而不是小細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what they don’t realise is that","meaning":"他們沒有意識到的是……","examples":[{"en":"What many managers don’t realise is that lack of training is a huge factor.","zh":"許多經理沒有意識到的是，缺乏培訓是一個重大因素。"},{"en":"What they don’t realise is that introduces an important fact people are missing.","zh":"what they don’t realise is that 用來引出人們忽略的重要事實。"},{"en":"What some parents don’t realise is that children may be tired, not lazy.","zh":"有些父母沒有意識到的是，孩子可能是疲倦，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when correcting a common misunderstanding.","zh":"這個短語適合用於糾正常見誤解。"},{"en":"It draws attention to something hidden or underestimated.","zh":"它把注意力帶到隱藏或被低估的事情上。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lack of training","meaning":"缺乏培訓","examples":[{"en":"The lack of training in many hotel jobs is a huge factor.","zh":"許多酒店工作缺乏培訓是一個重大因素。"},{"en":"Lack of training means workers have not been taught enough skills or knowledge for the job.","zh":"lack of training 的意思是員工沒有獲得足夠技能或工作知識教導。"},{"en":"New staff may make mistakes if there is a lack of training.","zh":"如果缺乏培訓，新職員可能會犯錯。"},{"en":"Lack of training can make employees feel unsupported and more likely to leave.","zh":"缺乏培訓可以令員工感到缺乏支援，並更可能離職。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gap in preparation.","zh":"這個短語描述準備上的缺口。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a huge factor","meaning":"重大因素","examples":[{"en":"Lack of training is a huge factor in high staff turnover.","zh":"缺乏培訓是員工流失率高的重大因素。"},{"en":"A huge factor is a very important reason that strongly affects a result.","zh":"a huge factor 是強烈影響結果的非常重要原因。"},{"en":"Long travel time can be a huge factor when workers decide whether to keep a job.","zh":"當員工決定是否保留一份工作，通勤時間長可以是重大因素。"},{"en":"If one factor strongly changes people’s behaviour, managers should not ignore it.","zh":"如果一個因素強烈改變人們行為，經理不應忽視它。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights major influence.","zh":"這個短語突出重大影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"high turnover of staff","meaning":"員工高流失率","examples":[{"en":"A high turnover of staff causes many problems for hotels.","zh":"員工高流失率為酒店造成許多問題。"},{"en":"A high turnover of staff means many workers leave and must be replaced often.","zh":"high turnover of staff 的意思是許多員工離開，而公司必須經常替換他們。"},{"en":"A shop with high staff turnover may struggle to keep service consistent.","zh":"員工高流失率的商店可能難以保持服務一致。"},{"en":"High staff turnover costs money because recruitment and training must happen repeatedly.","zh":"員工高流失率會花錢，因為招聘和培訓必須反覆進行。"},{"en":"This phrase is another way to say “high staff turnover”.","zh":"這個短語是 high staff turnover 的另一種說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recruit new staff","meaning":"招聘新職員","examples":[{"en":"Hotels with high turnover have to recruit new staff all the time.","zh":"員工流失率高的酒店必須一直招聘新職員。"},{"en":"To recruit new staff means to find and hire new workers.","zh":"recruit new staff 的意思是尋找並聘請新員工。"},{"en":"A restaurant may recruit new staff before the busy summer season.","zh":"餐廳可能在繁忙夏季前招聘新職員。"},{"en":"Recruiting new staff takes time because managers must advertise, interview, and train people.","zh":"招聘新職員需要時間，因為經理必須刊登招聘、面試和培訓人手。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the hiring process.","zh":"這個短語描述聘請過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"all the time","meaning":"一直；經常","examples":[{"en":"Managers may have to recruit new staff all the time.","zh":"經理可能必須一直招聘新職員。"},{"en":"All the time means very often or continuously.","zh":"all the time 的意思是非常經常或持續不斷。"},{"en":"If a printer breaks all the time, the office may need a new one.","zh":"如果打印機一直壞，辦公室可能需要一部新的。"},{"en":"Doing the same task all the time can stop managers from focusing on larger problems.","zh":"一直做同一任務可能令經理無法集中處理更大問題。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests repetition that becomes tiring.","zh":"這個短語常暗示令人疲累的重複。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"time-consuming","meaning":"耗時的","examples":[{"en":"Recruiting new staff all the time can be very time-consuming.","zh":"一直招聘新職員可能非常耗時。"},{"en":"Time-consuming means taking a lot of time to do.","zh":"time-consuming 的意思是做起來花很多時間。"},{"en":"Filling in long forms can be time-consuming for busy parents.","zh":"填寫冗長表格對忙碌父母來說可能很耗時。"},{"en":"Time-consuming tasks reduce the time available for planning, training, or improving services.","zh":"耗時任務會減少可用於規劃、培訓或改善服務的時間。"},{"en":"This word describes a task that uses up time.","zh":"這個詞描述會消耗時間的任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cover some duties","meaning":"暫時承擔部分職責","examples":[{"en":"Managers may have to cover some duties while waiting for new staff.","zh":"經理在等待新職員到任時，可能要暫時承擔部分職責。"},{"en":"To cover some duties means to do tasks that are normally done by someone else.","zh":"cover some duties 的意思是做一些通常由其他人負責的任務。"},{"en":"A teacher may cover another teacher’s duties when a colleague is sick.","zh":"當同事生病時，老師可能暫時承擔另一位老師的職責。"},{"en":"Covering duties can keep work going, but it may increase pressure on existing staff.","zh":"暫時承擔職責可以令工作繼續，但可能增加現有職員壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears when a workplace is short-staffed.","zh":"這個短語常出現在人手不足的工作場所中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"wait for new staff to arrive","meaning":"等待新職員到任","examples":[{"en":"Managers may cover duties while waiting for new staff to arrive.","zh":"經理在等待新職員到任時，可能要暫時承擔職責。"},{"en":"To wait for new staff to arrive means to continue working while newly hired employees have not yet started.","zh":"wait for new staff to arrive 的意思是在新聘員工尚未開始工作時繼續運作。"},{"en":"A café may use temporary workers while waiting for new staff to arrive.","zh":"咖啡店可能在等待新職員到任期間使用臨時工。"},{"en":"Waiting for new staff can create pressure because the remaining team must cover the gap.","zh":"等待新職員到任可以製造壓力，因為留下來的團隊必須填補空缺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the period between hiring and actual arrival.","zh":"這個短語描述聘請與實際到任之間的時期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"less immediate problems","meaning":"較不迫切的問題","examples":[{"en":"Managers may not have time to think about less immediate problems.","zh":"經理可能沒有時間思考較不迫切的問題。"},{"en":"Less immediate problems are issues that are important but not urgent right now.","zh":"less immediate problems 是重要但目前不緊急的問題。"},{"en":"A school may focus on broken air conditioning first and leave less immediate problems, such as library design, for later.","zh":"學校可能先處理壞掉的冷氣，把圖書館設計等較不迫切的問題留到之後。"},{"en":"If managers only deal with urgent tasks, less immediate problems may become serious later.","zh":"如果經理只處理緊急任務，較不迫切的問題之後可能變得嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts long-term concerns with urgent ones.","zh":"這個短語把長遠憂慮與緊急問題作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"improve their service","meaning":"改善服務","examples":[{"en":"Managers need time to think about how to improve their service.","zh":"經理需要時間思考如何改善服務。"},{"en":"To improve their service means to make the help or experience they provide better.","zh":"improve their service 的意思是令他們提供的幫助或體驗更好。"},{"en":"A hotel may improve its service by training staff to answer guest questions more clearly.","zh":"酒店可以透過培訓職員更清楚回答住客問題來改善服務。"},{"en":"Better service can lead to happier customers and stronger reviews.","zh":"更好的服務可以帶來更滿意顧客和更好評價。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on making customer experience better.","zh":"這個短語集中於改善顧客體驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"severely affect","meaning":"嚴重影響","examples":[{"en":"When staff leave, it can severely affect their colleagues.","zh":"當職員離職，這可以嚴重影響他們的同事。"},{"en":"To severely affect someone or something means to influence or harm them very seriously.","zh":"severely affect someone or something 的意思是非常嚴重地影響或傷害他們。"},{"en":"A sudden illness can severely affect a student’s exam preparation.","zh":"突然生病可以嚴重影響學生的考試準備。"},{"en":"When several workers leave, the remaining team may face heavier duties and stress.","zh":"當幾名員工離職，留下來的團隊可能面對更重職責和壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “affect”.","zh":"這個短語比 affect 更強。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"colleagues they leave behind","meaning":"他們留下來的同事","examples":[{"en":"Staff turnover affects the colleagues they leave behind.","zh":"員工流失會影響他們留下來的同事。"},{"en":"Colleagues they leave behind are the co-workers who remain after someone leaves the job.","zh":"colleagues they leave behind 是某人離職後仍留下工作的同事。"},{"en":"When a nurse resigns, the colleagues she leaves behind may need to cover extra shifts.","zh":"當護士辭職，她留下來的同事可能需要承擔額外更次。"},{"en":"People often forget that leaving staff can create pressure for those who stay.","zh":"人們常忘記離職員工可能為留下來的人製造壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the remaining team.","zh":"這個短語集中於留下來的團隊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have a negative effect on","meaning":"對……有負面影響","examples":[{"en":"Staff leaving can have a negative effect on remaining staff.","zh":"職員離職可以對留下來的職員有負面影響。"},{"en":"To have a negative effect on someone means to harm or influence them badly.","zh":"have a negative effect on someone 的意思是傷害或不良地影響某人。"},{"en":"Poor lighting can have a negative effect on students’ concentration.","zh":"照明不足可以對學生專注力有負面影響。"},{"en":"A negative effect at work may appear as stress, lower morale, or more mistakes.","zh":"工作中的負面影響可能表現為壓力、士氣下降或更多錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing harmful results.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論有害結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"remaining staff","meaning":"留下來的職員","examples":[{"en":"Remaining staff may start thinking about leaving too.","zh":"留下來的職員也可能開始考慮離職。"},{"en":"Remaining staff are the workers who stay after others have left.","zh":"remaining staff 是其他人離開後仍留在工作崗位的員工。"},{"en":"Remaining staff may have to work harder when several colleagues resign.","zh":"當幾名同事辭職，留下來的職員可能要更努力工作。"},{"en":"If remaining staff feel unsupported, turnover can spread through the whole team.","zh":"如果留下來的職員感到缺乏支援，流失問題可以擴散到整個團隊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the people still in the workplace.","zh":"這個短語描述仍在工作場所的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"think about leaving","meaning":"考慮離職","examples":[{"en":"Remaining staff may also start to think about leaving.","zh":"留下來的職員也可能開始考慮離職。"},{"en":"To think about leaving means to consider resigning or moving away from a job, place, or group.","zh":"think about leaving 的意思是考慮辭職或離開一份工作、地方或群體。"},{"en":"A worker may think about leaving if the workload becomes unfair.","zh":"如果工作量變得不公平，員工可能考慮離職。"},{"en":"When many people think about leaving, managers should ask what is wrong.","zh":"當許多人考慮離職，經理應該詢問出了甚麼問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows consideration before a final decision.","zh":"這個短語顯示在最終決定前的考慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"what can be done to","meaning":"可以做甚麼去……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker asks what can be done to change the situation.","zh":"講者問可以做甚麼去改變這種情況。"},{"en":"What can be done to means what actions are possible in order to solve or improve something.","zh":"what can be done to 的意思是可以採取哪些行動去解決或改善某事。"},{"en":"Teachers may ask what can be done to help students who are falling behind.","zh":"老師可能問可以做甚麼去幫助落後的學生。"},{"en":"This phrase turns attention from the problem to possible solutions.","zh":"這個短語把注意力從問題轉向可能解決方案。"},{"en":"It is useful in meetings, reports, and discussions.","zh":"它適合用於會議、報告和討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"change this situation","meaning":"改變這種情況","examples":[{"en":"Managers need to change the situation of high staff turnover.","zh":"經理需要改變員工流失率高的情況。"},{"en":"To change this situation means to improve or alter the current problem.","zh":"change this situation 的意思是改善或改變目前的問題。"},{"en":"If students are often late, the school must change the situation with clearer transport arrangements.","zh":"如果學生經常遲到，學校必須透過更清晰交通安排改變這種情況。"},{"en":"Changing a situation usually requires understanding its causes first.","zh":"要改變情況，通常需要先理解其原因。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on moving from a bad condition to a better one.","zh":"這個短語集中於從不好情況轉向較好情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make basic errors","meaning":"犯基本錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Managers should stop making basic errors.","zh":"經理應停止犯基本錯誤。"},{"en":"To make basic errors means to make simple mistakes that should usually be avoidable.","zh":"make basic errors 的意思是犯通常應可避免的簡單錯誤。"},{"en":"A restaurant makes basic errors if staff forget orders or ignore customers.","zh":"如果員工忘記訂單或忽視顧客，餐廳就是犯基本錯誤。"},{"en":"Basic errors can damage trust because people expect simple things to be done correctly.","zh":"基本錯誤可以破壞信任，因為人們期望簡單事情被正確完成。"},{"en":"This phrase is often critical because the mistakes seem unnecessary.","zh":"這個短語常帶批評意味，因為錯誤看似不必要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"leave someone feeling","meaning":"令某人感到……","examples":[{"en":"Some management errors leave staff feeling upset and resentful.","zh":"有些管理錯誤令職員感到不滿和怨憤。"},{"en":"To leave someone feeling a certain way means to make them feel that way after an event.","zh":"leave someone feeling a certain way 的意思是某事發生後令某人有某種感受。"},{"en":"Being ignored in a meeting can leave employees feeling unimportant.","zh":"在會議中被忽視可以令員工感到不重要。"},{"en":"Small unfair decisions may leave staff feeling angry even if managers did not intend harm.","zh":"小小的不公平決定可能令職員感到憤怒，即使經理無意傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an action with an emotional result.","zh":"這個短語把行動與情緒結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"upset and resentful","meaning":"不滿和怨憤","examples":[{"en":"Unfair decisions can make staff feel upset and resentful.","zh":"不公平決定可以令職員感到不滿和怨憤。"},{"en":"Upset and resentful means unhappy, hurt, and quietly angry because something feels unfair.","zh":"upset and resentful 的意思是因感到不公平而不開心、受傷並暗自憤怒。"},{"en":"A student may feel upset and resentful if the same classmates always get special treatment.","zh":"如果同一批同學總是得到特別待遇，學生可能感到不滿和怨憤。"},{"en":"Resentful staff may stop helping willingly because they feel badly treated.","zh":"怨憤的職員可能不再願意主動幫忙，因為他們覺得受到差劣對待。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional damage caused by unfairness.","zh":"這個短語描述不公平造成的情緒傷害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"organise shifts","meaning":"安排更次","examples":[{"en":"Managers need to be fair when organising shifts.","zh":"經理安排更次時需要公平。"},{"en":"To organise shifts means to arrange who works at different times of the day or week.","zh":"organise shifts 的意思是安排誰在一天或一星期中的不同時間工作。"},{"en":"A café manager organises shifts so enough staff are present during busy lunch hours.","zh":"咖啡店經理安排更次，確保繁忙午餐時段有足夠職員。"},{"en":"Poor shift organisation can make staff tired, angry, or unable to plan family life.","zh":"更次安排不佳可以令員工疲倦、憤怒或無法規劃家庭生活。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in workplaces with changing work hours.","zh":"這個短語常見於工作時間變動的職場。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"give someone preferential treatment","meaning":"給予某人優待","examples":[{"en":"Managers should not give certain staff preferential treatment.","zh":"經理不應給予某些職員優待。"},{"en":"To give someone preferential treatment means to treat them better than others without a fair reason.","zh":"give someone preferential treatment 的意思是在沒有公平理由下，對某人比其他人更好。"},{"en":"A teacher gives preferential treatment if one student always gets extra chances while others do not.","zh":"如果一名學生總是得到額外機會而其他人沒有，老師就是給予優待。"},{"en":"Preferential treatment creates resentment because people feel the rules are not equal.","zh":"優待會造成怨憤，因為人們覺得規則不平等。"},{"en":"This phrase usually has a negative meaning.","zh":"這個短語通常帶負面意思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"preferential treatment","meaning":"優待","examples":[{"en":"Preferential treatment can make other staff resentful.","zh":"優待可以令其他職員怨憤。"},{"en":"Preferential treatment is unfairly better treatment given to one person or group.","zh":"preferential treatment 是給予某人或某群體的不公平較好待遇。"},{"en":"Staff may complain if weekend shifts are avoided only by the manager’s favourite workers.","zh":"如果只有經理喜歡的員工不用值週末班，職員可能會投訴。"},{"en":"Preferential treatment damages teamwork because people stop trusting management.","zh":"優待會破壞團隊合作，因為人們不再信任管理層。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing fairness.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論公平。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be given some choice about","meaning":"獲給予對……的一些選擇","examples":[{"en":"All staff should be given some choice about when they work.","zh":"所有職員都應獲給予對工作時間的一些選擇。"},{"en":"To be given some choice about something means to have at least a limited say in the decision.","zh":"be given some choice about something 的意思是在決定中至少有有限發言權。"},{"en":"Students may be given some choice about which book to read for a project.","zh":"學生可能獲給予對項目閱讀書籍的一些選擇。"},{"en":"Giving staff some choice over shifts can improve morale because they feel respected.","zh":"讓職員對更次有一些選擇，可以改善士氣，因為他們感到被尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests flexibility, not complete freedom.","zh":"這個短語表示彈性，而不是完全自由。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"evening and weekend shifts","meaning":"晚班和週末班","examples":[{"en":"Everyone should have to work some evening and weekend shifts.","zh":"每個人都應該要做一些晚班和週末班。"},{"en":"Evening and weekend shifts are work periods scheduled at night or on Saturdays and Sundays.","zh":"evening and weekend shifts 是安排在晚上或星期六、星期日的工作時段。"},{"en":"Hotel staff often work evening and weekend shifts because guests need service every day.","zh":"酒店職員常要做晚班和週末班，因為住客每天都需要服務。"},{"en":"If evening and weekend shifts are shared fairly, staff are less likely to feel resentful.","zh":"如果晚班和週末班公平分配，職員較不容易感到怨憤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes less convenient working hours.","zh":"這個短語描述較不方便的工作時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"treat staff fairly","meaning":"公平對待職員","examples":[{"en":"If managers treat staff fairly, staff are more likely to help.","zh":"如果經理公平對待職員，職員更有可能幫忙。"},{"en":"To treat staff fairly means to apply rules and opportunities equally and respectfully.","zh":"treat staff fairly 的意思是平等而尊重地應用規則和機會。"},{"en":"A manager treats staff fairly by sharing unpopular shifts instead of giving them to the same people.","zh":"經理透過分配不受歡迎更次，而不是總給同一批人，來公平對待職員。"},{"en":"Fair treatment builds trust because employees feel decisions are not based on favouritism.","zh":"公平對待能建立信任，因為員工覺得決定不是基於偏袒。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to good management.","zh":"這個短語是良好管理的核心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be more likely to","meaning":"更有可能……","examples":[{"en":"Staff are more likely to help if they are treated fairly.","zh":"如果職員受到公平對待，他們更有可能幫忙。"},{"en":"Be more likely to means have a higher chance of doing something or having something happen.","zh":"be more likely to 的意思是做某事或某事發生的機會較高。"},{"en":"Students are more likely to ask questions if the teacher is patient.","zh":"如果老師有耐性，學生更有可能提問。"},{"en":"People are more likely to stay in a job when they feel respected and supported.","zh":"當人們感到被尊重和支持，他們更有可能留在一份工作中。"},{"en":"This phrase compares probability.","zh":"這個短語比較可能性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"step in and help","meaning":"主動介入幫忙","examples":[{"en":"Staff may step in and help when extra staff are needed.","zh":"當需要額外人手時，職員可能主動介入幫忙。"},{"en":"To step in and help means to offer help when there is a problem or shortage.","zh":"step in and help 的意思是在有問題或人手不足時提供幫助。"},{"en":"A colleague may step in and help if a team member is suddenly sick.","zh":"如果團隊成員突然生病，同事可能主動介入幫忙。"},{"en":"People are more willing to step in when they feel the workplace treats them fairly.","zh":"當人們覺得工作場所公平對待他們，他們更願意主動介入。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests practical support at the right moment.","zh":"這個短語表示在適當時候提供實際支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"extra staff are needed","meaning":"需要額外人手","examples":[{"en":"Staff may help when extra staff are needed.","zh":"當需要額外人手時，職員可能會幫忙。"},{"en":"Extra staff are needed means more workers are required than usual.","zh":"extra staff are needed 的意思是需要比平常更多員工。"},{"en":"Extra staff are needed in restaurants during public holidays and busy weekends.","zh":"餐廳在公眾假期和繁忙週末需要額外人手。"},{"en":"If extra staff are not available, customers may wait longer and service may suffer.","zh":"如果沒有額外人手，顧客可能等更久，服務也可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a temporary or practical staffing need.","zh":"這個短語描述臨時或實際的人手需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"keep staff happy","meaning":"令職員保持滿意","examples":[{"en":"Keeping staff happy has tangible benefits for the business.","zh":"令職員保持滿意對企業有實際好處。"},{"en":"To keep staff happy means to create conditions that make employees satisfied and motivated.","zh":"keep staff happy 的意思是創造令員工滿意和有動力的條件。"},{"en":"Fair schedules, clear training, and respectful managers can keep staff happy.","zh":"公平更表、清晰培訓和尊重人的經理可以令職員保持滿意。"},{"en":"Happy staff are more likely to serve customers well and stay longer.","zh":"滿意的職員更可能提供好服務並留任更久。"},{"en":"This phrase links employee satisfaction with business results.","zh":"這個短語把員工滿意度與企業成果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tangible benefits","meaning":"實際好處","examples":[{"en":"Happy staff bring tangible benefits for the business.","zh":"滿意的職員為企業帶來實際好處。"},{"en":"Tangible benefits are clear, real, and measurable advantages.","zh":"tangible benefits 是清楚、真實並可量度的好處。"},{"en":"Better training can bring tangible benefits such as fewer mistakes and faster service.","zh":"更好培訓可以帶來實際好處，例如錯誤減少和服務更快。"},{"en":"Managers value tangible benefits because they can see the practical results.","zh":"經理重視實際好處，因為他們能看見實際結果。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real outcomes with vague promises.","zh":"這個短語把真實成果與模糊承諾作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"for the business","meaning":"對企業而言","examples":[{"en":"Staff satisfaction brings benefits for the business.","zh":"職員滿意度對企業而言帶來好處。"},{"en":"For the business means from the company’s point of view or in terms of its success.","zh":"for the business 的意思是從公司的角度或就其成功而言。"},{"en":"Training may cost money at first, but it can be good for the business in the long run.","zh":"培訓初期可能要花錢，但長遠而言對企業有好處。"},{"en":"A policy is useful for the business when it improves service, income, or staff stability.","zh":"當政策改善服務、收入或員工穩定性，它對企業而言就是有用的。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an action with company interests.","zh":"這個短語把行動與公司利益連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take something as an example","meaning":"以……為例","examples":[{"en":"The speaker takes the Dunwich Hotel as an example.","zh":"講者以 Dunwich Hotel 為例。"},{"en":"To take something as an example means to use it to show or explain a wider point.","zh":"take something as an example 的意思是使用某事來展示或解釋更廣泛的觀點。"},{"en":"We can take the school library as an example of how small changes improve learning.","zh":"我們可以以學校圖書館為例，說明小改變如何改善學習。"},{"en":"Examples help listeners understand abstract ideas through real cases.","zh":"例子幫助聽眾透過真實案例理解抽象想法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces supporting evidence.","zh":"這個短語引出支持證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"experience a problem with","meaning":"遇到……的問題","examples":[{"en":"The Dunwich Hotel had been experiencing a problem with staff complaints.","zh":"Dunwich Hotel 一直遇到職員投訴的問題。"},{"en":"To experience a problem with something means to have difficulty related to that thing.","zh":"experience a problem with something 的意思是遇到與某事有關的困難。"},{"en":"A shop may experience a problem with late deliveries during bad weather.","zh":"商店可能在惡劣天氣期間遇到送貨延誤的問題。"},{"en":"When a company experiences a problem with complaints, it should ask what customers or staff are unhappy about.","zh":"當公司遇到投訴問題，它應詢問顧客或職員不滿甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an organisation with a specific difficulty.","zh":"這個短語把機構與特定困難連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"staff complaints","meaning":"職員投訴","examples":[{"en":"The Dunwich Hotel had a problem with staff complaints.","zh":"Dunwich Hotel 有職員投訴的問題。"},{"en":"Staff complaints are formal or informal expressions of dissatisfaction from employees.","zh":"staff complaints 是員工正式或非正式表達不滿。"},{"en":"Staff complaints may be about pay, shifts, training, safety, or unfair treatment.","zh":"職員投訴可能關於薪酬、更次、培訓、安全或不公平待遇。"},{"en":"Ignoring staff complaints can make workers feel unheard and more likely to leave.","zh":"忽視職員投訴可以令員工覺得不被聆聽，並更可能離職。"},{"en":"This phrase describes employee dissatisfaction.","zh":"這個短語描述員工不滿。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in order to deal with","meaning":"為了處理……","examples":[{"en":"The hotel invested in training in order to deal with staff complaints.","zh":"酒店投資於培訓，為了處理職員投訴。"},{"en":"In order to deal with something means for the purpose of managing or solving that problem.","zh":"in order to deal with something 的意思是為了管理或解決某個問題。"},{"en":"A school may hold extra lessons in order to deal with weak exam results.","zh":"學校可能舉辦額外課堂，為了處理考試成績薄弱的問題。"},{"en":"Dealing with a problem properly often requires action, not just discussion.","zh":"妥善處理問題通常需要行動，而不只是討論。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links an action to its purpose.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接行動與目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"invest in staff training","meaning":"投資於職員培訓","examples":[{"en":"The Dunwich Hotel invested in staff training.","zh":"Dunwich Hotel 投資於職員培訓。"},{"en":"To invest in staff training means to spend money, time, or effort teaching employees useful skills.","zh":"invest in staff training 的意思是花金錢、時間或精力教授員工有用技能。"},{"en":"A restaurant may invest in staff training so waiters can handle complaints calmly.","zh":"餐廳可能投資於職員培訓，讓侍應能冷靜處理投訴。"},{"en":"Training can reduce mistakes and make employees feel more confident.","zh":"培訓可以減少錯誤，並令員工更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase treats training as a long-term business investment.","zh":"這個短語把培訓視為長遠商業投資。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"improve staff conditions","meaning":"改善職員待遇；改善工作條件","examples":[{"en":"The hotel improved staff conditions to reduce complaints.","zh":"酒店改善職員待遇，以減少投訴。"},{"en":"To improve staff conditions means to make employees’ working lives better.","zh":"improve staff conditions 的意思是令員工的工作生活更好。"},{"en":"A company can improve staff conditions by offering fair shifts, safer equipment, and clearer breaks.","zh":"公司可以透過提供公平更次、更安全設備和更清晰休息時間來改善工作條件。"},{"en":"Better staff conditions can reduce complaints because workers feel respected.","zh":"更好的工作條件可以減少投訴，因為員工感到被尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the quality of the working environment.","zh":"這個短語集中於工作環境質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not only did…, but…","meaning":"不但……而且……","examples":[{"en":"Not only did complaints fall, but customer spending also increased.","zh":"投訴不但下降，而且顧客消費也增加。"},{"en":"Not only did…, but… is used to emphasise two related results, especially when both are important.","zh":"not only did…, but… 用來強調兩個相關結果，尤其當兩者都重要時。"},{"en":"Not only did the class finish the project, but they also won a prize.","zh":"這班學生不但完成項目，而且還贏得獎項。"},{"en":"This structure makes the second result feel like an extra strong benefit.","zh":"這個結構令第二個結果感覺像額外而有力的好處。"},{"en":"It is a formal and emphatic sentence pattern.","zh":"這是正式而強調性的句式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"level of complaints","meaning":"投訴水平","examples":[{"en":"The level of complaints fell after the hotel improved conditions.","zh":"酒店改善工作條件後，投訴水平下降。"},{"en":"The level of complaints means the amount or number of complaints.","zh":"level of complaints 的意思是投訴的數量或程度。"},{"en":"A school may track the level of complaints from parents after changing its lunch menu.","zh":"學校改變午餐餐單後，可能追蹤家長投訴水平。"},{"en":"If the level of complaints falls, it may show that the problem has improved.","zh":"如果投訴水平下降，可能顯示問題已有改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when measuring dissatisfaction.","zh":"這個短語適合用於量度不滿程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"notice a significant increase in","meaning":"注意到……顯著增加","examples":[{"en":"The hotel noticed a significant increase in customer spending.","zh":"酒店注意到顧客消費顯著增加。"},{"en":"To notice a significant increase in something means to observe a clear and important rise.","zh":"notice a significant increase in something 的意思是觀察到某事明顯而重要地上升。"},{"en":"A library may notice a significant increase in visitors after opening on Sundays.","zh":"圖書館星期日開放後，可能注意到訪客人數顯著增加。"},{"en":"Significant increases matter because they suggest a real change, not a tiny difference.","zh":"顯著增加很重要，因為它暗示真正改變，而不是微小差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reports and business analysis.","zh":"這個短語常見於報告和商業分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the amount each customer spent","meaning":"每位顧客的消費金額","examples":[{"en":"The amount each customer spent increased during their stay.","zh":"每位顧客在入住期間的消費金額增加。"},{"en":"The amount each customer spent means how much money each customer paid or used.","zh":"the amount each customer spent 的意思是每位顧客支付或花費了多少錢。"},{"en":"A café may track the amount each customer spends to understand buying habits.","zh":"咖啡店可能追蹤每位顧客的消費金額，以理解購買習慣。"},{"en":"If each customer spends more, total income can rise even without more visitors.","zh":"如果每位顧客消費更多，即使訪客沒有增加，總收入也可以上升。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on spending per person.","zh":"這個短語集中於每人消費。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"during their stay","meaning":"在入住期間","examples":[{"en":"Customers spent more during their stay.","zh":"顧客在入住期間消費更多。"},{"en":"During their stay means while they were staying at the hotel or accommodation.","zh":"during their stay 的意思是在他們入住酒店或住宿期間。"},{"en":"Guests can use the gym and pool during their stay.","zh":"住客在入住期間可以使用健身室和泳池。"},{"en":"Good service during a stay can encourage guests to spend more and return later.","zh":"入住期間的良好服務可以鼓勵住客消費更多並日後再來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the period when guests are present.","zh":"這個短語指住客在場的那段時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"introduce a customer loyalty scheme","meaning":"推出顧客忠誠計劃","examples":[{"en":"The hotel introduced a customer loyalty scheme.","zh":"酒店推出顧客忠誠計劃。"},{"en":"To introduce a customer loyalty scheme means to start a programme that rewards customers for returning or spending more.","zh":"introduce a customer loyalty scheme 的意思是開始一項獎勵顧客再次光顧或消費更多的計劃。"},{"en":"A café may introduce a loyalty card that gives customers a free drink after ten purchases.","zh":"咖啡店可能推出一張印花卡，顧客買十次後可獲一杯免費飲品。"},{"en":"Loyalty schemes encourage repeat business because customers feel rewarded.","zh":"忠誠計劃鼓勵顧客再次光顧，因為顧客感到受到獎勵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a business strategy for keeping customers.","zh":"這個短語描述挽留顧客的商業策略。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"customer loyalty scheme","meaning":"顧客忠誠計劃","examples":[{"en":"The customer loyalty scheme is going really well.","zh":"顧客忠誠計劃進展十分順利。"},{"en":"A customer loyalty scheme is a programme that rewards customers for repeated purchases or visits.","zh":"customer loyalty scheme 是獎勵顧客重複購買或光顧的計劃。"},{"en":"Supermarkets often use loyalty schemes to offer points, discounts, or special offers.","zh":"超級市場常使用忠誠計劃提供積分、折扣或特別優惠。"},{"en":"A good loyalty scheme can make customers feel valued and encourage them to return.","zh":"好的忠誠計劃可以令顧客感到被重視，並鼓勵他們再次光顧。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in marketing and retail.","zh":"這個短語常見於市場營銷和零售。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go really well","meaning":"進展十分順利","examples":[{"en":"The customer loyalty scheme is going really well.","zh":"顧客忠誠計劃進展十分順利。"},{"en":"To go really well means to progress successfully or produce good results.","zh":"go really well 的意思是進展成功或產生良好結果。"},{"en":"The school concert went really well because students were prepared and confident.","zh":"學校音樂會進展十分順利，因為學生準備充足又有信心。"},{"en":"When a plan goes well, people usually feel encouraged to continue it.","zh":"當計劃進展順利，人們通常會受到鼓勵而繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a positive judgement about progress.","zh":"這個短語對進展作出正面評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reduce staff turnover","meaning":"減低員工流失率","examples":[{"en":"The speaker discusses ways to reduce staff turnover.","zh":"講者討論減低員工流失率的方法。"},{"en":"To reduce staff turnover means to make fewer employees leave the organisation.","zh":"reduce staff turnover 的意思是令較少員工離開機構。"},{"en":"Better training and fairer schedules can reduce staff turnover in hotels.","zh":"更好培訓和更公平更表可以減低酒店員工流失率。"},{"en":"Reducing turnover saves money because fewer new workers need to be recruited and trained.","zh":"減低流失率可以節省金錢，因為需要招聘和培訓的新員工較少。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on keeping employees.","zh":"這個短語集中於留住員工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"give examples of","meaning":"舉出……的例子","examples":[{"en":"The speaker gives examples of hotels where she has done training.","zh":"講者舉出她曾進行培訓的酒店例子。"},{"en":"To give examples of something means to provide specific cases that show or explain it.","zh":"give examples of something 的意思是提供具體案例來展示或解釋某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may give examples of strong topic sentences before students write essays.","zh":"老師可能在學生寫文章前舉出有力主題句的例子。"},{"en":"Examples make ideas easier to understand because they show how something works in reality.","zh":"例子令想法更容易理解，因為它們顯示某事在現實中如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in teaching, reports, and presentations.","zh":"這個短語適合用於教學、報告和簡報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"do some training","meaning":"進行培訓","examples":[{"en":"The speaker has done some training at several hotels recently.","zh":"講者最近在幾間酒店進行培訓。"},{"en":"To do some training means to give or receive instruction to improve skills.","zh":"do some training 的意思是提供或接受指導，以改善技能。"},{"en":"New receptionists may do some training before they speak to guests alone.","zh":"新接待員可能在獨自接待住客前進行一些培訓。"},{"en":"Training helps workers avoid mistakes and feel more confident in their roles.","zh":"培訓幫助員工避免錯誤，並在崗位上更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to either teaching others or learning yourself.","zh":"這個短語可以指教導別人，也可以指自己學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"receive feedback","meaning":"收到意見","examples":[{"en":"The Sun Club received feedback from staff.","zh":"The Sun Club 收到職員的意見。"},{"en":"To receive feedback means to get comments, opinions, or suggestions about how something is working.","zh":"receive feedback 的意思是收到關於某事運作情況的評論、意見或建議。"},{"en":"Students receive feedback from teachers so they know how to improve their writing.","zh":"學生收到老師意見，才知道如何改善寫作。"},{"en":"Feedback from staff can show managers what is really happening at work.","zh":"職員意見可以向經理顯示工作中真實發生的事。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in learning and management.","zh":"這個短語在學習和管理中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"value someone’s opinions","meaning":"重視某人的意見","examples":[{"en":"Staff thought managers did not value their opinions.","zh":"職員認為經理不重視他們的意見。"},{"en":"To value someone’s opinions means to respect their ideas and take them seriously.","zh":"value someone’s opinions 的意思是尊重某人的想法並認真看待。"},{"en":"A good teacher values students’ opinions during class discussions.","zh":"好老師在課堂討論中重視學生的意見。"},{"en":"When workers feel their opinions are valued, they are more likely to speak honestly.","zh":"當員工覺得自己的意見受到重視，他們更可能誠實發言。"},{"en":"This phrase connects respect with listening.","zh":"這個短語把尊重與聆聽連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be made to feel","meaning":"被令覺得","examples":[{"en":"Staff were not made to feel like partners.","zh":"職員沒有被令覺得自己像合作夥伴。"},{"en":"To be made to feel a certain way means to be treated in a way that creates that feeling.","zh":"be made to feel 某種感覺，意思是因受到某種對待而產生該感覺。"},{"en":"New students should be made to feel welcome on their first day.","zh":"新學生第一天應被令覺得受歡迎。"},{"en":"If employees are made to feel ignored, they may stop offering ideas.","zh":"如果員工被令覺得遭忽視，他們可能停止提出想法。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how treatment creates emotion.","zh":"這個短語集中於待遇如何製造情緒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"contribute to","meaning":"對……作出貢獻","examples":[{"en":"Staff should feel that they are contributing to business success.","zh":"職員應感到自己正對企業成功作出貢獻。"},{"en":"To contribute to something means to help cause it or support it.","zh":"contribute to something 的意思是幫助促成或支持某事。"},{"en":"Good sleep contributes to better concentration in class.","zh":"良好睡眠對課堂專注力更好作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Employees feel more motivated when they can see how their work contributes to a larger goal.","zh":"當員工看見自己的工作如何對更大目標作出貢獻，他們會更有動力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows positive involvement in a result.","zh":"這個短語顯示對結果的正面參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the success of the business","meaning":"企業的成功","examples":[{"en":"Staff contribute to the success of the business as a whole.","zh":"職員對企業整體成功作出貢獻。"},{"en":"The success of the business means the company is doing well financially, operationally, and in customer satisfaction.","zh":"the success of the business 指公司在財務、營運和顧客滿意度方面表現良好。"},{"en":"Good teamwork can improve the success of the business by making service more reliable.","zh":"良好團隊合作可以透過令服務更可靠來提升企業成功。"},{"en":"When staff understand their role in business success, they may feel more valued.","zh":"當職員明白自己在企業成功中的角色，他們可能感到更受重視。"},{"en":"This phrase connects employees’ work with company performance.","zh":"這個短語把員工工作與公司表現連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as a whole","meaning":"整體而言","examples":[{"en":"Staff contribute to the success of the business as a whole.","zh":"職員對企業整體而言的成功作出貢獻。"},{"en":"As a whole means considering all parts together, not only one part.","zh":"as a whole 的意思是把所有部分一起考慮，而不是只看其中一部分。"},{"en":"The class as a whole improved, although some students still needed help.","zh":"整體而言，這班有所進步，雖然有些學生仍需要幫助。"},{"en":"Looking at a business as a whole helps managers see how departments affect one another.","zh":"整體看待企業有助經理看見部門之間如何互相影響。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a broad overall view.","zh":"這個短語提供廣闊整體角度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"junior staff","meaning":"初級職員","examples":[{"en":"Junior staff are now invited to meetings.","zh":"初級職員現在獲邀參加會議。"},{"en":"Junior staff are employees in lower-level or less senior positions.","zh":"junior staff 是職級較低或資歷較淺的員工。"},{"en":"Junior staff may have less authority, but they often know daily problems very well.","zh":"初級職員可能權力較少，但他們常非常了解日常問題。"},{"en":"Inviting junior staff to meetings can help managers hear practical suggestions.","zh":"邀請初級職員參加會議，可以幫助經理聽到實用建議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rank or experience level in a workplace.","zh":"這個短語描述工作場所中的職級或經驗程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at all levels","meaning":"各個級別","examples":[{"en":"Junior staff at all levels are invited to meetings.","zh":"各個級別的初級職員都獲邀參加會議。"},{"en":"At all levels means across every rank, stage, or position in an organisation.","zh":"at all levels 的意思是涵蓋組織中的每個職級、階段或位置。"},{"en":"A school improvement plan should involve staff at all levels, from assistants to senior teachers.","zh":"學校改善計劃應讓各個級別的職員參與，從助理到高級老師。"},{"en":"Involving people at all levels helps leaders understand problems from different viewpoints.","zh":"讓各級人士參與有助領袖從不同角度理解問題。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses inclusion across hierarchy.","zh":"這個短語強調跨越階層的共融。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be regularly invited to","meaning":"定期獲邀參加……","examples":[{"en":"Junior staff are regularly invited to meetings.","zh":"初級職員定期獲邀參加會議。"},{"en":"To be regularly invited to something means to be asked to attend it often or according to a routine.","zh":"be regularly invited to something 的意思是經常或按固定安排獲邀出席某活動。"},{"en":"Parents are regularly invited to school workshops on reading and homework.","zh":"家長定期獲邀參加關於閱讀和功課的學校工作坊。"},{"en":"Regular invitations show people that their participation is expected and valued.","zh":"定期邀請顯示人們的參與是被期待和重視的。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repeated inclusion, not a one-off event.","zh":"這個短語表示反覆被包括，而不是一次性事件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"their ideas are welcomed","meaning":"他們的想法受到歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Staff attend meetings where their ideas are welcomed.","zh":"職員參加他們的想法受到歡迎的會議。"},{"en":"Their ideas are welcomed means people are encouraged to share suggestions and are listened to respectfully.","zh":"their ideas are welcomed 的意思是人們被鼓勵分享建議，並受到尊重地聆聽。"},{"en":"Students speak more freely in classes where their ideas are welcomed.","zh":"在想法受到歡迎的課堂中，學生會更自由發言。"},{"en":"When staff ideas are welcomed, employees may feel like partners rather than tools.","zh":"當職員想法受到歡迎，員工可能感到自己像合作夥伴，而不是工具。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an open and respectful environment.","zh":"這個短語描述開放而尊重的環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"recognise the need to","meaning":"意識到有需要……","examples":[{"en":"The Portland recognised the need to invest in staff retention.","zh":"The Portland 意識到有需要投資於挽留職員。"},{"en":"To recognise the need to do something means to understand that an action is necessary.","zh":"recognise the need to do something 的意思是明白某行動是必要的。"},{"en":"A school may recognise the need to support students’ mental health after survey results.","zh":"學校可能在調查結果後意識到有需要支援學生精神健康。"},{"en":"Recognising a need is the first step before taking meaningful action.","zh":"意識到需要是採取有意義行動前的第一步。"},{"en":"This phrase shows awareness and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語顯示覺察和責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"invest in staff retention","meaning":"投資於挽留職員","examples":[{"en":"The Portland invested in staff retention.","zh":"The Portland 投資於挽留職員。"},{"en":"To invest in staff retention means to spend resources on keeping employees in the organisation.","zh":"invest in staff retention 的意思是投入資源，讓員工留在機構。"},{"en":"A hotel may invest in staff retention by offering training, fair pay, and career paths.","zh":"酒店可能透過提供培訓、公平薪酬和職業發展路徑來投資於挽留職員。"},{"en":"Investing in retention can save money because replacing staff is expensive.","zh":"投資於員工留任可以節省金錢，因為替換員工成本高。"},{"en":"This phrase treats keeping workers as a business priority.","zh":"這個短語把留住員工視為商業優先事項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"staff retention","meaning":"挽留職員；員工留任","examples":[{"en":"Staff retention became a priority for The Portland.","zh":"挽留職員成為 The Portland 的優先事項。"},{"en":"Staff retention means keeping employees in a company instead of losing them to resignation or other jobs.","zh":"staff retention 的意思是讓員工留在公司，而不是因辭職或其他工作而流失。"},{"en":"Good managers improve staff retention by making workers feel respected and supported.","zh":"好經理透過令員工感到被尊重和支持來改善員工留任。"},{"en":"Strong staff retention helps businesses keep experience, trust, and service quality.","zh":"強勁員工留任有助企業保留經驗、信任和服務質素。"},{"en":"This phrase is the opposite of staff turnover.","zh":"這個短語是 staff turnover 的相反。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"first step","meaning":"第一步","examples":[{"en":"Their first step was to introduce a talent-recognition scheme.","zh":"他們的第一步是推出人才識別計劃。"},{"en":"A first step is the first action taken in a plan or process.","zh":"first step 是計劃或過程中採取的第一個行動。"},{"en":"The first step in improving fitness may be walking for ten minutes a day.","zh":"改善體能的第一步可能是每天步行十分鐘。"},{"en":"A clear first step makes a big problem feel more manageable.","zh":"清晰第一步可以令大問題感覺較容易處理。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the beginning of action.","zh":"這個短語標示行動的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"introduce a scheme for","meaning":"推出一項……計劃","examples":[{"en":"The Portland introduced a scheme for recognising talent.","zh":"The Portland 推出一項識別人才的計劃。"},{"en":"To introduce a scheme for something means to start an organised plan for that purpose.","zh":"introduce a scheme for something 的意思是為某目的開始一項有組織的計劃。"},{"en":"A school may introduce a scheme for helping new students settle in.","zh":"學校可能推出一項幫助新學生適應的計劃。"},{"en":"A clear scheme gives people a system instead of leaving everything to chance.","zh":"清晰計劃給人一個制度，而不是讓一切靠運氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the launch of a planned programme.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃項目的推出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"recognising talent","meaning":"識別人才","examples":[{"en":"The scheme focuses on recognising talent among employees.","zh":"這項計劃集中於識別員工之中的人才。"},{"en":"Recognising talent means noticing and valuing people’s ability, promise, or strong performance.","zh":"recognising talent 的意思是注意並重視人的能力、潛質或優秀表現。"},{"en":"A teacher recognises talent when she encourages a quiet student who writes excellent stories.","zh":"當老師鼓勵一位寫作出色的安靜學生，就是在識別人才。"},{"en":"Recognising talent can motivate people because they feel their effort has been noticed.","zh":"識別人才可以激勵人，因為他們感到自己的努力被看見。"},{"en":"This phrase is about identifying potential, not only rewarding senior staff.","zh":"這個短語關乎識別潛質，而不只是獎勵高級員工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"amongst their employees","meaning":"在員工之中","examples":[{"en":"The hotel wanted to recognise talent amongst its employees.","zh":"酒店想在員工之中識別人才。"},{"en":"Amongst their employees means within the group of people who work for them.","zh":"amongst their employees 的意思是在為他們工作的員工群體之內。"},{"en":"A company may search for future leaders amongst its employees before hiring outsiders.","zh":"公司可能先在員工之中尋找未來領袖，再聘請外來人選。"},{"en":"Looking for talent among existing staff can show workers that promotion is possible.","zh":"在現有職員中尋找人才，可以向員工顯示晉升是可能的。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on people already inside the organisation.","zh":"這個短語集中於已在組織內的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"management potential","meaning":"管理潛質","examples":[{"en":"The hotel identifies individuals with management potential.","zh":"酒店識別具管理潛質的個人。"},{"en":"Management potential means the ability or promise to become a good manager in the future.","zh":"management potential 是將來成為好經理的能力或潛力。"},{"en":"A receptionist who solves problems calmly may show management potential.","zh":"一位冷靜解決問題的接待員可能展現管理潛質。"},{"en":"Training people with management potential helps a company build future leaders.","zh":"培訓具管理潛質的人，有助公司培養未來領袖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes future ability, not current job title.","zh":"這個短語描述未來能力，而不是目前職銜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"encourage them to stay","meaning":"鼓勵他們留下","examples":[{"en":"Training may encourage talented staff to stay with the business.","zh":"培訓可能鼓勵有才能的職員留在企業。"},{"en":"To encourage them to stay means to make people more willing to remain instead of leaving.","zh":"encourage them to stay 的意思是令他們更願意留下，而不是離開。"},{"en":"Career development can encourage young teachers to stay in a school.","zh":"職業發展可以鼓勵年輕老師留在學校。"},{"en":"People stay more readily when they see a future for themselves.","zh":"當人們看見自己的未來，他們更願意留下。"},{"en":"This phrase connects support with retention.","zh":"這個短語把支援與挽留連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stay with the business","meaning":"留在企業工作","examples":[{"en":"The hotel wants talented employees to stay with the business.","zh":"酒店希望有才能的員工留在企業工作。"},{"en":"To stay with the business means to continue working for the company.","zh":"stay with the business 的意思是繼續為公司工作。"},{"en":"Staff are more likely to stay with the business if they see promotion opportunities.","zh":"如果員工看見晉升機會，他們更可能留在企業工作。"},{"en":"Keeping talented people helps a business preserve knowledge and service quality.","zh":"留住有才能的人幫助企業保留知識和服務質素。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on employee loyalty and retention.","zh":"這個短語集中於員工忠誠和留任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"high achievers","meaning":"高績效員工","examples":[{"en":"Bluewater recognised 50 high achievers across the company.","zh":"Bluewater 表揚了公司內50名高績效員工。"},{"en":"High achievers are people who perform very well or reach strong results.","zh":"high achievers 是表現非常好或取得優秀成果的人。"},{"en":"Schools may invite high achievers to mentor younger students.","zh":"學校可能邀請高成就學生指導年幼學生。"},{"en":"Recognising high achievers can motivate others, but managers should also support ordinary staff.","zh":"表揚高績效員工可以激勵其他人，但經理也應支援普通職員。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong performers.","zh":"這個短語描述表現突出的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"from across the company","meaning":"來自整間公司","examples":[{"en":"Bluewater selected high achievers from across the company.","zh":"Bluewater 從整間公司選出高績效員工。"},{"en":"From across the company means from different departments, branches, or levels within the whole organisation.","zh":"from across the company 的意思是來自整個組織中不同部門、分店或級別。"},{"en":"A project team may include workers from across the company, not just one office.","zh":"項目團隊可能包括來自整間公司的員工，而不只是一個辦公室。"},{"en":"Selecting people from across the company can make recognition feel broader and fairer.","zh":"從整間公司選人可以令表揚感覺更廣泛和公平。"},{"en":"This phrase shows organisation-wide involvement.","zh":"這個短語顯示整個組織都有參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"huge hotel chain","meaning":"大型酒店連鎖集團","examples":[{"en":"Bluewater is a huge hotel chain.","zh":"Bluewater 是大型酒店連鎖集團。"},{"en":"A huge hotel chain is a very large hotel company with many hotels in different places.","zh":"huge hotel chain 是在不同地方擁有多間酒店的大型酒店公司。"},{"en":"A huge hotel chain may have branches in several countries.","zh":"大型酒店連鎖集團可能在多個國家都有分店。"},{"en":"Large chains need strong staff systems because thousands of employees may work under one brand.","zh":"大型連鎖集團需要強大員工制度，因為同一品牌下可能有數以千計員工。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both size and business structure.","zh":"這個短語同時描述規模和企業結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as a reward","meaning":"作為獎勵","examples":[{"en":"As a reward, high achievers are sent on a trip abroad.","zh":"作為獎勵，高績效員工會被送去海外旅行。"},{"en":"As a reward means given because someone has done well or achieved something.","zh":"as a reward 的意思是因某人表現良好或取得成就而給予。"},{"en":"As a reward for finishing the project, the class had a free reading afternoon.","zh":"作為完成項目的獎勵，這班學生有一個自由閱讀下午。"},{"en":"Rewards can encourage people because effort is recognised in a concrete way.","zh":"獎勵可以鼓勵人，因為努力以具體方式受到認可。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the benefit given after success.","zh":"這個短語引出成功後給予的好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"all-expenses-paid trip","meaning":"全費資助旅行","examples":[{"en":"High achievers are sent on an all-expenses-paid trip abroad.","zh":"高績效員工會被送去全費資助的海外旅行。"},{"en":"An all-expenses-paid trip is a trip where the organisation pays for all major costs.","zh":"all-expenses-paid trip 是由機構支付所有主要費用的旅行。"},{"en":"A company may offer an all-expenses-paid trip to reward top sales staff.","zh":"公司可能提供全費資助旅行，獎勵頂尖銷售員工。"},{"en":"Such trips are attractive because employees do not need to pay for travel, accommodation, or meals.","zh":"這類旅行很吸引，因為員工不用支付交通、住宿或餐飲費用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a generous reward.","zh":"這個短語描述慷慨獎勵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"trip abroad","meaning":"海外旅行","examples":[{"en":"The reward is a trip abroad every year.","zh":"這項獎勵是每年一次海外旅行。"},{"en":"A trip abroad is a journey to another country.","zh":"trip abroad 是前往另一個國家的旅行。"},{"en":"Students may take a trip abroad to practise a foreign language.","zh":"學生可能參加海外旅行來練習外語。"},{"en":"Trips abroad can broaden experience because people meet different cultures and workplaces.","zh":"海外旅行可以擴闊經驗，因為人們接觸不同文化和工作場所。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on international travel.","zh":"這個短語集中於國際旅行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an important element in","meaning":"……的重要元素","examples":[{"en":"Fun is an important element in the trips.","zh":"樂趣是這些旅行的重要元素。"},{"en":"An important element in something is a key part that helps make it successful or complete.","zh":"an important element in something 是幫助某事成功或完整的關鍵部分。"},{"en":"Trust is an important element in teamwork.","zh":"信任是團隊合作的重要元素。"},{"en":"If an important element is missing, the whole experience may feel weaker.","zh":"如果缺少重要元素，整個體驗可能感覺較弱。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a necessary part of a larger activity.","zh":"這個短語指出較大活動中的必要部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the opportunity to","meaning":"……的機會","examples":[{"en":"The trips also offer the opportunity to learn something useful.","zh":"這些旅行也提供學到有用東西的機會。"},{"en":"The opportunity to do something means the chance to do it.","zh":"the opportunity to do something 的意思是做某事的機會。"},{"en":"A work placement gives students the opportunity to learn real workplace skills.","zh":"工作實習給學生學習真實職場技能的機會。"},{"en":"Opportunities matter because people can grow through experience, not only theory.","zh":"機會很重要，因為人可以透過經驗成長，而不只是理論。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a positive chance.","zh":"這個短語突出正面的機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"learn something useful","meaning":"學到有用的東西","examples":[{"en":"Staff can learn something useful during the trips.","zh":"職員可以在旅行期間學到有用的東西。"},{"en":"To learn something useful means to gain knowledge or skills that can help in real situations.","zh":"learn something useful 的意思是獲得能在真實情況中幫助自己的知識或技能。"},{"en":"Students learn something useful when they practise how to write a clear email.","zh":"學生練習如何寫清晰電郵時，就是學到有用的東西。"},{"en":"Useful learning is easier to remember because people can apply it later.","zh":"有用的學習較容易記住，因為人們之後可以應用。"},{"en":"This phrase connects learning with practical value.","zh":"這個短語把學習與實用價值連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"include a visit to","meaning":"包括參觀……","examples":[{"en":"This year’s trip included a visit to a brewery.","zh":"今年的旅行包括參觀一間啤酒廠。"},{"en":"To include a visit to somewhere means that going to that place is part of the plan.","zh":"include a visit to somewhere 的意思是前往該地方是計劃的一部分。"},{"en":"The school tour included a visit to a science museum.","zh":"學校旅行包括參觀科學博物館。"},{"en":"Including a visit to a workplace can make training more practical.","zh":"包括參觀工作場所可以令培訓更實用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one activity within a larger trip.","zh":"這個短語描述較大旅程中的其中一項活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"brewery","meaning":"啤酒廠","examples":[{"en":"Staff visited a brewery during this year’s trip.","zh":"職員在今年的旅行中參觀了一間啤酒廠。"},{"en":"A brewery is a place where beer is made.","zh":"brewery 是製造啤酒的地方。"},{"en":"A hotel worker may visit a brewery to learn how drinks are produced and served.","zh":"酒店員工可能參觀啤酒廠，以了解飲品如何製作和供應。"},{"en":"Visiting a brewery can help staff explain products more confidently to customers.","zh":"參觀啤酒廠可以幫助職員更有信心向顧客解釋產品。"},{"en":"This word names a specific kind of production site.","zh":"這個詞指一種特定生產場所。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be served in","meaning":"在……供應","examples":[{"en":"Staff learned about the new beer that would be served in the hotel.","zh":"職員了解了將會在酒店供應的新啤酒。"},{"en":"To be served in a place means to be offered to customers there.","zh":"be served in a place 的意思是在該地方提供給顧客。"},{"en":"The new dessert will be served in the restaurant from next week.","zh":"新甜品將由下星期起在餐廳供應。"},{"en":"Staff should understand products served in the hotel so they can answer guests’ questions.","zh":"職員應了解酒店供應的產品，才能回答住客問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in food, drink, and hospitality contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於食物、飲品和款待業語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"identify that","meaning":"發現……","examples":[{"en":"Pentlow Hotels identified that retention of junior reception staff was an issue.","zh":"Pentlow Hotels 發現初級接待處職員留任是一個問題。"},{"en":"To identify that something is a problem means to recognise or discover it through evidence or observation.","zh":"identify that something is a problem 的意思是透過證據或觀察認出或發現某事是問題。"},{"en":"The school identified that many students were struggling with reading comprehension.","zh":"學校發現許多學生在閱讀理解上有困難。"},{"en":"Identifying a problem clearly helps an organisation choose the right solution.","zh":"清楚發現問題有助機構選擇正確解決方案。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in reports.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常見於報告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"junior reception staff","meaning":"初級接待處職員","examples":[{"en":"Pentlow Hotels wanted to retain junior reception staff.","zh":"Pentlow Hotels 想挽留初級接待處職員。"},{"en":"Junior reception staff are lower-level or less experienced employees who work at a hotel’s front desk.","zh":"junior reception staff 是在酒店前台工作的較低職級或較少經驗員工。"},{"en":"Junior reception staff may check guests in, answer calls, and pass messages to managers.","zh":"初級接待處職員可能辦理住客入住、接聽電話，並把訊息轉交經理。"},{"en":"Supporting junior reception staff matters because they often create guests’ first impression.","zh":"支援初級接待處職員很重要，因為他們常創造住客的第一印象。"},{"en":"This phrase combines job level with a specific hotel role.","zh":"這個短語結合職級和特定酒店崗位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be an issue","meaning":"是一個問題","examples":[{"en":"Retention of junior reception staff was an issue.","zh":"初級接待處職員留任是一個問題。"},{"en":"To be an issue means to be a problem or matter that needs attention.","zh":"be an issue 的意思是某事是一個需要關注的問題或事項。"},{"en":"Noise is an issue in the classroom because students cannot concentrate.","zh":"噪音在課室是一個問題，因為學生不能集中。"},{"en":"If staff retention is an issue, managers need to understand why people leave.","zh":"如果員工留任是一個問題，經理需要理解人們為何離開。"},{"en":"This phrase is a polite way to say something is a problem.","zh":"這個短語是表示某事有問題的禮貌說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in order to encourage","meaning":"為了鼓勵……","examples":[{"en":"Pentlow introduced a management programme in order to encourage staff.","zh":"Pentlow 推出管理培訓計劃，為了鼓勵職員。"},{"en":"In order to encourage someone means for the purpose of giving them motivation or confidence.","zh":"in order to encourage someone 的意思是為了給予某人動力或信心。"},{"en":"A school may give certificates in order to encourage students to keep reading.","zh":"學校可能頒發證書，為了鼓勵學生繼續閱讀。"},{"en":"Encouragement works best when people see a real path forward.","zh":"當人們看見真實前路，鼓勵最有效。"},{"en":"This phrase links an action with the aim of motivating people.","zh":"這個短語把行動與激勵人的目的連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"worthwhile and rewarding","meaning":"值得而有回報","examples":[{"en":"Working in a hotel can be worthwhile and rewarding.","zh":"在酒店工作可以是值得而有回報的。"},{"en":"Worthwhile and rewarding means valuable, meaningful, and satisfying because it gives good results or personal fulfilment.","zh":"worthwhile and rewarding 的意思是有價值、有意義並令人滿足，因為它帶來好結果或個人成就感。"},{"en":"Teaching children can be worthwhile and rewarding when you see them grow in confidence.","zh":"當你看見孩子信心成長，教導兒童可以是值得而有回報的。"},{"en":"A job feels rewarding when workers can see that their effort matters.","zh":"當員工看見自己的努力有意義，一份工作就會感到有回報。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a positive view of an activity or career.","zh":"這個短語對活動或職業作出正面評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"good prospects","meaning":"良好前景","examples":[{"en":"Hotel work can offer good prospects.","zh":"酒店工作可以提供良好前景。"},{"en":"Good prospects are good future opportunities for success, promotion, or development.","zh":"good prospects 是未來成功、晉升或發展的好機會。"},{"en":"A job with training and promotion paths offers good prospects for young workers.","zh":"有培訓和晉升路徑的工作，為年輕員工提供良好前景。"},{"en":"Workers may stay longer if they believe the job has good prospects.","zh":"如果員工相信工作有良好前景，他們可能留任更久。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on future potential.","zh":"這個短語集中於未來潛力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"management programme","meaning":"管理培訓計劃","examples":[{"en":"Pentlow introduced a management programme for junior staff.","zh":"Pentlow 為初級職員推出管理培訓計劃。"},{"en":"A management programme is a training plan that helps employees learn leadership and management skills.","zh":"management programme 是幫助員工學習領導和管理技能的培訓計劃。"},{"en":"A hotel management programme may teach scheduling, customer service, budgeting, and team leadership.","zh":"酒店管理培訓計劃可能教授排更、顧客服務、預算和團隊領導。"},{"en":"Such programmes can show junior staff that promotion is possible.","zh":"這類計劃可以向初級職員顯示晉升是可能的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structured career development.","zh":"這個短語描述有結構的職業發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be given additional responsibilities","meaning":"獲給予額外職責","examples":[{"en":"Staff were given additional responsibilities.","zh":"職員獲給予額外職責。"},{"en":"To be given additional responsibilities means to receive extra duties beyond one’s usual work.","zh":"be given additional responsibilities 的意思是獲分配平常工作以外的額外職務。"},{"en":"A junior employee may be given additional responsibilities after showing reliability.","zh":"初級員工表現可靠後，可能獲給予額外職責。"},{"en":"Extra responsibilities can build confidence if staff also receive support and training.","zh":"如果職員同時得到支援和培訓，額外職責可以建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase can signal trust and development.","zh":"這個短語可以表示信任和發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"additional responsibilities","meaning":"額外職責","examples":[{"en":"Junior staff were given additional responsibilities.","zh":"初級職員獲給予額外職責。"},{"en":"Additional responsibilities are extra tasks or duties added to someone’s normal role.","zh":"additional responsibilities 是加到某人正常崗位上的額外任務或職務。"},{"en":"A receptionist may receive additional responsibilities such as training new staff.","zh":"接待員可能獲得額外職責，例如培訓新職員。"},{"en":"Extra duties can help people develop, but too many can create stress.","zh":"額外職務可以幫助人成長，但太多會製造壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes added work or authority.","zh":"這個短語描述增加的工作或權責。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"chance to work in","meaning":"有機會在……工作","examples":[{"en":"Staff had the chance to work in various roles.","zh":"職員有機會在不同崗位工作。"},{"en":"A chance to work in a role means an opportunity to try or perform that job.","zh":"chance to work in a role 的意思是有機會嘗試或擔任某工作。"},{"en":"Interns may get the chance to work in marketing, sales, and customer service.","zh":"實習生可能有機會在市場推廣、銷售和顧客服務部工作。"},{"en":"Trying different roles helps employees understand the business better.","zh":"嘗試不同崗位有助員工更了解企業。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights practical experience.","zh":"這個短語突出實際經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"various roles","meaning":"不同崗位","examples":[{"en":"Junior staff could work in various roles in the hotel.","zh":"初級職員可以在酒店不同崗位工作。"},{"en":"Various roles means several different jobs, positions, or responsibilities.","zh":"various roles 的意思是幾種不同工作、職位或責任。"},{"en":"In a school play, students can take various roles such as acting, lighting, or backstage work.","zh":"在學校話劇中，學生可以擔任不同崗位，例如演出、燈光或後台工作。"},{"en":"Working in various roles helps people discover their strengths.","zh":"在不同崗位工作有助人們發現自己的強項。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises variety in duties.","zh":"這個短語強調職責上的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be seen as","meaning":"被視為……","examples":[{"en":"Green Planet wanted to be seen as a caring employer.","zh":"Green Planet 希望被視為關心員工的僱主。"},{"en":"To be seen as something means to be regarded or understood in that way by other people.","zh":"be seen as something 的意思是被其他人以某種方式看待或理解。"},{"en":"A school wants to be seen as safe and supportive by parents.","zh":"學校希望被家長視為安全而支持學生的地方。"},{"en":"Reputation matters because how an organisation is seen can affect trust and recruitment.","zh":"名聲很重要，因為機構被如何看待會影響信任和招聘。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on public image.","zh":"這個短語集中於公眾形象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"caring employer","meaning":"關心員工的僱主","examples":[{"en":"Green Planet wanted to be seen as a caring employer.","zh":"Green Planet 希望被視為關心員工的僱主。"},{"en":"A caring employer is a company or manager that looks after employees’ needs and well-being.","zh":"caring employer 是照顧員工需要和福祉的公司或經理。"},{"en":"A caring employer may offer flexible hours, training, and support during family emergencies.","zh":"關心員工的僱主可能提供彈性工時、培訓和家庭緊急情況支援。"},{"en":"Caring employers often keep staff longer because workers feel respected.","zh":"關心員工的僱主通常能留住員工更久，因為員工感到被尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive employer image.","zh":"這個短語描述正面的僱主形象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make life easier for","meaning":"令……生活更輕鬆","examples":[{"en":"The hotel wanted to make life easier for staff.","zh":"酒店想令職員生活更輕鬆。"},{"en":"To make life easier for someone means to reduce their difficulties or daily stress.","zh":"make life easier for someone 的意思是減少某人的困難或日常壓力。"},{"en":"Flexible working hours can make life easier for parents with young children.","zh":"彈性工時可以令有年幼子女的父母生活更輕鬆。"},{"en":"Small changes at work can make life easier and improve staff loyalty.","zh":"工作中的小改變可以令生活更輕鬆，並提升員工忠誠度。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical support.","zh":"這個短語集中於實際支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"many of whom","meaning":"其中許多人","examples":[{"en":"Many staff had childcare responsibilities.","zh":"許多職員有照顧子女的責任。"},{"en":"Many of whom means many people in the group just mentioned.","zh":"many of whom 的意思是剛提及群體中的許多人。"},{"en":"The company hired new workers, many of whom were recent graduates.","zh":"公司聘請了新員工，其中許多人是應屆畢業生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when adding extra information about a group.","zh":"這個短語適合用於補充一個群體的額外資訊。"},{"en":"It is more formal than saying “many of them”.","zh":"它比 many of them 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"childcare responsibilities","meaning":"照顧子女的責任","examples":[{"en":"Many staff had childcare responsibilities.","zh":"許多職員有照顧子女的責任。"},{"en":"Childcare responsibilities are duties related to looking after children.","zh":"childcare responsibilities 是與照顧兒童有關的責任。"},{"en":"Parents with childcare responsibilities may need predictable shifts and emergency leave.","zh":"有照顧子女責任的父母可能需要可預測更次和緊急假期。"},{"en":"If employers ignore childcare responsibilities, workers may struggle to stay in their jobs.","zh":"如果僱主忽視照顧子女的責任，員工可能難以留在工作崗位。"},{"en":"This phrase connects family duties with work arrangements.","zh":"這個短語把家庭責任與工作安排連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"issue vouchers","meaning":"發放代用券","examples":[{"en":"The hotel began issuing vouchers to help staff.","zh":"酒店開始發放代用券來幫助職員。"},{"en":"To issue vouchers means to give people coupons or documents that can be used to pay for something.","zh":"issue vouchers 的意思是向人發出可用來支付某些東西的券或文件。"},{"en":"A company may issue meal vouchers to staff who work late.","zh":"公司可能向加班職員發放膳食券。"},{"en":"Vouchers can provide practical support because they reduce workers’ real expenses.","zh":"代用券可以提供實際支援，因為它們減少員工真實開支。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an official act of giving vouchers.","zh":"這個短語描述正式發出代用券的行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cover the cost of","meaning":"支付……的費用","examples":[{"en":"The vouchers helped cover the cost of childcare.","zh":"代用券幫助支付兒童照顧服務的費用。"},{"en":"To cover the cost of something means to pay for all or part of it.","zh":"cover the cost of something 的意思是支付某事的全部或部分費用。"},{"en":"Scholarships can cover the cost of tuition for students from low-income families.","zh":"獎學金可以為低收入家庭學生支付學費。"},{"en":"If an employer covers part of childcare costs, parents may find it easier to keep working.","zh":"如果僱主支付部分兒童照顧費用，父母可能更容易繼續工作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on financial support.","zh":"這個短語集中於財務支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"childcare","meaning":"兒童照顧服務","examples":[{"en":"The vouchers helped staff pay for childcare.","zh":"代用券幫助職員支付兒童照顧服務費用。"},{"en":"Childcare is the service or activity of looking after children while parents work or are unavailable.","zh":"childcare 是在父母工作或不在時照顧兒童的服務或活動。"},{"en":"Childcare may include nurseries, babysitters, after-school clubs, or family care.","zh":"兒童照顧服務可能包括托兒所、保姆、課後託管或家人照顧。"},{"en":"Affordable childcare helps parents stay in work and reduces stress.","zh":"可負擔的兒童照顧服務幫助父母留在職場並減少壓力。"},{"en":"This word is important in discussions of family and employment.","zh":"這個詞在家庭和就業討論中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"staff retention rates","meaning":"員工留任率","examples":[{"en":"Louise Marsh has one of the best staff retention rates in the business.","zh":"Louise Marsh 擁有業內最佳員工留任率之一。"},{"en":"Staff retention rates measure how well an organisation keeps its employees over time.","zh":"staff retention rates 衡量一個機構長期留住員工的能力。"},{"en":"A hotel with strong staff retention rates loses fewer workers each year.","zh":"員工留任率強的酒店每年流失較少員工。"},{"en":"Good retention rates may show that staff feel supported, fairly treated, and hopeful about the future.","zh":"良好留任率可能顯示員工感到受支持、受到公平對待，並對未來有希望。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a measurable view of staff loyalty.","zh":"這個短語以可量度方式看員工忠誠度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in the business","meaning":"在業內","examples":[{"en":"The Amesbury has one of the best staff retention rates in the business.","zh":"The Amesbury 擁有業內最佳員工留任率之一。"},{"en":"In the business means within a particular industry or field of work.","zh":"in the business 的意思是在某個行業或工作領域內。"},{"en":"That bakery is known as one of the best in the business.","zh":"那間麵包店被視為業內最佳之一。"},{"en":"Comparing results within the business helps managers see how they perform against competitors.","zh":"在業內比較成果，有助經理了解自己與競爭者相比的表現。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to describe reputation in an industry.","zh":"這個短語常用來描述行業中的名聲。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"since she joined the company","meaning":"自她加入公司以來","examples":[{"en":"Since she joined the company, Louise has improved staff retention.","zh":"自 Louise 加入公司以來，她改善了員工留任。"},{"en":"Since she joined the company means from the time she began working there until now.","zh":"since she joined the company 的意思是從她開始在該公司工作到現在。"},{"en":"Since he joined the school, the music club has grown quickly.","zh":"自他加入學校以來，音樂學會快速成長。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a person’s arrival with later changes or results.","zh":"這個短語把某人的到來與後來改變或結果連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing impact over time.","zh":"它適合用於描述一段時間內的影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make a huge effort to","meaning":"付出巨大努力去……","examples":[{"en":"Louise has made a huge effort to improve staff retention.","zh":"Louise 付出巨大努力去改善員工留任。"},{"en":"To make a huge effort to do something means to try very hard to achieve it.","zh":"make a huge effort to do something 的意思是非常努力去達成某事。"},{"en":"A student may make a huge effort to improve speaking by practising every day.","zh":"學生可能每天練習，付出巨大努力去改善口語。"},{"en":"Big improvements often happen only when people make sustained effort.","zh":"重大改善通常只有在人們持續努力時才會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises hard work and commitment.","zh":"這個短語強調努力和承擔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"achieve this","meaning":"達到這一點","examples":[{"en":"Louise created a supportive environment to achieve this.","zh":"Louise 創造支持性的環境來達到這一點。"},{"en":"To achieve this means to reach the result just mentioned.","zh":"achieve this 的意思是達到剛才提及的結果。"},{"en":"The school wanted better reading results and introduced daily reading time to achieve this.","zh":"學校想要更好閱讀成績，於是推出每日閱讀時間來達到這一點。"},{"en":"Achieving a goal usually requires clear action, not only good intentions.","zh":"達成目標通常需要清晰行動，而不只是好意。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a stated aim.","zh":"這個短語指回已提出的目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"co-operative and supportive environment","meaning":"合作而互相支持的環境","examples":[{"en":"Louise created a co-operative and supportive environment.","zh":"Louise 創造了合作而互相支持的環境。"},{"en":"A co-operative and supportive environment is a workplace where people help one another and work together positively.","zh":"co-operative and supportive environment 是人們互相幫助並正面合作的工作場所。"},{"en":"A classroom becomes supportive when students share ideas and do not laugh at mistakes.","zh":"當學生分享想法並不取笑錯誤，課室就會變得互相支持。"},{"en":"Supportive environments reduce stress because people know they are not facing problems alone.","zh":"互相支持的環境能減少壓力，因為人們知道自己不是獨自面對問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a healthy group culture.","zh":"這個短語描述健康的群體文化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"part of a large family","meaning":"大家庭的一部分","examples":[{"en":"For Louise, the staff are part of a large family.","zh":"對 Louise 來說，職員是大家庭的一部分。"},{"en":"Part of a large family means belonging to a close group where people care about one another.","zh":"part of a large family 的意思是屬於一個親近、彼此關心的群體。"},{"en":"A small company may make workers feel part of a large family by celebrating birthdays and helping during difficulties.","zh":"小公司可能透過慶祝生日和困難時提供幫助，令員工感到自己是大家庭的一部分。"},{"en":"When staff feel like family, they may show more loyalty and teamwork.","zh":"當職員感覺像家人，他們可能展現更多忠誠和團隊合作。"},{"en":"This phrase is metaphorical and describes belonging.","zh":"這個短語是比喻，描述歸屬感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"everyone is valued","meaning":"每個人都受到重視","examples":[{"en":"In Louise’s hotel, everyone is valued.","zh":"在 Louise 的酒店裏，每個人都受到重視。"},{"en":"Everyone is valued means every person is respected and seen as important.","zh":"everyone is valued 的意思是每個人都受到尊重，並被視為重要。"},{"en":"In a good team, cleaners, receptionists, managers, and trainees are all valued.","zh":"在好團隊中，清潔工、接待員、經理和見習生都受到重視。"},{"en":"When everyone is valued, people are more willing to share ideas and help one another.","zh":"當每個人都受到重視，人們更願意分享想法和互相幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes respect across all roles.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越所有崗位的尊重。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/listening/Practice 15/task-3":[{"front":"enjoy the course so far","meaning":"到目前為止覺得課程怎樣","examples":[{"en":"Jeanne asks Thomas how he is enjoying the course so far.","zh":"Jeanne 問 Thomas 到目前為止覺得課程怎樣。"},{"en":"To enjoy the course so far means to like the course up to this point.","zh":"enjoy the course so far 是指到目前為止喜歡這門課。"},{"en":"A student may be asked how she is enjoying the course so far after the first month.","zh":"開課一個月後，學生可能會被問到目前為止覺得課程怎樣。"},{"en":"This question helps teachers know whether students are interested or struggling.","zh":"這個問題幫助老師了解學生是否感興趣或感到吃力。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the experience up to now, not the whole course.","zh":"這個短語著重目前為止的經驗，而不是整個課程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"remind me","meaning":"提醒我一下","examples":[{"en":"Jeanne says, “Remind me, why did you decide to study sports science?”","zh":"Jeanne 說：「提醒我一下，你為甚麼決定修讀運動科學？」"},{"en":"Remind me is used when you ask someone to tell you again something you may have forgotten.","zh":"remind me 用於請別人再次告訴你可能忘記了的事情。"},{"en":"Remind me, what time does the meeting start tomorrow?","zh":"提醒我一下，明天會議幾點開始？"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they know the information may have been mentioned before.","zh":"當人們知道資料可能之前已提過，就會用這個短語。"},{"en":"It sounds natural and polite in conversation.","zh":"它在對話中聽起來自然又有禮貌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"decide to study","meaning":"決定修讀","examples":[{"en":"Thomas decided to study sports science.","zh":"Thomas 決定修讀運動科學。"},{"en":"To decide to study something means to choose that subject as your course or area of learning.","zh":"decide to study something 是指選擇某科作為課程或學習範疇。"},{"en":"A student may decide to study nursing because she wants to help patients.","zh":"學生可能因為想幫助病人而決定修讀護理。"},{"en":"People often decide to study a subject because of interest, career plans, or personal experience.","zh":"人們通常因興趣、職業計劃或個人經驗而決定修讀某科。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on making an educational choice.","zh":"這個短語著重作出教育選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sports science","meaning":"運動科學","examples":[{"en":"Thomas is studying sports science at university.","zh":"Thomas 正在大學修讀運動科學。"},{"en":"Sports science is the study of how the body works during sport and exercise.","zh":"sports science 是研究身體在運動和鍛煉中如何運作的學科。"},{"en":"Sports science students may learn about training, nutrition, injuries, and performance.","zh":"運動科學學生可能學習訓練、營養、受傷和表現。"},{"en":"This subject helps coaches and athletes train more safely and effectively.","zh":"這門學科幫助教練和運動員更安全、更有效地訓練。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an academic field, not simply playing sport.","zh":"這個短語指一個學術範疇，而不只是做運動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"professional athlete","meaning":"職業運動員","examples":[{"en":"Thomas once wanted to be a professional athlete.","zh":"Thomas 曾經想成為職業運動員。"},{"en":"A professional athlete is someone who earns money by competing in sport.","zh":"professional athlete 是靠參加體育比賽賺取收入的人。"},{"en":"A young runner may dream of becoming a professional athlete after winning school races.","zh":"年輕跑手在學校比賽勝出後，可能夢想成為職業運動員。"},{"en":"Becoming a professional athlete requires talent, training, discipline, and opportunity.","zh":"成為職業運動員需要天賦、訓練、自律和機會。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to sport as a career, not just a hobby.","zh":"這個短語指把運動作為職業，而不只是興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"when you were at school","meaning":"你讀書時","examples":[{"en":"Thomas wanted to be a professional athlete when he was at school.","zh":"Thomas 讀書時想成為職業運動員。"},{"en":"When you were at school means during the time when you were a student.","zh":"when you were at school 是指你還是學生的時候。"},{"en":"When I was at school, I wanted to become a journalist.","zh":"我讀書時想成為記者。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when talking about memories or ambitions from student life.","zh":"人們談論學生時期的回憶或志向時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It refers to the past period of attending school.","zh":"它指過去上學的那段時期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"that was my goal","meaning":"那曾是我的目標","examples":[{"en":"Becoming a professional athlete was Thomas’s goal.","zh":"成為職業運動員曾是 Thomas 的目標。"},{"en":"That was my goal means that was the thing I wanted to achieve.","zh":"that was my goal 是指那曾是我想達成的事情。"},{"en":"A student may say, “Getting into university was my goal.”","zh":"學生可能會說：「入讀大學曾是我的目標。」"},{"en":"Goals guide choices because people work towards what they want.","zh":"目標會引導選擇，因為人們會朝自己想要的事努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a past ambition or target.","zh":"這個短語描述過去的志向或目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"assume someone would","meaning":"以為某人會……","examples":[{"en":"Thomas’s classmates assumed he would achieve his goal.","zh":"Thomas 的同學以為他會達成目標。"},{"en":"To assume someone would do something means to believe it would happen without being certain.","zh":"assume someone would do something 是指在未能確定下相信某人會做某事。"},{"en":"Teachers may assume a strong student will pass, but effort is still needed.","zh":"老師可能以為成績好的學生會及格，但仍然需要努力。"},{"en":"Assumptions can be wrong if people do not see hidden difficulties.","zh":"如果人們看不到隱藏困難，假設可能會錯。"},{"en":"This phrase shows expectation rather than proof.","zh":"這個短語表示預期，而不是證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"achieve it","meaning":"達成它","examples":[{"en":"Thomas’s classmates assumed he would achieve his sporting goal.","zh":"Thomas 的同學以為他會達成他的運動目標。"},{"en":"To achieve it means to succeed in reaching a goal or completing an aim.","zh":"achieve it 是指成功達到一個目標或完成一個目的。"},{"en":"If a student wants a scholarship, she must work steadily to achieve it.","zh":"如果學生想拿獎學金，她必須穩定努力去達成它。"},{"en":"Achieving a goal usually requires planning, practice, and persistence.","zh":"達成目標通常需要計劃、練習和堅持。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a goal already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語回指前面已提到的目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"that must have been","meaning":"那一定是……","examples":[{"en":"Jeanne says that must have been a nice feeling.","zh":"Jeanne 說那一定是很好的感覺。"},{"en":"That must have been is used to make a strong guess about a past experience.","zh":"that must have been 用來對過去經歷作出強烈推測。"},{"en":"You won the final race? That must have been exciting.","zh":"你贏了決賽？那一定很令人興奮。"},{"en":"This phrase shows empathy because the speaker imagines how the person felt.","zh":"這個短語顯示同理心，因為說話者想像對方的感受。"},{"en":"It is used when the speaker is not certain but feels the guess is very likely.","zh":"當說話者不完全肯定但覺得推測很可能正確時，會使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"win anything","meaning":"贏任何比賽","examples":[{"en":"Thomas thought he could win anything.","zh":"Thomas 以為自己可以贏任何比賽。"},{"en":"To win anything means to be able to win any competition or event.","zh":"win anything 是指能夠贏得任何比賽或項目。"},{"en":"A confident swimmer may feel she can win anything after several victories.","zh":"自信的泳手連勝幾場後，可能覺得自己可以贏任何比賽。"},{"en":"Winning often builds confidence, but too much confidence can hide weaknesses.","zh":"勝利常建立信心，但過度自信可能掩蓋弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase shows very strong belief in one’s ability.","zh":"這個短語顯示對自己能力的強烈信念。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"no one who could","meaning":"沒有人能夠……","examples":[{"en":"Thomas thought there was no one who could run faster than him.","zh":"Thomas 以為沒有人能跑得比他快。"},{"en":"No one who could means there was not any person able to do that thing.","zh":"no one who could 是指沒有任何人有能力做那件事。"},{"en":"A top student may think there is no one who could answer faster than her.","zh":"頂尖學生可能以為沒有人能比她更快回答。"},{"en":"This phrase can show confidence, but it may also reveal overconfidence.","zh":"這個短語可以顯示信心，但也可能透露過度自信。"},{"en":"It focuses on ability by comparing one person with everyone else.","zh":"它透過把一個人與所有人比較來著重能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be more academic","meaning":"更重視學業","examples":[{"en":"Jeanne asks whether Thomas’s parents wanted him to be more academic.","zh":"Jeanne 問 Thomas 的父母是否想他更重視學業。"},{"en":"To be more academic means to focus more on study, exams, and school subjects.","zh":"be more academic 是指更專注於學習、考試和學科。"},{"en":"Some parents want children to be more academic if they worry sport is too uncertain.","zh":"如果家長擔心運動前途太不穩定，可能希望孩子更重視學業。"},{"en":"Being academic can help with university paths, but it is not the only kind of success.","zh":"重視學業可以幫助升學，但不是唯一成功方式。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts study-focused achievement with practical, creative, or sporting ability.","zh":"這個短語把重視學習的成就與實用、創意或運動能力作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not at all","meaning":"完全不是","examples":[{"en":"Thomas says his parents did not push him to be academic at all.","zh":"Thomas 說他的父母完全沒有推動他重視學業。"},{"en":"Not at all means completely not or in no way.","zh":"not at all 是指完全不，或一點也不。"},{"en":"The homework was not difficult at all after the teacher explained it.","zh":"老師解釋後，功課一點也不難。"},{"en":"Adding “at all” makes a negative statement stronger.","zh":"加上 at all 會令否定意思更強。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to correct an assumption strongly.","zh":"這個短語常用來強烈修正一個假設。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"push someone harder","meaning":"更加督促某人","examples":[{"en":"Thomas thinks his parents perhaps should have pushed him harder.","zh":"Thomas 覺得他的父母也許應該更加督促他。"},{"en":"To push someone harder means to encourage or pressure them to work with more effort.","zh":"push someone harder 是指鼓勵或施壓，使某人更努力。"},{"en":"A coach may push an athlete harder before an important race.","zh":"重要比賽前，教練可能更加督促運動員。"},{"en":"Pushing someone harder can help them improve, but too much pressure can harm confidence.","zh":"更加督促某人可以幫助他進步，但壓力太大可能傷害信心。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests stronger encouragement or discipline.","zh":"這個短語表示更強的鼓勵或紀律要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what makes you say that?","meaning":"你為甚麼這樣說？","examples":[{"en":"Jeanne asks Thomas what makes him say that.","zh":"Jeanne 問 Thomas 為甚麼這樣說。"},{"en":"What makes you say that? asks why someone thinks or believes something.","zh":"What makes you say that? 是問某人為甚麼這樣想或相信某事。"},{"en":"If a friend says the plan will fail, you might ask, “What makes you say that?”","zh":"如果朋友說計劃會失敗，你可能會問：「你為甚麼這樣說？」"},{"en":"This question invites explanation instead of simply disagreeing.","zh":"這個問題邀請對方解釋，而不是直接不同意。"},{"en":"It is useful when you want to understand someone’s reason.","zh":"當你想理解某人的原因時，這句很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"practise more","meaning":"練習更多","examples":[{"en":"Thomas thinks he should have practised more.","zh":"Thomas 覺得自己本應練習更多。"},{"en":"To practise more means to spend additional time improving a skill through repeated effort.","zh":"practise more 是指花更多時間透過重複努力改善技能。"},{"en":"A pianist may practise more before a school concert.","zh":"鋼琴學生可能在學校音樂會前練習更多。"},{"en":"More practice can improve technique, confidence, and consistency.","zh":"更多練習可以改善技巧、信心和穩定性。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that improvement needs repeated action.","zh":"這個短語表示進步需要反覆行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go out to","meaning":"前往","examples":[{"en":"Thomas went out to Kenya for a couple of weeks to train.","zh":"Thomas 前往肯亞訓練了幾星期。"},{"en":"To go out to a place means to travel there, often for a particular purpose.","zh":"go out to a place 是指前往某地，通常為了特定目的。"},{"en":"A student may go out to a rural clinic for work experience.","zh":"學生可能前往鄉郊診所進行工作體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests travelling away from home to a specific location.","zh":"這個短語常表示離開家去某個特定地方。"},{"en":"It focuses on movement to another place.","zh":"它著重前往另一個地方的移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"for a couple of weeks","meaning":"幾星期","examples":[{"en":"Thomas trained in Kenya for a couple of weeks.","zh":"Thomas 在肯亞訓練了幾星期。"},{"en":"For a couple of weeks means for about two weeks or a short period of a few weeks.","zh":"for a couple of weeks 是指大約兩星期，或短短幾星期。"},{"en":"A student may stay with relatives for a couple of weeks during the holidays.","zh":"學生可能在假期與親戚住幾星期。"},{"en":"A couple of weeks can be enough time to gain experience but not master a skill.","zh":"幾星期足以獲得經驗，但未必足以精通一項技能。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate length of time.","zh":"這個短語提供約略時間長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be chosen to","meaning":"被選中去……","examples":[{"en":"Thomas was chosen to go to Kenya.","zh":"Thomas 被選中去肯亞。"},{"en":"To be chosen to do something means to be selected for a special opportunity or task.","zh":"be chosen to do something 是指被選中去獲得特別機會或完成任務。"},{"en":"A student may be chosen to represent the school in a debate.","zh":"學生可能被選中代表學校參加辯論。"},{"en":"Being chosen can feel exciting because it shows others trust your ability.","zh":"被選中可能令人興奮，因為它顯示別人信任你的能力。"},{"en":"This passive phrase focuses on the person selected.","zh":"這個被動短語著重被選中的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"out of loads of","meaning":"從很多……之中","examples":[{"en":"Thomas was chosen out of loads of kids.","zh":"Thomas 是從很多孩子之中被選中的。"},{"en":"Out of loads of means selected from a very large number of people or things.","zh":"out of loads of 是指從大量人或物之中被選出。"},{"en":"A singer may be chosen out of loads of applicants for a school show.","zh":"歌手可能從很多申請者之中被選中參加學校表演。"},{"en":"Being selected from many candidates can make an opportunity feel special.","zh":"從許多候選人中被選出，會令機會感覺特別。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and emphasises large numbers.","zh":"這個短語較口語，強調數量很多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"run with","meaning":"與……一起跑步","examples":[{"en":"Thomas ran with some of the top teenage athletes in the world.","zh":"Thomas 與世界上一些頂尖青少年運動員一起跑步。"},{"en":"To run with someone means to run alongside or train together with them.","zh":"run with someone 是指與某人並肩跑步或一起訓練。"},{"en":"A beginner may run with a faster friend to improve pace.","zh":"初學者可能與較快的朋友一起跑步，以改善速度。"},{"en":"Running with stronger athletes can reveal your own strengths and weaknesses.","zh":"與更強的運動員一起跑步，可以顯示自己的優勢和弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes training or competing together.","zh":"這個短語描述一起訓練或比賽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"top teenage athletes","meaning":"頂尖青少年運動員","examples":[{"en":"Thomas trained with some of the top teenage athletes in the world.","zh":"Thomas 與世界上一些頂尖青少年運動員一起訓練。"},{"en":"Top teenage athletes are young sportspeople who perform at a very high level.","zh":"top teenage athletes 是表現達到很高水平的年輕運動員。"},{"en":"Top teenage athletes may train every day and compete internationally.","zh":"頂尖青少年運動員可能每天訓練並參加國際比賽。"},{"en":"Training with top athletes can be inspiring but also intimidating.","zh":"與頂尖運動員訓練可以令人受鼓舞，但也可能令人有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes young people who are among the best in sport.","zh":"這個短語描述在運動方面屬於最佳行列的年輕人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the world","meaning":"世界上","examples":[{"en":"Thomas trained with some of the best teenage athletes in the world.","zh":"Thomas 與世界上一些最優秀的青少年運動員一起訓練。"},{"en":"In the world means across all countries or globally.","zh":"in the world 是指在所有國家中，或全球範圍內。"},{"en":"The Olympics bring together some of the fastest runners in the world.","zh":"奧運會聚集世界上一些最快的跑手。"},{"en":"Saying “in the world” emphasises a very high level of comparison.","zh":"說 in the world 會強調非常高層次的比較。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the achievement sound international and impressive.","zh":"這個短語令成就聽起來具有國際性並令人印象深刻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be calm about","meaning":"對……感到平靜","examples":[{"en":"Thomas was very calm about being selected.","zh":"Thomas 對自己被選中感到很平靜。"},{"en":"To be calm about something means not to feel very excited, nervous, or upset about it.","zh":"be calm about something 是指對某事不感到非常興奮、緊張或不安。"},{"en":"A student may stay calm about an interview because she has prepared well.","zh":"學生可能因準備充分而對面試感到平靜。"},{"en":"Calmness can help people handle big opportunities without panic.","zh":"平靜可以幫助人面對重大機會而不慌亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional control.","zh":"這個短語描述情緒控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"keep thinking","meaning":"一直在想","examples":[{"en":"Thomas kept thinking how fortunate he was.","zh":"Thomas 一直在想自己多麼幸運。"},{"en":"To keep thinking means to continue having the same thought again and again.","zh":"keep thinking 是指不斷反覆有同一個想法。"},{"en":"Before an exam, a student may keep thinking about difficult questions.","zh":"考試前，學生可能一直想着困難題目。"},{"en":"Repeated thoughts can show worry, excitement, or gratitude.","zh":"反覆的想法可以顯示擔心、興奮或感激。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a thought that stays in someone’s mind.","zh":"這個短語描述停留在某人腦海中的想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fortunate","meaning":"幸運的","examples":[{"en":"Thomas felt fortunate to have the chance to train in Kenya.","zh":"Thomas 覺得有機會在肯亞訓練很幸運。"},{"en":"Fortunate means lucky or having a good opportunity.","zh":"fortunate 是指幸運或擁有好機會。"},{"en":"A student may feel fortunate to receive help from a patient teacher.","zh":"學生得到有耐性的老師幫助時，可能會覺得幸運。"},{"en":"People feel fortunate when something good happens that not everyone gets.","zh":"當好事發生而不是人人都能得到，人們會覺得幸運。"},{"en":"This word is slightly more formal than “lucky”.","zh":"這個詞比 lucky 稍正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what a great chance","meaning":"多麼好的機會","examples":[{"en":"Thomas thought that training in Kenya was a great chance.","zh":"Thomas 覺得在肯亞訓練是多麼好的機會。"},{"en":"What a great chance means what an excellent opportunity.","zh":"what a great chance 是指多麼出色的機會。"},{"en":"Getting to visit a famous science lab is a great chance for students.","zh":"能參觀著名科學實驗室，對學生來說是很好的機會。"},{"en":"A great chance can help someone learn, grow, or prove their ability.","zh":"好機會可以幫助人學習、成長或證明能力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong appreciation of an opportunity.","zh":"這個短語強烈表達對機會的欣賞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"back home","meaning":"在家鄉","examples":[{"en":"Everyone back home was proud of Thomas.","zh":"家鄉所有人都為 Thomas 感到自豪。"},{"en":"Back home means in the place where someone lives or comes from.","zh":"back home 是指在某人居住或來自的地方。"},{"en":"A student studying abroad may miss friends back home.","zh":"留學生可能會掛念家鄉的朋友。"},{"en":"People back home often follow news about someone representing their community.","zh":"家鄉的人常會關注代表社區的人傳來的消息。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the current place with the person’s home area.","zh":"這個短語把目前所在地方與家鄉作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be proud of","meaning":"為……感到自豪","examples":[{"en":"Everyone back home was proud of Thomas.","zh":"家鄉所有人都為 Thomas 感到自豪。"},{"en":"To be proud of someone means to feel pleased because of their achievement or character.","zh":"be proud of someone 是指因某人的成就或品格而感到高興。"},{"en":"Parents may be proud of a child who works hard, even without winning a prize.","zh":"即使孩子沒有得獎，只要努力，父母也可能為他感到自豪。"},{"en":"Pride often comes when someone represents their family, school, or community well.","zh":"當某人好好代表家庭、學校或社區時，常會令人自豪。"},{"en":"This phrase shows positive admiration and support.","zh":"這個短語顯示正面欣賞和支持。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"once we started competing","meaning":"一開始比賽","examples":[{"en":"Once they started competing, Thomas realised he was not good enough.","zh":"一開始比賽，Thomas 就意識到自己未達水準。"},{"en":"Once we started competing means as soon as the competition began.","zh":"once we started competing 是指比賽一開始。"},{"en":"Once the teams started competing, the difference in skill became clear.","zh":"一開始比賽，隊伍之間的技術差距便變得清楚。"},{"en":"Real competition can reveal weaknesses that training alone may not show.","zh":"真正比賽可以揭示單靠訓練未必顯示的弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the moment when theory becomes tested in action.","zh":"這個短語標示理論被實際行動測試的一刻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"quickly realise","meaning":"很快意識到","examples":[{"en":"Thomas quickly realised that he was not good enough.","zh":"Thomas 很快意識到自己不夠好。"},{"en":"To quickly realise something means to understand it soon after something happens.","zh":"quickly realise something 是指某事發生後很快明白它。"},{"en":"A student may quickly realise the exam is harder than expected.","zh":"學生可能很快意識到考試比預期困難。"},{"en":"Quick realisation often comes when evidence is obvious.","zh":"當證據很明顯，人們常會很快意識到事實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fast understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述迅速理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"not good enough","meaning":"不夠好；未達水準","examples":[{"en":"Thomas realised he was not good enough to compete with the top athletes.","zh":"Thomas 意識到自己不夠好，無法與頂尖運動員競爭。"},{"en":"Not good enough means not yet reaching the required standard.","zh":"not good enough 是指尚未達到所需標準。"},{"en":"A first draft may be not good enough for submission, but it can be improved.","zh":"第一稿可能未達提交水準，但可以改善。"},{"en":"Realising you are not good enough can be painful, but it can guide future training.","zh":"意識到自己未達水準可能痛苦，但可以引導未來訓練。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gap between ability and standard.","zh":"這個短語描述能力與標準之間的差距。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a huge shock","meaning":"巨大打擊","examples":[{"en":"Losing to the other athletes was a huge shock for Thomas.","zh":"輸給其他運動員對 Thomas 來說是巨大打擊。"},{"en":"A huge shock is a very surprising and upsetting experience.","zh":"a huge shock 是非常令人意外和難受的經歷。"},{"en":"Failing a test after always getting high marks can be a huge shock.","zh":"一直高分卻考試不合格，可以是巨大打擊。"},{"en":"A huge shock often happens when reality is very different from expectation.","zh":"當現實與預期非常不同，巨大打擊常會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both surprise and emotional impact.","zh":"這個短語同時描述驚訝和情感衝擊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"this cannot be happening","meaning":"這不可能發生","examples":[{"en":"Thomas thought, “This cannot be happening.”","zh":"Thomas 心想：「這不可能發生。」"},{"en":"This cannot be happening means the situation feels impossible or too shocking to accept.","zh":"this cannot be happening 是指情況感覺不可能或太震驚而難以接受。"},{"en":"A student may think, “This cannot be happening,” when she misses an important exam.","zh":"學生錯過重要考試時，可能會想：「這不可能發生。」"},{"en":"People say this mentally when bad news feels unreal.","zh":"當壞消息感覺不真實時，人們心裏會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase shows disbelief.","zh":"這個短語顯示難以置信。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be used to winning","meaning":"習慣勝出","examples":[{"en":"Thomas was used to winning before he went to Kenya.","zh":"Thomas 去肯亞前習慣勝出。"},{"en":"To be used to winning means to be familiar with winning often.","zh":"be used to winning 是指因經常勝出而對勝利感到熟悉。"},{"en":"A school team used to winning may feel shocked after its first defeat.","zh":"習慣勝出的校隊在第一次落敗後可能感到震驚。"},{"en":"Being used to success can make failure harder to accept.","zh":"習慣成功會令人更難接受失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a habit or expectation built from repeated victories.","zh":"這個短語描述由反覆勝利建立的習慣或預期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sorry to hear that","meaning":"聽到這件事很遺憾","examples":[{"en":"Jeanne says she is sorry to hear that Thomas was disappointed.","zh":"Jeanne 說聽到 Thomas 失望，她很遺憾。"},{"en":"Sorry to hear that is used to show sympathy when someone tells you bad news.","zh":"sorry to hear that 用於聽到壞消息時表達同情。"},{"en":"If a friend says she failed an exam, you might say, “I’m sorry to hear that.”","zh":"如果朋友說她考試不合格，你可能會說：「聽到這件事很遺憾。」"},{"en":"This phrase shows care without needing to solve the problem immediately.","zh":"這個短語顯示關心，而不需要立即解決問題。"},{"en":"It is polite and common in conversations about disappointment or difficulty.","zh":"它在談及失望或困難時有禮而常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be over it","meaning":"已經走出來","examples":[{"en":"Thomas is over the disappointment now.","zh":"Thomas 現在已經走出失望。"},{"en":"To be over something means to have recovered emotionally from it.","zh":"be over something 是指已在情感上從某事恢復過來。"},{"en":"A student may be over a bad result after talking to a teacher and making a new plan.","zh":"學生與老師談過並制定新計劃後，可能已從差成績中走出來。"},{"en":"People are over a setback when it no longer hurts as strongly.","zh":"當挫折不再那麼刺痛，人們便算走出來。"},{"en":"This phrase means emotionally past the problem, not physically above it.","zh":"這個短語指情感上越過問題，不是身體上在它上方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"university course","meaning":"大學課程","examples":[{"en":"Thomas thinks it is better to do a university course.","zh":"Thomas 認為修讀大學課程更好。"},{"en":"A university course is a programme of study at a university.","zh":"university course 是大學中的學習課程。"},{"en":"A university course may include lectures, seminars, assignments, and exams.","zh":"大學課程可能包括講課、研討課、功課和考試。"},{"en":"Taking a course can open new career paths when another dream does not work out.","zh":"當另一個夢想不成功，修讀課程可以打開新的職業道路。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal higher education.","zh":"這個短語指正式高等教育。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"such a variety of","meaning":"如此多種不同的……","examples":[{"en":"The sports science course has such a variety of sports-related areas.","zh":"運動科學課程有如此多種不同的運動相關範疇。"},{"en":"Such a variety of means so many different types or examples of something.","zh":"such a variety of 是指有如此多不同類型或例子。"},{"en":"A library with such a variety of books can serve readers of many ages.","zh":"有如此多種書籍的圖書館，可以服務不同年齡讀者。"},{"en":"Variety makes a course interesting because students can explore different topics.","zh":"多樣性令課程有趣，因為學生可以探索不同主題。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a wide range of choices.","zh":"這個短語強調選擇範圍廣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sports-related areas","meaning":"與運動相關的範疇","examples":[{"en":"The course covers many sports-related areas.","zh":"這門課涵蓋許多與運動相關的範疇。"},{"en":"Sports-related areas are topics connected with sport, exercise, performance, or health.","zh":"sports-related areas 是與運動、鍛煉、表現或健康有關的主題。"},{"en":"Sports psychology, injury prevention, coaching, and nutrition are sports-related areas.","zh":"運動心理學、傷患預防、教練學和營養都是與運動相關的範疇。"},{"en":"A course with many sports-related areas can prepare students for different careers.","zh":"涵蓋多個運動相關範疇的課程，可以為學生準備不同職業。"},{"en":"This phrase groups subjects linked to sport.","zh":"這個短語把與運動有關的科目歸在一起。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"choose it because of","meaning":"因為……而選擇它","examples":[{"en":"Jeanne chose the course because of its variety.","zh":"Jeanne 因為課程多元而選擇它。"},{"en":"To choose it because of something means to select it for that reason.","zh":"choose it because of something 是指因某個原因而選擇它。"},{"en":"A student may choose a school because of its strong music programme.","zh":"學生可能因學校有強大的音樂課程而選擇它。"},{"en":"Reasons for choosing something can include cost, location, quality, or interest.","zh":"選擇某事的原因可以包括費用、地點、質素或興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the cause behind a choice.","zh":"這個短語解釋選擇背後的原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"think of ideas for","meaning":"想到……的點子","examples":[{"en":"Thomas asks Jeanne whether she has thought of any ideas for the discussion session.","zh":"Thomas 問 Jeanne 是否已想到討論課的點子。"},{"en":"To think of ideas for something means to create or consider possible points or topics for it.","zh":"think of ideas for something 是指為某事想出或考慮可能的觀點或題目。"},{"en":"Students may think of ideas for a group presentation before meeting their teammates.","zh":"學生可能在見組員前先想到小組匯報的點子。"},{"en":"Good ideas are easier to find when people understand the purpose of the task.","zh":"當人們明白任務目的，好點子會較容易找到。"},{"en":"This phrase is about preparing content.","zh":"這個短語關於準備內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"discussion session","meaning":"討論課","examples":[{"en":"The students will have a discussion session on technology and sport.","zh":"學生將有一節關於科技與運動的討論課。"},{"en":"A discussion session is a class or meeting where people exchange ideas about a topic.","zh":"discussion session 是人們就某主題交換想法的課堂或會議。"},{"en":"A teacher may hold a discussion session after students read an article.","zh":"老師可能在學生讀完文章後舉行討論課。"},{"en":"Discussion sessions help students practise speaking, listening, and thinking critically.","zh":"討論課幫助學生練習說話、聆聽和批判思考。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised conversation, not casual chatting only.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的對話，而不只是閒聊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"technology and sport","meaning":"科技與運動","examples":[{"en":"The discussion session is about technology and sport.","zh":"討論課是關於科技與運動。"},{"en":"Technology and sport means the connection between tools, equipment, science, and athletic performance.","zh":"technology and sport 是指工具、器材、科學與運動表現之間的關係。"},{"en":"Running shoes, helmets, timing systems, and video analysis all connect technology and sport.","zh":"跑鞋、頭盔、計時系統和影片分析都連繫科技與運動。"},{"en":"Technology can make sport safer, faster, or fairer.","zh":"科技可以令運動更安全、更快或更公平。"},{"en":"This phrase links sporting activity with human invention.","zh":"這個短語把體育活動與人類發明連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cover more than one","meaning":"涵蓋不止一個","examples":[{"en":"The students have to cover more than one sport.","zh":"學生必須涵蓋不止一項運動。"},{"en":"To cover more than one means to include at least two examples, topics, or cases.","zh":"cover more than one 是指包括至少兩個例子、主題或個案。"},{"en":"A report on transport should cover more than one method, such as buses and trains.","zh":"關於交通的報告應涵蓋不止一種方式，例如巴士和火車。"},{"en":"Covering more than one example gives a broader view.","zh":"涵蓋不止一個例子可以提供更廣闊視角。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one example is not enough.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個例子不足夠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"think technology is about","meaning":"認為科技是關於……","examples":[{"en":"People often think technology is about the future.","zh":"人們常認為科技是關於未來。"},{"en":"To think technology is about something means to believe that is its main focus or meaning.","zh":"think technology is about something 是指相信那是科技的主要焦點或意思。"},{"en":"Many people think technology is about phones and computers, but tools can be simple too.","zh":"很多人認為科技是關於電話和電腦，但工具也可以很簡單。"},{"en":"Thinking too narrowly about technology can make people ignore older inventions.","zh":"對科技理解太狹窄，可能令人忽略較舊的發明。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a common belief or assumption.","zh":"這個短語引入常見信念或假設。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"gather some ideas about","meaning":"收集一些關於……的想法","examples":[{"en":"The students could gather some ideas about past developments in sport.","zh":"學生可以收集一些關於運動過去發展的想法。"},{"en":"To gather some ideas about something means to collect possible points or information about it.","zh":"gather some ideas about something 是指收集關於某事的可能觀點或資料。"},{"en":"A student may gather ideas about climate change before writing an essay.","zh":"學生寫文章前可能收集一些關於氣候變化的想法。"},{"en":"Gathering ideas helps people plan before speaking or writing.","zh":"收集想法有助人在說話或寫作前作規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful at the early preparation stage.","zh":"這個短語適合用於初步準備階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"past developments in","meaning":"……過去的發展","examples":[{"en":"They could discuss past developments in sport.","zh":"他們可以討論運動過去的發展。"},{"en":"Past developments in something are changes or improvements that happened earlier.","zh":"past developments in something 是指某方面較早出現的變化或改進。"},{"en":"A history lesson may look at past developments in medicine.","zh":"歷史課可能探討醫學過去的發展。"},{"en":"Studying past developments helps people understand how current methods appeared.","zh":"研究過去的發展有助人們理解現行方法如何出現。"},{"en":"This phrase connects history with progress or change.","zh":"這個短語把歷史與進步或變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"early types of equipment","meaning":"早期器材類型","examples":[{"en":"Thomas suggests looking at early types of equipment.","zh":"Thomas 建議看看早期器材類型。"},{"en":"Early types of equipment are older forms of tools or gear used before modern versions.","zh":"early types of equipment 是現代版本之前使用的較舊工具或器材形式。"},{"en":"Early types of medical equipment were often simpler and less accurate than modern machines.","zh":"早期醫療器材通常比現代機器更簡單且較不準確。"},{"en":"Studying early equipment shows how design improves with experience and technology.","zh":"研究早期器材可以顯示設計如何隨經驗和科技改進。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing old and new tools.","zh":"這個短語適合用於比較新舊工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"table tennis bats","meaning":"乒乓球拍","examples":[{"en":"Thomas remembers reading about table tennis bats.","zh":"Thomas 記得讀過關於乒乓球拍的資料。"},{"en":"Table tennis bats are the small paddles players use to hit the ball in table tennis.","zh":"table tennis bats 是乒乓球員用來擊球的小球拍。"},{"en":"A table tennis bat may have rubber on both sides to control speed and spin.","zh":"乒乓球拍兩面可能有橡膠，以控制速度和旋轉。"},{"en":"Changes in bats can affect how the game is played.","zh":"球拍的改變可以影響比賽方式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to sports equipment, not flying animals.","zh":"這個短語指運動器材，而不是會飛的蝙蝠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"end up being covered with","meaning":"最後被覆蓋上……","examples":[{"en":"Table tennis bats ended up being covered with pimpled rubber.","zh":"乒乓球拍最後被覆蓋上顆粒膠。"},{"en":"To end up being covered with something means finally to have that material placed over the surface.","zh":"end up being covered with something 是指最後表面覆上某種材料。"},{"en":"A playground wall may end up being covered with children’s drawings after an art day.","zh":"美術日後，遊樂場牆壁可能最後被孩子的畫覆蓋。"},{"en":"“End up” suggests a result after changes or experiments.","zh":"end up 暗示經歷變化或嘗試後的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the final state of an object.","zh":"這個短語描述物件的最終狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pimpled rubber","meaning":"顆粒膠","examples":[{"en":"Table tennis bats became covered with pimpled rubber.","zh":"乒乓球拍變成覆蓋着顆粒膠。"},{"en":"Pimpled rubber is rubber with small raised dots on the surface.","zh":"pimpled rubber 是表面有細小凸點的橡膠。"},{"en":"Pimpled rubber on a bat can change how the ball spins and bounces.","zh":"球拍上的顆粒膠可以改變球的旋轉和反彈方式。"},{"en":"Surface texture matters in sport because it affects control and movement.","zh":"運動中的表面質感很重要，因為它影響控制和移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a material with a specific surface pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述具有特定表面紋理的材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"wooden at first","meaning":"起初是木製的","examples":[{"en":"Table tennis bats were just wooden at first.","zh":"乒乓球拍起初只是木製的。"},{"en":"Wooden at first means originally made only of wood.","zh":"wooden at first 是指最初只由木製成。"},{"en":"Early toys were often wooden at first before plastic became common.","zh":"早期玩具在塑膠普及前常起初是木製的。"},{"en":"Equipment may start simple and later gain new materials or features.","zh":"器材可能一開始很簡單，之後加入新材料或功能。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the original form with later developments.","zh":"這個短語把原本形式與後來發展作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in about the 1920s","meaning":"大約在1920年代","examples":[{"en":"A factory was producing the rubber in about the 1920s.","zh":"有一間工廠大約在1920年代生產這種橡膠。"},{"en":"In about the 1920s means around the decade from 1920 to 1929.","zh":"in about the 1920s 是指大約在1920至1929年這個年代。"},{"en":"Radio became important in many homes in about the 1920s.","zh":"收音機大約在1920年代開始在許多家庭中變得重要。"},{"en":"The word “about” shows the date is approximate, not exact.","zh":"about 顯示日期是約略的，不是精確的。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event roughly in historical time.","zh":"這個短語把事件大概放在歷史時間中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make rolls of","meaning":"製造成卷的……","examples":[{"en":"The factory was making rolls of rubber.","zh":"工廠把橡膠製造成卷。"},{"en":"To make rolls of a material means to produce it in long sheets wound into cylinders.","zh":"make rolls of a material 是指把材料製成長片並捲成圓筒狀。"},{"en":"A factory may make rolls of paper for printing companies.","zh":"工廠可能為印刷公司製造成卷的紙。"},{"en":"Making material in rolls makes it easier to store, transport, and cut.","zh":"把材料製造成卷更容易儲存、運輸和裁剪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a manufacturing form.","zh":"這個短語描述一種製造形式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in bulk","meaning":"大批量地","examples":[{"en":"The factory was making rubber in bulk.","zh":"工廠大批量地生產橡膠。"},{"en":"In bulk means in large quantities.","zh":"in bulk 是指大量地。"},{"en":"A school may buy pencils in bulk because many students need them.","zh":"學校可能大批量購買鉛筆，因為很多學生需要。"},{"en":"Buying or producing in bulk can reduce cost per item.","zh":"大批量購買或生產可以降低每件成本。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business, shopping, and manufacturing.","zh":"這個短語常見於商業、購物和製造業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"horse harnesses","meaning":"馬具","examples":[{"en":"The rubber was originally made for things like horse harnesses.","zh":"這種橡膠原本是為馬具之類的東西製造的。"},{"en":"Horse harnesses are straps and equipment used to attach a horse to a cart or control it.","zh":"horse harnesses 是用來把馬連接到車上或控制馬匹的帶子和器具。"},{"en":"In the past, farmers used horse harnesses when horses pulled heavy loads.","zh":"過去農夫在馬拉重物時會使用馬具。"},{"en":"Strong materials are needed for harnesses because they must handle pressure and movement.","zh":"馬具需要結實材料，因為它們必須承受拉力和活動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to equipment for working with horses.","zh":"這個短語指與馬匹工作相關的器具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make a perfect covering for","meaning":"非常適合作為……的覆蓋物","examples":[{"en":"Someone realised the rubber would make a perfect covering for wooden bats.","zh":"有人意識到這種橡膠非常適合作為木製球拍的覆蓋物。"},{"en":"To make a perfect covering for something means to be very suitable as a layer over it.","zh":"make a perfect covering for something 是指非常適合作為覆蓋某物的一層材料。"},{"en":"A waterproof fabric can make a perfect covering for outdoor furniture.","zh":"防水布料非常適合作為戶外家具的覆蓋物。"},{"en":"A good covering protects the surface and may improve how the object works.","zh":"好的覆蓋物能保護表面，也可能改善物件的功能。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a material fits a particular use.","zh":"這個短語解釋某種材料為何適合某用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"wooden bats","meaning":"木製球拍","examples":[{"en":"The rubber was used as a covering for wooden bats.","zh":"這種橡膠被用作木製球拍的覆蓋物。"},{"en":"Wooden bats are bats or paddles made of wood.","zh":"wooden bats 是由木製成的球拍。"},{"en":"Early table tennis players used wooden bats before rubber surfaces became common.","zh":"橡膠表面普及前，早期乒乓球員使用木製球拍。"},{"en":"Wooden equipment can be strong, but extra covering may improve control.","zh":"木製器材可以很結實，但額外覆蓋物可能改善控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the material of the sports equipment.","zh":"這個短語描述運動器材的材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"what about","meaning":"……又如何？","examples":[{"en":"Jeanne asks, “What about cricket?”","zh":"Jeanne 問：「板球又如何？」"},{"en":"What about is used to introduce another topic or example.","zh":"what about 用來引入另一個主題或例子。"},{"en":"We have discussed football; what about basketball?","zh":"我們已討論足球；那籃球又如何？"},{"en":"This phrase helps move a conversation to a related point.","zh":"這個短語幫助把對話轉到相關的另一點。"},{"en":"It is useful when brainstorming several ideas.","zh":"它在腦力激盪多個想法時很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"innovative changes","meaning":"創新變化","examples":[{"en":"Cricket has had a few innovative changes.","zh":"板球出現過一些創新變化。"},{"en":"Innovative changes are new and creative improvements or developments.","zh":"innovative changes 是新的、有創意的改進或發展。"},{"en":"A school may make innovative changes by using digital homework feedback.","zh":"學校可能透過使用數碼功課回饋作出創新變化。"},{"en":"Innovative changes can make old activities safer, faster, or more effective.","zh":"創新變化可以令舊活動更安全、更快速或更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights new ideas that improve the usual way of doing things.","zh":"這個短語突出改善慣常做法的新想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pads","meaning":"護墊","examples":[{"en":"Cricket players wear pads on their legs.","zh":"板球員在腿上戴護墊。"},{"en":"Pads are protective pieces of equipment worn to reduce injury.","zh":"pads 是用來減少受傷的保護裝備。"},{"en":"Hockey goalkeepers wear pads to protect their legs from fast shots.","zh":"曲棍球守門員戴護墊，以保護雙腿免受快速射門擊中。"},{"en":"Pads are useful when players may be hit by a ball, stick, or hard surface.","zh":"當球員可能被球、球棍或硬地面撞到時，護墊很有用。"},{"en":"This word refers to protective sports gear.","zh":"這個詞指保護性運動裝備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"look on the internet","meaning":"在網上查看","examples":[{"en":"Thomas looks on the internet for information about cricket helmets.","zh":"Thomas 在網上查看關於板球頭盔的資料。"},{"en":"To look on the internet means to search online for information.","zh":"look on the internet 是指在網上搜尋資料。"},{"en":"A student may look on the internet for train times before leaving home.","zh":"學生離家前可能在網上查看火車時間。"},{"en":"Looking online is quick, but sources still need to be checked.","zh":"網上查資料很快，但仍需要檢查來源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using the internet to find information.","zh":"這個短語描述使用互聯網尋找資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come in","meaning":"出現；開始使用","examples":[{"en":"The first cricket helmet came in in 1978.","zh":"第一個板球頭盔在1978年出現。"},{"en":"To come in means to appear, be introduced, or start being used.","zh":"come in 是指出現、被引入或開始使用。"},{"en":"Contactless payment came in before many people stopped carrying cash.","zh":"感應付款在很多人停止帶現金前已經出現。"},{"en":"When new equipment comes in, people may need time to accept it.","zh":"當新器材開始使用，人們可能需要時間接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the arrival of a new practice or item.","zh":"這個短語描述新做法或物件的出現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cricket helmet","meaning":"板球頭盔","examples":[{"en":"The first cricket helmet appeared in 1978.","zh":"第一個板球頭盔在1978年出現。"},{"en":"A cricket helmet is protective headgear worn by cricket players, especially batsmen.","zh":"cricket helmet 是板球員，尤其是擊球手所戴的保護頭部裝備。"},{"en":"A cricket helmet helps protect the head and face from a hard ball.","zh":"板球頭盔幫助保護頭部和面部免受硬球擊中。"},{"en":"Protective helmets reduce the risk of serious injury in fast sports.","zh":"保護頭盔可降低快速運動中嚴重受傷的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to safety equipment used in cricket.","zh":"這個短語指板球中的安全裝備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Australian batsman","meaning":"澳洲擊球手","examples":[{"en":"An Australian batsman was the first to wear the cricket helmet.","zh":"一名澳洲擊球手是第一個戴板球頭盔的人。"},{"en":"An Australian batsman is a cricket player from Australia whose role is to hit the ball.","zh":"Australian batsman 是來自澳洲、負責擊球的板球員。"},{"en":"A batsman must react quickly because the ball can travel very fast.","zh":"擊球手必須快速反應，因為球可以飛得很快。"},{"en":"Batsmen often need protective equipment because they face direct hits from the bowler.","zh":"擊球手常需要保護裝備，因為他們直接面對投球員的來球。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both nationality and playing role.","zh":"這個短語同時指出國籍和比賽角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be booed and jeered by","meaning":"被……喝倒采和嘲笑","examples":[{"en":"The batsman was booed and jeered by people watching.","zh":"那名擊球手被觀看的人喝倒采和嘲笑。"},{"en":"To be booed and jeered by people means to be loudly mocked or criticised by them.","zh":"be booed and jeered by people 是指被人高聲嘲笑或批評。"},{"en":"A player may be booed and jeered by a crowd after making an unpopular decision.","zh":"球員作出不受歡迎的決定後，可能被觀眾喝倒采和嘲笑。"},{"en":"Public mockery can make it harder for people to accept new ideas.","zh":"公眾嘲笑會令新想法更難被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes negative crowd reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述負面的群眾反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"people watching","meaning":"觀看的人","examples":[{"en":"People watching the match laughed at the first cricket helmet.","zh":"觀看比賽的人嘲笑第一個板球頭盔。"},{"en":"People watching means the spectators or viewers observing an event.","zh":"people watching 是指正在觀看某活動的觀眾。"},{"en":"People watching a street performance may clap if they enjoy it.","zh":"觀看街頭表演的人如果喜歡，可能會拍手。"},{"en":"Spectators can influence players because their reactions are visible and loud.","zh":"觀眾會影響球員，因為他們的反應明顯又大聲。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people who are present to see something happen.","zh":"這個短語指在場觀看某事發生的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"protect themselves from","meaning":"保護自己免受……","examples":[{"en":"Players have to protect themselves from getting hurt.","zh":"球員必須保護自己免受傷害。"},{"en":"To protect themselves from something means to take action to avoid danger or harm.","zh":"protect themselves from something 是指採取行動避免危險或傷害。"},{"en":"Cyclists wear helmets to protect themselves from head injuries.","zh":"單車人士戴頭盔以保護自己免受頭部受傷。"},{"en":"Protective equipment reduces risk when accidents are possible.","zh":"當意外可能發生，保護裝備可降低風險。"},{"en":"This phrase connects safety actions with the danger being avoided.","zh":"這個短語把安全行動與要避免的危險連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get hurt","meaning":"受傷","examples":[{"en":"Players wear helmets to avoid getting hurt.","zh":"球員戴頭盔以避免受傷。"},{"en":"To get hurt means to be injured physically or emotionally.","zh":"get hurt 是指身體或情感上受傷。"},{"en":"A child may get hurt if she runs on a wet playground.","zh":"如果孩子在濕滑遊樂場跑步，可能會受傷。"},{"en":"Safety rules exist to reduce the chance of people getting hurt.","zh":"安全規則存在是為了減少人們受傷的機會。"},{"en":"In sport, this phrase usually means physical injury.","zh":"在運動中，這個短語通常指身體受傷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"everyone wears one now","meaning":"現在人人都戴","examples":[{"en":"Everyone wears a cricket helmet now.","zh":"現在人人都戴板球頭盔。"},{"en":"Everyone wears one now means the item has become normal or standard for all users.","zh":"everyone wears one now 是指該物品已變成所有使用者的正常或標準配備。"},{"en":"Seat belts were once resisted, but everyone wears one now in many cars.","zh":"安全帶曾經有人抗拒，但現在許多汽車中人人都會戴上。"},{"en":"Safety equipment often becomes accepted after people understand the risk.","zh":"當人們明白風險，安全裝備通常會變得被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a change from unusual to common.","zh":"這個短語顯示從不尋常變成普遍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unlike","meaning":"與……不同","examples":[{"en":"Cricket helmets are now common, unlike cycle helmets among ordinary bikers.","zh":"板球頭盔現在很普遍，與普通踩單車人士中的單車頭盔不同。"},{"en":"Unlike means different from another person or thing.","zh":"unlike 是指與另一個人或事物不同。"},{"en":"Unlike buses, bicycles do not need fuel.","zh":"與巴士不同，單車不需要燃料。"},{"en":"This word clearly contrasts two situations or groups.","zh":"這個詞清楚對比兩種情況或群體。"},{"en":"It is useful when one example behaves differently from another.","zh":"當一個例子與另一個不同時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cycle helmet","meaning":"單車頭盔","examples":[{"en":"Many ordinary bikers do not wear a cycle helmet.","zh":"許多普通踩單車人士不戴單車頭盔。"},{"en":"A cycle helmet is protective headgear worn while riding a bicycle.","zh":"cycle helmet 是踩單車時戴的保護頭部裝備。"},{"en":"A child should wear a cycle helmet when learning to ride on the road.","zh":"孩子學習在馬路上踩單車時應戴單車頭盔。"},{"en":"Cycle helmets reduce the risk of head injury in falls or crashes.","zh":"單車頭盔可以減少跌倒或碰撞時頭部受傷的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to safety equipment for cycling.","zh":"這個短語指踩單車用的安全裝備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unless you are a professional","meaning":"除非你是職業人士","examples":[{"en":"Many ordinary bikers do not wear helmets unless they are professionals.","zh":"許多普通踩單車人士不戴頭盔，除非他們是職業人士。"},{"en":"Unless you are a professional means except if you do the activity as a trained job or serious career.","zh":"unless you are a professional 是指除非你把該活動作為受訓工作或嚴肅職業。"},{"en":"Some people do not buy expensive cameras unless they are professional photographers.","zh":"有些人不會買昂貴相機，除非他們是職業攝影師。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a condition that changes the statement.","zh":"這個短語設定會改變說法的條件。"},{"en":"It contrasts ordinary participants with trained experts.","zh":"它把普通參與者與受訓專家作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ordinary bikers","meaning":"普通踩單車人士","examples":[{"en":"Many ordinary bikers do not wear helmets.","zh":"許多普通踩單車人士不戴頭盔。"},{"en":"Ordinary bikers are everyday people who ride bicycles, not professional cyclists.","zh":"ordinary bikers 是日常踩單車的人，而不是職業單車手。"},{"en":"Ordinary bikers may cycle to work, school, shops, or the park.","zh":"普通踩單車人士可能踩單車上班、上學、去商店或去公園。"},{"en":"Safety habits among ordinary bikers can affect road injury rates.","zh":"普通踩單車人士的安全習慣可以影響道路受傷率。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts casual riders with serious or professional cyclists.","zh":"這個短語把休閒騎行者與認真或職業單車手作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"original helmet designs","meaning":"早期頭盔設計","examples":[{"en":"Thomas looks at pictures of original helmet designs.","zh":"Thomas 查看早期頭盔設計的圖片。"},{"en":"Original helmet designs are the earliest forms or first versions of helmets.","zh":"original helmet designs 是頭盔最早的形式或第一批版本。"},{"en":"Original helmet designs often look strange compared with modern ones.","zh":"早期頭盔設計與現代頭盔相比，常看起來奇怪。"},{"en":"Studying original designs shows how safety equipment improved over time.","zh":"研究早期設計可以顯示安全裝備如何隨時間改善。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to early design history.","zh":"這個短語指早期設計歷史。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"upside-down bowl","meaning":"倒轉的碗","examples":[{"en":"One original helmet design looks like an upside-down bowl.","zh":"其中一個早期頭盔設計看起來像倒轉的碗。"},{"en":"An upside-down bowl is a bowl turned over so the open side faces down.","zh":"upside-down bowl 是被翻轉、開口朝下的碗。"},{"en":"A child may use an upside-down bowl as a pretend helmet during play.","zh":"孩子玩耍時可能把倒轉的碗當作假頭盔。"},{"en":"Comparing a helmet to an upside-down bowl suggests it looks simple and rounded.","zh":"把頭盔比作倒轉的碗，表示它看起來簡單而圓。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear visual image.","zh":"這個短語提供清楚的視覺畫面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be proud to be wearing","meaning":"以戴着……為榮","examples":[{"en":"The woman looks proud to be wearing the strange helmet.","zh":"那位女士看起來以戴着那個奇怪頭盔為榮。"},{"en":"To be proud to be wearing something means to feel pleased or confident while wearing it.","zh":"be proud to be wearing something 是指穿戴某物時感到高興或有信心。"},{"en":"A graduate may be proud to be wearing her university gown.","zh":"畢業生可能以穿着大學畢業袍為榮。"},{"en":"People feel proud wearing something when it represents achievement, identity, or courage.","zh":"當某物代表成就、身份或勇氣，人們穿戴它時會感到自豪。"},{"en":"This phrase links clothing with emotion.","zh":"這個短語把衣着與情感連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"serious cyclists","meaning":"認真踩單車的人","examples":[{"en":"Serious cyclists used to end up with wet hair.","zh":"認真踩單車的人過去常最後頭髮濕掉。"},{"en":"Serious cyclists are people who ride bicycles regularly and train or compete seriously.","zh":"serious cyclists 是定期踩單車並認真訓練或比賽的人。"},{"en":"Serious cyclists may buy better bikes, helmets, and clothing for performance.","zh":"認真踩單車的人可能為表現購買較好的單車、頭盔和衣物。"},{"en":"People who cycle hard produce sweat, so equipment design matters.","zh":"用力踩單車的人會流汗，所以器材設計很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts committed riders with casual bikers.","zh":"這個短語把認真騎行者與休閒踩單車人士作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"end up with","meaning":"最後有……","examples":[{"en":"Serious cyclists ended up with wet hair after hard exercise.","zh":"認真踩單車的人在劇烈運動後最後頭髮濕掉。"},{"en":"To end up with something means to finally have it as a result.","zh":"end up with something 是指最後得到或出現某結果。"},{"en":"If you forget an umbrella, you may end up with wet clothes.","zh":"如果你忘記帶傘，最後可能衣服濕掉。"},{"en":"A result can happen even if it was not planned or wanted.","zh":"即使不是計劃或想要的，結果仍可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the final outcome of a situation.","zh":"這個短語顯示情況的最終結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"wet hair","meaning":"濕頭髮","examples":[{"en":"Serious cyclists got wet hair from hard exercise.","zh":"認真踩單車的人因劇烈運動而頭髮濕掉。"},{"en":"Wet hair is hair that has water or sweat in it.","zh":"wet hair 是帶有水或汗的頭髮。"},{"en":"A runner may have wet hair after training on a hot day.","zh":"跑手在炎熱天氣訓練後可能有濕頭髮。"},{"en":"Wet hair under a helmet can feel uncomfortable and hot.","zh":"頭盔下的濕頭髮可能令人感到不舒服和悶熱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical result of sweat, rain, or water.","zh":"這個短語描述汗水、雨水或清水造成的身體結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hard exercise","meaning":"劇烈運動","examples":[{"en":"Cyclists got wet hair from all the hard exercise.","zh":"單車手因所有劇烈運動而頭髮濕掉。"},{"en":"Hard exercise means intense physical activity that requires effort and causes tiredness or sweating.","zh":"hard exercise 是需要努力、令人疲累或流汗的高強度體能活動。"},{"en":"Running uphill for twenty minutes is hard exercise for many people.","zh":"對很多人來說，上斜跑二十分鐘是劇烈運動。"},{"en":"Hard exercise can improve fitness, but the body also needs rest afterwards.","zh":"劇烈運動可以改善體能，但身體之後也需要休息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exercise that is demanding.","zh":"這個短語描述要求高的運動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"large air vents","meaning":"大型通風孔","examples":[{"en":"Modern cycle helmets have large air vents.","zh":"現代單車頭盔有大型通風孔。"},{"en":"Large air vents are big openings that allow air to move through.","zh":"large air vents 是讓空氣通過的大開口。"},{"en":"A helmet with large air vents can feel cooler during cycling.","zh":"有大型通風孔的頭盔在踩單車時會感覺較涼。"},{"en":"Air vents reduce heat and sweat by improving airflow.","zh":"通風孔透過改善空氣流動來減少熱和汗。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a design feature for comfort.","zh":"這個短語指提升舒適度的設計特徵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the skin can breathe","meaning":"皮膚可以透氣","examples":[{"en":"Air vents allow the skin to breathe more easily.","zh":"通風孔讓皮膚更容易透氣。"},{"en":"The skin can breathe means air can reach the skin so it feels cooler and less sweaty.","zh":"the skin can breathe 是指空氣能接觸皮膚，使它感覺較涼和較少汗。"},{"en":"Light cotton clothes help the skin breathe in hot weather.","zh":"炎熱天氣中，輕薄棉衣有助皮膚透氣。"},{"en":"If skin cannot breathe under equipment, the person may feel hot and uncomfortable.","zh":"如果皮膚在裝備下不能透氣，人可能會感到悶熱和不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and describes comfort, not literal breathing like lungs.","zh":"這個短語較口語，描述舒適度，不是像肺那樣真正呼吸。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"more easily","meaning":"更容易地","examples":[{"en":"Air vents help the skin breathe more easily.","zh":"通風孔幫助皮膚更容易透氣。"},{"en":"More easily means with less difficulty or effort.","zh":"more easily 是指困難或努力較少地。"},{"en":"Students understand a topic more easily when examples are clear.","zh":"當例子清楚，學生會更容易理解主題。"},{"en":"Good design helps people use equipment more easily.","zh":"良好設計幫助人們更容易使用器材。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one situation with a less easy one.","zh":"這個短語把一種情況與較不容易的情況作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"better still","meaning":"更好的是","examples":[{"en":"Thomas suggests discussing golf balls, or better still, golf clubs.","zh":"Thomas 建議討論高爾夫球，或者更好的是，高爾夫球桿。"},{"en":"Better still means an even better choice or idea.","zh":"better still 是指更好的選擇或想法。"},{"en":"We could meet in the café, or better still, in the library where it is quieter.","zh":"我們可以在咖啡店見面，或者更好的是，在較安靜的圖書館見面。"},{"en":"This phrase improves on a previous suggestion.","zh":"這個短語在前一個建議上作出改進。"},{"en":"It is useful when thinking aloud and choosing a stronger option.","zh":"當邊想邊選擇更強選項時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"golf clubs","meaning":"高爾夫球桿","examples":[{"en":"Golf clubs have changed a lot over time.","zh":"高爾夫球桿隨時間改變很多。"},{"en":"Golf clubs are the sticks used to hit the ball in golf.","zh":"golf clubs 是高爾夫球中用來擊球的球桿。"},{"en":"Different golf clubs are used for long shots, short shots, and putting.","zh":"不同高爾夫球桿用於長距離擊球、短距離擊球和推桿。"},{"en":"Materials and design affect how powerful and accurate a golf club is.","zh":"材料和設計會影響高爾夫球桿的力量和準確度。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to sports equipment, not a club of people here.","zh":"這裏的短語指運動器材，不是人的會所或社團。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"change a lot","meaning":"改變很多","examples":[{"en":"Golf clubs have changed a lot.","zh":"高爾夫球桿改變很多。"},{"en":"To change a lot means to become very different over time.","zh":"change a lot 是指隨時間變得非常不同。"},{"en":"Mobile phones have changed a lot since the first simple models.","zh":"手提電話自早期簡單型號以來改變很多。"},{"en":"Things change a lot when new materials or needs appear.","zh":"當新材料或新需要出現，事物會改變很多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes major development, not a small adjustment.","zh":"這個短語描述重大發展，而不是小調整。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"great-grandfather","meaning":"曾祖父","examples":[{"en":"Jeanne remembers what her great-grandfather told her about golf clubs.","zh":"Jeanne 記得她曾祖父告訴她關於高爾夫球桿的事。"},{"en":"A great-grandfather is the father of someone’s grandparent.","zh":"great-grandfather 是某人祖父母的父親。"},{"en":"A child may hear family stories from a great-grandfather about life long ago.","zh":"孩子可能從曾祖父那裏聽到很久以前的家庭故事。"},{"en":"Older relatives can pass down memories that are not found in textbooks.","zh":"年長親人可以傳下教科書中找不到的回憶。"},{"en":"This word identifies an earlier generation in a family.","zh":"這個詞指出家庭中較早一代。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be made entirely of","meaning":"完全由……製成","examples":[{"en":"Old golf clubs were made entirely of wood.","zh":"舊高爾夫球桿完全由木材製成。"},{"en":"To be made entirely of something means to be made completely from that material.","zh":"be made entirely of something 是指完全由某種材料製成。"},{"en":"A table made entirely of glass may look elegant but be easy to damage.","zh":"完全由玻璃製成的桌子可能看起來優雅，但容易損壞。"},{"en":"The material something is made of affects its strength, weight, and cost.","zh":"某物由甚麼材料製成，會影響其強度、重量和成本。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that no other material is used.","zh":"這個短語強調沒有使用其他材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"easily break","meaning":"容易斷裂","examples":[{"en":"Wooden golf clubs would easily break.","zh":"木製高爾夫球桿很容易斷裂。"},{"en":"To easily break means to break without much force or difficulty.","zh":"easily break 是指不用很大力量或困難就會斷裂。"},{"en":"A cheap plastic ruler may easily break if it is bent too far.","zh":"便宜塑膠尺如果被彎得太厲害，可能容易斷裂。"},{"en":"Equipment that breaks easily can be expensive and inconvenient to replace.","zh":"容易斷裂的器材更換起來可能昂貴又不方便。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests weakness or lack of durability.","zh":"這個短語表示脆弱或缺乏耐用性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get another","meaning":"另取一支；再買一支","examples":[{"en":"Players had to get another club when the old one broke.","zh":"舊球桿斷裂時，球員必須另取一支。"},{"en":"To get another means to obtain a replacement or an additional one.","zh":"get another 是指取得替代品或額外一件。"},{"en":"If a pen stops working during an exam, you need to get another.","zh":"如果筆在考試中壞了，你需要另取一支。"},{"en":"People get another item when the first one is lost, broken, or not enough.","zh":"當第一件物品遺失、壞掉或不夠用，人們會再拿一件。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on replacing or adding one more.","zh":"這個短語著重替換或增加一件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"no wood at all","meaning":"完全沒有木材","examples":[{"en":"There is no wood at all in modern golf clubs.","zh":"現代高爾夫球桿中完全沒有木材。"},{"en":"No wood at all means there is completely no wood.","zh":"no wood at all 是指完全沒有木材。"},{"en":"Some modern desks have no wood at all because they are made of metal and plastic.","zh":"有些現代書桌完全沒有木材，因為它們由金屬和塑膠製成。"},{"en":"Adding “at all” makes the absence stronger and clearer.","zh":"加上 at all 會令「沒有」的意思更強、更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts modern materials with older wooden designs.","zh":"這個短語把現代材料與舊式木製設計作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"much more powerful","meaning":"強度大得多；威力大得多","examples":[{"en":"Modern golf clubs are much more powerful.","zh":"現代高爾夫球桿威力大得多。"},{"en":"Much more powerful means far stronger or able to produce greater force.","zh":"much more powerful 是指強得多，或能產生更大力量。"},{"en":"A modern computer is much more powerful than an old classroom computer.","zh":"現代電腦比舊式課室電腦強大得多。"},{"en":"In sport, more powerful equipment can change speed, distance, and performance.","zh":"在運動中，威力更大的器材可以改變速度、距離和表現。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a strong comparison between old and new.","zh":"這個短語在新舊之間作出強烈比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the same must be true of","meaning":"……也一定是這樣","examples":[{"en":"Thomas thinks the same must be true of hockey sticks.","zh":"Thomas 認為曲棍球棍也一定是這樣。"},{"en":"The same must be true of something means the same idea probably applies to that thing too.","zh":"the same must be true of something 是指同一想法很可能也適用於某物。"},{"en":"If football boots have improved, the same must be true of running shoes.","zh":"如果足球鞋已經改良，跑鞋也一定是這樣。"},{"en":"This phrase extends an idea from one example to another.","zh":"這個短語把一個例子的想法延伸到另一例子。"},{"en":"It shows a confident guess based on comparison.","zh":"它顯示基於比較的有信心推測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hockey sticks","meaning":"曲棍球棍","examples":[{"en":"Jeanne says players still use wooden hockey sticks today.","zh":"Jeanne 說球員今天仍使用木製曲棍球棍。"},{"en":"Hockey sticks are long sticks players use to hit the ball or puck in hockey.","zh":"hockey sticks 是曲棍球員用來擊球或冰球的長棍。"},{"en":"A hockey player needs a stick that is strong, light, and easy to control.","zh":"曲棍球員需要結實、輕身並容易控制的球棍。"},{"en":"Stick design affects passing, shooting, and handling.","zh":"球棍設計會影響傳球、射門和控球。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to key equipment in hockey.","zh":"這個短語指曲棍球中的主要器材。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"wooden sticks","meaning":"木製球棍","examples":[{"en":"Players still use wooden sticks in hockey today.","zh":"今天曲棍球員仍使用木製球棍。"},{"en":"Wooden sticks are sticks made from wood.","zh":"wooden sticks 是由木材製成的球棍。"},{"en":"Some sports still use wooden sticks because players like their feel and tradition.","zh":"有些運動仍使用木製球棍，因為球員喜歡其手感和傳統。"},{"en":"Wooden equipment may be less modern, but it can still work well.","zh":"木製器材可能較不現代，但仍然可以很好用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the object and its material.","zh":"這個短語同時描述物件和材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"what it does say here","meaning":"這裏確實說的是","examples":[{"en":"Jeanne says what the source does say is that players once made their own sticks.","zh":"Jeanne 說資料這裏確實說的是，球員曾經自己製作球棍。"},{"en":"What it does say here means the source clearly states this point, even if it does not say something else.","zh":"what it does say here 是指資料清楚說明這一點，即使沒有說其他內容。"},{"en":"The article does not mention cost, but what it does say is that safety improved.","zh":"文章沒有提及成本，但它確實說的是安全有所改善。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects or limits what can be claimed from a source.","zh":"這個短語用來修正或限制可以從資料中得出的說法。"},{"en":"It is useful when reading information carefully.","zh":"當仔細閱讀資料時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"when the game started","meaning":"這項運動開始時","examples":[{"en":"When hockey started, players had to make their own sticks.","zh":"曲棍球這項運動開始時，球員必須自己製作球棍。"},{"en":"When the game started means in the early period when the sport first began.","zh":"when the game started 是指該運動最初開始的早期。"},{"en":"When the game started, there may have been fewer rules and less equipment.","zh":"這項運動開始時，可能規則較少，器材也較少。"},{"en":"Early sports often developed from simple local practices.","zh":"早期運動常由簡單本地做法發展而來。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the beginning of a sport’s history.","zh":"這個短語指一項運動歷史的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"produce a stick yourself","meaning":"自己製作球棍","examples":[{"en":"Early hockey players had to produce a stick themselves.","zh":"早期曲棍球員必須自己製作球棍。"},{"en":"To produce a stick yourself means to make or create a stick by your own effort.","zh":"produce a stick yourself 是指靠自己努力製作或做出球棍。"},{"en":"Before shops sold sports equipment, players often had to make tools themselves.","zh":"商店售賣運動器材前，球員常需要自己製作工具。"},{"en":"Making equipment yourself can lead to different shapes and quality.","zh":"自己製作器材可能導致形狀和質素不同。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights self-made equipment.","zh":"這個短語突出自製器材。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be manufactured","meaning":"被生產；被製造","examples":[{"en":"Hockey sticks were not being manufactured at first.","zh":"曲棍球棍起初並不是被生產出來的。"},{"en":"To be manufactured means to be made in a factory or organised production process.","zh":"be manufactured 是指在工廠或有組織的生產流程中製造。"},{"en":"Many toys are manufactured in large factories before being shipped to shops.","zh":"許多玩具在大型工廠中被製造，然後運到商店。"},{"en":"Manufactured equipment is usually more consistent than handmade items.","zh":"工廠生產的器材通常比手製物品更一致。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on formal production rather than individual making.","zh":"這個短語著重正式生產，而不是個人製作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"what about football?","meaning":"足球又如何？","examples":[{"en":"Thomas asks, “What about football?”","zh":"Thomas 問：「足球又如何？」"},{"en":"What about football? introduces football as another topic to consider.","zh":"What about football? 是引入足球作為另一個要考慮的主題。"},{"en":"After discussing tennis and cricket, someone may ask, “What about football?”","zh":"討論完網球和板球後，有人可能會問：「足球又如何？」"},{"en":"This question helps add another example to a discussion.","zh":"這個問題幫助在討論中加入另一個例子。"},{"en":"It is a simple way to move the conversation forward.","zh":"它是推進對話的簡單方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be made of animal skin","meaning":"由動物皮製成","examples":[{"en":"The first footballs were made of animal skin.","zh":"最早的足球由動物皮製成。"},{"en":"To be made of animal skin means to consist of leather or hide from animals.","zh":"be made of animal skin 是指由來自動物的皮革或皮製成。"},{"en":"Old bags and shoes were often made of animal skin before synthetic materials became common.","zh":"合成材料普及前，舊式袋和鞋常由動物皮製成。"},{"en":"The material of a ball affects weight, durability, and how it reacts to water.","zh":"球的材料會影響重量、耐用性和遇水後反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the original material used.","zh":"這個短語描述原本使用的材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cover something with","meaning":"用……覆蓋某物","examples":[{"en":"Early footballs were covered with pieces of leather.","zh":"早期足球用皮革塊覆蓋。"},{"en":"To cover something with a material means to put that material over its surface.","zh":"cover something with a material 是指把某材料放在某物表面。"},{"en":"A cook may cover a dish with foil before putting it in the oven.","zh":"廚師可能在把菜放進焗爐前用錫紙覆蓋它。"},{"en":"Covering an object can protect it, strengthen it, or change how it looks.","zh":"覆蓋物件可以保護它、加強它或改變外觀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding an outer layer.","zh":"這個短語描述加上一層外層。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pieces of leather","meaning":"皮革塊","examples":[{"en":"Early footballs were covered with pieces of leather.","zh":"早期足球由皮革塊覆蓋。"},{"en":"Pieces of leather are cut sections of animal hide used as material.","zh":"pieces of leather 是切割出來、用作材料的動物皮革部分。"},{"en":"A craft worker may sew pieces of leather together to make a wallet.","zh":"手工藝人可能把皮革塊縫在一起製作銀包。"},{"en":"Leather pieces can be strong, but the joins may let in water if not sealed well.","zh":"皮革塊可以很結實，但如果接合位密封不好，可能會入水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes smaller parts of leather used to make something.","zh":"這個短語描述用來製作物件的較小皮革部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be stitched together","meaning":"被縫合在一起","examples":[{"en":"The pieces of leather were stitched together.","zh":"皮革塊被縫合在一起。"},{"en":"To be stitched together means to be joined using thread and stitches.","zh":"be stitched together 是指用線和針腳把物件連接起來。"},{"en":"A tailor stitched pieces of fabric together to make a jacket.","zh":"裁縫把布料片縫合在一起製作外套。"},{"en":"Strong stitching keeps separate pieces from coming apart.","zh":"結實的縫線可以防止分開的部分散開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how soft materials are joined.","zh":"這個短語描述柔軟材料如何連接。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"let in water","meaning":"入水","examples":[{"en":"Early footballs let in water when it rained.","zh":"早期足球下雨時會入水。"},{"en":"To let in water means to allow water to enter.","zh":"let in water 是指讓水進入。"},{"en":"Old shoes may let in water if the soles are cracked.","zh":"如果鞋底裂開，舊鞋可能會入水。"},{"en":"Equipment that lets in water can become heavy, damaged, or unsafe.","zh":"會入水的器材可能變重、受損或不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a problem with sealing or protection.","zh":"這個短語描述密封或保護方面的問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"when it rained","meaning":"下雨時","examples":[{"en":"The balls became heavier when it rained.","zh":"下雨時，球變得更重。"},{"en":"When it rained means during times of rain.","zh":"when it rained 是指下雨的時候。"},{"en":"The playground became slippery when it rained.","zh":"下雨時，遊樂場變得濕滑。"},{"en":"Weather can change how safe or practical equipment is.","zh":"天氣可以改變器材的安全性或實用性。"},{"en":"This phrase links a weather condition with its result.","zh":"這個短語把天氣情況與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"much heavier","meaning":"重得多","examples":[{"en":"The footballs became much heavier when they absorbed water.","zh":"足球吸水後變得重得多。"},{"en":"Much heavier means far greater in weight than before.","zh":"much heavier 是指重量比之前大得多。"},{"en":"A schoolbag becomes much heavier when it is full of textbooks.","zh":"書包裝滿課本後會重得多。"},{"en":"If sports equipment becomes heavier, it can be harder and riskier to use.","zh":"如果運動器材變重，使用起來可能更困難和更危險。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a strong comparison in weight.","zh":"這個短語在重量上作出強烈比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"damage to","meaning":"對……的傷害","examples":[{"en":"Thomas mentions the damage to players’ necks.","zh":"Thomas 提到對球員頸部的傷害。"},{"en":"Damage to something means harm or injury affecting that part or thing.","zh":"damage to something 是指影響某部位或事物的損害或傷害。"},{"en":"Poor posture can cause damage to a person’s back over time.","zh":"姿勢不良長遠可以造成對背部的傷害。"},{"en":"Repeated impact can lead to damage that is not obvious at first.","zh":"反覆撞擊可能造成一開始不明顯的傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what is harmed.","zh":"這個短語指出受傷害的是甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"players’ necks","meaning":"球員的頸部","examples":[{"en":"Heading wet footballs could damage players’ necks.","zh":"頂濕足球可能傷害球員的頸部。"},{"en":"Players’ necks are the necks of the people playing the sport.","zh":"players’ necks 是指參與運動的人士的頸部。"},{"en":"Strong neck muscles can help athletes reduce injury risk in contact sports.","zh":"強壯頸部肌肉可以幫助運動員在接觸性運動中減少受傷風險。"},{"en":"Heavy balls or sudden impact can strain players’ necks.","zh":"重球或突然撞擊可能拉傷球員的頸部。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a body part affected by sport.","zh":"這個短語著重運動中受影響的身體部位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"when the ball was headed","meaning":"頂球時","examples":[{"en":"Players’ necks could be hurt when the ball was headed.","zh":"頂球時，球員頸部可能會受傷。"},{"en":"When the ball was headed means when a player hit the ball with the head.","zh":"when the ball was headed 是指球員用頭擊球的時候。"},{"en":"In football, defenders often jump when the ball is headed away from goal.","zh":"在足球中，後衛在把球頂離球門時常會跳起。"},{"en":"Heading a heavy ball can put pressure on the neck and head.","zh":"頂重球可能對頸部和頭部造成壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the moment of heading in football.","zh":"這個短語描述足球中頂球的一刻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"how painful that must have been","meaning":"那一定很痛","examples":[{"en":"Jeanne says how painful heading a wet football must have been.","zh":"Jeanne 說頂濕足球一定很痛。"},{"en":"How painful that must have been means the speaker strongly imagines it was very painful.","zh":"how painful that must have been 是指說話者強烈想像那一定非常痛。"},{"en":"If someone ran a race with an injured ankle, you might say how painful that must have been.","zh":"如果有人腳踝受傷仍跑比賽，你可能會說那一定很痛。"},{"en":"This phrase shows sympathy by imagining another person’s pain.","zh":"這個短語透過想像別人的痛楚來表示同情。"},{"en":"It is used when the speaker did not feel the pain directly but can picture it.","zh":"當說話者沒有親身感受到痛楚，但能想像時，會使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"put together","meaning":"整理；拼湊出","examples":[{"en":"The students can put together some useful ideas for their discussion.","zh":"學生可以為討論整理出一些有用想法。"},{"en":"To put together ideas means to collect and organise them into a useful form.","zh":"put together ideas 是指收集並組織想法，使其成為有用形式。"},{"en":"A group may put together notes before giving a presentation.","zh":"小組可能在匯報前整理筆記。"},{"en":"Putting ideas together helps turn separate facts into a clear plan.","zh":"把想法整理起來，有助把零散資料變成清楚計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in preparation, teamwork, and writing.","zh":"這個短語常見於準備、合作和寫作中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"useful ideas","meaning":"有用的想法","examples":[{"en":"Thomas thinks they can put together some useful ideas.","zh":"Thomas 認為他們可以整理出一些有用的想法。"},{"en":"Useful ideas are ideas that help solve a problem, answer a question, or support a discussion.","zh":"useful ideas 是能幫助解決問題、回答問題或支持討論的想法。"},{"en":"Students need useful ideas before they can write a strong essay.","zh":"學生需要有用的想法，才能寫出有力文章。"},{"en":"An idea becomes useful when it is clear, relevant, and supported by examples.","zh":"當想法清楚、相關並有例子支持，它便變得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical value, not just creativity.","zh":"這個短語著重實際價值，而不只是創意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 15/task-4":[{"front":"natural food product","meaning":"天然食品","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup is a natural food product.","zh":"楓糖漿是一種天然食品。"},{"en":"A natural food product is made from natural sources rather than artificial chemicals.","zh":"natural food product 指由天然來源製成，而不是由人工化學物製成的食品。"},{"en":"Honey is often seen as a natural food product because it comes from bees.","zh":"蜜糖常被視為天然食品，因為它來自蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Many people prefer natural food products because they sound simpler and less processed.","zh":"許多人較喜歡天然食品，因為它們聽起來較簡單、較少加工。"},{"en":"This phrase describes food that comes from nature and is not heavily artificial.","zh":"這個短語描述來自自然、不是高度人工化的食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"maple syrup","meaning":"楓糖漿","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup is produced from the sap inside the maple tree.","zh":"楓糖漿由楓樹內的樹液製成。"},{"en":"Maple syrup is a sweet liquid made by boiling down maple tree sap.","zh":"maple syrup 指把楓樹樹液煮濃後製成的甜液體。"},{"en":"People often pour maple syrup over pancakes, waffles, or desserts.","zh":"人們常把楓糖漿倒在班戟、窩夫或甜品上。"},{"en":"Maple syrup has a rich flavour that is different from ordinary sugar.","zh":"楓糖漿有濃郁味道，與普通糖不同。"},{"en":"This phrase names a natural sweetener strongly associated with Canada.","zh":"這個短語指一種與加拿大密切相關的天然甜味劑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what exactly","meaning":"到底是甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The speaker asks, “What exactly is maple syrup?”","zh":"講者問：「楓糖漿到底是甚麼？」"},{"en":"What exactly is used when someone wants a clear and precise explanation.","zh":"what exactly 用於某人想得到清楚而準確的解釋時。"},{"en":"A student may ask, “What exactly is photosynthesis?” when the topic is new.","zh":"當題目很新，學生可能問：「光合作用到底是甚麼？」"},{"en":"The word “exactly” shows that a general answer is not enough.","zh":"“exactly” 顯示一般答案並不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a definition.","zh":"這個短語適合用於引入定義。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look rather like","meaning":"看起來有點像……","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup looks rather like clear honey.","zh":"楓糖漿看起來有點像清澈的蜜糖。"},{"en":"Look rather like means look quite similar to something, but not exactly the same.","zh":"look rather like 指看起來與某物相當相似，但不完全一樣。"},{"en":"The new school building looks rather like a library from the outside.","zh":"新校舍從外面看起來有點像圖書館。"},{"en":"This phrase helps listeners imagine something by comparing it with something familiar.","zh":"這個短語透過與熟悉事物比較，幫助聽者想像某物。"},{"en":"“Rather” makes the comparison softer and less absolute.","zh":"“rather” 令比較語氣較柔和，不那麼絕對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"clear honey","meaning":"清澈的蜜糖","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup looks rather like clear honey.","zh":"楓糖漿看起來有點像清澈的蜜糖。"},{"en":"Clear honey is honey that is smooth and transparent rather than thick and cloudy.","zh":"clear honey 指順滑透明，而不是濃厚混濁的蜜糖。"},{"en":"A jar of clear honey may shine golden in the light.","zh":"一罐清澈的蜜糖在光線下可能呈現金黃色。"},{"en":"Comparing maple syrup with clear honey helps people imagine its colour and texture.","zh":"把楓糖漿與清澈蜜糖比較，有助人想像它的顏色和質感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a familiar sweet liquid.","zh":"這個短語描述一種熟悉的甜液體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be made by","meaning":"由……製成","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup is not made by bees.","zh":"楓糖漿不是由蜜蜂製成。"},{"en":"Be made by someone or something means be produced through that person, animal, machine, or process.","zh":"be made by someone or something 指由某人、動物、機器或過程製造。"},{"en":"Honey is made by bees, but maple syrup is made from tree sap.","zh":"蜜糖由蜜蜂製成，但楓糖漿由樹液製成。"},{"en":"Saying what something is made by helps explain its origin.","zh":"說明某物由甚麼製成，有助解釋它的來源。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the maker or producer.","zh":"這個短語指出製造者或生產者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be produced from","meaning":"由……製成","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup is produced from the sap inside the maple tree.","zh":"楓糖漿由楓樹內的樹液製成。"},{"en":"Be produced from something means be made using that material as the source.","zh":"be produced from something 指使用某材料作來源來製造。"},{"en":"Paper is produced from wood pulp.","zh":"紙張由木漿製成。"},{"en":"If a food is produced from a plant fluid, the plant is the original source.","zh":"如果食物由植物液製成，植物就是最初來源。"},{"en":"This phrase explains raw material and origin.","zh":"這個短語解釋原材料和來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"plant fluid","meaning":"植物液","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup is produced from plant fluid inside the maple tree.","zh":"楓糖漿由楓樹內的植物液製成。"},{"en":"Plant fluid is liquid found inside a plant.","zh":"plant fluid 指植物內部的液體。"},{"en":"Sap is one kind of plant fluid that moves through trees.","zh":"樹液是一種在樹木中流動的植物液。"},{"en":"Plant fluids can carry water, sugar, and nutrients around the plant.","zh":"植物液可以把水分、糖分和營養物質運送到植物各部分。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain sap in simple scientific language.","zh":"這個短語用簡單科學語言解釋樹液。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sap","meaning":"樹液","examples":[{"en":"Sap is the plant fluid inside a maple tree.","zh":"樹液是楓樹內的植物液。"},{"en":"Sap is a liquid that carries water, sugar, and nutrients through a plant.","zh":"sap 指在植物內運送水分、糖分和營養物質的液體。"},{"en":"Maple sap is collected and boiled to make maple syrup.","zh":"楓樹樹液會被收集並煮沸，製成楓糖漿。"},{"en":"Fresh sap is much thinner and less sweet than finished syrup.","zh":"新鮮樹液比製成的糖漿稀得多，也沒有那麼甜。"},{"en":"This word names the raw liquid taken from the tree.","zh":"這個字指出從樹中取得的原始液體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"maple tree","meaning":"楓樹","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup comes from the maple tree.","zh":"楓糖漿來自楓樹。"},{"en":"A maple tree is a tree whose sap can be used to make maple products.","zh":"maple tree 指其樹液可用來製作楓糖產品的樹。"},{"en":"Maple trees are also known for their attractive leaves in autumn.","zh":"楓樹也以秋天漂亮的葉子聞名。"},{"en":"Only suitable mature maple trees can produce sap for syrup making.","zh":"只有合適而成熟的楓樹才能產生用於製糖漿的樹液。"},{"en":"This phrase names the tree that provides the raw material.","zh":"這個短語指出提供原材料的樹。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"thick, golden, sweet-tasting liquid","meaning":"濃稠、金黃色、味道甜美的液體","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup is a thick, golden, sweet-tasting liquid.","zh":"楓糖漿是一種濃稠、金黃色、味道甜美的液體。"},{"en":"A thick, golden, sweet-tasting liquid is dense, yellow-gold in colour, and sweet in flavour.","zh":"thick, golden, sweet-tasting liquid 指質地濃、顏色金黃、味道甜的液體。"},{"en":"Warm syrup becomes a thick, golden liquid when much of its water has evaporated.","zh":"當大量水分蒸發後，暖糖漿會變成濃稠的金黃色液體。"},{"en":"These three adjectives help describe texture, colour, and taste together.","zh":"這三個形容詞同時描述質感、顏色和味道。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a rich sensory description.","zh":"這個短語提供豐富的感官描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be bought in bottles or jars","meaning":"以瓶裝或罐裝購買","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup can be bought in bottles or jars.","zh":"楓糖漿可以以瓶裝或罐裝購買。"},{"en":"Be bought in bottles or jars means be sold inside these containers.","zh":"be bought in bottles or jars 指以這些容器包裝售賣。"},{"en":"Jam is usually bought in jars, while drinks are often bought in bottles.","zh":"果醬通常以罐裝購買，而飲品常以瓶裝購買。"},{"en":"Packaging helps protect food and makes it easier to store.","zh":"包裝有助保護食物，並令儲存更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a product is sold.","zh":"這個短語描述產品的售賣方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be poured onto","meaning":"被倒在……上","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup can be poured onto waffles and ice cream.","zh":"楓糖漿可以被倒在窩夫和雪糕上。"},{"en":"Be poured onto something means be made to flow from a container onto the surface of food or another object.","zh":"be poured onto something 指液體從容器流到食物或其他物件表面。"},{"en":"Sauce can be poured onto pasta before serving.","zh":"醬汁可以在上菜前倒在意粉上。"},{"en":"Pouring syrup onto food adds sweetness and flavour.","zh":"把糖漿倒在食物上可以增加甜味和風味。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a liquid being added from above.","zh":"這個短語描述液體從上方加入。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"such as","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup can be poured onto food such as waffles and ice cream.","zh":"楓糖漿可以倒在例如窩夫和雪糕等食物上。"},{"en":"Such as introduces examples of the thing just mentioned.","zh":"such as 用來引出剛才提到事物的例子。"},{"en":"Sweet toppings such as honey, syrup, and jam are common at breakfast.","zh":"蜜糖、糖漿和果醬等甜配料在早餐中很常見。"},{"en":"This phrase gives examples without listing every possibility.","zh":"這個短語提供例子，但不列出所有可能性。"},{"en":"It is useful in explanations and descriptions.","zh":"它適合用於解釋和描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"waffles","meaning":"窩夫","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup is often poured onto waffles.","zh":"楓糖漿常被倒在窩夫上。"},{"en":"Waffles are crisp, patterned cakes usually eaten for breakfast or dessert.","zh":"waffles 指通常作早餐或甜品食用、有格仔圖案的鬆脆糕點。"},{"en":"A hot waffle with butter and maple syrup is a popular sweet dish.","zh":"加牛油和楓糖漿的熱窩夫是一道受歡迎的甜食。"},{"en":"The square holes in waffles can hold syrup well.","zh":"窩夫上的方格凹位可以很好地盛住糖漿。"},{"en":"This word names a common food that is often served with syrup.","zh":"這個字指出常與糖漿一起食用的食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ice cream","meaning":"雪糕","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup can be poured onto ice cream.","zh":"楓糖漿可以被倒在雪糕上。"},{"en":"Ice cream is a cold, sweet dessert made from milk, cream, sugar, or similar ingredients.","zh":"ice cream 指由牛奶、忌廉、糖或類似材料製成的冰凍甜品。"},{"en":"Vanilla ice cream can taste richer when maple syrup is added.","zh":"加入楓糖漿後，雲呢拿雪糕味道可以更濃郁。"},{"en":"Cold desserts and sweet syrup create a strong contrast in temperature and texture.","zh":"冰凍甜品和甜糖漿在溫度和質感上形成強烈對比。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common dessert.","zh":"這個短語指出常見甜品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be used in","meaning":"被用於……","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup can be used in the baking of cakes and pastries.","zh":"楓糖漿可以被用於烘焙蛋糕和酥皮糕點。"},{"en":"Be used in means be included as part of a process, recipe, or activity.","zh":"be used in 指被包括在某個過程、食譜或活動中。"},{"en":"Chocolate can be used in cakes, biscuits, and drinks.","zh":"朱古力可以被用於蛋糕、餅乾和飲品中。"},{"en":"When an ingredient is used in baking, it affects flavour, colour, or texture.","zh":"當一種材料被用於烘焙，它會影響味道、顏色或質感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical use inside a process.","zh":"這個短語描述在過程中的實際用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"baking of cakes and pastries","meaning":"烘焙蛋糕和酥皮糕點","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup can be used in the baking of cakes and pastries.","zh":"楓糖漿可以用於烘焙蛋糕和酥皮糕點。"},{"en":"The baking of cakes and pastries means making sweet baked foods in an oven.","zh":"baking of cakes and pastries 指在焗爐中製作甜味烘焙食品。"},{"en":"Sugar, flour, butter, and eggs are often used in the baking of cakes and pastries.","zh":"糖、麵粉、牛油和雞蛋常用於烘焙蛋糕和酥皮糕點。"},{"en":"Maple syrup can add sweetness and flavour to baked goods.","zh":"楓糖漿可以為烘焙食品增加甜味和風味。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cooking process involving desserts and bakery items.","zh":"這個短語描述涉及甜品和烘焙食品的烹調過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pastries","meaning":"酥皮糕點","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup can be used in cakes and pastries.","zh":"楓糖漿可以用於蛋糕和酥皮糕點。"},{"en":"Pastries are baked foods made with dough, often sweet and sometimes filled.","zh":"pastries 指以麵糰製成的烘焙食品，常帶甜味，有時有餡料。"},{"en":"Croissants, fruit tarts, and Danish pastries are common examples.","zh":"牛角包、水果撻和丹麥酥都是常見例子。"},{"en":"Pastries can be flavoured with syrup, fruit, cream, or chocolate.","zh":"酥皮糕點可以用糖漿、水果、忌廉或朱古力調味。"},{"en":"This word describes a category of baked goods.","zh":"這個字描述一類烘焙食品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"contain no preservatives","meaning":"不含防腐劑","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup contains no preservatives.","zh":"楓糖漿不含防腐劑。"},{"en":"Contain no preservatives means have no added chemicals used to stop food from spoiling.","zh":"contain no preservatives 指沒有加入用來防止食物變壞的化學物。"},{"en":"Some natural juices contain no preservatives and must be kept cold.","zh":"有些天然果汁不含防腐劑，必須冷藏。"},{"en":"People may prefer foods with no preservatives because they seem less processed.","zh":"人們可能較喜歡不含防腐劑的食物，因為它們看起來較少加工。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what is not included in a food product.","zh":"這個短語描述食品中沒有包含甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"added ingredients","meaning":"添加成分","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup contains no added ingredients.","zh":"楓糖漿不含添加成分。"},{"en":"Added ingredients are extra substances put into a food product during production.","zh":"added ingredients 指在生產過程中額外加入食品的物質。"},{"en":"A simple yoghurt may have no added ingredients apart from milk and cultures.","zh":"簡單乳酪除了牛奶和菌種外，可能沒有添加成分。"},{"en":"Fewer added ingredients can make a product sound more natural.","zh":"添加成分較少，可以令產品聽起來更天然。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to ingredients that are not naturally part of the original food.","zh":"這個短語指原本不屬於食物本身的額外材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"provide a healthy alternative to","meaning":"提供較健康的替代品","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup provides a healthy alternative to refined sugar.","zh":"楓糖漿提供精製糖的較健康替代品。"},{"en":"To provide a healthy alternative to something means offer a choice that may be better for health.","zh":"provide a healthy alternative to something 指提供一個可能較有益健康的選擇。"},{"en":"Fruit can provide a healthy alternative to sweets after dinner.","zh":"晚餐後，水果可以提供糖果的較健康替代品。"},{"en":"A healthy alternative still needs to be used sensibly.","zh":"較健康替代品仍需要合理使用。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one option with another less healthy option.","zh":"這個短語把一個選項與另一個較不健康選項作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"refined sugar","meaning":"精製糖","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup can be used as an alternative to refined sugar.","zh":"楓糖漿可以作為精製糖的替代品。"},{"en":"Refined sugar is sugar that has been processed and purified from its natural source.","zh":"refined sugar 指從天然來源加工和提純而成的糖。"},{"en":"White table sugar is a common form of refined sugar.","zh":"白砂糖是常見的精製糖。"},{"en":"Some people use honey or maple syrup instead of refined sugar for flavour.","zh":"有些人因味道而使用蜜糖或楓糖漿代替精製糖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a processed sweetener.","zh":"這個短語描述一種加工甜味劑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"talk a bit about","meaning":"稍為談談……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker talks a bit about the maple tree itself.","zh":"講者稍為談談楓樹本身。"},{"en":"To talk a bit about something means to discuss it briefly, not in full detail.","zh":"talk a bit about something 指簡短談論某事，而不是詳細講解。"},{"en":"A teacher may talk a bit about exam rules before starting the lesson.","zh":"老師可能在開始課堂前稍為談談考試規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when moving to a short explanation.","zh":"轉到簡短解釋時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It sounds conversational and not too formal.","zh":"它聽起來較口語，不太正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"come from","meaning":"來自……","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup comes from the maple tree.","zh":"楓糖漿來自楓樹。"},{"en":"Come from means originate in or be obtained from a particular source.","zh":"come from 指源自或取得自某個特定來源。"},{"en":"Olive oil comes from olives.","zh":"橄欖油來自橄欖。"},{"en":"Knowing where a food comes from helps people understand how it is produced.","zh":"知道食物來自哪裏，有助人理解它如何生產。"},{"en":"This phrase explains origin.","zh":"這個短語解釋來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"species of","meaning":"……的品種","examples":[{"en":"There are many species of maple tree.","zh":"楓樹有許多品種。"},{"en":"Species of something means different biological kinds within a larger group.","zh":"species of something 指較大類別中的不同生物種類。"},{"en":"There are many species of birds in a forest.","zh":"森林中有許多鳥類品種。"},{"en":"Different species of maple tree may grow better in different climates.","zh":"不同楓樹品種可能在不同氣候中生長得較好。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in biology and nature descriptions.","zh":"這個短語用於生物學和自然描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"grow without fertiliser","meaning":"無須施肥也能生長","examples":[{"en":"Maple trees can grow without fertiliser in suitable areas.","zh":"楓樹在合適地區無須施肥也能生長。"},{"en":"Grow without fertiliser means grow without extra nutrients being added to the soil.","zh":"grow without fertiliser 指泥土不需額外添加營養也能生長。"},{"en":"Some wild plants can grow without fertiliser because the soil already provides enough nutrients.","zh":"有些野生植物無須施肥也能生長，因為泥土已有足夠養分。"},{"en":"If a tree grows without fertiliser, it needs the right natural conditions.","zh":"如果一棵樹無須施肥也能生長，它需要合適的自然條件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural growth without added plant food.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有額外植物養分下的自然生長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"areas where","meaning":"……的地區","examples":[{"en":"Maple trees grow in areas where there is plenty of moisture in the soil.","zh":"楓樹生長在泥土中有充足水分的地區。"},{"en":"Areas where means places in which a certain condition exists.","zh":"areas where 指某種條件存在的地方。"},{"en":"Rice grows well in areas where there is enough water.","zh":"稻米在有足夠水分的地區生長良好。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a place with the condition found there.","zh":"這個短語把地方與當地條件連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing habitats or suitable environments.","zh":"描述棲息地或合適環境時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"plenty of moisture","meaning":"充足水分","examples":[{"en":"Maple trees need plenty of moisture in the soil.","zh":"楓樹需要泥土中有充足水分。"},{"en":"Plenty of moisture means a large amount of water or dampness.","zh":"plenty of moisture 指大量水分或濕氣。"},{"en":"Ferns often grow well where there is plenty of moisture.","zh":"蕨類植物通常在有充足水分的地方生長良好。"},{"en":"Without enough moisture, trees may dry out and fail to grow properly.","zh":"如果沒有足夠水分，樹木可能乾枯並無法正常生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important water condition for plants.","zh":"這個短語描述植物的重要水分條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the soil","meaning":"在泥土中","examples":[{"en":"Maple trees need moisture in the soil.","zh":"楓樹需要泥土中有水分。"},{"en":"In the soil means inside the earth where plant roots grow.","zh":"in the soil 指在植物根部生長的泥土裏。"},{"en":"Seeds need water and nutrients in the soil to begin growing.","zh":"種子需要泥土中的水分和養分才能開始生長。"},{"en":"The condition of water in the soil affects how well plants survive.","zh":"泥土中的水分狀況會影響植物生存得多好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the underground growing environment.","zh":"這個短語描述地下生長環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"important criterion","meaning":"重要條件","examples":[{"en":"Sun exposure is an important criterion for maple trees.","zh":"日照是楓樹的重要條件。"},{"en":"An important criterion is a key condition used to judge whether something is suitable.","zh":"important criterion 指用來判斷某事是否合適的關鍵條件。"},{"en":"Safety is an important criterion when choosing a school trip location.","zh":"選擇學校旅行地點時，安全是一個重要條件。"},{"en":"If an important criterion is not met, the plan may not work.","zh":"如果重要條件未被滿足，計劃可能行不通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major standard or requirement.","zh":"這個短語描述主要標準或要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be fulfilled","meaning":"被滿足","examples":[{"en":"The criterion must be fulfilled before maple trees can grow well.","zh":"這個條件必須被滿足，楓樹才能生長良好。"},{"en":"Be fulfilled means be satisfied, met, or achieved.","zh":"be fulfilled 指被滿足、達到或實現。"},{"en":"All entry requirements must be fulfilled before a student can join the course.","zh":"所有入學要求必須被滿足，學生才能加入課程。"},{"en":"When a condition is fulfilled, the next step becomes possible.","zh":"當條件被滿足，下一步才變得可能。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used with requirements or criteria.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常與要求或準則一起使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"full or partial sun exposure","meaning":"全日照或部分日照","examples":[{"en":"Maple trees need full or partial sun exposure during the day.","zh":"楓樹在日間需要全日照或部分日照。"},{"en":"Full or partial sun exposure means receiving either direct sunlight for much of the day or some sunlight for part of the day.","zh":"full or partial sun exposure 指一天中大部分時間接受直射陽光，或部分時間接受陽光。"},{"en":"Some garden plants need full sun, while others grow well with partial sun exposure.","zh":"有些園藝植物需要全日照，而另一些在部分日照下也生長良好。"},{"en":"Sun exposure helps trees make food and grow strongly.","zh":"日照幫助樹木製造養分並強健生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how much sunlight a plant receives.","zh":"這個短語描述植物接受多少陽光。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"during the day","meaning":"在日間","examples":[{"en":"Maple trees need sun exposure during the day.","zh":"楓樹在日間需要日照。"},{"en":"During the day means in the daytime, not at night.","zh":"during the day 指在白天，而不是晚上。"},{"en":"Plants receive sunlight during the day and rest from strong light at night.","zh":"植物在日間接受陽光，晚上則避開強光休息。"},{"en":"Temperature during the day may be very different from temperature at night.","zh":"日間溫度可能與夜間溫度非常不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the daylight period.","zh":"這個短語描述有日光的時段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cool nights","meaning":"涼爽的夜晚","examples":[{"en":"Maple trees also need very cool nights.","zh":"楓樹也需要非常涼爽的夜晚。"},{"en":"Cool nights are nights with low but not necessarily freezing temperatures.","zh":"cool nights 指氣溫較低但不一定結冰的夜晚。"},{"en":"Some fruit trees need cool nights to develop properly.","zh":"有些果樹需要涼爽夜晚才能正常發育。"},{"en":"In maple syrup production, the difference between cool nights and warmer days is important.","zh":"在楓糖漿生產中，涼爽夜晚和較暖日間之間的差異很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a night-time temperature condition.","zh":"這個短語描述夜間溫度條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"talk more about","meaning":"多談……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker will talk more about temperature later.","zh":"講者稍後會多談溫度。"},{"en":"To talk more about something means discuss it in greater detail later or for a longer time.","zh":"talk more about something 指稍後或更長時間詳細討論某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “We will talk more about exam technique next week.”","zh":"老師可能說：「我們下星期會多談考試技巧。」"},{"en":"This phrase tells listeners that a topic will return later.","zh":"這個短語告訴聽者某題目稍後會再出現。"},{"en":"It helps organise a presentation.","zh":"它有助組織簡報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"certain parts of the world","meaning":"世界上某些地區","examples":[{"en":"Only certain parts of the world provide the right conditions.","zh":"只有世界上某些地區提供合適條件。"},{"en":"Certain parts of the world means particular regions, not everywhere.","zh":"certain parts of the world 指特定地區，而不是所有地方。"},{"en":"Cocoa trees grow well only in certain parts of the world.","zh":"可可樹只在世界上某些地區生長良好。"},{"en":"Climate and soil can make some places suitable and others unsuitable.","zh":"氣候和泥土會令某些地方合適，而其他地方不合適。"},{"en":"This phrase limits a statement to specific geographical areas.","zh":"這個短語把說法限制在特定地理區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"provide all these conditions","meaning":"提供所有這些條件","examples":[{"en":"Canada provides all the conditions maple trees need.","zh":"加拿大提供楓樹所需的所有條件。"},{"en":"Provide all these conditions means have every necessary feature or requirement.","zh":"provide all these conditions 指具備所有必要特徵或要求。"},{"en":"A good greenhouse can provide all the conditions young plants need.","zh":"好溫室可以提供幼苗所需的所有條件。"},{"en":"If a place provides all the conditions, plants can grow naturally and successfully.","zh":"如果一個地方提供所有條件，植物就能自然並成功地生長。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a location is suitable.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某地合適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"by that, I mean","meaning":"我所指的是……","examples":[{"en":"By Canada, the speaker means all parts of Canada.","zh":"講者說加拿大時，所指的是加拿大所有地區。"},{"en":"By that, I mean is used to clarify exactly what the speaker means.","zh":"by that, I mean 用來澄清說話者確切意思。"},{"en":"By “early”, I mean before 7 a.m., not before lunch.","zh":"我說「早」，指的是早上7時前，而不是午飯前。"},{"en":"This phrase prevents misunderstanding by defining a word or idea more clearly.","zh":"這個短語透過更清楚界定詞語或想法來避免誤解。"},{"en":"It is useful when a term could be interpreted in more than one way.","zh":"當一個詞可能有多種理解時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"north-eastern states","meaning":"東北部各州","examples":[{"en":"Maple trees also grow in the north-eastern states of North America.","zh":"楓樹也生長在北美洲東北部各州。"},{"en":"North-eastern states are states located in the north-east part of a country or region.","zh":"north-eastern states 指位於一個國家或地區東北部的州份。"},{"en":"The north-eastern states often have colder winters than southern states.","zh":"東北部各州的冬天通常比南部州份更寒冷。"},{"en":"Location affects climate, and climate affects whether maple trees can grow well.","zh":"位置影響氣候，而氣候影響楓樹是否能良好生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a regional area by direction.","zh":"這個短語按方向描述區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"North America","meaning":"北美洲","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup is produced in Canada and parts of North America.","zh":"楓糖漿在加拿大和北美洲部分地區生產。"},{"en":"North America is the continent that includes Canada, the United States, Mexico, and other regions.","zh":"North America 指包括加拿大、美國、墨西哥及其他地區的大洲。"},{"en":"Maple syrup is strongly connected with the cooler parts of North America.","zh":"楓糖漿與北美洲較寒冷地區有密切關係。"},{"en":"When a food is linked to a region, its production often depends on local climate.","zh":"當一種食物與某地區相關，其生產通常取決於當地氣候。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major geographical area.","zh":"這個短語指出一個主要地理區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"suit something perfectly","meaning":"非常適合……","examples":[{"en":"The climate suits the trees perfectly.","zh":"這種氣候非常適合楓樹。"},{"en":"Suit something perfectly means be exactly right or very suitable for it.","zh":"suit something perfectly 指完全合適或非常適合某物。"},{"en":"A cool, quiet room may suit studying perfectly.","zh":"涼爽安靜的房間可能非常適合溫習。"},{"en":"If the climate suits a tree perfectly, the tree can grow strongly and naturally.","zh":"如果氣候非常適合一棵樹，它就能強健自然地生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an excellent match between condition and need.","zh":"這個短語描述條件與需要之間的極佳配合。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"over two-thirds of","meaning":"超過三分之二","examples":[{"en":"Canada produces over two-thirds of the world’s maple syrup.","zh":"加拿大生產全球超過三分之二的楓糖漿。"},{"en":"Over two-thirds of means more than two out of three parts of a whole.","zh":"over two-thirds of 指整體中超過三份之二。"},{"en":"Over two-thirds of the class chose science as their favourite subject.","zh":"班中超過三分之二學生選擇科學為最喜歡科目。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a very large share or majority.","zh":"這個短語顯示非常大的比例或多數。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing proportions.","zh":"描述比例時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"five-pointed maple leaf","meaning":"五角楓葉","examples":[{"en":"The five-pointed maple leaf is a Canadian symbol.","zh":"五角楓葉是加拿大象徵。"},{"en":"A five-pointed maple leaf is a maple leaf shape with five main points or lobes.","zh":"five-pointed maple leaf 指有五個主要尖端或葉裂的楓葉形狀。"},{"en":"Many people recognise the five-pointed maple leaf from the Canadian flag.","zh":"許多人從加拿大國旗上認得五角楓葉。"},{"en":"A simple leaf shape can become a strong national image.","zh":"簡單葉子形狀可以成為強烈國家形象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the famous maple-leaf symbol.","zh":"這個短語描述著名楓葉符號。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Canadian symbol","meaning":"加拿大象徵","examples":[{"en":"The maple leaf is a Canadian symbol.","zh":"楓葉是加拿大象徵。"},{"en":"A Canadian symbol is an image or object strongly associated with Canada.","zh":"Canadian symbol 指與加拿大密切相關的圖像或物件。"},{"en":"The maple leaf is used as a Canadian symbol on flags, logos, and souvenirs.","zh":"楓葉作為加拿大象徵，用於國旗、標誌和紀念品上。"},{"en":"National symbols help people recognise a country quickly.","zh":"國家象徵幫助人快速認出一個國家。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something representing Canada.","zh":"這個短語描述代表加拿大的事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"feature on","meaning":"出現在……上","examples":[{"en":"The maple leaf has featured on the Canadian flag since 1964.","zh":"楓葉自1964年起出現在加拿大國旗上。"},{"en":"Feature on means appear as an important image or part of something.","zh":"feature on 指作為重要圖像或部分出現在某物上。"},{"en":"A school logo may feature on uniforms and notebooks.","zh":"學校標誌可能出現在校服和筆記簿上。"},{"en":"If a symbol features on a flag, it is part of national identity.","zh":"如果符號出現在國旗上，它就是國家身份的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible inclusion on a surface or object.","zh":"這個短語描述在某表面或物件上可見地出現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"long before","meaning":"早在……之前","examples":[{"en":"Indigenous communities produced maple sugar long before Europeans arrived.","zh":"原住民社群早在歐洲人到來之前已生產楓糖。"},{"en":"Long before means a long time earlier than another event.","zh":"long before 指比另一事件早很多時間。"},{"en":"People used herbal remedies long before modern medicine developed.","zh":"早在現代醫學發展之前，人們已使用草藥療法。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that something has a much older history.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示某事有更悠久歷史。"},{"en":"It compares two points in time.","zh":"它比較兩個時間點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"settle in","meaning":"定居於……","examples":[{"en":"Europeans later settled in these parts of the world.","zh":"歐洲人後來定居於世界上的這些地區。"},{"en":"To settle in a place means to move there and begin living there permanently or for a long time.","zh":"settle in a place 指搬到某地並開始永久或長期居住。"},{"en":"Families may settle in a new town after finding work there.","zh":"家庭找到工作後，可能定居於新城鎮。"},{"en":"When people settle in a region, they may learn from or affect local communities.","zh":"當人們定居於某地區，他們可能向本地社群學習或影響本地社群。"},{"en":"This phrase describes establishing a home in a place.","zh":"這個短語描述在某地建立居所。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"indigenous communities","meaning":"原住民社群","examples":[{"en":"Indigenous communities produced maple sugar before Europeans arrived.","zh":"原住民社群在歐洲人到來前已生產楓糖。"},{"en":"Indigenous communities are groups of people originally living in a place before later settlers arrived.","zh":"indigenous communities 指後來定居者到來前原本生活在某地的群體。"},{"en":"Indigenous communities often have deep knowledge of local plants and seasons.","zh":"原住民社群常對本地植物和季節有深厚知識。"},{"en":"Their traditional methods can show how natural resources were used carefully.","zh":"他們的傳統方法可以顯示自然資源如何被小心使用。"},{"en":"This phrase should be used respectfully for original peoples and cultures.","zh":"這個短語應尊重地用於原居民和文化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"maple sugar","meaning":"楓糖","examples":[{"en":"Indigenous communities had started producing maple sugar.","zh":"原住民社群已開始生產楓糖。"},{"en":"Maple sugar is sugar made from maple sap after much of the water has been removed.","zh":"maple sugar 指從楓樹樹液中去除大量水分後製成的糖。"},{"en":"Before bottles of syrup were common, maple sugar was easier to store.","zh":"在瓶裝糖漿普及前，楓糖較容易儲存。"},{"en":"Maple sugar could be used to sweeten food and drinks.","zh":"楓糖可以用來為食物和飲品增甜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a solid sweet product made from maple sap.","zh":"這個短語描述由楓樹樹液製成的固體甜味產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bore holes in","meaning":"在……鑽孔","examples":[{"en":"They bored holes in the trunks of maple trees.","zh":"他們在楓樹樹幹鑽孔。"},{"en":"To bore holes in something means to drill or make holes in it.","zh":"bore holes in something 指在某物上鑽出或製造孔洞。"},{"en":"Workers may bore holes in wood before inserting screws.","zh":"工人可能先在木材上鑽孔，再插入螺絲。"},{"en":"In maple syrup production, holes are bored so sap can flow out.","zh":"在楓糖漿生產中，鑽孔是為了讓樹液流出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making holes using tools.","zh":"這個短語描述用工具製造孔洞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"trunks of maple trees","meaning":"楓樹樹幹","examples":[{"en":"They collected sap from the trunks of maple trees.","zh":"他們從楓樹樹幹收集樹液。"},{"en":"The trunks of maple trees are the main wooden stems that support the branches and leaves.","zh":"trunks of maple trees 指支撐樹枝和葉子的主要木質莖部。"},{"en":"Sap is collected from the trunk because the fluid moves through the tree.","zh":"人們從樹幹收集樹液，因為液體會在樹內流動。"},{"en":"A mature maple tree trunk must be wide enough before it can be tapped.","zh":"成熟楓樹的樹幹必須足夠粗，才能被取樹液。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main body of the tree.","zh":"這個短語描述樹木的主體部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"containers made of","meaning":"由……製成的容器","examples":[{"en":"They used containers made of tree bark.","zh":"他們使用由樹皮製成的容器。"},{"en":"Containers made of a material are objects formed from that material and used to hold things.","zh":"containers made of a material 指由某材料形成、用來盛載東西的物件。"},{"en":"Picnic baskets may be containers made of woven reeds.","zh":"野餐籃可能是由編織蘆葦製成的容器。"},{"en":"The material of a container affects how strong, light, or waterproof it is.","zh":"容器的材料會影響它有多堅固、輕便或防水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what a container is made from.","zh":"這個短語描述容器由甚麼製成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tree bark","meaning":"樹皮","examples":[{"en":"They used containers made of tree bark to collect sap.","zh":"他們使用由樹皮製成的容器來收集樹液。"},{"en":"Tree bark is the outer protective layer of a tree trunk or branch.","zh":"tree bark 指樹幹或樹枝外層的保護層。"},{"en":"Some traditional containers, medicines, or crafts have used tree bark.","zh":"有些傳統容器、藥物或手工藝品曾使用樹皮。"},{"en":"Bark can protect the tree, but people have also used it as a natural material.","zh":"樹皮可以保護樹木，但人們也把它用作天然材料。"},{"en":"This phrase names the outside covering of a tree.","zh":"這個短語指出樹木外層覆蓋物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"collect the liquid sap","meaning":"收集液態樹液","examples":[{"en":"Indigenous communities collected the liquid sap as it poured out.","zh":"原住民社群在樹液流出時收集液態樹液。"},{"en":"To collect the liquid sap means to gather the flowing tree fluid into a container.","zh":"collect the liquid sap 指把流出的樹液收集到容器中。"},{"en":"Workers collect the liquid sap from tapped trees during the syrup season.","zh":"工人在糖漿季節從已鑽孔的樹上收集液態樹液。"},{"en":"Sap must be collected before it can be boiled into syrup or sugar.","zh":"樹液必須先被收集，才能煮成糖漿或糖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first practical step in maple production.","zh":"這個短語描述楓糖生產的第一個實際步驟。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pour out","meaning":"流出","examples":[{"en":"The sap poured out of the holes in the trunks.","zh":"樹液從樹幹上的孔流出。"},{"en":"Pour out means flow out in a steady stream.","zh":"pour out 指以穩定水流般流出。"},{"en":"Water may pour out of a broken pipe.","zh":"水可能從破裂水管中流出。"},{"en":"When sap pours out of a tree, it can be caught in a container.","zh":"當樹液從樹中流出，可以用容器接住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes liquid leaving an opening.","zh":"這個短語描述液體從開口離開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for any length of time","meaning":"長時間","examples":[{"en":"They were unable to keep the liquid for any length of time.","zh":"他們無法長時間保存這種液體。"},{"en":"For any length of time means for a long or noticeable period.","zh":"for any length of time 指一段較長或明顯的時間。"},{"en":"Fresh milk cannot be left in the sun for any length of time.","zh":"新鮮牛奶不能在陽光下放置長時間。"},{"en":"If food cannot be kept for any length of time, it must be used quickly.","zh":"如果食物不能長時間保存，就必須快速使用。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that storage time is very limited.","zh":"這個短語強調儲存時間非常有限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"storage facilities","meaning":"儲存設施","examples":[{"en":"They did not have storage facilities in those days.","zh":"他們當時沒有儲存設施。"},{"en":"Storage facilities are places, tools, or systems used to keep things safely for later use.","zh":"storage facilities 指用來安全保存東西以供日後使用的地方、工具或系統。"},{"en":"A school kitchen needs storage facilities for food, plates, and cleaning products.","zh":"學校廚房需要儲存設施來存放食物、碟子和清潔用品。"},{"en":"Without storage facilities, liquid food may spoil quickly.","zh":"沒有儲存設施，液態食物可能很快變壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised spaces or equipment for keeping things.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的保存空間或設備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in those days","meaning":"在當時","examples":[{"en":"People did not have storage facilities in those days.","zh":"人們在當時沒有儲存設施。"},{"en":"In those days means at that time in the past.","zh":"in those days 指在過去那個時候。"},{"en":"In those days, people often travelled by horse instead of car.","zh":"在當時，人們常騎馬而不是坐車出行。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare past conditions with modern ones.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較過去情況與現代情況。"},{"en":"It is often used when explaining history or old habits.","zh":"解釋歷史或舊習慣時常會使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"boil the liquid","meaning":"把液體煮沸","examples":[{"en":"They boiled the liquid by placing hot rocks into the sap.","zh":"他們透過把熱石放入樹液中把液體煮沸。"},{"en":"To boil the liquid means to heat it until it reaches boiling point and bubbles strongly.","zh":"boil the liquid 指把液體加熱至沸點，令其猛烈起泡。"},{"en":"Cooks boil water before making pasta.","zh":"廚師煮意粉前會先把水煮沸。"},{"en":"Boiling sap removes water and helps make it thicker and sweeter.","zh":"煮沸樹液會去除水分，並令它更濃稠、更甜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes heating a liquid intensely.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈加熱液體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"place something into","meaning":"把……放入……","examples":[{"en":"They placed hot pieces of rock into the sap.","zh":"他們把熱石塊放入樹液中。"},{"en":"To place something into something else means to put it carefully inside.","zh":"place something into something else 指小心地把某物放進另一物之中。"},{"en":"A teacher may place a thermometer into warm water during a science experiment.","zh":"老師可能在科學實驗中把溫度計放入溫水。"},{"en":"Placing hot rocks into sap was a way to transfer heat to the liquid.","zh":"把熱石放入樹液，是把熱力傳到液體中的方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes putting one object inside another substance or container.","zh":"這個短語描述把一件物件放進另一物質或容器中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pieces of rock","meaning":"石塊","examples":[{"en":"They used pieces of rock to heat the sap.","zh":"他們使用石塊來加熱樹液。"},{"en":"Pieces of rock are small or broken parts of stone.","zh":"pieces of rock 指小塊或碎開的石頭。"},{"en":"Campers may place pieces of rock around a fire to mark its edge.","zh":"露營者可能把石塊放在火堆周圍，以標示邊界。"},{"en":"In older methods, heated rocks could be used when metal pots were not available.","zh":"在較古老方法中，當沒有金屬鍋時，加熱石塊可以被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes separate chunks of stone.","zh":"這個短語描述分開的小石頭。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"scorching hot","meaning":"滾燙的","examples":[{"en":"The rocks had become scorching hot from the sun.","zh":"石塊被太陽曬得滾燙。"},{"en":"Scorching hot means extremely hot, almost burning.","zh":"scorching hot 指極熱，幾乎會燙傷。"},{"en":"Sand on a beach can become scorching hot at midday.","zh":"海灘上的沙在中午可以變得滾燙。"},{"en":"If something is scorching hot, people must handle it carefully.","zh":"如果某物滾燙，人們必須小心處理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intense heat.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈熱度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"from the sun","meaning":"被太陽曬熱","examples":[{"en":"The rocks became hot from the sun.","zh":"石塊被太陽曬熱。"},{"en":"From the sun means because of heat or light produced by the sun.","zh":"from the sun 指因太陽產生的熱力或光線而成。"},{"en":"Clothes dry quickly from the sun on a clear day.","zh":"晴天時，衣服會因太陽而很快乾。"},{"en":"Sunlight can heat stones, water, and soil over time.","zh":"陽光可以隨時間加熱石頭、水和泥土。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the natural source of heat or light.","zh":"這個短語解釋熱力或光線的自然來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"turn into","meaning":"變成","examples":[{"en":"The sap turned into sugar after being boiled.","zh":"樹液煮沸後變成糖。"},{"en":"Turn into means change from one form or state into another.","zh":"turn into 指由一種形式或狀態變成另一種。"},{"en":"Water turns into steam when it boils.","zh":"水煮沸時會變成蒸汽。"},{"en":"Sap can turn into syrup or sugar when water is removed.","zh":"當水分被去除，樹液可以變成糖漿或糖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transformation.","zh":"這個短語描述轉變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be able to","meaning":"能夠","examples":[{"en":"They were then able to use the sugar to sweeten food.","zh":"然後他們能夠用糖為食物增甜。"},{"en":"Be able to means have the ability, chance, or permission to do something.","zh":"be able to 指有能力、機會或許可做某事。"},{"en":"After learning the chords, a student is able to play a simple song.","zh":"學會和弦後，學生能夠彈奏簡單歌曲。"},{"en":"Turning sap into sugar meant people were able to store and use it more easily.","zh":"把樹液變成糖，意味着人們能夠更容易保存和使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability or possibility.","zh":"這個短語描述能力或可能性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sweeten food and drinks","meaning":"為食物和飲品增甜","examples":[{"en":"Maple sugar was used to sweeten food and drinks.","zh":"楓糖被用來為食物和飲品增甜。"},{"en":"To sweeten food and drinks means to make them taste sweeter.","zh":"sweeten food and drinks 指令食物和飲品味道更甜。"},{"en":"People may use honey to sweeten tea or yoghurt.","zh":"人們可能用蜜糖為茶或乳酪增甜。"},{"en":"Sweetening food can improve flavour, but too much sweetness may be unhealthy.","zh":"為食物增甜可以改善味道，但太甜可能不健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding sweetness to what people eat or drink.","zh":"這個短語描述為吃喝的東西加入甜味。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"since that time","meaning":"自那時起","examples":[{"en":"Since that time, improvements have been made to the process.","zh":"自那時起，這個過程已有改良。"},{"en":"Since that time means from that past moment until now.","zh":"since that time 指從過去那一刻直到現在。"},{"en":"The school opened in 1990, and since that time it has added many new buildings.","zh":"學校於1990年開辦，自那時起已增建許多新大樓。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a past event with later changes.","zh":"這個短語把過去事件與之後變化連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing historical development.","zh":"描述歷史發展時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"improvements have been made to","meaning":"……已有改良","examples":[{"en":"Improvements have been made to the maple syrup production process.","zh":"楓糖漿生產過程已有改良。"},{"en":"Improvements have been made to something means it has been changed in ways that make it better.","zh":"improvements have been made to something 指某事已被改變並變得更好。"},{"en":"Improvements have been made to the school playground to make it safer.","zh":"學校遊樂場已有改良，以令它更安全。"},{"en":"When improvements are made to a process, it may become faster, cleaner, or more efficient.","zh":"當過程已有改良，它可能變得更快、更乾淨或更有效率。"},{"en":"This phrase describes positive changes.","zh":"這個短語描述正面改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the process","meaning":"製作過程","examples":[{"en":"The process of making maple syrup has changed very little overall.","zh":"製作楓糖漿的過程整體變化很小。"},{"en":"The process means the series of steps used to do or make something.","zh":"process 指完成或製作某事的一系列步驟。"},{"en":"The process of baking bread includes mixing, kneading, rising, and baking.","zh":"烘焙麵包的過程包括混合、揉麵、發酵和烘焙。"},{"en":"Understanding the process helps people see how the final product is made.","zh":"理解過程有助人看見最終產品如何製成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes step-by-step production.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步生產。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"change very little overall","meaning":"整體變化很小","examples":[{"en":"The process has changed very little overall.","zh":"這個過程整體變化很小。"},{"en":"Change very little overall means remain mostly the same, even if some details have improved.","zh":"change very little overall 指大部分保持相同，即使某些細節已有改良。"},{"en":"The rules of chess have changed very little overall over many years.","zh":"多年來，國際象棋規則整體變化很小。"},{"en":"A process can use modern tools but still follow the same basic steps.","zh":"一個過程可以使用現代工具，但仍跟隨相同基本步驟。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong continuity.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈延續性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"maple syrup production","meaning":"楓糖漿生產","examples":[{"en":"The speaker explains maple syrup production today.","zh":"講者解釋現今的楓糖漿生產。"},{"en":"Maple syrup production is the process of collecting sap and turning it into syrup.","zh":"maple syrup production 指收集樹液並把它變成糖漿的過程。"},{"en":"Maple syrup production begins with mature maple trees and suitable weather.","zh":"楓糖漿生產由成熟楓樹和合適天氣開始。"},{"en":"Producers must collect, boil, filter, and package the syrup carefully.","zh":"生產者必須小心收集、煮沸、過濾和包裝糖漿。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the whole industry or process of making maple syrup.","zh":"這個短語描述製作楓糖漿的整個行業或過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"valuable resource","meaning":"寶貴資源","examples":[{"en":"Maple forests are a valuable resource in many communities.","zh":"楓樹林是許多社區的寶貴資源。"},{"en":"A valuable resource is something useful, important, and worth protecting.","zh":"valuable resource 指有用、重要並值得保護的東西。"},{"en":"Clean water is a valuable resource for every town.","zh":"清潔食水是每個城鎮的寶貴資源。"},{"en":"Maple forests are valuable because they provide sap, jobs, tourism, and cultural identity.","zh":"楓樹林很寶貴，因為它們提供樹液、工作、旅遊和文化身份。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that brings real benefit.","zh":"這個短語描述能帶來實際好處的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Canadian and North American communities","meaning":"加拿大及北美社區","examples":[{"en":"Maple forests are important to many Canadian and North American communities.","zh":"楓樹林對許多加拿大及北美社區很重要。"},{"en":"Canadian and North American communities are groups of people living in Canada and other parts of North America.","zh":"Canadian and North American communities 指生活在加拿大及北美其他地區的人群。"},{"en":"Some communities depend on maple syrup production for seasonal work and income.","zh":"有些社區依靠楓糖漿生產獲得季節性工作和收入。"},{"en":"A natural resource can become part of local culture and economy.","zh":"自然資源可以成為本地文化和經濟的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the communities connected with maple forests.","zh":"這個短語指出與楓樹林相關的社區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be well looked after","meaning":"得到良好照料","examples":[{"en":"The maple trees have to be well looked after.","zh":"楓樹必須得到良好照料。"},{"en":"Be well looked after means receive careful care, protection, and maintenance.","zh":"be well looked after 指得到仔細照顧、保護和保養。"},{"en":"School gardens must be well looked after if plants are to survive.","zh":"如果植物要生存，學校花園必須得到良好照料。"},{"en":"Maple trees need protection because syrup production depends on healthy trees.","zh":"楓樹需要保護，因為糖漿生產依賴健康樹木。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful long-term care.","zh":"這個短語描述長期而仔細的照顧。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make syrup","meaning":"製作糖漿","examples":[{"en":"The trees cannot be used to make syrup until they are mature.","zh":"樹木未成熟前不能用來製作糖漿。"},{"en":"To make syrup means to produce a thick sweet liquid by processing sap or sugar.","zh":"make syrup 指透過處理樹液或糖來生產濃稠甜液體。"},{"en":"Producers make syrup by boiling maple sap until much of the water evaporates.","zh":"生產者透過煮沸楓樹樹液，直到大量水分蒸發來製作糖漿。"},{"en":"Young trees should not be used to make syrup because they need time to grow.","zh":"幼樹不應用來製作糖漿，因為它們需要時間成長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing sweet syrup.","zh":"這個短語描述生產甜糖漿。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reach a diameter of","meaning":"達到……直徑","examples":[{"en":"The trunks must reach a diameter of around 25 centimetres.","zh":"樹幹必須達到約25厘米直徑。"},{"en":"Reach a diameter of means grow until the width across the trunk is a certain measurement.","zh":"reach a diameter of 指生長到橫跨樹幹的寬度達某個量度。"},{"en":"A tree may need many years to reach a diameter suitable for tapping.","zh":"樹可能需要多年才能達到適合取樹液的直徑。"},{"en":"Measuring diameter helps workers decide whether a tree is mature enough.","zh":"量度直徑幫助工人判斷樹是否足夠成熟。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching a required size.","zh":"這個短語描述達到所需大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"around 25 centimetres","meaning":"約25厘米","examples":[{"en":"The trunk must reach a diameter of around 25 centimetres.","zh":"樹幹必須達到約25厘米直徑。"},{"en":"Around 25 centimetres means approximately 25 centimetres, not exactly.","zh":"around 25 centimetres 指大約25厘米，不一定完全準確。"},{"en":"A ruler around 25 centimetres long is slightly shorter than a standard 30-centimetre ruler.","zh":"約25厘米長的間尺比標準30厘米間尺略短。"},{"en":"Approximate measurements are often enough when describing natural growth.","zh":"描述自然生長時，約略量度通常已足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an estimated size.","zh":"這個短語給出估計大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"take anything up to","meaning":"可能需要長達……","examples":[{"en":"This can take anything up to 40 years.","zh":"這可能需要長達40年。"},{"en":"Take anything up to a period means may require as long as that maximum time.","zh":"take anything up to a period 指可能需要長達某個最高時間。"},{"en":"Training a doctor can take anything up to ten years or more.","zh":"培訓一名醫生可能需要長達十年或更久。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the process may be very long.","zh":"這個短語強調過程可能很漫長。"},{"en":"It gives a possible upper limit rather than an exact time.","zh":"它給出可能上限，而不是精確時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as I’ve already mentioned","meaning":"正如我已經提過","examples":[{"en":"As I have already mentioned, maple trees need the right conditions.","zh":"正如我已經提過，楓樹需要合適條件。"},{"en":"As I’ve already mentioned is used to refer back to something said earlier.","zh":"as I’ve already mentioned 用來指回較早前說過的內容。"},{"en":"As I’ve already mentioned, regular practice is essential for progress.","zh":"正如我已經提過，定期練習對進步十分重要。"},{"en":"This phrase helps remind listeners of an earlier point.","zh":"這個短語幫助提醒聽眾早前的重點。"},{"en":"It is common in talks and explanations.","zh":"它常見於講座和解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the right conditions","meaning":"合適條件","examples":[{"en":"Maple trees need the right conditions to grow and produce sap.","zh":"楓樹需要合適條件才能生長並產生樹液。"},{"en":"The right conditions are the suitable environment or requirements needed for success.","zh":"right conditions 指成功所需的合適環境或要求。"},{"en":"Seeds need the right conditions, including water, warmth, and soil, to grow.","zh":"種子需要水分、溫暖和泥土等合適條件才能生長。"},{"en":"Without the right conditions, even healthy plants may fail to develop.","zh":"沒有合適條件，即使健康植物也可能無法發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes suitable circumstances.","zh":"這個短語描述合適情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"produce sap","meaning":"產生樹液","examples":[{"en":"Maple trees need the right conditions to produce sap.","zh":"楓樹需要合適條件才能產生樹液。"},{"en":"To produce sap means to create or release the plant fluid inside the tree.","zh":"produce sap 指在樹內製造或釋放植物液。"},{"en":"Trees produce sap as part of their natural movement of water and nutrients.","zh":"樹木產生樹液，是水分和營養物質自然流動的一部分。"},{"en":"In maple syrup production, enough sap must be produced before tapping is worthwhile.","zh":"在楓糖漿生產中，必須產生足夠樹液，取液才值得進行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the tree’s natural production of fluid.","zh":"這個短語描述樹木自然產生液體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"what happens is that","meaning":"情況是……","examples":[{"en":"What happens is that the tree absorbs water during a cold night.","zh":"情況是，樹木在寒冷夜晚從泥土中吸收水分。"},{"en":"What happens is that introduces an explanation of a process or cause.","zh":"what happens is that 用來引出一個過程或原因的解釋。"},{"en":"What happens is that the metal expands when it is heated.","zh":"情況是，金屬受熱時會膨脹。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining science in a conversational way.","zh":"這個短語適合用口語方式解釋科學。"},{"en":"It helps listeners follow the next step in a process.","zh":"它幫助聽者跟上過程中的下一步。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cold night","meaning":"寒冷夜晚","examples":[{"en":"During a cold night, the tree absorbs water from the soil.","zh":"在寒冷夜晚，樹木從泥土中吸收水分。"},{"en":"A cold night is a night when the temperature is low.","zh":"cold night 指氣溫較低的晚上。"},{"en":"Cold nights can affect how water moves inside maple trees.","zh":"寒冷夜晚會影響水分在楓樹內如何流動。"},{"en":"In some plants, cool night-time temperatures are important for growth cycles.","zh":"對某些植物來說，夜間低溫對生長循環很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a temperature condition after sunset.","zh":"這個短語描述日落後的溫度條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"absorb water from","meaning":"從……吸收水分","examples":[{"en":"The tree absorbs water from the soil.","zh":"樹木從泥土中吸收水分。"},{"en":"To absorb water from something means to take water in from that source.","zh":"absorb water from something 指從某來源吸入水分。"},{"en":"Plant roots absorb water from the ground.","zh":"植物根部從地面吸收水分。"},{"en":"A sponge absorbs water from a wet table.","zh":"海綿從濕桌面吸收水分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking in liquid.","zh":"這個短語描述吸入液體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rise through","meaning":"透過……向上移動","examples":[{"en":"Water rises through the tree’s vascular system.","zh":"水分透過樹木的維管系統向上移動。"},{"en":"Rise through means move upward inside or through something.","zh":"rise through 指在某物內部或穿過某物向上移動。"},{"en":"Warm air rises through a building if windows are open.","zh":"如果窗戶打開，暖空氣會透過建築物向上升。"},{"en":"Water rising through a tree helps carry nutrients to upper parts.","zh":"水分在樹內向上移動，有助把營養帶到較高部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upward movement.","zh":"這個短語描述向上移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"vascular system","meaning":"維管系統","examples":[{"en":"Water rises through the tree’s vascular system.","zh":"水分透過樹木的維管系統向上移動。"},{"en":"A vascular system is the network of tubes that carries water and nutrients inside a plant.","zh":"vascular system 指植物內運送水分和營養物質的管道網絡。"},{"en":"In trees, the vascular system helps move liquid between roots, trunk, branches, and leaves.","zh":"在樹木中，維管系統幫助液體在根、樹幹、樹枝和葉子之間移動。"},{"en":"Without this system, a tree could not transport what it needs to grow.","zh":"沒有這個系統，樹木就無法運送生長所需物質。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a plant’s internal transport system.","zh":"這個短語描述植物內部運輸系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"warmer daytime","meaning":"較溫暖的日間","examples":[{"en":"In the warmer daytime, the water is pushed back down.","zh":"在較溫暖的日間，水分被推回下方。"},{"en":"Warmer daytime means the part of the day when temperatures rise above the colder night level.","zh":"warmer daytime 指日間氣溫比寒冷夜晚升高的時段。"},{"en":"Snow may begin to melt in the warmer daytime.","zh":"在較溫暖的日間，雪可能開始融化。"},{"en":"The contrast between cold nights and warmer daytime helps sap move.","zh":"寒冷夜晚與較溫暖日間之間的對比幫助樹液流動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a temperature change during daylight hours.","zh":"這個短語描述白天的溫度變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"change in temperature","meaning":"溫度變化","examples":[{"en":"The change in temperature causes the water to move.","zh":"溫度變化令水分移動。"},{"en":"A change in temperature is a rise or fall in how hot or cold something is.","zh":"change in temperature 指某物冷熱程度上升或下降。"},{"en":"A sudden change in temperature can make glass crack.","zh":"突然的溫度變化會令玻璃裂開。"},{"en":"Temperature changes can affect plants, animals, and materials.","zh":"溫度變化可以影響植物、動物和材料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in heat level.","zh":"這個短語描述熱度水平的轉變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cause something to","meaning":"令……","examples":[{"en":"The change in temperature causes the water to be pushed down.","zh":"溫度變化令水分被推回下方。"},{"en":"Cause something to happen means make it happen.","zh":"cause something to happen 指令某事發生。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can cause rivers to rise quickly.","zh":"大雨可以令河水迅速上升。"},{"en":"In science explanations, this phrase links a cause with a result.","zh":"在科學解釋中，這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"},{"en":"It helps show why a process occurs.","zh":"它有助顯示過程為何發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be pushed back down","meaning":"被推回下方","examples":[{"en":"The water is pushed back down to the bottom of the tree.","zh":"水分被推回樹的底部。"},{"en":"Be pushed back down means be forced to move downward again.","zh":"be pushed back down 指再次被迫向下移動。"},{"en":"Air may be pushed back down by a fan in a ventilation system.","zh":"通風系統中的風扇可能把空氣推回下方。"},{"en":"In maple trees, pressure changes can push water back down through the trunk.","zh":"在楓樹中，壓力變化可以把水分經樹幹推回下方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes downward movement caused by force or pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述由力量或壓力造成的向下移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bottom of the tree","meaning":"樹的底部","examples":[{"en":"The water is pushed back down to the bottom of the tree.","zh":"水分被推回樹的底部。"},{"en":"The bottom of the tree is the lower part near the roots and base of the trunk.","zh":"bottom of the tree 指接近根部和樹幹基部的下方部分。"},{"en":"Leaves and fallen fruit often collect at the bottom of the tree.","zh":"葉子和掉落的果實常積在樹的底部。"},{"en":"In a tree, movement between the top and bottom helps distribute water and nutrients.","zh":"在樹木中，頂部與底部之間的流動有助分配水分和營養。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the lowest part of a tree.","zh":"這個短語描述樹的最低部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"continual movement","meaning":"持續流動","examples":[{"en":"This continual movement leads to the formation of sap.","zh":"這種持續流動促成樹液形成。"},{"en":"Continual movement means repeated or ongoing movement over time.","zh":"continual movement 指隨時間反覆或持續發生的移動。"},{"en":"The continual movement of waves shapes rocks along the coast.","zh":"海浪的持續流動會塑造海岸岩石。"},{"en":"In maple trees, continual movement of water helps create sap for syrup production.","zh":"在楓樹中，水分持續流動有助形成用於製糖漿的樹液。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement that keeps happening.","zh":"這個短語描述不斷發生的移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"up and down","meaning":"上下來回","examples":[{"en":"The water moves up and down inside the tree.","zh":"水分在樹內上下來回移動。"},{"en":"Up and down means moving upward and then downward repeatedly.","zh":"up and down 指反覆向上和向下移動。"},{"en":"A lift moves up and down between floors.","zh":"升降機在樓層之間上下來回移動。"},{"en":"Movement up and down inside a tree can be caused by temperature changes.","zh":"樹內上下來回的移動可以由溫度變化造成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement in two opposite vertical directions.","zh":"這個短語描述兩個相反垂直方向的移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lead to the formation of","meaning":"促成……的形成","examples":[{"en":"The movement leads to the formation of sap.","zh":"這種流動促成樹液的形成。"},{"en":"Lead to the formation of something means cause something to develop or be created.","zh":"lead to the formation of something 指導致某物發展或形成。"},{"en":"Cooling water can lead to the formation of ice.","zh":"水變冷可以促成冰的形成。"},{"en":"In nature, small changes can lead to the formation of larger structures or substances.","zh":"在自然界中，小變化可以促成較大結構或物質形成。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how something comes into being.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物如何產生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"needed for","meaning":"……所需","examples":[{"en":"The sap is needed for maple syrup production.","zh":"樹液是楓糖漿生產所需的。"},{"en":"Needed for something means required in order for that thing to happen.","zh":"needed for something 指為了某事發生而必需。"},{"en":"Flour is needed for making bread.","zh":"麵粉是製作麵包所需的。"},{"en":"Without sap, maple syrup production cannot begin.","zh":"沒有樹液，楓糖漿生產就無法開始。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies an essential requirement.","zh":"這個短語指出必要條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be tapped","meaning":"被取樹液","examples":[{"en":"When the tree is ready, it can be tapped.","zh":"當樹準備好後，它可以被取樹液。"},{"en":"Be tapped means have a hole made in the trunk so sap can be collected.","zh":"be tapped 指在樹幹上開孔，以便收集樹液。"},{"en":"Mature maple trees are tapped during the syrup season.","zh":"成熟楓樹會在糖漿季節被取樹液。"},{"en":"A tree should only be tapped when it is healthy and large enough.","zh":"只有健康且足夠大的樹才應被取樹液。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the method of taking sap from a tree.","zh":"這個短語描述從樹取得樹液的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"involve drilling","meaning":"涉及鑽孔","examples":[{"en":"Tapping involves drilling a small hole into the trunk.","zh":"取樹液涉及在樹幹鑽一個小孔。"},{"en":"Involve drilling means include the action of making a hole with a drill.","zh":"involve drilling 指包括用鑽製造孔洞的動作。"},{"en":"Putting up a shelf may involve drilling holes into a wall.","zh":"安裝層架可能涉及在牆上鑽孔。"},{"en":"In maple tapping, drilling must be done carefully to avoid harming the tree.","zh":"在楓樹取液中，鑽孔必須小心進行，以避免傷害樹木。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a process that includes making a hole.","zh":"這個短語描述包含鑽孔的過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"small hole","meaning":"小孔","examples":[{"en":"A small hole is drilled into the trunk.","zh":"一個小孔被鑽入樹幹。"},{"en":"A small hole is a narrow opening made in a surface.","zh":"small hole 指在表面製造的細小開口。"},{"en":"A tiny hole in a pipe can still let water leak out.","zh":"水管上一個細小孔洞仍可讓水漏出。"},{"en":"In a maple tree, the small hole allows sap to flow into a tube.","zh":"在楓樹中，小孔讓樹液流入管中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a minor opening with a practical purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述有實際用途的小開口。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"insert a tube into","meaning":"把管插入……","examples":[{"en":"Workers insert a tube into the hole.","zh":"工人把管插入孔中。"},{"en":"To insert a tube into something means to put a hollow pipe carefully inside it.","zh":"insert a tube into something 指小心把空心管放入某物之內。"},{"en":"A doctor may insert a tube into a container to transfer liquid safely.","zh":"醫生可能把管插入容器，以安全轉移液體。"},{"en":"In maple syrup production, the tube carries sap away from the tree.","zh":"在楓糖漿生產中，管把樹液從樹帶走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes placing a tube into an opening.","zh":"這個短語描述把管放進開口中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"end in a bucket","meaning":"末端接到桶","examples":[{"en":"The tube ends in a bucket.","zh":"管的末端接到桶。"},{"en":"End in a bucket means the final part of the tube reaches or leads into a bucket.","zh":"end in a bucket 指管的最後部分到達或通向一個桶。"},{"en":"A hose may end in a bucket when someone wants to collect rainwater.","zh":"如果有人想收集雨水，水喉末端可能接到桶。"},{"en":"If the tube ends in a bucket, the liquid can be collected instead of spilling.","zh":"如果管末端接到桶，液體就能被收集而不是灑出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where a tube or pipe finishes.","zh":"這個短語描述管或喉的終點位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take several taps","meaning":"可承受多個取液口","examples":[{"en":"The trees can often take several taps.","zh":"這些樹通常可以承受多個取液口。"},{"en":"Take several taps means be able to support several tapping holes without serious damage.","zh":"take several taps 指能承受幾個取液孔而不造成嚴重損害。"},{"en":"A large mature maple tree may take more than one tap.","zh":"大型成熟楓樹可能可以承受多於一個取液口。"},{"en":"Smaller trees should have fewer taps to protect their health.","zh":"較小的樹應有較少取液口，以保護健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how much tapping a tree can safely handle.","zh":"這個短語描述樹木安全承受取液的程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take care not to","meaning":"小心不要……","examples":[{"en":"Workers take care not to damage the trees.","zh":"工人小心不要損害樹木。"},{"en":"Take care not to means be careful so that something bad does not happen.","zh":"take care not to 指小心行事，以免壞事發生。"},{"en":"Students should take care not to spill chemicals during an experiment.","zh":"學生在實驗期間應小心不要濺出化學品。"},{"en":"This phrase shows careful action and prevention.","zh":"這個短語顯示謹慎行動和預防。"},{"en":"It is often used when there is a risk of harm or damage.","zh":"當有傷害或損壞風險時，常會使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cause damage to","meaning":"對……造成損害","examples":[{"en":"Workers avoid causing damage to the healthy growth of the tree.","zh":"工人避免對樹木的健康生長造成損害。"},{"en":"To cause damage to something means to harm it or make it weaker.","zh":"cause damage to something 指傷害某物或令它變弱。"},{"en":"Too much water can cause damage to a plant’s roots.","zh":"太多水會對植物根部造成損害。"},{"en":"Tapping must be controlled so it does not damage the tree’s future growth.","zh":"取樹液必須受控制，才不會損害樹木未來生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating harm.","zh":"這個短語描述造成傷害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"healthy growth","meaning":"健康生長","examples":[{"en":"Workers protect the healthy growth of the tree.","zh":"工人保護樹木的健康生長。"},{"en":"Healthy growth means normal, strong, and successful development.","zh":"healthy growth 指正常、強健而成功的發展。"},{"en":"Plants need water, sunlight, and suitable soil for healthy growth.","zh":"植物需要水分、陽光和合適泥土才能健康生長。"},{"en":"If tapping harms healthy growth, future syrup production may be reduced.","zh":"如果取樹液傷害健康生長，未來糖漿產量可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes proper development in living things.","zh":"這個短語描述生物的正常發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"consist of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"The sap consists of 98 percent water and 2 percent sugar.","zh":"樹液由98%水分和2%糖分組成。"},{"en":"Consist of means be made up of particular parts or materials.","zh":"consist of 指由特定部分或材料構成。"},{"en":"A simple salad may consist of lettuce, tomatoes, cucumbers, and dressing.","zh":"簡單沙律可能由生菜、番茄、青瓜和醬汁組成。"},{"en":"Knowing what sap consists of helps explain why so much water must be removed.","zh":"知道樹液由甚麼組成，有助解釋為何必須去除大量水分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes composition.","zh":"這個短語描述組成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"other nutrients","meaning":"其他營養物質","examples":[{"en":"The sap contains sugar and other nutrients.","zh":"樹液含有糖分和其他營養物質。"},{"en":"Other nutrients are additional substances that help living things grow or stay healthy.","zh":"other nutrients 指額外幫助生物生長或保持健康的物質。"},{"en":"Fruit contains vitamins, minerals, water, and other nutrients.","zh":"水果含有維他命、礦物質、水分和其他營養物質。"},{"en":"Sap carries nutrients through the tree to support growth.","zh":"樹液把營養物質運送到樹內各部分以支持生長。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to useful substances beyond the main one mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指除主要提到物質之外的有用物質。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"much of that water","meaning":"當中的大量水分","examples":[{"en":"Much of the water has to evaporate.","zh":"當中的大量水分必須蒸發。"},{"en":"Much of that water means a large amount of the water just mentioned.","zh":"much of that water 指剛才提到的水分中的大部分。"},{"en":"When soup boils for a long time, much of that water may disappear as steam.","zh":"湯煮很久時，當中的大量水分可能以蒸汽形式消失。"},{"en":"Removing much of the water makes sap thicker and sweeter.","zh":"去除大量水分會令樹液更濃稠、更甜。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to a large part of a liquid.","zh":"這個短語指回液體中的大部分水分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"evaporate","meaning":"蒸發","examples":[{"en":"The sap is boiled so that much of the water evaporates.","zh":"樹液被煮沸，使當中的大量水分蒸發。"},{"en":"Evaporate means change from liquid into vapour or gas.","zh":"evaporate 指由液體變成蒸氣或氣體。"},{"en":"Puddles evaporate when the sun heats the ground.","zh":"當太陽加熱地面，水窪會蒸發。"},{"en":"When water evaporates from sap, the remaining liquid becomes more concentrated.","zh":"當水分從樹液中蒸發，剩下的液體就變得更濃縮。"},{"en":"This verb describes liquid disappearing into the air as vapour.","zh":"這個動詞描述液體以蒸氣形式消失到空氣中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take place immediately","meaning":"立即進行","examples":[{"en":"The boiling process has to take place immediately.","zh":"煮沸過程必須立即進行。"},{"en":"Take place immediately means happen without delay.","zh":"take place immediately 指毫不拖延地發生。"},{"en":"If milk spills in a classroom, cleaning should take place immediately.","zh":"如果牛奶灑在課室中，清潔應立即進行。"},{"en":"Some food processes must happen quickly to keep the product fresh.","zh":"有些食品處理過程必須迅速進行，以保持產品新鮮。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses urgency.","zh":"這個短語強調緊急性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"what are called","meaning":"所謂的……","examples":[{"en":"The process uses what are called evaporators.","zh":"這個過程使用所謂的蒸發器。"},{"en":"What are called is used to introduce the name of something that may be unfamiliar.","zh":"what are called 用來引入可能陌生的事物名稱。"},{"en":"The teacher showed students what are called measuring cylinders.","zh":"老師向學生展示所謂的量筒。"},{"en":"This phrase helps listeners learn a technical term.","zh":"這個短語幫助聽者學習技術術語。"},{"en":"It signals that a special name is being given.","zh":"它表示正在給出一個特別名稱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"evaporators","meaning":"蒸發器","examples":[{"en":"Evaporators are used to boil the sap.","zh":"蒸發器用來煮沸樹液。"},{"en":"Evaporators are large pieces of equipment used to heat sap and remove water as steam.","zh":"evaporators 指用來加熱樹液並以蒸汽形式去除水分的大型設備。"},{"en":"A maple farm may use evaporators during the busiest syrup season.","zh":"楓糖農場可能在最繁忙的糖漿季節使用蒸發器。"},{"en":"Evaporators help turn thin sap into thick syrup.","zh":"蒸發器幫助把稀薄樹液變成濃稠糖漿。"},{"en":"This word names the equipment used in the boiling stage.","zh":"這個字指出煮沸階段使用的設備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"basically","meaning":"基本上","examples":[{"en":"Evaporators are basically extremely large pans.","zh":"蒸發器基本上是極大的鍋。"},{"en":"Basically means in simple terms or at the most basic level.","zh":"basically 指用簡單說法，或在最基本層面上。"},{"en":"A smartphone is basically a small computer you can carry.","zh":"智能手機基本上是一部可攜帶的小電腦。"},{"en":"This word helps simplify a technical explanation.","zh":"這個字有助簡化技術解釋。"},{"en":"It introduces the main idea without every detail.","zh":"它引出主要概念，而不講每個細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"large pans","meaning":"大鍋","examples":[{"en":"The evaporators are extremely large pans.","zh":"蒸發器是極大的鍋。"},{"en":"Large pans are wide, shallow containers used for heating or cooking food or liquid.","zh":"large pans 指用來加熱或烹煮食物或液體的寬而淺容器。"},{"en":"A restaurant kitchen may use large pans to cook soup for many people.","zh":"餐廳廚房可能用大鍋為很多人煮湯。"},{"en":"Wide pans help liquid evaporate more quickly because more surface is exposed.","zh":"寬闊的鍋令更多表面暴露，幫助液體更快蒸發。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the shape and function of evaporators simply.","zh":"這個短語簡單描述蒸發器的形狀和功能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be poured into","meaning":"被倒入……","examples":[{"en":"The sap is poured into the pans.","zh":"樹液被倒入鍋中。"},{"en":"Be poured into means be made to flow into a container.","zh":"be poured into 指被倒進某容器中。"},{"en":"Batter is poured into a cake tin before baking.","zh":"蛋糕糊在烘焙前會被倒入蛋糕模。"},{"en":"Pouring sap into the pans prepares it for heating.","zh":"把樹液倒入鍋中，是為加熱作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving liquid into a container.","zh":"這個短語描述把液體移入容器。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"build a fire","meaning":"生火","examples":[{"en":"A fire is built to heat the pans.","zh":"人們生火來加熱鍋。"},{"en":"To build a fire means to prepare and light wood, coal, or fuel so it burns.","zh":"build a fire 指準備並點燃木材、煤或燃料，使它燃燒。"},{"en":"Campers build a fire to cook food and keep warm.","zh":"露營者生火來煮食和保暖。"},{"en":"In syrup production, fire provides heat for boiling the sap.","zh":"在糖漿生產中，火提供煮沸樹液所需熱力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a controlled heat source.","zh":"這個短語描述製造受控熱源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be heated until","meaning":"被加熱至……","examples":[{"en":"The pans are heated until the sap boils.","zh":"鍋被加熱至樹液沸騰。"},{"en":"Be heated until means be warmed up to the point where a certain result happens.","zh":"be heated until 指被加熱到某個結果發生為止。"},{"en":"Milk is heated until it begins to steam.","zh":"牛奶被加熱至開始冒蒸汽。"},{"en":"Heating continues until the liquid reaches the required stage.","zh":"加熱會持續到液體達到所需階段。"},{"en":"This phrase links heating with a target condition.","zh":"這個短語把加熱與目標狀態連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the syrup begins to form","meaning":"糖漿開始形成","examples":[{"en":"As the water evaporates, the syrup begins to form.","zh":"隨着水分蒸發，糖漿開始形成。"},{"en":"The syrup begins to form means the liquid starts changing into syrup.","zh":"syrup begins to form 指液體開始變成糖漿。"},{"en":"As fruit juice boils, a thick jam-like syrup may begin to form.","zh":"當果汁煮沸時，濃厚像果醬的糖漿可能開始形成。"},{"en":"This stage happens when enough water has evaporated and the sugar becomes concentrated.","zh":"當足夠水分蒸發、糖分變得濃縮時，這個階段就會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the early stage of syrup creation.","zh":"這個短語描述糖漿形成的早期階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"evaporation process","meaning":"蒸發過程","examples":[{"en":"The evaporation process creates large quantities of steam.","zh":"蒸發過程產生大量蒸汽。"},{"en":"The evaporation process is the stage where liquid water changes into vapour.","zh":"evaporation process 指液態水變成蒸氣的階段。"},{"en":"In salt production, the evaporation process can leave salt behind.","zh":"在鹽生產中，蒸發過程可以留下鹽分。"},{"en":"In maple syrup production, this process removes water from sap.","zh":"在楓糖漿生產中，這個過程從樹液中去除水分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a key physical process.","zh":"這個短語描述一個關鍵物理過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"large quantities of","meaning":"大量","examples":[{"en":"The process creates large quantities of steam.","zh":"這個過程產生大量蒸汽。"},{"en":"Large quantities of means a lot of something, usually more than expected or easily handled.","zh":"large quantities of 指大量某物，通常比預期或容易處理的更多。"},{"en":"A school kitchen prepares large quantities of food for lunch.","zh":"學校廚房為午餐準備大量食物。"},{"en":"Boiling sap produces large quantities of steam because most of the sap is water.","zh":"煮沸樹液會產生大量蒸汽，因為樹液大部分是水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large amount.","zh":"這個短語描述大量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"steam","meaning":"蒸汽","examples":[{"en":"The evaporation process creates steam.","zh":"蒸發過程產生蒸汽。"},{"en":"Steam is the hot vapour produced when water boils.","zh":"steam 指水煮沸時產生的熱蒸氣。"},{"en":"Steam rises from a kettle when water reaches boiling point.","zh":"當水達到沸點，水壺會冒出蒸汽。"},{"en":"In maple syrup production, steam shows that water is leaving the sap.","zh":"在楓糖漿生產中，蒸汽顯示水分正在離開樹液。"},{"en":"This word describes hot water vapour.","zh":"這個字描述熱水蒸氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"become thicker and denser","meaning":"變得更濃稠","examples":[{"en":"The sap becomes thicker and denser as it boils.","zh":"樹液在煮沸時變得更濃稠。"},{"en":"Become thicker and denser means become less watery and more concentrated.","zh":"become thicker and denser 指變得較不水狀、更加濃縮。"},{"en":"Soup becomes thicker and denser when it is cooked for a long time.","zh":"湯煮得久會變得更濃稠。"},{"en":"As water leaves the sap, the sugar becomes more concentrated.","zh":"隨着水分離開樹液，糖分變得更濃縮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change in texture and concentration.","zh":"這個短語描述質地和濃度的變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at just the right moment","meaning":"在恰當時刻","examples":[{"en":"The worker removes the syrup at just the right moment.","zh":"工人在恰當時刻把糖漿移開。"},{"en":"At just the right moment means exactly when the timing is best.","zh":"at just the right moment 指正正在最佳時機。"},{"en":"A photographer must press the camera button at just the right moment to capture a jump.","zh":"攝影師必須在恰當時刻按下相機快門，才能拍到跳躍一刻。"},{"en":"Removing syrup too early or too late can affect its quality.","zh":"太早或太遲移開糖漿都會影響質素。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses precise timing.","zh":"這個短語強調準確時機。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"thick enough to be called","meaning":"濃稠到足以稱為……","examples":[{"en":"The sap becomes thick enough to be called maple syrup.","zh":"樹液變得濃稠到足以稱為楓糖漿。"},{"en":"Thick enough to be called something means it has reached the required texture or quality for that name.","zh":"thick enough to be called something 指達到該名稱所需的質地或品質。"},{"en":"Milk becomes thick enough to be called yoghurt after the right process.","zh":"牛奶經過正確過程後會變得濃稠到足以稱為乳酪。"},{"en":"A product may need to reach a certain standard before it earns a name.","zh":"產品可能需要達到某標準，才配得上某名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching a defining condition.","zh":"這個短語描述達到定義性條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"remove something from the heat","meaning":"把……從火上移開","examples":[{"en":"The worker removes the syrup from the heat.","zh":"工人把糖漿從火上移開。"},{"en":"To remove something from the heat means to take it away from the fire, stove, or heat source.","zh":"remove something from the heat 指把某物從火、爐或熱源移開。"},{"en":"A cook removes soup from the heat when it is ready.","zh":"湯煮好後，廚師會把它從火上移開。"},{"en":"Removing food from heat at the right time prevents burning or overcooking.","zh":"在合適時間把食物從熱源移開，可以防止燒焦或煮過頭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stopping the cooking process.","zh":"這個短語描述停止烹煮過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"after this process","meaning":"在這個過程之後","examples":[{"en":"After this process, sugar sand has to be filtered out.","zh":"在這個過程之後，糖砂必須被過濾掉。"},{"en":"After this process means once the step just described has finished.","zh":"after this process 指剛才描述的步驟完成後。"},{"en":"After this process, the bread dough is left to rise.","zh":"在這個過程之後，麵包麵糰會被放置發酵。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise production steps in order.","zh":"這個短語幫助按次序組織生產步驟。"},{"en":"It tells listeners what happens next.","zh":"它告訴聽者下一步會發生甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sugar sand","meaning":"糖砂；糖沉澱物","examples":[{"en":"Sugar sand has to be filtered out of the syrup.","zh":"糖砂必須從糖漿中被過濾掉。"},{"en":"Sugar sand is a grainy mineral-like sediment that can appear during maple syrup boiling.","zh":"sugar sand 指在楓糖漿煮沸過程中可能出現的顆粒狀礦物沉澱物。"},{"en":"Sugar sand is not dangerous, but it can make syrup cloudy and gritty.","zh":"糖砂並不危險，但會令糖漿混濁並帶沙粒口感。"},{"en":"Producers filter syrup to remove sugar sand before packaging.","zh":"生產者在包裝前會過濾糖漿以去除糖砂。"},{"en":"This phrase names the unwanted sediment in maple syrup.","zh":"這個短語指出楓糖漿中的不需要沉澱物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be filtered out","meaning":"被過濾掉","examples":[{"en":"Sugar sand has to be filtered out.","zh":"糖砂必須被過濾掉。"},{"en":"Be filtered out means be removed by passing a liquid through a filter.","zh":"be filtered out 指透過濾器讓液體通過，從而把某物去除。"},{"en":"Tea leaves can be filtered out before tea is served.","zh":"茶上桌前，茶葉可以被過濾掉。"},{"en":"Filtering removes unwanted solids while keeping the liquid.","zh":"過濾會去除不需要的固體，同時保留液體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a separation process.","zh":"這個短語描述分離過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"build up","meaning":"積聚；形成","examples":[{"en":"Sugar sand builds up during the boiling.","zh":"糖砂在煮沸過程中積聚。"},{"en":"Build up means gradually collect, increase, or form.","zh":"build up 指逐漸累積、增加或形成。"},{"en":"Dust can build up on shelves if they are not cleaned.","zh":"如果不清潔，灰塵會在架上積聚。"},{"en":"During boiling, unwanted particles may build up in the syrup.","zh":"在煮沸過程中，不需要的微粒可能在糖漿中形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual accumulation.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸累積。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"during the boiling","meaning":"在煮沸過程中","examples":[{"en":"Sugar sand builds up during the boiling process.","zh":"糖砂在煮沸過程中積聚。"},{"en":"During the boiling means while the liquid is being heated and bubbling.","zh":"during the boiling 指液體正在被加熱並起泡時。"},{"en":"During the boiling, soup may need to be stirred.","zh":"在煮沸過程中，湯可能需要攪拌。"},{"en":"Some changes in food happen only while it is being boiled.","zh":"有些食物變化只會在煮沸時發生。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the time when boiling is taking place.","zh":"這個短語指出煮沸正在進行的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cloudy appearance","meaning":"混濁外觀","examples":[{"en":"Sugar sand gives the syrup a cloudy appearance.","zh":"糖砂會令糖漿有混濁外觀。"},{"en":"A cloudy appearance means the liquid looks unclear or misty instead of transparent.","zh":"cloudy appearance 指液體看起來不清澈或有霧狀，而不是透明。"},{"en":"Orange juice with pulp may have a cloudy appearance.","zh":"有果肉的橙汁可能有混濁外觀。"},{"en":"Customers may expect syrup to look clear, so cloudiness can seem unattractive.","zh":"顧客可能期望糖漿看起來清澈，所以混濁可能顯得不吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a liquid looks.","zh":"這個短語描述液體外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"slightly gritty taste","meaning":"輕微沙粒口感","examples":[{"en":"Sugar sand gives the syrup a slightly gritty taste.","zh":"糖砂會令糖漿有輕微沙粒口感。"},{"en":"A slightly gritty taste means a mild rough or sandy feeling in the mouth.","zh":"slightly gritty taste 指口中有輕微粗糙或沙粒感。"},{"en":"Sugar that has not dissolved properly can leave a slightly gritty taste.","zh":"沒有完全溶解的糖會留下輕微沙粒口感。"},{"en":"Filtering syrup removes particles that create this unpleasant texture.","zh":"過濾糖漿會去除造成這種不佳質感的微粒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes texture as well as taste.","zh":"這個短語同時描述質感和味道。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"once this has been done","meaning":"完成這一步後","examples":[{"en":"Once this has been done, the syrup is ready to be packaged.","zh":"完成這一步後，糖漿便可以包裝。"},{"en":"Once this has been done means after this step has been completed.","zh":"once this has been done 指這個步驟完成之後。"},{"en":"Once the form has been signed, the application can be submitted.","zh":"表格簽好後，申請就可以提交。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show the next stage after a necessary action.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示必要行動後的下一階段。"},{"en":"It is useful in instructions and process descriptions.","zh":"它適合用於指示和過程描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be ready to be packaged","meaning":"可以包裝","examples":[{"en":"The syrup is ready to be packaged after filtering.","zh":"糖漿過濾後可以包裝。"},{"en":"Be ready to be packaged means be prepared for putting into bottles, jars, or containers for sale or storage.","zh":"be ready to be packaged 指已準備好放入瓶、罐或容器中售賣或儲存。"},{"en":"After biscuits cool, they are ready to be packaged.","zh":"餅乾冷卻後就可以包裝。"},{"en":"A product must be clean and finished before packaging.","zh":"產品必須乾淨並完成處理，才可以包裝。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the final stage before distribution.","zh":"這個短語描述分銷前的最後階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a whole variety of","meaning":"各式各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"Maple syrup can be used for a whole variety of products.","zh":"楓糖漿可以用於各式各樣的產品。"},{"en":"A whole variety of means many different kinds of something.","zh":"whole variety of 指許多不同種類的某物。"},{"en":"A bakery sells a whole variety of breads, cakes, and pastries.","zh":"麵包店售賣各式各樣的麵包、蛋糕和酥皮糕點。"},{"en":"Maple syrup can appear in drinks, desserts, sauces, and baked goods.","zh":"楓糖漿可以出現在飲品、甜品、醬汁和烘焙食品中。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a wide range of uses.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"take 40 litres of sap to","meaning":"需要40公升樹液去……","examples":[{"en":"It takes 40 litres of sap to produce one litre of maple syrup.","zh":"生產一公升楓糖漿需要40公升樹液。"},{"en":"Take 40 litres of sap to do something means require that amount of sap for the result.","zh":"take 40 litres of sap to do something 指需要那麼多樹液才能達成結果。"},{"en":"It may take many oranges to produce one bottle of fresh juice.","zh":"生產一瓶鮮榨橙汁可能需要很多個橙。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how much raw material is needed.","zh":"這個短語顯示需要多少原材料。"},{"en":"It helps explain why maple syrup can be expensive.","zh":"它幫助解釋為何楓糖漿可能昂貴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"produce one litre of","meaning":"生產一公升……","examples":[{"en":"Forty litres of sap produce one litre of maple syrup.","zh":"40公升樹液可生產一公升楓糖漿。"},{"en":"Produce one litre of something means make that amount of a finished liquid product.","zh":"produce one litre of something 指製成一公升的成品液體。"},{"en":"A small machine may produce one litre of juice in a few minutes.","zh":"小型機器可能在幾分鐘內生產一公升果汁。"},{"en":"Producing one litre of syrup requires removing a large amount of water.","zh":"生產一公升糖漿需要去除大量水分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes output quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述產出數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get an idea of","meaning":"大概了解","examples":[{"en":"You can get an idea of how much sap is needed.","zh":"你可以大概了解需要多少樹液。"},{"en":"To get an idea of something means to gain a general understanding of it.","zh":"get an idea of something 指對某事有大致理解。"},{"en":"Looking at the timetable helps parents get an idea of the school day.","zh":"查看時間表有助家長大概了解上課日安排。"},{"en":"Exact details may not be necessary if people just need a general idea.","zh":"如果人們只需要概念，未必需要精確細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forming a rough understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述形成粗略理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"how much is needed","meaning":"需要多少","examples":[{"en":"The figures show how much sap is needed.","zh":"這些數字顯示需要多少樹液。"},{"en":"How much is needed means the amount required for a purpose.","zh":"how much is needed 指某目的所需的數量。"},{"en":"A recipe tells cooks how much flour is needed.","zh":"食譜會告訴廚師需要多少麵粉。"},{"en":"Knowing how much is needed helps people plan resources and costs.","zh":"知道需要多少，有助人規劃資源和成本。"},{"en":"This phrase asks or explains required quantity.","zh":"這個短語詢問或解釋所需數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"basic process","meaning":"基本過程","examples":[{"en":"The speaker has explained the basic process of making maple syrup.","zh":"講者已解釋製作楓糖漿的基本過程。"},{"en":"The basic process is the simple main sequence of steps used to do something.","zh":"basic process 指完成某事的簡單主要步驟次序。"},{"en":"The basic process of writing an essay includes planning, drafting, editing, and checking.","zh":"寫文章的基本過程包括計劃、起稿、修改和檢查。"},{"en":"Understanding the basic process helps students follow more detailed explanations later.","zh":"理解基本過程有助學生之後跟上更詳細解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the essential steps, not every small detail.","zh":"這個短語描述必要步驟，而不是每個小細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"places like","meaning":"像……這樣的地方","examples":[{"en":"Places like Quebec are important in maple syrup production.","zh":"像魁北克這樣的地方在楓糖漿生產中很重要。"},{"en":"Places like means places similar to or including the example mentioned.","zh":"places like 指與所提例子相似或包括該例子的地方。"},{"en":"Places like coastal towns are popular for summer holidays.","zh":"像海邊城鎮這樣的地方很受暑假旅客歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an example without limiting the idea to that example only.","zh":"這個短語引入例子，但不把意思限制於該例子。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving representative examples.","zh":"給出代表性例子時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 15 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/listening/Practice 16/task-1":[{"front":"Children’s Engineering Workshops","meaning":"兒童工程工作坊","examples":[{"en":"The father phones Children’s Engineering Workshops to ask about holiday activities.","zh":"父親致電兒童工程工作坊，詢問假期活動。"},{"en":"Children’s Engineering Workshops are practical classes where children learn engineering through hands-on tasks.","zh":"Children’s Engineering Workshops是讓兒童透過動手任務學習工程的實踐課程。"},{"en":"Children’s Engineering Workshops may teach children to build bridges, cars or simple robots.","zh":"兒童工程工作坊可能教孩子建橋、製作小車或簡單機械人。"},{"en":"These workshops help children learn by making things rather than only listening to instructions.","zh":"這些工作坊幫助孩子透過製作東西學習，而不只是聽指示。"},{"en":"This phrase names a programme designed for young learners.","zh":"這個短語命名一個為年幼學習者設計的課程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"want some information about","meaning":"想了解關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"The father wants some information about the workshops in the school holidays.","zh":"父親想了解關於學校假期工作坊的資料。"},{"en":"To want some information about something means to ask for details about it.","zh":"want some information about某事，意思是想查詢關於它的詳情。"},{"en":"A parent may want some information about a summer course before enrolling a child.","zh":"家長在為孩子報名前，可能想了解關於暑期課程的資料。"},{"en":"People ask for information when they need to know times, prices or activities.","zh":"人們需要知道時間、價錢或活動內容時，就會查詢資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when making an enquiry.","zh":"這個短語適合用於作出查詢時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"workshops in the school holidays","meaning":"學校假期期間的工作坊","examples":[{"en":"The workshops are held during the school holidays.","zh":"這些工作坊在學校假期期間舉行。"},{"en":"Workshops in the school holidays are short learning activities offered when schools are closed.","zh":"workshops in the school holidays是在學校放假時提供的短期學習活動。"},{"en":"Many children join workshops in the school holidays to learn art, sport or science.","zh":"許多孩子在學校假期期間參加工作坊，學習藝術、運動或科學。"},{"en":"Holiday workshops can keep children active while parents are at work.","zh":"假期工作坊可以讓孩子保持活躍，同時方便上班的家長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the timing of the activities.","zh":"這個短語描述活動舉行的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be interested","meaning":"感興趣","examples":[{"en":"The father has two daughters who are interested in the workshops.","zh":"父親有兩個女兒對工作坊感興趣。"},{"en":"To be interested means to want to know more about something or take part in it.","zh":"be interested意思是想知道更多關於某事的資料，或想參與其中。"},{"en":"A child who loves building toys may be interested in an engineering class.","zh":"喜歡搭建玩具的孩子可能對工程課感興趣。"},{"en":"When students are interested, they usually listen more carefully and learn faster.","zh":"當學生感興趣時，他們通常會更仔細聆聽，也學得更快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes curiosity or attraction.","zh":"這個短語描述好奇或被吸引。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as young as that","meaning":"年紀這麼小","examples":[{"en":"The father asks whether the workshops take children as young as four.","zh":"父親問工作坊是否接受年紀小至四歲的孩子。"},{"en":"As young as that means as young as the age just mentioned.","zh":"as young as that意思是年紀低至剛才提到的年齡。"},{"en":"Some swimming classes accept children as young as three.","zh":"有些游泳班接受年紀小至三歲的孩子。"},{"en":"Parents often ask this when they are unsure whether a child is old enough.","zh":"當家長不確定孩子是否夠年齡參加時，常會這樣問。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a surprisingly young age.","zh":"這個短語突顯令人意外的年幼年齡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"four to five-year-olds","meaning":"四至五歲小朋友","examples":[{"en":"The Tiny Engineers workshop is for four to five-year-olds.","zh":"Tiny Engineers工作坊是為四至五歲小朋友而設。"},{"en":"Four to five-year-olds are children aged four or five.","zh":"four to five-year-olds是四歲或五歲的孩子。"},{"en":"Activities for four to five-year-olds should be simple, safe and playful.","zh":"為四至五歲小朋友設計的活動應簡單、安全和有遊戲感。"},{"en":"Children of this age often learn best through touching, building and experimenting.","zh":"這個年齡的孩子通常最適合透過觸摸、搭建和實驗學習。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a young age group.","zh":"這個短語指出一個年幼年齡組別。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what sorts of activities","meaning":"哪些類型的活動","examples":[{"en":"The father asks what sorts of activities the children do.","zh":"父親問孩子會做哪些類型的活動。"},{"en":"What sorts of activities means what kinds of tasks or events are included.","zh":"what sorts of activities意思是包括哪些種類的任務或活動。"},{"en":"A parent may ask what sorts of activities are offered at a science camp.","zh":"家長可能問科學營提供哪些類型的活動。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for examples, not just a general description.","zh":"這個短語是在要求例子，而不只是一般描述。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing courses for children.","zh":"當比較兒童課程時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"all sorts","meaning":"各式各樣","examples":[{"en":"The children do all sorts of engineering activities.","zh":"孩子會做各式各樣的工程活動。"},{"en":"All sorts means many different kinds.","zh":"all sorts意思是很多不同種類。"},{"en":"In a creative workshop, children may make all sorts of models and machines.","zh":"在創意工作坊中，孩子可能製作各式各樣的模型和機器。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests variety rather than one repeated activity.","zh":"這個短語暗示活動種類多，而不是重複同一件事。"},{"en":"It is informal and common in everyday speech.","zh":"它較口語，常見於日常說話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"work together to","meaning":"一起合作去……","examples":[{"en":"The children work together to design a special cover for an egg.","zh":"孩子一起合作去為雞蛋設計一個特別保護套。"},{"en":"To work together to do something means to cooperate in order to achieve a goal.","zh":"work together to do something意思是合作以達成一個目標。"},{"en":"Students may work together to build a model bridge in a science lesson.","zh":"學生可能在科學課中一起合作去建造模型橋。"},{"en":"Working together helps children share ideas and solve problems.","zh":"一起合作能幫助孩子分享想法和解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes teamwork with a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述有目的的團隊合作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"design a special cover","meaning":"設計一個特別保護套","examples":[{"en":"The children design a special cover that goes round an egg.","zh":"孩子設計一個圍住雞蛋的特別保護套。"},{"en":"To design a special cover means to plan and create a protective covering for something.","zh":"design a special cover意思是規劃並製作一個保護某物的外套。"},{"en":"Students may design a special cover to protect a phone from being dropped.","zh":"學生可能設計一個特別保護套，以保護手機不被摔壞。"},{"en":"Designing a cover requires thinking about shape, material and strength.","zh":"設計保護套需要思考形狀、材料和強度。"},{"en":"This phrase connects creativity with practical protection.","zh":"這個短語把創意與實際保護連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"go round","meaning":"圍住；包着","examples":[{"en":"The cover goes round an egg to protect it.","zh":"保護套圍住雞蛋，以保護它。"},{"en":"To go round something means to surround or wrap around it.","zh":"go round某物，意思是圍繞或包着它。"},{"en":"A bandage goes round a wrist to support it.","zh":"繃帶圍住手腕，以支撐它。"},{"en":"If a cover goes round an object properly, it can protect all sides.","zh":"如果保護套妥善包着物件，就能保護各個方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position around an object.","zh":"這個短語描述在物件周圍的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"drop it from a height","meaning":"從高處掉下來","examples":[{"en":"The children drop the egg from a height to test the cover.","zh":"孩子把雞蛋從高處掉下來，以測試保護套。"},{"en":"To drop it from a height means to let it fall from a high position.","zh":"drop it from a height意思是讓它從較高位置跌下來。"},{"en":"Students may drop a model from a height to see whether it breaks.","zh":"學生可能把模型從高處掉下來，看看它會否破裂。"},{"en":"Dropping something from a height tests whether the design can absorb impact.","zh":"從高處掉下某物可以測試設計能否吸收撞擊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple engineering test.","zh":"這個短語描述一項簡單工程測試。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"part of the fun","meaning":"樂趣的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Sometimes the egg breaks, but that is part of the fun.","zh":"有時雞蛋會破，但那是樂趣的一部分。"},{"en":"Part of the fun means one enjoyable or exciting part of an activity.","zh":"part of the fun意思是活動中令人愉快或刺激的一部分。"},{"en":"In a science experiment, small mistakes can be part of the fun.","zh":"在科學實驗中，小錯誤可以是樂趣的一部分。"},{"en":"Children often enjoy activities more when the result is uncertain.","zh":"當結果不確定，孩子通常會更享受活動。"},{"en":"This phrase makes failure sound playful rather than serious.","zh":"這個短語把失敗說得像遊戲，而不是嚴重問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"love building things","meaning":"喜歡搭建東西","examples":[{"en":"Lydia loves building things.","zh":"Lydia喜歡搭建東西。"},{"en":"To love building things means to enjoy making or constructing objects.","zh":"love building things意思是喜歡製作或建構物件。"},{"en":"A child who loves building things may spend hours with blocks or craft materials.","zh":"喜歡搭建東西的孩子可能花很多時間玩積木或手工材料。"},{"en":"Building activities can develop patience, imagination and problem-solving skills.","zh":"搭建活動可以培養耐性、想像力和解難能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong interest in making objects.","zh":"這個短語描述對製作物件的濃厚興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an opportunity for her to","meaning":"讓她……的機會","examples":[{"en":"The father asks whether there is an opportunity for Lydia to build things.","zh":"父親問是否有讓Lydia搭建東西的機會。"},{"en":"An opportunity for her to do something means a chance for her to do it.","zh":"an opportunity for her to do something意思是讓她做某事的機會。"},{"en":"A music club gives a shy student an opportunity for her to perform in front of others.","zh":"音樂社給害羞學生一個讓她在他人面前表演的機會。"},{"en":"Opportunities help children try activities that match their interests.","zh":"機會能幫助孩子嘗試符合自己興趣的活動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a chance to take part.","zh":"這個短語著重參與的機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have a competition to see who","meaning":"比賽看看誰能……","examples":[{"en":"The children have a competition to see who can make the highest tower.","zh":"孩子比賽看看誰能搭出最高的塔。"},{"en":"To have a competition to see who can do something means to compete and find the person who does it best.","zh":"have a competition to see who can do something意思是透過比賽找出誰最能做到某事。"},{"en":"Students may have a competition to see who can build the strongest bridge.","zh":"學生可能比賽看看誰能建造最堅固的橋。"},{"en":"Competitions can make learning exciting because children want to test their ideas.","zh":"比賽可以令學習更刺激，因為孩子想測試自己的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a challenge with a clear winner.","zh":"這個短語引入有明確勝方的挑戰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"make the highest tower","meaning":"搭出最高的塔","examples":[{"en":"The children try to make the highest tower.","zh":"孩子嘗試搭出最高的塔。"},{"en":"To make the highest tower means to build the tallest tower among the competitors.","zh":"make the highest tower意思是在參賽者中建造最高的塔。"},{"en":"Children may use paper, tape and straws to make the highest tower.","zh":"孩子可能用紙、膠紙和飲管搭出最高的塔。"},{"en":"A tall tower must be balanced, or it will fall over.","zh":"高塔必須保持平衡，否則會倒下。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a building challenge based on height.","zh":"這個短語描述以高度為目標的搭建挑戰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"you’d be amazed how","meaning":"你會驚訝於……有多","examples":[{"en":"You would be amazed how high the children’s towers can go.","zh":"你會驚訝於孩子的塔可以搭得多高。"},{"en":"You’d be amazed how means you would be very surprised by the degree or result.","zh":"you’d be amazed how意思是你會對程度或結果感到非常驚訝。"},{"en":"You’d be amazed how quickly children can learn a new skill when they enjoy it.","zh":"當孩子享受某項活動時，你會驚訝於他們學新技能有多快。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces something impressive or unexpected.","zh":"這個短語引入令人印象深刻或出乎意料的事情。"},{"en":"It is often used to express pleasant surprise.","zh":"它常用來表達愉快的驚訝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"learn all the time","meaning":"一直在學習","examples":[{"en":"The children are learning all the time as well as having fun.","zh":"孩子玩得開心的同時也一直在學習。"},{"en":"To learn all the time means to keep learning continuously during an activity.","zh":"learn all the time意思是在活動中持續不斷地學習。"},{"en":"Children learn all the time when they test ideas, fail and try again.","zh":"當孩子測試想法、失敗再重試時，他們一直在學習。"},{"en":"Learning can happen naturally when activities are playful and practical.","zh":"當活動有遊戲感和實踐性，學習可以自然發生。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses constant learning.","zh":"這個短語強調持續學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as well as having fun","meaning":"也玩得開心","examples":[{"en":"The children learn engineering skills as well as having fun.","zh":"孩子學習工程技能，也玩得開心。"},{"en":"As well as having fun means in addition to enjoying themselves.","zh":"as well as having fun意思是除了享受活動之外。"},{"en":"Students can practise teamwork as well as having fun during a group challenge.","zh":"學生在小組挑戰中可以練習團隊合作，也玩得開心。"},{"en":"Good workshops combine enjoyment with real learning.","zh":"好工作坊會把樂趣與真正學習結合。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that fun and learning happen together.","zh":"這個短語顯示樂趣和學習同時發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"design and build","meaning":"設計並製作","examples":[{"en":"The children design and build a balloon-powered car.","zh":"孩子設計並製作一架氣球動力小車。"},{"en":"To design and build something means to plan it first and then make it.","zh":"design and build某物，意思是先規劃它，然後製作它。"},{"en":"Students may design and build a small bridge using recycled materials.","zh":"學生可能使用回收材料設計並製作一條小橋。"},{"en":"Designing and building help children connect ideas with practical results.","zh":"設計並製作能幫助孩子把想法與實際成果連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase combines creative planning with construction.","zh":"這個短語結合創意規劃與建造。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be attached to","meaning":"連接到……","examples":[{"en":"The car is attached to a balloon.","zh":"小車連接到一個氣球。"},{"en":"To be attached to something means to be joined or connected to it.","zh":"be attached to某物，意思是與它連結或接上。"},{"en":"A small basket can be attached to a bicycle to carry books.","zh":"小籃子可以連接到單車上，用來載書。"},{"en":"If one part is not attached firmly, the model may not work properly.","zh":"如果某部分沒有穩固連接，模型可能不能正常運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical connection.","zh":"這個短語描述實體連接。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the force of the air","meaning":"空氣的力量","examples":[{"en":"The force of the air in the balloon powers the car.","zh":"氣球內空氣的力量推動小車。"},{"en":"The force of the air means the push created by air moving or escaping.","zh":"the force of the air意思是空氣移動或釋放時產生的推力。"},{"en":"The force of the air from a fan can move a light paper boat.","zh":"風扇吹出的空氣力量可以推動輕紙船。"},{"en":"Children can see how air pressure creates movement through this experiment.","zh":"孩子可以透過這個實驗看見氣壓如何產生移動。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the physical force behind the car’s motion.","zh":"這個短語解釋小車移動背後的物理力量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"power the car","meaning":"推動小車","examples":[{"en":"The air from the balloon powers the car.","zh":"氣球中的空氣推動小車。"},{"en":"To power the car means to provide the energy or force that makes it move.","zh":"power the car意思是提供令小車移動的能量或力量。"},{"en":"A small battery can power a toy car.","zh":"一粒小電池可以推動玩具車。"},{"en":"In this activity, air replaces an engine as the source of movement.","zh":"在這個活動中，空氣取代引擎成為移動來源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what makes the vehicle move.","zh":"這個短語描述甚麼令交通工具移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make it move along","meaning":"令它向前移動","examples":[{"en":"The force of the air makes the car move along.","zh":"空氣的力量令小車向前移動。"},{"en":"To make it move along means to cause it to travel forward or across a surface.","zh":"make it move along意思是令它向前或沿着表面移動。"},{"en":"A push from a child’s hand can make a toy train move along the track.","zh":"孩子用手一推，可以令玩具火車沿軌道向前移動。"},{"en":"The direction of force affects how smoothly the object moves along.","zh":"力的方向會影響物件移動得有多順暢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes causing movement.","zh":"這個短語描述造成移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"go really fast","meaning":"走得很快","examples":[{"en":"The balloon-powered cars can go really fast.","zh":"氣球動力小車可以走得很快。"},{"en":"To go really fast means to move at a very high speed.","zh":"go really fast意思是以很高速度移動。"},{"en":"A well-designed model car can go really fast on a smooth floor.","zh":"設計良好的模型車可以在平滑地面上走得很快。"},{"en":"Children may test different designs to see which one goes fastest.","zh":"孩子可能測試不同設計，看看哪一架走得最快。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses speed in an informal way.","zh":"這個短語以口語方式表達速度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sound perfect","meaning":"聽起來很適合","examples":[{"en":"The father thinks all the activities sound perfect.","zh":"父親覺得所有活動聽起來很適合。"},{"en":"To sound perfect means to seem exactly right from the description.","zh":"sound perfect意思是從描述聽來似乎完全合適。"},{"en":"A workshop with building, games and learning may sound perfect for a curious child.","zh":"有搭建、遊戲和學習元素的工作坊，對好奇的孩子來說可能聽起來很適合。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when something matches their needs very well.","zh":"當某事非常符合需要，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It gives a strong positive reaction.","zh":"它表達強烈正面反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have just had one’s birthday","meaning":"剛過生日","examples":[{"en":"Carly has just had her seventh birthday.","zh":"Carly剛過七歲生日。"},{"en":"To have just had one’s birthday means someone recently celebrated their birthday.","zh":"have just had one’s birthday意思是某人最近慶祝了生日。"},{"en":"My brother has just had his tenth birthday, so he is now old enough for the course.","zh":"我弟弟剛過十歲生日，所以現在夠年齡參加課程。"},{"en":"Parents may mention a recent birthday when checking age groups.","zh":"家長查詢年齡組別時，可能會提到最近剛過生日。"},{"en":"This phrase links someone’s age with recent timing.","zh":"這個短語把某人的年齡與近期時間連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"presumably","meaning":"想必；大概","examples":[{"en":"The father says Carly would presumably be in a different group.","zh":"父親說Carly想必會在另一個組別。"},{"en":"Presumably means probably, based on what seems reasonable.","zh":"presumably意思是根據合理推測，大概如此。"},{"en":"Presumably, older children will need a more advanced class.","zh":"想必年紀較大的孩子會需要較進階的班。"},{"en":"This word shows that the speaker is making a logical guess.","zh":"這個詞顯示說話者正在作合理猜測。"},{"en":"It is useful when checking an assumption politely.","zh":"它適合用於有禮地確認假設。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be in a different group","meaning":"在另一個組別","examples":[{"en":"Carly would be in a different group because she is older.","zh":"Carly因為年紀較大，會在另一個組別。"},{"en":"To be in a different group means to be placed with another set of people.","zh":"be in a different group意思是被安排到另一組人之中。"},{"en":"Children of different ages may be in different groups for safety and learning reasons.","zh":"不同年齡的孩子可能因安全和學習原因而在不同組別。"},{"en":"Grouping children by age helps teachers choose suitable activities.","zh":"按年齡分組幫助老師選擇合適活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes placement in another class or team.","zh":"這個短語描述被安排到另一班或另一隊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Junior Engineers","meaning":"初級工程師工作坊","examples":[{"en":"Carly would be in the Junior Engineers group.","zh":"Carly會在Junior Engineers組別。"},{"en":"Junior Engineers is a workshop group for slightly older children learning simple engineering tasks.","zh":"Junior Engineers是讓較年長兒童學習簡單工程任務的工作坊組別。"},{"en":"Junior Engineers may build model vehicles, bridges and robots.","zh":"初級工程師工作坊可能製作模型交通工具、橋和機械人。"},{"en":"The word “junior” suggests the children are still young but older than the youngest group.","zh":"junior一詞暗示孩子仍年幼，但比最年幼組別年長。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific workshop level.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定工作坊程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"from six to eight","meaning":"六至八歲","examples":[{"en":"The Junior Engineers workshop is for children from six to eight.","zh":"Junior Engineers工作坊是為六至八歲兒童而設。"},{"en":"From six to eight means aged between six and eight years old.","zh":"from six to eight意思是年齡介乎六至八歲。"},{"en":"A reading club from six to eight may use books suitable for early primary pupils.","zh":"六至八歲閱讀小組可能使用適合初小學生的書。"},{"en":"Age ranges help organisers choose safe and suitable activities.","zh":"年齡範圍幫助主辦方選擇安全和合適活動。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the age group for a class.","zh":"這個短語給出課程的年齡組別。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the same sorts of activities","meaning":"同類活動","examples":[{"en":"The father asks whether the older children do the same sorts of activities.","zh":"父親問年紀較大的孩子是否做同類活動。"},{"en":"The same sorts of activities means similar kinds of tasks or events.","zh":"the same sorts of activities意思是相似種類的任務或活動。"},{"en":"Younger and older children may do the same sorts of activities, but at different levels.","zh":"年幼和年長孩子可能做同類活動，但程度不同。"},{"en":"This phrase compares what two groups do.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個組別做甚麼。"},{"en":"It is useful when asking about course differences.","zh":"當詢問課程差異時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a bit more advanced","meaning":"稍為進階","examples":[{"en":"Some activities are the same but a bit more advanced.","zh":"有些活動相同，但稍為進階。"},{"en":"A bit more advanced means slightly more difficult or developed.","zh":"a bit more advanced意思是稍微更困難或更成熟。"},{"en":"Older children may use a bit more advanced tools than younger children.","zh":"年紀較大的孩子可能使用稍為進階的工具。"},{"en":"A more advanced task can challenge children without making it too hard.","zh":"較進階的任務可以挑戰孩子，而不會令任務太難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small increase in difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述難度略為增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"work out how to","meaning":"想出如何……","examples":[{"en":"The children work out how to build model vehicles.","zh":"孩子想出如何製作模型交通工具。"},{"en":"To work out how to do something means to figure out the method or solution.","zh":"work out how to do something意思是想出方法或解決方案。"},{"en":"Students may work out how to make a paper tower stand without falling.","zh":"學生可能想出如何令紙塔站穩而不倒。"},{"en":"Working things out helps children think like problem-solvers.","zh":"想出方法能幫助孩子像解難者一樣思考。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discovery through thinking and testing.","zh":"這個短語描述透過思考和測試來發現方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"build model vehicles","meaning":"製作模型交通工具","examples":[{"en":"The children learn how to build model vehicles.","zh":"孩子學習如何製作模型交通工具。"},{"en":"To build model vehicles means to make small versions of transport machines.","zh":"build model vehicles意思是製作交通工具的小型模型。"},{"en":"Children may build model vehicles using wheels, card, wood and simple motors.","zh":"孩子可能使用輪子、卡紙、木材和簡單摩打製作模型交通工具。"},{"en":"Building vehicles teaches ideas about movement, balance and structure.","zh":"製作交通工具能教導關於移動、平衡和結構的概念。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical engineering activity.","zh":"這個短語描述一項實踐工程活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"things like","meaning":"例如……之類","examples":[{"en":"The children build model vehicles, things like cars and trucks.","zh":"孩子製作模型交通工具，例如汽車和貨車之類。"},{"en":"Things like means examples such as.","zh":"things like意思是例如。"},{"en":"Children may use simple materials, things like paper, string and tape.","zh":"孩子可能使用簡單材料，例如紙、繩和膠紙之類。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples without giving a complete list.","zh":"這個短語引入例子，但不是完整列表。"},{"en":"It is informal and common in speech.","zh":"它較口語，常見於說話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cars and trucks","meaning":"汽車和貨車","examples":[{"en":"The children build model vehicles such as cars and trucks.","zh":"孩子製作汽車和貨車等模型交通工具。"},{"en":"Cars and trucks are road vehicles used for carrying people or goods.","zh":"cars and trucks是用來載人或載貨的道路交通工具。"},{"en":"A model car may be small and light, while a model truck may need a stronger frame.","zh":"模型汽車可能細小而輕，而模型貨車可能需要更堅固框架。"},{"en":"Building different vehicles helps children compare shapes and functions.","zh":"製作不同交通工具能幫助孩子比較形狀和功能。"},{"en":"This phrase gives examples of vehicle types.","zh":"這個短語給出交通工具種類的例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"construct animals","meaning":"製作動物模型","examples":[{"en":"The children also construct animals using the same materials and techniques.","zh":"孩子也使用相同材料和技巧製作動物模型。"},{"en":"To construct animals means to build models shaped like animals.","zh":"construct animals意思是建造動物形狀的模型。"},{"en":"Students may construct animals from cardboard, sticks and moving joints.","zh":"學生可能用卡紙、木棒和可活動關節製作動物模型。"},{"en":"This activity combines engineering with creativity and imagination.","zh":"這項活動把工程與創意和想像力結合。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making animal models.","zh":"這個短語描述製作動物模型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"materials and techniques","meaning":"材料和技巧","examples":[{"en":"The children use the same materials and techniques to construct animals.","zh":"孩子使用相同材料和技巧製作動物模型。"},{"en":"Materials and techniques are the physical things used and the methods applied.","zh":"materials and techniques是所使用的實體物料和所應用的方法。"},{"en":"In craft lessons, paper and glue are materials, while folding and cutting are techniques.","zh":"在手工課中，紙和膠水是材料，而摺疊和剪裁是技巧。"},{"en":"Good results depend on choosing suitable materials and using effective techniques.","zh":"良好成果取決於選擇合適材料和使用有效技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase connects what is used with how it is used.","zh":"這個短語把使用甚麼與如何使用連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"learn how to program","meaning":"學習如何編程","examples":[{"en":"The children learn how to program their models.","zh":"孩子學習如何為模型編程。"},{"en":"To learn how to program means to learn how to write or use instructions that control a machine or computer.","zh":"learn how to program意思是學習如何編寫或使用控制機器或電腦的指令。"},{"en":"Children may learn how to program a small robot to move forward.","zh":"孩子可能學習如何為小機械人編程，讓它向前走。"},{"en":"Programming teaches logical thinking because every instruction matters.","zh":"編程教導邏輯思維，因為每個指令都重要。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces basic coding or control skills.","zh":"這個短語引入基礎編程或控制技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make them move","meaning":"令它們動起來","examples":[{"en":"The children program the models and make them move.","zh":"孩子為模型編程，令它們動起來。"},{"en":"To make them move means to cause the models to start moving.","zh":"make them move意思是令模型開始移動。"},{"en":"A child can make a robot move by programming its wheels.","zh":"孩子可以透過為輪子編程，令機械人動起來。"},{"en":"Seeing a model move gives children a clear result from their coding.","zh":"看見模型移動，能讓孩子清楚看到編程成果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning a static model into a moving one.","zh":"這個短語描述把靜止模型變成會動的模型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"learn a bit of coding","meaning":"學一點編程","examples":[{"en":"The children learn a bit of coding in the workshop.","zh":"孩子在工作坊中學一點編程。"},{"en":"To learn a bit of coding means to learn a small amount of computer programming.","zh":"learn a bit of coding意思是學習少量電腦編程。"},{"en":"Younger students may learn a bit of coding through simple drag-and-drop blocks.","zh":"年幼學生可能透過簡單拖放方塊學一點編程。"},{"en":"Even a little coding can help children understand instructions and sequences.","zh":"即使只是一點編程，也能幫助孩子理解指令和次序。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an introductory level of programming.","zh":"這個短語暗示入門程度的編程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pick it up really quickly","meaning":"很快學會","examples":[{"en":"The children pick up coding really quickly.","zh":"孩子很快學會編程。"},{"en":"To pick it up really quickly means to learn it very fast.","zh":"pick it up really quickly意思是非常快速地學會它。"},{"en":"Children often pick up new software really quickly when it feels like a game.","zh":"當新軟件像遊戲一樣，孩子通常很快學會使用。"},{"en":"Picking up a skill quickly can make learners more confident.","zh":"快速學會技能可以令學習者更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and positive.","zh":"這個短語較口語，帶正面意思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be there to help","meaning":"在旁協助","examples":[{"en":"The instructors are there to help if the children need it.","zh":"如果孩子需要，導師會在旁協助。"},{"en":"To be there to help means to be available to give support when needed.","zh":"be there to help意思是在需要時可提供支援。"},{"en":"A teacher is there to help when students get stuck during a project.","zh":"當學生在專題中遇到困難，老師會在旁協助。"},{"en":"Support nearby helps children try difficult tasks without feeling alone.","zh":"附近有支援能幫助孩子嘗試困難任務，而不會感到孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures learners that help is available.","zh":"這個短語讓學習者放心，知道有人可以幫忙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"learn from one another","meaning":"互相學習","examples":[{"en":"The children learn from one another as well as from the instructors.","zh":"孩子不但向導師學習，也互相學習。"},{"en":"To learn from one another means to gain knowledge by watching, listening to or helping each other.","zh":"learn from one another意思是透過觀察、聆聽或互相幫助來獲得知識。"},{"en":"Students learn from one another when they compare different ways to solve a problem.","zh":"學生比較不同解題方法時，就會互相學習。"},{"en":"Peer learning can be powerful because children explain ideas in familiar language.","zh":"同輩學習可以很有效，因為孩子會用熟悉語言解釋想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning through classmates or group members.","zh":"這個短語描述透過同學或組員學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have competitions","meaning":"有比賽","examples":[{"en":"The Junior Engineers have competitions too.","zh":"Junior Engineers也有比賽。"},{"en":"To have competitions means to organise activities where people try to win.","zh":"have competitions意思是舉辦讓人嘗試取勝的活動。"},{"en":"Children may have competitions to see whose bridge holds the most weight.","zh":"孩子可能有比賽，看看誰的橋能承受最多重量。"},{"en":"Competitions can motivate students to improve their designs.","zh":"比賽可以激勵學生改善自己的設計。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding a challenge element to learning.","zh":"這個短語描述在學習中加入挑戰元素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"use recycled materials","meaning":"使用回收材料","examples":[{"en":"The children use recycled materials to build a bridge.","zh":"孩子使用回收材料建造一條橋。"},{"en":"To use recycled materials means to make something from materials that have been used before.","zh":"use recycled materials意思是用曾經被使用過的材料製作某物。"},{"en":"Students may use recycled materials such as cardboard boxes and old newspapers.","zh":"學生可能使用紙皮箱和舊報紙等回收材料。"},{"en":"Recycled materials can teach children about sustainability as well as design.","zh":"回收材料可以教孩子可持續發展，也教設計。"},{"en":"This phrase connects building with environmental awareness.","zh":"這個短語把建造與環保意識連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"card and wood","meaning":"卡紙和木材","examples":[{"en":"The children use recycled materials like card and wood.","zh":"孩子使用卡紙和木材等回收材料。"},{"en":"Card and wood are common craft or construction materials used in models.","zh":"card and wood是模型中常用的手工或建造材料。"},{"en":"Card is light and easy to cut, while wood can add strength.","zh":"卡紙輕而易剪，木材則可以增加強度。"},{"en":"Choosing between card and wood affects how strong and heavy a model is.","zh":"選擇卡紙還是木材，會影響模型有多堅固和多重。"},{"en":"This phrase gives examples of materials children may use.","zh":"這個短語給出孩子可能使用的材料例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"build a bridge","meaning":"建造一條橋","examples":[{"en":"The children use recycled materials to build a bridge.","zh":"孩子使用回收材料建造一條橋。"},{"en":"To build a bridge means to construct a structure that can cross a gap.","zh":"build a bridge意思是建造能跨越空隙的結構。"},{"en":"Students may build a bridge from straws and test how much weight it can hold.","zh":"學生可能用飲管建造一條橋，並測試它能承受多少重量。"},{"en":"Bridge-building activities teach balance, strength and design.","zh":"建橋活動教導平衡、強度和設計。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a classic engineering challenge.","zh":"這個短語描述典型工程挑戰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get a prize","meaning":"得獎","examples":[{"en":"The longest bridge gets a prize.","zh":"最長的橋會得獎。"},{"en":"To get a prize means to receive an award for winning or doing well.","zh":"get a prize意思是因勝出或表現好而獲得獎品。"},{"en":"The team with the strongest model may get a prize at the end of the workshop.","zh":"模型最堅固的隊伍可能在工作坊結束時得獎。"},{"en":"Prizes can make children excited and encourage effort.","zh":"獎品可以令孩子興奮並鼓勵努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reward for achievement.","zh":"這個短語描述對成就的獎勵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"I wouldn’t mind doing that myself","meaning":"我自己也不介意做那件事","examples":[{"en":"The father says he would not mind building a bridge himself.","zh":"父親說他自己也不介意建造一條橋。"},{"en":"I wouldn’t mind doing that myself means I would quite enjoy doing it too.","zh":"I wouldn’t mind doing that myself意思是我自己也會頗樂意做。"},{"en":"If a parent hears about a fun science activity, they may say, “I wouldn’t mind doing that myself.”","zh":"如果家長聽到有趣的科學活動，可能會說：「我自己也不介意做那件事。」"},{"en":"This phrase shows friendly interest, often with a little humour.","zh":"這個短語顯示友善興趣，通常帶一點幽默。"},{"en":"It suggests the activity sounds enjoyable even to an adult.","zh":"它暗示該活動聽起來連成人也會覺得有趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"something a bit different","meaning":"有點不同的活動","examples":[{"en":"The older children also do something a bit different.","zh":"年紀較大的孩子也會做有點不同的活動。"},{"en":"Something a bit different means an activity that is slightly unlike the others.","zh":"something a bit different意思是與其他活動稍為不同的事情。"},{"en":"After building models, students may try something a bit different, such as making a short film.","zh":"製作模型後，學生可能嘗試有點不同的活動，例如製作短片。"},{"en":"Different activities keep learners interested and prevent boredom.","zh":"不同活動能保持學習者興趣並防止沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces variety.","zh":"這個短語引入多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"think up an idea","meaning":"想出一個點子","examples":[{"en":"The children think up an idea for a five-minute movie.","zh":"孩子為一段五分鐘短片想出一個點子。"},{"en":"To think up an idea means to invent or create an idea in your mind.","zh":"think up an idea意思是在腦中創造或構思一個想法。"},{"en":"Students may think up an idea for a story before drawing the characters.","zh":"學生可能在畫角色前先為故事想出一個點子。"},{"en":"Thinking up ideas helps children practise imagination and planning.","zh":"想出點子能幫助孩子練習想像力和規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creative invention.","zh":"這個短語描述創意構思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a five-minute movie","meaning":"五分鐘短片","examples":[{"en":"The children make a five-minute movie using animation software.","zh":"孩子使用動畫軟件製作五分鐘短片。"},{"en":"A five-minute movie is a short film that lasts about five minutes.","zh":"five-minute movie是長約五分鐘的短片。"},{"en":"A class may make a five-minute movie to explain a science experiment.","zh":"班級可能製作五分鐘短片來解釋科學實驗。"},{"en":"Short movies help children learn storytelling without making the project too long.","zh":"短片能幫助孩子學習說故事，而不會令項目太長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the length and type of the project.","zh":"這個短語描述項目的長度和類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"film it","meaning":"把它拍攝下來","examples":[{"en":"The children think up an idea and then film it.","zh":"孩子想出一個點子，然後把它拍攝下來。"},{"en":"To film it means to record it as a video or movie.","zh":"film it意思是把它錄製成影片或短片。"},{"en":"Students may act out a scene and film it with a tablet.","zh":"學生可能演出一個場景，然後用平板電腦把它拍攝下來。"},{"en":"Filming an idea helps children turn imagination into a finished product.","zh":"拍攝想法能幫助孩子把想像變成完成品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recording a planned idea.","zh":"這個短語描述記錄已規劃好的點子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"animation software","meaning":"動畫軟件","examples":[{"en":"The children use special animation software to make a movie.","zh":"孩子使用特別動畫軟件製作短片。"},{"en":"Animation software is a computer programme used to create moving images.","zh":"animation software是用來創作動態影像的電腦程式。"},{"en":"Children may use animation software to make characters walk, jump or speak.","zh":"孩子可能使用動畫軟件令角色行走、跳躍或說話。"},{"en":"The software helps students create films without needing real actors or cameras.","zh":"這款軟件幫助學生不需要真人演員或相機也能製作影片。"},{"en":"This phrase names a digital tool for making animations.","zh":"這個短語命名製作動畫的數碼工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come up with","meaning":"想出","examples":[{"en":"You would be amazed what the children come up with.","zh":"你會驚訝於孩子想出的東西。"},{"en":"To come up with something means to think of or create an idea, answer or plan.","zh":"come up with某物，意思是想出或創造一個想法、答案或計劃。"},{"en":"Students can come up with surprising designs when they work in teams.","zh":"學生組隊工作時，可以想出令人驚喜的設計。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests creativity and originality.","zh":"這個短語常暗示創意和原創性。"},{"en":"It is common when talking about ideas.","zh":"它常用於談論想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put something on one’s phone","meaning":"把某物放到手機上","examples":[{"en":"The children can put the movie on their phone.","zh":"孩子可以把短片放到手機上。"},{"en":"To put something on one’s phone means to save or transfer it onto a mobile phone.","zh":"put something on one’s phone意思是把某物儲存或轉移到手機上。"},{"en":"A student may put a video project on her phone to show her parents.","zh":"學生可能把影片專題放到手機上，展示給父母看。"},{"en":"Saving work on a phone makes it easy to carry and share.","zh":"把作品儲存在手機上，能方便攜帶和分享。"},{"en":"This phrase describes storing digital content on a phone.","zh":"這個短語描述把數碼內容存到手機上。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take something home","meaning":"把某物帶回家","examples":[{"en":"The children can take the movie home to show their friends.","zh":"孩子可以把短片帶回家，展示給朋友看。"},{"en":"To take something home means to bring it back to one’s home after an activity.","zh":"take something home意思是在活動後把某物帶回自己家中。"},{"en":"Children like to take craft projects home after a workshop.","zh":"孩子喜歡在工作坊後把手工作品帶回家。"},{"en":"Taking work home lets families see what the child has created.","zh":"把作品帶回家能讓家人看見孩子創作了甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing away a finished product.","zh":"這個短語描述把完成品帶走。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"show someone something","meaning":"把某物展示給某人看","examples":[{"en":"The children can show the movie to all their friends.","zh":"孩子可以把短片展示給所有朋友看。"},{"en":"To show someone something means to let someone see it.","zh":"show someone something意思是讓某人看某物。"},{"en":"A child may show her robot to her classmates after finishing it.","zh":"孩子完成機械人後，可能把它展示給同學看。"},{"en":"Showing finished work can make children feel proud of what they made.","zh":"展示完成作品可以令孩子為自己的創作感到自豪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sharing a result with others.","zh":"這個短語描述與他人分享成果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the shape of","meaning":"呈……形狀","examples":[{"en":"The children build a robot in the shape of a human.","zh":"孩子建造一個呈人形的機械人。"},{"en":"In the shape of something means having the form or outline of that thing.","zh":"in the shape of某物，意思是具有該物的形態或輪廓。"},{"en":"Children may make biscuits in the shape of stars.","zh":"孩子可能製作星形餅乾。"},{"en":"A robot in the shape of a human may have a head, arms and legs.","zh":"呈人形的機械人可能有頭、手臂和雙腳。"},{"en":"This phrase describes appearance or form.","zh":"這個短語描述外觀或形態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"decorate it","meaning":"裝飾它","examples":[{"en":"The children decorate the robot after building it.","zh":"孩子建好機械人後會裝飾它。"},{"en":"To decorate it means to make it look more attractive by adding colours, shapes or details.","zh":"decorate it意思是透過加入顏色、形狀或細節令它更吸引。"},{"en":"Students may decorate a model car with paint and stickers.","zh":"學生可能用顏料和貼紙裝飾模型車。"},{"en":"Decoration lets children personalise a model after the engineering work is done.","zh":"裝飾讓孩子在完成工程部分後，把模型個人化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding visual details.","zh":"這個短語描述加入視覺細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"move its arms and legs","meaning":"移動手臂和雙腳","examples":[{"en":"The robot can move its arms and legs after being programmed.","zh":"機械人經編程後可以移動手臂和雙腳。"},{"en":"To move its arms and legs means to make the robot’s limbs move.","zh":"move its arms and legs意思是令機械人的四肢移動。"},{"en":"A simple robot may move its arms and legs using motors and joints.","zh":"簡單機械人可能使用摩打和關節移動手臂和雙腳。"},{"en":"Moving parts make a model feel more lifelike and exciting.","zh":"可移動部分令模型感覺更像真的，也更有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mechanical movement.","zh":"這個短語描述機械動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the same price as","meaning":"與……同價","examples":[{"en":"The father asks whether Junior Engineers is the same price as Tiny Engineers.","zh":"父親問Junior Engineers是否與Tiny Engineers同價。"},{"en":"The same price as means costing exactly the same amount as something else.","zh":"the same price as意思是價錢與另一物完全相同。"},{"en":"The art class is the same price as the science class.","zh":"藝術班與科學班同價。"},{"en":"Parents compare prices when deciding between courses for children.","zh":"家長在為孩子選擇課程時會比較價錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to compare costs.","zh":"這個短語用於比較費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"just a bit more","meaning":"只是貴一點","examples":[{"en":"The Junior Engineers workshop costs just a bit more.","zh":"Junior Engineers工作坊只是貴一點。"},{"en":"Just a bit more means only a little more in amount or price.","zh":"just a bit more意思是數量或價錢只多一點。"},{"en":"The longer workshop costs just a bit more than the shorter one.","zh":"較長的工作坊比短的只是貴一點。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the extra cost sound small.","zh":"這個短語令額外費用聽起來很少。"},{"en":"It is common when explaining a price difference.","zh":"它常見於解釋價錢差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for the five weeks","meaning":"五個星期的費用","examples":[{"en":"The Junior Engineers workshop costs £50 for the five weeks.","zh":"Junior Engineers工作坊五個星期的費用是50英鎊。"},{"en":"For the five weeks means covering the whole five-week period.","zh":"for the five weeks意思是涵蓋整個五星期期間。"},{"en":"The course costs £80 for the five weeks, including all materials.","zh":"課程五個星期的費用是80英鎊，包括所有材料。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what period the price covers.","zh":"這個短語解釋價錢涵蓋哪段時間。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing course fees.","zh":"它適合用於討論課程費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"used to be","meaning":"以前是……","examples":[{"en":"The Junior Engineers classes used to be on Mondays.","zh":"Junior Engineers課堂以前是在星期一。"},{"en":"Used to be means something was true in the past but is not true now.","zh":"used to be意思是某事過去屬實，但現在不再如此。"},{"en":"The library used to be closed on Sundays, but now it opens every day.","zh":"圖書館以前星期日關門，但現在每天開放。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining changes over time.","zh":"這個短語適合用於解釋隨時間出現的改變。"},{"en":"It contrasts the past with the present.","zh":"它把過去與現在作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"clear up after","meaning":"在……之後清理","examples":[{"en":"The staff needed more time to clear up after the first workshop.","zh":"職員需要更多時間在第一個工作坊之後清理。"},{"en":"To clear up after something means to clean and tidy the place once it has finished.","zh":"clear up after某事，意思是在它結束後清潔和整理地方。"},{"en":"Teachers may need time to clear up after a messy art lesson.","zh":"老師可能需要時間在混亂的美術課後清理。"},{"en":"Clearing up after practical activities can take longer than expected.","zh":"實踐活動後的清理可能比預期更花時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cleaning after an event or activity.","zh":"這個短語描述活動後清潔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"move them to Wednesdays","meaning":"把它們改到星期三","examples":[{"en":"The organisers moved the Junior Engineers classes to Wednesdays.","zh":"主辦方把Junior Engineers課堂改到星期三。"},{"en":"To move them to Wednesdays means to change their scheduled day to Wednesday.","zh":"move them to Wednesdays意思是把它們的上課日改為星期三。"},{"en":"The school moved music lessons to Wednesdays because the hall was free then.","zh":"學校把音樂課改到星期三，因為那時禮堂有空。"},{"en":"Changing the day can solve timetable or room problems.","zh":"更改日子可以解決時間表或房間問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a schedule change.","zh":"這個短語描述時間安排改動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be held in the morning","meaning":"在上午舉行","examples":[{"en":"The classes are held in the morning.","zh":"課堂在上午舉行。"},{"en":"To be held in the morning means to take place before midday.","zh":"be held in the morning意思是在中午前舉行。"},{"en":"Young children’s workshops are often held in the morning when they have more energy.","zh":"年幼孩子的工作坊常在上午舉行，因為他們較有精神。"},{"en":"Morning classes may be easier for families who prefer early schedules.","zh":"上午課堂對喜歡早些安排的家庭可能較方便。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the time of day for an event.","zh":"這個短語描述活動在一天中的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"from ten to eleven","meaning":"由十時至十一時","examples":[{"en":"The classes are held from ten to eleven.","zh":"課堂由十時至十一時舉行。"},{"en":"From ten to eleven means from 10:00 to 11:00.","zh":"from ten to eleven意思是由10:00到11:00。"},{"en":"The swimming lesson runs from ten to eleven every Saturday.","zh":"游泳課每星期六由十時至十一時舉行。"},{"en":"Clear start and finish times help parents plan transport.","zh":"清楚開始和結束時間有助家長安排交通。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the exact time period.","zh":"這個短語給出確切時間段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"that’s better for me","meaning":"那對我更方便","examples":[{"en":"The father says Wednesday morning is better for him.","zh":"父親說星期三上午對他更方便。"},{"en":"That’s better for me means that option is more convenient or suitable for me.","zh":"that’s better for me意思是那個選項對我更方便或更合適。"},{"en":"If a lesson is moved to Friday afternoon, a parent may say, “That’s better for me.”","zh":"如果課堂改到星期五下午，家長可能說：「那對我更方便。」"},{"en":"This phrase explains personal convenience.","zh":"這個短語解釋個人方便程度。"},{"en":"It is common in scheduling conversations.","zh":"它常見於時間安排對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"what about the location?","meaning":"地點方面怎樣？","examples":[{"en":"The father asks about the location of the workshops.","zh":"父親詢問工作坊地點方面怎樣。"},{"en":"What about the location? means where is it, or what should I know about the place?","zh":"what about the location?意思是地點在哪裏，或關於地點我需要知道甚麼？"},{"en":"After asking about price and time, parents often ask, “What about the location?”","zh":"問完價錢和時間後，家長常會問：「地點方面怎樣？」"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the next practical question.","zh":"這個短語引入下一個實際問題。"},{"en":"It is useful when gathering details about an event.","zh":"當收集活動詳情時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"where exactly","meaning":"確切在哪裏","examples":[{"en":"The father asks where exactly the workshops are held.","zh":"父親問工作坊確切在哪裏舉行。"},{"en":"Where exactly means the precise place, not just the general area.","zh":"where exactly意思是精確地點，而不只是大概區域。"},{"en":"A parent may ask where exactly the classroom is inside a large school.","zh":"家長可能問課室確切在大型學校內哪裏。"},{"en":"Exact location details help people arrive on time and avoid confusion.","zh":"確切地點資料能幫助人準時到達並避免混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for specific directions.","zh":"這個短語用來詢問具體方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be held","meaning":"舉行","examples":[{"en":"The workshops are held in building 10A.","zh":"工作坊在10A大樓舉行。"},{"en":"To be held means to take place or be organised at a particular time or place.","zh":"be held意思是在特定時間或地方進行或舉辦。"},{"en":"The parents’ meeting will be held in the school hall.","zh":"家長會將在學校禮堂舉行。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in announcements about events and classes.","zh":"這個短語常見於活動和課堂公告。"},{"en":"It tells people where or when something happens.","zh":"它告訴人們某事在哪裏或何時發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"building 10A","meaning":"10A 大樓","examples":[{"en":"The workshops are held in building 10A.","zh":"工作坊在10A大樓舉行。"},{"en":"Building 10A is the specific building where the workshops take place.","zh":"building 10A是工作坊舉行的特定建築物。"},{"en":"Visitors should check signs carefully if several buildings have similar numbers.","zh":"如果幾座大樓編號相似，訪客應仔細查看標誌。"},{"en":"Building numbers help people find the correct place in a large site.","zh":"大樓編號幫助人在大型場地中找到正確位置。"},{"en":"This phrase functions as a location label.","zh":"這個短語像位置標籤一樣使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a big sign on the door","meaning":"門上的大型標誌","examples":[{"en":"There is a big sign on the door of building 10A.","zh":"10A大樓門上有大型標誌。"},{"en":"A big sign on the door is a large notice attached to the entrance.","zh":"big sign on the door是貼在入口處的大型告示。"},{"en":"A big sign on the door can help visitors know they have arrived at the right room.","zh":"門上的大型標誌可以幫助訪客知道自己到了正確房間。"},{"en":"Clear signs reduce confusion for parents and children.","zh":"清晰標誌能減少家長和孩子的混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visible direction marker.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的方向標示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"you can’t miss it","meaning":"你不會錯過；很容易找到","examples":[{"en":"The building has a big sign, so visitors cannot miss it.","zh":"大樓有大型標誌，所以訪客不會錯過。"},{"en":"You can’t miss it means it is very easy to see or find.","zh":"you can’t miss it意思是它很容易看見或找到。"},{"en":"The reception desk is bright blue, so you can’t miss it.","zh":"接待處是鮮藍色的，所以你不會錯過。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures someone that directions are easy to follow.","zh":"這個短語讓對方放心，表示方向很容易跟。"},{"en":"It is common when giving directions.","zh":"它常見於指路時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"industrial estate","meaning":"工業邨","examples":[{"en":"The workshops are held in Fradstone Industrial Estate.","zh":"工作坊在Fradstone Industrial Estate舉行。"},{"en":"An industrial estate is an area with factories, warehouses or business buildings.","zh":"industrial estate是有工廠、倉庫或商業大樓的區域。"},{"en":"Some training centres are located in industrial estates because there is more space.","zh":"有些培訓中心位於工業邨，因為那裏空間較多。"},{"en":"Industrial estates may be less familiar to parents than schools or community centres.","zh":"工業邨對家長來說可能不如學校或社區中心熟悉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the type of area where the workshops are held.","zh":"這個短語描述工作坊所在區域的類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"up past the station","meaning":"過了車站再往前","examples":[{"en":"Fradstone Industrial Estate is up past the station.","zh":"Fradstone Industrial Estate在過了車站再往前的位置。"},{"en":"Up past the station means further along the road after you pass the station.","zh":"up past the station意思是沿路走，過了車站再往前。"},{"en":"The sports centre is up past the station, on the left after the bridge.","zh":"體育中心在過了車站再往前、過橋後左邊的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and used when giving directions.","zh":"這個短語較口語，用於指路時。"},{"en":"It helps someone understand the route from a known landmark.","zh":"它幫助人從已知地標理解路線。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"parking problems","meaning":"泊車問題","examples":[{"en":"The father asks whether he will have any parking problems there.","zh":"父親問自己在那裏會否有泊車問題。"},{"en":"Parking problems are difficulties finding a place to park a car.","zh":"parking problems是難以找到泊車位的問題。"},{"en":"Parents may worry about parking problems when a class is held in a busy area.","zh":"當課堂在繁忙地區舉行，家長可能擔心泊車問題。"},{"en":"Parking problems can make families late or stressed before an activity.","zh":"泊車問題可以令家庭遲到或在活動前感到壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical transport concern.","zh":"這個短語描述實際交通顧慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"plenty available","meaning":"有很多可用位置","examples":[{"en":"There is always plenty of parking available.","zh":"那裏總是有很多可用泊車位。"},{"en":"Plenty available means there is more than enough ready to use.","zh":"plenty available意思是有足夠甚至更多可用的東西。"},{"en":"At the sports centre, there are usually plenty of seats available in the morning.","zh":"在體育中心，上午通常有很多可用座位。"},{"en":"If parking is plenty available, visitors do not need to worry about arriving early.","zh":"如果泊車位很多，訪客就不用擔心要很早到達。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures people that supply is sufficient.","zh":"這個短語讓人放心，表示供應充足。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"enrol someone","meaning":"為某人報名","examples":[{"en":"The father decides to enrol Lydia and Carly in the workshops.","zh":"父親決定為Lydia和Carly報名參加工作坊。"},{"en":"To enrol someone means to register that person for a course, class or activity.","zh":"enrol someone意思是為某人登記參加課程、班級或活動。"},{"en":"Parents may enrol their children in swimming lessons before the summer holidays.","zh":"家長可能在暑假前為孩子報名游泳課。"},{"en":"Enrolling usually requires giving names, ages and contact details.","zh":"報名通常需要提供姓名、年齡和聯絡資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in course registration.","zh":"這個短語常見於課程登記。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"full name","meaning":"全名","examples":[{"en":"Sarah asks the father for his full name.","zh":"Sarah請父親提供他的全名。"},{"en":"Full name means a person’s complete name, usually including first name and surname.","zh":"full name意思是一個人的完整姓名，通常包括名字和姓氏。"},{"en":"A registration form may ask for the parent’s full name and phone number.","zh":"報名表可能要求填寫家長全名和電話號碼。"},{"en":"Giving a full name helps staff keep accurate records.","zh":"提供全名有助職員保持準確記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in forms, bookings and official conversations.","zh":"這個短語常見於表格、預訂和正式對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8}],"ielts/listening/Practice 16/task-2":[{"front":"one of the country’s major manufacturers","meaning":"全國主要製造商之一","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s is one of the country’s major manufacturers of metal goods.","zh":"Stevenson’s是全國主要金屬製品製造商之一。"},{"en":"One of the country’s major manufacturers means one of the most important companies that makes products in the country.","zh":"one of the country’s major manufacturers意思是該國其中一間最重要的產品製造公司。"},{"en":"A company may become one of the country’s major manufacturers if it supplies many shops and factories.","zh":"如果一間公司供應許多商店和工廠，它可能成為全國主要製造商之一。"},{"en":"Major manufacturers often employ many workers and produce goods on a large scale.","zh":"主要製造商通常僱用很多工人，並大規模生產貨品。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a company is large and important in its industry.","zh":"這個短語顯示公司在行業中規模大而重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"metal goods","meaning":"金屬製品","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s is a major manufacturer of metal goods.","zh":"Stevenson’s是一間主要金屬製品製造商。"},{"en":"Metal goods are products made from metal.","zh":"metal goods是由金屬製成的產品。"},{"en":"Tools, machine parts and metal frames are examples of metal goods.","zh":"工具、機器零件和金屬框架都是金屬製品的例子。"},{"en":"A company that makes metal goods often needs specialist machinery and skilled workers.","zh":"製造金屬製品的公司通常需要專門機械和熟練工人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the type of products a manufacturer produces.","zh":"這個短語描述製造商生產的產品類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"work experience","meaning":"工作體驗","examples":[{"en":"The students have chosen Stevenson’s for two weeks of work experience.","zh":"學生選擇到Stevenson’s進行兩星期工作體驗。"},{"en":"Work experience is a short period spent in a workplace to learn about real jobs.","zh":"work experience是在工作場所短期學習真實工作的經驗。"},{"en":"Students may do work experience in a factory, office, hospital or school.","zh":"學生可能在工廠、辦公室、醫院或學校進行工作體驗。"},{"en":"Work experience helps young people understand what different careers are really like.","zh":"工作體驗幫助年輕人了解不同職業的真實情況。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in school and career education.","zh":"這個短語常見於學校和職業教育。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"managing director","meaning":"董事總經理","examples":[{"en":"Julia Simmons has been the managing director since the beginning of this year.","zh":"Julia Simmons自今年年初以來一直擔任董事總經理。"},{"en":"A managing director is a senior manager who is responsible for running a company.","zh":"managing director是負責營運公司的高級管理人員。"},{"en":"The managing director makes important decisions about strategy, staff and business growth.","zh":"董事總經理會就策略、人手和業務增長作出重要決定。"},{"en":"In many companies, the managing director is one of the most powerful leaders.","zh":"在許多公司中，董事總經理是最有權力的領導之一。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a high-level business position.","zh":"這個短語描述高層商業職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"since the beginning of","meaning":"自……開始以來","examples":[{"en":"Julia Simmons has been managing director since the beginning of this year.","zh":"Julia Simmons自今年年初以來一直擔任董事總經理。"},{"en":"Since the beginning of a period means from the start of that period until now or a later time.","zh":"since the beginning of某段時間，意思是從該時段開始直到現在或之後某時。"},{"en":"The new manager has worked here since the beginning of June.","zh":"新經理自六月初以來一直在這裏工作。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show when a role, activity or situation started.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示某角色、活動或情況何時開始。"},{"en":"It is often used with present perfect tense.","zh":"它常與現在完成式一起使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"quite an old company","meaning":"相當老牌的公司","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s is quite an old company.","zh":"Stevenson’s是一間相當老牌的公司。"},{"en":"Quite an old company means a company that has existed for a fairly long time.","zh":"quite an old company意思是已存在相當長時間的公司。"},{"en":"A company founded nearly a hundred years ago can be described as quite an old company.","zh":"一間差不多一百年前創立的公司，可以稱為相當老牌的公司。"},{"en":"Old companies often have traditions, history and long-standing customers.","zh":"老牌公司通常有傳統、歷史和長期客戶。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the age and history of a business.","zh":"這個短語突顯企業的年資和歷史。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"founder","meaning":"創辦人","examples":[{"en":"Ronald Stevenson was the founder of Stevenson’s.","zh":"Ronald Stevenson是Stevenson’s的創辦人。"},{"en":"A founder is the person who starts a company, organisation or institution.","zh":"founder是創立公司、組織或機構的人。"},{"en":"The founder of a business often shapes its early values and direction.","zh":"企業創辦人通常塑造公司早期價值和方向。"},{"en":"People may remember a founder because the company carries their name or ideas.","zh":"人們可能因公司沿用創辦人的名字或理念而記住他。"},{"en":"This word identifies the person who created something.","zh":"這個詞指出創立某事的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"go into the steel industry","meaning":"進入鋼鐵業","examples":[{"en":"Ronald Stevenson went into the steel industry when he left school.","zh":"Ronald Stevenson離校後進入鋼鐵業。"},{"en":"To go into the steel industry means to start working in the business of producing or using steel.","zh":"go into the steel industry意思是開始從事生產或使用鋼材的行業。"},{"en":"A young worker may go into the steel industry as an apprentice.","zh":"年輕工人可能以學徒身份進入鋼鐵業。"},{"en":"People often go into an industry because of training, family links or available jobs.","zh":"人們進入某個行業，常因培訓、家庭關係或可獲得工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes entering a particular field of work.","zh":"這個短語描述進入某個特定工作領域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"steel industry","meaning":"鋼鐵業","examples":[{"en":"Ronald Stevenson went into the steel industry in 1923.","zh":"Ronald Stevenson於1923年進入鋼鐵業。"},{"en":"The steel industry is the business of making, processing and selling steel.","zh":"steel industry是製造、加工和銷售鋼材的行業。"},{"en":"The steel industry supplies materials for buildings, vehicles and machinery.","zh":"鋼鐵業為建築物、車輛和機械供應材料。"},{"en":"Work in the steel industry can involve factories, furnaces, machines and skilled labour.","zh":"鋼鐵業工作可能涉及工廠、熔爐、機器和熟練勞工。"},{"en":"This phrase names an important heavy industry.","zh":"這個短語命名一個重要重工業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"set up this company","meaning":"創立這間公司","examples":[{"en":"Ronald Stevenson set up this company in 1926.","zh":"Ronald Stevenson於1926年創立這間公司。"},{"en":"To set up this company means to start or establish this business.","zh":"set up this company意思是開始或創辦這間企業。"},{"en":"A young engineer may set up a company after gaining experience in a factory.","zh":"年輕工程師可能在工廠累積經驗後創立公司。"},{"en":"Setting up a company requires planning, money, customers and determination.","zh":"創立公司需要規劃、資金、客戶和決心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of a business.","zh":"這個短語描述企業的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"finish his apprenticeship","meaning":"完成學徒訓練","examples":[{"en":"Ronald Stevenson set up the company when he finished his apprenticeship.","zh":"Ronald Stevenson完成學徒訓練後創立公司。"},{"en":"To finish his apprenticeship means to complete a period of practical training in a trade.","zh":"finish his apprenticeship意思是完成某行業的一段實務培訓。"},{"en":"A mechanic may open a small garage after finishing his apprenticeship.","zh":"技工完成學徒訓練後，可能開設小型修車房。"},{"en":"Finishing an apprenticeship gives a worker skills and confidence to work independently.","zh":"完成學徒訓練能讓工人獲得技能和獨立工作的信心。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the end of formal practical training.","zh":"這個短語標誌正式實務培訓的結束。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"apprenticeship","meaning":"學徒訓練","examples":[{"en":"Ronald Stevenson finished his apprenticeship in 1926.","zh":"Ronald Stevenson於1926年完成學徒訓練。"},{"en":"An apprenticeship is a period of training where someone learns a trade by working with skilled people.","zh":"apprenticeship是一段透過與熟練人士工作來學習行業技能的培訓。"},{"en":"Apprenticeships are common in fields such as engineering, construction and cooking.","zh":"學徒訓練常見於工程、建築和烹飪等領域。"},{"en":"During an apprenticeship, learners gain practical skills rather than only classroom knowledge.","zh":"在學徒訓練期間，學習者獲得實用技能，而不只是課堂知識。"},{"en":"This word describes work-based training.","zh":"這個詞描述以工作為本的培訓。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"started making plans","meaning":"開始制訂計劃","examples":[{"en":"Ronald Stevenson actually started making plans two years earlier.","zh":"Ronald Stevenson其實早在兩年前已開始制訂計劃。"},{"en":"Started making plans means began preparing ideas or steps for a future goal.","zh":"started making plans意思是開始為未來目標準備想法或步驟。"},{"en":"A student may start making plans for university before the final exam results arrive.","zh":"學生可能在最終考試成績公布前已開始制訂大學計劃。"},{"en":"Planning early can help people act quickly when the right moment comes.","zh":"及早規劃可以幫助人在合適時機出現時快速行動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows preparation before action.","zh":"這個短語顯示行動前的準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"determined young man","meaning":"很有決心的年輕人","examples":[{"en":"Ronald Stevenson was a very determined young man.","zh":"Ronald Stevenson是一個很有決心的年輕人。"},{"en":"A determined young man is a young person who is strongly committed to achieving a goal.","zh":"determined young man是非常堅定地想達成目標的年輕人。"},{"en":"A determined young man may keep working even when money and support are limited.","zh":"很有決心的年輕人即使資金和支援有限，也可能繼續努力。"},{"en":"Determination helps people continue after setbacks.","zh":"決心幫助人在遇到挫折後繼續前進。"},{"en":"This phrase praises strength of will.","zh":"這個短語讚賞意志力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"long-term plan","meaning":"長遠計劃","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s long-term plan was to manufacture components.","zh":"Stevenson’s的長遠計劃是製造零件。"},{"en":"A long-term plan is a plan for the future over a long period.","zh":"long-term plan是針對較長時間未來的計劃。"},{"en":"A company’s long-term plan may include expanding factories and entering new markets.","zh":"公司的長遠計劃可能包括擴建工廠和進入新市場。"},{"en":"Long-term plans help businesses make decisions beyond immediate needs.","zh":"長遠計劃幫助企業作出超越即時需要的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes future strategy.","zh":"這個短語描述未來策略。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"manufacture components","meaning":"製造零件","examples":[{"en":"The company planned to manufacture components for the automotive industry.","zh":"公司計劃為汽車業製造零件。"},{"en":"To manufacture components means to produce parts used in larger machines or products.","zh":"manufacture components意思是生產用於較大型機器或產品的部件。"},{"en":"A factory may manufacture components for bicycles, computers or cars.","zh":"工廠可能為單車、電腦或汽車製造零件。"},{"en":"Component manufacturing requires accuracy because each part must fit correctly.","zh":"零件製造需要準確，因為每個部件都必須正確配合。"},{"en":"This phrase describes industrial production of parts.","zh":"這個短語描述工業零件生產。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"machine tools industry","meaning":"工具機行業","examples":[{"en":"The company wanted to manufacture components for the machine tools industry.","zh":"公司想為工具機行業製造零件。"},{"en":"The machine tools industry makes machines used to cut, shape or work on metal and other materials.","zh":"machine tools industry製造用來切割、塑形或加工金屬及其他材料的機器。"},{"en":"Factories depend on the machine tools industry for equipment that makes precise parts.","zh":"工廠依賴工具機行業提供製作精密零件的設備。"},{"en":"Supplying this industry would require strong technical knowledge.","zh":"供應這個行業需要強大的技術知識。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specialist manufacturing sector.","zh":"這個短語命名一個專門製造業範疇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, the plan to supply the machine tools industry never came about.","zh":"事實上，供應工具機行業的計劃從未實現。"},{"en":"In fact introduces a true point, often one that corrects or adds to what was said before.","zh":"in fact引入真實情況，通常用來修正或補充之前所說的內容。"},{"en":"The company looked new, but in fact it had been operating for fifty years.","zh":"這間公司看起來很新，但事實上已營運五十年。"},{"en":"This phrase helps speakers give more accurate information.","zh":"這個短語幫助講者提供更準確資訊。"},{"en":"It often signals contrast with expectation.","zh":"它常表示與預期形成對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"never came about","meaning":"從未實現","examples":[{"en":"The plan to manufacture components for the machine tools industry never came about.","zh":"為工具機行業製造零件的計劃從未實現。"},{"en":"Never came about means never happened or was never achieved.","zh":"never came about意思是從未發生或從未達成。"},{"en":"The proposal for a new sports hall never came about because funding was not approved.","zh":"新體育館的提議因資金未獲批准而從未實現。"},{"en":"Plans sometimes never come about because circumstances change.","zh":"計劃有時因情況改變而從未實現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unrealised plan.","zh":"這個短語描述未能實現的計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"automotive industry","meaning":"汽車業","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s manufactured components for the automotive industry.","zh":"Stevenson’s為汽車業製造零件。"},{"en":"The automotive industry is the business of designing, making and selling vehicles.","zh":"automotive industry是設計、製造和銷售車輛的行業。"},{"en":"The automotive industry includes companies that produce cars, lorries and vehicle parts.","zh":"汽車業包括生產汽車、貨車和車輛零件的公司。"},{"en":"Supplying the automotive industry often requires high safety and quality standards.","zh":"供應汽車業通常需要高安全和質量標準。"},{"en":"This phrase names the vehicle manufacturing sector.","zh":"這個短語命名車輛製造業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cars and lorries","meaning":"汽車及貨車","examples":[{"en":"The automotive industry includes cars and lorries.","zh":"汽車業包括汽車及貨車。"},{"en":"Cars and lorries are vehicles used for carrying people and goods.","zh":"cars and lorries是用來載人和載貨的車輛。"},{"en":"Factories may make different parts for cars and lorries because their sizes and uses differ.","zh":"工廠可能為汽車及貨車製造不同零件，因為它們大小和用途不同。"},{"en":"Lorries often need stronger components than small cars.","zh":"貨車通常比小型汽車需要更堅固零件。"},{"en":"This phrase gives examples of road vehicles.","zh":"這個短語給出道路車輛的例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a delay of five years","meaning":"五年的延誤","examples":[{"en":"There was a delay of five years before the company worked for the automotive industry.","zh":"公司為汽車業工作之前出現了五年的延誤。"},{"en":"A delay of five years means something happened five years later than expected or planned.","zh":"delay of five years意思是某事比預期或計劃遲了五年發生。"},{"en":"A factory expansion may face a delay of five years if permission is refused.","zh":"如果許可被拒，工廠擴建可能面對五年的延誤。"},{"en":"Long delays can change a company’s opportunities and direction.","zh":"長時間延誤可以改變公司的機會和方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a significant postponement.","zh":"這個短語描述重大的推遲。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"shortly before","meaning":"就在……之前不久","examples":[{"en":"Shortly before the company went into production, Stevenson was given a new opportunity.","zh":"就在公司投產之前不久，Stevenson獲得了一個新機會。"},{"en":"Shortly before means a little time before something happened.","zh":"shortly before意思是在某事發生前不久。"},{"en":"Shortly before the meeting began, the manager changed the agenda.","zh":"就在會議開始前不久，經理更改了議程。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show the timing between two events.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示兩件事之間的時間關係。"},{"en":"It is often used when a new development occurs just before an important moment.","zh":"它常用於重要時刻前出現新發展的情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"go into production","meaning":"投產","examples":[{"en":"The company went into production after Stevenson received an opportunity.","zh":"Stevenson獲得機會後，公司開始投產。"},{"en":"To go into production means to start manufacturing goods.","zh":"go into production意思是開始製造產品。"},{"en":"A new product goes into production after the design and testing stages are complete.","zh":"新產品在設計和測試階段完成後投產。"},{"en":"Going into production is a major step because plans become real products.","zh":"投產是重大一步，因為計劃變成真實產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in manufacturing.","zh":"這個短語常見於製造業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be given the opportunity to","meaning":"獲得機會去……","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson was given the opportunity to make goods for hospitals.","zh":"Stevenson獲得機會為醫院製造產品。"},{"en":"To be given the opportunity to do something means to receive a chance to do it.","zh":"be given the opportunity to do something意思是獲得做某事的機會。"},{"en":"A young worker may be given the opportunity to train in a new department.","zh":"年輕員工可能獲得機會到新部門接受培訓。"},{"en":"Opportunities can change a person’s career or a company’s direction.","zh":"機會可以改變個人的職業或公司的方向。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a chance offered by someone else.","zh":"這個短語突顯由他人提供的機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"healthcare industry","meaning":"醫療保健業","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s made goods for hospitals and other players in the healthcare industry.","zh":"Stevenson’s為醫院和醫療保健業其他參與者製造產品。"},{"en":"The healthcare industry includes organisations that provide medical care, equipment or services.","zh":"healthcare industry包括提供醫療護理、設備或服務的機構。"},{"en":"Hospitals, clinics, medical suppliers and care homes are part of the healthcare industry.","zh":"醫院、診所、醫療供應商和護老院都是醫療保健業的一部分。"},{"en":"Products for the healthcare industry must often meet strict safety standards.","zh":"供應醫療保健業的產品通常必須符合嚴格安全標準。"},{"en":"This phrase names the medical and health-related business sector.","zh":"這個短語命名醫療和健康相關商業範疇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"over the years","meaning":"多年來","examples":[{"en":"Over the years, Stevenson’s has expanded the premises considerably.","zh":"多年來，Stevenson’s大幅擴建廠房。"},{"en":"Over the years means during a long period of time.","zh":"over the years意思是在很長一段時間裏。"},{"en":"Over the years, the small workshop became a large factory.","zh":"多年來，小工場變成大型工廠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing gradual change.","zh":"這個短語適合描述逐步變化。"},{"en":"It shows that development happened slowly rather than all at once.","zh":"它顯示發展是慢慢發生，而不是一次完成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"expand the premises","meaning":"擴建廠房；擴展場地","examples":[{"en":"The company has expanded the premises considerably.","zh":"公司已大幅擴建廠房。"},{"en":"To expand the premises means to make the company’s buildings or site larger.","zh":"expand the premises意思是擴大公司的建築物或場地。"},{"en":"A factory may expand the premises by adding a new warehouse.","zh":"工廠可能透過增建新倉庫來擴建廠房。"},{"en":"Expanding premises can allow more machines, workers and storage space.","zh":"擴建場地可以容納更多機器、工人和儲存空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical growth of a business site.","zh":"這個短語描述企業場地的實體增長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"considerably","meaning":"大幅地","examples":[{"en":"The company has expanded the premises considerably.","zh":"公司已大幅擴建廠房。"},{"en":"Considerably means by a large amount or to a great degree.","zh":"considerably意思是數量很大或程度很高地。"},{"en":"The number of employees has grown considerably since the company won new contracts.","zh":"自公司取得新合約後，員工人數大幅增加。"},{"en":"This word makes a change sound significant, not small.","zh":"這個詞令變化聽起來顯著，而不是微小。"},{"en":"It is common in formal descriptions of growth or change.","zh":"它常見於正式描述增長或改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the site is big enough","meaning":"場地足夠大","examples":[{"en":"The site is big enough, so the company has never had to move.","zh":"場地足夠大，所以公司從來不用搬遷。"},{"en":"The site is big enough means the land or premises have sufficient space.","zh":"the site is big enough意思是土地或場地有足夠空間。"},{"en":"If a school site is big enough, it can add new classrooms without moving.","zh":"如果學校場地足夠大，就可以在不搬遷的情況下增建課室。"},{"en":"Having enough space allows an organisation to grow in the same location.","zh":"有足夠空間讓機構可以在同一地點成長。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why relocation was unnecessary.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何不需要搬遷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"moving to a new location","meaning":"搬到新地點","examples":[{"en":"Moving to a new location has never been necessary.","zh":"搬到新地點從來沒有必要。"},{"en":"Moving to a new location means relocating to another place.","zh":"moving to a new location意思是搬遷到另一個地方。"},{"en":"Moving to a new location can be expensive for a factory because machines must be transported.","zh":"對工廠而言，搬到新地點可能很昂貴，因為機器必須運走。"},{"en":"Companies prefer to stay where they are if the existing site still works.","zh":"如果現有場地仍可用，公司通常較想留在原址。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relocation.","zh":"這個短語描述搬遷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"has never been necessary","meaning":"從來沒有必要","examples":[{"en":"Moving to a new location has never been necessary.","zh":"搬到新地點從來沒有必要。"},{"en":"Has never been necessary means has not been needed at any time.","zh":"has never been necessary意思是在任何時候都不需要。"},{"en":"Because the room is large enough, booking another hall has never been necessary.","zh":"因為房間足夠大，預訂另一個禮堂從來沒有必要。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that a need has never arisen.","zh":"這個短語強調某需要從未出現。"},{"en":"It is often used to explain why something was not done.","zh":"它常用於解釋為何某事沒有做。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"layout","meaning":"佈局","examples":[{"en":"The layout is far from ideal for modern machinery.","zh":"這個佈局對現代機械而言遠非理想。"},{"en":"Layout means the arrangement of rooms, buildings, machines or spaces.","zh":"layout意思是房間、建築物、機器或空間的安排方式。"},{"en":"A factory layout affects how quickly materials move from one stage to another.","zh":"工廠佈局會影響材料從一個階段移到另一個階段的速度。"},{"en":"A poor layout can waste time and make work less efficient.","zh":"差劣佈局會浪費時間，並令工作效率較低。"},{"en":"This word is common in building, design and production contexts.","zh":"這個詞常見於建築、設計和生產語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"far from ideal","meaning":"遠非理想","examples":[{"en":"The layout is far from ideal for modern machinery and production methods.","zh":"這個佈局對現代機械和生產方式而言遠非理想。"},{"en":"Far from ideal means not suitable or not as good as it should be.","zh":"far from ideal意思是不合適，或不如應有狀態那麼好。"},{"en":"A classroom with no windows and little space is far from ideal for group work.","zh":"沒有窗又空間狹小的課室，對小組活動而言遠非理想。"},{"en":"This phrase is a polite way to say that something has serious weaknesses.","zh":"這個短語是有禮地表示某事有嚴重不足。"},{"en":"It highlights a gap between the current situation and the best situation.","zh":"它突顯現況與最佳情況之間的差距。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"modern machinery","meaning":"現代機械","examples":[{"en":"The current layout is not ideal for modern machinery.","zh":"現有佈局不適合現代機械。"},{"en":"Modern machinery means up-to-date machines used in production or industry.","zh":"modern machinery是生產或工業中使用的先進機器。"},{"en":"Modern machinery can produce parts faster and more accurately than older machines.","zh":"現代機械可以比舊機器更快、更準確地生產零件。"},{"en":"Factories may need wider spaces and better power systems for modern machinery.","zh":"工廠可能需要更寬敞空間和更好電力系統來配合現代機械。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts newer equipment with older production tools.","zh":"這個短語把較新設備與舊式生產工具作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"production methods","meaning":"生產方式","examples":[{"en":"The layout is not ideal for modern production methods.","zh":"這個佈局不適合現代生產方式。"},{"en":"Production methods are the ways goods are made in a factory or workshop.","zh":"production methods是在工廠或工場製造產品的方法。"},{"en":"New production methods may use automation, digital monitoring or lean processes.","zh":"新生產方式可能使用自動化、數碼監察或精益流程。"},{"en":"Better production methods can reduce waste and improve quality.","zh":"更好的生產方式可以減少浪費並改善品質。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how manufacturing work is carried out.","zh":"這個短語描述製造工作如何進行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"intend to","meaning":"打算","examples":[{"en":"The company intends to carry out major refurbishment of the site.","zh":"公司打算對場地進行大規模翻新。"},{"en":"To intend to do something means to plan or mean to do it.","zh":"intend to do something意思是計劃或打算做某事。"},{"en":"The school intends to improve its science rooms next year.","zh":"學校打算明年改善科學室。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a future plan but not necessarily something already completed.","zh":"這個短語顯示未來計劃，但不一定已完成。"},{"en":"It is common in formal announcements.","zh":"它常見於正式公告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"carry out major refurbishment","meaning":"進行大規模翻新","examples":[{"en":"The company intends to carry out major refurbishment of the site.","zh":"公司打算對場地進行大規模翻新。"},{"en":"To carry out major refurbishment means to do large-scale repair, improvement or modernisation work.","zh":"carry out major refurbishment意思是進行大規模維修、改善或現代化工程。"},{"en":"A hotel may carry out major refurbishment to update its rooms and reception area.","zh":"酒店可能進行大規模翻新，以更新房間和接待區。"},{"en":"Major refurbishment can be expensive but may improve efficiency and appearance.","zh":"大規模翻新可能昂貴，但可以提升效率和外觀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large improvement project.","zh":"這個短語描述大型改善項目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"over the next five years","meaning":"在未來五年","examples":[{"en":"The company will refurbish the site over the next five years.","zh":"公司將在未來五年翻新場地。"},{"en":"Over the next five years means during the coming five-year period.","zh":"over the next five years意思是在接下來五年期間。"},{"en":"The school plans to improve its sports facilities over the next five years.","zh":"學校計劃在未來五年改善體育設施。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a future time frame for a plan.","zh":"這個短語為計劃提供未來時間框架。"},{"en":"It suggests that the work will happen gradually.","zh":"它暗示工作會逐步進行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"give you some idea of","meaning":"讓你大概了解……","examples":[{"en":"Julia gives the students some idea of what they will be doing.","zh":"Julia讓學生大概了解他們將會做甚麼。"},{"en":"To give you some idea of something means to help you understand it roughly.","zh":"give you some idea of某事，意思是幫助你大概理解它。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students some idea of what the exam will include.","zh":"老師可能讓學生大概了解考試會包括甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase does not promise every detail, only a general understanding.","zh":"這個短語不承諾提供每個細節，只提供一般理解。"},{"en":"It is useful when introducing a plan or schedule.","zh":"它適合用於介紹計劃或時間表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"know what to expect","meaning":"知道會有甚麼安排","examples":[{"en":"The students will know what to expect during their two weeks.","zh":"學生會知道兩星期期間會有甚麼安排。"},{"en":"To know what to expect means to understand what is likely to happen.","zh":"know what to expect意思是知道很可能會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"New students feel less nervous when they know what to expect on the first day.","zh":"新學生如果知道第一天會有甚麼安排，就會較不緊張。"},{"en":"Clear information helps people prepare mentally and practically.","zh":"清晰資訊能幫助人在心理和實際上作好準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being ready because the situation is explained.","zh":"這個短語描述因情況已被解釋而有所準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"most mornings","meaning":"大多數上午","examples":[{"en":"Most mornings, the students will have a presentation from one of the managers.","zh":"大多數上午，學生會聽取其中一位經理的簡報。"},{"en":"Most mornings means on the majority of mornings, but not necessarily every morning.","zh":"most mornings意思是在大部分上午，但不一定是每一個上午。"},{"en":"Most mornings, the class begins with a short review activity.","zh":"大多數上午，課堂會以簡短溫習活動開始。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a general pattern rather than an exact schedule.","zh":"這個短語給出一般模式，而不是精確時間表。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing repeated activities.","zh":"它適合用於描述重複活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have a presentation from","meaning":"聽取……的簡報","examples":[{"en":"The students will have a presentation from one of the managers.","zh":"學生會聽取其中一位經理的簡報。"},{"en":"To have a presentation from someone means to listen to that person give an organised talk.","zh":"have a presentation from某人，意思是聆聽該人作有組織的講解。"},{"en":"New employees may have a presentation from the safety manager on their first day.","zh":"新員工第一天可能聽取安全經理的簡報。"},{"en":"Presentations help visitors learn important information efficiently.","zh":"簡報幫助訪客有效率地學習重要資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving information through a formal talk.","zh":"這個短語描述透過正式講解接收資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"learn about their department","meaning":"了解他們的部門","examples":[{"en":"The students will learn about each manager’s department.","zh":"學生會了解每位經理的部門。"},{"en":"To learn about a department means to understand what it does and how it works.","zh":"learn about a department意思是了解該部門做甚麼和如何運作。"},{"en":"Students may learn about the finance department during a company visit.","zh":"學生在公司參觀期間可能了解財務部。"},{"en":"Learning about departments helps visitors see how a company is organised.","zh":"了解部門能幫助訪客看見公司如何組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gaining workplace knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述獲得職場知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"research and development","meaning":"研究及發展","examples":[{"en":"The first presentation is about research and development.","zh":"第一個簡報是關於研究及發展。"},{"en":"Research and development means work done to create new products or improve existing ones.","zh":"research and development是為創造新產品或改善現有產品而做的工作。"},{"en":"A company’s research and development team may test new materials for stronger products.","zh":"公司的研究及發展團隊可能測試新材料，以製造更堅固產品。"},{"en":"This department is important because innovation helps companies stay competitive.","zh":"這個部門很重要，因為創新幫助公司保持競爭力。"},{"en":"This phrase is often shortened to R&D.","zh":"這個短語常縮寫為R&D。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spend some time in","meaning":"在……逗留一段時間","examples":[{"en":"The students will spend some time in each department.","zh":"學生會在每個部門逗留一段時間。"},{"en":"To spend some time in a place means to stay there for a period to observe or take part.","zh":"spend some time in某地，意思是在那裏停留一段時間，以觀察或參與。"},{"en":"Work experience students may spend some time in the warehouse and the office.","zh":"工作體驗學生可能在倉庫和辦公室逗留一段時間。"},{"en":"Spending time in different areas helps learners compare how each part works.","zh":"在不同地方逗留能幫助學習者比較各部分如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes temporary experience in a place.","zh":"這個短語描述在某地的短暫經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"observing what’s going on","meaning":"觀察正在發生的事；了解運作","examples":[{"en":"The students will observe what is going on in each department.","zh":"學生會觀察每個部門正在發生的事。"},{"en":"Observing what’s going on means watching carefully to understand the activities happening there.","zh":"observing what’s going on意思是仔細觀看，以了解那裏正在進行的活動。"},{"en":"Visitors may observe what is going on in a factory before asking questions.","zh":"訪客可能先觀察工廠正在發生的事，然後才提問。"},{"en":"Observation helps students learn without interrupting workers.","zh":"觀察幫助學生在不打擾工人的情況下學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning by watching real activity.","zh":"這個短語描述透過觀看真實活動來學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"talk to people","meaning":"與人交談","examples":[{"en":"The students will talk to people in each department.","zh":"學生會與每個部門的人交談。"},{"en":"To talk to people means to speak with them and exchange information.","zh":"talk to people意思是與人說話並交換資訊。"},{"en":"Work experience students can talk to people about their jobs and training.","zh":"工作體驗學生可以與人交談，了解他們的工作和培訓。"},{"en":"Talking to staff gives visitors personal insight that documents may not provide.","zh":"與職員交談能給訪客文件未必提供的個人見解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct communication.","zh":"這個短語描述直接溝通。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as long as","meaning":"只要","examples":[{"en":"The students can talk to staff as long as they do not stop them working.","zh":"學生可以與職員交談，只要不阻礙他們工作。"},{"en":"As long as means provided that or on the condition that.","zh":"as long as意思是只要，或在某條件成立的情況下。"},{"en":"Students may use the computer room as long as they follow the rules.","zh":"學生只要遵守規則，就可以使用電腦室。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a condition that must be met.","zh":"這個短語引入必須滿足的條件。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving permission with limits.","zh":"它適合用於有條件地給予許可。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stop someone from doing","meaning":"阻止某人做……","examples":[{"en":"The students should not stop staff from doing their work.","zh":"學生不應阻止職員做自己的工作。"},{"en":"To stop someone from doing something means to prevent them from continuing or completing it.","zh":"stop someone from doing something意思是阻止某人繼續或完成某事。"},{"en":"Too many questions may stop a worker from finishing an urgent task.","zh":"太多問題可能阻止工人完成緊急任務。"},{"en":"Visitors should learn without preventing employees from working.","zh":"訪客應學習，但不應阻礙員工工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interference with someone’s activity.","zh":"這個短語描述對某人活動的干擾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"altogether","meaning":"完全地","examples":[{"en":"The students should not stop staff from doing their work altogether.","zh":"學生不應完全阻止職員工作。"},{"en":"Altogether means completely or entirely.","zh":"altogether意思是完全地或整體地。"},{"en":"If a machine breaks down, production may stop altogether.","zh":"如果機器故障，生產可能完全停止。"},{"en":"In this sentence, altogether stresses the idea of preventing work completely.","zh":"在這句中，altogether強調完全阻礙工作的意思。"},{"en":"This word often strengthens the meaning of a statement.","zh":"這個詞常用來加強陳述的意思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"以往","examples":[{"en":"In the past, a teacher came in at the end of each week.","zh":"以往，老師會在每星期結束時到來。"},{"en":"In the past means at an earlier time before now.","zh":"in the past意思是在現在以前的較早時間。"},{"en":"In the past, factories often kept records on paper rather than computers.","zh":"以往，工廠通常用紙本而不是電腦保存記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts former practice with the present situation.","zh":"這個短語把以前做法與現在情況作對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining changes.","zh":"它適合用於解釋改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at the end of each week","meaning":"在每星期結束時","examples":[{"en":"A teacher used to visit at the end of each week.","zh":"以前老師會在每星期結束時探訪。"},{"en":"At the end of each week means when every week is nearly finished.","zh":"at the end of each week意思是在每個星期差不多完結時。"},{"en":"Students may submit a short report at the end of each week.","zh":"學生可能在每星期結束時提交簡短報告。"},{"en":"Weekly check-ins help supervisors see how students are progressing.","zh":"每週檢查能幫助督導了解學生進展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regular timing.","zh":"這個短語描述定期時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"find out how","meaning":"了解……如何","examples":[{"en":"The teacher came in to find out how the group were getting on.","zh":"老師前來了解小組進展如何。"},{"en":"To find out how something is going means to learn about its progress or condition.","zh":"find out how某事進行，意思是了解其進展或情況。"},{"en":"A manager may call to find out how new staff are settling in.","zh":"經理可能致電了解新員工適應得如何。"},{"en":"Asking questions helps people discover whether support is needed.","zh":"提問有助人發現是否需要支援。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a check on progress.","zh":"這個短語引入對進展的查問。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get on","meaning":"進展；適應","examples":[{"en":"The teacher wanted to know how the group were getting on.","zh":"老師想知道小組進展如何。"},{"en":"To get on means to progress, cope or manage in a situation.","zh":"get on意思是在某情況中進展、應付或適應。"},{"en":"A tutor may ask students how they are getting on with their project.","zh":"導師可能問學生專題進展如何。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English when checking progress.","zh":"這個短語在英式英語中常用於查問進展。"},{"en":"It can refer to work, adjustment or general experience.","zh":"它可以指工作、適應或整體經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"arrange that","meaning":"安排那件事","examples":[{"en":"The school is not able to arrange that this year.","zh":"學校今年不能安排那件事。"},{"en":"To arrange that means to organise the thing just mentioned.","zh":"arrange that意思是安排剛才提到的事情。"},{"en":"If students need weekly visits, the teacher must arrange that with the company.","zh":"如果學生需要每週探訪，老師必須與公司安排那件事。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a specific arrangement already discussed.","zh":"這個短語指回已討論的特定安排。"},{"en":"It is useful when talking about practical organisation.","zh":"它適合用於談論實際組織工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"briefly help you to","meaning":"簡單幫你……","examples":[{"en":"Julia briefly helps the students to orientate themselves around the site.","zh":"Julia簡單幫學生熟悉場地方位。"},{"en":"To briefly help you to do something means to give short support or explanation so you can do it.","zh":"briefly help you to do something意思是提供簡短支援或解釋，讓你可以做到某事。"},{"en":"A receptionist may briefly help visitors to find the correct meeting room.","zh":"接待員可能簡單幫訪客找到正確會議室。"},{"en":"Brief help gives enough information without taking too much time.","zh":"簡短協助提供足夠資訊，又不花太多時間。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces quick practical guidance.","zh":"這個短語引入快速實用指引。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"orientate yourselves around","meaning":"熟悉……的方位","examples":[{"en":"The students need to orientate themselves around the site.","zh":"學生需要熟悉場地的方位。"},{"en":"To orientate yourselves around a place means to learn where things are and how to move around it.","zh":"orientate yourselves around某地，意思是了解各處位置和如何在其中移動。"},{"en":"New employees should orientate themselves around the building on their first day.","zh":"新員工第一天應熟悉大樓方位。"},{"en":"Knowing the layout helps people feel confident and avoid getting lost.","zh":"知道佈局能幫助人更有信心並避免迷路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming familiar with a location.","zh":"這個短語描述熟悉某個地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"around the site","meaning":"在場地四周","examples":[{"en":"Julia helps the students find their way around the site.","zh":"Julia幫助學生在場地四周認路。"},{"en":"Around the site means in different parts of the company’s land or buildings.","zh":"around the site意思是在公司土地或建築物的不同部分。"},{"en":"Visitors may need a map to move around the site safely.","zh":"訪客可能需要地圖，才能安全地在場地四周移動。"},{"en":"Large industrial sites can be confusing without clear directions.","zh":"大型工業場地如果沒有清晰指示，可能令人混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement within a workplace area.","zh":"這個短語描述在工作場所範圍內移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reception area","meaning":"接待區","examples":[{"en":"The group is standing in the reception area.","zh":"小組正站在接待區。"},{"en":"A reception area is the place near the entrance where visitors arrive and are greeted.","zh":"reception area是入口附近讓訪客到達和被接待的地方。"},{"en":"A company’s reception area may have seats, a desk and signs for visitors.","zh":"公司的接待區可能有座位、接待桌和訪客指示牌。"},{"en":"Reception areas create the first impression of a business.","zh":"接待區塑造企業給人的第一印象。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the visitor entrance space.","zh":"這個短語指訪客入口空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"attractive and welcoming","meaning":"吸引而令人感到受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The company tries to make the reception area attractive and welcoming.","zh":"公司嘗試令接待區吸引而令人感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"Attractive and welcoming means pleasant to look at and friendly to visitors.","zh":"attractive and welcoming意思是外觀看起來舒服，並對訪客友善。"},{"en":"Bright lighting and comfortable chairs can make a waiting room attractive and welcoming.","zh":"明亮燈光和舒適椅子可以令等候室吸引而令人感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"A welcoming space helps visitors feel relaxed and respected.","zh":"令人感到受歡迎的空間能幫助訪客放鬆並感到受尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both appearance and atmosphere.","zh":"這個短語同時描述外觀和氣氛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"welcoming to visitors","meaning":"令訪客感到受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The reception area is designed to be welcoming to visitors.","zh":"接待區設計成令訪客感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"Welcoming to visitors means making visitors feel comfortable, accepted and guided.","zh":"welcoming to visitors意思是令訪客感到舒適、被接納並得到指引。"},{"en":"Clear signs and polite staff make a building welcoming to visitors.","zh":"清晰標誌和有禮職員能令大樓令訪客感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"A workplace that welcomes visitors well appears organised and professional.","zh":"能好好接待訪客的工作場所會顯得有組織和專業。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the visitor’s experience.","zh":"這個短語著重訪客體驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"corridor running left from","meaning":"從……向左延伸的走廊","examples":[{"en":"There is a corridor running left from the reception area.","zh":"有一條從接待區向左延伸的走廊。"},{"en":"A corridor running left from a place means a hallway that extends to the left from that point.","zh":"corridor running left from某處，意思是從該點向左延伸的走廊。"},{"en":"There is a corridor running left from the main entrance towards the classrooms.","zh":"有一條從正門向左延伸、通往課室的走廊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for giving directions inside a building.","zh":"這個短語適合用於在建築物內指路。"},{"en":"It describes both direction and layout.","zh":"它同時描述方向和佈局。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"go along","meaning":"沿着……走","examples":[{"en":"If you go along the corridor, you will reach the coffee room.","zh":"如果你沿着走廊走，就會到達咖啡室。"},{"en":"To go along something means to move forward following its length or direction.","zh":"go along某物，意思是沿着它的長度或方向向前走。"},{"en":"Go along the path until you see the school office on your right.","zh":"沿着小路走，直到你看見校務處在右邊。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in directions.","zh":"這個短語常見於指路。"},{"en":"It tells someone to continue on the same route.","zh":"它告訴某人沿同一路線繼續走。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"facing you","meaning":"正對着你的","examples":[{"en":"The door facing you at the end is the entrance to the coffee room.","zh":"盡頭正對着你的門是咖啡室入口。"},{"en":"Facing you means positioned directly in front of you.","zh":"facing you意思是位於你正前方。"},{"en":"The noticeboard facing you as you enter shows today’s timetable.","zh":"你進入時正對着你的通告板顯示今天時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people identify an object by its position.","zh":"這個短語幫助人根據位置辨認物件。"},{"en":"It is useful in indoor directions.","zh":"它適合用於室內指路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at the end","meaning":"在盡頭","examples":[{"en":"The entrance to the coffee room is at the end of the corridor.","zh":"咖啡室入口在走廊盡頭。"},{"en":"At the end means at the furthest or final point of something.","zh":"at the end意思是在某物最遠或最後的位置。"},{"en":"The science lab is at the end of the hallway.","zh":"科學實驗室在走廊盡頭。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear position in relation to a path or space.","zh":"這個短語根據路線或空間提供清楚位置。"},{"en":"It is common in directions.","zh":"它常見於指路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"entrance to","meaning":"……的入口","examples":[{"en":"The door at the end is the entrance to the coffee room.","zh":"盡頭的門是咖啡室的入口。"},{"en":"The entrance to a place is the door or opening used to go into it.","zh":"entrance to某地，是進入該地方所用的門或開口。"},{"en":"Visitors should use the main entrance to the factory.","zh":"訪客應使用工廠的正門入口。"},{"en":"Knowing the entrance helps people find where to go in.","zh":"知道入口位置能幫助人找到從哪裏進入。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the access point to a room or building.","zh":"這個短語指出進入房間或建築物的通道。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"look out onto","meaning":"望向","examples":[{"en":"The coffee room looks out onto the main road on one side.","zh":"咖啡室其中一邊望向大路。"},{"en":"To look out onto something means to have a view of it from a window.","zh":"look out onto某物，意思是從窗戶望出去可看見它。"},{"en":"The classroom looks out onto a garden, so students can see trees outside.","zh":"課室望向花園，所以學生可以看見外面的樹。"},{"en":"Views from rooms can affect how pleasant a space feels.","zh":"房間景觀會影響空間感覺是否舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what can be seen from inside.","zh":"這個短語描述從室內可看見甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"main road","meaning":"大路；主要道路","examples":[{"en":"The coffee room looks out onto the main road.","zh":"咖啡室望向大路。"},{"en":"A main road is a large or important road with more traffic than smaller streets.","zh":"main road是較大或較重要的道路，交通量比小街多。"},{"en":"Factories are often near a main road so lorries can arrive easily.","zh":"工廠常位於大路附近，方便貨車到達。"},{"en":"Rooms facing a main road may be noisier than rooms facing trees.","zh":"面向大路的房間可能比面向樹木的房間較嘈。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important traffic route.","zh":"這個短語描述重要交通路線。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on one side","meaning":"在一邊","examples":[{"en":"The coffee room looks onto the main road on one side.","zh":"咖啡室一邊望向大路。"},{"en":"On one side means on one of the two or more sides of something.","zh":"on one side意思是在某物其中一邊。"},{"en":"The playground has classrooms on one side and trees on the other.","zh":"操場一邊是課室，另一邊是樹木。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare different directions or views.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較不同方向或景觀。"},{"en":"It is often paired with “on the other”.","zh":"它常與on the other配合使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on the other","meaning":"在另一邊","examples":[{"en":"The coffee room looks onto some trees on the other side.","zh":"咖啡室另一邊望向一些樹木。"},{"en":"On the other means on the opposite or another side.","zh":"on the other意思是在相反或另一邊。"},{"en":"The office has a car park on one side and a garden on the other.","zh":"辦公室一邊有停車場，另一邊有花園。"},{"en":"This phrase completes a comparison between two sides.","zh":"這個短語完成兩邊之間的比較。"},{"en":"It helps describe layout clearly.","zh":"它幫助清楚描述佈局。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"meet each morning","meaning":"每天早上集合","examples":[{"en":"The students will meet in the coffee room each morning.","zh":"學生每天早上會在咖啡室集合。"},{"en":"To meet each morning means to gather every morning or on each morning of a period.","zh":"meet each morning意思是每天早上或某段期間的每個上午集合。"},{"en":"Work experience students may meet each morning to receive instructions.","zh":"工作體驗學生可能每天早上集合接收指示。"},{"en":"Regular morning meetings help people know the plan for the day.","zh":"定期早會能幫助人知道當天計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated daily arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述重複的每日安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"far side of the site","meaning":"場地遠端","examples":[{"en":"The factory is on the far side of the site.","zh":"工廠位於場地遠端。"},{"en":"The far side of the site means the part that is furthest away from where you are.","zh":"far side of the site意思是場地中距離你所在位置最遠的一邊。"},{"en":"The sports hall is on the far side of the school campus.","zh":"體育館位於校園遠端。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people understand distance and direction within a large place.","zh":"這個短語幫助人理解大型地方中的距離和方向。"},{"en":"It is useful in site descriptions.","zh":"它適合用於場地描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"next to it","meaning":"在它旁邊","examples":[{"en":"Next to the factory is the warehouse.","zh":"倉庫在工廠旁邊。"},{"en":"Next to it means beside it or immediately near it.","zh":"next to it意思是在它旁邊或緊鄰它。"},{"en":"The office is next to the meeting room.","zh":"辦公室在會議室旁邊。"},{"en":"This phrase gives location by using a nearby reference point.","zh":"這個短語使用附近參照物來提供位置。"},{"en":"It is common in directions and descriptions of layout.","zh":"它常見於指路和佈局描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"warehouse","meaning":"倉庫","examples":[{"en":"The warehouse is next to the factory.","zh":"倉庫在工廠旁邊。"},{"en":"A warehouse is a large building used for storing goods or materials.","zh":"warehouse是用來儲存貨品或材料的大型建築物。"},{"en":"A manufacturing company may keep finished products in a warehouse before delivery.","zh":"製造公司可能在送貨前把完成品存放在倉庫。"},{"en":"Warehouses need space for shelves, vehicles and loading areas.","zh":"倉庫需要貨架、車輛和裝卸區空間。"},{"en":"This word is common in logistics and manufacturing.","zh":"這個詞常見於物流和製造業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be accessed by","meaning":"可由……進入","examples":[{"en":"The warehouse can be accessed by lorries.","zh":"倉庫可由貨車進入。"},{"en":"To be accessed by something means that thing can enter or reach the place.","zh":"be accessed by某物，意思是該物可以進入或到達該地方。"},{"en":"The loading area can be accessed by delivery vans from the back road.","zh":"送貨客貨車可由後方道路進入裝卸區。"},{"en":"Access routes must be wide enough for the vehicles that use them.","zh":"通道必須足夠寬，讓使用它的車輛通過。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a place can be reached.","zh":"這個短語描述如何到達某地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lorries","meaning":"貨車","examples":[{"en":"Lorries can access the warehouse from the turning area.","zh":"貨車可以從迴旋區進入倉庫。"},{"en":"Lorries are large road vehicles used for carrying goods.","zh":"lorries是用來運送貨物的大型道路車輛。"},{"en":"Factories often need lorries to deliver materials and collect finished products.","zh":"工廠通常需要貨車運送材料和收取完成品。"},{"en":"Lorries require more turning space than cars because they are larger.","zh":"貨車比汽車需要更多轉彎空間，因為體積較大。"},{"en":"This word is common in British English for large goods vehicles.","zh":"這個詞在英式英語中常指大型貨運車輛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"turning area","meaning":"迴旋區；轉彎區","examples":[{"en":"Lorries go up the road to the turning area at the end.","zh":"貨車沿路駛到盡頭的迴旋區。"},{"en":"A turning area is a space where vehicles can turn around safely.","zh":"turning area是車輛可以安全掉頭或轉彎的空間。"},{"en":"A factory yard may have a turning area for delivery lorries.","zh":"工廠院子可能有供送貨貨車使用的轉彎區。"},{"en":"Without a turning area, large vehicles may block roads or reverse dangerously.","zh":"沒有迴旋區，大型車輛可能阻塞道路或危險倒車。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical traffic feature on a site.","zh":"這個短語描述場地內的實用交通設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"get to","meaning":"到達","examples":[{"en":"The students can get to the warehouse by crossing the courtyard.","zh":"學生可以橫過庭院到達倉庫。"},{"en":"To get to a place means to reach or arrive there.","zh":"get to某地，意思是到達或抵達那裏。"},{"en":"Visitors can get to the office by following the signs from reception.","zh":"訪客可以從接待處跟着指示牌到達辦公室。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in directions.","zh":"這個短語常見於指路。"},{"en":"It focuses on the route to a destination.","zh":"它著重前往目的地的路線。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cross to the far side of","meaning":"橫過至……另一邊","examples":[{"en":"You can get to the warehouse by crossing to the far side of the courtyard.","zh":"你可以橫過至庭院另一邊到達倉庫。"},{"en":"To cross to the far side of a place means to go across it to the side furthest away.","zh":"cross to the far side of某地，意思是橫過它到最遠的一邊。"},{"en":"Students must cross to the far side of the playground to reach the sports hall.","zh":"學生必須橫過至操場另一邊，才能到達體育館。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear direction across an open space.","zh":"這個短語為穿過開放空間提供清楚方向。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining routes on a site.","zh":"它適合用於解釋場地路線。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"courtyard","meaning":"庭院","examples":[{"en":"The students cross the courtyard to reach the warehouse.","zh":"學生橫過庭院到達倉庫。"},{"en":"A courtyard is an open area surrounded partly or completely by buildings.","zh":"courtyard是部分或完全由建築物圍繞的開放空間。"},{"en":"Workers may cross the courtyard between the factory and offices.","zh":"工人可能在工廠和辦公室之間橫過庭院。"},{"en":"Courtyards can connect different parts of a site.","zh":"庭院可以連接場地的不同部分。"},{"en":"This word describes an outdoor space within or between buildings.","zh":"這個詞描述建築物內部或之間的戶外空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on your right","meaning":"在你的右邊","examples":[{"en":"The warehouse door is on your right.","zh":"倉庫門在你的右邊。"},{"en":"On your right means on the right-hand side from your position or direction of travel.","zh":"on your right意思是從你的位置或行走方向看，在右手邊。"},{"en":"Walk past reception, and the lift will be on your right.","zh":"走過接待處，升降機就在你的右邊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in spoken directions.","zh":"這個短語適合用於口頭指路。"},{"en":"It tells someone which side to look at.","zh":"它告訴某人要看哪一邊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be keen to find","meaning":"很想找到","examples":[{"en":"The students will be keen to find the staff canteen.","zh":"學生會很想找到職員飯堂。"},{"en":"To be keen to find something means to be eager to locate it.","zh":"be keen to find某物，意思是很想找到它的位置。"},{"en":"New employees are often keen to find the coffee machine on their first day.","zh":"新員工第一天通常很想找到咖啡機。"},{"en":"People are keen to find places that they will need frequently.","zh":"人們會很想找到自己經常需要使用的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong interest in locating something.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈想找到某物的興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"staff canteen","meaning":"職員飯堂","examples":[{"en":"The staff canteen is right next to reception.","zh":"職員飯堂就在接待處旁邊。"},{"en":"A staff canteen is a dining area for employees at a workplace.","zh":"staff canteen是工作場所內供員工用餐的地方。"},{"en":"Factory workers may eat lunch in the staff canteen during their break.","zh":"工廠工人可能在休息時到職員飯堂吃午飯。"},{"en":"A canteen helps employees buy or eat meals without leaving the site.","zh":"飯堂幫助員工不用離開場地也能買飯或用餐。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a workplace eating facility.","zh":"這個短語指工作場所用餐設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"right next to","meaning":"就在……旁邊","examples":[{"en":"The staff canteen is right next to reception.","zh":"職員飯堂就在接待處旁邊。"},{"en":"Right next to means immediately beside something.","zh":"right next to意思是緊貼在某物旁邊。"},{"en":"The meeting room is right next to the main office.","zh":"會議室就在主辦公室旁邊。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that two places are very close.","zh":"這個短語強調兩個地方非常接近。"},{"en":"It is common in directions.","zh":"它常見於指路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"confidently say that","meaning":"有信心地說","examples":[{"en":"Julia can confidently say that the food is very good.","zh":"Julia可以有信心地說食物很好。"},{"en":"To confidently say that something is true means to say it with certainty and assurance.","zh":"confidently say that某事屬實，意思是有把握地說出它。"},{"en":"After years of experience, a teacher can confidently say that practice improves writing.","zh":"經過多年經驗，老師可以有信心地說練習能改善寫作。"},{"en":"Confidence in a statement often comes from personal knowledge or evidence.","zh":"對陳述有信心通常來自個人知識或證據。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong belief in what is being said.","zh":"這個短語顯示對所說內容有強烈信心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"look onto","meaning":"望向","examples":[{"en":"The windows look onto a corridor and courtyard.","zh":"窗戶望向走廊和庭院。"},{"en":"To look onto something means to face it and have a view of it.","zh":"look onto某物，意思是面向它並能看見它。"},{"en":"The classroom windows look onto the playground.","zh":"課室窗戶望向操場。"},{"en":"A room’s view can affect whether it feels pleasant or dull.","zh":"房間景觀會影響它感覺舒適還是沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what is visible from a room.","zh":"這個短語描述從房間可看見甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not very attractive at all","meaning":"完全不吸引","examples":[{"en":"The corridor and courtyard are not very attractive at all.","zh":"走廊和庭院完全不吸引。"},{"en":"Not very attractive at all means not pleasant or appealing in appearance.","zh":"not very attractive at all意思是外觀不令人愉快或不吸引。"},{"en":"A room with dark walls and no windows may not be very attractive at all.","zh":"有深色牆壁又沒有窗的房間可能完全不吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a negative opinion about appearance.","zh":"這個短語對外觀作出負面評價。"},{"en":"“At all” makes the criticism stronger.","zh":"at all令批評更強。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"access road","meaning":"通道道路","examples":[{"en":"The other windows look onto the access road.","zh":"另一邊窗戶望向通道道路。"},{"en":"An access road is a road used to enter a site or reach particular buildings.","zh":"access road是用來進入場地或到達特定建築物的道路。"},{"en":"Delivery vehicles use the access road to reach the warehouse.","zh":"送貨車輛使用通道道路到達倉庫。"},{"en":"Access roads are practical but may not provide attractive views.","zh":"通道道路很實用，但未必提供吸引景觀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a functional road within or near a site.","zh":"這個短語描述場地內或附近的功能性道路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not much better","meaning":"也好不了多少","examples":[{"en":"The view of the access road is not much better.","zh":"通道道路的景觀也好不了多少。"},{"en":"Not much better means only slightly better or almost as bad.","zh":"not much better意思是只稍微好一點，或差不多同樣差。"},{"en":"The second classroom has more space, but the lighting is not much better.","zh":"第二間課室空間較多，但燈光也好不了多少。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two unsatisfactory things.","zh":"這個短語比較兩件不太令人滿意的事。"},{"en":"It suggests that the improvement is small.","zh":"它暗示改善很少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"meeting room","meaning":"會議室","examples":[{"en":"The students will use the meeting room quite often.","zh":"學生會頗經常使用會議室。"},{"en":"A meeting room is a room used for discussions, presentations or group work.","zh":"meeting room是用於討論、簡報或小組工作的房間。"},{"en":"Students may gather in a meeting room before visiting different departments.","zh":"學生可能在參觀不同部門前於會議室集合。"},{"en":"Meeting rooms often have tables, chairs and presentation equipment.","zh":"會議室通常有桌椅和簡報設備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal discussion space.","zh":"這個短語描述正式討論空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"quite often","meaning":"頗經常","examples":[{"en":"The students will use the meeting room quite often.","zh":"學生會頗經常使用會議室。"},{"en":"Quite often means fairly frequently.","zh":"quite often意思是相當頻繁。"},{"en":"Work experience students may meet supervisors quite often during their placement.","zh":"工作體驗學生在實習期間可能頗經常與督導見面。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something happens many times but not constantly.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事多次發生，但不是持續不斷。"},{"en":"It is common in everyday descriptions of frequency.","zh":"它常見於日常描述頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"walking along","meaning":"沿着……走","examples":[{"en":"The students can find the room by walking along the corridor.","zh":"學生可以沿着走廊走找到房間。"},{"en":"Walking along something means moving forward following its path.","zh":"walking along某物，意思是沿着其路徑向前走。"},{"en":"You can reach the office by walking along the main corridor.","zh":"你可以沿着主走廊走到達辦公室。"},{"en":"This phrase gives directions by describing movement.","zh":"這個短語透過描述移動來指路。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining how to find a place.","zh":"它適合用於解釋如何找到某地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"to the left of","meaning":"在……左邊","examples":[{"en":"The meeting room is along the corridor to the left of the courtyard.","zh":"會議室在庭院左邊的走廊上。"},{"en":"To the left of something means on its left-hand side.","zh":"to the left of某物，意思是在它左手邊。"},{"en":"The staff office is to the left of the main staircase.","zh":"職員辦公室在主樓梯左邊。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a position by comparing it with another place.","zh":"這個短語透過與另一地方比較來提供位置。"},{"en":"It is common in directions and maps.","zh":"它常見於指路和地圖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"continue along","meaning":"繼續沿着……走","examples":[{"en":"The students should continue along the corridor to the end.","zh":"學生應繼續沿着走廊走到盡頭。"},{"en":"To continue along something means to keep moving forward on the same route.","zh":"continue along某物，意思是沿同一路線繼續向前走。"},{"en":"Continue along the corridor until you reach the red door.","zh":"繼續沿着走廊走，直到你到達紅色門。"},{"en":"This phrase tells someone not to turn yet.","zh":"這個短語告訴某人暫時不要轉彎。"},{"en":"It is useful in step-by-step directions.","zh":"它適合用於逐步指路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the last one on the right","meaning":"右邊最後一間","examples":[{"en":"The meeting room is the last one on the right.","zh":"會議室是右邊最後一間。"},{"en":"The last one on the right means the final room or object on the right-hand side.","zh":"the last one on the right意思是在右手邊最後一間房或最後一個物件。"},{"en":"The office you need is the last one on the right before the exit.","zh":"你需要的辦公室是在出口前右邊最後一間。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a very specific location.","zh":"這個短語給出非常具體的位置。"},{"en":"It is common when directing people along a corridor.","zh":"它常用於指引人沿走廊行走時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"I’m afraid","meaning":"恐怕","examples":[{"en":"I’m afraid there is no natural daylight in the meeting room.","zh":"恐怕會議室沒有自然日光。"},{"en":"I’m afraid is a polite phrase used before giving disappointing or negative information.","zh":"I’m afraid是在提供令人失望或負面資訊前使用的有禮短語。"},{"en":"I’m afraid the lift is not working today.","zh":"恐怕升降機今天不能使用。"},{"en":"This phrase softens bad news.","zh":"這個短語能柔化壞消息。"},{"en":"It is common in polite spoken English.","zh":"它常見於有禮英語口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"natural daylight","meaning":"自然日光","examples":[{"en":"There is no natural daylight in the meeting room.","zh":"會議室沒有自然日光。"},{"en":"Natural daylight is light from the sun, not from lamps or artificial lighting.","zh":"natural daylight是來自太陽的光，而不是燈或人工照明。"},{"en":"Offices with natural daylight often feel brighter and more pleasant.","zh":"有自然日光的辦公室通常感覺更明亮和舒適。"},{"en":"A room without natural daylight may need stronger lighting.","zh":"沒有自然日光的房間可能需要更強照明。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a feature of indoor spaces.","zh":"這個短語描述室內空間的特徵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"need to know where","meaning":"需要知道……在哪裏","examples":[{"en":"The students need to know where some of the offices are.","zh":"學生需要知道一些辦公室在哪裏。"},{"en":"To need to know where something is means to require its location for practical reasons.","zh":"need to know where某物is，意思是因實際原因需要知道其位置。"},{"en":"Visitors need to know where the toilets and exits are.","zh":"訪客需要知道洗手間和出口在哪裏。"},{"en":"Knowing locations helps people move around independently.","zh":"知道位置幫助人獨立四處移動。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces necessary direction information.","zh":"這個短語引入必要的方向資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"human resources department","meaning":"人力資源部","examples":[{"en":"The human resources department is at the front of the building.","zh":"人力資源部位於建築物前方。"},{"en":"The human resources department manages staff matters such as recruitment, training and employee records.","zh":"human resources department負責管理招聘、培訓和員工記錄等人事事務。"},{"en":"New workers may visit the human resources department to complete forms.","zh":"新員工可能到人力資源部填寫表格。"},{"en":"Human resources staff often help with workplace rules and employee support.","zh":"人力資源職員通常協助處理工作規則和員工支援。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a company department focused on people and employment.","zh":"這個短語指公司中負責人員和僱用事務的部門。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at the front of","meaning":"在……前方","examples":[{"en":"The human resources department is at the front of this building.","zh":"人力資源部在這座建築物前方。"},{"en":"At the front of something means near the front part or main entrance side.","zh":"at the front of某物，意思是在前部或靠近正門一邊。"},{"en":"The reception desk is at the front of the school building.","zh":"接待處在學校大樓前方。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people understand position within a building.","zh":"這個短語幫助人理解建築物內的位置。"},{"en":"It often contrasts with “at the back of”.","zh":"它常與at the back of形成對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"head to the left","meaning":"向左走","examples":[{"en":"The students should head to the left along the corridor from reception.","zh":"學生應從接待處沿走廊向左走。"},{"en":"To head to the left means to go towards the left-hand direction.","zh":"head to the left意思是朝左邊方向走。"},{"en":"From the entrance, head to the left and follow the signs to the library.","zh":"從入口向左走，跟着指示牌到圖書館。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in spoken directions.","zh":"這個短語常見於口頭指路。"},{"en":"It tells someone which way to go.","zh":"它告訴某人應往哪個方向走。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the second room you come to","meaning":"你經過的第二間房","examples":[{"en":"The human resources department is the second room you come to.","zh":"人力資源部是你經過的第二間房。"},{"en":"The second room you come to means the second room you reach as you walk along.","zh":"the second room you come to意思是你沿路走時到達的第二間房。"},{"en":"The nurse’s office is the second room you come to after the lift.","zh":"護士室是升降機後你經過的第二間房。"},{"en":"This phrase gives directions by counting rooms in order.","zh":"這個短語透過按次序數房間來指路。"},{"en":"It is useful when room signs may not be obvious.","zh":"當房間標誌未必明顯時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"look out onto the main road","meaning":"望向大路","examples":[{"en":"The human resources department looks out onto the main road.","zh":"人力資源部望向大路。"},{"en":"To look out onto the main road means to have windows facing the main road.","zh":"look out onto the main road意思是窗戶面向大路。"},{"en":"Offices that look out onto the main road may receive more light but also more noise.","zh":"望向大路的辦公室可能有更多光線，但也較嘈。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the view from a room.","zh":"這個短語描述房間景觀。"},{"en":"It helps identify the room’s position in the building.","zh":"它幫助識別房間在建築物中的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"boardroom","meaning":"董事會會議室","examples":[{"en":"The students will sometimes meet in the boardroom.","zh":"學生有時會在董事會會議室開會。"},{"en":"A boardroom is a formal meeting room where senior managers or directors meet.","zh":"boardroom是高級管理人員或董事開會的正式會議室。"},{"en":"Companies may use the boardroom for important presentations and decisions.","zh":"公司可能使用董事會會議室進行重要簡報和決策。"},{"en":"Boardrooms usually look more formal than ordinary meeting rooms.","zh":"董事會會議室通常比普通會議室更正式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a high-level meeting space.","zh":"這個短語指高層會議空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"quite a pleasant view","meaning":"景觀頗怡人","examples":[{"en":"The boardroom has quite a pleasant view.","zh":"董事會會議室景觀頗怡人。"},{"en":"Quite a pleasant view means a fairly nice or enjoyable view.","zh":"quite a pleasant view意思是相當不錯或令人舒服的景觀。"},{"en":"A classroom facing trees has quite a pleasant view compared with one facing a wall.","zh":"與面向牆壁的課室相比，面向樹木的課室景觀頗怡人。"},{"en":"A pleasant view can make a room feel calmer and more comfortable.","zh":"怡人景觀可以令房間感覺更平靜和舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase gives moderate praise for what can be seen.","zh":"這個短語對可見景色作出中度讚賞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"look out onto the trees","meaning":"望向樹木","examples":[{"en":"The boardroom looks out onto the trees.","zh":"董事會會議室望向樹木。"},{"en":"To look out onto the trees means to have windows with a view of trees.","zh":"look out onto the trees意思是窗戶能望見樹木。"},{"en":"A quiet office that looks out onto trees may feel more relaxing.","zh":"望向樹木的安靜辦公室可能感覺更放鬆。"},{"en":"Natural views can improve the atmosphere of a working space.","zh":"自然景觀可以改善工作空間的氣氛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a pleasant view from inside a room.","zh":"這個短語描述從室內看到的怡人景觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"go along the corridor past","meaning":"沿走廊經過……","examples":[{"en":"The students should go along the corridor past the courtyard.","zh":"學生應沿走廊經過庭院。"},{"en":"To go along the corridor past something means to walk down the corridor and continue beyond that place.","zh":"go along the corridor past某物，意思是沿走廊走並繼續經過該地方。"},{"en":"Go along the corridor past the library, and the office will be on your left.","zh":"沿走廊經過圖書館，辦公室就在你左邊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for giving step-by-step directions.","zh":"這個短語適合用於逐步指路。"},{"en":"It tells someone to continue beyond a landmark.","zh":"它告訴某人要繼續走過某個地標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"right to the end","meaning":"一直走到盡頭","examples":[{"en":"The students should go along the corridor right to the end.","zh":"學生應沿走廊一直走到盡頭。"},{"en":"Right to the end means all the way to the final point.","zh":"right to the end意思是一路走到最後位置。"},{"en":"Walk right to the end of the corridor before turning left.","zh":"沿走廊一直走到盡頭，然後左轉。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the person should not stop halfway.","zh":"這個短語強調不要中途停下。"},{"en":"It is common in directions.","zh":"它常見於指路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on the left","meaning":"在左邊","examples":[{"en":"The boardroom is on the left, next to the factory.","zh":"董事會會議室在左邊，工廠旁邊。"},{"en":"On the left means on the left-hand side.","zh":"on the left意思是在左手邊。"},{"en":"The staff room is on the left after the stairs.","zh":"職員室在樓梯後左邊。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people locate a room or object.","zh":"這個短語幫助人找到房間或物件。"},{"en":"It is a simple direction phrase.","zh":"它是簡單的方向短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"next to the factory","meaning":"在工廠旁邊","examples":[{"en":"The boardroom is next to the factory.","zh":"董事會會議室在工廠旁邊。"},{"en":"Next to the factory means immediately beside or very near the factory.","zh":"next to the factory意思是緊鄰或非常接近工廠。"},{"en":"The warehouse is next to the factory so goods can be moved easily.","zh":"倉庫在工廠旁邊，所以貨品可以容易移動。"},{"en":"Being next to the factory may make a room noisier but convenient for visits.","zh":"在工廠旁邊可能令房間較嘈，但方便參觀。"},{"en":"This phrase gives location by reference to the factory.","zh":"這個短語以工廠為參照提供位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"are there any questions before","meaning":"在……之前有沒有問題","examples":[{"en":"Julia asks whether there are any questions before the visit begins.","zh":"Julia問在參觀開始之前有沒有問題。"},{"en":"Are there any questions before...? means does anyone want to ask something before the next activity starts.","zh":"are there any questions before...?意思是在下一項活動開始前，有沒有人想提問。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask, “Are there any questions before we start the test?”","zh":"老師可能問：「在我們開始測驗之前有沒有問題？」"},{"en":"This phrase gives listeners a final chance to clarify information.","zh":"這個短語給聽眾最後機會澄清資訊。"},{"en":"It is common at the end of instructions or introductions.","zh":"它常見於指示或介紹的結尾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 16/task-3":[{"front":"get on with","meaning":"進展如何","examples":[{"en":"Jess asks Tom how he is getting on with his art project.","zh":"Jess 問 Tom 他的藝術專題進展如何。"},{"en":"To get on with something means to make progress with it.","zh":"get on with something 指某事進展如何。"},{"en":"The teacher asked how I was getting on with my essay.","zh":"老師問我文章寫作進展如何。"},{"en":"If you are getting on well with a task, it means the work is moving forward smoothly.","zh":"如果你某項工作進展順利，意思是工作正順暢向前推進。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to ask politely about someone’s progress.","zh":"這個片語常用來有禮貌地詢問某人的進度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"art project","meaning":"藝術專題","examples":[{"en":"Tom is working on an art project about birds.","zh":"Tom 正在做一個關於鳥的藝術專題。"},{"en":"An art project is a piece of creative work, often involving research, planning and final artwork.","zh":"art project 指一項創作作品，通常涉及研究、規劃和最終藝術作品。"},{"en":"Students may create an art project using painting, photography, sculpture or digital media.","zh":"學生可以用繪畫、攝影、雕塑或數碼媒體創作藝術專題。"},{"en":"A good art project usually shows both technical skill and personal ideas.","zh":"好的藝術專題通常同時展示技巧和個人想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in school, college and creative coursework.","zh":"這個片語常見於學校、大專和創意課業中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"give someone the theme of","meaning":"給某人……主題","examples":[{"en":"The teacher gave the students the theme of birds.","zh":"老師給學生「鳥」這個主題。"},{"en":"To give someone the theme of something means to set that topic as the focus of their work.","zh":"give someone the theme of something 指把某主題設定為某人作品的重點。"},{"en":"The teacher gave the class the theme of childhood memories for their writing task.","zh":"老師給全班「童年回憶」這個寫作主題。"},{"en":"A theme helps students narrow their ideas and organise their research.","zh":"主題幫助學生收窄想法並組織研究。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing assignments or creative projects.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論功課或創意專題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"base something on","meaning":"以……作為基礎","examples":[{"en":"The students have to base their project on the theme of birds.","zh":"學生必須以「鳥」這個主題作為專題基礎。"},{"en":"To base something on something else means to use it as the main foundation or starting point.","zh":"base something on something else 指以某事作為主要基礎或起點。"},{"en":"The film was based on a famous novel.","zh":"這部電影以一本著名小說作為基礎。"},{"en":"If a project is based on a theme, every part should connect back to that theme.","zh":"如果專題以某主題為基礎，每個部分都應連繫回該主題。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in art, writing, research and design.","zh":"這個片語常見於藝術、寫作、研究和設計中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"not all that interested in","meaning":"對……不是那麼感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Tom is not really all that interested in wildlife.","zh":"Tom 對野生動物其實不是那麼感興趣。"},{"en":"Not all that interested in something means not very interested in it.","zh":"not all that interested in something 指對某事不是很感興趣。"},{"en":"I am not all that interested in football, but I enjoy watching big matches with friends.","zh":"我對足球不是那麼感興趣，但喜歡和朋友一起看大型比賽。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds softer than saying “I am not interested at all”.","zh":"這個片語比說 “I am not interested at all” 語氣較柔和。"},{"en":"It is useful when expressing mild lack of interest.","zh":"它適合用於表達輕微缺乏興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"wildlife","meaning":"野生動物","examples":[{"en":"Tom is not very interested in wildlife.","zh":"Tom 對野生動物不是很感興趣。"},{"en":"Wildlife means animals, birds, insects and plants that live naturally in the wild.","zh":"wildlife 指自然生活在野外的動物、鳥類、昆蟲和植物。"},{"en":"Wildlife can be affected by pollution, climate change and loss of habitats.","zh":"野生動物可能受到污染、氣候變化和棲地流失影響。"},{"en":"Many artists use wildlife as a subject because it offers colour, movement and symbolism.","zh":"許多藝術家以野生動物為主題，因為它們提供色彩、動感和象徵意義。"},{"en":"This word is often used in nature, conservation and environmental topics.","zh":"這個字常用於自然、保育和環境議題中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"start to get into","meaning":"開始投入","examples":[{"en":"Tom is starting to get into the project.","zh":"Tom 開始投入這個專題。"},{"en":"To start to get into something means to begin to enjoy it or become interested in it.","zh":"start to get into something 指開始享受某事或對某事產生興趣。"},{"en":"At first I disliked the book, but I started to get into it after chapter three.","zh":"起初我不喜歡那本書，但第三章後我開始投入其中。"},{"en":"A student may start to get into a project once they find a personal angle.","zh":"學生一旦找到個人角度，可能會開始投入一個專題。"},{"en":"This phrase is conversational and often describes growing interest.","zh":"這個片語較口語，常描述興趣逐漸增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pretty well finished","meaning":"基本上完成","examples":[{"en":"Tom has pretty well finished the introductory stage.","zh":"Tom 已基本上完成引入階段。"},{"en":"Pretty well finished means almost finished or more or less completed.","zh":"pretty well finished 指幾乎完成或大致完成。"},{"en":"I have pretty well finished my presentation, but I still need to check the images.","zh":"我已基本上完成簡報，但仍需要檢查圖片。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the main work is done, though small changes may remain.","zh":"這個片語暗示主要工作已完成，但可能仍有小修改。"},{"en":"It is informal and common in conversation.","zh":"它較口語，常見於對話中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"introductory stage","meaning":"引入階段","examples":[{"en":"Tom has finished the introductory stage of the project.","zh":"Tom 已完成專題的引入階段。"},{"en":"The introductory stage is the first part of a project, where students explore the topic and gather basic ideas.","zh":"introductory stage 指專題的第一部分，學生會探索主題並收集基本想法。"},{"en":"In the introductory stage, students may read background material and collect examples.","zh":"在引入階段，學生可能閱讀背景資料並收集例子。"},{"en":"A strong introductory stage can make later planning easier.","zh":"扎實的引入階段可以令之後的規劃更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing project structure.","zh":"這個片語適合用於描述專題結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"handouts","meaning":"講義","examples":[{"en":"The students received handouts with details of books and websites.","zh":"學生收到載有書籍和網站詳情的講義。"},{"en":"Handouts are printed or digital materials given to students during a lesson or workshop.","zh":"handouts 指課堂或工作坊中派發給學生的印刷或數碼材料。"},{"en":"The teacher gave us handouts with key vocabulary and reading links.","zh":"老師給我們載有重點詞彙和閱讀連結的講義。"},{"en":"Handouts help students remember instructions and continue studying after class.","zh":"講義幫助學生記住指示，並在課後繼續學習。"},{"en":"This word is common in education and training contexts.","zh":"這個字常見於教育和培訓語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"with details of","meaning":"載有……詳情","examples":[{"en":"The handouts included details of books and websites to look at.","zh":"講義載有需要查看的書籍和網站詳情。"},{"en":"With details of something means containing specific information about it.","zh":"with details of something 指載有關於某事的具體資料。"},{"en":"The email came with details of the meeting time, room and agenda.","zh":"電郵載有會議時間、房間和議程詳情。"},{"en":"Details help students know exactly what resources to use.","zh":"詳情幫助學生準確知道要使用哪些資源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing information included in a document.","zh":"這個片語適合用於描述文件中包含的資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be put off","meaning":"被嚇退；失去興趣","examples":[{"en":"Jess was put off when she saw all the handouts.","zh":"Jess 看到所有講義時被嚇退了。"},{"en":"To be put off means to lose interest or confidence because something seems difficult, unpleasant or too much.","zh":"be put off 指因某事看似困難、不愉快或太多而失去興趣或信心。"},{"en":"Some students are put off by long reading lists.","zh":"有些學生會被長長的閱讀清單嚇退。"},{"en":"A large amount of information can put people off before they begin.","zh":"大量資料可能在人們開始前已令他們卻步。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing discouragement.","zh":"這個片語適合描述受挫或失去興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the more..., the more...","meaning":"越……越……","examples":[{"en":"The more Jess read, the more interested she got.","zh":"Jess 讀得越多，就越感興趣。"},{"en":"The more..., the more... shows that one thing increases as another thing increases.","zh":"the more..., the more... 表示一件事增加時，另一件事也跟着增加。"},{"en":"The more you practise drawing, the more confident you become.","zh":"你越練習繪畫，就越有信心。"},{"en":"This structure is useful for showing a clear relationship between two changes.","zh":"這個結構適合顯示兩種變化之間的清楚關係。"},{"en":"It is common in both speaking and writing.","zh":"它在口語和寫作中都很常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"research different aspects of","meaning":"研究……的不同面向","examples":[{"en":"Tom could research many different aspects of birds in art.","zh":"Tom 可以研究藝術中鳥的許多不同面向。"},{"en":"To research different aspects of something means to study several parts or angles of a topic.","zh":"research different aspects of something 指研究一個主題的不同部分或角度。"},{"en":"Students can research different aspects of climate change, such as causes, effects and solutions.","zh":"學生可以研究氣候變化的不同面向，例如成因、影響和解決方法。"},{"en":"Looking at different aspects makes a project richer and less one-sided.","zh":"從不同面向研究會令專題更豐富，而且不會太單一。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in academic and creative research.","zh":"這個片語適合用於學術和創意研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"birds in art","meaning":"藝術中的鳥","examples":[{"en":"The project explores birds in art.","zh":"這個專題探討藝術中的鳥。"},{"en":"Birds in art means the way birds are shown, used or symbolised in artworks.","zh":"birds in art 指鳥在藝術作品中如何被呈現、使用或象徵化。"},{"en":"Birds in art can represent freedom, danger, beauty or spiritual meaning.","zh":"藝術中的鳥可以代表自由、危險、美麗或精神意義。"},{"en":"Artists may paint birds realistically or use them as symbols.","zh":"藝術家可以寫實地畫鳥，也可以把鳥用作象徵。"},{"en":"This phrase links natural subjects with artistic interpretation.","zh":"這個片語把自然題材與藝術詮釋連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"movement","meaning":"動作；動感","examples":[{"en":"Movement is one aspect of birds in art that Tom could research.","zh":"動感是 Tom 可以研究的藝術中鳥的一個面向。"},{"en":"Movement means the sense of action or motion shown in an artwork.","zh":"movement 指藝術作品中呈現的動作或動態感。"},{"en":"An artist can show movement by painting wings, flowing lines or repeated shapes.","zh":"藝術家可以透過翅膀、流動線條或重複形狀來表現動感。"},{"en":"In bird paintings, movement may suggest flight, hunting or escape.","zh":"在鳥類畫作中，動感可能暗示飛行、獵食或逃脫。"},{"en":"This word is important when analysing visual energy in art.","zh":"分析藝術中的視覺能量時，這個字很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"texture","meaning":"質感","examples":[{"en":"Texture is one aspect of birds in art that Tom could research.","zh":"質感是 Tom 可以研究的藝術中鳥的一個面向。"},{"en":"Texture means the visual or physical quality of a surface.","zh":"texture 指表面的視覺或實體質素。"},{"en":"Artists can use brushstrokes to suggest the texture of feathers.","zh":"藝術家可以用筆觸表現羽毛的質感。"},{"en":"Texture can make a painting feel soft, rough, smooth or detailed.","zh":"質感可以令畫作感覺柔軟、粗糙、平滑或細緻。"},{"en":"This word is common in art analysis.","zh":"這個字常見於藝術分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"look forward to","meaning":"期待","examples":[{"en":"Tom was looking forward to the Bird Park visit.","zh":"Tom 很期待參觀 Bird Park。"},{"en":"To look forward to something means to feel excited about it before it happens.","zh":"look forward to something 指在某事發生前對它感到期待和興奮。"},{"en":"Jess was looking forward to seeing the paintings in the gallery.","zh":"Jess 很期待在畫廊看那些畫作。"},{"en":"People often look forward to trips that may give them new ideas.","zh":"人們常期待可能帶來新想法的參觀活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is followed by a noun or an -ing form.","zh":"這個片語後接名詞或 -ing 形式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Bird Park visit","meaning":"參觀 Bird Park","examples":[{"en":"Tom was looking forward to the Bird Park visit.","zh":"Tom 很期待參觀 Bird Park。"},{"en":"A Bird Park visit is a trip to a place where different birds are kept or observed.","zh":"Bird Park visit 指到一個飼養或觀察不同鳥類的地方參觀。"},{"en":"Students may use a Bird Park visit to sketch birds and study their movement.","zh":"學生可以透過參觀 Bird Park 素描鳥類並研究牠們的動作。"},{"en":"Such visits can be useful for art projects if students can observe birds closely.","zh":"如果學生能近距離觀察鳥類，這類參觀對藝術專題很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a learning visit connected with birds.","zh":"這個片語描述與鳥類相關的學習參觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what a letdown","meaning":"真令人失望","examples":[{"en":"The Bird Park visit was a letdown.","zh":"參觀 Bird Park 真令人失望。"},{"en":"What a letdown means something was disappointing after people expected more.","zh":"what a letdown 指某事在令人期待後卻令人失望。"},{"en":"The exhibition looked exciting online, but in real life it was a letdown.","zh":"那個展覽在網上看起來很精彩，但現場真令人失望。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses disappointment in a natural and conversational way.","zh":"這個片語以自然口語方式表達失望。"},{"en":"It is stronger than simply saying “not very good”.","zh":"它比單純說 “not very good” 更強烈。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pour with rain","meaning":"大雨傾盆","examples":[{"en":"It poured with rain during the Bird Park visit.","zh":"參觀 Bird Park 期間大雨傾盆。"},{"en":"To pour with rain means to rain very heavily.","zh":"pour with rain 指下很大的雨。"},{"en":"It poured with rain during the school trip, so everyone stayed indoors.","zh":"學校旅行期間大雨傾盆，所以大家都留在室內。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can ruin outdoor visits because it affects visibility and comfort.","zh":"大雨會破壞戶外參觀，因為它影響視野和舒適度。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English.","zh":"這個片語常見於英式英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hardly see a single","meaning":"幾乎連一個也看不到","examples":[{"en":"The students hardly saw a single bird at the Bird Park.","zh":"學生在 Bird Park 幾乎連一隻鳥也看不到。"},{"en":"To hardly see a single thing means to see almost none of it.","zh":"hardly see a single thing 指幾乎一個也看不到。"},{"en":"Because of the fog, we hardly saw a single building from the hill.","zh":"因為大霧，我們從山上幾乎連一棟建築物也看不到。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises how little someone saw.","zh":"這個片語強調某人看到的東西非常少。"},{"en":"It is often used when an experience was disappointing.","zh":"它常用於令人失望的經歷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"much less use than","meaning":"遠不如……有用","examples":[{"en":"The Bird Park visit was much less use than the trip to the Natural History Museum.","zh":"參觀 Bird Park 遠不如到自然歷史博物館參觀有用。"},{"en":"Much less use than means far less helpful or useful than something else.","zh":"much less use than 指遠不如另一件事有幫助或有用。"},{"en":"The short video was much less use than the detailed workshop.","zh":"那段短片遠不如詳細工作坊有用。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the practical value of two experiences.","zh":"這個片語比較兩種經歷的實際價值。"},{"en":"It is useful when evaluating study resources or visits.","zh":"它適合用於評估學習資源或參觀活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"trip to","meaning":"到……的參觀","examples":[{"en":"The trip to the Natural History Museum was useful.","zh":"到自然歷史博物館的參觀很有用。"},{"en":"A trip to a place is a visit made for learning, leisure or another purpose.","zh":"trip to a place 指為學習、休閒或其他目的到某地參觀。"},{"en":"The class went on a trip to the art gallery.","zh":"全班到美術館參觀。"},{"en":"A trip to a museum can give students direct experience of objects and displays.","zh":"到博物館參觀可以讓學生直接接觸展品和展示。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing school visits.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論學校參觀活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Natural History Museum","meaning":"自然歷史博物館","examples":[{"en":"The students visited the Natural History Museum.","zh":"學生參觀了自然歷史博物館。"},{"en":"A Natural History Museum displays objects connected with animals, plants, fossils, rocks and the natural world.","zh":"Natural History Museum 展示與動物、植物、化石、岩石和自然世界有關的物件。"},{"en":"Students can learn about evolution and habitats at a Natural History Museum.","zh":"學生可以在自然歷史博物館學習演化和棲地。"},{"en":"Such museums are useful for art students because they show real forms and structures.","zh":"這類博物館對藝術學生很有用，因為它展示真實形態和結構。"},{"en":"This phrase names a type of museum focused on nature and science.","zh":"這個片語命名一種以自然和科學為重點的博物館。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stuff about","meaning":"關於……的內容","examples":[{"en":"Tom liked all the stuff about evolution at the museum.","zh":"Tom 喜歡博物館裏所有關於演化的內容。"},{"en":"Stuff about something means information, material or displays connected with that topic.","zh":"stuff about something 指與某主題有關的資料、材料或展品。"},{"en":"I enjoyed the stuff about ancient birds in the exhibition.","zh":"我喜歡展覽中關於古代鳥類的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often used in conversation.","zh":"這個片語較口語，常用於對話。"},{"en":"In formal writing, “material about” or “information about” would be better.","zh":"在正式寫作中，用 “material about” 或 “information about” 較好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"evolution","meaning":"演化","examples":[{"en":"Tom liked learning about evolution at the museum.","zh":"Tom 喜歡在博物館學習演化。"},{"en":"Evolution is the process by which living things change over many generations.","zh":"evolution 指生物經過許多世代逐漸改變的過程。"},{"en":"The evolution of birds can be studied through fossils and modern species.","zh":"鳥類演化可以透過化石和現代物種研究。"},{"en":"Understanding evolution can help artists think about form, function and adaptation.","zh":"理解演化可以幫助藝術家思考形態、功能和適應。"},{"en":"This word is common in biology and natural history.","zh":"這個字常見於生物學和自然歷史。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"workshop sessions","meaning":"工作坊環節","examples":[{"en":"The workshop sessions with Dr Fletcher were good.","zh":"Dr Fletcher 帶領的工作坊環節很好。"},{"en":"Workshop sessions are practical learning sessions where people discuss, practise or develop ideas.","zh":"workshop sessions 指實用學習環節，人們會討論、練習或發展想法。"},{"en":"Art students often use workshop sessions to test materials and receive feedback.","zh":"藝術學生常利用工作坊環節測試材料並獲得回饋。"},{"en":"Workshops can be more active than lectures because students take part directly.","zh":"工作坊可以比講座更互動，因為學生直接參與。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in creative and educational contexts.","zh":"這個片語常見於創意和教育語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"brainstorming sessions","meaning":"腦力激盪環節","examples":[{"en":"Tom especially liked the brainstorming sessions.","zh":"Tom 特別喜歡腦力激盪環節。"},{"en":"Brainstorming sessions are meetings or activities where people generate many ideas freely.","zh":"brainstorming sessions 指人們自由產生大量想法的會議或活動。"},{"en":"In brainstorming sessions, students should not reject ideas too quickly.","zh":"在腦力激盪環節中，學生不應太快否定想法。"},{"en":"Brainstorming can help artists move beyond obvious ideas.","zh":"腦力激盪可以幫助藝術家超越明顯想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing creative planning.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論創意規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"miss something because","meaning":"因……而錯過某事","examples":[{"en":"Jess missed the workshop sessions because she was ill.","zh":"Jess 因為生病而錯過工作坊環節。"},{"en":"To miss something because of a reason means not to attend or experience it due to that reason.","zh":"miss something because of a reason 指因某原因而沒有出席或經歷某事。"},{"en":"He missed the school trip because he had a fever.","zh":"他因發燒而錯過學校旅行。"},{"en":"Missing a workshop can make it harder to understand later project requirements.","zh":"錯過工作坊可能令之後較難理解專題要求。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links absence with its cause.","zh":"這個片語清楚把缺席與原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"I wish we could have","meaning":"我真希望我們可以……","examples":[{"en":"Jess wishes they could have seen last year’s projects.","zh":"Jess 真希望他們可以看去年的專題作品。"},{"en":"I wish we could have means I regret that we were not able to do something.","zh":"I wish we could have 指我遺憾我們當時不能做某事。"},{"en":"I wish we could have visited the gallery before starting our own work.","zh":"我真希望我們開始自己作品前可以參觀畫廊。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses regret about a missed opportunity.","zh":"這個片語表達對錯過機會的遺憾。"},{"en":"It is often used when someone thinks something would have been helpful.","zh":"當某人覺得某事本來會有幫助時，常會使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"do one’s own thing","meaning":"做自己的東西","examples":[{"en":"Tom supposes the teachers want the students to do their own thing.","zh":"Tom 猜老師希望學生做自己的東西。"},{"en":"To do one’s own thing means to work in one’s own way or follow one’s own ideas.","zh":"do one’s own thing 指以自己的方式工作或跟從自己的想法。"},{"en":"The teacher gave us a theme but let us do our own thing.","zh":"老師給我們一個主題，但讓我們做自己的東西。"},{"en":"In art, doing your own thing can help your work feel personal and original.","zh":"在藝術中，做自己的東西可以令作品更個人化和原創。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often positive.","zh":"這個片語較口語，通常帶正面意思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"draft a proposal","meaning":"草擬提案","examples":[{"en":"Jess asks whether Tom has drafted his proposal yet.","zh":"Jess 問 Tom 是否已草擬提案。"},{"en":"To draft a proposal means to write a first version of a plan or idea.","zh":"draft a proposal 指寫出計劃或想法的初稿。"},{"en":"Students should draft a proposal before beginning the final artwork.","zh":"學生應在開始最終作品前草擬提案。"},{"en":"A draft proposal can be changed after feedback.","zh":"提案草稿可以在收到回饋後修改。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in coursework, projects and formal planning.","zh":"這個片語常見於課業、專題和正式規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hand it in","meaning":"交上去","examples":[{"en":"Tom has not handed in his proposal yet.","zh":"Tom 還未交上他的提案。"},{"en":"To hand something in means to submit it to a teacher, office or authority.","zh":"hand something in 指把某物提交給老師、辦公室或機構。"},{"en":"Students must hand in their art proposals by Friday.","zh":"學生必須在星期五前交上藝術提案。"},{"en":"If you hand work in late, you may lose marks.","zh":"如果你遲交作品，可能會被扣分。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in school and work contexts.","zh":"這個片語常見於學校和工作語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"amend some parts","meaning":"修改某些部分","examples":[{"en":"Tom needs to amend some parts of his proposal.","zh":"Tom 需要修改提案的某些部分。"},{"en":"To amend some parts means to change or improve certain sections.","zh":"amend some parts 指更改或改善某些部分。"},{"en":"The student amended some parts of the essay after reading the teacher’s comments.","zh":"學生閱讀老師評語後，修改了文章的某些部分。"},{"en":"Amending work is normal because first drafts are rarely perfect.","zh":"修改作品很正常，因為初稿很少完美。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than “change some bits”.","zh":"這個片語比 “change some bits” 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"notes from my research","meaning":"我的研究筆記","examples":[{"en":"Tom’s notes from his research are mostly descriptions.","zh":"Tom 的研究筆記大多是描述。"},{"en":"Notes from my research are written records of information found during research.","zh":"notes from my research 指研究期間找到資料後寫下的紀錄。"},{"en":"My notes from my research include dates, artist names and useful quotations.","zh":"我的研究筆記包括日期、藝術家姓名和有用引文。"},{"en":"Research notes should include both facts and personal analysis.","zh":"研究筆記應同時包括事實和個人分析。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing preparation for a project.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論專題準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"almost all just descriptions","meaning":"幾乎全都是描述","examples":[{"en":"Tom realised that his notes are almost all just descriptions.","zh":"Tom 意識到他的筆記幾乎全都是描述。"},{"en":"Almost all just descriptions means nearly everything is descriptive rather than analytical.","zh":"almost all just descriptions 指幾乎所有內容都是描述，而不是分析。"},{"en":"My first draft was almost all just descriptions, with very little evaluation.","zh":"我的初稿幾乎全都是描述，幾乎沒有評估。"},{"en":"Art projects need more than description; they also need interpretation and judgement.","zh":"藝術專題需要的不只是描述，還需要詮釋和判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase points out a weakness in academic work.","zh":"這個片語指出學術作品中的弱點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"evaluate anything","meaning":"評估任何內容","examples":[{"en":"Tom has not actually evaluated anything in his research notes.","zh":"Tom 其實沒有在研究筆記中評估任何內容。"},{"en":"To evaluate anything means to judge its value, quality, meaning or importance.","zh":"evaluate anything 指判斷某事的價值、質素、意義或重要性。"},{"en":"Students should evaluate paintings instead of only describing what they see.","zh":"學生應評估畫作，而不只是描述自己看到的東西。"},{"en":"Evaluation shows independent thinking and deeper understanding.","zh":"評估能顯示獨立思考和更深入理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in art, research and essay marking.","zh":"這個片語常見於藝術、研究和文章評分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fix that","meaning":"修正那一點","examples":[{"en":"Tom needs to fix the lack of evaluation in his proposal.","zh":"Tom 需要修正提案中缺乏評估那一點。"},{"en":"To fix that means to correct or improve that problem.","zh":"fix that 指更正或改善那個問題。"},{"en":"My conclusion is too weak, so I need to fix that before handing in the essay.","zh":"我的結論太弱，所以交文章前需要修正那一點。"},{"en":"Fixing a problem in a proposal can make the final project stronger.","zh":"修正提案中的問題可以令最終專題更強。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and practical.","zh":"這個片語較口語而實用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"look at that","meaning":"檢查那一點","examples":[{"en":"Jess will have to look at the evaluation part too.","zh":"Jess 也需要檢查評估部分。"},{"en":"To look at that means to check, examine or consider that point.","zh":"look at that 指檢查、審視或考慮那一點。"},{"en":"I need to look at that section again before submitting my proposal.","zh":"我提交提案前需要再檢查那一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone realises a part needs attention.","zh":"當某人意識到某部分需要注意時，這個片語很有用。"},{"en":"It is conversational and flexible.","zh":"它較口語，而且用法靈活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"timeline for","meaning":"……的時間表","examples":[{"en":"Tom has done a timeline for the project.","zh":"Tom 已為專題做了時間表。"},{"en":"A timeline for something is a plan showing when different tasks will happen.","zh":"timeline for something 指顯示不同任務何時進行的計劃。"},{"en":"Students should prepare a timeline for research, drafting and final artwork.","zh":"學生應為研究、草擬和最終作品準備時間表。"},{"en":"A timeline helps people manage deadlines and avoid last-minute work.","zh":"時間表幫助人們管理截止日期，避免最後一刻才工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in project planning.","zh":"這個片語適合用於專題規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mind map","meaning":"心智圖","examples":[{"en":"Tom has made a mind map for the project.","zh":"Tom 已為專題製作了一張心智圖。"},{"en":"A mind map is a visual plan that connects ideas around a central topic.","zh":"mind map 指圍繞中心主題連接不同想法的視覺計劃。"},{"en":"Students can use a mind map to organise research on birds, artists and techniques.","zh":"學生可以用心智圖整理關於鳥、藝術家和技巧的研究。"},{"en":"Mind maps help people see relationships between ideas.","zh":"心智圖幫助人們看見想法之間的關係。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in planning and brainstorming.","zh":"這個片語常見於規劃和腦力激盪中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"quite enjoy","meaning":"頗享受","examples":[{"en":"Jess quite enjoyed making the mind map.","zh":"Jess 頗享受製作心智圖。"},{"en":"To quite enjoy something means to enjoy it fairly much, though not necessarily extremely.","zh":"quite enjoy something 指頗享受某事，但不一定是極度喜歡。"},{"en":"I quite enjoyed researching the artists once I found good images.","zh":"一找到好圖片後，我頗享受研究那些藝術家。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses moderate pleasure.","zh":"這個片語表達中等程度的愉快。"},{"en":"In British English, “quite” can make the statement sound measured and natural.","zh":"在英式英語中，“quite” 會令說法聽起來有分寸而自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"explain the basis for","meaning":"解釋……的依據","examples":[{"en":"Jess found it hard to explain the basis for her decisions.","zh":"Jess 覺得很難解釋她決定的依據。"},{"en":"To explain the basis for something means to explain the reasons or evidence behind it.","zh":"explain the basis for something 指解釋某事背後的理由或證據。"},{"en":"Students must explain the basis for choosing a particular artist.","zh":"學生必須解釋選擇某位藝術家的依據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when teachers want students to justify creative decisions.","zh":"當老師希望學生為創作決定提出理據時，這個片語很有用。"},{"en":"It encourages thinking beyond personal preference.","zh":"它鼓勵學生超越個人喜好去思考。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"one’s decisions","meaning":"某人的決定","examples":[{"en":"Jess had to explain the basis for her decisions in the action plan.","zh":"Jess 必須在行動計劃中解釋她決定的依據。"},{"en":"One’s decisions are the choices a person has made.","zh":"one’s decisions 指某人作出的選擇。"},{"en":"An artist should understand the reasons behind their decisions about colour and composition.","zh":"藝術家應理解自己關於顏色和構圖的決定背後的原因。"},{"en":"Explaining decisions helps others see that the work is thoughtful.","zh":"解釋決定有助別人看見作品是經過思考的。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reflective writing.","zh":"這個片語常見於反思寫作中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"action plan","meaning":"行動計劃","examples":[{"en":"Jess had to give a rationale in her action plan.","zh":"Jess 必須在行動計劃中給出理據。"},{"en":"An action plan is a written plan showing what someone will do and why.","zh":"action plan 指顯示某人會做甚麼以及原因的書面計劃。"},{"en":"A project action plan may include research tasks, deadlines and materials.","zh":"專題行動計劃可能包括研究任務、截止日期和材料。"},{"en":"A clear action plan helps students work step by step.","zh":"清晰行動計劃幫助學生一步一步工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in coursework and project management.","zh":"這個片語常見於課業和項目管理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"give a rationale","meaning":"給出理據","examples":[{"en":"Jess explains that they need to give a rationale.","zh":"Jess 解釋他們需要給出理據。"},{"en":"To give a rationale means to explain the reasons behind a choice or plan.","zh":"give a rationale 指解釋某選擇或計劃背後的理由。"},{"en":"Students should give a rationale for choosing their final image.","zh":"學生應為選擇最終圖像給出理據。"},{"en":"A rationale shows that decisions are thoughtful, not random.","zh":"理據顯示決定經過思考，而不是隨意作出。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic and creative coursework.","zh":"這個片語常見於學術和創意課業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"I didn’t realise","meaning":"我沒有意識到","examples":[{"en":"Tom did not realise they had to give a rationale.","zh":"Tom 沒有意識到他們必須給出理據。"},{"en":"I didn’t realise means I did not know or understand something before.","zh":"I didn’t realise 指我之前不知道或沒有明白某事。"},{"en":"I didn’t realise the proposal had to include a timeline.","zh":"我沒有意識到提案必須包括時間表。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they discover new information.","zh":"人們發現新資訊時會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It often explains why someone has not done something yet.","zh":"它常解釋為何某人尚未做某事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"add it now","meaning":"現在補上","examples":[{"en":"Tom can add the rationale to his proposal now.","zh":"Tom 現在可以把理據補到提案中。"},{"en":"To add it now means to include the missing part at this point.","zh":"add it now 指在這個時候加入缺少的部分。"},{"en":"If your draft lacks examples, you can add them now before submission.","zh":"如果你的草稿缺少例子，你可以在提交前現在補上。"},{"en":"Adding a missing section early can prevent bigger problems later.","zh":"及早補上缺少部分可以防止之後出現更大問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is practical and action-focused.","zh":"這個片語實用，並以行動為重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"video diary presentation","meaning":"影片日誌匯報","examples":[{"en":"Tom has done the video diary presentation.","zh":"Tom 已完成影片日誌匯報。"},{"en":"A video diary presentation is a presentation using recorded reflections or progress updates in video form.","zh":"video diary presentation 指使用影片形式記錄反思或進度更新的匯報。"},{"en":"Students may use a video diary presentation to explain how their ideas changed over time.","zh":"學生可以用影片日誌匯報解釋自己的想法如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"Video diaries can show process as well as final results.","zh":"影片日誌可以展示過程以及最終結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in creative coursework.","zh":"這個片語常見於創意課業中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"work out","meaning":"想清楚；計算出","examples":[{"en":"Tom has worked out what he wants his outcome to be.","zh":"Tom 已想清楚他希望專題成果是甚麼。"},{"en":"To work out something means to figure it out after thinking carefully.","zh":"work out something 指經過仔細思考後弄清楚某事。"},{"en":"Jess worked out how to connect her paintings to the theme.","zh":"Jess 想清楚如何把她的畫作與主題連繫起來。"},{"en":"Working something out often takes time, research and reflection.","zh":"想清楚某事通常需要時間、研究和反思。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when solving problems or making decisions.","zh":"這個片語常用於解決問題或作決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"outcome","meaning":"成果","examples":[{"en":"Tom has worked out the outcome he wants for the project.","zh":"Tom 已想清楚他想要的專題成果。"},{"en":"An outcome is the final result or product of a process.","zh":"outcome 指一個過程的最終結果或作品。"},{"en":"The outcome of an art project might be a painting, sculpture, film or installation.","zh":"藝術專題的成果可以是一幅畫、雕塑、影片或裝置藝術。"},{"en":"A clear outcome helps students plan materials and time.","zh":"清晰成果有助學生規劃材料和時間。"},{"en":"This word is common in education and project planning.","zh":"這個字常見於教育和專題規劃中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"it’s best not to","meaning":"最好不要……","examples":[{"en":"Someone told Jess that it is best not to be too precise.","zh":"有人告訴 Jess 最好不要太精確。"},{"en":"It’s best not to means it is wiser or more suitable to avoid doing something.","zh":"it’s best not to 指最好或較明智的是避免做某事。"},{"en":"It is best not to decide the final design too early.","zh":"最好不要太早決定最終設計。"},{"en":"This phrase gives advice in a gentle way.","zh":"這個片語以柔和方式給出建議。"},{"en":"It often suggests caution.","zh":"它常暗示要謹慎。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"too precise about","meaning":"對……太精確","examples":[{"en":"Jess thinks students should not be too precise about their actual outcome.","zh":"Jess 認為學生不應對實際成果太精確。"},{"en":"Too precise about something means giving details that are too exact too early.","zh":"too precise about something 指太早給出過於準確的細節。"},{"en":"At the proposal stage, students should not be too precise about every colour and material.","zh":"在提案階段，學生不應對每種顏色和材料太精確。"},{"en":"Being too precise can limit creative development later.","zh":"太精確可能會限制之後的創意發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing flexible planning.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論彈性規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"actual outcome","meaning":"實際成果","examples":[{"en":"The actual outcome should not be too precise at this stage.","zh":"在這個階段，實際成果不應太精確。"},{"en":"The actual outcome means the real final result that will be produced.","zh":"actual outcome 指真正會製作出來的最終結果。"},{"en":"The actual outcome may change after more research and experimentation.","zh":"實際成果可能在更多研究和實驗後改變。"},{"en":"In creative work, the final outcome often develops gradually.","zh":"在創意作品中，最終成果常會逐漸發展。"},{"en":"This phrase distinguishes the final result from early ideas.","zh":"這個片語把最終結果與早期想法區分開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at this stage","meaning":"在這個階段","examples":[{"en":"Students should not be too precise at this stage.","zh":"學生在這個階段不應太精確。"},{"en":"At this stage means at this point in the process.","zh":"at this stage 指在過程中的這一刻或這一步。"},{"en":"At this stage, the proposal only needs to show the main direction.","zh":"在這個階段，提案只需要顯示主要方向。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain what is appropriate now, not later.","zh":"這個片語有助解釋現在合適的是甚麼，而不是之後的要求。"},{"en":"It is useful in project planning and feedback.","zh":"它適合用於專題規劃和回饋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have more scope to","meaning":"有更多空間去……","examples":[{"en":"A vague outcome gives students more scope to explore ideas later.","zh":"較模糊的成果讓學生之後有更多空間探索想法。"},{"en":"To have more scope to do something means to have more freedom or room to do it.","zh":"have more scope to do something 指有更多自由或空間去做某事。"},{"en":"A broad theme gives artists more scope to experiment.","zh":"寬泛主題給藝術家更多空間去實驗。"},{"en":"More scope can encourage creative risk-taking and discovery.","zh":"更多空間可以鼓勵創意冒險和發現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing flexibility.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論彈性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"explore one’s ideas","meaning":"探索自己的想法","examples":[{"en":"Jess wants more scope to explore her ideas later.","zh":"Jess 想之後有更多空間探索自己的想法。"},{"en":"To explore one’s ideas means to develop, test and examine them further.","zh":"explore one’s ideas 指進一步發展、測試和審視自己的想法。"},{"en":"Artists explore their ideas through sketches, experiments and research.","zh":"藝術家透過草圖、實驗和研究探索自己的想法。"},{"en":"Exploring ideas can lead to unexpected and stronger outcomes.","zh":"探索想法可以帶來意想不到而更有力的成果。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to creative work.","zh":"這個片語是創意工作的核心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"later on","meaning":"之後","examples":[{"en":"Students can explore their ideas later on.","zh":"學生可以之後探索自己的想法。"},{"en":"Later on means at a later time.","zh":"later on 指在較後的時間。"},{"en":"You can add more detail later on after the teacher gives feedback.","zh":"老師給回饋後，你可以之後加入更多細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something does not need to be decided immediately.","zh":"當某事不需要立即決定時，這個片語很有用。"},{"en":"It sounds natural in spoken English.","zh":"它在英語口語中聽起來自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"go back to","meaning":"回到……","examples":[{"en":"Jess is going to go back to her proposal.","zh":"Jess 打算回到她的提案。"},{"en":"To go back to something means to return to it and continue working on it.","zh":"go back to something 指回到某事並繼續處理。"},{"en":"After the discussion, Tom went back to his mind map.","zh":"討論後，Tom 回到他的心智圖。"},{"en":"Students often go back to earlier work after receiving new advice.","zh":"學生收到新建議後，常會回到早前作品修改。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for revision and improvement.","zh":"這個片語適合用於修訂和改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make it a bit more vague","meaning":"把它寫得稍微模糊一點","examples":[{"en":"Jess will make her proposal a bit more vague.","zh":"Jess 會把她的提案寫得稍微模糊一點。"},{"en":"To make it a bit more vague means to reduce exact detail so there is more flexibility.","zh":"make it a bit more vague 指減少精確細節，以便有更多彈性。"},{"en":"The teacher told me to make my outcome a bit more vague at the proposal stage.","zh":"老師叫我在提案階段把成果寫得稍微模糊一點。"},{"en":"A slightly vague plan can leave room for research to shape the final work.","zh":"稍微模糊的計劃可以留空間讓研究塑造最終作品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in creative planning.","zh":"這個片語適合用於創意規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be unsure about","meaning":"對……不確定","examples":[{"en":"Tom is unsure about one part of the project.","zh":"Tom 對專題其中一部分不確定。"},{"en":"To be unsure about something means to feel uncertain or not fully confident about it.","zh":"be unsure about something 指對某事感到不肯定或沒有十足信心。"},{"en":"Jess was unsure about how much detail to include in her proposal.","zh":"Jess 不確定提案應包括多少細節。"},{"en":"Students should ask for advice when they are unsure about requirements.","zh":"學生對要求不確定時，應尋求建議。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when expressing doubt.","zh":"這個片語適合用於表達疑惑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"choose paintings of","meaning":"選擇……的畫作","examples":[{"en":"The students have to choose paintings of birds.","zh":"學生必須選擇鳥的畫作。"},{"en":"To choose paintings of something means to select artworks that show that subject.","zh":"choose paintings of something 指選擇呈現某主題的藝術作品。"},{"en":"Students may choose paintings of animals, landscapes or people for analysis.","zh":"學生可以選擇動物、風景或人物畫作作分析。"},{"en":"Choosing suitable paintings is important because they shape the direction of the project.","zh":"選擇合適畫作很重要，因為它們會塑造專題方向。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in art study.","zh":"這個片語常見於藝術學習中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"what they mean to us","meaning":"它們對我們的意義","examples":[{"en":"The students have to say what the paintings mean to them.","zh":"學生必須說出那些畫作對他們的意義。"},{"en":"What they mean to us refers to the personal meaning or emotional effect something has for us.","zh":"what they mean to us 指某事對我們的個人意義或情感影響。"},{"en":"Students should explain what the image means to them, not only what it shows.","zh":"學生應解釋圖像對自己的意義，而不只是說它呈現甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages personal response and interpretation.","zh":"這個片語鼓勵個人回應和詮釋。"},{"en":"It is useful in reflective art writing.","zh":"它適合用於反思性藝術寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a painting of","meaning":"一幅……的畫","examples":[{"en":"Tom chose a painting of a falcon by Landseer.","zh":"Tom 選擇了 Landseer 一幅獵鷹的畫。"},{"en":"A painting of something is an artwork that shows that subject.","zh":"a painting of something 指呈現某主題的一幅畫。"},{"en":"The gallery displayed a painting of a bird beside a river.","zh":"畫廊展示了一幅河邊鳥類的畫。"},{"en":"A painting of an animal can show more than appearance; it can suggest mood and meaning.","zh":"一幅動物畫可以呈現的不只是外觀，也可以暗示情緒和意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying artworks.","zh":"這個片語適合用於識別藝術作品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"falcon","meaning":"獵鷹","examples":[{"en":"Tom chose a painting of a falcon.","zh":"Tom 選擇了一幅獵鷹的畫。"},{"en":"A falcon is a bird of prey known for sharp eyesight and fast flight.","zh":"falcon 指一種猛禽，以銳利視力和高速飛行聞名。"},{"en":"Falcons are often associated with power, hunting and control.","zh":"獵鷹常與力量、狩獵和控制聯繫起來。"},{"en":"In art, a falcon may suggest danger, nobility or wildness.","zh":"在藝術中，獵鷹可能暗示危險、高貴或野性。"},{"en":"This word names a specific type of bird.","zh":"這個字命名一種特定鳥類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"stand there with","meaning":"站在那裏，並……","examples":[{"en":"The bird is standing there with its head turned to one side.","zh":"那隻鳥站在那裏，頭轉向一邊。"},{"en":"To stand there with something in a certain position means to be standing while that detail is visible.","zh":"stand there with something in a certain position 指站在那裏，同時某個細節清楚可見。"},{"en":"The child stood there with a sketchbook under his arm.","zh":"那孩子站在那裏，腋下夾着一本素描簿。"},{"en":"This structure helps describe posture and appearance together.","zh":"這個結構有助同時描述姿勢和外觀。"},{"en":"It is useful when analysing figures in a painting.","zh":"它適合用於分析畫中人物或動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"head turned to one side","meaning":"頭轉向一邊","examples":[{"en":"The falcon has its head turned to one side.","zh":"那隻獵鷹頭轉向一邊。"},{"en":"Head turned to one side means the head is facing left or right rather than straight ahead.","zh":"head turned to one side 指頭部朝左或右，而不是正面向前。"},{"en":"A portrait may show a person with their head turned to one side.","zh":"肖像畫可能顯示人物頭轉向一邊。"},{"en":"This pose can make the subject look alert, watchful or uncertain.","zh":"這種姿勢可以令主體看起來警覺、注視着甚麼或不確定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visual detail in posture.","zh":"這個片語描述姿勢中的視覺細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"stare straight at","meaning":"直直盯着……","examples":[{"en":"The falcon seems to be staring straight at the viewer.","zh":"那隻獵鷹似乎直直盯着觀者。"},{"en":"To stare straight at someone means to look directly and intensely at them.","zh":"stare straight at someone 指直接而強烈地看着某人。"},{"en":"The animal in the painting stares straight at the audience.","zh":"畫中的動物直直盯着觀眾。"},{"en":"A direct stare can make a painting feel powerful or uncomfortable.","zh":"直接凝視可以令畫作感覺有力量或令人不安。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when analysing eye contact in art.","zh":"這個片語適合用於分析藝術中的眼神接觸。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a bit scary","meaning":"有點可怕","examples":[{"en":"Tom thinks the falcon looks a bit scary.","zh":"Tom 覺得那隻獵鷹看起來有點可怕。"},{"en":"A bit scary means slightly frightening or unsettling.","zh":"a bit scary 指有點令人害怕或不安。"},{"en":"The dark background made the bird look a bit scary.","zh":"深色背景令那隻鳥看起來有點可怕。"},{"en":"This phrase is softer than saying “very frightening”.","zh":"這個片語比說 “very frightening” 較柔和。"},{"en":"It is useful for expressing a mild emotional reaction.","zh":"它適合用於表達輕微情緒反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"possible danger","meaning":"潛在危險","examples":[{"en":"Jess suggests talking about the possible danger in the bird’s look.","zh":"Jess 建議談談那隻鳥眼神中的潛在危險。"},{"en":"Possible danger means danger that may be present or suggested, though not certain.","zh":"possible danger 指可能存在或被暗示的危險，但不一定確定。"},{"en":"The sharp beak and direct stare suggest possible danger.","zh":"銳利的鳥喙和直接凝視暗示潛在危險。"},{"en":"In art, danger can be implied through colour, expression or composition.","zh":"在藝術中，危險可以透過顏色、表情或構圖被暗示。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing mood and symbolism.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論氣氛和象徵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be suggested by","meaning":"由……暗示","examples":[{"en":"The possible danger is suggested by the bird’s look.","zh":"潛在危險由那隻鳥的眼神暗示出來。"},{"en":"To be suggested by something means to be implied or hinted at by it.","zh":"be suggested by something 指由某事暗示或提示出來。"},{"en":"The sadness of the scene is suggested by the grey sky.","zh":"場景中的悲傷由灰色天空暗示出來。"},{"en":"Artists often suggest meaning indirectly through visual details.","zh":"藝術家常透過視覺細節間接暗示意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in art analysis.","zh":"這個片語常見於藝術分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the bird’s look","meaning":"那隻鳥的眼神","examples":[{"en":"The bird’s look suggests possible danger.","zh":"那隻鳥的眼神暗示潛在危險。"},{"en":"The bird’s look means the expression, gaze or appearance of the bird.","zh":"the bird’s look 指那隻鳥的表情、凝視或外觀。"},{"en":"The bird’s look in the painting is sharp and watchful.","zh":"畫中那隻鳥的眼神銳利而警覺。"},{"en":"A look can suggest emotion even when the subject is an animal.","zh":"即使主體是動物，眼神也可以暗示情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase helps analyse visual expression.","zh":"這個片語有助分析視覺表情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fish hawk","meaning":"魚鷹","examples":[{"en":"Jess likes a picture of a fish hawk by Audubon.","zh":"Jess 喜歡 Audubon 一幅魚鷹的畫。"},{"en":"A fish hawk is another name for an osprey, a bird that catches fish.","zh":"fish hawk 是 osprey 的另一個名稱，指捕魚的鳥。"},{"en":"A fish hawk is often shown flying over water with strong wings.","zh":"魚鷹常被描繪為張開強壯翅膀飛過水面。"},{"en":"In art, a fish hawk can suggest speed, hunting and natural power.","zh":"在藝術中，魚鷹可以暗示速度、捕獵和自然力量。"},{"en":"This phrase names a bird of prey linked to water.","zh":"這個片語命名一種與水相關的猛禽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"swoop over","meaning":"掠過……上方","examples":[{"en":"The fish hawk is swooping over the water.","zh":"魚鷹正在水面上方掠過。"},{"en":"To swoop over something means to fly quickly downward or across it in a sweeping movement.","zh":"swoop over something 指以俯衝或弧形動作快速飛過某物上方。"},{"en":"The bird swooped over the river and caught a fish.","zh":"那隻鳥掠過河面並抓住一條魚。"},{"en":"Swooping movement can make a painting feel dramatic and energetic.","zh":"掠過的動作可以令畫作感覺戲劇化而充滿活力。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for birds of prey.","zh":"這個片語常用於猛禽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"talons","meaning":"爪","examples":[{"en":"The fish hawk has a fish in its talons.","zh":"魚鷹的爪中抓着一條魚。"},{"en":"Talons are the sharp claws of birds of prey.","zh":"talons 指猛禽銳利的爪。"},{"en":"Eagles and hawks use their talons to catch and hold prey.","zh":"鷹和隼用爪捕捉並抓住獵物。"},{"en":"Talons in a painting can suggest strength, danger and survival.","zh":"畫作中的爪可以暗示力量、危險和生存。"},{"en":"This word is often used when describing hunting birds.","zh":"這個字常用於描述捕獵鳥類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take up most of","meaning":"佔據……大部分","examples":[{"en":"The bird’s black wings take up most of the picture.","zh":"那隻鳥的黑色翅膀佔據畫面大部分。"},{"en":"To take up most of something means to occupy the largest part of it.","zh":"take up most of something 指佔據某物最大的部分。"},{"en":"The dark sky takes up most of the painting.","zh":"深色天空佔據畫作大部分。"},{"en":"When one object takes up most of the picture, it becomes visually dominant.","zh":"當一個物件佔據畫面大部分，它便成為視覺上的主導。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when analysing composition.","zh":"這個片語適合用於分析構圖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"discuss something in relation to","meaning":"從……角度討論某事","examples":[{"en":"Tom suggests discussing the painting in relation to predators and food chains.","zh":"Tom 建議從掠食者和食物鏈角度討論那幅畫。"},{"en":"To discuss something in relation to a topic means to analyse it through that topic or connection.","zh":"discuss something in relation to a topic 指透過某主題或連繫分析某事。"},{"en":"Students can discuss the painting in relation to power and survival.","zh":"學生可以從力量和生存角度討論那幅畫。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect an artwork to a wider idea.","zh":"這個片語有助把藝術作品與更廣泛概念連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is common in academic discussion.","zh":"它常見於學術討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"predators","meaning":"掠食者","examples":[{"en":"The painting could be discussed in relation to predators.","zh":"這幅畫可以從掠食者角度討論。"},{"en":"Predators are animals that hunt and eat other animals.","zh":"predators 指捕獵並吃其他動物的動物。"},{"en":"Hawks, lions and sharks are examples of predators.","zh":"鷹、獅子和鯊魚都是掠食者的例子。"},{"en":"Predators in art can symbolise power, danger or natural order.","zh":"藝術中的掠食者可以象徵力量、危險或自然秩序。"},{"en":"This word is common in biology and environmental discussion.","zh":"這個字常見於生物學和環境討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"food chains","meaning":"食物鏈","examples":[{"en":"The painting could be linked to food chains.","zh":"這幅畫可以與食物鏈連繫起來。"},{"en":"Food chains show how energy passes from one living thing to another through eating.","zh":"food chains 顯示能量如何透過進食由一種生物傳到另一種生物。"},{"en":"A fish hawk catching a fish is part of a food chain.","zh":"魚鷹捕魚是食物鏈的一部分。"},{"en":"Food chains remind viewers that nature involves survival and dependence.","zh":"食物鏈提醒觀者，自然包含生存和依存關係。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in ecology and biology.","zh":"這個片語常見於生態學和生物學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"concentrate on","meaning":"集中於……","examples":[{"en":"Jess will concentrate on the impression of rapid motion.","zh":"Jess 會集中於快速動作的印象。"},{"en":"To concentrate on something means to focus attention on it.","zh":"concentrate on something 指把注意力集中在某事上。"},{"en":"In her analysis, Jess decided to concentrate on colour and movement.","zh":"在分析中，Jess 決定集中於顏色和動感。"},{"en":"Concentrating on one feature can make an explanation clearer.","zh":"集中於一個特色可以令解釋更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when narrowing an analysis.","zh":"這個片語適合用於收窄分析範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"impression of","meaning":"……的印象","examples":[{"en":"The painting gives an impression of rapid motion.","zh":"這幅畫給人快速動作的印象。"},{"en":"An impression of something is the feeling or effect created by it.","zh":"impression of something 指某事營造出的感覺或效果。"},{"en":"The blurred lines give an impression of speed.","zh":"模糊線條給人速度感的印象。"},{"en":"In art, an impression may be more important than exact detail.","zh":"在藝術中，印象可能比精確細節更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing mood or visual effect.","zh":"這個片語適合用於描述氣氛或視覺效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rapid motion","meaning":"快速動作","examples":[{"en":"Jess wants to discuss the rapid motion in the picture.","zh":"Jess 想討論畫中的快速動作。"},{"en":"Rapid motion means very fast movement.","zh":"rapid motion 指非常快速的移動。"},{"en":"The bird’s open wings create a sense of rapid motion.","zh":"鳥張開的翅膀營造快速動作的感覺。"},{"en":"Artists can show rapid motion through diagonal lines, blurred forms or dramatic composition.","zh":"藝術家可以透過斜線、模糊形態或戲劇化構圖表現快速動作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when analysing dynamic images.","zh":"這個片語適合用於分析動態圖像。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"kingfisher","meaning":"翠鳥","examples":[{"en":"Jess mentions a picture of a kingfisher by van Gogh.","zh":"Jess 提到 van Gogh 一幅翠鳥的畫。"},{"en":"A kingfisher is a small brightly coloured bird often found near water.","zh":"kingfisher 指一種常見於水邊、顏色鮮艷的小鳥。"},{"en":"Kingfishers are known for their blue feathers and quick movement.","zh":"翠鳥以藍色羽毛和快速動作聞名。"},{"en":"In art, a kingfisher can suggest beauty, stillness or sudden speed.","zh":"在藝術中，翠鳥可以暗示美麗、靜止或突然速度。"},{"en":"This word names a specific bird often linked with streams and rivers.","zh":"這個字命名一種常與溪流和河流相關的特定鳥類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"perch on","meaning":"棲息在……上","examples":[{"en":"The kingfisher is perching on a reed near a stream.","zh":"翠鳥棲息在溪流附近的一根蘆葦上。"},{"en":"To perch on something means for a bird to sit or rest on it.","zh":"perch on something 指鳥坐在或停留在某物上。"},{"en":"The bird perched on a branch above the water.","zh":"那隻鳥棲息在水面上的一條樹枝上。"},{"en":"Perching can create a calm contrast with later movement.","zh":"棲息可以與之後的動作形成平靜對比。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when describing birds.","zh":"這個片語常用於描述鳥類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reed","meaning":"蘆葦","examples":[{"en":"The kingfisher is perching on a reed growing near a stream.","zh":"翠鳥棲息在溪流附近生長的一根蘆葦上。"},{"en":"A reed is a tall thin plant that often grows near water.","zh":"reed 指一種常生長在水邊的高而幼的植物。"},{"en":"Reeds can bend easily in the wind.","zh":"蘆葦在風中容易彎曲。"},{"en":"In a painting, reeds can help show a watery or natural environment.","zh":"在畫作中，蘆葦可以幫助呈現水邊或自然環境。"},{"en":"This word is common in descriptions of wetlands, rivers and streams.","zh":"這個字常見於濕地、河流和溪流描寫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"near a stream","meaning":"在溪流附近","examples":[{"en":"The reed is growing near a stream.","zh":"蘆葦生長在溪流附近。"},{"en":"Near a stream means close to a small flowing body of water.","zh":"near a stream 指接近一條流動的小水道。"},{"en":"Wildflowers were growing near a stream behind the village.","zh":"野花生長在村莊後方的溪流附近。"},{"en":"Birds such as kingfishers are often found near streams because they feed on fish.","zh":"翠鳥等鳥類常在溪流附近出現，因為牠們以魚為食。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a natural location.","zh":"這個片語描述自然位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"shades","meaning":"色調","examples":[{"en":"The picture has beautiful blue, red and black shades.","zh":"這幅畫有美麗的藍色、紅色和黑色色調。"},{"en":"Shades are different tones or variations of a colour.","zh":"shades 指一種顏色的不同深淺或變化。"},{"en":"The artist used several shades of blue to paint the bird’s feathers.","zh":"藝術家使用幾種藍色色調來畫鳥的羽毛。"},{"en":"Colour shades can create mood, depth and visual interest.","zh":"色調可以營造氣氛、深度和視覺趣味。"},{"en":"This word is useful in art and design analysis.","zh":"這個字適合用於藝術和設計分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"choose something because","meaning":"因……而選擇某物","examples":[{"en":"Jess chose the picture because it reminded her of a real kingfisher.","zh":"Jess 因為這幅畫令她想起真正的翠鳥而選擇它。"},{"en":"To choose something because of a reason means to select it for that reason.","zh":"choose something because of a reason 指因某理由而選擇某物。"},{"en":"Tom chose the painting because its colours were dramatic.","zh":"Tom 因為畫作顏色戲劇化而選擇它。"},{"en":"Explaining why you chose something helps show personal connection and purpose.","zh":"解釋為何選擇某物有助顯示個人連結和目的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reflective writing.","zh":"這個片語適合用於反思寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"real kingfisher","meaning":"真正的翠鳥","examples":[{"en":"Jess once saw a real kingfisher when she was little.","zh":"Jess 小時候曾見過一隻真正的翠鳥。"},{"en":"A real kingfisher is an actual living bird, not an image or symbol.","zh":"real kingfisher 指真實活着的鳥，而不是圖像或象徵。"},{"en":"Seeing a real kingfisher can make a painting of one feel more personal.","zh":"見過真正的翠鳥可以令相關畫作更有個人意義。"},{"en":"Real-life encounters often shape how people respond to artworks.","zh":"真實生活中的相遇常塑造人們如何回應藝術作品。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real experience with artistic representation.","zh":"這個片語把真實經驗與藝術呈現作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"when I was little","meaning":"我小時候","examples":[{"en":"Jess saw a real kingfisher when she was little.","zh":"Jess 小時候看見過真正的翠鳥。"},{"en":"When I was little means when I was a young child.","zh":"when I was little 指我還是小孩子的時候。"},{"en":"When I was little, I loved drawing animals from picture books.","zh":"我小時候很喜歡照着圖畫書畫動物。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces childhood memories.","zh":"這個片語常引入童年回憶。"},{"en":"It sounds natural and personal in spoken English.","zh":"它在英語口語中聽起來自然而個人化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be out walking with","meaning":"與……外出散步","examples":[{"en":"Jess was out walking with her grandfather.","zh":"Jess 當時與祖父外出散步。"},{"en":"To be out walking with someone means to be outside taking a walk together.","zh":"be out walking with someone 指與某人在戶外一起散步。"},{"en":"I was out walking with my friend when we saw a fox.","zh":"我與朋友外出散步時看見一隻狐狸。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a casual outdoor activity.","zh":"這個片語暗示輕鬆的戶外活動。"},{"en":"It often appears in stories about memories or chance encounters.","zh":"它常出現在關於回憶或偶然相遇的故事中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"never forgotten it","meaning":"一直沒有忘記","examples":[{"en":"Jess has never forgotten seeing the kingfisher.","zh":"Jess 一直沒有忘記看見翠鳥這件事。"},{"en":"To never forget something means to remember it clearly for a long time.","zh":"never forget something 指長時間清楚記得某事。"},{"en":"I have never forgotten the first time I saw a painting by van Gogh.","zh":"我一直沒有忘記第一次看見 van Gogh 畫作的情景。"},{"en":"Strong visual experiences can stay in memory for years.","zh":"強烈的視覺經驗可以多年留在記憶中。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an event was meaningful or powerful.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事件有意義或很有力量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"personal link","meaning":"個人連結","examples":[{"en":"Tom asks whether they can use a personal link in the project.","zh":"Tom 問他們是否可以在專題中使用個人連結。"},{"en":"A personal link is a connection between the topic and someone’s own life or memories.","zh":"personal link 指主題與某人自身生活或回憶之間的連繫。"},{"en":"Jess has a personal link to the kingfisher painting because of her childhood memory.","zh":"Jess 因童年回憶而與翠鳥畫作有個人連結。"},{"en":"Personal links can make analysis more honest and meaningful.","zh":"個人連結可以令分析更真誠和有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reflective art projects.","zh":"這個片語適合用於反思性藝術專題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"portrait","meaning":"肖像畫","examples":[{"en":"Tom chose a portrait called William Wells.","zh":"Tom 選擇了一幅名為 William Wells 的肖像畫。"},{"en":"A portrait is an artwork showing a person, especially their face and expression.","zh":"portrait 指呈現人物的藝術作品，尤其是臉部和表情。"},{"en":"A portrait can reveal personality, status, mood or social role.","zh":"肖像畫可以揭示性格、地位、情緒或社會角色。"},{"en":"Portraits often include objects that tell us more about the sitter.","zh":"肖像畫常包含物件，讓我們更了解畫中人物。"},{"en":"This word is central in art analysis.","zh":"這個字是藝術分析中的核心詞彙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"middle-aged man","meaning":"中年男子","examples":[{"en":"The portrait shows a middle-aged man who has just shot a bird.","zh":"肖像畫顯示一名剛射下一隻鳥的中年男子。"},{"en":"A middle-aged man is a man who is no longer young but not yet elderly.","zh":"middle-aged man 指已不年輕但尚未年老的男子。"},{"en":"The painting shows a middle-aged man dressed in formal clothes.","zh":"這幅畫顯示一名穿着正式衣服的中年男子。"},{"en":"Age can affect how viewers interpret a person’s expression and actions.","zh":"年齡會影響觀者如何詮釋人物表情和行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the subject’s stage of life.","zh":"這個片語描述主體的人生階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"shoot a bird","meaning":"射下一隻鳥","examples":[{"en":"The man in the portrait has just shot a bird.","zh":"肖像畫中的男子剛射下一隻鳥。"},{"en":"To shoot a bird means to kill or injure it with a gun.","zh":"shoot a bird 指用槍殺死或傷害一隻鳥。"},{"en":"In older hunting portraits, men were often shown after they had shot birds.","zh":"在較舊的狩獵肖像畫中，男子常被描繪為剛射下鳥類。"},{"en":"This action can raise questions about power, cruelty and attitudes to nature.","zh":"這個行動可以引發關於權力、殘酷和對自然態度的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when discussing hunting imagery.","zh":"討論狩獵圖像時，這個片語很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the way he is holding","meaning":"他拿着……的方式","examples":[{"en":"The way the man is holding the bird suggests uncertainty.","zh":"那名男子拿着鳥的方式暗示不確定。"},{"en":"The way he is holding something means the manner or position in which he holds it.","zh":"the way he is holding something 指他拿着某物的方式或姿勢。"},{"en":"The way he is holding the animal makes him look uncomfortable.","zh":"他拿着那隻動物的方式令他看起來不自在。"},{"en":"In art, body language can reveal feelings that are not spoken.","zh":"在藝術中，肢體語言可以揭示沒有說出的感受。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when analysing posture and gesture.","zh":"這個片語適合用於分析姿勢和動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"suggest he is not sure about","meaning":"暗示他不肯定……","examples":[{"en":"The man’s expression suggests he is not sure about what he has done.","zh":"那名男子的表情暗示他不肯定自己所做的事。"},{"en":"To suggest he is not sure about something means to imply that he feels uncertain or doubtful.","zh":"suggest he is not sure about something 指暗示他感到不確定或懷疑。"},{"en":"His hesitant look suggests he is not sure about his decision.","zh":"他猶豫的神情暗示他不肯定自己的決定。"},{"en":"A facial expression can suggest doubt without stating it directly.","zh":"面部表情可以不直接說明而暗示懷疑。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when interpreting emotional meaning in a painting.","zh":"這個片語適合用於詮釋畫作中的情感意義。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"what he has done","meaning":"他所做的事","examples":[{"en":"The man seems unsure about what he has done.","zh":"那名男子似乎不肯定自己所做的事。"},{"en":"What he has done means the action he has performed.","zh":"what he has done 指他已經做出的行動。"},{"en":"The child looked worried about what he had done to the broken vase.","zh":"孩子看起來擔心自己對破花瓶所做的事。"},{"en":"In the portrait, the phrase points to the moral weight of shooting the bird.","zh":"在肖像畫中，這個片語指向射鳥這件事的道德重量。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the action and its consequences.","zh":"這個片語着重行動及其後果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"to me","meaning":"對我來說","examples":[{"en":"To Tom, the portrait is about people’s ambiguous relationship with nature.","zh":"對 Tom 來說，這幅肖像畫是關於人與自然之間矛盾的關係。"},{"en":"To me means in my opinion or from my point of view.","zh":"to me 指以我的看法或從我的角度來說。"},{"en":"To me, the painting is more about guilt than victory.","zh":"對我來說，這幅畫更關乎內疚，而不是勝利。"},{"en":"This phrase makes interpretation personal rather than absolute.","zh":"這個片語令詮釋變得個人化，而不是絕對化。"},{"en":"It is useful in art discussions and reflective writing.","zh":"它適合用於藝術討論和反思寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ambiguous","meaning":"矛盾的；含糊的","examples":[{"en":"The painting shows how ambiguous people are about exploiting nature.","zh":"這幅畫顯示人們在利用自然方面是多麼矛盾。"},{"en":"Ambiguous means unclear, mixed or having more than one possible meaning.","zh":"ambiguous 指不清楚、混合，或有多於一種可能意思。"},{"en":"The man’s expression is ambiguous because he looks proud and uneasy at the same time.","zh":"那名男子的表情很矛盾，因為他看起來既自豪又不安。"},{"en":"Ambiguity can make an artwork more interesting to discuss.","zh":"含糊性可以令藝術作品更值得討論。"},{"en":"This word is useful when meaning is not simple or direct.","zh":"當意思不簡單或不直接時，這個字很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"exploit the natural world","meaning":"利用自然世界","examples":[{"en":"People exploit the natural world in ambiguous ways.","zh":"人們以矛盾方式利用自然世界。"},{"en":"To exploit the natural world means to use nature’s resources, sometimes selfishly or harmfully.","zh":"exploit the natural world 指使用自然資源，有時帶自私或有害意味。"},{"en":"Hunting, logging and mining can all exploit the natural world.","zh":"狩獵、伐木和採礦都可以是利用自然世界。"},{"en":"Art can question whether humans admire nature while also damaging it.","zh":"藝術可以質疑人類是否一邊欣賞自然，一邊破壞自然。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in environmental and ethical discussion.","zh":"這個片語適合用於環境和倫理討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Vairumati","meaning":"《Vairumati》","examples":[{"en":"Jess mentions Gauguin’s picture Vairumati.","zh":"Jess 提到 Gauguin 的畫作《Vairumati》。"},{"en":"Vairumati is the title of a painting by Paul Gauguin.","zh":"Vairumati 是 Paul Gauguin 一幅畫的標題。"},{"en":"When discussing Vairumati, students may focus on symbolism, colour and cultural context.","zh":"討論《Vairumati》時，學生可以集中於象徵、色彩和文化背景。"},{"en":"Titles can guide viewers towards possible meanings in a painting.","zh":"標題可以引導觀者理解畫作的可能意義。"},{"en":"This term names a specific artwork.","zh":"這個詞命名一件特定藝術作品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"do it in","meaning":"在……創作它","examples":[{"en":"Gauguin did the picture in Tahiti.","zh":"Gauguin 在大溪地創作了這幅畫。"},{"en":"To do a picture in a place means to create or paint it there.","zh":"do a picture in a place 指在某地創作或繪畫某作品。"},{"en":"The artist did many sketches in the countryside.","zh":"那位藝術家在郊外創作了許多素描。"},{"en":"The place where an artwork is made can affect its colours, subjects and meaning.","zh":"作品創作地可以影響其色彩、主題和意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and conversational.","zh":"這個片語較口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Tahiti","meaning":"大溪地","examples":[{"en":"Gauguin painted Vairumati in Tahiti.","zh":"Gauguin 在大溪地畫了《Vairumati》。"},{"en":"Tahiti is an island in French Polynesia in the South Pacific.","zh":"Tahiti 是南太平洋法屬波利尼西亞的一個島嶼。"},{"en":"Gauguin’s Tahiti paintings often show figures, nature and symbolic imagery.","zh":"Gauguin 的大溪地畫作常呈現人物、自然和象徵圖像。"},{"en":"The setting of Tahiti is important when discussing the cultural context of his work.","zh":"討論他的作品文化背景時，大溪地這個場景很重要。"},{"en":"This word names a real place connected with the artist’s work.","zh":"這個字命名一個與藝術家作品有關的真實地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"behind her","meaning":"在她身後","examples":[{"en":"There is a white bird behind the woman.","zh":"女子身後有一隻白鳥。"},{"en":"Behind her means at the back of the female figure.","zh":"behind her 指在女性人物的後方。"},{"en":"In the painting, a dark tree stands behind her.","zh":"在畫中，一棵深色樹站在她身後。"},{"en":"Objects placed behind a figure can add meaning or create depth.","zh":"放在人物身後的物件可以增加意義或製造深度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing composition.","zh":"這個片語適合用於描述構圖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"eat a lizard","meaning":"吃蜥蜴","examples":[{"en":"The white bird is eating a lizard.","zh":"那隻白鳥正在吃蜥蜴。"},{"en":"To eat a lizard means to consume a small reptile as food.","zh":"eat a lizard 指吃一隻小型爬行動物作食物。"},{"en":"In nature, some birds eat lizards, insects and small animals.","zh":"在自然界，有些鳥會吃蜥蜴、昆蟲和小動物。"},{"en":"In a painting, an animal eating another creature can suggest survival or the cycle of life.","zh":"在畫作中，一隻動物吃另一種生物可以暗示生存或生命循環。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an action that may carry symbolic meaning.","zh":"這個片語描述一個可能帶象徵意義的動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be interested in","meaning":"對……感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Jess is interested in what idea the bird refers to.","zh":"Jess 對那隻鳥指涉甚麼概念感興趣。"},{"en":"To be interested in something means to want to know more about it.","zh":"be interested in something 指想了解更多關於某事的資料。"},{"en":"Tom is interested in how birds are used as symbols in paintings.","zh":"Tom 對鳥在畫作中如何被用作象徵感興趣。"},{"en":"Interest often leads students to ask better research questions.","zh":"興趣常引導學生提出更好的研究問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in study and conversation.","zh":"這個片語常見於學習和對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"指涉；代表","examples":[{"en":"The bird refers to the never-ending cycle of existence.","zh":"那隻鳥指涉永無止境的生命循環。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to point to, represent or mention it.","zh":"refer to something 指指向、代表或提及某事。"},{"en":"In the painting, the bird may refer to death and rebirth.","zh":"在畫作中，那隻鳥可能指涉死亡和重生。"},{"en":"Symbols in art often refer to ideas beyond the visible object.","zh":"藝術中的象徵常指涉可見物件以外的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in interpretation and analysis.","zh":"這個片語適合用於詮釋和分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"apparently","meaning":"顯然；據說","examples":[{"en":"Apparently, the bird is a reference to the cycle of existence.","zh":"據說，那隻鳥是對生命循環的指涉。"},{"en":"Apparently means according to what people say or according to available information.","zh":"apparently 指根據人們所說或現有資料而言。"},{"en":"Apparently, the artist used the bird as a symbol of renewal.","zh":"據說，藝術家把那隻鳥用作重生的象徵。"},{"en":"This word can show that the speaker is reporting information rather than claiming personal certainty.","zh":"這個字可以顯示說話者是在報告資料，而不是表示個人完全確定。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing interpretations found in research.","zh":"當討論研究中找到的詮釋時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a reference to","meaning":"對……的指涉","examples":[{"en":"The white bird is a reference to the never-ending cycle of existence.","zh":"那隻白鳥是對永無止境生命循環的指涉。"},{"en":"A reference to something is a sign, symbol or mention that points to it.","zh":"a reference to something 指指向某事的標誌、象徵或提及。"},{"en":"The skull in the painting may be a reference to death.","zh":"畫中的骷髏可能是對死亡的指涉。"},{"en":"References in art can be cultural, religious, personal or historical.","zh":"藝術中的指涉可以是文化、宗教、個人或歷史性的。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in art analysis.","zh":"這個片語常見於藝術分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"never-ending cycle","meaning":"永無止境的循環","examples":[{"en":"The bird represents the never-ending cycle of existence.","zh":"那隻鳥代表永無止境的生命循環。"},{"en":"A never-ending cycle is a process that continues again and again without a clear end.","zh":"never-ending cycle 指不斷重複、沒有明確終點的過程。"},{"en":"Nature often shows a never-ending cycle of birth, death and renewal.","zh":"自然常呈現出生、死亡和更新的永無止境循環。"},{"en":"Artists use cycles to suggest that life continues beyond individual moments.","zh":"藝術家使用循環來暗示生命超越個別時刻而延續。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing symbolic meaning.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論象徵意義。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cycle of existence","meaning":"生命循環","examples":[{"en":"The painting refers to the cycle of existence.","zh":"這幅畫指涉生命循環。"},{"en":"The cycle of existence means the repeating pattern of life, death and renewal.","zh":"cycle of existence 指生命、死亡和更新的重複模式。"},{"en":"A bird eating a lizard can suggest the cycle of existence in nature.","zh":"一隻鳥吃蜥蜴可以暗示自然中的生命循環。"},{"en":"This idea often appears in art, religion and philosophy.","zh":"這個概念常出現在藝術、宗教和哲學中。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a deep symbolic reading of an image.","zh":"這個片語為圖像提供深層象徵解讀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hold something in one fist","meaning":"用一隻手握着某物","examples":[{"en":"Giovanni de Medici is holding a tiny bird in one fist.","zh":"Giovanni de Medici 用一隻手握着一隻小鳥。"},{"en":"To hold something in one fist means to hold it inside one closed hand.","zh":"hold something in one fist 指用一隻握緊的手拿着某物。"},{"en":"The child held a small stone in one fist.","zh":"那孩子用一隻手握着一粒小石頭。"},{"en":"Holding a bird in one fist can suggest control, care or danger depending on the image.","zh":"用一隻手握着鳥可以視乎圖像暗示控制、照顧或危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific hand gesture.","zh":"這個片語描述一個具體手勢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"tiny bird","meaning":"小鳥","examples":[{"en":"The little boy is holding a tiny bird.","zh":"那個小男孩正握着一隻小鳥。"},{"en":"A tiny bird is a very small bird.","zh":"tiny bird 指非常細小的鳥。"},{"en":"The tiny bird in the boy’s hand looks fragile.","zh":"男孩手中的小鳥看起來很脆弱。"},{"en":"Small size can make a subject seem vulnerable or delicate.","zh":"細小尺寸可以令主體顯得易受傷或精緻。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing scale and emotional effect.","zh":"這個片語適合用於描述比例和情感效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"carefully so he doesn’t hurt it","meaning":"小心地以免弄傷它","examples":[{"en":"The boy is holding the bird carefully so he does not hurt it.","zh":"那個男孩小心地握着小鳥，以免弄傷它。"},{"en":"Carefully so he doesn’t hurt it means gently and with attention to avoid causing harm.","zh":"carefully so he doesn’t hurt it 指輕柔並小心地做，以避免造成傷害。"},{"en":"The child held the butterfly carefully so he did not damage its wings.","zh":"那孩子小心地拿着蝴蝶，以免弄傷牠的翅膀。"},{"en":"This phrase shows both action and purpose.","zh":"這個片語同時顯示行動和目的。"},{"en":"It can suggest tenderness, responsibility and respect for life.","zh":"它可以暗示溫柔、責任感和對生命的尊重。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 16/task-4":[{"front":"ancient philosophy","meaning":"古代哲學","examples":[{"en":"Ancient philosophy is not just about talking or lecturing.","zh":"古代哲學不只是關於談論或講授。"},{"en":"Ancient philosophy means the ideas and teachings of thinkers from the ancient world.","zh":"古代哲學意思是古代世界思想家的理念和教導。"},{"en":"Students may study ancient philosophy to understand how people thought about life, virtue and happiness.","zh":"學生可能研究古代哲學，以了解人們如何思考人生、美德和幸福。"},{"en":"Ancient philosophy can still influence modern psychology, politics and business.","zh":"古代哲學至今仍可影響現代心理學、政治和商業。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing early systems of thought.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論早期思想體系。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"not just about","meaning":"不只是關於……","examples":[{"en":"Ancient philosophy is not just about talking or lecturing.","zh":"古代哲學不只是關於談論或講授。"},{"en":"Not just about means something includes more than the thing mentioned.","zh":"不只是關於某事意思是它包含的不止剛提及的內容。"},{"en":"Education is not just about exams; it is also about growth and confidence.","zh":"教育不只是關於考試，也關於成長和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase helps correct a narrow understanding of a subject.","zh":"這個短語有助修正對某主題的狹窄理解。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing that a topic has wider importance.","zh":"當顯示某主題有更廣泛重要性時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"talking or lecturing","meaning":"談論或講授","examples":[{"en":"Philosophy is not just about talking or lecturing.","zh":"哲學不只是關於談論或講授。"},{"en":"Talking or lecturing means speaking about a subject, often to explain or teach it.","zh":"談論或講授意思是就某主題說話，通常為了解釋或教導。"},{"en":"A philosophy class may include talking or lecturing, but it should also encourage reflection.","zh":"哲學課可以包括談論或講授，但也應鼓勵反思。"},{"en":"Practical philosophy is about action as well as discussion.","zh":"實用哲學關乎行動，也關乎討論。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts spoken teaching with lived practice.","zh":"這個短語把口頭教學與實際實踐作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"long, dense books","meaning":"冗長艱深的書","examples":[{"en":"Ancient philosophy is not just about reading long, dense books.","zh":"古代哲學不只是關於閱讀冗長艱深的書。"},{"en":"Long, dense books are lengthy books that are difficult to read because they contain complex ideas.","zh":"冗長艱深的書是篇幅長、思想複雜而難讀的書。"},{"en":"Some students avoid philosophy because they imagine only long, dense books.","zh":"有些學生避開哲學，因為他們只想到冗長艱深的書。"},{"en":"A dense book may require slow reading and careful note-taking.","zh":"艱深的書可能需要慢慢閱讀和仔細做筆記。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficult academic reading.","zh":"這個短語描述困難的學術閱讀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, people have used philosophy throughout history.","zh":"事實上，人們在整個歷史中都使用哲學。"},{"en":"In fact is used to add true information, often correcting or strengthening an earlier point.","zh":"事實上用來加入真實資訊，常用於修正或加強前一點。"},{"en":"Some people think philosophy is useless; in fact, it can shape daily decisions.","zh":"有些人認為哲學沒有用；事實上，它可以塑造日常決定。"},{"en":"This phrase helps introduce a stronger or clearer statement.","zh":"這個短語有助引入更強或更清楚的說法。"},{"en":"It is common in explanations and arguments.","zh":"它常見於解釋和論證。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"throughout history","meaning":"在整個歷史中","examples":[{"en":"People have used philosophy throughout history.","zh":"人們在整個歷史中都使用哲學。"},{"en":"Throughout history means during all periods of human history.","zh":"在整個歷史中意思是在人類歷史的所有時期。"},{"en":"Throughout history, people have looked for ways to deal with fear, loss and failure.","zh":"在整個歷史中，人們一直尋找處理恐懼、失去和失敗的方法。"},{"en":"Ideas that last throughout history often speak to common human problems.","zh":"能在整個歷史中延續的思想，通常回應共同的人類問題。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a very broad historical scope.","zh":"這個短語提供非常廣闊的歷史範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"solve their problems","meaning":"解決他們的問題","examples":[{"en":"People have used philosophy to solve their problems.","zh":"人們曾使用哲學來解決他們的問題。"},{"en":"To solve their problems means to find ways to deal with difficulties or challenges.","zh":"解決問題意思是找方法處理困難或挑戰。"},{"en":"Stoic thinking can help people solve problems by separating what they can and cannot control.","zh":"斯多葛思想可以透過區分可控制和不可控制的事，幫助人解決問題。"},{"en":"Philosophy may not remove every problem, but it can change how people respond.","zh":"哲學未必能移除所有問題，但可以改變人們的回應方式。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical usefulness.","zh":"這個短語重點是實際用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"achieve their greatest triumphs","meaning":"取得最偉大的成就","examples":[{"en":"People have used philosophy to achieve their greatest triumphs.","zh":"人們曾使用哲學來取得他們最偉大的成就。"},{"en":"To achieve their greatest triumphs means to reach their most important successes.","zh":"取得最偉大的成就意思是達到最重要的成功。"},{"en":"A leader may use philosophy to stay calm and achieve a great political victory.","zh":"領袖可能運用哲學保持冷靜，並取得重大政治勝利。"},{"en":"Triumphs often require discipline, courage and clear judgement.","zh":"成就通常需要自律、勇氣和清晰判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes major success after effort.","zh":"這個短語描述努力後的重大成功。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"specifically","meaning":"具體來說","examples":[{"en":"Specifically, the speaker is referring to Stoicism.","zh":"具體來說，講者指的是斯多葛主義。"},{"en":"Specifically means exactly or more precisely.","zh":"具體來說意思是更精確地說。"},{"en":"The lecture is about ancient philosophy, specifically Stoicism.","zh":"這場講座是關於古代哲學，具體來說是斯多葛主義。"},{"en":"This word helps narrow a broad topic to a more exact focus.","zh":"這個詞幫助把廣泛主題收窄到更精確的焦點。"},{"en":"It is useful in presentations and essays.","zh":"它適合用於匯報和文章。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"指的是……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker is referring to Stoicism.","zh":"講者指的是斯多葛主義。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to mention or mean it.","zh":"指的是某事意思是提及或表示該事。"},{"en":"When the teacher says “ancient philosophy,” she may refer to Stoicism, Epicureanism or Platonism.","zh":"當老師說「古代哲學」時，她可能指的是斯多葛主義、伊壁鳩魯主義或柏拉圖思想。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when clarifying what someone means.","zh":"當澄清某人的意思時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It often appears in explanations and discussions.","zh":"它常出現在解釋和討論中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Stoicism","meaning":"斯多葛主義","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism is described as the most practical of all philosophies.","zh":"斯多葛主義被形容為所有哲學中最實用的。"},{"en":"Stoicism is an ancient philosophy that teaches self-control, virtue and acceptance of what cannot be controlled.","zh":"斯多葛主義是一種古代哲學，教導自我控制、美德和接受不能控制的事。"},{"en":"Stoicism encourages people to respond calmly to difficulty.","zh":"斯多葛主義鼓勵人冷靜回應困難。"},{"en":"Many modern readers study Stoicism for guidance on resilience and discipline.","zh":"許多現代讀者研究斯多葛主義，以尋求抗逆力和自律方面的指引。"},{"en":"This word names an influential school of ancient philosophy.","zh":"這個詞命名一個有影響力的古代哲學學派。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in my opinion","meaning":"在我看來","examples":[{"en":"In the speaker’s opinion, Stoicism is the most practical philosophy.","zh":"在講者看來，斯多葛主義是最實用的哲學。"},{"en":"In my opinion means according to what I personally think.","zh":"在我看來意思是按照我個人的想法。"},{"en":"In my opinion, a useful philosophy should help people live better.","zh":"在我看來，有用的哲學應該幫助人活得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase makes clear that the statement is a personal view.","zh":"這個短語清楚表明該說法是個人觀點。"},{"en":"It is common in speaking and argumentative writing.","zh":"它常見於口語和議論文。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the most practical of all","meaning":"在所有……中最實用","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism is the most practical of all philosophies.","zh":"斯多葛主義是所有哲學中最實用的。"},{"en":"The most practical of all means more useful in real life than every other option in the group.","zh":"在所有選項中最實用意思是在現實生活中比同組所有其他選項更有用。"},{"en":"Some people consider Stoicism the most practical of all ancient philosophies because it gives daily advice.","zh":"有些人認為斯多葛主義是所有古代哲學中最實用的，因為它提供日常建議。"},{"en":"Practical ideas are valuable when they can be applied to real problems.","zh":"當思想可以應用於真實問題時，它們就很有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly compares one thing with all others.","zh":"這個短語強烈比較一件事與所有其他事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the most appealing","meaning":"最具吸引力","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism is practical and therefore appealing.","zh":"斯多葛主義很實用，因此具吸引力。"},{"en":"The most appealing means the most attractive or interesting.","zh":"最具吸引力意思是最吸引人或最有趣。"},{"en":"A philosophy may be appealing if it helps people handle stress.","zh":"如果一種哲學幫助人處理壓力，它可能具吸引力。"},{"en":"Practical usefulness can make an idea more appealing to modern readers.","zh":"實用性可以令一個想法對現代讀者更具吸引力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong attraction or interest.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈吸引力或興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be founded in","meaning":"創立於……","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism was founded in Ancient Greece.","zh":"斯多葛主義創立於古希臘。"},{"en":"To be founded in a place means to begin or be established there.","zh":"創立於某地意思是在該地開始或建立。"},{"en":"A school of thought may be founded in one city and later spread widely.","zh":"一個思想學派可能創立於一個城市，之後廣泛傳播。"},{"en":"Knowing where an idea was founded helps explain its historical background.","zh":"知道一個思想創立於哪裏，有助解釋其歷史背景。"},{"en":"This phrase describes origin.","zh":"這個短語描述起源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Ancient Greece","meaning":"古希臘","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism was founded in Ancient Greece by Zeno of Citium.","zh":"斯多葛主義由 Citium 的 Zeno 在古希臘創立。"},{"en":"Ancient Greece was a civilisation known for philosophy, art, politics and science.","zh":"古希臘是一個以哲學、藝術、政治和科學聞名的文明。"},{"en":"Many Western philosophical traditions can be traced back to Ancient Greece.","zh":"許多西方哲學傳統都可以追溯到古希臘。"},{"en":"Ancient Greek thinkers asked questions about ethics, knowledge and society.","zh":"古希臘思想家提出關於倫理、知識和社會的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a major historical civilisation.","zh":"這個短語指一個重要歷史文明。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Zeno of Citium","meaning":"Citium 的 Zeno","examples":[{"en":"Zeno of Citium founded Stoicism in the early third century BC.","zh":"Citium 的 Zeno 在公元前 3 世紀初創立斯多葛主義。"},{"en":"Zeno of Citium was the philosopher traditionally credited with founding Stoicism.","zh":"Citium 的 Zeno 是傳統上被認為創立斯多葛主義的哲學家。"},{"en":"Students of ancient philosophy often learn Zeno of Citium before studying later Stoics.","zh":"學習古代哲學的學生通常先認識 Citium 的 Zeno，再研究後來的斯多葛派。"},{"en":"His ideas later influenced Roman thinkers such as Seneca and Marcus Aurelius.","zh":"他的思想後來影響 Seneca 和 Marcus Aurelius 等羅馬思想家。"},{"en":"This phrase names the founder of Stoicism.","zh":"這個短語命名斯多葛主義的創始人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in the early 3rd century BC","meaning":"在公元前3世紀初","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism was founded in the early third century BC.","zh":"斯多葛主義創立於公元前 3 世紀初。"},{"en":"In the early 3rd century BC means near the beginning of the years 300 to 201 before Christ.","zh":"在公元前 3 世紀初意思是在公元前 300 年至公元前 201 年這段時間的早期。"},{"en":"Many ancient philosophical schools developed before the modern scientific age.","zh":"許多古代哲學學派在現代科學時代之前發展。"},{"en":"Giving the date helps place Stoicism in historical context.","zh":"提供日期有助把斯多葛主義放入歷史語境。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a specific ancient time period.","zh":"這個短語提供具體古代時期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be practised by","meaning":"由……實踐","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism was practised by Epictetus, Cato, Seneca and Marcus Aurelius.","zh":"斯多葛主義由 Epictetus、Cato、Seneca 和 Marcus Aurelius 實踐。"},{"en":"To be practised by someone means to be followed or lived out by that person.","zh":"由某人實踐意思是被那個人跟從或在生活中實行。"},{"en":"Stoicism was practised by people from different social positions, including slaves, statesmen and emperors.","zh":"斯多葛主義由不同社會地位的人實踐，包括奴隸、政治家和皇帝。"},{"en":"A philosophy becomes influential when people actually practise it in life.","zh":"當人們在生活中真正實踐哲學，它就會變得有影響力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on application, not just study.","zh":"這個短語重點是應用，而不只是研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the likes of","meaning":"……等人","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism was practised by the likes of Epictetus and Marcus Aurelius.","zh":"斯多葛主義由 Epictetus 和 Marcus Aurelius 等人實踐。"},{"en":"The likes of means people such as.","zh":"……等人意思是例如某些人。"},{"en":"Ancient philosophy influenced the likes of politicians, writers and soldiers.","zh":"古代哲學影響了政治家、作家和軍人等人。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples of people in a group.","zh":"這個短語引入某群體中的例子。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken and semi-formal English.","zh":"它常見於口語和半正式英文。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have access to","meaning":"能接觸到……","examples":[{"en":"We still have access to these Stoic ideas.","zh":"我們仍然能接觸到這些斯多葛思想。"},{"en":"To have access to something means to be able to reach, use or study it.","zh":"能接觸到某物意思是能取得、使用或研究它。"},{"en":"Modern readers have access to ancient texts through translations and online libraries.","zh":"現代讀者可以透過翻譯和網上圖書館接觸古代文本。"},{"en":"Access to old ideas allows people to learn from past thinkers.","zh":"能接觸舊思想，讓人向過去思想家學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes availability.","zh":"這個短語描述可取得性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"despite the fact that","meaning":"儘管……","examples":[{"en":"We still have access to these ideas despite the fact that many Stoics wrote nothing for publication.","zh":"儘管許多斯多葛派人士沒有為出版而寫下作品，我們仍能接觸到這些思想。"},{"en":"Despite the fact that means although something is true.","zh":"儘管某事意思是雖然該事是真的。"},{"en":"Despite the fact that the notes were private, they later became widely read.","zh":"儘管那些筆記本來是私人性質，它們後來仍被廣泛閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between an obstacle and the actual result.","zh":"這個短語引入障礙與實際結果之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful in formal explanation.","zh":"它適合用於正式解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"write something down","meaning":"寫下某事","examples":[{"en":"The most famous Stoics never wrote anything down for publication.","zh":"最著名的斯多葛派人士從未為出版而寫下任何東西。"},{"en":"To write something down means to record it in written form.","zh":"寫下某事意思是以文字形式記錄它。"},{"en":"A student writes ideas down so they will not forget them later.","zh":"學生寫下想法，以免之後忘記。"},{"en":"Some ancient teachings survived because students wrote them down.","zh":"有些古代教導因學生寫下來而流傳下來。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on recording speech or thoughts.","zh":"這個短語重點是記錄說話或思想。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for publication","meaning":"為出版","examples":[{"en":"The most famous Stoics did not write their ideas down for publication.","zh":"最著名的斯多葛派人士沒有為出版而寫下自己的思想。"},{"en":"For publication means intended to be printed or shared publicly as a text.","zh":"為出版意思是打算把文字印刷或公開分享。"},{"en":"A private diary is usually not written for publication.","zh":"私人日記通常不是為出版而寫。"},{"en":"Writing for publication often requires editing and preparing work for readers.","zh":"為出版而寫作通常需要編輯並為讀者準備作品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the intended public release of writing.","zh":"這個短語描述文字打算公開發行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"intend something to be","meaning":"打算讓某物成為……","examples":[{"en":"Marcus Aurelius never intended his Meditations to be public.","zh":"Marcus Aurelius 從未打算讓他的《沉思錄》公開。"},{"en":"To intend something to be a certain way means to plan or mean it to have that purpose or form.","zh":"打算讓某物成為某樣子意思是計劃或希望它具有該用途或形式。"},{"en":"A teacher may intend an exercise to be a short warm-up, not a full test.","zh":"老師可能打算讓一個練習成為短暖身，而不是完整測驗。"},{"en":"Authors’ intentions can differ from how later readers use their work.","zh":"作者意圖可以與後來讀者使用作品的方式不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes purpose or planned use.","zh":"這個短語描述目的或原本用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"anything but personal","meaning":"絕非私人以外的東西","examples":[{"en":"Marcus Aurelius intended his Meditations to be anything but personal.","zh":"Marcus Aurelius 原本打算他的《沉思錄》絕非私人以外的東西。"},{"en":"In this context, anything but personal means not meant to be anything other than personal.","zh":"在這個語境中，anything but personal 意思是並非打算成為私人性質以外的東西。"},{"en":"His notes were private reflections rather than a book prepared for public readers.","zh":"他的筆記是私人反思，而不是為公眾讀者準備的書。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights that the text was not originally written for publication.","zh":"這個短語突顯該文本原本不是為出版而寫。"},{"en":"This expression can be tricky because meaning depends strongly on the full sentence.","zh":"這個表達較容易混淆，因為意思很取決於完整句子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"come to us by way of","meaning":"透過……流傳到我們手上","examples":[{"en":"Epictetus’ thoughts come to us by way of a note-taking student.","zh":"Epictetus 的思想透過一名做筆記的學生流傳到我們手上。"},{"en":"To come to us by way of something means to reach us through that person, route or method.","zh":"透過某人或某方法流傳到我們手上，意思是經由該人、路徑或方式傳到我們這裏。"},{"en":"Many ancient teachings come to us by way of students’ notes.","zh":"許多古代教導透過學生筆記流傳到我們手上。"},{"en":"Ideas can survive even when the original speaker did not publish them.","zh":"即使原本的講者沒有出版，思想仍可以保存下來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transmission or preservation.","zh":"這個短語描述傳播或保存方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"note-taking student","meaning":"做筆記的學生","examples":[{"en":"Epictetus’ thoughts were preserved by a note-taking student.","zh":"Epictetus 的思想由一名做筆記的學生保存下來。"},{"en":"A note-taking student is a student who writes down what a teacher says.","zh":"做筆記的學生是寫下老師說話內容的學生。"},{"en":"A note-taking student can help preserve lectures for later readers.","zh":"做筆記的學生可以幫助保存講課內容，供後來讀者閱讀。"},{"en":"In ancient philosophy, students’ notes sometimes became major sources of knowledge.","zh":"在古代哲學中，學生筆記有時成為重要知識來源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a student who records ideas carefully.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細記錄思想的學生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Stoic principles","meaning":"斯多葛原則","examples":[{"en":"Stoic principles were based on the pursuit of virtue.","zh":"斯多葛原則建基於追求美德。"},{"en":"Stoic principles are the core beliefs and rules of Stoic philosophy.","zh":"斯多葛原則是斯多葛哲學的核心信念和規則。"},{"en":"A Stoic principle is to focus on what you can control.","zh":"一項斯多葛原則是專注於你能控制的事。"},{"en":"These principles aim to help people live calmly and morally.","zh":"這些原則旨在幫助人冷靜而有道德地生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the guiding ideas of Stoicism.","zh":"這個短語描述斯多葛主義的指導思想。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"建基於……","examples":[{"en":"Stoic principles were based on the idea of unshakable happiness.","zh":"斯多葛原則建基於不可動搖的幸福這個想法。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to be built from that idea, fact or foundation.","zh":"建基於某事意思是建立在該想法、事實或基礎之上。"},{"en":"A good argument should be based on evidence, not only emotion.","zh":"好論點應建基於證據，而不只是情緒。"},{"en":"Stoic practice is based on self-control and virtue.","zh":"斯多葛實踐建基於自我控制和美德。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the foundation of an idea.","zh":"這個短語解釋想法的基礎。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"followers","meaning":"追隨者","examples":[{"en":"Followers of Stoicism aimed to achieve unshakable happiness.","zh":"斯多葛主義的追隨者旨在實現不可動搖的幸福。"},{"en":"Followers are people who accept, practise or support a belief or teacher.","zh":"追隨者是接受、實踐或支持某種信念或老師的人。"},{"en":"Followers of a philosophy try to live according to its principles.","zh":"哲學的追隨者會嘗試按照其原則生活。"},{"en":"Stoic followers valued discipline, reason and virtue.","zh":"斯多葛追隨者重視自律、理性和美德。"},{"en":"This word describes people who follow a set of ideas.","zh":"這個詞描述跟從一套思想的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"unshakable happiness","meaning":"不可動搖的幸福","examples":[{"en":"Stoics believed that people could have unshakable happiness in this life.","zh":"斯多葛派相信，人們在此生可以擁有不可動搖的幸福。"},{"en":"Unshakable happiness means happiness that cannot easily be destroyed by external events.","zh":"不可動搖的幸福意思是不容易被外在事件摧毀的幸福。"},{"en":"Stoics thought unshakable happiness came from virtue rather than luck.","zh":"斯多葛派認為不可動搖的幸福來自美德，而不是運氣。"},{"en":"A person with unshakable happiness stays steady even during difficulty.","zh":"擁有不可動搖幸福的人，即使遇到困難也能保持穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep inner stability.","zh":"這個短語描述深層內在穩定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in this life","meaning":"在此生","examples":[{"en":"Stoics believed happiness could be achieved in this life.","zh":"斯多葛派相信幸福可以在此生實現。"},{"en":"In this life means during one’s present human life, not after death.","zh":"在此生意思是在一個人現在的人生中，而不是死後。"},{"en":"The Stoics focused on how people should live well in this life.","zh":"斯多葛派專注於人應如何在此生好好生活。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses practical living rather than distant promises.","zh":"這個短語強調實際生活，而不是遙遠承諾。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing ethics and life goals.","zh":"當討論倫理和人生目標時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the key to achieving this","meaning":"實現這一點的關鍵","examples":[{"en":"The key to achieving unshakable happiness was virtue.","zh":"實現不可動搖幸福的關鍵是美德。"},{"en":"The key to achieving this means the most important thing needed to reach that goal.","zh":"實現這一點的關鍵意思是達到該目標最重要的東西。"},{"en":"The key to achieving confidence is regular practice.","zh":"實現信心的關鍵是定期練習。"},{"en":"Stoics believed the key to happiness lay in character, not wealth.","zh":"斯多葛派相信幸福的關鍵在於品格，而不是財富。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the central requirement for success.","zh":"這個短語引入成功的核心條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"virtue","meaning":"美德","examples":[{"en":"For Stoics, virtue was the key to happiness.","zh":"對斯多葛派來說，美德是幸福的關鍵。"},{"en":"Virtue means moral goodness, including wisdom, courage, justice and self-control.","zh":"美德意思是道德上的善，包括智慧、勇氣、公義和自我控制。"},{"en":"A virtuous person tries to act rightly even under pressure.","zh":"有美德的人即使在壓力下也嘗試做正確的事。"},{"en":"Stoics saw virtue as more important than pleasure, money or reputation.","zh":"斯多葛派認為美德比享樂、金錢或名聲更重要。"},{"en":"This word is central to ethical philosophy.","zh":"這個詞是倫理哲學的核心概念。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the road to","meaning":"通往……的道路","examples":[{"en":"The road to virtue lay in understanding our emotions.","zh":"通往美德的道路在於理解我們的情緒。"},{"en":"The road to something means the way or path to achieve it.","zh":"通往某事的道路意思是達成它的方法或路徑。"},{"en":"The road to confidence is often repeated practice and honest feedback.","zh":"通往信心的道路通常是反覆練習和誠實回饋。"},{"en":"Stoics believed the road to virtue began with self-knowledge.","zh":"斯多葛派相信通往美德的道路始於自我認識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a path toward a goal.","zh":"這個短語描述朝向目標的路徑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in turn","meaning":"反過來；繼而","examples":[{"en":"The road to virtue, in turn, lay in emotional self-control.","zh":"通往美德的道路，繼而在於情緒上的自我控制。"},{"en":"In turn means as the next step or result in a sequence.","zh":"反過來或繼而意思是作為下一步或連鎖結果。"},{"en":"Clear thinking improves decisions, which in turn improves behaviour.","zh":"清晰思考改善決定，而這繼而改善行為。"},{"en":"This phrase links one idea to the next in a chain of reasoning.","zh":"這個短語把一個想法與推理鏈中的下一個想法連起來。"},{"en":"It is useful in structured explanations.","zh":"它適合用於有結構的解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lie in","meaning":"在於……","examples":[{"en":"The road to virtue lies in understanding destructive emotions.","zh":"通往美德的道路在於理解破壞性情緒。"},{"en":"To lie in something means to be found in it or depend on it.","zh":"在於某事意思是存在於其中或取決於它。"},{"en":"The strength of Stoicism lies in its practical advice.","zh":"斯多葛主義的力量在於其實用建議。"},{"en":"The answer may lie in changing how we interpret events.","zh":"答案可能在於改變我們如何詮釋事件。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where the essential point is.","zh":"這個短語指出核心所在。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"destructive emotions","meaning":"破壞性情緒","examples":[{"en":"Stoics believed that destructive emotions are under our control.","zh":"斯多葛派相信破壞性情緒受我們控制。"},{"en":"Destructive emotions are feelings that can damage judgement, relationships or behaviour.","zh":"破壞性情緒是會損害判斷、人際關係或行為的感受。"},{"en":"Anger, jealousy and fear can become destructive emotions if they control our actions.","zh":"如果憤怒、妒忌和恐懼控制我們的行動，它們可以變成破壞性情緒。"},{"en":"Stoics tried to understand destructive emotions instead of being ruled by them.","zh":"斯多葛派嘗試理解破壞性情緒，而不是被它們支配。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harmful emotional states.","zh":"這個短語描述有害的情緒狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"anger and jealousy","meaning":"憤怒和妒忌","examples":[{"en":"Anger and jealousy are examples of destructive emotions.","zh":"憤怒和妒忌是破壞性情緒的例子。"},{"en":"Anger and jealousy are strong feelings that can affect how people judge situations.","zh":"憤怒和妒忌是強烈情緒，會影響人們如何判斷情況。"},{"en":"Anger may make someone speak harshly, while jealousy may make them resent others.","zh":"憤怒可能令人說話刻薄，而妒忌可能令人怨恨他人。"},{"en":"Stoicism teaches people to examine these emotions before acting.","zh":"斯多葛主義教人先審視這些情緒，然後才行動。"},{"en":"This phrase gives examples of emotions that can become harmful.","zh":"這個短語提供可能變得有害的情緒例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be under our conscious control","meaning":"受我們有意識控制","examples":[{"en":"Destructive emotions are under our conscious control.","zh":"破壞性情緒受我們有意識控制。"},{"en":"To be under our conscious control means to be something we can deliberately influence or manage.","zh":"受我們有意識控制意思是我們可以有意地影響或管理它。"},{"en":"Our first reaction may be automatic, but our response can be under conscious control.","zh":"我們的第一反應可能是自動的，但回應可以受有意識控制。"},{"en":"Stoics believed people could train their minds to respond more wisely.","zh":"斯多葛派相信人可以訓練心智，更明智地回應。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on deliberate self-management.","zh":"這個短語重點是有意識的自我管理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"control us","meaning":"控制我們","examples":[{"en":"Destructive emotions do not have to control us.","zh":"破壞性情緒不一定要控制我們。"},{"en":"If emotions control us, they strongly direct our actions and decisions.","zh":"如果情緒控制我們，它們就會強烈主導我們的行動和決定。"},{"en":"Fear can control us if we avoid every difficult challenge.","zh":"如果我們避開每個困難挑戰，恐懼就可能控制我們。"},{"en":"Stoicism teaches that we can notice emotions without obeying them blindly.","zh":"斯多葛主義教導我們可以察覺情緒，而不用盲目服從它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being ruled by feelings.","zh":"這個短語描述被感受支配。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"learn to control them","meaning":"學會控制它們","examples":[{"en":"We can learn to control destructive emotions.","zh":"我們可以學會控制破壞性情緒。"},{"en":"To learn to control them means to gradually develop the ability to manage those emotions.","zh":"學會控制它們意思是逐步培養管理那些情緒的能力。"},{"en":"People can learn to control anger by pausing before replying.","zh":"人們可以透過回應前先停一停，學會控制憤怒。"},{"en":"Emotional control takes practice and self-awareness.","zh":"情緒控制需要練習和自我覺察。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a skill that improves over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間改善的技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the words of","meaning":"用……的話來說","examples":[{"en":"In the words of Epictetus, external events cannot be controlled.","zh":"用 Epictetus 的話來說，外在事件不能被控制。"},{"en":"In the words of someone means using that person’s exact idea or expression.","zh":"用某人的話來說意思是使用那個人的原意或表達。"},{"en":"In the words of Marcus Aurelius, we should examine our own thoughts.","zh":"用 Marcus Aurelius 的話來說，我們應審視自己的思想。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a quotation or paraphrase from an important person.","zh":"這個短語引入重要人物的引語或意譯。"},{"en":"It is useful in speeches, essays and lectures.","zh":"它適合用於演講、文章和講座。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"external events","meaning":"外在事件","examples":[{"en":"External events are beyond our control.","zh":"外在事件超出我們控制。"},{"en":"External events are things that happen outside our minds or choices.","zh":"外在事件是在我們思想或選擇以外發生的事情。"},{"en":"Bad weather, other people’s opinions and sudden delays are external events.","zh":"壞天氣、別人的意見和突發延誤都是外在事件。"},{"en":"Stoics believed we should focus on our response rather than external events themselves.","zh":"斯多葛派相信我們應專注於自己的回應，而不是外在事件本身。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts outside circumstances with inner judgement.","zh":"這個短語把外在情況與內在判斷作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make choices with regard to","meaning":"就……作出選擇","examples":[{"en":"We can control the choices we make with regard to external events.","zh":"我們可以控制自己就外在事件所作出的選擇。"},{"en":"To make choices with regard to something means to decide how to respond concerning that matter.","zh":"就某事作出選擇意思是關於該事情決定如何回應。"},{"en":"We cannot control criticism, but we can make choices with regard to how we answer it.","zh":"我們不能控制批評，但可以就如何回應批評作出選擇。"},{"en":"Stoicism puts emphasis on choices, not uncontrollable circumstances.","zh":"斯多葛主義重視選擇，而不是不可控制的情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes decision-making in relation to a situation.","zh":"這個短語描述與某情況相關的決策。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"with regard to","meaning":"關於；就……而言","examples":[{"en":"People can choose how to respond with regard to external events.","zh":"關於外在事件，人們可以選擇如何回應。"},{"en":"With regard to means concerning or in relation to.","zh":"關於或就……而言意思是有關或與某事相關。"},{"en":"With regard to stress, Stoics advise us to examine our judgements.","zh":"就壓力而言，斯多葛派建議我們審視自己的判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than “about”.","zh":"這個短語比 “about” 更正式。"},{"en":"It is useful in essays, reports and formal discussion.","zh":"它適合用於文章、報告和正式討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"modern-day philosopher","meaning":"現代哲學家","examples":[{"en":"Nassim Nicholas Taleb is a modern-day philosopher and writer.","zh":"Nassim Nicholas Taleb 是一位現代哲學家和作家。"},{"en":"A modern-day philosopher is a thinker living in recent or present times.","zh":"現代哲學家是生活在近代或當代的思想家。"},{"en":"Modern-day philosophers often apply old ideas to current problems.","zh":"現代哲學家常把古老思想應用於當前問題。"},{"en":"Taleb’s writing connects philosophy with risk, uncertainty and resilience.","zh":"Taleb 的寫作把哲學與風險、不確定性和抗逆力連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts contemporary thinkers with ancient philosophers.","zh":"這個短語把當代思想家與古代哲學家作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"define someone as","meaning":"將某人定義為……","examples":[{"en":"Taleb defines a Stoic as someone with a different perspective.","zh":"Taleb 將斯多葛派人士定義為具有不同視角的人。"},{"en":"To define someone as something means to explain what kind of person they are.","zh":"將某人定義為某類人意思是解釋他們是哪種人。"},{"en":"A teacher may define a good learner as someone who asks questions and keeps practising.","zh":"老師可能將好學習者定義為會發問並持續練習的人。"},{"en":"Definitions help clarify how a speaker understands a concept.","zh":"定義有助澄清說話者如何理解概念。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a description or explanation of identity.","zh":"這個短語引入身份的描述或解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a different perspective on","meaning":"對……有不同看法","examples":[{"en":"A Stoic has a different perspective on negative experiences.","zh":"斯多葛派人士對負面經歷有不同看法。"},{"en":"A different perspective on something means a different way of seeing or understanding it.","zh":"對某事有不同看法意思是以不同方式看待或理解它。"},{"en":"Stoicism offers a different perspective on failure by treating it as training.","zh":"斯多葛主義把失敗視為訓練，提供對失敗的不同看法。"},{"en":"Changing perspective can change the emotional effect of an event.","zh":"改變視角可以改變事件帶來的情感效果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing interpretation.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論詮釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"see something as","meaning":"將某事視為……","examples":[{"en":"Most people see certain experiences as wholly negative.","zh":"大多數人將某些經歷視為完全負面。"},{"en":"To see something as something means to regard or interpret it in that way.","zh":"將某事視為某物意思是以那種方式看待或詮釋它。"},{"en":"A Stoic may see difficulty as an opportunity to practise courage.","zh":"斯多葛派人士可能將困難視為練習勇氣的機會。"},{"en":"How we see events can influence how we feel about them.","zh":"我們如何看待事件，可以影響我們對它們的感受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interpretation.","zh":"這個短語描述詮釋方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"wholly negative","meaning":"完全負面的","examples":[{"en":"Most people would see these experiences as wholly negative.","zh":"大多數人會把這些經歷視為完全負面。"},{"en":"Wholly negative means completely bad or harmful, with no positive side.","zh":"完全負面的意思是完全不好或有害，沒有正面一面。"},{"en":"Failure may seem wholly negative at first, but it can teach useful lessons.","zh":"失敗起初可能看似完全負面，但它可以教人有用教訓。"},{"en":"Stoics question whether an experience is truly wholly negative.","zh":"斯多葛派會質疑一段經歷是否真的完全負面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a completely negative judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述完全負面的判斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"transform fear into caution","meaning":"將恐懼轉化為謹慎","examples":[{"en":"A Stoic transforms fear into caution.","zh":"斯多葛派人士將恐懼轉化為謹慎。"},{"en":"To transform fear into caution means to turn fear into careful, sensible action.","zh":"將恐懼轉化為謹慎意思是把恐懼變成小心而理性的行動。"},{"en":"Fear before an exam can be transformed into caution by preparing early.","zh":"考試前的恐懼可以透過提早準備轉化為謹慎。"},{"en":"Stoics try to use emotions as material for wiser behaviour.","zh":"斯多葛派嘗試把情緒用作更明智行為的材料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing a negative feeling into a useful response.","zh":"這個短語描述把負面感受變成有用回應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pain into transformation","meaning":"將痛苦轉化為蛻變","examples":[{"en":"A Stoic transforms pain into transformation.","zh":"斯多葛派人士將痛苦轉化為蛻變。"},{"en":"To transform pain into transformation means to use suffering as a force for personal change.","zh":"將痛苦轉化為蛻變意思是把痛苦用作個人成長改變的力量。"},{"en":"A setback can become transformation if it teaches discipline and patience.","zh":"如果挫折教會人自律和耐性，它可以變成蛻變。"},{"en":"Stoicism does not deny pain; it asks what pain can teach us.","zh":"斯多葛主義不否認痛苦，而是問痛苦能教我們甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth through suffering.","zh":"這個短語描述透過痛苦成長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mistakes into initiation","meaning":"將錯誤轉化為開端","examples":[{"en":"A Stoic transforms mistakes into initiation.","zh":"斯多葛派人士將錯誤轉化為開端。"},{"en":"To transform mistakes into initiation means to treat mistakes as the beginning of learning or growth.","zh":"將錯誤轉化為開端意思是把錯誤視為學習或成長的開始。"},{"en":"A failed project can become an initiation into better planning.","zh":"失敗的項目可以成為更好規劃的開端。"},{"en":"Mistakes can introduce people to skills they still need to develop.","zh":"錯誤可以讓人看見自己仍需發展的技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using error as a starting point.","zh":"這個短語描述把錯誤用作起點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"desire into undertaking","meaning":"將欲望轉化為行動","examples":[{"en":"A Stoic transforms desire into undertaking.","zh":"斯多葛派人士將欲望轉化為行動。"},{"en":"To transform desire into undertaking means to turn wanting something into committed action.","zh":"將欲望轉化為行動意思是把想要某事變成承諾實行。"},{"en":"A desire to become healthier can become an undertaking to exercise regularly.","zh":"想變得更健康的欲望可以變成定期運動的行動承諾。"},{"en":"Stoicism values action guided by reason rather than empty wishing.","zh":"斯多葛主義重視由理性引導的行動，而不是空想。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning inner desire into practical effort.","zh":"這個短語描述把內在欲望變成實際努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"use something as a model","meaning":"以某物作為模型","examples":[{"en":"The speaker uses Taleb’s definition as a model.","zh":"講者以 Taleb 的定義作為模型。"},{"en":"To use something as a model means to use it as an example or guide.","zh":"以某物作為模型意思是把它用作例子或指引。"},{"en":"Students may use a strong essay as a model for their own writing.","zh":"學生可能以一篇優秀文章作為自己寫作的模型。"},{"en":"A model helps people understand what good practice looks like.","zh":"模型幫助人理解良好做法是怎樣的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning from an example.","zh":"這個短語描述從例子學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"throughout the centuries","meaning":"數個世紀以來","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism has been practised throughout the centuries.","zh":"數個世紀以來，斯多葛主義一直被實踐。"},{"en":"Throughout the centuries means during many centuries of history.","zh":"數個世紀以來意思是在許多世紀的歷史期間。"},{"en":"Stoic ideas have influenced different societies throughout the centuries.","zh":"斯多葛思想數個世紀以來影響不同社會。"},{"en":"A philosophy that lasts through centuries usually speaks to repeated human concerns.","zh":"能延續數個世紀的哲學通常回應反覆出現的人類關注。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises long historical continuity.","zh":"這個短語強調長期歷史延續。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in more recent history","meaning":"在較近代歷史中","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism has been practised in more recent history by many leaders.","zh":"在較近代歷史中，許多領袖也實踐斯多葛主義。"},{"en":"In more recent history means in a period closer to the present than ancient history.","zh":"在較近代歷史中意思是在比古代史更接近現在的時期。"},{"en":"In more recent history, Stoicism has influenced politicians, artists and entrepreneurs.","zh":"在較近代歷史中，斯多葛主義影響了政治家、藝術家和企業家。"},{"en":"This phrase helps move from ancient examples to modern ones.","zh":"這個短語幫助由古代例子轉到現代例子。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing different historical periods.","zh":"當比較不同歷史時期時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"entrepreneurs","meaning":"企業家","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism has been practised by kings, artists, writers and entrepreneurs.","zh":"斯多葛主義由國王、藝術家、作家和企業家實踐。"},{"en":"Entrepreneurs are people who start or run businesses, often taking financial risks.","zh":"企業家是創立或經營企業的人，通常會承擔財務風險。"},{"en":"Entrepreneurs may use Stoic ideas to stay calm during failure or uncertainty.","zh":"企業家可能運用斯多葛思想，在失敗或不確定中保持冷靜。"},{"en":"Business founders often need resilience, judgement and discipline.","zh":"創業者通常需要抗逆力、判斷力和自律。"},{"en":"This word is common in business and innovation contexts.","zh":"這個詞常見於商業和創新語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"founding fathers","meaning":"開國元勳","examples":[{"en":"The founding fathers of the United States were inspired by Stoicism.","zh":"美國開國元勳受到斯多葛主義啟發。"},{"en":"Founding fathers are the early political leaders who helped establish a country or institution.","zh":"開國元勳是幫助建立一個國家或機構的早期政治領袖。"},{"en":"The founding fathers of the United States helped shape its early political principles.","zh":"美國開國元勳幫助塑造美國早期政治原則。"},{"en":"The phrase often refers to important national founders.","zh":"這個短語常指重要的國家創建者。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in historical and political discussion.","zh":"它常見於歷史和政治討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be inspired by","meaning":"受到……啟發","examples":[{"en":"The founding fathers were inspired by Stoic philosophy.","zh":"開國元勳受到斯多葛哲學啟發。"},{"en":"To be inspired by something means to be influenced or encouraged by it.","zh":"受到某事啟發意思是受它影響或鼓舞。"},{"en":"A leader may be inspired by ancient texts when facing difficult decisions.","zh":"領袖面對困難決定時，可能受到古代文本啟發。"},{"en":"Inspiration can come from books, people, events or ideas.","zh":"靈感可以來自書籍、人物、事件或思想。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive influence.","zh":"這個短語描述正面影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be introduced to","meaning":"被介紹接觸……","examples":[{"en":"George Washington was introduced to Stoicism at age seventeen.","zh":"George Washington 在 17 歲時被介紹接觸斯多葛主義。"},{"en":"To be introduced to something means to first learn about or encounter it.","zh":"被介紹接觸某事意思是首次認識或接觸它。"},{"en":"A student may be introduced to philosophy through a short story or quote.","zh":"學生可能透過短故事或引言首次接觸哲學。"},{"en":"Early exposure to an idea can influence a person for life.","zh":"早期接觸一個思想可以影響一個人的一生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes first contact with a subject.","zh":"這個短語描述與某主題的首次接觸。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at age seventeen","meaning":"在17歲時","examples":[{"en":"Washington was introduced to Stoicism at age seventeen.","zh":"Washington 在 17 歲時接觸斯多葛主義。"},{"en":"At age seventeen means when someone was seventeen years old.","zh":"在 17 歲時意思是某人十七歲的時候。"},{"en":"At age seventeen, many students begin thinking seriously about their future.","zh":"在 17 歲時，許多學生開始認真思考自己的未來。"},{"en":"Learning an idea at a young age can shape later values.","zh":"年輕時學到一個思想，可以塑造之後的價值觀。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the age when something happened.","zh":"這個短語提供事件發生時的年齡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put on a play","meaning":"上演一齣戲","examples":[{"en":"Washington later put on a play based on the life of Cato.","zh":"Washington 後來上演一齣以 Cato 生平為基礎的戲。"},{"en":"To put on a play means to organise and perform a theatre production.","zh":"上演一齣戲意思是組織並演出一個劇場製作。"},{"en":"A school may put on a play to teach students history through drama.","zh":"學校可能上演一齣戲，透過戲劇教授歷史。"},{"en":"Leaders can use theatre to inspire or educate an audience.","zh":"領袖可以利用戲劇激勵或教育觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes staging a performance.","zh":"這個短語描述舞台演出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"based on the life of","meaning":"以……的生平為基礎","examples":[{"en":"The play was based on the life of Cato.","zh":"這齣戲以 Cato 的生平為基礎。"},{"en":"Based on the life of someone means inspired by or telling events from that person’s life.","zh":"以某人的生平為基礎意思是受那人的人生啟發，或講述其人生事件。"},{"en":"A film based on the life of a scientist may show their struggles and discoveries.","zh":"以科學家生平為基礎的電影可能展示其掙扎和發現。"},{"en":"Stories based on real lives can inspire audiences strongly.","zh":"基於真實人生的故事可以強烈激勵觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a work with a historical person’s life.","zh":"這個短語把作品與歷史人物人生連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"inspire his men","meaning":"激勵他的部下","examples":[{"en":"Washington used the play to inspire his men.","zh":"Washington 用這齣戲激勵他的部下。"},{"en":"To inspire his men means to encourage and strengthen the spirit of the people under his leadership.","zh":"激勵他的部下意思是鼓舞並強化他所領導的人之士氣。"},{"en":"A general may inspire his men by reminding them of courage and duty.","zh":"將軍可以透過提醒士兵勇氣和責任來激勵部下。"},{"en":"Stories of virtue can inspire people during hardship.","zh":"美德故事可以在困難中激勵人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes motivating followers or soldiers.","zh":"這個短語描述鼓勵追隨者或士兵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"keep a copy of","meaning":"保存一本……","examples":[{"en":"Thomas Jefferson kept a copy of Seneca beside his bed.","zh":"Thomas Jefferson 在床邊保存一本 Seneca 的著作。"},{"en":"To keep a copy of a book means to own or store one version of it.","zh":"保存一本書意思是擁有或存放該書的一個版本。"},{"en":"A student may keep a copy of a favourite poem in their notebook.","zh":"學生可能在筆記簿裏保存一首最喜歡的詩。"},{"en":"Keeping a book nearby suggests it is important or often read.","zh":"把書放在附近暗示它很重要或經常被閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes possessing a text for use or reference.","zh":"這個短語描述擁有文本以供使用或參考。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"beside his bed","meaning":"在床邊","examples":[{"en":"Jefferson kept Seneca beside his bed.","zh":"Jefferson 把 Seneca 的著作放在床邊。"},{"en":"Beside his bed means next to his bed.","zh":"在床邊意思是在床旁邊。"},{"en":"People often keep important books beside their bed to read at night.","zh":"人們常把重要書籍放在床邊，以便晚上閱讀。"},{"en":"A book beside someone’s bed may show what they return to often.","zh":"放在床邊的書可能顯示某人經常重讀甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a nearby physical location.","zh":"這個短語描述附近的實體位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"renowned French Romantic artist","meaning":"著名法國浪漫主義藝術家","examples":[{"en":"Eugène Delacroix was a renowned French Romantic artist.","zh":"Eugène Delacroix 是著名法國浪漫主義藝術家。"},{"en":"A renowned French Romantic artist is a famous French artist connected with the Romantic movement.","zh":"著名法國浪漫主義藝術家是與浪漫主義運動有關的知名法國藝術家。"},{"en":"Romantic artists often emphasised emotion, drama and imagination.","zh":"浪漫主義藝術家常強調情感、戲劇性和想像力。"},{"en":"Delacroix is remembered as one of the major painters of French Romanticism.","zh":"Delacroix 被記住為法國浪漫主義主要畫家之一。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies fame, nationality and artistic movement.","zh":"這個短語指出名氣、國籍和藝術運動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"known best for","meaning":"最為人熟悉的是……","examples":[{"en":"Delacroix is known best for his painting Liberty Leading the People.","zh":"Delacroix 最為人熟悉的是他的畫作《自由引導人民》。"},{"en":"Known best for means most famous because of a particular work or achievement.","zh":"最為人熟悉的是某事，意思是因某作品或成就而最有名。"},{"en":"Shakespeare is known best for plays such as Hamlet and Romeo and Juliet.","zh":"Shakespeare 最為人熟悉的是《哈姆雷特》和《羅密歐與茱麗葉》等劇作。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the work people most strongly associate with someone.","zh":"這個短語引入人們最常與某人聯想在一起的作品。"},{"en":"It is useful in biographies.","zh":"它適合用於人物簡介。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Liberty Leading the People","meaning":"《自由引導人民》","examples":[{"en":"Delacroix is known best for Liberty Leading the People.","zh":"Delacroix 最為人熟悉的是《自由引導人民》。"},{"en":"Liberty Leading the People is a famous painting by Eugène Delacroix.","zh":"《自由引導人民》是 Eugène Delacroix 的著名畫作。"},{"en":"The painting is often associated with revolution, freedom and national struggle.","zh":"這幅畫常與革命、自由和民族抗爭聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Mentioning this work helps identify Delacroix quickly.","zh":"提到這幅作品有助快速識別 Delacroix。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major artwork.","zh":"這個短語命名一件重要藝術作品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ardent Stoic","meaning":"熱切的斯多葛派人士","examples":[{"en":"Delacroix was an ardent Stoic.","zh":"Delacroix 是熱切的斯多葛派人士。"},{"en":"An ardent Stoic is a passionate or devoted follower of Stoic ideas.","zh":"熱切的斯多葛派人士是熱情或忠誠跟隨斯多葛思想的人。"},{"en":"An ardent Stoic may turn to Stoic texts during emotional difficulty.","zh":"熱切的斯多葛派人士可能在情緒困難時求助於斯多葛文本。"},{"en":"The word ardent suggests strong commitment rather than casual interest.","zh":"ardent 這個詞暗示強烈投入，而不是隨便感興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep enthusiasm for Stoicism.","zh":"這個短語描述對斯多葛主義的深厚熱情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"refer to something as","meaning":"將某物稱為……","examples":[{"en":"Delacroix referred to Stoicism as his consoling religion.","zh":"Delacroix 將斯多葛主義稱為他的給予安慰的宗教。"},{"en":"To refer to something as something means to call or describe it in that way.","zh":"將某物稱為某事意思是以那種方式稱呼或描述它。"},{"en":"Some readers refer to Stoicism as a practical guide to life.","zh":"有些讀者將斯多葛主義稱為實用人生指南。"},{"en":"What people call something often reveals how they value it.","zh":"人們如何稱呼某物，常顯示他們如何看待其價值。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a description or label.","zh":"這個短語引入描述或標籤。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"consoling religion","meaning":"給予安慰的宗教","examples":[{"en":"Delacroix called Stoicism his consoling religion.","zh":"Delacroix 稱斯多葛主義為他的給予安慰的宗教。"},{"en":"A consoling religion is a belief system that gives comfort during suffering or uncertainty.","zh":"給予安慰的宗教是在人受苦或不確定時提供安慰的信念體系。"},{"en":"Delacroix’s phrase suggests Stoicism helped him feel steadier in life.","zh":"Delacroix 的說法暗示斯多葛主義幫助他在人生中更穩定。"},{"en":"Consoling ideas can help people endure pain or disappointment.","zh":"給予安慰的思想可以幫助人承受痛苦或失望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a source of emotional comfort.","zh":"這個短語描述情感安慰來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"theories on capitalism","meaning":"關於資本主義的理論","examples":[{"en":"Adam Smith’s theories on capitalism were influenced by Stoicism.","zh":"Adam Smith 關於資本主義的理論受到斯多葛主義影響。"},{"en":"Theories on capitalism are ideas explaining how capitalist economies work.","zh":"關於資本主義的理論是解釋資本主義經濟如何運作的想法。"},{"en":"A lecture on economics may discuss Smith’s theories on capitalism and markets.","zh":"經濟學講座可能討論 Smith 關於資本主義和市場的理論。"},{"en":"Philosophical ideas can influence economic theories about human behaviour.","zh":"哲學思想可以影響關於人類行為的經濟理論。"},{"en":"This phrase connects economic thought with a specific topic.","zh":"這個短語把經濟思想與特定主題連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be significantly influenced by","meaning":"深受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Adam Smith’s theories were significantly influenced by Stoicism.","zh":"Adam Smith 的理論深受斯多葛主義影響。"},{"en":"To be significantly influenced by something means to be strongly shaped or affected by it.","zh":"深受某事影響意思是被它強烈塑造或影響。"},{"en":"A writer’s style may be significantly influenced by the books they read as a child.","zh":"作家的風格可能深受童年閱讀書籍影響。"},{"en":"Major influences can shape the direction of a thinker’s work.","zh":"重大影響可以塑造思想家作品的方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong intellectual impact.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈的思想影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as a schoolboy","meaning":"在學生時代","examples":[{"en":"Adam Smith studied Stoicism as a schoolboy.","zh":"Adam Smith 在學生時代學習斯多葛主義。"},{"en":"As a schoolboy means when he was a male student at school.","zh":"在學生時代意思是他還是男學生的時候。"},{"en":"As a schoolboy, Smith was introduced to classical texts.","zh":"在學生時代，Smith 接觸到古典文本。"},{"en":"Ideas learned in youth can influence adult thinking.","zh":"年輕時學到的思想可以影響成年後的思考。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the stage of life when something happened.","zh":"這個短語交代事情發生的人生階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"translate someone’s works","meaning":"翻譯某人的著作","examples":[{"en":"Smith’s teacher had translated Marcus Aurelius’ works.","zh":"Smith 的老師曾翻譯 Marcus Aurelius 的著作。"},{"en":"To translate someone’s works means to change that person’s writings into another language.","zh":"翻譯某人的著作意思是把那人的作品轉換成另一種語言。"},{"en":"Translating ancient works allows new readers to access old ideas.","zh":"翻譯古代著作讓新讀者能接觸舊思想。"},{"en":"A teacher who translates texts can shape how students understand them.","zh":"翻譯文本的老師可以塑造學生如何理解它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes language transfer of writings.","zh":"這個短語描述文字的語言轉換。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"political leaders","meaning":"政治領袖","examples":[{"en":"Today’s political leaders are also inspired by ancient texts.","zh":"今天的政治領袖也受到古代文本啟發。"},{"en":"Political leaders are people who lead governments, parties or public institutions.","zh":"政治領袖是領導政府、政黨或公共機構的人。"},{"en":"Political leaders often need guidance on judgement, responsibility and pressure.","zh":"政治領袖常需要關於判斷、責任和壓力的指引。"},{"en":"Ancient philosophy can appeal to leaders because it discusses power and self-control.","zh":"古代哲學可能吸引領袖，因為它討論權力和自我控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes leaders in public life.","zh":"這個短語描述公共生活中的領導者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be no different","meaning":"也不例外","examples":[{"en":"Today’s political leaders are no different.","zh":"今天的政治領袖也不例外。"},{"en":"To be no different means to be the same in this respect.","zh":"也不例外意思是在這方面同樣如此。"},{"en":"Ancient rulers sought wisdom from books, and modern leaders are no different.","zh":"古代統治者從書中尋求智慧，現代領袖也不例外。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the same pattern applies to another group.","zh":"這個短語顯示同一模式也適用於另一群體。"},{"en":"It is useful when connecting past and present examples.","zh":"當連接過去與現在例子時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"find inspiration from","meaning":"從……找到靈感","examples":[{"en":"Many leaders find inspiration from ancient texts.","zh":"許多領袖從古代文本找到靈感。"},{"en":"To find inspiration from something means to gain ideas, courage or motivation from it.","zh":"從某事找到靈感意思是從中獲得想法、勇氣或動力。"},{"en":"A student may find inspiration from a biography of a great thinker.","zh":"學生可能從偉大思想家的傳記中找到靈感。"},{"en":"Ancient texts can inspire people because they deal with lasting human problems.","zh":"古代文本可以啟發人，因為它們處理持久的人類問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gaining motivation or insight.","zh":"這個短語描述獲得動力或見解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ancient texts","meaning":"古代文本","examples":[{"en":"Many political leaders read ancient texts for inspiration.","zh":"許多政治領袖閱讀古代文本以尋找靈感。"},{"en":"Ancient texts are writings from the ancient world.","zh":"古代文本是來自古代世界的文字作品。"},{"en":"Ancient texts may include philosophy, history, poetry and religious works.","zh":"古代文本可以包括哲學、歷史、詩歌和宗教作品。"},{"en":"Reading ancient texts can connect modern readers with older wisdom.","zh":"閱讀古代文本可以把現代讀者與古老智慧連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to old written sources.","zh":"這個短語指古老書面來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"former US president","meaning":"美國前總統","examples":[{"en":"Former US president Bill Clinton rereads Marcus Aurelius every year.","zh":"美國前總統 Bill Clinton 每年重讀 Marcus Aurelius。"},{"en":"A former US president is someone who previously served as president of the United States.","zh":"美國前總統是曾經擔任美國總統的人。"},{"en":"Former presidents often remain influential after leaving office.","zh":"前總統離任後通常仍具影響力。"},{"en":"Mentioning a former US president shows that ancient philosophy can appeal to modern leaders.","zh":"提到美國前總統顯示古代哲學可以吸引現代領袖。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a past political office-holder.","zh":"這個短語指出過去的政治職位持有人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"every single year","meaning":"每一年","examples":[{"en":"Bill Clinton rereads Marcus Aurelius every single year.","zh":"Bill Clinton 每一年都重讀 Marcus Aurelius。"},{"en":"Every single year means each year without exception.","zh":"每一年意思是每一個年份都如此，沒有例外。"},{"en":"A reader may return to the same book every single year for guidance.","zh":"讀者可能每一年都重讀同一本書，以尋找指引。"},{"en":"The phrase adds emphasis to regular repetition.","zh":"這個短語強調規律重複。"},{"en":"It suggests a strong habit or lasting value.","zh":"它暗示強烈習慣或持久價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"compare A to B","meaning":"將A比作B","examples":[{"en":"Many have compared Obama’s leadership style to that of Cato.","zh":"許多人將 Obama 的領導風格比作 Cato 的領導風格。"},{"en":"To compare A to B means to say A is similar to B in some way.","zh":"將 A 比作 B 意思是說 A 在某方面與 B 相似。"},{"en":"A writer may compare a modern leader to an ancient statesman.","zh":"作者可能將現代領袖比作古代政治家。"},{"en":"Comparisons help readers understand qualities through familiar examples.","zh":"比較有助讀者透過熟悉例子理解特質。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing similarity.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論相似性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"calm leadership style","meaning":"冷靜的領導風格","examples":[{"en":"Obama’s calm leadership style has been compared to Cato’s.","zh":"Obama 冷靜的領導風格曾被比作 Cato 的風格。"},{"en":"A calm leadership style means leading with composure, steadiness and control.","zh":"冷靜的領導風格意思是以沉着、穩定和自制方式領導。"},{"en":"A calm leader can make better decisions during crisis.","zh":"冷靜的領袖在危機中能作出較好決定。"},{"en":"Stoic influence is often associated with controlled emotion and clear judgement.","zh":"斯多葛影響常與情緒控制和清晰判斷聯繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a steady way of leading.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定的領導方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"former prime minister","meaning":"前總理","examples":[{"en":"Wen Jiabao is the former prime minister of China.","zh":"Wen Jiabao 是中國前總理。"},{"en":"A former prime minister is someone who previously served as a country’s prime minister.","zh":"前總理是曾經擔任一國總理的人。"},{"en":"Former prime ministers may continue to influence public discussion after leaving office.","zh":"前總理離任後可能仍影響公共討論。"},{"en":"Mentioning political figures shows the modern reach of ancient ideas.","zh":"提到政治人物顯示古代思想的現代影響範圍。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a past government leader.","zh":"這個短語指出過去的政府領袖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"claim that","meaning":"聲稱","examples":[{"en":"Wen Jiabao claims that Meditations is one of two books he travels with.","zh":"Wen Jiabao 聲稱《沉思錄》是他旅行時隨身帶着的兩本書之一。"},{"en":"To claim that something is true means to state it as a fact or belief.","zh":"聲稱某事為真意思是把它作為事實或信念陳述。"},{"en":"The author claims that Stoicism can help people face uncertainty.","zh":"作者聲稱斯多葛主義可以幫助人面對不確定性。"},{"en":"Claims should be supported by evidence when accuracy matters.","zh":"當準確性重要時，聲稱應有證據支持。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces someone’s statement.","zh":"這個短語引入某人的說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"travel with","meaning":"旅行時隨身帶着","examples":[{"en":"Wen Jiabao travels with a copy of Meditations.","zh":"Wen Jiabao 旅行時隨身帶着一本《沉思錄》。"},{"en":"To travel with something means to carry it while travelling.","zh":"旅行時隨身帶着某物意思是在旅途中攜帶它。"},{"en":"Some people travel with a favourite book for comfort and reflection.","zh":"有些人旅行時隨身帶着一本喜歡的書，以獲得安慰和反思。"},{"en":"Carrying a book while travelling suggests it has personal importance.","zh":"旅行時攜帶一本書，暗示它有個人重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking something on journeys.","zh":"這個短語描述在旅程中帶着某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"over the course of","meaning":"在……期間","examples":[{"en":"Wen Jiabao has read Meditations many times over the course of his life.","zh":"Wen Jiabao 在他一生期間多次閱讀《沉思錄》。"},{"en":"Over the course of means during the whole period of something.","zh":"在……期間意思是在某整段時間之中。"},{"en":"Over the course of a career, a leader may return to the same ideas many times.","zh":"在整個職業生涯期間，領袖可能多次回到同一套思想。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises development or repetition across time.","zh":"這個短語強調隨時間發展或重複。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing long-term patterns.","zh":"它適合用於描述長期模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have a profound influence on","meaning":"對……有深遠影響","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism had a profound influence on Albert Ellis.","zh":"斯多葛主義對 Albert Ellis 有深遠影響。"},{"en":"To have a profound influence on someone means to affect them deeply and significantly.","zh":"對某人有深遠影響意思是深刻而重大地影響他。"},{"en":"A book can have a profound influence on the way a person thinks.","zh":"一本書可以對一個人的思考方式有深遠影響。"},{"en":"Stoic ideas influenced Ellis’s view of thoughts, emotions and behaviour.","zh":"斯多葛思想影響 Ellis 對思想、情緒和行為的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep impact.","zh":"這個短語描述深層影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Cognitive Behaviour Therapy","meaning":"認知行為治療","examples":[{"en":"Albert Ellis invented Cognitive Behaviour Therapy.","zh":"Albert Ellis 發明了認知行為治療。"},{"en":"Cognitive Behaviour Therapy is a form of therapy that focuses on how thoughts affect feelings and behaviour.","zh":"認知行為治療是一種治療方法，重點是思想如何影響感受和行為。"},{"en":"CBT helps people identify unhelpful thinking patterns and respond differently.","zh":"認知行為治療幫助人識別無益思維模式，並以不同方式回應。"},{"en":"Its connection with Stoicism lies in examining beliefs and judgements.","zh":"它與斯多葛主義的聯繫在於審視信念和判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase names an important modern psychological treatment.","zh":"這個短語命名一種重要現代心理治療。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be used to help","meaning":"被用來幫助……","examples":[{"en":"Cognitive Behaviour Therapy is used to help people manage their problems.","zh":"認知行為治療被用來幫助人處理自己的問題。"},{"en":"To be used to help means to serve the purpose of supporting someone.","zh":"被用來幫助意思是用於支援某人的目的。"},{"en":"Breathing exercises can be used to help people calm down before speaking.","zh":"呼吸練習可以被用來幫助人在說話前冷靜下來。"},{"en":"A method is valuable when it is used to help people in practical ways.","zh":"當一種方法被用來以實際方式幫助人，它就有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase explains purpose.","zh":"這個短語解釋用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"manage their problems","meaning":"處理自己的問題","examples":[{"en":"Cognitive Behaviour Therapy helps people manage their problems.","zh":"認知行為治療幫助人處理自己的問題。"},{"en":"To manage their problems means to deal with difficulties in a more controlled and effective way.","zh":"處理自己的問題意思是以較受控和有效的方式應對困難。"},{"en":"People may manage anxiety by changing thoughts and practising coping skills.","zh":"人們可以透過改變想法和練習應對技巧來處理焦慮。"},{"en":"Managing problems does not always mean removing them completely.","zh":"處理問題不一定代表完全移除問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical handling of difficulties.","zh":"這個短語描述實際應對困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the way that they think and behave","meaning":"他們思考和行為的方式","examples":[{"en":"The therapy changes the way that people think and behave.","zh":"這種治療改變人們思考和行為的方式。"},{"en":"The way that they think and behave means their patterns of thought and action.","zh":"他們思考和行為的方式意思是他們的思想和行動模式。"},{"en":"Therapy may help people notice the way they think and behave under stress.","zh":"治療可能幫助人注意自己在壓力下思考和行為的方式。"},{"en":"Changing thought patterns can change behaviour over time.","zh":"改變思維模式可以隨時間改變行為。"},{"en":"This phrase connects mind and action.","zh":"這個短語把思想和行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be commonly used to","meaning":"常被用來……","examples":[{"en":"Cognitive Behaviour Therapy is commonly used to treat depression.","zh":"認知行為治療常被用來治療抑鬱症。"},{"en":"To be commonly used to do something means to be often used for that purpose.","zh":"常被用來做某事意思是經常被用於該目的。"},{"en":"Breathing techniques are commonly used to reduce stress.","zh":"呼吸技巧常被用來減輕壓力。"},{"en":"A method commonly used by professionals is usually well known in that field.","zh":"專業人士常用的方法通常在該領域中廣為人知。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequent use.","zh":"這個短語描述頻繁使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"treat depression","meaning":"治療抑鬱症","examples":[{"en":"Cognitive Behaviour Therapy is used to treat depression.","zh":"認知行為治療被用來治療抑鬱症。"},{"en":"To treat depression means to help reduce or manage symptoms of depression through therapy, medicine or support.","zh":"治療抑鬱症意思是透過治療、藥物或支援幫助減輕或管理抑鬱症狀。"},{"en":"A therapist may use CBT to treat depression by challenging negative thinking patterns.","zh":"治療師可能透過挑戰負面思維模式，使用認知行為治療治療抑鬱症。"},{"en":"Treatment aims to improve mood, functioning and quality of life.","zh":"治療目標是改善情緒、功能和生活質素。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to mental health and medical contexts.","zh":"這個短語屬於心理健康和醫療語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take control of our lives","meaning":"掌控自己的人生","examples":[{"en":"We can take control of our lives by challenging irrational beliefs.","zh":"我們可以透過挑戰非理性信念來掌控自己的人生。"},{"en":"To take control of our lives means to act more deliberately and responsibly instead of feeling helpless.","zh":"掌控自己的人生意思是更有意識和更負責任地行動，而不是感到無助。"},{"en":"People take control of their lives when they change habits that harm them.","zh":"當人們改變傷害自己的習慣時，就是在掌控自己的人生。"},{"en":"Stoic thinking encourages people to control their choices and judgements.","zh":"斯多葛思想鼓勵人控制自己的選擇和判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal agency.","zh":"這個短語描述個人自主性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"challenge irrational beliefs","meaning":"挑戰非理性信念","examples":[{"en":"Cognitive Behaviour Therapy challenges irrational beliefs.","zh":"認知行為治療挑戰非理性信念。"},{"en":"To challenge irrational beliefs means to question thoughts that are unreasonable or unsupported by evidence.","zh":"挑戰非理性信念意思是質疑不合理或沒有證據支持的想法。"},{"en":"A person may challenge the belief that one mistake means total failure.","zh":"一個人可能挑戰「一次錯誤就代表完全失敗」這個信念。"},{"en":"Challenging irrational beliefs can reduce emotional suffering.","zh":"挑戰非理性信念可以減少情緒痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to CBT and Stoic-style self-examination.","zh":"這個短語是認知行為治療和斯多葛式自我審視的核心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"create faulty thinking","meaning":"造成錯誤思維","examples":[{"en":"Irrational beliefs can create faulty thinking.","zh":"非理性信念可以造成錯誤思維。"},{"en":"To create faulty thinking means to produce mistaken or distorted patterns of thought.","zh":"造成錯誤思維意思是產生錯誤或扭曲的思考模式。"},{"en":"Believing that everyone must like you can create faulty thinking.","zh":"相信每個人都必須喜歡你，可以造成錯誤思維。"},{"en":"Faulty thinking may make problems feel worse than they are.","zh":"錯誤思維可能令問題感覺比實際更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how wrong beliefs shape the mind.","zh":"這個短語描述錯誤信念如何塑造思想。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"symptoms and behaviours","meaning":"症狀和行為","examples":[{"en":"Faulty thinking can create symptoms and behaviours.","zh":"錯誤思維可以造成症狀和行為。"},{"en":"Symptoms and behaviours are signs of a problem and the actions connected with it.","zh":"症狀和行為是問題的徵象，以及與它相關的行動。"},{"en":"Anxiety symptoms and avoidance behaviours may appear together.","zh":"焦慮症狀和逃避行為可能同時出現。"},{"en":"Changing thoughts can sometimes reduce unhelpful symptoms and behaviours.","zh":"改變思想有時可以減少無益的症狀和行為。"},{"en":"This phrase connects mental patterns with visible effects.","zh":"這個短語把心理模式與可見效果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"use logic instead","meaning":"改用邏輯","examples":[{"en":"People can challenge irrational beliefs by using logic instead.","zh":"人們可以透過改用邏輯來挑戰非理性信念。"},{"en":"To use logic instead means to replace emotional or mistaken thinking with reasoned thinking.","zh":"改用邏輯意思是以理性思考取代情緒化或錯誤思維。"},{"en":"Instead of assuming failure, a student can use logic and examine the evidence.","zh":"學生可以不再假設自己會失敗，而是改用邏輯檢視證據。"},{"en":"Logic can help people test whether their thoughts are true or exaggerated.","zh":"邏輯可以幫助人測試自己的想法是真的還是誇大了。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rational alternative.","zh":"這個短語描述理性的替代方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"become popular in","meaning":"在……變得流行","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism has become popular in the world of business.","zh":"斯多葛主義在商業世界變得流行。"},{"en":"To become popular in a field means to be widely liked, used or discussed there.","zh":"在某領域變得流行意思是在那裏被廣泛喜歡、使用或討論。"},{"en":"Mindfulness has become popular in schools and workplaces.","zh":"正念在學校和工作場所變得流行。"},{"en":"Stoicism became popular in business because it speaks to risk and pressure.","zh":"斯多葛主義在商業中流行，因為它回應風險和壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growing acceptance in a particular area.","zh":"這個短語描述在特定領域中越來越被接受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the world of business","meaning":"商業世界","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism has become popular in the world of business.","zh":"斯多葛主義在商業世界變得流行。"},{"en":"The world of business means the area of companies, markets, entrepreneurs and commercial activity.","zh":"商業世界意思是公司、市場、企業家和商業活動的領域。"},{"en":"The world of business often values resilience, leadership and clear decision-making.","zh":"商業世界通常重視抗逆力、領導力和清晰決策。"},{"en":"Stoic ideas can appeal to businesspeople facing uncertainty.","zh":"斯多葛思想可以吸引面對不確定性的商界人士。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the business sphere.","zh":"這個短語描述商業領域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"build resilience","meaning":"建立抗逆力","examples":[{"en":"Stoic principles can build resilience.","zh":"斯多葛原則可以建立抗逆力。"},{"en":"To build resilience means to develop the ability to recover from difficulty.","zh":"建立抗逆力意思是培養從困難中恢復的能力。"},{"en":"Facing small challenges calmly can build resilience over time.","zh":"冷靜面對小挑戰可以隨時間建立抗逆力。"},{"en":"Stoicism builds resilience by training people to accept what they cannot control.","zh":"斯多葛主義透過訓練人接受不能控制的事來建立抗逆力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strengthening mental endurance.","zh":"這個短語描述加強心理承受力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"state of mind","meaning":"心態","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism can build the state of mind required to overcome setbacks.","zh":"斯多葛主義可以建立克服挫折所需的心態。"},{"en":"State of mind means a person’s mental attitude or emotional condition.","zh":"心態意思是一個人的精神態度或情緒狀態。"},{"en":"A calm state of mind helps people make better decisions under pressure.","zh":"冷靜心態幫助人在壓力下作出更好決定。"},{"en":"Stoic practice aims to create a steady state of mind.","zh":"斯多葛實踐旨在建立穩定心態。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inner mental condition.","zh":"這個短語描述內在心理狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"required to","meaning":"……所需的","examples":[{"en":"Resilience is required to overcome setbacks.","zh":"抗逆力是克服挫折所需的。"},{"en":"Required to means needed in order to do something.","zh":"……所需的意思是為了做某事而需要的。"},{"en":"Patience is required to master a difficult skill.","zh":"掌握困難技能需要耐性。"},{"en":"In business, resilience is required to survive repeated failure.","zh":"在商業中，抗逆力是承受反覆失敗所需的。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a necessary quality or condition.","zh":"這個短語指出必要特質或條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"overcome setbacks","meaning":"克服挫折","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism teaches people how to overcome setbacks.","zh":"斯多葛主義教人如何克服挫折。"},{"en":"To overcome setbacks means to recover from difficulties, failures or delays.","zh":"克服挫折意思是從困難、失敗或延誤中恢復過來。"},{"en":"An entrepreneur must overcome setbacks when a product does not sell well.","zh":"當產品銷售不佳，企業家必須克服挫折。"},{"en":"Stoics see setbacks as opportunities to practise strength and judgement.","zh":"斯多葛派把挫折視為練習力量和判斷的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dealing successfully with difficulties.","zh":"這個短語描述成功應對困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"turn obstacles into opportunity","meaning":"將障礙轉化為機會","examples":[{"en":"Stoics teach turning obstacles into opportunity.","zh":"斯多葛派教導將障礙轉化為機會。"},{"en":"To turn obstacles into opportunity means to use difficulties as chances for growth or success.","zh":"將障礙轉化為機會意思是把困難用作成長或成功的機會。"},{"en":"A rejected application can become an opportunity to improve a CV.","zh":"被拒絕的申請可以變成改善履歷的機會。"},{"en":"This idea is central to resilience and entrepreneurship.","zh":"這個想法是抗逆力和企業家精神的核心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive transformation of difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述把困難正面轉化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"business entrepreneur","meaning":"企業家","examples":[{"en":"Every business entrepreneur needs to learn this lesson.","zh":"每位企業家都需要學習這一課。"},{"en":"A business entrepreneur is someone who starts or runs a business, often taking risks.","zh":"企業家是創立或經營企業的人，通常會承擔風險。"},{"en":"A business entrepreneur must handle uncertainty, competition and failure.","zh":"企業家必須處理不確定性、競爭和失敗。"},{"en":"Stoicism can help entrepreneurs stay disciplined during pressure.","zh":"斯多葛主義可以幫助企業家在壓力中保持自律。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a person active in starting or developing businesses.","zh":"這個短語描述積極創立或發展企業的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"I would argue that","meaning":"我會認為","examples":[{"en":"The speaker would argue that Stoicism is still relevant today.","zh":"講者會認為斯多葛主義今天仍然相關。"},{"en":"I would argue that means I believe and will give reasons for this view.","zh":"我會認為意思是我相信這個觀點，並會提出理由。"},{"en":"I would argue that ancient philosophy can still help modern people.","zh":"我會認為古代哲學仍能幫助現代人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when presenting an opinion in a reasoned way.","zh":"當以有理據方式提出意見時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It sounds more formal than simply saying “I think”.","zh":"它比單純說 “I think” 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be as relevant today as","meaning":"今天和……一樣有意義","examples":[{"en":"Studying Stoicism is as relevant today as it was 2,000 years ago.","zh":"研究斯多葛主義今天和 2,000 年前一樣有意義。"},{"en":"As relevant today as means equally meaningful or useful now compared with the past.","zh":"今天和過去一樣有意義，意思是現在與過去同樣有價值或有用。"},{"en":"Questions about courage and self-control are as relevant today as they were in ancient times.","zh":"關於勇氣和自我控制的問題，今天和古代一樣有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase compares present value with past value.","zh":"這個短語比較現在價值與過去價值。"},{"en":"It is useful when arguing that an old idea still matters.","zh":"當論證舊思想仍然重要時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"thanks to","meaning":"因為；有賴於","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism remains relevant thanks to its insights into life.","zh":"斯多葛主義因為它對人生的見解而仍然相關。"},{"en":"Thanks to means because of or as a result of something positive.","zh":"因為或有賴於某事意思是由於某個正面原因。"},{"en":"Thanks to regular practice, the student became more confident.","zh":"有賴於定期練習，那名學生變得更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces the reason for a good result.","zh":"這個短語常引入好結果的原因。"},{"en":"It is useful in explanations of cause.","zh":"它適合用於解釋原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"brilliant insights into","meaning":"對……的深刻見解","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism offers brilliant insights into how to lead a good life.","zh":"斯多葛主義提供關於如何過美好人生的深刻見解。"},{"en":"Brilliant insights into something are excellent and deep understandings of it.","zh":"對某事的深刻見解是對它出色而深入的理解。"},{"en":"Ancient philosophy can offer brilliant insights into fear, ambition and happiness.","zh":"古代哲學可以提供對恐懼、野心和幸福的深刻見解。"},{"en":"Insights are valuable when they change how people see their own lives.","zh":"當見解改變人們如何看待自己的人生，它就有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase praises depth of understanding.","zh":"這個短語讚賞理解的深度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lead a good life","meaning":"過美好人生","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism gives advice on how to lead a good life.","zh":"斯多葛主義提供關於如何過美好人生的建議。"},{"en":"To lead a good life means to live in a morally good, meaningful or fulfilling way.","zh":"過美好人生意思是以有道德、有意義或充實的方式生活。"},{"en":"Stoics believed people lead a good life through virtue and self-control.","zh":"斯多葛派相信人透過美德和自我控制過美好人生。"},{"en":"A good life may not depend on wealth, fame or pleasure.","zh":"美好人生未必取決於財富、名聲或享樂。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to ethical discussion.","zh":"這個短語是倫理討論的核心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at the very root of","meaning":"在……的根本","examples":[{"en":"At the very root of Stoic thinking is a simple way of living.","zh":"在斯多葛思想的根本，是一種簡單的生活方式。"},{"en":"At the very root of something means at its deepest or most basic foundation.","zh":"在某事的根本意思是在它最深層或最基本的基礎。"},{"en":"At the very root of the problem is a lack of trust.","zh":"在問題的根本，是缺乏信任。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the central foundation of an idea.","zh":"這個短語指向一個想法的核心基礎。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining core principles.","zh":"當解釋核心原則時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"way of living","meaning":"生活方式","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism offers a simple way of living.","zh":"斯多葛主義提供一種簡單的生活方式。"},{"en":"A way of living is a pattern of habits, values and choices in daily life.","zh":"生活方式是日常生活中的習慣、價值觀和選擇模式。"},{"en":"A Stoic way of living focuses on virtue, reason and acceptance.","zh":"斯多葛生活方式專注於美德、理性和接受。"},{"en":"Philosophy becomes practical when it becomes a way of living.","zh":"當哲學成為生活方式，它就變得實用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lifestyle and life practice.","zh":"這個短語描述生活風格和人生實踐。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"control what you can","meaning":"控制你能控制的事","examples":[{"en":"The Stoic rule is to control what you can.","zh":"斯多葛規則是控制你能控制的事。"},{"en":"Control what you can means focus on actions and choices that are within your power.","zh":"控制你能控制的事意思是專注於自己有能力掌握的行動和選擇。"},{"en":"You cannot control the weather, but you can control your preparation.","zh":"你不能控制天氣，但可以控制自己的準備。"},{"en":"This idea helps reduce wasted worry about uncontrollable events.","zh":"這個想法有助減少對不可控制事件的無謂憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase is one of the clearest Stoic principles.","zh":"這個短語是最清楚的斯多葛原則之一。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"accept what you can’t","meaning":"接受你不能控制的事","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism teaches people to accept what they cannot control.","zh":"斯多葛主義教人接受自己不能控制的事。"},{"en":"Accept what you can’t means stop resisting things outside your control.","zh":"接受你不能控制的事意思是不再抗拒超出自己控制的事情。"},{"en":"A Stoic accepts delays but still chooses how to use the waiting time.","zh":"斯多葛派人士接受延誤，但仍選擇如何使用等待時間。"},{"en":"Acceptance does not mean giving up; it means facing reality clearly.","zh":"接受不等於放棄，而是清楚面對現實。"},{"en":"This phrase balances action with calm acceptance.","zh":"這個短語平衡行動與平靜接受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not as easy as it sounds","meaning":"並不像聽起來那麼容易","examples":[{"en":"This rule is not as easy as it sounds.","zh":"這條規則並不像聽起來那麼容易。"},{"en":"Not as easy as it sounds means more difficult than it first appears.","zh":"並不像聽起來那麼容易意思是比起初看來更困難。"},{"en":"Staying calm during criticism is not as easy as it sounds.","zh":"面對批評時保持冷靜，並不像聽起來那麼容易。"},{"en":"Simple advice can require long practice in real life.","zh":"簡單建議在現實生活中可能需要長時間練習。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a simple idea may be difficult to apply.","zh":"這個短語提醒人，簡單想法可能難以應用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"require considerable practice","meaning":"需要大量練習","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism requires considerable practice.","zh":"斯多葛主義需要大量練習。"},{"en":"To require considerable practice means to need a lot of repeated effort to master.","zh":"需要大量練習意思是需要很多反覆努力才能掌握。"},{"en":"Emotional self-control requires considerable practice.","zh":"情緒自我控制需要大量練習。"},{"en":"Stoic ideas are easy to understand but harder to live by every day.","zh":"斯多葛思想容易理解，但較難每天實踐。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises effort and repetition.","zh":"這個短語強調努力和重複。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take a lifetime to master","meaning":"需要一生才能掌握","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism can take a lifetime to master.","zh":"斯多葛主義可能需要一生才能掌握。"},{"en":"To take a lifetime to master means to require a whole life of learning and practice.","zh":"需要一生才能掌握意思是需要整個人生的學習和練習。"},{"en":"Wisdom may take a lifetime to master because every stage of life brings new tests.","zh":"智慧可能需要一生才能掌握，因為人生每個階段都有新考驗。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deep difficulty and long-term growth.","zh":"這個短語暗示深層困難和長期成長。"},{"en":"It is often used for complex skills or philosophies.","zh":"它常用於複雜技能或哲學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"foundation for","meaning":"……的基礎","examples":[{"en":"The Stoics believed virtue was the foundation for a happy life.","zh":"斯多葛派相信美德是快樂人生的基礎。"},{"en":"Foundation for something means the basic support on which it is built.","zh":"某事的基礎意思是它建立其上的基本支撐。"},{"en":"Trust is the foundation for a strong friendship.","zh":"信任是穩固友誼的基礎。"},{"en":"Stoics believed character was the foundation for lasting happiness.","zh":"斯多葛派相信品格是持久幸福的基礎。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the base of something important.","zh":"這個短語指出重要事物的根基。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"good and happy life","meaning":"美好而快樂的人生","examples":[{"en":"A disciplined character is the foundation for a good and happy life.","zh":"自律的品格是美好而快樂的人生的基礎。"},{"en":"A good and happy life means a life that is morally good and emotionally fulfilling.","zh":"美好而快樂的人生意思是道德上良好並在情感上充實的人生。"},{"en":"Stoics believed a good and happy life depends more on character than circumstances.","zh":"斯多葛派相信美好而快樂的人生更取決於品格，而非環境。"},{"en":"People may seek a happy life through pleasure, but Stoics emphasised virtue.","zh":"人們可能透過享樂尋求快樂人生，但斯多葛派強調美德。"},{"en":"This phrase connects ethics with well-being.","zh":"這個短語把倫理與幸福連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"money, fame, power or pleasure","meaning":"金錢、名聲、權力或享樂","examples":[{"en":"The Stoics did not see money, fame, power or pleasure as the foundation of happiness.","zh":"斯多葛派不把金錢、名聲、權力或享樂視為幸福的基礎。"},{"en":"Money, fame, power or pleasure are external rewards many people chase.","zh":"金錢、名聲、權力或享樂是許多人追求的外在回報。"},{"en":"Stoics argued that these things are unstable and not fully under our control.","zh":"斯多葛派認為這些東西不穩定，而且不完全受我們控制。"},{"en":"A person can have money, fame, power or pleasure and still lack peace of mind.","zh":"一個人可以擁有金錢、名聲、權力或享樂，但仍缺乏內心平靜。"},{"en":"This phrase lists common but unreliable sources of happiness.","zh":"這個短語列出常見但不可靠的幸福來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"disciplined and principled character","meaning":"自律而有原則的品格","examples":[{"en":"The Stoics valued a disciplined and principled character.","zh":"斯多葛派重視自律而有原則的品格。"},{"en":"A disciplined and principled character is a personality guided by self-control and moral rules.","zh":"自律而有原則的品格是由自我控制和道德規則引導的人格。"},{"en":"Such a character stays steady even when tempted by comfort or status.","zh":"這樣的品格即使受到舒適或地位誘惑，也能保持穩定。"},{"en":"Stoics believed character mattered more than success or reputation.","zh":"斯多葛派相信品格比成功或名聲更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moral strength and self-control.","zh":"這個短語描述道德力量和自我控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"resonate with","meaning":"引起……共鳴","examples":[{"en":"Stoic ideas seem to resonate with many people today.","zh":"斯多葛思想似乎引起今天許多人的共鳴。"},{"en":"To resonate with someone means to feel meaningful, relevant or emotionally true to them.","zh":"引起某人共鳴意思是令他感到有意義、相關或情感上真實。"},{"en":"Stoic advice may resonate with people facing stress and uncertainty.","zh":"面對壓力和不確定性的人，可能會對斯多葛建議有共鳴。"},{"en":"An old idea resonates when modern readers feel it speaks to their lives.","zh":"當現代讀者覺得古老思想說中了自己的生活，它就會引起共鳴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep connection or appeal.","zh":"這個短語描述深層連繫或吸引力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"many people today","meaning":"今天許多人","examples":[{"en":"Stoicism still resonates with many people today.","zh":"斯多葛主義今天仍然引起許多人共鳴。"},{"en":"Many people today means a large number of people living in the present time.","zh":"今天許多人意思是現代生活中的大量人。"},{"en":"Many people today look for practical tools to handle anxiety and pressure.","zh":"今天許多人尋找實用工具來處理焦慮和壓力。"},{"en":"Stoicism appeals to many people today because it offers simple rules for difficult moments.","zh":"斯多葛主義吸引今天許多人，因為它為困難時刻提供簡單規則。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an old idea with modern readers.","zh":"這個短語把古老思想與現代讀者連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 16 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 17/task-1":[{"front":"Can I help you?","meaning":"請問有甚麼可以幫你？","examples":[{"en":"The employee answers the phone by saying, “Can I help you?”","zh":"職員接電話時說：「請問有甚麼可以幫你？」"},{"en":"“Can I help you?” is a polite way for staff to offer assistance.","zh":"Can I help you? 是職員禮貌地表示願意提供協助的說法。"},{"en":"A shop assistant may say, “Can I help you?” when a customer looks unsure.","zh":"當顧客看起來不太確定時，店員可能會說：「請問有甚麼可以幫你？」"},{"en":"This question opens a service conversation and invites the other person to explain their need.","zh":"這個問題開啟服務對話，並邀請對方說明需要。"},{"en":"It is common in shops, offices, customer service calls, and reception desks.","zh":"它常見於商店、辦公室、客戶服務電話和接待處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"see your advertisement about","meaning":"看到你們關於……的廣告","examples":[{"en":"The woman saw the advertisement about copying pictures to disk.","zh":"那位女士看到你們關於將相片複製到光碟的廣告。"},{"en":"To see your advertisement about something means to notice an advert that promotes that service or product.","zh":"see your advertisement about something 是指看到宣傳該服務或產品的廣告。"},{"en":"A customer may call a shop after seeing its advertisement about sofa repairs.","zh":"顧客可能看到一間店關於維修梳化的廣告後致電查詢。"},{"en":"Advertisements help people discover services they did not know were available.","zh":"廣告幫助人們發現自己原本不知道的服務。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how the customer first learned about the company.","zh":"這個短語解釋顧客最初如何得知該公司。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"copy pictures to disk","meaning":"將相片複製到光碟","examples":[{"en":"Picturerep copies pictures to disk.","zh":"Picturerep 將相片複製到光碟。"},{"en":"To copy pictures to disk means to scan or transfer photos onto a disk in digital form.","zh":"copy pictures to disk 是指把相片掃描或轉移到光碟，以數碼形式保存。"},{"en":"A family may copy pictures to disk to preserve old holiday photos.","zh":"家庭可能把相片複製到光碟，以保存舊旅行照片。"},{"en":"Copying pictures to disk can protect memories if the original photos fade or get damaged.","zh":"將相片複製到光碟可以在原相褪色或受損時保護回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing physical photos into stored digital files.","zh":"這個短語描述把實體相片變成可儲存的數碼檔案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a bit more information about","meaning":"多一點關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"The woman would like a bit more information about the service.","zh":"那位女士想知道多一點關於這項服務的資料。"},{"en":"A bit more information about something means some extra details about it.","zh":"a bit more information about something 是指關於某事的額外一些細節。"},{"en":"A parent may ask for a bit more information about a school trip before signing the form.","zh":"家長簽表格前，可能會想知道多一點關於學校旅行的資料。"},{"en":"Extra information helps people decide whether a service is suitable.","zh":"額外資料幫助人們決定服務是否合適。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and less demanding than asking for a full explanation.","zh":"這個短語有禮貌，比要求完整解釋更溫和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what you do","meaning":"你們所做的服務","examples":[{"en":"The woman wants to know more about what Picturerep does.","zh":"那位女士想更了解 Picturerep 所做的服務。"},{"en":"What you do means the service, work, or activity a person or company provides.","zh":"what you do 是指一個人或公司提供的服務、工作或活動。"},{"en":"A new client may ask an accountant to explain what they do before paying for advice.","zh":"新客戶在付款諮詢前，可能會請會計師解釋他們所做的服務。"},{"en":"Understanding what a company does helps customers know whether it can solve their problem.","zh":"了解公司所做的服務，有助顧客知道它能否解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about the nature of the work.","zh":"這個短語詢問工作的性質。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a box full of","meaning":"一整箱……","examples":[{"en":"The woman has a box full of old family photos.","zh":"那位女士有一整箱舊家庭相片。"},{"en":"A box full of something means a box containing many items.","zh":"a box full of something 是指裝滿很多物品的一個箱子。"},{"en":"A teacher may have a box full of old worksheets in the cupboard.","zh":"老師的櫃裏可能有一整箱舊工作紙。"},{"en":"A box full of photos can be difficult to organise if they have been stored for years.","zh":"如果相片存放多年，一整箱相片可能很難整理。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises quantity and storage.","zh":"這個短語強調數量和存放狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"old family photos","meaning":"舊家庭相片","examples":[{"en":"The woman wants to preserve her old family photos.","zh":"那位女士想保存她的舊家庭相片。"},{"en":"Old family photos are pictures of relatives or family events taken many years ago.","zh":"old family photos 是多年前拍下的親人或家庭事件照片。"},{"en":"Old family photos may show grandparents, weddings, childhood memories, or old homes.","zh":"舊家庭相片可能展示祖父母、婚禮、童年回憶或舊居。"},{"en":"Families often value old photos because they connect younger people with the past.","zh":"家庭常重視舊相片，因為它們把年輕一代與過去連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to personal historical pictures, not ordinary recent snapshots.","zh":"這個短語指個人歷史相片，而不是普通近照。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"up in the attic","meaning":"放在閣樓上","examples":[{"en":"The photos have been up in the attic for years.","zh":"這些相片多年來一直放在閣樓上。"},{"en":"Up in the attic means stored in the space under the roof of a house.","zh":"up in the attic 是指存放在屋頂下方的閣樓空間。"},{"en":"Families often keep old boxes, toys, and documents up in the attic.","zh":"家庭常把舊箱子、玩具和文件放在閣樓上。"},{"en":"Things left in an attic for years may become dusty, damp, or fragile.","zh":"放在閣樓多年的東西可能變得多塵、潮濕或脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear location inside a home.","zh":"這個短語清楚指出家中的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for years","meaning":"多年來","examples":[{"en":"The old photos have been stored in the attic for years.","zh":"這些舊相片多年來一直存放在閣樓。"},{"en":"For years means for a long period of many years.","zh":"for years 是指持續很多年、很長時間。"},{"en":"A family may keep old letters in a drawer for years.","zh":"一個家庭可能把舊信件多年來放在抽屜裏。"},{"en":"When something is stored for years, people may forget its condition until they check it.","zh":"當某物存放多年，人們可能到檢查時才知道其狀況。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a long duration.","zh":"這個短語強調長時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"must be 50 or 60 years old","meaning":"一定有五六十年歷史","examples":[{"en":"Some of the photos must be 50 or 60 years old.","zh":"有些相片一定有五六十年歷史。"},{"en":"Must be 50 or 60 years old means the speaker strongly believes the items are that old.","zh":"must be 50 or 60 years old 是指說話者強烈相信那些物品有那麼久歷史。"},{"en":"This school photo must be 40 years old because my father looks very young in it.","zh":"這張學校照片一定有40年歷史，因為我父親在相中看起來很年輕。"},{"en":"Old photos may need careful handling because age can make paper and colour fragile.","zh":"舊相片可能需要小心處理，因為年代久遠會令紙張和顏色變脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase uses “must” to make a strong guess.","zh":"這個短語用 must 作出強烈推測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get something converted to","meaning":"將某物轉換成……","examples":[{"en":"The woman would like to get the photos converted to digital format.","zh":"那位女士想把相片轉換成數碼格式。"},{"en":"To get something converted to another form means to have it changed into that form by someone or a service.","zh":"get something converted to another form 是指請人或服務把某物轉成另一種形式。"},{"en":"A company can get paper records converted to electronic files.","zh":"公司可以把紙本紀錄轉換成電子檔案。"},{"en":"Converting old materials can make them easier to store, search, and share.","zh":"轉換舊資料可以令它們更容易儲存、搜尋和分享。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on arranging a change in format.","zh":"這個短語著重安排格式轉換。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"digital format","meaning":"數碼格式","examples":[{"en":"The woman wants her old photos in digital format.","zh":"那位女士想把舊相片變成數碼格式。"},{"en":"Digital format means information stored as computer files rather than physical copies.","zh":"digital format 是指以電腦檔案形式儲存資料，而不是實體副本。"},{"en":"A song in digital format can be played on a phone or computer.","zh":"數碼格式的歌曲可以在電話或電腦播放。"},{"en":"Digital files are easier to copy, back up, and send to family members.","zh":"數碼檔案較容易複製、備份和傳送給家人。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts computer-based storage with paper or film.","zh":"這個短語把電腦儲存與紙本或菲林作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what about size?","meaning":"尺寸方面怎樣？","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks what about size when discussing the photos.","zh":"那位女士討論相片時問尺寸方面怎樣。"},{"en":"What about size? asks whether size matters or whether there are size rules.","zh":"What about size? 是問尺寸是否重要，或是否有尺寸規定。"},{"en":"If a shop copies documents, a customer may ask, “What about size?”","zh":"如果商店複印文件，顧客可能會問：「尺寸方面怎樣？」"},{"en":"This question helps check practical limits before sending items.","zh":"這個問題有助在寄出物品前確認實際限制。"},{"en":"It is a short way to move the conversation to the issue of size.","zh":"它是把對話轉到尺寸問題的簡短說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"all sorts of sizes","meaning":"各種尺寸","examples":[{"en":"The photos are all sorts of sizes.","zh":"這些相片有各種尺寸。"},{"en":"All sorts of sizes means many different sizes.","zh":"all sorts of sizes 是指很多不同尺寸。"},{"en":"A box of old clothes may contain shirts and jackets of all sorts of sizes.","zh":"一箱舊衣服可能有各種尺寸的恤衫和外套。"},{"en":"Different sizes can make processing or storage more complicated.","zh":"不同尺寸可能令處理或儲存更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises variety and irregularity.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣和不規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"restrictions","meaning":"限制","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether there are any restrictions on photo size.","zh":"那位女士問相片尺寸是否有任何限制。"},{"en":"Restrictions are rules or limits about what is allowed.","zh":"restrictions 是關於允許做甚麼的規則或限制。"},{"en":"A library may have restrictions on how many books students can borrow.","zh":"圖書館可能限制學生可借閱多少本書。"},{"en":"Restrictions help services work safely and within their equipment limits.","zh":"限制幫助服務安全運作，並符合設備能力。"},{"en":"This word often appears when checking rules before using a service.","zh":"這個詞常出現在使用服務前確認規則時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"maximum size of","meaning":"……的最大尺寸","examples":[{"en":"The maximum size of photo for the normal service is 30 centimetres.","zh":"普通服務可處理相片的最大尺寸是30厘米。"},{"en":"The maximum size of something is the largest size allowed.","zh":"maximum size of something 是指某物被允許的最大尺寸。"},{"en":"A suitcase may have a maximum size of 55 centimetres for cabin luggage.","zh":"手提行李箱的最大尺寸可能是55厘米。"},{"en":"Maximum size limits exist because machines or storage spaces cannot handle everything.","zh":"最大尺寸限制存在，是因為機器或儲存空間不能處理所有尺寸。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the upper limit.","zh":"這個短語提供上限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"normal service","meaning":"普通服務","examples":[{"en":"The normal service can copy photos up to 30 centimetres.","zh":"普通服務可以複製最多30厘米的相片。"},{"en":"The normal service means the standard service offered without special arrangements.","zh":"normal service 是指不需要特別安排的標準服務。"},{"en":"A laundry’s normal service may take three days, while express service costs more.","zh":"洗衣店的普通服務可能需時三天，而特快服務收費較高。"},{"en":"Normal services usually have fixed prices, limits, and procedures.","zh":"普通服務通常有固定價格、限制和程序。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts ordinary service with special or custom service.","zh":"這個短語把一般服務與特別或訂製服務作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at least","meaning":"至少","examples":[{"en":"Each picture must be at least 4 centimetres.","zh":"每張相片必須至少4厘米。"},{"en":"At least means no less than a stated amount or number.","zh":"at least 是指不少於指定數量或數字。"},{"en":"Students should arrive at least ten minutes before the exam starts.","zh":"學生應至少在考試開始前十分鐘到達。"},{"en":"Minimum limits help people know the smallest acceptable amount.","zh":"最低限制幫助人知道可接受的最小數量。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the lower limit.","zh":"這個短語提供下限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the minimum we can cope with","meaning":"我們能處理的最小尺寸","examples":[{"en":"Four centimetres is the minimum size the company can cope with.","zh":"4厘米是公司能處理的最小尺寸。"},{"en":"The minimum we can cope with means the smallest amount or size the service can handle.","zh":"the minimum we can cope with 是指服務能處理的最小數量或尺寸。"},{"en":"A printer may say A6 paper is the minimum size it can cope with.","zh":"打印機可能說 A6 紙是它能處理的最小尺寸。"},{"en":"If something is below the minimum, the equipment may not work properly.","zh":"如果某物低於最低尺寸，設備可能無法正常運作。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a practical limit.","zh":"這個短語解釋實際處理限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"that should be fine","meaning":"那應該沒問題","examples":[{"en":"The woman says that the size restriction should be fine.","zh":"那位女士說尺寸限制應該沒問題。"},{"en":"That should be fine means it is likely to be acceptable or not a problem.","zh":"that should be fine 是指很可能可以接受或沒有問題。"},{"en":"If the meeting ends at four, that should be fine for catching the train.","zh":"如果會議四點結束，那應該可以趕上火車。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they think an arrangement will work.","zh":"當人們認為安排可行時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It shows calm acceptance rather than strong excitement.","zh":"它表示平靜接受，而不是強烈興奮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in a frame","meaning":"放在相架裏","examples":[{"en":"Some of the woman’s photos are in a frame.","zh":"那位女士有些相片放在相架裏。"},{"en":"In a frame means placed inside a border or holder, often for display.","zh":"in a frame 是指放在邊框或固定架中，通常用作展示。"},{"en":"A wedding photo may be kept in a frame on a living-room shelf.","zh":"婚禮照片可能放在客廳架上的相架裏。"},{"en":"Framed photos may need to be removed before scanning or copying.","zh":"相架中的照片在掃描或複製前可能需要取出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a picture is held or displayed.","zh":"這個短語描述相片如何被固定或展示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"take them out","meaning":"將它們取出來","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether she should take the photos out of their frames.","zh":"那位女士問是否應該把相片從相架中取出來。"},{"en":"To take them out means to remove them from the place or container they are in.","zh":"take them out 是指把它們從所在位置或容器中移走。"},{"en":"A customer may take documents out of a plastic sleeve before copying them.","zh":"顧客可能在複印前把文件從膠套中取出來。"},{"en":"Taking photos out of frames can help staff scan them properly.","zh":"把相片從相架中取出來可以幫助職員正確掃描。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on removing items from where they are kept.","zh":"這個短語著重把物品從存放處移出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"before I send them","meaning":"在我寄出它們之前","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether she should remove the frames before she sends the photos.","zh":"那位女士問在她寄出相片之前是否應移除相架。"},{"en":"Before I send them means before I post, deliver, or hand over the items.","zh":"before I send them 是指在我郵寄、送交或交出那些物品之前。"},{"en":"Before I send the forms, I should check that every page is signed.","zh":"在我寄出表格之前，我應檢查每一頁是否已簽名。"},{"en":"Checking items before sending them can prevent delays and extra work.","zh":"寄出前檢查物品可以防止延誤和額外工夫。"},{"en":"This phrase marks an action that should happen first.","zh":"這個短語標示應先發生的行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"we cannot copy them otherwise","meaning":"否則我們無法複製它們","examples":[{"en":"The company cannot copy framed photos otherwise.","zh":"否則，公司無法複製有相架的相片。"},{"en":"We cannot copy them otherwise means we cannot do the task unless the condition is met.","zh":"we cannot copy them otherwise 是指除非符合條件，否則我們無法完成任務。"},{"en":"Please remove the staples; we cannot scan the pages otherwise.","zh":"請移除釘書釘；否則我們無法掃描頁面。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why an instruction is necessary.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某項指示是必要的。"},{"en":"It shows that the process depends on a required preparation.","zh":"它顯示流程取決於必要準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"must all be separate","meaning":"必須全部分開","examples":[{"en":"The photos must all be separate.","zh":"相片必須全部分開。"},{"en":"Must all be separate means every item must be apart from the others, not attached together.","zh":"must all be separate 是指每件物品必須彼此分開，不能連在一起。"},{"en":"Application forms must all be separate if each student needs an individual record.","zh":"如果每名學生需要個別紀錄，申請表必須全部分開。"},{"en":"Separate items are easier to scan, count, and organise.","zh":"分開的物品較容易掃描、點算和整理。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict preparation requirement.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格的準備要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be stuck into an album","meaning":"被貼在相簿裏","examples":[{"en":"The photos must not be stuck into an album.","zh":"相片不得被貼在相簿裏。"},{"en":"To be stuck into an album means to be glued or fixed onto album pages.","zh":"be stuck into an album 是指被黏貼或固定在相簿頁上。"},{"en":"Old photos stuck into an album can be difficult to remove without damage.","zh":"被貼在相簿裏的舊相片可能很難在不損壞下取出。"},{"en":"Scanning loose photos is easier than scanning photos fixed to thick pages.","zh":"掃描散開的相片比掃描固定在厚頁上的相片容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes photos attached to a photo album.","zh":"這個短語描述相片附在相簿中的狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give me an idea of","meaning":"讓我大概知道","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks the employee to give her an idea of the cost.","zh":"那位女士請職員讓她大概知道費用。"},{"en":"To give me an idea of something means to provide an approximate understanding of it.","zh":"give me an idea of something 是指提供對某事的大概了解。"},{"en":"A builder may give a homeowner an idea of the repair cost before making a full quote.","zh":"建築工人可能在正式報價前，讓屋主大概知道維修費用。"},{"en":"An approximate idea helps people decide whether to continue.","zh":"大概了解有助人們決定是否繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for a rough estimate, not necessarily an exact figure.","zh":"這個短語要求粗略估算，不一定是精確數字。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"how much this will cost","meaning":"這會花費多少","examples":[{"en":"The woman wants to know how much the service will cost.","zh":"那位女士想知道這項服務會花費多少。"},{"en":"How much this will cost asks about the price or total amount of money needed.","zh":"how much this will cost 是詢問價格或所需總金額。"},{"en":"Before booking a course, students often ask how much it will cost.","zh":"報讀課程前，學生常會問這會花費多少。"},{"en":"Knowing the cost helps people plan their budget.","zh":"知道費用有助人們規劃預算。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when checking price before agreeing to a service.","zh":"這個短語用於同意服務前確認價格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"charge £195 for","meaning":"收取195英鎊處理……","examples":[{"en":"The company charges £195 for 300 to 400 photos.","zh":"公司收取195英鎊處理300至400張相片。"},{"en":"To charge £195 for something means to ask customers to pay £195 for that service or item.","zh":"charge £195 for something 是指要求顧客為某服務或物品支付195英鎊。"},{"en":"A photographer may charge £80 for a family photo session.","zh":"攝影師可能收取80英鎊拍攝家庭相。"},{"en":"Prices often depend on the amount of work, materials, and time needed.","zh":"價格通常取決於所需工作量、材料和時間。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the cost of a specific service.","zh":"這個短語解釋某項具體服務的費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"basic service","meaning":"基本服務","examples":[{"en":"The basic service for 300 to 400 photos costs £195.","zh":"處理300至400張相片的基本服務費用是195英鎊。"},{"en":"A basic service is the standard or simplest level of service.","zh":"basic service 是標準或最簡單級別的服務。"},{"en":"A phone plan’s basic service may include calls and messages but no extra data.","zh":"電話計劃的基本服務可能包括通話和短訊，但沒有額外數據。"},{"en":"Basic services usually cost less than services with special options.","zh":"基本服務通常比附加特別選項的服務便宜。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the standard package with additional features.","zh":"這個短語把標準套餐與額外功能作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"include the disk","meaning":"包括光碟","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether the price includes the disk.","zh":"那位女士問價錢是否包括光碟。"},{"en":"To include the disk means the disk is part of what is provided for the price.","zh":"include the disk 是指光碟已包括在該價格所提供的內容中。"},{"en":"A course fee may include the textbook, but not the exam fee.","zh":"課程費用可能包括課本，但不包括考試費。"},{"en":"Asking what is included prevents surprise extra costs.","zh":"詢問包括甚麼可以避免意外額外費用。"},{"en":"This phrase checks whether an item is covered by the quoted price.","zh":"這個短語確認某物是否已包含在報價中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"extra ones","meaning":"額外的","examples":[{"en":"Customers can get extra disks for £5 each.","zh":"顧客可以每張5英鎊取得額外光碟。"},{"en":"Extra ones means additional copies or items beyond the first one.","zh":"extra ones 是指第一份以外的額外副本或物品。"},{"en":"A customer may order extra ones if several family members want their own copy.","zh":"如果幾位家庭成員都想有自己的副本，顧客可能會訂購額外的。"},{"en":"Extra copies are useful when people want to share files without passing one disk around.","zh":"額外副本很有用，因為人們可以分享檔案，而不用傳來傳去同一張光碟。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to items already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語回指前面已提及的物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pay when","meaning":"在……時付款","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether she needs to pay when she sends the photos.","zh":"那位女士問是否需要在寄出相片時付款。"},{"en":"Pay when means make payment at the same time as another action happens.","zh":"pay when 是指在另一行動發生的同時付款。"},{"en":"Some customers pay when they collect the order rather than when they place it.","zh":"有些顧客在取貨時付款，而不是下單時付款。"},{"en":"Payment timing matters because customers need to know when money is due.","zh":"付款時間很重要，因為顧客需要知道何時要付錢。"},{"en":"This phrase connects payment with a specific stage in a process.","zh":"這個短語把付款與流程中的某個階段連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"actually copied","meaning":"實際複製完成","examples":[{"en":"The company does not require payment until the pictures have actually been copied.","zh":"公司在相片實際複製完成前不要求付款。"},{"en":"Actually copied means really completed, not just received or planned.","zh":"actually copied 是指真正完成複製，而不只是收到或計劃處理。"},{"en":"A customer may pay only after the documents have actually been printed.","zh":"顧客可能只在文件實際打印完成後才付款。"},{"en":"Waiting until the work is actually done can reassure customers.","zh":"等到工作真正完成才付款，可以令顧客安心。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the service has been completed.","zh":"這個短語強調服務已完成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"let someone know","meaning":"通知某人","examples":[{"en":"The company will let the woman know how much the service costs.","zh":"公司會通知那位女士服務費用是多少。"},{"en":"To let someone know means to tell or inform them.","zh":"let someone know 是指告訴或通知某人。"},{"en":"Please let me know if you cannot attend the meeting.","zh":"如果你不能出席會議，請通知我。"},{"en":"Letting customers know the cost helps them decide whether to pay and continue.","zh":"通知顧客費用有助他們決定是否付款並繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in friendly and polite communication.","zh":"這個短語常見於友善和有禮貌的溝通。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"once we have received","meaning":"一旦我們收到","examples":[{"en":"Once the company has received the payment, it will return the parcel.","zh":"一旦公司收到款項，便會寄回包裹。"},{"en":"Once we have received means after we get or obtain something.","zh":"once we have received 是指在我們收到或取得某物之後。"},{"en":"Once we have received your form, we will confirm your place.","zh":"一旦我們收到你的表格，便會確認你的名額。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a condition that must happen before the next step.","zh":"這個短語設定下一步之前必須發生的條件。"},{"en":"It is common in service instructions and formal emails.","zh":"它常見於服務指引和正式電郵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"send the parcel off to","meaning":"將包裹寄給……","examples":[{"en":"The company will send the parcel off to the woman after payment.","zh":"公司會在付款後將包裹寄給那位女士。"},{"en":"To send the parcel off to someone means to post or dispatch the package to that person.","zh":"send the parcel off to someone 是指把包裹郵寄或寄送給某人。"},{"en":"A shop may send the parcel off to a customer once the order is ready.","zh":"訂單準備好後，商店可能將包裹寄給顧客。"},{"en":"Sending a parcel off usually means it has entered the postal or delivery system.","zh":"把包裹寄出通常表示它已進入郵寄或送遞系統。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on dispatching a package.","zh":"這個短語著重寄出包裹。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"anything else you would like to ask","meaning":"你還有其他想問的事嗎？","examples":[{"en":"The employee asks whether there is anything else the woman would like to ask.","zh":"職員問那位女士是否還有其他想問的事。"},{"en":"Anything else you would like to ask is a polite way to invite further questions.","zh":"anything else you would like to ask 是禮貌地邀請對方提出更多問題。"},{"en":"A receptionist may ask, “Is there anything else you would like to ask?” before ending a call.","zh":"接待員在結束通話前可能會問：「你還有其他想問的事嗎？」"},{"en":"This question helps make sure the customer has all the information they need.","zh":"這個問題有助確保顧客已得到所需資料。"},{"en":"It often appears near the end of a service conversation.","zh":"它常出現在服務對話接近結束時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"roughly sorted out","meaning":"大致整理好","examples":[{"en":"The woman has roughly sorted out the photos into groups.","zh":"那位女士已把相片大致整理成幾組。"},{"en":"Roughly sorted out means organised in a basic way, but not perfectly or finally.","zh":"roughly sorted out 是指以基本方式整理好，但不是完美或最終版本。"},{"en":"A student may roughly sort out notes before writing a full essay plan.","zh":"學生可能在寫完整文章大綱前，先大致整理筆記。"},{"en":"Rough organisation makes later work easier, even if details still need checking.","zh":"粗略整理可以令之後工作較容易，即使細節仍需檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an early stage of organisation.","zh":"這個短語表示整理的初步階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"into groups","meaning":"分成幾組","examples":[{"en":"The photos have been sorted into groups.","zh":"這些相片已分成幾組。"},{"en":"Into groups means divided into separate sets or categories.","zh":"into groups 是指被分成不同組別或類別。"},{"en":"A teacher may put students into groups for a speaking activity.","zh":"老師可能把學生分成幾組做說話活動。"},{"en":"Grouping items makes them easier to find, label, and manage.","zh":"分組能令物品更容易尋找、標記和管理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organisation by category or set.","zh":"這個短語描述按類別或組別整理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據","examples":[{"en":"The photos are sorted according to what they are about.","zh":"這些相片根據它們的內容分類。"},{"en":"According to means based on or following a particular rule, idea, or category.","zh":"according to 是指基於或按照某個規則、想法或類別。"},{"en":"Books in a library are arranged according to subject or author.","zh":"圖書館的書根據主題或作者排列。"},{"en":"Sorting according to topic helps people find things more quickly.","zh":"根據主題分類可以幫助人們更快找到東西。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the basis used for organisation.","zh":"這個短語解釋整理所依據的標準。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"what they are about","meaning":"它們的內容","examples":[{"en":"The groups are based on what the photos are about.","zh":"分組是基於相片的內容。"},{"en":"What they are about means the subject, theme, or content of the photos.","zh":"what they are about 是指相片的主題、題材或內容。"},{"en":"Holiday photos, wedding photos, and school photos are different because of what they are about.","zh":"旅行照、婚禮照和學校照因內容不同而不同。"},{"en":"Knowing what photos are about helps choose folder names.","zh":"知道相片內容有助選擇資料夾名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on content rather than size, date, or colour.","zh":"這個短語著重內容，而不是尺寸、日期或顏色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"keep them in those groups","meaning":"保持那些分組","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether the company can keep the photos in those groups.","zh":"那位女士問公司能否保持那些相片分組。"},{"en":"To keep them in those groups means to preserve the existing grouping and not mix them up.","zh":"keep them in those groups 是指保留現有分組，不把它們混在一起。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to keep worksheets in those groups for easy marking.","zh":"老師可能要求學生把工作紙保持那些分組，以便批改。"},{"en":"Keeping groups together prevents confusion and saves time later.","zh":"保持分組可以防止混亂，並節省之後時間。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the customer wants her organisation to be maintained.","zh":"這個短語顯示顧客希望維持自己的整理方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"save each group in","meaning":"將每組儲存在……","examples":[{"en":"The company will save each group in a different folder.","zh":"公司會將每組相片儲存在不同資料夾中。"},{"en":"To save each group in a place means to store each set of files there.","zh":"save each group in a place 是指把每一組檔案儲存在該位置。"},{"en":"A student may save each subject’s notes in a separate folder on a laptop.","zh":"學生可能把每科筆記儲存在手提電腦上的不同資料夾。"},{"en":"Saving groups separately makes files easier to open and search.","zh":"分別儲存各組檔案會令開啟和搜尋更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when organising digital files.","zh":"這個短語常用於整理數碼檔案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"different folder","meaning":"不同資料夾","examples":[{"en":"Each group of photos will be saved in a different folder.","zh":"每組相片會儲存在不同資料夾。"},{"en":"A different folder is a separate digital place for storing files.","zh":"different folder 是用來儲存檔案的另一個獨立數碼位置。"},{"en":"A family may create a different folder for each year of holiday photos.","zh":"家庭可能為每一年旅行照片建立不同資料夾。"},{"en":"Separate folders help people avoid mixing unrelated files.","zh":"分開資料夾有助人們避免把無關檔案混在一起。"},{"en":"This phrase is about organising digital information.","zh":"這個短語關於整理數碼資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on the disk","meaning":"在光碟上","examples":[{"en":"The folders will be saved on the disk.","zh":"資料夾會儲存在光碟上。"},{"en":"On the disk means stored on the physical or digital storage disk.","zh":"on the disk 是指儲存在實體或數碼儲存光碟上。"},{"en":"The photos on the disk can be opened on a computer.","zh":"光碟上的相片可以在電腦上開啟。"},{"en":"Saving files on a disk gives the customer a copy to keep or share.","zh":"把檔案儲存在光碟上，讓顧客有副本可保存或分享。"},{"en":"This phrase explains where the digital files will be stored.","zh":"這個短語解釋數碼檔案會儲存在哪裏。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"suggest a name for","meaning":"為……建議名稱","examples":[{"en":"The woman can suggest a name for each folder.","zh":"那位女士可以為每個資料夾建議名稱。"},{"en":"To suggest a name for something means to propose what it should be called.","zh":"suggest a name for something 是指提議某物應該叫甚麼。"},{"en":"Students may suggest a name for a new school club.","zh":"學生可能為新學會建議名稱。"},{"en":"Clear names help people find the right folder or file quickly.","zh":"清楚名稱有助人們快速找到正確資料夾或檔案。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the customer some control over organisation.","zh":"這個短語讓顧客在整理方面有一定控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"The woman suggests “Grandparents” as a folder name, for instance.","zh":"那位女士例如建議用「祖父母」作為資料夾名稱。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance 是指例如。"},{"en":"You can organise files by topic, for instance, “School”, “Work”, and “Family”.","zh":"你可以按主題整理檔案，例如「學校」、「工作」和「家庭」。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a specific example to make an idea clearer.","zh":"這個短語引入具體例子，使想法更清楚。"},{"en":"It is slightly more formal than “for example” but means the same thing.","zh":"它比 for example 稍正式，但意思相同。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"besides scan the photos","meaning":"除了掃描相片之外","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether the company does anything besides scan the photos.","zh":"那位女士問公司除了掃描相片之外，還會做甚麼。"},{"en":"Besides scan the photos means in addition to scanning the photos.","zh":"besides scan the photos 是指除了掃描相片之外。"},{"en":"A customer may ask whether a print shop does anything besides print documents.","zh":"顧客可能問影印店除了打印文件之外，還有沒有其他服務。"},{"en":"This phrase checks whether extra services are available.","zh":"這個短語確認是否有額外服務。"},{"en":"It contrasts the main service with possible additional work.","zh":"它把主要服務與可能的附加工作作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make improvements","meaning":"作出改善","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether the company can make improvements to the photos.","zh":"那位女士問公司能否對相片作出改善。"},{"en":"To make improvements means to make something better.","zh":"make improvements 是指令某物變得更好。"},{"en":"A teacher may make improvements to a worksheet after students find it confusing.","zh":"如果學生覺得工作紙混亂，老師可能會作出改善。"},{"en":"Improvements can make old photos clearer, brighter, or easier to enjoy.","zh":"改善可以令舊相片更清楚、更明亮或更易欣賞。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on positive changes.","zh":"這個短語著重正面改動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"standard service","meaning":"標準服務","examples":[{"en":"In the standard service, each photo is checked.","zh":"在標準服務中，每張相片都會被檢查。"},{"en":"Standard service means the normal level of service included in the usual price.","zh":"standard service 是一般價格中包括的正常服務級別。"},{"en":"A hotel’s standard service may include cleaning but not airport transport.","zh":"酒店的標準服務可能包括清潔，但不包括機場接送。"},{"en":"Standard services are useful because customers know what to expect.","zh":"標準服務很有用，因為顧客知道可以期待甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the normal package with special or premium options.","zh":"這個短語把普通套餐與特別或高級選項作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"each photo is checked","meaning":"每張相片都會被檢查","examples":[{"en":"Each photo is checked in the standard service.","zh":"在標準服務中，每張相片都會被檢查。"},{"en":"Each photo is checked means every individual photo is examined.","zh":"each photo is checked 是指每一張相片都會被查看。"},{"en":"Before printing, each document may be checked for missing pages.","zh":"打印前，每份文件可能會被檢查是否缺頁。"},{"en":"Checking every photo helps staff spot problems with colour, contrast, or damage.","zh":"檢查每張相片有助職員發現顏色、對比或損壞問題。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises careful attention to every item.","zh":"這個短語強調對每件物品都仔細處理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"touch up the colour","meaning":"修正顏色","examples":[{"en":"The company can sometimes touch up the colour of a photo.","zh":"公司有時可以修正相片顏色。"},{"en":"To touch up the colour means to make small corrections to improve the colours.","zh":"touch up the colour 是指作出小修正，使顏色更好。"},{"en":"A photographer may touch up the colour if an old picture looks faded.","zh":"如果舊相片看起來褪色，攝影師可能會修正顏色。"},{"en":"Colour touch-ups can make faces, clothes, and backgrounds look clearer.","zh":"顏色修正可以令面孔、衣服和背景看起來更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small improvement, not a complete change.","zh":"這個短語描述小型改善，而不是完全改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"improve the contrast","meaning":"改善對比度","examples":[{"en":"The company can improve the contrast of some photos.","zh":"公司可以改善一些相片的對比度。"},{"en":"To improve the contrast means to make light and dark areas clearer and more distinct.","zh":"improve the contrast 是指令明暗部分更清楚、更分明。"},{"en":"A dark photo may need improved contrast so people’s faces can be seen.","zh":"昏暗相片可能需要改善對比度，這樣才看得見人臉。"},{"en":"Better contrast can make old images look sharper and easier to view.","zh":"更好的對比度可以令舊影像看起來更清晰、更易觀看。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in photo editing.","zh":"這個短語常見於相片編輯。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make a big difference","meaning":"帶來很大分別","examples":[{"en":"Touching up the colour or contrast can make a big difference.","zh":"修正顏色或對比度可以帶來很大分別。"},{"en":"To make a big difference means to have a strong positive effect.","zh":"make a big difference 是指產生強烈正面影響。"},{"en":"A clear title can make a big difference to a student’s essay.","zh":"清楚標題可以對學生文章帶來很大分別。"},{"en":"Small changes can sometimes make a big difference if they solve the main problem.","zh":"如果小改動解決主要問題，有時也可以帶來很大分別。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an improvement is important and noticeable.","zh":"這個短語顯示改善很重要且明顯。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"quite fragile","meaning":"相當脆弱","examples":[{"en":"Some of the woman’s old photos are quite fragile.","zh":"那位女士有些舊相片相當脆弱。"},{"en":"Quite fragile means fairly easy to break, tear, or damage.","zh":"quite fragile 是指相當容易破裂、撕裂或受損。"},{"en":"Old letters can be quite fragile if the paper has become thin and dry.","zh":"如果紙張變薄變乾，舊信件可能相當脆弱。"},{"en":"Fragile items need careful handling to avoid permanent damage.","zh":"脆弱物品需要小心處理，以避免永久損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that something should be treated gently.","zh":"這個短語提醒某物應被輕柔對待。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get damaged in the process","meaning":"在過程中受損","examples":[{"en":"The woman worries that fragile photos may get damaged in the process.","zh":"那位女士擔心脆弱相片可能在過程中受損。"},{"en":"To get damaged in the process means to be harmed while the work is being done.","zh":"get damaged in the process 是指在工作進行期間受到損害。"},{"en":"A fragile vase may get damaged in the process of being moved.","zh":"易碎花瓶可能在搬運過程中受損。"},{"en":"People worry about damage when valuable items must be handled by others.","zh":"當貴重物品需要由別人處理，人們會擔心損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase connects possible harm with a procedure.","zh":"這個短語把可能傷害與流程連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"particularly fragile","meaning":"特別脆弱","examples":[{"en":"Photos that look particularly fragile are handled by hand.","zh":"看起來特別脆弱的相片會由人手處理。"},{"en":"Particularly fragile means especially delicate or easy to damage.","zh":"particularly fragile 是指尤其精細或容易受損。"},{"en":"A museum may use special gloves for particularly fragile documents.","zh":"博物館可能使用特別手套處理特別脆弱的文件。"},{"en":"Items that are particularly fragile need slower and more careful handling.","zh":"特別脆弱的物品需要更慢和更小心地處理。"},{"en":"This phrase singles out the most delicate items.","zh":"這個短語特別指出最脆弱的物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"do them by hand","meaning":"手工處理它們","examples":[{"en":"The company will do fragile photos by hand.","zh":"公司會手工處理脆弱相片。"},{"en":"To do them by hand means to handle or process them manually rather than by machine.","zh":"do them by hand 是指人手處理，而不是用機器自動處理。"},{"en":"A tailor may sew delicate beads by hand because a machine could damage them.","zh":"裁縫可能手工縫上精細珠飾，因為機器可能會損壞它們。"},{"en":"Doing fragile work by hand gives more control and care.","zh":"手工處理脆弱工作可提供更多控制和小心。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts manual work with automatic processing.","zh":"這個短語把人手工作與自動處理作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"realise how precious","meaning":"明白……有多珍貴","examples":[{"en":"The company realises how precious old photos can be.","zh":"公司明白舊相片可以有多珍貴。"},{"en":"To realise how precious something is means to understand how valuable or emotionally important it is.","zh":"realise how precious something is 是指明白某物有多有價值或多有情感意義。"},{"en":"People often realise how precious family videos are after an older relative passes away.","zh":"年長親人離世後，人們常會明白家庭影片有多珍貴。"},{"en":"Understanding emotional value helps staff handle personal items with care.","zh":"明白情感價值有助職員小心處理私人物品。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on recognising importance.","zh":"這個短語著重認識某物的重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"old photos","meaning":"舊相片","examples":[{"en":"Old photos can be very precious to families.","zh":"舊相片對家庭來說可以非常珍貴。"},{"en":"Old photos are pictures taken a long time ago.","zh":"old photos 是很久以前拍攝的相片。"},{"en":"Old photos may show relatives, places, and events that no longer exist in the same way.","zh":"舊相片可能展示已不再一樣的親人、地方和事件。"},{"en":"Families preserve old photos because they hold memories and history.","zh":"家庭保存舊相片，因為它們承載回憶和歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to photos valued for age, memory, or personal meaning.","zh":"這個短語指因年代、回憶或個人意義而有價值的相片。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make changes to","meaning":"對……作出修改","examples":[{"en":"The company can make changes to a photo if the customer wants.","zh":"如果顧客想要，公司可以對相片作出修改。"},{"en":"To make changes to something means to alter or adjust it.","zh":"make changes to something 是指改動或調整某物。"},{"en":"A teacher may make changes to a worksheet after students find it too hard.","zh":"如果學生覺得工作紙太難，老師可能會對它作出修改。"},{"en":"Photo changes can improve appearance, remove distractions, or correct problems.","zh":"相片修改可以改善外觀、移除干擾或修正問題。"},{"en":"This phrase covers many types of editing.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋多種編輯。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"remove an object from","meaning":"從……移除物件","examples":[{"en":"The company can remove an object from a photo.","zh":"公司可以從相片中移除物件。"},{"en":"To remove an object from a photo means to edit the picture so that the object is no longer visible.","zh":"remove an object from a photo 是指編輯相片，使該物件不再可見。"},{"en":"A photographer may remove a rubbish bin from a wedding photo.","zh":"攝影師可能從婚禮相片中移除垃圾桶。"},{"en":"Removing an object can make the main subject clearer.","zh":"移除物件可以令主要主體更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific kind of photo editing.","zh":"這個短語描述一種具體相片編輯。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"alter the background","meaning":"改變背景","examples":[{"en":"The company can alter the background of a photo.","zh":"公司可以改變相片背景。"},{"en":"To alter the background means to change what appears behind the main subject.","zh":"alter the background 是指改變主要主體後面出現的內容。"},{"en":"A studio may alter the background of a portrait to make it look cleaner.","zh":"攝影工作室可能改變人像背景，使相片看起來更乾淨。"},{"en":"Changing the background can improve a photo, but it may also make it look less natural.","zh":"改變背景可以改善相片，但也可能令相片看起來不夠自然。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to editing the area behind the person or object.","zh":"這個短語指編輯人物或物件後方的區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be interested in","meaning":"對……感興趣","examples":[{"en":"The woman might be interested in changing some photos.","zh":"那位女士可能對修改一些相片感興趣。"},{"en":"To be interested in something means to want to know more about it or consider doing it.","zh":"be interested in something 是指想了解更多或考慮做某事。"},{"en":"A parent may be interested in a holiday course if it fits the child’s needs.","zh":"如果假期課程符合孩子需要，家長可能會感興趣。"},{"en":"Interest often starts when a service seems useful or relevant.","zh":"當服務看起來有用或相關，興趣通常便會開始。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean a final decision has already been made.","zh":"這個短語不代表已作出最終決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have a look through","meaning":"翻看","examples":[{"en":"The woman will have a look through the photos.","zh":"那位女士會翻看這些相片。"},{"en":"To have a look through something means to examine a set of things one by one, usually fairly quickly.","zh":"have a look through something 是指逐一查看一組物品，通常較快速。"},{"en":"A student may have a look through old notes before choosing what to revise.","zh":"學生可能在選擇溫習內容前翻看舊筆記。"},{"en":"Looking through photos helps people decide which ones need editing.","zh":"翻看相片有助人們決定哪些需要編輯。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when checking a collection.","zh":"這個短語常用於檢查一組物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"talking of","meaning":"說到……","examples":[{"en":"The woman says, “Talking of fixing photos,” before asking about focus.","zh":"那位女士在問對焦前說：「說到修復相片。」"},{"en":"Talking of something is used to move to a related topic.","zh":"talking of something 用來轉到相關主題。"},{"en":"Talking of homework, did you finish the science worksheet?","zh":"說到功課，你完成科學工作紙了嗎？"},{"en":"This phrase connects a new question to something just mentioned.","zh":"這個短語把新問題與剛提到的事情連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is conversational and helps change topic smoothly.","zh":"它較口語，能幫助自然轉題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fixing photos","meaning":"修復相片","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks about fixing photos that are not in focus.","zh":"那位女士詢問修復沒有對焦的相片。"},{"en":"Fixing photos means improving or correcting problems in pictures.","zh":"fixing photos 是指改善或修正相片中的問題。"},{"en":"A photo editor may fix photos by adjusting colour, brightness, or small marks.","zh":"相片編輯員可能透過調整顏色、亮度或小痕跡來修復相片。"},{"en":"Some photo problems can be fixed, but others may be impossible to repair completely.","zh":"有些相片問題可以修復，但有些可能無法完全修好。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and refers to photo restoration or editing.","zh":"這個短語較口語，指相片修復或編輯。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not properly in focus","meaning":"沒有正確對焦","examples":[{"en":"A few of the woman’s photos are not properly in focus.","zh":"那位女士有幾張相片沒有正確對焦。"},{"en":"Not properly in focus means the image is not sharp or clear.","zh":"not properly in focus 是指影像不銳利或不清楚。"},{"en":"A photo may be not properly in focus if the camera moved when it was taken.","zh":"如果拍攝時相機移動，相片可能沒有正確對焦。"},{"en":"Out-of-focus pictures can be hard to repair because the missing detail was never captured clearly.","zh":"失焦相片可能很難修復，因為缺失細節從未被清楚捕捉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a problem with sharpness.","zh":"這個短語描述清晰度問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make that better","meaning":"改善那個問題","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether the company can make the focus better.","zh":"那位女士問公司能否改善對焦問題。"},{"en":"To make that better means to improve that particular problem or situation.","zh":"make that better 是指改善那個特定問題或情況。"},{"en":"If a recording is too quiet, an editor may try to make that better.","zh":"如果錄音太細聲，編輯可能嘗試改善那個問題。"},{"en":"Some problems can be improved, while others cannot be fixed fully.","zh":"有些問題可以改善，而有些不能完全修復。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple and conversational.","zh":"這個短語簡單而口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"I’m afraid","meaning":"恐怕","examples":[{"en":"The employee says, “I’m afraid that’s one thing we can’t do.”","zh":"職員說：「恐怕那是我們做不到的一件事。」"},{"en":"I’m afraid is a polite way to introduce bad news or refusal.","zh":"I’m afraid 是禮貌地引入壞消息或拒絕的說法。"},{"en":"I’m afraid the office is closed today.","zh":"恐怕辦公室今天關門。"},{"en":"This phrase softens a negative answer and sounds more respectful.","zh":"這個短語令否定回答較委婉，聽起來更尊重對方。"},{"en":"It does not usually mean the speaker is frightened.","zh":"它通常不是指說話者感到害怕。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"one thing we cannot do","meaning":"我們做不到的一件事","examples":[{"en":"Improving focus is one thing the company cannot do.","zh":"改善對焦是公司做不到的一件事。"},{"en":"One thing we cannot do means one specific task or service is not possible for us.","zh":"one thing we cannot do 是指我們無法做到的一項具體任務或服務。"},{"en":"A repair shop may say replacing lost data is one thing it cannot do.","zh":"維修店可能說恢復遺失數據是他們做不到的一件事。"},{"en":"Explaining limits clearly prevents customers from expecting impossible results.","zh":"清楚解釋限制可以避免顧客期待不可能的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a clear boundary of the service.","zh":"這個短語指出服務的明確界線。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"any other information","meaning":"其他資料","examples":[{"en":"The employee asks whether there is any other information he can give.","zh":"職員問是否還有其他資料可以提供。"},{"en":"Any other information means any extra details not already mentioned.","zh":"any other information 是指尚未提及的任何額外資料。"},{"en":"A receptionist may ask if the visitor needs any other information before leaving.","zh":"接待員可能在訪客離開前問是否需要其他資料。"},{"en":"Offering more information helps customers feel fully supported.","zh":"提供更多資料可以令顧客感到得到充分支援。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful near the end of an enquiry.","zh":"這個短語適合用於查詢接近結束時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"how long will it all take?","meaning":"整個過程需要多久？","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks how long the whole process will take.","zh":"那位女士問整個過程需要多久。"},{"en":"How long will it all take? asks about the total time needed to finish everything.","zh":"how long will it all take? 是詢問完成所有事情所需的總時間。"},{"en":"A customer may ask how long a phone repair will take before leaving the device.","zh":"顧客交出電話前，可能會問維修需要多久。"},{"en":"Knowing the time needed helps people plan when they will receive the finished work.","zh":"知道所需時間有助人們計劃何時收到完成品。"},{"en":"This question focuses on duration from start to finish.","zh":"這個問題著重從開始到完成的時間長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"aim to","meaning":"目標是","examples":[{"en":"The company aims to get the copying done in ten days.","zh":"公司目標是在十天內完成複製工作。"},{"en":"To aim to do something means to plan or intend to achieve it.","zh":"aim to do something 是指計劃或打算達成某事。"},{"en":"A school may aim to reply to parent emails within two working days.","zh":"學校可能目標是在兩個工作天內回覆家長電郵。"},{"en":"An aim gives customers an expected target, though delays may still happen.","zh":"目標給顧客一個預期標準，雖然仍可能有延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a goal or intended standard.","zh":"這個短語描述目標或預定標準。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get the copying done","meaning":"完成複製工作","examples":[{"en":"The company aims to get the copying done in ten days.","zh":"公司目標是在十天內完成複製工作。"},{"en":"To get the copying done means to complete the copying work.","zh":"get the copying done 是指完成複製的工作。"},{"en":"A teacher may try to get the photocopying done before the lesson starts.","zh":"老師可能嘗試在上課前完成影印工作。"},{"en":"Getting a task done on time helps the next stage happen smoothly.","zh":"準時完成任務有助下一階段順利進行。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on finishing a practical job.","zh":"這個短語著重完成實際工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in ten days","meaning":"十天內","examples":[{"en":"The copying should be completed in ten days.","zh":"複製工作應在十天內完成。"},{"en":"In ten days means within a period of ten days.","zh":"in ten days 是指在十天這段時間內。"},{"en":"A passport office may say the document will be ready in ten days.","zh":"護照辦公室可能說文件會在十天內準備好。"},{"en":"Time limits help customers know when to expect the result.","zh":"時間限制幫助顧客知道何時可以期待結果。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a deadline or expected completion time.","zh":"這個短語提供截止時間或預期完成時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pack something up","meaning":"將某物包裝好","examples":[{"en":"The woman will get the photos packed up in a box.","zh":"那位女士會把相片裝進箱子包裝好。"},{"en":"To pack something up means to put it safely into a container for storage or transport.","zh":"pack something up 是指把某物安全地放進容器中，以便儲存或運送。"},{"en":"A student may pack up books before moving to a new flat.","zh":"學生搬到新單位前，可能會把書包裝好。"},{"en":"Careful packing protects fragile items during travel.","zh":"小心包裝可以在運送途中保護脆弱物品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparing items to be sent or moved.","zh":"這個短語描述準備寄送或搬運物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"post them off to","meaning":"將它們寄給……","examples":[{"en":"The woman will post the photos off to the company.","zh":"那位女士會將相片寄給公司。"},{"en":"To post them off to someone means to send them by mail to that person or organisation.","zh":"post them off to someone 是指用郵寄方式把它們寄給某人或機構。"},{"en":"A customer may post documents off to a passport office.","zh":"顧客可能把文件寄給護照辦公室。"},{"en":"Posting items off requires careful packaging and the correct address.","zh":"寄出物品需要小心包裝和正確地址。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English.","zh":"這個短語常見於英式英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"strong cardboard box","meaning":"堅固紙皮箱","examples":[{"en":"A strong cardboard box is best for sending the photos.","zh":"寄送相片最好使用堅固紙皮箱。"},{"en":"A strong cardboard box is a sturdy paper-based container used for packing items safely.","zh":"strong cardboard box 是用來安全包裝物品的結實紙製容器。"},{"en":"A strong cardboard box can protect books or photos better than a thin envelope.","zh":"堅固紙皮箱比薄信封更能保護書本或相片。"},{"en":"Strong packaging reduces the risk of bending, tearing, or crushing.","zh":"結實包裝可減少彎曲、撕裂或壓壞風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical packing material.","zh":"這個短語描述實用包裝材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"plastic ones","meaning":"膠箱；塑膠的那些","examples":[{"en":"Plastic boxes sometimes break in the post.","zh":"膠箱有時會在郵寄途中破裂。"},{"en":"Plastic ones means plastic boxes or containers, referring back to the items just mentioned.","zh":"plastic ones 是指塑膠箱或塑膠容器，回指剛提到的物品。"},{"en":"Glass cups are heavier, but plastic ones may scratch more easily.","zh":"玻璃杯較重，但塑膠的那些可能較容易刮花。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the noun when the listener already knows what is meant.","zh":"當聽者已知道所指物品時，這個短語避免重複名詞。"},{"en":"It is useful in comparisons between different materials or types.","zh":"它適合用於比較不同材料或類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"break in the post","meaning":"在郵寄途中破裂","examples":[{"en":"Plastic boxes sometimes break in the post.","zh":"膠箱有時會在郵寄途中破裂。"},{"en":"To break in the post means to be damaged while being sent through the mail.","zh":"break in the post 是指物品在郵寄過程中受損或破裂。"},{"en":"A fragile picture frame may break in the post if it is not packed properly.","zh":"如果包裝不當，脆弱相架可能會在郵寄途中破裂。"},{"en":"Items can break during delivery because parcels are moved, stacked, or dropped.","zh":"物品在送遞時可能因搬動、堆疊或跌落而破裂。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why strong packaging is important.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何堅固包裝很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8}],"ielts/listening/Practice 17/task-2":[{"front":"thank you for coming","meaning":"感謝大家前來","examples":[{"en":"The speaker thanks the parents for coming to the school.","zh":"講者感謝家長前來學校。"},{"en":"“Thank you for coming” is a polite way to show appreciation to people who have attended an event.","zh":"thank you for coming 是有禮地感謝人們出席活動的說法。"},{"en":"A principal may say, “Thank you for coming,” at the start of a parents’ evening.","zh":"校長可能在家長晚會開始時說：「感謝大家前來。」"},{"en":"This phrase helps create a respectful and welcoming atmosphere.","zh":"這個短語有助營造尊重而歡迎的氣氛。"},{"en":"It is commonly used at meetings, talks, ceremonies, and school events.","zh":"它常用於會議、講座、典禮和學校活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"bring someone up to date with","meaning":"向某人介紹……的最新情況","examples":[{"en":"The speaker wants to bring parents up to date with changes in the school.","zh":"講者想向家長介紹學校變化的最新情況。"},{"en":"To bring someone up to date with something means to give them the latest information about it.","zh":"bring someone up to date with something 指向某人提供某事的最新資料。"},{"en":"A teacher may bring parents up to date with their child’s progress before exams.","zh":"老師可能在考試前向家長介紹孩子學習進度的最新情況。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people may not know recent developments.","zh":"當人們可能不知道近期發展時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It focuses on updating someone, not teaching them from the beginning.","zh":"它聚焦於更新資訊，而不是從頭教起。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"affect your children","meaning":"影響你的孩子","examples":[{"en":"The school changes will affect the parents’ children.","zh":"學校變化會影響家長的孩子。"},{"en":"To affect your children means to influence their daily life, learning, comfort, or routine.","zh":"affect your children 指影響孩子的日常生活、學習、舒適程度或常規。"},{"en":"A new bus timetable may affect your children if they travel to school alone.","zh":"如果孩子獨自上學，新的巴士時間表可能會影響你的孩子。"},{"en":"School decisions matter to parents because they can directly affect their children.","zh":"學校決定對家長很重要，因為它們可以直接影響孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an impact on children.","zh":"這個短語描述對孩子的影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as you know","meaning":"如你所知","examples":[{"en":"As parents know, the school buildings date from various times.","zh":"如家長所知，學校建築建於不同年代。"},{"en":"As you know means the speaker believes the listener already knows the information.","zh":"as you know 指說話者相信聽者已知道該資料。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “As you know, the exam is next Friday.”","zh":"老師可能說：「如你所知，考試在下星期五。」"},{"en":"This phrase politely reminds people of shared knowledge.","zh":"這個短語有禮地提醒人們共同知道的資料。"},{"en":"It is often used before giving background information.","zh":"它常用於提供背景資料之前。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"date from","meaning":"建於；可追溯至","examples":[{"en":"The school buildings date from various times.","zh":"學校建築建於不同年代。"},{"en":"Date from means come from or were built in a particular period.","zh":"date from 指來自或建於某個特定時期。"},{"en":"Some parts of the old library date from the nineteenth century.","zh":"舊圖書館有些部分可追溯至十九世紀。"},{"en":"Buildings that date from different times may have different styles and conditions.","zh":"建於不同年代的建築可能有不同風格和狀況。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing history and architecture.","zh":"討論歷史和建築時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"various times","meaning":"不同年代","examples":[{"en":"The school buildings date from various times.","zh":"學校建築建於不同年代。"},{"en":"Various times means several different periods in history.","zh":"various times 指歷史上的幾個不同時期。"},{"en":"The museum contains objects from various times, including Roman and Victorian periods.","zh":"博物館收藏來自不同年代的物件，包括羅馬時期和維多利亞時期。"},{"en":"If buildings come from various times, they may need different kinds of repair.","zh":"如果建築來自不同年代，它們可能需要不同類型維修。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety in age or period.","zh":"這個短語強調年代或時期的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over a century old","meaning":"有一百多年歷史","examples":[{"en":"Dartfield House is over a century old.","zh":"Dartfield House 有一百多年歷史。"},{"en":"Over a century old means more than one hundred years old.","zh":"over a century old 指超過一百年歷史。"},{"en":"A school hall over a century old may need careful maintenance.","zh":"有一百多年歷史的學校禮堂可能需要仔細保養。"},{"en":"Old buildings can have historical value as well as practical problems.","zh":"古老建築可以有歷史價值，也可能有實際問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes great age.","zh":"這個短語描述年代久遠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be commissioned by","meaning":"由……委託建造","examples":[{"en":"Dartfield House was commissioned by a businessman.","zh":"Dartfield House 由一名商人委託建造。"},{"en":"Be commissioned by someone means be officially ordered or paid for by that person.","zh":"be commissioned by someone 指由某人正式委託或出資製作。"},{"en":"A statue may be commissioned by the local council for a public square.","zh":"地方議會可能委託製作一座雕像，放在公共廣場。"},{"en":"Commissioning a building usually means someone requested and funded its design.","zh":"委託建築通常表示有人要求並資助其設計。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used for art, buildings, and projects.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於藝術品、建築和項目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be intended as","meaning":"原本打算作為……","examples":[{"en":"Dartfield House was intended as Neville Richards’ family home.","zh":"Dartfield House 原本打算作為 Neville Richards 的家庭住宅。"},{"en":"Be intended as means be planned or designed for a particular purpose.","zh":"be intended as 指原本計劃或設計作某用途。"},{"en":"A room may be intended as a library but later used as an office.","zh":"一個房間原本可能打算作為圖書館，但後來用作辦公室。"},{"en":"The original purpose of a building may change over time.","zh":"建築的原本用途可能隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planned use.","zh":"這個短語描述原定用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"family home","meaning":"家庭住宅","examples":[{"en":"Dartfield House was intended as a family home.","zh":"Dartfield House 原本打算作為家庭住宅。"},{"en":"A family home is a house where a family lives together.","zh":"family home 指一家人共同居住的房屋。"},{"en":"A large family home may have several bedrooms, a garden, and shared living spaces.","zh":"大型家庭住宅可能有幾間睡房、花園和共用生活空間。"},{"en":"Calling it a family home shows it was first planned for private life, not school use.","zh":"稱它為家庭住宅，顯示它最初是為私人生活而設，不是作學校用途。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a domestic living place.","zh":"這個短語描述家居生活場所。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"before it was completed","meaning":"在完工之前","examples":[{"en":"Neville Richards died before the house was completed.","zh":"Neville Richards 在房子完工之前去世。"},{"en":"Before it was completed means before the building or project was finished.","zh":"before it was completed 指在建築或項目完成之前。"},{"en":"The architect left the project before it was completed.","zh":"建築師在項目完成之前離開了。"},{"en":"If someone dies before a house is completed, they never get to use it as planned.","zh":"如果某人在房子完工之前去世，他就無法按原計劃使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase marks something happening before the final stage.","zh":"這個短語標示某事發生在最後階段之前。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"heir","meaning":"繼承人","examples":[{"en":"His heir chose to sell Dartfield House to the local council.","zh":"他的繼承人選擇把 Dartfield House 賣給地方議會。"},{"en":"An heir is a person who receives property, money, or a title after someone dies.","zh":"heir 指某人去世後繼承財產、金錢或頭銜的人。"},{"en":"The businessman’s heir inherited the unfinished house.","zh":"那名商人的繼承人繼承了未完工的房子。"},{"en":"An heir may decide whether to keep, sell, or use inherited property.","zh":"繼承人可以決定保留、出售或使用繼承得來的物業。"},{"en":"This word describes someone who legally receives something from a deceased person.","zh":"這個字描述合法從逝者身上繼承某物的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"choose to","meaning":"選擇去……","examples":[{"en":"His heir chose to sell the house to the local council.","zh":"他的繼承人選擇把房子賣給地方議會。"},{"en":"Choose to do something means decide to do it instead of other possible actions.","zh":"choose to do something 指決定做某事，而不是做其他可能行動。"},{"en":"A family may choose to move closer to a child’s school.","zh":"一個家庭可能選擇搬近孩子的學校。"},{"en":"Choosing one option often means rejecting other possibilities.","zh":"選擇一個選項通常意味著拒絕其他可能性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a deliberate decision.","zh":"這個短語描述有意識的決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"local council","meaning":"地方議會","examples":[{"en":"The local council bought the house and turned it into offices.","zh":"地方議會買下房子並把它改成辦公室。"},{"en":"A local council is the government body responsible for services in a town or district.","zh":"local council 指負責城鎮或地區服務的地方政府機構。"},{"en":"The local council may manage roads, libraries, planning permission, and public buildings.","zh":"地方議會可能管理道路、圖書館、規劃許可和公共建築。"},{"en":"If a local council buys a building, it may use it for community or administrative purposes.","zh":"如果地方議會購買一座建築，它可能用作社區或行政用途。"},{"en":"This phrase describes local government.","zh":"這個短語描述地方政府。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"turn something into","meaning":"把……改成……","examples":[{"en":"The local council turned the house into offices.","zh":"地方議會把房子改成辦公室。"},{"en":"To turn something into something else means to change its use, form, or character.","zh":"turn something into something else 指改變某物的用途、形式或性質。"},{"en":"A school may turn an old classroom into a computer room.","zh":"學校可能把舊課室改成電腦室。"},{"en":"Turning a house into offices changes it from private living space to workplace.","zh":"把房子改成辦公室，會令它由私人居住空間變成工作場所。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transformation.","zh":"這個短語描述轉變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a later plan to","meaning":"後來一項……的計劃","examples":[{"en":"A later plan to convert the building into a tourist information centre failed.","zh":"後來一項把建築改建成遊客資訊中心的計劃失敗了。"},{"en":"A later plan to do something means a plan made after an earlier event or decision.","zh":"a later plan to do something 指在較早事件或決定之後提出的計劃。"},{"en":"A later plan to build a sports hall was delayed because costs increased.","zh":"後來一項興建體育館的計劃因成本上升而延遲。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show the sequence of plans over time.","zh":"這個短語有助顯示計劃隨時間的先後次序。"},{"en":"It introduces a plan that came after the first use or idea.","zh":"它引出最初用途或想法之後出現的計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"convert something into","meaning":"把……改建成……","examples":[{"en":"There was a plan to convert the building into a tourist information centre.","zh":"曾有計劃把這座建築改建成遊客資訊中心。"},{"en":"To convert something into something else means to change it so it can be used for a new purpose.","zh":"convert something into something else 指改變某物，使它可作新用途。"},{"en":"An old factory can be converted into flats.","zh":"舊工廠可以被改建成住宅單位。"},{"en":"Conversion usually requires building work, planning, and money.","zh":"改建通常需要工程、規劃和資金。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for buildings and spaces.","zh":"這個短語常用於建築和空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tourist information centre","meaning":"遊客資訊中心","examples":[{"en":"The building was once planned as a tourist information centre.","zh":"這座建築曾計劃用作遊客資訊中心。"},{"en":"A tourist information centre is a place where visitors can get maps, advice, and local travel information.","zh":"tourist information centre 指遊客可取得地圖、建議和本地旅遊資訊的地方。"},{"en":"A tourist information centre may tell visitors about hotels, museums, and transport.","zh":"遊客資訊中心可能告訴訪客酒店、博物館和交通資料。"},{"en":"Such centres help tourists understand and enjoy an unfamiliar place.","zh":"這類中心幫助遊客了解並享受陌生地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a public service for visitors.","zh":"這個短語描述為訪客而設的公共服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"come about","meaning":"實現；發生","examples":[{"en":"The plan to convert the building did not come about.","zh":"改建這座建築的計劃沒有實現。"},{"en":"Come about means happen or become real.","zh":"come about 指發生或成為現實。"},{"en":"The new playground did not come about until parents raised enough money.","zh":"新遊樂場直到家長籌得足夠資金後才實現。"},{"en":"If a plan does not come about, it remains only an idea.","zh":"如果計劃沒有實現，它就仍只是想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether something actually happens.","zh":"這個短語描述某事是否實際發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"through lack of money","meaning":"由於缺乏資金","examples":[{"en":"The plan did not come about through lack of money.","zh":"該計劃由於缺乏資金而沒有實現。"},{"en":"Through lack of money means because there was not enough funding.","zh":"through lack of money 指因資金不足。"},{"en":"The school trip was cancelled through lack of money.","zh":"學校旅行由於缺乏資金而取消。"},{"en":"Even good ideas may fail if there is not enough money to support them.","zh":"即使是好想法，如果沒有足夠資金支持，也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase gives financial shortage as the reason.","zh":"這個短語把資金短缺列為原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"instead","meaning":"相反；取而代之","examples":[{"en":"Instead, Dartfield House formed the nucleus of the school.","zh":"相反，Dartfield House 成為學校的核心。"},{"en":"Instead means in place of the thing just mentioned.","zh":"instead 指取代剛才提到的事情。"},{"en":"The class could not go outside, so they watched a science video instead.","zh":"班級不能到室外，所以改為觀看科學影片。"},{"en":"This word shows that one plan was replaced by another result.","zh":"這個字顯示一個計劃被另一個結果取代。"},{"en":"It is useful when contrasting what happened with what was planned.","zh":"對比實際發生與原本計劃時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"form the nucleus of","meaning":"成為……的核心","examples":[{"en":"Dartfield House formed the nucleus of the school.","zh":"Dartfield House 成為學校的核心。"},{"en":"To form the nucleus of something means to become its central or most important part.","zh":"form the nucleus of something 指成為某事的中心或最重要部分。"},{"en":"A small reading group may form the nucleus of a new school library club.","zh":"小型閱讀小組可能成為新學校圖書館學會的核心。"},{"en":"The nucleus is the part around which other things grow or develop.","zh":"核心是其他事物圍繞其成長或發展的部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the central starting point of a larger development.","zh":"這個短語描述較大發展的中心起點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"open 40 years ago","meaning":"40年前開辦","examples":[{"en":"The school opened 40 years ago.","zh":"學校40年前開辦。"},{"en":"Open 40 years ago means began operating forty years before now.","zh":"open 40 years ago 指在現在之前40年開始營運。"},{"en":"The community centre opened twenty years ago and has served many families.","zh":"社區中心20年前開辦，服務了許多家庭。"},{"en":"Knowing when a school opened helps people understand its history.","zh":"知道學校何時開辦，有助人理解其歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the age of an organisation from its starting point.","zh":"這個短語從起點說明組織的年齡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as the local population has increased","meaning":"隨着本地人口增加","examples":[{"en":"The school has grown as the local population has increased.","zh":"隨着本地人口增加，學校也發展起來。"},{"en":"As the local population has increased means while or because more people have come to live in the area.","zh":"as the local population has increased 指隨着或因為更多人住到該區。"},{"en":"A town may need more buses as the local population increases.","zh":"隨着本地人口增加，城鎮可能需要更多巴士。"},{"en":"More local families usually mean more school places are needed.","zh":"更多本地家庭通常意味著需要更多學額。"},{"en":"This phrase links population growth with another change.","zh":"這個短語把人口增長與另一個變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lower school site","meaning":"低年級校區","examples":[{"en":"The speaker gives news about the lower school site.","zh":"講者提供低年級校區的消息。"},{"en":"A lower school site is the part of a school used by younger pupils.","zh":"lower school site 指供較年幼學生使用的學校部分。"},{"en":"The lower school site may have smaller classrooms and play areas for younger children.","zh":"低年級校區可能有較小課室和適合年幼孩子的遊樂區。"},{"en":"Separating lower and upper school sites can affect travel and supervision.","zh":"分開低年級和高年級校區會影響交通和監督。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the campus area for younger year groups.","zh":"這個短語描述供較低年級使用的校園區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be separated from","meaning":"與……分隔開","examples":[{"en":"The lower school site is separated from the main site by a road.","zh":"低年級校區與主校區被一條道路分隔開。"},{"en":"Be separated from something means be divided or kept apart from it.","zh":"be separated from something 指與某物分開或隔開。"},{"en":"The sports field is separated from the classroom block by a fence.","zh":"運動場與課室大樓被圍欄分隔開。"},{"en":"A road between two school sites can make movement less convenient.","zh":"兩個校區之間有道路，會令往來較不方便。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical distance or division.","zh":"這個短語描述實際距離或分隔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"main site","meaning":"主校區","examples":[{"en":"The lower school site is separated from the main site by a road.","zh":"低年級校區與主校區被一條道路分隔開。"},{"en":"The main site is the principal or largest campus area of a school.","zh":"main site 指學校主要或最大的校園區域。"},{"en":"The main site may contain the hall, offices, library, and older pupils’ classrooms.","zh":"主校區可能包括禮堂、辦公室、圖書館和較高年級課室。"},{"en":"Moving younger pupils to the main site can bring the school together in one place.","zh":"把年幼學生搬到主校區，可以把學校集中在一個地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the central campus location.","zh":"這個短語描述中心校園位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"planning permission","meaning":"規劃許可","examples":[{"en":"Planning permission has been granted for both sites.","zh":"兩個校區均已獲批規劃許可。"},{"en":"Planning permission is official approval to build, develop, or change land or buildings.","zh":"planning permission 指建造、發展或改變土地及建築的官方批准。"},{"en":"A school needs planning permission before constructing a new classroom block.","zh":"學校興建新課室大樓前需要規劃許可。"},{"en":"Without planning permission, building work may not legally begin.","zh":"沒有規劃許可，建築工程可能不能合法開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in construction and local government.","zh":"這個短語常見於建築和地方政府語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be granted for","meaning":"就……獲批","examples":[{"en":"Planning permission has been granted for development of both sites.","zh":"兩個校區的發展已獲批規劃許可。"},{"en":"Be granted for something means be officially given for a particular purpose.","zh":"be granted for something 指就某特定目的獲得正式批准或給予。"},{"en":"Funding may be granted for repairing the school roof.","zh":"學校屋頂維修可能獲批資助。"},{"en":"When permission is granted for a project, the project can move forward legally.","zh":"當項目獲批許可，就可以合法推進。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official approval being given.","zh":"這個短語描述正式批准被給予。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"development of both sites","meaning":"兩個校區的發展","examples":[{"en":"Planning permission has been granted for development of both sites.","zh":"兩個校區的發展已獲批規劃許可。"},{"en":"Development of both sites means building work or improvement planned for the two locations.","zh":"development of both sites 指兩個地點計劃中的建築工程或改善。"},{"en":"The development of both sites may include new classrooms and new housing.","zh":"兩個校區的發展可能包括新課室和新住宅。"},{"en":"When two sites are developed together, planning must consider how each affects the other.","zh":"當兩個地點一起發展，規劃必須考慮彼此影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changes to two pieces of land.","zh":"這個短語描述兩塊土地的變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"move to new buildings","meaning":"搬到新建築","examples":[{"en":"The lower school will move to new buildings on the main site.","zh":"低年級學校將搬到主校區的新建築。"},{"en":"Move to new buildings means transfer classes, staff, or pupils into newly built spaces.","zh":"move to new buildings 指把課堂、職員或學生遷到新建成的空間。"},{"en":"A department may move to new buildings after old classrooms become too small.","zh":"當舊課室太小，某部門可能搬到新建築。"},{"en":"Moving to new buildings can improve facilities and reduce travel between sites.","zh":"搬到新建築可以改善設施，並減少校區之間往來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relocation to newly constructed premises.","zh":"這個短語描述遷往新建成場所。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be constructed on","meaning":"建於……","examples":[{"en":"New buildings will be constructed on the main site.","zh":"新建築將建於主校區。"},{"en":"Be constructed on means be built on a particular piece of land.","zh":"be constructed on 指建造在某塊特定土地上。"},{"en":"A new sports hall may be constructed on the edge of the school field.","zh":"新體育館可能建於學校操場邊緣。"},{"en":"Where buildings are constructed affects access, noise, and future use.","zh":"建築建於何處會影響出入、噪音和未來使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the location of building work.","zh":"這個短語描述建築工程的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"developers","meaning":"發展商","examples":[{"en":"Developers will construct houses on the lower school site.","zh":"發展商將在低年級校區興建住宅。"},{"en":"Developers are companies or people who build houses, offices, or other property projects.","zh":"developers 指建造住宅、辦公室或其他物業項目的公司或人士。"},{"en":"Developers may buy land and turn it into flats or shops.","zh":"發展商可能購買土地，並把它改成住宅單位或商店。"},{"en":"Their work can change how a local area looks and is used.","zh":"他們的工作可以改變本區外觀和用途。"},{"en":"This word describes people or companies involved in property development.","zh":"這個字描述參與物業發展的人或公司。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"construct houses","meaning":"興建住宅","examples":[{"en":"Developers will construct houses on the existing lower school site.","zh":"發展商將在現有低年級校區興建住宅。"},{"en":"To construct houses means to build homes.","zh":"construct houses 指建造住宅。"},{"en":"A developer may construct houses on land that was once used for offices.","zh":"發展商可能在曾用作辦公室的土地上興建住宅。"},{"en":"Constructing houses can provide more homes but may change the character of an area.","zh":"興建住宅可以提供更多居所，但也可能改變地區特色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes residential building work.","zh":"這個短語描述住宅建築工程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"existing lower school site","meaning":"現有低年級校區","examples":[{"en":"Houses will be built on the existing lower school site.","zh":"住宅將建於現有低年級校區。"},{"en":"The existing lower school site is the current place where the lower school is located.","zh":"existing lower school site 指低年級學校目前所在的地方。"},{"en":"Once pupils move, the existing lower school site may become available for another use.","zh":"學生搬走後，現有低年級校區可能可作其他用途。"},{"en":"“Existing” shows that the site is already in use now.","zh":"“existing” 顯示該校區現在已在使用。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the present lower-school land.","zh":"這個短語指出目前的低年級校園土地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"work on","meaning":"……的工程","examples":[{"en":"Work on the new school buildings should start soon.","zh":"新校舍的工程應該很快開始。"},{"en":"Work on something means construction, repair, or development activity for that project.","zh":"work on something 指某項目的建築、維修或發展活動。"},{"en":"Work on the new library will begin during the summer holiday.","zh":"新圖書館的工程將於暑假期間開始。"},{"en":"Building work may affect noise, access, and daily routines.","zh":"建築工程可能影響噪音、出入和日常安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes project activity.","zh":"這個短語描述項目活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"within the next few months","meaning":"在未來幾個月內","examples":[{"en":"Work should start within the next few months.","zh":"工程應在未來幾個月內開始。"},{"en":"Within the next few months means before several months have passed from now.","zh":"within the next few months 指從現在起幾個月過去之前。"},{"en":"The school expects to publish the new timetable within the next few months.","zh":"學校預計在未來幾個月內公布新時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a near-future time frame without an exact date.","zh":"這個短語給出接近未來的時間範圍，但沒有確切日期。"},{"en":"It is useful when plans are expected soon but not scheduled precisely.","zh":"當計劃預計很快發生但未精確安排時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"imminent change","meaning":"即將發生的變化","examples":[{"en":"A more imminent change concerns the catering facilities.","zh":"一項更即將發生的變化涉及餐飲設施。"},{"en":"An imminent change is a change that will happen very soon.","zh":"imminent change 指很快會發生的變化。"},{"en":"Parents should be told about imminent changes to school transport.","zh":"家長應被告知校車安排即將發生的變化。"},{"en":"If a change is imminent, people need time to prepare immediately.","zh":"如果變化即將發生，人們需要立即準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a near and expected change.","zh":"這個短語描述接近並預期會發生的變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"concern","meaning":"涉及","examples":[{"en":"The change concerns the catering facilities and the canteen.","zh":"這項變化涉及餐飲設施和飯堂。"},{"en":"Concern means be about or relate to something.","zh":"concern 指關於或涉及某事。"},{"en":"The notice concerns changes to the school timetable.","zh":"該通告涉及學校時間表的改動。"},{"en":"This meaning of “concern” is different from “worry”.","zh":"這裏的 “concern” 與「擔心」意思不同。"},{"en":"It is often used in formal explanations.","zh":"它常用於正式解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"catering facilities","meaning":"餐飲設施","examples":[{"en":"The school is changing its catering facilities.","zh":"學校正在改變其餐飲設施。"},{"en":"Catering facilities are the places and equipment used to prepare, serve, or sell food.","zh":"catering facilities 指用來準備、供應或售賣食物的地方和設備。"},{"en":"A school’s catering facilities may include kitchens, counters, fridges, and eating areas.","zh":"學校餐飲設施可能包括廚房、櫃位、雪櫃和用餐區。"},{"en":"Better catering facilities can reduce waiting time and improve food choice.","zh":"更好的餐飲設施可以減少等候時間並改善食物選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes food-service arrangements.","zh":"這個短語描述供餐安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"canteen","meaning":"飯堂","examples":[{"en":"The school canteen is always busy during lunch.","zh":"學校飯堂在午餐時間總是很忙。"},{"en":"A canteen is a place in a school, college, or workplace where people buy and eat food.","zh":"canteen 指學校、學院或工作場所中人們購買和進食的地方。"},{"en":"Pupils may queue in the canteen for hot meals.","zh":"學生可能在飯堂排隊購買熱餐。"},{"en":"A busy canteen needs good organisation to serve people quickly.","zh":"忙碌的飯堂需要良好組織才能快速供餐。"},{"en":"This word describes a shared dining place.","zh":"這個字描述共用用餐地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"throughout the lunch period","meaning":"整個午膳時段","examples":[{"en":"The canteen is busy throughout the lunch period.","zh":"飯堂在整個午膳時段都很忙。"},{"en":"Throughout the lunch period means during the whole time set aside for lunch.","zh":"throughout the lunch period 指在整段午餐時間內。"},{"en":"The playground is noisy throughout the break period.","zh":"操場在整個小息時段都很嘈吵。"},{"en":"If a canteen is busy throughout lunch, there is no quiet moment for pupils to avoid queues.","zh":"如果飯堂整個午餐時間都很忙，學生就沒有安靜時段避開人龍。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses something continuing for the entire period.","zh":"這個短語強調某事持續整段時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"full to capacity","meaning":"滿座；達到最高容量","examples":[{"en":"The canteen is often full to capacity.","zh":"飯堂常常滿座。"},{"en":"Full to capacity means completely full, with no extra space available.","zh":"full to capacity 指完全滿了，沒有額外空間。"},{"en":"The school hall was full to capacity during the concert.","zh":"學校禮堂在音樂會期間滿座。"},{"en":"If a room is full to capacity, safety and comfort may become concerns.","zh":"如果房間達到最高容量，安全和舒適可能成為問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching the maximum possible number.","zh":"這個短語描述達到最高可容納人數。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"food on offer","meaning":"提供的食物","examples":[{"en":"Many pupils like the food on offer in the canteen.","zh":"許多學生喜歡飯堂提供的食物。"},{"en":"Food on offer means the food available for people to choose or buy.","zh":"food on offer 指可供人選擇或購買的食物。"},{"en":"The food on offer at the school fair included noodles, sandwiches, and fruit.","zh":"學校賣物會提供的食物包括麵、三文治和水果。"},{"en":"If the food on offer is varied, more pupils may find something they like.","zh":"如果提供的食物多元，更多學生可能找到喜歡的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes available food choices.","zh":"這個短語描述可供選擇的食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"serving point","meaning":"供餐點","examples":[{"en":"The old canteen has only one serving point.","zh":"舊飯堂只有一個供餐點。"},{"en":"A serving point is a counter or area where food is given or sold.","zh":"serving point 指派發或售賣食物的櫃位或區域。"},{"en":"If a canteen has only one serving point, queues can become very long.","zh":"如果飯堂只有一個供餐點，人龍可能變得很長。"},{"en":"More serving points can help pupils get food more quickly.","zh":"更多供餐點可以幫助學生更快取得食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a food-service location.","zh":"這個短語描述供餐位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"wait a considerable time","meaning":"等候相當長時間","examples":[{"en":"Most pupils have to wait a considerable time to be served.","zh":"大多數學生必須等候相當長時間才獲供餐。"},{"en":"Wait a considerable time means wait for quite a long period.","zh":"wait a considerable time 指等候相當長一段時間。"},{"en":"Patients may have to wait a considerable time in a busy clinic.","zh":"病人可能在繁忙診所等候相當長時間。"},{"en":"Long waiting time can make pupils rushed or frustrated.","zh":"長時間等候會令學生匆忙或沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a noticeably long wait.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯很長的等待。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be served","meaning":"獲供餐；獲服務","examples":[{"en":"Pupils have to wait to be served.","zh":"學生必須等候才獲供餐。"},{"en":"Be served means receive food, drink, or help from staff.","zh":"be served 指從職員那裏獲得食物、飲品或協助。"},{"en":"Customers in a café wait at the counter to be served.","zh":"咖啡店顧客在櫃位等候服務。"},{"en":"In a canteen, pupils are served when staff give them their meal.","zh":"在飯堂中，職員把餐點給學生時，學生就是獲供餐。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving service.","zh":"這個短語描述獲得服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"obviously unsatisfactory","meaning":"顯然不理想","examples":[{"en":"The long waiting time is obviously unsatisfactory.","zh":"長時間等候顯然不理想。"},{"en":"Obviously unsatisfactory means clearly not good enough or not acceptable.","zh":"obviously unsatisfactory 指明顯不夠好或不可接受。"},{"en":"A broken heating system in winter is obviously unsatisfactory for pupils.","zh":"冬天暖氣系統壞了，對學生來說顯然不理想。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the problem is clear and does not need much argument.","zh":"這個短語顯示問題很清楚，不需要太多爭辯。"},{"en":"It is formal and critical.","zh":"它較正式，並帶批評意味。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hardly finished","meaning":"幾乎剛完成","examples":[{"en":"Pupils may have hardly finished lunch before lessons start.","zh":"學生可能幾乎剛吃完午餐，下午課堂就開始。"},{"en":"Hardly finished means only just finished, with almost no time left.","zh":"hardly finished 指才剛完成，幾乎沒有剩餘時間。"},{"en":"A student may have hardly finished changing clothes before the next class begins.","zh":"學生可能幾乎剛換完衣服，下一堂課就開始。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests rushing and lack of time.","zh":"這個短語暗示匆忙和時間不足。"},{"en":"It is used when an action is completed only at the last moment.","zh":"當某行動在最後一刻才完成時，會使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"afternoon lessons","meaning":"下午課堂","examples":[{"en":"Afternoon lessons start soon after lunch.","zh":"下午課堂在午餐後不久開始。"},{"en":"Afternoon lessons are classes held after the lunch period.","zh":"afternoon lessons 指午餐時段後舉行的課堂。"},{"en":"Pupils may find afternoon lessons difficult if they have not had enough time to eat.","zh":"如果學生沒有足夠時間吃飯，下午課堂可能會較難集中。"},{"en":"The timing of lunch can affect concentration in afternoon lessons.","zh":"午餐時間安排會影響下午課堂的專注力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the second part of the school day.","zh":"這個短語描述上學日的後半部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"come into use","meaning":"投入使用","examples":[{"en":"The new Food Hall will come into use next week.","zh":"新 Food Hall 將於下星期投入使用。"},{"en":"Come into use means start being used.","zh":"come into use 指開始被使用。"},{"en":"The new science laboratory will come into use after the safety checks.","zh":"新科學實驗室完成安全檢查後會投入使用。"},{"en":"When a facility comes into use, people can begin using it for its intended purpose.","zh":"當設施投入使用，人們便可以開始按原定用途使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the start of practical operation.","zh":"這個短語描述實際運作的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"several serving areas","meaning":"多個供餐區","examples":[{"en":"The Food Hall will have several serving areas.","zh":"Food Hall 將有多個供餐區。"},{"en":"Several serving areas means more than two places where food can be collected or bought.","zh":"several serving areas 指有多於兩個取餐或購買食物的地方。"},{"en":"A large canteen may use several serving areas to reduce queues.","zh":"大飯堂可能使用多個供餐區來減少人龍。"},{"en":"Different serving areas can offer different kinds of food.","zh":"不同供餐區可以提供不同種類食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes multiple food-service sections.","zh":"這個短語描述多個供餐部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in a minute","meaning":"稍後；很快","examples":[{"en":"The speaker will give more details in a minute.","zh":"講者稍後會提供更多細節。"},{"en":"In a minute means very soon, usually after a short delay.","zh":"in a minute 指很快，通常在短暫延遲之後。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “I’ll explain the homework in a minute.”","zh":"老師可能說：「我稍後會解釋功課。」"},{"en":"This phrase tells listeners that the information is coming shortly.","zh":"這個短語告訴聽眾資料很快會來。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken explanations.","zh":"它常見於口頭解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"smooth running of","meaning":"……的順利運作","examples":[{"en":"Parents can help with the smooth running of the Food Hall.","zh":"家長可以幫助 Food Hall 順利運作。"},{"en":"The smooth running of something means its efficient and trouble-free operation.","zh":"smooth running of something 指某事有效率而少出問題地運作。"},{"en":"Clear rules help with the smooth running of a school trip.","zh":"清晰規則有助學校旅行順利運作。"},{"en":"If everyone knows what to do, a busy system can run more smoothly.","zh":"如果每個人都知道要做甚麼，繁忙系統就能更順暢運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised and successful operation.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織而成功的運作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"discuss with","meaning":"與……討論","examples":[{"en":"Parents should discuss food choices with their children each morning.","zh":"家長應每天早上與孩子討論食物選擇。"},{"en":"To discuss something with someone means to talk about it together and exchange ideas.","zh":"discuss something with someone 指一起談論某事並交換想法。"},{"en":"Parents may discuss homework routines with their children at the weekend.","zh":"家長可能在週末與孩子討論功課規律。"},{"en":"Discussing choices in advance can prevent confusion later.","zh":"事先討論選擇可以避免之後混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared decision-making through conversation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過對話共同作決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"type of food","meaning":"食物種類","examples":[{"en":"Children should decide which type of food they want.","zh":"孩子應決定自己想要哪種食物。"},{"en":"Type of food means a category or kind of food.","zh":"type of food 指食物的類別或種類。"},{"en":"Vegetarian food, Italian food, and hot meals are different types of food.","zh":"素食、意大利菜和熱餐都是不同食物種類。"},{"en":"Knowing the type of food pupils want helps them go to the correct counter.","zh":"知道學生想要哪種食物，有助他們前往正確櫃位。"},{"en":"This phrase describes food categories.","zh":"這個短語描述食物分類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"go straight to","meaning":"直接前往……","examples":[{"en":"Pupils can go straight to the relevant serving point.","zh":"學生可以直接前往相關供餐點。"},{"en":"Go straight to means go directly to a place without stopping elsewhere.","zh":"go straight to 指不在其他地方停留，直接去某地方。"},{"en":"After arriving at school, pupils should go straight to their classrooms.","zh":"學生到校後應直接前往課室。"},{"en":"Going straight to the right place saves time.","zh":"直接前往正確地方可以節省時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct movement.","zh":"這個短語描述直接移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"relevant serving point","meaning":"相關供餐點","examples":[{"en":"Pupils should go to the relevant serving point.","zh":"學生應前往相關供餐點。"},{"en":"The relevant serving point is the food counter that matches the pupil’s chosen meal.","zh":"relevant serving point 指與學生所選餐點相符的供餐櫃位。"},{"en":"A pupil who wants Italian food should go to the relevant serving point for that cuisine.","zh":"想吃意大利菜的學生應去相關菜式的供餐點。"},{"en":"Clear signs help pupils find the relevant serving point quickly.","zh":"清晰標示幫助學生快速找到相關供餐點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the correct food counter for a particular choice.","zh":"這個短語描述特定選擇的正確供餐櫃位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"junk food","meaning":"垃圾食物","examples":[{"en":"There will not be any junk food in the Food Hall.","zh":"Food Hall 不會有任何垃圾食物。"},{"en":"Junk food is food that is usually high in fat, sugar, or salt and low in nutrition.","zh":"junk food 指通常高脂、高糖或高鹽、營養較低的食物。"},{"en":"Crisps, sweets, and sugary drinks are often called junk food.","zh":"薯片、糖果和含糖飲品常被稱為垃圾食物。"},{"en":"Schools may avoid junk food to encourage healthier eating habits.","zh":"學校可能避免提供垃圾食物，以鼓勵較健康飲食習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unhealthy snack-style food.","zh":"這個短語描述不健康的小食類食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"current system","meaning":"現行制度","examples":[{"en":"There is no change to the current system of paying for lunches.","zh":"支付午餐費的現行制度沒有改變。"},{"en":"The current system is the method or arrangement being used now.","zh":"current system 指目前正在使用的方法或安排。"},{"en":"The current system for borrowing books uses student cards.","zh":"現行借書制度使用學生證。"},{"en":"Saying there is no change reassures parents that they can continue as before.","zh":"說明沒有改變，可以安撫家長繼續照舊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the existing arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述現有安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pay for lunches","meaning":"支付午餐費","examples":[{"en":"Parents pay for lunches by topping up a payment card.","zh":"家長透過為付款卡充值來支付午餐費。"},{"en":"To pay for lunches means to provide money for children’s midday meals.","zh":"pay for lunches 指為孩子的午餐提供款項。"},{"en":"Some schools ask parents to pay for lunches online each week.","zh":"有些學校要求家長每星期在網上支付午餐費。"},{"en":"A simple payment system helps pupils buy food quickly.","zh":"簡單付款系統有助學生快速購買食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes covering the cost of school meals.","zh":"這個短語描述支付學校餐膳費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"top up","meaning":"增值；充值","examples":[{"en":"Parents top up their child’s electronic payment card online.","zh":"家長在網上為孩子的電子付款卡充值。"},{"en":"To top up means to add more money or credit to an account or card.","zh":"top up 指向帳戶或卡加入更多金錢或額度。"},{"en":"A student may top up a travel card before taking the bus.","zh":"學生乘巴士前可能為交通卡增值。"},{"en":"Topping up online can save parents from sending cash to school.","zh":"網上充值可以令家長不用把現金帶到學校。"},{"en":"This phrase is common for payment cards and mobile accounts.","zh":"這個短語常用於付款卡和手機帳戶。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"electronic payment card","meaning":"電子付款卡","examples":[{"en":"Pupils use an electronic payment card for lunches.","zh":"學生使用電子付款卡支付午餐費。"},{"en":"An electronic payment card is a card used to pay without cash.","zh":"electronic payment card 指用來無現金付款的卡。"},{"en":"A school may give each pupil an electronic payment card for the canteen.","zh":"學校可能給每名學生一張飯堂電子付款卡。"},{"en":"Electronic cards can make payments faster and easier to track.","zh":"電子卡可以令付款更快，也更容易追蹤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a digital payment tool.","zh":"這個短語描述數碼付款工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"online","meaning":"網上","examples":[{"en":"Parents can top up the payment card online.","zh":"家長可以在網上為付款卡增值。"},{"en":"Online means using the internet.","zh":"online 指使用互聯網。"},{"en":"Parents can check school notices online instead of waiting for paper letters.","zh":"家長可以在網上查看學校通告，而不用等紙本信件。"},{"en":"Online systems can be convenient because they are available from home.","zh":"網上系統很方便，因為在家也可以使用。"},{"en":"This word describes actions done through the internet.","zh":"這個字描述透過互聯網完成的行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"wonder what will happen to","meaning":"想知道……會怎樣","examples":[{"en":"Parents may wonder what will happen to the old canteen.","zh":"家長可能想知道舊飯堂會怎樣。"},{"en":"Wonder what will happen to something means feel curious or uncertain about its future.","zh":"wonder what will happen to something 指對某物的未來感到好奇或不確定。"},{"en":"Pupils may wonder what will happen to the old library after the new one opens.","zh":"新圖書館開放後，學生可能想知道舊圖書館會怎樣。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a question about future use or change.","zh":"這個短語引出關於未來用途或變化的問題。"},{"en":"It shows uncertainty rather than a definite problem.","zh":"它顯示不確定，而不是明確問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"old canteen","meaning":"舊飯堂","examples":[{"en":"The old canteen will still have tables and chairs.","zh":"舊飯堂仍會有桌椅。"},{"en":"The old canteen is the previous dining area before the new Food Hall opens.","zh":"old canteen 指新 Food Hall 開放前原本的用餐區。"},{"en":"Pupils may use the old canteen if they bring lunch from home.","zh":"如果學生從家中帶午餐，可能會使用舊飯堂。"},{"en":"Old facilities can still be useful even after a newer one opens.","zh":"即使新設施開放，舊設施仍可以有用途。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the former food area.","zh":"這個短語描述原本的供餐區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"food from home","meaning":"從家中帶來的食物","examples":[{"en":"Pupils can eat lunch they have brought from home.","zh":"學生可以吃自己從家中帶來的午餐。"},{"en":"Food from home means food prepared at home and brought to school.","zh":"food from home 指在家中準備並帶到學校的食物。"},{"en":"A pupil with allergies may prefer food from home.","zh":"有過敏的學生可能較喜歡從家中帶來的食物。"},{"en":"Bringing food from home can save money and give families more control over meals.","zh":"從家中帶食物可以省錢，也讓家庭更能控制餐點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes packed lunches or home-prepared food.","zh":"這個短語描述飯盒或家中準備的食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"eventually","meaning":"最終","examples":[{"en":"Eventually, part of the canteen may be used for storage.","zh":"最終，飯堂的一部分可能用作儲物。"},{"en":"Eventually means finally, after some time or after other things happen first.","zh":"eventually 指經過一段時間或其他事情先發生後，最後。"},{"en":"The school may eventually replace all paper forms with online forms.","zh":"學校最終可能以網上表格取代所有紙本表格。"},{"en":"This word suggests that the change will not happen immediately.","zh":"這個字暗示改變不會立即發生。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing a possible later result.","zh":"描述可能的較後結果時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"use part of","meaning":"使用……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"The school may use part of the canteen for storage.","zh":"學校可能使用飯堂的一部分作儲物。"},{"en":"Use part of something means use only one section, not the whole thing.","zh":"use part of something 指只使用其中一部分，而不是整體。"},{"en":"A classroom may use part of a cupboard for sports equipment.","zh":"課室可能使用櫃子的一部分存放運動器材。"},{"en":"Using only part of a space leaves the rest available for another purpose.","zh":"只使用空間的一部分，會留下其餘部分作其他用途。"},{"en":"This phrase describes partial use.","zh":"這個短語描述部分使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"storage","meaning":"儲物","examples":[{"en":"Part of the old canteen may be used for storage.","zh":"舊飯堂的一部分可能用作儲物。"},{"en":"Storage means keeping things in a place until they are needed.","zh":"storage 指把東西存放在某地方，直至需要使用。"},{"en":"Schools need storage for chairs, books, sports equipment, and cleaning materials.","zh":"學校需要儲物空間來存放椅子、書本、運動器材和清潔用品。"},{"en":"Good storage keeps spaces tidy and safe.","zh":"良好儲物安排能保持空間整潔和安全。"},{"en":"This word describes organised keeping of items.","zh":"這個字描述有組織地存放物件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"see how many","meaning":"看看有多少……","examples":[{"en":"The school will see how many pupils use the old canteen.","zh":"學校會看看有多少學生使用舊飯堂。"},{"en":"See how many means find out the number of people or things.","zh":"see how many 指查明人或物的數量。"},{"en":"Teachers may see how many students want to join the trip before booking a bus.","zh":"老師可能先看看有多少學生想參加旅行，再預訂巴士。"},{"en":"Counting users helps schools decide whether a space is still needed.","zh":"統計使用者有助學校決定空間是否仍然需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes checking numbers before making a decision.","zh":"這個短語描述作決定前檢查數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at lunchtime","meaning":"在午膳時間","examples":[{"en":"The school will monitor how many pupils use the old canteen at lunchtime.","zh":"學校會監察午膳時間有多少學生使用舊飯堂。"},{"en":"At lunchtime means during the period when people eat lunch.","zh":"at lunchtime 指在人們吃午餐的時段。"},{"en":"The playground is busiest at lunchtime.","zh":"操場在午膳時間最繁忙。"},{"en":"Observing what happens at lunchtime helps the school improve lunch arrangements.","zh":"觀察午膳時間發生甚麼，有助學校改善午餐安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the midday meal period.","zh":"這個短語描述中午用餐時段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"back to","meaning":"回到……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker goes back to the serving points in the Food Hall.","zh":"講者回到 Food Hall 的供餐點話題。"},{"en":"Back to means returning to a previous topic or place.","zh":"back to 指回到先前的話題或地方。"},{"en":"After discussing homework, the teacher went back to the exam timetable.","zh":"討論功課後，老師回到考試時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise speech when the speaker returns to an earlier point.","zh":"當說話者回到早前重點時，這個短語有助組織說話。"},{"en":"It signals a return rather than a new topic.","zh":"它表示回到原題，而不是新話題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"side dishes","meaning":"配菜","examples":[{"en":"The serving points will sell side dishes.","zh":"供餐點會售賣配菜。"},{"en":"Side dishes are smaller dishes served with a main course.","zh":"side dishes 指與主菜一起供應的較小菜式。"},{"en":"Rice, salad, vegetables, and soup can be side dishes.","zh":"米飯、沙律、蔬菜和湯都可以是配菜。"},{"en":"Side dishes add variety and balance to a meal.","zh":"配菜為餐點增加變化和平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes food eaten alongside the main dish.","zh":"這個短語描述與主菜一起吃的食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"desserts","meaning":"甜品","examples":[{"en":"The serving points will sell desserts and drinks.","zh":"供餐點會售賣甜品和飲品。"},{"en":"Desserts are sweet foods usually eaten after the main meal.","zh":"desserts 指通常在主餐後食用的甜食。"},{"en":"Fruit salad, cake, yoghurt, and pudding can be desserts.","zh":"水果沙律、蛋糕、乳酪和布甸都可以是甜品。"},{"en":"Offering desserts gives pupils a small sweet choice after lunch.","zh":"提供甜品讓學生午餐後有小甜食選擇。"},{"en":"This word describes the sweet final part of a meal.","zh":"這個字描述餐點中甜味的最後部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"drinks on sale","meaning":"有飲品出售","examples":[{"en":"Drinks will be on sale at the serving points.","zh":"供餐點會有飲品出售。"},{"en":"Drinks on sale means drinks are available for people to buy.","zh":"drinks on sale 指飲品可供人購買。"},{"en":"Water, juice, and milk may be on sale in the school canteen.","zh":"學校飯堂可能有水、果汁和牛奶出售。"},{"en":"Clear drink options help pupils choose quickly.","zh":"清楚的飲品選項有助學生快速選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes beverages available for purchase.","zh":"這個短語描述可購買的飲品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"The serving points will sell side dishes as well as main courses.","zh":"供餐點除了主菜之外，也會售賣配菜。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to.","zh":"as well as 指此外，也包括。"},{"en":"The café sells sandwiches as well as hot meals.","zh":"咖啡店除了熱餐之外，也售賣三文治。"},{"en":"This phrase adds information without replacing the first item.","zh":"這個短語加入資料，而不是取代第一項。"},{"en":"It is useful when listing what is available.","zh":"列出可供選擇的項目時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"main courses","meaning":"主菜","examples":[{"en":"The Food Hall will serve main courses, side dishes and desserts.","zh":"Food Hall 會供應主菜、配菜和甜品。"},{"en":"Main courses are the largest or most important dishes in a meal.","zh":"main courses 指一餐中最大或最重要的菜式。"},{"en":"Pasta, curry, roast chicken, and vegetable pie can be main courses.","zh":"意粉、咖喱、烤雞和蔬菜批都可以是主菜。"},{"en":"Pupils usually choose a main course before adding side dishes or desserts.","zh":"學生通常先選主菜，再加配菜或甜品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the central part of a meal.","zh":"這個短語描述餐點的核心部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a different country’s cuisine","meaning":"不同國家的菜式","examples":[{"en":"World Adventures will serve a different country’s cuisine each day.","zh":"World Adventures 每天會供應不同國家的菜式。"},{"en":"A different country’s cuisine means the style of cooking from another nation.","zh":"a different country’s cuisine 指來自另一個國家的烹調風格。"},{"en":"A school lunch menu may feature a different country’s cuisine to help pupils try new flavours.","zh":"學校午餐餐單可能介紹不同國家的菜式，幫助學生嘗試新味道。"},{"en":"Serving different cuisines can make lunch more interesting and educational.","zh":"供應不同菜式可以令午餐更有趣，也更有教育意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes food linked to national cooking traditions.","zh":"這個短語描述與國家烹飪傳統相關的食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cuisine","meaning":"菜式；烹調風格","examples":[{"en":"The serving point will offer Chinese and Lebanese cuisine.","zh":"供餐點會提供中國菜和黎巴嫩菜。"},{"en":"Cuisine means a style of cooking, often linked to a country, region, or culture.","zh":"cuisine 指一種烹調風格，常與國家、地區或文化相關。"},{"en":"Italian cuisine is known for pasta, pizza, and olive oil.","zh":"意大利菜以意粉、薄餅和橄欖油聞名。"},{"en":"Cuisine includes ingredients, cooking methods, flavours, and eating traditions.","zh":"菜式包括材料、烹調方法、味道和飲食傳統。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “food”.","zh":"這個字比 “food” 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Chinese one day and Lebanese the next","meaning":"一天是中國菜，下一天是黎巴嫩菜","examples":[{"en":"The Food Hall may serve Chinese food one day and Lebanese food the next.","zh":"Food Hall 可能一天供應中國菜，下一天供應黎巴嫩菜。"},{"en":"Chinese one day and Lebanese the next means the food changes from one cuisine to another on different days.","zh":"Chinese one day and Lebanese the next 指不同日子從一種菜式轉到另一種菜式。"},{"en":"A school could offer Indian food one day and Mexican food the next.","zh":"學校可以一天提供印度菜，下一天提供墨西哥菜。"},{"en":"This kind of rotation gives pupils variety across the week.","zh":"這種輪換安排給學生一星期中的不同選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase illustrates alternating choices.","zh":"這個短語示範交替選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be planned for","meaning":"按……規劃","examples":[{"en":"The menus will be planned for a week at a time.","zh":"餐單會每次按一星期規劃。"},{"en":"Be planned for a period means be organised to cover that length of time.","zh":"be planned for a period 指安排好以涵蓋某段時間。"},{"en":"Lessons may be planned for a term at a time.","zh":"課堂可能每次按一個學期規劃。"},{"en":"Planning menus in advance helps pupils and parents know what to expect.","zh":"預先規劃餐單有助學生和家長知道會有甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparation for a specific period.","zh":"這個短語描述為特定時段作準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a week at a time","meaning":"每次一星期","examples":[{"en":"The menus will be planned for a week at a time.","zh":"餐單會每次規劃一星期。"},{"en":"A week at a time means one week as a single planning unit.","zh":"a week at a time 指以一星期作為一個規劃單位。"},{"en":"A teacher may set homework a week at a time so students can organise themselves.","zh":"老師可能每次安排一星期功課，讓學生可以自行規劃。"},{"en":"Planning a week at a time gives structure without looking too far ahead.","zh":"每次規劃一星期能提供結構，又不會看得太遠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a weekly planning method.","zh":"這個短語描述按星期規劃的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"available","meaning":"可供選擇；有供應","examples":[{"en":"Pupils will know what food is available for the whole week.","zh":"學生會知道整個星期有甚麼食物可供選擇。"},{"en":"Available means able to be chosen, used, bought, or obtained.","zh":"available 指可以被選擇、使用、購買或取得。"},{"en":"The library website shows which books are available.","zh":"圖書館網站顯示哪些書有供應。"},{"en":"If pupils know what is available, they can decide more quickly at lunchtime.","zh":"如果學生知道有甚麼可供選擇，午餐時就能更快決定。"},{"en":"This word describes what people can access or choose.","zh":"這個字描述人們可以取得或選擇的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the whole of that week","meaning":"整個星期","examples":[{"en":"Pupils will know what is available for the whole of that week.","zh":"學生會知道整個星期有甚麼供應。"},{"en":"The whole of that week means every day in that particular week.","zh":"the whole of that week 指該特定星期中的每一天。"},{"en":"The sports hall will be closed for the whole of that week.","zh":"體育館會在整個星期關閉。"},{"en":"Knowing information for the whole week helps families plan ahead.","zh":"知道整個星期的資訊有助家庭預先計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the entire week, not just one day.","zh":"這個短語強調整個星期，而不只是一日。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"food from three particular cultures","meaning":"來自三種特定文化的食物","examples":[{"en":"Street Life will serve food from three particular cultures.","zh":"Street Life 會供應來自三種特定文化的食物。"},{"en":"Food from three particular cultures means dishes linked to three selected cultural traditions.","zh":"food from three particular cultures 指與三種指定文化傳統相關的菜式。"},{"en":"A food festival may serve food from three particular cultures to celebrate diversity.","zh":"美食節可能供應來自三種特定文化的食物，以慶祝多元。"},{"en":"Choosing particular cultures gives the menu a clear theme.","zh":"選擇特定文化能令餐單有清晰主題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes culturally themed food choices.","zh":"這個短語描述以文化為主題的食物選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make suggestions","meaning":"提出建議","examples":[{"en":"Pupils will be asked to make suggestions.","zh":"學生會被要求提出建議。"},{"en":"To make suggestions means to offer ideas or recommendations.","zh":"make suggestions 指提出想法或推薦。"},{"en":"Students may make suggestions for new library books.","zh":"學生可能為新圖書館書籍提出建議。"},{"en":"Asking pupils to make suggestions helps them feel involved.","zh":"要求學生提出建議，可以令他們感到有參與感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes contributing ideas.","zh":"這個短語描述貢獻想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be replaced by","meaning":"被……取代","examples":[{"en":"One type of food may be replaced by Jamaican food.","zh":"一種食物可能被牙買加食物取代。"},{"en":"Be replaced by means be removed and have something else put in its place.","zh":"be replaced by 指某物被移走，並由另一物取代其位置。"},{"en":"The old computers were replaced by new laptops.","zh":"舊電腦被新手提電腦取代。"},{"en":"Replacing one food with another can keep the menu fresh.","zh":"用另一種食物取代一種食物，可以令餐單保持新鮮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes substitution.","zh":"這個短語描述替換。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Jamaican food","meaning":"牙買加食物","examples":[{"en":"Jamaican food may be served for a week or two.","zh":"牙買加食物可能會供應一兩星期。"},{"en":"Jamaican food is cuisine from Jamaica, often known for strong spices and Caribbean flavours.","zh":"Jamaican food 指來自牙買加的菜式，常以濃烈香料和加勒比風味聞名。"},{"en":"A school might introduce Jamaican food such as rice and peas or jerk-style chicken.","zh":"學校可能介紹牙買加食物，例如米飯配豆或 jerk 風味雞。"},{"en":"Serving Jamaican food can help pupils experience a different food culture.","zh":"供應牙買加食物可以幫助學生體驗不同飲食文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes food linked to Jamaica.","zh":"這個短語描述與牙買加相關的食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for a week or two","meaning":"一兩星期","examples":[{"en":"One cuisine may be offered for a week or two.","zh":"一種菜式可能會供應一兩星期。"},{"en":"For a week or two means for about one or two weeks.","zh":"for a week or two 指大約一至兩星期。"},{"en":"The school may test a new breakfast menu for a week or two.","zh":"學校可能試行新早餐餐單一兩星期。"},{"en":"A short trial period lets people see whether an idea works.","zh":"短暫試行期讓人觀察一個想法是否可行。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate short duration.","zh":"這個短語給出大約的短時間長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cater particularly for","meaning":"特別照顧……的需要","examples":[{"en":"The Speedy Italian serving point will cater particularly for pupils who do not eat meat or fish.","zh":"Speedy Italian 供餐點會特別照顧不吃肉或魚的學生需要。"},{"en":"To cater particularly for a group means to provide food or services especially suited to that group’s needs.","zh":"cater particularly for a group 指提供特別適合該群體需要的食物或服務。"},{"en":"A school trip may cater particularly for pupils with mobility difficulties.","zh":"學校旅行可能特別照顧行動不便學生的需要。"},{"en":"Catering for a group shows that their needs have been considered.","zh":"照顧某群體需要顯示其需要已被考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes targeted provision.","zh":"這個短語描述有針對性的提供。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pupils who don’t eat meat or fish","meaning":"不吃肉或魚的學生","examples":[{"en":"The serving point will cater for pupils who do not eat meat or fish.","zh":"供餐點會照顧不吃肉或魚的學生。"},{"en":"Pupils who don’t eat meat or fish are students who avoid these foods, often for health, religious, ethical, or personal reasons.","zh":"pupils who don’t eat meat or fish 指避免這些食物的學生，常因健康、宗教、道德或個人原因。"},{"en":"Vegetarian pupils may be pupils who do not eat meat or fish.","zh":"素食學生可能是不吃肉或魚的學生。"},{"en":"Schools need suitable food choices for pupils with different diets.","zh":"學校需要為不同飲食習慣的學生提供合適食物選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a dietary group.","zh":"這個短語指出一個飲食群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be sure that","meaning":"可以肯定……","examples":[{"en":"Pupils can be sure that the food is suitable for them.","zh":"學生可以肯定食物適合他們。"},{"en":"Be sure that means feel confident or certain that something is true.","zh":"be sure that 指對某事是真實的感到有信心或確定。"},{"en":"Parents need to be sure that school meals are safe for children with allergies.","zh":"家長需要可以肯定學校餐點對有過敏的孩子安全。"},{"en":"Clear labels help pupils be sure that they are choosing the right food.","zh":"清晰標籤幫助學生肯定自己選對食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes confidence and certainty.","zh":"這個短語描述信心和確定性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be suitable for","meaning":"適合……","examples":[{"en":"All the food served there is suitable for them.","zh":"那裏供應的所有食物都適合他們。"},{"en":"Be suitable for someone means fit that person’s needs, restrictions, or situation.","zh":"be suitable for someone 指符合某人的需要、限制或情況。"},{"en":"A quiet reading corner is suitable for pupils who need calm time.","zh":"安靜閱讀角適合需要冷靜時間的學生。"},{"en":"Food suitable for vegetarians should not contain meat or fish.","zh":"適合素食者的食物不應含肉或魚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a good match.","zh":"這個短語描述良好配合。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"plenty of variety","meaning":"很多變化；選擇多","examples":[{"en":"There will be plenty of variety at Speedy Italian.","zh":"Speedy Italian 會有很多變化。"},{"en":"Plenty of variety means many different choices or forms.","zh":"plenty of variety 指有許多不同選擇或形式。"},{"en":"A good school menu has plenty of variety so pupils do not eat the same thing every day.","zh":"好的學校餐單有很多變化，讓學生不會每天吃同一樣東西。"},{"en":"Variety can make meals more interesting and balanced.","zh":"多樣性可以令餐點更有趣和更均衡。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures people that choices will not be limited.","zh":"這個短語讓人放心，表示選擇不會有限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get bored with","meaning":"對……感到厭倦","examples":[{"en":"Pupils should not get bored with the food.","zh":"學生應該不會對食物感到厭倦。"},{"en":"To get bored with something means to lose interest because it is repeated or no longer exciting.","zh":"get bored with something 指因某事重複或不再有趣而失去興趣。"},{"en":"Students may get bored with the same sandwich every day.","zh":"學生可能對每天同一款三文治感到厭倦。"},{"en":"Offering different choices helps people avoid getting bored with meals.","zh":"提供不同選擇有助人避免對餐點感到厭倦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes losing interest over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間失去興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"after-school lessons","meaning":"課後課程","examples":[{"en":"The speaker moves on to after-school lessons.","zh":"講者轉到課後課程。"},{"en":"After-school lessons are classes or activities held after the normal school day.","zh":"after-school lessons 指正常上課日後舉行的課堂或活動。"},{"en":"Pupils may take after-school lessons in swimming, drama, music, or cycling.","zh":"學生可能參加游泳、戲劇、音樂或單車課後課程。"},{"en":"These lessons give pupils extra opportunities beyond normal classes.","zh":"這些課程給學生正常課堂以外的額外機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised learning after school.","zh":"這個短語描述放學後的有組織學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be popular with","meaning":"受……歡迎","examples":[{"en":"After-school lessons are popular with pupils.","zh":"課後課程受學生歡迎。"},{"en":"Be popular with a group means be liked or chosen by many people in that group.","zh":"be popular with a group 指被該群體中許多人喜歡或選擇。"},{"en":"Football is popular with many pupils during lunchtime.","zh":"足球在午膳時間受許多學生歡迎。"},{"en":"If an activity is popular with pupils, there may be a waiting list.","zh":"如果活動受學生歡迎，可能會有輪候名單。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong interest from a group.","zh":"這個短語描述來自某群體的強烈興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"waiting list","meaning":"輪候名單","examples":[{"en":"There is a waiting list for swimming lessons.","zh":"游泳課有輪候名單。"},{"en":"A waiting list is a list of people who want a place but must wait until one becomes available.","zh":"waiting list 指想取得名額但要等有空缺的人名單。"},{"en":"A popular music class may have a long waiting list.","zh":"受歡迎的音樂班可能有很長輪候名單。"},{"en":"Waiting lists happen when demand is greater than the number of places.","zh":"當需求大於名額數量，就會出現輪候名單。"},{"en":"This phrase describes delayed access because places are full.","zh":"這個短語描述因名額已滿而延遲參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"another favourite","meaning":"另一項受歡迎的活動","examples":[{"en":"Cycling is another favourite among pupils.","zh":"單車是學生之間另一項受歡迎的活動。"},{"en":"Another favourite means another activity or thing that is also very popular.","zh":"another favourite 指另一個也很受歡迎的活動或事物。"},{"en":"If football is the most popular sport, basketball may be another favourite.","zh":"如果足球是最受歡迎的運動，籃球可能是另一項受歡迎的活動。"},{"en":"This phrase adds one more liked option to a list.","zh":"這個短語在清單中加入另一個受喜愛選項。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing popular choices.","zh":"描述受歡迎選擇時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"dozens of","meaning":"數十名……","examples":[{"en":"Dozens of pupils learn to ride in off-road conditions.","zh":"數十名學生學習在越野環境中騎單車。"},{"en":"Dozens of means many, usually at least twenty-four or a large number.","zh":"dozens of 指很多，通常至少二十四個或表示相當多。"},{"en":"Dozens of parents attended the school meeting.","zh":"數十名家長出席了學校會議。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a sense of quantity without an exact number.","zh":"這個短語給出數量感，但不提供精確數字。"},{"en":"It is often used when the number is large but approximate.","zh":"當數字大但只是大約時，常會使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make use of","meaning":"利用……","examples":[{"en":"Many pupils make use of the chance to learn cycling.","zh":"許多學生利用學習騎單車的機會。"},{"en":"To make use of something means to use an opportunity, object, or resource well.","zh":"make use of something 指好好使用機會、物件或資源。"},{"en":"Students should make use of the library before exams.","zh":"學生應在考試前利用圖書館。"},{"en":"Making use of a chance means not wasting it.","zh":"利用機會意味著不浪費它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical and positive use.","zh":"這個短語描述實際而正面的使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the chance to","meaning":"……的機會","examples":[{"en":"Pupils make use of the chance to learn to ride.","zh":"學生利用學習騎單車的機會。"},{"en":"The chance to do something means the opportunity to do it.","zh":"chance to do something 指做某事的機會。"},{"en":"A school trip gives pupils the chance to visit a museum.","zh":"學校旅行給學生參觀博物館的機會。"},{"en":"Chances can help pupils try new skills outside normal lessons.","zh":"機會可以幫助學生在正常課堂以外嘗試新技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes opportunity.","zh":"這個短語描述機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"learn to ride","meaning":"學習騎單車","examples":[{"en":"Pupils learn to ride in off-road conditions.","zh":"學生學習在越野環境中騎單車。"},{"en":"Learn to ride means learn how to control and travel on a bicycle, horse, or similar vehicle.","zh":"learn to ride 指學習如何控制並乘坐單車、馬或類似交通工具。"},{"en":"Children often learn to ride a bicycle with help from an adult.","zh":"孩子通常在成人幫助下學習騎單車。"},{"en":"Learning to ride safely requires balance, control, and confidence.","zh":"安全學習騎車需要平衡、控制和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes developing riding skill.","zh":"這個短語描述發展騎乘技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"off-road conditions","meaning":"越野環境","examples":[{"en":"Pupils learn to ride in off-road conditions.","zh":"學生學習在越野環境中騎單車。"},{"en":"Off-road conditions are surfaces away from normal roads, such as paths, grass, mud, or uneven ground.","zh":"off-road conditions 指離開普通道路的路面，例如小徑、草地、泥地或不平地面。"},{"en":"Riding in off-road conditions is harder than cycling on a smooth street.","zh":"在越野環境中騎車比在平滑街道上更難。"},{"en":"Pupils need balance and control when riding over rough ground.","zh":"學生在粗糙地面騎行時需要平衡和控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes outdoor riding environments away from roads.","zh":"這個短語描述離開道路的戶外騎行環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"more and more","meaning":"越來越多","examples":[{"en":"More and more pupils cycle to and from school.","zh":"越來越多學生騎單車往返學校。"},{"en":"More and more means an increasing number over time.","zh":"more and more 指數量隨時間增加。"},{"en":"More and more families are choosing school lunches instead of packed lunches.","zh":"越來越多家庭選擇學校午餐，而不是自備午餐。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a growing trend.","zh":"這個短語描述增長趨勢。"},{"en":"It shows that something is becoming more common.","zh":"它顯示某事變得更常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cycle to and from school","meaning":"騎單車往返學校","examples":[{"en":"More pupils cycle to and from school every day.","zh":"每天有更多學生騎單車往返學校。"},{"en":"To cycle to and from school means to travel to school and return home by bicycle.","zh":"cycle to and from school 指騎單車上學並回家。"},{"en":"Pupils who live nearby may cycle to and from school safely using bike lanes.","zh":"住得近的學生可以使用單車徑安全地騎單車往返學校。"},{"en":"Cycling to school can improve fitness and reduce traffic.","zh":"騎單車上學可以改善體能並減少交通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes daily travel by bicycle.","zh":"這個短語描述以單車作日常交通。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"well-equipped performance centre","meaning":"設備完善的表演中心","examples":[{"en":"The school has a well-equipped performance centre.","zh":"學校有一個設備完善的表演中心。"},{"en":"A well-equipped performance centre has good facilities for drama, music, lighting, sound, and shows.","zh":"well-equipped performance centre 指有良好戲劇、音樂、燈光、音響和演出設施的中心。"},{"en":"A well-equipped performance centre can help pupils learn stage skills properly.","zh":"設備完善的表演中心可以幫助學生正確學習舞台技能。"},{"en":"Good equipment makes rehearsals and performances safer and more professional.","zh":"良好設備令排練和表演更安全、更專業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a performance space with strong facilities.","zh":"這個短語描述設施充足的表演空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"start drama classes","meaning":"開辦戲劇班","examples":[{"en":"The school will start drama classes in the performance centre.","zh":"學校將在表演中心開辦戲劇班。"},{"en":"To start drama classes means begin offering lessons in acting, performance, or theatre skills.","zh":"start drama classes 指開始提供演技、表演或戲劇技巧課程。"},{"en":"A school may start drama classes after opening a new stage.","zh":"學校開放新舞台後，可能開辦戲劇班。"},{"en":"Drama classes can help pupils build confidence, voice control, and teamwork.","zh":"戲劇班可以幫助學生建立信心、聲線控制和團隊合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes introducing theatre-related lessons.","zh":"這個短語描述引入戲劇相關課程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be able to join in","meaning":"能夠參加","examples":[{"en":"Pupils will be able to join in just for fun.","zh":"學生能夠只是為了好玩而參加。"},{"en":"Be able to join in means have the chance or permission to take part.","zh":"be able to join in 指有機會或許可參與。"},{"en":"Pupils who are shy may still be able to join in group drama games.","zh":"害羞學生仍能夠參加小組戲劇遊戲。"},{"en":"Joining in does not always mean performing seriously.","zh":"參加不一定代表要認真表演。"},{"en":"This phrase describes participation.","zh":"這個短語描述參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"just for fun","meaning":"只是為了好玩","examples":[{"en":"Pupils can join the drama classes just for fun.","zh":"學生可以只是為了好玩而參加戲劇班。"},{"en":"Just for fun means for enjoyment, not for marks, competition, or serious pressure.","zh":"just for fun 指為了享受，而不是為了分數、比賽或嚴肅壓力。"},{"en":"Some pupils play music just for fun after school.","zh":"有些學生放學後只是為了好玩而玩音樂。"},{"en":"Activities done for fun can still help pupils learn useful skills.","zh":"為了好玩而做的活動仍可以幫助學生學到有用技能。"},{"en":"This phrase removes pressure from participation.","zh":"這個短語減輕參與壓力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"work up to","meaning":"逐步準備至……","examples":[{"en":"Pupils can work up to taking part in a play.","zh":"學生可以逐步準備至參與戲劇演出。"},{"en":"To work up to something means gradually prepare for a more difficult goal.","zh":"work up to something 指逐步準備，直到能達成較難目標。"},{"en":"A beginner swimmer may work up to swimming a full length of the pool.","zh":"初學游泳者可能逐步準備至游完整個泳池長度。"},{"en":"Drama pupils can start with games and work up to performing on stage.","zh":"戲劇學生可以由遊戲開始，逐步準備至上台表演。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual progress toward a bigger challenge.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步走向較大挑戰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"take part in a play","meaning":"參與戲劇演出","examples":[{"en":"Pupils can work towards taking part in a play.","zh":"學生可以逐步朝參與戲劇演出努力。"},{"en":"To take part in a play means to participate in a theatre performance.","zh":"take part in a play 指參與劇場表演。"},{"en":"A pupil may take part in a play as an actor, narrator, or backstage helper.","zh":"學生可以作為演員、旁白或後台助手參與戲劇演出。"},{"en":"Taking part in a play can build confidence and teamwork.","zh":"參與戲劇演出可以建立信心和團隊合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes involvement in drama performance.","zh":"這個短語描述參與戲劇表演。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"put on","meaning":"上演；舉辦","examples":[{"en":"The school hopes to put on at least one play a year.","zh":"學校希望每年至少上演一齣戲劇。"},{"en":"To put on a play means to organise and perform it for an audience.","zh":"put on a play 指組織並向觀眾演出一齣戲。"},{"en":"A drama club may put on a comedy at the end of term.","zh":"戲劇學會可能在學期末上演一齣喜劇。"},{"en":"Putting on a play requires rehearsals, costumes, lighting, and teamwork.","zh":"上演戲劇需要排練、服裝、燈光和團隊合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes staging a performance.","zh":"這個短語描述呈現舞台演出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at least one a year","meaning":"每年至少一個","examples":[{"en":"The school hopes to put on at least one play a year.","zh":"學校希望每年至少上演一個戲劇演出。"},{"en":"At least one a year means one or more each year.","zh":"at least one a year 指每年一個或以上。"},{"en":"The music department hopes to hold at least one concert a year.","zh":"音樂科希望每年至少舉辦一場音樂會。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a minimum annual target.","zh":"這個短語給出最低年度目標。"},{"en":"It shows a regular but modest plan.","zh":"它顯示定期但適度的計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a number of","meaning":"一些","examples":[{"en":"The school already teaches a number of pupils to use the systems.","zh":"學校已教一些學生使用這些系統。"},{"en":"A number of means several or some, without giving an exact number.","zh":"a number of 指幾個或一些，而不給出確切數字。"},{"en":"A number of students help in the library after school.","zh":"一些學生放學後在圖書館幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the exact number is not important.","zh":"當確切數字不重要時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It indicates more than one person or thing.","zh":"它表示多於一個人或物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sound and lighting systems","meaning":"音響和燈光系統","examples":[{"en":"Pupils learn to use the sound and lighting systems.","zh":"學生學習使用音響和燈光系統。"},{"en":"Sound and lighting systems are the equipment used to control audio and lights during performances.","zh":"sound and lighting systems 指表演期間用來控制聲音和燈光的設備。"},{"en":"Pupils using the sound and lighting systems may control microphones, speakers, spotlights, and stage lights.","zh":"使用音響和燈光系統的學生可能控制咪高峰、揚聲器、聚光燈和舞台燈。"},{"en":"These systems are important because they affect what the audience hears and sees.","zh":"這些系統很重要，因為它們影響觀眾聽到和看到的效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes technical theatre equipment.","zh":"這個短語描述劇場技術設備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"former pupil","meaning":"舊生","examples":[{"en":"A former pupil gave a grand piano to the school.","zh":"一名舊生送了一部三角鋼琴給學校。"},{"en":"A former pupil is someone who used to study at the school but no longer does.","zh":"former pupil 指以前在該校讀書、現在已不再就讀的人。"},{"en":"A former pupil may return years later to speak to current students.","zh":"舊生可能多年後回校向現有學生演講。"},{"en":"Former pupils sometimes support schools because they feel grateful or connected.","zh":"舊生有時會支持學校，因為他們感到感激或有連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an ex-student.","zh":"這個短語描述以前的學生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"magnificent grand piano","meaning":"漂亮的三角鋼琴","examples":[{"en":"A former pupil gave a magnificent grand piano to the school.","zh":"一名舊生送了一部漂亮的三角鋼琴給學校。"},{"en":"A magnificent grand piano is a large, beautiful, high-quality piano used for serious performance.","zh":"magnificent grand piano 指大型、美麗、高質素並用於正式表演的鋼琴。"},{"en":"A magnificent grand piano can make a performance centre feel more professional.","zh":"漂亮的三角鋼琴可以令表演中心感覺更專業。"},{"en":"Grand pianos are larger and often richer in sound than upright pianos.","zh":"三角鋼琴比直立式鋼琴更大，聲音通常更豐富。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly praises the instrument’s beauty and quality.","zh":"這個短語強烈稱讚樂器的美感和質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be able to learn at","meaning":"能夠在……學習","examples":[{"en":"Some pupils will be able to learn piano at school.","zh":"有些學生將能夠在學校學習鋼琴。"},{"en":"Be able to learn at a place means have the chance to study there.","zh":"be able to learn at a place 指有機會在某地方學習。"},{"en":"Pupils may be able to learn dance at school if a teacher is available.","zh":"如果有老師，學生可能能夠在學校學習舞蹈。"},{"en":"Learning at school can be more convenient than travelling elsewhere.","zh":"在學校學習可以比到其他地方更方便。"},{"en":"This phrase describes opportunity and location together.","zh":"這個短語同時描述機會和地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"instead of","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Some pupils can learn at school instead of going to the local college.","zh":"有些學生可以在學校學習，而不是去本地學院。"},{"en":"Instead of means in place of another action or choice.","zh":"instead of 指取代另一個行動或選擇。"},{"en":"A pupil may bring lunch from home instead of buying food in the canteen.","zh":"學生可能從家中帶午餐，而不是在飯堂購買食物。"},{"en":"This phrase compares what will happen with the alternative not chosen.","zh":"這個短語把會發生的事與未選擇的替代方案作比較。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining replacement or preference.","zh":"解釋取代或偏好時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"local college","meaning":"本地學院","examples":[{"en":"Many pupils currently go to the local college for piano lessons.","zh":"許多學生目前到本地學院上鋼琴課。"},{"en":"A local college is a nearby educational institution offering courses or lessons.","zh":"local college 指附近提供課程或課堂的教育機構。"},{"en":"Pupils may attend a local college after school for music, art, or language classes.","zh":"學生可能放學後到本地學院上音樂、美術或語言課。"},{"en":"If lessons are offered at school, fewer pupils need to travel to the local college.","zh":"如果學校提供課程，較少學生需要前往本地學院。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a nearby place of further learning.","zh":"這個短語描述附近的進修學習場所。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at the moment","meaning":"目前","examples":[{"en":"Many pupils go to the local college at the moment.","zh":"許多學生目前到本地學院上課。"},{"en":"At the moment means currently or right now.","zh":"at the moment 指目前或現在。"},{"en":"At the moment, the library is closed for repairs.","zh":"目前，圖書館因維修而關閉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the present situation, which may change later.","zh":"這個短語描述現在情況，而它之後可能改變。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken English.","zh":"它常見於口語英文。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 17/task-3":[{"front":"psychology assignment","meaning":"心理學課業","examples":[{"en":"Susie and Luke have to prepare their next psychology assignment.","zh":"Susie 和 Luke 要準備下一份心理學課業。"},{"en":"A psychology assignment is a piece of coursework about the study of the mind and behaviour.","zh":"psychology assignment 指一份關於心智和行為研究的課業。"},{"en":"Students may write a psychology assignment on memory, dreams, stress or learning.","zh":"學生可能寫一份關於記憶、夢、壓力或學習的心理學課業。"},{"en":"A good psychology assignment usually needs research, evidence and clear analysis.","zh":"好的心理學課業通常需要研究、證據和清晰分析。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in school and university study.","zh":"這個片語常見於學校和大學學習中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"do something on","meaning":"做一個關於……的題目","examples":[{"en":"The students have to do something on sleep and dreams.","zh":"學生要做一個關於睡眠與夢的題目。"},{"en":"To do something on a topic means to prepare work about that topic.","zh":"do something on a topic 指準備一份關於某主題的作品。"},{"en":"We have to do a presentation on memory next week.","zh":"我們下星期要做一個關於記憶的簡報。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and often used when talking about schoolwork.","zh":"這個片語較口語，常用於談論學業。"},{"en":"It means the topic will be the focus of the task.","zh":"它表示該主題會成為任務的重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sleep and dreams","meaning":"睡眠與夢","examples":[{"en":"The assignment focuses on sleep and dreams.","zh":"這份課業聚焦於睡眠與夢。"},{"en":"Sleep and dreams refers to the study of sleeping patterns and the experiences people have while asleep.","zh":"sleep and dreams 指研究睡眠模式以及人在睡眠中經歷的夢境。"},{"en":"Psychologists study sleep and dreams to understand memory, emotion and the brain.","zh":"心理學家研究睡眠與夢，以了解記憶、情緒和大腦。"},{"en":"Sleep and dreams can be researched through diaries, questionnaires and experiments.","zh":"睡眠與夢可以透過日記、問卷和實驗研究。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common topic in psychology.","zh":"這個片語命名心理學中的常見題目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"read an article suggesting why","meaning":"讀到一篇文章解釋為甚麼……","examples":[{"en":"Luke has read an article suggesting why people forget most of their dreams.","zh":"Luke 讀到一篇文章，解釋為甚麼人們會忘記大部分夢境。"},{"en":"To read an article suggesting why means to read a text that offers an explanation for something.","zh":"read an article suggesting why 指讀到一篇提出某事原因的文章。"},{"en":"I read an article suggesting why teenagers need more sleep.","zh":"我讀到一篇文章，解釋為甚麼青少年需要更多睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a theory found in reading.","zh":"這個片語適合用於引入閱讀中找到的理論。"},{"en":"It suggests the article gives a possible explanation, not necessarily a final answer.","zh":"它暗示文章提出的是可能解釋，而不一定是最終答案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tend to forget","meaning":"往往會忘記","examples":[{"en":"People tend to forget most of their dreams soon after waking up.","zh":"人們醒來後不久往往會忘記大部分夢境。"},{"en":"To tend to forget means to usually forget something.","zh":"tend to forget 指通常會忘記某事。"},{"en":"Students tend to forget new vocabulary if they never review it.","zh":"如果學生從不溫習新詞，他們往往會忘記。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common pattern rather than something that always happens.","zh":"這個片語描述常見模式，而不是一定每次都發生。"},{"en":"It is useful when talking about habits or general behaviour.","zh":"它適合用於談論習慣或一般行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"soon after","meaning":"在……之後不久","examples":[{"en":"People often forget their dreams soon after they wake up.","zh":"人們醒來後不久常會忘記夢境。"},{"en":"Soon after means a short time after something happens.","zh":"soon after 指某事發生後很短時間。"},{"en":"She wrote down her dream soon after waking up.","zh":"她醒來後不久便把夢寫下來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing timing.","zh":"這個片語適合用於描述時間。"},{"en":"It suggests the second event happens quickly after the first.","zh":"它暗示第二件事在第一件事後很快發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"wake up","meaning":"醒來","examples":[{"en":"People may forget most of their dreams soon after they wake up.","zh":"人們醒來後不久可能會忘記大部分夢境。"},{"en":"To wake up means to stop sleeping and become conscious.","zh":"wake up 指停止睡眠並恢復清醒。"},{"en":"I usually wake up at seven o’clock on weekdays.","zh":"我平日通常七時醒來。"},{"en":"Some people remember dreams more clearly if they write them down as soon as they wake up.","zh":"有些人一醒來便寫下夢境，會記得更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday life and sleep research.","zh":"這個片語常見於日常生活和睡眠研究中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get mixed up about","meaning":"對……感到混淆","examples":[{"en":"If we remembered every dream, we might get mixed up about what really happened.","zh":"如果我們記得每個夢，可能會對真正發生的事感到混淆。"},{"en":"To get mixed up about something means to become confused about it.","zh":"get mixed up about something 指對某事感到混亂。"},{"en":"I got mixed up about the dates of the two assignments.","zh":"我把兩份課業的日期搞混了。"},{"en":"Dreams and memories could become confusing if both felt equally real.","zh":"如果夢和記憶感覺同樣真實，兩者可能會變得混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing confusion between similar things.","zh":"這個片語適合描述相似事物之間的混亂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what actually happened","meaning":"實際發生的事","examples":[{"en":"Dreams might become confused with what actually happened.","zh":"夢境可能會與實際發生的事混淆。"},{"en":"What actually happened means the real events that took place.","zh":"what actually happened 指真正發生過的事件。"},{"en":"After a vivid dream, she was not sure what actually happened and what she imagined.","zh":"做了一個很鮮明的夢後，她不確定哪些是實際發生的事，哪些是想像。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts reality with memory, imagination or dreams.","zh":"這個片語把現實與記憶、想像或夢境作對比。"},{"en":"It is useful in psychology and everyday storytelling.","zh":"它適合用於心理學和日常敘事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what we dreamed","meaning":"我們夢見的事","examples":[{"en":"People might confuse what actually happened with what they dreamed.","zh":"人們可能把實際發生的事與自己夢見的事混淆。"},{"en":"What we dreamed means the events or images we experienced in dreams.","zh":"what we dreamed 指我們在夢中經歷的事件或影像。"},{"en":"Children may sometimes mix up what they dreamed with what happened at school.","zh":"兒童有時可能把夢見的事與學校發生的事混淆。"},{"en":"Remembering what we dreamed can be interesting, but it may not reflect reality.","zh":"記得自己夢見的事可以很有趣，但它未必反映現實。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on dream content.","zh":"這個片語着重夢境內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a sort of protection","meaning":"一種保護","examples":[{"en":"Forgetting dreams may be a sort of protection.","zh":"忘記夢境可能是一種保護。"},{"en":"A sort of protection means a kind of defence against harm or confusion.","zh":"a sort of protection 指一種避免傷害或混亂的防護。"},{"en":"Forgetting unpleasant details can sometimes act as a sort of protection.","zh":"忘記不愉快細節有時可以作為一種保護。"},{"en":"In this theory, dream forgetting protects people from mixing dreams with real life.","zh":"在這個理論中，忘記夢境可以保護人們不把夢與現實混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a possible helpful function.","zh":"這個片語暗示某事可能有幫助功能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"I hadn’t heard that idea before","meaning":"我以前未聽過這個想法","examples":[{"en":"Luke had not heard that idea about dream forgetting before.","zh":"Luke 以前未聽過這個關於忘記夢境的想法。"},{"en":"I hadn’t heard that idea before means the idea is new to me.","zh":"I hadn’t heard that idea before 指這個想法對我來說是新的。"},{"en":"I hadn’t heard that idea before, but it makes sense.","zh":"我以前未聽過這個想法，但它很合理。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when responding to a new explanation.","zh":"這個片語適合用於回應新的解釋。"},{"en":"It shows surprise or interest without rejecting the idea.","zh":"它顯示驚訝或興趣，而不是否定該想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I’d always assumed that","meaning":"我一直以為","examples":[{"en":"Luke had always assumed that memory space was the reason people forgot dreams.","zh":"Luke 一直以為記憶空間是人們忘記夢境的原因。"},{"en":"I’d always assumed that means I had believed something was true without checking carefully.","zh":"I’d always assumed that 指我一直以為某事是真的，但未必仔細核實過。"},{"en":"I’d always assumed that dreams disappeared because the brain was too busy.","zh":"我一直以為夢境消失是因為大腦太忙。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces an old belief that may now be questioned.","zh":"這個片語常引入一個現在可能被質疑的舊想法。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing previous assumptions with new information.","zh":"它適合比較過去假設和新資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have room in our memories for","meaning":"記憶中有空間容納……","examples":[{"en":"Luke assumed that people did not have room in their memories for all their dreams.","zh":"Luke 以為人們記憶中沒有空間容納所有夢境。"},{"en":"To have room in our memories for something means to have enough mental capacity to store it.","zh":"have room in our memories for something 指有足夠心理容量去儲存某事。"},{"en":"We may not have room in our memories for every small detail of a normal day.","zh":"我們記憶中未必有空間容納普通一天的每個小細節。"},{"en":"This phrase uses physical space as a metaphor for memory capacity.","zh":"這個片語用實體空間比喻記憶容量。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing forgetting and information overload.","zh":"它適合用於討論遺忘和資訊過量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"all that stuff","meaning":"所有那些東西","examples":[{"en":"Luke thought people did not have room in their memories for all that stuff.","zh":"Luke 以為人們記憶中沒有空間容納所有那些東西。"},{"en":"All that stuff means all those things or all that information.","zh":"all that stuff 指所有那些事情或所有那些資訊。"},{"en":"I cannot remember all that stuff from the lecture without taking notes.","zh":"如果不做筆記，我記不住講座中的所有那些東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and slightly vague.","zh":"這個片語較口語，而且意思略籠統。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken English when the exact details are not important.","zh":"當準確細節不是重點時，它常見於英語口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what do you think about","meaning":"你對……有甚麼看法","examples":[{"en":"Susie asks Luke what he thinks about dreams predicting the future.","zh":"Susie 問 Luke 對夢境預知未來有甚麼看法。"},{"en":"What do you think about asks for someone’s opinion on a topic.","zh":"what do you think about 用來詢問某人對某主題的意見。"},{"en":"What do you think about using dream diaries for the experiment?","zh":"你對在實驗中使用夢境日記有甚麼看法？"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when starting discussion or inviting ideas.","zh":"這個片語適合用於開始討論或邀請意見。"},{"en":"It sounds open and conversational.","zh":"它聽起來開放而口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"predict the future","meaning":"預知未來","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe dreams can predict the future.","zh":"有些人相信夢可以預知未來。"},{"en":"To predict the future means to say what will happen before it happens.","zh":"predict the future 指在事情發生前說出將會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"No scientific method can perfectly predict the future of every person.","zh":"沒有科學方法可以完全預知每個人的未來。"},{"en":"Dreams may feel predictive when later events seem similar to them.","zh":"當之後的事件似乎與夢境相似時，夢可能感覺像能預知未來。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in discussions of belief, chance and evidence.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論信念、機會率和證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a belief that","meaning":"一種……的信念","examples":[{"en":"The idea that dreams predict the future is a belief found around the world.","zh":"夢能預知未來這個想法，是一種世界各地都有的信念。"},{"en":"A belief that something is true is an idea people accept or trust.","zh":"a belief that something is true 指人們接受或相信某事為真的想法。"},{"en":"There is a belief that sleep helps memory become stronger.","zh":"有一種信念認為睡眠有助增強記憶。"},{"en":"Beliefs may be cultural, personal, religious or based on experience.","zh":"信念可以是文化、個人、宗教或基於經驗的。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an idea that people hold.","zh":"這個片語引入人們持有的想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"all over the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Belief in dreams predicting the future exists all over the world.","zh":"相信夢境能預知未來的信念存在於世界各地。"},{"en":"All over the world means in many different countries and cultures.","zh":"all over the world 指在許多不同國家和文化中。"},{"en":"Stories about meaningful dreams appear all over the world.","zh":"關於有意義夢境的故事出現在世界各地。"},{"en":"A belief found all over the world may reflect a common human experience.","zh":"一種信念若存在於世界各地，可能反映共同的人類經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises global spread.","zh":"這個片語強調全球分布。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have a story of","meaning":"有一個關於……的經歷","examples":[{"en":"Many people have a story of a dream coming true.","zh":"許多人都有一個關於夢境成真的經歷。"},{"en":"To have a story of something means to have a personal account or experience connected with it.","zh":"have a story of something 指有一個與某事相關的個人說法或經驗。"},{"en":"My grandmother has a story of dreaming about a visitor before he arrived.","zh":"我祖母有一個關於在客人到達前夢見他的經歷。"},{"en":"Personal stories can feel convincing even when they are not scientific proof.","zh":"個人經歷可能感覺很有說服力，即使它們不是科學證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing anecdotes.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論軼事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"happen to someone","meaning":"發生在某人身上","examples":[{"en":"Many people say that a dream prediction has happened to them.","zh":"許多人說夢境預言曾發生在自己身上。"},{"en":"To happen to someone means to be experienced by that person.","zh":"happen to someone 指某人經歷某事。"},{"en":"A strange coincidence once happened to me after I had a dream.","zh":"我曾在做夢後遇到一件奇怪巧合。"},{"en":"People often remember unusual events that happen to them personally.","zh":"人們常記得親身經歷的不尋常事件。"},{"en":"This phrase links an event with the person affected by it.","zh":"這個片語把事件與受影響的人連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the explanation I’ve read","meaning":"我讀過的解釋","examples":[{"en":"Susie explains the theory she has read about dream predictions.","zh":"Susie 解釋她讀過的關於夢境預言的理論。"},{"en":"The explanation I’ve read means the account or theory I found in reading.","zh":"the explanation I’ve read 指我在閱讀中找到的說明或理論。"},{"en":"The explanation I’ve read suggests that memory selects unusual matches.","zh":"我讀過的解釋指出，記憶會選擇不尋常的相似情況。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting information from a source.","zh":"這個片語適合用於報告來源中的資訊。"},{"en":"It shows the speaker is not inventing the idea but referring to something studied.","zh":"它顯示說話者不是自己創造想法，而是在引用讀過的內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"come true","meaning":"成真","examples":[{"en":"For every dream that comes true, thousands do not.","zh":"每一個成真的夢背後，都有成千上萬個沒有成真。"},{"en":"To come true means to happen in real life after being imagined, hoped for or dreamed.","zh":"come true 指想像、希望或夢見的事情在現實中發生。"},{"en":"Her dream of studying psychology came true when she entered university.","zh":"她讀心理學的夢想在入讀大學時成真。"},{"en":"A dream may seem to come true if a later event resembles it.","zh":"如果後來的事件與夢境相似，夢可能看似成真。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing hopes, predictions and dreams.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論希望、預言和夢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"thousands that don’t","meaning":"成千上萬個沒有成真的","examples":[{"en":"For each dream that comes true, we have thousands that do not.","zh":"每一個成真的夢，都有成千上萬個沒有成真的。"},{"en":"Thousands that don’t means thousands of cases that do not happen or do not come true.","zh":"thousands that don’t 指成千上萬個沒有發生或沒有成真的情況。"},{"en":"People remember one accurate dream but forget thousands that do not match reality.","zh":"人們記得一個準確的夢，卻忘記成千上萬個與現實不符的夢。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the large number of failed predictions.","zh":"這個片語突出大量失敗預測。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining coincidence and selective memory.","zh":"它適合用於解釋巧合和選擇性記憶。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"notice those","meaning":"注意到那些","examples":[{"en":"People do not notice the dreams that fail to come true.","zh":"人們不會注意到那些沒有成真的夢。"},{"en":"To notice those means to pay attention to those examples or cases.","zh":"notice those 指留意那些例子或情況。"},{"en":"We notice successful predictions but rarely notice those that fail.","zh":"我們會注意到成功預測，卻很少注意到那些失敗的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing selective attention.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論選擇性注意。"},{"en":"It shows that people may remember some cases and ignore others.","zh":"它顯示人們可能記得某些情況，卻忽略另一些。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the ones where","meaning":"那些……的情況","examples":[{"en":"People remember the ones where something in real life triggers a memory.","zh":"人們記得那些現實生活中某事觸發夢境記憶的情況。"},{"en":"The ones where means the cases in which something happens.","zh":"the ones where 指某事發生的那些情況。"},{"en":"We remember the dreams where a real event later feels similar.","zh":"我們會記得那些後來有真實事件感覺相似的夢。"},{"en":"This phrase helps refer to a specific group of examples.","zh":"這個片語有助指稱一組特定例子。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken explanation.","zh":"它常見於口頭解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the real world","meaning":"在現實世界中","examples":[{"en":"Something in the real world may trigger a dream memory.","zh":"現實世界中的某事可能會觸發夢境記憶。"},{"en":"In the real world means in actual life, not in dreams, imagination or theory.","zh":"in the real world 指在真實生活中，而不是在夢、想像或理論中。"},{"en":"A sound in the real world can sometimes appear inside a dream.","zh":"現實世界中的聲音有時可能出現在夢裏。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts reality with mental experience.","zh":"這個片語把現實與心理經驗作對比。"},{"en":"It is useful in psychology discussions about dreams and memory.","zh":"它適合用於關於夢與記憶的心理學討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"trigger a dream memory","meaning":"觸發夢境記憶","examples":[{"en":"A view or action in the real world may trigger a dream memory.","zh":"現實世界中的景象或行動可能會觸發夢境記憶。"},{"en":"To trigger a dream memory means to cause someone to remember a dream.","zh":"trigger a dream memory 指引起某人記起一個夢。"},{"en":"Seeing a red door may trigger a dream memory from the night before.","zh":"看見一道紅門可能會觸發前一晚的夢境記憶。"},{"en":"Triggers can be sights, sounds, smells or situations.","zh":"觸發因素可以是景象、聲音、氣味或情境。"},{"en":"This phrase links external events with remembered dreams.","zh":"這個片語把外在事件與被記起的夢連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"just a coincidence","meaning":"只是巧合","examples":[{"en":"Luke concludes that apparent dream predictions are just a coincidence.","zh":"Luke 得出結論，表面上的夢境預言只是巧合。"},{"en":"Just a coincidence means something happened by chance, not because of a real connection.","zh":"just a coincidence 指某事只是偶然發生，而不是因真正關聯而發生。"},{"en":"Dreaming about an old friend before they call may be just a coincidence.","zh":"在舊朋友來電前夢見他，可能只是巧合。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining events that seem meaningful but may be random.","zh":"當解釋看似有意義但可能隨機的事件時，這個片語很有用。"},{"en":"It reduces the idea of mystery or prediction.","zh":"它削弱了神秘或預言的意味。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"something else I read about","meaning":"我讀到的另一件事","examples":[{"en":"Luke mentions something else he read about.","zh":"Luke 提到他讀到的另一件事。"},{"en":"Something else I read about means another topic or idea found while reading.","zh":"something else I read about 指閱讀時找到的另一個主題或想法。"},{"en":"Something else I read about was the link between sleep and creativity.","zh":"我讀到的另一件事是睡眠與創意之間的關係。"},{"en":"This phrase helps introduce an additional piece of information.","zh":"這個片語有助引入另一項資訊。"},{"en":"It sounds natural in study discussions.","zh":"它在學習討論中聽起來自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what they call","meaning":"他們所稱的……","examples":[{"en":"Luke talks about what they call segmented sleeping.","zh":"Luke 談到他們所稱的分段睡眠。"},{"en":"What they call means the name people use for something.","zh":"what they call 指人們用來稱呼某事的名稱。"},{"en":"The article describes what they call lucid dreaming.","zh":"文章描述他們所稱的清醒夢。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a term that may be unfamiliar.","zh":"這個片語適合用於引入可能不熟悉的術語。"},{"en":"It suggests the speaker is borrowing a term from others.","zh":"它暗示說話者是在借用別人的用語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"segmented sleeping","meaning":"分段睡眠","examples":[{"en":"Segmented sleeping means sleeping in separate periods during the night.","zh":"分段睡眠指晚上分成幾段時間睡覺。"},{"en":"Segmented sleeping is a sleep pattern divided into two or more blocks.","zh":"segmented sleeping 指把睡眠分成兩段或多段的睡眠模式。"},{"en":"Some researchers believe segmented sleeping was common before modern lighting.","zh":"有些研究者認為，在現代照明出現前，分段睡眠很常見。"},{"en":"People following segmented sleeping may wake up for a period in the middle of the night.","zh":"採用分段睡眠的人可能會在半夜醒來一段時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in discussions of sleep history and sleep patterns.","zh":"這個片語用於討論睡眠歷史和睡眠模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"that’s a theory that","meaning":"這是一個……的理論","examples":[{"en":"Segmented sleeping is a theory that people once slept in two separate periods.","zh":"分段睡眠是一個認為人們曾分兩段睡覺的理論。"},{"en":"That’s a theory that means this is an explanation or idea suggesting something.","zh":"that’s a theory that 指這是一個提出某種說法的解釋或想法。"},{"en":"That’s a theory that memory becomes stronger during sleep.","zh":"這是一個認為記憶會在睡眠中變強的理論。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a possible explanation rather than a proven fact.","zh":"這個片語引入可能解釋，而不是已證實事實。"},{"en":"It is useful in academic discussion when presenting ideas carefully.","zh":"它適合在學術討論中謹慎提出想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hundreds of years ago","meaning":"數百年前","examples":[{"en":"Hundreds of years ago, people may have slept in segmented patterns.","zh":"數百年前，人們可能以分段模式睡覺。"},{"en":"Hundreds of years ago means many centuries in the past.","zh":"hundreds of years ago 指很多個世紀以前。"},{"en":"Hundreds of years ago, people lived without electric lights.","zh":"數百年前，人們生活中沒有電燈。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a broad historical time frame.","zh":"這個片語提供廣泛的歷史時間框架。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing past habits with modern life.","zh":"它適合比較過去習慣與現代生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"used to get up","meaning":"以前會起床","examples":[{"en":"People used to get up in the middle of the night.","zh":"人們以前會在半夜起床。"},{"en":"Used to get up means regularly got up in the past but not necessarily now.","zh":"used to get up 指過去經常起床，但現在未必如此。"},{"en":"Before electric lighting, some people used to get up during the night and then sleep again.","zh":"在電燈出現前，有些人以前會半夜起床，然後再睡。"},{"en":"This structure describes past habits.","zh":"這個結構描述過去習慣。"},{"en":"It often contrasts old routines with present routines.","zh":"它常把舊日常與現在日常作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the middle of the night","meaning":"在半夜","examples":[{"en":"People used to get up in the middle of the night.","zh":"人們以前會在半夜起床。"},{"en":"In the middle of the night means during the late night hours, when most people are asleep.","zh":"in the middle of the night 指深夜時分，通常大部分人都在睡覺。"},{"en":"I woke up in the middle of the night after a strange dream.","zh":"我做了一個奇怪的夢後在半夜醒來。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an unusual or quiet time.","zh":"這個片語暗示一個不尋常或安靜的時間。"},{"en":"It is common in stories about sleep and dreams.","zh":"它常見於關於睡眠和夢的故事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have a chat","meaning":"聊天","examples":[{"en":"People might have a chat before going back to bed.","zh":"人們可能在回去睡覺前聊天。"},{"en":"To have a chat means to talk informally for a short time.","zh":"have a chat 指非正式地談一會兒。"},{"en":"The two students had a chat about their assignment after class.","zh":"兩名學生下課後聊了一下課業。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds relaxed and conversational.","zh":"這個片語聽起來輕鬆而口語。"},{"en":"It usually suggests friendly, casual conversation.","zh":"它通常暗示友善、隨意的對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"something to eat","meaning":"一點吃的東西","examples":[{"en":"People might get up in the night and have something to eat.","zh":"人們可能半夜起床並吃一點東西。"},{"en":"Something to eat means some food, usually without specifying exactly what.","zh":"something to eat 指一些食物，通常不特別說明是甚麼。"},{"en":"After waking up early, he had something to eat before studying.","zh":"他提早醒來後，在溫習前吃了一點東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and general.","zh":"這個片語較口語而籠統。"},{"en":"It is useful when the type of food is not important.","zh":"當食物種類不重要時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"go back to bed","meaning":"回去睡覺","examples":[{"en":"After chatting or eating, people would go back to bed.","zh":"聊天或吃東西後，人們會回去睡覺。"},{"en":"To go back to bed means to return to bed and sleep again.","zh":"go back to bed 指回到床上並再次睡覺。"},{"en":"She woke up at three but went back to bed after drinking some water.","zh":"她三時醒來，喝水後便回去睡覺。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when talking about interrupted sleep.","zh":"這個片語常用於談論睡眠被打斷。"},{"en":"It suggests the person had already been sleeping earlier.","zh":"它暗示該人之前已經在睡覺。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"try it myself","meaning":"自己試試","examples":[{"en":"Luke tried segmented sleeping himself.","zh":"Luke 自己試了分段睡眠。"},{"en":"To try it myself means to test or experience something personally.","zh":"try it myself 指親自測試或體驗某事。"},{"en":"After reading about dream diaries, I decided to try it myself.","zh":"讀到夢境日記後，我決定自己試試。"},{"en":"Trying something personally can help people understand a theory better.","zh":"親自嘗試可以幫助人更好理解理論。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises first-hand experience.","zh":"這個片語強調第一手經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be meant to","meaning":"據說會；本意是","examples":[{"en":"Segmented sleeping is meant to make people more creative.","zh":"分段睡眠據說會令人更有創意。"},{"en":"Be meant to means be intended or believed to have a certain effect.","zh":"be meant to 指本意是某事，或據說有某種效果。"},{"en":"This breathing exercise is meant to help people relax before sleep.","zh":"這個呼吸練習據說可以幫助人睡前放鬆。"},{"en":"The phrase does not guarantee the effect will actually happen.","zh":"這個片語不保證效果真的會發生。"},{"en":"It is often used when reporting claims about methods or treatments.","zh":"它常用於轉述關於方法或治療的說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make someone more creative","meaning":"令某人更有創意","examples":[{"en":"Segmented sleeping is meant to make people more creative.","zh":"分段睡眠據說會令人更有創意。"},{"en":"To make someone more creative means to help them produce more original ideas.","zh":"make someone more creative 指幫助某人產生更多原創想法。"},{"en":"Keeping a dream diary may make some people more creative.","zh":"記夢境日記可能令某些人更有創意。"},{"en":"Sleep may influence creativity because the mind connects ideas in unusual ways.","zh":"睡眠可能影響創意，因為大腦會以不尋常方式連接想法。"},{"en":"This phrase links an activity with improved imagination.","zh":"這個片語把某活動與想像力提升連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"give it up","meaning":"放棄","examples":[{"en":"Luke gave up segmented sleeping after a week.","zh":"Luke 試了一星期後放棄分段睡眠。"},{"en":"To give something up means to stop doing it.","zh":"give something up 指停止做某事。"},{"en":"She gave up drinking coffee late at night because it affected her sleep.","zh":"她放棄晚上喝咖啡，因為它影響睡眠。"},{"en":"People give up a routine if it does not suit their life.","zh":"如果某個習慣不適合生活，人們就會放棄。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests stopping after trying.","zh":"這個片語常暗示嘗試後停止。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fit in with","meaning":"配合；適合……","examples":[{"en":"Segmented sleeping did not fit in with Luke’s lifestyle.","zh":"分段睡眠不配合 Luke 的生活方式。"},{"en":"To fit in with something means to match or suit it well.","zh":"fit in with something 指與某事配合或適合某事。"},{"en":"Early morning lectures do not fit in with his sleep pattern.","zh":"清晨講課不配合他的睡眠模式。"},{"en":"A routine has to fit in with work, study and social life.","zh":"一個日常安排必須配合工作、學習和社交生活。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing practical compatibility.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論實際配合程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lifestyle","meaning":"生活方式","examples":[{"en":"Segmented sleeping did not fit in with Luke’s lifestyle.","zh":"分段睡眠不適合 Luke 的生活方式。"},{"en":"Lifestyle means the way a person lives, including habits, work, sleep and leisure.","zh":"lifestyle 指一個人的生活方式，包括習慣、工作、睡眠和休閒。"},{"en":"A student’s lifestyle may affect how much sleep they get.","zh":"學生的生活方式可能影響他們睡眠時間。"},{"en":"Changing sleep patterns can be difficult if someone has a busy lifestyle.","zh":"如果某人生活方式很忙碌，改變睡眠模式可能很困難。"},{"en":"This word is common in health and psychology topics.","zh":"這個字常見於健康和心理學題目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pre-school children","meaning":"學前兒童","examples":[{"en":"Most pre-school children have a short sleep during the day.","zh":"大多數學前兒童在日間會小睡一會。"},{"en":"Pre-school children are young children who have not yet started primary school.","zh":"pre-school children 指尚未開始讀小學的幼兒。"},{"en":"Pre-school children often need more sleep than older children.","zh":"學前兒童通常比年長兒童需要更多睡眠。"},{"en":"Sleep patterns in pre-school children can affect mood and learning.","zh":"學前兒童的睡眠模式會影響情緒和學習。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in child development research.","zh":"這個片語常見於兒童發展研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have a short sleep","meaning":"小睡一會","examples":[{"en":"Most pre-school children have a short sleep during the day.","zh":"大多數學前兒童在日間會小睡一會。"},{"en":"To have a short sleep means to sleep for a brief period.","zh":"have a short sleep 指睡一小段時間。"},{"en":"Some children have a short sleep after lunch.","zh":"有些兒童午飯後會小睡一會。"},{"en":"A short sleep during the day can help young children feel rested.","zh":"日間小睡一會可以幫助幼兒恢復精神。"},{"en":"This phrase is similar to “take a nap”.","zh":"這個片語與 “take a nap” 意思相近。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"during the day","meaning":"在日間","examples":[{"en":"Pre-school children often have a short sleep during the day.","zh":"學前兒童常在日間小睡一會。"},{"en":"During the day means in the daytime, not at night.","zh":"during the day 指在白天，而不是晚上。"},{"en":"Some people feel sleepy during the day if they slept badly at night.","zh":"如果晚上睡得不好，有些人在日間會覺得睏。"},{"en":"Daytime sleep may affect how easily someone falls asleep later.","zh":"日間睡眠可能影響之後是否容易入睡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing day and night routines.","zh":"這個片語適合比較日間和夜間習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"do an experiment","meaning":"進行實驗","examples":[{"en":"Some students did an experiment on children’s naps.","zh":"有些學生進行了一個關於兒童午睡的實驗。"},{"en":"To do an experiment means to carry out a controlled test or study.","zh":"do an experiment 指進行受控制的測試或研究。"},{"en":"The psychology class did an experiment on memory and sleep.","zh":"心理學班做了一個關於記憶和睡眠的實驗。"},{"en":"Experiments help researchers test ideas with evidence.","zh":"實驗幫助研究者用證據測試想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in science and psychology.","zh":"這個片語常見於科學和心理學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"last term","meaning":"上學期","examples":[{"en":"The experiment was carried out here last term.","zh":"該實驗上學期在這裡進行。"},{"en":"Last term means during the previous school or university term.","zh":"last term 指上一個學校或大學學期。"},{"en":"We studied memory last term and are studying dreams now.","zh":"我們上學期學記憶，現在學夢境。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when referring to recent academic time.","zh":"這個片語適合用於指近期學術時間。"},{"en":"It depends on the school or university calendar.","zh":"它取決於學校或大學的學期安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at what age","meaning":"在甚麼年齡","examples":[{"en":"The experiment tried to find out at what age children should stop having naps.","zh":"該實驗嘗試找出兒童應在甚麼年齡停止午睡。"},{"en":"At what age asks about the age when something happens or should happen.","zh":"at what age 用來詢問某事在甚麼年齡發生或應該發生。"},{"en":"Researchers asked at what age children begin to remember dreams clearly.","zh":"研究者詢問兒童在甚麼年齡開始清楚記得夢境。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in child development questions.","zh":"這個片語適合用於兒童發展問題。"},{"en":"It focuses on timing in a person’s growth.","zh":"它着重人成長過程中的時間點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stop having naps","meaning":"停止午睡","examples":[{"en":"The students studied when children should stop having naps.","zh":"學生研究兒童應何時停止午睡。"},{"en":"To stop having naps means to no longer sleep for a short time during the day.","zh":"stop having naps 指不再在日間短時間睡覺。"},{"en":"Some children stop having naps before they start primary school.","zh":"有些兒童在入讀小學前已停止午睡。"},{"en":"Stopping naps too early may make some young children tired and irritable.","zh":"太早停止午睡可能令部分幼兒疲倦和易怒。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in discussions of child sleep routines.","zh":"這個片語常見於討論兒童睡眠習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"find an answer","meaning":"找到答案","examples":[{"en":"The students did not really find an answer.","zh":"學生其實沒有真正找到答案。"},{"en":"To find an answer means to discover a solution or conclusion.","zh":"find an answer 指找到解決方法或結論。"},{"en":"The researchers could not find a clear answer from the data.","zh":"研究者無法從數據中找到清晰答案。"},{"en":"Not every experiment produces a simple answer.","zh":"不是每個實驗都會產生簡單答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing research results.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論研究結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spend time doing","meaning":"花時間做某事","examples":[{"en":"The students spent a lot of time working out the methodology.","zh":"學生花了很多時間制定研究方法。"},{"en":"To spend time doing something means to use time on that activity.","zh":"spend time doing something 指用時間做某活動。"},{"en":"Susie spent time reading articles before choosing a research question.","zh":"Susie 花時間閱讀文章，然後才選定研究問題。"},{"en":"Spending time on planning can make the final assignment stronger.","zh":"花時間規劃可以令最終課業更好。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights effort and time use.","zh":"這個片語突出努力和時間使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"work out","meaning":"制定；想出","examples":[{"en":"The students spent time working out the most appropriate methodology.","zh":"學生花時間制定最合適的研究方法。"},{"en":"To work out something means to think carefully and decide or solve it.","zh":"work out something 指仔細思考並決定或解決某事。"},{"en":"They worked out how many participants they would need.","zh":"他們想出需要多少參加者。"},{"en":"Working out a method carefully can prevent problems later.","zh":"仔細制定方法可以防止之後出現問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in planning and problem-solving.","zh":"這個片語常見於規劃和解難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the most appropriate methodology","meaning":"最合適的研究方法","examples":[{"en":"The students worked out the most appropriate methodology for the experiment.","zh":"學生為實驗制定了最合適的研究方法。"},{"en":"The most appropriate methodology means the best research method for the question being studied.","zh":"the most appropriate methodology 指最適合研究問題的研究方法。"},{"en":"For dream research, self-reporting may be the most appropriate methodology.","zh":"對夢境研究而言，自我報告可能是最合適的研究方法。"},{"en":"A good methodology should match the aim, participants and ethical requirements.","zh":"好的研究方法應配合目標、參加者和倫理要求。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in academic research.","zh":"這個片語在學術研究中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the results didn’t seem to","meaning":"結果似乎沒有……","examples":[{"en":"The results did not seem to show any obvious patterns.","zh":"結果似乎沒有顯示任何明顯模式。"},{"en":"The results didn’t seem to means the findings appeared not to do something.","zh":"the results didn’t seem to 指研究結果看起來沒有做到某事。"},{"en":"The results did not seem to support the original theory.","zh":"結果似乎沒有支持原本理論。"},{"en":"This phrase is cautious because it avoids sounding too absolute.","zh":"這個片語較謹慎，避免語氣過於絕對。"},{"en":"It is useful when interpreting uncertain data.","zh":"它適合用於詮釋不確定數據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"show obvious patterns","meaning":"顯示明顯模式","examples":[{"en":"The results did not show any obvious patterns.","zh":"結果沒有顯示任何明顯模式。"},{"en":"To show obvious patterns means to reveal clear repeated trends or relationships.","zh":"show obvious patterns 指顯示清楚重複出現的趨勢或關係。"},{"en":"The sleep data did not show obvious patterns between bedtime and dream recall.","zh":"睡眠數據沒有顯示就寢時間與夢境回憶之間有明顯模式。"},{"en":"If results show no obvious pattern, researchers may need more data or a better method.","zh":"如果結果沒有顯示明顯模式，研究者可能需要更多數據或更好的方法。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in data analysis.","zh":"這個片語常見於數據分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"let’s think about","meaning":"我們來想想……","examples":[{"en":"Luke suggests that they think about their assignment.","zh":"Luke 建議他們想想自己的課業。"},{"en":"Let’s think about means let us consider or plan something together.","zh":"let’s think about 指我們一起考慮或規劃某事。"},{"en":"Let’s think about the research question before choosing participants.","zh":"我們先想想研究問題，再選擇參加者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for moving a discussion into planning.","zh":"這個片語適合把討論轉入規劃。"},{"en":"It sounds cooperative and conversational.","zh":"它聽起來合作而口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"last time","meaning":"上一次","examples":[{"en":"Luke had problems with the final stage last time.","zh":"Luke 上一次在最後階段遇到問題。"},{"en":"Last time means on the previous occasion.","zh":"last time 指上一次的情況。"},{"en":"Last time, Susie lost marks because her self-assessment was weak.","zh":"上一次，Susie 因自我評估薄弱而失分。"},{"en":"This phrase connects the current task with earlier experience.","zh":"這個片語把目前任務與早前經驗連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when learning from previous mistakes.","zh":"它適合用於從過往錯誤中學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have problems with","meaning":"在……方面遇到問題","examples":[{"en":"Luke had problems with the final stage of the previous assignment.","zh":"Luke 在上一份課業的最後階段遇到問題。"},{"en":"To have problems with something means to find it difficult or troublesome.","zh":"have problems with something 指覺得某事困難或麻煩。"},{"en":"Many students have problems with statistical analysis.","zh":"很多學生在統計分析方面遇到問題。"},{"en":"Identifying where you had problems helps you improve next time.","zh":"找出自己在哪裡遇到問題，有助下次改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing learning difficulties.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論學習困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the final stage","meaning":"最後階段","examples":[{"en":"Luke struggled with the final stage of the previous assignment.","zh":"Luke 在上一份課業的最後階段感到吃力。"},{"en":"The final stage means the last part of a process or task.","zh":"final stage 指一個過程或任務的最後部分。"},{"en":"The final stage of the assignment involved evaluation and self-assessment.","zh":"課業的最後階段涉及評估和自我評估。"},{"en":"Students may rush the final stage if they leave work too late.","zh":"如果學生太遲才做功課，可能會匆忙處理最後階段。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe project structure.","zh":"這個片語有助描述項目結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"describe and justify","meaning":"描述並說明……的理據","examples":[{"en":"The students had to describe and justify how successful they thought they had been.","zh":"學生必須描述並說明他們認為自己有多成功的理據。"},{"en":"To describe and justify means to explain what happened and give reasons for your judgement.","zh":"describe and justify 指解釋發生了甚麼，並為自己的判斷提供理由。"},{"en":"Students must describe and justify their research method in the report.","zh":"學生必須在報告中描述並說明研究方法的理據。"},{"en":"Justifying an answer shows that it is based on evidence, not only opinion.","zh":"說明理據顯示答案基於證據，而不只是意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic assignments.","zh":"這個片語常見於學術課業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"how successful we thought we’d been","meaning":"我們認為自己有多成功","examples":[{"en":"The students had to judge how successful they thought they had been.","zh":"學生必須判斷他們認為自己有多成功。"},{"en":"How successful we thought we’d been means our judgement of how well we had done.","zh":"how successful we thought we’d been 指我們對自己表現有多好的判斷。"},{"en":"In the self-assessment, we explained how successful we thought we had been.","zh":"在自我評估中，我們解釋了自己認為有多成功。"},{"en":"This phrase involves reflection on performance.","zh":"這個片語涉及對表現的反思。"},{"en":"It is useful when evaluating group work or assignments.","zh":"它適合用於評估小組工作或課業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"struggle with","meaning":"在……方面吃力","examples":[{"en":"Luke struggled a bit with the action plan.","zh":"Luke 在行動計劃方面有點吃力。"},{"en":"To struggle with something means to find it difficult.","zh":"struggle with something 指覺得某事困難。"},{"en":"Susie struggled with the statistical section of the assignment.","zh":"Susie 在課業的統計部分很吃力。"},{"en":"Students may struggle with a task if they are unsure what is expected.","zh":"如果學生不清楚要求，他們可能會在任務中感到吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when talking about learning challenges.","zh":"這個片語常用於談論學習挑戰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"action plan","meaning":"行動計劃","examples":[{"en":"Luke struggled with the action plan in the previous assignment.","zh":"Luke 在上一份課業的行動計劃方面很吃力。"},{"en":"An action plan is a plan showing what steps will be taken and when.","zh":"action plan 指顯示將採取哪些步驟以及何時進行的計劃。"},{"en":"Their action plan should include research, data collection and analysis.","zh":"他們的行動計劃應包括研究、收集數據和分析。"},{"en":"A clear action plan helps students manage a complex assignment.","zh":"清晰行動計劃幫助學生管理複雜課業。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in project planning.","zh":"這個片語常見於項目規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be OK with","meaning":"對……應付得來","examples":[{"en":"Susie was OK with the planning part of the assignment.","zh":"Susie 對課業的規劃部分應付得來。"},{"en":"To be OK with something means to manage it without too much difficulty.","zh":"be OK with something 指能夠處理某事，而沒有太大困難。"},{"en":"I am OK with research, but I find statistics difficult.","zh":"我對研究應付得來，但覺得統計困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suggests moderate confidence.","zh":"這個片語較口語，表示中等程度的信心。"},{"en":"It does not mean perfect, only acceptable or manageable.","zh":"它不代表完美，只代表可接受或能處理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get marked down for","meaning":"因……被扣分","examples":[{"en":"Susie got marked down for the self-assessment.","zh":"Susie 因自我評估被扣分。"},{"en":"To get marked down for something means to lose marks because of it.","zh":"get marked down for something 指因某事而失分。"},{"en":"Students may get marked down for weak explanations or missing references.","zh":"學生可能因解釋薄弱或缺少參考資料而被扣分。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing grading.","zh":"這個片語常見於討論評分。"},{"en":"It helps identify why a student lost marks.","zh":"它有助指出學生失分原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"self-assessment","meaning":"自我評估","examples":[{"en":"Susie lost marks for the self-assessment.","zh":"Susie 因自我評估而失分。"},{"en":"Self-assessment is the process of judging your own work or performance.","zh":"self-assessment 指評價自己作品或表現的過程。"},{"en":"A self-assessment may ask students to explain what went well and what could be improved.","zh":"自我評估可能要求學生解釋哪些地方做得好，以及哪些可以改善。"},{"en":"Good self-assessment needs honesty, detail and evidence.","zh":"好的自我評估需要誠實、細節和證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reflective coursework.","zh":"這個片語常見於反思性課業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have big problems with","meaning":"在……方面有很大困難","examples":[{"en":"Susie had big problems with the statistical work.","zh":"Susie 在統計工作方面有很大困難。"},{"en":"To have big problems with something means to find it very difficult.","zh":"have big problems with something 指覺得某事非常困難。"},{"en":"Many students have big problems with interpreting graphs.","zh":"許多學生在解讀圖表方面有很大困難。"},{"en":"Big problems in one section can strongly affect the final mark.","zh":"某部分有很大問題，可能嚴重影響最終分數。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises serious difficulty.","zh":"這個片語強調嚴重困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"statistical stuff","meaning":"統計方面的內容","examples":[{"en":"Susie lost many marks on the statistical stuff.","zh":"Susie 在統計方面的內容失了很多分。"},{"en":"Statistical stuff means the parts involving numbers, data and statistical analysis.","zh":"statistical stuff 指涉及數字、數據和統計分析的部分。"},{"en":"The statistical stuff included averages, graphs and correlations.","zh":"統計方面的內容包括平均數、圖表和相關性。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and slightly vague.","zh":"這個片語較口語，而且有點籠統。"},{"en":"In formal writing, “statistical analysis” would be better.","zh":"在正式寫作中，用 “statistical analysis” 較好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lose marks","meaning":"失分","examples":[{"en":"Susie really lost marks on the statistical section.","zh":"Susie 在統計部分真的失了很多分。"},{"en":"To lose marks means to receive fewer points in an assessment.","zh":"lose marks 指在評估中得到較少分數。"},{"en":"Students can lose marks for unclear methodology or weak evaluation.","zh":"學生可能因研究方法不清或評估薄弱而失分。"},{"en":"Understanding where you lost marks helps you improve next time.","zh":"了解自己在哪裡失分，有助下次改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in school and exam contexts.","zh":"這個片語常見於學校和考試語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"plan what we have to do","meaning":"規劃我們要做的事","examples":[{"en":"The students decide to plan what they have to do for the assignment.","zh":"學生決定規劃他們要為課業做的事。"},{"en":"To plan what we have to do means to organise the tasks that must be completed.","zh":"plan what we have to do 指組織必須完成的任務。"},{"en":"Before starting, we should plan what we have to do each week.","zh":"開始前，我們應規劃每星期要做的事。"},{"en":"Planning tasks helps avoid confusion and last-minute pressure.","zh":"規劃任務有助避免混亂和最後一刻壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for group assignments.","zh":"這個片語適合小組課業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"decide on","meaning":"決定；選定","examples":[{"en":"The students first have to decide on their research question.","zh":"學生首先要選定研究問題。"},{"en":"To decide on something means to choose it after thinking about options.","zh":"decide on something 指在考慮選項後作出選擇。"},{"en":"They decided on sleep and dream recall as their topic.","zh":"他們選定睡眠與夢境回憶作為題目。"},{"en":"Deciding on a clear question is important before choosing a method.","zh":"在選擇方法前，決定清晰問題很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in planning and decision-making.","zh":"這個片語常見於規劃和決策。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"research question","meaning":"研究問題","examples":[{"en":"The students need to decide on their research question.","zh":"學生需要選定研究問題。"},{"en":"A research question is the main question a study tries to answer.","zh":"research question 指研究嘗試回答的主要問題。"},{"en":"Their research question might ask whether sleep length affects dream recall.","zh":"他們的研究問題可能是睡眠長短是否影響夢境回憶。"},{"en":"A strong research question should be clear, focused and measurable.","zh":"強的研究問題應清晰、聚焦並可量度。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to academic research.","zh":"這個片語是學術研究的核心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a relationship between","meaning":"……之間的關係","examples":[{"en":"The proposed research question asks whether there is a relationship between sleep and dreams.","zh":"擬議研究問題詢問睡眠與夢之間是否有關係。"},{"en":"A relationship between two things means a connection or link between them.","zh":"a relationship between two things 指兩件事之間的連繫或關聯。"},{"en":"The study looks for a relationship between hours of sleep and dream recall.","zh":"研究尋找睡眠時數與夢境回憶之間的關係。"},{"en":"Finding a relationship does not always prove cause and effect.","zh":"找到關係不一定證明因果。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research and statistics.","zh":"這個片語常見於研究和統計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hours of sleep","meaning":"睡眠時數","examples":[{"en":"The students may study the relationship between hours of sleep and number of dreams.","zh":"學生可能研究睡眠時數與夢的數量之間的關係。"},{"en":"Hours of sleep means the amount of time someone spends sleeping.","zh":"hours of sleep 指某人睡覺所花的時間。"},{"en":"Participants will record their hours of sleep each night.","zh":"參加者會記錄每晚睡眠時數。"},{"en":"Hours of sleep can be compared with mood, memory or dream recall.","zh":"睡眠時數可以與情緒、記憶或夢境回憶作比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in sleep research.","zh":"這個片語適合用於睡眠研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"number of dreams","meaning":"夢的數量","examples":[{"en":"The students may compare hours of sleep with number of dreams.","zh":"學生可能比較睡眠時數與夢的數量。"},{"en":"Number of dreams means how many dreams a person remembers or reports.","zh":"number of dreams 指一個人記得或報告的夢有多少個。"},{"en":"The questionnaire asks participants to record the number of dreams they recall.","zh":"問卷要求參加者記錄自己記得的夢的數量。"},{"en":"The number of dreams may depend on memory, sleep stage and how soon people write them down.","zh":"夢的數量可能取決於記憶、睡眠階段和人們多快寫下夢境。"},{"en":"This phrase gives one possible variable for a dream study.","zh":"這個片語提供夢境研究中的一個可能變項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"think about who","meaning":"考慮誰……","examples":[{"en":"The students need to think about who they will study.","zh":"學生需要考慮他們要研究誰。"},{"en":"To think about who means to consider which people will be involved.","zh":"think about who 指考慮哪些人會參與。"},{"en":"Before collecting data, researchers must think about who the participants should be.","zh":"收集數據前，研究者必須考慮參加者應該是誰。"},{"en":"Choosing the right group affects how useful the results will be.","zh":"選擇合適群體會影響結果有多有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in research planning.","zh":"這個片語在研究規劃中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"do the study on","meaning":"以……為研究對象","examples":[{"en":"The students need to decide who they will do the study on.","zh":"學生需要決定以誰為研究對象。"},{"en":"To do the study on a group means to use that group as research participants.","zh":"do the study on a group 指以某群體作研究參加者。"},{"en":"They might do the study on university students.","zh":"他們可能以大學生為研究對象。"},{"en":"Researchers should choose participants who fit the research question.","zh":"研究者應選擇符合研究問題的參加者。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal but common in student discussions.","zh":"這個片語較口語，但常見於學生討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"use other psychology students","meaning":"使用其他心理學學生","examples":[{"en":"Susie suggests using other psychology students as participants.","zh":"Susie 建議使用其他心理學學生作為參加者。"},{"en":"To use other psychology students means to choose students from the same subject as research participants.","zh":"use other psychology students 指選擇同一學科的學生作為研究參加者。"},{"en":"Using other psychology students may be convenient because they are easy to contact.","zh":"使用其他心理學學生可能方便，因為容易聯絡他們。"},{"en":"However, psychology students may know the topic too well and affect the results.","zh":"不過，心理學學生可能太熟悉題目，從而影響結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one possible participant choice.","zh":"這個片語描述一種可能的參加者選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"people from a different department","meaning":"來自另一個學系的人","examples":[{"en":"Luke suggests using people from a different department.","zh":"Luke 建議使用來自另一個學系的人。"},{"en":"People from a different department are students or staff from another academic subject area.","zh":"people from a different department 指來自另一個學科範疇的學生或職員。"},{"en":"Researchers may use people from a different department to avoid bias.","zh":"研究者可能使用另一個學系的人，以避免偏差。"},{"en":"Different departments can provide participants with different backgrounds and habits.","zh":"不同學系可以提供背景和習慣不同的參加者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in university research contexts.","zh":"這個片語適合大學研究語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"history students","meaning":"歷史系學生","examples":[{"en":"Luke suggests doing the study on history students.","zh":"Luke 建議以歷史系學生為研究對象。"},{"en":"History students are students who study history as their subject.","zh":"history students 指修讀歷史作為學科的學生。"},{"en":"History students may be less familiar with psychology experiments than psychology students.","zh":"歷史系學生可能比心理學學生較不熟悉心理學實驗。"},{"en":"Using history students could give the study a different participant group.","zh":"使用歷史系學生可以為研究提供不同參加者群體。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific academic group.","zh":"這個片語識別一個特定學術群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"literature students","meaning":"文學系學生","examples":[{"en":"Susie considers using literature students for the study.","zh":"Susie 考慮使用文學系學生作研究。"},{"en":"Literature students are students who study novels, poems, plays and other written texts.","zh":"literature students 指研究小說、詩歌、戲劇和其他文本的學生。"},{"en":"Literature students may be interested in dreams because dreams often appear in stories.","zh":"文學系學生可能對夢感興趣，因為夢常出現在故事中。"},{"en":"However, their subject background might influence how they describe dreams.","zh":"不過，他們的學科背景可能影響他們如何描述夢境。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies another possible participant group.","zh":"這個片語識別另一個可能參加者群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"forget that idea","meaning":"算了；放棄那個想法","examples":[{"en":"Susie decides to forget the idea of using literature students.","zh":"Susie 決定放棄使用文學系學生這個想法。"},{"en":"To forget that idea means to stop considering it.","zh":"forget that idea 指停止考慮某個想法。"},{"en":"We thought about using online questions, but then we forgot that idea.","zh":"我們想過使用網上問題，但後來放棄了那個想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and suggests dropping a plan.","zh":"這個片語較口語，暗示放下某個計劃。"},{"en":"It is useful when one option no longer seems suitable.","zh":"當某選項不再合適時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"think about our methodology","meaning":"考慮我們的研究方法","examples":[{"en":"The students then have to think about their methodology.","zh":"學生接着要考慮他們的研究方法。"},{"en":"To think about our methodology means to consider how the research will be carried out.","zh":"think about our methodology 指考慮研究將如何進行。"},{"en":"They need to think about their methodology before collecting data.","zh":"他們需要在收集數據前考慮研究方法。"},{"en":"A weak methodology can make results difficult to trust.","zh":"薄弱的研究方法會令結果難以被信任。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to research planning.","zh":"這個片語是研究規劃的核心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"use observation","meaning":"使用觀察法","examples":[{"en":"The students consider using observation as a methodology.","zh":"學生考慮使用觀察法作為研究方法。"},{"en":"To use observation means to collect data by watching behaviour directly.","zh":"use observation 指透過直接觀察行為收集數據。"},{"en":"Psychologists may use observation to study children’s play.","zh":"心理學家可能使用觀察法研究兒童遊戲。"},{"en":"Observation may not suit dream research because dreams cannot be watched directly.","zh":"觀察法未必適合夢境研究，因為夢不能被直接觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase names one research method.","zh":"這個片語命名一種研究方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not seem appropriate","meaning":"似乎不合適","examples":[{"en":"Observation does not seem appropriate for this study.","zh":"觀察法似乎不適合這項研究。"},{"en":"Not seem appropriate means does not appear suitable or right for the purpose.","zh":"not seem appropriate 指看來不適合某目的。"},{"en":"A phone survey does not seem appropriate if participants must answer immediately after waking up.","zh":"如果參加者必須醒來後立即回答，電話調查似乎不合適。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a careful judgement rather than a blunt rejection.","zh":"這個片語給出謹慎判斷，而不是直接否定。"},{"en":"It is useful in academic discussion.","zh":"它適合用於學術討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"self-reporting","meaning":"自我報告","examples":[{"en":"Luke thinks the study needs to use self-reporting.","zh":"Luke 認為這項研究需要使用自我報告。"},{"en":"Self-reporting means participants provide information about their own experiences or behaviour.","zh":"self-reporting 指參加者提供關於自己經驗或行為的資料。"},{"en":"Dream research often uses self-reporting because only the dreamer knows the dream content.","zh":"夢境研究常使用自我報告，因為只有做夢者知道夢的內容。"},{"en":"Self-reporting can be useful, but memory and honesty may affect the data.","zh":"自我報告可以有用，但記憶和誠實程度可能影響數據。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in psychology research.","zh":"這個片語常見於心理學研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"answer questions online","meaning":"在網上回答問題","examples":[{"en":"The students could ask participants to answer questions online.","zh":"學生可以要求參加者在網上回答問題。"},{"en":"To answer questions online means to respond through a website, form or digital platform.","zh":"answer questions online 指透過網站、表格或數碼平台作答。"},{"en":"Participants can answer questions online if they receive a survey link.","zh":"如果收到問卷連結，參加者可以在網上回答問題。"},{"en":"Online questionnaires are convenient, but they may not suit every research situation.","zh":"網上問卷很方便，但未必適合每種研究情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a digital data-collection method.","zh":"這個片語描述數碼數據收集方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in this case","meaning":"在這種情況下","examples":[{"en":"In this case, paper might be better than online questions.","zh":"在這種情況下，紙本可能比網上問題更好。"},{"en":"In this case means in this particular situation.","zh":"in this case 指在這個特定情況下。"},{"en":"In this case, a short paper diary may be easier for participants.","zh":"在這種情況下，簡短紙本日記可能對參加者更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase helps apply a general idea to one specific example.","zh":"這個片語有助把一般想法應用到具體例子。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining a decision.","zh":"它適合用於解釋決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"paper might be better","meaning":"紙本可能較好","examples":[{"en":"Paper might be better because participants will answer just after waking up.","zh":"紙本可能較好，因為參加者會在剛醒來後作答。"},{"en":"Paper might be better means a paper form may be more suitable than another method.","zh":"paper might be better 指紙本表格可能比另一方法更合適。"},{"en":"Paper might be better if participants are too sleepy to use a phone.","zh":"如果參加者太睏而不想用電話，紙本可能較好。"},{"en":"A paper diary beside the bed can make immediate recording easier.","zh":"放在床邊的紙本日記可以令即時記錄更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a cautious suggestion.","zh":"這個片語給出謹慎建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"straight after","meaning":"剛……之後立即","examples":[{"en":"The participants will answer the questions straight after they wake up.","zh":"參加者會在醒來後立即回答問題。"},{"en":"Straight after means immediately after something happens.","zh":"straight after 指某事發生後立即。"},{"en":"Participants should write down their dreams straight after waking up.","zh":"參加者應在醒來後立即寫下夢境。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that there should be no delay.","zh":"這個片語強調不應有延誤。"},{"en":"It is useful when timing affects memory.","zh":"當時間會影響記憶時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"half-asleep","meaning":"半睡半醒","examples":[{"en":"The participants may still be half-asleep when answering the questions.","zh":"參加者回答問題時可能仍然半睡半醒。"},{"en":"Half-asleep means not fully awake and still partly sleepy.","zh":"half-asleep 指尚未完全清醒，仍帶有睡意。"},{"en":"I wrote down my dream while I was still half-asleep.","zh":"我仍半睡半醒時便寫下夢境。"},{"en":"People who are half-asleep may make mistakes or write unclearly.","zh":"半睡半醒的人可能會犯錯或寫得不清楚。"},{"en":"This word is useful in sleep-related contexts.","zh":"這個字適合用於睡眠相關語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"check the ethical guidelines","meaning":"查閱倫理指引","examples":[{"en":"The students have to check the ethical guidelines for the research.","zh":"學生必須查閱研究的倫理指引。"},{"en":"To check the ethical guidelines means to read rules about how research should be done responsibly.","zh":"check the ethical guidelines 指閱讀關於如何負責任地進行研究的規則。"},{"en":"Psychology students must check ethical guidelines before involving participants.","zh":"心理學學生在涉及參加者前必須查閱倫理指引。"},{"en":"Ethical guidelines protect participants from harm, pressure and misuse of data.","zh":"倫理指引保護參加者免受傷害、壓力和數據濫用。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in research planning.","zh":"這個片語在研究規劃中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"this sort of research","meaning":"這類研究","examples":[{"en":"The students need to check the ethical guidelines for this sort of research.","zh":"學生需要為這類研究查閱倫理指引。"},{"en":"This sort of research means this kind or type of research.","zh":"this sort of research 指這種類型的研究。"},{"en":"This sort of research involves personal information about sleep and dreams.","zh":"這類研究涉及關於睡眠與夢的個人資料。"},{"en":"Different sorts of research may have different ethical requirements.","zh":"不同類型研究可能有不同倫理要求。"},{"en":"This phrase is conversational but still useful in academic discussion.","zh":"這個片語較口語，但仍適合學術討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"involve humans","meaning":"涉及人類","examples":[{"en":"The experiment involves humans, so there are special regulations.","zh":"實驗涉及人類，所以有特別規例。"},{"en":"To involve humans means to include people as participants in research.","zh":"involve humans 指研究中包括人類參加者。"},{"en":"Studies that involve humans must consider consent and privacy.","zh":"涉及人類的研究必須考慮同意和私隱。"},{"en":"Human participants need protection because research can affect their wellbeing.","zh":"人類參加者需要受到保護，因為研究可能影響他們的福祉。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research ethics.","zh":"這個片語常見於研究倫理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"special regulations","meaning":"特別規例","examples":[{"en":"Research involving humans has special regulations.","zh":"涉及人類的研究有特別規例。"},{"en":"Special regulations are specific rules made for a particular situation.","zh":"special regulations 指為特定情況制定的具體規則。"},{"en":"Experiments with children usually have special regulations.","zh":"涉及兒童的實驗通常有特別規例。"},{"en":"These regulations help make sure research is safe and fair.","zh":"這些規例幫助確保研究安全而公平。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing official rules.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論正式規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have a look at","meaning":"看一看","examples":[{"en":"Luke had a look at the ethical guidelines for another assignment.","zh":"Luke 為另一份課業看過倫理指引。"},{"en":"To have a look at something means to check or examine it briefly.","zh":"have a look at something 指簡短查看或檢視某物。"},{"en":"Susie had a look at the questionnaire before sending it out.","zh":"Susie 發出問卷前看了一看。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and softer than “examine carefully”.","zh":"這個片語較口語，比 “examine carefully” 語氣柔和。"},{"en":"It is common in everyday conversation.","zh":"它常見於日常對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for another assignment","meaning":"為另一份課業","examples":[{"en":"Luke looked at the ethical guidelines for another assignment.","zh":"Luke 為另一份課業查閱過倫理指引。"},{"en":"For another assignment means for a different piece of coursework.","zh":"for another assignment 指為另一份不同的課業。"},{"en":"I read about consent forms for another assignment last term.","zh":"我上學期為另一份課業讀過同意書的資料。"},{"en":"Knowledge from one assignment can help with a later one.","zh":"一份課業中的知識可以幫助之後另一份課業。"},{"en":"This phrase connects current work with previous coursework.","zh":"這個片語把目前工作與之前課業連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a whole section on","meaning":"一整節關於……","examples":[{"en":"The guidelines include a whole section on risk assessment.","zh":"指引包括一整節關於風險評估。"},{"en":"A whole section on something means a complete part of a document devoted to that topic.","zh":"a whole section on something 指文件中有完整一部分專門討論某題目。"},{"en":"The report has a whole section on research ethics.","zh":"報告有一整節關於研究倫理。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the topic is important enough to receive detailed treatment.","zh":"這個片語暗示該主題重要得需要詳細處理。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing documents and guidelines.","zh":"它適合用於描述文件和指引。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"risk assessment","meaning":"風險評估","examples":[{"en":"The ethical guidelines include a section on risk assessment.","zh":"倫理指引包括一節關於風險評估。"},{"en":"Risk assessment is the process of identifying possible harms and deciding how to reduce them.","zh":"risk assessment 指識別可能傷害並決定如何減低風險的過程。"},{"en":"A psychology experiment needs risk assessment before participants take part.","zh":"心理學實驗在參加者參與前需要風險評估。"},{"en":"Risk assessment protects both participants and researchers.","zh":"風險評估可以保護參加者和研究者。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research, safety and planning.","zh":"這個片語常見於研究、安全和規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"The guidelines include a section on making sure participants are not stressed unnecessarily.","zh":"指引包括一節關於確保參加者不會承受不必要壓力。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check or arrange things so that something happens or does not happen.","zh":"make sure 指檢查或安排事情，以確保某事會或不會發生。"},{"en":"Researchers must make sure participants understand the instructions.","zh":"研究者必須確保參加者明白指示。"},{"en":"In ethics, making sure participants are safe is a basic responsibility.","zh":"在倫理方面，確保參加者安全是基本責任。"},{"en":"This phrase shows careful control and responsibility.","zh":"這個片語顯示仔細控制和責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be put under stress","meaning":"承受壓力","examples":[{"en":"Participants should not be put under any unnecessary stress.","zh":"參加者不應承受任何不必要壓力。"},{"en":"To be put under stress means to be placed in a situation that causes pressure or anxiety.","zh":"be put under stress 指被置於造成壓力或焦慮的情況中。"},{"en":"Participants may be put under stress if questions are too personal or upsetting.","zh":"如果問題太私人或令人不安，參加者可能會承受壓力。"},{"en":"Ethical research avoids putting people under pressure without good reason.","zh":"合乎倫理的研究會避免無充分理由地令他人受壓。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in psychology and ethics.","zh":"這個片語常見於心理學和倫理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"unnecessary stress","meaning":"不必要的壓力","examples":[{"en":"The researchers must avoid putting participants under unnecessary stress.","zh":"研究者必須避免令參加者承受不必要壓力。"},{"en":"Unnecessary stress means pressure or worry that is not needed for the purpose of the study.","zh":"unnecessary stress 指對研究目的而言不需要的壓力或憂慮。"},{"en":"Long, confusing questions may create unnecessary stress for participants.","zh":"冗長而混亂的問題可能為參加者製造不必要壓力。"},{"en":"Researchers should design tasks that collect data without causing avoidable discomfort.","zh":"研究者應設計能收集數據但避免不必要不適的任務。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in ethical research.","zh":"這個片語在倫理研究中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have bad dreams","meaning":"發惡夢","examples":[{"en":"Susie hopes the participants will not have any bad dreams.","zh":"Susie 希望參加者不會發惡夢。"},{"en":"To have bad dreams means to experience unpleasant or frightening dreams.","zh":"have bad dreams 指經歷不愉快或令人害怕的夢。"},{"en":"Some people have bad dreams when they are stressed.","zh":"有些人在壓力大時會發惡夢。"},{"en":"A study about dreams should avoid encouraging upsetting dream experiences.","zh":"關於夢的研究應避免鼓勵令人不安的夢境經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday speech about sleep.","zh":"這個片語常見於關於睡眠的日常說話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"collect all our data","meaning":"收集所有數據","examples":[{"en":"The students need to collect all their data before analysing it.","zh":"學生需要先收集所有數據，然後才分析。"},{"en":"To collect all our data means to gather all the information needed for the study.","zh":"collect all our data 指收集研究所需的所有資料。"},{"en":"They will collect all their data from participants’ sleep diaries.","zh":"他們會從參加者的睡眠日記中收集所有數據。"},{"en":"Data collection must be complete before reliable analysis can begin.","zh":"數據收集必須完成，可靠分析才可以開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to research work.","zh":"這個片語是研究工作的核心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"analyse the data","meaning":"分析數據","examples":[{"en":"The students have to analyse the data they collect.","zh":"學生必須分析他們收集的數據。"},{"en":"To analyse the data means to examine information carefully to find patterns, relationships or meaning.","zh":"analyse the data 指仔細檢視資料，以找出模式、關係或意義。"},{"en":"They will analyse the data to see whether sleep length relates to dream recall.","zh":"他們會分析數據，看看睡眠長短是否與夢境回憶有關。"},{"en":"Data analysis turns raw answers into useful results.","zh":"數據分析把原始答案轉化為有用結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research and statistics.","zh":"這個片語常見於研究和統計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"calculate the correlation between","meaning":"計算……之間的相關性","examples":[{"en":"The students have to calculate the correlation between two variables.","zh":"學生必須計算兩個變項之間的相關性。"},{"en":"To calculate the correlation between two things means to work out how strongly they are related.","zh":"calculate the correlation between two things 指計算兩者之間關係有多強。"},{"en":"They will calculate the correlation between hours of sleep and number of dreams remembered.","zh":"他們會計算睡眠時數與記得的夢數量之間的相關性。"},{"en":"A correlation can be positive, negative or weak.","zh":"相關性可以是正相關、負相關或很弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in statistical analysis.","zh":"這個片語常見於統計分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"two variables","meaning":"兩個變項","examples":[{"en":"The study has two variables: time sleeping and number of dreams.","zh":"這項研究有兩個變項：睡眠時間和夢的數量。"},{"en":"Two variables are two factors that can change and be measured in a study.","zh":"two variables 指研究中可以變化並被量度的兩個因素。"},{"en":"In this experiment, the two variables might be sleep length and dream recall.","zh":"在這個實驗中，兩個變項可能是睡眠長度和夢境回憶。"},{"en":"Researchers compare variables to see whether they are connected.","zh":"研究者比較變項，以查看它們是否有關聯。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in experimental design.","zh":"這個片語在實驗設計中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"time sleeping","meaning":"睡眠時間","examples":[{"en":"One variable in the study is time spent sleeping.","zh":"研究中的一個變項是睡眠時間。"},{"en":"Time sleeping means the amount of time a person sleeps.","zh":"time sleeping 指一個人睡覺的時間長短。"},{"en":"Participants will record their time sleeping each night.","zh":"參加者會記錄每晚睡眠時間。"},{"en":"Time sleeping may affect memory, mood and dream recall.","zh":"睡眠時間可能影響記憶、情緒和夢境回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase is a measurable factor in sleep research.","zh":"這個片語是睡眠研究中可量度的因素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"present our results visually","meaning":"以視覺方式呈現結果","examples":[{"en":"The students need to present their results visually in a graph.","zh":"學生需要用圖表以視覺方式呈現結果。"},{"en":"To present results visually means to show findings using images, charts or graphs.","zh":"present results visually 指用圖像、圖表或圖形顯示研究結果。"},{"en":"A graph can present results visually more clearly than a long paragraph.","zh":"圖表可以比長段文字更清楚地以視覺方式呈現結果。"},{"en":"Visual presentation helps readers see patterns quickly.","zh":"視覺呈現幫助讀者快速看見模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reports and presentations.","zh":"這個片語適合用於報告和簡報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in a graph","meaning":"以圖表形式","examples":[{"en":"The students will present their results in a graph.","zh":"學生會以圖表形式呈現結果。"},{"en":"In a graph means using a visual chart to show data.","zh":"in a graph 指用視覺圖表顯示數據。"},{"en":"They may show the relationship between sleep and dreams in a graph.","zh":"他們可能以圖表形式顯示睡眠與夢之間的關係。"},{"en":"Graphs can make numerical results easier to understand.","zh":"圖表可以令數字結果更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in statistics and science reports.","zh":"這個片語常見於統計和科學報告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the final thing","meaning":"最後一件事","examples":[{"en":"The final thing is to evaluate the research.","zh":"最後一件事是評估研究。"},{"en":"The final thing means the last task or point to deal with.","zh":"the final thing 指最後要處理的任務或重點。"},{"en":"The final thing on the assignment plan is writing the conclusion.","zh":"課業計劃中的最後一件事是寫結論。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise a sequence of tasks.","zh":"這個片語有助組織一系列任務。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken planning.","zh":"它常見於口頭規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"evaluate the research","meaning":"評估研究","examples":[{"en":"The students have to think about and evaluate their research.","zh":"學生必須思考並評估自己的研究。"},{"en":"To evaluate the research means to judge its strengths, weaknesses and reliability.","zh":"evaluate the research 指判斷研究的優點、缺點和可靠性。"},{"en":"Students should evaluate the research by discussing sample size, method and possible bias.","zh":"學生應透過討論樣本大小、方法和可能偏差來評估研究。"},{"en":"Evaluation helps show whether the results can be trusted.","zh":"評估有助顯示結果是否可信。"},{"en":"This phrase is essential in academic assignments.","zh":"這個片語在學術課業中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"seem quite straightforward","meaning":"看起來相當清晰直接","examples":[{"en":"The assignment plan seems quite straightforward.","zh":"課業計劃看起來相當清晰直接。"},{"en":"To seem quite straightforward means to appear fairly clear and not too complicated.","zh":"seem quite straightforward 指看起來頗清楚，而且不太複雜。"},{"en":"The methodology seems quite straightforward once the variables are chosen.","zh":"一旦選定變項，研究方法看起來相當清晰直接。"},{"en":"A task may seem straightforward at first but still need careful planning.","zh":"一項任務起初可能看似簡單，但仍需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses cautious confidence.","zh":"這個片語表達謹慎的信心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 17/task-4":[{"front":"have a good time","meaning":"玩得開心；享受愉快時光","examples":[{"en":"Dancing is something that humans do when they want to have a good time.","zh":"跳舞是人類想玩得開心時會做的事情。"},{"en":"To have a good time means to enjoy yourself and feel happy during an activity.","zh":"have a good time 的意思是在活動中享受自己並感到快樂。"},{"en":"Children usually have a good time at a birthday party with games and music.","zh":"孩子在有遊戲和音樂的生日派對上通常玩得很開心。"},{"en":"People remember events more warmly when they have a good time with others.","zh":"當人們與別人享受愉快時光，他們會更溫暖地記住活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when talking about enjoyment and leisure.","zh":"這個短語常用於談論享受和休閒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"universal response to","meaning":"對……的普遍反應","examples":[{"en":"Dancing is a universal response to music.","zh":"跳舞是人類對音樂的普遍反應。"},{"en":"A universal response to something is a reaction that appears among many or all groups of people.","zh":"universal response to something 是許多或所有群體中都會出現的反應。"},{"en":"Smiling can be a universal response to kindness.","zh":"微笑可以是對善意的普遍反應。"},{"en":"If an action is universal, it suggests that many humans naturally understand or share it.","zh":"如果一種行動是普遍的，這表示許多人類自然理解或共有它。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a stimulus with a widely shared reaction.","zh":"這個短語把刺激與廣泛共享的反應連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"found in all cultures","meaning":"存在於所有文化中","examples":[{"en":"Dancing is found in all cultures.","zh":"跳舞存在於所有文化中。"},{"en":"Found in all cultures means existing among people in every society or cultural group.","zh":"found in all cultures 的意思是存在於每個社會或文化群體之中。"},{"en":"Music, storytelling, and family celebrations are found in all cultures in different forms.","zh":"音樂、說故事和家庭慶祝以不同形式存在於所有文化中。"},{"en":"When something is found in all cultures, it may show a deep human need or habit.","zh":"當某事存在於所有文化中，它可能顯示深層人類需要或習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses worldwide presence.","zh":"這個短語強調全球存在。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"only been discovered recently","meaning":"直到最近才被發現","examples":[{"en":"It has only been discovered recently that dancing is good for our health.","zh":"直到最近才被發現，跳舞對我們健康有益。"},{"en":"Only been discovered recently means people found out or proved something not long ago.","zh":"only been discovered recently 的意思是人們不久前才發現或證明某事。"},{"en":"It has only been discovered recently that some classroom activities can improve memory.","zh":"直到最近才被發現，有些課堂活動可以改善記憶。"},{"en":"New research can change how people understand an old habit.","zh":"新研究可以改變人們對一個舊習慣的理解。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that the knowledge is new, even if the activity is old.","zh":"這個短語強調知識是新的，即使活動本身很古老。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"not only…but also","meaning":"不但……而且……","examples":[{"en":"Dancing not only makes us feel good, but also benefits our health.","zh":"跳舞不但令我們感覺良好，而且有益健康。"},{"en":"Not only…but also is used to emphasise two connected points.","zh":"not only…but also 用來強調兩個互相關連的要點。"},{"en":"Reading not only improves vocabulary, but also develops imagination.","zh":"閱讀不但改善詞彙，而且培養想像力。"},{"en":"This structure makes the second point feel like an additional strong benefit.","zh":"這個結構令第二點感覺像額外而有力的好處。"},{"en":"It is useful in essays when you want to add force to an argument.","zh":"當你想加強論點時，這個結構很適合用於文章。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"extremely good for","meaning":"對……極有益","examples":[{"en":"Dancing is extremely good for our health.","zh":"跳舞對我們健康極有益。"},{"en":"Extremely good for something means very beneficial to it.","zh":"extremely good for something 的意思是對某事非常有好處。"},{"en":"Regular sleep is extremely good for concentration and mood.","zh":"規律睡眠對專注力和心情極有益。"},{"en":"Activities that are good for health can improve both body and mind.","zh":"對健康有益的活動可以同時改善身體和心理。"},{"en":"This phrase gives strong positive emphasis.","zh":"這個短語帶有強烈正面強調。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"forms of exercise","meaning":"運動形式","examples":[{"en":"Dancing, like other forms of exercise, releases hormones.","zh":"跳舞像其他運動形式一樣，會釋放荷爾蒙。"},{"en":"Forms of exercise are different types of physical activity that help the body move and work.","zh":"forms of exercise 是幫助身體活動和運作的不同類型體力活動。"},{"en":"Swimming, jogging, cycling, and yoga are all forms of exercise.","zh":"游泳、緩跑、踩單車和瑜伽都是運動形式。"},{"en":"Different forms of exercise suit different ages, abilities, and interests.","zh":"不同運動形式適合不同年齡、能力和興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase groups physical activities into categories.","zh":"這個短語把體力活動歸入不同類別。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"release hormones","meaning":"釋放荷爾蒙","examples":[{"en":"Dancing releases hormones such as dopamine.","zh":"跳舞會釋放多巴胺等荷爾蒙。"},{"en":"To release hormones means for the body to produce and send chemical messengers into the body.","zh":"release hormones 的意思是身體產生並釋出化學信使。"},{"en":"Exercise can release hormones that affect mood, energy, and stress.","zh":"運動可以釋放影響心情、能量和壓力的荷爾蒙。"},{"en":"When the body releases helpful hormones, people may feel calmer or happier.","zh":"當身體釋放有幫助的荷爾蒙，人可能感到更平靜或更快樂。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in health and biology discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於健康和生物討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"such as","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"Dancing releases hormones, such as dopamine.","zh":"跳舞會釋放荷爾蒙，例如多巴胺。"},{"en":"Such as means for example.","zh":"such as 的意思是例如。"},{"en":"Healthy habits, such as sleeping well and drinking water, can support learning.","zh":"健康習慣，例如睡得好和喝水，可以支援學習。"},{"en":"Giving examples makes an explanation clearer and more concrete.","zh":"給出例子能令解釋更清楚和更具體。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples from a wider group.","zh":"這個短語從較大類別中引出例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dopamine","meaning":"多巴胺","examples":[{"en":"Dopamine can make people feel relaxed and happy.","zh":"多巴胺可以令人感到放鬆和快樂。"},{"en":"Dopamine is a chemical in the brain linked with pleasure, motivation, and reward.","zh":"dopamine 是大腦中的一種化學物質，與愉悅、動力和獎賞有關。"},{"en":"Enjoyable activities, such as exercise or music, can affect dopamine levels.","zh":"愉快活動，例如運動或音樂，可以影響多巴胺水平。"},{"en":"Dopamine is often discussed when people talk about mood and motivation.","zh":"當人們談論心情和動力時，常會討論多巴胺。"},{"en":"This word is scientific but common in health discussions.","zh":"這個詞是科學用語，但在健康討論中很常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"feel relaxed and happy","meaning":"感到放鬆和快樂","examples":[{"en":"Dancing can make us feel relaxed and happy.","zh":"跳舞可以令我們感到放鬆和快樂。"},{"en":"To feel relaxed and happy means to feel calm, comfortable, and pleased.","zh":"feel relaxed and happy 的意思是感到平靜、舒服和愉快。"},{"en":"Listening to gentle music after work can make people feel relaxed and happy.","zh":"下班後聽柔和音樂可以令人感到放鬆和快樂。"},{"en":"Activities that reduce pressure can improve mood and help people enjoy the moment.","zh":"減少壓力的活動可以改善心情，幫助人享受當下。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive emotional state.","zh":"這個短語描述正面情緒狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reduce feelings of","meaning":"減少……感覺","examples":[{"en":"Dancing reduces feelings of stress or anxiety.","zh":"跳舞可以減少壓力或焦慮感。"},{"en":"To reduce feelings of something means to make that emotion weaker or less frequent.","zh":"reduce feelings of something 的意思是令某種情緒變弱或較少出現。"},{"en":"Talking to a trusted friend can reduce feelings of loneliness.","zh":"與可信任朋友傾談可以減少孤獨感。"},{"en":"Activities that reduce negative feelings can help people cope better with daily life.","zh":"減少負面感覺的活動可以幫助人更好應付日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on lowering emotional intensity.","zh":"這個短語集中於降低情緒強度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stress or anxiety","meaning":"壓力或焦慮","examples":[{"en":"Dancing can reduce feelings of stress or anxiety.","zh":"跳舞可以減少壓力或焦慮感。"},{"en":"Stress or anxiety means pressure, worry, nervousness, or fear about situations or problems.","zh":"stress or anxiety 指因情況或問題而產生的壓力、擔心、緊張或恐懼。"},{"en":"Students may feel stress or anxiety before important exams.","zh":"學生在重要考試前可能感到壓力或焦慮。"},{"en":"If stress or anxiety lasts too long, people may need support from friends, family, or professionals.","zh":"如果壓力或焦慮持續太久，人可能需要朋友、家人或專業人士支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes common emotional difficulties.","zh":"這個短語描述常見情緒困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sociable activity","meaning":"社交活動","examples":[{"en":"Dancing is also a sociable activity.","zh":"跳舞也是一項社交活動。"},{"en":"A sociable activity is something people do together and use to meet, talk, or interact with others.","zh":"sociable activity 是人們一起做，並用來認識、交談或互動的活動。"},{"en":"Board games can be a sociable activity because friends talk while playing.","zh":"桌上遊戲可以是社交活動，因為朋友在玩時會聊天。"},{"en":"Sociable activities can improve mood because people feel connected.","zh":"社交活動可以改善心情，因為人們感到有連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an activity with a social side.","zh":"這個短語描述帶有社交一面的活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"another reason","meaning":"另一個原因","examples":[{"en":"Dancing is sociable, which is another reason it makes us feel good.","zh":"跳舞具社交性，這是它令我們感覺良好的另一個原因。"},{"en":"Another reason means an additional explanation for why something happens or is true.","zh":"another reason 的意思是解釋某事發生或成立的另一個理由。"},{"en":"Exercise improves sleep; another reason it helps mood is that it reduces stress.","zh":"運動改善睡眠；它幫助心情的另一個原因是它減少壓力。"},{"en":"Adding another reason makes an argument stronger and more complete.","zh":"加入另一個原因會令論點更有力和完整。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when building an explanation step by step.","zh":"這個短語適合逐步建立解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"compared people’s enjoyment of","meaning":"比較人們對……的享受程度","examples":[{"en":"One study compared people’s enjoyment of dancing alone and dancing in a group.","zh":"一項研究比較人們對獨自跳舞和集體跳舞的享受程度。"},{"en":"To compare people’s enjoyment of two activities means to examine which one they liked more or how they felt about each.","zh":"compare people’s enjoyment of two activities 的意思是研究人們較喜歡哪一項，或對各項活動有何感受。"},{"en":"A school survey compared students’ enjoyment of online lessons and classroom lessons.","zh":"學校問卷比較學生對網課和實體課的享受程度。"},{"en":"Comparing enjoyment helps researchers understand what makes an activity more satisfying.","zh":"比較享受程度有助研究人員理解甚麼令活動更令人滿足。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research descriptions.","zh":"這個短語常見於研究描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in front of a video","meaning":"對着影片","examples":[{"en":"Some people danced at home in front of a video.","zh":"有些人在家對着影片跳舞。"},{"en":"In front of a video means while watching or following a video on a screen.","zh":"in front of a video 的意思是一邊觀看或跟隨螢幕上的影片一邊做某事。"},{"en":"Many people exercise in front of a video when they cannot attend a class.","zh":"許多人不能上課時會對着影片做運動。"},{"en":"Following a video can be convenient, but it may feel less social than joining a group.","zh":"跟着影片可以很方便，但可能不如參加小組那麼有社交感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an activity guided by a screen.","zh":"這個短語描述由螢幕引導的活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"dancing in a group","meaning":"集體跳舞","examples":[{"en":"The study compared dancing alone with dancing in a group.","zh":"研究比較獨自跳舞和集體跳舞。"},{"en":"Dancing in a group means dancing together with other people.","zh":"dancing in a group 的意思是與其他人一起跳舞。"},{"en":"Children often enjoy dancing in a group because they can copy and encourage one another.","zh":"孩子常喜歡集體跳舞，因為他們可以互相模仿和鼓勵。"},{"en":"Group dancing can feel more enjoyable because people share rhythm and energy.","zh":"集體跳舞可以更令人享受，因為人們共享節奏和能量。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the social side of dance.","zh":"這個短語突出跳舞的社交一面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in a studio","meaning":"在舞蹈室","examples":[{"en":"Some participants danced in a group in a studio.","zh":"有些參加者在舞蹈室集體跳舞。"},{"en":"In a studio means inside a room or space designed for practice, recording, or creative work.","zh":"in a studio 的意思是在為練習、錄製或創意工作而設計的房間或空間內。"},{"en":"Dancers practise in a studio because there is space, mirrors, and suitable flooring.","zh":"舞者在舞蹈室練習，因為那裡有空間、鏡子和合適地板。"},{"en":"A studio setting can make an activity feel more structured and focused.","zh":"舞蹈室環境可以令活動感覺更有結構和更專注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the location of an organised activity.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織活動的地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"report feeling happier","meaning":"表示感覺更快樂","examples":[{"en":"People dancing in a group reported feeling happier.","zh":"集體跳舞的人表示感覺更快樂。"},{"en":"To report feeling happier means to say or state that one feels more happy than before.","zh":"report feeling happier 的意思是說出或表示自己比以前更快樂。"},{"en":"Students reported feeling calmer after a short breathing exercise.","zh":"學生在短暫呼吸練習後表示感覺更平靜。"},{"en":"Researchers often use reported feelings to understand how an activity affects mood.","zh":"研究人員常使用受訪者表示的感受，了解活動如何影響心情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes self-reported emotional change.","zh":"這個短語描述自行報告的情緒變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而","examples":[{"en":"People dancing in a group felt happier, whereas those dancing alone did not.","zh":"集體跳舞的人感覺更快樂，然而獨自跳舞的人則沒有。"},{"en":"Whereas is used to show contrast between two facts or groups.","zh":"whereas 用來顯示兩個事實或群體之間的對比。"},{"en":"Some students prefer quiet study, whereas others learn better through discussion.","zh":"有些學生喜歡安靜溫習，然而另一些學生透過討論學得更好。"},{"en":"This word helps compare different results clearly.","zh":"這個詞幫助清楚比較不同結果。"},{"en":"It is more formal than “but”.","zh":"它比 but 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in another experiment","meaning":"在另一項實驗中","examples":[{"en":"In another experiment, researchers studied students’ responses to music and movement.","zh":"在另一項實驗中，研究人員研究學生對音樂和動作的反應。"},{"en":"In another experiment means in a different study or test.","zh":"in another experiment 的意思是在另一項不同研究或測試中。"},{"en":"In another experiment, scientists asked participants to exercise before doing memory tasks.","zh":"在另一項實驗中，科學家要求參加者在做記憶任務前運動。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces additional evidence from a separate study.","zh":"這個短語引入來自另一研究的額外證據。"},{"en":"It helps organise research findings.","zh":"它幫助組織研究發現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"university researchers","meaning":"大學研究人員","examples":[{"en":"University researchers at York and Sheffield conducted the experiment.","zh":"York 和 Sheffield 的大學研究人員進行了這項實驗。"},{"en":"University researchers are people who work at universities and carry out studies to create knowledge.","zh":"university researchers 是在大學工作並進行研究以創造知識的人。"},{"en":"University researchers may design experiments, collect data, and publish results.","zh":"大學研究人員可能設計實驗、收集數據並發表結果。"},{"en":"Research from universities can influence education, health, and public policy.","zh":"大學研究可以影響教育、健康和公共政策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes academic investigators.","zh":"這個短語描述學術研究者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take a group of students","meaning":"找來一組學生","examples":[{"en":"The researchers took a group of students into a lab.","zh":"研究人員找來一組學生進入實驗室。"},{"en":"To take a group of students somewhere means to bring several students to that place.","zh":"take a group of students somewhere 的意思是帶幾名學生到某個地方。"},{"en":"A teacher may take a group of students to a museum for a history lesson.","zh":"老師可能帶一組學生到博物館上歷史課。"},{"en":"Taking students into a controlled setting helps researchers observe behaviour more carefully.","zh":"把學生帶到受控環境，有助研究人員更仔細觀察行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving a group for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為某目的移動一組人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"send someone into","meaning":"讓某人進入","examples":[{"en":"The researchers sent each student into a lab.","zh":"研究人員讓每位學生進入實驗室。"},{"en":"To send someone into a place means to ask or direct them to go inside it.","zh":"send someone into a place 的意思是要求或指示某人進入某地方。"},{"en":"The nurse sent the patient into the consultation room.","zh":"護士讓病人進入診症室。"},{"en":"In an experiment, sending people into separate rooms can help control conditions.","zh":"在實驗中，讓人進入分開房間可以幫助控制條件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes directed movement into a space.","zh":"這個短語描述被指示進入一個空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"play music","meaning":"播放音樂","examples":[{"en":"Music was played for five minutes in the lab.","zh":"實驗室內播放了五分鐘音樂。"},{"en":"To play music means to make music heard through instruments, speakers, or a device.","zh":"play music 的意思是透過樂器、揚聲器或裝置讓音樂被聽到。"},{"en":"Teachers may play music quietly while students draw.","zh":"老師可能在學生繪畫時輕聲播放音樂。"},{"en":"Playing music can change the mood of a room and influence how people move.","zh":"播放音樂可以改變房間氣氛，並影響人們如何移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing or broadcasting music.","zh":"這個短語描述演奏或播放音樂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"choose from three options","meaning":"從三個選項中選擇","examples":[{"en":"Each student had to choose from three options.","zh":"每位學生都必須從三個選項中選擇。"},{"en":"To choose from three options means to select one of three possible choices.","zh":"choose from three options 的意思是從三個可能選擇中選一個。"},{"en":"Students may choose from three essay questions in an exam.","zh":"學生可能在考試中從三條作文題目中選擇。"},{"en":"Clear options make a task easier because people know exactly what choices are available.","zh":"清晰選項令任務更容易，因為人們確切知道有哪些選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited choice.","zh":"這個短語描述有限選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sit and listen quietly","meaning":"坐着安靜聆聽","examples":[{"en":"One option was to sit and listen quietly to the music.","zh":"其中一個選項是坐着安靜聆聽音樂。"},{"en":"To sit and listen quietly means to remain seated and hear something without talking or moving much.","zh":"sit and listen quietly 的意思是坐着聽某事，不說話或不太移動。"},{"en":"Students may sit and listen quietly during a short story reading.","zh":"學生在短篇故事朗讀期間可能坐着安靜聆聽。"},{"en":"Quiet listening helps people focus on sound without distraction.","zh":"安靜聆聽幫助人們專注於聲音而不被分心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes passive and calm participation.","zh":"這個短語描述被動而平靜的參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"exercise bike","meaning":"健身單車","examples":[{"en":"Some students could cycle on an exercise bike while listening.","zh":"有些學生可以一邊聆聽，一邊踩健身單車。"},{"en":"An exercise bike is a stationary bicycle used indoors for fitness training.","zh":"exercise bike 是室內使用、用於健身訓練的固定單車。"},{"en":"People use exercise bikes at gyms when they want low-impact cardio exercise.","zh":"人們在健身室使用健身單車，進行低衝擊帶氧運動。"},{"en":"Exercise bikes allow people to move their legs without travelling anywhere.","zh":"健身單車讓人活動雙腳，而不用真的前往任何地方。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common piece of gym equipment.","zh":"這個短語指一種常見健身器材。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get up and dance","meaning":"起身跳舞","examples":[{"en":"One option was to get up and dance.","zh":"其中一個選項是起身跳舞。"},{"en":"To get up and dance means to stand up and start dancing.","zh":"get up and dance 的意思是站起來開始跳舞。"},{"en":"At a party, children may get up and dance when their favourite song begins.","zh":"在派對上，孩子聽到最喜歡的歌時可能起身跳舞。"},{"en":"Getting up to dance changes listening from a passive activity into a physical one.","zh":"起身跳舞把聆聽從被動活動變成身體活動。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active movement.","zh":"這個短語表示主動移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cognitive tasks","meaning":"認知任務","examples":[{"en":"All the students were given cognitive tasks.","zh":"所有學生都獲安排認知任務。"},{"en":"Cognitive tasks are activities that test or use thinking, memory, attention, language, or problem-solving.","zh":"cognitive tasks 是測試或使用思考、記憶、注意力、語言或解難能力的活動。"},{"en":"A puzzle can be a cognitive task because it requires planning and reasoning.","zh":"砌圖可以是認知任務，因為它需要規劃和推理。"},{"en":"Researchers use cognitive tasks to measure how well people think after different activities.","zh":"研究人員使用認知任務來量度人在不同活動後的思考表現。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in psychology and education.","zh":"這個短語常見於心理學和教育。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"perform before and after","meaning":"在前後完成","examples":[{"en":"The students had to perform tasks before and after the activity.","zh":"學生必須在活動前後完成任務。"},{"en":"To perform before and after an activity means to do a task once before it and once after it for comparison.","zh":"perform before and after an activity 的意思是在活動前做一次任務，活動後再做一次，以作比較。"},{"en":"Researchers may ask children to do memory tests before and after a lesson.","zh":"研究人員可能要求兒童在課堂前後做記憶測試。"},{"en":"Comparing performance before and after an activity helps show whether the activity made a difference.","zh":"比較活動前後的表現，有助顯示活動是否帶來改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in experiments.","zh":"這個短語常見於實驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"showed much more creativity","meaning":"展現出更多創意","examples":[{"en":"Those who chose to dance showed much more creativity.","zh":"選擇跳舞的人展現出更多創意。"},{"en":"Showed much more creativity means produced more original, flexible, or imaginative ideas.","zh":"showed much more creativity 的意思是產生更多原創、靈活或富想像力的想法。"},{"en":"Students showed much more creativity after they were allowed to choose their own topics.","zh":"學生獲准選擇自己的題目後，展現出更多創意。"},{"en":"Creative thinking can improve when people feel energised and relaxed.","zh":"當人們感到有活力和放鬆，創意思維可以改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear increase in creative performance.","zh":"這個短語描述創意表現明顯增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"problem-solving tasks","meaning":"解難任務","examples":[{"en":"The dancers showed more creativity when doing problem-solving tasks.","zh":"跳舞者在做解難任務時展現出更多創意。"},{"en":"Problem-solving tasks are activities that require people to find answers or solutions.","zh":"problem-solving tasks 是要求人們找出答案或解決方法的活動。"},{"en":"A maths puzzle is a problem-solving task because students must work out the method.","zh":"數學謎題是解難任務，因為學生必須想出方法。"},{"en":"Problem-solving tasks test flexibility because one answer may require several steps.","zh":"解難任務測試靈活性，因為一個答案可能需要幾個步驟。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in education and psychology.","zh":"這個短語常見於教育和心理學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"suffering from","meaning":"患有；受……困擾","examples":[{"en":"Dance may help people suffering from mental health problems.","zh":"舞蹈可能幫助受精神健康問題困擾的人。"},{"en":"Suffering from a problem means experiencing pain, difficulty, or illness because of it.","zh":"suffering from a problem 的意思是因某問題而經歷痛苦、困難或疾病。"},{"en":"People suffering from long-term stress may find daily tasks harder.","zh":"受長期壓力困擾的人，可能覺得日常任務更困難。"},{"en":"Someone suffering from a health problem may need support, treatment, or lifestyle changes.","zh":"患有健康問題的人可能需要支援、治療或生活方式改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in health contexts.","zh":"這個短語常用於健康語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mental health problems","meaning":"精神健康問題","examples":[{"en":"Dance may help people with mental health problems.","zh":"舞蹈可能幫助有精神健康問題的人。"},{"en":"Mental health problems are difficulties that affect mood, thinking, behaviour, or emotional well-being.","zh":"mental health problems 是影響心情、思考、行為或情緒健康的困難。"},{"en":"Anxiety and depression are examples of mental health problems.","zh":"焦慮和抑鬱是精神健康問題的例子。"},{"en":"People with mental health problems may benefit from support, connection, and professional care.","zh":"有精神健康問題的人可能受益於支援、連繫和專業照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase should be used with respect and sensitivity.","zh":"使用這個短語時應尊重和敏感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be prescribed as therapy","meaning":"被處方為治療方式","examples":[{"en":"Dance should be prescribed as therapy.","zh":"舞蹈應被處方為治療方式。"},{"en":"To be prescribed as therapy means to be recommended by a professional as part of treatment or support.","zh":"be prescribed as therapy 的意思是由專業人士建議作為治療或支援的一部分。"},{"en":"Exercise may be prescribed as therapy for some people under medical guidance.","zh":"在醫療指導下，運動可能被處方為某些人的治療方式。"},{"en":"If an activity is prescribed as therapy, it should be used carefully and appropriately.","zh":"如果一項活動被處方為治療方式，就應小心並適當使用。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an activity with health treatment.","zh":"這個短語把活動與健康治療連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"overcome issues such as","meaning":"克服例如……的問題","examples":[{"en":"Dance may help people overcome issues such as depression.","zh":"舞蹈可能幫助人們克服例如抑鬱的問題。"},{"en":"To overcome issues such as something means to deal successfully with problems of that kind.","zh":"overcome issues such as something 的意思是成功處理該類問題。"},{"en":"Counselling may help students overcome issues such as anxiety or low confidence.","zh":"輔導可能幫助學生克服例如焦慮或低自信的問題。"},{"en":"Overcoming serious issues usually requires time, support, and suitable strategies.","zh":"克服嚴重問題通常需要時間、支援和合適策略。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples of problems that may be improved.","zh":"這個短語引出可能改善的問題例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"depression","meaning":"抑鬱","examples":[{"en":"Dance may help people overcome depression.","zh":"舞蹈可能幫助人們克服抑鬱。"},{"en":"Depression is a mental health condition involving lasting sadness, low energy, and loss of interest.","zh":"depression 是一種精神健康狀況，涉及持續悲傷、低能量和失去興趣。"},{"en":"A person with depression may need support from doctors, counsellors, friends, or family.","zh":"抑鬱患者可能需要醫生、輔導員、朋友或家人的支援。"},{"en":"Enjoyable activities can support well-being, but serious depression should not be ignored.","zh":"愉快活動可以支援身心健康，但嚴重抑鬱不應被忽視。"},{"en":"This word should be used carefully because it refers to more than ordinary sadness.","zh":"這個詞應謹慎使用，因為它不只是普通傷心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"well established","meaning":"已被廣泛確認","examples":[{"en":"It is well established that dance encourages adolescent girls to exercise.","zh":"舞蹈能鼓勵青春期少女做運動，這一點已被廣泛確認。"},{"en":"Well established means widely accepted because there is strong evidence or long experience.","zh":"well established 的意思是因有強證據或長期經驗而被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"It is well established that regular reading helps vocabulary development.","zh":"規律閱讀有助詞彙發展，這一點已被廣泛確認。"},{"en":"A well-established idea is not just a guess; many people or studies support it.","zh":"已被廣泛確認的想法不只是猜測；有許多人或研究支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic and research writing.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術和研究寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a good way of encouraging","meaning":"鼓勵……的好方法","examples":[{"en":"Dance is a good way of encouraging adolescent girls to take exercise.","zh":"舞蹈是鼓勵青春期少女做運動的好方法。"},{"en":"A good way of encouraging someone to do something is an effective method for motivating them.","zh":"a good way of encouraging someone to do something 是激勵某人做某事的有效方法。"},{"en":"Games are a good way of encouraging young children to practise English.","zh":"遊戲是鼓勵幼兒練習英文的好方法。"},{"en":"Encouragement works better when the activity feels enjoyable rather than forced.","zh":"當活動感覺愉快而不是被迫，鼓勵效果更好。"},{"en":"This phrase connects method with motivation.","zh":"這個短語把方法與動機連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"adolescent girls","meaning":"青春期少女","examples":[{"en":"Dance can encourage adolescent girls to take exercise.","zh":"舞蹈可以鼓勵青春期少女做運動。"},{"en":"Adolescent girls are girls in the teenage stage between childhood and adulthood.","zh":"adolescent girls 是處於兒童與成人之間青少年階段的女孩。"},{"en":"Adolescent girls may avoid some sports if they feel embarrassed or judged.","zh":"如果青春期少女感到尷尬或被評價，她們可能避免某些運動。"},{"en":"Activities that feel fun and social can help adolescent girls stay active.","zh":"感覺有趣和具社交性的活動，可以幫助青春期少女保持活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific age and gender group.","zh":"這個短語指出特定年齡和性別群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take exercise","meaning":"做運動","examples":[{"en":"Dance encourages adolescent girls to take exercise.","zh":"舞蹈鼓勵青春期少女做運動。"},{"en":"To take exercise means to do physical activity to keep healthy.","zh":"take exercise 的意思是進行體力活動以保持健康。"},{"en":"Older adults may take exercise by walking, swimming, or joining dance classes.","zh":"長者可能透過步行、游泳或參加舞蹈課做運動。"},{"en":"Taking exercise regularly can improve strength, mood, and heart health.","zh":"規律做運動可以改善力量、心情和心臟健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English.","zh":"這個短語常見於英式英文。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"what about","meaning":"那……又如何","examples":[{"en":"Dance helps young people, but what about older people?","zh":"舞蹈幫助年輕人，但長者又如何？"},{"en":"What about is used to ask how a topic, group, or situation fits into the discussion.","zh":"what about 用來詢問某題目、群體或情況如何放入討論中。"},{"en":"Exercise is important for children, but what about busy adults?","zh":"運動對兒童很重要，但忙碌成年人又如何？"},{"en":"This phrase shifts attention to another group or question.","zh":"這個短語把注意力轉向另一群體或問題。"},{"en":"It is common in conversation and presentations.","zh":"它常見於對話和簡報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"enormous benefits","meaning":"巨大好處","examples":[{"en":"Dance has enormous benefits for people in their sixties and beyond.","zh":"舞蹈對六十多歲及以上人士有巨大好處。"},{"en":"Enormous benefits are very large or very important advantages.","zh":"enormous benefits 是非常大或非常重要的好處。"},{"en":"Regular social contact can have enormous benefits for older people’s well-being.","zh":"規律社交接觸可以對長者身心健康有巨大好處。"},{"en":"When an activity brings enormous benefits, it can affect health, mood, and daily life.","zh":"當一項活動帶來巨大好處，它可以影響健康、心情和日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase gives strong positive emphasis.","zh":"這個短語帶有強烈正面強調。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in their sixties and beyond","meaning":"六十多歲及以上","examples":[{"en":"Dance benefits people in their sixties and beyond.","zh":"舞蹈對六十多歲及以上人士有益。"},{"en":"In their sixties and beyond means aged sixty to sixty-nine and older than that.","zh":"in their sixties and beyond 的意思是年齡在六十至六十九歲，以及更年長。"},{"en":"People in their sixties and beyond may prefer gentle exercise that protects the joints.","zh":"六十多歲及以上人士可能較喜歡保護關節的溫和運動。"},{"en":"Activities for this age group should consider balance, safety, and enjoyment.","zh":"為這個年齡群體而設的活動應考慮平衡、安全和樂趣。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies older adults by age range.","zh":"這個短語以年齡範圍指出長者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"one of the great things about","meaning":"……的一大好處","examples":[{"en":"One of the great things about dance is that there are no barriers to participation.","zh":"舞蹈的一大好處是沒有參與門檻。"},{"en":"One of the great things about something introduces one major advantage of it.","zh":"one of the great things about something 用來引出某事的一個主要優點。"},{"en":"One of the great things about walking is that it costs nothing.","zh":"步行的一大好處是不用花錢。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain why an activity is attractive or useful.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋為何一項活動吸引或有用。"},{"en":"It is conversational and positive.","zh":"它語氣像對話，而且很正面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"barriers to participation","meaning":"參與門檻","examples":[{"en":"There are no barriers to participation in dance.","zh":"舞蹈沒有參與門檻。"},{"en":"Barriers to participation are things that stop or discourage people from joining an activity.","zh":"barriers to participation 是阻止或令人不願參與活動的事物。"},{"en":"High fees, difficult transport, and embarrassment can be barriers to participation.","zh":"高收費、交通困難和尷尬感都可以是參與門檻。"},{"en":"Removing barriers helps more people feel welcome and included.","zh":"移除門檻能幫助更多人感到受歡迎和被包括。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in education, sport, and community work.","zh":"這個短語常用於教育、運動和社區工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have a go","meaning":"試一試","examples":[{"en":"Anyone can have a go at dancing.","zh":"任何人都可以試一試跳舞。"},{"en":"To have a go means to try something, even if you are not sure you will be good at it.","zh":"have a go 的意思是嘗試某事，即使你不確定自己是否擅長。"},{"en":"A beginner can have a go at painting before taking formal lessons.","zh":"初學者可以先試一試繪畫，再正式上課。"},{"en":"Trying something once can reduce fear and build confidence.","zh":"嘗試一次可以減少恐懼並建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and encouraging.","zh":"這個短語是非正式而帶鼓勵意味的說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"standard of fitness","meaning":"體能水平","examples":[{"en":"People whose standard of fitness is low can still dance.","zh":"體能水平低的人仍然可以跳舞。"},{"en":"Standard of fitness means a person’s level of physical strength, stamina, and health.","zh":"standard of fitness 是一個人的體力、耐力和健康水平。"},{"en":"A beginner’s standard of fitness may be low, but gentle exercise can still help.","zh":"初學者的體能水平可能較低，但溫和運動仍有幫助。"},{"en":"Knowing someone’s fitness level helps instructors choose suitable movements.","zh":"了解某人的體能水平有助教練選擇合適動作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical ability in relation to exercise.","zh":"這個短語描述與運動有關的身體能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"quite low","meaning":"相當低","examples":[{"en":"Even people whose fitness level is quite low can have a go.","zh":"即使體能水平相當低的人也可以試一試。"},{"en":"Quite low means fairly low, but not necessarily the lowest possible.","zh":"quite low 的意思是相當低，但不一定是最低。"},{"en":"A person with quite low confidence may still speak if the group is friendly.","zh":"自信相當低的人，如果小組友善，仍可能願意發言。"},{"en":"If a difficulty level is quite low, beginners may feel less afraid to try.","zh":"如果難度相當低，初學者可能較不害怕嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a moderate degree of lowness.","zh":"這個短語描述中等程度的低。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"especially beneficial for","meaning":"對……尤其有益","examples":[{"en":"Dance can be especially beneficial for older adults.","zh":"舞蹈對長者尤其有益。"},{"en":"Especially beneficial for someone means particularly helpful or good for that group.","zh":"especially beneficial for someone 的意思是對該群體特別有幫助或有好處。"},{"en":"Gentle stretching can be especially beneficial for people who sit at desks all day.","zh":"溫和伸展對整天坐辦公桌的人尤其有益。"},{"en":"An activity may help everyone but be especially beneficial for those with a specific need.","zh":"一項活動可能幫助所有人，但對有特定需要的人尤其有益。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a group that gains extra benefit.","zh":"這個短語突出獲得額外好處的群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"older adults","meaning":"年長成年人；長者","examples":[{"en":"Dance can be especially beneficial for older adults.","zh":"舞蹈對年長成年人尤其有益。"},{"en":"Older adults are people in later adulthood, often meaning senior or elderly people.","zh":"older adults 是較後成年階段的人，常指長者或年長人士。"},{"en":"Older adults may choose gentle activities that support balance and heart health.","zh":"長者可能選擇支援平衡力和心臟健康的溫和活動。"},{"en":"Social exercise can help older adults stay active and connected.","zh":"社交性運動可以幫助長者保持活躍和有連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase is respectful and common in health discussions.","zh":"這個短語較尊重，常見於健康討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"intense workouts","meaning":"高強度運動訓練","examples":[{"en":"Some older adults cannot do more intense workouts.","zh":"有些長者不能做更高強度的運動訓練。"},{"en":"Intense workouts are exercise sessions that require high effort, strength, speed, or stamina.","zh":"intense workouts 是需要高努力、力量、速度或耐力的運動課節。"},{"en":"Sprint training and heavy circuit classes can be intense workouts.","zh":"短跑訓練和高強度循環訓練可以是高強度運動訓練。"},{"en":"Intense workouts may not suit people with low fitness, injury, or health concerns.","zh":"高強度運動訓練未必適合體能低、有傷患或有健康憂慮的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes demanding exercise.","zh":"這個短語描述要求高的運動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"gentle dance workout","meaning":"溫和的舞蹈運動","examples":[{"en":"Even a gentle dance workout helps promote heart health.","zh":"即使是溫和的舞蹈運動也有助促進心臟健康。"},{"en":"A gentle dance workout is a light exercise session using dance movements without high intensity.","zh":"gentle dance workout 是使用舞蹈動作但強度不高的輕量運動課節。"},{"en":"Older beginners may prefer a gentle dance workout with simple steps and slower music.","zh":"年長初學者可能較喜歡配合簡單步法和較慢音樂的溫和舞蹈運動。"},{"en":"Gentle workouts help people move safely while still gaining health benefits.","zh":"溫和運動幫助人安全活動，同時仍獲得健康好處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accessible exercise through dance.","zh":"這個短語描述透過舞蹈進行的易參與運動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"promote a healthy heart","meaning":"促進心臟健康","examples":[{"en":"A gentle dance workout helps to promote a healthy heart.","zh":"溫和的舞蹈運動有助促進心臟健康。"},{"en":"To promote a healthy heart means to support good heart function and circulation.","zh":"promote a healthy heart 的意思是支援良好心臟功能和血液循環。"},{"en":"Regular walking can help promote a healthy heart.","zh":"規律步行可以幫助促進心臟健康。"},{"en":"Activities that raise the heart rate safely can support long-term heart health.","zh":"安全提高心跳率的活動可以支援長遠心臟健康。"},{"en":"This phrase connects exercise with cardiovascular well-being.","zh":"這個短語把運動與心血管健康連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"plenty of evidence","meaning":"大量證據","examples":[{"en":"There is plenty of evidence that dancing lowers the risk of falls.","zh":"有大量證據顯示跳舞會降低跌倒風險。"},{"en":"Plenty of evidence means a large amount of information or research supports a point.","zh":"plenty of evidence 的意思是有大量資訊或研究支持某觀點。"},{"en":"There is plenty of evidence that smoking damages health.","zh":"有大量證據顯示吸煙損害健康。"},{"en":"Strong evidence makes an argument more convincing than opinion alone.","zh":"強證據令論點比單靠意見更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research-based writing.","zh":"這個短語常見於研究型寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lowers the risk of","meaning":"降低……風險","examples":[{"en":"Dancing lowers the risk of falls.","zh":"跳舞會降低跌倒風險。"},{"en":"To lower the risk of something means to make it less likely to happen.","zh":"lower the risk of something 的意思是令某事發生的可能性降低。"},{"en":"Wearing a seat belt lowers the risk of serious injury in a car crash.","zh":"扣安全帶可以降低車禍中嚴重受傷的風險。"},{"en":"Activities that improve balance can lower the risk of accidents among older adults.","zh":"改善平衡力的活動可以降低長者意外風險。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an action with prevention.","zh":"這個短語把行動與預防連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"A fall could result in a broken hip.","zh":"跌倒可能導致髖部骨折。"},{"en":"To result in something means to cause that outcome.","zh":"result in something 的意思是造成某結果。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can result in weak concentration the next day.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致翌日專注力差。"},{"en":"A small accident can result in serious injury if the person is vulnerable.","zh":"如果某人較脆弱，小意外也可能導致嚴重受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase connects cause and result.","zh":"這個短語連接原因與結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"broken hip","meaning":"髖部骨折","examples":[{"en":"A serious fall could result in a broken hip.","zh":"嚴重跌倒可能導致髖部骨折。"},{"en":"A broken hip is a fracture in the upper part of the thigh bone near the hip joint.","zh":"broken hip 是靠近髖關節的大腿骨上部骨折。"},{"en":"Older adults may need surgery and long recovery after a broken hip.","zh":"長者髖部骨折後可能需要手術和長時間康復。"},{"en":"Preventing falls is important because a broken hip can seriously reduce independence.","zh":"預防跌倒很重要，因為髖部骨折可以嚴重降低獨立生活能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious injury, especially for older people.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重傷患，尤其對長者而言。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"improve their balance","meaning":"改善平衡力","examples":[{"en":"Dancing helps people improve their balance.","zh":"跳舞幫助人們改善平衡力。"},{"en":"To improve their balance means to become better at staying steady while standing or moving.","zh":"improve their balance 的意思是更能在站立或移動時保持穩定。"},{"en":"Tai chi can help older adults improve their balance slowly and safely.","zh":"太極可以幫助長者慢慢並安全地改善平衡力。"},{"en":"Better balance reduces the chance of falling during daily activities.","zh":"較好的平衡力會減少日常活動中跌倒的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical skill that can be trained.","zh":"這個短語描述可以訓練的身體技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"less obvious benefits","meaning":"不太明顯的好處","examples":[{"en":"There are some less obvious benefits of dance for older people.","zh":"舞蹈對長者有一些不太明顯的好處。"},{"en":"Less obvious benefits are advantages that are real but not easy to notice at first.","zh":"less obvious benefits 是真實存在但一開始不容易注意到的好處。"},{"en":"Reading aloud has less obvious benefits, such as improving listening and family connection.","zh":"朗讀有不太明顯的好處，例如改善聆聽和家庭連繫。"},{"en":"Less obvious benefits may become clear only after careful research or experience.","zh":"不太明顯的好處可能只有在仔細研究或經驗後才變得清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase points beyond the most visible advantages.","zh":"這個短語指向最明顯優點以外的好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"realised before researching","meaning":"在研究前意識到","examples":[{"en":"The speaker had not realised one point before researching the topic.","zh":"講者在研究這個題目前沒有意識到其中一點。"},{"en":"Realised before researching means understood something before studying the topic in detail.","zh":"realised before researching 的意思是在詳細研究題目之前已理解某事。"},{"en":"I had not realised before researching that sleep affects memory so strongly.","zh":"在研究前，我沒有意識到睡眠對記憶影響如此大。"},{"en":"Research often changes what people think they already know.","zh":"研究常會改變人們以為自己已經知道的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase connects discovery with investigation.","zh":"這個短語把發現與調查連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"physical challenge","meaning":"身體上的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Dance is not just a physical challenge.","zh":"舞蹈不只是身體上的挑戰。"},{"en":"A physical challenge is something that tests the body’s strength, balance, stamina, or coordination.","zh":"physical challenge 是測試身體力量、平衡、耐力或協調的事情。"},{"en":"Climbing stairs with a heavy bag can be a physical challenge.","zh":"拿着重袋上樓梯可以是身體上的挑戰。"},{"en":"Dance can be a physical challenge because it involves movement, rhythm, and control.","zh":"舞蹈可以是身體上的挑戰，因為它涉及動作、節奏和控制。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on bodily effort.","zh":"這個短語集中於身體努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"require a lot of concentration","meaning":"需要高度集中","examples":[{"en":"Dance requires a lot of concentration.","zh":"舞蹈需要高度集中。"},{"en":"To require a lot of concentration means to need strong mental focus and attention.","zh":"require a lot of concentration 的意思是需要強烈精神專注和注意力。"},{"en":"Learning a new dance routine requires concentration because every step matters.","zh":"學習新的舞蹈動作組合需要高度集中，因為每個步法都重要。"},{"en":"Activities requiring concentration can train the brain as well as the body.","zh":"需要集中力的活動可以訓練大腦以及身體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental effort.","zh":"這個短語描述精神努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"different steps and routines","meaning":"不同舞步及動作組合","examples":[{"en":"Dancers need to remember different steps and routines.","zh":"舞者需要記住不同舞步及動作組合。"},{"en":"Different steps and routines are the various movements and repeated patterns in a dance.","zh":"different steps and routines 是舞蹈中的不同動作和重複模式。"},{"en":"A beginner may practise simple steps before learning longer routines.","zh":"初學者可能先練習簡單舞步，再學較長動作組合。"},{"en":"Remembering routines trains memory because dancers must keep movements in order.","zh":"記住動作組合可以訓練記憶，因為舞者必須保持動作次序。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the structure of dance movement.","zh":"這個短語描述舞蹈動作的結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"this kind of activity","meaning":"這類活動","examples":[{"en":"This kind of activity is especially important for older people.","zh":"這類活動對長者尤其重要。"},{"en":"This kind of activity means this type of action, exercise, or task.","zh":"this kind of activity 的意思是這種類型的行動、運動或任務。"},{"en":"This kind of activity can help children learn because it combines movement and thinking.","zh":"這類活動可以幫助兒童學習，因為它結合動作和思考。"},{"en":"When a speaker says this kind of activity, they are referring back to the activity already discussed.","zh":"當講者說 this kind of activity，就是指回已討論的活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for grouping similar actions.","zh":"這個短語適合用於歸納相似行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"force someone to","meaning":"迫使某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Dance forces the brain to process things more quickly.","zh":"舞蹈迫使大腦更快處理事物。"},{"en":"To force someone to do something means to make them do it because the situation requires it.","zh":"force someone to do something 的意思是因情況要求而令某人必須做某事。"},{"en":"A sudden deadline can force students to organise their work quickly.","zh":"突然的截止日期可以迫使學生快速整理工作。"},{"en":"Challenging activities can force the brain to adapt and respond faster.","zh":"具挑戰性的活動可以迫使大腦適應並更快回應。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe pressure, not only physical force.","zh":"這個短語可以描述壓力，而不只是身體上的強迫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"process things more quickly","meaning":"更快處理事物","examples":[{"en":"Dance forces the brain to process things more quickly.","zh":"舞蹈迫使大腦更快處理事物。"},{"en":"To process things more quickly means to understand, organise, or respond to information faster.","zh":"process things more quickly 的意思是更快理解、整理或回應資訊。"},{"en":"Practising mental maths can help students process numbers more quickly.","zh":"練習心算可以幫助學生更快處理數字。"},{"en":"Fast movement and changing steps may train the brain to react quickly.","zh":"快速動作和變化步法可能訓練大腦快速反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quicker mental handling of information.","zh":"這個短語描述更快的心理資訊處理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"retain more information","meaning":"記住更多資料","examples":[{"en":"Dance helps the brain retain more information.","zh":"舞蹈幫助大腦記住更多資料。"},{"en":"To retain more information means to remember and keep more information in the mind.","zh":"retain more information 的意思是在腦中記住並保留更多資訊。"},{"en":"Students retain more information when they review notes soon after class.","zh":"學生課後很快重溫筆記時，會記住更多資料。"},{"en":"Activities that combine movement and memory may help people remember sequences better.","zh":"結合動作和記憶的活動，可能幫助人更好記住次序。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on memory and learning.","zh":"這個短語集中於記憶和學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"current research","meaning":"目前研究","examples":[{"en":"Current research shows that dance promotes well-being.","zh":"目前研究顯示舞蹈促進身心健康。"},{"en":"Current research means studies and findings available at the present time.","zh":"current research 是目前已有的研究和發現。"},{"en":"Current research suggests that sleep affects learning and emotional control.","zh":"目前研究顯示睡眠會影響學習和情緒控制。"},{"en":"Research can change over time as new evidence appears.","zh":"隨着新證據出現，研究可能隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing recent academic findings.","zh":"這個短語常見於討論近期學術發現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"general sense of well-being","meaning":"整體身心健康感","examples":[{"en":"Dance promotes a general sense of well-being in older participants.","zh":"舞蹈促進年長參加者的整體身心健康感。"},{"en":"A general sense of well-being means an overall feeling of being healthy, comfortable, and positive.","zh":"general sense of well-being 是整體感到健康、舒服和正面的感覺。"},{"en":"A good routine can give people a general sense of well-being.","zh":"良好日常習慣可以給人整體身心健康感。"},{"en":"Well-being includes more than physical health; mood and confidence also matter.","zh":"身心健康不只包括身體健康；心情和信心也重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes overall wellness rather than one single symptom.","zh":"這個短語描述整體健康感，而不是單一症狀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"older participants","meaning":"年長參加者","examples":[{"en":"Older participants reported feeling better after dance classes.","zh":"年長參加者表示舞蹈課後感覺更好。"},{"en":"Older participants are the older people who take part in a study, class, or activity.","zh":"older participants 是參與研究、課堂或活動的年長人士。"},{"en":"Older participants may need clear instructions and safe movement options.","zh":"年長參加者可能需要清晰指示和安全動作選擇。"},{"en":"Researchers study older participants to understand how activities affect ageing and health.","zh":"研究人員研究年長參加者，以了解活動如何影響衰老和健康。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the age group involved in an activity.","zh":"這個短語指出參與活動的年齡群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"last up to","meaning":"持續長達","examples":[{"en":"The sense of well-being can last up to a week after class.","zh":"這種身心健康感可以在課堂後持續長達一星期。"},{"en":"To last up to a period means to continue for as long as that amount of time.","zh":"last up to 某段時間的意思是最多持續到該時間長度。"},{"en":"A phone battery may last up to two days if it is used lightly.","zh":"如果輕量使用，電話電池可以持續長達兩天。"},{"en":"If a positive effect lasts up to a week, it continues beyond the activity itself.","zh":"如果正面效果持續長達一星期，它就超越活動本身繼續存在。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a maximum duration.","zh":"這個短語提供最長持續時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"after a class","meaning":"課堂後","examples":[{"en":"The positive feeling can last up to a week after a class.","zh":"這種正面感覺可以在課堂後持續長達一星期。"},{"en":"After a class means following a lesson or training session.","zh":"after a class 的意思是在課堂或訓練環節之後。"},{"en":"Students often feel tired but satisfied after a dance class.","zh":"學生在舞蹈課後常感到疲倦但滿足。"},{"en":"What people do after a class can affect how much they remember or practise.","zh":"人們課堂後做甚麼，可以影響他們記得多少或練習多少。"},{"en":"This phrase marks time after a learning activity.","zh":"這個短語標示學習活動之後的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"report feeling less tired","meaning":"表示感覺較少疲倦","examples":[{"en":"Participants report feeling less tired after dancing.","zh":"參加者表示跳舞後感覺較少疲倦。"},{"en":"To report feeling less tired means to say that one has more energy or less fatigue.","zh":"report feeling less tired 的意思是表示自己更有精神或疲勞較少。"},{"en":"Some workers report feeling less tired after taking short walking breaks.","zh":"有些員工在短暫步行休息後表示感覺較少疲倦。"},{"en":"If people feel less tired, they may be more willing to stay active.","zh":"如果人們感覺較少疲倦，他們可能更願意保持活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a self-reported improvement in energy.","zh":"這個短語描述自行報告的精力改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"greater motivation to","meaning":"更大動力去……","examples":[{"en":"Participants have greater motivation to be more active.","zh":"參加者有更大動力去變得更活躍。"},{"en":"Greater motivation to do something means a stronger desire or reason to do it.","zh":"greater motivation to do something 的意思是做某事的欲望或理由更強。"},{"en":"Students have greater motivation to study when they see clear progress.","zh":"當學生看見清晰進步，他們有更大動力去學習。"},{"en":"Motivation increases when an activity feels enjoyable and achievable.","zh":"當活動感覺愉快且可做到，動力會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stronger willingness to act.","zh":"這個短語描述更強的行動意願。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be more active","meaning":"更活躍","examples":[{"en":"Participants feel motivated to be more active.","zh":"參加者感到有動力變得更活躍。"},{"en":"To be more active means to move more, do more physical activity, or take part more often.","zh":"be more active 的意思是活動更多、做更多體力活動或更常參與。"},{"en":"Older adults can be more active by walking, gardening, or joining gentle classes.","zh":"長者可以透過步行、園藝或參加溫和課堂變得更活躍。"},{"en":"Being more active can improve energy, mood, and independence.","zh":"更活躍可以改善精力、心情和獨立能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a healthier level of movement and participation.","zh":"這個短語描述更健康的活動和參與程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"daily activities","meaning":"日常活動","examples":[{"en":"Dancing motivates people to do daily activities.","zh":"跳舞推動人們進行日常活動。"},{"en":"Daily activities are ordinary things people do in everyday life.","zh":"daily activities 是人們在日常生活中做的普通事情。"},{"en":"Cooking, shopping, cleaning, and walking to the bus stop are daily activities.","zh":"煮飯、購物、清潔和步行到巴士站都是日常活動。"},{"en":"If exercise improves energy, people may find daily activities easier.","zh":"如果運動改善精力，人們可能覺得日常活動更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on normal everyday actions.","zh":"這個短語集中於普通日常行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"such as gardening","meaning":"例如園藝","examples":[{"en":"Participants do daily activities such as gardening.","zh":"參加者會做日常活動，例如園藝。"},{"en":"Such as gardening introduces gardening as an example of the kind of activity being discussed.","zh":"such as gardening 是把園藝作為正在討論活動類型的一個例子。"},{"en":"Gentle hobbies, such as gardening, can keep older adults active.","zh":"溫和嗜好，例如園藝，可以令長者保持活躍。"},{"en":"Giving examples such as gardening helps listeners picture the activity clearly.","zh":"給出例如園藝的例子，能幫助聽眾清楚想像該活動。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a concrete example.","zh":"這個短語引出具體例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"walking to the shops","meaning":"步行去商店","examples":[{"en":"Some participants feel motivated to walk to the shops.","zh":"有些參加者感到有動力步行去商店。"},{"en":"Walking to the shops means going to nearby shops on foot.","zh":"walking to the shops 的意思是徒步前往附近商店。"},{"en":"Older adults may walk to the shops to buy food and get gentle exercise.","zh":"長者可能步行去商店買食物並做溫和運動。"},{"en":"Walking to shops can support independence because people do not always need transport.","zh":"步行去商店可以支援獨立能力，因為人們不總是需要交通工具。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple everyday activity.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單日常活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ballroom dancing","meaning":"交誼舞","examples":[{"en":"Ballroom dancing is popular with older people.","zh":"交誼舞受長者歡迎。"},{"en":"Ballroom dancing is formal partner dancing, often done to structured music and steps.","zh":"ballroom dancing 是正式的雙人舞，通常配合有結構的音樂和舞步。"},{"en":"Waltz and foxtrot are examples of ballroom dancing.","zh":"華爾茲和狐步舞都是交誼舞的例子。"},{"en":"Ballroom dancing can be social because dancers usually move with a partner.","zh":"交誼舞可以很有社交性，因為舞者通常與舞伴一起移動。"},{"en":"This phrase names a traditional form of social dance.","zh":"這個短語指一種傳統社交舞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"country dancing","meaning":"鄉村舞","examples":[{"en":"Country dancing is popular with older people.","zh":"鄉村舞受長者歡迎。"},{"en":"Country dancing is a traditional social dance often done in lines, circles, or groups.","zh":"country dancing 是一種傳統社交舞，常以排、圈或小組形式進行。"},{"en":"Country dancing can be enjoyable because people move together in repeated patterns.","zh":"鄉村舞可以令人享受，因為人們一起按重複模式移動。"},{"en":"Group dances help participants interact without needing advanced technique.","zh":"集體舞幫助參加者互動，而不需要高階技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase names a communal dance style.","zh":"這個短語指一種群體舞蹈風格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"popular with","meaning":"受……歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Ballroom and country dancing are popular with older people.","zh":"交誼舞和鄉村舞受長者歡迎。"},{"en":"Popular with a group means liked or enjoyed by many people in that group.","zh":"popular with a group 的意思是受該群體中許多人喜歡或享受。"},{"en":"Swimming lessons are popular with parents because they help children stay safe.","zh":"游泳課受家長歡迎，因為它幫助兒童保持安全。"},{"en":"An activity becomes popular with older adults when it feels safe, social, and enjoyable.","zh":"當活動感覺安全、有社交性和愉快，它就會受長者歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase connects popularity with a specific group.","zh":"這個短語把受歡迎程度與特定群體連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have to be done in groups","meaning":"必須集體進行","examples":[{"en":"Ballroom and country dancing have to be done in groups.","zh":"交誼舞和鄉村舞必須集體進行。"},{"en":"Have to be done in groups means the activity needs several people to take part together.","zh":"have to be done in groups 的意思是該活動需要幾個人一起參與。"},{"en":"Some drama games have to be done in groups because they depend on interaction.","zh":"有些戲劇遊戲必須集體進行，因為它們依賴互動。"},{"en":"Group activities can build connection because people must notice and respond to one another.","zh":"集體活動可以建立連繫，因為人們必須留意並回應彼此。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a requirement for participation.","zh":"這個短語描述參與上的要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"require collaboration","meaning":"需要合作","examples":[{"en":"These dances require collaboration.","zh":"這些舞蹈需要合作。"},{"en":"To require collaboration means to need people to work together.","zh":"require collaboration 的意思是需要人們一起合作。"},{"en":"A group presentation requires collaboration because everyone must share tasks.","zh":"小組匯報需要合作，因為每個人都必須分擔任務。"},{"en":"Collaboration helps people succeed when one person cannot complete the activity alone.","zh":"當一個人無法獨自完成活動，合作能幫助人們成功。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses teamwork.","zh":"這個短語強調團隊合作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"involve touching","meaning":"涉及觸碰","examples":[{"en":"These dances often involve touching a dance partner.","zh":"這些舞蹈常涉及觸碰舞伴。"},{"en":"To involve touching means to include physical contact as part of the activity.","zh":"involve touching 的意思是把身體接觸包括在活動之中。"},{"en":"Some sports involve touching, while others keep players apart.","zh":"有些運動涉及觸碰，而另一些則保持參加者分開。"},{"en":"Activities involving touch require clear consent, comfort, and respect.","zh":"涉及觸碰的活動需要清楚同意、舒適感和尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what is included in an activity.","zh":"這個短語描述活動中包括甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dance partner","meaning":"舞伴","examples":[{"en":"Ballroom dancing often involves touching a dance partner.","zh":"交誼舞常涉及觸碰舞伴。"},{"en":"A dance partner is the person you dance with, especially in paired dancing.","zh":"dance partner 是與你一起跳舞的人，尤其是在雙人舞中。"},{"en":"A good dance partner listens to the rhythm and responds to the other person’s movement.","zh":"好舞伴會聆聽節奏並回應對方動作。"},{"en":"Dancing with a partner requires trust because both people must coordinate their steps.","zh":"與舞伴跳舞需要信任，因為兩人必須協調步法。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in social and ballroom dance.","zh":"這個短語常見於社交舞和交誼舞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"all of which","meaning":"這一切都","examples":[{"en":"The dances require collaboration and touch, all of which encourages interaction.","zh":"這些舞蹈需要合作和觸碰，這一切都促進互動。"},{"en":"All of which means all the things just mentioned.","zh":"all of which 的意思是剛提到的所有事情。"},{"en":"The class involved discussion, movement, and teamwork, all of which helped students learn.","zh":"課堂包括討論、動作和團隊合作，這一切都幫助學生學習。"},{"en":"This phrase links several points to one shared result.","zh":"這個短語把幾個要點與一個共同結果連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful for summarising combined effects.","zh":"它適合用於總結綜合效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"encourage interaction","meaning":"促進互動","examples":[{"en":"Group dancing encourages interaction on the dance floor.","zh":"集體跳舞促進舞池上的互動。"},{"en":"To encourage interaction means to make people more likely to communicate or respond to one another.","zh":"encourage interaction 的意思是令人們更可能溝通或互相回應。"},{"en":"Group games encourage interaction among students who do not know each other well.","zh":"小組遊戲促進不太熟悉彼此的學生之間的互動。"},{"en":"Interaction can reduce loneliness because people feel noticed and involved.","zh":"互動可以減少孤獨感，因為人們感到被注意和被包括。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an activity with social contact.","zh":"這個短語把活動與社交接觸連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on the dance floor","meaning":"在舞池上","examples":[{"en":"Dancing encourages interaction on the dance floor.","zh":"跳舞促進舞池上的互動。"},{"en":"On the dance floor means in the area where people dance.","zh":"on the dance floor 的意思是在供人跳舞的區域。"},{"en":"At weddings, guests often meet and laugh together on the dance floor.","zh":"在婚禮上，賓客常在舞池上相遇並一起笑。"},{"en":"The dance floor becomes a social space when people move together to the same music.","zh":"當人們跟着同一音樂一起移動，舞池就成為社交空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical place for dancing.","zh":"這個短語描述跳舞的實際地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"develop new relationships","meaning":"發展新關係","examples":[{"en":"Dance can help older people develop new relationships.","zh":"舞蹈可以幫助長者發展新關係。"},{"en":"To develop new relationships means to build new friendships, social connections, or supportive contacts.","zh":"develop new relationships 的意思是建立新友誼、社交連繫或支援網絡。"},{"en":"Joining a club can help newcomers develop new relationships in a town.","zh":"加入學會可以幫助新居民在城鎮中發展新關係。"},{"en":"New relationships can reduce loneliness because people have others to talk to and meet.","zh":"新關係可以減少孤獨，因為人們有其他人可以交談和見面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social growth over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間發展的社交成長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sense of isolation","meaning":"孤立感","examples":[{"en":"Dance can reduce older people’s sense of isolation.","zh":"舞蹈可以減少長者的孤立感。"},{"en":"A sense of isolation is the feeling of being alone, separate, or disconnected from others.","zh":"sense of isolation 是感到孤單、分離或與他人沒有連繫的感覺。"},{"en":"People living alone may feel a sense of isolation if they rarely meet friends.","zh":"如果獨居人士很少見朋友，他們可能感到孤立。"},{"en":"Social activities reduce isolation by giving people regular contact and shared experiences.","zh":"社交活動透過提供規律接觸和共同經歷來減少孤立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional loneliness, not only physical distance.","zh":"這個短語描述情感上的孤單，而不只是身體距離。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a huge problem","meaning":"嚴重問題","examples":[{"en":"Isolation among older people is a huge problem in many countries.","zh":"長者孤立在許多國家是一個嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A huge problem is a very serious or widespread difficulty.","zh":"a huge problem 是非常嚴重或廣泛存在的困難。"},{"en":"Long waiting times in hospitals can be a huge problem for patients and families.","zh":"醫院輪候時間長可以是病人和家庭的嚴重問題。"},{"en":"Huge problems usually need organised action, not only individual effort.","zh":"嚴重問題通常需要有組織的行動，而不只是個人努力。"},{"en":"This phrase gives strong negative emphasis.","zh":"這個短語帶有強烈負面強調。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"look at the benefits of","meaning":"研究……的好處","examples":[{"en":"The speaker also looked at the benefits of Zumba.","zh":"講者也研究了 Zumba 的好處。"},{"en":"To look at the benefits of something means to examine its advantages or positive effects.","zh":"look at the benefits of something 的意思是審視某事的優點或正面影響。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to look at the benefits of daily reading.","zh":"老師可能要求學生研究每日閱讀的好處。"},{"en":"Looking at benefits helps people judge whether an activity is worth doing.","zh":"研究好處能幫助人們判斷一項活動是否值得做。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research and presentations.","zh":"這個短語常見於研究和簡報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"regularly take a class","meaning":"定期上課","examples":[{"en":"Millions of people regularly take a Zumba class.","zh":"數以百萬計的人定期上 Zumba 課。"},{"en":"To regularly take a class means to attend lessons often or according to a routine.","zh":"regularly take a class 的意思是經常或按固定習慣上課。"},{"en":"Students who regularly take speaking classes usually gain confidence over time.","zh":"定期上口語課的學生通常會隨時間建立信心。"},{"en":"Regular attendance helps people build skill because learning becomes a habit.","zh":"定期出席有助人建立技能，因為學習會成為習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated participation in lessons.","zh":"這個短語描述重複參與課堂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"aerobic workout","meaning":"帶氧運動","examples":[{"en":"Zumba is an aerobic workout based on Latin American dance moves.","zh":"Zumba 是以拉丁美洲舞步為基礎的帶氧運動。"},{"en":"An aerobic workout is exercise that raises the heart rate and uses oxygen over a period of time.","zh":"aerobic workout 是在一段時間內提高心跳率並使用氧氣的運動。"},{"en":"Running, swimming, and fast dancing can be aerobic workouts.","zh":"跑步、游泳和快節奏跳舞都可以是帶氧運動。"},{"en":"Aerobic workouts can support heart health, stamina, and calorie burning.","zh":"帶氧運動可以支援心臟健康、耐力和卡路里消耗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exercise focused on sustained movement.","zh":"這個短語描述集中於持續活動的運動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"based on","meaning":"以……為基礎","examples":[{"en":"Zumba is based on Latin American dance moves.","zh":"Zumba 以拉丁美洲舞步為基礎。"},{"en":"Based on something means using it as the foundation or main source.","zh":"based on something 的意思是使用某事作為基礎或主要來源。"},{"en":"A film may be based on a true story.","zh":"一部電影可能以真實故事為基礎。"},{"en":"When a workout is based on dance moves, the exercise follows dance patterns and rhythm.","zh":"當運動以舞步為基礎，該運動會跟隨舞蹈模式和節奏。"},{"en":"This phrase shows where an idea or design comes from.","zh":"這個短語顯示想法或設計來自哪裡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Latin American dance moves","meaning":"拉丁美洲舞步","examples":[{"en":"Zumba is based on Latin American dance moves.","zh":"Zumba 以拉丁美洲舞步為基礎。"},{"en":"Latin American dance moves are dance steps and rhythms linked to Latin American dance styles.","zh":"Latin American dance moves 是與拉丁美洲舞蹈風格有關的舞步和節奏。"},{"en":"Salsa and merengue can inspire Latin American dance moves in fitness classes.","zh":"莎莎和梅倫格舞可以啟發健身課中的拉丁美洲舞步。"},{"en":"These dance moves can make exercise feel energetic and musical.","zh":"這些舞步可以令運動感覺充滿活力和音樂感。"},{"en":"This phrase connects culture, rhythm, and movement.","zh":"這個短語連繫文化、節奏和動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"exercise and sport science","meaning":"運動及體育科學","examples":[{"en":"John Porcari is a professor of exercise and sport science.","zh":"John Porcari 是運動及體育科學教授。"},{"en":"Exercise and sport science is the study of how physical activity affects the body and performance.","zh":"exercise and sport science 是研究體力活動如何影響身體和表現的學科。"},{"en":"Students in exercise and sport science may learn about muscles, heart health, training, and injury prevention.","zh":"修讀運動及體育科學的學生可能學習肌肉、心臟健康、訓練和傷患預防。"},{"en":"This field helps people design safer and more effective exercise programmes.","zh":"這個領域幫助人設計更安全和更有效的運動課程。"},{"en":"This phrase names an academic subject.","zh":"這個短語指一門學術科目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"analyse a group of","meaning":"分析一組……","examples":[{"en":"John Porcari analysed a group of women who were Zumba regulars.","zh":"John Porcari 分析了一組經常上 Zumba 課的女性。"},{"en":"To analyse a group of people means to study their behaviour, data, or results carefully.","zh":"analyse a group of people 的意思是仔細研究他們的行為、數據或結果。"},{"en":"Researchers may analyse a group of students to see how sleep affects exam performance.","zh":"研究人員可能分析一組學生，看看睡眠如何影響考試表現。"},{"en":"Analysis helps researchers find patterns instead of relying on guesses.","zh":"分析幫助研究人員找出模式，而不是依靠猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於研究語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Zumba regulars","meaning":"經常上Zumba課的人","examples":[{"en":"The study analysed women who were Zumba regulars.","zh":"研究分析了經常上 Zumba 課的女性。"},{"en":"Zumba regulars are people who attend Zumba classes often or as a routine.","zh":"Zumba regulars 是經常或按習慣參加 Zumba 課的人。"},{"en":"Gym staff may recognise Zumba regulars because they come to the same class each week.","zh":"健身室職員可能認得經常上 Zumba 課的人，因為她們每星期都上同一堂。"},{"en":"Regular participants are useful in studies because they have real experience of the activity.","zh":"經常參加者對研究有用，因為她們對活動有真實經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequent class attendees.","zh":"這個短語描述經常上課的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lasting 40 minutes","meaning":"持續40分鐘","examples":[{"en":"A class lasting 40 minutes burns about 370 calories.","zh":"一堂持續40分鐘的課會消耗約370卡路里。"},{"en":"Lasting 40 minutes means continuing for a period of forty minutes.","zh":"lasting 40 minutes 的意思是持續四十分鐘。"},{"en":"A workout lasting 40 minutes can be long enough to raise the heart rate.","zh":"持續40分鐘的運動可以足以提高心跳率。"},{"en":"The length of a class affects how much energy people use.","zh":"課堂長度會影響人們使用多少能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes duration.","zh":"這個短語描述持續時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"burn calories","meaning":"消耗卡路里","examples":[{"en":"A Zumba class burns about 370 calories.","zh":"一堂 Zumba 課會消耗約370卡路里。"},{"en":"To burn calories means to use energy from food during physical activity or body processes.","zh":"burn calories 的意思是在體力活動或身體過程中使用來自食物的能量。"},{"en":"Walking, cycling, and dancing can all burn calories.","zh":"步行、踩單車和跳舞都可以消耗卡路里。"},{"en":"More intense movement usually burns more calories in the same amount of time.","zh":"在相同時間內，更高強度的動作通常消耗更多卡路里。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in fitness discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於健身討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"similar to","meaning":"與……相似","examples":[{"en":"Zumba is similar to moderately intense exercises.","zh":"Zumba 與中等強度運動相似。"},{"en":"Similar to means like something else in some important ways.","zh":"similar to 的意思是在某些重要方面像另一事物。"},{"en":"Cycling on a flat road can be similar to brisk walking in effort level.","zh":"在平路踩單車在用力程度上可以與快步走相似。"},{"en":"Comparing activities helps people choose exercise that matches their fitness.","zh":"比較活動有助人們選擇符合自己體能的運動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows resemblance, not complete sameness.","zh":"這個短語表示相似，而不是完全相同。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"moderately intense exercises","meaning":"中等強度運動","examples":[{"en":"Zumba is similar to moderately intense exercises.","zh":"Zumba 與中等強度運動相似。"},{"en":"Moderately intense exercises are physical activities that raise the heart rate but are not extremely hard.","zh":"moderately intense exercises 是會提高心跳率但不是極端辛苦的體力活動。"},{"en":"Brisk walking and steady cycling can be moderately intense exercises.","zh":"快步走和穩定踩單車都可以是中等強度運動。"},{"en":"Moderate exercise can be suitable for many people because it is challenging but manageable.","zh":"中等強度運動適合許多人，因為它有挑戰但仍可應付。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a middle level of exercise intensity.","zh":"這個短語描述中等運動強度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"step aerobics","meaning":"踏板健身操","examples":[{"en":"Zumba has a similar intensity to step aerobics.","zh":"Zumba 的強度與踏板健身操相似。"},{"en":"Step aerobics is an exercise class where people step up and down on a raised platform to music.","zh":"step aerobics 是一種運動課，參加者跟着音樂在升高踏板上上下踏步。"},{"en":"Step aerobics can improve fitness because it keeps the body moving continuously.","zh":"踏板健身操可以改善體能，因為它令身體持續活動。"},{"en":"People compare Zumba with step aerobics because both are rhythmic aerobic workouts.","zh":"人們把 Zumba 與踏板健身操比較，因為兩者都是有節奏的帶氧運動。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific fitness activity.","zh":"這個短語指一種特定健身活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"kickboxing","meaning":"踢拳","examples":[{"en":"Zumba has a similar intensity to kickboxing.","zh":"Zumba 的強度與踢拳相似。"},{"en":"Kickboxing is a sport or workout using punching and kicking movements.","zh":"kickboxing 是使用出拳和踢腿動作的運動或健身活動。"},{"en":"Fitness kickboxing classes can raise the heart rate and train coordination.","zh":"健身踢拳課可以提高心跳率並訓練協調。"},{"en":"People may compare kickboxing with dance workouts when discussing exercise intensity.","zh":"人們討論運動強度時，可能把踢拳與舞蹈運動比較。"},{"en":"This phrase names a physically energetic activity.","zh":"這個短語指一種充滿體力活動的運動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"women with obesity","meaning":"患有肥胖症的女性","examples":[{"en":"The study looked at women with obesity.","zh":"這項研究研究了患有肥胖症的女性。"},{"en":"Women with obesity are women whose body weight is medically classified as high enough to affect health risk.","zh":"women with obesity 是體重在醫學上被歸類為高到可能影響健康風險的女性。"},{"en":"Health studies may include women with obesity to understand which exercise programmes are realistic and helpful.","zh":"健康研究可能包括患有肥胖症的女性，以了解哪些運動課程實際而有幫助。"},{"en":"Respectful language matters because people are more than their body size.","zh":"尊重語言很重要，因為人不只是自己的身形。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in medical or health research contexts.","zh":"這個短語用於醫學或健康研究語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"three times a week","meaning":"每星期三次","examples":[{"en":"The women did Zumba three times a week.","zh":"這些女性每星期做三次 Zumba。"},{"en":"Three times a week means on three separate occasions each week.","zh":"three times a week 的意思是每星期分三次做。"},{"en":"Students may practise speaking three times a week to build fluency.","zh":"學生可能每星期練習三次口語，以建立流暢度。"},{"en":"Regular practice several times a week can help habits develop.","zh":"每星期幾次規律練習可以幫助習慣形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequency.","zh":"這個短語描述頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"for 16 weeks","meaning":"為期16星期","examples":[{"en":"The women did Zumba for 16 weeks.","zh":"這些女性做 Zumba，為期16星期。"},{"en":"For 16 weeks means during a period of sixteen weeks.","zh":"for 16 weeks 的意思是在十六星期的期間內。"},{"en":"A reading programme may run for 16 weeks before results are measured.","zh":"閱讀計劃可能運行16星期後才量度結果。"},{"en":"A long enough period helps researchers see whether an activity creates change.","zh":"足夠長的時間有助研究人員看見活動是否帶來改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes duration.","zh":"這個短語描述持續時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lose an average of","meaning":"平均減去","examples":[{"en":"The women lost an average of 1.2 kilos.","zh":"這些女性平均減去1.2公斤。"},{"en":"To lose an average of an amount means the average decrease across the group was that amount.","zh":"lose an average of 某數量的意思是整個群體平均下降該數量。"},{"en":"Students in the programme improved by an average of five marks.","zh":"參加計劃的學生平均進步五分。"},{"en":"Averages show the general result, but individual results may be different.","zh":"平均數顯示一般結果，但個別結果可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting study data.","zh":"這個短語適合用於報告研究數據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lower their percentage of body fat","meaning":"降低體脂率","examples":[{"en":"The women lowered their percentage of body fat by 1%.","zh":"這些女性把體脂率降低了1%。"},{"en":"To lower percentage of body fat means to reduce the proportion of the body made up of fat.","zh":"lower percentage of body fat 的意思是減少身體由脂肪組成的比例。"},{"en":"Exercise and balanced eating can lower body fat percentage over time.","zh":"運動和均衡飲食可以隨時間降低體脂率。"},{"en":"Body fat percentage can change even when weight changes only a little.","zh":"即使體重只改變少許，體脂率也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in fitness and health studies.","zh":"這個短語常見於健身和健康研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"more importantly","meaning":"更重要的是","examples":[{"en":"More importantly, the women enjoyed the class.","zh":"更重要的是，這些女性享受課堂。"},{"en":"More importantly is used to introduce a point that matters more than the previous one.","zh":"more importantly 用來引出比前一點更重要的內容。"},{"en":"The programme was cheap; more importantly, students actually wanted to attend.","zh":"這個課程很便宜；更重要的是，學生真的想參加。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show which point carries greater weight.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示哪一點份量更重。"},{"en":"It is useful when shifting from facts to the key message.","zh":"它適合用於從事實轉向核心訊息。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"so much that","meaning":"如此……以致","examples":[{"en":"The women enjoyed the class so much that they made it a habit.","zh":"這些女性如此享受課堂，以致把它變成習慣。"},{"en":"So much that shows a result caused by a very strong feeling or degree.","zh":"so much that 顯示由非常強烈的感受或程度造成的結果。"},{"en":"He liked the book so much that he read it twice.","zh":"他如此喜歡這本書，以致讀了兩次。"},{"en":"When people enjoy an activity so much, they are more likely to continue it.","zh":"當人們如此享受一項活動，他們更可能繼續做。"},{"en":"This structure links intensity with consequence.","zh":"這個結構把強度與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make it a habit","meaning":"將其變成習慣","examples":[{"en":"The women enjoyed Zumba and made it a habit.","zh":"這些女性享受 Zumba，並將其變成習慣。"},{"en":"To make something a habit means to do it regularly until it becomes part of normal life.","zh":"make something a habit 的意思是定期做某事，直到它成為日常生活的一部分。"},{"en":"Students can make reading a habit by reading ten minutes every night.","zh":"學生可以透過每晚閱讀十分鐘，將閱讀變成習慣。"},{"en":"Enjoyable activities are easier to turn into habits because people want to repeat them.","zh":"愉快活動較容易變成習慣，因為人們想重複做。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regular behaviour becoming routine.","zh":"這個短語描述規律行為成為常規。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"continue to attend","meaning":"繼續參加","examples":[{"en":"The women continued to attend classes at least once a week.","zh":"這些女性繼續每星期至少參加一次課堂。"},{"en":"To continue to attend means to keep going to classes, meetings, or activities.","zh":"continue to attend 的意思是繼續去上課、開會或參加活動。"},{"en":"Students who continue to attend lessons regularly usually improve more steadily.","zh":"繼續規律上課的學生通常進步較穩定。"},{"en":"Continued attendance shows that people find the activity useful or enjoyable.","zh":"持續參加顯示人們覺得活動有用或有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing participation.","zh":"這個短語描述持續參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at least once a week","meaning":"每星期至少一次","examples":[{"en":"The women attended Zumba classes at least once a week.","zh":"這些女性每星期至少參加一次 Zumba 課。"},{"en":"At least once a week means one time or more every week.","zh":"at least once a week 的意思是每星期一次或以上。"},{"en":"Older adults may benefit from social exercise at least once a week.","zh":"長者可能從每星期至少一次的社交運動中受益。"},{"en":"Doing something at least weekly helps keep the habit alive.","zh":"每星期至少做一次某事，有助保持習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a minimum frequency.","zh":"這個短語給出最低頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"aerobic exercise programme","meaning":"帶氧運動課程","examples":[{"en":"Continuing attendance is unusual for an aerobic exercise programme.","zh":"對帶氧運動課程而言，持續參加並不常見。"},{"en":"An aerobic exercise programme is a planned set of classes or activities that improve fitness through sustained movement.","zh":"aerobic exercise programme 是透過持續活動改善體能的一套有計劃課堂或活動。"},{"en":"A gym may offer an aerobic exercise programme for people who want to improve heart health.","zh":"健身室可能為想改善心臟健康的人提供帶氧運動課程。"},{"en":"Many people stop exercise programmes if they do not enjoy them.","zh":"如果人們不享受運動課程，他們很容易停止參加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a structured fitness plan.","zh":"這個短語描述有結構的健身計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"compete with","meaning":"與……競爭","examples":[{"en":"Dance is never going to compete with high-intensity workouts.","zh":"舞蹈永遠不會與高強度運動訓練競爭。"},{"en":"To compete with something means to match or challenge it in quality, effectiveness, or appeal.","zh":"compete with something 的意思是在質素、成效或吸引力上與某物匹敵或較量。"},{"en":"Small shops compete with supermarkets by offering personal service.","zh":"小店透過提供個人化服務與超級市場競爭。"},{"en":"Dance may not compete with intense exercise for fitness gains, but it can win on enjoyment.","zh":"舞蹈在體能提升方面未必能與高強度運動競爭，但在樂趣方面可能勝出。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when comparing performance or attractiveness.","zh":"這個短語用於比較表現或吸引力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"high-intensity workouts","meaning":"高強度運動訓練","examples":[{"en":"Dance cannot compete with high-intensity workouts for fitness gains.","zh":"舞蹈在體能提升方面不能與高強度運動訓練相比。"},{"en":"High-intensity workouts are exercise sessions that require very strong effort and raise the heart rate quickly.","zh":"high-intensity workouts 是需要非常強烈努力並迅速提高心跳率的運動課節。"},{"en":"Sprint intervals and hard circuit training are high-intensity workouts.","zh":"短跑間歇訓練和高強度循環訓練都是高強度運動訓練。"},{"en":"These workouts can improve fitness quickly, but they may not suit everyone.","zh":"這類訓練可以快速改善體能，但未必適合所有人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes demanding exercise.","zh":"這個短語描述要求高的運動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"when it comes to","meaning":"談到……","examples":[{"en":"Dance is less effective when it comes to physical fitness gains.","zh":"談到體能提升，舞蹈效果較低。"},{"en":"When it comes to something means when discussing or considering that particular topic.","zh":"when it comes to something 的意思是在討論或考慮某特定題目時。"},{"en":"When it comes to learning vocabulary, regular review is very important.","zh":"談到學習詞彙，規律重溫非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the discussion to one area.","zh":"這個短語把討論收窄到一個範疇。"},{"en":"It is common in comparisons and opinions.","zh":"它常見於比較和意見表達。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"physical fitness gains","meaning":"體能提升","examples":[{"en":"Dance may not match high-intensity workouts for physical fitness gains.","zh":"舞蹈在體能提升方面可能比不上高強度運動訓練。"},{"en":"Physical fitness gains are improvements in strength, stamina, speed, flexibility, or overall fitness.","zh":"physical fitness gains 是力量、耐力、速度、柔韌度或整體體能的改善。"},{"en":"Regular swimming can produce physical fitness gains over several months.","zh":"規律游泳可以在幾個月內帶來體能提升。"},{"en":"Fitness gains depend on intensity, frequency, recovery, and personal health.","zh":"體能提升取決於強度、頻率、恢復和個人健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in exercise science.","zh":"這個短語常見於運動科學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"popularity is likely to","meaning":"受歡迎程度很可能會……","examples":[{"en":"The popularity of dance is likely to keep rising.","zh":"舞蹈的受歡迎程度很可能會持續上升。"},{"en":"Popularity is likely to means something will probably become more popular.","zh":"popularity is likely to 的意思是某事很可能會變得更受歡迎。"},{"en":"The popularity of online learning is likely to grow if courses become more flexible.","zh":"如果課程變得更彈性，網上學習的受歡迎程度很可能會上升。"},{"en":"When an activity is enjoyable and accessible, its popularity is likely to rise.","zh":"當活動有趣又容易參與，其受歡迎程度很可能會上升。"},{"en":"This phrase predicts a probable trend.","zh":"這個短語預測可能趨勢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"keep on rising","meaning":"持續上升","examples":[{"en":"The popularity of dance is likely to keep on rising.","zh":"舞蹈的受歡迎程度很可能持續上升。"},{"en":"To keep on rising means to continue increasing.","zh":"keep on rising 的意思是繼續增加。"},{"en":"If food prices keep on rising, families may need to change their budgets.","zh":"如果食物價格持續上升，家庭可能需要改變預算。"},{"en":"A trend keeps rising when more people join or support it over time.","zh":"當越來越多人加入或支持，趨勢就會持續上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continued growth.","zh":"這個短語描述持續增長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"such a fun way to","meaning":"如此有趣的……方式","examples":[{"en":"Dance is such a fun way to keep fit.","zh":"舞蹈是如此有趣的健身方式。"},{"en":"Such a fun way to do something means a very enjoyable method of doing it.","zh":"such a fun way to do something 的意思是做某事的一種非常愉快方法。"},{"en":"Games are such a fun way to practise English vocabulary.","zh":"遊戲是如此有趣的練習英文詞彙方式。"},{"en":"When a method is fun, people are more likely to continue using it.","zh":"當方法有趣，人們更可能繼續使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase gives enthusiastic praise for a method.","zh":"這個短語對某種方法作出熱情讚賞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"keep fit","meaning":"保持健康；健身","examples":[{"en":"Dancing is a fun way to keep fit.","zh":"跳舞是保持健康的有趣方式。"},{"en":"To keep fit means to stay physically healthy and active.","zh":"keep fit 的意思是保持身體健康和活躍。"},{"en":"People can keep fit by walking, swimming, cycling, or dancing regularly.","zh":"人們可以透過規律步行、游泳、踩單車或跳舞來保持健康。"},{"en":"Keeping fit helps with energy, mood, heart health, and daily movement.","zh":"保持健康有助精力、心情、心臟健康和日常活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday health advice.","zh":"這個短語常見於日常健康建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 17 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/listening/Practice 18/task-1":[{"front":"Junior Cycle Camp","meaning":"青少年單車營","examples":[{"en":"Jake answers the phone at Junior Cycle Camp.","zh":"Jake 在青少年單車營接電話。"},{"en":"Junior Cycle Camp is a cycling camp designed for children or young learners.","zh":"Junior Cycle Camp 是為兒童或年輕學員而設的單車營。"},{"en":"Parents may call Junior Cycle Camp to ask about classes, safety, and fees.","zh":"家長可能致電青少年單車營，查詢課程、安全和費用。"},{"en":"A camp for young cyclists helps children learn skills before riding on roads.","zh":"青少年單車營幫助孩子在上路前學習技巧。"},{"en":"This name refers to an organised programme, not just one cycling lesson.","zh":"這個名稱指有組織的課程，而不只是一堂單車課。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"call for information about","meaning":"致電查詢關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"The woman is calling for information about the cycle camp.","zh":"那位女士致電查詢關於單車營的資料。"},{"en":"To call for information about something means to phone someone to ask for details.","zh":"call for information about something 是指打電話向某人詢問詳情。"},{"en":"A parent may call for information about a summer course before booking a place.","zh":"家長可能在預訂名額前致電查詢暑期課程資料。"},{"en":"Calling for information helps people decide whether a service is suitable.","zh":"致電查詢資料有助人們決定服務是否合適。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in enquiries by phone.","zh":"這個短語常見於電話查詢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cycle camp","meaning":"單車營","examples":[{"en":"The woman is thinking of sending her son to a cycle camp.","zh":"那位女士正在考慮送兒子去單車營。"},{"en":"A cycle camp is a programme where children learn and practise cycling.","zh":"cycle camp 是孩子學習和練習踩單車的活動營。"},{"en":"A cycle camp may teach balance, road safety, turning, and braking.","zh":"單車營可能教授平衡、道路安全、轉彎和煞車。"},{"en":"Children who attend a cycle camp can become more confident on a bike.","zh":"參加單車營的孩子可以對踩單車更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised cycling training, often during holidays.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的單車訓練，通常在假期舉行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"think of sending","meaning":"考慮送……去","examples":[{"en":"The woman is thinking of sending her son to the camp.","zh":"那位女士正在考慮送兒子去單車營。"},{"en":"To think of sending someone somewhere means to consider arranging for them to go there.","zh":"think of sending someone somewhere 是指考慮安排某人去某地。"},{"en":"A parent may think of sending a child to swimming lessons in summer.","zh":"家長可能考慮在夏天送孩子去學游水。"},{"en":"People think of sending children to activities when they want them to learn or gain confidence.","zh":"當人們希望孩子學習或建立信心時，會考慮送他們去活動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows consideration, not a final decision.","zh":"這個短語表示正在考慮，並非最終決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be held every weekday morning","meaning":"每個平日早上舉行","examples":[{"en":"The camp is held every weekday morning over the summer holiday.","zh":"這個營在暑假期間每個平日早上舉行。"},{"en":"To be held every weekday morning means to take place each morning from Monday to Friday.","zh":"be held every weekday morning 是指星期一至星期五每天早上舉行。"},{"en":"A revision class may be held every weekday morning before the exam.","zh":"考試前，溫習班可能每個平日早上舉行。"},{"en":"Regular weekday sessions help families plan transport and childcare.","zh":"定期平日早上課程有助家庭安排交通和照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the schedule of an organised activity.","zh":"這個短語解釋有組織活動的時間表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over the summer holiday","meaning":"在暑假期間","examples":[{"en":"The cycle camp takes place over the summer holiday.","zh":"單車營在暑假期間舉行。"},{"en":"Over the summer holiday means during the period when school is closed in summer.","zh":"over the summer holiday 是指在夏天學校放假的期間。"},{"en":"Many children join sports camps over the summer holiday.","zh":"許多孩子在暑假期間參加運動營。"},{"en":"Holiday programmes help children stay active when regular lessons stop.","zh":"假期活動幫助孩子在正常課堂暫停時保持活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes when an activity happens.","zh":"這個短語描述活動發生的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"以……為重點","examples":[{"en":"The camp focuses on basic cycling skills and safety.","zh":"這個營以基本踏單車技巧和安全為重點。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give most attention to it.","zh":"focus on something 是指把主要注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"A writing class may focus on grammar and paragraph structure.","zh":"寫作班可能以文法和段落結構為重點。"},{"en":"Focusing on safety helps children avoid accidents while learning.","zh":"以安全為重點有助孩子在學習時避免意外。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the main purpose of a course or activity.","zh":"這個短語顯示課程或活動的主要目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"basic cycling skills","meaning":"基本踏單車技巧","examples":[{"en":"The camp helps children develop basic cycling skills.","zh":"這個營幫助孩子培養基本踏單車技巧。"},{"en":"Basic cycling skills are simple abilities needed to ride a bike safely.","zh":"basic cycling skills 是安全踏單車所需的基本能力。"},{"en":"These skills may include balancing, braking, turning, and looking around.","zh":"這些技巧可能包括平衡、煞車、轉彎和觀察周圍。"},{"en":"Children need basic cycling skills before they ride near traffic.","zh":"孩子在車流附近踏單車前，需要基本踏單車技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to foundation skills, not advanced racing techniques.","zh":"這個短語指基礎技能，而不是高階比賽技巧。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"from three years upwards","meaning":"三歲或以上","examples":[{"en":"The camp has eight levels for children from three years upwards.","zh":"這個營為三歲或以上的孩子設有八個級別。"},{"en":"From three years upwards means for children aged three and older.","zh":"from three years upwards 是指三歲及更年長的孩子。"},{"en":"A playgroup may accept children from two years upwards.","zh":"遊戲小組可能接受兩歲或以上的孩子。"},{"en":"Age ranges help organisers choose suitable activities and safety rules.","zh":"年齡範圍幫助組織者選擇合適活動和安全規則。"},{"en":"This phrase sets the minimum age for joining.","zh":"這個短語設定參加的最低年齡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ride a bike","meaning":"踏單車","examples":[{"en":"Charlie can ride a bike, but he needs more training.","zh":"Charlie 會踏單車，但需要更多訓練。"},{"en":"To ride a bike means to sit on and control a bicycle.","zh":"ride a bike 是指坐在單車上並控制它。"},{"en":"Many children learn to ride a bike with stabilisers before cycling independently.","zh":"許多孩子會先用輔助輪學踏單車，之後才獨立踩。"},{"en":"Riding a bike safely requires balance, control, and awareness of other people.","zh":"安全踏單車需要平衡、控制和留意其他人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the basic action of cycling.","zh":"這個短語描述踩單車的基本動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"need a little more training","meaning":"需要再多一點訓練","examples":[{"en":"Charlie needs a little more training before he can ride safely on the road.","zh":"Charlie 在能安全上路前，需要再多一點訓練。"},{"en":"To need a little more training means to require some extra practice or instruction.","zh":"need a little more training 是指需要額外一些練習或指導。"},{"en":"A swimmer may need a little more training before joining the advanced class.","zh":"游泳學生可能需要再多一點訓練，才可加入進階班。"},{"en":"Extra training helps children correct small weaknesses before facing harder situations.","zh":"額外訓練幫助孩子在面對較難情況前修正小弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the person already has some ability but is not fully ready.","zh":"這個短語表示那個人已有一些能力，但尚未完全準備好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"safe to go on the road","meaning":"安全上路","examples":[{"en":"Charlie needs training before he is safe to go on the road.","zh":"Charlie 需要訓練後才可安全上路。"},{"en":"To be safe to go on the road means to have enough skill and awareness to ride near traffic.","zh":"safe to go on the road 是指有足夠技巧和意識在車流附近踏單車。"},{"en":"A child should be safe to go on the road before cycling to school alone.","zh":"孩子獨自踩單車上學前，應該能安全上路。"},{"en":"Road safety matters because cars, buses, and pedestrians create risks.","zh":"道路安全很重要，因為汽車、巴士和行人都會帶來風險。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on readiness for real road conditions.","zh":"這個短語著重是否準備好面對真實道路情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be best in","meaning":"最適合在……","examples":[{"en":"Charlie would probably be best in Level 5.","zh":"Charlie 可能最適合在第五級。"},{"en":"To be best in a level means that level is the most suitable one for someone’s ability.","zh":"be best in a level 是指某級別最適合某人的能力。"},{"en":"A child who can swim but lacks confidence may be best in an intermediate class.","zh":"會游水但缺乏信心的孩子可能最適合在中級班。"},{"en":"Choosing the right level helps children learn without feeling bored or unsafe.","zh":"選擇正確級別有助孩子學習，而不會感到沉悶或不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when placing someone in a suitable group.","zh":"這個短語用於把某人安排到合適組別。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"start off practising","meaning":"一開始練習","examples":[{"en":"The children start off practising on the site.","zh":"孩子一開始在場地內練習。"},{"en":"To start off practising means to begin by doing practice before moving to harder tasks.","zh":"start off practising 是指先從練習開始，然後才進入較難任務。"},{"en":"New swimmers start off practising in shallow water.","zh":"初學游泳者一開始在淺水區練習。"},{"en":"Starting with practice in a safe place helps beginners build confidence.","zh":"先在安全地方練習有助初學者建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first stage of training.","zh":"這個短語描述訓練的第一階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on the site","meaning":"在場地內","examples":[{"en":"The children first practise cycling on the site.","zh":"孩子首先在場地內練習踏單車。"},{"en":"On the site means at the place where the activity or organisation is based.","zh":"on the site 是指在活動或機構所在的地方。"},{"en":"A school fair may have food stalls on the site near the playground.","zh":"學校市集可能在操場附近的場地內設小食攤。"},{"en":"Practising on the site is safer because staff can control the area.","zh":"在場地內練習較安全，因為職員可以控制範圍。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the activity’s own location.","zh":"這個短語指活動本身所在位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"aim to get someone doing","meaning":"目標是令某人做到……","examples":[{"en":"The camp aims to get the children riding on the road.","zh":"這個營目標是令孩子能在路上踏單車。"},{"en":"To aim to get someone doing something means to plan to help them start doing it successfully.","zh":"aim to get someone doing something 是指計劃幫助某人成功開始做某事。"},{"en":"A music course may aim to get beginners playing simple songs within a month.","zh":"音樂課程可能目標是一個月內令初學者能演奏簡單歌曲。"},{"en":"This phrase links a teaching goal with the learner’s final action.","zh":"這個短語把教學目標與學習者最終行動連繫起來。"},{"en":"It suggests practical progress, not just theory.","zh":"它表示實際進步，而不只是理論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be taken to","meaning":"被帶去……","examples":[{"en":"The children are taken to ride in the park before going on the road.","zh":"孩子在上路前會被帶去公園踏單車。"},{"en":"To be taken to a place means to be brought or led there by someone.","zh":"be taken to a place 是指由某人帶到某地。"},{"en":"Children may be taken to the library for a reading activity.","zh":"孩子可能被帶去圖書館參加閱讀活動。"},{"en":"Being taken to a safer place helps learners practise before facing real risks.","zh":"被帶到較安全地方練習，有助學習者在面對真實風險前準備。"},{"en":"This passive phrase focuses on where the children are brought.","zh":"這個被動短語著重孩子被帶到哪裏。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"away from the traffic","meaning":"遠離車流","examples":[{"en":"The children practise in the park, away from the traffic.","zh":"孩子在公園練習，遠離車流。"},{"en":"Away from the traffic means not close to cars, buses, or busy roads.","zh":"away from the traffic 是指不靠近汽車、巴士或繁忙道路。"},{"en":"Beginners should practise cycling away from the traffic until they can control the bike well.","zh":"初學者應遠離車流練習踩單車，直到能好好控制單車。"},{"en":"Being away from traffic reduces risk and allows children to concentrate.","zh":"遠離車流可降低風險，讓孩子集中精神。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a safer location.","zh":"這個短語描述較安全的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tell me a bit about","meaning":"跟我說一點關於……","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks Jake to tell her a bit about the instructors.","zh":"那位女士請 Jake 跟她說一點關於教練的資料。"},{"en":"Tell me a bit about means give me some basic information about something.","zh":"tell me a bit about 是指給我一些基本資料。"},{"en":"A parent may ask a teacher to tell her a bit about the school’s reading programme.","zh":"家長可能請老師跟她說一點關於學校閱讀計劃的資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and invites a short explanation.","zh":"這個短語有禮貌，並邀請對方作簡短解釋。"},{"en":"It is useful when the listener wants an overview, not every detail.","zh":"當聽者想要概覽而非所有細節時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"instructors","meaning":"教練","examples":[{"en":"The instructors are responsible for teaching the cycling classes.","zh":"教練負責教授單車課。"},{"en":"Instructors are people who teach practical skills or activities.","zh":"instructors 是教授實用技能或活動的人。"},{"en":"A swimming instructor teaches children how to move safely in water.","zh":"游泳教練教孩子如何在水中安全活動。"},{"en":"Good instructors explain clearly, watch learners carefully, and correct mistakes.","zh":"好教練會清楚解釋、仔細觀察學員並修正錯誤。"},{"en":"This word is often used for sport, driving, fitness, and practical training.","zh":"這個詞常用於運動、駕駛、健身和實用訓練。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"different-coloured shirts","meaning":"不同顏色的恤衫","examples":[{"en":"All the staff wear different-coloured shirts.","zh":"所有職員都穿不同顏色的恤衫。"},{"en":"Different-coloured shirts are shirts in different colours used to identify roles or groups.","zh":"different-coloured shirts 是用不同顏色識別角色或組別的恤衫。"},{"en":"At a school event, helpers may wear different-coloured shirts so parents know whom to ask.","zh":"在學校活動中，幫手可能穿不同顏色的恤衫，方便家長知道找誰。"},{"en":"Colour coding makes staff easier to recognise in a busy place.","zh":"顏色分類令職員在繁忙地方更容易被認出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible clothing differences.","zh":"這個短語描述衣着上的明顯顏色差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"supervisors","meaning":"主管","examples":[{"en":"The supervisors wear red shirts.","zh":"主管穿紅色恤衫。"},{"en":"Supervisors are people who oversee work, staff, or activities.","zh":"supervisors 是負責監督工作、職員或活動的人。"},{"en":"A playground supervisor watches children to make sure they are safe.","zh":"遊樂場主管會看管孩子，確保他們安全。"},{"en":"Supervisors help solve problems and support other staff.","zh":"主管幫助解決問題並支援其他職員。"},{"en":"This word suggests a higher level of responsibility than ordinary helpers.","zh":"這個詞表示比普通助手更高的責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"support the instructors","meaning":"支援教練","examples":[{"en":"The supervisors support the instructors during the camp.","zh":"主管在單車營期間支援教練。"},{"en":"To support the instructors means to help the teachers or coaches do their job.","zh":"support the instructors 是指幫助老師或教練做好工作。"},{"en":"Classroom assistants support teachers by helping children who need extra attention.","zh":"課室助理透過幫助需要額外照顧的孩子來支援老師。"},{"en":"Support allows instructors to focus on teaching while others help with safety or organisation.","zh":"支援讓教練專注教學，同時其他人協助安全或組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes teamwork behind a lesson.","zh":"這個短語描述課堂背後的團隊合作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stand in for","meaning":"代替……","examples":[{"en":"The supervisors stand in for Jake if he is not around.","zh":"如果 Jake 不在場，主管會代替他。"},{"en":"To stand in for someone means to take their place temporarily.","zh":"stand in for someone 是指暫時代替某人。"},{"en":"A deputy head teacher may stand in for the principal during a meeting.","zh":"副校長可能在會議中代替校長。"},{"en":"Having someone to stand in prevents work from stopping when a person is absent.","zh":"有人可以代替，能防止某人缺席時工作停頓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes temporary replacement.","zh":"這個短語描述臨時替代。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be not around","meaning":"不在場","examples":[{"en":"The supervisors help if Jake is not around.","zh":"如果 Jake 不在場，主管會幫忙。"},{"en":"Not around means not present or not available at that time.","zh":"not around 是指當時不在場或不能提供協助。"},{"en":"If the manager is not around, customers can speak to the assistant manager.","zh":"如果經理不在場，顧客可以找副經理。"},{"en":"When a key person is not around, clear backup arrangements are important.","zh":"當重要人物不在場，清楚的後備安排很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and refers to absence.","zh":"這個短語較口語，指某人缺席。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be responsible for","meaning":"負責……","examples":[{"en":"One instructor is responsible for each class.","zh":"每班由一名教練負責。"},{"en":"To be responsible for something means to have the duty to manage or look after it.","zh":"be responsible for something 是指有職責管理或照顧某事。"},{"en":"A class monitor may be responsible for collecting homework.","zh":"班長可能負責收功課。"},{"en":"Clear responsibility helps people know who should act when something happens.","zh":"清楚責任有助人們知道發生事情時由誰處理。"},{"en":"This phrase shows duty and accountability.","zh":"這個短語顯示職責和承擔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in order to be accepted","meaning":"為了被取錄","examples":[{"en":"In order to be accepted, instructors must submit a reference.","zh":"為了被取錄，教練必須提交推薦信。"},{"en":"In order to be accepted means so that someone can be approved or allowed to join.","zh":"in order to be accepted 是指為了獲批准或被允許加入。"},{"en":"In order to be accepted for the course, students must send their certificates.","zh":"為了被課程取錄，學生必須提交證書。"},{"en":"Requirements help organisations choose suitable and safe applicants.","zh":"要求幫助機構選擇合適而安全的申請者。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose of a condition.","zh":"這個短語解釋某條件的目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"submit a reference","meaning":"提交推薦信","examples":[{"en":"All instructors have to submit a reference.","zh":"所有教練都必須提交推薦信。"},{"en":"To submit a reference means to provide a letter or contact from someone who can recommend you.","zh":"submit a reference 是指提供能推薦你的人的信件或聯絡資料。"},{"en":"A job applicant may submit a reference from a former teacher or employer.","zh":"求職者可能提交前老師或僱主的推薦信。"},{"en":"References help organisations check a person’s character and experience.","zh":"推薦信幫助機構核實一個人的品格和經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in job and course applications.","zh":"這個短語常見於求職和課程申請。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"work with children","meaning":"與兒童一起工作","examples":[{"en":"The reference must come from someone who has seen them work with children.","zh":"推薦信必須來自曾見過他們與兒童一起工作的人。"},{"en":"To work with children means to teach, care for, supervise, or support children.","zh":"work with children 是指教導、照顧、監督或支援兒童。"},{"en":"A sports coach needs patience and safety awareness when working with children.","zh":"運動教練與兒童一起工作時需要耐性和安全意識。"},{"en":"Experience with children helps staff understand behaviour, emotions, and communication.","zh":"與兒童相處的經驗幫助職員理解行為、情緒和溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical experience with young people.","zh":"這個短語著重與年幼人士一起工作的實際經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"work as a babysitter","meaning":"做過保姆","examples":[{"en":"An applicant may have worked as a babysitter before.","zh":"申請者以前可能做過保姆。"},{"en":"To work as a babysitter means to look after children while their parents are away.","zh":"work as a babysitter 是指在家長不在時照顧孩子。"},{"en":"A teenager may work as a babysitter for neighbours at weekends.","zh":"青少年可能在週末為鄰居做保姆。"},{"en":"Babysitting experience can show that a person is trusted with children.","zh":"保姆經驗可以顯示某人被信任照顧孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a childcare role, often part-time or temporary.","zh":"這個短語描述托兒角色，通常是兼職或臨時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"complete a training course","meaning":"完成培訓課程","examples":[{"en":"All instructors have to complete the camp’s training course.","zh":"所有教練都必須完成單車營的培訓課程。"},{"en":"To complete a training course means to finish all required lessons or practice sessions.","zh":"complete a training course 是指完成所有規定課堂或練習。"},{"en":"A new lifeguard must complete a training course before working at a pool.","zh":"新救生員在泳池工作前必須完成培訓課程。"},{"en":"Training courses prepare staff to follow rules and handle problems safely.","zh":"培訓課程讓職員準備好遵守規則並安全處理問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that learning must be finished before taking responsibility.","zh":"這個短語顯示在承擔責任前必須完成學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lesson plans","meaning":"教案；課堂計劃","examples":[{"en":"The training course includes how to do lesson plans.","zh":"培訓課程包括如何制定教案。"},{"en":"Lesson plans are written plans showing what a teacher will teach and how.","zh":"lesson plans 是顯示老師會教甚麼和如何教的書面計劃。"},{"en":"A swimming instructor may prepare lesson plans for beginners and advanced learners.","zh":"游泳教練可能為初學者和進階學員準備教案。"},{"en":"Lesson plans help classes run safely and in a clear order.","zh":"教案幫助課堂安全並有清楚次序地進行。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in teaching and training.","zh":"這個短語常見於教學和培訓。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"care for","meaning":"照顧","examples":[{"en":"Instructors learn how to care for the well-being of the children.","zh":"教練學習如何照顧孩子的身心健康。"},{"en":"To care for someone means to look after their needs, safety, and comfort.","zh":"care for someone 是指照顧某人的需要、安全和舒適。"},{"en":"Nurses care for patients by checking their condition and giving medicine.","zh":"護士透過檢查病人情況和給藥來照顧病人。"},{"en":"Caring for children requires attention, patience, and responsibility.","zh":"照顧孩子需要留意、耐性和責任感。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on protection and support.","zh":"這個短語著重保護和支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"well-being","meaning":"身心健康","examples":[{"en":"Instructors must care for the well-being of the children in their class.","zh":"教練必須照顧班中孩子的身心健康。"},{"en":"Well-being means a person’s health, happiness, safety, and general condition.","zh":"well-being 是指一個人的健康、快樂、安全和整體狀況。"},{"en":"Schools support well-being by giving children safe spaces and trusted adults.","zh":"學校透過提供安全空間和值得信任的成人來支援身心健康。"},{"en":"A child’s well-being can affect learning, confidence, and behaviour.","zh":"孩子的身心健康可以影響學習、信心和行為。"},{"en":"This word is broader than physical health only.","zh":"這個詞比單純身體健康更廣泛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"do a great job","meaning":"做得出色","examples":[{"en":"Jake says the instructors do a great job.","zh":"Jake 說教練做得很出色。"},{"en":"To do a great job means to perform work very well.","zh":"do a great job 是指工作表現非常好。"},{"en":"A teacher does a great job when students feel safe and learn clearly.","zh":"當學生感到安全並清楚學習，老師就是做得出色。"},{"en":"People do a great job when they are skilled, prepared, and caring.","zh":"有技能、有準備和有愛心的人通常會做得出色。"},{"en":"This phrase gives strong positive praise.","zh":"這個短語表示強烈正面稱讚。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"class size","meaning":"班級人數","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks what size Charlie’s class will be.","zh":"那位女士問 Charlie 的班級人數會是多少。"},{"en":"Class size means the number of students in a class.","zh":"class size 是指一班有多少名學生。"},{"en":"A smaller class size allows teachers to give more individual attention.","zh":"較小班級人數讓老師能給予更多個別關注。"},{"en":"Class size affects safety, noise, and how well children can be supervised.","zh":"班級人數會影響安全、噪音和孩子是否能被妥善看管。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when parents compare courses.","zh":"這個短語在家長比較課程時很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have a limit of","meaning":"設有……上限","examples":[{"en":"The camp has a limit of eight children in each class.","zh":"這個營每班設有八名孩子的上限。"},{"en":"To have a limit of a number means that number is the maximum allowed.","zh":"have a limit of a number 是指該數字是可允許的最高數量。"},{"en":"A swimming class may have a limit of six beginners for safety.","zh":"為了安全，游泳初班可能設有六人的上限。"},{"en":"Limits help staff manage groups and reduce risk.","zh":"上限幫助職員管理組別並降低風險。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the largest permitted number.","zh":"這個短語解釋最高允許數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get to know someone well","meaning":"很好地了解某人","examples":[{"en":"The instructor can get to know each child well.","zh":"教練可以很好地了解每個孩子。"},{"en":"To get to know someone well means to learn about their personality, needs, and ability.","zh":"get to know someone well 是指了解某人的性格、需要和能力。"},{"en":"A teacher gets to know students well by watching how they learn and behave.","zh":"老師透過觀察學生如何學習和表現來更了解學生。"},{"en":"Knowing each child well helps staff give safer and more suitable support.","zh":"了解每個孩子有助職員提供更安全和更合適的支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes developing understanding over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間建立理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be out riding","meaning":"在外面踏單車","examples":[{"en":"The children are out riding most of the time.","zh":"孩子大部分時間都在外面踏單車。"},{"en":"To be out riding means to be outside riding bicycles.","zh":"be out riding 是指在戶外踏單車。"},{"en":"Children at a cycle camp are usually out riding instead of sitting in a classroom.","zh":"單車營的孩子通常在外面踏單車，而不是坐在課室裏。"},{"en":"Being out riding gives learners practical experience and confidence.","zh":"在外面踏單車讓學員獲得實際經驗和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on active outdoor practice.","zh":"這個短語著重主動的戶外練習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"quiet times","meaning":"安靜活動時間","examples":[{"en":"The children have quiet times during the camp.","zh":"孩子在營中有安靜活動時間。"},{"en":"Quiet times are calmer periods when children rest or do low-energy activities.","zh":"quiet times 是較平靜的時段，孩子休息或做低活動量的事情。"},{"en":"After outdoor games, children may have quiet time for reading or listening to a story.","zh":"戶外遊戲後，孩子可能有閱讀或聽故事的安靜時間。"},{"en":"Quiet times help children recover energy and avoid becoming too tired.","zh":"安靜活動時間幫助孩子恢復精力，避免過度疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts rest periods with active sessions.","zh":"這個短語把休息時段與活動時段作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have something to do with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The story may have something to do with cycling.","zh":"這個故事可能與踩單車有關。"},{"en":"To have something to do with something means to be connected with it in some way.","zh":"have something to do with something 是指以某種方式與某事有關。"},{"en":"A classroom game may have something to do with road signs if children are learning cycling safety.","zh":"如果孩子正在學單車安全，課堂遊戲可能與道路標誌有關。"},{"en":"Connections between activities and the main topic make learning more meaningful.","zh":"活動與主要主題之間的連繫會令學習更有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a link, even if the link is not very strong.","zh":"這個短語表示有關聯，即使關聯不一定很強。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get someone to play","meaning":"叫某人玩……","examples":[{"en":"The instructor may get the children to play a game together.","zh":"教練可能會叫孩子一起玩遊戲。"},{"en":"To get someone to play means to encourage or arrange for them to take part in a game.","zh":"get someone to play 是指鼓勵或安排某人參加遊戲。"},{"en":"A teacher may get shy students to play a simple team game.","zh":"老師可能會叫害羞學生玩簡單小組遊戲。"},{"en":"Games can help children relax and practise social skills.","zh":"遊戲可以幫助孩子放鬆並練習社交技能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows someone causing or encouraging an action.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人促成或鼓勵一個行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"classes still run","meaning":"課堂仍然照常舉行","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether the classes still run if it rains.","zh":"那位女士問如果下雨，課堂是否仍然照常舉行。"},{"en":"Classes still run means lessons continue as planned.","zh":"classes still run 是指課堂按計劃繼續進行。"},{"en":"Outdoor sports classes may still run in light rain if conditions are safe.","zh":"如果情況安全，戶外運動課可能在小雨中仍照常舉行。"},{"en":"Knowing whether classes continue helps parents prepare clothing and transport.","zh":"知道課堂是否繼續，有助家長準備衣物和交通。"},{"en":"This phrase checks whether bad weather changes the schedule.","zh":"這個短語確認壞天氣是否會改變時間表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"put someone off","meaning":"令某人卻步","examples":[{"en":"The camp does not let rain put the children off.","zh":"這個營不會讓下雨令孩子卻步。"},{"en":"To put someone off means to discourage them or make them not want to do something.","zh":"put someone off 是指令某人失去興趣或不想做某事。"},{"en":"A difficult first lesson may put a child off learning piano.","zh":"困難的第一堂課可能令孩子不想學鋼琴。"},{"en":"Good support can stop small problems from putting learners off.","zh":"良好支援可以防止小問題令學習者卻步。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something reduces motivation or confidence.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事降低動力或信心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"put on waterproofs","meaning":"穿上防水衣物","examples":[{"en":"The children put on waterproofs and keep cycling.","zh":"孩子穿上防水衣物並繼續踏單車。"},{"en":"To put on waterproofs means to wear waterproof clothing to stay dry.","zh":"put on waterproofs 是指穿上防水衣物以保持乾爽。"},{"en":"Hikers put on waterproofs when heavy rain begins.","zh":"遠足人士在大雨開始時會穿上防水衣物。"},{"en":"Waterproof clothing allows outdoor activities to continue in wet weather.","zh":"防水衣物讓戶外活動在潮濕天氣中繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparing for rain.","zh":"這個短語描述為下雨作準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"keep cycling","meaning":"繼續踏單車","examples":[{"en":"The children keep cycling even when it rains.","zh":"即使下雨，孩子仍繼續踏單車。"},{"en":"To keep cycling means to continue riding a bike.","zh":"keep cycling 是指繼續踩單車。"},{"en":"A cyclist may keep cycling slowly if the rain is light and the road is safe.","zh":"如果雨勢很小且道路安全，單車手可能慢慢繼續踏單車。"},{"en":"Continuing practice helps children build resilience and confidence.","zh":"持續練習幫助孩子建立韌性和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an activity does not stop.","zh":"這個短語顯示活動沒有停止。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bring along","meaning":"帶同","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether Charlie should bring anything along.","zh":"那位女士問 Charlie 是否應帶同任何東西。"},{"en":"To bring along something means to take it with you to a place or event.","zh":"bring along something 是指把某物帶去某地方或活動。"},{"en":"Students should bring along a water bottle for sports day.","zh":"學生應在運動會帶同水樽。"},{"en":"Bringing the right items helps children feel prepared and comfortable.","zh":"帶同合適物品能幫助孩子感到準備好和舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when giving practical instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於實用指示中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spare clothes","meaning":"後備衣物","examples":[{"en":"Charlie should bring some spare clothes.","zh":"Charlie 應帶一些後備衣物。"},{"en":"Spare clothes are extra clothes kept ready in case the first set becomes wet or dirty.","zh":"spare clothes 是預備好的額外衣物，以防原本衣服弄濕或弄髒。"},{"en":"Young children often bring spare clothes on school trips.","zh":"年幼孩子學校旅行時常帶後備衣物。"},{"en":"Spare clothes are useful when outdoor activities involve rain, mud, or sweat.","zh":"當戶外活動涉及雨水、泥土或汗水，後備衣物很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to backup clothing.","zh":"這個短語指備用衣服。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"especially if","meaning":"尤其如果……","examples":[{"en":"Spare clothes are useful, especially if the weather is not good.","zh":"後備衣物很有用，尤其如果天氣不好。"},{"en":"Especially if means particularly in the situation where something happens.","zh":"especially if 是指特別是在某情況發生時。"},{"en":"Take a jacket, especially if you will be outside in the evening.","zh":"帶件外套吧，尤其如果你晚上會在戶外。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the condition that makes advice more important.","zh":"這個短語突出令建議更重要的條件。"},{"en":"It helps explain when something matters most.","zh":"它有助解釋某事何時最重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"break time","meaning":"小息時間","examples":[{"en":"Charlie should bring a snack for break time.","zh":"Charlie 應為小息時間帶小食。"},{"en":"Break time is a short rest period between activities or lessons.","zh":"break time 是活動或課堂之間的短暫休息時間。"},{"en":"Children may eat fruit or drink water during break time.","zh":"孩子可能在小息時間吃水果或喝水。"},{"en":"Break time helps children recover energy before continuing.","zh":"小息時間幫助孩子恢復精力再繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a planned pause.","zh":"這個短語指有計劃的暫停。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"provide that","meaning":"提供那樣東西","examples":[{"en":"The camp will provide drinks for the children.","zh":"單車營會為孩子提供飲品。"},{"en":"To provide that means to supply that item or thing.","zh":"provide that 是指供應那件物品或那樣東西。"},{"en":"A school trip may ask children to bring lunch but provide water.","zh":"學校旅行可能要求孩子帶午餐，但會提供清水。"},{"en":"When organisers provide something, families do not need to bring it themselves.","zh":"當組織者提供某物，家庭就不用自己帶。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to supplying a specific item already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指提供剛提到的特定物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"The woman should make sure Charlie has proper shoes.","zh":"那位女士應確保 Charlie 有合適鞋子。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check carefully so that something is true or done.","zh":"make sure 是指仔細檢查，確保某事屬實或已完成。"},{"en":"Parents should make sure children wear helmets before cycling.","zh":"家長應確保孩子踩單車前戴上頭盔。"},{"en":"Making sure prevents mistakes, accidents, and missing items.","zh":"確保某事可以防止錯誤、意外和遺漏物品。"},{"en":"This phrase shows care and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語顯示小心和責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"shoes, not sandals","meaning":"鞋，不是涼鞋","examples":[{"en":"Charlie should wear shoes, not sandals.","zh":"Charlie 應穿鞋，不是涼鞋。"},{"en":"Shoes, not sandals means closed shoes are needed instead of open footwear.","zh":"shoes, not sandals 是指需要包腳鞋，而不是露腳涼鞋。"},{"en":"Children should wear shoes, not sandals, for climbing or cycling activities.","zh":"孩子做攀爬或單車活動時應穿鞋，不是涼鞋。"},{"en":"Proper shoes protect feet better and reduce the risk of injury.","zh":"合適鞋子能更好保護雙腳，並減少受傷風險。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear contrast between suitable and unsuitable footwear.","zh":"這個短語清楚對比合適和不合適的鞋履。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at present","meaning":"目前","examples":[{"en":"At present, Charlie has to take medication every few hours.","zh":"目前，Charlie 必須每隔幾小時服藥。"},{"en":"At present means at the current time or now.","zh":"at present 是指目前或現在。"},{"en":"At present, the library is open only in the mornings.","zh":"目前，圖書館只在早上開放。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the situation may change later.","zh":"這個短語暗示情況之後可能會改變。"},{"en":"It is slightly more formal than “right now”.","zh":"它比 right now 稍正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take medication","meaning":"服藥","examples":[{"en":"Charlie has to take medication every few hours.","zh":"Charlie 必須每隔幾小時服藥。"},{"en":"To take medication means to use medicine as instructed.","zh":"take medication 是指按照指示使用藥物。"},{"en":"A child may need to take medication after lunch if the doctor says so.","zh":"如果醫生這樣吩咐，孩子可能需要午飯後服藥。"},{"en":"Taking medication at the right time helps treatment work properly.","zh":"準時服藥有助治療正常發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in health and care contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於健康和照顧語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"every few hours","meaning":"每隔幾小時","examples":[{"en":"Charlie needs to take medication every few hours.","zh":"Charlie 需要每隔幾小時服藥。"},{"en":"Every few hours means repeatedly after several hours each time.","zh":"every few hours 是指每次相隔幾小時反覆進行。"},{"en":"A nurse may check a patient’s temperature every few hours.","zh":"護士可能每隔幾小時檢查病人體溫。"},{"en":"Regular timing matters when medicine must stay effective in the body.","zh":"當藥物需要在身體內保持效力，定時很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated intervals.","zh":"這個短語描述重複的時間間隔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"give us details of","meaning":"把……的詳情告訴我們","examples":[{"en":"The woman should give the camp details of when Charlie needs his medication.","zh":"那位女士應把 Charlie 何時需要服藥的詳情告訴單車營。"},{"en":"To give us details of something means to provide specific information about it.","zh":"give us details of something 是指提供關於某事的具體資料。"},{"en":"Parents should give the school details of allergies, medicine, or emergency contacts.","zh":"家長應把過敏、藥物或緊急聯絡人的詳情告訴學校。"},{"en":"Detailed information helps staff care for children safely.","zh":"詳細資料幫助職員安全照顧孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for exact facts, not just a general statement.","zh":"這個短語要求確切事實，而不只是籠統說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make sure he does","meaning":"確保他做到","examples":[{"en":"The staff will make sure Charlie takes his medication.","zh":"職員會確保 Charlie 服藥。"},{"en":"Make sure he does means check that he actually does the required action.","zh":"make sure he does 是指確認他真的完成所需行動。"},{"en":"If a child must bring homework, a parent may make sure he does before leaving home.","zh":"如果孩子必須帶功課，家長可能在離家前確保他做到。"},{"en":"Staff supervision helps children follow important instructions.","zh":"職員監督幫助孩子遵守重要指示。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to an action already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語回指前面已提及的行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a few things you should know","meaning":"你應該知道的幾件事","examples":[{"en":"There are a few things the woman should know about Day 1.","zh":"關於營期第一日，有幾件事那位女士應該知道。"},{"en":"A few things you should know means several important pieces of information you need before something happens.","zh":"a few things you should know 是指在某事發生前你需要知道的幾項重要資料。"},{"en":"Before the school trip, there are a few things parents should know.","zh":"學校旅行前，有幾件事家長應該知道。"},{"en":"Giving key information early helps people prepare properly.","zh":"及早提供重點資料幫助人們好好準備。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces practical instructions or warnings.","zh":"這個短語引入實用指示或提醒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Day 1 of the camp","meaning":"營期第一日","examples":[{"en":"Jake explains what happens on Day 1 of the camp.","zh":"Jake 解釋營期第一日會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Day 1 of the camp means the first day of the camp programme.","zh":"Day 1 of the camp 是指營隊課程的第一天。"},{"en":"Day 1 of a course often includes registration, introductions, and safety checks.","zh":"課程第一日通常包括登記、介紹和安全檢查。"},{"en":"The first day may need extra time because children and staff are getting organised.","zh":"第一天可能需要額外時間，因為孩子和職員都要安排好。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the beginning of a multi-day activity.","zh":"這個短語標示多日活動的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"normally start at","meaning":"通常在……開始","examples":[{"en":"The classes normally start at 9:30 every morning.","zh":"課堂通常每天早上9時30分開始。"},{"en":"Normally start at means usually begin at a particular time.","zh":"normally start at 是指通常在某個時間開始。"},{"en":"School assemblies normally start at eight o’clock.","zh":"學校早會通常在八點開始。"},{"en":"Knowing the normal start time helps families arrive on time.","zh":"知道正常開始時間有助家庭準時到達。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the usual schedule.","zh":"這個短語描述通常時間表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"aim to get someone somewhere by","meaning":"盡量在……前把某人送到某處","examples":[{"en":"The woman should aim to get Charlie there by 9:20.","zh":"那位女士應盡量在9時20分前把 Charlie 送到那裏。"},{"en":"To aim to get someone somewhere by a time means to try to have them arrive there no later than that time.","zh":"aim to get someone somewhere by a time 是指盡量讓某人在該時間前到達某地。"},{"en":"Parents should aim to get children to the station by seven thirty.","zh":"家長應盡量在七點半前把孩子送到車站。"},{"en":"Arriving early gives time for registration, equipment checks, or instructions.","zh":"早到可預留時間登記、檢查器材或聽指示。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a target arrival time.","zh":"這個短語設定目標到達時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"finishing time","meaning":"結束時間","examples":[{"en":"The finishing time will be 12:30 as usual.","zh":"結束時間會如常是12時30分。"},{"en":"Finishing time is the time when an activity, class, or event ends.","zh":"finishing time 是活動、課堂或事件結束的時間。"},{"en":"Parents need to know the finishing time so they can collect children on time.","zh":"家長需要知道結束時間，才能準時接孩子。"},{"en":"Clear finishing times prevent waiting and confusion.","zh":"清楚結束時間可以避免等候和混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the scheduled end time.","zh":"這個短語指預定結束時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as usual","meaning":"如常","examples":[{"en":"The camp will finish at 12:30 as usual.","zh":"單車營會如常在12時30分結束。"},{"en":"As usual means in the normal or expected way.","zh":"as usual 是指按正常或預期方式。"},{"en":"The library opens at nine as usual after the holiday.","zh":"假期後，圖書館如常在九點開門。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures people that something has not changed.","zh":"這個短語安撫人們，表示某事沒有改變。"},{"en":"It contrasts normal arrangements with special changes.","zh":"它把正常安排與特別改動作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"additional time","meaning":"額外時間","examples":[{"en":"The camp needs additional time on the first day.","zh":"單車營第一天需要額外時間。"},{"en":"Additional time means extra time beyond the usual amount.","zh":"additional time 是指正常所需時間以外的額外時間。"},{"en":"A teacher may give additional time if students need to set up equipment.","zh":"如果學生需要設置器材，老師可能會給額外時間。"},{"en":"Extra time helps staff complete tasks that do not happen every day.","zh":"額外時間幫助職員完成並非每天都有的任務。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why people may need to arrive earlier.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何人們可能需要早到。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"extra things to do","meaning":"額外要做的事情","examples":[{"en":"There are a few extra things to do on Day 1.","zh":"營期第一日有幾件額外要做的事情。"},{"en":"Extra things to do are additional tasks beyond the normal routine.","zh":"extra things to do 是正常流程以外的額外任務。"},{"en":"On the first day of school, there may be extra things to do, such as collecting forms.","zh":"開學第一天可能有額外要做的事情，例如收表格。"},{"en":"Extra tasks can make the first day take longer than usual.","zh":"額外任務可以令第一天比平常需時更長。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to added practical requirements.","zh":"這個短語指額外的實際要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"careful check","meaning":"仔細檢查","examples":[{"en":"The staff do a careful check of every child’s helmet.","zh":"職員會仔細檢查每個孩子的頭盔。"},{"en":"A careful check is a close and detailed examination.","zh":"careful check 是近距離而詳細的檢查。"},{"en":"Before a flight, engineers do a careful check of the aircraft.","zh":"飛行前，工程師會仔細檢查飛機。"},{"en":"Careful checks help prevent accidents caused by faulty equipment.","zh":"仔細檢查有助防止因器材故障造成意外。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that safety is being taken seriously.","zh":"這個短語顯示安全受到認真對待。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fit properly","meaning":"尺寸合適；戴得合適","examples":[{"en":"Every child’s helmet must fit properly.","zh":"每個孩子的頭盔都必須戴得合適。"},{"en":"To fit properly means to be the right size and position for safe use.","zh":"fit properly 是指尺寸和位置正確，可以安全使用。"},{"en":"A pair of shoes fits properly when it is not too tight or too loose.","zh":"鞋子不太緊也不太鬆時，就是尺寸合適。"},{"en":"A helmet that does not fit properly may not protect the head well.","zh":"如果頭盔戴得不合適，可能無法好好保護頭部。"},{"en":"This phrase is important for clothing and safety equipment.","zh":"這個短語對衣物和安全裝備很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"adjust it","meaning":"調整它","examples":[{"en":"If the helmet does not fit, the staff will adjust it.","zh":"如果頭盔不合適，職員會調整它。"},{"en":"To adjust it means to change its position, size, or setting so it works better.","zh":"adjust it 是指改變其位置、尺寸或設定，使它更好用。"},{"en":"A teacher may adjust a child’s bike seat before a lesson.","zh":"老師可能在課前調整孩子的單車座位。"},{"en":"Adjusting equipment can improve comfort and safety.","zh":"調整器材可以改善舒適度和安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a small practical change.","zh":"這個短語描述小型實際改動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"find someone another one","meaning":"另找一個給某人","examples":[{"en":"The staff will find Charlie another helmet if necessary.","zh":"如有需要，職員會另找一個頭盔給 Charlie。"},{"en":"To find someone another one means to get a different item for that person.","zh":"find someone another one 是指為某人找另一件物品。"},{"en":"If a child’s chair is broken, the teacher will find him another one.","zh":"如果孩子的椅子壞了，老師會另找一張給他。"},{"en":"Replacing unsuitable equipment helps keep the activity safe.","zh":"替換不合適器材有助保持活動安全。"},{"en":"This phrase shows practical help in solving a problem.","zh":"這個短語顯示解決問題的實際幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"wear it all the time","meaning":"全程戴着它","examples":[{"en":"Charlie must wear his helmet all the time he is on the bike.","zh":"Charlie 在單車上時必須全程戴着頭盔。"},{"en":"To wear it all the time means to keep wearing it continuously during the activity.","zh":"wear it all the time 是指在活動期間一直穿戴着它。"},{"en":"Children must wear safety goggles all the time they are in the lab.","zh":"孩子在實驗室期間必須全程戴着安全眼罩。"},{"en":"Continuous use of safety equipment reduces the chance of injury.","zh":"持續使用安全裝備可減低受傷機會。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the rule applies without breaks.","zh":"這個短語強調規則沒有中斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"meet up in","meaning":"在……集合","examples":[{"en":"The children will meet up in the tent.","zh":"孩子會在帳篷集合。"},{"en":"To meet up in a place means to gather there at an arranged time.","zh":"meet up in a place 是指在安排好的時間於某地聚集。"},{"en":"Students may meet up in the school hall before a trip.","zh":"學生旅行前可能在學校禮堂集合。"},{"en":"A meeting point helps organisers check everyone has arrived.","zh":"集合地點幫助組織者確認所有人已到達。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gathering together in a specific place.","zh":"這個短語描述在特定地方聚在一起。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"you can’t miss it","meaning":"你不會錯過；很易找到","examples":[{"en":"The tent is easy to find, so the woman cannot miss it.","zh":"帳篷很容易找到，所以那位女士不會錯過。"},{"en":"You can’t miss it means it is very easy to see or find.","zh":"you can’t miss it 是指它非常容易看見或找到。"},{"en":"The school office is beside the main gate; you can’t miss it.","zh":"學校辦公室就在大門旁邊，你不會錯過。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures someone who may worry about getting lost.","zh":"這個短語安撫可能擔心迷路的人。"},{"en":"It is used when a place or object is obvious.","zh":"它用於地方或物件很明顯時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take their class away","meaning":"帶自己的班離開","examples":[{"en":"Each instructor will take their class away and get started.","zh":"每位教練會帶自己的班離開並開始活動。"},{"en":"To take their class away means to lead their group to another place for an activity.","zh":"take their class away 是指帶領自己的組別到另一個地方活動。"},{"en":"After registration, teachers may take their classes away to different rooms.","zh":"登記後，老師可能帶自己的班到不同課室。"},{"en":"Moving groups separately helps activities begin in an organised way.","zh":"分組移動有助活動有秩序地開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a teacher leading their own group.","zh":"這個短語描述老師帶領自己的組別。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get started","meaning":"開始","examples":[{"en":"The instructors will take their classes away and get started.","zh":"教練會帶自己的班離開並開始。"},{"en":"To get started means to begin an activity or task.","zh":"get started 是指開始活動或任務。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “Let’s get started,” when everyone is ready.","zh":"當大家準備好時，老師可能會說：「我們開始吧。」"},{"en":"Starting clearly helps learners know what to do next.","zh":"清楚開始有助學習者知道下一步做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the beginning of action.","zh":"這個短語標示行動開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"how much the camp costs","meaning":"營費是多少","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks how much the camp costs a week.","zh":"那位女士問單車營每星期收費是多少。"},{"en":"How much the camp costs asks about the price of attending the camp.","zh":"how much the camp costs 是詢問參加營隊的費用。"},{"en":"Parents often ask how much a summer camp costs before booking.","zh":"家長報名前常會問暑期營費用是多少。"},{"en":"Knowing the cost helps families decide whether the programme is affordable.","zh":"知道費用有助家庭決定課程是否負擔得起。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when asking about fees.","zh":"這個短語用於詢問收費。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"costs a week","meaning":"每星期收費","examples":[{"en":"The camp costs 199 dollars a week.","zh":"這個營每星期收費199美元。"},{"en":"Costs a week means the price charged for one week.","zh":"costs a week 是指每一星期的收費。"},{"en":"The sports course costs 80 dollars a week, including equipment use.","zh":"運動課每星期收費80美元，包括器材使用。"},{"en":"Weekly fees help parents compare short-term and long-term costs.","zh":"每週費用有助家長比較短期和長期成本。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the price for a weekly period.","zh":"這個短語提供每週價格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"manage to keep","meaning":"成功保持","examples":[{"en":"The camp has managed to keep the price almost the same as last year.","zh":"這個營成功保持價格幾乎與去年相同。"},{"en":"To manage to keep something means to succeed in maintaining it despite difficulty.","zh":"manage to keep something 是指即使有困難仍成功維持某事。"},{"en":"A shop may manage to keep prices low by buying supplies carefully.","zh":"商店可能透過小心採購成功保持低價。"},{"en":"Keeping prices stable can be difficult when costs rise.","zh":"成本上升時，保持價格穩定可能很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase shows successful control of a situation.","zh":"這個短語顯示成功控制情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"more or less the same as","meaning":"與……差不多一樣","examples":[{"en":"The price is more or less the same as last year.","zh":"價格與去年差不多一樣。"},{"en":"More or less the same as means almost the same, with only small differences.","zh":"more or less the same as 是指幾乎相同，只有小差異。"},{"en":"This year’s timetable is more or less the same as last year’s.","zh":"今年的時間表與去年的差不多一樣。"},{"en":"Small changes may exist, but the general situation has not changed much.","zh":"可能有小變化，但整體情況沒有太大改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for approximate comparisons.","zh":"這個短語適合用於約略比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"places are filling up","meaning":"名額快將額滿","examples":[{"en":"The places are filling up quite quickly.","zh":"名額很快就快將額滿。"},{"en":"Places are filling up means available spaces are being booked or taken.","zh":"places are filling up 是指可用名額正在被預訂或佔用。"},{"en":"Swimming lesson places fill up quickly before summer.","zh":"夏天前，游泳課名額很快額滿。"},{"en":"When places fill up, late applicants may not get a spot.","zh":"當名額快滿，遲申請者可能得不到位置。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests people should book soon.","zh":"這個短語暗示人們應盡快報名。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"book for","meaning":"預訂……","examples":[{"en":"The woman would like to book a place for Charlie.","zh":"那位女士想為 Charlie 預訂一個名額。"},{"en":"To book for someone means to reserve a place or service for that person.","zh":"book for someone 是指為某人預留名額或服務。"},{"en":"A parent may book a swimming lesson for her daughter.","zh":"家長可能為女兒預訂游泳課。"},{"en":"Booking early helps secure a place before it fills up.","zh":"提早預訂有助在額滿前確保位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for reservations.","zh":"這個短語用於預約或預訂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"recruitment consultant","meaning":"招聘顧問","examples":[{"en":"Megan Baker is a recruitment consultant at AVT Recruitment Specialists.","zh":"Megan Baker 是 AVT Recruitment Specialists 的招聘顧問。"},{"en":"A recruitment consultant helps employers find workers and helps candidates find jobs.","zh":"recruitment consultant 幫助僱主找員工，也幫助求職者找工作。"},{"en":"A recruitment consultant may interview applicants and match them with suitable roles.","zh":"招聘顧問可能面試申請者，並把他們配對到合適職位。"},{"en":"Good recruitment advice can save companies time and help job seekers understand opportunities.","zh":"良好的招聘建議可以為公司節省時間，並幫助求職者了解機會。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a professional job in hiring.","zh":"這個短語指招聘領域中的專業職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"recruitment specialists","meaning":"專業招聘公司","examples":[{"en":"AVT Recruitment Specialists helps people find work in specialist sectors.","zh":"AVT Recruitment Specialists 幫助人們在專門界別找工作。"},{"en":"Recruitment specialists are people or companies with expert knowledge of hiring in particular fields.","zh":"recruitment specialists 是對特定領域招聘有專業知識的人或公司。"},{"en":"Recruitment specialists in healthcare understand nursing roles and hospital requirements.","zh":"醫療招聘專家了解護理職位和醫院要求。"},{"en":"Specialist recruiters can match candidates more accurately because they know the industry.","zh":"專業招聘者因了解行業，所以能更準確配對候選人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to expert hiring services.","zh":"這個短語指專業招聘服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"specialise in","meaning":"專門從事……","examples":[{"en":"The company specialises in positions in agriculture and horticulture.","zh":"這間公司專門從事農業和園藝職位招聘。"},{"en":"To specialise in something means to focus on one particular area and develop expertise in it.","zh":"specialise in something 是指專注於某個特定範疇並發展專業知識。"},{"en":"A doctor may specialise in children’s health.","zh":"醫生可能專門從事兒童健康。"},{"en":"Companies that specialise in one field often understand its needs better.","zh":"專門從事某一領域的公司通常更了解該領域需要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a specific professional focus.","zh":"這個短語顯示特定專業焦點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"positions that involve","meaning":"涉及……的職位","examples":[{"en":"The company specialises in positions that involve working outdoors.","zh":"這間公司專門招聘涉及戶外工作的職位。"},{"en":"Positions that involve something are jobs that include that activity or responsibility.","zh":"positions that involve something 是指包括該活動或責任的工作。"},{"en":"Some school jobs involve working with young children every day.","zh":"有些學校職位每天涉及與年幼孩子工作。"},{"en":"Knowing what a position involves helps applicants decide if it suits them.","zh":"知道職位涉及甚麼，有助申請者決定是否適合自己。"},{"en":"This phrase links a job with its main tasks.","zh":"這個短語把工作與主要任務連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"agriculture and horticulture sectors","meaning":"農業及園藝界別","examples":[{"en":"The company recruits for the agriculture and horticulture sectors.","zh":"這間公司為農業及園藝界別招聘。"},{"en":"Agriculture and horticulture sectors are industries connected with farming, crops, plants, and food production.","zh":"agriculture and horticulture sectors 是與農耕、作物、植物和食品生產相關的行業。"},{"en":"These sectors may include farms, nurseries, parks, and fresh produce companies.","zh":"這些界別可能包括農場、苗圃、公園和新鮮農產品公司。"},{"en":"Jobs in these sectors can involve outdoor work, machinery, science, or sales.","zh":"這些界別的工作可能涉及戶外工作、機器、科學或銷售。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to two related land-based industries.","zh":"這個短語指兩個相關的土地產業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fresh food production","meaning":"新鮮食品生產","examples":[{"en":"Agriculture and horticulture include fresh food production.","zh":"農業和園藝包括新鮮食品生產。"},{"en":"Fresh food production means growing, harvesting, preparing, or supplying fresh food.","zh":"fresh food production 是指種植、收割、處理或供應新鮮食品。"},{"en":"Farms involved in fresh food production may grow vegetables, fruit, or salad crops.","zh":"從事新鮮食品生產的農場可能種植蔬菜、水果或沙律作物。"},{"en":"Fresh food production needs speed because products can spoil quickly.","zh":"新鮮食品生產需要速度，因為產品可能很快變壞。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on food that is not heavily processed.","zh":"這個短語著重未經高度加工的食品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"garden and park maintenance","meaning":"花園及公園維護","examples":[{"en":"The sectors include garden and park maintenance.","zh":"這些界別包括花園及公園維護。"},{"en":"Garden and park maintenance means caring for outdoor green spaces.","zh":"garden and park maintenance 是指照顧戶外綠化空間。"},{"en":"Workers may cut grass, prune trees, water plants, and repair paths.","zh":"工人可能割草、修剪樹木、澆水和維修小路。"},{"en":"Good maintenance keeps public spaces safe, clean, and attractive.","zh":"良好維護令公共空間安全、清潔和吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical work that keeps gardens and parks in good condition.","zh":"這個短語指讓花園和公園保持良好狀態的實際工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"career opportunities","meaning":"事業機會","examples":[{"en":"These sectors provide some very special career opportunities.","zh":"這些界別提供一些非常特別的事業機會。"},{"en":"Career opportunities are chances to get jobs, develop skills, or move forward in work.","zh":"career opportunities 是獲得工作、發展技能或在職場前進的機會。"},{"en":"A growing industry can create career opportunities for young people.","zh":"成長中的行業可以為年輕人創造事業機會。"},{"en":"Good opportunities help people build experience and earn a living.","zh":"好機會幫助人們累積經驗和謀生。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to possible paths in employment.","zh":"這個短語指就業中的可能發展道路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for a start","meaning":"首先","examples":[{"en":"For a start, these jobs often offer flexible opportunities.","zh":"首先，這些工作通常提供彈性機會。"},{"en":"For a start is used to introduce the first reason or point.","zh":"for a start 用來引入第一個理由或觀點。"},{"en":"This flat is convenient; for a start, it is near the station.","zh":"這個單位很方便；首先，它靠近車站。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests there may be more points after the first one.","zh":"這個短語暗示第一點之後可能還有更多觀點。"},{"en":"It helps organise an explanation.","zh":"它有助組織解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"offer opportunities for","meaning":"為……提供機會","examples":[{"en":"These sectors offer opportunities for people with other responsibilities.","zh":"這些界別為有其他責任的人提供機會。"},{"en":"To offer opportunities for someone means to provide chances that may suit them.","zh":"offer opportunities for someone 是指提供可能適合某人的機會。"},{"en":"Part-time courses offer opportunities for adults who work during the day.","zh":"兼讀課程為日間工作的成年人提供機會。"},{"en":"Flexible opportunities help people balance work with family or study.","zh":"彈性機會幫助人們平衡工作、家庭或學習。"},{"en":"This phrase shows who may benefit from an option.","zh":"這個短語顯示誰可能從某選項中受益。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be stuck with","meaning":"被……困住；受……限制","examples":[{"en":"Some recruits do not want to be stuck with a 40-hour week.","zh":"有些新入職者不想被每週40小時工作制限制。"},{"en":"To be stuck with something means to have no choice but to accept it.","zh":"be stuck with something 是指沒有選擇，只能接受某事。"},{"en":"A student may feel stuck with a timetable that leaves no free afternoons.","zh":"學生可能覺得被沒有空閒下午的時間表困住。"},{"en":"People dislike being stuck with rigid arrangements when they need flexibility.","zh":"當人們需要彈性，他們會不喜歡被僵硬安排限制。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests frustration or lack of choice.","zh":"這個短語常暗示不滿或缺乏選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a 40-hour week","meaning":"每週40小時工作制","examples":[{"en":"Some people do not want a fixed 40-hour week.","zh":"有些人不想要固定的每週40小時工作制。"},{"en":"A 40-hour week means working forty hours in one week, often full-time.","zh":"a 40-hour week 是指一星期工作40小時，通常是全職。"},{"en":"Many office jobs are based on a 40-hour week.","zh":"許多辦公室工作以每週40小時為基礎。"},{"en":"A fixed weekly schedule may be difficult for people with childcare responsibilities.","zh":"對有照顧子女責任的人來說，固定每週工時可能很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to standard working hours.","zh":"這個短語指標準工作時數。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"juggle work with","meaning":"同時兼顧工作與……","examples":[{"en":"Many recruits need to juggle work with child care.","zh":"許多新入職者需要同時兼顧工作與照顧子女。"},{"en":"To juggle work with something means to manage work and another responsibility at the same time.","zh":"juggle work with something 是指同時管理工作和另一項責任。"},{"en":"Parents often juggle work with school runs and family meals.","zh":"家長常要同時兼顧工作、接送孩子和家庭晚餐。"},{"en":"Flexible hours help people juggle different responsibilities more successfully.","zh":"彈性工時幫助人們更成功地兼顧不同責任。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests balancing several demands.","zh":"這個短語表示平衡多項要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"other responsibilities","meaning":"其他責任","examples":[{"en":"Some recruits need to balance work with other responsibilities.","zh":"有些新入職者需要平衡工作與其他責任。"},{"en":"Other responsibilities are duties besides the main job, such as family care or study.","zh":"other responsibilities 是主要工作以外的職責，例如家庭照顧或學習。"},{"en":"A worker may have other responsibilities, including caring for an elderly parent.","zh":"員工可能有其他責任，包括照顧年長父母。"},{"en":"Extra responsibilities can affect when and how much someone can work.","zh":"額外責任會影響某人何時和能工作多少。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why flexible work may be important.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何彈性工作可能重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"child care","meaning":"照顧子女","examples":[{"en":"Child care is an important responsibility for many recruits.","zh":"照顧子女是許多新入職者的重要責任。"},{"en":"Child care means looking after children and meeting their daily needs.","zh":"child care 是指照顧孩子並滿足他們的日常需要。"},{"en":"Parents may need child care before school, after school, or during holidays.","zh":"家長可能在上學前、放學後或假期需要照顧子女安排。"},{"en":"Lack of child care can stop people from accepting certain jobs.","zh":"缺乏托兒支援可能令人無法接受某些工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical care for children.","zh":"這個短語指對孩子的實際照顧。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rural setting","meaning":"鄉郊環境","examples":[{"en":"Some people like working in a rural setting.","zh":"有些人喜歡在鄉郊環境工作。"},{"en":"A rural setting is a countryside environment away from large towns and cities.","zh":"rural setting 是遠離大型城鎮和城市的鄉村環境。"},{"en":"A farm, orchard, or plant nursery may be in a rural setting.","zh":"農場、果園或苗圃可能位於鄉郊環境。"},{"en":"Rural settings can offer fresh air and space, but may be far from shops or transport.","zh":"鄉郊環境可以提供新鮮空氣和空間，但可能離商店或交通很遠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the location and atmosphere of work.","zh":"這個短語描述工作的地點和氣氛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be surrounded by","meaning":"被……包圍","examples":[{"en":"Some jobs are surrounded by plants and trees instead of buildings.","zh":"有些工作被植物和樹木包圍，而不是建築物。"},{"en":"To be surrounded by something means to have it all around you.","zh":"be surrounded by something 是指周圍都是某物。"},{"en":"A village may be surrounded by hills and fields.","zh":"村莊可能被山丘和田野包圍。"},{"en":"Being surrounded by nature can make work feel calmer and more open.","zh":"被大自然包圍可以令工作感覺更平靜和開闊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the environment around a person or place.","zh":"這個短語描述人或地方周圍的環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"instead of","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Some people prefer plants and trees instead of buildings.","zh":"有些人較喜歡植物和樹木，而不是建築物。"},{"en":"Instead of means in place of or rather than something else.","zh":"instead of 是指用某物代替另一物，或選擇某物而非另一物。"},{"en":"A student may cycle instead of taking the bus.","zh":"學生可能踩單車，而不是乘巴士。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly shows a choice between two alternatives.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示兩個選項之間的選擇。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing what someone chooses and what they avoid.","zh":"它適合用於比較某人選擇甚麼和避免甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"guarantee that","meaning":"保證那一點","examples":[{"en":"The company cannot guarantee that every job will be in a rural setting.","zh":"公司不能保證每份工作都會在鄉郊環境。"},{"en":"To guarantee that something will happen means to promise it will definitely happen.","zh":"guarantee that something will happen 是指承諾某事一定會發生。"},{"en":"A school cannot guarantee that every child will get their first-choice activity.","zh":"學校不能保證每個孩子都能參加首選活動。"},{"en":"Companies avoid guarantees when conditions depend on clients, locations, or availability.","zh":"當情況取決於客戶、地點或供應時，公司會避免保證。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing certainty or promises.","zh":"這個短語用於討論確定性或承諾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"health benefits","meaning":"健康益處","examples":[{"en":"Outdoor jobs can offer health benefits.","zh":"戶外工作可以提供健康益處。"},{"en":"Health benefits are positive effects on physical or mental health.","zh":"health benefits 是對身體或心理健康的正面影響。"},{"en":"Walking to work can have health benefits because it adds daily exercise.","zh":"步行上班可以有健康益處，因為它增加日常運動。"},{"en":"Fresh air and movement may improve mood and fitness.","zh":"新鮮空氣和活動可能改善心情和體能。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to advantages for health.","zh":"這個短語指健康方面的好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sit all day looking at a screen","meaning":"整天坐着望住螢幕","examples":[{"en":"Some workers dislike sitting all day looking at a screen.","zh":"有些員工不喜歡整天坐着望住螢幕。"},{"en":"To sit all day looking at a screen means to spend the whole working day seated at a computer or device.","zh":"sit all day looking at a screen 是指整個工作天坐着看電腦或裝置螢幕。"},{"en":"Office workers may get tired eyes from sitting all day looking at a screen.","zh":"辦公室員工整天望住螢幕可能會眼睛疲勞。"},{"en":"Outdoor work appeals to people who want more movement and less screen time.","zh":"戶外工作吸引想要更多活動和更少螢幕時間的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sedentary modern work pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述靜態的現代工作模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a big plus","meaning":"一大優點","examples":[{"en":"Not sitting at a screen all day is a big plus for many people.","zh":"不用整天坐着望螢幕對很多人來說是一大優點。"},{"en":"A big plus is a major advantage.","zh":"a big plus 是一個重大好處。"},{"en":"A job close to home is a big plus for parents with young children.","zh":"對有年幼孩子的家長來說，工作地點近家是一大優點。"},{"en":"A strong advantage can make a job more attractive even if there are challenges.","zh":"強大的優點可以令工作更吸引，即使也有挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and positive.","zh":"這個短語較口語，帶正面意思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"there’s a lot of variety","meaning":"差異很大","examples":[{"en":"Salaries can be good, although there is a lot of variety.","zh":"薪金可以不錯，雖然差異很大。"},{"en":"There’s a lot of variety means there are many differences between cases or options.","zh":"there’s a lot of variety 是指不同個案或選項之間有很多差異。"},{"en":"There is a lot of variety in restaurant prices across the city.","zh":"城市中餐廳價格差異很大。"},{"en":"Variety means people should check details rather than assume all jobs are the same.","zh":"有差異代表人們應查看細節，而不是假設所有工作都一樣。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that the situation is not uniform.","zh":"這個短語提醒情況並不一致。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have the opportunity for","meaning":"有機會……","examples":[{"en":"Some jobs give workers the opportunity for travel overseas.","zh":"有些工作讓員工有機會到海外公幹。"},{"en":"To have the opportunity for something means to have the chance to experience or do it.","zh":"have the opportunity for something 是指有機會經歷或做某事。"},{"en":"A university course may give students the opportunity for a work placement abroad.","zh":"大學課程可能讓學生有機會到海外實習。"},{"en":"Opportunities for travel can make a job more attractive to some applicants.","zh":"旅遊或出差機會可以令工作對某些申請者更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible benefit.","zh":"這個短語描述可能的好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"travel overseas","meaning":"到海外公幹；海外出差","examples":[{"en":"Some jobs may involve travel overseas.","zh":"有些工作可能涉及到海外公幹。"},{"en":"To travel overseas means to go to another country, usually across a border or sea.","zh":"travel overseas 是指前往另一個國家，通常跨越國界或海洋。"},{"en":"A sales manager may travel overseas to meet suppliers.","zh":"銷售經理可能到海外出差會見供應商。"},{"en":"Overseas travel can bring experience but may also disrupt family life.","zh":"海外出差可以帶來經驗，但也可能打亂家庭生活。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for international journeys.","zh":"這個短語用於國際行程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"取決於","examples":[{"en":"The chance to travel overseas depends on the job.","zh":"到海外出差的機會取決於工作。"},{"en":"To depend on something means to be decided or affected by it.","zh":"depend on something 是指由某事決定或受其影響。"},{"en":"Whether the picnic happens depends on the weather.","zh":"野餐是否舉行取決於天氣。"},{"en":"If travel depends on the job, not every role will offer it.","zh":"如果出差取決於工作，並非每個職位都有這機會。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the answer changes according to a condition.","zh":"這個短語顯示答案會按條件改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be keen to do it","meaning":"熱衷於做這件事","examples":[{"en":"Not everyone is keen to travel overseas for work.","zh":"不是每個人都熱衷於為工作到海外出差。"},{"en":"To be keen to do something means to be eager or enthusiastic about doing it.","zh":"be keen to do something 是指渴望或熱衷於做某事。"},{"en":"Some workers are keen to learn new skills, while others prefer familiar tasks.","zh":"有些員工熱衷於學新技能，另一些則較喜歡熟悉任務。"},{"en":"People may not be keen to travel if they have family duties or dislike flying.","zh":"如果人們有家庭責任或不喜歡坐飛機，可能不熱衷於出差。"},{"en":"This phrase describes willingness and interest.","zh":"這個短語描述意願和興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"work outdoors","meaning":"戶外工作","examples":[{"en":"Working outdoors has both advantages and challenges.","zh":"戶外工作既有好處，也有挑戰。"},{"en":"To work outdoors means to do your job outside rather than inside a building.","zh":"work outdoors 是指在室外而不是建築物內工作。"},{"en":"Gardeners, farm workers, and tree technicians often work outdoors.","zh":"園丁、農場工人和樹木技術員常在戶外工作。"},{"en":"Outdoor work can provide fresh air but can also be affected by weather.","zh":"戶外工作可以提供新鮮空氣，但也會受天氣影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical work environment.","zh":"這個短語描述實際工作環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have its challenges","meaning":"有其挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Working outdoors does have its challenges.","zh":"戶外工作的確有其挑戰。"},{"en":"To have its challenges means to include difficulties or problems as well as benefits.","zh":"have its challenges 是指除了好處之外，也有困難或問題。"},{"en":"Teaching young children has its challenges, even when it is rewarding.","zh":"教年幼孩子即使有成就感，也有其挑戰。"},{"en":"A job can be attractive and still have difficult parts.","zh":"一份工作可以吸引，但仍有困難部分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a balanced view.","zh":"這個短語提供平衡看法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"extremely unpleasant","meaning":"非常不舒服","examples":[{"en":"Outdoor work can be extremely unpleasant when it is cold and windy.","zh":"天氣寒冷又大風時，戶外工作可能非常不舒服。"},{"en":"Extremely unpleasant means very uncomfortable or difficult to tolerate.","zh":"extremely unpleasant 是指非常不舒服或難以忍受。"},{"en":"Waiting for a bus in heavy rain can be extremely unpleasant.","zh":"大雨中等巴士可能非常不舒服。"},{"en":"Bad weather can turn enjoyable outdoor work into a hard experience.","zh":"惡劣天氣可以把令人享受的戶外工作變成艱難經歷。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly describes discomfort.","zh":"這個短語強烈描述不適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pretty fit","meaning":"體能相當好","examples":[{"en":"Some outdoor jobs require workers to be pretty fit.","zh":"有些戶外工作要求員工體能相當好。"},{"en":"Pretty fit means fairly physically strong and healthy.","zh":"pretty fit 是指身體相當強健和健康。"},{"en":"A delivery worker needs to be pretty fit if the job involves carrying heavy boxes.","zh":"如果送貨工作涉及搬重箱，員工需要體能相當好。"},{"en":"Physical fitness helps workers cope with lifting, walking, and long hours outside.","zh":"良好體能幫助員工應付搬運、步行和長時間戶外工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and means reasonably fit, not necessarily athletic.","zh":"這個短語較口語，指相當健康，不一定是運動員水平。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not as important as it once was","meaning":"不像以前那麼重要","examples":[{"en":"Physical fitness is not as important as it once was because of modern technology.","zh":"由於現代科技，體能不像以前那麼重要。"},{"en":"Not as important as it once was means less important now than in the past.","zh":"not as important as it once was 是指現在不如過去重要。"},{"en":"Handwriting is not as important as it once was because many people type.","zh":"由於很多人打字，手寫不像以前那麼重要。"},{"en":"Technology can reduce the need for certain physical skills.","zh":"科技可以減少對某些體力技能的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase compares present importance with past importance.","zh":"這個短語比較現在與過去的重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"standards of health and safety","meaning":"健康及安全標準","examples":[{"en":"Standards of health and safety are much higher now.","zh":"現在健康及安全標準高得多。"},{"en":"Standards of health and safety are rules and practices that protect people from illness and injury at work.","zh":"standards of health and safety 是保護人們在工作中免受疾病和受傷的規則與做法。"},{"en":"Construction sites need strong health and safety standards to protect workers.","zh":"建築地盤需要嚴格健康及安全標準來保護工人。"},{"en":"Higher standards reduce accidents and improve working conditions.","zh":"較高標準可減少意外並改善工作環境。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in workplace and legal contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於職場和法律語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"higher than they used to be","meaning":"比以往高得多","examples":[{"en":"Safety standards are much higher than they used to be.","zh":"安全標準比以往高得多。"},{"en":"Higher than they used to be means greater or better now than in the past.","zh":"higher than they used to be 是指現在比過去更高或更好。"},{"en":"Food hygiene standards are higher than they used to be in many restaurants.","zh":"許多餐廳的食品衛生標準比以往高。"},{"en":"Improvements over time can make work safer and more professional.","zh":"隨時間改善可以令工作更安全和更專業。"},{"en":"This phrase compares now with earlier conditions.","zh":"這個短語把現在與以往情況作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"work-related accidents","meaning":"工傷意外","examples":[{"en":"There are fewer work-related accidents now.","zh":"現在工傷意外較少。"},{"en":"Work-related accidents are injuries or incidents that happen because of someone’s job.","zh":"work-related accidents 是因工作而發生的受傷或事故。"},{"en":"A fall from a ladder during work is a work-related accident.","zh":"工作期間從梯子跌下就是工傷意外。"},{"en":"Training and safety equipment can reduce work-related accidents.","zh":"培訓和安全裝備可以減少工傷意外。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing workplace safety.","zh":"這個短語用於討論職場安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lively city environment","meaning":"熱鬧的城市環境","examples":[{"en":"These jobs may not suit people who prefer a lively city environment.","zh":"這些工作可能不適合喜歡熱鬧城市環境的人。"},{"en":"A lively city environment is a busy urban place with shops, transport, people, and entertainment.","zh":"lively city environment 是有商店、交通、人群和娛樂的繁忙城市地方。"},{"en":"Some young workers prefer a lively city environment because there is always something to do.","zh":"有些年輕員工喜歡熱鬧的城市環境，因為總有事情可做。"},{"en":"Rural jobs may feel too quiet for people who enjoy city energy.","zh":"對喜歡城市活力的人來說，鄉郊工作可能太安靜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an active urban setting.","zh":"這個短語描述活躍的城市環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not for you","meaning":"不適合你","examples":[{"en":"Outdoor rural jobs are probably not for people who love city life.","zh":"戶外鄉郊工作可能不適合熱愛城市生活的人。"},{"en":"Not for you means not suitable for you or not something you would enjoy.","zh":"not for you 是指不適合你，或不是你會喜歡的東西。"},{"en":"If you hate early mornings, bakery work may not be for you.","zh":"如果你討厭早起，麵包店工作可能不適合你。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people decide whether an option fits their preferences.","zh":"這個短語幫助人們判斷選項是否符合偏好。"},{"en":"It is informal and direct.","zh":"它較口語而直接。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"remote areas","meaning":"偏遠地區","examples":[{"en":"These jobs are often in pretty remote areas.","zh":"這些工作通常位於相當偏遠地區。"},{"en":"Remote areas are places far from towns, services, or transport links.","zh":"remote areas 是遠離城鎮、服務或交通連接的地方。"},{"en":"A farm in a remote area may be beautiful but difficult to reach without a car.","zh":"偏遠地區的農場可能很美，但沒有車就難以到達。"},{"en":"Working in remote areas can affect housing, shopping, and social life.","zh":"在偏遠地區工作可能影響住宿、購物和社交生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distance and isolation.","zh":"這個短語描述距離和孤立。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"suitable place to live","meaning":"合適住所","examples":[{"en":"Some people worry about finding a suitable place to live.","zh":"有些人擔心找不到合適住所。"},{"en":"A suitable place to live is accommodation that meets someone’s needs, budget, and location.","zh":"suitable place to live 是符合某人需要、預算和地點要求的住處。"},{"en":"A worker may need a suitable place to live near the farm.","zh":"員工可能需要農場附近的合適住所。"},{"en":"Housing matters because long travel can make a job harder.","zh":"住宿很重要，因為長途通勤會令工作更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical accommodation.","zh":"這個短語著重實際住宿安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in our experience","meaning":"根據我們的經驗","examples":[{"en":"In the company’s experience, accommodation usually turns out fine.","zh":"根據公司的經驗，住宿情況通常結果沒問題。"},{"en":"In our experience means based on what we have seen or dealt with before.","zh":"in our experience 是指根據我們以前見過或處理過的情況。"},{"en":"In our experience, new staff settle in faster when housing is arranged early.","zh":"根據我們的經驗，住宿早安排好，新員工會更快適應。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an opinion based on past cases.","zh":"這個短語提供基於過往個案的意見。"},{"en":"It is common in professional advice.","zh":"它常見於專業建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"turn out fine","meaning":"結果通常沒問題","examples":[{"en":"The housing situation usually turns out fine.","zh":"住宿情況通常結果沒問題。"},{"en":"To turn out fine means to end well or become satisfactory after some worry.","zh":"turn out fine 是指在擔心之後結果良好或令人滿意。"},{"en":"A student may worry about a presentation, but it can turn out fine with practice.","zh":"學生可能擔心匯報，但經過練習後結果可以沒問題。"},{"en":"Things turn out fine when problems are solved before they become serious.","zh":"當問題在變嚴重前得到解決，事情通常會結果不錯。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures people about a possible concern.","zh":"這個短語安撫人們對可能問題的憂慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on our books","meaning":"在我們名冊上；現有職位中","examples":[{"en":"The company has several exciting jobs on its books.","zh":"公司現有職位中有幾個令人期待的工作。"},{"en":"On our books means listed or recorded with the agency as available.","zh":"on our books 是指在中介名冊上登記為可申請或可提供。"},{"en":"A recruitment agency may have fifty teaching jobs on its books.","zh":"招聘中介名冊上可能有50個教學職位。"},{"en":"Jobs on the books are roles the agency can discuss with candidates.","zh":"名冊上的工作是中介可以與候選人討論的職位。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in recruitment and business records.","zh":"這個短語常見於招聘和商業紀錄。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fresh food commercial manager","meaning":"新鮮食品商務經理","examples":[{"en":"One available role is for a fresh food commercial manager.","zh":"其中一個可申請職位是新鮮食品商務經理。"},{"en":"A fresh food commercial manager manages business activity connected with fresh food sales and supply.","zh":"fresh food commercial manager 是管理與新鮮食品銷售和供應相關商務活動的人。"},{"en":"This role may involve prices, supermarket relationships, and product planning.","zh":"這個職位可能涉及價格、超市關係和產品規劃。"},{"en":"Fresh food managers must work quickly because products have short shelf lives.","zh":"新鮮食品經理必須快速工作，因為產品保質期短。"},{"en":"This phrase names a business role in the fresh food industry.","zh":"這個短語指新鮮食品行業中的商務職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fresh food producer","meaning":"新鮮食品生產商","examples":[{"en":"The client is a very large fresh food producer.","zh":"客戶是一間非常大型的新鮮食品生產商。"},{"en":"A fresh food producer is a company or farm that grows, prepares, or supplies fresh food.","zh":"fresh food producer 是種植、處理或供應新鮮食品的公司或農場。"},{"en":"A fresh food producer may supply vegetables, fruit, salads, or dairy products.","zh":"新鮮食品生產商可能供應蔬菜、水果、沙律或乳製品。"},{"en":"Fresh food producers need strong logistics because food can spoil quickly.","zh":"新鮮食品生產商需要強大物流，因為食物可能很快變壞。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a business that provides fresh food products.","zh":"這個短語指提供新鮮食品產品的企業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"supply a range of","meaning":"供應一系列……","examples":[{"en":"The producer supplies a range of top supermarkets.","zh":"這間生產商供應一系列頂級超市。"},{"en":"To supply a range of places or products means to provide several different ones.","zh":"supply a range of places or products 是指提供多個不同地點或產品。"},{"en":"A farm may supply a range of restaurants with fresh herbs.","zh":"農場可能向一系列餐廳供應新鮮香草。"},{"en":"Supplying a range of customers can make a business more stable.","zh":"供應多種客戶可以令業務更穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase shows variety in what or whom a company supplies.","zh":"這個短語顯示公司供應對象或產品的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"top supermarkets","meaning":"頂級超市","examples":[{"en":"The client supplies fresh food to top supermarkets.","zh":"客戶向頂級超市供應新鮮食品。"},{"en":"Top supermarkets are leading or high-profile supermarket chains.","zh":"top supermarkets 是主要或知名的連鎖超市。"},{"en":"Top supermarkets expect reliable supply, good quality, and safe products.","zh":"頂級超市期望可靠供應、高質素和安全產品。"},{"en":"Supplying major supermarkets can increase pressure because standards are high.","zh":"供應大型超市可能增加壓力，因為標準很高。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to important retailers in the food market.","zh":"這個短語指食品市場中的重要零售商。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"operate in","meaning":"在……中運作","examples":[{"en":"The company operates in a fast-paced environment.","zh":"這間公司在節奏急速的環境中運作。"},{"en":"To operate in an environment means to work or function within that setting.","zh":"operate in an environment 是指在某種環境中工作或運作。"},{"en":"Hospitals operate in a busy environment where decisions must be made quickly.","zh":"醫院在繁忙環境中運作，必須快速作決定。"},{"en":"The environment a company operates in affects how staff work.","zh":"公司運作的環境會影響員工如何工作。"},{"en":"This phrase links a business with its working conditions.","zh":"這個短語把企業與其工作條件連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fast-paced environment","meaning":"節奏急速的環境","examples":[{"en":"The fresh food producer operates in a fast-paced environment.","zh":"這間新鮮食品生產商在節奏急速的環境中運作。"},{"en":"A fast-paced environment is a workplace where things happen quickly and decisions must be made fast.","zh":"fast-paced environment 是事情快速發生、必須快速決策的工作環境。"},{"en":"Newsrooms and busy kitchens are often fast-paced environments.","zh":"新聞編輯室和繁忙廚房通常是節奏急速的環境。"},{"en":"Fresh food work is fast-paced because products must reach shops quickly.","zh":"新鮮食品工作節奏急速，因為產品必須快速送到商店。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests energy, speed, and pressure.","zh":"這個短語暗示活力、速度和壓力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"low profit margins","meaning":"低利潤率","examples":[{"en":"The business has low profit margins.","zh":"這門生意利潤率低。"},{"en":"Low profit margins mean the company earns only a small profit from each sale.","zh":"low profit margins 是指公司每次銷售只賺取少量利潤。"},{"en":"Supermarkets often operate with low profit margins on basic food items.","zh":"超市在基本食品上通常以低利潤率運作。"},{"en":"Low margins can make cost control and efficiency very important.","zh":"低利潤率會令成本控制和效率非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business and finance.","zh":"這個短語常見於商業和財務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"work hard, play hard","meaning":"努力工作，也盡情玩樂","examples":[{"en":"The staff work hard, but they play hard as well.","zh":"員工努力工作，但也盡情玩樂。"},{"en":"Work hard, play hard means people put strong effort into work and also enjoy social life or relaxation fully.","zh":"work hard, play hard 是指人們工作非常努力，也充分享受社交或休閒生活。"},{"en":"A busy sales team may work hard, play hard after meeting targets.","zh":"忙碌銷售團隊達標後，可能努力工作也盡情玩樂。"},{"en":"This culture can be exciting, but it may not suit everyone.","zh":"這種文化可以令人興奮，但未必適合所有人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both effort and social energy.","zh":"這個短語同時描述努力和社交活力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sociable personality","meaning":"外向合群的性格","examples":[{"en":"This role may suit someone with a sociable personality.","zh":"這個職位可能適合有外向合群性格的人。"},{"en":"A sociable personality means a person enjoys talking to and working with other people.","zh":"sociable personality 是指一個人喜歡與他人交談和合作。"},{"en":"A customer service job suits someone with a sociable personality.","zh":"客戶服務工作適合有外向合群性格的人。"},{"en":"Sociable people often build relationships more easily in sales or team roles.","zh":"外向合群的人通常在銷售或團隊職位中較容易建立關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a personal quality useful in people-focused work.","zh":"這個短語描述在人際工作中有用的個人特質。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"exciting post","meaning":"令人期待的職位","examples":[{"en":"The company has an exciting post as an agronomist.","zh":"公司有一個令人期待的農藝師職位。"},{"en":"An exciting post is a job that seems interesting, challenging, or full of opportunity.","zh":"exciting post 是看起來有趣、有挑戰或充滿機會的職位。"},{"en":"A new role in a growing company may be an exciting post for a young graduate.","zh":"成長中公司的新職位對年輕畢業生來說可能令人期待。"},{"en":"Jobs feel exciting when they offer learning, responsibility, or career progress.","zh":"當工作提供學習、責任或事業進展，它會令人期待。"},{"en":"This phrase is recruitment language used to attract applicants.","zh":"這個短語是用來吸引申請者的招聘用語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"agronomist","meaning":"農藝師","examples":[{"en":"An agronomist advises farmers on crop and farming issues.","zh":"農藝師就作物和耕作問題向農夫提供建議。"},{"en":"An agronomist is a specialist who studies crops, soil, and farming methods.","zh":"agronomist 是研究作物、土壤和耕作方法的專家。"},{"en":"An agronomist may help farmers choose fertilisers or manage pests.","zh":"農藝師可能幫助農夫選擇肥料或管理害蟲。"},{"en":"Good agronomic advice can improve crop yield and reduce waste.","zh":"良好農藝建議可以提高作物產量並減少浪費。"},{"en":"This word refers to a professional role in agriculture.","zh":"這個詞指農業中的專業角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"advise someone on","meaning":"就……向某人提供建議","examples":[{"en":"The agronomist advises farmers on crop nutrition and pests.","zh":"農藝師就作物營養和害蟲問題向農夫提供建議。"},{"en":"To advise someone on something means to give them expert guidance about it.","zh":"advise someone on something 是指就某事給某人專業指導。"},{"en":"A career adviser may advise students on university choices.","zh":"升學顧問可能就大學選擇向學生提供建議。"},{"en":"Advice is useful when decisions require specialist knowledge.","zh":"當決定需要專門知識時，建議很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase links the adviser, the person receiving advice, and the topic.","zh":"這個短語連接顧問、接受建議的人和主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"crop nutrition","meaning":"作物營養","examples":[{"en":"The agronomist advises farmers on crop nutrition.","zh":"農藝師就作物營養向農夫提供建議。"},{"en":"Crop nutrition means the nutrients crops need to grow well.","zh":"crop nutrition 是作物良好生長所需的營養。"},{"en":"Farmers manage crop nutrition by using fertilisers, compost, or soil testing.","zh":"農夫透過使用肥料、堆肥或土壤測試來管理作物營養。"},{"en":"Poor crop nutrition can reduce yield and plant health.","zh":"作物營養不足可以降低產量和植物健康。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the feeding needs of plants.","zh":"這個短語指植物的營養需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"protection against pests","meaning":"防治蟲害","examples":[{"en":"The agronomist advises on protection against pests.","zh":"農藝師就防治蟲害提供建議。"},{"en":"Protection against pests means methods used to stop insects or other harmful organisms damaging crops.","zh":"protection against pests 是防止昆蟲或其他有害生物破壞作物的方法。"},{"en":"Farmers may use nets, natural predators, or safe sprays for protection against pests.","zh":"農夫可能使用網、天敵或安全噴劑來防治蟲害。"},{"en":"Pest protection is important because insects can destroy harvests quickly.","zh":"防治蟲害很重要，因為昆蟲可以很快破壞收成。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on preventing crop damage.","zh":"這個短語著重防止作物受損。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"latest legislation","meaning":"最新法例","examples":[{"en":"The agronomist must understand the latest legislation on farming.","zh":"農藝師必須了解最新農業法例。"},{"en":"Latest legislation means the newest laws or legal rules about a topic.","zh":"latest legislation 是關於某主題的最新法律或法規。"},{"en":"Employers must follow the latest legislation on workplace safety.","zh":"僱主必須遵守最新職場安全法例。"},{"en":"Knowing current law helps professionals avoid illegal or unsafe advice.","zh":"了解現行法律有助專業人士避免提供違法或不安全建議。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in regulated industries.","zh":"這個短語常見於受規管行業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"agricultural practices","meaning":"農業實務","examples":[{"en":"The job involves knowledge of farming and agricultural practices.","zh":"這份工作涉及耕作和農業實務知識。"},{"en":"Agricultural practices are the methods farmers use to grow crops and manage land or animals.","zh":"agricultural practices 是農夫用來種植作物和管理土地或動物的方法。"},{"en":"Crop rotation and careful irrigation are agricultural practices.","zh":"輪作和小心灌溉都是農業實務。"},{"en":"Good practices can improve production while protecting soil and water.","zh":"良好實務可以提高產量，同時保護土壤和水源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical farming methods.","zh":"這個短語指實際耕作方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make one’s way up","meaning":"向上晉升","examples":[{"en":"The right person can quickly make their way up the career ladder.","zh":"合適的人可以很快在事業階梯上向上晉升。"},{"en":"To make one’s way up means to gradually move to higher or better positions.","zh":"make one’s way up 是指逐漸升到更高或更好的職位。"},{"en":"A junior assistant can make her way up by learning quickly and taking responsibility.","zh":"初級助理可以透過快速學習和承擔責任向上晉升。"},{"en":"Career progress often requires skill, effort, and good opportunities.","zh":"事業進展通常需要技能、努力和好機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upward career movement.","zh":"這個短語描述事業上的向上移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"career ladder","meaning":"事業階梯","examples":[{"en":"The role offers a chance to move up the career ladder.","zh":"這個職位提供在事業階梯上向上發展的機會。"},{"en":"The career ladder is the series of higher positions someone can move through in a career.","zh":"career ladder 是某人在事業中可以逐步晉升的一系列較高職位。"},{"en":"A trainee may start low on the career ladder and become a manager later.","zh":"見習員可能從事業階梯較低位置開始，之後成為經理。"},{"en":"Clear career ladders help employees see how they can progress.","zh":"清晰事業階梯幫助員工看見如何進步。"},{"en":"This phrase imagines career growth as climbing upward.","zh":"這個短語把事業成長想像成向上攀登。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"deep knowledge of","meaning":"對……有深入認識","examples":[{"en":"Applicants are expected to have deep knowledge of the agricultural sector.","zh":"申請者應對農業界別有深入認識。"},{"en":"Deep knowledge of something means strong and detailed understanding of it.","zh":"deep knowledge of something 是指對某事有強而詳細的理解。"},{"en":"A doctor needs deep knowledge of the human body.","zh":"醫生需要對人體有深入認識。"},{"en":"Deep knowledge helps professionals make better decisions and solve complex problems.","zh":"深入認識幫助專業人士作出更好決定並解決複雜問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests more than basic familiarity.","zh":"這個短語表示不只是基本熟悉。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"agricultural sector","meaning":"農業界別","examples":[{"en":"Applicants need deep knowledge of the agricultural sector.","zh":"申請者需要對農業界別有深入認識。"},{"en":"The agricultural sector is the part of the economy connected with farming and food production.","zh":"agricultural sector 是經濟中與耕作和食品生產相關的部分。"},{"en":"The agricultural sector includes farms, suppliers, advisers, and food producers.","zh":"農業界別包括農場、供應商、顧問和食品生產商。"},{"en":"Changes in weather, law, and markets can strongly affect the agricultural sector.","zh":"天氣、法律和市場變化都可以強烈影響農業界別。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to agriculture as an industry.","zh":"這個短語指作為行業的農業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be expected of","meaning":"對……有所要求","examples":[{"en":"Deep knowledge is expected of applicants for the agronomist role.","zh":"農藝師職位對申請者有深入知識要求。"},{"en":"To be expected of someone means to be required or considered necessary for that person.","zh":"be expected of someone 是指某人被要求具備某事，或某事被視為必要。"},{"en":"Good communication is expected of teachers.","zh":"教師被期望具備良好溝通能力。"},{"en":"Expectations help applicants understand the standard they must meet.","zh":"要求幫助申請者了解必須達到的標準。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in job descriptions.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於職位描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"applicants","meaning":"申請者","examples":[{"en":"Applicants need strong knowledge of the sector.","zh":"申請者需要對該界別有扎實知識。"},{"en":"Applicants are people who apply for a job, course, or opportunity.","zh":"applicants 是申請工作、課程或機會的人。"},{"en":"Applicants for a teaching job may need references and qualifications.","zh":"教學職位的申請者可能需要推薦信和資格。"},{"en":"Employers compare applicants to decide who best fits the role.","zh":"僱主會比較申請者，以決定誰最適合職位。"},{"en":"This word is common in recruitment and admissions.","zh":"這個詞常見於招聘和招生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"leading supermarket","meaning":"主要超市","examples":[{"en":"A leading supermarket is looking for a fresh produce buyer.","zh":"一間主要超市正在尋找新鮮農產品採購員。"},{"en":"A leading supermarket is a major and successful supermarket company.","zh":"leading supermarket 是大型而成功的超市公司。"},{"en":"A leading supermarket may have many branches and high customer demand.","zh":"主要超市可能有很多分店和高顧客需求。"},{"en":"Working for a leading supermarket can bring pressure because standards are high.","zh":"為主要超市工作可能帶來壓力，因為標準很高。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the company is important in its market.","zh":"這個短語表示該公司在市場中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fresh produce buyer","meaning":"新鮮農產品採購員","examples":[{"en":"The supermarket needs a fresh produce buyer.","zh":"超市需要一名新鮮農產品採購員。"},{"en":"A fresh produce buyer buys fruit, vegetables, and other fresh foods for a retailer.","zh":"fresh produce buyer 是為零售商採購水果、蔬菜和其他新鮮食品的人。"},{"en":"A buyer must choose suppliers, compare prices, and check quality.","zh":"採購員必須選擇供應商、比較價格和檢查質素。"},{"en":"Fresh produce buyers work quickly because fresh food has a short life.","zh":"新鮮農產品採購員工作要快，因為新鮮食品保質期短。"},{"en":"This phrase names a purchasing role in food retail.","zh":"這個短語指食品零售中的採購職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be available for","meaning":"可接受……","examples":[{"en":"The buyer must be available for a 12-month contract.","zh":"採購員必須可接受12個月合約。"},{"en":"To be available for something means to be free and willing to do it during that period.","zh":"be available for something 是指在該段時間有空並願意做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may need to be available for a summer programme in July.","zh":"老師可能需要在七月有空參與暑期課程。"},{"en":"Employers ask about availability to check whether candidates can meet the job schedule.","zh":"僱主詢問可用時間，是為了確認候選人能否配合工作安排。"},{"en":"This phrase links a person’s time with a role or commitment.","zh":"這個短語把個人時間與職位或承諾連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"maternity cover contract","meaning":"產假替工合約","examples":[{"en":"The role is a 12-month maternity cover contract.","zh":"這個職位是12個月產假替工合約。"},{"en":"A maternity cover contract is a temporary job replacing someone who is away on maternity leave.","zh":"maternity cover contract 是暫時頂替放產假員工的合約工作。"},{"en":"A school may hire a teacher on a maternity cover contract for one term.","zh":"學校可能聘請一名教師做一學期產假替工。"},{"en":"These contracts have fixed periods because the original employee is expected to return.","zh":"這些合約有固定期限，因為原本員工預計會回來。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in job advertisements.","zh":"這個短語常見於招聘廣告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"experience in administration","meaning":"行政經驗","examples":[{"en":"The applicant needs experience in administration.","zh":"申請者需要行政經驗。"},{"en":"Experience in administration means past work handling office tasks, records, emails, or organisation.","zh":"experience in administration 是處理辦公室任務、紀錄、電郵或組織工作的過往經驗。"},{"en":"A receptionist often gains experience in administration by managing bookings and documents.","zh":"接待員常透過管理預約和文件累積行政經驗。"},{"en":"Administrative experience helps workers keep systems accurate and organised.","zh":"行政經驗幫助員工保持系統準確和有條理。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical office management skills.","zh":"這個短語指實際辦公室管理技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"planning and buying","meaning":"規劃及採購","examples":[{"en":"The role requires experience in planning and buying.","zh":"這個職位需要規劃及採購經驗。"},{"en":"Planning and buying means organising future needs and purchasing products or supplies.","zh":"planning and buying 是安排未來需要並購買產品或物資。"},{"en":"A supermarket buyer needs planning and buying skills to keep shelves stocked.","zh":"超市採購員需要規劃及採購技能，以保持貨架有貨。"},{"en":"Poor planning and buying can lead to waste, shortages, or high costs.","zh":"規劃及採購不佳可能導致浪費、缺貨或高成本。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in retail and supply roles.","zh":"這個短語常見於零售和供應職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fresh produce industry","meaning":"新鮮農產品行業","examples":[{"en":"The applicant needs experience in the fresh produce industry.","zh":"申請者需要新鮮農產品行業經驗。"},{"en":"The fresh produce industry includes businesses that grow, buy, sell, and distribute fresh fruit and vegetables.","zh":"fresh produce industry 包括種植、採購、銷售和分銷新鮮水果及蔬菜的企業。"},{"en":"Workers in the fresh produce industry must understand quality, freshness, and delivery speed.","zh":"新鮮農產品行業的員工必須了解質素、新鮮度和送貨速度。"},{"en":"Experience in this industry helps buyers make better purchasing decisions.","zh":"這個行業的經驗幫助採購員作出更好採購決定。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific food sector.","zh":"這個短語指特定食品界別。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in return","meaning":"作為回報","examples":[{"en":"In return, the buyer will receive a competitive salary.","zh":"作為回報，採購員會獲得具競爭力的薪酬。"},{"en":"In return means as a reward or exchange for work, effort, or help.","zh":"in return 是指作為工作、努力或幫助的回報或交換。"},{"en":"Volunteers give their time, and in return they gain experience and friendship.","zh":"義工付出時間，作為回報，他們獲得經驗和友誼。"},{"en":"Job adverts use “in return” before describing pay or benefits.","zh":"招聘廣告會在描述薪酬或福利前使用 in return。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what someone gets back.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人得到甚麼回報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"competitive salary","meaning":"具競爭力的薪酬","examples":[{"en":"The fresh produce buyer will receive a competitive salary.","zh":"新鮮農產品採購員會獲得具競爭力的薪酬。"},{"en":"A competitive salary is pay that is attractive compared with similar jobs.","zh":"competitive salary 是與類似工作相比具吸引力的薪酬。"},{"en":"A company may offer a competitive salary to attract skilled workers.","zh":"公司可能提供具競爭力的薪酬來吸引熟練員工。"},{"en":"Good pay can make a demanding job more appealing.","zh":"良好薪酬可以令要求高的工作更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in recruitment advertisements.","zh":"這個短語常見於招聘廣告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"receive a request for","meaning":"收到……的要求","examples":[{"en":"The agency has received a request for a sales manager.","zh":"中介收到招聘銷售經理的要求。"},{"en":"To receive a request for something means to get an official or direct demand for it.","zh":"receive a request for something 是指收到對某事的正式或直接要求。"},{"en":"A school may receive a request for extra support from a parent.","zh":"學校可能收到家長要求額外支援。"},{"en":"Recruitment agencies act when clients request particular workers.","zh":"當客戶要求特定員工時，招聘中介便會行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a need being communicated.","zh":"這個短語描述某項需要被傳達。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sales manager","meaning":"銷售經理","examples":[{"en":"A chain of garden centres needs a sales manager.","zh":"一間連鎖園藝中心需要銷售經理。"},{"en":"A sales manager leads sales staff and helps a business increase sales.","zh":"sales manager 是帶領銷售員工並幫助企業增加銷售的人。"},{"en":"A sales manager may train staff, set targets, and check customer service.","zh":"銷售經理可能培訓員工、設定目標和檢查客戶服務。"},{"en":"Strong sales management can improve income and customer satisfaction.","zh":"強大的銷售管理可以改善收入和顧客滿意度。"},{"en":"This phrase names a business leadership role.","zh":"這個短語指商業領導職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"chain of garden centres","meaning":"連鎖園藝中心","examples":[{"en":"The sales manager will work for a chain of garden centres.","zh":"銷售經理會為一間連鎖園藝中心工作。"},{"en":"A chain of garden centres is a group of garden shops under the same company.","zh":"chain of garden centres 是同一公司旗下的一組園藝店。"},{"en":"A garden centre chain may sell plants, tools, soil, pots, and outdoor furniture.","zh":"連鎖園藝中心可能售賣植物、工具、泥土、花盆和戶外家具。"},{"en":"Managing a chain can be complex because several sites must keep the same standards.","zh":"管理連鎖店可能複雜，因為多個地點都要保持相同標準。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a multi-branch business.","zh":"這個短語描述多分店企業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"visit centres in the region","meaning":"走訪區內各中心","examples":[{"en":"The sales manager will visit centres in the region.","zh":"銷售經理會走訪區內各中心。"},{"en":"To visit centres in the region means to travel to different branches within that area.","zh":"visit centres in the region 是指前往該區內不同分店或中心。"},{"en":"A regional manager may visit stores in the region every month.","zh":"區域經理可能每月走訪區內商店。"},{"en":"Visiting sites helps managers check standards and support staff.","zh":"走訪各地點幫助經理檢查標準和支援員工。"},{"en":"This phrase describes travel within a work area.","zh":"這個短語描述工作範圍內的出行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ensure that","meaning":"確保……","examples":[{"en":"The sales manager ensures that high levels of customer service are maintained.","zh":"銷售經理確保高水平客戶服務得以維持。"},{"en":"To ensure that something happens means to make certain it happens.","zh":"ensure that something happens 是指確保某事發生。"},{"en":"Teachers check attendance to ensure that all students are safe.","zh":"老師點名以確保所有學生安全。"},{"en":"Managers create systems to ensure standards stay consistent.","zh":"經理建立系統以確保標準保持一致。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used for responsibilities.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於職責描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"high levels of customer service","meaning":"高水平客戶服務","examples":[{"en":"The company wants to maintain high levels of customer service.","zh":"公司希望維持高水平客戶服務。"},{"en":"High levels of customer service mean very good support, politeness, and help for customers.","zh":"high levels of customer service 是指為顧客提供非常好的支援、禮貌和幫助。"},{"en":"Shops with high customer service levels answer questions quickly and solve problems politely.","zh":"客戶服務水平高的商店會快速回答問題並有禮解決問題。"},{"en":"Good service can make customers return and recommend the business.","zh":"良好服務可以令顧客再次光顧並推薦企業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong service standards.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的服務標準。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be maintained","meaning":"得以維持","examples":[{"en":"The sales manager ensures that customer service standards are maintained.","zh":"銷售經理確保客戶服務標準得以維持。"},{"en":"To be maintained means to be kept at the same good level.","zh":"be maintained 是指保持在同樣良好水平。"},{"en":"School equipment must be maintained so it stays safe to use.","zh":"學校設備必須得到維護，才可保持安全使用。"},{"en":"Standards can fall if they are not checked and maintained regularly.","zh":"如果不定期檢查和維持，標準可能下降。"},{"en":"This passive phrase focuses on keeping quality steady.","zh":"這個被動短語著重保持質素穩定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be prepared to","meaning":"願意……","examples":[{"en":"The post is suitable for someone who is prepared to live in the region.","zh":"這個職位適合願意住在該區的人。"},{"en":"To be prepared to do something means to be willing and ready to do it.","zh":"be prepared to do something 是指願意並準備好做某事。"},{"en":"A worker may be prepared to relocate if the job offers good prospects.","zh":"如果工作前景好，員工可能願意搬遷。"},{"en":"Employers mention this when a role requires flexibility or commitment.","zh":"當職位需要彈性或承諾，僱主會提到這一點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes willingness.","zh":"這個短語描述意願。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"live in the region","meaning":"住在該區","examples":[{"en":"The sales manager must be prepared to live in the region.","zh":"銷售經理必須願意住在該區。"},{"en":"To live in the region means to have your home in that particular area.","zh":"live in the region 是指住在該特定地區。"},{"en":"A rural job may require workers to live in the region because travel is difficult.","zh":"鄉郊工作可能要求員工住在該區，因為交通困難。"},{"en":"Living near the work area helps staff visit sites and respond quickly.","zh":"住在工作區附近有助員工走訪地點並快速回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a location requirement.","zh":"這個短語描述地點要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"vacancy for","meaning":"……的空缺","examples":[{"en":"There is also a vacancy for a tree technician.","zh":"另外還有一個樹木技術員的空缺。"},{"en":"A vacancy for a job means an available job position that needs to be filled.","zh":"vacancy for a job 是指需要招聘的可用職位。"},{"en":"A school may have a vacancy for a science teacher.","zh":"學校可能有科學老師空缺。"},{"en":"Vacancies appear when a company grows or someone leaves a role.","zh":"當公司擴張或有人離職，空缺便會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in job advertisements.","zh":"這個短語常見於招聘廣告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tree technician","meaning":"樹木技術員","examples":[{"en":"A tree technician carries out tree cutting and conservation work.","zh":"樹木技術員進行樹木修剪和保育工作。"},{"en":"A tree technician is a trained worker who cares for, cuts, inspects, or manages trees.","zh":"tree technician 是受訓照顧、修剪、檢查或管理樹木的工人。"},{"en":"Tree technicians may work in parks, gardens, forests, or roadside areas.","zh":"樹木技術員可能在公園、花園、森林或路邊工作。"},{"en":"Their work protects trees, people, buildings, and public spaces.","zh":"他們的工作保護樹木、人、建築物和公共空間。"},{"en":"This phrase names a skilled outdoor job.","zh":"這個短語指一種有技能的戶外工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"carry out","meaning":"執行；進行","examples":[{"en":"The tree technician carries out tree cutting and forestry work.","zh":"樹木技術員執行樹木修剪和林業工作。"},{"en":"To carry out work means to perform or complete it.","zh":"carry out work 是指進行或完成工作。"},{"en":"Engineers carry out safety checks before opening a bridge.","zh":"工程師在橋樑開放前進行安全檢查。"},{"en":"Carrying out tasks properly helps prevent accidents and poor results.","zh":"正確執行任務有助防止意外和不良結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in formal job descriptions.","zh":"這個短語常見於正式職位描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"tree cutting","meaning":"樹木修剪","examples":[{"en":"The vacancy involves tree cutting and forestry work.","zh":"這個空缺涉及樹木修剪和林業工作。"},{"en":"Tree cutting means trimming, pruning, or removing parts of trees.","zh":"tree cutting 是指修剪、剪枝或移除樹木部分。"},{"en":"Councils may arrange tree cutting if branches block roads or power lines.","zh":"如果樹枝阻塞道路或電線，市政部門可能安排樹木修剪。"},{"en":"Tree cutting must be done safely because falling branches can injure people.","zh":"樹木修剪必須安全進行，因為掉落樹枝可能傷人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical tree management.","zh":"這個短語指實際樹木管理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"forestry","meaning":"林業","examples":[{"en":"The role includes forestry and conservation work.","zh":"這個職位包括林業和保育工作。"},{"en":"Forestry is the management, planting, protection, and use of forests and trees.","zh":"forestry 是對森林和樹木的管理、種植、保護和使用。"},{"en":"Forestry workers may plant trees, manage woodland, and check tree health.","zh":"林業工人可能種樹、管理林地和檢查樹木健康。"},{"en":"Good forestry balances human needs with environmental protection.","zh":"良好林業會平衡人類需要與環境保護。"},{"en":"This word refers to work connected with forests.","zh":"這個詞指與森林相關的工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"conservation work","meaning":"保育工作","examples":[{"en":"The tree technician will carry out conservation work.","zh":"樹木技術員會進行保育工作。"},{"en":"Conservation work means work that protects nature, wildlife, habitats, or resources.","zh":"conservation work 是保護自然、野生動物、棲息地或資源的工作。"},{"en":"Volunteers may do conservation work by clearing litter from wetlands.","zh":"義工可能透過清理濕地垃圾進行保育工作。"},{"en":"Conservation work helps prevent environmental damage and preserve biodiversity.","zh":"保育工作幫助防止環境破壞並保存生物多樣性。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on protecting the natural environment.","zh":"這個短語著重保護自然環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"clean driving licence","meaning":"無違規紀錄的駕駛執照","examples":[{"en":"Candidates must have a clean driving licence.","zh":"候選人必須有無違規紀錄的駕駛執照。"},{"en":"A clean driving licence is a driving licence with no serious offences or penalty points.","zh":"clean driving licence 是沒有嚴重違規或扣分紀錄的駕駛執照。"},{"en":"Employers may require a clean driving licence for jobs involving company vehicles.","zh":"涉及公司車輛的工作可能要求無違規紀錄的駕駛執照。"},{"en":"A clean licence suggests the driver has followed road rules safely.","zh":"乾淨駕照表示司機一直安全遵守道路規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in job requirements for driving roles.","zh":"這個短語常見於需要駕駛的職位要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"training in safety procedures","meaning":"安全程序培訓","examples":[{"en":"Candidates must have training in safety procedures.","zh":"候選人必須接受過安全程序培訓。"},{"en":"Training in safety procedures means learning the correct steps for working safely.","zh":"training in safety procedures 是學習安全工作的正確步驟。"},{"en":"Tree workers need safety training before using chainsaws or climbing equipment.","zh":"樹木工人在使用電鋸或攀爬設備前需要安全培訓。"},{"en":"Safety training reduces accidents and helps workers respond to danger.","zh":"安全培訓可以減少意外，並幫助工人應對危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes required preparation for risky work.","zh":"這個短語描述高風險工作所需準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"would be preferred","meaning":"會較優先考慮","examples":[{"en":"A year’s experience would be preferred.","zh":"有一年經驗會較優先考慮。"},{"en":"Would be preferred means something is not always essential, but it would make an applicant more suitable.","zh":"would be preferred 是指某條件不一定必須，但會令申請者更合適。"},{"en":"Experience with children would be preferred for a summer camp job.","zh":"暑期營工作會較優先考慮有兒童工作經驗的人。"},{"en":"Preferred requirements help employers choose between similar candidates.","zh":"優先條件幫助僱主在相似候選人之間作選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in job adverts.","zh":"這個短語常見於招聘廣告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be prepared to consider","meaning":"願意考慮","examples":[{"en":"The company might be prepared to consider a recently trained candidate.","zh":"公司可能願意考慮最近受訓的候選人。"},{"en":"To be prepared to consider someone means to be willing to think about accepting them.","zh":"be prepared to consider someone 是指願意考慮接受某人。"},{"en":"An employer may be prepared to consider graduates if they show strong motivation.","zh":"如果畢業生表現出強烈動機，僱主可能願意考慮他們。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests flexibility rather than a strict rule.","zh":"這個短語表示彈性，而不是嚴格規則。"},{"en":"It is useful when a candidate does not meet every ideal requirement.","zh":"當候選人未符合所有理想要求時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"appropriate training course","meaning":"合適的培訓課程","examples":[{"en":"The company may consider someone who has completed an appropriate training course.","zh":"公司可能考慮已完成合適培訓課程的人。"},{"en":"An appropriate training course is a course that matches the skills needed for the job.","zh":"appropriate training course 是符合工作所需技能的課程。"},{"en":"A tree technician may need an appropriate training course in chainsaw safety.","zh":"樹木技術員可能需要關於電鋸安全的合適培訓課程。"},{"en":"Proper training helps employers trust that a new worker can work safely.","zh":"適當培訓幫助僱主相信新員工能安全工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to relevant preparation, not any course at all.","zh":"這個短語指相關準備，而不是任何課程都可以。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"position for","meaning":"……的職位","examples":[{"en":"The agency has a position for a farm worker.","zh":"中介有一個農場工人的職位。"},{"en":"A position for someone means an available job role of that type.","zh":"position for someone 是指某類型工作者的可用職位。"},{"en":"A hotel may have a position for a receptionist.","zh":"酒店可能有一個接待員職位。"},{"en":"Job positions describe what kind of worker an employer needs.","zh":"工作職位描述僱主需要哪類員工。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in recruitment.","zh":"這個短語常見於招聘。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"farm worker","meaning":"農場工人","examples":[{"en":"The farm worker role involves a wide range of duties.","zh":"農場工人職位涉及各式各樣的職責。"},{"en":"A farm worker is someone who does practical work on a farm.","zh":"farm worker 是在農場做實際工作的人。"},{"en":"Farm workers may feed animals, plant crops, repair fences, or drive machinery.","zh":"農場工人可能餵動物、種植作物、修理圍欄或駕駛機器。"},{"en":"The job can be physically demanding because tasks change with seasons and weather.","zh":"這份工作可能體力要求高，因為任務會隨季節和天氣改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a hands-on agricultural role.","zh":"這個短語指實務型農業職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"involve a wide range of","meaning":"涉及各式各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"The farm worker job involves a wide range of farm duties.","zh":"農場工人工作涉及各式各樣的農場職責。"},{"en":"To involve a wide range of things means to include many different types of tasks or areas.","zh":"involve a wide range of things 是指包括許多不同類型的任務或範疇。"},{"en":"A teacher’s job involves a wide range of duties, from planning lessons to speaking with parents.","zh":"老師工作涉及各式各樣的職責，從備課到與家長溝通。"},{"en":"A wide range of tasks can make work varied but demanding.","zh":"多種任務可以令工作多元，但也要求高。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights variety in responsibilities.","zh":"這個短語突出責任的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"farm duties","meaning":"農場職責","examples":[{"en":"The job includes a wide range of farm duties.","zh":"這份工作包括各式各樣的農場職責。"},{"en":"Farm duties are tasks that need to be done on a farm.","zh":"farm duties 是農場上需要完成的任務。"},{"en":"Farm duties may include feeding animals, sowing crops, cleaning sheds, and repairing equipment.","zh":"農場職責可能包括餵動物、播種、清潔棚舍和維修設備。"},{"en":"These duties change with the season, weather, and type of farm.","zh":"這些職責會隨季節、天氣和農場類型而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical farm responsibilities.","zh":"這個短語指實際農場責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"crop sowing","meaning":"播種","examples":[{"en":"The farm worker will be involved in crop sowing.","zh":"農場工人會參與播種。"},{"en":"Crop sowing means planting seeds in the soil so crops can grow.","zh":"crop sowing 是把種子種入泥土，讓作物生長。"},{"en":"Farmers do crop sowing at the right season for each plant.","zh":"農夫會在每種植物合適季節進行播種。"},{"en":"Good sowing affects how evenly crops grow and how strong the harvest is.","zh":"良好播種會影響作物生長是否均勻和收成是否好。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the early stage of crop production.","zh":"這個短語指作物生產的早期階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"harvesting","meaning":"收成；收割","examples":[{"en":"The farm worker will help with harvesting.","zh":"農場工人會幫忙收成。"},{"en":"Harvesting means gathering crops when they are ready.","zh":"harvesting 是在作物成熟時收集它們。"},{"en":"Workers may help with harvesting apples, potatoes, wheat, or vegetables.","zh":"工人可能幫忙收割蘋果、薯仔、小麥或蔬菜。"},{"en":"Harvesting must often happen quickly before weather or spoilage damages crops.","zh":"收割通常必須快速進行，以免天氣或變壞破壞作物。"},{"en":"This word refers to collecting the finished crop.","zh":"這個詞指收集成熟作物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"machine maintenance","meaning":"機器維修保養","examples":[{"en":"The role includes machine maintenance.","zh":"這個職位包括機器維修保養。"},{"en":"Machine maintenance means checking, cleaning, repairing, and keeping machines working properly.","zh":"machine maintenance 是檢查、清潔、維修和保持機器正常運作。"},{"en":"A farm worker may do machine maintenance on tractors or harvesters.","zh":"農場工人可能為拖拉機或收割機做維修保養。"},{"en":"Regular maintenance prevents breakdowns during busy farming periods.","zh":"定期保養可以防止機器在繁忙農季故障。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to care of equipment, not using the machine only.","zh":"這個短語指照顧設備，而不只是使用機器。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"animal care","meaning":"動物照料","examples":[{"en":"The role also involves animal care.","zh":"這個職位也涉及動物照料。"},{"en":"Animal care means looking after animals’ food, health, comfort, and safety.","zh":"animal care 是照顧動物的食物、健康、舒適和安全。"},{"en":"Farm workers may provide animal care by feeding livestock and checking for illness.","zh":"農場工人可能透過餵牲畜和檢查疾病來提供動物照料。"},{"en":"Good animal care improves welfare and farm productivity.","zh":"良好動物照料可以改善動物福祉和農場產量。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in farming, veterinary, and pet-care contexts.","zh":"這個短語用於農業、獸醫和寵物照顧語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"perks of the job","meaning":"工作福利","examples":[{"en":"The perks of the job include the possibility of renting a cottage.","zh":"這份工作的福利包括可能租住一間小屋。"},{"en":"Perks of the job are extra benefits that come with a job, beyond the basic salary.","zh":"perks of the job 是基本薪金以外，工作附帶的額外好處。"},{"en":"Free meals, staff discounts, and housing support can be perks of the job.","zh":"免費膳食、員工折扣和住宿支援都可以是工作福利。"},{"en":"Perks can make a job more attractive even if the work is demanding.","zh":"即使工作要求高，福利也可以令職位更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to additional advantages.","zh":"這個短語指額外好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the possibility of","meaning":"……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"The job includes the possibility of renting a small cottage.","zh":"這份工作包括租住小屋的可能性。"},{"en":"The possibility of something means it may happen or may be available.","zh":"the possibility of something 是指某事可能發生或可能可用。"},{"en":"A course may include the possibility of studying abroad for one term.","zh":"課程可能包括到海外學習一個學期的可能性。"},{"en":"A possibility is not a guarantee, so applicants should check details.","zh":"可能性不是保證，所以申請者應查清細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a potential option.","zh":"這個短語描述潛在選項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"rent a small cottage","meaning":"租一間小屋","examples":[{"en":"The worker may be able to rent a small cottage on the estate.","zh":"工人可能可以在莊園範圍內租一間小屋。"},{"en":"To rent a small cottage means to pay to live in a small countryside house.","zh":"rent a small cottage 是指付租金住在一間鄉郊小屋。"},{"en":"A farm worker may rent a cottage near the fields to avoid long travel.","zh":"農場工人可能租住田地附近的小屋，以避免長途通勤。"},{"en":"On-site housing can make rural jobs easier to accept.","zh":"場內住宿可以令鄉郊工作更容易接受。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to accommodation as part of a work arrangement.","zh":"這個短語指作為工作安排一部分的住宿。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"on the estate","meaning":"在莊園／農場範圍內","examples":[{"en":"The cottage is located on the estate.","zh":"小屋位於莊園範圍內。"},{"en":"On the estate means within the land or property owned or managed by the employer.","zh":"on the estate 是指在僱主擁有或管理的土地或物業範圍內。"},{"en":"A farm worker may live on the estate so they can reach work quickly.","zh":"農場工人可能住在農場範圍內，這樣能快速到達工作地點。"},{"en":"Living on the estate can reduce travel time but may feel remote.","zh":"住在莊園內可以減少通勤時間，但可能感覺偏遠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location within a large property.","zh":"這個短語描述大型物業範圍內的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the chance to earn","meaning":"有機會賺取","examples":[{"en":"The job offers the chance to earn a competitive salary.","zh":"這份工作提供有機會賺取具競爭力薪酬。"},{"en":"The chance to earn means the opportunity to receive money through work.","zh":"the chance to earn 是指透過工作獲得金錢收入的機會。"},{"en":"A part-time job gives students the chance to earn their own spending money.","zh":"兼職工作讓學生有機會賺取自己的零用錢。"},{"en":"Earnings matter when applicants compare different job options.","zh":"當申請者比較不同工作選項，收入很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on income opportunity.","zh":"這個短語著重收入機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"tractor driving experience","meaning":"駕駛拖拉機經驗","examples":[{"en":"Tractor driving experience is essential for the farm worker role.","zh":"農場工人職位必須有駕駛拖拉機經驗。"},{"en":"Tractor driving experience means previous practical experience operating a tractor.","zh":"tractor driving experience 是過往實際操作拖拉機的經驗。"},{"en":"A farm worker with tractor driving experience can help with ploughing, towing, and moving supplies.","zh":"有駕駛拖拉機經驗的農場工人可以協助犁田、拖運和搬運物資。"},{"en":"Tractors are powerful machines, so experience improves safety and efficiency.","zh":"拖拉機是強力機器，所以經驗能提升安全和效率。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific farming skill.","zh":"這個短語指一項具體農業技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be essential","meaning":"必不可少","examples":[{"en":"A driving licence and tractor driving experience are essential.","zh":"駕駛執照和駕駛拖拉機經驗是必不可少的。"},{"en":"To be essential means to be absolutely necessary.","zh":"be essential 是指絕對必要。"},{"en":"A first-aid certificate may be essential for a childcare job.","zh":"急救證書對托兒工作可能是必不可少的。"},{"en":"Essential requirements must be met before an applicant can be seriously considered.","zh":"申請者必須符合必備要求，才會被認真考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “preferred”.","zh":"這個短語比 preferred 更強。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/listening/Practice 18/task-2":[{"front":"recruitment consultant","meaning":"招聘顧問","examples":[{"en":"Megan Baker is a recruitment consultant at AVT Recruitment Specialists.","zh":"Megan Baker 是 AVT Recruitment Specialists 的招聘顧問。"},{"en":"A recruitment consultant helps employers find suitable workers and helps jobseekers find suitable jobs.","zh":"recruitment consultant 指幫助僱主尋找合適員工，並幫助求職者尋找合適工作的專業人士。"},{"en":"A recruitment consultant may check CVs, interview candidates, and match people with vacancies.","zh":"招聘顧問可能會檢查履歷、面試求職者，並把人配對到職位空缺。"},{"en":"If you are unsure which job suits you, a recruitment consultant can give advice.","zh":"如果你不確定哪份工作適合自己，招聘顧問可以給予建議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a professional who works in hiring and job placement.","zh":"這個短語描述從事招聘和職位配對的專業人士。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"recruitment specialists","meaning":"專業招聘公司","examples":[{"en":"AVT Recruitment Specialists helps people find jobs in agriculture and horticulture.","zh":"AVT Recruitment Specialists 幫助人們在農業和園藝業尋找工作。"},{"en":"Recruitment specialists are companies or people with expert knowledge of hiring in a particular area.","zh":"recruitment specialists 指在某個範疇的招聘方面有專門知識的公司或人士。"},{"en":"A recruitment specialist for schools may help find teachers and classroom assistants.","zh":"學校專業招聘公司可能幫忙尋找教師和課室助理。"},{"en":"Specialist recruiters understand the skills, qualifications, and experience employers need.","zh":"專業招聘者了解僱主需要的技能、資格和經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes experts in finding staff or jobs.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找員工或工作的專家。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"specialise in","meaning":"專門從事……","examples":[{"en":"The company specialises in positions in agriculture and horticulture.","zh":"這間公司專門從事農業和園藝職位招聘。"},{"en":"To specialise in something means to focus mainly on that area and build expertise in it.","zh":"specialise in something 指主要集中於某個範疇，並在該範疇建立專業知識。"},{"en":"A doctor may specialise in children’s health.","zh":"醫生可能專門從事兒童健康。"},{"en":"A company that specialises in one sector usually understands that sector well.","zh":"專門從事某行業的公司通常很了解該行業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a focused area of professional work.","zh":"這個短語描述專業工作的集中範疇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"positions that involve","meaning":"涉及……的職位","examples":[{"en":"The company specialises in positions that involve working in agriculture.","zh":"這間公司專門招聘涉及農業工作的職位。"},{"en":"Positions that involve something are jobs that include that activity or responsibility.","zh":"positions that involve something 指包含某活動或責任的職位。"},{"en":"Some school jobs involve working with young children every day.","zh":"有些學校職位涉及每天與年幼孩子工作。"},{"en":"If a position involves travel, applicants must be ready to spend time away from home.","zh":"如果職位涉及出差，申請人必須準備離家工作。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what a job includes.","zh":"這個短語解釋一份工作包括甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"agriculture and horticulture sectors","meaning":"農業及園藝業界","examples":[{"en":"The company works with the agriculture and horticulture sectors.","zh":"這間公司與農業及園藝業界合作。"},{"en":"The agriculture sector is about farming, while the horticulture sector is about growing plants, gardens, fruit, and vegetables.","zh":"agriculture sector 指農業，而 horticulture sector 指種植植物、花園、水果和蔬菜的園藝業。"},{"en":"Jobs in the agriculture and horticulture sectors may involve crops, animals, trees, or garden centres.","zh":"農業及園藝業界的工作可能涉及作物、動物、樹木或園藝中心。"},{"en":"These sectors are important because they provide food, plants, and land management.","zh":"這些行業很重要，因為它們提供食物、植物和土地管理。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to two related land-based industries.","zh":"這個短語指兩個相關的土地產業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fresh food production","meaning":"新鮮食品生產","examples":[{"en":"Fresh food production is one area covered by the company.","zh":"新鮮食品生產是這間公司涵蓋的範疇之一。"},{"en":"Fresh food production means growing, preparing, and supplying food that is not heavily processed.","zh":"fresh food production 指種植、準備和供應未經高度加工的食品。"},{"en":"Fruit farms, vegetable growers, and salad producers are part of fresh food production.","zh":"水果農場、蔬菜種植者和沙律生產商都屬於新鮮食品生產。"},{"en":"Fresh food production often requires quick transport because products can spoil.","zh":"新鮮食品生產通常需要快速運輸，因為產品容易變壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the industry of producing fresh food.","zh":"這個短語描述生產新鮮食品的行業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"garden and park maintenance","meaning":"花園及公園保養","examples":[{"en":"The sectors include garden and park maintenance.","zh":"這些行業包括花園及公園保養。"},{"en":"Garden and park maintenance means caring for outdoor spaces by cutting grass, planting, pruning, and keeping areas tidy.","zh":"garden and park maintenance 指透過剪草、種植、修剪和保持整潔來照顧戶外空間。"},{"en":"Local councils often hire workers for garden and park maintenance.","zh":"地方議會常聘請工人負責花園及公園保養。"},{"en":"This work helps public spaces remain safe, clean, and attractive.","zh":"這類工作幫助公共空間保持安全、清潔和吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical care of green spaces.","zh":"這個短語描述綠化空間的實際護理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"and so on","meaning":"等等","examples":[{"en":"The company covers fresh food production, garden maintenance and so on.","zh":"這間公司涵蓋新鮮食品生產、花園保養等等。"},{"en":"And so on means and other similar things.","zh":"and so on 指以及其他類似東西。"},{"en":"A farm job may involve feeding animals, repairing fences, cleaning equipment and so on.","zh":"農場工作可能涉及餵飼動物、修理圍欄、清潔設備等等。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids listing every example.","zh":"這個短語避免列出每一個例子。"},{"en":"It is useful when the listener can guess the rest of the category.","zh":"當聽者能猜到其餘同類項目時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"career opportunities","meaning":"事業機會","examples":[{"en":"These sectors provide some special career opportunities.","zh":"這些行業提供一些特別的事業機會。"},{"en":"Career opportunities are chances to get jobs, develop skills, and progress in work.","zh":"career opportunities 指取得工作、發展技能和在職場進步的機會。"},{"en":"Agriculture can offer career opportunities in science, sales, management, and conservation.","zh":"農業可以提供科學、銷售、管理和保育方面的事業機會。"},{"en":"Good career opportunities help people build a long-term future.","zh":"好的事業機會幫助人建立長遠未來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes possible paths for work and advancement.","zh":"這個短語描述工作和晉升的可能路徑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for a start","meaning":"首先","examples":[{"en":"For a start, the sectors offer flexible working opportunities.","zh":"首先，這些行業提供彈性工作機會。"},{"en":"For a start means as the first point or first reason.","zh":"for a start 指作為第一點或第一個理由。"},{"en":"For a start, outdoor work gives people fresh air and exercise.","zh":"首先，戶外工作給人新鮮空氣和運動。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the first item in an explanation.","zh":"這個短語引出解釋中的第一項。"},{"en":"It often suggests that more points will follow.","zh":"它常暗示之後還有更多重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"offer opportunities for","meaning":"為……提供機會","examples":[{"en":"These sectors offer opportunities for people who need flexible work.","zh":"這些行業為需要彈性工作的人提供機會。"},{"en":"To offer opportunities for someone means to provide chances that suit that group.","zh":"offer opportunities for someone 指提供適合某群體的機會。"},{"en":"Part-time roles can offer opportunities for parents returning to work.","zh":"兼職職位可以為重返職場的父母提供機會。"},{"en":"Good industries offer opportunities for people with different skills and lifestyles.","zh":"好行業會為擁有不同技能和生活方式的人提供機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving people a chance to do something.","zh":"這個短語描述給予人做某事的機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be stuck with","meaning":"被……困住","examples":[{"en":"Some people do not want to be stuck with a 40-hour week.","zh":"有些人不想被每週40小時工作困住。"},{"en":"Be stuck with something means be forced to accept or continue with something unpleasant or limiting.","zh":"be stuck with something 指被迫接受或繼續某件不愉快或有限制的事。"},{"en":"A worker may feel stuck with a timetable that leaves no time for family.","zh":"工人可能覺得自己被一個沒有家庭時間的時間表困住。"},{"en":"Flexible work helps people avoid being stuck with one fixed pattern.","zh":"彈性工作幫助人避免被單一固定模式困住。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests lack of choice.","zh":"這個短語暗示缺乏選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"40-hour week","meaning":"每週40小時工作","examples":[{"en":"Not everyone wants to be stuck with a 40-hour week.","zh":"不是每個人都想被每週40小時工作困住。"},{"en":"A 40-hour week means working forty hours in one week, often as a full-time schedule.","zh":"40-hour week 指一星期工作40小時，通常是全職工作安排。"},{"en":"Many office jobs follow a 40-hour week from Monday to Friday.","zh":"許多辦公室工作採用星期一至五的每週40小時工作模式。"},{"en":"Some people need fewer or more flexible hours because of family or study.","zh":"有些人因家庭或學業需要較少或較彈性的工時。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a standard full-time working pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述標準全職工作模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"juggle work with","meaning":"兼顧工作與……","examples":[{"en":"Some recruits need to juggle work with other responsibilities.","zh":"有些求職者需要兼顧工作與其他責任。"},{"en":"To juggle work with something means to manage work and another duty at the same time.","zh":"juggle work with something 指同時處理工作和另一項責任。"},{"en":"Many parents juggle work with childcare every day.","zh":"許多家長每天都要兼顧工作與照顧子女。"},{"en":"People who study part-time may need to juggle work with evening classes.","zh":"兼讀學生可能需要兼顧工作與夜校課程。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests balancing competing demands.","zh":"這個短語暗示平衡互相競爭的需求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"other responsibilities","meaning":"其他責任","examples":[{"en":"Some workers have other responsibilities such as childcare.","zh":"有些工人有其他責任，例如照顧子女。"},{"en":"Other responsibilities are additional duties outside the main job.","zh":"other responsibilities 指主要工作以外的額外職責。"},{"en":"A worker may have other responsibilities, such as caring for elderly parents.","zh":"工人可能有其他責任，例如照顧年長父母。"},{"en":"Employers who understand other responsibilities may offer flexible hours.","zh":"理解其他責任的僱主可能會提供彈性工時。"},{"en":"This phrase describes duties beyond work itself.","zh":"這個短語描述工作本身以外的責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"childcare","meaning":"照顧子女","examples":[{"en":"Many recruits need to juggle work with childcare.","zh":"許多求職者需要兼顧工作與照顧子女。"},{"en":"Childcare means looking after children, especially while parents are working.","zh":"childcare 指照顧孩子，尤其是在父母工作期間。"},{"en":"Some parents need childcare before school, after school, or during holidays.","zh":"有些家長在上學前、放學後或假期需要托兒。"},{"en":"Childcare responsibilities can affect what hours a person is able to work.","zh":"照顧子女的責任會影響一個人能工作的時間。"},{"en":"This word describes care for children.","zh":"這個字描述對兒童的照顧。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"many of our recruits","meaning":"我們許多求職者","examples":[{"en":"Flexible hours are important for many of our recruits.","zh":"彈性工時對我們許多求職者很重要。"},{"en":"Many of our recruits means many of the people who apply through or are placed by the agency.","zh":"many of our recruits 指許多透過該機構申請或被安排工作的人。"},{"en":"Many of our recruits are looking for work that fits family life.","zh":"我們許多求職者正在尋找能配合家庭生活的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the speaker is talking from the company’s experience.","zh":"這個短語顯示說話者是根據公司經驗發言。"},{"en":"It refers to a large group of jobseekers connected with the agency.","zh":"它指與招聘公司相關的一大群求職者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rural setting","meaning":"鄉郊環境","examples":[{"en":"Some people like working in a rural setting.","zh":"有些人喜歡在鄉郊環境工作。"},{"en":"A rural setting is a countryside environment, away from large towns and cities.","zh":"rural setting 指遠離大城鎮和城市的鄉村環境。"},{"en":"Farms, villages, and open fields are part of a rural setting.","zh":"農場、村莊和開闊田野都屬於鄉郊環境。"},{"en":"People who enjoy quiet spaces may prefer a rural setting.","zh":"喜歡安靜空間的人可能較喜歡鄉郊環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a countryside work environment.","zh":"這個短語描述鄉村工作環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"surrounded by","meaning":"被……包圍","examples":[{"en":"Some people like working surrounded by plants and trees.","zh":"有些人喜歡在被植物和樹木包圍的環境工作。"},{"en":"Surrounded by means having something all around you.","zh":"surrounded by 指四周都有某物。"},{"en":"A gardener may spend the day surrounded by flowers and soil.","zh":"園丁可能整天被花和泥土包圍。"},{"en":"Being surrounded by nature can feel calmer than being in an office.","zh":"被大自然包圍可能比在辦公室更令人平靜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the environment around a person.","zh":"這個短語描述人周圍的環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"instead of","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Some people prefer being surrounded by plants instead of buildings.","zh":"有些人較喜歡被植物包圍，而不是被建築物包圍。"},{"en":"Instead of means in place of another thing or choice.","zh":"instead of 指取代另一件事或選擇。"},{"en":"Some workers choose outdoor jobs instead of office jobs.","zh":"有些工人選擇戶外工作，而不是辦公室工作。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the chosen option with the one not chosen.","zh":"這個短語把已選選項與未選選項作比較。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining preference or replacement.","zh":"解釋偏好或替代時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"guarantee that","meaning":"保證……","examples":[{"en":"The company cannot guarantee that every job will be in a rural setting.","zh":"公司不能保證每份工作都在鄉郊環境。"},{"en":"Guarantee that means promise that something will certainly happen or be true.","zh":"guarantee that 指承諾某事一定會發生或是真的。"},{"en":"A recruitment agency cannot guarantee that every applicant will get an interview.","zh":"招聘公司不能保證每名申請人都會獲面試。"},{"en":"If something cannot be guaranteed, people should not assume it will happen.","zh":"如果某事不能被保證，人們就不應假設它一定會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes certainty or lack of certainty.","zh":"這個短語描述確定性或缺乏確定性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"health benefits","meaning":"健康益處","examples":[{"en":"Outdoor jobs can offer health benefits.","zh":"戶外工作可以帶來健康益處。"},{"en":"Health benefits are positive effects on the body or mind.","zh":"health benefits 指對身體或心理的正面影響。"},{"en":"Walking, fresh air, and physical activity can bring health benefits.","zh":"步行、新鮮空氣和體力活動可以帶來健康益處。"},{"en":"A job with health benefits may help workers feel fitter and less stressed.","zh":"有健康益處的工作可能幫助員工更健康、壓力更少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advantages for wellbeing.","zh":"這個短語描述對身心健康的好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sit all day","meaning":"整天坐着","examples":[{"en":"Some jobs do not require workers to sit all day.","zh":"有些工作不需要員工整天坐着。"},{"en":"To sit all day means spend most of the working day seated.","zh":"sit all day 指工作日大部分時間都坐着。"},{"en":"Office workers may sit all day in front of computers.","zh":"辦公室員工可能整天坐在電腦前。"},{"en":"Some people dislike sitting all day because it can feel unhealthy or boring.","zh":"有些人不喜歡整天坐着，因為這可能感覺不健康或沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mostly sedentary routine.","zh":"這個短語描述主要坐着不動的日常。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"look at a screen","meaning":"看着螢幕","examples":[{"en":"Some workers dislike looking at a screen all day.","zh":"有些員工不喜歡整天看着螢幕。"},{"en":"To look at a screen means to spend time viewing a computer, phone, or tablet display.","zh":"look at a screen 指花時間觀看電腦、手機或平板顯示屏。"},{"en":"Many office jobs require people to look at a screen for hours.","zh":"許多辦公室工作要求人長時間看着螢幕。"},{"en":"Outdoor workers may prefer jobs where they do not need to look at a screen constantly.","zh":"戶外工作者可能較喜歡不需要不停看螢幕的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes screen-based work.","zh":"這個短語描述以螢幕為主的工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a big plus","meaning":"一大優點","examples":[{"en":"Not sitting at a screen all day is a big plus for many people.","zh":"不用整天坐在螢幕前對很多人來說是一大優點。"},{"en":"A big plus is a major advantage or positive point.","zh":"big plus 指主要好處或正面因素。"},{"en":"For some jobseekers, flexible hours are a big plus.","zh":"對有些求職者來說，彈性工時是一大優點。"},{"en":"A benefit becomes a big plus when it strongly affects someone’s decision.","zh":"當一項好處強烈影響某人的決定，它就成為一大優點。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and positive.","zh":"這個短語較口語，帶正面意思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a lot of variety","meaning":"差異很大","examples":[{"en":"There is a lot of variety in salaries.","zh":"薪酬差異很大。"},{"en":"A lot of variety means many differences or many types.","zh":"a lot of variety 指有很多差異或很多種類。"},{"en":"There is a lot of variety in agriculture jobs, from field work to management.","zh":"農業工作差異很大，從田間工作到管理都有。"},{"en":"Variety can make a sector interesting because not every role is the same.","zh":"多樣性可以令一個行業有趣，因為不是每個職位都一樣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a wide range.","zh":"這個短語描述範圍很廣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have the opportunity for","meaning":"有……的機會","examples":[{"en":"Some jobs offer the opportunity for overseas travel.","zh":"有些工作提供海外出行的機會。"},{"en":"Have the opportunity for something means have the chance to experience or do it.","zh":"have the opportunity for something 指有機會經歷或做某事。"},{"en":"A graduate role may offer the opportunity for training abroad.","zh":"畢業生職位可能提供海外培訓的機會。"},{"en":"Opportunities for travel can make a job more attractive to some people.","zh":"出差機會可以令工作對某些人更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible benefit.","zh":"這個短語描述可能的好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"travel overseas","meaning":"到海外公幹；海外出行","examples":[{"en":"Some types of jobs may involve travel overseas.","zh":"某些類型的工作可能涉及海外出行。"},{"en":"To travel overseas means to go to another country, usually across the sea or abroad.","zh":"travel overseas 指前往另一個國家，通常是跨海或到國外。"},{"en":"A sales manager may travel overseas to meet clients or visit suppliers.","zh":"銷售經理可能到海外公幹，會見客戶或拜訪供應商。"},{"en":"Overseas travel can be exciting, but it may also be tiring.","zh":"海外出行可以令人興奮，但也可能令人疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase describes international travel.","zh":"這個短語描述國際出行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"取決於……","examples":[{"en":"The chance to travel overseas depends on the job.","zh":"到海外出行的機會取決於工作。"},{"en":"Depend on means be decided or affected by something.","zh":"depend on 指由某事決定或受某事影響。"},{"en":"Whether you need a driving licence depends on the role.","zh":"是否需要駕駛執照取決於職位。"},{"en":"If something depends on the job, different jobs may have different requirements.","zh":"如果某事取決於工作，不同工作可能有不同要求。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what controls the result.","zh":"這個短語解釋結果由甚麼控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be keen to","meaning":"熱衷於……","examples":[{"en":"Not everyone is keen to travel overseas for work.","zh":"不是每個人都熱衷於為工作到海外出行。"},{"en":"Be keen to do something means be eager or enthusiastic to do it.","zh":"be keen to do something 指渴望或熱心做某事。"},{"en":"Some graduates are keen to work outdoors after years of studying inside.","zh":"有些畢業生在室內讀書多年後，很熱衷於戶外工作。"},{"en":"If someone is not keen to travel, a local role may suit them better.","zh":"如果某人不熱衷於出差，本地職位可能更適合他。"},{"en":"This phrase describes willingness and interest.","zh":"這個短語描述意願和興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"working outdoors","meaning":"戶外工作","examples":[{"en":"Working outdoors has its challenges.","zh":"戶外工作有其挑戰。"},{"en":"Working outdoors means doing a job outside rather than inside a building.","zh":"working outdoors 指在建築物外工作，而不是在室內工作。"},{"en":"Gardeners, farm workers, and tree technicians often spend their days working outdoors.","zh":"園丁、農場工人和樹木技術員常常整天戶外工作。"},{"en":"Outdoor work can involve fresh air, physical movement, and changing weather.","zh":"戶外工作可能涉及新鮮空氣、身體活動和變化的天氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes jobs done in open-air environments.","zh":"這個短語描述在露天環境中進行的工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have its challenges","meaning":"有其挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Working outdoors does have its challenges.","zh":"戶外工作確實有其挑戰。"},{"en":"Have its challenges means include difficulties as well as advantages.","zh":"have its challenges 指除了好處外，也包含困難。"},{"en":"Teaching young children has its challenges, even when the work is rewarding.","zh":"教導年幼孩子即使有回報，也有其挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a balanced view by admitting problems.","zh":"這個短語透過承認問題來給出平衡看法。"},{"en":"It suggests that something is not easy all the time.","zh":"它暗示某事並非一直容易。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"extremely unpleasant","meaning":"極不舒服","examples":[{"en":"Outdoor work can be extremely unpleasant when it is cold and windy.","zh":"天氣寒冷大風時，戶外工作可以極不舒服。"},{"en":"Extremely unpleasant means very uncomfortable, difficult, or disagreeable.","zh":"extremely unpleasant 指非常不舒服、困難或令人不快。"},{"en":"Working in heavy rain without proper clothing can be extremely unpleasant.","zh":"沒有合適衣物而在大雨中工作可以極不舒服。"},{"en":"Weather can turn an enjoyable outdoor job into an unpleasant one.","zh":"天氣可以把愉快的戶外工作變成不舒服的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly describes discomfort.","zh":"這個短語強烈描述不適感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cold and windy","meaning":"寒冷大風","examples":[{"en":"Working outdoors can be unpleasant when it is cold and windy.","zh":"天氣寒冷大風時，戶外工作可能令人不舒服。"},{"en":"Cold and windy means low in temperature and with strong moving air.","zh":"cold and windy 指氣溫低而且風很大。"},{"en":"A field can feel much harsher when it is cold and windy.","zh":"當天氣寒冷大風，田野會感覺更加惡劣。"},{"en":"Workers need warm clothing if they work outside in cold and windy weather.","zh":"如果工人在寒冷大風的天氣戶外工作，就需要保暖衣物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficult weather conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述困難天氣狀況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pretty fit","meaning":"身體頗健壯","examples":[{"en":"Some jobs require workers to be pretty fit.","zh":"有些工作要求員工身體頗健壯。"},{"en":"Pretty fit means fairly healthy, strong, and physically able.","zh":"pretty fit 指相當健康、強壯並有體能。"},{"en":"A tree technician needs to be pretty fit because the work can involve climbing and lifting.","zh":"樹木技術員需要身體頗健壯，因為工作可能涉及攀爬和搬運。"},{"en":"You do not need to be an athlete, but you may need good stamina.","zh":"你不需要成為運動員，但可能需要良好耐力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reasonable level of physical fitness.","zh":"這個短語描述合理程度的體能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"modern technology","meaning":"現代科技","examples":[{"en":"Modern technology has reduced the need for physical strength.","zh":"現代科技已減少對體力的需求。"},{"en":"Modern technology means new machines, tools, and systems used today.","zh":"modern technology 指現今使用的新機器、工具和系統。"},{"en":"Tractors and lifting equipment are examples of modern technology in farming.","zh":"拖拉機和起重設備是農業中現代科技的例子。"},{"en":"Technology can make heavy work safer and less physically demanding.","zh":"科技可以令繁重工作更安全，也較不消耗體力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes current technical tools and methods.","zh":"這個短語描述現代技術工具和方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not as important as it once was","meaning":"不像以前那麼重要","examples":[{"en":"Fitness is not as important as it once was in some jobs.","zh":"在有些工作中，體能不像以前那麼重要。"},{"en":"Not as important as it once was means less important now than in the past.","zh":"not as important as it once was 指現在不像過去那麼重要。"},{"en":"Handwriting is not as important as it once was in many office jobs.","zh":"在許多辦公室工作中，手寫不像以前那麼重要。"},{"en":"Technology can make an old requirement less important.","zh":"科技可以令舊有要求變得沒那麼重要。"},{"en":"This phrase compares present importance with past importance.","zh":"這個短語比較現在和過去的重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"standards of health and safety","meaning":"健康及安全標準","examples":[{"en":"Standards of health and safety are much higher now.","zh":"現在健康及安全標準高得多。"},{"en":"Standards of health and safety are rules and expectations designed to protect workers from harm.","zh":"standards of health and safety 指為保護工人免受傷害而設的規則和要求。"},{"en":"Farms now have higher standards of health and safety than in the past.","zh":"現今農場的健康及安全標準比過去更高。"},{"en":"Better safety standards can reduce accidents and injuries.","zh":"更好的安全標準可以減少意外和受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes workplace protection requirements.","zh":"這個短語描述工作場所保護要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"work-related accidents","meaning":"工傷意外","examples":[{"en":"There are fewer work-related accidents now.","zh":"現在工傷意外較少。"},{"en":"Work-related accidents are accidents that happen because of or during someone’s job.","zh":"work-related accidents 指因工作或在工作期間發生的意外。"},{"en":"A fall from a ladder at work is a work-related accident.","zh":"在工作中從梯子跌下就是工傷意外。"},{"en":"Training and safety equipment can reduce work-related accidents.","zh":"培訓和安全設備可以減少工傷意外。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accidents connected with employment.","zh":"這個短語描述與工作相關的意外。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lively city environment","meaning":"熱鬧城市環境","examples":[{"en":"These jobs may not suit people who like a lively city environment.","zh":"這些工作可能不適合喜歡熱鬧城市環境的人。"},{"en":"A lively city environment is a busy urban setting with shops, crowds, transport, and entertainment.","zh":"lively city environment 指有商店、人群、交通和娛樂的繁忙都市環境。"},{"en":"Some people enjoy a lively city environment because there is always something happening.","zh":"有些人喜歡熱鬧城市環境，因為總有事情發生。"},{"en":"Rural jobs may feel too quiet for people who love city life.","zh":"對熱愛城市生活的人來說，鄉郊工作可能太安靜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an energetic urban setting.","zh":"這個短語描述有活力的都市環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not for you","meaning":"不適合你","examples":[{"en":"These jobs are probably not for people who love city life.","zh":"這些工作大概不適合熱愛城市生活的人。"},{"en":"Not for you means not suitable for you or not matching your preferences.","zh":"not for you 指不適合你，或不符合你的偏好。"},{"en":"If you dislike physical work, a farm worker role may not be for you.","zh":"如果你不喜歡體力工作，農場工人職位可能不適合你。"},{"en":"This phrase is direct but useful when giving career advice.","zh":"給予職業建議時，這個短語直接但實用。"},{"en":"It helps people avoid unsuitable choices.","zh":"它幫助人避免不合適選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"remote areas","meaning":"偏遠地區","examples":[{"en":"Many agriculture and horticulture jobs are in remote areas.","zh":"許多農業和園藝工作位於偏遠地區。"},{"en":"Remote areas are places far from towns, cities, or major services.","zh":"remote areas 指遠離城鎮、城市或主要服務的地方。"},{"en":"A farm in a remote area may be difficult to reach without a car.","zh":"位於偏遠地區的農場如果沒有車可能很難到達。"},{"en":"Working in remote areas can be peaceful but may feel isolated.","zh":"在偏遠地區工作可以很寧靜，但也可能感到孤立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distant or less accessible places.","zh":"這個短語描述遙遠或較難到達的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"worry about","meaning":"擔心……","examples":[{"en":"Some people worry about finding a suitable place to live.","zh":"有些人擔心找不到合適住所。"},{"en":"Worry about means feel anxious or concerned about something.","zh":"worry about 指對某事感到焦慮或擔憂。"},{"en":"New recruits may worry about moving to a rural area.","zh":"新入職者可能擔心搬到鄉郊地區。"},{"en":"People often worry about housing before accepting a job far from home.","zh":"人們在接受離家很遠的工作前，常擔心住屋問題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the thing causing anxiety.","zh":"這個短語引出造成焦慮的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"suitable place to live","meaning":"合適住所","examples":[{"en":"Some recruits worry about finding a suitable place to live.","zh":"有些求職者擔心找不到合適住所。"},{"en":"A suitable place to live is accommodation that fits a person’s budget, work location, and needs.","zh":"suitable place to live 指符合某人預算、工作地點和需要的住所。"},{"en":"A farm worker may need a suitable place to live near the estate.","zh":"農場工人可能需要在莊園附近找合適住所。"},{"en":"Housing matters because it affects travel, comfort, and daily life.","zh":"住屋很重要，因為它影響交通、舒適和日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes appropriate accommodation.","zh":"這個短語描述合適的住宿。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in our experience","meaning":"根據我們的經驗","examples":[{"en":"In the company’s experience, accommodation usually turns out fine.","zh":"根據公司的經驗，住宿問題通常結果沒問題。"},{"en":"In our experience means based on what we have seen or dealt with before.","zh":"in our experience 指根據我們以前見過或處理過的情況。"},{"en":"In our experience, rural employers often help new workers find housing.","zh":"根據我們的經驗，鄉郊僱主常幫助新員工找住所。"},{"en":"This phrase makes advice sound practical and based on real cases.","zh":"這個短語令建議聽起來實際，並基於真實案例。"},{"en":"It is useful when reassuring people.","zh":"安撫別人時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"turn out fine","meaning":"結果通常沒問題","examples":[{"en":"The accommodation issue usually turns out fine.","zh":"住宿問題結果通常沒問題。"},{"en":"Turn out fine means end in a satisfactory or problem-free way.","zh":"turn out fine 指最後以令人滿意或沒有問題的方式結束。"},{"en":"A job interview may feel stressful but turn out fine in the end.","zh":"面試可能令人緊張，但最後結果通常沒問題。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures people that a worry may be manageable.","zh":"這個短語安撫人，表示擔憂可能可以處理。"},{"en":"It describes a positive final result.","zh":"它描述正面的最終結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on our books","meaning":"在我們手頭職位名單上","examples":[{"en":"The company has some exciting jobs on its books right now.","zh":"公司目前在手頭職位名單上有一些令人期待的工作。"},{"en":"On our books means listed or registered with our agency or organisation.","zh":"on our books 指在我們機構或組織中列出或登記。"},{"en":"A recruitment agency may have hundreds of candidates on its books.","zh":"招聘公司名冊上可能有數百名求職者。"},{"en":"Jobs on the books are vacancies the agency is currently handling.","zh":"在名單上的職位是該機構目前正在處理的空缺。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in recruitment and agency work.","zh":"這個短語常見於招聘和中介工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fresh food commercial manager","meaning":"新鮮食品商務經理","examples":[{"en":"One job is for a fresh food commercial manager.","zh":"其中一份工作是新鮮食品商務經理。"},{"en":"A fresh food commercial manager is a manager who handles business decisions for fresh food products.","zh":"fresh food commercial manager 指負責新鮮食品產品商業決策的經理。"},{"en":"This role may involve sales, pricing, supermarket relationships, and product planning.","zh":"這個角色可能涉及銷售、定價、超市關係和產品規劃。"},{"en":"The manager needs to understand both food production and commercial targets.","zh":"經理需要同時了解食品生產和商業目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a business-management role in fresh food.","zh":"這個短語描述新鮮食品行業中的商務管理職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fresh food producer","meaning":"新鮮食品生產商","examples":[{"en":"The client is a very large fresh food producer.","zh":"客戶是一間非常大型的新鮮食品生產商。"},{"en":"A fresh food producer is a company or farm that grows, prepares, or supplies fresh food.","zh":"fresh food producer 指種植、準備或供應新鮮食品的公司或農場。"},{"en":"A fresh food producer may sell vegetables, fruit, salads, or herbs to supermarkets.","zh":"新鮮食品生產商可能向超市出售蔬菜、水果、沙律或香草。"},{"en":"Large producers must manage quality, speed, and supply carefully.","zh":"大型生產商必須小心管理質素、速度和供應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a business that produces fresh food.","zh":"這個短語描述生產新鮮食品的企業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"supply a range of","meaning":"為一系列……供貨","examples":[{"en":"The producer supplies a range of top supermarkets.","zh":"該生產商為一系列頂級超市供貨。"},{"en":"Supply a range of something means provide goods or services to several types or examples.","zh":"supply a range of something 指向多種類型或多個例子提供貨品或服務。"},{"en":"A farm may supply a range of restaurants with fresh vegetables.","zh":"農場可能為一系列餐廳供應新鮮蔬菜。"},{"en":"Supplying a range of customers can make a business more stable.","zh":"為一系列客戶供貨可以令企業更穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes providing products to multiple buyers or groups.","zh":"這個短語描述向多個買家或群體提供產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"top supermarkets","meaning":"頂級超市","examples":[{"en":"The company supplies fresh food to top supermarkets.","zh":"這間公司向頂級超市供應新鮮食品。"},{"en":"Top supermarkets are major or high-ranking supermarket chains.","zh":"top supermarkets 指主要或排名較高的連鎖超市。"},{"en":"Supplying top supermarkets can be demanding because quality standards are high.","zh":"向頂級超市供貨要求很高，因為質量標準很高。"},{"en":"A producer that works with top supermarkets must deliver reliably.","zh":"與頂級超市合作的生產商必須可靠交貨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes leading supermarket businesses.","zh":"這個短語描述領先的超市企業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"operate in","meaning":"在……中營運","examples":[{"en":"The client operates in a very fast-paced environment.","zh":"該客戶在非常快節奏的環境中營運。"},{"en":"Operate in means work or do business within a particular situation or market.","zh":"operate in 指在某特定情況或市場中工作或經營。"},{"en":"Many food companies operate in markets where prices change quickly.","zh":"許多食品公司在價格快速變化的市場中營運。"},{"en":"The environment a company operates in affects its decisions.","zh":"公司營運的環境會影響其決策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the setting in which a business works.","zh":"這個短語描述企業工作的背景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fast-paced environment","meaning":"快節奏環境","examples":[{"en":"The fresh food producer operates in a fast-paced environment.","zh":"該新鮮食品生產商在快節奏環境中營運。"},{"en":"A fast-paced environment is a workplace where things move quickly and decisions must be made fast.","zh":"fast-paced environment 指事情進展很快、決策必須迅速作出的工作場所。"},{"en":"Fresh food businesses are fast-paced because products must be sold before they spoil.","zh":"新鮮食品企業節奏很快，因為產品必須在變壞前出售。"},{"en":"People in fast-paced environments need energy, organisation, and quick thinking.","zh":"在快節奏環境工作的人需要精力、組織能力和快速思考。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a busy and demanding workplace.","zh":"這個短語描述繁忙而要求高的工作場所。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"low profit margins","meaning":"低利潤率","examples":[{"en":"The company operates with low profit margins.","zh":"這間公司以低利潤率營運。"},{"en":"Low profit margins mean the company earns only a small profit compared with its costs or sales.","zh":"low profit margins 指公司相對成本或銷售額只賺取少量利潤。"},{"en":"Food producers often face low profit margins because prices are competitive.","zh":"食品生產商常面對低利潤率，因為價格競爭激烈。"},{"en":"Low margins require careful control of waste, transport, and labour costs.","zh":"低利潤率需要仔細控制浪費、運輸和人手成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited profit per product or sale.","zh":"這個短語描述每件產品或每次銷售的有限利潤。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"work hard, play hard","meaning":"努力工作，也盡情玩樂","examples":[{"en":"The staff work hard, but they play hard as well.","zh":"員工努力工作，但也盡情玩樂。"},{"en":"Work hard, play hard means people put great effort into work but also enjoy social life energetically.","zh":"work hard, play hard 指人們工作時非常努力，同時也積極享受社交生活。"},{"en":"A company with this culture may expect long hours but also organise lively events.","zh":"有這種文化的公司可能要求長時間工作，但也會舉辦熱鬧活動。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests both pressure and fun.","zh":"這個短語暗示既有壓力，也有樂趣。"},{"en":"It describes a sociable, high-energy workplace attitude.","zh":"它描述社交性強、能量高的工作態度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sociable personality","meaning":"善於交際的性格","examples":[{"en":"This job may suit someone with a sociable personality.","zh":"這份工作可能適合性格善於交際的人。"},{"en":"A sociable personality means a person enjoys talking to and spending time with other people.","zh":"sociable personality 指喜歡與人交談和相處的性格。"},{"en":"Sales roles often suit people with sociable personalities.","zh":"銷售職位通常適合性格善於交際的人。"},{"en":"Someone sociable may build relationships with clients more easily.","zh":"善於交際的人可能更容易與客戶建立關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an outgoing and people-friendly character.","zh":"這個短語描述外向而友善待人的性格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"this may be for you","meaning":"這可能適合你","examples":[{"en":"If you have a sociable personality, this job may be for you.","zh":"如果你性格善於交際，這份工作可能適合你。"},{"en":"This may be for you means this might suit your skills, personality, or interests.","zh":"this may be for you 指這可能符合你的技能、性格或興趣。"},{"en":"If you enjoy working outdoors, a farm role may be for you.","zh":"如果你喜歡戶外工作，農場職位可能適合你。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when recommending a possible match.","zh":"這個短語用於推薦可能合適的選擇。"},{"en":"It is common in recruitment and advertising.","zh":"它常見於招聘和廣告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"exciting post","meaning":"令人期待的職位","examples":[{"en":"The company has an exciting post as an agronomist.","zh":"公司有一個令人期待的農藝師職位。"},{"en":"An exciting post is a job that sounds interesting, attractive, or full of opportunity.","zh":"exciting post 指聽起來有趣、吸引或充滿機會的工作。"},{"en":"A new research role in crop science could be an exciting post for a graduate.","zh":"作物科學的新研究職位對畢業生來說可能是令人期待的職位。"},{"en":"Calling a post exciting makes it sound appealing to applicants.","zh":"稱一個職位 exciting 會令它對申請人聽起來更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an attractive job vacancy.","zh":"這個短語描述吸引人的職位空缺。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"agronomist","meaning":"農藝師","examples":[{"en":"An agronomist advises farmers on crops and farming practices.","zh":"農藝師就作物和耕作方法向農民提供建議。"},{"en":"An agronomist is a specialist who studies crops, soil, and farming methods.","zh":"agronomist 指研究作物、泥土和耕作方法的專家。"},{"en":"Agronomists help farmers choose fertilisers, protect crops, and improve yields.","zh":"農藝師幫助農民選擇肥料、保護作物和提升產量。"},{"en":"This job combines science with practical farm advice.","zh":"這份工作結合科學和實際農場建議。"},{"en":"This word names a crop and farming expert.","zh":"這個字指出作物和農業專家。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"advise farmers on","meaning":"就……向農民提供建議","examples":[{"en":"The agronomist advises farmers on crop nutrition and pests.","zh":"農藝師就作物營養和害蟲向農民提供建議。"},{"en":"To advise farmers on something means to give them expert guidance about that topic.","zh":"advise farmers on something 指就某題目向農民提供專業指導。"},{"en":"An agronomist may advise farmers on when to plant a crop.","zh":"農藝師可能就何時種植作物向農民提供建議。"},{"en":"Good advice can help farmers reduce waste and improve harvests.","zh":"好建議可以幫助農民減少浪費並改善收成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes professional agricultural guidance.","zh":"這個短語描述專業農業指導。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"crop nutrition","meaning":"作物營養","examples":[{"en":"The agronomist gives advice on crop nutrition.","zh":"農藝師就作物營養提供建議。"},{"en":"Crop nutrition means the nutrients crops need to grow well.","zh":"crop nutrition 指作物良好生長所需的營養。"},{"en":"Nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium are important parts of crop nutrition.","zh":"氮、磷和鉀是作物營養的重要部分。"},{"en":"Poor crop nutrition can lead to weak plants and smaller harvests.","zh":"作物營養不足會導致植物弱小和收成較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes feeding crops correctly.","zh":"這個短語描述正確供給作物養分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"protection against pests","meaning":"防治害蟲","examples":[{"en":"The agronomist advises farmers on protection against pests.","zh":"農藝師就防治害蟲向農民提供建議。"},{"en":"Protection against pests means ways to stop insects, animals, or diseases from damaging crops.","zh":"protection against pests 指防止昆蟲、動物或疾病破壞作物的方法。"},{"en":"Nets, natural predators, and safe sprays can provide protection against pests.","zh":"網、天敵和安全噴劑都可以提供防治害蟲的保護。"},{"en":"Without pest protection, crops may be eaten or infected.","zh":"如果沒有防治害蟲，作物可能被吃掉或受感染。"},{"en":"This phrase describes crop defence.","zh":"這個短語描述作物防護。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"latest legislation","meaning":"最新法例","examples":[{"en":"The agronomist needs to understand the latest legislation on farming.","zh":"農藝師需要了解關於農業的最新法例。"},{"en":"Latest legislation means the most recent laws or official rules.","zh":"latest legislation 指最新的法律或官方規則。"},{"en":"Farmers must follow the latest legislation on chemical use and animal welfare.","zh":"農民必須遵守關於化學品使用和動物福利的最新法例。"},{"en":"In regulated industries, old knowledge may not be enough.","zh":"在受規管行業中，舊知識可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes current legal requirements.","zh":"這個短語描述現行法律要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"farming and agricultural practices","meaning":"耕作及農業實務","examples":[{"en":"The job involves advice on farming and agricultural practices.","zh":"這份工作涉及就耕作及農業實務提供建議。"},{"en":"Farming and agricultural practices are the methods used to grow crops and manage farms.","zh":"farming and agricultural practices 指種植作物和管理農場所用的方法。"},{"en":"Crop rotation, irrigation, fertiliser use, and pest control are agricultural practices.","zh":"輪作、灌溉、施肥和害蟲控制都是農業實務。"},{"en":"Good practices can improve productivity and protect the environment.","zh":"良好做法可以提升生產力並保護環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical methods used in farming.","zh":"這個短語描述農業中的實際方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"good opportunities for","meaning":"給予……的好機會","examples":[{"en":"There are good opportunities for the right person to advance quickly.","zh":"對合適人選來說，有快速晉升的好機會。"},{"en":"Good opportunities for someone are favourable chances that can help that person succeed.","zh":"good opportunities for someone 指能幫助某人成功的有利機會。"},{"en":"A growing company may offer good opportunities for young managers.","zh":"成長中的公司可能給年輕經理好機會。"},{"en":"Good opportunities are valuable when they match a person’s skills and ambition.","zh":"當好機會配合一個人的技能和抱負，它就很有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes promising chances for progress.","zh":"這個短語描述有前景的進步機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the right person","meaning":"合適人選","examples":[{"en":"The agronomist role offers opportunities for the right person.","zh":"農藝師職位為合適人選提供機會。"},{"en":"The right person is someone whose skills, experience, personality, and goals fit the role.","zh":"right person 指技能、經驗、性格和目標都符合職位的人。"},{"en":"A difficult outdoor job needs the right person, not just any applicant.","zh":"困難的戶外工作需要合適人選，而不是任何申請人都可以。"},{"en":"Employers look for the right person because hiring mistakes can be costly.","zh":"僱主尋找合適人選，因為招聘錯誤代價可能很高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a suitable candidate.","zh":"這個短語描述合適候選人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make one’s way up","meaning":"逐步晉升","examples":[{"en":"The right person can quickly make their way up the career ladder.","zh":"合適人選可以很快在事業階梯上逐步晉升。"},{"en":"To make one’s way up means gradually progress to higher positions.","zh":"make one’s way up 指逐漸進步到較高職位。"},{"en":"A farm worker may make his way up to supervisor through training and experience.","zh":"農場工人可能透過培訓和經驗逐步晉升為主管。"},{"en":"People usually make their way up by proving ability over time.","zh":"人們通常透過長時間證明能力來逐步晉升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes career progress.","zh":"這個短語描述事業進展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"career ladder","meaning":"事業階梯","examples":[{"en":"The right person can move up the career ladder quickly.","zh":"合適人選可以很快在事業階梯上晉升。"},{"en":"The career ladder is the series of higher positions someone can move through in a career.","zh":"career ladder 指一個人在事業中可以逐步升上的一系列較高職位。"},{"en":"A trainee may climb the career ladder to become a manager.","zh":"實習生可能沿事業階梯晉升成經理。"},{"en":"A clear career ladder helps employees see their future path.","zh":"清晰的事業階梯幫助員工看見未來路徑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structured job advancement.","zh":"這個短語描述有結構的職位晉升。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"deep knowledge of","meaning":"對……有深入認識","examples":[{"en":"Applicants need a deep knowledge of the agricultural sector.","zh":"申請人需要對農業界有深入認識。"},{"en":"Deep knowledge of something means detailed and strong understanding of it.","zh":"deep knowledge of something 指對某事有詳細而深厚的理解。"},{"en":"An agronomist needs deep knowledge of soil, crops, and farming law.","zh":"農藝師需要對泥土、作物和農業法例有深入認識。"},{"en":"Deep knowledge helps professionals give accurate advice.","zh":"深入認識幫助專業人士提供準確建議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes more than basic familiarity.","zh":"這個短語描述超越基本熟悉的知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"agricultural sector","meaning":"農業界","examples":[{"en":"A deep knowledge of the agricultural sector is expected.","zh":"申請人需對農業界有深入認識。"},{"en":"The agricultural sector is the part of the economy connected with farming and food production.","zh":"agricultural sector 指經濟中與耕作和食品生產相關的部分。"},{"en":"The agricultural sector includes farms, crop advisers, machinery suppliers, and food producers.","zh":"農業界包括農場、作物顧問、機械供應商和食品生產商。"},{"en":"Changes in weather and law can strongly affect the agricultural sector.","zh":"天氣和法律變化可以強烈影響農業界。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the farming industry as a whole.","zh":"這個短語描述整個農業行業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be expected of","meaning":"對……有所要求","examples":[{"en":"A deep knowledge of agriculture is expected of applicants.","zh":"對申請人有所要求的是，他們需對農業有深入認識。"},{"en":"Be expected of someone means be required or considered necessary for that person.","zh":"be expected of someone 指某事被要求或被視為該人必須具備。"},{"en":"Professional behaviour is expected of all employees.","zh":"對所有員工都有專業行為的要求。"},{"en":"If knowledge is expected of applicants, they should already have it before applying.","zh":"如果對申請人有某種知識要求，他們申請前應已具備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a requirement or standard.","zh":"這個短語描述要求或標準。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"applicants","meaning":"申請人","examples":[{"en":"Applicants need knowledge of the agricultural sector.","zh":"申請人需要具備農業界知識。"},{"en":"Applicants are people who apply for a job, course, or opportunity.","zh":"applicants 指申請工作、課程或機會的人。"},{"en":"Applicants should send a CV and cover letter before the deadline.","zh":"申請人應在截止日期前提交履歷和求職信。"},{"en":"Employers compare applicants to find the strongest candidate.","zh":"僱主會比較申請人以找出最強候選人。"},{"en":"This word describes people seeking a position or place.","zh":"這個字描述尋求職位或名額的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"leading supermarket","meaning":"主要超市","examples":[{"en":"A leading supermarket is looking for a fresh produce buyer.","zh":"一間主要超市正在尋找新鮮農產品採購員。"},{"en":"A leading supermarket is a major, successful, or well-known supermarket company.","zh":"leading supermarket 指大型、成功或知名的超市公司。"},{"en":"Working for a leading supermarket may give buyers strong industry experience.","zh":"為主要超市工作可能給採購員很強的行業經驗。"},{"en":"Leading supermarkets often have high standards for quality and supply.","zh":"主要超市通常對質素和供應有很高標準。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a prominent supermarket business.","zh":"這個短語描述具影響力的超市企業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fresh produce buyer","meaning":"新鮮農產品採購員","examples":[{"en":"A fresh produce buyer is needed for a maternity cover contract.","zh":"一份產假替工合約需要新鮮農產品採購員。"},{"en":"A fresh produce buyer chooses and purchases fruit, vegetables, and other fresh food for a business.","zh":"fresh produce buyer 指為企業選購水果、蔬菜和其他新鮮食品的人。"},{"en":"The buyer must understand quality, price, season, and supplier reliability.","zh":"採購員必須了解質素、價格、季節和供應商可靠性。"},{"en":"This role affects what fresh food customers see in supermarkets.","zh":"這個角色會影響顧客在超市看到的新鮮食品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a purchasing role in fresh food.","zh":"這個短語描述新鮮食品採購職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be available for","meaning":"可應徵；可接受……","examples":[{"en":"The buyer must be available for a 12-month contract.","zh":"採購員必須可接受一份12個月合約。"},{"en":"Be available for something means be free and able to accept or take part in it.","zh":"be available for something 指有空並能夠接受或參與某事。"},{"en":"A candidate may need to be available for interviews next week.","zh":"候選人可能需要下星期可應徵面試。"},{"en":"If a worker is available for a contract, they can commit to that period.","zh":"如果工人可接受某合約，他就能承諾該段時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes time availability and readiness.","zh":"這個短語描述時間上的可行性和準備程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"maternity cover contract","meaning":"產假替工合約","examples":[{"en":"The job is a 12-month maternity cover contract.","zh":"這份工作是一份12個月產假替工合約。"},{"en":"A maternity cover contract is a temporary job replacing someone who is away on maternity leave.","zh":"maternity cover contract 指臨時接替正在放產假的員工的合約工作。"},{"en":"A school may hire a teacher on a maternity cover contract for one year.","zh":"學校可能聘請教師以產假替工合約工作一年。"},{"en":"This kind of contract has a fixed period because the original employee is expected to return.","zh":"這類合約有固定期限，因為原本員工預期會回來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes temporary cover for parental leave.","zh":"這個短語描述為產假提供的臨時替工安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"experience in","meaning":"在……方面的經驗","examples":[{"en":"Applicants need experience in administration, planning and buying.","zh":"申請人需要在行政、規劃和採購方面的經驗。"},{"en":"Experience in something means practical knowledge gained by doing that type of work.","zh":"experience in something 指透過做某類工作而取得的實際知識。"},{"en":"A sales manager needs experience in customer service and team leadership.","zh":"銷售經理需要在客戶服務和團隊領導方面的經驗。"},{"en":"Experience helps employers trust that applicants can handle the job.","zh":"經驗幫助僱主相信申請人能應付工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relevant work background.","zh":"這個短語描述相關工作背景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"administration","meaning":"行政","examples":[{"en":"The buyer needs experience in administration.","zh":"採購員需要行政經驗。"},{"en":"Administration means organising records, documents, communication, schedules, and office tasks.","zh":"administration 指組織紀錄、文件、溝通、時間表和辦公室任務。"},{"en":"Farm businesses need good administration to manage orders and invoices.","zh":"農場企業需要良好行政來管理訂單和發票。"},{"en":"Strong administration keeps a workplace organised and efficient.","zh":"強大的行政工作能令工作場所有組織且有效率。"},{"en":"This word describes office and organisational work.","zh":"這個字描述辦公室和組織工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"planning and buying","meaning":"規劃及採購","examples":[{"en":"The job requires experience in planning and buying.","zh":"這份工作要求規劃及採購經驗。"},{"en":"Planning and buying means organising future needs and purchasing the right products.","zh":"planning and buying 指安排未來需要並購買合適產品。"},{"en":"A supermarket buyer uses planning and buying to make sure shelves have enough fresh food.","zh":"超市採購員使用規劃及採購能力，確保貨架有足夠新鮮食品。"},{"en":"Poor planning and buying can lead to waste or shortages.","zh":"規劃及採購不足會導致浪費或短缺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two key commercial skills.","zh":"這個短語描述兩項關鍵商業技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fresh produce industry","meaning":"新鮮農產品行業","examples":[{"en":"The buyer needs experience in the fresh produce industry.","zh":"採購員需要新鮮農產品行業經驗。"},{"en":"The fresh produce industry deals with fruit, vegetables, salads, herbs, and similar fresh foods.","zh":"fresh produce industry 涉及水果、蔬菜、沙律、香草和類似新鮮食品。"},{"en":"People in the fresh produce industry must understand seasonality and shelf life.","zh":"新鮮農產品行業的人必須了解季節性和保鮮期。"},{"en":"This industry moves quickly because products can spoil.","zh":"這個行業運作很快，因為產品會變壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the business area of fresh fruit and vegetables.","zh":"這個短語描述新鮮水果和蔬菜的商業範疇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in return","meaning":"作為回報","examples":[{"en":"In return, the successful applicant will receive a competitive salary.","zh":"作為回報，成功申請人會獲得具競爭力的薪酬。"},{"en":"In return means as a reward or exchange for what someone gives or does.","zh":"in return 指作為某人付出或所做事情的回報或交換。"},{"en":"The job requires long hours; in return, it offers excellent training.","zh":"這份工作要求長工時；作為回報，它提供優秀培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what someone receives for their effort.","zh":"這個短語引出某人因努力而得到的東西。"},{"en":"It describes exchange or compensation.","zh":"它描述交換或補償。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"competitive salary","meaning":"具競爭力的薪酬","examples":[{"en":"The job offers a very competitive salary.","zh":"這份工作提供非常具競爭力的薪酬。"},{"en":"A competitive salary is pay that is attractive compared with similar jobs.","zh":"competitive salary 指與類似工作相比具吸引力的薪酬。"},{"en":"Employers offer competitive salaries to attract strong applicants.","zh":"僱主提供具競爭力的薪酬以吸引強申請人。"},{"en":"A competitive salary may include good pay, benefits, or bonuses.","zh":"具競爭力的薪酬可能包括良好薪金、福利或獎金。"},{"en":"This phrase describes salary that compares well in the market.","zh":"這個短語描述在市場上有優勢的薪酬。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"receive a request for","meaning":"收到……的招聘要求","examples":[{"en":"The agency has received a request for a sales manager.","zh":"代理公司收到一個銷售經理的招聘要求。"},{"en":"Receive a request for something means get an official or informal demand asking for it.","zh":"receive a request for something 指收到正式或非正式要求某物的請求。"},{"en":"A recruitment agency may receive a request for temporary farm workers.","zh":"招聘公司可能收到臨時農場工人的招聘要求。"},{"en":"When an agency receives a request, it starts looking for suitable candidates.","zh":"當代理公司收到要求，就會開始尋找合適候選人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being asked to provide something.","zh":"這個短語描述被要求提供某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sales manager","meaning":"銷售經理","examples":[{"en":"A chain of garden centres needs a sales manager.","zh":"一間連鎖園藝中心需要銷售經理。"},{"en":"A sales manager is responsible for leading sales staff and increasing sales.","zh":"sales manager 指負責帶領銷售員工並提升銷售的人。"},{"en":"A sales manager may train staff, check targets, and visit different branches.","zh":"銷售經理可能培訓員工、檢查目標並到訪不同分店。"},{"en":"Good sales managers need communication, planning, and customer service skills.","zh":"好銷售經理需要溝通、規劃和客戶服務技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a management role in selling products or services.","zh":"這個短語描述銷售產品或服務的管理職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"chain of","meaning":"連鎖……","examples":[{"en":"The sales manager will work for a chain of garden centres.","zh":"銷售經理將為一間連鎖園藝中心工作。"},{"en":"A chain of businesses means several shops or centres owned or managed by the same company.","zh":"chain of businesses 指由同一公司擁有或管理的多間店舖或中心。"},{"en":"A chain of cafés may have branches in many towns.","zh":"連鎖咖啡店可能在許多城鎮有分店。"},{"en":"Working for a chain may involve visiting different locations.","zh":"為連鎖企業工作可能涉及到訪不同地點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a group of connected businesses.","zh":"這個短語描述一組相連企業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"garden centres","meaning":"園藝中心","examples":[{"en":"The company runs a chain of garden centres.","zh":"這間公司營運一系列園藝中心。"},{"en":"Garden centres are shops that sell plants, gardening tools, compost, pots, and outdoor products.","zh":"garden centres 指售賣植物、園藝工具、堆肥、花盆和戶外用品的商店。"},{"en":"Customers visit garden centres to buy flowers, shrubs, and advice for their gardens.","zh":"顧客到園藝中心購買花卉、灌木和園藝建議。"},{"en":"Garden centres may also sell furniture, seeds, and seasonal decorations.","zh":"園藝中心也可能售賣家具、種子和季節裝飾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes retail businesses for gardening.","zh":"這個短語描述園藝零售業務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"visit centres in the region","meaning":"到訪區內各中心","examples":[{"en":"The sales manager will visit centres in the region.","zh":"銷售經理會到訪區內各中心。"},{"en":"To visit centres in the region means to travel to different branches or sites in a particular area.","zh":"visit centres in the region 指前往某地區內不同分店或地點。"},{"en":"A regional manager may visit centres in the region to check staff and sales.","zh":"區域經理可能到訪區內各中心，檢查員工和銷售。"},{"en":"Visiting branches helps managers understand local problems.","zh":"到訪分店幫助經理了解本地問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes travelling around a work area.","zh":"這個短語描述在工作區域內四處走訪。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ensure that","meaning":"確保……","examples":[{"en":"The manager must ensure that customer service standards are maintained.","zh":"經理必須確保客戶服務標準得以維持。"},{"en":"Ensure that means make certain that something happens or remains true.","zh":"ensure that 指確保某事發生或保持真實。"},{"en":"A teacher must ensure that all pupils understand the safety rules.","zh":"老師必須確保所有學生明白安全規則。"},{"en":"Managers ensure quality by checking systems and correcting problems.","zh":"經理透過檢查系統和糾正問題來確保質素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes responsibility for making something certain.","zh":"這個短語描述確保某事的責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"high levels of customer service","meaning":"高水平客戶服務","examples":[{"en":"The centres must maintain high levels of customer service.","zh":"這些中心必須維持高水平客戶服務。"},{"en":"High levels of customer service mean very good help, advice, politeness, and support for customers.","zh":"high levels of customer service 指為顧客提供很好的幫助、建議、禮貌和支援。"},{"en":"Garden centres need high levels of customer service because customers often ask for plant advice.","zh":"園藝中心需要高水平客戶服務，因為顧客常詢問植物建議。"},{"en":"Good customer service can make people return to the same shop.","zh":"良好客戶服務可以令人再次光顧同一間店。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong service quality.","zh":"這個短語描述優質服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be maintained","meaning":"得以維持","examples":[{"en":"High levels of customer service must be maintained.","zh":"高水平客戶服務必須得以維持。"},{"en":"Be maintained means be kept at the same good level or condition.","zh":"be maintained 指保持在同樣良好水平或狀態。"},{"en":"Safety standards must be maintained throughout the event.","zh":"安全標準必須在整個活動中得以維持。"},{"en":"If quality is not maintained, customers may lose trust.","zh":"如果質素未能維持，顧客可能失去信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping something stable and good.","zh":"這個短語描述保持某事穩定和良好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be prepared to","meaning":"願意……","examples":[{"en":"The post is suitable for someone prepared to live in the region.","zh":"這個職位適合願意居於該地區的人。"},{"en":"Be prepared to do something means be willing and ready to do it.","zh":"be prepared to do something 指願意並準備好做某事。"},{"en":"A farm worker must be prepared to start early in the morning.","zh":"農場工人必須願意清晨開始工作。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests acceptance of a condition before taking a job.","zh":"這個短語暗示接受工作前願意接受某條件。"},{"en":"It describes willingness and readiness.","zh":"它描述意願和準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"live in the region","meaning":"居於該地區","examples":[{"en":"The sales manager must be prepared to live in the region.","zh":"銷售經理必須願意居於該地區。"},{"en":"To live in the region means to have your home in that particular area.","zh":"live in the region 指在該特定地區居住。"},{"en":"A regional sales role may require the employee to live in the region they manage.","zh":"區域銷售職位可能要求員工居於自己管理的地區。"},{"en":"Living locally can make travel between centres easier.","zh":"居住在本地可以令中心之間的往來更方便。"},{"en":"This phrase describes residence in a work area.","zh":"這個短語描述住在工作區域內。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"vacancy for","meaning":"……的空缺","examples":[{"en":"There is also a vacancy for a tree technician.","zh":"也有一個樹木技術員的空缺。"},{"en":"A vacancy for a role means an open job position that needs to be filled.","zh":"vacancy for a role 指需要填補的職位空缺。"},{"en":"A school may have a vacancy for a science teacher.","zh":"學校可能有科學老師的空缺。"},{"en":"When there is a vacancy, suitable applicants can apply.","zh":"當有空缺時，合適申請人可以申請。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an available job.","zh":"這個短語描述可申請工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tree technician","meaning":"樹木技術員","examples":[{"en":"The company needs a tree technician for forestry and conservation work.","zh":"公司需要一名樹木技術員負責林業和保育工作。"},{"en":"A tree technician is a trained worker who inspects, maintains, cuts, or cares for trees.","zh":"tree technician 指受過訓練、檢查、保養、修剪或照顧樹木的工人。"},{"en":"Tree technicians may climb trees, use cutting tools, and check tree health.","zh":"樹木技術員可能攀樹、使用切割工具並檢查樹木健康。"},{"en":"Their work can protect people, property, and woodland habitats.","zh":"他們的工作可以保護人、財產和林地棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a skilled tree-care role.","zh":"這個短語描述具技能的樹木護理職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"carry out","meaning":"進行；執行","examples":[{"en":"The tree technician will carry out tree cutting and conservation work.","zh":"樹木技術員會進行樹木修剪和保育工作。"},{"en":"To carry out work means to do or perform it.","zh":"carry out work 指做或執行該工作。"},{"en":"Workers carry out safety checks before using machinery.","zh":"工人在使用機器前會進行安全檢查。"},{"en":"Carrying out a task properly requires training and care.","zh":"正確執行任務需要培訓和小心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes performing duties or procedures.","zh":"這個短語描述履行職責或程序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tree cutting","meaning":"樹木修剪；砍樹工作","examples":[{"en":"The tree technician will carry out tree cutting.","zh":"樹木技術員會進行樹木修剪工作。"},{"en":"Tree cutting means cutting branches or parts of trees, sometimes for safety or maintenance.","zh":"tree cutting 指切割樹枝或樹木部分，有時為安全或保養需要。"},{"en":"Tree cutting may be needed when branches grow too close to roads or buildings.","zh":"當樹枝長得太接近道路或建築物時，可能需要樹木修剪。"},{"en":"This work must be done safely because falling branches can be dangerous.","zh":"這項工作必須安全進行，因為掉落樹枝可能危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical tree-management work.","zh":"這個短語描述實際樹木管理工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"forestry","meaning":"林業","examples":[{"en":"The vacancy involves forestry and conservation work.","zh":"這個空缺涉及林業和保育工作。"},{"en":"Forestry is the management, planting, care, and use of forests.","zh":"forestry 指森林的管理、種植、護理和使用。"},{"en":"Forestry workers may plant trees, manage woodland, and protect habitats.","zh":"林業工人可能種樹、管理林地並保護棲息地。"},{"en":"Good forestry balances timber use with environmental protection.","zh":"良好林業會平衡木材使用和環境保護。"},{"en":"This word describes forest-related work and science.","zh":"這個字描述與森林相關的工作和科學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"conservation work","meaning":"保育工作","examples":[{"en":"The tree technician will carry out conservation work.","zh":"樹木技術員會進行保育工作。"},{"en":"Conservation work means protecting nature, wildlife, landscapes, or historic resources.","zh":"conservation work 指保護自然、野生動物、景觀或歷史資源的工作。"},{"en":"Conservation work may involve planting native trees or protecting rare habitats.","zh":"保育工作可能涉及種植本地樹木或保護稀有棲息地。"},{"en":"This work helps maintain the environment for future generations.","zh":"這項工作幫助為下一代維持環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical environmental protection.","zh":"這個短語描述實際環境保護工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"candidates must have","meaning":"申請人必須具備……","examples":[{"en":"Candidates must have a clean driving licence.","zh":"申請人必須具備無違規紀錄駕駛執照。"},{"en":"Candidates must have means applicants are required to possess something.","zh":"candidates must have 指申請人被要求擁有某物。"},{"en":"Candidates must have first-aid training for this outdoor role.","zh":"申請人必須具備急救培訓，才能申請這個戶外職位。"},{"en":"If candidates must have a qualification, those without it may not be considered.","zh":"如果申請人必須具備某資格，沒有該資格的人可能不獲考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a job requirement.","zh":"這個短語引出工作要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"clean driving licence","meaning":"無違規紀錄駕駛執照","examples":[{"en":"Candidates must have a clean driving licence.","zh":"申請人必須持有無違規紀錄駕駛執照。"},{"en":"A clean driving licence is a driving licence with no serious offences or penalty points.","zh":"clean driving licence 指沒有嚴重違規或扣分紀錄的駕駛執照。"},{"en":"Employers may ask for a clean driving licence if workers need to drive company vehicles.","zh":"如果員工需要駕駛公司車輛，僱主可能要求無違規紀錄駕駛執照。"},{"en":"A clean record suggests the driver is responsible and safe.","zh":"乾淨紀錄顯示司機負責任且安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a licence without problematic driving history.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有問題駕駛歷史的執照。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"training in","meaning":"……方面的培訓","examples":[{"en":"Candidates must have training in safety procedures.","zh":"申請人必須有安全程序方面的培訓。"},{"en":"Training in something means instruction and practice in that skill or subject.","zh":"training in something 指在某技能或題目上的指導和練習。"},{"en":"Tree technicians need training in using cutting equipment safely.","zh":"樹木技術員需要安全使用切割設備方面的培訓。"},{"en":"Training helps workers understand risks before doing dangerous tasks.","zh":"培訓幫助工人在做危險任務前了解風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparation in a specific area.","zh":"這個短語描述某特定範疇的準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"safety procedures","meaning":"安全程序","examples":[{"en":"The company requires training in safety procedures.","zh":"公司要求安全程序方面的培訓。"},{"en":"Safety procedures are rules and steps designed to prevent accidents or injury.","zh":"safety procedures 指為防止意外或受傷而設的規則和步驟。"},{"en":"Workers must follow safety procedures when using chainsaws or tractors.","zh":"工人使用電鋸或拖拉機時必須遵守安全程序。"},{"en":"Ignoring safety procedures can put workers and the public at risk.","zh":"忽視安全程序會令工人和公眾面臨風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised safety rules.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的安全規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"would be preferred","meaning":"較為優先","examples":[{"en":"A year’s experience would be preferred.","zh":"有一年經驗會較為優先。"},{"en":"Would be preferred means would be liked or considered better, but may not be absolutely required.","zh":"would be preferred 指會較受歡迎或被視為較佳，但未必絕對必需。"},{"en":"Experience with farm machinery would be preferred for this role.","zh":"有農業機械經驗對這個職位會較為優先。"},{"en":"Preferred qualifications can make an applicant stronger.","zh":"優先條件可以令申請人更有競爭力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an advantage rather than a strict requirement.","zh":"這個短語描述優勢，而不是硬性要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be prepared to consider","meaning":"願意考慮……","examples":[{"en":"The company might be prepared to consider a newly trained applicant.","zh":"公司可能願意考慮剛受訓的申請人。"},{"en":"Be prepared to consider means be willing to think seriously about accepting someone or something.","zh":"be prepared to consider 指願意認真考慮接受某人或某事。"},{"en":"An employer may be prepared to consider candidates without experience if they have strong training.","zh":"如果候選人有紮實培訓，僱主可能願意考慮沒有經驗的人。"},{"en":"This phrase gives hope but does not promise acceptance.","zh":"這個短語給予希望，但不承諾一定接受。"},{"en":"It describes openness to a possibility.","zh":"它描述對可能性的開放態度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"just completed","meaning":"剛剛完成","examples":[{"en":"The company may consider someone who has just completed a training course.","zh":"公司可能考慮剛剛完成培訓課程的人。"},{"en":"Just completed means finished very recently.","zh":"just completed 指最近剛完成。"},{"en":"A candidate who has just completed an agricultural course may still need workplace experience.","zh":"剛剛完成農業課程的候選人可能仍需要工作經驗。"},{"en":"Recent training can show current knowledge and motivation.","zh":"近期培訓可以顯示最新知識和動機。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very recent completion.","zh":"這個短語描述非常近期的完成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"appropriate training course","meaning":"合適培訓課程","examples":[{"en":"The applicant should have completed an appropriate training course.","zh":"申請人應已完成合適培訓課程。"},{"en":"An appropriate training course is a course that matches the skills and safety needs of the job.","zh":"appropriate training course 指符合工作技能和安全需要的課程。"},{"en":"A tree technician needs an appropriate training course in climbing and cutting safely.","zh":"樹木技術員需要合適培訓課程，學習安全攀爬和切割。"},{"en":"Not every course is appropriate for every role.","zh":"不是每個課程都適合每個職位。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relevant and suitable training.","zh":"這個短語描述相關而合適的培訓。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"farm worker","meaning":"農場工人","examples":[{"en":"The final position is for a farm worker.","zh":"最後一個職位是農場工人。"},{"en":"A farm worker is a person who carries out practical work on a farm.","zh":"farm worker 指在農場進行實際工作的人。"},{"en":"Farm workers may feed animals, sow crops, harvest produce, and maintain machines.","zh":"農場工人可能餵飼動物、播種、收割農產品和保養機器。"},{"en":"This role often requires physical work and outdoor conditions.","zh":"這個角色通常需要體力勞動和面對戶外環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a general agricultural labour role.","zh":"這個短語描述一般農業勞動職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"involve a wide range of","meaning":"涉及各種……","examples":[{"en":"The farm worker role will involve a wide range of farm duties.","zh":"農場工人角色會涉及各種農場職務。"},{"en":"Involve a wide range of something means include many different types of tasks or responsibilities.","zh":"involve a wide range of something 指包括許多不同類型的任務或責任。"},{"en":"A countryside job may involve a wide range of outdoor duties.","zh":"鄉郊工作可能涉及各種戶外職務。"},{"en":"A wide range of tasks can make a job varied but demanding.","zh":"各種任務可以令工作多變，但也要求高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad and varied responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛而多樣的責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"farm duties","meaning":"農場職務","examples":[{"en":"The job involves a wide range of farm duties.","zh":"這份工作涉及各種農場職務。"},{"en":"Farm duties are tasks that need to be done to keep a farm working.","zh":"farm duties 指維持農場運作所需完成的任務。"},{"en":"Farm duties may include feeding animals, repairing fences, sowing crops, and cleaning equipment.","zh":"農場職務可能包括餵飼動物、修理圍欄、播種和清潔設備。"},{"en":"These duties can change with the season and weather.","zh":"這些職務會隨季節和天氣改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes everyday farm responsibilities.","zh":"這個短語描述日常農場責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"crop sowing and harvesting","meaning":"播種及收割","examples":[{"en":"The duties include crop sowing and harvesting.","zh":"職務包括播種及收割。"},{"en":"Crop sowing and harvesting means planting seeds and later collecting the mature crops.","zh":"crop sowing and harvesting 指播下種子，之後收集成熟作物。"},{"en":"Farm workers may sow crops in spring and harvest them in late summer.","zh":"農場工人可能在春天播種，夏末收割。"},{"en":"These tasks are central to food production.","zh":"這些任務是食品生產的核心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning and end stages of crop growing.","zh":"這個短語描述作物生長的開始和結束階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"machine maintenance","meaning":"機器保養","examples":[{"en":"The farm worker will help with machine maintenance.","zh":"農場工人會協助機器保養。"},{"en":"Machine maintenance means checking, cleaning, repairing, and looking after machines.","zh":"machine maintenance 指檢查、清潔、維修和照顧機器。"},{"en":"Tractors need regular machine maintenance to work safely.","zh":"拖拉機需要定期機器保養才能安全運作。"},{"en":"Poor maintenance can lead to breakdowns and accidents.","zh":"保養不足會導致故障和意外。"},{"en":"This phrase describes care of equipment.","zh":"這個短語描述設備護理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"animal care","meaning":"動物照料","examples":[{"en":"The farm worker will also be responsible for animal care.","zh":"農場工人也會負責動物照料。"},{"en":"Animal care means feeding, cleaning, checking, and protecting animals.","zh":"animal care 指餵飼、清潔、檢查和保護動物。"},{"en":"Farm animal care may involve giving water, checking health, and cleaning shelters.","zh":"農場動物照料可能涉及供水、檢查健康和清潔住所。"},{"en":"Good animal care is important for welfare and farm productivity.","zh":"良好動物照料對動物福利和農場生產力都很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical responsibility for animals.","zh":"這個短語描述對動物的實際責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"perks of the job","meaning":"這份工作的額外福利","examples":[{"en":"Perks of the job include the possibility of renting a cottage.","zh":"這份工作的額外福利包括可能租住一間小屋。"},{"en":"Perks of the job are extra benefits that come with a role, apart from salary.","zh":"perks of the job 指薪酬以外隨職位而來的額外好處。"},{"en":"Free meals, travel allowance, or accommodation can be perks of the job.","zh":"免費膳食、交通津貼或住宿都可以是工作額外福利。"},{"en":"Perks can make a job more attractive to applicants.","zh":"額外福利可以令工作對申請人更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes additional advantages of employment.","zh":"這個短語描述就業的附加好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"include the possibility of","meaning":"包括……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"The perks include the possibility of renting a small cottage.","zh":"額外福利包括租住一間小屋的可能性。"},{"en":"Include the possibility of means contain a chance that something may happen, though it is not guaranteed.","zh":"include the possibility of 指包含某事可能發生的機會，但不保證。"},{"en":"The contract may include the possibility of extension after one year.","zh":"合約可能包括一年後續約的可能性。"},{"en":"This phrase is careful because it offers a chance, not a promise.","zh":"這個短語語氣謹慎，因為它提供機會而不是承諾。"},{"en":"It describes a possible benefit.","zh":"它描述可能的好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rent a small cottage","meaning":"租住一間小屋","examples":[{"en":"The farm worker may be able to rent a small cottage on the estate.","zh":"農場工人可能能夠在莊園內租住一間小屋。"},{"en":"To rent a small cottage means to pay money regularly to live in a small countryside house.","zh":"rent a small cottage 指定期付款居住在一間小型鄉村房屋。"},{"en":"Some farm workers rent cottages near their workplace to avoid long travel.","zh":"有些農場工人租住工作地點附近的小屋，以避免長途交通。"},{"en":"A cottage on the estate can make rural work more convenient.","zh":"莊園內的小屋可以令鄉郊工作更方便。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a housing option.","zh":"這個短語描述住屋選項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"on the estate","meaning":"在莊園內；在農場範圍內","examples":[{"en":"The cottage is on the estate.","zh":"小屋位於莊園內。"},{"en":"On the estate means located within the land owned or managed as one property.","zh":"on the estate 指位於同一物業擁有或管理的土地範圍內。"},{"en":"Farm workers may live on the estate so they can reach animals and fields quickly.","zh":"農場工人可能住在莊園內，以便快速到達動物和田地。"},{"en":"An estate may include houses, farmland, woods, and farm buildings.","zh":"莊園可能包括房屋、農地、樹林和農場建築。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location within a large property.","zh":"這個短語描述大型物業範圍內的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the chance to earn","meaning":"賺取……的機會","examples":[{"en":"The job offers the chance to earn a competitive salary.","zh":"這份工作提供賺取具競爭力薪酬的機會。"},{"en":"The chance to earn means the opportunity to receive money through work.","zh":"chance to earn 指透過工作獲得金錢的機會。"},{"en":"Seasonal farm work may give students the chance to earn money during holidays.","zh":"季節性農場工作可能給學生在假期賺錢的機會。"},{"en":"A chance to earn a good salary can make a difficult job more attractive.","zh":"賺取良好薪酬的機會可以令困難工作更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an income opportunity.","zh":"這個短語描述收入機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"tractor driving experience","meaning":"駕駛拖拉機經驗","examples":[{"en":"Tractor driving experience is essential for the farm worker role.","zh":"駕駛拖拉機經驗對農場工人職位必不可少。"},{"en":"Tractor driving experience means practical experience in operating a tractor safely.","zh":"tractor driving experience 指安全操作拖拉機的實際經驗。"},{"en":"Farm workers with tractor driving experience can help with transport, ploughing, and heavy tasks.","zh":"有駕駛拖拉機經驗的農場工人可以協助運輸、犁田和重型任務。"},{"en":"Employers may require this experience because tractors are powerful machines.","zh":"僱主可能要求這項經驗，因為拖拉機是強力機器。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific farming skill.","zh":"這個短語描述特定農業技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be essential","meaning":"必不可少","examples":[{"en":"A driving licence and tractor driving experience are essential.","zh":"駕駛執照和駕駛拖拉機經驗必不可少。"},{"en":"Be essential means be absolutely necessary.","zh":"be essential 指絕對必要。"},{"en":"Safety training is essential for workers who use cutting equipment.","zh":"對使用切割設備的工人來說，安全培訓必不可少。"},{"en":"If a requirement is essential, applicants without it may not be suitable.","zh":"如果某要求必不可少，沒有該要求的申請人可能不合適。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that cannot be left out.","zh":"這個短語描述不能缺少的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 18/task-3":[{"front":"get some ideas together","meaning":"整理一些想法","examples":[{"en":"Adam and Rosie try to get some ideas together for their presentation.","zh":"Adam 和 Rosie 嘗試為他們的簡報整理一些想法。"},{"en":"To get some ideas together means to collect and organise possible points before doing a task.","zh":"get some ideas together 指在做任務前收集並整理可能的重點。"},{"en":"The group met after school to get some ideas together for the debate.","zh":"小組放學後見面，為辯論整理一些想法。"},{"en":"If students get ideas together early, their presentation will be easier to plan.","zh":"如果學生及早整理想法，簡報會更容易規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first stage of planning.","zh":"這個短語描述計劃的初始階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"presentation on","meaning":"關於……的簡報","examples":[{"en":"The students are preparing a presentation on diet and obesity.","zh":"學生正在準備一個關於飲食與肥胖的簡報。"},{"en":"A presentation on a topic is a talk that explains information about that subject.","zh":"presentation on a topic 指解釋某主題資料的演講或匯報。"},{"en":"The class gave a presentation on climate change and recycling.","zh":"這班學生作了一個關於氣候變化和回收的簡報。"},{"en":"If a presentation on a topic is well organised, listeners can follow the ideas clearly.","zh":"如果關於某題目的簡報組織良好，聽眾就能清楚跟上想法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the subject of a presentation.","zh":"這個短語引出簡報的主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"diet and obesity","meaning":"飲食與肥胖","examples":[{"en":"The presentation is about diet and obesity.","zh":"這個簡報是關於飲食與肥胖。"},{"en":"Diet and obesity refers to the relationship between what people eat and excessive body weight.","zh":"diet and obesity 指人們的飲食與過重或肥胖之間的關係。"},{"en":"Doctors often discuss diet and obesity when advising people on health.","zh":"醫生給予健康建議時，常會討論飲食與肥胖。"},{"en":"If a presentation covers diet and obesity, it may include food choices, calories, and exercise.","zh":"如果簡報涵蓋飲食與肥胖，可能包括食物選擇、卡路里和運動。"},{"en":"This phrase combines nutrition with a public health issue.","zh":"這個短語把營養與公共健康問題結合起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"talk about","meaning":"談及","examples":[{"en":"Adam can talk about the experiment he did.","zh":"Adam 可以談及他做過的實驗。"},{"en":"To talk about something means to discuss or explain it.","zh":"talk about something 指討論或解釋某事。"},{"en":"The teacher asked students to talk about their favourite book.","zh":"老師要求學生談及自己最喜歡的書。"},{"en":"If Adam talks about his experiment, he can explain the method and results.","zh":"如果 Adam 談及他的實驗，他可以解釋方法和結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for introducing a topic in speech.","zh":"這個短語適合用來引入演講中的話題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"do an experiment","meaning":"做實驗","examples":[{"en":"Adam did an experiment on sugar and artificial sweeteners.","zh":"Adam 做了一個關於糖和人工甜味劑的實驗。"},{"en":"To do an experiment means to carry out a test to discover or prove something.","zh":"do an experiment 指進行測試，以發現或證明某事。"},{"en":"Students did an experiment to see which material kept water warmest.","zh":"學生做實驗，看看哪種材料最能保溫。"},{"en":"If you do an experiment carefully, your results are more reliable.","zh":"如果你仔細做實驗，結果會更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical scientific investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述實際科學探究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tell the difference between","meaning":"分辨……之間的差別","examples":[{"en":"Adam wanted to see if people could tell the difference between sugar and sweeteners.","zh":"Adam 想看看人們能否分辨糖和甜味劑之間的差別。"},{"en":"To tell the difference between two things means to recognise how they are not the same.","zh":"tell the difference between two things 指辨認兩者有何不同。"},{"en":"Some people cannot tell the difference between two similar perfumes.","zh":"有些人不能分辨兩種相似香水之間的差別。"},{"en":"If participants can tell the difference, the two drinks probably taste noticeably different.","zh":"如果參加者能分辨差別，兩種飲品的味道很可能明顯不同。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on identifying contrast.","zh":"這個短語重點在辨認對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"real sugar","meaning":"真糖","examples":[{"en":"The experiment compared real sugar with artificial sweeteners.","zh":"這個實驗比較真糖和人工甜味劑。"},{"en":"Real sugar means natural sugar rather than a sugar substitute.","zh":"real sugar 指天然或普通糖，而不是代糖。"},{"en":"Some people prefer tea with real sugar because they dislike the taste of sweeteners.","zh":"有些人較喜歡加真糖的茶，因為不喜歡甜味劑的味道。"},{"en":"If a drink contains real sugar, it usually has more calories than one with sweeteners.","zh":"如果飲品含真糖，通常比含甜味劑的飲品有更多卡路里。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts ordinary sugar with artificial alternatives.","zh":"這個短語把普通糖與人工替代品作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"artificial sweeteners","meaning":"人工甜味劑","examples":[{"en":"The drinks contained either sugar or artificial sweeteners.","zh":"飲品含有糖或人工甜味劑其中一種。"},{"en":"Artificial sweeteners are substances used to make food or drinks taste sweet without using ordinary sugar.","zh":"artificial sweeteners 指用來令食物或飲品有甜味、但不是普通糖的物質。"},{"en":"Diet drinks often use artificial sweeteners to reduce calories.","zh":"健怡飲品常使用人工甜味劑來減少卡路里。"},{"en":"If people dislike the aftertaste of artificial sweeteners, they may choose real sugar instead.","zh":"如果人們不喜歡人工甜味劑的餘味，可能會選擇真糖。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to sugar substitutes.","zh":"這個短語指代糖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"drinks with either","meaning":"含有其中一種……的飲品","examples":[{"en":"Adam gave people drinks with either sugar or artificial sweeteners.","zh":"Adam 給人們含有糖或人工甜味劑其中一種的飲品。"},{"en":"Drinks with either one thing or another contain one of two possible ingredients.","zh":"drinks with either one thing or another 指飲品含有兩種可能材料中的其中一種。"},{"en":"The teacher gave students cups with either lemon juice or vinegar for a taste test.","zh":"老師給學生含有檸檬汁或醋其中一種的杯子作味覺測試。"},{"en":"If participants receive drinks with either sugar or sweeteners, they must identify which one it is.","zh":"如果參加者收到含糖或甜味劑其中一種的飲品，就必須辨認是哪一種。"},{"en":"This phrase shows two possible alternatives.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個可能選項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have to say which","meaning":"必須說出是哪一種","examples":[{"en":"The participants had to say which drink they thought it was.","zh":"參加者必須說出他們認為那是哪一種飲品。"},{"en":"To have to say which means to be required to choose or identify one option.","zh":"have to say which 指被要求選擇或辨認其中一個選項。"},{"en":"In the listening test, students had to say which speaker agreed with the statement.","zh":"在聆聽測驗中，學生必須說出哪位講者同意該陳述。"},{"en":"If participants have to say which drink they tasted, guessing may affect the results.","zh":"如果參加者必須說出喝到哪種飲品，猜測可能影響結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a required choice.","zh":"這個短語描述必須作出的選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"take someone ages to","meaning":"花了某人很長時間去……","examples":[{"en":"It took Adam ages to decide how to organise the experiment.","zh":"Adam 花了很長時間去決定如何安排實驗。"},{"en":"To take someone ages to do something means to take that person a very long time.","zh":"take someone ages to do something 指某人花很長時間做某事。"},{"en":"It took me ages to understand the new timetable.","zh":"我花了很長時間才理解新時間表。"},{"en":"If it takes someone ages to plan an experiment, the design is probably complicated.","zh":"如果某人花很長時間規劃實驗，設計很可能很複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and emphasises a long time.","zh":"這個短語較口語，強調時間很長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"decide exactly how","meaning":"確切決定如何……","examples":[{"en":"Adam had to decide exactly how he would organise the experiment.","zh":"Adam 必須確切決定如何安排實驗。"},{"en":"To decide exactly how means to choose the precise method or arrangement.","zh":"decide exactly how 指選定精確的方法或安排。"},{"en":"The group had to decide exactly how they would divide the presentation.","zh":"小組必須確切決定如何分配簡報內容。"},{"en":"If researchers decide exactly how to collect data, the results will be clearer.","zh":"如果研究人員確切決定如何收集數據，結果會更清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses detailed planning.","zh":"這個短語強調詳細規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"organise it","meaning":"安排它","examples":[{"en":"Adam found it difficult to organise the experiment.","zh":"Adam 覺得安排這個實驗很困難。"},{"en":"To organise it means to arrange the details, order, people, and materials needed for a task.","zh":"organise it 指安排任務所需的細節、次序、人員和材料。"},{"en":"The teacher helped the students organise their survey.","zh":"老師協助學生安排他們的問卷調查。"},{"en":"If an experiment is not organised well, information may be lost.","zh":"如果實驗沒有妥善安排，資料可能會遺失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arranging a task properly.","zh":"這個短語描述妥善安排任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"make sure that","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Adam had to make sure that people did not know which drink they had.","zh":"Adam 必須確保人們不知道自己喝的是哪種飲品。"},{"en":"To make sure that something happens means to check or arrange things so it definitely happens.","zh":"make sure that something happens 指檢查或安排事情，以確保某事確實發生。"},{"en":"The teacher made sure that every student had a worksheet.","zh":"老師確保每名學生都有工作紙。"},{"en":"If Adam makes sure participants do not know the drink, the test becomes fairer.","zh":"如果 Adam 確保參加者不知道飲品種類，測試會更公平。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses careful checking or control.","zh":"這個短語表達仔細檢查或控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"keep track of","meaning":"追蹤；記錄","examples":[{"en":"It was hard for Adam to keep track of all the information.","zh":"Adam 很難追蹤所有資料。"},{"en":"To keep track of something means to record or follow information so you do not lose it.","zh":"keep track of something 指記錄或跟進資料，以免遺失。"},{"en":"Students used a spreadsheet to keep track of their survey answers.","zh":"學生用試算表記錄問卷答案。"},{"en":"If many people take part, it becomes harder to keep track of every result.","zh":"如果很多人參與，就更難追蹤每個結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for data, tasks, and progress.","zh":"這個短語適用於數據、任務和進度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"especially as","meaning":"尤其因為","examples":[{"en":"It was hard to keep track of it all, especially as many people took part.","zh":"要記錄所有資料很困難，尤其因為很多人參與。"},{"en":"Especially as means particularly because.","zh":"especially as 指尤其是因為。"},{"en":"The project was difficult, especially as several group members were absent.","zh":"這個專題很困難，尤其因為幾名組員缺席。"},{"en":"If many people join an experiment, organisation becomes harder, especially as each person has different data.","zh":"如果很多人參加實驗，安排會更困難，尤其因為每個人有不同數據。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an important reason.","zh":"這個短語給出重要原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have so many people doing it","meaning":"有很多人參與","examples":[{"en":"Adam had so many people doing the experiment.","zh":"Adam 有很多人參與這個實驗。"},{"en":"To have so many people doing something means a large number of people are taking part in the activity.","zh":"have so many people doing something 指有大量人參加某活動。"},{"en":"The teacher had so many students doing the survey that she needed extra forms.","zh":"老師有很多學生參與問卷調查，所以需要額外表格。"},{"en":"If you have many people doing an experiment, records must be very clear.","zh":"如果有很多人參與實驗，紀錄必須非常清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the number of participants.","zh":"這個短語強調參與者數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"keep a proper record of","meaning":"妥善記錄","examples":[{"en":"Adam had to keep a proper record of what each person had had.","zh":"Adam 必須妥善記錄每個人喝過甚麼。"},{"en":"To keep a proper record of something means to write it down accurately and systematically.","zh":"keep a proper record of something 指準確而有系統地把某事記下。"},{"en":"A nurse must keep a proper record of each patient’s medicine.","zh":"護士必須妥善記錄每位病人的藥物。"},{"en":"If Adam keeps proper records, he can compare the results fairly.","zh":"如果 Adam 妥善記錄，他就能公平比較結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful and reliable documentation.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細可靠的記錄。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what each person had had","meaning":"每個人喝過甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Adam recorded what each person had had in the experiment.","zh":"Adam 記錄了每個人在實驗中喝過甚麼。"},{"en":"What each person had had means what each participant had drunk or received earlier.","zh":"what each person had had 指每位參加者之前喝過或收到過甚麼。"},{"en":"The researcher noted what each patient had had before measuring the results.","zh":"研究人員在量度結果前，記下每位病人之前服用過甚麼。"},{"en":"If you know what each person had had, you can match responses with the correct drink.","zh":"如果你知道每個人喝過甚麼，就能把回答與正確飲品配對。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to previous consumption or treatment in an experiment.","zh":"這個短語指實驗中先前的飲用或處理內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"most people","meaning":"大多數人","examples":[{"en":"Most people could tell the difference between sugar and sweeteners.","zh":"大多數人能分辨糖和甜味劑之間的差別。"},{"en":"Most people means the majority of people, but not everyone.","zh":"most people 指大部分人，但不是所有人。"},{"en":"Most people in the class preferred the healthier lunch option.","zh":"班上大多數人較喜歡較健康的午餐選擇。"},{"en":"If most people identify the drink correctly, the taste difference is probably noticeable.","zh":"如果大多數人能正確辨認飲品，味道差別可能很明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes more than half of a group.","zh":"這個短語描述一群人中超過一半。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I hadn’t thought they would","meaning":"我原本沒想到他們會……","examples":[{"en":"Adam had not thought people would be able to tell the difference.","zh":"Adam 原本沒想到人們會能夠分辨差別。"},{"en":"I hadn’t thought they would means I had not expected them to do that.","zh":"I hadn’t thought they would 指我原本沒有預期他們會那樣做。"},{"en":"I hadn’t thought the younger students would understand the lecture so quickly.","zh":"我原本沒想到較年幼學生會這麼快理解講座。"},{"en":"If results are better than expected, you might say you hadn’t thought they would succeed.","zh":"如果結果比預期好，你可能會說原本沒想到他們會成功。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses surprise about an outcome.","zh":"這個短語表達對結果的驚訝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be able to","meaning":"能夠","examples":[{"en":"Most people were able to identify the drink correctly.","zh":"大多數人能夠正確辨認飲品。"},{"en":"To be able to do something means to have the ability or opportunity to do it.","zh":"be able to do something 指有能力或機會做某事。"},{"en":"After practice, students were able to explain the graph clearly.","zh":"練習後，學生能夠清楚解釋圖表。"},{"en":"If participants are able to identify the drink, the experiment has useful findings.","zh":"如果參加者能夠辨認飲品，實驗就有有用發現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability or possibility.","zh":"這個短語描述能力或可能性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"measure the fat content of","meaning":"測量……的脂肪含量","examples":[{"en":"Rosie did an experiment measuring the fat content of nuts.","zh":"Rosie 做了一個測量堅果脂肪含量的實驗。"},{"en":"To measure the fat content of something means to find out how much fat it contains.","zh":"measure the fat content of something 指找出某物含有多少脂肪。"},{"en":"Scientists measured the fat content of different snacks in the laboratory.","zh":"科學家在實驗室測量不同小食的脂肪含量。"},{"en":"If you measure the fat content accurately, you can compare it with the packet information.","zh":"如果你準確測量脂肪含量，就可以與包裝資料比較。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a scientific measurement of food.","zh":"這個短語描述對食物作科學測量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fat content","meaning":"脂肪含量","examples":[{"en":"The fat content of the nuts seemed lower than the packet said.","zh":"堅果的脂肪含量似乎低於包裝所寫。"},{"en":"Fat content means the amount of fat contained in food.","zh":"fat content 指食物中所含脂肪的分量。"},{"en":"People checking their diet may compare the fat content of different snacks.","zh":"注意飲食的人可能會比較不同小食的脂肪含量。"},{"en":"If the fat content is high, the food may contain more calories.","zh":"如果脂肪含量高，食物可能含有更多卡路里。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in nutrition information.","zh":"這個短語常見於營養資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"nutritional information","meaning":"營養資料","examples":[{"en":"Rosie checked whether the nutritional information on the packet was accurate.","zh":"Rosie 檢查包裝上的營養資料是否準確。"},{"en":"Nutritional information is information about calories, fat, sugar, protein, and other nutrients in food.","zh":"nutritional information 指關於食物中的卡路里、脂肪、糖、蛋白質和其他營養素的資料。"},{"en":"Shoppers may read nutritional information before buying breakfast cereal.","zh":"購物者可能在購買早餐穀物前閱讀營養資料。"},{"en":"If nutritional information is clear, people can make healthier choices.","zh":"如果營養資料清晰，人們可以作出更健康選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to food-label data.","zh":"這個短語指食物標籤上的數據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"given on the packet","meaning":"標示在包裝上","examples":[{"en":"The nutritional information given on the packet may not match the results.","zh":"標示在包裝上的營養資料可能與結果不符。"},{"en":"Given on the packet means printed or shown on the food packaging.","zh":"given on the packet 指印在或顯示在食物包裝上。"},{"en":"The cooking instructions given on the packet were easy to follow.","zh":"標示在包裝上的烹調指示很容易跟從。"},{"en":"If information given on the packet is wrong, consumers may be misled.","zh":"如果標示在包裝上的資料錯誤，消費者可能被誤導。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information displayed on packaging.","zh":"這個短語描述包裝上顯示的資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be accurate","meaning":"準確","examples":[{"en":"Rosie wanted to see whether the packet information was accurate.","zh":"Rosie 想看看包裝資料是否準確。"},{"en":"To be accurate means to be correct and free from mistakes.","zh":"be accurate 指正確而沒有錯誤。"},{"en":"A science report should be accurate when giving measurements.","zh":"科學報告提供測量數據時應該準確。"},{"en":"If food labels are accurate, people can trust the nutritional information.","zh":"如果食物標籤準確，人們就能信任營養資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes correctness and precision.","zh":"這個短語描述正確性和精準度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"grind up","meaning":"磨碎","examples":[{"en":"Rosie ground up the nuts for her experiment.","zh":"Rosie 為實驗磨碎了堅果。"},{"en":"To grind up something means to crush it into small pieces or powder.","zh":"grind up something 指把某物壓碎成小塊或粉末。"},{"en":"The chef ground up the spices before adding them to the sauce.","zh":"廚師把香料磨碎後加入醬汁。"},{"en":"If nuts are not ground up enough, some fat may not be released properly.","zh":"如果堅果磨得不夠碎，有些脂肪可能未能充分釋出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes breaking solid food into smaller pieces.","zh":"這個短語描述把固體食物弄成較小碎片。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mix something with","meaning":"將某物與……混合","examples":[{"en":"Rosie mixed the nuts with a chemical to absorb the fat.","zh":"Rosie 將堅果與一種化學物質混合，以吸收脂肪。"},{"en":"To mix something with something else means to combine them together.","zh":"mix something with something else 指把兩者混合在一起。"},{"en":"Students mixed flour with water to make a simple dough.","zh":"學生把麵粉與水混合，製作簡單麵糰。"},{"en":"If the nuts are mixed well with the chemical, the test may work better.","zh":"如果堅果與化學物質充分混合，測試可能更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes combining materials.","zh":"這個短語描述結合材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"chemical","meaning":"化學物質","examples":[{"en":"Rosie used a chemical to absorb the fat from the nuts.","zh":"Rosie 使用一種化學物質來吸收堅果中的脂肪。"},{"en":"A chemical is a substance used in science or produced through chemical processes.","zh":"chemical 指科學中使用或透過化學過程產生的物質。"},{"en":"Students must wear goggles when handling a strong chemical in the laboratory.","zh":"學生在實驗室處理強烈化學物質時必須戴護目鏡。"},{"en":"If a chemical is used in an experiment, safety instructions must be followed carefully.","zh":"如果實驗使用化學物質，必須仔細遵守安全指示。"},{"en":"This word refers to a scientific substance.","zh":"這個字指科學物質。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"absorb the fat","meaning":"吸收脂肪","examples":[{"en":"The chemical was used to absorb the fat.","zh":"這種化學物質被用來吸收脂肪。"},{"en":"To absorb the fat means to take in or soak up the fat.","zh":"absorb the fat 指吸收或吸走脂肪。"},{"en":"Kitchen paper can absorb the fat from fried food.","zh":"廚房紙可以吸收油炸食物上的脂肪。"},{"en":"If the chemical does not absorb the fat fully, the measurement may be inaccurate.","zh":"如果化學物質沒有完全吸收脂肪，測量結果可能不準確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking fat into another material.","zh":"這個短語描述把脂肪吸入另一種材料中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a bit problematic","meaning":"有點問題","examples":[{"en":"Rosie’s results were a bit problematic.","zh":"Rosie 的結果有點問題。"},{"en":"A bit problematic means slightly difficult, doubtful, or causing some problems.","zh":"a bit problematic 指有點困難、可疑或造成一些問題。"},{"en":"The survey results were a bit problematic because only ten people answered.","zh":"問卷結果有點問題，因為只有十個人回答。"},{"en":"If experimental results are problematic, students should explain possible errors.","zh":"如果實驗結果有問題，學生應解釋可能誤差。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a mild negative judgement.","zh":"這個短語作出溫和負面評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"that type of","meaning":"那一類……","examples":[{"en":"The fat content for that type of nut seemed much lower.","zh":"那一類堅果的脂肪含量似乎低得多。"},{"en":"That type of something means that particular kind or category.","zh":"that type of something 指某一特定種類或類別。"},{"en":"That type of exercise is useful for people who dislike running.","zh":"那一類運動對不喜歡跑步的人很有用。"},{"en":"If that type of nut has less fat, it may be marketed as a healthier snack.","zh":"如果那一類堅果脂肪較低，它可能被包裝成較健康小食。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a specific category.","zh":"這個短語指出特定類別。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"much lower than","meaning":"比……低得多","examples":[{"en":"The fat content seemed much lower than it said on the packet.","zh":"脂肪含量似乎比包裝上所寫低得多。"},{"en":"Much lower than means far below another amount, number, or level.","zh":"much lower than 指遠低於另一數量、數字或水平。"},{"en":"The temperature today is much lower than yesterday’s temperature.","zh":"今天氣溫比昨天低得多。"},{"en":"If the measured fat content is much lower than the packet says, the method may need checking.","zh":"如果測得的脂肪含量比包裝標示低得多，方法可能需要檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a large downward difference.","zh":"這個短語顯示很大的向下差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on the package","meaning":"在包裝上","examples":[{"en":"The information on the package was probably right.","zh":"包裝上的資料可能是正確的。"},{"en":"On the package means printed or shown on the outside of the product packaging.","zh":"on the package 指印在或顯示在產品包裝外面。"},{"en":"The allergy warning on the package was written in bold letters.","zh":"包裝上的致敏警告以粗體字寫出。"},{"en":"If information on the package is right, the experimental error may come from the method.","zh":"如果包裝上的資料正確，實驗誤差可能來自方法。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to packaging information.","zh":"這個短語指包裝資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reckon","meaning":"認為","examples":[{"en":"Rosie reckons the package information was right.","zh":"Rosie 認為包裝資料是正確的。"},{"en":"To reckon means to think or believe something, often based on judgement rather than proof.","zh":"reckon 指認為或相信某事，通常基於判斷而不是證明。"},{"en":"I reckon the library will be crowded before the exam.","zh":"我認為考試前圖書館會很擠。"},{"en":"If Rosie reckons the label is right, she may suspect her experiment had errors.","zh":"如果 Rosie 認為標籤正確，她可能懷疑實驗有誤差。"},{"en":"This word is informal and common in spoken English.","zh":"這個字較口語，常見於英語口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"should probably have","meaning":"可能本應……","examples":[{"en":"Rosie thinks she should probably have ground up the nuts more.","zh":"Rosie 認為她可能本應把堅果磨得更碎。"},{"en":"Should probably have means something was likely the better action in the past.","zh":"should probably have 指過去某做法很可能才是較好的選擇。"},{"en":"I should probably have checked the instructions before starting the experiment.","zh":"我可能本應在開始實驗前先檢查指示。"},{"en":"If Rosie should have ground the nuts more, the original method may have been incomplete.","zh":"如果 Rosie 本應把堅果磨得更碎，原本方法可能不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses mild regret or hindsight.","zh":"這個短語表達輕微後悔或事後判斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"more than I did","meaning":"比我實際做的更多","examples":[{"en":"Rosie should have ground up the nuts more than she did.","zh":"Rosie 本應把堅果磨得比她實際做的更多。"},{"en":"More than I did means to a greater degree or amount than I actually did.","zh":"more than I did 指比我實際做的程度或數量更多。"},{"en":"I should have revised more than I did before the vocabulary test.","zh":"我在詞彙測驗前本應比實際做的溫習更多。"},{"en":"If Rosie ground the nuts less than needed, the fat may not have been fully absorbed.","zh":"如果 Rosie 磨堅果的程度不足，脂肪可能未被完全吸收。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the ideal action with the actual action.","zh":"這個短語比較理想行動和實際行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"it is possible that","meaning":"有可能","examples":[{"en":"It is possible that the scales were not accurate enough.","zh":"有可能磅不夠準確。"},{"en":"It is possible that means something may be true, though it is not certain.","zh":"it is possible that 指某事可能是真的，但未能肯定。"},{"en":"It is possible that the results changed because the room was too warm.","zh":"有可能結果改變是因為房間太熱。"},{"en":"If it is possible that equipment was inaccurate, the experiment should be repeated.","zh":"如果有可能設備不準確，實驗就應重做。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a cautious explanation.","zh":"這個短語引出謹慎解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"scales for weighing","meaning":"用來量度……的磅","examples":[{"en":"The scales for weighing the fat may not have been accurate enough.","zh":"用來量度脂肪的磅可能不夠準確。"},{"en":"Scales for weighing are instruments used to measure weight.","zh":"scales for weighing 指用來量度重量的儀器。"},{"en":"The science lab has scales for weighing chemicals before experiments.","zh":"科學實驗室有用來量度化學物質的磅。"},{"en":"If scales for weighing are not sensitive enough, small amounts may be measured wrongly.","zh":"如果用來量度的磅不夠靈敏，少量物質可能被量錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes measuring equipment.","zh":"這個短語描述量度設備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"accurate enough","meaning":"夠準確","examples":[{"en":"The scales may not have been accurate enough.","zh":"磅可能不夠準確。"},{"en":"Accurate enough means sufficiently correct for the purpose.","zh":"accurate enough 指對某目的而言足夠正確。"},{"en":"The ruler was not accurate enough for the science experiment.","zh":"這把間尺對科學實驗來說不夠準確。"},{"en":"If equipment is not accurate enough, the results may be unreliable.","zh":"如果設備不夠準確，結果可能不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase judges whether precision is sufficient.","zh":"這個短語判斷精準度是否足夠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"try the experiment again","meaning":"再做一次實驗","examples":[{"en":"Rosie would like to try the experiment again some time.","zh":"Rosie 想找個時間再做一次實驗。"},{"en":"To try the experiment again means to repeat the experiment, often to check or improve the results.","zh":"try the experiment again 指重複實驗，通常為了檢查或改善結果。"},{"en":"The students tried the experiment again after correcting their measuring method.","zh":"學生修正量度方法後，再做一次實驗。"},{"en":"If results are unclear, trying the experiment again can help confirm the findings.","zh":"如果結果不清楚，再做一次實驗可以幫助確認發現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeating scientific work.","zh":"這個短語描述重複科學工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"some time","meaning":"找個時間","examples":[{"en":"Rosie would like to repeat the experiment some time.","zh":"Rosie 想找個時間重做實驗。"},{"en":"Some time means at an unspecified time in the future.","zh":"some time 指未來某個未指定時間。"},{"en":"We should visit the new science museum some time.","zh":"我們應該找個時間參觀新的科學博物館。"},{"en":"If Rosie repeats the experiment some time, she may improve the method.","zh":"如果 Rosie 找個時間重做實驗，她可能可以改善方法。"},{"en":"This phrase is vague and does not give an exact date.","zh":"這個短語較籠統，沒有給出確切日期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"helping people to","meaning":"幫助人們……","examples":[{"en":"The students discuss helping people to lose weight.","zh":"學生討論幫助人們減肥。"},{"en":"Helping people to do something means supporting them so they can achieve that action.","zh":"helping people to do something 指支援人們，使他們能做到某事。"},{"en":"Schools can help pupils to develop healthier habits.","zh":"學校可以幫助學生養成更健康習慣。"},{"en":"If information helps people to make better choices, it can improve health.","zh":"如果資訊幫助人們作出更好選擇，就能改善健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes support toward a goal.","zh":"這個短語描述朝目標提供支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lose weight","meaning":"減肥","examples":[{"en":"The presentation may discuss how people can lose weight.","zh":"這個簡報可能討論人們如何減肥。"},{"en":"To lose weight means to reduce body weight, often through diet, exercise, or lifestyle changes.","zh":"lose weight 指減少體重，常透過飲食、運動或生活方式改變。"},{"en":"Some people try to lose weight by eating smaller portions.","zh":"有些人透過吃較少分量來減肥。"},{"en":"If people lose weight safely, they should still get enough nutrition.","zh":"如果人們安全地減肥，仍應攝取足夠營養。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in health and diet discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於健康和飲食討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"there is a lot we could say about","meaning":"我們有很多可以談","examples":[{"en":"There is a lot the students could say about restaurants and obesity.","zh":"學生有很多可以談關於餐廳與肥胖的內容。"},{"en":"There is a lot we could say about something means the topic has many possible points to discuss.","zh":"there is a lot we could say about something 指某題目有很多可討論重點。"},{"en":"There is a lot we could say about social media and teenagers.","zh":"關於社交媒體和青少年，我們有很多可以談。"},{"en":"If there is a lot to say, students need to choose the most relevant points.","zh":"如果有很多內容可談，學生就需要選擇最相關的重點。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a topic is rich and broad.","zh":"這個短語顯示題目豐富而廣泛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reduce obesity","meaning":"減低肥胖","examples":[{"en":"Restaurants could do more to reduce obesity.","zh":"餐廳可以做更多來減低肥胖。"},{"en":"To reduce obesity means to lower the level or frequency of excessive body weight in a population.","zh":"reduce obesity 指降低人口中過重或肥胖的程度或比例。"},{"en":"Clear food labels can help reduce obesity by guiding healthier choices.","zh":"清楚的食物標籤可以透過引導較健康選擇來減低肥胖。"},{"en":"If restaurants offer smaller portions, they may help reduce obesity.","zh":"如果餐廳提供較小份量，可能有助減低肥胖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes action against a health problem.","zh":"這個短語描述應對健康問題的行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"items at the start of","meaning":"在……開頭的項目","examples":[{"en":"Items at the start of a menu are more likely to be chosen.","zh":"在餐牌開頭的項目更有可能被選擇。"},{"en":"Items at the start of something are the choices placed at the beginning.","zh":"items at the start of something 指放在開首位置的選項。"},{"en":"Items at the start of a list often receive more attention.","zh":"在清單開頭的項目通常較受注意。"},{"en":"If healthy dishes are placed at the start of a menu, customers may notice them first.","zh":"如果健康菜式放在餐牌開頭，顧客可能最先注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position at the beginning.","zh":"這個短語描述位於開首的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"items at the end of","meaning":"在……結尾的項目","examples":[{"en":"Items at the end of a menu are also more likely to be chosen.","zh":"在餐牌結尾的項目也更有可能被選擇。"},{"en":"Items at the end of something are the choices placed in the final part.","zh":"items at the end of something 指放在最後部分的選項。"},{"en":"Items at the end of a worksheet may still stand out because they are seen last.","zh":"工作紙結尾的項目仍可能突出，因為它們最後被看到。"},{"en":"If low-calorie dishes appear at the end of a menu, customers may remember them.","zh":"如果低卡路里菜式出現在餐牌結尾，顧客可能會記得。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position at the final part.","zh":"這個短語描述位於最後部分的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"much more likely to","meaning":"更有可能","examples":[{"en":"Menu items at the beginning and end are much more likely to be chosen.","zh":"餐牌開頭和結尾的項目更有可能被選擇。"},{"en":"Much more likely to means having a far greater chance of doing or experiencing something.","zh":"much more likely to 指做某事或經歷某事的機會大得多。"},{"en":"Students are much more likely to revise if the test is next week.","zh":"如果測驗在下星期，學生更有可能溫習。"},{"en":"If a dish is easier to notice, customers are much more likely to order it.","zh":"如果菜式更容易被注意到，顧客更有可能點選它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong increase in probability.","zh":"這個短語描述可能性大幅增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"items in the middle","meaning":"中間的項目","examples":[{"en":"Items in the middle of a menu are less likely to be chosen.","zh":"餐牌中間的項目較少被選擇。"},{"en":"Items in the middle are choices placed between the beginning and the end.","zh":"items in the middle 指放在開頭和結尾之間的選項。"},{"en":"Students sometimes ignore examples in the middle of a long handout.","zh":"學生有時會忽略長講義中間的例子。"},{"en":"If a dish is placed in the middle, it may receive less attention.","zh":"如果菜式放在中間，它可能較少受到注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position between two ends.","zh":"這個短語描述位於兩端之間的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"low-calorie items","meaning":"低卡路里食品","examples":[{"en":"Restaurants could put low-calorie items at the beginning and end of the menu.","zh":"餐廳可以把低卡路里食品放在餐牌開頭和結尾。"},{"en":"Low-calorie items are foods or drinks that contain fewer calories.","zh":"low-calorie items 指含較少卡路里的食物或飲品。"},{"en":"Salads, soups, and grilled vegetables can be low-calorie items.","zh":"沙律、湯和烤蔬菜都可以是低卡路里食品。"},{"en":"If low-calorie items are easy to see, customers may choose healthier meals.","zh":"如果低卡路里食品容易看見，顧客可能選擇較健康餐點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes food with lower energy content.","zh":"這個短語描述能量較低的食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at the beginning and end of","meaning":"在……的開首和結尾","examples":[{"en":"Low-calorie items could be placed at the beginning and end of the menu.","zh":"低卡路里食品可以放在餐牌的開首和結尾。"},{"en":"At the beginning and end of something means in both the first part and the final part.","zh":"at the beginning and end of something 指在某物的第一部分和最後部分。"},{"en":"Important reminders were placed at the beginning and end of the notice.","zh":"重要提醒放在通告的開首和結尾。"},{"en":"If healthy dishes appear at the beginning and end of a menu, people may notice them more.","zh":"如果健康菜式出現在餐牌開首和結尾，人們可能更留意它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two prominent positions.","zh":"這個短語描述兩個顯眼位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"go for","meaning":"選擇","examples":[{"en":"People may go for food with fewer calories.","zh":"人們可能會選擇卡路里較低的食物。"},{"en":"To go for something means to choose it.","zh":"go for something 指選擇某物。"},{"en":"Many pupils go for pasta when they want a quick lunch.","zh":"許多學生想快點吃午餐時會選擇意粉。"},{"en":"If healthier food is easier to notice, customers may go for it without much thought.","zh":"如果較健康食物更容易被看到，顧客可能不太思考就選擇它。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and common in conversation.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常見於對話中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"food with fewer calories","meaning":"卡路里較低的食物","examples":[{"en":"People may choose food with fewer calories without realising it.","zh":"人們可能在沒有意識到的情況下選擇卡路里較低的食物。"},{"en":"Food with fewer calories contains less energy than other food choices.","zh":"food with fewer calories 指比其他食物選擇含較少能量的食物。"},{"en":"A grilled chicken salad is often food with fewer calories than fried chicken.","zh":"烤雞沙律通常比炸雞是卡路里較低的食物。"},{"en":"If people choose food with fewer calories regularly, it may help control weight.","zh":"如果人們經常選擇卡路里較低的食物，可能有助控制體重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lower-energy food.","zh":"這個短語描述能量較低的食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"without even realising","meaning":"甚至沒有意識到","examples":[{"en":"People may choose healthier food without even realising what they are doing.","zh":"人們可能甚至沒有意識到自己在做甚麼，就選擇較健康食物。"},{"en":"Without even realising means without being consciously aware of it.","zh":"without even realising 指沒有自覺地意識到某事。"},{"en":"Students may copy a teacher’s pronunciation without even realising it.","zh":"學生可能甚至沒有意識到自己在模仿老師的發音。"},{"en":"If menu design changes behaviour without people realising, it can quietly encourage healthier choices.","zh":"如果餐牌設計在人們沒意識到下改變行為，就能悄悄鼓勵較健康選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unconscious action.","zh":"這個短語描述無意識行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"healthy eating","meaning":"健康飲食","examples":[{"en":"Food manufacturers could do more to encourage healthy eating.","zh":"食品製造商可以做更多來鼓勵健康飲食。"},{"en":"Healthy eating means choosing food that supports good health and balanced nutrition.","zh":"healthy eating 指選擇有助健康和均衡營養的食物。"},{"en":"Schools can encourage healthy eating by offering fruit and vegetables every day.","zh":"學校可以透過每天提供水果和蔬菜來鼓勵健康飲食。"},{"en":"If labels are clear, healthy eating becomes easier for busy families.","zh":"如果標籤清晰，忙碌家庭會更容易做到健康飲食。"},{"en":"This phrase describes good dietary habits.","zh":"這個短語描述良好飲食習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"food manufacturers","meaning":"食品製造商","examples":[{"en":"Food manufacturers could encourage healthy eating more clearly.","zh":"食品製造商可以更清楚地鼓勵健康飲食。"},{"en":"Food manufacturers are companies that produce packaged or processed food.","zh":"food manufacturers 指生產包裝或加工食品的公司。"},{"en":"Food manufacturers design labels, recipes, and packaging for their products.","zh":"食品製造商為產品設計標籤、配方和包裝。"},{"en":"If food manufacturers reduce sugar and salt, they can improve public health.","zh":"如果食品製造商減少糖和鹽，就能改善公共健康。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to businesses that make food products.","zh":"這個短語指製造食品產品的企業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"calorie counts","meaning":"卡路里數值","examples":[{"en":"Calorie counts on food labels are sometimes confusing.","zh":"食物標籤上的卡路里數值有時令人混淆。"},{"en":"Calorie counts are numbers showing how much energy food contains.","zh":"calorie counts 指顯示食物含有多少能量的數字。"},{"en":"People on a diet may compare calorie counts before choosing lunch.","zh":"節食的人可能在選午餐前比較卡路里數值。"},{"en":"If calorie counts are unclear, consumers may underestimate how much they eat.","zh":"如果卡路里數值不清楚，消費者可能低估自己吃了多少。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to energy information on food.","zh":"這個短語指食物中的能量資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on the label","meaning":"在標籤上","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers put calorie counts on the label.","zh":"製造商把卡路里數值放在標籤上。"},{"en":"On the label means printed or shown on the product label.","zh":"on the label 指印在或顯示在產品標籤上。"},{"en":"The allergy warning is clearly written on the label.","zh":"致敏警告清楚寫在標籤上。"},{"en":"If calorie information is on the label, shoppers can check it before buying.","zh":"如果卡路里資料在標籤上，購物者購買前可以查看。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to product information displayed on packaging.","zh":"這個短語指包裝上顯示的產品資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"really confusing","meaning":"非常令人混淆","examples":[{"en":"Some calorie labels are really confusing.","zh":"有些卡路里標籤非常令人混淆。"},{"en":"Really confusing means very difficult to understand clearly.","zh":"really confusing 指非常難以清楚理解。"},{"en":"The new timetable was really confusing because the room numbers kept changing.","zh":"新時間表非常令人混淆，因為課室編號不停改變。"},{"en":"If labels are really confusing, people may make poor food choices by mistake.","zh":"如果標籤非常令人混淆，人們可能錯誤地作出不佳食物選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly criticises lack of clarity.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評不清晰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"suspect that","meaning":"懷疑","examples":[{"en":"Rosie suspects that manufacturers do it on purpose.","zh":"Rosie 懷疑製造商是故意這樣做。"},{"en":"To suspect that something is true means to think it may be true, often without full proof.","zh":"suspect that something is true 指認為某事可能是真的，但通常沒有完整證據。"},{"en":"The teacher suspected that some students had not read the article.","zh":"老師懷疑有些學生沒有讀文章。"},{"en":"If Rosie suspects labels are confusing on purpose, she thinks manufacturers may benefit from confusion.","zh":"如果 Rosie 懷疑標籤故意令人混淆，她認為製造商可能從混亂中得益。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a cautious belief.","zh":"這個短語引出謹慎的看法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on purpose","meaning":"故意","examples":[{"en":"Rosie suspects that confusing labels are used on purpose.","zh":"Rosie 懷疑令人混淆的標籤是故意使用的。"},{"en":"On purpose means deliberately or intentionally.","zh":"on purpose 指蓄意或有意地。"},{"en":"The child did not spill the water on purpose; it was an accident.","zh":"那孩子不是故意灑水；那是意外。"},{"en":"If labels are confusing on purpose, the company may be trying to hide unhealthy information.","zh":"如果標籤故意令人混淆，公司可能想隱藏不健康資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intentional action.","zh":"這個短語描述有意行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"high in calories","meaning":"高卡路里","examples":[{"en":"Food that is high in calories often tastes better.","zh":"高卡路里的食物通常味道更好。"},{"en":"High in calories means containing a lot of energy from sugar, fat, or other nutrients.","zh":"high in calories 指含有大量來自糖、脂肪或其他營養素的能量。"},{"en":"Fried snacks and creamy desserts are often high in calories.","zh":"油炸小食和忌廉甜品通常高卡路里。"},{"en":"If food is high in calories, eating too much of it can contribute to weight gain.","zh":"如果食物高卡路里，吃太多可能導致體重增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes energy-dense food.","zh":"這個短語描述能量密度高的食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"taste better","meaning":"味道更好","examples":[{"en":"High-calorie food often tastes better.","zh":"高卡路里食物通常味道更好。"},{"en":"To taste better means to have a more pleasant flavour.","zh":"taste better 指味道更令人愉快。"},{"en":"Some people think soup tastes better with a little salt.","zh":"有些人認為湯加一點鹽味道更好。"},{"en":"If high-calorie food tastes better, people may choose it more often.","zh":"如果高卡路里食物味道更好，人們可能更常選擇它。"},{"en":"This phrase compares flavour quality.","zh":"這個短語比較味道質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sell more","meaning":"賣得更多","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers may sell more if high-calorie food tastes better.","zh":"如果高卡路里食物味道更好，製造商可能賣得更多。"},{"en":"To sell more means to sell a larger quantity of products.","zh":"sell more 指售出更大數量的產品。"},{"en":"A café may sell more sandwiches if they are displayed near the entrance.","zh":"如果咖啡店把三文治放在入口附近，可能賣得更多。"},{"en":"If sweeter food tastes better to many customers, manufacturers may sell more of it.","zh":"如果較甜食物對許多顧客來說味道更好，製造商可能賣得更多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increased sales.","zh":"這個短語描述銷量增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the amount of calories in","meaning":"……中的卡路里量","examples":[{"en":"Adam talks about the amount of calories in a pizza.","zh":"Adam 談及薄餅中的卡路里量。"},{"en":"The amount of calories in something means how much energy that food contains.","zh":"the amount of calories in something 指某食物含有多少能量。"},{"en":"The amount of calories in a snack may be higher than people expect.","zh":"小食中的卡路里量可能比人們預期高。"},{"en":"If the amount of calories in a meal is shown clearly, people can make informed choices.","zh":"如果一餐中的卡路里量清楚顯示，人們可以作出知情選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to discuss food energy.","zh":"這個短語用於討論食物能量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"calories per quarter pizza","meaning":"每四分之一個薄餅的卡路里","examples":[{"en":"Some labels give the calories per quarter pizza.","zh":"有些標籤列出每四分之一個薄餅的卡路里。"},{"en":"Calories per quarter pizza means the number of calories in one fourth of a pizza.","zh":"calories per quarter pizza 指四分之一個薄餅所含的卡路里數。"},{"en":"A label may look lower if it shows calories per small serving rather than for the whole item.","zh":"如果標籤顯示小份量而不是整件食品的卡路里，數字可能看起來較低。"},{"en":"If people eat the whole pizza, they need to multiply the calories per quarter by four.","zh":"如果人們吃完整個薄餅，就需要把每四分之一個薄餅的卡路里乘以四。"},{"en":"This phrase describes calories by portion size.","zh":"這個短語按食用份量描述卡路里。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not too bad","meaning":"不算太差","examples":[{"en":"A quarter pizza may not seem too bad in terms of calories.","zh":"從卡路里角度看，四分之一個薄餅可能不算太差。"},{"en":"Not too bad means acceptable or not as bad as expected.","zh":"not too bad 指可以接受，或不像預期那麼差。"},{"en":"The test result was not too bad, although there was room for improvement.","zh":"測驗結果不算太差，雖然仍有改善空間。"},{"en":"If a label shows calories for only a small portion, the number may not look too bad.","zh":"如果標籤只顯示小份量的卡路里，數字可能看起來不算太差。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a mild positive judgement.","zh":"這個短語作出溫和正面評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"who is going to","meaning":"誰會……","examples":[{"en":"Adam asks who is going to eat only a quarter pizza.","zh":"Adam 問誰會只吃四分之一個薄餅。"},{"en":"Who is going to asks which person will actually do something.","zh":"who is going to 用來問哪個人實際上會做某事。"},{"en":"Who is going to finish the group report before Friday?","zh":"誰會在星期五前完成小組報告？"},{"en":"If Adam asks who will eat only a quarter pizza, he doubts that many people will.","zh":"如果 Adam 問誰會只吃四分之一個薄餅，他懷疑很多人不會這樣做。"},{"en":"This phrase can express a real question or a rhetorical challenge.","zh":"這個短語可以是真問題，也可以是反問式質疑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"another approach to","meaning":"另一種處理……的方法","examples":[{"en":"Another approach to obesity is to get people to exercise more.","zh":"另一種處理肥胖的方法是令人們多做運動。"},{"en":"Another approach to a problem means another way of dealing with it.","zh":"another approach to a problem 指處理某問題的另一種方法。"},{"en":"Another approach to bullying is to train students to support victims.","zh":"另一種處理欺凌的方法是訓練學生支援受害者。"},{"en":"If one approach focuses on diet, another approach may focus on exercise.","zh":"如果一種方法聚焦飲食，另一種方法可能聚焦運動。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an alternative method.","zh":"這個短語引入替代方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get people to","meaning":"令別人……","examples":[{"en":"One approach is to get people to exercise more.","zh":"一種方法是令人們多做運動。"},{"en":"To get people to do something means to persuade, encourage, or arrange for them to do it.","zh":"get people to do something 指說服、鼓勵或安排人們做某事。"},{"en":"Schools can get pupils to read more by creating attractive book displays.","zh":"學校可以透過設計吸引人的書展，令學生多閱讀。"},{"en":"If cities want to get people to walk more, they need safe and convenient paths.","zh":"如果城市想令人們多步行，就需要安全方便的行人路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes influencing behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述影響行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"exercise more","meaning":"多做運動","examples":[{"en":"People need to exercise more to help control obesity.","zh":"人們需要多做運動，以幫助控制肥胖。"},{"en":"To exercise more means to do physical activity more often or for longer.","zh":"exercise more 指更常或更長時間做體能活動。"},{"en":"Students can exercise more by walking to school or joining sports clubs.","zh":"學生可以透過步行上學或參加運動學會來多做運動。"},{"en":"If people exercise more regularly, they may improve fitness and manage weight better.","zh":"如果人們更定期多做運動，可能改善體能並更好管理體重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing physical activity.","zh":"這個短語描述增加體能活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"current guidelines","meaning":"現行指引","examples":[{"en":"The current guidelines recommend brisk walking five days a week.","zh":"現行指引建議每星期五日急步行。"},{"en":"Current guidelines are the official or accepted advice used now.","zh":"current guidelines 指現時使用的官方或公認建議。"},{"en":"The current guidelines tell pupils how much exercise they should do each week.","zh":"現行指引告訴學生每星期應做多少運動。"},{"en":"If current guidelines change, health advice may also need updating.","zh":"如果現行指引改變，健康建議也可能需要更新。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to present recommendations.","zh":"這個短語指目前建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at least","meaning":"至少","examples":[{"en":"The guidelines recommend at least 30 minutes of brisk walking.","zh":"指引建議至少30分鐘急步行。"},{"en":"At least means no less than a stated amount.","zh":"at least 指不少於所說的數量。"},{"en":"Students should read for at least twenty minutes each day.","zh":"學生每天應至少閱讀二十分鐘。"},{"en":"If people exercise for at least 30 minutes, they meet the minimum recommendation.","zh":"如果人們運動至少30分鐘，就達到最低建議。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a minimum requirement.","zh":"這個短語給出最低要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"brisk walking","meaning":"急步行","examples":[{"en":"The current guidelines recommend brisk walking.","zh":"現行指引建議急步行。"},{"en":"Brisk walking is walking quickly enough to raise the heart rate but still allow conversation.","zh":"brisk walking 指步行速度快到能提升心跳，但仍能說話。"},{"en":"Many people choose brisk walking because it needs no special equipment.","zh":"許多人選擇急步行，因為不需要特別設備。"},{"en":"If done regularly, brisk walking can improve fitness and support weight control.","zh":"如果定期進行，急步行可以改善體能並支援體重控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a moderate form of exercise.","zh":"這個短語描述中等強度運動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"five days a week","meaning":"每星期五日","examples":[{"en":"People are advised to walk briskly five days a week.","zh":"人們被建議每星期五日急步行。"},{"en":"Five days a week means on five days during each week.","zh":"five days a week 指每星期其中五日。"},{"en":"The swimmer trains five days a week before competitions.","zh":"這名泳手比賽前每星期訓練五日。"},{"en":"If people exercise five days a week, the habit becomes part of their routine.","zh":"如果人們每星期五日運動，習慣就會成為日常的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequency across a week.","zh":"這個短語描述每星期的頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"when you ask them","meaning":"當你問他們時","examples":[{"en":"When you ask people, many say they follow the exercise guidelines.","zh":"當你問人們時，許多人說自己有遵守運動指引。"},{"en":"When you ask them means when you question those people directly.","zh":"when you ask them 指當你直接詢問那些人時。"},{"en":"When you ask students, many say they revise every day.","zh":"當你問學生時，許多人說自己每天溫習。"},{"en":"If answers depend on what people say, they may not match actual behaviour.","zh":"如果答案取決於人們所說，可能與實際行為不符。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces self-reported information.","zh":"這個短語引出自我報告的資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"objectively measure","meaning":"客觀量度","examples":[{"en":"Motion sensors can objectively measure how much people walk.","zh":"動作感應器可以客觀量度人們步行多少。"},{"en":"To objectively measure something means to measure it using evidence or tools rather than personal opinion.","zh":"objectively measure something 指用證據或工具而不是個人意見來量度某事。"},{"en":"A fitness watch can objectively measure heart rate during exercise.","zh":"健身手錶可以客觀量度運動時的心跳。"},{"en":"If researchers objectively measure activity, the data may be more reliable than memory.","zh":"如果研究人員客觀量度活動，數據可能比記憶更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes neutral measurement.","zh":"這個短語描述中立量度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the amount of walking","meaning":"步行量","examples":[{"en":"Researchers measured the amount of walking people actually did.","zh":"研究人員量度人們實際做了多少步行。"},{"en":"The amount of walking means how much walking someone does.","zh":"the amount of walking 指某人步行的多少。"},{"en":"The app records the amount of walking a pupil does each day.","zh":"這個應用程式記錄學生每天的步行量。"},{"en":"If the amount of walking is low, people may need more opportunities to move.","zh":"如果步行量低，人們可能需要更多活動機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quantity of walking activity.","zh":"這個短語描述步行活動的數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"motion sensors","meaning":"動作感應器","examples":[{"en":"Motion sensors show how much walking people actually do.","zh":"動作感應器顯示人們實際步行多少。"},{"en":"Motion sensors are devices that detect and record movement.","zh":"motion sensors 指偵測和記錄動作的裝置。"},{"en":"Some phones use motion sensors to count daily steps.","zh":"有些手機使用動作感應器計算每日步數。"},{"en":"If motion sensors are used in research, activity levels can be measured more accurately.","zh":"如果研究使用動作感應器，活動量可以更準確量度。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to technology that tracks movement.","zh":"這個短語指追蹤動作的科技。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"recommended amount of exercise","meaning":"建議運動量","examples":[{"en":"Very few people do the recommended amount of exercise.","zh":"很少人做到建議運動量。"},{"en":"The recommended amount of exercise is the level of physical activity advised by health guidelines.","zh":"recommended amount of exercise 指健康指引建議的體能活動水平。"},{"en":"Many teenagers do not reach the recommended amount of exercise each week.","zh":"許多青少年每星期未達建議運動量。"},{"en":"If people fall below the recommended amount, health risks may increase.","zh":"如果人們低於建議運動量，健康風險可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to advised exercise levels.","zh":"這個短語指建議的運動水平。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"you can see why","meaning":"你可以看出為甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Adam says you can see why obesity is growing.","zh":"Adam 說你可以看出為甚麼肥胖問題正在增加。"},{"en":"You can see why means the reason becomes clear or understandable.","zh":"you can see why 指原因變得清楚或可以理解。"},{"en":"When you look at the long queues, you can see why students complain about lunch.","zh":"當你看到長長的隊伍，就可以看出為甚麼學生投訴午餐。"},{"en":"If exercise levels are low, you can see why obesity may rise.","zh":"如果運動量低，你可以看出為甚麼肥胖可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an obvious explanation.","zh":"這個短語引出明顯解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"obesity is growing","meaning":"肥胖問題正在增加","examples":[{"en":"The low level of exercise helps explain why obesity is growing.","zh":"運動量低有助解釋為甚麼肥胖問題正在增加。"},{"en":"Obesity is growing means obesity is becoming more common.","zh":"obesity is growing 指肥胖變得越來越常見。"},{"en":"Doctors worry that obesity is growing among children and teenagers.","zh":"醫生擔心兒童和青少年肥胖問題正在增加。"},{"en":"If people eat more calories and exercise less, obesity may grow in society.","zh":"如果人們攝取更多卡路里而運動較少，社會中的肥胖問題可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increasing public health problem.","zh":"這個短語描述正在加劇的公共健康問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be encouraged to","meaning":"被鼓勵去……","examples":[{"en":"Rosie asks how people can be encouraged to take more exercise.","zh":"Rosie 問人們可以如何被鼓勵去多做運動。"},{"en":"To be encouraged to do something means to be motivated or persuaded to do it.","zh":"be encouraged to do something 指被推動或說服去做某事。"},{"en":"Pupils can be encouraged to read more by joining a book challenge.","zh":"學生可以透過參加閱讀挑戰被鼓勵去多閱讀。"},{"en":"If people are encouraged gently, they may change behaviour without feeling forced.","zh":"如果人們被溫和鼓勵，可能會在不感到被迫下改變行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes positive influence.","zh":"這個短語描述正面影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"take more exercise","meaning":"多做運動","examples":[{"en":"People need to be encouraged to take more exercise.","zh":"人們需要被鼓勵多做運動。"},{"en":"To take more exercise means to do more physical activity.","zh":"take more exercise 指做更多體能活動。"},{"en":"Office workers may take more exercise by walking during lunch breaks.","zh":"辦公室員工可以透過午飯時間散步來多做運動。"},{"en":"If people take more exercise, they may reduce health risks linked to inactivity.","zh":"如果人們多做運動，可能減低與缺乏活動有關的健康風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English.","zh":"這個短語常見於英式英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"for example","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"Adam gives the location of stairs in a train station as an example.","zh":"Adam 以火車站中樓梯的位置作為例子。"},{"en":"For example introduces a specific case that explains or supports a point.","zh":"for example 用來引出解釋或支持某觀點的具體例子。"},{"en":"Healthy snacks, for example fruit and yoghurt, could be sold in the canteen.","zh":"健康小食，例如水果和乳酪，可以在飯堂出售。"},{"en":"If students use examples, their presentation becomes easier to understand.","zh":"如果學生使用例子，簡報會更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces illustration.","zh":"這個短語引出例證。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"location of stairs","meaning":"樓梯的位置","examples":[{"en":"The location of stairs can affect how much people walk.","zh":"樓梯的位置可以影響人們步行多少。"},{"en":"The location of stairs means where the stairs are placed in a building or public space.","zh":"location of stairs 指樓梯在建築或公共空間中的位置。"},{"en":"The location of stairs near the entrance may encourage people to use them.","zh":"樓梯設於入口附近可能鼓勵人們使用。"},{"en":"If stairs are hidden behind a corner, fewer people may choose them.","zh":"如果樓梯藏在角落後面，較少人可能選擇使用。"},{"en":"This phrase connects building design with movement.","zh":"這個短語把建築設計與行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"train station","meaning":"火車站","examples":[{"en":"Adam uses a train station as an example.","zh":"Adam 以火車站作為例子。"},{"en":"A train station is a place where passengers get on and off trains.","zh":"train station 指乘客上落火車的地方。"},{"en":"A busy train station often has stairs, escalators, lifts, and ticket gates.","zh":"繁忙火車站通常有樓梯、扶手電梯、升降機和閘口。"},{"en":"If a train station is designed well, passengers can move safely and quickly.","zh":"如果火車站設計良好，乘客可以安全而快速地流動。"},{"en":"This phrase names a public transport place.","zh":"這個短語指出公共交通地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"reach the stairs before","meaning":"先到達樓梯","examples":[{"en":"People are more likely to use stairs if they reach them before the escalator.","zh":"如果人們先到達樓梯，再到扶手電梯，就更有可能使用樓梯。"},{"en":"To reach the stairs before the escalator means to arrive at the stairs first while walking through a space.","zh":"reach the stairs before the escalator 指人在空間中行走時先到達樓梯。"},{"en":"If students reach the library stairs before the lift, some may choose to walk up.","zh":"如果學生先到達圖書館樓梯，再到升降機，有些人可能會走樓梯。"},{"en":"If stairs come first, people may use them without thinking much.","zh":"如果樓梯先出現，人們可能不太思考就使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes order and position affecting behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述次序和位置如何影響行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"escalator","meaning":"扶手電梯","examples":[{"en":"People may avoid the escalator if the stairs come first.","zh":"如果樓梯先出現，人們可能避開扶手電梯。"},{"en":"An escalator is a moving staircase that carries people between floors.","zh":"escalator 指把人運送到不同樓層的自動移動樓梯。"},{"en":"Shoppers used the escalator to reach the second floor of the mall.","zh":"購物者使用扶手電梯到達商場二樓。"},{"en":"If the escalator is easier to find than the stairs, more people may use it.","zh":"如果扶手電梯比樓梯更容易找到，更多人可能使用它。"},{"en":"This word describes a common transport feature inside buildings and stations.","zh":"這個字描述建築物和車站內常見的交通設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"leave the station","meaning":"離開車站","examples":[{"en":"People choose between stairs and escalators when leaving the station.","zh":"人們離開車站時會在樓梯和扶手電梯之間選擇。"},{"en":"To leave the station means to go out of the train station after arriving or travelling.","zh":"leave the station 指到達或乘車後走出火車站。"},{"en":"Passengers followed the signs when leaving the station.","zh":"乘客離開車站時跟隨指示牌。"},{"en":"If people see stairs first when leaving the station, they may walk instead of using the escalator.","zh":"如果人們離開車站時先看見樓梯，可能會步行而不是使用扶手電梯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exiting a transport place.","zh":"這個短語描述離開交通地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be more likely to take the stairs","meaning":"更有可能行樓梯","examples":[{"en":"People are more likely to take the stairs if they see them first.","zh":"如果人們先看見樓梯，就更有可能行樓梯。"},{"en":"To be more likely to take the stairs means to have a higher chance of choosing the stairs.","zh":"be more likely to take the stairs 指選擇行樓梯的機會較高。"},{"en":"Students are more likely to take the stairs if the lift is crowded.","zh":"如果升降機擠迫，學生更有可能行樓梯。"},{"en":"If stairs are wide, bright, and easy to find, people may choose them more often.","zh":"如果樓梯寬闊、明亮又容易找到，人們可能更常選擇它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increased probability of stair use.","zh":"這個短語描述使用樓梯的可能性增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"increase the width of","meaning":"增加……的闊度","examples":[{"en":"Increasing the width of the stairs can make more people use them.","zh":"增加樓梯的闊度可以令更多人使用它們。"},{"en":"To increase the width of something means to make it wider.","zh":"increase the width of something 指令某物變得更闊。"},{"en":"The school increased the width of the corridor to reduce crowding.","zh":"學校增加走廊的闊度，以減少擠迫。"},{"en":"If stairs are wider, more people can use them comfortably.","zh":"如果樓梯更闊，更多人可以舒適地使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing physical design.","zh":"這個短語描述改變實體設計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同時","examples":[{"en":"Wider stairs allow more people to use them at the same time.","zh":"較闊的樓梯容許更多人同時使用。"},{"en":"At the same time means simultaneously or during the same moment.","zh":"at the same time 指在同一時間或同時。"},{"en":"Several students cannot speak to the teacher at the same time clearly.","zh":"幾名學生不能同時清楚地和老師說話。"},{"en":"If many people can use the stairs at the same time, movement becomes smoother.","zh":"如果很多人能同時使用樓梯，人流會更順暢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes simultaneous action.","zh":"這個短語描述同步行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unconscious process","meaning":"無意識過程","examples":[{"en":"Choosing the stairs can be an unconscious process.","zh":"選擇行樓梯可以是一個無意識過程。"},{"en":"An unconscious process is something people do without deliberately thinking about it.","zh":"unconscious process 指人們沒有刻意思考而做的事情。"},{"en":"Choosing the nearest seat in a classroom can be an unconscious process.","zh":"在課室選擇最近的座位可以是一個無意識過程。"},{"en":"If behaviour is unconscious, small environmental changes can influence it quietly.","zh":"如果行為是無意識的，細微環境變化就能悄悄影響它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes automatic decision-making.","zh":"這個短語描述自動化決策。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be influenced by","meaning":"受到……影響","examples":[{"en":"People’s choices are influenced by minor changes in the environment.","zh":"人們的選擇受到環境中細微變化影響。"},{"en":"To be influenced by something means to be affected by it.","zh":"be influenced by something 指受到某事影響。"},{"en":"Students’ study habits can be influenced by their friends.","zh":"學生的溫習習慣可能受到朋友影響。"},{"en":"If food choices are influenced by menu design, restaurants can encourage healthier decisions.","zh":"如果食物選擇受到餐牌設計影響，餐廳就能鼓勵較健康決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the effect of one thing on another.","zh":"這個短語描述一事物對另一事物的影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"minor modifications","meaning":"細微修改","examples":[{"en":"Minor modifications in the environment can change behaviour.","zh":"環境中的細微修改可以改變行為。"},{"en":"Minor modifications are small changes or adjustments.","zh":"minor modifications 指小型改變或調整。"},{"en":"Minor modifications to a classroom layout can make group work easier.","zh":"課室布局的細微修改可以令小組活動更容易。"},{"en":"If minor modifications make stairs easier to use, people may become more active.","zh":"如果細微修改令樓梯更易使用，人們可能變得更活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes small but purposeful changes.","zh":"這個短語描述小而有目的的改動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in their environment","meaning":"在他們的環境中","examples":[{"en":"People’s behaviour can be influenced by changes in their environment.","zh":"人們的行為可以受到他們環境中的變化影響。"},{"en":"In their environment means in the surroundings where people live, work, or move.","zh":"in their environment 指在人們生活、工作或活動的周邊環境中。"},{"en":"Children’s habits can change when healthy food is visible in their environment.","zh":"當健康食物在孩子的環境中清楚可見時，他們的習慣可能改變。"},{"en":"If stairs are placed clearly in people’s environment, they may walk more.","zh":"如果樓梯在人們的環境中擺放清楚，他們可能步行更多。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to surrounding conditions.","zh":"這個短語指周邊條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not a big change","meaning":"不是很大的改變","examples":[{"en":"Using the stairs may not be a big change.","zh":"使用樓梯可能不是很大的改變。"},{"en":"Not a big change means not a major or difficult change.","zh":"not a big change 指不是重大或困難的改變。"},{"en":"Drinking water instead of a sugary drink is not a big change for some people.","zh":"對有些人來說，喝水代替含糖飲品不是很大的改變。"},{"en":"If a change is small, people may be more willing to accept it.","zh":"如果改變很小，人們可能更願意接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a manageable adjustment.","zh":"這個短語描述容易處理的調整。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"it all adds up","meaning":"累積起來就有效","examples":[{"en":"Small changes add up if they happen every day.","zh":"如果小改變每天發生，累積起來就有效。"},{"en":"It all adds up means small actions become important when combined over time.","zh":"it all adds up 指小行動隨時間結合起來會變得重要。"},{"en":"Walking ten minutes each day may not seem much, but it all adds up.","zh":"每天步行十分鐘看似不多，但累積起來就有效。"},{"en":"If people make small healthy choices repeatedly, the effects can add up.","zh":"如果人們反覆作出小健康選擇，效果可以累積。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses cumulative impact.","zh":"這個短語強調累積影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"talk about exercise","meaning":"談及運動","examples":[{"en":"Adam is not sure whether they should talk about exercise in the presentation.","zh":"Adam 不確定他們是否應在簡報中談及運動。"},{"en":"To talk about exercise means to discuss physical activity as a topic.","zh":"talk about exercise 指把體能活動作為話題討論。"},{"en":"The doctor talked about exercise during the health seminar.","zh":"醫生在健康講座中談及運動。"},{"en":"If the presentation focuses on nutrition, talking about exercise may make it too broad.","zh":"如果簡報聚焦營養，談及運動可能令範圍太廣。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces exercise as a possible subject.","zh":"這個短語引入運動作為可能主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"quite a bit of reading","meaning":"相當多閱讀","examples":[{"en":"The students have done quite a bit of reading about exercise.","zh":"學生已經就運動做了相當多閱讀。"},{"en":"Quite a bit of reading means a fairly large amount of reading.","zh":"quite a bit of reading 指相當大量的閱讀。"},{"en":"The group did quite a bit of reading before writing the report.","zh":"小組在寫報告前做了相當多閱讀。"},{"en":"If students have done quite a bit of reading, they may have more information than they need.","zh":"如果學生做了相當多閱讀，資料可能比需要更多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes substantial preparation.","zh":"這個短語描述充分準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"mean we have","meaning":"意味着我們有","examples":[{"en":"Including exercise will mean they have a very wide focus.","zh":"加入運動內容意味着他們會有很廣的焦點。"},{"en":"Mean we have means result in us having something or lead to that situation.","zh":"mean we have 指導致我們有某情況或結果。"},{"en":"Adding another case study will mean we have a longer presentation.","zh":"加入另一個案例研究意味着我們會有更長的簡報。"},{"en":"If they include exercise, it may mean they have too many topics to cover.","zh":"如果他們加入運動，可能意味着要涵蓋太多題目。"},{"en":"This phrase links a choice with its consequence.","zh":"這個短語把選擇與後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"wide focus","meaning":"很廣的焦點","examples":[{"en":"Talking about exercise would give the presentation a very wide focus.","zh":"談及運動會令簡報有很廣的焦點。"},{"en":"A wide focus means covering many different areas rather than one narrow topic.","zh":"wide focus 指涵蓋許多不同範圍，而不是單一狹窄題目。"},{"en":"A report on health, education, transport, and housing has a very wide focus.","zh":"一份關於健康、教育、交通和房屋的報告有很廣的焦點。"},{"en":"If a presentation has too wide a focus, it may lack depth.","zh":"如果簡報焦點太廣，可能缺乏深度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad scope.","zh":"這個短語描述範圍廣泛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tutor","meaning":"導師","examples":[{"en":"Their tutor told them to focus on nutrition.","zh":"他們的導師告訴他們聚焦於營養。"},{"en":"A tutor is a teacher or adviser who guides students, often in a subject or project.","zh":"tutor 指指導學生的老師或顧問，常見於科目或專題中。"},{"en":"The tutor helped the students narrow their presentation topic.","zh":"導師協助學生收窄簡報題目。"},{"en":"If a tutor gives clear advice, students can avoid going off topic.","zh":"如果導師給出清楚建議，學生可以避免離題。"},{"en":"This word describes an academic guide or teacher.","zh":"這個字描述學術指導者或老師。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"focus on causes and solutions","meaning":"聚焦於成因和解決方法","examples":[{"en":"The tutor wants them to focus on causes and solutions.","zh":"導師希望他們聚焦於成因和解決方法。"},{"en":"To focus on causes and solutions means to concentrate on why a problem happens and how to deal with it.","zh":"focus on causes and solutions 指集中討論問題為何發生，以及如何處理。"},{"en":"A report on pollution should focus on causes and solutions rather than only descriptions.","zh":"關於污染的報告應聚焦於成因和解決方法，而不只是描述。"},{"en":"If students focus on causes and solutions, their presentation becomes more analytical.","zh":"如果學生聚焦於成因和解決方法，簡報會更具分析性。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear structure for discussion.","zh":"這個短語為討論提供清晰結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in terms of","meaning":"從……角度","examples":[{"en":"The presentation should discuss causes and solutions in terms of nutrition.","zh":"簡報應從營養角度討論成因和解決方法。"},{"en":"In terms of means from the point of view of a particular subject or area.","zh":"in terms of 指從某一主題或範疇的角度來看。"},{"en":"The city is expensive in terms of rent, but convenient in terms of transport.","zh":"這個城市從租金角度看很昂貴，但從交通角度看很方便。"},{"en":"If they discuss obesity in terms of nutrition, they should focus on food rather than exercise.","zh":"如果他們從營養角度討論肥胖，就應聚焦食物而不是運動。"},{"en":"This phrase limits the angle of discussion.","zh":"這個短語限制討論角度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"nutrition","meaning":"營養","examples":[{"en":"The tutor wants the presentation to focus on nutrition.","zh":"導師希望簡報聚焦於營養。"},{"en":"Nutrition is the study or practice of how food affects health and the body.","zh":"nutrition 指研究或實踐食物如何影響健康和身體。"},{"en":"Good nutrition includes enough protein, vitamins, fibre, and energy.","zh":"良好營養包括足夠蛋白質、維他命、纖維和能量。"},{"en":"If a presentation focuses on nutrition, it may discuss labels, calories, and food choices.","zh":"如果簡報聚焦營養，可能討論標籤、卡路里和食物選擇。"},{"en":"This word is central to diet and health.","zh":"這個字是飲食和健康的核心概念。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"I suppose so","meaning":"我想也是","examples":[{"en":"Rosie agrees and says, “I suppose so.”","zh":"Rosie 同意並說：「我想也是。」"},{"en":"I suppose so means I think you are probably right, though not very strongly.","zh":"I suppose so 指我覺得你大概是對的，但語氣不是很強烈。"},{"en":"When asked whether the plan was simpler, she said, “I suppose so.”","zh":"當被問到計劃是否較簡單時，她說：「我想也是。」"},{"en":"This phrase shows reluctant or mild agreement.","zh":"這個短語表示有點保留或溫和同意。"},{"en":"It is softer than saying “yes, definitely.”","zh":"它比說 yes, definitely 語氣更柔和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"plenty of information","meaning":"很多資料","examples":[{"en":"The students have plenty of information about nutrition.","zh":"學生有很多關於營養的資料。"},{"en":"Plenty of information means more than enough facts or details.","zh":"plenty of information 指有超過足夠的事實或細節。"},{"en":"The group had plenty of information after reading five articles.","zh":"小組閱讀五篇文章後，有很多資料。"},{"en":"If students have plenty of information, they need to select the best points carefully.","zh":"如果學生有很多資料，就需要仔細選出最佳重點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes having a lot of useful material.","zh":"這個短語描述擁有大量有用材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"that will be simpler","meaning":"那樣會較簡單","examples":[{"en":"Rosie agrees that focusing on nutrition will be simpler.","zh":"Rosie 同意聚焦於營養會較簡單。"},{"en":"That will be simpler means that option will be easier to organise or understand.","zh":"that will be simpler 指該選擇會更容易安排或理解。"},{"en":"If we use three main points instead of six, that will be simpler.","zh":"如果我們用三個重點而不是六個，那樣會較簡單。"},{"en":"If the presentation focuses only on nutrition, the structure will be clearer.","zh":"如果簡報只聚焦營養，結構會更清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a simpler choice with a more complicated one.","zh":"這個短語把較簡單選擇與較複雜選擇作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"what shall we do now?","meaning":"我們現在應該做甚麼？","examples":[{"en":"Adam asks what they should do next.","zh":"Adam 問他們下一步應該做甚麼。"},{"en":"What shall we do now? asks what action should be taken next.","zh":"what shall we do now? 用來問接下來應採取甚麼行動。"},{"en":"After finishing the research, the students asked, “What shall we do now?”","zh":"完成研究後，學生問：「我們現在應該做甚麼？」"},{"en":"This question is useful when a group needs to decide the next step.","zh":"當小組需要決定下一步時，這個問題很有用。"},{"en":"It invites planning and decision-making.","zh":"它邀請大家進行規劃和決策。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"next lecture","meaning":"下一堂課","examples":[{"en":"The students have half an hour before their next lecture.","zh":"學生在下一堂課前有半小時。"},{"en":"The next lecture is the following formal class or talk in a timetable.","zh":"next lecture 指時間表中接下來的正式課堂或講座。"},{"en":"Students bought coffee before their next lecture began.","zh":"學生在下一堂課開始前買咖啡。"},{"en":"If there is time before the next lecture, students can plan their presentation.","zh":"如果下一堂課前有時間，學生可以規劃簡報。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the upcoming class session.","zh":"這個短語指即將到來的課堂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"what we are going to include","meaning":"我們將會包括甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The students need to decide what they are going to include.","zh":"學生需要決定他們將會包括甚麼。"},{"en":"What we are going to include means which information, examples, or sections will be part of the work.","zh":"what we are going to include 指哪些資料、例子或部分會成為作品內容。"},{"en":"Before writing the report, the group decided what they were going to include.","zh":"在寫報告前，小組決定了他們將會包括甚麼。"},{"en":"If students decide what to include early, they can avoid adding irrelevant details.","zh":"如果學生及早決定包括甚麼，就能避免加入無關細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing content.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"what will go where","meaning":"哪部分放在哪裏","examples":[{"en":"The students need to decide what will go where in the presentation.","zh":"學生需要決定簡報中哪部分放在哪裏。"},{"en":"What will go where means which information will be placed in each part or slide.","zh":"what will go where 指哪些資料會放在每一部分或每張投影片中。"},{"en":"The group planned what would go where before designing the poster.","zh":"小組在設計海報前，先規劃哪部分放在哪裏。"},{"en":"If students know what goes where, the presentation will have a clearer structure.","zh":"如果學生知道哪部分放在哪裏，簡報結構會更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising content into the right order.","zh":"這個短語描述把內容按正確次序組織。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"decide what slides we need","meaning":"決定需要哪些投影片","examples":[{"en":"The students can then decide what slides they need.","zh":"學生之後可以決定需要哪些投影片。"},{"en":"To decide what slides we need means to choose which presentation slides should be created.","zh":"decide what slides we need 指選擇需要製作哪些簡報投影片。"},{"en":"After making an outline, the group decided what slides they needed.","zh":"完成大綱後，小組決定需要哪些投影片。"},{"en":"If students decide the slides after choosing content, the visual design becomes easier.","zh":"如果學生在選好內容後才決定投影片，視覺設計會更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planning presentation materials.","zh":"這個短語描述規劃簡報材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 18/task-4":[{"front":"creative activity","meaning":"創意活動","examples":[{"en":"Hand knitting is an important creative activity.","zh":"手工編織是一項重要的創意活動。"},{"en":"A creative activity is something that allows people to make, design or express ideas.","zh":"創意活動是讓人製作、設計或表達想法的活動。"},{"en":"Painting, writing, dancing and knitting are all examples of creative activities.","zh":"繪畫、寫作、跳舞和編織都是創意活動的例子。"},{"en":"Creative activities can help people relax and use their imagination.","zh":"創意活動可以幫助人放鬆並運用想像力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing art, craft and self-expression.","zh":"這個短語適合用於描述藝術、手工藝和自我表達。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hand knitting","meaning":"手工編織","examples":[{"en":"The lecture is about hand knitting.","zh":"這場講座是關於手工編織。"},{"en":"Hand knitting is the activity of making fabric or garments by using needles and yarn by hand.","zh":"手工編織是用手拿編織針和紗線製作布料或衣物的活動。"},{"en":"Hand knitting can be used to make scarves, socks, gloves and sweaters.","zh":"手工編織可以用來製作頸巾、襪子、手套和毛衣。"},{"en":"Unlike machine production, hand knitting involves direct personal skill and time.","zh":"與機器生產不同，手工編織涉及個人技巧和時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes knitting done manually rather than by machine.","zh":"這個短語描述以人手而非機器進行的編織。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"knitted garments","meaning":"針織衣物","examples":[{"en":"Ancient knitted garments have been found in many different countries.","zh":"許多不同國家都發現了古代針織衣物。"},{"en":"Knitted garments are clothes made by knitting yarn into fabric.","zh":"針織衣物是透過把紗線編成布料而製成的衣服。"},{"en":"Sweaters, cardigans and socks are common knitted garments.","zh":"毛衣、開襟冷衫和襪子都是常見針織衣物。"},{"en":"Ancient knitted garments can show what materials and techniques people used in the past.","zh":"古代針織衣物可以顯示過去人們使用的材料和技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in clothing history and textile studies.","zh":"這個短語常見於服裝史和紡織研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be found in","meaning":"在……被發現","examples":[{"en":"Ancient knitted garments have been found in many different countries.","zh":"古代針織衣物在許多不同國家被發現。"},{"en":"To be found in a place means to be discovered or located there.","zh":"在某地被發現意思是在那裏被找到或出現。"},{"en":"Old coins have been found in several archaeological sites.","zh":"舊硬幣在幾個考古遺址被發現。"},{"en":"When similar objects are found in many countries, they may show a widespread practice.","zh":"當類似物件在許多國家被發現，可能顯示一種廣泛做法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing discoveries and locations.","zh":"這個短語適合用於描述發現和地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"global activity","meaning":"全球性活動","examples":[{"en":"Knitting is a global activity with a long history.","zh":"編織是一項有悠久歷史的全球性活動。"},{"en":"A global activity is an activity practised in many parts of the world.","zh":"全球性活動是在世界許多地方都有人從事的活動。"},{"en":"Cooking is a global activity, although different cultures use different methods.","zh":"烹飪是一項全球性活動，雖然不同文化使用不同方法。"},{"en":"Calling knitting a global activity shows that it is not limited to one country or culture.","zh":"把編織稱為全球性活動，顯示它不限於一個國家或文化。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises worldwide participation.","zh":"這個短語強調世界各地的參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"with a long history","meaning":"有悠久歷史","examples":[{"en":"Knitting is a global activity with a long history.","zh":"編織是一項有悠久歷史的全球性活動。"},{"en":"With a long history means something has existed or been practised for a very long time.","zh":"有悠久歷史意思是某事存在或被實踐了很長時間。"},{"en":"Tea drinking is a tradition with a long history in many cultures.","zh":"飲茶在許多文化中都是有悠久歷史的傳統。"},{"en":"An activity with a long history may have changed across different periods and places.","zh":"有悠久歷史的活動可能在不同時期和地方出現變化。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights historical depth.","zh":"這個短語突顯歷史深度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"might well","meaning":"很可能會","examples":[{"en":"When someone says “knitting”, we might well picture an elderly person.","zh":"當有人說「編織」時，我們很可能會想像一位老人。"},{"en":"Might well means there is a good chance that something will happen or be true.","zh":"很可能會意思是某事很有可能發生或屬實。"},{"en":"If people hear the word “library”, they might well imagine a quiet room full of books.","zh":"如果人們聽到「圖書館」這個詞，很可能會想像一間充滿書本的安靜房間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a likely reaction or assumption.","zh":"這個短語適合用於描述可能出現的反應或假設。"},{"en":"It sounds more natural than saying “probably” in some formal contexts.","zh":"在某些正式語境中，它比 “probably” 聽起來更自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"picture an elderly person","meaning":"想像一位老人","examples":[{"en":"We might picture an elderly person sitting by the fire.","zh":"我們可能會想像一位老人坐在火爐旁。"},{"en":"To picture an elderly person means to imagine an old person in your mind.","zh":"想像一位老人意思是在腦中形成一位長者的畫面。"},{"en":"Many people picture an elderly person when they think of traditional crafts.","zh":"許多人想到傳統手工藝時，會想像一位老人。"},{"en":"Mental images can shape how people feel about an activity.","zh":"腦中的畫面可以塑造人們對一項活動的感覺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes imagining a person visually.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺上想像一個人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"elderly person","meaning":"長者","examples":[{"en":"Many people associate knitting with an elderly person.","zh":"許多人把編織與長者聯想在一起。"},{"en":"An elderly person is an older adult, often someone of advanced age.","zh":"長者是年紀較大的成年人，通常指高齡人士。"},{"en":"An elderly person may pass traditional skills on to younger family members.","zh":"長者可能把傳統技能傳授給較年輕的家庭成員。"},{"en":"However, crafts like knitting are not only for elderly people.","zh":"然而，像編織這類手工藝並不只屬於長者。"},{"en":"This phrase is a polite way to refer to an older person.","zh":"這個短語是稱呼年長人士的禮貌說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sitting by the fire","meaning":"坐在火爐旁","examples":[{"en":"We might picture a grandmother sitting by the fire.","zh":"我們可能會想像一位祖母坐在火爐旁。"},{"en":"Sitting by the fire means sitting near a fireplace or source of warmth.","zh":"坐在火爐旁意思是坐在壁爐或暖源附近。"},{"en":"The image of someone sitting by the fire often feels warm and traditional.","zh":"有人坐在火爐旁的畫面通常感覺溫暖而傳統。"},{"en":"In stories, people may sit by the fire while sewing, reading or telling tales.","zh":"在故事中，人們可能坐在火爐旁縫紉、閱讀或講故事。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a cosy domestic image.","zh":"這個短語營造舒適的家庭畫面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"members of the family","meaning":"家庭成員","examples":[{"en":"The grandmother may knit garments for members of the family.","zh":"祖母可能為家庭成員編織衣物。"},{"en":"Members of the family are people who belong to the same family group.","zh":"家庭成員是屬於同一家庭群體的人。"},{"en":"A parent may cook dinner for members of the family every evening.","zh":"家長可能每天晚上為家庭成員煮晚餐。"},{"en":"Making clothes for family members can show care and affection.","zh":"為家庭成員製作衣服可以表達關心和愛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relatives or people in a household.","zh":"這個短語描述親人或同住家人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"homely image","meaning":"溫馨的家庭形象","examples":[{"en":"It is a homely image, but it may make knitting seem old-fashioned.","zh":"這是一個溫馨的家庭形象，但它可能令編織顯得老套。"},{"en":"A homely image is a warm, simple and comfortable picture of home life.","zh":"溫馨的家庭形象是關於家庭生活的溫暖、簡單和舒適畫面。"},{"en":"A grandmother knitting by the fire creates a homely image.","zh":"祖母在火爐旁編織營造出溫馨的家庭形象。"},{"en":"Homely images can feel comforting, but they may also make an activity seem old-fashioned.","zh":"溫馨家庭形象可以令人感到安慰，但也可能令活動顯得過時。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a domestic and familiar picture.","zh":"這個短語描述家庭化而熟悉的畫面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lead someone to feel that","meaning":"令某人覺得……","examples":[{"en":"The image may lead people to feel that knitting belongs to the past.","zh":"這個形象可能令人覺得編織屬於過去。"},{"en":"To lead someone to feel that something is true means to make them think or believe it.","zh":"令某人覺得某事是真的，意思是使他們這樣想或相信。"},{"en":"Old photographs may lead people to feel that a craft is no longer modern.","zh":"舊照片可能令人覺得一種手工藝已不再現代。"},{"en":"Images and stereotypes can influence how people judge an activity.","zh":"形象和刻板印象可以影響人們如何判斷一項活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how one idea creates another reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述一個想法如何引起另一種反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"activity of the past","meaning":"過去的活動","examples":[{"en":"Some people think knitting is an activity of the past.","zh":"有些人認為編織是過去的活動。"},{"en":"An activity of the past is something people associate with earlier times rather than the present.","zh":"過去的活動是人們與較早時代而非現在聯想在一起的事情。"},{"en":"Letter writing is sometimes seen as an activity of the past.","zh":"寫信有時被視為過去的活動。"},{"en":"An activity can look old-fashioned but still become popular again.","zh":"一項活動可以看似老套，但仍重新流行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something viewed as outdated.","zh":"這個短語描述被視為過時的事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"indeed","meaning":"確實；事實上","examples":[{"en":"Indeed, knitting was once predicted to vanish from everyday life.","zh":"確實，編織曾被預測會從日常生活中消失。"},{"en":"Indeed is used to emphasise or confirm a point.","zh":"確實或事實上用來強調或確認一個重點。"},{"en":"Many people thought handwriting would disappear; indeed, fewer people write long letters now.","zh":"許多人以為手寫會消失；確實，現在較少人寫長信。"},{"en":"This word often strengthens the sentence that follows.","zh":"這個詞通常加強後面的句子。"},{"en":"It is common in formal speech and writing.","zh":"它常見於正式口語和寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"during the previous decade","meaning":"在前一個十年","examples":[{"en":"During the previous decade, knitting was predicted to vanish.","zh":"在前一個十年，編織被預測會消失。"},{"en":"During the previous decade means in the ten-year period before the time being discussed.","zh":"在前一個十年意思是在所討論時間之前的十年期間。"},{"en":"During the previous decade, many people began using smartphones daily.","zh":"在前一個十年，許多人開始每天使用智能手機。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when referring to a recent historical period.","zh":"當提及較近的歷史時期時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It gives a clear time frame of ten years.","zh":"它提供十年的清楚時間框架。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be predicted to","meaning":"被預測會……","examples":[{"en":"Knitting was predicted to vanish from everyday life.","zh":"編織被預測會從日常生活中消失。"},{"en":"To be predicted to do something means people expected it to happen in the future.","zh":"被預測會做某事意思是人們預期它將來會發生。"},{"en":"Some traditional jobs were predicted to disappear because of machines.","zh":"有些傳統工作因機器出現而被預測會消失。"},{"en":"Predictions can be wrong when social trends change unexpectedly.","zh":"當社會趨勢意外改變，預測可以出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing forecasts.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論預測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"vanish from","meaning":"從……消失","examples":[{"en":"Knitting was predicted to vanish from everyday life.","zh":"編織被預測會從日常生活中消失。"},{"en":"To vanish from a place means to disappear from it completely.","zh":"從某處消失意思是完全不再在那裏出現。"},{"en":"Some old skills seemed to vanish from schools when technology became popular.","zh":"當科技流行後，有些舊技能似乎從學校消失。"},{"en":"A practice may vanish from daily life if younger people stop learning it.","zh":"如果年輕人停止學習，一種做法可能從日常生活中消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disappearance from a particular area or context.","zh":"這個短語描述從某個地方或語境消失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"everyday life","meaning":"日常生活","examples":[{"en":"Knitting was predicted to disappear from everyday life.","zh":"編織被預測會從日常生活中消失。"},{"en":"Everyday life means ordinary daily activities and routines.","zh":"日常生活意思是普通每日活動和常規。"},{"en":"Mobile phones have become part of everyday life for many people.","zh":"手機已成為許多人日常生活的一部分。"},{"en":"When a craft returns to everyday life, it becomes more than a hobby for specialists.","zh":"當一種手工藝重回日常生活，它就不只是專家的興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes normal daily living.","zh":"這個短語描述正常每日生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"for although","meaning":"雖然……但是","examples":[{"en":"For although humans have knitted clothing for a long time, the skill declined.","zh":"雖然人類編織衣服已有很長時間，但是這項技能衰退了。"},{"en":"For although means because, although; it introduces a contrast with an explanation.","zh":"for although 意思是「因為雖然……」，用來引入帶解釋的對比。"},{"en":"For although the skill was ancient, machines changed how clothes were made.","zh":"雖然這項技能古老，但是機器改變了衣物製作方式。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and literary.","zh":"這個短語聽起來較正式和文學化。"},{"en":"It helps link a historical fact with an unexpected result.","zh":"它有助把歷史事實與意外結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sew and knit","meaning":"縫製和編織","examples":[{"en":"Humans have sewn and knitted their own clothing for a very long time.","zh":"人類縫製和編織自己的衣服已有很長時間。"},{"en":"To sew and knit means to make or repair clothing using stitching and knitting methods.","zh":"縫製和編織意思是使用針縫和編織方法製作或修補衣物。"},{"en":"In the past, many families learned to sew and knit at home.","zh":"在過去，許多家庭在家中學習縫製和編織。"},{"en":"Sewing and knitting were practical skills before cheap factory clothing became common.","zh":"在廉價工廠衣物普及前，縫製和編織是實用技能。"},{"en":"This phrase groups two traditional clothing-making skills.","zh":"這個短語集合兩種傳統製衣技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"craft-based skills","meaning":"手工藝技能","examples":[{"en":"Many craft-based skills went into decline.","zh":"許多手工藝技能開始衰退。"},{"en":"Craft-based skills are practical making skills done by hand or with simple tools.","zh":"手工藝技能是用手或簡單工具完成的實用製作技能。"},{"en":"Pottery, weaving, embroidery and knitting are craft-based skills.","zh":"陶藝、編織、刺繡和手工編織都是手工藝技能。"},{"en":"Craft-based skills can decline when machines make products faster and cheaper.","zh":"當機器更快更便宜地製造產品，手工藝技能可能衰退。"},{"en":"This phrase describes skills linked to handmade production.","zh":"這個短語描述與手製生產有關的技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go into decline","meaning":"開始衰退","examples":[{"en":"Many craft-based skills went into decline when machines took over.","zh":"當機器接管後，許多手工藝技能開始衰退。"},{"en":"To go into decline means to become less common, less popular or less successful.","zh":"開始衰退意思是變得較不常見、較不流行或較不成功。"},{"en":"Traditional letter writing went into decline after email became common.","zh":"電郵普及後，傳統寫信開始衰退。"},{"en":"Skills can go into decline if fewer people teach them to the next generation.","zh":"如果較少人把技能教給下一代，技能可能開始衰退。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a downward trend.","zh":"這個短語描述下降趨勢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"industrial machines","meaning":"工業機器","examples":[{"en":"Industrial machines took over many clothing-production tasks.","zh":"工業機器接管了許多衣物生產工作。"},{"en":"Industrial machines are large machines used in factories to produce goods.","zh":"工業機器是在工廠用來生產貨品的大型機器。"},{"en":"Industrial machines can make clothing much faster than hand workers.","zh":"工業機器可以比手工工人更快製作衣物。"},{"en":"The rise of industrial machines changed the value of many craft skills.","zh":"工業機器的興起改變了許多手工技能的價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing manufacturing and industry.","zh":"這個短語常見於製造業和工業討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take over","meaning":"取代；接管","examples":[{"en":"Industrial machines took over from hand sewing and knitting.","zh":"工業機器取代了手工縫製和編織。"},{"en":"To take over means to replace someone or something in doing a task.","zh":"取代或接管意思是在執行任務方面代替某人或某物。"},{"en":"Computers took over many office tasks that people once did by hand.","zh":"電腦接管了許多以前由人手完成的辦公室工作。"},{"en":"When machines take over, human skills may become less necessary in production.","zh":"當機器接管，人的技能在生產中可能變得較不必要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes replacement or control.","zh":"這個短語描述取代或控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mainly because","meaning":"主要因為","examples":[{"en":"The skills declined mainly because they were no longer passed down.","zh":"這些技能衰退，主要因為它們不再代代相傳。"},{"en":"Mainly because means mostly for this reason.","zh":"主要因為意思是大多數原因在於這一點。"},{"en":"The club closed mainly because too few students joined.","zh":"該學會關閉，主要因為太少學生參加。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the most important cause.","zh":"這個短語指出最重要原因。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why something happened.","zh":"當解釋某事為何發生時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be passed down from one generation to another","meaning":"代代相傳","examples":[{"en":"Knitting was no longer passed down from one generation to another.","zh":"編織不再代代相傳。"},{"en":"To be passed down from one generation to another means to be taught or given from older people to younger people.","zh":"代代相傳意思是由年長一代教給或傳給年輕一代。"},{"en":"Family recipes are often passed down from one generation to another.","zh":"家庭食譜常常代代相傳。"},{"en":"Skills may disappear if they are not passed down to children and grandchildren.","zh":"如果技能沒有傳給子女和孫輩，它們可能會消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cultural transmission.","zh":"這個短語描述文化傳承。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"that’s all changing","meaning":"這一切正在改變","examples":[{"en":"However, that is all changing as interest in knitting rises.","zh":"然而，隨着對編織的興趣上升，這一切正在改變。"},{"en":"That’s all changing means the situation is now becoming different.","zh":"這一切正在改變意思是情況現在正變得不同。"},{"en":"People once thought handwriting was dying out, but that is all changing in calligraphy classes.","zh":"人們曾以為手寫正在消失，但在書法班中，這一切正在改變。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a shift from an old trend to a new one.","zh":"這個短語引入由舊趨勢到新趨勢的轉變。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken explanations.","zh":"它常見於口頭解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"interest in","meaning":"對……的興趣","examples":[{"en":"Interest in knitting classes is rising in many countries.","zh":"在許多國家，人們對編織班的興趣正在上升。"},{"en":"Interest in something means curiosity, attention or enthusiasm about it.","zh":"對某事的興趣意思是對它有好奇、關注或熱情。"},{"en":"Interest in traditional crafts has increased among young people.","zh":"年輕人對傳統手工藝的興趣有所增加。"},{"en":"Rising interest can lead to more classes, shops and online communities.","zh":"興趣上升可以帶來更多課程、商店和網上社群。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public or personal attention.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾或個人關注。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"knitting classes","meaning":"編織班","examples":[{"en":"Interest in knitting classes is rising.","zh":"人們對編織班的興趣正在上升。"},{"en":"Knitting classes are lessons where people learn how to knit.","zh":"編織班是教人如何編織的課堂。"},{"en":"Beginners may join knitting classes to learn basic stitches and patterns.","zh":"初學者可能參加編織班，學習基本針法和圖樣。"},{"en":"Classes can help people learn faster than trying alone.","zh":"課堂可以幫助人比獨自嘗試更快學會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised instruction in knitting.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的編織教學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be actually rising","meaning":"實際上正在上升","examples":[{"en":"Interest in knitting classes is actually rising.","zh":"人們對編織班的興趣實際上正在上升。"},{"en":"Actually rising means really increasing, perhaps contrary to what people expected.","zh":"實際上正在上升意思是真的在增加，可能與人們預期相反。"},{"en":"Demand for handmade goods is actually rising in some cities.","zh":"在一些城市，對手製品的需求實際上正在上升。"},{"en":"The word “actually” suggests the fact may surprise listeners.","zh":"“actually” 這個詞暗示該事實可能令聽眾驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a real upward trend.","zh":"這個短語描述真實的上升趨勢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"more and more people","meaning":"越來越多人","examples":[{"en":"More and more people are seeking formal instruction.","zh":"越來越多人正在尋求正式教學。"},{"en":"More and more people means an increasing number of people.","zh":"越來越多人意思是人數正在增加。"},{"en":"More and more people are learning crafts to reduce stress.","zh":"越來越多人學習手工藝以減壓。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a growing trend.","zh":"當描述增長趨勢時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It emphasises continuous increase.","zh":"它強調持續增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"seek formal instruction","meaning":"尋求正式教學","examples":[{"en":"More people are seeking formal instruction in knitting.","zh":"更多人正在尋求編織方面的正式教學。"},{"en":"To seek formal instruction means to look for organised teaching from a teacher or course.","zh":"尋求正式教學意思是尋找由老師或課程提供的有組織教導。"},{"en":"A beginner may seek formal instruction instead of learning only from videos.","zh":"初學者可能尋求正式教學，而不是只靠影片自學。"},{"en":"Formal instruction can help learners build correct habits from the start.","zh":"正式教學可以幫助學習者從一開始建立正確習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes looking for structured learning.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找有結構的學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the skill","meaning":"在這項技能方面","examples":[{"en":"People are seeking formal instruction in the skill of knitting.","zh":"人們正在這項編織技能方面尋求正式教學。"},{"en":"In the skill means in that particular ability or practical technique.","zh":"在這項技能方面意思是在該特定能力或實用技巧方面。"},{"en":"Students may need guidance in the skill of public speaking.","zh":"學生可能需要在公開演說這項技能方面得到指導。"},{"en":"Learning a skill often requires practice, feedback and patience.","zh":"學習技能通常需要練習、回饋和耐性。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the specific ability being learned.","zh":"這個短語指出正在學習的具體能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"with that trend","meaning":"隨着這股趨勢","examples":[{"en":"With that trend, sales of knitting equipment are increasing.","zh":"隨着這股趨勢，編織工具的銷售正在增加。"},{"en":"With that trend means as a result of or alongside that development.","zh":"隨着這股趨勢意思是由於或伴隨着該發展。"},{"en":"More people are learning cooking; with that trend, sales of kitchen tools have risen.","zh":"更多人學習烹飪；隨着這股趨勢，廚具銷量上升。"},{"en":"This phrase links one social change to another result.","zh":"這個短語把一個社會變化與另一個結果連起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing trends and consequences.","zh":"當討論趨勢和後果時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an increase in","meaning":"……的增加","examples":[{"en":"There has been an increase in sales figures for knitting equipment.","zh":"編織工具銷售數字有所增加。"},{"en":"An increase in something means a rise in amount, number or level.","zh":"某事的增加意思是數量、數目或水平上升。"},{"en":"There has been an increase in students joining craft workshops.","zh":"參加手工藝工作坊的學生人數有所增加。"},{"en":"An increase in demand can encourage shops to sell more supplies.","zh":"需求增加可以鼓勵商店售賣更多用品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upward change.","zh":"這個短語描述上升變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sales figures","meaning":"銷售數字","examples":[{"en":"Sales figures for knitting equipment are rising.","zh":"編織工具的銷售數字正在上升。"},{"en":"Sales figures are numbers showing how much has been sold.","zh":"銷售數字是顯示已售出多少的數字。"},{"en":"A shop checks sales figures to see which products are popular.","zh":"商店查看銷售數字，以了解哪些產品受歡迎。"},{"en":"Rising sales figures may show that more people are interested in a hobby.","zh":"銷售數字上升可能顯示更多人對某興趣有興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business and market reports.","zh":"這個短語常見於商業和市場報告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"knitting equipment","meaning":"編織工具","examples":[{"en":"Sales of knitting equipment have increased.","zh":"編織工具的銷售有所增加。"},{"en":"Knitting equipment means tools and materials used for knitting.","zh":"編織工具意思是用於編織的工具和材料。"},{"en":"Needles, yarn, stitch markers and patterns are examples of knitting equipment.","zh":"編織針、紗線、記號扣和圖樣都是編織工具的例子。"},{"en":"Beginners need only basic knitting equipment to start.","zh":"初學者只需要基本編織工具便能開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the supplies needed for knitting.","zh":"這個短語描述編織所需用品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be taught to","meaning":"被教授去……","examples":[{"en":"Many people want to be taught to knit.","zh":"許多人想被教授如何編織。"},{"en":"To be taught to do something means to receive instruction on how to do it.","zh":"被教授去做某事意思是接受如何做該事的教導。"},{"en":"Children may be taught to sew simple stitches in art class.","zh":"孩子可能在美術課被教授縫簡單針法。"},{"en":"Being taught by someone experienced can reduce mistakes.","zh":"由有經驗的人教授可以減少錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning through instruction.","zh":"這個短語描述透過教導學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at a time when","meaning":"在……的時代","examples":[{"en":"People want to learn knitting at a time when machines can do the job.","zh":"人們在機器可以完成這項工作的時代想學編織。"},{"en":"At a time when means during a period in which a particular situation exists.","zh":"在某情況存在的時代意思是在某種情況出現的時期。"},{"en":"People are returning to handwriting at a time when typing is easier than ever.","zh":"人們在打字比以往更容易的時代重新重視手寫。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights an interesting contrast between context and behaviour.","zh":"這個短語突顯背景與行為之間的有趣對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing social change.","zh":"當討論社會變化時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"readily","meaning":"輕易地","examples":[{"en":"A machine can readily do the job for them.","zh":"機器可以輕易地替他們完成這項工作。"},{"en":"Readily means easily or without difficulty.","zh":"輕易地意思是容易或沒有困難地。"},{"en":"Modern machines can readily produce large quantities of fabric.","zh":"現代機器可以輕易地生產大量布料。"},{"en":"If something can be done readily by machine, people may still do it by hand for pleasure.","zh":"即使某事可以由機器輕易完成，人們仍可能為了樂趣而親手做。"},{"en":"This word describes ease and availability.","zh":"這個詞描述容易程度和可行性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"do the job","meaning":"完成這項工作","examples":[{"en":"A machine can readily do the job of knitting.","zh":"機器可以輕易完成編織這項工作。"},{"en":"To do the job means to perform the task that needs to be done.","zh":"完成這項工作意思是執行需要完成的任務。"},{"en":"A simple tool can do the job if it is used correctly.","zh":"如果使用得當，簡單工具也可以完成這項工作。"},{"en":"Machines may do the job faster, but handmade work can feel more personal.","zh":"機器可以更快完成工作，但手作品可以感覺更有個人味道。"},{"en":"This phrase describes completing a task.","zh":"這個短語描述完成任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"handicraft","meaning":"手工藝","examples":[{"en":"Knitting, as a handicraft, has numerous benefits.","zh":"編織作為一種手工藝，有許多好處。"},{"en":"A handicraft is an activity in which people make things by hand.","zh":"手工藝是人們用手製作東西的活動。"},{"en":"Basket-making, embroidery and pottery are examples of handicrafts.","zh":"編籃、刺繡和陶藝都是手工藝例子。"},{"en":"Handicrafts can be practical, creative and relaxing.","zh":"手工藝可以實用、有創意並令人放鬆。"},{"en":"This word describes handmade craft work.","zh":"這個詞描述手製工藝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"numerous benefits","meaning":"許多好處","examples":[{"en":"Knitting has numerous benefits for those doing it.","zh":"編織對從事這件事的人有許多好處。"},{"en":"Numerous benefits means many advantages or positive effects.","zh":"許多好處意思是很多優點或正面效果。"},{"en":"Exercise has numerous benefits for both physical and mental health.","zh":"運動對身體和心理健康都有許多好處。"},{"en":"Knitting may bring numerous benefits, from saving money to reducing stress.","zh":"編織可能帶來許多好處，由慳錢到減壓都有。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises many positive results.","zh":"這個短語強調許多正面結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"those doing it","meaning":"從事這件事的人","examples":[{"en":"Knitting benefits those doing it.","zh":"編織令從事這件事的人受益。"},{"en":"Those doing it means the people who are carrying out the activity.","zh":"從事這件事的人意思是正在進行該活動的人。"},{"en":"A hobby may benefit those doing it more than those only watching.","zh":"一項興趣可能比起只觀看的人，更令從事者受益。"},{"en":"People doing a craft can gain skill, focus and satisfaction.","zh":"做手工藝的人可以獲得技能、專注力和滿足感。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the participants in an activity.","zh":"這個短語指活動參與者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"let’s consider","meaning":"讓我們考慮","examples":[{"en":"Let’s consider what some of these benefits might be.","zh":"讓我們考慮這些好處可能是甚麼。"},{"en":"Let’s consider means let us think about or examine something.","zh":"讓我們考慮意思是讓我們思考或檢視某事。"},{"en":"Let’s consider why traditional crafts are becoming popular again.","zh":"讓我們考慮為何傳統手工藝再次流行。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase to guide listeners to the next point.","zh":"講者使用這個短語引導聽眾進入下一個重點。"},{"en":"It is common in lectures and presentations.","zh":"它常見於講座和匯報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"在過去","examples":[{"en":"Many people knitted garments in the past because they could not afford clothes.","zh":"在過去，許多人編織衣物，因為他們負擔不起買衣服。"},{"en":"In the past means at an earlier time before now.","zh":"在過去意思是在現在之前的較早時間。"},{"en":"In the past, families often repaired clothes instead of throwing them away.","zh":"在過去，家庭常會修補衣物，而不是丟掉。"},{"en":"Looking at the past helps explain why certain skills were once necessary.","zh":"觀察過去有助解釋為何某些技能曾經必要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing old and modern life.","zh":"當比較舊時和現代生活時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"afford to buy","meaning":"負擔得起購買","examples":[{"en":"Many people knitted because they could not afford to buy clothes.","zh":"許多人編織，是因為他們負擔不起買衣服。"},{"en":"To afford to buy something means to have enough money to purchase it.","zh":"負擔得起購買某物意思是有足夠金錢購買它。"},{"en":"Some families could not afford to buy warm coats every winter.","zh":"有些家庭每年冬天都負擔不起買保暖外套。"},{"en":"When people cannot afford to buy something, they may make it themselves.","zh":"當人們買不起某物時，可能會自己製作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on financial ability.","zh":"這個短語重點是財政能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be helpful if","meaning":"如果……會有幫助","examples":[{"en":"Knitting can be helpful if you are experiencing economic hardship.","zh":"如果你正在經歷經濟困難，編織會有幫助。"},{"en":"Be helpful if means useful in a particular situation.","zh":"如果某情況下會有幫助，意思是在該特定情況中有用。"},{"en":"Cooking at home can be helpful if a family wants to save money.","zh":"如果家庭想慳錢，在家煮飯會有幫助。"},{"en":"A skill is practical when it is helpful in difficult circumstances.","zh":"當一項技能在困難情況中有幫助，它就是實用的。"},{"en":"This phrase connects usefulness with a condition.","zh":"這個短語把用途與條件連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"experience economic hardship","meaning":"經歷經濟困難","examples":[{"en":"Knitting can help people experiencing economic hardship.","zh":"編織可以幫助正在經歷經濟困難的人。"},{"en":"To experience economic hardship means to face financial difficulty.","zh":"經歷經濟困難意思是面對財政困難。"},{"en":"Families experiencing economic hardship may look for ways to reduce spending.","zh":"經歷經濟困難的家庭可能尋找減少開支的方法。"},{"en":"Practical skills can support people during difficult financial times.","zh":"實用技能可以在人面對財政困難時提供支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a period of money-related difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述與金錢有關的困難時期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"warm winter clothes","meaning":"保暖冬衣","examples":[{"en":"Several children may need warm winter clothes.","zh":"幾個孩子可能需要保暖冬衣。"},{"en":"Warm winter clothes are clothes that keep people warm in cold weather.","zh":"保暖冬衣是在寒冷天氣中令人保暖的衣物。"},{"en":"Scarves, hats, gloves and sweaters are warm winter clothes.","zh":"頸巾、帽、手套和毛衣都是保暖冬衣。"},{"en":"Knitting can help families make warm winter clothes at lower cost.","zh":"編織可以幫助家庭以較低成本製作保暖冬衣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clothing for cold seasons.","zh":"這個短語描述寒冷季節的衣物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"save someone money","meaning":"幫某人慳錢","examples":[{"en":"Knitting may save parents a lot of money.","zh":"編織可能幫家長慳很多錢。"},{"en":"To save someone money means to reduce the amount that person has to spend.","zh":"幫某人慳錢意思是減少那人需要花費的金額。"},{"en":"Repairing clothes at home can save families money.","zh":"在家修補衣服可以幫家庭慳錢。"},{"en":"A skill that saves money can be useful during economic hardship.","zh":"能慳錢的技能在經濟困難時會很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes financial benefit.","zh":"這個短語描述財務好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the results of","meaning":"……的成果","examples":[{"en":"The results of knitting your own clothes can be very rewarding.","zh":"自己編織衣服的成果可以很有成就感。"},{"en":"The results of something are the outcomes or products that come from it.","zh":"某事的成果是由它產生的結果或作品。"},{"en":"The results of careful practice can be seen in a cleaner finished scarf.","zh":"仔細練習的成果可以在更整齊的完成頸巾中看見。"},{"en":"People often feel proud when they can see the results of their effort.","zh":"當人們能看見自己努力的成果，通常會感到自豪。"},{"en":"This phrase connects effort with outcome.","zh":"這個短語把努力與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"knit your own clothes","meaning":"自己編織衣服","examples":[{"en":"Knitting your own clothes can be very rewarding.","zh":"自己編織衣服可以很有成就感。"},{"en":"To knit your own clothes means to make clothes for yourself by knitting.","zh":"自己編織衣服意思是透過編織為自己製作衣物。"},{"en":"Someone may knit their own sweater to choose the exact colour and size.","zh":"有人可能自己編織毛衣，以選擇準確顏色和尺寸。"},{"en":"Making your own clothes can give a strong sense of independence.","zh":"自己製作衣服可以帶來強烈獨立感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes self-made clothing through knitting.","zh":"這個短語描述透過編織製作自用衣物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rewarding","meaning":"有成就感的","examples":[{"en":"The results of knitting can be very rewarding.","zh":"編織的成果可以很有成就感。"},{"en":"Rewarding means giving satisfaction, pleasure or a sense of achievement.","zh":"有成就感的意思是帶來滿足、快樂或成就感。"},{"en":"Finishing a handmade scarf can feel rewarding after many hours of work.","zh":"花很多小時完成一條手織頸巾後，會感到很有成就感。"},{"en":"A rewarding activity does not have to be easy.","zh":"有成就感的活動不一定容易。"},{"en":"This word describes emotional value from effort.","zh":"這個詞描述努力帶來的情感價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"even though","meaning":"即使","examples":[{"en":"The results can be rewarding even though the skills are basic.","zh":"即使技巧很基本，成果也可以很有成就感。"},{"en":"Even though means although.","zh":"即使意思是雖然。"},{"en":"The scarf looked beautiful even though the pattern was simple.","zh":"即使圖樣簡單，那條頸巾也看起來很美。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces contrast between two ideas.","zh":"這個短語引入兩個想法之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when the result seems surprising despite a limitation.","zh":"當結果在某限制下仍令人意外時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get going","meaning":"開始做起來","examples":[{"en":"The skills you need to get going are quite basic.","zh":"你開始做起來所需的技巧相當基本。"},{"en":"To get going means to start doing an activity.","zh":"開始做起來意思是開始進行一項活動。"},{"en":"Beginners only need a few simple stitches to get going with knitting.","zh":"初學者只需要幾個簡單針法，就可以開始編織。"},{"en":"Once people get going, they often become more confident through practice.","zh":"一旦人們開始做起來，通常會透過練習變得更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes starting a task.","zh":"這個短語描述開始一項任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"quite basic","meaning":"相當基本","examples":[{"en":"The skills needed to start knitting are quite basic.","zh":"開始編織所需的技巧相當基本。"},{"en":"Quite basic means fairly simple and not advanced.","zh":"相當基本意思是頗簡單而不進階。"},{"en":"A beginner knitting class teaches quite basic skills at first.","zh":"初級編織班一開始教授相當基本的技巧。"},{"en":"Basic skills are important because more complex work depends on them.","zh":"基本技巧很重要，因為更複雜作品依賴它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a low level of difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述較低難度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"financial outlay","meaning":"金錢開支","examples":[{"en":"The financial outlay for knitting is minimal.","zh":"編織的金錢開支很少。"},{"en":"Financial outlay means the amount of money you need to spend to start or do something.","zh":"金錢開支意思是開始或進行某事所需花費的金額。"},{"en":"The financial outlay for jogging can be low if you already have suitable shoes.","zh":"如果你已有合適鞋履，慢跑的金錢開支可以很低。"},{"en":"A low financial outlay makes a hobby more accessible.","zh":"低金錢開支令一項興趣更容易參與。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing costs.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論成本。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"minimal","meaning":"很少；最低限度的","examples":[{"en":"The financial outlay is minimal.","zh":"金錢開支很少。"},{"en":"Minimal means very small or the least amount needed.","zh":"很少或最低限度的意思是非常少或所需最少量。"},{"en":"The materials for a simple knitting project may cost only a minimal amount.","zh":"簡單編織項目的材料可能只需很少費用。"},{"en":"Minimal cost can encourage beginners to try a new hobby.","zh":"很低成本可以鼓勵初學者嘗試新興趣。"},{"en":"This word describes a very low level or amount.","zh":"這個詞描述非常低的水平或數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"significant benefits","meaning":"重要好處","examples":[{"en":"The more significant benefits today are linked to well-being.","zh":"今天更重要的好處與身心健康有關。"},{"en":"Significant benefits are important advantages or positive effects.","zh":"重要好處是重要的優點或正面效果。"},{"en":"Creative hobbies can have significant benefits for stress reduction.","zh":"創意興趣可以對減壓有重要好處。"},{"en":"Significant benefits may be emotional rather than financial.","zh":"重要好處可能是情緒上的，而不是金錢上的。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the most important positive effects.","zh":"這個短語突顯最重要的正面效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be to do with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The benefits are to do with well-being.","zh":"這些好處與身心健康有關。"},{"en":"To be to do with something means to be connected with it.","zh":"與某事有關意思是與它有聯繫。"},{"en":"The problem is to do with poor planning, not lack of effort.","zh":"問題與規劃不足有關，而不是努力不足。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in spoken English.","zh":"這個短語常見於口語英語。"},{"en":"It helps explain what a topic is related to.","zh":"它有助解釋主題與甚麼相關。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"well-being","meaning":"身心健康","examples":[{"en":"Knitting can have benefits for well-being.","zh":"編織可以對身心健康有好處。"},{"en":"Well-being means physical, mental and emotional health.","zh":"身心健康意思是身體、心理和情緒健康。"},{"en":"Activities such as knitting, walking and reading can support well-being.","zh":"編織、散步和閱讀等活動可以支持身心健康。"},{"en":"Well-being is not only about avoiding illness but also feeling balanced and fulfilled.","zh":"身心健康不只是避免疾病，也包括感到平衡和充實。"},{"en":"This word is common in health and lifestyle discussions.","zh":"這個詞常見於健康和生活方式討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"it is estimated that","meaning":"據估計","examples":[{"en":"It is estimated that we spend up to nine hours a day online.","zh":"據估計，我們每天花多達九小時上網。"},{"en":"It is estimated that means experts or sources believe a figure is approximately true.","zh":"據估計意思是專家或資料來源相信某數字大約正確。"},{"en":"It is estimated that many adults spend several hours a day looking at screens.","zh":"據估計，許多成年人每天花數小時看屏幕。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when exact numbers are difficult to know.","zh":"當準確數字難以知道時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It signals that the number is an estimate.","zh":"它表示該數字是一個估計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spend up to","meaning":"花多達……","examples":[{"en":"Many people spend up to nine hours a day online.","zh":"許多人每天花多達九小時上網。"},{"en":"To spend up to an amount means to use as much as that amount, but not necessarily always.","zh":"花多達某數量意思是最多使用到該數量，但不一定每次都如此。"},{"en":"Some students spend up to two hours a night on homework.","zh":"有些學生每晚花多達兩小時做功課。"},{"en":"Saying “up to” gives the maximum possible amount.","zh":"說 “up to” 提供可能的最高數量。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing time, money or quantity.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論時間、金錢或數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"craft-based","meaning":"以手工藝為本的","examples":[{"en":"Doing something craft-based with our hands makes us feel good.","zh":"用雙手做以手工藝為本的事情會令我們感覺良好。"},{"en":"Craft-based means connected with making things by hand.","zh":"以手工藝為本的意思是與用手製作東西有關。"},{"en":"A craft-based hobby may involve sewing, knitting, pottery or woodwork.","zh":"以手工藝為本的興趣可能包括縫紉、編織、陶藝或木工。"},{"en":"Craft-based activities can slow people down and encourage focus.","zh":"手工藝活動可以令人放慢節奏並鼓勵專注。"},{"en":"This adjective describes activities rooted in hand-making.","zh":"這個形容詞描述以手作為核心的活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make us feel good","meaning":"令我們感覺良好","examples":[{"en":"Craft-based activities can make us feel good.","zh":"手工藝活動可以令我們感覺良好。"},{"en":"To make us feel good means to improve our mood or give us satisfaction.","zh":"令我們感覺良好意思是改善我們的心情或給我們滿足感。"},{"en":"Finishing a handmade item can make us feel good because we see the result of our effort.","zh":"完成一件手作品可以令我們感覺良好，因為我們看見努力的成果。"},{"en":"Activities that use the hands can calm the mind and make people feel good.","zh":"使用雙手的活動可以令心神平靜，並令人感覺良好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive emotional effect.","zh":"這個短語描述正面的情緒效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"release someone from","meaning":"使某人從……中釋放","examples":[{"en":"Knitting releases people from the stress of modern life.","zh":"編織使人從現代生活的壓力中釋放出來。"},{"en":"To release someone from something means to free them from pressure, worry or restriction.","zh":"使某人從某事中釋放意思是讓他們擺脫壓力、憂慮或限制。"},{"en":"A quiet hobby can release people from the noise of a busy day.","zh":"安靜的興趣可以使人從忙碌一天的嘈雜中釋放出來。"},{"en":"Knitting may not remove stress completely, but it can give mental relief.","zh":"編織未必完全消除壓力，但可以帶來心理舒緩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional or practical freedom.","zh":"這個短語描述情緒或實際上的自由。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the stress of","meaning":"……的壓力","examples":[{"en":"Knitting can release us from the stress of a fast-paced life.","zh":"編織可以使我們從快節奏生活的壓力中釋放出來。"},{"en":"The stress of something means the pressure or worry caused by it.","zh":"某事的壓力意思是由它造成的壓迫感或憂慮。"},{"en":"The stress of exams can make students sleep badly.","zh":"考試的壓力可以令學生睡得不好。"},{"en":"People often look for hobbies to escape the stress of work.","zh":"人們常尋找興趣來逃離工作的壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the source of pressure.","zh":"這個短語指出壓力來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"technological, fast-paced life","meaning":"科技化、快節奏的生活","examples":[{"en":"Knitting offers relief from a technological, fast-paced life.","zh":"編織為科技化、快節奏的生活提供舒緩。"},{"en":"A technological, fast-paced life is a modern life shaped by technology and speed.","zh":"科技化、快節奏的生活是由科技和速度塑造的現代生活。"},{"en":"Many people feel tired by a technological, fast-paced life full of screens and messages.","zh":"許多人因充滿屏幕和訊息的科技化、快節奏生活而感到疲倦。"},{"en":"Slow crafts can offer a contrast to speed and constant digital connection.","zh":"慢手工藝可以與速度和持續數碼連接形成對比。"},{"en":"This phrase describes modern life as quick and technology-driven.","zh":"這個短語描述快速且由科技推動的現代生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"look back","meaning":"回顧","examples":[{"en":"Now, let’s look back to early knitting activities.","zh":"現在，讓我們回顧早期編織活動。"},{"en":"To look back means to consider or remember something from the past.","zh":"回顧意思是考慮或回想過去的事情。"},{"en":"A history lecture may look back at how people made clothing before machines.","zh":"歷史講座可能回顧機器出現前人們如何製作衣物。"},{"en":"Looking back helps us understand how modern practices developed.","zh":"回顧過去有助我們理解現代做法如何發展。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a discussion of the past.","zh":"這個短語引入對過去的討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"early knitting activities","meaning":"早期編織活動","examples":[{"en":"The speaker looks back to early knitting activities.","zh":"講者回顧早期編織活動。"},{"en":"Early knitting activities are knitting practices from the earlier periods of history.","zh":"早期編織活動是歷史早期的編織做法。"},{"en":"Early knitting activities can be studied through ancient clothing remains.","zh":"早期編織活動可以透過古代衣物遺存來研究。"},{"en":"These activities show how people used available tools and materials.","zh":"這些活動顯示人們如何使用可取得的工具和材料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes historical knitting practices.","zh":"這個短語描述歷史上的編織做法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"no one really knows","meaning":"沒有人真正知道","examples":[{"en":"No one really knows when knitting first began.","zh":"沒有人真正知道編織最早何時開始。"},{"en":"No one really knows means the answer is uncertain or not fully known.","zh":"沒有人真正知道意思是答案不確定或未被完全知道。"},{"en":"No one really knows exactly who invented the first knitting needle.","zh":"沒有人真正知道第一支編織針到底是誰發明的。"},{"en":"Historical questions can be difficult when evidence has not survived.","zh":"當證據沒有保存下來，歷史問題可能很難回答。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語表達不確定性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"first began","meaning":"最早開始","examples":[{"en":"No one really knows when knitting first began.","zh":"沒有人真正知道編織最早開始於何時。"},{"en":"First began means started for the first time.","zh":"最早開始意思是第一次開始。"},{"en":"Researchers may not know exactly when a craft first began.","zh":"研究人員可能不知道一種手工藝最早何時開始。"},{"en":"The beginning of an old skill can be hard to trace.","zh":"一項古老技能的開端可能難以追溯。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the earliest origin of something.","zh":"這個短語指某事最早的起源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"archaeological remains","meaning":"考古遺跡","examples":[{"en":"Archaeological remains have disclosed information about knitting.","zh":"考古遺跡揭示了關於編織的資料。"},{"en":"Archaeological remains are old objects or materials left behind by past human societies.","zh":"考古遺跡是過去人類社會留下的舊物件或材料。"},{"en":"Ancient clothing fragments are archaeological remains that can reveal textile techniques.","zh":"古代衣物碎片是可以揭示紡織技巧的考古遺跡。"},{"en":"Archaeological remains help researchers study periods without written records.","zh":"考古遺跡幫助研究人員研究沒有文字記錄的時期。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in history and archaeology.","zh":"這個短語常見於歷史和考古學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"disclose information","meaning":"揭示資料","examples":[{"en":"Archaeological remains have disclosed plenty of information.","zh":"考古遺跡揭示了大量資料。"},{"en":"To disclose information means to reveal or make information known.","zh":"揭示資料意思是顯露或使資料被知道。"},{"en":"Old tools can disclose information about how people worked in the past.","zh":"舊工具可以揭示過去人們如何工作的資料。"},{"en":"Objects sometimes disclose information that written records do not provide.","zh":"物件有時揭示文字記錄沒有提供的資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes revealing facts or evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述揭露事實或證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"plenty of information","meaning":"大量資料","examples":[{"en":"Archaeological remains have disclosed plenty of information.","zh":"考古遺跡揭示了大量資料。"},{"en":"Plenty of information means a large amount of useful information.","zh":"大量資料意思是很多有用資訊。"},{"en":"A museum display can provide plenty of information about ancient crafts.","zh":"博物館展覽可以提供大量關於古代手工藝的資料。"},{"en":"Plenty of information helps researchers build a clearer picture of the past.","zh":"大量資料有助研究人員建立更清楚的過去圖像。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an abundant supply of facts.","zh":"這個短語描述豐富的事實供應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"one of the interesting things about","meaning":"關於……有趣的一點","examples":[{"en":"One of the interesting things about knitting is the shape of early items.","zh":"關於編織有趣的一點，是早期物品的形狀。"},{"en":"One of the interesting things about something means one notable or curious feature of it.","zh":"關於某事有趣的一點意思是其中一個值得注意或令人好奇的特徵。"},{"en":"One of the interesting things about language is how words change over time.","zh":"關於語言有趣的一點，是詞語如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a point that may attract attention.","zh":"這個短語引入可能吸引注意的重點。"},{"en":"It is useful in lectures and explanations.","zh":"它適合用於講座和解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"earliest pieces of clothing","meaning":"最早的衣物","examples":[{"en":"The earliest pieces of clothing suggest that early knitted items were round.","zh":"最早的衣物顯示早期針織物品是圓形的。"},{"en":"The earliest pieces of clothing are the oldest known clothing items or fragments.","zh":"最早的衣物是已知最古老的衣物或衣物碎片。"},{"en":"The earliest pieces of clothing can show what people wore and how they made garments.","zh":"最早的衣物可以顯示人們穿甚麼，以及如何製作衣服。"},{"en":"Studying early clothing helps researchers understand ancient daily life.","zh":"研究早期衣物有助研究人員理解古代日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very old clothing evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述非常古老的衣物證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"顯示；暗示","examples":[{"en":"The earliest pieces of clothing suggest that most items were round.","zh":"最早的衣物顯示大多數物品是圓形的。"},{"en":"Suggest that means indicate or imply that something may be true.","zh":"顯示或暗示某事意思是指出某事可能是真的。"},{"en":"The shape of the socks suggests that they were knitted in one piece.","zh":"襪子的形狀顯示它們是一次過織成的。"},{"en":"Evidence can suggest a conclusion without proving every detail completely.","zh":"證據可以暗示一個結論，而不一定完全證明每個細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic explanation.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"items produced","meaning":"製成品","examples":[{"en":"Most of the items produced were round rather than flat.","zh":"大多數製成品是圓形而不是平面的。"},{"en":"Items produced means the objects that were made.","zh":"製成品意思是被製作出來的物件。"},{"en":"The items produced in the workshop included scarves, gloves and small bags.","zh":"工作坊中的製成品包括頸巾、手套和小袋。"},{"en":"Looking at items produced by ancient knitters helps researchers understand techniques.","zh":"觀察古代編織者的製成品，有助研究人員理解技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on finished products.","zh":"這個短語重點是完成品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"round rather than flat","meaning":"圓形而不是平面","examples":[{"en":"The earliest knitted items were round rather than flat.","zh":"最早的針織物品是圓形而不是平面。"},{"en":"Round rather than flat means circular or tube-shaped instead of flat and sheet-like.","zh":"圓形而不是平面意思是圓形或筒狀，而不是平坦片狀。"},{"en":"Socks are usually round rather than flat because they fit around the foot.","zh":"襪子通常是圓形而不是平面，因為它們包着腳。"},{"en":"The shape of early knitted items tells us something about how they were made.","zh":"早期針織物品的形狀告訴我們它們是如何製作的。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two different forms.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種不同形態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"discoveries from","meaning":"來自……的發現","examples":[{"en":"Discoveries from the 3rd and 4th centuries in Egypt show early knitting methods.","zh":"來自埃及三、四世紀的發現顯示早期編織方法。"},{"en":"Discoveries from a period or place are things found that come from that time or location.","zh":"來自某時期或地方的發現，是指源自該時間或地點的被發現物。"},{"en":"Discoveries from ancient tombs can reveal clothing and tools.","zh":"來自古墓的發現可以揭示衣物和工具。"},{"en":"Historical discoveries help researchers reconstruct old techniques.","zh":"歷史發現幫助研究人員重建古老技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase links evidence to its origin.","zh":"這個短語把證據與其來源連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"3rd and 4th centuries","meaning":"三、四世紀","examples":[{"en":"Discoveries from the 3rd and 4th centuries show ancient knitting techniques.","zh":"來自三、四世紀的發現顯示古代編織技巧。"},{"en":"The 3rd and 4th centuries mean the years from 201 to 400 AD.","zh":"三、四世紀意思是公元 201 年至 400 年期間。"},{"en":"Objects from the 3rd and 4th centuries can be very valuable to historians.","zh":"來自三、四世紀的物件對歷史學家可能很有價值。"},{"en":"Dating objects helps researchers place techniques in time.","zh":"為物件斷代有助研究人員把技術放入時間脈絡。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a historical period.","zh":"這個短語提供歷史時期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"things like","meaning":"例如……之類的東西","examples":[{"en":"Things like socks and gloves were knitted in one piece.","zh":"襪子和手套之類的東西是一次過織成的。"},{"en":"Things like means examples such as.","zh":"例如……之類的東西意思是舉出例子。"},{"en":"Ancient knitters made things like socks, gloves and small bags.","zh":"古代編織者製作襪子、手套和小袋之類的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples without giving a complete list.","zh":"這個短語引入例子，而不是給出完整清單。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken English.","zh":"它常見於口語英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"socks and gloves","meaning":"襪子和手套","examples":[{"en":"Socks and gloves were knitted to keep hands and feet warm.","zh":"襪子和手套被編織出來讓手腳保暖。"},{"en":"Socks and gloves are clothing items worn on the feet and hands.","zh":"襪子和手套是穿在腳和手上的衣物。"},{"en":"Knitted socks and gloves are useful in cold weather.","zh":"針織襪子和手套在寒冷天氣中很有用。"},{"en":"These items are often round or tube-shaped because they fit around body parts.","zh":"這些物品通常是圓形或筒狀，因為它們包着身體部位。"},{"en":"This phrase gives examples of practical knitted garments.","zh":"這個短語提供實用針織衣物的例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"keep hands and feet warm","meaning":"讓手腳保暖","examples":[{"en":"Socks and gloves were needed to keep hands and feet warm.","zh":"襪子和手套是為了讓手腳保暖而需要的。"},{"en":"To keep hands and feet warm means to protect them from cold.","zh":"讓手腳保暖意思是保護手和腳免受寒冷。"},{"en":"Wool gloves help keep hands warm in winter.","zh":"羊毛手套有助冬天讓雙手保暖。"},{"en":"Warm clothing is especially important in cold climates.","zh":"在寒冷氣候中，保暖衣物特別重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the practical purpose of winter garments.","zh":"這個短語描述冬季衣物的實際用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be knitted in one piece","meaning":"一次過織成","examples":[{"en":"Early socks and gloves were knitted in one piece.","zh":"早期襪子和手套是一次過織成的。"},{"en":"To be knitted in one piece means to be made as a single complete item without separate parts being sewn together.","zh":"一次過織成意思是製成一件完整物品，而不是由分開部分縫合。"},{"en":"A sock knitted in one piece may have no seam along the side.","zh":"一次過織成的襪子側面可能沒有縫線。"},{"en":"Knitting in one piece requires careful shaping as the work progresses.","zh":"一次過編織需要在過程中仔細塑形。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a construction method.","zh":"這個短語描述製作方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"using four or five needles","meaning":"使用四五支針","examples":[{"en":"Early knitted items were made using four or five needles.","zh":"早期針織物品是使用四五支針製成的。"},{"en":"Using four or five needles means knitting with several needles at the same time.","zh":"使用四五支針意思是同時用幾支針編織。"},{"en":"Round items such as socks may be knitted using four or five needles.","zh":"襪子等圓形物品可能使用四五支針編織。"},{"en":"This method helps create tube-shaped items without seams.","zh":"這種方法有助製作沒有縫線的筒狀物品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a traditional knitting technique.","zh":"這個短語描述傳統編織技巧。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"knitting patterns","meaning":"編織圖樣；編織方式","examples":[{"en":"Most knitting patterns today only require two needles.","zh":"今天大多數編織圖樣只需要兩支針。"},{"en":"Knitting patterns are instructions or designs showing how to make knitted items.","zh":"編織圖樣是顯示如何製作針織物品的指示或設計。"},{"en":"A knitting pattern may tell you how many stitches to make in each row.","zh":"編織圖樣可能告訴你每行要織多少針。"},{"en":"Patterns help knitters create consistent shapes and designs.","zh":"圖樣幫助編織者製作一致的形狀和設計。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to both written instructions and repeated designs.","zh":"這個短語可以指書面指示，也可以指重複設計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"require","meaning":"需要","examples":[{"en":"Most knitting patterns today require only two needles.","zh":"今天大多數編織圖樣只需要兩支針。"},{"en":"To require something means to need it.","zh":"需要某物意思是必須有它。"},{"en":"This pattern requires thick yarn and large needles.","zh":"這個圖樣需要粗紗線和大針。"},{"en":"Knowing what a project requires helps beginners prepare properly.","zh":"知道一個項目需要甚麼，有助初學者妥善準備。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing necessary materials or conditions.","zh":"這個詞適合用於描述必要材料或條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"what’s more","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"What’s more, the first needles were hand-carved.","zh":"此外，最早的編織針是手工雕刻的。"},{"en":"What’s more means in addition, especially when adding an interesting or important point.","zh":"此外意思是另外，尤其用於加入有趣或重要重點。"},{"en":"The craft is relaxing; what’s more, it can save money.","zh":"這項手工藝令人放鬆；此外，它可以慳錢。"},{"en":"This phrase helps add another supporting detail.","zh":"這個短語有助加入另一個支持細節。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken and written explanation.","zh":"它常見於口頭和書面解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the very first","meaning":"最早的","examples":[{"en":"The very first needles were hand-carved from wood.","zh":"最早的編織針是由木材手工雕刻而成的。"},{"en":"The very first means the earliest examples of something.","zh":"最早的意思是某事物最初的例子。"},{"en":"The very first knitting tools were probably much simpler than modern ones.","zh":"最早的編織工具可能比現代工具簡單得多。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises the beginning of a history.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調歷史的開端。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing origins.","zh":"當討論起源時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"needles","meaning":"編織針","examples":[{"en":"The first knitting needles were made from natural materials.","zh":"最早的編織針由天然材料製成。"},{"en":"Needles are long, thin tools used in knitting or sewing.","zh":"編織針是用於編織或縫紉的細長工具。"},{"en":"Knitting needles hold loops of yarn while the fabric is being made.","zh":"編織針在製作布料時承托紗線線圈。"},{"en":"Different needle sizes create different textures and stitch sizes.","zh":"不同尺寸的編織針會創造不同質感和針目大小。"},{"en":"This word names an essential knitting tool.","zh":"這個詞命名一種必要編織工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be hand-carved out of","meaning":"由……手工雕刻而成","examples":[{"en":"The first needles were hand-carved out of wood.","zh":"最早的編織針由木材手工雕刻而成。"},{"en":"To be hand-carved out of something means to be shaped by hand from that material.","zh":"由某物手工雕刻而成意思是用手把該材料雕刻成形。"},{"en":"A wooden spoon can be hand-carved out of a piece of wood.","zh":"木匙可以由一塊木材手工雕刻而成。"},{"en":"Hand-carved objects often show personal skill and careful work.","zh":"手工雕刻物品通常顯示個人技巧和細心工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes handmade shaping from a material.","zh":"這個短語描述從材料手工塑形。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"natural materials","meaning":"天然材料","examples":[{"en":"The earliest needles were made from wood and other natural materials.","zh":"最早的編織針由木材和其他天然材料製成。"},{"en":"Natural materials are materials that come from nature rather than factories.","zh":"天然材料是來自自然界而不是工廠的材料。"},{"en":"Wood, bone, wool, cotton and bamboo are natural materials.","zh":"木材、骨、羊毛、棉和竹都是天然材料。"},{"en":"Ancient crafts often used natural materials available nearby.","zh":"古代手工藝常使用附近可取得的天然材料。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts natural sources with synthetic ones.","zh":"這個短語把天然來源與合成來源作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而；相比之下","examples":[{"en":"The first needles were made of wood, whereas today’s are made of steel or plastic.","zh":"最早的編織針由木材製成，而今天的則由鋼或塑膠製成。"},{"en":"Whereas is used to compare two different facts or situations.","zh":"whereas 用來比較兩個不同事實或情況。"},{"en":"Ancient tools were handmade, whereas modern tools are often mass-produced.","zh":"古代工具是手製的，而現代工具通常是大量生產的。"},{"en":"This word is useful when showing contrast.","zh":"當顯示對比時，這個詞很有用。"},{"en":"It is common in formal comparison.","zh":"它常見於正式比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be largely made of","meaning":"大多由……製成","examples":[{"en":"Today’s needles are largely made of steel or plastic.","zh":"今天的編織針大多由鋼或塑膠製成。"},{"en":"To be largely made of something means to be mostly made from that material.","zh":"大多由某物製成意思是主要由該材料構成。"},{"en":"Modern chairs may be largely made of plastic and metal.","zh":"現代椅子可能大多由塑膠和金屬製成。"},{"en":"The material affects how heavy, smooth or durable a tool is.","zh":"材料會影響工具的重量、順滑度和耐用性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main material used.","zh":"這個短語描述主要使用的材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"steel or plastic","meaning":"鋼或塑膠","examples":[{"en":"Modern needles are usually made of steel or plastic.","zh":"現代編織針通常由鋼或塑膠製成。"},{"en":"Steel or plastic are common modern materials used to make tools and household items.","zh":"鋼或塑膠是用來製作工具和家居物品的常見現代材料。"},{"en":"Steel needles may feel strong and smooth, while plastic needles may be lighter.","zh":"鋼針可能感覺堅固順滑，而塑膠針可能較輕。"},{"en":"Material choice can affect the knitting experience.","zh":"材料選擇可以影響編織體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase gives examples of modern needle materials.","zh":"這個短語提供現代編織針材料例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"characteristic clicking sound","meaning":"特有的喀嗒聲","examples":[{"en":"Modern knitting needles make a characteristic clicking sound.","zh":"現代編織針會發出特有的喀嗒聲。"},{"en":"A characteristic clicking sound is a typical short repeated sound associated with something.","zh":"特有的喀嗒聲是與某事物相關的典型短促重複聲音。"},{"en":"Metal knitting needles often make a clicking sound as they touch each other.","zh":"金屬編織針互相碰觸時常會發出喀嗒聲。"},{"en":"Sounds can become part of how people recognise an activity.","zh":"聲音可以成為人們辨認一項活動的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a distinctive noise.","zh":"這個短語描述獨特聲音。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"use yarns made from","meaning":"使用由……製成的紗線","examples":[{"en":"Ancient people knitted using yarns made from linen, hemp, cotton and wool.","zh":"古代人使用由亞麻、大麻纖維、棉和羊毛製成的紗線編織。"},{"en":"To use yarns made from something means to knit with yarn produced from those materials.","zh":"使用由某物製成的紗線意思是用那些材料製成的紗線編織。"},{"en":"Modern knitters may use yarns made from wool, cotton or synthetic fibres.","zh":"現代編織者可能使用由羊毛、棉或合成纖維製成的紗線。"},{"en":"Different yarn materials create different textures and levels of warmth.","zh":"不同紗線材料會創造不同質感和保暖程度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the source material of yarn.","zh":"這個短語描述紗線的來源材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"yarns","meaning":"紗線","examples":[{"en":"Ancient people knitted with different kinds of yarns.","zh":"古代人使用不同種類的紗線編織。"},{"en":"Yarns are long threads used for knitting, weaving or sewing.","zh":"紗線是用於編織、織布或縫紉的長線。"},{"en":"Thick yarns make warm, heavy garments, while fine yarns create lighter fabric.","zh":"粗紗線製成溫暖厚重衣物，而幼細紗線創造較輕布料。"},{"en":"Choosing the right yarn is important for the feel and look of a knitted item.","zh":"選擇合適紗線對針織物品的觸感和外觀很重要。"},{"en":"This word is central to knitting and textile crafts.","zh":"這個詞是編織和紡織手工藝的核心詞語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"linen","meaning":"亞麻","examples":[{"en":"Ancient yarns were made from linen, hemp, cotton and wool.","zh":"古代紗線由亞麻、大麻纖維、棉和羊毛製成。"},{"en":"Linen is a fabric or fibre made from the flax plant.","zh":"亞麻是由亞麻植物製成的布料或纖維。"},{"en":"Linen is often valued because it is strong and breathable.","zh":"亞麻常因堅韌和透氣而受重視。"},{"en":"Ancient people used linen for clothing and household textiles.","zh":"古代人使用亞麻製作衣物和家居紡織品。"},{"en":"This word names a natural textile material.","zh":"這個詞命名一種天然紡織材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hemp","meaning":"大麻纖維","examples":[{"en":"Hemp was one of the materials used to make ancient yarns.","zh":"大麻纖維是用來製作古代紗線的材料之一。"},{"en":"Hemp is a strong natural fibre from the hemp plant.","zh":"大麻纖維是來自大麻植物的堅韌天然纖維。"},{"en":"Hemp can be used to make rope, cloth and other durable materials.","zh":"大麻纖維可以用來製作繩、布和其他耐用材料。"},{"en":"Ancient crafts often used hemp because it was tough and widely available.","zh":"古代手工藝常使用大麻纖維，因為它堅韌且容易取得。"},{"en":"This word names a plant-based fibre.","zh":"這個詞命名一種植物纖維。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cotton","meaning":"棉","examples":[{"en":"Ancient knitters used cotton yarns.","zh":"古代編織者使用棉紗線。"},{"en":"Cotton is a soft natural fibre from the cotton plant.","zh":"棉是來自棉花植物的柔軟天然纖維。"},{"en":"Cotton yarn can feel cooler and softer than some rough fibres.","zh":"棉紗線可能比一些粗糙纖維感覺更涼快柔軟。"},{"en":"Cotton is widely used in modern clothing and textiles.","zh":"棉廣泛用於現代衣物和紡織品。"},{"en":"This word names a common natural fibre.","zh":"這個詞命名一種常見天然纖維。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"wool","meaning":"羊毛","examples":[{"en":"Wool became dominant in the knitting industry.","zh":"羊毛在編織業中變得佔主導地位。"},{"en":"Wool is a warm natural fibre usually obtained from sheep.","zh":"羊毛是通常來自羊身上的保暖天然纖維。"},{"en":"Wool is useful for winter clothing because it keeps heat well.","zh":"羊毛適合冬季衣物，因為它保暖能力好。"},{"en":"Many knitters prefer wool for sweaters, scarves and hats.","zh":"許多編織者喜歡用羊毛製作毛衣、頸巾和帽。"},{"en":"This word names one of the most important knitting materials.","zh":"這個詞命名最重要的編織材料之一。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rough on the skin","meaning":"接觸皮膚時粗糙","examples":[{"en":"Ancient yarns were often rough on the skin.","zh":"古代紗線接觸皮膚時常很粗糙。"},{"en":"Rough on the skin means uncomfortable or scratchy when touching the body.","zh":"接觸皮膚時粗糙意思是碰到身體時不舒服或刺癢。"},{"en":"Some cheap wool can feel rough on the skin if it is not processed well.","zh":"如果處理不好，有些廉價羊毛接觸皮膚時會粗糙。"},{"en":"Soft yarns are preferred for clothing worn close to the body.","zh":"貼身衣物通常較適合使用柔軟紗線。"},{"en":"This phrase describes texture and comfort.","zh":"這個短語描述質感和舒適度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"spinning wheel","meaning":"紡車","examples":[{"en":"The spinning wheel allowed people to make finer yarns.","zh":"紡車讓人們能夠製作較幼細的紗線。"},{"en":"A spinning wheel is a tool used to spin fibres into yarn.","zh":"紡車是用來把纖維紡成紗線的工具。"},{"en":"Before industrial machines, spinning wheels helped people produce yarn by hand.","zh":"在工業機器出現前，紡車幫助人們用手生產紗線。"},{"en":"The spinning wheel improved the speed and quality of yarn production.","zh":"紡車改善了紗線生產的速度和質素。"},{"en":"This phrase names an important textile tool.","zh":"這個短語命名一種重要紡織工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"allow someone to","meaning":"讓某人能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The spinning wheel allowed people to produce more yarn.","zh":"紡車讓人們能夠生產更多紗線。"},{"en":"To allow someone to do something means to make it possible for them to do it.","zh":"讓某人能夠做某事意思是令他們可以做到該事。"},{"en":"Better tools allowed knitters to work faster and more accurately.","zh":"更好的工具讓編織者能夠更快和更準確地工作。"},{"en":"Technology can allow people to produce more with less effort.","zh":"科技可以讓人用較少努力生產更多。"},{"en":"This phrase links a tool or condition with a new ability.","zh":"這個短語把工具或條件與新能力連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"finer yarns","meaning":"較幼細的紗線","examples":[{"en":"The spinning wheel allowed people to make finer yarns.","zh":"紡車讓人們能夠製作較幼細的紗線。"},{"en":"Finer yarns are thinner and smoother threads.","zh":"較幼細的紗線是較薄和較順滑的線。"},{"en":"Finer yarns can be used to make lighter and softer garments.","zh":"較幼細的紗線可以用來製作較輕和較柔軟的衣物。"},{"en":"Producing finer yarns was an important improvement in textile history.","zh":"生產較幼細紗線是紡織史上的重要改進。"},{"en":"This phrase describes yarn quality and thickness.","zh":"這個短語描述紗線質素和粗幼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"greater quantities of","meaning":"更多數量的……","examples":[{"en":"People could produce greater quantities of yarn.","zh":"人們能夠生產更多數量的紗線。"},{"en":"Greater quantities of something means larger amounts of it.","zh":"更多數量的某物意思是更大的數量。"},{"en":"Machines made it possible to produce greater quantities of cloth.","zh":"機器使人們能夠生產更多數量的布料。"},{"en":"Producing more yarn helped knitting become more widespread.","zh":"生產更多紗線幫助編織變得更普及。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase in amount.","zh":"這個短語描述數量增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致；帶來","examples":[{"en":"The spinning wheel led to the dominance of wool.","zh":"紡車帶來羊毛的主導地位。"},{"en":"To lead to something means to cause or result in it.","zh":"導致或帶來某事意思是造成或引起它。"},{"en":"Better tools can lead to faster production.","zh":"更好的工具可以帶來更快生產。"},{"en":"Changes in technology often lead to changes in materials and methods.","zh":"科技變化常導致材料和方法改變。"},{"en":"This phrase links cause and effect.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"dominance of","meaning":"……的主導地位","examples":[{"en":"The spinning wheel led to the dominance of wool in knitting.","zh":"紡車帶來羊毛在編織中的主導地位。"},{"en":"Dominance of something means its leading or most important position.","zh":"某物的主導地位意思是它處於領先或最重要的位置。"},{"en":"The dominance of cotton in some clothing industries came from comfort and availability.","zh":"棉在一些服裝業中的主導地位來自舒適度和可取得性。"},{"en":"Wool gained dominance because it was warm and easier to produce in large amounts.","zh":"羊毛取得主導地位，因為它保暖且較容易大量生產。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming the main material or force.","zh":"這個短語描述成為主要材料或力量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"knitting industry","meaning":"編織業","examples":[{"en":"Wool became dominant in the knitting industry.","zh":"羊毛在編織業中變得佔主導地位。"},{"en":"The knitting industry is the business or production sector connected with knitted goods.","zh":"編織業是與針織產品有關的商業或生產行業。"},{"en":"The knitting industry includes yarn producers, designers, factories and craft suppliers.","zh":"編織業包括紗線生產商、設計師、工廠和手工藝供應商。"},{"en":"Changes in materials can affect the whole knitting industry.","zh":"材料變化可以影響整個編織業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the commercial side of knitting.","zh":"這個短語描述編織的商業層面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be favoured for","meaning":"因……而受青睞","examples":[{"en":"Wool was often favoured for its warmth.","zh":"羊毛常因其保暖性而受青睞。"},{"en":"To be favoured for something means to be preferred because of that quality.","zh":"因某特質而受青睞意思是因該特質而被偏好。"},{"en":"Cotton is favoured for its softness in summer clothes.","zh":"棉因柔軟而在夏季衣物中受青睞。"},{"en":"Materials are chosen according to the qualities they offer.","zh":"材料會根據其提供的特質被選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why something is preferred.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物為何受偏好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"warmth","meaning":"保暖性","examples":[{"en":"Wool was favoured for its warmth.","zh":"羊毛因其保暖性而受青睞。"},{"en":"Warmth means the ability to keep heat or provide a feeling of heat.","zh":"保暖性意思是保持熱量或提供暖意的能力。"},{"en":"Wool is valued for warmth in winter clothing.","zh":"羊毛在冬季衣物中因保暖性而受重視。"},{"en":"A garment’s warmth depends on material, thickness and design.","zh":"衣物的保暖性取決於材料、厚度和設計。"},{"en":"This word is important when discussing clothing for cold weather.","zh":"當討論寒冷天氣衣物時，這個詞很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"interesting fact about","meaning":"關於……的有趣事實","examples":[{"en":"Another interesting fact about knitting is its regional differences.","zh":"關於編織的另一個有趣事實，是它的地區差異。"},{"en":"An interesting fact about something is a piece of information that is worth noticing.","zh":"關於某事的有趣事實，是值得注意的一項資料。"},{"en":"An interesting fact about wool is that it can remain warm even when damp.","zh":"關於羊毛的一個有趣事實，是它即使潮濕仍能保暖。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase to introduce a new detail.","zh":"講者使用這個短語引入新細節。"},{"en":"It helps make an explanation more engaging.","zh":"它有助令解釋更吸引。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be practised in","meaning":"在……被實行","examples":[{"en":"Knitting was practised in many parts of the world.","zh":"編織在世界許多地方被實行。"},{"en":"To be practised in a place means to be done or carried out there.","zh":"在某地被實行意思是在那裏被進行或實踐。"},{"en":"Different forms of weaving are practised in many cultures.","zh":"不同形式的織布在許多文化中被實行。"},{"en":"A craft practised in many regions may develop local styles.","zh":"在許多地區被實行的手工藝可能發展出地方風格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where an activity is done.","zh":"這個短語描述活動在哪裏進行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"for so many purposes","meaning":"為了許多用途","examples":[{"en":"Knitting was practised for so many purposes.","zh":"編織為了許多用途而被實行。"},{"en":"For so many purposes means for many different uses or reasons.","zh":"為了許多用途意思是為了許多不同用途或原因。"},{"en":"People knitted for warmth, income, decoration and family needs.","zh":"人們為了保暖、收入、裝飾和家庭需要而編織。"},{"en":"A craft used for many purposes can become deeply connected with daily life.","zh":"用途很多的手工藝可以與日常生活深深連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a wide range of uses.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"regional differences","meaning":"地區差異","examples":[{"en":"Regional differences in knitting style developed.","zh":"編織風格上的地區差異逐漸形成。"},{"en":"Regional differences are variations between different areas or places.","zh":"地區差異是不同地區或地方之間的變化。"},{"en":"Regional differences in food, clothing and language can reveal local culture.","zh":"食物、衣着和語言的地區差異可以揭示地方文化。"},{"en":"Knitting styles changed because communities used different materials and patterns.","zh":"編織風格因社群使用不同材料和圖樣而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes local variation.","zh":"這個短語描述地方變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in style","meaning":"在風格上","examples":[{"en":"Regional differences in style developed over time.","zh":"風格上的地區差異隨時間形成。"},{"en":"In style means in the way something looks, is made or is expressed.","zh":"在風格上意思是在外觀、製作方式或表達方式方面。"},{"en":"Knitted clothing may differ in style from one region to another.","zh":"針織衣物在風格上可能因地區而異。"},{"en":"Style can show local taste, climate and tradition.","zh":"風格可以顯示地方品味、氣候和傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on appearance or method.","zh":"這個短語重點是外觀或方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"visual identity","meaning":"視覺特徵","examples":[{"en":"Knitted clothing developed a visual identity.","zh":"針織衣物發展出視覺特徵。"},{"en":"Visual identity means a recognisable appearance or style.","zh":"視覺特徵意思是可辨認的外觀或風格。"},{"en":"A region’s knitting may have a visual identity through repeated patterns and colours.","zh":"一個地區的編織可以透過重複圖案和顏色形成視覺特徵。"},{"en":"Visual identity helps researchers identify where an item may have come from.","zh":"視覺特徵幫助研究人員識別物品可能來自哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distinctive visual features.","zh":"這個短語描述獨特的視覺特色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"allow researchers to","meaning":"讓研究人員能夠……","examples":[{"en":"This visual identity allows researchers to identify origins.","zh":"這種視覺特徵讓研究人員能夠識別來源。"},{"en":"To allow researchers to do something means to make it possible for them to do it.","zh":"讓研究人員能夠做某事意思是使他們可以做到該事。"},{"en":"Patterns in old clothing allow researchers to trace regional traditions.","zh":"舊衣物上的圖案讓研究人員能夠追溯地區傳統。"},{"en":"Evidence allows researchers to move from guessing to stronger conclusions.","zh":"證據讓研究人員能夠由猜測走向更有力結論。"},{"en":"This phrase links evidence with research ability.","zh":"這個短語把證據與研究能力連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"match A to B","meaning":"把A與B配對","examples":[{"en":"Researchers can match bits of clothing to the wearer’s region or job.","zh":"研究人員可以把衣物碎片與穿着者的地區或職業配對。"},{"en":"To match A to B means to connect or pair A with B because they belong together.","zh":"把 A 與 B 配對意思是因兩者相關而把它們連接起來。"},{"en":"Researchers may match a pattern to a particular village or trade.","zh":"研究人員可能把一種圖案與特定村莊或行業配對。"},{"en":"Matching evidence to a place can help reconstruct history.","zh":"把證據與地方配對可以幫助重建歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase describes linking one thing with another.","zh":"這個短語描述把一件事與另一件事連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"bits of knitted clothing","meaning":"針織衣物碎片","examples":[{"en":"Researchers study bits of knitted clothing that have been unearthed.","zh":"研究人員研究被挖掘出土的針織衣物碎片。"},{"en":"Bits of knitted clothing are small pieces or fragments of knitted garments.","zh":"針織衣物碎片是針織衣物的小塊或殘片。"},{"en":"Even small bits of knitted clothing can show yarn type, colour and pattern.","zh":"即使是小片針織衣物，也可以顯示紗線種類、顏色和圖案。"},{"en":"Fragments may survive when complete garments do not.","zh":"當完整衣物不能保存時，碎片仍可能留下。"},{"en":"This phrase describes textile remains used in research.","zh":"這個短語描述用於研究的紡織遺存。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be unearthed","meaning":"被挖掘出土","examples":[{"en":"Bits of knitted clothing have been unearthed over time.","zh":"針織衣物碎片隨着時間被挖掘出土。"},{"en":"To be unearthed means to be dug up or discovered, often from the ground.","zh":"被挖掘出土意思是被挖出或發現，通常是從地下。"},{"en":"Archaeologists unearthed old tools near the ancient settlement.","zh":"考古學家在古代聚落附近挖掘出舊工具。"},{"en":"Unearthed objects can provide evidence about daily life in the past.","zh":"出土物品可以提供關於過去日常生活的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in archaeology.","zh":"這個短語常見於考古學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"over time","meaning":"隨着時間","examples":[{"en":"Many knitted items have been unearthed over time.","zh":"許多針織物品隨着時間被挖掘出土。"},{"en":"Over time means gradually during a long period.","zh":"隨着時間意思是在長時間內逐漸地。"},{"en":"Over time, knitting styles changed in different regions.","zh":"隨着時間，不同地區的編織風格發生變化。"},{"en":"Historical understanding often improves over time as more evidence is discovered.","zh":"隨着更多證據被發現，歷史理解通常會逐漸改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual development.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the region from which","meaning":"……所來自的地區","examples":[{"en":"Researchers can identify the region from which the wearer came.","zh":"研究人員可以識別穿着者所來自的地區。"},{"en":"The region from which someone came means the area where that person originated.","zh":"某人所來自的地區意思是那人的原居地或來源地。"},{"en":"A clothing pattern may reveal the region from which the wearer came.","zh":"衣物圖案可能揭示穿着者所來自的地區。"},{"en":"Regional styles can act like clues in historical research.","zh":"地區風格可以像歷史研究中的線索。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies origin by place.","zh":"這個短語以地點指出來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"wearer","meaning":"穿着者","examples":[{"en":"The clothing can reveal where the wearer came from.","zh":"衣物可以揭示穿着者來自哪裏。"},{"en":"A wearer is the person who wears a piece of clothing.","zh":"穿着者是穿某件衣物的人。"},{"en":"The size and style of a garment may tell us something about the wearer.","zh":"衣物的尺寸和風格可能告訴我們關於穿着者的一些資料。"},{"en":"Researchers can sometimes infer a wearer’s job, region or status from clothing.","zh":"研究人員有時可以從衣物推斷穿着者的職業、地區或身份。"},{"en":"This word is common when discussing garments.","zh":"這個詞常見於討論衣物時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as I’ve mentioned","meaning":"正如我提到","examples":[{"en":"As I’ve mentioned, knitting offered poor communities a way to earn money.","zh":"正如我提到，編織為貧困社群提供了賺錢的方法。"},{"en":"As I’ve mentioned means as I have already said earlier.","zh":"正如我提到意思是正如我之前已經說過。"},{"en":"As I’ve mentioned, handmade skills were once important for survival.","zh":"正如我提到，手工技能曾經對生存很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase helps remind listeners of an earlier point.","zh":"這個短語幫助提醒聽眾較早的重點。"},{"en":"It is common in lectures and presentations.","zh":"它常見於講座和匯報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"offer someone a way of","meaning":"為某人提供……的方法","examples":[{"en":"Knitting offered poor communities a way of making extra money.","zh":"編織為貧困社群提供了賺取額外收入的方法。"},{"en":"To offer someone a way of doing something means to provide a method or opportunity for them to do it.","zh":"為某人提供做某事的方法意思是給他們做該事的途徑或機會。"},{"en":"Online selling offers craftspeople a way of reaching more customers.","zh":"網上銷售為手工藝人提供了接觸更多顧客的方法。"},{"en":"A practical skill can offer people a way of improving their situation.","zh":"實用技能可以為人們提供改善處境的方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes providing a useful route or method.","zh":"這個短語描述提供有用途徑或方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"poor communities","meaning":"貧困社群","examples":[{"en":"Knitting helped people from poor communities.","zh":"編織幫助來自貧困社群的人。"},{"en":"Poor communities are groups of people with limited money and resources.","zh":"貧困社群是金錢和資源有限的人群。"},{"en":"In poor communities, handmade goods could provide extra income.","zh":"在貧困社群中，手製品可以提供額外收入。"},{"en":"Practical crafts often became important where factory-made items were expensive.","zh":"當工廠製品昂貴時，實用手工藝常變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes economically disadvantaged groups.","zh":"這個短語描述經濟上處於劣勢的群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make extra money","meaning":"賺取額外收入","examples":[{"en":"Knitting allowed people to make extra money.","zh":"編織讓人們能夠賺取額外收入。"},{"en":"To make extra money means to earn additional income beyond one’s usual earnings.","zh":"賺取額外收入意思是在平常收入之外賺更多錢。"},{"en":"A family might make extra money by selling handmade scarves.","zh":"家庭可能透過售賣手織頸巾賺取額外收入。"},{"en":"Extra income can help people buy food, clothing or tools.","zh":"額外收入可以幫助人購買食物、衣服或工具。"},{"en":"This phrase describes earning additional money.","zh":"這個短語描述賺取更多金錢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"while doing other tasks","meaning":"一邊做其他工作時","examples":[{"en":"People could knit while doing other tasks.","zh":"人們可以一邊做其他工作時一邊編織。"},{"en":"While doing other tasks means at the same time as carrying out other activities.","zh":"一邊做其他工作時意思是在進行其他活動的同時。"},{"en":"People once knitted while watching animals or walking to market.","zh":"人們曾一邊看管動物或步行去市場，一邊編織。"},{"en":"Portable crafts can be done while people are busy with other work.","zh":"便於攜帶的手工藝可以在人忙着做其他工作時進行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doing two things at once.","zh":"這個短語描述同時做兩件事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"for many centuries","meaning":"幾個世紀以來","examples":[{"en":"For many centuries, people knitted whenever they could.","zh":"幾個世紀以來，人們一有機會就編織。"},{"en":"For many centuries means during a very long period of several hundred years.","zh":"幾個世紀以來意思是在幾百年的漫長時期中。"},{"en":"For many centuries, families passed craft skills down at home.","zh":"幾個世紀以來，家庭在家中傳承手工藝技能。"},{"en":"A habit practised for centuries often becomes part of culture.","zh":"一個實踐了數百年的習慣，常會成為文化的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a long historical duration.","zh":"這個短語提供長歷史時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"take every opportunity to","meaning":"把握一切機會去……","examples":[{"en":"Men, women and children took every opportunity to knit.","zh":"男人、女人和孩子都把握一切機會去編織。"},{"en":"To take every opportunity to do something means to do it whenever there is a chance.","zh":"把握一切機會做某事意思是一有機會就做。"},{"en":"Students should take every opportunity to practise speaking English.","zh":"學生應把握一切機會練習說英文。"},{"en":"People took every opportunity to knit because the work could bring income.","zh":"人們把握一切機會編織，因為這項工作可以帶來收入。"},{"en":"This phrase shows eagerness and regular effort.","zh":"這個短語顯示積極和持續努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"watch over sheep","meaning":"看管羊群","examples":[{"en":"People knitted while watching over sheep.","zh":"人們一邊看管羊群一邊編織。"},{"en":"To watch over sheep means to look after and guard sheep.","zh":"看管羊群意思是照顧和守護羊。"},{"en":"Shepherds could knit while watching over sheep in the fields.","zh":"牧羊人可以在田野看管羊群時編織。"},{"en":"This shows that knitting could be done during other daily duties.","zh":"這顯示編織可以在其他日常職責期間進行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes caring for animals.","zh":"這個短語描述照顧動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"walking to market","meaning":"步行去市場","examples":[{"en":"People knitted while walking to market.","zh":"人們一邊步行去市場一邊編織。"},{"en":"Walking to market means going to a market on foot.","zh":"步行去市場意思是徒步前往市場。"},{"en":"In the past, people might knit while walking to market to use time efficiently.","zh":"在過去，人們可能一邊步行去市場一邊編織，以善用時間。"},{"en":"Markets were important places for buying, selling and exchanging goods.","zh":"市場是購買、售賣和交換貨物的重要地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement during daily economic life.","zh":"這個短語描述日常經濟生活中的移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"riding in boats","meaning":"乘船時","examples":[{"en":"People knitted while riding in boats.","zh":"人們乘船時也會編織。"},{"en":"Riding in boats means travelling by boat.","zh":"乘船時意思是坐船旅行時。"},{"en":"People could knit while riding in boats if the journey was long and steady.","zh":"如果旅程漫長而平穩，人們可以乘船時編織。"},{"en":"This example shows how portable knitting was as a task.","zh":"這個例子顯示編織作為任務有多便於攜帶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes travelling on water.","zh":"這個短語描述在水上交通中旅行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"move on to","meaning":"轉到……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker moves on to take a closer look at another topic.","zh":"講者轉到更仔細看看另一個主題。"},{"en":"To move on to something means to stop discussing one point and begin discussing the next.","zh":"轉到某事意思是停止討論一個重點，開始討論下一個。"},{"en":"After explaining the history of knitting, the lecturer moves on to regional styles.","zh":"解釋完編織歷史後，講師轉到地區風格。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise a talk or lesson clearly.","zh":"這個短語有助清楚組織演講或課堂。"},{"en":"It is common in presentations, lectures and discussions.","zh":"它常見於匯報、講座和討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 18 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/listening/Practice 19/task-1":[{"front":"I was hoping to speak to","meaning":"我想找……談談","examples":[{"en":"Tom was hoping to speak to Jack Fitzgerald about renting a cottage.","zh":"Tom 想找 Jack Fitzgerald 談談租用小屋的事。"},{"en":"I was hoping to speak to is a polite way to say that you would like to talk to someone.","zh":"I was hoping to speak to 是一種有禮貌地表示想與某人交談的說法。"},{"en":"I was hoping to speak to the manager about my booking.","zh":"我想找經理談談我的預訂。"},{"en":"This phrase is softer and more polite than “I want to speak to”.","zh":"這個片語比 “I want to speak to” 語氣更柔和、更有禮貌。"},{"en":"It is common in phone calls and formal enquiries.","zh":"它常見於電話和正式查詢中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"about renting a cottage","meaning":"關於租用小屋","examples":[{"en":"Tom wanted to speak to Jack about renting a cottage.","zh":"Tom 想找 Jack 談談關於租用小屋的事。"},{"en":"About renting a cottage means concerning the possibility or details of hiring a small holiday house.","zh":"about renting a cottage 指關於租用一間小型度假屋的可能性或詳情。"},{"en":"The couple called the owner about renting a cottage for the summer.","zh":"那對夫婦致電業主，查詢夏天租用小屋的事。"},{"en":"People usually ask about prices, dates and facilities when renting a cottage.","zh":"人們租用小屋時通常會詢問價錢、日期和設施。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in holiday accommodation enquiries.","zh":"這個片語適合用於度假住宿查詢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"own something together","meaning":"共同擁有某物","examples":[{"en":"Shirley and Jack own the cottages together.","zh":"Shirley 和 Jack 共同擁有那些小屋。"},{"en":"To own something together means two or more people share legal ownership of it.","zh":"own something together 指兩個或更多人共同擁有某物的法律所有權。"},{"en":"The sisters own the family house together.","zh":"那對姊妹共同擁有家族房子。"},{"en":"If people own a business together, they usually share responsibility and decisions.","zh":"如果人們共同擁有一盤生意，他們通常會共同承擔責任和作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared ownership.","zh":"這個片語描述共同擁有。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"I’m sure I can help you","meaning":"我相信我可以幫到你","examples":[{"en":"Shirley says she is sure she can help Tom.","zh":"Shirley 說她相信自己可以幫到 Tom。"},{"en":"I’m sure I can help you means I believe I am able to give you useful assistance.","zh":"I’m sure I can help you 指我相信自己能夠提供有用協助。"},{"en":"I’m sure I can help you find a suitable room.","zh":"我相信我可以幫你找到合適房間。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds friendly and reassuring in customer service.","zh":"這個片語在客戶服務中聽起來友善而令人安心。"},{"en":"It shows confidence without sounding too forceful.","zh":"它顯示信心，但不會太強硬。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"some friends of ours","meaning":"我們的一些朋友","examples":[{"en":"Some friends of Tom’s rented Granary Cottage last year.","zh":"Tom 的一些朋友去年租用了 Granary Cottage。"},{"en":"Some friends of ours means some people who are our friends.","zh":"some friends of ours 指我們的一些朋友。"},{"en":"Some friends of ours stayed in the same village last summer.","zh":"我們的一些朋友去年夏天住在同一條村。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when explaining how someone heard about a place or service.","zh":"這個片語常用於解釋某人如何知道某地方或服務。"},{"en":"It sounds natural and conversational.","zh":"它聽起來自然口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rent something from someone","meaning":"向某人租用某物","examples":[{"en":"Tom’s friends rented Granary Cottage from Shirley and Jack.","zh":"Tom 的朋友向 Shirley 和 Jack 租用了 Granary Cottage。"},{"en":"To rent something from someone means to pay that person to use their property for a period of time.","zh":"rent something from someone 指付款給某人，以在一段時間內使用其物業或物品。"},{"en":"We rented a flat from a local landlord for six months.","zh":"我們向一位本地業主租了一個單位六個月。"},{"en":"When you rent something from someone, you do not own it permanently.","zh":"當你向某人租用某物時，你並不是永久擁有它。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in accommodation and property contexts.","zh":"這個片語常見於住宿和物業語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"think something is great","meaning":"覺得某物很好","examples":[{"en":"Tom’s friends thought Granary Cottage was very good.","zh":"Tom 的朋友覺得 Granary Cottage 很好。"},{"en":"To think something is great means to have a very positive opinion of it.","zh":"think something is great 指對某物有非常正面的看法。"},{"en":"The guests thought the cottage was great because it was clean and quiet.","zh":"客人覺得那間小屋很好，因為它乾淨又安靜。"},{"en":"Personal recommendations are powerful when friends think a place is great.","zh":"當朋友覺得某地方很好，個人推薦會很有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple, informal and positive.","zh":"這個片語簡單、口語而正面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be hoping to come","meaning":"希望前來","examples":[{"en":"Tom and his wife are hoping to come in May.","zh":"Tom 和他的妻子希望五月前來。"},{"en":"To be hoping to come means to want and plan to visit, though it may not be confirmed yet.","zh":"be hoping to come 指希望並計劃前來，但可能尚未完全確認。"},{"en":"We are hoping to come for a weekend in June.","zh":"我們希望六月來住一個週末。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds polite because it leaves room for availability and arrangements.","zh":"這個片語語氣有禮，因為它為空檔和安排留有餘地。"},{"en":"It is common in accommodation enquiries.","zh":"它常見於住宿查詢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in May","meaning":"在五月","examples":[{"en":"Tom and his wife hope to stay at the cottage in May.","zh":"Tom 和他的妻子希望在五月入住那間小屋。"},{"en":"In May means during the month of May.","zh":"in May 指在五月期間。"},{"en":"The cottage is often popular in May because the weather is mild.","zh":"那間小屋在五月通常很受歡迎，因為天氣溫和。"},{"en":"When booking accommodation, the month affects price and availability.","zh":"預訂住宿時，月份會影響價格和空檔。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the general time of the visit.","zh":"這個片語提供到訪的大概時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for a week","meaning":"為期一星期","examples":[{"en":"Tom and his wife want to rent a cottage for a week.","zh":"Tom 和他的妻子想租用小屋為期一星期。"},{"en":"For a week means for seven days or approximately seven nights.","zh":"for a week 指七天或大約七晚。"},{"en":"The family booked the cottage for a week during the school holiday.","zh":"那個家庭在學校假期預訂小屋一星期。"},{"en":"Holiday cottages are often rented for a week at a time.","zh":"度假小屋通常以一星期為單位出租。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the length of stay.","zh":"這個片語描述入住時間長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what date did you have in mind?","meaning":"你心目中是哪個日期？","examples":[{"en":"Shirley asks Tom what date he has in mind.","zh":"Shirley 問 Tom 心目中是哪個日期。"},{"en":"What date did you have in mind? means what date were you thinking of choosing?","zh":"what date did you have in mind? 指你原本想選哪一天？"},{"en":"The receptionist asked, “What date did you have in mind for your stay?”","zh":"接待員問：「你心目中是哪個入住日期？」"},{"en":"This question is polite and useful when checking availability.","zh":"這個問題有禮，並適合用於查詢空檔。"},{"en":"It invites the customer to suggest a preferred date.","zh":"它邀請客戶提出偏好的日期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have something in mind","meaning":"心中有……","examples":[{"en":"Tom has the week beginning 14th May in mind.","zh":"Tom 心中想的是由五月十四日開始那一星期。"},{"en":"To have something in mind means to already be thinking of a particular idea, plan or choice.","zh":"have something in mind 指心中已有某個想法、計劃或選擇。"},{"en":"Do you have a particular cottage in mind?","zh":"你心中有特別想租的小屋嗎？"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when asking about preferences.","zh":"這個片語適合用於詢問偏好。"},{"en":"It suggests the person may already have a choice before the discussion.","zh":"它暗示對方在討論前可能已有選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the week beginning","meaning":"由……開始的那一星期","examples":[{"en":"Tom wants the week beginning the 14th, if possible.","zh":"如果可以的話，Tom 想要由十四日開始的那一星期。"},{"en":"The week beginning a date means the seven-day period starting on that date.","zh":"the week beginning a date 指由某日期開始的七天期間。"},{"en":"The cottage is available for the week beginning 28th May.","zh":"小屋在由五月二十八日開始的那一星期有空檔。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in holiday bookings and schedules.","zh":"這個片語常見於度假預訂和時間表。"},{"en":"It helps identify a whole week by its starting date.","zh":"它用開始日期來標示整個星期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"if possible","meaning":"如果可以的話","examples":[{"en":"Tom would like to come in the week beginning the 14th, if possible.","zh":"如果可以的話，Tom 想在由十四日開始的那一星期前來。"},{"en":"If possible means if it can be arranged or if circumstances allow it.","zh":"if possible 指如果能安排，或如果情況容許。"},{"en":"We would like a sea view, if possible.","zh":"如果可以的話，我們想要海景房。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a request sound polite and flexible.","zh":"這個片語令要求聽起來有禮而有彈性。"},{"en":"It shows that the speaker understands the request may not be possible.","zh":"它顯示說話者明白要求未必能做到。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I’ll just check","meaning":"我查一查","examples":[{"en":"Shirley says she will just check whether the cottage is available.","zh":"Shirley 說她會查一查那間小屋是否有空。"},{"en":"I’ll just check means I will quickly look at the information to confirm it.","zh":"I’ll just check 指我會快速查看資料以確認。"},{"en":"I’ll just check the booking calendar for you.","zh":"我幫你查一查預訂日曆。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in customer service conversations.","zh":"這個片語常見於客戶服務對話。"},{"en":"It reassures the customer that the speaker is checking before answering.","zh":"它讓客戶安心，知道說話者正在確認後才回答。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"already booked","meaning":"已被預訂","examples":[{"en":"Granary Cottage is already booked for the week beginning the 14th.","zh":"Granary Cottage 在由十四日開始那一星期已被預訂。"},{"en":"Already booked means someone has reserved it before now.","zh":"already booked 指已經有人預留。"},{"en":"The cottage is already booked for most of August.","zh":"那間小屋八月大部分時間已被預訂。"},{"en":"If accommodation is already booked, new customers must choose another date or place.","zh":"如果住宿已被預訂，新客戶必須選擇另一日期或地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in travel and accommodation enquiries.","zh":"這個片語常見於旅遊和住宿查詢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"free the week beginning","meaning":"由……開始那星期有空檔","examples":[{"en":"The cottage is free the week beginning the 28th.","zh":"那間小屋由二十八日開始那星期有空檔。"},{"en":"Free the week beginning a date means available for booking during the week starting on that date.","zh":"free the week beginning a date 指由某日期開始那星期可供預訂。"},{"en":"The room is free the week beginning 3rd June.","zh":"那間房由六月三日開始那星期有空檔。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when checking accommodation availability.","zh":"這個片語用於查詢住宿空檔。"},{"en":"Here, “free” means available, not without cost.","zh":"在這裡，“free” 指有空檔，不是免費。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"for seven nights","meaning":"住七晚","examples":[{"en":"The cottage is available for seven nights.","zh":"那間小屋可供入住七晚。"},{"en":"For seven nights means for a stay lasting seven nights.","zh":"for seven nights 指入住時間為七晚。"},{"en":"The couple booked the cottage for seven nights in May.","zh":"那對夫婦在五月預訂了小屋住七晚。"},{"en":"Accommodation prices are often calculated by the night or by the week.","zh":"住宿價格常按晚數或星期計算。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly states the length of the booking.","zh":"這個片語清楚說明預訂長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, the week beginning the 28th is the only available week in May.","zh":"事實上，由二十八日開始那星期是五月唯一有空檔的一星期。"},{"en":"In fact introduces extra information that strengthens or corrects what has just been said.","zh":"in fact 引入額外資料，用來加強或修正剛才所說。"},{"en":"The cottage is quite popular; in fact, it is fully booked until June.","zh":"那間小屋相當受歡迎；事實上，它到六月前都已滿。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when adding a more precise point.","zh":"這個片語適合用於加入更準確的重點。"},{"en":"It often prepares the listener for something slightly surprising.","zh":"它常讓聽者準備聽到稍微令人意外的資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the only time","meaning":"唯一時間","examples":[{"en":"The week beginning the 28th is the only time available in May.","zh":"由二十八日開始那星期是五月唯一有空檔的時間。"},{"en":"The only time means the single possible time or period.","zh":"the only time 指唯一可行的時間或時段。"},{"en":"Friday morning is the only time the cleaner can come this week.","zh":"星期五早上是清潔員本週唯一可以上門的時間。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that there are no other options.","zh":"這個片語強調沒有其他選擇。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing limited availability.","zh":"它適合用於討論有限空檔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"manage that","meaning":"可以安排得到","examples":[{"en":"Tom thinks he and his wife could manage that week.","zh":"Tom 覺得他和妻子可以安排得到那一星期。"},{"en":"To manage that means to be able to arrange or cope with that option.","zh":"manage that 指能夠安排或應付那個選項。"},{"en":"We cannot come on the 14th, but we could manage the following week.","zh":"我們十四日不能來，但下一星期可以安排得到。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when adjusting plans.","zh":"這個片語常用於調整計劃時。"},{"en":"It suggests the option is possible, though not necessarily ideal.","zh":"它暗示該選項可行，但未必最理想。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"change a couple of things","meaning":"改動幾件事","examples":[{"en":"Tom and his wife would need to change a couple of things.","zh":"Tom 和他的妻子需要改動幾件事。"},{"en":"To change a couple of things means to make two or a few adjustments.","zh":"change a couple of things 指作出兩三個調整。"},{"en":"We can travel that week, but we need to change a couple of things at work.","zh":"我們可以那星期旅行，但需要在工作上改動幾件事。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds casual and suggests the changes are manageable.","zh":"這個片語語氣輕鬆，暗示改動可以應付。"},{"en":"It is often used when plans need small adjustments.","zh":"它常用於計劃需要小調整時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"how much would it cost?","meaning":"費用是多少？","examples":[{"en":"Tom asks how much the cottage would cost.","zh":"Tom 問那間小屋的費用是多少。"},{"en":"How much would it cost? asks about the price of something.","zh":"how much would it cost? 用來詢問某物的價格。"},{"en":"How much would it cost to stay for seven nights?","zh":"住七晚費用是多少？"},{"en":"This question is polite and practical in booking conversations.","zh":"這個問題在預訂對話中有禮而實用。"},{"en":"It helps the customer check whether the option fits their budget.","zh":"它幫助客戶確認該選項是否符合預算。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the beginning of high season","meaning":"旺季開始","examples":[{"en":"The week beginning the 28th is the beginning of high season.","zh":"由二十八日開始那星期是旺季開始。"},{"en":"The beginning of high season means the start of the busiest and most expensive holiday period.","zh":"the beginning of high season 指最繁忙和最昂貴旅遊時段的開始。"},{"en":"Prices often rise at the beginning of high season.","zh":"價格通常在旺季開始時上升。"},{"en":"Accommodation may be harder to book once high season begins.","zh":"旺季一開始，住宿可能更難預訂。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in travel and tourism.","zh":"這個片語常見於旅遊和觀光業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"high season","meaning":"旺季","examples":[{"en":"Granary Cottage costs more during high season.","zh":"Granary Cottage 在旺季期間費用較高。"},{"en":"High season is the time of year when many tourists travel and prices are higher.","zh":"high season 指很多旅客出行、價格較高的一年中某段時間。"},{"en":"Summer is high season for many seaside cottages.","zh":"對許多海邊小屋來說，夏天是旺季。"},{"en":"During high season, accommodation can be fully booked months in advance.","zh":"旺季期間，住宿可能提前數月已被訂滿。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with low season or off-season.","zh":"這個片語與淡季或非旺季相對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for the week","meaning":"一星期的費用","examples":[{"en":"Granary Cottage costs £550 for the week.","zh":"Granary Cottage 一星期的費用是 550 英鎊。"},{"en":"For the week means for the whole seven-day booking period.","zh":"for the week 指整個七天預訂期間。"},{"en":"The cottage costs £500 for the week, including basic facilities.","zh":"那間小屋一星期費用為 500 英鎊，包括基本設施。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving a weekly accommodation price.","zh":"這個片語適合用於提供每星期住宿價格。"},{"en":"It shows that the price is not per night.","zh":"它顯示價格不是每晚計算。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a bit more than","meaning":"比……多一點","examples":[{"en":"The price is a bit more than Tom wanted to pay.","zh":"這個價格比 Tom 想支付的多一點。"},{"en":"A bit more than means slightly above a certain amount or expectation.","zh":"a bit more than 指稍微高於某個金額或期望。"},{"en":"The cottage was a bit more than our budget.","zh":"那間小屋比我們預算多一點。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds softer than saying something is too expensive.","zh":"這個片語比直接說某物太貴更柔和。"},{"en":"It is useful when politely discussing cost.","zh":"它適合用於有禮地討論費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"I’m afraid","meaning":"恐怕","examples":[{"en":"Tom says the price is a bit more than he wanted to pay, I’m afraid.","zh":"Tom 說，恐怕這個價格比他想支付的多一點。"},{"en":"I’m afraid is used to soften bad news or disagreement.","zh":"I’m afraid 用來柔化壞消息或不同意見。"},{"en":"I’m afraid the cottage is already booked that week.","zh":"恐怕那間小屋那星期已被預訂。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds polite and slightly apologetic.","zh":"這個片語聽起來有禮並帶一點歉意。"},{"en":"It does not always mean fear; it often means “unfortunately”.","zh":"它不一定表示害怕；常有「可惜」的意思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"budget up to","meaning":"預算最高為……","examples":[{"en":"Tom and his wife have budgeted up to £500 for accommodation.","zh":"Tom 和他的妻子住宿預算最高為 500 英鎊。"},{"en":"To budget up to an amount means to plan to spend no more than that amount.","zh":"budget up to an amount 指計劃花費不超過某金額。"},{"en":"We budgeted up to £800 for the holiday cottage.","zh":"我們度假小屋預算最高為 800 英鎊。"},{"en":"Having a clear budget helps customers decide which option is realistic.","zh":"有清晰預算有助客戶決定哪個選項現實可行。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing money and travel plans.","zh":"這個片語常見於討論金錢和旅遊計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"accommodation","meaning":"住宿","examples":[{"en":"Tom has budgeted up to £500 for accommodation.","zh":"Tom 的住宿預算最高為 500 英鎊。"},{"en":"Accommodation means a place to stay, such as a hotel room, flat or cottage.","zh":"accommodation 指可住宿的地方，例如酒店房、單位或小屋。"},{"en":"Students often look for cheap accommodation when they study abroad.","zh":"學生海外升學時常尋找便宜住宿。"},{"en":"Accommodation costs can be one of the largest parts of a holiday budget.","zh":"住宿費可以是假期預算中最大開支之一。"},{"en":"This word is common in travel, housing and education contexts.","zh":"這個字常見於旅遊、住屋和教育語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"finish converting something into","meaning":"剛完成把某物改建成……","examples":[{"en":"Shirley has just finished converting another building into a cottage.","zh":"Shirley 剛完成把另一棟建築物改建成小屋。"},{"en":"To finish converting something into something else means to complete the work of changing its use or form.","zh":"finish converting something into something else 指完成把某物用途或形式改變成另一物的工程。"},{"en":"They finished converting an old barn into a guest house.","zh":"他們剛完成把舊穀倉改建成賓館。"},{"en":"Conversion work may involve rebuilding, decorating and adding facilities.","zh":"改建工程可能涉及重建、裝修和加設設施。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in property and renovation contexts.","zh":"這個片語常見於物業和翻新語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"convert something into","meaning":"把某物改建成……","examples":[{"en":"Shirley converted another building into Chervil Cottage.","zh":"Shirley 把另一棟建築物改建成 Chervil Cottage。"},{"en":"To convert something into something else means to change it so that it has a new use or form.","zh":"convert something into something else 指改變某物，使它有新用途或形式。"},{"en":"The family converted the garage into a small studio.","zh":"那個家庭把車房改建成一間小工作室。"},{"en":"Converting an old building can give it new life.","zh":"改建舊建築可以給它新生命。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in building, design and renovation.","zh":"這個片語常見於建築、設計和翻新。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be called","meaning":"名為……","examples":[{"en":"The new cottage is called Chervil Cottage.","zh":"那間新小屋名為 Chervil Cottage。"},{"en":"To be called something means to have that name.","zh":"be called something 指名稱是某個名字。"},{"en":"The small cottage is called Rose Cottage.","zh":"那間小屋名為 Rose Cottage。"},{"en":"Names can help guests remember and identify different cottages.","zh":"名稱可以幫助客人記住和識別不同小屋。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when naming people, places or things.","zh":"這個片語用於命名人物、地方或事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what was that again?","meaning":"剛才那是甚麼？","examples":[{"en":"Tom asks Shirley to repeat the name of the cottage.","zh":"Tom 請 Shirley 重複小屋的名字。"},{"en":"What was that again? is used when asking someone to repeat something you did not catch clearly.","zh":"what was that again? 用於請別人重複自己剛才沒有聽清楚的內容。"},{"en":"“What was that again?” Tom asked when he heard the unusual cottage name.","zh":"Tom 聽到那個不常見的小屋名時問：「剛才那是甚麼？」"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and natural in conversation.","zh":"這個片語在對話中有禮而自然。"},{"en":"It is useful when a word, name or number is unfamiliar.","zh":"當字詞、名字或數字不熟悉時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"V for Victor","meaning":"V，即 Victor 的 V","examples":[{"en":"Shirley spells Chervil with “V for Victor”.","zh":"Shirley 用 “V for Victor” 來串 Chervil。"},{"en":"V for Victor is a way to clarify the letter V by using a familiar word.","zh":"V for Victor 是用熟悉詞語 Victor 來清楚說明字母 V 的方法。"},{"en":"She said, “It’s V for Victor, not B for Bravo.”","zh":"她說：「是 Victor 的 V，不是 Bravo 的 B。」"},{"en":"People use this method on the phone to avoid spelling mistakes.","zh":"人們在電話中用這種方法避免串字錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when spelling names or addresses.","zh":"這個片語常用於串姓名或地址。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"that’s a herb, isn’t it?","meaning":"那是一種香草，對吧？","examples":[{"en":"Tom realises that chervil is a herb.","zh":"Tom 意識到 chervil 是一種香草。"},{"en":"That’s a herb, isn’t it? is a tag question used to check or confirm information.","zh":"that’s a herb, isn’t it? 是反意疑問句，用來確認資料。"},{"en":"“Chervil? That’s a herb, isn’t it?” Tom asked.","zh":"Tom 問：「Chervil？那是一種香草，對吧？」"},{"en":"This structure sounds conversational and invites confirmation.","zh":"這個結構聽起來口語，並邀請對方確認。"},{"en":"It is useful when the speaker is fairly sure but wants to check.","zh":"當說話者頗肯定但想查證時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"grow fairly wild","meaning":"生長得頗為野生；到處生長","examples":[{"en":"Chervil grows fairly wild around the area.","zh":"Chervil 在該區生長得頗為野生。"},{"en":"To grow fairly wild means to grow naturally and quite freely without much control.","zh":"grow fairly wild 指自然並相當自由地生長，沒有太多控制。"},{"en":"Mint grows fairly wild near the old garden wall.","zh":"薄荷在舊花園牆附近生長得頗為野生。"},{"en":"Plants that grow wild often spread without being deliberately planted.","zh":"野生生長的植物常會在無人刻意種植下擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural growth in an area.","zh":"這個片語描述某地的自然生長情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"around here","meaning":"在這附近","examples":[{"en":"Chervil grows fairly wild around here.","zh":"Chervil 在這附近到處生長。"},{"en":"Around here means in this local area or nearby.","zh":"around here 指在本區或附近地方。"},{"en":"There are several good walking routes around here.","zh":"這附近有幾條很好的步行路線。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when describing a place familiar to the speaker.","zh":"這個片語常用於描述說話者熟悉的地方。"},{"en":"It is conversational and location-based.","zh":"它較口語，並與地點有關。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tell me something about","meaning":"告訴我一些關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"Tom asks Shirley to tell him something about Chervil Cottage.","zh":"Tom 請 Shirley 告訴他一些關於 Chervil Cottage 的資料。"},{"en":"Tell me something about means give me some basic information about a person, place or thing.","zh":"tell me something about 指給我一些關於某人、某地或某物的基本資料。"},{"en":"Could you tell me something about the facilities in the cottage?","zh":"你可以告訴我一些關於小屋設施的資料嗎？"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and open-ended.","zh":"這個片語有禮，而且問題較開放。"},{"en":"It is useful when asking for an introduction before making a decision.","zh":"它適合在作決定前請對方作簡介。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"built as a garage","meaning":"原本建作車房","examples":[{"en":"The building was originally built as a garage.","zh":"該建築物原本建作車房。"},{"en":"Built as a garage means constructed for the purpose of storing cars or equipment.","zh":"built as a garage 指建造時用途是存放汽車或設備。"},{"en":"The small stone building was built as a garage before it became a cottage.","zh":"那棟小石屋在變成小屋前原本建作車房。"},{"en":"Knowing the original use of a building can explain its size and shape.","zh":"知道建築物原本用途，可以解釋其大小和形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first purpose of a building.","zh":"這個片語描述建築物最初的用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a little smaller than","meaning":"比……稍小","examples":[{"en":"Chervil Cottage is a little smaller than Granary Cottage.","zh":"Chervil Cottage 比 Granary Cottage 稍小。"},{"en":"A little smaller than means slightly smaller in size.","zh":"a little smaller than 指尺寸上稍微較小。"},{"en":"This cottage is a little smaller than the one you first asked about.","zh":"這間小屋比你最初查詢的那間稍小。"},{"en":"A smaller cottage may still be suitable if only two people are staying.","zh":"如果只有兩人入住，較小的小屋仍可能合適。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a gentle comparison.","zh":"這個片語作出溫和比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sleep two people","meaning":"可供兩人入住","examples":[{"en":"Chervil Cottage can sleep two people.","zh":"Chervil Cottage 可供兩人入住。"},{"en":"To sleep two people means to have enough beds or space for two people to stay overnight.","zh":"sleep two people 指有足夠床位或空間讓兩人過夜住宿。"},{"en":"The guest room can sleep two people comfortably.","zh":"那間客房可舒適地供兩人入住。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in accommodation descriptions.","zh":"這個片語常見於住宿描述。"},{"en":"Here, “sleep” means accommodate overnight, not the act of sleeping.","zh":"在這裡，“sleep” 指容納過夜，而不是睡覺這個動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a double bedroom","meaning":"雙人睡房","examples":[{"en":"Chervil Cottage has a double bedroom.","zh":"Chervil Cottage 有一間雙人睡房。"},{"en":"A double bedroom is a bedroom with a double bed or space for two people.","zh":"double bedroom 指有雙人床或可供兩人使用的睡房。"},{"en":"The cottage has one double bedroom and a small living room.","zh":"那間小屋有一間雙人睡房和一個小客廳。"},{"en":"A double bedroom is suitable for a couple.","zh":"雙人睡房適合一對夫婦或伴侶。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in property and hotel descriptions.","zh":"這個片語常見於物業和酒店描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get to it from","meaning":"從……到達那裏","examples":[{"en":"Guests can get to the garden from the living room.","zh":"客人可以從客廳到達花園。"},{"en":"To get to it from somewhere means to reach that place by going from another place.","zh":"get to it from somewhere 指從某地方到達那裏。"},{"en":"You can get to the patio from the kitchen.","zh":"你可以從廚房到達庭院。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing layout and access.","zh":"這個片語適合用於描述佈局和通道。"},{"en":"It helps guests understand how rooms and outdoor areas connect.","zh":"它幫助客人理解房間和戶外區域如何連接。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"French doors","meaning":"落地玻璃門；法式玻璃門","examples":[{"en":"The living room has French doors leading to the garden.","zh":"客廳有通往花園的法式玻璃門。"},{"en":"French doors are glass doors, usually in a pair, that open out to a garden or patio.","zh":"French doors 指玻璃門，通常成對，通往花園或庭院。"},{"en":"French doors can make a room brighter by letting in natural light.","zh":"法式玻璃門可以讓自然光進入，使房間更明亮。"},{"en":"They often create an attractive connection between indoor and outdoor space.","zh":"它們常在室內和戶外空間之間形成美觀連接。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in home and property descriptions.","zh":"這個片語常見於家居和物業描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"provide two deckchairs","meaning":"提供兩張摺椅","examples":[{"en":"Shirley provides two deckchairs for guests.","zh":"Shirley 為客人提供兩張摺椅。"},{"en":"To provide two deckchairs means to make two outdoor folding chairs available for guests.","zh":"provide two deckchairs 指提供兩張戶外摺椅給客人使用。"},{"en":"The cottage owner provides two deckchairs for sitting in the garden.","zh":"小屋主人提供兩張摺椅，讓客人在花園坐下。"},{"en":"Small extras like deckchairs can make a holiday stay more comfortable.","zh":"摺椅這類小配套可以令度假住宿更舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an included facility.","zh":"這個片語描述已包括的設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"build a patio","meaning":"建一個庭院","examples":[{"en":"Shirley hopes to build a patio in the near future.","zh":"Shirley 希望在不久將來建一個庭院。"},{"en":"To build a patio means to make a paved outdoor area for sitting or eating.","zh":"build a patio 指建造一個鋪砌的戶外區域，供人坐下或用餐。"},{"en":"They plan to build a patio outside the cottage next summer.","zh":"他們計劃明年夏天在小屋外建一個庭院。"},{"en":"A patio can make a garden more useful for guests.","zh":"庭院可以令花園對客人更實用。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in home improvement.","zh":"這個片語常見於家居改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the near future","meaning":"在不久將來","examples":[{"en":"Shirley hopes to build a patio in the near future.","zh":"Shirley 希望在不久將來建一個庭院。"},{"en":"In the near future means soon, but not immediately or on a fixed date.","zh":"in the near future 指很快，但不是立即或在固定日期。"},{"en":"The owners hope to add outdoor seating in the near future.","zh":"業主希望在不久將來增設戶外座位。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a general future time without promising exactly when.","zh":"這個片語提供大概未來時間，而不承諾確切日期。"},{"en":"It is useful when plans are not yet confirmed.","zh":"當計劃尚未確定時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"I wouldn’t like to guarantee","meaning":"我不敢保證","examples":[{"en":"Shirley would not like to guarantee that the patio will be finished by May.","zh":"Shirley 不敢保證庭院會在五月前完成。"},{"en":"I wouldn’t like to guarantee means I cannot promise something with certainty.","zh":"I wouldn’t like to guarantee 指我不能百分百承諾某事。"},{"en":"I wouldn’t like to guarantee that the work will be finished before your stay.","zh":"我不敢保證工程會在你入住前完成。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and honest when something is uncertain.","zh":"當某事不確定時，這個片語有禮而誠實。"},{"en":"It avoids making a promise that may not be kept.","zh":"它避免作出可能無法兌現的承諾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be finished by","meaning":"在……前完成","examples":[{"en":"The patio may not be finished by May.","zh":"庭院可能未能在五月前完成。"},{"en":"To be finished by a time means to be completed no later than that time.","zh":"be finished by a time 指不遲於某時間完成。"},{"en":"The renovation should be finished by the end of April.","zh":"翻新工程應在四月底前完成。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing deadlines.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論截止日期。"},{"en":"It focuses on completion before a specific date or period.","zh":"它着重在特定日期或時段前完成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"open onto","meaning":"通往；面向","examples":[{"en":"The front door opens onto the old farmyard.","zh":"前門通往舊農家庭院。"},{"en":"To open onto a place means for a door or window to lead directly to that place.","zh":"open onto a place 指門或窗直接通往某地方。"},{"en":"The kitchen door opens onto a small garden.","zh":"廚房門通往一個小花園。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe how a building connects with its surroundings.","zh":"這個片語有助描述建築物如何與周圍環境連接。"},{"en":"It is common in property descriptions.","zh":"它常見於物業描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the old farmyard","meaning":"舊農家庭院","examples":[{"en":"The front door of the cottage opens onto the old farmyard.","zh":"小屋前門通往舊農家庭院。"},{"en":"The old farmyard is the outdoor area of a former farm, often surrounded by farm buildings.","zh":"old farmyard 指舊農場的戶外庭院區域，通常被農場建築包圍。"},{"en":"Guests can park in the old farmyard in front of the cottage.","zh":"客人可以把車停在小屋前的舊農家庭院。"},{"en":"An old farmyard can give a cottage a rural and historic feeling.","zh":"舊農家庭院可以令小屋帶有鄉村和歷史感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the setting outside the cottage.","zh":"這個片語描述小屋外的環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"parking isn’t a problem","meaning":"泊車不是問題","examples":[{"en":"Parking is not a problem at Chervil Cottage.","zh":"在 Chervil Cottage 泊車不是問題。"},{"en":"Parking isn’t a problem means there is enough space or an easy arrangement for cars.","zh":"parking isn’t a problem 指有足夠空間或容易安排車位。"},{"en":"Parking is not a problem because there is a large yard outside.","zh":"泊車不是問題，因為外面有一個大庭院。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures guests who plan to drive.","zh":"這個片語讓打算駕車的客人安心。"},{"en":"It is common in accommodation enquiries.","zh":"它常見於住宿查詢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"plenty of room","meaning":"有很多空間","examples":[{"en":"There is plenty of room at the front for parking.","zh":"前面有很多空間可供泊車。"},{"en":"Plenty of room means more than enough space.","zh":"plenty of room 指有超過足夠的空間。"},{"en":"There is plenty of room in the yard for two cars.","zh":"院子裏有很多空間可以泊兩架車。"},{"en":"Having plenty of room makes guests feel less worried about practical arrangements.","zh":"有很多空間會令客人較少擔心實際安排。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests comfort and convenience.","zh":"這個片語暗示舒適和方便。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at the front","meaning":"在前面","examples":[{"en":"There is plenty of room at the front for parking.","zh":"前面有很多空間可供泊車。"},{"en":"At the front means in the area in front of a building or object.","zh":"at the front 指在建築物或物件前方的區域。"},{"en":"There are flowers at the front of the cottage.","zh":"小屋前面有花。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe location clearly.","zh":"這個片語有助清楚描述位置。"},{"en":"It contrasts with “at the back” or “inside”.","zh":"它與 “at the back” 或 “inside” 相對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"potted plants","meaning":"盆栽","examples":[{"en":"There are some trees and potted plants in front of the cottage.","zh":"小屋前面有一些樹和盆栽。"},{"en":"Potted plants are plants grown in containers or pots.","zh":"potted plants 指種在容器或花盆中的植物。"},{"en":"Potted plants can make the entrance of a cottage look more attractive.","zh":"盆栽可以令小屋入口看起來更吸引。"},{"en":"They are easier to move than plants growing directly in the ground.","zh":"它們比直接種在地上的植物更容易移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in garden and home descriptions.","zh":"這個片語常見於花園和家居描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"facilities in the cottage","meaning":"小屋內的設施","examples":[{"en":"Tom asks about the facilities in the cottage.","zh":"Tom 詢問小屋內的設施。"},{"en":"Facilities in the cottage are the equipment and features available for guests to use.","zh":"facilities in the cottage 指小屋內供客人使用的設備和特色。"},{"en":"The facilities in the cottage include heating, a cooker and a shower.","zh":"小屋內的設施包括暖氣、煮食爐和淋浴。"},{"en":"Guests ask about facilities to know whether the cottage will meet their needs.","zh":"客人詢問設施，是為了知道小屋是否符合需要。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in accommodation descriptions.","zh":"這個片語常見於住宿描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"standard things like","meaning":"例如……的基本設備","examples":[{"en":"Tom expects standard things like a cooker and fridge.","zh":"Tom 預期有煮食爐和雪櫃等基本設備。"},{"en":"Standard things like means normal basic items such as the examples mentioned.","zh":"standard things like 指正常基本物品，例如提到的例子。"},{"en":"A rented cottage should have standard things like bedding, heating and kitchen equipment.","zh":"出租小屋應有床上用品、暖氣和廚房設備等基本設備。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples of expected facilities.","zh":"這個片語引入預期設施的例子。"},{"en":"It sounds conversational and practical.","zh":"它聽起來口語而實用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"I presume","meaning":"我想；我推測","examples":[{"en":"Tom presumes that the cottage has a cooker and a fridge.","zh":"Tom 推測小屋有煮食爐和雪櫃。"},{"en":"I presume means I suppose or I assume something is true.","zh":"I presume 指我想或我推測某事是真的。"},{"en":"I presume towels are included in the booking.","zh":"我想預訂中已包括毛巾。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and slightly formal.","zh":"這個片語有禮並略正式。"},{"en":"It is useful when checking something that seems likely.","zh":"當確認看似很可能的事情時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"kitchen area","meaning":"廚房區","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen area has a fridge-freezer and an electric cooker.","zh":"廚房區有雪櫃連冰格和電煮食爐。"},{"en":"A kitchen area is the part of a room or cottage used for cooking and food preparation.","zh":"kitchen area 指用於煮食和準備食物的區域。"},{"en":"The kitchen area is small but has everything guests need.","zh":"廚房區很小，但有客人需要的一切。"},{"en":"In small cottages, the kitchen area may be part of the living room.","zh":"在小屋中，廚房區可能是客廳的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a functional space rather than necessarily a separate room.","zh":"這個片語描述功能區域，不一定是獨立房間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fridge-freezer","meaning":"雪櫃連冰格","examples":[{"en":"The cottage has a fridge-freezer in the kitchen area.","zh":"小屋的廚房區有雪櫃連冰格。"},{"en":"A fridge-freezer is an appliance with both a refrigerator and a freezer section.","zh":"fridge-freezer 指同時有冷藏和冷凍部分的電器。"},{"en":"Guests can keep fresh food in the fridge and frozen food in the freezer.","zh":"客人可以把新鮮食物放在雪櫃，把冷凍食物放在冰格。"},{"en":"A fridge-freezer is useful for people staying for a whole week.","zh":"對住一整星期的人來說，雪櫃連冰格很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English accommodation descriptions.","zh":"這個片語常見於英式英語住宿描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put in","meaning":"安裝","examples":[{"en":"Shirley has just put in an electric cooker.","zh":"Shirley 剛安裝了一個電煮食爐。"},{"en":"To put in something means to install or add it.","zh":"put in something 指安裝或加設某物。"},{"en":"The owner put in a new shower before the summer season.","zh":"業主在夏季前安裝了新的淋浴設備。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when talking about home improvements.","zh":"這個片語常用於談論家居改善。"},{"en":"It often refers to adding equipment permanently.","zh":"它常指永久加裝設備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"electric cooker","meaning":"電煮食爐","examples":[{"en":"Shirley has just put in an electric cooker.","zh":"Shirley 剛安裝了一個電煮食爐。"},{"en":"An electric cooker is a cooking appliance powered by electricity.","zh":"electric cooker 指以電力運作的煮食設備。"},{"en":"Guests can use the electric cooker to prepare meals in the cottage.","zh":"客人可以用電煮食爐在小屋內準備餐點。"},{"en":"Electric cookers are common in rental accommodation because they are convenient and easy to use.","zh":"電煮食爐常見於出租住宿，因為方便而易用。"},{"en":"This phrase names a basic kitchen facility.","zh":"這個片語命名一項基本廚房設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"washing machine","meaning":"洗衣機","examples":[{"en":"Tom asks whether the cottage has a washing machine.","zh":"Tom 問小屋是否有洗衣機。"},{"en":"A washing machine is an appliance used for washing clothes.","zh":"washing machine 指用來清洗衣物的電器。"},{"en":"A washing machine is useful for guests staying for a week or more.","zh":"洗衣機對住一星期或以上的客人很有用。"},{"en":"Holiday accommodation with a washing machine can be more convenient for families.","zh":"有洗衣機的度假住宿對家庭來說更方便。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common household appliance.","zh":"這個片語命名一種常見家電。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the living room","meaning":"在客廳","examples":[{"en":"There is a TV in the living room.","zh":"客廳裏有一部電視。"},{"en":"In the living room means in the main room used for relaxing or sitting.","zh":"in the living room 指在主要用作放鬆或坐下的房間。"},{"en":"Guests can watch DVDs in the living room after dinner.","zh":"客人晚飯後可以在客廳看 DVD。"},{"en":"The living room is often where guests spend most of their indoor time.","zh":"客廳通常是客人在室內逗留最多時間的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the location of a facility.","zh":"這個片語描述設施的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"play DVDs","meaning":"播放 DVD","examples":[{"en":"The TV in the living room plays DVDs too.","zh":"客廳的電視也可以播放 DVD。"},{"en":"To play DVDs means to show films or videos from DVD discs.","zh":"play DVDs 指播放 DVD 光碟中的電影或影片。"},{"en":"The cottage TV can play DVDs if guests bring their own films.","zh":"如果客人自備電影，小屋電視可以播放 DVD。"},{"en":"DVD facilities may be useful where internet access is limited.","zh":"在互聯網有限的地方，DVD 設施可能很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a media function of a television or player.","zh":"這個片語指電視或播放器的媒體功能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"too small for","meaning":"太小，容不下……","examples":[{"en":"The bathroom is too small for a bath.","zh":"浴室太小，容不下浴缸。"},{"en":"Too small for something means not large enough to contain or suit it.","zh":"too small for something 指不夠大，不能容納或適合某物。"},{"en":"The kitchen is too small for a dining table.","zh":"廚房太小，容不下餐桌。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why something cannot be included.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何某物不能包括在內。"},{"en":"It is common in property descriptions.","zh":"它常見於物業描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a bath","meaning":"浴缸","examples":[{"en":"The bathroom is too small for a bath.","zh":"浴室太小，容不下浴缸。"},{"en":"A bath is a large container that people fill with water to wash or relax in.","zh":"bath 指可注水讓人清洗或放鬆的大容器。"},{"en":"Some guests prefer a bath after a long walk.","zh":"有些客人在長途步行後較喜歡浸浴。"},{"en":"Baths use more water than quick showers.","zh":"浴缸用水量比快速淋浴多。"},{"en":"This word can refer to the object or the act of bathing.","zh":"這個字可指浴缸本身，也可指浸浴這個動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a shower instead","meaning":"改為淋浴","examples":[{"en":"The bathroom has a shower instead of a bath.","zh":"浴室改為設有淋浴，而不是浴缸。"},{"en":"A shower instead means a shower is provided as the alternative.","zh":"a shower instead 指以淋浴作為替代安排。"},{"en":"The cottage has a shower instead because the bathroom is small.","zh":"小屋因浴室細小而改為設有淋浴。"},{"en":"Many guests are happy with a shower if it is clean and powerful.","zh":"如果淋浴乾淨而水力足，許多客人也會滿意。"},{"en":"This phrase shows replacement or alternative choice.","zh":"這個片語顯示替代或另一選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prefer that nowadays","meaning":"現在較喜歡那樣","examples":[{"en":"Many people prefer a shower nowadays.","zh":"現在許多人較喜歡淋浴。"},{"en":"Prefer that nowadays means like that option more in modern times.","zh":"prefer that nowadays 指現今較喜歡那個選項。"},{"en":"Many guests prefer showers nowadays because they are quicker.","zh":"現在很多客人較喜歡淋浴，因為更快捷。"},{"en":"This phrase compares present preferences with past habits.","zh":"這個片語比較現今偏好與過去習慣。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining changing lifestyles.","zh":"它適合用於解釋生活方式變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"environmentally friendly","meaning":"環保","examples":[{"en":"A shower is usually more environmentally friendly than a bath.","zh":"淋浴通常比浸浴更環保。"},{"en":"Environmentally friendly means less harmful to the environment.","zh":"environmentally friendly 指對環境傷害較少。"},{"en":"Using less water is more environmentally friendly.","zh":"使用較少水更環保。"},{"en":"A shower can be environmentally friendly if it does not last too long.","zh":"如果淋浴時間不太長，它可以是環保的。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in discussions of energy, water and sustainability.","zh":"這個片語常見於能源、用水和可持續性討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unless","meaning":"除非","examples":[{"en":"A shower is more environmentally friendly unless you spend half the day in it.","zh":"淋浴更環保，除非你在裏面花上大半天。"},{"en":"Unless means except if.","zh":"unless 指除非某情況發生。"},{"en":"The cottage will be warm enough unless the weather becomes extremely cold.","zh":"除非天氣變得極冷，否則小屋應該夠暖。"},{"en":"This word introduces a condition that changes the main statement.","zh":"這個字引入會改變主要說法的條件。"},{"en":"It is common in warnings and practical explanations.","zh":"它常見於警告和實用解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"spend half the day in it","meaning":"在裏面花上大半天","examples":[{"en":"A shower saves water unless you spend half the day in it.","zh":"淋浴可以節省用水，除非你在裏面花上大半天。"},{"en":"To spend half the day in it means to stay in it for an extremely long time.","zh":"spend half the day in it 指在裏面待非常久。"},{"en":"A shower is efficient unless someone spends half the day in it.","zh":"淋浴很有效率，除非有人在裏面花上大半天。"},{"en":"This phrase is humorous and exaggerated.","zh":"這個片語帶幽默和誇張語氣。"},{"en":"It means using something so long that the benefit disappears.","zh":"它意思是使用某物太久，以致好處消失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"what about heating?","meaning":"暖氣方面怎樣？","examples":[{"en":"Tom asks Shirley about heating in the cottage.","zh":"Tom 問 Shirley 小屋暖氣方面怎樣。"},{"en":"What about heating? asks for information about how the place is warmed.","zh":"what about heating? 用來詢問某地方如何供暖。"},{"en":"What about heating in the bedroom during winter?","zh":"冬天睡房暖氣方面怎樣？"},{"en":"This question is short, practical and natural in accommodation enquiries.","zh":"這個問題簡短、實用，並自然見於住宿查詢。"},{"en":"It introduces a new topic connected with comfort.","zh":"它引入與舒適度有關的新話題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get quite cool","meaning":"變得頗涼","examples":[{"en":"It sometimes gets quite cool in May.","zh":"五月有時會變得頗涼。"},{"en":"To get quite cool means to become fairly cold.","zh":"get quite cool 指變得相當涼。"},{"en":"The evenings can get quite cool near the hills.","zh":"山邊晚上可能變得頗涼。"},{"en":"Guests may ask about heating if the weather gets cool at night.","zh":"如果晚上天氣變涼，客人可能會詢問暖氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change in temperature.","zh":"這個片語描述溫度變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at that time of year","meaning":"在一年中的那個時候","examples":[{"en":"It can get quite cool at that time of year.","zh":"在一年中的那個時候，天氣可能會變得頗涼。"},{"en":"At that time of year means during that particular season or period.","zh":"at that time of year 指在某個特定季節或時段。"},{"en":"At that time of year, the weather can change quickly.","zh":"在一年中的那個時候，天氣可能變化很快。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing seasonal conditions.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論季節性情況。"},{"en":"It refers to a time already mentioned or understood.","zh":"它指已提及或雙方都明白的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"central heating","meaning":"中央暖氣","examples":[{"en":"The cottage has central heating.","zh":"小屋有中央暖氣。"},{"en":"Central heating is a system that heats the whole building from one main source.","zh":"central heating 指由一個主要來源為整棟建築物供暖的系統。"},{"en":"Central heating keeps rooms warm during cool evenings.","zh":"中央暖氣可以在涼爽晚上保持房間溫暖。"},{"en":"Guests often ask about central heating before booking cottages in colder months.","zh":"客人在較冷月份預訂小屋前，常會詢問中央暖氣。"},{"en":"This phrase names an important home comfort facility.","zh":"這個片語命名一項重要家居舒適設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"light a fire","meaning":"生火","examples":[{"en":"Guests can light a fire in the stove.","zh":"客人可以在火爐裏生火。"},{"en":"To light a fire means to start a fire burning.","zh":"light a fire 指點火並讓火燃燒起來。"},{"en":"They lit a fire in the stove after returning from a walk.","zh":"他們散步回來後在火爐裏生火。"},{"en":"Lighting a fire can make a room warmer and more comfortable.","zh":"生火可以令房間更暖和、更舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when talking about fireplaces and stoves.","zh":"這個片語常用於談論壁爐和火爐。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"provide all the wood","meaning":"提供所有木柴","examples":[{"en":"Shirley can provide all the wood needed for the stove.","zh":"Shirley 可以提供火爐所需的所有木柴。"},{"en":"To provide all the wood means to supply all the firewood required.","zh":"provide all the wood 指供應所需的全部柴枝或木柴。"},{"en":"The cottage owner provides all the wood for guests during winter.","zh":"小屋主人在冬天為客人提供所有木柴。"},{"en":"Providing wood saves guests from having to buy it themselves.","zh":"提供木柴可以省卻客人自行購買的麻煩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an included practical service.","zh":"這個片語描述一項已包括的實用服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"smell so much nicer than","meaning":"聞起來比……好得多","examples":[{"en":"Wood smells so much nicer than coal.","zh":"木柴聞起來比煤好得多。"},{"en":"Smell so much nicer than means have a much more pleasant smell than something else.","zh":"smell so much nicer than 指氣味比另一物舒服得多。"},{"en":"Fresh bread smells so much nicer than packaged snacks.","zh":"新鮮麵包聞起來比包裝零食好得多。"},{"en":"This phrase compares smells in a strong but informal way.","zh":"這個片語以強烈但口語方式比較氣味。"},{"en":"It is often used when describing comfort or atmosphere.","zh":"它常用於描述舒適感或氣氛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make the room cosy","meaning":"令房間很舒適","examples":[{"en":"The stove makes the room very cosy.","zh":"火爐令房間非常舒適。"},{"en":"To make the room cosy means to make it feel warm, comfortable and pleasant.","zh":"make the room cosy 指令房間感覺溫暖、舒服和宜人。"},{"en":"Soft lighting and a fire can make the room cosy.","zh":"柔和燈光和爐火可以令房間很舒適。"},{"en":"A cosy room is especially attractive in cold weather.","zh":"在寒冷天氣中，舒適房間特別吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes atmosphere as well as temperature.","zh":"這個片語同時描述氣氛和溫度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in our own house","meaning":"在我們自己家中","examples":[{"en":"Shirley and Jack have a stove in their own house.","zh":"Shirley 和 Jack 在自己家中也有火爐。"},{"en":"In our own house means in the house where we ourselves live.","zh":"in our own house 指在我們自己居住的房子裏。"},{"en":"We have the same kind of stove in our own house.","zh":"我們自己家中也有同一種火爐。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the comment more personal and trustworthy.","zh":"這個片語令評論更個人化，也更可信。"},{"en":"It contrasts the speaker’s home with the rental cottage.","zh":"它把說話者自己的家與出租小屋作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sound very pleasant","meaning":"聽起來很舒適","examples":[{"en":"Tom thinks the stove sounds very pleasant.","zh":"Tom 覺得那個火爐聽起來很舒適。"},{"en":"To sound very pleasant means to seem nice or enjoyable from the description.","zh":"sound very pleasant 指根據描述聽起來舒服或令人喜歡。"},{"en":"The idea of sitting by the fire sounds very pleasant.","zh":"坐在火邊這個想法聽起來很舒適。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they like what they hear about something.","zh":"人們聽到某事描述並覺得喜歡時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It is polite and positive in conversation.","zh":"它在對話中有禮而正面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make the most of","meaning":"充分利用","examples":[{"en":"Tom jokes that they should come in winter to make the most of the stove.","zh":"Tom 開玩笑說他們應該冬天來，以充分利用火爐。"},{"en":"To make the most of something means to use or enjoy it as fully as possible.","zh":"make the most of something 指盡量充分使用或享受某物。"},{"en":"Guests should make the most of the garden when the weather is sunny.","zh":"天氣晴朗時，客人應充分利用花園。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests taking full advantage of an opportunity or facility.","zh":"這個片語常暗示充分把握機會或設施。"},{"en":"It is common in travel and everyday conversation.","zh":"它常見於旅遊和日常對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"we find","meaning":"我們發現","examples":[{"en":"Shirley says they find they do not want to go out when the fire is burning.","zh":"Shirley 說他們發現火爐燃燒時不想外出。"},{"en":"We find means we have discovered from experience.","zh":"we find 指我們從經驗中發現。"},{"en":"We find that guests often stay indoors when the weather is cold.","zh":"我們發現天氣寒冷時，客人常留在室內。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a statement sound based on personal experience.","zh":"這個片語令說法聽起來基於個人經驗。"},{"en":"It is common when giving friendly advice or observations.","zh":"它常用於給出友善建議或觀察。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the fire burning","meaning":"火爐燃燒着","examples":[{"en":"Shirley does not want to go out when the fire is burning.","zh":"火爐燃燒着時，Shirley 不想外出。"},{"en":"The fire burning means the fire is lit and producing heat and flames.","zh":"the fire burning 指火已點燃，正在產生熱力和火焰。"},{"en":"The room feels cosy with the fire burning in the stove.","zh":"火爐燃燒着時，房間感覺很舒適。"},{"en":"A burning fire can create warmth, light and atmosphere.","zh":"燃燒的火可以營造溫暖、光線和氣氛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an ongoing state.","zh":"這個片語描述正在持續的狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"attractive views","meaning":"迷人的景色","examples":[{"en":"There are some attractive views from the cottage.","zh":"從小屋望出去有一些迷人的景色。"},{"en":"Attractive views are pleasant sights that people enjoy looking at.","zh":"attractive views 指令人喜歡欣賞的美麗景色。"},{"en":"The cottage has attractive views of the hills and old bridge.","zh":"那間小屋可欣賞山丘和古老石橋的迷人景色。"},{"en":"Good views can make accommodation feel more special.","zh":"好景色可以令住宿感覺更特別。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in holiday property descriptions.","zh":"這個片語常見於度假物業描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"from the cottage","meaning":"從小屋望出去","examples":[{"en":"Guests can enjoy attractive views from the cottage.","zh":"客人可以從小屋望出去欣賞迷人的景色。"},{"en":"From the cottage means as seen or experienced while staying at the cottage.","zh":"from the cottage 指從小屋所在位置看到或感受到的。"},{"en":"From the cottage, you can see the hills in the distance.","zh":"從小屋望出去，你可以看到遠處的山丘。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the viewpoint or starting point.","zh":"這個片語描述視角或起點。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing views and nearby places.","zh":"它適合用於討論景色和附近地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"I haven’t mentioned","meaning":"我還未提到","examples":[{"en":"Shirley mentions some attractive views that she has not mentioned before.","zh":"Shirley 提到一些她之前還未提到的迷人景色。"},{"en":"I haven’t mentioned means I have not said this earlier.","zh":"I haven’t mentioned 指我之前還沒有說到這件事。"},{"en":"I haven’t mentioned the garden yet, but it is one of the best features.","zh":"我還未提到花園，但它是最好的特色之一。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces extra information.","zh":"這個片語引入額外資料。"},{"en":"It is natural in conversation when adding a detail.","zh":"當補充細節時，它在對話中很自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a famous stone bridge","meaning":"一條著名的石橋","examples":[{"en":"Guests can see a famous stone bridge from the living room.","zh":"客人可以從客廳看到一條著名的石橋。"},{"en":"A famous stone bridge is a well-known bridge made of stone.","zh":"famous stone bridge 指一條由石頭建成而且廣為人知的橋。"},{"en":"The village is proud of its famous stone bridge.","zh":"那條村以其著名石橋為傲。"},{"en":"A historic bridge can make a view more interesting for visitors.","zh":"歷史悠久的橋可以令景色對遊客更有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a local landmark.","zh":"這個片語描述本地地標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one of the oldest","meaning":"最古老的……之一","examples":[{"en":"The stone bridge is one of the oldest in the region.","zh":"那條石橋是該地區最古老的石橋之一。"},{"en":"One of the oldest means among the oldest examples of something.","zh":"one of the oldest 指某物屬於同類中最古老的一批。"},{"en":"The church is one of the oldest buildings in the village.","zh":"那座教堂是村中最古老的建築之一。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights historical importance.","zh":"這個片語突出歷史重要性。"},{"en":"It is often used when describing landmarks.","zh":"它常用於描述地標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the region","meaning":"在該地區","examples":[{"en":"The bridge is one of the oldest in the region.","zh":"那條橋是該地區最古老的橋之一。"},{"en":"In the region means in that local area or wider district.","zh":"in the region 指在該本地區域或較大地區內。"},{"en":"This cottage is one of the most popular in the region.","zh":"這間小屋是該地區最受歡迎的小屋之一。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing places within an area.","zh":"這個片語適合比較某區內的地方。"},{"en":"It is slightly formal and often appears in travel descriptions.","zh":"它略正式，常見於旅遊描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not far away","meaning":"不遠","examples":[{"en":"The stone bridge is not far away from the cottage.","zh":"那條石橋離小屋不遠。"},{"en":"Not far away means close enough to reach easily.","zh":"not far away 指距離近，容易到達。"},{"en":"The village shop is not far away from the cottage.","zh":"村中商店離小屋不遠。"},{"en":"Guests like nearby attractions because they do not need to travel far.","zh":"客人喜歡附近景點，因為不用走很遠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes convenient distance.","zh":"這個片語描述方便的距離。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"look in the opposite direction","meaning":"朝相反方向望出去","examples":[{"en":"The bedroom window looks in the opposite direction.","zh":"睡房窗戶朝相反方向望出去。"},{"en":"To look in the opposite direction means to face the other way.","zh":"look in the opposite direction 指面向另一邊。"},{"en":"The kitchen window looks towards the garden, but the bedroom window looks in the opposite direction.","zh":"廚房窗戶朝花園望出去，但睡房窗戶朝相反方向。"},{"en":"Windows facing different directions can offer different views.","zh":"面向不同方向的窗戶可以提供不同景色。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing layout and scenery.","zh":"這個片語適合用於描述佈局和景觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a lovely view of","meaning":"……的美麗景色","examples":[{"en":"The bedroom has a lovely view of the hills.","zh":"睡房可欣賞山丘的美麗景色。"},{"en":"A lovely view of something means a beautiful and pleasant sight of it.","zh":"a lovely view of something 指某物的美麗宜人景色。"},{"en":"The cottage has a lovely view of the old bridge.","zh":"那間小屋可欣賞古老石橋的美麗景色。"},{"en":"A good view can make a bedroom feel peaceful and special.","zh":"好景色可以令睡房感覺平靜而特別。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in accommodation descriptions.","zh":"這個片語常見於住宿描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at the top","meaning":"在頂部","examples":[{"en":"The bedroom window has a view of the monument at the top of the hills.","zh":"睡房窗戶可以看到山頂上的紀念碑。"},{"en":"At the top means at the highest part of something.","zh":"at the top 指在某物最高處。"},{"en":"There is a small monument at the top of the hill.","zh":"山頂上有一座小紀念碑。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing landscape features.","zh":"這個片語適合用於描述景觀特色。"},{"en":"It can refer to physical height or a position on a map.","zh":"它可以指實際高度，也可以指地圖上的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"that all sounds perfect","meaning":"一切聽起來都很理想","examples":[{"en":"Tom says that all the details about the cottage sound perfect.","zh":"Tom 說關於小屋的一切細節聽起來都很理想。"},{"en":"That all sounds perfect means everything mentioned seems ideal or exactly right.","zh":"that all sounds perfect 指剛才提及的一切都看似理想或完全合適。"},{"en":"The price, dates and facilities all sound perfect to us.","zh":"價格、日期和設施對我們來說都聽起來很理想。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong satisfaction before making a booking.","zh":"這個片語在預訂前表達強烈滿意。"},{"en":"It is friendly and natural in spoken English.","zh":"它在英語口語中友善自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"book it","meaning":"預訂它","examples":[{"en":"Tom would like to book Chervil Cottage.","zh":"Tom 想預訂 Chervil Cottage。"},{"en":"To book it means to reserve it for a particular date.","zh":"book it 指為特定日期預留某物。"},{"en":"After hearing the details, they decided to book it.","zh":"聽完詳情後，他們決定預訂它。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when confirming travel or accommodation plans.","zh":"這個片語常見於確認旅遊或住宿計劃。"},{"en":"It means the customer wants to make the arrangement official.","zh":"它表示客戶想正式作出安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"would you want a deposit?","meaning":"你需要訂金嗎？","examples":[{"en":"Tom asks whether Shirley wants a deposit.","zh":"Tom 問 Shirley 是否需要訂金。"},{"en":"Would you want a deposit? asks whether an initial payment is required to confirm the booking.","zh":"would you want a deposit? 用來詢問是否需要先付款以確認預訂。"},{"en":"Would you want a deposit now, or can I pay later?","zh":"你現在需要訂金，還是我可以遲些付款？"},{"en":"This question is polite and practical in booking conversations.","zh":"這個問題在預訂對話中有禮而實用。"},{"en":"It helps clarify payment arrangements.","zh":"它有助釐清付款安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ask for thirty percent","meaning":"要求百分之三十","examples":[{"en":"Shirley asks for thirty percent to secure the booking.","zh":"Shirley 要求支付百分之三十，以確保預訂。"},{"en":"To ask for thirty percent means to require payment of 30% of the total price.","zh":"ask for thirty percent 指要求支付總價的 30%。"},{"en":"The hotel asks for thirty percent when guests confirm the room.","zh":"酒店在客人確認房間時要求支付百分之三十。"},{"en":"A percentage deposit reduces the risk of cancellation.","zh":"百分比訂金可以減低取消預訂的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in payment and booking arrangements.","zh":"這個片語常見於付款和預訂安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"secure your booking","meaning":"確保你的預訂","examples":[{"en":"The deposit secures Tom’s booking.","zh":"訂金可以確保 Tom 的預訂。"},{"en":"To secure your booking means to confirm and hold the reservation for you.","zh":"secure your booking 指確認並為你保留預訂。"},{"en":"Paying the deposit will secure your booking for the week.","zh":"支付訂金後，便可確保你那一星期的預訂。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures customers that the accommodation will not be given to someone else.","zh":"這個片語讓客戶安心，知道住宿不會被租給別人。"},{"en":"It is common in travel and rental arrangements.","zh":"它常見於旅遊和租住安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the rest of the money","meaning":"餘款","examples":[{"en":"Tom asks when Shirley would like the rest of the money.","zh":"Tom 問 Shirley 希望何時收取餘款。"},{"en":"The rest of the money means the remaining amount after the deposit has been paid.","zh":"the rest of the money 指支付訂金後剩下的金額。"},{"en":"You can pay the deposit today and the rest of the money next month.","zh":"你今天可以先付訂金，下個月再付餘款。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when a payment is split into stages.","zh":"當付款分階段進行時，這個片語很常見。"},{"en":"It helps clarify the balance still owed.","zh":"它有助釐清尚欠的餘額。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the last day of March","meaning":"三月最後一天","examples":[{"en":"Tom needs to pay the rest of the money by the last day of March.","zh":"Tom 需要在三月最後一天前支付餘款。"},{"en":"The last day of March means 31 March.","zh":"the last day of March 指三月三十一日。"},{"en":"The balance must be paid by the last day of March.","zh":"餘款必須在三月最後一天前支付。"},{"en":"Giving a clear payment deadline helps avoid confusion.","zh":"給出清楚付款期限有助避免混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific deadline by month.","zh":"這個片語用月份標示具體截止日期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take your details","meaning":"記下你的資料","examples":[{"en":"Shirley asks Tom for his details after he decides to book.","zh":"Tom 決定預訂後，Shirley 請他提供資料。"},{"en":"To take your details means to record your personal or booking information.","zh":"take your details 指記下你的個人或預訂資料。"},{"en":"The receptionist took my details before confirming the reservation.","zh":"接待員在確認預訂前記下了我的資料。"},{"en":"Details may include name, address, phone number and payment information.","zh":"資料可能包括姓名、地址、電話號碼和付款資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in bookings and customer service.","zh":"這個片語常見於預訂和客戶服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10}],"ielts/listening/Practice 19/task-2":[{"front":"next on the agenda","meaning":"下一項議程","examples":[{"en":"Next on the agenda, we have traffic and highways.","zh":"下一項議程是交通及道路。"},{"en":"Next on the agenda means the next item or topic to be discussed in a meeting.","zh":"next on the agenda 的意思是會議中下一個要討論的項目或題目。"},{"en":"Next on the agenda is the school library budget.","zh":"下一項議程是學校圖書館預算。"},{"en":"Saying what is next on the agenda helps everyone follow the order of the meeting.","zh":"說明下一項議程有助所有人跟上會議次序。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in meetings.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常見於會議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"traffic and highways","meaning":"交通及道路","examples":[{"en":"The next item on the agenda is traffic and highways.","zh":"下一項議程是交通及道路。"},{"en":"Traffic and highways refers to road use, vehicles, transport flow, and road systems.","zh":"traffic and highways 指道路使用、車輛、交通流量和道路系統。"},{"en":"A council meeting may discuss traffic and highways when residents complain about congestion.","zh":"當居民投訴交通擠塞，議會會議可能討論交通及道路。"},{"en":"Problems with traffic and highways can affect safety, travel time, and local businesses.","zh":"交通及道路問題可以影響安全、出行時間和本地商戶。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in local government discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於地方政府討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Councillor","meaning":"議員","examples":[{"en":"Councillor Thornton presents the survey results.","zh":"Thornton 議員匯報調查結果。"},{"en":"A councillor is an elected local government representative.","zh":"councillor 是經選舉產生的地方政府代表。"},{"en":"A councillor may speak for residents about roads, parks, housing, or local services.","zh":"議員可能代表居民討論道路、公園、房屋或本地服務。"},{"en":"Councillors discuss public issues and help make decisions for the local area.","zh":"議員討論公共議題，並協助為本區作出決定。"},{"en":"This word is common in British local government contexts.","zh":"這個詞常見於英國地方政府語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"results of the survey","meaning":"調查結果","examples":[{"en":"The council now has the results of the survey about traffic.","zh":"議會現在有關於交通的調查結果。"},{"en":"Results of the survey are the findings or answers collected from people who took part.","zh":"results of the survey 是從參與者收集得來的發現或答案。"},{"en":"The results of the survey showed that most students wanted longer library hours.","zh":"調查結果顯示大多數學生希望圖書館開放時間更長。"},{"en":"Survey results help decision-makers understand what people think or experience.","zh":"調查結果幫助決策者理解人們的想法或經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting public opinion or research findings.","zh":"這個短語適合用於報告民意或研究發現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"carried out last month","meaning":"上月進行的","examples":[{"en":"The survey was carried out last month.","zh":"這項調查是上月進行的。"},{"en":"Carried out last month means done or conducted during the previous month.","zh":"carried out last month 的意思是在上一個月完成或進行。"},{"en":"The safety inspection was carried out last month.","zh":"安全檢查是上月進行的。"},{"en":"Recent work carried out last month may still reflect current conditions.","zh":"上月進行的工作可能仍反映目前情況。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the time when an action happened.","zh":"這個短語說明行動發生的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"road transport","meaning":"道路交通","examples":[{"en":"The survey was about traffic and road transport in the town.","zh":"這項調查是關於鎮內交通及道路交通。"},{"en":"Road transport means travel or movement using roads, such as cars, buses, lorries, and bicycles.","zh":"road transport 指使用道路的出行或運輸，例如汽車、巴士、貨車和單車。"},{"en":"Good road transport helps people get to work, school, and shops more easily.","zh":"良好道路交通幫助人們更容易上班、上學和購物。"},{"en":"Poor road transport can cause delays, pollution, and safety problems.","zh":"差劣道路交通可以造成延誤、污染和安全問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on transport that happens on roads.","zh":"這個短語集中於道路上的交通運輸。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"generally satisfied with","meaning":"整體上對……感到滿意","examples":[{"en":"People were generally satisfied with the state of the roads.","zh":"人們整體上對道路狀況感到滿意。"},{"en":"Generally satisfied with something means mostly pleased with it, though not necessarily completely happy.","zh":"generally satisfied with something 的意思是大致滿意，但未必完全滿意。"},{"en":"Parents were generally satisfied with the new school lunch menu.","zh":"家長整體上對新的學校午餐餐單感到滿意。"},{"en":"If people are generally satisfied, only a few problems may still need attention.","zh":"如果人們整體滿意，可能只剩少數問題需要處理。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a broad positive judgement.","zh":"這個短語給出概括正面評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"state of the roads","meaning":"道路狀況","examples":[{"en":"People were generally satisfied with the state of the roads.","zh":"人們整體上對道路狀況感到滿意。"},{"en":"The state of the roads means the condition of road surfaces, signs, markings, and safety.","zh":"state of the roads 指路面、標誌、標線和安全的狀況。"},{"en":"After heavy rain, drivers complained about the poor state of the roads.","zh":"大雨後，司機投訴道路狀況欠佳。"},{"en":"The state of the roads affects travel speed, vehicle damage, and pedestrian safety.","zh":"道路狀況影響行車速度、車輛損耗和行人安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing local transport conditions.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論本地交通情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one or two complaints about","meaning":"一兩宗關於……的投訴","examples":[{"en":"There were one or two complaints about potholes.","zh":"有一兩宗關於路面坑洞的投訴。"},{"en":"One or two complaints about something means a small number of people complained about it.","zh":"one or two complaints about something 的意思是有少數人投訴某事。"},{"en":"There were one or two complaints about the noise after the school concert.","zh":"學校音樂會後有一兩宗關於噪音的投訴。"},{"en":"A few complaints may show a minor problem that still needs checking.","zh":"少量投訴可能顯示有小問題仍需檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the issue is not widespread.","zh":"這個短語暗示問題並不普遍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"potholes","meaning":"路面坑洞","examples":[{"en":"There were complaints about potholes in the roads.","zh":"有人投訴道路上的路面坑洞。"},{"en":"Potholes are holes or broken areas in a road surface.","zh":"potholes 是路面上的洞或破損位置。"},{"en":"Cars can be damaged if they hit deep potholes at speed.","zh":"如果汽車高速撞上深坑洞，可能會受損。"},{"en":"Potholes may form after heavy rain, freezing weather, or poor road maintenance.","zh":"路面坑洞可能在大雨、結冰天氣或道路維修不足後形成。"},{"en":"This word is common in discussions about road safety and repairs.","zh":"這個詞常見於道路安全和維修討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be addressed","meaning":"會被處理","examples":[{"en":"The complaints about potholes will be addressed.","zh":"關於路面坑洞的投訴會被處理。"},{"en":"To be addressed means to be dealt with or given attention.","zh":"be addressed 的意思是會被處理或得到關注。"},{"en":"The teacher said the students’ concerns would be addressed in the next meeting.","zh":"老師說學生的憂慮會在下次會議中被處理。"},{"en":"Problems are less likely to grow if they are addressed early.","zh":"如果問題及早被處理，就較不容易惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in official responses.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於官方回應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a significant number of","meaning":"相當多的……","examples":[{"en":"A significant number of people complained about heavy vehicles.","zh":"相當多的人投訴重型車輛。"},{"en":"A significant number of means quite a large or important number.","zh":"a significant number of 的意思是數量相當多或相當重要。"},{"en":"A significant number of parents asked for safer crossings near the school.","zh":"相當多的家長要求學校附近設置更安全的過路處。"},{"en":"When a significant number of people complain, officials usually need to investigate.","zh":"當相當多人投訴，官員通常需要調查。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the number is too important to ignore.","zh":"這個短語表示數量重要到不能忽視。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"heavy vehicles","meaning":"重型車輛","examples":[{"en":"Many people complained about heavy vehicles using local roads.","zh":"許多人投訴重型車輛使用本地道路。"},{"en":"Heavy vehicles are large vehicles such as lorries, trucks, and buses.","zh":"heavy vehicles 是大型車輛，例如貨車、卡車和巴士。"},{"en":"Heavy vehicles can damage small roads if the roads are not designed for them.","zh":"如果小路不是為重型車輛而設，路面可能被損壞。"},{"en":"Too many heavy vehicles may create noise, traffic danger, and air pollution.","zh":"太多重型車輛可能造成噪音、交通危險和空氣污染。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in transport and planning discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於交通和規劃討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"local roads","meaning":"本地道路","examples":[{"en":"Heavy vehicles are using local roads to avoid traffic elsewhere.","zh":"重型車輛正在使用本地道路，以避開其他地方的交通。"},{"en":"Local roads are roads used mainly by people in the nearby area.","zh":"local roads 是主要由附近地區居民使用的道路。"},{"en":"Local roads near schools should be safe for children and residents.","zh":"學校附近的本地道路應對兒童和居民安全。"},{"en":"When heavy traffic moves onto local roads, neighbourhoods can become noisier and less safe.","zh":"當繁忙交通轉到本地道路，社區可能變得更嘈雜和不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts smaller community roads with main roads or highways.","zh":"這個短語把較小社區道路與主要道路或公路作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"avoid traffic elsewhere","meaning":"避開其他地方的交通","examples":[{"en":"Heavy vehicles use local roads to avoid traffic elsewhere.","zh":"重型車輛使用本地道路，以避開其他地方的交通。"},{"en":"To avoid traffic elsewhere means to use another route so that you do not meet congestion in another place.","zh":"avoid traffic elsewhere 的意思是使用另一條路線，以免遇到其他地方的交通擠塞。"},{"en":"Drivers may go through side streets to avoid traffic elsewhere in the city.","zh":"司機可能穿過小街，以避開城市其他地方的交通。"},{"en":"Avoiding traffic can save drivers time, but it may create problems for local residents.","zh":"避開交通可以為司機節省時間，但可能為本地居民製造問題。"},{"en":"This phrase connects route choice with congestion.","zh":"這個短語把路線選擇與交通擠塞連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"we had expected","meaning":"我們原本預期","examples":[{"en":"The council had expected more complaints about the train service.","zh":"議會原本預期會有更多關於火車服務的投訴。"},{"en":"We had expected means we thought something would happen before we saw the actual result.","zh":"we had expected 的意思是我們在看到實際結果前，原本以為某事會發生。"},{"en":"We had expected more students to join the trip, but only ten signed up.","zh":"我們原本預期會有更多學生參加旅行，但只有十人報名。"},{"en":"This phrase compares an earlier prediction with what really happened.","zh":"這個短語把早前預測與實際情況作比較。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing surprising results.","zh":"它適合用於討論令人意外的結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"complaints by commuters","meaning":"通勤人士的投訴","examples":[{"en":"The council expected more complaints by commuters.","zh":"議會原本預期會有更多通勤人士的投訴。"},{"en":"Complaints by commuters are complaints made by people who travel regularly between home and work or school.","zh":"complaints by commuters 是由經常往返住所與工作地點或學校的人提出的投訴。"},{"en":"Complaints by commuters may focus on late trains, crowded buses, or high fares.","zh":"通勤人士的投訴可能集中於火車遲到、巴士擠迫或車費高。"},{"en":"Commuter complaints can reveal transport problems that happen every day.","zh":"通勤人士的投訴可以揭示每天發生的交通問題。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who made the complaints.","zh":"這個短語指出投訴由誰提出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"commuters","meaning":"通勤人士","examples":[{"en":"Commuters may be affected by changes to train services.","zh":"通勤人士可能受火車服務改變影響。"},{"en":"Commuters are people who travel regularly between home and work or school.","zh":"commuters 是經常往返住所與工作地點或學校的人。"},{"en":"Many commuters rely on buses and trains every morning.","zh":"許多通勤人士每天早上依靠巴士和火車。"},{"en":"If transport is delayed, commuters may arrive late and feel stressed.","zh":"如果交通延誤，通勤人士可能遲到並感到壓力。"},{"en":"This word is common in transport discussions.","zh":"這個詞常見於交通討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reduction in the train service","meaning":"火車服務減少","examples":[{"en":"There were fewer complaints than expected about the reduction in the train service.","zh":"關於火車服務減少的投訴比預期少。"},{"en":"A reduction in the train service means fewer trains, shorter operating hours, or less frequent service.","zh":"reduction in the train service 的意思是火車班次較少、營運時間較短或服務不那麼頻密。"},{"en":"A reduction in train service can make commuting harder for people without cars.","zh":"火車服務減少可以令沒有汽車的人通勤更困難。"},{"en":"When train services are reduced, passengers may need to change routes or travel earlier.","zh":"當火車服務減少，乘客可能需要改變路線或更早出門。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decrease in public transport provision.","zh":"這個短語描述公共交通服務下降。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"affect people too much","meaning":"對人影響太大","examples":[{"en":"The reduction in train service does not seem to have affected people too much.","zh":"火車服務減少似乎沒有對人影響太大。"},{"en":"To affect people too much means to cause a large or serious impact on their lives.","zh":"affect people too much 的意思是對人們生活造成很大或嚴重影響。"},{"en":"The timetable change did not affect students too much because most classes started later.","zh":"時間表改動沒有對學生影響太大，因為大部分課堂較遲開始。"},{"en":"If a change affects people too much, they are more likely to complain.","zh":"如果改變對人影響太大，他們更可能投訴。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when judging the seriousness of an impact.","zh":"這個短語常用於判斷影響的嚴重程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cycle path","meaning":"單車徑","examples":[{"en":"The cycle path runs alongside the river.","zh":"單車徑沿着河流延伸。"},{"en":"A cycle path is a route designed for people riding bicycles.","zh":"cycle path 是為踩單車人士設計的路線。"},{"en":"A safe cycle path helps cyclists travel without mixing too much with cars.","zh":"安全單車徑幫助單車人士出行，而不用太多與汽車混在一起。"},{"en":"Cycle paths can encourage people to ride bikes instead of driving short distances.","zh":"單車徑可以鼓勵人們踩單車，而不是短途駕車。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in transport planning.","zh":"這個短語常見於交通規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"run alongside","meaning":"沿着……延伸","examples":[{"en":"The cycle path runs alongside the river.","zh":"單車徑沿着河流延伸。"},{"en":"To run alongside something means to follow the same direction next to it.","zh":"run alongside something 的意思是在某物旁邊沿同一方向延伸。"},{"en":"A footpath runs alongside the beach for several kilometres.","zh":"一條行人徑沿着海灘延伸數公里。"},{"en":"Routes that run alongside rivers can be scenic and easy to follow.","zh":"沿河延伸的路線可以風景優美，而且容易跟隨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the position and direction of a path or road.","zh":"這個短語描述路徑或道路的位置和方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cyclists and pedestrians","meaning":"單車人士及行人","examples":[{"en":"The path is used by both cyclists and pedestrians.","zh":"這條路徑由單車人士及行人共同使用。"},{"en":"Cyclists and pedestrians are people riding bicycles and people walking.","zh":"cyclists and pedestrians 是踩單車的人和步行的人。"},{"en":"Shared paths must be safe for both cyclists and pedestrians.","zh":"共用路徑必須對單車人士及行人都安全。"},{"en":"If cyclists move too fast, pedestrians may feel unsafe.","zh":"如果單車人士行得太快，行人可能感到不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two common groups using public paths.","zh":"這個短語描述使用公共路徑的兩個常見群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"very well used","meaning":"使用率很高","examples":[{"en":"The cycle path is very well used by cyclists and pedestrians.","zh":"這條單車徑在單車人士及行人之間使用率很高。"},{"en":"Very well used means used often by many people.","zh":"very well used 的意思是被許多人經常使用。"},{"en":"The school library is very well used during exam season.","zh":"學校圖書館在考試季使用率很高。"},{"en":"When a facility is well used, it usually shows that people find it useful.","zh":"當設施使用率高，通常顯示人們覺得它有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes high usage.","zh":"這個短語描述高使用量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the surface was improved","meaning":"路面獲改善","examples":[{"en":"The path has been popular since the surface was improved.","zh":"自路面獲改善後，這條路徑一直很受歡迎。"},{"en":"The surface was improved means the top layer of the path or road was made better.","zh":"the surface was improved 的意思是路徑或道路的表層變得更好。"},{"en":"The playground became safer after the surface was improved.","zh":"遊樂場地面獲改善後變得更安全。"},{"en":"Improving a surface can reduce accidents and make walking or cycling more comfortable.","zh":"改善路面可以減少意外，並令步行或踩單車更舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on physical repair or upgrading.","zh":"這個短語集中於實際維修或升級。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"overtaking","meaning":"超車","examples":[{"en":"Overtaking can be a problem on the cycle path.","zh":"在單車徑上，超車可能是一個問題。"},{"en":"Overtaking means moving past a slower person or vehicle going in the same direction.","zh":"overtaking 是從同一方向行進、較慢的人或車旁邊越過。"},{"en":"A fast cyclist may overtake a slower cyclist on a shared path.","zh":"快速單車人士可能在共用路徑上超越較慢單車人士。"},{"en":"Overtaking can be dangerous if the path is too narrow.","zh":"如果路徑太窄，超車可能危險。"},{"en":"This word is common in road and cycling safety.","zh":"這個詞常見於道路和單車安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"add a bit on the side","meaning":"在旁邊加闊一點","examples":[{"en":"The council will add a bit on the side to make the path wider.","zh":"議會會在旁邊加闊一點，令路徑更闊。"},{"en":"To add a bit on the side means to increase the width by adding a small extra section along one edge.","zh":"add a bit on the side 的意思是在一邊加一小段額外空間來增加闊度。"},{"en":"The school added a bit on the side of the playground to create more space for children.","zh":"學校在遊樂場旁邊加闊一點，為孩子創造更多空間。"},{"en":"Adding space at the side can make a narrow route safer and more comfortable.","zh":"在旁邊增加空間可以令狹窄路線更安全和舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and practical.","zh":"這個短語是非正式而實用的說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make it wider","meaning":"令它更闊","examples":[{"en":"The council will make the cycle path wider.","zh":"議會會令單車徑更闊。"},{"en":"To make it wider means to increase its width.","zh":"make it wider 的意思是增加它的寬度。"},{"en":"The school made the doorway wider so wheelchair users could enter more easily.","zh":"學校把門口加闊，讓輪椅使用者更容易進入。"},{"en":"Wider paths can reduce accidents because people have more room to pass one another.","zh":"較闊路徑可以減少意外，因為人們有更多空間互相經過。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical change in size.","zh":"這個短語描述物理尺寸上的改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at some stage","meaning":"在某個階段","examples":[{"en":"At some stage, the council would like to extend the path.","zh":"在某個階段，議會希望延長路徑。"},{"en":"At some stage means at an unspecified time in the future or in a process.","zh":"at some stage 的意思是在未來或某過程中一個未指定的時間。"},{"en":"At some stage, the school hopes to build a new sports hall.","zh":"在某個階段，學校希望興建新的體育館。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an intention without giving a fixed date.","zh":"這個短語顯示意向，但沒有給出固定日期。"},{"en":"It is useful when plans are not immediate.","zh":"當計劃不是即時進行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"extend the path","meaning":"延長路徑","examples":[{"en":"The council would like to extend the path through the town.","zh":"議會希望把路徑延長至貫穿全鎮。"},{"en":"To extend the path means to make the path longer.","zh":"extend the path 的意思是令路徑更長。"},{"en":"The park plans to extend the walking path to reach the lake.","zh":"公園計劃延長步行徑，使它到達湖邊。"},{"en":"Extending a path can connect more places and make travel easier.","zh":"延長路徑可以連接更多地方，令出行更方便。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lengthening a route.","zh":"這個短語描述加長路線。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"go all the way through","meaning":"一直貫穿","examples":[{"en":"The path may one day go all the way through the town.","zh":"這條路徑將來可能一直貫穿全鎮。"},{"en":"To go all the way through a place means to continue from one side or end to the other.","zh":"go all the way through a place 的意思是從某地一邊或一端一直延伸到另一邊或另一端。"},{"en":"The bus route goes all the way through the city centre.","zh":"這條巴士線一直貫穿市中心。"},{"en":"A path that goes through the whole town can be useful for commuters and visitors.","zh":"貫穿整個城鎮的路徑對通勤人士和訪客都有用。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises full coverage from start to finish.","zh":"這個短語強調從頭到尾完整覆蓋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the immediate future","meaning":"在短期內","examples":[{"en":"The extension will not happen in the immediate future.","zh":"延長工程不會在短期內發生。"},{"en":"In the immediate future means very soon or in the near future.","zh":"in the immediate future 的意思是很快或近期。"},{"en":"The school wants a new library, but it will not happen in the immediate future.","zh":"學校想要新圖書館，但短期內不會實現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a plan exists but will not happen soon.","zh":"當計劃存在但不會很快發生，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It helps manage expectations.","zh":"它有助管理期望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pedestrian crossing","meaning":"行人過路處","examples":[{"en":"The council planned to build a pedestrian crossing next to the Post Office.","zh":"議會原計劃在郵局旁邊興建行人過路處。"},{"en":"A pedestrian crossing is a marked place where people can cross a road safely.","zh":"pedestrian crossing 是標示出來讓人安全橫過馬路的地方。"},{"en":"A pedestrian crossing near a school helps children cross busy roads.","zh":"學校附近的行人過路處幫助兒童橫過繁忙道路。"},{"en":"Crossings improve safety when they are placed where drivers can see people clearly.","zh":"過路處設在司機能清楚看見行人的地方，才能提升安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in road safety planning.","zh":"這個短語常見於道路安全規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"next to","meaning":"在……旁邊","examples":[{"en":"The pedestrian crossing was planned next to the Post Office.","zh":"行人過路處原計劃在郵局旁邊。"},{"en":"Next to means beside or very close to something.","zh":"next to 的意思是在某物旁邊或非常接近某物。"},{"en":"The bus stop is next to the library.","zh":"巴士站在圖書館旁邊。"},{"en":"Placing a crossing next to a busy building can help pedestrians reach it safely.","zh":"把過路處設在繁忙建築旁邊，可以幫助行人安全到達。"},{"en":"This phrase describes close physical position.","zh":"這個短語描述接近的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be put on hold","meaning":"被暫時擱置","examples":[{"en":"The plans for the pedestrian crossing have been put on hold.","zh":"行人過路處計劃已被暫時擱置。"},{"en":"To be put on hold means to be delayed or paused for the moment.","zh":"be put on hold 的意思是目前被延遲或暫停。"},{"en":"The school trip was put on hold because of bad weather.","zh":"學校旅行因天氣惡劣而被暫時擱置。"},{"en":"Plans are often put on hold when more information is needed.","zh":"當需要更多資訊時，計劃常會被暫時擱置。"},{"en":"This phrase does not always mean cancellation.","zh":"這個短語不一定表示取消。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"for the time being","meaning":"暫時","examples":[{"en":"The pedestrian crossing has been put on hold for the time being.","zh":"行人過路處暫時被擱置。"},{"en":"For the time being means temporarily or for now.","zh":"for the time being 的意思是暫時或目前。"},{"en":"For the time being, students will use the old classroom.","zh":"暫時，學生會使用舊課室。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the situation may change later.","zh":"這個短語暗示情況之後可能改變。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining temporary arrangements.","zh":"它適合用於解釋臨時安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"budget for","meaning":"為……編列預算","examples":[{"en":"The council had budgeted for the crossing this financial year.","zh":"議會已在本財政年度為過路處編列預算。"},{"en":"To budget for something means to plan and set aside money for it.","zh":"budget for something 的意思是計劃並預留金錢給某事。"},{"en":"A school may budget for new computers next year.","zh":"學校可能為明年的新電腦編列預算。"},{"en":"Budgeting for a project does not mean it will definitely happen immediately.","zh":"為項目編列預算不代表它一定會立即進行。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in finance and planning.","zh":"這個短語常見於財務和規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"this financial year","meaning":"本財政年度","examples":[{"en":"The crossing was budgeted for this financial year.","zh":"這個過路處已在本財政年度編列預算。"},{"en":"This financial year means the current twelve-month accounting period used by an organisation.","zh":"this financial year 指機構目前使用的十二個月會計年度。"},{"en":"The council plans to repair three parks this financial year.","zh":"議會計劃在本財政年度維修三個公園。"},{"en":"Projects planned for this financial year must fit within that year’s budget.","zh":"計劃在本財政年度進行的項目必須符合該年度預算。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in official and financial discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於官方和財務討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rumours that","meaning":"關於……的傳聞","examples":[{"en":"There were rumours that the Post Office was going to move.","zh":"有關於郵局將會搬遷的傳聞。"},{"en":"Rumours that something will happen are unofficial stories or claims that may not be true.","zh":"rumours that something will happen 是未經官方確認、可能不真實的說法或消息。"},{"en":"There were rumours that the shop would close, but the owner denied them.","zh":"有傳聞說那間店會結業，但店主否認了。"},{"en":"Rumours can affect planning if officials do not know whether they are true.","zh":"如果官員不知道傳聞是否屬實，傳聞可能影響規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces unconfirmed information.","zh":"這個短語引出未經確認的資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"would have meant","meaning":"本來會意味著","examples":[{"en":"The Post Office moving would have meant there was no need for a crossing.","zh":"郵局搬遷本來會意味著沒有設置過路處的需要。"},{"en":"Would have meant is used to explain what a past or possible situation would have caused.","zh":"would have meant 用來解釋過去或可能情況本來會造成甚麼結果。"},{"en":"If the class had been cancelled, it would have meant students had more time to revise.","zh":"如果課堂取消，本來會意味著學生有更多時間溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing consequences that did not fully happen.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論未完全發生的後果。"},{"en":"It connects an imagined condition with an imagined result.","zh":"它把想像條件與想像結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"no need for","meaning":"沒有……的需要","examples":[{"en":"If the Post Office moved, there would be no need for a crossing.","zh":"如果郵局搬遷，就沒有設置過路處的需要。"},{"en":"No need for something means it is not necessary.","zh":"no need for something 的意思是某事不是必要的。"},{"en":"If everyone brings lunch, there is no need for a restaurant booking.","zh":"如果每個人都帶午餐，就沒有預訂餐廳的需要。"},{"en":"Plans can change when there is no longer a need for the original facility.","zh":"當原本設施不再有需要，計劃可以改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes absence of necessity.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有必要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"confirm that","meaning":"確認","examples":[{"en":"The Post Office has confirmed that it is staying where it is.","zh":"郵局已確認會留在原址。"},{"en":"To confirm that something is true means to state it clearly and officially.","zh":"confirm that something is true 的意思是清楚而正式地說明某事屬實。"},{"en":"The school confirmed that the exam would take place on Monday.","zh":"學校確認考試會在星期一舉行。"},{"en":"Confirmation helps stop rumours and allows people to plan properly.","zh":"確認資訊有助停止傳聞，並讓人們妥善規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in official announcements.","zh":"這個短語常見於官方公告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stay where they are","meaning":"留在原址","examples":[{"en":"The Post Office has confirmed that it is staying where it is.","zh":"郵局已確認會留在原址。"},{"en":"To stay where they are means to remain in the same location and not move.","zh":"stay where they are 的意思是留在同一地點，不搬遷。"},{"en":"The library will stay where it is because residents find the location convenient.","zh":"圖書館會留在原址，因為居民覺得位置方便。"},{"en":"If an important service stays in the same place, nearby facilities may still be needed.","zh":"如果重要服務留在同一地方，附近設施可能仍然需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes remaining in the current position.","zh":"這個短語描述保持現時位置不變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Highways Department","meaning":"道路部門","examples":[{"en":"The Highways Department warned that the planned crossing would be dangerous.","zh":"道路部門警告，計劃中的過路處會有危險。"},{"en":"The Highways Department is a government department responsible for roads and related safety matters.","zh":"Highways Department 是負責道路及相關安全事務的政府部門。"},{"en":"The Highways Department may inspect junctions before approving road changes.","zh":"道路部門可能在批准道路改動前檢查路口。"},{"en":"Its advice matters because road design affects drivers and pedestrians.","zh":"其建議重要，因為道路設計影響司機和行人。"},{"en":"This phrase names an official road authority.","zh":"這個短語指官方道路機構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"originally planned","meaning":"原本計劃的","examples":[{"en":"The crossing would be dangerous where it was originally planned.","zh":"過路處在原本計劃的位置會有危險。"},{"en":"Originally planned means planned at first, before changes or new information appeared.","zh":"originally planned 的意思是一開始計劃的，在改動或新資訊出現之前。"},{"en":"The picnic was originally planned for Saturday, but it moved to Sunday because of rain.","zh":"野餐原本計劃在星期六舉行，但因下雨改到星期日。"},{"en":"Original plans may need revision when safety problems are found.","zh":"當發現安全問題，原本計劃可能需要修改。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the first plan with later changes.","zh":"這個短語把最初計劃與後來改動作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bend in the road","meaning":"道路彎位","examples":[{"en":"There is a bend in the road near the planned crossing.","zh":"計劃中的過路處附近有道路彎位。"},{"en":"A bend in the road is a curve or turn in the road.","zh":"bend in the road 是道路中的彎曲或轉彎位置。"},{"en":"Drivers should slow down when approaching a sharp bend in the road.","zh":"司機接近急彎時應減速。"},{"en":"Crossings near bends can be dangerous because drivers may not see pedestrians early enough.","zh":"在彎位附近設過路處可能危險，因為司機可能不夠早看見行人。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in road safety.","zh":"這個短語在道路安全中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"need some more thought","meaning":"需要進一步考慮","examples":[{"en":"The pedestrian crossing will need some more thought.","zh":"行人過路處需要進一步考慮。"},{"en":"To need some more thought means to require further consideration before a decision is made.","zh":"need some more thought 的意思是在作決定前需要更多考慮。"},{"en":"The school timetable needs some more thought because several classes overlap.","zh":"學校時間表需要進一步考慮，因為幾堂課重疊。"},{"en":"More thought is needed when a plan may create safety problems.","zh":"當計劃可能造成安全問題，就需要更多考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase politely suggests that the plan is not ready yet.","zh":"這個短語禮貌地表示計劃尚未準備好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Station Road","meaning":"Station Road","examples":[{"en":"Drivers can face long waits on Station Road near the station.","zh":"司機在車站附近的 Station Road 可能面對長時間等候。"},{"en":"Station Road is the name of a road, usually one near a railway station.","zh":"Station Road 是道路名稱，通常指靠近火車站的道路。"},{"en":"Many towns have a Station Road because it leads towards the station.","zh":"許多城鎮都有 Station Road，因為它通往車站。"},{"en":"Named roads help people locate traffic problems more clearly.","zh":"有名稱的道路幫助人更清楚定位交通問題。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific local road.","zh":"這個短語指出特定本地道路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"level crossing","meaning":"平交道","examples":[{"en":"Drivers may wait when the level crossing is closed.","zh":"當平交道關閉時，司機可能要等候。"},{"en":"A level crossing is a place where a road crosses a railway line at the same level.","zh":"level crossing 是道路與鐵路線在同一高度交叉的地方。"},{"en":"Cars must stop at a level crossing when a train is passing.","zh":"火車經過時，汽車必須在平交道停下。"},{"en":"Level crossings can cause delays because barriers may stay down for several minutes.","zh":"平交道可能造成延誤，因為欄杆可能降下數分鐘。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in road and railway safety.","zh":"這個短語常見於道路和鐵路安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"face quite long waits","meaning":"面對頗長時間的等候","examples":[{"en":"Drivers can face quite long waits if the level crossing is closed.","zh":"如果平交道關閉，司機可能面對頗長時間的等候。"},{"en":"To face quite long waits means to have to wait for a fairly long time.","zh":"face quite long waits 的意思是必須等候相當長時間。"},{"en":"Patients may face quite long waits at a busy clinic.","zh":"病人在繁忙診所可能面對頗長時間的等候。"},{"en":"Long waits can cause frustration and encourage people to look for other routes.","zh":"長時間等候可以令人沮喪，並鼓勵人尋找其他路線。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an inconvenient delay.","zh":"這個短語描述不便的延誤。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get signs up","meaning":"豎立標誌","examples":[{"en":"The council has got signs up near the level crossing.","zh":"議會已在平交道附近豎立標誌。"},{"en":"To get signs up means to put signs in place so people can see instructions or warnings.","zh":"get signs up 的意思是設置標誌，讓人們看見指示或警告。"},{"en":"The school got signs up to remind drivers to slow down.","zh":"學校豎立標誌，提醒司機減速。"},{"en":"Clear signs can change behaviour because people know what is expected.","zh":"清晰標誌可以改變行為，因為人們知道應該怎樣做。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and practical.","zh":"這個短語是非正式而實用的說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"request someone not to","meaning":"要求某人不要……","examples":[{"en":"The signs request drivers not to leave their engines running.","zh":"標誌要求司機不要讓引擎繼續運轉。"},{"en":"To request someone not to do something means to politely ask them to avoid doing it.","zh":"request someone not to do something 的意思是禮貌地要求某人避免做某事。"},{"en":"The library notices request visitors not to use phones inside.","zh":"圖書館告示要求訪客不要在內使用電話。"},{"en":"Requests are often used when authorities want cooperation rather than punishment.","zh":"當當局希望人們合作而不是懲罰時，常會使用要求。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds more formal and polite than “tell someone not to”.","zh":"這個短語比 tell someone not to 更正式和禮貌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"leave their engines running","meaning":"讓引擎繼續運轉","examples":[{"en":"Drivers should not leave their engines running while waiting.","zh":"司機等候時不應讓引擎繼續運轉。"},{"en":"To leave engines running means to keep vehicle engines on while the vehicle is not moving.","zh":"leave engines running 的意思是在車輛沒有移動時仍讓引擎開着。"},{"en":"Drivers outside schools should not leave their engines running because children breathe the fumes.","zh":"學校外的司機不應讓引擎繼續運轉，因為兒童會吸入廢氣。"},{"en":"Leaving engines running wastes fuel and increases air pollution.","zh":"讓引擎繼續運轉會浪費燃油並增加空氣污染。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in environmental and traffic notices.","zh":"這個短語常用於環保和交通告示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at that time","meaning":"在那段時間","examples":[{"en":"Drivers should not leave their engines running at that time.","zh":"司機在那段時間不應讓引擎繼續運轉。"},{"en":"At that time means during that particular moment or period.","zh":"at that time 的意思是在那個特定時刻或時段。"},{"en":"The shop was closed at that time, so we came back later.","zh":"那段時間商店關門了，所以我們之後再回來。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect an action with a specific situation.","zh":"這個短語幫助把行動與特定情況連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining timing.","zh":"它適合用於解釋時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pedestrians waiting on the pavement","meaning":"在行人路等候的行人","examples":[{"en":"Pedestrians waiting on the pavement should not have to breathe in fumes.","zh":"在行人路等候的行人不應被迫吸入廢氣。"},{"en":"Pedestrians waiting on the pavement are people standing on the footpath beside the road.","zh":"pedestrians waiting on the pavement 是站在道路旁行人路上的人。"},{"en":"Pedestrians waiting on the pavement may include children, older people, and commuters.","zh":"在行人路等候的行人可能包括兒童、長者和通勤人士。"},{"en":"People waiting beside roads are affected by traffic fumes if engines keep running.","zh":"如果引擎持續運轉，在路邊等候的人會受汽車廢氣影響。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a group exposed to road conditions.","zh":"這個短語指出暴露於道路情況中的一群人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pavement","meaning":"行人路","examples":[{"en":"Pedestrians wait on the pavement to cross the railway line.","zh":"行人在行人路上等候橫過鐵路線。"},{"en":"A pavement is the raised path beside a road where people walk.","zh":"pavement 是道路旁供人行走的高起步道。"},{"en":"Children should stay on the pavement until it is safe to cross.","zh":"兒童應留在行人路上，直到可以安全橫過馬路。"},{"en":"Clear pavements protect pedestrians by keeping them away from moving vehicles.","zh":"清晰行人路透過讓人遠離行駛車輛來保護行人。"},{"en":"This word is British English; American English often uses “sidewalk”.","zh":"這個詞是英式英文；美式英文常用 sidewalk。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cross the railway line","meaning":"橫過鐵路線","examples":[{"en":"Pedestrians wait on the pavement to cross the railway line.","zh":"行人在行人路上等候橫過鐵路線。"},{"en":"To cross the railway line means to go from one side of the railway tracks to the other.","zh":"cross the railway line 的意思是從鐵路軌道一邊走到另一邊。"},{"en":"People should cross the railway line only at a safe crossing.","zh":"人們只應在安全過路處橫過鐵路線。"},{"en":"Crossing railway lines can be dangerous if barriers or warning lights are ignored.","zh":"如果忽視欄杆或警示燈，橫過鐵路線可能很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement across train tracks.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越火車軌道的移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"breathe in","meaning":"吸入","examples":[{"en":"Pedestrians do not have to breathe in car fumes.","zh":"行人不必吸入汽車廢氣。"},{"en":"To breathe in something means to take air, gas, smoke, or smell into the lungs.","zh":"breathe in something 的意思是把空氣、氣體、煙或氣味吸入肺部。"},{"en":"People should avoid breathing in smoke during a fire.","zh":"火災期間，人們應避免吸入煙霧。"},{"en":"Breathing in polluted air can affect the lungs and throat.","zh":"吸入污染空氣可以影響肺部和喉嚨。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on inhaling air or substances.","zh":"這個短語集中於吸入空氣或物質。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"car fumes","meaning":"汽車廢氣","examples":[{"en":"Pedestrians should not have to breathe in car fumes.","zh":"行人不應被迫吸入汽車廢氣。"},{"en":"Car fumes are gases and smoke produced by car engines.","zh":"car fumes 是汽車引擎產生的氣體和煙霧。"},{"en":"Car fumes can be unpleasant and harmful, especially near busy roads.","zh":"汽車廢氣可能令人不適並有害，尤其在繁忙道路附近。"},{"en":"Reducing car fumes can improve air quality for pedestrians and cyclists.","zh":"減少汽車廢氣可以改善行人和單車人士的空氣質素。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in pollution and traffic discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於污染和交通討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have problems with","meaning":"在……方面遇到問題","examples":[{"en":"The council has had problems with cyclists leaving bikes outside the station.","zh":"議會在單車人士把單車留在車站外面方面遇到問題。"},{"en":"To have problems with something means to experience difficulties related to it.","zh":"have problems with something 的意思是遇到與某事有關的困難。"},{"en":"The school has had problems with cars parking near the gate.","zh":"學校在汽車停泊在校門附近方面遇到問題。"},{"en":"Problems with public spaces often need clear rules and better facilities.","zh":"公共空間問題通常需要清晰規則和更好設施。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a difficulty that needs attention.","zh":"這個短語引出需要關注的困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"leave bikes chained to","meaning":"把單車鎖在……","examples":[{"en":"Cyclists have left their bikes chained to the railings.","zh":"單車人士把單車鎖在欄杆上。"},{"en":"To leave bikes chained to something means to lock bicycles to that object and leave them there.","zh":"leave bikes chained to something 的意思是把單車鎖在某物上並留在那裡。"},{"en":"Students sometimes leave bikes chained to fences when there are no bike racks.","zh":"沒有單車架時，學生有時會把單車鎖在圍欄上。"},{"en":"Bikes chained to railings can block pedestrians and make entrances look messy.","zh":"鎖在欄杆上的單車可以阻塞行人，並令入口看起來凌亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a parking and access problem.","zh":"這個短語描述泊單車和通道問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"railings","meaning":"欄杆","examples":[{"en":"Cyclists chained their bikes to the railings outside the ticket office.","zh":"單車人士把單車鎖在售票處外面的欄杆上。"},{"en":"Railings are metal bars used as a fence or barrier.","zh":"railings 是用作圍欄或屏障的金屬欄。"},{"en":"Railings near steps can help people walk safely.","zh":"樓梯附近的欄杆可以幫助人安全行走。"},{"en":"If bikes are chained to railings, they may block space meant for pedestrians.","zh":"如果單車鎖在欄杆上，可能阻塞原本供行人使用的空間。"},{"en":"This word describes a common public safety structure.","zh":"這個詞描述常見公共安全設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ticket office","meaning":"售票處","examples":[{"en":"Cyclists left their bikes outside the ticket office.","zh":"單車人士把單車留在售票處外面。"},{"en":"A ticket office is a place where people buy tickets or ask about travel information.","zh":"ticket office 是人們購買車票或詢問旅遊資料的地方。"},{"en":"Passengers may queue at the ticket office before taking a train.","zh":"乘客乘火車前可能在售票處排隊。"},{"en":"Blocking the area outside a ticket office can inconvenience many travellers.","zh":"阻塞售票處外的區域會為許多旅客帶來不便。"},{"en":"This phrase names a service point in a station or venue.","zh":"這個短語指車站或場地中的服務點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"bike racks","meaning":"單車架","examples":[{"en":"The station has agreed to provide bike racks.","zh":"車站已同意提供單車架。"},{"en":"Bike racks are structures where cyclists can park and lock their bicycles.","zh":"bike racks 是讓單車人士停放並鎖好單車的設施。"},{"en":"Schools need bike racks if many students cycle to class.","zh":"如果許多學生踩單車上學，學校需要單車架。"},{"en":"Good bike racks reduce clutter because cyclists have a proper place to leave bikes.","zh":"好的單車架可以減少雜亂，因為單車人士有適當地方停放單車。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bicycle parking facilities.","zh":"這個短語描述單車泊車設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"agree to provide","meaning":"同意提供","examples":[{"en":"The station has agreed to provide bike racks.","zh":"車站已同意提供單車架。"},{"en":"To agree to provide something means to accept responsibility for supplying it.","zh":"agree to provide something 的意思是接受提供某物的責任。"},{"en":"The school agreed to provide extra chairs for the meeting.","zh":"學校同意為會議提供額外椅子。"},{"en":"When an organisation agrees to provide a facility, people can expect practical action later.","zh":"當機構同意提供設施，人們可以期待之後有實際行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in planning and negotiation.","zh":"這個短語常見於規劃和協商。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"proposals for improvements to","meaning":"改善……的建議","examples":[{"en":"The next agenda item is proposals for improvements to the recreation ground.","zh":"下一項議程是改善休憩運動場的建議。"},{"en":"Proposals for improvements to something are suggested plans to make it better.","zh":"proposals for improvements to something 是令某事變得更好的建議計劃。"},{"en":"Parents gave proposals for improvements to the school playground.","zh":"家長提出改善學校遊樂場的建議。"},{"en":"Improvement proposals help decision-makers compare possible changes before spending money.","zh":"改善建議幫助決策者在花錢前比較可行改動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in meetings and planning documents.","zh":"這個短語常見於會議和規劃文件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"recreation ground","meaning":"康樂場地；休憩運動場","examples":[{"en":"The council discusses improvements to the recreation ground.","zh":"議會討論改善休憩運動場。"},{"en":"A recreation ground is an open public area used for sport, play, and leisure.","zh":"recreation ground 是用於運動、玩耍和休閒的開放公共空間。"},{"en":"A recreation ground may include football pitches, playgrounds, paths, and benches.","zh":"休憩運動場可能包括足球場、遊樂場、步道和長椅。"},{"en":"Improving a recreation ground can benefit children, sports teams, and local residents.","zh":"改善休憩運動場可以令兒童、運動隊和本地居民受益。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English.","zh":"這個短語常見於英式英文。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"manage to","meaning":"成功做到","examples":[{"en":"The council managed to extend the recreation ground.","zh":"議會成功擴建休憩運動場。"},{"en":"To manage to do something means to succeed in doing it, often despite difficulty.","zh":"manage to do something 的意思是成功做到某事，通常是在有困難下做到。"},{"en":"We managed to finish the project before the deadline.","zh":"我們成功在截止日期前完成專題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests effort, difficulty, or achievement.","zh":"這個短語暗示努力、困難或成就。"},{"en":"It is useful when someone succeeds after trying.","zh":"當某人努力後成功時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"extend the recreation ground","meaning":"擴建休憩運動場","examples":[{"en":"The council managed to extend the recreation ground.","zh":"議會成功擴建休憩運動場。"},{"en":"To extend the recreation ground means to make the public leisure area larger.","zh":"extend the recreation ground 的意思是令公共休閒場地變得更大。"},{"en":"The town extended the recreation ground by buying land beside the park.","zh":"城鎮透過購買公園旁土地來擴建休憩運動場。"},{"en":"Extending a recreation ground can create space for more sports and community facilities.","zh":"擴建休憩運動場可以為更多運動和社區設施創造空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing the size of a public leisure area.","zh":"這個短語描述增加公共休閒場地面積。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"spend time doing","meaning":"花時間做……","examples":[{"en":"The council spent time talking to local people.","zh":"議會花時間與本地居民交談。"},{"en":"To spend time doing something means to use time for that activity.","zh":"spend time doing something 的意思是用時間做某活動。"},{"en":"Teachers spend time preparing lessons before class.","zh":"老師上課前花時間備課。"},{"en":"Spending time listening to residents can lead to better public decisions.","zh":"花時間聆聽居民意見可以帶來更好的公共決定。"},{"en":"This phrase connects time with an activity.","zh":"這個短語把時間與活動連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"local people","meaning":"本地居民","examples":[{"en":"The council talked to local people about the recreation ground.","zh":"議會與本地居民討論休憩運動場。"},{"en":"Local people are the residents who live in the area being discussed.","zh":"local people 是住在正在討論地區的居民。"},{"en":"Local people often know which roads, parks, or services cause daily problems.","zh":"本地居民通常知道哪些道路、公園或服務造成日常問題。"},{"en":"Consulting local people can make a plan more realistic and accepted.","zh":"諮詢本地居民可以令計劃更現實，也更容易被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the community directly affected.","zh":"這個短語指出直接受影響的社區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be made more attractive and useful","meaning":"變得更吸引和實用","examples":[{"en":"The council asked how the space could be made more attractive and useful.","zh":"議會詢問這個空間可以如何變得更吸引和實用。"},{"en":"To be made more attractive and useful means to be improved so it looks better and serves people better.","zh":"be made more attractive and useful 的意思是被改善到看起來更好，並更能服務人們。"},{"en":"A school courtyard can be made more attractive and useful with plants, seats, and shade.","zh":"學校庭院可以透過植物、座位和樹蔭變得更吸引和實用。"},{"en":"Public spaces work best when they are pleasant to look at and practical to use.","zh":"公共空間在外觀舒適且使用實際時效果最好。"},{"en":"This phrase combines appearance and function.","zh":"這個短語結合外觀和功能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have a look at","meaning":"看一看","examples":[{"en":"The chairperson asks people to have a look at the map.","zh":"主席請大家看一看地圖。"},{"en":"To have a look at something means to look at it briefly or carefully.","zh":"have a look at something 的意思是簡短或仔細地看某物。"},{"en":"Please have a look at the timetable before choosing your class.","zh":"選課前請看一看時間表。"},{"en":"Looking at a map helps people understand where proposed changes will be.","zh":"看地圖有助人們理解建議改動會在哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and conversational.","zh":"這個短語禮貌而口語化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"up on the screen","meaning":"在螢幕上","examples":[{"en":"The map is up on the screen.","zh":"地圖在螢幕上。"},{"en":"Up on the screen means displayed on a screen where people can see it.","zh":"up on the screen 的意思是顯示在螢幕上，讓人看見。"},{"en":"The teacher put the diagram up on the screen.","zh":"老師把圖表放在螢幕上。"},{"en":"Information on a screen helps a group look at the same thing at the same time.","zh":"螢幕上的資訊幫助一群人同時看同一樣東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in presentations and meetings.","zh":"這個短語常見於簡報和會議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"near the entrance from the road","meaning":"靠近道路入口","examples":[{"en":"The Community Hall is near the entrance from the road.","zh":"社區禮堂靠近道路入口。"},{"en":"Near the entrance from the road means close to the point where people enter from the roadside.","zh":"near the entrance from the road 的意思是靠近人們從路邊進入的入口位置。"},{"en":"A car park near the entrance from the road is convenient for visitors.","zh":"靠近道路入口的停車場對訪客方便。"},{"en":"Facilities near entrances are easier to find and use.","zh":"靠近入口的設施較容易找到和使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position in relation to access.","zh":"這個短語描述與進出口有關的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at present","meaning":"目前","examples":[{"en":"At present, cars can park near the Community Hall.","zh":"目前，汽車可以停泊在社區禮堂附近。"},{"en":"At present means now or currently.","zh":"at present 的意思是現在或目前。"},{"en":"At present, the library is open only on weekdays.","zh":"目前，圖書館只在平日開放。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining a current arrangement that may change later.","zh":"當解釋日後可能改變的現行安排時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It sounds more formal than “now”.","zh":"它比 now 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"line of trees","meaning":"一排樹木","examples":[{"en":"Cars can park between the Community Hall and the line of trees.","zh":"汽車可以停泊在社區禮堂和一排樹木之間。"},{"en":"A line of trees is a row of trees growing or planted in a straight or clear line.","zh":"line of trees 是以直線或清楚排列生長或種植的一排樹木。"},{"en":"A line of trees can separate a park from a road.","zh":"一排樹木可以把公園和道路分隔開。"},{"en":"Trees in a line can act as a visual boundary or provide shade.","zh":"排成一行的樹可以作為視覺邊界或提供樹蔭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a natural or planted feature on a map.","zh":"這個短語描述地圖上的自然或種植特徵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"to the east","meaning":"在東面","examples":[{"en":"The line of trees is to the east of the Community Hall.","zh":"那排樹木在社區禮堂東面。"},{"en":"To the east means on the eastern side of a place.","zh":"to the east 的意思是在某地方的東邊。"},{"en":"The playground is to the east of the main building.","zh":"遊樂場在主樓東面。"},{"en":"Direction words help people understand maps and locations clearly.","zh":"方向詞幫助人們清楚理解地圖和位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position using compass direction.","zh":"這個短語使用方位描述位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dangerous for pedestrians","meaning":"對行人危險","examples":[{"en":"The current parking arrangement is dangerous for pedestrians.","zh":"目前的泊車安排對行人危險。"},{"en":"Dangerous for pedestrians means unsafe for people walking.","zh":"dangerous for pedestrians 的意思是對步行的人不安全。"},{"en":"Cars reversing near a playground can be dangerous for pedestrians.","zh":"汽車在遊樂場附近倒車可能對行人危險。"},{"en":"If a space is dangerous for pedestrians, planners should separate people from vehicles.","zh":"如果空間對行人危險，規劃者應把人和車分隔開。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on walking safety.","zh":"這個短語集中於步行安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"suggest a new car park","meaning":"建議設置新停車場","examples":[{"en":"The council is suggesting a new car park next to the Community Hall.","zh":"議會建議在社區禮堂旁邊設置新停車場。"},{"en":"To suggest a new car park means to propose building or creating a new place for cars to park.","zh":"suggest a new car park 的意思是提議興建或設置新的泊車地方。"},{"en":"Residents suggested a new car park because street parking was full every weekend.","zh":"因為街邊泊車位每個週末都爆滿，居民建議設置新停車場。"},{"en":"Suggesting a new car park can solve parking problems but may also affect green space.","zh":"建議設置新停車場可以解決泊車問題，但也可能影響綠化空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a planning proposal.","zh":"這個短語描述規劃建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on the opposite side of","meaning":"在……的另一邊","examples":[{"en":"The new car park will be on the opposite side of the Community Hall.","zh":"新停車場會在社區禮堂的另一邊。"},{"en":"On the opposite side of something means on the other side from a particular point or object.","zh":"on the opposite side of something 的意思是在某點或某物相對的另一邊。"},{"en":"The toilets are on the opposite side of the playground.","zh":"洗手間在遊樂場的另一邊。"},{"en":"Moving a facility to the opposite side can change how people enter and move through a space.","zh":"把設施移到另一邊可以改變人們如何進入和穿過空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position by contrast.","zh":"這個短語透過對比描述位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"right next to","meaning":"就在……旁邊","examples":[{"en":"The new car park will be right next to the Community Hall.","zh":"新停車場會就在社區禮堂旁邊。"},{"en":"Right next to means directly beside or extremely close to something.","zh":"right next to 的意思是直接在某物旁邊或非常接近某物。"},{"en":"The bus stop is right next to the school gate.","zh":"巴士站就在校門旁邊。"},{"en":"A facility right next to the entrance is easy for visitors to find.","zh":"就在入口旁邊的設施，訪客很容易找到。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises closeness.","zh":"這個短語強調距離很近。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"new location for","meaning":"……的新位置","examples":[{"en":"The council has a new location for the cricket pitch.","zh":"議會為板球場安排了新位置。"},{"en":"A new location for something is a different place where it will be put or moved.","zh":"new location for something 是某物將被放置或搬到的另一個地方。"},{"en":"The school found a new location for the bicycle racks.","zh":"學校為單車架找到新位置。"},{"en":"Choosing a new location can improve safety, access, or space.","zh":"選擇新位置可以改善安全、通達度或空間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is being relocated.","zh":"這個短語適合用於某物需要搬遷時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cricket pitch","meaning":"板球場","examples":[{"en":"The cricket pitch will be moved to a new area.","zh":"板球場會搬到新區域。"},{"en":"A cricket pitch is the playing area used for cricket.","zh":"cricket pitch 是用來打板球的場地。"},{"en":"A cricket pitch needs enough space so players can bat, bowl, and field safely.","zh":"板球場需要足夠空間，讓球員安全擊球、投球和防守。"},{"en":"If a cricket pitch is too close to a road, stray balls may become dangerous.","zh":"如果板球場太靠近道路，飛偏的球可能變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase names a sports facility.","zh":"這個短語指一種運動設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"purchase additional space","meaning":"購買額外空間","examples":[{"en":"The council has purchased additional space to the east of the recreation ground.","zh":"議會已在休憩運動場東面購買額外空間。"},{"en":"To purchase additional space means to buy extra land or area.","zh":"purchase additional space 的意思是購買額外土地或地方。"},{"en":"A school may purchase additional space to build new classrooms.","zh":"學校可能購買額外空間來興建新課室。"},{"en":"Buying extra space can allow planners to move facilities away from dangerous areas.","zh":"購買額外空間可以讓規劃者把設施移離危險地區。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in planning.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常見於規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"additional space","meaning":"額外空間","examples":[{"en":"The new cricket pitch will use additional space beyond the trees.","zh":"新板球場會使用樹木之外的額外空間。"},{"en":"Additional space means extra area beyond what was already available.","zh":"additional space 的意思是原本可用地方以外的額外面積。"},{"en":"A library may need additional space for study desks and computers.","zh":"圖書館可能需要額外空間放置自修桌和電腦。"},{"en":"Extra space can reduce crowding and allow safer movement.","zh":"額外空間可以減少擠迫，並讓人更安全移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes more physical room.","zh":"這個短語描述更多實體空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"beyond the trees","meaning":"在樹木之外","examples":[{"en":"The cricket pitch will be moved beyond the line of trees.","zh":"板球場會搬到那排樹木之外。"},{"en":"Beyond the trees means on the far side of the trees.","zh":"beyond the trees 的意思是在樹木另一邊較遠的位置。"},{"en":"The new playground is beyond the trees, away from the main road.","zh":"新遊樂場在樹木之外，遠離主要道路。"},{"en":"Placing something beyond trees can create separation and a clearer boundary.","zh":"把某物放在樹木之外可以創造分隔和更清晰邊界。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location past a natural feature.","zh":"這個短語描述越過自然特徵後的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"current location","meaning":"現時位置","examples":[{"en":"The cricket pitch will move away from its current location.","zh":"板球場會離開其現時位置。"},{"en":"Current location means the place where something is now.","zh":"current location 的意思是某物現在所在的地方。"},{"en":"The notice board’s current location is near the main entrance.","zh":"告示板的現時位置在主入口附近。"},{"en":"Moving away from a current location may be necessary if that place is unsafe or inconvenient.","zh":"如果現時位置不安全或不方便，可能需要搬離。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts present position with a future one.","zh":"這個短語把目前位置與未來位置作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rather near","meaning":"頗接近","examples":[{"en":"The current cricket pitch is rather near the road.","zh":"現時的板球場頗接近道路。"},{"en":"Rather near means quite close, perhaps closer than is ideal.","zh":"rather near 的意思是相當接近，可能比理想距離更近。"},{"en":"The playground is rather near the car park, so a fence may be needed.","zh":"遊樂場頗接近停車場，所以可能需要圍欄。"},{"en":"When a sports area is rather near a road, safety risks can increase.","zh":"當運動場頗接近道路，安全風險可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a mild warning about distance.","zh":"這個短語對距離作出溫和警示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"move it away from","meaning":"把它移離……","examples":[{"en":"The council plans to move the cricket pitch away from the road.","zh":"議會計劃把板球場移離道路。"},{"en":"To move it away from something means to place it farther from that thing.","zh":"move it away from something 的意思是把它放到離某物較遠的位置。"},{"en":"The school moved the play area away from the car park.","zh":"學校把遊戲區移離停車場。"},{"en":"Moving a facility away from danger can make it safer for users.","zh":"把設施移離危險源可以令使用者更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relocation for distance or safety.","zh":"這個短語描述為距離或安全而搬遷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"into this new area","meaning":"移到這個新區域","examples":[{"en":"The cricket pitch will be moved into this new area.","zh":"板球場會移到這個新區域。"},{"en":"Into this new area means to a newly chosen or newly added space.","zh":"into this new area 的意思是移到新選定或新增加的空間。"},{"en":"The picnic tables will be moved into this new area beside the trees.","zh":"野餐桌會移到樹旁這個新區域。"},{"en":"Moving facilities into a new area can change how people use the whole site.","zh":"把設施移到新區域可以改變人們使用整個場地的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a specific planned location.","zh":"這個短語指向特定計劃位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"line of trees","meaning":"一排樹木","examples":[{"en":"The new area is beyond the line of trees.","zh":"新區域在一排樹木之外。"},{"en":"A line of trees is a row of trees forming a visible natural boundary.","zh":"line of trees 是形成可見自然邊界的一排樹木。"},{"en":"The footpath follows the line of trees through the park.","zh":"行人徑沿着公園中的一排樹木延伸。"},{"en":"A line of trees can help divide different parts of a recreation ground.","zh":"一排樹木可以幫助分隔休憩運動場的不同部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear landscape feature.","zh":"這個短語描述清晰的地景特徵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stray balls","meaning":"飛偏的球","examples":[{"en":"Moving the cricket pitch reduces the danger of stray balls.","zh":"搬遷板球場可以減少飛偏的球造成的危險。"},{"en":"Stray balls are balls that fly or roll away from where they are meant to go.","zh":"stray balls 是飛或滾到原本方向以外的球。"},{"en":"A stray football can hit a window if the pitch is too close to houses.","zh":"如果球場太靠近房屋，飛偏的足球可以擊中窗戶。"},{"en":"Stray balls near roads can be dangerous for drivers and pedestrians.","zh":"道路附近的飛偏球可能對司機和行人危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes balls that go off course.","zh":"這個短語描述偏離路線的球。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hit cars or pedestrians","meaning":"擊中車輛或行人","examples":[{"en":"Stray balls may hit cars or pedestrians.","zh":"飛偏的球可能擊中車輛或行人。"},{"en":"To hit cars or pedestrians means to strike vehicles or people walking nearby.","zh":"hit cars or pedestrians 的意思是撞到附近車輛或步行的人。"},{"en":"A ball from a sports field could hit cars or pedestrians if there is no fence.","zh":"如果沒有圍欄，運動場飛出的球可能擊中車輛或行人。"},{"en":"Preventing balls from hitting people or vehicles is an important safety concern.","zh":"防止球擊中人或車輛是重要安全問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible accident.","zh":"這個短語描述可能發生的意外。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"plans for","meaning":"關於……的計劃","examples":[{"en":"The council has plans for a children’s playground.","zh":"議會有關於兒童遊樂場的計劃。"},{"en":"Plans for something are ideas or arrangements for creating or doing it.","zh":"plans for something 是創建或做某事的想法或安排。"},{"en":"The school has plans for a new reading room.","zh":"學校有關於新閱讀室的計劃。"},{"en":"Plans become clearer when people decide location, budget, and design.","zh":"當人們決定位置、預算和設計，計劃會變得更清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a proposed project.","zh":"這個短語引出建議項目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"children’s playground","meaning":"兒童遊樂場","examples":[{"en":"The council plans to build a children’s playground.","zh":"議會計劃興建兒童遊樂場。"},{"en":"A children’s playground is an outdoor area with equipment for children to play on.","zh":"children’s playground 是設有器材供兒童玩耍的戶外地方。"},{"en":"A playground may include swings, slides, climbing frames, and soft surfaces.","zh":"遊樂場可能包括鞦韆、滑梯、攀爬架和軟墊地面。"},{"en":"Good playgrounds help children exercise, socialise, and develop confidence.","zh":"好的遊樂場幫助兒童運動、社交和建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a public play facility.","zh":"這個短語描述公共遊樂設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"accessible by","meaning":"可經由……前往","examples":[{"en":"The playground will be accessible by a footpath from the Community Hall.","zh":"遊樂場可經由社區禮堂通往的行人徑前往。"},{"en":"Accessible by something means reachable using that route or method.","zh":"accessible by something 的意思是可以使用該路線或方法到達。"},{"en":"The beach is accessible by a short path from the car park.","zh":"海灘可經由停車場旁一條短路前往。"},{"en":"Good access matters because families, older people, and wheelchair users need safe routes.","zh":"良好通達度很重要，因為家庭、長者和輪椅使用者都需要安全路線。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how people can reach a place.","zh":"這個短語描述人們如何到達某地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"footpath","meaning":"行人徑","examples":[{"en":"A footpath will connect the Community Hall to the playground.","zh":"一條行人徑會連接社區禮堂和遊樂場。"},{"en":"A footpath is a path for people walking, not vehicles.","zh":"footpath 是供行人行走、不是供車輛使用的路徑。"},{"en":"A footpath through a park helps children and parents move safely.","zh":"穿過公園的行人徑幫助兒童和家長安全移動。"},{"en":"Footpaths can improve access by connecting buildings, playgrounds, and open spaces.","zh":"行人徑可以透過連接建築物、遊樂場和開放空間來改善通達度。"},{"en":"This word is common in maps and planning.","zh":"這個詞常見於地圖和規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"alongside the river","meaning":"在河邊","examples":[{"en":"The playground will be alongside the river.","zh":"遊樂場會在河邊。"},{"en":"Alongside the river means beside or next to the river, following its edge.","zh":"alongside the river 的意思是在河流旁邊或沿着河邊。"},{"en":"The walking path runs alongside the river.","zh":"步行徑沿着河邊延伸。"},{"en":"Riverside locations can be attractive, but safety barriers may be needed.","zh":"河邊位置可以很吸引，但可能需要安全欄杆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position beside a river.","zh":"這個短語描述在河流旁的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"originally thought of","meaning":"原本考慮過","examples":[{"en":"The council originally thought of having the playground close to the road.","zh":"議會原本考慮過把遊樂場設在靠近道路的位置。"},{"en":"Originally thought of means first considered before choosing another plan.","zh":"originally thought of 的意思是在選擇其他計劃前最初考慮過。"},{"en":"We originally thought of holding the event outside, but rain changed our plan.","zh":"我們原本考慮過在戶外舉辦活動，但雨天改變了計劃。"},{"en":"Early ideas may change when safety, cost, or convenience is considered.","zh":"當考慮安全、成本或便利時，早期想法可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts an initial idea with a later decision.","zh":"這個短語把最初想法與後來決定作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"close to the road","meaning":"靠近道路","examples":[{"en":"The playground was originally planned close to the road.","zh":"遊樂場原本計劃靠近道路。"},{"en":"Close to the road means near the road.","zh":"close to the road 的意思是在道路附近。"},{"en":"A playground close to the road may need a strong fence.","zh":"靠近道路的遊樂場可能需要堅固圍欄。"},{"en":"Places near roads can be convenient but may involve noise and traffic risks.","zh":"靠近道路的地方可以方便，但可能涉及噪音和交通風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distance from a road.","zh":"這個短語描述與道路的距離。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"more attractive location","meaning":"更吸引的位置","examples":[{"en":"The riverside is a more attractive location for the playground.","zh":"河邊是遊樂場更吸引的位置。"},{"en":"A more attractive location is a place that is nicer, more pleasant, or more appealing.","zh":"more attractive location 是較美觀、較舒服或更有吸引力的地方。"},{"en":"A garden beside a lake may be a more attractive location for a café than a busy road.","zh":"湖邊花園可能比繁忙道路旁更適合作為咖啡店位置。"},{"en":"Attractive locations can make public facilities more enjoyable to use.","zh":"吸引的位置可以令公共設施更令人享受。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the appeal of places.","zh":"這個短語比較地方的吸引力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"skateboard ramp","meaning":"滑板坡道","examples":[{"en":"The skateboard ramp is popular with children.","zh":"滑板坡道受兒童歡迎。"},{"en":"A skateboard ramp is a sloping structure used for skateboarding tricks and movement.","zh":"skateboard ramp 是供滑板動作和技巧使用的斜面設施。"},{"en":"Teenagers may practise turns and jumps on a skateboard ramp.","zh":"青少年可能在滑板坡道上練習轉彎和跳躍。"},{"en":"Skateboard ramps should be placed where users have enough space and safety.","zh":"滑板坡道應設在使用者有足夠空間和安全的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase names a sports and play facility.","zh":"這個短語指運動和玩樂設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"popular with","meaning":"受……歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The skateboard ramp is popular with both younger and older children.","zh":"滑板坡道受較年幼及較年長兒童歡迎。"},{"en":"Popular with a group means liked or used by many people in that group.","zh":"popular with a group 的意思是受該群體中許多人喜歡或使用。"},{"en":"The new reading corner is popular with younger students.","zh":"新閱讀角受較年幼學生歡迎。"},{"en":"Facilities that are popular with many age groups are usually valuable community resources.","zh":"受多個年齡層歡迎的設施通常是有價值的社區資源。"},{"en":"This phrase connects popularity with a specific group.","zh":"這個短語把受歡迎程度與特定群體連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"younger and older children","meaning":"較年幼及較年長的兒童","examples":[{"en":"The skateboard ramp is used by both younger and older children.","zh":"滑板坡道由較年幼及較年長的兒童使用。"},{"en":"Younger and older children means children from different age groups.","zh":"younger and older children 的意思是來自不同年齡組別的兒童。"},{"en":"A good playground should include activities for both younger and older children.","zh":"好遊樂場應包括適合較年幼及較年長兒童的活動。"},{"en":"Designing for different ages helps prevent boredom and unsafe use.","zh":"為不同年齡設計有助避免沉悶和不安全使用。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the facility serves a wide child age range.","zh":"這個短語顯示設施服務廣泛兒童年齡層。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"consider moving","meaning":"考慮搬遷","examples":[{"en":"The council considered moving the skateboard ramp towards the river.","zh":"議會考慮把滑板坡道搬向河邊。"},{"en":"To consider moving something means to think about relocating it before making a decision.","zh":"consider moving something 的意思是在作決定前思考是否搬遷某物。"},{"en":"The school considered moving the bike racks closer to the entrance.","zh":"學校考慮把單車架搬近入口。"},{"en":"Considering relocation helps planners compare safety, convenience, and cost.","zh":"考慮搬遷有助規劃者比較安全、便利和成本。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a plan was discussed but not necessarily chosen.","zh":"這個短語顯示計劃曾被討論，但未必被選中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"up towards the river","meaning":"向河邊移上去","examples":[{"en":"The council considered moving the ramp up towards the river.","zh":"議會考慮把坡道向河邊移上去。"},{"en":"Up towards the river means in the direction of the river, often slightly farther along the site.","zh":"up towards the river 的意思是朝河流方向，通常是沿場地再往上或往前移。"},{"en":"The path leads up towards the river from the car park.","zh":"這條路從停車場向河邊延伸。"},{"en":"Direction phrases help people follow positions on a map.","zh":"方向短語幫助人們理解地圖上的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement or placement toward a river area.","zh":"這個短語描述向河邊移動或放置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in the end","meaning":"最後","examples":[{"en":"In the end, the council chose the southeast corner.","zh":"最後，議會選擇了東南角。"},{"en":"In the end means finally, after discussion, changes, or consideration.","zh":"in the end 的意思是在討論、改變或考慮之後最終。"},{"en":"We looked at three hotels, and in the end we chose the cheapest one.","zh":"我們看了三間酒店，最後選擇最便宜的一間。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the final result after a process.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個過程後的最終結果。"},{"en":"It often contrasts earlier possibilities with the final choice.","zh":"它常把早前可能性與最終選擇作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"southeast corner","meaning":"東南角","examples":[{"en":"The skateboard ramp will be in the southeast corner near the road.","zh":"滑板坡道會設在靠近道路的東南角。"},{"en":"The southeast corner is the corner located between south and east on a map or site.","zh":"southeast corner 是地圖或場地上介乎南面與東面之間的角落。"},{"en":"The new garden will be placed in the southeast corner of the school grounds.","zh":"新花園會設在校園東南角。"},{"en":"Compass directions help planners describe exact locations clearly.","zh":"方位有助規劃者清楚描述準確位置。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific corner by direction.","zh":"這個短語以方向指出特定角落。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pavilion","meaning":"亭；涼亭","examples":[{"en":"The pavilion is used by football players and cricketers.","zh":"亭子由足球員和板球員使用。"},{"en":"A pavilion is a small building used for shelter, changing, meetings, or sports support.","zh":"pavilion 是用於遮蔽、更衣、會面或支援運動的小型建築。"},{"en":"Players may use a pavilion to change clothes or store equipment.","zh":"球員可能使用亭子更衣或存放裝備。"},{"en":"A well-placed pavilion is useful when several sports areas share the same facilities.","zh":"位置合適的亭子在幾個運動場共用設施時很有用。"},{"en":"This word describes a small public or sports building.","zh":"這個詞描述小型公共或運動建築。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"very well used","meaning":"使用率很高","examples":[{"en":"The pavilion is very well used at present.","zh":"亭子目前使用率很高。"},{"en":"Very well used means used often by many people.","zh":"very well used 的意思是被許多人經常使用。"},{"en":"The community hall is very well used on weekends.","zh":"社區禮堂週末使用率很高。"},{"en":"A well-used facility should be kept in a convenient location if possible.","zh":"如果可能，使用率高的設施應保留在方便位置。"},{"en":"This phrase shows high demand or regular use.","zh":"這個短語顯示高需求或經常使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at present","meaning":"目前","examples":[{"en":"The pavilion is very well used at present.","zh":"亭子目前使用率很高。"},{"en":"At present means now or currently.","zh":"at present 的意思是現在或目前。"},{"en":"At present, the playground is closed for repairs.","zh":"目前，遊樂場正關閉維修。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the current situation may change later.","zh":"當目前情況之後可能改變時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It sounds formal and clear.","zh":"它聽起來正式而清楚。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"stay where it is now","meaning":"保留在現址","examples":[{"en":"The pavilion will stay where it is now.","zh":"亭子會保留在現址。"},{"en":"To stay where it is now means to remain in its current location.","zh":"stay where it is now 的意思是留在目前所在位置。"},{"en":"The bus stop will stay where it is now because residents find it convenient.","zh":"巴士站會保留在現址，因為居民覺得它方便。"},{"en":"Keeping a facility in its current place can avoid confusion and unnecessary cost.","zh":"把設施保留在原位可以避免混亂和不必要成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes no relocation.","zh":"這個短語描述不搬遷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"to the left of","meaning":"在……左邊","examples":[{"en":"The pavilion is to the left of the line of trees.","zh":"亭子在那排樹木左邊。"},{"en":"To the left of something means on its left-hand side.","zh":"to the left of something 的意思是在某物左手邊。"},{"en":"The notice board is to the left of the main gate.","zh":"告示板在正門左邊。"},{"en":"Left and right descriptions help people read maps and diagrams.","zh":"左右位置描述幫助人們閱讀地圖和圖示。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relative position.","zh":"這個短語描述相對位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"near to the river","meaning":"靠近河流","examples":[{"en":"The pavilion is near to the river.","zh":"亭子靠近河流。"},{"en":"Near to the river means close to the river.","zh":"near to the river 的意思是在河流附近。"},{"en":"The picnic area is near to the river, so visitors can enjoy the view.","zh":"野餐區靠近河流，所以訪客可以欣賞景色。"},{"en":"Facilities near water may need safety measures, especially for children.","zh":"靠近水邊的設施可能需要安全措施，尤其是為兒童而設。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location beside or close to a river.","zh":"這個短語描述在河流旁或附近的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"handy for","meaning":"對……方便","examples":[{"en":"The pavilion is handy for both the football and cricket pitches.","zh":"亭子對足球場及板球場都方便。"},{"en":"Handy for something means conveniently located or useful for it.","zh":"handy for something 的意思是位置方便或對某事有用。"},{"en":"A car park near the entrance is handy for families with young children.","zh":"靠近入口的停車場對有年幼孩子的家庭方便。"},{"en":"Facilities are more useful when they are handy for the people who need them.","zh":"設施靠近需要它的人時會更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and practical.","zh":"這個短語是非正式而實用的說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"football and cricket pitches","meaning":"足球場及板球場","examples":[{"en":"The pavilion is handy for the football and cricket pitches.","zh":"亭子對足球場及板球場都方便。"},{"en":"Football and cricket pitches are sports fields used for playing football and cricket.","zh":"football and cricket pitches 是用來踢足球和打板球的運動場地。"},{"en":"A recreation ground may include football and cricket pitches for different teams.","zh":"休憩運動場可能包括足球場及板球場，供不同隊伍使用。"},{"en":"Shared facilities near sports pitches help players change clothes, rest, and store equipment.","zh":"運動場附近的共用設施幫助球員更衣、休息和存放裝備。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies two outdoor sports areas.","zh":"這個短語指出兩種戶外運動場地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"new notice board","meaning":"新告示板","examples":[{"en":"The council will get a new notice board for local information.","zh":"議會會設置一塊新告示板展示本地資料。"},{"en":"A new notice board is a display board used to show public notices or information.","zh":"new notice board 是用來展示公共告示或資訊的展示板。"},{"en":"A school may put a new notice board near the entrance for event announcements.","zh":"學校可能在入口附近放置新告示板，用於活動公告。"},{"en":"Notice boards help communities share information in a visible place.","zh":"告示板幫助社區在顯眼地方分享資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a public information display.","zh":"這個短語描述公共資訊展示設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"local information","meaning":"本地資料","examples":[{"en":"The notice board will display local information.","zh":"告示板會展示本地資料。"},{"en":"Local information is information about the nearby area, community, services, or events.","zh":"local information 是關於附近地區、社區、服務或活動的資訊。"},{"en":"Local information may include bus times, club meetings, and safety notices.","zh":"本地資料可能包括巴士時間、學會會議和安全告示。"},{"en":"Displaying local information helps residents know what is happening around them.","zh":"展示本地資料幫助居民知道身邊發生甚麼事。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on information relevant to a particular community.","zh":"這個短語集中於與特定社區相關的資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"directly on people’s right","meaning":"就在大家右邊","examples":[{"en":"The notice board will be directly on people’s right.","zh":"告示板會就在大家右邊。"},{"en":"Directly on people’s right means immediately to the right-hand side of people as they move or enter.","zh":"directly on people’s right 的意思是在人們移動或進入時立即位於右手邊。"},{"en":"The reception desk is directly on your right when you enter the building.","zh":"你進入大樓時，接待處就在你右邊。"},{"en":"Placing information directly on people’s right can make it easy to notice.","zh":"把資訊放在大家右邊顯眼位置，可以令人容易注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exact position from the visitor’s viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語從訪客視角描述準確位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"go from A into B","meaning":"從A進入B","examples":[{"en":"People will see the notice board as they go from the road into the recreation ground.","zh":"當人們從道路進入休憩運動場時，會看見告示板。"},{"en":"To go from A into B means to move from one place and enter another.","zh":"go from A into B 的意思是從一個地方移動並進入另一個地方。"},{"en":"Students go from the playground into the classroom when the bell rings.","zh":"鐘聲響起時，學生從操場進入課室。"},{"en":"Describing movement from one place into another helps explain routes clearly.","zh":"描述從一地進入另一地的移動，有助清楚解釋路線。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving directions or describing maps.","zh":"這個短語適合用於指路或描述地圖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/listening/Practice 19/task-3":[{"front":"now that","meaning":"既然","examples":[{"en":"Now that they have done the research, they need to organise their report.","zh":"既然他們已完成研究，就需要組織報告。"},{"en":"Now that means because something has happened, the next step can happen.","zh":"now that 指因為某事已經發生，下一步便可以發生。"},{"en":"Now that the survey is finished, the students can analyse the results.","zh":"既然問卷已完成，學生可以分析結果。"},{"en":"This phrase links a completed action with a new situation.","zh":"這個短語把已完成的行動與新情況連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining what should happen next.","zh":"解釋接下來應做甚麼時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"research into","meaning":"對……的研究","examples":[{"en":"The students have done research into bike-sharing schemes in cities around the world.","zh":"學生已對世界各地城市的共享單車計劃做研究。"},{"en":"Research into something means careful study of that topic.","zh":"research into something 指對某題目作仔細研究。"},{"en":"A student may do research into air pollution before writing a report.","zh":"學生寫報告前可能對空氣污染做研究。"},{"en":"Research into a subject helps people understand facts before giving opinions.","zh":"對某題目做研究，有助人在發表意見前理解事實。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic and project work.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術和專題研習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"bike-sharing schemes","meaning":"共享單車計劃","examples":[{"en":"Many cities around the world have introduced bike-sharing schemes.","zh":"世界各地許多城市已推出共享單車計劃。"},{"en":"Bike-sharing schemes are public systems that let people rent bicycles for short journeys.","zh":"bike-sharing schemes 指讓人租用單車作短途旅程的公共系統。"},{"en":"A bike-sharing scheme may allow users to unlock bikes with an app.","zh":"共享單車計劃可能讓使用者用應用程式解鎖單車。"},{"en":"These schemes can make short city journeys cheaper and cleaner.","zh":"這些計劃可以令城市短途旅程更便宜、更環保。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised shared bicycle services.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的共享單車服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"around the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"The report looks at bike-sharing schemes in cities around the world.","zh":"報告探討世界各地城市的共享單車計劃。"},{"en":"Around the world means in many different countries or places globally.","zh":"around the world 指在全球許多不同國家或地方。"},{"en":"Cities around the world are trying to reduce traffic congestion.","zh":"世界各地城市都在嘗試減少交通擠塞。"},{"en":"Looking around the world gives students a wider range of examples.","zh":"觀察世界各地例子，可以讓學生有更廣泛的材料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes global coverage.","zh":"這個短語描述全球範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"organise our report","meaning":"組織我們的報告","examples":[{"en":"Jake and Amy need to think about how to organise their report.","zh":"Jake 和 Amy 需要思考如何組織他們的報告。"},{"en":"To organise our report means to arrange its sections and ideas clearly.","zh":"organise our report 指清楚安排報告的章節和想法。"},{"en":"Students may organise their report by starting with background, then benefits, then problems.","zh":"學生可以先寫背景，再寫好處，最後寫問題來組織報告。"},{"en":"A well-organised report is easier for readers to follow.","zh":"組織良好的報告較容易讓讀者跟上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planning the structure of writing.","zh":"這個短語描述規劃文章結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"start by","meaning":"由……開始","examples":[{"en":"Amy thinks they should start by talking about the benefits.","zh":"Amy 認為他們應由談論好處開始。"},{"en":"Start by means begin with a particular first action or topic.","zh":"start by 指以某個第一行動或題目開始。"},{"en":"A presentation may start by explaining the problem.","zh":"簡報可以由解釋問題開始。"},{"en":"Starting by giving benefits can make a report sound positive at first.","zh":"由好處開始可以令報告一開始聽起來較正面。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show the order of ideas.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示想法次序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"introduce a scheme","meaning":"推出一項計劃","examples":[{"en":"Many cities have introduced bike-sharing schemes.","zh":"許多城市已推出共享單車計劃。"},{"en":"To introduce a scheme means to start or launch an organised plan.","zh":"introduce a scheme 指開始或推出一項有組織的計劃。"},{"en":"A city may introduce a scheme to encourage recycling.","zh":"城市可能推出一項鼓勵回收的計劃。"},{"en":"Introducing a scheme usually requires planning, money, and public support.","zh":"推出計劃通常需要規劃、資金和公眾支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes putting a new plan into use.","zh":"這個短語描述把新計劃投入使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pick up a bike","meaning":"取車；取用單車","examples":[{"en":"Users can pick up a bike from dozens of different locations.","zh":"使用者可以從數十個不同地點取用單車。"},{"en":"To pick up a bike means to collect or take a bike from a place where it is available.","zh":"pick up a bike 指從可用地點取走或領取單車。"},{"en":"A commuter may pick up a bike near the train station.","zh":"通勤者可能在火車站附近取用單車。"},{"en":"Easy pick-up points make bike-sharing more convenient.","zh":"方便的取車點令共享單車更便利。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first step in using a shared bike.","zh":"這個短語描述使用共享單車的第一步。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dozens of","meaning":"數十個","examples":[{"en":"Users can pick up bikes from dozens of different locations.","zh":"使用者可以從數十個不同地點取用單車。"},{"en":"Dozens of means many, usually several tens of something.","zh":"dozens of 指很多，通常是數十個。"},{"en":"A large city may have dozens of bike stations.","zh":"大城市可能有數十個單車站。"},{"en":"Dozens of locations make a system easier to access.","zh":"數十個地點令系統更容易使用。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate large number.","zh":"這個短語給出約略的大數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hire it for","meaning":"租用……一段時間","examples":[{"en":"People can hire a bike for a few hours.","zh":"人們可以租用單車幾小時。"},{"en":"To hire it for a period means to pay to use it during that length of time.","zh":"hire it for a period 指付費在某段時間內使用它。"},{"en":"Tourists may hire a bike for an afternoon to explore a city.","zh":"遊客可能租用單車一個下午來探索城市。"},{"en":"Short-term hire is useful for people who do not own bikes.","zh":"短期租用對沒有單車的人很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes renting something temporarily.","zh":"這個短語描述暫時租用某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"make riding a bike convenient","meaning":"令踏單車變得方便","examples":[{"en":"Bike-sharing makes riding a bike very convenient for people.","zh":"共享單車令踏單車對人們來說非常方便。"},{"en":"To make riding a bike convenient means to make cycling easy to access and use.","zh":"make riding a bike convenient 指令踩單車容易取得和使用。"},{"en":"Bike stations near offices make riding a bike convenient for workers.","zh":"辦公室附近的單車站令踏單車對員工更方便。"},{"en":"Convenience is important because people may not cycle if the system is difficult.","zh":"方便性很重要，因為如果系統困難，人們可能不會踩單車。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing practical barriers to cycling.","zh":"這個短語描述減少踩單車的實際障礙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the costs can add up","meaning":"費用可以累積起來","examples":[{"en":"Jake points out that the costs can add up.","zh":"Jake 指出費用可以累積起來。"},{"en":"The costs can add up means small payments can become expensive over time.","zh":"the costs can add up 指小額付款隨時間可以變得昂貴。"},{"en":"A short bike hire may seem cheap, but daily use can add up.","zh":"短時間租單車可能看似便宜，但每天使用費用會累積。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that repeated small costs matter.","zh":"這個短語提醒人反覆的小開支也很重要。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing affordability.","zh":"討論負擔能力時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"put someone off","meaning":"令某人卻步","examples":[{"en":"High costs can put people on low incomes off using bike-sharing.","zh":"高昂費用會令低收入人士對使用共享單車卻步。"},{"en":"To put someone off something means to discourage them from doing it.","zh":"put someone off something 指令某人不想做某事。"},{"en":"Complicated apps may put older users off bike-sharing.","zh":"複雜的應用程式可能令年長使用者對共享單車卻步。"},{"en":"If prices are too high, people may be put off even if they like the idea.","zh":"如果價格太高，即使人們喜歡這個想法，也可能卻步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discouragement.","zh":"這個短語描述被打消念頭。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"people on low incomes","meaning":"低收入人士","examples":[{"en":"Bike-sharing can be expensive for people on low incomes.","zh":"共享單車對低收入人士來說可能很昂貴。"},{"en":"People on low incomes are people who earn relatively little money.","zh":"people on low incomes 指收入相對較少的人。"},{"en":"Transport costs can be a serious concern for people on low incomes.","zh":"交通費對低收入人士來說可能是嚴重負擔。"},{"en":"Public schemes need to consider whether low-income users can afford them.","zh":"公共計劃需要考慮低收入使用者是否負擔得起。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a group with limited financial resources.","zh":"這個短語描述財政資源有限的群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in some places","meaning":"在某些地方","examples":[{"en":"Bike-sharing costs put some people off in some places.","zh":"在某些地方，共享單車費用會令一些人卻步。"},{"en":"In some places means in certain locations, but not everywhere.","zh":"in some places 指在某些地點，但不是所有地方。"},{"en":"In some places, bike lanes are safe and well connected.","zh":"在某些地方，單車徑安全而連貫。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids making a claim about all cities.","zh":"這個短語避免把說法套用到所有城市。"},{"en":"It is useful when conditions vary by location.","zh":"當情況因地點而異時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in general","meaning":"整體而言","examples":[{"en":"Bike-sharing may mean that more people in general are cycling.","zh":"共享單車可能意味著整體而言有更多人踩單車。"},{"en":"In general means usually or overall, without focusing on every single case.","zh":"in general 指通常或整體上，而不是聚焦每一個個案。"},{"en":"In general, people are more likely to cycle if routes are safe.","zh":"整體而言，如果路線安全，人們較可能踩單車。"},{"en":"This phrase helps make a broad statement carefully.","zh":"這個短語幫助謹慎地作出概括說法。"},{"en":"It is useful when summarising a general trend.","zh":"總結一般趨勢時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"More people may cycle rather than drive.","zh":"更多人可能會踩單車，而不是駕車。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of.","zh":"rather than 指而不是。"},{"en":"Some commuters choose to cycle rather than take the bus.","zh":"有些通勤者選擇踩單車，而不是乘巴士。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the chosen action with the alternative.","zh":"這個短語把已選行動與替代行動作比較。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining a change in behaviour.","zh":"解釋行為轉變時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"increase the amount of","meaning":"增加……的量","examples":[{"en":"Cycling increases the amount of physical activity people do.","zh":"踩單車會增加人們進行體能活動的量。"},{"en":"To increase the amount of something means to make there be more of it.","zh":"increase the amount of something 指令某物的數量增加。"},{"en":"Walking to school can increase the amount of exercise children get.","zh":"步行上學可以增加孩子得到的運動量。"},{"en":"A transport scheme can improve health if it increases daily movement.","zh":"如果交通計劃增加日常活動量，它就能改善健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth in quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述數量增長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"physical activity","meaning":"體能活動","examples":[{"en":"Bike-sharing can increase people’s physical activity.","zh":"共享單車可以增加人們的體能活動。"},{"en":"Physical activity means movement of the body that uses energy.","zh":"physical activity 指使用能量的身體活動。"},{"en":"Cycling, walking, swimming, and running are forms of physical activity.","zh":"踩單車、步行、游泳和跑步都是體能活動。"},{"en":"Regular physical activity can support health and fitness.","zh":"定期體能活動可以支持健康和體適能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active movement rather than sitting still.","zh":"這個短語描述主動身體活動，而不是靜坐。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"of less importance","meaning":"較不重要","examples":[{"en":"Jake asks whether that benefit is of less importance.","zh":"Jake 問那個好處是否較不重要。"},{"en":"Of less importance means not as important as something else.","zh":"of less importance 指不如另一件事重要。"},{"en":"Saving time may be of less importance than reducing pollution in this report.","zh":"在這份報告中，節省時間可能較減少污染不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare priorities.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較優先次序。"},{"en":"It is more formal than saying “less important”.","zh":"它比 “less important” 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reduced emissions","meaning":"減少排放","examples":[{"en":"Bike-sharing can contribute to reduced emissions.","zh":"共享單車可以有助減少排放。"},{"en":"Reduced emissions means a lower amount of gases or pollutants released into the air.","zh":"reduced emissions 指釋放到空氣中的氣體或污染物減少。"},{"en":"Fewer car journeys can lead to reduced emissions in a city.","zh":"汽車旅程減少可以令城市排放減少。"},{"en":"Reduced emissions may improve air quality and public health.","zh":"減少排放可能改善空氣質素和公共健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in environmental discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於環保討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"air pollution","meaning":"空氣污染","examples":[{"en":"Reduced emissions can improve air pollution.","zh":"減少排放可以改善空氣污染。"},{"en":"Air pollution is the presence of harmful substances in the air.","zh":"air pollution 指空氣中存在有害物質。"},{"en":"Traffic fumes are a major cause of air pollution in many cities.","zh":"交通廢氣是許多城市空氣污染的主要原因。"},{"en":"Reducing car use can help lower air pollution.","zh":"減少汽車使用可以幫助降低空氣污染。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dirty or harmful air.","zh":"這個短語描述骯髒或有害的空氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have a significant effect on","meaning":"對……有重大影響","examples":[{"en":"Reduced emissions can have a significant effect on people’s health.","zh":"減少排放可以對人們的健康有重大影響。"},{"en":"Have a significant effect on something means strongly influence it in an important way.","zh":"have a significant effect on something 指以重要方式強烈影響某事。"},{"en":"Cleaner air can have a significant effect on children with asthma.","zh":"更清潔的空氣可以對患哮喘的孩子有重大影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing important results.","zh":"討論重要結果時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It suggests the impact is noticeable and meaningful.","zh":"它暗示影響明顯而有意義。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make a big contribution to","meaning":"對……作出重大貢獻","examples":[{"en":"Bike-sharing has made a big contribution to reducing air pollution in some cities.","zh":"共享單車在某些城市對減少空氣污染作出重大貢獻。"},{"en":"To make a big contribution to something means to help it greatly.","zh":"make a big contribution to something 指大大幫助某事。"},{"en":"Better public transport can make a big contribution to reducing traffic.","zh":"更好的公共交通可以對減少交通擠塞作出重大貢獻。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights an important positive role.","zh":"這個短語突出重要的正面作用。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining the value of a policy or action.","zh":"解釋政策或行動價值時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cut the number of","meaning":"減少……的數量","examples":[{"en":"Bike-sharing can help cut the number of cars on the road.","zh":"共享單車可以幫助減少路上的汽車數量。"},{"en":"To cut the number of something means to reduce how many there are.","zh":"cut the number of something 指減少某物的數量。"},{"en":"A new bus service may cut the number of private cars near schools.","zh":"新巴士服務可能減少學校附近私家車數量。"},{"en":"Cutting the number of cars can reduce congestion and emissions.","zh":"減少汽車數量可以降低擠塞和排放。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述數量減少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cars on the road","meaning":"路上的汽車","examples":[{"en":"Bike-sharing can reduce the number of cars on the road.","zh":"共享單車可以減少路上的汽車數量。"},{"en":"Cars on the road means vehicles currently being driven or used on streets.","zh":"cars on the road 指正在街道上行駛或使用的車輛。"},{"en":"Fewer cars on the road usually means less traffic.","zh":"路上的汽車較少通常意味著交通較少。"},{"en":"Cities often try to reduce cars on the road during rush hour.","zh":"城市常嘗試在繁忙時間減少路上的汽車。"},{"en":"This phrase describes road traffic volume.","zh":"這個短語描述道路交通量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"significantly","meaning":"顯著地","examples":[{"en":"Bike-sharing has helped to cut the number of cars significantly.","zh":"共享單車已幫助顯著減少汽車數量。"},{"en":"Significantly means by a large or important amount.","zh":"significantly 指以很大或重要程度。"},{"en":"Better cycle lanes can significantly increase cycling rates.","zh":"更好的單車徑可以顯著提高踩單車比例。"},{"en":"This word shows that the change is not small.","zh":"這個字顯示變化並不小。"},{"en":"It is often used in reports and analysis.","zh":"它常用於報告和分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the main point","meaning":"重點","examples":[{"en":"Jake thinks reducing cars on the road is the main point.","zh":"Jake 認為減少路上的汽車是重點。"},{"en":"The main point is the most important idea or argument.","zh":"main point 指最重要的想法或論點。"},{"en":"The main point of the report may be that bike-sharing reduces pollution.","zh":"報告的重點可能是共享單車能減少污染。"},{"en":"Identifying the main point helps writers avoid unnecessary details.","zh":"找出重點幫助作者避免不必要細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the central idea.","zh":"這個短語描述核心想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have less of an impact on","meaning":"對……影響較小","examples":[{"en":"Bike-sharing has had less of an impact on noise pollution.","zh":"共享單車對噪音污染的影響較小。"},{"en":"Have less of an impact on something means affect it less strongly.","zh":"have less of an impact on something 指對某事影響較弱。"},{"en":"Cycling may have less of an impact on noise than on air quality.","zh":"踩單車對噪音的影響可能比對空氣質素的影響小。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare different effects.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較不同影響。"},{"en":"It shows that one benefit may be weaker than another.","zh":"它顯示某項好處可能比另一項弱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"noise pollution","meaning":"噪音污染","examples":[{"en":"Bike-sharing has had limited impact on noise pollution.","zh":"共享單車對噪音污染的影響有限。"},{"en":"Noise pollution is harmful or unwanted sound in the environment.","zh":"noise pollution 指環境中有害或不需要的聲音。"},{"en":"Traffic, construction, and aircraft can create noise pollution.","zh":"交通、建築工程和飛機都可以造成噪音污染。"},{"en":"Bikes are quiet, but buses and lorries may continue to make noise.","zh":"單車很安靜，但巴士和貨車可能仍會製造噪音。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sound-related environmental harm.","zh":"這個短語描述與聲音有關的環境傷害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"loads of","meaning":"很多","examples":[{"en":"There are still loads of buses and lorries around.","zh":"周圍仍有很多巴士和貨車。"},{"en":"Loads of means a lot of something.","zh":"loads of 指很多某物。"},{"en":"There are loads of bikes near the station during rush hour.","zh":"繁忙時間車站附近有很多單車。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and common in spoken English.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常見於英語口語。"},{"en":"It stresses a large number.","zh":"它強調數量很多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"buses and lorries","meaning":"巴士和貨車","examples":[{"en":"Noise pollution remains because there are still many buses and lorries.","zh":"噪音污染仍然存在，因為仍有很多巴士和貨車。"},{"en":"Buses and lorries are large road vehicles used for carrying people or goods.","zh":"buses and lorries 指用來載人或運貨的大型道路車輛。"},{"en":"Buses and lorries can be noisier than bicycles.","zh":"巴士和貨車可能比單車更嘈。"},{"en":"Reducing cars alone may not remove noise if buses and lorries remain.","zh":"如果巴士和貨車仍在，只減少私家車未必能消除噪音。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large traffic vehicles.","zh":"這個短語描述大型交通車輛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"recommendations","meaning":"建議","examples":[{"en":"The students discuss the recommendations they are going to make.","zh":"學生討論他們將提出的建議。"},{"en":"Recommendations are suggestions about what should be done.","zh":"recommendations 指關於應做甚麼的建議。"},{"en":"A report may include recommendations for improving a bike-sharing scheme.","zh":"報告可能包括改善共享單車計劃的建議。"},{"en":"Good recommendations should be practical and based on evidence.","zh":"好建議應該實際並建基於證據。"},{"en":"This word describes advice at the end of analysis.","zh":"這個字描述分析後提出的建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in order to ensure","meaning":"為了確保","examples":[{"en":"The recommendations aim to ensure bike-sharing schemes are successful.","zh":"這些建議旨在確保共享單車計劃成功。"},{"en":"In order to ensure means for the purpose of making certain that something happens.","zh":"in order to ensure 指為了確保某事發生。"},{"en":"Cities need clear signs in order to ensure users can find bikes easily.","zh":"城市需要清晰標示，以確保使用者能容易找到單車。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in reports.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於報告。"},{"en":"It explains the purpose of an action.","zh":"它解釋行動目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"state-of-the-art bikes","meaning":"最先進的單車","examples":[{"en":"State-of-the-art bikes with GPS are useful but not absolutely necessary.","zh":"配備 GPS 的最先進單車有用，但不是絕對必要。"},{"en":"State-of-the-art bikes use the newest and most advanced technology.","zh":"state-of-the-art bikes 指使用最新、最先進科技的單車。"},{"en":"A state-of-the-art bike may have GPS tracking and electronic locks.","zh":"最先進的單車可能有 GPS 追蹤和電子鎖。"},{"en":"Advanced bikes can help management, but they may also cost more.","zh":"先進單車可以幫助管理，但也可能成本更高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very modern bicycles.","zh":"這個短語描述非常現代化的單車。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"things like","meaning":"例如……之類的東西","examples":[{"en":"State-of-the-art bikes may include things like GPS.","zh":"最先進的單車可能包括 GPS 之類的東西。"},{"en":"Things like means examples such as.","zh":"things like 指例如某些東西。"},{"en":"A bike-sharing app needs things like maps, payment tools, and booking functions.","zh":"共享單車應用程式需要地圖、付款工具和預訂功能之類的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples in an informal way.","zh":"這個短語以較口語方式引入例子。"},{"en":"It does not mean the list is complete.","zh":"它不代表清單完整。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"absolutely necessary","meaning":"絕對必要","examples":[{"en":"Jake does not think GPS-equipped bikes are absolutely necessary.","zh":"Jake 不認為配備 GPS 的單車是絕對必要的。"},{"en":"Absolutely necessary means completely required, not just useful.","zh":"absolutely necessary 指完全必需，而不只是有用。"},{"en":"A safe braking system is absolutely necessary for shared bikes.","zh":"安全煞車系統對共享單車來說絕對必要。"},{"en":"Some features are nice to have but not absolutely necessary.","zh":"有些功能是錦上添花，但不是絕對必要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strict requirement.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴格要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"technical things","meaning":"技術方面的東西","examples":[{"en":"Some technical things are really important for bike-sharing schemes.","zh":"一些技術方面的東西對共享單車計劃非常重要。"},{"en":"Technical things are practical technology-related features or systems.","zh":"technical things 指與科技相關的實際功能或系統。"},{"en":"Apps, GPS tracking, locks, and payment systems are technical things in bike-sharing.","zh":"應用程式、GPS 追蹤、鎖和付款系統都是共享單車中的技術方面。"},{"en":"If technical things fail, users may not be able to rent bikes smoothly.","zh":"如果技術系統失靈，使用者可能無法順利租車。"},{"en":"This phrase describes technology and system details.","zh":"這個短語描述科技和系統細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fully functional app","meaning":"功能完整的應用程式","examples":[{"en":"A fully functional app is important for a bike-sharing scheme.","zh":"功能完整的應用程式對共享單車計劃很重要。"},{"en":"A fully functional app works properly and includes all the features users need.","zh":"fully functional app 指運作正常並包含使用者所需功能的應用程式。"},{"en":"A bike-sharing app should let users find bikes, pay, and report problems.","zh":"共享單車應用程式應讓使用者找車、付款和報告問題。"},{"en":"If the app is not fully functional, users may stop using the scheme.","zh":"如果應用程式功能不完整，使用者可能停止使用該計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an app that works completely.","zh":"這個短語描述完全可運作的應用程式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make payments","meaning":"付款","examples":[{"en":"Users need an app so they can make payments easily.","zh":"使用者需要應用程式，以便輕鬆付款。"},{"en":"To make payments means to pay money for a service or product.","zh":"make payments 指為服務或產品支付金錢。"},{"en":"Bike-sharing users may make payments through a phone app.","zh":"共享單車使用者可能透過手機應用程式付款。"},{"en":"Easy payment systems reduce delay and frustration.","zh":"簡單付款系統可以減少延誤和挫敗感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the act of paying.","zh":"這個短語描述付款行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"book bikes","meaning":"預訂單車","examples":[{"en":"A good app allows users to book bikes easily.","zh":"好的應用程式讓使用者容易預訂單車。"},{"en":"To book bikes means to reserve bicycles before using them.","zh":"book bikes 指在使用前預留單車。"},{"en":"A commuter may book a bike in advance before leaving the office.","zh":"通勤者可能在離開辦公室前預先訂單車。"},{"en":"Booking bikes can help users know a bike will be available.","zh":"預訂單車可以幫助使用者知道會有車可用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reserving shared bicycles.","zh":"這個短語描述預留共享單車。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"invest in","meaning":"投資於……","examples":[{"en":"Places that have not invested in a good app have struggled.","zh":"沒有投資於良好應用程式的地方遇到了困難。"},{"en":"To invest in something means to spend money, time, or effort to improve it.","zh":"invest in something 指投入金錢、時間或努力去改善某事。"},{"en":"Cities should invest in safe cycle lanes if they want more people to cycle.","zh":"如果城市想更多人踩單車，就應投資於安全單車徑。"},{"en":"Investing in technology can make a bike-sharing scheme easier to use.","zh":"投資於科技可以令共享單車計劃更容易使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes putting resources into something for future benefit.","zh":"這個短語描述為未來好處而投入資源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"struggle","meaning":"遇到困難","examples":[{"en":"Some cities have struggled because they did not invest in technology.","zh":"有些城市因沒有投資於科技而遇到困難。"},{"en":"To struggle means to have difficulty dealing with something.","zh":"struggle 指處理某事時有困難。"},{"en":"A city may struggle to manage bikes if the app often crashes.","zh":"如果應用程式經常故障，城市可能難以管理單車。"},{"en":"Schemes can struggle when users find them expensive or confusing.","zh":"如果使用者覺得計劃昂貴或混亂，計劃可能遇到困難。"},{"en":"This verb describes facing difficulty.","zh":"這個動詞描述面對困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"good point","meaning":"有道理；說得好","examples":[{"en":"Jake says “Good point” when Amy explains the importance of the app.","zh":"當 Amy 解釋應用程式的重要性時，Jake 說「說得好」。"},{"en":"Good point means that someone has made a useful or sensible comment.","zh":"good point 指某人提出了有用或合理的看法。"},{"en":"A student may say “Good point” when a classmate mentions safety.","zh":"當同學提到安全問題時，學生可能說「有道理」。"},{"en":"This phrase shows agreement and appreciation.","zh":"這個短語顯示同意和欣賞。"},{"en":"It is common in discussions and teamwork.","zh":"它常見於討論和團隊合作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"competing companies","meaning":"互相競爭的公司","examples":[{"en":"Some people think competing companies should not offer separate schemes.","zh":"有些人認為互相競爭的公司不應提供各自的計劃。"},{"en":"Competing companies are businesses trying to attract the same customers.","zh":"competing companies 指嘗試吸引同一批顧客的企業。"},{"en":"Two bike-sharing companies in one city may be competing companies.","zh":"同一城市中的兩間共享單車公司可能是互相競爭的公司。"},{"en":"Competition can improve service, but it can also confuse users.","zh":"競爭可以改善服務，但也可能令使用者混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes businesses in rivalry.","zh":"這個短語描述處於競爭關係的企業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"offer separate schemes","meaning":"提供各自的計劃","examples":[{"en":"Competing companies may offer separate bike-sharing schemes.","zh":"互相競爭的公司可能提供各自的共享單車計劃。"},{"en":"To offer separate schemes means to provide different systems instead of one shared system.","zh":"offer separate schemes 指提供不同系統，而不是一個共同系統。"},{"en":"Two companies may offer separate schemes with different apps and prices.","zh":"兩間公司可能提供各自的計劃，有不同應用程式和價格。"},{"en":"Separate schemes can give choice, but they may reduce convenience.","zh":"各自的計劃可以提供選擇，但可能降低便利性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes parallel services run independently.","zh":"這個短語描述獨立運作的平行服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"beneficial","meaning":"有益的","examples":[{"en":"Competition can be beneficial in very large cities.","zh":"在非常大的城市中，競爭可以是有益的。"},{"en":"Beneficial means helpful or producing good results.","zh":"beneficial 指有幫助或帶來好結果。"},{"en":"More cycle lanes can be beneficial for both cyclists and drivers.","zh":"更多單車徑可以對踏單車人士和司機都有益。"},{"en":"A policy is beneficial if it improves people’s daily lives.","zh":"如果政策改善人們日常生活，它就是有益的。"},{"en":"This word describes a positive effect.","zh":"這個字描述正面效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"manage the whole thing","meaning":"管理整件事","examples":[{"en":"One company might not be able to manage the whole thing.","zh":"一間公司未必能管理整件事。"},{"en":"To manage the whole thing means to control or operate the entire system or project.","zh":"manage the whole thing 指控制或營運整個系統或項目。"},{"en":"A small company may not manage the whole city’s bike-sharing network alone.","zh":"小公司未必能單獨管理整個城市的共享單車網絡。"},{"en":"Large schemes need staff, technology, maintenance, and customer support.","zh":"大型計劃需要人手、科技、維修和客戶支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes responsibility for everything involved.","zh":"這個短語描述對所有相關事情的責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"decide how much to invest","meaning":"決定投資多少","examples":[{"en":"Deciding how much to invest is a big question.","zh":"決定投資多少是一個大問題。"},{"en":"Decide how much to invest means choose the amount of money or resources to put into something.","zh":"decide how much to invest 指選擇向某事投入多少金錢或資源。"},{"en":"A city must decide how much to invest in apps, bike lanes, and maintenance.","zh":"城市必須決定在應用程式、單車徑和維修方面投資多少。"},{"en":"Investing too little can make a scheme fail.","zh":"投資太少可能令計劃失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a key planning decision.","zh":"這個短語描述關鍵規劃決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"open bike lanes","meaning":"開闢單車徑","examples":[{"en":"Some cities have opened new bike lanes while introducing bike-sharing.","zh":"有些城市在推出共享單車時開闢了新單車徑。"},{"en":"To open bike lanes means to create or make available special lanes for bicycles.","zh":"open bike lanes 指設立或開放專供單車使用的車道。"},{"en":"Cities may open bike lanes to make cycling safer.","zh":"城市可能開闢單車徑，以令踩單車更安全。"},{"en":"Bike lanes help separate cyclists from cars and buses.","zh":"單車徑幫助把騎車人士與汽車和巴士分開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding cycling infrastructure.","zh":"這個短語描述增加單車基礎設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at the same time as","meaning":"與……同時","examples":[{"en":"Some cities opened bike lanes at the same time as introducing bike-sharing.","zh":"有些城市在推出共享單車計劃的同時開闢單車徑。"},{"en":"At the same time as means while another action is happening.","zh":"at the same time as 指在另一行動發生的同時。"},{"en":"A city may improve bus services at the same time as reducing car parking.","zh":"城市可能在減少泊車位的同時改善巴士服務。"},{"en":"Doing two related things together can strengthen a policy.","zh":"同時做兩件相關事情可以加強政策效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes simultaneous actions.","zh":"這個短語描述同時發生的行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"introduce bike-sharing schemes","meaning":"推出共享單車計劃","examples":[{"en":"Cities may open new bike lanes when they introduce bike-sharing schemes.","zh":"城市推出共享單車計劃時，可能會開闢新單車徑。"},{"en":"To introduce bike-sharing schemes means to start public bicycle rental systems.","zh":"introduce bike-sharing schemes 指開始公共單車租用系統。"},{"en":"A city should prepare parking stations before it introduces bike-sharing schemes.","zh":"城市在推出共享單車計劃前，應準備停泊站。"},{"en":"Introducing a scheme without infrastructure may create problems.","zh":"沒有基礎設施就推出計劃可能造成問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes launching shared bicycle services.","zh":"這個短語描述推出共享單車服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"generally be more successful","meaning":"通常較成功","examples":[{"en":"Cities with new bike lanes have generally been more successful.","zh":"有新單車徑的城市通常較成功。"},{"en":"Generally be more successful means usually achieve better results overall.","zh":"generally be more successful 指整體上通常取得較好結果。"},{"en":"Schemes with clear instructions are generally more successful than confusing ones.","zh":"有清晰指示的計劃通常比混亂的計劃較成功。"},{"en":"This phrase allows for exceptions while describing a trend.","zh":"這個短語容許例外，同時描述趨勢。"},{"en":"It is useful in report analysis.","zh":"它適合用於報告分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"examples of successful schemes","meaning":"成功計劃的例子","examples":[{"en":"There are examples of successful schemes without many new bike lanes.","zh":"也有沒有很多新單車徑卻成功的計劃例子。"},{"en":"Examples of successful schemes are cases where plans worked well.","zh":"examples of successful schemes 指計劃運作良好的案例。"},{"en":"A report can use examples of successful schemes to support its recommendations.","zh":"報告可以使用成功計劃的例子來支持建議。"},{"en":"Successful examples show what conditions may lead to good results.","zh":"成功例子顯示哪些條件可能帶來好結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence from real cases.","zh":"這個短語描述來自真實案例的證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"what does matter","meaning":"真正重要的是","examples":[{"en":"What does matter is having a big publicity campaign.","zh":"真正重要的是有大型宣傳活動。"},{"en":"What does matter means the thing that is truly important.","zh":"what does matter 指真正重要的事情。"},{"en":"Bikes with GPS may not matter most; what does matter is easy access.","zh":"配備 GPS 的單車未必最重要；真正重要的是容易使用。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects or redirects attention to the key issue.","zh":"這個短語把注意力糾正或轉向關鍵問題。"},{"en":"It is useful when contrasting minor and major factors.","zh":"對比次要和主要因素時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"publicity campaign","meaning":"宣傳活動","examples":[{"en":"A big publicity campaign is important for bike-sharing schemes.","zh":"大型宣傳活動對共享單車計劃很重要。"},{"en":"A publicity campaign is an organised effort to inform and persuade the public.","zh":"publicity campaign 指有組織地通知和說服公眾的行動。"},{"en":"A city may run a publicity campaign to teach people how to use shared bikes.","zh":"城市可能舉辦宣傳活動，教人如何使用共享單車。"},{"en":"Posters, videos, social media, and school visits can be part of a campaign.","zh":"海報、影片、社交媒體和校園探訪都可以是宣傳活動的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planned promotion.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃的推廣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"know how to use","meaning":"知道如何使用","examples":[{"en":"People will not use the scheme if they do not know how to use it.","zh":"如果人們不知道如何使用這項計劃，就不會使用它。"},{"en":"Know how to use something means understand the steps needed to operate it.","zh":"know how to use something 指明白操作某物所需的步驟。"},{"en":"New users need to know how to use the app before renting a bike.","zh":"新使用者在租單車前需要知道如何使用應用程式。"},{"en":"Clear instructions help people use a system confidently.","zh":"清楚指示幫助人有信心地使用系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical user knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述實際使用知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"understand its benefits","meaning":"了解其好處","examples":[{"en":"People need to understand the benefits of the scheme.","zh":"人們需要了解這項計劃的好處。"},{"en":"Understand its benefits means know why something is useful or valuable.","zh":"understand its benefits 指知道某事為何有用或有價值。"},{"en":"Drivers may not switch to cycling unless they understand its benefits.","zh":"司機如果不了解其好處，可能不會轉為踩單車。"},{"en":"Explaining benefits can make people more willing to try something new.","zh":"解釋好處可以令人更願意嘗試新事物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes awareness of advantages.","zh":"這個短語描述對優點的認識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"need a lot of persuasion","meaning":"需要大量說服","examples":[{"en":"People need a lot of persuasion to stop using their cars.","zh":"人們需要大量說服才會停止使用汽車。"},{"en":"Need a lot of persuasion means require strong reasons or repeated encouragement before changing behaviour.","zh":"need a lot of persuasion 指在改變行為前需要很強理由或反覆鼓勵。"},{"en":"Some commuters need a lot of persuasion before they try cycling to work.","zh":"有些通勤者需要大量說服才會嘗試踩單車上班。"},{"en":"Habits are difficult to change, so persuasion may be necessary.","zh":"習慣很難改變，所以說服可能是必要的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resistance to change.","zh":"這個短語描述對改變的抗拒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"stop using","meaning":"停止使用","examples":[{"en":"A successful scheme must persuade people to stop using their cars.","zh":"成功的計劃必須說服人們停止使用汽車。"},{"en":"Stop using something means no longer use it.","zh":"stop using something 指不再使用某物。"},{"en":"Some people may stop using cars for short journeys if shared bikes are convenient.","zh":"如果共享單車方便，有些人可能停止短途使用汽車。"},{"en":"People are more likely to stop using something when there is a better alternative.","zh":"當有更好替代選擇，人們較可能停止使用某物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ending a habit or practice.","zh":"這個短語描述終止習慣或做法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"look at some examples","meaning":"看一些例子","examples":[{"en":"The students decide to look at some examples of bike-sharing schemes.","zh":"學生決定看一些共享單車計劃的例子。"},{"en":"To look at some examples means to examine several cases.","zh":"look at some examples 指研究幾個案例。"},{"en":"A report may look at examples from Amsterdam, Dublin, and London.","zh":"報告可能看 Amsterdam、Dublin 和 London 的例子。"},{"en":"Examples help students compare success and failure.","zh":"例子幫助學生比較成功和失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using cases for analysis.","zh":"這個短語描述用案例作分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"what is good or bad about","meaning":"……有甚麼好處或壞處","examples":[{"en":"The students discuss what is good or bad about different schemes.","zh":"學生討論不同計劃有甚麼好處或壞處。"},{"en":"What is good or bad about something means its strengths and weaknesses.","zh":"what is good or bad about something 指某事的優點和缺點。"},{"en":"Students can discuss what is good or bad about a city’s transport system.","zh":"學生可以討論一個城市的交通系統有甚麼好處或壞處。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise evaluation.","zh":"這個短語有助組織評估。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing different options.","zh":"比較不同選項時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"start with","meaning":"由……開始","examples":[{"en":"The students decide to start with Amsterdam.","zh":"學生決定由 Amsterdam 開始。"},{"en":"Start with means begin by discussing or doing one particular thing first.","zh":"start with 指首先討論或做某一件事。"},{"en":"A report about transport may start with the most successful city.","zh":"交通報告可以由最成功的城市開始。"},{"en":"Starting with a strong example can make the discussion clearer.","zh":"由強例子開始可以令討論更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the first item in a sequence.","zh":"這個短語顯示次序中的第一項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"one of the first cities to","meaning":"最早……的城市之一","examples":[{"en":"Amsterdam was one of the first cities to have a bike-sharing scheme.","zh":"Amsterdam 是最早擁有共享單車計劃的城市之一。"},{"en":"One of the first cities to means among the earliest cities that did something.","zh":"one of the first cities to 指最早做某事的一批城市之一。"},{"en":"A city can be one of the first to test a new transport idea.","zh":"一個城市可以是最早測試新交通概念的城市之一。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights early adoption.","zh":"這個短語突出早期採用。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing history or development.","zh":"討論歷史或發展時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"strong culture of cycling","meaning":"濃厚的單車文化","examples":[{"en":"Amsterdam already had a strong culture of cycling.","zh":"Amsterdam 本來已有濃厚的單車文化。"},{"en":"A strong culture of cycling means cycling is common, accepted, and part of everyday life.","zh":"strong culture of cycling 指踩單車很常見、被接受並成為日常生活一部分。"},{"en":"In a city with a strong cycling culture, children and adults both ride regularly.","zh":"在有濃厚單車文化的城市，兒童和成人都會定期踩單車。"},{"en":"A cycling culture can make bike-sharing easier to introduce.","zh":"單車文化可以令共享單車較容易推出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social habits around cycling.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞踩單車的社會習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in a way","meaning":"從某方面來說","examples":[{"en":"In a way, the demand for bike-sharing in Amsterdam is surprising.","zh":"從某方面來說，Amsterdam 對共享單車的需求令人驚訝。"},{"en":"In a way means from one point of view or in one respect.","zh":"in a way 指從一個角度或某方面來看。"},{"en":"In a way, the scheme’s success is surprising because many people already own bikes.","zh":"從某方面來說，計劃成功令人驚訝，因為很多人本來已有單車。"},{"en":"This phrase softens a statement by limiting it to one perspective.","zh":"這個短語把說法限制在某個角度，令語氣較柔和。"},{"en":"It is useful when making a careful comment.","zh":"作謹慎評論時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"demand for","meaning":"對……的需求","examples":[{"en":"There was strong demand for bike-sharing in Amsterdam.","zh":"Amsterdam 對共享單車有強大需求。"},{"en":"Demand for something means people’s need or desire for it.","zh":"demand for something 指人們對某物的需要或渴望。"},{"en":"There may be high demand for bikes near train stations.","zh":"火車站附近可能對單車有很高需求。"},{"en":"Strong demand shows that many people want to use a service.","zh":"強大需求顯示許多人想使用服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public need or market interest.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾需要或市場興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"you would have thought","meaning":"你原本會以為","examples":[{"en":"You would have thought most people in Amsterdam used their own bikes.","zh":"你原本會以為 Amsterdam 大多數人使用自己的單車。"},{"en":"You would have thought means it would seem reasonable to expect something.","zh":"you would have thought 指看似合理地預期某事。"},{"en":"You would have thought a rainy city would have fewer cyclists.","zh":"你原本會以為多雨城市會有較少踏單車人士。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces an expectation that turns out to be wrong.","zh":"這個短語常引出後來證明不一定正確的預期。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken discussion.","zh":"它常見於口語討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"use their own bikes","meaning":"使用自己的單車","examples":[{"en":"Most people in Amsterdam might have been expected to use their own bikes.","zh":"人們可能原本預期 Amsterdam 大多數人使用自己的單車。"},{"en":"To use their own bikes means ride bicycles they personally own.","zh":"use their own bikes 指騎自己擁有的單車。"},{"en":"In cycling cities, many residents use their own bikes for daily travel.","zh":"在單車城市中，許多居民使用自己的單車作日常交通。"},{"en":"Bike-sharing can still be useful for visitors or people without their bikes nearby.","zh":"對遊客或身邊沒有單車的人來說，共享單車仍然有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes private bicycle use.","zh":"這個短語描述私人單車使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"and yet","meaning":"然而","examples":[{"en":"And yet Amsterdam has one of the best-used schemes.","zh":"然而 Amsterdam 擁有使用率最高的計劃之一。"},{"en":"And yet introduces a surprising contrast with what was just said.","zh":"and yet 用來引出與剛才所說內容形成驚訝對比的事情。"},{"en":"The city already has many bikes, and yet the sharing scheme is popular.","zh":"這個城市本來已有很多單車，然而共享計劃仍很受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the result is unexpected.","zh":"這個短語顯示結果出乎意料。"},{"en":"It is useful when presenting contrast.","zh":"呈現對比時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"best-used schemes","meaning":"使用率最高的計劃","examples":[{"en":"Amsterdam has one of the best-used bike-sharing schemes.","zh":"Amsterdam 擁有使用率最高的共享單車計劃之一。"},{"en":"Best-used schemes are systems with very high levels of use.","zh":"best-used schemes 指使用量非常高的系統。"},{"en":"A best-used scheme has many regular users and frequent bike rentals.","zh":"使用率最高的計劃有許多固定使用者和頻繁租車。"},{"en":"High use can show that the scheme matches people’s needs.","zh":"高使用率可以顯示計劃符合人們需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong user participation.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的使用者參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"success story","meaning":"成功例子","examples":[{"en":"Dublin is an interesting example of a bike-sharing success story.","zh":"Dublin 是共享單車成功例子中一個有趣案例。"},{"en":"A success story is an example of something that worked very well.","zh":"success story 指某事運作非常良好的例子。"},{"en":"A city can become a success story if its transport scheme attracts many users.","zh":"如果城市的交通計劃吸引許多使用者，它可以成為成功例子。"},{"en":"Success stories are useful because they show what others can learn from.","zh":"成功例子很有用，因為它們顯示其他人可以學到甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive case study.","zh":"這個短語描述正面案例研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"public transport system","meaning":"公共交通系統","examples":[{"en":"Amy thinks Dublin’s public transport system is quite limited.","zh":"Amy 認為 Dublin 的公共交通系統相當有限。"},{"en":"A public transport system is the network of buses, trains, trams, or other shared transport.","zh":"public transport system 指巴士、火車、電車或其他公共交通工具組成的網絡。"},{"en":"A strong public transport system helps people travel without cars.","zh":"強大的公共交通系統幫助人們不用汽車也能出行。"},{"en":"If public transport is limited, bike-sharing may fill a gap.","zh":"如果公共交通有限，共享單車可能填補缺口。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised transport for the public.","zh":"這個短語描述為公眾而設的交通系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"quite limited","meaning":"相當有限","examples":[{"en":"Dublin’s public transport system may seem quite limited.","zh":"Dublin 的公共交通系統可能看似相當有限。"},{"en":"Quite limited means fairly restricted or not very extensive.","zh":"quite limited 指相當受限制或不太廣泛。"},{"en":"A town with only two bus routes has quite limited public transport.","zh":"只有兩條巴士路線的城鎮公共交通相當有限。"},{"en":"If options are limited, people may look for alternatives.","zh":"如果選擇有限，人們可能尋找替代方案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lack of range or coverage.","zh":"這個短語描述範圍或覆蓋不足。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not really","meaning":"不完全是","examples":[{"en":"Jake says Dublin’s public transport is not really that limited.","zh":"Jake 說 Dublin 的公共交通不完全是那麼有限。"},{"en":"Not really means not exactly or not to a great extent.","zh":"not really 指不完全是或程度不高。"},{"en":"The app is not really difficult once you have used it twice.","zh":"你用過兩次後，這個應用程式其實不太難。"},{"en":"This phrase softens disagreement.","zh":"這個短語令不同意見較柔和。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken English.","zh":"它常見於英語口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"underground","meaning":"地鐵","examples":[{"en":"Dublin does not have an underground railway system.","zh":"Dublin 沒有地下鐵路系統。"},{"en":"An underground is a railway system that runs below the city streets.","zh":"underground 指在城市街道下方運行的鐵路系統。"},{"en":"London’s underground carries millions of passengers.","zh":"London 地鐵運載數以百萬計乘客。"},{"en":"A city without an underground may rely more on buses, trams, or cycling.","zh":"沒有地鐵的城市可能更依靠巴士、電車或單車。"},{"en":"This word describes a subway or metro system.","zh":"這個字描述地下鐵路或城市鐵路系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tram","meaning":"電車","examples":[{"en":"Dublin has trams and a good bus network.","zh":"Dublin 有電車和良好的巴士網絡。"},{"en":"A tram is a public vehicle that runs on tracks along city streets.","zh":"tram 指沿城市街道軌道行駛的公共交通工具。"},{"en":"Trams can carry many passengers through busy urban areas.","zh":"電車可以在繁忙市區運載許多乘客。"},{"en":"Cities may use trams to connect places not served by underground trains.","zh":"城市可能使用電車連接地鐵未覆蓋的地方。"},{"en":"This word describes a street-level rail vehicle.","zh":"這個字描述街道路面上的軌道交通工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"bus network","meaning":"巴士網絡","examples":[{"en":"Dublin has a good bus network.","zh":"Dublin 有良好的巴士網絡。"},{"en":"A bus network is the system of bus routes serving an area.","zh":"bus network 指服務某地區的一系列巴士路線。"},{"en":"A good bus network helps people travel across a city without a car.","zh":"良好的巴士網絡幫助人們不用汽車也能橫跨城市。"},{"en":"Bike-sharing can work well alongside a bus network.","zh":"共享單車可以與巴士網絡配合得很好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes connected bus services.","zh":"這個短語描述互相連接的巴士服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have a lot to do with","meaning":"與……有很大關係","examples":[{"en":"Jake says price has a lot to do with Dublin’s success.","zh":"Jake 說價格與 Dublin 的成功有很大關係。"},{"en":"Have a lot to do with something means be strongly connected with it or strongly influence it.","zh":"have a lot to do with something 指與某事有強烈關聯或強烈影響它。"},{"en":"The success of a bike scheme has a lot to do with price and convenience.","zh":"共享單車計劃的成功與價格和方便程度有很大關係。"},{"en":"This phrase explains an important cause or factor.","zh":"這個短語解釋重要原因或因素。"},{"en":"It is common in discussion and analysis.","zh":"它常見於討論和分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one of the cheapest schemes","meaning":"最便宜的計劃之一","examples":[{"en":"Dublin has one of the cheapest bike-sharing schemes in Europe.","zh":"Dublin 擁有歐洲最便宜的共享單車計劃之一。"},{"en":"One of the cheapest schemes means among the lowest-cost schemes in a group.","zh":"one of the cheapest schemes 指在一組計劃中成本最低之一。"},{"en":"A cheap scheme can attract students and people on low incomes.","zh":"便宜計劃可以吸引學生和低收入人士。"},{"en":"Low price may help explain high usage.","zh":"低價格可能有助解釋高使用率。"},{"en":"This phrase compares cost with other schemes.","zh":"這個短語把成本與其他計劃作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be a factor","meaning":"是一個因素","examples":[{"en":"The weather certainly cannot be a factor in Dublin’s success.","zh":"天氣肯定不可能是 Dublin 成功的一個因素。"},{"en":"Be a factor means be one of the things that influences a result.","zh":"be a factor 指是影響結果的其中一件事。"},{"en":"Price can be a factor when people decide whether to use bike-sharing.","zh":"當人們決定是否使用共享單車時，價格可以是一個因素。"},{"en":"If something is not a factor, it probably does not explain the outcome.","zh":"如果某事不是因素，它大概不能解釋結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible cause or influence.","zh":"這個短語描述可能原因或影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be quite successful","meaning":"頗為成功","examples":[{"en":"The London scheme has been quite successful.","zh":"London 的計劃頗為成功。"},{"en":"Be quite successful means achieve a fairly good result.","zh":"be quite successful 指取得相當好的結果。"},{"en":"A scheme can be quite successful even if it still has problems.","zh":"一項計劃即使仍有問題，也可以頗為成功。"},{"en":"This phrase gives positive but moderate praise.","zh":"這個短語給出正面但適度的讚賞。"},{"en":"It suggests success, but not perfection.","zh":"它暗示成功，但不是完美。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a really good thing for","meaning":"對……來說是好事","examples":[{"en":"The London bike-sharing scheme has been a really good thing for the city.","zh":"London 共享單車計劃對這座城市來說是非常好的事。"},{"en":"A really good thing for someone or something means a very positive development for them.","zh":"a really good thing for someone or something 指對某人或某事非常正面的發展。"},{"en":"More cycle lanes would be a really good thing for cyclists.","zh":"更多單車徑對踏單車人士來說會是非常好的事。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and strongly positive.","zh":"這個短語較口語，語氣很正面。"},{"en":"It describes a benefit to a person, group, or place.","zh":"它描述對人、群體或地方的好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"well maintained","meaning":"保養良好","examples":[{"en":"The whole system in London is well maintained.","zh":"London 的整個系統保養良好。"},{"en":"Well maintained means kept in good working condition through regular care.","zh":"well maintained 指透過定期照顧而保持良好運作狀態。"},{"en":"Well-maintained bikes are safer and more pleasant to use.","zh":"保養良好的單車較安全，也較舒適。"},{"en":"A bike-sharing system needs regular repairs and checks.","zh":"共享單車系統需要定期維修和檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes good maintenance.","zh":"這個短語描述良好保養。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"expand quickly enough","meaning":"擴展得夠快","examples":[{"en":"The London scheme is not expanding quickly enough.","zh":"London 的計劃擴展得不夠快。"},{"en":"Expand quickly enough means grow or spread at a fast enough speed.","zh":"expand quickly enough 指以足夠快的速度成長或擴散。"},{"en":"A successful bike scheme may need to expand quickly enough to meet demand.","zh":"成功的單車計劃可能需要擴展得夠快，以滿足需求。"},{"en":"If a scheme expands too slowly, some areas may remain underserved.","zh":"如果計劃擴展太慢，有些地區可能仍服務不足。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether growth is fast enough.","zh":"這個短語描述增長速度是否足夠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not enough has been spent on","meaning":"在……方面投入不足","examples":[{"en":"Not enough has been spent on increasing the number of cycle lanes.","zh":"在增加單車徑數量方面投入不足。"},{"en":"Not enough has been spent on something means insufficient money has been invested in it.","zh":"not enough has been spent on something 指在某事上投放的金錢不足。"},{"en":"Not enough has been spent on maintaining older bikes.","zh":"在保養較舊單車方面投入不足。"},{"en":"Underinvestment can limit a scheme’s success.","zh":"投資不足會限制計劃成功。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises a lack of funding.","zh":"這個短語批評資金不足。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"increasing the number of","meaning":"增加……的數量","examples":[{"en":"More money should be spent on increasing the number of cycle lanes.","zh":"應投入更多金錢增加單車徑的數量。"},{"en":"Increasing the number of something means making there be more of it.","zh":"increasing the number of something 指令某物數量增加。"},{"en":"Increasing the number of bike stations can make a scheme more useful.","zh":"增加單車站數量可以令計劃更有用。"},{"en":"Cities increase numbers when existing supply is not enough.","zh":"當現有供應不足，城市就會增加數量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planned growth in quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃地增加數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cycle lanes","meaning":"單車徑","examples":[{"en":"London needs more cycle lanes to support bike-sharing.","zh":"London 需要更多單車徑來支持共享單車。"},{"en":"Cycle lanes are parts of roads marked or built for bicycles.","zh":"cycle lanes 指道路上標示或建造給單車使用的部分。"},{"en":"Safe cycle lanes can encourage nervous riders to try cycling.","zh":"安全單車徑可以鼓勵緊張的騎車人士嘗試踩單車。"},{"en":"Without cycle lanes, cyclists may have to share busy roads with cars.","zh":"沒有單車徑，騎車人士可能要與汽車共用繁忙道路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cycling infrastructure.","zh":"這個短語描述單車基礎設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hopefully","meaning":"希望","examples":[{"en":"Hopefully, London will invest more in cycle lanes.","zh":"希望 London 會在單車徑方面投資更多。"},{"en":"Hopefully means the speaker hopes something will happen.","zh":"hopefully 指說話者希望某事會發生。"},{"en":"Hopefully, the new app will make booking bikes easier.","zh":"希望新的應用程式會令預訂單車更容易。"},{"en":"This word shows optimism but not certainty.","zh":"這個字顯示樂觀，但不是肯定。"},{"en":"It is common when discussing future improvements.","zh":"討論未來改善時，它很常用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"outside Europe","meaning":"歐洲以外","examples":[{"en":"The students then discuss bike-sharing schemes outside Europe.","zh":"學生接着討論歐洲以外的共享單車計劃。"},{"en":"Outside Europe means in places that are not part of Europe.","zh":"outside Europe 指不屬於歐洲的地方。"},{"en":"Examples outside Europe can include cities in South America, Asia, or Australia.","zh":"歐洲以外的例子可以包括南美洲、亞洲或澳洲的城市。"},{"en":"Looking outside Europe gives the report a wider perspective.","zh":"觀察歐洲以外的地方讓報告有更廣闊角度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes geographical contrast.","zh":"這個短語描述地理對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take off","meaning":"開始流行；迅速發展","examples":[{"en":"Bike-sharing schemes have taken off in places like Buenos Aires.","zh":"共享單車計劃在 Buenos Aires 這類地方開始流行。"},{"en":"Take off means become popular or successful quickly.","zh":"take off 指迅速變得受歡迎或成功。"},{"en":"Electric bikes have taken off in some busy cities.","zh":"電動單車在一些繁忙城市開始流行。"},{"en":"A scheme takes off when many people begin using it.","zh":"當許多人開始使用某計劃，它就迅速發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rapid growth in popularity.","zh":"這個短語描述受歡迎程度快速增長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"places like","meaning":"像……這樣的地方","examples":[{"en":"Bike-sharing has taken off in places like Buenos Aires.","zh":"共享單車在像 Buenos Aires 這樣的地方迅速流行。"},{"en":"Places like means places similar to or including the example mentioned.","zh":"places like 指與所提例子相似或包括該例子的地方。"},{"en":"Places like large coastal cities may need good cycling routes.","zh":"像大型海岸城市這樣的地方可能需要良好單車路線。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an example without limiting the idea to only that place.","zh":"這個短語給出例子，但不把意思限於該地方。"},{"en":"It is useful when introducing representative cases.","zh":"引入代表性案例時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"huge network of","meaning":"龐大的……網絡","examples":[{"en":"Buenos Aires built a huge network of cycle lanes.","zh":"Buenos Aires 建立了龐大的單車徑網絡。"},{"en":"A huge network of something means a very large connected system.","zh":"huge network of something 指非常大型的連接系統。"},{"en":"A huge network of cycle lanes allows riders to travel across the city safely.","zh":"龐大的單車徑網絡讓騎車人士安全橫跨城市。"},{"en":"A network is more useful when its parts are connected.","zh":"當網絡各部分互相連接，它就更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large linked system.","zh":"這個短語描述大型連接系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"support the introduction of","meaning":"支持……的引入","examples":[{"en":"The city built cycle lanes to support the introduction of the scheme.","zh":"該城市興建單車徑，以支持該計劃的引入。"},{"en":"To support the introduction of something means to help a new system begin successfully.","zh":"support the introduction of something 指幫助新系統成功開始。"},{"en":"Clear signs can support the introduction of a new transport scheme.","zh":"清晰標示可以支持新交通計劃的引入。"},{"en":"Infrastructure can support a policy by making it easier to use.","zh":"基礎設施可以透過令政策更容易使用來支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes helping a new plan start well.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助新計劃順利開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"attract huge numbers of","meaning":"吸引大量……","examples":[{"en":"The scheme attracted huge numbers of cyclists.","zh":"該計劃吸引大量踏單車人士。"},{"en":"Attract huge numbers of people means bring in very many people.","zh":"attract huge numbers of people 指吸引非常多人。"},{"en":"A cheap and convenient scheme can attract huge numbers of users.","zh":"便宜而方便的計劃可以吸引大量使用者。"},{"en":"High numbers show that the public is interested.","zh":"高人數顯示公眾有興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong public response.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈公眾反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cyclists","meaning":"踏單車人士","examples":[{"en":"Buenos Aires attracted huge numbers of cyclists through good planning.","zh":"Buenos Aires 透過良好規劃吸引大量踏單車人士。"},{"en":"Cyclists are people who ride bicycles.","zh":"cyclists 指騎單車的人。"},{"en":"Safe cycle lanes protect cyclists from heavy traffic.","zh":"安全單車徑保護踏單車人士免受繁忙交通影響。"},{"en":"Bike-sharing can create new cyclists who did not cycle before.","zh":"共享單車可以創造以前不踩單車的新踏單車人士。"},{"en":"This word describes bicycle riders.","zh":"這個字描述騎單車者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"previously","meaning":"以往；之前","examples":[{"en":"Previously, there had been hardly any cyclists in Buenos Aires.","zh":"以往，Buenos Aires 幾乎沒有踏單車人士。"},{"en":"Previously means before the time being discussed.","zh":"previously 指在正在討論的時間之前。"},{"en":"Previously, the city had very few cycle lanes.","zh":"以往，該城市只有很少單車徑。"},{"en":"This word helps compare the past with the present.","zh":"這個字幫助比較過去與現在。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing change over time.","zh":"顯示隨時間變化時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hardly any","meaning":"幾乎沒有","examples":[{"en":"There were hardly any cyclists before the scheme was introduced.","zh":"在該計劃推出前，幾乎沒有踏單車人士。"},{"en":"Hardly any means almost none.","zh":"hardly any 指幾乎沒有。"},{"en":"Before the new lanes opened, there were hardly any bikes on the road.","zh":"新單車徑開通前，路上幾乎沒有單車。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a very small number.","zh":"這個短語強調數量非常少。"},{"en":"It is stronger than simply saying “few”.","zh":"它比單純說 “few” 更強烈。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"good planning","meaning":"良好規劃","examples":[{"en":"Buenos Aires is an example of good planning.","zh":"Buenos Aires 是良好規劃的例子。"},{"en":"Good planning means careful preparation before action is taken.","zh":"good planning 指在採取行動前仔細準備。"},{"en":"Good planning can include bike lanes, publicity, apps, and pricing.","zh":"良好規劃可以包括單車徑、宣傳、應用程式和定價。"},{"en":"A scheme with good planning is more likely to succeed.","zh":"有良好規劃的計劃較可能成功。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised preparation.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"how not to introduce","meaning":"如何不應該推行……","examples":[{"en":"New York is a good example of how not to introduce a scheme.","zh":"New York 是如何不應該推行計劃的好例子。"},{"en":"How not to introduce something means the wrong way to launch or start it.","zh":"how not to introduce something 指推出或開始某事的錯誤方式。"},{"en":"A city shows how not to introduce a scheme if prices are too high and information is unclear.","zh":"如果價格太高、資訊不清楚，一個城市就示範了如何不應該推行計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when learning from mistakes.","zh":"從錯誤中學習時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It highlights a bad example.","zh":"它突出反面例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"launch a scheme","meaning":"推出一項計劃","examples":[{"en":"New York’s bike-sharing scheme was too expensive when it was launched.","zh":"New York 的共享單車計劃推出時太昂貴。"},{"en":"To launch a scheme means to start it officially.","zh":"launch a scheme 指正式開始一項計劃。"},{"en":"A city may launch a scheme after months of planning and testing.","zh":"城市可能在數月規劃和測試後推出一項計劃。"},{"en":"The first price and publicity can affect how people react when a scheme is launched.","zh":"計劃推出時的首個價格和宣傳會影響人們反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the official beginning of a plan.","zh":"這個短語描述計劃的正式開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"more than ten times","meaning":"十倍以上","examples":[{"en":"New York’s scheme was more than ten times the price of most other schemes.","zh":"New York 的計劃價格是大多數其他計劃的十倍以上。"},{"en":"More than ten times means over ten times greater than another amount.","zh":"more than ten times 指比另一數量高出十倍以上。"},{"en":"If one ride costs more than ten times another, many users will avoid it.","zh":"如果一次騎行比另一次貴十倍以上，許多使用者會避開。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a very large difference.","zh":"這個短語顯示非常大的差距。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing costs.","zh":"比較成本時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"more than it costs to","meaning":"比……的費用更高","examples":[{"en":"The scheme cost more than it costs to take a taxi.","zh":"該計劃的費用比乘的士更高。"},{"en":"More than it costs to do something means higher in price than that action.","zh":"more than it costs to do something 指價格高於做某事的費用。"},{"en":"A bike ride should not cost more than it costs to take a bus.","zh":"一次單車旅程不應比乘巴士的費用更高。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one cost with another familiar cost.","zh":"這個短語把一個成本與另一個熟悉成本比較。"},{"en":"It helps show why something seems unreasonable.","zh":"它幫助顯示某事為何似乎不合理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take a taxi","meaning":"乘的士","examples":[{"en":"Using the scheme cost more than taking a taxi.","zh":"使用該計劃比乘的士更昂貴。"},{"en":"To take a taxi means to travel in a taxi as a passenger.","zh":"take a taxi 指作為乘客乘坐的士。"},{"en":"People may take a taxi when public transport is slow or unavailable.","zh":"當公共交通很慢或沒有服務時，人們可能乘的士。"},{"en":"If bike-sharing is more expensive than taking a taxi, users may choose the taxi instead.","zh":"如果共享單車比乘的士更貴，使用者可能改選的士。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a taxi service.","zh":"這個短語描述使用的士服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lack vision and ambition","meaning":"缺乏遠見和抱負","examples":[{"en":"Jake thinks the organisers lacked vision and ambition.","zh":"Jake 認為組織者缺乏遠見和抱負。"},{"en":"To lack vision and ambition means not have enough imagination, long-term thinking, or desire to succeed.","zh":"lack vision and ambition 指沒有足夠想像力、長遠思維或成功慾望。"},{"en":"A transport scheme may lack vision if it only solves today’s problem and ignores future growth.","zh":"如果交通計劃只解決今天問題而忽略未來增長，它可能缺乏遠見。"},{"en":"Ambition matters when cities want major behaviour change.","zh":"當城市希望重大行為改變，抱負很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises weak planning or low goals.","zh":"這個短語批評規劃薄弱或目標太低。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"organisers","meaning":"組織者","examples":[{"en":"The organisers of the New York scheme lacked vision and ambition.","zh":"New York 計劃的組織者缺乏遠見和抱負。"},{"en":"Organisers are people or groups responsible for planning and running an event or scheme.","zh":"organisers 指負責規劃和運作活動或計劃的人或團體。"},{"en":"The organisers of a bike-sharing scheme must decide prices, locations, and publicity.","zh":"共享單車計劃的組織者必須決定價格、地點和宣傳。"},{"en":"Good organisers prepare carefully before a scheme is launched.","zh":"好組織者會在計劃推出前仔細準備。"},{"en":"This word describes people in charge of planning.","zh":"這個字描述負責規劃的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"good example to use","meaning":"可採用的好例子","examples":[{"en":"Sydney would be a good example to use in the report.","zh":"Sydney 會是報告中可採用的好例子。"},{"en":"A good example to use is a case that helps explain or support an argument.","zh":"good example to use 指能幫助解釋或支持論點的案例。"},{"en":"London may be a good example to use when discussing maintenance.","zh":"討論保養時，London 可能是可採用的好例子。"},{"en":"Choosing the right example can make a report more convincing.","zh":"選擇合適例子可以令報告更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a useful case for analysis.","zh":"這個短語描述可用於分析的有用案例。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"expect something to","meaning":"預期某事會……","examples":[{"en":"Amy expected the Sydney scheme to grow quickly.","zh":"Amy 預期 Sydney 的計劃會快速發展。"},{"en":"Expect something to happen means believe it will probably happen.","zh":"expect something to happen 指相信某事很可能會發生。"},{"en":"Many people expected the new bike lanes to attract more cyclists.","zh":"許多人預期新單車徑會吸引更多踏單車人士。"},{"en":"Expectations may be wrong if local conditions are different.","zh":"如果本地情況不同，預期可能會錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes prediction.","zh":"這個短語描述預測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"grow pretty quickly","meaning":"發展得相當快","examples":[{"en":"The Sydney scheme was expected to grow pretty quickly.","zh":"Sydney 的計劃原本被預期會發展得相當快。"},{"en":"Grow pretty quickly means develop or increase fairly fast.","zh":"grow pretty quickly 指相當快速地發展或增加。"},{"en":"A bike-sharing scheme can grow pretty quickly if the price is low and stations are convenient.","zh":"如果價格低而車站方便，共享單車計劃可以發展得相當快。"},{"en":"Quick growth may require extra bikes and maintenance staff.","zh":"快速增長可能需要額外單車和維修人員。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fairly rapid development.","zh":"這個短語描述相當快速的發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"work out why","meaning":"弄清楚原因","examples":[{"en":"Jake cannot quite work out why Sydney has not been an instant success.","zh":"Jake 不太能弄清楚為何 Sydney 沒有即時成功。"},{"en":"To work out why means to understand the reason for something.","zh":"work out why 指理解某事的原因。"},{"en":"Researchers may work out why one scheme failed and another succeeded.","zh":"研究者可能弄清楚為何一個計劃失敗而另一個成功。"},{"en":"If the cause is unclear, it can be hard to make recommendations.","zh":"如果原因不清楚，就很難提出建議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes figuring out an explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述找出解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"instant success","meaning":"即時成功","examples":[{"en":"Sydney has not been an instant success like some other schemes.","zh":"Sydney 不像其他一些計劃那樣即時成功。"},{"en":"An instant success is something that becomes successful very quickly after it starts.","zh":"instant success 指某事開始後很快成功。"},{"en":"A new app may be an instant success if many people download it immediately.","zh":"如果很多人立即下載，一個新應用程式可能即時成功。"},{"en":"Not every good idea becomes an instant success.","zh":"不是每個好想法都會即時成功。"},{"en":"This phrase describes immediate positive results.","zh":"這個短語描述立即出現的正面結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"like some of the others","meaning":"像其他一些那樣","examples":[{"en":"Sydney has not succeeded as quickly as some of the other schemes.","zh":"Sydney 沒有像其他一些計劃那樣迅速成功。"},{"en":"Like some of the others means similar to some other examples in the same group.","zh":"like some of the others 指與同一組中的其他一些例子相似。"},{"en":"This scheme did not take off like some of the others in Europe.","zh":"這個計劃沒有像歐洲其他一些計劃那樣迅速流行。"},{"en":"The phrase compares one case with similar cases.","zh":"這個短語把一個案例與相似案例作比較。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing examples together.","zh":"一起討論多個例子時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"it’s a shame","meaning":"真可惜","examples":[{"en":"Jake thinks Sydney’s slow progress is a shame.","zh":"Jake 認為 Sydney 進展緩慢真可惜。"},{"en":"It’s a shame means it is disappointing or unfortunate.","zh":"it’s a shame 指令人失望或可惜。"},{"en":"It’s a shame that the scheme has good bikes but not enough users.","zh":"這個計劃有好單車卻沒有足夠使用者，真可惜。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses mild regret.","zh":"這個短語表達輕微遺憾。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken English.","zh":"它常見於英語口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"think about","meaning":"思考；考慮","examples":[{"en":"The students have thought about several examples of bike-sharing schemes.","zh":"學生已思考幾個共享單車計劃的例子。"},{"en":"Think about means consider or reflect on something.","zh":"think about 指考慮或反思某事。"},{"en":"Students should think about both the benefits and problems before writing conclusions.","zh":"學生在寫結論前應思考好處和問題。"},{"en":"Thinking about examples helps writers form stronger arguments.","zh":"思考例子有助作者形成更強論點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful consideration.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細考慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 19/task-4":[{"front":"one of the most famous cases of","meaning":"最著名的……案例之一","examples":[{"en":"One of the most famous cases of extinction is that of the dodo.","zh":"最著名的滅絕案例之一，就是渡渡鳥的案例。"},{"en":"One of the most famous cases of something means one of the best-known examples of it.","zh":"one of the most famous cases of something 是指某事最廣為人知的例子之一。"},{"en":"The fall of the Roman Empire is one of the most famous cases of political collapse.","zh":"羅馬帝國的衰落是政治崩潰最著名的案例之一。"},{"en":"Famous cases are often used in lessons because students can remember them easily.","zh":"著名案例常用於課堂，因為學生較容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an example that many people recognise.","zh":"這個短語用來引入很多人都認識的例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"extinction","meaning":"滅絕","examples":[{"en":"The dodo is a famous example of extinction.","zh":"渡渡鳥是滅絕的著名例子。"},{"en":"Extinction means the complete disappearance of a species.","zh":"extinction 是指一個物種完全消失。"},{"en":"Dinosaurs are often discussed when students first learn about extinction.","zh":"學生初次學習滅絕時，常會討論恐龍。"},{"en":"Extinction can happen when animals lose their habitat, food, or ability to reproduce.","zh":"當動物失去棲息地、食物或繁殖能力時，可能會滅絕。"},{"en":"This word describes a permanent loss, not just a temporary decline.","zh":"這個詞描述永久消失，而不只是暫時減少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be known as","meaning":"被稱為……","examples":[{"en":"The bird was known as the dodo.","zh":"這種鳥被稱為渡渡鳥。"},{"en":"To be known as something means to be called by that name.","zh":"be known as something 是指被叫作某個名稱。"},{"en":"Hong Kong is known as a busy international city.","zh":"香港被稱為繁忙的國際城市。"},{"en":"Names help people recognise and talk about a person, place, or thing.","zh":"名稱幫助人們辨認和談論一個人、地方或事物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a name or title.","zh":"這個短語適合用於介紹名稱或稱號。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, there is even a saying about the dodo in English.","zh":"事實上，英語中甚至有一句關於渡渡鳥的說法。"},{"en":"In fact is used to add a true point that supports, strengthens, or corrects what was just said.","zh":"in fact 用來加入真實資料，以支持、加強或修正剛才所說的內容。"},{"en":"The museum is popular; in fact, tickets often sell out by noon.","zh":"這間博物館很受歡迎；事實上，門票常在中午前售罄。"},{"en":"This phrase can make the next detail sound surprising or important.","zh":"這個短語可以令下一個細節聽起來令人意外或重要。"},{"en":"It helps speakers add stronger evidence or clarification.","zh":"它幫助說話者加入更強證據或澄清。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a saying in English","meaning":"英語中的一句說法","examples":[{"en":"There is a saying in English: “as dead as the dodo”.","zh":"英語中有一句說法：“as dead as the dodo”。"},{"en":"A saying in English is a common expression used by English speakers.","zh":"a saying in English 是英語使用者常用的固定說法。"},{"en":"“Better late than never” is a saying in English about doing something even if it is delayed.","zh":"“Better late than never” 是英語中一句關於即使遲了也比不做好更好的說法。"},{"en":"Sayings often carry cultural meanings that are not fully literal.","zh":"諺語或固定說法常帶有文化意思，不一定完全按字面理解。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a fixed expression or proverb.","zh":"這個短語用來引入固定表達或諺語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as dead as the dodo","meaning":"已徹底消失；早已不復存在","examples":[{"en":"The phrase “as dead as the dodo” refers to something that no longer exists.","zh":"“as dead as the dodo” 這個短語指已經不再存在的東西。"},{"en":"As dead as the dodo means completely gone or no longer used.","zh":"as dead as the dodo 是指徹底消失或不再使用。"},{"en":"Some people say handwritten letters are almost as dead as the dodo, though not everyone agrees.","zh":"有些人說手寫信幾乎早已不復存在，不過並非所有人都同意。"},{"en":"The phrase is strong because the dodo is a famous extinct bird.","zh":"這個短語很強烈，因為渡渡鳥是著名的滅絕鳥類。"},{"en":"It is used for things that feel totally finished or outdated.","zh":"它用於形容完全結束或過時的事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be used to refer to","meaning":"用來指……","examples":[{"en":"The saying is used to refer to something which no longer exists.","zh":"這句說法用來指不再存在的東西。"},{"en":"To be used to refer to something means to be used when talking about or identifying it.","zh":"be used to refer to something 是指用來談及或指認某事物。"},{"en":"The word “teenager” is used to refer to someone aged between thirteen and nineteen.","zh":"“teenager” 這個詞用來指13至19歲的人。"},{"en":"Expressions are useful because they refer to ideas quickly.","zh":"表達方式很有用，因為它們能快速指向某些概念。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what a word or saying points to.","zh":"這個短語解釋某個詞或說法指向甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"no longer exist","meaning":"不再存在","examples":[{"en":"The saying refers to something which no longer exists.","zh":"這句說法指不再存在的東西。"},{"en":"No longer exist means not exist anymore.","zh":"no longer exist 是指現在已不再存在。"},{"en":"Some old village paths no longer exist because new roads have replaced them.","zh":"有些舊村路因新道路取代而不再存在。"},{"en":"When something no longer exists, people may only know it through records or memories.","zh":"當某物不再存在，人們可能只能透過記錄或回憶認識它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disappearance from the present world.","zh":"這個短語描述某事物從現今世界消失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"alive and well","meaning":"健在；好好地生存","examples":[{"en":"For many centuries, the dodo was alive and well.","zh":"許多世紀以來，渡渡鳥都好好地生存。"},{"en":"Alive and well means living safely and in good condition.","zh":"alive and well 是指仍然活着，而且狀況良好。"},{"en":"A tradition may be alive and well if people still practise it every year.","zh":"如果人們每年仍實踐某個傳統，這傳統就是仍然健在。"},{"en":"The phrase often surprises listeners when they assumed something had disappeared.","zh":"當聽者原本以為某事已消失時，這個短語常帶來意外感。"},{"en":"It shows that something is still existing strongly.","zh":"它表示某事物仍然穩定存在。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for many centuries","meaning":"許多世紀以來","examples":[{"en":"For many centuries, the dodo lived on Mauritius.","zh":"許多世紀以來，渡渡鳥生活在毛里裘斯島。"},{"en":"For many centuries means for hundreds of years.","zh":"for many centuries 是指持續數百年。"},{"en":"For many centuries, people used horses for transport before cars became common.","zh":"汽車普及前，許多世紀以來人們都使用馬匹作交通工具。"},{"en":"A long period can make a species or tradition seem secure.","zh":"長時間存在會令一個物種或傳統看起來很穩固。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a very long duration.","zh":"這個短語強調非常長的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"could only be found in","meaning":"只能在……找到","examples":[{"en":"The dodo could only be found in one place.","zh":"渡渡鳥只能在一個地方找到。"},{"en":"Could only be found in means existed only in that particular place.","zh":"could only be found in 是指只存在於某個特定地方。"},{"en":"Some rare plants can only be found in one mountain region.","zh":"有些稀有植物只能在一個山區找到。"},{"en":"Species found in only one place are vulnerable if that habitat is damaged.","zh":"如果棲息地受損，只存在於一地的物種會很脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights limited distribution.","zh":"這個短語突出分布範圍有限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the island of Mauritius","meaning":"毛里裘斯島","examples":[{"en":"The dodo lived on the island of Mauritius.","zh":"渡渡鳥生活在毛里裘斯島。"},{"en":"The island of Mauritius is an island in the Indian Ocean.","zh":"毛里裘斯島是印度洋上的一座島。"},{"en":"Many island species develop differently because they are separated from other places.","zh":"許多島嶼物種因與其他地方分隔而有不同發展。"},{"en":"Islands can support unique wildlife, but small habitats can be easily disturbed.","zh":"島嶼可以孕育獨特野生動物，但小型棲息地容易受干擾。"},{"en":"This phrase names the dodo’s home.","zh":"這個短語指出渡渡鳥的家園。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Indian Ocean","meaning":"印度洋","examples":[{"en":"Mauritius is an island in the Indian Ocean.","zh":"毛里裘斯是印度洋上的一座島。"},{"en":"The Indian Ocean is the ocean between Africa, Asia, Australia, and the Southern Ocean.","zh":"Indian Ocean 是位於非洲、亞洲、澳洲和南冰洋之間的海洋。"},{"en":"Many trading ships crossed the Indian Ocean carrying spices and other goods.","zh":"許多商船橫渡印度洋，運送香料和其他貨物。"},{"en":"Ocean routes helped people travel, trade, and colonise distant islands.","zh":"海上航線幫助人們旅行、貿易和殖民遙遠島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the wider geographical location.","zh":"這個短語指出較大的地理位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"over the centuries","meaning":"數百年間","examples":[{"en":"Over the centuries, the dodo lost the ability to fly.","zh":"數百年間，渡渡鳥失去了飛行能力。"},{"en":"Over the centuries means gradually across hundreds of years.","zh":"over the centuries 是指在數百年間逐漸發生。"},{"en":"Over the centuries, city walls became less useful as weapons changed.","zh":"數百年間，隨着武器改變，城牆變得較不實用。"},{"en":"Long-term change can happen so slowly that people do not notice it at the time.","zh":"長期變化可以慢得令人當時沒有察覺。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for historical development.","zh":"這個短語用於描述歷史發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lose the ability to","meaning":"失去……的能力","examples":[{"en":"The dodo lost the ability to fly.","zh":"渡渡鳥失去了飛行能力。"},{"en":"To lose the ability to do something means to no longer be able to do it.","zh":"lose the ability to do something 是指不再能夠做某事。"},{"en":"A person may lose the ability to read small print as eyesight worsens.","zh":"視力變差時，人可能失去閱讀細小字體的能力。"},{"en":"Species can lose abilities when they no longer need them for survival.","zh":"當物種不再需要某些能力生存時，可能會失去它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change from being able to being unable.","zh":"這個短語描述從能夠變成不能夠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"survive happily","meaning":"安然生存","examples":[{"en":"The dodo survived happily under the trees.","zh":"渡渡鳥在樹木下安然生存。"},{"en":"To survive happily means to live successfully and comfortably.","zh":"survive happily 是指成功而舒適地生活。"},{"en":"A plant may survive happily in shade if it does not need much sunlight.","zh":"如果植物不需要太多陽光，它可能在陰涼處安然生長。"},{"en":"Animals survive happily when food, shelter, and safety are available.","zh":"當有食物、住所和安全，動物便能安然生存。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests life was stable before danger arrived.","zh":"這個短語暗示危險來臨前生活穩定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"under the trees","meaning":"在樹木下","examples":[{"en":"The dodo lived under the trees that covered the island.","zh":"渡渡鳥生活在覆蓋島嶼的樹木下。"},{"en":"Under the trees means beneath the shade or cover of trees.","zh":"under the trees 是指在樹蔭或樹木遮蓋之下。"},{"en":"Children may sit under the trees to stay cool during summer.","zh":"夏天時，孩子可能坐在樹下乘涼。"},{"en":"Animals may live under trees because they provide shade, shelter, and food.","zh":"動物可能生活在樹下，因為樹木提供陰影、庇護和食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a natural living space.","zh":"這個短語描述自然生活空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cover the island","meaning":"覆蓋整座島","examples":[{"en":"Trees once covered the island of Mauritius.","zh":"樹木曾經覆蓋整座毛里裘斯島。"},{"en":"To cover the island means to spread across most or all of the island.","zh":"cover the island 是指遍布整座或大部分島嶼。"},{"en":"Dense forest can cover an island and provide habitats for many species.","zh":"茂密森林可以覆蓋整座島，並為許多物種提供棲息地。"},{"en":"If forest cover is removed, animals may lose food and shelter.","zh":"如果森林覆蓋被移除，動物可能失去食物和庇護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the extent of natural vegetation.","zh":"這個短語描述自然植被的覆蓋範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Portuguese ships","meaning":"葡萄牙船隻","examples":[{"en":"The first Portuguese ships stopped at the island in 1507.","zh":"第一批葡萄牙船隻於1507年停靠在島上。"},{"en":"Portuguese ships were ships from Portugal or sailed by Portuguese crews.","zh":"Portuguese ships 是來自葡萄牙或由葡萄牙船員駕駛的船。"},{"en":"Portuguese ships travelled long distances during early ocean exploration.","zh":"葡萄牙船隻在早期海洋探索中長途航行。"},{"en":"Ships brought people, goods, animals, and new dangers to islands.","zh":"船隻把人、貨物、動物和新危險帶到島上。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the origin of the arriving vessels.","zh":"這個短語指出抵達船隻的來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stop at the island","meaning":"停靠在島上","examples":[{"en":"The first Portuguese ships stopped at the island.","zh":"第一批葡萄牙船隻停靠在島上。"},{"en":"To stop at the island means to pause or land there during a journey.","zh":"stop at the island 是指在旅途中暫停或登陸該島。"},{"en":"A ship may stop at an island to repair damage or collect supplies.","zh":"船隻可能停靠島上修理損壞或補充物資。"},{"en":"Stopping places were important on long voyages before modern engines and refrigeration.","zh":"在沒有現代引擎和冷藏技術的長途航程中，停靠點很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a temporary visit, not settlement.","zh":"這個短語描述暫時停留，而不是定居。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"carry spices back to","meaning":"將香料運回……","examples":[{"en":"The sailors were carrying spices back to Europe.","zh":"水手正在將香料運回歐洲。"},{"en":"To carry spices back to a place means to transport spices back there.","zh":"carry spices back to a place 是指把香料運回某地。"},{"en":"Traders carried tea and silk back to Europe along long trade routes.","zh":"商人沿着漫長貿易路線把茶葉和絲綢運回歐洲。"},{"en":"Valuable goods encouraged sailors to travel long and dangerous routes.","zh":"貴重貨物促使水手走上漫長而危險的航線。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transporting goods to a home market.","zh":"這個短語描述把貨物運回本地市場。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"convenient stopping place","meaning":"方便停靠的地方","examples":[{"en":"The sailors found Mauritius a convenient stopping place.","zh":"水手覺得毛里裘斯是方便停靠的地方。"},{"en":"A convenient stopping place is a useful location where travellers can rest or collect supplies.","zh":"convenient stopping place 是旅客可以休息或補充物資的有用地點。"},{"en":"A petrol station can be a convenient stopping place on a long drive.","zh":"長途駕車時，油站可以是方便停靠的地方。"},{"en":"Convenient stops reduce risk because travellers can get food, water, or repairs.","zh":"方便的停靠點能降低風險，因為旅客可取得食物、水或維修。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a location is useful during a journey.","zh":"這個短語解釋某地為何在旅途中有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stock up with","meaning":"補充；儲備","examples":[{"en":"The sailors could stock up with food and water.","zh":"水手可以補充食物和食水。"},{"en":"To stock up with something means to collect or buy enough supplies for later use.","zh":"stock up with something 是指收集或購買足夠物資以備日後使用。"},{"en":"Families may stock up with bottled water before a storm.","zh":"颱風前，家庭可能儲備樽裝水。"},{"en":"Travellers stock up when they will not find supplies easily later.","zh":"當旅客之後不容易找到物資時，便會補充儲備。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on preparing for future needs.","zh":"這個短語著重為未來需要作準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for the rest of","meaning":"為……餘下部分","examples":[{"en":"The sailors needed supplies for the rest of the voyage.","zh":"水手需要為餘下航程準備物資。"},{"en":"For the rest of something means for the remaining part of it.","zh":"for the rest of something 是指為某事剩餘的部分。"},{"en":"A student may save snacks for the rest of the school trip.","zh":"學生可能把小食留給學校旅行餘下部分。"},{"en":"Planning for the remaining journey helps prevent shortages later.","zh":"為剩餘旅程作計劃有助防止之後物資不足。"},{"en":"This phrase points to what is still left.","zh":"這個短語指向仍未完成的部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the voyage","meaning":"航程","examples":[{"en":"The sailors needed food and water for the rest of the voyage.","zh":"水手需要為餘下航程準備食物和食水。"},{"en":"A voyage is a long journey by sea or through space.","zh":"voyage 是海上或太空中的長途旅程。"},{"en":"In the past, a voyage from Asia to Europe could take many months.","zh":"過去，從亞洲到歐洲的航程可能需時數月。"},{"en":"Long voyages required careful planning because supplies could run out.","zh":"長途航程需要仔細規劃，因為物資可能耗盡。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than a short trip.","zh":"這個詞比短途旅行更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"settle on","meaning":"在……定居","examples":[{"en":"The Portuguese sailors did not settle on Mauritius.","zh":"葡萄牙水手沒有在毛里裘斯定居。"},{"en":"To settle on a place means to start living there permanently or for a long time.","zh":"settle on a place 是指開始在某地永久或長期生活。"},{"en":"Families may settle on an island if they build homes and farms there.","zh":"如果家庭在島上建屋和耕作，他們可能就在島上定居。"},{"en":"Visiting a place is different from settling there.","zh":"到訪某地與在那裏定居不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a place one’s home.","zh":"這個短語描述把某地變成自己的家。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"set up a colony","meaning":"建立殖民地","examples":[{"en":"The Dutch arrived and set up a colony there.","zh":"荷蘭人到達並在那裏建立殖民地。"},{"en":"To set up a colony means to establish a settlement controlled by people from another country.","zh":"set up a colony 是指建立由另一國人民控制的定居地。"},{"en":"European powers set up colonies in many parts of the world during the age of exploration.","zh":"在大航海時代，歐洲勢力在世界許多地方建立殖民地。"},{"en":"Colonies changed local land use, economies, and wildlife.","zh":"殖民地改變了當地土地使用、經濟和野生動物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes political settlement and control.","zh":"這個短語描述政治上的定居與控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"human inhabitants","meaning":"人類居民","examples":[{"en":"The first human inhabitants found the dodo a source of meat.","zh":"最早的人類居民發現渡渡鳥是一種肉類來源。"},{"en":"Human inhabitants are people who live in a particular place.","zh":"human inhabitants 是居住在某個地方的人。"},{"en":"The first human inhabitants of an island often change its environment.","zh":"一座島上的最早人類居民往往會改變其環境。"},{"en":"When humans arrive in a new habitat, local animals may face new threats.","zh":"當人類到達新棲息地，當地動物可能面對新威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts people with the animals already living there.","zh":"這個短語把人類與原本生活在當地的動物作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"source of meat","meaning":"肉類來源","examples":[{"en":"The dodo became a convenient source of meat.","zh":"渡渡鳥成為方便的肉類來源。"},{"en":"A source of meat is an animal or food supply used for meat.","zh":"source of meat 是指用來供應肉類的動物或食物來源。"},{"en":"Chickens are a common source of meat in many countries.","zh":"雞在許多國家都是常見肉類來源。"},{"en":"When sailors needed food, large flightless birds seemed easy to use as meat.","zh":"當水手需要食物時，大型不會飛的鳥似乎容易被用作肉食。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical food supply.","zh":"這個短語著重實際食物供應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"not everyone liked","meaning":"不是每個人都喜歡","examples":[{"en":"Not everyone liked the taste of the dodo.","zh":"不是每個人都喜歡渡渡鳥的味道。"},{"en":"Not everyone liked means some people liked it, but others did not.","zh":"not everyone liked 是指有些人喜歡，但另一些人不喜歡。"},{"en":"Not everyone likes spicy food, even if it is popular.","zh":"即使辛辣食物很受歡迎，也不是每個人都喜歡。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids making an overgeneral statement.","zh":"這個短語避免作出過度概括。"},{"en":"It shows that opinions were mixed.","zh":"它顯示意見並不一致。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"accurate description","meaning":"準確描述","examples":[{"en":"It is hard to get an accurate description of the dodo.","zh":"要得到渡渡鳥的準確描述很困難。"},{"en":"An accurate description is a correct and reliable explanation of what something is like.","zh":"accurate description 是對某物樣子的正確而可靠說明。"},{"en":"Police need an accurate description of a missing bag to find it.","zh":"警方需要失物的準確描述，才能找到它。"},{"en":"Without clear evidence, descriptions can be exaggerated or mistaken.","zh":"沒有清楚證據，描述可能被誇大或出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on correctness.","zh":"這個短語著重正確性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"actually looked like","meaning":"真正長甚麼樣子","examples":[{"en":"It is hard to know what the dodo actually looked like.","zh":"很難知道渡渡鳥真正長甚麼樣子。"},{"en":"Actually looked like means what something really looked like, not what people imagined.","zh":"actually looked like 是指某物真實外貌，而不是人們想像的樣子。"},{"en":"Historians use paintings and bones to understand what ancient animals actually looked like.","zh":"歷史學家利用畫作和骨骼了解古代動物真正長甚麼樣子。"},{"en":"Images from the past may be inaccurate, so evidence must be compared.","zh":"過去的圖像可能不準確，所以必須比較證據。"},{"en":"This phrase separates reality from artistic impression.","zh":"這個短語把現實與藝術印象分開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"written records","meaning":"文字記錄","examples":[{"en":"There are some written records from sailors.","zh":"有一些來自水手的文字記錄。"},{"en":"Written records are information written down in documents, journals, or reports.","zh":"written records 是寫在文件、日記或報告中的資料。"},{"en":"Old written records can help historians learn about past events.","zh":"舊文字記錄可以幫助歷史學家了解過去事件。"},{"en":"Records are useful, but they may reflect the writer’s mistakes or bias.","zh":"記錄有用，但也可能反映作者的錯誤或偏見。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to text evidence from the past.","zh":"這個短語指來自過去的文字證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reliable","meaning":"可靠的","examples":[{"en":"We do not know how reliable the records are.","zh":"我們不知道這些記錄有多可靠。"},{"en":"Reliable means trustworthy and likely to be correct.","zh":"reliable 是指值得信任，而且很可能正確。"},{"en":"A reliable witness gives information that matches other evidence.","zh":"可靠證人提供的資料會與其他證據相符。"},{"en":"Sources may be unreliable if they are based on memory, rumour, or exaggeration.","zh":"如果資料來源基於記憶、傳聞或誇張，它可能不可靠。"},{"en":"This word is important when judging evidence.","zh":"這個詞在判斷證據時很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"best-known picture","meaning":"最著名的圖片","examples":[{"en":"The best-known picture of the dodo is a Dutch painting.","zh":"渡渡鳥最著名的圖片是一幅荷蘭畫作。"},{"en":"Best-known picture means the image most people recognise or remember.","zh":"best-known picture 是最多人認識或記得的圖像。"},{"en":"The best-known picture of the Mona Lisa is the portrait in the Louvre.","zh":"蒙娜麗莎最著名的圖片是羅浮宮中的那幅肖像。"},{"en":"Famous images can shape public imagination, even if they are not fully accurate.","zh":"著名圖像可以塑造公眾想像，即使它們未必完全準確。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the most widely recognised image.","zh":"這個短語指出最廣為人知的圖像。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Dutch painting","meaning":"荷蘭畫作","examples":[{"en":"A Dutch painting shows the dodo as an extremely fat bird.","zh":"一幅荷蘭畫作把渡渡鳥畫成非常肥胖的鳥。"},{"en":"A Dutch painting is a painting made by a Dutch artist or from the Netherlands.","zh":"Dutch painting 是由荷蘭畫家創作或來自荷蘭的畫作。"},{"en":"Old Dutch paintings often show ships, merchants, homes, and animals.","zh":"舊荷蘭畫作常展示船隻、商人、家居和動物。"},{"en":"Paintings can preserve details, but artists may also change what they see.","zh":"畫作可以保存細節，但藝術家也可能改變所見之物。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the origin or style of the artwork.","zh":"這個短語指出藝術品的來源或風格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"appear to be","meaning":"看起來是……","examples":[{"en":"In the Dutch painting, the bird appears to be extremely fat.","zh":"在荷蘭畫作中，那隻鳥看起來非常肥胖。"},{"en":"To appear to be something means to seem to be that way.","zh":"appear to be something 是指看起來似乎是那樣。"},{"en":"The water appears to be clean, but it still needs testing.","zh":"這些水看起來很乾淨，但仍需要測試。"},{"en":"Appearances can be misleading when evidence is incomplete.","zh":"當證據不完整，外表可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a judgement is based on what is seen.","zh":"這個短語顯示判斷是基於所見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"extremely fat","meaning":"非常肥胖","examples":[{"en":"The dodo appears to be extremely fat in the painting.","zh":"渡渡鳥在畫作中看起來非常肥胖。"},{"en":"Extremely fat means very large and heavy in body shape.","zh":"extremely fat 是指體型非常大和肥重。"},{"en":"An animal in a painting may look extremely fat if the artist exaggerates its size.","zh":"如果藝術家誇大動物體型，畫中的動物可能看起來非常肥胖。"},{"en":"Describing an extinct animal as extremely fat may affect how people imagine it.","zh":"把滅絕動物描述成非常肥胖，可能影響人們如何想像它。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly describes body size.","zh":"這個短語強烈描述身體大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"may not be accurate","meaning":"可能並不準確","examples":[{"en":"The Dutch painting may not be accurate.","zh":"這幅荷蘭畫作可能並不準確。"},{"en":"May not be accurate means may not be correct or true to reality.","zh":"may not be accurate 是指可能不正確或不符合現實。"},{"en":"A memory from childhood may not be accurate after many years.","zh":"多年後，童年記憶可能並不準確。"},{"en":"Historical sources may need checking against other evidence.","zh":"歷史資料可能需要與其他證據核對。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses uncertainty about correctness.","zh":"這個短語表達對正確性的懷疑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同一時期","examples":[{"en":"An Indian painting done at the same time shows a thinner bird.","zh":"同一時期完成的一幅印度畫作展示一隻較瘦的鳥。"},{"en":"At the same time means during the same period.","zh":"at the same time 是指在同一段時期。"},{"en":"Two newspapers published reports at the same time but described the event differently.","zh":"兩份報紙同一時期刊登報道，但對事件描述不同。"},{"en":"Comparing sources from the same time can reveal disagreement.","zh":"比較同一時期的資料來源可以揭示分歧。"},{"en":"This phrase links events or works by time.","zh":"這個短語以時間連繫事件或作品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a much thinner bird","meaning":"瘦得多的鳥","examples":[{"en":"The Indian painting shows a much thinner bird.","zh":"這幅印度畫作展示一隻瘦得多的鳥。"},{"en":"A much thinner bird means a bird with a far slimmer body.","zh":"a much thinner bird 是指身體苗條得多的鳥。"},{"en":"The second drawing shows a much thinner animal than the first one.","zh":"第二幅畫展示的動物比第一幅瘦得多。"},{"en":"Different pictures can create very different ideas about the same species.","zh":"不同圖片可以令人對同一物種產生很不同的想像。"},{"en":"This phrase compares body shape strongly.","zh":"這個短語強烈比較身形。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"attempts were made to","meaning":"有人嘗試去……","examples":[{"en":"Attempts were made to preserve the bodies of some dodos.","zh":"有人嘗試保存一些渡渡鳥的屍體。"},{"en":"Attempts were made to do something means people tried to do it.","zh":"attempts were made to do something 是指有人嘗試做某事。"},{"en":"Attempts were made to save the old library after the roof collapsed.","zh":"舊圖書館屋頂倒塌後，有人嘗試拯救它。"},{"en":"This passive phrase focuses on the effort rather than naming who did it.","zh":"這個被動短語著重努力本身，而不是指出誰做。"},{"en":"It often appears in historical or formal writing.","zh":"它常見於歷史或正式寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"preserve the bodies of","meaning":"保存……的屍體","examples":[{"en":"People tried to preserve the bodies of some dodos.","zh":"人們嘗試保存一些渡渡鳥的屍體。"},{"en":"To preserve the bodies of animals means to keep them from decaying so they can be studied or displayed.","zh":"preserve the bodies of animals 是指防止動物屍體腐爛，以便研究或展示。"},{"en":"Museums may preserve the bodies of rare animals for scientific collections.","zh":"博物館可能保存稀有動物的屍體作科學收藏。"},{"en":"Preservation is difficult because soft tissue decays quickly.","zh":"保存很困難，因為軟組織會很快腐爛。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to keeping physical remains.","zh":"這個短語指保存實體遺骸。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"complete specimen","meaning":"完整標本","examples":[{"en":"No complete specimen of the dodo survives.","zh":"沒有完整的渡渡鳥標本保存至今。"},{"en":"A complete specimen is a whole preserved example of an animal, plant, or object.","zh":"complete specimen 是完整保存下來的動物、植物或物件樣本。"},{"en":"A museum may have a complete specimen of a rare butterfly.","zh":"博物館可能有一個稀有蝴蝶的完整標本。"},{"en":"Without a complete specimen, scientists must study fragments, pictures, and written records.","zh":"沒有完整標本，科學家必須研究碎片、圖像和文字記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in natural history and research.","zh":"這個短語常見於自然史和研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the early 17th century","meaning":"在17世紀初","examples":[{"en":"In the early 17th century, four dried parts of a dodo were known to exist.","zh":"在17世紀初，據知有四個渡渡鳥乾燥身體部位存在。"},{"en":"In the early 17th century means in the early years of the 1600s.","zh":"in the early 17th century 是指1600年代早期。"},{"en":"In the early 17th century, European ships were travelling widely for trade.","zh":"在17世紀初，歐洲船隻已廣泛進行貿易航行。"},{"en":"Giving the century helps place events in historical time.","zh":"指出世紀有助把事件放入歷史時間。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an approximate historical period.","zh":"這個短語指大概的歷史時期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dried parts","meaning":"乾燥的身體部位","examples":[{"en":"Four dried parts of a dodo were known to exist.","zh":"據知有四個渡渡鳥乾燥身體部位存在。"},{"en":"Dried parts are body parts preserved after moisture has been removed.","zh":"dried parts 是去除水分後保存下來的身體部位。"},{"en":"Museums may keep dried parts of plants, insects, or animals for study.","zh":"博物館可能保存植物、昆蟲或動物的乾燥部位作研究。"},{"en":"Dried remains can survive longer than soft tissue, but they can still be lost or damaged.","zh":"乾燥遺骸比軟組織保存更久，但仍可能遺失或受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preserved fragments, not a whole body.","zh":"這個短語描述保存下來的碎片，而不是整具身體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be known to exist","meaning":"據知存在","examples":[{"en":"Four dried parts of a dodo were known to exist.","zh":"據知有四個渡渡鳥乾燥身體部位存在。"},{"en":"To be known to exist means people have evidence that something exists.","zh":"be known to exist 是指人們有證據知道某物存在。"},{"en":"Only a few original copies of the book are known to exist.","zh":"據知只有幾本該書的原版仍存在。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when something is rare and carefully recorded.","zh":"當某物稀有並被仔細記錄時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It focuses on confirmed existence.","zh":"它著重已確認的存在。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"disappear","meaning":"消失","examples":[{"en":"Three of the four dried parts have disappeared.","zh":"四個乾燥身體部位中有三個已經消失。"},{"en":"To disappear means to become lost, unseen, or no longer present.","zh":"disappear 是指遺失、看不見或不再存在於原處。"},{"en":"A file may disappear from a computer if it is deleted by mistake.","zh":"如果電腦檔案被誤刪，它可能會消失。"},{"en":"Historical objects can disappear through damage, theft, neglect, or war.","zh":"歷史物件可能因損壞、盜竊、忽視或戰爭而消失。"},{"en":"This verb shows that something once existed but cannot now be found.","zh":"這個動詞顯示某物曾經存在，但現在找不到。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"soft tissue","meaning":"軟組織","examples":[{"en":"Only one example of soft tissue from the dodo survives.","zh":"只有一個渡渡鳥軟組織樣本保存至今。"},{"en":"Soft tissue means body material such as skin, muscle, or organs, not bone.","zh":"soft tissue 是指皮膚、肌肉或器官等身體組織，而不是骨頭。"},{"en":"Soft tissue usually decays faster than bones after an animal dies.","zh":"動物死亡後，軟組織通常比骨頭腐爛得更快。"},{"en":"Preserved soft tissue can give scientists rare information about extinct animals.","zh":"保存下來的軟組織可以給科學家關於滅絕動物的珍貴資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in biology and medicine.","zh":"這個短語常見於生物學和醫學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bones have been found","meaning":"骨頭已被發現","examples":[{"en":"Bones of the dodo have also been found.","zh":"渡渡鳥的骨頭也已被發現。"},{"en":"Bones have been found means remains of the skeleton have been discovered.","zh":"bones have been found 是指骨骼遺骸已被發現。"},{"en":"Dinosaur bones have been found in many parts of the world.","zh":"世界許多地方都已發現恐龍骨頭。"},{"en":"Found bones help scientists reconstruct the size, movement, and life of an animal.","zh":"發現的骨頭幫助科學家重建動物的大小、活動和生活。"},{"en":"This phrase reports a scientific discovery.","zh":"這個短語報告科學發現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"complete skeleton","meaning":"完整骨架","examples":[{"en":"There is only one complete skeleton of the dodo in existence.","zh":"現存只有一副完整渡渡鳥骨架。"},{"en":"A complete skeleton is the full set of bones of an animal.","zh":"complete skeleton 是動物完整的一套骨頭。"},{"en":"A complete skeleton lets scientists study body shape more accurately.","zh":"完整骨架讓科學家更準確研究身體形態。"},{"en":"Without complete skeletons, researchers must guess from separate bones.","zh":"沒有完整骨架，研究人員只能從分散骨頭推測。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in fossil and museum studies.","zh":"這個短語在化石和博物館研究中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in existence","meaning":"現存","examples":[{"en":"Only one complete dodo skeleton is in existence.","zh":"現存只有一副完整渡渡鳥骨架。"},{"en":"In existence means currently existing or still present.","zh":"in existence 是指目前仍然存在。"},{"en":"Only a few copies of the original map are still in existence.","zh":"原版地圖現存只有少數幾份。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for rare objects or records.","zh":"這個短語常用於稀有物件或記錄。"},{"en":"It emphasises that something has survived until now.","zh":"它強調某物保存至今。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be the subject of","meaning":"成為……的研究對象","examples":[{"en":"The dodo skeleton has recently been the subject of scientific research.","zh":"渡渡鳥骨架最近成為科學研究對象。"},{"en":"To be the subject of research means to be what researchers study.","zh":"be the subject of research 是指成為研究人員研究的對象。"},{"en":"Air pollution has been the subject of many health studies.","zh":"空氣污染一直是許多健康研究的對象。"},{"en":"When something becomes the subject of research, experts examine it carefully.","zh":"當某物成為研究對象，專家會仔細檢查它。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the focus of investigation.","zh":"這個短語指出調查焦點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"scientific research","meaning":"科學研究","examples":[{"en":"The skeleton has been examined in scientific research.","zh":"這副骨架已在科學研究中被檢查。"},{"en":"Scientific research is careful study using evidence, observation, and testing.","zh":"scientific research 是使用證據、觀察和測試進行的仔細研究。"},{"en":"Scientific research can help correct old beliefs about animals.","zh":"科學研究可以幫助修正關於動物的舊看法。"},{"en":"Research findings are stronger when they are based on physical evidence.","zh":"研究結果如果基於實體證據，會更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to systematic investigation.","zh":"這個短語指有系統的調查。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"顯示；表明","examples":[{"en":"The research suggests that earlier beliefs about dodos were incorrect.","zh":"研究顯示，關於渡渡鳥的早期看法是不正確的。"},{"en":"Suggest that means indicate or show that something may be true.","zh":"suggest that 是指顯示或表明某事可能是真的。"},{"en":"The test results suggest that the water is not safe to drink.","zh":"測試結果顯示這些水不適合飲用。"},{"en":"Researchers use this phrase when evidence points to a conclusion but may not prove everything absolutely.","zh":"當證據指向某結論但未必絕對證明所有事情時，研究人員會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It is careful academic language.","zh":"這是謹慎的學術用語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"earlier beliefs about","meaning":"關於……的早期看法","examples":[{"en":"Many earlier beliefs about dodos may have been incorrect.","zh":"許多關於渡渡鳥的早期看法可能一直是錯誤的。"},{"en":"Earlier beliefs about something are ideas people held in the past.","zh":"earlier beliefs about something 是人們過去持有的想法。"},{"en":"Earlier beliefs about disease changed when scientists discovered bacteria.","zh":"當科學家發現細菌後，關於疾病的早期看法改變了。"},{"en":"New evidence can challenge older beliefs.","zh":"新證據可以挑戰舊有看法。"},{"en":"This phrase compares past understanding with newer knowledge.","zh":"這個短語把過去理解與較新知識作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"may have been incorrect","meaning":"可能一直是錯誤的","examples":[{"en":"Earlier beliefs about dodos may have been incorrect.","zh":"關於渡渡鳥的早期看法可能一直是錯誤的。"},{"en":"May have been incorrect means may have been wrong in the past.","zh":"may have been incorrect 是指過去可能是錯的。"},{"en":"The old map may have been incorrect because the coastline was drawn badly.","zh":"舊地圖可能一直不準確，因為海岸線畫得不好。"},{"en":"This phrase is cautious because the speaker is not claiming absolute certainty.","zh":"這個短語很謹慎，因為說話者不是宣稱絕對肯定。"},{"en":"It is useful when new evidence questions old ideas.","zh":"當新證據質疑舊想法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"early accounts of","meaning":"關於……的早期記載","examples":[{"en":"Early accounts of the birds described them as slow and clumsy.","zh":"關於這些鳥的早期記載把牠們描述成緩慢而笨拙。"},{"en":"Early accounts of something are old descriptions or reports about it.","zh":"early accounts of something 是關於某事的舊描述或報告。"},{"en":"Early accounts of a city may describe streets that no longer exist.","zh":"關於一座城市的早期記載可能描述現已不存在的街道。"},{"en":"Such accounts can be useful, but they may contain mistakes.","zh":"這些記載可能有用，但也可能包含錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to historical written or spoken descriptions.","zh":"這個短語指歷史上的文字或口頭描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"mention how","meaning":"提到……有多……","examples":[{"en":"Early accounts mention how slow and clumsy the dodo was.","zh":"早期記載提到渡渡鳥有多緩慢和笨拙。"},{"en":"To mention how something was means to refer to the degree or manner of it.","zh":"mention how something was 是指提及某事的程度或方式。"},{"en":"A report may mention how quickly a fire spread through a building.","zh":"報告可能提到火勢在建築物中蔓延得有多快。"},{"en":"Mentioning details helps readers picture the situation more clearly.","zh":"提及細節有助讀者更清楚想像情況。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a described quality.","zh":"這個短語引入被描述的特質。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"slow and clumsy","meaning":"緩慢而笨拙","examples":[{"en":"The dodo was once thought to be slow and clumsy.","zh":"渡渡鳥曾被認為緩慢而笨拙。"},{"en":"Slow and clumsy means moving slowly and awkwardly.","zh":"slow and clumsy 是指動作慢，而且不靈活。"},{"en":"A person carrying too many boxes may look slow and clumsy on the stairs.","zh":"一個人拿着太多箱子上樓梯時，可能看起來緩慢而笨拙。"},{"en":"If an animal is slow and clumsy, people may think it is easy to catch.","zh":"如果動物緩慢而笨拙，人們可能以為牠容易捕捉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement and coordination.","zh":"這個短語描述移動和協調能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"strong knee joints","meaning":"強壯的膝關節","examples":[{"en":"The dodo’s strong knee joints may have allowed it to move quickly.","zh":"渡渡鳥強壯的膝關節可能讓牠快速移動。"},{"en":"Strong knee joints are powerful joints in the legs that support movement.","zh":"strong knee joints 是腿部中支撐活動的有力關節。"},{"en":"Athletes need strong knee joints for running, jumping, and changing direction.","zh":"運動員需要強壯的膝關節來跑步、跳躍和轉向。"},{"en":"Strong joints can help an animal move over rough ground.","zh":"強壯關節可以幫助動物越過崎嶇地面。"},{"en":"This phrase links body structure with movement ability.","zh":"這個短語把身體結構與移動能力連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make it capable of","meaning":"使其能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The bird’s strong knee joints made it capable of fast movement.","zh":"這種鳥強壯的膝關節使其能夠快速移動。"},{"en":"To make it capable of something means to give it the ability to do that thing.","zh":"make it capable of something 是指讓它有能力做到某事。"},{"en":"Strong tyres make a bicycle capable of travelling on rough paths.","zh":"結實輪胎使單車能夠在崎嶇小路上行駛。"},{"en":"Physical features can make an animal capable of actions people did not expect.","zh":"身體特徵可以使動物能夠做出人們意想不到的行動。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with an ability.","zh":"這個短語把原因與能力連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"movement","meaning":"移動","examples":[{"en":"The dodo was capable of movement that was quite fast.","zh":"渡渡鳥能夠作出相當快的移動。"},{"en":"Movement means the act or ability of moving from one place or position to another.","zh":"movement 是指從一個地方或姿勢移到另一個地方或姿勢的動作或能力。"},{"en":"Exercise improves movement by strengthening muscles and joints.","zh":"運動透過強化肌肉和關節改善移動能力。"},{"en":"Studying an animal’s bones can reveal how it moved.","zh":"研究動物骨骼可以揭示牠如何移動。"},{"en":"This word is about physical motion.","zh":"這個詞關於身體動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"quite fast","meaning":"相當快","examples":[{"en":"The dodo may actually have moved quite fast.","zh":"渡渡鳥實際上可能移動得相當快。"},{"en":"Quite fast means fairly quick or faster than expected.","zh":"quite fast 是指相當快速，或比預期快。"},{"en":"A child may become quite fast on a bicycle after a few weeks of practice.","zh":"孩子練習幾星期後，踩單車可能變得相當快。"},{"en":"If the dodo moved quite fast, old descriptions of it as clumsy may be misleading.","zh":"如果渡渡鳥移動得相當快，把牠描述為笨拙的舊說法可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a moderate but clear degree of speed.","zh":"這個短語給出中等但清楚的速度程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"17th-century sailor","meaning":"17世紀水手","examples":[{"en":"One 17th-century sailor found the birds hard to catch.","zh":"一名17世紀水手覺得這些鳥難以捕捉。"},{"en":"A 17th-century sailor was a person working on ships in the 1600s.","zh":"17th-century sailor 是1600年代在船上工作的人。"},{"en":"A 17th-century sailor might write about animals seen during long voyages.","zh":"17世紀水手可能記錄長途航行中見到的動物。"},{"en":"Sailors’ accounts can provide historical evidence, though not always accurate evidence.","zh":"水手記載可以提供歷史證據，但不一定完全準確。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both time period and occupation.","zh":"這個短語同時指出時期和職業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hard to catch","meaning":"難以捕捉","examples":[{"en":"One sailor found the dodos hard to catch.","zh":"一名水手覺得渡渡鳥難以捕捉。"},{"en":"Hard to catch means difficult to capture or get hold of.","zh":"hard to catch 是指難以捕獲或抓住。"},{"en":"A fast chicken in a garden can be hard to catch.","zh":"花園中跑得快的雞可能很難捕捉。"},{"en":"If an animal is hard to catch, it may be quicker or more alert than people think.","zh":"如果動物難以捕捉，牠可能比人們想像中更快或更警覺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulty in capturing something.","zh":"這個短語描述捕捉上的困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"it is true that","meaning":"的確","examples":[{"en":"It is true that the dodo’s small wings could not lift it off the ground.","zh":"渡渡鳥的小翅膀的確不能把牠帶離地面。"},{"en":"It is true that introduces a fact the speaker accepts before adding more information.","zh":"it is true that 用來引入說話者接受的事實，然後再補充其他資料。"},{"en":"It is true that online learning is convenient, but some students miss classroom discussion.","zh":"網上學習的確方便，但有些學生掛念課堂討論。"},{"en":"This phrase helps make an argument balanced.","zh":"這個短語有助令論點較平衡。"},{"en":"It often appears before a contrast or qualification.","zh":"它常出現在對比或補充限制之前。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"small wings","meaning":"小翅膀","examples":[{"en":"The dodo had small wings.","zh":"渡渡鳥有小翅膀。"},{"en":"Small wings are wings that are short or not large compared with the body.","zh":"small wings 是相對於身體較短或不大的翅膀。"},{"en":"Some flightless birds have small wings because they no longer need to fly.","zh":"有些不會飛的鳥有小翅膀，因為牠們不再需要飛行。"},{"en":"Wing size affects whether a bird can lift itself into the air.","zh":"翅膀大小會影響鳥能否把自己升到空中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical feature of the bird.","zh":"這個短語描述鳥的身體特徵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"leave the ground","meaning":"離開地面","examples":[{"en":"The dodo’s wings would not have allowed it to leave the ground.","zh":"渡渡鳥的翅膀不會讓牠離開地面。"},{"en":"To leave the ground means to rise into the air.","zh":"leave the ground 是指升到空中。"},{"en":"A plane leaves the ground when it takes off from the runway.","zh":"飛機從跑道起飛時會離開地面。"},{"en":"Birds need enough wing power to leave the ground and fly.","zh":"鳥需要足夠翅膀力量才能離開地面飛行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the start of flight.","zh":"這個短語描述飛行的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be employed for","meaning":"被用於……","examples":[{"en":"The wings were probably employed for balance.","zh":"這些翅膀可能被用於保持平衡。"},{"en":"To be employed for something means to be used for that purpose.","zh":"be employed for something 是指被用於某個目的。"},{"en":"A walking stick may be employed for support on uneven paths.","zh":"手杖可能被用於在不平小路上支撐身體。"},{"en":"Body parts can have uses other than their original or most obvious function.","zh":"身體部位可以有原本或最明顯功能以外的用途。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and means “be used for”.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是 be used for。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"balance","meaning":"平衡","examples":[{"en":"The dodo’s wings may have been used for balance.","zh":"渡渡鳥的翅膀可能被用來保持平衡。"},{"en":"Balance is the ability to keep steady without falling.","zh":"balance 是保持穩定而不跌倒的能力。"},{"en":"Cyclists need balance to stay upright on a bike.","zh":"單車手需要平衡才能在單車上保持直立。"},{"en":"Animals moving over rough ground need balance to avoid falling.","zh":"動物越過崎嶇地面時需要平衡，以免跌倒。"},{"en":"This word describes physical steadiness.","zh":"這個詞描述身體穩定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"while going over","meaning":"在越過……時","examples":[{"en":"The wings may have helped the bird while going over uneven ground.","zh":"翅膀可能在渡渡鳥越過不平地面時幫助牠。"},{"en":"While going over something means during the action of crossing or moving across it.","zh":"while going over something 是指在越過或橫過某物期間。"},{"en":"Hikers use walking poles while going over rocky ground.","zh":"遠足人士在越過多石地面時會使用行山杖。"},{"en":"Extra balance helps when moving across difficult surfaces.","zh":"在困難表面上移動時，額外平衡很有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase links an action with a situation happening at the same time.","zh":"這個短語把一個動作與同時發生的情況連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"uneven ground","meaning":"不平地面","examples":[{"en":"The dodo may have used its wings for balance on uneven ground.","zh":"渡渡鳥可能在不平地面上用翅膀保持平衡。"},{"en":"Uneven ground is ground that is not flat or smooth.","zh":"uneven ground 是不平坦或不平滑的地面。"},{"en":"Running on uneven ground can increase the risk of twisting an ankle.","zh":"在不平地面上跑步可能增加扭傷腳踝的風險。"},{"en":"Animals need good balance to move over uneven ground safely.","zh":"動物需要良好平衡，才能安全越過不平地面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a difficult walking surface.","zh":"這個短語描述難行的地面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"carry out analysis of","meaning":"對……進行分析","examples":[{"en":"Another group of scientists carried out analysis of the dodo’s skull.","zh":"另一組科學家對渡渡鳥頭骨進行分析。"},{"en":"To carry out analysis of something means to examine it carefully and systematically.","zh":"carry out analysis of something 是指仔細而有系統地檢查某物。"},{"en":"Doctors may carry out analysis of blood samples to check for disease.","zh":"醫生可能對血液樣本進行分析，以檢查疾病。"},{"en":"Careful analysis can reveal information that is not obvious at first sight.","zh":"仔細分析可以揭示一開始不明顯的資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in research.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常見於研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"skull","meaning":"頭骨","examples":[{"en":"Scientists analysed the dodo’s skull.","zh":"科學家分析了渡渡鳥的頭骨。"},{"en":"A skull is the bone structure of the head that protects the brain.","zh":"skull 是保護大腦的頭部骨骼結構。"},{"en":"Animal skulls can show the size of the brain and the shape of the senses.","zh":"動物頭骨可以顯示大腦大小和感官形狀。"},{"en":"Studying skulls helps scientists understand feeding, movement, and intelligence.","zh":"研究頭骨幫助科學家了解進食、活動和智力。"},{"en":"This word refers to a key part of the skeleton.","zh":"這個詞指骨架中的重要部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lack of intelligence","meaning":"缺乏智力","examples":[{"en":"Reports of the dodo’s lack of intelligence were not supported by research.","zh":"關於渡渡鳥缺乏智力的報道並未得到研究支持。"},{"en":"Lack of intelligence means having little ability to learn, reason, or solve problems.","zh":"lack of intelligence 是指學習、推理或解決問題的能力低。"},{"en":"It is unfair to assume an animal has a lack of intelligence without evidence.","zh":"沒有證據就假設動物缺乏智力是不公平的。"},{"en":"Research can challenge old labels based on appearance or prejudice.","zh":"研究可以挑戰基於外表或偏見的舊標籤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a claimed weakness in mental ability.","zh":"這個短語描述一種被指稱的智力弱點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be borne out by","meaning":"得到……證實","examples":[{"en":"The reports were not borne out by the research.","zh":"這些報道並未得到研究證實。"},{"en":"To be borne out by evidence means to be supported or confirmed by it.","zh":"be borne out by evidence 是指得到證據支持或確認。"},{"en":"The witness’s story was borne out by camera footage.","zh":"證人的說法得到閉路電視片段證實。"},{"en":"If a claim is not borne out by research, people should be careful about believing it.","zh":"如果某說法未得到研究證實，人們應小心相信。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used with evidence.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常與證據一起使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"average in size","meaning":"大小屬平均","examples":[{"en":"The dodo’s brain was average in size.","zh":"渡渡鳥的大腦大小屬平均。"},{"en":"Average in size means neither unusually large nor unusually small.","zh":"average in size 是指既不特別大，也不特別小。"},{"en":"A class may be average in size if it has about the usual number of students.","zh":"如果一班學生人數大約符合一般水平，班級大小便屬平均。"},{"en":"Calling something average in size does not mean it is unimportant.","zh":"說某物大小屬平均，不代表它不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase compares size with a normal standard.","zh":"這個短語把大小與正常標準作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in relation to","meaning":"相對於……","examples":[{"en":"In relation to its body size, the dodo’s brain was similar to that of a pigeon.","zh":"相對於身體大小，渡渡鳥的大腦與鴿子的相似。"},{"en":"In relation to means compared with or considered together with something else.","zh":"in relation to 是指與某物比較，或與某物一併考慮。"},{"en":"A child’s schoolbag may be too heavy in relation to their body size.","zh":"相對於孩子的身體大小，書包可能太重。"},{"en":"Comparing one feature in relation to another gives a fairer judgement.","zh":"把一個特徵相對於另一特徵比較，可以得到較公平判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for careful comparison.","zh":"這個短語用於仔細比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"body size","meaning":"身體大小","examples":[{"en":"The dodo’s brain was average in relation to its body size.","zh":"相對於身體大小，渡渡鳥的大腦大小屬平均。"},{"en":"Body size means the overall physical size of an animal or person.","zh":"body size 是指動物或人的整體身體尺寸。"},{"en":"A small dog and a large dog may need different amounts of food because of body size.","zh":"小狗和大狗因身體大小不同，可能需要不同食量。"},{"en":"Scientists compare brain size with body size to judge animal intelligence more fairly.","zh":"科學家把大腦大小與身體大小比較，以較公平判斷動物智力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to total physical scale.","zh":"這個短語指整體身體規模。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"similar to that of","meaning":"與……的相似","examples":[{"en":"The dodo’s brain was similar to that of the pigeon.","zh":"渡渡鳥的大腦與鴿子的大腦相似。"},{"en":"Similar to that of means like the one belonging to another person, animal, or thing.","zh":"similar to that of 是指與另一人、動物或事物所擁有的東西相似。"},{"en":"The school’s timetable is similar to that of many other local schools.","zh":"這間學校的時間表與許多本地學校的相似。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the same noun twice.","zh":"這個短語避免重複同一名詞兩次。"},{"en":"It is useful in formal comparisons.","zh":"它適合用於正式比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"highly intelligent bird","meaning":"高度聰明的鳥","examples":[{"en":"The pigeon is known to be a highly intelligent bird.","zh":"鴿子被認為是高度聰明的鳥。"},{"en":"A highly intelligent bird is a bird with strong learning and problem-solving ability.","zh":"highly intelligent bird 是具有強大學習和解難能力的鳥。"},{"en":"Crows are often described as highly intelligent birds because they can use tools.","zh":"烏鴉常被形容為高度聰明的鳥，因為牠們會使用工具。"},{"en":"Intelligence in birds may appear in memory, navigation, or recognising patterns.","zh":"鳥類智力可能表現在記憶、導航或辨認模式上。"},{"en":"This phrase challenges the idea that birds are simple-minded.","zh":"這個短語挑戰鳥類頭腦簡單的想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"structure of the skull","meaning":"頭骨結構","examples":[{"en":"The structure of the skull revealed clues about the dodo’s senses.","zh":"頭骨結構揭示了關於渡渡鳥感官的線索。"},{"en":"Structure of the skull means the shape and arrangement of the bones in the head.","zh":"structure of the skull 是指頭部骨骼的形狀和排列。"},{"en":"The structure of a skull can show where eyes, muscles, and nerves were positioned.","zh":"頭骨結構可以顯示眼睛、肌肉和神經的位置。"},{"en":"Bone structure can help scientists understand how an extinct animal lived.","zh":"骨骼結構可以幫助科學家了解滅絕動物如何生活。"},{"en":"This phrase links physical form with biological function.","zh":"這個短語把身體形態與生物功能連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"particularly well-developed","meaning":"特別發達","examples":[{"en":"The dodo’s sense of smell was particularly well-developed.","zh":"渡渡鳥的嗅覺特別發達。"},{"en":"Particularly well-developed means especially strong or advanced.","zh":"particularly well-developed 是指尤其強大或發展成熟。"},{"en":"A dog’s sense of smell is particularly well-developed compared with humans’.","zh":"與人類相比，狗的嗅覺特別發達。"},{"en":"A well-developed sense can help an animal find food or avoid danger.","zh":"發達的感官可以幫助動物尋找食物或避開危險。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a strong feature.","zh":"這個短語突出強項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sense of smell","meaning":"嗅覺","examples":[{"en":"The dodo probably had a strong sense of smell.","zh":"渡渡鳥可能有很強的嗅覺。"},{"en":"Sense of smell is the ability to detect scents or odours.","zh":"sense of smell 是察覺氣味的能力。"},{"en":"Dogs use their sense of smell to find people, food, or hidden objects.","zh":"狗利用嗅覺尋找人、食物或隱藏物件。"},{"en":"A strong sense of smell can help animals locate food in thick vegetation.","zh":"強嗅覺可以幫助動物在茂密植被中尋找食物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one of the body’s senses.","zh":"這個短語指身體感官之一。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be good at","meaning":"擅長……","examples":[{"en":"The dodo may have been good at locating ripe fruit.","zh":"渡渡鳥可能擅長找到成熟水果。"},{"en":"To be good at something means to have skill or ability in doing it.","zh":"be good at something 是指有能力或技巧做好某事。"},{"en":"Some students are good at remembering maps and directions.","zh":"有些學生擅長記住地圖和方向。"},{"en":"An animal good at finding food has a better chance of survival.","zh":"擅長尋找食物的動物有更大生存機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strength or ability.","zh":"這個短語描述強項或能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"locate ripe fruit","meaning":"找到成熟水果","examples":[{"en":"The dodo may have used smell to locate ripe fruit.","zh":"渡渡鳥可能用嗅覺找到成熟水果。"},{"en":"To locate ripe fruit means to find fruit that is ready to eat.","zh":"locate ripe fruit 是指找到已經可以食用的成熟水果。"},{"en":"Birds may locate ripe fruit by colour, smell, or softness.","zh":"鳥類可能透過顏色、氣味或柔軟度找到成熟水果。"},{"en":"Finding ripe fruit is important because it provides energy and nutrients.","zh":"找到成熟水果很重要，因為它提供能量和營養。"},{"en":"This phrase links searching with food readiness.","zh":"這個短語把尋找與食物成熟度連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"thick vegetation","meaning":"茂密植被","examples":[{"en":"The dodo found food in the island’s thick vegetation.","zh":"渡渡鳥在島上的茂密植被中尋找食物。"},{"en":"Thick vegetation means dense plant growth with many trees, bushes, or leaves.","zh":"thick vegetation 是指樹木、灌木或葉子很多的茂密植物生長。"},{"en":"A forest path can be hard to walk through if the vegetation is thick.","zh":"如果植被茂密，森林小路可能很難走。"},{"en":"Thick vegetation can hide food, animals, and nests from view.","zh":"茂密植被可以把食物、動物和鳥巢藏起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a dense natural environment.","zh":"這個短語描述濃密的自然環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"it looks as if","meaning":"看起來好像……","examples":[{"en":"It looks as if the dodo was better able to survive than people once believed.","zh":"看起來好像渡渡鳥比人們曾經相信的更有能力生存。"},{"en":"It looks as if means it seems that something is true based on the evidence.","zh":"it looks as if 是指根據證據，某事似乎是真的。"},{"en":"It looks as if the shop is closed because the lights are off.","zh":"燈關了，看起來好像商店已經關門。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a reasonable judgement, not absolute certainty.","zh":"這個短語表達合理判斷，而不是絕對肯定。"},{"en":"It is useful when drawing a careful conclusion.","zh":"當謹慎作結論時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"better able to survive","meaning":"更有能力生存","examples":[{"en":"The dodo was better able to survive than was originally believed.","zh":"渡渡鳥比原本相信的更有能力生存。"},{"en":"Better able to survive means having a stronger ability to stay alive than expected.","zh":"better able to survive 是指比預期有更強生存能力。"},{"en":"Animals with good senses may be better able to survive in difficult habitats.","zh":"感官良好的動物可能更有能力在困難棲息地生存。"},{"en":"New evidence can show that a species was tougher than people assumed.","zh":"新證據可以顯示某物種比人們假設的更堅韌。"},{"en":"This phrase compares survival ability with earlier beliefs.","zh":"這個短語把生存能力與早期看法作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"defend itself","meaning":"保護自己","examples":[{"en":"The dodo was better able to defend itself than was originally believed.","zh":"渡渡鳥比原本相信的更有能力保護自己。"},{"en":"To defend itself means to protect itself from danger or attack.","zh":"defend itself 是指保護自己免受危險或攻擊。"},{"en":"A porcupine defends itself with sharp quills.","zh":"豪豬用尖刺保護自己。"},{"en":"Animals that can defend themselves are less easy for predators to kill.","zh":"能保護自己的動物較不容易被捕食者殺死。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on self-protection.","zh":"這個短語著重自我保護。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"than was originally believed","meaning":"比最初所相信的……","examples":[{"en":"The dodo was stronger than was originally believed.","zh":"渡渡鳥比最初所相信的更強壯。"},{"en":"Than was originally believed means than people first thought.","zh":"than was originally believed 是指比人們一開始所想的更……。"},{"en":"The old bridge was stronger than was originally believed after engineers tested it.","zh":"工程師測試後，舊橋比最初所相信的更堅固。"},{"en":"New evidence can change an original belief.","zh":"新證據可以改變最初看法。"},{"en":"This phrase compares new understanding with earlier assumptions.","zh":"這個短語把新理解與早期假設作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"less than","meaning":"少於……","examples":[{"en":"Less than 200 years after Europeans arrived, the dodo was extinct.","zh":"歐洲人到達後少於200年，渡渡鳥便滅絕。"},{"en":"Less than means a smaller amount or shorter time than the number given.","zh":"less than 是指數量或時間少於所給數字。"},{"en":"The journey took less than thirty minutes by train.","zh":"這趟火車旅程少於三十分鐘。"},{"en":"“Less than” can emphasise how quickly something happened.","zh":"less than 可以強調某事發生得很快。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an upper limit that was not reached.","zh":"這個短語提供未達到的上限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"become extinct","meaning":"滅絕","examples":[{"en":"The dodo became extinct less than 200 years after Europeans arrived.","zh":"歐洲人到達後少於200年，渡渡鳥便滅絕。"},{"en":"To become extinct means for a species to die out completely.","zh":"become extinct 是指一個物種完全消失。"},{"en":"A species may become extinct if it cannot adapt to habitat loss.","zh":"如果物種不能適應棲息地喪失，便可能滅絕。"},{"en":"Once a species becomes extinct, it cannot naturally return.","zh":"一旦物種滅絕，它不能自然回來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the final disappearance of a species.","zh":"這個短語描述物種的最終消失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the reason for","meaning":"……的原因","examples":[{"en":"The speaker asks about the reason for the dodo’s extinction.","zh":"講者詢問渡渡鳥滅絕的原因。"},{"en":"The reason for something is the cause or explanation behind it.","zh":"the reason for something 是某事背後的原因或解釋。"},{"en":"Scientists study the reason for sudden changes in animal populations.","zh":"科學家研究動物族群突然變化的原因。"},{"en":"Understanding the reason for a problem helps people prevent it in future.","zh":"理解問題的原因有助人們將來預防它。"},{"en":"This phrase asks why something happened.","zh":"這個短語詢問某事為何發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for a long time","meaning":"很長時間以來","examples":[{"en":"For a long time, people believed dodos were hunted to extinction.","zh":"很長時間以來，人們相信渡渡鳥是被獵殺至滅絕。"},{"en":"For a long time means during many years or a long period.","zh":"for a long time 是指許多年或很長一段時期。"},{"en":"For a long time, people believed the Earth was the centre of the universe.","zh":"很長時間以來，人們相信地球是宇宙中心。"},{"en":"Long-held beliefs can change when new evidence appears.","zh":"長期持有的信念可能因新證據出現而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises duration.","zh":"這個短語強調持續時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be hunted to extinction","meaning":"被獵殺至滅絕","examples":[{"en":"People believed the dodos were hunted to extinction.","zh":"人們相信渡渡鳥是被獵殺至滅絕。"},{"en":"To be hunted to extinction means to be killed by hunting until the species disappears.","zh":"be hunted to extinction 是指因被獵殺到物種消失。"},{"en":"Some animals were hunted to extinction because their fur or meat was valuable.","zh":"有些動物因毛皮或肉有價值而被獵殺至滅絕。"},{"en":"Overhunting can destroy a population faster than it can reproduce.","zh":"過度捕獵可以比族群繁殖更快地摧毀牠們。"},{"en":"This phrase links human hunting with species loss.","zh":"這個短語把人類狩獵與物種消失連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"more complicated than this","meaning":"比這更複雜","examples":[{"en":"Scientists now believe the situation was more complicated than this.","zh":"科學家現在相信情況比這更複雜。"},{"en":"More complicated than this means not as simple as the explanation just given.","zh":"more complicated than this 是指事情不像剛才的解釋那麼簡單。"},{"en":"A student’s poor result may be more complicated than laziness alone.","zh":"學生成績差可能比單純懶惰更複雜。"},{"en":"Problems often have several causes working together.","zh":"問題通常有多個原因共同作用。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against an overly simple explanation.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要接受過分簡化的解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"another factor","meaning":"另一個因素","examples":[{"en":"Another factor may have been new species brought by sailors.","zh":"另一個因素可能是水手帶來的新物種。"},{"en":"Another factor means an additional cause or influence.","zh":"another factor 是另一個原因或影響。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is one reason students struggle; another factor may be stress.","zh":"睡眠不足是學生感到吃力的一個原因；另一個因素可能是壓力。"},{"en":"Complex problems often require looking at several factors.","zh":"複雜問題通常需要觀察多個因素。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another possible explanation.","zh":"這個短語加入另一個可能解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"species","meaning":"物種","examples":[{"en":"New species were brought to the island by sailors.","zh":"新物種由水手帶到島上。"},{"en":"Species means a group of living things that can reproduce with one another.","zh":"species 是能彼此繁殖的一類生物。"},{"en":"Lions and tigers are different species of big cats.","zh":"獅子和老虎是不同的大型貓科物種。"},{"en":"Introducing new species to an island can disturb local wildlife.","zh":"把新物種引入島嶼可以干擾當地野生動物。"},{"en":"This word is central in biology and ecology.","zh":"這個詞在生物學和生態學中很核心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be brought to","meaning":"被帶到……","examples":[{"en":"New species were brought to Mauritius by sailors.","zh":"新物種被水手帶到毛里裘斯。"},{"en":"To be brought to a place means to be carried or taken there.","zh":"be brought to a place 是指被攜帶或帶到某地。"},{"en":"Plants from Europe were brought to many colonies by settlers.","zh":"歐洲植物被定居者帶到許多殖民地。"},{"en":"Species brought to new places may become harmful if there are no natural predators.","zh":"被帶到新地方的物種，如果沒有天敵，可能變得有害。"},{"en":"This passive phrase focuses on arrival at a place.","zh":"這個被動短語著重到達某地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be a threat to","meaning":"對……構成威脅","examples":[{"en":"Dogs would have been a threat to the dodos.","zh":"狗會對渡渡鳥構成威脅。"},{"en":"To be a threat to something means to be a danger to it.","zh":"be a threat to something 是指對某物有危險。"},{"en":"Pollution is a threat to river wildlife.","zh":"污染對河流野生動物構成威脅。"},{"en":"New predators can be a serious threat to animals that have never faced them before.","zh":"新捕食者會對從未面對過牠們的動物構成嚴重威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase describes danger or risk.","zh":"這個短語描述危險或風險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"main part of","meaning":"……的主要部分","examples":[{"en":"Fruit was the main part of the dodos’ diet.","zh":"水果是渡渡鳥飲食的主要部分。"},{"en":"The main part of something means the largest or most important part.","zh":"main part of something 是指某事最大或最重要的部分。"},{"en":"Rice is the main part of many meals in some countries.","zh":"在一些國家，米飯是許多餐膳的主要部分。"},{"en":"Knowing the main part of an animal’s diet helps scientists understand its habitat.","zh":"了解動物飲食的主要部分有助科學家理解其棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the central component.","zh":"這個短語指出核心組成部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"diet","meaning":"飲食","examples":[{"en":"Fruit was the main part of the dodos’ diet.","zh":"水果是渡渡鳥飲食的主要部分。"},{"en":"Diet means the food and drink that a person or animal usually consumes.","zh":"diet 是人或動物通常進食和飲用的東西。"},{"en":"A rabbit’s diet includes grass, hay, and vegetables.","zh":"兔子的飲食包括草、乾草和蔬菜。"},{"en":"Diet affects health, growth, and survival.","zh":"飲食會影響健康、成長和生存。"},{"en":"This word refers to eating patterns, not only weight loss.","zh":"這個詞指飲食模式，而不只是減肥。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deliberately","meaning":"故意地；刻意地","examples":[{"en":"Dogs and monkeys were brought to the island deliberately.","zh":"狗和猴子是被刻意帶到島上的。"},{"en":"Deliberately means on purpose, not by accident.","zh":"deliberately 是指有意地，不是意外地。"},{"en":"A teacher may deliberately choose easy examples before harder ones.","zh":"老師可能刻意先選簡單例子，再選較難例子。"},{"en":"Deliberate actions show intention and planning.","zh":"刻意行動顯示意圖和計劃。"},{"en":"This word contrasts with accidentally.","zh":"這個詞與 accidentally 相對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"another type of creature","meaning":"另一種生物","examples":[{"en":"The ships also brought another type of creature: rats.","zh":"船隻也帶來另一種生物：老鼠。"},{"en":"Another type of creature means a different kind of living animal.","zh":"another type of creature 是指另一類活生生的動物。"},{"en":"A pond may contain fish, frogs, and another type of creature, such as insects.","zh":"池塘可能有魚、青蛙和另一種生物，例如昆蟲。"},{"en":"Different creatures can affect an ecosystem in different ways.","zh":"不同生物可以以不同方式影響生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a new animal group.","zh":"這個短語引入新的動物類別。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"come to land from","meaning":"從……登陸","examples":[{"en":"Rats came to land from the ships.","zh":"老鼠從船上登陸。"},{"en":"To come to land from somewhere means to leave a ship or the sea and reach land.","zh":"come to land from somewhere 是指離開船隻或海上並到達陸地。"},{"en":"Sailors came to land from the boat to collect fresh water.","zh":"水手從船上登陸，以收集淡水。"},{"en":"Animals leaving ships can accidentally enter new habitats.","zh":"從船上離開的動物可能意外進入新棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arrival on land from a vessel.","zh":"這個短語描述從船隻到達陸地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rapidly overrun","meaning":"迅速遍布","examples":[{"en":"Rats rapidly overran the island.","zh":"老鼠迅速遍布整座島。"},{"en":"To rapidly overrun a place means to spread through it very quickly and in large numbers.","zh":"rapidly overrun a place 是指以大量數目非常快速地擴散到某地。"},{"en":"Weeds can rapidly overrun a garden if they are not removed.","zh":"如果不清除雜草，雜草可以迅速遍布花園。"},{"en":"When an invasive species overruns an area, native species may suffer.","zh":"當入侵物種遍布某區，本地物種可能受害。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests uncontrolled spread.","zh":"這個短語暗示不受控制的擴散。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"upset the ecology of","meaning":"破壞……的生態","examples":[{"en":"Rats upset the ecology of the island.","zh":"老鼠破壞了島上的生態。"},{"en":"To upset the ecology of a place means to disturb the natural relationships between living things there.","zh":"upset the ecology of a place 是指干擾當地生物之間的自然關係。"},{"en":"Pollution can upset the ecology of a river by killing insects and fish.","zh":"污染可以透過殺死昆蟲和魚類來破壞河流生態。"},{"en":"When ecology is disturbed, many species can be affected at once.","zh":"當生態受干擾，許多物種可能同時受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage to a natural system.","zh":"這個短語描述對自然系統的破壞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ecology","meaning":"生態","examples":[{"en":"The ecology of Mauritius was damaged by rats.","zh":"毛里裘斯的生態受到老鼠破壞。"},{"en":"Ecology is the relationship between living things and their environment.","zh":"ecology 是生物與其環境之間的關係。"},{"en":"A forest’s ecology includes trees, insects, birds, soil, water, and climate.","zh":"森林生態包括樹木、昆蟲、鳥類、土壤、水和氣候。"},{"en":"Changing one part of an ecosystem can affect many other parts.","zh":"改變生態系統的一部分，可能影響許多其他部分。"},{"en":"This word is central to environmental science.","zh":"這個詞是環境科學的核心詞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not just…but…too","meaning":"不只是……，也……","examples":[{"en":"Rats affected not just the dodos but other species too.","zh":"老鼠影響的不只是渡渡鳥，也包括其他物種。"},{"en":"Not just…but…too means one thing is affected, and another thing is also affected.","zh":"not just…but…too 是指不只一件事受影響，另一件事也受影響。"},{"en":"Pollution harms not just fish but people too.","zh":"污染不只傷害魚類，也傷害人類。"},{"en":"This structure widens the effect beyond the first example.","zh":"這個結構把影響擴展到第一個例子以外。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing that a problem is broader than expected.","zh":"當顯示問題比預期更廣時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a particular danger to","meaning":"對……特別危險","examples":[{"en":"Rats were a particular danger to the dodos.","zh":"老鼠對渡渡鳥特別危險。"},{"en":"A particular danger to something means an especially serious threat to it.","zh":"a particular danger to something 是指對某物尤其嚴重的威脅。"},{"en":"Plastic bags are a particular danger to sea turtles.","zh":"膠袋對海龜特別危險。"},{"en":"Some dangers are worse for certain species because of how those species live or reproduce.","zh":"有些危險對某些物種特別嚴重，因為那些物種有特定生活或繁殖方式。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a specific high risk.","zh":"這個短語突出特定高風險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"consume their eggs","meaning":"吃掉牠們的蛋","examples":[{"en":"Rats consumed the dodos’ eggs.","zh":"老鼠吃掉渡渡鳥的蛋。"},{"en":"To consume their eggs means to eat their eggs.","zh":"consume their eggs 是指吃掉牠們的蛋。"},{"en":"Predators may consume birds’ eggs before the chicks can hatch.","zh":"捕食者可能在雛鳥孵化前吃掉鳥蛋。"},{"en":"Egg loss reduces the number of young animals that survive.","zh":"蛋被吃掉會減少能存活的幼小動物數量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes predation on reproduction.","zh":"這個短語描述對繁殖的捕食。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lay one at a time","meaning":"一次只下一隻蛋","examples":[{"en":"Each dodo only laid one egg at a time.","zh":"每隻渡渡鳥一次只下一隻蛋。"},{"en":"To lay one at a time means to produce only one egg on each occasion.","zh":"lay one at a time 是指每次只產下一隻蛋。"},{"en":"Some birds lay several eggs, but others lay one at a time.","zh":"有些鳥會下幾隻蛋，但另一些一次只下一隻蛋。"},{"en":"If an animal lays only one egg at a time, losing that egg is serious.","zh":"如果動物一次只下一隻蛋，失去那隻蛋便很嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a reproductive limit.","zh":"這個短語解釋繁殖上的限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"devastating effect on","meaning":"對……造成毀滅性影響","examples":[{"en":"Egg predation probably had a devastating effect on dodo populations.","zh":"蛋被捕食可能對渡渡鳥族群造成毀滅性影響。"},{"en":"A devastating effect on something is a very severe and damaging impact.","zh":"devastating effect on something 是對某事造成非常嚴重和破壞性的影響。"},{"en":"A fire can have a devastating effect on a small village.","zh":"火災可以對小村莊造成毀滅性影響。"},{"en":"Repeated loss of eggs can destroy a bird population over time.","zh":"鳥蛋反覆損失可以隨時間摧毀鳥類族群。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage that is extremely serious.","zh":"這個短語描述極其嚴重的破壞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"populations","meaning":"族群","examples":[{"en":"The loss of eggs affected dodo populations.","zh":"蛋的損失影響了渡渡鳥族群。"},{"en":"Populations are groups of the same species living in a particular area.","zh":"populations 是生活在某個地區的同一物種群體。"},{"en":"Scientists count animal populations to see whether species are increasing or declining.","zh":"科學家點算動物族群，以了解物種是在增加還是減少。"},{"en":"If young animals do not survive, populations may shrink quickly.","zh":"如果幼小動物無法存活，族群可能快速縮小。"},{"en":"This word is common in ecology and conservation.","zh":"這個詞常見於生態和保育。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"main cause of","meaning":"……的主要原因","examples":[{"en":"The main cause of the birds’ extinction may have been agriculture.","zh":"這些鳥滅絕的主要原因可能是農業。"},{"en":"The main cause of something is the most important reason it happened.","zh":"main cause of something 是某事發生的最重要原因。"},{"en":"The main cause of the delay was heavy traffic.","zh":"延誤的主要原因是交通擠塞。"},{"en":"Identifying the main cause helps people understand which factor mattered most.","zh":"找出主要原因有助人們理解哪個因素最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase separates the biggest cause from smaller contributing factors.","zh":"這個短語把最大原因與較小因素分開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"introduction of non-native species","meaning":"外來物種的引入","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of non-native species was not the only problem.","zh":"外來物種的引入並不是唯一問題。"},{"en":"The introduction of non-native species means bringing animals or plants into a place where they do not naturally belong.","zh":"introduction of non-native species 是把動物或植物帶到它們非自然屬於的地方。"},{"en":"The introduction of non-native species can damage islands with delicate ecosystems.","zh":"外來物種的引入可能破壞生態脆弱的島嶼。"},{"en":"New species may compete with, kill, or disturb native species.","zh":"新物種可能與本地物種競爭、捕食牠們或干擾牠們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major ecological change.","zh":"這個短語描述重大生態變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"non-native species","meaning":"外來物種","examples":[{"en":"Dogs, monkeys and rats were non-native species on Mauritius.","zh":"狗、猴子和老鼠在毛里裘斯都是外來物種。"},{"en":"Non-native species are species introduced to a place where they did not originally live.","zh":"non-native species 是被引入到原本不生活在該地的物種。"},{"en":"A plant from another continent can become a non-native species in a local forest.","zh":"來自另一大洲的植物可以成為本地森林中的外來物種。"},{"en":"Non-native species can be harmless, but some become invasive and damaging.","zh":"外來物種可以無害，但有些會變成入侵性並造成破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts introduced species with native species.","zh":"這個短語把引入物種與本地物種作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"introduction of agriculture","meaning":"農業的引入","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of agriculture may have caused the dodo’s extinction.","zh":"農業的引入可能導致渡渡鳥滅絕。"},{"en":"The introduction of agriculture means farming began in a place where it had not been practised before.","zh":"introduction of agriculture 是指某地開始進行以前沒有的農業活動。"},{"en":"The introduction of agriculture often changes forests into fields.","zh":"農業的引入常把森林變成田地。"},{"en":"Farming can support people, but it may also remove wildlife habitats.","zh":"農業可以支持人類生活，但也可能移除野生動物棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase links human land use with environmental change.","zh":"這個短語把人類土地使用與環境變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"had once covered","meaning":"曾經覆蓋","examples":[{"en":"The forest had once covered the whole island.","zh":"森林曾經覆蓋整座島。"},{"en":"Had once covered means had covered something in the past, but no longer does.","zh":"had once covered 是指過去曾經覆蓋某地，但現在不再如此。"},{"en":"Grassland had once covered the area before the city was built.","zh":"在城市建成前，草地曾經覆蓋該區。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a contrast between the past landscape and the present one.","zh":"這個短語顯示過去景觀與現在景觀的對比。"},{"en":"It often appears when describing environmental loss.","zh":"它常用於描述環境喪失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"provide a perfect home for","meaning":"為……提供理想棲息地","examples":[{"en":"The forest had provided a perfect home for the dodo.","zh":"森林曾為渡渡鳥提供理想棲息地。"},{"en":"To provide a perfect home for a species means to give it an ideal habitat.","zh":"provide a perfect home for a species 是指為某物種提供理想棲息地。"},{"en":"Wetlands provide a perfect home for many frogs and water birds.","zh":"濕地為許多青蛙和水鳥提供理想棲息地。"},{"en":"A good habitat gives animals food, shelter, and places to reproduce.","zh":"良好棲息地為動物提供食物、庇護和繁殖地方。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why an environment suits a species.","zh":"這個短語解釋環境為何適合某物種。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be cut down","meaning":"被砍伐","examples":[{"en":"The forest was cut down so that crops could be grown.","zh":"森林被砍伐，以便種植農作物。"},{"en":"To be cut down means trees are chopped or removed.","zh":"be cut down 是指樹木被砍倒或移除。"},{"en":"A forest may be cut down to make space for roads or farms.","zh":"森林可能被砍伐，以騰出空間建道路或農田。"},{"en":"Cutting down forests can destroy habitats and reduce biodiversity.","zh":"砍伐森林可以破壞棲息地並減少生物多樣性。"},{"en":"This passive phrase focuses on the removal of trees.","zh":"這個被動短語著重樹木被移除。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"so that crops could be grown","meaning":"以便種植農作物","examples":[{"en":"The forest was cut down so that crops could be grown.","zh":"森林被砍伐，以便種植農作物。"},{"en":"So that crops could be grown means in order to make space for farming plants.","zh":"so that crops could be grown 是指為了騰出空間種植農作物。"},{"en":"Land may be cleared so that rice, vegetables, or sugar can be grown.","zh":"土地可能被清理，以便種植稻米、蔬菜或甘蔗。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose behind cutting down the forest.","zh":"這個短語解釋砍伐森林背後的目的。"},{"en":"It links human farming needs with environmental change.","zh":"它把人類農業需要與環境變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"crops such as sugar","meaning":"甘蔗等農作物","examples":[{"en":"Crops such as sugar were grown on the island.","zh":"島上種植了甘蔗等農作物。"},{"en":"Crops such as sugar means farm plants including sugar cane and similar examples.","zh":"crops such as sugar 是指包括甘蔗在內的農作物。"},{"en":"Tropical islands often grew crops such as sugar, coffee, or cotton in colonial times.","zh":"殖民時期，熱帶島嶼常種植甘蔗、咖啡或棉花等農作物。"},{"en":"Cash crops can bring income but may replace natural habitats.","zh":"經濟作物可以帶來收入，但也可能取代自然棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase gives sugar as an example of cultivated crops.","zh":"這個短語以甘蔗作為栽培作物的例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"survive for thousands of years","meaning":"生存了數千年","examples":[{"en":"The dodo had survived for thousands of years.","zh":"渡渡鳥已經生存了數千年。"},{"en":"To survive for thousands of years means to continue living as a species for a very long time.","zh":"survive for thousands of years 是指一個物種持續生存非常長時間。"},{"en":"Some trees can survive for thousands of years in stable environments.","zh":"有些樹可以在穩定環境中生存數千年。"},{"en":"Long survival can end quickly if a habitat changes suddenly.","zh":"如果棲息地突然改變，長久生存也可以很快結束。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises both endurance and later tragedy.","zh":"這個短語同時強調持久生命力和之後的悲劇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"suddenly it was gone","meaning":"突然消失了","examples":[{"en":"Although the dodo had survived for thousands of years, suddenly it was gone.","zh":"雖然渡渡鳥已生存數千年，牠卻突然消失了。"},{"en":"Suddenly it was gone means it disappeared quickly after existing for a long time.","zh":"suddenly it was gone 是指某物存在很久後迅速消失。"},{"en":"A local shop may serve a community for decades, and then suddenly it is gone.","zh":"一間本地店舖可能服務社區數十年，然後突然消失。"},{"en":"Sudden loss can feel shocking because people assume long-lasting things will continue.","zh":"突然失去會令人震驚，因為人們常以為長久存在的東西會繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strong ending to a story of disappearance.","zh":"這個短語為消失的故事帶來強烈結尾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 19 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 2/task-1":[{"front":"caring for her elderly mother","meaning":"照顧年邁母親","examples":[{"en":"A woman is caring for her elderly mother at home.","zh":"一名女子正在家中照顧年邁母親。"},{"en":"Caring for her elderly mother means helping an older mother with daily needs, health, and safety.","zh":"照顧年邁母親指協助年老母親處理日常需要、健康和安全。"},{"en":"Carol spends every morning caring for her elderly mother before doing housework.","zh":"Carol 每天早上先照顧年邁母親，然後才做家務。"},{"en":"Caring for an elderly parent can be loving but also physically and emotionally tiring.","zh":"照顧年邁父母可以是充滿愛的事，但也可能在身體和情緒上令人疲累。"},{"en":"People caring for elderly relatives may need support from family or local services.","zh":"照顧年長親人的人可能需要家人或本地服務支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"It’s really good to see you","meaning":"見到你真的很高興","examples":[{"en":"It’s really good to see you, Tom.","zh":"Tom，見到你真的很高興。"},{"en":"“It’s really good to see you” is a warm greeting used when you are happy to meet someone.","zh":"「It’s really good to see you」是一種溫暖的問候，表示很高興見到某人。"},{"en":"It’s really good to see you after such a long time.","zh":"這麼久沒見，見到你真的很高興。"},{"en":"People often say this when meeting an old friend or someone they have missed.","zh":"人們見到舊朋友或掛念的人時，常會這樣說。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds warmer than simply saying “hello.”","zh":"這個短語比單純說「你好」更溫暖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"give up work","meaning":"辭去工作；放棄工作","examples":[{"en":"Carol had to give up work to look after her mother.","zh":"Carol 不得不辭去工作，以照顧母親。"},{"en":"To give up work means to stop working, often because of another responsibility.","zh":"Give up work 指停止工作，通常是因為有另一項責任。"},{"en":"He gave up work for a year to care for his sick child.","zh":"他辭去工作一年，照顧生病的孩子。"},{"en":"Giving up work can reduce income and make people feel isolated.","zh":"放棄工作可能減少收入，並令人感到孤立。"},{"en":"Some carers give up work because full-time care leaves them no choice.","zh":"有些照顧者辭去工作，是因為全職照顧令他們別無選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lose touch with","meaning":"與……失去聯繫","examples":[{"en":"She feels she is losing touch with her friends and colleagues.","zh":"她覺得自己正與朋友和同事失去聯繫。"},{"en":"To lose touch with someone means to communicate with them less and gradually become less close.","zh":"Lose touch with 某人，指與對方溝通減少，並逐漸變得不親近。"},{"en":"After moving away, Mia lost touch with many classmates.","zh":"搬走後，Mia 與許多同學失去聯繫。"},{"en":"People may lose touch with colleagues when they leave a job.","zh":"人們離職後可能與同事失去聯繫。"},{"en":"Regular messages or short meetings can help friends avoid losing touch.","zh":"定期傳訊息或短暫見面，可以幫助朋友避免失去聯繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"friends and colleagues","meaning":"朋友和同事","examples":[{"en":"She misses her friends and colleagues from work.","zh":"她想念工作上的朋友和同事。"},{"en":"Friends and colleagues are people you know personally and people you work with.","zh":"朋友和同事指你私下認識的人，以及與你一起工作的人。"},{"en":"Carol enjoyed chatting with her friends and colleagues during lunch breaks.","zh":"Carol 喜歡在午飯時間與朋友和同事聊天。"},{"en":"Leaving a job can mean losing daily contact with friends and colleagues.","zh":"離職可能意味與朋友和同事失去日常接觸。"},{"en":"Support from friends and colleagues can make difficult times easier.","zh":"朋友和同事的支持可以令困難時期較易度過。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be sorry someone had to leave","meaning":"對某人不得不離開感到難過","examples":[{"en":"Everyone was sorry Carol had to leave the office.","zh":"大家都對 Carol 不得不離開辦公室感到難過。"},{"en":"To be sorry someone had to leave means to feel sad or regretful that the person needed to go.","zh":"Be sorry someone had to leave 指因某人需要離開而感到傷心或遺憾。"},{"en":"The team was sorry Mei had to leave because she was helpful and kind.","zh":"團隊對 Mei 不得不離開感到難過，因為她樂於助人又友善。"},{"en":"People may be sorry a colleague has to leave, even if they understand the reason.","zh":"即使明白原因，人們仍可能對同事不得不離開感到難過。"},{"en":"This phrase shows sympathy for both the person leaving and those who will miss them.","zh":"這個短語表達對離開者和想念他的人雙方的同情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be relieved to","meaning":"因……而鬆一口氣","examples":[{"en":"She may be relieved to have more time to look after her mother.","zh":"她可能因有更多時間照顧母親而鬆一口氣。"},{"en":"To be relieved to do something means to feel less worried because something helpful has happened.","zh":"Be relieved to 做某事，指因有幫助的事情發生而減少擔心。"},{"en":"I was relieved to hear that the test results were normal.","zh":"聽到檢查結果正常，我鬆了一口氣。"},{"en":"A carer may feel relieved to receive help from a support worker.","zh":"照顧者得到支援工作者幫助時，可能會鬆一口氣。"},{"en":"Feeling relieved does not mean the whole situation is easy.","zh":"感到鬆一口氣並不表示整個情況很容易。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look after someone","meaning":"照顧某人","examples":[{"en":"Carol has more time to look after her mother.","zh":"Carol 有更多時間照顧母親。"},{"en":"To look after someone means to take care of their needs and safety.","zh":"Look after someone 指照顧某人的需要和安全。"},{"en":"My aunt looks after my grandmother every afternoon.","zh":"我姨姨每天下午照顧祖母。"},{"en":"Looking after someone may include cooking, cleaning, medicine, and emotional support.","zh":"照顧某人可能包括煮食、清潔、服藥和情感支持。"},{"en":"People who look after others also need time to rest.","zh":"照顧別人的人也需要時間休息。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cheerful","meaning":"開朗；心情愉快","examples":[{"en":"Her mother is very cheerful, although she needs help.","zh":"她的母親雖然需要幫助，但非常開朗。"},{"en":"Cheerful means happy, positive, and pleasant in mood.","zh":"Cheerful 指心情愉快、正面和令人舒服。"},{"en":"The nurse was cheerful and helped the patient feel calm.","zh":"護士很開朗，幫助病人感到安心。"},{"en":"A cheerful person can make a difficult situation feel less heavy.","zh":"開朗的人可以令困難情況感覺不那麼沉重。"},{"en":"Someone may be cheerful even when they are facing health problems.","zh":"即使面對健康問題，一個人仍可能保持開朗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get support from","meaning":"向……尋求支援","examples":[{"en":"Carol has not tried to get support from the local council.","zh":"Carol 尚未嘗試向地方議會尋求支援。"},{"en":"To get support from someone means to receive help, advice, money, or services from them.","zh":"Get support from 某人或機構，指從他們獲得幫助、建議、金錢或服務。"},{"en":"Families can get support from community centres when caring becomes difficult.","zh":"照顧工作變得困難時，家庭可以向社區中心尋求支援。"},{"en":"Getting support from professionals can reduce pressure on carers.","zh":"向專業人士尋求支援可以減輕照顧者壓力。"},{"en":"People sometimes delay getting support because they do not know what help is available.","zh":"人們有時會延遲尋求支援，因為不知道有哪些幫助可用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the local council","meaning":"地方議會；地方政府機構","examples":[{"en":"The local council can offer practical support to carers.","zh":"地方議會可以向照顧者提供實際支援。"},{"en":"The local council is a local government organisation that provides services for people in an area.","zh":"地方議會是為某一地區居民提供服務的地方政府機構。"},{"en":"The local council may help with housing, care services, rubbish collection, and community support.","zh":"地方議會可能協助處理房屋、照顧服務、垃圾收集和社區支援。"},{"en":"Carers can contact the local council to ask about available services.","zh":"照顧者可以聯絡地方議會，查詢可用服務。"},{"en":"Each local council may have different rules and support programmes.","zh":"每個地方議會可能有不同規則和支援計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"offer practical support","meaning":"提供實際支援","examples":[{"en":"They offer different kinds of practical support.","zh":"他們提供不同種類的實際支援。"},{"en":"To offer practical support means to provide useful, real help with everyday problems.","zh":"Offer practical support 指為日常問題提供有用而實際的幫助。"},{"en":"The council may offer practical support such as home visits and transport help.","zh":"地方議會可能提供家訪和交通協助等實際支援。"},{"en":"Practical support can make daily caring tasks easier to manage.","zh":"實際支援可以令日常照顧任務更容易處理。"},{"en":"Emotional encouragement is important, but carers often need practical support too.","zh":"情感鼓勵很重要，但照顧者往往也需要實際支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"carers","meaning":"照顧者","examples":[{"en":"Carers sometimes need help with their other responsibilities.","zh":"照顧者有時需要幫助處理其他責任。"},{"en":"Carers are people who look after someone who needs help because of age, illness, or disability.","zh":"照顧者是照顧因年老、疾病或殘疾而需要幫助的人的人。"},{"en":"Carers may help with meals, washing, medicine, and appointments.","zh":"照顧者可能協助用餐、洗澡、服藥和赴約。"},{"en":"Many carers are family members, not paid workers.","zh":"許多照顧者是家人，而不是受薪工作者。"},{"en":"Carers need support because caring can take a lot of time and energy.","zh":"照顧者需要支援，因為照顧工作可能耗費大量時間和精力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"other responsibilities","meaning":"其他責任","examples":[{"en":"Carers need time for their other responsibilities.","zh":"照顧者需要時間處理其他責任。"},{"en":"Other responsibilities are duties someone has besides the main task being discussed.","zh":"其他責任是除了正在討論的主要任務之外的職責。"},{"en":"A carer may also have other responsibilities such as paying bills or looking after children.","zh":"照顧者可能還有其他責任，例如繳費或照顧孩子。"},{"en":"Support services can give carers time to handle their other responsibilities.","zh":"支援服務可以給照顧者時間處理其他責任。"},{"en":"Ignoring other responsibilities can create stress and practical problems.","zh":"忽視其他責任可能造成壓力和實際問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"apart from","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"Carers have responsibilities apart from the person they are caring for.","zh":"除了他們正在照顧的對象之外，照顧者還有其他責任。"},{"en":"Apart from means except for or in addition to something.","zh":"Apart from 指除了某事之外，或除了某事還有。"},{"en":"Apart from caring for her mother, Carol has to manage the house.","zh":"除了照顧母親之外，Carol 還要打理家居。"},{"en":"A person may have many duties apart from paid work.","zh":"一個人除了受薪工作之外，可能還有許多責任。"},{"en":"The phrase helps separate one main thing from other related things.","zh":"這個短語有助把一件主要事情與其他相關事情分開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the person they are caring for","meaning":"他們正在照顧的對象","examples":[{"en":"The person they are caring for may need help every day.","zh":"他們正在照顧的對象可能每天都需要幫助。"},{"en":"The person they are caring for is the person who receives regular help from a carer.","zh":"他們正在照顧的對象，是定期接受照顧者幫助的人。"},{"en":"The person they are caring for may be elderly, ill, disabled, or recovering from an injury.","zh":"他們正在照顧的對象可能是長者、病人、殘疾人士或康復者。"},{"en":"Carers should think about both their own needs and the needs of the person they care for.","zh":"照顧者應同時考慮自己的需要和被照顧者的需要。"},{"en":"Support plans often begin by understanding the person being cared for.","zh":"支援計劃通常由了解被照顧者開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"need a break","meaning":"需要休息一下","examples":[{"en":"Carers sometimes need a break from their daily responsibilities.","zh":"照顧者有時需要從日常責任中休息一下。"},{"en":"To need a break means to need time to rest or stop doing a tiring activity for a while.","zh":"Need a break 指需要時間休息，或暫時停止做令人疲累的活動。"},{"en":"After a long morning of caring, Carol needed a break.","zh":"經過一整個上午的照顧後，Carol 需要休息一下。"},{"en":"Needing a break does not mean a carer is selfish or uncaring.","zh":"需要休息並不表示照顧者自私或不關心。"},{"en":"Short breaks can help carers continue their responsibilities more safely.","zh":"短暫休息可以幫助照顧者更安全地繼續承擔責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Absolutely","meaning":"完全沒錯","examples":[{"en":"Carol says, “Absolutely,” when Tom explains that carers need a break.","zh":"Tom 解釋照顧者需要休息時，Carol 說：「完全沒錯。」"},{"en":"“Absolutely” means completely, definitely, or strongly yes.","zh":"Absolutely 指完全、肯定或強烈地表示同意。"},{"en":"“Do you think carers need more support?” “Absolutely.”","zh":"「你認為照顧者需要更多支援嗎？」「完全沒錯。」"},{"en":"The word shows strong agreement rather than a weak or uncertain answer.","zh":"這個詞表示強烈同意，而不是微弱或不確定的回答。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken English when someone strongly accepts a point.","zh":"當某人強烈接受一個觀點時，這個詞常見於口語英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tell me more","meaning":"再說多一點；詳細說說","examples":[{"en":"Carol asks Tom to tell her more about the support.","zh":"Carol 請 Tom 再詳細說說支援服務。"},{"en":"“Tell me more” asks someone to give additional details or explanation.","zh":"「Tell me more」是請某人提供更多細節或解釋。"},{"en":"That support service sounds useful. Tell me more.","zh":"那個支援服務聽起來很有用。再說多一點吧。"},{"en":"The phrase shows interest and invites the speaker to continue.","zh":"這個短語表示感興趣，並邀請說話者繼續。"},{"en":"It is useful when the listener wants practical information, not just a general idea.","zh":"當聽者想要實際資料，而不只是一般概念時，這句話很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go about doing something","meaning":"著手做某事；開始處理某事","examples":[{"en":"Carol wants to know how to go about getting support.","zh":"Carol 想知道如何著手尋求支援。"},{"en":"To go about doing something means to begin or deal with a task in a particular way.","zh":"Go about doing something 指以某種方式開始或處理一項任務。"},{"en":"How should I go about applying for financial help?","zh":"我應如何著手申請經濟援助？"},{"en":"People often ask this when they know what they need but not how to start.","zh":"當人們知道自己需要甚麼，但不知道如何開始時，常會這樣問。"},{"en":"Clear advice can show carers how to go about getting the support they need.","zh":"清楚建議可以告訴照顧者如何開始尋求所需支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have an assessment of someone’s needs","meaning":"接受對某人需求的評估","examples":[{"en":"Carol would have to have an assessment of her mother’s needs.","zh":"Carol 需要接受對母親需求的評估。"},{"en":"To have an assessment of someone’s needs means to have a formal review of what help that person requires.","zh":"Have an assessment of someone’s needs 指正式檢視某人需要哪些幫助。"},{"en":"The council arranged an assessment of the elderly man’s needs.","zh":"地方議會安排了對那位長者需求的評估。"},{"en":"An assessment can look at health, safety, daily tasks, and emotional support.","zh":"評估可以查看健康、安全、日常任務和情感支援。"},{"en":"The results help decide what kind of care or support should be offered.","zh":"結果有助決定應提供哪種照顧或支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"assessment of needs","meaning":"需求評估","examples":[{"en":"An assessment of needs helps the council understand the situation.","zh":"需求評估幫助地方議會了解情況。"},{"en":"An assessment of needs is a review that identifies what support a person requires.","zh":"需求評估是找出某人需要哪些支援的檢視。"},{"en":"The assessment of needs showed that the family required home-care visits.","zh":"需求評估顯示該家庭需要家居照顧探訪。"},{"en":"A proper assessment should include both the carer and the person being cared for.","zh":"適當評估應包括照顧者和被照顧者雙方。"},{"en":"Without an assessment of needs, support may not match the real situation.","zh":"沒有需求評估，支援可能不符合真實情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"come round","meaning":"到家中探訪；過來","examples":[{"en":"Someone would come round and talk to Carol about the situation.","zh":"會有人到家中探訪，並與 Carol 談談情況。"},{"en":"To come round means to visit someone’s home, usually for a short time.","zh":"Come round 指到某人家中探訪，通常時間不長。"},{"en":"A council worker will come round on Tuesday afternoon.","zh":"一名地方議會職員會在星期二下午過來。"},{"en":"Friends may come round to check whether a carer needs help.","zh":"朋友可能會過來看看照顧者是否需要幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in British English and sounds conversational.","zh":"這個短語常見於英式英語，聽起來較口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"talk to someone about the situation","meaning":"和某人談談情況","examples":[{"en":"A council worker would talk to Carol about the situation.","zh":"地方議會職員會和 Carol 談談情況。"},{"en":"To talk to someone about the situation means to discuss what is happening and what help may be needed.","zh":"Talk to someone about the situation 指與某人討論正在發生的事情，以及可能需要的幫助。"},{"en":"The nurse talked to the family about the patient’s situation.","zh":"護士與家人談談病人的情況。"},{"en":"Talking openly about the situation can help people find practical solutions.","zh":"坦誠談論情況可以幫助人們找到實際解決方法。"},{"en":"A good conversation should include facts, feelings, and possible next steps.","zh":"良好對話應包括事實、感受和可能的下一步。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for a start","meaning":"首先","examples":[{"en":"For a start, they would ask how much time she spends caring for her mother.","zh":"首先，他們會問她花多少時間照顧母親。"},{"en":"“For a start” introduces the first point or first example in an explanation.","zh":"「For a start」用來引出解釋中的第一點或第一個例子。"},{"en":"For a start, we need to understand the family’s daily routine.","zh":"首先，我們需要了解這個家庭的日常安排。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that more points will follow.","zh":"這個短語暗示之後還會有更多重點。"},{"en":"It helps organise information by beginning with one basic issue.","zh":"它以一個基本問題開始，幫助整理資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the amount of time","meaning":"所花的時間；時間量","examples":[{"en":"They would want to know the amount of time Carol spends caring for her mother.","zh":"他們想知道 Carol 花多少時間照顧母親。"},{"en":"The amount of time means how much time is used for an activity.","zh":"The amount of time 指某項活動所花費的時間。"},{"en":"The form asks about the amount of time spent on housework each week.","zh":"表格詢問每週花在家務上的時間。"},{"en":"Knowing the amount of time caring takes helps decide what support is needed.","zh":"知道照顧工作所需時間，有助決定需要甚麼支援。"},{"en":"A task may feel small, but the amount of time it takes can be large.","zh":"一項任務可能看似細小，但所花時間可以很長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"spend time doing something","meaning":"花時間做某事","examples":[{"en":"Carol spends a lot of time looking after her mother every day.","zh":"Carol 每天花很多時間照顧母親。"},{"en":"To spend time doing something means to use time on that activity.","zh":"Spend time doing something 指把時間用在某項活動上。"},{"en":"She spends two hours every morning preparing meals and medicine.","zh":"她每天早上花兩小時準備膳食和藥物。"},{"en":"People who spend a lot of time caring may have little time for themselves.","zh":"花很多時間照顧別人的人，可能很少有自己的時間。"},{"en":"How people spend their time shows what responsibilities they carry.","zh":"人們如何花時間，可以顯示他們承擔哪些責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"during the day","meaning":"在白天；日間","examples":[{"en":"They will ask what tasks Carol does during the day.","zh":"他們會問 Carol 在白天做哪些任務。"},{"en":"During the day means in the daytime, not at night.","zh":"During the day 指在白天，而不是夜晚。"},{"en":"Carol helps her mother move around during the day.","zh":"Carol 在白天幫助母親四處走動。"},{"en":"Some carers have different tasks during the day and at night.","zh":"有些照顧者在白天和夜晚有不同任務。"},{"en":"Daytime support can give carers time for shopping or appointments.","zh":"日間支援可以讓照顧者有時間購物或赴約。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sorts of tasks","meaning":"各類任務；各種事情","examples":[{"en":"They will ask what sorts of tasks Carol does for her mother.","zh":"他們會問 Carol 為母親做哪些種類的任務。"},{"en":"Sorts of tasks means types or kinds of jobs or duties.","zh":"Sorts of tasks 指不同類型的工作或職責。"},{"en":"The assessment asks about sorts of tasks such as cooking, washing, and lifting.","zh":"評估會詢問煮食、洗澡和扶抱等各類任務。"},{"en":"Different sorts of tasks may require different kinds of support.","zh":"不同類型的任務可能需要不同支援。"},{"en":"Listing the tasks clearly helps others understand the carer’s workload.","zh":"清楚列出任務，可以幫助別人了解照顧者的工作量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"help with getting dressed","meaning":"幫忙穿衣服","examples":[{"en":"Her mother needs help with getting dressed.","zh":"她母親需要幫忙穿衣服。"},{"en":"Help with getting dressed means assistance with putting on clothes.","zh":"Help with getting dressed 指協助穿上衣服。"},{"en":"Carol gives her mother help with getting dressed every morning.","zh":"Carol 每天早上幫母親穿衣服。"},{"en":"Someone with weak hands or poor balance may need help getting dressed safely.","zh":"手部無力或平衡力差的人，可能需要安全地幫忙穿衣服。"},{"en":"This kind of help protects dignity when it is done patiently and respectfully.","zh":"這類幫助如果耐心而尊重地進行，可以保護被照顧者尊嚴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"help someone get into the shower","meaning":"幫某人進淋浴間","examples":[{"en":"Carol helps her mother get into the shower in the morning.","zh":"Carol 早上幫母親進淋浴間。"},{"en":"To help someone get into the shower means to assist them to enter the shower area safely.","zh":"Help someone get into the shower 指協助某人安全進入淋浴區。"},{"en":"A carer may help an elderly person get into the shower to prevent slipping.","zh":"照顧者可能幫長者進淋浴間，以防滑倒。"},{"en":"Handrails and non-slip mats can make showering safer.","zh":"扶手和防滑墊可以令洗澡更安全。"},{"en":"Helping someone shower requires respect for privacy and safety.","zh":"幫助某人洗澡需要尊重私隱和注意安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"that sort of thing","meaning":"這類事情","examples":[{"en":"Tom says that getting dressed and showering are that sort of thing.","zh":"Tom 說穿衣和洗澡都屬於這類事情。"},{"en":"“That sort of thing” means similar types of actions, tasks, or examples.","zh":"「That sort of thing」指相似類型的行動、任務或例子。"},{"en":"The assessment asks about cooking, washing, shopping, and that sort of thing.","zh":"評估會問煮食、洗衣、購物和這類事情。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and avoids listing every possible example.","zh":"這個短語較口語，可以避免列出所有可能例子。"},{"en":"It is useful when the listener already understands the general category.","zh":"當聽者已明白大致類別時，這個說法很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"do the shopping for someone","meaning":"替某人購物","examples":[{"en":"They may ask whether Carol does the shopping for her mother.","zh":"他們可能會問 Carol 是否替母親購物。"},{"en":"To do the shopping for someone means to buy food or other necessary items for that person.","zh":"Do the shopping for someone 指為某人購買食物或其他必需品。"},{"en":"Ben does the shopping for his grandfather every Friday.","zh":"Ben 每星期五替祖父購物。"},{"en":"Doing the shopping for someone can help them stay at home safely.","zh":"替某人購物可以幫助他們安全留在家中。"},{"en":"Shopping for another person requires knowing what they need and can eat.","zh":"替別人購物需要知道他們需要甚麼和能吃甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at mealtimes","meaning":"在用餐時","examples":[{"en":"Carol may need to help her mother at mealtimes.","zh":"Carol 可能需要在用餐時幫助母親。"},{"en":"At mealtimes means during breakfast, lunch, dinner, or other times when people eat.","zh":"At mealtimes 指在早餐、午餐、晚餐或其他進食時間。"},{"en":"Some elderly people need reminders at mealtimes.","zh":"有些長者在用餐時需要提醒。"},{"en":"At mealtimes, carers may prepare food, serve drinks, or check medicine.","zh":"在用餐時，照顧者可能要準備食物、遞飲品或檢查藥物。"},{"en":"Regular support at mealtimes can help a person eat enough.","zh":"用餐時的定期支援可以幫助一個人吃得足夠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cope with money","meaning":"應付金錢；處理金錢","examples":[{"en":"They may ask whether her mother can cope with money.","zh":"他們可能會問她母親能否應付金錢。"},{"en":"To cope with money means to manage payments, change, bills, or financial decisions.","zh":"Cope with money 指處理付款、找續、帳單或財務決定。"},{"en":"Carol’s mother finds it harder to cope with money at the supermarket.","zh":"Carol 的母親在超級市場處理金錢時越來越困難。"},{"en":"Memory problems can make coping with money difficult.","zh":"記憶問題可以令處理金錢變得困難。"},{"en":"Someone who cannot cope with money may need help to avoid mistakes or scams.","zh":"無法處理金錢的人可能需要幫助，以避免錯誤或騙案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"become a bit of a problem","meaning":"變成一個小問題","examples":[{"en":"Using money is becoming a bit of a problem for Carol’s mother.","zh":"使用金錢對 Carol 的母親來說正變成一個小問題。"},{"en":"If something is becoming a bit of a problem, it is starting to cause difficulty or concern.","zh":"如果某事 is becoming a bit of a problem，即表示它開始造成困難或擔憂。"},{"en":"Remembering appointments is becoming a bit of a problem for him.","zh":"記住預約時間對他來說開始變成一個問題。"},{"en":"A small problem can become serious if it is ignored.","zh":"如果小問題被忽視，可能會變得嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds gentle, but it may introduce an important issue.","zh":"這個說法語氣溫和，但可能引出重要問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"used to be good at something","meaning":"以前很擅長某事","examples":[{"en":"Carol’s mother used to be very good at using money.","zh":"Carol 的母親以前很擅長使用金錢。"},{"en":"To used to be good at something means someone was skilled at it in the past, but the situation may have changed.","zh":"Used to be good at something 指某人過去擅長某事，但情況現在可能已改變。"},{"en":"My grandfather used to be good at fixing radios.","zh":"我祖父以前很擅長修理收音機。"},{"en":"People may lose confidence when they can no longer do things they used to be good at.","zh":"當人們不能再做到以前擅長的事情時，可能會失去信心。"},{"en":"The phrase compares past ability with the present.","zh":"這個短語把過去能力與現在作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not any more","meaning":"不再","examples":[{"en":"She used to be good at using money, but not any more.","zh":"她以前很擅長使用金錢，但現在不再是這樣。"},{"en":"“Not any more” means something was true before but is no longer true now.","zh":"「Not any more」表示某事以前是真的，但現在不再如此。"},{"en":"He used to drive every day, but not any more.","zh":"他以前每天駕車，但現在不再這樣。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly contrasts past habits or abilities with the present.","zh":"這個短語清楚對比過去習慣或能力與現在情況。"},{"en":"It can sound sad when it describes a lost ability.","zh":"當它描述失去的能力時，可能聽起來令人難過。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be ready to tell someone about","meaning":"準備好告訴某人……","examples":[{"en":"Carol should be ready to tell them about difficult aspects of caring.","zh":"Carol 應準備好告訴他們照顧工作中的困難方面。"},{"en":"To be ready to tell someone about something means to prepare yourself to explain it clearly.","zh":"Be ready to tell someone about 某事，指準備好清楚向某人解釋。"},{"en":"Before the assessment, be ready to tell the worker about daily problems.","zh":"評估前，應準備好告訴工作人員日常問題。"},{"en":"Preparing examples helps people explain difficult situations honestly.","zh":"準備例子可以幫助人們誠實解釋困難情況。"},{"en":"Being ready to speak can make an assessment more useful.","zh":"準備好表達，可以令評估更有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"particularly difficult","meaning":"特別困難","examples":[{"en":"She should describe anything she finds particularly difficult.","zh":"她應描述任何她覺得特別困難的事情。"},{"en":"Particularly difficult means especially hard compared with other things.","zh":"Particularly difficult 指與其他事情相比尤其困難。"},{"en":"Lifting her mother safely is particularly difficult for Carol.","zh":"對 Carol 來說，安全扶起母親特別困難。"},{"en":"A task may be particularly difficult because it is emotional, physical, or time-consuming.","zh":"一項任務可能因情感、身體或時間因素而特別困難。"},{"en":"Identifying what is particularly difficult helps support workers target help.","zh":"找出特別困難的地方，可以幫助支援人員提供針對性協助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"caring for someone","meaning":"照顧某人","examples":[{"en":"Carol finds some parts of caring for her mother difficult.","zh":"Carol 覺得照顧母親的某些部分很困難。"},{"en":"Caring for someone means helping and supporting a person who cannot manage fully alone.","zh":"Caring for someone 指幫助和支援不能完全獨立生活的人。"},{"en":"Caring for someone may involve physical help, emotional support, and daily planning.","zh":"照顧某人可能涉及身體協助、情感支援和日常規劃。"},{"en":"People caring for someone often need breaks and advice.","zh":"照顧別人的人通常需要休息和建議。"},{"en":"Caring can be meaningful, but it can also affect the carer’s health and social life.","zh":"照顧工作可以很有意義，但也可能影響照顧者的健康和社交生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"recently I’ve noticed","meaning":"最近我注意到","examples":[{"en":"Recently, Carol has noticed problems with her mother’s memory.","zh":"最近，Carol 注意到母親的記憶力出現問題。"},{"en":"“Recently I’ve noticed” introduces something the speaker has begun to observe in the near past.","zh":"「Recently I’ve noticed」用來引出說話者近來開始觀察到的事情。"},{"en":"Recently I’ve noticed that Dad forgets appointments more often.","zh":"最近我注意到爸爸更常忘記預約。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when describing a new or developing concern.","zh":"這個短語適合描述新出現或正在發展的擔憂。"},{"en":"Noticing changes early can help families seek support sooner.","zh":"及早注意變化，可以幫助家庭更早尋求支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have problems with memory","meaning":"記憶力有問題","examples":[{"en":"Carol’s mother has started to have problems with memory.","zh":"Carol 的母親開始記憶力有問題。"},{"en":"To have problems with memory means to find it difficult to remember information, events, or routines.","zh":"Have problems with memory 指難以記住資料、事件或日常程序。"},{"en":"He has problems with memory and often forgets where he put his keys.","zh":"他記憶力有問題，常忘記把鎖匙放在哪裏。"},{"en":"Memory problems can make daily tasks and safety more difficult.","zh":"記憶問題可以令日常任務和安全變得更困難。"},{"en":"Families should seek advice if memory problems become frequent or serious.","zh":"如果記憶問題變得頻繁或嚴重，家人應尋求建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"quite bad problems with","meaning":"相當嚴重的……問題","examples":[{"en":"She has started to have quite bad problems with her memory.","zh":"她開始有相當嚴重的記憶問題。"},{"en":"Quite bad problems with something means fairly serious difficulties in that area.","zh":"Quite bad problems with 某方面，指在該方面有頗嚴重困難。"},{"en":"The patient has quite bad problems with balance, so walking alone is risky.","zh":"病人的平衡力有相當嚴重問題，所以獨自行走有風險。"},{"en":"Quite bad problems should not be ignored just because they are not yet extreme.","zh":"相當嚴重的問題即使尚未到極端程度，也不應被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests the issue is more than a small inconvenience.","zh":"這個短語表示問題不只是小小不便。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"if I wasn’t there","meaning":"如果我不在的話","examples":[{"en":"If Carol wasn’t there, her mother might forget to eat.","zh":"如果 Carol 不在的話，她母親可能會忘記吃飯。"},{"en":"“If I wasn’t there” describes what might happen without the speaker’s presence or help.","zh":"「If I wasn’t there」描述如果說話者不在場或沒有幫忙，可能會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"If I wasn’t there, my grandfather might forget his medicine.","zh":"如果我不在的話，祖父可能會忘記吃藥。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how important the carer’s role has become.","zh":"這個短語顯示照顧者角色已變得多麼重要。"},{"en":"It can also reveal the risk if support is not available.","zh":"它也可以揭示如果沒有支援會出現的風險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"forget to do something","meaning":"忘記做某事","examples":[{"en":"Carol thinks her mother would forget to eat.","zh":"Carol 認為她母親會忘記吃飯。"},{"en":"To forget to do something means to fail to remember to do a planned or necessary action.","zh":"Forget to do something 指沒有記起去做已計劃或必要的行動。"},{"en":"He forgot to take his medicine after breakfast.","zh":"他早餐後忘記吃藥。"},{"en":"Forgetting to eat or drink can become dangerous for elderly people.","zh":"忘記吃飯或喝水可能對長者造成危險。"},{"en":"Reminders, notes, or carers can help someone remember daily tasks.","zh":"提醒、紙條或照顧者可以幫助某人記住日常任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not seem quite sure","meaning":"似乎不太確定","examples":[{"en":"Her mother does not seem quite sure what day it is.","zh":"她母親似乎不太確定今天是星期幾。"},{"en":"To not seem quite sure means to appear uncertain or confused about something.","zh":"Not seem quite sure 指看起來對某事不確定或感到混亂。"},{"en":"He did not seem quite sure where he had parked the car.","zh":"他似乎不太確定自己把車停在哪裏。"},{"en":"Someone with memory problems may not seem sure about dates or appointments.","zh":"有記憶問題的人可能不太確定日期或預約。"},{"en":"The phrase is gentle and describes uncertainty without sounding too harsh.","zh":"這個短語語氣溫和，用來描述不確定而不會太嚴厲。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"what day it is","meaning":"今天是星期幾","examples":[{"en":"Her mother often does not know what day it is.","zh":"她母親經常不知道今天是星期幾。"},{"en":"What day it is means which day of the week or date it is today.","zh":"What day it is 指今天是星期幾或甚麼日期。"},{"en":"After staying in hospital, he sometimes forgot what day it was.","zh":"住院後，他有時會忘記今天是星期幾。"},{"en":"Not knowing what day it is can make appointments and medicine routines difficult.","zh":"不知道今天是星期幾，可能令預約和服藥安排變得困難。"},{"en":"Calendars and daily reminders can help someone keep track of the day.","zh":"日曆和每日提醒可以幫助某人掌握日期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"physical difficulties","meaning":"身體上的困難","examples":[{"en":"Tom asks whether Carol has any physical difficulties caring for her mother.","zh":"Tom 問 Carol 照顧母親時是否有任何身體上的困難。"},{"en":"Physical difficulties are problems involving the body, such as lifting, moving, pain, or tiredness.","zh":"身體上的困難，是涉及身體的問題，例如扶抱、移動、疼痛或疲倦。"},{"en":"Carol has physical difficulties when helping her mother stand up.","zh":"Carol 幫母親站起來時有身體上的困難。"},{"en":"Physical difficulties can make caring unsafe for both the carer and the patient.","zh":"身體上的困難可能令照顧者和被照顧者都不安全。"},{"en":"Equipment and training can reduce physical difficulties in care work.","zh":"設備和訓練可以減少照顧工作中的身體困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lift someone","meaning":"扶起某人；抬起某人","examples":[{"en":"Carol finds lifting her mother physically difficult.","zh":"Carol 覺得扶起母親在身體上很困難。"},{"en":"To lift someone means to raise or help move their body, often from a chair, bed, or floor.","zh":"Lift someone 指扶起或移動某人的身體，常見於從椅子、床或地上移動。"},{"en":"Nurses are trained to lift patients safely.","zh":"護士接受訓練，學習安全扶起病人。"},{"en":"Lifting someone incorrectly can injure the carer’s back.","zh":"不正確地扶起某人可能令照顧者背部受傷。"},{"en":"Mechanical aids may help carers lift someone with less risk.","zh":"機械輔助設備可以幫助照顧者較安全地扶起某人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be afraid of doing something","meaning":"擔心做某事；害怕做某事","examples":[{"en":"Carol is afraid of hurting her back.","zh":"Carol 擔心傷到自己的背部。"},{"en":"To be afraid of doing something means to worry that an action may lead to something bad.","zh":"Be afraid of doing something 指擔心某項行動會導致不好的結果。"},{"en":"He is afraid of falling when he walks down the stairs.","zh":"他害怕下樓梯時跌倒。"},{"en":"Carers may be afraid of lifting someone without proper training.","zh":"照顧者如果沒有接受適當訓練，可能會害怕扶起某人。"},{"en":"Fear can be useful if it encourages people to ask for safer methods.","zh":"如果恐懼促使人尋求更安全方法，它也可以是有用的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hurt my back","meaning":"傷到背部","examples":[{"en":"Carol is worried that she might hurt her back.","zh":"Carol 擔心自己可能會傷到背部。"},{"en":"To hurt my back means to injure or strain the muscles, bones, or joints in my back.","zh":"Hurt my back 指令背部肌肉、骨骼或關節受傷或拉傷。"},{"en":"I hurt my back when I lifted the heavy box incorrectly.","zh":"我錯誤搬起重箱時傷到背部。"},{"en":"Carers should learn safe lifting techniques to avoid hurting their backs.","zh":"照顧者應學習安全扶抱技巧，以避免傷到背部。"},{"en":"A back injury can make daily caring tasks much harder.","zh":"背部受傷會令日常照顧任務困難得多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be in real trouble","meaning":"真的會很麻煩","examples":[{"en":"Carol would be in real trouble if she hurt her back.","zh":"如果 Carol 傷到背部，她真的會很麻煩。"},{"en":"To be in real trouble means to face a serious problem or difficult situation.","zh":"Be in real trouble 指面對嚴重問題或困難處境。"},{"en":"If the only carer becomes ill, the family may be in real trouble.","zh":"如果唯一的照顧者生病，這個家庭可能真的會很麻煩。"},{"en":"A back injury could leave Carol in real trouble because her mother depends on her.","zh":"背部受傷可能令 Carol 陷入大麻煩，因為母親依賴她。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the consequences would be serious, not minor.","zh":"這個短語顯示後果會很嚴重，而不是小事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"give someone advice about","meaning":"就……給某人建議","examples":[{"en":"The council can give Carol advice about lifting her mother safely.","zh":"地方議會可以就如何安全扶起母親給 Carol 建議。"},{"en":"To give someone advice about something means to offer guidance or suggestions on that topic.","zh":"Give someone advice about 某事，指就該主題向某人提供指引或建議。"},{"en":"A nurse can give carers advice about safe movement.","zh":"護士可以就安全移動給照顧者建議。"},{"en":"Good advice should be practical and suited to the person’s situation.","zh":"好建議應該實用，並適合當事人的情況。"},{"en":"Advice about lifting can prevent injuries and falls.","zh":"關於扶抱的建議可以預防受傷和跌倒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"avoid the possibility of","meaning":"避免……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"They can advise her how to avoid the possibility of her mother having a fall.","zh":"他們可以建議她如何避免母親跌倒的可能性。"},{"en":"To avoid the possibility of something means to reduce the chance that it will happen.","zh":"Avoid the possibility of 某事，指減低該事發生的機會。"},{"en":"Remove loose rugs to avoid the possibility of someone tripping.","zh":"移走鬆動地氈，以避免有人絆倒的可能性。"},{"en":"Good lighting can help avoid the possibility of falls at night.","zh":"良好照明可以幫助避免夜間跌倒的可能性。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used when discussing prevention and safety.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論預防和安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have a fall","meaning":"跌倒；跌一跤","examples":[{"en":"Carol wants to prevent her mother from having a fall.","zh":"Carol 想防止母親跌倒。"},{"en":"To have a fall means to fall down accidentally, often causing injury.","zh":"Have a fall 指意外跌倒，常可能造成受傷。"},{"en":"Elderly people may have a fall if the floor is wet or uneven.","zh":"如果地面濕滑或不平，長者可能會跌倒。"},{"en":"A fall can lead to broken bones, fear, and loss of confidence.","zh":"跌倒可以導致骨折、恐懼和失去信心。"},{"en":"Handrails, good lighting, and clear floors can reduce the risk of a fall.","zh":"扶手、良好照明和清空地面可以減少跌倒風險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"once they have done the assessment","meaning":"一旦他們完成評估","examples":[{"en":"Once they have done the assessment, Carol may receive support.","zh":"一旦他們完成評估，Carol 可能會獲得支援。"},{"en":"Once they have done the assessment means after the assessment has been completed.","zh":"Once they have done the assessment 指評估完成之後。"},{"en":"Once they have done the assessment, the council will decide what help is suitable.","zh":"一旦他們完成評估，地方議會便會決定甚麼幫助合適。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one step must happen before the next step begins.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個步驟必須先完成，下一步才會開始。"},{"en":"Support decisions often depend on what the assessment finds.","zh":"支援決定通常取決於評估結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be eligible","meaning":"符合資格","examples":[{"en":"If Carol is eligible, she may receive financial support.","zh":"如果 Carol 符合資格，她可能會獲得經濟支援。"},{"en":"To be eligible means to meet the rules or conditions needed to receive something or take part.","zh":"Be eligible 指符合獲得某物或參與某事所需的規則或條件。"},{"en":"People over sixty-five may be eligible for this service.","zh":"六十五歲以上人士可能符合資格使用這項服務。"},{"en":"Eligibility can depend on income, health, caring hours, or local rules.","zh":"資格可能取決於收入、健康、照顧時間或本地規則。"},{"en":"Someone may need an assessment before being confirmed as eligible.","zh":"某人可能需要接受評估後，才確認是否符合資格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"what happens next","meaning":"接下來會怎樣","examples":[{"en":"Carol asks what happens next after the assessment.","zh":"Carol 問評估後接下來會怎樣。"},{"en":"“What happens next?” asks about the next step in a process or situation.","zh":"「What happens next?」用來詢問一個過程或情況中的下一步。"},{"en":"The form is finished. What happens next?","zh":"表格填好了。接下來會怎樣？"},{"en":"This question is useful when someone needs to understand a procedure.","zh":"當某人需要了解程序時，這個問題很有用。"},{"en":"Clear explanations of what happens next can reduce anxiety.","zh":"清楚解釋接下來會怎樣，可以減少焦慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"support someone financially","meaning":"在經濟上支援某人","examples":[{"en":"The council might support Carol financially.","zh":"地方議會可能在經濟上支援 Carol。"},{"en":"To support someone financially means to give them money or help with costs.","zh":"Support someone financially 指給某人金錢或協助支付費用。"},{"en":"The charity supports families financially when medical bills are high.","zh":"醫療費高昂時，慈善機構會在經濟上支援家庭。"},{"en":"Financial support can help carers pay for transport, equipment, or services.","zh":"經濟支援可以幫助照顧者支付交通、設備或服務費用。"},{"en":"Supporting someone financially may reduce stress but may not solve every problem.","zh":"在經濟上支援某人可以減輕壓力，但未必能解決所有問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"transport costs","meaning":"交通費","examples":[{"en":"They might help Carol with transport costs.","zh":"他們可能幫助 Carol 支付交通費。"},{"en":"Transport costs are expenses for travelling from one place to another.","zh":"交通費是從一個地方前往另一個地方所需的費用。"},{"en":"Transport costs may include taxi fares, petrol, bus tickets, or parking fees.","zh":"交通費可能包括的士費、汽油費、巴士票或泊車費。"},{"en":"Regular hospital visits can make transport costs expensive for carers.","zh":"定期到醫院覆診可能令照顧者的交通費變得昂貴。"},{"en":"Help with transport costs can make appointments easier to attend.","zh":"交通費支援可以令赴約更容易。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get a taxi","meaning":"叫的士","examples":[{"en":"Carol might need to get a taxi to take her mother to an appointment.","zh":"Carol 可能需要叫的士帶母親去赴約。"},{"en":"To get a taxi means to take or arrange a taxi for a journey.","zh":"Get a taxi 指乘搭或安排的士出行。"},{"en":"We got a taxi because the bus stop was too far away.","zh":"因為巴士站太遠，我們叫了的士。"},{"en":"A taxi may be safer for an elderly person who cannot walk far.","zh":"對不能走太遠的長者來說，的士可能較安全。"},{"en":"Getting a taxi regularly can become expensive.","zh":"經常叫的士可能變得昂貴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take someone for an appointment","meaning":"帶某人去赴約","examples":[{"en":"Carol sometimes has to take her mother for an appointment.","zh":"Carol 有時必須帶母親去赴約。"},{"en":"To take someone for an appointment means to bring them to a planned meeting, usually medical or official.","zh":"Take someone for an appointment 指帶某人前往已安排的會面，通常是醫療或正式約見。"},{"en":"Ben takes his father for a hospital appointment every month.","zh":"Ben 每月帶父親去醫院赴約。"},{"en":"Taking someone to appointments may require transport, waiting time, and paperwork.","zh":"帶某人赴約可能需要交通、等候時間和文件。"},{"en":"Carers often arrange their own schedules around appointments.","zh":"照顧者常要圍繞預約安排自己的時間表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"drive someone myself","meaning":"親自開車載某人","examples":[{"en":"Carol usually drives her mother herself.","zh":"Carol 通常親自開車載母親。"},{"en":"To drive someone myself means to personally take someone somewhere by car.","zh":"Drive someone myself 指親自駕車載某人到某地。"},{"en":"I usually drive my grandmother myself because she finds buses difficult.","zh":"我通常親自開車載祖母，因為她覺得坐巴士困難。"},{"en":"Driving someone yourself can be convenient, but fuel and parking cost money.","zh":"親自開車載某人可以很方便，但汽油和泊車都要費用。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises that the speaker does the driving personally.","zh":"這個短語強調是說話者本人負責駕車。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"claim for the petrol","meaning":"申請汽油費補助；申領汽油費","examples":[{"en":"Carol asks whether she can claim for the petrol.","zh":"Carol 問她是否可以申領汽油費。"},{"en":"To claim for the petrol means to request repayment or financial help for petrol costs.","zh":"Claim for the petrol 指申請報銷或資助汽油費。"},{"en":"Volunteers can claim for the petrol used during official visits.","zh":"義工可以申領官方探訪期間使用的汽油費。"},{"en":"Keeping receipts helps people claim travel costs accurately.","zh":"保留收據可以幫助人們準確申領交通費用。"},{"en":"Rules may state which journeys can be claimed for and which cannot.","zh":"規則可能列明哪些旅程可以申領，哪些不可以。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"claim for the insurance","meaning":"申請保險費補助","examples":[{"en":"Carol can claim for the insurance too.","zh":"Carol 也可以申請保險費補助。"},{"en":"To claim for the insurance means to request payment or support connected with insurance costs.","zh":"Claim for the insurance 指申請與保險費相關的付款或支援。"},{"en":"The carer asked whether she could claim for the insurance on her car.","zh":"照顧者詢問是否可以申領汽車保險費。"},{"en":"Insurance claims often require documents, receipts, or proof of use.","zh":"申請保險相關補助通常需要文件、收據或使用證明。"},{"en":"Being allowed to claim insurance costs can reduce the financial burden of caring.","zh":"能夠申領保險費，可以減輕照顧工作的財政負擔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"help with the housework","meaning":"幫忙做家務","examples":[{"en":"The council can arrange help with the housework.","zh":"地方議會可以安排幫忙做家務。"},{"en":"Help with the housework means assistance with cleaning, laundry, cooking, or other home tasks.","zh":"Help with the housework 指協助清潔、洗衣、煮食或其他家居任務。"},{"en":"A support worker came twice a week to help with the housework.","zh":"一名支援工作者每週來兩次幫忙做家務。"},{"en":"Housework support can give carers more time to rest or attend appointments.","zh":"家務支援可以讓照顧者有更多時間休息或赴約。"},{"en":"Even simple help with housework can make daily life easier.","zh":"即使是簡單的家務協助，也可以令日常生活更容易。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"arrange for someone to come along","meaning":"安排某人過來","examples":[{"en":"They can arrange for someone to come along once or twice a week.","zh":"他們可以安排某人每週過來一兩次。"},{"en":"To arrange for someone to come along means to organise a person to visit or help.","zh":"Arrange for someone to come along 指安排某人到訪或提供幫助。"},{"en":"The council arranged for a care worker to come along on Mondays.","zh":"地方議會安排一名照顧工作者逢星期一過來。"},{"en":"Regular visits can reduce the pressure on family carers.","zh":"定期探訪可以減輕家庭照顧者壓力。"},{"en":"Arranging for help requires choosing suitable times and clear tasks.","zh":"安排幫助需要選擇合適時間和清楚任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"once or twice a week","meaning":"每週一兩次","examples":[{"en":"Someone could come along once or twice a week.","zh":"有人可以每週過來一兩次。"},{"en":"Once or twice a week means one or two times each week.","zh":"Once or twice a week 指每週一次或兩次。"},{"en":"A helper visits once or twice a week to clean and check supplies.","zh":"助手每週探訪一兩次，負責清潔和檢查物資。"},{"en":"Support once or twice a week may be enough for some families but not others.","zh":"每週一兩次支援對某些家庭可能足夠，但對其他家庭未必足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate frequency, not a daily schedule.","zh":"這個短語表示大概頻率，而不是每日安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"I hope you don’t mind me saying this","meaning":"希望你不介意我這樣說","examples":[{"en":"Tom says, “I hope you don’t mind me saying this.”","zh":"Tom 說：「希望你不介意我這樣說。」"},{"en":"“I hope you don’t mind me saying this” politely introduces a personal or sensitive comment.","zh":"「I hope you don’t mind me saying this」用來有禮貌地引出個人或敏感評論。"},{"en":"I hope you don’t mind me saying this, but you look very tired.","zh":"希望你不介意我這樣說，但你看起來很疲倦。"},{"en":"The phrase softens advice that might feel direct or uncomfortable.","zh":"這個短語可以緩和可能顯得直接或令人不舒服的建議。"},{"en":"It shows the speaker wants to be helpful, not rude.","zh":"它表示說話者想幫忙，而不是無禮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"look after yourself","meaning":"照顧好自己","examples":[{"en":"Tom tells Carol that she needs to look after herself.","zh":"Tom 告訴 Carol，她需要照顧好自己。"},{"en":"To look after yourself means to take care of your own health, rest, and wellbeing.","zh":"Look after yourself 指照顧自己的健康、休息和福祉。"},{"en":"Carers must look after themselves if they want to continue helping others.","zh":"照顧者如果想繼續幫助別人，就必須照顧好自己。"},{"en":"Eating properly and sleeping enough are ways to look after yourself.","zh":"好好飲食和睡眠充足都是照顧自己的方法。"},{"en":"Looking after yourself is not selfish; it helps you stay strong.","zh":"照顧好自己並不是自私，而是幫助自己保持力量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"it seems to me","meaning":"我覺得；在我看來","examples":[{"en":"It seems to Tom that Carol is under quite a bit of stress.","zh":"在 Tom 看來，Carol 承受不少壓力。"},{"en":"“It seems to me” introduces a personal impression or opinion.","zh":"「It seems to me」用來引出個人印象或意見。"},{"en":"It seems to me that you need more support at home.","zh":"我覺得你在家中需要更多支援。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds less forceful than saying “I know.”","zh":"這個短語比說「我知道」語氣較不強硬。"},{"en":"It allows the speaker to share an observation politely.","zh":"它讓說話者有禮貌地分享觀察。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"under quite a bit of stress","meaning":"承受不少壓力","examples":[{"en":"Carol is under quite a bit of stress.","zh":"Carol 承受不少壓力。"},{"en":"To be under quite a bit of stress means to be experiencing a noticeable amount of pressure or worry.","zh":"Be under quite a bit of stress 指正在經歷相當明顯的壓力或憂慮。"},{"en":"She is under quite a bit of stress because she cares for her mother day and night.","zh":"她日夜照顧母親，因此承受不少壓力。"},{"en":"Stress can affect sleep, mood, health, and patience.","zh":"壓力可以影響睡眠、情緒、健康和耐性。"},{"en":"People under stress may need both emotional and practical support.","zh":"承受壓力的人可能需要情感和實際支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"give advice on how to","meaning":"就如何……提供建議","examples":[{"en":"The council may give Carol advice on how to reduce stress.","zh":"地方議會可能就如何減低壓力給 Carol 建議。"},{"en":"To give advice on how to do something means to explain practical ways of doing it.","zh":"Give advice on how to 做某事，指解釋實際方法。"},{"en":"A nurse can give advice on how to prevent falls at home.","zh":"護士可以就如何在家中預防跌倒提供建議。"},{"en":"Good advice should be clear, realistic, and suited to the person’s life.","zh":"好建議應清楚、實際，並適合當事人的生活。"},{"en":"Advice on how to manage stress can help carers protect their own health.","zh":"關於如何管理壓力的建議，可以幫助照顧者保護自己的健康。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"minimise stress","meaning":"減低壓力","examples":[{"en":"They may give Carol advice on how to minimise stress.","zh":"他們可能給 Carol 建議，教她如何減低壓力。"},{"en":"To minimise stress means to reduce stress as much as possible.","zh":"Minimise stress 指盡量減少壓力。"},{"en":"Planning breaks can help carers minimise stress.","zh":"安排休息時間可以幫助照顧者減低壓力。"},{"en":"Sharing tasks with others may minimise stress and prevent exhaustion.","zh":"與他人分擔任務可以減低壓力並防止過度疲勞。"},{"en":"Stress may not disappear completely, but it can often be reduced.","zh":"壓力未必會完全消失，但通常可以減少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"feel so much better","meaning":"感覺好多了","examples":[{"en":"Carol feels so much better after talking to Tom.","zh":"Carol 與 Tom 交談後感覺好多了。"},{"en":"To feel so much better means to feel a lot more comfortable, hopeful, or relieved.","zh":"Feel so much better 指感到舒服、安心或有希望得多。"},{"en":"After speaking to the nurse, Carol felt so much better.","zh":"與護士交談後，Carol 感覺好多了。"},{"en":"Good advice can make a worried person feel much better.","zh":"好建議可以令憂慮的人感覺好多了。"},{"en":"Feeling better does not solve everything, but it can give someone energy to act.","zh":"感覺好些不代表解決所有問題，但可以給人行動的力量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"having talked to you","meaning":"跟你談過之後","examples":[{"en":"Carol feels better having talked to Tom.","zh":"跟 Tom 談過之後，Carol 感覺好多了。"},{"en":"“Having talked to you” means after talking to you.","zh":"Having talked to you 指跟你交談之後。"},{"en":"Having talked to the adviser, I understand the process more clearly.","zh":"跟顧問談過之後，我更清楚了解程序。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the conversation has changed how someone feels or thinks.","zh":"這個短語顯示對話改變了某人的感受或想法。"},{"en":"It is often used to explain the reason for a later feeling or decision.","zh":"它常用來解釋之後的感受或決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"get in touch with","meaning":"聯絡","examples":[{"en":"Carol will get in touch with the council straight away.","zh":"Carol 會立即聯絡地方議會。"},{"en":"To get in touch with someone means to contact them by phone, email, message, or visit.","zh":"Get in touch with 某人或機構，指透過電話、電郵、訊息或探訪聯絡。"},{"en":"You should get in touch with the local council if you need care support.","zh":"如果你需要照顧支援，應聯絡地方議會。"},{"en":"Getting in touch early can help problems be dealt with sooner.","zh":"及早聯絡可以幫助問題更快處理。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in both spoken and written English.","zh":"這個短語常見於口語和書面英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"straight away","meaning":"馬上；立即","examples":[{"en":"Carol will contact the council straight away.","zh":"Carol 會馬上聯絡地方議會。"},{"en":"Straight away means immediately or without delay.","zh":"Straight away 指立即或毫不拖延。"},{"en":"If someone falls, call for help straight away.","zh":"如果有人跌倒，應立即求助。"},{"en":"Acting straight away can prevent a small problem from becoming worse.","zh":"立即行動可以防止小問題惡化。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in spoken English and sounds urgent but natural.","zh":"這個短語常見於口語英語，聽起來有急切感但自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Help for carers","meaning":"照顧者支援","examples":[{"en":"The leaflet gives information about help for carers.","zh":"這份單張提供關於照顧者支援的資料。"},{"en":"Help for carers means support, advice, or services for people who look after others.","zh":"照顧者支援指為照顧他人的人提供的支援、建議或服務。"},{"en":"Help for carers may include breaks, financial advice, training, and home support.","zh":"照顧者支援可能包括休息安排、財務建議、培訓和家居支援。"},{"en":"A leaflet about help for carers should explain who is eligible.","zh":"關於照顧者支援的單張應解釋誰符合資格。"},{"en":"Carers often need help before they feel completely exhausted.","zh":"照顧者往往在完全精疲力竭前已需要幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"arrange practical support","meaning":"安排實際支援","examples":[{"en":"Local councils can arrange practical support for carers.","zh":"地方議會可以為照顧者安排實際支援。"},{"en":"To arrange practical support means to organise real help with daily tasks or problems.","zh":"Arrange practical support 指安排對日常任務或問題有實際幫助的支援。"},{"en":"The council arranged practical support such as cleaning help and transport advice.","zh":"地方議會安排了清潔幫助和交通建議等實際支援。"},{"en":"Practical support can reduce the pressure on family members.","zh":"實際支援可以減輕家庭成員壓力。"},{"en":"Arranging support requires understanding what the carer and the cared-for person need.","zh":"安排支援需要了解照顧者和被照顧者的需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"elderly people at home","meaning":"在家中的長者","examples":[{"en":"Local councils support those caring for elderly people at home.","zh":"地方議會支援那些在家中照顧長者的人。"},{"en":"Elderly people at home are older people who live in their own homes rather than in care homes or hospitals.","zh":"在家中的長者是住在自己家中，而不是住在院舍或醫院的年長人士。"},{"en":"Many elderly people at home need help with meals, washing, or medicine.","zh":"許多在家中的長者需要膳食、洗澡或服藥方面的幫助。"},{"en":"Supporting elderly people at home can help them remain in familiar surroundings.","zh":"支援在家中的長者，可以幫助他們留在熟悉環境。"},{"en":"Home support should consider both safety and independence.","zh":"家居支援應同時考慮安全和獨立性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"time for other responsibilities","meaning":"處理其他責任的時間","examples":[{"en":"Support can give the carer time for other responsibilities.","zh":"支援可以給照顧者處理其他責任的時間。"},{"en":"Time for other responsibilities means time to deal with duties besides caring.","zh":"Time for other responsibilities 指處理照顧工作以外職責的時間。"},{"en":"A home helper can give Carol time for shopping, bills, and rest.","zh":"家務助手可以給 Carol 時間購物、繳費和休息。"},{"en":"Carers need time for other responsibilities so their own lives do not collapse.","zh":"照顧者需要處理其他責任的時間，讓自己的生活不至於崩潰。"},{"en":"Support that creates time can be as valuable as direct financial help.","zh":"能創造時間的支援可以與直接金錢幫助同樣有價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"assessment of mother’s needs","meaning":"母親需求評估","examples":[{"en":"The assessment of the mother’s needs may include several questions.","zh":"母親需求評估可能包括幾個問題。"},{"en":"An assessment of mother’s needs is a review of what help the mother requires.","zh":"母親需求評估是檢視母親需要哪些幫助。"},{"en":"The assessment of her mother’s needs may cover memory, movement, meals, and safety.","zh":"母親需求評估可能涵蓋記憶、活動、用餐和安全。"},{"en":"A careful assessment helps match support to real daily problems.","zh":"仔細評估可以令支援配合真實日常問題。"},{"en":"The carer should give honest examples during the assessment.","zh":"照顧者在評估期間應提供誠實例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"include discussion of","meaning":"包括討論……","examples":[{"en":"The assessment may include discussion of the caring situation.","zh":"評估可能包括討論照顧情況。"},{"en":"To include discussion of something means to contain a conversation or examination of that topic.","zh":"Include discussion of 某事，指包含對該主題的對話或檢視。"},{"en":"The meeting will include discussion of transport costs.","zh":"會議會包括討論交通費。"},{"en":"A care assessment should include discussion of both physical and emotional needs.","zh":"照顧評估應包括討論身體和情緒需要。"},{"en":"Including discussion of difficult issues helps make the support plan more complete.","zh":"包括討論困難問題，可以令支援計劃更完整。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"how much time the caring involves","meaning":"照顧工作涉及多少時間","examples":[{"en":"The assessment asks how much time the caring involves.","zh":"評估會詢問照顧工作涉及多少時間。"},{"en":"How much time the caring involves means how many hours or how much of the day the care takes.","zh":"How much time the caring involves 指照顧工作需要多少小時或佔用一天中多少時間。"},{"en":"The worker asked how much time caring involved each morning and evening.","zh":"工作人員問早晚照顧工作各涉及多少時間。"},{"en":"Knowing the time involved helps decide whether the carer needs regular breaks.","zh":"知道所需時間有助決定照顧者是否需要定期休息。"},{"en":"Some caring tasks look small but involve many hours each week.","zh":"有些照顧任務看似細小，但每週涉及很多小時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"types of tasks are involved","meaning":"涉及哪些類型的任務","examples":[{"en":"They ask what types of tasks are involved in caring for her mother.","zh":"他們會問照顧母親涉及哪些類型的任務。"},{"en":"“Types of tasks are involved” means what kinds of duties or actions are included.","zh":"Types of tasks are involved 指包括哪些種類的職責或行動。"},{"en":"The assessment asks what types of tasks are involved each day.","zh":"評估會問每天涉及哪些類型的任務。"},{"en":"Different task types may need different skills, equipment, or support.","zh":"不同任務類型可能需要不同技能、設備或支援。"},{"en":"Explaining the tasks involved helps others understand the carer’s workload.","zh":"解釋涉及的任務，可以幫助別人了解照顧者的工作量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"help with dressing","meaning":"幫忙穿衣","examples":[{"en":"Carol gives her mother help with dressing.","zh":"Carol 幫母親穿衣。"},{"en":"Help with dressing means assistance with choosing clothes, putting them on, or fastening them.","zh":"Help with dressing 指協助選衣、穿衣或扣好衣物。"},{"en":"Some elderly people need help with dressing because buttons and zips are difficult.","zh":"有些長者因鈕扣和拉鏈困難而需要幫忙穿衣。"},{"en":"Help with dressing should be given respectfully and patiently.","zh":"幫忙穿衣應以尊重和耐心的方式進行。"},{"en":"Clothing that is easy to put on can reduce the need for help.","zh":"容易穿上的衣物可以減少所需幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"helping someone have a shower","meaning":"幫某人洗澡","examples":[{"en":"Carol is helping her mother have a shower safely.","zh":"Carol 正在安全地幫母親洗澡。"},{"en":"Helping someone have a shower means assisting them to wash safely and comfortably.","zh":"Helping someone have a shower 指協助某人安全舒適地洗澡。"},{"en":"A carer may help someone have a shower by preparing towels and supporting their balance.","zh":"照顧者可以準備毛巾並支撐對方平衡，幫某人洗澡。"},{"en":"Showering support must protect privacy as well as safety.","zh":"洗澡支援必須同時保護私隱和安全。"},{"en":"Non-slip mats and shower chairs can make helping someone shower safer.","zh":"防滑墊和洗澡椅可以令幫人洗澡更安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dealing with money","meaning":"處理金錢","examples":[{"en":"Her mother now has difficulty dealing with money.","zh":"她母親現在處理金錢有困難。"},{"en":"Dealing with money means handling cash, payments, bills, change, or financial decisions.","zh":"Dealing with money 指處理現金、付款、帳單、找續或財務決定。"},{"en":"Dealing with money can become difficult when memory or eyesight declines.","zh":"記憶力或視力下降時，處理金錢可能變得困難。"},{"en":"A trusted family member may help with dealing with bills and payments.","zh":"可信任的家人可以協助處理帳單和付款。"},{"en":"Support with money should protect the person’s independence and safety.","zh":"金錢支援應保護當事人的獨立性和安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"aspects of caring","meaning":"照顧工作的各方面","examples":[{"en":"The assessment covers aspects of caring that are especially difficult.","zh":"評估涵蓋照顧工作中特別困難的各方面。"},{"en":"Aspects of caring are the different parts or areas of the caring role.","zh":"Aspects of caring 指照顧角色中的不同部分或範疇。"},{"en":"Emotional support, lifting, cooking, and medicine are all aspects of caring.","zh":"情感支援、扶抱、煮食和服藥都是照顧工作的各方面。"},{"en":"Some aspects of caring are practical, while others are emotional.","zh":"照顧工作的某些方面是實際的，另一些則是情感上的。"},{"en":"Understanding different aspects of caring helps identify where support is needed.","zh":"了解照顧工作的不同方面，有助找出需要支援的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"especially difficult","meaning":"特別困難","examples":[{"en":"Some aspects of caring are especially difficult for Carol.","zh":"對 Carol 來說，照顧工作的某些方面特別困難。"},{"en":"Especially difficult means more difficult than most other things in the situation.","zh":"Especially difficult 指比該情況中的大多數事情更困難。"},{"en":"Helping her mother move safely is especially difficult in the morning.","zh":"早上幫母親安全移動特別困難。"},{"en":"Tasks can become especially difficult when the carer is tired.","zh":"當照顧者疲倦時，任務可能變得特別困難。"},{"en":"Support should focus first on the parts that are especially difficult.","zh":"支援應先集中在特別困難的部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"loss of memory","meaning":"記憶力衰退","examples":[{"en":"Loss of memory is one of the problems Carol has noticed.","zh":"記憶力衰退是 Carol 注意到的問題之一。"},{"en":"Loss of memory means a reduced ability to remember information, events, or routines.","zh":"記憶力衰退指記住資料、事件或日常程序的能力下降。"},{"en":"Loss of memory may cause someone to forget meals, appointments, or medication.","zh":"記憶力衰退可能令某人忘記用餐、預約或服藥。"},{"en":"Families should note when memory loss happens and how often.","zh":"家人應記下記憶力衰退何時發生以及頻密程度。"},{"en":"Memory loss can affect safety, independence, and confidence.","zh":"記憶力衰退可以影響安全、獨立性和信心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"preventing a fall","meaning":"預防跌倒","examples":[{"en":"The council can give advice on preventing a fall.","zh":"地方議會可以就預防跌倒提供建議。"},{"en":"Preventing a fall means taking steps to stop someone from falling.","zh":"Preventing a fall 指採取措施阻止某人跌倒。"},{"en":"Removing loose wires is one way of preventing a fall at home.","zh":"移走鬆散電線是在家中預防跌倒的方法之一。"},{"en":"Preventing falls is important because elderly people can be seriously injured.","zh":"預防跌倒很重要，因為長者跌倒可能造成嚴重受傷。"},{"en":"Good shoes, handrails, and clear floors all help prevent falls.","zh":"合適鞋子、扶手和清空地面都有助預防跌倒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"types of support","meaning":"支援類型","examples":[{"en":"The form lists different types of support that may be offered.","zh":"表格列出可能提供的不同支援類型。"},{"en":"Types of support are the different forms of help available.","zh":"支援類型是可用幫助的不同形式。"},{"en":"Types of support may include money, transport, housework help, and advice.","zh":"支援類型可能包括金錢、交通、家務協助和建議。"},{"en":"Different carers need different types of support depending on their situation.","zh":"不同照顧者因情況不同而需要不同支援類型。"},{"en":"Knowing the support types helps families ask for the right help.","zh":"了解支援類型可以幫助家庭尋求合適幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"may be offered to carers","meaning":"可能會提供給照顧者","examples":[{"en":"Several types of support may be offered to carers.","zh":"數種支援類型可能會提供給照顧者。"},{"en":"“May be offered to carers” means carers might be given certain forms of help if they qualify.","zh":"「May be offered to carers」指如果照顧者符合資格，可能會獲得某些形式的幫助。"},{"en":"Financial advice may be offered to carers after an assessment.","zh":"評估後，可能會向照顧者提供財務建議。"},{"en":"Home visits may be offered to carers who need practical help.","zh":"對需要實際幫助的照顧者，可能會提供家訪服務。"},{"en":"“May” shows possibility, not a guarantee.","zh":"May 表示可能性，而不是保證。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"car-related costs","meaning":"汽車相關費用","examples":[{"en":"The council may help with car-related costs.","zh":"地方議會可能協助支付汽車相關費用。"},{"en":"Car-related costs are expenses connected with using, maintaining, or insuring a car.","zh":"汽車相關費用是與使用、保養或投保汽車有關的開支。"},{"en":"Petrol, parking, repairs, and insurance are car-related costs.","zh":"汽油、泊車、維修和保險都是汽車相關費用。"},{"en":"Car-related costs can rise when a carer drives someone to frequent appointments.","zh":"當照顧者經常開車帶某人赴約時，汽車相關費用可能增加。"},{"en":"Support with car costs can make medical visits easier to manage.","zh":"汽車費用支援可以令醫療赴約更容易安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fuel and insurance","meaning":"燃油及保險","examples":[{"en":"Fuel and insurance may be included in the support.","zh":"支援可能包括燃油及保險。"},{"en":"Fuel and insurance are costs for running a vehicle and protecting it financially.","zh":"燃油及保險是使用車輛和為車輛提供財務保障的費用。"},{"en":"A carer who drives often may spend a lot on fuel and insurance.","zh":"經常駕車的照顧者可能在燃油及保險上花費很多。"},{"en":"Support with fuel and insurance can reduce the cost of attending appointments.","zh":"燃油及保險支援可以減少赴約成本。"},{"en":"Receipts or documents may be needed when claiming these costs.","zh":"申領這些費用時，可能需要收據或文件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reduce stress","meaning":"減輕壓力","examples":[{"en":"The council may give advice to help reduce stress.","zh":"地方議會可能提供建議，幫助減輕壓力。"},{"en":"To reduce stress means to lower the amount of worry, pressure, or tension someone feels.","zh":"Reduce stress 指降低一個人感受到的憂慮、壓力或緊張程度。"},{"en":"Taking short breaks can help carers reduce stress.","zh":"短暫休息可以幫助照顧者減輕壓力。"},{"en":"Talking to support workers may reduce stress by making problems feel more manageable.","zh":"與支援工作者交談可能令問題感覺較可處理，從而減輕壓力。"},{"en":"Reducing stress is important because long-term stress can affect health.","zh":"減輕壓力很重要，因為長期壓力可以影響健康。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10}],"ielts/listening/Practice 2/task-2":[{"front":"works for","meaning":"為……工作","examples":[{"en":"The man works for Elmleigh Town Council.","zh":"那名男子為 Elmleigh 鎮議會工作。"},{"en":"To work for an organisation means to be employed by it.","zh":"為某機構工作，是指受該機構僱用。"},{"en":"My cousin works for a local charity.","zh":"我的表親為一間本地慈善機構工作。"},{"en":"If you work for the council, you may help organise public services.","zh":"如果你為議會工作，可能會協助安排公共服務。"},{"en":"She works for a company that supports community events.","zh":"她為一間支持社區活動的公司工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Town Council","meaning":"鎮議會","examples":[{"en":"Steve Wainwright works for Elmleigh Town Council.","zh":"Steve Wainwright 為 Elmleigh 鎮議會工作。"},{"en":"A town council is a local government body that manages services and activities in a town.","zh":"鎮議會是管理小鎮服務和活動的地方政府機構。"},{"en":"The Town Council arranged a meeting for residents.","zh":"鎮議會為居民安排了一場會議。"},{"en":"A town council may organise festivals, maintain public areas, and support local groups.","zh":"鎮議會可能會舉辦節慶、維護公共地方和支援本地團體。"},{"en":"Residents can contact the Town Council about community issues.","zh":"居民可以就社區問題聯絡鎮議會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"join the scheme","meaning":"加入計劃","examples":[{"en":"Many people want to join the volunteer scheme.","zh":"許多人想加入義工計劃。"},{"en":"To join the scheme means to become part of an organised programme.","zh":"加入計劃是指成為一個有組織項目的一部分。"},{"en":"Students can join the scheme by completing an online form.","zh":"學生可以透過填寫網上表格加入計劃。"},{"en":"If more people join the scheme, the town can run more community activities.","zh":"如果更多人加入計劃，小鎮便可以舉辦更多社區活動。"},{"en":"Anyone interested in helping local residents may want to join the scheme.","zh":"任何有興趣幫助本地居民的人都可能想加入計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"volunteer scheme","meaning":"義工計劃","examples":[{"en":"I organise the town’s volunteer scheme.","zh":"我負責組織小鎮的義工計劃。"},{"en":"A volunteer scheme is an organised programme in which people help without being paid.","zh":"義工計劃是人們無償提供協助的有組織項目。"},{"en":"The school started a volunteer scheme for students who wanted to serve the community.","zh":"學校為想服務社區的學生開展了一個義工計劃。"},{"en":"A good volunteer scheme gives helpers clear duties and training.","zh":"良好的義工計劃會給義工清晰職責和培訓。"},{"en":"The town’s volunteer scheme helps events run smoothly.","zh":"小鎮的義工計劃幫助活動順利進行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be delighted","meaning":"很高興","examples":[{"en":"I’m delighted you’re all interested in joining the scheme.","zh":"我很高興你們都對加入計劃感興趣。"},{"en":"To be delighted means to be very pleased or happy.","zh":"很高興是指感到非常愉快或滿意。"},{"en":"We are delighted that so many residents came to the meeting.","zh":"這麼多居民來參加會議，我們很高興。"},{"en":"Organisers are delighted when volunteers show strong interest.","zh":"當義工表現出濃厚興趣時，主辦者會很高興。"},{"en":"She was delighted to receive a thank-you message from the community.","zh":"她收到社區的感謝訊息時很高興。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be interested in joining","meaning":"對加入……感興趣","examples":[{"en":"They are interested in joining the volunteer scheme.","zh":"他們對加入義工計劃感興趣。"},{"en":"To be interested in joining means to want to become part of something.","zh":"對加入某事感興趣，是指想成為其中一部分。"},{"en":"Many students are interested in joining the drama club.","zh":"許多學生對加入戲劇學會感興趣。"},{"en":"People who are interested in joining should learn about the duties first.","zh":"對加入有興趣的人應先了解職責。"},{"en":"If you are interested in joining, you can attend the information session.","zh":"如果你對加入感興趣，可以參加簡介會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"create a sense of community","meaning":"建立社區歸屬感","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers help to create a sense of community in the town.","zh":"義工幫助在小鎮建立社區歸屬感。"},{"en":"To create a sense of community means to help people feel connected and part of the same place.","zh":"建立社區歸屬感，是指幫助人們感到彼此連繫，並屬於同一地方。"},{"en":"Local festivals can create a sense of community among residents.","zh":"本地節慶可以在居民之間建立社區歸屬感。"},{"en":"When volunteers welcome visitors, they make the town feel warmer and more united.","zh":"當義工歡迎遊客時，他們令小鎮感覺更溫暖和團結。"},{"en":"Shared activities create a stronger sense of community.","zh":"共同活動能建立更強的社區歸屬感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"historic town","meaning":"歷史悠久的小鎮","examples":[{"en":"Elmleigh is described as a historic town.","zh":"Elmleigh 被形容為一個歷史悠久的小鎮。"},{"en":"A historic town is a town with important old buildings, traditions, or events from the past.","zh":"歷史悠久的小鎮是擁有重要古建築、傳統或過去事件的小鎮。"},{"en":"Tourists visit the historic town to see its ancient market square.","zh":"遊客到這個歷史悠久的小鎮參觀古老市集廣場。"},{"en":"A historic town often needs volunteers to help visitors understand its heritage.","zh":"歷史悠久的小鎮通常需要義工幫助遊客了解其文化遺產。"},{"en":"Living in a historic town can make residents proud of their local identity.","zh":"住在歷史悠久的小鎮，可以令居民對本地身份感到自豪。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"residents and visitors","meaning":"居民和遊客","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers make residents and visitors feel welcome.","zh":"義工令居民和遊客感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"Residents and visitors means people who live in a place and people who come to visit it.","zh":"居民和遊客是指住在某地的人，以及前來參觀的人。"},{"en":"The festival is designed for both residents and visitors.","zh":"這個節日是為居民和遊客而設。"},{"en":"Good signs and friendly volunteers help residents and visitors enjoy local events.","zh":"清楚指示牌和友善義工幫助居民和遊客享受本地活動。"},{"en":"A town council must consider the needs of residents and visitors.","zh":"鎮議會必須考慮居民和遊客的需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"feel welcome","meaning":"感到受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers help people feel welcome at local events.","zh":"義工幫助人們在本地活動中感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"To feel welcome means to feel accepted, comfortable, and wanted in a place.","zh":"感到受歡迎是指在某地方感到被接納、舒服和被重視。"},{"en":"A friendly greeting can make new residents feel welcome.","zh":"友善問候可以令新居民感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"Visitors are more likely to return if they feel welcome.","zh":"如果遊客感到受歡迎，他們較可能再次到訪。"},{"en":"Volunteers help people feel welcome by giving directions and answering questions.","zh":"義工透過指路和回答問題，幫助人們感到受歡迎。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"local events","meaning":"本地活動","examples":[{"en":"Residents and visitors feel welcome at local events.","zh":"居民和遊客在本地活動中感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"Local events are activities organised for people in a particular town or community.","zh":"本地活動是為某個小鎮或社區的人而舉辦的活動。"},{"en":"The town holds local events in the park every summer.","zh":"這個小鎮每年夏天在公園舉辦本地活動。"},{"en":"Local events bring residents together and attract visitors.","zh":"本地活動把居民聚在一起，並吸引遊客。"},{"en":"Volunteers are important because local events often need extra support.","zh":"義工很重要，因為本地活動通常需要額外支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"mention just a few of","meaning":"只簡單提及幾項……","examples":[{"en":"I’ll mention just a few of the activities that volunteers carry out.","zh":"我只會簡單提及義工進行的幾項活動。"},{"en":"To mention just a few of something means to talk briefly about only some examples.","zh":"只簡單提及幾項某事，是指只簡短談及其中一些例子。"},{"en":"I will mention just a few of the clubs you can join.","zh":"我只會簡單提及你可以加入的幾個學會。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that there are more examples than the speaker has time to describe.","zh":"這個短語顯示例子比講者有時間描述的更多。"},{"en":"The organiser mentioned just a few of the volunteer duties during the introduction.","zh":"主辦人在介紹中只簡單提及了幾項義工職責。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"carry out activities","meaning":"進行活動","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers carry out a range of activities in the town.","zh":"義工在鎮內進行一系列活動。"},{"en":"To carry out activities means to do or perform organised tasks.","zh":"進行活動是指做或執行有組織的任務。"},{"en":"Students carry out activities such as cleaning parks and helping visitors.","zh":"學生進行清潔公園和協助遊客等活動。"},{"en":"A volunteer scheme needs clear instructions so people can carry out activities safely.","zh":"義工計劃需要清楚指示，讓人們可以安全進行活動。"},{"en":"Volunteers carry out different activities depending on local needs.","zh":"義工會根據本地需要進行不同活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"walk around the town centre","meaning":"在鎮中心四處巡走","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers walk around the town centre wearing a T-shirt.","zh":"義工穿着 T 恤在鎮中心四處巡走。"},{"en":"To walk around the town centre means to move through the main shopping or public area of the town.","zh":"在鎮中心四處巡走，是指在小鎮主要購物或公共區域中走動。"},{"en":"Volunteers walk around the town centre to answer tourists’ questions.","zh":"義工在鎮中心四處巡走，以回答遊客問題。"},{"en":"Walking around the town centre makes volunteers visible and easy to approach.","zh":"在鎮中心四處巡走令義工容易被看見，也較容易接近。"},{"en":"On busy days, several volunteers walk around the town centre together.","zh":"在繁忙日子，幾名義工會一起在鎮中心四處巡走。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"town centre streets","meaning":"鎮中心街道","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers walk around the town centre streets.","zh":"義工在鎮中心街道四處巡走。"},{"en":"Town centre streets are the roads and pedestrian areas in the main part of a town.","zh":"鎮中心街道是小鎮主要區域內的道路和行人區。"},{"en":"The town centre streets are busy during the summer festival.","zh":"夏季節日期間，鎮中心街道非常繁忙。"},{"en":"Volunteers on town centre streets can give directions quickly.","zh":"在鎮中心街道上的義工可以迅速提供方向。"},{"en":"Clear signs on town centre streets help both residents and visitors.","zh":"鎮中心街道上的清楚指示牌能幫助居民和遊客。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ask how to get to","meaning":"詢問怎樣前往……","examples":[{"en":"Tourists often ask how to get to a particular shop.","zh":"遊客經常詢問怎樣前往某一間指定商店。"},{"en":"To ask how to get to a place means to ask for directions to that place.","zh":"詢問怎樣前往某地，是指詢問到達該地方的路線。"},{"en":"Visitors asked how to get to the museum.","zh":"遊客詢問怎樣前往博物館。"},{"en":"Tourists may feel more confident if volunteers explain how to get to local attractions.","zh":"如果義工解釋怎樣前往本地景點，遊客可能會更有信心。"},{"en":"People often ask how to get to a place when street signs are unclear.","zh":"當街道指示不清楚時，人們經常詢問怎樣前往某地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a particular shop","meaning":"某一間指定商店","examples":[{"en":"Tourists may ask how to get to a particular shop.","zh":"遊客可能詢問怎樣前往某一間指定商店。"},{"en":"A particular shop means one specific shop, not just any shop.","zh":"某一間指定商店是指一間特定商店，而不是任何商店。"},{"en":"The visitor was looking for a particular shop that sold handmade gifts.","zh":"那名遊客正在尋找一間售賣手工禮品的指定商店。"},{"en":"Knowing local streets helps volunteers direct tourists to a particular shop.","zh":"熟悉本地街道有助義工指引遊客前往某一間指定商店。"},{"en":"A map can help visitors find a particular shop in the town centre.","zh":"地圖可以幫助遊客在鎮中心找到某一間指定商店。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be grateful for","meaning":"感激……","examples":[{"en":"Tourists may be grateful for recommendations about what to visit.","zh":"遊客可能會感激關於參觀地點的推薦。"},{"en":"To be grateful for something means to feel thankful because it is helpful or kind.","zh":"感激某事，是指因它有幫助或出於善意而感到感謝。"},{"en":"Visitors were grateful for the volunteer’s clear directions.","zh":"遊客感激義工清楚的指示。"},{"en":"People are often grateful for advice when they are in an unfamiliar town.","zh":"當人們身處陌生小鎮時，通常會感激別人的建議。"},{"en":"A simple recommendation can make tourists grateful and more relaxed.","zh":"一個簡單推薦可以令遊客感激並更放鬆。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recommendations about what to visit","meaning":"關於參觀地點的推薦","examples":[{"en":"Tourists are grateful for recommendations about what to visit.","zh":"遊客感激關於參觀地點的推薦。"},{"en":"Recommendations about what to visit are suggestions of places or attractions worth seeing.","zh":"關於參觀地點的推薦，是指值得觀看的地方或景點建議。"},{"en":"The volunteer gave recommendations about what to visit in the old town.","zh":"義工就舊城區的參觀地點提供推薦。"},{"en":"Good recommendations help tourists use their time well.","zh":"好的推薦可以幫助遊客好好利用時間。"},{"en":"Visitors may ask locals for recommendations about what to visit.","zh":"遊客可能會向本地人詢問關於參觀地點的推薦。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hold concerts","meaning":"舉辦音樂會","examples":[{"en":"The town holds a large number of concerts each year.","zh":"這個小鎮每年舉辦大量音樂會。"},{"en":"To hold concerts means to organise and host musical performances.","zh":"舉辦音樂會是指組織和主辦音樂表演。"},{"en":"The school holds concerts at the end of each term.","zh":"學校每個學期末都舉辦音樂會。"},{"en":"Towns that hold concerts need volunteers to guide audiences and answer questions.","zh":"舉辦音樂會的小鎮需要義工引導觀眾和回答問題。"},{"en":"Holding concerts can attract visitors and support local culture.","zh":"舉辦音樂會可以吸引遊客並支持本地文化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a large number of","meaning":"大量；很多","examples":[{"en":"The town holds a large number of concerts each year.","zh":"這個小鎮每年舉辦大量音樂會。"},{"en":"A large number of something means many of them.","zh":"大量某物表示有很多。"},{"en":"A large number of visitors came to the book festival.","zh":"很多遊客來到書展。"},{"en":"When a town has a large number of events, it needs good organisation.","zh":"當一個小鎮有大量活動時，便需要良好組織。"},{"en":"A large number of volunteers may be required for major festivals.","zh":"大型節慶活動可能需要大量義工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"part of someone’s role","meaning":"某人職責的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Part of the volunteers’ role is to help the audience.","zh":"義工職責的一部分是協助觀眾。"},{"en":"Part of someone’s role means one duty or responsibility included in their job or position.","zh":"某人職責的一部分，是指其工作或身份中包括的一項責任。"},{"en":"Part of a teacher’s role is to support students outside class.","zh":"老師職責的一部分是在課堂外支援學生。"},{"en":"If volunteers understand their role, events run more smoothly.","zh":"如果義工了解自己的職責，活動會更順利。"},{"en":"Greeting visitors is part of the volunteers’ role at local events.","zh":"迎接遊客是義工在本地活動中職責的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the audience","meaning":"觀眾","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers help everyone in the audience get to the right place.","zh":"義工幫助觀眾中的每個人前往正確地方。"},{"en":"The audience is the group of people watching or listening to a performance or event.","zh":"觀眾是觀看或聆聽表演或活動的一群人。"},{"en":"The audience clapped loudly after the concert.","zh":"音樂會後，觀眾熱烈鼓掌。"},{"en":"Volunteers help the audience by checking tickets and giving directions.","zh":"義工透過檢查門票和指路來幫助觀眾。"},{"en":"A confused audience can delay the start of a performance.","zh":"如果觀眾感到混亂，表演開始時間可能會延遲。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get someone to the right place","meaning":"把某人帶到正確地方","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers get everyone in the audience to the right place.","zh":"義工把觀眾中的每個人帶到正確地方。"},{"en":"To get someone to the right place means to guide them to where they should be.","zh":"把某人帶到正確地方，是指引導他們到應該到達的位置。"},{"en":"Staff helped visitors get to the right place before the talk began.","zh":"講座開始前，職員幫助訪客到達正確地方。"},{"en":"Clear directions help avoid people entering the wrong section.","zh":"清楚指示可以避免人們進入錯誤區域。"},{"en":"Volunteers get people to the right place by reading their tickets carefully.","zh":"義工透過仔細查看門票，把人帶到正確地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as smoothly as possible","meaning":"盡可能順利地","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers try to guide the audience as smoothly as possible.","zh":"義工盡可能順利地引導觀眾。"},{"en":"As smoothly as possible means with as few problems, delays, or interruptions as can be managed.","zh":"盡可能順利地，是指盡量減少問題、延誤或中斷。"},{"en":"The organisers wanted the festival to run as smoothly as possible.","zh":"主辦者希望節日盡可能順利地進行。"},{"en":"Good planning helps volunteers move crowds as smoothly as possible.","zh":"良好規劃幫助義工盡可能順利地引導人群。"},{"en":"Clear signs and calm communication make entry as smooth as possible.","zh":"清楚指示和冷靜溝通令入場過程盡可能順利。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"You’d be surprised how many","meaning":"你會驚訝有這麼多人……","examples":[{"en":"You’d be surprised how many people buy tickets and then do not check them.","zh":"你會驚訝有這麼多人買了票卻不檢查。"},{"en":"“You’d be surprised how many” means the number is larger than people might expect.","zh":"「You’d be surprised how many」表示數量比人們可能預期的更多。"},{"en":"You’d be surprised how many visitors ask for directions to the same shop.","zh":"你會驚訝有這麼多遊客詢問同一間商店的方向。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an unexpected fact in a conversational way.","zh":"這個句式以對話方式介紹出乎意料的事實。"},{"en":"You’d be surprised how many people go to the wrong door at a concert.","zh":"你會驚訝有這麼多人在音樂會走錯門口。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"head for","meaning":"前往","examples":[{"en":"Some people head for the wrong section of the hall.","zh":"有些人前往禮堂錯誤的區域。"},{"en":"To head for a place means to move towards it.","zh":"前往某地是指向該地方移動。"},{"en":"Visitors headed for the information desk after arriving.","zh":"遊客到達後前往詢問處。"},{"en":"If people head for the wrong section, volunteers must redirect them quickly.","zh":"如果人們前往錯誤區域，義工必須迅速重新指引他們。"},{"en":"The audience should head for the entrance printed on their tickets.","zh":"觀眾應前往門票上印出的入口。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the wrong section of","meaning":"……錯誤的區域","examples":[{"en":"Some visitors head for the wrong section of the hall.","zh":"一些訪客前往禮堂錯誤的區域。"},{"en":"The wrong section of a place is an incorrect area within it.","zh":"某地錯誤的區域，是指該地方內不正確的部分。"},{"en":"The family sat in the wrong section of the theatre.","zh":"那個家庭坐在劇院錯誤的區域。"},{"en":"People may go to the wrong section if they do not check their tickets.","zh":"如果人們不檢查門票，可能會走到錯誤區域。"},{"en":"Volunteers prevent delays by guiding visitors away from the wrong section.","zh":"義工透過把訪客帶離錯誤區域來避免延誤。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get involved with","meaning":"參與；加入……的工作","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers may get involved with community groups.","zh":"義工可能會參與社區團體的工作。"},{"en":"To get involved with a group means to take part in its work or activities.","zh":"參與某個團體，是指加入其工作或活動。"},{"en":"She got involved with a local sports club after moving to the town.","zh":"她搬到小鎮後加入了本地運動俱樂部的工作。"},{"en":"Getting involved with community groups helps volunteers understand local needs.","zh":"參與社區團體可以幫助義工了解本地需要。"},{"en":"Residents who get involved with local groups often build stronger friendships.","zh":"參與本地團體的居民通常會建立更深厚友誼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"community groups","meaning":"社區團體","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers may get involved with community groups.","zh":"義工可能會參與社區團體。"},{"en":"Community groups are local organisations formed by people with shared interests or needs.","zh":"社區團體是由有共同興趣或需要的人組成的本地組織。"},{"en":"The town has community groups for gardening, sport, music, and writing.","zh":"小鎮有園藝、運動、音樂和寫作方面的社區團體。"},{"en":"Community groups can support one another by sharing transport and publicity.","zh":"社區團體可以透過分享交通和宣傳互相支持。"},{"en":"Volunteers help community groups communicate and cooperate.","zh":"義工幫助社區團體溝通和合作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sports clubs","meaning":"運動俱樂部","examples":[{"en":"Sports clubs are one type of community group.","zh":"運動俱樂部是社區團體的一種類型。"},{"en":"Sports clubs are organisations where people practise or play sports together.","zh":"運動俱樂部是人們一起練習或參與運動的組織。"},{"en":"The town has sports clubs for football, tennis, and running.","zh":"這個小鎮有足球、網球和跑步運動俱樂部。"},{"en":"Sports clubs can bring residents together through regular activities.","zh":"運動俱樂部可以透過定期活動把居民聚在一起。"},{"en":"Volunteers may help sports clubs connect with other local organisations.","zh":"義工可能會幫助運動俱樂部與其他本地組織連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"gardeners’ associations","meaning":"園藝協會","examples":[{"en":"Gardeners’ associations may work with other local groups.","zh":"園藝協會可能會與其他本地團體合作。"},{"en":"Gardeners’ associations are organised groups of people interested in gardening.","zh":"園藝協會是由對園藝感興趣的人組成的組織。"},{"en":"The gardeners’ association planted flowers near the town hall.","zh":"園藝協會在市政廳附近種植花卉。"},{"en":"Gardeners’ associations can share tools, knowledge, and event space with other groups.","zh":"園藝協會可以與其他團體分享工具、知識和活動空間。"},{"en":"Volunteers may help gardeners’ associations find partners for community projects.","zh":"義工可能會幫助園藝協會尋找社區項目的合作伙伴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"help each other","meaning":"互相幫助","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers talk about how groups can help each other.","zh":"義工談論各團體可以如何互相幫助。"},{"en":"To help each other means to give support to one another.","zh":"互相幫助是指彼此提供支援。"},{"en":"Local clubs can help each other by sharing equipment.","zh":"本地學會可以透過分享設備互相幫助。"},{"en":"When community groups help each other, the whole town benefits.","zh":"當社區團體互相幫助時，整個小鎮都會受益。"},{"en":"Volunteers encourage groups to help each other instead of working alone.","zh":"義工鼓勵各團體互相幫助，而不是各自工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"For instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"For instance, a writing group might want to travel to another town.","zh":"例如，一個寫作小組可能想前往另一個城鎮。"},{"en":"“For instance” introduces an example that explains a general point.","zh":"「For instance」用來介紹例子，以解釋一般重點。"},{"en":"Some clubs share transport; for instance, a drama group may borrow a coach.","zh":"一些學會會分享交通工具；例如，戲劇小組可能借用旅遊巴士。"},{"en":"This phrase helps listeners understand an idea through a specific case.","zh":"這個短語透過具體個案幫助聽眾理解想法。"},{"en":"For instance, gardeners and sports clubs might share volunteers for an event.","zh":"例如，園藝協會和運動俱樂部可能在活動中共享義工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"travel to another town","meaning":"前往另一個城鎮","examples":[{"en":"A writing group might want to travel to another town.","zh":"一個寫作小組可能想前往另一個城鎮。"},{"en":"To travel to another town means to go from one town to a different town.","zh":"前往另一個城鎮，是指從一個城鎮去到不同的城鎮。"},{"en":"The choir travelled to another town for a music competition.","zh":"合唱團前往另一個城鎮參加音樂比賽。"},{"en":"Groups may need transport when they travel to another town together.","zh":"團體一起前往另一個城鎮時，可能需要交通安排。"},{"en":"Volunteers can help clubs arrange ways to travel to another town.","zh":"義工可以幫助學會安排前往另一個城鎮的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hear a talk by","meaning":"聽……的演講","examples":[{"en":"The group wants to hear a talk by a well-known author.","zh":"這個小組想聽一名知名作家的演講。"},{"en":"To hear a talk by someone means to attend and listen to their speech or presentation.","zh":"聽某人的演講，是指出席並聆聽其講話或簡報。"},{"en":"Students went to hear a talk by a famous scientist.","zh":"學生去聽一位著名科學家的演講。"},{"en":"Hearing a talk by an expert can inspire a community group.","zh":"聽專家的演講可以啟發社區團體。"},{"en":"The writing group wanted transport so members could hear the author speak.","zh":"寫作小組需要交通，好讓成員能聽該作家演講。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a well-known author","meaning":"知名作家","examples":[{"en":"A writing group may want to hear a talk by a well-known author.","zh":"寫作小組可能想聽一名知名作家的演講。"},{"en":"A well-known author is a writer who is famous or widely recognised.","zh":"知名作家是有名或廣為人知的作家。"},{"en":"The library invited a well-known author to speak about her novels.","zh":"圖書館邀請了一名知名作家談論她的小說。"},{"en":"A talk by a well-known author can attract many local residents.","zh":"知名作家的演講可以吸引許多本地居民。"},{"en":"Meeting a well-known author may encourage young people to write more.","zh":"見到知名作家可能會鼓勵年輕人多寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"travel by coach","meaning":"乘旅遊巴士前往","examples":[{"en":"Another club has a coach that the group could travel in.","zh":"另一個俱樂部有一輛可供該小組乘坐的旅遊巴士。"},{"en":"To travel by coach means to go somewhere in a large bus used for group travel.","zh":"乘旅遊巴士前往，是指乘坐供團體出行的大型巴士去某地。"},{"en":"The club travelled by coach to the theatre.","zh":"俱樂部乘旅遊巴士前往劇院。"},{"en":"Travelling by coach can be cheaper and easier for a large group.","zh":"對大型團體來說，乘旅遊巴士可能較便宜和方便。"},{"en":"Community groups may share a coach when visiting another town.","zh":"社區團體前往另一個城鎮時，可能會共用旅遊巴士。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"produce a monthly magazine","meaning":"出版月刊","examples":[{"en":"The town produces a monthly magazine.","zh":"這個小鎮出版月刊。"},{"en":"To produce a monthly magazine means to create and publish a magazine every month.","zh":"出版月刊是指每月製作並發布一本雜誌。"},{"en":"The school produces a monthly magazine for students and parents.","zh":"學校為學生和家長出版月刊。"},{"en":"Producing a monthly magazine requires writers, editors, design work, and funding.","zh":"出版月刊需要作者、編輯、設計工作和資金。"},{"en":"A town magazine can share news, opinions, and upcoming events.","zh":"小鎮月刊可以分享新聞、意見和即將舉行的活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"monthly magazine","meaning":"月刊","examples":[{"en":"Anyone who lives in the town can write for the monthly magazine.","zh":"任何住在鎮內的人都可以為月刊撰稿。"},{"en":"A monthly magazine is a magazine published once every month.","zh":"月刊是每月出版一次的雜誌。"},{"en":"The monthly magazine includes interviews, local news, and event reports.","zh":"月刊包括訪問、本地新聞和活動報道。"},{"en":"A monthly magazine helps residents stay informed about community life.","zh":"月刊幫助居民了解社區生活。"},{"en":"Volunteers collect comments that may be used in the monthly magazine.","zh":"義工收集可能用於月刊的意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"send in articles","meaning":"投稿","examples":[{"en":"Residents can send in articles for the town magazine.","zh":"居民可以為小鎮雜誌投稿。"},{"en":"To send in articles means to submit written pieces for possible publication.","zh":"投稿是指提交文章以供可能刊登。"},{"en":"Students sent in articles about their volunteer experiences.","zh":"學生投稿分享自己的義工經歷。"},{"en":"A community magazine becomes richer when many residents send in articles.","zh":"當許多居民投稿時，社區雜誌會變得更豐富。"},{"en":"Anyone who sends in an article should include their name and contact details.","zh":"投稿的人應附上姓名和聯絡資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"free to residents","meaning":"對居民免費","examples":[{"en":"The magazine is free to residents.","zh":"這本雜誌對居民免費。"},{"en":"Free to residents means local people can receive or use something without paying.","zh":"對居民免費，是指本地居民可以不用付款便收到或使用某物。"},{"en":"The town’s newsletter is free to residents every month.","zh":"小鎮通訊每月對居民免費。"},{"en":"If a service is free to residents, more people may use it.","zh":"如果一項服務對居民免費，更多人可能會使用它。"},{"en":"Local businesses help pay for the magazine so it can be free to residents.","zh":"本地商戶協助支付雜誌費用，使它能對居民免費。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be paid for by","meaning":"由……支付費用","examples":[{"en":"The magazine is paid for by local businesses.","zh":"這本雜誌由本地商戶支付費用。"},{"en":"If something is paid for by someone, that person or group provides the money for it.","zh":"如果某物由某人支付費用，即表示該人或群體提供相關金錢。"},{"en":"The festival decorations were paid for by local sponsors.","zh":"節日裝飾由本地贊助商支付費用。"},{"en":"When a magazine is paid for by businesses, advertising may be involved.","zh":"當雜誌由商戶支付費用時，可能涉及廣告。"},{"en":"Public services can sometimes be paid for by grants or donations.","zh":"公共服務有時可以由撥款或捐款支付費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"local businesses","meaning":"本地商戶","examples":[{"en":"The magazine is paid for by local businesses.","zh":"這本雜誌由本地商戶支付費用。"},{"en":"Local businesses are shops, companies, or services based in the local area.","zh":"本地商戶是在本地經營的店舖、公司或服務機構。"},{"en":"Local businesses advertised in the town magazine.","zh":"本地商戶在小鎮雜誌上刊登廣告。"},{"en":"Supporting local businesses helps money stay within the community.","zh":"支持本地商戶有助金錢留在社區內。"},{"en":"The advertising department contacts local businesses for magazine funding.","zh":"廣告部門聯絡本地商戶，以取得雜誌資金。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the responsibility of","meaning":"……的責任","examples":[{"en":"Advertising is the responsibility of the council’s advertising department.","zh":"廣告是議會廣告部門的責任。"},{"en":"The responsibility of someone means the duty that person or group must handle.","zh":"某人的責任，是指該人或群體必須處理的職責。"},{"en":"Safety at the event is the responsibility of the organisers.","zh":"活動安全是主辦者的責任。"},{"en":"Knowing who has responsibility prevents confusion and repeated work.","zh":"知道誰有責任可以避免混亂和重複工作。"},{"en":"Collecting advertising money is the responsibility of a specific department.","zh":"收取廣告費是特定部門的責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"advertising department","meaning":"廣告部門","examples":[{"en":"The council’s advertising department deals with payment from local businesses.","zh":"議會的廣告部門處理來自本地商戶的付款。"},{"en":"An advertising department manages advertisements, sponsors, and related payments.","zh":"廣告部門管理廣告、贊助商和相關付款。"},{"en":"The advertising department designed a page for local shops.","zh":"廣告部門為本地店舖設計了一個版面。"},{"en":"A magazine needs an advertising department if businesses help fund it.","zh":"如果企業幫助資助雜誌，雜誌便需要廣告部門。"},{"en":"Volunteers do not contact businesses because the advertising department handles that task.","zh":"義工不聯絡商戶，因為廣告部門負責該任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"depend on volunteers","meaning":"依靠義工","examples":[{"en":"The council depends on volunteers to collect people’s opinions.","zh":"議會依靠義工收集人們的意見。"},{"en":"To depend on volunteers means to need volunteers in order to complete a task.","zh":"依靠義工，是指需要義工才能完成任務。"},{"en":"The festival depends on volunteers to welcome visitors.","zh":"節日依靠義工迎接遊客。"},{"en":"If an event depends on volunteers, training and support are important.","zh":"如果活動依靠義工，培訓和支援便很重要。"},{"en":"The council depends on volunteers because staff cannot speak to every resident alone.","zh":"議會依靠義工，因為職員不能獨自與每位居民交談。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"find out what people think of","meaning":"了解人們對……的看法","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers find out what people think of events they have attended.","zh":"義工了解人們對他們參加過的活動的看法。"},{"en":"To find out what people think of something means to ask for and learn their opinions.","zh":"了解人們對某事的看法，是指詢問並得知他們的意見。"},{"en":"The school surveyed parents to find out what they thought of the new timetable.","zh":"學校調查家長，以了解他們對新時間表的看法。"},{"en":"Finding out what people think helps organisers improve future events.","zh":"了解人們的看法有助主辦者改善未來活動。"},{"en":"Volunteers can find out opinions by asking simple questions after an event.","zh":"義工可以在活動後透過簡單提問了解意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"events they have attended","meaning":"他們參加過的活動","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers ask people about events they have attended.","zh":"義工詢問人們對他們參加過的活動的看法。"},{"en":"Events they have attended are activities or programmes that people have gone to.","zh":"他們參加過的活動，是指人們曾經出席的活動或節目。"},{"en":"Residents gave opinions about concerts and talks they had attended.","zh":"居民就自己參加過的音樂會和講座提供意見。"},{"en":"Feedback on events people have attended is more useful than guesses from people who were not there.","zh":"參加過活動的人提供的回饋，比沒有到場者的猜測更有用。"},{"en":"Volunteers record comments about events residents have attended recently.","zh":"義工記錄居民最近參加過的活動意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"suggestions for the future","meaning":"對未來的建議","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers collect any suggestions people have for the future.","zh":"義工收集人們對未來的任何建議。"},{"en":"Suggestions for the future are ideas about how things can be improved later.","zh":"對未來的建議，是關於日後如何改善事情的想法。"},{"en":"Residents gave suggestions for future festivals.","zh":"居民提出了對未來節慶的建議。"},{"en":"Collecting suggestions for the future helps editors and organisers plan better.","zh":"收集對未來的建議，可以幫助編輯和主辦者更好地規劃。"},{"en":"A useful suggestion for the future should be clear and practical.","zh":"有用的未來建議應清楚而實際。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"send a summary to","meaning":"把摘要發給……","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers send a summary to the editors.","zh":"義工把摘要發給編輯。"},{"en":"To send a summary to someone means to give them a short version of the main points.","zh":"把摘要發給某人，是指把主要重點的簡短版本交給他們。"},{"en":"The volunteer sent a summary of the survey results to the council.","zh":"義工把調查結果摘要發給議會。"},{"en":"Summaries help editors understand public opinion without reading every comment.","zh":"摘要幫助編輯不用閱讀每條意見也能了解民意。"},{"en":"After collecting feedback, volunteers send a summary to the magazine team.","zh":"收集回饋後，義工把摘要發給雜誌團隊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the editors","meaning":"編輯","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers send a summary to the editors.","zh":"義工把摘要發給編輯。"},{"en":"The editors are the people who choose, correct, and prepare material for publication.","zh":"編輯是選擇、修改和準備出版材料的人。"},{"en":"The editors decided which articles would appear in the magazine.","zh":"編輯決定哪些文章會刊登在雜誌中。"},{"en":"Editors need clear summaries so they can understand readers’ opinions.","zh":"編輯需要清楚摘要，以了解讀者意見。"},{"en":"Volunteers support the editors by collecting feedback from residents.","zh":"義工透過收集居民回饋來支援編輯。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a number of clubs","meaning":"一些；若干","examples":[{"en":"There are a number of clubs for retired people.","zh":"有一些為退休人士而設的俱樂部。"},{"en":"A number of clubs means several clubs.","zh":"一些俱樂部表示有數個俱樂部。"},{"en":"The town has a number of clubs for music, reading, and gardening.","zh":"小鎮有一些音樂、閱讀和園藝俱樂部。"},{"en":"Having a number of clubs gives residents more ways to meet people.","zh":"有若干俱樂部讓居民有更多方式認識別人。"},{"en":"Volunteers may work with a number of clubs during the year.","zh":"義工一年中可能會與一些俱樂部合作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"retired people","meaning":"退休人士","examples":[{"en":"The town has clubs for retired people.","zh":"這個小鎮有為退休人士而設的俱樂部。"},{"en":"Retired people are people who have stopped working, usually because of age.","zh":"退休人士是通常因年齡而停止工作的人。"},{"en":"Retired people may join clubs to stay active and social.","zh":"退休人士可能會加入俱樂部，以保持活躍和社交。"},{"en":"Community events for retired people can reduce loneliness.","zh":"為退休人士而設的社區活動可以減少孤獨感。"},{"en":"Volunteers help retired people enjoy lunches, shows, and conversations.","zh":"義工幫助退休人士享受午餐、表演和交談。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"arrange lunch for","meaning":"為……安排午餐","examples":[{"en":"Every year, the council arranges lunch for all the members.","zh":"每年，議會都為所有成員安排午餐。"},{"en":"To arrange lunch for people means to organise a meal for them.","zh":"為某人安排午餐，是指為他們組織一餐飯。"},{"en":"The school arranged lunch for visiting speakers.","zh":"學校為到訪講者安排午餐。"},{"en":"Arranging lunch for club members gives them a chance to meet and relax.","zh":"為俱樂部成員安排午餐，讓他們有機會見面和放鬆。"},{"en":"Volunteers may help welcome guests before lunch begins.","zh":"義工可能會在午餐開始前協助迎接賓客。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"welcome the guests","meaning":"迎接賓客","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers welcome the guests at the lunch.","zh":"義工在午餐活動中迎接賓客。"},{"en":"To welcome the guests means to greet them politely when they arrive.","zh":"迎接賓客，是指賓客到達時有禮貌地問候他們。"},{"en":"Volunteers welcomed the guests at the door of the hall.","zh":"義工在禮堂門口迎接賓客。"},{"en":"A warm welcome helps guests feel comfortable and valued.","zh":"溫暖的迎接可以令賓客感到舒服和受重視。"},{"en":"Welcoming guests is an important role at community meals.","zh":"迎接賓客是社區餐聚中的重要角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"relax after the meal","meaning":"餐後放鬆","examples":[{"en":"The guests sit down and relax after the meal.","zh":"賓客坐下並在餐後放鬆。"},{"en":"To relax after the meal means to rest and feel comfortable after eating.","zh":"餐後放鬆，是指用餐後休息並感到舒服。"},{"en":"After lunch, the club members relaxed and chatted with volunteers.","zh":"午餐後，俱樂部成員放鬆下來並與義工聊天。"},{"en":"Entertainment after a meal helps guests relax and enjoy the event.","zh":"餐後娛樂有助賓客放鬆並享受活動。"},{"en":"A calm atmosphere allows retired people to relax after the meal.","zh":"平靜的氣氛讓退休人士在餐後放鬆。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put on a show","meaning":"表演節目","examples":[{"en":"Some volunteers put on a show after the meal.","zh":"一些義工在餐後表演節目。"},{"en":"To put on a show means to organise and perform entertainment for an audience.","zh":"表演節目是指為觀眾組織並演出娛樂內容。"},{"en":"Students put on a show for elderly residents.","zh":"學生為年長居民表演節目。"},{"en":"A short show after lunch can make the event more enjoyable.","zh":"午餐後的短表演可以令活動更愉快。"},{"en":"Volunteers put on songs and plays to entertain the guests.","zh":"義工表演歌曲和短劇來娛樂賓客。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"around half an hour of","meaning":"大約半小時的……","examples":[{"en":"The show usually includes around half an hour of songs and short plays.","zh":"表演通常包括大約半小時的歌曲和短劇。"},{"en":"Around half an hour of something means approximately thirty minutes of it.","zh":"大約半小時的某事，是指約三十分鐘的內容。"},{"en":"The programme included around half an hour of music.","zh":"節目包括大約半小時的音樂。"},{"en":"A show of around half an hour is long enough to entertain but not tire the audience.","zh":"大約半小時的表演足以娛樂觀眾，又不會令他們疲倦。"},{"en":"Volunteers prepared around half an hour of entertainment for the lunch.","zh":"義工為午餐活動準備了大約半小時的娛樂節目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"short plays","meaning":"短劇","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers perform songs and short plays.","zh":"義工表演歌曲和短劇。"},{"en":"Short plays are brief dramatic performances with characters and dialogue.","zh":"短劇是有角色和對白的簡短戲劇表演。"},{"en":"The drama club wrote short plays for the community lunch.","zh":"戲劇學會為社區午餐寫了短劇。"},{"en":"Short plays are useful because they can entertain an audience in a limited time.","zh":"短劇很有用，因為它們可以在有限時間內娛樂觀眾。"},{"en":"Volunteers may perform short plays that are funny, simple, and easy to follow.","zh":"義工可能會表演有趣、簡單而容易理解的短劇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"welcome the chance to","meaning":"很樂意有機會……","examples":[{"en":"The club members welcome the chance to chat to the volunteers.","zh":"俱樂部成員很樂意有機會與義工聊天。"},{"en":"To welcome the chance to do something means to be pleased to have that opportunity.","zh":"很樂意有機會做某事，是指很高興擁有該機會。"},{"en":"Residents welcomed the chance to ask questions about the website.","zh":"居民很樂意有機會詢問關於網站的問題。"},{"en":"People may welcome the chance to talk when they feel included and respected.","zh":"當人們感到被接納和尊重時，可能會樂意有機會交談。"},{"en":"Retired members welcome the chance to meet friendly volunteers.","zh":"退休成員很樂意有機會認識友善的義工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"chat to","meaning":"與……聊天","examples":[{"en":"The club members enjoy chatting to the volunteers.","zh":"俱樂部成員喜歡與義工聊天。"},{"en":"To chat to someone means to talk with them in a friendly and informal way.","zh":"與某人聊天，是指以友善和非正式方式與他們交談。"},{"en":"Visitors chatted to volunteers about the town’s history.","zh":"遊客與義工聊天，談論小鎮歷史。"},{"en":"Chatting to people can make a community event feel warmer.","zh":"與人聊天可以令社區活動感覺更溫暖。"},{"en":"Volunteers should be willing to chat to residents as well as help with tasks.","zh":"義工應願意與居民聊天，也要協助處理任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be asked to help by","meaning":"被要求透過……協助","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers are asked to help by making sure residents know about the website.","zh":"義工被要求透過確保居民知道網站來協助。"},{"en":"To be asked to help by doing something means to be requested to assist through that action.","zh":"被要求透過做某事協助，是指被請求以該行動提供幫助。"},{"en":"Students were asked to help by handing out leaflets.","zh":"學生被要求透過派發傳單協助。"},{"en":"Volunteers can help a project by spreading information clearly.","zh":"義工可以透過清楚傳遞資訊來幫助項目。"},{"en":"The council asked volunteers to help by telling residents about the website.","zh":"議會要求義工透過告訴居民網站資訊來協助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers make sure residents know about the council website.","zh":"義工確保居民知道議會網站。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check or take action so that something definitely happens.","zh":"確保是指檢查或採取行動，使某事一定發生。"},{"en":"Please make sure all guests know where the hall is.","zh":"請確保所有賓客都知道禮堂在哪裏。"},{"en":"Volunteers make sure information reaches people who may not use the internet often.","zh":"義工確保資訊傳達給可能不常使用互聯網的人。"},{"en":"Making sure residents know about services helps them take part in community life.","zh":"確保居民知道服務，有助他們參與社區生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be updated every day","meaning":"每日更新","examples":[{"en":"The website is updated every day.","zh":"網站每日更新。"},{"en":"If a website is updated every day, new information is added or changed daily.","zh":"如果網站每日更新，即表示每天加入或更改新資料。"},{"en":"The council calendar is updated every day with new events.","zh":"議會日曆每日更新，加入新活動。"},{"en":"A website that is updated every day can provide reliable current information.","zh":"每日更新的網站可以提供可靠的最新資訊。"},{"en":"Residents are more likely to use the website if it is updated every day.","zh":"如果網站每日更新，居民較可能使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"information about future activities","meaning":"關於未來活動的資料","examples":[{"en":"The website gives information about future activities.","zh":"網站提供關於未來活動的資料。"},{"en":"Information about future activities means details of events or programmes that will happen later.","zh":"關於未來活動的資料，是指稍後舉行的活動或節目的詳情。"},{"en":"Residents check the website for information about future concerts.","zh":"居民查看網站，以取得關於未來音樂會的資料。"},{"en":"Clear information about future activities helps people plan ahead.","zh":"清楚的未來活動資料可以幫助人們提前計劃。"},{"en":"Volunteers encourage residents to use the website for future activity details.","zh":"義工鼓勵居民使用網站查閱未來活動詳情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as many people as possible","meaning":"盡可能多的人","examples":[{"en":"The council wants as many people as possible to use the website.","zh":"議會希望盡可能多的人使用網站。"},{"en":"As many people as possible means the greatest number of people that can realistically be reached.","zh":"盡可能多的人，是指在實際情況下能接觸到的最大人數。"},{"en":"The organisers wanted as many people as possible to attend the festival.","zh":"主辦者希望盡可能多的人參加節日。"},{"en":"If as many people as possible use the website, fewer residents will miss important information.","zh":"如果盡可能多的人使用網站，較少居民會錯過重要資訊。"},{"en":"Volunteers spread the message so as many people as possible know about the service.","zh":"義工傳遞訊息，讓盡可能多的人知道這項服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go on to","meaning":"接着談及","examples":[{"en":"I’ll go on to some practical matters.","zh":"我接着談及一些實際事項。"},{"en":"To go on to something means to move forward to the next topic.","zh":"接着談及某事，是指繼續轉到下一個題目。"},{"en":"After explaining the activities, the speaker went on to training details.","zh":"解釋活動後，講者接着談及培訓詳情。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise a talk or presentation.","zh":"這個短語有助組織演講或簡報。"},{"en":"Let’s go on to the festival schedule.","zh":"讓我們接着談及節日時間表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"practical matters","meaning":"實際事項","examples":[{"en":"The speaker goes on to some practical matters.","zh":"講者接着談及一些實際事項。"},{"en":"Practical matters are real arrangements or details that need to be handled.","zh":"實際事項是需要處理的真實安排或細節。"},{"en":"Training dates and duty schedules are practical matters.","zh":"培訓日期和值勤時間表都是實際事項。"},{"en":"Discussing practical matters helps volunteers know what will actually happen.","zh":"討論實際事項可以幫助義工知道實際會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"After the introduction, the organiser explained practical matters such as training and support.","zh":"簡介後，主辦者解釋了培訓和支援等實際事項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"As you probably know","meaning":"你們可能知道","examples":[{"en":"As you probably know, the town arranges three major festivals every year.","zh":"你們可能知道，這個小鎮每年安排三個大型節慶活動。"},{"en":"“As you probably know” introduces information that the listener may already be aware of.","zh":"「As you probably know」用來介紹聽者可能已知道的資料。"},{"en":"As you probably know, the book festival is very popular.","zh":"你們可能知道，書展非常受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase gently reminds listeners of shared knowledge.","zh":"這個短語溫和地提醒聽眾共同知道的事情。"},{"en":"As you probably know, volunteers are essential for large events.","zh":"你們可能知道，大型活動少不了義工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"major festivals","meaning":"大型節慶活動","examples":[{"en":"The town arranges three major festivals every year.","zh":"這個小鎮每年安排三個大型節慶活動。"},{"en":"Major festivals are large and important public celebrations or events.","zh":"大型節慶活動是規模大而重要的公眾慶祝或活動。"},{"en":"The town’s major festivals attract visitors from nearby areas.","zh":"小鎮的大型節慶活動吸引附近地區的遊客。"},{"en":"Major festivals require planning, volunteers, venues, and publicity.","zh":"大型節慶活動需要規劃、義工、場地和宣傳。"},{"en":"A book festival, music festival, and science festival are major events for the town.","zh":"書展、音樂節和科學節都是小鎮的大型活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"depend on a large number of","meaning":"需要依靠大量……","examples":[{"en":"The festivals depend on a large number of volunteers.","zh":"這些節慶活動需要依靠大量義工。"},{"en":"To depend on a large number of people means to need many people in order to succeed.","zh":"需要依靠大量人手，是指需要很多人才能成功。"},{"en":"The charity event depends on a large number of helpers.","zh":"慈善活動需要依靠大量助手。"},{"en":"Large festivals depend on many volunteers because there are many visitors and venues.","zh":"大型節日需要依靠許多義工，因為有很多遊客和場地。"},{"en":"If not enough volunteers join, events that depend on many helpers may struggle.","zh":"如果沒有足夠義工加入，依靠大量人手的活動可能會遇到困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"book festival","meaning":"書展；書籍節","examples":[{"en":"The book festival lasts three days.","zh":"書展持續三日。"},{"en":"A book festival is an event where people celebrate books, reading, authors, and writing.","zh":"書展是人們慶祝書籍、閱讀、作家和寫作的活動。"},{"en":"The book festival included talks by writers and book stalls.","zh":"書展包括作家講座和書攤。"},{"en":"Volunteers help visitors find venues during the book festival.","zh":"義工在書展期間幫助遊客尋找場地。"},{"en":"A book festival can encourage reading and support local culture.","zh":"書展可以鼓勵閱讀並支持本地文化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"last three days","meaning":"持續三日","examples":[{"en":"The book festival lasts three days.","zh":"書展持續三日。"},{"en":"To last three days means to continue for a period of three days.","zh":"持續三日是指延續三天時間。"},{"en":"The training course lasts three days.","zh":"培訓課程持續三日。"},{"en":"A festival that lasts three days still needs careful volunteer scheduling.","zh":"即使節日只持續三日，仍需要仔細編排義工時間。"},{"en":"If an event lasts three days, organisers must plan for different shifts.","zh":"如果活動持續三日，主辦者必須安排不同班次。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"several venues","meaning":"幾個場地","examples":[{"en":"The book festival uses several venues.","zh":"書展使用幾個場地。"},{"en":"Several venues means a number of different places where events are held.","zh":"幾個場地是指舉行活動的多個不同地點。"},{"en":"The music festival took place in several venues around town.","zh":"音樂節在鎮內幾個場地舉行。"},{"en":"Using several venues makes clear signs and helpful volunteers more important.","zh":"使用幾個場地會令清楚指示和有幫助的義工更重要。"},{"en":"Visitors may need directions when a festival uses several venues.","zh":"當節日使用幾個場地時，遊客可能需要指路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"music festival","meaning":"音樂節","examples":[{"en":"More volunteers are needed for the music festival.","zh":"音樂節需要更多義工。"},{"en":"A music festival is an event with concerts, performances, or music-related activities.","zh":"音樂節是有音樂會、表演或音樂相關活動的活動。"},{"en":"The music festival lasts a whole week.","zh":"音樂節持續整整一星期。"},{"en":"A music festival needs volunteers to guide audiences and manage venues.","zh":"音樂節需要義工引導觀眾和管理場地。"},{"en":"Local musicians and visitors both benefit from a well-organised music festival.","zh":"組織良好的音樂節能令本地音樂人和遊客都受益。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"last a whole week","meaning":"持續整整一星期","examples":[{"en":"The music festival lasts a whole week.","zh":"音樂節持續整整一星期。"},{"en":"To last a whole week means to continue for seven days.","zh":"持續整整一星期，是指持續七天。"},{"en":"The summer programme lasts a whole week.","zh":"夏季課程持續整整一星期。"},{"en":"A festival lasting a whole week requires more volunteer shifts.","zh":"持續一星期的節日需要更多義工班次。"},{"en":"If an event lasts a whole week, volunteers need flexible schedules.","zh":"如果活動持續整整一星期，義工需要有彈性的時間表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"even more help is required","meaning":"需要更多協助","examples":[{"en":"Even more help is required for the science festival.","zh":"科學節需要更多協助。"},{"en":"“Even more help is required” means a greater amount of assistance is needed than before.","zh":"「Even more help is required」表示需要比之前更多的幫助。"},{"en":"Even more help is required when an event uses many venues.","zh":"當活動使用許多場地時，需要更多協助。"},{"en":"The science festival needs more volunteers because its activities are spread out.","zh":"科學節需要更多義工，因為活動分布在多個地方。"},{"en":"If even more help is required, organisers should recruit early.","zh":"如果需要更多協助，主辦者應早點招募。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"science festival","meaning":"科學節","examples":[{"en":"The science festival is only two days long.","zh":"科學節只有兩天。"},{"en":"A science festival is an event where people explore science through talks, displays, and activities.","zh":"科學節是人們透過講座、展示和活動探索科學的活動。"},{"en":"Children enjoyed experiments at the science festival.","zh":"小朋友在科學節享受實驗活動。"},{"en":"A science festival may need many volunteers because demonstrations require guidance and safety.","zh":"科學節可能需要很多義工，因為示範活動需要指引和安全管理。"},{"en":"The science festival involves many venues despite lasting only two days.","zh":"科學節雖然只持續兩天，但涉及許多場地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"even though","meaning":"即使；雖然","examples":[{"en":"More help is required even though the festival is only two days long.","zh":"即使節日只有兩天，仍需要更多協助。"},{"en":"“Even though” introduces a contrast between two ideas.","zh":"「Even though」用來介紹兩個想法之間的對比。"},{"en":"Even though the event is short, it needs many volunteers.","zh":"即使活動很短，仍需要很多義工。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one fact is surprising because of another fact.","zh":"這個句式顯示某事因另一事實而顯得出乎意料。"},{"en":"Even though the weather was bad, many visitors came.","zh":"即使天氣不好，仍有許多遊客到來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"involve quite a lot of venues","meaning":"涉及相當多場地","examples":[{"en":"The science festival involves quite a lot of venues.","zh":"科學節涉及相當多場地。"},{"en":"To involve quite a lot of venues means to use many different event locations.","zh":"涉及相當多場地，是指使用許多不同活動地點。"},{"en":"The art festival involves quite a lot of venues across the town centre.","zh":"藝術節涉及鎮中心相當多場地。"},{"en":"Events involving many venues need more signs and volunteers.","zh":"涉及多個場地的活動需要更多指示牌和義工。"},{"en":"The science festival needs many helpers because it involves quite a lot of venues.","zh":"科學節需要許多幫手，因為它涉及相當多場地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"It’s a good idea to","meaning":"……是個好主意","examples":[{"en":"It’s a good idea to help at the festival you are most interested in.","zh":"協助你最感興趣的節日是個好主意。"},{"en":"“It’s a good idea to” introduces sensible advice.","zh":"「It’s a good idea to」用來介紹合理建議。"},{"en":"It’s a good idea to arrive early for training.","zh":"早點到達培訓是個好主意。"},{"en":"Volunteers enjoy their work more when they choose activities they care about.","zh":"當義工選擇自己關心的活動時，會更享受工作。"},{"en":"It’s a good idea to ask questions before your first duty.","zh":"第一次值勤前提問是個好主意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be most interested in","meaning":"對……最感興趣","examples":[{"en":"You should help at the festival you are most interested in.","zh":"你應協助你最感興趣的節日。"},{"en":"To be most interested in something means to care about or enjoy it more than other options.","zh":"對某事最感興趣，是指比其他選項更關心或更喜歡它。"},{"en":"She is most interested in the book festival because she loves reading.","zh":"她最感興趣的是書展，因為她喜歡閱讀。"},{"en":"Volunteers who are interested in an event may be more motivated.","zh":"對活動有興趣的義工可能更有動力。"},{"en":"Choose the activity you are most interested in if your schedule allows.","zh":"如果時間容許，選擇你最感興趣的活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"attend events for free","meaning":"免費參加活動","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers can attend most of the events for free.","zh":"義工可以免費參加大部分活動。"},{"en":"To attend events for free means to go to events without paying for tickets.","zh":"免費參加活動，是指不用買票便可以出席活動。"},{"en":"Volunteers attended the concert for free after helping at the entrance.","zh":"義工在入口協助後免費參加音樂會。"},{"en":"Free entry can be a way to thank volunteers for their time.","zh":"免費入場可以是感謝義工付出時間的一種方式。"},{"en":"Volunteers should still follow event rules when attending for free.","zh":"義工免費參加活動時仍應遵守活動規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"flexible volunteers","meaning":"有彈性的義工","examples":[{"en":"The council tries to use flexible volunteers.","zh":"議會嘗試使用有彈性的義工。"},{"en":"Flexible volunteers are people who can adapt to different tasks, times, or changes.","zh":"有彈性的義工是能適應不同任務、時間或變動的人。"},{"en":"Flexible volunteers are useful when events move indoors because of rain.","zh":"當活動因下雨而移到室內時，有彈性的義工很有用。"},{"en":"A festival needs flexible volunteers because arrangements may change quickly.","zh":"節日需要有彈性的義工，因為安排可能快速改變。"},{"en":"Being flexible helps volunteers solve problems calmly.","zh":"保持彈性有助義工冷靜解決問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be held outdoors","meaning":"在戶外舉行","examples":[{"en":"Some festival events are held outdoors.","zh":"一些節日活動在戶外舉行。"},{"en":"If an event is held outdoors, it takes place outside rather than inside a building.","zh":"如果活動在戶外舉行，即表示它在建築物外而非室內進行。"},{"en":"The concert was held outdoors in the park.","zh":"音樂會在公園戶外舉行。"},{"en":"Outdoor events can be enjoyable, but the weather may cause problems.","zh":"戶外活動可以很愉快，但天氣可能造成問題。"},{"en":"Volunteers at outdoor events should be ready for rain or heat.","zh":"戶外活動的義工應準備好應對下雨或炎熱天氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"affect the size of the audience","meaning":"影響觀眾人數","examples":[{"en":"The weather may affect the size of the audience.","zh":"天氣可能影響觀眾人數。"},{"en":"To affect the size of the audience means to change how many people attend.","zh":"影響觀眾人數，是指改變出席的人數。"},{"en":"Heavy rain affected the size of the audience at the outdoor concert.","zh":"大雨影響了戶外音樂會的觀眾人數。"},{"en":"Good weather can increase audience numbers for outdoor events.","zh":"好天氣可以增加戶外活動的觀眾人數。"},{"en":"Organisers must plan for weather because it affects attendance.","zh":"主辦者必須為天氣作準備，因為它會影響出席人數。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"whether the event can take place","meaning":"活動是否可以舉行","examples":[{"en":"The weather may affect whether the event can take place.","zh":"天氣可能影響活動是否可以舉行。"},{"en":"“Whether the event can take place” means whether the event is able to happen as planned.","zh":"「Whether the event can take place」表示活動是否能按計劃進行。"},{"en":"Strong winds may decide whether the outdoor show can take place.","zh":"強風可能決定戶外表演是否可以舉行。"},{"en":"Safety concerns can affect whether an event goes ahead.","zh":"安全問題可以影響活動是否繼續進行。"},{"en":"Volunteers need updates if weather affects whether the event can take place.","zh":"如果天氣影響活動是否可以舉行，義工需要最新消息。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take place","meaning":"舉行","examples":[{"en":"Some outdoor events may not take place in bad weather.","zh":"一些戶外活動在惡劣天氣下可能不會舉行。"},{"en":"To take place means to happen or be held.","zh":"舉行是指發生或被安排進行。"},{"en":"The science festival will take place in several venues.","zh":"科學節會在幾個場地舉行。"},{"en":"If an event cannot take place, organisers may postpone or cancel it.","zh":"如果活動不能舉行，主辦者可能會延期或取消。"},{"en":"The concert will take place outdoors if the weather is good.","zh":"如果天氣好，音樂會會在戶外舉行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"changes at short notice","meaning":"臨時變動","examples":[{"en":"There can be changes at short notice.","zh":"可能會有臨時變動。"},{"en":"Changes at short notice are changes made with very little warning time.","zh":"臨時變動是指在很短通知時間內作出的改變。"},{"en":"Outdoor events may move indoors at short notice.","zh":"戶外活動可能會臨時移到室內。"},{"en":"Volunteers need flexibility because changes at short notice can happen during festivals.","zh":"義工需要彈性，因為節日期間可能出現臨時變動。"},{"en":"Clear communication helps everyone deal with last-minute changes.","zh":"清晰溝通有助大家處理最後一刻的變動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"What’s essential is","meaning":"最重要的是","examples":[{"en":"What’s essential is being able to get on well with other people.","zh":"最重要的是能夠與其他人相處融洽。"},{"en":"“What’s essential is” introduces the most important requirement.","zh":"「What’s essential is」用來介紹最重要的要求。"},{"en":"What’s essential is staying calm when visitors are confused.","zh":"最重要的是在遊客感到困惑時保持冷靜。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the quality that matters most.","zh":"這個句式突出最重要的特質。"},{"en":"For volunteers, what is essential is good communication with people.","zh":"對義工來說，最重要的是與人良好溝通。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get on well with","meaning":"與……相處融洽","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers need to get on well with other people.","zh":"義工需要與其他人相處融洽。"},{"en":"To get on well with someone means to have a friendly and cooperative relationship with them.","zh":"與某人相處融洽，是指與他們有友善和合作的關係。"},{"en":"She gets on well with visitors because she is patient and kind.","zh":"她與遊客相處融洽，因為她有耐性又友善。"},{"en":"Volunteers who get on well with others can handle busy events more easily.","zh":"與人相處融洽的義工較容易應付繁忙活動。"},{"en":"Getting on well with people is important when dealing with difficult situations.","zh":"在處理困難情況時，與人相處融洽很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deal with","meaning":"應付；處理","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers need to deal with someone who is behaving badly.","zh":"義工需要應付行為不當的人。"},{"en":"To deal with someone or something means to handle or manage the situation.","zh":"應付或處理某人或某事，是指處理或管理該情況。"},{"en":"Staff had to deal with a lost child during the festival.","zh":"職員在節日期間需要處理一名走失兒童的情況。"},{"en":"Volunteers need calm communication when dealing with difficult visitors.","zh":"義工處理難應付遊客時需要冷靜溝通。"},{"en":"Training helps volunteers deal with problems safely.","zh":"培訓幫助義工安全處理問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"behave badly","meaning":"行為不當","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers may have to deal with someone who is behaving badly.","zh":"義工可能需要應付行為不當的人。"},{"en":"To behave badly means to act in an impolite, disruptive, or unacceptable way.","zh":"行為不當是指以無禮、滋擾或不可接受的方式行事。"},{"en":"A visitor behaved badly by shouting at staff.","zh":"一名遊客對職員大叫，行為不當。"},{"en":"If someone behaves badly, volunteers should stay calm and ask for support if needed.","zh":"如果有人行為不當，義工應保持冷靜，並在需要時尋求支援。"},{"en":"Clear rules can reduce the chance of people behaving badly at events.","zh":"清楚規則可以減少人們在活動中行為不當的機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as occasionally happens","meaning":"偶爾會出現這種情況","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers may meet someone behaving badly, as occasionally happens.","zh":"義工可能會遇到行為不當的人，偶爾會出現這種情況。"},{"en":"“As occasionally happens” means that something happens sometimes, though not often.","zh":"「As occasionally happens」表示某事有時會發生，但不常見。"},{"en":"Visitors may arrive late, as occasionally happens at busy events.","zh":"遊客可能會遲到，在繁忙活動中偶爾會出現這種情況。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the situation is possible but not usual.","zh":"這個短語顯示情況可能發生，但不是通常情況。"},{"en":"Volunteers should be prepared for difficult behaviour, as occasionally happens.","zh":"義工應準備應對困難行為，因為偶爾會出現這種情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a week’s training","meaning":"一星期的培訓","examples":[{"en":"New volunteers have a week’s training before they start work.","zh":"新義工在開始工作前有一星期的培訓。"},{"en":"A week’s training is training that lasts for one week.","zh":"一星期的培訓是持續一星期的訓練。"},{"en":"The volunteers completed a week’s training before helping at festivals.","zh":"義工在協助節日前完成了一星期的培訓。"},{"en":"A week’s training can prepare volunteers for directions, safety, and difficult visitors.","zh":"一星期的培訓可以讓義工準備好處理指路、安全和難應付遊客。"},{"en":"After a week’s training, volunteers should feel more confident.","zh":"完成一星期的培訓後，義工應感到更有信心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"timetable someone for duties","meaning":"為某人編排值勤時間","examples":[{"en":"The council will timetable volunteers for duties from the following week.","zh":"議會會由接下來的一星期起為義工編排值勤時間。"},{"en":"To timetable someone for duties means to schedule when they will work or help.","zh":"為某人編排值勤時間，是指安排他們何時工作或提供協助。"},{"en":"The organiser timetabled volunteers for morning and afternoon shifts.","zh":"主辦者為義工編排上午和下午班次。"},{"en":"A clear timetable prevents too many volunteers being placed in one venue.","zh":"清楚時間表可以避免太多義工被安排在同一場地。"},{"en":"Volunteers will be timetabled for duties after their training week.","zh":"義工會在培訓週後被編排值勤時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the following week","meaning":"接下來的一星期","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers start duties the following week.","zh":"義工在接下來的一星期開始值勤。"},{"en":"The following week means the week after the current or mentioned week.","zh":"接下來的一星期，是指目前或已提及那一星期之後的一星期。"},{"en":"Training ends on Friday, and duties begin the following week.","zh":"培訓在星期五結束，值勤在接下來的一星期開始。"},{"en":"Volunteers need to check their timetable before the following week starts.","zh":"義工需要在接下來的一星期開始前查看時間表。"},{"en":"The council will contact volunteers again the following week.","zh":"議會會在接下來的一星期再次聯絡義工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"from the 9th onward","meaning":"由九號起","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers will be given duties from the 9th onward.","zh":"義工會由九號起獲編排值勤。"},{"en":"From the 9th onward means starting on the 9th and continuing after that date.","zh":"由九號起，是指由九號開始並在之後繼續。"},{"en":"The new timetable applies from the 9th onward.","zh":"新時間表由九號起生效。"},{"en":"Volunteers should be available from the 9th onward if they want early duties.","zh":"如果義工想早點值勤，應由九號起有空。"},{"en":"Duties will not begin before the 9th.","zh":"值勤不會在九號之前開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in the week beginning","meaning":"在……開始的那一星期","examples":[{"en":"The council will meet volunteers in the week beginning September 23rd.","zh":"議會會在九月二十三日開始的那一星期與義工會面。"},{"en":"In the week beginning a date means during the week that starts on that date.","zh":"在某日期開始的那一星期，是指由該日期開始的一星期內。"},{"en":"Interviews will take place in the week beginning May 6th.","zh":"面試會在五月六日開始的那一星期進行。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when the exact day has not yet been chosen.","zh":"當確實日期尚未選定時，可以使用這個短語。"},{"en":"Volunteers should keep the week beginning September 23rd free for a meeting.","zh":"義工應預留九月二十三日開始的那一星期參加會面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have a chat with","meaning":"與……談一談","examples":[{"en":"The council will have a chat with each volunteer.","zh":"議會會與每名義工談一談。"},{"en":"To have a chat with someone means to talk with them informally.","zh":"與某人談一談，是指以非正式方式與他們交談。"},{"en":"The organiser had a chat with the new volunteer after training.","zh":"主辦者在培訓後與新義工談了一談。"},{"en":"A short chat can help staff understand how volunteers feel.","zh":"簡短談話可以幫助職員了解義工的感受。"},{"en":"Having a chat with volunteers can reveal whether they need extra support.","zh":"與義工談一談可以了解他們是否需要額外支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"how you feel about","meaning":"對……的感受","examples":[{"en":"The council wants to know how volunteers feel about the work.","zh":"議會想知道義工對工作的感受。"},{"en":"“How you feel about” asks for someone’s opinion, reaction, or emotion towards something.","zh":"「How you feel about」詢問某人對某事的意見、反應或情緒。"},{"en":"We want to know how you feel about your first day of volunteering.","zh":"我們想知道你對第一天做義工的感受。"},{"en":"Asking how volunteers feel helps organisers improve training and support.","zh":"詢問義工的感受有助主辦者改善培訓和支援。"},{"en":"Tell us honestly how you feel about dealing with visitors.","zh":"請坦誠告訴我們你對應付遊客的感受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"extra support","meaning":"額外支援","examples":[{"en":"The council asks what extra support volunteers need.","zh":"議會詢問義工需要甚麼額外支援。"},{"en":"Extra support means additional help beyond what is already provided.","zh":"額外支援是指現有安排以外的額外幫助。"},{"en":"New volunteers may need extra support during their first festival.","zh":"新義工在第一次節日活動中可能需要額外支援。"},{"en":"Asking about extra support can prevent volunteers from feeling overwhelmed.","zh":"詢問額外支援可以防止義工感到不知所措。"},{"en":"Extra support might include more training, clearer instructions, or a partner on duty.","zh":"額外支援可能包括更多培訓、更清楚指示或值勤伙伴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as a thank you to","meaning":"為了感謝……","examples":[{"en":"As a thank you to the volunteers, the council arranges an annual event.","zh":"為了感謝義工，議會安排一項年度活動。"},{"en":"As a thank you to someone means as a way of showing gratitude to them.","zh":"為了感謝某人，是指以某種方式向他們表達謝意。"},{"en":"The school held a dinner as a thank you to its helpers.","zh":"學校舉辦晚宴，感謝幫手。"},{"en":"A thank-you event can make volunteers feel appreciated.","zh":"感謝活動可以令義工感到受重視。"},{"en":"The council organises a special activity as a thank you to volunteers.","zh":"議會舉辦特別活動，以感謝義工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"annual event","meaning":"年度活動","examples":[{"en":"The council arranges an annual event for volunteers.","zh":"議會為義工安排年度活動。"},{"en":"An annual event is an event that happens once every year.","zh":"年度活動是每年舉行一次的活動。"},{"en":"The town’s annual event for volunteers changes each year.","zh":"小鎮為義工而設的年度活動每年都會改變。"},{"en":"Annual events help maintain relationships between organisers and volunteers.","zh":"年度活動有助維持主辦者與義工之間的關係。"},{"en":"This year’s annual event will be a trip along the canal.","zh":"今年的年度活動將會是沿運河的旅程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in recent years","meaning":"近年來","examples":[{"en":"In recent years, the volunteers have had a party in the town hall.","zh":"近年來，義工曾在市政廳舉行派對。"},{"en":"In recent years means during the last few years.","zh":"近年來是指過去幾年期間。"},{"en":"In recent years, more residents have joined the volunteer scheme.","zh":"近年來，更多居民加入義工計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase connects present arrangements with relatively recent history.","zh":"這個短語把現時安排與較近期歷史連接起來。"},{"en":"In recent years, the council has tried different ways to thank volunteers.","zh":"近年來，議會嘗試用不同方式感謝義工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"town hall","meaning":"市政廳","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers once had a party in the town hall.","zh":"義工曾在市政廳舉行派對。"},{"en":"A town hall is a public building used for local government and community events.","zh":"市政廳是用於地方政府和社區活動的公共建築。"},{"en":"The meeting took place in the town hall.","zh":"會議在市政廳舉行。"},{"en":"Town halls are often central places for ceremonies, meetings, and celebrations.","zh":"市政廳通常是典禮、會議和慶祝活動的中心地點。"},{"en":"A party in the town hall can bring volunteers together.","zh":"在市政廳舉行派對可以把義工聚在一起。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"barbecue","meaning":"燒烤活動","examples":[{"en":"Last year, the volunteers had a barbecue in Chamber Park.","zh":"去年，義工在 Chamber Park 舉行燒烤活動。"},{"en":"A barbecue is an outdoor meal where food is cooked on a grill or open heat.","zh":"燒烤活動是在戶外用烤架或明火烹調食物的聚餐。"},{"en":"The community held a barbecue after the summer festival.","zh":"社區在夏季節日後舉行燒烤活動。"},{"en":"A barbecue can be a relaxed way to thank volunteers.","zh":"燒烤活動可以是感謝義工的輕鬆方式。"},{"en":"Good weather makes a park barbecue more enjoyable.","zh":"好天氣令公園燒烤活動更愉快。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"forthcoming event","meaning":"即將舉行的活動","examples":[{"en":"The forthcoming event is a trip along the canal.","zh":"即將舉行的活動是沿運河的旅程。"},{"en":"A forthcoming event is an event that will happen soon or in the future.","zh":"即將舉行的活動是很快或未來會發生的活動。"},{"en":"The forthcoming event for volunteers will take place next month.","zh":"義工即將舉行的活動會在下月進行。"},{"en":"Announcing a forthcoming event helps people plan ahead.","zh":"宣布即將舉行的活動可以幫助人們提前計劃。"},{"en":"Volunteers can sign up for the forthcoming event after they start work.","zh":"義工開始工作後可以報名參加即將舉行的活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a trip along the canal","meaning":"沿運河的旅程","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers will take a trip along the canal from here to Dewhurst and back.","zh":"義工將會沿運河從這裏前往 Dewhurst 再返回。"},{"en":"A trip along the canal is a journey following a waterway.","zh":"沿運河的旅程是沿着水道進行的旅程。"},{"en":"The group enjoyed a peaceful trip along the canal in the afternoon.","zh":"小組下午享受了一趟寧靜的沿運河旅程。"},{"en":"A canal trip can be a relaxing reward for volunteers.","zh":"運河旅程可以作為給義工的輕鬆獎勵。"},{"en":"Travelling along the canal lets people see the town from a different view.","zh":"沿運河前進讓人們從不同角度觀看小鎮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"from here to Dewhurst and back","meaning":"從這裏到 Dewhurst 再返回","examples":[{"en":"The trip goes from here to Dewhurst and back.","zh":"這趟旅程從這裏到 Dewhurst 再返回。"},{"en":"From here to Dewhurst and back means travelling from the starting place to Dewhurst and then returning.","zh":"從這裏到 Dewhurst 再返回，是指由起點前往 Dewhurst，然後回來。"},{"en":"The boat travels from here to Dewhurst and back in one afternoon.","zh":"船在一個下午內從這裏到 Dewhurst 再返回。"},{"en":"A return route is useful because volunteers end where they started.","zh":"來回路線很方便，因為義工會回到出發地。"},{"en":"The trip is simple because it goes out and comes back along the same canal.","zh":"這趟旅程很簡單，因為它沿同一條運河去程和回程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"if you’d like to attend","meaning":"如果你想參加","examples":[{"en":"If you’d like to attend, you can sign up once you start work.","zh":"如果你想參加，一開始工作後便可以報名。"},{"en":"“If you’d like to attend” politely introduces information for people who want to go to an event.","zh":"「If you’d like to attend」有禮貌地向想參加活動的人提供資訊。"},{"en":"If you’d like to attend the lunch, please write your name on the list.","zh":"如果你想參加午餐，請在名單上寫上名字。"},{"en":"This phrase makes an invitation sound polite and optional.","zh":"這個句式令邀請聽起來有禮貌而不強迫。"},{"en":"If you’d like to attend the canal trip, you should sign up early.","zh":"如果你想參加運河旅程，應早點報名。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sign up","meaning":"報名","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers can sign up once they start work.","zh":"義工一開始工作後便可以報名。"},{"en":"To sign up means to register your name for an activity, service, or event.","zh":"報名是指為活動、服務或事件登記姓名。"},{"en":"New volunteers can sign up for training online.","zh":"新義工可以在網上報名參加培訓。"},{"en":"Signing up early helps organisers know how many people will attend.","zh":"早點報名可以幫助主辦者知道有多少人會出席。"},{"en":"You need to sign up if you want to join the canal trip.","zh":"如果你想參加運河旅程，便需要報名。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"once you start work","meaning":"一開始工作後","examples":[{"en":"You can sign up once you start work.","zh":"你一開始工作後便可以報名。"},{"en":"Once you start work means after you begin your duties or job.","zh":"一開始工作後，是指在你開始職責或工作之後。"},{"en":"Once you start work, you will receive a volunteer badge.","zh":"你一開始工作後，便會收到義工名牌。"},{"en":"Some benefits become available only after volunteers begin their duties.","zh":"一些福利只有在義工開始值勤後才可獲得。"},{"en":"You can ask for the event form once you start work.","zh":"你一開始工作後，便可以索取活動表格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the role of the volunteers","meaning":"義工的角色","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the role of the volunteers in each activity.","zh":"題目詢問義工在每項活動中的角色。"},{"en":"The role of the volunteers means what volunteers are expected to do.","zh":"義工的角色是指義工被期望做的事情。"},{"en":"The role of the volunteers at concerts is to help people find their seats.","zh":"義工在音樂會的角色是幫助人們找到座位。"},{"en":"Understanding the role of volunteers helps candidates choose the correct answer.","zh":"了解義工的角色可以幫助考生選出正確答案。"},{"en":"The role of volunteers changes depending on the activity.","zh":"義工的角色會因活動而改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the following activities","meaning":"以下活動","examples":[{"en":"The roles must be matched to the following activities.","zh":"這些角色必須配對到以下活動。"},{"en":"The following activities means the activities listed next or below.","zh":"以下活動是指接下來或下方列出的活動。"},{"en":"Match each volunteer role to the following activities.","zh":"請把每個義工角色配對到以下活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in exam instructions and worksheets.","zh":"這個短語常見於考試指示和工作紙。"},{"en":"The following activities include concerts, lunches, and website support.","zh":"以下活動包括音樂會、午餐活動和網站支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"choose answers from the box","meaning":"從方格中選出答案","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose six answers from the box.","zh":"考生從方格中選出六個答案。"},{"en":"To choose answers from the box means to select responses from a given list of options.","zh":"從方格中選出答案，是指從提供的選項清單中選擇回應。"},{"en":"Students must choose answers from the box and write the correct letters.","zh":"學生必須從方格中選出答案，並寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"This instruction limits possible answers to the options provided.","zh":"這項指示把可能答案限制在提供的選項之內。"},{"en":"Reading the question carefully helps candidates choose the right answers from the box.","zh":"仔細閱讀題目有助考生從方格中選出正確答案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"write the correct letter next to","meaning":"在……旁寫上正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the correct letter next to each question.","zh":"考生在每條問題旁寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"To write the correct letter next to something means to put the answer letter beside it.","zh":"在某物旁寫上正確字母，是指把答案字母放在其旁邊。"},{"en":"Write the correct letter next to each activity on the answer sheet.","zh":"請在答案紙上每項活動旁寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"This instruction is common in matching tasks.","zh":"這項指示常見於配對題。"},{"en":"Candidates should check spelling and position when writing the correct letter.","zh":"考生寫正確字母時，應檢查字母和位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"provide entertainment","meaning":"提供娛樂","examples":[{"en":"Some volunteers provide entertainment at lunches for retired people.","zh":"一些義工在退休人士午餐活動中提供娛樂。"},{"en":"To provide entertainment means to perform or organise enjoyable activities for others.","zh":"提供娛樂是指為別人表演或安排令人愉快的活動。"},{"en":"The students provided entertainment with songs and short plays.","zh":"學生以歌曲和短劇提供娛樂。"},{"en":"Providing entertainment can make a lunch event more cheerful.","zh":"提供娛樂可以令午餐活動更愉快。"},{"en":"Volunteers provide entertainment so guests can relax after the meal.","zh":"義工提供娛樂，讓賓客在餐後放鬆。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"provide publicity about","meaning":"為……作宣傳","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers provide publicity about a council service.","zh":"義工為一項議會服務作宣傳。"},{"en":"To provide publicity about something means to spread information so people know about it.","zh":"為某事作宣傳，是指傳播資訊，讓人們知道它。"},{"en":"Volunteers provided publicity about the new recycling service.","zh":"義工為新的回收服務作宣傳。"},{"en":"Publicity helps residents learn about services they may otherwise miss.","zh":"宣傳幫助居民了解他們可能錯過的服務。"},{"en":"The website needs publicity so as many people as possible use it.","zh":"網站需要宣傳，讓盡可能多的人使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a council service","meaning":"議會服務","examples":[{"en":"The website is an example of a council service.","zh":"網站是議會服務的一個例子。"},{"en":"A council service is a service provided or supported by the local council.","zh":"議會服務是由地方議會提供或支援的服務。"},{"en":"Waste collection is a council service.","zh":"垃圾收集是一項議會服務。"},{"en":"Residents need to know how to use council services effectively.","zh":"居民需要知道如何有效使用議會服務。"},{"en":"Volunteers may help publicise a council service by telling residents about it.","zh":"義工可能透過告知居民來協助宣傳議會服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"contact local businesses","meaning":"聯絡本地商戶","examples":[{"en":"The advertising department contacts local businesses.","zh":"廣告部門聯絡本地商戶。"},{"en":"To contact local businesses means to communicate with shops or companies in the area.","zh":"聯絡本地商戶，是指與本區的店舖或公司溝通。"},{"en":"The council contacted local businesses about festival sponsorship.","zh":"議會就節日贊助聯絡本地商戶。"},{"en":"Contacting local businesses can help raise money for community projects.","zh":"聯絡本地商戶可以幫助為社區項目籌集資金。"},{"en":"Volunteers do not need to contact local businesses because the advertising department handles it.","zh":"義工不需要聯絡本地商戶，因為廣告部門負責處理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"give advice to visitors","meaning":"向遊客提供建議","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers give advice to visitors in the town centre.","zh":"義工在鎮中心向遊客提供建議。"},{"en":"To give advice to visitors means to offer helpful information or suggestions to people visiting a place.","zh":"向遊客提供建議，是指向到訪某地的人提供有用資訊或建議。"},{"en":"Volunteers gave advice to visitors about museums and cafés.","zh":"義工向遊客提供關於博物館和咖啡店的建議。"},{"en":"Good advice can help visitors enjoy the town and avoid getting lost.","zh":"好建議可以幫助遊客享受小鎮並避免迷路。"},{"en":"Giving advice to visitors is one way volunteers make people feel welcome.","zh":"向遊客提供建議是義工令人感到受歡迎的方法之一。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"collect feedback on events","meaning":"收集活動意見","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers collect feedback on events people have attended.","zh":"義工收集人們參加過的活動意見。"},{"en":"To collect feedback on events means to gather opinions about those events.","zh":"收集活動意見，是指收集人們對活動的看法。"},{"en":"Volunteers collected feedback on the music festival after each concert.","zh":"義工在每場音樂會後收集音樂節意見。"},{"en":"Feedback helps organisers know what worked well and what should change.","zh":"回饋幫助主辦者知道哪些地方做得好，哪些應改變。"},{"en":"Collecting feedback on events can improve future programmes.","zh":"收集活動意見可以改善未來節目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sell tickets","meaning":"售票","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers are not described as selling tickets in this activity.","zh":"在這項活動中，義工並沒有被描述為負責售票。"},{"en":"To sell tickets means to take money and give people entry tickets for an event.","zh":"售票是指收取金錢並向人們提供活動入場票。"},{"en":"The box office sells tickets for the concert.","zh":"票房售賣音樂會門票。"},{"en":"Ticket selling requires careful money handling and clear records.","zh":"售票需要小心處理金錢和清楚記錄。"},{"en":"In this scheme, volunteers guide audiences rather than sell tickets.","zh":"在這個計劃中，義工負責引導觀眾，而不是售票。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"introduce guest speakers","meaning":"介紹嘉賓講者","examples":[{"en":"Some events require someone to introduce guest speakers.","zh":"一些活動需要有人介紹嘉賓講者。"},{"en":"To introduce guest speakers means to present speakers to an audience before they talk.","zh":"介紹嘉賓講者，是指在講者發言前向觀眾介紹他們。"},{"en":"The host introduced the guest speaker at the book festival.","zh":"主持人在書展中介紹嘉賓講者。"},{"en":"A clear introduction helps the audience understand who the speaker is.","zh":"清楚介紹可以幫助觀眾了解講者是誰。"},{"en":"Volunteers may introduce guest speakers at talks and community meetings.","zh":"義工可能會在講座和社區會議中介紹嘉賓講者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"guest speakers","meaning":"嘉賓講者","examples":[{"en":"A writing group may attend a talk by a guest speaker.","zh":"寫作小組可能會出席嘉賓講者的演講。"},{"en":"Guest speakers are invited people who give talks or presentations at events.","zh":"嘉賓講者是受邀在活動中發表演講或簡報的人。"},{"en":"The school invited guest speakers to discuss careers.","zh":"學校邀請嘉賓講者討論職業。"},{"en":"Guest speakers can bring expert knowledge and new perspectives.","zh":"嘉賓講者可以帶來專業知識和新觀點。"},{"en":"Volunteers may help guest speakers find the right room before a talk.","zh":"義工可能會在講座前幫助嘉賓講者找到正確房間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"encourage cooperation between","meaning":"鼓勵……之間合作","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers encourage cooperation between local organisations.","zh":"義工鼓勵本地組織之間合作。"},{"en":"To encourage cooperation between groups means to help them work together.","zh":"鼓勵團體之間合作，是指幫助它們一起工作。"},{"en":"The council encouraged cooperation between sports clubs and schools.","zh":"議會鼓勵運動俱樂部和學校之間合作。"},{"en":"Cooperation between local organisations can save money and share resources.","zh":"本地組織之間合作可以節省金錢並分享資源。"},{"en":"Volunteers encourage cooperation by introducing groups with similar needs.","zh":"義工透過介紹有相似需要的團體來鼓勵合作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"local organisations","meaning":"本地組織","examples":[{"en":"Sports clubs and gardeners’ associations are local organisations.","zh":"運動俱樂部和園藝協會都是本地組織。"},{"en":"Local organisations are groups or bodies that operate in a particular community.","zh":"本地組織是在特定社區運作的團體或機構。"},{"en":"Local organisations often support festivals, clubs, and public services.","zh":"本地組織通常支持節日、俱樂部和公共服務。"},{"en":"Cooperation between local organisations can strengthen community life.","zh":"本地組織之間合作可以加強社區生活。"},{"en":"Volunteers help local organisations find ways to support each other.","zh":"義工幫助本地組織尋找互相支援的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"help people find their seats","meaning":"幫人找到座位","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers help people find their seats at concerts.","zh":"義工在音樂會幫人找到座位。"},{"en":"To help people find their seats means to guide audience members to the correct places to sit.","zh":"幫人找到座位，是指引導觀眾到正確位置坐下。"},{"en":"Ushers helped people find their seats before the play began.","zh":"引座員在戲劇開始前幫人找到座位。"},{"en":"Helping people find their seats prevents confusion and delays.","zh":"幫人找到座位可以避免混亂和延誤。"},{"en":"Volunteers check tickets to help people find their seats accurately.","zh":"義工查看門票，以準確幫人找到座位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"helping at concerts","meaning":"在音樂會協助","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers have an important role when helping at concerts.","zh":"義工在音樂會協助時有重要角色。"},{"en":"Helping at concerts means assisting with audience guidance, seating, information, or event support.","zh":"在音樂會協助，是指協助引導觀眾、安排座位、提供資訊或支援活動。"},{"en":"Students helped at concerts by showing visitors to their seats.","zh":"學生透過帶訪客到座位來在音樂會協助。"},{"en":"Helping at concerts requires calm communication and attention to tickets.","zh":"在音樂會協助需要冷靜溝通和留意門票。"},{"en":"Volunteers who help at concerts make performances start more smoothly.","zh":"在音樂會協助的義工令表演能更順利開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"getting involved with community groups","meaning":"參與社區團體工作","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers may support the town by getting involved with community groups.","zh":"義工可以透過參與社區團體工作來支援小鎮。"},{"en":"Getting involved with community groups means taking part in the work of local organisations.","zh":"參與社區團體工作，是指加入本地組織的工作。"},{"en":"Getting involved with community groups can help volunteers meet active residents.","zh":"參與社區團體工作可以幫助義工認識活躍居民。"},{"en":"This work may involve encouraging clubs to share resources and cooperate.","zh":"這項工作可能包括鼓勵俱樂部分享資源和合作。"},{"en":"Volunteers support community life by getting involved with local groups.","zh":"義工透過參與本地團體工作來支持社區生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"helping with a magazine","meaning":"協助處理雜誌工作","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers help with a magazine by collecting people’s opinions.","zh":"義工透過收集人們的意見來協助處理雜誌工作。"},{"en":"Helping with a magazine means assisting with tasks connected to producing or improving it.","zh":"協助處理雜誌工作，是指幫助與製作或改善雜誌相關的任務。"},{"en":"Residents helped with the magazine by sending in articles.","zh":"居民透過投稿協助處理雜誌工作。"},{"en":"Volunteers do not handle advertising, but they help by collecting feedback.","zh":"義工不處理廣告，但會透過收集回饋提供協助。"},{"en":"Helping with a magazine can involve writing, editing, or gathering information.","zh":"協助處理雜誌工作可以包括寫作、編輯或收集資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"participating at lunches","meaning":"參與午餐活動","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers participate at lunches for retired people.","zh":"義工參與退休人士午餐活動。"},{"en":"Participating at lunches means taking part in lunch events and helping them run well.","zh":"參與午餐活動，是指加入午餐活動並協助其順利進行。"},{"en":"Volunteers participated at the lunch by welcoming guests and performing songs.","zh":"義工透過迎接賓客和表演歌曲參與午餐活動。"},{"en":"Participating at lunches can give volunteers a chance to talk with older residents.","zh":"參與午餐活動可以讓義工有機會與年長居民交談。"},{"en":"Lunch events need friendly volunteers who can help guests feel comfortable.","zh":"午餐活動需要友善義工幫助賓客感到舒服。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"helping with the website","meaning":"協助處理網站工作","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers help with the website by making sure residents know about it.","zh":"義工透過確保居民知道網站來協助處理網站工作。"},{"en":"Helping with the website means supporting the use or publicity of the council website.","zh":"協助處理網站工作，是指支援議會網站的使用或宣傳。"},{"en":"Volunteers helped with the website by explaining where to find event information.","zh":"義工透過解釋在哪裏找到活動資訊來協助網站工作。"},{"en":"A website is more useful when residents know it exists and understand how to use it.","zh":"當居民知道網站存在並明白如何使用時，網站會更有用。"},{"en":"Helping with the website may involve giving information rather than updating pages directly.","zh":"協助處理網站工作可能涉及提供資訊，而不是直接更新網頁。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"require the largest number of","meaning":"需要最多……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which event requires the largest number of volunteers.","zh":"題目問哪項活動需要最多義工。"},{"en":"To require the largest number of something means to need more of it than any other option.","zh":"需要最多某物，是指比其他任何選項都需要更多該物。"},{"en":"The science festival requires the largest number of helpers.","zh":"科學節需要最多幫手。"},{"en":"Events with many venues often require the largest number of volunteers.","zh":"有許多場地的活動通常需要最多義工。"},{"en":"Knowing which event requires the largest number of people helps with planning.","zh":"知道哪項活動需要最多人手，有助規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the largest number of volunteers","meaning":"最多義工","examples":[{"en":"The science festival requires the largest number of volunteers.","zh":"科學節需要最多義工。"},{"en":"The largest number of volunteers means more volunteers than any other event needs.","zh":"最多義工表示比其他任何活動都需要更多義工。"},{"en":"The music festival needs many helpers, but the science festival needs the largest number.","zh":"音樂節需要很多幫手，但科學節需要最多。"},{"en":"An event may need the largest number of volunteers because it is spread across many venues.","zh":"一項活動可能因分布在多個場地而需要最多義工。"},{"en":"The council must plan carefully for the event needing the largest number of volunteers.","zh":"議會必須仔細規劃需要最多義工的活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the most important requirement for","meaning":"對……最重要的要求","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the most important requirement for volunteers.","zh":"題目問對義工最重要的要求。"},{"en":"The most important requirement for someone is the main ability or condition they need.","zh":"對某人最重要的要求，是他們最需要的主要能力或條件。"},{"en":"The most important requirement for festival volunteers is getting on well with people.","zh":"對節日義工最重要的要求是與人相處融洽。"},{"en":"Identifying the most important requirement helps applicants know what matters most.","zh":"找出最重要的要求，可以幫助申請人知道甚麼最關鍵。"},{"en":"Flexibility is useful, but interpersonal skill is described as essential.","zh":"彈性很有用，但人際能力被形容為必不可少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"interpersonal skills","meaning":"人際溝通能力","examples":[{"en":"Interpersonal skills are essential for festival volunteers.","zh":"人際溝通能力對節日義工來說是必不可少的。"},{"en":"Interpersonal skills are abilities used to communicate and get along with other people.","zh":"人際溝通能力是用來與他人溝通和相處的能力。"},{"en":"Good interpersonal skills help volunteers stay calm with difficult visitors.","zh":"良好人際溝通能力幫助義工面對難應付遊客時保持冷靜。"},{"en":"People with strong interpersonal skills can make residents and visitors feel welcome.","zh":"人際溝通能力強的人可以令居民和遊客感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"Listening, patience, and politeness are important interpersonal skills.","zh":"聆聽、耐性和禮貌都是重要的人際溝通能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"personal interest in the event","meaning":"對活動的個人興趣","examples":[{"en":"Personal interest in the event can make volunteering more enjoyable.","zh":"對活動的個人興趣可以令做義工更愉快。"},{"en":"Personal interest in the event means caring about or enjoying that particular activity.","zh":"對活動的個人興趣，是指關心或喜歡該特定活動。"},{"en":"A volunteer with personal interest in books may prefer the book festival.","zh":"對書本有個人興趣的義工可能較喜歡書展。"},{"en":"Personal interest can increase motivation, but it is not the only requirement.","zh":"個人興趣可以提高動力，但不是唯一要求。"},{"en":"Choosing an event you like can make the work feel more meaningful.","zh":"選擇你喜歡的活動可以令工作感覺更有意義。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"flexibility","meaning":"彈性；靈活性","examples":[{"en":"Flexibility is useful because festival arrangements may change.","zh":"彈性很有用，因為節日安排可能會改變。"},{"en":"Flexibility is the ability to adapt to changes or different situations.","zh":"彈性是適應變化或不同情況的能力。"},{"en":"Volunteers need flexibility when events move indoors at short notice.","zh":"當活動臨時移到室內時，義工需要彈性。"},{"en":"Flexibility helps teams deal with weather, delays, and unexpected problems.","zh":"彈性幫助團隊處理天氣、延誤和突發問題。"},{"en":"A flexible volunteer can switch duties without becoming upset.","zh":"有彈性的義工可以轉換職責而不會不安。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"start working","meaning":"開始工作","examples":[{"en":"New volunteers will start working after their training.","zh":"新義工會在培訓後開始工作。"},{"en":"To start working means to begin doing duties or tasks.","zh":"開始工作是指開始履行職責或任務。"},{"en":"Volunteers start working after they receive their timetable.","zh":"義工收到時間表後開始工作。"},{"en":"Training before starting work helps people feel prepared.","zh":"開始工作前接受培訓可以令人感到有準備。"},{"en":"New helpers should know who to contact before they start working.","zh":"新幫手開始工作前應知道可以聯絡誰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the week beginning","meaning":"……開始的那一星期","examples":[{"en":"New volunteers will start working in the week beginning September 9th.","zh":"新義工會在九月九日開始的那一星期開始工作。"},{"en":"The week beginning a date means the week that starts on that date.","zh":"某日期開始的那一星期，是指由該日期開始的一整個星期。"},{"en":"The training will happen in the week beginning August 12th.","zh":"培訓會在八月十二日開始的那一星期進行。"},{"en":"This expression is used when referring to a whole week rather than one exact day.","zh":"當提及整個星期而非確實一天時，可以使用這個說法。"},{"en":"The week beginning September 9th is when duties start.","zh":"九月九日開始的那一星期是值勤開始的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the next annual event","meaning":"下一個年度活動","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the next annual event for volunteers.","zh":"題目詢問義工的下一個年度活動。"},{"en":"The next annual event is the yearly event that will happen next.","zh":"下一個年度活動是即將舉行的下一次每年活動。"},{"en":"The next annual event will be a boat trip along the canal.","zh":"下一個年度活動將會是沿運河的乘船旅程。"},{"en":"Annual events are organised to thank volunteers for their service.","zh":"年度活動是為了感謝義工服務而舉辦。"},{"en":"Volunteers can sign up for the next annual event after they start work.","zh":"義工開始工作後可以報名參加下一個年度活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"boat trip","meaning":"乘船旅程","examples":[{"en":"The trip along the canal is a boat trip.","zh":"沿運河的旅程是一趟乘船旅程。"},{"en":"A boat trip is a journey made by boat for travel, sightseeing, or enjoyment.","zh":"乘船旅程是乘船進行的旅程，可以是交通、觀光或娛樂用途。"},{"en":"The volunteers enjoyed a boat trip from the town to Dewhurst.","zh":"義工享受了一趟由小鎮前往 Dewhurst 的乘船旅程。"},{"en":"A boat trip can be a relaxing reward after months of volunteer work.","zh":"乘船旅程可以成為數月義工工作後的輕鬆獎勵。"},{"en":"People should sign up early if places on the boat trip are limited.","zh":"如果乘船旅程名額有限，人們應早點報名。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"ielts/listening/Practice 2/task-3":[{"front":"human geography assignment","meaning":"人文地理作業","examples":[{"en":"Two students are discussing their human geography assignment.","zh":"兩名學生正在討論他們的人文地理作業。"},{"en":"A human geography assignment is schoolwork about how people, places, societies, and environments are connected.","zh":"人文地理作業是關於人、地方、社會和環境如何互相關聯的學校作業。"},{"en":"A student may write a human geography assignment about urbanisation, migration, or poverty.","zh":"學生可能寫一份關於城市化、遷移或貧窮的人文地理作業。"},{"en":"A good human geography assignment uses examples, maps, facts, and clear explanations.","zh":"好的人文地理作業會使用例子、地圖、事實和清楚解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an academic task about people and places.","zh":"這個短語描述關於人與地方的學術任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"discuss their assignment","meaning":"討論他們的作業","examples":[{"en":"Rosie and Colin discuss their assignment together.","zh":"Rosie 和 Colin 一起討論他們的作業。"},{"en":"To discuss their assignment means to talk about what topic, ideas, and evidence they should use.","zh":"討論他們的作業意思是談論應使用甚麼題目、想法和證據。"},{"en":"Students often discuss their assignment before deciding on a final title.","zh":"學生常在決定最終題目前討論他們的作業。"},{"en":"Discussing an assignment together can help students notice problems and better options.","zh":"一起討論作業可以幫助學生留意問題和更好的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes talking through schoolwork before doing it.","zh":"這個短語描述在做作業前討論學校功課。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"struggle to think of","meaning":"很難想出","examples":[{"en":"Rosie is struggling to think of a topic for the assignment.","zh":"Rosie 很難想出作業題目。"},{"en":"To struggle to think of something means to find it difficult to come up with an idea.","zh":"很難想出某事，意思是難以想到一個想法。"},{"en":"I struggled to think of a good example for my geography essay.","zh":"我很難想出地理文章的好例子。"},{"en":"Students may struggle to think of a topic when the subject is too broad.","zh":"當題目太廣泛時，學生可能很難想出作業題目。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental difficulty in finding an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述在構思想法時的困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"I’ll tell you what","meaning":"這樣吧","examples":[{"en":"I’ll tell you what, let’s narrow the topic down first.","zh":"這樣吧，我們先縮小題目範圍。"},{"en":"“I’ll tell you what” introduces a suggestion or practical idea.","zh":"「I’ll tell you what」用來引出建議或實際想法。"},{"en":"I’ll tell you what, let’s list the possible topics before choosing one.","zh":"這樣吧，我們先列出可能題目，再選一個。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they want to move a discussion forward.","zh":"當人們想推動討論向前時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds conversational and helpful.","zh":"這個短語聽起來口語而有幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"different aspects of","meaning":"……的不同面向","examples":[{"en":"They discuss different aspects of human geography.","zh":"他們討論人文地理的不同面向。"},{"en":"Different aspects of something are the different parts, angles, or areas within it.","zh":"某事的不同面向是指其中不同部分、角度或範疇。"},{"en":"Human geography includes different aspects of society, such as population, culture, health, and cities.","zh":"人文地理包括社會的不同面向，例如人口、文化、健康和城市。"},{"en":"Looking at different aspects of a subject helps students choose a clearer focus.","zh":"看一個學科的不同面向，有助學生選擇更清楚的焦點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes separate parts of a larger topic.","zh":"這個短語描述較大題目中的不同部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"narrow the topic down","meaning":"縮小題目範圍","examples":[{"en":"They try to narrow the topic down before making a decision.","zh":"他們在作決定前嘗試縮小題目範圍。"},{"en":"To narrow the topic down means to make a broad subject smaller and more specific.","zh":"縮小題目範圍意思是把廣泛主題變得較細和較具體。"},{"en":"Instead of writing about cities, they narrowed the topic down to urbanisation.","zh":"他們沒有寫整個城市題目，而是把題目縮小到城市化。"},{"en":"Narrowing the topic down makes an assignment easier to research and organise.","zh":"縮小題目範圍令作業更容易研究和組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing a wide topic to a manageable focus.","zh":"這個短語描述把廣泛題目縮減到可處理的焦點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"help us decide","meaning":"幫助我們決定","examples":[{"en":"Looking at different areas may help us decide on a topic.","zh":"看不同範疇可能會幫助我們決定題目。"},{"en":"“Help us decide” means make it easier for us to choose.","zh":"「Help us decide」意思是令我們更容易作出選擇。"},{"en":"Reading the lecture notes may help us decide which topic is strongest.","zh":"閱讀課堂筆記可能會幫助我們決定哪個題目最有力。"},{"en":"Comparing poverty, health, culture, and urbanisation can help students decide.","zh":"比較貧窮、健康、文化和城市化可以幫助學生決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes support in making a choice.","zh":"這個短語描述對作選擇的支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one aspect is","meaning":"其中一個面向是","examples":[{"en":"One aspect is population.","zh":"其中一個面向是人口。"},{"en":"“One aspect is” introduces one part of a larger subject.","zh":"「One aspect is」用來引出較大主題中的一個部分。"},{"en":"One aspect is health, because disease can be linked to geography.","zh":"其中一個面向是健康，因為疾病可以與地理有關。"},{"en":"Students use this phrase when listing possible areas to study.","zh":"學生列出可能研究範疇時會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise a broad topic into smaller parts.","zh":"這個短語有助把廣泛題目組織成較小部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"population density","meaning":"人口密度","examples":[{"en":"Population density is an important topic in human geography.","zh":"人口密度是人文地理中的重要題目。"},{"en":"Population density means how many people live in a particular area.","zh":"人口密度意思是某個地區居住了多少人。"},{"en":"A city with many people in a small space has high population density.","zh":"一個小範圍內有很多人居住的城市，人口密度很高。"},{"en":"Population density can affect housing, transport, schools, and public health.","zh":"人口密度可以影響住屋、交通、學校和公共健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the relationship between people and space.","zh":"這個短語描述人口與空間之間的關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"migration","meaning":"遷移；移民","examples":[{"en":"The topic would include population density and migration.","zh":"這個題目會包括人口密度和遷移。"},{"en":"Migration means the movement of people from one place to another to live or work.","zh":"遷移或移民意思是人們從一個地方移到另一個地方生活或工作。"},{"en":"Migration can happen within a country or across national borders.","zh":"遷移可以發生在國內，也可以跨越國界。"},{"en":"Migration affects cities because newcomers need housing, jobs, schools, and services.","zh":"遷移會影響城市，因為新來者需要住屋、工作、學校和服務。"},{"en":"This word describes movement of people and its social effects.","zh":"這個詞描述人口流動及其社會影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"and so on","meaning":"等等","examples":[{"en":"The assignment could cover population density, migration and so on.","zh":"這份作業可以涵蓋人口密度、遷移等等。"},{"en":"“And so on” means and other similar things.","zh":"「And so on」意思是以及其他類似事物。"},{"en":"Human geography includes population, migration, urbanisation, culture and so on.","zh":"人文地理包括人口、遷移、城市化、文化等等。"},{"en":"People use “and so on” when they do not need to list every example.","zh":"當人們不需要列出所有例子時，會使用「and so on」。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a list open-ended.","zh":"這個短語令清單保持開放。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"facts and statistics","meaning":"事實和統計資料","examples":[{"en":"The topic would involve lots of facts and statistics.","zh":"這個題目會涉及很多事實和統計資料。"},{"en":"Facts and statistics are true information and numerical data.","zh":"事實和統計資料是真實資料和數字數據。"},{"en":"Population density research needs facts and statistics about people and land area.","zh":"人口密度研究需要關於人口和土地面積的事實和統計資料。"},{"en":"Facts and statistics can support an argument, but they should be reliable.","zh":"事實和統計資料可以支持論點，但必須可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence made from information and numbers.","zh":"這個短語描述由資料和數字構成的證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a bit boring","meaning":"有點沉悶","examples":[{"en":"Rosie thinks the topic may be a bit boring.","zh":"Rosie 覺得這個題目可能有點沉悶。"},{"en":"A bit boring means slightly dull or not very interesting.","zh":"有點沉悶意思是稍微乏味或不太有趣。"},{"en":"A topic full of statistics may feel a bit boring if there are no real-life examples.","zh":"如果沒有真實生活例子，一個充滿統計資料的題目可能有點沉悶。"},{"en":"Students may avoid a topic that seems a bit boring because it is harder to write with enthusiasm.","zh":"學生可能避開看起來有點沉悶的題目，因為較難有熱情地寫。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a mild negative opinion.","zh":"這個短語給出溫和負面意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"quite straightforward to","meaning":"相當容易去……","examples":[{"en":"The facts are quite straightforward to find online.","zh":"這些事實相當容易在網上找到。"},{"en":"Quite straightforward to do something means fairly easy and not complicated.","zh":"相當容易做某事，意思是頗簡單而不複雜。"},{"en":"It is quite straightforward to find population statistics on government websites.","zh":"在政府網站上找到人口統計資料相當容易。"},{"en":"A topic is easier to research if the data is quite straightforward to locate.","zh":"如果數據相當容易找到，題目就較容易研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a task that is not very difficult.","zh":"這個短語描述不是很困難的任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"find facts about","meaning":"找到關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"It will be easy to find facts about population.","zh":"找到關於人口的資料會很容易。"},{"en":"To find facts about something means to look for true information on that topic.","zh":"找到關於某事的資料，意思是尋找該題目的真實資訊。"},{"en":"Students can find facts about migration from census reports.","zh":"學生可以從人口普查報告找到關於遷移的資料。"},{"en":"Finding facts about a topic helps make an assignment more accurate.","zh":"找到關於題目的資料有助令作業更準確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes searching for reliable information.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找可靠資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I suppose so","meaning":"我想也是","examples":[{"en":"Rosie says, “I suppose so,” when Colin makes his point.","zh":"Colin 提出觀點時，Rosie 說：「我想也是。」"},{"en":"“I suppose so” means I think you are probably right, but I am not fully enthusiastic.","zh":"「I suppose so」意思是我想你大概是對的，但我不是非常熱烈同意。"},{"en":"The facts are easy to find, so I suppose so.","zh":"這些事實容易找到，所以我想也是。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they agree weakly or reluctantly.","zh":"當人們不太強烈或有點勉強地同意時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase shows cautious agreement.","zh":"這個短語表示謹慎同意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the links between","meaning":"……之間的關聯","examples":[{"en":"Rosie had never thought about the links between health and geography.","zh":"Rosie 從未想過健康與地理之間的關聯。"},{"en":"The links between two things are the connections or relationships between them.","zh":"兩件事之間的關聯是指它們之間的連繫或關係。"},{"en":"The links between poverty and urbanisation can be seen in housing and employment patterns.","zh":"貧窮與城市化之間的關聯可以從住屋和就業模式中看見。"},{"en":"Studying links between health and geography helps explain why diseases spread in certain places.","zh":"研究健康與地理之間的關聯，有助解釋疾病為何在某些地方傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relationships between ideas or issues.","zh":"這個短語描述想法或議題之間的關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"give a lecture on","meaning":"講授關於……的課","examples":[{"en":"Professor Lee gave a lecture on cholera.","zh":"Lee 教授講授了一課關於霍亂的內容。"},{"en":"To give a lecture on a topic means to teach or speak formally about it.","zh":"講授關於某題目的課，意思是正式教導或講解該題目。"},{"en":"The professor gave a lecture on urbanisation and city growth.","zh":"教授講授了一課關於城市化和城市增長的內容。"},{"en":"A lecture on disease and geography can show how maps help public health.","zh":"關於疾病與地理的課可以展示地圖如何幫助公共健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal teaching about a subject.","zh":"這個短語描述對某學科的正式教學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cholera","meaning":"霍亂","examples":[{"en":"Professor Lee gave the students a lecture on cholera.","zh":"Lee 教授給學生講授了一課關於霍亂的內容。"},{"en":"Cholera is a serious disease often spread through dirty water.","zh":"霍亂是一種嚴重疾病，通常透過骯髒食水傳播。"},{"en":"A cholera outbreak can happen when water supplies become contaminated.","zh":"當供水受污染時，可能會爆發霍亂。"},{"en":"Studying cholera helps students understand the link between health, water, and geography.","zh":"研究霍亂有助學生理解健康、水和地理之間的關聯。"},{"en":"This word describes a disease important in public health history.","zh":"這個詞描述公共健康歷史中重要的疾病。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in the nineteenth century","meaning":"在十九世紀","examples":[{"en":"In the nineteenth century, a physician investigated a cholera epidemic.","zh":"在十九世紀，一位醫生調查了一場霍亂疫情。"},{"en":"In the nineteenth century means during the years from 1801 to 1900.","zh":"在十九世紀意思是在 1801 年至 1900 年期間。"},{"en":"Many cities grew quickly in the nineteenth century, creating new health problems.","zh":"許多城市在十九世紀快速增長，造成新的健康問題。"},{"en":"Public health improved after doctors studied disease patterns in the nineteenth century.","zh":"醫生在十九世紀研究疾病模式後，公共健康有所改善。"},{"en":"This phrase gives historical time context.","zh":"這個短語提供歷史時間背景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"physician","meaning":"醫生；內科醫生","examples":[{"en":"A physician used street plans to find the source of the epidemic.","zh":"一位醫生使用街道圖找出疫情源頭。"},{"en":"A physician is a medical doctor, especially one who diagnoses and treats illness.","zh":"醫生或內科醫生是診斷和治療疾病的醫療專業人士。"},{"en":"The physician studied maps to understand where sick people lived.","zh":"那位醫生研究地圖，以了解病人住在哪裏。"},{"en":"A physician can use geography to investigate how disease spreads.","zh":"醫生可以使用地理知識調查疾病如何傳播。"},{"en":"This word describes a trained medical professional.","zh":"這個詞描述受訓醫療專業人士。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"street plans","meaning":"街道圖","examples":[{"en":"The physician used street plans in his investigation.","zh":"那位醫生在調查中使用街道圖。"},{"en":"Street plans are maps or drawings showing streets, roads, and nearby buildings.","zh":"街道圖是顯示街道、道路和附近建築的地圖或圖則。"},{"en":"Street plans helped the doctor see where cholera cases were concentrated.","zh":"街道圖幫助醫生看出霍亂個案集中在哪裏。"},{"en":"Using street plans can reveal patterns that are hard to see from numbers alone.","zh":"使用街道圖可以揭示單靠數字難以看見的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes maps used to understand urban space.","zh":"這個短語描述用來理解城市空間的地圖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"water supplies","meaning":"供水系統；供水情況","examples":[{"en":"Plans of water supplies helped identify the source of the disease.","zh":"供水系統圖有助找出疾病源頭。"},{"en":"Water supplies are the systems or sources that provide water to people.","zh":"供水系統是向人們提供食水的系統或來源。"},{"en":"Contaminated water supplies can spread diseases such as cholera.","zh":"受污染的供水系統可以傳播霍亂等疾病。"},{"en":"Mapping water supplies can help researchers find where a public health problem began.","zh":"繪製供水情況地圖可以幫助研究人員找出公共健康問題從何開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the way water reaches a community.","zh":"這個短語描述水如何到達社區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"find the source of","meaning":"找出……的源頭","examples":[{"en":"The physician used maps to find the source of the epidemic.","zh":"那位醫生使用地圖找出疫情源頭。"},{"en":"To find the source of something means to discover where it started or came from.","zh":"找出某事的源頭，意思是發現它從哪裏開始或來自哪裏。"},{"en":"Investigators used water maps to find the source of the illness.","zh":"調查人員使用供水地圖找出疾病源頭。"},{"en":"Finding the source of a disease can help stop it from spreading.","zh":"找出疾病源頭可以幫助阻止它傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase describes identifying the origin of a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述辨認問題的起源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a cholera epidemic","meaning":"霍亂疫情","examples":[{"en":"The lecture explained how a cholera epidemic was investigated.","zh":"這堂課解釋了一場霍亂疫情如何被調查。"},{"en":"A cholera epidemic is a serious outbreak of cholera affecting many people in an area.","zh":"霍亂疫情是指在某地區影響很多人的嚴重霍亂爆發。"},{"en":"A cholera epidemic may spread quickly if clean water is not available.","zh":"如果沒有潔淨食水，霍亂疫情可能會快速傳播。"},{"en":"Investigating a cholera epidemic requires medical knowledge and geographical information.","zh":"調查霍亂疫情需要醫學知識和地理資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major public health crisis.","zh":"這個短語描述重大的公共健康危機。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"something more general","meaning":"比較廣泛的題目","examples":[{"en":"Colin suggests doing something more general, like economies.","zh":"Colin 建議做比較廣泛的題目，例如經濟。"},{"en":"Something more general is a topic that is broader and less specific.","zh":"比較廣泛的題目是範圍較大、較不具體的題目。"},{"en":"Instead of studying one disease, they could choose something more general like health and geography.","zh":"他們可以不研究單一疾病，而選擇健康與地理這類比較廣泛的題目。"},{"en":"A more general topic can be easier to start, but harder to focus.","zh":"比較廣泛的題目可能較容易開始，但較難聚焦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broader subject choice.","zh":"這個短語描述較寬闊的題目選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"financial and commercial factors","meaning":"財務和商業因素","examples":[{"en":"They discuss how financial and commercial factors relate to geography.","zh":"他們討論財務和商業因素如何與地理有關。"},{"en":"Financial and commercial factors are money, business, trade, and market-related influences.","zh":"財務和商業因素是與金錢、生意、貿易和市場有關的影響因素。"},{"en":"Financial and commercial factors can shape where shops, offices, and factories are built.","zh":"財務和商業因素可以影響商店、辦公室和工廠建在哪裏。"},{"en":"A city’s growth may depend on financial and commercial factors as well as transport.","zh":"一個城市的增長可能取決於財務和商業因素，以及交通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes economic influences on places.","zh":"這個短語描述對地方的經濟影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be linked to","meaning":"與……有關聯","examples":[{"en":"Financial factors are linked to the physical environment.","zh":"財務因素與自然環境有關聯。"},{"en":"To be linked to something means to be connected with it in some way.","zh":"與某事有關聯，意思是在某方面與它有連繫。"},{"en":"Disease spread can be linked to water supplies and population density.","zh":"疾病傳播可能與供水系統和人口密度有關聯。"},{"en":"Economic development may be linked to transport, land, and natural resources.","zh":"經濟發展可能與交通、土地和自然資源有關聯。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a relationship between two things.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩件事之間的關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the physical environment","meaning":"自然環境；物質環境","examples":[{"en":"Economies can be linked to the physical environment.","zh":"經濟可以與自然環境或物質環境有關聯。"},{"en":"The physical environment means natural and built surroundings, such as land, water, climate, and buildings.","zh":"自然環境或物質環境是指自然和建成的周遭環境，例如土地、水、氣候和建築物。"},{"en":"The physical environment can affect where people live and work.","zh":"物質環境可以影響人們在哪裏居住和工作。"},{"en":"Floods, mountains, ports, and roads are all parts of the physical environment that shape economies.","zh":"洪水、山脈、港口和道路都是塑造經濟的物質環境部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the surroundings that influence human activity.","zh":"這個短語描述影響人類活動的周遭環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be taken off the syllabus","meaning":"從課程大綱中刪去","examples":[{"en":"Rosie thinks economies may have been taken off the syllabus.","zh":"Rosie 覺得經濟可能已從課程大綱中刪去。"},{"en":"To be taken off the syllabus means to be removed from the list of topics students must study.","zh":"從課程大綱中刪去，意思是從學生必須學習的題目清單中移除。"},{"en":"If a topic is taken off the syllabus, it may not be safe for an assignment.","zh":"如果一個題目從課程大綱中刪去，用它做作業可能不安全。"},{"en":"Students should check before choosing a topic that may have been taken off the syllabus.","zh":"學生在選擇可能已從課程大綱中刪去的題目前，應先查清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a course content change.","zh":"這個短語描述課程內容的改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the syllabus","meaning":"課程大綱","examples":[{"en":"The topic may not be on the syllabus this year.","zh":"這個題目今年可能不在課程大綱內。"},{"en":"The syllabus is the official list of topics, skills, and requirements for a course.","zh":"課程大綱是一門課的官方題目、技能和要求清單。"},{"en":"Students should check the syllabus before choosing an assignment topic.","zh":"學生在選擇作業題目前應查看課程大綱。"},{"en":"If poverty is on the syllabus, it is likely suitable for the assignment.","zh":"如果貧窮在課程大綱內，它很可能適合作業。"},{"en":"This word describes the planned content of a course.","zh":"這個詞描述一門課的規劃內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it might be best to","meaning":"最好還是……","examples":[{"en":"It might be best to avoid that topic.","zh":"最好還是避開那個題目。"},{"en":"“It might be best to” gives careful advice about the most sensible action.","zh":"「It might be best to」用來謹慎建議最合理的行動。"},{"en":"It might be best to choose a topic clearly included in the syllabus.","zh":"最好還是選擇明確包括在課程大綱中的題目。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they want to sound cautious, not forceful.","zh":"當人們想聽起來謹慎而不是強硬時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a wise choice.","zh":"這個短語建議明智選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"avoid it","meaning":"避開它","examples":[{"en":"They decide it may be safer to avoid it.","zh":"他們決定避開它可能較安全。"},{"en":"To avoid it means to stay away from it or choose not to use it.","zh":"避開它意思是遠離它或選擇不使用它。"},{"en":"If the topic is not on the syllabus, students may avoid it.","zh":"如果題目不在課程大綱內，學生可能會避開它。"},{"en":"Avoiding a risky topic can prevent problems later in the assignment.","zh":"避開有風險的題目可以防止作業後來出現問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing not to deal with something.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇不處理某事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"do something on","meaning":"做關於……的題目","examples":[{"en":"They could do something on culture.","zh":"他們可以做關於文化的題目。"},{"en":"To do something on a topic means to prepare work, research, or an assignment about it.","zh":"做關於某題目的東西，意思是準備有關它的工作、研究或作業。"},{"en":"They might do something on urbanisation because many people now live in cities.","zh":"他們可能做關於城市化的題目，因為現在很多人住在城市。"},{"en":"Students use this phrase casually when discussing possible assignment topics.","zh":"學生討論可能的作業題目時，常口語地使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase means choosing a subject to work on.","zh":"這個短語表示選擇一個主題來做。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"culture and geography","meaning":"文化與地理","examples":[{"en":"They had a lecture about culture and geography last week.","zh":"他們上星期有一堂關於文化與地理的課。"},{"en":"Culture and geography explores how traditions, beliefs, languages, and lifestyles connect with places.","zh":"文化與地理探討傳統、信念、語言和生活方式如何與地方連繫。"},{"en":"A study of culture and geography may examine how festivals shape a city’s identity.","zh":"文化與地理研究可能考察節日如何塑造城市身份。"},{"en":"Culture and geography can be interesting when clear examples are provided.","zh":"當有清楚例子時，文化與地理可以很有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase connects human traditions with location and space.","zh":"這個短語把人類傳統與地點和空間連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get much out of","meaning":"從……中學到很多","examples":[{"en":"Rosie did not get much out of the lecture.","zh":"Rosie 沒有從那堂課中學到很多。"},{"en":"To get much out of something means to learn or gain a lot from it.","zh":"從某事中學到很多，意思是從中獲得很多知識或收穫。"},{"en":"I did not get much out of the lecture because the examples were too vague.","zh":"我沒有從那堂課中學到很多，因為例子太含糊。"},{"en":"Students get more out of a class when the lecturer gives clear cases.","zh":"當講師給出清楚個案時，學生會從課堂中學到更多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how useful an experience is.","zh":"這個短語描述一次經驗有多有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"useful examples","meaning":"有用的例子","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer did not give any useful examples.","zh":"講師沒有給任何有用的例子。"},{"en":"Useful examples are clear cases that help explain an idea.","zh":"有用的例子是能幫助解釋想法的清楚個案。"},{"en":"A cholera map is a useful example of the link between health and geography.","zh":"霍亂地圖是健康與地理之間關聯的有用例子。"},{"en":"Without useful examples, a topic may feel too abstract.","zh":"沒有有用的例子，題目可能感覺太抽象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes examples that help students understand.","zh":"這個短語描述能幫助學生理解的例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take notes","meaning":"做筆記","examples":[{"en":"Colin hardly took any notes during the lecture.","zh":"Colin 在那堂課期間幾乎沒有做筆記。"},{"en":"To take notes means to write down important points while listening or reading.","zh":"做筆記意思是在聆聽或閱讀時寫下重要重點。"},{"en":"Students take notes during lectures so they can review ideas later.","zh":"學生在課堂上做筆記，以便之後溫習想法。"},{"en":"If a lecture seems vague, students may not take many notes.","zh":"如果課堂感覺含糊，學生可能不會做很多筆記。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recording information for study.","zh":"這個短語描述為學習而記錄資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"it didn’t seem worth it","meaning":"感覺不值得","examples":[{"en":"Colin did not take many notes because it did not seem worth it.","zh":"Colin 沒有做很多筆記，因為他覺得不值得。"},{"en":"“It didn’t seem worth it” means it did not appear useful enough for the effort.","zh":"「It didn’t seem worth it」意思是它看起來不夠有用，不值得付出努力。"},{"en":"The lecture gave no clear examples, so writing detailed notes did not seem worth it.","zh":"那堂課沒有清楚例子，所以詳細做筆記感覺不值得。"},{"en":"Students may stop taking notes if the material does not seem worth it.","zh":"如果材料感覺不值得，學生可能會停止做筆記。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why someone chooses not to spend effort.","zh":"這個短語解釋某人為何選擇不花力氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"focus on poverty","meaning":"聚焦於貧窮問題","examples":[{"en":"They could focus on poverty for the assignment.","zh":"他們可以在作業中聚焦於貧窮問題。"},{"en":"To focus on poverty means to make poverty the main topic of study.","zh":"聚焦於貧窮問題，意思是把貧窮作為主要研究題目。"},{"en":"Students can focus on poverty by looking at income, housing, jobs, and access to services.","zh":"學生可以透過研究收入、住屋、工作和服務使用情況來聚焦於貧窮問題。"},{"en":"Focusing on poverty may reveal how geography affects people’s opportunities.","zh":"聚焦於貧窮問題可能揭示地理如何影響人的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing poverty as the central subject.","zh":"這個短語描述把貧窮選為中心主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a global problem","meaning":"全球性問題","examples":[{"en":"Poverty is a global problem.","zh":"貧窮是全球性問題。"},{"en":"A global problem is an issue affecting many countries or the whole world.","zh":"全球性問題是影響很多國家或整個世界的議題。"},{"en":"Climate change, poverty, and migration can all be global problems.","zh":"氣候變化、貧窮和遷移都可以是全球性問題。"},{"en":"A global problem may look different in different cities and regions.","zh":"全球性問題在不同城市和地區可能有不同表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an issue beyond one place.","zh":"這個短語描述超越單一地方的議題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the trouble is","meaning":"問題是","examples":[{"en":"The trouble is that poverty figures may be unreliable.","zh":"問題是貧窮數據可能不可靠。"},{"en":"“The trouble is” introduces the main problem with an idea or situation.","zh":"「The trouble is」用來引出某個想法或情況的主要問題。"},{"en":"The trouble is that the topic is interesting, but the data may not be reliable.","zh":"問題是這個題目很有趣，但數據可能不可靠。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they want to explain why something is difficult.","zh":"當人們想解釋為何某事困難時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a problem or complication.","zh":"這個短語表示問題或複雜之處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have to be careful with","meaning":"處理……時要小心","examples":[{"en":"You have to be careful with some poverty figures.","zh":"你處理一些貧窮數據時要小心。"},{"en":"To have to be careful with something means to use it cautiously because it may be wrong, sensitive, or risky.","zh":"處理某事時要小心，意思是要謹慎使用它，因為它可能錯誤、敏感或有風險。"},{"en":"Students have to be careful with statistics that may have been manipulated.","zh":"學生處理可能被操控的統計資料時要小心。"},{"en":"You should be careful with poverty figures because different governments may measure poverty differently.","zh":"你處理貧窮數據時要小心，因為不同政府可能用不同方式量度貧窮。"},{"en":"This phrase warns people not to accept information too quickly.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們不要太快接受資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"figures relating to poverty","meaning":"與貧窮相關的數據","examples":[{"en":"Some figures relating to poverty may be manipulated.","zh":"一些與貧窮相關的數據可能被操控。"},{"en":"Figures relating to poverty are numbers or statistics about poverty levels, income, or living conditions.","zh":"與貧窮相關的數據是關於貧窮水平、收入或生活條件的數字或統計資料。"},{"en":"Figures relating to poverty can show how many people lack secure housing or enough income.","zh":"與貧窮相關的數據可以顯示多少人缺乏穩定住屋或足夠收入。"},{"en":"If figures relating to poverty are unreliable, the assignment’s argument may become weak.","zh":"如果與貧窮相關的數據不可靠，作業的論點可能會變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes numerical evidence about poverty.","zh":"這個短語描述關於貧窮的數字證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"deliberately manipulated","meaning":"被刻意操控","examples":[{"en":"The figures are sometimes deliberately manipulated.","zh":"這些數據有時被刻意操控。"},{"en":"Deliberately manipulated means changed on purpose, often to mislead people.","zh":"被刻意操控意思是被有意改動，通常是為了誤導人。"},{"en":"Poverty figures may be deliberately manipulated to make a government look successful.","zh":"貧窮數據可能被刻意操控，以令政府看起來成功。"},{"en":"Deliberately manipulated data can damage trust in research.","zh":"被刻意操控的數據會損害人們對研究的信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intentional distortion of information.","zh":"這個短語描述有意扭曲資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"for political reasons","meaning":"因政治原因","examples":[{"en":"The information may be changed for political reasons.","zh":"資料可能因政治原因而被改動。"},{"en":"For political reasons means because of government, power, elections, or public image.","zh":"因政治原因意思是因政府、權力、選舉或公眾形象而造成。"},{"en":"Poverty statistics may be presented differently for political reasons.","zh":"貧窮統計資料可能因政治原因而以不同方式呈現。"},{"en":"If figures are changed for political reasons, students should question their reliability.","zh":"如果數據因政治原因被改動，學生應質疑其可靠性。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a motive connected to politics.","zh":"這個短語解釋與政治有關的動機。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"that sort of thing","meaning":"差不多是那樣的事情","examples":[{"en":"Rosie agrees that it is that sort of thing.","zh":"Rosie 同意差不多是那樣的事情。"},{"en":"“That sort of thing” means things like the example just mentioned.","zh":"「That sort of thing」意思是像剛才提到的例子那類事情。"},{"en":"Data manipulation, political pressure, unclear definitions and that sort of thing can affect poverty figures.","zh":"數據操控、政治壓力、定義不清和那類事情都可能影響貧窮數據。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they do not need to list every similar example.","zh":"當人們不需要列出每個相似例子時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase keeps a list general and informal.","zh":"這個短語令清單保持概括和口語化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the rest of the discussion","meaning":"餘下的討論","examples":[{"en":"Students hear the rest of the discussion after reading the questions.","zh":"學生讀完問題後會聽到餘下的討論。"},{"en":"The rest of the discussion means the remaining part of the conversation.","zh":"餘下的討論意思是對話剩下的部分。"},{"en":"The rest of the discussion focused on urbanisation and sustainable cities.","zh":"餘下的討論聚焦於城市化和可持續城市。"},{"en":"Listening to the rest of the discussion helps students answer later questions.","zh":"聆聽餘下的討論有助學生回答後面的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the part that has not yet been heard or covered.","zh":"這個短語描述尚未聽到或涵蓋的部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"what are we going to do","meaning":"我們打算做甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Rosie asks what they are going to do their assignment on.","zh":"Rosie 問他們打算以甚麼作為作業題目。"},{"en":"“What are we going to do” asks what plan or choice will be made.","zh":"「What are we going to do」是在問將會作出甚麼計劃或選擇。"},{"en":"What are we going to do if poverty figures are unreliable?","zh":"如果貧窮數據不可靠，我們打算怎樣做？"},{"en":"Students ask this when they need to make a decision and move forward.","zh":"當學生需要作出決定並繼續前進時，會問這個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a practical planning question.","zh":"這個短語引出實際規劃問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"do our assignment on","meaning":"以……作為作業題目","examples":[{"en":"They need to decide what to do their assignment on.","zh":"他們需要決定以甚麼作為作業題目。"},{"en":"To do an assignment on a topic means to choose that topic as the subject of the assignment.","zh":"以某題目作為作業題目，意思是選擇該題目作為作業主題。"},{"en":"They may do their assignment on urbanisation because it affects many cities.","zh":"他們可能以城市化作為作業題目，因為它影響很多城市。"},{"en":"Choosing what to do an assignment on is easier after comparing possible topics.","zh":"比較可能題目後，選擇以甚麼作業題目會更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes selecting the main subject of schoolwork.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇學校作業的主要主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"one of the possibilities","meaning":"其中一個可能性","examples":[{"en":"Urbanisation is one of the possibilities they have not discussed.","zh":"城市化是他們尚未討論的其中一個可能性。"},{"en":"One of the possibilities means one option among several choices.","zh":"其中一個可能性意思是幾個選擇中的一個選項。"},{"en":"Poverty is one possibility, and urbanisation is another possibility.","zh":"貧窮是一個可能性，城市化是另一個可能性。"},{"en":"Listing one of the possibilities helps students compare topics before deciding.","zh":"列出其中一個可能性有助學生在決定前比較題目。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an option that could be chosen.","zh":"這個短語描述可以被選擇的選項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"urbanisation","meaning":"城市化","examples":[{"en":"Urbanisation is an important topic in human geography.","zh":"城市化是人文地理中的重要題目。"},{"en":"Urbanisation is the process in which more people live in cities and cities grow larger.","zh":"城市化是更多人住進城市、城市變得更大的過程。"},{"en":"Urbanisation can create jobs, shopping centres, housing pressure, and traffic problems.","zh":"城市化可以帶來職位、購物中心、住屋壓力和交通問題。"},{"en":"Studying urbanisation helps explain how modern societies are changing.","zh":"研究城市化有助解釋現代社會如何改變。"},{"en":"This word describes city growth and movement toward city life.","zh":"這個詞描述城市增長和走向城市生活的過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"over half the world’s population","meaning":"世界超過一半人口","examples":[{"en":"Over half the world’s population lives in cities.","zh":"世界超過一半人口住在城市。"},{"en":"Over half the world’s population means more than 50 percent of all people on Earth.","zh":"世界超過一半人口意思是地球上所有人中超過百分之五十。"},{"en":"If over half the world’s population lives in cities, urban issues affect billions of people.","zh":"如果世界超過一半人口住在城市，城市問題就影響數十億人。"},{"en":"This fact makes urbanisation a strong topic for human geography.","zh":"這個事實令城市化成為人文地理的有力題目。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very large global proportion.","zh":"這個短語描述非常大的全球比例。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"live in cities","meaning":"住在城市","examples":[{"en":"Over half the world’s population now lives in cities.","zh":"現在世界超過一半人口住在城市。"},{"en":"To live in cities means to reside in urban areas rather than rural areas.","zh":"住在城市意思是居住在都市地區，而不是鄉郊地區。"},{"en":"People live in cities for jobs, education, services, and transport.","zh":"人們因工作、教育、服務和交通而住在城市。"},{"en":"When more people live in cities, demand for housing and infrastructure increases.","zh":"當更多人住在城市，對住屋和基建的需求會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where people make their homes.","zh":"這個短語描述人們在哪裏安家。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"good idea","meaning":"好主意","examples":[{"en":"Colin thinks urbanisation is a good idea for the assignment.","zh":"Colin 覺得城市化是作業的好主意。"},{"en":"A good idea is a plan or suggestion that seems useful, sensible, or interesting.","zh":"好主意是看起來有用、合理或有趣的計劃或建議。"},{"en":"Choosing urbanisation is a good idea because there are many examples to discuss.","zh":"選擇城市化是好主意，因為有很多例子可討論。"},{"en":"A topic is a good idea if it is relevant, clear, and supported by evidence.","zh":"如果一個題目相關、清楚並有證據支持，它就是好主意。"},{"en":"This phrase gives positive judgement about a suggestion.","zh":"這個短語對建議給出正面評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a big city","meaning":"大城市","examples":[{"en":"Rosie loves living in a big city.","zh":"Rosie 喜歡住在大城市。"},{"en":"A big city is a large urban area with many people, services, buildings, and activities.","zh":"大城市是有很多人口、服務、建築和活動的大型都市地區。"},{"en":"A big city may offer jobs, universities, transport, and entertainment.","zh":"大城市可能提供工作、大學、交通和娛樂。"},{"en":"Living in a big city can be exciting, but it may also bring problems such as crime and unemployment.","zh":"住在大城市可以很刺激，但也可能帶來犯罪和失業等問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large and busy urban place.","zh":"這個短語描述大型而繁忙的都市地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"of course","meaning":"當然","examples":[{"en":"Of course, there are problems in big cities.","zh":"當然，大城市中有問題。"},{"en":"“Of course” shows that something is expected, obvious, or already understood.","zh":"「Of course」表示某事是預期之中、明顯或已被理解的。"},{"en":"Of course, urbanisation brings benefits, but it also creates pressure on housing.","zh":"當然，城市化帶來好處，但也造成住屋壓力。"},{"en":"Speakers use “of course” when they think listeners will not be surprised.","zh":"當說話者認為聽眾不會驚訝時，會使用「of course」。"},{"en":"This phrase helps introduce a point that seems natural or obvious.","zh":"這個短語有助引出看起來自然或明顯的重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"things like","meaning":"像……之類的事物","examples":[{"en":"Colin mentions things like theft and robbery.","zh":"Colin 提到像偷竊和搶劫之類的事。"},{"en":"“Things like” introduces examples without giving a complete list.","zh":"「Things like」用來引出例子，而不是提供完整清單。"},{"en":"Big cities may have problems like traffic, pollution, and homelessness.","zh":"大城市可能有交通、污染和無家可歸之類的問題。"},{"en":"People use “things like” when giving simple examples of a broader issue.","zh":"當人們給出較大議題的簡單例子時，會使用「things like」。"},{"en":"This phrase keeps examples open-ended.","zh":"這個短語令例子保持開放。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"theft and robbery","meaning":"偷竊和搶劫","examples":[{"en":"The students discuss theft and robbery as urban problems.","zh":"學生討論偷竊和搶劫作為城市問題。"},{"en":"Theft and robbery are crimes involving stealing; robbery usually involves force or threat.","zh":"偷竊和搶劫都是涉及偷取他人財物的罪行；搶劫通常涉及武力或威脅。"},{"en":"Theft and robbery may increase in areas with poverty and weak security.","zh":"偷竊和搶劫可能在貧窮和保安薄弱的地區增加。"},{"en":"Discussing theft and robbery helps students consider safety in cities.","zh":"討論偷竊和搶劫有助學生思考城市安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes crime-related urban issues.","zh":"這個短語描述與犯罪有關的城市問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"where I come from","meaning":"在我來的地方","examples":[{"en":"Rosie explains the situation where she comes from.","zh":"Rosie 解釋她來的地方的情況。"},{"en":"“Where I come from” means the place, city, or country I am originally from.","zh":"「Where I come from」意思是我原本來自的地方、城市或國家。"},{"en":"Where I come from, unemployment is a bigger problem than theft.","zh":"在我來的地方，失業比偷竊更嚴重。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when comparing their own place with another place.","zh":"當人們比較自己的地方與另一個地方時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase connects personal experience with geography.","zh":"這個短語把個人經驗與地理連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a more serious issue","meaning":"更嚴重的問題","examples":[{"en":"Unemployment is a more serious issue in Rosie’s city.","zh":"在 Rosie 的城市，失業是更嚴重的問題。"},{"en":"A more serious issue is a problem that is more important, harmful, or urgent than another.","zh":"更嚴重的問題是比另一問題更重要、更有害或更迫切的問題。"},{"en":"In some cities, homelessness is a more serious issue than traffic.","zh":"在一些城市，無家可歸比交通更嚴重。"},{"en":"Identifying the more serious issue helps students focus their argument.","zh":"找出更嚴重的問題有助學生聚焦論點。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the importance of problems.","zh":"這個短語比較問題的重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a lot of people don’t have jobs","meaning":"很多人沒有工作","examples":[{"en":"A lot of people do not have jobs in Rosie’s city.","zh":"在 Rosie 的城市，很多人沒有工作。"},{"en":"“A lot of people don’t have jobs” means many people are unemployed.","zh":"「A lot of people don’t have jobs」意思是很多人失業。"},{"en":"If a lot of people do not have jobs, families may struggle to pay for food and housing.","zh":"如果很多人沒有工作，家庭可能難以支付食物和住屋費用。"},{"en":"A city with many people without jobs may face poverty and social tension.","zh":"很多人沒有工作的城市可能面對貧窮和社會緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase describes widespread unemployment in simple language.","zh":"這個短語以簡單語言描述普遍失業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get worse and worse","meaning":"變得越來越差","examples":[{"en":"The unemployment problem is getting worse and worse.","zh":"失業問題正變得越來越差。"},{"en":"To get worse and worse means to become increasingly bad over time.","zh":"變得越來越差意思是隨時間變得愈來愈不好。"},{"en":"Traffic can get worse and worse if a city grows without planning.","zh":"如果城市在沒有規劃下增長，交通可能變得越來越差。"},{"en":"When unemployment gets worse and worse, more people may need public support.","zh":"當失業變得越來越差時，更多人可能需要公共支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a problem that is steadily deteriorating.","zh":"這個短語描述問題持續惡化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"quite a lot of","meaning":"相當多","examples":[{"en":"There are still quite a lot of homeless people.","zh":"仍然有相當多無家可歸的人。"},{"en":"Quite a lot of means a fairly large number or amount.","zh":"相當多意思是數量或份量頗大。"},{"en":"There are quite a lot of empty shops in the city centre.","zh":"市中心有相當多空置商店。"},{"en":"If there are quite a lot of homeless people, housing policy may need attention.","zh":"如果有相當多無家可歸的人，住屋政策可能需要關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a noticeable but not exact amount.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯但不精確的數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"homeless","meaning":"無家可歸的","examples":[{"en":"Some people in Rosie’s city are homeless.","zh":"Rosie 的城市中有些人無家可歸。"},{"en":"Homeless means not having a safe or permanent place to live.","zh":"無家可歸的意思是沒有安全或永久住所。"},{"en":"Homeless people may sleep on streets, in shelters, or in temporary accommodation.","zh":"無家可歸的人可能睡在街上、庇護中心或臨時住所。"},{"en":"Urbanisation can worsen homelessness if housing becomes too expensive.","zh":"如果住屋變得太昂貴，城市化可能加劇無家可歸問題。"},{"en":"This word describes a serious housing problem.","zh":"這個詞描述嚴重住屋問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not quite so bad as","meaning":"不像……那麼差","examples":[{"en":"The homelessness problem is not quite so bad as it was.","zh":"無家可歸問題不像以前那麼差。"},{"en":"“Not quite so bad as” means less bad than before or less bad than another situation.","zh":"「Not quite so bad as」意思是沒有以前或另一情況那麼差。"},{"en":"The city centre is not quite so bad as it was after new housing opened.","zh":"新住屋落成後，市中心不像以前那麼差。"},{"en":"A problem can improve but still remain serious.","zh":"一個問題可以有所改善，但仍然嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes partial improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述部分改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"positive developments","meaning":"正面的發展","examples":[{"en":"Colin wants to talk about some positive developments.","zh":"Colin 想談談一些正面的發展。"},{"en":"Positive developments are changes that bring improvement or benefits.","zh":"正面的發展是帶來改善或好處的變化。"},{"en":"New shopping centres and conference centres can be positive developments for some cities.","zh":"新購物中心和會議中心可以是一些城市的正面發展。"},{"en":"Positive developments should still be examined carefully for costs and side effects.","zh":"正面的發展仍應仔細檢視成本和副作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes encouraging changes.","zh":"這個短語描述令人鼓舞的變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on the outskirts of cities","meaning":"在城市郊區","examples":[{"en":"New developments have appeared on the outskirts of cities.","zh":"新發展項目已出現在城市郊區。"},{"en":"On the outskirts of cities means in the outer areas near the edge of cities.","zh":"在城市郊區意思是在城市邊緣附近的外圍地區。"},{"en":"Large shopping centres are often built on the outskirts of cities because land is cheaper.","zh":"大型購物中心常建在城市郊區，因為土地較便宜。"},{"en":"Development on the outskirts of cities can change travel patterns and local communities.","zh":"在城市郊區的發展可以改變交通模式和本地社區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location near but not in the city centre.","zh":"這個短語描述接近但不在市中心的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"massive new shopping centres","meaning":"大型新購物中心","examples":[{"en":"Massive new shopping centres have opened outside Rosie’s city.","zh":"Rosie 的城市外開設了大型新購物中心。"},{"en":"Massive new shopping centres are very large recently built places with many shops.","zh":"大型新購物中心是最近建成、有很多商店的非常大型購物場所。"},{"en":"Massive new shopping centres can attract customers away from the city centre.","zh":"大型新購物中心可以把顧客從市中心吸引走。"},{"en":"They may create jobs, but they can also cause small shops to close down.","zh":"它們可能創造職位，但也可能令小商店倒閉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large retail developments.","zh":"這個短語描述大型零售發展項目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the same with mine","meaning":"我那邊也是一樣","examples":[{"en":"Colin says it is the same with his city.","zh":"Colin 說他那邊的城市也是一樣。"},{"en":"“The same with mine” means the situation is similar in my place or example too.","zh":"「The same with mine」意思是我的地方或例子情況也相似。"},{"en":"Rosie says shops are closing; Colin says it is the same with mine.","zh":"Rosie 說商店正在倒閉；Colin 說我那邊也是一樣。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when someone recognises a similar situation in their own experience.","zh":"當某人在自己的經驗中看到相似情況時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It helps compare two places or cases.","zh":"它有助比較兩個地方或個案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"city centre","meaning":"市中心","examples":[{"en":"Many shops in the city centre are closing down.","zh":"市中心很多商店正在倒閉。"},{"en":"The city centre is the main central area of a city, often with shops, offices, and transport links.","zh":"市中心是一個城市的主要中央地區，通常有商店、辦公室和交通連接。"},{"en":"A city centre may become quieter if shopping moves to the outskirts.","zh":"如果購物活動移到郊區，市中心可能變得較冷清。"},{"en":"The health of the city centre can show how urban development is changing.","zh":"市中心的狀況可以顯示城市發展如何改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the central urban area.","zh":"這個短語描述城市中央區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"close down","meaning":"倒閉；停業","examples":[{"en":"Shops in the city centre are closing down.","zh":"市中心的商店正在倒閉。"},{"en":"To close down means to stop operating permanently or for a long time.","zh":"倒閉或停業意思是永久或長時間停止營運。"},{"en":"Small shops may close down when customers move to large shopping centres.","zh":"當顧客轉到大型購物中心時，小商店可能倒閉。"},{"en":"If many businesses close down, the city centre may lose energy and jobs.","zh":"如果很多企業倒閉，市中心可能失去活力和職位。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the end of a business or service.","zh":"這個短語描述企業或服務結束營運。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be ideal for","meaning":"非常適合……","examples":[{"en":"The outskirts are ideal for buildings that need a lot of space.","zh":"郊區非常適合需要大量空間的建築。"},{"en":"To be ideal for something means to be very suitable for it.","zh":"非常適合某事，意思是對它來說很合適。"},{"en":"Large empty sites are ideal for conference centres and shopping malls.","zh":"大型空置用地非常適合會議中心和購物商場。"},{"en":"The outskirts may be ideal for big buildings because land is more available.","zh":"郊區可能非常適合大型建築，因為土地較充足。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong suitability.","zh":"這個短語描述高度適合。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"buildings that need a lot of space","meaning":"需要大量空間的建築","examples":[{"en":"Conference centres are buildings that need a lot of space.","zh":"會議中心是需要大量空間的建築。"},{"en":"Buildings that need a lot of space are large structures requiring wide land areas.","zh":"需要大量空間的建築，是指需要寬廣土地的大型結構。"},{"en":"Shopping centres, sports stadiums, and conference centres are buildings that need a lot of space.","zh":"購物中心、體育場和會議中心都是需要大量空間的建築。"},{"en":"These buildings are often placed outside city centres because land is limited downtown.","zh":"這些建築常設在市中心以外，因為市中心土地有限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large-scale buildings.","zh":"這個短語描述大型建築。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"conference centres","meaning":"會議中心","examples":[{"en":"Several large conference centres have opened on the outskirts.","zh":"幾個大型會議中心已在郊區開幕。"},{"en":"Conference centres are large buildings where meetings, exhibitions, and business events are held.","zh":"會議中心是舉行會議、展覽和商務活動的大型建築。"},{"en":"A conference centre needs halls, meeting rooms, parking, and transport access.","zh":"會議中心需要大廳、會議室、停車位和交通連接。"},{"en":"Building conference centres on the outskirts can bring visitors but may also affect the city centre.","zh":"在郊區興建會議中心可以帶來訪客，但也可能影響市中心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes places for large professional events.","zh":"這個短語描述舉行大型專業活動的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"facilities for","meaning":"……的設施","examples":[{"en":"Rosie wants more facilities for sports such as football.","zh":"Rosie 想要更多足球等運動的設施。"},{"en":"Facilities for something are buildings, spaces, or equipment provided for that activity.","zh":"某事的設施是為該活動提供的建築、空間或設備。"},{"en":"A city needs facilities for sports, health care, education, and transport.","zh":"城市需要運動、醫療、教育和交通的設施。"},{"en":"Better facilities for football can give young people safe places to exercise.","zh":"更好的足球設施可以給年輕人安全運動的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resources that support an activity.","zh":"這個短語描述支援某活動的資源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"where I live","meaning":"在我住的地方","examples":[{"en":"More sports facilities are not being built where Rosie lives.","zh":"Rosie 住的地方沒有興建更多運動設施。"},{"en":"“Where I live” means in the place or area where I have my home.","zh":"「Where I live」意思是在我居住的地方或地區。"},{"en":"Where I live, there are many shops but not enough sports fields.","zh":"在我住的地方，有很多商店，但運動場不足。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to connect a topic to their own local experience.","zh":"人們使用這個短語，把題目連繫到自己的本地經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal location.","zh":"這個短語描述個人所在地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in my area","meaning":"在我那區","examples":[{"en":"Colin says the situation is the same in his area.","zh":"Colin 說在他那區情況也是一樣。"},{"en":"In my area means in the district, neighbourhood, or place where I live.","zh":"在我那區意思是在我居住的地區、社區或地方。"},{"en":"In my area, new shopping centres have opened on the outskirts.","zh":"在我那區，郊區開了新的購物中心。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when describing local conditions.","zh":"人們描述本地情況時會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a general issue with a specific local place.","zh":"這個短語把一般問題與具體本地地方連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"developing disused industrial sites","meaning":"開發廢棄工業用地","examples":[{"en":"They could include developing disused industrial sites in the assignment.","zh":"他們可以在作業中包括開發廢棄工業用地。"},{"en":"Developing disused industrial sites means changing old unused factory or industrial land for new uses.","zh":"開發廢棄工業用地意思是把舊的、未使用的工廠或工業土地改作新用途。"},{"en":"A city may develop disused industrial sites into housing, parks, or offices.","zh":"城市可能把廢棄工業用地開發成住宅、公園或辦公室。"},{"en":"Developing disused industrial sites can reuse land instead of building on natural areas.","zh":"開發廢棄工業用地可以重用土地，而不是在自然地區興建。"},{"en":"This phrase describes urban redevelopment of old industrial land.","zh":"這個短語描述舊工業土地的城市再發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"disused industrial sites","meaning":"廢棄工業用地","examples":[{"en":"Disused industrial sites can be redeveloped.","zh":"廢棄工業用地可以被重新開發。"},{"en":"Disused industrial sites are old factory or industrial areas that are no longer being used.","zh":"廢棄工業用地是已不再使用的舊工廠或工業區。"},{"en":"Disused industrial sites may contain empty warehouses, old machinery, or polluted land.","zh":"廢棄工業用地可能有空置倉庫、舊機器或受污染土地。"},{"en":"Redeveloping disused industrial sites can improve cities if safety problems are solved.","zh":"如果安全問題得到解決，重新開發廢棄工業用地可以改善城市。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unused industrial land.","zh":"這個短語描述未使用的工業土地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"do harm to","meaning":"對……造成傷害","examples":[{"en":"Redeveloping these sites may not do harm to the natural environment.","zh":"重新開發這些用地可能不會對自然環境造成傷害。"},{"en":"To do harm to something means to damage or hurt it.","zh":"對某事造成傷害意思是損害或傷害它。"},{"en":"Building on green land can do harm to the natural environment.","zh":"在綠地上建設可能對自然環境造成傷害。"},{"en":"Reusing old industrial sites may do less harm than expanding into forests or farmland.","zh":"重用舊工業用地可能比擴展到森林或農地造成較少傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes causing damage.","zh":"這個短語描述造成損害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the natural environment","meaning":"自然環境","examples":[{"en":"Developing old industrial sites may protect the natural environment.","zh":"開發舊工業用地可能保護自然環境。"},{"en":"The natural environment includes land, air, water, plants, animals, and ecosystems.","zh":"自然環境包括土地、空氣、水、植物、動物和生態系統。"},{"en":"Protecting the natural environment is important when cities expand.","zh":"當城市擴張時，保護自然環境很重要。"},{"en":"Building on disused industrial land can reduce pressure on the natural environment.","zh":"在廢棄工業用地上建設可以減少對自然環境的壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes nature around human settlements.","zh":"這個短語描述人類聚居地周圍的自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"architecturally significant","meaning":"具有建築價值的","examples":[{"en":"Colin asks whether the buildings are architecturally significant.","zh":"Colin 問這些建築是否具有建築價值。"},{"en":"Architecturally significant means important or valuable because of design, style, age, or building history.","zh":"具有建築價值的意思是因設計、風格、年代或建築歷史而重要或有價值。"},{"en":"An old factory may be architecturally significant if it shows a rare industrial style.","zh":"如果一間舊工廠展示罕見工業風格，它可能具有建築價值。"},{"en":"Developers should be careful if disused buildings are architecturally significant.","zh":"如果廢棄建築具有建築價值，發展商應小心處理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes buildings with design or heritage value.","zh":"這個短語描述有設計或歷史價值的建築。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dangerous materials","meaning":"危險物料","examples":[{"en":"Old industrial sites often contain dangerous materials.","zh":"舊工業用地常含有危險物料。"},{"en":"Dangerous materials are substances that can harm people, animals, or the environment.","zh":"危險物料是可能傷害人、動物或環境的物質。"},{"en":"Chemicals, asbestos, and polluted soil can be dangerous materials on old industrial sites.","zh":"化學品、石棉和受污染泥土都可以是舊工業用地上的危險物料。"},{"en":"Dangerous materials must be removed before redevelopment begins.","zh":"重新開發開始前，必須清除危險物料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes safety risks found in some places.","zh":"這個短語描述某些地方存在的安全風險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"chemicals and things","meaning":"化學品之類的東西","examples":[{"en":"The sites may contain chemicals and things like that.","zh":"這些用地可能含有化學品之類的東西。"},{"en":"“Chemicals and things” informally means chemicals and other similar materials.","zh":"「Chemicals and things」以口語方式表示化學品和其他類似物料。"},{"en":"Old factories may leave behind chemicals and things that are unsafe.","zh":"舊工廠可能留下化學品之類的不安全東西。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they do not want to list every similar substance.","zh":"當人們不想列出每一種相似物質時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and general.","zh":"這個短語較口語和概括。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be properly cleared away","meaning":"被妥善清除","examples":[{"en":"The chemicals have not always been properly cleared away.","zh":"這些化學品並不總是被妥善清除。"},{"en":"To be properly cleared away means to be removed safely and completely.","zh":"被妥善清除意思是被安全而完整地移除。"},{"en":"Dangerous materials must be properly cleared away before people can live on the site.","zh":"危險物料必須被妥善清除，人們才可以在該地居住。"},{"en":"If chemicals are not properly cleared away, redevelopment may create health risks.","zh":"如果化學品沒有被妥善清除，重新開發可能造成健康風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes safe removal.","zh":"這個短語描述安全移除。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the whole site","meaning":"整個場地","examples":[{"en":"The whole site has to be made safe.","zh":"整個場地必須被處理至安全。"},{"en":"The whole site means every part of the area being discussed or developed.","zh":"整個場地意思是正在討論或開發的範圍內每一部分。"},{"en":"Before building homes, the whole site must be checked for dangerous materials.","zh":"興建住宅前，整個場地必須檢查是否有危險物料。"},{"en":"Cleaning only one corner is not enough if the whole site may be polluted.","zh":"如果整個場地可能受污染，只清理一角並不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the complete area.","zh":"這個短語強調完整範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be made safe","meaning":"被處理至安全","examples":[{"en":"The whole site has to be made safe before development.","zh":"整個場地在開發前必須被處理至安全。"},{"en":"To be made safe means to be changed or cleaned so it no longer causes danger.","zh":"被處理至安全意思是被改造或清理，以不再造成危險。"},{"en":"Old industrial land must be made safe before a school is built there.","zh":"舊工業土地在興建學校前必須被處理至安全。"},{"en":"Making a site safe may involve removing chemicals and checking the soil.","zh":"令場地安全可能涉及清除化學品和檢查泥土。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning a dangerous place into a safe one.","zh":"這個短語描述把危險地方變成安全地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"That can’t be cheap","meaning":"那肯定不便宜","examples":[{"en":"Colin says that making the site safe cannot be cheap.","zh":"Colin 說令場地安全肯定不便宜。"},{"en":"“That can’t be cheap” means that must be expensive.","zh":"「That can’t be cheap」意思是那一定很昂貴。"},{"en":"Removing dangerous chemicals from a whole site cannot be cheap.","zh":"從整個場地清除危險化學品肯定不便宜。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they realise a task probably costs a lot.","zh":"當人們意識到一項任務可能花很多錢時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a practical concern about money.","zh":"這個短語表達對金錢的實際憂慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be budgeted for","meaning":"被列入預算","examples":[{"en":"The cost is often not budgeted for.","zh":"這項成本通常沒有被列入預算。"},{"en":"To be budgeted for means to be included in a financial plan.","zh":"被列入預算意思是被包括在財政計劃中。"},{"en":"Cleaning dangerous materials should be budgeted for before redevelopment starts.","zh":"清理危險物料應在重新開發開始前被列入預算。"},{"en":"If safety costs are not budgeted for, a project may become much more expensive.","zh":"如果安全成本沒有被列入預算，項目可能變得昂貴得多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planning money for a future cost.","zh":"這個短語描述為未來成本作金錢規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"You’re right","meaning":"你說得對","examples":[{"en":"Rosie agrees and says, “You’re right.”","zh":"Rosie 同意並說：「你說得對。」"},{"en":"“You’re right” means I agree that what you said is correct.","zh":"「You’re right」意思是我同意你所說的是正確的。"},{"en":"You’re right; cleaning an industrial site can be very expensive.","zh":"你說得對；清理工業用地可以非常昂貴。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to accept another person’s point.","zh":"人們使用這個短語來接受另一個人的觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase shows agreement clearly and simply.","zh":"這個短語清楚簡單地表示同意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"read about","meaning":"讀過關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"Colin asks whether Rosie has read about Masdar City.","zh":"Colin 問 Rosie 是否讀過關於 Masdar City 的資料。"},{"en":"To read about something means to get information on it by reading.","zh":"讀過關於某事的資料，意思是透過閱讀獲得關於它的資訊。"},{"en":"Rosie read about Masdar City in an article on sustainable planning.","zh":"Rosie 在一篇關於可持續規劃的文章中讀過 Masdar City。"},{"en":"Reading about examples can help students choose evidence for an assignment.","zh":"閱讀關於例子的資料，可以幫助學生為作業選擇證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning through written material.","zh":"這個短語描述透過文字材料學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Masdar City","meaning":"Masdar City","examples":[{"en":"Masdar City is used as an example in their assignment.","zh":"Masdar City 被用作他們作業中的例子。"},{"en":"Masdar City is a planned city in Abu Dhabi designed with green and sustainable ideas.","zh":"Masdar City 是阿布扎比一個以綠色和可持續理念設計的規劃城市。"},{"en":"Students may discuss Masdar City when studying renewable energy and urban planning.","zh":"學生研究再生能源和城市規劃時可能會討論 Masdar City。"},{"en":"Masdar City is useful as an example because it tried to reduce waste and depend on clean energy.","zh":"Masdar City 作為例子很有用，因為它嘗試減少廢物並依賴清潔能源。"},{"en":"This name refers to a city project connected with sustainability.","zh":"這個名稱指一個與可持續性有關的城市項目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Abu Dhabi","meaning":"阿布扎比","examples":[{"en":"Masdar City is in Abu Dhabi.","zh":"Masdar City 位於阿布扎比。"},{"en":"Abu Dhabi is the capital of the United Arab Emirates.","zh":"阿布扎比是阿拉伯聯合酋長國的首都。"},{"en":"A sustainable city project in Abu Dhabi can show how hot-climate cities plan for the future.","zh":"阿布扎比的可持續城市項目可以展示炎熱氣候城市如何規劃未來。"},{"en":"Mentioning Abu Dhabi tells readers where Masdar City is located.","zh":"提到阿布扎比可以告訴讀者 Masdar City 位於哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the geographical setting of the example.","zh":"這個短語提供例子的地理背景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be designed to","meaning":"被設計成","examples":[{"en":"Masdar City was designed to be a green city.","zh":"Masdar City 被設計成一座綠色城市。"},{"en":"To be designed to do something means to be planned for that purpose.","zh":"被設計成做某事，意思是為該目的而規劃。"},{"en":"The transport system was designed to run underground.","zh":"交通系統被設計成在地下運行。"},{"en":"A city designed to save energy needs careful planning from the beginning.","zh":"被設計成節約能源的城市，從一開始就需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intention in planning or design.","zh":"這個短語描述規劃或設計中的意圖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a green city","meaning":"綠色城市","examples":[{"en":"Masdar City was designed to be a green city.","zh":"Masdar City 被設計成一座綠色城市。"},{"en":"A green city is a city planned to reduce environmental damage and use resources sustainably.","zh":"綠色城市是被規劃來減少環境傷害並可持續使用資源的城市。"},{"en":"A green city may use renewable energy, recycling systems, and pedestrian areas.","zh":"綠色城市可能使用再生能源、回收系統和行人專用區。"},{"en":"Building a green city can reduce pollution and waste if the plans are realistic.","zh":"如果計劃切實可行，建設綠色城市可以減少污染和廢物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an environmentally friendly urban model.","zh":"這個短語描述環保的城市模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"set out to","meaning":"以……為目標；著手去","examples":[{"en":"The city set out to depend on renewable energy.","zh":"這座城市以依賴再生能源為目標。"},{"en":"To set out to do something means to begin with the aim of doing it.","zh":"以做某事為目標，意思是從一開始就帶着該目的去做。"},{"en":"The planners set out to create a city with less waste and cleaner transport.","zh":"規劃者以創造更少廢物和更潔淨交通的城市為目標。"},{"en":"A project may set out to achieve big goals, even if it later faces difficulties.","zh":"一個項目可能一開始以實現宏大目標為方向，即使之後遇到困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an intended goal from the start.","zh":"這個短語描述一開始的預定目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"depend entirely on","meaning":"完全依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Masdar City set out to depend entirely on renewable energy.","zh":"Masdar City 以完全依賴再生能源為目標。"},{"en":"To depend entirely on something means to rely on it completely.","zh":"完全依賴某物，意思是完全依靠它。"},{"en":"A city that depends entirely on solar power needs reliable sunlight and storage systems.","zh":"完全依賴太陽能的城市需要可靠陽光和儲能系統。"},{"en":"Depending entirely on renewable energy is ambitious and difficult.","zh":"完全依賴再生能源很有雄心，也很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes total reliance.","zh":"這個短語描述完全依靠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"renewable energy","meaning":"再生能源","examples":[{"en":"Masdar City aimed to depend on renewable energy.","zh":"Masdar City 目標是依賴再生能源。"},{"en":"Renewable energy is energy from sources that naturally replace themselves, such as sunlight, wind, and water.","zh":"再生能源是來自會自然補充的來源的能源，例如陽光、風和水。"},{"en":"Solar power is a common form of renewable energy in sunny regions.","zh":"太陽能是在陽光充足地區常見的再生能源。"},{"en":"Using renewable energy can reduce reliance on fossil fuels.","zh":"使用再生能源可以減少對化石燃料的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cleaner energy sources that can be naturally renewed.","zh":"這個短語描述可以自然更新的較潔淨能源來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pedestrianised","meaning":"行人專用化的","examples":[{"en":"The city was designed to be totally pedestrianised.","zh":"這座城市被設計成完全行人專用化。"},{"en":"Pedestrianised means designed mainly or only for people walking, not for cars.","zh":"行人專用化的意思是主要或完全為行人而設，而不是為汽車而設。"},{"en":"A pedestrianised street can be safer and quieter for shoppers.","zh":"行人專用化的街道對購物人士來說可以更安全和安靜。"},{"en":"A totally pedestrianised city would need strong public transport and careful planning.","zh":"完全行人專用化的城市需要強大的公共交通和仔細規劃。"},{"en":"This word describes spaces made for pedestrians.","zh":"這個詞描述為行人而設的空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"transport underground","meaning":"地下交通系統","examples":[{"en":"The transport system was planned to run underground.","zh":"交通系統被規劃在地下運行。"},{"en":"Transport underground means transport routes or systems operate below street level.","zh":"地下交通系統意思是交通路線或系統在街道以下運行。"},{"en":"A city may put transport underground to keep surface streets free for pedestrians.","zh":"城市可能把交通放在地下，以讓地面街道留給行人。"},{"en":"Underground transport can save space but may be expensive to build.","zh":"地下交通系統可以節省空間，但建造成本可能很高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a transport system below the ground.","zh":"這個短語描述地底下的交通系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"big plans for","meaning":"關於……的大型計劃","examples":[{"en":"The city had big plans for recycling.","zh":"這座城市有關於回收的大型計劃。"},{"en":"Big plans for something are ambitious ideas or programmes for developing it.","zh":"關於某事的大型計劃，是指發展它的有雄心想法或方案。"},{"en":"Masdar City had big plans for renewable energy and waste reduction.","zh":"Masdar City 有關於再生能源和減少廢物的大型計劃。"},{"en":"Big plans can attract attention, but they must be realistic to succeed.","zh":"大型計劃可以吸引注意，但必須切實可行才會成功。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ambitious planning.","zh":"這個短語描述有雄心的規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"recycling","meaning":"回收","examples":[{"en":"Masdar City had plans for recycling.","zh":"Masdar City 有回收計劃。"},{"en":"Recycling is the process of collecting and reusing materials instead of throwing them away.","zh":"回收是收集並重新使用材料，而不是把它們丟棄的過程。"},{"en":"Recycling paper, plastic, metal, and glass can reduce waste.","zh":"回收紙、塑膠、金屬和玻璃可以減少廢物。"},{"en":"A green city needs good recycling systems to manage rubbish sustainably.","zh":"綠色城市需要良好的回收系統，以可持續方式管理垃圾。"},{"en":"This word describes turning waste into usable material again.","zh":"這個詞描述把廢物重新變成可用材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reduce waste","meaning":"減少廢物","examples":[{"en":"The plans aimed to reduce waste.","zh":"這些計劃旨在減少廢物。"},{"en":"To reduce waste means to produce less rubbish or use materials more efficiently.","zh":"減少廢物意思是產生更少垃圾或更有效使用材料。"},{"en":"Daily recycling collections can help reduce waste in a city.","zh":"每日回收收集可以幫助城市減少廢物。"},{"en":"Reducing waste saves resources and lowers pressure on landfills.","zh":"減少廢物可以節省資源並減低堆填區壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an environmental goal.","zh":"這個短語描述環保目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"to the lowest possible level","meaning":"到最低可能水平","examples":[{"en":"The city aimed to reduce waste to the lowest possible level.","zh":"這座城市目標是把廢物減少到最低可能水平。"},{"en":"To the lowest possible level means as low as it can realistically become.","zh":"到最低可能水平意思是降低到實際上可以達到的最低程度。"},{"en":"The project tried to cut energy use to the lowest possible level.","zh":"這個項目嘗試把能源使用減至最低可能水平。"},{"en":"Reducing waste to the lowest possible level requires planning, recycling, and public cooperation.","zh":"把廢物減少到最低可能水平需要規劃、回收和公眾合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the strongest realistic reduction.","zh":"這個短語描述最強而可行的減少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stick to talking about","meaning":"專注談論……","examples":[{"en":"Rosie suggests sticking to talking about power sources.","zh":"Rosie 建議專注談論能源來源。"},{"en":"To stick to talking about something means to keep the discussion focused on that topic.","zh":"專注談論某事，意思是讓討論保持聚焦於該題目。"},{"en":"They decided to stick to talking about renewable energy instead of covering every green feature.","zh":"他們決定專注談論再生能源，而不是涵蓋每個綠色特色。"},{"en":"Sticking to one focus can make an assignment clearer.","zh":"專注於一個焦點可以令作業更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes staying on one topic.","zh":"這個短語描述停留在一個題目上。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"power sources","meaning":"能源來源","examples":[{"en":"The students decide to focus on power sources.","zh":"學生決定聚焦於能源來源。"},{"en":"Power sources are the places or methods from which energy is obtained.","zh":"能源來源是取得能源的地方或方法。"},{"en":"Solar panels, wind turbines, coal, and gas are different power sources.","zh":"太陽能板、風力渦輪、煤和天然氣都是不同能源來源。"},{"en":"Studying power sources helps explain whether a city can be sustainable.","zh":"研究能源來源有助解釋城市是否能夠可持續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes energy origins.","zh":"這個短語描述能源的來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ecotown","meaning":"生態小鎮","examples":[{"en":"Greenhill Abbots is described as an ecotown in England.","zh":"Greenhill Abbots 被描述為英格蘭的一個生態小鎮。"},{"en":"An ecotown is a town planned to be environmentally friendly and sustainable.","zh":"生態小鎮是被規劃為環保和可持續的小鎮。"},{"en":"An ecotown may use renewable energy, green transport, recycling, and efficient housing.","zh":"生態小鎮可能使用再生能源、綠色交通、回收和節能房屋。"},{"en":"Building an ecotown can test whether sustainable planning works in real life.","zh":"建設生態小鎮可以測試可持續規劃在現實中是否有效。"},{"en":"This word describes a town designed around environmental principles.","zh":"這個詞描述圍繞環保原則設計的小鎮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"set out to conform to","meaning":"旨在符合……","examples":[{"en":"The ecotown set out to conform to the usual principles.","zh":"這個生態小鎮旨在符合一般原則。"},{"en":"To set out to conform to something means to begin with the aim of following certain rules or standards.","zh":"旨在符合某事，意思是一開始就以遵循某些規則或標準為目標。"},{"en":"The project set out to conform to principles of sustainability and low waste.","zh":"這個項目旨在符合可持續性和低廢物原則。"},{"en":"A town that sets out to conform to green planning must design transport, energy, and housing carefully.","zh":"旨在符合綠色規劃的小鎮，必須仔細設計交通、能源和住屋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes aiming to follow a recognised standard.","zh":"這個短語描述以遵循公認標準為目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the usual principles","meaning":"一般原則","examples":[{"en":"The project aimed to follow the usual principles of sustainable planning.","zh":"這個項目旨在遵循可持續規劃的一般原則。"},{"en":"The usual principles are the commonly accepted rules, ideas, or standards in a field.","zh":"一般原則是某領域中普遍接受的規則、想法或標準。"},{"en":"The usual principles of sustainable planning include energy efficiency, recycling, and reduced car use.","zh":"可持續規劃的一般原則包括能源效益、回收和減少汽車使用。"},{"en":"Following the usual principles can make an ecotown more credible.","zh":"遵循一般原則可以令生態小鎮更可信。"},{"en":"This phrase describes standard guiding ideas.","zh":"這個短語描述標準指導理念。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sustainability","meaning":"可持續性；永續性","examples":[{"en":"The ecotown followed principles such as sustainability.","zh":"這個生態小鎮遵循可持續性等原則。"},{"en":"Sustainability means using resources in a way that can continue without damaging the future.","zh":"可持續性意思是以不損害未來的方式使用資源。"},{"en":"Sustainability in cities may involve renewable energy, public transport, and waste reduction.","zh":"城市中的可持續性可能涉及再生能源、公共交通和減少廢物。"},{"en":"A project with poor sustainability may harm the environment over time.","zh":"可持續性差的項目隨時間可能傷害環境。"},{"en":"This word describes long-term environmental and social responsibility.","zh":"這個詞描述長期環境和社會責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"and so on","meaning":"等等","examples":[{"en":"The project followed principles such as sustainability and so on.","zh":"這個項目遵循可持續性等等原則。"},{"en":"“And so on” means and other similar things that do not need to be listed fully.","zh":"「And so on」意思是以及其他類似而不需要完整列出的事物。"},{"en":"The ecotown considered sustainability, recycling, renewable energy and so on.","zh":"這個生態小鎮考慮可持續性、回收、再生能源等等。"},{"en":"Students use “and so on” when the remaining examples are easy to guess.","zh":"當其餘例子容易推測時，學生會使用「and so on」。"},{"en":"This phrase keeps a list open and general.","zh":"這個短語令清單保持開放和概括。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be against","meaning":"反對……","examples":[{"en":"A lot of people were against the project at first.","zh":"起初很多人反對這個項目。"},{"en":"To be against something means to oppose it or disagree with it.","zh":"反對某事意思是不同意或反對它。"},{"en":"Some residents were against the ecotown because they thought it was unrealistic.","zh":"有些居民反對生態小鎮，因為他們認為它不切實際。"},{"en":"People may be against a development if they fear traffic, cost, or environmental harm.","zh":"如果人們擔心交通、成本或環境傷害，可能會反對一項發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes opposition.","zh":"這個短語描述反對意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at first","meaning":"起初","examples":[{"en":"Many people were against the ecotown at first.","zh":"起初很多人反對這個生態小鎮。"},{"en":"At first means in the beginning or at the early stage.","zh":"起初意思是在開始時或早期階段。"},{"en":"At first, the plan seemed unrealistic, but later people became more interested.","zh":"起初，這個計劃看起來不切實際，但後來人們變得更感興趣。"},{"en":"Opinions can change after people learn more details.","zh":"人們了解更多細節後，意見可以改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the early part of a situation.","zh":"這個短語描述情況的早期部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"unrealistic","meaning":"不切實際的","examples":[{"en":"Opponents said the plans were unrealistic.","zh":"反對者說這些計劃不切實際。"},{"en":"Unrealistic means not practical or not likely to happen successfully.","zh":"不切實際的意思是不實用或不太可能成功發生。"},{"en":"A city depending entirely on renewable energy may seem unrealistic without enough technology.","zh":"如果沒有足夠科技，完全依賴再生能源的城市可能看起來不切實際。"},{"en":"Plans can be inspiring but unrealistic if they ignore cost and time.","zh":"如果計劃忽略成本和時間，它可以很鼓舞人心但不切實際。"},{"en":"This word describes ideas that may not work in real life.","zh":"這個詞描述在現實中可能行不通的想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"how far they’ve got with it","meaning":"進展到甚麼程度","examples":[{"en":"Colin is not sure how far they have got with the ecotown.","zh":"Colin 不確定他們的生態小鎮進展到甚麼程度。"},{"en":"“How far they’ve got with it” means how much progress has been made on the project.","zh":"「How far they’ve got with it」意思是這個項目已取得多少進展。"},{"en":"We should check how far they’ve got with building the ecotown.","zh":"我們應該查一下他們建設生態小鎮進展到甚麼程度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a plan has started but may not be complete.","zh":"當計劃已開始但可能尚未完成時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It asks about progress, not physical distance.","zh":"它詢問的是進度，而不是實際距離。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"I’ll check","meaning":"我會去查一下","examples":[{"en":"Colin says he will check the progress of the project.","zh":"Colin 說他會去查一下這個項目的進度。"},{"en":"“I’ll check” means I will look for information or confirm something.","zh":"「I’ll check」意思是我會尋找資料或確認某事。"},{"en":"I’ll check whether the ecotown has actually been built.","zh":"我會去查一下這個生態小鎮是否實際上已建成。"},{"en":"Students say “I’ll check” when they need to verify facts before writing.","zh":"學生在寫作前需要核實事實時，會說「I’ll check」。"},{"en":"This phrase shows willingness to confirm information.","zh":"這個短語表示願意確認資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Rosie and Colin’s opinion about","meaning":"Rosie 和 Colin 對……的看法","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about Rosie and Colin’s opinion about different aspects of human geography.","zh":"這條問題問 Rosie 和 Colin 對人文地理不同面向的看法。"},{"en":"Rosie and Colin’s opinion about something means what they think or believe about it.","zh":"Rosie 和 Colin 對某事的看法，意思是他們對它的想法或信念。"},{"en":"The task asks for Rosie and Colin’s opinion about population, culture, poverty, and urbanisation.","zh":"這項任務問 Rosie 和 Colin 對人口、文化、貧窮和城市化的看法。"},{"en":"Understanding their opinion helps candidates match answers correctly.","zh":"理解他們的看法有助考生正確配對答案。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the students’ views.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於學生的觀點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the following aspects of","meaning":"以下……的面向","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match opinions with the following aspects of human geography.","zh":"考生把意見與以下人文地理面向配對。"},{"en":"The following aspects of something are the parts or categories listed next.","zh":"以下某事的面向，是指接下來列出的部分或類別。"},{"en":"The following aspects of human geography include health, poverty, culture, and urbanisation.","zh":"以下人文地理面向包括健康、貧窮、文化和城市化。"},{"en":"This phrase prepares readers to look at a list.","zh":"這個短語讓讀者準備查看清單。"},{"en":"It is common in exam instructions.","zh":"它常見於考試指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"choose five answers from the box","meaning":"從方格中選出五個答案","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose five answers from the box.","zh":"考生從方格中選出五個答案。"},{"en":"To choose five answers from the box means to select five options from a given list.","zh":"從方格中選出五個答案，意思是從給定清單中選擇五個選項。"},{"en":"Students must read the statements carefully before choosing five answers from the box.","zh":"學生在從方格中選出五個答案前，必須仔細閱讀陳述。"},{"en":"Choosing too many answers from the box would not follow the instruction.","zh":"從方格中選太多答案就不符合指示。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an exam selection task.","zh":"這個短語描述考試中的選擇任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"write the correct letter next to","meaning":"在……旁邊寫上正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the correct letter next to each question.","zh":"考生在每條問題旁邊寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"To write the correct letter next to something means to put the chosen option letter beside it.","zh":"在某處旁邊寫上正確字母，意思是把所選選項的字母寫在它旁邊。"},{"en":"Write the correct letter next to the topic “poverty.”","zh":"在「貧窮」這個題目旁邊寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"In matching tasks, writing the correct letter next to each question records the answer clearly.","zh":"在配對題中，在每條問題旁邊寫上正確字母可以清楚記錄答案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how to mark answers in an exam.","zh":"這個短語描述考試中標示答案的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the information given about","meaning":"關於……所提供的資料","examples":[{"en":"The information given about culture was too vague.","zh":"關於文化所提供的資料太籠統。"},{"en":"The information given about something means the details or explanation provided on that topic.","zh":"關於某事所提供的資料，意思是就該題目給出的細節或解釋。"},{"en":"The information given about poverty may not be reliable.","zh":"關於貧窮所提供的資料可能不可靠。"},{"en":"If the information given about a topic is unclear, students may avoid using it.","zh":"如果關於某題目所提供的資料不清楚，學生可能會避免使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to provided content or evidence.","zh":"這個短語指所提供的內容或證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"too vague","meaning":"太籠統；太含糊","examples":[{"en":"The information in the lecture was too vague.","zh":"課堂中的資料太籠統。"},{"en":"Too vague means too unclear, general, or lacking detail.","zh":"太籠統或太含糊意思是太不清楚、太概括或缺乏細節。"},{"en":"The culture lecture was too vague because it gave no useful examples.","zh":"文化課太籠統，因為沒有給出有用例子。"},{"en":"If assignment guidance is too vague, students may not know what to write.","zh":"如果作業指引太含糊，學生可能不知道要寫甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises unclear information.","zh":"這個短語批評資料不清楚。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"may not be relevant to","meaning":"可能與……無關","examples":[{"en":"The topic may not be relevant to their course.","zh":"這個題目可能與他們的課程無關。"},{"en":"May not be relevant to something means may not be connected, useful, or appropriate for it.","zh":"可能與某事無關，意思是可能與它沒有連繫、沒有用或不合適。"},{"en":"Economies may not be relevant to the course if they were removed from the syllabus.","zh":"如果經濟已從課程大綱中刪去，它可能與課程無關。"},{"en":"Students should avoid topics that may not be relevant to the assignment requirements.","zh":"學生應避開可能與作業要求無關的題目。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a topic may not fit.","zh":"這個短語提醒題目可能不合適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"involve only a small number of","meaning":"只涉及少量……","examples":[{"en":"The task may involve only a small number of statistics.","zh":"這項任務可能只涉及少量統計資料。"},{"en":"To involve only a small number of something means to include just a few of them.","zh":"只涉及少量某物，意思是只包括很少數量。"},{"en":"A culture topic may involve only a small number of statistics and more discussion.","zh":"文化題目可能只涉及少量統計資料，而有更多討論。"},{"en":"If a topic involves only a small number of statistics, it may be easier for students who dislike data.","zh":"如果題目只涉及少量統計資料，對不喜歡數據的學生可能較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述數量有限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"easy to find facts about","meaning":"容易找到關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"Population is easy to find facts about.","zh":"人口很容易找到相關資料。"},{"en":"Easy to find facts about means information on the topic is simple to locate.","zh":"容易找到關於某事的資料，意思是該題目的資訊很容易找到。"},{"en":"Population density is easy to find facts about because governments publish census data.","zh":"人口密度很容易找到資料，因為政府會發布人口普查數據。"},{"en":"A topic that is easy to find facts about can save research time.","zh":"容易找到資料的題目可以節省研究時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes convenient access to information.","zh":"這個短語描述取得資訊很方便。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"may not be reliable","meaning":"可能不可靠","examples":[{"en":"The facts about poverty may not be reliable.","zh":"關於貧窮的資料可能不可靠。"},{"en":"May not be reliable means may not be trustworthy, accurate, or dependable.","zh":"可能不可靠意思是可能不可信、不準確或不能依靠。"},{"en":"Poverty figures may not be reliable if they are politically manipulated.","zh":"如果貧窮數據被政治操控，它可能不可靠。"},{"en":"Students should check sources carefully when data may not be reliable.","zh":"當數據可能不可靠時，學生應仔細檢查來源。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against trusting information too easily.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要太輕易相信資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"useful research has been done on","meaning":"已就……進行有用研究","examples":[{"en":"Useful research has been done on this topic.","zh":"已就這個題目進行有用研究。"},{"en":"“Useful research has been done on” means scholars have already studied the topic in a helpful way.","zh":"「Useful research has been done on」意思是學者已經以有幫助的方式研究該題目。"},{"en":"Useful research has been done on the link between cholera and water supplies.","zh":"已就霍亂與供水系統之間的關聯進行有用研究。"},{"en":"A topic with useful research already available can support a stronger assignment.","zh":"已有有用研究的題目可以支持更有力的作業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes existing academic evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述已有的學術證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生為每條問題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the option letter that matches the answer.","zh":"選出正確字母意思是選擇與答案相配的選項字母。"},{"en":"Candidates must choose the correct letter after listening to Rosie and Colin.","zh":"考生聽完 Rosie 和 Colin 後，必須選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choosing the correct letter requires understanding the speaker’s opinion.","zh":"選出正確字母需要理解說話者的意見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common exam answer method.","zh":"這個短語描述常見考試答題方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the main problem","meaning":"主要問題","examples":[{"en":"Rosie explains the main problem in her own city.","zh":"Rosie 解釋她自己城市中的主要問題。"},{"en":"The main problem is the most important or serious issue.","zh":"主要問題是最重要或最嚴重的議題。"},{"en":"In Rosie’s city, unemployment is the main problem.","zh":"在 Rosie 的城市，失業是主要問題。"},{"en":"Identifying the main problem helps writers focus their analysis.","zh":"找出主要問題有助作者聚焦分析。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the central issue.","zh":"這個短語描述核心議題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in her own city","meaning":"在她自己的城市","examples":[{"en":"Rosie talks about the situation in her own city.","zh":"Rosie 談論她自己城市中的情況。"},{"en":"In her own city means in the city where she lives or comes from.","zh":"在她自己的城市，意思是在她居住或來自的城市。"},{"en":"In her own city, unemployment is worse than homelessness.","zh":"在她自己的城市，失業比無家可歸更嚴重。"},{"en":"Personal examples from her own city can make the assignment more concrete.","zh":"來自她自己城市的個人例子可以令作業更具體。"},{"en":"This phrase connects discussion with personal local experience.","zh":"這個短語把討論與個人本地經驗連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"recent additions to","meaning":"最近新增到……的設施","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about recent additions to the outskirts of their cities.","zh":"問題問最近新增到他們城市郊區的設施。"},{"en":"Recent additions to a place are new things that have recently been built or added there.","zh":"最近新增到某地的設施，是指最近在那裏興建或加入的新事物。"},{"en":"Recent additions to the outskirts include shopping centres and conference centres.","zh":"最近新增到郊區的設施包括購物中心和會議中心。"},{"en":"Discussing recent additions helps show how cities are changing.","zh":"討論最近新增的設施有助顯示城市如何改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes new developments in a place.","zh":"這個短語描述某地的新發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be happy about","meaning":"對……感到高興","examples":[{"en":"Both students are happy about some recent additions.","zh":"兩位學生對一些最近新增的設施感到高興。"},{"en":"To be happy about something means to feel pleased with it.","zh":"對某事感到高興，意思是對它感到滿意或開心。"},{"en":"Colin is happy about the new conference centres on the outskirts.","zh":"Colin 對郊區的新會議中心感到高興。"},{"en":"People may be happy about new facilities if they create jobs or services.","zh":"如果新設施創造職位或服務，人們可能會感到高興。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses positive feeling toward a change.","zh":"這個短語表達對變化的正面感受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"retail centres","meaning":"零售中心；購物中心","examples":[{"en":"Retail centres have opened outside the cities.","zh":"城市外開設了零售中心。"},{"en":"Retail centres are large areas or buildings with many shops and services.","zh":"零售中心是有很多商店和服務的大型區域或建築。"},{"en":"Retail centres on the outskirts can attract shoppers away from the city centre.","zh":"郊區零售中心可以把購物者從市中心吸引走。"},{"en":"New retail centres may create jobs but also affect small local shops.","zh":"新零售中心可能創造職位，但也影響本地小商店。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shopping-focused developments.","zh":"這個短語描述以購物為主的發展項目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"may have unexpected costs","meaning":"可能有意想不到的成本","examples":[{"en":"Developing disused industrial sites may have unexpected costs.","zh":"開發廢棄工業用地可能有意想不到的成本。"},{"en":"May have unexpected costs means may require extra money that was not planned.","zh":"可能有意想不到的成本，意思是可能需要原本沒有計劃的額外金錢。"},{"en":"Cleaning dangerous materials may have unexpected costs for developers.","zh":"清理危險物料可能為發展商帶來意想不到的成本。"},{"en":"A project may seem cheap at first but have unexpected costs later.","zh":"一個項目一開始可能看似便宜，但後來有意想不到的成本。"},{"en":"This phrase warns about hidden financial problems.","zh":"這個短語提醒隱藏財務問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"damage the urban environment","meaning":"破壞城市環境","examples":[{"en":"Poor development can damage the urban environment.","zh":"差劣發展可以破壞城市環境。"},{"en":"To damage the urban environment means to harm the quality, safety, beauty, or function of a city area.","zh":"破壞城市環境意思是傷害城市地區的質素、安全、美觀或功能。"},{"en":"Bad planning can damage the urban environment by increasing traffic and pollution.","zh":"糟糕規劃可以透過增加交通和污染破壞城市環境。"},{"en":"Redevelopment should improve, not damage, the urban environment.","zh":"重新開發應該改善，而不是破壞城市環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harm to city surroundings.","zh":"這個短語描述對城市周遭環境的傷害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"valuable historical buildings","meaning":"有價值的歷史建築","examples":[{"en":"Some projects may destroy valuable historical buildings.","zh":"有些項目可能摧毀有價值的歷史建築。"},{"en":"Valuable historical buildings are old buildings important for history, culture, or architecture.","zh":"有價值的歷史建築是對歷史、文化或建築有重要性的舊建築。"},{"en":"A former factory may be one of the city’s valuable historical buildings.","zh":"一間舊工廠可能是城市中有價值的歷史建築之一。"},{"en":"Redevelopment should protect valuable historical buildings when possible.","zh":"重新開發應盡可能保護有價值的歷史建築。"},{"en":"This phrase describes buildings worth preserving.","zh":"這個短語描述值得保存的建築。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as an example of","meaning":"作為……的例子","examples":[{"en":"Masdar City will be mentioned as an example of sustainable planning.","zh":"Masdar City 將被提及作為可持續規劃的例子。"},{"en":"As an example of something means used to show or illustrate that idea.","zh":"作為某事的例子，意思是用來展示或說明該想法。"},{"en":"Masdar City can be used as an example of a planned green city.","zh":"Masdar City 可以作為規劃綠色城市的例子。"},{"en":"Examples help readers understand abstract ideas like sustainability.","zh":"例子可以幫助讀者理解可持續性等抽象想法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a concrete case.","zh":"這個短語引出具體個案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"an attempt to achieve","meaning":"嘗試實現……","examples":[{"en":"The city is an attempt to achieve sustainable energy use.","zh":"這座城市是嘗試實現可持續能源使用的例子。"},{"en":"An attempt to achieve something is an effort to reach a goal, even if success is not certain.","zh":"嘗試實現某事，是指努力達成某目標，即使成功並不確定。"},{"en":"Masdar City is an attempt to achieve greener urban living.","zh":"Masdar City 是嘗試實現更綠色城市生活的例子。"},{"en":"An attempt to achieve sustainability may face cost, technology, and planning problems.","zh":"嘗試實現可持續性可能面對成本、科技和規劃問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious effort toward a goal.","zh":"這個短語描述朝目標作出的認真努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"daily collections for waste recycling","meaning":"每日回收廢物收集","examples":[{"en":"Daily collections for waste recycling can reduce waste.","zh":"每日回收廢物收集可以減少廢物。"},{"en":"Daily collections for waste recycling are regular daily services that collect recyclable materials.","zh":"每日回收廢物收集是定期每天收集可回收材料的服務。"},{"en":"A city with daily collections for waste recycling can make recycling easier for residents.","zh":"有每日回收廢物收集的城市可以令居民更容易回收。"},{"en":"Daily recycling collections reduce waste only if people separate materials properly.","zh":"每日回收收集只有在人們妥善分類材料時才能減少廢物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical waste management service.","zh":"這個短語描述實用的廢物管理服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sustainable energy use","meaning":"可持續能源使用","examples":[{"en":"Masdar City is an example of sustainable energy use.","zh":"Masdar City 是可持續能源使用的例子。"},{"en":"Sustainable energy use means using energy in a way that can continue without damaging the environment or future resources.","zh":"可持續能源使用意思是以不傷害環境或未來資源的方式使用能源。"},{"en":"Solar power can support sustainable energy use in sunny cities.","zh":"太陽能可以支持陽光充足城市的可持續能源使用。"},{"en":"Sustainable energy use reduces reliance on fuels that create pollution.","zh":"可持續能源使用減少對會造成污染的燃料的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes responsible long-term energy planning.","zh":"這個短語描述負責任的長期能源規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"free transport for everyone","meaning":"人人免費交通","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to free transport for everyone.","zh":"這個選項指人人免費交通。"},{"en":"Free transport for everyone means public transport that all people can use without paying fares.","zh":"人人免費交通意思是所有人都可以不用付車費使用公共交通。"},{"en":"Free transport for everyone could reduce car use if the service is reliable.","zh":"如果服務可靠，人人免費交通可以減少汽車使用。"},{"en":"A city may consider free transport for everyone to improve equality and reduce traffic.","zh":"城市可能考慮人人免費交通，以改善平等和減少交通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a transport policy with no user payment.","zh":"這個短語描述不需使用者付款的交通政策。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be uncertain about","meaning":"對……不確定","examples":[{"en":"Colin is uncertain about the progress of Greenhill Abbots.","zh":"Colin 對 Greenhill Abbots 的進度不確定。"},{"en":"To be uncertain about something means to be unsure or not know clearly.","zh":"對某事不確定，意思是不肯定或不清楚知道。"},{"en":"Colin is uncertain about how much of the ecotown has actually been built.","zh":"Colin 對這個生態小鎮實際上已建成多少不確定。"},{"en":"Students should check facts when they are uncertain about a case study.","zh":"當學生對個案研究不確定時，應查核事實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lack of certainty.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"its objectives","meaning":"它的目標","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Colin is uncertain about its objectives.","zh":"問題問 Colin 是否對它的目標不確定。"},{"en":"Its objectives are the aims or goals of the project being discussed.","zh":"它的目標是正在討論的項目的目的或想達成的成果。"},{"en":"The ecotown’s objectives include sustainability and green planning.","zh":"這個生態小鎮的目標包括可持續性和綠色規劃。"},{"en":"If its objectives are unclear, it is harder to judge whether the project has succeeded.","zh":"如果它的目標不清楚，就較難判斷項目是否成功。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what a project is trying to achieve.","zh":"這個短語指一個項目試圖達成的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"opposition to","meaning":"對……的反對","examples":[{"en":"There was opposition to the ecotown at first.","zh":"起初有人反對這個生態小鎮。"},{"en":"Opposition to something means disagreement with it or resistance against it.","zh":"對某事的反對，意思是不同意它或抵抗它。"},{"en":"There may be opposition to an ecotown if residents think the plans are unrealistic.","zh":"如果居民認為計劃不切實際，可能會反對生態小鎮。"},{"en":"Opposition to a project can delay development and force planners to explain their ideas better.","zh":"對項目的反對可以延誤發展，並迫使規劃者更好地解釋想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised or general resistance.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織或一般性的抵抗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"actually been built","meaning":"實際上已建成","examples":[{"en":"Colin is unsure how much of the ecotown has actually been built.","zh":"Colin 不確定這個生態小鎮實際上已建成多少。"},{"en":"Actually been built means really completed in physical form, not just planned.","zh":"實際上已建成意思是真的以實體形式完成，而不只是被計劃。"},{"en":"The plans sound impressive, but students need to know what has actually been built.","zh":"這些計劃聽起來令人印象深刻，但學生需要知道實際上已建成甚麼。"},{"en":"A project may have strong objectives even if only a small part has actually been built.","zh":"即使只有小部分實際上已建成，一個項目仍可能有很強目標。"},{"en":"This phrase separates real construction from ideas or promises.","zh":"這個短語把真實建設與想法或承諾分開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14}],"ielts/listening/Practice 2/task-4":[{"front":"food science lecture","meaning":"食品科學講座","examples":[{"en":"You will hear part of a food science lecture on fashions in food.","zh":"你會聽到一段關於食品潮流的食品科學講座。"},{"en":"A food science lecture is an academic talk about food, nutrition, production, or food-related technology.","zh":"食品科學講座是關於食物、營養、生產或食品相關科技的學術演講。"},{"en":"The food science lecture explained why some foods become fashionable.","zh":"那場食品科學講座解釋了為何某些食物會變得流行。"},{"en":"A lecture on food science may connect chemistry, health, marketing, and consumer behaviour.","zh":"食品科學講座可能把化學、健康、市場推廣和消費者行為連繫起來。"},{"en":"Students should listen for key examples during a food science lecture.","zh":"學生聽食品科學講座時應留意重點例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fashions in food","meaning":"食品潮流","examples":[{"en":"The lecture is about fashions in food.","zh":"這場講座是關於食品潮流的。"},{"en":"Fashions in food are changing preferences for certain foods, ingredients, or eating habits.","zh":"食品潮流是人們對某些食物、食材或飲食習慣不斷改變的偏好。"},{"en":"Avocado toast became one of the fashions in food in many cafés.","zh":"牛油果多士在許多咖啡店成為食品潮流之一。"},{"en":"Fashions in food can be shaped by social media, health claims, and celebrity chefs.","zh":"食品潮流可以受社交媒體、健康聲稱和名廚影響。"},{"en":"A food fashion may be popular for a short time or become part of everyday eating.","zh":"一種食品潮流可能只流行一段短時間，也可能成為日常飲食的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"trends in food","meaning":"食品潮流","examples":[{"en":"There are trends in food, much as there are trends in clothing.","zh":"食品有潮流，就像服裝有潮流一樣。"},{"en":"Trends in food are patterns in what people choose to eat or buy at a particular time.","zh":"食品潮流是某一時期人們選擇吃甚麼或購買甚麼的模式。"},{"en":"Plant-based milk is one of the recent trends in food.","zh":"植物奶是近期食品潮流之一。"},{"en":"Trends in food can create new opportunities for farmers and companies.","zh":"食品潮流可以為農民和公司創造新機會。"},{"en":"Some food trends are driven by health, while others are driven by fashion or convenience.","zh":"有些食品潮流由健康因素推動，另一些則由時尚或方便程度推動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"much as","meaning":"就像……一樣","examples":[{"en":"There are trends in food, much as there are trends in clothing.","zh":"食品有潮流，就像服裝有潮流一樣。"},{"en":"“Much as” means in a similar way to something else.","zh":"「就像……一樣」表示與另一事物以相似方式發生。"},{"en":"Food companies follow consumer taste, much as fashion brands follow clothing trends.","zh":"食品公司跟隨消費者口味，就像時裝品牌跟隨服裝潮流一樣。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to compare two similar situations.","zh":"這個說法用來比較兩個相似情況。"},{"en":"“Much as” helps readers understand a new idea by connecting it to a familiar one.","zh":"「就像……一樣」透過連接熟悉事物，幫助讀者理解新想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"trends in clothing","meaning":"服裝潮流","examples":[{"en":"There are trends in food, much as there are trends in clothing.","zh":"食品有潮流，就像服裝有潮流一樣。"},{"en":"Trends in clothing are popular styles, colours, or designs at a particular time.","zh":"服裝潮流是某一時期流行的款式、顏色或設計。"},{"en":"Oversized jackets became a trend in clothing among young people.","zh":"寬鬆外套在年輕人中成為服裝潮流。"},{"en":"Trends in clothing can change quickly because of celebrities and social media.","zh":"服裝潮流可以因名人和社交媒體而迅速改變。"},{"en":"Comparing food trends with clothing trends shows how taste can be socially influenced.","zh":"把食品潮流與服裝潮流比較，可以顯示品味如何受社會影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"interest in food fashions","meaning":"對食品潮流的興趣","examples":[{"en":"Interest in food fashions has risen rapidly since the birth of the smartphone.","zh":"自智能手機誕生以來，人們對食品潮流的興趣迅速上升。"},{"en":"Interest in food fashions means people’s curiosity about fashionable foods and eating trends.","zh":"對食品潮流的興趣，是指人們對流行食物和飲食趨勢的好奇。"},{"en":"Social media increased interest in food fashions by making meals easy to share visually.","zh":"社交媒體令餐點容易以圖像分享，增加了人們對食品潮流的興趣。"},{"en":"Restaurants may change menus when public interest in food fashions grows.","zh":"當大眾對食品潮流的興趣增加，餐廳可能會改變餐牌。"},{"en":"Interest in food fashions can influence what shops choose to sell.","zh":"對食品潮流的興趣可以影響商店選擇售賣甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"has risen rapidly","meaning":"迅速上升","examples":[{"en":"Interest in food fashions has risen rapidly since the birth of the smartphone.","zh":"自智能手機誕生以來，對食品潮流的興趣迅速上升。"},{"en":"If something has risen rapidly, it has increased quickly over a period of time.","zh":"某事迅速上升，是指它在一段時間內快速增加。"},{"en":"Demand for oat milk has risen rapidly in some countries.","zh":"燕麥奶的需求在一些國家迅速上升。"},{"en":"Interest can rise rapidly when a product is promoted by influencers.","zh":"當產品由網紅推廣，興趣可能迅速上升。"},{"en":"Rapid growth may create both business opportunities and supply problems.","zh":"快速增長可能帶來商機，也可能造成供應問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the birth of the smartphone","meaning":"智能手機的誕生","examples":[{"en":"Interest in food fashions has risen rapidly since the birth of the smartphone.","zh":"自智能手機誕生以來，人們對食品潮流的興趣迅速上升。"},{"en":"The birth of the smartphone refers to the time when smartphones first appeared and became widely used.","zh":"智能手機的誕生，是指智能手機首次出現並逐漸廣泛使用的時期。"},{"en":"The birth of the smartphone changed how people shared photos and opinions.","zh":"智能手機的誕生改變了人們分享相片和意見的方式。"},{"en":"Food trends spread faster after smartphones made instant sharing easy.","zh":"智能手機令即時分享變得容易後，食品潮流傳播得更快。"},{"en":"This phrase treats a technology’s beginning as if it were a living thing being born.","zh":"這個說法把科技的開始比喻成生命的誕生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"taking photos of their food","meaning":"拍攝食物照片","examples":[{"en":"People first began taking photos of their food and sharing them with friends.","zh":"人們最初開始拍攝食物照片，並與朋友分享。"},{"en":"Taking photos of food means using a camera or phone to record meals visually.","zh":"拍攝食物照片是指用相機或手機記錄餐點的畫面。"},{"en":"Diners often take photos of colourful desserts before eating them.","zh":"食客常在吃色彩鮮艷的甜品前拍攝食物照片。"},{"en":"Taking photos of food can help spread trends online.","zh":"拍攝食物照片可以幫助潮流在網上傳播。"},{"en":"Some restaurants design dishes that look attractive in photographs.","zh":"有些餐廳會設計在相片中看起來吸引的菜式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"instantly sharing","meaning":"即時分享","examples":[{"en":"People began instantly sharing photos of their food with their friends.","zh":"人們開始即時與朋友分享食物照片。"},{"en":"Instantly sharing means sending or posting something immediately.","zh":"即時分享是指立即發送或發佈某物。"},{"en":"Social media allows people to share food photos instantly.","zh":"社交媒體讓人們即時分享食物照片。"},{"en":"Instantly sharing images can make a new food trend spread quickly.","zh":"即時分享影像可以令新的食品潮流迅速傳播。"},{"en":"Immediate sharing increases visibility, but it may also encourage people to focus on appearance.","zh":"即時分享增加曝光度，但也可能令人過分重視外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the food industry","meaning":"食品業","examples":[{"en":"The food industry in the UK is obsessed with finding the next big food trend.","zh":"英國食品業熱衷於尋找下一個重大食品潮流。"},{"en":"The food industry includes companies and workers involved in producing, selling, and promoting food.","zh":"食品業包括生產、銷售和推廣食物的公司和從業人員。"},{"en":"The food industry watches consumer behaviour closely.","zh":"食品業會密切觀察消費者行為。"},{"en":"Changes in taste, health concerns, and technology can affect the food industry.","zh":"口味變化、健康關注和科技都可以影響食品業。"},{"en":"A competitive food industry often tries to predict the next popular product.","zh":"競爭激烈的食品業常嘗試預測下一個受歡迎產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in particular","meaning":"尤其是","examples":[{"en":"The food industry in the UK, in particular, is obsessed with the next big food trend.","zh":"尤其是英國食品業，十分熱衷於下一個重大食品潮流。"},{"en":"“In particular” singles out one person, place, or thing from a wider group.","zh":"「尤其是」從較大群體中特別指出一個人、地方或事物。"},{"en":"Supermarkets, in particular, are interested in social media trends.","zh":"尤其是超級市場，對社交媒體潮流很感興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase helps the speaker focus attention on a specific example.","zh":"這個說法幫助講者把注意力集中於特定例子。"},{"en":"It is useful when a general statement applies especially strongly to one case.","zh":"當一般陳述對某個個案特別適用時，這個說法很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be obsessed with","meaning":"對……着迷；熱衷於……","examples":[{"en":"The UK food industry is obsessed with finding and exploiting the next big food trend.","zh":"英國食品業熱衷於尋找並利用下一個重大食品潮流。"},{"en":"To be obsessed with something means to think about it constantly or care about it too much.","zh":"對某事着迷，是指不斷想着它或過分重視它。"},{"en":"Some companies are obsessed with viral food products.","zh":"有些公司對爆紅食品產品非常着迷。"},{"en":"Being obsessed with trends can make businesses innovative but also short-sighted.","zh":"熱衷於潮流可以令企業創新，但也可能變得短視。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests an excessive level of interest.","zh":"這個說法通常暗示興趣程度過高。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"finding and exploiting","meaning":"尋找並利用","examples":[{"en":"The industry is obsessed with finding and exploiting the next big food trend.","zh":"食品業熱衷於尋找並利用下一個重大食品潮流。"},{"en":"Finding and exploiting a trend means discovering it and using it for advantage or profit.","zh":"尋找並利用一種潮流，是指發現它並用它取得優勢或利潤。"},{"en":"Companies try to profit by finding and exploiting changing tastes.","zh":"公司嘗試透過尋找並利用口味變化來獲利。"},{"en":"Exploiting a trend can increase sales quickly, but it may also create ethical concerns.","zh":"利用潮流可以迅速提高銷量，但也可能帶來倫理關注。"},{"en":"The phrase can sound critical if it suggests using popularity mainly for money.","zh":"如果暗示主要為了金錢而利用人氣，這個說法可能帶批評意味。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the next big food trend","meaning":"下一個重大食品潮流","examples":[{"en":"Companies want to exploit the next big food trend.","zh":"公司希望利用下一個重大食品潮流。"},{"en":"The next big food trend is a food or ingredient expected to become highly popular soon.","zh":"下一個重大食品潮流是預期很快會大受歡迎的食品或食材。"},{"en":"Marketeers search for the next big food trend by watching social media.","zh":"市場推廣人員透過觀察社交媒體尋找下一個重大食品潮流。"},{"en":"A product can become the next big food trend if it is fashionable, available, and well promoted.","zh":"如果產品時尚、容易買到並得到良好推廣，便可能成為下一個重大食品潮流。"},{"en":"Not every predicted food trend becomes successful.","zh":"並非每個被預測的食品潮流都會成功。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"marketeers","meaning":"市場推廣人員","examples":[{"en":"Marketeers aim to create a huge demand for a new food item.","zh":"市場推廣人員旨在為新食品創造巨大需求。"},{"en":"Marketeers are people who promote products and try to influence what consumers buy.","zh":"市場推廣人員是推廣產品並嘗試影響消費者購買選擇的人。"},{"en":"Marketeers use stories, images, and influencers to promote food products.","zh":"市場推廣人員使用故事、影像和網紅推廣食品產品。"},{"en":"Good marketeers understand both customer emotions and market data.","zh":"優秀市場推廣人員了解顧客情感和市場數據。"},{"en":"Their work can make an unknown product seem exciting and desirable.","zh":"他們的工作可以令不知名產品顯得令人興奮和吸引。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"aim to","meaning":"目標是；旨在","examples":[{"en":"Marketeers aim to create a huge demand for a food item.","zh":"市場推廣人員旨在為一種食品創造巨大需求。"},{"en":"To aim to do something means to have that action as a goal.","zh":"旨在做某事，是指把該行動作為目標。"},{"en":"The campaign aims to introduce oat milk to more consumers.","zh":"這項宣傳活動旨在向更多消費者介紹燕麥奶。"},{"en":"A company may aim to increase sales through social media.","zh":"公司可能旨在透過社交媒體提高銷量。"},{"en":"A clear aim helps a team choose suitable methods.","zh":"清楚目標有助團隊選擇合適方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"create a huge demand for","meaning":"為……創造巨大需求","examples":[{"en":"Marketeers aim to create a huge demand for a previously unknown food item.","zh":"市場推廣人員旨在為一種以前不為人知的食品創造巨大需求。"},{"en":"To create a huge demand for something means to make many people want to buy it.","zh":"為某物創造巨大需求，是指令很多人想購買它。"},{"en":"Influencer posts can create huge demand for a new snack.","zh":"網紅貼文可以為新小食創造巨大需求。"},{"en":"A huge demand can increase profits but also put pressure on supply.","zh":"巨大需求可以增加利潤，但也會對供應造成壓力。"},{"en":"Demand created by marketing may disappear if the product disappoints consumers.","zh":"由市場推廣創造的需求，如果產品令消費者失望，可能會消失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"food item","meaning":"食品項目；食品","examples":[{"en":"Marketeers try to create demand for a food item that was previously unknown.","zh":"市場推廣人員嘗試為一種以前不為人知的食品創造需求。"},{"en":"A food item is a particular product, ingredient, dish, or type of food.","zh":"食品項目是某種特定產品、食材、菜式或食物種類。"},{"en":"Quinoa became a fashionable food item in many health-food shops.","zh":"藜麥在許多健康食品店成為時尚食品。"},{"en":"A food item may become popular because of taste, health claims, or online attention.","zh":"一種食品可能因味道、健康聲稱或網上關注而流行。"},{"en":"Companies often choose one food item to promote as special or new.","zh":"公司常選擇一種食品作為特別或新穎產品來推廣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"previously unknown","meaning":"之前不為人知的","examples":[{"en":"The product was previously unknown to most consumers.","zh":"該產品之前對大多數消費者來說不為人知。"},{"en":"Previously unknown means not known before a particular time.","zh":"之前不為人知，是指在某一時間之前未被認識。"},{"en":"The fruit was previously unknown outside its local region.","zh":"這種水果以前在本地地區以外不為人知。"},{"en":"Social media can make a previously unknown product famous quickly.","zh":"社交媒體可以令之前不為人知的產品迅速成名。"},{"en":"A previously unknown food may need explanation before consumers try it.","zh":"之前不為人知的食品可能需要解釋，消費者才會嘗試。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"effective ways of promoting","meaning":"推廣……的有效方法","examples":[{"en":"One of the most effective ways of promoting a new food product is to use influencers.","zh":"推廣新食品產品最有效的方法之一，是使用網紅。"},{"en":"Effective ways of promoting something are methods that successfully increase interest or sales.","zh":"推廣某物的有效方法，是成功增加興趣或銷量的方式。"},{"en":"Free tastings are effective ways of promoting some food products.","zh":"免費試食是推廣某些食品產品的有效方法。"},{"en":"An effective promotion method depends on the audience and the product.","zh":"有效的推廣方法取決於受眾和產品。"},{"en":"Social media can be effective when the product looks attractive and is easy to share.","zh":"當產品外觀吸引且容易分享，社交媒體可以很有效。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a new food product","meaning":"新食品產品","examples":[{"en":"Influencers can help promote a new food product.","zh":"網紅可以幫助推廣新食品產品。"},{"en":"A new food product is a recently introduced food item or drink.","zh":"新食品產品是最近推出的食品或飲品。"},{"en":"The company launched a new food product made from oats.","zh":"公司推出了一款由燕麥製成的新食品產品。"},{"en":"A new food product needs visibility before customers decide to try it.","zh":"新食品產品需要曝光，顧客才會決定嘗試。"},{"en":"Successful new food products often match current tastes or values.","zh":"成功的新食品產品通常符合當前口味或價值觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"social media influencers","meaning":"社交媒體網紅","examples":[{"en":"Companies use social media influencers as brand ambassadors.","zh":"公司使用社交媒體網紅作為品牌大使。"},{"en":"Social media influencers are people with online audiences who can affect followers’ opinions or purchases.","zh":"社交媒體網紅是擁有網上受眾、能影響追隨者意見或購買行為的人。"},{"en":"Food brands pay social media influencers to show their products.","zh":"食品品牌付錢給社交媒體網紅展示產品。"},{"en":"Influencers can make a new food seem fashionable through photos and videos.","zh":"網紅可以透過相片和影片令新食品顯得時尚。"},{"en":"Their influence depends on trust, audience size, and content style.","zh":"他們的影響力取決於信任、受眾規模和內容風格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"brand ambassadors","meaning":"品牌大使","examples":[{"en":"Influencers often act as brand ambassadors for food companies.","zh":"網紅常擔任食品公司的品牌大使。"},{"en":"Brand ambassadors are people who represent and promote a brand publicly.","zh":"品牌大使是公開代表和推廣品牌的人。"},{"en":"The chef became a brand ambassador for a new oat milk company.","zh":"那名廚師成為一間新燕麥奶公司的品牌大使。"},{"en":"Brand ambassadors can increase trust if audiences believe they genuinely like the product.","zh":"如果觀眾相信品牌大使真心喜歡產品，品牌大使可以增加信任。"},{"en":"A poor choice of ambassador can damage a brand’s reputation.","zh":"選錯品牌大使可能損害品牌聲譽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in return for","meaning":"作為……的回報","examples":[{"en":"In return for free samples, many influencers will post content about a product.","zh":"作為免費樣本的回報，許多網紅會發佈關於產品的內容。"},{"en":"“In return for” means as an exchange for something received or given.","zh":"「作為……的回報」表示用某物交換收到或給出的東西。"},{"en":"The blogger wrote a review in return for a free meal.","zh":"那名博客寫了一篇評論，作為免費餐點的回報。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two sides are exchanging benefits.","zh":"這個說法顯示雙方正在交換利益。"},{"en":"Audiences should know when content is posted in return for gifts or payment.","zh":"觀眾應知道內容是否因禮物或報酬而發佈。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"free samples","meaning":"免費樣本；免費試食","examples":[{"en":"Influencers may receive free samples from food companies.","zh":"網紅可能從食品公司收到免費樣本。"},{"en":"Free samples are small amounts of a product given without payment.","zh":"免費樣本是不需付款便獲得的小量產品。"},{"en":"The supermarket offered free samples of a new plant-based drink.","zh":"超級市場提供一款新植物飲品的免費試食。"},{"en":"Free samples allow consumers to try a product before buying it.","zh":"免費樣本讓消費者在購買前先試用產品。"},{"en":"Free samples can create interest, but they do not guarantee long-term sales.","zh":"免費樣本可以引起興趣，但不保證長期銷量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"post content about","meaning":"發佈關於……的內容","examples":[{"en":"Influencers will post content about a product on social media.","zh":"網紅會在社交媒體上發佈關於產品的內容。"},{"en":"To post content about something means to publish text, photos, or videos about it online.","zh":"發佈關於某事的內容，是指在網上發布有關它的文字、相片或影片。"},{"en":"The influencer posted content about the new vegan dessert.","zh":"那名網紅發佈了關於新純素甜品的內容。"},{"en":"Posted content can quickly reach thousands of followers.","zh":"發佈的內容可以迅速接觸成千上萬名追隨者。"},{"en":"Promotional content should be honest and clearly labelled when paid.","zh":"推廣內容應誠實，而且若屬付費內容應清楚標示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hundreds of thousands of followers","meaning":"數十萬名追隨者","examples":[{"en":"Some influencers have hundreds of thousands of followers.","zh":"有些網紅擁有數十萬名追隨者。"},{"en":"Hundreds of thousands of followers means a very large online audience numbering in the hundreds of thousands.","zh":"數十萬名追隨者是指數量達數十萬的大型網上受眾。"},{"en":"An influencer with hundreds of thousands of followers can spread a food trend quickly.","zh":"擁有數十萬名追隨者的網紅可以迅速傳播食品潮流。"},{"en":"Large follower numbers can attract brands seeking publicity.","zh":"大量追隨者可以吸引尋求曝光的品牌。"},{"en":"Follower numbers matter, but engagement and trust also matter.","zh":"追隨者數量很重要，但互動和信任也很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"command large fees","meaning":"收取高額費用","examples":[{"en":"Influencers with many followers can command large fees for their services.","zh":"擁有大量追隨者的網紅可以為其服務收取高額費用。"},{"en":"To command large fees means to be able to charge high prices because of value or demand.","zh":"收取高額費用，是指因價值或需求而能夠收取高價。"},{"en":"Famous chefs can command large fees for promotional events.","zh":"名廚可以為推廣活動收取高額費用。"},{"en":"People with rare skills or large audiences often command higher fees.","zh":"擁有稀有技能或大量受眾的人通常能收取較高費用。"},{"en":"A large fee may be justified only if the promotion produces real results.","zh":"只有當推廣帶來真正成果，高額費用才可能合理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for their services","meaning":"為其服務","examples":[{"en":"Some influencers command large fees for their services.","zh":"有些網紅為其服務收取高額費用。"},{"en":"“For their services” means in exchange for the work or help they provide.","zh":"「為其服務」表示作為他們所提供工作或幫助的交換。"},{"en":"The marketing agency charged a fee for its services.","zh":"那間市場推廣公司為其服務收取費用。"},{"en":"Influencers may be paid for their services in money, products, or travel.","zh":"網紅可能以金錢、產品或旅程作為服務回報。"},{"en":"Clear agreements should state exactly what services are being paid for.","zh":"清楚協議應說明究竟為哪些服務付款。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"vegan produce","meaning":"純素食品","examples":[{"en":"Companies which sell vegan produce increased sales quickly in this way.","zh":"售賣純素食品的公司以這種方式迅速提高銷量。"},{"en":"Vegan produce is food made without animal products such as meat, milk, or eggs.","zh":"純素食品是不含肉類、牛奶或雞蛋等動物產品的食品。"},{"en":"The shop sells vegan produce including plant-based burgers and dairy-free desserts.","zh":"那間商店售賣純素漢堡和無奶甜品等純素食品。"},{"en":"Vegan produce became more popular as consumers considered health and animal welfare.","zh":"隨着消費者考慮健康和動物福利，純素食品變得更受歡迎。"},{"en":"Clear labelling helps shoppers identify vegan produce easily.","zh":"清楚標籤可以幫助購物者容易辨認純素食品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pioneers in","meaning":"……方面的先驅","examples":[{"en":"Vegan food companies were pioneers in increasing sales through influencers.","zh":"純素食品公司是透過網紅提高銷量方面的先驅。"},{"en":"Pioneers in a field are among the first people or groups to use a new method or idea.","zh":"某領域的先驅，是最早使用新方法或新想法的人或團體之一。"},{"en":"Some brands were pioneers in using social media for food marketing.","zh":"有些品牌是使用社交媒體進行食品推廣方面的先驅。"},{"en":"Pioneers take risks because the method has not yet been widely tested.","zh":"先驅需要承擔風險，因為方法尚未被廣泛測試。"},{"en":"Successful pioneers can influence how the whole industry behaves.","zh":"成功的先驅可以影響整個行業的做法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"increase sales","meaning":"提高銷量","examples":[{"en":"Vegan food companies were able to increase sales really quickly.","zh":"純素食品公司能夠非常迅速地提高銷量。"},{"en":"To increase sales means to sell more products or services than before.","zh":"提高銷量是指比以前售出更多產品或服務。"},{"en":"The campaign helped increase sales of oat milk.","zh":"該宣傳活動幫助提高燕麥奶銷量。"},{"en":"Companies use advertising, discounts, and influencers to increase sales.","zh":"公司使用廣告、折扣和網紅提高銷量。"},{"en":"Sales can increase quickly during a trend but may fall when interest fades.","zh":"銷量可以在潮流期間迅速上升，但當興趣減退時也可能下降。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in this way","meaning":"以這種方式","examples":[{"en":"Vegan food companies increased sales really quickly in this way.","zh":"純素食品公司以這種方式非常迅速地提高銷量。"},{"en":"“In this way” means by using the method just described.","zh":"「以這種方式」表示使用剛才描述的方法。"},{"en":"The brand worked with influencers and increased attention in this way.","zh":"品牌與網紅合作，並以這種方式增加關注。"},{"en":"The phrase links a result to a previous method.","zh":"這個說法把結果與前面的方法連接起來。"},{"en":"It helps avoid repeating the whole explanation.","zh":"它有助避免重複整個解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"readily available","meaning":"容易買到的","examples":[{"en":"A food item has to be readily available to become really popular.","zh":"一種食品要變得真正流行，必須容易買到。"},{"en":"If something is readily available, people can get it easily and quickly.","zh":"容易買到是指人們可以輕易和快速取得。"},{"en":"Oat milk became popular partly because it was readily available in cafés.","zh":"燕麥奶變得流行，部分原因是它在咖啡店容易買到。"},{"en":"A trend cannot grow far if the product is difficult to buy.","zh":"如果產品難以購買，潮流便難以大幅發展。"},{"en":"Availability in supermarkets can turn online interest into real purchases.","zh":"在超級市場有售可以把網上興趣轉化為實際購買。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have a role to play in","meaning":"在……方面有角色；有作用","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets have a role to play in creating a new food trend.","zh":"超級市場在創造新的食品潮流方面有作用。"},{"en":"To have a role to play in something means to contribute to it or influence it.","zh":"在某事方面有作用，是指對它作出貢獻或產生影響。"},{"en":"Schools have a role to play in encouraging healthy eating.","zh":"學校在鼓勵健康飲食方面有角色。"},{"en":"Supermarkets influence trends by deciding what to stock and promote.","zh":"超級市場透過決定入貨和推廣甚麼來影響潮流。"},{"en":"A role may be important even if it is not the only cause.","zh":"即使不是唯一成因，一個角色仍可能很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"creating a new food trend","meaning":"創造新的食品潮流","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets have a role to play in creating a new food trend.","zh":"超級市場在創造新的食品潮流方面有作用。"},{"en":"Creating a new food trend means helping a food become fashionable or widely desired.","zh":"創造新的食品潮流，是指幫助某種食品變得時尚或廣受渴求。"},{"en":"Supermarkets can create a new food trend by placing products in visible areas.","zh":"超級市場可以透過把產品放在顯眼位置來創造新的食品潮流。"},{"en":"A trend is easier to create when the product is attractive and easy to buy.","zh":"當產品吸引且容易購買，潮流較容易被創造。"},{"en":"Creating a trend may involve marketing, supply, pricing, and timing.","zh":"創造潮流可能涉及市場推廣、供應、價格和時機。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dedicated teams","meaning":"專門團隊","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets have dedicated teams following new food trends.","zh":"超級市場有專門團隊跟進新的食品潮流。"},{"en":"Dedicated teams are groups of workers assigned specifically to a particular task.","zh":"專門團隊是被特別安排負責某項任務的一組員工。"},{"en":"The supermarket created a dedicated team to study social media food trends.","zh":"超級市場成立專門團隊研究社交媒體食品潮流。"},{"en":"Dedicated teams can respond faster because they focus on one area.","zh":"專門團隊因集中於一個範疇，可以更快回應。"},{"en":"A dedicated team needs clear goals and reliable information.","zh":"專門團隊需要清楚目標和可靠資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"closely following","meaning":"密切關注","examples":[{"en":"Supermarket teams are closely following which ingredients are trending.","zh":"超級市場團隊正密切關注哪些食材正在流行。"},{"en":"Closely following something means watching or monitoring it carefully.","zh":"密切關注某事，是指仔細觀察或監察它。"},{"en":"Food companies are closely following changes in consumer taste.","zh":"食品公司正密切關注消費者口味的變化。"},{"en":"Closely following social media helps supermarkets react to demand quickly.","zh":"密切關注社交媒體可以幫助超級市場迅速回應需求。"},{"en":"Monitoring trends closely can be useful, but companies should avoid copying every temporary fashion.","zh":"密切監察潮流很有用，但公司應避免盲目跟隨每個短暫潮流。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"new products or ingredients","meaning":"新產品或食材","examples":[{"en":"Teams follow which new products or ingredients are trending on social media.","zh":"團隊跟進哪些新產品或食材正在社交媒體上流行。"},{"en":"New products or ingredients are recently introduced foods, drinks, or components used in cooking.","zh":"新產品或食材是最近推出的食品、飲品或烹調成分。"},{"en":"Supermarkets track new products or ingredients such as plant-based drinks and unusual grains.","zh":"超級市場追蹤植物飲品和不尋常穀物等新產品或食材。"},{"en":"New ingredients may become popular if chefs and influencers use them.","zh":"如果名廚和網紅使用新食材，它們可能變得流行。"},{"en":"Not every new product is practical for ordinary shoppers.","zh":"並非每款新產品都適合普通購物者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"trending on social media","meaning":"在社交媒體上流行","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets track ingredients that are trending on social media.","zh":"超級市場追蹤在社交媒體上流行的食材。"},{"en":"If something is trending on social media, many people are discussing, posting, or sharing it online.","zh":"某事在社交媒體上流行，是指很多人在網上討論、發佈或分享它。"},{"en":"A colourful dessert can start trending on social media overnight.","zh":"一款色彩鮮艷的甜品可以一夜之間在社交媒體上流行。"},{"en":"Foods that trend online often attract attention from shops and restaurants.","zh":"網上流行的食品通常會吸引商店和餐廳注意。"},{"en":"Trending online does not always mean a product will sell well long term.","zh":"在網上流行並不一定表示產品長期銷量良好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"particularly interested in","meaning":"特別關注；特別感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets are particularly interested in what well-known chefs put on their menus.","zh":"超級市場特別關注知名廚師把甚麼放入餐牌。"},{"en":"To be particularly interested in something means to give it special attention.","zh":"特別關注某事，是指對它給予特別注意。"},{"en":"Food companies are particularly interested in ingredients that chefs use repeatedly.","zh":"食品公司特別關注廚師反覆使用的食材。"},{"en":"Being interested in chefs’ menus helps supermarkets predict future demand.","zh":"關注名廚餐牌可以幫助超級市場預測未來需求。"},{"en":"The word “particularly” highlights one focus among many possible sources of information.","zh":"「特別」突出了眾多資訊來源中的一個焦點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"well-known chefs","meaning":"知名廚師；名廚","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets follow what well-known chefs are putting on their menus.","zh":"超級市場會跟進知名廚師把甚麼放入餐牌。"},{"en":"Well-known chefs are cooks who are widely recognised by the public or food industry.","zh":"知名廚師是被公眾或食品業廣泛認識的廚師。"},{"en":"A well-known chef can make an unusual ingredient popular.","zh":"一名名廚可以令不尋常食材變得流行。"},{"en":"Restaurants led by well-known chefs often influence food trends.","zh":"由知名廚師主理的餐廳通常會影響食品潮流。"},{"en":"Fame can increase a chef’s power to shape consumer taste.","zh":"名氣可以增加廚師塑造消費者口味的能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"put something on the menu","meaning":"把……放入餐牌","examples":[{"en":"Chefs put fashionable ingredients on their menus.","zh":"廚師把時尚食材放入餐牌。"},{"en":"To put something on the menu means to include it as a dish or ingredient offered by a restaurant.","zh":"把某物放入餐牌，是指把它列為餐廳供應的菜式或食材。"},{"en":"The chef put oat milk drinks on the menu.","zh":"廚師把燕麥奶飲品放入餐牌。"},{"en":"When famous restaurants put an ingredient on the menu, supermarkets may notice.","zh":"當著名餐廳把某種食材放入餐牌，超級市場可能會注意到。"},{"en":"Menu choices can influence what customers think is fashionable.","zh":"餐牌選擇可以影響顧客認為甚麼是時尚。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a few examples of","meaning":"幾個……例子","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer looks at a few examples of successful marketing campaigns.","zh":"講者會看幾個成功市場推廣活動的例子。"},{"en":"“A few examples of” means a small number of cases used to illustrate a point.","zh":"「幾個……例子」是用來說明一點的少數個案。"},{"en":"The report gives a few examples of food trends that spread through social media.","zh":"報告列舉了幾個透過社交媒體傳播的食品潮流例子。"},{"en":"Examples make an abstract idea easier to understand.","zh":"例子可以令抽象想法更容易理解。"},{"en":"A few examples can support an argument, but they may not show the whole picture.","zh":"幾個例子可以支持論點，但未必顯示全貌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"marketing campaigns","meaning":"市場推廣活動","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer discusses marketing campaigns that launched new food trends.","zh":"講者討論成功推出新食品潮流的市場推廣活動。"},{"en":"Marketing campaigns are planned activities designed to promote a product, service, or idea.","zh":"市場推廣活動是為推廣產品、服務或想法而策劃的活動。"},{"en":"The avocado campaign used journalists and advertisements.","zh":"牛油果推廣活動使用了記者和廣告。"},{"en":"A successful marketing campaign can change how consumers view a food.","zh":"成功的市場推廣活動可以改變消費者對食品的看法。"},{"en":"Campaigns may use media, influencers, samples, or celebrity support.","zh":"推廣活動可能使用媒體、網紅、試食樣本或名人支持。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"successful in launching","meaning":"成功推出；成功帶動","examples":[{"en":"Some marketing campaigns were successful in launching new food trends.","zh":"有些市場推廣活動成功帶動新的食品潮流。"},{"en":"To be successful in launching something means to introduce it effectively and gain attention or demand.","zh":"成功推出某物，是指有效地把它介紹給市場並獲得關注或需求。"},{"en":"The company was successful in launching its new oat drink.","zh":"公司成功推出新的燕麥飲品。"},{"en":"A launch is successful when consumers notice, try, and continue buying the product.","zh":"當消費者注意、嘗試並繼續購買產品，推出便算成功。"},{"en":"Being successful in launching a trend requires timing, supply, and strong messaging.","zh":"成功帶動潮流需要時機、供應和有力訊息。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a fashion trend","meaning":"潮流；時尚趨勢","examples":[{"en":"The campaign helped launch a new fashion trend in food.","zh":"該推廣活動幫助帶動一個新的食品時尚趨勢。"},{"en":"A fashion trend is a style or preference that becomes popular for a period of time.","zh":"潮流是某段時間內變得受歡迎的風格或偏好。"},{"en":"Brightly coloured drinks became a fashion trend online.","zh":"色彩鮮艷的飲品在網上成為潮流。"},{"en":"In food, a fashion trend can affect restaurants, supermarkets, and home cooking.","zh":"在食品方面，潮流可以影響餐廳、超級市場和家居烹調。"},{"en":"Some fashion trends fade quickly, while others change everyday habits.","zh":"有些潮流很快消退，另一些則改變日常習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the avocado","meaning":"牛油果","examples":[{"en":"The first example from the 1990s is the avocado.","zh":"來自二十世紀九十年代的第一個例子是牛油果。"},{"en":"The avocado is a green fruit with soft flesh and a large seed.","zh":"牛油果是一種綠色水果，果肉柔軟並有一顆大核。"},{"en":"Avocados are often used in salads, sandwiches, and guacamole.","zh":"牛油果常用於沙律、三文治和牛油果醬。"},{"en":"Marketing helped the avocado become associated with health and fashionable eating.","zh":"市場推廣幫助牛油果與健康和時尚飲食聯繫起來。"},{"en":"A once-unfamiliar food can become common through successful promotion.","zh":"一種曾經陌生的食品可以透過成功推廣變得普遍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"PR company","meaning":"公關公司","examples":[{"en":"A British PR company was hired to raise the avocado’s profile.","zh":"一間英國公關公司受聘提高牛油果的知名度。"},{"en":"A PR company manages public relations and helps shape how people view a product or organisation.","zh":"公關公司管理公共關係，並幫助塑造人們對產品或組織的看法。"},{"en":"The PR company arranged interviews and media stories about the new fruit.","zh":"公關公司安排有關這種新水果的訪問和媒體報道。"},{"en":"PR companies use communication strategies to build interest and trust.","zh":"公關公司使用溝通策略建立興趣和信任。"},{"en":"Good public relations can make a product seem familiar and desirable.","zh":"良好公關可以令產品顯得熟悉和吸引。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be hired to","meaning":"受聘去……","examples":[{"en":"A British PR company was hired to raise the avocado’s profile.","zh":"一間英國公關公司受聘去提高牛油果的知名度。"},{"en":"To be hired to do something means to be employed or paid to perform a task.","zh":"受聘去做某事，是指被僱用或付費去完成某項任務。"},{"en":"The agency was hired to promote a new drink.","zh":"那間機構受聘去推廣一款新飲品。"},{"en":"Companies hire specialists when they need skills they do not have internally.","zh":"當公司需要內部沒有的技能時，便會聘請專家。"},{"en":"Being hired for a campaign usually involves clear goals and deadlines.","zh":"受聘進行推廣活動通常涉及清楚目標和期限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"raise its profile","meaning":"提高其知名度","examples":[{"en":"The PR company was hired to raise the avocado’s profile.","zh":"公關公司受聘提高牛油果的知名度。"},{"en":"To raise something’s profile means to increase public awareness or attention to it.","zh":"提高某物的知名度，是指增加公眾對它的認識或關注。"},{"en":"The campaign raised the profile of oat milk among young consumers.","zh":"該活動提高了燕麥奶在年輕消費者中的知名度。"},{"en":"Raising a product’s profile can make shops more willing to stock it.","zh":"提高產品知名度可以令商店更願意入貨。"},{"en":"Publicity, articles, and celebrity use can all raise a food’s profile.","zh":"宣傳、文章和名人使用都可以提高食品知名度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"stimulate demand","meaning":"刺激需求","examples":[{"en":"The campaign was designed to stimulate demand for avocados.","zh":"該推廣活動旨在刺激對牛油果的需求。"},{"en":"To stimulate demand means to encourage more people to want or buy something.","zh":"刺激需求是指鼓勵更多人想要或購買某物。"},{"en":"Discounts can stimulate demand for a new product.","zh":"折扣可以刺激新產品需求。"},{"en":"Advertising health benefits may stimulate demand among health-conscious consumers.","zh":"宣傳健康益處可能刺激注重健康消費者的需求。"},{"en":"Demand stimulated too quickly can create supply or price problems.","zh":"需求被過快刺激起來，可能造成供應或價格問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"paid for","meaning":"出資；支付……費用","examples":[{"en":"The company paid for journalists to travel to South Africa.","zh":"公司出資讓記者前往南非。"},{"en":"To pay for something means to provide the money needed for it.","zh":"支付某事費用，是指提供完成該事所需的金錢。"},{"en":"The PR company paid for the journalists’ flights and hotel rooms.","zh":"公關公司支付記者的機票和酒店費用。"},{"en":"Paying for travel can help journalists see a product’s origin directly.","zh":"支付旅費可以幫助記者親眼了解產品來源。"},{"en":"Sponsored trips should be transparent so readers understand the arrangement.","zh":"受贊助旅程應保持透明，讓讀者理解安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a group of journalists","meaning":"一班記者","examples":[{"en":"A group of journalists travelled to South Africa to meet avocado farmers.","zh":"一班記者前往南非會見牛油果農民。"},{"en":"A group of journalists is several reporters or writers working on news or media stories.","zh":"一班記者是幾名從事新聞或媒體報道的記者或撰稿人。"},{"en":"A group of journalists visited farms to learn about avocado production.","zh":"一班記者參觀農場，了解牛油果生產。"},{"en":"Journalists can influence public opinion through the articles they write.","zh":"記者可以透過所寫文章影響公眾看法。"},{"en":"Inviting journalists can be part of a wider public relations strategy.","zh":"邀請記者可以是更廣泛公關策略的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"travel out to","meaning":"前往……","examples":[{"en":"Journalists travelled out to South Africa to meet avocado farmers.","zh":"記者前往南非會見牛油果農民。"},{"en":"To travel out to a place means to make a trip there, often from another country or region.","zh":"前往某地是指到該地旅行，通常從另一國家或地區出發。"},{"en":"The writers travelled out to Norway to learn about skrei.","zh":"撰稿人前往挪威了解skrei魚。"},{"en":"Travelling out to the source can make a story more vivid.","zh":"前往來源地可以令故事更生動。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests a purposeful journey.","zh":"這個說法通常暗示有目的的旅程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"avocado farmers","meaning":"牛油果農民","examples":[{"en":"The journalists met avocado farmers in South Africa.","zh":"記者在南非會見牛油果農民。"},{"en":"Avocado farmers are people who grow avocados for sale.","zh":"牛油果農民是種植牛油果出售的人。"},{"en":"Avocado farmers explained how the fruit was planted and harvested.","zh":"牛油果農民解釋這種水果如何種植和收成。"},{"en":"Farmers can benefit when a food trend increases demand for their crop.","zh":"當食品潮流增加作物需求時，農民可以受益。"},{"en":"They may also face pressure if demand rises too quickly.","zh":"如果需求上升太快，他們也可能面對壓力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"articles written following this visit","meaning":"這次訪問後撰寫的文章","examples":[{"en":"Articles written following this visit helped educate the British public.","zh":"這次訪問後撰寫的文章幫助英國大眾認識牛油果。"},{"en":"Articles written following this visit are pieces published after the journalists returned from the trip.","zh":"這次訪問後撰寫的文章，是記者旅程後發表的文章。"},{"en":"Articles written following the farm visit described how avocados were grown.","zh":"參觀農場後撰寫的文章描述牛油果如何種植。"},{"en":"Such articles can turn a marketing event into public education.","zh":"這類文章可以把市場活動轉化為公眾教育。"},{"en":"The phrase links the articles directly to the visit that inspired them.","zh":"這個說法把文章直接與啟發它們的訪問連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"educate the British public about","meaning":"讓英國大眾認識……","examples":[{"en":"The articles helped educate the British public about the avocado.","zh":"這些文章幫助英國大眾認識牛油果。"},{"en":"To educate the British public about something means to give people in Britain useful information about it.","zh":"讓英國大眾認識某事，是指向英國人提供有用資料。"},{"en":"The campaign educated the British public about how to prepare avocados.","zh":"該活動讓英國大眾認識如何準備牛油果。"},{"en":"Public education can make an unfamiliar food easier to accept.","zh":"公眾教育可以令陌生食品更容易被接受。"},{"en":"Marketing can educate consumers, but it should not mislead them.","zh":"市場推廣可以教育消費者，但不應誤導他們。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the British public","meaning":"英國大眾","examples":[{"en":"The British public learned more about the avocado through the campaign.","zh":"英國大眾透過該活動更加認識牛油果。"},{"en":"The British public means people in Britain generally.","zh":"英國大眾是指英國的一般民眾。"},{"en":"The British public became more familiar with avocados after media coverage.","zh":"經過媒體報道後，英國大眾對牛油果更熟悉。"},{"en":"A campaign aimed at the public must use clear and accessible language.","zh":"面向大眾的活動必須使用清楚易明的語言。"},{"en":"Public opinion can change when people receive repeated information.","zh":"當人們反覆收到資訊，公眾意見可能改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at this time","meaning":"在當時","examples":[{"en":"At this time, the avocado was not yet a daily staple.","zh":"在當時，牛油果還不是日常主食。"},{"en":"“At this time” refers to the particular period being discussed.","zh":"「在當時」是指正在討論的特定時期。"},{"en":"At this time, many consumers had never tasted oat milk.","zh":"在當時，許多消費者從未喝過燕麥奶。"},{"en":"The phrase helps place an event in its historical context.","zh":"這個說法幫助把事件放入歷史背景中。"},{"en":"What was unusual at this time may later become normal.","zh":"在當時不尋常的事物，後來可能變得正常。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a daily staple","meaning":"日常主食","examples":[{"en":"The avocado was not the daily staple it has since become.","zh":"牛油果當時還未成為後來那樣的日常主食。"},{"en":"A daily staple is a food commonly eaten as part of everyday life.","zh":"日常主食是日常生活中經常進食的食物。"},{"en":"Rice is a daily staple in many places.","zh":"米飯在許多地方是日常主食。"},{"en":"A fashionable food becomes more important when it turns into a daily staple.","zh":"當時尚食品變成日常主食，它的重要性便更大。"},{"en":"Not every trendy food becomes a daily staple.","zh":"並非每種潮流食品都會成為日常主食。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"advertisements were designed to","meaning":"廣告被設計用來……","examples":[{"en":"Advertisements were designed to promote the avocado as a superfood.","zh":"廣告被設計用來把牛油果宣傳為超級食物。"},{"en":"“Advertisements were designed to” means the ads were created for a specific purpose.","zh":"「廣告被設計用來……」表示廣告是為某個特定目的而製作。"},{"en":"Advertisements were designed to make the new drink look healthy and modern.","zh":"廣告被設計用來令新飲品看起來健康和現代。"},{"en":"The design of an advertisement depends on the message it wants to send.","zh":"廣告設計取決於它想傳達的訊息。"},{"en":"Ads can shape how people understand a product.","zh":"廣告可以塑造人們如何理解一件產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"promote something as","meaning":"把……宣傳為……","examples":[{"en":"The campaign promoted the avocado as a superfood.","zh":"該活動把牛油果宣傳為超級食物。"},{"en":"To promote something as a particular thing means to present it publicly in that way.","zh":"把某物宣傳為某種東西，是指公開以該方式呈現它。"},{"en":"The company promoted oat milk as an environmentally friendly drink.","zh":"公司把燕麥奶宣傳為環保飲品。"},{"en":"Promoting a food as healthy can attract consumers who care about wellbeing.","zh":"把食品宣傳為健康，可以吸引注重健康的消費者。"},{"en":"Claims used in promotion should be truthful and supported by evidence.","zh":"推廣中的聲稱應真實並有證據支持。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"superfood","meaning":"超級食物","examples":[{"en":"Advertisements promoted the avocado as a superfood.","zh":"廣告把牛油果宣傳為超級食物。"},{"en":"A superfood is a food promoted as especially nutritious or beneficial for health.","zh":"超級食物是被宣傳為特別有營養或對健康有益的食品。"},{"en":"Blueberries and quinoa are often described as superfoods.","zh":"藍莓和藜麥常被形容為超級食物。"},{"en":"The word superfood is popular in marketing, but it should be examined critically.","zh":"「超級食物」一詞在市場推廣中很受歡迎，但應批判地看待。"},{"en":"No single superfood can replace a balanced diet.","zh":"沒有任何單一超級食物可以取代均衡飲食。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rich in nutrients","meaning":"營養豐富","examples":[{"en":"Avocados were promoted as rich in nutrients.","zh":"牛油果被宣傳為營養豐富。"},{"en":"Rich in nutrients means containing many substances that help the body grow and stay healthy.","zh":"營養豐富是指含有許多幫助身體成長和保持健康的物質。"},{"en":"Nuts, beans, and leafy vegetables are rich in nutrients.","zh":"堅果、豆類和綠葉蔬菜都營養豐富。"},{"en":"Foods rich in nutrients can support a balanced diet.","zh":"營養豐富的食物可以支持均衡飲食。"},{"en":"A food can be nutrient-rich but still should be eaten in reasonable amounts.","zh":"食物可以營養豐富，但仍應適量食用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"beneficial for health","meaning":"對健康有益","examples":[{"en":"The avocado was advertised as beneficial for health.","zh":"牛油果被宣傳為對健康有益。"},{"en":"Beneficial for health means having a positive effect on the body or mind.","zh":"對健康有益是指對身體或心理有正面影響。"},{"en":"Regular exercise is beneficial for health.","zh":"定期運動對健康有益。"},{"en":"A food may be beneficial for health when eaten as part of a balanced diet.","zh":"如果作為均衡飲食的一部分食用，某種食物可能對健康有益。"},{"en":"Health claims should be clear and not exaggerated.","zh":"健康聲稱應清楚，而且不應誇大。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"became hugely fashionable","meaning":"變得非常流行","examples":[{"en":"Avocados became hugely fashionable within a few years.","zh":"牛油果在幾年內變得非常流行。"},{"en":"If something becomes hugely fashionable, it becomes extremely popular and stylish.","zh":"某物變得非常流行，是指它變得極受歡迎和時尚。"},{"en":"Oat milk became hugely fashionable in many cafés.","zh":"燕麥奶在許多咖啡店變得非常流行。"},{"en":"Social media can help foods become fashionable quickly.","zh":"社交媒體可以幫助食品迅速變得流行。"},{"en":"Something fashionable may later become ordinary if people keep buying it.","zh":"如果人們持續購買，流行事物後來可能變得普通。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"within a few years","meaning":"在幾年內","examples":[{"en":"Within a few years, UK avocado sales had grown sharply.","zh":"在幾年內，英國牛油果銷量大幅增長。"},{"en":"“Within a few years” means before several years had passed.","zh":"「在幾年內」表示在數年過去之前。"},{"en":"Within a few years, the new drink appeared in most supermarkets.","zh":"在幾年內，這款新飲品出現在大多數超級市場。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that change happened over a fairly short period.","zh":"這個說法顯示變化在相對短時間內發生。"},{"en":"A food trend can move from unfamiliar to common within a few years.","zh":"食品潮流可以在幾年內由陌生變成普遍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sales had grown from","meaning":"銷量由……增長至……","examples":[{"en":"UK avocado sales had grown from 13 million pounds to around 150 million.","zh":"英國牛油果銷量由1,300萬英鎊增長至約1億5,000萬英鎊。"},{"en":"“Sales had grown from” describes an increase beginning at one amount and reaching another.","zh":"「銷量由……增長至……」描述銷量從一個金額增加到另一個金額。"},{"en":"Sales had grown from a few thousand units to over a million.","zh":"銷量由幾千件增長至超過一百萬件。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when showing the scale of business growth.","zh":"這個結構適合顯示商業增長幅度。"},{"en":"A large increase in sales may show successful marketing or changing consumer habits.","zh":"銷量大幅上升可能顯示市場推廣成功或消費習慣改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"annually","meaning":"每年","examples":[{"en":"UK avocado sales reached around 150 million pounds annually.","zh":"英國牛油果銷售額每年達約1億5,000萬英鎊。"},{"en":"Annually means every year or per year.","zh":"「每年」表示一年一次或以一年計算。"},{"en":"The company sells millions of cartons annually.","zh":"公司每年售出數百萬盒產品。"},{"en":"Annual figures help compare performance from year to year.","zh":"年度數字有助比較每年的表現。"},{"en":"A product that sells well annually may become important to retailers.","zh":"每年銷量良好的產品可能對零售商很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fresh produce campaigns","meaning":"新鮮農產品推廣活動","examples":[{"en":"The avocado campaign became one of the most successful fresh produce campaigns in UK history.","zh":"牛油果推廣活動成為英國歷史上最成功的新鮮農產品推廣活動之一。"},{"en":"Fresh produce campaigns promote fresh fruits, vegetables, or similar agricultural products.","zh":"新鮮農產品推廣活動是推廣新鮮水果、蔬菜或相似農產品的活動。"},{"en":"A fresh produce campaign may teach consumers how to use a new fruit.","zh":"新鮮農產品推廣活動可能教消費者如何使用一種新水果。"},{"en":"Successful campaigns can change shopping habits.","zh":"成功活動可以改變購物習慣。"},{"en":"Fresh produce promotion often depends on health messages and appealing recipes.","zh":"新鮮農產品推廣通常依靠健康訊息和吸引人的食譜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in UK history","meaning":"在英國歷史上","examples":[{"en":"The campaign was one of the most successful in UK history.","zh":"該活動是英國歷史上最成功的活動之一。"},{"en":"“In UK history” means within the history of the United Kingdom.","zh":"「在英國歷史上」是指在英國的歷史範圍內。"},{"en":"The campaign became one of the most famous food promotions in UK history.","zh":"該活動成為英國歷史上最著名的食品推廣之一。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises the scale or importance of an event.","zh":"這個說法強調事件的規模或重要性。"},{"en":"It is often used to compare one case with many earlier examples.","zh":"它常用來把一個個案與許多較早例子比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"oat milk","meaning":"燕麥奶","examples":[{"en":"Oat milk is a recent example of a product that became fashionable quickly.","zh":"燕麥奶是一個很快變得流行的產品近期例子。"},{"en":"Oat milk is a plant-based drink made from oats and water.","zh":"燕麥奶是由燕麥和水製成的植物飲品。"},{"en":"Many cafés offer oat milk as an alternative to dairy milk.","zh":"許多咖啡店提供燕麥奶作為牛奶替代品。"},{"en":"Oat milk became popular partly because it works well in coffee.","zh":"燕麥奶變得流行，部分原因是它很適合咖啡。"},{"en":"Consumers may choose oat milk for taste, health, ethics, or environmental reasons.","zh":"消費者可能因味道、健康、倫理或環境原因選擇燕麥奶。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a recent example of","meaning":"……的近期例子","examples":[{"en":"Oat milk is a recent example of a new food trend.","zh":"燕麥奶是新食品潮流的近期例子。"},{"en":"A recent example of something is a case that happened or became important not long ago.","zh":"某事的近期例子，是最近發生或變得重要的個案。"},{"en":"Plant-based meat is a recent example of changing consumer taste.","zh":"植物肉是消費者口味變化的近期例子。"},{"en":"Recent examples help show how a general idea works today.","zh":"近期例子可以顯示一個一般想法在今天如何運作。"},{"en":"Comparing recent and older examples can show how marketing methods have changed.","zh":"比較近期和較早例子，可以顯示市場推廣方法如何改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"became fashionable very quickly","meaning":"很快變得流行","examples":[{"en":"Oat milk became fashionable very quickly.","zh":"燕麥奶很快變得流行。"},{"en":"If something becomes fashionable very quickly, it turns popular and stylish in a short time.","zh":"某物很快變得流行，是指它在短時間內變得受歡迎和時尚。"},{"en":"The new dessert became fashionable very quickly after going viral online.","zh":"那款新甜品在網上爆紅後很快變得流行。"},{"en":"Rapid popularity often depends on publicity, availability, and timing.","zh":"快速流行通常取決於宣傳、供應和時機。"},{"en":"A product may become fashionable quickly but still need quality to remain successful.","zh":"產品可以很快流行，但仍需要質素才能持續成功。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"brands available","meaning":"市面上有售的品牌","examples":[{"en":"There are now many oat milk brands available.","zh":"現在市面上有很多燕麥奶品牌有售。"},{"en":"Brands available are the different named products that consumers can buy.","zh":"市面上有售的品牌，是消費者可以購買的不同命名產品。"},{"en":"Many plant-based milk brands are available in supermarkets.","zh":"超級市場有很多植物奶品牌可供購買。"},{"en":"More brands available can give consumers more choice.","zh":"有更多品牌可供選擇，可以給消費者更多選擇。"},{"en":"When many brands are available, competition may lower prices or improve quality.","zh":"當市面上有很多品牌，競爭可能降低價格或提升質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"had early success","meaning":"早期取得成功","examples":[{"en":"Oatly was one company that had early success with oat milk.","zh":"Oatly是早期在燕麥奶方面取得成功的公司之一。"},{"en":"To have early success means to do well at the beginning of a product’s growth or market development.","zh":"早期取得成功，是指在產品成長或市場發展初期表現良好。"},{"en":"The brand had early success by placing its product in popular cafés.","zh":"該品牌透過把產品放入受歡迎咖啡店而早期取得成功。"},{"en":"Early success can help a company attract investment and attention.","zh":"早期成功可以幫助公司吸引投資和關注。"},{"en":"Early success does not guarantee permanent market leadership.","zh":"早期成功不保證永久市場領導地位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Swedish brand","meaning":"瑞典品牌","examples":[{"en":"Oatly is a Swedish brand that became successful early.","zh":"Oatly是一個早期成功的瑞典品牌。"},{"en":"A Swedish brand is a company or product brand from Sweden.","zh":"瑞典品牌是來自瑞典的公司或產品品牌。"},{"en":"The Swedish brand became known for its oat milk.","zh":"這個瑞典品牌因燕麥奶而聞名。"},{"en":"A brand’s national origin can become part of its marketing identity.","zh":"品牌的國家來源可以成為其市場形象的一部分。"},{"en":"Consumers may associate Swedish brands with design, quality, or sustainability.","zh":"消費者可能把瑞典品牌與設計、質素或可持續性聯繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"attracted a lot of attention","meaning":"吸引大量關注","examples":[{"en":"The brand attracted a lot of attention with its media campaign.","zh":"該品牌透過媒體宣傳活動吸引大量關注。"},{"en":"To attract a lot of attention means to make many people notice something.","zh":"吸引大量關注，是指令許多人注意到某事。"},{"en":"The poster attracted a lot of attention because it was provocative.","zh":"那張海報因具挑釁性而吸引大量關注。"},{"en":"Attention can help a new food product enter public conversation.","zh":"關注可以幫助新食品產品進入公眾討論。"},{"en":"Attracting attention is useful only if it leads to interest and trust.","zh":"吸引關注只有在帶來興趣和信任時才有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"media campaign","meaning":"媒體宣傳活動","examples":[{"en":"The Swedish brand used a media campaign to promote oat milk.","zh":"這個瑞典品牌使用媒體宣傳活動推廣燕麥奶。"},{"en":"A media campaign is a planned use of media channels to spread a message.","zh":"媒體宣傳活動是有計劃地使用媒體渠道傳播訊息。"},{"en":"The media campaign included advertisements, interviews, and online posts.","zh":"該媒體宣傳活動包括廣告、訪問和網上貼文。"},{"en":"A strong media campaign can make a product widely recognisable.","zh":"有力的媒體宣傳活動可以令產品廣為人知。"},{"en":"Media campaigns may use humour, emotion, controversy, or information.","zh":"媒體宣傳活動可能使用幽默、情感、爭議或資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"used provocation as a way of","meaning":"以挑釁手法來……","examples":[{"en":"The campaign used provocation as a way of getting its message across.","zh":"該活動以挑釁手法來傳達訊息。"},{"en":"To use provocation as a way of doing something means to deliberately shock or annoy people to gain attention.","zh":"以挑釁手法來做某事，是指故意震撼或惹怒人們以吸引注意。"},{"en":"The advertisement used provocation as a way of challenging the dairy industry.","zh":"該廣告以挑釁手法來挑戰乳製品行業。"},{"en":"Provocation can make a campaign memorable, but it can also create backlash.","zh":"挑釁可以令宣傳活動令人難忘，但也可能引起反彈。"},{"en":"This strategy works only when the audience understands the intended message.","zh":"這種策略只有在觀眾明白訊息時才有效。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get the message across","meaning":"有效傳達訊息","examples":[{"en":"The campaign got its message across effectively.","zh":"該活動有效傳達了訊息。"},{"en":"To get a message across means to communicate an idea clearly to an audience.","zh":"傳達訊息是指清楚地向受眾溝通一個想法。"},{"en":"The simple slogan helped the brand get its message across.","zh":"簡單口號幫助品牌傳達訊息。"},{"en":"Visual images can sometimes get a message across faster than long explanations.","zh":"視覺影像有時比長篇解釋更快傳達訊息。"},{"en":"A message is successful when the audience understands and remembers it.","zh":"當受眾理解並記住訊息，訊息便算成功。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"effectively","meaning":"有效地","examples":[{"en":"The brand got its message across effectively.","zh":"該品牌有效地傳達了訊息。"},{"en":"Effectively means in a successful and useful way.","zh":"有效地是指以成功而有用的方式。"},{"en":"The campaign effectively introduced oat milk to coffee drinkers.","zh":"該活動有效地向咖啡飲用者介紹燕麥奶。"},{"en":"A message can be simple and still work effectively.","zh":"訊息可以很簡單，但仍然有效。"},{"en":"To act effectively, a company must choose methods suited to its audience.","zh":"公司要有效行動，必須選擇適合受眾的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"aggravated competitors","meaning":"激怒競爭對手","examples":[{"en":"The campaign aggravated competitors who produced milk from dairy cows.","zh":"該活動激怒了生產牛奶的競爭對手。"},{"en":"To aggravate competitors means to annoy or anger rival companies.","zh":"激怒競爭對手，是指惹怒或刺激競爭公司。"},{"en":"The bold advertisement aggravated competitors in the dairy industry.","zh":"大膽廣告激怒了乳製品行業的競爭對手。"},{"en":"Aggravating competitors can create publicity, but it may also lead to conflict.","zh":"激怒競爭對手可以帶來宣傳，但也可能引發衝突。"},{"en":"A brand may treat competitors’ anger as proof that its campaign is being noticed.","zh":"品牌可能把競爭對手的憤怒視為活動受到注意的證明。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dairy cows","meaning":"奶牛","examples":[{"en":"The competitors produced milk from dairy cows.","zh":"競爭對手生產來自奶牛的牛奶。"},{"en":"Dairy cows are cows kept mainly for producing milk.","zh":"奶牛是主要用來生產牛奶的牛。"},{"en":"Farms with dairy cows supply milk to food companies.","zh":"飼養奶牛的農場向食品公司供應牛奶。"},{"en":"Dairy cow farming is often compared with plant-based milk production in environmental debates.","zh":"在環境辯論中，奶牛養殖常與植物奶生產比較。"},{"en":"Products from dairy cows compete with alternative milk products.","zh":"來自奶牛的產品與植物奶替代品競爭。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be seen as a plus","meaning":"被視為好處","examples":[{"en":"Annoying competitors was seen as a plus by the brand.","zh":"惹怒競爭對手被該品牌視為好處。"},{"en":"If something is seen as a plus, it is regarded as an advantage or positive point.","zh":"某事被視為好處，是指它被看作優勢或正面之處。"},{"en":"The controversy was seen as a plus because it brought free publicity.","zh":"這場爭議被視為好處，因為它帶來免費宣傳。"},{"en":"A feature may be seen as a plus by one company but as a problem by another.","zh":"一項特色可能被一間公司視為好處，卻被另一間公司視為問題。"},{"en":"Whether something is a plus depends on the goal and context.","zh":"某事是否算好處，取決於目標和情境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make something seem cool","meaning":"令……顯得很酷","examples":[{"en":"The controversy helped make oat milk seem cool.","zh":"爭議幫助令燕麥奶顯得很酷。"},{"en":"To make something seem cool means to make it appear fashionable, modern, or attractive.","zh":"令某物顯得很酷，是指令它看起來時尚、現代或吸引。"},{"en":"The café campaign made plant-based drinks seem cool to young consumers.","zh":"咖啡店宣傳活動令植物飲品對年輕消費者顯得很酷。"},{"en":"Design, humour, and social media can make a product seem cool.","zh":"設計、幽默和社交媒體都可以令產品顯得很酷。"},{"en":"A product that seems cool still needs good taste and quality to survive.","zh":"一件產品即使顯得很酷，也需要好味道和質素才能持續。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"decided against","meaning":"決定不採用……","examples":[{"en":"The brand decided against a big retail launch in the USA.","zh":"該品牌決定不採用在美國大規模零售推出的策略。"},{"en":"To decide against something means to choose not to do it.","zh":"決定不採用某事，是指選擇不去做它。"},{"en":"The company decided against using television advertisements.","zh":"公司決定不採用電視廣告。"},{"en":"A business may decide against a plan if it is too expensive or risky.","zh":"如果計劃太昂貴或風險太高，企業可能決定不採用。"},{"en":"Deciding against one option often means choosing a different strategy.","zh":"決定不採用一個選項，通常意味着選擇另一個策略。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a big retail launch","meaning":"大規模零售推出","examples":[{"en":"The company decided against a big retail launch in the USA.","zh":"公司決定不在美國進行大規模零售推出。"},{"en":"A big retail launch is a large-scale introduction of a product into shops.","zh":"大規模零售推出，是把產品大規模引入商店銷售。"},{"en":"The drink company planned a big retail launch across national supermarkets.","zh":"飲品公司計劃在全國超級市場進行大規模零售推出。"},{"en":"A big launch can be expensive because it needs supply, advertising, and shelf space.","zh":"大規模推出可能很昂貴，因為需要供應、廣告和貨架空間。"},{"en":"Some brands avoid a big retail launch and grow through selected outlets first.","zh":"有些品牌避免大規模零售推出，先透過指定銷售點成長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in favour of","meaning":"轉而選擇；寧願選擇","examples":[{"en":"The brand chose coffee chains in favour of a big retail launch.","zh":"該品牌放棄大規模零售推出，轉而選擇連鎖咖啡店。"},{"en":"“In favour of” means choosing one option instead of another.","zh":"「轉而選擇」表示選擇一個選項而不是另一個。"},{"en":"The company rejected supermarket samples in favour of café partnerships.","zh":"公司不採用超市試食，轉而選擇咖啡店合作。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show a strategic preference.","zh":"這個說法有助顯示策略偏好。"},{"en":"Choosing one method in favour of another may reflect cost, audience, or brand image.","zh":"寧願選擇一種方法而非另一種，可能反映成本、受眾或品牌形象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get the product into","meaning":"讓產品進入……","examples":[{"en":"The brand focused on getting the product into coffee chains.","zh":"該品牌集中讓產品進入連鎖咖啡店。"},{"en":"To get a product into a place means to make it available there for sale or use.","zh":"讓產品進入某地，是指令它在該處可供銷售或使用。"},{"en":"The company worked hard to get oat milk into popular cafés.","zh":"公司努力讓燕麥奶進入受歡迎咖啡店。"},{"en":"Getting a product into the right place can introduce it to the right customers.","zh":"讓產品進入合適地方，可以把它介紹給合適顧客。"},{"en":"Distribution strategy can be as important as advertising.","zh":"分銷策略可以和廣告一樣重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"coffee chains","meaning":"連鎖咖啡店","examples":[{"en":"The company got oat milk into coffee chains in the USA.","zh":"公司讓燕麥奶進入美國的連鎖咖啡店。"},{"en":"Coffee chains are groups of coffee shops under the same brand or company.","zh":"連鎖咖啡店是同一品牌或公司旗下的一組咖啡店。"},{"en":"Large coffee chains can introduce products to millions of customers.","zh":"大型連鎖咖啡店可以把產品介紹給數百萬顧客。"},{"en":"If a drink works well in coffee chains, consumers may later buy it for home use.","zh":"如果飲品在連鎖咖啡店表現良好，消費者之後可能會買回家使用。"},{"en":"Coffee chains helped oat milk become familiar to regular coffee drinkers.","zh":"連鎖咖啡店幫助燕麥奶被日常咖啡飲用者熟悉。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"remove the need for","meaning":"免去……的需要","examples":[{"en":"This strategy removed the need for a big advertising budget.","zh":"這個策略免去了大筆廣告預算的需要。"},{"en":"To remove the need for something means to make it unnecessary.","zh":"免去某事的需要，是指令它變得不再必要。"},{"en":"Placing the drink in cafés removed the need for expensive sampling events.","zh":"把飲品放入咖啡店，免去了昂貴試飲活動的需要。"},{"en":"A smart distribution plan can reduce the need for paid advertising.","zh":"聰明的分銷計劃可以減少付費廣告的需要。"},{"en":"Removing one need may still create other costs or responsibilities.","zh":"免去一項需要仍可能產生其他成本或責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"advertising budget","meaning":"廣告預算","examples":[{"en":"The company did not need a big advertising budget.","zh":"公司不需要龐大的廣告預算。"},{"en":"An advertising budget is the amount of money planned for advertising activities.","zh":"廣告預算是為廣告活動而計劃使用的金額。"},{"en":"A small company may have a limited advertising budget.","zh":"小公司可能只有有限廣告預算。"},{"en":"Social media and word of mouth can help when the advertising budget is small.","zh":"當廣告預算較少，社交媒體和口碑可以幫忙。"},{"en":"A large budget does not guarantee a successful campaign.","zh":"龐大預算不保證宣傳活動成功。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"proved far more effective than","meaning":"證明比……有效得多","examples":[{"en":"This proved far more effective than offering samples in supermarkets.","zh":"這證明比在超級市場提供試食樣本有效得多。"},{"en":"“Proved far more effective than” means turned out to work much better than another method.","zh":"「證明比……有效得多」表示結果顯示某方法比另一方法好很多。"},{"en":"Café placement proved far more effective than ordinary posters.","zh":"放入咖啡店證明比普通海報有效得多。"},{"en":"The phrase is used after results show a clear difference.","zh":"這個說法用於結果顯示明顯差異之後。"},{"en":"A method that proves effective in one market may not work everywhere.","zh":"在一個市場證明有效的方法，未必在所有地方都有效。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"offering samples","meaning":"提供試食樣本","examples":[{"en":"Offering samples in supermarkets was less effective.","zh":"在超級市場提供試食樣本較不有效。"},{"en":"Offering samples means giving small amounts of a product for people to try.","zh":"提供試食樣本是指給人小量產品試用或試吃。"},{"en":"The company considered offering samples of oat milk to shoppers.","zh":"公司考慮向購物者提供燕麥奶試飲樣本。"},{"en":"Samples can introduce taste, but they may not create a lasting habit.","zh":"試食樣本可以介紹味道，但未必建立持久習慣。"},{"en":"Offering samples works best when customers can buy the product immediately afterward.","zh":"當顧客試完後能立即購買產品，提供樣本最有效。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in supermarkets","meaning":"在超級市場","examples":[{"en":"The company avoided relying on samples in supermarkets.","zh":"公司避免依賴在超級市場提供樣本。"},{"en":"“In supermarkets” means inside large shops that sell food and household goods.","zh":"「在超級市場」是指在售賣食物和家居用品的大型商店內。"},{"en":"Many new drinks are first tested in supermarkets.","zh":"許多新飲品先在超級市場測試。"},{"en":"Supermarkets give products access to large numbers of shoppers.","zh":"超級市場讓產品接觸大量購物者。"},{"en":"A product in supermarkets still needs shelf space, pricing, and visibility.","zh":"產品在超級市場銷售仍需要貨架空間、價格策略和可見度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"had an advantage over","meaning":"比……有優勢","examples":[{"en":"Oat milk had an advantage over other alternative milk products.","zh":"燕麥奶比其他替代奶產品有優勢。"},{"en":"To have an advantage over something means to be better or more useful in a particular way.","zh":"比某物有優勢，是指在某方面更好或更有用。"},{"en":"Oat milk had an advantage over almond milk because it needed less water.","zh":"燕麥奶比杏仁奶有優勢，因為它需要較少水。"},{"en":"A product’s advantage can come from taste, price, image, or environmental impact.","zh":"產品優勢可以來自味道、價格、形象或環境影響。"},{"en":"An advantage may matter only if consumers know about it.","zh":"優勢只有在消費者知道時才可能發揮作用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"alternative milk products","meaning":"替代奶產品；植物奶產品","examples":[{"en":"Oat milk competed with other alternative milk products such as almond milk.","zh":"燕麥奶與杏仁奶等其他植物奶產品競爭。"},{"en":"Alternative milk products are drinks used instead of dairy milk.","zh":"替代奶產品是用來代替牛奶的飲品。"},{"en":"Soy milk, almond milk, and oat milk are alternative milk products.","zh":"豆奶、杏仁奶和燕麥奶都是植物奶產品。"},{"en":"Some consumers choose alternative milks because of diet, ethics, or allergies.","zh":"有些消費者因飲食、倫理或過敏原因選擇替代奶。"},{"en":"Alternative milk products differ in taste, nutrition, cost, and environmental impact.","zh":"植物奶產品在味道、營養、成本和環境影響方面各有不同。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"almond milk","meaning":"杏仁奶","examples":[{"en":"Almond milk is another alternative milk product.","zh":"杏仁奶是另一種替代奶產品。"},{"en":"Almond milk is a plant-based drink made from almonds and water.","zh":"杏仁奶是由杏仁和水製成的植物飲品。"},{"en":"Some people use almond milk in cereal or coffee.","zh":"有些人把杏仁奶加入穀物早餐或咖啡。"},{"en":"Almond milk competes with oat milk and soy milk in supermarkets.","zh":"杏仁奶在超級市場與燕麥奶和豆奶競爭。"},{"en":"Environmental concerns can affect how consumers compare almond milk with other alternatives.","zh":"環境關注會影響消費者如何比較杏仁奶與其他替代品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"consumers","meaning":"消費者","examples":[{"en":"Many consumers prefer oat milk because of its environmental benefits.","zh":"許多消費者因燕麥奶的環境益處而較喜歡它。"},{"en":"Consumers are people who buy or use goods and services.","zh":"消費者是購買或使用商品和服務的人。"},{"en":"Consumers often compare price, taste, and health claims before buying food.","zh":"消費者在購買食物前通常會比較價格、味道和健康聲稱。"},{"en":"Consumer preferences can make a new food trend grow quickly.","zh":"消費者偏好可以令新的食品潮流迅速成長。"},{"en":"Companies study consumers to understand what they want.","zh":"公司研究消費者，以了解他們想要甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"less of an impact on","meaning":"對……影響較小","examples":[{"en":"Oat milk has less of an impact on the environment.","zh":"燕麥奶對環境的影響較小。"},{"en":"To have less of an impact on something means to affect it less strongly.","zh":"對某事影響較小，是指對它造成的影響沒那麼強。"},{"en":"Reusable packaging has less of an impact on waste than single-use plastic.","zh":"可重用包裝對廢物的影響比即棄塑膠小。"},{"en":"Products with less environmental impact may appeal to concerned consumers.","zh":"對環境影響較小的產品可能吸引關注環境的消費者。"},{"en":"Impact should be measured carefully rather than assumed from marketing claims.","zh":"影響應仔細量度，而不是只根據市場宣傳假設。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the environment","meaning":"環境","examples":[{"en":"Consumers prefer products that have less impact on the environment.","zh":"消費者較喜歡對環境影響較小的產品。"},{"en":"The environment is the natural world, including air, water, land, plants, and animals.","zh":"環境是自然世界，包括空氣、水、土地、植物和動物。"},{"en":"Food production can affect the environment through water use and emissions.","zh":"食品生產可以透過用水和排放影響環境。"},{"en":"Many shoppers consider the environment when choosing food.","zh":"許多購物者選擇食物時會考慮環境。"},{"en":"Protecting the environment often requires changes in production and consumption.","zh":"保護環境通常需要改變生產和消費方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"requires significantly less water","meaning":"需要少得多的水","examples":[{"en":"Oat milk requires significantly less water to produce.","zh":"生產燕麥奶需要少得多的水。"},{"en":"If something requires significantly less water, it needs much less water than another option.","zh":"某物需要少得多的水，是指與另一選項相比，用水量大幅較少。"},{"en":"Growing oats may require significantly less water than growing some nuts.","zh":"種植燕麥可能比種植某些堅果需要少得多的水。"},{"en":"Water use is an important factor in judging environmental impact.","zh":"用水量是評估環境影響的重要因素。"},{"en":"“Significantly” shows that the difference is large enough to matter.","zh":"“Significantly”表示差異大到值得重視。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"to produce","meaning":"生產……","examples":[{"en":"Oat milk requires less water to produce than other alternative milk products.","zh":"生產燕麥奶所需的水比其他替代奶產品少。"},{"en":"“To produce” means to make, grow, or manufacture something.","zh":"生產某物是指製造、種植或加工某物。"},{"en":"It takes energy and water to produce packaged food.","zh":"生產包裝食品需要能源和水。"},{"en":"Different foods require different resources to produce.","zh":"不同食物需要不同資源來生產。"},{"en":"Understanding what it takes to produce food helps consumers compare environmental costs.","zh":"了解生產食物需要甚麼，可以幫助消費者比較環境成本。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"relatively low","meaning":"相對較低的","examples":[{"en":"Oat milk has a relatively low carbon footprint.","zh":"燕麥奶的碳足跡相對較低。"},{"en":"Relatively low means low when compared with something else.","zh":"相對較低是指與其他事物比較時較低。"},{"en":"The product has a relatively low price compared with imported alternatives.","zh":"與進口替代品相比，該產品價格相對較低。"},{"en":"A relatively low impact can still matter if the product is consumed in large quantities.","zh":"如果產品消耗量很大，即使影響相對較低仍然重要。"},{"en":"The word “relatively” shows that the judgement depends on comparison.","zh":"「相對」顯示判斷取決於比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"carbon footprint","meaning":"碳足跡","examples":[{"en":"Oat milk has a relatively low carbon footprint.","zh":"燕麥奶的碳足跡相對較低。"},{"en":"A carbon footprint is the amount of greenhouse gases caused by a person, product, or activity.","zh":"碳足跡是個人、產品或活動所造成的溫室氣體排放量。"},{"en":"Transport, packaging, and production all affect a food’s carbon footprint.","zh":"運輸、包裝和生產都會影響食品的碳足跡。"},{"en":"Consumers may choose products with a lower carbon footprint.","zh":"消費者可能選擇碳足跡較低的產品。"},{"en":"Carbon footprint is only one part of a product’s environmental impact.","zh":"碳足跡只是產品環境影響的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Norwegian skrei","meaning":"挪威 skrei 魚","examples":[{"en":"Norwegian skrei is a rarely available seasonal fish delicacy.","zh":"挪威skrei魚是一種很少有售的季節性魚類珍饈。"},{"en":"Norwegian skrei is a type of Arctic cod associated with Norway.","zh":"挪威skrei魚是一種與挪威相關的北極鱈。"},{"en":"Chefs may use Norwegian skrei when it is in season.","zh":"名廚可能在當造季節使用挪威skrei魚。"},{"en":"A rare seasonal product can become fashionable in high-end restaurants.","zh":"稀有季節性產品可以在高級餐廳變得流行。"},{"en":"Marketing skrei helps connect Norway with premium seafood.","zh":"推廣skrei魚有助把挪威與高級海鮮連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rarely available","meaning":"很少有售的；稀有的","examples":[{"en":"Norwegian skrei is a rarely available seasonal fish delicacy.","zh":"挪威skrei魚是一種很少有售的季節性魚類珍饈。"},{"en":"If something is rarely available, people can buy or find it only occasionally.","zh":"某物很少有售，是指人們只能偶爾購買或找到它。"},{"en":"The fruit is rarely available outside its harvest season.","zh":"這種水果在收成季節以外很少有售。"},{"en":"Rare availability can make a food seem more special.","zh":"稀有供應可以令食品顯得更特別。"},{"en":"A product that is rarely available may attract chefs looking for exclusivity.","zh":"很少有售的產品可能吸引追求獨特性的廚師。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"seasonal fish delicacy","meaning":"季節性魚類珍饈","examples":[{"en":"Skrei is a seasonal fish delicacy from Norway.","zh":"Skrei是來自挪威的季節性魚類珍饈。"},{"en":"A seasonal fish delicacy is a highly valued fish available only at certain times of year.","zh":"季節性魚類珍饈是只在一年中某些時段有供應的珍貴魚類。"},{"en":"Restaurants advertise seasonal fish delicacies when they are fresh.","zh":"餐廳會在季節性魚類珍饈新鮮時作宣傳。"},{"en":"Seasonal foods can create excitement because they are not always available.","zh":"季節性食品因不是長期供應，可以令人感到期待。"},{"en":"Delicacies often depend on freshness, rarity, and reputation.","zh":"珍饈通常取決於新鮮、稀有和聲譽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"otherwise known as","meaning":"又稱為","examples":[{"en":"Norwegian skrei is otherwise known as Arctic cod.","zh":"挪威skrei魚又稱為北極鱈。"},{"en":"“Otherwise known as” introduces another name for the same thing.","zh":"「又稱為」用來引入同一事物的另一個名稱。"},{"en":"Skrei, otherwise known as Arctic cod, appears on many restaurant menus.","zh":"Skrei又稱為北極鱈，出現在許多餐廳餐牌上。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when a specialist name may be unfamiliar.","zh":"當專門名稱可能令人陌生時，這個說法很有用。"},{"en":"It helps connect a new term with a name listeners may understand.","zh":"它幫助把新詞與聽眾可能明白的名稱連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Arctic cod","meaning":"北極鱈","examples":[{"en":"Skrei is otherwise known as Arctic cod.","zh":"Skrei又稱為北極鱈。"},{"en":"Arctic cod is a name used for a cod associated with cold northern waters.","zh":"北極鱈是與寒冷北方水域相關的鱈魚名稱。"},{"en":"Chefs value Arctic cod for its quality and seasonal appeal.","zh":"廚師重視北極鱈的品質和季節吸引力。"},{"en":"Calling skrei Arctic cod helps consumers understand what type of fish it is.","zh":"把skrei稱為北極鱈，可以幫助消費者了解它是哪類魚。"},{"en":"A familiar name can make an unusual food easier to market.","zh":"熟悉名稱可以令不尋常食品更容易推廣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"found on the menus of","meaning":"出現在……的餐牌上","examples":[{"en":"Skrei is now found on the menus of Michelin starred restaurants.","zh":"Skrei現在出現在米芝蓮星級餐廳的餐牌上。"},{"en":"If a food is found on the menus of restaurants, those restaurants serve it.","zh":"如果某食品出現在餐廳餐牌上，表示那些餐廳供應它。"},{"en":"Oat milk drinks are now found on the menus of many coffee shops.","zh":"燕麥奶飲品現在出現在許多咖啡店餐牌上。"},{"en":"Appearing on famous menus can raise a food’s status.","zh":"出現在著名餐牌上可以提高食品地位。"},{"en":"A dish found on many menus may become familiar to consumers.","zh":"出現在許多餐牌上的菜式可能變得為消費者熟悉。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Michelin starred restaurants","meaning":"米芝蓮星級餐廳","examples":[{"en":"Skrei appears on the menus of Michelin starred restaurants throughout Europe.","zh":"Skrei出現在全歐洲米芝蓮星級餐廳的餐牌上。"},{"en":"Michelin starred restaurants are restaurants awarded stars by the Michelin Guide for high quality.","zh":"米芝蓮星級餐廳是獲《米芝蓮指南》因高質素而頒星的餐廳。"},{"en":"A dish served in Michelin starred restaurants may gain prestige.","zh":"在米芝蓮星級餐廳供應的菜式可能獲得聲望。"},{"en":"Chefs in Michelin starred restaurants often influence food trends.","zh":"米芝蓮星級餐廳的廚師常影響食品潮流。"},{"en":"Such restaurants can introduce rare ingredients to wealthy or curious diners.","zh":"這類餐廳可以把稀有食材介紹給富裕或好奇的食客。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"throughout Europe","meaning":"全歐洲","examples":[{"en":"Skrei is served in restaurants throughout Europe.","zh":"Skrei在全歐洲的餐廳供應。"},{"en":"“Throughout Europe” means in many places across Europe.","zh":"「全歐洲」是指歐洲各地許多地方。"},{"en":"Oat milk became available in cafés throughout Europe.","zh":"燕麥奶在全歐洲的咖啡店有售。"},{"en":"A food served throughout Europe has moved beyond one local market.","zh":"在全歐洲供應的食品已超越單一本地市場。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises wide geographical spread.","zh":"這個說法強調廣泛地理傳播。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"demand for","meaning":"對……的需求","examples":[{"en":"The demand for skrei has helped promote Norway’s fisheries.","zh":"對skrei魚的需求幫助推廣挪威漁業。"},{"en":"Demand for something is the desire or willingness of consumers to buy it.","zh":"對某物的需求，是消費者想購買它的意願。"},{"en":"Demand for avocados increased after the marketing campaign.","zh":"市場推廣活動後，對牛油果的需求增加。"},{"en":"High demand can raise prices and encourage producers to increase supply.","zh":"高需求可以提高價格，並鼓勵生產者增加供應。"},{"en":"Demand may be created by taste, fashion, availability, and reputation.","zh":"需求可能由味道、潮流、供應和聲譽創造。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"food marketing agency","meaning":"食品市場推廣機構","examples":[{"en":"A food marketing agency used skrei to build Norway’s reputation.","zh":"一間食品市場推廣機構利用skrei魚建立挪威聲譽。"},{"en":"A food marketing agency is a company or organisation that promotes food products or food industries.","zh":"食品市場推廣機構是推廣食品產品或食品行業的公司或組織。"},{"en":"The agency designed a campaign for Norwegian seafood.","zh":"該機構為挪威海鮮設計宣傳活動。"},{"en":"Food marketing agencies often work with farmers, fisheries, and retailers.","zh":"食品市場推廣機構常與農民、漁業和零售商合作。"},{"en":"Their goal is to make products more attractive to consumers and businesses.","zh":"它們的目標是令產品對消費者和企業更具吸引力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"build the reputation of","meaning":"建立……的聲譽","examples":[{"en":"The agency helped build the reputation of Norway’s fisheries.","zh":"該機構幫助建立挪威漁業的聲譽。"},{"en":"To build the reputation of something means to strengthen public respect or recognition for it.","zh":"建立某事的聲譽，是指加強公眾對它的尊重或認識。"},{"en":"The campaign built the reputation of local cheese producers.","zh":"該活動建立了本地芝士生產者的聲譽。"},{"en":"Reputation grows when people repeatedly associate a place with quality.","zh":"當人們反覆把一個地方與品質聯繫起來，聲譽便會增長。"},{"en":"Building reputation usually takes time, consistent quality, and effective promotion.","zh":"建立聲譽通常需要時間、穩定質素和有效推廣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fisheries","meaning":"漁業","examples":[{"en":"The campaign built the reputation of Norway’s fisheries in general.","zh":"該活動整體上建立了挪威漁業的聲譽。"},{"en":"Fisheries are industries or places involved in catching, farming, processing, or selling fish.","zh":"漁業是涉及捕魚、養殖、加工或銷售魚類的行業或地方。"},{"en":"Norway’s fisheries are closely connected with seafood exports.","zh":"挪威漁業與海鮮出口密切相關。"},{"en":"Fisheries can benefit when one premium product becomes famous.","zh":"當一種高級產品成名時，漁業可以受益。"},{"en":"Sustainable management is important for protecting fisheries long term.","zh":"可持續管理對長期保護漁業十分重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in general","meaning":"整體而言","examples":[{"en":"The demand for skrei helped Norway’s fisheries in general.","zh":"對skrei魚的需求整體而言幫助了挪威漁業。"},{"en":"“In general” means overall or in most cases, not focusing on one small detail.","zh":"「整體而言」表示從整體或多數情況來看，而不是集中於細節。"},{"en":"Food trends can help producers in general when demand rises.","zh":"當需求上升時，食品潮流整體而言可以幫助生產者。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to make a broad statement.","zh":"這個說法用來作概括陳述。"},{"en":"It allows for exceptions while describing the overall situation.","zh":"它容許存在例外，同時描述整體情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"marketing surveys","meaning":"市場調查","examples":[{"en":"Marketing surveys show that shoppers associate Norway with seafood.","zh":"市場調查顯示購物者把挪威與海鮮聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Marketing surveys are research tools used to collect consumers’ opinions and behaviour.","zh":"市場調查是用來收集消費者意見和行為的研究工具。"},{"en":"The agency used marketing surveys to measure Norway’s seafood reputation.","zh":"該機構使用市場調查量度挪威海鮮聲譽。"},{"en":"Surveys can show whether a campaign has changed public perception.","zh":"調查可以顯示宣傳活動是否改變了公眾看法。"},{"en":"Survey results should be interpreted carefully because samples may not represent everyone.","zh":"調查結果應小心解讀，因為樣本未必代表所有人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a significant number of","meaning":"相當多的……","examples":[{"en":"A significant number of shoppers now associate Norway with excellent seafood.","zh":"相當多的購物者現在把挪威與優質海鮮聯繫起來。"},{"en":"A significant number of people means enough people to be important or noticeable.","zh":"相當多的人表示人數足夠重要或明顯。"},{"en":"A significant number of consumers prefer sustainable products.","zh":"相當多的消費者較喜歡可持續產品。"},{"en":"The phrase does not give an exact amount, but it suggests the number matters.","zh":"這個說法沒有給出精確數字，但暗示數量值得重視。"},{"en":"A significant number of responses can support a conclusion in a report.","zh":"相當多的回應可以支持報告中的結論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"shoppers","meaning":"購物者；消費者","examples":[{"en":"Many shoppers now associate Norway with excellent seafood.","zh":"許多購物者現在把挪威與優質海鮮聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Shoppers are people who buy or look for goods in shops or online.","zh":"購物者是在商店或網上購買或尋找商品的人。"},{"en":"Shoppers often compare brands before choosing seafood.","zh":"購物者在選擇海鮮前通常會比較品牌。"},{"en":"Marketing aims to influence what shoppers notice and buy.","zh":"市場推廣旨在影響購物者注意和購買甚麼。"},{"en":"Shoppers’ views can shape what supermarkets decide to stock.","zh":"購物者的看法可以影響超級市場決定入貨甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"associate A with B","meaning":"把 A 與 B 聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"Shoppers associate Norway with excellent seafood.","zh":"購物者把挪威與優質海鮮聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To associate A with B means to connect one thing with another in the mind.","zh":"把A與B聯繫起來，是指在腦海中把一件事物與另一件事物相連。"},{"en":"Many consumers associate Italy with pasta and coffee.","zh":"許多消費者把意大利與意粉和咖啡聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Marketing can make people associate a country with a particular product.","zh":"市場推廣可以令人把一個國家與某種產品聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Strong associations can help build reputation and increase demand.","zh":"強烈聯繫可以幫助建立聲譽並增加需求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"excellent seafood","meaning":"優質海鮮","examples":[{"en":"Norway is now associated with excellent seafood.","zh":"挪威現在與優質海鮮聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Excellent seafood is seafood judged to be very high in quality, freshness, or taste.","zh":"優質海鮮是被認為在質素、新鮮度或味道方面很高的海鮮。"},{"en":"The restaurant became famous for excellent seafood.","zh":"那間餐廳因優質海鮮而聞名。"},{"en":"A reputation for excellent seafood can help a country’s exports.","zh":"優質海鮮的聲譽可以幫助一個國家的出口。"},{"en":"Consumers may pay more for seafood they believe is excellent.","zh":"消費者可能願意為他們相信是優質的海鮮支付更多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be considered a good thing","meaning":"被視為好事","examples":[{"en":"Food trends can be considered a good thing in some ways.","zh":"食品潮流在某些方面可以被視為好事。"},{"en":"If something is considered a good thing, people regard it as positive or beneficial.","zh":"某事被視為好事，是指人們認為它正面或有益。"},{"en":"Increased interest in healthy food can be considered a good thing.","zh":"人們對健康食品的興趣增加，可以被視為好事。"},{"en":"A trend may be considered good for producers but harmful for local consumers.","zh":"一種潮流對生產者可能被視為好事，但對本地消費者可能有害。"},{"en":"Whether something is good depends on which effects are being considered.","zh":"某事是否好，取決於正在考慮哪些影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in some ways","meaning":"在某些方面","examples":[{"en":"Food trends can be considered a good thing in some ways.","zh":"食品潮流在某些方面可以被視為好事。"},{"en":"“In some ways” means from certain points of view, but not completely.","zh":"「在某些方面」表示從某些角度來看，但不是完全如此。"},{"en":"In some ways, social media has helped small food producers.","zh":"在某些方面，社交媒體幫助了小型食品生產者。"},{"en":"The phrase allows a balanced view by admitting both benefits and problems.","zh":"這個說法承認好處和問題，令觀點更平衡。"},{"en":"It suggests that the situation is more complex than a simple yes or no.","zh":"它暗示情況比簡單的是或否更複雜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"benefit farmers and food producers","meaning":"令農民和食品生產者受益","examples":[{"en":"Food trends can benefit farmers and food producers enormously.","zh":"食品潮流可以令農民和食品生產者大大受益。"},{"en":"To benefit farmers and food producers means to help people who grow, make, or sell food.","zh":"令農民和食品生產者受益，是指幫助種植、製造或銷售食物的人。"},{"en":"A rise in demand for avocados benefited farmers and food producers.","zh":"對牛油果需求上升令農民和食品生產者受益。"},{"en":"Trends can create higher income, larger markets, and new business opportunities.","zh":"潮流可以創造更高收入、更大市場和新商機。"},{"en":"Benefits should be weighed against possible environmental or social costs.","zh":"好處應與可能的環境或社會成本一起衡量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"enormously","meaning":"大大地；非常","examples":[{"en":"Food producers can benefit enormously from food trends.","zh":"食品生產者可以從食品潮流中大大受益。"},{"en":"Enormously means very greatly or to a very large degree.","zh":"「大大地」表示程度非常大。"},{"en":"Farmers benefited enormously when demand for their crop increased.","zh":"當作物需求增加，農民大大受益。"},{"en":"A company can grow enormously after a successful marketing campaign.","zh":"一間公司可以在成功市場推廣活動後大幅成長。"},{"en":"The word strongly emphasises the size of the effect.","zh":"這個詞強烈強調影響的大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the public can be encouraged to","meaning":"大眾可被鼓勵去……","examples":[{"en":"The public can be encouraged to buy more sustainable products.","zh":"大眾可被鼓勵去購買更多可持續產品。"},{"en":"If the public can be encouraged to do something, people can be persuaded or motivated to do it.","zh":"大眾可被鼓勵去做某事，是指人們可以被說服或推動去做。"},{"en":"The public can be encouraged to waste less food through clear labels.","zh":"清楚標籤可以鼓勵大眾減少浪費食物。"},{"en":"Campaigns can encourage consumers to choose healthier or more ethical products.","zh":"宣傳活動可以鼓勵消費者選擇較健康或較合乎倫理的產品。"},{"en":"Encouragement works better when products are affordable and easy to find.","zh":"當產品價格合理且容易找到，鼓勵會更有效。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"sustainably produced","meaning":"以可持續方式生產的","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may buy things that are more sustainably produced.","zh":"消費者可能購買更多以可持續方式生產的東西。"},{"en":"Sustainably produced goods are made in ways that reduce harm to the environment and future resources.","zh":"以可持續方式生產的商品，是以減少對環境和未來資源傷害的方法製造。"},{"en":"Sustainably produced seafood may come from well-managed fisheries.","zh":"以可持續方式生產的海鮮可能來自管理良好的漁業。"},{"en":"Consumers often need labels to identify sustainably produced products.","zh":"消費者通常需要標籤來辨認可持續產品。"},{"en":"A product should not be called sustainable unless the claim is supported by evidence.","zh":"除非有證據支持，否則產品不應被稱為可持續。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ethical concerns","meaning":"倫理方面的關注","examples":[{"en":"Ethical concerns have been raised about the effects of food trends.","zh":"有人就食品潮流的影響提出倫理方面的關注。"},{"en":"Ethical concerns are worries about whether something is morally right or fair.","zh":"倫理方面的關注，是對某事在道德上是否正確或公平的擔心。"},{"en":"The high price of quinoa created ethical concerns about local access to food.","zh":"藜麥價格高企引發了當地人能否取得食物的倫理關注。"},{"en":"Ethical concerns may involve workers, farmers, animals, consumers, or the environment.","zh":"倫理關注可能涉及工人、農民、動物、消費者或環境。"},{"en":"A profitable trend can still raise serious ethical concerns.","zh":"有利可圖的潮流仍可能引發嚴重倫理關注。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have been raised about","meaning":"就……被提出","examples":[{"en":"Concerns have been raised about the effects of a surge in demand.","zh":"有人就需求急增的影響提出了關注。"},{"en":"If concerns have been raised about something, people have publicly expressed worries about it.","zh":"就某事提出關注，是指人們公開表達對它的憂慮。"},{"en":"Questions have been raised about the environmental cost of the trend.","zh":"有人就該潮流的環境成本提出疑問。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in reports and academic writing.","zh":"這個說法常用於報告和學術寫作。"},{"en":"Raised concerns should be investigated rather than ignored.","zh":"被提出的關注應被調查，而不是被忽視。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a surge in demand","meaning":"需求急增","examples":[{"en":"A surge in demand can create serious problems.","zh":"需求急增可以造成嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A surge in demand is a sudden and large increase in people wanting to buy something.","zh":"需求急增是人們想購買某物的需求突然大幅增加。"},{"en":"A surge in demand for quinoa pushed prices higher.","zh":"對藜麥的需求急增推高了價格。"},{"en":"Producers may struggle to respond to a sudden surge in demand.","zh":"生產者可能難以應付突然的需求急增。"},{"en":"A surge can benefit sellers but harm consumers if prices rise too much.","zh":"需求急增可以令賣方受益，但若價格升得太高，會傷害消費者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a classic example","meaning":"典型例子","examples":[{"en":"Quinoa is a classic example of the negative effects of food trends.","zh":"藜麥是食品潮流負面影響的典型例子。"},{"en":"A classic example is a clear and typical case of something.","zh":"典型例子是某事清楚而具代表性的個案。"},{"en":"The avocado campaign is a classic example of successful food marketing.","zh":"牛油果推廣活動是成功食品市場推廣的典型例子。"},{"en":"Classic examples help students understand a general argument.","zh":"典型例子幫助學生理解一般論點。"},{"en":"Calling something classic suggests that it is widely recognised or often used as evidence.","zh":"稱某事為典型，表示它被廣泛認識或常被用作證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"quinoa","meaning":"藜麥","examples":[{"en":"Quinoa became very popular but also caused ethical concerns.","zh":"藜麥變得非常流行，但也引起倫理關注。"},{"en":"Quinoa is a grain-like seed often eaten as a healthy food.","zh":"藜麥是一種像穀物般食用的種子，常被視為健康食品。"},{"en":"Quinoa became popular in salads and health-food recipes.","zh":"藜麥在沙律和健康食品食譜中變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"Rising demand for quinoa affected both farmers and local consumers.","zh":"對藜麥需求上升影響了農民和本地消費者。"},{"en":"A healthy food trend can still create social and environmental problems.","zh":"健康食品潮流仍可能造成社會和環境問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be native to","meaning":"原產於……","examples":[{"en":"This plant is native to Peru.","zh":"這種植物原產於秘魯。"},{"en":"If a plant is native to a place, it originally grows there naturally.","zh":"某植物原產於某地，是指它原本自然生長在該地。"},{"en":"Quinoa is native to parts of South America.","zh":"藜麥原產於南美洲部分地區。"},{"en":"Native crops often have cultural and historical importance.","zh":"原生作物通常具有文化和歷史重要性。"},{"en":"A plant can become popular globally while remaining native to one region.","zh":"一種植物可以在全球流行，但仍原產於某一地區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"demand peaked","meaning":"需求達到高峰","examples":[{"en":"When demand peaked, the price of quinoa soared.","zh":"當需求達到高峰時，藜麥價格飆升。"},{"en":"If demand peaked, it reached its highest level.","zh":"需求達到高峰，是指需求達到最高水平。"},{"en":"Demand peaked after several celebrity chefs promoted the food.","zh":"幾位名廚推廣該食品後，需求達到高峰。"},{"en":"Prices often rise when demand peaks and supply cannot keep up.","zh":"當需求達到高峰而供應追不上，價格通常會上升。"},{"en":"After demand peaks, interest may stay high or gradually decline.","zh":"需求達到高峰後，興趣可能保持高企，也可能逐漸下降。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the price soared","meaning":"價格飆升","examples":[{"en":"The price soared when demand for quinoa peaked.","zh":"當藜麥需求達到高峰時，價格飆升。"},{"en":"If the price soared, it rose very quickly and sharply.","zh":"價格飆升是指價格非常快速而大幅上升。"},{"en":"The price of the ingredient soared after it became fashionable.","zh":"該食材變得流行後，價格飆升。"},{"en":"A soaring price can make a local staple unaffordable.","zh":"價格飆升可以令本地日常食品變得負擔不起。"},{"en":"Rapid price increases can create winners and losers in the same market.","zh":"快速價格上升可以在同一市場中創造受益者和受害者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unaffordable for local people","meaning":"當地人負擔不起的","examples":[{"en":"Quinoa became unaffordable for local people.","zh":"藜麥變成當地人負擔不起的食品。"},{"en":"If something is unaffordable for local people, they cannot reasonably pay for it.","zh":"某物對當地人來說負擔不起，是指他們無法合理支付其價格。"},{"en":"Rising prices made the traditional food unaffordable for many families.","zh":"價格上升令許多家庭負擔不起這種傳統食品。"},{"en":"A global trend can harm local people if it raises the price of their staple food.","zh":"如果全球潮流推高本地日常食品價格，便可能傷害當地人。"},{"en":"Food justice requires considering who loses access when demand increases.","zh":"食品公義需要考慮需求增加時誰會失去取得食物的機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the popularity of","meaning":"……的流行","examples":[{"en":"The popularity of quinoa has benefitted farmers financially.","zh":"藜麥的流行令農民在經濟上受益。"},{"en":"The popularity of something means how widely liked, bought, or discussed it is.","zh":"某物的流行，是指它被喜愛、購買或討論的廣泛程度。"},{"en":"The popularity of oat milk changed what many cafés offered.","zh":"燕麥奶的流行改變了許多咖啡店提供的飲品。"},{"en":"A product’s popularity can rise quickly through media attention.","zh":"產品的流行可以透過媒體關注迅速上升。"},{"en":"Popularity can bring money, but it can also create pressure on resources.","zh":"流行可以帶來金錢，但也會對資源造成壓力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"benefitted farmers financially","meaning":"令農民在經濟上受益","examples":[{"en":"The popularity of quinoa benefitted farmers financially.","zh":"藜麥的流行令農民在經濟上受益。"},{"en":"If something benefits farmers financially, it helps them earn more money.","zh":"令農民在經濟上受益，是指幫助他們賺取更多金錢。"},{"en":"Higher quinoa prices benefitted some farmers financially.","zh":"藜麥價格較高令一些農民在經濟上受益。"},{"en":"Financial benefits may improve income, equipment, and living standards.","zh":"經濟收益可能改善收入、設備和生活水平。"},{"en":"However, financial benefit for farmers does not remove all social or environmental concerns.","zh":"然而，農民在經濟上受益並不能消除所有社會或環境關注。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"negative consequences","meaning":"負面後果","examples":[{"en":"The popularity of quinoa also had negative consequences.","zh":"藜麥的流行也帶來負面後果。"},{"en":"Negative consequences are harmful or unwanted results of an action or situation.","zh":"負面後果是行動或情況帶來的有害或不想要的結果。"},{"en":"A sudden food trend can have negative consequences for local consumers.","zh":"突然出現的食品潮流可能對本地消費者造成負面後果。"},{"en":"Negative consequences may appear after the first economic benefits.","zh":"負面後果可能在最初經濟好處之後才出現。"},{"en":"Responsible marketing should consider both benefits and negative consequences.","zh":"負責任的市場推廣應同時考慮好處和負面後果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"as demand grew","meaning":"隨着需求增加","examples":[{"en":"As demand grew, farmers began working the land all year round.","zh":"隨着需求增加，農民開始全年耕作土地。"},{"en":"“As demand grew” means while or because more people wanted the product.","zh":"「隨着需求增加」表示在更多人想要該產品時或因為此原因。"},{"en":"As demand grew, producers planted more quinoa.","zh":"隨着需求增加，生產者種植更多藜麥。"},{"en":"The phrase links rising demand with a later change in behaviour.","zh":"這個說法把需求上升與後來行為轉變連接起來。"},{"en":"Growing demand can push producers to increase output quickly.","zh":"需求增加可以推動生產者迅速增加產量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"work the land","meaning":"耕作土地","examples":[{"en":"Farmers began working the land all year round.","zh":"農民開始全年耕作土地。"},{"en":"To work the land means to farm it by planting, growing, and harvesting crops.","zh":"耕作土地是指透過種植、栽培和收割作物來使用土地。"},{"en":"Families worked the land to produce quinoa for sale.","zh":"一些家庭耕作土地，以生產藜麥出售。"},{"en":"Working the land too intensively can damage soil quality.","zh":"過度密集耕作土地會損害土壤質素。"},{"en":"Sustainable farming gives the land time to recover.","zh":"可持續農業會給土地恢復的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"all year round","meaning":"全年","examples":[{"en":"Farmers worked the land all year round to produce more quinoa.","zh":"農民全年耕作土地，以生產更多藜麥。"},{"en":"“All year round” means throughout the entire year without seasonal breaks.","zh":"「全年」表示整整一年都持續，沒有季節性休息。"},{"en":"The farm produced vegetables all year round.","zh":"該農場全年生產蔬菜。"},{"en":"Farming all year round can increase output but may exhaust the soil.","zh":"全年耕作可以增加產量，但也可能耗盡土壤。"},{"en":"Some crops and soils need rest periods rather than constant use.","zh":"有些作物和土壤需要休耕期，而不是持續使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了","examples":[{"en":"Farmers worked the land all year round in order to produce more quinoa.","zh":"農民全年耕作土地，為了生產更多藜麥。"},{"en":"“In order to” introduces the purpose of an action.","zh":"「為了」用來引入一項行動的目的。"},{"en":"Companies use influencers in order to increase sales.","zh":"公司使用網紅，為了提高銷量。"},{"en":"The phrase is slightly more formal than simply saying “to.”","zh":"英文“in order to”比單純使用“to”略為正式。"},{"en":"It helps explain why someone takes a particular action.","zh":"它幫助解釋某人為何採取特定行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"one issue has been that","meaning":"其中一個問題是","examples":[{"en":"One issue has been that the fertility of the soil decreased dramatically.","zh":"其中一個問題是土壤肥力大幅下降。"},{"en":"“One issue has been that” introduces one problem among several possible problems.","zh":"「其中一個問題是」用來引入多個可能問題中的一個。"},{"en":"One issue has been that farmers have had to work the land too often.","zh":"其中一個問題是農民不得不過度耕作土地。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reports when explaining consequences.","zh":"這個說法在報告中解釋後果時很有用。"},{"en":"It signals that the following point is a concern, not a benefit.","zh":"它表示接下來的重點是一項憂慮，而不是好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the fertility of the soil","meaning":"土壤肥力","examples":[{"en":"The fertility of the soil decreased dramatically.","zh":"土壤肥力大幅下降。"},{"en":"The fertility of the soil is its ability to support healthy plant growth.","zh":"土壤肥力是土壤支持植物健康生長的能力。"},{"en":"Farmers protect the fertility of the soil by rotating crops.","zh":"農民透過輪作保護土壤肥力。"},{"en":"Overuse of land can reduce soil fertility.","zh":"過度使用土地可以降低土壤肥力。"},{"en":"Healthy soil is essential for long-term food production.","zh":"健康土壤對長期食品生產至關重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"decreased dramatically","meaning":"大幅下降","examples":[{"en":"The fertility of the soil decreased dramatically.","zh":"土壤肥力大幅下降。"},{"en":"If something decreased dramatically, it fell greatly and noticeably.","zh":"某事大幅下降，是指它明顯而大量減少。"},{"en":"Soil quality decreased dramatically after years of overuse.","zh":"經過多年過度使用後，土壤質素大幅下降。"},{"en":"A dramatic decrease can create serious long-term problems.","zh":"大幅下降可以造成嚴重長期問題。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises both the size and seriousness of the fall.","zh":"這個說法強調下降幅度和嚴重性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"could potentially lead to","meaning":"可能導致","examples":[{"en":"Poor soil fertility could potentially lead to desertification.","zh":"土壤肥力差可能導致沙漠化。"},{"en":"“Could potentially lead to” means may possibly cause a later result.","zh":"「可能導致」表示可能造成之後的結果。"},{"en":"Overfarming could potentially lead to serious environmental damage.","zh":"過度耕作可能導致嚴重環境損害。"},{"en":"The phrase is cautious because the result is possible rather than certain.","zh":"這個說法較謹慎，因為結果是可能發生而非必然。"},{"en":"It is often used when discussing risks.","zh":"它常用於討論風險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"desertification","meaning":"沙漠化","examples":[{"en":"Overuse of the land could lead to desertification in some areas.","zh":"過度使用土地可能在某些地區導致沙漠化。"},{"en":"Desertification is the process by which fertile land becomes dry, degraded, and desert-like.","zh":"沙漠化是肥沃土地變得乾旱、退化並像沙漠的過程。"},{"en":"Poor farming practices can contribute to desertification.","zh":"不良農業做法可能促成沙漠化。"},{"en":"Desertification reduces the land’s ability to support crops and communities.","zh":"沙漠化會降低土地支持作物和社區的能力。"},{"en":"Preventing desertification requires careful land and water management.","zh":"防止沙漠化需要謹慎管理土地和水資源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in some areas","meaning":"在某些地區","examples":[{"en":"Desertification could occur in some areas.","zh":"沙漠化可能在某些地區發生。"},{"en":"“In some areas” means in certain places, but not everywhere.","zh":"「在某些地區」表示在某些地方，但不是所有地方。"},{"en":"Soil quality fell sharply in some areas.","zh":"在某些地區，土壤質素急劇下降。"},{"en":"Problems may appear in some areas before they spread more widely.","zh":"問題可能先在某些地區出現，然後才更廣泛擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase limits a statement to particular locations.","zh":"這個說法把陳述限制於特定地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"developing food trends","meaning":"發展中的食品潮流","examples":[{"en":"The question sheet focuses on developing food trends.","zh":"問題紙集中於發展中的食品潮流。"},{"en":"Developing food trends are food fashions that are emerging or still growing.","zh":"發展中的食品潮流是正在出現或仍在增長的食品潮流。"},{"en":"Supermarkets study developing food trends before deciding what to stock.","zh":"超級市場會在決定入貨前研究發展中的食品潮流。"},{"en":"Developing trends may become major markets or disappear quickly.","zh":"發展中的潮流可能成為大型市場，也可能迅速消失。"},{"en":"Tracking developing food trends helps companies plan future products.","zh":"追蹤發展中的食品潮流可以幫助公司規劃未來產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the growth in interest","meaning":"興趣的增長","examples":[{"en":"The growth in interest in food fashions started with photos shared online.","zh":"對食品潮流興趣的增長由網上分享食物照片開始。"},{"en":"The growth in interest means an increase in people’s attention or curiosity.","zh":"興趣的增長是指人們的關注或好奇增加。"},{"en":"The growth in interest in oat milk followed its appearance in cafés.","zh":"對燕麥奶興趣的增長出現在它進入咖啡店之後。"},{"en":"Growth in interest can lead to higher demand and more products.","zh":"興趣增長可以帶來更高需求和更多產品。"},{"en":"Public interest often grows when people see attractive images repeatedly.","zh":"當人們反覆看見吸引人的影像，公眾興趣通常會增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"started with","meaning":"由……開始","examples":[{"en":"The growth in interest started with food photos on social media.","zh":"興趣的增長由社交媒體上的食物照片開始。"},{"en":"“Started with” means began from a particular action, event, or cause.","zh":"「由……開始」表示從某項行動、事件或原因開始。"},{"en":"The campaign started with a small group of journalists.","zh":"該活動由一小組記者開始。"},{"en":"A major food trend may start with a simple online post.","zh":"重大食品潮流可能由一篇簡單網上貼文開始。"},{"en":"The phrase helps identify the beginning of a process.","zh":"這個說法有助指出一個過程的起點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"shared on social media","meaning":"在社交媒體上分享","examples":[{"en":"Photos of food were shared on social media.","zh":"食物照片在社交媒體上被分享。"},{"en":"Shared on social media means posted or circulated through online platforms.","zh":"在社交媒體上分享，是指透過網上平台發佈或傳播。"},{"en":"The dessert became famous after photos were shared on social media.","zh":"那款甜品的照片在社交媒體上分享後變得有名。"},{"en":"Food images shared online can influence what people want to eat.","zh":"網上分享的食物影像可以影響人們想吃甚麼。"},{"en":"Social media sharing can turn a local product into a global trend.","zh":"社交媒體分享可以把本地產品變成全球潮流。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"constantly developing products","meaning":"不斷開發產品","examples":[{"en":"The UK food industry is constantly developing products which are new or different.","zh":"英國食品業不斷開發新穎或與別不同的產品。"},{"en":"Constantly developing products means continually creating or improving goods for the market.","zh":"不斷開發產品，是指持續創造或改良市場商品。"},{"en":"Food companies are constantly developing products to match new tastes.","zh":"食品公司不斷開發產品，以配合新口味。"},{"en":"Constant product development helps companies stay competitive.","zh":"持續產品開發有助公司保持競爭力。"},{"en":"Developing too many new products can also create waste or confusion.","zh":"開發太多新產品也可能造成浪費或混亂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"new or different","meaning":"新穎或與別不同的","examples":[{"en":"The industry develops products which are new or different.","zh":"食品業開發新穎或與別不同的產品。"},{"en":"“New or different” means not previously available or not the same as existing options.","zh":"「新穎或與別不同」表示以前沒有或與現有選項不同。"},{"en":"Consumers often notice products that look new or different.","zh":"消費者通常會注意看起來新穎或與別不同的產品。"},{"en":"A product can be different because of ingredients, packaging, taste, or story.","zh":"產品可以因食材、包裝、味道或故事而與別不同。"},{"en":"New or different products still need quality and usefulness to succeed.","zh":"新穎或與別不同的產品仍需要質素和實用性才能成功。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"track demand for ingredients","meaning":"追蹤對食材的需求","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets track demand for ingredients on social media.","zh":"超級市場在社交媒體上追蹤對食材的需求。"},{"en":"To track demand for ingredients means to monitor how much people want particular food components.","zh":"追蹤對食材的需求，是指監察人們對特定食物成分的需求有多大。"},{"en":"Supermarkets track demand for ingredients such as oats, avocado, and quinoa.","zh":"超級市場追蹤對燕麥、牛油果和藜麥等食材的需求。"},{"en":"Tracking demand helps retailers decide what to stock.","zh":"追蹤需求幫助零售商決定入貨甚麼。"},{"en":"Demand signals can come from searches, posts, recipes, and restaurant menus.","zh":"需求訊號可以來自搜尋、貼文、食譜和餐廳餐牌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"are influential","meaning":"有影響力","examples":[{"en":"Famous chefs are influential in creating food trends.","zh":"名廚在創造食品潮流方面很有影響力。"},{"en":"If people are influential, they can affect others’ ideas, choices, or behaviour.","zh":"有影響力的人可以影響他人的想法、選擇或行為。"},{"en":"Social media influencers are influential among younger consumers.","zh":"社交媒體網紅在年輕消費者中很有影響力。"},{"en":"Influential chefs can make a little-known ingredient fashionable.","zh":"有影響力的廚師可以令不知名食材變得流行。"},{"en":"Being influential carries responsibility because others may copy your choices.","zh":"有影響力也帶來責任，因為其他人可能模仿你的選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"invited to visit growers","meaning":"受邀探訪種植者","examples":[{"en":"Journalists were invited to visit growers in South Africa.","zh":"記者受邀探訪南非的種植者。"},{"en":"To be invited to visit growers means to be asked to go and meet people who grow crops.","zh":"受邀探訪種植者，是指被邀請去會見種植作物的人。"},{"en":"Food writers were invited to visit growers during the harvest season.","zh":"食品撰稿人在收成季節受邀探訪種植者。"},{"en":"Visiting growers can help journalists understand the origin of a product.","zh":"探訪種植者可以幫助記者了解產品來源。"},{"en":"Such visits may be educational, but they can also be part of marketing.","zh":"這類探訪可以具教育意義，但也可能是市場推廣的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"growers","meaning":"種植者","examples":[{"en":"The journalists visited avocado growers in South Africa.","zh":"記者探訪了南非的牛油果種植者。"},{"en":"Growers are people or businesses that cultivate crops for sale.","zh":"種植者是種植作物以出售的人或企業。"},{"en":"Avocado growers explained how climate affects their harvests.","zh":"牛油果種植者解釋氣候如何影響收成。"},{"en":"Growers may benefit when demand for their crop increases.","zh":"當作物需求增加，種植者可能受益。"},{"en":"They also face risks from weather, pests, and changing market prices.","zh":"他們也面對天氣、害蟲和市場價格變化的風險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"advertising focused on","meaning":"廣告集中於……","examples":[{"en":"Advertising focused on the health benefits of avocados.","zh":"廣告集中於牛油果的健康益處。"},{"en":"If advertising focuses on something, it gives that point special attention.","zh":"廣告集中於某事，是指特別強調該點。"},{"en":"The campaign focused on the environmental benefits of oat milk.","zh":"該活動集中於燕麥奶的環境益處。"},{"en":"Advertising often focuses on the feature most likely to persuade consumers.","zh":"廣告通常集中於最可能說服消費者的特色。"},{"en":"A narrow focus can be powerful, but it may leave out important information.","zh":"集中於單一重點可以很有力，但也可能忽略重要資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"health benefits","meaning":"健康益處","examples":[{"en":"The campaign highlighted the health benefits of avocados.","zh":"該活動突出了牛油果的健康益處。"},{"en":"Health benefits are positive effects on the body or wellbeing.","zh":"健康益處是對身體或身心健康的正面影響。"},{"en":"The health benefits of a food should be explained accurately.","zh":"食品的健康益處應被準確解釋。"},{"en":"Consumers may buy a product because they believe it offers health benefits.","zh":"消費者可能因相信產品有健康益處而購買。"},{"en":"Health benefits should be considered as part of an overall diet, not in isolation.","zh":"健康益處應作為整體飲食的一部分考慮，而不是孤立看待。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"received publicity by","meaning":"透過……獲得宣傳曝光","examples":[{"en":"The media campaign received publicity by upsetting competitors.","zh":"該媒體宣傳活動透過令競爭對手不滿而獲得宣傳曝光。"},{"en":"To receive publicity by doing something means to gain public attention through that action.","zh":"透過做某事獲得宣傳曝光，是指因該行動而得到公眾關注。"},{"en":"The brand received publicity by challenging traditional milk producers.","zh":"該品牌透過挑戰傳統牛奶生產者而獲得宣傳。"},{"en":"Controversial actions can receive publicity quickly.","zh":"具爭議行動可以迅速獲得宣傳曝光。"},{"en":"Publicity gained this way may be useful but can also damage relationships.","zh":"以這種方式獲得的曝光可能有用，但也可能損害關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"upsetting competitors","meaning":"令競爭對手不滿","examples":[{"en":"The campaign gained attention by upsetting competitors.","zh":"該活動透過令競爭對手不滿而獲得關注。"},{"en":"Upsetting competitors means making rival companies angry, annoyed, or worried.","zh":"令競爭對手不滿，是指令競爭公司生氣、不快或擔心。"},{"en":"The slogan upset competitors in the dairy industry.","zh":"這句口號令乳製品行業的競爭對手不滿。"},{"en":"Upsetting competitors can make a campaign seem bold and newsworthy.","zh":"令競爭對手不滿可以令活動顯得大膽並具新聞價值。"},{"en":"However, it may also lead to complaints or negative publicity.","zh":"然而，這也可能導致投訴或負面宣傳。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"promotion through","meaning":"透過……推廣","examples":[{"en":"Promotion through coffee shops reduced the need for advertising.","zh":"透過咖啡店推廣減少了對廣告的需要。"},{"en":"Promotion through something means using that channel or place to advertise or spread a product.","zh":"透過某渠道推廣，是指使用該渠道或地方宣傳或傳播產品。"},{"en":"Promotion through influencers helped the vegan brand grow.","zh":"透過網紅推廣幫助純素品牌成長。"},{"en":"Coffee shops can promote oat milk by serving it in popular drinks.","zh":"咖啡店可以透過在受歡迎飲品中使用燕麥奶來推廣它。"},{"en":"Promotion through trusted locations may feel more natural than direct advertising.","zh":"透過受信任地點推廣，可能比直接廣告更自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reduced the need for","meaning":"減少對……的需要","examples":[{"en":"Promotion through coffee shops reduced the need for advertising.","zh":"透過咖啡店推廣減少了對廣告的需要。"},{"en":"To reduce the need for something means to make it less necessary.","zh":"減少對某事的需要，是指令它變得較不必要。"},{"en":"Word of mouth reduced the need for expensive posters.","zh":"口碑減少了對昂貴海報的需要。"},{"en":"A strong distribution strategy can reduce the need for a large media campaign.","zh":"強大的分銷策略可以減少對大型媒體活動的需要。"},{"en":"Reducing the need for advertising can save money.","zh":"減少對廣告的需要可以節省金錢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"appealed to consumers","meaning":"吸引消費者","examples":[{"en":"Oat milk appealed to consumers who were concerned about the environment.","zh":"燕麥奶吸引了關注環境的消費者。"},{"en":"To appeal to consumers means to attract or interest people who might buy a product.","zh":"吸引消費者是指引起可能購買產品的人興趣。"},{"en":"The low price appealed to students.","zh":"低價格吸引了學生。"},{"en":"Environmental benefits can appeal to consumers who want ethical choices.","zh":"環境益處可以吸引想作出合乎倫理選擇的消費者。"},{"en":"A product may appeal to different consumers for different reasons.","zh":"一件產品可能因不同原因吸引不同消費者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"concerned about","meaning":"關注……","examples":[{"en":"Many consumers are concerned about the environment.","zh":"許多消費者關注環境。"},{"en":"To be concerned about something means to be worried about it or care seriously about it.","zh":"關注某事是指擔心它或認真在意它。"},{"en":"Shoppers are increasingly concerned about plastic waste.","zh":"購物者越來越關注塑膠廢物。"},{"en":"Consumers concerned about climate change may choose lower-impact foods.","zh":"關注氣候變化的消費者可能選擇影響較低的食品。"},{"en":"Concern can influence buying habits when better options are available.","zh":"當有更好選項時，關注可以影響購買習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"strengthen the reputation of","meaning":"加強……的聲譽","examples":[{"en":"Skrei helped strengthen the reputation of Norwegian seafood.","zh":"Skrei魚幫助加強挪威海鮮的聲譽。"},{"en":"To strengthen the reputation of something means to make people respect or trust it more.","zh":"加強某事的聲譽，是指令人們更尊重或信任它。"},{"en":"A successful campaign strengthened the reputation of the local farming region.","zh":"一項成功活動加強了本地農業地區的聲譽。"},{"en":"Quality products can strengthen the reputation of an entire industry.","zh":"優質產品可以加強整個行業的聲譽。"},{"en":"Reputation grows stronger when positive experiences are repeated.","zh":"當正面經驗反覆出現，聲譽會變得更強。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"led to an increase in","meaning":"導致……增加","examples":[{"en":"The success of quinoa led to an increase in its price.","zh":"藜麥的成功導致其價格上升。"},{"en":"“Led to an increase in” means caused something to rise.","zh":"「導致……增加」表示造成某事上升。"},{"en":"The campaign led to an increase in avocado sales.","zh":"該活動導致牛油果銷量增加。"},{"en":"Increased demand often leads to higher prices when supply is limited.","zh":"當供應有限，需求增加通常會導致價格上升。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a cause-and-effect relationship.","zh":"這個說法解釋因果關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"overuse of resources","meaning":"過度使用資源","examples":[{"en":"Overuse of resources resulted in poor-quality soil.","zh":"過度使用資源導致土壤質素差。"},{"en":"Overuse of resources means using land, water, soil, or other materials too much or too quickly.","zh":"過度使用資源是指過量或過快使用土地、水、土壤或其他材料。"},{"en":"Overuse of water can harm farming communities.","zh":"過度用水會傷害農業社區。"},{"en":"A food trend may cause overuse of resources if producers rush to meet demand.","zh":"如果生產者急於滿足需求，食品潮流可能造成資源過度使用。"},{"en":"Sustainable production tries to prevent overuse of natural resources.","zh":"可持續生產嘗試防止自然資源被過度使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"resulted in","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"Overuse of resources resulted in poor-quality soil.","zh":"過度使用資源導致土壤質素差。"},{"en":"“Resulted in” means caused or produced a particular outcome.","zh":"「導致」表示造成或產生某個結果。"},{"en":"Heavy demand resulted in higher prices.","zh":"強烈需求導致價格上升。"},{"en":"Working the land all year round resulted in lower soil fertility.","zh":"全年耕作土地導致土壤肥力下降。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful for explaining consequences.","zh":"這個說法適合用來解釋後果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"poor-quality soil","meaning":"質素差的土壤","examples":[{"en":"Overuse of resources resulted in poor-quality soil.","zh":"過度使用資源導致土壤質素差。"},{"en":"Poor-quality soil is soil that lacks the nutrients or structure needed for healthy crops.","zh":"質素差的土壤是缺乏健康作物所需營養或結構的土壤。"},{"en":"Poor-quality soil can reduce harvests and increase farmers’ costs.","zh":"質素差的土壤可以減少收成並增加農民成本。"},{"en":"Overfarming may turn fertile land into poor-quality soil.","zh":"過度耕作可能把肥沃土地變成質素差的土壤。"},{"en":"Resting the land and improving farming methods can help restore soil quality.","zh":"讓土地休息和改善耕作方法可以幫助恢復土壤質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 2 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/listening/Practice 20/task-1":[{"front":"phone if","meaning":"如果……就致電","examples":[{"en":"William said Amber could phone if she wanted more information.","zh":"William 說，如果 Amber 想了解更多資料，可以致電。"},{"en":"To phone if something happens means to call someone in that situation.","zh":"phone if something happens 指在某情況出現時致電某人。"},{"en":"You can phone if you need help with the application form.","zh":"如果你需要申請表方面的幫助，可以致電。"},{"en":"If Amber has questions, phoning Becky may be quicker than sending an email.","zh":"如果 Amber 有問題，致電 Becky 可能比發電郵更快。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a condition for making a call.","zh":"這個短語引出致電的條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get more information about","meaning":"了解更多關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"Amber wants to get more information about the job agency.","zh":"Amber 想了解更多關於職業介紹所的資料。"},{"en":"To get more information about something means to learn extra details about it.","zh":"get more information about something 指了解某事的更多細節。"},{"en":"Students can visit the website to get more information about the course.","zh":"學生可以瀏覽網站，以了解更多關於課程的資料。"},{"en":"If Amber gets more information about the agency, she can decide whether to register.","zh":"如果 Amber 了解更多關於介紹所的資料，她就能決定是否登記。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding out further details.","zh":"這個短語描述查找進一步資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"job agency","meaning":"職業介紹所","examples":[{"en":"William told Amber about a job agency called Bankside.","zh":"William 向 Amber 提到一間名為 Bankside 的職業介紹所。"},{"en":"A job agency is a company that helps people find work and helps employers find staff.","zh":"job agency 指幫助求職者找工作，也幫僱主找員工的公司。"},{"en":"A job agency may arrange interviews for people looking for temporary office work.","zh":"職業介紹所可能為尋找臨時辦公室工作的人安排面試。"},{"en":"If someone lacks contacts, a job agency can help them find suitable opportunities.","zh":"如果某人缺乏人脈，職業介紹所可以幫他找到合適機會。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an employment service.","zh":"這個短語指就業服務機構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mention","meaning":"提到","examples":[{"en":"William mentioned the job agency to Amber earlier.","zh":"William 早前向 Amber 提到那間職業介紹所。"},{"en":"To mention something means to refer to it briefly in speech or writing.","zh":"mention something 指在說話或寫作中簡略提及某事。"},{"en":"The teacher mentioned the deadline at the end of the lesson.","zh":"老師在課堂結束時提到截止日期。"},{"en":"If William mentions an agency, Amber may ask for more details later.","zh":"如果 William 提到一間介紹所，Amber 之後可能會問更多細節。"},{"en":"This word describes bringing up a topic briefly.","zh":"這個字描述簡短帶出一個話題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"is now a good time?","meaning":"現在方便嗎？","examples":[{"en":"Amber asks William whether now is a good time to talk.","zh":"Amber 問 William 現在是否方便談話。"},{"en":"Is now a good time? is a polite way to ask whether someone is available.","zh":"is now a good time? 是禮貌地詢問某人是否有空的說法。"},{"en":"Before asking for advice, she said, “Is now a good time?”","zh":"在尋求建議前，她說：「現在方便嗎？」"},{"en":"If someone is busy, asking this question shows respect for their time.","zh":"如果對方很忙，問這個問題能顯示尊重對方時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for starting a conversation politely.","zh":"這個短語適合用來禮貌地開始對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"talk about","meaning":"談到","examples":[{"en":"William talks about a job agency called Bankside.","zh":"William 談到一間名為 Bankside 的職業介紹所。"},{"en":"To talk about something means to discuss or explain it.","zh":"talk about something 指討論或解釋某事。"},{"en":"The careers adviser talked about summer jobs during assembly.","zh":"職業顧問在早會中談到暑期工作。"},{"en":"If William talks about the agency, Amber can learn whether it suits her needs.","zh":"如果 William 談到那間介紹所，Amber 就能了解它是否適合自己需要。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the subject of a conversation.","zh":"這個短語引出對話主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be based in","meaning":"位於；總部設於","examples":[{"en":"The agency is based in Docklands.","zh":"這間介紹所位於 Docklands。"},{"en":"To be based in a place means to have the main office or main operations there.","zh":"be based in a place 指主要辦公室或主要營運設於某地。"},{"en":"The charity is based in London but works across the country.","zh":"這間慈善機構總部設於倫敦，但在全國工作。"},{"en":"If the agency is based nearby, Amber may find it easier to attend an interview.","zh":"如果介紹所位於附近，Amber 可能較容易出席面試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location or headquarters.","zh":"這個短語描述地點或總部位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tell you the address","meaning":"告訴你地址","examples":[{"en":"William tells Amber the address of the agency.","zh":"William 告訴 Amber 介紹所的地址。"},{"en":"To tell you the address means to give you the exact location of a place.","zh":"tell you the address 指告訴你某地方的確實位置。"},{"en":"The receptionist told me the address of the training centre.","zh":"接待員告訴我培訓中心的地址。"},{"en":"If Amber knows the address, she can plan how to get there.","zh":"如果 Amber 知道地址，就可以計劃如何前往。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sharing location details.","zh":"這個短語描述分享地點資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"anyone in particular","meaning":"某個特定的人","examples":[{"en":"Amber asks whether there is anyone in particular she should speak to.","zh":"Amber 問是否有某個特定的人她應該聯絡。"},{"en":"Anyone in particular means a specific person rather than just anyone.","zh":"anyone in particular 指某個特定的人，而不是隨便任何人。"},{"en":"The visitor asked if there was anyone in particular he should contact about the course.","zh":"訪客問是否有某個特定的人可以聯絡查詢課程。"},{"en":"If Amber speaks to the right person, she may get more useful advice.","zh":"如果 Amber 與正確的人交談，可能得到更有用的建議。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether a specific person is recommended.","zh":"這個短語用來詢問是否推薦某個指定人士。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"speak to","meaning":"與……交談","examples":[{"en":"Amber wants to know who she should speak to at the agency.","zh":"Amber 想知道她應該與介紹所的誰交談。"},{"en":"To speak to someone means to talk with that person.","zh":"speak to someone 指與某人談話。"},{"en":"The student asked to speak to the careers adviser after class.","zh":"學生課後要求與職業顧問交談。"},{"en":"If Amber speaks to an experienced agent, she can ask practical questions.","zh":"如果 Amber 與有經驗的職業代理交談，就可以問實際問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct communication.","zh":"這個短語描述直接溝通。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"deal with","meaning":"與……打交道；聯絡","examples":[{"en":"William always deals with an agent called Becky Jamieson.","zh":"William 一直與一名叫 Becky Jamieson 的代理聯絡。"},{"en":"To deal with someone means to communicate or work with that person regularly.","zh":"deal with someone 指經常與某人溝通或合作。"},{"en":"The school usually deals with the same travel agent for trips.","zh":"學校通常與同一位旅行代理聯絡安排旅行。"},{"en":"If William always deals with Becky, he probably trusts her service.","zh":"如果 William 一直與 Becky 打交道，他大概信任她的服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regular contact or business interaction.","zh":"這個短語描述固定聯絡或業務互動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"let me write that down","meaning":"讓我記下來","examples":[{"en":"Amber says, “Let me write that down,” when William gives the name.","zh":"William 給出名字時，Amber 說：「讓我記下來。」"},{"en":"Let me write that down means allow me to record that information so I do not forget it.","zh":"let me write that down 指讓我把資料記下，以免忘記。"},{"en":"When the teacher gave the room number, a student said, “Let me write that down.”","zh":"老師給出房號時，一名學生說：「讓我記下來。」"},{"en":"If Amber writes the name down, she is less likely to spell it wrongly later.","zh":"如果 Amber 把名字記下，之後較不容易拼錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when receiving useful details.","zh":"這個短語常用於接收有用細節時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"direct line","meaning":"直線電話","examples":[{"en":"Amber asks whether William has Becky’s direct line.","zh":"Amber 問 William 是否有 Becky 的直線電話。"},{"en":"A direct line is a phone number that reaches a person directly rather than through a general switchboard.","zh":"direct line 指能直接聯絡某人的電話號碼，而不是總機號碼。"},{"en":"The manager gave me her direct line so I could contact her quickly.","zh":"經理給了我她的直線電話，讓我可以快速聯絡她。"},{"en":"If Amber has Becky’s direct line, she may not need to go through reception.","zh":"如果 Amber 有 Becky 的直線電話，就可能不用經過接待處。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a direct telephone contact.","zh":"這個短語指直接電話聯絡方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in my contacts","meaning":"在我的聯絡人中","examples":[{"en":"William has Becky’s phone number in his contacts.","zh":"William 的聯絡人中有 Becky 的電話號碼。"},{"en":"In my contacts means saved in the contact list on a phone or device.","zh":"in my contacts 指儲存在手機或裝置的聯絡人清單中。"},{"en":"I have the tutor’s email address in my contacts.","zh":"我的聯絡人中有導師的電郵地址。"},{"en":"If William has the number in his contacts, he can find it quickly.","zh":"如果 William 的聯絡人中有該號碼，他就能很快找到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stored contact information.","zh":"這個短語描述已儲存的聯絡資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"here we are","meaning":"找到了","examples":[{"en":"William finds the number and says, “Here we are.”","zh":"William 找到號碼後說：「找到了。」"},{"en":"Here we are is used when someone finds or reaches what they were looking for.","zh":"here we are 用於某人找到或到達正在尋找的東西時。"},{"en":"After searching his bag, he found the ticket and said, “Here we are.”","zh":"他翻找書包後找到門票，說：「找到了。」"},{"en":"If William says this, it means he has found Becky’s number.","zh":"如果 William 這樣說，即表示他已找到 Becky 的號碼。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when presenting something found.","zh":"這個短語常用於展示找到的東西時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"double six","meaning":"兩個六","examples":[{"en":"William says “double six” when giving Becky’s phone number.","zh":"William 讀 Becky 的電話號碼時說「兩個六」。"},{"en":"Double six means two sixes together in a number.","zh":"double six 指號碼中連續兩個六。"},{"en":"A phone number containing 66 may be read aloud as “double six.”","zh":"含有66的電話號碼可以讀作 double six。"},{"en":"Saying double six makes the number easier to hear and remember.","zh":"說 double six 令號碼更容易聽清和記住。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when reading numbers aloud.","zh":"這個短語用於朗讀數字。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"triple three","meaning":"三個三","examples":[{"en":"William says “triple three” when giving Becky’s phone number.","zh":"William 讀 Becky 的電話號碼時說「三個三」。"},{"en":"Triple three means three threes together in a number.","zh":"triple three 指號碼中連續三個三。"},{"en":"A number ending in 333 may be read aloud as “triple three.”","zh":"以333結尾的號碼可以讀作 triple three。"},{"en":"If a number has repeated digits, saying triple three can reduce mistakes.","zh":"如果號碼有重複數字，說 triple three 可以減少錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for giving phone numbers clearly.","zh":"這個短語適合用來清楚提供電話號碼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"if I were you","meaning":"如果我是你","examples":[{"en":"William says he would call Becky in the afternoon if he were Amber.","zh":"William 說如果他是 Amber，就會下午打電話給 Becky。"},{"en":"If I were you is used to give advice by imagining oneself in another person’s situation.","zh":"if I were you 用來透過想像自己處於對方情況來提出建議。"},{"en":"If I were you, I would prepare a short CV before calling the agency.","zh":"如果我是你，我會先準備一份簡短履歷再致電介紹所。"},{"en":"This phrase makes advice sound personal but still polite.","zh":"這個短語令建議聽起來個人化但仍然有禮。"},{"en":"It is often followed by “I would” and a suggested action.","zh":"它常接 I would 和建議行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"last-minute vacancies","meaning":"臨時職位空缺","examples":[{"en":"Becky is busy in the morning trying to fill last-minute vacancies.","zh":"Becky 早上忙於嘗試填補臨時職位空缺。"},{"en":"Last-minute vacancies are job openings that appear suddenly and need to be filled quickly.","zh":"last-minute vacancies 指突然出現並需要快速填補的職位空缺。"},{"en":"The hotel had several last-minute vacancies after staff called in sick.","zh":"酒店有員工請病假後，出現幾個臨時職位空缺。"},{"en":"If an agency handles last-minute vacancies, mornings can be very busy.","zh":"如果介紹所處理臨時職位空缺，早上可能非常繁忙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes urgent job openings.","zh":"這個短語描述緊急職位空缺。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fill vacancies","meaning":"填補職位空缺","examples":[{"en":"Becky tries to fill last-minute vacancies in the morning.","zh":"Becky 早上嘗試填補臨時職位空缺。"},{"en":"To fill vacancies means to find people to take available jobs or positions.","zh":"fill vacancies 指找人擔任空缺職位。"},{"en":"The school used an agency to fill teaching vacancies before term began.","zh":"學校在學期開始前使用介紹所填補教師空缺。"},{"en":"If vacancies are filled quickly, companies can continue operating smoothly.","zh":"如果職位空缺能快速填補，公司就能順利繼續運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recruiting people for open posts.","zh":"這個短語描述招聘人手填補空缺。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"really helpful and friendly","meaning":"很樂意幫忙而且友善","examples":[{"en":"Becky is really helpful and friendly.","zh":"Becky 很樂意幫忙而且友善。"},{"en":"Really helpful and friendly means very willing to assist and pleasant to talk to.","zh":"really helpful and friendly 指非常願意協助，而且容易相處。"},{"en":"The receptionist was really helpful and friendly when I asked for directions.","zh":"我問路時，接待員很樂意幫忙而且友善。"},{"en":"If an agent is helpful and friendly, new candidates may feel less nervous.","zh":"如果代理樂意幫忙又友善，新應徵者可能較不緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase gives strong positive praise for someone’s manner.","zh":"這個短語強烈稱讚某人的態度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be worth getting in touch with","meaning":"值得聯絡","examples":[{"en":"William says it would be worth getting in touch with Becky.","zh":"William 說值得聯絡 Becky。"},{"en":"To be worth getting in touch with someone means contacting that person is likely to be useful.","zh":"be worth getting in touch with someone 指聯絡某人很可能有用。"},{"en":"It is worth getting in touch with the careers adviser before applying.","zh":"申請前值得聯絡職業顧問。"},{"en":"If Becky can offer suitable temporary work, she is worth contacting.","zh":"如果 Becky 能提供合適臨時工作，她就值得聯絡。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a useful action.","zh":"這個短語提出有用的行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"get in touch with","meaning":"聯絡","examples":[{"en":"Amber should get in touch with Becky for an informal chat.","zh":"Amber 應聯絡 Becky，進行一次非正式傾談。"},{"en":"To get in touch with someone means to contact them.","zh":"get in touch with someone 指聯絡某人。"},{"en":"Students should get in touch with the office if they lose their ID cards.","zh":"如果學生遺失身份證，應聯絡辦公室。"},{"en":"If Amber gets in touch with Becky, she can ask about possible jobs.","zh":"如果 Amber 聯絡 Becky，就可以詢問可能的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in spoken and written English.","zh":"這個短語常見於英語口語和書面語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"informal chat","meaning":"非正式傾談","examples":[{"en":"Amber can contact Becky for an informal chat.","zh":"Amber 可以聯絡 Becky 進行非正式傾談。"},{"en":"An informal chat is a relaxed conversation rather than an official interview.","zh":"informal chat 指輕鬆談話，而不是正式面試。"},{"en":"The tutor had an informal chat with the student about university choices.","zh":"導師與學生就大學選擇進行了一次非正式傾談。"},{"en":"If Amber has an informal chat first, she may feel more confident later.","zh":"如果 Amber 先進行非正式傾談，之後可能更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a friendly and low-pressure conversation.","zh":"這個短語描述友善而低壓力的對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"clerical and admin jobs","meaning":"文書及行政工作","examples":[{"en":"The agency mainly deals with clerical and admin jobs.","zh":"這間介紹所主要處理文書及行政工作。"},{"en":"Clerical and admin jobs involve office tasks such as filing, answering phones, organising records, and supporting staff.","zh":"clerical and admin jobs 涉及歸檔、接聽電話、整理紀錄和支援員工等辦公室任務。"},{"en":"Many students start with clerical and admin jobs to gain office experience.","zh":"許多學生先從文書及行政工作開始，以累積辦公室經驗。"},{"en":"If Amber wants office work, clerical and admin jobs may be a good starting point.","zh":"如果 Amber 想做辦公室工作，文書及行政工作可能是不錯起點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes general office support roles.","zh":"這個短語描述一般辦公室支援職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"deal with","meaning":"處理；負責","examples":[{"en":"The agency deals mainly with temporary office jobs.","zh":"這間介紹所主要處理臨時辦公室工作。"},{"en":"To deal with a type of work means to handle, arrange, or specialise in it.","zh":"deal with a type of work 指處理、安排或專門負責某類工作。"},{"en":"This agency deals with teaching jobs, while another one deals with healthcare work.","zh":"這間介紹所處理教學工作，而另一間負責醫療工作。"},{"en":"If Bankside deals with temporary office jobs, Amber should expect short-term placements.","zh":"如果 Bankside 處理臨時辦公室工作，Amber 應預期短期職位安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the area a company handles.","zh":"這個短語描述公司負責的範疇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"that’s right","meaning":"沒錯","examples":[{"en":"William says, “That’s right,” when Amber asks about clerical work.","zh":"Amber 問到文書工作時，William 說：「沒錯。」"},{"en":"That’s right means yes, that is correct.","zh":"that’s right 指是的，正確。"},{"en":"When the student checked the room number, the teacher said, “That’s right.”","zh":"學生確認房號時，老師說：「沒錯。」"},{"en":"This phrase confirms that someone has understood correctly.","zh":"這個短語確認對方理解正確。"},{"en":"It is common in conversation and sounds natural.","zh":"它常見於對話中，語氣自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hope to find","meaning":"希望找到","examples":[{"en":"Amber hopes to find a full-time job in the media.","zh":"Amber 希望找到一份傳媒行業的全職工作。"},{"en":"To hope to find something means to want and expect that you may discover or obtain it.","zh":"hope to find something 指希望並期待可以發現或得到某物。"},{"en":"Many graduates hope to find work related to their studies.","zh":"許多畢業生希望找到與所學相關的工作。"},{"en":"If Amber hopes to find media work, temporary office jobs may still help her CV.","zh":"如果 Amber 希望找到傳媒工作，臨時辦公室工作仍可能幫助她的履歷。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a future aim.","zh":"這個短語表達未來目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"full-time job","meaning":"全職工作","examples":[{"en":"Amber hopes to find a full-time job eventually.","zh":"Amber 最終希望找到一份全職工作。"},{"en":"A full-time job is a job with regular working hours, usually close to a full working week.","zh":"full-time job 指有固定工作時間、通常接近完整工作週的工作。"},{"en":"After graduation, he looked for a full-time job in marketing.","zh":"畢業後，他尋找市場營銷方面的全職工作。"},{"en":"If Amber gets a full-time job, she may have more stable income than with temporary work.","zh":"如果 Amber 找到全職工作，收入可能比臨時工作更穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with part-time or temporary work.","zh":"這個短語與兼職或臨時工作作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the media","meaning":"在傳媒行業","examples":[{"en":"Amber wants to work in the media eventually.","zh":"Amber 最終想在傳媒行業工作。"},{"en":"In the media means in industries such as television, radio, journalism, publishing, or digital content.","zh":"in the media 指在電視、電台、新聞、出版或數碼內容等行業。"},{"en":"Many people in the media need strong writing and communication skills.","zh":"許多在傳媒行業工作的人需要良好寫作和溝通能力。"},{"en":"If Amber wants to work in the media, office experience may still be useful.","zh":"如果 Amber 想在傳媒行業工作，辦公室經驗仍可能有用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the media industry.","zh":"這個短語指傳媒產業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"eventually","meaning":"最終","examples":[{"en":"Amber hopes to find a full-time media job eventually.","zh":"Amber 最終希望找到一份傳媒全職工作。"},{"en":"Eventually means in the end or after some time has passed.","zh":"eventually 指最後，或經過一段時間後。"},{"en":"She started as an assistant and eventually became a producer.","zh":"她最初做助理，最終成為製作人。"},{"en":"If Amber gains temporary experience now, she may eventually reach her career goal.","zh":"如果 Amber 現在累積臨時工作經驗，最終可能達到職業目標。"},{"en":"This word points to a later result.","zh":"這個字指較後出現的結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"recruit temporary staff","meaning":"招聘臨時職員","examples":[{"en":"Becky mostly recruits temporary staff for the finance sector.","zh":"Becky 主要為金融業招聘臨時職員。"},{"en":"To recruit temporary staff means to find and hire workers for short-term jobs.","zh":"recruit temporary staff 指尋找並聘請短期工作員工。"},{"en":"Shops recruit temporary staff before the Christmas rush.","zh":"商店在聖誕繁忙期前招聘臨時職員。"},{"en":"If Becky recruits temporary staff, she needs candidates who can start quickly.","zh":"如果 Becky 招聘臨時職員，她需要能快速上班的應徵者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes short-term hiring.","zh":"這個短語描述短期招聘。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"temporary staff","meaning":"臨時職員","examples":[{"en":"The agency recruits temporary staff for finance companies.","zh":"介紹所為金融公司招聘臨時職員。"},{"en":"Temporary staff are workers employed for a limited period rather than permanently.","zh":"temporary staff 指受聘一段有限時間，而不是永久聘用的員工。"},{"en":"A company may hire temporary staff when permanent workers are on holiday.","zh":"當正式員工放假時，公司可能聘請臨時職員。"},{"en":"If Amber joins as temporary staff, she may work for different companies.","zh":"如果 Amber 以臨時職員身份加入，她可能為不同公司工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes short-term workers.","zh":"這個短語描述短期員工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"finance sector","meaning":"金融業","examples":[{"en":"Becky mostly recruits staff for the finance sector.","zh":"Becky 主要為金融業招聘員工。"},{"en":"The finance sector is the part of the economy involving banks, investment, insurance, and financial services.","zh":"finance sector 指涉及銀行、投資、保險和金融服務的經濟領域。"},{"en":"Many office jobs in the finance sector require accuracy and confidentiality.","zh":"金融業的許多辦公室工作需要準確和保密。"},{"en":"If Amber works in the finance sector, the experience may look professional on her CV.","zh":"如果 Amber 在金融業工作，這段經驗在履歷上可能顯得專業。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the financial services industry.","zh":"這個短語指金融服務行業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"look good on your CV","meaning":"令你的履歷更好看","examples":[{"en":"Finance-sector experience will look good on Amber’s CV.","zh":"金融業經驗會令 Amber 的履歷更好看。"},{"en":"To look good on your CV means to improve how your work history appears to employers.","zh":"look good on your CV 指令你的工作經歷在僱主眼中更有吸引力。"},{"en":"Volunteering for a charity can look good on your CV if it shows useful skills.","zh":"如果慈善義工經驗能展示有用技能，它可以令你的履歷更好看。"},{"en":"If Amber gains office experience, it may make her CV stronger.","zh":"如果 Amber 累積辦公室經驗，履歷可能更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improving employability.","zh":"這個短語描述提升就業競爭力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"CV","meaning":"履歷","examples":[{"en":"Temporary finance jobs can improve Amber’s CV.","zh":"臨時金融工作可以改善 Amber 的履歷。"},{"en":"A CV is a document listing a person’s education, work experience, skills, and achievements.","zh":"CV 指列出個人教育、工作經驗、技能和成就的文件。"},{"en":"Students should update their CV before applying for internships.","zh":"學生申請實習前應更新履歷。"},{"en":"If Amber adds relevant experience to her CV, employers may take her more seriously.","zh":"如果 Amber 在履歷加入相關經驗，僱主可能更認真考慮她。"},{"en":"This word refers to a résumé used for job applications.","zh":"這個字指求職用的履歷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"generally pays better","meaning":"通常薪酬較好","examples":[{"en":"Finance-sector temporary work generally pays better.","zh":"金融業臨時工作通常薪酬較好。"},{"en":"Generally pays better means usually offers higher wages than other options.","zh":"generally pays better 指通常比其他選擇提供較高薪金。"},{"en":"Weekend tutoring generally pays better than ordinary shop work.","zh":"週末補習通常比一般店舖工作薪酬較好。"},{"en":"If a job generally pays better, it may attract more applicants.","zh":"如果一份工作通常薪酬較好，可能吸引更多申請者。"},{"en":"This phrase compares typical pay levels.","zh":"這個短語比較一般薪酬水平。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be a bit worried because","meaning":"有點擔心，因為……","examples":[{"en":"Amber is a bit worried because she does not have much office experience.","zh":"Amber 有點擔心，因為她沒有太多辦公室工作經驗。"},{"en":"To be a bit worried because of something means to feel slightly anxious for that reason.","zh":"be a bit worried because of something 指因某原因感到有點焦慮。"},{"en":"The student was a bit worried because he had never given a speech before.","zh":"這名學生有點擔心，因為他以前從未演講過。"},{"en":"If Amber lacks experience, it is natural for her to feel a little worried.","zh":"如果 Amber 缺乏經驗，她有點擔心是自然的。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a reason for mild anxiety.","zh":"這個短語給出輕微焦慮的原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"office experience","meaning":"辦公室工作經驗","examples":[{"en":"Amber does not have much office experience.","zh":"Amber 沒有太多辦公室工作經驗。"},{"en":"Office experience means experience of working in an office environment.","zh":"office experience 指在辦公室環境工作的經驗。"},{"en":"Office experience may include answering phones, using email, and organising files.","zh":"辦公室工作經驗可能包括接電話、使用電郵和整理檔案。"},{"en":"If Amber gains office experience, she may become more confident in administrative work.","zh":"如果 Amber 累積辦公室經驗，她可能對行政工作更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical workplace experience in an office.","zh":"這個短語指辦公室中的實際工作經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"I wouldn’t worry","meaning":"我不會擔心","examples":[{"en":"William tells Amber that he would not worry.","zh":"William 告訴 Amber 他不會擔心。"},{"en":"I wouldn’t worry is used to reassure someone that a problem is not too serious.","zh":"I wouldn’t worry 用來安慰某人，表示問題不是太嚴重。"},{"en":"If you forgot one small detail, I wouldn’t worry too much.","zh":"如果你忘了一個小細節，我不會太擔心。"},{"en":"William says this to make Amber feel less anxious about her lack of experience.","zh":"William 這樣說，是為了減少 Amber 對缺乏經驗的焦慮。"},{"en":"This phrase gives calm reassurance.","zh":"這個短語給予平靜安慰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"start someone as","meaning":"先安排某人做……","examples":[{"en":"The agency will probably start Amber as a receptionist.","zh":"介紹所可能會先安排 Amber 做接待員。"},{"en":"To start someone as something means to give them that role at the beginning.","zh":"start someone as something 指一開始安排某人擔任某角色。"},{"en":"The restaurant started him as a waiter before training him as a manager.","zh":"餐廳先安排他做侍應，然後培訓他成為經理。"},{"en":"If Amber starts as a receptionist, she can learn basic office routines first.","zh":"如果 Amber 先做接待員，就可以先學習基本辦公室流程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an initial job placement.","zh":"這個短語描述初始職位安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"receptionist","meaning":"接待員","examples":[{"en":"Amber may start work as a receptionist.","zh":"Amber 可能開始做接待員。"},{"en":"A receptionist is a person who greets visitors, answers calls, and handles front-desk duties.","zh":"receptionist 指接待訪客、接聽電話和處理前台工作的員工。"},{"en":"A hotel receptionist checks guests in and answers their questions.","zh":"酒店接待員為住客辦理入住並回答問題。"},{"en":"If Amber works as a receptionist, communication skills will be very important.","zh":"如果 Amber 做接待員，溝通能力會非常重要。"},{"en":"This word describes a front-desk office role.","zh":"這個字描述前台辦公室職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"something like that","meaning":"類似的工作","examples":[{"en":"Amber may work as a receptionist or something like that.","zh":"Amber 可能做接待員或類似的工作。"},{"en":"Something like that means a similar kind of thing or role.","zh":"something like that 指類似的事物或角色。"},{"en":"She wants to work as an assistant, receptionist, or something like that.","zh":"她想做助理、接待員或類似的工作。"},{"en":"If William says something like that, he is giving an approximate example, not a fixed job title.","zh":"如果 William 說 something like that，他只是給出大約例子，不是固定職銜。"},{"en":"This phrase keeps the meaning general.","zh":"這個短語令意思保持概括。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"that kind of job","meaning":"那類工作","examples":[{"en":"Communication is important for that kind of job.","zh":"溝通對那類工作很重要。"},{"en":"That kind of job means that type of work or role.","zh":"that kind of job 指那種類型的工作或角色。"},{"en":"That kind of job suits people who enjoy talking to customers.","zh":"那類工作適合喜歡與顧客交談的人。"},{"en":"If that kind of job involves visitors, politeness and patience matter.","zh":"如果那類工作涉及訪客，禮貌和耐性就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a job type already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回已提到的工作類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"it isn’t so much… it’s…","meaning":"與其說是……不如說是……","examples":[{"en":"For receptionist work, it is not so much business skills as communication that matters.","zh":"對接待員工作而言，重要的與其說是商業技能，不如說是溝通能力。"},{"en":"It isn’t so much A as B means B is more important than A.","zh":"it isn’t so much A as B 指 B 比 A 更重要。"},{"en":"For teaching young children, it isn’t so much strict rules as patience that matters.","zh":"對教導幼兒而言，重要的與其說是嚴格規則，不如說是耐性。"},{"en":"This structure shifts attention from one factor to a more important one.","zh":"這個結構把注意力從一個因素轉到更重要的因素。"},{"en":"It is useful for making a contrast in a formal way.","zh":"它適合用來以正式方式作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"business skills","meaning":"商業技能","examples":[{"en":"Receptionist work does not mainly depend on business skills.","zh":"接待員工作並不主要依賴商業技能。"},{"en":"Business skills are abilities used in workplaces, such as organisation, sales, finance, and professional communication.","zh":"business skills 指工作場所使用的能力，例如組織、銷售、財務和專業溝通。"},{"en":"Business skills can help people manage projects and deal with clients.","zh":"商業技能可以幫助人們管理項目和處理客戶。"},{"en":"If a job is entry-level, advanced business skills may not be required at first.","zh":"如果一份工作是入門級，起初未必需要高階商業技能。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical skills for working in business.","zh":"這個短語指商業工作中的實用技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"computer systems","meaning":"電腦系統","examples":[{"en":"Amber does not need to know lots of different computer systems at first.","zh":"Amber 一開始不需要懂很多不同電腦系統。"},{"en":"Computer systems are software or digital platforms used to carry out work tasks.","zh":"computer systems 指用來完成工作任務的軟件或數碼平台。"},{"en":"Office workers may use computer systems for booking, records, and email.","zh":"辦公室員工可能使用電腦系統處理預約、紀錄和電郵。"},{"en":"If Amber does not know many systems yet, she can learn them on the job.","zh":"如果 Amber 暫時不懂很多系統，她可以在工作中學會。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to workplace technology platforms.","zh":"這個短語指工作場所中的科技平台。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"communication really matters","meaning":"溝通能力真正重要","examples":[{"en":"Communication really matters in receptionist work.","zh":"在接待員工作中，溝通能力真正重要。"},{"en":"Communication really matters means speaking, listening, and passing information clearly are very important.","zh":"communication really matters 指清楚說話、聆聽和傳遞資料非常重要。"},{"en":"In customer service, communication really matters because people need quick answers.","zh":"在顧客服務中，溝通能力真正重要，因為人們需要快速答案。"},{"en":"If Amber communicates well, she can make a good impression as a receptionist.","zh":"如果 Amber 溝通良好，她做接待員時可以留下好印象。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises communication skills.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調溝通技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be fine there","meaning":"在那方面會沒問題","examples":[{"en":"William thinks Amber would be fine in that kind of job.","zh":"William 認為 Amber 在那類工作方面會沒問題。"},{"en":"To be fine there means to manage well in that situation or role.","zh":"be fine there 指能在該情況或角色中應付得來。"},{"en":"You would be fine there because you are polite and organised.","zh":"你在那裡會沒問題，因為你有禮又有條理。"},{"en":"If communication is the main skill, William believes Amber can cope.","zh":"如果主要技能是溝通，William 相信 Amber 可以應付。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures someone about their ability.","zh":"這個短語用來安慰某人有能力做到。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pick up","meaning":"學會；掌握","examples":[{"en":"Amber will pick up office skills quickly on the job.","zh":"Amber 會在工作中很快學會辦公室技能。"},{"en":"To pick up a skill means to learn it naturally or gradually through experience.","zh":"pick up a skill 指透過經驗自然或逐漸學會某技能。"},{"en":"New staff often pick up phone manners after a few days at reception.","zh":"新員工在接待處工作幾天後，常會學會電話禮儀。"},{"en":"If Amber is observant, she may pick up office routines quickly.","zh":"如果 Amber 觀察力強，她可能很快掌握辦公室流程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning through practice.","zh":"這個短語描述透過實踐學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"office skills","meaning":"辦公室技能","examples":[{"en":"Amber can learn office skills on the job.","zh":"Amber 可以在工作中學習辦公室技能。"},{"en":"Office skills are abilities needed in an office, such as using email, filing, answering calls, and organising information.","zh":"office skills 指辦公室所需能力，例如使用電郵、歸檔、接聽電話和整理資料。"},{"en":"Temporary work can help students build office skills.","zh":"臨時工作可以幫助學生建立辦公室技能。"},{"en":"If Amber improves her office skills, she may qualify for better jobs later.","zh":"如果 Amber 改善辦公室技能，之後可能符合更好工作的要求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical abilities for office work.","zh":"這個短語描述辦公室工作的實用能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on the job","meaning":"在工作中","examples":[{"en":"Amber will pick up office skills on the job.","zh":"Amber 會在工作中掌握辦公室技能。"},{"en":"On the job means while actually working rather than through separate training.","zh":"on the job 指在實際工作期間，而不是透過獨立培訓。"},{"en":"Many receptionists learn the company’s booking system on the job.","zh":"許多接待員在工作中學會公司的預約系統。"},{"en":"If Amber learns on the job, real tasks will help her improve quickly.","zh":"如果 Amber 在工作中學習，真實任務會幫助她快速進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical workplace learning.","zh":"這個短語描述實際工作場所中的學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not that complicated","meaning":"沒有那麼複雜","examples":[{"en":"William says office work is not that complicated.","zh":"William 說辦公室工作沒有那麼複雜。"},{"en":"Not that complicated means not as difficult or complex as someone may think.","zh":"not that complicated 指不像某人想像中那麼困難或複雜。"},{"en":"The registration form is not that complicated once you read the instructions.","zh":"只要閱讀指示，登記表其實沒有那麼複雜。"},{"en":"If office work is not too complicated, Amber may learn the basics quickly.","zh":"如果辦公室工作沒有太複雜，Amber 可能很快學會基本內容。"},{"en":"This phrase reduces someone’s worry about difficulty.","zh":"這個短語減少某人對難度的擔心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"temporary staff","meaning":"臨時職員","examples":[{"en":"Amber asks how long companies generally need temporary staff.","zh":"Amber 問公司一般需要臨時職員多久。"},{"en":"Temporary staff are workers employed for a short or limited period.","zh":"temporary staff 指受聘短期或有限時間的員工。"},{"en":"Companies often need temporary staff during busy seasons or staff absences.","zh":"公司在繁忙季節或員工缺席時常需要臨時職員。"},{"en":"If a company needs temporary staff for longer, a short placement may be extended.","zh":"如果公司需要臨時職員更久，短期職位可能會被延長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes non-permanent employees.","zh":"這個短語描述非永久員工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lasting at least","meaning":"持續至少……","examples":[{"en":"Amber wants a job lasting at least a month.","zh":"Amber 想要一份持續至少一個月的工作。"},{"en":"Lasting at least a period means continuing for no less than that amount of time.","zh":"lasting at least a period 指持續不少於該段時間。"},{"en":"She wanted a placement lasting at least six weeks.","zh":"她想要一個持續至少六星期的實習。"},{"en":"If a job lasts at least a month, Amber can gain more meaningful experience.","zh":"如果一份工作持續至少一個月，Amber 可以獲得更有意義的經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a minimum duration.","zh":"這個短語設定最低持續時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at least a month","meaning":"至少一個月","examples":[{"en":"Amber hopes to get temporary work lasting at least a month.","zh":"Amber 希望找到至少一個月的臨時工作。"},{"en":"At least a month means one month or longer.","zh":"at least a month 指一個月或更長時間。"},{"en":"The project will take at least a month to complete.","zh":"這個項目至少需要一個月完成。"},{"en":"If temporary work lasts at least a month, it may look better on a CV.","zh":"如果臨時工作持續至少一個月，在履歷上可能更好看。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a minimum time period.","zh":"這個短語給出最低時間長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"should not be too difficult","meaning":"應該不太難","examples":[{"en":"William says finding a month-long job should not be too difficult.","zh":"William 說找到一份為期一個月的工作應該不太難。"},{"en":"Should not be too difficult means it is likely to be fairly manageable.","zh":"should not be too difficult 指很可能相當容易處理。"},{"en":"Finding the agency’s office should not be too difficult if Amber has the address.","zh":"如果 Amber 有地址，找到介紹所辦公室應該不太難。"},{"en":"If many companies need temporary staff, finding work may not be too hard.","zh":"如果許多公司需要臨時職員，找工作可能不太難。"},{"en":"This phrase gives reassurance about difficulty.","zh":"這個短語對難度作出安慰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be more likely to","meaning":"更有可能","examples":[{"en":"Amber is more likely to be offered something for a week at first.","zh":"Amber 起初更有可能獲提供一份為期一星期的工作。"},{"en":"To be more likely to do something means to have a higher chance of doing or receiving it.","zh":"be more likely to do something 指做某事或得到某事的機會較高。"},{"en":"New workers are more likely to start with simple duties.","zh":"新員工更有可能先做簡單職責。"},{"en":"If Amber has little experience, the agency may first offer her a short placement.","zh":"如果 Amber 經驗較少，介紹所可能先提供短期職位。"},{"en":"This phrase describes greater probability.","zh":"這個短語描述較高可能性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be offered something for","meaning":"獲提供一份為期……的工作","examples":[{"en":"Amber may be offered a job for a week at first.","zh":"Amber 起初可能獲提供一份為期一星期的工作。"},{"en":"To be offered something for a period means to be given the chance to take it for that length of time.","zh":"be offered something for a period 指獲得某段時間內接受某事的機會。"},{"en":"He was offered a contract for three months.","zh":"他獲提供一份為期三個月的合約。"},{"en":"If Amber is offered work for one week, it may later be extended.","zh":"如果 Amber 獲提供一星期工作，之後可能會延長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving an opportunity with a time limit.","zh":"這個短語描述收到有時限的機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at first","meaning":"起初","examples":[{"en":"Amber may first be offered a one-week job.","zh":"Amber 起初可能獲提供一份一星期的工作。"},{"en":"At first means at the beginning or in the early stage.","zh":"at first 指在開始時或早期階段。"},{"en":"At first, the new worker only answered phones and greeted visitors.","zh":"起初，新員工只負責接電話和接待訪客。"},{"en":"If Amber starts with a short job at first, she can prove herself gradually.","zh":"如果 Amber 起初先做短期工作，她可以逐步證明自己。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the initial stage.","zh":"這個短語指初始階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get extended","meaning":"被延長","examples":[{"en":"A one-week job might get extended.","zh":"一份一星期的工作可能會被延長。"},{"en":"To get extended means to be made longer in time.","zh":"get extended 指時間被加長。"},{"en":"The temporary contract got extended because the company still needed help.","zh":"臨時合約因公司仍需要幫手而被延長。"},{"en":"If Amber performs well, a short placement may get extended.","zh":"如果 Amber 表現良好，短期職位可能會被延長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a time period being lengthened.","zh":"這個短語描述時間被拉長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"it is unusual to","meaning":"……並不常見","examples":[{"en":"It is unusual to be sent somewhere for just a day or two.","zh":"被派到某處只工作一兩天並不常見。"},{"en":"It is unusual to do something means that action does not happen very often.","zh":"it is unusual to do something 指某行動不常發生。"},{"en":"It is unusual to have an interview without any questions.","zh":"面試完全沒有問題並不常見。"},{"en":"If one-day placements are unusual, Amber can expect longer assignments.","zh":"如果一日職位不常見，Amber 可以預期較長的工作安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something uncommon.","zh":"這個短語描述不尋常的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be sent somewhere","meaning":"被派到某處","examples":[{"en":"Temporary workers are rarely sent somewhere for only one or two days.","zh":"臨時員工很少被派到某處只工作一兩天。"},{"en":"To be sent somewhere means to be assigned or told to go to a particular place for work.","zh":"be sent somewhere 指被安排或指示到某地方工作。"},{"en":"The agency sent her to a bank office for a short placement.","zh":"介紹所把她派到一間銀行辦公室做短期工作。"},{"en":"If Amber is sent somewhere new, she should check the address and start time carefully.","zh":"如果 Amber 被派到新地方，她應仔細核對地址和上班時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being assigned to a location.","zh":"這個短語描述被安排到某地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"just a day or two","meaning":"只有一兩天","examples":[{"en":"It is unusual to be sent somewhere for just a day or two.","zh":"被派到某處只有一兩天並不常見。"},{"en":"Just a day or two means only one or two days.","zh":"just a day or two 指只有一天或兩天。"},{"en":"The training lasted just a day or two, but it was useful.","zh":"培訓只有一兩天，但很有用。"},{"en":"If a job lasts just a day or two, it may not give much experience.","zh":"如果工作只有一兩天，可能不能提供太多經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a very short period.","zh":"這個短語強調時間非常短。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the pay is not too bad","meaning":"薪酬不算差","examples":[{"en":"Amber has heard that the pay is not too bad.","zh":"Amber 聽說薪酬不算差。"},{"en":"The pay is not too bad means the wages are fairly acceptable or better than expected.","zh":"the pay is not too bad 指工資相當可以接受，或比預期好。"},{"en":"The pay is not too bad for a weekend job.","zh":"以週末工作來說，薪酬不算差。"},{"en":"If the pay is not too bad, Amber may feel the temporary work is worthwhile.","zh":"如果薪酬不算差，Amber 可能覺得臨時工作值得做。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a mild positive judgement about wages.","zh":"這個短語對工資作出溫和正面評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"better than working in","meaning":"比在……工作更好","examples":[{"en":"Temporary office work pays better than working in a shop or restaurant.","zh":"臨時辦公室工作的薪酬比在商店或餐廳工作更好。"},{"en":"Better than working in a place means more favourable than having that type of job.","zh":"better than working in a place 指比做某類地方的工作更有利。"},{"en":"For some students, tutoring pays better than working in a café.","zh":"對有些學生來說，補習比在咖啡店工作薪酬更好。"},{"en":"If office work pays better than shop work, Amber may prefer the agency route.","zh":"如果辦公室工作薪酬比店舖工作好，Amber 可能較喜歡透過介紹所找工作。"},{"en":"This phrase compares job options.","zh":"這個短語比較工作選項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"definitely","meaning":"肯定地","examples":[{"en":"William says the pay is definitely better than shop or restaurant work.","zh":"William 說薪酬肯定比商店或餐廳工作好。"},{"en":"Definitely means certainly or without doubt.","zh":"definitely 指肯定或毫無疑問。"},{"en":"This route is definitely faster than walking through the town centre.","zh":"這條路肯定比穿過市中心步行更快。"},{"en":"If William says definitely, he is strongly confirming Amber’s idea.","zh":"如果 William 說 definitely，他是在強烈確認 Amber 的想法。"},{"en":"This word adds confidence and emphasis.","zh":"這個字增加信心和強調語氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hourly rate","meaning":"時薪","examples":[{"en":"The hourly rate is about £10.","zh":"時薪大約是10英鎊。"},{"en":"The hourly rate is the amount of money paid for each hour of work.","zh":"hourly rate 指每工作一小時獲得的薪金。"},{"en":"The hourly rate for the tutoring job is higher at weekends.","zh":"補習工作的週末時薪較高。"},{"en":"If the hourly rate is £10, working eight hours earns about £80 before deductions.","zh":"如果時薪是10英鎊，工作八小時扣款前大約賺80英鎊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pay per hour.","zh":"這個短語描述每小時薪酬。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"if you are lucky","meaning":"如果你幸運的話","examples":[{"en":"The hourly rate may be £11 if Amber is lucky.","zh":"如果 Amber 幸運的話，時薪可能是11英鎊。"},{"en":"If you are lucky means if things go especially well for you.","zh":"if you are lucky 指如果事情對你特別順利。"},{"en":"You may get a seat on the bus if you are lucky.","zh":"如果你幸運的話，可能在巴士上有座位。"},{"en":"If Amber is lucky, she may get a slightly higher hourly rate.","zh":"如果 Amber 幸運的話，可能獲得稍高時薪。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a good result is possible but not guaranteed.","zh":"這個短語暗示好結果有可能，但不能保證。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"expect to get","meaning":"預期得到","examples":[{"en":"Amber was only expecting to get eight or nine pounds an hour.","zh":"Amber 原本只預期得到每小時八至九英鎊。"},{"en":"To expect to get something means to think you will receive it.","zh":"expect to get something 指認為自己會收到某物。"},{"en":"The student expected to get feedback after the interview.","zh":"學生預期面試後會得到回饋。"},{"en":"If Amber expected lower pay, the actual rate may surprise her.","zh":"如果 Amber 原本預期較低薪酬，實際時薪可能令她驚喜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a predicted result.","zh":"這個短語描述預測的結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"eight or nine pounds an hour","meaning":"每小時八至九英鎊","examples":[{"en":"Amber expected to get eight or nine pounds an hour.","zh":"Amber 預期每小時得到八至九英鎊。"},{"en":"Eight or nine pounds an hour means a wage of £8 or £9 for each hour worked.","zh":"eight or nine pounds an hour 指每工作一小時獲得8或9英鎊。"},{"en":"A student job may pay eight or nine pounds an hour depending on the employer.","zh":"學生工作可能按僱主不同，每小時支付八至九英鎊。"},{"en":"If office work pays more than that, Amber may see it as a good opportunity.","zh":"如果辦公室工作薪酬高於這個水平，Amber 可能視之為好機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an expected hourly wage.","zh":"這個短語描述預期時薪。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"registration process","meaning":"登記程序","examples":[{"en":"William explains the agency’s registration process.","zh":"William 解釋介紹所的登記程序。"},{"en":"A registration process is the set of steps needed to sign up or join officially.","zh":"registration process 指正式登記或加入所需的一系列步驟。"},{"en":"The college registration process includes filling in a form and showing ID.","zh":"學院登記程序包括填表和出示身份證明。"},{"en":"If Amber understands the registration process, she can prepare the right documents.","zh":"如果 Amber 了解登記程序，就可以準備正確文件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal sign-up procedures.","zh":"這個短語描述正式登記手續。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have an interview","meaning":"接受面試","examples":[{"en":"Amber knows she has to have an interview.","zh":"Amber 知道她必須接受面試。"},{"en":"To have an interview means to attend a formal meeting where questions are asked to assess suitability.","zh":"have an interview 指出席正式會面，對方會提問以評估是否合適。"},{"en":"She had an interview with the agency before getting her first placement.","zh":"她在得到第一份工作安排前，接受了介紹所面試。"},{"en":"If Amber has an interview, the agency can learn about her skills and preferences.","zh":"如果 Amber 接受面試，介紹所就能了解她的技能和偏好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attending an assessment meeting.","zh":"這個短語描述出席評估會面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take about an hour","meaning":"需時約一小時","examples":[{"en":"The interview usually takes about an hour.","zh":"面試通常需時約一小時。"},{"en":"To take about an hour means to last approximately sixty minutes.","zh":"take about an hour 指大約持續六十分鐘。"},{"en":"The registration meeting takes about an hour if all documents are ready.","zh":"如果所有文件都準備好，登記會面需時約一小時。"},{"en":"If Amber knows the interview takes about an hour, she can plan her day.","zh":"如果 Amber 知道面試需時約一小時，就可以安排當日行程。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate duration.","zh":"這個短語提供大約時間長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"arrange that","meaning":"安排那件事","examples":[{"en":"Amber should arrange the interview about a week in advance.","zh":"Amber 應大約提前一星期安排面試。"},{"en":"To arrange that means to organise or schedule that event or task.","zh":"arrange that 指組織或預約那件事。"},{"en":"Please call the office to arrange that before Friday.","zh":"請在星期五前致電辦公室安排那件事。"},{"en":"If Amber arranges the interview early, she is more likely to get a convenient time.","zh":"如果 Amber 及早安排面試，就更可能得到方便的時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making practical arrangements.","zh":"這個短語描述作出實際安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"about a week in advance","meaning":"大約提前一星期","examples":[{"en":"The interview should be arranged about a week in advance.","zh":"面試應大約提前一星期安排。"},{"en":"About a week in advance means roughly one week before the event.","zh":"about a week in advance 指大約在活動前一星期。"},{"en":"Students should book the practice room about a week in advance.","zh":"學生應大約提前一星期預訂練習室。"},{"en":"If Amber arranges the interview a week in advance, the agency has time to prepare.","zh":"如果 Amber 提前一星期安排面試，介紹所有時間準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes early planning.","zh":"這個短語描述預早規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dress smartly","meaning":"穿得整齊得體","examples":[{"en":"Amber thinks she should dress smartly for office work.","zh":"Amber 認為自己應為辦公室工作穿得整齊得體。"},{"en":"To dress smartly means to wear neat, tidy, and fairly formal clothes.","zh":"dress smartly 指穿着整潔、端正而較正式的衣服。"},{"en":"Candidates should dress smartly for an agency interview.","zh":"應徵者應在介紹所面試時穿得整齊得體。"},{"en":"If Amber dresses smartly, she may make a professional first impression.","zh":"如果 Amber 穿得整齊得體，就可能留下專業的第一印象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes appropriate appearance for formal situations.","zh":"這個短語描述正式場合中的合適外表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"office work","meaning":"辦公室工作","examples":[{"en":"Amber wants temporary office work.","zh":"Amber 想找臨時辦公室工作。"},{"en":"Office work is work done in an office, often involving administration, communication, and records.","zh":"office work 指在辦公室進行的工作，常涉及行政、溝通和紀錄。"},{"en":"Office work may include filing documents, answering phones, and using email.","zh":"辦公室工作可能包括整理文件、接聽電話和使用電郵。"},{"en":"If Amber wants office work, she should show that she is organised and polite.","zh":"如果 Amber 想做辦公室工作，就應表現出有條理和有禮貌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes general work in an office setting.","zh":"這個短語描述辦公室環境中的一般工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"borrow a suit from","meaning":"向……借一套西裝","examples":[{"en":"Amber can probably borrow a suit from her mother.","zh":"Amber 大概可以向母親借一套西裝。"},{"en":"To borrow a suit from someone means to use that person’s formal clothing temporarily.","zh":"borrow a suit from someone 指暫時使用某人的正式服裝。"},{"en":"He borrowed a suit from his brother for the interview.","zh":"他為了面試向哥哥借了一套西裝。"},{"en":"If Amber borrows a suit, she can look professional without buying new clothes.","zh":"如果 Amber 借一套西裝，就能不用買新衣服也顯得專業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes temporarily using someone else’s formal outfit.","zh":"這個短語描述暫時使用別人的正式服裝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"look too smart","meaning":"看起來太正式","examples":[{"en":"It is better to look too smart than too casual.","zh":"看起來太正式總比太隨便好。"},{"en":"To look too smart means to appear more formally dressed than necessary.","zh":"look too smart 指穿得比所需更正式。"},{"en":"For an interview, it is safer to look too smart than untidy.","zh":"面試時，看起來太正式比不整潔更安全。"},{"en":"If Amber looks very smart, the agency may see her as serious and professional.","zh":"如果 Amber 看起來很正式，介紹所可能認為她認真而專業。"},{"en":"This phrase compares overdressing with underdressing.","zh":"這個短語比較穿得過於正式和穿得不夠正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"too casual","meaning":"太隨便","examples":[{"en":"For an agency interview, it is better not to look too casual.","zh":"對介紹所面試而言，最好不要看起來太隨便。"},{"en":"Too casual means too informal or not smart enough for the situation.","zh":"too casual 指太不正式或不夠得體。"},{"en":"Trainers and an old T-shirt may look too casual for an interview.","zh":"運動鞋和舊T恤對面試來說可能太隨便。"},{"en":"If Amber looks too casual, the agency may doubt her professionalism.","zh":"如果 Amber 看起來太隨便，介紹所可能懷疑她的專業態度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clothing that is not formal enough.","zh":"這個短語描述不夠正式的衣着。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"copies of","meaning":"……的副本","examples":[{"en":"Amber asks whether she needs copies of her exam certificates.","zh":"Amber 問她是否需要考試證書副本。"},{"en":"Copies of documents are duplicated versions of the originals.","zh":"copies of documents 指原件的複製版本。"},{"en":"Candidates may bring copies of their CVs to interviews.","zh":"應徵者可能帶履歷副本去面試。"},{"en":"If Amber needs copies of certificates, she should prepare them before registration.","zh":"如果 Amber 需要證書副本，就應在登記前準備好。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to duplicate documents.","zh":"這個短語指文件副本。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"exam certificates","meaning":"考試證書","examples":[{"en":"Amber does not need to bring her exam certificates.","zh":"Amber 不需要帶考試證書。"},{"en":"Exam certificates are official documents showing a person’s exam results or qualifications.","zh":"exam certificates 指顯示個人考試成績或資格的官方文件。"},{"en":"Students often keep exam certificates in a safe folder.","zh":"學生通常把考試證書放在安全文件夾中。"},{"en":"If an employer asks for exam certificates, candidates may need to show proof of qualifications.","zh":"如果僱主要求考試證書，應徵者可能需要出示資格證明。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official proof of exam achievement.","zh":"這個短語描述考試成就的官方證明。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"anything like that","meaning":"諸如此類的東西","examples":[{"en":"Amber asks whether she needs certificates or anything like that.","zh":"Amber 問她是否需要證書或諸如此類的東西。"},{"en":"Anything like that means similar things of the same general type.","zh":"anything like that 指同一大類的類似東西。"},{"en":"The teacher asked students not to bring food, drinks, or anything like that into the lab.","zh":"老師要求學生不要把食物、飲品或諸如此類的東西帶入實驗室。"},{"en":"If Amber asks about certificates or anything like that, she means official documents in general.","zh":"如果 Amber 問證書或諸如此類的東西，她泛指官方文件。"},{"en":"This phrase keeps a list general rather than exact.","zh":"這個短語令清單保持概括，而不是精確列出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ask to see","meaning":"要求查看","examples":[{"en":"The agency will ask to see Amber’s passport.","zh":"介紹所會要求查看 Amber 的護照。"},{"en":"To ask to see something means to request that someone show it.","zh":"ask to see something 指要求某人出示某物。"},{"en":"The receptionist asked to see my ID card before giving me a visitor badge.","zh":"接待員在給我訪客證前要求查看我的身份證。"},{"en":"If the agency asks to see Amber’s passport, it may need to check her identity.","zh":"如果介紹所要求查看 Amber 的護照，可能需要核實她的身份。"},{"en":"This phrase describes requesting proof or evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述要求出示證明或資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"get stressed about","meaning":"因……感到緊張","examples":[{"en":"William says Amber should not get stressed about the interview.","zh":"William 說 Amber 不應因面試感到緊張。"},{"en":"To get stressed about something means to become anxious or tense because of it.","zh":"get stressed about something 指因某事變得焦慮或緊張。"},{"en":"Many students get stressed about oral presentations.","zh":"許多學生因口頭匯報感到緊張。"},{"en":"If Amber understands the interview is informal, she may not get too stressed.","zh":"如果 Amber 明白面試較非正式，可能不會太緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming worried or tense.","zh":"這個短語描述變得擔心或緊繃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"just a chance for","meaning":"只是……的機會","examples":[{"en":"The interview is just a chance for the agency to build a relationship with Amber.","zh":"面試只是介紹所與 Amber 建立關係的機會。"},{"en":"Just a chance for something means simply an opportunity for that purpose, not something more serious.","zh":"just a chance for something 指只是為某目的而設的機會，不是更嚴重的事情。"},{"en":"The meeting is just a chance for students to ask questions.","zh":"這次會議只是學生提問的機會。"},{"en":"If the interview is just a chance to talk, Amber does not need to panic.","zh":"如果面試只是傾談的機會，Amber 不需要驚慌。"},{"en":"This phrase makes an event sound less intimidating.","zh":"這個短語令事件聽起來較不嚇人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"build a relationship with","meaning":"與……建立關係","examples":[{"en":"The agency uses the interview to build a relationship with candidates.","zh":"介紹所利用面試與應徵者建立關係。"},{"en":"To build a relationship with someone means to develop trust, understanding, and regular contact with them.","zh":"build a relationship with someone 指與某人發展信任、了解和固定聯繫。"},{"en":"A teacher builds a relationship with students by listening and giving support.","zh":"老師透過聆聽和支援與學生建立關係。"},{"en":"If the agency builds a relationship with Amber, it can understand what jobs suit her.","zh":"如果介紹所與 Amber 建立關係，就能了解甚麼工作適合她。"},{"en":"This phrase describes developing a useful connection.","zh":"這個短語描述建立有用連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"try and match","meaning":"嘗試配對","examples":[{"en":"The agency will try and match Amber to a suitable job.","zh":"介紹所會嘗試把 Amber 配對到合適工作。"},{"en":"To try and match someone to something means to attempt to pair them with something suitable.","zh":"try and match someone to something 指嘗試把某人與合適事物配對。"},{"en":"The tutor tried to match students to projects that suited their interests.","zh":"導師嘗試把學生配對到符合他們興趣的專題。"},{"en":"If the agency understands Amber well, it can try to match her more accurately.","zh":"如果介紹所了解 Amber，就能更準確地嘗試配對。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attempting to make a suitable pairing.","zh":"這個短語描述嘗試作出合適配對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"match someone to a job","meaning":"為某人配對一份工作","examples":[{"en":"The agency tries to match each candidate to a job they will like.","zh":"介紹所嘗試為每位應徵者配對一份他們會喜歡的工作。"},{"en":"To match someone to a job means to connect that person with work that suits their skills, personality, or needs.","zh":"match someone to a job 指把某人與符合其技能、性格或需要的工作連繫起來。"},{"en":"A careers adviser can match students to jobs based on their strengths.","zh":"職業顧問可以根據學生強項為他們配對工作。"},{"en":"If Amber is matched to the right job, she may perform better and enjoy the work more.","zh":"如果 Amber 被配對到合適工作，她可能表現更好，也更享受工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fitting a person to a role.","zh":"這個短語描述把人配合到職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"questions about personality","meaning":"關於性格的問題","examples":[{"en":"The interview includes questions about personality.","zh":"面試包括關於性格的問題。"},{"en":"Questions about personality ask what kind of person someone is or how they behave.","zh":"questions about personality 會問某人是甚麼類型的人或如何行事。"},{"en":"An interviewer may ask questions about personality to see whether a candidate suits customer service.","zh":"面試官可能問關於性格的問題，以了解應徵者是否適合顧客服務。"},{"en":"If Amber answers these questions honestly, the agency can find a better match.","zh":"如果 Amber 誠實回答這些問題，介紹所就能找到更好配對。"},{"en":"This phrase describes questions about character and behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述關於性格和行為的問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ask candidates","meaning":"問應徵者","examples":[{"en":"The agency asks candidates fairly basic questions.","zh":"介紹所問應徵者相當基本的問題。"},{"en":"To ask candidates means to question people who are applying for jobs.","zh":"ask candidates 指詢問正在申請工作的人。"},{"en":"Employers ask candidates about their experience and availability.","zh":"僱主會問應徵者有關經驗和可上班時間的問題。"},{"en":"If the agency asks candidates simple questions, the interview may feel less formal.","zh":"如果介紹所問應徵者簡單問題，面試可能感覺較不正式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interviewing job applicants.","zh":"這個短語描述面試求職者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fairly basic ones","meaning":"相當基本的問題","examples":[{"en":"The personality questions are fairly basic ones.","zh":"性格問題是相當基本的問題。"},{"en":"Fairly basic ones means quite simple questions or items.","zh":"fairly basic ones 指相當簡單的問題或項目。"},{"en":"The grammar exercises were fairly basic ones for beginners.","zh":"那些文法練習對初學者來說是相當基本的題目。"},{"en":"If the questions are fairly basic, Amber should not feel too anxious.","zh":"如果問題相當基本，Amber 不應太焦慮。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the difficulty level is low.","zh":"這個短語暗示難度較低。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"plans for the future","meaning":"未來計劃","examples":[{"en":"The agency probably will not ask about Amber’s plans for the future.","zh":"介紹所大概不會問 Amber 的未來計劃。"},{"en":"Plans for the future are ideas or intentions about what someone hopes to do later.","zh":"plans for the future 指某人希望日後做甚麼的想法或打算。"},{"en":"Students often discuss their plans for the future with careers teachers.","zh":"學生常與職業老師討論未來計劃。"},{"en":"If an interviewer asks about future plans, they may want to understand long-term goals.","zh":"如果面試官問未來計劃，可能想了解長遠目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes future aims.","zh":"這個短語描述未來目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hope not","meaning":"希望不會","examples":[{"en":"Amber says, “Hope not,” when William mentions difficult questions.","zh":"William 提到困難問題時，Amber 說：「希望不會。」"},{"en":"Hope not means I hope that will not happen.","zh":"hope not 指我希望那件事不會發生。"},{"en":"When asked whether the test would be harder this year, the student said, “Hope not.”","zh":"當被問到今年測驗是否會更難時，學生說：「希望不會。」"},{"en":"Amber says this because she does not want difficult questions in the interview.","zh":"Amber 這樣說，是因為她不想面試有困難問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is short and informal.","zh":"這個短語簡短而口語化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"benefits to using","meaning":"使用……的好處","examples":[{"en":"There are many benefits to using a job agency.","zh":"使用職業介紹所有很多好處。"},{"en":"Benefits to using something are the advantages gained from using it.","zh":"benefits to using something 指使用某物所得到的優點。"},{"en":"There are benefits to using a timetable when preparing for exams.","zh":"準備考試時，使用時間表有好處。"},{"en":"If Amber understands the benefits of using an agency, she may feel more confident about registering.","zh":"如果 Amber 明白使用介紹所的好處，可能對登記更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces advantages.","zh":"這個短語引出優點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"give feedback on","meaning":"就……給予意見","examples":[{"en":"The agency will give Amber feedback on her performance.","zh":"介紹所會就 Amber 的表現給予意見。"},{"en":"To give feedback on something means to provide comments about how well someone did.","zh":"give feedback on something 指就某人的表現提供評語。"},{"en":"The teacher gave feedback on the students’ presentations.","zh":"老師就學生的簡報給予意見。"},{"en":"If Amber receives feedback, she can improve her interview technique.","zh":"如果 Amber 收到意見，就能改善面試技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving useful comments for improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述提供有助改進的評語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"your performance","meaning":"你的表現","examples":[{"en":"The agency will give Amber feedback on her interview performance.","zh":"介紹所會就 Amber 的面試表現給予意見。"},{"en":"Your performance means how well you do in a task, interview, exam, or activity.","zh":"your performance 指你在任務、面試、考試或活動中的表現如何。"},{"en":"The coach praised the team’s performance after the match.","zh":"教練在比賽後稱讚隊伍的表現。"},{"en":"If Amber knows how her performance was judged, she can prepare better next time.","zh":"如果 Amber 知道自己的表現如何被評價，下次就能準備得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the quality of someone’s actions.","zh":"這個短語指某人行動的質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"improve next time","meaning":"下次改進","examples":[{"en":"The feedback can help Amber improve next time.","zh":"這些意見可以幫助 Amber 下次改進。"},{"en":"To improve next time means to do better on a future attempt.","zh":"improve next time 指在下一次嘗試中做得更好。"},{"en":"After reading the teacher’s comments, the student improved next time.","zh":"閱讀老師評語後，學生下次改進了。"},{"en":"If Amber acts on the feedback, her next interview may be stronger.","zh":"如果 Amber 根據意見行動，下一次面試可能更好。"},{"en":"This phrase connects feedback with future progress.","zh":"這個短語把回饋與未來進步連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have access to","meaning":"可以接觸到","examples":[{"en":"Agencies have access to jobs which are not advertised.","zh":"介紹所可以接觸到沒有公開刊登的工作。"},{"en":"To have access to something means to be able to reach, use, or obtain it.","zh":"have access to something 指能接觸、使用或取得某物。"},{"en":"Students have access to online journals through the school library.","zh":"學生可以透過學校圖書館使用網上期刊。"},{"en":"If agencies have access to hidden jobs, candidates may find opportunities they cannot find alone.","zh":"如果介紹所可以接觸到隱藏職位，求職者可能找到自己無法獨自找到的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being able to use or reach something.","zh":"這個短語描述能使用或接觸某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"jobs which are not advertised","meaning":"沒有公開刊登的工作","examples":[{"en":"Agencies can find jobs which are not advertised.","zh":"介紹所可以找到沒有公開刊登的工作。"},{"en":"Jobs which are not advertised are vacancies that are not publicly posted online or in newspapers.","zh":"jobs which are not advertised 指沒有在網上或報章公開發布的職位空缺。"},{"en":"Some companies give jobs which are not advertised directly to trusted agencies.","zh":"有些公司會把沒有公開刊登的工作直接交給信任的介紹所。"},{"en":"If Amber uses an agency, she may hear about jobs that ordinary applicants never see.","zh":"如果 Amber 使用介紹所，可能聽到一般求職者看不到的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hidden job opportunities.","zh":"這個短語描述隱藏工作機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"temporary jobs","meaning":"臨時工作","examples":[{"en":"Most temporary jobs are not advertised.","zh":"大多數臨時工作沒有公開刊登。"},{"en":"Temporary jobs are jobs that last for a limited period rather than permanently.","zh":"temporary jobs 指持續有限時間而不是永久的工作。"},{"en":"Students may take temporary jobs during summer holidays.","zh":"學生可能在暑假做臨時工作。"},{"en":"If temporary jobs are not advertised, agencies become especially useful.","zh":"如果臨時工作沒有公開刊登，介紹所就特別有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes short-term employment.","zh":"這個短語描述短期就業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"finding a temporary job","meaning":"尋找臨時工作","examples":[{"en":"Amber expects finding a temporary job through an agency to take less time.","zh":"Amber 預期透過介紹所尋找臨時工作會花較少時間。"},{"en":"Finding a temporary job means looking for and getting short-term work.","zh":"finding a temporary job 指尋找並得到短期工作。"},{"en":"Finding a temporary job can be easier if someone has a clear CV.","zh":"如果有清晰履歷，尋找臨時工作可能更容易。"},{"en":"If Amber uses an agency, finding temporary work may be quicker.","zh":"如果 Amber 使用介紹所，尋找臨時工作可能更快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of getting short-term employment.","zh":"這個短語描述取得短期工作的過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"this way","meaning":"以這種方式","examples":[{"en":"Finding a temporary job this way takes less time.","zh":"以這種方式尋找臨時工作花較少時間。"},{"en":"This way means by using this method or approach.","zh":"this way 指使用這種方法或途徑。"},{"en":"Applying online this way saves students from posting paper forms.","zh":"以這種方式網上申請，可以省去學生郵寄紙本表格。"},{"en":"If Amber searches through an agency, this way may save time and effort.","zh":"如果 Amber 透過介紹所尋找工作，這種方式可能節省時間和精力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the method just mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指剛提到的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take a lot less time","meaning":"花少很多時間","examples":[{"en":"Using an agency takes a lot less time.","zh":"使用介紹所花少很多時間。"},{"en":"To take a lot less time means to require much fewer hours or days than another method.","zh":"take a lot less time 指比另一方法需要少很多小時或日子。"},{"en":"Booking online takes a lot less time than queuing at the counter.","zh":"網上預訂比在櫃位排隊花少很多時間。"},{"en":"If Amber uses an agency, she may avoid contacting many companies one by one.","zh":"如果 Amber 使用介紹所，就可能避免逐間公司聯絡。"},{"en":"This phrase compares time saved.","zh":"這個短語比較節省的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ring up","meaning":"致電","examples":[{"en":"Using an agency is easier than ringing up individual companies.","zh":"使用介紹所比致電個別公司更容易。"},{"en":"To ring up someone means to phone them.","zh":"ring up someone 指致電給某人。"},{"en":"She rang up the school office to ask about the interview time.","zh":"她致電學校辦公室查詢面試時間。"},{"en":"If Amber rings up many companies herself, the search may take longer.","zh":"如果 Amber 自己致電很多公司，求職可能需時更長。"},{"en":"This British phrase means to call by phone.","zh":"這個英式短語意思是打電話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"individual companies","meaning":"個別公司","examples":[{"en":"Amber thinks using an agency is easier than calling individual companies.","zh":"Amber 認為使用介紹所比致電個別公司更容易。"},{"en":"Individual companies means separate companies contacted one by one.","zh":"individual companies 指逐一聯絡的不同公司。"},{"en":"Instead of emailing individual companies, students used a job website.","zh":"學生沒有逐間電郵個別公司，而是使用求職網站。"},{"en":"If Amber contacts individual companies herself, she may need to repeat the same information many times.","zh":"如果 Amber 自己聯絡個別公司，可能需要多次重複相同資料。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises separate organisations rather than one central service.","zh":"這個短語強調不同獨立機構，而不是一個集中服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"yes indeed","meaning":"的確是","examples":[{"en":"William says, “Yes indeed,” when Amber mentions saving time.","zh":"Amber 提到節省時間時，William 說：「的確是。」"},{"en":"Yes indeed means yes, certainly, and often strongly agrees with what someone has said.","zh":"yes indeed 指是的，確實如此，常表示強烈同意對方所說。"},{"en":"When the student said the new system was faster, the teacher replied, “Yes indeed.”","zh":"當學生說新系統更快時，老師回答：「的確是。」"},{"en":"William uses this phrase to confirm that using an agency saves time.","zh":"William 使用這個短語來確認使用介紹所能節省時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and emphatic.","zh":"這個短語有禮而帶強調。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10}],"ielts/listening/Practice 20/task-2":[{"front":"island holidays","meaning":"海島假期","examples":[{"en":"Matthews Island Holidays offers holidays to island destinations.","zh":"Matthews Island Holidays 提供前往海島目的地的假期。"},{"en":"Island holidays are trips or vacations spent on islands.","zh":"海島假期是在島嶼上度過的旅程或假期。"},{"en":"Many people choose island holidays because they enjoy the sea, scenery and slower pace of life.","zh":"許多人選擇海島假期，因為他們喜歡海、風景和較慢的生活節奏。"},{"en":"Island holidays may include ferry travel, coastal walks and visits to historic sites.","zh":"海島假期可能包括渡輪旅程、海岸散步和參觀歷史景點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing travel packages to islands.","zh":"這個短語適合用於描述前往島嶼的旅遊套票。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"owner of","meaning":"……的負責人；東主","examples":[{"en":"Erica Matthews is the owner of Matthews Island Holidays.","zh":"Erica Matthews 是 Matthews Island Holidays 的負責人。"},{"en":"The owner of a company is the person who owns or runs it.","zh":"一間公司的負責人或東主是擁有或經營它的人。"},{"en":"The owner of a small travel company often deals directly with customers.","zh":"小型旅遊公司的負責人通常會直接與顧客溝通。"},{"en":"Knowing the owner of a business can make the service feel more personal.","zh":"知道一間公司的東主是誰，可以令服務感覺更有人情味。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who is responsible for or possesses something.","zh":"這個短語指出誰負責或擁有某事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"company set up by","meaning":"由……創立的公司","examples":[{"en":"Matthews Island Holidays is a company set up by Erica’s parents.","zh":"Matthews Island Holidays 是由 Erica 父母創立的公司。"},{"en":"A company set up by someone is a business that person started or founded.","zh":"由某人創立的公司，是由那個人開始或建立的企業。"},{"en":"A family shop set up by grandparents may later be run by their children.","zh":"由祖父母創立的家庭店舖，之後可能由子女經營。"},{"en":"Knowing who set up a company can explain its history and values.","zh":"知道公司由誰創立，可以解釋其歷史和價值觀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the founder of a business.","zh":"這個短語描述企業的創辦人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"thank you for coming to","meaning":"感謝大家來到……","examples":[{"en":"Erica thanks the audience for coming to the presentation.","zh":"Erica 感謝觀眾來到介紹會。"},{"en":"Thank you for coming to is a polite way to show appreciation for someone’s attendance.","zh":"感謝大家來到某活動，是有禮貌地感謝別人出席。"},{"en":"A speaker may say, “Thank you for coming to our travel talk.”","zh":"講者可能說：「感謝大家來到我們的旅遊講座。」"},{"en":"This phrase is often used at the beginning of meetings, talks and events.","zh":"這個短語常用於會議、講座和活動開頭。"},{"en":"It helps create a friendly and respectful opening.","zh":"它有助營造友善而尊重的開場。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"presentation","meaning":"介紹會；簡報","examples":[{"en":"Erica gives a presentation about the holidays her company offers.","zh":"Erica 就她公司提供的假期作介紹會。"},{"en":"A presentation is a talk given to explain information to an audience.","zh":"介紹會或簡報是向觀眾解釋資訊的講話。"},{"en":"A travel company may give a presentation to introduce new holiday packages.","zh":"旅遊公司可能舉辦介紹會，介紹新的假期套票。"},{"en":"Good presentations use clear examples, useful details and a confident speaker.","zh":"好的簡報會使用清楚例子、有用細節和有信心的講者。"},{"en":"This word is common in school, business and public events.","zh":"這個詞常見於學校、商業和公共活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"interest someone in","meaning":"令某人對……感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Erica hopes to interest the audience in what the company offers.","zh":"Erica 希望令觀眾對公司所提供的東西感興趣。"},{"en":"To interest someone in something means to make them curious about it or want to know more.","zh":"令某人對某事感興趣意思是使他們好奇或想了解更多。"},{"en":"A guide may interest tourists in a destination by showing beautiful photos.","zh":"導遊可能透過展示美麗照片，令旅客對目的地感興趣。"},{"en":"Interesting details can help customers imagine the holiday experience.","zh":"有趣細節可以幫助顧客想像假期體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attracting someone’s attention.","zh":"這個短語描述吸引某人的注意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what we have to offer","meaning":"我們所提供的東西","examples":[{"en":"Erica explains what Matthews Island Holidays has to offer.","zh":"Erica 解釋 Matthews Island Holidays 所提供的東西。"},{"en":"What we have to offer means the services, products or advantages we can provide.","zh":"我們所提供的東西意思是我們能提供的服務、產品或優點。"},{"en":"A hotel may describe what it has to offer, such as rooms, meals and tours.","zh":"酒店可能描述它所提供的東西，例如房間、餐飲和旅行團。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a business or service.","zh":"這個短語適合用於介紹公司或服務。"},{"en":"It focuses on the value given to customers.","zh":"它重點是提供給顧客的價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"family-run company","meaning":"家族經營的公司","examples":[{"en":"Matthews Island Holidays is a small, family-run company.","zh":"Matthews Island Holidays 是一間小型家族經營的公司。"},{"en":"A family-run company is a business managed by members of the same family.","zh":"家族經營的公司是由同一家族成員管理的企業。"},{"en":"A family-run company may offer a more personal and friendly service.","zh":"家族經營的公司可能提供更個人化和友善的服務。"},{"en":"Customers may feel that a family-run business cares more about individual needs.","zh":"顧客可能覺得家族企業更關心個別需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the ownership and management style of a business.","zh":"這個短語描述企業的擁有和管理方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"believe in","meaning":"相信……的重要性","examples":[{"en":"The company believes in the importance of the personal touch.","zh":"公司相信個人化服務的重要性。"},{"en":"To believe in something means to think it is valuable, important or true.","zh":"相信某事意思是認為它有價值、重要或真實。"},{"en":"A small company may believe in honest service and long-term relationships.","zh":"小公司可能相信誠實服務和長期關係的重要性。"},{"en":"What a company believes in often shapes how it treats customers.","zh":"公司相信甚麼，通常會塑造它如何對待顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes values or principles.","zh":"這個短語描述價值觀或原則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"personal touch","meaning":"個人化服務；人情味","examples":[{"en":"The company believes in the importance of the personal touch.","zh":"公司相信個人化服務的重要性。"},{"en":"The personal touch means friendly, individual care rather than a standard impersonal service.","zh":"個人化服務或人情味意思是友善而照顧個別需要，而不是標準化、冷冰冰的服務。"},{"en":"A travel agent adds a personal touch by remembering a customer’s preferences.","zh":"旅遊代理記住顧客偏好，就是加入人情味。"},{"en":"The personal touch can make customers feel valued and understood.","zh":"個人化服務可以令顧客感到受重視和被理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in service and hospitality contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於服務和款待語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"aim to","meaning":"旨在；目的是","examples":[{"en":"The company does not aim to compete on the number of customers.","zh":"公司並不旨在以顧客數量來競爭。"},{"en":"To aim to do something means to have that goal or intention.","zh":"旨在做某事意思是有該目標或意圖。"},{"en":"Some small businesses aim to provide quality rather than serve huge numbers.","zh":"有些小企業旨在提供質素，而不是服務極大量顧客。"},{"en":"Clear aims help customers understand what a company values.","zh":"清楚目標有助顧客理解公司重視甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase explains purpose.","zh":"這個短語解釋目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"compete with","meaning":"與……競爭","examples":[{"en":"The company does not aim to compete with larger companies.","zh":"公司並不旨在與較大型公司競爭。"},{"en":"To compete with someone means to try to succeed against them in the same market or activity.","zh":"與某人競爭意思是在同一市場或活動中嘗試勝過對方。"},{"en":"A small hotel may not compete with big chains on price.","zh":"小型酒店未必會在價格上與大型連鎖酒店競爭。"},{"en":"Instead, it may compete through service, knowledge and personal care.","zh":"相反，它可能透過服務、知識和個人照顧來競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business and sport.","zh":"這個短語常見於商業和運動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the number of customers","meaning":"顧客數量","examples":[{"en":"The company does not compete on the number of customers.","zh":"公司不以顧客數量作競爭重點。"},{"en":"The number of customers means how many customers a business has or serves.","zh":"顧客數量意思是一間公司擁有或服務多少顧客。"},{"en":"Some companies focus on the number of customers, while others focus on service quality.","zh":"有些公司重視顧客數量，而另一些重視服務質素。"},{"en":"A small tour company may prefer fewer customers and more personal attention.","zh":"小型旅行公司可能較喜歡較少顧客和更多個人照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes customer quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述顧客的數目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"build on","meaning":"建基於；憑藉","examples":[{"en":"The company builds on its many years of experience.","zh":"公司建基於其多年經驗。"},{"en":"To build on something means to use it as a foundation for further development.","zh":"建基於某事意思是把它用作進一步發展的基礎。"},{"en":"A teacher builds on students’ basic vocabulary before teaching harder texts.","zh":"老師先建基於學生的基本詞彙，再教授較難文本。"},{"en":"A company can build on experience to improve future services.","zh":"公司可以憑藉經驗改善未來服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes developing from an existing strength.","zh":"這個短語描述從已有優勢發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"many years’ experience","meaning":"多年經驗","examples":[{"en":"The company builds on its many years’ experience.","zh":"公司憑藉其多年經驗。"},{"en":"Many years’ experience means knowledge and skill gained over a long period.","zh":"多年經驗意思是在長時間中累積的知識和技能。"},{"en":"A tour manager with many years’ experience can solve travel problems quickly.","zh":"有多年經驗的旅行領隊可以快速解決旅程問題。"},{"en":"Experience helps a company understand what customers need.","zh":"經驗幫助公司理解顧客需要甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises long-term practical knowledge.","zh":"這個短語強調長期實用知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rail holiday company","meaning":"鐵路假期公司","examples":[{"en":"Matthews Island Holidays has more experience than almost any other rail holiday company.","zh":"Matthews Island Holidays 比幾乎任何其他鐵路假期公司都有更多經驗。"},{"en":"A rail holiday company is a travel business that organises holidays involving train journeys.","zh":"鐵路假期公司是安排包含火車旅程的假期的旅遊公司。"},{"en":"Rail holiday companies may arrange tickets, hotels, tours and local transport.","zh":"鐵路假期公司可能安排車票、酒店、行程和本地交通。"},{"en":"Train-based holidays can appeal to travellers who enjoy scenic journeys.","zh":"以火車為主的假期可以吸引喜歡風景旅程的旅客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specialised travel company.","zh":"這個短語描述專門的旅遊公司。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ensure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"The company uses its experience to ensure perfect holidays.","zh":"公司運用其經驗來確保完美假期。"},{"en":"To ensure means to make certain that something happens.","zh":"確保意思是使某事必定發生。"},{"en":"A tour company checks hotel bookings carefully to ensure a smooth trip.","zh":"旅行公司仔細核對酒店預訂，以確保旅程順利。"},{"en":"Good planning helps ensure customers feel relaxed during the holiday.","zh":"良好規劃有助確保顧客在假期中感到輕鬆。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing responsibility and quality control.","zh":"這個詞適合用於描述責任和質素控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"provide perfect holidays","meaning":"提供完美假期","examples":[{"en":"The company aims to provide perfect holidays in a few destinations.","zh":"公司旨在於少數目的地提供完美假期。"},{"en":"To provide perfect holidays means to offer trips that are well-planned and highly satisfying.","zh":"提供完美假期意思是提供規劃周全、令人非常滿意的旅程。"},{"en":"A company may provide perfect holidays by choosing good hotels and reliable transport.","zh":"公司可以透過選擇好酒店和可靠交通來提供完美假期。"},{"en":"Perfect holidays depend on careful organisation and local knowledge.","zh":"完美假期取決於細心安排和本地知識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the company’s service goal.","zh":"這個短語描述公司的服務目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"small number of destinations","meaning":"少數目的地","examples":[{"en":"The company focuses on a small number of destinations.","zh":"公司集中於少數目的地。"},{"en":"A small number of destinations means only a few places.","zh":"少數目的地意思是只有幾個地方。"},{"en":"A travel company may focus on a small number of destinations so it can know them deeply.","zh":"旅行公司可能集中於少數目的地，以便深入了解它們。"},{"en":"Fewer destinations can allow better planning and more personal advice.","zh":"較少目的地可以帶來更好規劃和更個人化建議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a limited but focused range.","zh":"這個短語描述有限但集中的範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"get to know extremely well","meaning":"對……非常熟悉","examples":[{"en":"The company has got to know its destinations extremely well.","zh":"公司已經對其目的地非常熟悉。"},{"en":"To get to know something extremely well means to become very familiar with it over time.","zh":"對某事非常熟悉意思是隨時間變得非常了解它。"},{"en":"A guide gets to know an island extremely well after leading tours there for years.","zh":"導遊在某島帶團多年後，會對該島非常熟悉。"},{"en":"Deep knowledge of destinations helps companies answer customers’ questions accurately.","zh":"對目的地有深入認識，有助公司準確回答顧客問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong familiarity built through experience.","zh":"這個短語描述透過經驗建立的高度熟悉。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"six-day holiday","meaning":"六天假期","examples":[{"en":"Erica starts with the company’s six-day Isle of Man holiday.","zh":"Erica 先介紹公司的六天 Isle of Man 假期。"},{"en":"A six-day holiday is a trip that lasts six days.","zh":"六天假期是持續六日的旅程。"},{"en":"A six-day holiday gives travellers enough time to visit several places without rushing too much.","zh":"六天假期讓旅客有足夠時間參觀幾個地方，而不會太趕。"},{"en":"Shorter holidays may be easier for people with limited time.","zh":"較短假期對時間有限的人可能較容易安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the length of a travel package.","zh":"這個短語描述旅遊套票的長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fascinating island","meaning":"迷人的島嶼","examples":[{"en":"The Isle of Man is a fascinating island in the Irish Sea.","zh":"Isle of Man 是愛爾蘭海上一個迷人的島嶼。"},{"en":"A fascinating island is an island that is very interesting or attractive.","zh":"迷人的島嶼是非常有趣或吸引人的島。"},{"en":"A fascinating island may have unusual history, scenery and traditions.","zh":"迷人的島嶼可能有獨特歷史、風景和傳統。"},{"en":"Describing a place as fascinating can make travellers curious about it.","zh":"把一個地方形容為迷人，可以令旅客對它好奇。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a positive description of a destination.","zh":"這個短語對目的地作出正面描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Irish Sea","meaning":"愛爾蘭海","examples":[{"en":"The Isle of Man is in the Irish Sea.","zh":"Isle of Man 位於愛爾蘭海。"},{"en":"The Irish Sea is the sea between Great Britain and Ireland.","zh":"愛爾蘭海是位於大不列顛和愛爾蘭之間的海。"},{"en":"Ferries cross the Irish Sea to reach islands and coastal ports.","zh":"渡輪會橫越愛爾蘭海，前往島嶼和沿岸港口。"},{"en":"Knowing the sea location helps travellers understand the island’s geography.","zh":"知道海域位置有助旅客理解島嶼地理。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific body of water.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定水域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"to the south","meaning":"在南面","examples":[{"en":"Wales is to the south of the Isle of Man.","zh":"Wales 在 Isle of Man 的南面。"},{"en":"To the south means located in the southern direction from a place.","zh":"在南面意思是位於某地的南方方向。"},{"en":"A town to the south of the island may be warmer or easier to reach by ferry.","zh":"島南面的城鎮可能較暖或較容易乘渡輪到達。"},{"en":"Direction phrases help describe a location clearly.","zh":"方位短語有助清楚描述位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in geography and travel.","zh":"這個短語適合用於地理和旅遊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"to the east","meaning":"在東面","examples":[{"en":"England is to the east of the Isle of Man.","zh":"England 在 Isle of Man 的東面。"},{"en":"To the east means located in the eastern direction from a place.","zh":"在東面意思是位於某地的東方方向。"},{"en":"The mainland lies to the east of the island.","zh":"大陸位於該島的東面。"},{"en":"Travellers use directions like east and west to understand maps.","zh":"旅客使用東西南北等方向來理解地圖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relative location.","zh":"這個短語描述相對位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"to the north","meaning":"在北面","examples":[{"en":"Scotland is to the north of the Isle of Man.","zh":"Scotland 在 Isle of Man 的北面。"},{"en":"To the north means located in the northern direction from a place.","zh":"在北面意思是位於某地的北方方向。"},{"en":"Mountains to the north of a town may affect its weather.","zh":"城鎮北面的山脈可能影響其天氣。"},{"en":"Directional language helps listeners picture geography.","zh":"方位語言有助聽眾想像地理位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where one place is compared with another.","zh":"這個短語描述一個地方相對於另一個地方的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"to the west","meaning":"在西面","examples":[{"en":"Northern Ireland is to the west of the Isle of Man.","zh":"Northern Ireland 在 Isle of Man 的西面。"},{"en":"To the west means located in the western direction from a place.","zh":"在西面意思是位於某地的西方方向。"},{"en":"The harbour is to the west of the town centre.","zh":"港口在市中心的西面。"},{"en":"West, east, north and south are basic map directions.","zh":"東、西、南、北是基本地圖方向。"},{"en":"This phrase gives geographical orientation.","zh":"這個短語提供地理方位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"start in","meaning":"從……開始","examples":[{"en":"The holiday starts in Heysham.","zh":"假期從 Heysham 開始。"},{"en":"To start in a place means to begin there.","zh":"從某地開始意思是在那裏開始。"},{"en":"The tour starts in London before travelling north.","zh":"旅程從 London 開始，然後向北前往。"},{"en":"Knowing where a holiday starts helps customers plan how to get there.","zh":"知道假期從哪裏開始，有助顧客安排如何前往。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the starting point of a trip.","zh":"這個短語指出旅程起點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"tour manager","meaning":"旅行領隊","examples":[{"en":"Your tour manager will meet you in Heysham.","zh":"你的旅行領隊會在 Heysham 接你。"},{"en":"A tour manager is the person responsible for organising and guiding a tour group.","zh":"旅行領隊是負責組織和帶領旅行團的人。"},{"en":"The tour manager checks tickets, gives information and helps solve travel problems.","zh":"旅行領隊會檢查車票、提供資訊並協助解決旅程問題。"},{"en":"A good tour manager can make customers feel relaxed and well looked after.","zh":"好的旅行領隊可以令顧客感到輕鬆和被照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase names an important role in organised travel.","zh":"這個短語命名有組織旅遊中的重要角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"travel by ferry","meaning":"乘渡輪前往","examples":[{"en":"Customers travel by ferry to the Isle of Man.","zh":"顧客乘渡輪前往 Isle of Man。"},{"en":"To travel by ferry means to go by a boat that carries passengers across water.","zh":"乘渡輪前往意思是乘坐載客船橫越水域。"},{"en":"Many island holidays involve travelling by ferry from a coastal port.","zh":"許多海島假期都涉及從沿岸港口乘渡輪前往。"},{"en":"Ferry travel can be scenic and relaxing for tourists.","zh":"對旅客來說，渡輪旅程可以風景優美而令人放鬆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the method of transport.","zh":"這個短語描述交通方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prefer to","meaning":"較喜歡……","examples":[{"en":"Some people prefer to fly from Luton instead.","zh":"有些人則較喜歡從 Luton 乘飛機。"},{"en":"To prefer to do something means to like that option more than another.","zh":"較喜歡做某事意思是比另一選項更喜歡該做法。"},{"en":"Some travellers prefer to fly because it is faster than taking a ferry.","zh":"有些旅客較喜歡乘飛機，因為比乘渡輪快。"},{"en":"Preferences often depend on time, cost and comfort.","zh":"偏好通常取決於時間、費用和舒適程度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing one option over another.","zh":"這個短語描述在選項中偏好其中一個。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fly from","meaning":"從……乘飛機","examples":[{"en":"Some people prefer to fly from Luton.","zh":"有些人較喜歡從 Luton 乘飛機。"},{"en":"To fly from a place means to take a plane starting at that airport or city.","zh":"從某地乘飛機意思是從該機場或城市出發乘搭飛機。"},{"en":"Travellers can fly from Manchester to reach the island more quickly.","zh":"旅客可以從 Manchester 乘飛機，更快到達島上。"},{"en":"The departure airport affects convenience and travel time.","zh":"出發機場會影響便利程度和旅程時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the starting point of an air journey.","zh":"這個短語描述飛行旅程的起點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"popular option","meaning":"受歡迎的選擇","examples":[{"en":"Another popular option is to go by train to Liverpool.","zh":"另一個受歡迎的選擇是乘火車前往 Liverpool。"},{"en":"A popular option is a choice that many people like or choose.","zh":"受歡迎的選擇是許多人喜歡或選擇的方案。"},{"en":"Taking the train may be a popular option because it is comfortable and scenic.","zh":"乘火車可能是受歡迎的選擇，因為它舒適且風景優美。"},{"en":"Travel companies often explain popular options to help customers decide.","zh":"旅行公司常解釋受歡迎的選擇，以幫助顧客決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a widely chosen alternative.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛被選擇的替代方案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"go by train","meaning":"乘火車前往","examples":[{"en":"Some customers go by train to Liverpool.","zh":"有些顧客乘火車前往 Liverpool。"},{"en":"To go by train means to travel using a train.","zh":"乘火車前往意思是使用火車作交通方式。"},{"en":"Tourists may go by train before taking a ferry to an island.","zh":"旅客可能先乘火車，再轉乘渡輪前往島嶼。"},{"en":"Train travel can be convenient when stations are close to ferry ports.","zh":"當車站靠近渡輪碼頭，火車旅程會很方便。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mode of transport.","zh":"這個短語描述交通方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take a ferry from","meaning":"從……乘渡輪","examples":[{"en":"Customers can take a ferry from Liverpool.","zh":"顧客可以從 Liverpool 乘渡輪。"},{"en":"To take a ferry from a place means to board a ferry starting there.","zh":"從某地乘渡輪意思是在那裏登上渡輪出發。"},{"en":"Visitors may take a ferry from the port after arriving by train.","zh":"訪客乘火車到達後，可能從港口乘渡輪。"},{"en":"Taking a ferry from a convenient city can make the journey easier.","zh":"從方便的城市乘渡輪可以令旅程更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the departure point for ferry travel.","zh":"這個短語提供渡輪旅程的出發地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"five nights in the hotel","meaning":"在酒店住五晚","examples":[{"en":"Customers have five nights in the hotel.","zh":"顧客會在酒店住五晚。"},{"en":"Five nights in the hotel means staying at the hotel for five overnight periods.","zh":"在酒店住五晚意思是在酒店過夜五次。"},{"en":"A six-day holiday often includes five nights in a hotel.","zh":"六天假期通常包括在酒店住五晚。"},{"en":"Knowing the number of nights helps customers understand the accommodation included.","zh":"知道住宿晚數有助顧客理解包含的住宿安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the length of a hotel stay.","zh":"這個短語描述酒店住宿長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the price covers","meaning":"價格包括","examples":[{"en":"The price covers five breakfasts and dinners.","zh":"價格包括五份早餐和晚餐。"},{"en":"The price covers something means it is included in the amount customers pay.","zh":"價格包括某物意思是顧客支付的金額已包含它。"},{"en":"The tour price covers transport, accommodation and some meals.","zh":"團費包括交通、住宿和部分餐食。"},{"en":"Customers should check what the price covers before booking.","zh":"顧客在預訂前應查看價格包括甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what is included in a fee.","zh":"這個短語解釋費用包含內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"organised trips","meaning":"已安排的團體行程","examples":[{"en":"Lunch is included on the three days with organised trips.","zh":"在有已安排團體行程的三天，午餐也包括在內。"},{"en":"Organised trips are planned outings arranged by a company, school or group.","zh":"已安排的團體行程是由公司、學校或團體規劃的外出活動。"},{"en":"Organised trips may include transport, guides and entrance tickets.","zh":"已安排的團體行程可能包括交通、導遊和門票。"},{"en":"Meals are sometimes included when trips last most of the day.","zh":"當行程持續大半天，餐食有時會包括在內。"},{"en":"This phrase describes scheduled group excursions.","zh":"這個短語描述已排定的團體遊覽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"day four is free","meaning":"第四天是自由活動","examples":[{"en":"Day four is free for customers to explore.","zh":"第四天是讓顧客自由探索的日子。"},{"en":"Day four is free means there are no fixed group activities on the fourth day.","zh":"第四天是自由活動意思是第四天沒有固定團體活動。"},{"en":"A free day lets travellers choose their own pace and interests.","zh":"自由活動日讓旅客按自己的節奏和興趣安排。"},{"en":"Some customers may use a free day to rest, shop or visit extra places.","zh":"有些顧客可能利用自由活動日休息、購物或參觀額外地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unscheduled day in a tour.","zh":"這個短語描述旅行團中的非固定行程日。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the price of the holiday","meaning":"假期價格","examples":[{"en":"The price of the holiday includes ferry travel and accommodation.","zh":"假期價格包括渡輪旅程和住宿。"},{"en":"The price of the holiday means the total cost customers pay for the trip.","zh":"假期價格意思是顧客為旅程支付的總費用。"},{"en":"Customers compare the price of the holiday with what is included.","zh":"顧客會比較假期價格和包含內容。"},{"en":"A clear holiday price helps people budget before booking.","zh":"清楚的假期價格有助人們在預訂前做預算。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the cost of a travel package.","zh":"這個短語指旅遊套票的費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"all travel on the island","meaning":"島上所有交通","examples":[{"en":"The price includes all travel on the island.","zh":"價格包括島上所有交通。"},{"en":"All travel on the island means every journey within the island during the holiday.","zh":"島上所有交通意思是假期期間在島內的每段旅程。"},{"en":"If all travel on the island is included, customers do not need to buy separate local tickets.","zh":"如果島上所有交通已包括，顧客就不用另買本地車票。"},{"en":"This can make the holiday simpler and easier to budget for.","zh":"這可以令假期更簡單，也更容易做預算。"},{"en":"This phrase describes included local transport.","zh":"這個短語描述已包含的本地交通。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"meals I’ve mentioned","meaning":"我提到的餐食","examples":[{"en":"The price includes the meals Erica has mentioned.","zh":"價格包括 Erica 提到的餐食。"},{"en":"Meals I’ve mentioned means the breakfasts, dinners or lunches already referred to by the speaker.","zh":"我提到的餐食意思是講者之前已說過的早餐、晚餐或午餐。"},{"en":"A speaker may say the price includes the meals I’ve mentioned to avoid repeating the list.","zh":"講者可能說價格包括我提到的餐食，以免重複清單。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to earlier information.","zh":"這個短語指回較早資訊。"},{"en":"It is useful in spoken explanations.","zh":"它適合用於口頭解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"incidentally","meaning":"順帶一提","examples":[{"en":"Incidentally, the company tries to make booking simple and fair.","zh":"順帶一提，公司嘗試令預訂簡單而公平。"},{"en":"Incidentally means by the way or as an additional point.","zh":"順帶一提意思是附帶提及或補充一點。"},{"en":"Incidentally, customers can also change their travel date for a small fee.","zh":"順帶一提，顧客也可以支付小額費用更改出發日期。"},{"en":"This word introduces extra information that is related but not the main point.","zh":"這個詞引入相關但非主要重點的額外資訊。"},{"en":"It is common in presentations and conversation.","zh":"它常見於匯報和對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make booking simple and fair","meaning":"令預訂簡單而公平","examples":[{"en":"The company tries to make booking its holidays simple and fair.","zh":"公司嘗試令其假期預訂簡單而公平。"},{"en":"To make booking simple and fair means to make the reservation process easy and equal for customers.","zh":"令預訂簡單而公平意思是令預約過程容易，並對顧客公平。"},{"en":"Clear prices and flexible date changes can make booking simple and fair.","zh":"清楚價格和靈活改期可以令預訂簡單而公平。"},{"en":"Customers appreciate booking systems that are easy to understand.","zh":"顧客欣賞容易理解的預訂系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a customer-friendly booking policy.","zh":"這個短語描述顧客友善的預訂政策。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"as simple and fair as possible","meaning":"盡量簡單和公平","examples":[{"en":"The company makes booking as simple and fair as possible.","zh":"公司令預訂盡量簡單和公平。"},{"en":"As simple and fair as possible means to the greatest reasonable degree of simplicity and fairness.","zh":"盡量簡單和公平意思是在合理情況下最大程度地簡單和公平。"},{"en":"A school tries to make registration as simple and fair as possible for all parents.","zh":"學校嘗試令所有家長的報名過程盡量簡單和公平。"},{"en":"This phrase shows effort to improve a process for everyone.","zh":"這個短語顯示為每個人改善流程的努力。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing service aims.","zh":"它適合用於描述服務目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"unlike with","meaning":"不像……","examples":[{"en":"Unlike with many companies, the price stays the same.","zh":"不像許多公司，價格保持不變。"},{"en":"Unlike with means different from the situation with something else.","zh":"不像某事意思是與另一情況不同。"},{"en":"Unlike with some airlines, this company does not change the price at the last minute.","zh":"不像有些航空公司，這家公司不會在最後一刻改變價格。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between two cases.","zh":"這個短語引入兩種情況之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing policies.","zh":"當比較政策時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"book six months in advance","meaning":"提前六個月預訂","examples":[{"en":"The price is the same if customers book six months in advance.","zh":"如果顧客提前六個月預訂，價格也一樣。"},{"en":"To book six months in advance means to reserve something six months before it happens.","zh":"提前六個月預訂意思是在事情發生前六個月作出預約。"},{"en":"Some travellers book six months in advance to secure their preferred dates.","zh":"有些旅客提前六個月預訂，以確保自己想要的日期。"},{"en":"Booking early can help with planning, but this company keeps the price the same.","zh":"提早預訂有助規劃，但這家公司保持價格不變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes early reservation.","zh":"這個短語描述早期預約。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at the last minute","meaning":"在最後一刻","examples":[{"en":"The price is the same even if customers book at the last minute.","zh":"即使顧客在最後一刻預訂，價格也一樣。"},{"en":"At the last minute means very close to the time when something will happen.","zh":"在最後一刻意思是非常接近事情發生的時間。"},{"en":"Some people book holidays at the last minute because their work schedule changes suddenly.","zh":"有些人因工作時間突然改變而在最後一刻預訂假期。"},{"en":"Last-minute booking can be stressful if prices rise or places are limited.","zh":"如果價格上升或名額有限，最後一刻預訂可能令人緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doing something very late.","zh":"這個短語描述很遲才做某事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"no supplement for","meaning":"……無須額外收費","examples":[{"en":"There is no supplement for single rooms in hotels.","zh":"酒店單人房無須額外收費。"},{"en":"No supplement for something means customers do not need to pay an extra charge for it.","zh":"某事無須額外收費意思是顧客不用為它支付附加費。"},{"en":"Some tours charge extra for single rooms, but this one has no supplement.","zh":"有些旅行團會為單人房額外收費，但這個團沒有附加費。"},{"en":"Removing supplements can make holidays fairer for solo travellers.","zh":"取消附加費可以令假期對獨遊旅客更公平。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the absence of an additional fee.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有額外費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"single rooms","meaning":"單人房","examples":[{"en":"The company does not charge a supplement for single rooms.","zh":"公司不會為單人房收取附加費。"},{"en":"Single rooms are hotel rooms intended for one person.","zh":"單人房是供一個人入住的酒店房間。"},{"en":"Solo travellers often ask whether single rooms cost extra.","zh":"獨遊旅客常詢問單人房是否需要額外收費。"},{"en":"A single room can give a traveller more privacy during a tour.","zh":"單人房可以讓旅客在旅行團中有更多私人空間。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in hotel and travel booking.","zh":"這個短語常見於酒店和旅遊預訂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make a booking","meaning":"預訂","examples":[{"en":"A customer may need to change the date after making a booking.","zh":"顧客預訂後可能需要更改日期。"},{"en":"To make a booking means to reserve a place, room, ticket or service.","zh":"預訂意思是預留名額、房間、票或服務。"},{"en":"Travellers usually make a booking before a tour becomes full.","zh":"旅客通常會在旅行團額滿前預訂。"},{"en":"After making a booking, customers should check the details carefully.","zh":"預訂後，顧客應仔細核對細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in travel, restaurants and hotels.","zh":"這個短語常見於旅遊、餐廳和酒店。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"change the start date","meaning":"更改出發日期","examples":[{"en":"Customers can change the start date for a small fee.","zh":"顧客可以支付小額費用更改出發日期。"},{"en":"To change the start date means to move the beginning of a holiday or activity to another date.","zh":"更改出發日期意思是把假期或活動的開始日期改到另一日。"},{"en":"A customer may change the start date if they become ill before travelling.","zh":"如果顧客在出發前生病，可能需要更改出發日期。"},{"en":"Flexible date changes can reduce stress for travellers.","zh":"靈活改期可以減少旅客壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes altering the departure or beginning date.","zh":"這個短語描述更改出發或開始日期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"because of illness","meaning":"因為生病","examples":[{"en":"A customer may need to change the start date because of illness.","zh":"顧客可能因為生病而需要更改出發日期。"},{"en":"Because of illness means due to being sick or having a health problem.","zh":"因為生病意思是由於身體不適或有健康問題。"},{"en":"A traveller may cancel a tour because of illness in the family.","zh":"旅客可能因家人生病而取消旅程。"},{"en":"Travel companies often need policies for changes caused by illness.","zh":"旅行公司通常需要處理因疾病而更改安排的政策。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a health-related reason.","zh":"這個短語解釋與健康有關的原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be welcome to","meaning":"可以；歡迎……","examples":[{"en":"Customers are welcome to change to an alternative date.","zh":"顧客可以改到其他日期。"},{"en":"To be welcome to do something means to be allowed or invited to do it.","zh":"可以或歡迎做某事意思是被允許或被邀請做該事。"},{"en":"Visitors are welcome to ask the tour manager for advice.","zh":"訪客可以向旅行領隊詢問建議。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds friendly and helpful.","zh":"這個短語聽起來友善而樂於幫助。"},{"en":"It is useful when offering permission politely.","zh":"當有禮貌地給予許可時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"alternative date","meaning":"其他日期","examples":[{"en":"Customers can change to an alternative date.","zh":"顧客可以改到其他日期。"},{"en":"An alternative date is another possible date that can be chosen instead.","zh":"其他日期是可以代替原日期選擇的另一個可能日期。"},{"en":"If the original tour is inconvenient, customers may choose an alternative date.","zh":"如果原本旅行日期不方便，顧客可以選擇其他日期。"},{"en":"Offering alternative dates gives travellers more flexibility.","zh":"提供其他日期讓旅客有更多彈性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a replacement date.","zh":"這個短語描述替代日期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"different tour","meaning":"不同旅程","examples":[{"en":"Customers may change to a different tour.","zh":"顧客可以改到不同旅程。"},{"en":"A different tour means another travel package or itinerary.","zh":"不同旅程意思是另一個旅遊套票或行程。"},{"en":"If a customer cannot join the Isle of Man holiday, they may choose a different tour.","zh":"如果顧客不能參加 Isle of Man 假期，可以選擇不同旅程。"},{"en":"Changing to a different tour can help customers keep their holiday plans.","zh":"改到不同旅程可以幫助顧客保留假期計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an alternative trip.","zh":"這個短語描述替代旅程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"administrative fee","meaning":"行政費","examples":[{"en":"Customers pay a small administrative fee to change the booking.","zh":"顧客支付小額行政費來更改預訂。"},{"en":"An administrative fee is a charge for office work or processing.","zh":"行政費是為辦公室工作或處理程序而收取的費用。"},{"en":"A travel company may charge an administrative fee when staff change booking records.","zh":"當職員更改預訂紀錄時，旅行公司可能收取行政費。"},{"en":"Small administrative fees cover the cost of managing changes.","zh":"小額行政費用於支付處理更改的成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a service-related charge.","zh":"這個短語描述與服務處理相關的收費。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"consist of","meaning":"包括；由……組成","examples":[{"en":"Erica explains what the holiday consists of.","zh":"Erica 解釋這個假期包括甚麼。"},{"en":"To consist of something means to be made up of particular parts.","zh":"包括或由某些部分組成，意思是由特定部分構成。"},{"en":"The holiday consists of ferry travel, hotel stays, meals and organised trips.","zh":"假期包括渡輪旅程、酒店住宿、餐食和已安排的行程。"},{"en":"Knowing what a package consists of helps customers compare value.","zh":"知道套票包括甚麼，有助顧客比較價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes contents or components.","zh":"這個短語描述內容或組成部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"arrive in time for","meaning":"及時到達參加……","examples":[{"en":"Customers arrive in time for a short introduction.","zh":"顧客及時到達參加簡短介紹。"},{"en":"To arrive in time for something means to arrive early enough to attend it.","zh":"及時到達參加某事意思是到得夠早，可以出席該活動。"},{"en":"Travellers should arrive in time for the ferry check-in.","zh":"旅客應及時到達辦理渡輪登船手續。"},{"en":"Arriving in time prevents people from missing important information.","zh":"及時到達可以防止人錯過重要資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes punctual arrival before an event.","zh":"這個短語描述在活動前準時到達。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"short introduction","meaning":"簡短介紹","examples":[{"en":"The tour manager gives a short introduction on day one.","zh":"旅行領隊在第一天作簡短介紹。"},{"en":"A short introduction is a brief explanation at the beginning of an event or activity.","zh":"簡短介紹是在活動開始時的簡短解釋。"},{"en":"The tour manager may give a short introduction to the hotel, schedule and safety points.","zh":"旅行領隊可能簡短介紹酒店、時間表和安全事項。"},{"en":"A clear introduction helps travellers understand what will happen next.","zh":"清楚介紹有助旅客理解接下來會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a brief opening explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述簡短開場說明。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"followed by","meaning":"隨後是……","examples":[{"en":"The introduction is followed by dinner in the hotel.","zh":"簡介之後是在酒店用晚餐。"},{"en":"Followed by means coming after something in time or order.","zh":"隨後是某事意思是在時間或次序上跟在某事後面。"},{"en":"The meeting is followed by a guided walk around the town.","zh":"會議之後是市內導賞步行。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain the sequence of events.","zh":"這個短語有助解釋事件次序。"},{"en":"It is common in itineraries and schedules.","zh":"它常見於行程和時間表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dining room","meaning":"飯廳","examples":[{"en":"The dining room looks out at the river.","zh":"飯廳面向河流。"},{"en":"A dining room is a room where people eat meals.","zh":"飯廳是人們用餐的房間。"},{"en":"The hotel dining room may serve breakfast and dinner to tour guests.","zh":"酒店飯廳可能為旅行團客人供應早餐和晚餐。"},{"en":"A pleasant dining room can improve the holiday experience.","zh":"舒適的飯廳可以改善假期體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a meal area in a hotel or home.","zh":"這個短語描述酒店或家中的用餐空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"look out at","meaning":"面向；望向","examples":[{"en":"The dining room looks out at the river.","zh":"飯廳面向河流。"},{"en":"To look out at something means to face it or have a view of it.","zh":"面向或望向某物意思是朝向它或可以看見它。"},{"en":"The hotel room looks out at the harbour and the boats.","zh":"酒店房間望向港口和船隻。"},{"en":"A room with a good view can make meals more enjoyable.","zh":"有好景觀的房間可以令用餐更愉快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what can be seen from a place.","zh":"這個短語描述從某處可以看見甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"close to where","meaning":"靠近……的地方","examples":[{"en":"The dining room is close to where the river flows into the harbour.","zh":"飯廳靠近河流流入港口的地方。"},{"en":"Close to where means near the place at which something happens.","zh":"靠近某事發生的地方意思是接近該位置。"},{"en":"The café is close to where the ferry leaves.","zh":"咖啡店靠近渡輪出發的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a location by referring to a nearby action or feature.","zh":"這個短語透過附近動作或特徵來交代位置。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing geography.","zh":"它適合用於描述地理位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"flow into","meaning":"流入……","examples":[{"en":"The river flows into the harbour near the hotel.","zh":"河流在酒店附近流入港口。"},{"en":"To flow into a place means for water to move into it naturally.","zh":"流入某處意思是水自然移動進入該地方。"},{"en":"A small river may flow into the sea near a coastal town.","zh":"小河可能在沿海城鎮附近流入大海。"},{"en":"Rivers flowing into harbours can create busy and scenic waterfront areas.","zh":"河流流入港口可以形成繁忙而有景色的海濱地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the movement of water.","zh":"這個短語描述水的流動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"harbour","meaning":"港口","examples":[{"en":"The river flows into the harbour.","zh":"河流流入港口。"},{"en":"A harbour is a sheltered area of water where boats can stay safely.","zh":"港口是讓船隻能安全停泊的受保護水域。"},{"en":"Ferries often arrive at and leave from harbours.","zh":"渡輪通常在港口抵達和出發。"},{"en":"Harbours can be lively places with boats, shops and visitors.","zh":"港口可以是有船隻、商店和遊客的熱鬧地方。"},{"en":"This word is common in travel and coastal geography.","zh":"這個詞常見於旅遊和海岸地理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"plenty of activity going on","meaning":"有很多活動在進行","examples":[{"en":"There is usually plenty of activity going on near the harbour.","zh":"港口附近通常有很多活動在進行。"},{"en":"Plenty of activity going on means many things are happening in a place.","zh":"有很多活動在進行意思是某地有許多事情正在發生。"},{"en":"Near a harbour, there may be plenty of activity with ferries, fishing boats and tourists.","zh":"港口附近可能有渡輪、漁船和旅客，很多活動在進行。"},{"en":"A busy view can make a hotel dining room more interesting.","zh":"熱鬧景觀可以令酒店飯廳更有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lively scene.","zh":"這個短語描述熱鬧場景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take the coach to","meaning":"乘旅遊巴前往","examples":[{"en":"On day two, customers take the coach to Peel.","zh":"第二天，顧客乘旅遊巴前往 Peel。"},{"en":"To take the coach to a place means to travel there by coach.","zh":"乘旅遊巴前往某地意思是乘坐旅遊巴去那裏。"},{"en":"Tour groups often take the coach to towns that are not easy to reach by train.","zh":"旅行團常乘旅遊巴前往不容易乘火車到達的城鎮。"},{"en":"Coach travel allows the group to move together according to the itinerary.","zh":"旅遊巴讓團體按行程一起移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised bus transport.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的巴士交通。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on the way","meaning":"途中","examples":[{"en":"On the way, customers call in at the Tynwald Exhibition.","zh":"途中，顧客順道參觀 Tynwald Exhibition。"},{"en":"On the way means during the journey to another place.","zh":"途中意思是在前往另一地的旅程中。"},{"en":"On the way to the hotel, the group stopped for lunch.","zh":"前往酒店途中，團體停下來吃午餐。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces something that happens before reaching the final destination.","zh":"這個短語引入到達最終目的地前發生的事。"},{"en":"It is useful in travel descriptions.","zh":"它適合用於旅遊描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"call in at","meaning":"順道參觀","examples":[{"en":"Customers call in at the Tynwald Exhibition on the way to Peel.","zh":"顧客在前往 Peel 途中順道參觀 Tynwald Exhibition。"},{"en":"To call in at a place means to make a short visit there.","zh":"順道參觀某地意思是短暫到訪該地。"},{"en":"The group may call in at a museum before continuing to the coast.","zh":"團體可能先順道參觀博物館，再繼續前往海岸。"},{"en":"Calling in at a place can add interest without taking the whole day.","zh":"順道參觀可以增加趣味，而不會花上一整天。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a brief stop during a journey.","zh":"這個短語描述旅程中的短暫停留。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be part of","meaning":"屬於……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"The Isle of Man is not part of the United Kingdom.","zh":"Isle of Man 並不屬於 United Kingdom 的一部分。"},{"en":"To be part of something means to belong to it or be included in it.","zh":"屬於某事的一部分意思是歸屬於它或被包括在其中。"},{"en":"A small island may be close to a country but not part of it politically.","zh":"一個小島可能接近某國，但政治上不屬於它的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain political or geographical relationships.","zh":"這個短語有助解釋政治或地理關係。"},{"en":"It describes membership or inclusion.","zh":"它描述成員身份或包含關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have its own parliament","meaning":"有自己的議會","examples":[{"en":"The Isle of Man has its own parliament.","zh":"Isle of Man 有自己的議會。"},{"en":"To have its own parliament means to have a separate law-making body.","zh":"有自己的議會意思是有獨立的立法機構。"},{"en":"A territory with its own parliament may make many of its own laws.","zh":"有自己議會的地區可能制定許多自己的法律。"},{"en":"This detail helps visitors understand the island’s political identity.","zh":"這個細節幫助訪客理解該島的政治身份。"},{"en":"This phrase describes self-government.","zh":"這個短語描述自治。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it is claimed that","meaning":"據稱","examples":[{"en":"It is claimed that Tynwald is the world’s oldest functioning parliament.","zh":"據稱，Tynwald 是世界上最古老且仍在運作的議會。"},{"en":"It is claimed that means people say this is true, although the speaker may be cautious.","zh":"據稱意思是有人說某事是真的，但講者可能保持謹慎。"},{"en":"It is claimed that the building is the oldest hotel on the island.","zh":"據稱，這棟建築是島上最古老的酒店。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting a statement without fully proving it.","zh":"當報告一個說法但未完全證明時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It sounds careful and formal.","zh":"它聽起來謹慎而正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the world’s oldest parliament","meaning":"世界上最古老的議會","examples":[{"en":"Tynwald is claimed to be the world’s oldest parliament still functioning.","zh":"據稱，Tynwald 是世界上最古老且仍在運作的議會。"},{"en":"The world’s oldest parliament means the oldest law-making assembly in the world.","zh":"世界上最古老的議會意思是全球最早的立法議會。"},{"en":"Historical claims about the world’s oldest parliament may depend on how records are interpreted.","zh":"關於世界最古老議會的歷史說法，可能取決於如何詮釋紀錄。"},{"en":"Such a claim can make a heritage site especially interesting to visitors.","zh":"這樣的說法可以令歷史景點對訪客特別有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes historical importance.","zh":"這個短語描述歷史重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"still functioning","meaning":"仍在運作","examples":[{"en":"Tynwald is still functioning today.","zh":"Tynwald 今天仍在運作。"},{"en":"Still functioning means continuing to operate or work.","zh":"仍在運作意思是繼續運行或工作。"},{"en":"Some ancient institutions are still functioning in modern forms.","zh":"有些古老機構仍以現代形式運作。"},{"en":"A parliament still functioning today connects history with present-day government.","zh":"今天仍在運作的議會把歷史與現代政府連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continued operation.","zh":"這個短語描述持續運行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"date back to","meaning":"可追溯至……","examples":[{"en":"Tynwald is claimed to date back to 979.","zh":"據稱，Tynwald 可追溯至 979 年。"},{"en":"To date back to a time means to have existed since that time.","zh":"可追溯至某時間意思是自該時間已經存在。"},{"en":"The castle dates back to the medieval period.","zh":"這座城堡可追溯至中世紀。"},{"en":"Dates help visitors understand how old a place or institution may be.","zh":"日期幫助訪客理解一個地方或機構可能有多古老。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in history and heritage descriptions.","zh":"這個短語常見於歷史和文化遺產描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"earliest surviving reference to","meaning":"現存最早提及……的文獻","examples":[{"en":"The earliest surviving reference to Tynwald is from 1422.","zh":"現存最早提及 Tynwald 的文獻來自 1422 年。"},{"en":"The earliest surviving reference to something means the oldest existing written mention of it.","zh":"現存最早提及某事的文獻意思是仍存在、最古老的書面提及。"},{"en":"The earliest surviving reference to a town may appear in a tax record.","zh":"現存最早提及某城鎮的文獻可能出現在稅務紀錄中。"},{"en":"Surviving references are important because older records may have been lost.","zh":"現存文獻很重要，因為更早紀錄可能已經遺失。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in historical evidence discussion.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論歷史證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"quite as old as","meaning":"和……宣稱的一樣古老","examples":[{"en":"Tynwald may not be quite as old as it claims.","zh":"Tynwald 可能並不和它宣稱的一樣古老。"},{"en":"Quite as old as means exactly as old as something is said to be, often used in a negative sentence.","zh":"和某物宣稱的一樣古老意思是正正有它聲稱的年紀，常用於否定句。"},{"en":"The building may not be quite as old as the guidebook suggests.","zh":"這棟建築可能並不和旅遊指南所說的一樣古老。"},{"en":"This phrase softens disagreement with a historical claim.","zh":"這個短語柔和地表示不同意某歷史說法。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing claimed age with evidence.","zh":"當比較聲稱年代與證據時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"trip to","meaning":"前往……的行程","examples":[{"en":"On day three, customers take a trip to the mountain Snaefell.","zh":"第三天，顧客參加前往 Snaefell 山的行程。"},{"en":"A trip to a place is a journey or visit to that location.","zh":"前往某地的行程是到該地的旅程或參觀。"},{"en":"The tour includes a trip to a famous mountain and a fishing village.","zh":"旅行團包括前往著名山峰和漁村的行程。"},{"en":"Trips to scenic places often become highlights of holidays.","zh":"前往風景名勝的行程常成為假期亮點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a planned visit.","zh":"這個短語描述已安排的到訪。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"leisurely ride","meaning":"悠閒車程","examples":[{"en":"The day begins with a leisurely ride along the promenade.","zh":"這一天以沿着海濱長廊的悠閒車程開始。"},{"en":"A leisurely ride is a relaxed journey without hurry.","zh":"悠閒車程是不趕急、放鬆的旅程。"},{"en":"A leisurely ride by the sea allows tourists to enjoy the view.","zh":"沿海的悠閒車程讓旅客欣賞景色。"},{"en":"Leisurely activities can make a holiday feel calm and pleasant.","zh":"悠閒活動可以令假期感覺平靜而愉快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a relaxed form of travel.","zh":"這個短語描述放鬆的交通體驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"along the promenade","meaning":"沿着海濱長廊","examples":[{"en":"Customers ride along the promenade in Douglas.","zh":"顧客在 Douglas 沿着海濱長廊乘車。"},{"en":"Along the promenade means following the seafront walkway or road.","zh":"沿着海濱長廊意思是沿着海邊步道或道路行進。"},{"en":"Visitors may walk along the promenade to enjoy sea views.","zh":"訪客可能沿着海濱長廊散步，欣賞海景。"},{"en":"Promenades are often popular places for sightseeing and gentle exercise.","zh":"海濱長廊通常是觀光和輕鬆運動的熱門地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement beside the seafront.","zh":"這個短語描述沿海邊移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"horse-drawn tram","meaning":"馬拉電車","examples":[{"en":"Customers ride in a horse-drawn tram.","zh":"顧客乘坐馬拉電車。"},{"en":"A horse-drawn tram is a tram pulled by horses instead of an engine.","zh":"馬拉電車是由馬匹拉動而不是由引擎推動的電車。"},{"en":"A horse-drawn tram can feel historic and charming for tourists.","zh":"對旅客來說，馬拉電車可以感覺有歷史味和吸引力。"},{"en":"Heritage transport often helps visitors experience the past.","zh":"文化遺產交通工具常幫助訪客體驗過去。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an old-fashioned form of transport.","zh":"這個短語描述舊式交通工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"board an electric train","meaning":"登上電車","examples":[{"en":"Customers board an electric train to Laxey.","zh":"顧客登上前往 Laxey 的電車。"},{"en":"To board an electric train means to get onto a train powered by electricity.","zh":"登上電車意思是上車乘坐由電力驅動的列車。"},{"en":"Passengers board the electric train after leaving the tram.","zh":"乘客離開電車後登上另一列電車。"},{"en":"Electric trains can provide a comfortable way to travel between towns.","zh":"電車可以提供城鎮之間舒適的交通方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes getting onto a train.","zh":"這個短語描述上車動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fishing village","meaning":"漁村","examples":[{"en":"Laxey is a fishing village.","zh":"Laxey 是一條漁村。"},{"en":"A fishing village is a small village where fishing has traditionally been important.","zh":"漁村是傳統上以捕魚為重要活動的小村莊。"},{"en":"A fishing village may have a harbour, boats and seafood restaurants.","zh":"漁村可能有港口、漁船和海鮮餐廳。"},{"en":"Such villages often attract visitors because of their scenery and local character.","zh":"這類村莊常因風景和地方特色吸引訪客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a coastal community.","zh":"這個短語描述沿海社區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"eight-kilometre ride","meaning":"八公里車程","examples":[{"en":"There is an eight-kilometre ride to the top.","zh":"到山頂有八公里車程。"},{"en":"An eight-kilometre ride is a journey of eight kilometres by vehicle, train or bicycle.","zh":"八公里車程是乘交通工具、火車或單車行走八公里的旅程。"},{"en":"The mountain railway offers an eight-kilometre ride through scenic countryside.","zh":"山區鐵路提供穿越美麗鄉郊的八公里車程。"},{"en":"Giving the distance helps travellers understand the length of the journey.","zh":"提供距離有助旅客理解旅程長度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a measured travel section.","zh":"這個短語描述有量度的旅程段落。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"to the top","meaning":"到山頂","examples":[{"en":"The Snaefell Mountain Railway takes customers to the top.","zh":"Snaefell Mountain Railway 帶顧客到山頂。"},{"en":"To the top means to the highest point of a hill, mountain or structure.","zh":"到山頂意思是到山丘、山峰或建築物的最高點。"},{"en":"A cable car may take visitors to the top of a mountain.","zh":"纜車可能把訪客帶到山頂。"},{"en":"Reaching the top often gives travellers wide views of the area.","zh":"到達山頂通常能讓旅客看到廣闊景色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upward travel to a summit.","zh":"這個短語描述前往最高點的上行旅程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"spectacular views of","meaning":"……的壯麗景色","examples":[{"en":"The café gives customers spectacular views of the island.","zh":"咖啡店讓顧客看到島嶼的壯麗景色。"},{"en":"Spectacular views of something are extremely impressive sights of it.","zh":"某物的壯麗景色是極其令人印象深刻的景觀。"},{"en":"From the mountain, visitors may enjoy spectacular views of the coast.","zh":"從山上，訪客可能欣賞到海岸的壯麗景色。"},{"en":"Beautiful views can become a memorable part of a holiday.","zh":"美麗景色可以成為假期令人難忘的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visually impressive scenery.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺上壯觀的風景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"free to explore","meaning":"自由探索","examples":[{"en":"Day four is free for customers to explore.","zh":"第四天讓顧客自由探索。"},{"en":"Free to explore means able to look around independently without a fixed group plan.","zh":"自由探索意思是可以在沒有固定團體安排下自行四處看看。"},{"en":"Travellers may be free to explore the town after lunch.","zh":"旅客可能午餐後可以自由探索城鎮。"},{"en":"Free time lets customers choose activities that suit their interests.","zh":"自由時間讓顧客選擇配合自己興趣的活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes independent sightseeing time.","zh":"這個短語描述獨立觀光時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"use the pass","meaning":"使用通行證","examples":[{"en":"Customers can use the pass provided by the company.","zh":"顧客可以使用公司提供的通行證。"},{"en":"To use the pass means to show or present a ticket or card that gives access to services.","zh":"使用通行證意思是出示或使用一張可取得服務的票或卡。"},{"en":"Visitors can use the pass to travel on local buses and trains.","zh":"訪客可以使用通行證乘搭本地巴士和火車。"},{"en":"A pass can save customers time and money during a holiday.","zh":"通行證可以在假期中為顧客節省時間和金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a travel or entry card.","zh":"這個短語描述使用交通或入場卡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pay for travel","meaning":"支付交通費","examples":[{"en":"Customers do not have to pay for travel on local transport.","zh":"顧客不用支付本地交通費。"},{"en":"To pay for travel means to spend money on transport journeys.","zh":"支付交通費意思是為交通旅程花錢。"},{"en":"If local travel is included, customers do not need to pay for each bus ride.","zh":"如果本地交通已包括，顧客就不用為每程巴士付費。"},{"en":"Included transport makes the holiday easier to manage.","zh":"包含交通安排令假期更容易管理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transport costs.","zh":"這個短語描述交通費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"local transport","meaning":"本地交通","examples":[{"en":"The pass covers travel on local transport.","zh":"通行證包括本地交通旅程。"},{"en":"Local transport means buses, trains, trams or other transport within a local area.","zh":"本地交通意思是在本地區域內的巴士、火車、電車或其他交通。"},{"en":"Tourists use local transport to visit towns, museums and heritage sites.","zh":"旅客使用本地交通前往城鎮、博物館和歷史景點。"},{"en":"Good local transport helps visitors explore independently.","zh":"良好的本地交通幫助訪客自行探索。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transport services within a destination.","zh":"這個短語描述目的地內的交通服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"entrance to","meaning":"……的入場費","examples":[{"en":"Customers do not have to pay for entrance to heritage sites.","zh":"顧客不用支付歷史景點的入場費。"},{"en":"Entrance to a place means admission or access to go inside it.","zh":"某地的入場意思是進入該地的許可或入場資格。"},{"en":"The pass includes entrance to museums and historic buildings.","zh":"通行證包括博物館和歷史建築的入場費。"},{"en":"Free entrance can encourage customers to visit more attractions.","zh":"免費入場可以鼓勵顧客參觀更多景點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes admission to a site.","zh":"這個短語描述進入景點的入場安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"heritage sites","meaning":"歷史景點","examples":[{"en":"The pass includes entrance to the island’s heritage sites.","zh":"通行證包括島上歷史景點的入場費。"},{"en":"Heritage sites are places important because of history, culture or tradition.","zh":"歷史景點是因歷史、文化或傳統而重要的地方。"},{"en":"Castles, old parliament buildings and museums can be heritage sites.","zh":"城堡、舊議會建築和博物館都可以是歷史景點。"},{"en":"Visiting heritage sites helps travellers understand local identity.","zh":"參觀歷史景點幫助旅客理解地方身份。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in tourism and history.","zh":"這個短語常見於旅遊和歷史語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take it easy","meaning":"放鬆一下","examples":[{"en":"Customers may just want to take it easy in Douglas.","zh":"顧客可能只想在 Douglas 放鬆一下。"},{"en":"To take it easy means to relax and avoid doing too much.","zh":"放鬆一下意思是休息，不做太多事情。"},{"en":"After several organised trips, travellers may take it easy with a gentle walk.","zh":"經過幾天已安排的行程後，旅客可能散步放鬆一下。"},{"en":"Taking it easy can make a holiday feel restful rather than tiring.","zh":"放鬆一下可以令假期感覺休閒，而不是疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and common in spoken English.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常見於英語口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"do a little light shopping","meaning":"輕鬆逛街購物","examples":[{"en":"Some customers may do a little light shopping in Douglas.","zh":"有些顧客可能在 Douglas 輕鬆逛街購物。"},{"en":"To do a little light shopping means to shop casually without buying too much or spending too long.","zh":"輕鬆逛街購物意思是隨意購物，不買太多或花太長時間。"},{"en":"Travellers may do a little light shopping for souvenirs on a free afternoon.","zh":"旅客可能在自由活動下午輕鬆購買紀念品。"},{"en":"Light shopping can be a relaxed way to explore a town.","zh":"輕鬆購物可以是探索城鎮的放鬆方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes easy, casual shopping.","zh":"這個短語描述輕鬆隨意的購物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"last full day","meaning":"最後一個完整日","examples":[{"en":"Day five is the last full day of the holiday.","zh":"第五天是假期的最後一個完整日。"},{"en":"The last full day means the final day with a complete schedule before departure.","zh":"最後一個完整日意思是出發回家前最後一個有完整行程的日子。"},{"en":"Tour companies often plan a special activity on the last full day.","zh":"旅行公司通常會在最後一個完整日安排特別活動。"},{"en":"The last full day can leave a strong final impression of the trip.","zh":"最後一個完整日可以留下強烈的旅程最終印象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes timing near the end of a holiday.","zh":"這個短語描述假期接近結束時的時間安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"highlight of the holiday","meaning":"假期亮點","examples":[{"en":"For some people, the steam railway is the highlight of the holiday.","zh":"對有些人來說，蒸汽鐵路是假期亮點。"},{"en":"The highlight of the holiday is the most enjoyable or memorable part of the trip.","zh":"假期亮點是旅程中最愉快或最難忘的部分。"},{"en":"A mountain view may be the highlight of the holiday for nature lovers.","zh":"對自然愛好者來說，山景可能是假期亮點。"},{"en":"Travel companies often mention highlights to attract customers.","zh":"旅行公司常提及亮點來吸引顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the best or most special moment.","zh":"這個短語描述最好或最特別的時刻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ride on","meaning":"乘坐……","examples":[{"en":"Customers take a ride on the steam railway.","zh":"顧客乘坐蒸汽鐵路。"},{"en":"To take a ride on something means to travel on it for enjoyment or transport.","zh":"乘坐某物意思是為了享受或交通而乘搭它。"},{"en":"Visitors may take a ride on a historic tram along the seafront.","zh":"訪客可能乘坐歷史電車沿海濱前行。"},{"en":"A ride on an old railway can be both transport and sightseeing.","zh":"乘坐舊鐵路既可以是交通，也可以是觀光。"},{"en":"This phrase describes travelling on a vehicle or attraction.","zh":"這個短語描述乘搭交通工具或景點設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"steam railway","meaning":"蒸汽鐵路","examples":[{"en":"The steam railway goes from Douglas to Port Erin.","zh":"蒸汽鐵路由 Douglas 前往 Port Erin。"},{"en":"A steam railway is a railway that uses steam-powered trains.","zh":"蒸汽鐵路是使用蒸汽火車的鐵路。"},{"en":"Steam railways are often preserved as heritage attractions.","zh":"蒸汽鐵路常被保存為文化遺產景點。"},{"en":"Travelling by steam railway can feel historic and scenic.","zh":"乘坐蒸汽鐵路可以感覺有歷史味且風景優美。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an old-fashioned railway system.","zh":"這個短語描述舊式鐵路系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"some time to explore","meaning":"一些探索時間","examples":[{"en":"Customers have some time to explore Port Erin.","zh":"顧客有一些時間探索 Port Erin。"},{"en":"Some time to explore means a period available for looking around a place.","zh":"一些探索時間意思是有一段時間可以四處看看。"},{"en":"The tour gives visitors some time to explore the harbour before lunch.","zh":"旅行團在午餐前給訪客一些時間探索港口。"},{"en":"Exploration time lets travellers discover shops, views and local details.","zh":"探索時間讓旅客發現商店、景色和本地細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes flexible sightseeing time.","zh":"這個短語描述彈性的觀光時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"headland","meaning":"海岬","examples":[{"en":"A coach takes customers to the headland.","zh":"旅遊巴帶顧客前往海岬。"},{"en":"A headland is a piece of land that sticks out into the sea.","zh":"海岬是伸出海中的一片陸地。"},{"en":"Headlands often provide wide views of the coastline and nearby islands.","zh":"海岬通常提供海岸線和附近島嶼的廣闊景色。"},{"en":"A coach trip to a headland can be popular with photographers and nature lovers.","zh":"前往海岬的旅遊巴行程可能受攝影愛好者和自然愛好者歡迎。"},{"en":"This word describes a coastal landform.","zh":"這個詞描述海岸地形。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"overlook","meaning":"俯瞰","examples":[{"en":"The headland overlooks the Calf of Man.","zh":"海岬俯瞰 Calf of Man。"},{"en":"To overlook a place means to have a view over it from above or nearby.","zh":"俯瞰某地意思是從高處或附近望向它。"},{"en":"The hotel balcony overlooks the harbour.","zh":"酒店露台俯瞰港口。"},{"en":"Places that overlook the sea are often attractive to visitors.","zh":"俯瞰大海的地方通常吸引訪客。"},{"en":"This word describes a viewpoint or position.","zh":"這個詞描述視角或位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"just off the coast","meaning":"離岸不遠","examples":[{"en":"The Calf of Man is a small island just off the coast.","zh":"Calf of Man 是一個離岸不遠的小島。"},{"en":"Just off the coast means very close to the land but separated by water.","zh":"離岸不遠意思是非常接近陸地，但被水隔開。"},{"en":"A small island just off the coast may be visible from the headland.","zh":"離岸不遠的小島可能可以從海岬看見。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe a nearby island’s location.","zh":"這個短語有助描述附近島嶼的位置。"},{"en":"It is common in coastal geography and travel writing.","zh":"它常見於海岸地理和旅遊寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"continue to","meaning":"繼續前往","examples":[{"en":"From there, customers continue to Castletown.","zh":"從那裏，顧客繼續前往 Castletown。"},{"en":"To continue to a place means to go on travelling until reaching that place.","zh":"繼續前往某地意思是繼續旅程直到到達該地。"},{"en":"After visiting the mountain, the group continues to a historic town.","zh":"參觀山峰後，團體繼續前往歷史城鎮。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe the next stage of a journey.","zh":"這個短語有助描述旅程的下一階段。"},{"en":"It is useful in itineraries.","zh":"它適合用於行程表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"used to be","meaning":"曾經是……","examples":[{"en":"Castletown used to be the capital of the Isle of Man.","zh":"Castletown 曾經是 Isle of Man 的首府。"},{"en":"Used to be means something was true in the past but is not true now.","zh":"曾經是某事意思是過去如此，但現在不再如此。"},{"en":"The old town used to be the main trading centre of the island.","zh":"這座舊城鎮曾經是島上的主要貿易中心。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining historical change.","zh":"這個短語適合用於解釋歷史變化。"},{"en":"It contrasts the past with the present.","zh":"它把過去與現在作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"capital of","meaning":"……的首府","examples":[{"en":"Castletown used to be the capital of the Isle of Man.","zh":"Castletown 曾經是 Isle of Man 的首府。"},{"en":"The capital of a place is its main city or administrative centre.","zh":"某地的首府是其主要城市或行政中心。"},{"en":"A former capital may still have important historic buildings.","zh":"前首府可能仍有重要歷史建築。"},{"en":"Visiting an old capital can help travellers understand a place’s history.","zh":"參觀舊首府可以幫助旅客理解一個地方的歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase describes political or administrative importance.","zh":"這個短語描述政治或行政重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"medieval castle","meaning":"中世紀城堡","examples":[{"en":"Castletown has a medieval castle.","zh":"Castletown 有一座中世紀城堡。"},{"en":"A medieval castle is a castle built or used during the Middle Ages.","zh":"中世紀城堡是在中世紀建造或使用的城堡。"},{"en":"Medieval castles often have thick walls, towers and defensive features.","zh":"中世紀城堡通常有厚牆、塔樓和防禦設施。"},{"en":"A medieval castle can be a major attraction for visitors interested in history.","zh":"中世紀城堡可以成為對歷史有興趣的訪客的重要景點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a historic building from the medieval period.","zh":"這個短語描述來自中世紀的歷史建築。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"it’s back to","meaning":"返回……","examples":[{"en":"On day six, it is back to the ferry or the airport.","zh":"第六天，就是返回渡輪碼頭或機場。"},{"en":"It’s back to a place means it is time to return there.","zh":"返回某地意思是時候回到那裏。"},{"en":"After the final visit, it is back to the hotel to collect luggage.","zh":"最後一次參觀後，就是返回酒店取行李。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used informally in travel schedules.","zh":"這個短語常較口語地用於旅遊時間表。"},{"en":"It describes returning to a previous transport point or place.","zh":"它描述返回先前的交通點或地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"time to go home","meaning":"是回家的時候","examples":[{"en":"On day six, it is time to go home.","zh":"第六天，就是回家的時候。"},{"en":"Time to go home means the holiday or activity has ended and people should return home.","zh":"是回家的時候意思是假期或活動已結束，人們應返回家中。"},{"en":"After six days of sightseeing, it is time to go home by ferry or plane.","zh":"經過六天觀光後，就是乘渡輪或飛機回家的時候。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the end of a trip.","zh":"這個短語標示旅程結束。"},{"en":"It often carries a simple, final tone.","zh":"它通常帶有簡單而總結性的語氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10}],"ielts/listening/Practice 20/task-3":[{"front":"get on with","meaning":"進展如何","examples":[{"en":"Ed is getting on with the reading for next week’s presentation.","zh":"Ed 正在處理下星期簡報所需的閱讀資料。"},{"en":"To get on with something means to make progress with it.","zh":"get on with something 指某事進展如何。"},{"en":"Ruth asked Ed how he was getting on with the research.","zh":"Ruth 問 Ed 研究進展如何。"},{"en":"If you are getting on well with a task, the work is moving forward smoothly.","zh":"如果你某項工作進展順利，意思是工作正順暢推進。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to ask about progress in a friendly way.","zh":"這個片語常用來友善地詢問進度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the reading for","meaning":"……所需的閱讀資料","examples":[{"en":"Ruth asks Ed about the reading for their presentation.","zh":"Ruth 問 Ed 關於他們簡報所需的閱讀資料。"},{"en":"The reading for something means the books, articles or materials someone needs to read for a task.","zh":"the reading for something 指某任務所需閱讀的書籍、文章或材料。"},{"en":"The reading for the seminar took much longer than I expected.","zh":"研討課所需的閱讀資料比我預期花更久時間。"},{"en":"Students often need to organise the reading for a presentation before writing notes.","zh":"學生寫筆記前，通常需要整理簡報所需的閱讀資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic study.","zh":"這個片語常見於學術學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"presentation next week","meaning":"下星期的簡報","examples":[{"en":"The students are preparing for their presentation next week.","zh":"學生正在準備下星期的簡報。"},{"en":"Presentation next week means a talk or report that will take place in the following week.","zh":"presentation next week 指將於下一星期進行的匯報或演講。"},{"en":"We need to finish the slides for our presentation next week.","zh":"我們需要完成下星期簡報的投影片。"},{"en":"A presentation next week requires early preparation and clear division of work.","zh":"下星期的簡報需要及早準備和清楚分工。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the deadline and the type of task.","zh":"這個片語交代截止時間和任務類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"there’s so much of it","meaning":"數量很多","examples":[{"en":"Ed says there is so much reading to do.","zh":"Ed 說要讀的資料數量很多。"},{"en":"There’s so much of it means the amount is very large.","zh":"there’s so much of it 指某物數量非常多。"},{"en":"I wanted to finish the research, but there was so much of it.","zh":"我想完成研究，但資料實在太多。"},{"en":"This phrase often expresses surprise or stress about quantity.","zh":"這個片語常表達對數量的驚訝或壓力。"},{"en":"It is natural in spoken English when a task feels heavy.","zh":"當任務感覺沉重時，它在英語口語中很自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hadn’t realised","meaning":"之前沒有意識到","examples":[{"en":"Ruth had not realised that birth order was such a popular area of research.","zh":"Ruth 之前沒有意識到出生順序是如此熱門的研究範疇。"},{"en":"Hadn’t realised means did not know or understand something before.","zh":"hadn’t realised 指之前不知道或沒有明白某事。"},{"en":"I hadn’t realised there were so many studies on twins.","zh":"我之前沒有意識到有這麼多關於雙胞胎的研究。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when someone discovers new information.","zh":"當某人發現新資訊時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It often shows mild surprise.","zh":"它常帶有輕微驚訝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"birth order","meaning":"出生順序","examples":[{"en":"Their presentation focuses on birth order and personality.","zh":"他們的簡報聚焦於出生順序與性格。"},{"en":"Birth order means a person’s position among their siblings, such as oldest, middle, youngest or only child.","zh":"birth order 指一個人在兄弟姊妹中的排行，例如老大、中間、最年幼或獨生子女。"},{"en":"Some people believe birth order affects confidence and responsibility.","zh":"有些人相信出生順序會影響自信和責任感。"},{"en":"Psychologists have studied birth order for many years.","zh":"心理學家多年來一直研究出生順序。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in family and personality research.","zh":"這個片語常見於家庭和性格研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a popular area of research","meaning":"熱門研究範疇","examples":[{"en":"Birth order is a popular area of research.","zh":"出生順序是一個熱門研究範疇。"},{"en":"A popular area of research is a topic that many researchers study.","zh":"popular area of research 指很多研究者研究的主題。"},{"en":"Sleep and memory is a popular area of research in psychology.","zh":"睡眠與記憶是心理學中的熱門研究範疇。"},{"en":"A topic may become popular if it connects with everyday experience.","zh":"如果一個題目與日常經驗有關，它可能會變成熱門研究範疇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in academic introductions.","zh":"這個片語適合用於學術引言。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the stuff on","meaning":"關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"The stuff on birth order and personality is mostly unreliable.","zh":"關於出生順序與性格的資料大多不可靠。"},{"en":"The stuff on something means the information, writing or material about that topic.","zh":"the stuff on something 指關於某主題的資訊、文章或材料。"},{"en":"The stuff on personality tests was interesting but not always scientific.","zh":"關於性格測試的資料很有趣，但不一定科學。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and should be replaced by “material on” in formal writing.","zh":"這個片語較口語，正式寫作中可改用 “material on”。"},{"en":"It is common in student conversations.","zh":"它常見於學生對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"birth order and personality","meaning":"出生順序與性格","examples":[{"en":"Ed thinks research on birth order and personality is mostly unreliable.","zh":"Ed 認為關於出生順序與性格的研究大多不可靠。"},{"en":"Birth order and personality refers to the possible link between family position and character traits.","zh":"birth order and personality 指家庭排行與性格特質之間可能存在的關係。"},{"en":"Some writers claim there is a relationship between birth order and personality.","zh":"有些作者聲稱出生順序與性格之間有關係。"},{"en":"However, such claims need strong evidence before they can be accepted.","zh":"然而，這類說法需要有力證據才可接受。"},{"en":"This phrase names the main research topic of the discussion.","zh":"這個片語命名討論中的主要研究題目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mostly unreliable","meaning":"大多不可靠","examples":[{"en":"The research claims about birth order are mostly unreliable.","zh":"關於出生順序的研究說法大多不可靠。"},{"en":"Mostly unreliable means generally not dependable or not supported well enough.","zh":"mostly unreliable 指整體而言不可信，或沒有足夠支持。"},{"en":"The online personality quiz was mostly unreliable.","zh":"那個網上性格測驗大多不可靠。"},{"en":"Research can be unreliable if the sample is small or the method is weak.","zh":"如果樣本太小或方法薄弱，研究可能不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evaluating evidence.","zh":"這個片語適合用於評估證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"from what I’ve been reading","meaning":"從我讀到的資料來看","examples":[{"en":"From what Ed has been reading, many claims about birth order are stereotypes.","zh":"從 Ed 讀到的資料來看，許多關於出生順序的說法都是刻板印象。"},{"en":"From what I’ve been reading means based on the material I have read recently.","zh":"from what I’ve been reading 指根據我最近讀到的材料。"},{"en":"From what I’ve been reading, the evidence is not very strong.","zh":"從我讀到的資料來看，證據不是很強。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that the speaker’s opinion comes from research.","zh":"這個片語有助顯示說話者的意見來自研究。"},{"en":"It is useful in academic discussion and presentations.","zh":"它適合用於學術討論和簡報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"claims about","meaning":"關於……的說法","examples":[{"en":"Many claims about birth order are not supported by robust evidence.","zh":"許多關於出生順序的說法沒有有力證據支持。"},{"en":"Claims about something are statements or arguments saying that something is true.","zh":"claims about something 指聲稱某事為真的陳述或論點。"},{"en":"Some claims about personality are based more on stereotypes than research.","zh":"有些關於性格的說法更多建基於刻板印象，而不是研究。"},{"en":"Claims need evidence before they should be trusted.","zh":"說法需要有證據支持才值得相信。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic evaluation.","zh":"這個片語常見於學術評估。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"position in the family","meaning":"家庭中的排行","examples":[{"en":"Some studies claim that a person’s position in the family determines personality traits.","zh":"有些研究聲稱一個人在家庭中的排行會決定性格特質。"},{"en":"Position in the family means whether someone is the oldest, youngest, middle child or only child.","zh":"position in the family 指某人是老大、最年幼、中間孩子或獨生子女。"},{"en":"A child’s position in the family may affect responsibilities at home.","zh":"孩子在家庭中的排行可能影響其家中責任。"},{"en":"Researchers sometimes examine family position when studying development.","zh":"研究者研究成長時，有時會檢視家庭排行。"},{"en":"This phrase is closely linked to birth order.","zh":"這個片語與出生順序密切相關。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"determine personality traits","meaning":"決定性格特質","examples":[{"en":"Some writers claim that birth order determines personality traits.","zh":"有些作者聲稱出生順序會決定性格特質。"},{"en":"To determine personality traits means to decide or strongly shape someone’s character qualities.","zh":"determine personality traits 指決定或強烈塑造某人的性格特點。"},{"en":"It is too simple to say that birth order determines personality traits completely.","zh":"說出生順序完全決定性格特質太簡化了。"},{"en":"Personality is usually shaped by many factors, not one single cause.","zh":"性格通常由許多因素塑造，而不是單一原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing cause and effect.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論因果關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"personality traits","meaning":"性格特質","examples":[{"en":"The discussion focuses on whether birth order affects personality traits.","zh":"討論聚焦於出生順序是否影響性格特質。"},{"en":"Personality traits are stable qualities in how a person thinks, feels or behaves.","zh":"personality traits 指一個人在思想、感受或行為上的穩定特點。"},{"en":"Confidence, shyness and responsibility can be described as personality traits.","zh":"自信、害羞和責任感都可以被描述為性格特質。"},{"en":"Psychologists measure personality traits using questionnaires and observations.","zh":"心理學家會用問卷和觀察量度性格特質。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to psychology.","zh":"這個片語是心理學中的核心詞彙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"just stereotypes","meaning":"只是刻板印象","examples":[{"en":"Ed says many claims about birth order are just stereotypes.","zh":"Ed 說許多關於出生順序的說法只是刻板印象。"},{"en":"Just stereotypes means only over-simple fixed ideas about a group of people.","zh":"just stereotypes 指只是對某群人的過度簡化固定看法。"},{"en":"Saying all youngest children are selfish is just a stereotype.","zh":"說所有最年幼的孩子都自私，只是刻板印象。"},{"en":"Stereotypes can sound convincing, but they may not match real people.","zh":"刻板印象可能聽起來有說服力，但未必符合真人情況。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising weak generalisations.","zh":"這個片語適合用於批評薄弱概括。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"robust evidence","meaning":"有力證據","examples":[{"en":"There is no robust evidence to support many birth-order claims.","zh":"沒有有力證據支持許多出生順序的說法。"},{"en":"Robust evidence is strong, reliable evidence that can stand up to careful examination.","zh":"robust evidence 指強而可靠、能經得起仔細檢視的證據。"},{"en":"A small survey is not enough to provide robust evidence.","zh":"一項小型調查不足以提供有力證據。"},{"en":"Academic claims need robust evidence if they are to be taken seriously.","zh":"學術說法若要被認真看待，就需要有力證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research evaluation.","zh":"這個片語常見於研究評估。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"support them","meaning":"支持它們","examples":[{"en":"Many claims have no robust evidence to support them.","zh":"許多說法沒有有力證據支持它們。"},{"en":"To support them means to provide evidence or reasons that make those claims believable.","zh":"support them 指提供證據或理由，令那些說法可信。"},{"en":"The theory sounds interesting, but there is little data to support it.","zh":"這個理論聽起來有趣，但幾乎沒有數據支持它。"},{"en":"Arguments become stronger when reliable evidence supports them.","zh":"當可靠證據支持論點時，論點會更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to claims or ideas already mentioned.","zh":"這個片語指回前面提及的說法或想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an interesting point","meaning":"有趣的觀點","examples":[{"en":"Ruth thinks Ed has made an interesting point.","zh":"Ruth 認為 Ed 提出了一個有趣的觀點。"},{"en":"An interesting point is an idea worth thinking about or discussing.","zh":"interesting point 指值得思考或討論的想法。"},{"en":"The lack of strong evidence is an interesting point for the presentation.","zh":"缺乏有力證據是簡報中一個有趣的觀點。"},{"en":"Good presentations often include interesting points that challenge common beliefs.","zh":"好簡報常包含挑戰常見信念的有趣觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when responding positively to someone’s idea.","zh":"這個片語適合用於正面回應別人的想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"start by outlining","meaning":"先概述……","examples":[{"en":"The students could start by outlining previous research.","zh":"學生可以先概述過往研究。"},{"en":"To start by outlining something means to begin by giving a brief summary of it.","zh":"start by outlining something 指先簡要總結某事。"},{"en":"We can start by outlining the main theories on birth order.","zh":"我們可以先概述出生順序的主要理論。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise the beginning of a presentation.","zh":"這個片語有助組織簡報開頭。"},{"en":"It suggests giving the audience a clear overview first.","zh":"它暗示先給聽眾清晰概覽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"previous research","meaning":"過往研究","examples":[{"en":"The presentation could begin with what previous research has shown.","zh":"簡報可以由過往研究顯示了甚麼開始。"},{"en":"Previous research means studies that have already been carried out before the current discussion.","zh":"previous research 指目前討論之前已經進行過的研究。"},{"en":"Previous research on birth order produced mixed results.","zh":"關於出生順序的過往研究得出混合結果。"},{"en":"Referring to previous research helps show background knowledge.","zh":"提及過往研究有助顯示背景知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic presentations.","zh":"這個片語常見於學術簡報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"studies going back over","meaning":"可追溯至……以前的研究","examples":[{"en":"There are studies on birth order going back over a hundred years.","zh":"關於出生順序的研究可追溯至一百多年前。"},{"en":"Studies going back over a period means research that began more than that amount of time ago.","zh":"studies going back over a period 指早於某段時間已開始的研究。"},{"en":"There are studies on memory going back over a century.","zh":"關於記憶的研究可追溯至一個多世紀前。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that a topic has a long research history.","zh":"這個片語強調某主題有悠久研究歷史。"},{"en":"It is useful when introducing background.","zh":"它適合用於引入背景資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"run through","meaning":"快速介紹","examples":[{"en":"The students could run through some typical traits.","zh":"學生可以快速介紹一些典型特質。"},{"en":"To run through something means to go over it quickly.","zh":"run through something 指快速講解或回顧某事。"},{"en":"The presenter ran through the main findings before discussing criticism.","zh":"匯報者先快速介紹主要發現，再討論批評。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving a quick summary.","zh":"這個片語適合用於簡短總結。"},{"en":"It is more informal than “examine in detail”.","zh":"它比 “examine in detail” 較口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"typical traits","meaning":"典型特質","examples":[{"en":"The students could describe some typical traits linked to birth order.","zh":"學生可以描述一些與出生順序相關的典型特質。"},{"en":"Typical traits are qualities commonly associated with a person or group.","zh":"typical traits 指常被聯想到某人或某群體的特質。"},{"en":"Responsibility is often described as a typical trait of oldest children.","zh":"責任感常被描述為家中老大的典型特質。"},{"en":"Typical traits may be stereotypes if they are not supported by evidence.","zh":"如果沒有證據支持，典型特質可能只是刻板印象。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in personality discussion.","zh":"這個片語適合用於性格討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the consensus seems to be that","meaning":"普遍看法似乎是","examples":[{"en":"The consensus seems to be that oldest children are less well-adjusted.","zh":"普遍看法似乎是家中老大適應能力較差。"},{"en":"The consensus seems to be that means the general view appears to be that something is true.","zh":"the consensus seems to be that 指整體看法似乎認為某事是真的。"},{"en":"The consensus seems to be that the evidence is mixed.","zh":"普遍看法似乎是證據好壞參半。"},{"en":"This phrase is cautious because it does not claim complete certainty.","zh":"這個片語較謹慎，因為沒有聲稱完全確定。"},{"en":"It is useful when summarising what many studies or people suggest.","zh":"它適合用於總結許多研究或人士的看法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"oldest children","meaning":"家中老大","examples":[{"en":"Some studies claim that oldest children are less well-adjusted.","zh":"有些研究聲稱家中老大適應能力較差。"},{"en":"Oldest children are the first-born children in a family.","zh":"oldest children 指家庭中的第一個孩子。"},{"en":"Oldest children may be given more responsibility than their younger siblings.","zh":"家中老大可能比年幼弟妹承擔更多責任。"},{"en":"Some theories suggest oldest children behave differently because family expectations are different.","zh":"有些理論認為家中老大行為不同，是因為家庭期望不同。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies one birth-order group.","zh":"這個片語識別一個出生順序群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"generally less well-adjusted","meaning":"一般適應能力較差","examples":[{"en":"Oldest children are sometimes described as generally less well-adjusted.","zh":"家中老大有時被描述為一般適應能力較差。"},{"en":"Generally less well-adjusted means usually less emotionally or socially adapted.","zh":"generally less well-adjusted 指通常在情緒或社交上較不適應。"},{"en":"A child who is less well-adjusted may find change harder to accept.","zh":"適應能力較差的孩子可能較難接受改變。"},{"en":"Such descriptions need evidence because they can easily become stereotypes.","zh":"這類描述需要證據，因為它們很容易變成刻板印象。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing psychological adaptation.","zh":"這個片語用於討論心理適應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get over","meaning":"從……中恢復過來","examples":[{"en":"Some studies claim that oldest children never get over the arrival of a younger sibling.","zh":"有些研究聲稱家中老大永遠不能從年幼弟妹出生中恢復過來。"},{"en":"To get over something means to recover emotionally from it.","zh":"get over something 指情感上從某事恢復過來。"},{"en":"Some children take time to get over a major change at home.","zh":"有些孩子需要時間從家中重大變化中恢復過來。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for difficult experiences or disappointments.","zh":"這個片語常用於困難經歷或失望。"},{"en":"It suggests moving past an emotional impact.","zh":"它暗示走出情感影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the arrival of","meaning":"……的到來；……的出生","examples":[{"en":"The arrival of a younger sibling may affect the oldest child.","zh":"年幼弟妹的出生可能影響家中老大。"},{"en":"The arrival of someone means that person comes or is born into a situation.","zh":"the arrival of someone 指某人到來或出生進入某情況。"},{"en":"The arrival of a new baby can change family routines.","zh":"新嬰兒的出生可以改變家庭日常。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about changes caused by a new person.","zh":"這個片語適合談論因新成員出現而帶來的變化。"},{"en":"It sounds more formal than “when someone comes”.","zh":"它比 “when someone comes” 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a younger sibling","meaning":"年幼的兄弟姊妹","examples":[{"en":"The arrival of a younger sibling may be difficult for the oldest child.","zh":"年幼弟妹的出生對家中老大來說可能困難。"},{"en":"A younger sibling is a brother or sister who is younger than you.","zh":"younger sibling 指比你年幼的兄弟或姊妹。"},{"en":"An oldest child may feel jealous when a younger sibling is born.","zh":"年幼弟妹出生時，家中老大可能感到妒忌。"},{"en":"Younger siblings can change how attention and responsibilities are shared at home.","zh":"年幼兄弟姊妹可以改變家中關注和責任的分配。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in family and psychology topics.","zh":"這個片語常見於家庭和心理學題目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on a positive note","meaning":"從正面來看","examples":[{"en":"On a positive note, oldest children are often thought to be good at nurturing.","zh":"從正面來看，家中老大常被認為擅長照顧和培育。"},{"en":"On a positive note means looking at the good side of a situation.","zh":"on a positive note 指從情況中較好的一面來看。"},{"en":"On a positive note, the research gave them useful ideas for the presentation.","zh":"從正面來看，這些研究給了他們簡報的有用想法。"},{"en":"This phrase helps balance criticism with something encouraging.","zh":"這個片語有助用鼓勵資訊平衡批評。"},{"en":"It is common in discussion and presentations.","zh":"它常見於討論和簡報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be thought to be","meaning":"被認為是……","examples":[{"en":"Oldest children are thought to be good at nurturing younger siblings.","zh":"家中老大被認為擅長照顧年幼弟妹。"},{"en":"To be thought to be means to be believed or considered to be something.","zh":"be thought to be 指被相信或被視為某種人或事。"},{"en":"Middle children are often thought to be easy-going.","zh":"排行中間的孩子常被認為隨和。"},{"en":"This phrase reports a common belief without saying it is definitely true.","zh":"這個片語報告常見看法，但不表示它一定是真的。"},{"en":"It is useful when summarising theories carefully.","zh":"它適合用於謹慎總結理論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"good at nurturing","meaning":"擅長照顧和培育","examples":[{"en":"Some studies claim that oldest children are good at nurturing.","zh":"有些研究聲稱家中老大擅長照顧和培育。"},{"en":"To be good at nurturing means to be skilled at caring for and supporting others as they grow.","zh":"good at nurturing 指擅長照顧和支持他人成長。"},{"en":"Older siblings may become good at nurturing if they help look after younger children.","zh":"如果年長兄姊幫忙照顧幼兒，他們可能變得擅長照顧和培育。"},{"en":"Nurturing behaviour includes patience, protection and encouragement.","zh":"培育行為包括耐性、保護和鼓勵。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in family and child development contexts.","zh":"這個片語常用於家庭和兒童發展語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"在過去","examples":[{"en":"In the past, older children in large families often looked after younger ones.","zh":"在過去，大家庭中的年長孩子常照顧年幼弟妹。"},{"en":"In the past means in earlier times.","zh":"in the past 指在較早的時代。"},{"en":"In the past, families were often larger than they are today.","zh":"在過去，家庭通常比今天更大。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare old habits with modern life.","zh":"這個片語有助比較舊習慣與現代生活。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving historical background.","zh":"它適合用於提供歷史背景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"large families","meaning":"大家庭","examples":[{"en":"In large families, older children were expected to look after the younger ones.","zh":"在大家庭中，年長孩子被期望照顧年幼弟妹。"},{"en":"Large families are families with many children or members.","zh":"large families 指有很多孩子或成員的家庭。"},{"en":"In large families, siblings may share responsibilities more often.","zh":"在大家庭中，兄弟姊妹可能更常分擔責任。"},{"en":"Family size can affect how much attention each child receives.","zh":"家庭規模會影響每個孩子得到多少關注。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in family and social research.","zh":"這個片語常見於家庭和社會研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be expected to","meaning":"被期望要……","examples":[{"en":"Older children were expected to look after their younger siblings.","zh":"年長孩子被期望要照顧年幼弟妹。"},{"en":"To be expected to do something means people believe or require that you should do it.","zh":"be expected to do something 指人們相信或要求你應該做某事。"},{"en":"Oldest children may be expected to help with chores.","zh":"家中老大可能被期望幫忙做家務。"},{"en":"Expectations can shape children’s behaviour and confidence.","zh":"期望可以塑造孩子的行為和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing social roles.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論社會角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"look after the younger ones","meaning":"照顧年幼的弟妹","examples":[{"en":"Oldest children were often expected to look after the younger ones.","zh":"家中老大常被期望照顧年幼的弟妹。"},{"en":"To look after the younger ones means to care for younger children or siblings.","zh":"look after the younger ones 指照顧較年幼的孩子或兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"Ruth sometimes had to look after the younger ones while her parents were busy.","zh":"父母忙碌時，Ruth 有時要照顧年幼弟妹。"},{"en":"Looking after younger siblings can teach responsibility.","zh":"照顧年幼弟妹可以培養責任感。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in family situations.","zh":"這個片語常見於家庭情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a clear picture","meaning":"清晰的圖像；明確情況","examples":[{"en":"There is not such a clear picture for middle children.","zh":"對排行中間的孩子來說，情況沒有那麼明確。"},{"en":"A clear picture means an easy-to-understand situation or pattern.","zh":"clear picture 指容易理解的情況或模式。"},{"en":"The research does not give a clear picture of youngest children.","zh":"研究沒有給出關於最年幼孩子的清晰圖像。"},{"en":"If studies disagree, it is hard to form a clear picture.","zh":"如果研究互相矛盾，就很難形成明確情況。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing mixed evidence.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論混合證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"middle children","meaning":"排行中間的孩子","examples":[{"en":"Middle children are often described as easier to get on with.","zh":"排行中間的孩子常被描述為較容易相處。"},{"en":"Middle children are children who have both older and younger siblings.","zh":"middle children 指同時有年長和年幼兄弟姊妹的孩子。"},{"en":"Middle children may need to find their role between older and younger siblings.","zh":"排行中間的孩子可能需要在年長和年幼弟妹之間找到自己的角色。"},{"en":"Some theories claim middle children become flexible because of their family position.","zh":"有些理論聲稱排行中間的孩子因家庭位置而變得靈活。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies another birth-order group.","zh":"這個片語識別另一個出生順序群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"one trait that","meaning":"其中一個……的特質","examples":[{"en":"One trait that many studies mention is that middle children are easy-going.","zh":"許多研究提到的其中一個特質，是排行中間的孩子較隨和。"},{"en":"One trait that means one characteristic which.","zh":"one trait that 指其中一個……的特質。"},{"en":"One trait that people often mention is confidence.","zh":"人們常提到的其中一個特質是自信。"},{"en":"This phrase helps introduce a specific quality from a list of possible traits.","zh":"這個片語有助從可能特質中引入一項具體特質。"},{"en":"It is useful in descriptions and analysis.","zh":"它適合用於描述和分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"studies mention","meaning":"研究提到","examples":[{"en":"Many studies mention that middle children are easier to get on with.","zh":"許多研究提到排行中間的孩子較容易相處。"},{"en":"Studies mention something when they include or refer to it.","zh":"studies mention something 指研究包括或提及某事。"},{"en":"Several studies mention the role of family size.","zh":"幾項研究提到家庭規模的作用。"},{"en":"Mentioning a point does not always mean proving it strongly.","zh":"提到某點不一定代表強力證明它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when summarising research.","zh":"這個片語適合用於總結研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"easier to get on with","meaning":"較容易相處","examples":[{"en":"Middle children are said to be easier to get on with.","zh":"排行中間的孩子據說較容易相處。"},{"en":"Easier to get on with means more pleasant or less difficult to have a good relationship with.","zh":"easier to get on with 指較容易建立良好關係，或相處起來較舒服。"},{"en":"People who listen well are often easier to get on with.","zh":"善於聆聽的人通常較容易相處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social compatibility.","zh":"這個片語描述社交上的合拍程度。"},{"en":"It is common in everyday discussion of personality.","zh":"它常見於日常性格討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"older or younger siblings","meaning":"年長或年幼的兄弟姊妹","examples":[{"en":"Middle children may be easier to get on with than older or younger siblings.","zh":"排行中間的孩子可能比年長或年幼的兄弟姊妹較容易相處。"},{"en":"Older or younger siblings means brothers or sisters who are older or younger than someone.","zh":"older or younger siblings 指比某人年長或年幼的兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"A middle child has both older and younger siblings.","zh":"排行中間的孩子同時有年長和年幼的兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"Relationships with older or younger siblings can shape confidence and behaviour.","zh":"與年長或年幼兄弟姊妹的關係可以塑造自信和行為。"},{"en":"This phrase compares different sibling positions.","zh":"這個片語比較不同兄弟姊妹位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"eager to please","meaning":"渴望討好別人","examples":[{"en":"Middle children are sometimes described as eager to please.","zh":"排行中間的孩子有時被描述為渴望討好別人。"},{"en":"Eager to please means very willing to make others happy or gain approval.","zh":"eager to please 指非常願意令別人開心或得到認同。"},{"en":"A child who is eager to please may agree too quickly with others.","zh":"渴望討好別人的孩子可能太快同意別人。"},{"en":"This trait can be positive, but it may also suggest a need for approval.","zh":"這個特質可以是正面的，但也可能暗示需要認可。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in personality descriptions.","zh":"這個片語常用於性格描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"as far as my family goes","meaning":"就我家庭而言","examples":[{"en":"Ruth says that the description is not accurate as far as her family goes.","zh":"Ruth 說就她家庭而言，這個描述並不準確。"},{"en":"As far as my family goes means when considering my family’s situation.","zh":"as far as my family goes 指就我家庭的情況來說。"},{"en":"As far as my family goes, the youngest child is not confident at all.","zh":"就我家庭而言，最年幼的孩子一點也不自信。"},{"en":"This phrase limits a statement to one personal example.","zh":"這個片語把說法限制在一個個人例子。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing research claims with personal experience.","zh":"它適合用於比較研究說法與個人經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be a nightmare","meaning":"是一場惡夢；很難相處","examples":[{"en":"Ruth says her middle brother was a nightmare.","zh":"Ruth 說她排行中間的哥哥很難相處。"},{"en":"To be a nightmare means to be extremely difficult, annoying or unpleasant.","zh":"be a nightmare 指非常困難、煩人或令人不快。"},{"en":"My younger brother was a nightmare when he wanted attention.","zh":"我弟弟想要關注時真的很難搞。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often exaggerated.","zh":"這個片語較口語，常帶誇張意味。"},{"en":"It does not literally mean a bad dream in this context.","zh":"在這個語境中，它不是字面上的惡夢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cause fights","meaning":"挑起爭吵","examples":[{"en":"Ruth’s middle brother was always causing fights.","zh":"Ruth 排行中間的哥哥總是挑起爭吵。"},{"en":"To cause fights means to start arguments or conflicts.","zh":"cause fights 指引發爭論或衝突。"},{"en":"The children caused fights over toys and attention.","zh":"孩子們為玩具和關注而挑起爭吵。"},{"en":"Someone who often causes fights can make family life stressful.","zh":"經常挑起爭吵的人會令家庭生活充滿壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes behaviour that creates conflict.","zh":"這個片語描述製造衝突的行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be envious of","meaning":"嫉妒……","examples":[{"en":"Ruth’s brother was envious of whatever she had.","zh":"Ruth 的哥哥嫉妒她擁有的任何東西。"},{"en":"To be envious of someone or something means to want what another person has.","zh":"be envious of someone or something 指想要別人擁有的東西。"},{"en":"He was envious of his sister’s new bicycle.","zh":"他嫉妒妹妹的新單車。"},{"en":"Envy between siblings can lead to arguments.","zh":"兄弟姊妹之間的嫉妒可能導致爭吵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes jealousy or desire.","zh":"這個片語描述妒忌或渴望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as I said","meaning":"正如我所說","examples":[{"en":"Ed says, “As I said, none of this relates to my own experience.”","zh":"Ed 說：「正如我所說，這些都與我自己的經驗無關。」"},{"en":"As I said means as I mentioned earlier.","zh":"as I said 指正如我之前提過。"},{"en":"As I said, the evidence is not very strong.","zh":"正如我所說，證據不是很強。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a previous point.","zh":"這個片語指回之前的重點。"},{"en":"It can sound helpful or slightly impatient depending on tone.","zh":"它可以聽起來有幫助，也可能因語氣而顯得有點不耐煩。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"relate to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The studies do not seem to relate to Ed’s own experience.","zh":"這些研究似乎與 Ed 自己的經驗無關。"},{"en":"To relate to something means to connect with it or be relevant to it.","zh":"relate to something 指與某事有連繫或相關。"},{"en":"Some research findings do not relate to every family.","zh":"有些研究發現未必與每個家庭有關。"},{"en":"Personal experience may not always relate to general theories.","zh":"個人經驗未必總是與一般理論相符。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing evidence with real life.","zh":"這個片語適合比較證據與現實生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"my own experience","meaning":"我自己的經驗","examples":[{"en":"Ed does not recognise his own experience in the studies.","zh":"Ed 在研究中看不到自己的經驗。"},{"en":"My own experience means what I personally have lived through or observed.","zh":"my own experience 指我個人經歷或觀察到的事。"},{"en":"My own experience of being the youngest child was very different.","zh":"我作為最年幼孩子的自身經驗非常不同。"},{"en":"Personal experience can challenge general claims.","zh":"個人經驗可以挑戰一般說法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reflective discussion.","zh":"這個片語適合用於反思討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the youngest in my family","meaning":"家中最年幼的孩子","examples":[{"en":"Ed is the youngest in his family.","zh":"Ed 是家中最年幼的孩子。"},{"en":"The youngest in my family means the child born last among the siblings.","zh":"youngest in my family 指兄弟姊妹中最後出生的孩子。"},{"en":"I am the youngest in my family, with two older sisters.","zh":"我是家中最年幼的孩子，有兩個姐姐。"},{"en":"Youngest children are often described in research as sociable or confident.","zh":"研究中常把最年幼孩子描述為外向或自信。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a person’s birth order.","zh":"這個片語識別一個人的出生順序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"recognise myself in","meaning":"在……中看到自己的影子","examples":[{"en":"Ed does not recognise himself in any of the studies he has read.","zh":"Ed 在讀過的任何研究中都看不到自己的影子。"},{"en":"To recognise myself in something means to see my own behaviour or experience reflected in it.","zh":"recognise myself in something 指在某事中看到自己的行為或經驗被反映出來。"},{"en":"I do not recognise myself in the description of youngest children.","zh":"我在最年幼孩子的描述中看不到自己的影子。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing research with personal identity.","zh":"這個片語適合用於比較研究和個人身份。"},{"en":"It often suggests that a general description does not fit the speaker.","zh":"它常暗示一般描述並不符合說話者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be supposed to have been","meaning":"按理說本應是","examples":[{"en":"Ed is supposed to have been sociable and confident as a child.","zh":"Ed 按理說小時候本應外向而自信。"},{"en":"Be supposed to have been means people say or expect that someone was a certain way in the past.","zh":"be supposed to have been 指人們說或預期某人過去應該是某種樣子。"},{"en":"As the youngest child, he was supposed to have been outgoing.","zh":"作為最年幼的孩子，他按理說本應外向。"},{"en":"This phrase can show a contrast between theory and reality.","zh":"這個片語可以顯示理論與現實之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when questioning stereotypes.","zh":"它適合用於質疑刻板印象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sociable and confident","meaning":"外向而自信","examples":[{"en":"Youngest children are often described as sociable and confident.","zh":"最年幼的孩子常被描述為外向而自信。"},{"en":"Sociable and confident means friendly with others and sure of oneself.","zh":"sociable and confident 指善於與人相處，而且對自己有信心。"},{"en":"A sociable and confident child may enjoy meeting new people.","zh":"外向而自信的孩子可能喜歡認識新朋友。"},{"en":"These traits are often associated with ease in social situations.","zh":"這些特質常與在社交場合自在有關。"},{"en":"This phrase describes positive personality qualities.","zh":"這個片語描述正面的性格特質。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make friends easily","meaning":"容易交朋友","examples":[{"en":"Youngest children are said to make friends easily.","zh":"最年幼的孩子據說容易交朋友。"},{"en":"To make friends easily means to form friendships without much difficulty.","zh":"make friends easily 指不太困難便能建立友誼。"},{"en":"Ruth makes friends easily because she is open and cheerful.","zh":"Ruth 因為開朗而容易交朋友。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social confidence and approachability.","zh":"這個片語描述社交自信和親和力。"},{"en":"It is often used in personality descriptions.","zh":"它常用於性格描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"terribly shy","meaning":"非常害羞","examples":[{"en":"Ed was actually terribly shy as a child.","zh":"Ed 小時候其實非常害羞。"},{"en":"Terribly shy means extremely shy.","zh":"terribly shy 指極度害羞。"},{"en":"He was terribly shy and hated speaking in front of the class.","zh":"他非常害羞，討厭在全班面前說話。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises shyness.","zh":"這個片語強烈強調害羞。"},{"en":"It contrasts with being sociable and confident.","zh":"它與外向和自信形成對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hundreds of studies on","meaning":"有數以百計關於……的研究","examples":[{"en":"There have been hundreds of studies on twins.","zh":"有數以百計關於雙胞胎的研究。"},{"en":"Hundreds of studies on something means a very large number of research projects about that topic.","zh":"hundreds of studies on something 指大量關於某題目的研究。"},{"en":"There are hundreds of studies on memory and learning.","zh":"有數以百計關於記憶與學習的研究。"},{"en":"A large number of studies can show that a topic is important.","zh":"大量研究可以顯示某題目很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic discussion.","zh":"這個片語常見於學術討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"nurture versus nature","meaning":"後天養育與先天本性","examples":[{"en":"Most studies on twins are about nurture versus nature.","zh":"大多數關於雙胞胎的研究都關於後天養育與先天本性。"},{"en":"Nurture versus nature refers to the debate over whether behaviour is shaped more by upbringing or biology.","zh":"nurture versus nature 指行為更多由後天環境還是先天生物因素塑造的爭論。"},{"en":"Twin studies are often used to examine nurture versus nature.","zh":"雙胞胎研究常用來檢視後天養育與先天本性。"},{"en":"The issue asks whether personality comes from genes, environment or both.","zh":"這個議題詢問性格來自基因、環境，還是兩者。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to psychology.","zh":"這個片語是心理學中的核心概念。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be likely to be","meaning":"很可能是……","examples":[{"en":"A twin is likely to be shy in social situations.","zh":"雙胞胎在社交場合很可能會害羞。"},{"en":"To be likely to be something means to probably be that way.","zh":"be likely to be something 指很可能是某種情況。"},{"en":"A child with a very close sibling may be likely to be less independent.","zh":"與兄弟姊妹非常親近的孩子很可能較不獨立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes probability, not certainty.","zh":"這個片語描述可能性，而不是確定性。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing research findings carefully.","zh":"它適合用於謹慎討論研究發現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"social situations","meaning":"社交場合","examples":[{"en":"Twins may be shy in social situations.","zh":"雙胞胎在社交場合可能會害羞。"},{"en":"Social situations are occasions where people interact with others.","zh":"social situations 指人們與他人互動的場合。"},{"en":"Parties, group work and class discussions are social situations.","zh":"派對、小組工作和課堂討論都是社交場合。"},{"en":"Some people feel confident at home but shy in social situations.","zh":"有些人在家很自信，但在社交場合會害羞。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in psychology and everyday conversation.","zh":"這個片語常見於心理學和日常對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have someone around","meaning":"有某人在身邊","examples":[{"en":"A twin often has their twin around for support.","zh":"雙胞胎常有自己的雙胞胎兄弟姊妹在身邊作支持。"},{"en":"To have someone around means to have someone nearby or available.","zh":"have someone around 指有某人在附近或可提供幫助。"},{"en":"Ruth always had her brother around when she was small.","zh":"Ruth 小時候總有哥哥在身邊。"},{"en":"Having someone around can make a child feel safer.","zh":"有某人在身邊可以令孩子感到更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in conversations about relationships and support.","zh":"這個片語常見於關係和支援的對話中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"depend on someone for support","meaning":"依靠某人支持","examples":[{"en":"A twin may depend on their twin for support.","zh":"雙胞胎可能依靠自己的雙胞胎兄弟姊妹作支持。"},{"en":"To depend on someone for support means to rely on that person for help or confidence.","zh":"depend on someone for support 指依靠某人提供幫助或信心。"},{"en":"Some children depend on an older sibling for emotional support.","zh":"有些孩子依靠年長兄姊作情感支持。"},{"en":"Dependence can be comforting, but it may also reduce independence.","zh":"依靠可以令人安心，但也可能減少獨立性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in psychological discussion.","zh":"這個片語適合用於心理學討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be only interested in","meaning":"只對……感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Ruth’s cousins were only interested in each other when they were small.","zh":"Ruth 的表親小時候只對彼此感興趣。"},{"en":"To be only interested in something means to care about that thing and not much else.","zh":"be only interested in something 指只關心某事，而不太理會其他事物。"},{"en":"The twins were only interested in playing together.","zh":"那對雙胞胎只對一起玩感興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest a narrow focus.","zh":"這個片語可以暗示焦點狹窄。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing social behaviour.","zh":"它適合描述社交行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"engage with","meaning":"與……互動","examples":[{"en":"Ruth’s cousins found it hard to engage with other children.","zh":"Ruth 的表親覺得很難與其他小朋友互動。"},{"en":"To engage with someone means to interact with them in a meaningful way.","zh":"engage with someone 指與某人有意義地互動。"},{"en":"Some shy children find it hard to engage with classmates.","zh":"有些害羞的孩子覺得很難與同學互動。"},{"en":"Engagement involves attention, response and social connection.","zh":"互動涉及注意、回應和社交連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in education and psychology.","zh":"這個片語常見於教育和心理學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be fine now","meaning":"現在沒有問題","examples":[{"en":"Ruth says her cousins are fine now.","zh":"Ruth 說她的表親現在沒有問題。"},{"en":"To be fine now means to be okay or no longer have the earlier problem.","zh":"be fine now 指現在沒問題，或不再有早前的困難。"},{"en":"He was shy as a child, but he is fine now.","zh":"他小時候很害羞，但現在沒有問題。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures the listener that the situation has improved.","zh":"這個片語讓聽者放心，表示情況已改善。"},{"en":"It is common in everyday conversation.","zh":"它常見於日常對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have a bad press","meaning":"名聲不好；評價很差","examples":[{"en":"Only children have had a really bad press.","zh":"獨生子女一直評價很差。"},{"en":"To have a bad press means to receive negative public comments or reputation.","zh":"have a bad press 指得到負面公眾評論或名聲。"},{"en":"Only children often have a bad press in popular discussions.","zh":"在大眾討論中，獨生子女常名聲不好。"},{"en":"A group can have a bad press even if the criticism is unfair.","zh":"即使批評不公平，一個群體也可能評價很差。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often refers to public image.","zh":"這個片語較口語，常指公眾形象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"brand someone as","meaning":"把某人標籤為……","examples":[{"en":"Some studies have branded only children as loners.","zh":"有些研究把獨生子女標籤為孤僻的人。"},{"en":"To brand someone as something means to label them in a strong and often unfair way.","zh":"brand someone as something 指以強烈而常不公平的方式標籤某人。"},{"en":"The media sometimes brands teenagers as lazy.","zh":"媒體有時把青少年標籤為懶惰。"},{"en":"Branding people can create stereotypes that are hard to change.","zh":"標籤人會製造難以改變的刻板印象。"},{"en":"This phrase often has a negative tone.","zh":"這個片語通常帶負面語氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"loners","meaning":"孤僻的人","examples":[{"en":"Some studies describe only children as loners.","zh":"有些研究把獨生子女描述為孤僻的人。"},{"en":"Loners are people who prefer being alone or have few close social connections.","zh":"loners 指較喜歡獨處或親密社交連繫較少的人。"},{"en":"Calling only children loners may be unfair and over-simple.","zh":"把獨生子女稱為孤僻的人可能不公平而且過度簡化。"},{"en":"A person can enjoy time alone without being antisocial.","zh":"一個人可以喜歡獨處，但不代表不合群。"},{"en":"This word can sound negative depending on context.","zh":"這個字視乎語境可帶負面意思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the world revolves around them","meaning":"世界圍着他們轉","examples":[{"en":"Some studies claim that only children think the world revolves around them.","zh":"有些研究聲稱獨生子女認為世界圍着他們轉。"},{"en":"To think the world revolves around them means to believe everything should focus on them.","zh":"think the world revolves around them 指認為所有事情都應以自己為中心。"},{"en":"A spoiled child may behave as if the world revolves around him.","zh":"被寵壞的孩子可能表現得好像世界圍着他轉。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly criticises selfish or self-centred behaviour.","zh":"這個片語強烈批評自私或以自我為中心的行為。"},{"en":"It is an idiom, not a literal description.","zh":"它是習語，不是字面描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fight for","meaning":"爭取……","examples":[{"en":"Only children have never had to fight for their parents’ attention.","zh":"獨生子女從來不用爭取父母的關注。"},{"en":"To fight for something means to compete or struggle to get it.","zh":"fight for something 指競爭或努力得到某物。"},{"en":"In large families, children may fight for time with their parents.","zh":"在大家庭中，孩子可能要爭取與父母相處的時間。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal or figurative.","zh":"這個片語可以是字面或比喻意思。"},{"en":"Here, it means competing for emotional attention.","zh":"在這裡，它指競爭情感上的關注。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"parents’ attention","meaning":"父母的關注","examples":[{"en":"Only children do not have to compete for their parents’ attention.","zh":"獨生子女不用爭取父母的關注。"},{"en":"Parents’ attention means the time, care and focus parents give to their children.","zh":"parents’ attention 指父母給予孩子的時間、照顧和專注。"},{"en":"Younger siblings may compete for parents’ attention after a new baby is born.","zh":"新嬰兒出生後，年幼兄弟姊妹可能會爭取父母的關注。"},{"en":"Attention from parents can affect a child’s confidence and behaviour.","zh":"父母的關注會影響孩子的自信和行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in family psychology.","zh":"這個片語常見於家庭心理學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a bit harsh","meaning":"有點苛刻","examples":[{"en":"Ruth thinks the criticism of only children is a bit harsh.","zh":"Ruth 覺得對獨生子女的批評有點苛刻。"},{"en":"A bit harsh means slightly too critical or unfair.","zh":"a bit harsh 指稍為太批判或不公平。"},{"en":"Saying all only children are selfish is a bit harsh.","zh":"說所有獨生子女都自私有點苛刻。"},{"en":"This phrase softens disagreement while still criticising the statement.","zh":"這個片語柔化不同意見，同時仍批評該說法。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken English.","zh":"它常見於英語口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"one category","meaning":"一個類別","examples":[{"en":"Ruth mentions one category she had not considered before.","zh":"Ruth 提到一個她之前沒有考慮過的類別。"},{"en":"One category means one group or type within a larger classification.","zh":"one category 指較大分類中的一個群體或類型。"},{"en":"One category in birth-order research is only children.","zh":"出生順序研究中的一個類別是獨生子女。"},{"en":"Categories help researchers organise people or ideas.","zh":"類別幫助研究者組織人或想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when classifying information.","zh":"這個片語適合用於分類資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hadn’t considered before","meaning":"之前沒有考慮過","examples":[{"en":"Ruth had not considered children with much older siblings before.","zh":"Ruth 之前沒有考慮過有年長很多兄弟姊妹的孩子。"},{"en":"Hadn’t considered before means had not thought about it earlier.","zh":"hadn’t considered before 指之前沒有想過某事。"},{"en":"I hadn’t considered before how family size could affect the results.","zh":"我之前沒有考慮過家庭規模如何影響結果。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a new idea has entered the discussion.","zh":"這個片語顯示有新想法進入討論。"},{"en":"It is useful in reflective academic talk.","zh":"它適合用於反思性學術討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"much older siblings","meaning":"年長很多的兄弟姊妹","examples":[{"en":"Some children have siblings who are much older than them.","zh":"有些孩子有年長很多的兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"Much older siblings are brothers or sisters who are far older in age.","zh":"much older siblings 指年齡大很多的兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"A child with much older siblings may grow up around teenagers or adults.","zh":"有年長很多兄弟姊妹的孩子可能在青少年或成年人身邊長大。"},{"en":"A large age gap can change family roles and expectations.","zh":"年齡差距大會改變家庭角色和期望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific sibling relationship.","zh":"這個片語描述一種特定兄弟姊妹關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a couple of studies","meaning":"幾項研究","examples":[{"en":"A couple of studies mention children with much older siblings.","zh":"幾項研究提到有年長很多兄弟姊妹的孩子。"},{"en":"A couple of studies means two or a few research studies.","zh":"a couple of studies 指兩項或幾項研究。"},{"en":"A couple of studies suggest that family size matters.","zh":"幾項研究指出家庭規模很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a small amount of evidence.","zh":"這個片語提供少量證據。"},{"en":"It is less strong than saying “many studies”.","zh":"它沒有 “many studies” 那麼有力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"grow up more quickly","meaning":"較快長大","examples":[{"en":"Children with much older siblings may grow up more quickly.","zh":"有年長很多兄弟姊妹的孩子可能較快長大。"},{"en":"To grow up more quickly means to become mature earlier than expected.","zh":"grow up more quickly 指比預期更早成熟。"},{"en":"Children surrounded by older siblings may grow up more quickly in some ways.","zh":"被年長兄姊圍繞的孩子在某些方面可能較快長大。"},{"en":"They may learn adult behaviour earlier because they spend time with older family members.","zh":"他們可能因與年長家人相處而更早學到成人行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional or practical maturity.","zh":"這個片語描述情感或實際成熟。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"do basic things for themselves","meaning":"自己做基本事情","examples":[{"en":"These children may be expected to do basic things for themselves.","zh":"這些孩子可能被期望自己做基本事情。"},{"en":"To do basic things for themselves means to manage simple daily tasks independently.","zh":"do basic things for themselves 指獨立處理簡單日常任務。"},{"en":"Young children may learn to do basic things for themselves, such as washing or dressing.","zh":"幼兒可能學會自己做洗漱或穿衣等基本事情。"},{"en":"Independence can develop when adults expect children to manage small tasks.","zh":"當成年人期望孩子處理小任務時，獨立性可以發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in child development discussion.","zh":"這個片語常見於兒童發展討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"get dressed","meaning":"自己穿衣服","examples":[{"en":"Young children may be expected to get dressed by themselves.","zh":"年幼孩子可能被期望自己穿衣服。"},{"en":"To get dressed means to put on clothes.","zh":"get dressed 指穿上衣服。"},{"en":"By the age of five, many children can get dressed without help.","zh":"到五歲時，許多孩子可以不用幫忙自己穿衣服。"},{"en":"Learning to get dressed is one step towards independence.","zh":"學會自己穿衣服是走向獨立的一步。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday routines.","zh":"這個片語常見於日常習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"I can see how","meaning":"我明白為甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Ed says, “I can see how that might be true.”","zh":"Ed 說：「我明白為甚麼那可能是真的。」"},{"en":"I can see how means I understand why something might be possible or reasonable.","zh":"I can see how 指我明白為甚麼某事可能合理或可能發生。"},{"en":"I can see how older siblings might influence a child’s behaviour.","zh":"我明白為甚麼年長兄姊可能影響孩子行為。"},{"en":"This phrase shows partial agreement or understanding.","zh":"這個片語表示部分同意或理解。"},{"en":"It does not necessarily mean full agreement.","zh":"它不一定代表完全同意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the exact opposite","meaning":"完全相反","examples":[{"en":"Ed expects that some children may be the exact opposite.","zh":"Ed 預期有些孩子可能完全相反。"},{"en":"The exact opposite means completely different from what has just been described.","zh":"exact opposite 指與剛才描述的情況完全不同。"},{"en":"Some children become independent, while others do the exact opposite.","zh":"有些孩子變得獨立，而另一些則完全相反。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a strong contrast.","zh":"這個片語強調強烈對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing that one theory does not fit everyone.","zh":"它適合用於顯示一個理論不適用於所有人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"play the baby role","meaning":"扮演小寶寶角色","examples":[{"en":"Some younger children may play the baby role in the family.","zh":"有些年幼孩子可能在家中扮演小寶寶角色。"},{"en":"To play the baby role means to behave like the youngest or most dependent child in order to receive care.","zh":"play the baby role 指表現得像最年幼或最依賴的孩子，以得到照顧。"},{"en":"A child may play the baby role if everyone treats them as little.","zh":"如果人人都把孩子當成小朋友，他可能會扮演小寶寶角色。"},{"en":"This behaviour may bring attention, protection or special treatment.","zh":"這種行為可能帶來關注、保護或特別待遇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing family roles.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論家庭角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"clamour for","meaning":"吵着要求……","examples":[{"en":"Some children clamour for special treatment.","zh":"有些孩子吵着要求特別待遇。"},{"en":"To clamour for something means to demand it loudly or repeatedly.","zh":"clamour for something 指大聲或反覆要求某事。"},{"en":"The youngest child clamoured for attention whenever guests arrived.","zh":"每當客人到訪，最年幼的孩子就吵着要關注。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests noisy or insistent demand.","zh":"這個片語暗示吵鬧或堅持要求。"},{"en":"It is stronger than simply “ask for”.","zh":"它比單純 “ask for” 更強烈。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"special treatment","meaning":"特別待遇","examples":[{"en":"Some younger children demand special treatment from their family.","zh":"有些年幼孩子向家人要求特別待遇。"},{"en":"Special treatment means different or extra favourable treatment given to someone.","zh":"special treatment 指給某人不同或額外優待。"},{"en":"A child may expect special treatment if adults always give in to them.","zh":"如果成年人總是讓步，孩子可能會期待特別待遇。"},{"en":"Special treatment can create tension between siblings.","zh":"特別待遇可能在兄弟姊妹之間造成緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing fairness.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論公平。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the problem with","meaning":"……的問題","examples":[{"en":"Ruth asks about the problem with most of the studies.","zh":"Ruth 問大多數研究的問題是甚麼。"},{"en":"The problem with something means the weakness, difficulty or fault connected with it.","zh":"the problem with something 指與某事相關的弱點、困難或缺陷。"},{"en":"The problem with small samples is that results may not be reliable.","zh":"小樣本的問題是結果可能不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evaluating research.","zh":"這個片語適合用於評估研究。"},{"en":"It introduces criticism or limitation.","zh":"它引入批評或限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in a lot of cases","meaning":"在很多情況下","examples":[{"en":"In a lot of cases, the data were collected from only one sibling per family.","zh":"在很多情況下，數據只收集自每個家庭一名兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"In a lot of cases means in many situations or examples.","zh":"in a lot of cases 指在許多情況或例子中。"},{"en":"In a lot of cases, the studies relied on self-reports.","zh":"在很多情況下，研究依賴自我報告。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something happens often but not always.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事經常發生，但不是永遠如此。"},{"en":"It is useful when making careful generalisations.","zh":"它適合用於謹慎概括。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"data were collected from","meaning":"數據收集自……","examples":[{"en":"In many studies, data were collected from only one sibling per family.","zh":"在許多研究中，數據只收集自每個家庭一名兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"Data were collected from means information was gathered from a particular source or group.","zh":"data were collected from 指資料從某來源或群體收集而來。"},{"en":"In the survey, data were collected from university students.","zh":"在調查中，數據收集自大學生。"},{"en":"The source of data affects how reliable the study is.","zh":"數據來源會影響研究有多可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research methodology.","zh":"這個片語常見於研究方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one sibling per family","meaning":"每個家庭一名兄弟姊妹","examples":[{"en":"Many studies used only one sibling per family as a source of data.","zh":"許多研究只使用每個家庭一名兄弟姊妹作為數據來源。"},{"en":"One sibling per family means only one brother or sister from each family.","zh":"one sibling per family 指每個家庭只選一名兄弟或姊妹。"},{"en":"Studying only one sibling per family may give a one-sided view.","zh":"只研究每個家庭一名兄弟姊妹，可能會得到單方面看法。"},{"en":"Researchers may miss disagreements between siblings if they ask only one person.","zh":"如果研究者只問一個人，可能會錯過兄弟姊妹之間的不同看法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sampling limitation.","zh":"這個片語描述抽樣限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rate themselves and their siblings","meaning":"評價自己和自己的兄弟姊妹","examples":[{"en":"Participants rated themselves and their siblings at the same time.","zh":"參加者同時評價自己和自己的兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"To rate themselves and their siblings means to judge or score their own traits and their siblings’ traits.","zh":"rate themselves and their siblings 指評分或判斷自己及兄弟姊妹的特質。"},{"en":"Participants rated themselves and their siblings for confidence and sociability.","zh":"參加者就自信和社交能力評價自己和兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"This method may be biased because one person judges everyone.","zh":"這種方法可能有偏差，因為由同一人評價所有人。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in questionnaire-based research.","zh":"這個片語常見於問卷研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同時","examples":[{"en":"One sibling rated themselves and their siblings at the same time.","zh":"一名兄弟姊妹同時評價自己和自己的兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"At the same time means during the same period or on the same occasion.","zh":"at the same time 指在同一時段或同一場合。"},{"en":"The student completed the survey and rated her brother at the same time.","zh":"那名學生完成調查時，同時評價她哥哥。"},{"en":"Doing two evaluations at the same time may affect objectivity.","zh":"同時進行兩項評估可能影響客觀性。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday and academic English.","zh":"這個片語常見於日常和學術英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"research into","meaning":"對……的研究","examples":[{"en":"Some old research into birth order and academic achievement has proved accurate.","zh":"一些對出生順序與學業成就的舊研究已被證明是準確的。"},{"en":"Research into something means study or investigation of that topic.","zh":"research into something 指對某主題的研究或調查。"},{"en":"Research into twins has helped psychologists understand nature and nurture.","zh":"對雙胞胎的研究幫助心理學家了解先天與後天因素。"},{"en":"This phrase is slightly formal and common in academic writing.","zh":"這個片語略正式，常見於學術寫作。"},{"en":"It focuses on the subject being investigated.","zh":"它着重正在被研究的主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the relationship between","meaning":"……之間的關係","examples":[{"en":"The research examined the relationship between birth order and academic achievement.","zh":"研究檢視出生順序與學業成就之間的關係。"},{"en":"The relationship between two things means the connection or link between them.","zh":"relationship between two things 指兩件事之間的連繫或關聯。"},{"en":"Researchers studied the relationship between sleep and memory.","zh":"研究者研究睡眠與記憶之間的關係。"},{"en":"A relationship in data does not always prove direct cause and effect.","zh":"數據中的關係不一定證明直接因果。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於研究問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"academic achievement","meaning":"學業成就","examples":[{"en":"Some studies examine the link between birth order and academic achievement.","zh":"有些研究檢視出生順序與學業成就之間的關聯。"},{"en":"Academic achievement means success in school, college or university work.","zh":"academic achievement 指在學校、大專或大學學業上的成功。"},{"en":"Exam results and grades are common measures of academic achievement.","zh":"考試成績和分數是量度學業成就的常見方式。"},{"en":"Many factors can affect academic achievement, including family background and motivation.","zh":"許多因素會影響學業成就，包括家庭背景和動機。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in education research.","zh":"這個片語常見於教育研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be proved to be accurate","meaning":"被證明是準確的","examples":[{"en":"Some old research has been proved to be accurate.","zh":"一些舊研究已被證明是準確的。"},{"en":"To be proved to be accurate means to be shown by later evidence to be correct.","zh":"be proved to be accurate 指後來證據顯示某事正確。"},{"en":"The early findings were later proved to be accurate by larger studies.","zh":"早期發現後來被更大型研究證明是準確的。"},{"en":"Research becomes more convincing when later studies confirm it.","zh":"當後來研究確認早前結果，研究會更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing evidence over time.","zh":"這個片語適合討論隨時間累積的證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"intelligence tests","meaning":"智力測驗","examples":[{"en":"Performances in intelligence tests decline slightly among younger siblings.","zh":"年幼兄弟姊妹在智力測驗中的表現略微下降。"},{"en":"Intelligence tests are assessments designed to measure reasoning, problem-solving or cognitive ability.","zh":"intelligence tests 指用來量度推理、解難或認知能力的評估。"},{"en":"Researchers sometimes use intelligence tests to compare academic-related ability.","zh":"研究者有時使用智力測驗比較與學業相關的能力。"},{"en":"Test results can be influenced by education, background and testing conditions.","zh":"測驗結果可能受教育、背景和測驗環境影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in psychology and education research.","zh":"這個片語常見於心理學和教育研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"decline slightly","meaning":"略微下降","examples":[{"en":"Performance in intelligence tests may decline slightly from the eldest child to younger siblings.","zh":"智力測驗表現可能由家中老大至年幼兄弟姊妹略微下降。"},{"en":"To decline slightly means to decrease a little.","zh":"decline slightly 指輕微下降。"},{"en":"Scores declined slightly when family size increased.","zh":"當家庭規模增加，分數略微下降。"},{"en":"A slight decline may be statistically real but small in everyday terms.","zh":"輕微下降在統計上可能真實，但日常意義上幅度很小。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing data trends.","zh":"這個片語適合用於描述數據趨勢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"from … to …","meaning":"由……至……","examples":[{"en":"Performance declines slightly from the eldest child to younger siblings.","zh":"表現由家中老大至年幼兄弟姊妹略微下降。"},{"en":"From … to … shows the starting point and ending point of a change or range.","zh":"from … to … 顯示變化或範圍的起點和終點。"},{"en":"The scores changed from high to moderate across the group.","zh":"分數在群體中由高變成中等。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when describing movement, change or comparison.","zh":"這個結構適合用於描述移動、變化或比較。"},{"en":"It helps show direction clearly.","zh":"它有助清楚顯示方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"recent studies","meaning":"近期研究","examples":[{"en":"This pattern has been proved in many recent studies.","zh":"這個模式已在許多近期研究中被證明。"},{"en":"Recent studies are research studies carried out not long ago.","zh":"recent studies 指不久前進行的研究。"},{"en":"Recent studies use larger samples and better statistical methods.","zh":"近期研究使用較大樣本和較好的統計方法。"},{"en":"Referring to recent studies helps update older research claims.","zh":"提及近期研究有助更新較舊研究說法。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic discussion.","zh":"這個片語常見於學術討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take into consideration","meaning":"把……納入考慮","examples":[{"en":"Many studies did not take family size into consideration.","zh":"許多研究沒有把家庭規模納入考慮。"},{"en":"To take something into consideration means to include it when thinking or judging.","zh":"take something into consideration 指思考或判斷時包括某因素。"},{"en":"Researchers should take socioeconomic status into consideration.","zh":"研究者應把社會經濟地位納入考慮。"},{"en":"If a factor is ignored, the results may be misleading.","zh":"如果忽略某因素，結果可能會令人誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and useful in evaluation.","zh":"這個片語較正式，適合用於評估。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"family size","meaning":"家庭規模","examples":[{"en":"Family size can affect academic performance.","zh":"家庭規模可以影響學業表現。"},{"en":"Family size means the number of people or children in a family.","zh":"family size 指一個家庭的人數或孩子數目。"},{"en":"Larger family size may mean resources and attention are shared among more children.","zh":"較大家庭規模可能代表資源和關注要由更多孩子分享。"},{"en":"Family size can influence study time, support and household responsibilities.","zh":"家庭規模可以影響學習時間、支援和家務責任。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in social and educational research.","zh":"這個片語常見於社會和教育研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the more…, the likelier…","meaning":"越……，就越可能……","examples":[{"en":"The more siblings there are, the likelier the family is to have a low socioeconomic status.","zh":"兄弟姊妹越多，家庭就越可能有較低社會經濟地位。"},{"en":"The more…, the likelier… means as one thing increases, another becomes more likely.","zh":"the more…, the likelier… 指一件事增加時，另一件事變得更可能。"},{"en":"The more distractions there are, the likelier students are to lose focus.","zh":"干擾越多，學生就越可能失去專注。"},{"en":"This structure shows a relationship between two changing factors.","zh":"這個結構顯示兩個變化因素之間的關係。"},{"en":"It is useful in academic explanation.","zh":"它適合用於學術解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"low socioeconomic status","meaning":"較低社會經濟地位","examples":[{"en":"Larger families are more likely to have a low socioeconomic status.","zh":"較大家庭更可能有較低社會經濟地位。"},{"en":"Low socioeconomic status means having relatively low income, education or social resources.","zh":"low socioeconomic status 指收入、教育或社會資源相對較低。"},{"en":"Children from low socioeconomic status families may have fewer educational opportunities.","zh":"來自較低社會經濟地位家庭的孩子，可能有較少教育機會。"},{"en":"Socioeconomic status can affect health, housing and academic outcomes.","zh":"社會經濟地位可以影響健康、住屋和學業結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in social science research.","zh":"這個片語常見於社會科學研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"account for","meaning":"解釋……的原因","examples":[{"en":"Socioeconomic status can account for differences in academic performance.","zh":"社會經濟地位可以解釋學業表現差異的原因。"},{"en":"To account for something means to explain the reason for it.","zh":"account for something 指解釋某事的原因。"},{"en":"Family income may account for some differences in exam results.","zh":"家庭收入可能解釋部分考試成績差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying possible causes.","zh":"這個片語適合用於識別可能原因。"},{"en":"It is common in research analysis.","zh":"它常見於研究分析。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"differences between siblings","meaning":"兄弟姊妹之間的差異","examples":[{"en":"Family background can account for differences between siblings.","zh":"家庭背景可以解釋兄弟姊妹之間的差異。"},{"en":"Differences between siblings are ways in which brothers and sisters are not the same.","zh":"differences between siblings 指兄弟姊妹彼此不同的地方。"},{"en":"Differences between siblings may appear in confidence, grades or behaviour.","zh":"兄弟姊妹之間的差異可能出現在自信、成績或行為上。"},{"en":"These differences may be caused by birth order, personality or environment.","zh":"這些差異可能由出生順序、性格或環境造成。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in family research.","zh":"這個片語常見於家庭研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"academic performance","meaning":"學業表現","examples":[{"en":"Socioeconomic status may affect academic performance.","zh":"社會經濟地位可能影響學業表現。"},{"en":"Academic performance means how well someone does in school or university work.","zh":"academic performance 指某人在學校或大學學業上的表現。"},{"en":"Academic performance can be measured by grades, tests and coursework.","zh":"學業表現可以透過分數、測驗和課業量度。"},{"en":"Family support and school resources can influence academic performance.","zh":"家庭支援和學校資源會影響學業表現。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in education research.","zh":"這個片語常見於教育研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be given more opportunities","meaning":"獲得更多機會","examples":[{"en":"The oldest boy might be given more opportunities than his younger sisters.","zh":"家中老大男孩可能比年幼妹妹獲得更多機會。"},{"en":"To be given more opportunities means to receive more chances to learn, develop or succeed.","zh":"be given more opportunities 指得到更多學習、發展或成功的機會。"},{"en":"In some families, older children are given more opportunities for education.","zh":"在有些家庭中，年長孩子獲得更多教育機會。"},{"en":"Unequal opportunities can affect confidence and achievement.","zh":"不平等機會會影響自信和成就。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing fairness and social factors.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論公平和社會因素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"marginally higher","meaning":"略高的","examples":[{"en":"Oldest children may have marginally higher academic performance.","zh":"家中老大的學業表現可能略高。"},{"en":"Marginally higher means slightly higher by a small amount.","zh":"marginally higher 指稍微高一點。"},{"en":"The oldest siblings scored marginally higher in the test.","zh":"年長兄姊在測驗中得分略高。"},{"en":"A marginal difference may be real but not very large.","zh":"輕微差異可能是真實的，但幅度不大。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in statistics and comparison.","zh":"這個片語常見於統計和比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"benefit intellectually from","meaning":"在智力上受惠於……","examples":[{"en":"Oldest children may benefit intellectually from extra attention.","zh":"家中老大可能在智力上受惠於額外關注。"},{"en":"To benefit intellectually from something means to gain mental or learning advantages from it.","zh":"benefit intellectually from something 指從某事中獲得智力或學習上的好處。"},{"en":"Children can benefit intellectually from reading with adults.","zh":"兒童可以在智力上受惠於與成年人一起閱讀。"},{"en":"Extra discussion at home may support language and reasoning skills.","zh":"家中額外討論可能支援語言和推理能力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in education and development topics.","zh":"這個片語適合用於教育和發展題目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"extra attention","meaning":"額外關注","examples":[{"en":"Oldest children may receive extra attention at a young age.","zh":"家中老大在年幼時可能得到額外關注。"},{"en":"Extra attention means additional time, care or focus from other people.","zh":"extra attention 指來自他人的額外時間、照顧或專注。"},{"en":"First-born children may receive extra attention before siblings are born.","zh":"第一個孩子在弟妹出生前可能得到額外關注。"},{"en":"Extra attention can support early learning and confidence.","zh":"額外關注可以支援早期學習和自信。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in family and education discussion.","zh":"這個片語常見於家庭和教育討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at a young age","meaning":"在年幼時","examples":[{"en":"Oldest children may benefit from extra attention at a young age.","zh":"家中老大可能在年幼時受惠於額外關注。"},{"en":"At a young age means when someone is still a child or very young.","zh":"at a young age 指某人仍是孩子或很年幼時。"},{"en":"Children who read at a young age may develop strong vocabulary.","zh":"在年幼時閱讀的孩子可能發展出強大詞彙。"},{"en":"Early experiences can shape later habits and abilities.","zh":"早期經驗可以塑造日後習慣和能力。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in development and education topics.","zh":"這個片語常見於發展和教育題目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"benefit from being","meaning":"從身為……中受益","examples":[{"en":"Oldest children may benefit from being teachers for their younger siblings.","zh":"家中老大可能從擔任年幼弟妹的老師中受益。"},{"en":"To benefit from being something means to gain advantages from having that role.","zh":"benefit from being something 指從擁有某角色中得到好處。"},{"en":"Older siblings may benefit from being helpers at home.","zh":"年長兄姊可能從在家中擔任幫手中受益。"},{"en":"Teaching others can strengthen understanding and confidence.","zh":"教導他人可以增強理解和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a role with a positive effect.","zh":"這個片語把角色與正面效果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"verbalise processes","meaning":"把過程用說話表達出來","examples":[{"en":"Oldest children learn by verbalising processes to younger siblings.","zh":"家中老大透過向年幼弟妹把過程用說話表達出來而學習。"},{"en":"To verbalise processes means to explain steps or thinking aloud in words.","zh":"verbalise processes 指用語言大聲解釋步驟或思考過程。"},{"en":"A student can learn maths better by verbalising the process to a classmate.","zh":"學生可以透過向同學說明步驟，更好地學習數學。"},{"en":"Explaining processes aloud can make thinking clearer.","zh":"大聲解釋過程可以令思考更清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in learning and cognitive development.","zh":"這個片語常見於學習和認知發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"give someone status and confidence","meaning":"給予某人地位和信心","examples":[{"en":"Teaching younger siblings gives oldest children status and confidence.","zh":"教導年幼弟妹給予家中老大地位和信心。"},{"en":"To give someone status and confidence means to make them feel important and capable.","zh":"give someone status and confidence 指令某人感到重要和有能力。"},{"en":"Helping younger pupils can give older students status and confidence.","zh":"幫助年幼學生可以給年長學生地位和信心。"},{"en":"Feeling useful may encourage children to take responsibility.","zh":"感到自己有用可能鼓勵孩子承擔責任。"},{"en":"This phrase links social role with self-esteem.","zh":"這個片語把社會角色與自尊連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"contribute to","meaning":"促成；有助於","examples":[{"en":"Status and confidence contribute to better academic performance.","zh":"地位和信心有助於更好的學業表現。"},{"en":"To contribute to something means to help cause or improve it.","zh":"contribute to something 指幫助造成或改善某事。"},{"en":"Good sleep can contribute to better concentration.","zh":"良好睡眠有助於更好的專注力。"},{"en":"Many small factors may contribute to academic success.","zh":"許多小因素可能有助於學業成功。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing causes.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in a small way","meaning":"在小程度上","examples":[{"en":"Status and confidence may contribute in a small way to better performance.","zh":"地位和信心可能在小程度上有助於更好的表現。"},{"en":"In a small way means to a limited but still possible degree.","zh":"in a small way 指程度有限但仍可能有作用。"},{"en":"Family support may help academic performance in a small way.","zh":"家庭支援可能在小程度上幫助學業表現。"},{"en":"This phrase prevents a claim from sounding too strong.","zh":"這個片語避免說法聽起來太強。"},{"en":"It is useful when making cautious arguments.","zh":"它適合用於提出謹慎論點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sibling rivalry","meaning":"兄弟姊妹之間的競爭","examples":[{"en":"Ed asks whether sibling rivalry has been useful for Ruth.","zh":"Ed 問兄弟姊妹之間的競爭是否對 Ruth 有用。"},{"en":"Sibling rivalry means competition, jealousy or conflict between brothers and sisters.","zh":"sibling rivalry 指兄弟姊妹之間的競爭、嫉妒或衝突。"},{"en":"Sibling rivalry can appear when children compete for toys or attention.","zh":"當孩子爭玩具或關注時，兄弟姊妹之間的競爭可能出現。"},{"en":"It can be stressful, but it may also teach negotiation and resilience.","zh":"它可能帶來壓力，但也可能教會協商和抗逆力。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in family psychology.","zh":"這個片語常見於家庭心理學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a useful thing","meaning":"有用的事","examples":[{"en":"Ruth thinks sibling rivalry has been a useful thing for her.","zh":"Ruth 認為兄弟姊妹之間的競爭對她來說是一件有用的事。"},{"en":"A useful thing means something that has practical value or brings benefit.","zh":"useful thing 指有實際價值或帶來好處的事。"},{"en":"Learning to argue calmly can be a useful thing in adult life.","zh":"學會冷靜爭論在成人生活中可以是一件有用的事。"},{"en":"A difficult childhood experience may still become useful later.","zh":"困難的童年經歷日後仍可能變得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple and conversational.","zh":"這個片語簡單而口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"incredibly annoying","meaning":"極其煩人","examples":[{"en":"Ruth’s younger brother was incredibly annoying.","zh":"Ruth 的弟弟極其煩人。"},{"en":"Incredibly annoying means extremely irritating or frustrating.","zh":"incredibly annoying 指非常令人惱火或沮喪。"},{"en":"Her brother was incredibly annoying when he kept taking her things.","zh":"她弟弟不停拿她的東西時，極其煩人。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises irritation.","zh":"這個片語強烈強調煩躁感。"},{"en":"It is informal and expressive.","zh":"它較口語而有表現力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fight a lot","meaning":"經常爭吵","examples":[{"en":"Ruth and her younger brother fought a lot.","zh":"Ruth 和她的弟弟經常爭吵。"},{"en":"To fight a lot means to argue or quarrel frequently.","zh":"fight a lot 指經常爭論或吵架。"},{"en":"The siblings fought a lot when they were children.","zh":"那對兄妹小時候經常爭吵。"},{"en":"Frequent fighting can be tiring, but it may also teach children how to handle conflict.","zh":"經常爭吵可以令人疲累，但也可能教孩子處理衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in family stories.","zh":"這個片語常見於家庭故事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make someone a stronger person","meaning":"令某人變得更堅強","examples":[{"en":"Sibling rivalry made Ruth a stronger person.","zh":"兄弟姊妹之間的競爭令 Ruth 變得更堅強。"},{"en":"To make someone a stronger person means to help them become more resilient or confident.","zh":"make someone a stronger person 指幫助某人變得更有抗逆力或更自信。"},{"en":"Difficult experiences can make someone a stronger person.","zh":"困難經歷可以令某人變得更堅強。"},{"en":"Having to defend herself helped Ruth become tougher.","zh":"需要為自己辯護幫助 Ruth 變得更強韌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal growth through challenge.","zh":"這個片語描述透過挑戰而成長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"defend myself","meaning":"保護自己；為自己辯護","examples":[{"en":"Ruth says she knows how to defend herself.","zh":"Ruth 說她知道如何保護自己。"},{"en":"To defend myself means to protect myself or argue for myself.","zh":"defend myself 指保護自己或為自己辯護。"},{"en":"Growing up with siblings taught her to defend herself.","zh":"與兄弟姊妹一起長大教會她保護自己。"},{"en":"Defending yourself can mean speaking up when you are treated unfairly.","zh":"為自己辯護可以指在受到不公平對待時發聲。"},{"en":"This phrase can be physical, verbal or emotional.","zh":"這個片語可以指身體上、言語上或情感上的保護。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"terrible arguments","meaning":"激烈爭吵","examples":[{"en":"Ruth and her brother had some terrible arguments.","zh":"Ruth 和她的弟弟有過一些激烈爭吵。"},{"en":"Terrible arguments are very serious, angry or unpleasant disagreements.","zh":"terrible arguments 指非常嚴重、憤怒或不愉快的分歧。"},{"en":"The siblings had terrible arguments over shared toys.","zh":"那對兄妹曾因共用玩具而激烈爭吵。"},{"en":"Even close siblings can have terrible arguments when emotions run high.","zh":"即使感情好的兄弟姊妹，在情緒高漲時也可能有激烈爭吵。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises conflict intensity.","zh":"這個片語強調衝突強度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"would have died rather than","meaning":"寧死也不願……","examples":[{"en":"Ruth says she would have died rather than apologise to her brother.","zh":"Ruth 說她寧死也不願向弟弟道歉。"},{"en":"Would have died rather than means would absolutely refuse to do something.","zh":"would have died rather than 指絕對不願意做某事。"},{"en":"As a child, he would have died rather than admit he was wrong.","zh":"他小時候寧死也不願承認自己錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is exaggerated and humorous.","zh":"這個片語帶誇張和幽默語氣。"},{"en":"It shows very strong unwillingness.","zh":"它顯示非常強烈的不願意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"apologise to","meaning":"向……道歉","examples":[{"en":"Ruth would not apologise to her younger brother after an argument.","zh":"Ruth 爭吵後不願向弟弟道歉。"},{"en":"To apologise to someone means to say sorry to that person.","zh":"apologise to someone 指向某人說對不起。"},{"en":"Children often find it hard to apologise to their siblings.","zh":"孩子常覺得很難向兄弟姊妹道歉。"},{"en":"Apologising can repair relationships after conflict.","zh":"道歉可以在衝突後修補關係。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday social situations.","zh":"這個片語常見於日常社交情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"put up with each other","meaning":"忍受彼此","examples":[{"en":"Ruth and her brother had to put up with each other.","zh":"Ruth 和她的弟弟不得不忍受彼此。"},{"en":"To put up with each other means to tolerate each other even when there are difficulties.","zh":"put up with each other 指即使有困難也要互相忍受。"},{"en":"Siblings often have to put up with each other in the same house.","zh":"兄弟姊妹住在同一屋簷下，常不得不忍受彼此。"},{"en":"Tolerance can develop when people cannot simply avoid one another.","zh":"當人們不能簡單避開彼此，容忍力可能會發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and practical.","zh":"這個片語較口語而實用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"co-exist amicably","meaning":"友好共處","examples":[{"en":"Most of the time, Ruth and her brother co-existed amicably enough.","zh":"大多數時間，Ruth 和她的弟弟都算能友好共處。"},{"en":"To co-exist amicably means to live or stay together in a reasonably friendly way.","zh":"co-exist amicably 指以相當友善的方式一起生活或相處。"},{"en":"The siblings argued sometimes but co-existed amicably most days.","zh":"那對兄妹有時爭吵，但大多數日子都能友好共處。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests peaceful tolerance rather than perfect closeness.","zh":"這個片語暗示和平容忍，而不是完美親密。"},{"en":"It is slightly formal and humorous in family contexts.","zh":"它略正式，在家庭語境中帶點幽默。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"pretty similar","meaning":"頗相似","examples":[{"en":"Ed says his situation was pretty similar.","zh":"Ed 說他的情況頗相似。"},{"en":"Pretty similar means quite alike or almost the same in some ways.","zh":"pretty similar 指相當相似，或在某些方面差不多。"},{"en":"My experience as the youngest child was pretty similar to Ed’s.","zh":"我作為最年幼孩子的經驗與 Ed 頗相似。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and useful when comparing experiences.","zh":"這個片語較口語，適合用於比較經驗。"},{"en":"It suggests similarity without saying two things are identical.","zh":"它暗示相似，但不表示兩者完全相同。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make someone any less selfish","meaning":"令某人變得較不自私","examples":[{"en":"Having two older brothers did not make Ed any less selfish.","zh":"有兩個哥哥並沒有令 Ed 變得較不自私。"},{"en":"To make someone any less selfish means to reduce that person’s selfishness even a little.","zh":"make someone any less selfish 指令某人的自私程度哪怕稍為減少。"},{"en":"Sharing a room did not make him any less selfish with his things.","zh":"共用房間並沒有令他對自己的東西變得較不自私。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in negative sentences.","zh":"這個片語常用於否定句。"},{"en":"It suggests that the expected change did not happen.","zh":"它暗示預期中的改變沒有發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be prepared to","meaning":"願意；準備好","examples":[{"en":"Ed was never prepared to let his brothers use his things.","zh":"Ed 從不願意讓哥哥們使用他的東西。"},{"en":"To be prepared to do something means to be willing or ready to do it.","zh":"be prepared to do something 指願意或準備好做某事。"},{"en":"He was not prepared to share his toys with his brothers.","zh":"他不願意與哥哥們分享玩具。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes willingness rather than physical preparation.","zh":"這個片語常描述意願，而不是身體上的準備。"},{"en":"It is common in everyday and formal English.","zh":"它常見於日常和正式英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"use any of my stuff","meaning":"使用我的任何東西","examples":[{"en":"Ed did not let his brothers use any of his stuff.","zh":"Ed 不讓哥哥們使用他的任何東西。"},{"en":"Use any of my stuff means use any of my belongings or personal things.","zh":"use any of my stuff 指使用我的任何物品或私人東西。"},{"en":"As a child, I hated it when my siblings used any of my stuff.","zh":"我小時候很討厭兄弟姊妹使用我的任何東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and common in spoken English.","zh":"這個片語較口語，常見於英語口語。"},{"en":"It suggests personal ownership and boundaries.","zh":"它暗示個人物品所有權和界線。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"perfectly normal","meaning":"完全正常","examples":[{"en":"Ruth says Ed’s behaviour is perfectly normal.","zh":"Ruth 說 Ed 的行為完全正常。"},{"en":"Perfectly normal means completely ordinary or understandable.","zh":"perfectly normal 指完全普通或可以理解。"},{"en":"It is perfectly normal for siblings to argue about personal belongings.","zh":"兄弟姊妹為個人物品爭吵是完全正常的。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures someone that their behaviour is not strange.","zh":"這個片語安撫某人，表示其行為並不奇怪。"},{"en":"It is common in friendly conversation.","zh":"它常見於友善對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 20/task-4":[{"front":"eucalyptus tree","meaning":"桉樹","examples":[{"en":"Today I’m going to talk about the eucalyptus tree.","zh":"今天我要談談桉樹。"},{"en":"A eucalyptus tree is a tree, often found in Australia, with aromatic leaves and many ecological uses.","zh":"eucalyptus tree 是一種常見於澳洲、葉子有香氣並有多種生態用途的樹。"},{"en":"A biology student may study the eucalyptus tree because it supports many animals.","zh":"生物學生可能研究桉樹，因為它支援許多動物。"},{"en":"The eucalyptus tree is important because its leaves, flowers, and shelter help wildlife survive.","zh":"桉樹很重要，因為它的葉、花和棲身之所幫助野生動物生存。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific kind of tree.","zh":"這個短語指一種特定樹木。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"common tree","meaning":"常見樹木","examples":[{"en":"The eucalyptus is a very common tree in Australia.","zh":"桉樹是澳洲非常常見的樹木。"},{"en":"A common tree is a tree that is found in many places and is not rare.","zh":"common tree 是在許多地方都可見、並不罕見的樹木。"},{"en":"The banyan is a common tree in many warm cities.","zh":"榕樹是許多溫暖城市中的常見樹木。"},{"en":"Common trees can still be ecologically important because many animals depend on them.","zh":"常見樹木仍可以在生態上很重要，因為許多動物依賴它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how often a tree is seen in a place.","zh":"這個短語描述某種樹在某地有多常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"gum tree","meaning":"膠樹；桉樹","examples":[{"en":"In Australia, the eucalyptus is also sometimes called the gum tree.","zh":"在澳洲，桉樹有時也被稱為膠樹。"},{"en":"A gum tree is another name often used for a eucalyptus tree in Australia.","zh":"gum tree 是澳洲常用來稱呼桉樹的另一個名稱。"},{"en":"Children in Australia may learn that koalas live in gum trees.","zh":"澳洲孩子可能會學到樹熊生活在膠樹上。"},{"en":"Different common names can refer to the same plant, so context matters.","zh":"不同俗名可以指同一種植物，所以語境很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common everyday name rather than a scientific name.","zh":"這個短語是日常名稱，而不是科學名稱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for lots of reasons","meaning":"基於很多原因","examples":[{"en":"The eucalyptus tree is important for lots of reasons.","zh":"桉樹基於很多原因而重要。"},{"en":"For lots of reasons means because there are many different explanations or benefits.","zh":"for lots of reasons 的意思是因為有許多不同解釋或好處。"},{"en":"Reading is useful for lots of reasons, including vocabulary, knowledge, and concentration.","zh":"閱讀基於很多原因而有用，包括詞彙、知識和專注力。"},{"en":"When something matters for many reasons, it is usually worth studying carefully.","zh":"當某事基於很多原因而重要，通常值得仔細研究。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces several possible points.","zh":"這個短語引出多個可能要點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"gives shelter to","meaning":"為……提供棲身之所","examples":[{"en":"The eucalyptus tree gives shelter to creatures like birds and bats.","zh":"桉樹為鳥類和蝙蝠等生物提供棲身之所。"},{"en":"To give shelter to animals means to provide a safe place for them to live, rest, or hide.","zh":"give shelter to animals 的意思是為動物提供安全地方生活、休息或躲藏。"},{"en":"A large tree can give shelter to insects, birds, and small mammals.","zh":"大樹可以為昆蟲、鳥類和小型哺乳動物提供棲身之所。"},{"en":"Shelter is important because animals need protection from weather and predators.","zh":"棲身之所很重要，因為動物需要保護，免受天氣和捕食者影響。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a place or object with protection.","zh":"這個短語把地方或物件與保護連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"creatures like","meaning":"像……這類生物","examples":[{"en":"The tree gives shelter to creatures like birds and bats.","zh":"這棵樹為像鳥類和蝙蝠這類生物提供棲身之所。"},{"en":"Creatures like something means animals or living things such as the examples mentioned.","zh":"creatures like something 的意思是像所提例子那樣的動物或生物。"},{"en":"A pond may support creatures like frogs, dragonflies, and small fish.","zh":"池塘可能支援像青蛙、蜻蜓和小魚這類生物。"},{"en":"Giving examples of creatures helps readers imagine the wildlife being discussed.","zh":"舉出生物例子能幫助讀者想像正在討論的野生動物。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples from a broader group of living things.","zh":"這個短語從較廣泛生物群體中引出例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"depend on it for food","meaning":"依靠它作為食物來源","examples":[{"en":"Many species depend on the eucalyptus for food.","zh":"許多物種依靠桉樹作為食物來源。"},{"en":"To depend on it for food means to need it as a regular food source.","zh":"depend on it for food 的意思是需要它作為穩定食物來源。"},{"en":"Bees may depend on flowers for food because they collect nectar.","zh":"蜜蜂可能依靠花朵作為食物來源，因為牠們採集花蜜。"},{"en":"If a food source disappears, the species that depend on it may decline.","zh":"如果食物來源消失，依靠它的物種可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a survival relationship.","zh":"這個短語顯示一種生存關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"particularly","meaning":"尤其是","examples":[{"en":"Some species depend on the eucalyptus, particularly the nectar from its flowers.","zh":"有些物種依靠桉樹，尤其是其花朵中的花蜜。"},{"en":"Particularly means especially, or more than other things.","zh":"particularly 的意思是尤其是，或比其他事物更特別。"},{"en":"Many students enjoy science, particularly experiments they can do themselves.","zh":"許多學生喜歡科學，尤其是可以親自做的實驗。"},{"en":"This word highlights the most important example in a group.","zh":"這個詞突出一組例子中最重要的一個。"},{"en":"It is useful when narrowing attention to one detail.","zh":"它適合用於把注意力收窄到某個細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"nectar from its flowers","meaning":"花朵中的花蜜","examples":[{"en":"Birds and bats feed on the nectar from eucalyptus flowers.","zh":"鳥類和蝙蝠以桉樹花朵中的花蜜為食。"},{"en":"Nectar from its flowers is the sweet liquid produced by flowers that some animals drink.","zh":"nectar from its flowers 是花朵產生、供某些動物飲用的甜液。"},{"en":"Bees collect nectar from flowers and use it to make honey.","zh":"蜜蜂採集花朵中的花蜜，並用它製造蜂蜜。"},{"en":"Nectar can attract animals that help pollinate plants.","zh":"花蜜可以吸引幫助植物授粉的動物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a food source produced by flowers.","zh":"這個短語描述由花朵產生的食物來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"support biodiversity","meaning":"支持生物多樣性","examples":[{"en":"The eucalyptus tree supports biodiversity.","zh":"桉樹支持生物多樣性。"},{"en":"To support biodiversity means to help many different living things survive in an ecosystem.","zh":"support biodiversity 的意思是幫助許多不同生物在生態系統中生存。"},{"en":"A wetland supports biodiversity by providing homes for birds, fish, insects, and plants.","zh":"濕地透過為鳥類、魚類、昆蟲和植物提供棲息地來支持生物多樣性。"},{"en":"Trees support biodiversity when they provide food, shelter, and nesting places.","zh":"當樹木提供食物、棲身之所和築巢地點，它們就支持生物多樣性。"},{"en":"This phrase connects one species or habitat with wider ecological health.","zh":"這個短語把一個物種或棲息地與更廣泛的生態健康連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"useful to us humans","meaning":"對我們人類也有用","examples":[{"en":"The eucalyptus tree is useful to us humans too.","zh":"桉樹對我們人類也有用。"},{"en":"Useful to us humans means helpful or beneficial to people.","zh":"useful to us humans 的意思是對人有幫助或有益。"},{"en":"Trees are useful to us humans because they give shade, clean air, and materials.","zh":"樹木對我們人類有用，因為它們提供樹蔭、潔淨空氣和材料。"},{"en":"A plant may be useful to humans while also being important to wildlife.","zh":"一種植物可以對人類有用，同時也對野生動物重要。"},{"en":"This phrase links nature with human needs.","zh":"這個短語把自然與人類需要連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"kill germs","meaning":"殺死細菌","examples":[{"en":"We can kill germs with a disinfectant made from eucalyptus oil.","zh":"我們可以用由桉樹油製成的消毒劑殺死細菌。"},{"en":"To kill germs means to destroy tiny organisms that may cause disease.","zh":"kill germs 的意思是消滅可能引起疾病的微小生物。"},{"en":"Washing hands properly can help kill germs and reduce infection.","zh":"正確洗手可以幫助殺死細菌並減少感染。"},{"en":"Disinfectants kill germs on surfaces such as tables, door handles, and floors.","zh":"消毒劑會殺死桌面、門柄和地板等表面的細菌。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in health and cleaning contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於健康和清潔語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"disinfectant","meaning":"消毒劑","examples":[{"en":"A disinfectant can be made from oil extracted from eucalyptus leaves.","zh":"消毒劑可以由從桉樹葉提取的油製成。"},{"en":"A disinfectant is a substance used to kill germs on surfaces.","zh":"disinfectant 是用來殺死表面細菌的物質。"},{"en":"Hospitals use disinfectant to clean equipment and reduce the spread of disease.","zh":"醫院使用消毒劑清潔設備並減少疾病傳播。"},{"en":"A good disinfectant helps keep shared spaces safer and cleaner.","zh":"好的消毒劑有助保持共用空間更安全和清潔。"},{"en":"This word is common in hygiene and cleaning discussions.","zh":"這個詞常見於衛生和清潔討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"made from","meaning":"由……製成","examples":[{"en":"The disinfectant is made from oil extracted from eucalyptus leaves.","zh":"這種消毒劑由從桉樹葉提取的油製成。"},{"en":"Made from means produced using a particular material or ingredient.","zh":"made from 的意思是使用某種材料或成分製造。"},{"en":"Paper is made from wood fibres.","zh":"紙由木纖維製成。"},{"en":"Knowing what a product is made from helps people understand its source and possible uses.","zh":"知道產品由甚麼製成，有助人們理解其來源和可能用途。"},{"en":"This phrase describes material origin.","zh":"這個短語描述材料來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"oil extracted from","meaning":"從……提取的油","examples":[{"en":"The disinfectant is made from oil extracted from eucalyptus leaves.","zh":"這種消毒劑由從桉樹葉提取的油製成。"},{"en":"Oil extracted from something is oil taken out of that material.","zh":"oil extracted from something 是從某種材料中取出的油。"},{"en":"Olive oil is extracted from olives.","zh":"橄欖油是從橄欖中提取的油。"},{"en":"Extracted oils can be used in medicine, cleaning products, food, or cosmetics.","zh":"提取出的油可以用於醫藥、清潔產品、食物或化妝品。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on obtaining oil from a natural source.","zh":"這個短語集中於從天然來源取得油。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"eucalyptus leaves","meaning":"桉樹葉","examples":[{"en":"Oil can be extracted from eucalyptus leaves.","zh":"油可以從桉樹葉中提取。"},{"en":"Eucalyptus leaves are the leaves of the eucalyptus tree, often known for their strong smell.","zh":"eucalyptus leaves 是桉樹的葉子，通常以強烈氣味聞名。"},{"en":"Koalas eat eucalyptus leaves as their main food.","zh":"樹熊以桉樹葉作為主要食物。"},{"en":"Leaves can contain oils and chemicals useful to both plants and humans.","zh":"葉子可以含有對植物和人類都有用的油和化學物質。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific part of the eucalyptus tree.","zh":"這個短語指桉樹的一個特定部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"grow all over","meaning":"遍布……生長","examples":[{"en":"The eucalyptus grows all over Australia.","zh":"桉樹遍布澳洲生長。"},{"en":"To grow all over a place means to grow in many parts of that area.","zh":"grow all over a place 的意思是在某地許多部分生長。"},{"en":"Wildflowers grow all over the hillside in spring.","zh":"春天時，野花遍布山坡生長。"},{"en":"If a plant grows all over a country, it may be well adapted to different local conditions.","zh":"如果一種植物遍布一個國家生長，它可能很能適應不同本地環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wide distribution.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛分布。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"live for up to","meaning":"可活長達","examples":[{"en":"Eucalyptus trees can live for up to four hundred years.","zh":"桉樹可活長達四百年。"},{"en":"To live for up to a period means to be able to survive for as long as that amount of time.","zh":"live for up to 某段時間的意思是最多能存活到該時間長度。"},{"en":"Some turtles can live for up to a hundred years.","zh":"有些龜可活長達一百年。"},{"en":"Long-lived trees can support ecosystems across many human generations.","zh":"長壽樹木可以跨越多個人類世代支援生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a maximum lifespan.","zh":"這個短語提供最長壽命。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"it’s alarming that","meaning":"令人憂慮的是","examples":[{"en":"It is alarming that numbers of eucalyptus trees are falling.","zh":"令人憂慮的是，桉樹數量正在下降。"},{"en":"It’s alarming that means something is worrying or frightening because it may be serious.","zh":"it’s alarming that 的意思是某事令人擔心或害怕，因為它可能很嚴重。"},{"en":"It is alarming that more students are reporting high stress before exams.","zh":"令人憂慮的是，越來越多學生表示考試前壓力很大。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when a situation deserves urgent attention.","zh":"當一個情況值得緊急關注，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a serious concern.","zh":"這個短語引出嚴重憂慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"all across the country","meaning":"全國各地","examples":[{"en":"All across the country, numbers of eucalyptus trees are falling.","zh":"全國各地的桉樹數量正在下降。"},{"en":"All across the country means in many places throughout the whole country.","zh":"all across the country 的意思是在整個國家許多地方。"},{"en":"Schools all across the country are trying to improve students’ reading habits.","zh":"全國各地的學校都在嘗試改善學生閱讀習慣。"},{"en":"If a problem appears across a whole country, it may need national action.","zh":"如果問題出現在全國各地，可能需要全國性行動。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises wide geographical spread.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛地理分布。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"numbers of","meaning":"……的數量","examples":[{"en":"Numbers of eucalyptus trees are falling across Australia.","zh":"澳洲各地桉樹的數量正在下降。"},{"en":"Numbers of something means the amount or population of that thing.","zh":"numbers of something 的意思是某物的數量或族群數目。"},{"en":"Numbers of butterflies may fall if their habitats disappear.","zh":"如果棲息地消失，蝴蝶的數量可能下降。"},{"en":"Tracking numbers helps scientists see whether a species is increasing or declining.","zh":"追蹤數量有助科學家了解物種正在增加還是減少。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in environmental reports.","zh":"這個短語適合用於環境報告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"are falling","meaning":"正在下降","examples":[{"en":"The numbers of eucalyptus trees are falling.","zh":"桉樹的數量正在下降。"},{"en":"Are falling means are decreasing or becoming lower.","zh":"are falling 的意思是正在減少或變低。"},{"en":"The number of library visitors is falling because opening hours have been reduced.","zh":"由於開放時間減少，圖書館訪客人數正在下降。"},{"en":"Falling numbers can show that a species or service is under pressure.","zh":"數量下降可以顯示物種或服務正承受壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a downward trend.","zh":"這個短語描述向下趨勢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"die off prematurely","meaning":"過早死亡","examples":[{"en":"The trees are dying off prematurely.","zh":"這些樹正在過早死亡。"},{"en":"To die off prematurely means to die earlier than expected or before reaching a normal lifespan.","zh":"die off prematurely 的意思是比預期更早死亡，或未達正常壽命就死亡。"},{"en":"Young plants may die off prematurely if the soil is polluted.","zh":"如果土壤受污染，幼苗可能過早死亡。"},{"en":"When trees die prematurely, the animals depending on them may also suffer.","zh":"當樹木過早死亡，依賴它們的動物也可能受害。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an unnatural or worrying death pattern.","zh":"這個短語暗示不自然或令人憂慮的死亡模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"one possible reason","meaning":"一個可能原因","examples":[{"en":"One possible reason for the decline is disease.","zh":"數量下降的一個可能原因是疾病。"},{"en":"One possible reason means one explanation that may be true, though others may also exist.","zh":"one possible reason 的意思是一個可能正確的解釋，但也可能有其他原因。"},{"en":"One possible reason for low exam scores is lack of sleep.","zh":"考試成績低的一個可能原因是睡眠不足。"},{"en":"Using “possible” shows the speaker is being careful rather than claiming certainty.","zh":"使用 possible 顯示講者態度謹慎，而不是聲稱絕對肯定。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a cautious explanation.","zh":"這個短語引出審慎解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as far back as","meaning":"早在……","examples":[{"en":"As far back as the 1970s, the trees started getting a disease.","zh":"早在1970年代，這些樹就開始染病。"},{"en":"As far back as means as early as a particular time in the past.","zh":"as far back as 的意思是早在過去某個時間。"},{"en":"As far back as the 1950s, scientists were already studying air pollution.","zh":"早在1950年代，科學家已經在研究空氣污染。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that something began a long time ago.","zh":"這個短語強調某事很久以前已經開始。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving historical background.","zh":"它適合用於提供歷史背景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"start getting a disease","meaning":"開始染病","examples":[{"en":"The trees started getting a disease called Mundulla Yellows.","zh":"這些樹開始染上一種名為 Mundulla Yellows 的病。"},{"en":"To start getting a disease means to begin showing signs of illness or infection.","zh":"start getting a disease 的意思是開始出現疾病或感染跡象。"},{"en":"Plants may start getting a disease if insects spread harmful organisms.","zh":"如果昆蟲傳播有害生物，植物可能開始染病。"},{"en":"Early signs of disease are important because treatment may still be possible.","zh":"早期病徵很重要，因為治療可能仍然可行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of illness.","zh":"這個短語描述疾病開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Mundulla Yellows","meaning":"Mundulla Yellows病","examples":[{"en":"Mundulla Yellows affected eucalyptus trees from the 1970s.","zh":"Mundulla Yellows 病自1970年代起影響桉樹。"},{"en":"Mundulla Yellows is the name of a disease that caused eucalyptus leaves to turn yellow.","zh":"Mundulla Yellows 是一種令桉樹葉變黃的疾病名稱。"},{"en":"Scientists studied Mundulla Yellows to understand why affected trees were weakening.","zh":"科學家研究 Mundulla Yellows，以了解受影響樹木為何變弱。"},{"en":"Naming a disease helps researchers discuss the same problem clearly.","zh":"為疾病命名有助研究人員清楚討論同一問題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific tree disease.","zh":"這個短語指一種特定樹病。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"gradually turn yellow","meaning":"逐漸變黃","examples":[{"en":"The trees’ leaves would gradually turn yellow.","zh":"這些樹的葉子會逐漸變黃。"},{"en":"To gradually turn yellow means to become yellow slowly over time.","zh":"gradually turn yellow 的意思是隨時間慢慢變成黃色。"},{"en":"Plant leaves may gradually turn yellow if they lack nutrients.","zh":"如果植物缺乏養分，葉子可能逐漸變黃。"},{"en":"Slow colour change can be a warning sign that a plant is unhealthy.","zh":"緩慢顏色變化可以是植物不健康的警號。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visible change happening over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間出現的可見變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"It wasn’t until…that","meaning":"直到……才……","examples":[{"en":"It wasn’t until 2004 that scientists found the cause of the problem.","zh":"直到2004年，科學家才找到問題成因。"},{"en":"It wasn’t until…that means something happened only after a particular time.","zh":"It wasn’t until…that 的意思是某事直到某個時間之後才發生。"},{"en":"It wasn’t until university that she became interested in biology.","zh":"直到大學時，她才對生物學產生興趣。"},{"en":"This structure emphasises delay or late discovery.","zh":"這個結構強調延遲或較晚發現。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing that something took a long time to happen.","zh":"當要顯示某事花了很久才發生時，這個句式很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cause of the problem","meaning":"問題成因","examples":[{"en":"Scientists found the cause of the problem in 2004.","zh":"科學家在2004年找到問題成因。"},{"en":"The cause of the problem is the reason why the problem happened.","zh":"cause of the problem 是問題發生的原因。"},{"en":"The cause of the computer problem was a loose cable.","zh":"電腦問題成因是一條鬆脫的電線。"},{"en":"Finding the cause of a problem helps people choose the right solution.","zh":"找到問題成因有助人們選擇正確解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the source of difficulty.","zh":"這個短語集中於困難的來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"calcium hydroxide","meaning":"氫氧化鈣","examples":[{"en":"Calcium hydroxide is the proper chemical name for lime.","zh":"氫氧化鈣是石灰的正式化學名稱。"},{"en":"Calcium hydroxide is a chemical compound commonly known as lime in this context.","zh":"calcium hydroxide 是一種化合物，在這個語境中通常稱為石灰。"},{"en":"Chemistry students may learn the formula and uses of calcium hydroxide.","zh":"化學學生可能學習氫氧化鈣的化學式和用途。"},{"en":"Chemical names help scientists identify substances precisely.","zh":"化學名稱幫助科學家準確識別物質。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific chemical substance.","zh":"這個短語指一種特定化學物質。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"proper chemical name","meaning":"正式化學名稱","examples":[{"en":"Calcium hydroxide is lime’s proper chemical name.","zh":"氫氧化鈣是石灰的正式化學名稱。"},{"en":"A proper chemical name is the exact scientific name of a substance.","zh":"proper chemical name 是某物質的準確科學名稱。"},{"en":"Water’s proper chemical name is dihydrogen monoxide, though people rarely say that in daily life.","zh":"水的正式化學名稱是 dihydrogen monoxide，但人們日常很少這樣說。"},{"en":"Proper chemical names reduce confusion because common names can vary.","zh":"正式化學名稱可以減少混亂，因為俗名可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts scientific naming with everyday naming.","zh":"這個短語把科學命名與日常命名作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be used in","meaning":"被用於……","examples":[{"en":"Lime was being used in the construction of roads.","zh":"石灰當時被用於道路建設。"},{"en":"To be used in something means to be applied as part of a process, product, or activity.","zh":"be used in something 的意思是作為某個過程、產品或活動的一部分被使用。"},{"en":"Concrete is used in the construction of buildings and bridges.","zh":"混凝土被用於建築物和橋樑建設。"},{"en":"Knowing what materials are used in a project helps explain its effects.","zh":"知道項目中使用了甚麼材料，有助解釋其影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical use.","zh":"這個短語描述實際用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"construction of roads","meaning":"道路建設","examples":[{"en":"Lime was used in the construction of roads.","zh":"石灰被用於道路建設。"},{"en":"Construction of roads means the building or repair of roads.","zh":"construction of roads 的意思是道路興建或維修。"},{"en":"The construction of roads can improve transport but may affect nearby land and plants.","zh":"道路建設可以改善交通，但可能影響附近土地和植物。"},{"en":"Road construction uses materials such as stone, asphalt, concrete, and chemicals.","zh":"道路建設會使用石材、瀝青、混凝土和化學品等材料。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in engineering and planning.","zh":"這個短語常見於工程和規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be washed away into","meaning":"被沖入……","examples":[{"en":"The lime was being washed away into the ground.","zh":"石灰正被沖入地下。"},{"en":"To be washed away into something means to be carried there by water.","zh":"be washed away into something 的意思是被水帶到某處。"},{"en":"Fertiliser can be washed away into rivers after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，肥料可能被沖入河流。"},{"en":"Substances washed into soil can affect plant roots and water quality.","zh":"被沖入土壤的物質可以影響植物根部和水質。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement caused by water.","zh":"這個短語描述由水造成的移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"affect the roots of","meaning":"影響……的根部","examples":[{"en":"The lime affected the roots of nearby eucalyptus trees.","zh":"石灰影響了附近桉樹的根部。"},{"en":"To affect the roots of a plant means to influence or harm the part underground that absorbs water and nutrients.","zh":"affect the roots of a plant 的意思是影響或傷害植物地下吸收水分和養分的部分。"},{"en":"Polluted soil can affect the roots of vegetables in a garden.","zh":"受污染土壤可以影響菜園蔬菜的根部。"},{"en":"When roots are affected, the whole plant may become weak.","zh":"當根部受到影響，整株植物可能變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase connects underground damage with plant health.","zh":"這個短語把地下損害與植物健康連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"nearby","meaning":"附近的","examples":[{"en":"The lime affected eucalyptus trees nearby.","zh":"石灰影響了附近的桉樹。"},{"en":"Nearby means close to the place being discussed.","zh":"nearby 的意思是靠近正在討論的地方。"},{"en":"A nearby school may be affected by traffic noise.","zh":"附近的學校可能受交通噪音影響。"},{"en":"Problems in one location can affect nearby plants, homes, or services.","zh":"一個地點的問題可以影響附近植物、住屋或服務。"},{"en":"This word describes short distance.","zh":"這個詞描述距離近。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"prevent someone from doing","meaning":"阻止……做……","examples":[{"en":"The lime prevented the trees from sucking up iron.","zh":"石灰阻止樹木吸收鐵。"},{"en":"To prevent someone or something from doing an action means to stop that action from happening.","zh":"prevent someone or something from doing an action 的意思是阻止該行動發生。"},{"en":"A locked gate prevents children from entering a dangerous building.","zh":"上鎖大閘阻止兒童進入危險建築物。"},{"en":"If roots are prevented from absorbing nutrients, the plant may become unhealthy.","zh":"如果根部被阻止吸收養分，植物可能變得不健康。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with a blocked action.","zh":"這個短語把原因與被阻止的行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"suck up","meaning":"吸收","examples":[{"en":"The roots could not suck up the iron they needed.","zh":"根部不能吸收所需的鐵。"},{"en":"To suck up something means to absorb or draw it in, especially liquid or nutrients.","zh":"suck up something 的意思是吸收或吸入某物，尤其是液體或養分。"},{"en":"Plant roots suck up water from the soil.","zh":"植物根部從土壤中吸收水分。"},{"en":"If roots cannot suck up enough nutrients, leaves may change colour.","zh":"如果根部不能吸收足夠養分，葉子可能變色。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal but clear in plant descriptions.","zh":"這個短語較口語，但在植物描述中很清楚。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"healthy growth","meaning":"健康生長","examples":[{"en":"The trees needed iron for healthy growth.","zh":"這些樹需要鐵來健康生長。"},{"en":"Healthy growth means normal, strong development in a living thing.","zh":"healthy growth 是生物正常而強健的發展。"},{"en":"Children need sleep and food for healthy growth.","zh":"兒童需要睡眠和食物來健康成長。"},{"en":"Plants need water, light, and nutrients for healthy growth.","zh":"植物需要水、光和養分來健康生長。"},{"en":"This phrase connects necessary conditions with development.","zh":"這個短語把必要條件與發展連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be injected back into","meaning":"被重新注入","examples":[{"en":"Iron was injected back into the affected trees.","zh":"鐵被重新注入受影響的樹木中。"},{"en":"To be injected back into something means to be put into it again using a needle or similar method.","zh":"be injected back into something 的意思是用針或類似方法再次注入某物之中。"},{"en":"Medicine can be injected into a patient’s body to treat illness.","zh":"藥物可以被注入病人體內以治療疾病。"},{"en":"Injecting nutrients into trees may help them recover when roots cannot absorb enough.","zh":"當根部不能吸收足夠養分，把養分注入樹木可能幫助它們恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a direct treatment method.","zh":"這個短語描述直接治療方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"affected trees","meaning":"受影響的樹木","examples":[{"en":"The affected trees immediately recovered after iron was injected.","zh":"鐵被注入後，受影響的樹木立即恢復。"},{"en":"Affected trees are trees that have been harmed or changed by a problem.","zh":"affected trees 是受到問題傷害或改變的樹木。"},{"en":"After the storm, affected trees had broken branches and damaged roots.","zh":"風暴後，受影響的樹木有折斷樹枝和受損根部。"},{"en":"Identifying affected trees helps experts decide which ones need treatment first.","zh":"識別受影響的樹木有助專家決定哪些樹要優先治療。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trees suffering from a particular condition.","zh":"這個短語描述受某種情況影響的樹。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"immediately recovered","meaning":"立即恢復","examples":[{"en":"The affected trees immediately recovered after treatment.","zh":"受影響的樹木在治療後立即恢復。"},{"en":"Immediately recovered means became healthy again very quickly after a problem or treatment.","zh":"immediately recovered 的意思是在問題或治療後很快恢復健康。"},{"en":"The plant immediately recovered after being watered.","zh":"這株植物澆水後立即恢復。"},{"en":"Quick recovery can show that the treatment dealt with the real cause.","zh":"快速恢復可以顯示治療處理了真正原因。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises speed of improvement.","zh":"這個短語強調改善速度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"relatively small number of","meaning":"相對少數的……","examples":[{"en":"This problem only affected a relatively small number of trees.","zh":"這個問題只影響相對少數的樹木。"},{"en":"A relatively small number of something means a number that is small compared with the whole group.","zh":"relatively small number of something 的意思是與整體相比數量較少。"},{"en":"A relatively small number of students missed the trip because of illness.","zh":"相對少數的學生因病錯過旅行。"},{"en":"Saying “relatively” shows the number is being judged in comparison with a larger total.","zh":"說 relatively 顯示該數量是與更大總數相比而得出的判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a careful comparison.","zh":"這個短語給出審慎比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"huge numbers of","meaning":"大量的……","examples":[{"en":"Huge numbers of eucalyptus trees were dying along Australia’s East Coast.","zh":"大量桉樹沿澳洲東岸死亡。"},{"en":"Huge numbers of means very many.","zh":"huge numbers of 的意思是數量非常多。"},{"en":"Huge numbers of fish died after the river was polluted.","zh":"河流受污染後，大量魚類死亡。"},{"en":"When huge numbers of trees die, the whole ecosystem may change.","zh":"當大量樹木死亡，整個生態系統可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a very large quantity.","zh":"這個短語強調非常大的數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"along Australia’s East Coast","meaning":"沿澳洲東岸","examples":[{"en":"Huge numbers of eucalyptus trees were dying along Australia’s East Coast.","zh":"大量桉樹沿澳洲東岸死亡。"},{"en":"Along Australia’s East Coast means in areas beside or near the eastern coastline of Australia.","zh":"along Australia’s East Coast 的意思是在澳洲東部海岸線旁或附近地區。"},{"en":"Many towns along Australia’s East Coast are close to beaches and forests.","zh":"澳洲東岸許多城鎮靠近海灘和森林。"},{"en":"Environmental problems along a coast can affect both land and marine communities.","zh":"沿海岸出現的環境問題可以影響陸地和海洋社群。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a geographical region.","zh":"這個短語描述地理區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"known as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The disease is known as Bell-miner Associated Die-back.","zh":"這種疾病被稱為鐘礦鳥相關枯死病。"},{"en":"Known as means called or recognised by a particular name.","zh":"known as 的意思是被稱作某個名稱或以某名稱為人所知。"},{"en":"The city is known as a centre for art and music.","zh":"這座城市被稱為藝術和音樂中心。"},{"en":"Scientific problems are often known by names that describe their cause or symptoms.","zh":"科學問題常以描述其原因或病徵的名稱為人所知。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a name or label.","zh":"這個短語引出名稱或標籤。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Bell-miner Associated Die-back","meaning":"鐘礦鳥相關枯死病","examples":[{"en":"Many eucalyptus trees died of Bell-miner Associated Die-back.","zh":"許多桉樹死於鐘礦鳥相關枯死病。"},{"en":"Bell-miner Associated Die-back is a condition linked with bell-miner birds, insects, and eucalyptus decline.","zh":"Bell-miner Associated Die-back 是與鐘礦鳥、昆蟲和桉樹衰退有關的狀況。"},{"en":"Scientists study Bell-miner Associated Die-back to understand why eucalyptus forests weaken.","zh":"科學家研究鐘礦鳥相關枯死病，以了解桉樹林為何變弱。"},{"en":"The name suggests that bird behaviour and tree death are connected.","zh":"這個名稱暗示鳥類行為與樹木死亡有關。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific ecological disease problem.","zh":"這個短語指一個特定生態疾病問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"high populations of","meaning":"數量眾多的……","examples":[{"en":"The disease is common where there are high populations of bell-miners.","zh":"這種疾病常見於鐘礦鳥數量眾多的地方。"},{"en":"High populations of something means large numbers of that living thing in an area.","zh":"high populations of something 的意思是某地有大量某種生物。"},{"en":"High populations of mosquitoes can increase the risk of disease transmission.","zh":"蚊子數量眾多可以增加疾病傳播風險。"},{"en":"When one species has very high numbers, it may affect the balance of an ecosystem.","zh":"當一個物種數量非常多，它可能影響生態系統平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes abundance in a particular place.","zh":"這個短語描述某地的數量豐富程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bell-miners","meaning":"鐘礦鳥","examples":[{"en":"Bell-miners are birds associated with this disease.","zh":"鐘礦鳥是與這種疾病相關的鳥類。"},{"en":"Bell-miners are a type of bird linked in this context to eucalyptus die-back.","zh":"bell-miners 是在這個語境中與桉樹枯死相關的一種鳥。"},{"en":"Bell-miners may affect ecosystems by protecting insects that damage leaves.","zh":"鐘礦鳥可能透過保護損害葉子的昆蟲而影響生態系統。"},{"en":"A bird species can influence a forest if its behaviour changes the balance among other species.","zh":"如果一種鳥的行為改變其他物種之間的平衡，它就可以影響森林。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific bird group.","zh":"這個短語指一種特定鳥類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be affected","meaning":"受到影響","examples":[{"en":"The leaves of the trees are affected.","zh":"樹葉受到影響。"},{"en":"To be affected means to be changed, harmed, or influenced by something.","zh":"be affected 的意思是受到某事改變、傷害或影響。"},{"en":"Crops were affected by the long drought.","zh":"農作物受到長期乾旱影響。"},{"en":"When leaves are affected, the whole tree may struggle to grow.","zh":"當葉子受到影響，整棵樹可能難以生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the result of an outside influence.","zh":"這個短語描述外來因素造成的結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"settle on","meaning":"停留在……上","examples":[{"en":"Insects settle on the leaves and damage them.","zh":"昆蟲停留在葉子上並破壞它們。"},{"en":"To settle on something means to land on it and stay there for a time.","zh":"settle on something 的意思是落在某物上並停留一段時間。"},{"en":"Dust can settle on furniture if a room is not cleaned.","zh":"如果房間沒有清潔，灰塵可以停留在家具上。"},{"en":"Insects that settle on leaves may feed, lay eggs, or damage the plant.","zh":"停留在葉子上的昆蟲可能進食、產卵或破壞植物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes coming to rest on a surface.","zh":"這個短語描述落下並停在表面上。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"eat their way round","meaning":"沿着……一路啃食","examples":[{"en":"Insects eat their way round the leaves.","zh":"昆蟲沿着葉子一路啃食。"},{"en":"To eat their way round something means to move around it while eating and damaging it.","zh":"eat their way round something 的意思是一邊移動一邊進食並破壞某物。"},{"en":"Caterpillars may eat their way round a cabbage leaf.","zh":"毛蟲可能沿着椰菜葉一路啃食。"},{"en":"When insects eat around leaves, the plant loses surface area needed for growth.","zh":"當昆蟲啃食葉子，植物會失去生長所需的葉面面積。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement through feeding.","zh":"這個短語描述透過進食而移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"destroying them as they go","meaning":"一邊前進一邊破壞","examples":[{"en":"The insects destroy the leaves as they go.","zh":"昆蟲一邊前進一邊破壞葉子。"},{"en":"Destroying them as they go means damaging them continuously while moving along.","zh":"destroying them as they go 的意思是在移動時持續破壞它們。"},{"en":"Termites can eat through wood, destroying it as they go.","zh":"白蟻可以啃穿木材，一邊前進一邊破壞它。"},{"en":"Continuous damage can be worse than one small injury because it spreads across the surface.","zh":"持續破壞可能比一次小傷害更嚴重，因為它會在表面擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase combines movement and ongoing destruction.","zh":"這個短語結合移動和持續破壞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同時","examples":[{"en":"At the same time, the insects secrete a sugary solution.","zh":"同時，昆蟲會分泌含糖溶液。"},{"en":"At the same time means while another thing is happening.","zh":"at the same time 的意思是另一件事發生的同時。"},{"en":"Students listened to the teacher and took notes at the same time.","zh":"學生同時聆聽老師並做筆記。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two actions happen together.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個行動一起發生。"},{"en":"It is useful for explaining linked processes.","zh":"它適合用於解釋互相關連的過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"secrete a solution","meaning":"分泌溶液","examples":[{"en":"The insects secrete a solution containing sugar.","zh":"這些昆蟲分泌含糖溶液。"},{"en":"To secrete a solution means for an organism to produce and release a liquid.","zh":"secrete a solution 的意思是生物產生並釋放液體。"},{"en":"Some insects secrete sticky liquids that attract other animals.","zh":"有些昆蟲會分泌黏性液體，吸引其他動物。"},{"en":"Secreted liquids can affect relationships between insects, birds, and plants.","zh":"分泌出的液體可以影響昆蟲、鳥類和植物之間的關係。"},{"en":"This phrase is biological and describes a natural process.","zh":"這個短語屬生物學用語，描述自然過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了","examples":[{"en":"The bell-miners keep other creatures away in order to get the solution.","zh":"鐘礦鳥趕走其他生物，為了取得這種溶液。"},{"en":"In order to means for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"in order to 的意思是為了達到某個目的。"},{"en":"Students revise past papers in order to understand exam question styles.","zh":"學生操練歷屆試題，為了理解考試題型。"},{"en":"Animals may defend territory in order to protect food sources.","zh":"動物可能保衛領地，為了保護食物來源。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly connects action with purpose.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接行動與目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as much as possible","meaning":"盡可能多","examples":[{"en":"The birds try to get as much of the sugary solution as possible.","zh":"這些鳥嘗試取得盡可能多的含糖溶液。"},{"en":"As much as possible means the largest amount that can be obtained or done.","zh":"as much as possible 的意思是在可行範圍內取得或做最多。"},{"en":"Students should practise speaking as much as possible before an oral exam.","zh":"學生應在口試前盡可能多練習說話。"},{"en":"Animals compete for food when they try to get as much as possible.","zh":"當動物嘗試取得盡可能多的食物，就會競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises maximum effort or quantity.","zh":"這個短語強調最大努力或數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"keep away","meaning":"趕走","examples":[{"en":"The bell-miners keep away other creatures.","zh":"鐘礦鳥會趕走其他生物。"},{"en":"To keep away someone or something means to stop them from coming near.","zh":"keep away someone or something 的意思是阻止他們或它們靠近。"},{"en":"A fence can keep animals away from young plants.","zh":"圍欄可以把動物趕離幼苗。"},{"en":"Keeping other species away can change the balance of an ecosystem.","zh":"趕走其他物種可以改變生態系統平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exclusion or protection of an area.","zh":"這個短語描述排除或保護某個區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"flourish at the expense of","meaning":"以犧牲……為代價而繁盛","examples":[{"en":"The birds and insects flourish at the expense of other species.","zh":"這些鳥和昆蟲以犧牲其他物種為代價而繁盛。"},{"en":"To flourish at the expense of others means to grow or succeed while harming or disadvantaging them.","zh":"flourish at the expense of others 的意思是自己成長或成功，同時傷害或令他人處於不利。"},{"en":"One company may flourish at the expense of smaller shops if it drives them out of business.","zh":"如果一間公司令小店結業，它可能以犧牲小店為代價而繁盛。"},{"en":"In an ecosystem, one species flourishing too much can reduce biodiversity.","zh":"在生態系統中，一個物種過度繁盛可以減少生物多樣性。"},{"en":"This phrase shows unequal benefit and harm.","zh":"這個短語顯示不平等的得益和傷害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"other species","meaning":"其他物種","examples":[{"en":"The birds and insects flourish at the expense of other species.","zh":"這些鳥和昆蟲以犧牲其他物種為代價而繁盛。"},{"en":"Other species means different kinds of living things apart from the one being discussed.","zh":"other species 的意思是除了正在討論的物種以外的其他生物種類。"},{"en":"If one plant spreads too fast, other species may lose space and light.","zh":"如果一種植物擴散太快，其他物種可能失去空間和光線。"},{"en":"Ecosystems stay healthier when many species can survive together.","zh":"當許多物種能共同生存，生態系統會更健康。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare one species with the rest of the community.","zh":"這個短語幫助把一個物種與其餘生物群落作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"eventually","meaning":"最終","examples":[{"en":"Eventually, the tree dies because the leaves are badly damaged.","zh":"最終，這棵樹因葉子嚴重受損而死亡。"},{"en":"Eventually means in the end, after a period of time or a series of events.","zh":"eventually 的意思是在一段時間或一連串事件之後，最後。"},{"en":"If a plant gets no water, it will eventually die.","zh":"如果植物沒有水，最終會死亡。"},{"en":"This word shows the final result of a process.","zh":"這個詞顯示一個過程的最終結果。"},{"en":"It often follows a chain of causes.","zh":"它常跟在一連串原因之後。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"so much damage is done to","meaning":"對……造成如此嚴重破壞","examples":[{"en":"So much damage is done to the leaves that the tree dies.","zh":"葉子受到如此嚴重破壞，以致樹木死亡。"},{"en":"So much damage is done to something means it is harmed to a very serious degree.","zh":"so much damage is done to something 的意思是某物受到非常嚴重傷害。"},{"en":"So much damage was done to the bridge that it had to be closed.","zh":"橋樑受到如此嚴重破壞，以致必須關閉。"},{"en":"Severe damage to one part of a system can cause the whole system to fail.","zh":"系統某一部分受到嚴重破壞，可以導致整個系統失效。"},{"en":"This structure links extreme damage with a serious result.","zh":"這個結構把極端破壞與嚴重結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"before any sign of","meaning":"在出現任何……跡象之前","examples":[{"en":"Trees can look sick before any sign of Bell-miner Associated Die-back.","zh":"樹木可能在出現任何鐘礦鳥相關枯死病跡象之前已看起來生病。"},{"en":"Before any sign of something means earlier than any visible evidence of it appears.","zh":"before any sign of something 的意思是在任何可見證據出現之前。"},{"en":"A patient may feel tired before any sign of illness is obvious.","zh":"病人可能在任何明顯病徵出現之前已感到疲倦。"},{"en":"Early symptoms can appear before clear signs of the main problem.","zh":"早期症狀可以在主要問題的清晰跡象出現前出現。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights an earlier warning stage.","zh":"這個短語突出較早的警告階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it looks as if","meaning":"看來好像","examples":[{"en":"It looks as if the problem might have another explanation.","zh":"看來好像這個問題可能有另一個解釋。"},{"en":"It looks as if means it seems that something may be true.","zh":"it looks as if 的意思是某事看起來似乎可能是真的。"},{"en":"It looks as if the rain will stop soon.","zh":"看來好像雨很快會停。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when making a judgement based on available evidence.","zh":"這個短語用於根據現有證據作出判斷。"},{"en":"It sounds less certain than “it is clear that”.","zh":"它聽起來沒有 it is clear that 那麼肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"another explanation","meaning":"另一個解釋","examples":[{"en":"The problem might have another explanation.","zh":"這個問題可能有另一個解釋。"},{"en":"Another explanation means a different possible reason for something.","zh":"another explanation 的意思是某事的另一個可能原因。"},{"en":"If a student is quiet, another explanation may be tiredness rather than laziness.","zh":"如果學生很安靜，另一個解釋可能是疲倦，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"Considering another explanation helps people avoid jumping to conclusions.","zh":"考慮另一個解釋有助人避免太快下結論。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an alternative cause.","zh":"這個短語引出另一個成因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"to do with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"One possibility is that the problem is to do with bushfires.","zh":"一個可能性是，這個問題與山火有關。"},{"en":"To do with something means related or connected to it.","zh":"to do with something 的意思是與某事相關或有連繫。"},{"en":"The delay was to do with signal problems on the railway.","zh":"延誤與鐵路信號問題有關。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the exact connection is not yet fully explained.","zh":"當確切關係尚未完全解釋，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken English.","zh":"它常見於口語英文。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"huge bushfires","meaning":"大型山火","examples":[{"en":"The problem may be connected to Australia’s huge bushfires.","zh":"這個問題可能與澳洲大型山火有關。"},{"en":"Huge bushfires are very large fires that burn through bush land or forest areas.","zh":"huge bushfires 是燃燒灌木林地或森林地區的大型火災。"},{"en":"Huge bushfires can destroy homes, wildlife habitats, and large areas of vegetation.","zh":"大型山火可以摧毀家園、野生動物棲息地和大片植被。"},{"en":"Fire can damage ecosystems, but in some places it also shapes what grows later.","zh":"火可以破壞生態系統，但在某些地方也會塑造之後生長的植物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large-scale natural or environmental fires.","zh":"這個短語描述大規模自然或環境火災。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"theory proposed by","meaning":"由……提出的理論","examples":[{"en":"The theory was proposed by ecologist William Jackson.","zh":"這個理論由生態學家 William Jackson 提出。"},{"en":"A theory proposed by someone is an explanation or idea that person suggested.","zh":"theory proposed by someone 是由某人提出的解釋或想法。"},{"en":"A theory proposed by a scientist must be tested with evidence.","zh":"由科學家提出的理論必須用證據測試。"},{"en":"Naming who proposed a theory helps readers understand where the idea came from.","zh":"說明理論由誰提出，有助讀者理解想法來源。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic writing.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ecologist","meaning":"生態學家","examples":[{"en":"William Jackson was an ecologist who studied bushfires.","zh":"William Jackson 是研究山火的生態學家。"},{"en":"An ecologist is a scientist who studies relationships between living things and their environment.","zh":"ecologist 是研究生物與環境之間關係的科學家。"},{"en":"An ecologist may study how fires affect forests and animals.","zh":"生態學家可能研究火災如何影響森林和動物。"},{"en":"Ecologists help explain how changes in one species or habitat affect others.","zh":"生態學家幫助解釋一個物種或棲息地的變化如何影響其他部分。"},{"en":"This word names a scientific profession.","zh":"這個詞指一種科學職業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"frequency of","meaning":"……的頻率","examples":[{"en":"The frequency of bushfires affects the type of vegetation that grows.","zh":"山火的頻率會影響生長的植被類型。"},{"en":"Frequency of something means how often it happens.","zh":"frequency of something 的意思是某事發生得有多頻繁。"},{"en":"The frequency of buses affects how easy it is for people to commute.","zh":"巴士班次頻率影響人們通勤有多方便。"},{"en":"If fires happen too often or too rarely, the ecosystem may change.","zh":"如果火災發生得太頻繁或太少，生態系統可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how often an event occurs.","zh":"這個短語集中於事件發生頻密程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in a particular region","meaning":"在某一特定地區","examples":[{"en":"The frequency of bushfires in a particular region affects vegetation.","zh":"在某一特定地區，山火頻率會影響植被。"},{"en":"In a particular region means in one specific area.","zh":"in a particular region 的意思是在某個特定區域。"},{"en":"Rainfall in a particular region can affect the crops farmers choose.","zh":"某一特定地區的降雨量可以影響農民選擇的農作物。"},{"en":"Local conditions matter because different regions may respond differently to the same event.","zh":"本地情況很重要，因為不同地區對同一事件可能反應不同。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the discussion to a specific place.","zh":"這個短語把討論收窄到特定地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"type of vegetation","meaning":"植被類型","examples":[{"en":"Bushfires affect the type of vegetation that grows there.","zh":"山火會影響那裡生長的植被類型。"},{"en":"Type of vegetation means the kinds of plants found in an area.","zh":"type of vegetation 的意思是某地的植物種類。"},{"en":"Wetlands, grasslands, and forests all have different types of vegetation.","zh":"濕地、草地和森林都有不同植被類型。"},{"en":"The type of vegetation can influence which animals can live in a place.","zh":"植被類型可以影響哪些動物能在某地生活。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in ecology and geography.","zh":"這個短語適合用於生態學和地理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"encourage grass to grow","meaning":"促進草類生長","examples":[{"en":"Very frequent bushfires encourage grass to grow afterwards.","zh":"非常頻繁的山火會促進之後草類生長。"},{"en":"To encourage grass to grow means to create conditions that help grass develop.","zh":"encourage grass to grow 的意思是創造有助草類發展的條件。"},{"en":"Cutting back tall weeds can encourage grass to grow in a garden.","zh":"清除高大的雜草可以促進花園中的草類生長。"},{"en":"Fire may encourage grass growth if it removes competing plants and returns nutrients.","zh":"如果火清除競爭植物並把養分帶回土壤，就可能促進草類生長。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an action with plant growth.","zh":"這個短語把行動與植物生長連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rather less frequent","meaning":"頻率較低的","examples":[{"en":"Less frequent bushfires can support the growth of eucalyptus forests.","zh":"頻率較低的山火可以支持桉樹林生長。"},{"en":"Rather less frequent means happening somewhat less often than another pattern.","zh":"rather less frequent 的意思是比另一種模式發生得稍微少一些。"},{"en":"If tests are rather less frequent, students may feel less pressure but still need to revise.","zh":"如果測驗頻率較低，學生可能壓力較少，但仍需要溫習。"},{"en":"In ecology, a slightly lower frequency can change which species survive.","zh":"在生態學中，稍低的頻率可以改變哪些物種能生存。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how often something happens.","zh":"這個短語比較某事發生得有多頻繁。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致；帶來","examples":[{"en":"Less frequent bushfires result in the growth of eucalyptus forests.","zh":"頻率較低的山火會帶來桉樹林生長。"},{"en":"To result in something means to cause that outcome.","zh":"result in something 的意思是造成某結果。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can result in weak concentration the next day.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致翌日專注力差。"},{"en":"Changes in fire patterns can result in major changes to vegetation.","zh":"火災模式的變化可以導致植被出現重大改變。"},{"en":"This phrase connects cause and result.","zh":"這個短語連接原因與結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"growth of eucalyptus forests","meaning":"桉樹林生長","examples":[{"en":"Less frequent bushfires support the growth of eucalyptus forests.","zh":"頻率較低的山火支持桉樹林生長。"},{"en":"Growth of eucalyptus forests means the development or expansion of forests dominated by eucalyptus trees.","zh":"growth of eucalyptus forests 的意思是以桉樹為主的森林發展或擴展。"},{"en":"The growth of eucalyptus forests depends on fire patterns, soil, water, and competition from other plants.","zh":"桉樹林生長取決於火災模式、土壤、水分和其他植物競爭。"},{"en":"When the right conditions exist, eucalyptus forests can regenerate after fire.","zh":"當條件合適，桉樹林可以在火後再生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forest development.","zh":"這個短語描述森林發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fairly frequent bushfires","meaning":"頗頻繁的山火","examples":[{"en":"Fairly frequent bushfires can support the growth of eucalyptus.","zh":"頗頻繁的山火可以支持桉樹生長。"},{"en":"Fairly frequent bushfires are fires that happen quite often but not constantly.","zh":"fairly frequent bushfires 是相當經常發生但不是不斷發生的山火。"},{"en":"Fairly frequent fires may remove competing plants without destroying the whole ecosystem.","zh":"頗頻繁的火災可能清除競爭植物，而不摧毀整個生態系統。"},{"en":"The right fire frequency can support some species and harm others.","zh":"合適的火災頻率可以支持某些物種，同時傷害其他物種。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a moderate pattern of repeated fires.","zh":"這個短語描述中等程度的重複火災模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"support the growth of","meaning":"支持……的生長","examples":[{"en":"Bushfires can support the growth of eucalyptus trees.","zh":"山火可以支持桉樹生長。"},{"en":"To support the growth of something means to help it develop or increase.","zh":"support the growth of something 的意思是幫助某物發展或增加。"},{"en":"Good soil supports the growth of vegetables in a garden.","zh":"良好土壤支持花園中蔬菜生長。"},{"en":"Some environmental pressures can support one species while limiting another.","zh":"有些環境壓力可以支持一個物種，同時限制另一個物種。"},{"en":"This phrase connects conditions with development.","zh":"這個短語把條件與發展連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stop the growth of","meaning":"阻止……生長","examples":[{"en":"Fire stops the growth of other species.","zh":"火會阻止其他物種生長。"},{"en":"To stop the growth of something means to prevent it from developing or spreading.","zh":"stop the growth of something 的意思是防止某物發展或擴散。"},{"en":"Cutting weeds can stop the growth of plants that compete with vegetables.","zh":"清除雜草可以阻止與蔬菜競爭的植物生長。"},{"en":"Stopping one species from growing may give another species more space and resources.","zh":"阻止一個物種生長，可能給另一個物種更多空間和資源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limiting development.","zh":"這個短語描述限制發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"consume water","meaning":"消耗水分","examples":[{"en":"Other species would consume water needed by eucalyptus trees.","zh":"其他物種會消耗桉樹所需的水分。"},{"en":"To consume water means to use up water.","zh":"consume water 的意思是用掉水分。"},{"en":"Fast-growing crops can consume water quickly during hot weather.","zh":"生長快速的農作物在炎熱天氣中可以很快消耗水分。"},{"en":"When many plants consume the same water, competition increases.","zh":"當許多植物消耗同一水源，競爭就會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in ecology and resource discussions.","zh":"這個短語適合用於生態和資源討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"quick-growing species","meaning":"生長迅速的物種","examples":[{"en":"Quick-growing species can harm eucalyptus trees.","zh":"生長迅速的物種可以傷害桉樹。"},{"en":"Quick-growing species are plants or organisms that grow rapidly.","zh":"quick-growing species 是快速生長的植物或生物。"},{"en":"Quick-growing weeds may cover young trees and block sunlight.","zh":"生長迅速的雜草可能覆蓋幼樹並阻擋陽光。"},{"en":"Fast growth can become a problem when one species takes resources from another.","zh":"當一個物種奪走另一個物種的資源，快速生長就可能成為問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes species that develop quickly.","zh":"這個短語描述發展快速的物種。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bushes and plants","meaning":"灌木和植物","examples":[{"en":"Other species of bushes and plants may proliferate.","zh":"其他灌木和植物物種可能大量繁殖。"},{"en":"Bushes and plants means shrubs and other kinds of vegetation.","zh":"bushes and plants 指灌木及其他植被。"},{"en":"Bushes and plants can provide shelter, but too many may crowd out young trees.","zh":"灌木和植物可以提供庇護，但太多可能擠走幼樹。"},{"en":"The balance between bushes, plants, and trees affects the whole habitat.","zh":"灌木、植物和樹木之間的平衡影響整個棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase refers broadly to vegetation.","zh":"這個短語泛指植被。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be allowed to proliferate","meaning":"被容許大量繁殖","examples":[{"en":"If other species are allowed to proliferate, they harm the eucalyptus.","zh":"如果其他物種被容許大量繁殖，它們會傷害桉樹。"},{"en":"To be allowed to proliferate means to be left to increase or spread rapidly.","zh":"be allowed to proliferate 的意思是被放任快速增加或擴散。"},{"en":"If weeds are allowed to proliferate, they may take over a garden.","zh":"如果雜草被容許大量繁殖，它們可能佔據整個花園。"},{"en":"Uncontrolled growth can become harmful when one species dominates others.","zh":"當一個物種支配其他物種，不受控制的生長可能有害。"},{"en":"This phrase warns about unchecked expansion.","zh":"這個短語提醒人注意未受控制的擴張。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"harm something in another way","meaning":"以另一種方式傷害……","examples":[{"en":"Other plants harm the eucalyptus in another way.","zh":"其他植物會以另一種方式傷害桉樹。"},{"en":"To harm something in another way means to damage it through a different method or effect.","zh":"harm something in another way 的意思是透過不同方法或影響傷害某物。"},{"en":"Noise can harm students in one way, while lack of sleep harms them in another way.","zh":"噪音可以以一種方式傷害學生，而睡眠不足以另一種方式傷害他們。"},{"en":"A plant may harm another by taking water, shade, or nutrients.","zh":"一種植物可能透過奪走水分、陽光或養分來傷害另一種植物。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an additional form of damage.","zh":"這個短語引出另一種損害形式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"composition of the soil","meaning":"土壤成分","examples":[{"en":"Other plants can affect the composition of the soil.","zh":"其他植物可以影響土壤成分。"},{"en":"Composition of the soil means what the soil is made of, including minerals, nutrients, organic matter, and chemicals.","zh":"composition of the soil 指土壤由甚麼組成，包括礦物、養分、有機物和化學物質。"},{"en":"Farmers test the composition of the soil before choosing crops.","zh":"農夫在選擇農作物前會檢測土壤成分。"},{"en":"Soil composition affects how well plants can grow.","zh":"土壤成分影響植物能否良好生長。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in environmental science and farming.","zh":"這個短語常見於環境科學和農業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"remove nutrients from","meaning":"從……帶走養分","examples":[{"en":"Other plants remove nutrients from the soil.","zh":"其他植物會從土壤中帶走養分。"},{"en":"To remove nutrients from something means to take away substances needed for growth or health.","zh":"remove nutrients from something 的意思是帶走生長或健康所需的物質。"},{"en":"Heavy farming can remove nutrients from soil if farmers do not restore them.","zh":"如果農夫不補充養分，密集耕作可以從土壤中帶走養分。"},{"en":"When nutrients are removed, plants may grow slowly or become weak.","zh":"當養分被帶走，植物可能生長緩慢或變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase explains resource loss.","zh":"這個短語解釋資源流失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"essential for","meaning":"對……至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Some bushfires are essential for the eucalyptus to survive.","zh":"有些山火對桉樹生存至關重要。"},{"en":"Essential for something means absolutely necessary for it to happen or continue.","zh":"essential for something 的意思是對某事發生或延續絕對必要。"},{"en":"Clean water is essential for human health.","zh":"潔淨食水對人類健康至關重要。"},{"en":"Some ecological processes are essential for keeping habitats balanced.","zh":"有些生態過程對保持棲息地平衡至關重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “helpful”.","zh":"這個短語比 helpful 更強。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as long as","meaning":"只要","examples":[{"en":"Bushfires are useful as long as they are not too frequent.","zh":"只要山火不太頻繁，它們就是有用的。"},{"en":"As long as means provided that or only if a condition is met.","zh":"as long as 的意思是只要某條件得到滿足。"},{"en":"You can join the trip as long as you return the form by Friday.","zh":"只要你星期五前交回表格，就可以參加旅行。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a condition for something to be true or acceptable.","zh":"這個短語為某事成立或可接受設定條件。"},{"en":"It is useful when something is helpful only within limits.","zh":"當某事只有在限制內才有幫助時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"there’s evidence that","meaning":"有證據顯示","examples":[{"en":"There is evidence that Australia’s indigenous people practised regular burning.","zh":"有證據顯示澳洲原住民曾定期焚燒。"},{"en":"There’s evidence that means information or proof suggests something is true.","zh":"there’s evidence that 的意思是有資訊或證明顯示某事屬實。"},{"en":"There is evidence that regular exercise improves mood.","zh":"有證據顯示規律運動改善心情。"},{"en":"Evidence makes an argument stronger because it is not based only on opinion.","zh":"證據令論點更有力，因為它不是只基於意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research and academic writing.","zh":"這個短語常見於研究和學術寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"indigenous people","meaning":"原住民","examples":[{"en":"Australia’s indigenous people practised regular burning of bush land.","zh":"澳洲原住民曾定期焚燒灌木林地。"},{"en":"Indigenous people are the original peoples of a place and their descendants.","zh":"indigenous people 是某地原本的民族及其後代。"},{"en":"Indigenous communities often have deep knowledge of local land, plants, and seasons.","zh":"原住民社群常對本地土地、植物和季節有深厚知識。"},{"en":"Respecting indigenous knowledge can improve environmental management.","zh":"尊重原住民知識可以改善環境管理。"},{"en":"This phrase should be used respectfully.","zh":"使用這個短語時應保持尊重。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"practise regular burning","meaning":"定期焚燒","examples":[{"en":"Indigenous people practised regular burning of bush land.","zh":"原住民曾定期焚燒灌木林地。"},{"en":"To practise regular burning means to deliberately burn land at repeated intervals as a management method.","zh":"practise regular burning 的意思是以重複間隔有意焚燒土地作為管理方法。"},{"en":"Some communities practise regular burning to reduce dry fuel and shape vegetation.","zh":"有些社群會定期焚燒，以減少乾燥燃料並塑造植被。"},{"en":"Regular burning can affect which plants grow and how severe later fires become.","zh":"定期焚燒可以影響哪些植物生長，以及之後火災有多嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a land-management practice.","zh":"這個短語描述土地管理做法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bush land","meaning":"灌木林地","examples":[{"en":"Indigenous people burned bush land for thousands of years.","zh":"原住民數千年來焚燒灌木林地。"},{"en":"Bush land is land covered with natural shrubs, small trees, grasses, and native vegetation.","zh":"bush land 是覆蓋天然灌木、小樹、草和本土植被的土地。"},{"en":"Bush land can provide habitat for birds, insects, reptiles, and mammals.","zh":"灌木林地可以為鳥類、昆蟲、爬行動物和哺乳動物提供棲息地。"},{"en":"Managing bush land carefully can reduce fire risk and protect biodiversity.","zh":"細心管理灌木林地可以減少火災風險並保護生物多樣性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a natural landscape type.","zh":"這個短語描述一種自然地貌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"for thousands of years","meaning":"數千年來","examples":[{"en":"Regular burning was practised for thousands of years.","zh":"定期焚燒已實行數千年。"},{"en":"For thousands of years means during a very long period across many generations.","zh":"for thousands of years 的意思是跨越許多世代的非常長時間。"},{"en":"People have used plants as medicine for thousands of years.","zh":"人們使用植物作藥已有數千年。"},{"en":"Practices that continue for thousands of years often contain deep cultural knowledge.","zh":"持續數千年的做法通常包含深厚文化知識。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises long historical duration.","zh":"這個短語強調漫長歷史時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"before the arrival of","meaning":"在……到來之前","examples":[{"en":"Regular burning happened before the arrival of the Europeans.","zh":"定期焚燒在歐洲人到來之前已經發生。"},{"en":"Before the arrival of someone means before that group came to a place.","zh":"before the arrival of someone 的意思是在某個群體來到某地之前。"},{"en":"Local traditions existed before the arrival of modern tourism.","zh":"本地傳統在現代旅遊業到來之前已存在。"},{"en":"This phrase helps place events in historical order.","zh":"這個短語幫助把事件放入歷史次序。"},{"en":"It often marks a major change in history.","zh":"它常標示歷史上的重大轉變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on the continent","meaning":"在這片大陸上","examples":[{"en":"Europeans arrived on the continent and controlled bushfires.","zh":"歐洲人來到這片大陸上，並控制山火。"},{"en":"On the continent means on a large landmass, in this case Australia.","zh":"on the continent 的意思是在一大片陸地上，在這裡指澳洲。"},{"en":"The animals on the continent evolved in different conditions from island species.","zh":"這片大陸上的動物在與島嶼物種不同的條件下演化。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where events happened geographically.","zh":"這個短語從地理上指出事件發生在哪裡。"},{"en":"It is often used when discussing large regions of land.","zh":"它常用於討論大型陸地區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"strictly controlled","meaning":"受到嚴格控制","examples":[{"en":"The number of bushfires has been strictly controlled.","zh":"山火數量受到嚴格控制。"},{"en":"Strictly controlled means managed very tightly according to rules or limits.","zh":"strictly controlled 的意思是按照規則或限制非常嚴格地管理。"},{"en":"Access to dangerous chemicals is strictly controlled in laboratories.","zh":"實驗室中危險化學品的使用受到嚴格控制。"},{"en":"Strict control can prevent harm, but it may also change natural processes.","zh":"嚴格控制可以防止傷害，但也可能改變自然過程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong management or regulation.","zh":"這個短語描述強力管理或規管。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reduced frequency of","meaning":"……頻率降低","examples":[{"en":"The reduced frequency of bushfires has led to dry rainforest.","zh":"山火頻率降低導致乾性雨林出現。"},{"en":"Reduced frequency of something means it happens less often than before.","zh":"reduced frequency of something 的意思是某事比以前較少發生。"},{"en":"The reduced frequency of buses made commuting harder for residents.","zh":"巴士班次頻率降低令居民通勤更困難。"},{"en":"When natural events become less frequent, ecosystems may change in unexpected ways.","zh":"當自然事件發生頻率降低，生態系統可能以意想不到的方式改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decrease in how often something happens.","zh":"這個短語描述某事發生頻率下降。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"low levels","meaning":"低水平","examples":[{"en":"The frequency of bushfires has been reduced to low levels.","zh":"山火頻率已被降低至低水平。"},{"en":"Low levels means small amounts, numbers, or degrees.","zh":"low levels 的意思是數量、程度或水平較低。"},{"en":"Low levels of rainfall can cause water shortages.","zh":"低水平降雨可以造成缺水。"},{"en":"When something falls to low levels, its effects on a system may change.","zh":"當某事下降至低水平，它對系統的影響可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for measurement and comparison.","zh":"這個短語用於量度和比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"The reduction in bushfires has led to dry rainforest.","zh":"山火減少導致乾性雨林出現。"},{"en":"To lead to something means to cause it or make it happen.","zh":"lead to something 的意思是造成或促成某事發生。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can lead to weak concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致課堂專注力差。"},{"en":"Changes in land management can lead to changes in vegetation.","zh":"土地管理方式改變可以導致植被變化。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with a result.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"what’s known as","meaning":"所謂的……","examples":[{"en":"The reduced frequency has led to what is known as dry rainforest.","zh":"頻率降低導致所謂的乾性雨林出現。"},{"en":"What’s known as means what people call or refer to by a particular name.","zh":"what’s known as 的意思是人們稱作某個名稱的事物。"},{"en":"This condition is what’s known as burnout.","zh":"這種狀況就是所謂的 burnout。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a term that may be new to the listener.","zh":"這個短語引出聽者可能不熟悉的術語。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining technical names.","zh":"它適合用於解釋專門名稱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"dry rainforest","meaning":"乾性雨林","examples":[{"en":"Dry rainforest has thick vegetation but little variety of species.","zh":"乾性雨林有厚密植被，但物種多樣性較少。"},{"en":"Dry rainforest is a forest type with dense vegetation but usually less species variety than tropical rainforest.","zh":"dry rainforest 是一種森林類型，植被濃密，但物種多樣性通常少於熱帶雨林。"},{"en":"Dry rainforest can create deep shade that changes which plants and animals thrive.","zh":"乾性雨林可以形成濃蔭，改變哪些植物和動物能繁盛。"},{"en":"A dry rainforest environment may not suit eucalyptus trees if competing vegetation becomes too dense.","zh":"如果競爭植被變得太濃密，乾性雨林環境可能不適合桉樹。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific ecosystem type.","zh":"這個短語描述一種特定生態系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"associate A with B","meaning":"將A與B聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"We usually associate tropical rainforest with wet conditions.","zh":"我們通常將熱帶雨林與潮濕環境聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To associate A with B means to connect one idea with another in your mind.","zh":"associate A with B 的意思是在腦中把一個想法與另一個想法連結。"},{"en":"Many people associate exams with stress.","zh":"許多人將考試與壓力聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Associations can shape expectations, even when reality is more complicated.","zh":"聯想可以塑造期望，即使現實更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental connection.","zh":"這個短語描述心理連結。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"tropical rainforest","meaning":"熱帶雨林","examples":[{"en":"Tropical rainforest is usually associated with wet conditions.","zh":"熱帶雨林通常與潮濕環境聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Tropical rainforest is a rich forest ecosystem found in warm, wet regions near the tropics.","zh":"tropical rainforest 是位於熱帶附近溫暖潮濕地區的豐富森林生態系統。"},{"en":"Tropical rainforest often contains many species of plants, insects, birds, and mammals.","zh":"熱帶雨林通常包含許多植物、昆蟲、鳥類和哺乳動物物種。"},{"en":"These forests are important because they support biodiversity and store carbon.","zh":"這些森林很重要，因為它們支持生物多樣性並儲存碳。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a globally important ecosystem.","zh":"這個短語描述全球重要的生態系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"wet conditions","meaning":"潮濕環境","examples":[{"en":"Tropical rainforest is usually associated with wet conditions.","zh":"熱帶雨林通常與潮濕環境聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Wet conditions mean an environment with a lot of rain, moisture, or water.","zh":"wet conditions 的意思是有大量雨水、濕氣或水分的環境。"},{"en":"Wet conditions can make paths slippery and difficult to walk on.","zh":"潮濕環境可以令路面濕滑，難以行走。"},{"en":"Some plants grow best in wet conditions, while others need drier soil.","zh":"有些植物在潮濕環境中長得最好，而另一些需要較乾土壤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes environmental moisture.","zh":"這個短語描述環境濕度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"what’s special about","meaning":"……有甚麼特別之處","examples":[{"en":"What is special about this type of rainforest?","zh":"這種雨林有甚麼特別之處？"},{"en":"What’s special about something asks what makes it unusual, important, or different.","zh":"what’s special about something 是問某事有甚麼不尋常、重要或不同之處。"},{"en":"What’s special about this painting is the way light is used.","zh":"這幅畫特別之處在於光線的運用方式。"},{"en":"This question helps focus attention on distinctive features.","zh":"這個問題幫助把注意力集中於獨特特徵。"},{"en":"It is useful in explanations and presentations.","zh":"它適合用於解釋和簡報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"unlike","meaning":"與……不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike tropical rainforest, dry rainforest is usually a simple ecosystem.","zh":"與熱帶雨林不同，乾性雨林通常是簡單的生態系統。"},{"en":"Unlike means different from someone or something else.","zh":"unlike 的意思是與某人或某物不同。"},{"en":"Unlike buses, trains do not usually get stuck in road traffic.","zh":"與巴士不同，火車通常不會被道路交通阻塞。"},{"en":"This word introduces a contrast between two things.","zh":"這個詞引出兩件事之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing features.","zh":"它適合用於比較特徵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rich ecosystem","meaning":"豐富的生態系統","examples":[{"en":"Tropical rainforest is a rich ecosystem.","zh":"熱帶雨林是豐富的生態系統。"},{"en":"A rich ecosystem contains many different species and complex relationships between them.","zh":"rich ecosystem 包含許多不同物種以及牠們之間的複雜關係。"},{"en":"Coral reefs are rich ecosystems because many fish, plants, and animals live there.","zh":"珊瑚礁是豐富的生態系統，因為許多魚、植物和動物生活在那裡。"},{"en":"Rich ecosystems are valuable because they support biodiversity and resilience.","zh":"豐富的生態系統很有價值，因為它們支持生物多樣性和韌性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ecological variety and complexity.","zh":"這個短語描述生態多樣性和複雜性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"simple ecosystem","meaning":"簡單的生態系統","examples":[{"en":"Dry rainforest is usually a simple ecosystem.","zh":"乾性雨林通常是簡單的生態系統。"},{"en":"A simple ecosystem has fewer species and less complex relationships than a rich ecosystem.","zh":"simple ecosystem 比豐富生態系統有較少物種和較少複雜關係。"},{"en":"A pond with only a few plant and animal species may be a simple ecosystem.","zh":"只有少量植物和動物物種的池塘可能是簡單的生態系統。"},{"en":"Simple ecosystems can be more vulnerable if one important species changes.","zh":"如果一個重要物種改變，簡單生態系統可能更脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lower ecological complexity.","zh":"這個短語描述較低生態複雜性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"thick, dense vegetation","meaning":"厚密植被","examples":[{"en":"Dry rainforest has thick, dense vegetation.","zh":"乾性雨林有厚密植被。"},{"en":"Thick, dense vegetation means plants grow closely together and form heavy cover.","zh":"thick, dense vegetation 的意思是植物生長得很密集，形成厚重覆蓋。"},{"en":"Thick vegetation can make it difficult to walk through a forest.","zh":"厚密植被可以令人難以穿過森林。"},{"en":"Dense vegetation provides shade and shelter but may also limit which plants can grow beneath it.","zh":"密集植被提供樹蔭和庇護，但也可能限制下方植物生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes crowded plant growth.","zh":"這個短語描述擁擠的植物生長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"variety of species","meaning":"物種多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Dry rainforest does not have much variety of species.","zh":"乾性雨林沒有很多物種多樣性。"},{"en":"Variety of species means the number and range of different living things in an ecosystem.","zh":"variety of species 是生態系統中不同生物的數量和範圍。"},{"en":"A garden with many flowers, insects, and birds has a good variety of species.","zh":"有許多花、昆蟲和鳥的花園有良好物種多樣性。"},{"en":"More species variety often makes ecosystems stronger and more balanced.","zh":"更多物種多樣性通常令生態系統更強韌和更平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase is closely related to biodiversity.","zh":"這個短語與生物多樣性密切相關。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"provide lots of shade","meaning":"提供大量樹蔭","examples":[{"en":"The vegetation provides lots of shade.","zh":"這些植被提供大量樹蔭。"},{"en":"To provide lots of shade means to block sunlight and create many shaded areas.","zh":"provide lots of shade 的意思是阻擋陽光並創造許多陰涼位置。"},{"en":"Large trees provide lots of shade for people waiting at a bus stop.","zh":"大樹為在巴士站等候的人提供大量樹蔭。"},{"en":"Shade can cool an area, but too much shade may stop some plants from growing.","zh":"樹蔭可以令地方降溫，但太多樹蔭可能阻止某些植物生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one effect of dense plants or trees.","zh":"這個短語描述密集植物或樹木的一種效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"find it ideal","meaning":"覺得它很理想","examples":[{"en":"The bell-miner bird finds the shaded vegetation ideal.","zh":"鐘礦鳥覺得有樹蔭的植被很理想。"},{"en":"To find something ideal means to think it is perfectly suitable for a purpose.","zh":"find something ideal 的意思是認為某事物對某目的完全合適。"},{"en":"Students may find a quiet library ideal for revision.","zh":"學生可能覺得安靜圖書館很適合溫習。"},{"en":"Animals choose habitats they find ideal because food, shelter, or safety is available.","zh":"動物選擇牠們覺得理想的棲息地，因為那裡有食物、庇護或安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes suitability from someone’s or something’s point of view.","zh":"這個短語從某人或某物角度描述合適性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"build nests","meaning":"築巢","examples":[{"en":"Bell-miner birds build nests in the undergrowth.","zh":"鐘礦鳥在下層灌木叢中築巢。"},{"en":"To build nests means to make places where birds lay eggs and raise young.","zh":"build nests 的意思是建造鳥類產卵和養育幼鳥的地方。"},{"en":"Birds may build nests using twigs, leaves, grass, and feathers.","zh":"鳥類可能用小樹枝、葉、草和羽毛築巢。"},{"en":"Safe nesting places help bird populations survive.","zh":"安全築巢地點有助鳥類族群生存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a key part of bird reproduction.","zh":"這個短語描述鳥類繁殖的重要部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"undergrowth","meaning":"下層灌木叢","examples":[{"en":"Bell-miner birds build their nests in the undergrowth.","zh":"鐘礦鳥在下層灌木叢中築巢。"},{"en":"Undergrowth is the low plants, bushes, and young trees growing beneath taller trees.","zh":"undergrowth 是高樹下方生長的低矮植物、灌木和幼樹。"},{"en":"Thick undergrowth can provide shelter for birds and small animals.","zh":"厚密下層灌木叢可以為鳥類和小動物提供庇護。"},{"en":"Undergrowth can also compete with young trees for light, water, and nutrients.","zh":"下層灌木叢也可以與幼樹競爭光線、水分和養分。"},{"en":"This word describes the lower layer of forest vegetation.","zh":"這個詞描述森林植被的低層。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not helpful for","meaning":"對……沒有幫助","examples":[{"en":"The dry rainforest environment is not helpful for the eucalyptus tree.","zh":"乾性雨林環境對桉樹沒有幫助。"},{"en":"Not helpful for something means not supporting it or making its situation better.","zh":"not helpful for something 的意思是不支持某事，或沒有令其情況變好。"},{"en":"Too much shade is not helpful for plants that need strong sunlight.","zh":"太多樹蔭對需要強烈陽光的植物沒有幫助。"},{"en":"An environment may be good for one species but not helpful for another.","zh":"一種環境可能對一個物種有利，但對另一個物種沒有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lack of benefit or support.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏好處或支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 20 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 3/task-1":[{"front":"phone the owner of a house","meaning":"打電話給屋主","examples":[{"en":"A woman phones the owner of a house she is going to rent.","zh":"一名女士打電話給她將會租住房子的屋主。"},{"en":"To phone the owner of a house means to call the person who owns the house.","zh":"phone the owner of a house 意思是致電擁有那間房子的人。"},{"en":"A tenant may phone the owner of a house to ask about repairs.","zh":"租客可能會打電話給屋主詢問維修問題。"},{"en":"Shelley phones the owner because she needs information before moving in.","zh":"Shelley 打電話給屋主，因為她搬入前需要資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone contacts a landlord directly.","zh":"當某人直接聯絡業主時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rent a house","meaning":"租住房子","examples":[{"en":"Shelley is going to rent a house on Archwood Avenue.","zh":"Shelley 將會租住 Archwood Avenue 的一間房子。"},{"en":"To rent a house means to pay money regularly to live in a house owned by someone else.","zh":"rent a house 意思是定期付錢住在別人擁有的房子裏。"},{"en":"A family may rent a house for one year before buying their own home.","zh":"一個家庭在買自己的家之前，可能會租住房子一年。"},{"en":"Shelley rents the house because she needs somewhere to live while working in the city.","zh":"Shelley 租住房子，因為她在市內工作時需要住處。"},{"en":"Renting a house is different from buying it because the tenant does not own it.","zh":"租住房子與買房不同，因為租客並不擁有那間房子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rent furniture from","meaning":"向……租用家具","examples":[{"en":"She asks about companies she could rent furniture from.","zh":"她詢問可以向哪些公司租用家具。"},{"en":"To rent furniture from a company means to pay to use that company’s furniture for a period of time.","zh":"rent furniture from a company 意思是付錢在一段時間內使用那間公司的家具。"},{"en":"Students may rent furniture from a shop if they stay in a flat for only six months.","zh":"如果學生只在單位住六個月，可能會向商店租用家具。"},{"en":"Shelley wants to rent furniture because she is not bringing many things with her.","zh":"Shelley 想租用家具，因為她沒有帶很多東西過來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone needs furniture temporarily.","zh":"當某人暫時需要家具時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"furniture rental companies","meaning":"家具租賃公司","examples":[{"en":"The man gives Shelley information about furniture rental companies in the city.","zh":"那名男子向 Shelley 提供市內家具租賃公司的資料。"},{"en":"Furniture rental companies are businesses that lend furniture to customers for a fee.","zh":"家具租賃公司是收費把家具租給顧客使用的公司。"},{"en":"A furniture rental company may provide beds, tables, sofas, and chairs.","zh":"家具租賃公司可能提供床、桌子、梳化和椅子。"},{"en":"Shelley compares furniture rental companies to find one that fits her budget.","zh":"Shelley 比較家具租賃公司，以找出符合她預算的一間。"},{"en":"These companies are useful for people who move often or stay somewhere temporarily.","zh":"這些公司對經常搬屋或暫時居住的人很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"This is Shelley Mayer","meaning":"我是 Shelley Mayer","examples":[{"en":"Shelley says, “This is Shelley Mayer,” when she phones the owner.","zh":"Shelley 打電話給屋主時說：「我是 Shelley Mayer。」"},{"en":"This is Shelley Mayer is a way to identify yourself on the phone.","zh":"This is Shelley Mayer 是在電話中表明自己身份的說法。"},{"en":"When calling a school office, a parent may say, “This is Mrs Chan.”","zh":"家長致電學校辦公室時，可能會說：「我是 Chan 太太。」"},{"en":"Shelley says her name so the owner knows who is calling.","zh":"Shelley 說出自己的名字，讓屋主知道來電者是誰。"},{"en":"This phrase is common at the beginning of a phone conversation.","zh":"這個短語常用於電話對話開頭。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on Archwood Avenue","meaning":"在 Archwood Avenue","examples":[{"en":"Shelley is renting the house on Archwood Avenue.","zh":"Shelley 正在租住 Archwood Avenue 的那間房子。"},{"en":"On Archwood Avenue means located on the street called Archwood Avenue.","zh":"on Archwood Avenue 意思是位於名為 Archwood Avenue 的街道上。"},{"en":"The new café is on Queen Street, near the station.","zh":"新咖啡店在 Queen Street，靠近車站。"},{"en":"Shelley mentions Archwood Avenue so the owner knows which house she means.","zh":"Shelley 提到 Archwood Avenue，讓屋主知道她指哪間房子。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the street location of a place.","zh":"這個短語提供某地方的街道位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be due to move in","meaning":"預計搬入","examples":[{"en":"Shelley is due to move in next week.","zh":"Shelley 預計下星期搬入。"},{"en":"To be due to move in means to be expected or scheduled to start living somewhere.","zh":"be due to move in 意思是預計或安排好開始搬進某地居住。"},{"en":"The new tenants are due to move in on Monday.","zh":"新租客預計星期一搬入。"},{"en":"Shelley needs furniture soon because she is moving in next week.","zh":"Shelley 很快需要家具，因為她下星期就要搬入。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a planned future arrangement.","zh":"這個短語顯示已計劃好的未來安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"What can I do for you?","meaning":"有甚麼可以幫到你？","examples":[{"en":"The owner asks Shelley, “What can I do for you?”","zh":"屋主問 Shelley：「有甚麼可以幫到你？」"},{"en":"What can I do for you? is a polite way to ask how you can help someone.","zh":"What can I do for you? 是禮貌地詢問可以如何幫助某人。"},{"en":"A receptionist may ask, “What can I do for you?” when a visitor arrives.","zh":"接待員在訪客到達時可能會問：「有甚麼可以幫到你？」"},{"en":"The owner asks this because Shelley has called with a question.","zh":"屋主這樣問，因為 Shelley 打電話來有問題想問。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in service, work, and polite phone conversations.","zh":"這個短語適合用於服務、工作和禮貌電話對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"view the house","meaning":"睇樓；看房","examples":[{"en":"Shelley told the owner about the furniture when she viewed the house.","zh":"Shelley 睇樓時曾向屋主提過家具問題。"},{"en":"To view the house means to visit and look around a house before renting or buying it.","zh":"view the house 意思是在租住或購買前參觀並查看房子。"},{"en":"A couple may view the house before deciding whether to rent it.","zh":"一對夫婦可能會先睇樓，再決定是否租住。"},{"en":"Shelley noticed the furniture issue when she visited the house earlier.","zh":"Shelley 早前看房時注意到家具問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in renting and property situations.","zh":"這個短語常用於租屋和物業情境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"most probably","meaning":"很可能","examples":[{"en":"Shelley will most probably need to rent some furniture.","zh":"Shelley 很可能需要租用一些家具。"},{"en":"Most probably means very likely.","zh":"most probably 意思是很有可能。"},{"en":"It will most probably rain later, so bring an umbrella.","zh":"稍後很可能下雨，所以帶雨傘吧。"},{"en":"Shelley says this because she is not bringing much furniture with her.","zh":"Shelley 這樣說，因為她沒有帶很多家具過來。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong possibility, but not complete certainty.","zh":"這個短語表示很高可能性，但不是百分百肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"at least until","meaning":"至少直到","examples":[{"en":"She will rent furniture at least until she knows about her work contract.","zh":"她會租用家具，至少直到她知道工作合約的情況。"},{"en":"At least until means up to a certain time, and possibly longer.","zh":"at least until 意思是到某個時間為止，而且可能更久。"},{"en":"I will stay in the library at least until I finish my homework.","zh":"我會留在圖書館，至少直到完成功課。"},{"en":"Shelley will rent furniture temporarily until she knows whether her job is permanent.","zh":"Shelley 會暫時租用家具，直到知道工作是否轉為永久。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a minimum time limit.","zh":"這個短語設定最低時間限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"temporary work contract","meaning":"臨時工作合約","examples":[{"en":"Shelley has a temporary work contract.","zh":"Shelley 有一份臨時工作合約。"},{"en":"A temporary work contract is a job agreement that lasts for a limited period.","zh":"臨時工作合約是一份只維持有限時間的工作協議。"},{"en":"A teacher may have a temporary work contract for one school term.","zh":"老師可能有一份為期一個學期的臨時工作合約。"},{"en":"Shelley is unsure about buying furniture because her job may not last long.","zh":"Shelley 不確定是否購買家具，因為她的工作可能不會持續很久。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why someone may avoid long-term decisions.","zh":"這個短語解釋為甚麼某人可能避免作長期決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be made permanent","meaning":"轉為永久","examples":[{"en":"She does not yet know whether her temporary contract will be made permanent.","zh":"她還不知道她的臨時合約會否轉為永久。"},{"en":"To be made permanent means to be changed from temporary to lasting or long-term.","zh":"be made permanent 意思是由臨時改為長期或永久。"},{"en":"A temporary worker may hope their job will be made permanent after six months.","zh":"臨時員工可能希望工作在六個月後轉為永久。"},{"en":"Shelley may buy furniture later if her contract is made permanent.","zh":"如果 Shelley 的合約轉為永久，她之後可能會買家具。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for jobs, contracts, and appointments.","zh":"這個短語常用於工作、合約和任命。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"of course","meaning":"當然","examples":[{"en":"The owner says, “Yes, of course, I remember.”","zh":"屋主說：「是的，當然，我記得。」"},{"en":"Of course means certainly or naturally.","zh":"of course 意思是當然或自然是這樣。"},{"en":"“Can I borrow a pen?” “Of course.”","zh":"「我可以借一支筆嗎？」「當然。」"},{"en":"The owner says this to show that he clearly remembers Shelley’s earlier question.","zh":"屋主這樣說，是表示他清楚記得 Shelley 早前的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase can make an answer sound friendly and reassuring.","zh":"這個短語可以令回答聽起來友善而令人安心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"give someone information about","meaning":"向某人提供關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"The owner can give Shelley information about furniture rental companies.","zh":"屋主可以向 Shelley 提供關於家具租賃公司的資料。"},{"en":"To give someone information about something means to tell them useful facts or details.","zh":"give someone information about something 意思是告訴某人有用事實或細節。"},{"en":"The school office gave parents information about the summer course.","zh":"學校辦公室向家長提供關於暑期課程的資料。"},{"en":"The owner helps Shelley by explaining different rental companies.","zh":"屋主透過解釋不同租賃公司來幫助 Shelley。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone needs guidance before making a choice.","zh":"當某人在作選擇前需要指引時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in the city","meaning":"在市內；在城中","examples":[{"en":"The owner knows about furniture rental companies in the city.","zh":"屋主知道市內一些家具租賃公司。"},{"en":"In the city means located within the urban area or town being discussed.","zh":"in the city 意思是位於所討論的城市或市區內。"},{"en":"There are many restaurants in the city, but fewer in the countryside.","zh":"市內有很多餐廳，但郊區較少。"},{"en":"Shelley needs companies in the city because she will live nearby.","zh":"Shelley 需要市內的公司，因為她會住在附近。"},{"en":"This phrase tells us the general location of services or places.","zh":"這個短語告訴我們服務或地方的大概位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the biggest company","meaning":"最大的公司","examples":[{"en":"The biggest company is called Peak Rentals.","zh":"最大的公司名叫 Peak Rentals。"},{"en":"The biggest company means the company with the largest size, business, or market share.","zh":"the biggest company 意思是規模、業務或市場佔有率最大的公司。"},{"en":"The biggest company in town may have more delivery trucks and more stock.","zh":"城中最大的公司可能有更多送貨車和更多存貨。"},{"en":"Peak Rentals may be well known because it serves many customers.","zh":"Peak Rentals 可能很有名，因為它服務很多顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one company with others in the same field.","zh":"這個短語把一間公司與同一行業的其他公司作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be called","meaning":"名叫；稱為","examples":[{"en":"The biggest company is called Peak Rentals.","zh":"最大的公司名叫 Peak Rentals。"},{"en":"Be called means have the name of something or someone.","zh":"be called 意思是有某個名稱。"},{"en":"The new café is called Morning Light.","zh":"新咖啡店名叫 Morning Light。"},{"en":"The owner says the company is called Peak Rentals so Shelley knows its name.","zh":"屋主說那間公司名叫 Peak Rentals，讓 Shelley 知道它的名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to introduce names clearly.","zh":"這個短語用來清楚介紹名稱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recommend something to someone","meaning":"向某人推薦某物","examples":[{"en":"The owner has recommended Peak Rentals to other people.","zh":"屋主曾向其他人推薦 Peak Rentals。"},{"en":"To recommend something to someone means to suggest it because you think it is good or useful.","zh":"recommend something to someone 意思是因為你認為某物好或有用而向某人建議它。"},{"en":"My friend recommended a moving company to me.","zh":"我的朋友向我推薦一間搬屋公司。"},{"en":"The owner recommends Peak Rentals because he has heard good things about it.","zh":"屋主推薦 Peak Rentals，因為他聽過關於它的好評。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when giving advice based on experience or trust.","zh":"這個短語常用於根據經驗或信任給建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"positive reports about","meaning":"關於……的正面評價","examples":[{"en":"The owner has heard positive reports about Peak Rentals.","zh":"屋主聽過關於 Peak Rentals 的正面評價。"},{"en":"Positive reports about something are good comments or favourable feedback about it.","zh":"positive reports about something 是對某事的好評或正面回饋。"},{"en":"The school received positive reports about the new lunch service.","zh":"學校收到關於新午餐服務的正面評價。"},{"en":"Positive reports make Shelley more willing to consider Peak Rentals.","zh":"正面評價令 Shelley 更願意考慮 Peak Rentals。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that other people have had good experiences.","zh":"這個短語暗示其他人有良好經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"give me an idea of","meaning":"大概告訴我……","examples":[{"en":"Shelley asks the owner to give her an idea of their costs.","zh":"Shelley 請屋主大概告訴她他們的收費。"},{"en":"To give me an idea of something means to give me a rough understanding of it.","zh":"give me an idea of something 意思是讓我大概了解某事。"},{"en":"Can you give me an idea of how long the repair will take?","zh":"你可以大概告訴我維修需要多久嗎？"},{"en":"Shelley asks this because she wants to know the approximate price before choosing.","zh":"Shelley 這樣問，因為她想在選擇前知道大概價格。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when exact details are not needed yet.","zh":"當暫時不需要準確細節時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"their costs","meaning":"他們的收費","examples":[{"en":"Shelley wants to know their costs before choosing a company.","zh":"Shelley 想在選擇公司前知道他們的收費。"},{"en":"Their costs means the prices or fees charged by that company or group.","zh":"their costs 意思是那間公司或群組收取的價格或費用。"},{"en":"We compared the costs of three moving companies before booking one.","zh":"我們預訂前比較了三間搬屋公司的收費。"},{"en":"Shelley checks the costs because furniture rental may become expensive over time.","zh":"Shelley 查看收費，因為家具租賃長遠可能變得昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people compare services by price.","zh":"這個短語幫助人們按價格比較服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have one of their brochures","meaning":"有他們其中一本小冊子","examples":[{"en":"The owner has one of Peak Rentals’ brochures.","zh":"屋主有 Peak Rentals 其中一本小冊子。"},{"en":"To have one of their brochures means to possess an information leaflet from that company.","zh":"have one of their brochures 意思是擁有那間公司的一本資料小冊子。"},{"en":"The travel agent had one of the hotel’s brochures on her desk.","zh":"旅行社職員桌上有其中一本酒店小冊子。"},{"en":"The brochure helps the owner explain prices and offers to Shelley.","zh":"小冊子幫助屋主向 Shelley 解釋價格和優惠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that someone has written information from a company.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人有來自公司的書面資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"monthly price","meaning":"每月價格","examples":[{"en":"The brochure gives the monthly price for each room.","zh":"小冊子列出每個房間的每月價格。"},{"en":"A monthly price is the amount paid every month.","zh":"monthly price 是每個月支付的金額。"},{"en":"The gym has a monthly price for members who do not want a yearly plan.","zh":"健身室為不想買年費計劃的會員提供每月價格。"},{"en":"Shelley needs the monthly price because she may rent furniture for several months.","zh":"Shelley 需要知道每月價格，因為她可能租用家具幾個月。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people calculate repeated costs.","zh":"這個短語幫助人們計算重複費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"per room","meaning":"每個房間","examples":[{"en":"The price is calculated per room.","zh":"價格是按每個房間計算。"},{"en":"Per room means for each separate room.","zh":"per room 意思是按每一個獨立房間計算。"},{"en":"The hotel charges a cleaning fee per room.","zh":"酒店按每個房間收取清潔費。"},{"en":"If Shelley rents furniture for three rooms, she must count the price for each room.","zh":"如果 Shelley 為三個房間租用家具，她必須計算每個房間的價格。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain how the total cost is worked out.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋總費用如何計算。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"start at","meaning":"由……起","examples":[{"en":"The monthly price per room starts at a hundred and five dollars.","zh":"每個房間的每月價格由 105 元起。"},{"en":"Start at means the lowest price or amount begins from that number.","zh":"start at 意思是最低價格或數量由該數字開始。"},{"en":"Tickets for the concert start at fifty dollars.","zh":"演唱會門票由 50 元起。"},{"en":"Peak Rentals’ prices start at $105, but more expensive rooms cost more.","zh":"Peak Rentals 的價格由 105 元起，但較昂貴房間收費更高。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the minimum price, not the full range.","zh":"這個短語提供最低價格，而不是完整範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"go up to","meaning":"最高達到","examples":[{"en":"The monthly price can go up to two hundred and thirty-nine dollars.","zh":"每月價格最高可達 239 元。"},{"en":"Go up to means reach a highest possible amount.","zh":"go up to 意思是達到最高可能數量。"},{"en":"The temperature can go up to thirty-five degrees in summer.","zh":"夏天氣溫可高達 35 度。"},{"en":"The furniture price can go up to $239 depending on the room and items.","zh":"家具價格可高達 239 元，視乎房間和物品而定。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the upper limit of a range.","zh":"這個短語提供範圍的上限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"取決於","examples":[{"en":"The price depends on which rooms need furniture.","zh":"價格取決於哪些房間需要家具。"},{"en":"Depend on means be affected or decided by something else.","zh":"depend on 意思是受另一件事影響或由它決定。"},{"en":"The travel time depends on traffic.","zh":"旅程時間取決於交通情況。"},{"en":"Shelley’s total cost depends on how many rooms she wants to furnish.","zh":"Shelley 的總費用取決於她想為多少個房間添置家具。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the answer changes with the situation.","zh":"這個短語顯示答案會按情況改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"need furniture for","meaning":"需要為……添置家具","examples":[{"en":"The price depends on which rooms Shelley needs furniture for.","zh":"價格取決於 Shelley 需要為哪些房間添置家具。"},{"en":"To need furniture for a room means to require furniture to make that room usable.","zh":"need furniture for a room 意思是某個房間需要家具才可使用。"},{"en":"A bedroom needs furniture such as a bed, wardrobe, and small table.","zh":"睡房需要床、衣櫃和小桌等家具。"},{"en":"Shelley may need furniture for the living room first because it is used every day.","zh":"Shelley 可能先需要為客廳添置家具，因為每天都會使用。"},{"en":"This phrase connects furniture needs with specific rooms.","zh":"這個短語把家具需要與特定房間連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get a general idea of","meaning":"大概了解……","examples":[{"en":"Shelley wants to get a general idea of the cost.","zh":"Shelley 想大概了解費用。"},{"en":"To get a general idea of something means to understand it roughly, not exactly.","zh":"get a general idea of something 意思是大致理解某事，而不是精確了解。"},{"en":"Before choosing a course, students should get a general idea of the workload.","zh":"選擇課程前，學生應大概了解工作量。"},{"en":"Shelley needs a rough cost before deciding which company to contact.","zh":"Shelley 在決定聯絡哪間公司前，需要知道大概費用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when planning but not yet making a final decision.","zh":"這個短語適合用於計劃階段，而不是最終決定階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"how much it is going to cost","meaning":"會花多少錢","examples":[{"en":"She wants to know how much it is going to cost.","zh":"她想知道會花多少錢。"},{"en":"How much it is going to cost means the amount of money that will be needed.","zh":"how much it is going to cost 意思是將會需要的金額。"},{"en":"Before repairing the car, we asked how much it was going to cost.","zh":"修車前，我們問會花多少錢。"},{"en":"Shelley asks because renting furniture every month can affect her budget.","zh":"Shelley 這樣問，因為每月租家具會影響她的預算。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when someone wants to estimate future spending.","zh":"這個短語用於某人想估計未來開支時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"positive feedback about","meaning":"關於……的正面評價","examples":[{"en":"Shelley says the owner has had positive feedback about the company.","zh":"Shelley 說屋主收到過關於那間公司的正面評價。"},{"en":"Positive feedback about something means good opinions or comments about it.","zh":"positive feedback about something 意思是關於某事的好意見或好評。"},{"en":"The restaurant received positive feedback about its service.","zh":"餐廳收到關於服務的正面評價。"},{"en":"Positive feedback makes Shelley feel the company may be reliable.","zh":"正面評價令 Shelley 覺得那間公司可能可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that other people have responded well.","zh":"這個短語顯示其他人反應良好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"more modern than","meaning":"比……更現代","examples":[{"en":"The furniture from Peak Rentals is more modern than furniture from the other companies.","zh":"Peak Rentals 的家具比其他公司的家具更現代。"},{"en":"More modern than means newer in style, design, or technology compared with something else.","zh":"more modern than 意思是在款式、設計或科技上比另一事物更新。"},{"en":"This apartment looks more modern than the old one because it has simple furniture and bright lighting.","zh":"這間公寓比舊公寓更現代，因為它有簡約家具和明亮燈光。"},{"en":"Shelley may prefer Peak Rentals if she wants stylish furniture.","zh":"如果 Shelley 想要時尚家具，她可能較喜歡 Peak Rentals。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the modern style of two things.","zh":"這個短語比較兩件事物的現代感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"any of the other companies","meaning":"任何其他公司","examples":[{"en":"The furniture is more modern than any of the other companies’ furniture.","zh":"這些家具比任何其他公司的家具都更現代。"},{"en":"Any of the other companies means each company apart from the one being discussed.","zh":"any of the other companies 意思是除了正在討論的公司以外，每一間其他公司。"},{"en":"This shop is cheaper than any of the other shops nearby.","zh":"這間店比附近任何其他店都便宜。"},{"en":"The owner compares Peak Rentals with all the other rental companies.","zh":"屋主把 Peak Rentals 與所有其他租賃公司作比較。"},{"en":"This phrase helps make a strong comparison with a whole group.","zh":"這個短語幫助與整個群組作強烈比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"place an order","meaning":"下單","examples":[{"en":"Once Shelley places an order, the furniture will be delivered quickly.","zh":"Shelley 一下單，家具就會很快送到。"},{"en":"To place an order means to formally request to buy or rent something.","zh":"place an order 意思是正式要求購買或租用某物。"},{"en":"We placed an order for two desks online.","zh":"我們在網上訂購了兩張書桌。"},{"en":"Shelley must place an order before the company can deliver the furniture.","zh":"Shelley 必須先下單，公司才可以送家具。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in shopping, renting, and business services.","zh":"這個短語常用於購物、租賃和商業服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be delivered to someone","meaning":"送到某人那裏","examples":[{"en":"The furniture will be delivered to Shelley in one or two days.","zh":"家具會在一兩天內送到 Shelley 那裏。"},{"en":"Be delivered to someone means be brought or sent to that person.","zh":"be delivered to someone 意思是被送到某人那裏。"},{"en":"The new sofa was delivered to my grandmother yesterday.","zh":"新梳化昨天送到我祖母那裏。"},{"en":"Shelley likes fast delivery because she is moving in soon.","zh":"Shelley 喜歡快速送貨，因為她很快要搬入。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on where or to whom something is sent.","zh":"這個短語著重某物被送到哪裏或送給誰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in just one or two days","meaning":"只需一兩日內","examples":[{"en":"The furniture will be delivered in just one or two days.","zh":"家具只需一兩日內就會送到。"},{"en":"In just one or two days means within a very short time of one or two days.","zh":"in just one or two days 意思是在一兩天這麼短的時間內。"},{"en":"The book arrived in just one or two days after I ordered it.","zh":"我訂書後，那本書只需一兩日內就送到。"},{"en":"Fast delivery is helpful because Shelley needs furniture before moving in.","zh":"快速送貨很有幫助，因為 Shelley 搬入前需要家具。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the service is quick.","zh":"這個短語強調服務很快。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"That would be really helpful","meaning":"那會很有幫助","examples":[{"en":"Shelley says, “That would be really helpful.”","zh":"Shelley 說：「那會很有幫助。」"},{"en":"That would be really helpful means that action or information would help a lot.","zh":"That would be really helpful 意思是那個行動或資料會幫到很多。"},{"en":"If you could send me the address, that would be really helpful.","zh":"如果你能把地址發給我，那會很有幫助。"},{"en":"Shelley says this because fast delivery would make moving easier.","zh":"Shelley 這樣說，因為快速送貨會令搬屋更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase politely shows appreciation before or after receiving help.","zh":"這個短語禮貌地表示感謝某種幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"special offer","meaning":"特別優惠","examples":[{"en":"The brochure says there is a special offer at the moment.","zh":"小冊子說目前有特別優惠。"},{"en":"A special offer is a temporary deal that gives customers a lower price or extra benefit.","zh":"special offer 是暫時性的優惠，給顧客較低價格或額外好處。"},{"en":"The shop has a special offer: buy one notebook and get one free.","zh":"這間店有特別優惠：買一本筆記簿送一本。"},{"en":"Shelley may save money if the furniture package includes a free lamp.","zh":"如果家具套裝包括免費座燈，Shelley 可能可以省錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in advertisements and brochures.","zh":"這個短語常見於廣告和小冊子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at the moment","meaning":"目前；現時","examples":[{"en":"There is a special offer at the moment.","zh":"目前有特別優惠。"},{"en":"At the moment means now or during the present period.","zh":"at the moment 意思是現在或目前這段時間。"},{"en":"The library is closed at the moment because of repairs.","zh":"圖書館目前因維修而關閉。"},{"en":"The offer may not last forever because it is available only now.","zh":"這項優惠可能不會一直持續，因為它只是現時提供。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a situation is current.","zh":"這個短語顯示情況是當前的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"living room furniture","meaning":"客廳家具","examples":[{"en":"If Shelley rents living room furniture, she can get a lamp for free.","zh":"如果 Shelley 租用客廳家具，她可以免費得到一盞燈。"},{"en":"Living room furniture means furniture used in the main room where people relax or receive guests.","zh":"living room furniture 意思是用於人們休息或接待客人的主要房間的家具。"},{"en":"Living room furniture may include a sofa, chairs, a coffee table, and a TV table.","zh":"客廳家具可能包括梳化、椅子、茶几和電視桌。"},{"en":"Shelley may need living room furniture first because guests usually sit there.","zh":"Shelley 可能首先需要客廳家具，因為客人通常坐在那裏。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to furniture for one specific room.","zh":"這個短語指某一特定房間的家具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"I believe that","meaning":"我相信","examples":[{"en":"The owner says, “I believe that’s a set of chairs and a TV table.”","zh":"屋主說：「我相信那是一套椅子和一張電視桌。」"},{"en":"I believe that means I think this is true, though I may not be completely certain.","zh":"I believe that 意思是我認為這是真的，但可能不是完全肯定。"},{"en":"I believe that the office opens at nine, but we should check.","zh":"我相信辦公室九點開門，但我們應該查一查。"},{"en":"The owner uses this phrase because he is reading or remembering details from the brochure.","zh":"屋主使用這個短語，因為他正在閱讀或回想小冊子的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase gives information in a careful way.","zh":"這個短語以謹慎方式提供資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a set of chairs","meaning":"一套椅子","examples":[{"en":"The living room furniture includes a set of chairs.","zh":"客廳家具包括一套椅子。"},{"en":"A set of chairs means several chairs that belong together or match.","zh":"a set of chairs 意思是幾張屬於同一組或互相配襯的椅子。"},{"en":"The dining room has a table and a set of chairs.","zh":"飯廳有一張桌子和一套椅子。"},{"en":"A matching set of chairs can make a room look organised.","zh":"配套的一套椅子可以令房間看起來更整齊。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to more than one chair sold or rented together.","zh":"這個短語通常指一起出售或出租的不止一張椅子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a TV table","meaning":"電視桌","examples":[{"en":"The living room set includes a TV table.","zh":"客廳套裝包括一張電視桌。"},{"en":"A TV table is a small table or stand used to hold a television.","zh":"TV table 是用來放電視的小桌或架。"},{"en":"The family placed the TV table opposite the sofa.","zh":"那家人把電視桌放在梳化對面。"},{"en":"Shelley may need a TV table if she wants to set up the living room properly.","zh":"如果 Shelley 想好好布置客廳，她可能需要電視桌。"},{"en":"This phrase names a piece of furniture with a specific use.","zh":"這個短語指出一件有特定用途的家具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at no extra cost","meaning":"無需額外收費","examples":[{"en":"Shelley can get a lamp at no extra cost.","zh":"Shelley 可以無需額外收費得到一盞燈。"},{"en":"At no extra cost means without paying more money.","zh":"at no extra cost 意思是不需要支付更多錢。"},{"en":"The hotel provides breakfast at no extra cost.","zh":"酒店無需額外收費提供早餐。"},{"en":"The free lamp makes the offer more attractive to Shelley.","zh":"免費座燈令這項優惠對 Shelley 更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when something is included in the original price.","zh":"這個短語用於某物已包含在原本價格中時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"price range","meaning":"價格範圍","examples":[{"en":"The price range is more than Shelley was hoping to pay.","zh":"這個價格範圍比 Shelley 原本希望支付的更多。"},{"en":"A price range is the lowest and highest possible price for something.","zh":"price range 是某物可能的最低和最高價格。"},{"en":"The phone’s price range is from $800 to $1200.","zh":"這部手機的價格範圍是 800 至 1200 元。"},{"en":"Shelley checks the price range to see whether the company fits her budget.","zh":"Shelley 查看價格範圍，看看那間公司是否符合她的預算。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people understand possible costs before choosing.","zh":"這個短語幫助人們在選擇前了解可能費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"more than I was hoping to pay","meaning":"比我原本希望支付的更多","examples":[{"en":"The price range is more than Shelley was hoping to pay.","zh":"這個價格範圍比 Shelley 原本希望支付的更多。"},{"en":"More than I was hoping to pay means the cost is higher than my expected budget.","zh":"more than I was hoping to pay 意思是費用高於我的預期預算。"},{"en":"The hotel was more than I was hoping to pay, so I chose a cheaper one.","zh":"那間酒店比我原本希望支付的更多，所以我選了較便宜的一間。"},{"en":"Shelley says this because Peak Rentals may be too expensive for her.","zh":"Shelley 這樣說，因為 Peak Rentals 對她來說可能太貴。"},{"en":"This phrase politely expresses that something costs too much.","zh":"這個短語禮貌地表示某物太昂貴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"try another company","meaning":"試試另一間公司","examples":[{"en":"The owner suggests that Shelley could try another company.","zh":"屋主建議 Shelley 可以試試另一間公司。"},{"en":"To try another company means to consider or contact a different business.","zh":"try another company 意思是考慮或聯絡另一間公司。"},{"en":"If one repair shop is too expensive, you can try another company.","zh":"如果一間維修店太貴，你可以試試另一間公司。"},{"en":"Shelley may try another company because Peak Rentals costs more than she hoped.","zh":"Shelley 可能會試試另一間公司，因為 Peak Rentals 的費用比她預期高。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests looking for a better or cheaper option.","zh":"這個短語建議尋找更好或更便宜的選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"double A","meaning":"兩個 A","examples":[{"en":"The name Aaron is spelled with double A.","zh":"Aaron 這個名字用兩個 A 拼寫。"},{"en":"Double A means two letter As together or two As in a word.","zh":"double A 意思是兩個 A 字母連在一起，或一個字裏有兩個 A。"},{"en":"The name Aaliyah starts with double A.","zh":"Aaliyah 這個名字以兩個 A 開頭。"},{"en":"The owner explains the spelling so Shelley can write the company name correctly.","zh":"屋主解釋拼寫，讓 Shelley 正確寫下公司名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when spelling names aloud.","zh":"這個短語在口頭拼寫名稱時很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mid-price company","meaning":"中等價位的公司","examples":[{"en":"Aaron and Oliver is a mid-price company.","zh":"Aaron and Oliver 是一間中等價位的公司。"},{"en":"A mid-price company charges prices that are neither very cheap nor very expensive.","zh":"mid-price company 是收費既不很便宜也不很昂貴的公司。"},{"en":"A mid-price restaurant may cost more than fast food but less than a luxury restaurant.","zh":"中等價位餐廳可能比快餐貴，但比高級餐廳便宜。"},{"en":"Shelley may consider a mid-price company if Peak Rentals is too expensive.","zh":"如果 Peak Rentals 太貴，Shelley 可能會考慮中等價位的公司。"},{"en":"This phrase places a company in the middle of a price range.","zh":"這個短語把公司放在價格範圍的中間位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"choose them","meaning":"選擇他們","examples":[{"en":"If Shelley chooses Aaron and Oliver, she needs to consider the extra fee.","zh":"如果 Shelley 選擇 Aaron and Oliver，她需要考慮額外費用。"},{"en":"To choose them means to select that company or group from the available options.","zh":"choose them 意思是從可用選項中選擇那間公司或那群人。"},{"en":"We compared three hotels and chose the cheapest one.","zh":"我們比較了三間酒店，並選擇最便宜的一間。"},{"en":"Shelley should check all fees before she chooses them.","zh":"Shelley 在選擇他們前應查看所有費用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to making a decision among several choices.","zh":"這個短語指在幾個選擇中作決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be aware that","meaning":"要注意","examples":[{"en":"Shelley needs to be aware that they charge an extra fee.","zh":"Shelley 需要注意他們會收取額外費用。"},{"en":"To be aware that means to know or realise an important fact.","zh":"be aware that 意思是知道或意識到一個重要事實。"},{"en":"Visitors should be aware that the museum closes early on Mondays.","zh":"遊客應注意博物館逢星期一較早關門。"},{"en":"Shelley must know about the extra fee before signing a rental agreement.","zh":"Shelley 在簽租賃協議前必須知道額外費用。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to warn someone about a detail.","zh":"這個短語常用來提醒某人注意細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"charge an extra twelve per cent","meaning":"額外收取百分之十二","examples":[{"en":"They charge an extra twelve per cent every month.","zh":"他們每月額外收取百分之十二。"},{"en":"To charge an extra twelve per cent means to add twelve per cent to the normal price.","zh":"charge an extra twelve per cent 意思是在正常價格之外加收百分之十二。"},{"en":"Some hotels charge an extra ten per cent for service.","zh":"有些酒店額外收取百分之十服務費。"},{"en":"The fee increases Shelley’s total monthly cost.","zh":"這項費用會增加 Shelley 的每月總支出。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an added charge beyond the basic price.","zh":"這個短語顯示基本價格以外的額外收費。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"every month","meaning":"每月","examples":[{"en":"The extra fee is charged every month.","zh":"額外費用每月收取。"},{"en":"Every month means once each month or in each month.","zh":"every month 意思是每個月一次或在每個月中。"},{"en":"I pay my phone bill every month.","zh":"我每月支付電話費。"},{"en":"Shelley must include the extra fee in her monthly budget.","zh":"Shelley 必須把額外費用包括在每月預算中。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a cost or action repeats regularly.","zh":"這個短語顯示費用或行動定期重複。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in case of damage","meaning":"以防損壞","examples":[{"en":"The extra fee is charged in case of damage.","zh":"額外費用是以防損壞而收取的。"},{"en":"In case of damage means to cover or prepare for possible harm to the furniture.","zh":"in case of damage 意思是為可能對家具造成的損害作保障或準備。"},{"en":"A deposit may be kept in case of damage to a hotel room.","zh":"酒店可能保留按金，以防房間損壞。"},{"en":"The company charges extra because rented furniture might be broken or scratched.","zh":"公司額外收費，因為租用家具可能被弄壞或刮花。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the reason for protection or insurance.","zh":"這個短語解釋保障或保險的原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"do the math carefully","meaning":"仔細計算","examples":[{"en":"Shelley would have to do the math carefully.","zh":"Shelley 必須仔細計算。"},{"en":"To do the math carefully means to calculate the total cost with attention.","zh":"do the math carefully 意思是小心計算總費用。"},{"en":"Before buying a phone plan, do the math carefully and include all fees.","zh":"購買電話計劃前，要仔細計算並包括所有費用。"},{"en":"Shelley needs to add the monthly price and the extra twelve per cent fee.","zh":"Shelley 需要把每月價格和額外百分之十二費用加起來。"},{"en":"This phrase warns someone to check the numbers before deciding.","zh":"這個短語提醒某人在決定前核對數字。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"one helpful thing","meaning":"一個方便之處","examples":[{"en":"One helpful thing is that the company also does cleaning.","zh":"一個方便之處是那間公司也提供清潔服務。"},{"en":"One helpful thing means one useful advantage or detail.","zh":"one helpful thing 意思是一個有用的優點或細節。"},{"en":"One helpful thing about this flat is that it is near the station.","zh":"這個單位的一個方便之處是它靠近車站。"},{"en":"The cleaning service may help customers who are too busy to clean.","zh":"清潔服務可能幫助太忙而無法清潔的顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a positive point after other information.","zh":"這個短語在其他資料後引入一個正面重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"do cleaning for customers","meaning":"為顧客提供清潔服務","examples":[{"en":"Aaron and Oliver also do cleaning for customers.","zh":"Aaron and Oliver 也為顧客提供清潔服務。"},{"en":"To do cleaning for customers means to provide a service that cleans their homes or furniture.","zh":"do cleaning for customers 意思是提供清潔家居或家具的服務。"},{"en":"Some moving companies do cleaning for customers after they leave a flat.","zh":"有些搬屋公司會在顧客搬離單位後提供清潔服務。"},{"en":"Aaron and Oliver may be useful for people who want furniture and cleaning from one company.","zh":"如果人們想同一間公司提供家具和清潔，Aaron and Oliver 可能很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical customer service.","zh":"這個短語描述一種實用顧客服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cleaning service","meaning":"清潔服務","examples":[{"en":"Aaron and Oliver offers a cleaning service.","zh":"Aaron and Oliver 提供清潔服務。"},{"en":"A cleaning service is a paid service where people clean a home, office, or furniture.","zh":"清潔服務是由人清潔家居、辦公室或家具的收費服務。"},{"en":"A busy family may use a cleaning service once a week.","zh":"忙碌家庭可能每星期使用一次清潔服務。"},{"en":"Shelley probably does not need this service because she only asks about furniture.","zh":"Shelley 大概不需要這項服務，因為她只是詢問家具。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to cleaning done professionally for customers.","zh":"這個短語指為顧客專業提供的清潔工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"probably won’t need that","meaning":"大概不需要那個","examples":[{"en":"Shelley says she probably won’t need the cleaning service.","zh":"Shelley 說她大概不需要清潔服務。"},{"en":"Probably won’t need that means it is unlikely that the thing will be necessary.","zh":"probably won’t need that 意思是那件事物很可能沒有必要。"},{"en":"I probably won’t need a taxi because the station is nearby.","zh":"我大概不需要的士，因為車站很近。"},{"en":"Shelley says this because her main problem is furniture, not cleaning.","zh":"Shelley 這樣說，因為她的主要問題是家具，而不是清潔。"},{"en":"This phrase politely refuses or lowers interest in an extra service.","zh":"這個短語禮貌地拒絕或降低對額外服務的興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"quite new","meaning":"相當新","examples":[{"en":"Larch Furniture is quite new.","zh":"Larch Furniture 相當新。"},{"en":"Quite new means fairly recent or not long established.","zh":"quite new 意思是較近期出現或成立時間不長。"},{"en":"The café is quite new, so many people have not tried it yet.","zh":"這間咖啡店相當新，所以很多人還未試過。"},{"en":"Larch Furniture may not have a long history, but it offers low prices.","zh":"Larch Furniture 可能歷史不長，但提供低價格。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something has not existed for a long time.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事物存在時間不久。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the lowest prices in town","meaning":"城中最低價格","examples":[{"en":"Larch Furniture has the lowest prices in town.","zh":"Larch Furniture 有城中最低價格。"},{"en":"The lowest prices in town means cheaper prices than other local companies.","zh":"the lowest prices in town 意思是比本地其他公司更便宜的價格。"},{"en":"A shop may advertise the lowest prices in town to attract customers.","zh":"商店可能用城中最低價格來吸引顧客。"},{"en":"Shelley may like Larch Furniture because she wants to control costs.","zh":"Shelley 可能喜歡 Larch Furniture，因為她想控制開支。"},{"en":"This phrase compares prices within the same city or area.","zh":"這個短語比較同一城市或地區內的價格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"both furniture and electronic equipment","meaning":"家具和電子設備兩方面","examples":[{"en":"The lowest prices apply to both furniture and electronic equipment.","zh":"最低價格適用於家具和電子設備兩方面。"},{"en":"Both furniture and electronic equipment means the two categories are included together.","zh":"both furniture and electronic equipment 意思是兩個類別都包括在內。"},{"en":"A rental shop may offer both furniture and electronic equipment for new tenants.","zh":"租賃店可能為新租客提供家具和電子設備兩方面的租用服務。"},{"en":"Shelley may need both because she is bringing very few things with her.","zh":"Shelley 可能兩者都需要，因為她帶來的東西很少。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly includes two different kinds of items.","zh":"這個短語清楚包括兩種不同物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"electronic equipment","meaning":"電子設備","examples":[{"en":"Larch Furniture rents out electronic equipment as well as furniture.","zh":"Larch Furniture 除了家具外，也出租電子設備。"},{"en":"Electronic equipment means devices that use electricity, such as TVs, microwaves, or computers.","zh":"electronic equipment 意思是使用電力的設備，例如電視、微波爐或電腦。"},{"en":"A new tenant may rent electronic equipment if they do not own a television.","zh":"如果新租客沒有電視，可能會租用電子設備。"},{"en":"Shelley may need electronic equipment because she is not bringing much with her.","zh":"Shelley 可能需要電子設備，因為她沒有帶很多東西過來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to useful electrical devices, not ordinary furniture.","zh":"這個短語指有用的電器裝置，而不是普通家具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"bring much with me","meaning":"帶很多東西過來","examples":[{"en":"Shelley is not bringing much with her.","zh":"Shelley 沒有帶很多東西過來。"},{"en":"To not bring much with me means to take only a small number of belongings when moving or travelling.","zh":"not bring much with me 意思是在搬屋或旅行時只帶少量個人物品。"},{"en":"I did not bring much with me because the trip was only two days.","zh":"我沒有帶很多東西過來，因為旅程只有兩天。"},{"en":"Shelley needs rentals because she does not have many household items with her.","zh":"Shelley 需要租用服務，因為她身邊沒有很多家居物品。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why someone may need to buy or rent things later.","zh":"這個短語解釋為甚麼某人之後可能需要購買或租用東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have much time to","meaning":"有很多時間去……","examples":[{"en":"Shelley will not have much time to go shopping after she starts her job.","zh":"Shelley 開始工作後不會有很多時間去購物。"},{"en":"To not have much time to do something means to have little free time for it.","zh":"not have much time to do something 意思是沒有很多空閒時間做某事。"},{"en":"Students may not have much time to relax during exam week.","zh":"考試週期間，學生可能沒有很多時間去放鬆。"},{"en":"Shelley wants to arrange furniture early because work will make her busy.","zh":"Shelley 想提早安排家具，因為工作會令她忙碌。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why someone wants a quick or convenient solution.","zh":"這個短語解釋為甚麼某人想要快速或方便的解決方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go shopping","meaning":"去購物","examples":[{"en":"Shelley will not have much time to go shopping.","zh":"Shelley 不會有很多時間去購物。"},{"en":"To go shopping means to visit shops or websites to buy things.","zh":"go shopping 意思是到商店或網站購買東西。"},{"en":"We went shopping for school supplies before the new term.","zh":"新學期前，我們去購物買學校用品。"},{"en":"Shelley may rent items because she will be too busy to shop for furniture.","zh":"Shelley 可能會租用物品，因為她會太忙而沒時間買家具。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to buying things, not just walking around shops.","zh":"這個短語指購買東西，而不只是逛商店。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"after I start my job","meaning":"開始工作後","examples":[{"en":"Shelley will be busy after she starts her job.","zh":"Shelley 開始工作後會很忙。"},{"en":"After I start my job means after I begin working in my new position.","zh":"after I start my job 意思是在我開始新職位工作之後。"},{"en":"After I start my job, I may have less time to visit friends.","zh":"開始工作後，我可能較少時間探朋友。"},{"en":"Shelley wants to prepare the house before her work routine begins.","zh":"Shelley 想在工作日程開始前準備好房子。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a time after a new job begins.","zh":"這個短語設定新工作開始後的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"things you need to know about","meaning":"需要知道的事情","examples":[{"en":"There are two things Shelley needs to know about Larch Furniture.","zh":"Shelley 有兩件關於 Larch Furniture 需要知道的事情。"},{"en":"Things you need to know about something are important details you should understand before deciding.","zh":"things you need to know about something 是你在決定前應了解的重要細節。"},{"en":"There are three things you need to know about this course before you enrol.","zh":"報讀這個課程前，你有三件需要知道的事情。"},{"en":"The owner warns Shelley about insurance and contract length.","zh":"屋主提醒 Shelley 關於保險和合約期的事。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces important information that may affect a choice.","zh":"這個短語引入可能影響選擇的重要資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"first of all","meaning":"首先","examples":[{"en":"First of all, Shelley has to take out insurance.","zh":"首先，Shelley 必須購買保險。"},{"en":"First of all means the first point or action to mention.","zh":"first of all 意思是首先要提到的重點或行動。"},{"en":"First of all, check the address before you leave.","zh":"首先，離開前先檢查地址。"},{"en":"The owner uses this phrase before explaining the first condition.","zh":"屋主在解釋第一個條件前使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise information in order.","zh":"這個短語幫助按次序組織資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take out insurance on","meaning":"為……購買保險","examples":[{"en":"Shelley has to take out insurance on the furniture.","zh":"Shelley 必須為家具購買保險。"},{"en":"To take out insurance on something means to buy insurance to protect it against loss or damage.","zh":"take out insurance on something 意思是為某物購買保險，以防遺失或損壞。"},{"en":"A driver must take out insurance on a car before using it on the road.","zh":"司機在路上駕駛汽車前必須為汽車購買保險。"},{"en":"Shelley needs insurance because rented furniture could be damaged.","zh":"Shelley 需要保險，因為租用家具可能會損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when protecting valuable property.","zh":"這個短語常用於保護有價值財物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"organise that yourself","meaning":"自己安排那件事","examples":[{"en":"Shelley needs to organise the insurance herself.","zh":"Shelley 需要自己安排保險。"},{"en":"To organise that yourself means to arrange it without the company doing it for you.","zh":"organise that yourself 意思是自己安排那件事，而不是由公司代辦。"},{"en":"If the school does not book transport, parents must organise that themselves.","zh":"如果學校不預訂交通，家長就必須自己安排。"},{"en":"Larch Furniture requires Shelley to arrange her own insurance.","zh":"Larch Furniture 要求 Shelley 自行安排保險。"},{"en":"This phrase makes clear who is responsible for the arrangement.","zh":"這個短語清楚說明誰負責安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"That wouldn’t be too hard","meaning":"那應該不會太難","examples":[{"en":"Shelley says that arranging insurance would not be too hard.","zh":"Shelley 說安排保險應該不會太難。"},{"en":"That wouldn’t be too hard means that task would probably not be very difficult.","zh":"That wouldn’t be too hard 意思是那項任務大概不會很困難。"},{"en":"Filling in the online form would not be too hard if the instructions are clear.","zh":"如果指示清楚，填寫網上表格應該不會太難。"},{"en":"Shelley thinks she can arrange insurance without much trouble.","zh":"Shelley 認為自己可以不太麻煩地安排保險。"},{"en":"This phrase shows mild confidence about a task.","zh":"這個短語表示對任務有輕微信心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"take out a contract","meaning":"簽訂合約","examples":[{"en":"Shelley cannot take out a contract for less than six months.","zh":"Shelley 不能簽訂少於六個月的合約。"},{"en":"To take out a contract means to formally agree to a service for a period of time.","zh":"take out a contract 意思是正式同意在一段時間內使用某項服務。"},{"en":"Many people take out a phone contract for one or two years.","zh":"很多人會簽訂一至兩年的電話合約。"},{"en":"Shelley must accept a contract if she wants to rent from Larch Furniture.","zh":"如果 Shelley 想向 Larch Furniture 租用，她必須接受合約。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for formal service agreements.","zh":"這個短語用於正式服務協議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"for less than six months","meaning":"少於六個月","examples":[{"en":"Larch Furniture does not offer contracts for less than six months.","zh":"Larch Furniture 不提供少於六個月的合約。"},{"en":"For less than six months means for a period shorter than six months.","zh":"for less than six months 意思是為期短於六個月。"},{"en":"The landlord will not rent the flat for less than six months.","zh":"業主不會把單位出租少於六個月。"},{"en":"Shelley must decide whether a six-month commitment is acceptable.","zh":"Shelley 必須決定六個月承諾是否可以接受。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a minimum length of time.","zh":"這個短語設定最低時間長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"I figure that","meaning":"我估計；我想","examples":[{"en":"The owner figures that the six-month minimum may not be a problem.","zh":"屋主估計六個月的最低合約期可能不是問題。"},{"en":"I figure that means I think or reason that something is probably true.","zh":"I figure that 意思是我認為或推斷某事大概是真的。"},{"en":"I figure that we should leave early because traffic will be heavy.","zh":"我想我們應該早點離開，因為交通會很擠塞。"},{"en":"The owner figures this because Shelley is renting the house for twelve months.","zh":"屋主這樣估計，因為 Shelley 租住房子十二個月。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and shows a logical guess.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，表示合乎邏輯的推測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"might not be a problem","meaning":"可能不是問題","examples":[{"en":"The minimum contract length might not be a problem for Shelley.","zh":"最短合約期對 Shelley 來說可能不是問題。"},{"en":"Might not be a problem means something may be acceptable or not cause difficulty.","zh":"might not be a problem 意思是某事可能可以接受或不會造成困難。"},{"en":"A later meeting time might not be a problem if everyone is free.","zh":"如果大家都有空，較遲的會議時間可能不是問題。"},{"en":"Since Shelley is renting for a year, a six-month contract may suit her.","zh":"由於 Shelley 會租住一年，六個月合約可能適合她。"},{"en":"This phrase shows possibility, not certainty.","zh":"這個短語表示可能性，而不是肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"after all","meaning":"畢竟","examples":[{"en":"Shelley is renting the house for twelve months after all.","zh":"畢竟 Shelley 會租住房子十二個月。"},{"en":"After all is used to give a reason that supports what has just been said.","zh":"after all 用來給出支持剛才說法的原因。"},{"en":"We can walk there; after all, it is only five minutes away.","zh":"我們可以走路去；畢竟那裏只有五分鐘路程。"},{"en":"The owner says this because a six-month contract is short compared with Shelley’s one-year rental.","zh":"屋主這樣說，因為六個月合約相對 Shelley 一年租期來說不算長。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain why an idea makes sense.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋為何某個想法合理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sorry to interrupt","meaning":"抱歉打斷你","examples":[{"en":"The owner says, “Sorry to interrupt,” before mentioning another company.","zh":"屋主在提到另一間公司前說：「抱歉打斷你。」"},{"en":"Sorry to interrupt is used when you politely stop someone while they are speaking.","zh":"sorry to interrupt 用於你禮貌地在某人說話時打斷對方。"},{"en":"Sorry to interrupt, but the phone is ringing.","zh":"抱歉打斷你，但電話在響。"},{"en":"The owner says this because he suddenly remembers another company.","zh":"屋主這樣說，因為他突然想起另一間公司。"},{"en":"This phrase helps make an interruption sound polite.","zh":"這個短語令打斷別人聽起來較有禮貌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"I just thought of","meaning":"我剛想到","examples":[{"en":"The owner has just thought of another furniture rental company.","zh":"屋主剛想到另一間家具租賃公司。"},{"en":"I just thought of means I have suddenly remembered or had an idea.","zh":"I just thought of 意思是我剛剛突然記起或想到一個想法。"},{"en":"I just thought of a better place for lunch.","zh":"我剛想到一個更好的午餐地方。"},{"en":"The owner uses this phrase because Space Rentals suddenly comes to mind.","zh":"屋主使用這個短語，因為 Space Rentals 突然浮現在腦海中。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a new idea that appears during conversation.","zh":"這個短語引入對話中突然出現的新想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"another furniture rental company","meaning":"另一間家具租賃公司","examples":[{"en":"The owner mentions another furniture rental company called Space Rentals.","zh":"屋主提到另一間名為 Space Rentals 的家具租賃公司。"},{"en":"Another furniture rental company means one more business that rents furniture.","zh":"another furniture rental company 意思是另一間出租家具的公司。"},{"en":"If the first shop is too expensive, you can ask about another furniture rental company.","zh":"如果第一間店太貴，你可以詢問另一間家具租賃公司。"},{"en":"Space Rentals gives Shelley one more option to compare.","zh":"Space Rentals 給 Shelley 多一個可比較的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase adds an extra company to the list of choices.","zh":"這個短語把額外公司加入選擇清單中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be located very near to","meaning":"位於離……很近的地方","examples":[{"en":"Space Rentals is located very near to the house.","zh":"Space Rentals 位於離那間房子很近的地方。"},{"en":"To be located very near to something means to be placed close to it.","zh":"be located very near to something 意思是位於靠近某物的地方。"},{"en":"The supermarket is located very near to the station.","zh":"超級市場位於離車站很近的地方。"},{"en":"Space Rentals may be convenient because it is close to Shelley’s new home.","zh":"Space Rentals 可能很方便，因為它靠近 Shelley 的新家。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a useful nearby location.","zh":"這個短語描述有用的鄰近位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"information about their charges","meaning":"關於他們收費的資料","examples":[{"en":"The owner does not have information about their charges.","zh":"屋主沒有關於他們收費的資料。"},{"en":"Information about their charges means details about how much they ask customers to pay.","zh":"information about their charges 意思是關於他們向顧客收多少錢的細節。"},{"en":"Before joining the gym, I asked for information about their charges.","zh":"加入健身室前，我詢問了關於他們收費的資料。"},{"en":"Shelley needs this information to compare Space Rentals with other companies.","zh":"Shelley 需要這些資料來比較 Space Rentals 與其他公司。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to price details, not general company information.","zh":"這個短語指價格細節，而不是一般公司資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"it’s best to","meaning":"最好","examples":[{"en":"It is best to use their app to find out the cost.","zh":"最好使用他們的應用程式查明費用。"},{"en":"It’s best to means the recommended or most sensible action is to do something.","zh":"it’s best to 意思是最建議或最明智的做法是做某事。"},{"en":"It’s best to check the timetable before leaving home.","zh":"離家前最好查看時間表。"},{"en":"The owner suggests the app because it gives the latest prices.","zh":"屋主建議使用應用程式，因為它提供最新價格。"},{"en":"This phrase gives practical advice.","zh":"這個短語給出實用建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"use their app","meaning":"使用他們的應用程式","examples":[{"en":"Shelley should use their app to check the prices.","zh":"Shelley 應使用他們的應用程式查看價格。"},{"en":"To use their app means to open and operate the company’s mobile application.","zh":"use their app 意思是打開並操作那間公司的手機應用程式。"},{"en":"Customers use the shop’s app to check delivery times.","zh":"顧客使用商店的應用程式查看送貨時間。"},{"en":"Shelley can use the app because the owner does not know Space Rentals’ charges.","zh":"Shelley 可以使用應用程式，因為屋主不知道 Space Rentals 的收費。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to getting information through a digital tool.","zh":"這個短語指透過數碼工具取得資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"find out","meaning":"查明；找出","examples":[{"en":"Shelley can use the app to find out the cost.","zh":"Shelley 可以使用應用程式查明費用。"},{"en":"To find out means to discover or learn information.","zh":"find out 意思是發現或得知資料。"},{"en":"We checked the website to find out when the museum opens.","zh":"我們查看網站以找出博物館何時開放。"},{"en":"Shelley uses the app to learn the exact price for her situation.","zh":"Shelley 使用應用程式來得知她情況下的準確價格。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone does not yet know the answer.","zh":"當某人尚未知答案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"what it would cost you","meaning":"會花你多少錢","examples":[{"en":"The app shows what it would cost Shelley to use Space Rentals.","zh":"應用程式會顯示 Shelley 使用 Space Rentals 會花多少錢。"},{"en":"What it would cost you means the amount you personally would need to pay.","zh":"what it would cost you 意思是你個人需要支付的金額。"},{"en":"The website can show what it would cost you to insure your phone.","zh":"網站可以顯示為手機購買保險會花你多少錢。"},{"en":"The app may calculate Shelley’s cost based on the furniture she chooses.","zh":"應用程式可能根據 Shelley 選擇的家具計算她的費用。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a personalised price estimate.","zh":"這個短語提供個人化價格估算。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one good thing about","meaning":"……的一個好處","examples":[{"en":"One good thing about Space Rentals is that exchanges are allowed.","zh":"Space Rentals 的一個好處是可以更換家具。"},{"en":"One good thing about something means one positive point or advantage.","zh":"one good thing about something 意思是某事的一個正面重點或優點。"},{"en":"One good thing about this flat is that it is close to the bus stop.","zh":"這個單位的一個好處是靠近巴士站。"},{"en":"Space Rentals has an advantage because customers can change furniture they dislike.","zh":"Space Rentals 有一個優點，因為顧客可以更換不喜歡的家具。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a benefit after discussing a company or idea.","zh":"這個短語在討論公司或想法後引入好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"once it is delivered","meaning":"一送到之後","examples":[{"en":"Shelley can request an exchange once the furniture is delivered.","zh":"家具一送到之後，Shelley 可以要求更換。"},{"en":"Once it is delivered means after it has been brought to the customer.","zh":"once it is delivered 意思是在它被送到顧客那裏之後。"},{"en":"Once the package is delivered, you should check whether anything is broken.","zh":"包裹一送到之後，你應檢查是否有東西損壞。"},{"en":"Shelley can decide whether she likes the furniture after seeing it in the house.","zh":"Shelley 可以在家裏看到家具後，決定自己是否喜歡。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one action happens after delivery.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個行動在送貨後發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"request exchanges","meaning":"要求更換","examples":[{"en":"Shelley can request exchanges if she does not like the furniture.","zh":"如果 Shelley 不喜歡家具，她可以要求更換。"},{"en":"To request exchanges means to ask formally to replace items with different ones.","zh":"request exchanges 意思是正式要求以不同物品替換原本物品。"},{"en":"Customers can request exchanges if clothes are the wrong size.","zh":"如果衣服尺碼不對，顧客可以要求更換。"},{"en":"Shelley may request exchanges if the furniture does not fit the room.","zh":"如果家具不適合房間，Shelley 可能要求更換。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in shopping and rental services.","zh":"這個短語常用於購物和租賃服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as long as","meaning":"只要","examples":[{"en":"She can request exchanges as long as she does it within a week.","zh":"只要她在一星期內提出，她就可以要求更換。"},{"en":"As long as means only if a condition is met.","zh":"as long as 意思是只在某條件達成時。"},{"en":"You can borrow the book as long as you return it by Friday.","zh":"只要你星期五前歸還，就可以借這本書。"},{"en":"Shelley can exchange the furniture only if she asks within the allowed time.","zh":"Shelley 只有在允許時間內提出，才可以更換家具。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a condition or rule.","zh":"這個短語引入條件或規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"within a week of receiving it","meaning":"收到後一星期內","examples":[{"en":"She must request exchanges within a week of receiving the furniture.","zh":"她必須在收到家具後一星期內要求更換。"},{"en":"Within a week of receiving it means no later than seven days after getting it.","zh":"within a week of receiving it 意思是在收到它後不遲於七天內。"},{"en":"Customers must report damage within a week of receiving the product.","zh":"顧客必須在收到產品後一星期內報告損壞。"},{"en":"Shelley should inspect the furniture quickly after delivery.","zh":"Shelley 應在送貨後盡快檢查家具。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a deadline after an item arrives.","zh":"這個短語設定物品到達後的截止時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"thanks very much","meaning":"非常感謝","examples":[{"en":"Shelley says, “Thanks very much,” at the end of the call.","zh":"Shelley 在通話結束時說：「非常感謝。」"},{"en":"Thanks very much is a polite way to express strong thanks.","zh":"thanks very much 是表達強烈感謝的禮貌說法。"},{"en":"Thanks very much for explaining the bus route to me.","zh":"非常感謝你向我解釋巴士路線。"},{"en":"Shelley says this because the owner has given her useful information.","zh":"Shelley 這樣說，因為屋主給了她有用資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is common at the end of helpful conversations.","zh":"這個短語常用於有幫助的對話結束時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"That’s so helpful","meaning":"這太有幫助了","examples":[{"en":"Shelley says the information is so helpful.","zh":"Shelley 說那些資料太有幫助了。"},{"en":"That’s so helpful means that information or action helps a lot.","zh":"That’s so helpful 意思是那些資料或行動幫助很大。"},{"en":"Your map is so helpful because I do not know this area.","zh":"你的地圖太有幫助了，因為我不熟悉這區。"},{"en":"Shelley says this because the owner’s advice makes choosing furniture easier.","zh":"Shelley 這樣說，因為屋主的建議令選擇家具更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase shows appreciation for useful support.","zh":"這個短語表達對有用支援的感謝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"information about costs","meaning":"關於費用的資料","examples":[{"en":"The table gives information about costs for each company.","zh":"表格提供每間公司關於費用的資料。"},{"en":"Information about costs means details about prices, fees, and possible payments.","zh":"information about costs 意思是關於價格、收費和可能付款的細節。"},{"en":"A travel website gives information about costs for hotels and transport.","zh":"旅遊網站提供關於酒店和交通費用的資料。"},{"en":"Shelley needs cost information to compare rental companies fairly.","zh":"Shelley 需要費用資料，才能公平比較租賃公司。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on money-related details.","zh":"這個短語著重與金錢有關的細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"additional notes","meaning":"附加資料；補充說明","examples":[{"en":"The table includes additional notes about delivery, cleaning and contracts.","zh":"表格包括關於送貨、清潔和合約的附加資料。"},{"en":"Additional notes are extra pieces of information added after the main details.","zh":"additional notes 是在主要細節後加入的額外資料。"},{"en":"The form has additional notes explaining how to pay the fee.","zh":"表格有補充說明，解釋如何付款。"},{"en":"These notes help Shelley notice conditions that are not just about price.","zh":"這些資料幫助 Shelley 注意到不只是價格的條件。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to useful extra comments or reminders.","zh":"這個短語指有用的額外評論或提醒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"prices range from","meaning":"價格由……至……不等","examples":[{"en":"Peak Rentals’ prices range from $105 to $239 per room per month.","zh":"Peak Rentals 的價格由每個房間每月 105 元至 239 元不等。"},{"en":"Prices range from one amount to another means the lowest price and highest price are given.","zh":"prices range from 一個金額 to 另一個金額 意思是給出最低和最高價格。"},{"en":"Tickets range from $50 to $200 depending on the seat.","zh":"門票視乎座位由 50 元至 200 元不等。"},{"en":"Shelley can use the range to estimate the cheapest and most expensive possibilities.","zh":"Shelley 可以使用這個範圍估計最便宜和最昂貴的可能情況。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when prices are not all the same.","zh":"當價格不完全相同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"per room per month","meaning":"每個房間每月","examples":[{"en":"The furniture rental price is given per room per month.","zh":"家具租賃價格以每個房間每月計算。"},{"en":"Per room per month means for each room during each month.","zh":"per room per month 意思是每個房間在每個月的費用。"},{"en":"The cleaning service costs $80 per room per month.","zh":"清潔服務每個房間每月收費 80 元。"},{"en":"Shelley must multiply the price by the number of rooms and months.","zh":"Shelley 必須把價格乘以房間數量和月份數量。"},{"en":"This phrase explains exactly how recurring costs are calculated.","zh":"這個短語準確解釋重複費用如何計算。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deliver in 1–2 days","meaning":"一至兩日內送貨","examples":[{"en":"Peak Rentals delivers in 1–2 days.","zh":"Peak Rentals 一至兩日內送貨。"},{"en":"To deliver in 1–2 days means to bring items to the customer within one or two days.","zh":"deliver in 1–2 days 意思是在一至兩天內把物品送到顧客那裏。"},{"en":"The online shop delivers in 1–2 days if the item is in stock.","zh":"如果有存貨，網店會在一至兩日內送貨。"},{"en":"This fast delivery may help Shelley prepare the house before moving in.","zh":"這種快速送貨可能幫助 Shelley 在搬入前準備好房子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a short delivery time.","zh":"這個短語描述較短的送貨時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"living room set","meaning":"客廳套裝","examples":[{"en":"The special offer gives a free lamp with every living room set.","zh":"特別優惠為每套客廳套裝送一盞免費座燈。"},{"en":"A living room set is a group of furniture pieces for a living room.","zh":"living room set 是一組用於客廳的家具。"},{"en":"A living room set may include chairs, a sofa, a table, and a TV stand.","zh":"客廳套裝可能包括椅子、梳化、桌子和電視架。"},{"en":"Renting a set can be easier than choosing each item separately.","zh":"租用套裝可能比逐件選擇更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to furniture designed to work together in one room.","zh":"這個短語指設計成在同一房間一起使用的家具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"monthly fee","meaning":"每月費用","examples":[{"en":"Aaron and Oliver charges a monthly fee for damage cover.","zh":"Aaron and Oliver 就損壞保障收取每月費用。"},{"en":"A monthly fee is money paid every month for a service or protection.","zh":"monthly fee 是每個月為服務或保障支付的費用。"},{"en":"The gym charges a monthly fee for membership.","zh":"健身室收取會籍每月費用。"},{"en":"Shelley must include the monthly damage fee when comparing total prices.","zh":"Shelley 比較總價時必須包括每月損壞保障費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeating payment.","zh":"這個短語描述重複付款。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cheapest prices for renting","meaning":"租用……的最低價格","examples":[{"en":"Larch Furniture offers the cheapest prices for renting furniture.","zh":"Larch Furniture 提供租用家具的最低價格。"},{"en":"Cheapest prices for renting means the lowest rental costs among the available choices.","zh":"cheapest prices for renting 意思是在可選項中最低的租賃費用。"},{"en":"Students often look for the cheapest prices for renting rooms near campus.","zh":"學生常尋找校園附近租房的最低價格。"},{"en":"Shelley may consider Larch Furniture if saving money is her main concern.","zh":"如果省錢是 Shelley 的主要考慮，她可能會考慮 Larch Furniture。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on low cost for temporary use, not buying.","zh":"這個短語著重暫時使用的低成本，而不是購買。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"electronic items","meaning":"電子用品","examples":[{"en":"Larch Furniture offers cheap prices for electronic items.","zh":"Larch Furniture 為電子用品提供便宜價格。"},{"en":"Electronic items are electrical products such as TVs, microwaves, lamps, or small appliances.","zh":"electronic items 是電視、微波爐、燈或小型電器等電子產品。"},{"en":"A new flat may need electronic items as well as furniture.","zh":"新單位可能除了家具外，也需要電子用品。"},{"en":"Shelley might rent electronic items because she is not bringing much with her.","zh":"Shelley 可能會租用電子用品，因為她沒有帶很多東西過來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to useful electrical products for daily life.","zh":"這個短語指日常生活中有用的電器產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"must have own insurance","meaning":"必須自行購買保險","examples":[{"en":"Customers must have their own insurance.","zh":"顧客必須自行購買保險。"},{"en":"Must have own insurance means customers are required to arrange insurance themselves.","zh":"must have own insurance 意思是顧客被要求自己安排保險。"},{"en":"Some rental car companies say drivers must have their own insurance.","zh":"有些租車公司規定司機必須自行購買保險。"},{"en":"Larch Furniture may be cheaper, but Shelley must organise insurance separately.","zh":"Larch Furniture 可能較便宜，但 Shelley 必須另外安排保險。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an important condition of using a service.","zh":"這個短語顯示使用服務的一個重要條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"minimum contract length","meaning":"最短合約期","examples":[{"en":"The minimum contract length is six months.","zh":"最短合約期是六個月。"},{"en":"Minimum contract length means the shortest period a contract can last.","zh":"minimum contract length 意思是一份合約可以維持的最短時間。"},{"en":"The internet plan has a minimum contract length of one year.","zh":"這個上網計劃的最短合約期是一年。"},{"en":"Shelley cannot rent from Larch Furniture for only two or three months.","zh":"Shelley 不能只向 Larch Furniture 租用兩三個月。"},{"en":"This phrase tells customers the shortest commitment they must accept.","zh":"這個短語告訴顧客必須接受的最短承諾期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the most up-to-date prices","meaning":"最新價格","examples":[{"en":"The app shows the most up-to-date prices.","zh":"應用程式顯示最新價格。"},{"en":"The most up-to-date prices are the newest and most current prices available.","zh":"the most up-to-date prices 是目前可得的最新和最即時價格。"},{"en":"Train apps show the most up-to-date ticket prices before passengers buy.","zh":"火車應用程式在乘客購票前顯示最新票價。"},{"en":"Shelley should use the app because old brochures may not show current charges.","zh":"Shelley 應使用應用程式，因為舊小冊子可能不顯示現時收費。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when prices change often.","zh":"當價格經常改變時，這個短語很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"within 7 days of delivery","meaning":"送貨後七日內","examples":[{"en":"Exchanges are allowed within 7 days of delivery.","zh":"送貨後七日內可以更換。"},{"en":"Within 7 days of delivery means no later than seven days after the items arrive.","zh":"within 7 days of delivery 意思是在物品送到後不遲於七天內。"},{"en":"Customers must report missing parts within 7 days of delivery.","zh":"顧客必須在送貨後七日內報告缺少零件。"},{"en":"Shelley should check the furniture quickly if she wants the option to exchange it.","zh":"如果 Shelley 想保留更換選項，她應盡快檢查家具。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear deadline after delivery.","zh":"這個短語給出送貨後的清楚截止日期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 3/task-2":[{"front":"be part of","meaning":"是……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologist is part of a community project to excavate an ancient village.","zh":"這位考古學家是一個發掘古代村莊的社區計劃的一部分。"},{"en":"To be part of something means to belong to it or take a role in it.","zh":"是某事的一部分，意思是屬於它或在其中擔任角色。"},{"en":"A student can be part of a history club if they join its activities.","zh":"如果學生參加歷史學會的活動，他就可以成為該學會的一部分。"},{"en":"Being part of a project means helping the group reach its goal.","zh":"成為一個項目的一部分，意思是幫助小組達成目標。"},{"en":"Volunteers may feel proud when they are part of an important local project.","zh":"當義工成為重要本地項目的一部分時，可能會感到自豪。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"community project","meaning":"社區計劃","examples":[{"en":"This is the third summer for this community project.","zh":"這是這個社區計劃進行的第三個夏天。"},{"en":"A community project is a project organised for or by people in a local area.","zh":"社區計劃，是為本地居民或由本地居民組織的項目。"},{"en":"A community project may clean a park, record local history, or support elderly residents.","zh":"社區計劃可能會清潔公園、記錄本地歷史或支援長者。"},{"en":"Community projects can bring neighbours together to work toward a shared goal.","zh":"社區計劃可以把鄰里聚在一起，朝共同目標努力。"},{"en":"This phrase usually suggests public benefit, not private profit.","zh":"這個短語通常表示為公眾帶來好處，而不是私人利潤。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"excavate an ancient village","meaning":"發掘古代村莊","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to excavate an ancient village.","zh":"這個項目旨在發掘古代村莊。"},{"en":"To excavate an ancient village means to carefully dig up and study the remains of an old settlement.","zh":"發掘古代村莊，意思是小心挖掘和研究古老聚落的遺跡。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may excavate an ancient village to learn how people lived hundreds of years ago.","zh":"考古學家可能會發掘古代村莊，以了解幾百年前的人如何生活。"},{"en":"Excavating an ancient village can reveal houses, tools, pottery, and food remains.","zh":"發掘古代村莊可以揭示房屋、工具、陶器和食物殘留。"},{"en":"This work must be done slowly so important evidence is not damaged.","zh":"這項工作必須慢慢進行，以免損壞重要證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ancient village","meaning":"古代村莊","examples":[{"en":"The team believes there was an ancient village on this site.","zh":"團隊相信這處遺址上曾經有一條古代村莊。"},{"en":"An ancient village is a small settlement where people lived a very long time ago.","zh":"古代村莊，是很久以前人們居住的小型聚落。"},{"en":"An ancient village may contain the remains of houses, paths, fields, and tools.","zh":"古代村莊可能包含房屋、道路、田地和工具的遺跡。"},{"en":"Finding an ancient village can help historians understand local life in the past.","zh":"發現古代村莊可以幫助歷史學家了解昔日的本地生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place older than modern towns or cities.","zh":"這個短語描述比現代城鎮更古老的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"members of the public","meaning":"公眾人士","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologist is talking to members of the public.","zh":"考古學家正在向公眾人士講話。"},{"en":"Members of the public are ordinary people, not officials or project workers.","zh":"公眾人士是普通人，不是官員或項目工作人員。"},{"en":"Members of the public may visit a museum during open days.","zh":"公眾人士可以在開放日參觀博物館。"},{"en":"When experts speak to members of the public, they should explain ideas clearly.","zh":"當專家向公眾人士講話時，應清楚解釋概念。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for open events, notices, and public services.","zh":"這個短語常用於開放活動、通告和公共服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"visit the site","meaning":"參觀遺址","examples":[{"en":"Members of the public are visiting the site.","zh":"公眾人士正在參觀遺址。"},{"en":"To visit the site means to go to the place where the project, building, or discovery is located.","zh":"參觀遺址，意思是前往項目、建築或發現所在的地方。"},{"en":"Students may visit the site of an old fort during a history trip.","zh":"學生可能會在歷史旅行中參觀舊堡壘遺址。"},{"en":"Visiting the site helps people understand the discovery better than reading about it only.","zh":"親身參觀遺址比只閱讀資料更能幫助人理解發現。"},{"en":"Visitors should follow rules when they visit an archaeological site.","zh":"訪客參觀考古遺址時應遵守規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"investigate the site","meaning":"調查遺址","examples":[{"en":"Hayden is one of the archaeologists investigating the site at Bidcaster.","zh":"Hayden 是調查 Bidcaster 遺址的其中一位考古學家。"},{"en":"To investigate the site means to study the place carefully to find evidence and understand what happened there.","zh":"調查遺址，意思是仔細研究該地方，以尋找證據並了解那裏曾發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Archaeologists investigate a site by digging, measuring, recording, and comparing objects.","zh":"考古學家透過挖掘、量度、記錄和比較物件來調查遺址。"},{"en":"If experts investigate the site properly, they can avoid jumping to false conclusions.","zh":"如果專家正確調查遺址，就能避免過早作出錯誤結論。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in archaeology, science, and police work.","zh":"這個短語常見於考古、科學和警務工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the site here at Bidcaster","meaning":"Bidcaster 這處遺址","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologists are investigating the site here at Bidcaster.","zh":"考古學家正在調查 Bidcaster 這處遺址。"},{"en":"The site here at Bidcaster means this particular archaeological location in Bidcaster.","zh":"Bidcaster 這處遺址，意思是位於 Bidcaster 的這個特定考古地點。"},{"en":"The site here at Bidcaster may contain evidence of homes, fields, and tools.","zh":"Bidcaster 這處遺址可能包含房屋、田地和工具的證據。"},{"en":"Saying “here at Bidcaster” helps listeners know the exact place being discussed.","zh":"說「Bidcaster 這裏」有助聽眾知道正在討論的確切地方。"},{"en":"This phrase connects the discovery with its local setting.","zh":"這個短語把發現與其本地環境連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the third summer for","meaning":"……進行的第三個夏天","examples":[{"en":"This is the third summer for the community project.","zh":"這是這個社區計劃進行的第三個夏天。"},{"en":"The third summer for a project means the project has continued across three summer seasons.","zh":"某項目進行的第三個夏天，意思是該項目已跨越三個夏季。"},{"en":"This is the third summer for our beach-cleaning project.","zh":"這是我們清潔海灘計劃進行的第三個夏天。"},{"en":"If it is the third summer for a project, the team has probably gathered experience.","zh":"如果這是一個項目進行的第三個夏天，團隊很可能已累積經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how long a seasonal project has been running.","zh":"這個短語顯示季節性項目已進行多久。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dig here","meaning":"在這裏發掘","examples":[{"en":"Most of the people digging here are volunteers.","zh":"大多數在這裏發掘的人都是義工。"},{"en":"To dig here means to remove earth carefully at this place, often to search for something.","zh":"在這裏發掘，意思是在這個地方小心移走泥土，通常是為了尋找東西。"},{"en":"Archaeology students may dig here under the guidance of experts.","zh":"考古學生可能會在專家指導下在這裏發掘。"},{"en":"People must dig carefully because old objects can break easily.","zh":"人們必須小心發掘，因為古物很容易破裂。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both the action and the location.","zh":"這個短語同時指出行動和地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"full-time archaeologist","meaning":"全職考古學家","examples":[{"en":"Hayden is a full-time archaeologist for the town council.","zh":"Hayden 是鎮議會的全職考古學家。"},{"en":"A full-time archaeologist is someone whose main paid job is archaeology.","zh":"全職考古學家，是主要受薪工作為考古的人。"},{"en":"A full-time archaeologist may spend weeks recording objects from one site.","zh":"全職考古學家可能花數星期記錄一處遺址出土的物件。"},{"en":"Unlike volunteers, a full-time archaeologist works professionally throughout the year.","zh":"與義工不同，全職考古學家全年以專業身份工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the job and the amount of work time.","zh":"這個短語同時描述職業和工作時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"town council","meaning":"鎮議會","examples":[{"en":"Hayden works as an archaeologist for the town council.","zh":"Hayden 為鎮議會擔任考古學家。"},{"en":"A town council is a local government body that manages services and decisions for a town.","zh":"鎮議會，是管理一個城鎮服務和決策的地方政府機構。"},{"en":"A town council may look after parks, roads, local events, and heritage sites.","zh":"鎮議會可能負責公園、道路、本地活動和文化遺址。"},{"en":"If a town council supports archaeology, local history can be protected.","zh":"如果鎮議會支持考古，本地歷史就能得到保護。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to local government, not a private company.","zh":"這個短語指地方政府，而不是私人公司。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be asked to join","meaning":"受邀加入","examples":[{"en":"Hayden was asked to join the project by NHA.","zh":"Hayden 受 NHA 邀請加入這個項目。"},{"en":"To be asked to join means to be invited to take part in something.","zh":"受邀加入，意思是被邀請參與某事。"},{"en":"A student may be asked to join the debate team after doing well in class.","zh":"學生在課堂表現好後，可能會受邀加入辯論隊。"},{"en":"Being asked to join a project often means others value your skills.","zh":"受邀加入一個項目，通常表示別人重視你的技能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that someone did not simply join by themselves.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人不是單純自行加入。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"charity","meaning":"慈善機構","examples":[{"en":"NHA is a charity which sets up projects around the country.","zh":"NHA 是一個在全國各地設立項目的慈善機構。"},{"en":"A charity is an organisation that works to help people, communities, animals, or causes rather than to make profit.","zh":"慈善機構，是為幫助人、社區、動物或某些事業而工作，而不是為盈利的組織。"},{"en":"A charity may collect money to support hospitals or protect historic sites.","zh":"慈善機構可能籌款支援醫院或保護歷史遺址。"},{"en":"Charities often depend on donations and volunteers.","zh":"慈善機構通常依靠捐款和義工。"},{"en":"This word describes an organisation with a public or social purpose.","zh":"這個詞描述具有公共或社會目的的組織。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"set up projects","meaning":"設立項目","examples":[{"en":"NHA sets up projects like this up and down the country.","zh":"NHA 在全國各地設立像這樣的項目。"},{"en":"To set up projects means to organise and start them.","zh":"設立項目，意思是組織並開始項目。"},{"en":"A charity may set up projects to support local history education.","zh":"慈善機構可能會設立項目來支援本地歷史教育。"},{"en":"Setting up projects requires planning, funding, staff, and volunteers.","zh":"設立項目需要規劃、資金、人手和義工。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on creating and launching organised work.","zh":"這個短語着重創立和啟動有組織的工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"up and down the country","meaning":"全國各地","examples":[{"en":"NHA sets up archaeology projects up and down the country.","zh":"NHA 在全國各地設立考古項目。"},{"en":"Up and down the country means in many different places across the whole country.","zh":"全國各地，意思是在整個國家的許多不同地方。"},{"en":"Schools up and down the country are preparing for the same public exam.","zh":"全國各地的學校都在準備同一個公開考試。"},{"en":"If a charity works up and down the country, it is not limited to one town.","zh":"如果慈善機構在全國各地工作，它就不只限於一個城鎮。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises wide national coverage.","zh":"這個短語強調覆蓋全國的範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"next to","meaning":"在……旁邊","examples":[{"en":"The site is next to Bidcaster Castle.","zh":"這處遺址在 Bidcaster 城堡旁邊。"},{"en":"Next to means beside or very close to something.","zh":"在……旁邊，意思是在某物旁邊或非常接近它。"},{"en":"The bus stop is next to the school gate.","zh":"巴士站在學校大門旁邊。"},{"en":"A site next to a castle may contain objects connected with the castle’s history.","zh":"在城堡旁邊的遺址可能包含與城堡歷史有關的物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location in a simple way.","zh":"這個短語以簡單方式描述位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"let someone use","meaning":"讓某人使用","examples":[{"en":"The owners let the archaeologists use their facilities.","zh":"業主讓考古學家使用他們的設施。"},{"en":"To let someone use something means to allow them to use it.","zh":"讓某人使用某物，意思是允許他們使用它。"},{"en":"The school let students use the hall for a charity event.","zh":"學校讓學生使用禮堂舉辦慈善活動。"},{"en":"Letting researchers use facilities can make a project easier to run.","zh":"讓研究人員使用設施可以令項目更容易進行。"},{"en":"This phrase shows permission.","zh":"這個短語表示許可。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"facilities","meaning":"設施","examples":[{"en":"The castle owners let the team use their facilities.","zh":"城堡主人讓團隊使用他們的設施。"},{"en":"Facilities are buildings, rooms, equipment, or services provided for a particular purpose.","zh":"設施，是為特定目的提供的建築、房間、設備或服務。"},{"en":"A sports centre has facilities such as changing rooms, courts, and showers.","zh":"運動中心有更衣室、球場和淋浴間等設施。"},{"en":"Good facilities can help volunteers work safely and comfortably.","zh":"良好設施可以幫助義工安全而舒適地工作。"},{"en":"This word often refers to practical support provided by a place.","zh":"這個詞常指某地方提供的實用支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"How did we get to where we are today?","meaning":"我們是怎樣發展到今天這一步的？","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologist explains how the project got to where it is today.","zh":"考古學家解釋這個項目是怎樣發展到今天這一步的。"},{"en":"How did we get to where we are today? asks how a situation developed over time.","zh":"我們是怎樣發展到今天這一步的，是詢問一個情況如何隨時間發展。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask, “How did we get to where we are today?” before explaining a historical change.","zh":"老師在解釋歷史變化前，可能會問：「我們是怎樣發展到今天這一步的？」"},{"en":"This question invites a story about the steps that led to the present situation.","zh":"這個問題引出導致目前情況的一連串步驟。"},{"en":"It is useful when introducing background information.","zh":"它適合用來介紹背景資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ancient object","meaning":"古代物件","examples":[{"en":"Many archaeology projects begin when an ancient object is found.","zh":"許多考古項目都是在發現古代物件時開始的。"},{"en":"An ancient object is an item made or used by people a very long time ago.","zh":"古代物件，是很久以前由人製造或使用的物品。"},{"en":"An ancient object may be a coin, tool, pot, or piece of jewellery.","zh":"古代物件可能是硬幣、工具、陶罐或首飾。"},{"en":"Finding an ancient object can suggest that people once lived or worked nearby.","zh":"發現古代物件可以暗示人們曾在附近生活或工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to physical evidence from the past.","zh":"這個短語指來自過去的實物證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in our case","meaning":"在我們的情況下","examples":[{"en":"In our case, that object was a gold coin.","zh":"在我們的情況下，那件物件是一枚金幣。"},{"en":"In our case means in our particular situation.","zh":"在我們的情況下，意思是在我們這個特定情況中。"},{"en":"Many teams need extra money; in our case, we needed more volunteers.","zh":"很多團隊需要額外資金；在我們的情況下，我們需要更多義工。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain how one example is different from others.","zh":"這個短語有助解釋一個例子如何不同於其他例子。"},{"en":"It is useful when moving from a general point to a specific example.","zh":"它適合用於由一般觀點轉到具體例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"gold coin","meaning":"金幣","examples":[{"en":"The object found on the site was a gold coin.","zh":"在遺址上發現的物件是一枚金幣。"},{"en":"A gold coin is a coin made of gold or containing gold.","zh":"金幣，是由黃金製成或含有黃金的硬幣。"},{"en":"A gold coin found underground may be valuable to historians and collectors.","zh":"在地下發現的金幣可能對歷史學家和收藏家都有價值。"},{"en":"Finding a gold coin can suggest trade, wealth, or settlement in the area.","zh":"發現金幣可能暗示該區曾有貿易、財富或聚落。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small object that may carry important historical evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述一件可能帶有重要歷史證據的小物件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"metal detector","meaning":"金屬探測器","examples":[{"en":"People sometimes use a metal detector to look for buried objects.","zh":"人們有時使用金屬探測器尋找埋藏物件。"},{"en":"A metal detector is a device that finds metal objects hidden underground or inside other materials.","zh":"金屬探測器，是尋找地下或其他材料內隱藏金屬物件的裝置。"},{"en":"Security guards use metal detectors to check bags at some public events.","zh":"保安員在一些公共活動中使用金屬探測器檢查袋子。"},{"en":"A person using a metal detector may find coins, tools, or jewellery in a field.","zh":"使用金屬探測器的人可能在田野中找到硬幣、工具或首飾。"},{"en":"This phrase names a tool used for finding metal.","zh":"這個短語命名一種尋找金屬的工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"look for things buried in the ground","meaning":"尋找埋在地下的物件","examples":[{"en":"People use metal detectors to look for things buried in the ground.","zh":"人們使用金屬探測器尋找埋在地下的物件。"},{"en":"To look for things buried in the ground means to search for objects hidden under soil.","zh":"尋找埋在地下的物件，意思是搜尋隱藏在泥土下的物品。"},{"en":"Archaeologists look for things buried in the ground by digging carefully.","zh":"考古學家透過小心挖掘尋找埋在地下的物件。"},{"en":"People must follow laws when looking for buried objects, especially on historic sites.","zh":"人們尋找埋藏物件時必須遵守法律，尤其是在歷史遺址上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a search for hidden physical evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述對隱藏實物證據的搜尋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"buried in the ground","meaning":"埋在地下","examples":[{"en":"Coins may be found buried in the ground.","zh":"硬幣可能被發現埋在地下。"},{"en":"Buried in the ground means covered by soil under the surface of the earth.","zh":"埋在地下，意思是被泥土覆蓋在地表以下。"},{"en":"Old tools can remain buried in the ground for hundreds of years.","zh":"舊工具可以埋在地下數百年。"},{"en":"Objects buried in the ground may be protected from weather but damaged by pressure.","zh":"埋在地下的物件可能不受天氣影響，但會受壓力損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where hidden objects are located.","zh":"這個短語描述隱藏物件的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be uncovered when","meaning":"在……時被翻出來","examples":[{"en":"Coins are sometimes uncovered when animals dig tunnels.","zh":"硬幣有時會在動物挖洞時被翻出來。"},{"en":"To be uncovered when something happens means to become visible because that event removes the covering.","zh":"在某事發生時被翻出來，意思是因該事件移走覆蓋物而變得可見。"},{"en":"Old stones may be uncovered when workers repair a road.","zh":"工人修路時，舊石頭可能會被翻出來。"},{"en":"Objects can be uncovered when rain washes away soil.","zh":"當雨水沖走泥土時，物件可能會被翻出來。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the event that reveals something hidden.","zh":"這個短語解釋令隱藏物件顯露的事件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"wild animals","meaning":"野生動物","examples":[{"en":"Wild animals like rabbits may uncover objects when they dig.","zh":"像兔子這樣的野生動物在挖洞時可能會翻出物件。"},{"en":"Wild animals are animals that live naturally and are not kept as pets or farm animals.","zh":"野生動物，是在自然中生活，而不是作為寵物或農場動物飼養的動物。"},{"en":"Wild animals may leave tracks, holes, or nests in fields.","zh":"野生動物可能會在田野留下足跡、洞穴或巢穴。"},{"en":"In archaeology, wild animals can accidentally disturb buried objects.","zh":"在考古中，野生動物可能會意外擾動埋藏物件。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts animals in nature with animals controlled by people.","zh":"這個短語把自然中的動物與受人控制的動物作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"dig tunnels","meaning":"挖洞穴","examples":[{"en":"Rabbits can uncover objects when they dig tunnels.","zh":"兔子挖洞穴時可以翻出物件。"},{"en":"To dig tunnels means to make long narrow holes underground.","zh":"挖洞穴，意思是在地下挖出狹長的洞。"},{"en":"Some animals dig tunnels to live in, hide, or find food.","zh":"一些動物挖洞穴來居住、躲藏或尋找食物。"},{"en":"Digging tunnels can move soil and reveal buried objects.","zh":"挖洞穴可以移動泥土，並顯露埋藏物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an underground action by animals or people.","zh":"這個短語描述動物或人在地下進行的動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rainstorm","meaning":"暴雨","examples":[{"en":"A rainstorm washed away some of the earth and sand.","zh":"暴雨沖走了一些泥土和沙。"},{"en":"A rainstorm is a period of heavy rain, often with strong wind or thunder.","zh":"暴雨，是一段大雨天氣，常伴隨強風或雷聲。"},{"en":"A rainstorm can flood roads and damage outdoor sites.","zh":"暴雨可以淹浸道路並損壞戶外地點。"},{"en":"At an archaeological site, a rainstorm may uncover or damage old remains.","zh":"在考古遺址，暴雨可能會顯露或損壞古老遺跡。"},{"en":"This word describes weather that can change the ground quickly.","zh":"這個詞描述能快速改變地面的天氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"wash away","meaning":"沖走","examples":[{"en":"The rainstorm washed away some of the earth and sand.","zh":"暴雨沖走了一些泥土和沙。"},{"en":"To wash away something means to remove it by the force of water.","zh":"沖走某物，意思是用水的力量移走它。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can wash away soil from a hillside.","zh":"大雨可以沖走山坡上的泥土。"},{"en":"If water washes away the top layer of soil, buried objects may appear.","zh":"如果水沖走表層泥土，埋藏物件可能會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement caused by water.","zh":"這個短語描述由水造成的移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"earth and sand","meaning":"泥土和沙","examples":[{"en":"The rain washed away some of the earth and sand.","zh":"雨水沖走了一些泥土和沙。"},{"en":"Earth and sand are natural ground materials made of soil and tiny rock particles.","zh":"泥土和沙，是由土壤和細小岩石顆粒組成的天然地面材料。"},{"en":"Archaeologists remove earth and sand carefully when they dig a site.","zh":"考古學家發掘遺址時會小心移走泥土和沙。"},{"en":"If earth and sand cover old objects, they may protect them for a long time.","zh":"如果泥土和沙覆蓋古物，它們可能長時間保護古物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the material that often covers archaeological remains.","zh":"這個短語描述常覆蓋考古遺跡的材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hit the news","meaning":"成為新聞","examples":[{"en":"The story of the gold coin hit the news.","zh":"金幣的故事成為新聞。"},{"en":"To hit the news means to become reported by newspapers, television, or online media.","zh":"成為新聞，意思是被報章、電視或網上媒體報道。"},{"en":"The discovery of an old ship hit the news after photos were released.","zh":"一艘古船的發現，在相片發布後成為新聞。"},{"en":"When a story hits the news, many people begin to hear about it.","zh":"當一件事成為新聞時，很多人開始聽到它。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests sudden public attention.","zh":"這個短語表示突然受到公眾注意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"amateur historian","meaning":"業餘歷史學家","examples":[{"en":"Peter Swift is an amateur historian.","zh":"Peter Swift 是一位業餘歷史學家。"},{"en":"An amateur historian is someone who studies history as an interest, not as a full-time professional job.","zh":"業餘歷史學家，是把歷史作為興趣研究，而不是以此作全職專業工作的人。"},{"en":"An amateur historian may collect old maps and local stories.","zh":"業餘歷史學家可能會收集舊地圖和本地故事。"},{"en":"Amateur historians can sometimes help experts by knowing local records well.","zh":"業餘歷史學家有時熟悉本地記錄，可以幫助專家。"},{"en":"This phrase shows interest and knowledge without professional status.","zh":"這個短語表示有興趣和知識，但不是專業身份。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"contact someone to say","meaning":"聯絡某人說","examples":[{"en":"Peter Swift contacted Hayden to say there had been a village on the site.","zh":"Peter Swift 聯絡 Hayden，說這處遺址上曾經有一條村莊。"},{"en":"To contact someone to say something means to get in touch with them in order to give information.","zh":"聯絡某人說某事，意思是與對方取得聯繫，以提供資料。"},{"en":"A parent may contact the school to say their child is ill.","zh":"家長可能會聯絡學校，說孩子生病了。"},{"en":"Contacting an expert to share information can help a project develop.","zh":"聯絡專家分享資料可以幫助項目發展。"},{"en":"This phrase links communication with a message.","zh":"這個短語把溝通與訊息連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"there had been","meaning":"曾經有","examples":[{"en":"Peter believed there had been a village on this site.","zh":"Peter 相信這處遺址上曾經有一條村莊。"},{"en":"There had been means something existed there before another past time.","zh":"There had been 的意思是在另一個過去時間之前，某物曾經存在。"},{"en":"The old photo showed that there had been a market near the river.","zh":"舊照片顯示河邊曾經有一個市場。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about something that existed in the past but may not exist now.","zh":"當談論過去曾存在但現在可能不存在的東西時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It helps place one past situation before another.","zh":"它有助把一個過去情況放在另一個過去情況之前。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on this site","meaning":"在這處遺址上","examples":[{"en":"Peter believed there had been a village on this site.","zh":"Peter 相信在這處遺址上曾經有一條村莊。"},{"en":"On this site means at this particular place or area.","zh":"在這處遺址上，意思是在這個特定地方或範圍內。"},{"en":"Archaeologists found pottery on this site last summer.","zh":"考古學家去年夏天在這處遺址上發現陶器。"},{"en":"Evidence found on this site can help explain who lived there.","zh":"在這處遺址上發現的證據可以幫助解釋誰曾在那裏生活。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the exact location being studied.","zh":"這個短語指出正在研究的確切位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"centuries before","meaning":"幾個世紀之前","examples":[{"en":"The village existed centuries before the castle was built.","zh":"這條村莊在城堡建成幾個世紀之前已經存在。"},{"en":"Centuries before means hundreds of years earlier than another event.","zh":"幾個世紀之前，意思是比另一件事早數百年。"},{"en":"People lived in the valley centuries before the modern town appeared.","zh":"在現代城鎮出現幾個世紀之前，人們已住在山谷中。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare two historical periods.","zh":"這個短語有助比較兩個歷史時期。"},{"en":"It shows that one event happened a very long time before another.","zh":"它顯示一件事比另一件事早很久發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Just by chance","meaning":"純屬偶然","examples":[{"en":"Just by chance, the team found some old maps and documents.","zh":"純屬偶然，團隊找到一些舊地圖和文件。"},{"en":"Just by chance means by luck, not because it was planned.","zh":"純屬偶然，意思是因運氣而發生，不是計劃好的。"},{"en":"Just by chance, I found an old letter inside the library book.","zh":"純屬偶然，我在圖書館書本中發現一封舊信。"},{"en":"Many discoveries happen just by chance when people notice something unexpected.","zh":"許多發現都是在人們注意到意外東西時純屬偶然發生的。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises luck or accident.","zh":"這個短語強調運氣或意外。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"old maps and documents","meaning":"舊地圖和文件","examples":[{"en":"The team found old maps and documents in the library.","zh":"團隊在圖書館找到舊地圖和文件。"},{"en":"Old maps and documents are historical records that can show what places looked like in the past.","zh":"舊地圖和文件，是可以顯示過去地方面貌的歷史記錄。"},{"en":"Old maps and documents may reveal forgotten roads, buildings, or field names.","zh":"舊地圖和文件可能揭示被遺忘的道路、建築或田地名稱。"},{"en":"Archaeologists use old maps and documents to decide where to search.","zh":"考古學家使用舊地圖和文件來決定在哪裏搜尋。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to written and drawn evidence from earlier times.","zh":"這個短語指早期的文字和圖像證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"five-hundred-year-old drawings","meaning":"五百年前的圖畫","examples":[{"en":"The documents showed five-hundred-year-old drawings of ruined buildings.","zh":"文件顯示了五百年前的廢墟建築圖畫。"},{"en":"Five-hundred-year-old drawings are pictures created about five centuries ago.","zh":"五百年前的圖畫，是大約五個世紀前創作的圖片。"},{"en":"Five-hundred-year-old drawings can preserve details of buildings that no longer exist.","zh":"五百年前的圖畫可以保存已不存在建築物的細節。"},{"en":"Such drawings help researchers compare old records with the modern landscape.","zh":"這類圖畫幫助研究人員把舊記錄與現代地貌比較。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the age and type of evidence.","zh":"這個短語同時描述證據的年代和類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ruined buildings","meaning":"廢墟建築","examples":[{"en":"The drawings showed ruined buildings near the castle.","zh":"圖畫顯示城堡附近有廢墟建築。"},{"en":"Ruined buildings are buildings that are damaged, broken, or partly collapsed.","zh":"廢墟建築，是受損、破爛或部分倒塌的建築物。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit ruined buildings to learn about history.","zh":"遊客可能會參觀廢墟建築來了解歷史。"},{"en":"Ruined buildings can show where people once lived, worked, or gathered.","zh":"廢墟建築可以顯示人們曾經居住、工作或聚集的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structures that are no longer complete.","zh":"這個短語描述已不完整的結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"grassy area","meaning":"草地範圍","examples":[{"en":"The ruined buildings were shown on the grassy area between the castle and the river.","zh":"廢墟建築被標示在城堡與河流之間的草地範圍。"},{"en":"A grassy area is a piece of land covered with grass.","zh":"草地範圍，是覆蓋着草的土地。"},{"en":"Students may sit in a grassy area during lunch on a sunny day.","zh":"天氣晴朗時，學生可能會在草地範圍坐下吃午飯。"},{"en":"Archaeological remains can lie hidden under a grassy area for centuries.","zh":"考古遺跡可以在草地範圍下隱藏數百年。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the surface appearance of a place.","zh":"這個短語描述一個地方的表面外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"outer stone walls","meaning":"外圍石牆","examples":[{"en":"The drawings showed buildings between the outer stone walls of the castle and the river.","zh":"圖畫顯示建築物位於城堡外圍石牆與河流之間。"},{"en":"Outer stone walls are the outside walls made of stone that protect or surround a place.","zh":"外圍石牆，是由石頭建成、位於外側並保護或包圍某地的牆。"},{"en":"A castle’s outer stone walls helped defend it from attack.","zh":"城堡的外圍石牆幫助抵禦攻擊。"},{"en":"Buildings near outer stone walls may have been connected to castle life.","zh":"外圍石牆附近的建築可能與城堡生活有關。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both material and position.","zh":"這個短語同時描述材料和位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be onto something","meaning":"找到重要線索","examples":[{"en":"The team knew then that they were onto something.","zh":"團隊當時知道他們找到重要線索了。"},{"en":"To be onto something means to have found an important clue or promising idea.","zh":"找到重要線索，意思是發現了一個重要提示或有希望的想法。"},{"en":"A scientist may feel she is onto something after repeated experiments show the same result.","zh":"如果重複實驗顯示相同結果，科學家可能會覺得自己找到重要線索。"},{"en":"In archaeology, finding matching records and objects may suggest the team is onto something.","zh":"在考古中，找到相符的記錄和物件可能表示團隊找到重要線索。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a discovery may lead to something important.","zh":"這個短語顯示某個發現可能通往重要結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the remains of","meaning":"……的遺跡","examples":[{"en":"The team has found the remains of several buildings.","zh":"團隊已找到幾棟建築的遺跡。"},{"en":"The remains of something are the parts left after most of it has disappeared or been destroyed.","zh":"某物的遺跡，是大部分消失或被破壞後留下的部分。"},{"en":"Archaeologists found the remains of an old wall under the field.","zh":"考古學家在田地下發現一堵舊牆的遺跡。"},{"en":"The remains of buildings can show their size, shape, and purpose.","zh":"建築遺跡可以顯示其大小、形狀和用途。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing ruins and archaeology.","zh":"這個短語常見於討論廢墟和考古。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"several buildings","meaning":"幾棟建築","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologists found the remains of several buildings.","zh":"考古學家發現了幾棟建築的遺跡。"},{"en":"Several buildings means more than two buildings, but not necessarily a large number.","zh":"幾棟建築，意思是多於兩棟，但不一定很多。"},{"en":"The old map showed several buildings near the river.","zh":"舊地圖顯示河邊有幾棟建築。"},{"en":"Finding several buildings suggests the site may have been a settlement, not just one house.","zh":"發現幾棟建築表示該處可能是一個聚落，而不只是一間屋。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate number without being exact.","zh":"這個短語給出大約數量，而不是精確數字。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"broken pots","meaning":"破碎陶罐","examples":[{"en":"The team found more broken pots than they could count.","zh":"團隊找到多到數不清的破碎陶罐。"},{"en":"Broken pots are pieces of pottery that have cracked or fallen apart.","zh":"破碎陶罐，是裂開或碎裂的陶器。"},{"en":"Archaeologists often find broken pots because pottery can last for a long time underground.","zh":"考古學家常發現破碎陶罐，因為陶器可以在地下保存很久。"},{"en":"Broken pots can show what people cooked, stored, or traded.","zh":"破碎陶罐可以顯示人們煮食、儲存或交易甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to damaged everyday objects from the past.","zh":"這個短語指過去受損的日常物件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"more than you can count","meaning":"多到數不清","examples":[{"en":"They found more broken pots than you can count.","zh":"他們找到多到數不清的破碎陶罐。"},{"en":"More than you can count means so many that counting them would be difficult or impossible.","zh":"多到數不清，意思是數量太多，難以或無法數清。"},{"en":"There were more stars in the sky than you can count.","zh":"天上的星星多到數不清。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to emphasise a very large number.","zh":"這個短語常用來強調數量非常多。"},{"en":"It is not always literal; it can be a strong way to say “many.”","zh":"它不一定是字面意思，也可以是強烈地表示「很多」。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"normally you’d expect to","meaning":"通常你會預期","examples":[{"en":"Normally you’d expect to find brooches and other jewellery.","zh":"通常你會預期找到胸針及其他首飾。"},{"en":"Normally you’d expect to means people would usually think something is likely.","zh":"通常你會預期，意思是人們一般會認為某事很可能發生。"},{"en":"In an old kitchen, normally you’d expect to find pots, bowls, and cooking tools.","zh":"在舊廚房中，通常你會預期找到鍋、碗和煮食工具。"},{"en":"This phrase compares what is usual with what has actually been found.","zh":"這個短語把通常情況與實際發現作比較。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining surprise in research.","zh":"它適合用來解釋研究中的意外之處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"brooches and other jewellery","meaning":"胸針及其他首飾","examples":[{"en":"The team is still hoping to find brooches and other jewellery.","zh":"團隊仍希望找到胸針及其他首飾。"},{"en":"Brooches and other jewellery are decorative items people wear, such as pins, rings, and necklaces.","zh":"胸針及其他首飾，是人們佩戴的裝飾品，例如別針、戒指和項鏈。"},{"en":"A brooch can be used to fasten clothing and also show personal style.","zh":"胸針可以用來扣緊衣物，也可以展示個人風格。"},{"en":"Finding brooches and other jewellery can reveal wealth, fashion, or trade in the past.","zh":"發現胸針及其他首飾可以揭示過去的財富、時尚或貿易。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to personal ornaments rather than tools or pots.","zh":"這個短語指個人裝飾品，而不是工具或陶罐。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be still waiting to","meaning":"仍在等待","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologists are still waiting to uncover such items.","zh":"考古學家仍在等待發掘出這類物品。"},{"en":"To be still waiting to do something means the expected action has not happened yet.","zh":"仍在等待做某事，意思是預期的行動尚未發生。"},{"en":"The students are still waiting to receive feedback on their project.","zh":"學生仍在等待收到項目意見。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may be still waiting to find rare objects after many weeks of digging.","zh":"考古學家發掘數星期後，可能仍在等待找到稀有物件。"},{"en":"This phrase shows delay or continued hope.","zh":"這個短語表示延遲或持續希望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"uncover items","meaning":"發掘出物件","examples":[{"en":"The team hopes to uncover jewellery on the site.","zh":"團隊希望在遺址上發掘出首飾。"},{"en":"To uncover items means to find and reveal objects that were hidden or buried.","zh":"發掘出物件，意思是找到並顯露原本被隱藏或埋藏的物品。"},{"en":"Workers may uncover items from an old house during renovation.","zh":"工人在翻新舊屋時可能會發掘出物件。"},{"en":"In archaeology, uncovering items must be done carefully so evidence is not lost.","zh":"在考古中，發掘物件必須小心進行，以免失去證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discovery through digging or searching.","zh":"這個短語描述透過挖掘或搜尋而發現東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"such items","meaning":"這類物品","examples":[{"en":"The team is still waiting to uncover any such items.","zh":"團隊仍在等待發掘出任何這類物品。"},{"en":"Such items means items of the kind just mentioned.","zh":"這類物品，意思是剛提到的那一類物件。"},{"en":"The museum collects old coins, jewellery, and such items from local history.","zh":"博物館收集舊硬幣、首飾和這類本地歷史物品。"},{"en":"If such items are found, they may help date the site.","zh":"如果找到這類物品，它們可能有助判斷遺址年代。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the same list again.","zh":"這個短語避免再次重複同一清單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be skilled at","meaning":"擅長","examples":[{"en":"The people who lived here were skilled at making tools.","zh":"曾住在這裏的人擅長製作工具。"},{"en":"To be skilled at something means to be good at doing it because of practice or knowledge.","zh":"擅長某事，意思是因練習或知識而做得好。"},{"en":"A carpenter is skilled at shaping wood.","zh":"木匠擅長塑造木材。"},{"en":"People skilled at making tools could solve daily problems more easily.","zh":"擅長製作工具的人可以更容易解決日常問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability learned through experience.","zh":"這個短語描述透過經驗學到的能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make tools from","meaning":"用……製作工具","examples":[{"en":"The villagers were skilled at making tools from animal bones.","zh":"村民擅長用動物骨頭製作工具。"},{"en":"To make tools from a material means to use that material to create useful objects.","zh":"用某種材料製作工具，意思是使用該材料製造有用物件。"},{"en":"Early people made tools from stone, wood, and bone.","zh":"早期人類用石頭、木材和骨頭製作工具。"},{"en":"Making tools from available materials shows creativity and practical skill.","zh":"用可取得的材料製作工具，顯示創意和實用技能。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a finished object with the material used to create it.","zh":"這個短語把完成品與製作材料連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"animal bones","meaning":"動物骨頭","examples":[{"en":"The villagers made tools from animal bones.","zh":"村民用動物骨頭製作工具。"},{"en":"Animal bones are the hard parts left from the bodies of animals.","zh":"動物骨頭，是動物身體留下的堅硬部分。"},{"en":"Animal bones found at a site can show what people ate or used.","zh":"在遺址發現的動物骨頭可以顯示人們吃甚麼或使用甚麼。"},{"en":"Ancient people sometimes shaped animal bones into needles, handles, or small tools.","zh":"古人有時把動物骨頭加工成針、手柄或小工具。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a material that can be both evidence and resource.","zh":"這個短語指一種既可作證據又可作資源的材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"visit the exhibition","meaning":"參觀展覽","examples":[{"en":"You will see the bone tools when you visit the exhibition.","zh":"當你參觀展覽時，會看到骨製工具。"},{"en":"To visit the exhibition means to go and look at a public display of objects or information.","zh":"參觀展覽，意思是前往觀看公開展示的物件或資料。"},{"en":"Students may visit the exhibition to learn about local archaeology.","zh":"學生可能會參觀展覽，學習本地考古。"},{"en":"Visiting the exhibition lets people see real objects from the project.","zh":"參觀展覽讓人們看到項目中的真實物件。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when inviting people to museums or displays.","zh":"這個短語常用於邀請人們參觀博物館或展覽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Besides the discovery of","meaning":"除了發現……之外","examples":[{"en":"Besides the discovery of the village, the team found evidence across the river.","zh":"除了發現村莊之外，團隊還在河的另一邊找到證據。"},{"en":"Besides the discovery of something means in addition to finding that thing.","zh":"除了發現某物之外，意思是在找到那件事物以外還有其他發現。"},{"en":"Besides the discovery of old coins, archaeologists found pottery and bones.","zh":"除了發現舊硬幣之外，考古學家還找到陶器和骨頭。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another important finding to the first one.","zh":"這個短語在第一項發現之外加入另一項重要發現。"},{"en":"It is useful when reporting several discoveries.","zh":"它適合用來報告多項發現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"evidence of human activity","meaning":"人類活動的證據","examples":[{"en":"The team found evidence of human activity on the other side of the river.","zh":"團隊在河的另一邊發現人類活動的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence of human activity means signs that people lived, worked, farmed, or travelled in a place.","zh":"人類活動的證據，意思是顯示人們曾在某地生活、工作、耕作或經過的跡象。"},{"en":"Old paths, tools, fire marks, and pottery can be evidence of human activity.","zh":"舊路、工具、火痕和陶器都可以是人類活動的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence of human activity helps archaeologists understand how a landscape was used.","zh":"人類活動的證據幫助考古學家理解一片土地如何被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to clues left by people in the past.","zh":"這個短語指過去人類留下的線索。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on the other side of","meaning":"在……的另一邊","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologists found evidence on the other side of the river.","zh":"考古學家在河的另一邊發現證據。"},{"en":"On the other side of something means across from it or beyond it.","zh":"在某物的另一邊，意思是在它對面或越過它的地方。"},{"en":"The car park is on the other side of the school building.","zh":"停車場在學校大樓的另一邊。"},{"en":"Evidence on the other side of a river may show that people used both banks.","zh":"河的另一邊的證據可能顯示人們曾使用兩岸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location by comparing two sides.","zh":"這個短語透過比較兩邊來描述位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"so far","meaning":"到目前為止","examples":[{"en":"No other houses or huts have been found so far.","zh":"到目前為止，尚未發現其他房屋或小屋。"},{"en":"So far means up to this point in time.","zh":"到目前為止，意思是直到現在這一刻。"},{"en":"So far, the team has found pottery but no jewellery.","zh":"到目前為止，團隊找到了陶器，但沒有找到首飾。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that more discoveries may happen later.","zh":"這個短語暗示之後可能還會有更多發現。"},{"en":"It is useful when a project or investigation is still continuing.","zh":"當項目或調查仍在繼續時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"houses or huts","meaning":"房屋或小屋","examples":[{"en":"No other houses or huts have been found across the river.","zh":"河對岸尚未發現其他房屋或小屋。"},{"en":"Houses or huts are places where people may have lived, with huts usually being smaller or simpler.","zh":"房屋或小屋，是人們可能居住的地方，其中小屋通常較細小或簡單。"},{"en":"Ancient villages may include houses or huts made of wood, mud, or stone.","zh":"古代村莊可能包括由木、泥或石建成的房屋或小屋。"},{"en":"Finding houses or huts would show where people lived on the site.","zh":"發現房屋或小屋會顯示人們曾在遺址哪裏居住。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to possible living structures.","zh":"這個短語指可能的居住結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the borders of","meaning":"……的邊界","examples":[{"en":"The team can see the borders of an ancient field system.","zh":"團隊可以看見古代田地系統的邊界。"},{"en":"The borders of something are its edges or limits.","zh":"某物的邊界，是它的邊緣或範圍限制。"},{"en":"A fence can mark the borders of a school garden.","zh":"圍欄可以標示學校花園的邊界。"},{"en":"In archaeology, the borders of fields may appear as lines in the ground.","zh":"在考古中，田地的邊界可能以地面線條形式出現。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe the shape and limits of an area.","zh":"這個短語有助描述一個區域的形狀和範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ancient field system","meaning":"古代田地系統","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologists found evidence of an ancient field system.","zh":"考古學家發現了古代田地系統的證據。"},{"en":"An ancient field system is an old arrangement of fields used for farming.","zh":"古代田地系統，是過去用於耕作的田地排列方式。"},{"en":"An ancient field system may show where people grew crops or kept animals.","zh":"古代田地系統可能顯示人們在哪裏種植作物或飼養動物。"},{"en":"Finding an ancient field system can prove that people used the land for agriculture.","zh":"發現古代田地系統可以證明人們曾把土地用於農業。"},{"en":"This phrase connects archaeology with farming and land use.","zh":"這個短語把考古與農耕和土地使用連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"At one point","meaning":"有一次；在某個階段","examples":[{"en":"At one point, the team thought they had found an ancient palace.","zh":"在某個階段，團隊以為他們找到了古代宮殿。"},{"en":"At one point means at one stage or moment during a process.","zh":"At one point 的意思是在過程中的某一階段或某一刻。"},{"en":"At one point, we thought the project would be cancelled.","zh":"有一段時間，我們以為項目會被取消。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing how ideas changed over time.","zh":"這個短語適合用來描述想法如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"It shows that something was true or believed for a while, but not necessarily later.","zh":"它顯示某事曾在一段時間內是真的或被相信，但之後未必如此。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ancient palace","meaning":"古代宮殿","examples":[{"en":"The team first thought the long wall was part of an ancient palace.","zh":"團隊起初以為那道長牆是古代宮殿的一部分。"},{"en":"An ancient palace is a large important building where rulers or powerful people may have lived.","zh":"古代宮殿，是統治者或有權勢的人可能居住的大型重要建築。"},{"en":"An ancient palace may contain halls, courtyards, decorated rooms, and official spaces.","zh":"古代宮殿可能包含大廳、庭院、裝飾房間和官方空間。"},{"en":"Finding an ancient palace would be a major archaeological discovery.","zh":"發現古代宮殿會是重大的考古發現。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a high-status building from the distant past.","zh":"這個短語表示來自遠古時代的高地位建築。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"turn out to be","meaning":"結果是；證明是","examples":[{"en":"The long wall turned out to be a modern wall.","zh":"那道長牆結果是一道現代牆。"},{"en":"To turn out to be something means to prove to be that thing after more information is found.","zh":"結果是某物，意思是在找到更多資料後證明是那樣東西。"},{"en":"The old coin turned out to be a modern copy.","zh":"那枚舊硬幣結果是一件現代仿製品。"},{"en":"In research, early guesses can turn out to be wrong.","zh":"在研究中，早期猜測可能證明是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the final result after uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語顯示不確定之後的最終結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the meantime","meaning":"在此期間","examples":[{"en":"In the meantime, the team is putting on guided tours.","zh":"在此期間，團隊正在舉辦導賞團。"},{"en":"In the meantime means during the period before something else happens.","zh":"在此期間，意思是在另一件事發生之前的這段時間。"},{"en":"The museum will open next month; in the meantime, visitors can see the online exhibition.","zh":"博物館下月開放；在此期間，訪客可以觀看網上展覽。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing temporary activities.","zh":"這個短語適合用來描述臨時活動。"},{"en":"It connects the current action with a future event.","zh":"它把目前行動與未來事件連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"put on a series of","meaning":"舉辦一系列","examples":[{"en":"The team is putting on a series of guided tours.","zh":"團隊正在舉辦一系列導賞團。"},{"en":"To put on a series of events means to organise and offer several related events.","zh":"舉辦一系列活動，意思是組織並提供幾個相關活動。"},{"en":"The library is putting on a series of talks about local history.","zh":"圖書館正在舉辦一系列關於本地歷史的講座。"},{"en":"A series of guided tours can attract different groups over several weeks.","zh":"一系列導賞團可以在數星期內吸引不同團體。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for planned public activities.","zh":"這個短語適合用於有計劃的公共活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"guided tours","meaning":"導賞團","examples":[{"en":"The project will offer guided tours for school groups.","zh":"這個項目會為學校團體提供導賞團。"},{"en":"Guided tours are visits led by a guide who explains what people are seeing.","zh":"導賞團，是由導遊帶領並解釋人們正在觀看內容的參觀。"},{"en":"Museums often offer guided tours for visitors who want more background information.","zh":"博物館常為想了解更多背景資料的訪客提供導賞團。"},{"en":"A guided tour of an archaeological site can help students understand the remains.","zh":"考古遺址導賞團可以幫助學生理解遺跡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an organised visit with explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述有講解的有組織參觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"school groups","meaning":"學校團體","examples":[{"en":"The guided tours are for school groups.","zh":"這些導賞團是為學校團體而設的。"},{"en":"School groups are groups of students and teachers visiting or doing an activity together.","zh":"學校團體，是一起參觀或參與活動的學生和老師群體。"},{"en":"School groups often visit museums as part of history lessons.","zh":"學校團體常作為歷史課的一部分參觀博物館。"},{"en":"Tours for school groups need clear explanations and safe routes.","zh":"為學校團體而設的導賞需要清楚解釋和安全路線。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised groups from schools.","zh":"這個短語指來自學校的有組織團體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"this autumn","meaning":"今年秋天","examples":[{"en":"The team will organise guided tours this autumn.","zh":"團隊會在今年秋天組織導賞團。"},{"en":"This autumn means during the autumn season of the current year.","zh":"今年秋天，意思是在今年的秋季期間。"},{"en":"The school will start a new history club this autumn.","zh":"學校會在今年秋天開設新的歷史學會。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a general time without naming exact dates.","zh":"這個短語給出大概時間，而不是具體日期。"},{"en":"It is useful when future plans are arranged by season.","zh":"當未來計劃按季節安排時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"TV documentary","meaning":"電視紀錄片","examples":[{"en":"There was a TV documentary about the project.","zh":"有一部關於這個項目的電視紀錄片。"},{"en":"A TV documentary is a factual television programme about real people, events, or issues.","zh":"電視紀錄片，是關於真實人物、事件或議題的事實性電視節目。"},{"en":"A TV documentary about archaeology may show digging, interviews, and old objects.","zh":"關於考古的電視紀錄片可能展示挖掘、訪問和古物。"},{"en":"Documentaries can help the public understand a project more deeply.","zh":"紀錄片可以幫助公眾更深入理解一個項目。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a non-fiction television programme.","zh":"這個短語指非虛構電視節目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"暗示；表示","examples":[{"en":"The documentary suggested that the objects would go to the town’s museum.","zh":"紀錄片表示這些物件會送到鎮上的博物館。"},{"en":"To suggest that something is true means to indicate it without saying it with complete certainty.","zh":"Suggest that 的意思是指出某事可能是真的，但不是完全肯定地說。"},{"en":"The evidence suggests that people lived near the river.","zh":"證據顯示人們曾住在河邊附近。"},{"en":"A report may suggest that more research is needed.","zh":"報告可能表示需要更多研究。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a claim is possible but not fully confirmed.","zh":"當某說法可能成立但尚未完全確認時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"for sure","meaning":"確定地","examples":[{"en":"The team does not know that for sure yet.","zh":"團隊尚未確定地知道那件事。"},{"en":"For sure means definitely or with certainty.","zh":"For sure 的意思是肯定地或確定地。"},{"en":"We do not know for sure whether the building was a house or a workshop.","zh":"我們尚未確定地知道那棟建築是房屋還是工場。"},{"en":"Researchers avoid saying something for sure until they have enough evidence.","zh":"研究人員在有足夠證據前，會避免確定地說某事。"},{"en":"This phrase separates confirmed facts from guesses.","zh":"這個短語把已確認事實與猜測分開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"enter the site","meaning":"進入遺址","examples":[{"en":"Visitors should follow the rules when they enter the site.","zh":"訪客進入遺址時應遵守規則。"},{"en":"To enter the site means to go into the archaeological area.","zh":"進入遺址，意思是走進考古區域。"},{"en":"Visitors may need permission before they enter the site.","zh":"訪客進入遺址前可能需要許可。"},{"en":"When people enter the site, they must avoid damaging the ground.","zh":"當人們進入遺址時，必須避免損壞地面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the moment visitors go inside a protected area.","zh":"這個短語描述訪客進入受保護區域的一刻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Please make sure you keep to the paths.","zh":"請確保你沿小路行走。"},{"en":"Make sure means check carefully or do something so that it definitely happens.","zh":"確保，意思是仔細檢查或採取行動，令某事一定發生。"},{"en":"Make sure you close the gate before leaving the site.","zh":"離開遺址前，請確保關上閘門。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in instructions and safety rules.","zh":"這個短語常用於指示和安全規則。"},{"en":"It shows that the action is important.","zh":"它顯示該行動很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"keep to the paths","meaning":"沿小路行走；不要離開小路","examples":[{"en":"Visitors must keep to the paths at all times.","zh":"訪客任何時候都必須沿小路行走。"},{"en":"To keep to the paths means to walk only on the marked paths and not leave them.","zh":"沿小路行走，意思是只走在標示的小路上，不要離開。"},{"en":"In a nature reserve, visitors should keep to the paths to protect plants.","zh":"在自然保護區，訪客應沿小路行走以保護植物。"},{"en":"Keeping to the paths prevents people from damaging fragile archaeological remains.","zh":"沿小路行走可以防止人們損壞脆弱的考古遺跡。"},{"en":"This phrase is a clear safety and protection instruction.","zh":"這個短語是清楚的安全和保護指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at all times","meaning":"任何時候；一直","examples":[{"en":"Visitors must keep to the paths at all times.","zh":"訪客任何時候都必須沿小路行走。"},{"en":"At all times means always, without exception.","zh":"At all times 的意思是一直，沒有例外。"},{"en":"Students must wear safety glasses in the laboratory at all times.","zh":"學生在實驗室任何時候都必須佩戴安全眼鏡。"},{"en":"At an archaeological site, rules must be followed at all times to protect evidence.","zh":"在考古遺址，任何時候都必須遵守規則，以保護證據。"},{"en":"This phrase makes an instruction stronger and clearer.","zh":"這個短語令指示更強而清楚。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the highlights of the site","meaning":"遺址的亮點","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologist mentions the highlights of the site.","zh":"考古學家提到遺址的亮點。"},{"en":"The highlights of the site are the most interesting or important things to see there.","zh":"遺址的亮點，是那裏最有趣或最重要的可看之處。"},{"en":"A guide may point out the highlights of the site before a tour begins.","zh":"導遊可能在導賞開始前指出遺址的亮點。"},{"en":"Knowing the highlights helps visitors decide where to go first.","zh":"知道亮點有助訪客決定先去哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a place to visitors.","zh":"這個短語適合用來向訪客介紹地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Take a look at","meaning":"看一看","examples":[{"en":"Take a look at the map before entering the site.","zh":"進入遺址前，先看一看地圖。"},{"en":"Take a look at means look at something briefly or carefully.","zh":"Take a look at 的意思是簡短或仔細地看某物。"},{"en":"Take a look at the notice before you enter the museum.","zh":"進入博物館前，先看一看告示。"},{"en":"This phrase is a friendly way to ask someone to check information.","zh":"這個短語是請人查看資料的友善說法。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken instructions.","zh":"它常見於口頭指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"present location","meaning":"目前位置","examples":[{"en":"The group’s present location is marked at the bottom of the map.","zh":"小組的目前位置標在地圖底部。"},{"en":"Present location means the place where someone is now.","zh":"目前位置，意思是某人現在所在的地方。"},{"en":"A map app shows your present location with a blue dot.","zh":"地圖應用程式會用藍點顯示你的目前位置。"},{"en":"Knowing your present location helps you follow directions correctly.","zh":"知道目前位置有助你正確跟隨方向。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reading maps or giving routes.","zh":"這個短語適合用於閱讀地圖或指路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be marked at the bottom","meaning":"標在底部","examples":[{"en":"The present location is marked at the bottom of the map.","zh":"目前位置標在地圖底部。"},{"en":"To be marked at the bottom means to be shown with a sign or label in the lower part.","zh":"標在底部，意思是在下方位置用標記或標籤顯示。"},{"en":"The meeting point is marked at the bottom of the poster.","zh":"集合地點標在海報底部。"},{"en":"If your location is marked at the bottom, you should begin reading the map from there.","zh":"如果你的位置標在底部，你應該從那裏開始看地圖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both a label and its position.","zh":"這個短語同時描述標記和位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"identify the foundations of","meaning":"確認……的地基","examples":[{"en":"The team has identified the foundations of an ancient bridge.","zh":"團隊已確認一座古橋的地基。"},{"en":"To identify the foundations of something means to recognise the base parts that once supported it.","zh":"確認某物的地基，意思是辨認出曾支撐它的底部部分。"},{"en":"Archaeologists identified the foundations of a Roman house under the field.","zh":"考古學家在田地下確認了一座羅馬房屋的地基。"},{"en":"Identifying foundations helps researchers understand the size and shape of a lost structure.","zh":"確認地基有助研究人員了解已消失結構的大小和形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when studying ruined buildings or bridges.","zh":"這個短語常用於研究廢墟建築或橋樑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bridge foundations","meaning":"橋樑地基","examples":[{"en":"The bridge foundations are one of the highlights of the site.","zh":"橋樑地基是遺址的亮點之一。"},{"en":"Bridge foundations are the base structures that supported a bridge.","zh":"橋樑地基，是支撐橋樑的底部結構。"},{"en":"Bridge foundations may remain even after the wooden or stone bridge has disappeared.","zh":"即使木橋或石橋已消失，橋樑地基仍可能留下。"},{"en":"Finding bridge foundations can show where people crossed a river in the past.","zh":"發現橋樑地基可以顯示過去人們在哪裏過河。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the lower supporting parts of a bridge.","zh":"這個短語指橋的下方支撐部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ancient bridge","meaning":"古橋","examples":[{"en":"The team has found the foundations of an ancient bridge.","zh":"團隊已找到一座古橋的地基。"},{"en":"An ancient bridge is a bridge built a very long time ago.","zh":"古橋，是很久以前建造的橋。"},{"en":"An ancient bridge may have connected a village to fields, roads, or a castle.","zh":"古橋可能曾把村莊與田地、道路或城堡連接起來。"},{"en":"Finding an ancient bridge can explain how people travelled across the landscape.","zh":"發現古橋可以解釋人們過去如何在地區中移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an old transport structure.","zh":"這個短語描述古老的交通結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a team of divers","meaning":"一隊潛水員","examples":[{"en":"A team of divers are searching in the river.","zh":"一隊潛水員正在河裏搜尋。"},{"en":"A team of divers is a group of people trained to work or search underwater.","zh":"一隊潛水員，是受過訓練在水下工作或搜尋的一群人。"},{"en":"A team of divers may look for objects at the bottom of a lake.","zh":"一隊潛水員可能會在湖底尋找物件。"},{"en":"Divers are useful when archaeological evidence may be under water.","zh":"當考古證據可能在水底時，潛水員很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specialist group working below the surface.","zh":"這個短語描述在水面下工作的專門團隊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"search for lost objects","meaning":"尋找遺失物件","examples":[{"en":"The divers are searching for lost objects in the river.","zh":"潛水員正在河中尋找遺失物件。"},{"en":"To search for lost objects means to look carefully for things that have been dropped, hidden, or forgotten.","zh":"尋找遺失物件，意思是仔細尋找掉落、隱藏或被遺忘的東西。"},{"en":"Volunteers may search for lost objects after a flood.","zh":"洪水後，義工可能會尋找遺失物件。"},{"en":"In a river, lost objects can sink into mud and become hard to find.","zh":"在河中，遺失物件可能沉入泥中，變得難以找到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a careful search for missing items.","zh":"這個短語描述對失蹤物品的仔細搜尋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lost objects","meaning":"遺失物件","examples":[{"en":"The divers are looking for lost objects in the river.","zh":"潛水員正在河中尋找遺失物件。"},{"en":"Lost objects are things that have been misplaced, dropped, or left behind.","zh":"遺失物件，是被放錯地方、掉落或留下的東西。"},{"en":"Lost objects in a river may include coins, tools, weapons, or personal items.","zh":"河中的遺失物件可能包括硬幣、工具、武器或個人物品。"},{"en":"Finding lost objects can help archaeologists understand past movement and daily life.","zh":"發現遺失物件可以幫助考古學家了解過去的活動和日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to items no longer in their original owner’s control.","zh":"這個短語指不再由原主人掌控的物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"To reach","meaning":"要到達","examples":[{"en":"To reach the bridge, take the main path ahead of you.","zh":"要到達橋的位置，請沿你前方的主路走。"},{"en":"To reach a place means to arrive at it.","zh":"到達某地，意思是抵達那裏。"},{"en":"To reach the library, walk past the office and turn left.","zh":"要到達圖書館，先經過辦公室，然後左轉。"},{"en":"Directions often begin with “to reach” when explaining how to get somewhere.","zh":"指路時常用 “to reach” 來解釋如何到某地。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a goal with the route needed to get there.","zh":"這個短語把目標地點與所需路線連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the main path ahead of you","meaning":"你前方的主路","examples":[{"en":"Take the main path ahead of you to reach the bridge.","zh":"沿着你前方的主路走，便可到達橋的位置。"},{"en":"The main path ahead of you means the largest or clearest path in front of you.","zh":"你前方的主路，意思是在你面前最大或最清楚的道路。"},{"en":"At the park entrance, follow the main path ahead of you until you see the lake.","zh":"在公園入口，沿你前方的主路走，直到看見湖。"},{"en":"This phrase helps visitors know which path to take when several routes exist.","zh":"當有幾條路線時，這個短語幫助訪客知道走哪一條。"},{"en":"It gives both direction and position.","zh":"它同時給出方向和位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"go straight on","meaning":"一直向前行","examples":[{"en":"Go straight on until the path bends to the left.","zh":"一直向前行，直到小路向左彎。"},{"en":"Go straight on means continue moving forward without turning.","zh":"一直向前行，意思是繼續向前，不要轉彎。"},{"en":"Go straight on past the school gate, and the library will be on your right.","zh":"一直向前行，經過學校大門，圖書館會在你右邊。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in directions.","zh":"這個短語常見於指路。"},{"en":"It tells people to keep the same direction.","zh":"它告訴人們保持同一方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"keep going till","meaning":"繼續走到……為止","examples":[{"en":"Keep going till the path bends to the left.","zh":"繼續走到小路向左彎為止。"},{"en":"Keep going till means continue until a certain point or event happens.","zh":"繼續走到……為止，意思是持續前進，直到某個地點或事情出現。"},{"en":"Keep going till you see the blue sign.","zh":"繼續走到你看見藍色指示牌為止。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving step-by-step directions.","zh":"這個短語適合用於逐步指路。"},{"en":"It tells someone when to stop or change direction.","zh":"它告訴某人何時停止或改變方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bend to the left","meaning":"向左彎","examples":[{"en":"The path bends to the left near the bridge.","zh":"小路在橋附近向左彎。"},{"en":"To bend to the left means to curve or turn left gradually.","zh":"向左彎，意思是逐漸向左彎曲或轉向。"},{"en":"The road bends to the left after the old church.","zh":"道路經過舊教堂後向左彎。"},{"en":"If a path bends to the left, walkers should follow the curve instead of going straight.","zh":"如果小路向左彎，行人應跟着彎位走，而不是一直直行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gentle change in direction.","zh":"這個短語描述溫和的方向改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"smaller track","meaning":"較小的小徑","examples":[{"en":"You will see a smaller track leading off to the right.","zh":"你會看見一條較小的小徑向右岔出。"},{"en":"A smaller track is a narrower or less important path.","zh":"較小的小徑，是較窄或較不主要的路。"},{"en":"A smaller track may lead from the main path into the woods.","zh":"較小的小徑可能從主路通往樹林。"},{"en":"Visitors should check signs before taking a smaller track.","zh":"訪客走較小的小徑前應查看指示牌。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a side path with a main path.","zh":"這個短語把支路與主路作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lead off to the right","meaning":"向右岔出","examples":[{"en":"A smaller track leads off to the right.","zh":"一條較小的小徑向右岔出。"},{"en":"To lead off to the right means to branch away toward the right side.","zh":"向右岔出，意思是向右邊分支出去。"},{"en":"A small path leads off to the right near the playground.","zh":"遊樂場附近有一條小路向右岔出。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people identify a side route.","zh":"這個短語幫助人們辨認支路。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving walking directions.","zh":"它適合用於步行指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"follow that","meaning":"沿着那條路走","examples":[{"en":"Follow that to take you to the river.","zh":"沿着那條路走，它會帶你到河邊。"},{"en":"Follow that means take that path, route, or instruction.","zh":"沿着那條路走，意思是走剛才提到的道路、路線或指示。"},{"en":"When you see the red signs, follow that route to the exit.","zh":"當你看見紅色標誌時，沿着那條路線走到出口。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to something just mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回剛提到的東西。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken directions.","zh":"它常見於口頭指路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"You might be interested to","meaning":"你可能會有興趣","examples":[{"en":"You might be interested to see the rubbish pit.","zh":"你可能會有興趣看看垃圾坑。"},{"en":"You might be interested to means you may find something worth seeing or knowing.","zh":"你可能會有興趣，意思是你可能覺得某事值得看或知道。"},{"en":"You might be interested to know that this building is over two hundred years old.","zh":"你可能會有興趣知道這棟建築已有二百多年歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase politely introduces extra information.","zh":"這個短語有禮貌地引出額外資料。"},{"en":"It is often used by guides and presenters.","zh":"它常由導遊和匯報者使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rubbish pit","meaning":"垃圾坑","examples":[{"en":"The rubbish pit is near the castle walls.","zh":"垃圾坑靠近城堡牆。"},{"en":"A rubbish pit is a hole or area where people threw waste in the past.","zh":"垃圾坑，是過去人們丟棄廢物的洞或區域。"},{"en":"Archaeologists study rubbish pits because waste can reveal what people ate and used.","zh":"考古學家研究垃圾坑，因為垃圾可以揭示人們吃甚麼和使用甚麼。"},{"en":"A rubbish pit may contain shells, bones, pottery, and broken tools.","zh":"垃圾坑可能包含貝殼、骨頭、陶器和破損工具。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a waste area that can become useful evidence.","zh":"這個短語指一個可成為有用證據的廢物區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"castle walls","meaning":"城堡牆","examples":[{"en":"The rubbish pit is very near the castle walls.","zh":"垃圾坑非常接近城堡牆。"},{"en":"Castle walls are the strong walls built around or as part of a castle.","zh":"城堡牆，是圍繞城堡或作為城堡一部分建造的堅固牆壁。"},{"en":"Castle walls were designed to protect people inside from attack.","zh":"城堡牆的設計是為了保護裏面的人免受攻擊。"},{"en":"Objects near castle walls may be connected to castle life.","zh":"城堡牆附近的物件可能與城堡生活有關。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to defensive stone structures.","zh":"這個短語指防禦性的石造結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"northwest corner","meaning":"西北角","examples":[{"en":"The rubbish pit is in the northwest corner of the site.","zh":"垃圾坑位於遺址的西北角。"},{"en":"Northwest corner means the corner between north and west.","zh":"西北角，意思是北方與西方之間的角落。"},{"en":"The car park is in the northwest corner of the school grounds.","zh":"停車場位於校園的西北角。"},{"en":"Using compass directions helps visitors find exact areas on a map.","zh":"使用羅盤方向有助訪客在地圖上找到準確區域。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise location within a larger area.","zh":"這個短語在較大範圍內給出精確位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"date to the time of","meaning":"追溯至……時期","examples":[{"en":"The rubbish pit dates to the time of the castle.","zh":"垃圾坑可追溯至城堡時期。"},{"en":"To date to the time of something means to come from the same historical period as it.","zh":"追溯至某時期，意思是來自與該事物相同的歷史時期。"},{"en":"The pottery dates to the time of the old village.","zh":"這些陶器可追溯至舊村莊時期。"},{"en":"Dating an object helps archaeologists connect it with a particular period.","zh":"判斷物件年代有助考古學家把它與特定時期連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing age and historical context.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論年代和歷史背景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not the ancient village","meaning":"不是古代村莊","examples":[{"en":"The rubbish pit dates to the castle, not the ancient village.","zh":"垃圾坑可追溯至城堡時期，不是古代村莊時期。"},{"en":"Not the ancient village means the object or feature belongs to another period or place, not that village.","zh":"不是古代村莊，意思是該物件或特徵屬於另一個時期或地方，而不是那條村莊。"},{"en":"These bones came from the castle kitchen, not the ancient village.","zh":"這些骨頭來自城堡廚房，不是古代村莊。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects a possible misunderstanding.","zh":"這個短語糾正可能的誤解。"},{"en":"It helps separate evidence from different historical periods.","zh":"它有助分開不同歷史時期的證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"oyster shells","meaning":"蠔殼","examples":[{"en":"The team found oyster shells in the rubbish pit.","zh":"團隊在垃圾坑中找到蠔殼。"},{"en":"Oyster shells are the hard outer shells of oysters, a type of shellfish.","zh":"蠔殼，是蠔這種貝類的堅硬外殼。"},{"en":"Oyster shells in a rubbish pit can show that people ate seafood.","zh":"垃圾坑中的蠔殼可以顯示人們曾吃海鮮。"},{"en":"Old oyster shells may help researchers understand diet and trade.","zh":"舊蠔殼可能幫助研究人員了解飲食和貿易。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to food remains that can become archaeological evidence.","zh":"這個短語指可以成為考古證據的食物殘留。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fish bones","meaning":"魚骨","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologists found fish bones in the rubbish pit.","zh":"考古學家在垃圾坑中找到魚骨。"},{"en":"Fish bones are the hard skeletal parts left after fish have been eaten or decomposed.","zh":"魚骨，是魚被吃掉或分解後留下的堅硬骨骼部分。"},{"en":"Fish bones can show what kinds of fish people caught or bought.","zh":"魚骨可以顯示人們捕捉或購買了哪些魚。"},{"en":"Finding fish bones near a castle kitchen suggests seafood was part of the diet.","zh":"在城堡廚房附近發現魚骨，暗示海鮮是飲食的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to animal remains connected with food.","zh":"這個短語指與食物有關的動物遺骸。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"assume","meaning":"推測；假設","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologists assume the shells and bones were thrown from the kitchen.","zh":"考古學家推測這些殼和骨頭是從廚房丟下來的。"},{"en":"To assume means to think something is probably true without complete proof.","zh":"推測或假設，意思是在沒有完整證明下認為某事可能是真的。"},{"en":"We should not assume a building was a house until we have more evidence.","zh":"在有更多證據前，我們不應假設一棟建築是房屋。"},{"en":"Researchers may assume something at first, then test it with evidence.","zh":"研究人員可能先作出假設，然後用證據測試它。"},{"en":"This word shows a careful guess rather than a confirmed fact.","zh":"這個詞表示謹慎猜測，而不是已確認事實。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be thrown from","meaning":"從……被丟下","examples":[{"en":"The oyster shells were probably thrown from the castle kitchen.","zh":"蠔殼很可能是從城堡廚房被丟下來的。"},{"en":"To be thrown from somewhere means to be tossed or dropped out of that place.","zh":"從某處被丟下，意思是從那個地方被拋出或掉下。"},{"en":"Old rubbish may have been thrown from windows into a pit below.","zh":"舊垃圾可能曾從窗戶被丟到下面的坑中。"},{"en":"Objects thrown from a kitchen can reveal food habits.","zh":"從廚房被丟下的物件可以揭示飲食習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the likely movement of discarded items.","zh":"這個短語描述被丟棄物件的可能移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"castle kitchen","meaning":"城堡廚房","examples":[{"en":"The rubbish may have come from the castle kitchen above.","zh":"這些垃圾可能來自上方的城堡廚房。"},{"en":"A castle kitchen is the place in a castle where food was prepared and cooked.","zh":"城堡廚房，是城堡中準備和烹調食物的地方。"},{"en":"A castle kitchen may have produced bones, shells, broken pots, and ash.","zh":"城堡廚房可能產生骨頭、貝殼、破陶器和灰燼。"},{"en":"Rubbish from a castle kitchen can show what people in the castle ate.","zh":"來自城堡廚房的垃圾可以顯示城堡裏的人吃甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase connects food waste with castle life.","zh":"這個短語把食物廢料與城堡生活連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"excavate an area","meaning":"發掘一個區域","examples":[{"en":"The team excavated one area in the first summer.","zh":"團隊在第一個夏天發掘了一個區域。"},{"en":"To excavate an area means to dig and study one specific part of a site.","zh":"發掘一個區域，意思是挖掘並研究遺址中的某個特定部分。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may excavate an area slowly to record every layer of soil.","zh":"考古學家可能會慢慢發掘一個區域，以記錄每一層泥土。"},{"en":"Excavating one area first helps the team decide where to dig next.","zh":"先發掘一個區域有助團隊決定下一步在哪裏挖掘。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful archaeological digging in a chosen place.","zh":"這個短語描述在選定地方進行的仔細考古挖掘。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"uncover the site of","meaning":"揭露……的遺址","examples":[{"en":"The excavation uncovered the site of a meeting hall.","zh":"發掘揭露了一座會議廳的遺址。"},{"en":"To uncover the site of a building means to reveal where that building once stood.","zh":"揭露某建築的遺址，意思是顯示該建築曾經所在的位置。"},{"en":"Digging uncovered the site of an old workshop near the river.","zh":"挖掘揭露了河邊一個舊工場的遺址。"},{"en":"Uncovering the site of a building helps researchers map the settlement.","zh":"揭露建築遺址有助研究人員繪製聚落地圖。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when remains reveal a former location.","zh":"當遺跡顯示昔日位置時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"meeting hall","meaning":"會議廳","examples":[{"en":"The team uncovered the site of a meeting hall.","zh":"團隊揭露了一座會議廳的遺址。"},{"en":"A meeting hall is a large building or room where people gather for discussions or events.","zh":"會議廳，是人們聚集討論或舉行活動的大型建築或房間。"},{"en":"An ancient meeting hall may have been used for village decisions or ceremonies.","zh":"古代會議廳可能用於村莊決策或儀式。"},{"en":"Finding a meeting hall suggests the settlement had organised community life.","zh":"發現會議廳暗示該聚落有組織化的社區生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important public gathering place.","zh":"這個短語描述重要的公共聚集場所。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"important building","meaning":"重要建築","examples":[{"en":"The meeting hall was an important building.","zh":"會議廳是一座重要建築。"},{"en":"An important building is a structure that has special social, political, religious, or practical value.","zh":"重要建築，是具有特殊社會、政治、宗教或實用價值的結構。"},{"en":"A town hall is an important building because local decisions may be made there.","zh":"市政廳是重要建築，因為本地決策可能在那裏作出。"},{"en":"Important buildings often appear in central or visible parts of a settlement.","zh":"重要建築通常出現在聚落中央或顯眼位置。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a structure matters more than ordinary buildings.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某結構比普通建築更重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"two rows of","meaning":"兩排","examples":[{"en":"The building had two rows of post holes.","zh":"這棟建築有兩排柱洞。"},{"en":"Two rows of something means two straight lines or groups of items.","zh":"兩排某物，意思是兩條直線或兩組物件。"},{"en":"The classroom had two rows of desks near the windows.","zh":"課室窗邊有兩排書桌。"},{"en":"Two rows of post holes can show where roof supports once stood.","zh":"兩排柱洞可以顯示屋頂支撐曾經所在的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe arrangement and structure.","zh":"這個短語有助描述排列和結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"post holes","meaning":"柱洞","examples":[{"en":"The meeting hall had two rows of post holes.","zh":"會議廳有兩排柱洞。"},{"en":"Post holes are holes in the ground where wooden posts once stood.","zh":"柱洞，是地面上曾放置木柱的洞。"},{"en":"Archaeologists use post holes to understand the shape of ancient buildings.","zh":"考古學家利用柱洞了解古代建築的形狀。"},{"en":"Rows of post holes may show where walls or roof supports were placed.","zh":"一排排柱洞可能顯示牆壁或屋頂支撐的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to small but important evidence of former structures.","zh":"這個短語指舊結構留下的小而重要的證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"deep enough to support","meaning":"深度足以支撐","examples":[{"en":"The post holes were deep enough to support a large roof.","zh":"這些柱洞深度足以支撐大型屋頂。"},{"en":"Deep enough to support something means having enough depth to hold it safely.","zh":"深度足以支撐某物，意思是有足夠深度安全承托它。"},{"en":"Fence posts must be deep enough to support the fence in strong wind.","zh":"圍欄柱必須有足夠深度來在強風中支撐圍欄。"},{"en":"If post holes are deep enough to support a large roof, the building was probably substantial.","zh":"如果柱洞深度足以支撐大型屋頂，該建築很可能相當堅固。"},{"en":"This phrase connects depth with strength and function.","zh":"這個短語把深度與強度和功能連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"large roof","meaning":"大型屋頂","examples":[{"en":"The post holes could support a large roof.","zh":"這些柱洞可以支撐大型屋頂。"},{"en":"A large roof is a big covering structure over a building.","zh":"大型屋頂，是覆蓋建築物的大型上方結構。"},{"en":"A hall needs a large roof if many people gather inside.","zh":"如果很多人在大廳內聚集，大廳就需要大型屋頂。"},{"en":"Evidence for a large roof suggests the building may have been important.","zh":"有大型屋頂的證據暗示該建築可能很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the size of the upper part of a structure.","zh":"這個短語描述結構上方部分的大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the largest structure","meaning":"最大的結構","examples":[{"en":"The meeting hall is the largest structure in the central area.","zh":"會議廳是中央區域最大的結構。"},{"en":"The largest structure is the biggest building or built feature in a group or area.","zh":"最大的結構，是一組或一個區域中最大的建築或人工特徵。"},{"en":"The largest structure in the park is the sports hall.","zh":"公園中最大的結構是體育館。"},{"en":"The largest structure on a site often attracts special attention from archaeologists.","zh":"遺址上最大的結構通常會特別吸引考古學家注意。"},{"en":"This phrase compares size within a particular place.","zh":"這個短語比較某地內部的大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"central area of the site","meaning":"遺址中央區域","examples":[{"en":"The meeting hall is in the central area of the site.","zh":"會議廳位於遺址中央區域。"},{"en":"The central area of the site is the middle part of the archaeological location.","zh":"遺址中央區域，是考古地點的中間部分。"},{"en":"Important buildings are often found in the central area of a settlement.","zh":"重要建築通常在聚落中央區域被發現。"},{"en":"Studying the central area of the site helps researchers understand how the settlement was organised.","zh":"研究遺址中央區域有助研究人員了解聚落如何組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both position and archaeological focus.","zh":"這個短語同時描述位置和考古焦點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"current excavation area","meaning":"目前發掘區","examples":[{"en":"The meeting hall is next to the current excavation area.","zh":"會議廳位於目前發掘區旁邊。"},{"en":"The current excavation area is the part of the site being dug and studied now.","zh":"目前發掘區，是遺址中現在正在挖掘和研究的部分。"},{"en":"Visitors should not enter the current excavation area without permission.","zh":"未經許可，訪客不應進入目前發掘區。"},{"en":"The current excavation area may change as the project develops.","zh":"隨着項目發展，目前發掘區可能會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where active archaeological work is happening.","zh":"這個短語指出考古工作正在進行的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fish pond","meaning":"魚塘","examples":[{"en":"The team discovered a fish pond in the ancient village.","zh":"團隊在古代村莊中發現一個魚塘。"},{"en":"A fish pond is a small area of water where fish are kept or raised.","zh":"魚塘，是用來養魚或飼養魚類的小型水域。"},{"en":"A fish pond near a village may have provided food for local people.","zh":"村莊附近的魚塘可能為本地人提供食物。"},{"en":"Finding a fish pond can show how people managed water and food supplies.","zh":"發現魚塘可以顯示人們如何管理水和食物供應。"},{"en":"This phrase connects archaeology with daily life and farming.","zh":"這個短語把考古與日常生活和農業連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"beside a river","meaning":"在河邊","examples":[{"en":"Fish ponds were normally beside a river.","zh":"魚塘通常在河邊。"},{"en":"Beside a river means next to or very near a river.","zh":"在河邊，意思是在河流旁邊或非常接近河流。"},{"en":"Many old villages were built beside a river because water was useful.","zh":"許多舊村莊建在河邊，因為水很有用。"},{"en":"A fish pond beside a river can be easier to fill and maintain.","zh":"在河邊的魚塘可能較容易注水和維持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location near running water.","zh":"這個短語描述接近流水的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"further away","meaning":"較遠","examples":[{"en":"The pond here is further away from the river.","zh":"這裏的魚塘離河較遠。"},{"en":"Further away means at a greater distance from something.","zh":"較遠，意思是與某物的距離更大。"},{"en":"The newer houses are further away from the town centre.","zh":"較新的房屋離市中心較遠。"},{"en":"If a pond is further away from the river, researchers may ask whether the river once moved.","zh":"如果魚塘離河較遠，研究人員可能會問河流是否曾經移動。"},{"en":"This phrase compares distance.","zh":"這個短語用來比較距離。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"move slightly","meaning":"稍微移動","examples":[{"en":"It is possible that the river has moved slightly.","zh":"河流有可能稍微移動過。"},{"en":"To move slightly means to change position by a small amount.","zh":"稍微移動，意思是位置有小幅改變。"},{"en":"Over many years, a river can move slightly across a valley.","zh":"經過多年，河流可以在山谷中稍微移動。"},{"en":"If the river moved slightly, old water features may now appear farther away.","zh":"如果河流稍微移動，舊水利設施現在可能看起來較遠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small change in position.","zh":"這個短語描述位置上的小變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Anyway","meaning":"總之","examples":[{"en":"Anyway, turn right at the first information board.","zh":"總之，在你遇到的第一個資料牌右轉。"},{"en":"Anyway is used to return to the main point or continue after a side comment.","zh":"Anyway 用來回到重點或在插話後繼續。"},{"en":"Anyway, let’s go back to the map and check the route.","zh":"總之，讓我們回到地圖並檢查路線。"},{"en":"This word helps a speaker move the conversation forward.","zh":"這個詞幫助說話者推進對話。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken English.","zh":"它常見於口語英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"turn right at","meaning":"在……右轉","examples":[{"en":"Turn right at the first information board.","zh":"在第一個資料牌右轉。"},{"en":"To turn right at a place means to change direction to the right when you reach that place.","zh":"在某處右轉，意思是到達那個地方時向右改變方向。"},{"en":"Turn right at the traffic lights to reach the museum.","zh":"在交通燈右轉即可到達博物館。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in directions with a landmark.","zh":"這個短語用於帶有地標的指路。"},{"en":"It tells the listener exactly where to change direction.","zh":"它告訴聽者在哪裏改變方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"information board","meaning":"資料牌","examples":[{"en":"Turn right at the first information board you come to.","zh":"在你遇到的第一個資料牌右轉。"},{"en":"An information board is a sign that gives facts, maps, rules, or explanations.","zh":"資料牌，是提供事實、地圖、規則或解說的標誌。"},{"en":"Visitors can read the information board to learn about the ancient village.","zh":"訪客可以閱讀資料牌，了解古代村莊。"},{"en":"Information boards help people understand a site without needing a guide all the time.","zh":"資料牌幫助人們即使沒有導遊也能了解遺址。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a public display of useful information.","zh":"這個短語指公開展示實用資料的牌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"follow the path into","meaning":"沿小路進入……","examples":[{"en":"Follow the path into the trees.","zh":"沿小路進入樹林。"},{"en":"To follow the path into a place means to continue along the path until it enters that place.","zh":"沿小路進入某處，意思是沿着小路繼續走，直到進入那個地方。"},{"en":"Follow the path into the garden and you will see the pond.","zh":"沿小路進入花園，你會看到池塘。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear walking direction.","zh":"這個短語給出清楚的步行方向。"},{"en":"It connects a route with the area it leads into.","zh":"它把路線與其通往的區域連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"come out of the trees","meaning":"走出樹林","examples":[{"en":"Before you come out of the trees, you will see the pond.","zh":"在你走出樹林之前，你會看見魚塘。"},{"en":"To come out of the trees means to leave the wooded area and enter open space.","zh":"走出樹林，意思是離開樹木覆蓋的區域並進入開闊地方。"},{"en":"When you come out of the trees, the river will be ahead of you.","zh":"當你走出樹林時，河流會在你前方。"},{"en":"This phrase helps walkers recognise a point on the route.","zh":"這個短語幫助行人辨認路線上的一點。"},{"en":"It describes movement from a wooded area to a more open area.","zh":"它描述由樹林區移到較開闊地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on your right","meaning":"在你右手邊","examples":[{"en":"You will see the fish pond on your right.","zh":"你會在右手邊看見魚塘。"},{"en":"On your right means on the right-hand side of where you are facing or moving.","zh":"在你右手邊，意思是在你面向或前進方向的右側。"},{"en":"The library is on your right after you pass the office.","zh":"你經過辦公室後，圖書館在你右手邊。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in spoken directions.","zh":"這個短語常見於口頭指路。"},{"en":"It helps people locate something while walking.","zh":"它幫助人們在步行時找到某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"go too far","meaning":"走得太遠","examples":[{"en":"If you reach the river, you have gone too far.","zh":"如果你到達河邊，就表示你走得太遠了。"},{"en":"To go too far means to pass the place where you should have stopped or turned.","zh":"走得太遠，意思是越過了你應該停下或轉彎的地方。"},{"en":"If you see the supermarket, you have gone too far; the clinic is before it.","zh":"如果你看見超級市場，就表示你走得太遠了；診所在它之前。"},{"en":"This phrase helps correct someone’s route.","zh":"這個短語有助糾正某人的路線。"},{"en":"It is useful in directions when a landmark marks a mistake.","zh":"當某個地標表示走錯時，它在指路中很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be responsible for starting","meaning":"負責開展","examples":[{"en":"The question asks who was responsible for starting the community project.","zh":"這個問題問誰負責開展這個社區計劃。"},{"en":"To be responsible for starting something means to be the person or group that began it.","zh":"負責開展某事，意思是成為開始該事的人或團體。"},{"en":"The history teacher was responsible for starting the school museum club.","zh":"歷史老師負責開展學校博物館學會。"},{"en":"Knowing who was responsible for starting a project helps explain its origins.","zh":"知道誰負責開展一個項目，有助解釋其起源。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a person or organisation with the beginning of an activity.","zh":"這個短語把人或組織與活動的開始連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"castle owners","meaning":"城堡主人","examples":[{"en":"The castle owners let the archaeologists use their facilities.","zh":"城堡主人讓考古學家使用他們的設施。"},{"en":"Castle owners are the people or organisation that own the castle.","zh":"城堡主人，是擁有城堡的人或組織。"},{"en":"Castle owners may allow visitors to tour the building during summer.","zh":"城堡主人可能允許訪客在夏天參觀建築。"},{"en":"If castle owners support a project, researchers may gain access to useful spaces.","zh":"如果城堡主人支持項目，研究人員可能可以使用有用空間。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the people with control over the castle property.","zh":"這個短語指出控制城堡物業的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"national charity","meaning":"全國性慈善機構","examples":[{"en":"NHA is described as a national charity.","zh":"NHA 被描述為全國性慈善機構。"},{"en":"A national charity is a charity that works across a whole country.","zh":"全國性慈善機構，是在整個國家範圍內工作的慈善組織。"},{"en":"A national charity may run projects in many towns and cities.","zh":"全國性慈善機構可能在許多城鎮和城市推行項目。"},{"en":"If a national charity supports a local project, it can bring experience and resources.","zh":"如果全國性慈善機構支持本地項目，它可以帶來經驗和資源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the organisation’s purpose and its wide reach.","zh":"這個短語同時描述組織目的和廣泛覆蓋範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"local council","meaning":"本地議會","examples":[{"en":"The local council is connected with the archaeology project.","zh":"本地議會與這個考古項目有關。"},{"en":"A local council is a government organisation that manages services in a local area.","zh":"本地議會，是管理本地區服務的政府組織。"},{"en":"A local council may support heritage projects, parks, roads, and community events.","zh":"本地議會可能支援文化遺產項目、公園、道路和社區活動。"},{"en":"If the local council is involved, the project may receive official support.","zh":"如果本地議會參與，項目可能得到官方支持。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to local government rather than national government.","zh":"這個短語指地方政府，而不是中央政府。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"heavy rain","meaning":"大雨","examples":[{"en":"Heavy rain had removed some of the soil.","zh":"大雨移走了部分泥土。"},{"en":"Heavy rain means a large amount of rain falling strongly.","zh":"大雨，意思是大量而強烈的降雨。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can flood streets and wash soil from fields.","zh":"大雨可以淹浸街道並沖走田地泥土。"},{"en":"At an archaeological site, heavy rain may reveal objects but also damage evidence.","zh":"在考古遺址，大雨可能顯露物件，但也可能損壞證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weather that can have strong physical effects.","zh":"這個短語描述會造成強烈實際影響的天氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"remove some of the soil","meaning":"移走部分泥土","examples":[{"en":"Heavy rain removed some of the soil from the ground.","zh":"大雨從地面移走了部分泥土。"},{"en":"To remove some of the soil means to take away part of the earth covering a surface.","zh":"移走部分泥土，意思是取走覆蓋表面的部分泥土。"},{"en":"Builders removed some of the soil before laying the foundation.","zh":"建築工人在鋪設地基前移走了部分泥土。"},{"en":"When rain removes soil, buried objects may become visible.","zh":"當雨水移走泥土時，埋藏物件可能會變得可見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change to the ground surface.","zh":"這個短語描述地面表層的改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"dig up","meaning":"挖起；翻出","examples":[{"en":"The ground may be dug up by wild rabbits.","zh":"地面可能被野兔挖起。"},{"en":"To dig up something means to bring it to the surface by digging.","zh":"挖起某物，意思是透過挖掘把它帶到地面。"},{"en":"A dog may dig up a bone in the garden.","zh":"狗可能會在花園裏挖出骨頭。"},{"en":"Wild animals can dig up old objects without meaning to.","zh":"野生動物可能會無意中挖出古老物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uncovering something from underground.","zh":"這個短語描述從地下顯露某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"wild rabbits","meaning":"野兔","examples":[{"en":"Wild rabbits can dig tunnels in the ground.","zh":"野兔可以在地下挖洞穴。"},{"en":"Wild rabbits are rabbits that live in nature rather than as pets.","zh":"野兔，是在自然中生活，而不是作為寵物飼養的兔子。"},{"en":"Wild rabbits often dig burrows to live safely underground.","zh":"野兔常挖洞穴，在地下安全生活。"},{"en":"Their digging can disturb soil and uncover hidden objects.","zh":"牠們的挖掘可以擾動泥土並翻出隱藏物件。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a common wild animal that can affect archaeological sites.","zh":"這個短語指一種常見、可能影響考古遺址的野生動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a person with a metal detector","meaning":"持金屬探測器的人","examples":[{"en":"A person with a metal detector may search an archaeological area.","zh":"持金屬探測器的人可能會搜尋考古區域。"},{"en":"A person with a metal detector is someone using a device to find metal objects.","zh":"持金屬探測器的人，是使用裝置尋找金屬物件的人。"},{"en":"A person with a metal detector might find coins on a beach or in a field.","zh":"持金屬探測器的人可能會在海灘或田野找到硬幣。"},{"en":"On historic sites, such searching may need permission.","zh":"在歷史遺址上，這類搜尋可能需要許可。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the person and the tool they are using.","zh":"這個短語同時描述人和他使用的工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lead someone to believe","meaning":"令某人相信","examples":[{"en":"The records led archaeologists to believe there was an ancient village.","zh":"這些記錄令考古學家相信曾有一條古代村莊。"},{"en":"To lead someone to believe something means to make them think it is probably true.","zh":"令某人相信某事，意思是使他們認為某事很可能是真的。"},{"en":"The footprints led police to believe someone had entered the building.","zh":"足跡令警方相信有人曾進入建築物。"},{"en":"Old maps can lead researchers to believe a settlement once existed.","zh":"舊地圖可以令研究人員相信某處曾有聚落。"},{"en":"This phrase connects evidence with a conclusion.","zh":"這個短語把證據與結論連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lucky discovery","meaning":"幸運發現","examples":[{"en":"The lucky discovery of old records helped the team understand the site.","zh":"舊記錄的幸運發現幫助團隊了解遺址。"},{"en":"A lucky discovery is something useful found by chance.","zh":"幸運發現，是偶然找到的有用東西。"},{"en":"Finding an old photo in a cupboard was a lucky discovery for the family historian.","zh":"在櫃中找到一張舊照片，對家族歷史研究者來說是幸運發現。"},{"en":"A lucky discovery can change the direction of a research project.","zh":"幸運發現可以改變研究項目的方向。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises both usefulness and chance.","zh":"這個短語同時強調有用和偶然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"old records","meaning":"舊記錄","examples":[{"en":"Old records showed drawings of ruined buildings.","zh":"舊記錄顯示了廢墟建築的圖畫。"},{"en":"Old records are written, printed, or drawn documents from the past.","zh":"舊記錄，是來自過去的書寫、印刷或繪畫文件。"},{"en":"Old records may include maps, letters, tax lists, and drawings.","zh":"舊記錄可能包括地圖、信件、稅務清單和圖畫。"},{"en":"Researchers use old records to compare past information with present evidence.","zh":"研究人員使用舊記錄把過去資料與現有證據比較。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to historical documents that can support research.","zh":"這個短語指可以支援研究的歷史文件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bases of several structures","meaning":"幾座結構的基座","examples":[{"en":"The bases of several structures may suggest an ancient settlement.","zh":"幾座結構的基座可能暗示有古代聚落。"},{"en":"The bases of several structures are the lower parts or foundations of more than one building.","zh":"幾座結構的基座，是多於一座建築的底部或地基。"},{"en":"Archaeologists found the bases of several structures under the grass.","zh":"考古學家在草地下面找到幾座結構的基座。"},{"en":"Bases of structures can reveal where walls and posts once stood.","zh":"結構基座可以揭示牆壁和柱子曾經所在的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to physical remains that help map a site.","zh":"這個短語指幫助繪製遺址地圖的實體遺跡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"visible in the grass","meaning":"在草地上可見","examples":[{"en":"Some archaeological features can be visible in the grass.","zh":"一些考古特徵可以在草地上可見。"},{"en":"Visible in the grass means able to be seen as marks, shapes, or changes in grassy land.","zh":"在草地上可見，意思是可以以痕跡、形狀或草地變化被看見。"},{"en":"Old walls may be visible in the grass as raised lines.","zh":"舊牆可能以凸起線條形式在草地上可見。"},{"en":"Features visible in the grass can guide archaeologists to places worth digging.","zh":"在草地上可見的特徵可以引導考古學家找到值得挖掘的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence seen on the ground surface.","zh":"這個短語描述在地面表層可見的證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unusual stones","meaning":"不尋常的石頭","examples":[{"en":"Unusual stones near the castle could be important evidence.","zh":"城堡附近不尋常的石頭可能是重要證據。"},{"en":"Unusual stones are stones that look different from the natural ground or ordinary stones nearby.","zh":"不尋常的石頭，是看起來與天然地面或附近普通石頭不同的石頭。"},{"en":"Unusual stones in a straight line may suggest an old wall or path.","zh":"排成直線的不尋常石頭可能暗示舊牆或道路。"},{"en":"Archaeologists examine unusual stones because they may have been placed by people.","zh":"考古學家檢查不尋常的石頭，因為它們可能曾由人放置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes objects that stand out and may need investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述突出的、可能需要調查的物件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"still hoping to find","meaning":"仍希望找到","examples":[{"en":"The team is still hoping to find pieces of jewellery.","zh":"團隊仍希望找到首飾碎件。"},{"en":"Still hoping to find means continuing to wish or expect that something will be discovered.","zh":"仍希望找到，意思是繼續希望或期待某物會被發現。"},{"en":"The students are still hoping to find more information for their report.","zh":"學生仍希望為報告找到更多資料。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may be still hoping to find rare objects after many ordinary finds.","zh":"考古學家在找到很多普通物件後，可能仍希望找到稀有物件。"},{"en":"This phrase shows continued expectation.","zh":"這個短語表示持續期待。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"everyday pottery","meaning":"日常陶器","examples":[{"en":"Everyday pottery is often found on ancient village sites.","zh":"古代村莊遺址常發現日常陶器。"},{"en":"Everyday pottery means ordinary pots, bowls, and containers used in daily life.","zh":"日常陶器，是日常生活中使用的普通陶罐、碗和容器。"},{"en":"Everyday pottery can show what people cooked, stored, and ate.","zh":"日常陶器可以顯示人們煮甚麼、儲存甚麼和吃甚麼。"},{"en":"Even simple everyday pottery can provide important evidence about past life.","zh":"即使是簡單的日常陶器，也可以提供關於過去生活的重要證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to common objects, not luxury items.","zh":"這個短語指常見物件，而不是奢侈品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"pieces of jewellery","meaning":"首飾碎件","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologists are hoping to find pieces of jewellery.","zh":"考古學家希望找到首飾碎件。"},{"en":"Pieces of jewellery are items such as rings, necklaces, brooches, or decorative metal objects.","zh":"首飾碎件，是戒指、項鏈、胸針或裝飾金屬物件等物品。"},{"en":"Pieces of jewellery can show fashion, wealth, and personal identity in the past.","zh":"首飾碎件可以顯示過去的時尚、財富和個人身份。"},{"en":"If archaeologists find pieces of jewellery, they may learn about trade and craftsmanship.","zh":"如果考古學家找到首飾碎件，他們可能了解貿易和工藝。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to decorative personal objects.","zh":"這個短語指裝飾性的個人物件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the outline of fields","meaning":"田地輪廓","examples":[{"en":"The team found the outline of fields across the river.","zh":"團隊在河對岸發現田地輪廓。"},{"en":"The outline of fields means the visible shape or borders of old farming areas.","zh":"田地輪廓，意思是舊農田區域的可見形狀或邊界。"},{"en":"The outline of fields may appear as lines, banks, or changes in grass colour.","zh":"田地輪廓可能以線條、土壟或草色變化出現。"},{"en":"Finding the outline of fields can show where people farmed.","zh":"發現田地輪廓可以顯示人們曾在哪裏耕作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the shape of past land use.","zh":"這個短語描述過去土地使用的形狀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a number of small huts","meaning":"若干小屋","examples":[{"en":"The team has not found a number of small huts.","zh":"團隊尚未發現若干小屋。"},{"en":"A number of small huts means several small, simple buildings.","zh":"若干小屋，意思是幾座細小而簡單的建築。"},{"en":"Archaeologists expected a number of small huts near the field system.","zh":"考古學家原本預期在田地系統附近找到若干小屋。"},{"en":"Finding a number of small huts would suggest people lived or worked there.","zh":"發現若干小屋會暗示人們曾在那裏居住或工作。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate number and type of structure.","zh":"這個短語給出大約數量和結構類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"after work ends","meaning":"工作結束後","examples":[{"en":"The team has plans for after work ends this summer.","zh":"團隊有今年夏天工作結束後的計劃。"},{"en":"After work ends means after the current work or project activity is finished.","zh":"工作結束後，意思是目前工作或項目活動完成之後。"},{"en":"After work ends on the site, the team will clean and label the objects.","zh":"遺址工作結束後，團隊會清潔和標籤物件。"},{"en":"Plans for after work ends help a project continue beyond digging.","zh":"工作結束後的計劃有助項目在挖掘之外繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase connects the end of one stage with the next stage.","zh":"這個短語把一個階段的結束與下一個階段連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"prepare a display for a museum","meaning":"為博物館準備展覽","examples":[{"en":"The team may prepare a display for a museum.","zh":"團隊可能會為博物館準備展覽。"},{"en":"To prepare a display for a museum means to organise objects, labels, and information for public viewing.","zh":"為博物館準備展覽，意思是組織物件、標籤和資料，供公眾觀看。"},{"en":"Students helped prepare a display for a museum about local farming history.","zh":"學生幫忙為博物館準備一個關於本地農業歷史的展覽。"},{"en":"Preparing a museum display helps share research with the public.","zh":"準備博物館展覽有助把研究與公眾分享。"},{"en":"This phrase connects archaeological finds with education and exhibition.","zh":"這個短語把考古發現與教育和展覽連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take part in a television programme","meaning":"參與電視節目","examples":[{"en":"The team may take part in a television programme.","zh":"團隊可能會參與電視節目。"},{"en":"To take part in a television programme means to appear in or contribute to a TV show.","zh":"參與電視節目，意思是在電視節目中出現或作出貢獻。"},{"en":"A scientist may take part in a television programme to explain a discovery.","zh":"科學家可能會參與電視節目來解釋一項發現。"},{"en":"Taking part in a programme can help the public learn about the project.","zh":"參與節目可以幫助公眾了解項目。"},{"en":"This phrase describes participation in broadcast media.","zh":"這個短語描述參與廣播媒體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"organise school visits","meaning":"組織學校參觀","examples":[{"en":"The project will organise school visits in the autumn.","zh":"這個項目會在秋天組織學校參觀。"},{"en":"To organise school visits means to plan visits for groups of students and teachers.","zh":"組織學校參觀，意思是為學生和老師團體策劃參觀活動。"},{"en":"A museum may organise school visits with worksheets and guided tours.","zh":"博物館可能會配合工作紙和導賞團來組織學校參觀。"},{"en":"Organising school visits helps young people learn from real places and objects.","zh":"組織學校參觀有助年輕人從真實地方和物件中學習。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to planning educational trips for schools.","zh":"這個短語指為學校策劃教育參觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"ielts/listening/Practice 3/task-3":[{"front":"theatre studies students","meaning":"戲劇研究學生","examples":[{"en":"Two theatre studies students discuss their project.","zh":"兩名戲劇研究學生討論他們的專題。"},{"en":"Theatre studies students are students who study plays, acting, performance, and theatre history.","zh":"戲劇研究學生是研究戲劇、演技、表演和劇場歷史的學生。"},{"en":"Theatre studies students may visit theatres to learn how performances are prepared.","zh":"戲劇研究學生可能會參觀劇院，學習演出如何準備。"},{"en":"Theatre studies students often analyse scripts, actors, audiences, and stage design.","zh":"戲劇研究學生常分析劇本、演員、觀眾和舞台設計。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies students whose subject is theatre.","zh":"這個片語指出學生的學科是戲劇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"project on theatre programmes","meaning":"關於劇場節目單的專題","examples":[{"en":"Maya and Finn are working on a project on theatre programmes.","zh":"Maya 和 Finn 正在做一個關於劇場節目單的專題。"},{"en":"A project on theatre programmes is a study about printed or digital booklets given to theatre audiences.","zh":"關於劇場節目單的專題，是研究提供給劇場觀眾的印刷或數碼小冊子。"},{"en":"Students may do a project on theatre programmes to learn how theatres communicated with audiences.","zh":"學生可能做關於劇場節目單的專題，以了解劇院如何與觀眾溝通。"},{"en":"A project on theatre programmes can include history, design, advertising, and audience information.","zh":"關於劇場節目單的專題可以包括歷史、設計、廣告和觀眾資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the topic of Maya and Finn’s research.","zh":"這個片語描述 Maya 和 Finn 的研究題目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look at questions","meaning":"閱讀題目","examples":[{"en":"The students have time to look at the questions before listening.","zh":"學生在聆聽前有時間閱讀題目。"},{"en":"Look at questions means read the questions carefully before answering them.","zh":"閱讀題目意思是在回答前仔細看問題。"},{"en":"In a listening test, students should look at the questions before the recording starts.","zh":"在聆聽測驗中，學生應在錄音開始前閱讀題目。"},{"en":"Looking at questions first helps listeners know what information to listen for.","zh":"先閱讀題目可以幫助聆聽者知道要聽甚麼資料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an exam preparation step.","zh":"這個片語描述考試前的準備步驟。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"listen carefully","meaning":"仔細聆聽","examples":[{"en":"Candidates listen carefully and answer the questions.","zh":"考生仔細聆聽並回答問題。"},{"en":"Listen carefully means pay close attention to what is being said.","zh":"仔細聆聽意思是專心留意正在說的內容。"},{"en":"Students must listen carefully when the teacher explains safety rules.","zh":"當老師解釋安全規則時，學生必須仔細聆聽。"},{"en":"Listening carefully helps people catch names, dates, and important details.","zh":"仔細聆聽幫助人捕捉名字、日期和重要細節。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used in exams and instructions.","zh":"這個片語常用於考試和指示中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as much as I can","meaning":"盡我所能","examples":[{"en":"Maya has done as much as she can for the project.","zh":"Maya 已經為這個專題盡她所能。"},{"en":"As much as I can means the greatest amount I am able to do.","zh":"盡我所能意思是我能做到的最大程度。"},{"en":"I revised as much as I could before the exam.","zh":"考試前，我盡我所能溫習。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they have tried their best within limits.","zh":"當人們在限制內已經盡力時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It shows effort, even if the work may not be completely finished.","zh":"它顯示努力，即使工作可能尚未完全完成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"How’s your research coming along?","meaning":"你的研究進行得怎麼樣？","examples":[{"en":"Maya asks Finn how his research is coming along.","zh":"Maya 問 Finn 他的研究進行得怎麼樣。"},{"en":"How’s your research coming along? means how is your research progressing?","zh":"你的研究進行得怎麼樣？意思是你的研究進展如何。"},{"en":"“How’s your history research coming along?” the teacher asked.","zh":"老師問：「你的歷史研究進行得怎麼樣？」"},{"en":"People ask this question to check progress in a friendly way.","zh":"人們用這個問題友善地查看進度。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when discussing projects and assignments.","zh":"這個片語在討論專題和功課時很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"theatre programmes","meaning":"劇場節目單","examples":[{"en":"Theatre programmes give audiences information about a performance.","zh":"劇場節目單為觀眾提供關於演出的資料。"},{"en":"Theatre programmes are booklets that tell audiences about a play, musical, cast, and production.","zh":"劇場節目單是介紹戲劇、音樂劇、演員陣容和製作的小冊子。"},{"en":"People may buy theatre programmes before a show to learn about the actors.","zh":"人們可能在演出前購買劇場節目單，以了解演員。"},{"en":"Theatre programmes can also include adverts, articles, pictures, and historical notes.","zh":"劇場節目單也可以包括廣告、文章、圖片和歷史註釋。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to printed or digital information given for a theatre performance.","zh":"這個片語指劇場演出所提供的印刷或數碼資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be called playbills","meaning":"被稱為 playbills","examples":[{"en":"Theatre programmes are called playbills in the USA.","zh":"劇場節目單在美國被稱為 playbills。"},{"en":"Be called playbills means be known by the name “playbills”.","zh":"被稱為 playbills 意思是以 “playbills” 這個名稱為人所知。"},{"en":"In some countries, the same object may be called by a different name.","zh":"在某些國家，同一件物件可能有不同名稱。"},{"en":"Theatre programmes are called playbills in the USA, so researchers should recognise both terms.","zh":"劇場節目單在美國被稱為 playbills，所以研究者應認識兩個詞。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a difference in vocabulary.","zh":"這個片語解釋詞彙上的差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the USA","meaning":"在美國","examples":[{"en":"Theatre programmes are called playbills in the USA.","zh":"劇場節目單在美國被稱為 playbills。"},{"en":"In the USA means in the United States of America.","zh":"在美國意思是在美利堅合眾國。"},{"en":"Some spelling and vocabulary are different in the USA and the UK.","zh":"在美國和英國，有些串字和詞彙不同。"},{"en":"A theatre term used in the USA may not be used in Britain.","zh":"在美國使用的劇場詞語，在英國可能不常用。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the country or cultural context.","zh":"這個片語指出國家或文化背景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"till I started looking into","meaning":"直到我開始研究……才","examples":[{"en":"Finn did not know the term until he started looking into the topic.","zh":"Finn 直到開始研究這個題目，才知道這個詞。"},{"en":"Till I started looking into something means before I began researching it, I did not know it.","zh":"直到我開始研究某事才，意思是在我開始研究之前，我並不知道它。"},{"en":"I had never heard of that artist till I started looking into modern sculpture.","zh":"我直到開始研究現代雕塑，才聽過那位藝術家。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when research changes what they know.","zh":"當研究改變了人們的知識時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It shows that new knowledge came from investigation.","zh":"它顯示新知識來自調查研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look into the topic","meaning":"研究這個題目","examples":[{"en":"Finn started looking into the topic for the project.","zh":"Finn 為這個專題開始研究這個題目。"},{"en":"Look into the topic means research or investigate the subject carefully.","zh":"研究這個題目意思是仔細調查或研究該主題。"},{"en":"Before writing the essay, students looked into the topic online and in the library.","zh":"寫作文前，學生在網上和圖書館研究這個題目。"},{"en":"Looking into a topic helps people find facts, examples, and different views.","zh":"研究題目幫助人找到事實、例子和不同觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in academic research.","zh":"這個片語常用於學術研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"struggle to find","meaning":"很難找到","examples":[{"en":"Finn struggled to find many useful websites.","zh":"Finn 很難找到很多有用的網站。"},{"en":"Struggle to find means have difficulty finding something.","zh":"很難找到意思是尋找某物時遇到困難。"},{"en":"I struggled to find reliable information for my science project.","zh":"我很難為科學專題找到可靠資料。"},{"en":"Students may struggle to find sources when a topic is unusual.","zh":"當題目不常見時，學生可能很難找到資料來源。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the research process was not easy.","zh":"這個片語顯示研究過程並不容易。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"useful websites","meaning":"有用的網站","examples":[{"en":"Finn struggled to find many useful websites about theatre programmes.","zh":"Finn 很難找到很多關於劇場節目單的有用網站。"},{"en":"Useful websites are websites that provide helpful, relevant, and reliable information.","zh":"有用的網站是提供有幫助、相關和可靠資料的網站。"},{"en":"A student needs useful websites when researching a project.","zh":"學生研究專題時需要有用的網站。"},{"en":"Useful websites can save time because they organise information clearly.","zh":"有用的網站能清楚整理資料，因此可以節省時間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes online sources that actually help the researcher.","zh":"這個片語描述真正幫到研究者的網上來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"picked this subject","meaning":"選了這個主題","examples":[{"en":"Finn is glad they picked this subject.","zh":"Finn 很高興他們選了這個主題。"},{"en":"Picked this subject means chose this topic for study or discussion.","zh":"選了這個主題意思是選擇這個題目作研究或討論。"},{"en":"We picked this subject because it connects history with modern media.","zh":"我們選了這個主題，因為它把歷史和現代媒體連起來。"},{"en":"Choosing an unusual subject can make a project more original.","zh":"選擇不常見的主題可以令專題更有原創性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to deciding what topic to research.","zh":"這個片語指決定研究甚麼題目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on the course","meaning":"在課程裏","examples":[{"en":"No one else on the course is doing the same topic.","zh":"課程裏沒有其他人做相同題目。"},{"en":"On the course means studying the same academic course or programme.","zh":"在課程裏意思是修讀同一個學術課程或科目。"},{"en":"Everyone on the course has to give a presentation.","zh":"課程裏每個人都要做簡報。"},{"en":"If no one else on the course chooses the same topic, the project may stand out.","zh":"如果課程裏沒有其他人選相同題目，專題可能更突出。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies people taking the same class or programme.","zh":"這個片語指出修讀同一課程或班別的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the same as us","meaning":"和我們一樣","examples":[{"en":"No one else is doing the same as Maya and Finn.","zh":"沒有其他人和 Maya 及 Finn 做一樣的題目。"},{"en":"The same as us means identical to what we are doing or choosing.","zh":"和我們一樣意思是與我們正在做或選擇的事情相同。"},{"en":"No other group chose the same research question as us.","zh":"沒有其他小組選擇和我們一樣的研究問題。"},{"en":"When no one is doing the same as us, our work may feel more original.","zh":"當沒有人和我們做一樣的事時，我們的作品可能更有原創性。"},{"en":"The phrase compares other people’s choices with our own.","zh":"這個片語把別人的選擇與我們的選擇作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"research areas","meaning":"研究領域","examples":[{"en":"The topic is one of the research areas of the module convenor.","zh":"這個題目是模組負責人的其中一個研究領域。"},{"en":"Research areas are subjects that a person studies seriously or professionally.","zh":"研究領域是某人認真或專業研究的主題。"},{"en":"A professor’s research areas may include theatre history and performance design.","zh":"教授的研究領域可能包括劇場歷史和表演設計。"},{"en":"Knowing a teacher’s research areas can help students choose useful sources.","zh":"知道老師的研究領域可以幫助學生選擇有用資料來源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fields of academic interest.","zh":"這個片語描述學術興趣範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"module convenor","meaning":"模組負責人","examples":[{"en":"The module convenor researches theatre programmes.","zh":"模組負責人研究劇場節目單。"},{"en":"A module convenor is the person responsible for organising and managing a course module.","zh":"模組負責人是負責組織和管理某個課程模組的人。"},{"en":"The module convenor told students when the final essay was due.","zh":"模組負責人告訴學生期末論文何時截止。"},{"en":"A module convenor may choose readings, assessments, and lecture topics.","zh":"模組負責人可能會選擇閱讀材料、評核和講課題目。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the teacher or academic in charge of a module.","zh":"這個片語指出負責某個模組的老師或學者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"put some people off","meaning":"令某人卻步","examples":[{"en":"The module convenor’s interest might put some people off.","zh":"模組負責人的興趣可能會令一些人卻步。"},{"en":"Put some people off means make some people less interested or willing to do something.","zh":"令某人卻步意思是令某些人對做某事較不感興趣或不太願意。"},{"en":"A very difficult title may put some students off choosing a topic.","zh":"一個很困難的題目可能會令一些學生卻步。"},{"en":"People may be put off if they think the teacher knows too much about their subject.","zh":"如果學生認為老師對他們的主題太熟悉，他們可能會卻步。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that discourages people.","zh":"這個片語描述令人不敢或不願嘗試的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I suppose so","meaning":"我想也是","examples":[{"en":"Finn says, “I suppose so,” when Maya makes her point.","zh":"Maya 提出觀點時，Finn 說：「我想也是。」"},{"en":"I suppose so means I think that is probably true, although I am not strongly certain.","zh":"我想也是意思是我認為那大概是真的，但不是非常肯定。"},{"en":"“This topic may be hard.” “I suppose so.”","zh":"「這個題目可能很難。」「我想也是。」"},{"en":"People use this phrase to agree gently or reluctantly.","zh":"人們用這個片語溫和或有點勉強地表示同意。"},{"en":"It sounds less confident than “yes, definitely.”","zh":"它比「是的，絕對如此」語氣較不肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I hadn’t realised","meaning":"我之前沒有意識到","examples":[{"en":"Finn had not realised that companies specialise in theatre programmes.","zh":"Finn 之前沒有意識到有公司專門製作劇場節目單。"},{"en":"I hadn’t realised means I did not know or understand this before.","zh":"我之前沒有意識到意思是我以前不知道或不明白這件事。"},{"en":"I hadn’t realised that the library kept old theatre posters.","zh":"我之前沒有意識到圖書館保存舊劇場海報。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when new information surprises them.","zh":"當新資料令人驚訝時，人們會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It shows a change in understanding.","zh":"它顯示理解上的改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"specialise in creating","meaning":"專門製作","examples":[{"en":"Some companies specialise in creating theatre programmes.","zh":"有些公司專門製作劇場節目單。"},{"en":"Specialise in creating something means focus professionally on making that particular thing.","zh":"專門製作某物意思是專業地集中製作那種特定東西。"},{"en":"Some studios specialise in creating posters for films and plays.","zh":"有些工作室專門製作電影和戲劇海報。"},{"en":"Companies that specialise in one product often develop strong skills in that area.","zh":"專門製作某種產品的公司，通常會在該範疇培養強大技能。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a focused kind of professional work.","zh":"這個片語顯示一種專注的專業工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"quite common nowadays","meaning":"現在相當常見","examples":[{"en":"Companies that create theatre programmes are quite common nowadays.","zh":"製作劇場節目單的公司現在相當常見。"},{"en":"Quite common nowadays means fairly usual or often seen in modern times.","zh":"現在相當常見意思是在現代頗普遍或經常見到。"},{"en":"Online ticket booking is quite common nowadays.","zh":"網上訂票現在相當常見。"},{"en":"Something that was rare before may become quite common nowadays because of new business needs.","zh":"以前罕見的東西可能因新的商業需要而現在相當常見。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the present with the past.","zh":"這個片語把現在和過去作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Contrary to what many people think","meaning":"與許多人所想的相反","examples":[{"en":"Contrary to what many people think, theatres do not usually hire people to produce programmes.","zh":"與許多人所想的相反，劇院通常不會僱人製作節目單。"},{"en":"Contrary to what many people think means the truth is different from the common belief.","zh":"與許多人所想的相反，意思是真相與普遍想法不同。"},{"en":"Contrary to what many people think, not all actors want to be famous.","zh":"與許多人所想的相反，並非所有演員都想成名。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to correct a mistaken assumption.","zh":"作者用這個片語來糾正錯誤假設。"},{"en":"It prepares readers for surprising information.","zh":"它讓讀者準備接收令人意外的資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hire people to","meaning":"僱用人去","examples":[{"en":"Theatres do not usually hire people to produce programmes.","zh":"劇院通常不會僱用人去製作節目單。"},{"en":"Hire people to do something means pay people to do a job.","zh":"僱用人去做某事意思是付錢請人做一項工作。"},{"en":"The museum hired people to design a new exhibition.","zh":"博物館僱用人去設計一個新展覽。"},{"en":"Companies hire people when they need skills or labour for a task.","zh":"公司需要某項任務的技能或人手時，會僱用人。"},{"en":"The phrase explains who is paid to do the work.","zh":"這個片語解釋誰被付錢去做工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"buy the rights to","meaning":"購買……的權利","examples":[{"en":"Companies buy the rights to publish theatre programmes.","zh":"公司購買出版劇場節目單的權利。"},{"en":"Buy the rights to do something means pay for legal permission to do it.","zh":"購買做某事的權利意思是付錢取得合法許可去做該事。"},{"en":"A publisher may buy the rights to print a famous novel.","zh":"出版商可能購買印刷一本著名小說的權利。"},{"en":"Buying rights allows a company to use or sell something legally.","zh":"購買權利讓公司可以合法使用或銷售某物。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in publishing, theatre, music, and film.","zh":"這個片語常見於出版、劇場、音樂和電影。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"publish programmes","meaning":"出版節目單","examples":[{"en":"Companies buy the rights to publish programmes for theatres.","zh":"公司購買為劇院出版節目單的權利。"},{"en":"Publish programmes means produce and distribute theatre programme booklets.","zh":"出版節目單意思是製作並發行劇場節目小冊子。"},{"en":"A theatre company may publish programmes before each new production.","zh":"劇團可能在每齣新作品上演前出版節目單。"},{"en":"Publishing programmes helps audiences learn about the show and the performers.","zh":"出版節目單幫助觀眾了解演出和表演者。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to making theatre programmes available to the public.","zh":"這個片語指向公眾提供劇場節目單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on the theatre’s behalf","meaning":"代表劇院","examples":[{"en":"Companies publish programmes on the theatre’s behalf.","zh":"公司代表劇院出版節目單。"},{"en":"On the theatre’s behalf means for the theatre or as the theatre’s representative.","zh":"代表劇院意思是為劇院或作為劇院代表去做某事。"},{"en":"The agency sold tickets on the theatre’s behalf.","zh":"代理公司代表劇院售票。"},{"en":"Doing work on someone’s behalf means acting for them with permission.","zh":"代表某人做事意思是在得到許可下替他們行動。"},{"en":"The phrase explains that companies act for the theatre, not independently.","zh":"這個片語解釋公司是代表劇院行事，而不是完全獨立行事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make their money","meaning":"賺錢","examples":[{"en":"The companies make their money by selling advertising space.","zh":"這些公司透過出售廣告版面賺錢。"},{"en":"Make their money means earn income or profit.","zh":"賺錢意思是取得收入或利潤。"},{"en":"Some websites make their money by showing adverts.","zh":"有些網站透過展示廣告賺錢。"},{"en":"Understanding how companies make their money helps explain their business model.","zh":"了解公司如何賺錢，有助解釋其商業模式。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how income is earned.","zh":"這個片語集中於收入如何取得。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"selling advertising space","meaning":"出售廣告版面","examples":[{"en":"Companies make money by selling advertising space in the programme.","zh":"公司透過在節目單中出售廣告版面賺錢。"},{"en":"Selling advertising space means charging businesses to place adverts in a publication or platform.","zh":"出售廣告版面意思是向商戶收費，讓他們在出版物或平台放廣告。"},{"en":"A school magazine may raise money by selling advertising space to local shops.","zh":"校刊可能透過向本地商店出售廣告版面籌款。"},{"en":"Selling advertising space can reduce the cost of producing a booklet.","zh":"出售廣告版面可以降低製作小冊子的成本。"},{"en":"The phrase explains one way programme publishers earn money.","zh":"這個片語解釋節目單出版商賺錢的一種方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"within the programme booklet","meaning":"在節目冊內","examples":[{"en":"Advertising space is sold within the programme booklet.","zh":"廣告版面在節目冊內出售。"},{"en":"Within the programme booklet means inside the printed programme.","zh":"在節目冊內意思是在印刷節目單裏面。"},{"en":"The theatre placed cast notes within the programme booklet.","zh":"劇院在節目冊內放入演員介紹。"},{"en":"Adverts within the programme booklet can reach people who are already attending the show.","zh":"節目冊內的廣告可以接觸到已經來看演出的觀眾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where the content appears.","zh":"這個片語描述內容出現的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"do it that way","meaning":"以那種方式做","examples":[{"en":"It must be easier for theatres to do it that way.","zh":"劇院以那種方式做一定更容易。"},{"en":"Do it that way means use that method or arrangement.","zh":"以那種方式做意思是使用那種方法或安排。"},{"en":"We can print the posters ourselves, but it may be cheaper to do it that way through a company.","zh":"我們可以自己印海報，但透過公司以那種方式做可能更便宜。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when comparing different methods.","zh":"人們比較不同方法時會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It refers back to the method already mentioned.","zh":"它指回前面已提到的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"early British theatre","meaning":"早期英國劇場","examples":[{"en":"Finn reads about programmes in early British theatre.","zh":"Finn 閱讀關於早期英國劇場節目單的資料。"},{"en":"Early British theatre refers to theatre in Britain during earlier historical periods.","zh":"早期英國劇場指英國較早歷史時期的劇場。"},{"en":"Students study early British theatre to understand how audiences and actors behaved in the past.","zh":"學生研究早期英國劇場，以了解過去觀眾和演員如何行動。"},{"en":"Early British theatre had different customs from modern theatre.","zh":"早期英國劇場有與現代劇場不同的習俗。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the historical setting for Finn’s research.","zh":"這個片語為 Finn 的研究提供歷史背景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the cast","meaning":"演員陣容","examples":[{"en":"The cast was always very important in early British theatre.","zh":"在早期英國劇場，演員陣容一直非常重要。"},{"en":"The cast is the group of actors performing in a play, film, or show.","zh":"演員陣容是指在戲劇、電影或演出中表演的一組演員。"},{"en":"The programme listed the cast so audiences knew who was acting.","zh":"節目單列出演員陣容，讓觀眾知道誰在演出。"},{"en":"A famous cast can attract more people to a performance.","zh":"著名演員陣容可以吸引更多人觀看演出。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the performers, not the audience or crew.","zh":"這個片語指表演者，不是觀眾或工作人員。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be familiar with","meaning":"熟悉……","examples":[{"en":"Audiences were very familiar with leading actors.","zh":"觀眾非常熟悉主要演員。"},{"en":"Be familiar with something means know it well or recognise it easily.","zh":"熟悉某事意思是很了解或容易認出它。"},{"en":"Students are familiar with the school rules because they hear them often.","zh":"學生很熟悉校規，因為他們經常聽到。"},{"en":"Audiences familiar with famous actors may buy tickets because of those names.","zh":"熟悉著名演員的觀眾可能會因那些名字而買票。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge gained through experience or repeated exposure.","zh":"這個片語描述透過經驗或反覆接觸而得來的認識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"leading actors","meaning":"主要演員；主演","examples":[{"en":"Audiences were familiar with leading actors.","zh":"觀眾熟悉主要演員。"},{"en":"Leading actors are the main or most important performers in a play or show.","zh":"主要演員或主演是戲劇或演出中最重要的表演者。"},{"en":"The leading actors received loud applause at the end of the performance.","zh":"演出結束時，主演獲得熱烈掌聲。"},{"en":"A theatre programme often names leading actors clearly because audiences care about them.","zh":"劇場節目單通常清楚列出主要演員，因為觀眾重視他們。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to major performers, not minor roles.","zh":"這個片語指主要表演者，不是小角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"big names","meaning":"知名人物；大牌演員","examples":[{"en":"Big names would draw huge crowds.","zh":"大牌演員會吸引大量人潮。"},{"en":"Big names are famous people whose names are widely recognised.","zh":"知名人物或大牌演員是名字廣為人知的人。"},{"en":"A festival with big names may sell tickets quickly.","zh":"有知名人物參與的節日活動可能很快售罄。"},{"en":"Big names attract attention because audiences already know and admire them.","zh":"知名人物吸引注意，因為觀眾已經認識並欣賞他們。"},{"en":"In theatre, the phrase often refers to famous actors.","zh":"在劇場中，這個片語常指著名演員。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"draw huge crowds","meaning":"吸引大量人潮","examples":[{"en":"Famous actors would draw huge crowds to the theatre.","zh":"著名演員會吸引大量人潮到劇院。"},{"en":"Draw huge crowds means attract very large numbers of people.","zh":"吸引大量人潮意思是吸引非常多的人。"},{"en":"A free concert in the park can draw huge crowds.","zh":"公園裏的免費音樂會可以吸引大量人潮。"},{"en":"Famous performers draw huge crowds because people want to see them live.","zh":"著名表演者會吸引大量人潮，因為人們想現場觀看他們。"},{"en":"The phrase shows strong public interest.","zh":"這個片語顯示強烈的公眾興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"named a famous actor","meaning":"列出一位知名演員","examples":[{"en":"The programme named a famous actor expected to perform.","zh":"節目單列出一位被期望演出的知名演員。"},{"en":"Named a famous actor means listed or mentioned a famous actor by name.","zh":"列出一位知名演員意思是以名字提及或列明一位著名演員。"},{"en":"The poster named a famous actor as the star of the show.","zh":"海報列出一位知名演員作為演出的明星主演。"},{"en":"Naming a famous actor can increase audience expectations.","zh":"列出知名演員會提高觀眾期望。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the programme made a specific promise to audiences.","zh":"這個片語顯示節目單向觀眾作出具體承諾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the public expected to","meaning":"公眾期望……","examples":[{"en":"The public expected the named actor to perform.","zh":"公眾期望被列名的演員演出。"},{"en":"The public expected to means ordinary people believed something should or would happen.","zh":"公眾期望意思是一般人相信某事應該或將會發生。"},{"en":"The public expected the singer to appear because her name was on the poster.","zh":"因為歌手的名字在海報上，公眾期望她會出現。"},{"en":"When publicity promises something, the public expects it to be true.","zh":"當宣傳承諾某事時，公眾期望它是真的。"},{"en":"The phrase shows audience expectation.","zh":"這個片語顯示觀眾期望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"expected to perform","meaning":"被期望演出","examples":[{"en":"Audiences expected the famous actor to perform.","zh":"觀眾期望那位知名演員演出。"},{"en":"Expected to perform means believed or promised to appear and act in the show.","zh":"被期望演出意思是被相信或承諾會出現並參與表演。"},{"en":"The lead actress was expected to perform, but she became ill.","zh":"那位女主演本被期望演出，但她生病了。"},{"en":"If an actor is expected to perform, audiences may feel disappointed if they do not appear.","zh":"如果演員被期望演出而沒有出現，觀眾可能會失望。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what the audience believed would happen.","zh":"這個片語顯示觀眾相信會發生的事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"accused the theatre of","meaning":"指責劇院……","examples":[{"en":"People accused the theatre of breaking its agreement with the audience.","zh":"人們指責劇院違反了與觀眾的約定。"},{"en":"Accused the theatre of something means said the theatre had done something wrong.","zh":"指責劇院某事意思是說劇院做錯了某事。"},{"en":"Audience members accused the theatre of misleading them with the poster.","zh":"觀眾指責劇院用海報誤導他們。"},{"en":"People accuse an organisation when they believe it is responsible for a problem.","zh":"當人們相信某機構要為問題負責時，會指責它。"},{"en":"The phrase shows blame or complaint.","zh":"這個片語顯示責備或投訴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"break an agreement with","meaning":"違反與……的約定","examples":[{"en":"The theatre was accused of breaking an agreement with the audience.","zh":"劇院被指違反與觀眾的約定。"},{"en":"Break an agreement with someone means fail to do what was promised to that person.","zh":"違反與某人的約定意思是沒有做到向那人承諾的事。"},{"en":"The company broke an agreement with customers when it changed the service without warning.","zh":"公司在沒有通知下改變服務，違反了與顧客的約定。"},{"en":"Breaking an agreement can make people angry because trust is lost.","zh":"違反約定會令人憤怒，因為信任被破壞。"},{"en":"In early theatre, naming an actor could feel like an agreement with the audience.","zh":"在早期劇場，列出演員名字可能像是與觀眾的約定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"demand refunds","meaning":"要求退款","examples":[{"en":"Audiences would demand refunds if the named actor did not perform.","zh":"如果被列名的演員沒有演出，觀眾會要求退款。"},{"en":"Demand refunds means strongly ask to get money back.","zh":"要求退款意思是強烈要求取回金錢。"},{"en":"Customers demanded refunds after the concert was cancelled.","zh":"音樂會取消後，顧客要求退款。"},{"en":"People demand refunds when they feel they did not receive what they paid for.","zh":"當人們覺得沒有得到自己付錢購買的東西時，會要求退款。"},{"en":"The phrase shows strong dissatisfaction.","zh":"這個片語顯示強烈不滿。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"riots","meaning":"騷亂；暴動","examples":[{"en":"If audiences did not get refunds, there were sometimes riots.","zh":"如果觀眾得不到退款，有時會發生騷亂。"},{"en":"Riots are violent public disturbances involving groups of angry people.","zh":"騷亂或暴動是由憤怒群眾造成的暴力公共混亂。"},{"en":"Riots can break windows, damage streets, and frighten local residents.","zh":"騷亂可能打破窗戶、損壞街道，並嚇壞本地居民。"},{"en":"A crowd may turn into a riot if anger grows and control is lost.","zh":"如果憤怒升級並失去控制，人群可能變成暴動。"},{"en":"The word shows that audience reactions could become extreme.","zh":"這個詞顯示觀眾反應可能變得極端。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"outrageous","meaning":"太離譜；太過分","examples":[{"en":"Maya thinks the audience reaction was outrageous.","zh":"Maya 認為觀眾的反應太離譜。"},{"en":"Outrageous means shocking, unreasonable, or completely unacceptable.","zh":"太離譜或太過分意思是令人震驚、不合理或完全不能接受。"},{"en":"Charging students a huge fee for a small worksheet would be outrageous.","zh":"為一張小工作紙向學生收取高昂費用，會太離譜。"},{"en":"People use this word when they strongly disapprove of behaviour.","zh":"人們強烈不認同行為時會使用這個詞。"},{"en":"The word shows Maya thinks the reaction was far too extreme.","zh":"這個詞顯示 Maya 認為反應極端得過分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"That’d never happen now","meaning":"現在絕不會發生","examples":[{"en":"Maya says that would never happen now.","zh":"Maya 說那種事現在絕不會發生。"},{"en":"That’d never happen now means such a thing would not happen in the present day.","zh":"現在絕不會發生意思是這樣的事情在今天不會發生。"},{"en":"A theatre riot over one missing actor would probably never happen now.","zh":"因一位演員缺席而發生劇場騷亂，現在大概絕不會發生。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to compare past behaviour with modern behaviour.","zh":"人們用這個片語比較過去行為和現代行為。"},{"en":"It suggests that social expectations have changed.","zh":"它暗示社會期望已經改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"even when","meaning":"即使在……的時候","examples":[{"en":"People are polite even when they are disappointed.","zh":"人們即使在失望的時候也很有禮貌。"},{"en":"Even when means despite the fact that something happens or is true.","zh":"即使在……的時候意思是雖然某事發生或屬實。"},{"en":"She stayed calm even when the computer stopped working.","zh":"即使在電腦停止運作時，她仍保持冷靜。"},{"en":"This phrase shows contrast between a situation and someone’s reaction.","zh":"這個片語顯示情況和某人反應之間的對比。"},{"en":"It helps explain that disappointment does not always lead to rude behaviour.","zh":"它幫助解釋失望不一定導致無禮行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be disappointed if","meaning":"如果……會感到失望","examples":[{"en":"Audiences may be disappointed if the star misses a performance.","zh":"如果明星主演缺席一場演出，觀眾可能會感到失望。"},{"en":"Be disappointed if means feel unhappy or let down when something happens.","zh":"如果……會感到失望，意思是當某事發生時感到不開心或被辜負。"},{"en":"Students may be disappointed if the school trip is cancelled.","zh":"如果學校旅行取消，學生可能會感到失望。"},{"en":"Audiences are disappointed if they pay to see a star who does not appear.","zh":"如果觀眾付錢看一位明星，但他沒有出現，他們會感到失望。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a condition with an emotional result.","zh":"這個片語把條件和情緒結果連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the star of the show","meaning":"演出的明星主演","examples":[{"en":"The star of the show may miss a performance.","zh":"演出的明星主演可能會缺席一場演出。"},{"en":"The star of the show is the most famous or important performer in a production.","zh":"演出的明星主演是一部作品中最著名或最重要的表演者。"},{"en":"Many people bought tickets because the star of the show was well known.","zh":"許多人買票，因為演出的明星主演很有名。"},{"en":"If the star of the show is absent, some audience members may feel disappointed.","zh":"如果演出的明星主演缺席，有些觀眾可能會失望。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main attraction of a performance.","zh":"這個片語指出演出的主要吸引力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"miss a performance","meaning":"缺席一場演出","examples":[{"en":"The star of the show might miss a performance.","zh":"演出的明星主演可能會缺席一場演出。"},{"en":"Miss a performance means not appear in or attend a scheduled show.","zh":"缺席一場演出意思是沒有出現在或參與預定的一場表演。"},{"en":"The actor missed a performance because he was ill.","zh":"那位演員因病缺席一場演出。"},{"en":"If a performer misses a performance, another actor may replace them.","zh":"如果表演者缺席一場演出，另一位演員可能會替代他。"},{"en":"The phrase describes absence from one specific show.","zh":"這個片語描述缺席某一場特定演出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"definitely include","meaning":"絕對包括","examples":[{"en":"Maya thinks they should definitely include the information.","zh":"Maya 認為他們應該絕對包括這些資料。"},{"en":"Definitely include means certainly put something into a piece of work.","zh":"絕對包括意思是一定把某些內容放進作品中。"},{"en":"You should definitely include the date and title in your report.","zh":"你的報告絕對應該包括日期和標題。"},{"en":"People say this when information is too important to leave out.","zh":"當資料太重要而不能遺漏時，人們會這樣說。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses strong agreement about including something.","zh":"這個片語強烈表示同意加入某內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"early audiences","meaning":"早期觀眾","examples":[{"en":"Their project should include information about early audiences.","zh":"他們的專題應包括關於早期觀眾的資料。"},{"en":"Early audiences are people who watched performances in earlier historical periods.","zh":"早期觀眾是指較早歷史時期觀看演出的人。"},{"en":"Early audiences behaved differently from modern audiences in many theatres.","zh":"早期觀眾在許多劇院中的行為與現代觀眾不同。"},{"en":"Studying early audiences helps us understand how theatre culture has changed.","zh":"研究早期觀眾幫助我們理解劇場文化如何改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to past theatre-goers.","zh":"這個片語指過去的劇場觀眾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ordinary people","meaning":"普通人","examples":[{"en":"Many ordinary people at that time were illiterate.","zh":"當時許多普通人都不識字。"},{"en":"Ordinary people are normal members of society, not rich, famous, or powerful people.","zh":"普通人是社會中的一般成員，不是富有、著名或有權勢的人。"},{"en":"Ordinary people often learned about events through public announcements.","zh":"普通人過去常透過公開宣布了解事件。"},{"en":"If ordinary people could not read, printed programmes were less useful for them.","zh":"如果普通人不識字，印刷節目單對他們就較不有用。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on common people in daily life.","zh":"這個片語集中於日常生活中的一般人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at that time","meaning":"在當時","examples":[{"en":"Many ordinary people at that time could not read.","zh":"在當時，許多普通人不能閱讀。"},{"en":"At that time means during that particular period in the past.","zh":"在當時意思是在過去那個特定時期。"},{"en":"At that time, theatre announcements were often made in the streets.","zh":"在當時，劇場演出通知常在街上宣布。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers understand a fact in its historical context.","zh":"這個片語幫助讀者把事實放進歷史背景中理解。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing the past with the present.","zh":"它在比較過去和現在時很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"illiterate","meaning":"不識字的","examples":[{"en":"Many ordinary people were illiterate in early theatre history.","zh":"在早期劇場歷史中，許多普通人都不識字。"},{"en":"Illiterate means unable to read or write.","zh":"不識字的意思是不能閱讀或書寫。"},{"en":"An illiterate person may need information to be spoken aloud instead of printed.","zh":"不識字的人可能需要別人口頭說出資料，而不是閱讀印刷文字。"},{"en":"If many people are illiterate, printed advertisements may not reach them well.","zh":"如果很多人不識字，印刷廣告可能不容易有效接觸他們。"},{"en":"The word explains why street announcements were important.","zh":"這個詞解釋為何街頭宣布很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"of limited value","meaning":"價值有限","examples":[{"en":"Theatre programmes were of limited value in advertising plays.","zh":"劇場節目單在宣傳戲劇方面價值有限。"},{"en":"Of limited value means useful only in a small or restricted way.","zh":"價值有限意思是只在小範圍或受限制情況下有用。"},{"en":"A map is of limited value if many roads are missing.","zh":"如果地圖缺少很多道路，它的價值有限。"},{"en":"Printed programmes were of limited value when many people could not read them.","zh":"當許多人不能閱讀時，印刷節目單的價值有限。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something has some use but not enough.","zh":"這個片語顯示某物有一些用途，但不足夠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"advertising plays","meaning":"宣傳戲劇","examples":[{"en":"Theatre programmes were of limited value in advertising plays.","zh":"劇場節目單在宣傳戲劇方面價值有限。"},{"en":"Advertising plays means promoting theatre performances so people know about them and attend.","zh":"宣傳戲劇意思是推廣劇場演出，讓人知道並前來觀看。"},{"en":"Posters, street announcements, and newspaper notices were used for advertising plays.","zh":"海報、街頭宣布和報紙告示都曾用來宣傳戲劇。"},{"en":"Advertising plays is important because audiences need to know when and where shows happen.","zh":"宣傳戲劇很重要，因為觀眾需要知道演出何時何地舉行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the act of publicising theatre performances.","zh":"這個片語描述向公眾推廣劇場演出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a company of actors","meaning":"劇團","examples":[{"en":"A company of actors arrived in a town to promote their plays.","zh":"一個劇團來到一個城鎮宣傳他們的戲劇。"},{"en":"A company of actors is a group of actors who perform together.","zh":"劇團是一組一起演出的演員。"},{"en":"A company of actors may travel from town to town with the same play.","zh":"劇團可能帶着同一齣戲從一個城鎮巡迴到另一個城鎮。"},{"en":"In earlier theatre, a company of actors often had to advertise its own performances.","zh":"在早期劇場中，劇團常要自己宣傳演出。"},{"en":"The phrase is similar to “theatre company.”","zh":"這個片語與 “theatre company” 意思相近。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"arrive in a town","meaning":"來到一個城鎮","examples":[{"en":"A company of actors arrived in a town.","zh":"一個劇團來到一個城鎮。"},{"en":"Arrive in a town means reach or come to a town after travelling.","zh":"來到一個城鎮意思是旅行後抵達或進入一個城鎮。"},{"en":"The travelling musicians arrived in a town before the festival began.","zh":"巡迴音樂人在節日開始前來到一個城鎮。"},{"en":"When actors arrived in a town, they needed to let people know about their shows.","zh":"當演員來到一個城鎮時，他們需要讓人知道自己的演出。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the starting point of the actors’ local promotion.","zh":"這個片語提供演員本地宣傳的起點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"parade around the streets","meaning":"在街上遊行","examples":[{"en":"Actors would parade around the streets in their costumes.","zh":"演員會穿着戲服在街上遊行。"},{"en":"Parade around the streets means walk publicly through streets, often to attract attention.","zh":"在街上遊行意思是在街道上公開行走，通常為了吸引注意。"},{"en":"Festival performers paraded around the streets with drums and bright clothes.","zh":"節日表演者穿着鮮艷衣服、敲着鼓在街上遊行。"},{"en":"Actors paraded around the streets because many people could not read printed notices.","zh":"演員在街上遊行，因為許多人不能閱讀印刷告示。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a public and visible form of promotion.","zh":"這個片語描述一種公開而顯眼的宣傳方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in their costumes","meaning":"穿著戲服","examples":[{"en":"The actors walked around the streets in their costumes.","zh":"演員穿着戲服在街上走動。"},{"en":"In their costumes means wearing the special clothes used for a performance or role.","zh":"穿着戲服意思是穿上表演或角色所用的特別衣服。"},{"en":"The students arrived on stage in their costumes before the play began.","zh":"話劇開始前，學生穿着戲服走上舞台。"},{"en":"Costumes help audiences recognise characters quickly.","zh":"戲服幫助觀眾快速認出角色。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that actors used visual appearance to attract attention.","zh":"這個片語顯示演員利用視覺外觀吸引注意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"beat drums","meaning":"敲鼓","examples":[{"en":"The actors beat drums to attract attention.","zh":"演員敲鼓以吸引注意。"},{"en":"Beat drums means hit drums repeatedly to make a loud rhythm.","zh":"敲鼓意思是反覆擊打鼓，發出響亮節奏。"},{"en":"Performers beat drums during the parade so people would come outside.","zh":"表演者在遊行中敲鼓，讓人們走出來觀看。"},{"en":"Beating drums can announce an event when many people are nearby.","zh":"當附近有很多人時，敲鼓可以宣布活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a noisy way to attract an audience.","zh":"這個片語描述一種以聲音吸引觀眾的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"announce upcoming performances","meaning":"宣布即將上演的劇目","examples":[{"en":"The actors announced their upcoming performances in the streets.","zh":"演員在街上宣布即將上演的劇目。"},{"en":"Announce upcoming performances means publicly tell people about shows that will happen soon.","zh":"宣布即將上演的劇目意思是公開告訴人們即將舉行的演出。"},{"en":"The theatre announced upcoming performances on posters and social media.","zh":"劇院在海報和社交媒體上宣布即將上演的劇目。"},{"en":"Announcing upcoming performances helps people decide whether to buy tickets.","zh":"宣布即將上演的劇目幫助人們決定是否買票。"},{"en":"The phrase describes promoting future shows.","zh":"這個片語描述推廣未來演出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"I couldn’t imagine that happening now","meaning":"我無法想像現在會發生這種事","examples":[{"en":"Finn could not imagine actors promoting plays that way now.","zh":"Finn 無法想像演員現在會那樣宣傳戲劇。"},{"en":"I couldn’t imagine that happening now means I find it hard to believe such a thing would happen today.","zh":"我無法想像現在會發生這種事，意思是我很難相信這樣的事今天會發生。"},{"en":"I couldn’t imagine actors walking through busy streets with drums now.","zh":"我無法想像演員現在拿着鼓走過繁忙街道。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to show that past customs seem strange in modern life.","zh":"當過去習俗在現代生活中顯得奇怪時，人們會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It compares historical behaviour with present expectations.","zh":"它把歷史行為與現代期望作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an interesting comparison to make","meaning":"一個值得作出的有趣比較","examples":[{"en":"There is an interesting comparison to make between eighteenth- and nineteenth-century programmes.","zh":"十八世紀和十九世紀節目單之間有一個值得作出的有趣比較。"},{"en":"An interesting comparison to make means two things are worth comparing because their differences reveal something useful.","zh":"一個值得作出的有趣比較，意思是兩件事值得比較，因為它們的差異揭示有用內容。"},{"en":"There is an interesting comparison to make between printed books and e-books.","zh":"印刷書和電子書之間有一個值得作出的有趣比較。"},{"en":"Comparisons help students notice change over time.","zh":"比較幫助學生注意隨時間出現的變化。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a useful analytical point.","zh":"這個片語引出有用的分析重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"eighteenth-century programmes","meaning":"十八世紀的節目單","examples":[{"en":"Eighteenth-century programmes gave theatre-goers a lot of information.","zh":"十八世紀的節目單給劇場觀眾很多資料。"},{"en":"Eighteenth-century programmes are theatre programmes from the 1700s.","zh":"十八世紀的節目單是來自 1700 年代的劇場節目單。"},{"en":"Eighteenth-century programmes often included details about the writer, plot, and play history.","zh":"十八世紀的節目單常包括關於作者、劇情和戲劇歷史的細節。"},{"en":"Studying eighteenth-century programmes helps researchers understand early theatre culture.","zh":"研究十八世紀的節目單幫助研究者理解早期劇場文化。"},{"en":"The phrase places the programmes in a specific historical period.","zh":"這個片語把節目單放在特定歷史時期中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"nineteenth-century programmes","meaning":"十九世紀的節目單","examples":[{"en":"Nineteenth-century programmes started to resemble modern programmes.","zh":"十九世紀的節目單開始變得像現代節目單。"},{"en":"Nineteenth-century programmes are theatre programmes from the 1800s.","zh":"十九世紀的節目單是來自 1800 年代的劇場節目單。"},{"en":"Nineteenth-century programmes often used colour and more varied designs.","zh":"十九世紀的節目單常使用色彩和更多樣的設計。"},{"en":"They are useful for studying how theatre publicity changed over time.","zh":"它們有助研究劇場宣傳如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to programmes from a later historical period than eighteenth-century ones.","zh":"這個片語指比十八世紀節目單較後期的節目單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"started to resemble","meaning":"開始變得像","examples":[{"en":"Theatre programmes started to resemble programmes today.","zh":"劇場節目單開始變得像今天的節目單。"},{"en":"Started to resemble means began to look like or become similar to something.","zh":"開始變得像意思是開始看起來像某物或與某物相似。"},{"en":"Early mobile phones started to resemble small computers when internet access was added.","zh":"當加入上網功能後，早期手提電話開始變得像小型電腦。"},{"en":"When designs start to resemble modern ones, we can see historical development.","zh":"當設計開始變得像現代設計時，我們可以看到歷史發展。"},{"en":"The phrase shows gradual change toward similarity.","zh":"這個片語顯示逐漸走向相似的變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"programmes today","meaning":"今天的節目單","examples":[{"en":"Nineteenth-century theatre programmes resembled programmes today.","zh":"十九世紀的劇場節目單像今天的節目單。"},{"en":"Programmes today are modern theatre programme booklets used by current audiences.","zh":"今天的節目單是現代觀眾使用的劇場節目小冊子。"},{"en":"Programmes today often include cast lists, production notes, images, and adverts.","zh":"今天的節目單常包括演員名單、製作筆記、圖片和廣告。"},{"en":"Comparing old programmes with programmes today shows how theatre communication has changed.","zh":"比較舊節目單和今天的節目單，可以顯示劇場溝通如何改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to current theatre programmes.","zh":"這個片語指現今的劇場節目單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unlike programmes from","meaning":"與……的節目單不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike programmes from the eighteenth century, later programmes always used colour.","zh":"與十八世紀的節目單不同，後來的節目單總是使用色彩。"},{"en":"Unlike programmes from a period means different from programmes from that time.","zh":"與某時期的節目單不同，意思是與那個時期的節目單有差異。"},{"en":"Unlike posters from the past, modern posters often include QR codes.","zh":"與過去的海報不同，現代海報常包括 QR code。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly introduces contrast between two groups.","zh":"這個片語清楚引出兩組事物之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing historical changes.","zh":"它在比較歷史變化時很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"use colour","meaning":"使用色彩","examples":[{"en":"Nineteenth-century programmes always used colour.","zh":"十九世紀的節目單總是使用色彩。"},{"en":"Use colour means include coloured ink, images, or design elements.","zh":"使用色彩意思是加入彩色油墨、圖片或設計元素。"},{"en":"Designers use colour to make a programme more attractive.","zh":"設計師使用色彩令節目單更吸引。"},{"en":"Using colour can help important information stand out.","zh":"使用色彩可以幫助重要資料突出。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visual design choice.","zh":"這個片語描述一種視覺設計選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a greater variety of","meaning":"更多種類的……","examples":[{"en":"There was a greater variety of designs in nineteenth-century programmes.","zh":"十九世紀的節目單有更多種類的設計。"},{"en":"A greater variety of something means more different types or styles of it.","zh":"更多種類的某物意思是有更多不同類型或風格。"},{"en":"Modern students have a greater variety of learning tools than students in the past.","zh":"現代學生比過去學生有更多種類的學習工具。"},{"en":"A greater variety of designs can make programmes more visually interesting.","zh":"更多種類的設計可以令節目單在視覺上更有趣。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises increased diversity.","zh":"這個片語強調多樣性增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"designs","meaning":"設計","examples":[{"en":"Nineteenth-century programmes had a greater variety of designs.","zh":"十九世紀的節目單有更多種類的設計。"},{"en":"Designs are the planned visual styles, layouts, or patterns of something.","zh":"設計是某物經規劃的視覺風格、排版或圖案。"},{"en":"The theatre displayed several programme designs from different periods.","zh":"劇院展示了來自不同時期的幾款節目單設計。"},{"en":"Good designs help information look clear and attractive.","zh":"好設計幫助資料看起來清晰而吸引。"},{"en":"The word refers to how something is arranged and presented visually.","zh":"這個詞指某物如何以視覺方式安排和呈現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"personally","meaning":"就個人而言","examples":[{"en":"Personally, Finn thinks eighteenth-century programmes were superior.","zh":"就個人而言，Finn 認為十八世紀的節目單更優勝。"},{"en":"Personally means in my own opinion.","zh":"就個人而言意思是按我自己的看法。"},{"en":"Personally, I prefer simple programme designs with clear information.","zh":"就個人而言，我較喜歡資料清晰的簡單節目單設計。"},{"en":"People use this word to show they are giving a personal view, not a fact.","zh":"人們用這個詞表示自己是在表達個人觀點，而不是事實。"},{"en":"It makes an opinion sound direct but polite.","zh":"它令意見聽起來直接但有禮貌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be superior","meaning":"更好；更優勝","examples":[{"en":"Finn thinks eighteenth-century programmes were superior.","zh":"Finn 認為十八世紀的節目單更優勝。"},{"en":"Be superior means be better in quality, usefulness, or value.","zh":"更好或更優勝意思是在質素、用途或價值上較好。"},{"en":"Some people think printed books are superior to e-books for serious reading.","zh":"有些人認為紙本書比電子書更適合認真閱讀。"},{"en":"A programme can be superior if it gives audiences clearer and richer information.","zh":"如果節目單給觀眾更清楚和更豐富的資料，它就可以更優勝。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses comparison and judgement.","zh":"這個片語表達比較和判斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"theatre-goers","meaning":"劇場觀眾","examples":[{"en":"Eighteenth-century programmes told theatre-goers many things.","zh":"十八世紀的節目單告訴劇場觀眾很多事情。"},{"en":"Theatre-goers are people who attend theatre performances.","zh":"劇場觀眾是去觀看劇場演出的人。"},{"en":"Theatre-goers may buy programmes before sitting down to watch a play.","zh":"劇場觀眾可能在坐下看戲前購買節目單。"},{"en":"Theatre-goers use programmes to learn about the cast, plot, and production.","zh":"劇場觀眾使用節目單了解演員陣容、劇情和製作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to audience members at the theatre.","zh":"這個片語指劇院中的觀眾成員。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the writer","meaning":"作者；編劇","examples":[{"en":"The programmes included information about the writer.","zh":"節目單包括關於作者的資料。"},{"en":"The writer is the person who wrote the play or text.","zh":"作者或編劇是寫出戲劇或文本的人。"},{"en":"A programme may introduce the writer’s life and earlier works.","zh":"節目單可能介紹作者的生平和早期作品。"},{"en":"Knowing the writer helps audiences understand the themes of a play.","zh":"認識作者有助觀眾理解戲劇主題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the author or playwright.","zh":"這個片語指作者或劇作家。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the plot","meaning":"劇情","examples":[{"en":"The programmes included information about the plot.","zh":"節目單包括關於劇情的資料。"},{"en":"The plot is the main story or sequence of events in a play, book, or film.","zh":"劇情是戲劇、書本或電影中的主要故事或事件次序。"},{"en":"A programme may explain the plot so audiences can follow the performance more easily.","zh":"節目單可能解釋劇情，讓觀眾更容易跟上演出。"},{"en":"If the plot is complicated, a short summary can be helpful.","zh":"如果劇情複雜，簡短摘要會很有幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what happens in the story.","zh":"這個片語指故事中發生的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the history of the play","meaning":"戲劇的歷史","examples":[{"en":"Some programmes included the history of the play.","zh":"有些節目單包括戲劇的歷史。"},{"en":"The history of the play means information about when, why, and how the play was written or performed before.","zh":"戲劇的歷史意思是關於該劇何時、為何和如何寫成或曾經演出的資料。"},{"en":"The history of the play may include its first performance and famous productions.","zh":"戲劇的歷史可能包括首演和著名製作。"},{"en":"Learning the history of a play can make the performance more meaningful.","zh":"了解戲劇的歷史可以令演出更有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase gives background beyond the plot.","zh":"這個片語提供劇情以外的背景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"What should we say about","meaning":"我們應該怎樣談……","examples":[{"en":"Finn asks what they should say about twentieth-century programmes.","zh":"Finn 問他們應該怎樣談二十世紀的節目單。"},{"en":"What should we say about something means what information or opinion should we include about it?","zh":"我們應該怎樣談某事，意思是我們應該包括關於它的哪些資料或意見。"},{"en":"What should we say about the design changes in our presentation?","zh":"我們在簡報中應該怎樣談設計變化？"},{"en":"Students use this question when deciding what content belongs in a project.","zh":"學生決定專題中應放入甚麼內容時，會使用這個問題。"},{"en":"The phrase helps organise discussion and planning.","zh":"這個片語幫助組織討論和計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"twentieth century","meaning":"二十世紀","examples":[{"en":"Theatre programmes changed dramatically in the twentieth century.","zh":"劇場節目單在二十世紀有巨大變化。"},{"en":"The twentieth century means the years from 1901 to 2000.","zh":"二十世紀意思是 1901 年至 2000 年。"},{"en":"Theatre design and printing changed greatly during the twentieth century.","zh":"劇場設計和印刷在二十世紀發生很大變化。"},{"en":"Studying the twentieth century helps researchers understand modern theatre development.","zh":"研究二十世紀有助研究者理解現代劇場發展。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a major historical period.","zh":"這個片語指出一個重要歷史時期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"I reckon","meaning":"我認為","examples":[{"en":"Maya says, “I reckon the most important thing is the dramatic change.”","zh":"Maya 說：「我認為最重要的是那個巨大變化。」"},{"en":"I reckon means I think or I believe, often in an informal way.","zh":"我認為意思是我覺得或我相信，語氣通常較口語。"},{"en":"I reckon this source is useful for our project.","zh":"我認為這個資料來源對我們的專題有用。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to give an opinion rather than a proven fact.","zh":"人們用這個片語表達意見，而不是已證實事實。"},{"en":"It sounds conversational and personal.","zh":"它聽起來較口語和個人化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the most important thing","meaning":"最重要的事情","examples":[{"en":"Maya thinks the most important thing is the change during the war.","zh":"Maya 認為最重要的事情是戰爭期間的變化。"},{"en":"The most important thing means the point that matters more than all the others.","zh":"最重要的事情意思是比其他所有事情都更重要的重點。"},{"en":"In a presentation, the most important thing is to make the main idea clear.","zh":"在簡報中，最重要的事情是令主要想法清晰。"},{"en":"Identifying the most important thing helps students focus their research.","zh":"找出最重要的事情幫助學生集中研究。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the key point.","zh":"這個片語突出關鍵重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dramatic change","meaning":"巨大的變化","examples":[{"en":"Theatre programmes underwent a dramatic change during World War Two.","zh":"劇場節目單在第二次世界大戰期間經歷了巨大變化。"},{"en":"Dramatic change means a very big and noticeable change.","zh":"巨大的變化意思是非常大而明顯的改變。"},{"en":"The internet caused a dramatic change in how people buy tickets.","zh":"互聯網令購票方式出現巨大變化。"},{"en":"A dramatic change often affects design, behaviour, or organisation strongly.","zh":"巨大的變化通常會強烈影響設計、行為或組織方式。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the change was not small or gradual.","zh":"這個片語顯示變化並不小，也不只是緩慢改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"underwent","meaning":"經歷了","examples":[{"en":"Theatre programmes underwent a dramatic change during the war.","zh":"劇場節目單在戰爭期間經歷了巨大變化。"},{"en":"Underwent means experienced a change, process, or event.","zh":"經歷了意思是經過某種變化、過程或事件。"},{"en":"The old theatre underwent major repairs before reopening.","zh":"那座舊劇院在重新開放前經歷了大型維修。"},{"en":"A design may undergo changes because of money, materials, or audience needs.","zh":"設計可能因金錢、材料或觀眾需要而經歷變化。"},{"en":"The word is often used in formal writing about change.","zh":"這個詞常用於關於變化的正式寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"World War Two","meaning":"第二次世界大戰","examples":[{"en":"Theatre programmes changed during World War Two.","zh":"劇場節目單在第二次世界大戰期間改變。"},{"en":"World War Two was the global war that lasted from 1939 to 1945.","zh":"第二次世界大戰是 1939 年至 1945 年的全球戰爭。"},{"en":"During World War Two, many countries controlled materials such as paper and fuel.","zh":"第二次世界大戰期間，許多國家管制紙張和燃料等物資。"},{"en":"World War Two affected theatre because supplies and daily life were disrupted.","zh":"第二次世界大戰影響劇場，因為供應和日常生活受到干擾。"},{"en":"The phrase provides the historical context for the change in programmes.","zh":"這個片語為節目單變化提供歷史背景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"impose restrictions on","meaning":"對……施加限制","examples":[{"en":"The government imposed restrictions on the use of paper.","zh":"政府對紙張使用施加限制。"},{"en":"Impose restrictions on something means officially limit or control it.","zh":"對某事施加限制意思是正式限制或控制它。"},{"en":"The school imposed restrictions on phone use during exams.","zh":"學校對考試期間使用電話施加限制。"},{"en":"Governments may impose restrictions on materials during wartime.","zh":"政府可能在戰時對物資施加限制。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the limits were official, not voluntary.","zh":"這個片語顯示限制是官方的，不是自願的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the use of paper","meaning":"紙張使用","examples":[{"en":"The government restricted the use of paper during the war.","zh":"政府在戰爭期間限制紙張使用。"},{"en":"The use of paper means how much paper people or organisations are allowed to use.","zh":"紙張使用意思是人們或機構可以使用多少紙。"},{"en":"Offices reduced the use of paper by sending documents electronically.","zh":"辦公室透過電子傳送文件來減少紙張使用。"},{"en":"During a shortage, the use of paper may be limited to save supplies.","zh":"在短缺期間，紙張使用可能受到限制，以節省物資。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on paper as a material.","zh":"這個片語集中於紙張作為一種材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"or rather","meaning":"更準確地說","examples":[{"en":"In the USA, programmes, or rather playbills, continued in the same format.","zh":"在美國，節目單——更準確地說是 playbills——繼續以相同形式出版。"},{"en":"Or rather means more accurately or more exactly.","zh":"更準確地說意思是更精確或更正確地表達。"},{"en":"The show opens next week, or rather, next Friday.","zh":"這場演出下星期開演，更準確地說，是下星期五。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to correct or refine what they have just said.","zh":"人們用這個片語修正或調整剛才說的話。"},{"en":"It helps make wording more precise.","zh":"它幫助令措辭更精確。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"continued to be published","meaning":"繼續出版","examples":[{"en":"Playbills continued to be published in the same format.","zh":"Playbills 繼續以相同形式出版。"},{"en":"Continued to be published means kept being produced and made available.","zh":"繼續出版意思是持續被製作並提供給讀者。"},{"en":"The magazine continued to be published even during difficult times.","zh":"那本雜誌即使在困難時期仍繼續出版。"},{"en":"If a booklet continues to be published, readers can still obtain it regularly.","zh":"如果小冊子繼續出版，讀者仍能定期取得它。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that publication did not stop.","zh":"這個片語顯示出版沒有停止。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in the same format","meaning":"以相同形式","examples":[{"en":"American playbills continued to be published in the same format.","zh":"美國的 playbills 繼續以相同形式出版。"},{"en":"In the same format means using the same layout, size, structure, or style.","zh":"以相同形式意思是使用相同排版、大小、結構或風格。"},{"en":"The report must be submitted in the same format as last year’s report.","zh":"報告必須以與去年報告相同的形式提交。"},{"en":"Keeping the same format can make documents easier to recognise.","zh":"保持相同形式可以令文件更容易被認出。"},{"en":"The phrase describes consistency in presentation.","zh":"這個片語描述呈現方式的一致性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"merely a single sheet of paper","meaning":"只是一張紙","examples":[{"en":"British programmes became merely a single sheet of paper.","zh":"英國節目單變成只是一張紙。"},{"en":"Merely a single sheet of paper means only one piece of paper and nothing more elaborate.","zh":"只是一張紙意思是只有一張紙，沒有更精美或複雜的形式。"},{"en":"Because of the shortage, the newsletter was merely a single sheet of paper.","zh":"因為短缺，通訊變成只是一張紙。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests something became much simpler than before.","zh":"這個片語暗示某物變得比以前簡單得多。"},{"en":"It shows how paper restrictions changed programme design.","zh":"它顯示紙張限制如何改變節目單設計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"folded to create","meaning":"對摺成","examples":[{"en":"The sheet was folded to create four pages for text.","zh":"那張紙被對摺成四頁文字。"},{"en":"Folded to create means bent or doubled over so that a new shape or number of pages is formed.","zh":"對摺成意思是把紙彎摺或折疊，使它形成新形狀或頁數。"},{"en":"The paper was folded to create a small booklet.","zh":"那張紙被對摺成一本小冊子。"},{"en":"Folding one sheet can create more surfaces for printing.","zh":"折疊一張紙可以製造更多可印刷表面。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how a simple sheet became a programme.","zh":"這個片語解釋一張簡單紙張如何變成節目單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"four pages for text","meaning":"四頁文字","examples":[{"en":"The single sheet created four pages for text.","zh":"一張紙形成了四頁文字。"},{"en":"Four pages for text means four printed surfaces where words can be placed.","zh":"四頁文字意思是四個可以放文字的印刷頁面。"},{"en":"By folding the paper, the designer made four pages for text and adverts.","zh":"透過摺紙，設計師製成四頁文字和廣告空間。"},{"en":"Four pages for text gives more space than one flat sheet.","zh":"四頁文字比一張平面紙有更多空間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the practical result of folding paper.","zh":"這個片語描述摺紙後的實際結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"What I don’t really get is","meaning":"我真正不明白的是","examples":[{"en":"Maya says what she does not really get is the lack of change after the war.","zh":"Maya 說她真正不明白的是戰後沒有變化。"},{"en":"What I don’t really get is means what I do not fully understand is this point.","zh":"我真正不明白的是，意思是我不完全理解的是這一點。"},{"en":"What I don’t really get is why the rule stayed the same after the problem ended.","zh":"我真正不明白的是，為甚麼問題結束後規則仍然不變。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to introduce confusion or a question.","zh":"人們用這個片語引出困惑或疑問。"},{"en":"It sounds conversational and honest.","zh":"它聽起來口語而坦白。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"after the war","meaning":"戰後","examples":[{"en":"After the war, British programmes did not change for many years.","zh":"戰後，英國節目單多年來沒有改變。"},{"en":"After the war means in the period following a war.","zh":"戰後意思是在戰爭結束後的時期。"},{"en":"After the war, many cities had to rebuild theatres and public buildings.","zh":"戰後，許多城市需要重建劇院和公共建築。"},{"en":"The phrase helps explain changes or delays caused by wartime conditions.","zh":"這個片語幫助解釋由戰爭情況造成的變化或延遲。"},{"en":"It gives a historical time reference.","zh":"它提供歷史時間參考。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"go back to being","meaning":"恢復成","examples":[{"en":"The programmes did not go back to being more than one sheet.","zh":"節目單沒有恢復成多於一張紙。"},{"en":"Go back to being something means return to an earlier condition or form.","zh":"恢復成某種狀態意思是回到較早的狀態或形式。"},{"en":"After repairs, the hall went back to being a theatre.","zh":"維修後，那個大廳恢復成劇院。"},{"en":"A design may not go back to being complicated if people get used to a simpler style.","zh":"如果人們習慣了較簡單風格，設計可能不會恢復成複雜形式。"},{"en":"The phrase shows an expected return that did not happen.","zh":"這個片語顯示預期中的恢復沒有發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"more than one sheet","meaning":"多於一張紙","examples":[{"en":"British programmes did not return to being more than one sheet.","zh":"英國節目單沒有恢復成多於一張紙。"},{"en":"More than one sheet means two or more pieces of paper.","zh":"多於一張紙意思是兩張或以上的紙。"},{"en":"The handout was more than one sheet, so the teacher stapled it together.","zh":"那份講義多於一張紙，所以老師把它釘起來。"},{"en":"Programmes with more than one sheet can include more articles and images.","zh":"多於一張紙的節目單可以包括更多文章和圖片。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the physical length or size of a printed item.","zh":"這個片語描述印刷物的實際長度或大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in any way","meaning":"以任何方式","examples":[{"en":"The programmes did not change in any way for over twenty-five years.","zh":"這些節目單超過二十五年沒有以任何方式改變。"},{"en":"In any way means in any form, method, or respect.","zh":"以任何方式意思是以任何形式、方法或方面。"},{"en":"The rules did not change in any way after the meeting.","zh":"會議後，規則沒有以任何方式改變。"},{"en":"Saying something did not change in any way strongly emphasises no change at all.","zh":"說某事沒有以任何方式改變，是強調完全沒有改變。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to stress complete lack of difference.","zh":"這個片語用來強調完全沒有差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"for over twenty-five years","meaning":"超過二十五年","examples":[{"en":"British programmes did not develop for over twenty-five years.","zh":"英國節目單超過二十五年沒有發展。"},{"en":"For over twenty-five years means for more than twenty-five years.","zh":"超過二十五年意思是多於二十五年。"},{"en":"The old cinema remained closed for over twenty-five years.","zh":"那間舊戲院關閉了超過二十五年。"},{"en":"If something does not change for over twenty-five years, the delay feels surprising.","zh":"如果某事超過二十五年沒有改變，這種延遲會令人驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a long period of time.","zh":"這個片語表示一段很長的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"paper shortages","meaning":"紙張短缺","examples":[{"en":"There were paper shortages after the war.","zh":"戰後出現紙張短缺。"},{"en":"Paper shortages are situations where there is not enough paper available.","zh":"紙張短缺是指可用紙張不足的情況。"},{"en":"During paper shortages, publishers may print fewer pages.","zh":"在紙張短缺期間，出版商可能印刷較少頁數。"},{"en":"Paper shortages can affect books, newspapers, theatre programmes, and school materials.","zh":"紙張短缺可以影響書籍、報紙、劇場節目單和學校材料。"},{"en":"The phrase explains one possible reason programmes stayed short.","zh":"這個片語解釋節目單保持簡短的一個可能原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the rest of the discussion","meaning":"餘下的討論","examples":[{"en":"Candidates hear the rest of the discussion after reading the questions.","zh":"考生閱讀題目後聽餘下的討論。"},{"en":"The rest of the discussion means the remaining part of the conversation.","zh":"餘下的討論意思是對話中剩下的部分。"},{"en":"The class listened to the rest of the discussion after the break.","zh":"小息後，全班聽餘下的討論。"},{"en":"Hearing the rest of a discussion can provide answers not mentioned earlier.","zh":"聽餘下的討論可以提供之前未提到的答案。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what comes after the first part.","zh":"這個片語指第一部分之後的內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pictures of programmes","meaning":"節目單圖片","examples":[{"en":"Maya has pictures of programmes for the presentation slides.","zh":"Maya 有節目單圖片可用於簡報投影片。"},{"en":"Pictures of programmes are images showing theatre programme pages or covers.","zh":"節目單圖片是展示劇場節目單頁面或封面的圖像。"},{"en":"Pictures of programmes help audiences see how design changed over time.","zh":"節目單圖片幫助觀眾看見設計如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"Including pictures can make a presentation clearer and more interesting.","zh":"加入圖片可以令簡報更清晰和有趣。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to visual examples used in the project.","zh":"這個片語指專題中使用的視覺例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"include on the slides","meaning":"放進投影片","examples":[{"en":"They could include the pictures on the slides.","zh":"他們可以把圖片放進投影片。"},{"en":"Include on the slides means put information or images into presentation slides.","zh":"放進投影片意思是把資料或圖片加入簡報投影片中。"},{"en":"We should include the timeline on the slides so the audience can follow the history.","zh":"我們應該把時間線放進投影片，讓觀眾跟上歷史。"},{"en":"Choosing what to include on slides helps keep a presentation focused.","zh":"選擇要放進投影片的內容，有助保持簡報聚焦。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when preparing visual presentation materials.","zh":"這個片語用於準備視覺簡報材料時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"slides for our presentation","meaning":"簡報投影片","examples":[{"en":"The students need slides for their presentation.","zh":"學生需要簡報投影片。"},{"en":"Slides for our presentation are digital pages used to show key points, pictures, and examples while speaking.","zh":"簡報投影片是演講時用來展示重點、圖片和例子的數碼頁面。"},{"en":"We made slides for our presentation about theatre history.","zh":"我們為關於劇場歷史的簡報製作了投影片。"},{"en":"Good slides support the speaker without putting too much text on the screen.","zh":"好的投影片支持講者，而不會在螢幕上放太多文字。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to visual materials for a talk.","zh":"這個片語指演講用的視覺材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a couple","meaning":"幾個；兩三個","examples":[{"en":"Finn found a couple of pictures too.","zh":"Finn 也找到幾張圖片。"},{"en":"A couple means two or a few.","zh":"幾個或兩三個意思是兩個或少數幾個。"},{"en":"I found a couple of useful books in the library.","zh":"我在圖書館找到幾本有用的書。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when the exact number is small and not very important.","zh":"當確切數量很少且不太重要時，人們會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It sounds natural and conversational.","zh":"它聽起來自然和口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"go through","meaning":"逐一查看","examples":[{"en":"They go through the pictures together.","zh":"他們一起逐一查看圖片。"},{"en":"Go through means examine or discuss items one by one.","zh":"逐一查看意思是一項一項地檢查或討論。"},{"en":"The students went through their notes before the presentation.","zh":"學生在簡報前逐一查看筆記。"},{"en":"Going through pictures together helps people decide which ones to use.","zh":"一起逐一查看圖片幫助人們決定使用哪些。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests careful review.","zh":"這個片語暗示仔細檢視。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a play called","meaning":"一齣名為……的戲","examples":[{"en":"Maya shows a programme for a play called Ruy Blas.","zh":"Maya 展示一份一齣名為《Ruy Blas》的戲的節目單。"},{"en":"A play called something means a play with that title.","zh":"一齣名為某某的戲，意思是以該名稱作標題的戲劇。"},{"en":"The class watched a play called The Glass Menagerie.","zh":"全班觀看了一齣名為《玻璃動物園》的戲。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when introducing the title of a play.","zh":"人們介紹戲劇名稱時會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It helps listeners recognise that the following words are a title.","zh":"它幫助聽眾明白接下來的字是標題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Ruy Blas","meaning":"《Ruy Blas》","examples":[{"en":"The programme for Ruy Blas looks very decorative.","zh":"《Ruy Blas》的節目單看起來很有裝飾性。"},{"en":"Ruy Blas is the title of a play discussed in Maya and Finn’s project.","zh":"《Ruy Blas》是 Maya 和 Finn 專題中討論的一齣戲的名稱。"},{"en":"A programme for Ruy Blas could show how theatre design looked in its period.","zh":"《Ruy Blas》的節目單可以展示該時期劇場設計的樣貌。"},{"en":"The title helps identify which performance the programme belongs to.","zh":"標題幫助指出節目單屬於哪場演出。"},{"en":"In the discussion, Ruy Blas is used as a visual example.","zh":"在討論中，《Ruy Blas》被用作視覺例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Never heard of","meaning":"從未聽過","examples":[{"en":"Finn has never heard of Ruy Blas.","zh":"Finn 從未聽過《Ruy Blas》。"},{"en":"Never heard of something means not know about it at all before.","zh":"從未聽過某事意思是以前完全不知道它。"},{"en":"I have never heard of that playwright, so I need to research him.","zh":"我從未聽過那位劇作家，所以需要研究他。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when a name or title is unfamiliar.","zh":"當名字或標題不熟悉時，人們會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It shows lack of previous knowledge.","zh":"它顯示以前沒有相關知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"look very decorative","meaning":"看起來很有裝飾性","examples":[{"en":"The programme looks very decorative.","zh":"這份節目單看起來很有裝飾性。"},{"en":"Look very decorative means appear attractive because of detailed patterns, images, or design.","zh":"看起來很有裝飾性意思是因細緻圖案、圖像或設計而顯得吸引。"},{"en":"The old theatre poster looks very decorative with flowers around the title.","zh":"那張舊劇場海報標題周圍有花紋，看起來很有裝飾性。"},{"en":"Decorative design can make a programme feel like a collectable object.","zh":"裝飾性設計可以令節目單感覺像收藏品。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on visual beauty rather than information.","zh":"這個片語集中於視覺美感，而不是資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"good enough to","meaning":"好到足以……","examples":[{"en":"The programme is good enough to put in a frame.","zh":"這份節目單好到足以裝框。"},{"en":"Good enough to do something means of sufficient quality for that action.","zh":"好到足以做某事，意思是質素足夠高，可以做那件事。"},{"en":"The photograph was good enough to use on the presentation cover.","zh":"那張照片好到足以用作簡報封面。"},{"en":"If a programme is good enough to frame, it must look very attractive.","zh":"如果一份節目單好到足以裝框，它一定看起來很吸引。"},{"en":"The phrase shows praise by saying what the item deserves.","zh":"這個片語透過說物件值得怎樣處理來表達稱讚。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"put in a frame","meaning":"裝框","examples":[{"en":"The programme is beautiful enough to put in a frame.","zh":"這份節目單漂亮到足以裝框。"},{"en":"Put in a frame means place something inside a frame so it can be displayed or protected.","zh":"裝框意思是把某物放進框中，以便展示或保護。"},{"en":"She put the old theatre poster in a frame and hung it in her room.","zh":"她把那張舊劇場海報裝框，掛在房間裏。"},{"en":"People frame pictures or documents when they think they are attractive or important.","zh":"當人們覺得圖片或文件漂亮或重要時，會把它們裝框。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests the programme looks like artwork.","zh":"這個片語暗示節目單看起來像藝術品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on the wall","meaning":"在牆上","examples":[{"en":"The programme could be put in a frame on the wall.","zh":"這份節目單可以裝框掛在牆上。"},{"en":"On the wall means attached to or hanging from a wall.","zh":"在牆上意思是貼在或掛在牆壁上。"},{"en":"The theatre hung old programme covers on the wall.","zh":"劇院把舊節目單封面掛在牆上。"},{"en":"Putting something on the wall makes it visible as decoration.","zh":"把某物放在牆上可以使它成為可見的裝飾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where the framed programme could be displayed.","zh":"這個片語描述裝框節目單可以展示的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"beautiful images","meaning":"美麗的圖像","examples":[{"en":"The images in the programme are beautiful.","zh":"節目單中的圖像很美麗。"},{"en":"Beautiful images are pictures that look attractive, artistic, or pleasing.","zh":"美麗的圖像是看起來吸引、有藝術感或令人愉悅的圖片。"},{"en":"The programme used beautiful images to make the play feel special.","zh":"節目單使用美麗的圖像，令那齣戲感覺特別。"},{"en":"Beautiful images can make a theatre programme worth keeping.","zh":"美麗的圖像可以令劇場節目單值得保存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the visual quality of the programme.","zh":"這個片語描述節目單的視覺質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"pages from a programme","meaning":"節目單的幾頁","examples":[{"en":"Finn has some pages from a programme for Man of La Mancha.","zh":"Finn 有幾頁《Man of La Mancha》的節目單。"},{"en":"Pages from a programme are selected pages taken from a theatre programme booklet.","zh":"節目單的幾頁是從劇場節目小冊子中取出的選定頁面。"},{"en":"The archive showed pages from a programme printed in the 1950s.","zh":"檔案館展示了幾頁 1950 年代印刷的節目單。"},{"en":"Pages from a programme can reveal articles, cast lists, and design style.","zh":"節目單的幾頁可以顯示文章、演員名單和設計風格。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to parts of a programme, not the whole booklet.","zh":"這個片語指節目單的一部分，不是整本小冊子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Man of La Mancha","meaning":"《Man of La Mancha》","examples":[{"en":"Finn found pages from a programme for Man of La Mancha.","zh":"Finn 找到幾頁《Man of La Mancha》的節目單。"},{"en":"Man of La Mancha is the title of a theatre production discussed in the project.","zh":"《Man of La Mancha》是專題中討論的一部劇場作品名稱。"},{"en":"A programme for Man of La Mancha may include articles by the theatre company.","zh":"《Man of La Mancha》的節目單可能包括劇團成員撰寫的文章。"},{"en":"The title helps identify which show the programme belongs to.","zh":"標題幫助指出節目單屬於哪齣演出。"},{"en":"In the discussion, Man of La Mancha is useful because of its written content.","zh":"在討論中，《Man of La Mancha》因其文字內容而有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a good programme to show","meaning":"值得展示的節目單","examples":[{"en":"Finn thinks this is a good programme to show.","zh":"Finn 認為這是一份值得展示的節目單。"},{"en":"A good programme to show means a programme that is useful or suitable as an example.","zh":"值得展示的節目單意思是適合或有用作例子的節目單。"},{"en":"This old booklet is a good programme to show because it includes notes from the actors.","zh":"這本舊小冊子值得展示，因為它包括演員筆記。"},{"en":"A good example helps audiences understand the project’s main point.","zh":"好例子幫助觀眾理解專題的主要重點。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why a programme should be included in the presentation.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何應在簡報中加入某份節目單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not because of","meaning":"不是因為……","examples":[{"en":"The programme is useful not because of the pictures, but because of its articles.","zh":"這份節目單有用，不是因為圖片，而是因為文章。"},{"en":"Not because of means the reason is not this thing.","zh":"不是因為……意思是原因並不是這件事。"},{"en":"The book is valuable not because of its cover, but because of its rare notes.","zh":"這本書有價值，不是因為封面，而是因為稀有筆記。"},{"en":"This phrase helps contrast a false reason with the real reason.","zh":"這個片語幫助對比錯誤原因和真正原因。"},{"en":"It guides listeners toward the correct explanation.","zh":"它引導聽眾走向正確解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"contain articles written by","meaning":"載有由……撰寫的文章","examples":[{"en":"The programme contains articles written by members of the theatre company.","zh":"這份節目單載有由劇團成員撰寫的文章。"},{"en":"Contain articles written by someone means include written pieces created by those people.","zh":"載有由某人撰寫的文章，意思是包括那些人寫的文章。"},{"en":"The magazine contains articles written by students and teachers.","zh":"這本雜誌載有由學生和老師撰寫的文章。"},{"en":"Articles written by theatre company members can give inside views of a production.","zh":"由劇團成員撰寫的文章可以提供作品的內部觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what kind of written content the programme includes.","zh":"這個片語解釋節目單包括哪類文字內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"members of the theatre company","meaning":"劇團成員","examples":[{"en":"Members of the theatre company wrote articles for the programme.","zh":"劇團成員為節目單撰寫文章。"},{"en":"Members of the theatre company are people involved in the theatre group, such as actors, directors, or production staff.","zh":"劇團成員是參與劇團的人，例如演員、導演或製作人員。"},{"en":"Members of the theatre company may explain how they prepared the show.","zh":"劇團成員可能會解釋他們如何準備演出。"},{"en":"Their writing can help audiences understand the production from the inside.","zh":"他們的文字可以幫助觀眾從內部理解製作。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the people connected with creating the performance.","zh":"這個片語指出與創作演出有關的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"learn how","meaning":"了解如何……","examples":[{"en":"Readers can learn how the production was created.","zh":"讀者可以了解這部作品是如何創作的。"},{"en":"Learn how means find out the method, process, or way something happened.","zh":"了解如何……意思是知道某事發生或完成的方法、過程或方式。"},{"en":"Students can learn how costumes are designed by reading interviews with designers.","zh":"學生可以透過閱讀設計師訪問，了解戲服如何設計。"},{"en":"Learning how something was made helps people appreciate the work behind it.","zh":"了解某物如何製作，可以幫助人欣賞背後的工作。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces practical or process-based information.","zh":"這個片語引出實用或過程性的資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the production was created","meaning":"這部作品是如何創作的","examples":[{"en":"The programme explains how the production was created.","zh":"節目單解釋這部作品是如何創作的。"},{"en":"The production was created means the show was planned, rehearsed, designed, and brought to the stage.","zh":"這部作品是如何創作的，意思是演出如何被計劃、排練、設計並搬上舞台。"},{"en":"A documentary may show how the production was created from the first rehearsal to opening night.","zh":"紀錄片可能展示這部作品如何由第一次排練到首演被創作出來。"},{"en":"Understanding how a production was created helps audiences see the effort behind the performance.","zh":"理解一部作品如何創作，幫助觀眾看見演出背後的努力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the making of a theatre show.","zh":"這個片語指劇場演出的製作過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"thoughts and feelings","meaning":"想法和感受","examples":[{"en":"The articles reveal the thoughts and feelings of the cast.","zh":"這些文章揭示演員陣容的想法和感受。"},{"en":"Thoughts and feelings are what people think and emotionally experience.","zh":"想法和感受是人們思考的內容和情緒經驗。"},{"en":"An actor’s diary can show their thoughts and feelings during rehearsals.","zh":"演員日記可以顯示他們在排練期間的想法和感受。"},{"en":"Sharing thoughts and feelings helps audiences understand performers as people.","zh":"分享想法和感受幫助觀眾把表演者視為真實的人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to inner ideas and emotions.","zh":"這個片語指內心想法和情緒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a copy of a programme","meaning":"一份節目單副本","examples":[{"en":"Maya has a copy of a programme that is now in a museum.","zh":"Maya 有一份現收藏於博物館的節目單副本。"},{"en":"A copy of a programme is a reproduced or saved version of a theatre programme.","zh":"一份節目單副本是劇場節目單的複製或保存版本。"},{"en":"The archive kept a copy of a programme from the first performance.","zh":"檔案館保存了一份首演節目單副本。"},{"en":"A copy can be useful when the original is rare or protected.","zh":"當原件稀有或受保護時，副本會很有用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a version of the programme that can be shown or studied.","zh":"這個片語指可以展示或研究的節目單版本。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"now in a museum","meaning":"現收藏於博物館","examples":[{"en":"The programme is now in a museum.","zh":"這份節目單現收藏於博物館。"},{"en":"Now in a museum means currently kept or displayed in a museum collection.","zh":"現收藏於博物館意思是目前保存在或展示於博物館館藏中。"},{"en":"The old theatre poster is now in a museum because it is historically important.","zh":"那張舊劇場海報因具有歷史重要性，現收藏於博物館。"},{"en":"If an object is now in a museum, it may be protected and studied by experts.","zh":"如果物件現收藏於博物館，它可能受到保護並由專家研究。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the item has cultural or historical value.","zh":"這個片語顯示物件有文化或歷史價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"The Tragedy of Jane Shore","meaning":"《The Tragedy of Jane Shore》","examples":[{"en":"The programme for The Tragedy of Jane Shore is historically important.","zh":"《The Tragedy of Jane Shore》的節目單具有歷史重要性。"},{"en":"The Tragedy of Jane Shore is the title of a play connected with an early printed programme.","zh":"《The Tragedy of Jane Shore》是一齣戲的名稱，與早期印刷節目單有關。"},{"en":"A programme for The Tragedy of Jane Shore can be studied as a historical document.","zh":"《The Tragedy of Jane Shore》的節目單可以作為歷史文件研究。"},{"en":"The title helps identify the performance linked to Australia’s early printing history.","zh":"這個標題幫助指出與澳洲早期印刷歷史有關的演出。"},{"en":"In the discussion, this programme is important because of its origin.","zh":"在討論中，這份節目單因其來源而重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be said to be","meaning":"據說是","examples":[{"en":"The document is said to be the earliest surviving printed item from Australia’s first printing press.","zh":"這份文件據說是來自澳洲第一台印刷機的現存最早印刷品。"},{"en":"Be said to be means people claim or believe something is true.","zh":"據說是意思是人們聲稱或相信某事是真的。"},{"en":"The old theatre ticket is said to be the first one printed in the city.","zh":"那張舊劇場門票據說是該城市第一張印刷門票。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when information is reported but may not be directly proven by the speaker.","zh":"當資料是被轉述、但說話者未必親自證實時，這個片語很有用。"},{"en":"It presents a claim carefully.","zh":"它謹慎地提出一個說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the earliest surviving document","meaning":"現存最早的文件","examples":[{"en":"It is the earliest surviving document printed on Australia’s first printing press.","zh":"它是由澳洲第一台印刷機印刷的現存最早文件。"},{"en":"The earliest surviving document means the oldest document that still exists today.","zh":"現存最早的文件意思是今天仍存在的最古老文件。"},{"en":"The earliest surviving document in the archive is kept in a special case.","zh":"檔案館中的現存最早文件保存在特別箱中。"},{"en":"Such a document is valuable because many older items may have been lost or destroyed.","zh":"這樣的文件很有價值，因為很多更舊的物品可能已遺失或被毀。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises age and survival.","zh":"這個片語強調年代久遠和保存下來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be printed on","meaning":"由……印刷","examples":[{"en":"The document was printed on Australia’s first printing press.","zh":"這份文件由澳洲第一台印刷機印刷。"},{"en":"Be printed on means be produced using a particular machine, material, or surface.","zh":"由……印刷意思是使用某部機器、某種材料或某個表面製作出來。"},{"en":"The poster was printed on thick paper.","zh":"海報印刷在厚紙上。"},{"en":"If a document was printed on an early press, it may have historical value.","zh":"如果文件由早期印刷機印刷，它可能具有歷史價值。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the tool or surface used for printing.","zh":"這個片語解釋印刷所使用的工具或表面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Australia’s first printing press","meaning":"澳洲第一台印刷機","examples":[{"en":"The programme was printed on Australia’s first printing press.","zh":"這份節目單由澳洲第一台印刷機印刷。"},{"en":"Australia’s first printing press was the first machine used to print documents in Australia.","zh":"澳洲第一台印刷機是在澳洲用來印刷文件的第一部機器。"},{"en":"A programme printed on Australia’s first printing press is historically important.","zh":"由澳洲第一台印刷機印刷的節目單具有歷史重要性。"},{"en":"Printing presses changed how information could be copied and shared.","zh":"印刷機改變了資料被複製和分享的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase connects the programme with printing history.","zh":"這個片語把節目單與印刷歷史連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"another programme to talk about","meaning":"另一份可以談論的節目單","examples":[{"en":"Another programme to talk about is for The Sailors’ Festival.","zh":"另一份可以談論的節目單是《The Sailors’ Festival》的節目單。"},{"en":"Another programme to talk about means one more programme that should be discussed.","zh":"另一份可以談論的節目單意思是另一個應該討論的節目單例子。"},{"en":"Another programme to talk about is useful because it comes from a digital archive.","zh":"另一份可以談論的節目單很有用，因為它來自數碼檔案。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when adding a further example to a presentation.","zh":"人們在簡報中加入另一個例子時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It helps continue the list of examples.","zh":"它幫助繼續例子清單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"The Sailors’ Festival","meaning":"《The Sailors’ Festival》","examples":[{"en":"The Sailors’ Festival programme comes from a digitised collection.","zh":"《The Sailors’ Festival》的節目單來自數碼化館藏。"},{"en":"The Sailors’ Festival is the title of a show linked with a theatre programme in the discussion.","zh":"《The Sailors’ Festival》是討論中與劇場節目單有關的一齣演出名稱。"},{"en":"A programme for The Sailors’ Festival can be used as an example of archived theatre material.","zh":"《The Sailors’ Festival》的節目單可以作為劇場檔案材料的例子。"},{"en":"The title helps identify the item in the collection.","zh":"標題幫助在館藏中識別該項目。"},{"en":"In the project, The Sailors’ Festival is useful because it is part of a recent digitisation project.","zh":"在專題中，《The Sailors’ Festival》有用，因為它屬於近期數碼化項目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"come from","meaning":"來自","examples":[{"en":"The programme comes from the British Library’s digitised collection.","zh":"這份節目單來自大英圖書館的數碼化館藏。"},{"en":"Come from means originate in or be taken from a particular place or source.","zh":"來自意思是源自或取自某個地方或來源。"},{"en":"This image comes from an online archive.","zh":"這張圖片來自網上檔案。"},{"en":"Saying where information comes from helps make research more reliable.","zh":"說明資料來自哪裏，有助令研究更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of an item.","zh":"這個片語指出項目的來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the British Library","meaning":"大英圖書館","examples":[{"en":"The programme comes from the British Library’s collection.","zh":"這份節目單來自大英圖書館的館藏。"},{"en":"The British Library is a major library in the UK with large historical and cultural collections.","zh":"大英圖書館是英國一間主要圖書館，擁有大量歷史和文化館藏。"},{"en":"Researchers may use the British Library to find rare books, manuscripts, and theatre materials.","zh":"研究者可能使用大英圖書館尋找稀有書籍、手稿和劇場材料。"},{"en":"A theatre programme from the British Library can be a useful academic source.","zh":"來自大英圖書館的劇場節目單可以是有用的學術資料來源。"},{"en":"The phrase names the institution that holds the collection.","zh":"這個片語指出收藏該館藏的機構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"digitised collection","meaning":"數碼化館藏","examples":[{"en":"The British Library has a digitised collection of theatre programmes.","zh":"大英圖書館有一個劇場節目單數碼化館藏。"},{"en":"A digitised collection is a group of materials converted into digital form.","zh":"數碼化館藏是被轉換成數碼形式的一批材料。"},{"en":"A digitised collection lets researchers view old documents online.","zh":"數碼化館藏讓研究者在網上查看舊文件。"},{"en":"Digitising theatre programmes protects the originals while making them easier to access.","zh":"將劇場節目單數碼化可以保護原件，同時令它們更容易取用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to archive materials made available digitally.","zh":"這個片語指以數碼形式提供的檔案材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a few years ago","meaning":"幾年前","examples":[{"en":"The digitised collection was started a few years ago.","zh":"這個數碼化館藏在幾年前開始。"},{"en":"A few years ago means several years before now.","zh":"幾年前意思是現在之前數年。"},{"en":"The theatre archive project began a few years ago.","zh":"劇場檔案項目在幾年前開始。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when the exact year is not necessary.","zh":"當確切年份不重要時，人們會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It gives a general time reference in the recent past.","zh":"它提供近年過去的大概時間參考。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"comprise over","meaning":"包含超過","examples":[{"en":"The collection comprises over two hundred thousand programmes.","zh":"這個館藏包含超過二十萬份節目單。"},{"en":"Comprise over means contain more than a particular number.","zh":"包含超過意思是含有多於某個數量。"},{"en":"The archive comprises over ten thousand photographs.","zh":"這個檔案館包含超過一萬張照片。"},{"en":"A collection that comprises over two hundred thousand items is very large.","zh":"一個包含超過二十萬項物件的館藏非常龐大。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and often used in academic description.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常用於學術描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"over two hundred thousand","meaning":"超過二十萬","examples":[{"en":"The collection already comprises over two hundred thousand programmes.","zh":"這個館藏已經包含超過二十萬份節目單。"},{"en":"Over two hundred thousand means more than 200,000.","zh":"超過二十萬意思是多於 200,000。"},{"en":"The website has over two hundred thousand images in its archive.","zh":"這個網站的檔案中有超過二十萬張圖片。"},{"en":"Such a large number shows the collection is extensive.","zh":"這樣大的數字顯示館藏非常龐大。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a sense of scale.","zh":"這個片語提供規模感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Wish I’d known about it","meaning":"真希望我早知道","examples":[{"en":"Finn wishes he had known about the collection during his research.","zh":"Finn 真希望他做研究時早知道這個館藏。"},{"en":"Wish I’d known about it means I regret not knowing about it earlier.","zh":"真希望我早知道意思是我後悔之前不知道它。"},{"en":"Wish I’d known about that archive before I finished my essay.","zh":"真希望我在完成文章前早知道那個檔案館。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when useful information comes too late.","zh":"當有用資料來得太遲時，人們會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It expresses regret about missed help or opportunity.","zh":"它表達對錯過幫助或機會的遺憾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"while I was doing my research","meaning":"當我做研究時","examples":[{"en":"Finn did not know about the collection while he was doing his research.","zh":"Finn 當他做研究時不知道這個館藏。"},{"en":"While I was doing my research means during the time I was researching the topic.","zh":"當我做研究時意思是在我研究該題目的期間。"},{"en":"While I was doing my research, I found several old newspaper reviews.","zh":"當我做研究時，我找到幾篇舊報紙評論。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event inside the research period.","zh":"這個片語把某事件放在研究期間之內。"},{"en":"It helps explain when information was or was not discovered.","zh":"它幫助解釋資料是在何時被發現或沒有被發現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Project on Theatre Programmes","meaning":"關於劇場節目單的專題","examples":[{"en":"The question section is about a project on theatre programmes.","zh":"題目部分是關於劇場節目單的專題。"},{"en":"A project on theatre programmes studies the history, design, and purpose of theatre programme booklets.","zh":"關於劇場節目單的專題研究劇場節目小冊子的歷史、設計和用途。"},{"en":"Students doing a project on theatre programmes may compare examples from different centuries.","zh":"做關於劇場節目單專題的學生可能比較不同世紀的例子。"},{"en":"Such a project can show how theatre audiences received information in the past.","zh":"這樣的專題可以顯示過去劇場觀眾如何取得資料。"},{"en":"The phrase names the academic task being discussed.","zh":"這個片語指出正在討論的學術任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be pleased to discover that","meaning":"很高興發現","examples":[{"en":"Finn was pleased to discover that their topic had not been chosen by others.","zh":"Finn 很高興發現他們的題目沒有被其他人選擇。"},{"en":"Be pleased to discover that means feel happy when you find out something.","zh":"很高興發現意思是在得知某事時感到高興。"},{"en":"The students were pleased to discover that the archive was free to use.","zh":"學生很高興發現那個檔案館可以免費使用。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when new information brings satisfaction.","zh":"當新資料帶來滿足感時，人們會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It shows a positive reaction to a finding.","zh":"它顯示對發現的正面反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"not familiar to","meaning":"對……不熟悉","examples":[{"en":"The option says the topic was not familiar to the module leader.","zh":"選項說這個題目對模組負責人不熟悉。"},{"en":"Not familiar to someone means not known well by that person.","zh":"對某人不熟悉意思是那人不太了解或不太認得它。"},{"en":"The old theatre term was not familiar to most students.","zh":"這個舊劇場詞語對大多數學生來說不熟悉。"},{"en":"If a topic is not familiar to a teacher, students may need to explain it clearly.","zh":"如果一個題目對老師不熟悉，學生可能需要清楚解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lack of knowledge or recognition.","zh":"這個片語描述缺乏認識或辨認。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"module leader","meaning":"模組負責人","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to their module leader.","zh":"題目提到他們的模組負責人。"},{"en":"A module leader is the person responsible for leading a course module.","zh":"模組負責人是負責帶領某個課程模組的人。"},{"en":"The module leader explained the marking rules for the project.","zh":"模組負責人解釋專題的評分規則。"},{"en":"A module leader may also be called a module convenor.","zh":"模組負責人也可稱為 module convenor。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the person in charge of a unit of study.","zh":"這個片語指出負責某個學習單元的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be chosen by","meaning":"被……選擇","examples":[{"en":"The topic had not been chosen by other students.","zh":"這個題目沒有被其他學生選擇。"},{"en":"Be chosen by means be selected by someone.","zh":"被……選擇意思是由某人選中。"},{"en":"The play was chosen by the class for their final performance.","zh":"那齣戲被全班選為期末演出。"},{"en":"If a topic is not chosen by others, it may feel more original.","zh":"如果題目沒有被其他人選擇，它可能感覺更有原創性。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who selected something.","zh":"這個片語指出某物由誰選中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"prove to be difficult to research","meaning":"證明難以研究","examples":[{"en":"The topic did not prove to be difficult to research.","zh":"這個題目並沒有證明難以研究。"},{"en":"Prove to be difficult to research means turn out to be hard to investigate.","zh":"證明難以研究意思是結果顯示它很難調查。"},{"en":"The rare theatre topic proved to be difficult to research because few sources existed.","zh":"這個罕見劇場題目證明難以研究，因為資料來源很少。"},{"en":"A subject may prove difficult to research if information is hidden, old, or unreliable.","zh":"如果資料隱藏、古老或不可靠，一個主題可能證明難以研究。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what becomes clear during the research process.","zh":"這個片語描述研究過程中逐漸清楚的情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"mistaken belief about","meaning":"對……的錯誤看法","examples":[{"en":"Maya explains a mistaken belief about theatre programmes.","zh":"Maya 解釋一個對劇場節目單的錯誤看法。"},{"en":"A mistaken belief about something is an incorrect idea people have about it.","zh":"對某事的錯誤看法是人們對它持有的不正確想法。"},{"en":"A common mistaken belief about online learning is that it is always easier.","zh":"對網上學習的一個常見錯誤看法是它總是較容易。"},{"en":"Explaining mistaken beliefs helps correct misunderstanding.","zh":"解釋錯誤看法有助糾正誤解。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an idea that needs to be corrected.","zh":"這個片語引出需要被更正的想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"far more adverts than previously","meaning":"比以前多得多的廣告","examples":[{"en":"The option says programmes contain far more adverts than previously.","zh":"選項說節目單包含比以前多得多的廣告。"},{"en":"Far more adverts than previously means many more advertisements than before.","zh":"比以前多得多的廣告意思是廣告數量比以前多很多。"},{"en":"Modern magazines often contain far more adverts than previously because advertising brings income.","zh":"現代雜誌常包含比以前多得多的廣告，因為廣告帶來收入。"},{"en":"More adverts can change the balance between information and promotion.","zh":"更多廣告可能改變資料和宣傳之間的平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the amount of advertising across time.","zh":"這個片語比較不同時期的廣告數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be seen as","meaning":"被視為","examples":[{"en":"Early programmes were seen as a kind of contract.","zh":"早期節目單被視為一種合約。"},{"en":"Be seen as means be regarded or understood as something.","zh":"被視為意思是被看作或理解為某物。"},{"en":"A ticket can be seen as proof that someone paid for entry.","zh":"門票可以被視為某人已付款入場的證明。"},{"en":"If programmes were seen as contracts, audiences expected theatres to keep their promises.","zh":"如果節目單被視為合約，觀眾就期望劇院履行承諾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how people interpreted something.","zh":"這個片語描述人們如何理解某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a kind of contract","meaning":"一種合約","examples":[{"en":"Programmes were seen as a kind of contract with the audience.","zh":"節目單被視為與觀眾的一種合約。"},{"en":"A kind of contract means something like an agreement, even if it is not a formal legal document.","zh":"一種合約意思是像協議一樣的東西，即使不是正式法律文件。"},{"en":"A poster naming a singer can feel like a kind of contract with fans.","zh":"列出歌手名字的海報可能像是與粉絲的一種合約。"},{"en":"If the promised performer does not appear, audiences may feel the contract was broken.","zh":"如果承諾的表演者沒有出現，觀眾可能覺得合約被違反。"},{"en":"The phrase helps explain why early audiences demanded refunds.","zh":"這個片語幫助解釋為何早期觀眾要求退款。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"an explanation of why","meaning":"對……原因的解釋","examples":[{"en":"The project should include an explanation of why actors promoted plays.","zh":"專題應包括對演員為何宣傳戲劇的原因解釋。"},{"en":"An explanation of why means a clear reason for something.","zh":"對……原因的解釋意思是清楚說明某事的原因。"},{"en":"The essay needs an explanation of why paper became scarce during the war.","zh":"文章需要對戰時紙張為何短缺作出解釋。"},{"en":"Giving an explanation of why helps readers understand causes, not only facts.","zh":"提供原因解釋幫助讀者理解成因，而不只是事實。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a reason-based answer.","zh":"這個片語引出基於原因的答案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"promote their own plays","meaning":"宣傳自己的戲劇","examples":[{"en":"Companies of actors promoted their own plays in the streets.","zh":"劇團在街上宣傳自己的戲劇。"},{"en":"Promote their own plays means advertise or publicise the plays they perform themselves.","zh":"宣傳自己的戲劇意思是推廣或宣傳他們自己演出的戲劇。"},{"en":"A small theatre group may promote its own plays by handing out flyers.","zh":"小劇團可能透過派傳單宣傳自己的戲劇。"},{"en":"Actors promoted their own plays because printed programmes could not reach everyone.","zh":"演員宣傳自己的戲劇，因為印刷節目單不能接觸所有人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes self-advertising by performers.","zh":"這個片語描述表演者自行宣傳。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"perform plays outdoors","meaning":"在戶外演出戲劇","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to companies performing plays outdoors.","zh":"選項提到劇團在戶外演出戲劇。"},{"en":"Perform plays outdoors means act out theatre performances outside rather than inside a theatre.","zh":"在戶外演出戲劇意思是在劇院以外的地方演出戲劇。"},{"en":"Some festivals perform plays outdoors in parks or town squares.","zh":"有些節日在公園或市鎮廣場戶外演出戲劇。"},{"en":"Outdoor performances can reach people who may not enter a theatre.","zh":"戶外演出可以接觸到可能不會進入劇院的人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the location of a performance.","zh":"這個片語描述演出的地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"tour with their plays","meaning":"帶同戲劇巡迴演出","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to actors touring with their plays.","zh":"選項提到演員帶同戲劇巡迴演出。"},{"en":"Tour with their plays means travel to different places to perform the same plays.","zh":"帶同戲劇巡迴演出意思是到不同地方演出同一批戲劇。"},{"en":"The company toured with its plays across several towns.","zh":"劇團帶同戲劇到幾個城鎮巡迴演出。"},{"en":"Touring with plays helps performers reach audiences in different areas.","zh":"巡迴演出幫助表演者接觸不同地區的觀眾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes travelling performance work.","zh":"這個片語描述巡迴表演工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"compared to","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Compared to later programmes, eighteenth-century programmes were more informative.","zh":"與後來的節目單相比，十八世紀的節目單資料更豐富。"},{"en":"Compared to means when examined beside another thing.","zh":"與……相比意思是把某物放在另一物旁邊考察。"},{"en":"Compared to handwritten notes, printed programmes looked more formal.","zh":"與手寫筆記相比，印刷節目單看起來更正式。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to show similarities or differences.","zh":"這個片語用來顯示相似或差異。"},{"en":"It helps make a judgement by using a second item as a reference.","zh":"它透過另一項目作參考來幫助判斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"more original","meaning":"更有原創性","examples":[{"en":"The option describes earlier programmes as more original.","zh":"選項形容較早期節目單更有原創性。"},{"en":"More original means more new, creative, or unlike copies of other things.","zh":"更有原創性意思是更新穎、更有創意或較不像抄襲其他東西。"},{"en":"A student’s essay is more original when it uses personal examples.","zh":"學生作文使用個人例子時會更有原創性。"},{"en":"Originality matters when work should show fresh thinking.","zh":"當作品需要顯示新想法時，原創性很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase compares creativity between two things.","zh":"這個片語比較兩者的創意程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"more colourful","meaning":"色彩更豐富","examples":[{"en":"The option describes programmes as more colourful.","zh":"選項形容節目單色彩更豐富。"},{"en":"More colourful means having more colours or a brighter visual appearance.","zh":"色彩更豐富意思是有更多顏色或更鮮明的視覺外觀。"},{"en":"The modern poster is more colourful than the old black-and-white one.","zh":"現代海報比舊黑白海報色彩更豐富。"},{"en":"A more colourful design can attract attention quickly.","zh":"色彩更豐富的設計可以更快吸引注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visual appearance.","zh":"這個片語描述視覺外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"more informative","meaning":"資料更豐富","examples":[{"en":"Eighteenth-century programmes were more informative than nineteenth-century ones.","zh":"十八世紀的節目單比十九世紀的節目單資料更豐富。"},{"en":"More informative means giving more useful information.","zh":"資料更豐富意思是提供更多有用資料。"},{"en":"A programme with plot notes and cast biographies is more informative than one with only pictures.","zh":"有劇情介紹和演員簡介的節目單，比只有圖片的節目單資料更豐富。"},{"en":"Informative materials help audiences understand a performance better.","zh":"資料豐富的材料幫助觀眾更好地理解演出。"},{"en":"The phrase compares how much useful information two things provide.","zh":"這個片語比較兩者提供多少有用資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"doesn’t fully understand why","meaning":"不完全明白為何","examples":[{"en":"Maya does not fully understand why British programmes failed to develop.","zh":"Maya 不完全明白為何英國節目單未能發展。"},{"en":"Doesn’t fully understand why means does not completely know the reason.","zh":"不完全明白為何意思是沒有完全知道原因。"},{"en":"I don’t fully understand why the theatre kept the old design for so long.","zh":"我不完全明白為何劇院保留舊設計那麼久。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they have some idea but still feel uncertain.","zh":"當人們有一些想法但仍不確定時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It introduces a question or puzzle.","zh":"它引出問題或疑惑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"fail to develop","meaning":"未能發展","examples":[{"en":"British theatre programmes failed to develop for a long time.","zh":"英國劇場節目單長時間未能發展。"},{"en":"Fail to develop means not grow, improve, or change as expected.","zh":"未能發展意思是沒有按預期成長、改善或改變。"},{"en":"The project failed to develop because the team had too little funding.","zh":"由於團隊資金太少，項目未能發展。"},{"en":"A design may fail to develop if people keep using an old format.","zh":"如果人們一直使用舊格式，設計可能未能發展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lack of progress.","zh":"這個片語描述缺乏進步。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"for so long","meaning":"這麼長時間","examples":[{"en":"The programmes failed to develop for so long after the war.","zh":"戰後，這些節目單這麼長時間都未能發展。"},{"en":"For so long means for such a long period of time.","zh":"這麼長時間意思是如此長的一段時間。"},{"en":"I cannot understand why the theatre stayed closed for so long.","zh":"我不明白那間劇院為何關閉這麼長時間。"},{"en":"The phrase often shows surprise about the length of time.","zh":"這個片語常顯示對時間長度感到驚訝。"},{"en":"It emphasises that the delay was unusually long.","zh":"它強調延遲異常地長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"copy fashions from","meaning":"模仿來自……的潮流","examples":[{"en":"The option says British programmes copied fashions from the USA.","zh":"選項說英國節目單模仿來自美國的潮流。"},{"en":"Copy fashions from somewhere means imitate styles or trends from that place.","zh":"模仿來自某地的潮流意思是仿效那個地方的風格或趨勢。"},{"en":"Local theatres may copy fashions from overseas productions.","zh":"本地劇院可能模仿海外製作的潮流。"},{"en":"Copying fashions can make designs look modern, but it may reduce originality.","zh":"模仿潮流可以令設計看起來現代，但也可能減少原創性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes influence from another place.","zh":"這個片語描述來自另一地方的影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"What comment is made about","meaning":"對……作出甚麼評論","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what comment is made about each programme.","zh":"題目問對每份節目單作出甚麼評論。"},{"en":"What comment is made about something means what opinion or remark is given about it.","zh":"對某事作出甚麼評論，意思是對它提出了甚麼意見或說法。"},{"en":"The worksheet asks what comment is made about the old poster.","zh":"工作紙問對那張舊海報作出甚麼評論。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in listening and reading questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於聆聽和閱讀題目。"},{"en":"It asks students to match a statement with an item.","zh":"它要求學生把說法與項目配對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the following shows","meaning":"以下劇目","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match comments with the following shows.","zh":"考生把評論與以下劇目配對。"},{"en":"The following shows means the shows listed below or next in the question.","zh":"以下劇目意思是在題目下方或接下來列出的劇目。"},{"en":"Match the following shows with the correct theatre posters.","zh":"請把以下劇目與正確劇場海報配對。"},{"en":"This phrase directs readers to a list that comes after it.","zh":"這個片語引導讀者看接下來的清單。"},{"en":"It is common in exam instructions.","zh":"它常見於考試指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"somewhat controversial","meaning":"有點具爭議","examples":[{"en":"The option says the programme’s origin is somewhat controversial.","zh":"選項說這份節目單的來源有點具爭議。"},{"en":"Somewhat controversial means causing some disagreement or debate, but not necessarily extreme conflict.","zh":"有點具爭議意思是引起一些分歧或討論，但不一定是極端衝突。"},{"en":"The date of the old document is somewhat controversial among researchers.","zh":"那份舊文件的日期在研究者之間有點具爭議。"},{"en":"A controversial claim may need careful evidence.","zh":"具爭議的說法可能需要仔細證據。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that people do not fully agree.","zh":"這個片語暗示人們並不完全同意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"historically significant","meaning":"具有歷史意義","examples":[{"en":"The programme is historically significant for a country.","zh":"這份節目單對一個國家具有歷史意義。"},{"en":"Historically significant means important because of its connection with past events or development.","zh":"具有歷史意義意思是因與過去事件或發展有關而重要。"},{"en":"The first printed newspaper in a country is historically significant.","zh":"一個國家的第一份印刷報紙具有歷史意義。"},{"en":"A theatre programme can be historically significant if it is linked to early printing history.","zh":"如果劇場節目單與早期印刷歷史有關，它可以具有歷史意義。"},{"en":"The phrase shows value beyond appearance.","zh":"這個片語顯示價值不只是外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"effective at attracting audiences","meaning":"有效吸引觀眾","examples":[{"en":"The programme was effective at attracting audiences.","zh":"這份節目單有效吸引觀眾。"},{"en":"Effective at attracting audiences means successful in making people want to attend.","zh":"有效吸引觀眾意思是成功令人想出席觀看。"},{"en":"A colourful poster can be effective at attracting audiences to a new play.","zh":"色彩豐富的海報可以有效吸引觀眾觀看新戲。"},{"en":"Publicity is effective when it turns attention into ticket sales.","zh":"當宣傳把注意力轉化成門票銷售時，它就是有效的。"},{"en":"The phrase judges how well something brings in viewers.","zh":"這個片語評價某物吸引觀眾的效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"included in a recent project","meaning":"被收錄於近期項目","examples":[{"en":"The programme is included in a recent project.","zh":"這份節目單被收錄於近期項目。"},{"en":"Included in a recent project means made part of a project that began or happened not long ago.","zh":"被收錄於近期項目意思是成為不久前開始或進行的項目的一部分。"},{"en":"The old poster was included in a recent digitisation project.","zh":"那張舊海報被收錄於近期數碼化項目。"},{"en":"Being included in a project can make an item easier for researchers to find.","zh":"被收錄於項目可以令研究者更容易找到該物件。"},{"en":"The phrase connects the item with current research or archive work.","zh":"這個片語把項目與目前研究或檔案工作連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contains insights into","meaning":"載有對……的深入了解","examples":[{"en":"The programme contains insights into the show.","zh":"這份節目單載有對該演出的深入了解。"},{"en":"Contains insights into something means includes deeper understanding or inside information about it.","zh":"載有對某事的深入了解，意思是包括關於它的更深層理解或內部資料。"},{"en":"The director’s article contains insights into how the play was created.","zh":"導演的文章載有對該劇如何創作的深入了解。"},{"en":"Insights help readers understand more than basic facts.","zh":"深入了解幫助讀者理解基本事實以外的內容。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests useful and thoughtful information.","zh":"這個片語暗示有用而有思想的資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"resembles an artwork","meaning":"像一件藝術品","examples":[{"en":"The programme resembles an artwork.","zh":"這份節目單像一件藝術品。"},{"en":"Resembles an artwork means looks like a piece of art because of its beauty or design.","zh":"像一件藝術品意思是因其美感或設計而看起來像藝術作品。"},{"en":"The old theatre programme resembles an artwork with its detailed cover and elegant lettering.","zh":"那份舊劇場節目單有細緻封面和優雅字體，像一件藝術品。"},{"en":"A programme that resembles an artwork may be collected or framed.","zh":"像藝術品的節目單可能會被收藏或裝框。"},{"en":"The phrase praises the visual quality of the programme.","zh":"這個片語稱讚節目單的視覺質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/listening/Practice 3/task-4":[{"front":"design and technology lecturer","meaning":"設計與科技講師","examples":[{"en":"You will hear a design and technology lecturer talking about inclusive design.","zh":"你會聽到一位設計與科技講師談論包容性設計。"},{"en":"A design and technology lecturer teaches students about designing, making, and improving products.","zh":"design and technology lecturer 指教學生設計、製作和改良產品的講師。"},{"en":"The design and technology lecturer showed how a chair can be made safer and more comfortable.","zh":"設計與科技講師展示一張椅子如何可以變得更安全和舒適。"},{"en":"A design and technology lecturer often explains how design choices affect real users.","zh":"設計與科技講師常解釋設計選擇如何影響真實使用者。"},{"en":"Students asked the design and technology lecturer how technology can solve daily problems.","zh":"學生問設計與科技講師科技如何解決日常問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"inclusive design","meaning":"包容性設計","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer is talking about inclusive design.","zh":"講師正在談論包容性設計。"},{"en":"Inclusive design means designing products or spaces that can be used by many different kinds of people.","zh":"inclusive design 指設計能讓許多不同類型的人使用的產品或空間。"},{"en":"Inclusive design helps children, older people, disabled people, and ordinary users use things more easily.","zh":"包容性設計幫助兒童、長者、殘疾人士和一般使用者更容易使用物品。"},{"en":"A website with clear text and simple buttons is an example of inclusive design.","zh":"有清晰文字和簡單按鈕的網站是包容性設計的例子。"},{"en":"Inclusive design matters because badly designed products can exclude people.","zh":"包容性設計很重要，因為設計不佳的產品可能排除某些人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"relatively recently","meaning":"相對近年","examples":[{"en":"It is only relatively recently that designers have become aware of inclusive design.","zh":"設計師只是相對近年才意識到包容性設計。"},{"en":"Relatively recently means not very long ago when compared with a longer period of history.","zh":"relatively recently 指與較長歷史相比，不算很久以前。"},{"en":"It is only relatively recently that many schools have used tablets in class.","zh":"很多學校只是相對近年才在課堂使用平板電腦。"},{"en":"Electric cars became common relatively recently, even though cars have existed for over a century.","zh":"雖然汽車已存在超過一個世紀，電動車只是相對近年才普及。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is new compared with what came before.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事相對於過去而言較新。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"become aware of","meaning":"意識到……","examples":[{"en":"Designers have become aware of the need to be inclusive.","zh":"設計師已意識到具備包容性的需要。"},{"en":"To become aware of something means to start noticing or understanding it.","zh":"become aware of something 指開始注意或理解某事。"},{"en":"Students became aware of plastic waste after visiting the beach.","zh":"學生參觀海灘後意識到塑膠廢物問題。"},{"en":"Companies become aware of users’ problems when they listen to complaints.","zh":"公司聆聽投訴時，會意識到使用者的問題。"},{"en":"People often change their behaviour after they become aware of a problem.","zh":"人們意識到問題後，常會改變自己的行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the need to be inclusive","meaning":"具備包容性的需要","examples":[{"en":"Designers have become aware of the need to be inclusive when designing products.","zh":"設計師已意識到設計產品時具備包容性的需要。"},{"en":"The need to be inclusive means the importance of considering many different users, not only one group.","zh":"the need to be inclusive 指考慮許多不同使用者，而不只是一個群體的重要性。"},{"en":"Schools recognise the need to be inclusive when students have different learning needs.","zh":"當學生有不同學習需要時，學校會認識到具備包容性的需要。"},{"en":"The need to be inclusive is clear when elderly users cannot read tiny text on a screen.","zh":"當長者無法閱讀螢幕上的細小文字，具備包容性的需要就很明顯。"},{"en":"Good design responds to the need to be inclusive from the beginning.","zh":"好設計會從一開始回應具備包容性的需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"designing products","meaning":"設計產品","examples":[{"en":"Inclusive design is important when designing products.","zh":"設計產品時，包容性設計很重要。"},{"en":"Designing products means planning how objects, tools, or systems will look and work.","zh":"designing products 指規劃物件、工具或系統的外觀和運作方式。"},{"en":"When designing products for children, safety must come first.","zh":"為兒童設計產品時，安全必須放在首位。"},{"en":"Designers should test real users’ needs before designing products.","zh":"設計師在設計產品前應測試真實使用者的需要。"},{"en":"Designing products well can make daily life easier for many people.","zh":"設計產品設計得好，可以令許多人的日常生活更容易。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what does that mean exactly?","meaning":"這到底是甚麼意思？","examples":[{"en":"But what does that mean exactly?","zh":"但這到底是甚麼意思？"},{"en":"“What does that mean exactly?” asks for a clearer or more precise explanation.","zh":"“What does that mean exactly?” 是要求更清楚或更準確的解釋。"},{"en":"You said the app is accessible, but what does that mean exactly?","zh":"你說這個應用程式具無障礙性，但這到底是甚麼意思？"},{"en":"Students ask this question when a term sounds important but unclear.","zh":"當一個詞聽起來重要但不清楚時，學生會問這個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase helps move from a general idea to a clear definition.","zh":"這個短語幫助人從一般想法轉到清楚定義。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"span barriers","meaning":"跨越障礙","examples":[{"en":"Inclusive design means designing products that span economic, social and cultural barriers.","zh":"包容性設計指設計能跨越經濟、社會和文化障礙的產品。"},{"en":"To span barriers means to cross or overcome limits that separate different groups.","zh":"span barriers 指跨越或克服分隔不同群體的限制。"},{"en":"A simple public health poster can span language barriers if it uses clear pictures.","zh":"如果使用清楚圖片，簡單公共健康海報可以跨越語言障礙。"},{"en":"Good technology can span barriers between young and older users.","zh":"好科技可以跨越年輕和年長使用者之間的障礙。"},{"en":"Designs that span barriers help more people take part in society.","zh":"能跨越障礙的設計幫助更多人參與社會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"economic, social and cultural barriers","meaning":"經濟、社會及文化障礙","examples":[{"en":"Inclusive design spans economic, social and cultural barriers.","zh":"包容性設計跨越經濟、社會及文化障礙。"},{"en":"Economic, social and cultural barriers are limits caused by money, social position, language, habits, or traditions.","zh":"economic, social and cultural barriers 指由金錢、社會位置、語言、習慣或傳統造成的限制。"},{"en":"High prices create economic barriers for low-income families.","zh":"高價格會為低收入家庭造成經濟障礙。"},{"en":"A lack of translation can create cultural barriers for new immigrants.","zh":"缺乏翻譯可能為新移民造成文化障礙。"},{"en":"Designers should understand economic, social and cultural barriers before making public products.","zh":"設計公共產品前，設計師應理解經濟、社會及文化障礙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"making sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"It means making sure products are accessible.","zh":"它意思是確保產品容易使用。"},{"en":"Making sure means checking carefully so that something is true or happens.","zh":"making sure 指仔細檢查，以確保某事屬實或會發生。"},{"en":"Teachers are responsible for making sure students understand the safety rules.","zh":"老師有責任確保學生明白安全規則。"},{"en":"Designers make sure buttons are large enough before releasing an app.","zh":"設計師在推出應用程式前，會確保按鈕足夠大。"},{"en":"Making sure small details are correct can prevent serious problems later.","zh":"確保小細節正確，可以防止之後出現嚴重問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"products are accessible","meaning":"產品容易使用；產品具無障礙性","examples":[{"en":"Inclusive design means making sure products are accessible.","zh":"包容性設計指確保產品容易使用。"},{"en":"Products are accessible when many different users can reach, understand, and use them easily.","zh":"當許多不同使用者都能接觸、理解和輕易使用時，產品就是具無障礙性的。"},{"en":"A website is more accessible if the text is large and easy to read.","zh":"如果網站文字較大而易讀，它就更容易使用。"},{"en":"Products are accessible when people with disabilities can use them without extra difficulty.","zh":"當殘疾人士能在沒有額外困難下使用產品，產品就是具無障礙性的。"},{"en":"Accessible products reduce exclusion and frustration.","zh":"容易使用的產品可以減少排除和挫敗感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as many different types of people as possible","meaning":"盡可能多不同類型的人","examples":[{"en":"Accessible products can be used by as many different types of people as possible.","zh":"容易使用的產品可以讓盡可能多不同類型的人使用。"},{"en":"As many different types of people as possible means the widest practical range of users.","zh":"as many different types of people as possible 指實際上最廣泛的使用者群體。"},{"en":"A public library should serve as many different types of people as possible.","zh":"公共圖書館應服務盡可能多不同類型的人。"},{"en":"A good app should be clear for as many different types of people as possible.","zh":"好應用程式應讓盡可能多不同類型的人都覺得清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the goal of including users with different ages, abilities, and backgrounds.","zh":"這個短語顯示目標是包括不同年齡、能力和背景的使用者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"without any adaptation","meaning":"無須任何改動","examples":[{"en":"People should be able to use the product without any adaptation.","zh":"人們應能無須任何改動就使用該產品。"},{"en":"Without any adaptation means without changing the product first.","zh":"without any adaptation 指不需要先改變產品。"},{"en":"A ramp allows wheelchair users to enter a building without any adaptation to the chair.","zh":"斜道讓輪椅使用者無須改動輪椅就能進入建築物。"},{"en":"Good design lets older users read the screen without any adaptation.","zh":"好設計讓年長使用者無須任何改動就能閱讀螢幕。"},{"en":"If a product works without any adaptation, more people can use it immediately.","zh":"如果產品無須任何改動就能使用，更多人可以立即使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"adaptation having to be made","meaning":"需要作出改動","examples":[{"en":"The product can be used without any adaptation having to be made.","zh":"產品可以使用，而無須作出任何改動。"},{"en":"Adaptation having to be made means changes needing to be made before something can be used.","zh":"adaptation having to be made 指在使用前需要作出的改動。"},{"en":"The entrance should be usable without a special adaptation having to be made.","zh":"入口應該可以使用，而無須作出特別改動。"},{"en":"A classroom tool is better if students can use it without adaptation having to be made.","zh":"如果學生能在無須改動下使用課堂工具，它會更好。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that extra changes should not be necessary.","zh":"這個短語強調不應需要額外改動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"original design","meaning":"原本設計","examples":[{"en":"No adaptation has to be made to the original design.","zh":"原本設計不需要作出改動。"},{"en":"The original design is the first planned form of a product before changes are added.","zh":"original design 指產品加入改動前最初規劃的形式。"},{"en":"The original design of the chair did not suit wheelchair users.","zh":"那張椅子的原本設計不適合輪椅使用者。"},{"en":"If the original design is inclusive, fewer later changes are needed.","zh":"如果原本設計具包容性，之後需要的改動會較少。"},{"en":"Designers should test the original design with real users before production.","zh":"設計師應在生產前用真實使用者測試原本設計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be linked with","meaning":"與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"Inclusive design is often linked with universal design.","zh":"包容性設計常與通用設計聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To be linked with something means to be connected or associated with it.","zh":"be linked with something 指與某事有連繫或相關。"},{"en":"Poor posture is often linked with back pain.","zh":"不良姿勢常與背痛聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Clear signs are linked with safer public transport.","zh":"清楚標誌與更安全的公共交通有關。"},{"en":"Two ideas may be linked with each other even if they are not exactly the same.","zh":"兩個概念即使不完全相同，也可能互相聯繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"universal design","meaning":"通用設計","examples":[{"en":"Universal design aims to make products that work for everyone.","zh":"通用設計旨在製作適合所有人使用的產品。"},{"en":"Universal design is the idea of designing things so all people can use them as much as possible.","zh":"universal design 指盡可能設計讓所有人都能使用的事物。"},{"en":"A step-free entrance is an example of universal design.","zh":"無梯級入口是通用設計的例子。"},{"en":"Universal design helps parents with prams, wheelchair users, and travellers with luggage.","zh":"通用設計幫助推嬰兒車的家長、輪椅使用者和帶行李的旅客。"},{"en":"Universal design reduces the need for separate special solutions.","zh":"通用設計減少另設特殊方案的需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not quite the same thing","meaning":"並不完全相同","examples":[{"en":"Inclusive design and universal design are not quite the same thing.","zh":"包容性設計和通用設計並不完全相同。"},{"en":"Not quite the same thing means similar, but not exactly identical.","zh":"not quite the same thing 指相似，但並非完全一樣。"},{"en":"Being busy and being productive are not quite the same thing.","zh":"忙碌和有生產力並不完全相同。"},{"en":"Translation and interpretation are not quite the same thing, although both involve languages.","zh":"翻譯和傳譯並不完全相同，雖然兩者都涉及語言。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain a small but important difference.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋細小但重要的差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"aims to make","meaning":"旨在製作","examples":[{"en":"Universal design aims to make products that work for everyone.","zh":"通用設計旨在製作適合所有人使用的產品。"},{"en":"Aims to make means has the goal of creating or achieving something.","zh":"aims to make 指目標是創造或達成某事。"},{"en":"The course aims to make students more confident speakers.","zh":"這課程旨在令學生成為更有信心的說話者。"},{"en":"This new policy aims to make public transport easier to use.","zh":"這項新政策旨在令公共交通更容易使用。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly states the purpose behind an action or design.","zh":"這個短語清楚說明行動或設計背後的目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"work for everyone","meaning":"適合所有人使用","examples":[{"en":"Universal design aims to make products that work for everyone.","zh":"通用設計旨在製作適合所有人使用的產品。"},{"en":"To work for everyone means to be usable or suitable for all users as far as possible.","zh":"work for everyone 指盡可能讓所有使用者都能使用或覺得合適。"},{"en":"A school timetable rarely works for everyone perfectly.","zh":"學校時間表很少能完全適合所有人。"},{"en":"Designers try to make public signs that work for everyone, including tourists.","zh":"設計師嘗試製作適合所有人使用的公共標誌，包括遊客。"},{"en":"A product that works for everyone saves users from needing separate versions.","zh":"適合所有人使用的產品，能令使用者不需要不同版本。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"considering the needs of","meaning":"考慮……的需要","examples":[{"en":"Universal design includes considering the needs of people with cognitive difficulties.","zh":"通用設計包括考慮有認知困難人士的需要。"},{"en":"Considering the needs of someone means thinking carefully about what that person requires.","zh":"considering the needs of someone 指仔細思考某人的需要。"},{"en":"Schools should consider the needs of students who learn more slowly.","zh":"學校應考慮學習較慢學生的需要。"},{"en":"Designers consider the needs of older users when choosing font size.","zh":"設計師選擇字體大小時會考慮年長使用者的需要。"},{"en":"Considering people’s needs early can prevent exclusion later.","zh":"及早考慮人們的需要，可以防止之後出現排除。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cognitive difficulties","meaning":"認知困難","examples":[{"en":"Universal design considers the needs of people who have cognitive difficulties.","zh":"通用設計會考慮有認知困難人士的需要。"},{"en":"Cognitive difficulties are problems with thinking, memory, understanding, learning, or decision-making.","zh":"cognitive difficulties 指在思考、記憶、理解、學習或作決定方面的困難。"},{"en":"People with cognitive difficulties may need simpler instructions.","zh":"有認知困難的人可能需要較簡單的指示。"},{"en":"Clear icons and plain language can help users with cognitive difficulties.","zh":"清楚圖示和簡單語言可以幫助有認知困難的使用者。"},{"en":"Designers should avoid confusing layouts when supporting people with cognitive difficulties.","zh":"設計師支援有認知困難的人時，應避免混亂版面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"present quite a challenge","meaning":"構成相當大的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Cognitive difficulties can present quite a challenge for designers.","zh":"認知困難會對設計師構成相當大的挑戰。"},{"en":"To present quite a challenge means to create a fairly difficult problem to solve.","zh":"present quite a challenge 指造成相當難解決的問題。"},{"en":"Designing a website for all age groups can present quite a challenge.","zh":"為所有年齡組別設計網站可能構成相當大的挑戰。"},{"en":"A small screen can present quite a challenge when information is complex.","zh":"當資料複雜時，小螢幕會構成相當大的挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the problem is serious but not impossible to handle.","zh":"這個短語顯示問題嚴重，但不是無法處理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"successful inclusive design","meaning":"成功的包容性設計","examples":[{"en":"Examples of successful inclusive design can be seen all around us.","zh":"成功的包容性設計例子在我們周圍隨處可見。"},{"en":"Successful inclusive design is design that truly helps many different users use something well.","zh":"successful inclusive design 指真正幫助許多不同使用者好好使用某物的設計。"},{"en":"A lift with clear buttons and audio instructions is successful inclusive design.","zh":"有清楚按鈕和語音提示的升降機是成功的包容性設計。"},{"en":"Successful inclusive design often feels natural because everyone can use it easily.","zh":"成功的包容性設計通常感覺自然，因為人人都能輕易使用。"},{"en":"Designers learn from successful inclusive design when improving public spaces.","zh":"設計師改善公共空間時，會從成功的包容性設計中學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"can be seen all around us","meaning":"在我們周圍隨處可見","examples":[{"en":"Examples of successful inclusive design can be seen all around us.","zh":"成功的包容性設計例子在我們周圍隨處可見。"},{"en":"Can be seen all around us means something is common and visible in daily life.","zh":"can be seen all around us 指某事在日常生活中常見而可見。"},{"en":"Good design can be seen all around us, from traffic lights to door handles.","zh":"好設計在我們周圍隨處可見，從交通燈到門柄都是。"},{"en":"Signs of climate change can be seen all around us in extreme weather.","zh":"氣候變化的跡象在極端天氣中隨處可見。"},{"en":"This phrase helps listeners notice examples in ordinary surroundings.","zh":"這個短語幫助聽眾注意普通環境中的例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"adjustable desks","meaning":"可調校高度的桌子","examples":[{"en":"Adjustable desks can suit people of different heights.","zh":"可調校高度的桌子可以適合不同身高的人。"},{"en":"Adjustable desks are desks whose height or position can be changed.","zh":"adjustable desks 指高度或位置可以改變的桌子。"},{"en":"Adjustable desks help workers sit or stand more comfortably.","zh":"可調校高度的桌子幫助員工更舒適地坐着或站着工作。"},{"en":"A classroom with adjustable desks can support students of different sizes.","zh":"有可調校高度桌子的課室可以支援不同身形的學生。"},{"en":"Adjustable desks are useful because one design can fit many users.","zh":"可調校高度的桌子很有用，因為一種設計可以適合很多使用者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be adjusted to suit","meaning":"調校至適合……","examples":[{"en":"Desks can be adjusted to suit people of different heights.","zh":"桌子可以調校至適合不同身高的人。"},{"en":"To be adjusted to suit someone means to be changed so it fits that person’s needs.","zh":"be adjusted to suit someone 指作出調整，使其符合某人的需要。"},{"en":"The chair can be adjusted to suit a child or an adult.","zh":"椅子可以調校至適合兒童或成人。"},{"en":"Screen brightness should be adjusted to suit the user’s eyes.","zh":"螢幕亮度應調校至適合使用者的眼睛。"},{"en":"Products that can be adjusted to suit different users are often more inclusive.","zh":"能調校至適合不同使用者的產品通常更具包容性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"people of different heights","meaning":"不同身高的人","examples":[{"en":"Adjustable desks can suit people of different heights.","zh":"可調校高度的桌子可以適合不同身高的人。"},{"en":"People of different heights means users who are tall, short, or somewhere in between.","zh":"people of different heights 指高、矮或中等身高的使用者。"},{"en":"Public counters should serve people of different heights comfortably.","zh":"公共櫃台應舒適地服務不同身高的人。"},{"en":"A fixed desk may not suit people of different heights equally well.","zh":"固定高度桌子未必同樣適合不同身高的人。"},{"en":"Designing for people of different heights helps prevent discomfort and poor posture.","zh":"為不同身高的人設計，有助防止不適和不良姿勢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"wheelchair users","meaning":"輪椅使用者","examples":[{"en":"Adjustable desks can also suit wheelchair users.","zh":"可調校高度的桌子也可以適合輪椅使用者。"},{"en":"Wheelchair users are people who use wheelchairs for mobility.","zh":"wheelchair users 指使用輪椅行動的人。"},{"en":"Wheelchair users need enough space under tables and around doorways.","zh":"輪椅使用者需要桌子下方和門口周圍有足夠空間。"},{"en":"Ramps and lifts help wheelchair users move around independently.","zh":"斜道和升降機幫助輪椅使用者獨立出行。"},{"en":"Designers should involve wheelchair users when testing public facilities.","zh":"設計師測試公共設施時，應讓輪椅使用者參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"this isn’t always the case","meaning":"情況並非總是如此","examples":[{"en":"Adjustable desks are common, but this isn’t always the case.","zh":"可調校高度的桌子很常見，但情況並非總是如此。"},{"en":"This isn’t always the case means something is not true in every situation.","zh":"this isn’t always the case 指某事並非在每種情況下都是真的。"},{"en":"Many buses are accessible, but this isn’t always the case in older areas.","zh":"許多巴士具無障礙設計，但在較舊地區情況並非總是如此。"},{"en":"Some apps are easy to use, but this isn’t always the case for older users.","zh":"有些應用程式易用，但對年長使用者來說情況並非總是如此。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds listeners that there are exceptions.","zh":"這個短語提醒聽眾存在例外。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"one reason why","meaning":"……的其中一個原因","examples":[{"en":"This is one reason why office workers often suffer from back or neck problems.","zh":"這是辦公室工作者常受背部或頸部問題困擾的其中一個原因。"},{"en":"One reason why introduces one cause of a result.","zh":"one reason why 用來引出某結果的一個原因。"},{"en":"Poor lighting is one reason why students may get tired while reading.","zh":"燈光不足是學生閱讀時可能疲倦的其中一個原因。"},{"en":"A badly designed chair is one reason why workers feel pain after sitting all day.","zh":"設計不佳的椅子是員工坐一整天後疼痛的其中一個原因。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect a problem with one of its causes.","zh":"這個短語幫助把問題與其中一個成因連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"office workers","meaning":"辦公室工作者","examples":[{"en":"Office workers often suffer from back or neck problems.","zh":"辦公室工作者常受背部或頸部問題困擾。"},{"en":"Office workers are people who work in offices, often at desks or computers.","zh":"office workers 指在辦公室工作、常坐在桌前或電腦前的人。"},{"en":"Office workers may sit for many hours each day.","zh":"辦公室工作者每天可能坐很多小時。"},{"en":"Good chairs and desks can help office workers avoid pain.","zh":"好椅子和桌子可以幫助辦公室工作者避免疼痛。"},{"en":"Office workers need breaks because long screen time can affect health.","zh":"辦公室工作者需要休息，因為長時間看螢幕會影響健康。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"suffer from","meaning":"受……困擾；患有……","examples":[{"en":"Office workers often suffer from back or neck problems.","zh":"辦公室工作者常受背部或頸部問題困擾。"},{"en":"To suffer from something means to experience pain, illness, or difficulty because of it.","zh":"suffer from something 指因某事而經歷痛楚、疾病或困難。"},{"en":"Many students suffer from stress before exams.","zh":"許多學生考試前受壓力困擾。"},{"en":"People may suffer from headaches after using screens for too long.","zh":"人們長時間使用螢幕後可能受頭痛困擾。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for ongoing problems, not small one-time discomfort.","zh":"這個短語用於持續問題，而不是一次性小不適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"back or neck problems","meaning":"背部或頸部問題","examples":[{"en":"Poor desk design can cause back or neck problems.","zh":"不良桌子設計可以造成背部或頸部問題。"},{"en":"Back or neck problems are pain, stiffness, or injury in the back or neck.","zh":"back or neck problems 指背部或頸部的疼痛、僵硬或受傷。"},{"en":"Bad posture at a computer may lead to back or neck problems.","zh":"在電腦前姿勢不良可能導致背部或頸部問題。"},{"en":"Adjustable furniture can reduce back or neck problems in offices.","zh":"可調校家具可以減少辦公室中的背部或頸部問題。"},{"en":"People should not ignore back or neck problems if they last for weeks.","zh":"如果背部或頸部問題持續數星期，人們不應忽視。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"public toilets","meaning":"公共洗手間","examples":[{"en":"Another example can be found in the public toilets of hotels, airports and offices.","zh":"另一個例子可見於酒店、機場和辦公室的公共洗手間。"},{"en":"Public toilets are toilets provided for people to use in shared places.","zh":"public toilets 指在共享地方供人使用的洗手間。"},{"en":"Public toilets should be clean, safe, and easy for different users to access.","zh":"公共洗手間應乾淨、安全，並讓不同使用者容易進入。"},{"en":"Airports need public toilets that suit travellers with luggage and disabilities.","zh":"機場需要適合帶行李旅客和殘疾人士的公共洗手間。"},{"en":"Good public toilets show that a building considers visitors’ needs.","zh":"好的公共洗手間顯示建築物有考慮訪客需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"countless hotels, airports and offices","meaning":"無數酒店、機場和辦公室","examples":[{"en":"Sensor taps are found in countless hotels, airports and offices.","zh":"感應式水龍頭可見於無數酒店、機場和辦公室。"},{"en":"Countless hotels, airports and offices means a very large number of these places.","zh":"countless hotels, airports and offices 指數量非常多的這些地方。"},{"en":"Automatic doors are used in countless hotels, airports and offices.","zh":"自動門被用於無數酒店、機場和辦公室。"},{"en":"Wi-Fi is available in countless hotels, airports and offices today.","zh":"如今無數酒店、機場和辦公室都有 Wi-Fi。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that something is extremely common.","zh":"這個短語強調某事極為常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sensor taps","meaning":"感應式水龍頭","examples":[{"en":"Sensor taps require no pressing or twisting movements.","zh":"感應式水龍頭不需要按壓或扭動動作。"},{"en":"Sensor taps are taps that turn water on when they detect hands nearby.","zh":"sensor taps 指偵測到手靠近時會出水的水龍頭。"},{"en":"Sensor taps help people wash their hands without touching handles.","zh":"感應式水龍頭幫助人們無須觸碰把手就能洗手。"},{"en":"Sensor taps are useful for people who find twisting taps difficult.","zh":"對覺得扭水龍頭困難的人來說，感應式水龍頭很有用。"},{"en":"Public toilets often use sensor taps to improve hygiene.","zh":"公共洗手間常使用感應式水龍頭來改善衞生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"activate by sensor","meaning":"以感應器啟動","examples":[{"en":"You activate these taps by sensor.","zh":"你以感應器啟動這些水龍頭。"},{"en":"To activate something by sensor means to make it start working when a sensor detects movement or presence.","zh":"activate something by sensor 指當感應器偵測到動作或存在時啟動某物。"},{"en":"Automatic doors are activated by sensor when someone walks near them.","zh":"自動門在有人走近時會以感應器啟動。"},{"en":"Lights that activate by sensor can save energy in empty rooms.","zh":"以感應器啟動的燈可以在空房間中節省能源。"},{"en":"Sensor-activated products are useful when touching controls is difficult or unhygienic.","zh":"當觸碰控制裝置困難或不衞生時，感應啟動產品很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pressing or twisting movements","meaning":"按壓或扭動動作","examples":[{"en":"Sensor taps require no pressing or twisting movements.","zh":"感應式水龍頭不需要按壓或扭動動作。"},{"en":"Pressing or twisting movements are hand actions used to push, turn, or operate something.","zh":"pressing or twisting movements 指用手推、轉或操作某物的動作。"},{"en":"Some older people find pressing or twisting movements painful.","zh":"有些年長人士覺得按壓或扭動動作會令人疼痛。"},{"en":"A door handle that needs strong twisting movements may exclude some users.","zh":"需要用力扭動的門柄可能排除某些使用者。"},{"en":"Reducing pressing or twisting movements can make products easier to use.","zh":"減少按壓或扭動動作可以令產品更容易使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"more hygienic","meaning":"更衞生","examples":[{"en":"Sensor taps are more hygienic than ordinary taps.","zh":"感應式水龍頭比普通水龍頭更衞生。"},{"en":"More hygienic means cleaner and less likely to spread germs.","zh":"more hygienic 指更清潔，也較不容易傳播細菌。"},{"en":"Touch-free soap dispensers are more hygienic in public toilets.","zh":"免觸式洗手液機在公共洗手間中更衞生。"},{"en":"Washing hands properly makes food preparation more hygienic.","zh":"正確洗手令食物準備過程更衞生。"},{"en":"A more hygienic design protects users by reducing contact with dirty surfaces.","zh":"更衞生的設計透過減少接觸骯髒表面來保護使用者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"easier for people with","meaning":"對有……的人較容易使用","examples":[{"en":"Sensor taps are easier for people with dexterity or mobility issues.","zh":"感應式水龍頭對有手部靈活度或行動能力問題的人較容易使用。"},{"en":"Easier for people with something means less difficult for people who have that condition or need.","zh":"easier for people with something 指對有某種情況或需要的人較不困難。"},{"en":"Large buttons are easier for people with poor eyesight.","zh":"大按鈕對視力差的人較容易使用。"},{"en":"Step-free entrances are easier for people with wheelchairs or prams.","zh":"無梯級入口對使用輪椅或嬰兒車的人較容易使用。"},{"en":"Good design asks what would be easier for people with different abilities.","zh":"好設計會詢問甚麼對有不同能力的人較容易使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dexterity issues","meaning":"手部靈活度問題","examples":[{"en":"Sensor taps are easier for people with dexterity issues.","zh":"感應式水龍頭對有手部靈活度問題的人較容易使用。"},{"en":"Dexterity issues are difficulties using the hands and fingers accurately or smoothly.","zh":"dexterity issues 指準確或流暢使用手和手指方面的困難。"},{"en":"People with dexterity issues may struggle to open small bottle caps.","zh":"有手部靈活度問題的人可能難以打開小瓶蓋。"},{"en":"Large handles can help users with dexterity issues.","zh":"大手柄可以幫助有手部靈活度問題的使用者。"},{"en":"Designers should avoid tiny controls when supporting people with dexterity issues.","zh":"設計師支援有手部靈活度問題的人時，應避免細小控制鍵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mobility issues","meaning":"行動能力問題","examples":[{"en":"Sensor taps are easier for people with mobility issues.","zh":"感應式水龍頭對有行動能力問題的人較容易使用。"},{"en":"Mobility issues are difficulties moving the body, walking, reaching, or using limbs.","zh":"mobility issues 指移動身體、步行、伸手或使用肢體方面的困難。"},{"en":"People with mobility issues may need lifts, ramps, or wider doors.","zh":"有行動能力問題的人可能需要升降機、斜道或較寬門口。"},{"en":"A bathroom designed for mobility issues should leave enough turning space.","zh":"為行動能力問題設計的洗手間應留有足夠轉身空間。"},{"en":"Inclusive design helps people with mobility issues move and act more independently.","zh":"包容性設計幫助有行動能力問題的人更獨立地移動和行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the tech industry","meaning":"科技業","examples":[{"en":"The tech industry has been criticised for focusing too much on young consumers.","zh":"科技業因過度關注年輕消費者而受到批評。"},{"en":"The tech industry includes companies and workers who create technology products and services.","zh":"tech industry 指創造科技產品和服務的公司及工作者。"},{"en":"The tech industry designs phones, apps, software, and digital platforms.","zh":"科技業設計手機、應用程式、軟件和數碼平台。"},{"en":"The tech industry can influence how people learn, shop, work, and communicate.","zh":"科技業可以影響人們學習、購物、工作和溝通的方式。"},{"en":"Critics say the tech industry should consider older and disabled users more carefully.","zh":"批評者說科技業應更仔細考慮年長和殘疾使用者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be criticised for","meaning":"因……而受到批評","examples":[{"en":"The tech industry has been criticised for focusing too much on young consumers.","zh":"科技業因過度關注年輕消費者而受到批評。"},{"en":"To be criticised for something means to receive negative comments because of it.","zh":"be criticised for something 指因某事而收到負面評論。"},{"en":"The company was criticised for making its website difficult to read.","zh":"公司因網站難以閱讀而受到批評。"},{"en":"Designers may be criticised for ignoring disabled users.","zh":"設計師可能因忽視殘疾使用者而受到批評。"},{"en":"Being criticised for a problem can push organisations to improve.","zh":"因問題而受到批評可以推動機構改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"focusing too much on","meaning":"過度關注……","examples":[{"en":"The tech industry focused too much on young consumers in the past.","zh":"科技業過去過度關注年輕消費者。"},{"en":"Focusing too much on one group means giving that group too much attention and ignoring others.","zh":"focusing too much on one group 指給某群體過多注意，而忽略其他人。"},{"en":"A school may focus too much on exam scores and forget students’ wellbeing.","zh":"學校可能過度關注考試成績，而忘記學生身心健康。"},{"en":"Designers can make mistakes by focusing too much on stylish looks.","zh":"設計師可能因過度關注時尚外觀而犯錯。"},{"en":"Focusing too much on young users can make products harder for older people.","zh":"過度關注年輕使用者，可能令產品對年長人士更難使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"young consumers","meaning":"年輕消費者","examples":[{"en":"The tech industry used to focus too much on young consumers.","zh":"科技業過去過度關注年輕消費者。"},{"en":"Young consumers are young people who buy or use products and services.","zh":"young consumers 指購買或使用產品和服務的年輕人。"},{"en":"Young consumers often influence trends in phones and social media.","zh":"年輕消費者常影響手機和社交媒體潮流。"},{"en":"Companies may design colourful apps to attract young consumers.","zh":"公司可能設計色彩鮮明的應用程式來吸引年輕消費者。"},{"en":"Products should not serve young consumers only if the whole public needs them.","zh":"如果整個公眾都需要某產品，它不應只服務年輕消費者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"designed with the elderly in mind","meaning":"設計時考慮到長者","examples":[{"en":"Many products are now designed with the elderly in mind.","zh":"現在許多產品設計時都考慮到長者。"},{"en":"Designed with the elderly in mind means created while considering older people’s needs.","zh":"designed with the elderly in mind 指創作時有考慮長者的需要。"},{"en":"A phone with large buttons is designed with the elderly in mind.","zh":"有大按鈕的電話是設計時考慮到長者的產品。"},{"en":"Websites designed with the elderly in mind use clear text and simple steps.","zh":"設計時考慮到長者的網站會使用清楚文字和簡單步驟。"},{"en":"Products designed with the elderly in mind can still be useful for younger users.","zh":"設計時考慮到長者的產品，對年輕使用者也可能有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"it’s well known that","meaning":"眾所周知","examples":[{"en":"It’s well known that vision declines with age.","zh":"眾所周知，視力會隨年齡下降。"},{"en":"It’s well known that means many people already understand or accept this fact.","zh":"it’s well known that 指許多人已經明白或接受這個事實。"},{"en":"It’s well known that regular exercise supports health.","zh":"眾所周知，定期運動有助健康。"},{"en":"It’s well known that small text is difficult for many older readers.","zh":"眾所周知，細小文字對許多年長讀者來說很難。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a fact that is not meant to be surprising.","zh":"這個短語用來引出一個不令人意外的事實。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"vision declines with age","meaning":"視力隨年齡下降","examples":[{"en":"Vision declines with age.","zh":"視力會隨年齡下降。"},{"en":"Vision declines with age means people’s eyesight often becomes weaker as they grow older.","zh":"vision declines with age 指人變老時視力通常會變弱。"},{"en":"Because vision declines with age, older users may need larger text.","zh":"因為視力隨年齡下降，年長使用者可能需要較大文字。"},{"en":"Designers should remember that vision declines with age when choosing colours.","zh":"設計師選擇顏色時，應記住視力會隨年齡下降。"},{"en":"Good lighting helps people whose vision declines with age.","zh":"良好照明能幫助視力隨年齡下降的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"distinguishing between similar colours","meaning":"分辨相近顏色","examples":[{"en":"Older people may become worse at distinguishing between similar colours.","zh":"年長人士可能變得較難分辨相近顏色。"},{"en":"Distinguishing between similar colours means telling close colours apart.","zh":"distinguishing between similar colours 指分辨接近的顏色。"},{"en":"Some users have difficulty distinguishing between similar colours on a screen.","zh":"有些使用者在螢幕上難以分辨相近顏色。"},{"en":"Designers should not rely only on colour when users may struggle to distinguish between similar colours.","zh":"當使用者可能難以分辨相近顏色時，設計師不應只依賴顏色。"},{"en":"Clear labels help when distinguishing between similar colours is difficult.","zh":"當分辨相近顏色有困難時，清楚標籤會有幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in particular","meaning":"尤其是","examples":[{"en":"Software designers avoid certain colours, in particular shades of blue.","zh":"軟件設計師避免使用某些顏色，尤其是藍色色調。"},{"en":"In particular means especially or more specifically.","zh":"in particular 指尤其是或更具體來說。"},{"en":"Many users dislike confusing menus, in particular older users.","zh":"許多使用者不喜歡混亂選單，尤其是年長使用者。"},{"en":"Good design helps everyone, in particular people with disabilities.","zh":"好設計幫助每個人，尤其是殘疾人士。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights one important example from a wider group.","zh":"這個短語從較大群體中突出一個重要例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"shades of blue","meaning":"藍色色調","examples":[{"en":"Older people may have difficulty distinguishing between shades of blue.","zh":"年長人士可能難以分辨藍色色調。"},{"en":"Shades of blue are different versions or tones of the colour blue.","zh":"shades of blue 指藍色的不同版本或色調。"},{"en":"A website using many shades of blue may confuse some users.","zh":"使用許多藍色色調的網站可能令某些使用者困惑。"},{"en":"Designers test shades of blue to make sure buttons are easy to see.","zh":"設計師測試藍色色調，以確保按鈕容易看見。"},{"en":"Similar shades of blue can be hard to separate on a small screen.","zh":"相近藍色色調在小螢幕上可能難以分辨。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"software designers","meaning":"軟件設計師","examples":[{"en":"Software designers rarely create interfaces with shades of blue.","zh":"軟件設計師很少用藍色色調設計介面。"},{"en":"Software designers are people who plan how apps, websites, or computer programmes look and work.","zh":"software designers 指規劃應用程式、網站或電腦程式外觀和運作方式的人。"},{"en":"Software designers choose colours, buttons, menus, and user paths.","zh":"軟件設計師選擇顏色、按鈕、選單和使用者路徑。"},{"en":"Good software designers test their designs with real users.","zh":"好軟件設計師會用真實使用者測試設計。"},{"en":"Software designers must think about accessibility, not only appearance.","zh":"軟件設計師必須考慮無障礙性，而不只是外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"create interfaces with","meaning":"以……設計介面","examples":[{"en":"Software designers rarely create interfaces with shades of blue.","zh":"軟件設計師很少以藍色色調設計介面。"},{"en":"To create interfaces with something means to design screens using particular colours, tools, or features.","zh":"create interfaces with something 指使用特定顏色、工具或功能來設計螢幕介面。"},{"en":"Designers create interfaces with large icons for older users.","zh":"設計師為年長使用者以大圖示設計介面。"},{"en":"A banking app should not create interfaces with confusing symbols.","zh":"銀行應用程式不應以令人困惑的符號設計介面。"},{"en":"Creating interfaces with clear labels makes technology easier to use.","zh":"以清楚標籤設計介面，會令科技更易使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"interfaces","meaning":"介面","examples":[{"en":"Software designers consider colour carefully when creating interfaces.","zh":"軟件設計師建立介面時會仔細考慮顏色。"},{"en":"Interfaces are the screens or controls that let users interact with a machine, app, or system.","zh":"interfaces 指讓使用者與機器、應用程式或系統互動的螢幕或控制裝置。"},{"en":"Clear interfaces help users find what they need quickly.","zh":"清楚介面幫助使用者快速找到需要的東西。"},{"en":"Complicated interfaces can make people give up using a product.","zh":"複雜介面可能令人放棄使用產品。"},{"en":"Good interfaces use readable text, logical buttons, and helpful feedback.","zh":"好介面使用易讀文字、合乎邏輯的按鈕和有用回饋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"motor skills","meaning":"動作技能","examples":[{"en":"Motor skills also decline with age.","zh":"動作技能也會隨年齡下降。"},{"en":"Motor skills are physical abilities used to move and control the body, especially the hands and fingers.","zh":"motor skills 指用來移動和控制身體，尤其是手和手指的身體能力。"},{"en":"Writing, typing, and picking up objects all require motor skills.","zh":"寫字、打字和拿起物件都需要動作技能。"},{"en":"Some illnesses can affect motor skills and make daily tasks harder.","zh":"有些疾病會影響動作技能，令日常任務更困難。"},{"en":"Designers should consider motor skills when making buttons, handles, and controls.","zh":"設計師製作按鈕、手柄和控制裝置時，應考慮動作技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"decline with age","meaning":"隨年齡下降","examples":[{"en":"Motor skills decline with age.","zh":"動作技能會隨年齡下降。"},{"en":"To decline with age means to become weaker or less effective as people grow older.","zh":"decline with age 指隨着人變老而變弱或效率降低。"},{"en":"Hearing may decline with age for many people.","zh":"許多人的聽力可能隨年齡下降。"},{"en":"If strength declines with age, heavy doors can become difficult to open.","zh":"如果力量隨年齡下降，沉重的門可能變得難以打開。"},{"en":"Designers must plan for abilities that decline with age.","zh":"設計師必須為會隨年齡下降的能力作規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have difficulty doing","meaning":"做……有困難","examples":[{"en":"Some people have difficulty doing everyday things.","zh":"有些人做日常事情有困難。"},{"en":"To have difficulty doing something means to find it hard to do that action.","zh":"have difficulty doing something 指做某動作時覺得困難。"},{"en":"Older users may have difficulty reading small text on phones.","zh":"年長使用者可能閱讀手機上的細小文字有困難。"},{"en":"People with hand pain may have difficulty turning small knobs.","zh":"手痛的人可能扭動細小旋鈕有困難。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe a practical problem clearly.","zh":"這個短語幫助清楚描述實際問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"everyday things","meaning":"日常事情","examples":[{"en":"Some people have difficulty doing everyday things like picking up a cup.","zh":"有些人做拿起杯子等日常事情有困難。"},{"en":"Everyday things are ordinary tasks or objects that people use or do in daily life.","zh":"everyday things 指日常生活中普通的任務或物件。"},{"en":"Opening doors and using taps are everyday things many people take for granted.","zh":"開門和使用水龍頭是許多人視為理所當然的日常事情。"},{"en":"Inclusive design makes everyday things easier for people with different abilities.","zh":"包容性設計令不同能力的人更容易做日常事情。"},{"en":"When everyday things become difficult, independence can be affected.","zh":"當日常事情變得困難，獨立生活可能受到影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"affect their ability to","meaning":"影響其……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Motor problems can affect their ability to use a mouse or keyboard.","zh":"動作問題可以影響他們使用滑鼠或鍵盤的能力。"},{"en":"To affect someone’s ability to do something means to make it easier or harder for them to do it.","zh":"affect someone’s ability to do something 指令某人做某事的能力變得較容易或較困難。"},{"en":"Poor eyesight can affect a person’s ability to read small print.","zh":"視力差可以影響一個人閱讀細小字體的能力。"},{"en":"Hand pain may affect workers’ ability to type quickly.","zh":"手痛可能影響員工快速打字的能力。"},{"en":"Designers should ask what might affect users’ ability to complete a task.","zh":"設計師應詢問甚麼可能影響使用者完成任務的能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"use a mouse or keyboard","meaning":"使用滑鼠或鍵盤","examples":[{"en":"Some people have difficulty using a mouse or keyboard.","zh":"有些人使用滑鼠或鍵盤有困難。"},{"en":"To use a mouse or keyboard means to control a computer with these input devices.","zh":"use a mouse or keyboard 指用這些輸入裝置控制電腦。"},{"en":"People with hand tremors may find it hard to use a mouse or keyboard.","zh":"手震的人可能覺得使用滑鼠或鍵盤很困難。"},{"en":"Voice commands can help users who cannot easily use a mouse or keyboard.","zh":"語音指令可以幫助不易使用滑鼠或鍵盤的使用者。"},{"en":"Interfaces should not require perfect hand control to use a mouse or keyboard.","zh":"介面不應要求完美手部控制才能使用滑鼠或鍵盤。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"voice access","meaning":"語音控制","examples":[{"en":"Voice access is now a routine way of making commands.","zh":"語音控制現在是發出指令的常見方式。"},{"en":"Voice access lets users control a device or system by speaking.","zh":"voice access 讓使用者透過說話控制裝置或系統。"},{"en":"Voice access helps people who cannot easily type or press buttons.","zh":"語音控制幫助不能輕易打字或按按鈕的人。"},{"en":"Smart speakers use voice access to answer questions and control lights.","zh":"智能喇叭使用語音控制來回答問題和控制燈光。"},{"en":"Voice access can make technology more inclusive for people with mobility issues.","zh":"語音控制可以令科技對有行動能力問題的人更具包容性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a routine way of","meaning":"……的常見方式","examples":[{"en":"Voice access is now a routine way of making commands.","zh":"語音控制現在是發出指令的常見方式。"},{"en":"A routine way of doing something is a normal or common method.","zh":"a routine way of doing something 指做某事的正常或常見方法。"},{"en":"Online payment is now a routine way of buying tickets.","zh":"網上付款現在是購買門票的常見方式。"},{"en":"Email is a routine way of sending formal messages at work.","zh":"電郵是在工作中發送正式訊息的常見方式。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something has become ordinary, not unusual.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事已變得普通，而不是不尋常。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"making commands","meaning":"發出指令","examples":[{"en":"Voice access is a routine way of making commands.","zh":"語音控制是發出指令的常見方式。"},{"en":"Making commands means giving instructions to a machine, system, or person.","zh":"making commands 指向機器、系統或人給予指示。"},{"en":"Users make commands by saying “open email” or “turn on the light.”","zh":"使用者透過說「打開電郵」或「開燈」來發出指令。"},{"en":"Clear commands help a device understand what the user wants.","zh":"清楚指令幫助裝置理解使用者想要甚麼。"},{"en":"Voice systems should recognise different accents when people are making commands.","zh":"當人們發出指令時，語音系統應能識別不同口音。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it’s worth looking at","meaning":"值得看看……","examples":[{"en":"It’s worth looking at the problems caused by non-inclusive designs.","zh":"值得看看非包容性設計造成的問題。"},{"en":"It’s worth looking at means something deserves attention or careful thought.","zh":"it’s worth looking at 指某事值得注意或仔細思考。"},{"en":"It’s worth looking at how older users actually use the app.","zh":"值得看看年長使用者實際如何使用這個應用程式。"},{"en":"Before buying new furniture, it’s worth looking at users’ comfort.","zh":"購買新家具前，值得看看使用者的舒適度。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a topic is important enough to examine.","zh":"這個短語表示某課題重要，值得研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"non-inclusive designs","meaning":"非包容性設計","examples":[{"en":"Non-inclusive designs can have a serious impact on people’s lives.","zh":"非包容性設計可以對人們的生活造成嚴重影響。"},{"en":"Non-inclusive designs are designs that fail to consider different users’ needs.","zh":"non-inclusive designs 指未能考慮不同使用者需要的設計。"},{"en":"Stairs without ramps are non-inclusive designs for wheelchair users.","zh":"沒有斜道的樓梯對輪椅使用者來說是非包容性設計。"},{"en":"Tiny text on a screen can be part of non-inclusive design for older people.","zh":"螢幕上的細小文字對年長人士來說可能屬於非包容性設計。"},{"en":"Non-inclusive designs can make people dependent on others unnecessarily.","zh":"非包容性設計可能令人不必要地依賴他人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not enough consideration is given to","meaning":"對……考慮不足","examples":[{"en":"Problems arise when not enough consideration is given to a range of users.","zh":"當對不同類型使用者考慮不足時，問題就會出現。"},{"en":"Not enough consideration is given to something means it is not thought about carefully enough.","zh":"not enough consideration is given to something 指沒有足夠仔細思考某事。"},{"en":"Mistakes happen when not enough consideration is given to disabled users.","zh":"當對殘疾使用者考慮不足時，錯誤就會發生。"},{"en":"If not enough consideration is given to safety, a product may be dangerous.","zh":"如果對安全考慮不足，產品可能會危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for explaining why a design fails.","zh":"這個短語適合用來解釋設計為何失敗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a range of users","meaning":"不同類型的使用者","examples":[{"en":"Designers should give enough consideration to a range of users.","zh":"設計師應充分考慮不同類型的使用者。"},{"en":"A range of users means different kinds of people who may use a product or service.","zh":"a range of users 指可能使用某產品或服務的不同種類人士。"},{"en":"A public website should serve a range of users, including children and older people.","zh":"公共網站應服務不同類型的使用者，包括兒童和長者。"},{"en":"Testing with a range of users reveals problems designers may miss.","zh":"與不同類型的使用者測試，可以揭示設計師可能錯過的問題。"},{"en":"Considering a range of users makes design fairer and more useful.","zh":"考慮不同類型的使用者，會令設計更公平和有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have a serious impact on","meaning":"對……造成嚴重影響","examples":[{"en":"Non-inclusive designs can have a serious impact on people’s lives.","zh":"非包容性設計可以對人們的生活造成嚴重影響。"},{"en":"To have a serious impact on something means to affect it in an important and possibly harmful way.","zh":"have a serious impact on something 指以重要且可能有害的方式影響某事。"},{"en":"Poor housing can have a serious impact on children’s health.","zh":"惡劣住屋可以對兒童健康造成嚴重影響。"},{"en":"A badly designed workplace can have a serious impact on workers’ comfort.","zh":"設計不佳的工作場所可以對員工舒適度造成嚴重影響。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the effect is not small or temporary.","zh":"這個短語顯示影響不是小或短暫的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"people’s lives","meaning":"人們的生活","examples":[{"en":"Design choices can have a serious impact on people’s lives.","zh":"設計選擇可以對人們的生活造成嚴重影響。"},{"en":"People’s lives means the daily experiences, independence, work, health, and comfort of people.","zh":"people’s lives 指人們的日常經驗、獨立性、工作、健康和舒適度。"},{"en":"Public transport design affects people’s lives every day.","zh":"公共交通設計每天都影響人們的生活。"},{"en":"A small design change can improve people’s lives if it removes a daily difficulty.","zh":"如果小設計改動能消除日常困難，就可以改善人們的生活。"},{"en":"Designers should remember that products are used in real people’s lives.","zh":"設計師應記住產品是在真實人們的生活中被使用的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an obvious example","meaning":"明顯例子","examples":[{"en":"Access is an obvious example of the impact of non-inclusive design.","zh":"使用權是非包容性設計影響的一個明顯例子。"},{"en":"An obvious example is an example that is clear and easy to understand.","zh":"obvious example 指清楚而容易理解的例子。"},{"en":"A staircase without a ramp is an obvious example of poor access.","zh":"沒有斜道的樓梯是通達性差的明顯例子。"},{"en":"Small text is an obvious example of a problem for people with weak eyesight.","zh":"細小文字是視力弱人士面對問題的明顯例子。"},{"en":"Obvious examples help listeners understand an idea quickly.","zh":"明顯例子幫助聽眾快速理解想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have a huge impact on","meaning":"對……有巨大影響","examples":[{"en":"Access has a huge impact on disabled people’s independence.","zh":"使用權對殘疾人士的獨立生活有巨大影響。"},{"en":"To have a huge impact on something means to affect it very strongly.","zh":"have a huge impact on something 指非常強烈地影響某事。"},{"en":"A lift can have a huge impact on an elderly person’s daily freedom.","zh":"升降機可以對長者的日常自由有巨大影響。"},{"en":"Poor transport access has a huge impact on people who cannot drive.","zh":"交通通達性差對不能駕駛的人有巨大影響。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the effect is very large.","zh":"這個短語強調影響非常大。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"disabled people’s independence","meaning":"殘疾人士的獨立生活","examples":[{"en":"Access has a huge impact on disabled people’s independence.","zh":"使用權對殘疾人士的獨立生活有巨大影響。"},{"en":"Disabled people’s independence means their ability to live, travel, work, and make choices without unnecessary help.","zh":"disabled people’s independence 指殘疾人士在無須不必要幫助下生活、出行、工作和作選擇的能力。"},{"en":"Wheelchair-friendly transport supports disabled people’s independence.","zh":"適合輪椅使用者的交通支援殘疾人士的獨立生活。"},{"en":"Poor building access can reduce disabled people’s independence.","zh":"建築物通達性差可以削弱殘疾人士的獨立生活。"},{"en":"Inclusive design protects disabled people’s independence by removing barriers.","zh":"包容性設計透過移除障礙來保障殘疾人士的獨立生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not being able to access","meaning":"無法使用……","examples":[{"en":"Not being able to access public transport limits independence.","zh":"無法使用公共交通會限制獨立性。"},{"en":"Not being able to access something means being unable to enter, reach, or use it.","zh":"not being able to access something 指無法進入、到達或使用某物。"},{"en":"Not being able to access a lift can stop a wheelchair user from entering a building.","zh":"無法使用升降機可能令輪椅使用者不能進入建築物。"},{"en":"Students suffer when they are not able to access online learning materials.","zh":"學生無法使用網上學習材料時會受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights exclusion caused by poor design or limited services.","zh":"這個短語突出由不良設計或有限服務造成的排除。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"public transport","meaning":"公共交通","examples":[{"en":"Disabled people may not be able to access public transport.","zh":"殘疾人士可能無法使用公共交通。"},{"en":"Public transport includes buses, trains, trams, ferries, and other shared transport services.","zh":"public transport 包括巴士、火車、電車、渡輪和其他共享交通服務。"},{"en":"Accessible public transport helps people travel to work, school, and medical appointments.","zh":"無障礙公共交通幫助人們前往工作、學校和醫療預約。"},{"en":"Public transport should be designed for wheelchair users, older people, and parents with prams.","zh":"公共交通應為輪椅使用者、長者和推嬰兒車的家長而設計。"},{"en":"When public transport is not accessible, people may become isolated.","zh":"當公共交通不具無障礙性，人們可能變得孤立。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"wheelchair-friendly","meaning":"適合輪椅使用者的","examples":[{"en":"Some buses and trains are not wheelchair-friendly.","zh":"有些巴士和火車並不適合輪椅使用者。"},{"en":"Wheelchair-friendly means designed so wheelchair users can use it safely and easily.","zh":"wheelchair-friendly 指設計上讓輪椅使用者能安全而容易地使用。"},{"en":"A wheelchair-friendly entrance has a ramp or lift instead of only steps.","zh":"適合輪椅使用者的入口有斜道或升降機，而不只有樓梯。"},{"en":"A wheelchair-friendly toilet needs enough space to turn around.","zh":"適合輪椅使用者的洗手間需要足夠轉身空間。"},{"en":"Wheelchair-friendly design often helps many other users too.","zh":"適合輪椅使用者的設計通常也幫助許多其他使用者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"unless someone goes with them","meaning":"除非有人陪同","examples":[{"en":"Some disabled people cannot go out unless someone goes with them.","zh":"有些殘疾人士除非有人陪同，否則不能外出。"},{"en":"Unless someone goes with them means except if another person accompanies or helps them.","zh":"unless someone goes with them 指除非有另一個人陪伴或幫助。"},{"en":"The child cannot cross the busy road unless someone goes with him.","zh":"那孩子除非有人陪同，否則不能橫過繁忙道路。"},{"en":"If transport is not accessible, a wheelchair user may not travel unless someone goes with them.","zh":"如果交通不具無障礙性，輪椅使用者可能除非有人陪同，否則不能出行。"},{"en":"This phrase shows dependence created by barriers.","zh":"這個短語顯示障礙造成的依賴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"safety implications","meaning":"安全影響","examples":[{"en":"Crash testing has safety implications for women.","zh":"撞擊測試對女性有安全影響。"},{"en":"Safety implications are possible effects on people’s safety.","zh":"safety implications 指對人們安全可能造成的影響。"},{"en":"Poor lighting has safety implications for workers leaving late at night.","zh":"照明不足對深夜離開的員工有安全影響。"},{"en":"A badly fitted seatbelt has serious safety implications in a car crash.","zh":"不合身的安全帶在車禍中有嚴重安全影響。"},{"en":"Designers must consider safety implications before releasing a product.","zh":"設計師推出產品前必須考慮安全影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"inexplicably","meaning":"令人費解地","examples":[{"en":"Inexplicably, most cars are still crash-tested using a male dummy.","zh":"令人費解地，大部分汽車仍使用男性測試假人進行撞擊測試。"},{"en":"Inexplicably means in a way that is difficult to explain or understand.","zh":"inexplicably 指以難以解釋或理解的方式。"},{"en":"Inexplicably, the door opened even though nobody touched it.","zh":"令人費解地，門在沒有人觸碰的情況下打開了。"},{"en":"The form inexplicably asked for information that was not needed.","zh":"表格令人費解地要求一些不需要的資料。"},{"en":"This word suggests surprise because something seems unreasonable.","zh":"這個詞表示某事似乎不合理，因此令人驚訝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"crash-tested","meaning":"進行撞擊測試","examples":[{"en":"Most cars are still crash-tested using a dummy based on an average-sized male.","zh":"大部分汽車仍使用以平均身形男性為基準的假人進行撞擊測試。"},{"en":"Crash-tested means tested in a controlled crash to measure safety.","zh":"crash-tested 指在受控撞擊中測試安全性。"},{"en":"Child seats are crash-tested before they are sold to the public.","zh":"兒童安全座椅在向公眾出售前會進行撞擊測試。"},{"en":"A car that is crash-tested well may protect passengers better.","zh":"撞擊測試表現好的汽車可能更好地保護乘客。"},{"en":"Crash-tested products give users more information about safety.","zh":"經撞擊測試的產品給使用者更多安全資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"using a dummy","meaning":"使用測試假人","examples":[{"en":"Cars are crash-tested using a dummy based on an average-sized male.","zh":"汽車使用以平均身形男性為基準的測試假人進行撞擊測試。"},{"en":"Using a dummy means using a model of a human body for testing instead of a real person.","zh":"using a dummy 指使用人體模型進行測試，而不是使用真人。"},{"en":"Engineers test seatbelts using a dummy to measure injury risk.","zh":"工程師使用測試假人測試安全帶，以衡量受傷風險。"},{"en":"Using a dummy can make dangerous tests safer and more controlled.","zh":"使用測試假人可以令危險測試更安全和更受控。"},{"en":"The dummy should represent different body types if the product is for everyone.","zh":"如果產品是給所有人使用，測試假人應代表不同身形。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"based on","meaning":"以……為基準","examples":[{"en":"The dummy is based on an average-sized male.","zh":"測試假人以平均身形男性為基準。"},{"en":"Based on means designed, built, or judged using something as the model or standard.","zh":"based on 指以某事作為模型、標準或判斷依據來設計、建立或判斷。"},{"en":"The film is based on a true story.","zh":"這部電影以真實故事為基礎。"},{"en":"A chair based on only one body type may not suit everyone.","zh":"只以一種身形為基準的椅子未必適合所有人。"},{"en":"Designs based on limited data can exclude many users.","zh":"以有限數據為基準的設計可能排除許多使用者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"average-sized male","meaning":"平均身形男性","examples":[{"en":"The crash-test dummy is based on an average-sized male.","zh":"撞擊測試假人以平均身形男性為基準。"},{"en":"An average-sized male is a man whose body size is considered typical in a chosen group.","zh":"average-sized male 指在某個群體中身形被視為典型的男性。"},{"en":"Clothes designed for an average-sized male may not fit many women.","zh":"為平均身形男性設計的衣服未必適合許多女性。"},{"en":"A safety test based only on an average-sized male may miss risks for smaller people.","zh":"只以平均身形男性為基準的安全測試，可能忽略較小身形人士的風險。"},{"en":"Designers should not assume every user is an average-sized male.","zh":"設計師不應假設每位使用者都是平均身形男性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"particularly those who are pregnant","meaning":"尤其是懷孕女性","examples":[{"en":"Seatbelt design is especially important for women, particularly those who are pregnant.","zh":"安全帶設計對女性尤其重要，尤其是懷孕女性。"},{"en":"Particularly those who are pregnant means especially pregnant women within a larger group.","zh":"particularly those who are pregnant 指在較大群體中尤其是懷孕女性。"},{"en":"Public transport seats should consider older passengers, particularly those who are pregnant or unwell.","zh":"公共交通座位應考慮年長乘客，尤其是懷孕或身體不適的人。"},{"en":"Safety information should be clear for all users, particularly those who are pregnant.","zh":"安全資訊應對所有使用者清楚，尤其是懷孕女性。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a subgroup with special safety needs.","zh":"這個短語突出有特別安全需要的子群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"seatbelts","meaning":"安全帶","examples":[{"en":"The seatbelts worn by the dummy are not adapted for pregnant women.","zh":"測試假人所繫的安全帶並沒有為懷孕女性作調整。"},{"en":"Seatbelts are safety straps worn in vehicles to hold passengers in place during sudden stops or crashes.","zh":"seatbelts 指車輛中用來在急停或撞車時固定乘客的安全帶。"},{"en":"Seatbelts can reduce serious injuries in car accidents.","zh":"安全帶可以減少車禍中的嚴重傷害。"},{"en":"A seatbelt must fit properly across the body to work safely.","zh":"安全帶必須合身地繫在身體上，才能安全發揮作用。"},{"en":"Seatbelt design should consider different body shapes and conditions.","zh":"安全帶設計應考慮不同身形和身體狀況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"adapted to accommodate","meaning":"調整至適合……","examples":[{"en":"The seatbelts are not adapted to accommodate pregnant women.","zh":"安全帶沒有調整至適合懷孕女性。"},{"en":"To be adapted to accommodate someone means to be changed so that person’s needs can be met.","zh":"be adapted to accommodate someone 指作出調整以滿足某人的需要。"},{"en":"The classroom was adapted to accommodate a student using a wheelchair.","zh":"課室被調整至適合使用輪椅的學生。"},{"en":"Software can be adapted to accommodate users with weak eyesight.","zh":"軟件可以調整至適合視力弱的使用者。"},{"en":"Products should be adapted to accommodate real users when the original design excludes them.","zh":"當原本設計排除真實使用者時，產品應調整至適合他們。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"over the past 100 years","meaning":"在過去一百年","examples":[{"en":"Over the past 100 years, workplaces in the UK have become safer.","zh":"在過去一百年，英國工作場所變得更安全。"},{"en":"Over the past 100 years means during the last century up to the present.","zh":"over the past 100 years 指從過去一個世紀直到現在。"},{"en":"Over the past 100 years, transport has changed dramatically.","zh":"在過去一百年，交通有巨大變化。"},{"en":"Medicine has improved greatly over the past 100 years.","zh":"醫學在過去一百年有很大進步。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare present conditions with a long historical period.","zh":"這個短語幫助把現況與長期歷史作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on the whole","meaning":"整體而言","examples":[{"en":"On the whole, workplaces in the UK have become considerably safer.","zh":"整體而言，英國工作場所已變得安全得多。"},{"en":"On the whole means generally, considering the whole situation.","zh":"on the whole 指整體考慮時，一般來說。"},{"en":"On the whole, the new timetable works well for most students.","zh":"整體而言，新時間表對大部分學生都有效。"},{"en":"The project had a few problems, but on the whole it was successful.","zh":"這個項目有幾個問題，但整體而言是成功的。"},{"en":"This phrase allows small exceptions while giving a general view.","zh":"這個短語在給出整體看法時容許有小例外。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"considerably safer","meaning":"安全得多","examples":[{"en":"Workplaces in the UK have become considerably safer.","zh":"英國工作場所已變得安全得多。"},{"en":"Considerably safer means much safer than before.","zh":"considerably safer 指比以前安全很多。"},{"en":"Roads became considerably safer after better lighting was installed.","zh":"安裝更好照明後，道路變得安全得多。"},{"en":"A factory is considerably safer when workers wear proper PPE.","zh":"當工人穿戴適當個人防護裝備，工廠會安全得多。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a clear and important improvement in safety.","zh":"這個短語顯示安全方面有清楚而重要的改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"legally required to","meaning":"法律規定要……","examples":[{"en":"Employers are legally required to provide PPE to workers who need it.","zh":"法律規定僱主須向有需要的工人提供個人防護裝備。"},{"en":"Legally required to do something means the law says someone must do it.","zh":"legally required to do something 指法律規定某人必須做某事。"},{"en":"Drivers are legally required to wear seatbelts in many places.","zh":"在許多地方，法律規定司機要繫安全帶。"},{"en":"Employers may be legally required to provide a safe workplace.","zh":"法律可能規定僱主要提供安全工作場所。"},{"en":"If something is legally required, ignoring it can lead to punishment.","zh":"如果某事是法律規定要做的，忽視它可能導致處罰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"well-maintained","meaning":"保養良好的","examples":[{"en":"Employers must provide well-maintained personal protective equipment.","zh":"僱主必須提供保養良好的個人防護裝備。"},{"en":"Well-maintained means kept in good condition through care, cleaning, or repair.","zh":"well-maintained 指透過照料、清潔或維修而保持良好狀態。"},{"en":"A well-maintained lift is safer for daily users.","zh":"保養良好的升降機對日常使用者較安全。"},{"en":"Workers should not use safety equipment that is not well-maintained.","zh":"工人不應使用保養不良的安全裝備。"},{"en":"Well-maintained tools last longer and reduce accidents.","zh":"保養良好的工具更耐用，並能減少意外。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"personal protective equipment","meaning":"個人防護裝備","examples":[{"en":"Employers must provide personal protective equipment to workers who need it.","zh":"僱主必須向有需要的工人提供個人防護裝備。"},{"en":"Personal protective equipment is clothing or equipment that protects workers from injury or illness.","zh":"personal protective equipment 指保護工人免受傷害或疾病的衣物或裝備。"},{"en":"Helmets, gloves, masks, and goggles are personal protective equipment.","zh":"頭盔、手套、口罩和護目鏡都是個人防護裝備。"},{"en":"Personal protective equipment must fit properly to protect the user.","zh":"個人防護裝備必須合身，才能保護使用者。"},{"en":"Providing personal protective equipment is part of workplace safety.","zh":"提供個人防護裝備是工作場所安全的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"PPE","meaning":"個人防護裝備","examples":[{"en":"PPE includes anything from goggles to full body suits.","zh":"PPE 包括由護目鏡到全身防護服等各種裝備。"},{"en":"PPE stands for personal protective equipment.","zh":"PPE 是 personal protective equipment 的縮寫。"},{"en":"Workers wear PPE to reduce risk in dangerous jobs.","zh":"工人在危險工作中穿戴 PPE 以降低風險。"},{"en":"PPE is not useful if it is damaged, dirty, or the wrong size.","zh":"如果 PPE 損壞、骯髒或尺寸不對，就沒有用。"},{"en":"Employers should train workers to use PPE correctly.","zh":"僱主應訓練工人正確使用 PPE。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"anything from A to B","meaning":"由 A 到 B 都包括","examples":[{"en":"PPE includes anything from goggles to full body suits.","zh":"PPE 由護目鏡到全身防護服都包括。"},{"en":"Anything from A to B means a wide range that includes both simple and more complete examples.","zh":"anything from A to B 指範圍很廣，包含簡單和較完整的例子。"},{"en":"The shop sells anything from pens to laptops.","zh":"這間店由筆到手提電腦都出售。"},{"en":"The course covers anything from basic drawing to product testing.","zh":"課程由基本繪圖到產品測試都涵蓋。"},{"en":"This phrase shows variety across a broad range.","zh":"這個短語顯示廣泛範圍內的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"goggles","meaning":"護目鏡","examples":[{"en":"Goggles are one type of personal protective equipment.","zh":"護目鏡是一種個人防護裝備。"},{"en":"Goggles are protective glasses that cover the eyes closely.","zh":"goggles 指緊貼覆蓋眼睛的防護眼鏡。"},{"en":"Science students wear goggles during chemistry experiments.","zh":"科學學生在化學實驗中佩戴護目鏡。"},{"en":"Goggles protect workers from dust, chemicals, or flying pieces.","zh":"護目鏡保護工人免受灰塵、化學品或飛濺碎片傷害。"},{"en":"Goggles must fit properly so dangerous material cannot reach the eyes.","zh":"護目鏡必須合身，危險物質才不會接觸眼睛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"full body suits","meaning":"全身防護服","examples":[{"en":"Full body suits are a form of personal protective equipment.","zh":"全身防護服是一種個人防護裝備。"},{"en":"Full body suits are protective clothing that covers most or all of the body.","zh":"full body suits 指覆蓋身體大部分或全部的防護衣物。"},{"en":"Workers may wear full body suits when handling dangerous chemicals.","zh":"工人處理危險化學品時可能穿全身防護服。"},{"en":"Full body suits protect skin and clothes from harmful substances.","zh":"全身防護服保護皮膚和衣物免受有害物質影響。"},{"en":"Full body suits must fit well so workers can move safely.","zh":"全身防護服必須合身，工人才能安全活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"free of charge","meaning":"免費","examples":[{"en":"Employers must provide PPE free of charge.","zh":"僱主必須免費提供 PPE。"},{"en":"Free of charge means without asking people to pay.","zh":"free of charge 指不要求人們付款。"},{"en":"The school provides safety goggles free of charge during experiments.","zh":"學校在實驗期間免費提供護目鏡。"},{"en":"Public libraries let people borrow books free of charge.","zh":"公共圖書館讓人們免費借書。"},{"en":"If safety equipment is required, workers should not have to buy it themselves.","zh":"如果安全裝備是必需的，工人不應要自己購買。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"designed to fit","meaning":"設計成適合……","examples":[{"en":"Most PPE is designed to fit men.","zh":"大部分 PPE 設計成適合男性。"},{"en":"Designed to fit someone means made in a size or shape suitable for that person.","zh":"designed to fit someone 指尺寸或形狀製作得適合某人。"},{"en":"School chairs should be designed to fit children, not adults only.","zh":"學校椅子應設計成適合兒童，而不只是成人。"},{"en":"Gloves designed to fit large hands may be unsafe for users with smaller hands.","zh":"設計成適合大手的手套，對手較小的使用者可能不安全。"},{"en":"Equipment designed to fit only one group may exclude others.","zh":"只設計成適合一個群體的裝備可能排除其他人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a recent report found that","meaning":"最近一份報告發現","examples":[{"en":"A recent report found that employers often misunderstand women’s PPE needs.","zh":"最近一份報告發現，僱主常誤解女性的 PPE 需要。"},{"en":"A recent report found that introduces a new finding from a document published not long ago.","zh":"a recent report found that 用來引出不久前發表的文件中的新發現。"},{"en":"A recent report found that many workers do not take enough breaks.","zh":"最近一份報告發現，許多員工沒有足夠休息。"},{"en":"A recent report found that office temperatures often suit men better than women.","zh":"最近一份報告發現，辦公室溫度常較適合男性而非女性。"},{"en":"This phrase uses evidence to support a point.","zh":"這個短語用證據支持觀點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"when it comes to","meaning":"談到……；至於……","examples":[{"en":"When it comes to female workers, employers often buy jackets designed for small men.","zh":"談到女性員工，僱主常購買為小個子男性設計的外套。"},{"en":"When it comes to means when discussing or dealing with a particular topic.","zh":"when it comes to 指談論或處理某個特定主題時。"},{"en":"When it comes to safety, small details matter.","zh":"談到安全，小細節很重要。"},{"en":"When it comes to older users, designers should avoid tiny buttons.","zh":"至於年長使用者，設計師應避免細小按鈕。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the discussion to a specific area.","zh":"這個短語把討論收窄到特定範疇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"female workers","meaning":"女性員工","examples":[{"en":"Employers often misunderstand the needs of female workers.","zh":"僱主常誤解女性員工的需要。"},{"en":"Female workers are women who work in a job or workplace.","zh":"female workers 指在工作或工作場所中的女性。"},{"en":"Female workers may need PPE designed for women’s body shapes.","zh":"女性員工可能需要按女性身形設計的 PPE。"},{"en":"Workplaces should listen to female workers when choosing safety equipment.","zh":"工作場所選擇安全裝備時，應聆聽女性員工的意見。"},{"en":"Ignoring female workers’ needs can create safety and comfort problems.","zh":"忽視女性員工的需要可能造成安全和舒適問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"comply with","meaning":"遵守；符合","examples":[{"en":"Employers must comply with this legal requirement.","zh":"僱主必須遵守這項法律要求。"},{"en":"To comply with something means to obey a rule, law, or requirement.","zh":"comply with something 指遵守規則、法律或要求。"},{"en":"Drivers must comply with speed limits near schools.","zh":"司機必須遵守學校附近的車速限制。"},{"en":"Companies comply with safety laws by providing proper equipment.","zh":"公司透過提供適當裝備來遵守安全法律。"},{"en":"If employers do not comply with the law, they may face penalties.","zh":"如果僱主不遵守法律，可能面對懲罰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"legal requirement","meaning":"法律要求","examples":[{"en":"Providing suitable PPE is a legal requirement.","zh":"提供合適 PPE 是一項法律要求。"},{"en":"A legal requirement is something the law says must be done.","zh":"legal requirement 指法律規定必須做的事情。"},{"en":"Wearing a seatbelt is a legal requirement in many places.","zh":"在許多地方，繫安全帶是法律要求。"},{"en":"Providing safe equipment can be a legal requirement for employers.","zh":"提供安全裝備可以是僱主的法律要求。"},{"en":"A legal requirement is not optional; people must follow it.","zh":"法律要求不是可選擇的；人們必須遵守。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"small man","meaning":"小個子男性","examples":[{"en":"Some employers buy jackets designed for a small man.","zh":"有些僱主購買為小個子男性設計的外套。"},{"en":"A small man is an adult male with a smaller body size than average.","zh":"small man 指身形比平均較小的成年男性。"},{"en":"A jacket designed for a small man may still not fit many women.","zh":"為小個子男性設計的外套仍未必適合許多女性。"},{"en":"Using a small man as the model ignores differences in shoulders, chest, and hips.","zh":"以小個子男性作模型會忽視肩膀、胸部和臀部差異。"},{"en":"This example shows why smaller does not automatically mean suitable for women.","zh":"這個例子顯示較小不一定自動等於適合女性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"much smaller shoulders","meaning":"窄得多的肩膀","examples":[{"en":"Women can be tall and still have much smaller shoulders than the average man.","zh":"女性可以很高，但肩膀仍比一般男性窄得多。"},{"en":"Much smaller shoulders means shoulders that are far narrower than another person’s.","zh":"much smaller shoulders 指肩膀比另一個人窄很多。"},{"en":"A tall woman may still have much smaller shoulders than the man a jacket was designed for.","zh":"高個子女性的肩膀仍可能比外套設計對象男性窄得多。"},{"en":"PPE with much wider shoulders can slip and reduce protection.","zh":"肩位過寬的 PPE 可能會滑動並降低保護。"},{"en":"Designers should measure real users instead of assuming shoulder size from height.","zh":"設計師應量度真實使用者，而不是從身高假設肩膀大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ill-fitting PPE","meaning":"不合身的個人防護裝備","examples":[{"en":"Ill-fitting PPE can put women at risk.","zh":"不合身的 PPE 會令女性面臨風險。"},{"en":"Ill-fitting PPE is protective equipment that does not fit the user’s body properly.","zh":"ill-fitting PPE 指不合使用者身形的個人防護裝備。"},{"en":"Ill-fitting PPE may leave gaps, restrict movement, or fall out of place.","zh":"不合身的 PPE 可能留下空隙、限制動作或移位。"},{"en":"Workers may avoid using ill-fitting PPE because it is uncomfortable.","zh":"工人可能因不舒服而避免使用不合身的 PPE。"},{"en":"Ill-fitting PPE can be dangerous even if the material is strong.","zh":"即使材料堅固，不合身的 PPE 仍可能危險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hi-vis jackets","meaning":"高能見度外套","examples":[{"en":"Hi-vis jackets are one type of PPE that may not fit women properly.","zh":"高能見度外套是一種可能不合女性身形的 PPE。"},{"en":"Hi-vis jackets are high-visibility jackets that make workers easier to see.","zh":"hi-vis jackets 指令工人更容易被看見的高能見度外套。"},{"en":"Road workers often wear hi-vis jackets so drivers can notice them.","zh":"道路工人常穿高能見度外套，讓司機能注意到他們。"},{"en":"Hi-vis jackets must fit well so they do not catch on tools or machines.","zh":"高能見度外套必須合身，才不會被工具或機器勾住。"},{"en":"If hi-vis jackets are too large, they may become a safety problem.","zh":"如果高能見度外套太大，它們可能變成安全問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"vests","meaning":"背心","examples":[{"en":"Vests can be unsuitable if they are designed to fit men.","zh":"如果背心設計成適合男性，它們可能不合適。"},{"en":"Vests are sleeveless pieces of clothing, often worn for visibility, warmth, or protection.","zh":"vests 指無袖衣物，常用於提高能見度、保暖或保護。"},{"en":"Safety vests help workers be seen in dark or busy areas.","zh":"安全背心幫助工人在昏暗或繁忙地方被看見。"},{"en":"A vest that is too loose may move around and distract the worker.","zh":"太鬆的背心可能會移位並分散工人注意力。"},{"en":"Vests should be available in shapes and sizes that fit different bodies.","zh":"背心應有適合不同身形的款式和尺寸。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"body armour","meaning":"防彈護具；防護裝備","examples":[{"en":"Body armour can put women at risk if it does not fit properly.","zh":"如果防護裝備不合身，可能令女性面臨風險。"},{"en":"Body armour is protective clothing or equipment worn to reduce injury from attacks or impacts.","zh":"body armour 指用來減少攻擊或撞擊傷害的防護衣物或裝備。"},{"en":"Police officers may wear body armour during dangerous operations.","zh":"警務人員在危險行動中可能穿戴防彈護具。"},{"en":"Body armour that is too large can leave important areas unprotected.","zh":"太大的防護裝備可能令重要部位沒有保護。"},{"en":"Properly fitted body armour can save lives in emergencies.","zh":"合身的防護裝備可以在緊急情況中拯救生命。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"put women at risk","meaning":"令女性面臨風險","examples":[{"en":"Ill-fitting PPE can put women at risk.","zh":"不合身的 PPE 會令女性面臨風險。"},{"en":"To put women at risk means to create danger for women.","zh":"put women at risk 指為女性造成危險。"},{"en":"Safety tests based only on men can put women at risk.","zh":"只以男性為基準的安全測試可能令女性面臨風險。"},{"en":"Poorly fitted body armour may put women at risk during police work.","zh":"不合身的防護裝備可能在警務工作中令女性面臨風險。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that design problems can become safety problems.","zh":"這個短語顯示設計問題可以變成安全問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hampered their work","meaning":"妨礙工作","examples":[{"en":"Many women said their PPE hampered their work.","zh":"許多女性說她們的 PPE 妨礙工作。"},{"en":"To hamper someone’s work means to make their work harder or slower.","zh":"hamper someone’s work 指令某人的工作更困難或更慢。"},{"en":"A heavy jacket hampered the worker’s movement.","zh":"厚重外套妨礙了工人的動作。"},{"en":"Poor software can hamper office work by making simple tasks slow.","zh":"差劣軟件會令簡單任務變慢，從而妨礙辦公室工作。"},{"en":"Equipment should protect workers without hampering their work.","zh":"裝備應保護工人，而不妨礙工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"emergency services","meaning":"緊急服務部門","examples":[{"en":"This problem was worst in the emergency services.","zh":"這個問題在緊急服務部門最嚴重。"},{"en":"Emergency services are organisations that respond to urgent danger, such as police, fire, and ambulance services.","zh":"emergency services 指應對緊急危險的機構，例如警察、消防和救護服務。"},{"en":"Emergency services need equipment that works quickly and safely.","zh":"緊急服務部門需要快速而安全運作的裝備。"},{"en":"Workers in emergency services cannot afford PPE that restricts movement.","zh":"緊急服務部門的工作者不能使用限制動作的 PPE。"},{"en":"Inclusive design is especially important in emergency services because lives may depend on it.","zh":"包容性設計在緊急服務部門尤其重要，因為生命可能取決於此。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"particularly the police","meaning":"尤其是警察部門","examples":[{"en":"The PPE problem was worst in the emergency services, particularly the police.","zh":"PPE 問題在緊急服務部門最嚴重，尤其是警察部門。"},{"en":"Particularly the police means especially the police among the groups being discussed.","zh":"particularly the police 指在所討論群體中尤其是警察部門。"},{"en":"The issue affects emergency workers, particularly the police, who face dangerous situations.","zh":"這個問題影響緊急服務人員，尤其是面對危險情況的警察。"},{"en":"Poor body armour is a serious problem, particularly for the police.","zh":"防護裝備差劣是嚴重問題，尤其是對警察部門而言。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights one group as especially affected.","zh":"這個短語突出某群體尤其受影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"comfort at work","meaning":"工作時的舒適度","examples":[{"en":"Another problem is related to comfort at work.","zh":"另一個問題與工作時的舒適度有關。"},{"en":"Comfort at work means how physically comfortable people feel while doing their jobs.","zh":"comfort at work 指人們工作時身體感到舒適的程度。"},{"en":"Good chairs, proper lighting, and fair temperatures improve comfort at work.","zh":"好椅子、適當照明和合適溫度可以改善工作時的舒適度。"},{"en":"Poor comfort at work can reduce concentration and productivity.","zh":"工作時舒適度低會降低集中力和生產力。"},{"en":"Employers should treat comfort at work as part of health and safety.","zh":"僱主應把工作時的舒適度視為健康與安全的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a common scenario","meaning":"常見情況","examples":[{"en":"A common scenario in offices is to see women wrapped in blankets.","zh":"在辦公室常見情況是看見女性裹着毛氈。"},{"en":"A common scenario is a situation that happens often or is easy to recognise.","zh":"common scenario 指經常發生或容易認出的情況。"},{"en":"A common scenario in classrooms is students looking tired after lunch.","zh":"課室中的常見情況是學生午飯後看起來疲倦。"},{"en":"In offices, a common scenario is people arguing about air-conditioning.","zh":"在辦公室，常見情況是人們因冷氣而爭論。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a typical real-life situation.","zh":"這個短語用來引出典型現實情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in summertime","meaning":"在夏天","examples":[{"en":"In summertime, women in offices may wear sweaters while the air conditioning is on high.","zh":"在夏天，辦公室女性可能在冷氣開得很強時穿着冷衫。"},{"en":"In summertime means during the summer season.","zh":"in summertime 指在夏季期間。"},{"en":"In summertime, many offices use strong air conditioning.","zh":"在夏天，許多辦公室使用很強的冷氣。"},{"en":"People drink more water in summertime because the weather is hot.","zh":"在夏天，天氣炎熱，人們喝更多水。"},{"en":"This phrase sets the time of year for the situation.","zh":"這個短語設定情況發生的季節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"wrapped in blankets","meaning":"裹着毛氈","examples":[{"en":"Women are often wrapped in blankets in cold offices.","zh":"女性在寒冷辦公室中常裹着毛氈。"},{"en":"Wrapped in blankets means covered or surrounded by blankets to keep warm.","zh":"wrapped in blankets 指用毛氈覆蓋或包裹身體以保暖。"},{"en":"Students were wrapped in blankets after the outdoor activity in cold weather.","zh":"學生在寒冷天氣的戶外活動後裹着毛氈。"},{"en":"If office workers are wrapped in blankets, the room may be too cold.","zh":"如果辦公室員工裹着毛氈，房間可能太冷。"},{"en":"This image shows discomfort caused by poor temperature settings.","zh":"這個畫面顯示溫度設定不佳造成的不適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"wearing sweaters","meaning":"穿着冷衫","examples":[{"en":"Women may be wearing sweaters while the air conditioning is on high.","zh":"女性可能在冷氣開得很強時穿着冷衫。"},{"en":"Wearing sweaters means having warm knitted tops on the body.","zh":"wearing sweaters 指身上穿着保暖針織上衣。"},{"en":"Some office workers are wearing sweaters even in summer because the room is cold.","zh":"有些辦公室工作者即使在夏天也穿着冷衫，因為房間很冷。"},{"en":"If people are wearing sweaters indoors, the air conditioning may be set too low.","zh":"如果人們在室內穿着冷衫，冷氣可能設定得太低。"},{"en":"Clothing choices can reveal whether a workplace is comfortable.","zh":"衣着選擇可以反映工作場所是否舒適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"air conditioning is on high","meaning":"冷氣開得很強","examples":[{"en":"The air conditioning is on high in many offices.","zh":"許多辦公室的冷氣開得很強。"},{"en":"Air conditioning is on high means the cooling system is set to a strong or cold level.","zh":"air conditioning is on high 指冷氣系統設定在很強或很冷的程度。"},{"en":"When the air conditioning is on high, some workers may feel too cold.","zh":"當冷氣開得很強，有些員工可能覺得太冷。"},{"en":"Offices waste energy if the air conditioning is on high all day.","zh":"如果冷氣整天開得很強，辦公室會浪費能源。"},{"en":"Temperature settings should suit the people in the room, not only the system.","zh":"溫度設定應適合房間內的人，而不只是系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"meanwhile","meaning":"與此同時","examples":[{"en":"Meanwhile, the men are in shorts and T-shirts.","zh":"與此同時，男性穿着短褲和 T 恤。"},{"en":"Meanwhile means at the same time, often showing a contrast.","zh":"meanwhile 指在同一時間，常用來顯示對比。"},{"en":"The women felt cold; meanwhile, the men wanted the room cooler.","zh":"女性覺得寒冷；與此同時，男性想房間更涼。"},{"en":"Students were studying in the library; meanwhile, others were playing outside.","zh":"學生在圖書館溫習；與此同時，其他人在外面玩。"},{"en":"This word helps compare two things happening together.","zh":"這個詞幫助比較同時發生的兩件事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in shorts and T-shirts","meaning":"穿着短褲和 T 恤","examples":[{"en":"The men are in shorts and T-shirts while the women feel cold.","zh":"女性覺得冷時，男性卻穿着短褲和 T 恤。"},{"en":"In shorts and T-shirts means wearing light casual clothes for warm conditions.","zh":"in shorts and T-shirts 指穿着適合溫暖環境的輕便休閒衣服。"},{"en":"Some workers were in shorts and T-shirts while others wore jackets indoors.","zh":"有些員工穿着短褲和 T 恤，而其他人在室內穿外套。"},{"en":"If one group is in shorts and T-shirts and another is wrapped in blankets, the temperature may not suit everyone.","zh":"如果一組人穿着短褲和 T 恤，另一組人裹着毛氈，溫度可能不適合所有人。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a clear contrast in comfort.","zh":"這個短語顯示舒適度上的清楚對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be due to","meaning":"由於……","examples":[{"en":"This difference is due to differences in metabolic rates.","zh":"這種差異是由於新陳代謝率不同。"},{"en":"To be due to something means to be caused by it.","zh":"be due to something 指由某事造成。"},{"en":"The delay was due to heavy traffic.","zh":"延誤是由於交通繁忙。"},{"en":"Some discomfort is due to poor chair design.","zh":"有些不適是由於椅子設計不良。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a result with its cause.","zh":"這個短語把結果與原因連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"metabolic rates","meaning":"新陳代謝率","examples":[{"en":"Men and women often have different metabolic rates.","zh":"男性和女性通常有不同的新陳代謝率。"},{"en":"Metabolic rates are the speeds at which bodies use energy.","zh":"metabolic rates 指身體使用能量的速度。"},{"en":"People with different metabolic rates may feel warm or cold at different temperatures.","zh":"新陳代謝率不同的人，在不同溫度下可能感到冷暖不同。"},{"en":"Office temperature settings based on one metabolic rate may not suit everyone.","zh":"以單一新陳代謝率為基準的辦公室溫度設定未必適合所有人。"},{"en":"Understanding metabolic rates can help explain comfort differences at work.","zh":"理解新陳代謝率可以幫助解釋工作時舒適度差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"standard setting","meaning":"標準設定","examples":[{"en":"There is a standard setting for air conditioning.","zh":"冷氣有一個標準設定。"},{"en":"A standard setting is a usual or default level chosen for a machine or system.","zh":"standard setting 指機器或系統通常或預設的水平。"},{"en":"The printer uses a standard setting unless users change it.","zh":"如果使用者不更改，打印機會使用標準設定。"},{"en":"A standard setting for office temperature may not suit everyone.","zh":"辦公室溫度的標準設定未必適合所有人。"},{"en":"Designers should check whether standard settings exclude some users.","zh":"設計師應檢查標準設定是否排除某些使用者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"designed to suit men","meaning":"設計成適合男性","examples":[{"en":"The temperature setting is designed to suit men.","zh":"溫度設定設計成適合男性。"},{"en":"Designed to suit men means planned around men’s bodies, habits, or needs.","zh":"designed to suit men 指以男性身體、習慣或需要為中心而設計。"},{"en":"PPE designed to suit men may not protect women properly.","zh":"設計成適合男性的 PPE 未必能妥善保護女性。"},{"en":"Office temperatures designed to suit men may make many women feel cold.","zh":"設計成適合男性的辦公室溫度可能令許多女性感到寒冷。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a design standard may favour one group.","zh":"這個短語顯示設計標準可能偏向某一群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"turn the air conditioning up or down","meaning":"調高或調低冷氣","examples":[{"en":"In many offices, it is not possible to turn the air conditioning up or down.","zh":"在許多辦公室，不可能調高或調低冷氣。"},{"en":"To turn the air conditioning up or down means to make it stronger, weaker, warmer, or cooler.","zh":"turn the air conditioning up or down 指令冷氣更強、更弱、更暖或更冷。"},{"en":"Workers asked if they could turn the air conditioning down because the room was freezing.","zh":"房間冷得像冰一樣，員工問能否調低冷氣。"},{"en":"People should be able to turn the air conditioning up or down in small meeting rooms.","zh":"人們在小型會議室應能調高或調低冷氣。"},{"en":"If no one can adjust the temperature, comfort problems may continue.","zh":"如果沒有人能調整溫度，舒適度問題可能持續。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"mainly employ women","meaning":"主要僱用女性","examples":[{"en":"Many offices mainly employ women.","zh":"許多辦公室主要僱用女性。"},{"en":"To mainly employ women means to have women as most of the workers.","zh":"mainly employ women 指員工大多數是女性。"},{"en":"A company that mainly employs women should consider women’s comfort and safety needs.","zh":"主要僱用女性的公司應考慮女性的舒適和安全需要。"},{"en":"If an office mainly employs women, its temperature settings should reflect that.","zh":"如果辦公室主要僱用女性，溫度設定應反映這一點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the makeup of a workplace.","zh":"這個短語描述工作場所的人員組成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"wasting energy","meaning":"浪費能源","examples":[{"en":"Some offices are wasting energy by having the air conditioning set too high.","zh":"有些辦公室因冷氣開得太強而浪費能源。"},{"en":"Wasting energy means using more electricity or power than necessary.","zh":"wasting energy 指使用多於所需的電力或能源。"},{"en":"Leaving lights on in empty rooms is wasting energy.","zh":"空房間仍開着燈是在浪費能源。"},{"en":"Offices waste energy when they cool rooms more than workers need.","zh":"當辦公室冷卻程度超過員工需要時，就是浪費能源。"},{"en":"Reducing wasted energy can lower costs and help the environment.","zh":"減少浪費能源可以降低成本並幫助環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"set too high","meaning":"冷氣開得太強","examples":[{"en":"The air conditioning is often set too high.","zh":"冷氣經常開得太強。"},{"en":"Set too high means adjusted to a level that is stronger or greater than needed.","zh":"set too high 指調校到比需要更強或更高的程度。"},{"en":"The volume was set too high, so students could not concentrate.","zh":"音量調得太高，所以學生無法集中。"},{"en":"If the heating is set too high, the room becomes uncomfortable.","zh":"如果暖氣開得太強，房間會變得不舒服。"},{"en":"A setting that is too high can waste energy and reduce comfort.","zh":"設定太高會浪費能源並降低舒適度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"serious consequences","meaning":"嚴重後果","examples":[{"en":"There are serious consequences for designs that ignore users’ needs.","zh":"忽視使用者需要的設計會帶來嚴重後果。"},{"en":"Serious consequences are important and harmful results of an action or decision.","zh":"serious consequences 指某行動或決定帶來的重要而有害結果。"},{"en":"Poor safety design can have serious consequences during an accident.","zh":"安全設計不佳可能在意外中造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"Ignoring disabled users’ needs may lead to serious consequences for their independence.","zh":"忽視殘疾使用者的需要可能對他們的獨立生活造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that the result is not minor.","zh":"這個短語警告結果並非小事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"consider the needs of all users","meaning":"考慮所有使用者的需要","examples":[{"en":"Good design should consider the needs of all users.","zh":"好設計應考慮所有使用者的需要。"},{"en":"To consider the needs of all users means to think about everyone who may use the product.","zh":"consider the needs of all users 指思考所有可能使用產品的人的需要。"},{"en":"A public website should consider the needs of all users, including people with weak eyesight.","zh":"公共網站應考慮所有使用者的需要，包括視力較弱的人。"},{"en":"Designers consider the needs of all users by testing with different age groups.","zh":"設計師透過與不同年齡組別測試，來考慮所有使用者的需要。"},{"en":"Products become fairer when they consider the needs of all users.","zh":"當產品考慮所有使用者的需要，它們會更公平。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a diverse range of people","meaning":"多元化的人群","examples":[{"en":"Inclusive design serves a diverse range of people.","zh":"包容性設計服務多元化的人群。"},{"en":"A diverse range of people means people with many different ages, abilities, cultures, and needs.","zh":"diverse range of people 指有不同年齡、能力、文化和需要的人群。"},{"en":"Public libraries serve a diverse range of people every day.","zh":"公共圖書館每天服務多元化的人群。"},{"en":"A product tested by a diverse range of people is more likely to reveal hidden problems.","zh":"由多元化的人群測試的產品更有可能揭示隱藏問題。"},{"en":"Designing for a diverse range of people makes products more useful in real life.","zh":"為多元化的人群設計，會令產品在現實生活中更有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"without the need for","meaning":"無須……","examples":[{"en":"Products should be accessible without the need for adaptation.","zh":"產品應無須改動即可容易使用。"},{"en":"Without the need for something means without requiring that thing.","zh":"without the need for something 指不需要某事物。"},{"en":"A clear website can be used without the need for extra instructions.","zh":"清楚網站可以無須額外說明就被使用。"},{"en":"A step-free entrance allows access without the need for help from staff.","zh":"無梯級入口讓人無須職員幫助也能進入。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an extra action should not be necessary.","zh":"這個短語顯示額外行動不應是必要的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"catering for","meaning":"照顧……的需要","examples":[{"en":"Universal design includes catering for people with cognitive problems.","zh":"通用設計包括照顧有認知問題人士的需要。"},{"en":"Catering for someone means providing for their needs.","zh":"catering for someone 指照顧或滿足某人的需要。"},{"en":"Schools cater for students with different learning speeds.","zh":"學校照顧學習速度不同學生的需要。"},{"en":"A transport system should cater for wheelchair users and parents with prams.","zh":"交通系統應照顧輪椅使用者和推嬰兒車家長的需要。"},{"en":"Good design caters for real users instead of an imaginary average user.","zh":"好設計照顧真實使用者，而不是想像中的平均使用者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"adjustable","meaning":"可調校的","examples":[{"en":"Desks which are adjustable can help avoid back or neck problems.","zh":"可調校的桌子可以幫助避免背部或頸部問題。"},{"en":"Adjustable means able to be changed in position, height, size, or setting.","zh":"adjustable 指位置、高度、大小或設定可以改變的。"},{"en":"An adjustable chair can fit both tall and short users.","zh":"可調校的椅子可以適合高個子和矮個子使用者。"},{"en":"Adjustable lighting helps people read comfortably at different times of day.","zh":"可調校的燈光幫助人在一天中不同時間舒適閱讀。"},{"en":"Adjustable products are often more inclusive because users can fit them to their needs.","zh":"可調校的產品通常更具包容性，因為使用者可以按需要調整。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"avoiding back or neck problems","meaning":"避免背部或頸部問題","examples":[{"en":"Adjustable desks help people avoid back or neck problems.","zh":"可調校桌子幫助人避免背部或頸部問題。"},{"en":"Avoiding back or neck problems means preventing pain or injury in those areas.","zh":"avoiding back or neck problems 指預防這些部位的疼痛或受傷。"},{"en":"Correct screen height helps workers avoid back or neck problems.","zh":"正確螢幕高度幫助員工避免背部或頸部問題。"},{"en":"Taking short breaks can help students avoid back or neck problems during long study sessions.","zh":"短暫休息可以幫助學生在長時間溫習中避免背部或頸部問題。"},{"en":"Good furniture design supports posture and helps avoid back or neck problems.","zh":"好家具設計支援姿勢，並幫助避免背部或頸部問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"to assist the elderly","meaning":"幫助長者","examples":[{"en":"Designers make changes to assist the elderly.","zh":"設計師作出改變以幫助長者。"},{"en":"To assist the elderly means to help older people use, move, or understand something more easily.","zh":"to assist the elderly 指幫助年長人士更容易使用、移動或理解某事。"},{"en":"Large buttons on phones are used to assist the elderly.","zh":"電話上的大按鈕用來幫助長者。"},{"en":"Clear signs in hospitals assist the elderly when they look for clinics.","zh":"醫院中的清楚標誌幫助長者尋找診所。"},{"en":"Technology designed to assist the elderly can also help many other users.","zh":"為幫助長者而設計的科技，也可以幫助許多其他使用者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"concerned with access","meaning":"關注使用權；關注可達性","examples":[{"en":"Inclusive design is strongly concerned with access.","zh":"包容性設計非常關注使用權。"},{"en":"Concerned with access means focused on whether people can enter, reach, or use something.","zh":"concerned with access 指聚焦人們能否進入、到達或使用某物。"},{"en":"Public transport design is concerned with access for disabled passengers.","zh":"公共交通設計關注殘疾乘客的可達性。"},{"en":"A school website should be concerned with access for students who use screen readers.","zh":"學校網站應關注使用螢幕閱讀器學生的可達性。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that access is a central issue, not a minor detail.","zh":"這個短語顯示使用權是核心問題，而不是小細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"loss of independence","meaning":"失去獨立性","examples":[{"en":"Poor access can lead to a loss of independence for disabled people.","zh":"使用權不足可能導致殘疾人士失去獨立性。"},{"en":"Loss of independence means no longer being able to do things without help.","zh":"loss of independence 指不再能在無幫助下做事。"},{"en":"If a lift is broken every day, wheelchair users may experience a loss of independence.","zh":"如果升降機每天都壞，輪椅使用者可能會失去獨立性。"},{"en":"Poor transport design can cause a loss of independence for older people.","zh":"交通設計不佳可能導致年長人士失去獨立性。"},{"en":"Inclusive design protects people from unnecessary loss of independence.","zh":"包容性設計保護人們免於不必要地失去獨立性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"especially problematic for","meaning":"對……尤其有問題","examples":[{"en":"Seatbelts are especially problematic for pregnant women.","zh":"安全帶對懷孕女性尤其有問題。"},{"en":"Especially problematic for someone means causing particular difficulty or risk for that group.","zh":"especially problematic for someone 指對某群體造成特別困難或風險。"},{"en":"Tiny buttons are especially problematic for people with hand tremors.","zh":"細小按鈕對手震人士尤其有問題。"},{"en":"Low public counters are especially problematic for wheelchair users.","zh":"低矮公共櫃台對輪椅使用者尤其有問題。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the group most affected by a design problem.","zh":"這個短語突出最受設計問題影響的群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"unsuitable because of","meaning":"因……而不合適","examples":[{"en":"PPE jackets are often unsuitable because of the size of women’s shoulders.","zh":"PPE 外套常因女性肩膀尺寸而不合適。"},{"en":"Unsuitable because of something means not appropriate or safe due to that reason.","zh":"unsuitable because of something 指因某原因而不適合或不安全。"},{"en":"A chair may be unsuitable because of its height.","zh":"椅子可能因高度而不合適。"},{"en":"A website can be unsuitable because of small text and low contrast.","zh":"網站可能因文字細小和對比度低而不合適。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly gives the reason why something does not work.","zh":"這個短語清楚給出某物不適用的原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"police officers","meaning":"警務人員","examples":[{"en":"PPE for female police officers dealing with emergencies is often unsuitable.","zh":"處理緊急情況的女性警務人員所用 PPE 常常不合適。"},{"en":"Police officers are people whose job is to enforce the law and protect the public.","zh":"police officers 指負責執法和保護公眾的人。"},{"en":"Police officers need equipment that fits well and allows quick movement.","zh":"警務人員需要合身並容許快速移動的裝備。"},{"en":"Female police officers may face extra risk if body armour is designed for men.","zh":"如果防護裝備按男性設計，女性警務人員可能面對額外風險。"},{"en":"Police officers dealing with danger should not be slowed by poor equipment.","zh":"處理危險的警務人員不應被差劣裝備拖慢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"dealing with emergencies","meaning":"處理緊急情況","examples":[{"en":"Police officers dealing with emergencies need properly fitting PPE.","zh":"處理緊急情況的警務人員需要合身的 PPE。"},{"en":"Dealing with emergencies means responding to urgent, dangerous, or unexpected situations.","zh":"dealing with emergencies 指應對緊急、危險或意外情況。"},{"en":"Firefighters dealing with emergencies must move quickly and safely.","zh":"處理緊急情況的消防員必須快速而安全地移動。"},{"en":"Equipment for people dealing with emergencies must not restrict movement.","zh":"處理緊急情況的人所用裝備不可限制動作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work where speed, safety, and clear action are essential.","zh":"這個短語描述速度、安全和清晰行動都很重要的工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"comfort in the workplace","meaning":"工作場所的舒適度","examples":[{"en":"Air-conditioning settings affect comfort in the workplace.","zh":"冷氣設定影響工作場所的舒適度。"},{"en":"Comfort in the workplace means how physically and mentally comfortable employees feel while working.","zh":"comfort in the workplace 指員工工作時身體和心理感到舒適的程度。"},{"en":"Good lighting improves comfort in the workplace.","zh":"良好照明能改善工作場所的舒適度。"},{"en":"Poor temperature control can reduce comfort in the workplace.","zh":"溫度控制不佳會降低工作場所的舒適度。"},{"en":"Comfort in the workplace matters because uncomfortable workers may be less productive.","zh":"工作場所的舒適度很重要，因為不舒服的員工可能生產力較低。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"temperature in offices","meaning":"辦公室溫度","examples":[{"en":"The temperature in offices is often too low for women.","zh":"辦公室溫度對女性來說常常太低。"},{"en":"Temperature in offices means how warm or cold office spaces are.","zh":"temperature in offices 指辦公室空間的冷暖程度。"},{"en":"The temperature in offices should suit the people who work there.","zh":"辦公室溫度應適合在那裡工作的人。"},{"en":"If the temperature in offices is too low, workers may wear jackets indoors.","zh":"如果辦公室溫度太低，員工可能在室內穿外套。"},{"en":"Managing temperature in offices well can improve comfort and save energy.","zh":"妥善管理辦公室溫度可以改善舒適度並節省能源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 3 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"ielts/listening/Practice 4/task-1":[{"front":"asking a friend for advice on","meaning":"向朋友詢問關於……的建議","examples":[{"en":"A man is asking a friend for advice on things to do in the city.","zh":"一名男子正向朋友詢問關於城中可做活動的建議。"},{"en":"Asking a friend for advice on something means requesting their suggestions or opinions about that topic.","zh":"Asking a friend for advice on 某事，指就該主題請朋友提供建議或意見。"},{"en":"Mia is asking a friend for advice on where to buy a birthday gift.","zh":"Mia 正向朋友詢問關於在哪裏買生日禮物的建議。"},{"en":"People ask friends for advice when they trust their experience.","zh":"人們信任朋友的經驗時，會向朋友詢問建議。"},{"en":"Asking for advice can help you avoid mistakes and make better plans.","zh":"詢問建議可以幫助你避免錯誤並作出更好計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"things to do in the city","meaning":"城中可做的活動","examples":[{"en":"He wants advice on things to do in the city with visitors.","zh":"他想知道和訪客一起在城中可做的活動。"},{"en":"Things to do in the city are activities, places, and experiences people can enjoy there.","zh":"城中可做的活動，是人們可以在城市中享受的活動、地點和體驗。"},{"en":"Museums, markets, parks, and walking tours are things to do in the city.","zh":"博物館、市集、公園和步行導賞團都是城中可做的活動。"},{"en":"Visitors need different things to do depending on their age, budget, and interests.","zh":"訪客需要哪些活動，取決於他們的年齡、預算和興趣。"},{"en":"A good city plan includes indoor and outdoor activities.","zh":"好的城市行程應包括室內和戶外活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a family of visitors","meaning":"來訪的一家人","examples":[{"en":"He needs ideas for entertaining a family of visitors.","zh":"他需要一些招待來訪一家人的點子。"},{"en":"A family of visitors is a group of visiting relatives or guests who are members of one family.","zh":"A family of visitors 指來探訪的一家親戚或客人。"},{"en":"A family of visitors may include adults, children, and older relatives.","zh":"來訪的一家人可能包括成人、孩子和年長親戚。"},{"en":"Planning for a family of visitors can be difficult because everyone may like different things.","zh":"為來訪的一家人安排行程可能很困難，因為每個人興趣不同。"},{"en":"Family-friendly activities are useful when entertaining a family of visitors.","zh":"招待來訪的一家人時，適合一家大小的活動很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"I seem to remember","meaning":"我好像記得","examples":[{"en":"I seem to remember you had some family visitors staying with you recently.","zh":"我好像記得你最近有家人來探訪並暫住在你那裏。"},{"en":"“I seem to remember” means I think I remember something, but I am not completely certain.","zh":"「I seem to remember」表示我好像記得某事，但並非完全肯定。"},{"en":"I seem to remember that the museum is closed on Mondays.","zh":"我好像記得博物館逢星期一休館。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when checking a memory politely.","zh":"人們想有禮貌地確認記憶時會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It sounds less direct than saying “I remember exactly.”","zh":"它比說「我確實記得」語氣較不肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"family visitors","meaning":"來訪的家人","examples":[{"en":"Sandra had some family visitors staying with her recently.","zh":"Sandra 最近有一些家人來探訪並暫住在她那裏。"},{"en":"Family visitors are relatives who come to stay with or visit someone.","zh":"Family visitors 指來探訪或暫住的親戚。"},{"en":"My family visitors arrived on Friday and stayed for the weekend.","zh":"我的來訪家人星期五到達，並逗留了一個週末。"},{"en":"Family visitors may need accommodation, meals, and activities.","zh":"來訪的家人可能需要住宿、膳食和活動安排。"},{"en":"Having family visitors can be enjoyable, but it also requires planning.","zh":"有家人來訪可以很愉快，但也需要計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"staying with you","meaning":"暫住在你那裏","examples":[{"en":"You had some family visitors staying with you recently.","zh":"最近有一些家人暫住在你那裏。"},{"en":"Staying with you means living temporarily in your home as a guest.","zh":"Staying with you 指作為客人暫時住在你家中。"},{"en":"My aunt is staying with us while she visits the city.","zh":"我姨姨探訪這個城市時暫住在我們家。"},{"en":"If guests are staying with you, you may need extra beds and meals.","zh":"如果客人暫住在你那裏，你可能需要額外床位和膳食。"},{"en":"People staying with you may share your daily routine for a short time.","zh":"暫住在你那裏的人可能短時間內與你共享日常生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"recently","meaning":"最近","examples":[{"en":"My brother and his family were here recently.","zh":"我的哥哥和他的家人最近來過這裏。"},{"en":"Recently means not long ago or during the near past.","zh":"Recently 指不久之前或在近來。"},{"en":"I recently visited a new café near the station.","zh":"我最近去了車站附近一間新咖啡店。"},{"en":"Something that happened recently is still fresh in people’s memory.","zh":"最近發生的事情通常仍令人記憶猶新。"},{"en":"The exact time is not always stated when we use “recently.”","zh":"使用 recently 時，不一定說明確實時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a couple of months ago","meaning":"幾個月前","examples":[{"en":"My brother and his family were here a couple of months ago.","zh":"我的哥哥和他的家人幾個月前來過這裏。"},{"en":"A couple of months ago means about two months before now.","zh":"A couple of months ago 指大約兩個月前。"},{"en":"We moved into this flat a couple of months ago.","zh":"我們幾個月前搬進這個單位。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when the exact date is not important.","zh":"當確實日期不重要時，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"An event from a couple of months ago may still affect current plans.","zh":"幾個月前發生的事情可能仍會影響現在的計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"I wanted to ask your advice","meaning":"我想問問你的意見","examples":[{"en":"I wanted to ask your advice about where to take my visitors.","zh":"我想問問你的意見，應該帶我的訪客去哪裏。"},{"en":"“I wanted to ask your advice” politely introduces a request for someone’s opinion.","zh":"「I wanted to ask your advice」有禮貌地引出請求對方提供意見。"},{"en":"I wanted to ask your advice about choosing a hotel.","zh":"我想問問你關於選酒店的意見。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds polite because it prepares the listener before asking.","zh":"這個短語先讓聽者有心理準備，所以聽起來有禮貌。"},{"en":"People often ask advice from someone who has useful experience.","zh":"人們常向有相關經驗的人請教意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"I’ve got someone visiting","meaning":"有某人要來探訪我","examples":[{"en":"I’ve got my cousin and her family visiting next month.","zh":"我下個月有表姐和她的家人來探訪我。"},{"en":"“I’ve got someone visiting” means someone is coming to see or stay with me.","zh":"「I’ve got someone visiting」指有人要來看我或暫住在我這裏。"},{"en":"I’ve got my parents visiting this weekend.","zh":"我這個週末有父母來探訪。"},{"en":"When someone is visiting, the host may need to plan accommodation and activities.","zh":"當有人來探訪時，主人可能需要安排住宿和活動。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and common in everyday conversation.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常見於日常對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have no idea","meaning":"完全不知道","examples":[{"en":"I have no idea where to take them.","zh":"我完全不知道該帶他們去哪裏。"},{"en":"To have no idea means to not know something at all.","zh":"Have no idea 指完全不知道某事。"},{"en":"I have no idea which restaurant they would like.","zh":"我完全不知道他們會喜歡哪間餐廳。"},{"en":"People often ask for advice when they have no idea what to do.","zh":"當人們完全不知道該怎樣做時，常會尋求建議。"},{"en":"The phrase shows complete uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語表示完全不確定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"where to take them","meaning":"帶他們去哪裏","examples":[{"en":"I have no idea where to take them.","zh":"我完全不知道帶他們去哪裏。"},{"en":"Where to take them means which places to bring visitors to.","zh":"Where to take them 指帶訪客去哪些地方。"},{"en":"If the children like science, I know where to take them.","zh":"如果孩子喜歡科學，我知道該帶他們去哪裏。"},{"en":"Choosing where to take visitors depends on weather, budget, and interests.","zh":"選擇帶訪客去哪裏取決於天氣、預算和興趣。"},{"en":"Good hosts think about where to take guests before they arrive.","zh":"好主人會在客人到達前思考帶他們去哪裏。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"What about accommodation?","meaning":"住宿方面呢？","examples":[{"en":"What about accommodation for your cousin’s family?","zh":"你表姐一家人的住宿方面呢？"},{"en":"“What about accommodation?” asks whether a place to stay has been arranged.","zh":"「What about accommodation?」是詢問是否已安排住宿地方。"},{"en":"You have planned the tours, but what about accommodation?","zh":"你已計劃導賞團，但住宿方面呢？"},{"en":"The question introduces another practical issue to consider.","zh":"這個問題引出另一個需要考慮的實際事項。"},{"en":"It is useful when planning trips for visitors.","zh":"為訪客計劃旅程時，這句話很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"accommodation","meaning":"住宿","examples":[{"en":"My cousin needs accommodation in the city.","zh":"我表姐需要在城中找住宿。"},{"en":"Accommodation means a place where people can stay, such as a hotel, flat, or guesthouse.","zh":"Accommodation 指人們可以暫住的地方，例如酒店、單位或旅館。"},{"en":"The family booked accommodation near the station.","zh":"那家人在車站附近預訂了住宿。"},{"en":"Good accommodation should be safe, clean, and convenient.","zh":"好的住宿應安全、乾淨和方便。"},{"en":"Accommodation can be expensive during busy holiday periods.","zh":"旅遊旺季期間，住宿可能很昂貴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stay with you in your flat","meaning":"住在你單位","examples":[{"en":"Are they going to stay with you in your flat?","zh":"他們會住在你單位嗎？"},{"en":"To stay with you in your flat means to live temporarily in your apartment as your guests.","zh":"Stay with you in your flat 指作為你的客人暫時住在你的單位。"},{"en":"My cousins stayed with me in my flat for three nights.","zh":"我的表親在我單位住了三晚。"},{"en":"Guests staying in a small flat may make the space feel crowded.","zh":"客人住在小單位裏，可能令空間顯得擠迫。"},{"en":"If people cannot stay in your flat, a hotel may be better.","zh":"如果別人不能住在你單位，酒店可能較好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"thankfully","meaning":"幸好","examples":[{"en":"No, thankfully, they are not staying in my flat.","zh":"不，幸好他們不會住在我的單位。"},{"en":"Thankfully means fortunately or luckily, especially because a problem has been avoided.","zh":"Thankfully 指幸運地，尤其是因為避免了一個問題。"},{"en":"Thankfully, the train arrived before the storm began.","zh":"幸好火車在暴風雨開始前到達。"},{"en":"People use “thankfully” when they feel relieved about a situation.","zh":"人們對某情況感到鬆一口氣時會使用 thankfully。"},{"en":"It often introduces good news after a possible worry.","zh":"它常在可能令人擔心的事情後，引出好消息。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"there wouldn’t be room","meaning":"沒有足夠空間","examples":[{"en":"There wouldn’t be room for my cousin’s family in my flat.","zh":"我的單位沒有足夠空間容納表姐一家。"},{"en":"There wouldn’t be room means there would not be enough space.","zh":"There wouldn’t be room 指沒有足夠空間。"},{"en":"There wouldn’t be room for six guests in one small bedroom.","zh":"一間小睡房沒有足夠空間容納六位客人。"},{"en":"If there is not enough room, visitors may feel uncomfortable.","zh":"如果空間不足，訪客可能會不舒服。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when explaining why accommodation is impossible.","zh":"這個短語適合用來解釋為何無法安排住宿。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recommend a hotel","meaning":"推薦一間酒店","examples":[{"en":"My cousin wants me to recommend a hotel.","zh":"我表姐想我推薦一間酒店。"},{"en":"To recommend a hotel means to suggest a hotel that you think is suitable.","zh":"Recommend a hotel 指建議一間你認為合適的酒店。"},{"en":"Can you recommend a hotel near the train station?","zh":"你可以推薦一間火車站附近的酒店嗎？"},{"en":"People usually recommend hotels based on price, location, and comfort.","zh":"人們通常根據價格、位置和舒適度推薦酒店。"},{"en":"A good recommendation can save visitors time and worry.","zh":"好推薦可以為訪客節省時間和煩惱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I do actually","meaning":"其實我是知道的","examples":[{"en":"Yes, I do actually know a good hotel.","zh":"是的，其實我是知道一間好酒店的。"},{"en":"“I do actually” emphasises that something is true, especially when it may be unexpected.","zh":"「I do actually」強調某事是真的，尤其是當它可能有點意外時。"},{"en":"I do actually remember the name of that restaurant.","zh":"其實我真的記得那間餐廳的名字。"},{"en":"The phrase often corrects an assumption that the speaker may not know something.","zh":"這個短語常用來糾正別人以為說話者不知道某事的想法。"},{"en":"It sounds conversational and slightly emphatic.","zh":"它聽起來口語化，並帶有少許強調。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"about five minutes’ walk from","meaning":"離……步行大約五分鐘","examples":[{"en":"The hotel is about five minutes’ walk from Murray Station.","zh":"酒店離 Murray Station 步行大約五分鐘。"},{"en":"About five minutes’ walk from a place means it takes roughly five minutes to walk there from that place.","zh":"About five minutes’ walk from 某地，指從該地步行到那裏大約需五分鐘。"},{"en":"The café is about five minutes’ walk from the museum.","zh":"咖啡店離博物館步行大約五分鐘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for explaining location and convenience.","zh":"這個短語適合用來說明位置和方便程度。"},{"en":"“About” shows that the walking time is approximate.","zh":"About 表示步行時間是大約估計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"nice and central","meaning":"地點方便，在市中心","examples":[{"en":"The hotel is nice and central.","zh":"這間酒店很好，而且位於市中心，地點方便。"},{"en":"Nice and central means pleasant and located conveniently near the middle of a city or area.","zh":"Nice and central 指環境不錯，而且位置方便，接近城市或地區中心。"},{"en":"The flat is nice and central, so we can walk to most attractions.","zh":"這個單位不錯又在市中心，所以我們可以步行到大部分景點。"},{"en":"A central hotel is useful for visitors who do not know the city well.","zh":"市中心酒店對不熟悉城市的訪客很有用。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds informal and positive.","zh":"這個短語聽起來口語而正面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on George Street","meaning":"位於 George Street","examples":[{"en":"The hotel is on George Street.","zh":"酒店位於 George Street。"},{"en":"On George Street means located along or at an address on George Street.","zh":"On George Street 指位於 George Street 這條街上。"},{"en":"The theatre is on George Street, near the market.","zh":"劇院位於 George Street，靠近市場。"},{"en":"Giving the street name helps visitors find the place more easily.","zh":"提供街名可以幫助訪客更容易找到地方。"},{"en":"If a place is on a main street, it may be convenient for transport.","zh":"如果一個地方位於主要街道上，交通可能較方便。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a tight budget","meaning":"預算頗緊絀","examples":[{"en":"They are on quite a tight budget.","zh":"他們的預算頗緊絀。"},{"en":"A tight budget means there is not much money available to spend.","zh":"A tight budget 指可花費的金錢不多。"},{"en":"We chose a small hotel because we were on a tight budget.","zh":"因為預算緊絀，我們選擇了一間小酒店。"},{"en":"People on a tight budget need to compare prices carefully.","zh":"預算緊絀的人需要仔細比較價格。"},{"en":"A tight budget does not mean the trip cannot be enjoyable.","zh":"預算緊絀並不表示旅程不能愉快。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"how much roughly","meaning":"大約多少錢","examples":[{"en":"How much roughly is it to stay there?","zh":"住在那裏大約多少錢？"},{"en":"“How much roughly?” asks for an approximate price, not an exact amount.","zh":"「How much roughly?」用來詢問大約價格，而不是確實金額。"},{"en":"How much roughly is a taxi from the station to the hotel?","zh":"從車站坐的士到酒店大約多少錢？"},{"en":"People ask this when planning a budget before making a booking.","zh":"人們在預訂前計劃預算時會這樣問。"},{"en":"“Roughly” shows that an estimated answer is acceptable.","zh":"Roughly 表示估計答案已可以接受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"book a family room","meaning":"預訂家庭房","examples":[{"en":"If you book a family room, it is about £125 per night.","zh":"如果你預訂家庭房，每晚大約 125 英鎊。"},{"en":"To book a family room means to reserve a hotel room suitable for a family.","zh":"Book a family room 指預訂適合一家人入住的酒店房間。"},{"en":"We booked a family room with two beds and a sofa bed.","zh":"我們預訂了一間有兩張床和一張梳化床的家庭房。"},{"en":"Booking a family room may be cheaper than booking several separate rooms.","zh":"預訂家庭房可能比預訂幾間獨立房間便宜。"},{"en":"Always check how many people the family room can sleep.","zh":"應經常檢查家庭房可容納多少人入住。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"family room","meaning":"家庭房","examples":[{"en":"A family room costs about £125 per night.","zh":"家庭房每晚大約 125 英鎊。"},{"en":"A family room is a hotel room designed for parents and children or several family members.","zh":"家庭房是為父母與孩子或幾位家庭成員而設的酒店房間。"},{"en":"The family room had two beds, a small table, and extra towels.","zh":"家庭房有兩張床、一張小桌子和額外毛巾。"},{"en":"A family room can help parents keep children in the same space.","zh":"家庭房可以幫助父母讓孩子留在同一空間。"},{"en":"Family rooms may sell out quickly during school holidays.","zh":"學校假期期間，家庭房可能很快訂滿。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"per night","meaning":"每晚","examples":[{"en":"The family room costs about £125 per night.","zh":"家庭房每晚大約 125 英鎊。"},{"en":"Per night means for each night of staying somewhere.","zh":"Per night 指每住一晚。"},{"en":"The hotel charges £80 per night for a single room.","zh":"酒店單人房每晚收費 80 英鎊。"},{"en":"To find the total cost, multiply the price per night by the number of nights.","zh":"要計算總費用，把每晚價格乘以住宿晚數。"},{"en":"Prices per night may be higher at weekends.","zh":"週末每晚價格可能較高。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"double rooms","meaning":"雙人房","examples":[{"en":"My brother paid for two double rooms.","zh":"我哥哥訂了兩間雙人房。"},{"en":"Double rooms are hotel rooms designed for two people, usually with one large bed or two beds.","zh":"雙人房是為兩人入住而設的酒店房間，通常有一張大床或兩張床。"},{"en":"The couple booked a double room near the theatre.","zh":"那對夫婦在劇院附近預訂了一間雙人房。"},{"en":"Two double rooms may be useful when a family needs more space.","zh":"當一家人需要更多空間時，兩間雙人房可能很有用。"},{"en":"Always check whether a double room has one bed or twin beds.","zh":"應檢查雙人房是一張床還是兩張床。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the end","meaning":"最後","examples":[{"en":"My brother paid for two double rooms in the end.","zh":"我哥哥最後訂了兩間雙人房。"},{"en":"In the end means finally, after considering or trying other possibilities.","zh":"In the end 指經過考慮或嘗試其他可能後，最終結果如何。"},{"en":"We looked at several hotels, but in the end we chose the cheapest one.","zh":"我們看了幾間酒店，但最後選了最便宜的一間。"},{"en":"The phrase often introduces the final decision or result.","zh":"這個短語常引出最後決定或結果。"},{"en":"What happens in the end may be different from the original plan.","zh":"最後發生的事可能與原本計劃不同。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"around £95 for each room","meaning":"每間房大約 95 英鎊","examples":[{"en":"Each double room was around £95.","zh":"每間雙人房大約 95 英鎊。"},{"en":"Around £95 for each room means each room cost approximately ninety-five pounds.","zh":"Around £95 for each room 指每間房大約收費九十五英鎊。"},{"en":"The hotel charges around £95 for each room on weekdays.","zh":"這間酒店平日每間房大約收費 95 英鎊。"},{"en":"“Around” shows the price is approximate, not exact.","zh":"Around 表示價格是大約，而不是精確。"},{"en":"Knowing the price for each room helps calculate the total cost.","zh":"知道每間房價格，有助計算總費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"that’s not too bad","meaning":"那還不算太差","examples":[{"en":"Oh, that’s not too bad.","zh":"哦，那還不算太差。"},{"en":"“That’s not too bad” means something is acceptable or better than expected.","zh":"「That’s not too bad」表示某事可以接受，或比預期好。"},{"en":"£95 for a central hotel? That’s not too bad.","zh":"市中心酒店 95 英鎊？那還不算太差。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when a price, result, or situation is reasonable.","zh":"當價格、結果或情況算合理時，人們會使用這句話。"},{"en":"It is positive, but not as strong as saying “that’s excellent.”","zh":"它是正面的，但不及「非常好」那麼強烈。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"organise some trips","meaning":"安排一些行程","examples":[{"en":"I want to organise some trips while they are here.","zh":"我想在他們逗留期間安排一些行程。"},{"en":"To organise some trips means to plan visits or journeys for people.","zh":"Organise some trips 指為人們計劃探訪或旅程。"},{"en":"Sandra organised some day trips for her relatives.","zh":"Sandra 為親戚安排了一些一日遊行程。"},{"en":"Organising trips requires checking times, costs, transport, and weather.","zh":"安排行程需要查看時間、費用、交通和天氣。"},{"en":"Good trips can help visitors enjoy a city without feeling rushed.","zh":"好行程可以幫助訪客享受城市，而不會感到匆忙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"while they’re here","meaning":"在他們逗留期間","examples":[{"en":"I want to organise some trips while they’re here.","zh":"我想在他們逗留期間安排一些行程。"},{"en":"While they’re here means during the period when the visitors are staying or visiting.","zh":"While they’re here 指訪客停留或探訪的那段時間。"},{"en":"We should visit the market while they’re here.","zh":"他們逗留期間，我們應該去市集。"},{"en":"The phrase helps connect plans to a limited visiting period.","zh":"這個短語把計劃與有限的探訪時間連接起來。"},{"en":"Activities must fit the days while the visitors are here.","zh":"活動必須配合訪客逗留的日子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"I was thinking of doing","meaning":"我原本想……","examples":[{"en":"I was thinking of doing a bus tour of the city centre.","zh":"我原本想參加市中心巴士觀光團。"},{"en":"“I was thinking of doing” introduces a plan or idea that someone is considering.","zh":"「I was thinking of doing」用來引出某人正在考慮的計劃或想法。"},{"en":"I was thinking of booking a walking tour for Saturday.","zh":"我原本想預訂星期六的步行導賞團。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds open to discussion rather than final.","zh":"這個短語聽起來像可以討論，而不是最終決定。"},{"en":"People use it when they want advice on a possible plan.","zh":"人們想就可能的計劃尋求意見時會使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a bus tour of the city centre","meaning":"市中心巴士觀光團","examples":[{"en":"I was thinking of doing a bus tour of the city centre.","zh":"我原本想參加市中心巴士觀光團。"},{"en":"A bus tour of the city centre is a sightseeing trip around central areas by bus.","zh":"市中心巴士觀光團是乘巴士遊覽城市中心地區的觀光行程。"},{"en":"A bus tour of the city centre is useful for visitors who cannot walk far.","zh":"市中心巴士觀光團適合不便走太遠的訪客。"},{"en":"Bus tours often include recorded information about famous buildings.","zh":"巴士觀光團常包括關於著名建築的錄音講解。"},{"en":"A bus tour can show many places quickly, but it may feel less personal than walking.","zh":"巴士觀光團可以快速展示很多地方，但可能不如步行親切。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"city centre","meaning":"市中心","examples":[{"en":"The visitors have not been to the city centre before.","zh":"這些訪客以前沒有去過市中心。"},{"en":"The city centre is the main central area of a city, often with shops, offices, transport, and attractions.","zh":"市中心是城市的主要中央地區，通常有商店、辦公室、交通和景點。"},{"en":"The hotel is close to the city centre.","zh":"酒店靠近市中心。"},{"en":"Visitors often begin their trip in the city centre because many sights are nearby.","zh":"訪客常從市中心開始旅程，因為許多景點都在附近。"},{"en":"City centres can be busy, especially at weekends.","zh":"市中心可能很繁忙，尤其在週末。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"none of them have been here before","meaning":"他們全都未來過這裏","examples":[{"en":"I want to show them the city because none of them have been here before.","zh":"我想帶他們看看這座城市，因為他們全都未來過這裏。"},{"en":"“None of them have been here before” means not one person in the group has visited this place previously.","zh":"「None of them have been here before」指這個群組中沒有任何人以前來過這裏。"},{"en":"None of them have been here before, so we should start with the main sights.","zh":"他們全都未來過這裏，所以我們應先從主要景點開始。"},{"en":"First-time visitors usually need clear directions and simple plans.","zh":"第一次來的訪客通常需要清楚方向和簡單計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why a basic introduction to the city is useful.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何基本城市介紹很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"quite expensive","meaning":"頗昂貴","examples":[{"en":"Those bus tours are quite expensive.","zh":"那些巴士觀光團頗昂貴。"},{"en":"Quite expensive means fairly costly, but not necessarily impossible to afford.","zh":"Quite expensive 指相當昂貴，但不一定完全負擔不起。"},{"en":"The restaurant is quite expensive, so we only go there on special days.","zh":"那間餐廳頗昂貴，所以我們只在特別日子去。"},{"en":"If an activity is quite expensive, families may look for cheaper alternatives.","zh":"如果活動頗昂貴，家庭可能會尋找較便宜選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses concern about price without saying it is completely unaffordable.","zh":"這個短語表示對價格的擔憂，但沒有說完全負擔不起。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"it’s better to do","meaning":"做……會更好","examples":[{"en":"I think it’s better to do a walking tour.","zh":"我認為參加步行導賞團會更好。"},{"en":"“It’s better to do” introduces an action the speaker thinks is a wiser or more suitable choice.","zh":"「It’s better to do」用來引出說話者認為較明智或較合適的行動。"},{"en":"It’s better to book early if the theatre is popular.","zh":"如果劇院很受歡迎，提早預訂會更好。"},{"en":"The phrase compares one option with another.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個選擇。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving advice based on experience.","zh":"根據經驗給建議時，這個說法很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a walking tour","meaning":"步行導賞團","examples":[{"en":"A walking tour gives you a better feel for the city.","zh":"步行導賞團讓你更能感受這座城市。"},{"en":"A walking tour is a guided visit where people explore a place on foot.","zh":"步行導賞團是人們步行探索某地的導賞活動。"},{"en":"We joined a walking tour of the old town.","zh":"我們參加了舊城區的步行導賞團。"},{"en":"Walking tours help visitors notice streets, shops, and small details.","zh":"步行導賞團幫助訪客注意街道、商店和小細節。"},{"en":"A walking tour is best when the weather is comfortable.","zh":"天氣舒適時，步行導賞團最合適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"give you a much better feel for","meaning":"讓你更能感受……","examples":[{"en":"A walking tour gives you a much better feel for the city.","zh":"步行導賞團讓你更能感受這座城市。"},{"en":"To give you a better feel for something means to help you understand its atmosphere and character.","zh":"Give you a better feel for 某事，指幫助你了解它的氣氛和特色。"},{"en":"Walking through the market gives visitors a better feel for local life.","zh":"穿過市場可以讓訪客更能感受本地生活。"},{"en":"Personal experience often gives a better feel for a place than reading about it.","zh":"親身體驗通常比閱讀資料更能感受一個地方。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on atmosphere, not just facts.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於氣氛，而不只是事實。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a feel for the city","meaning":"對城市的感覺","examples":[{"en":"The walking tour gives visitors a feel for the city.","zh":"步行導賞團讓訪客對城市有感覺。"},{"en":"A feel for the city means an understanding of its atmosphere, people, streets, and character.","zh":"A feel for the city 指對城市氣氛、人、街道和特色的理解。"},{"en":"After one afternoon walking around, I got a feel for the city.","zh":"步行遊覽一個下午後，我對這座城市有了感覺。"},{"en":"Visitors need time in local areas to get a real feel for the city.","zh":"訪客需要在本地區域花時間，才能真正感受城市。"},{"en":"A feel for a city cannot come only from looking at a map.","zh":"只看地圖無法真正獲得對城市的感覺。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"starts from","meaning":"從……開始","examples":[{"en":"The walking tour starts from Carlton Square.","zh":"步行導賞團從 Carlton Square 開始。"},{"en":"Starts from means begins at a particular place.","zh":"Starts from 指從某個特定地點開始。"},{"en":"The bus tour starts from the main station.","zh":"巴士觀光團從主要車站開始。"},{"en":"Knowing where a tour starts from helps visitors arrive on time.","zh":"知道導賞團從哪裏開始，可以幫助訪客準時到達。"},{"en":"A clear starting point prevents people from getting lost.","zh":"清楚的起點可以防止人們迷路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"takes a couple of hours","meaning":"需時幾個小時","examples":[{"en":"The walking tour takes a couple of hours.","zh":"步行導賞團需時幾個小時。"},{"en":"Takes a couple of hours means needs about two hours to finish.","zh":"Takes a couple of hours 指完成大約需要兩小時。"},{"en":"The museum visit takes a couple of hours if you see every gallery.","zh":"如果參觀每個展廳，博物館之旅需時幾個小時。"},{"en":"Visitors should wear comfortable shoes for an activity that takes a couple of hours.","zh":"參加需時幾個小時的活動時，訪客應穿舒適鞋。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate time, not an exact length.","zh":"這個短語提供大約時間，而不是確實長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"doesn’t cost that much","meaning":"費用不算高","examples":[{"en":"The walking tour doesn’t cost that much.","zh":"步行導賞團費用不算高。"},{"en":"Doesn’t cost that much means is not very expensive.","zh":"Doesn’t cost that much 指不是很昂貴。"},{"en":"The local ferry ride does not cost that much.","zh":"本地渡輪旅程費用不算高。"},{"en":"An activity that does not cost much is useful for visitors on a tight budget.","zh":"費用不高的活動適合預算緊絀的訪客。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the cost with what someone might expect.","zh":"這個短語把費用與人們可能預期的價格作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Sounds good.","meaning":"聽起來不錯。","examples":[{"en":"Sounds good. I’ll look that up.","zh":"聽起來不錯。我會查一下。"},{"en":"“Sounds good” means the idea seems suitable, pleasant, or worth trying.","zh":"「Sounds good」表示這個想法看來合適、愉快或值得嘗試。"},{"en":"“We could visit the old fort.” “Sounds good.”","zh":"「我們可以參觀古堡。」「聽起來不錯。」"},{"en":"The phrase is a short, friendly way to show approval.","zh":"這個短語是簡短而友善地表示認同的方法。"},{"en":"It does not mean the speaker has already made a final decision.","zh":"它不表示說話者已經作出最終決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"look that up","meaning":"查一下","examples":[{"en":"I’ll look that up later.","zh":"我稍後會查一下。"},{"en":"To look something up means to search for information about it.","zh":"Look something up 指搜尋關於某事的資料。"},{"en":"I’ll look up the museum opening hours online.","zh":"我會在網上查一下博物館開放時間。"},{"en":"Looking something up helps confirm details before making plans.","zh":"查資料有助在制定計劃前確認細節。"},{"en":"You can look up prices, locations, and reviews before booking.","zh":"預訂前，你可以查價格、地點和評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"If the weather’s nice","meaning":"如果天氣好的話","examples":[{"en":"If the weather’s nice, you could visit the old fort.","zh":"如果天氣好的話，你可以參觀古堡。"},{"en":"“If the weather’s nice” introduces a plan that depends on good weather.","zh":"「If the weather’s nice」用來引出取決於好天氣的計劃。"},{"en":"If the weather’s nice, we can eat lunch in the park.","zh":"如果天氣好的話，我們可以在公園吃午餐。"},{"en":"Outdoor activities are easier to enjoy when the weather is nice.","zh":"天氣好時，戶外活動較容易享受。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when making flexible travel plans.","zh":"制定彈性旅遊計劃時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"one thing you could do is","meaning":"你可以做的一件事是","examples":[{"en":"One thing you could do is visit the old fort.","zh":"你可以做的一件事是參觀古堡。"},{"en":"“One thing you could do is” introduces a possible suggestion.","zh":"「One thing you could do is」用來引出一個可能建議。"},{"en":"One thing you could do is take them to the market.","zh":"你可以做的一件事是帶他們去市場。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds helpful because it offers an option rather than an order.","zh":"這個短語提供選項而不是命令，所以聽起來有幫助。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving advice without being too forceful.","zh":"當你想給建議但不想太強硬時，這句話很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"visit the old fort","meaning":"參觀古堡","examples":[{"en":"You could visit the old fort if the weather is nice.","zh":"如果天氣好，你可以參觀古堡。"},{"en":"To visit the old fort means to go and see a historic defensive building.","zh":"Visit the old fort 指去參觀一座歷史防禦建築。"},{"en":"Families can visit the old fort and learn about the city’s past.","zh":"家庭可以參觀古堡，了解城市過去。"},{"en":"Old forts often have walls, towers, and views over the sea or city.","zh":"古堡通常有城牆、塔樓，以及海景或城市景觀。"},{"en":"Visiting historic places can make a trip more memorable.","zh":"參觀歷史地方可以令旅程更難忘。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get there by boat","meaning":"乘船前往那裏","examples":[{"en":"You can get there by boat.","zh":"你可以乘船前往那裏。"},{"en":"To get there by boat means to travel to that place using a boat.","zh":"Get there by boat 指乘船到達該地。"},{"en":"Visitors get to the island by boat from the harbour.","zh":"訪客從港口乘船前往小島。"},{"en":"Travelling by boat can make a trip feel more special.","zh":"乘船出行可以令旅程感覺更特別。"},{"en":"Check the boat timetable before planning the visit.","zh":"計劃參觀前，應查看船期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the whole trip","meaning":"整個行程","examples":[{"en":"The whole trip takes half a day.","zh":"整個行程需時半日。"},{"en":"The whole trip means the complete journey or activity from start to finish.","zh":"The whole trip 指由開始到結束的完整旅程或活動。"},{"en":"The whole trip includes the boat ride, the visit, and the return journey.","zh":"整個行程包括船程、參觀和回程。"},{"en":"Knowing the length of the whole trip helps visitors plan meals and rest.","zh":"知道整個行程需時多久，可以幫助訪客安排用餐和休息。"},{"en":"A short visit may become a long day when the whole trip is counted.","zh":"計算整個行程後，短暫參觀也可能變成半天活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"takes half a day","meaning":"需時半日","examples":[{"en":"The whole trip takes half a day.","zh":"整個行程需時半日。"},{"en":"Takes half a day means needs about half of one day to complete.","zh":"Takes half a day 指完成大約需要半天時間。"},{"en":"The boat tour takes half a day, so start early.","zh":"船上觀光團需時半日，所以應早點出發。"},{"en":"A half-day activity leaves time for another plan later.","zh":"半日活動之後仍有時間安排其他計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a practical estimate for planning.","zh":"這個短語提供實用的時間估計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a really good idea","meaning":"非常好的主意","examples":[{"en":"That’s a really good idea.","zh":"那是一個非常好的主意。"},{"en":"A really good idea is a suggestion that seems very useful, suitable, or enjoyable.","zh":"A really good idea 指看來很有用、合適或令人愉快的建議。"},{"en":"Taking the children to the Science Museum is a really good idea.","zh":"帶孩子去科學博物館是一個非常好的主意。"},{"en":"A really good idea solves a problem or fits the situation well.","zh":"非常好的主意能解決問題或很好地配合情況。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly praises someone’s suggestion.","zh":"這個短語強烈讚賞某人的建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"I’d like to do that myself","meaning":"我自己也想做那件事","examples":[{"en":"I’d like to do that myself.","zh":"我自己也想做那件事。"},{"en":"“I’d like to do that myself” means the speaker personally wants to try the activity.","zh":"「I’d like to do that myself」表示說話者本人也想嘗試該活動。"},{"en":"A boat trip to the old fort sounds fun. I’d like to do that myself.","zh":"乘船去古堡聽起來很有趣。我自己也想做那件事。"},{"en":"The phrase shows personal interest, not only advice for others.","zh":"這個短語表示個人興趣，而不只是給別人的建議。"},{"en":"It can make a suggestion sound more attractive.","zh":"它可以令建議聽起來更吸引。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"if the weather’s bad","meaning":"如果天氣差的話","examples":[{"en":"If the weather’s bad, they could go to the Science Museum.","zh":"如果天氣差的話，他們可以去科學博物館。"},{"en":"“If the weather’s bad” introduces a plan for rain, cold, or unpleasant weather.","zh":"「If the weather’s bad」用來引出雨天、寒冷或惡劣天氣下的計劃。"},{"en":"If the weather’s bad, we can choose an indoor activity.","zh":"如果天氣差的話，我們可以選擇室內活動。"},{"en":"Bad-weather plans are useful when visitors have limited time.","zh":"當訪客時間有限時，惡劣天氣後備計劃很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase helps create a backup plan.","zh":"這個短語有助制定後備方案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Science Museum","meaning":"科學博物館","examples":[{"en":"They could go to the Science Museum when the weather is bad.","zh":"天氣差時，他們可以去科學博物館。"},{"en":"A Science Museum is a museum with displays about science, technology, experiments, and discoveries.","zh":"科學博物館是展示科學、科技、實驗和發現的博物館。"},{"en":"The Science Museum has activities for children and adults.","zh":"科學博物館有適合兒童和成人的活動。"},{"en":"Museums are good choices on rainy days because they are indoors.","zh":"博物館是雨天的好選擇，因為它們在室內。"},{"en":"A Science Museum can make learning feel practical and fun.","zh":"科學博物館可以令學習變得實用而有趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"when I’m at work","meaning":"我上班的時候","examples":[{"en":"They could go to the museum when I’m at work.","zh":"我上班的時候，他們可以去博物館。"},{"en":"“When I’m at work” means during the time when I am working.","zh":"「When I’m at work」指我正在工作那段時間。"},{"en":"My parents can visit the market when I’m at work.","zh":"我上班的時候，父母可以去市場。"},{"en":"Visitors may need activities they can do independently when the host is busy.","zh":"當主人忙碌時，訪客可能需要可以自己進行的活動。"},{"en":"The phrase helps separate the host’s working time from shared free time.","zh":"這個短語有助區分主人的工作時間和共同空閒時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"don’t forget","meaning":"別忘記","examples":[{"en":"Don’t forget it’s closed on Mondays.","zh":"別忘記它星期一休館。"},{"en":"“Don’t forget” reminds someone to remember an important fact or action.","zh":"「Don’t forget」用來提醒某人記住重要事實或行動。"},{"en":"Don’t forget to book the tickets before Friday.","zh":"別忘記星期五前訂票。"},{"en":"People say this when a missed detail could cause problems.","zh":"當遺漏細節可能造成問題時，人們會這樣說。"},{"en":"It is a friendly warning rather than a new plan.","zh":"這是一種友善提醒，而不是新計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"closed on Mondays","meaning":"星期一休館","examples":[{"en":"The Science Museum is closed on Mondays.","zh":"科學博物館星期一休館。"},{"en":"Closed on Mondays means not open to visitors every Monday.","zh":"Closed on Mondays 指每逢星期一不對訪客開放。"},{"en":"The gallery is closed on Mondays for cleaning and maintenance.","zh":"畫廊星期一休館，以進行清潔和維修。"},{"en":"Always check opening days before planning a museum visit.","zh":"計劃參觀博物館前，應先查看開放日。"},{"en":"If a place is closed on Mondays, Tuesday may be a better choice.","zh":"如果一個地方星期一休館，星期二可能是更好選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for four nights","meaning":"住四晚","examples":[{"en":"They are here from Saturday for four nights.","zh":"他們從星期六開始在這裏住四晚。"},{"en":"For four nights means staying overnight four times.","zh":"For four nights 指過夜住宿四次。"},{"en":"The family booked the hotel for four nights.","zh":"那家人預訂酒店住四晚。"},{"en":"A four-night stay gives visitors time for several activities.","zh":"住四晚讓訪客有時間參加幾項活動。"},{"en":"Knowing the number of nights helps calculate accommodation costs.","zh":"知道住宿晚數有助計算住宿費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"would be best","meaning":"會最合適","examples":[{"en":"Tuesday would be best for the museum visit.","zh":"星期二參觀博物館會最合適。"},{"en":"“Would be best” means would be the most suitable choice.","zh":"「Would be best」表示會是最合適的選擇。"},{"en":"Sunday morning would be best for the market because it is less crowded.","zh":"星期日上午去市場會最合適，因為人較少。"},{"en":"The phrase gives advice while still sounding flexible.","zh":"這個短語給出建議，同時聽起來仍有彈性。"},{"en":"The best choice often depends on opening hours, crowds, and weather.","zh":"最合適的選擇通常取決於開放時間、人流和天氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"won’t be so crowded","meaning":"不會那麼擠迫","examples":[{"en":"It won’t be so crowded on Tuesday.","zh":"星期二不會那麼擠迫。"},{"en":"Won’t be so crowded means there will probably be fewer people there.","zh":"Won’t be so crowded 指那裏大概不會有太多人。"},{"en":"The museum won’t be so crowded if you go early.","zh":"如果早點去，博物館不會那麼擠迫。"},{"en":"Less crowded places are easier for families with children.","zh":"人較少的地方對有孩子的家庭較方便。"},{"en":"Choosing quieter times can make visits more comfortable.","zh":"選擇較安靜時段可以令參觀更舒適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"took my kids to","meaning":"帶我的孩子去……","examples":[{"en":"I took my kids to the exhibition on old computers.","zh":"我帶孩子去看舊電腦展覽。"},{"en":"To take my kids to a place means to bring my children there.","zh":"Take my kids to 某地，指帶我的孩子去那裏。"},{"en":"I took my kids to the zoo during the school holiday.","zh":"學校假期期間，我帶孩子去動物園。"},{"en":"Parents often take children to places that are educational and fun.","zh":"父母常帶孩子去既有教育意義又有趣的地方。"},{"en":"Taking children to exhibitions can help them learn outside the classroom.","zh":"帶孩子去展覽可以幫助他們在課室以外學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"exhibition on old computers","meaning":"舊電腦展覽","examples":[{"en":"The Science Museum had an exhibition on old computers.","zh":"科學博物館曾有一個舊電腦展覽。"},{"en":"An exhibition on old computers is a public display about earlier computer technology.","zh":"舊電腦展覽是關於早期電腦科技的公開展示。"},{"en":"The exhibition on old computers showed machines from the 1980s.","zh":"舊電腦展覽展示了 1980 年代的機器。"},{"en":"Such an exhibition can help children understand how technology has changed.","zh":"這類展覽可以幫助孩子理解科技如何改變。"},{"en":"Exhibitions on old technology often make modern devices seem more impressive.","zh":"舊科技展覽常令人覺得現代裝置更了不起。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"far too crowded","meaning":"太擠迫","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition was far too crowded.","zh":"展覽太擠迫。"},{"en":"Far too crowded means much more crowded than comfortable or acceptable.","zh":"Far too crowded 指擠迫程度遠超舒適或可接受範圍。"},{"en":"The market was far too crowded for young children.","zh":"對年幼孩子來說，市場太擠迫了。"},{"en":"When a place is far too crowded, visitors cannot enjoy it properly.","zh":"當一個地方太擠迫，訪客便不能好好享受。"},{"en":"The phrase is stronger than simply saying “crowded.”","zh":"這個短語比單純說「擠迫」語氣更強。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go back","meaning":"再去一次","examples":[{"en":"I wanted to go back, but the exhibition has finished now.","zh":"我本來想再去一次，但展覽現在已經結束。"},{"en":"To go back means to return to a place you have visited before.","zh":"Go back 指返回以前去過的地方。"},{"en":"The children enjoyed the museum so much that they wanted to go back.","zh":"孩子們很喜歡博物館，所以想再去一次。"},{"en":"People often go back to places where they had a good experience.","zh":"人們常會再去曾經有美好經驗的地方。"},{"en":"You cannot go back to an exhibition if it has already ended.","zh":"如果展覽已經結束，就不能再去一次。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"finished now","meaning":"現在已經結束","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition on old computers has finished now.","zh":"舊電腦展覽現在已經結束。"},{"en":"Finished now means no longer happening or available.","zh":"Finished now 指現在不再進行或不再提供。"},{"en":"The festival has finished now, so the park is quiet again.","zh":"節慶現在已經結束，所以公園再次變得安靜。"},{"en":"If an exhibition has finished, visitors need to choose another activity.","zh":"如果展覽已經結束，訪客需要選擇另一項活動。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the change from available in the past to unavailable now.","zh":"這個短語標示由過去可參加到現在不可參加的改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"that’s a shame","meaning":"真可惜","examples":[{"en":"That’s a shame. My cousin’s kids would have enjoyed that.","zh":"真可惜。我表姐的孩子本來會喜歡那個展覽。"},{"en":"“That’s a shame” expresses disappointment or regret about something.","zh":"「That’s a shame」用來表達對某事的失望或遺憾。"},{"en":"The tickets are sold out? That’s a shame.","zh":"門票售罄了？真可惜。"},{"en":"The phrase is common when something useful or enjoyable is no longer possible.","zh":"當有用或愉快的事情不再可能時，人們常使用這句話。"},{"en":"It shows mild sadness, not deep tragedy.","zh":"它表示輕微遺憾，而不是深刻悲劇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"would have enjoyed","meaning":"本來會喜歡","examples":[{"en":"My cousin’s kids would have enjoyed the exhibition.","zh":"我表姐的孩子本來會喜歡那個展覽。"},{"en":"Would have enjoyed means someone probably would have liked something, but did not get the chance.","zh":"Would have enjoyed 指某人本來很可能會喜歡某事，但沒有機會經歷。"},{"en":"She would have enjoyed the concert, but she was ill.","zh":"她本來會喜歡那場音樂會，但她病了。"},{"en":"The phrase imagines a missed opportunity in the past.","zh":"這個短語想像過去錯過的機會。"},{"en":"It often expresses regret about something that cannot happen now.","zh":"它常表達對現在無法發生的事情感到遺憾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"starting soon","meaning":"很快開始","examples":[{"en":"There is another exhibition starting soon on space.","zh":"另一個關於太空的展覽很快開始。"},{"en":"Starting soon means beginning in the near future.","zh":"Starting soon 指在不久後開始。"},{"en":"A new art course is starting soon at the community centre.","zh":"社區中心有一個新的藝術課程很快開始。"},{"en":"If an event is starting soon, visitors may need to book early.","zh":"如果活動很快開始，訪客可能需要提早預訂。"},{"en":"The phrase creates interest because the activity is close but not yet open.","zh":"這個短語製造興趣，因為活動快將開放但尚未開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on space","meaning":"關於太空","examples":[{"en":"There is another exhibition on space starting soon.","zh":"另一個關於太空的展覽很快開始。"},{"en":"On space means about outer space, planets, stars, or space travel.","zh":"On space 指關於外太空、行星、星星或太空旅行。"},{"en":"The museum has a talk on space exploration.","zh":"博物館有一場關於太空探索的講座。"},{"en":"Children often enjoy exhibitions on space because they include rockets and planets.","zh":"孩子常喜歡關於太空的展覽，因為當中包括火箭和行星。"},{"en":"“On” can introduce the subject of an exhibition, talk, or book.","zh":"On 可以引出展覽、講座或書本的主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"looks really good","meaning":"看起來很不錯","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition on space looks really good.","zh":"關於太空的展覽看起來很不錯。"},{"en":"Looks really good means appears interesting, enjoyable, or high quality.","zh":"Looks really good 指看來有趣、令人享受或質素很高。"},{"en":"The new science show looks really good for families.","zh":"新科學表演看起來很適合家庭參加。"},{"en":"People often say this after seeing posters, reviews, or descriptions.","zh":"人們在看過海報、評價或介紹後常會這樣說。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a positive first impression.","zh":"這個短語表達正面的第一印象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"mention that to","meaning":"向……提起那件事","examples":[{"en":"I’ll mention that to my cousin.","zh":"我會向表姐提起那件事。"},{"en":"To mention something to someone means to tell them about it briefly.","zh":"Mention something to someone 指簡短地告訴某人某事。"},{"en":"I’ll mention the hotel to my parents tonight.","zh":"我今晚會向父母提起那間酒店。"},{"en":"Mentioning an idea lets someone consider it without pressure.","zh":"提起一個想法，可以讓對方在沒有壓力下考慮。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when passing on information or suggestions.","zh":"傳達資料或建議時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the rest of the conversation","meaning":"對話餘下部分","examples":[{"en":"You have some time to look at the questions before the rest of the conversation.","zh":"在聆聽對話餘下部分前，你有些時間看問題。"},{"en":"The rest of the conversation means the remaining part of the discussion.","zh":"The rest of the conversation 指討論中剩下的部分。"},{"en":"The teacher asked students to predict the rest of the conversation.","zh":"老師請學生預測對話餘下部分。"},{"en":"Understanding the first part can help listeners follow the rest of the conversation.","zh":"理解前半部分可以幫助聽者跟上對話餘下部分。"},{"en":"The phrase separates what has already happened from what will come next.","zh":"這個短語把已發生的內容和接下來的內容分開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"thought about where to","meaning":"有沒有想過去哪裏……","examples":[{"en":"Have you thought about where to take them to eat?","zh":"你有沒有想過帶他們去哪裏吃飯？"},{"en":"“Thought about where to” means considered the place for doing something.","zh":"Thought about where to 指考慮去哪個地方做某事。"},{"en":"Have you thought about where to stay during the trip?","zh":"你有沒有想過旅程期間住在哪裏？"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether someone has planned a practical detail.","zh":"這個短語詢問某人是否已計劃實際細節。"},{"en":"Thinking about where to go early can avoid last-minute stress.","zh":"早點想好去哪裏，可以避免最後一刻的壓力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"food stalls","meaning":"食物攤檔","examples":[{"en":"I really like all the food stalls at Clacton Market.","zh":"我很喜歡 Clacton Market 的所有食物攤檔。"},{"en":"Food stalls are small stands or counters that sell food, often in a market or street area.","zh":"食物攤檔是在市場或街道區域售賣食物的小攤位或櫃位。"},{"en":"The market has food stalls selling noodles, cakes, and vegetarian snacks.","zh":"市場有食物攤檔售賣麵食、蛋糕和素食小吃。"},{"en":"Food stalls can offer quick, informal, and varied meals.","zh":"食物攤檔可以提供快捷、輕鬆和多樣化的餐點。"},{"en":"Visitors often enjoy food stalls because they can try many dishes in one place.","zh":"訪客常喜歡食物攤檔，因為可以在一個地方嘗試多種菜式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Clacton Market","meaning":"Clacton Market","examples":[{"en":"Clacton Market has many food stalls.","zh":"Clacton Market 有很多食物攤檔。"},{"en":"Clacton Market is the name of the market being recommended in the conversation.","zh":"Clacton Market 是對話中被推薦的市場名稱。"},{"en":"Visitors can go to Clacton Market for lunch and local snacks.","zh":"訪客可以去 Clacton Market 吃午餐和本地小吃。"},{"en":"A market with many food stalls is useful when visitors have different tastes.","zh":"有很多食物攤檔的市場適合口味不同的訪客。"},{"en":"Clacton Market sounds suitable for families because it offers choice and atmosphere.","zh":"Clacton Market 聽起來適合家庭，因為它提供選擇和氣氛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"vegetarian","meaning":"素食者","examples":[{"en":"My cousin is vegetarian.","zh":"我的表姐是素食者。"},{"en":"A vegetarian is a person who does not eat meat or fish.","zh":"素食者是不吃肉類或魚類的人。"},{"en":"The restaurant has several vegetarian dishes.","zh":"這間餐廳有幾款素食菜式。"},{"en":"If a guest is vegetarian, the host should check food choices before booking.","zh":"如果客人是素食者，主人訂位前應查看食物選擇。"},{"en":"Vegetarian food can include vegetables, beans, grains, cheese, and eggs, depending on the person’s diet.","zh":"素食可以包括蔬菜、豆類、穀物、芝士和雞蛋，視乎個人飲食習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one of the best places for","meaning":"最適合……的地方之一","examples":[{"en":"Clacton Market is one of the best places for vegetarian food.","zh":"Clacton Market 是最適合素食的地方之一。"},{"en":"One of the best places for something means among the most suitable or highly recommended places for it.","zh":"One of the best places for 某事，指最合適或最值得推薦的地方之一。"},{"en":"The old town is one of the best places for walking tours.","zh":"舊城區是最適合步行導賞團的地方之一。"},{"en":"People often use this phrase when strongly recommending a place.","zh":"人們強烈推薦一個地方時，常使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It does not mean it is the only good place.","zh":"它不表示那是唯一好的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"that kind of food","meaning":"那類食物","examples":[{"en":"It is one of the best places for that kind of food.","zh":"那裏是最適合那類食物的地方之一。"},{"en":"That kind of food means the type of food just mentioned or understood from context.","zh":"That kind of food 指剛才提到或從語境可知的食物類型。"},{"en":"If you like vegetarian food, this café is good for that kind of food.","zh":"如果你喜歡素食，這間咖啡店很適合那類食物。"},{"en":"The phrase avoids repeating the exact food name.","zh":"這個短語可以避免重複確切食物名稱。"},{"en":"It is useful when both speakers already know what type is being discussed.","zh":"當雙方都知道正在討論哪類食物時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Definitely.","meaning":"絕對是。","examples":[{"en":"Definitely, and there will be loads of choice for the kids too.","zh":"絕對是，而且孩子們也會有大量選擇。"},{"en":"“Definitely” means certainly or without doubt.","zh":"Definitely 指肯定地或毫無疑問。"},{"en":"“Is the market good for families?” “Definitely.”","zh":"「這個市場適合家庭嗎？」「絕對是。」"},{"en":"The word shows strong agreement or confidence.","zh":"這個詞表示強烈同意或有信心。"},{"en":"It is more certain than saying “probably.”","zh":"它比說 probably 更肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"loads of choice","meaning":"大量選擇","examples":[{"en":"There will be loads of choice for the kids.","zh":"孩子們會有大量選擇。"},{"en":"Loads of choice means many different options.","zh":"Loads of choice 指有很多不同選項。"},{"en":"The food court has loads of choice, from noodles to desserts.","zh":"美食廣場有大量選擇，由麵食到甜品都有。"},{"en":"Loads of choice is helpful when children have different tastes.","zh":"當孩子口味不同時，大量選擇很有用。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and means “a lot of choice.”","zh":"這個短語較口語，意思是「很多選擇」。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get there quite early","meaning":"需要頗早到達","examples":[{"en":"You need to get there quite early.","zh":"你需要頗早到達。"},{"en":"To get there quite early means to arrive before the busiest or latest suitable time.","zh":"Get there quite early 指在最繁忙或最遲合適時間之前到達。"},{"en":"You should get to the market quite early if you want lunch.","zh":"如果你想吃午餐，應該頗早到達市場。"},{"en":"Arriving early can help visitors avoid queues and sold-out food.","zh":"早點到達可以幫助訪客避免排隊和食物售罄。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that timing is important.","zh":"這個短語暗示時間安排很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at the weekend","meaning":"週末","examples":[{"en":"At the weekend, most stalls stop serving lunch at 2.30.","zh":"週末時，大部分攤檔下午二時三十分停止供應午餐。"},{"en":"At the weekend means on Saturday, Sunday, or both days.","zh":"At the weekend 指在星期六、星期日或兩天期間。"},{"en":"The market is much busier at the weekend.","zh":"市場在週末繁忙得多。"},{"en":"Families often plan trips at the weekend because children are not at school.","zh":"家庭常在週末安排行程，因為孩子不用上學。"},{"en":"Opening times may be different at the weekend.","zh":"週末開放時間可能不同。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stop serving lunch","meaning":"停止供應午餐","examples":[{"en":"Most of the stalls stop serving lunch at 2.30.","zh":"大部分攤檔下午二時三十分停止供應午餐。"},{"en":"To stop serving lunch means to no longer provide lunch after a certain time.","zh":"Stop serving lunch 指在某個時間後不再提供午餐。"},{"en":"The café stops serving lunch at three o’clock.","zh":"咖啡店下午三時停止供應午餐。"},{"en":"If visitors arrive late, they may find that stalls have stopped serving lunch.","zh":"如果訪客太遲到達，可能發現攤檔已停止供應午餐。"},{"en":"Knowing meal service times helps avoid disappointment.","zh":"知道供餐時間可以避免失望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Good point.","meaning":"說得好；有道理","examples":[{"en":"Good point. It’s all going to need careful planning.","zh":"說得好。這一切都需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"“Good point” means the speaker thinks the other person has said something useful or sensible.","zh":"「Good point」表示說話者認為對方說了有用或合理的話。"},{"en":"“The museum is closed on Mondays.” “Good point.”","zh":"「博物館星期一休館。」「說得好。」"},{"en":"The phrase recognises that a detail matters.","zh":"這個短語承認某個細節很重要。"},{"en":"It helps keep a discussion friendly and practical.","zh":"它有助令討論保持友善和實際。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"careful planning","meaning":"仔細規劃","examples":[{"en":"The visit is going to need careful planning.","zh":"這次探訪將需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"Careful planning means thinking through details before doing something.","zh":"Careful planning 指做事前仔細思考細節。"},{"en":"A family visit needs careful planning if children and budgets are involved.","zh":"如果涉及孩子和預算，家庭探訪需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"Careful planning can prevent wasted time and unnecessary cost.","zh":"仔細規劃可以避免浪費時間和不必要開支。"},{"en":"Good plans include transport, meals, weather, and opening hours.","zh":"好計劃包括交通、膳食、天氣和開放時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"would love to","meaning":"很想","examples":[{"en":"My cousin said she’d love to take the kids to a show.","zh":"我表姐說她很想帶孩子去看演出。"},{"en":"Would love to means would very much like to do something.","zh":"Would love to 指非常想做某事。"},{"en":"I’d love to visit the old fort if we have time.","zh":"如果有時間，我很想參觀古堡。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses strong interest or enthusiasm.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈興趣或熱情。"},{"en":"It is warmer than simply saying “want to.”","zh":"它比單純說 want to 更溫暖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take the kids to a show","meaning":"帶孩子去看演出","examples":[{"en":"She would love to take the kids to a show at the theatre.","zh":"她很想帶孩子去劇院看演出。"},{"en":"To take the kids to a show means to bring children to watch a performance.","zh":"Take the kids to a show 指帶孩子去觀看表演。"},{"en":"We took the kids to a musical during the holidays.","zh":"我們在假期帶孩子去看音樂劇。"},{"en":"Shows for children should be suitable in length, language, and content.","zh":"適合孩子的演出在長度、語言和內容上都應合適。"},{"en":"Taking kids to live performances can create special family memories.","zh":"帶孩子去看現場演出可以創造特別的家庭回憶。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a show at the theatre","meaning":"劇院演出","examples":[{"en":"The family might go to a show at the theatre.","zh":"這家人可能會去看劇院演出。"},{"en":"A show at the theatre is a live performance such as a play, musical, or concert.","zh":"劇院演出是現場表演，例如話劇、音樂劇或音樂會。"},{"en":"The children enjoyed a show at the theatre last weekend.","zh":"孩子們上週末欣賞了一場劇院演出。"},{"en":"Theatre shows often need advance booking because seats are limited.","zh":"劇院演出通常需要提早預訂，因為座位有限。"},{"en":"A theatre show can be a good evening activity for visitors.","zh":"劇院演出可以是適合訪客的晚間活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tickets are so expensive","meaning":"門票很貴","examples":[{"en":"Theatre tickets are so expensive.","zh":"劇院門票很貴。"},{"en":"“Tickets are so expensive” means the price of tickets is very high.","zh":"「Tickets are so expensive」表示門票價格非常高。"},{"en":"Concert tickets are so expensive that we decided to watch a free festival instead.","zh":"音樂會門票很貴，所以我們決定改看免費節慶活動。"},{"en":"Expensive tickets can make family activities difficult for people on a budget.","zh":"門票昂貴會令預算有限的人較難安排家庭活動。"},{"en":"Discounts can make expensive shows more affordable.","zh":"折扣可以令昂貴演出較容易負擔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get some good deals","meaning":"找到一些優惠","examples":[{"en":"You can get some good deals if you book online.","zh":"如果你網上預訂，可以找到一些優惠。"},{"en":"To get some good deals means to find lower prices or better offers.","zh":"Get some good deals 指找到較低價格或較好的優惠。"},{"en":"We got a good deal on theatre tickets by booking early.","zh":"我們提早預訂，買到了劇院門票優惠。"},{"en":"Good deals can help families enjoy activities without spending too much.","zh":"好優惠可以幫助家庭享受活動而不用花太多錢。"},{"en":"Compare prices carefully because not every offer is a real deal.","zh":"應仔細比較價格，因為並非每個優惠都真正划算。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"book online with","meaning":"透過……網上預訂","examples":[{"en":"You can book online with bargaintickets.com.","zh":"你可以透過 bargaintickets.com 網上預訂。"},{"en":"To book online with a website means to reserve tickets or services using that website.","zh":"Book online with 某網站，指使用該網站預訂門票或服務。"},{"en":"We booked online with the theatre’s official website.","zh":"我們透過劇院官方網站網上預訂。"},{"en":"Booking online can be convenient, but users should check the website is reliable.","zh":"網上預訂很方便，但使用者應檢查網站是否可靠。"},{"en":"Online booking usually requires payment details and an email address.","zh":"網上預訂通常需要付款資料和電郵地址。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"for the following day","meaning":"訂翌日的票","examples":[{"en":"You can book tickets online for the following day.","zh":"你可以在網上訂翌日的票。"},{"en":"For the following day means for the next day after the current or mentioned day.","zh":"For the following day 指為當天或提及日期之後的下一天。"},{"en":"We booked museum tickets for the following day.","zh":"我們預訂了翌日的博物館門票。"},{"en":"Last-minute theatre websites often sell seats for the following day.","zh":"臨時劇院售票網站常售賣翌日座位。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show that the booking is for tomorrow, not today.","zh":"這個短語幫助說明預訂是為明天，而不是今天。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on some seats","meaning":"部分座位","examples":[{"en":"On some seats, there is a 75% discount.","zh":"部分座位有七五折優惠。"},{"en":"On some seats means the offer applies only to certain seats, not all seats.","zh":"On some seats 指優惠只適用於某些座位，而不是所有座位。"},{"en":"There is a discount on some seats near the back of the theatre.","zh":"劇院後排部分座位有折扣。"},{"en":"Cheaper seats may have a restricted view or be less popular.","zh":"較便宜座位可能視線受阻或較不受歡迎。"},{"en":"Always check which seats the discount applies to before booking.","zh":"預訂前應查看折扣適用於哪些座位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a 75% discount","meaning":"七五折優惠","examples":[{"en":"Some seats have a 75% discount.","zh":"部分座位有七五折優惠。"},{"en":"A 75% discount means the price is reduced by seventy-five percent.","zh":"A 75% discount 指價格減少百分之七十五。"},{"en":"A £40 ticket with a 75% discount costs £10.","zh":"一張 40 英鎊門票有七五折優惠後，價格是 10 英鎊。"},{"en":"A large discount can make expensive shows affordable for families.","zh":"大折扣可以令昂貴演出變得適合家庭負擔。"},{"en":"Check whether the discount includes booking fees or extra charges.","zh":"應檢查折扣是否包括訂票費或額外收費。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"I must try and get some","meaning":"我一定要試着買一些","examples":[{"en":"I must try and get some discounted tickets.","zh":"我一定要試着買一些折扣門票。"},{"en":"“I must try and get some” means the speaker intends to make an effort to obtain something.","zh":"「I must try and get some」表示說話者打算努力取得某物。"},{"en":"I must try and get some tickets before they sell out.","zh":"在門票售罄前，我一定要試着買一些。"},{"en":"The phrase shows determination but not certainty of success.","zh":"這個短語顯示決心，但不保證成功。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken English when planning to look for something.","zh":"它常見於口語英語，用於計劃尋找某物時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"for free","meaning":"免費","examples":[{"en":"There are lots of things you can do for free.","zh":"有很多事情你可以免費做。"},{"en":"For free means without paying any money.","zh":"For free 指不需要付任何金錢。"},{"en":"Visitors can enter the park for free.","zh":"訪客可以免費進入公園。"},{"en":"Free activities are helpful when guests are on a tight budget.","zh":"當客人預算緊絀時，免費活動很有幫助。"},{"en":"Something can be free and still be enjoyable or valuable.","zh":"免費的東西仍然可以很愉快或有價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"no need to","meaning":"無須","examples":[{"en":"There is no need to spend a fortune.","zh":"無須花一大筆錢。"},{"en":"“No need to” means it is not necessary to do something.","zh":"「No need to」表示沒有必要做某事。"},{"en":"There is no need to book a taxi because the hotel is nearby.","zh":"酒店很近，無須叫的士。"},{"en":"The phrase reassures someone that a difficult or costly action is unnecessary.","zh":"這個短語讓人放心，表示困難或昂貴的行動並非必要。"},{"en":"It often introduces a simpler or cheaper option.","zh":"它常引出較簡單或較便宜的選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"spend a fortune","meaning":"花一大筆錢","examples":[{"en":"There is no need to spend a fortune on activities.","zh":"無須在活動上花一大筆錢。"},{"en":"To spend a fortune means to spend a very large amount of money.","zh":"Spend a fortune 指花非常大量金錢。"},{"en":"You do not need to spend a fortune to entertain visitors.","zh":"招待訪客不一定要花一大筆錢。"},{"en":"Free festivals and markets can be fun without costing much.","zh":"免費節慶和市集可以很有趣，而且花費不多。"},{"en":"The phrase is an exaggeration used to describe very high spending.","zh":"這個短語是誇張說法，用來形容很高開支。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"check and see if","meaning":"查查看是否","examples":[{"en":"Check and see if it is the same weekend as the festival.","zh":"查查看是否與節日是同一個週末。"},{"en":"To check and see if something is true means to confirm it by looking or asking.","zh":"Check and see if 某事屬實，指透過查看或詢問來確認。"},{"en":"Check and see if the museum is open on Tuesday.","zh":"查查看博物館星期二是否開放。"},{"en":"Checking first can prevent mistakes in planning.","zh":"先查清楚可以避免計劃出錯。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds practical and conversational.","zh":"這個短語聽起來實用而口語化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the same weekend as","meaning":"與……同一個週末","examples":[{"en":"The visit may be the same weekend as the Roots Music Festival.","zh":"這次探訪可能與 Roots Music Festival 是同一個週末。"},{"en":"The same weekend as something means during the same Saturday and Sunday period.","zh":"The same weekend as 某事，指在同一個星期六和星期日期間。"},{"en":"Their trip is the same weekend as the food festival.","zh":"他們的旅程與美食節是同一個週末。"},{"en":"If two events are on the same weekend, visitors may combine them.","zh":"如果兩個活動在同一個週末，訪客可以把它們結合。"},{"en":"Checking dates helps avoid missing a good event.","zh":"查清日期有助避免錯過好活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Roots Music Festival","meaning":"Roots Music Festival","examples":[{"en":"The Roots Music Festival takes place in Blakewell Gardens.","zh":"Roots Music Festival 在 Blakewell Gardens 舉行。"},{"en":"Roots Music Festival is the name of a music event mentioned in the conversation.","zh":"Roots Music Festival 是對話中提到的音樂活動名稱。"},{"en":"Visitors can hear live music at the Roots Music Festival.","zh":"訪客可以在 Roots Music Festival 聽現場音樂。"},{"en":"A festival in a garden can be suitable for families if it has open space.","zh":"在花園舉行的節日如果有開放空間，可能適合家庭。"},{"en":"Checking the festival date helps visitors plan their weekend.","zh":"查看節日日期可以幫助訪客安排週末。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"family-friendly event","meaning":"適合一家大小參加的活動","examples":[{"en":"It is always a family-friendly event.","zh":"它一向是適合一家大小參加的活動。"},{"en":"A family-friendly event is suitable and enjoyable for adults and children.","zh":"Family-friendly event 是適合成人和兒童參加並享受的活動。"},{"en":"The festival is family-friendly because it has music, food, and space for children.","zh":"這個節日有音樂、食物和兒童活動空間，因此適合一家大小參加。"},{"en":"Family-friendly events usually avoid unsuitable content and provide safe spaces.","zh":"適合家庭的活動通常避免不合適內容，並提供安全空間。"},{"en":"Parents often look for family-friendly activities when visitors include children.","zh":"當訪客包括孩子時，父母常尋找適合一家大小的活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"no entry charge","meaning":"不收入場費","examples":[{"en":"There is no entry charge for the festival.","zh":"這個節日不收入場費。"},{"en":"No entry charge means people do not need to pay to enter.","zh":"No entry charge 指人們進場不需要付款。"},{"en":"The museum has no entry charge on Sundays.","zh":"博物館星期日不收入場費。"},{"en":"Free entry can make an event more accessible to families.","zh":"免費入場可以令活動更適合家庭參加。"},{"en":"There may be no entry charge, but food or activities inside may still cost money.","zh":"活動可能不收入場費，但場內食物或活動仍可能收費。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"That sounds perfect.","meaning":"聽起來很理想。","examples":[{"en":"That sounds perfect for my cousin’s family.","zh":"那聽起來很適合我表姐一家。"},{"en":"“That sounds perfect” means the suggestion seems exactly suitable.","zh":"「That sounds perfect」表示這個建議聽起來完全合適。"},{"en":"A free music festival for children? That sounds perfect.","zh":"適合兒童的免費音樂節？聽起來很理想。"},{"en":"The phrase shows strong approval of an idea.","zh":"這個短語表示強烈認同某個想法。"},{"en":"It is often used when advice matches someone’s needs very well.","zh":"當建議非常配合某人的需要時，常會使用這句話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"climb Telegraph Hill","meaning":"爬上 Telegraph Hill","examples":[{"en":"If you are in Blakewell Gardens, climb Telegraph Hill.","zh":"如果你在 Blakewell Gardens，可以爬上 Telegraph Hill。"},{"en":"To climb Telegraph Hill means to walk up the hill called Telegraph Hill.","zh":"Climb Telegraph Hill 指步行登上名為 Telegraph Hill 的山丘。"},{"en":"Visitors can climb Telegraph Hill after visiting the festival.","zh":"訪客參加節日後可以爬上 Telegraph Hill。"},{"en":"Climbing a hill may be tiring, but it can reward visitors with a good view.","zh":"爬山可能很累，但可以讓訪客欣賞好景色。"},{"en":"Wear comfortable shoes if you plan to climb Telegraph Hill.","zh":"如果你打算爬上 Telegraph Hill，應穿舒適鞋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"look right down on","meaning":"直接俯瞰","examples":[{"en":"You can look right down on the port from Telegraph Hill.","zh":"你可以從 Telegraph Hill 直接俯瞰港口。"},{"en":"To look right down on something means to see it clearly from a high position above it.","zh":"Look right down on 某地，指從高處清楚看見下方的地方。"},{"en":"From the tower, visitors can look right down on the old town.","zh":"從塔上，訪客可以直接俯瞰舊城區。"},{"en":"High viewpoints help people understand the size and layout of a place.","zh":"高處觀景點可以幫助人們理解地方的大小和佈局。"},{"en":"The phrase creates the image of looking from above.","zh":"這個短語營造從上往下看的畫面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the port","meaning":"港口","examples":[{"en":"You can see the port from Telegraph Hill.","zh":"你可以從 Telegraph Hill 看見港口。"},{"en":"The port is the area where ships arrive, leave, load goods, or take passengers.","zh":"港口是船隻抵達、離開、裝卸貨物或接載乘客的區域。"},{"en":"The city’s port is busy with ferries and cargo ships.","zh":"這個城市的港口有渡輪和貨船，非常繁忙。"},{"en":"Seeing the port from above can show how important trade is to the city.","zh":"從高處看港口，可以顯示貿易對城市有多重要。"},{"en":"Ports often have cranes, docks, warehouses, and ships.","zh":"港口通常有起重機、碼頭、倉庫和船隻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be really impressed","meaning":"印象很深刻","examples":[{"en":"Everyone is always really impressed by the view.","zh":"每個人總是對景色印象很深刻。"},{"en":"To be really impressed means to admire something strongly because it is excellent or surprising.","zh":"Be really impressed 指因某事優秀或令人驚訝而非常欣賞。"},{"en":"Visitors were really impressed by the view from the hill.","zh":"訪客對山上的景色印象很深刻。"},{"en":"A dramatic view can make a simple walk feel special.","zh":"壯觀景色可以令簡單步行變得特別。"},{"en":"People are often impressed when something is bigger or more beautiful than expected.","zh":"當某事比預期更大或更美，人們常會印象深刻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"so huge","meaning":"非常巨大","examples":[{"en":"Everyone is impressed because the port is so huge.","zh":"每個人都印象深刻，因為港口非常巨大。"},{"en":"So huge means extremely large.","zh":"So huge 指極其巨大。"},{"en":"The ship was so huge that it looked like a floating building.","zh":"那艘船非常巨大，看起來像一座漂浮建築物。"},{"en":"Large places can feel impressive when seen from above.","zh":"從高處觀看時，大型地方會令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"The word “so” adds emphasis to the size.","zh":"So 加強了對大小的強調。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"I’ve been meaning to","meaning":"我一直想","examples":[{"en":"I’ve been meaning to do that for ages.","zh":"我一直想做那件事很久了。"},{"en":"“I’ve been meaning to” means I have intended to do something for some time but have not done it yet.","zh":"「I’ve been meaning to」表示我一段時間以來一直打算做某事，但尚未做到。"},{"en":"I’ve been meaning to visit that museum.","zh":"我一直想去參觀那間博物館。"},{"en":"People use this phrase for plans they keep delaying.","zh":"人們用這個短語形容一直拖延的計劃。"},{"en":"It often suggests genuine interest but lack of opportunity or time.","zh":"它常暗示有真正興趣，但缺少機會或時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"for ages","meaning":"很久","examples":[{"en":"I’ve been meaning to climb Telegraph Hill for ages.","zh":"我很久以來一直想爬上 Telegraph Hill。"},{"en":"For ages means for a very long time.","zh":"For ages 指很長時間。"},{"en":"I have wanted to try that restaurant for ages.","zh":"我很久以來一直想試那間餐廳。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and often exaggerates the length of time.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常誇張時間之長。"},{"en":"It shows that the idea is not new to the speaker.","zh":"它顯示這個想法對說話者來說並不新。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the view’s amazing","meaning":"景色非常好","examples":[{"en":"I’ve heard the view’s amazing.","zh":"我聽說景色非常好。"},{"en":"“The view’s amazing” means the scenery looks extremely beautiful or impressive.","zh":"「The view’s amazing」表示景色非常美麗或令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"The view from the top of the hill is amazing at sunset.","zh":"日落時，山頂景色非常好。"},{"en":"People often climb viewpoints because they expect an amazing view.","zh":"人們常爬上觀景點，因為期待看到壯觀景色。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly praises what can be seen from a place.","zh":"這個短語強烈讚賞從某地看到的景色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"worth the effort","meaning":"值得花力氣","examples":[{"en":"Climbing Telegraph Hill is really worth the effort.","zh":"爬上 Telegraph Hill 真的值得花力氣。"},{"en":"Worth the effort means the result is good enough to justify the work or difficulty.","zh":"Worth the effort 指結果好到足以值得付出努力或克服困難。"},{"en":"The walk is steep, but the view is worth the effort.","zh":"這段路很斜，但景色值得花力氣。"},{"en":"An activity can be tiring and still worth doing.","zh":"一項活動可以很累，但仍值得做。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when the reward is greater than the inconvenience.","zh":"當回報大於不便時，人們會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"given me loads of ideas","meaning":"給了我很多想法","examples":[{"en":"That has given me loads of ideas.","zh":"那給了我很多想法。"},{"en":"To give someone loads of ideas means to provide many suggestions or possibilities.","zh":"Give someone loads of ideas 指提供很多建議或可能性。"},{"en":"Your advice has given me loads of ideas for the weekend.","zh":"你的建議給了我很多週末活動的想法。"},{"en":"A helpful conversation can give someone new plans and confidence.","zh":"有用的對話可以給人新計劃和信心。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and shows appreciation for useful advice.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並表示感謝有用建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Thanks so much.","meaning":"非常感謝。","examples":[{"en":"Thanks so much for all your advice.","zh":"非常感謝你所有的建議。"},{"en":"“Thanks so much” is a warm way to thank someone strongly.","zh":"「Thanks so much」是一種溫暖而強烈地感謝某人的說法。"},{"en":"Thanks so much for helping me plan the visit.","zh":"非常感謝你幫我計劃這次探訪。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds friendly and more emotional than a simple “thanks.”","zh":"這個短語比簡單說「thanks」更友善、更有情感。"},{"en":"It is often used after someone has given useful help or support.","zh":"當某人提供有用幫助或支援後，常會使用這句話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 4/task-2":[{"front":"talking to members of the public","meaning":"向公眾人士講話","examples":[{"en":"A guide is talking to members of the public who are visiting a football stadium.","zh":"一名導遊正在向參觀足球場的公眾人士講話。"},{"en":"Talking to members of the public means speaking to ordinary people, not just staff or officials.","zh":"向公眾人士講話，是指向普通市民說話，而不只是向職員或官員說話。"},{"en":"The guide was talking to members of the public before the tour began.","zh":"導遊在導覽開始前向公眾人士講話。"},{"en":"When talking to members of the public, staff should use clear and friendly language.","zh":"向公眾人士講話時，職員應使用清楚而友善的語言。"},{"en":"Volunteers often practise talking to members of the public during training.","zh":"義工在培訓期間經常練習向公眾人士講話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"visiting a football stadium","meaning":"參觀足球場","examples":[{"en":"Members of the public are visiting a football stadium in the UK.","zh":"公眾人士正在參觀英國一個足球場。"},{"en":"Visiting a football stadium means going to see the place where football matches are played.","zh":"參觀足球場是指前往觀看舉行足球比賽的場地。"},{"en":"The children enjoyed visiting a football stadium during their school trip.","zh":"孩子們在學校旅行中很享受參觀足球場。"},{"en":"Visitors may learn about the club’s history when visiting a football stadium.","zh":"遊客參觀足球場時，可能會了解球會歷史。"},{"en":"People visiting a football stadium should follow safety instructions during the tour.","zh":"參觀足球場的人在導覽期間應遵守安全指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"welcome to","meaning":"歡迎來到","examples":[{"en":"Good morning, and welcome to City Football Club.","zh":"早安，歡迎來到 City 足球會。"},{"en":"“Welcome to” is used to greet people when they arrive at a place or event.","zh":"「Welcome to」用來在別人到達某地方或活動時表示歡迎。"},{"en":"Welcome to our stadium tour.","zh":"歡迎來到我們的球場導覽。"},{"en":"A guide often says “welcome to” before giving visitors information.","zh":"導遊通常會在提供資料前說「歡迎來到」。"},{"en":"Welcome to the museum, and please stay with your group.","zh":"歡迎來到博物館，請與你的團體同行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"City Football Club","meaning":"City 足球會","examples":[{"en":"The guide welcomes visitors to City Football Club.","zh":"導遊歡迎遊客來到 City 足球會。"},{"en":"City Football Club is the football club that owns or uses the stadium being visited.","zh":"City 足球會是擁有或使用這個參觀球場的足球會。"},{"en":"City Football Club offers tours for fans and tourists.","zh":"City 足球會為球迷和遊客提供導覽。"},{"en":"Visitors can learn about City Football Club’s history during the tour.","zh":"遊客可以在導覽中了解 City 足球會的歷史。"},{"en":"The stadium shop sells shirts and souvenirs from City Football Club.","zh":"球場商店售賣 City 足球會的球衣和紀念品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"I’d like to give you","meaning":"我想給你……","examples":[{"en":"I’d like to give you some useful information about your visit.","zh":"我想給你們一些關於參觀的實用資料。"},{"en":"“I’d like to give you” is a polite way to say that the speaker wants to provide something.","zh":"「I’d like to give you」是有禮貌地表示講者想提供某物。"},{"en":"I’d like to give you a map before we start the tour.","zh":"在導覽開始前，我想給你們一張地圖。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds more polite than simply saying “I will give you.”","zh":"這個句式比直接說「我會給你」更有禮貌。"},{"en":"I’d like to give you a few safety reminders.","zh":"我想給你們幾個安全提醒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"useful information about","meaning":"關於……的實用資料","examples":[{"en":"The guide gives visitors useful information about their visit to the stadium.","zh":"導遊向遊客提供關於參觀球場的實用資料。"},{"en":"Useful information about something is practical information that helps people understand or do it better.","zh":"關於某事的實用資料，是幫助人們更好理解或進行該事的實際資訊。"},{"en":"The leaflet gives useful information about stadium opening hours.","zh":"傳單提供關於球場開放時間的實用資料。"},{"en":"Useful information about safety can prevent accidents during a tour.","zh":"關於安全的實用資料可以避免導覽期間發生意外。"},{"en":"Visitors need useful information about tickets, food, and toilets.","zh":"遊客需要關於門票、食物和洗手間的實用資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"your visit to the stadium","meaning":"你們參觀球場","examples":[{"en":"The guide explains some details about their visit to the stadium.","zh":"導遊解釋一些關於他們參觀球場的細節。"},{"en":"Your visit to the stadium means the time you spend touring or seeing the stadium.","zh":"你們參觀球場，是指你們遊覽或觀看球場的時間。"},{"en":"During your visit to the stadium, you will see the pitch and dressing rooms.","zh":"在你們參觀球場期間，你們會看到草地球場和更衣室。"},{"en":"Information about your visit to the stadium helps you know what to expect.","zh":"關於你們參觀球場的資料，可以幫助你們知道會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Please follow the guide throughout your visit to the stadium.","zh":"請在你們參觀球場期間一直跟隨導遊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"start the tour","meaning":"開始導覽","examples":[{"en":"The group will start the tour after the guide gives some information.","zh":"導遊提供一些資料後，團體會開始導覽。"},{"en":"To start the tour means to begin the guided visit.","zh":"開始導覽是指展開有導遊帶領的參觀。"},{"en":"We will start the tour at the main entrance.","zh":"我們會在正門開始導覽。"},{"en":"The guide gives safety advice before starting the tour.","zh":"導遊在開始導覽前提供安全建議。"},{"en":"Visitors should stay together when they start the tour.","zh":"遊客開始導覽時應留在一起。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"areas of the stadium","meaning":"球場的區域","examples":[{"en":"The tour includes areas of the stadium that are open to visitors.","zh":"導覽包括對遊客開放的球場區域。"},{"en":"Areas of the stadium are different parts of the stadium, such as the pitch, seats, and dressing rooms.","zh":"球場的區域是指球場的不同部分，例如草地球場、座位區和更衣室。"},{"en":"Some areas of the stadium are only for players and staff.","zh":"球場某些區域只供球員和職員使用。"},{"en":"Visitors will see several areas of the stadium during the tour.","zh":"遊客在導覽期間會參觀球場幾個區域。"},{"en":"Safety rules may be different in different areas of the stadium.","zh":"球場不同區域的安全規則可能不同。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"open to visitors","meaning":"對遊客開放","examples":[{"en":"Some areas of the stadium are open to visitors.","zh":"球場部分區域對遊客開放。"},{"en":"If a place is open to visitors, visitors are allowed to enter it.","zh":"如果某地方對遊客開放，即表示遊客可以進入。"},{"en":"The dressing rooms are open to visitors during the tour.","zh":"更衣室在導覽期間對遊客開放。"},{"en":"Areas not open to visitors may be locked for safety reasons.","zh":"基於安全原因，未對遊客開放的區域可能會上鎖。"},{"en":"The club shop is open to visitors after the tour.","zh":"球會商店在導覽後對遊客開放。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"just to let someone know","meaning":"只是想讓某人知道","examples":[{"en":"The guide wants to let mums and dads know a few things before the tour starts.","zh":"導遊在導覽開始前只是想讓爸爸媽媽知道幾件事。"},{"en":"“Just to let someone know” introduces information politely and casually.","zh":"「Just to let someone know」用來有禮貌而自然地介紹資訊。"},{"en":"Just to let you know, the players’ tunnel is quite dark.","zh":"只是想讓你知道，球員通道相當昏暗。"},{"en":"Guides use this phrase before giving reminders or warnings.","zh":"導遊在提供提醒或警告前會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"Just to let parents know, children should stay close during the tour.","zh":"只是想讓家長知道，孩子在導覽期間應留在附近。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"mums and dads","meaning":"爸爸媽媽；家長","examples":[{"en":"The guide gives some safety advice to mums and dads.","zh":"導遊向爸爸媽媽提供一些安全建議。"},{"en":"Mums and dads means parents, especially in informal speech.","zh":"「Mums and dads」指父母，特別用於非正式說話。"},{"en":"Mums and dads should keep their children close in busy places.","zh":"爸爸媽媽應在繁忙地方讓孩子留在身邊。"},{"en":"The guide speaks directly to mums and dads because children may need supervision.","zh":"導遊直接向家長說話，因為孩子可能需要看管。"},{"en":"Mums and dads can take photos during the penalty activity.","zh":"爸爸媽媽可以在踢十二碼活動中拍照。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"before we start","meaning":"在我們開始之前","examples":[{"en":"The guide explains a few things before they start.","zh":"導遊在他們開始之前解釋幾件事。"},{"en":"“Before we start” means before the activity begins.","zh":"「Before we start」表示在活動開始之前。"},{"en":"Before we start, please check that your children are with you.","zh":"在我們開始之前，請確認你的孩子在你身邊。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used before giving instructions.","zh":"這個短語常用於給出指示之前。"},{"en":"The guide gives practical information before they start the tour.","zh":"導遊在開始導覽之前提供實用資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the players’ tunnel","meaning":"球員通道","examples":[{"en":"The players’ tunnel is very dark.","zh":"球員通道非常昏暗。"},{"en":"The players’ tunnel is the passage players use to move between the dressing rooms and the pitch.","zh":"球員通道是球員在更衣室和球場之間行走的通道。"},{"en":"Visitors walked through the players’ tunnel during the tour.","zh":"遊客在導覽期間穿過球員通道。"},{"en":"Children should not wander off in the players’ tunnel because it may be dark.","zh":"孩子不應在球員通道亂走，因為那裏可能很暗。"},{"en":"Walking through the players’ tunnel can make visitors imagine match day.","zh":"走過球員通道可以令遊客想像比賽日情景。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"wander off","meaning":"走開；亂走","examples":[{"en":"Parents should not let their children wander off.","zh":"家長不應讓孩子走開亂走。"},{"en":"To wander off means to walk away from the group without a clear purpose or permission.","zh":"走開或亂走，是指沒有清楚目的或未經允許便離開團體。"},{"en":"A child wandered off while the guide was speaking.","zh":"導遊說話時，一名孩子走開了。"},{"en":"In a large stadium, children can get lost if they wander off.","zh":"在大型球場中，如果孩子亂走，可能會迷路。"},{"en":"Parents should hold younger children’s hands so they do not wander off.","zh":"家長應牽着年幼孩子的手，以免他們走開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on their own","meaning":"獨自；自己一個","examples":[{"en":"Children should not wander off on their own.","zh":"孩子不應獨自走開。"},{"en":"On their own means alone, without help or supervision from others.","zh":"獨自是指沒有他人幫助或看管。"},{"en":"Young children should not explore the stadium on their own.","zh":"年幼孩子不應自己一個探索球場。"},{"en":"Visitors can use the audio guide on their own if they choose a self-guided tour.","zh":"如果遊客選擇自助導覽，可以自己使用語音導覽。"},{"en":"Parents should not leave children on their own in dark areas.","zh":"家長不應把孩子獨自留在昏暗區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"even for a minute","meaning":"即使只是一分鐘","examples":[{"en":"Children should not wander off, even for a minute.","zh":"孩子不應走開，即使只是一分鐘。"},{"en":"“Even for a minute” means not even for a very short time.","zh":"「Even for a minute」表示即使是非常短的時間也不可以。"},{"en":"Do not leave your bag unattended, even for a minute.","zh":"不要把袋子無人看管，即使只是一分鐘。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the rule is important at all times.","zh":"這個短語強調規則在任何時候都很重要。"},{"en":"A child can become frightened quickly, even after only a minute alone.","zh":"孩子即使只獨處一分鐘，也可能很快受到驚嚇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"get frightened","meaning":"受到驚嚇","examples":[{"en":"The guide does not want anyone to get frightened.","zh":"導遊不希望任何人受到驚嚇。"},{"en":"To get frightened means to become scared or worried suddenly.","zh":"受到驚嚇，是指突然變得害怕或擔心。"},{"en":"A child may get frightened in a dark tunnel.","zh":"孩子在昏暗通道中可能會受到驚嚇。"},{"en":"Clear instructions can prevent visitors from getting frightened during the tour.","zh":"清楚指示可以避免遊客在導覽期間受到驚嚇。"},{"en":"Parents should stay close so children do not get frightened.","zh":"家長應留在附近，以免孩子受到驚嚇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cameras are permitted","meaning":"可以使用相機","examples":[{"en":"Cameras are permitted everywhere in the stadium.","zh":"球場內所有地方都可以使用相機。"},{"en":"If cameras are permitted, people are allowed to use cameras.","zh":"如果可以使用相機，即表示人們獲准使用相機。"},{"en":"Cameras are permitted during the stadium tour, but flash may not be allowed in some areas.","zh":"球場導覽期間可以使用相機，但某些區域可能不准使用閃光燈。"},{"en":"Visitors are happy when cameras are permitted because they can keep memories of the trip.","zh":"遊客知道可以使用相機時會很高興，因為可以留下旅程回憶。"},{"en":"The guide clearly states where cameras are permitted.","zh":"導遊清楚說明哪些地方可以使用相機。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"take pictures of","meaning":"拍攝……的照片","examples":[{"en":"Parents can take pictures of their child shooting a penalty.","zh":"家長可以拍攝孩子踢十二碼的照片。"},{"en":"To take pictures of something means to photograph it.","zh":"拍攝某物的照片，是指為它拍照。"},{"en":"Visitors took pictures of the pitch from the seating area.","zh":"遊客從座位區拍攝球場照片。"},{"en":"Parents often like taking pictures of special activities during family visits.","zh":"家長通常喜歡在家庭參觀中拍攝特別活動的照片。"},{"en":"You can take pictures of the stadium as long as you do not block the tour group.","zh":"只要不阻礙導覽團，你可以拍攝球場照片。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"shoot a penalty","meaning":"踢十二碼","examples":[{"en":"A child can shoot a penalty during the stadium visit.","zh":"孩子可以在參觀球場期間踢十二碼。"},{"en":"To shoot a penalty means to take a penalty kick in football.","zh":"踢十二碼是指在足球中射十二碼罰球。"},{"en":"The young visitor was excited to shoot a penalty on the pitch.","zh":"年輕遊客很興奮能在球場上踢十二碼。"},{"en":"Shooting a penalty gives children a fun memory of the stadium tour.","zh":"踢十二碼讓孩子對球場導覽留下有趣回憶。"},{"en":"Assistants help organise the activity so each child can shoot safely.","zh":"助手協助安排活動，讓每個孩子都能安全射門。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"organise this","meaning":"安排這件事","examples":[{"en":"Assistants are helping to organise the penalty activity.","zh":"助手正在協助安排踢十二碼活動。"},{"en":"To organise this means to arrange the activity or task being discussed.","zh":"安排這件事，是指安排正在談論的活動或任務。"},{"en":"Staff will organise this so that children take turns safely.","zh":"職員會安排這件事，讓孩子安全輪流參與。"},{"en":"Good organisation helps the queue move quickly.","zh":"良好安排可以令隊伍更快前進。"},{"en":"The assistants organise this activity near the pitch.","zh":"助手在球場附近安排這項活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hopefully","meaning":"希望","examples":[{"en":"Hopefully, the queue will not be too long.","zh":"希望人龍不會太長。"},{"en":"“Hopefully” means the speaker hopes that something will happen.","zh":"「Hopefully」表示講者希望某事會發生。"},{"en":"Hopefully, everyone will get a chance to shoot a penalty.","zh":"希望每個人都有機會踢十二碼。"},{"en":"This word expresses a wish, not a certainty.","zh":"這個詞表達願望，而不是肯定。"},{"en":"Hopefully, the weather will stay dry during the tour.","zh":"希望導覽期間天氣保持乾爽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the queue won’t be too long","meaning":"人龍不會太長","examples":[{"en":"The guide hopes the queue will not be too long.","zh":"導遊希望人龍不會太長。"},{"en":"If the queue is not too long, people will not have to wait for a long time.","zh":"如果人龍不太長，人們便不用等很久。"},{"en":"The queue for the penalty activity was not too long in the morning.","zh":"早上的踢十二碼活動人龍不算太長。"},{"en":"A shorter queue makes the activity more enjoyable for children.","zh":"較短的人龍令孩子更享受活動。"},{"en":"Assistants help organise the queue so it does not become too long.","zh":"助手協助安排隊伍，以免人龍變得太長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"out on the pitch","meaning":"在球場上","examples":[{"en":"It is very hot and sunny out on the pitch today.","zh":"今天在球場上非常炎熱和陽光猛烈。"},{"en":"Out on the pitch means outside on the playing field.","zh":"在球場上是指在戶外比賽草地上。"},{"en":"Visitors should wear sunhats out on the pitch.","zh":"遊客在球場上應戴太陽帽。"},{"en":"It can feel hotter out on the pitch because there is little shade.","zh":"球場上可能感覺更熱，因為遮蔭較少。"},{"en":"Children should drink water before going out on the pitch.","zh":"孩子到球場上之前應喝水。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the pitch","meaning":"球場；草地球場","examples":[{"en":"The pitch is very hot and sunny today.","zh":"今天草地球場非常炎熱和陽光猛烈。"},{"en":"The pitch is the playing field where football matches take place.","zh":"草地球場是舉行足球比賽的比賽場地。"},{"en":"The players walked onto the pitch before the match.","zh":"球員在比賽前走上球場。"},{"en":"Visitors may be allowed to stand near the pitch during the tour.","zh":"遊客在導覽期間可能可以站在草地球場附近。"},{"en":"The pitch must be protected so visitors should follow the guide’s instructions.","zh":"草地球場需要受到保護，所以遊客應遵守導遊指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get food and drink","meaning":"買食物和飲品","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can get food and drink at the café.","zh":"遊客可以在咖啡店買食物和飲品。"},{"en":"To get food and drink means to buy or receive something to eat and drink.","zh":"買食物和飲品，是指購買或取得吃喝的東西。"},{"en":"Families can get food and drink after the stadium tour.","zh":"家庭可以在球場導覽後買食物和飲品。"},{"en":"On a hot day, visitors should get drinks before going outside.","zh":"在炎熱日子，遊客外出前應買飲品。"},{"en":"The café is the best place to get food and drink inside the stadium.","zh":"咖啡店是球場內買食物和飲品的最佳地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"I really recommend","meaning":"我非常推薦","examples":[{"en":"The guide really recommends the healthy lunch boxes for children.","zh":"導遊非常推薦兒童健康午餐盒。"},{"en":"“I really recommend” means the speaker strongly suggests something because they think it is good.","zh":"「I really recommend」表示講者因認為某物很好而強烈建議。"},{"en":"I really recommend bringing water on a sunny day.","zh":"我非常推薦在陽光猛烈的日子帶水。"},{"en":"Guides use this phrase when they want visitors to consider a useful option.","zh":"導遊想遊客考慮有用選項時，會使用這個句式。"},{"en":"I really recommend the audio guide if you prefer a self-guided visit.","zh":"如果你較喜歡自助導覽，我非常推薦語音導覽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"healthy lunch boxes","meaning":"健康午餐盒","examples":[{"en":"The café sells healthy lunch boxes for children.","zh":"咖啡店售賣兒童健康午餐盒。"},{"en":"Healthy lunch boxes are packed meals with food chosen to be nutritious and balanced.","zh":"健康午餐盒是含有營養和均衡食物的外帶餐盒。"},{"en":"The healthy lunch boxes include fruit, sandwiches, and water.","zh":"健康午餐盒包括水果、三文治和水。"},{"en":"Parents may prefer healthy lunch boxes to sweets and fried snacks.","zh":"家長可能較喜歡健康午餐盒，而不是糖果和油炸小食。"},{"en":"A healthy lunch box can help children stay energetic during the visit.","zh":"健康午餐盒可以幫助孩子在參觀期間保持活力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be invited to do something","meaning":"獲邀做某事","examples":[{"en":"Children are invited to do a football-themed drawing.","zh":"孩子獲邀畫一幅足球主題繪畫。"},{"en":"To be invited to do something means to be asked or encouraged to take part in an activity.","zh":"獲邀做某事，是指被請求或鼓勵參與一項活動。"},{"en":"Visitors are invited to take photos on the pitch.","zh":"遊客獲邀在球場上拍照。"},{"en":"Children may feel excited when they are invited to join a competition.","zh":"當孩子獲邀參加比賽時，可能會感到興奮。"},{"en":"At the café, children are invited to create drawings for a prize.","zh":"在咖啡店，孩子獲邀創作畫作以競逐獎品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"football-themed drawing","meaning":"足球主題繪畫","examples":[{"en":"Children can do a football-themed drawing in the café.","zh":"孩子可以在咖啡店畫足球主題繪畫。"},{"en":"A football-themed drawing is a picture connected with football.","zh":"足球主題繪畫是與足球有關的圖畫。"},{"en":"The boy drew a football-themed drawing of a goalkeeper saving a penalty.","zh":"那個男孩畫了一幅守門員撲出十二碼的足球主題繪畫。"},{"en":"A football-themed drawing activity keeps children busy during the visit.","zh":"足球主題繪畫活動可以讓孩子在參觀期間有事可做。"},{"en":"Staff will choose the best football-themed drawing at the end of the afternoon.","zh":"職員會在下午結束時選出最佳足球主題繪畫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pick the best one","meaning":"選出最好的那一個","examples":[{"en":"The staff will pick the best drawing at the end of the afternoon.","zh":"職員會在下午結束時選出最好的畫作。"},{"en":"To pick the best one means to choose the one judged to be the strongest or most suitable.","zh":"選出最好的那一個，是指選擇被評為最出色或最合適的一個。"},{"en":"The judges will pick the best one from all the children’s pictures.","zh":"評判會從所有孩子的圖畫中選出最好的那一個。"},{"en":"Staff should use fair criteria when they pick the best one.","zh":"職員選出最好的那一個時，應使用公平標準。"},{"en":"Children should write their contact details so the prize can be sent if their drawing is picked.","zh":"孩子應寫上聯絡資料，這樣如果畫作獲選，獎品便可以寄出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at the end of the afternoon","meaning":"在下午結束時","examples":[{"en":"The best drawing will be chosen at the end of the afternoon.","zh":"最佳畫作會在下午結束時選出。"},{"en":"At the end of the afternoon means near the time when the afternoon finishes.","zh":"在下午結束時，是指接近下午完結的時間。"},{"en":"The winner will be announced at the end of the afternoon.","zh":"得獎者會在下午結束時公布。"},{"en":"Visitors may have left by the end of the afternoon, so contact details are needed.","zh":"遊客到下午結束時可能已離開，所以需要聯絡資料。"},{"en":"The café closes at the end of the afternoon after the competition.","zh":"比賽後，咖啡店會在下午結束時關門。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"don’t forget to","meaning":"不要忘記","examples":[{"en":"Visitors should not forget to put their contact details on the drawing.","zh":"遊客不要忘記把聯絡資料寫在畫作上。"},{"en":"“Don’t forget to” reminds someone to do something important.","zh":"「Don’t forget to」提醒某人做重要事情。"},{"en":"Don’t forget to bring water for the tour.","zh":"不要忘記帶水參加導覽。"},{"en":"Guides use this phrase to prevent visitors from missing important steps.","zh":"導遊使用這個句式，以免遊客遺漏重要步驟。"},{"en":"Don’t forget to write your name on the back of the drawing.","zh":"不要忘記在畫作背面寫上名字。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"contact details","meaning":"聯絡資料","examples":[{"en":"Children should put their name and contact details on the back of the drawing.","zh":"孩子應在畫作背面寫上姓名和聯絡資料。"},{"en":"Contact details are information used to reach someone, such as a phone number, email, or address.","zh":"聯絡資料是用來聯絡某人的資訊，例如電話號碼、電郵或地址。"},{"en":"Please write your contact details clearly on the form.","zh":"請在表格上清楚寫上聯絡資料。"},{"en":"Staff need contact details so they can send the prize to the winner.","zh":"職員需要聯絡資料，才能把獎品寄給得獎者。"},{"en":"Visitors should be careful when sharing contact details.","zh":"遊客分享聯絡資料時應小心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on the back","meaning":"在背面","examples":[{"en":"Visitors should write their contact details on the back.","zh":"遊客應在背面寫上聯絡資料。"},{"en":"On the back means on the reverse side of a page, card, or drawing.","zh":"在背面是指在紙張、卡片或畫作的反面。"},{"en":"Write your name on the back of the ticket.","zh":"請在門票背面寫上你的名字。"},{"en":"Putting details on the back keeps the front of the drawing clean.","zh":"把資料寫在背面，可以保持畫作正面整潔。"},{"en":"Staff can check the back of the drawing to find the winner’s address.","zh":"職員可以查看畫作背面，以找到得獎者地址。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"That way","meaning":"這樣一來","examples":[{"en":"That way, the staff can send the prize if the visitor has left.","zh":"這樣一來，如果遊客已經離開，職員可以寄出獎品。"},{"en":"“That way” means by doing this, a particular result can happen.","zh":"「That way」表示透過這樣做，某個結果便可以發生。"},{"en":"Write your address clearly; that way, we can contact you later.","zh":"清楚寫上地址；這樣一來，我們之後可以聯絡你。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an action with its practical result.","zh":"這個短語把行動與實際結果連接起來。"},{"en":"Put your details on the back; that way, the staff can send your prize.","zh":"把資料寫在背面；這樣一來，職員可以寄出你的獎品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"leave the stadium","meaning":"離開球場","examples":[{"en":"Some visitors may leave the stadium before the prize is chosen.","zh":"一些遊客可能在獎品選出前離開球場。"},{"en":"To leave the stadium means to go out of the stadium and no longer stay there.","zh":"離開球場是指走出球場，不再留在裏面。"},{"en":"Visitors can leave the stadium through the main exit.","zh":"遊客可以經正門出口離開球場。"},{"en":"If families leave the stadium early, staff may need their contact details.","zh":"如果家庭提早離開球場，職員可能需要他們的聯絡資料。"},{"en":"Please check you have all your belongings before you leave the stadium.","zh":"離開球場前，請檢查自己是否帶齊所有物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"send your prize","meaning":"寄出你的獎品","examples":[{"en":"The staff will send the prize if the winner has already left.","zh":"如果得獎者已經離開，職員會寄出獎品。"},{"en":"To send your prize means to deliver the prize to you after the event.","zh":"寄出你的獎品，是指活動後把獎品送到你手上。"},{"en":"We will send your prize to the address on the back of your drawing.","zh":"我們會把你的獎品寄到畫作背面的地址。"},{"en":"Contact details are needed so staff can send the prize correctly.","zh":"需要聯絡資料，職員才能正確寄出獎品。"},{"en":"If the winner is not present, the club will send the prize later.","zh":"如果得獎者不在場，球會稍後會寄出獎品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"return drawings","meaning":"退還畫作","examples":[{"en":"The stadium cannot return drawings after the competition.","zh":"球場在比賽後不能退還畫作。"},{"en":"To return drawings means to give the drawings back to the people who made them.","zh":"退還畫作是指把圖畫交回創作者。"},{"en":"The school returned the drawings after the art show.","zh":"學校在藝術展後退還畫作。"},{"en":"Visitors should understand that competition drawings may not be returned.","zh":"遊客應明白比賽畫作可能不會退還。"},{"en":"Since the stadium cannot return drawings, children may want to take a photo first.","zh":"既然球場不能退還畫作，孩子可能想先拍照留念。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mention some features of","meaning":"提及……的一些特色","examples":[{"en":"The guide mentions some features of the tour.","zh":"導遊提及導覽的一些特色。"},{"en":"To mention some features of something means to briefly describe some of its important parts.","zh":"提及某事的一些特色，是指簡短描述其中一些重要部分。"},{"en":"The guide mentioned some features of the new audio guide.","zh":"導遊提及新語音導覽的一些特色。"},{"en":"Mentioning features helps visitors decide what interests them most.","zh":"提及特色可以幫助遊客決定自己最感興趣的部分。"},{"en":"The speaker mentioned some features of the tour before it began.","zh":"講者在導覽開始前提及了一些特色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"features of the tour","meaning":"導覽的特色","examples":[{"en":"The guide explains the main features of the stadium tour.","zh":"導遊解釋球場導覽的主要特色。"},{"en":"Features of the tour are the main parts or activities included in the visit.","zh":"導覽的特色是參觀中包括的主要部分或活動。"},{"en":"The features of the tour include the cinema experience and dressing rooms.","zh":"導覽特色包括影院體驗和更衣室。"},{"en":"Visitors should listen carefully to learn the features of the tour.","zh":"遊客應仔細聆聽，以了解導覽的特色。"},{"en":"Some features of the tour may be new this year.","zh":"導覽的一些特色可能是今年新增的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"start with","meaning":"以……開始","examples":[{"en":"The tour will start with the 360 cinema experience.","zh":"導覽會以 360 度影院體驗開始。"},{"en":"To start with something means to begin by doing or seeing that thing first.","zh":"以某事開始，是指首先做或觀看該事。"},{"en":"The visit starts with a short safety talk.","zh":"參觀以簡短安全講解開始。"},{"en":"Starting with a cinema experience can introduce the club’s history dramatically.","zh":"以影院體驗開始，可以用戲劇化方式介紹球會歷史。"},{"en":"The guide starts with practical information before leading the group inside.","zh":"導遊先以實用資料開始，然後帶團體進入場內。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the 360 cinema experience","meaning":"360 度影院體驗","examples":[{"en":"The 360 cinema experience has been very popular over the years.","zh":"360 度影院體驗多年來非常受歡迎。"},{"en":"The 360 cinema experience is a film or visual show that surrounds viewers with images and sound.","zh":"360 度影院體驗是以影像和聲音包圍觀眾的電影或視覺節目。"},{"en":"Visitors begin the tour with the 360 cinema experience.","zh":"遊客以 360 度影院體驗開始導覽。"},{"en":"A 360 cinema experience can make people feel as if they are inside a match.","zh":"360 度影院體驗可以令人感覺自己置身比賽之中。"},{"en":"The club uses the 360 cinema experience to show its history in an exciting way.","zh":"球會使用 360 度影院體驗，以刺激方式展示其歷史。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"over the years","meaning":"多年來","examples":[{"en":"The cinema experience has been popular over the years.","zh":"影院體驗多年來一直受歡迎。"},{"en":"Over the years means during a long period of time.","zh":"多年來是指在一段很長時間內。"},{"en":"The stadium has changed a lot over the years.","zh":"這座球場多年來改變了很多。"},{"en":"Features that remain popular over the years are often worth keeping.","zh":"多年來仍受歡迎的特色通常值得保留。"},{"en":"Over the years, many fans have visited the stadium tour.","zh":"多年來，許多球迷參加過球場導覽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the players’ dressing rooms","meaning":"球員更衣室","examples":[{"en":"The guide will take visitors to the players’ dressing rooms.","zh":"導遊會帶遊客到球員更衣室。"},{"en":"The players’ dressing rooms are rooms where players change clothes and prepare for matches.","zh":"球員更衣室是球員換衣服和準備比賽的房間。"},{"en":"Fans were excited to see the players’ dressing rooms.","zh":"球迷很興奮能參觀球員更衣室。"},{"en":"Dressing rooms can show visitors what happens before a match.","zh":"更衣室可以讓遊客了解比賽前會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"The players’ dressing rooms are usually not open to the public except on tours.","zh":"球員更衣室通常不對公眾開放，只有導覽期間例外。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the seating area","meaning":"座位區","examples":[{"en":"Visitors will go outside to the seating area and the pitch.","zh":"遊客會到外面的座位區和球場。"},{"en":"The seating area is the part of the stadium where spectators sit to watch matches.","zh":"座位區是球場中觀眾坐下觀看比賽的部分。"},{"en":"The seating area gives visitors a clear view of the pitch.","zh":"座位區讓遊客清楚看到草地球場。"},{"en":"The guide explained which seating area belonged to home supporters.","zh":"導遊解釋哪個座位區屬於主隊球迷。"},{"en":"Visitors should walk carefully in the seating area because there may be steps.","zh":"遊客在座位區應小心行走，因為可能有梯級。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"I should say","meaning":"我應該說明一下","examples":[{"en":"The guide says, “I should say, if you’d prefer your visit to be self-guided…”","zh":"導遊說：「我應該說明一下，如果你較喜歡自助導覽……」"},{"en":"“I should say” introduces extra information that the speaker thinks should be mentioned.","zh":"「I should say」用來引入講者認為應該補充的資料。"},{"en":"I should say that cameras are permitted everywhere.","zh":"我應該說明一下，所有地方都可以使用相機。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when adding an important note.","zh":"這個短語適合用來補充重要說明。"},{"en":"I should say that visitors can choose an audio guide instead of a guided tour.","zh":"我應該說明一下，遊客可以選擇語音導覽，而不是跟團導覽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prefer something to be self-guided","meaning":"比較喜歡自助導覽","examples":[{"en":"Some visitors may prefer their visit to be self-guided.","zh":"一些遊客可能比較喜歡自助導覽。"},{"en":"To prefer something to be self-guided means to want to do it independently without a live guide.","zh":"比較喜歡某事自助導覽，是指想獨立進行，而不是由現場導遊帶領。"},{"en":"Some tourists prefer museum visits to be self-guided.","zh":"一些遊客比較喜歡自助參觀博物館。"},{"en":"A self-guided visit allows people to spend more time in areas they like.","zh":"自助導覽讓人們在喜歡的區域花更多時間。"},{"en":"Visitors who prefer the tour to be self-guided can use headphones.","zh":"比較喜歡自助導覽的遊客可以使用耳機。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"self-guided","meaning":"自助導覽的","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can choose a self-guided stadium visit.","zh":"遊客可以選擇自助導覽的球場參觀。"},{"en":"Self-guided means done independently, with information provided but without a guide leading you.","zh":"自助導覽的意思是獨立進行，雖有資料提供，但沒有導遊帶領。"},{"en":"The museum offers a self-guided tour with an audio device.","zh":"博物館提供配有語音設備的自助導覽。"},{"en":"A self-guided visit is useful for people who want to move at their own speed.","zh":"自助導覽適合想按自己速度參觀的人。"},{"en":"Some visitors prefer self-guided tours because they can pause whenever they like.","zh":"一些遊客喜歡自助導覽，因為可以隨時停下來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"collect headphones from","meaning":"從……領取耳機","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can collect headphones from the reception.","zh":"遊客可以從接待處領取耳機。"},{"en":"To collect headphones from a place means to go there and receive headphones.","zh":"從某處領取耳機，是指到該地方取得耳機。"},{"en":"Please collect headphones from the information desk before the audio tour.","zh":"語音導覽前，請從詢問處領取耳機。"},{"en":"Visitors need headphones to listen to the pre-recorded information.","zh":"遊客需要耳機來聆聽預錄資料。"},{"en":"After the tour, visitors should return the headphones to reception.","zh":"導覽後，遊客應把耳機交還接待處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the reception","meaning":"接待處","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can get headphones from the reception.","zh":"遊客可以從接待處取得耳機。"},{"en":"The reception is the place where visitors are welcomed and given information.","zh":"接待處是迎接遊客和提供資訊的地方。"},{"en":"The reception is near the stadium entrance.","zh":"接待處位於球場入口附近。"},{"en":"Visitors should go to reception if they have questions about the tour.","zh":"如果遊客對導覽有問題，應前往接待處。"},{"en":"The audio guide headphones are collected from reception.","zh":"語音導覽耳機在接待處領取。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pre-recorded information","meaning":"預錄資料","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can listen to the pre-recorded information through headphones.","zh":"遊客可以透過耳機聆聽預錄資料。"},{"en":"Pre-recorded information is information recorded earlier and played back later.","zh":"預錄資料是較早錄製並稍後播放的資訊。"},{"en":"The audio guide provides pre-recorded information about the club’s history.","zh":"語音導覽提供關於球會歷史的預錄資料。"},{"en":"Pre-recorded information lets visitors learn without following a live guide.","zh":"預錄資料讓遊客不用跟隨現場導遊也能學習。"},{"en":"The stadium may update the pre-recorded information after receiving feedback.","zh":"球場可能會在收到意見後更新預錄資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at your own speed","meaning":"按自己的速度","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can listen to the information at their own speed.","zh":"遊客可以按自己的速度聆聽資料。"},{"en":"At your own speed means at the pace that suits you personally.","zh":"按自己的速度，是指以適合自己的節奏進行。"},{"en":"A self-guided tour allows visitors to move at their own speed.","zh":"自助導覽讓遊客按自己的速度移動。"},{"en":"Learning at your own speed can make information easier to understand.","zh":"按自己的速度學習可以令資料更容易理解。"},{"en":"Some visitors prefer to stop and read signs at their own speed.","zh":"一些遊客喜歡按自己的速度停下來閱讀指示牌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"only just introduced","meaning":"剛剛推出","examples":[{"en":"The stadium has only just introduced the audio guide.","zh":"球場剛剛推出語音導覽。"},{"en":"“Only just introduced” means something has been made available very recently.","zh":"「Only just introduced」表示某物最近才開始提供。"},{"en":"The club has only just introduced online booking for tours.","zh":"球會剛剛推出導覽網上預訂。"},{"en":"A newly introduced service may still need feedback and improvement.","zh":"新推出的服務可能仍需要意見和改善。"},{"en":"Since the audio guide has only just been introduced, visitors’ comments are especially useful.","zh":"由於語音導覽剛剛推出，遊客意見特別有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"appreciate your feedback","meaning":"希望得到你的意見","examples":[{"en":"The stadium would appreciate visitors’ feedback.","zh":"球場希望得到遊客的意見。"},{"en":"To appreciate your feedback means to value your opinions and comments.","zh":"希望得到你的意見，是指重視你的看法和評語。"},{"en":"We would appreciate your feedback on the new audio guide.","zh":"我們希望得到你對新語音導覽的意見。"},{"en":"Feedback helps the stadium improve future tours.","zh":"意見可以幫助球場改善日後導覽。"},{"en":"Visitors can leave feedback at reception after the tour.","zh":"遊客可以在導覽後到接待處留下意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"offer tours in other languages","meaning":"提供其他語言導覽","examples":[{"en":"The stadium may offer tours in other languages in future.","zh":"球場日後可能提供其他語言導覽。"},{"en":"To offer tours in other languages means to provide guided visits in languages besides the usual one.","zh":"提供其他語言導覽，是指提供常用語言以外的導覽。"},{"en":"The museum offers tours in Spanish and French.","zh":"博物館提供西班牙語和法語導覽。"},{"en":"Offering tours in other languages can attract more international visitors.","zh":"提供其他語言導覽可以吸引更多國際遊客。"},{"en":"Visitor feedback may help the stadium decide which languages to add.","zh":"遊客意見可能幫助球場決定增加哪些語言。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in future","meaning":"將來；日後","examples":[{"en":"The stadium may offer more language options in future.","zh":"球場日後可能提供更多語言選項。"},{"en":"In future means at a later time, not now.","zh":"將來或日後是指較後時間，而不是現在。"},{"en":"The club hopes to add more tour times in future.","zh":"球會希望日後增加更多導覽時段。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when talking about possible later plans.","zh":"這個短語用於談論稍後可能實行的計劃。"},{"en":"In future, visitors may be able to book tours in several languages.","zh":"將來，遊客可能可以預訂多種語言導覽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have any thoughts on","meaning":"對……有任何想法","examples":[{"en":"The guide welcomes any thoughts visitors have on language options.","zh":"導遊歡迎遊客對語言選項有任何想法。"},{"en":"To have thoughts on something means to have opinions, ideas, or suggestions about it.","zh":"對某事有想法，是指對它有意見、想法或建議。"},{"en":"Do you have any thoughts on the new audio guide?","zh":"你對新的語音導覽有任何想法嗎？"},{"en":"Asking for thoughts encourages visitors to share suggestions freely.","zh":"詢問想法可以鼓勵遊客自由分享建議。"},{"en":"The stadium wants to know visitors’ thoughts on future language tours.","zh":"球場想知道遊客對未來語言導覽的想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"welcome those too","meaning":"也歡迎那些意見","examples":[{"en":"The stadium would welcome visitors’ thoughts on future tours.","zh":"球場也歡迎遊客對未來導覽的想法。"},{"en":"“Welcome those too” means those ideas or comments are also invited and appreciated.","zh":"「Welcome those too」表示那些想法或意見也受到歡迎和重視。"},{"en":"If you have suggestions about languages, we would welcome those too.","zh":"如果你有關於語言的建議，我們也歡迎那些意見。"},{"en":"This phrase shows openness to extra feedback.","zh":"這個短語顯示願意接受額外回饋。"},{"en":"The guide welcomes comments on the audio guide and on future tour options too.","zh":"導遊歡迎對語音導覽的意見，也歡迎對未來導覽選項的意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"plan to return another time","meaning":"打算下次再來","examples":[{"en":"Visitors who plan to return another time might book a VIP tour.","zh":"打算下次再來的遊客可以預訂 VIP 導覽。"},{"en":"To plan to return another time means to intend to come back on a later occasion.","zh":"打算下次再來，是指計劃在日後另一次再回來。"},{"en":"If you plan to return another time, check the website for VIP tours.","zh":"如果你打算下次再來，請查看網站上的 VIP 導覽。"},{"en":"Visitors may return another time if they enjoy the first tour.","zh":"如果遊客喜歡第一次導覽，可能會下次再來。"},{"en":"Planning to return gives fans a chance to try a different tour experience.","zh":"打算再次來訪讓球迷有機會嘗試不同導覽體驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"book one of our VIP tours","meaning":"預訂其中一個 VIP 導覽","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can book one of the VIP tours online.","zh":"遊客可以在網上預訂其中一個 VIP 導覽。"},{"en":"To book one of our VIP tours means to reserve a special premium tour offered by the stadium.","zh":"預訂其中一個 VIP 導覽，是指預留球場提供的特別高級導覽。"},{"en":"Fans can book one of the VIP tours for a birthday celebration.","zh":"球迷可以為生日慶祝預訂其中一個 VIP 導覽。"},{"en":"VIP tours may include extra areas not available on the normal tour.","zh":"VIP 導覽可能包括普通導覽沒有的額外區域。"},{"en":"Visitors should book VIP tours early because spaces may be limited.","zh":"遊客應早點預訂 VIP 導覽，因為名額可能有限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"can be booked online","meaning":"可以網上預訂","examples":[{"en":"VIP tours can be booked online.","zh":"VIP 導覽可以網上預訂。"},{"en":"If something can be booked online, people can reserve it through a website.","zh":"如果某物可以網上預訂，即表示人們可以透過網站預留它。"},{"en":"Stadium tickets can be booked online before match day.","zh":"球場門票可以在比賽日前網上預訂。"},{"en":"Online booking is convenient because visitors can choose a date before arriving.","zh":"網上預訂很方便，因為遊客可以在到達前選擇日期。"},{"en":"VIP tours can be booked online, so visitors do not need to phone the club.","zh":"VIP 導覽可以網上預訂，所以遊客不需要打電話給球會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the stadium you see today","meaning":"你們今天看到的球場","examples":[{"en":"The stadium you see today was built in 1989.","zh":"你們今天看到的球場建於 1989 年。"},{"en":"The stadium you see today means the current stadium building that visitors are looking at now.","zh":"你們今天看到的球場，是指遊客現在正在看的現有球場建築。"},{"en":"The stadium you see today is different from the old ground used in the past.","zh":"你們今天看到的球場與過去使用的舊主場不同。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect present-day visitors with the stadium’s history.","zh":"這個短語幫助把今天的遊客與球場歷史連接起來。"},{"en":"Although the club is old, the stadium you see today is more modern.","zh":"雖然球會歷史悠久，但你們今天看到的球場較現代化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be built in","meaning":"建於","examples":[{"en":"The stadium was built in 1989.","zh":"這座球場建於 1989 年。"},{"en":"To be built in a year means to have been constructed during that year.","zh":"建於某一年，是指在該年建造完成或建造。"},{"en":"The new stand was built in 2005.","zh":"新看台建於 2005 年。"},{"en":"Knowing when a stadium was built helps visitors understand its history.","zh":"知道球場建於何時，可以幫助遊客理解其歷史。"},{"en":"The stadium was built in 1989 as part of a redevelopment project.","zh":"這座球場作為重建項目的一部分，建於 1989 年。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as part of","meaning":"作為……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"The stadium was built as part of a three-year redevelopment project.","zh":"這座球場作為三年重建項目的一部分而建成。"},{"en":"As part of something means included within a larger plan, project, or activity.","zh":"作為某事的一部分，是指包括在較大的計劃、項目或活動之內。"},{"en":"The museum was rebuilt as part of the town improvement project.","zh":"博物館作為城鎮改善項目的一部分而重建。"},{"en":"A stadium may be modernised as part of wider redevelopment.","zh":"球場可能作為更大規模重建的一部分而現代化。"},{"en":"The new seating area was added as part of the renovation.","zh":"新座位區作為翻新工程的一部分加入。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"redevelopment project","meaning":"重建項目","examples":[{"en":"The stadium was built during a three-year redevelopment project.","zh":"這座球場是在一項三年重建項目期間建成的。"},{"en":"A redevelopment project is a planned project to rebuild or improve an existing area or building.","zh":"重建項目是有計劃地重建或改善現有地區或建築的項目。"},{"en":"The town centre redevelopment project included shops and public spaces.","zh":"鎮中心重建項目包括商店和公共空間。"},{"en":"A stadium redevelopment project may require the team to play elsewhere temporarily.","zh":"球場重建項目可能需要球隊暫時到其他地方比賽。"},{"en":"Redevelopment projects can improve facilities but may disrupt normal activities.","zh":"重建項目可以改善設施，但可能打亂正常活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"while that project was going on","meaning":"在該項目進行期間","examples":[{"en":"The team played elsewhere while that project was going on.","zh":"在該項目進行期間，球隊在其他地方比賽。"},{"en":"While that project was going on means during the time when the project was happening.","zh":"在該項目進行期間，是指該項目正在發生的時間內。"},{"en":"While the stadium work was going on, fans used a temporary entrance.","zh":"在球場工程進行期間，球迷使用臨時入口。"},{"en":"Teams sometimes need alternative arrangements while redevelopment is going on.","zh":"重建進行期間，球隊有時需要替代安排。"},{"en":"The club had to move matches while that project was going on.","zh":"在該項目進行期間，球會不得不把比賽移到別處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"play its matches","meaning":"進行比賽","examples":[{"en":"The team had to play its matches at another club’s ground.","zh":"球隊不得不在另一間球會的主場進行比賽。"},{"en":"To play its matches means for a team to hold or compete in its games.","zh":"進行比賽，是指球隊舉行或參與比賽。"},{"en":"The club played its matches on a rented pitch during redevelopment.","zh":"球會在重建期間於租用球場進行比賽。"},{"en":"A team may lose some home advantage if it cannot play its matches at its own ground.","zh":"如果球隊不能在自己主場進行比賽，可能會失去部分主場優勢。"},{"en":"Fans had to travel farther when the team played its matches elsewhere.","zh":"球隊在其他地方進行比賽時，球迷需要走更遠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the ground of another club","meaning":"另一間球會的主場","examples":[{"en":"The team had to use the ground of another club during redevelopment.","zh":"球隊在重建期間不得不使用另一間球會的主場。"},{"en":"The ground of another club means another football club’s stadium or home playing field.","zh":"另一間球會的主場，是指另一間足球會的球場或主場比賽場地。"},{"en":"During repairs, the team used the ground of another club.","zh":"維修期間，球隊使用另一間球會的主場。"},{"en":"Sharing another club’s ground can be inconvenient for players and fans.","zh":"共用另一間球會的主場可能對球員和球迷不便。"},{"en":"The redevelopment forced City Football Club to play away from its own site.","zh":"重建迫使 City 足球會離開自己的場址比賽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"apart from that","meaning":"除此之外","examples":[{"en":"Apart from that, the club has been on this site since 1870.","zh":"除此之外，球會自 1870 年起一直在這個場址。"},{"en":"Apart from that means except for the thing just mentioned.","zh":"除此之外，是指除了剛才提到的事情。"},{"en":"Apart from that one year, the team has always played here.","zh":"除了那一年之外，球隊一直在這裏比賽。"},{"en":"This phrase separates an exception from the general situation.","zh":"這個短語把例外情況與一般情況分開。"},{"en":"Apart from redevelopment, the club’s connection with this site has been continuous.","zh":"除了重建期間外，球會與這個場址的連繫一直持續。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on this site","meaning":"在這個場址","examples":[{"en":"The club has been on this site since 1870.","zh":"球會自 1870 年起一直在這個場址。"},{"en":"On this site means at this particular location or piece of land.","zh":"在這個場址，是指在這個特定位置或土地上。"},{"en":"The old stadium stood on this site before the new one was built.","zh":"新球場建成前，舊球場就位於這個場址。"},{"en":"Being on the same site for many years gives the club historical importance.","zh":"多年來一直在同一場址，令球會具有歷史意義。"},{"en":"Visitors are standing on the site where the club has played for generations.","zh":"遊客正站在球會多代以來比賽的場址上。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as some of you may know","meaning":"你們有些人可能知道","examples":[{"en":"As some of you may know, 1870 was an important year in football history.","zh":"你們有些人可能知道，1870 年是足球歷史中的重要年份。"},{"en":"“As some of you may know” introduces information that some listeners may already understand.","zh":"「As some of you may know」用來介紹部分聽眾可能已經知道的資料。"},{"en":"As some of you may know, football rules changed a lot in the 1870s.","zh":"你們有些人可能知道，足球規則在 1870 年代有很多改變。"},{"en":"This phrase politely includes both knowledgeable and less knowledgeable listeners.","zh":"這個短語有禮貌地照顧熟悉和不熟悉資料的聽眾。"},{"en":"As some of you may know, early football looked very different from today’s game.","zh":"你們有些人可能知道，早期足球與今天的比賽非常不同。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an important decade in","meaning":"……中重要的十年","examples":[{"en":"That was the start of an important decade in the history of football.","zh":"那是足球歷史中重要十年的開始。"},{"en":"An important decade in a subject is a ten-year period when major changes happened.","zh":"某範疇中重要的十年，是指發生重大改變的十年時期。"},{"en":"The 1870s were an important decade in the development of football rules.","zh":"1870 年代是足球規則發展中重要的十年。"},{"en":"An important decade can shape how a sport is played for generations.","zh":"重要的十年可以塑造一項運動之後多代人的玩法。"},{"en":"The guide explains why that period was important in football history.","zh":"導遊解釋為甚麼那段時期在足球歷史中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the history of football","meaning":"足球歷史","examples":[{"en":"The 1870s were important in the history of football.","zh":"1870 年代在足球歷史中很重要。"},{"en":"The history of football is the study or story of how football developed over time.","zh":"足球歷史是研究或講述足球如何隨時間發展的內容。"},{"en":"Goalkeepers and crossbars are part of the history of football.","zh":"守門員和橫樑都是足球歷史的一部分。"},{"en":"The history of football includes changes to rules, clubs, and stadiums.","zh":"足球歷史包括規則、球會和球場的變化。"},{"en":"Learning the history of football helps fans understand the modern game.","zh":"學習足球歷史可以幫助球迷理解現代足球。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"include a player whose role was to","meaning":"加入一名職責是……的球員","examples":[{"en":"Teams started to include a player whose role was to guard the goal.","zh":"球隊開始加入一名職責是把守球門的球員。"},{"en":"To include a player whose role was to do something means to add a team member with that specific job.","zh":"加入一名職責是做某事的球員，是指增加一名有特定工作的隊員。"},{"en":"Early teams began to include a player whose role was to stop shots.","zh":"早期球隊開始加入一名職責是阻擋射門的球員。"},{"en":"Adding a specialised player changed team structure.","zh":"加入專門球員改變了球隊結構。"},{"en":"Modern teams include players whose roles are clearly defined.","zh":"現代球隊會加入職責清晰的球員。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"guard the goal","meaning":"守門；把守球門","examples":[{"en":"The goalkeeper’s role was to guard the goal.","zh":"守門員的職責是把守球門。"},{"en":"To guard the goal means to protect the goal and stop the other team from scoring.","zh":"把守球門，是指保護球門並阻止對方入球。"},{"en":"The goalkeeper stood ready to guard the goal during the penalty.","zh":"守門員在十二碼期間準備好守門。"},{"en":"A player who guards the goal must react quickly.","zh":"把守球門的球員必須反應迅速。"},{"en":"Before goalkeepers were introduced, teams did not have one player whose only job was to guard the goal.","zh":"在守門員被引入前，球隊沒有一名唯一職責是守門的球員。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"It’s hard to imagine","meaning":"很難想像","examples":[{"en":"It is hard to imagine what football was like without goalkeepers.","zh":"很難想像沒有守門員的足球是甚麼樣子。"},{"en":"“It’s hard to imagine” means something is difficult to picture or understand.","zh":"「It’s hard to imagine」表示某事難以想像或理解。"},{"en":"It’s hard to imagine football without a fixed match length.","zh":"很難想像沒有固定比賽時長的足球。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the past situation feels strange to modern listeners.","zh":"這個短語顯示過去情況對現代聽眾來說很陌生。"},{"en":"It’s hard to imagine a goal without a solid crossbar today.","zh":"今天很難想像沒有實心橫樑的球門。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"someone in that position","meaning":"擔任那個位置的人","examples":[{"en":"The game was different before there was someone in that position.","zh":"在有擔任那個位置的人之前，比賽很不一樣。"},{"en":"Someone in that position means a person filling that role or place in a team.","zh":"擔任那個位置的人，是指在球隊中負責該角色或位置的人。"},{"en":"A goalkeeper is someone in the position of guarding the goal.","zh":"守門員就是擔任把守球門位置的人。"},{"en":"Without someone in that position, defending the goal was less specialised.","zh":"沒有擔任那個位置的人，守門工作較不專門。"},{"en":"Football changed when teams added someone in that position.","zh":"當球隊加入擔任那個位置的人時，足球改變了。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"clubs were established","meaning":"球會成立","examples":[{"en":"Many other clubs were established in 1872 and 1873.","zh":"許多其他球會在 1872 年和 1873 年成立。"},{"en":"If clubs were established, they were officially started or founded.","zh":"球會成立，是指它們正式開始或創辦。"},{"en":"Several football clubs were established during the 1870s.","zh":"幾間足球會在 1870 年代成立。"},{"en":"When clubs are established, they can join competitions and develop supporters.","zh":"球會成立後，可以參加比賽並發展支持者。"},{"en":"The establishment of clubs helped football become more organised.","zh":"球會的成立幫助足球變得更有組織。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"here and abroad","meaning":"本地及海外","examples":[{"en":"Many clubs were established both here and abroad.","zh":"許多球會在本地及海外成立。"},{"en":"Here and abroad means in this country and in other countries.","zh":"本地及海外是指在本國和其他國家。"},{"en":"Football became popular here and abroad during that period.","zh":"足球在那段時期於本地及海外變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"Clubs founded here and abroad helped spread the game internationally.","zh":"在本地及海外成立的球會幫助足球走向國際。"},{"en":"The guide explains how football developed both here and abroad.","zh":"導遊解釋足球如何在本地及海外發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the following year","meaning":"翌年；下一年","examples":[{"en":"The following year, referees were allowed to send players off.","zh":"翌年，裁判獲准罰球員離場。"},{"en":"The following year means the year after the one just mentioned.","zh":"翌年是指剛提及年份之後的一年。"},{"en":"The club was founded in 1872, and the following year it joined a league.","zh":"球會在 1872 年成立，翌年加入聯賽。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise historical events in order.","zh":"這個短語有助按時間順序整理歷史事件。"},{"en":"The following year brought another important rule change.","zh":"翌年帶來了另一項重要規則改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"referees were allowed to","meaning":"裁判獲准……","examples":[{"en":"Referees were allowed to send players off for certain offences.","zh":"裁判獲准因某些違規行為罰球員離場。"},{"en":"If referees were allowed to do something, the rules gave them permission to do it.","zh":"如果裁判獲准做某事，即表示規則給予他們做該事的權力。"},{"en":"Referees were allowed to stop the match in dangerous conditions.","zh":"裁判獲准在危險情況下停止比賽。"},{"en":"Giving referees clear powers helped make football more organised.","zh":"給予裁判清晰權力，幫助足球變得更有組織。"},{"en":"When referees were allowed to punish offences, players had to follow rules more carefully.","zh":"當裁判獲准處罰違規行為時，球員必須更小心遵守規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"send players off","meaning":"罰球員離場","examples":[{"en":"Referees could send players off if they committed certain offences.","zh":"如果球員犯下某些違規行為，裁判可以罰他們離場。"},{"en":"To send players off means to order players to leave the match as a punishment.","zh":"罰球員離場，是指命令球員離開比賽作為懲罰。"},{"en":"The referee sent the player off after a dangerous tackle.","zh":"裁判在一次危險攔截後罰該球員離場。"},{"en":"The ability to send players off helps referees control serious misconduct.","zh":"罰球員離場的權力幫助裁判控制嚴重不當行為。"},{"en":"A player who is sent off cannot continue playing in that match.","zh":"被罰離場的球員不能在該場比賽中繼續作賽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"commit certain offences","meaning":"犯下某些違規行為","examples":[{"en":"Players could be sent off if they committed certain offences.","zh":"如果球員犯下某些違規行為，便可能被罰離場。"},{"en":"To commit certain offences means to break particular rules.","zh":"犯下某些違規行為，是指違反特定規則。"},{"en":"A player may be punished if he commits a serious offence.","zh":"如果球員犯下嚴重違規行為，可能會受罰。"},{"en":"Football rules list offences that can lead to being sent off.","zh":"足球規則列出可能導致被罰離場的違規行為。"},{"en":"Referees need to judge whether a player has committed an offence.","zh":"裁判需要判斷球員是否犯規。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"swap ends at half-time","meaning":"中場時交換場地","examples":[{"en":"Teams started having to swap ends at half-time.","zh":"球隊開始必須在中場時交換場地。"},{"en":"To swap ends at half-time means for teams to change which goal they attack after the first half.","zh":"中場時交換場地，是指球隊在上半場後改變進攻方向。"},{"en":"Teams swap ends at half-time to make conditions fairer.","zh":"球隊中場交換場地，以令比賽條件更公平。"},{"en":"Wind, sunlight, and pitch conditions can affect why teams change ends.","zh":"風向、陽光和場地狀況都可能影響球隊為何要交換場地。"},{"en":"Swapping ends is now a normal part of football matches.","zh":"交換場地現在是足球比賽的正常部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one fact I was interested to discover","meaning":"我有興趣發現的一件事","examples":[{"en":"One fact the guide was interested to discover concerned early football goals.","zh":"導遊有興趣發現的一件事與早期足球球門有關。"},{"en":"“One fact I was interested to discover” introduces information the speaker found surprising or engaging.","zh":"「One fact I was interested to discover」用來介紹講者覺得驚訝或有趣的資料。"},{"en":"One fact I was interested to discover was that early goals used tape.","zh":"我有興趣發現的一件事是早期球門使用膠帶。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a historical detail sound personal and interesting.","zh":"這個短語令歷史細節聽起來較個人化和有趣。"},{"en":"The guide uses this phrase before explaining how goal design changed.","zh":"導遊在解釋球門設計如何改變前使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"early football games","meaning":"早期足球比賽","examples":[{"en":"Early football games used different kinds of goals.","zh":"早期足球比賽使用不同種類的球門。"},{"en":"Early football games were matches played in the earlier period of football history.","zh":"早期足球比賽是足球歷史較早時期進行的比賽。"},{"en":"Early football games often had rules that were less standardised than today’s rules.","zh":"早期足球比賽的規則通常不像今天那樣標準化。"},{"en":"Learning about early football games shows how much the sport has changed.","zh":"了解早期足球比賽可以看出這項運動改變了多少。"},{"en":"In early football games, goal structures were simpler than modern ones.","zh":"在早期足球比賽中，球門結構比現代球門簡單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the aim was for someone to","meaning":"目標是讓某人……","examples":[{"en":"The aim was for the scorer to get the ball between two flag posts.","zh":"目標是讓入球者把球踢進兩支旗桿之間。"},{"en":"“The aim was for someone to” explains what a person was supposed to achieve.","zh":"「The aim was for someone to」解釋某人應該達成甚麼。"},{"en":"The aim was for players to pass the ball into the goal area.","zh":"目標是讓球員把球傳入球門區域。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the purpose of an action or rule.","zh":"這個句式描述行動或規則的目的。"},{"en":"In early football, the aim was for the attacker to send the ball between posts.","zh":"在早期足球中，目標是讓進攻球員把球送入柱之間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get the ball between","meaning":"把球踢進……之間","examples":[{"en":"The scorer had to get the ball between two flag posts.","zh":"入球者必須把球踢進兩支旗桿之間。"},{"en":"To get the ball between two objects means to make the ball pass through the space between them.","zh":"把球踢進兩物之間，是指令球穿過它們之間的空間。"},{"en":"The player tried to get the ball between the goalposts.","zh":"球員嘗試把球踢進門柱之間。"},{"en":"Early football goals were scored by getting the ball between two posts.","zh":"早期足球是透過把球踢進兩支柱之間來得分。"},{"en":"Accuracy was needed to get the ball between the markers.","zh":"要把球踢進標記物之間，需要準確度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"flag posts","meaning":"旗桿","examples":[{"en":"Early football goals used two flag posts.","zh":"早期足球球門使用兩支旗桿。"},{"en":"Flag posts are upright poles that hold flags or mark positions.","zh":"旗桿是用來掛旗或標記位置的直立柱子。"},{"en":"The early goal was marked by two flag posts.","zh":"早期球門由兩支旗桿標示。"},{"en":"Flag posts were simpler than today’s goalposts and crossbars.","zh":"旗桿比今天的門柱和橫樑簡單。"},{"en":"Players had to send the ball between the flag posts to score.","zh":"球員必須把球送進旗桿之間才能得分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"joined at the top","meaning":"在頂端連接起來","examples":[{"en":"The sticks were joined at the top with a piece of tape.","zh":"這些木枝用一條膠帶在頂端連接起來。"},{"en":"Joined at the top means connected at the upper end.","zh":"在頂端連接起來，是指在上方末端相連。"},{"en":"The two poles were joined at the top to show the height of the goal.","zh":"兩支柱在頂端連接起來，以顯示球門高度。"},{"en":"A temporary goal can be made by joining two sticks at the top.","zh":"臨時球門可以透過把兩支木枝在頂端連接起來製成。"},{"en":"Later, tape joined at the top was replaced by a solid crossbar.","zh":"後來，在頂端連接的膠帶被實心橫樑取代。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a piece of tape","meaning":"一條膠帶","examples":[{"en":"The sticks were joined with a piece of tape.","zh":"這些木枝用一條膠帶連接起來。"},{"en":"A piece of tape is a strip of sticky material used to join or hold things together.","zh":"一條膠帶是用來黏合或固定物件的黏性材料。"},{"en":"The coach used a piece of tape to mark the goal height.","zh":"教練用一條膠帶標示球門高度。"},{"en":"A piece of tape was not as strong or clear as a crossbar.","zh":"一條膠帶不如橫樑堅固或清晰。"},{"en":"Early football goals sometimes used a piece of tape instead of a solid bar.","zh":"早期足球球門有時使用一條膠帶，而不是實心橫樑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be replaced with","meaning":"被……取代","examples":[{"en":"The tape was replaced with a solid crossbar in 1875.","zh":"膠帶在 1875 年被實心橫樑取代。"},{"en":"To be replaced with something means to be removed and changed for something else.","zh":"被某物取代，是指被移除並換成另一物。"},{"en":"The old seats were replaced with modern ones.","zh":"舊座椅被現代座椅取代。"},{"en":"Replacing tape with a crossbar made the goal clearer and stronger.","zh":"用橫樑取代膠帶令球門更清楚和堅固。"},{"en":"Many early football features were later replaced with more standard designs.","zh":"許多早期足球元素後來被更標準化的設計取代。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"solid crossbar","meaning":"實心橫樑","examples":[{"en":"The solid crossbar replaced the tape in 1875.","zh":"實心橫樑在 1875 年取代了膠帶。"},{"en":"A solid crossbar is the firm horizontal bar across the top of a football goal.","zh":"實心橫樑是足球球門頂部堅固的水平橫條。"},{"en":"The ball hit the solid crossbar and bounced back.","zh":"球擊中實心橫樑後彈回。"},{"en":"The introduction of a solid crossbar made goal design more like today’s.","zh":"引入實心橫樑令球門設計更接近今天。"},{"en":"A solid crossbar gives players and referees a clear boundary for the goal.","zh":"實心橫樑為球員和裁判提供清楚的球門界線。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be familiar with","meaning":"對……熟悉","examples":[{"en":"The solid crossbar is the design we are familiar with today.","zh":"實心橫樑是我們今天熟悉的設計。"},{"en":"To be familiar with something means to know it well because you have seen or used it before.","zh":"對某事熟悉，是指因曾見過或使用過而很了解它。"},{"en":"Most football fans are familiar with modern goalposts.","zh":"大多數足球迷都熟悉現代球門柱。"},{"en":"Visitors are familiar with today’s stadium design but may not know its history.","zh":"遊客熟悉今天的球場設計，但未必知道其歷史。"},{"en":"The crossbar design is familiar because it is used in football worldwide.","zh":"橫樑設計很熟悉，因為它在世界各地足球中使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"saw the founding of","meaning":"見證……的成立","examples":[{"en":"The year 1877 saw the founding of further new clubs.","zh":"1877 年見證了更多新球會的成立。"},{"en":"“Saw the founding of” means that something was founded during that time.","zh":"「Saw the founding of」表示某事在該時期成立。"},{"en":"The 1870s saw the founding of many football clubs.","zh":"1870 年代見證了許多足球會的成立。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in historical writing.","zh":"這個短語常用於歷史寫作。"},{"en":"The year saw the founding of organisations that helped football grow.","zh":"那一年見證了一些幫助足球發展的組織成立。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"further new clubs","meaning":"更多新球會","examples":[{"en":"Further new clubs were founded in 1877.","zh":"更多新球會在 1877 年成立。"},{"en":"Further new clubs means additional new clubs beyond those already mentioned.","zh":"更多新球會是指除了已提及的球會外，額外成立的新球會。"},{"en":"Further new clubs joined the football league as the sport grew.","zh":"隨着足球發展，更多新球會加入足球聯賽。"},{"en":"The founding of further new clubs showed football’s rising popularity.","zh":"更多新球會的成立顯示足球越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"More clubs meant more matches and stronger competition.","zh":"更多球會意味着更多比賽和更激烈競爭。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the history books tell us that","meaning":"歷史書告訴我們","examples":[{"en":"The history books tell us that clubs agreed on a 90-minute limit.","zh":"歷史書告訴我們，球會同意了九十分鐘限制。"},{"en":"“The history books tell us that” introduces information recorded in historical sources.","zh":"「The history books tell us that」用來介紹歷史資料中記載的資訊。"},{"en":"The history books tell us that early matches did not always have the same length.","zh":"歷史書告訴我們，早期比賽並不總是有相同時長。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a statement a historical and factual tone.","zh":"這個短語令說法帶有歷史和事實語氣。"},{"en":"The history books tell us that rule changes helped organise football.","zh":"歷史書告訴我們，規則改變幫助足球變得有組織。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"set a limit of","meaning":"設定……的限制","examples":[{"en":"The clubs decided to set a limit of ninety minutes for each match.","zh":"球會決定為每場比賽設定九十分鐘限制。"},{"en":"To set a limit of an amount means to decide the maximum or fixed amount allowed.","zh":"設定某數量的限制，是指決定容許的最高或固定數量。"},{"en":"The organisers set a limit of twenty visitors per group.","zh":"主辦者設定每團二十名遊客的限制。"},{"en":"Setting a time limit helped reduce arguments about when games should end.","zh":"設定時間限制有助減少關於比賽何時結束的爭論。"},{"en":"A ninety-minute limit became an important part of football.","zh":"九十分鐘限制成為足球的重要部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"for each match","meaning":"每場比賽","examples":[{"en":"A ninety-minute limit was set for each match.","zh":"每場比賽設定了九十分鐘限制。"},{"en":"For each match means for every individual game.","zh":"每場比賽是指每一場個別比賽。"},{"en":"The rules apply for each match in the league.","zh":"這些規則適用於聯賽中的每場比賽。"},{"en":"A fixed length for each match made competitions fairer.","zh":"每場比賽有固定時長，令競賽更公平。"},{"en":"Referees needed to know the time limit for each match.","zh":"裁判需要知道每場比賽的時間限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a more casual arrangement","meaning":"較隨意的安排","examples":[{"en":"Before that, the length of a match was a more casual arrangement.","zh":"在那之前，比賽時長是一種較隨意的安排。"},{"en":"A more casual arrangement is a less formal or less clearly fixed system.","zh":"較隨意的安排是較不正式或較不清晰固定的制度。"},{"en":"Early football used a more casual arrangement for match length.","zh":"早期足球對比賽時長採用較隨意的安排。"},{"en":"Casual arrangements can work for friendly games but cause problems in serious matches.","zh":"隨意安排可以適用於友誼賽，但在正式比賽中會造成問題。"},{"en":"The 90-minute rule replaced a more casual arrangement.","zh":"九十分鐘規則取代了較隨意的安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cause huge arguments","meaning":"引發激烈爭論","examples":[{"en":"The casual arrangement sometimes caused huge arguments.","zh":"這種隨意安排有時引發激烈爭論。"},{"en":"To cause huge arguments means to create serious disagreements.","zh":"引發激烈爭論，是指造成嚴重分歧。"},{"en":"Unclear rules can cause huge arguments between teams.","zh":"不清晰的規則可以引發球隊之間的激烈爭論。"},{"en":"A fixed match length helped prevent arguments about when to stop.","zh":"固定比賽時長有助防止關於何時停止的爭論。"},{"en":"The old system caused huge arguments because teams did not always agree.","zh":"舊制度引發激烈爭論，因為球隊不一定同意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"during matches","meaning":"在比賽期間","examples":[{"en":"Arguments sometimes happened during matches.","zh":"爭論有時在比賽期間發生。"},{"en":"During matches means while games are being played.","zh":"在比賽期間，是指比賽正在進行的時候。"},{"en":"Referees make decisions during matches.","zh":"裁判在比賽期間作出判決。"},{"en":"Rules are important because emotions can become strong during matches.","zh":"規則很重要，因為在比賽期間情緒可能變得激烈。"},{"en":"In early football, disputes about time sometimes happened during matches.","zh":"在早期足球中，關於時間的爭議有時在比賽期間發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"call the end of the game","meaning":"宣布比賽結束","examples":[{"en":"One team might call the end of the game before the other team agreed.","zh":"一隊可能在另一隊同意前宣布比賽結束。"},{"en":"To call the end of the game means to announce that the match is finished.","zh":"宣布比賽結束，是指表示比賽已完成。"},{"en":"The referee now calls the end of the game by blowing the whistle.","zh":"現在裁判會吹哨宣布比賽結束。"},{"en":"If one team called the end too early, the other team might object.","zh":"如果一隊太早宣布結束，另一隊可能會反對。"},{"en":"Fixed match lengths made it clearer who could call the end of the game.","zh":"固定比賽時長令誰可以宣布比賽結束更清楚。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"play on","meaning":"繼續比賽","examples":[{"en":"The other team might want to play on.","zh":"另一隊可能想繼續比賽。"},{"en":"To play on means to continue playing instead of stopping.","zh":"繼續比賽是指不停下來而繼續作賽。"},{"en":"The referee allowed the teams to play on after a minor foul.","zh":"輕微犯規後，裁判容許球隊繼續比賽。"},{"en":"A team losing by one goal may want to play on to try to equalise.","zh":"落後一球的球隊可能想繼續比賽，嘗試追平。"},{"en":"Without a fixed time limit, teams could argue about whether to play on.","zh":"沒有固定時間限制時，球隊可能會為是否繼續比賽而爭論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"score a winning goal","meaning":"射入致勝球","examples":[{"en":"A team might play on to try and score a winning goal.","zh":"一隊可能想繼續比賽，嘗試射入致勝球。"},{"en":"To score a winning goal means to score the goal that makes a team win the match.","zh":"射入致勝球，是指射入令球隊贏得比賽的一球。"},{"en":"The striker scored a winning goal in the final minute.","zh":"前鋒在最後一分鐘射入致勝球。"},{"en":"Teams may become desperate to score a winning goal near the end of a match.","zh":"球隊在比賽尾段可能會急於射入致勝球。"},{"en":"A fixed time limit prevents teams from playing on endlessly to score a winning goal.","zh":"固定時間限制可以防止球隊無止境地繼續比賽以求射入致勝球。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"football league","meaning":"足球聯賽","examples":[{"en":"The number of teams in the football league increased again.","zh":"足球聯賽中的球隊數目再次增加。"},{"en":"A football league is an organised competition in which teams play matches against one another.","zh":"足球聯賽是球隊互相作賽的有組織競賽。"},{"en":"The football league became larger as more clubs joined.","zh":"隨着更多球會加入，足球聯賽變得更大。"},{"en":"Leagues helped football become more regular and structured.","zh":"聯賽幫助足球變得更有規律和結構。"},{"en":"A football league needs common rules so all teams compete fairly.","zh":"足球聯賽需要共同規則，讓所有球隊公平競爭。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in addition","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"In addition, referees started using whistles.","zh":"此外，裁判開始使用哨子。"},{"en":"“In addition” introduces an extra point or fact.","zh":"「In addition」用來介紹額外重點或事實。"},{"en":"The tour includes the dressing rooms; in addition, visitors see the pitch.","zh":"導覽包括更衣室；此外，遊客還會看到草地球場。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when adding more information in an organised way.","zh":"這個短語適合有條理地加入更多資料。"},{"en":"In addition to rule changes, football equipment also changed.","zh":"除了規則改變外，足球設備也有所改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"use whistles","meaning":"使用哨子","examples":[{"en":"Referees started using whistles in 1878.","zh":"裁判在 1878 年開始使用哨子。"},{"en":"To use whistles means to blow small instruments to signal decisions or stop play.","zh":"使用哨子是指吹響小型工具來示意判決或停止比賽。"},{"en":"Referees use whistles to start and end matches.","zh":"裁判使用哨子開始和結束比賽。"},{"en":"Whistles made it easier for referees to control noisy games.","zh":"哨子令裁判更容易控制嘈吵的比賽。"},{"en":"Before referees used whistles, communication on the pitch was less clear.","zh":"在裁判使用哨子之前，球場上的溝通較不清楚。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"electric lamps were installed","meaning":"安裝了電燈","examples":[{"en":"Electric lamps were installed on certain pitches.","zh":"某些球場安裝了電燈。"},{"en":"If electric lamps were installed, lights were fitted and made ready for use.","zh":"如果安裝了電燈，即表示燈具被裝上並準備使用。"},{"en":"Electric lamps were installed so evening matches could take place.","zh":"安裝電燈是為了讓晚間比賽可以舉行。"},{"en":"Installing lamps changed when football could be played.","zh":"安裝電燈改變了足球可以進行的時間。"},{"en":"Electric lighting was a major improvement for stadiums.","zh":"電力照明是球場的一項重大改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"certain pitches","meaning":"某些球場","examples":[{"en":"Electric lamps were installed on certain pitches.","zh":"電燈被安裝在某些球場上。"},{"en":"Certain pitches means particular playing fields, not all of them.","zh":"某些球場是指特定的比賽場地，而不是全部。"},{"en":"Only certain pitches had electric lighting at first.","zh":"起初只有某些球場有電力照明。"},{"en":"Certain pitches became more useful because they could host evening games.","zh":"某些球場因可以舉行晚間比賽而變得更實用。"},{"en":"The guide explains that lights were not installed everywhere immediately.","zh":"導遊解釋電燈並非立即安裝在所有地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a significant change","meaning":"重大改變","examples":[{"en":"The use of electric lamps was a significant change.","zh":"使用電燈是一項重大改變。"},{"en":"A significant change is an important change that has noticeable effects.","zh":"重大改變是有重要影響並明顯可見的改變。"},{"en":"The introduction of goalkeepers was a significant change in football.","zh":"引入守門員是足球中的重大改變。"},{"en":"Electric lighting was significant because it allowed evening games.","zh":"電力照明很重大，因為它容許晚間比賽。"},{"en":"Significant changes in rules helped create the modern game.","zh":"規則上的重大改變幫助形成現代足球。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"all year round","meaning":"全年","examples":[{"en":"Games could be played in the evenings all year round.","zh":"比賽可以全年在晚上進行。"},{"en":"All year round means throughout the whole year.","zh":"全年是指整年期間。"},{"en":"The stadium offers tours all year round.","zh":"球場全年提供導覽。"},{"en":"Electric lamps allowed evening matches to happen all year round.","zh":"電燈令晚間比賽可以全年進行。"},{"en":"Activities held all year round need regular staff and maintenance.","zh":"全年舉行的活動需要定期人手和保養。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"charge fans for admission","meaning":"向球迷收取入場費","examples":[{"en":"Clubs began to charge fans for admission to games.","zh":"球會開始向球迷收取比賽入場費。"},{"en":"To charge fans for admission means to ask supporters to pay to enter and watch games.","zh":"向球迷收取入場費，是指要求支持者付款入場觀看比賽。"},{"en":"The club charged fans for admission to raise money.","zh":"球會向球迷收取入場費以籌集資金。"},{"en":"Charging admission helped clubs pay for grounds and equipment.","zh":"收取入場費幫助球會支付場地和設備費用。"},{"en":"Once clubs charged fans for admission, football became more commercial.","zh":"球會開始向球迷收取入場費後，足球變得更商業化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"admission to games","meaning":"比賽入場","examples":[{"en":"Fans had to pay for admission to games.","zh":"球迷必須支付比賽入場費。"},{"en":"Admission to games means entry to watch matches.","zh":"比賽入場是指進入場地觀看比賽。"},{"en":"The ticket gives admission to the game and the museum area.","zh":"門票包括比賽入場和博物館區域入場。"},{"en":"Charging for admission to games changed the relationship between clubs and fans.","zh":"收取比賽入場費改變了球會和球迷之間的關係。"},{"en":"Free admission was less common once football became organised commercially.","zh":"足球變得有商業組織後，免費入場較不常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"even though","meaning":"儘管","examples":[{"en":"Clubs charged fans even though players were still amateurs.","zh":"儘管球員仍是業餘球員，球會仍向球迷收費。"},{"en":"“Even though” introduces a contrast between two facts.","zh":"「Even though」用來介紹兩個事實之間的對比。"},{"en":"Fans paid to watch even though the players were not professionals.","zh":"儘管球員不是職業球員，球迷仍付費觀看。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the second fact makes the first one more surprising.","zh":"這個句式顯示第二個事實令第一個事實更令人意外。"},{"en":"Even though the players had other jobs, football was becoming a paid spectator event.","zh":"儘管球員有其他工作，足球正變成收費觀賞活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"amateurs","meaning":"業餘球員","examples":[{"en":"Players were still amateurs in 1880.","zh":"1880 年時，球員仍是業餘球員。"},{"en":"Amateurs are people who take part in an activity without being paid as professionals.","zh":"業餘球員是不以職業身份收取薪酬而參與活動的人。"},{"en":"Early football players were often amateurs with ordinary jobs.","zh":"早期足球員通常是有普通工作的業餘球員。"},{"en":"Amateurs may be skilled even if they do not earn money from the sport.","zh":"業餘球員即使不靠運動賺錢，也可能很有技巧。"},{"en":"Football changed greatly when amateur players began to be replaced by professionals.","zh":"當職業球員開始取代業餘球員時，足球發生巨大變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"proper jobs","meaning":"正式工作","examples":[{"en":"The players had other proper jobs.","zh":"球員有其他正式工作。"},{"en":"Proper jobs means regular paid employment outside the activity being discussed.","zh":"正式工作是指在所談活動以外的固定有薪工作。"},{"en":"Early players had proper jobs during the week and played football at weekends.","zh":"早期球員平日有正式工作，週末踢足球。"},{"en":"Having proper jobs showed that football was not yet a full-time profession.","zh":"有正式工作顯示足球尚未成為全職職業。"},{"en":"Many amateurs balanced football with proper jobs.","zh":"許多業餘球員要在足球和正式工作之間取得平衡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the modern professional game","meaning":"現代職業足球","examples":[{"en":"Top players earn a lot in the modern professional game.","zh":"頂級球員在現代職業足球中賺很多錢。"},{"en":"The modern professional game means football today as a paid, organised professional sport.","zh":"現代職業足球是指今天作為有薪、有組織職業運動的足球。"},{"en":"The modern professional game includes clubs, contracts, sponsors, and global audiences.","zh":"現代職業足球包括球會、合約、贊助商和全球觀眾。"},{"en":"Compared with early football, the modern professional game involves much more money.","zh":"與早期足球相比，現代職業足球涉及更多金錢。"},{"en":"The guide contrasts amateur football with the modern professional game.","zh":"導遊把業餘足球與現代職業足球作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"top players","meaning":"頂級球員","examples":[{"en":"Top players earn significant sums of money.","zh":"頂級球員賺取巨額金錢。"},{"en":"Top players are the best or most successful players in a sport.","zh":"頂級球員是運動中最好或最成功的球員。"},{"en":"Top players train hard and often attract large crowds.","zh":"頂級球員努力訓練，通常能吸引大量觀眾。"},{"en":"In modern football, top players can earn money from salaries and sponsorships.","zh":"在現代足球中，頂級球員可以從薪酬和贊助中賺錢。"},{"en":"Fans often visit stadiums because they want to see top players.","zh":"球迷經常到球場，因為想看頂級球員。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"earn significant sums of money","meaning":"賺取巨額金錢","examples":[{"en":"Top players earn significant sums of money from football.","zh":"頂級球員從足球中賺取巨額金錢。"},{"en":"To earn significant sums of money means to receive large amounts of money.","zh":"賺取巨額金錢，是指獲得大量金錢。"},{"en":"Famous footballers can earn significant sums of money through contracts.","zh":"著名足球員可以透過合約賺取巨額金錢。"},{"en":"Commercial activities help players earn more than match salaries alone.","zh":"商業活動幫助球員賺取比單靠比賽薪酬更多的收入。"},{"en":"The contrast with early amateurs shows how much football has changed.","zh":"與早期業餘球員的對比顯示足球改變了很多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"commercial activities","meaning":"商業活動","examples":[{"en":"Players can earn money from both playing and commercial activities.","zh":"球員可以從比賽和商業活動中賺錢。"},{"en":"Commercial activities are business-related activities intended to make money.","zh":"商業活動是以賺錢為目的的商業相關活動。"},{"en":"Advertising and sponsorship deals are commercial activities.","zh":"廣告和贊助合約都是商業活動。"},{"en":"Modern players may earn more from commercial activities than from matches.","zh":"現代球員從商業活動中賺的錢可能比比賽薪酬更多。"},{"en":"Commercial activities have become an important part of professional football.","zh":"商業活動已成為職業足球的重要部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Which TWO things does the speaker say about","meaning":"講者提到哪兩件關於……的事","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which two things the speaker says about visiting the stadium with children.","zh":"題目問講者提到哪兩件關於帶孩子參觀球場的事。"},{"en":"“Which TWO things does the speaker say about” asks listeners to choose two correct points from several options.","zh":"「Which TWO things does the speaker say about」要求聽者從多個選項中選出兩個正確重點。"},{"en":"Which two things does the speaker say about the stadium tour?","zh":"講者提到哪兩件關於球場導覽的事？"},{"en":"This type of question tests careful listening for specific details.","zh":"這類問題測試仔細聆聽特定細節的能力。"},{"en":"Listeners must identify exactly two pieces of information mentioned by the guide.","zh":"聽者必須準確找出導遊提到的兩項資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"visiting the football stadium with children","meaning":"帶同孩子參觀足球場","examples":[{"en":"The question focuses on visiting the football stadium with children.","zh":"題目集中於帶同孩子參觀足球場。"},{"en":"Visiting the football stadium with children means taking children on a tour of the stadium.","zh":"帶同孩子參觀足球場，是指帶孩子參加球場導覽。"},{"en":"Parents visiting the football stadium with children must stay close to them.","zh":"帶同孩子參觀足球場的家長必須留在孩子身邊。"},{"en":"Safety advice is important when families visit large public places.","zh":"家庭參觀大型公共場所時，安全建議很重要。"},{"en":"Children can enjoy special activities when visiting the football stadium.","zh":"孩子帶同參觀足球場時，可以享受特別活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get their photo taken with","meaning":"與……合照","examples":[{"en":"Some visitors may want to get their photo taken with a football player.","zh":"一些遊客可能想與足球員合照。"},{"en":"To get your photo taken with someone means to have someone photograph you standing with that person.","zh":"與某人合照，是指讓別人拍下你與該人站在一起的照片。"},{"en":"Fans hoped to get their photo taken with the club captain.","zh":"球迷希望與球隊隊長合照。"},{"en":"Getting a photo taken with a player would be exciting, but it may not be part of the tour.","zh":"與球員合照會很令人興奮，但未必是導覽的一部分。"},{"en":"Visitors can take photos, but they may not meet a football player.","zh":"遊客可以拍照，但未必會見到足球員。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"football player","meaning":"足球員","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions a football player.","zh":"題目提到一名足球員。"},{"en":"A football player is someone who plays football, especially as part of a team.","zh":"足球員是踢足球的人，尤其是球隊成員。"},{"en":"The football player signed shirts for young fans.","zh":"那名足球員為年輕球迷在球衣上簽名。"},{"en":"A football player trains regularly to improve skill and fitness.","zh":"足球員定期訓練，以改善技巧和體能。"},{"en":"Stadium visitors may learn where football players prepare before matches.","zh":"球場遊客可能會了解足球員賽前在哪裏準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a competition for children","meaning":"兒童比賽","examples":[{"en":"There is a competition for children today.","zh":"今天有一項兒童比賽。"},{"en":"A competition for children is an activity where children enter and try to win a prize.","zh":"兒童比賽是讓孩子參加並嘗試贏取獎品的活動。"},{"en":"The café organised a drawing competition for children.","zh":"咖啡店舉辦了一項兒童繪畫比賽。"},{"en":"Competitions for children should be fun and easy to join.","zh":"兒童比賽應有趣而容易參加。"},{"en":"Children need to put contact details on their drawings for the competition.","zh":"孩子需要在畫作上寫上聯絡資料，以參加比賽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stay with their children at all times","meaning":"時刻陪伴孩子","examples":[{"en":"Parents should stay with their children at all times.","zh":"家長應時刻陪伴孩子。"},{"en":"To stay with their children at all times means not to leave children alone at any moment.","zh":"時刻陪伴孩子，是指任何時候都不要讓孩子獨自一人。"},{"en":"Parents should stay with their children in the players’ tunnel.","zh":"家長在球員通道中應時刻陪伴孩子。"},{"en":"This rule helps prevent children from getting lost or frightened.","zh":"這條規則有助防止孩子迷路或受到驚嚇。"},{"en":"During the stadium tour, parents must supervise children continuously.","zh":"在球場導覽期間，家長必須持續看管孩子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"at all times","meaning":"任何時候；時刻","examples":[{"en":"Parents should supervise their children at all times.","zh":"家長應時刻看管孩子。"},{"en":"At all times means always, with no exceptions.","zh":"任何時候是指一直如此，沒有例外。"},{"en":"Visitors must keep their tickets with them at all times.","zh":"遊客應任何時候都帶着門票。"},{"en":"Safety rules should be followed at all times during the tour.","zh":"導覽期間應時刻遵守安全規則。"},{"en":"Children should remain with an adult at all times.","zh":"孩子應任何時候都與成人同行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sunhats and drinks","meaning":"太陽帽和飲品","examples":[{"en":"Visitors may need sunhats and drinks on a hot day.","zh":"遊客在炎熱日子可能需要太陽帽和飲品。"},{"en":"Sunhats and drinks help protect people from sun and heat.","zh":"太陽帽和飲品有助保護人們免受陽光和高溫影響。"},{"en":"The guide reminded families to bring sunhats and drinks for the pitch visit.","zh":"導遊提醒家庭為參觀球場帶太陽帽和飲品。"},{"en":"On hot sunny days, children especially need sunhats and drinks.","zh":"在炎熱晴朗的日子，孩子尤其需要太陽帽和飲品。"},{"en":"Sunhats and drinks can make an outdoor stadium visit safer and more comfortable.","zh":"太陽帽和飲品可以令戶外球場參觀更安全和舒適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a special offer on meals","meaning":"餐點特別優惠","examples":[{"en":"The café may have a special offer on meals for children.","zh":"咖啡店可能有兒童餐點特別優惠。"},{"en":"A special offer on meals is a reduced price or deal for food.","zh":"餐點特別優惠是食物的減價或優惠套餐。"},{"en":"The café advertised a special offer on lunch boxes.","zh":"咖啡店宣傳午餐盒特別優惠。"},{"en":"A special offer can encourage families to buy meals at the stadium.","zh":"特別優惠可以鼓勵家庭在球場購買餐點。"},{"en":"Visitors should check whether the café has any special offers before ordering.","zh":"遊客點餐前應查看咖啡店是否有任何特別優惠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"features of the stadium tour","meaning":"球場導覽的特色","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about features of the stadium tour.","zh":"題目詢問球場導覽的特色。"},{"en":"Features of the stadium tour are the main parts, activities, or services included in the visit.","zh":"球場導覽的特色是參觀中包括的主要部分、活動或服務。"},{"en":"The audio guide is one of the new features of the stadium tour.","zh":"語音導覽是球場導覽的新特色之一。"},{"en":"Visitors compare features of the tour before deciding whether to book.","zh":"遊客預訂前會比較導覽特色。"},{"en":"The cinema experience and dressing rooms are important tour features.","zh":"影院體驗和更衣室是重要導覽特色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"new this year","meaning":"今年新增的","examples":[{"en":"Visitors need to identify which features are new this year.","zh":"遊客需要辨認哪些特色是今年新增的。"},{"en":"New this year means introduced or made available during the current year.","zh":"今年新增的，是指在今年推出或提供的。"},{"en":"The audio guide is new this year.","zh":"語音導覽是今年新增的。"},{"en":"Features new this year may still need visitor feedback.","zh":"今年新增的特色可能仍需要遊客意見。"},{"en":"The club added several activities, but only one may be new this year.","zh":"球會增加了幾項活動，但可能只有一項是今年新增的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"audio guide","meaning":"語音導覽","examples":[{"en":"The audio guide lets visitors listen to pre-recorded information.","zh":"語音導覽讓遊客聆聽預錄資料。"},{"en":"An audio guide is a recorded guide that visitors listen to through headphones or a device.","zh":"語音導覽是遊客透過耳機或裝置聆聽的錄音導覽。"},{"en":"The audio guide explains the history of the club at each stop.","zh":"語音導覽在每個停留點解釋球會歷史。"},{"en":"An audio guide is useful for visitors who prefer a self-guided tour.","zh":"語音導覽適合較喜歡自助導覽的遊客。"},{"en":"The stadium asks for feedback because the audio guide is newly introduced.","zh":"球場因語音導覽剛推出而徵求意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"dressing room tour","meaning":"更衣室導覽","examples":[{"en":"The dressing room tour takes visitors into the players’ dressing rooms.","zh":"更衣室導覽帶遊客進入球員更衣室。"},{"en":"A dressing room tour is a visit to the rooms where players prepare for matches.","zh":"更衣室導覽是參觀球員準備比賽的房間。"},{"en":"Fans enjoyed the dressing room tour because they saw where players sit.","zh":"球迷很喜歡更衣室導覽，因為看到球員坐的位置。"},{"en":"A dressing room tour can make visitors feel closer to the team.","zh":"更衣室導覽可以令遊客感覺更接近球隊。"},{"en":"The dressing room tour is usually one of the most popular parts of a stadium visit.","zh":"更衣室導覽通常是球場參觀中最受歡迎的部分之一。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"tours in other languages","meaning":"其他語言導覽","examples":[{"en":"The stadium may offer tours in other languages in future.","zh":"球場日後可能提供其他語言導覽。"},{"en":"Tours in other languages are guided visits presented in languages different from the main one.","zh":"其他語言導覽是使用主要語言以外語言進行的導覽。"},{"en":"International visitors asked for tours in other languages.","zh":"國際遊客要求提供其他語言導覽。"},{"en":"Tours in other languages can make the stadium more welcoming to tourists.","zh":"其他語言導覽可以令球場對遊客更友善。"},{"en":"The club is considering tours in other languages but has not introduced them yet.","zh":"球會正考慮其他語言導覽，但尚未推出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"took place in","meaning":"發生於","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which event took place in each year.","zh":"題目詢問每項事件發生於哪一年。"},{"en":"“Took place in” means happened during a particular year, place, or period.","zh":"「Took place in」表示在某一年、地方或時期發生。"},{"en":"The rule change took place in 1875.","zh":"規則改變發生於 1875 年。"},{"en":"Historical questions often ask when events took place.","zh":"歷史題目經常詢問事件何時發生。"},{"en":"Listeners must match each football event with the year it took place in.","zh":"聽者必須把每項足球事件與其發生年份配對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the following years","meaning":"以下年份","examples":[{"en":"The events must be matched with the following years.","zh":"這些事件必須與以下年份配對。"},{"en":"The following years means the years listed next or below.","zh":"以下年份是指接下來或下方列出的年份。"},{"en":"Match each event with one of the following years.","zh":"請把每項事件與以下年份之一配對。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in listening and history exercises.","zh":"這個短語常見於聆聽和歷史練習。"},{"en":"The following years include important dates from football history.","zh":"以下年份包括足球歷史中的重要日期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"events in the history of football","meaning":"足球歷史事件","examples":[{"en":"The box lists events in the history of football.","zh":"方格列出足球歷史事件。"},{"en":"Events in the history of football are important happenings that helped football develop.","zh":"足球歷史事件是幫助足球發展的重要事情。"},{"en":"The introduction of goalkeepers is one event in the history of football.","zh":"引入守門員是足球歷史事件之一。"},{"en":"Learning events in football history helps explain the modern rules.","zh":"學習足球歷史事件有助解釋現代規則。"},{"en":"The guide describes several events in the history of football during the tour.","zh":"導遊在導覽中描述了幾項足球歷史事件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the introduction of pay for the players","meaning":"引入球員薪酬","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of pay for the players changed professional football.","zh":"引入球員薪酬改變了職業足球。"},{"en":"The introduction of pay for the players means players began to receive money for playing.","zh":"引入球員薪酬，是指球員開始因踢球而收取金錢。"},{"en":"Once pay for players was introduced, football became more professional.","zh":"球員薪酬一旦被引入，足球便變得更職業化。"},{"en":"Paying players changed football from a pastime into a career for some people.","zh":"支付球員薪酬令足球對一些人來說從消遣變成職業。"},{"en":"The introduction of player pay helped create the modern professional game.","zh":"引入球員薪酬幫助形成現代職業足球。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a change to the design of the goal","meaning":"球門設計的改變","examples":[{"en":"The solid crossbar was a change to the design of the goal.","zh":"實心橫樑是球門設計的一項改變。"},{"en":"A change to the design of the goal means an alteration in the structure of the football goal.","zh":"球門設計的改變，是指足球球門結構上的改動。"},{"en":"Replacing tape with a crossbar was a major change to the goal design.","zh":"用橫樑取代膠帶是球門設計的一項重大改變。"},{"en":"Changes to equipment can affect how the game is played.","zh":"設備上的改變可以影響比賽方式。"},{"en":"The goal became more standard after the design changed.","zh":"球門設計改變後變得更標準化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the first use of lights for matches","meaning":"首次使用球場燈進行比賽","examples":[{"en":"The first use of lights for matches allowed evening games.","zh":"首次使用球場燈進行比賽讓晚間比賽成為可能。"},{"en":"The first use of lights for matches means the first time electric lighting was used for football games.","zh":"首次使用球場燈進行比賽，是指第一次在足球比賽中使用電力照明。"},{"en":"The first use of lights changed when spectators could watch games.","zh":"首次使用球場燈改變了觀眾可以觀看比賽的時間。"},{"en":"Lights made evening football possible throughout the year.","zh":"燈光令全年晚間足球比賽成為可能。"},{"en":"The use of electric lamps was a significant moment in football history.","zh":"使用電燈是足球歷史中的重要時刻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the introduction of goalkeepers","meaning":"引入守門員","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of goalkeepers changed the structure of football teams.","zh":"引入守門員改變了足球隊的結構。"},{"en":"The introduction of goalkeepers means teams began using a specific player to guard the goal.","zh":"引入守門員，是指球隊開始使用一名特定球員把守球門。"},{"en":"Before the introduction of goalkeepers, football was harder to imagine in its modern form.","zh":"在引入守門員前，很難把足球想像成現代形式。"},{"en":"Goalkeepers gave teams a specialised defensive role.","zh":"守門員給球隊一個專門防守角色。"},{"en":"The introduction of goalkeepers was one of the major changes in early football.","zh":"引入守門員是早期足球中的重大改變之一。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the first international match","meaning":"首場國際賽","examples":[{"en":"The first international match was an important event in football history.","zh":"首場國際賽是足球歷史中的重要事件。"},{"en":"The first international match means the earliest football match played between national teams.","zh":"首場國際賽是指最早由國家隊之間進行的足球比賽。"},{"en":"Fans remember the first international match as a key step in football’s growth.","zh":"球迷把首場國際賽視為足球發展的重要一步。"},{"en":"International matches helped football spread beyond local clubs.","zh":"國際賽幫助足球超越本地球會傳播開去。"},{"en":"The first international match showed that football could become a global sport.","zh":"首場國際賽顯示足球可以成為全球性運動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"two changes to the rules of the game","meaning":"比賽規則的兩項改變","examples":[{"en":"Two changes to the rules of the game happened in the same year.","zh":"比賽規則的兩項改變在同一年發生。"},{"en":"Two changes to the rules of the game means two alterations in how football was officially played.","zh":"比賽規則的兩項改變，是指足球正式玩法中的兩項改動。"},{"en":"Sending players off and swapping ends were two changes to the rules.","zh":"罰球員離場和交換場地是兩項規則改變。"},{"en":"Rule changes helped make football fairer and easier to manage.","zh":"規則改變幫助足球變得更公平和更易管理。"},{"en":"The guide asks visitors to match two rule changes with the correct year.","zh":"導遊要求遊客把兩項規則改變與正確年份配對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the introduction of a fee for spectators","meaning":"引入觀眾入場費","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of a fee for spectators meant fans had to pay to watch games.","zh":"引入觀眾入場費意味着球迷必須付費觀看比賽。"},{"en":"The introduction of a fee for spectators means spectators began being charged for entry.","zh":"引入觀眾入場費，是指觀眾開始被收取入場費。"},{"en":"Charging spectators created a new source of income for clubs.","zh":"向觀眾收費為球會創造了新收入來源。"},{"en":"The introduction of spectator fees was part of football becoming more commercial.","zh":"引入觀眾入場費是足球變得更商業化的一部分。"},{"en":"Fans paying for admission showed that football was attracting a larger audience.","zh":"球迷付費入場顯示足球正在吸引更多觀眾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"an agreement on the length of a game","meaning":"就比賽時長達成協議","examples":[{"en":"An agreement on the length of a game helped reduce arguments.","zh":"就比賽時長達成協議有助減少爭論。"},{"en":"An agreement on the length of a game means a shared decision about how long a match should last.","zh":"就比賽時長達成協議，是指共同決定一場比賽應持續多久。"},{"en":"Clubs agreed on a 90-minute limit for each match.","zh":"球會同意每場比賽限制為九十分鐘。"},{"en":"This agreement made it clearer when a game should end.","zh":"這項協議令比賽何時結束更清楚。"},{"en":"Without an agreement on match length, teams could argue about playing on.","zh":"如果沒有就比賽時長達成協議，球隊可能會為是否繼續比賽而爭論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"ielts/listening/Practice 4/task-3":[{"front":"education students","meaning":"教育系學生","examples":[{"en":"Two education students are discussing an assignment on handwriting.","zh":"兩名教育系學生正在討論一份關於書寫的作業。"},{"en":"Education students are people studying how to teach and support learners.","zh":"教育系學生是學習如何教導和支援學習者的人。"},{"en":"Education students often learn about child development and classroom methods.","zh":"教育系學生通常學習兒童發展和課堂方法。"},{"en":"The education students compared handwriting with typing.","zh":"這些教育系學生比較了手寫和打字。"},{"en":"Education students need to understand how children learn basic skills.","zh":"教育系學生需要理解孩子如何學習基本技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"discuss an assignment","meaning":"討論一份作業","examples":[{"en":"The students discuss an assignment on teaching handwriting.","zh":"學生討論一份關於教孩子書寫的作業。"},{"en":"To discuss an assignment means to talk about its topic, ideas, and requirements.","zh":"討論一份作業意思是談論它的題目、想法和要求。"},{"en":"The students discussed the assignment before starting their research.","zh":"學生在開始研究前討論了這份作業。"},{"en":"Discussing an assignment can help students find a clearer focus.","zh":"討論作業可以幫助學生找到更清楚的焦點。"},{"en":"They met after class to discuss their assignment together.","zh":"他們課後見面，一起討論作業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"teaching handwriting to children","meaning":"教孩子書寫","examples":[{"en":"The assignment is about teaching handwriting to children.","zh":"這份作業是關於教孩子書寫。"},{"en":"Teaching handwriting to children means helping children learn to form letters clearly by hand.","zh":"教孩子書寫意思是幫助孩子學會用手清楚寫出字母。"},{"en":"Teachers use practice sheets when teaching handwriting to children.","zh":"老師教孩子書寫時會使用練習紙。"},{"en":"Teaching handwriting to children also supports concentration and motor skills.","zh":"教孩子書寫也能支援專注力和動作能力。"},{"en":"The students researched methods for teaching handwriting to children.","zh":"學生研究了教孩子書寫的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get on with","meaning":"……進行得怎樣","examples":[{"en":"How are you getting on with the assignment on handwriting?","zh":"你那份關於書寫的作業進行得怎樣？"},{"en":"To get on with something means to make progress with it.","zh":"某事進行得怎樣，意思是某事進展如何。"},{"en":"How are you getting on with your research notes?","zh":"你的研究筆記進行得怎樣？"},{"en":"She is getting on well with the handwriting assignment.","zh":"她的書寫作業進行得不錯。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about progress in a friendly way.","zh":"這個短語以友善方式詢問進度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"assignment on handwriting","meaning":"關於書寫的作業","examples":[{"en":"The students are working on an assignment on handwriting.","zh":"學生正在做一份關於書寫的作業。"},{"en":"An assignment on handwriting is schoolwork about writing by hand.","zh":"關於書寫的作業是有關手寫的學校功課。"},{"en":"Their assignment on handwriting included children with learning difficulties.","zh":"他們關於書寫的作業包括有學習困難的孩子。"},{"en":"An assignment on handwriting may discuss memory, concentration, and legibility.","zh":"關於書寫的作業可能討論記憶、專注力和可讀性。"},{"en":"The topic of their assignment on handwriting was surprisingly broad.","zh":"他們這份關於書寫的作業題目出乎意料地廣泛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Not too bad","meaning":"還不錯","examples":[{"en":"The woman says the assignment is going not too bad.","zh":"那位女士說作業進行得還不錯。"},{"en":"“Not too bad” means quite good or better than expected.","zh":"「Not too bad」意思是相當好或比預期好。"},{"en":"My research is going not too bad so far.","zh":"到目前為止，我的研究進行得還不錯。"},{"en":"The assignment is difficult, but not too bad.","zh":"這份作業很難，但還不錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a mild positive answer.","zh":"這個短語給出溫和正面的回答。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"I hadn’t realised that","meaning":"我以前沒有意識到","examples":[{"en":"I hadn’t realised that children benefit in so many ways from learning to write.","zh":"我以前沒有意識到孩子可以從學習書寫中獲得多方面好處。"},{"en":"“I hadn’t realised that” means I did not know or understand it before.","zh":"「I hadn’t realised that」意思是我以前不知道或不理解這件事。"},{"en":"I hadn’t realised that handwriting could help memory.","zh":"我以前沒有意識到手寫可以幫助記憶。"},{"en":"She hadn’t realised that spacing letters mattered so much.","zh":"她以前沒有意識到字母間距那麼重要。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a new understanding.","zh":"這個短語引出新的理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"benefit in so many ways from","meaning":"從……中獲得多方面好處","examples":[{"en":"Children benefit in so many ways from learning to write.","zh":"孩子從學習書寫中獲得多方面好處。"},{"en":"To benefit in so many ways from something means to gain many different advantages from it.","zh":"從某事中獲得多方面好處，意思是從中得到很多不同優點。"},{"en":"Children benefit in so many ways from reading every day.","zh":"孩子從每天閱讀中獲得多方面好處。"},{"en":"Students benefit from handwriting through memory, focus, and coordination.","zh":"學生透過手寫在記憶、專注和協調方面受益。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises multiple positive effects.","zh":"這個短語強調多種正面效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"learning to write","meaning":"學習書寫","examples":[{"en":"Children benefit from learning to write.","zh":"孩子從學習書寫中受益。"},{"en":"Learning to write means developing the ability to form letters and words by hand or in text.","zh":"學習書寫意思是發展用手或文字形成字母和詞語的能力。"},{"en":"Learning to write helps children communicate their ideas.","zh":"學習書寫幫助孩子表達自己的想法。"},{"en":"Young children need practice when learning to write.","zh":"年幼孩子學習書寫時需要練習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important early literacy skill.","zh":"這個短語描述重要的早期讀寫技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"such an important skill","meaning":"如此重要的技能","examples":[{"en":"Handwriting is such an important skill.","zh":"手寫是如此重要的技能。"},{"en":"Such an important skill means a skill that is very valuable or necessary.","zh":"如此重要的技能意思是非常有價值或必要的技能。"},{"en":"Reading is such an important skill for school success.","zh":"閱讀是對學業成功如此重要的技能。"},{"en":"Handwriting is such an important skill because it supports learning in many ways.","zh":"手寫是如此重要的技能，因為它以多種方式支援學習。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises the value of a skill.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調技能的價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"less important than in the past","meaning":"不如過去重要","examples":[{"en":"Many people think handwriting is less important than in the past.","zh":"很多人認為手寫不如過去重要。"},{"en":"Less important than in the past means not as important as it used to be.","zh":"不如過去重要意思是沒有以前那麼重要。"},{"en":"Some people believe spelling is less important than in the past because of spellcheckers.","zh":"有些人認為因為有拼寫檢查，拼寫不如過去重要。"},{"en":"Handwriting may seem less important than in the past, but it still has value.","zh":"手寫可能看似不如過去重要，但仍有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase compares present importance with past importance.","zh":"這個短語比較現在和過去的重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hardly ever","meaning":"幾乎不","examples":[{"en":"People hardly ever write by hand these days.","zh":"現在人們幾乎不手寫。"},{"en":"Hardly ever means almost never.","zh":"「Hardly ever」意思是幾乎從不。"},{"en":"I hardly ever write letters by hand now.","zh":"我現在幾乎不手寫信。"},{"en":"Children may hardly ever practise handwriting outside school.","zh":"孩子在校外可能幾乎不練習手寫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that happens very rarely.","zh":"這個短語描述很少發生的事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"write by hand","meaning":"手寫","examples":[{"en":"People hardly ever write by hand these days.","zh":"現在人們幾乎不手寫。"},{"en":"To write by hand means to write with a pen or pencil rather than typing.","zh":"手寫意思是用筆或鉛筆寫字，而不是打字。"},{"en":"Children should learn to write by hand before learning to type.","zh":"孩子應先學手寫，再學打字。"},{"en":"Writing by hand can help children remember letters.","zh":"手寫可以幫助孩子記住字母。"},{"en":"This phrase describes handwriting.","zh":"這個短語描述書寫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"these days","meaning":"現在；如今","examples":[{"en":"People write by hand less often these days.","zh":"現在人們較少手寫。"},{"en":"These days means nowadays or in the present time.","zh":"「These days」意思是現在或如今。"},{"en":"These days, many children use tablets at school.","zh":"現在很多孩子在學校使用平板電腦。"},{"en":"People rely on digital devices more these days.","zh":"如今人們更依賴數碼裝置。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the present with the past.","zh":"這個短語把現在與過去作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"all the evidence suggests","meaning":"所有證據都顯示","examples":[{"en":"All the evidence suggests children should learn to write by hand first.","zh":"所有證據都顯示孩子應先學手寫。"},{"en":"“All the evidence suggests” means the available facts point to this conclusion.","zh":"「All the evidence suggests」意思是現有事實都指向這個結論。"},{"en":"All the evidence suggests handwriting supports memory.","zh":"所有證據都顯示手寫有助記憶。"},{"en":"Teachers should consider what all the evidence suggests before changing methods.","zh":"老師改變方法前應考慮所有證據所顯示的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strong evidence-based claim.","zh":"這個短語提出有強證據支持的說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"learn to write by hand before","meaning":"先學手寫，再……","examples":[{"en":"Children should learn to write by hand before they learn to type.","zh":"孩子應先學手寫，再學打字。"},{"en":"To learn to write by hand before something means to master handwriting first.","zh":"先學手寫再做某事，意思是先掌握手寫。"},{"en":"Many teachers believe children should learn to write by hand before using keyboards.","zh":"很多老師認為孩子應先學手寫，再使用鍵盤。"},{"en":"Learning to write by hand before typing may support letter recognition.","zh":"先學手寫再學打字可能有助認字母。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a recommended learning order.","zh":"這個短語顯示建議的學習次序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"learn to type","meaning":"學習打字","examples":[{"en":"Children should learn to write by hand before they learn to type.","zh":"孩子應先學手寫，再學習打字。"},{"en":"To learn to type means to learn how to use a keyboard to write text.","zh":"學習打字意思是學會用鍵盤輸入文字。"},{"en":"Children may learn to type after they understand letter shapes.","zh":"孩子可能在理解字母形狀後學習打字。"},{"en":"Learning to type is useful, but it should not replace early handwriting practice.","zh":"學習打字很有用，但不應取代早期手寫練習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keyboard writing skills.","zh":"這個短語描述鍵盤書寫技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not least because","meaning":"尤其是因為","examples":[{"en":"Children should write by hand first, not least because it helps their memory.","zh":"孩子應先手寫，尤其是因為它有助記憶。"},{"en":"“Not least because” means especially because, among other reasons.","zh":"「Not least because」意思是在多個原因中尤其是因為。"},{"en":"Handwriting matters, not least because it helps children concentrate.","zh":"手寫很重要，尤其是因為它幫助孩子專注。"},{"en":"Teachers value handwriting, not least because it supports early literacy.","zh":"老師重視手寫，尤其是因為它支援早期讀寫。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an important reason.","zh":"這個短語引出重要原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"help someone’s memory","meaning":"有助某人的記憶","examples":[{"en":"Writing by hand helps children’s memory.","zh":"手寫有助孩子的記憶。"},{"en":"To help someone’s memory means to make it easier for them to remember information.","zh":"有助某人的記憶意思是令他們更容易記住資料。"},{"en":"Copying letters by hand can help a child’s memory.","zh":"用手抄寫字母可以有助孩子的記憶。"},{"en":"Physical movement may help memory more than simply looking at letters.","zh":"身體動作可能比單純看字母更有助記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes support for remembering.","zh":"這個短語描述對記憶的支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the physical act of writing","meaning":"書寫這個身體動作","examples":[{"en":"The physical act of writing helps children remember letters.","zh":"書寫這個身體動作幫助孩子記住字母。"},{"en":"The physical act of writing is the movement of the hand and fingers when forming letters.","zh":"書寫這個身體動作是形成字母時手和手指的移動。"},{"en":"The physical act of writing connects movement with learning.","zh":"書寫這個身體動作把動作與學習連繫起來。"},{"en":"Children may remember shapes better through the physical act of writing.","zh":"孩子可能透過書寫這個身體動作更好地記住形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on writing as a body movement.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於書寫作為身體動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"remember letters","meaning":"記住字母","examples":[{"en":"Writing helps children remember letters.","zh":"書寫幫助孩子記住字母。"},{"en":"To remember letters means to recognise and recall letter shapes and names.","zh":"記住字母意思是認出並回想字母形狀和名稱。"},{"en":"Tracing letters can help children remember letters more easily.","zh":"描摹字母可以幫助孩子更容易記住字母。"},{"en":"Children who remember letters well may learn to read faster.","zh":"能好好記住字母的孩子可能學閱讀更快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes early literacy learning.","zh":"這個短語描述早期讀寫學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pretty obvious","meaning":"相當明顯","examples":[{"en":"That seems pretty obvious when you think about it.","zh":"仔細想想，那似乎相當明顯。"},{"en":"Pretty obvious means quite easy to understand or notice.","zh":"相當明顯意思是頗容易理解或注意到。"},{"en":"It is pretty obvious that practice helps handwriting improve.","zh":"練習有助改善書寫，這相當明顯。"},{"en":"The link between movement and memory seems pretty obvious after the explanation.","zh":"解釋後，動作與記憶之間的關聯似乎相當明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something fairly clear.","zh":"這個短語描述相當清楚的事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"when you think about it","meaning":"仔細想想","examples":[{"en":"It seems obvious when you think about it.","zh":"仔細想想，這似乎很明顯。"},{"en":"“When you think about it” means after considering it carefully.","zh":"「When you think about it」意思是仔細考慮之後。"},{"en":"When you think about it, handwriting uses both the brain and body.","zh":"仔細想想，手寫同時使用大腦和身體。"},{"en":"A simple idea may become clearer when you think about it.","zh":"仔細想想，一個簡單想法可能變得更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase invites reflection.","zh":"這個短語邀請人反思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"What’s less obvious is","meaning":"較不明顯的是","examples":[{"en":"What’s less obvious is how handwriting helps develop concentration.","zh":"較不明顯的是手寫如何幫助培養專注力。"},{"en":"“What’s less obvious is” introduces a point that is not immediately clear.","zh":"「What’s less obvious is」用來引出不是馬上清楚的重點。"},{"en":"What’s less obvious is the link between handwriting and imagination.","zh":"較不明顯的是手寫與想像力之間的關聯。"},{"en":"Teachers may notice benefits that are less obvious to parents.","zh":"老師可能注意到對家長而言較不明顯的好處。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a surprising or hidden point.","zh":"這個短語突出令人驚訝或隱藏的重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"develop concentration","meaning":"培養專注力","examples":[{"en":"Handwriting helps children develop concentration.","zh":"手寫幫助孩子培養專注力。"},{"en":"To develop concentration means to build the ability to focus carefully.","zh":"培養專注力意思是建立仔細集中的能力。"},{"en":"Copying letters slowly can help children develop concentration.","zh":"慢慢抄寫字母可以幫助孩子培養專注力。"},{"en":"Children develop concentration when they sit still and focus on one task.","zh":"孩子坐定並專注一項任務時會培養專注力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth in attention skills.","zh":"這個短語描述注意力能力的成長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sit still","meaning":"坐定；坐好","examples":[{"en":"Children have to sit still when they practise handwriting.","zh":"孩子練習手寫時必須坐定。"},{"en":"To sit still means to sit without moving around.","zh":"坐定意思是坐着而不四處移動。"},{"en":"Some young children find it hard to sit still for long.","zh":"有些年幼孩子很難長時間坐定。"},{"en":"Handwriting practice can teach children to sit still and focus.","zh":"手寫練習可以教孩子坐定並專注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled body behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述受控制的身體行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"focus on one thing","meaning":"專注於一件事","examples":[{"en":"Children have to focus on one thing when they write.","zh":"孩子書寫時必須專注於一件事。"},{"en":"To focus on one thing means to give attention to a single task.","zh":"專注於一件事意思是把注意力放在單一任務上。"},{"en":"Handwriting requires children to focus on one thing for a short period.","zh":"手寫要求孩子短時間專注於一件事。"},{"en":"Focusing on one thing helps children improve concentration.","zh":"專注於一件事有助孩子提升專注力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes directing attention.","zh":"這個短語描述集中注意力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"that aspect of","meaning":"……的那一面","examples":[{"en":"That aspect of handwriting had never occurred to the woman before.","zh":"手寫的那一面以前從未出現在那位女士腦海中。"},{"en":"That aspect of something means that particular part or feature of it.","zh":"某事的那一面意思是它的某個特定部分或特點。"},{"en":"That aspect of handwriting is connected to concentration.","zh":"手寫的那一面與專注力有關。"},{"en":"Students had not considered that aspect of child development before.","zh":"學生以前沒有考慮兒童發展的那一面。"},{"en":"This phrase points to one part of a larger topic.","zh":"這個短語指出較大題目中的某一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"handwriting","meaning":"手寫；書寫","examples":[{"en":"Handwriting helps children develop several important skills.","zh":"手寫幫助孩子培養幾項重要技能。"},{"en":"Handwriting is writing done by hand with a pen, pencil, or similar tool.","zh":"手寫是用筆、鉛筆或類似工具以手寫出的文字。"},{"en":"Good handwriting is clear enough for others to read.","zh":"好的字跡應清楚到讓別人能讀。"},{"en":"Handwriting can support memory, concentration, and spatial awareness.","zh":"手寫可以支援記憶、專注力和空間感。"},{"en":"This word describes written work produced by hand.","zh":"這個詞描述用手寫出的文字作品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"had never occurred to me","meaning":"我以前從沒想過","examples":[{"en":"That aspect of handwriting had never occurred to me before.","zh":"手寫的那一面我以前從沒想過。"},{"en":"“Had never occurred to me” means I had never thought of it before.","zh":"「Had never occurred to me」意思是我以前從未想到它。"},{"en":"It had never occurred to me that handwriting could improve imagination.","zh":"我以前從沒想過手寫可以提升想像力。"},{"en":"The link between spacing and legibility had never occurred to him.","zh":"間距與可讀性之間的關聯他以前從沒想過。"},{"en":"This phrase shows surprise at a new idea.","zh":"這個短語顯示對新想法感到驚訝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Same here","meaning":"我也是","examples":[{"en":"The man says, “Same here,” when he agrees with the woman.","zh":"那位男士同意女士時說：「我也是。」"},{"en":"“Same here” means I feel or think the same way.","zh":"「Same here」意思是我也有同樣感受或想法。"},{"en":"I had never thought about spatial awareness either. Same here.","zh":"我也從未想過空間感。我也是。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to show quick agreement.","zh":"人們用這個短語快速表示同意。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and conversational.","zh":"這個短語較口語化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"improve children’s imagination","meaning":"提升孩子的想像力","examples":[{"en":"The man is not sure how handwriting improves children’s imagination.","zh":"那位男士不確定手寫如何提升孩子的想像力。"},{"en":"To improve children’s imagination means to help children create more ideas and mental images.","zh":"提升孩子的想像力意思是幫助孩子創造更多想法和腦海畫面。"},{"en":"Writing stories by hand may improve children’s imagination.","zh":"手寫故事可能提升孩子的想像力。"},{"en":"A study suggested handwriting can help children generate more ideas.","zh":"一項研究顯示手寫可以幫助孩子產生更多想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth in creative thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述創意思維的成長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"primary aged children","meaning":"小學年齡的孩子","examples":[{"en":"A study looked at primary aged children writing by hand.","zh":"一項研究觀察小學年齡的孩子手寫。"},{"en":"Primary aged children are children old enough to attend primary school.","zh":"小學年齡的孩子是指到了上小學年齡的孩子。"},{"en":"Primary aged children are still developing handwriting and reading skills.","zh":"小學年齡的孩子仍在發展書寫和閱讀技能。"},{"en":"Research on primary aged children can help teachers choose better methods.","zh":"關於小學年齡孩子的研究可以幫助老師選擇更好方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes children in the primary school age group.","zh":"這個短語描述小學年齡組別的孩子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"generate more ideas","meaning":"產生更多想法","examples":[{"en":"Children generated more ideas when they were writing by hand.","zh":"孩子手寫時產生更多想法。"},{"en":"To generate more ideas means to produce more thoughts, suggestions, or creative possibilities.","zh":"產生更多想法意思是創造更多思路、建議或創意可能性。"},{"en":"Students generated more ideas after drawing and writing by hand.","zh":"學生畫圖和手寫後產生更多想法。"},{"en":"Handwriting may help children generate more ideas because it slows thinking in a useful way.","zh":"手寫可能幫助孩子產生更多想法，因為它以有用方式放慢思考。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing more creative content.","zh":"這個短語描述產出更多創意內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"using a keyboard","meaning":"使用鍵盤","examples":[{"en":"The children generated fewer ideas when using a keyboard.","zh":"孩子使用鍵盤時產生較少想法。"},{"en":"Using a keyboard means typing on a computer, laptop, or digital device.","zh":"使用鍵盤意思是在電腦、手提電腦或數碼裝置上打字。"},{"en":"Some children type faster when using a keyboard.","zh":"有些孩子使用鍵盤時打字較快。"},{"en":"Using a keyboard may reduce frustration for children with handwriting difficulties.","zh":"使用鍵盤可能減少有書寫困難孩子的沮喪感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes writing through typing.","zh":"這個短語描述透過打字書寫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"I would’ve guessed that","meaning":"我本來就會猜到","examples":[{"en":"I would’ve guessed that children write more creatively by hand.","zh":"我本來就會猜到孩子手寫時更有創意。"},{"en":"“I would’ve guessed that” means that is what I would have expected.","zh":"「I would’ve guessed that」意思是那正是我本來預期的。"},{"en":"I would’ve guessed that handwriting helps memory.","zh":"我本來就會猜到手寫有助記憶。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when research matches their expectation.","zh":"當研究結果符合預期時，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the speaker is not surprised.","zh":"這個短語顯示說話者並不驚訝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be the case","meaning":"情況是這樣","examples":[{"en":"The woman guessed that this would be the case.","zh":"那位女士猜到情況會是這樣。"},{"en":"“Be the case” means be true or be the actual situation.","zh":"「Be the case」意思是屬實或實際情況如此。"},{"en":"She thought handwriting would help imagination, and the study showed that was the case.","zh":"她以為手寫會幫助想像力，而研究顯示情況確實如此。"},{"en":"It may not always be the case that typing is faster for every child.","zh":"打字對每個孩子都較快，未必總是這樣。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what is true in a situation.","zh":"這個短語指某情況中的真實狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"associate something with","meaning":"把……與……聯想起來","examples":[{"en":"The man had never associated spatial awareness with handwriting.","zh":"那位男士從未把空間感與手寫聯想起來。"},{"en":"To associate something with something else means to connect them in your mind.","zh":"把某物與另一物聯想起來，意思是在腦中把它們連接。"},{"en":"Many people associate handwriting with memory, but not with spatial awareness.","zh":"很多人把手寫與記憶聯想起來，但不會與空間感聯想起來。"},{"en":"Teachers may associate neat writing with good letter spacing.","zh":"老師可能把工整字跡與良好字母間距聯想起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a mental connection.","zh":"這個短語描述建立心理連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"spatial awareness","meaning":"空間感","examples":[{"en":"Good spatial awareness is essential for writing.","zh":"良好的空間感對書寫很重要。"},{"en":"Spatial awareness is the ability to understand where objects are in relation to each other.","zh":"空間感是理解物件彼此相對位置的能力。"},{"en":"Children need spatial awareness to place letters and words correctly on a page.","zh":"孩子需要空間感，才能在紙上正確放置字母和單字。"},{"en":"Poor spatial awareness can make handwriting untidy.","zh":"空間感弱可能令字跡不整齊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes understanding space and position.","zh":"這個短語描述對空間和位置的理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have more to do with","meaning":"與……更有關","examples":[{"en":"The man thought spatial awareness had more to do with knowing where you are.","zh":"那位男士以為空間感與知道自己在哪裏更有關。"},{"en":"To have more to do with something means to be more closely connected with it.","zh":"與某事更有關，意思是與它有更密切連繫。"},{"en":"He thought spatial awareness had more to do with movement than writing.","zh":"他以為空間感與動作比與書寫更有關。"},{"en":"Handwriting has more to do with spacing than many people realise.","zh":"手寫與間距的關係比很多人想像中更密切。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the strength of connections.","zh":"這個短語比較關聯的強弱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in relation to","meaning":"相對於……","examples":[{"en":"Spatial awareness involves knowing where you are in relation to objects.","zh":"空間感包括知道自己相對於物件的位置。"},{"en":"In relation to means compared with or connected to something else.","zh":"「In relation to」意思是與某物相比或與某物有關。"},{"en":"Children learn where letters sit in relation to lines on the page.","zh":"孩子學習字母相對於紙上線條的位置。"},{"en":"Spatial awareness helps children judge spaces in relation to words.","zh":"空間感幫助孩子判斷相對於單字的空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relative position or connection.","zh":"這個短語描述相對位置或連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be essential for","meaning":"對……很重要","examples":[{"en":"Good spatial awareness is essential for writing.","zh":"良好的空間感對書寫很重要。"},{"en":"To be essential for something means to be very necessary for it.","zh":"對某事很重要，意思是對它非常必要。"},{"en":"Fine motor skills are essential for forming letters.","zh":"精細動作能力對形成字母很重要。"},{"en":"Clear spacing is essential for legible handwriting.","zh":"清楚間距對字跡易讀很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something necessary for success.","zh":"這個短語描述成功所必需的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"space words correctly","meaning":"正確安排單字間距","examples":[{"en":"Children need to space words correctly when they write.","zh":"孩子書寫時需要正確安排單字間距。"},{"en":"To space words correctly means to leave suitable gaps between words.","zh":"正確安排單字間距意思是在單字之間留下合適空位。"},{"en":"Children who space words correctly produce clearer handwriting.","zh":"能正確安排單字間距的孩子寫出的字較清楚。"},{"en":"Grid paper can help children learn to space words correctly.","zh":"方格紙可以幫助孩子學習正確安排單字間距。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arranging written words clearly.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚排列書面單字。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fine motor skills","meaning":"精細動作能力","examples":[{"en":"Writing helps children improve their fine motor skills.","zh":"書寫幫助孩子提升精細動作能力。"},{"en":"Fine motor skills are small, controlled movements of the fingers and hands.","zh":"精細動作能力是手指和手部的小而受控的動作。"},{"en":"Holding a pencil helps develop fine motor skills.","zh":"握鉛筆有助發展精細動作能力。"},{"en":"Children with weak fine motor skills may find handwriting difficult.","zh":"精細動作能力弱的孩子可能覺得手寫困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes precise hand movement ability.","zh":"這個短語描述精準手部動作能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"improve through","meaning":"透過……提升","examples":[{"en":"Fine motor skills improve through writing.","zh":"精細動作能力透過書寫提升。"},{"en":"To improve through something means to get better because of that activity or method.","zh":"透過某事提升，意思是因該活動或方法而變得更好。"},{"en":"Children’s concentration can improve through regular handwriting practice.","zh":"孩子的專注力可以透過定期手寫練習提升。"},{"en":"Spacing may improve through using grid paper.","zh":"間距可以透過使用方格紙而改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how progress happens.","zh":"這個短語描述進步如何發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as I’d always assumed","meaning":"正如我一直以為的那樣","examples":[{"en":"Writing improves more than fine motor skills, as I’d always assumed.","zh":"書寫提升的不只是精細動作能力，正如我一直以為的那樣。"},{"en":"“As I’d always assumed” means as I had always believed or expected.","zh":"「As I’d always assumed」意思是正如我一直相信或預期的那樣。"},{"en":"I thought handwriting only improved hand control, as I’d always assumed.","zh":"我以為手寫只提升手部控制，正如我一直以為的那樣。"},{"en":"Research can challenge what we had always assumed.","zh":"研究可以挑戰我們一直以為的事。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a previous belief.","zh":"這個短語指先前的信念。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"children with dyspraxia","meaning":"有動作協調障礙的孩子","examples":[{"en":"Handwriting is much harder for children with dyspraxia.","zh":"對有動作協調障礙的孩子來說，手寫困難得多。"},{"en":"Children with dyspraxia are children who have difficulties with movement and coordination.","zh":"有動作協調障礙的孩子是在動作和協調方面有困難的孩子。"},{"en":"Children with dyspraxia may struggle to form letters clearly.","zh":"有動作協調障礙的孩子可能很難清楚寫出字母。"},{"en":"Teachers can support children with dyspraxia through games and special tools.","zh":"老師可以透過遊戲和特別工具支援有動作協調障礙的孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes children who need extra movement-related support.","zh":"這個短語描述需要額外動作支援的孩子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have problems coordinating movement","meaning":"在協調動作方面有困難","examples":[{"en":"Children with dyspraxia have problems coordinating movement.","zh":"有動作協調障礙的孩子在協調動作方面有困難。"},{"en":"To have problems coordinating movement means to find it hard to control body movements smoothly.","zh":"在協調動作方面有困難，意思是難以流暢控制身體動作。"},{"en":"A child may have problems coordinating movement when using a pencil.","zh":"孩子使用鉛筆時可能在協調動作方面有困難。"},{"en":"Movement coordination problems can affect handwriting and classroom tasks.","zh":"動作協調問題可以影響手寫和課堂任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulty controlling movement.","zh":"這個短語描述控制動作的困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the classroom","meaning":"在課堂上","examples":[{"en":"There are many things teachers can do in the classroom to help them.","zh":"老師在課堂上可以做很多事情來幫助他們。"},{"en":"In the classroom means during lessons or within the school learning space.","zh":"在課堂上意思是在課堂期間或學校學習空間內。"},{"en":"Teachers can use grid paper in the classroom.","zh":"老師可以在課堂上使用方格紙。"},{"en":"In the classroom, small changes can support children with handwriting difficulties.","zh":"在課堂上，小改變可以支援有書寫困難的孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the teaching environment.","zh":"這個短語描述教學環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"support with letter formation","meaning":"字母成形方面的支援","examples":[{"en":"Children with dyspraxia need more support with letter formation.","zh":"有動作協調障礙的孩子需要更多字母成形方面的支援。"},{"en":"Support with letter formation means help in learning how to shape letters correctly.","zh":"字母成形方面的支援是指幫助孩子學會正確寫出字母形狀。"},{"en":"Teachers can give support with letter formation through tracing activities.","zh":"老師可以透過描摹活動提供字母成形方面的支援。"},{"en":"Children who struggle with movement may need extra support with letter formation.","zh":"在動作方面有困難的孩子可能需要額外字母成形支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes help with writing letter shapes.","zh":"這個短語描述對書寫字母形狀的幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"letter formation","meaning":"字母成形","examples":[{"en":"Teachers can support children with letter formation.","zh":"老師可以支援孩子的字母成形。"},{"en":"Letter formation is the way letters are shaped and written.","zh":"字母成形是字母被塑造和寫出的方式。"},{"en":"Good letter formation makes handwriting easier to read.","zh":"良好的字母成形令字跡更容易閱讀。"},{"en":"Children practise letter formation by tracing and copying letters.","zh":"孩子透過描摹和抄寫字母練習字母成形。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how letters are made by hand.","zh":"這個短語描述字母如何用手寫成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"play lots of games to","meaning":"玩很多遊戲去……","examples":[{"en":"Teachers can play lots of games to help children distinguish letter shapes.","zh":"老師可以玩很多遊戲去幫助孩子分辨字母形狀。"},{"en":"To play lots of games to do something means to use many game activities for that purpose.","zh":"玩很多遊戲去做某事，意思是使用很多遊戲活動達到該目的。"},{"en":"Teachers play lots of games to help children remember letters.","zh":"老師玩很多遊戲去幫助孩子記住字母。"},{"en":"Games can make handwriting practice less stressful.","zh":"遊戲可以令手寫練習壓力較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning through repeated playful activities.","zh":"這個短語描述透過重複而有趣的活動學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"distinguish letter shapes","meaning":"分辨字母形狀","examples":[{"en":"Games can help children distinguish letter shapes.","zh":"遊戲可以幫助孩子分辨字母形狀。"},{"en":"To distinguish letter shapes means to see the differences between letters.","zh":"分辨字母形狀意思是看出字母之間的差異。"},{"en":"Children must distinguish letter shapes such as b and d.","zh":"孩子必須分辨 b 和 d 等字母形狀。"},{"en":"Distinguishing letter shapes helps children read and write more accurately.","zh":"分辨字母形狀有助孩子更準確地閱讀和書寫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognising visual differences in letters.","zh":"這個短語描述辨認字母的視覺差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take a lot of patience","meaning":"需要很大耐性","examples":[{"en":"Helping children with dyspraxia takes a lot of patience.","zh":"幫助有動作協調障礙的孩子需要很大耐性。"},{"en":"To take a lot of patience means to require calmness and time.","zh":"需要很大耐性意思是需要冷靜和時間。"},{"en":"Teaching handwriting can take a lot of patience.","zh":"教手寫可能需要很大耐性。"},{"en":"Children may need repeated support, so teachers need patience.","zh":"孩子可能需要反覆支援，所以老師需要耐性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a task that cannot be rushed.","zh":"這個短語描述不能急於完成的任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pens that light up","meaning":"會亮起來的筆","examples":[{"en":"Some pens light up if a child presses too hard.","zh":"有些筆在孩子用力過大時會亮起來。"},{"en":"Pens that light up are pens with lights that turn on under certain conditions.","zh":"會亮起來的筆是指在特定情況下燈會開啟的筆。"},{"en":"Pens that light up can show children when they are pressing too hard.","zh":"會亮起來的筆可以告訴孩子他們用力過大。"},{"en":"A light-up pen gives immediate feedback during handwriting practice.","zh":"發光筆在手寫練習中提供即時回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a special learning tool.","zh":"這個短語描述一種特別學習工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"press too hard","meaning":"用力過大","examples":[{"en":"The pen lights up if you press too hard.","zh":"如果你用力過大，這支筆會亮起來。"},{"en":"To press too hard means to use too much force when writing or touching something.","zh":"用力過大意思是書寫或觸碰某物時使用太多力量。"},{"en":"Some children press too hard with a pencil and tire their hands.","zh":"有些孩子用鉛筆時用力過大，令手感到疲倦。"},{"en":"Pressing too hard can make handwriting messy or uncomfortable.","zh":"用力過大可以令字跡凌亂或令人不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase describes excessive pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述過多壓力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a simple solution","meaning":"簡單的解決辦法","examples":[{"en":"The woman thinks the special pen is a simple solution.","zh":"那位女士認為這支特別的筆是一個簡單的解決辦法。"},{"en":"A simple solution is an easy way to solve a problem.","zh":"簡單的解決辦法是解決問題的容易方法。"},{"en":"Grid paper can be a simple solution for spacing problems.","zh":"方格紙可以是間距問題的簡單解決辦法。"},{"en":"A simple solution is useful when teachers need something practical in class.","zh":"當老師需要課堂上的實用方法時，簡單的解決辦法很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an easy and direct answer to a difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述對困難的容易而直接答案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"there’s much you can do about","meaning":"對……可以做很多","examples":[{"en":"The man is not sure there is much you can do about slow handwriting.","zh":"那位男士不確定對書寫慢可以做很多。"},{"en":"“There’s much you can do about” means there are many possible ways to improve or solve it.","zh":"「There’s much you can do about」意思是有很多方法可以改善或解決它。"},{"en":"There may not be much you can do about speed at first.","zh":"一開始對速度可能沒有很多可以做。"},{"en":"Teachers can do more about accuracy than speed in early handwriting.","zh":"老師在早期手寫中對準確性可以做的比速度更多。"},{"en":"This phrase discusses whether a problem can be changed.","zh":"這個短語討論問題是否可以改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"write very slowly","meaning":"寫得很慢","examples":[{"en":"Some children with dyspraxia write very slowly.","zh":"有些有動作協調障礙的孩子寫得很慢。"},{"en":"To write very slowly means to produce handwriting at a slow speed.","zh":"寫得很慢意思是以很慢速度手寫。"},{"en":"Children may write very slowly when forming letters takes great effort.","zh":"當形成字母很費力時，孩子可能寫得很慢。"},{"en":"Writing very slowly can make classroom tasks frustrating.","zh":"寫得很慢可以令課堂任務令人沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow handwriting speed.","zh":"這個短語描述手寫速度慢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"focus on accuracy","meaning":"注重準確性","examples":[{"en":"It is more important to focus on accuracy first.","zh":"先注重準確性更重要。"},{"en":"To focus on accuracy means to pay attention to correctness before speed.","zh":"注重準確性意思是在速度之前先注意正確性。"},{"en":"Teachers may focus on accuracy before asking children to write faster.","zh":"老師可能先注重準確性，再要求孩子寫快一點。"},{"en":"Focusing on accuracy can help children form good habits.","zh":"注重準確性可以幫助孩子形成良好習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes prioritising correct work.","zh":"這個短語描述優先處理正確性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get more confident","meaning":"變得更有信心","examples":[{"en":"Children may speed up as they get more confident.","zh":"孩子變得更有信心時，速度可能會加快。"},{"en":"To get more confident means to begin feeling more sure of your ability.","zh":"變得更有信心意思是開始對自己的能力更有把握。"},{"en":"Children get more confident when they practise handwriting regularly.","zh":"孩子定期練習手寫時會變得更有信心。"},{"en":"As students get more confident, they may worry less about mistakes.","zh":"當學生變得更有信心時，他們可能較少擔心錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growing self-belief.","zh":"這個短語描述自信心增長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"eventually speed up","meaning":"最終加快速度","examples":[{"en":"Children may eventually speed up when they become more confident.","zh":"孩子變得更有信心時，最終可能加快速度。"},{"en":"To eventually speed up means to become faster after some time.","zh":"最終加快速度意思是過一段時間後變得更快。"},{"en":"A child may eventually speed up after mastering letter formation.","zh":"孩子掌握字母成形後，最終可能加快速度。"},{"en":"Teachers should not force speed too early because children may eventually speed up naturally.","zh":"老師不應太早強迫速度，因為孩子最終可能自然加快速度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes later improvement in speed.","zh":"這個短語描述之後在速度上的改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"grid paper","meaning":"方格紙","examples":[{"en":"Teachers can use grid paper to help children space letters correctly.","zh":"老師可以使用方格紙幫助孩子正確安排字母間距。"},{"en":"Grid paper is paper printed with small boxes or squares.","zh":"方格紙是印有小格或方格的紙。"},{"en":"Grid paper helps children see where each letter should go.","zh":"方格紙幫助孩子看見每個字母應該放在哪裏。"},{"en":"Teachers use grid paper for spacing, size, and alignment practice.","zh":"老師使用方格紙練習間距、大小和對齊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical handwriting support tool.","zh":"這個短語描述實用的書寫支援工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"write each letter in a box","meaning":"把每個字母寫在一個格內","examples":[{"en":"Children write each letter in a box on grid paper.","zh":"孩子在方格紙上把每個字母寫在一個格內。"},{"en":"To write each letter in a box means to put one letter inside each square.","zh":"把每個字母寫在一個格內，意思是每個方格裏放一個字母。"},{"en":"Writing each letter in a box helps children control letter size.","zh":"把每個字母寫在一個格內有助孩子控制字母大小。"},{"en":"This method can train children to leave correct spaces.","zh":"這個方法可以訓練孩子留下正確間距。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a structured handwriting activity.","zh":"這個短語描述有結構的手寫活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"train someone to","meaning":"訓練某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Grid paper trains children to space letters correctly.","zh":"方格紙訓練孩子正確安排字母間距。"},{"en":"To train someone to do something means to teach them through practice.","zh":"訓練某人去做某事，意思是透過練習教導他們。"},{"en":"Repeated exercises train children to form letters clearly.","zh":"重複練習訓練孩子清楚形成字母。"},{"en":"Teachers can train students to write more legibly.","zh":"老師可以訓練學生寫得更清楚易讀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes skill-building through practice.","zh":"這個短語描述透過練習建立技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"space the letters correctly","meaning":"正確安排字母間距","examples":[{"en":"Grid paper helps children space the letters correctly.","zh":"方格紙幫助孩子正確安排字母間距。"},{"en":"To space the letters correctly means to leave suitable gaps between letters.","zh":"正確安排字母間距意思是在字母之間留下合適空位。"},{"en":"Children need to space the letters correctly so words are easy to read.","zh":"孩子需要正確安排字母間距，讓單字容易閱讀。"},{"en":"Poor spacing can make handwriting unclear.","zh":"間距差會令字跡不清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arranging letters clearly on the page.","zh":"這個短語描述在紙上清楚排列字母。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"legibility","meaning":"清晰易讀程度","examples":[{"en":"Correct spacing is important for legibility.","zh":"正確間距對清晰易讀程度很重要。"},{"en":"Legibility is how easy handwriting or text is to read.","zh":"清晰易讀程度是字跡或文字有多容易閱讀。"},{"en":"Good spacing improves legibility even if letters are not perfect.","zh":"良好間距可以提升清晰易讀程度，即使字母不是完美。"},{"en":"Examiners need legibility so they can understand a student’s answer.","zh":"考官需要清晰易讀程度，才能理解學生答案。"},{"en":"This word describes the readability of writing.","zh":"這個詞描述文字的可讀性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"more important for legibility than","meaning":"對可讀性比……更重要","examples":[{"en":"Spacing letters correctly is more important for legibility than writing in a straight line.","zh":"正確安排字母間距對可讀性比寫成一直線更重要。"},{"en":"“More important for legibility than” compares which factor helps readability more.","zh":"「More important for legibility than」比較哪個因素對可讀性更有幫助。"},{"en":"Letter spacing may be more important for legibility than perfect decoration.","zh":"字母間距對可讀性可能比完美裝飾更重要。"},{"en":"Teachers should know what is more important for legibility than neat appearance alone.","zh":"老師應知道甚麼對可讀性比單純外觀工整更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two influences on readability.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個對可讀性的影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"write in a straight line","meaning":"寫成一直線","examples":[{"en":"Some children find it difficult to write in a straight line.","zh":"有些孩子覺得很難寫成一直線。"},{"en":"To write in a straight line means to keep writing level across the page.","zh":"寫成一直線意思是讓文字在紙上保持水平。"},{"en":"Grid paper can help children write in a straight line.","zh":"方格紙可以幫助孩子寫成一直線。"},{"en":"Writing in a straight line matters, but spacing may matter more.","zh":"寫成一直線很重要，但間距可能更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes alignment in handwriting.","zh":"這個短語描述手寫中的對齊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"write on a laptop","meaning":"用手提電腦書寫","examples":[{"en":"For some children, it may be better to write on a laptop.","zh":"對有些孩子來說，用手提電腦書寫可能更好。"},{"en":"To write on a laptop means to type text using a laptop computer.","zh":"用手提電腦書寫意思是使用手提電腦打字輸入文字。"},{"en":"Children with severe handwriting difficulties may write better on a laptop.","zh":"有嚴重書寫困難的孩子可能用手提電腦書寫得更好。"},{"en":"Writing on a laptop can reduce frustration for some learners.","zh":"用手提電腦書寫可以減少一些學習者的沮喪感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes digital writing.","zh":"這個短語描述數碼書寫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rather than by hand","meaning":"而不是手寫","examples":[{"en":"Some children may write better on a laptop rather than by hand.","zh":"有些孩子用手提電腦而不是手寫可能寫得更好。"},{"en":"Rather than by hand means instead of writing with a pen or pencil.","zh":"而不是手寫意思是不用筆或鉛筆書寫，而改用其他方式。"},{"en":"A child with dyslexia may prefer typing rather than writing by hand.","zh":"有讀寫障礙的孩子可能較喜歡打字，而不是手寫。"},{"en":"Teachers may allow laptops rather than handwriting in some cases.","zh":"在某些情況下，老師可能允許使用手提電腦而不是手寫。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a contrast between typing and handwriting.","zh":"這個短語顯示打字與手寫之間的對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"children with dyslexia","meaning":"有讀寫障礙的孩子","examples":[{"en":"Children with dyslexia often struggle with handwriting.","zh":"有讀寫障礙的孩子常在手寫方面很吃力。"},{"en":"Children with dyslexia are children who have difficulties with reading, spelling, or language processing.","zh":"有讀寫障礙的孩子是在閱讀、拼寫或語言處理方面有困難的孩子。"},{"en":"Children with dyslexia may find writing by hand slow and frustrating.","zh":"有讀寫障礙的孩子可能覺得手寫很慢又令人沮喪。"},{"en":"Some children with dyslexia feel more confident using a keyboard.","zh":"有些有讀寫障礙的孩子使用鍵盤時更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learners who may need literacy support.","zh":"這個短語描述可能需要讀寫支援的學習者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"struggle with handwriting","meaning":"在手寫方面很吃力","examples":[{"en":"Children with dyslexia often struggle with handwriting.","zh":"有讀寫障礙的孩子常在手寫方面很吃力。"},{"en":"To struggle with handwriting means to find handwriting difficult or frustrating.","zh":"在手寫方面很吃力，意思是覺得手寫困難或令人沮喪。"},{"en":"A child may struggle with handwriting because of spelling or motor problems.","zh":"孩子可能因拼寫或動作問題而在手寫方面吃力。"},{"en":"Students who struggle with handwriting may write less than they know.","zh":"在手寫方面吃力的學生，可能寫出的內容少於他們知道的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulty with written work by hand.","zh":"這個短語描述手寫工作的困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"give up","meaning":"放棄","examples":[{"en":"Some children give up because handwriting is too frustrating.","zh":"有些孩子因手寫太令人沮喪而放棄。"},{"en":"To give up means to stop trying.","zh":"放棄意思是停止嘗試。"},{"en":"A child may give up if every handwriting task feels painful.","zh":"如果每項手寫任務都令人痛苦，孩子可能會放棄。"},{"en":"Teachers want children to keep trying rather than give up.","zh":"老師希望孩子繼續嘗試，而不是放棄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes losing motivation to continue.","zh":"這個短語描述失去繼續的動力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"frustrating for someone","meaning":"令某人沮喪","examples":[{"en":"Writing is less frustrating for them on a keyboard.","zh":"對他們來說，用鍵盤書寫較不令人沮喪。"},{"en":"Frustrating for someone means causing that person to feel upset or annoyed because something is difficult.","zh":"令某人沮喪意思是因某事困難而令那個人感到不快或煩躁。"},{"en":"Handwriting can be frustrating for children who make frequent mistakes.","zh":"對經常犯錯的孩子來說，手寫可能令人沮喪。"},{"en":"Typing may be less frustrating for some children with dyslexia.","zh":"對一些有讀寫障礙的孩子來說，打字可能較不令人沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an emotional reaction to difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述面對困難時的情緒反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get things wrong","meaning":"做錯；寫錯","examples":[{"en":"Children may feel less frustrated if they get things wrong on a keyboard.","zh":"如果孩子在鍵盤上做錯，他們可能較少感到沮喪。"},{"en":"To get things wrong means to make mistakes.","zh":"做錯或寫錯意思是犯錯。"},{"en":"Children may get spelling or punctuation wrong when they write.","zh":"孩子書寫時可能拼寫或標點錯誤。"},{"en":"On a keyboard, it is easier to correct things when children get them wrong.","zh":"在鍵盤上，孩子做錯時較容易修改。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making errors.","zh":"這個短語描述犯錯。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be willing to have a go","meaning":"更願意嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Children may be more willing to have a go when using a keyboard.","zh":"使用鍵盤時，孩子可能更願意嘗試。"},{"en":"To be willing to have a go means to be ready to try something.","zh":"更願意嘗試意思是準備好去試做某事。"},{"en":"A child may be willing to have a go if mistakes are easy to fix.","zh":"如果錯誤容易修正，孩子可能更願意嘗試。"},{"en":"Using a laptop can make some children more willing to write.","zh":"使用手提電腦可以令一些孩子更願意寫作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes readiness to try.","zh":"這個短語描述願意嘗試的狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"develop fluency","meaning":"培養流暢度","examples":[{"en":"Using a laptop does not necessarily help children develop fluency faster.","zh":"使用手提電腦不一定幫助孩子更快培養流暢度。"},{"en":"To develop fluency means to become able to write or express ideas smoothly and easily.","zh":"培養流暢度意思是變得能夠順暢而容易地書寫或表達想法。"},{"en":"Children develop fluency through regular practice.","zh":"孩子透過定期練習培養流暢度。"},{"en":"Typing may help confidence, but it may not develop fluency faster.","zh":"打字可能幫助信心，但未必更快培養流暢度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth in smooth expression.","zh":"這個短語描述順暢表達能力的成長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"any faster","meaning":"更快","examples":[{"en":"Developing fluency is not any faster on a laptop.","zh":"在手提電腦上培養流暢度並沒有更快。"},{"en":"Not any faster means not faster at all.","zh":"沒有更快意思是一點也沒有加快。"},{"en":"Typing did not make the children develop fluency any faster.","zh":"打字沒有令孩子更快培養流暢度。"},{"en":"A laptop may reduce frustration without making learning any faster.","zh":"手提電腦可能減少沮喪，但不會令學習更快。"},{"en":"This phrase denies an increase in speed.","zh":"這個短語否定速度增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an article on the benefits of","meaning":"一篇關於……好處的文章","examples":[{"en":"The man read an article on the benefits of teaching print.","zh":"那位男士讀了一篇關於教印刷體書寫好處的文章。"},{"en":"An article on the benefits of something is a written piece explaining its advantages.","zh":"一篇關於某事好處的文章，是解釋其優點的文字作品。"},{"en":"She read an article on the benefits of handwriting practice.","zh":"她讀了一篇關於手寫練習好處的文章。"},{"en":"Articles on education benefits can help students support their assignment.","zh":"關於教育好處的文章可以幫助學生支持作業。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a written source about advantages.","zh":"這個短語引出一個關於優點的文字來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"teaching print","meaning":"教印刷體書寫","examples":[{"en":"The article discussed the benefits of teaching print rather than cursive handwriting.","zh":"這篇文章討論教印刷體書寫而不是草寫體書寫的好處。"},{"en":"Teaching print means teaching children to write separate, unjoined letters.","zh":"教印刷體書寫意思是教孩子寫分開、不連筆的字母。"},{"en":"Teaching print may be easier for children with learning difficulties.","zh":"對有學習困難的孩子來說，教印刷體書寫可能較容易。"},{"en":"Some teachers now prefer teaching print before cursive.","zh":"有些老師現在較喜歡先教印刷體書寫，再教草寫體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes instruction in printed letter writing.","zh":"這個短語描述教授印刷字母書寫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cursive handwriting","meaning":"草寫體書寫","examples":[{"en":"Cursive handwriting is harder for some children to learn.","zh":"草寫體書寫對有些孩子來說較難學。"},{"en":"Cursive handwriting is a style of writing in which letters are joined together.","zh":"草寫體書寫是一種字母連在一起的書寫方式。"},{"en":"Cursive handwriting was once considered stylish and educated.","zh":"草寫體書寫曾被認為有風格和有教養。"},{"en":"Children with learning difficulties may find cursive handwriting challenging.","zh":"有學習困難的孩子可能覺得草寫體書寫很有挑戰性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes joined-up handwriting.","zh":"這個短語描述連筆書寫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be joined up","meaning":"連在一起","examples":[{"en":"In cursive handwriting, the letters are joined up.","zh":"在草寫體書寫中，字母是連在一起的。"},{"en":"To be joined up means to be connected together.","zh":"連在一起意思是彼此連接。"},{"en":"In cursive, many letters are joined up in one flowing line.","zh":"在草寫中，很多字母以流暢線條連在一起。"},{"en":"Joined-up letters can be difficult for some children to read and write.","zh":"連在一起的字母對有些孩子來說可能難讀也難寫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes connected writing.","zh":"這個短語描述連接的書寫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"過去","examples":[{"en":"In the past, cursive writing was considered more stylish.","zh":"過去，草寫體書寫被認為更有風格。"},{"en":"In the past means during an earlier time.","zh":"過去意思是在較早的時間。"},{"en":"In the past, many schools strongly taught cursive handwriting.","zh":"過去，很多學校很重視教草寫體書寫。"},{"en":"Attitudes to handwriting have changed since the past.","zh":"人們對書寫的態度自過去以來已改變。"},{"en":"This phrase compares earlier times with now.","zh":"這個短語比較以前與現在。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be considered more stylish","meaning":"被認為更有風格","examples":[{"en":"Cursive writing was once considered more stylish.","zh":"草寫體書寫曾被認為更有風格。"},{"en":"To be considered more stylish means people thought it looked more elegant or attractive.","zh":"被認為更有風格，意思是人們覺得它看起來更優雅或吸引。"},{"en":"In the past, joined-up writing was considered more stylish than print.","zh":"過去，連筆書寫被認為比印刷體更有風格。"},{"en":"What is considered stylish can change over time.","zh":"被認為有風格的事物可以隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social judgement about appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述社會對外觀的評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"educated","meaning":"有教養的","examples":[{"en":"Cursive writing was considered more stylish and educated.","zh":"草寫體書寫被認為更有風格和有教養。"},{"en":"Educated means showing learning, schooling, or cultural refinement.","zh":"有教養的意思是顯示出學識、教育或文化修養。"},{"en":"In the past, neat cursive handwriting was seen as educated.","zh":"過去，工整的草寫體字跡被視為有教養。"},{"en":"People should not judge a child’s knowledge only by handwriting that looks educated.","zh":"人們不應只因字跡看起來有教養而評判孩子的知識。"},{"en":"This word can describe the impression created by writing style.","zh":"這個詞可以描述書寫風格造成的印象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not anymore","meaning":"現在不再是這樣","examples":[{"en":"Cursive writing was once preferred, but not anymore.","zh":"草寫體書寫曾經較受歡迎，但現在不再是這樣。"},{"en":"Not anymore means something was true before but is no longer true now.","zh":"現在不再是這樣意思是某事以前是真的，但現在不再如此。"},{"en":"Schools once insisted on cursive, but not anymore.","zh":"學校曾經堅持草寫，但現在不再是這樣。"},{"en":"People used to write letters by hand often, but not anymore.","zh":"人們以前常手寫信，但現在不再是這樣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a change from past to present.","zh":"這個短語顯示從過去到現在的改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"attitudes have changed","meaning":"態度已經改變","examples":[{"en":"Teachers’ attitudes have changed.","zh":"老師的態度已經改變。"},{"en":"Attitudes have changed means people now think differently from before.","zh":"態度已經改變意思是人們現在的想法與以前不同。"},{"en":"Attitudes have changed about whether cursive should be taught first.","zh":"對是否應先教草寫體，態度已經改變。"},{"en":"Teachers’ attitudes have changed because evidence shows print may be easier.","zh":"老師的態度已經改變，因為證據顯示印刷體可能較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in opinions.","zh":"這個短語描述意見轉變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"it has been proved that","meaning":"事實證明","examples":[{"en":"It has been proved that cursive is more difficult to learn.","zh":"事實證明草寫體較難學。"},{"en":"“It has been proved that” means evidence has shown something to be true.","zh":"「It has been proved that」意思是證據已顯示某事是真的。"},{"en":"It has been proved that handwriting helps memory.","zh":"事實證明手寫有助記憶。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to introduce a strong research finding.","zh":"作者使用這個短語來引出有力研究發現。"},{"en":"This phrase presents a claim as supported by proof.","zh":"這個短語把說法呈現為有證據支持。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"learning difficulties","meaning":"學習困難","examples":[{"en":"Cursive writing is especially difficult for children with learning difficulties.","zh":"草寫體書寫對有學習困難的孩子尤其困難。"},{"en":"Learning difficulties are conditions that make learning certain skills harder.","zh":"學習困難是令學習某些技能變得較困難的情況。"},{"en":"Children with learning difficulties may need extra time and support.","zh":"有學習困難的孩子可能需要額外時間和支援。"},{"en":"A child with learning difficulties may find joined-up letters confusing.","zh":"有學習困難的孩子可能覺得連筆字母很混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes barriers to learning.","zh":"這個短語描述學習上的障礙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"join up letters","meaning":"把字母連起來","examples":[{"en":"Some children find it challenging to join up letters.","zh":"有些孩子覺得把字母連起來很有挑戰性。"},{"en":"To join up letters means to connect letters together when writing.","zh":"把字母連起來意思是書寫時把字母彼此連接。"},{"en":"Cursive handwriting requires children to join up letters smoothly.","zh":"草寫體書寫要求孩子流暢地把字母連起來。"},{"en":"Children with learning difficulties may struggle to join up letters.","zh":"有學習困難的孩子可能難以把字母連起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes connected letter writing.","zh":"這個短語描述連筆書寫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"find something challenging","meaning":"覺得……很有挑戰性","examples":[{"en":"Children with learning difficulties find joining up letters really challenging.","zh":"有學習困難的孩子覺得把字母連起來很有挑戰性。"},{"en":"To find something challenging means to think it is difficult but possibly worth trying.","zh":"覺得某事很有挑戰性，意思是認為它困難但可能值得嘗試。"},{"en":"Some children find handwriting challenging at first.","zh":"有些孩子一開始覺得手寫很有挑戰性。"},{"en":"Teachers should support children who find letter formation challenging.","zh":"老師應支援覺得字母成形很有挑戰性的孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes perceived difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述感受到的困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"poor handwriting","meaning":"糟糕的字跡","examples":[{"en":"The man was worried that his poor handwriting affected his exam results.","zh":"那位男士擔心自己糟糕的字跡影響考試成績。"},{"en":"Poor handwriting is writing that is unclear, messy, or hard to read.","zh":"糟糕的字跡是指不清楚、凌亂或難以閱讀的字。"},{"en":"Poor handwriting can make it difficult for examiners to read an answer.","zh":"糟糕的字跡可以令考官難以看懂答案。"},{"en":"A student with poor handwriting may lose marks unfairly if the script is unclear.","zh":"如果答卷不清楚，字跡糟糕的學生可能會不公平地失分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low handwriting quality.","zh":"這個短語描述低質素字跡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"affect exam results","meaning":"影響考試成績","examples":[{"en":"Poor handwriting can affect exam results.","zh":"糟糕的字跡可以影響考試成績。"},{"en":"To affect exam results means to influence the marks or grades a student receives.","zh":"影響考試成績意思是影響學生得到的分數或等級。"},{"en":"If examiners cannot read a script, handwriting may affect exam results.","zh":"如果考官看不懂答卷，字跡可能影響考試成績。"},{"en":"Poor spelling and punctuation can also affect exam results.","zh":"糟糕的拼寫和標點也可以影響考試成績。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an influence on assessment outcomes.","zh":"這個短語描述對評核結果的影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"research shows that","meaning":"研究顯示","examples":[{"en":"Research shows that poor handwriting can affect marks.","zh":"研究顯示糟糕的字跡可以影響分數。"},{"en":"“Research shows that” means studies provide evidence for a claim.","zh":"「Research shows that」意思是研究為某說法提供證據。"},{"en":"Research shows that handwriting can help children remember letters.","zh":"研究顯示手寫可以幫助孩子記住字母。"},{"en":"Teachers should consider what research shows before changing classroom practice.","zh":"老師改變課堂做法前，應考慮研究顯示的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence from studies.","zh":"這個短語引出來自研究的證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be right to worry","meaning":"擔心得有道理","examples":[{"en":"The man thinks he was right to worry about his handwriting.","zh":"那位男士認為自己擔心字跡是有道理的。"},{"en":"To be right to worry means the concern was reasonable or justified.","zh":"擔心得有道理意思是該憂慮合理或有根據。"},{"en":"He was right to worry because poor handwriting can affect marks.","zh":"他擔心得有道理，因為糟糕字跡可以影響分數。"},{"en":"Parents may be right to worry if a child cannot write legibly.","zh":"如果孩子不能寫得清楚易讀，家長可能擔心得有道理。"},{"en":"This phrase confirms that a concern makes sense.","zh":"這個短語確認某個憂慮是合理的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be judged on","meaning":"因……而被評分","examples":[{"en":"Students may feel unfairly judged on their handwriting.","zh":"學生可能覺得因字跡而被評分很不公平。"},{"en":"To be judged on something means to be assessed according to that thing.","zh":"因某事而被評分，意思是根據該事被評估。"},{"en":"Students should be judged on knowledge, not only handwriting.","zh":"學生應因知識而被評分，而不只是因字跡。"},{"en":"If scripts are hard to read, candidates may be judged on legibility too.","zh":"如果答卷難讀，考生也可能因可讀性而被評分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the basis for evaluation.","zh":"這個短語描述評估的依據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not just their knowledge","meaning":"不只是他們的知識","examples":[{"en":"Students are judged on their handwriting, not just their knowledge.","zh":"學生因字跡而被評分，不只是因他們的知識。"},{"en":"Not just their knowledge means more than only what they know.","zh":"不只是他們的知識，意思是不只包括他們知道的內容。"},{"en":"Exam marks may reflect handwriting, not just knowledge.","zh":"考試分數可能反映字跡，而不只是知識。"},{"en":"Students may feel frustrated if presentation matters, not just their knowledge.","zh":"如果呈現方式也重要，而不只是他們的知識，學生可能會沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts content with another factor.","zh":"這個短語把內容與另一因素作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"marks are affected","meaning":"分數會受影響","examples":[{"en":"Marks are affected if examiners cannot read the script.","zh":"如果考官看不懂答卷，分數會受影響。"},{"en":"Marks are affected means scores are changed or influenced.","zh":"分數會受影響意思是成績被改變或影響。"},{"en":"Marks may be affected by unclear handwriting.","zh":"分數可能會因字跡不清而受影響。"},{"en":"If the examiner cannot understand an answer, marks are affected.","zh":"如果考官不能理解答案，分數會受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change in assessment results.","zh":"這個短語描述評核結果受到改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"examiners","meaning":"考官","examples":[{"en":"Examiners need to be able to read the script.","zh":"考官需要能夠看懂答卷。"},{"en":"Examiners are people who mark exams or assess candidates’ work.","zh":"考官是批改考試或評估考生作品的人。"},{"en":"Examiners may struggle if handwriting is unclear.","zh":"如果字跡不清，考官可能會很吃力。"},{"en":"Clear answers help examiners judge knowledge fairly.","zh":"清楚答案幫助考官公平判斷知識。"},{"en":"This word describes people who evaluate exam scripts.","zh":"這個詞描述評估考試答卷的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"read the script","meaning":"看懂答卷","examples":[{"en":"Marks are affected if examiners cannot read the script.","zh":"如果考官看不懂答卷，分數會受影響。"},{"en":"To read the script means to understand the written exam answer or paper.","zh":"看懂答卷意思是理解書面考試答案或試卷。"},{"en":"Examiners must read the script before giving marks.","zh":"考官必須先看懂答卷，才能給分。"},{"en":"If handwriting is too messy, it may be hard to read the script.","zh":"如果字跡太凌亂，可能難以看懂答卷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reading a student’s written answer.","zh":"這個短語描述閱讀學生的書面答案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"write legibly","meaning":"寫得清楚易讀","examples":[{"en":"It is important to teach children to write legibly.","zh":"教孩子寫得清楚易讀很重要。"},{"en":"To write legibly means to write clearly enough for others to read.","zh":"寫得清楚易讀意思是字跡清楚到別人能閱讀。"},{"en":"Children need practice to write legibly in exams.","zh":"孩子需要練習，才能在考試中寫得清楚易讀。"},{"en":"Writing legibly can help students communicate their ideas clearly.","zh":"寫得清楚易讀可以幫助學生清楚表達想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes readable handwriting.","zh":"這個短語描述可讀的手寫字。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the role of handwriting","meaning":"手寫的作用","examples":[{"en":"The students discuss whether the role of handwriting will change in the future.","zh":"學生討論手寫的作用將來是否會改變。"},{"en":"The role of handwriting means the purpose or importance handwriting has.","zh":"手寫的作用意思是手寫具有的目的或重要性。"},{"en":"The role of handwriting may change as digital devices become more common.","zh":"隨着數碼裝置更普遍，手寫的作用可能會改變。"},{"en":"Teachers still see the role of handwriting as important in early learning.","zh":"老師仍然認為手寫在早期學習中的作用很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes handwriting’s function in life and education.","zh":"這個短語描述手寫在生活和教育中的功能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"I can’t see that changing much","meaning":"我看不出那會有太大改變","examples":[{"en":"The man says he cannot see the role of handwriting changing much.","zh":"那位男士說他看不出手寫的作用會有太大改變。"},{"en":"“I can’t see that changing much” means I do not think it will become very different.","zh":"「I can’t see that changing much」意思是我不認為它會變得很不同。"},{"en":"I can’t see handwriting disappearing from schools anytime soon.","zh":"我看不出手寫會很快從學校消失。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they predict little change.","zh":"當人們預測變化不大時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a cautious prediction.","zh":"這個短語表達謹慎預測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"touch typing","meaning":"盲打","examples":[{"en":"Touch typing still is not taught in most schools.","zh":"大多數學校仍然沒有教授盲打。"},{"en":"Touch typing is typing without looking at the keyboard.","zh":"盲打是不看鍵盤打字。"},{"en":"Touch typing can help people type quickly and accurately.","zh":"盲打可以幫助人快速而準確打字。"},{"en":"Some students use keyboards often but never learn touch typing.","zh":"有些學生經常使用鍵盤，但從未學過盲打。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a keyboard skill.","zh":"這個短語描述一種鍵盤技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"which is a shame","meaning":"這很可惜","examples":[{"en":"Touch typing is not taught in most schools, which is a shame.","zh":"大多數學校不教盲打，這很可惜。"},{"en":"“Which is a shame” means this is unfortunate or disappointing.","zh":"「Which is a shame」意思是這件事令人遺憾或失望。"},{"en":"Many children cannot type efficiently, which is a shame.","zh":"很多孩子不能有效率地打字，這很可惜。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when something could be better.","zh":"當某事本可以更好時，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses mild regret.","zh":"這個短語表達輕微遺憾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be necessary in the future","meaning":"將來有必要","examples":[{"en":"Touch typing may not be necessary in the future.","zh":"盲打將來可能不是必要的。"},{"en":"To be necessary in the future means to be needed later.","zh":"將來有必要意思是之後會需要。"},{"en":"Handwriting may still be necessary in the future for young children.","zh":"對年幼孩子來說，手寫將來可能仍有必要。"},{"en":"Touch typing may become less necessary if voice technology improves.","zh":"如果語音技術改善，盲打將來可能較不必要。"},{"en":"This phrase discusses future need.","zh":"這個短語討論未來需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"digital devices","meaning":"數碼裝置","examples":[{"en":"People may write by hand on digital devices.","zh":"人們可能會在數碼裝置上手寫。"},{"en":"Digital devices are electronic tools such as tablets, laptops, phones, and computers.","zh":"數碼裝置是平板電腦、手提電腦、手機和電腦等電子工具。"},{"en":"Children use digital devices for typing, drawing, and handwriting practice.","zh":"孩子使用數碼裝置來打字、繪畫和練習手寫。"},{"en":"Digital devices can support learning, but they may also reduce handwriting practice.","zh":"數碼裝置可以支援學習，但也可能減少手寫練習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes modern electronic tools.","zh":"這個短語描述現代電子工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"understand the value of","meaning":"理解……的價值","examples":[{"en":"Teachers understand the value of handwriting.","zh":"老師理解手寫的價值。"},{"en":"To understand the value of something means to know why it is useful or important.","zh":"理解某事的價值，意思是知道它為何有用或重要。"},{"en":"Teachers understand the value of handwriting for memory and concentration.","zh":"老師理解手寫對記憶和專注力的價值。"},{"en":"Parents may not always understand the value of slow handwriting practice.","zh":"家長未必總是理解慢速手寫練習的價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognising importance.","zh":"這個短語描述認識重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a basic life skill","meaning":"基本生活技能","examples":[{"en":"Handwriting is a basic life skill.","zh":"手寫是一項基本生活技能。"},{"en":"A basic life skill is a practical ability needed in everyday life.","zh":"基本生活技能是日常生活所需的實用能力。"},{"en":"Reading, writing, and basic money management are basic life skills.","zh":"閱讀、書寫和基本理財都是基本生活技能。"},{"en":"Handwriting remains a basic life skill even when people use computers.","zh":"即使人們使用電腦，手寫仍是一項基本生活技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fundamental practical ability.","zh":"這個短語描述根本的實用能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the fact is that","meaning":"事實是","examples":[{"en":"The fact is that people are writing by hand less and less.","zh":"事實是人們手寫越來越少。"},{"en":"“The fact is that” introduces a real situation, often one that must be accepted.","zh":"「The fact is that」用來引出真實情況，通常是必須接受的情況。"},{"en":"The fact is that children now use keyboards more often.","zh":"事實是孩子現在更常使用鍵盤。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to emphasise reality.","zh":"人們使用這個短語來強調現實。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a clear factual point.","zh":"這個短語引出清楚事實。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"less and less","meaning":"越來越少","examples":[{"en":"People are writing by hand less and less.","zh":"人們手寫越來越少。"},{"en":"Less and less means decreasing over time.","zh":"越來越少意思是隨時間逐漸減少。"},{"en":"Students are using pens less and less in some classrooms.","zh":"在一些課室中，學生使用筆越來越少。"},{"en":"As people type more, they may practise handwriting less and less.","zh":"隨着人們打字更多，他們可能越來越少練習手寫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gradual decrease.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸減少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rely on digital devices","meaning":"依賴數碼裝置","examples":[{"en":"People are relying on digital devices more and more.","zh":"人們越來越依賴數碼裝置。"},{"en":"To rely on digital devices means to depend on electronic tools for tasks.","zh":"依賴數碼裝置意思是依靠電子工具完成任務。"},{"en":"Students rely on digital devices for notes, spelling, and research.","zh":"學生依賴數碼裝置記筆記、拼寫和研究。"},{"en":"Relying on digital devices can make handwriting less common.","zh":"依賴數碼裝置可以令手寫變得較少見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dependence on technology.","zh":"這個短語描述對科技的依靠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cause some problems","meaning":"造成一些問題","examples":[{"en":"Relying on digital devices does cause some problems.","zh":"依賴數碼裝置確實會造成一些問題。"},{"en":"To cause some problems means to create difficulties or negative effects.","zh":"造成一些問題意思是產生困難或負面影響。"},{"en":"Too much typing can cause some problems with spelling practice.","zh":"過多打字可能對拼寫練習造成一些問題。"},{"en":"Digital devices help learning, but they may also cause some problems.","zh":"數碼裝置幫助學習，但也可能造成一些問題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces disadvantages.","zh":"這個短語引出缺點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"note taking","meaning":"記筆記","examples":[{"en":"The man mentions note taking as one possible issue.","zh":"那位男士提到記筆記是其中一個可能問題。"},{"en":"Note taking is writing down important information while listening or reading.","zh":"記筆記是在聆聽或閱讀時寫下重要資料。"},{"en":"Students use note taking during lectures and discussions.","zh":"學生在講座和討論期間會記筆記。"},{"en":"Digital apps can support note taking, but handwriting may help memory.","zh":"數碼應用程式可以支援記筆記，但手寫可能幫助記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recording key points.","zh":"這個短語描述記錄重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"apps for that","meaning":"用來做那件事的應用程式","examples":[{"en":"There are lots of apps for note taking.","zh":"有很多用來記筆記的應用程式。"},{"en":"Apps for that means applications designed for that particular task.","zh":"用來做那件事的應用程式，意思是為該特定任務設計的應用程式。"},{"en":"There are apps for handwriting practice and spelling correction.","zh":"有用來練習手寫和改正拼寫的應用程式。"},{"en":"If you need to take detailed notes, there are apps for that.","zh":"如果你需要做詳細筆記，也有用來做那件事的應用程式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to digital tools for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語指為某目的而設的數碼工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"historical documents","meaning":"歷史文件","examples":[{"en":"Some apps can help people read historical documents.","zh":"有些應用程式可以幫助人閱讀歷史文件。"},{"en":"Historical documents are old written records from the past.","zh":"歷史文件是來自過去的舊書面記錄。"},{"en":"Historical documents may include letters, diaries, laws, and official papers.","zh":"歷史文件可能包括信件、日記、法律和官方文件。"},{"en":"Reading historical documents can be difficult if the handwriting is old-fashioned.","zh":"如果字跡很舊式，閱讀歷史文件可能很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes written sources from history.","zh":"這個短語描述來自歷史的書面資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"apparently","meaning":"顯然；看來","examples":[{"en":"Apparently, there are apps for reading historical documents.","zh":"看來有用來閱讀歷史文件的應用程式。"},{"en":"Apparently means it seems true based on what someone has heard or read.","zh":"「Apparently」意思是根據聽到或讀到的資料，某事看來是真的。"},{"en":"Apparently, some apps can recognise old handwriting.","zh":"看來有些應用程式可以辨認舊字跡。"},{"en":"People use “apparently” when they are not fully certain.","zh":"當人們不是完全肯定時，會使用「apparently」。"},{"en":"This word introduces reported information.","zh":"這個詞引出轉述資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be shocked by","meaning":"對……感到震驚","examples":[{"en":"The woman’s mother is shocked by her awful spelling.","zh":"那位女士的母親對她糟糕的拼寫感到震驚。"},{"en":"To be shocked by something means to feel very surprised or upset by it.","zh":"對某事感到震驚，意思是因它而非常驚訝或不安。"},{"en":"The teacher was shocked by the student’s poor punctuation.","zh":"老師對學生糟糕的標點感到震驚。"},{"en":"Parents may be shocked by how little children write by hand.","zh":"家長可能對孩子手寫如此少感到震驚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"awful spelling","meaning":"糟糕的拼寫","examples":[{"en":"The woman says her spelling is awful.","zh":"那位女士說她的拼寫很糟糕。"},{"en":"Awful spelling means very poor spelling with many mistakes.","zh":"糟糕的拼寫意思是拼寫很差，有很多錯誤。"},{"en":"She blamed her awful spelling on lack of practice.","zh":"她把糟糕的拼寫歸因於缺乏練習。"},{"en":"Digital spellcheckers may hide awful spelling until someone writes by hand.","zh":"數碼拼寫檢查可能會掩蓋糟糕拼寫，直到某人手寫。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly criticises spelling ability.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評拼寫能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"punctuation","meaning":"標點","examples":[{"en":"The woman’s punctuation is really inconsistent.","zh":"那位女士的標點真的不一致。"},{"en":"Punctuation is the use of marks such as full stops, commas, and question marks.","zh":"標點是使用句號、逗號和問號等符號。"},{"en":"Good punctuation helps readers understand sentences.","zh":"良好標點幫助讀者理解句子。"},{"en":"Poor punctuation can make writing confusing.","zh":"糟糕標點可以令文字令人困惑。"},{"en":"This word describes the marks used to organise writing.","zh":"這個詞描述用來組織文字的符號。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"inconsistent","meaning":"不一致","examples":[{"en":"Her punctuation is really inconsistent.","zh":"她的標點真的不一致。"},{"en":"Inconsistent means not staying the same or not following one clear pattern.","zh":"不一致意思是沒有保持相同，或沒有遵循清楚模式。"},{"en":"Her spelling is sometimes correct and sometimes wrong, so it is inconsistent.","zh":"她的拼寫有時正確有時錯誤，所以不一致。"},{"en":"Inconsistent punctuation can make an essay look careless.","zh":"不一致的標點可以令文章看起來粗心。"},{"en":"This word describes lack of regularity.","zh":"這個詞描述缺乏規律性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"put that down to","meaning":"把……歸因於","examples":[{"en":"The woman puts her poor spelling down to lack of practice.","zh":"那位女士把糟糕拼寫歸因於缺乏練習。"},{"en":"To put something down to a cause means to explain it as being caused by that thing.","zh":"把某事歸因於某原因，意思是解釋它是由該原因造成的。"},{"en":"He put his slow handwriting down to lack of practice.","zh":"他把自己手寫慢歸因於缺乏練習。"},{"en":"Teachers may put poor spelling down to too much reliance on digital devices.","zh":"老師可能把糟糕拼寫歸因於過度依賴數碼裝置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving a reason for something.","zh":"這個短語描述為某事提供原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lack of practice","meaning":"缺乏練習","examples":[{"en":"Poor spelling may be due to lack of practice.","zh":"糟糕拼寫可能是因缺乏練習。"},{"en":"Lack of practice means not having enough repeated experience doing something.","zh":"缺乏練習意思是沒有足夠重複經驗去做某事。"},{"en":"Lack of practice can make handwriting slower and less fluent.","zh":"缺乏練習可以令手寫更慢、更不流暢。"},{"en":"If people type all the time, lack of handwriting practice may become a problem.","zh":"如果人們一直打字，缺乏手寫練習可能變成問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes insufficient practice.","zh":"這個短語描述練習不足。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"I expect so","meaning":"我想是這樣","examples":[{"en":"The man says, “I expect so,” when he agrees with the explanation.","zh":"那位男士同意解釋時說：「我想是這樣。」"},{"en":"“I expect so” means I think that is probably true.","zh":"「I expect so」意思是我認為那大概是真的。"},{"en":"Lack of practice affects spelling? I expect so.","zh":"缺乏練習會影響拼寫？我想是這樣。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to agree in a careful way.","zh":"人們使用這個短語以謹慎方式同意。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses probable agreement.","zh":"這個短語表達大概同意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Personally","meaning":"就我個人而言","examples":[{"en":"Personally, the man misses writing by hand.","zh":"就那位男士個人而言，他懷念手寫。"},{"en":"Personally means speaking from my own point of view.","zh":"就我個人而言，意思是從我自己的角度來說。"},{"en":"Personally, I think handwriting still matters.","zh":"就我個人而言，我認為手寫仍然重要。"},{"en":"People use “personally” before giving their own opinion.","zh":"人們在表達個人意見前會使用「personally」。"},{"en":"This word signals a personal view.","zh":"這個詞表示個人看法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"miss writing by hand","meaning":"懷念手寫","examples":[{"en":"The man misses writing by hand.","zh":"那位男士懷念手寫。"},{"en":"To miss writing by hand means to feel sad or nostalgic because you do it less often now.","zh":"懷念手寫意思是因現在較少手寫而感到懷舊或惋惜。"},{"en":"She misses writing by hand because typing feels less personal.","zh":"她懷念手寫，因為打字感覺較沒有個人特色。"},{"en":"People may miss writing by hand when they remember letters and diaries.","zh":"人們想起信件和日記時可能會懷念手寫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional longing for handwriting.","zh":"這個短語描述對手寫的情感懷念。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"beautiful handwriting","meaning":"漂亮的字跡","examples":[{"en":"The man’s grandparents had beautiful handwriting.","zh":"那位男士的祖父母有漂亮的字跡。"},{"en":"Beautiful handwriting is writing that looks attractive, neat, and personal.","zh":"漂亮的字跡是看起來吸引、工整並有個人特色的書寫。"},{"en":"Beautiful handwriting can make a letter feel special.","zh":"漂亮的字跡可以令一封信感覺特別。"},{"en":"Some people admire old diaries because of the beautiful handwriting.","zh":"有些人因漂亮的字跡而欣賞舊日記。"},{"en":"This phrase praises the appearance of writing.","zh":"這個短語稱讚書寫外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"so individual","meaning":"很有個人特色","examples":[{"en":"Their handwriting was so individual.","zh":"他們的字跡很有個人特色。"},{"en":"So individual means very personal, unique, and different from others.","zh":"很有個人特色意思是非常個人化、獨特並與別人不同。"},{"en":"Her handwriting was so individual that everyone recognised it.","zh":"她的字跡很有個人特色，所以每個人都認得出。"},{"en":"Digital text is often less individual than handwriting.","zh":"數碼文字通常比手寫較少個人特色。"},{"en":"This phrase praises personal uniqueness.","zh":"這個短語稱讚個人獨特性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be able to identify","meaning":"能夠辨認出","examples":[{"en":"Nobody would be able to identify the man’s handwriting now.","zh":"現在沒有人能夠辨認出那位男士的字跡。"},{"en":"To be able to identify something means to recognise it.","zh":"能夠辨認出某物，意思是認出它。"},{"en":"I can identify my grandmother’s handwriting immediately.","zh":"我能立即辨認出祖母的字跡。"},{"en":"If everyone types, it becomes harder to identify a person’s writing style.","zh":"如果每個人都打字，就更難辨認出一個人的書寫風格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the ability to recognise.","zh":"這個短語描述認出的能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"It’s a shame","meaning":"真可惜","examples":[{"en":"The man says it is a shame that handwriting has become less personal.","zh":"那位男士說手寫變得較少個人特色，真可惜。"},{"en":"“It’s a shame” means it is disappointing or regrettable.","zh":"「It’s a shame」意思是令人失望或遺憾。"},{"en":"It’s a shame that people write fewer letters by hand now.","zh":"現在人們較少手寫信，真可惜。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they feel something valuable is being lost.","zh":"當人們覺得有價值的東西正在消失時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses regret.","zh":"這個短語表達遺憾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"I feel the same way","meaning":"我也有同感","examples":[{"en":"The woman feels the same way about handwriting.","zh":"那位女士對手寫也有同感。"},{"en":"“I feel the same way” means I have the same opinion or feeling.","zh":"「I feel the same way」意思是我有同樣的看法或感受。"},{"en":"You miss handwriting? I feel the same way.","zh":"你懷念手寫？我也有同感。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to show agreement and shared emotion.","zh":"人們使用這個短語表示同意和共同感受。"},{"en":"This phrase is warm and conversational.","zh":"這個短語溫暖而口語化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"write a diary by hand","meaning":"手寫日記","examples":[{"en":"The woman used to write a diary by hand.","zh":"那位女士以前會手寫日記。"},{"en":"To write a diary by hand means to keep a personal record using handwriting.","zh":"手寫日記意思是用手寫方式記錄個人生活。"},{"en":"She wrote a diary by hand every night when she was younger.","zh":"她年輕時每晚都手寫日記。"},{"en":"Writing a diary by hand can feel more personal than typing.","zh":"手寫日記可以比打字更有個人感覺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes handwritten personal journaling.","zh":"這個短語描述手寫個人日誌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"do that digitally","meaning":"以數碼方式做那件事","examples":[{"en":"The woman now writes her diary digitally.","zh":"那位女士現在以數碼方式寫日記。"},{"en":"To do that digitally means to do the same task using a digital device or software.","zh":"以數碼方式做那件事，意思是用數碼裝置或軟件完成同一任務。"},{"en":"She used to write by hand, but now she does that digitally.","zh":"她以前手寫，但現在以數碼方式做那件事。"},{"en":"Doing that digitally may be easier, but it can feel less personal.","zh":"以數碼方式做那件事可能較容易，但感覺較少個人特色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes replacing a physical activity with a digital one.","zh":"這個短語描述用數碼方式取代實體活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"less effort to","meaning":"較省力去……","examples":[{"en":"It seems less effort to write a diary digitally.","zh":"以數碼方式寫日記似乎較省力。"},{"en":"Less effort to do something means it takes less work, time, or energy.","zh":"較省力去做某事，意思是需要較少工作、時間或精力。"},{"en":"It is less effort to type notes than to write them by hand.","zh":"打字記筆記比手寫較省力。"},{"en":"Digital writing may seem less effort, but handwriting has other benefits.","zh":"數碼書寫可能較省力，但手寫有其他好處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something being easier to do.","zh":"這個短語描述某事較容易做。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"benefits for children of","meaning":"對孩子的好處","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about benefits for children of learning to write.","zh":"問題問學習書寫對孩子的好處。"},{"en":"Benefits for children of something are the advantages children gain from it.","zh":"某事對孩子的好處，是孩子從中獲得的優點。"},{"en":"Benefits for children of handwriting include memory, concentration, and motor skills.","zh":"手寫對孩子的好處包括記憶、專注力和動作能力。"},{"en":"Teachers should understand the benefits for children of writing by hand.","zh":"老師應理解手寫對孩子的好處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes positive effects on children.","zh":"這個短語描述對孩子的正面影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"find surprising","meaning":"覺得令人驚訝","examples":[{"en":"The students discuss which benefits they found surprising.","zh":"學生討論哪些好處令他們覺得令人驚訝。"},{"en":"To find something surprising means to think it is unexpected.","zh":"覺得某事令人驚訝，意思是認為它出乎意料。"},{"en":"The students found the link between handwriting and concentration surprising.","zh":"學生覺得手寫與專注力之間的關聯令人驚訝。"},{"en":"People may find spatial awareness surprising as a handwriting benefit.","zh":"人們可能覺得空間感作為手寫好處令人驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reaction of surprise.","zh":"這個短語描述驚訝反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"improved fine motor skills","meaning":"精細動作能力提升","examples":[{"en":"Improved fine motor skills are often linked with handwriting.","zh":"精細動作能力提升常與手寫有關。"},{"en":"Improved fine motor skills mean better control of small hand and finger movements.","zh":"精細動作能力提升意思是手和手指的小動作控制更好。"},{"en":"Handwriting practice can lead to improved fine motor skills.","zh":"手寫練習可以帶來精細動作能力提升。"},{"en":"Improved fine motor skills help children hold pencils and form letters.","zh":"精細動作能力提升幫助孩子握筆和形成字母。"},{"en":"This phrase describes better precise movement ability.","zh":"這個短語描述精準動作能力改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"improved memory","meaning":"記憶力提升","examples":[{"en":"Improved memory can be a benefit of learning to write.","zh":"記憶力提升可以是學習書寫的好處。"},{"en":"Improved memory means a better ability to remember information.","zh":"記憶力提升意思是記住資料的能力更好。"},{"en":"Writing letters by hand may lead to improved memory of their shapes.","zh":"手寫字母可能帶來對字母形狀的記憶力提升。"},{"en":"Improved memory helps children recognise letters more quickly.","zh":"記憶力提升幫助孩子更快認出字母。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stronger remembering ability.","zh":"這個短語描述更強的記憶能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"improved concentration","meaning":"專注力提升","examples":[{"en":"Improved concentration may come from handwriting practice.","zh":"專注力提升可能來自手寫練習。"},{"en":"Improved concentration means a better ability to focus attention.","zh":"專注力提升意思是集中注意力的能力更好。"},{"en":"Sitting still and forming letters can lead to improved concentration.","zh":"坐定並形成字母可以帶來專注力提升。"},{"en":"Improved concentration helps children complete classroom tasks.","zh":"專注力提升幫助孩子完成課堂任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes better attention control.","zh":"這個短語描述更好的注意力控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"improved imagination","meaning":"想像力提升","examples":[{"en":"Improved imagination may be linked to writing by hand.","zh":"想像力提升可能與手寫有關。"},{"en":"Improved imagination means a stronger ability to create ideas and mental images.","zh":"想像力提升意思是創造想法和腦海畫面的能力更強。"},{"en":"Children who write stories by hand may show improved imagination.","zh":"手寫故事的孩子可能展現想像力提升。"},{"en":"Improved imagination can help children produce richer writing.","zh":"想像力提升可以幫助孩子寫出更豐富的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth in creativity.","zh":"這個短語描述創造力成長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"improved spatial awareness","meaning":"空間感提升","examples":[{"en":"Improved spatial awareness can help children write clearly.","zh":"空間感提升可以幫助孩子寫得清楚。"},{"en":"Improved spatial awareness means better understanding of space, position, and distance.","zh":"空間感提升意思是對空間、位置和距離有更好理解。"},{"en":"Handwriting practice may lead to improved spatial awareness.","zh":"手寫練習可能帶來空間感提升。"},{"en":"Improved spatial awareness helps children space letters and words correctly.","zh":"空間感提升幫助孩子正確安排字母和單字間距。"},{"en":"This phrase describes better control of layout and position.","zh":"這個短語描述對版面和位置的更好控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be easiest to correct","meaning":"最容易糾正","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which problems are easiest to correct.","zh":"問題問哪些問題最容易糾正。"},{"en":"To be easiest to correct means to be the simplest to fix or improve.","zh":"最容易糾正意思是最簡單修正或改善。"},{"en":"Pressing too hard may be easiest to correct with a light-up pen.","zh":"用力過大可能最容易用發光筆糾正。"},{"en":"Some handwriting problems are easier to correct than others.","zh":"有些手寫問題比其他問題更容易糾正。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how difficult problems are to fix.","zh":"這個短語比較問題修正的難度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"not spacing letters correctly","meaning":"未能正確安排字母間距","examples":[{"en":"Some children have problems with not spacing letters correctly.","zh":"有些孩子有未能正確安排字母間距的問題。"},{"en":"Not spacing letters correctly means failing to leave suitable gaps between letters.","zh":"未能正確安排字母間距意思是沒有在字母之間留下合適空位。"},{"en":"Not spacing letters correctly can make words hard to read.","zh":"未能正確安排字母間距可以令單字難以閱讀。"},{"en":"Grid paper helps children who are not spacing letters correctly.","zh":"方格紙幫助未能正確安排字母間距的孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a handwriting layout problem.","zh":"這個短語描述手寫版面問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"applying too much pressure when writing","meaning":"書寫時用力過大","examples":[{"en":"Some children have difficulty with applying too much pressure when writing.","zh":"有些孩子在書寫時用力過大方面有困難。"},{"en":"Applying too much pressure when writing means pressing the pen or pencil too hard.","zh":"書寫時用力過大意思是把筆或鉛筆壓得太重。"},{"en":"Applying too much pressure can make writing tiring and messy.","zh":"書寫時用力過大可以令書寫很累又凌亂。"},{"en":"A special pen can help children notice when they are applying too much pressure.","zh":"特別的筆可以幫助孩子注意自己何時用力過大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes excessive force during handwriting.","zh":"這個短語描述手寫時力量過大。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"confusing letter shapes","meaning":"混淆字母形狀","examples":[{"en":"Children may have problems with confusing letter shapes.","zh":"孩子可能有混淆字母形狀的問題。"},{"en":"Confusing letter shapes means mixing up letters that look similar.","zh":"混淆字母形狀意思是把看起來相似的字母弄混。"},{"en":"Some children confuse letter shapes such as p and q.","zh":"有些孩子會混淆 p 和 q 等字母形狀。"},{"en":"Games can help children stop confusing letter shapes.","zh":"遊戲可以幫助孩子停止混淆字母形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulty recognising letter forms.","zh":"這個短語描述辨認字母形狀的困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"using laptops to teach writing","meaning":"用手提電腦教寫作","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about using laptops to teach writing.","zh":"問題問關於用手提電腦教寫作。"},{"en":"Using laptops to teach writing means using computers as tools for writing instruction.","zh":"用手提電腦教寫作意思是使用電腦作為寫作教學工具。"},{"en":"Using laptops to teach writing may help children who struggle with handwriting.","zh":"用手提電腦教寫作可能幫助在手寫方面吃力的孩子。"},{"en":"Teachers should consider when using laptops is helpful and when handwriting is better.","zh":"老師應考慮何時使用手提電腦有幫助，何時手寫更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes digital support for writing lessons.","zh":"這個短語描述寫作課中的數碼支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"react more positively","meaning":"反應較正面","examples":[{"en":"Children may react more positively if they make a mistake.","zh":"如果孩子犯錯，他們可能反應較正面。"},{"en":"To react more positively means to respond with less fear, frustration, or discouragement.","zh":"反應較正面意思是以較少恐懼、沮喪或灰心的方式回應。"},{"en":"Children may react more positively on a keyboard because mistakes are easy to correct.","zh":"孩子在鍵盤上可能反應較正面，因為錯誤容易修正。"},{"en":"A positive reaction can make children more willing to try again.","zh":"正面反應可以令孩子更願意再試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a better emotional response.","zh":"這個短語描述較好的情緒回應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"make a mistake","meaning":"犯錯","examples":[{"en":"Children may feel less frustrated if they make a mistake on a keyboard.","zh":"如果孩子在鍵盤上犯錯，他們可能較少感到沮喪。"},{"en":"To make a mistake means to do something incorrectly.","zh":"犯錯意思是做錯某事。"},{"en":"Children often make mistakes when learning to write.","zh":"孩子學習書寫時常會犯錯。"},{"en":"It is easier to correct a mistake on a computer than on paper.","zh":"在電腦上改正錯誤比在紙上容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doing something wrong.","zh":"這個短語描述做錯事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"relatively quickly","meaning":"相對較快地","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests children may become fluent relatively quickly.","zh":"這個選項表示孩子可能相對較快地變得流暢。"},{"en":"Relatively quickly means quite quickly compared with another situation.","zh":"相對較快地意思是與另一情況相比頗快。"},{"en":"Some children learn keyboard skills relatively quickly.","zh":"有些孩子相對較快地學會鍵盤技能。"},{"en":"Writing fluency may not develop relatively quickly just because a child uses a laptop.","zh":"寫作流暢度不一定只因使用手提電腦而相對較快地發展。"},{"en":"This phrase compares speed.","zh":"這個短語比較速度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cursive or print writing","meaning":"草寫體或印刷體書寫","examples":[{"en":"The students discuss whether to teach cursive or print writing.","zh":"學生討論應教草寫體還是印刷體書寫。"},{"en":"Cursive or print writing refers to the choice between joined-up writing and separate-letter writing.","zh":"草寫體或印刷體書寫指在連筆書寫和分開字母書寫之間作選擇。"},{"en":"Teachers may choose print writing before cursive for younger children.","zh":"老師可能先為年幼孩子選擇印刷體書寫，再教草寫體。"},{"en":"The debate about cursive or print writing affects children with learning difficulties.","zh":"草寫體或印刷體書寫的討論會影響有學習困難的孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two handwriting styles.","zh":"這個短語描述兩種手寫風格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"disadvantage a certain group of children","meaning":"令某一類孩子處於不利位置","examples":[{"en":"Cursive writing may disadvantage a certain group of children.","zh":"草寫體書寫可能令某一類孩子處於不利位置。"},{"en":"To disadvantage a certain group of children means to make learning harder or less fair for that group.","zh":"令某一類孩子處於不利位置，意思是令該群體學習更困難或不公平。"},{"en":"Teaching cursive too early may disadvantage children with learning difficulties.","zh":"太早教草寫體可能令有學習困難的孩子處於不利位置。"},{"en":"Schools should avoid methods that disadvantage a certain group of children.","zh":"學校應避免令某一類孩子處於不利位置的方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating unfair difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述造成不公平困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Print writing may be associated with lower academic performance.","zh":"印刷體書寫可能與較低的學業表現有關。"},{"en":"To be associated with something means to be connected with it in some way.","zh":"與某事有關，意思是在某方面與它有連繫。"},{"en":"Poor handwriting may be associated with lower exam marks.","zh":"糟糕字跡可能與較低考試分數有關。"},{"en":"Being associated with something does not always prove direct cause.","zh":"與某事有關並不一定證明直接原因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a relationship between two things.","zh":"這個短語描述兩件事之間的關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lower academic performance","meaning":"較低的學業表現","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions lower academic performance.","zh":"這個選項提到較低的學業表現。"},{"en":"Lower academic performance means weaker results or achievement in school or university.","zh":"較低的學業表現意思是在學校或大學中的成績或成就較弱。"},{"en":"Poor handwriting may appear to affect academic performance if examiners cannot read answers.","zh":"如果考官看不懂答案，糟糕字跡可能看似影響學業表現。"},{"en":"Lower academic performance can be caused by many different factors.","zh":"較低的學業表現可以由很多不同因素造成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weaker educational results.","zh":"這個短語描述較弱的教育成果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a traditional approach to","meaning":"對……的傳統做法","examples":[{"en":"Some teachers may prefer a traditional approach to handwriting.","zh":"有些老師可能較喜歡對手寫的傳統做法。"},{"en":"A traditional approach to something is an older or long-established way of doing it.","zh":"對某事的傳統做法是較舊或長久建立的方法。"},{"en":"Teaching cursive first was once a traditional approach to handwriting.","zh":"先教草寫體曾是對手寫的傳統做法。"},{"en":"A traditional approach may not suit every child today.","zh":"傳統做法今天未必適合每個孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an established method.","zh":"這個短語描述既有方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"impact on exam performance","meaning":"對考試表現的影響","examples":[{"en":"The students discuss the impact of poor handwriting on exam performance.","zh":"學生討論糟糕字跡對考試表現的影響。"},{"en":"Impact on exam performance means the effect something has on test results.","zh":"對考試表現的影響意思是某事對測驗結果造成的效果。"},{"en":"Illegible writing can have a negative impact on exam performance.","zh":"難以辨認的字跡可以對考試表現造成負面影響。"},{"en":"Teaching children to write legibly may reduce the impact on exam performance.","zh":"教孩子寫得清楚易讀可能減少對考試表現的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how something affects exams.","zh":"這個短語描述某事如何影響考試。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"there is evidence to suggest","meaning":"有證據顯示","examples":[{"en":"There is evidence to suggest grades are affected by poor handwriting.","zh":"有證據顯示成績會受糟糕字跡影響。"},{"en":"“There is evidence to suggest” means research or information supports a possible conclusion.","zh":"「There is evidence to suggest」意思是研究或資料支持某個可能結論。"},{"en":"There is evidence to suggest handwriting helps memory.","zh":"有證據顯示手寫有助記憶。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when the evidence points toward an idea.","zh":"當證據指向某個想法時，作者會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds careful and academic.","zh":"這個短語聽起來謹慎而具學術性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"grades are affected by","meaning":"成績受到……影響","examples":[{"en":"Grades may be affected by poor handwriting.","zh":"成績可能受到糟糕字跡影響。"},{"en":"Grades are affected by something when that thing influences the marks students receive.","zh":"成績受到某事影響，意思是該事影響學生得到的分數。"},{"en":"Grades may be affected by spelling, punctuation, and handwriting.","zh":"成績可能受到拼寫、標點和字跡影響。"},{"en":"If examiners cannot read answers, grades are affected by legibility.","zh":"如果考官看不懂答案，成績會受到可讀性影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a factor influencing academic results.","zh":"這個短語描述影響學業結果的因素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"neat handwriting","meaning":"工整的字跡","examples":[{"en":"Neat handwriting may help examiners read a script more easily.","zh":"工整的字跡可能幫助考官更容易看懂答卷。"},{"en":"Neat handwriting is tidy, clear, and well-organised writing.","zh":"工整的字跡是整齊、清楚而有條理的書寫。"},{"en":"Neat handwriting can make an exam answer easier to understand.","zh":"工整的字跡可以令考試答案更容易理解。"},{"en":"Neat handwriting does not replace knowledge, but it helps communication.","zh":"工整的字跡不能取代知識，但有助溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visually tidy writing.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺上整齊的字跡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"used to be","meaning":"過去曾經","examples":[{"en":"Neat handwriting may be less important now than it used to be.","zh":"工整字跡現在可能不如過去曾經那麼重要。"},{"en":"Used to be means was true in the past but may not be true now.","zh":"過去曾經意思是以前是真的，但現在未必如此。"},{"en":"Cursive writing used to be considered very stylish.","zh":"草寫體過去曾經被認為很有風格。"},{"en":"Handwritten letters used to be much more common.","zh":"手寫信過去曾經常見得多。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the past with the present.","zh":"這個短語比較過去和現在。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"produce shorter answers","meaning":"寫出較短的答案","examples":[{"en":"Poor handwriting may cause candidates to produce shorter answers.","zh":"糟糕字跡可能令考生寫出較短的答案。"},{"en":"To produce shorter answers means to write answers with fewer words or less detail.","zh":"寫出較短的答案意思是用較少字數或較少細節回答。"},{"en":"Students who write slowly may produce shorter answers in exams.","zh":"寫得慢的學生可能在考試中寫出較短的答案。"},{"en":"Poor handwriting may lead candidates to produce shorter answers to save time.","zh":"糟糕字跡可能令考生為了省時間而寫出較短答案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reduced written output.","zh":"這個短語描述書面產出減少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make a prediction about","meaning":"對……作出預測","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what prediction the man makes about handwriting.","zh":"問題問那位男士對手寫作出甚麼預測。"},{"en":"To make a prediction about something means to say what you think will happen in the future.","zh":"對某事作出預測，意思是說出你認為將來會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"The man makes a prediction about whether children will keep learning handwriting.","zh":"那位男士對孩子是否會繼續學手寫作出預測。"},{"en":"Predictions about education may change as technology develops.","zh":"隨着科技發展，對教育的預測可能會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forecasting a future situation.","zh":"這個短語描述預測未來情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"continue to learn to","meaning":"繼續學習去……","examples":[{"en":"The man believes children will continue to learn to write by hand.","zh":"那位男士相信孩子會繼續學習手寫。"},{"en":"To continue to learn to do something means to keep being taught or practising it.","zh":"繼續學習去做某事，意思是繼續被教授或練習它。"},{"en":"Children will probably continue to learn to write by hand in primary school.","zh":"孩子很可能會在小學繼續學習手寫。"},{"en":"Even with tablets, students may continue to learn handwriting.","zh":"即使有平板電腦，學生仍可能繼續學習手寫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing learning.","zh":"這個短語描述持續學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"dislike handwriting on digital devices","meaning":"不喜歡在數碼裝置上手寫","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests people may dislike handwriting on digital devices.","zh":"這個選項表示人們可能不喜歡在數碼裝置上手寫。"},{"en":"To dislike handwriting on digital devices means to not enjoy writing by hand on screens or tablets.","zh":"不喜歡在數碼裝置上手寫，意思是不享受在屏幕或平板上用手書寫。"},{"en":"Some people dislike handwriting on digital devices because it feels unnatural.","zh":"有些人不喜歡在數碼裝置上手寫，因為感覺不自然。"},{"en":"Others like handwriting on digital devices because it combines writing and technology.","zh":"其他人喜歡在數碼裝置上手寫，因為它結合書寫和科技。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a negative feeling about digital handwriting.","zh":"這個短語描述對數碼手寫的負面感受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be concerned that","meaning":"擔心","examples":[{"en":"The woman is concerned that relying on digital devices has caused problems.","zh":"那位女士擔心依賴數碼裝置已造成問題。"},{"en":"To be concerned that something is true means to be worried it may be true.","zh":"擔心某事是真的，意思是憂慮它可能是真的。"},{"en":"Teachers are concerned that children write by hand less and less.","zh":"老師擔心孩子手寫越來越少。"},{"en":"Parents may be concerned that spelling has become weaker.","zh":"家長可能擔心拼寫能力變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses worry about a possible problem.","zh":"這個短語表達對可能問題的憂慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make it difficult for someone to","meaning":"令某人難以……","examples":[{"en":"Digital devices have made it difficult for her to spell and punctuate.","zh":"數碼裝置令她難以拼寫和使用標點。"},{"en":"To make it difficult for someone to do something means to make that action harder for them.","zh":"令某人難以做某事，意思是令該行動對他們來說更困難。"},{"en":"Lack of practice made it difficult for her to write neatly.","zh":"缺乏練習令她難以寫得工整。"},{"en":"Relying on spellcheckers may make it difficult for students to spell independently.","zh":"依賴拼寫檢查可能令學生難以獨立拼寫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述造成困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"take detailed notes","meaning":"做詳細筆記","examples":[{"en":"Some people use apps to take detailed notes.","zh":"有些人使用應用程式做詳細筆記。"},{"en":"To take detailed notes means to write down information carefully and fully.","zh":"做詳細筆記意思是仔細而完整地寫下資料。"},{"en":"Students take detailed notes during lectures to prepare for assignments.","zh":"學生在講座期間做詳細筆記，以準備作業。"},{"en":"Apps can help people take detailed notes with images and recordings.","zh":"應用程式可以幫助人用圖片和錄音做詳細筆記。"},{"en":"This phrase describes thorough note recording.","zh":"這個短語描述詳細記錄筆記。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"spell and punctuate","meaning":"拼寫和使用標點","examples":[{"en":"The woman finds it harder to spell and punctuate accurately.","zh":"那位女士覺得更難準確拼寫和使用標點。"},{"en":"To spell and punctuate means to write words correctly and use punctuation marks correctly.","zh":"拼寫和使用標點意思是正確寫出單字並正確使用標點符號。"},{"en":"Children need practice to spell and punctuate well.","zh":"孩子需要練習才能良好拼寫和使用標點。"},{"en":"Digital tools may correct spelling, but students still need to spell and punctuate independently.","zh":"數碼工具可能會改正拼寫，但學生仍需要獨立拼寫和使用標點。"},{"en":"This phrase combines two writing accuracy skills.","zh":"這個短語結合兩項寫作準確技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"feel about","meaning":"對……的感受","examples":[{"en":"The question asks how the students feel about their own handwriting.","zh":"問題問學生對自己字跡的感受。"},{"en":"To feel about something means to have an opinion or emotion about it.","zh":"對某事的感受，意思是對它有看法或情緒。"},{"en":"How do you feel about writing by hand now?","zh":"你現在對手寫有甚麼感受？"},{"en":"Students may feel differently about their own handwriting after using keyboards for years.","zh":"使用鍵盤多年後，學生對自己的字跡可能有不同感受。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about personal attitude.","zh":"這個短語詢問個人態度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"own handwriting","meaning":"自己的字跡","examples":[{"en":"The students talk about their own handwriting.","zh":"學生談論自己的字跡。"},{"en":"Own handwriting means a person’s personal way of writing by hand.","zh":"自己的字跡是指一個人用手書寫的個人方式。"},{"en":"My own handwriting has become less neat because I type so often.","zh":"因為我經常打字，自己的字跡變得沒那麼工整。"},{"en":"People can sometimes recognise a friend’s own handwriting.","zh":"人們有時可以認出朋友自己的字跡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone’s personal written style.","zh":"這個短語描述某人的個人書寫風格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"unable to write quickly","meaning":"未能快速書寫","examples":[{"en":"The option describes people who are unable to write quickly.","zh":"這個選項描述未能快速書寫的人。"},{"en":"Unable to write quickly means not able to produce handwriting at a fast speed.","zh":"未能快速書寫意思是不能以快速度手寫。"},{"en":"Some children with handwriting difficulties are unable to write quickly in exams.","zh":"有手寫困難的孩子在考試中可能未能快速書寫。"},{"en":"Being unable to write quickly may lead to shorter answers.","zh":"未能快速書寫可能導致答案較短。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a limitation in writing speed.","zh":"這個短語描述書寫速度上的限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"embarrassed by comments","meaning":"因評論而尷尬","examples":[{"en":"Some people may feel embarrassed by comments about their handwriting.","zh":"有些人可能因關於自己字跡的評論而尷尬。"},{"en":"Embarrassed by comments means feeling awkward or ashamed because of what others say.","zh":"因評論而尷尬，意思是因別人的說話而感到不自在或羞愧。"},{"en":"A child may feel embarrassed by comments about messy handwriting.","zh":"孩子可能因關於凌亂字跡的評論而尷尬。"},{"en":"Teachers should give handwriting feedback carefully so students do not feel embarrassed.","zh":"老師應小心給予字跡意見，以免學生感到尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discomfort caused by remarks.","zh":"這個短語描述由評論造成的不舒服感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"regretful that","meaning":"對……感到遺憾","examples":[{"en":"The students feel regretful that they have lost the habit.","zh":"學生對自己失去這個習慣感到遺憾。"},{"en":"Regretful that something happened means feeling sorry or sad about it.","zh":"對某事感到遺憾，意思是因它發生而感到惋惜或難過。"},{"en":"The man is regretful that he no longer writes by hand often.","zh":"那位男士對自己不再經常手寫感到遺憾。"},{"en":"She felt regretful that her diary was now less personal.","zh":"她對自己的日記現在較少個人特色感到遺憾。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses sadness about a change.","zh":"這個短語表達對變化的惋惜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lose the habit","meaning":"失去……的習慣","examples":[{"en":"The students have lost the habit of writing by hand.","zh":"學生已失去手寫的習慣。"},{"en":"To lose the habit means to stop doing something regularly over time.","zh":"失去某習慣，意思是隨時間不再定期做某事。"},{"en":"Many people lose the habit of handwriting because they type every day.","zh":"很多人因每天打字而失去手寫的習慣。"},{"en":"Once students lose the habit, handwriting may feel slow and awkward.","zh":"一旦學生失去這個習慣，手寫可能感覺慢而不自然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated behaviour disappearing.","zh":"這個短語描述重複行為逐漸消失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"ielts/listening/Practice 4/task-4":[{"front":"environmental science lecture","meaning":"環境科學講座","examples":[{"en":"The students hear part of an environmental science lecture.","zh":"學生會聽到一段環境科學講座。"},{"en":"An environmental science lecture is an academic talk about the natural world and human effects on it.","zh":"環境科學講座是關於自然世界和人類對其影響的學術演講。"},{"en":"The environmental science lecture explained how wildlife and farming can affect each other.","zh":"那場環境科學講座解釋野生動物和農業如何互相影響。"},{"en":"Students should listen for examples, causes, and solutions in an environmental science lecture.","zh":"學生聽環境科學講座時，應留意例子、原因和解決方法。"},{"en":"A good environmental science lecture connects scientific facts with real community problems.","zh":"良好的環境科學講座會把科學事實與真實社區問題連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the impact of","meaning":"……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The lecture is about the impact of birds of prey on a farming community.","zh":"這場講座是關於猛禽對一個農業社群的影響。"},{"en":"The impact of something is the effect or influence it has on people, places, or situations.","zh":"某事的影響，是指它對人、地方或情況造成的效果或作用。"},{"en":"The report studied the impact of tourism on local wildlife.","zh":"報告研究旅遊業對本地野生動物的影響。"},{"en":"Understanding the impact of a problem helps people decide what action is needed.","zh":"了解一個問題的影響，可以幫助人們決定需要採取甚麼行動。"},{"en":"An impact can be positive, negative, or both at the same time.","zh":"影響可以是正面的、負面的，或兩者同時存在。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"birds of prey","meaning":"猛禽","examples":[{"en":"Birds of prey can have both positive and negative effects on farmers.","zh":"猛禽可以對農民產生正面和負面影響。"},{"en":"Birds of prey are birds that hunt and eat other animals.","zh":"猛禽是捕獵並吃其他動物的鳥類。"},{"en":"Eagles, hawks, and owls are common examples of birds of prey.","zh":"鷹、隼和貓頭鷹都是常見猛禽例子。"},{"en":"Birds of prey help control pests, but they may also attack farm animals.","zh":"猛禽有助控制害獸，但也可能攻擊農場動物。"},{"en":"Protecting birds of prey can be difficult when farmers feel threatened by them.","zh":"當農民感到受到威脅時，保護猛禽會變得困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"farming community","meaning":"農業社群","examples":[{"en":"The research focuses on a farming community in Africa.","zh":"這項研究集中於非洲一個農業社群。"},{"en":"A farming community is a group of people whose lives and work are closely connected with farming.","zh":"農業社群是一群生活和工作與農業密切相關的人。"},{"en":"The farming community depends on crops, animals, and seasonal rain.","zh":"該農業社群依靠作物、牲畜和季節性雨水生活。"},{"en":"Wildlife problems can affect a farming community both economically and socially.","zh":"野生動物問題可以在經濟和社會層面影響農業社群。"},{"en":"A farming community may have deep local knowledge about animals and land.","zh":"農業社群可能對動物和土地有深厚本地知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in Africa","meaning":"在非洲","examples":[{"en":"The farming community is located in Africa.","zh":"這個農業社群位於非洲。"},{"en":"“In Africa” means on or within the continent of Africa.","zh":"「在非洲」是指在非洲大陸上或其範圍內。"},{"en":"The researchers studied wildlife conflicts in Africa.","zh":"研究人員研究非洲的野生動物衝突。"},{"en":"Farming conditions in Africa vary greatly from region to region.","zh":"非洲各地的農業環境差異很大。"},{"en":"When discussing a place in Africa, it is important to name the specific country or region when possible.","zh":"討論非洲某地時，如有可能，應指出具體國家或地區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"different types of conflicts","meaning":"不同類型的衝突","examples":[{"en":"The lecture examines different types of conflicts between wildlife and humans.","zh":"講座探討野生動物與人類之間不同類型的衝突。"},{"en":"Different types of conflicts are different forms of disagreement, danger, or competition.","zh":"不同類型的衝突，是不同形式的分歧、危險或競爭。"},{"en":"Farmers may face different types of conflicts with elephants, birds, or predators.","zh":"農民可能與大象、鳥類或捕食者面對不同類型的衝突。"},{"en":"Identifying different types of conflicts helps researchers design suitable solutions.","zh":"找出不同類型的衝突，有助研究人員設計合適方案。"},{"en":"One conflict may involve money, while another may involve safety or culture.","zh":"一種衝突可能涉及金錢，另一種可能涉及安全或文化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"arise between","meaning":"在……之間產生","examples":[{"en":"Conflicts may arise between wildlife and humans.","zh":"衝突可能在野生動物與人類之間產生。"},{"en":"If something arises between two groups, it begins or develops in their relationship.","zh":"某事在兩個群體之間產生，是指它在雙方關係中開始或發展。"},{"en":"Problems can arise between farmers and conservation officers.","zh":"農民與保育人員之間可能產生問題。"},{"en":"Conflicts often arise between groups when they compete for the same resources.","zh":"當群體競爭同一資源時，衝突常會產生。"},{"en":"When tensions arise between people and wildlife, both sides’ needs should be examined.","zh":"當人與野生動物之間出現緊張關係時，應檢視雙方需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"wildlife and humans","meaning":"野生動物與人類","examples":[{"en":"Protected areas can create contact between wildlife and humans.","zh":"保護區可以增加野生動物與人類之間的接觸。"},{"en":"Wildlife and humans refers to wild animals and people living or working near them.","zh":"野生動物與人類是指野生動物和在附近生活或工作的人。"},{"en":"Roads and farms often bring wildlife and humans closer together.","zh":"道路和農田常令野生動物與人類更加接近。"},{"en":"Contact between wildlife and humans can create both benefits and risks.","zh":"野生動物與人類接觸可以帶來好處，也可以帶來風險。"},{"en":"Good conservation planning tries to reduce harmful conflict between wildlife and humans.","zh":"良好保育規劃會嘗試減少野生動物與人類之間的有害衝突。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"at the boundaries of","meaning":"在……的邊界","examples":[{"en":"Conflicts may arise at the boundaries of protected areas.","zh":"衝突可能在保護區的邊界產生。"},{"en":"“At the boundaries of” means at the edges or borders of a place.","zh":"「在……的邊界」是指在某地方的邊緣或界線位置。"},{"en":"Farmers often live at the boundaries of national parks.","zh":"農民常住在國家公園邊界附近。"},{"en":"Wildlife may cross boundaries when looking for food or shelter.","zh":"野生動物尋找食物或棲息地時可能跨越邊界。"},{"en":"Problems at the boundaries of protected areas require cooperation between local people and conservation managers.","zh":"保護區邊界的問題需要本地人和保育管理者合作處理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"protected areas","meaning":"保護區","examples":[{"en":"National parks and animal sanctuaries are protected areas.","zh":"國家公園和動物保護區都是保護區。"},{"en":"Protected areas are places where wildlife, plants, or landscapes are legally conserved.","zh":"保護區是依法保護野生動物、植物或景觀的地方。"},{"en":"Protected areas can help endangered species survive.","zh":"保護區可以幫助瀕危物種生存。"},{"en":"People living near protected areas may benefit from tourism but also face wildlife conflicts.","zh":"住在保護區附近的人可能受惠於旅遊業，但也面對野生動物衝突。"},{"en":"Protected areas need careful management to balance conservation and local needs.","zh":"保護區需要謹慎管理，以平衡保育和本地需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"national parks","meaning":"國家公園","examples":[{"en":"National parks are examples of protected areas.","zh":"國家公園是保護區的例子。"},{"en":"National parks are large areas protected by governments for wildlife, landscapes, and public enjoyment.","zh":"國家公園是由政府保護、用於野生動物、景觀和公眾享用的大型地區。"},{"en":"Some national parks attract tourists who want to see wild animals.","zh":"有些國家公園吸引想看野生動物的遊客。"},{"en":"National parks can bring income to nearby communities through tourism.","zh":"國家公園可以透過旅遊業為附近社區帶來收入。"},{"en":"However, animals from national parks may sometimes damage nearby farms.","zh":"然而，國家公園中的動物有時可能破壞附近農場。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"animal sanctuaries","meaning":"動物保護區","examples":[{"en":"Animal sanctuaries are designed to protect wildlife.","zh":"動物保護區旨在保護野生動物。"},{"en":"Animal sanctuaries are places where animals are protected from hunting, harm, or habitat loss.","zh":"動物保護區是保護動物免受捕獵、傷害或棲息地喪失的地方。"},{"en":"The sanctuary provides a safe place for injured birds.","zh":"該保護區為受傷鳥類提供安全地方。"},{"en":"Animal sanctuaries may also educate the public about conservation.","zh":"動物保護區也可能教育公眾有關保育的知識。"},{"en":"A sanctuary can protect animals, but it may still create challenges for nearby residents.","zh":"保護區可以保護動物，但仍可能為附近居民帶來挑戰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"illustrate this by","meaning":"透過……說明這一點","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer illustrates this by describing recent research.","zh":"講者透過描述近期研究來說明這一點。"},{"en":"To illustrate this by doing something means to explain an idea using an example or evidence.","zh":"透過做某事說明這一點，是指用例子或證據解釋一個想法。"},{"en":"The lecturer illustrated the problem by telling a story about local farmers.","zh":"講者透過講述本地農民的故事來說明問題。"},{"en":"Examples help illustrate complex relationships between wildlife and people.","zh":"例子可以幫助說明野生動物與人類之間的複雜關係。"},{"en":"A good lecture illustrates key points with real data or case studies.","zh":"良好講座會透過真實數據或個案研究說明重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be involved in","meaning":"參與……","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer has been involved in research in Zambia.","zh":"講者曾參與尚比亞的研究。"},{"en":"To be involved in something means to take part in it or contribute to it.","zh":"參與某事，是指加入其中或作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Several local farmers were involved in the research project.","zh":"幾位本地農民參與了該研究項目。"},{"en":"Being involved in field research can give scientists practical experience.","zh":"參與實地研究可以讓科學家獲得實際經驗。"},{"en":"People involved in a project may have different roles and responsibilities.","zh":"參與項目的人可能有不同角色和責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recently","meaning":"最近","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer has been involved in this research recently.","zh":"講者最近參與了這項研究。"},{"en":"Recently means not long ago or during the near past.","zh":"最近是指不久以前或近一段時間。"},{"en":"The sanctuary has recently attracted more tourists.","zh":"該保護區最近吸引了更多遊客。"},{"en":"Recent research can update older ideas about conservation.","zh":"近期研究可以更新較舊的保育觀點。"},{"en":"The word helps show that the information is current or fairly new.","zh":"這個詞有助顯示資訊是當前或較新的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the central African country of","meaning":"中非國家……","examples":[{"en":"The research took place in the central African country of Zambia.","zh":"研究在中非國家尚比亞進行。"},{"en":"“The central African country of” introduces a country located in central Africa.","zh":"「中非國家……」用來介紹位於非洲中部的國家。"},{"en":"The documentary discussed the central African country of Zambia.","zh":"紀錄片討論了中非國家尚比亞。"},{"en":"This phrase gives geographical context before naming the country.","zh":"這個說法在說出國名之前提供地理背景。"},{"en":"It is useful when listeners may not know where the country is located.","zh":"當聽眾未必知道國家位置時，這個說法很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Zambia","meaning":"尚比亞","examples":[{"en":"The research was carried out in Zambia.","zh":"這項研究在尚比亞進行。"},{"en":"Zambia is a country in southern-central Africa.","zh":"尚比亞是位於非洲中南部的國家。"},{"en":"The researchers visited farming communities in Zambia.","zh":"研究人員探訪了尚比亞的農業社群。"},{"en":"Zambia has wildlife areas that may affect nearby farmers.","zh":"尚比亞有野生動物區，可能影響附近農民。"},{"en":"Studying Zambia can help researchers understand conservation challenges in rural communities.","zh":"研究尚比亞可以幫助研究人員理解鄉郊社群的保育挑戰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the area around","meaning":"……周邊地區","examples":[{"en":"The study focuses on the area around the Chembe Bird Sanctuary.","zh":"研究集中於Chembe鳥類保護區周邊地區。"},{"en":"“The area around” a place means the surrounding region near it.","zh":"某地周邊地區，是指靠近該地的附近區域。"},{"en":"Farmers in the area around the sanctuary were interviewed.","zh":"保護區周邊地區的農民接受了訪問。"},{"en":"Wildlife often affects the area around a protected site.","zh":"野生動物常影響保護地點周邊地區。"},{"en":"Studying the area around a sanctuary helps show how conservation affects local people.","zh":"研究保護區周邊地區，有助顯示保育如何影響本地人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Chembe Bird Sanctuary","meaning":"Chembe 鳥類保護區","examples":[{"en":"Chembe Bird Sanctuary contains many listed birds of Zambia.","zh":"Chembe鳥類保護區有許多尚比亞列名鳥類。"},{"en":"Chembe Bird Sanctuary is a protected place for birds in Zambia.","zh":"Chembe鳥類保護區是尚比亞一個保護鳥類的地方。"},{"en":"The research studied farmers living near Chembe Bird Sanctuary.","zh":"研究探討住在Chembe鳥類保護區附近的農民。"},{"en":"Bird sanctuaries can protect species while attracting tourists.","zh":"鳥類保護區可以保護物種，同時吸引遊客。"},{"en":"A sanctuary’s effects may extend beyond its official boundary.","zh":"保護區的影響可能延伸至其官方邊界以外。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"listed birds","meaning":"列名鳥類","examples":[{"en":"The sanctuary contains over three hundred listed birds of Zambia.","zh":"該保護區有三百多種尚比亞列名鳥類。"},{"en":"Listed birds are bird species officially recorded or recognised in a particular area.","zh":"列名鳥類是某地區官方記錄或承認的鳥類物種。"},{"en":"The guidebook includes listed birds found in the sanctuary.","zh":"導覽手冊包括在保護區發現的列名鳥類。"},{"en":"A high number of listed birds can make a sanctuary important for conservation.","zh":"大量列名鳥類可以令保護區在保育上十分重要。"},{"en":"Listed species may attract scientists, birdwatchers, and tourists.","zh":"列名物種可能吸引科學家、觀鳥者和遊客。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a number of","meaning":"一些；若干","examples":[{"en":"The sanctuary contains a number of birds of prey.","zh":"該保護區有一些猛禽。"},{"en":"“A number of” means several or some.","zh":"「一些」表示幾個或若干。"},{"en":"A number of farmers reported problems with birds of prey.","zh":"一些農民報告受到猛禽影響。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate quantity without saying the exact number.","zh":"這個說法提供大概數量，而不是精確數字。"},{"en":"It is useful when the precise figure is not necessary.","zh":"當不需要準確數字時，這個說法很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"eagles, hawks and owls","meaning":"鷹、隼和貓頭鷹","examples":[{"en":"Eagles, hawks and owls are examples of birds of prey.","zh":"鷹、隼和貓頭鷹都是猛禽的例子。"},{"en":"Eagles, hawks and owls are hunting birds that catch other animals for food.","zh":"鷹、隼和貓頭鷹是捕獵其他動物為食的鳥類。"},{"en":"Farmers may see eagles, hawks and owls near fields and chicken areas.","zh":"農民可能在田地和養雞區附近看見鷹、隼和貓頭鷹。"},{"en":"These birds can help control rats, snakes, and other small animals.","zh":"這些鳥可以幫助控制老鼠、蛇和其他小動物。"},{"en":"Although they are useful, they may sometimes be seen as threats by farmers.","zh":"雖然牠們有用，但農民有時可能把牠們視為威脅。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"live by hunting and killing","meaning":"以捕獵和殺死……為生","examples":[{"en":"Birds of prey live by hunting and killing other birds and animals.","zh":"猛禽以捕獵和殺死其他鳥類及動物為生。"},{"en":"To live by hunting and killing means to survive by catching and eating other living creatures.","zh":"以捕獵和殺死某些生物為生，是指靠捕捉並吃其他生物來生存。"},{"en":"Owls live by hunting and killing small animals at night.","zh":"貓頭鷹在夜間以捕獵和殺死小動物為生。"},{"en":"Predators are part of the food chain because they live by hunting prey.","zh":"捕食者是食物鏈的一部分，因為牠們靠捕獵獵物生存。"},{"en":"This way of living can benefit ecosystems by controlling animal populations.","zh":"這種生存方式可以透過控制動物數量而有益於生態系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"local communities","meaning":"本地社區","examples":[{"en":"Most people in the local communities are small-scale farmers.","zh":"本地社區的大多數人都是小規模農民。"},{"en":"Local communities are groups of people who live in the same area.","zh":"本地社區是居住在同一地區的一群人。"},{"en":"Local communities near the sanctuary depend on farming and livestock.","zh":"保護區附近的本地社區依靠農業和牲畜生活。"},{"en":"Conservation projects should include the views of local communities.","zh":"保育項目應包括本地社區的意見。"},{"en":"Local communities may benefit from tourism but also face wildlife problems.","zh":"本地社區可能受惠於旅遊業，但也面對野生動物問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"near to","meaning":"接近；靠近","examples":[{"en":"The farmers live near to the bird sanctuary.","zh":"農民住在鳥類保護區附近。"},{"en":"“Near to” means close to a place or thing.","zh":"「靠近」是指距離某地或某物不遠。"},{"en":"The village is near to the protected area.","zh":"那條村靠近保護區。"},{"en":"Living near to a sanctuary can bring both opportunities and risks.","zh":"住在保護區附近可以帶來機會，也會帶來風險。"},{"en":"Farmers near to wildlife areas may experience more contact with animals.","zh":"靠近野生動物區的農民可能更常接觸動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"small-scale farmers","meaning":"小規模農民","examples":[{"en":"Most local residents near the sanctuary are small-scale farmers.","zh":"保護區附近大多數本地居民都是小規模農民。"},{"en":"Small-scale farmers farm on a limited amount of land, often mainly to support their families.","zh":"小規模農民在有限土地上耕作，通常主要為了支持家庭生活。"},{"en":"Small-scale farmers may grow crops and rear chickens.","zh":"小規模農民可能種植作物並飼養雞。"},{"en":"Losing crops or livestock can seriously affect small-scale farmers.","zh":"失去作物或牲畜會嚴重影響小規模農民。"},{"en":"Conservation plans should consider the limited resources of small-scale farmers.","zh":"保育計劃應考慮小規模農民資源有限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"provide important benefits to","meaning":"為……提供重要益處","examples":[{"en":"Birds of prey provide important benefits to local farmers.","zh":"猛禽為本地農民提供重要益處。"},{"en":"To provide important benefits to someone means to give them valuable advantages or help.","zh":"為某人提供重要益處，是指給予他們有價值的好處或幫助。"},{"en":"Owls provide important benefits to farmers by eating rodents.","zh":"貓頭鷹透過吃囓齒動物為農民提供重要益處。"},{"en":"Wildlife can provide benefits to people even when it also creates problems.","zh":"野生動物即使帶來問題，也可以為人類提供益處。"},{"en":"Recognising benefits helps communities see why conservation matters.","zh":"認識這些益處可以幫助社區明白保育的重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"social and ecological benefits","meaning":"社會和生態益處","examples":[{"en":"The birds provide social and ecological benefits to the farmers.","zh":"這些鳥為農民提供社會和生態益處。"},{"en":"Social and ecological benefits are advantages for human communities and natural systems.","zh":"社會和生態益處是對人類社區和自然系統的好處。"},{"en":"Tourism provides social benefits, while pest control provides ecological benefits.","zh":"旅遊業提供社會益處，而害獸控制提供生態益處。"},{"en":"Birds of prey can support culture, income, and ecosystem balance.","zh":"猛禽可以支持文化、收入和生態系統平衡。"},{"en":"A conservation plan should measure both social and ecological benefits.","zh":"保育計劃應衡量社會和生態兩方面的益處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"damage can be caused to","meaning":"可能對……造成損害","examples":[{"en":"A lot of damage can be caused to farmers’ crops by rodents.","zh":"囓齒動物可能對農民的作物造成大量損害。"},{"en":"If damage can be caused to something, it can be harmed or destroyed.","zh":"可能對某物造成損害，是指它可能被傷害或破壞。"},{"en":"Damage can be caused to fields by floods, insects, or animals.","zh":"水災、昆蟲或動物都可能對田地造成損害。"},{"en":"Rodent damage can reduce a farmer’s income.","zh":"囓齒動物造成的損害可以減少農民收入。"},{"en":"Understanding how damage is caused helps farmers choose protective methods.","zh":"了解損害如何造成，有助農民選擇保護方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"farmers’ crops","meaning":"農民的作物","examples":[{"en":"Rodents can damage farmers’ crops.","zh":"囓齒動物可以破壞農民的作物。"},{"en":"Farmers’ crops are the plants farmers grow for food, sale, or animal feed.","zh":"農民的作物是農民種植作為食物、出售或動物飼料的植物。"},{"en":"Rats may eat farmers’ crops before harvest.","zh":"老鼠可能在收成前吃掉農民的作物。"},{"en":"Protecting farmers’ crops is essential for food security and income.","zh":"保護農民的作物對糧食安全和收入至關重要。"},{"en":"Wildlife management can help reduce losses to farmers’ crops.","zh":"野生動物管理可以幫助減少農民作物的損失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rodents such as rats","meaning":"像老鼠這樣的囓齒動物","examples":[{"en":"Rodents such as rats can consume crops in the fields.","zh":"像老鼠這樣的囓齒動物可以吃掉田裏的作物。"},{"en":"Rodents such as rats are small mammals with strong front teeth that gnaw food and materials.","zh":"像老鼠這樣的囓齒動物，是具有強壯門牙、會啃咬食物和材料的小型哺乳動物。"},{"en":"Rodents such as rats can multiply quickly when food is available.","zh":"當食物充足時，像老鼠這樣的囓齒動物可以迅速繁殖。"},{"en":"Birds of prey help control rodents such as rats by hunting them.","zh":"猛禽透過捕獵老鼠等囓齒動物幫助控制牠們的數量。"},{"en":"Without natural predators, rodents can become a serious farming problem.","zh":"沒有天敵時，囓齒動物可能成為嚴重農業問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"consume the crops","meaning":"吃掉作物","examples":[{"en":"Rats would consume the crops if they were not hunted.","zh":"如果沒有被捕獵，老鼠會吃掉作物。"},{"en":"To consume the crops means to eat or use up the plants grown by farmers.","zh":"吃掉作物是指吃掉或耗盡農民種植的植物。"},{"en":"Rodents can consume the crops before farmers have time to harvest them.","zh":"囓齒動物可能在農民收割前吃掉作物。"},{"en":"Birds of prey reduce the number of animals that consume crops.","zh":"猛禽減少會吃掉作物的動物數量。"},{"en":"Crop consumption by pests can lead to financial loss.","zh":"害獸吃掉作物可能導致經濟損失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as they grow in the fields","meaning":"當作物在田裏生長時","examples":[{"en":"Rodents eat crops as they grow in the fields.","zh":"囓齒動物會在作物在田裏生長時吃掉它們。"},{"en":"“As they grow in the fields” means while the crops are still growing on farmland.","zh":"「當作物在田裏生長時」是指作物仍在農田中生長的期間。"},{"en":"Insects attacked the plants as they grew in the fields.","zh":"昆蟲在植物於田裏生長時攻擊它們。"},{"en":"Damage during the growing period can reduce the final harvest.","zh":"生長期間的損害可以減少最終收成。"},{"en":"Farmers must protect crops both while they grow and after they are harvested.","zh":"農民必須在作物生長時和收成後都加以保護。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"after harvesting","meaning":"收成後","examples":[{"en":"Rodents may also consume crops after harvesting.","zh":"囓齒動物也可能在收成後吃掉作物。"},{"en":"After harvesting means after crops have been collected from the fields.","zh":"收成後是指作物從田裏收集起來之後。"},{"en":"Farmers store grain carefully after harvesting.","zh":"農民在收成後仔細儲存穀物。"},{"en":"Pests can still damage crops after harvesting if storage is poor.","zh":"如果儲存環境不佳，害獸在收成後仍可以破壞作物。"},{"en":"Protecting crops after harvesting is as important as protecting them in the field.","zh":"收成後保護作物和在田裏保護作物同樣重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"predatory habits","meaning":"捕食習性","examples":[{"en":"The predatory habits of these birds protect farmers in other ways.","zh":"這些鳥的捕食習性在其他方面保護農民。"},{"en":"Predatory habits are behaviours connected with hunting and eating other animals.","zh":"捕食習性是與捕獵和吃其他動物有關的行為。"},{"en":"Owls’ predatory habits help reduce the number of rats.","zh":"貓頭鷹的捕食習性有助減少老鼠數量。"},{"en":"Predatory habits can benefit ecosystems by controlling populations.","zh":"捕食習性可以透過控制種群數量而有益於生態系統。"},{"en":"Farmers may value predatory birds when they understand what those birds hunt.","zh":"當農民了解猛禽捕食甚麼，便可能更重視牠們。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"protect farmers in other ways","meaning":"在其他方面保護農民","examples":[{"en":"Birds of prey protect farmers in other ways.","zh":"猛禽在其他方面保護農民。"},{"en":"To protect farmers in other ways means to help them beyond the first benefit already mentioned.","zh":"在其他方面保護農民，是指除了先前提到的好處外，還幫助農民。"},{"en":"Birds protect farmers by eating rats and also by controlling snakes.","zh":"鳥類透過吃老鼠保護農民，也透過控制蛇類數量保護農民。"},{"en":"One animal can support farming in several different ways.","zh":"一種動物可以用幾種不同方式支援農業。"},{"en":"Recognising these different forms of protection may reduce hostility toward wildlife.","zh":"認識這些不同形式的保護，可能減少對野生動物的敵意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a major danger to","meaning":"對……的一大危險","examples":[{"en":"Snakes are a major danger to rural workers.","zh":"蛇對農村工作者是一大危險。"},{"en":"A major danger to someone is a serious source of risk or harm.","zh":"對某人的一大危險，是嚴重風險或傷害來源。"},{"en":"Flooding is a major danger to farmers during the rainy season.","zh":"在雨季，水災對農民是一大危險。"},{"en":"Snakes become a major danger when people work in fields without protection.","zh":"當人們在田裏工作而缺乏保護時，蛇會成為一大危險。"},{"en":"Identifying major dangers helps communities prepare safety measures.","zh":"找出主要危險有助社區準備安全措施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rural workers","meaning":"農村工作者","examples":[{"en":"Snakes can be dangerous to rural workers.","zh":"蛇可能對農村工作者構成危險。"},{"en":"Rural workers are people who work in countryside areas, often in farming or related jobs.","zh":"農村工作者是在鄉郊地區工作的人，通常從事農業或相關工作。"},{"en":"Rural workers may walk through fields, grass, and bushland every day.","zh":"農村工作者每天可能穿過田地、草地和灌木叢。"},{"en":"Rural workers can face risks from animals, weather, and difficult transport.","zh":"農村工作者可能面對動物、天氣和交通不便的風險。"},{"en":"Protecting rural workers is important for both safety and local food production.","zh":"保護農村工作者對安全和本地糧食生產都很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"may be dangerous or even fatal","meaning":"可能危險甚至致命","examples":[{"en":"A snake bite may be dangerous or even fatal.","zh":"蛇咬可能危險甚至致命。"},{"en":"“May be dangerous or even fatal” means something can cause serious harm or death.","zh":"「可能危險甚至致命」表示某事可以造成嚴重傷害或死亡。"},{"en":"A bite from a poisonous snake may be dangerous or even fatal.","zh":"毒蛇咬傷可能危險甚至致命。"},{"en":"The phrase warns listeners that the risk is severe.","zh":"這個說法警告聽眾風險很嚴重。"},{"en":"Quick medical treatment can reduce the chance of a fatal outcome.","zh":"迅速醫療處理可以減低致命結果的機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have a major role in","meaning":"在……方面發揮重要作用","examples":[{"en":"Birds of prey have a major role in controlling snake populations.","zh":"猛禽在控制蛇類數量方面發揮重要作用。"},{"en":"To have a major role in something means to be very important in making it happen.","zh":"在某事方面發揮重要作用，是指對該事的發生十分重要。"},{"en":"Predators have a major role in keeping ecosystems balanced.","zh":"捕食者在保持生態系統平衡方面發揮重要作用。"},{"en":"Birds may have a major role in reducing pests on farms.","zh":"鳥類可能在減少農場害獸方面發揮重要作用。"},{"en":"A major role does not mean the only role; other factors may also matter.","zh":"重要作用不等於唯一作用，其他因素也可能重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"keep populations under control","meaning":"控制數量","examples":[{"en":"Birds of prey help keep snake populations under control.","zh":"猛禽幫助控制蛇類數量。"},{"en":"To keep populations under control means to prevent animal numbers from becoming too high.","zh":"控制種群數量，是指防止動物數量變得過高。"},{"en":"Owls help keep rat populations under control.","zh":"貓頭鷹幫助控制老鼠數量。"},{"en":"Natural predators can reduce the need for chemical pest control.","zh":"天然捕食者可以減少對化學害蟲控制的需要。"},{"en":"If predator numbers fall, prey populations may increase too much.","zh":"如果捕食者數量下降，獵物數量可能增加過多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be aware of","meaning":"知道；意識到","examples":[{"en":"Local people have always been aware of these benefits.","zh":"本地人一直知道這些好處。"},{"en":"To be aware of something means to know about it or understand it.","zh":"意識到某事，是指知道或理解它。"},{"en":"Farmers are aware of the danger snakes pose in the fields.","zh":"農民知道蛇在田裏造成的危險。"},{"en":"Being aware of both benefits and risks can lead to better decisions.","zh":"同時意識到好處和風險，可以帶來更好的決定。"},{"en":"Education can make people more aware of the value of wildlife.","zh":"教育可以令人更意識到野生動物的價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"for years","meaning":"多年來","examples":[{"en":"For years, the birds have played a key role in local culture.","zh":"多年來，這些鳥一直在本地文化中扮演關鍵角色。"},{"en":"“For years” means over a long period of time lasting several years or more.","zh":"「多年來」是指持續幾年或更長的一段時間。"},{"en":"Farmers have known about the birds’ benefits for years.","zh":"農民多年來都知道這些鳥的好處。"},{"en":"A belief held for years may become part of local tradition.","zh":"一個持續多年的信念可能成為本地傳統的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises that something is not new.","zh":"這個說法強調某事並不是新的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"play a key role in","meaning":"在……中扮演關鍵角色","examples":[{"en":"The birds played a key role in the culture of the region.","zh":"這些鳥在該地區文化中扮演關鍵角色。"},{"en":"To play a key role in something means to be very important in it.","zh":"在某事中扮演關鍵角色，是指在其中非常重要。"},{"en":"Birds of prey play a key role in controlling pests.","zh":"猛禽在控制害獸方面扮演關鍵角色。"},{"en":"Tourism can play a key role in supporting local income.","zh":"旅遊業可以在支持本地收入方面扮演關鍵角色。"},{"en":"A key role may be cultural, ecological, or economic.","zh":"關鍵角色可以是文化、生態或經濟方面的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the culture of the region","meaning":"該地區文化","examples":[{"en":"The birds are important in the culture of the region.","zh":"這些鳥在該地區文化中很重要。"},{"en":"The culture of the region is the shared beliefs, stories, customs, and practices of people living there.","zh":"該地區文化是當地居民共同的信念、故事、習俗和做法。"},{"en":"Local stories about birds of prey are part of the culture of the region.","zh":"關於猛禽的本地故事是該地區文化的一部分。"},{"en":"Conservation is easier when it respects the culture of the region.","zh":"當保育尊重該地區文化時，推行會較容易。"},{"en":"Cultural importance can make wildlife valuable beyond its ecological role.","zh":"文化重要性可以令野生動物的價值超越其生態角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"increasingly important to","meaning":"對……越來越重要","examples":[{"en":"The sanctuary has become increasingly important to the community.","zh":"該保護區對社區變得越來越重要。"},{"en":"Increasingly important to someone means becoming more important over time.","zh":"對某人越來越重要，是指隨時間變得更重要。"},{"en":"Tourism has become increasingly important to local farmers.","zh":"旅遊業對本地農民變得越來越重要。"},{"en":"A protected area may become increasingly important as visitor numbers grow.","zh":"隨着遊客數量增加，保護區可能變得越來越重要。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a gradual increase in value or influence.","zh":"這個說法顯示價值或影響力逐漸增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in economic terms","meaning":"在經濟層面上","examples":[{"en":"The birds are increasingly important in economic terms.","zh":"這些鳥在經濟層面上越來越重要。"},{"en":"“In economic terms” means from the point of view of money, income, jobs, or financial value.","zh":"「在經濟層面上」是從金錢、收入、工作或財務價值角度來看。"},{"en":"Tourism is important in economic terms for the village.","zh":"旅遊業在經濟層面上對村莊很重要。"},{"en":"A species can be valuable in economic terms if it attracts visitors.","zh":"如果一個物種吸引遊客，它在經濟層面上可能很有價值。"},{"en":"Looking only in economic terms may ignore cultural or ecological value.","zh":"只從經濟層面看，可能忽略文化或生態價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at present","meaning":"目前","examples":[{"en":"At present, tourism is an important source of revenue.","zh":"目前，旅遊業是一個重要收入來源。"},{"en":"“At present” means now or currently.","zh":"「目前」是指現在或當前。"},{"en":"At present, many villagers earn money from visitors.","zh":"目前，許多村民從遊客身上賺取收入。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the current situation, which may change later.","zh":"這個說法描述當前情況，而情況日後可能改變。"},{"en":"It is often used in reports and lectures.","zh":"它常用於報告和講座中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"after a relatively slow start","meaning":"在起步較慢之後","examples":[{"en":"Tourism became important after a relatively slow start.","zh":"旅遊業在起步較慢之後變得重要。"},{"en":"“After a relatively slow start” means after beginning slowly compared with expectations.","zh":"「在起步較慢之後」表示開始時比預期慢。"},{"en":"The project grew successful after a relatively slow start.","zh":"該項目在起步較慢之後變得成功。"},{"en":"A slow start does not mean a project will fail.","zh":"起步較慢並不表示項目一定會失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that progress improved later.","zh":"這個說法暗示後來進展有所改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an important source of revenue","meaning":"重要收入來源","examples":[{"en":"Tourism has become an important source of revenue for the community.","zh":"旅遊業已成為該社區的重要收入來源。"},{"en":"An important source of revenue is something that provides significant income.","zh":"重要收入來源是能提供大量收入的事物。"},{"en":"Visitor fees became an important source of revenue for the sanctuary.","zh":"遊客費用成為保護區的重要收入來源。"},{"en":"Revenue from tourism can support local businesses and conservation work.","zh":"旅遊收入可以支持本地企業和保育工作。"},{"en":"Relying on one source of revenue can be risky if visitor numbers fall.","zh":"如果遊客數量下降，依賴單一收入來源會有風險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be protected by the government","meaning":"受政府保護","examples":[{"en":"The birds of prey are protected by the government.","zh":"猛禽受政府保護。"},{"en":"If animals are protected by the government, laws or policies are used to stop people harming them.","zh":"動物受政府保護，是指法律或政策用來阻止人們傷害牠們。"},{"en":"Endangered birds are protected by the government in many countries.","zh":"在許多國家，瀕危鳥類受政府保護。"},{"en":"Legal protection can reduce hunting but may not remove all threats.","zh":"法律保護可以減少捕獵，但未必消除所有威脅。"},{"en":"Government protection works best when local communities understand and support it.","zh":"當本地社區理解並支持時，政府保護最有效。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"numbers are falling","meaning":"數量正在下降","examples":[{"en":"The numbers of birds of prey are falling.","zh":"猛禽數量正在下降。"},{"en":"If numbers are falling, the population or quantity is decreasing.","zh":"數量正在下降，是指種群或數量正在減少。"},{"en":"Bird numbers are falling because of traffic, poisoning, and power lines.","zh":"由於交通、毒殺和電線，鳥類數量正在下降。"},{"en":"Falling numbers may indicate that a species is under serious pressure.","zh":"數量下降可能表示一個物種正承受嚴重壓力。"},{"en":"Conservation action is needed when wildlife numbers fall too quickly.","zh":"當野生動物數量下降太快，便需要保育行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"accidental deaths","meaning":"意外死亡","examples":[{"en":"Some accidental deaths happen when birds land on roads.","zh":"有些意外死亡發生在鳥類降落在道路上時。"},{"en":"Accidental deaths are deaths that happen unintentionally or by chance.","zh":"意外死亡是非故意或偶然發生的死亡。"},{"en":"Road traffic can cause accidental deaths among birds of prey.","zh":"道路交通可以造成猛禽意外死亡。"},{"en":"Accidental deaths may still be reduced through planning and awareness.","zh":"透過規劃和提高意識，意外死亡仍可減少。"},{"en":"Even accidental deaths can seriously affect a small wildlife population.","zh":"即使是意外死亡，也可以嚴重影響小型野生動物種群。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fatalities occur","meaning":"死亡事故發生","examples":[{"en":"Fatalities occur when birds are hit by traffic.","zh":"當鳥類被車輛撞到時，死亡事故會發生。"},{"en":"“Fatalities occur” means deaths happen.","zh":"「死亡事故發生」表示有人或動物死亡。"},{"en":"Fatalities occur when animals cross busy roads at night.","zh":"動物夜間橫過繁忙道路時，死亡事故可能發生。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and often used in reports.","zh":"這個說法較正式，常用於報告。"},{"en":"Researchers study where fatalities occur in order to reduce future deaths.","zh":"研究人員研究死亡事故發生的位置，以減少未來死亡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"alight on roads","meaning":"降落在道路上","examples":[{"en":"Birds may alight on roads to catch their prey.","zh":"鳥類可能降落在道路上捕捉獵物。"},{"en":"To alight on roads means to land on roads after flying.","zh":"降落在道路上，是指飛行後停落在道路表面。"},{"en":"Owls sometimes alight on quiet roads at night.","zh":"貓頭鷹有時夜間會降落在安靜道路上。"},{"en":"Birds that alight on roads may be hard for drivers to see.","zh":"降落在道路上的鳥可能很難被司機看見。"},{"en":"Road design and warning signs can help reduce risks to birds.","zh":"道路設計和警告標誌可以幫助減少鳥類面對的風險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"catch and eat their prey","meaning":"捕捉並吃掉獵物","examples":[{"en":"Birds alight on roads to catch and eat their prey.","zh":"鳥類降落在道路上捕捉並吃掉獵物。"},{"en":"To catch and eat prey means to capture another animal and consume it as food.","zh":"捕捉並吃掉獵物，是指抓住另一動物並把牠作為食物。"},{"en":"Hawks catch and eat small animals in open fields.","zh":"隼會在空曠田野捕捉並吃掉小動物。"},{"en":"Roads may attract birds if prey animals are visible there.","zh":"如果道路上容易看見獵物，便可能吸引鳥類。"},{"en":"Hunting behaviour can accidentally place birds in danger.","zh":"捕獵行為可能意外地令鳥類身處危險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fast-moving traffic","meaning":"高速行駛的車輛","examples":[{"en":"Birds may be hit by fast-moving traffic.","zh":"鳥類可能被高速行駛的車輛撞到。"},{"en":"Fast-moving traffic is vehicles travelling quickly along a road.","zh":"高速行駛的車輛是指在道路上快速行駛的交通工具。"},{"en":"Fast-moving traffic can be dangerous for people and animals.","zh":"高速行駛的車輛對人和動物都可能危險。"},{"en":"Birds on roads may not escape quickly enough from fast-moving traffic.","zh":"在道路上的鳥可能來不及避開高速車輛。"},{"en":"Slower driving near sanctuaries can reduce wildlife deaths.","zh":"在保護區附近慢駛可以減少野生動物死亡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take special care","meaning":"特別小心","examples":[{"en":"Drivers in Zambia have to take special care at night.","zh":"尚比亞的司機夜間必須特別小心。"},{"en":"To take special care means to be extra careful because the situation is risky.","zh":"特別小心是指因情況有風險而更加謹慎。"},{"en":"Drivers should take special care near wildlife areas.","zh":"司機在野生動物區附近應特別小心。"},{"en":"Taking special care at night can prevent collisions with animals.","zh":"夜間特別小心可以防止與動物相撞。"},{"en":"Signs and education can remind people to take care.","zh":"標誌和教育可以提醒人們小心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"regard something as","meaning":"把……視為","examples":[{"en":"Birds may regard quieter roads as safe places to sleep.","zh":"鳥類可能把較安靜的道路視為安全的睡覺地點。"},{"en":"To regard something as a particular thing means to consider or see it in that way.","zh":"把某物視為某事，是指以該方式看待或理解它。"},{"en":"Farmers may regard birds of prey as both useful and dangerous.","zh":"農民可能把猛禽視為既有用又危險。"},{"en":"Animals may regard open roads as safe because they are quiet at night.","zh":"動物可能因夜間道路安靜而把它們視為安全。"},{"en":"How people regard wildlife can affect whether they protect or harm it.","zh":"人們如何看待野生動物，會影響他們保護還是傷害牠們。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"quieter roads","meaning":"較安靜的道路","examples":[{"en":"Birds may regard quieter roads as safe places to sleep.","zh":"鳥類可能把較安靜的道路視為安全的睡覺地點。"},{"en":"Quieter roads are roads with less traffic and noise.","zh":"較安靜的道路是交通和噪音較少的道路。"},{"en":"At night, quieter roads may attract birds looking for resting places.","zh":"夜間，較安靜的道路可能吸引尋找休息地點的鳥類。"},{"en":"Quieter roads can still be dangerous if vehicles move quickly.","zh":"即使道路較安靜，如果車輛行駛很快，仍然危險。"},{"en":"Wildlife risks should be considered even on roads that seem quiet.","zh":"即使道路看似安靜，也應考慮野生動物風險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"safe places to sleep","meaning":"安全的睡覺地點","examples":[{"en":"Roads may seem like safe places to sleep for birds.","zh":"對鳥類來說，道路可能看似安全的睡覺地點。"},{"en":"Safe places to sleep are locations where an animal or person can rest without danger.","zh":"安全的睡覺地點是動物或人可以無危險地休息的地方。"},{"en":"Trees are safer places for birds to sleep than roads.","zh":"樹木比道路更適合作為鳥類安全的睡覺地點。"},{"en":"Animals may choose sleeping places based on quietness rather than real safety.","zh":"動物可能根據安靜程度，而不是真正安全性來選擇睡覺地點。"},{"en":"What seems safe to an animal may become dangerous because of human activity.","zh":"對動物看似安全的地方，可能因人類活動而變得危險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"high-voltage power lines","meaning":"高壓電線","examples":[{"en":"Birds may be electrocuted near high-voltage power lines.","zh":"鳥類可能在高壓電線附近觸電死亡。"},{"en":"High-voltage power lines are cables that carry electricity at very high levels.","zh":"高壓電線是輸送高電壓電力的電纜。"},{"en":"Large birds can be at risk near high-voltage power lines.","zh":"大型鳥類在高壓電線附近可能有風險。"},{"en":"Power lines can threaten birds when they fly, land, or spread their wings near them.","zh":"鳥類在高壓電線附近飛行、停落或張開翅膀時可能受威脅。"},{"en":"Safer designs can reduce bird deaths near power lines.","zh":"更安全的設計可以減少電線附近的鳥類死亡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be electrocuted","meaning":"觸電死亡","examples":[{"en":"Birds may be electrocuted if they fly close to power lines.","zh":"鳥類如果飛近電線，可能會觸電死亡。"},{"en":"To be electrocuted means to be injured or killed by electric shock.","zh":"觸電是指因電擊而受傷或死亡。"},{"en":"A bird can be electrocuted when it touches two electrical points at once.","zh":"當鳥同時接觸兩個電力點，便可能觸電。"},{"en":"Electrocution is a serious threat to large birds of prey.","zh":"觸電是大型猛禽面對的嚴重威脅。"},{"en":"Preventing electrocution may require changes to power-line structures.","zh":"防止觸電可能需要改變電線結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a particular danger","meaning":"特別危險的情況","examples":[{"en":"Electrocution is a particular danger during heavy rain.","zh":"觸電在大雨期間是特別危險的情況。"},{"en":"A particular danger is a specific risk that is especially important in a situation.","zh":"特別危險的情況，是在某情境中特別重要的具體風險。"},{"en":"Fast traffic is a particular danger at night.","zh":"夜間高速車輛是特別危險的情況。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can make power lines a particular danger for birds.","zh":"大雨可以令電線對鳥類變得特別危險。"},{"en":"Identifying particular dangers helps conservationists target solutions.","zh":"找出特別危險的情況，有助保育人員制定針對性方案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"heavy rain","meaning":"大雨","examples":[{"en":"Heavy rain can increase the danger from power lines.","zh":"大雨可以增加電線帶來的危險。"},{"en":"Heavy rain is a large amount of rain falling strongly or for a long time.","zh":"大雨是大量雨水強烈或長時間降下。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may occur in the region during certain months.","zh":"該地區在某些月份可能出現大雨。"},{"en":"Wet conditions can increase risks around electricity.","zh":"潮濕環境可以增加電力相關風險。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can also affect roads, farms, and animal behaviour.","zh":"大雨也會影響道路、農田和動物行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the region","meaning":"在該地區","examples":[{"en":"Heavy rain can occur in the region from December to April.","zh":"該地區從十二月至四月可能出現大雨。"},{"en":"“In the region” means in the particular area being discussed.","zh":"「在該地區」是指在正在討論的特定區域內。"},{"en":"Many farmers in the region rear chickens.","zh":"該地區許多農民飼養雞。"},{"en":"Conditions in the region may affect both wildlife and farming.","zh":"該地區的環境可能同時影響野生動物和農業。"},{"en":"The phrase helps keep the focus on a specific geographical area.","zh":"這個說法有助把焦點保持在特定地理區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"from December to April","meaning":"從十二月至四月","examples":[{"en":"Heavy rain can occur from December to April.","zh":"大雨可能從十二月至四月出現。"},{"en":"“From December to April” gives the period between those months.","zh":"「從十二月至四月」表示這兩個月份之間的時段。"},{"en":"The wet season lasts from December to April.","zh":"雨季從十二月至四月持續。"},{"en":"Farmers may change their work patterns from December to April.","zh":"農民可能在十二月至四月改變工作模式。"},{"en":"Seasonal risks should be planned for before December begins.","zh":"季節性風險應在十二月開始前作好規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pose a threat to","meaning":"對……構成威脅","examples":[{"en":"Local farmers also pose a threat to these birds.","zh":"本地農民也對這些鳥構成威脅。"},{"en":"To pose a threat to something means to create a danger or risk for it.","zh":"對某事構成威脅，是指為它造成危險或風險。"},{"en":"Poisoning poses a threat to birds of prey and the wider ecosystem.","zh":"毒殺對猛禽和更廣泛生態系統構成威脅。"},{"en":"Human activity can pose a threat to protected species.","zh":"人類活動可以對受保護物種構成威脅。"},{"en":"A threat may be intentional or accidental.","zh":"威脅可以是有意的，也可以是意外的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as well as growing crops","meaning":"除了種植作物外","examples":[{"en":"As well as growing crops, farmers also rear chickens.","zh":"除了種植作物外，農民也飼養雞。"},{"en":"“As well as growing crops” means in addition to planting and harvesting crops.","zh":"「除了種植作物外」表示除了栽種和收割作物之外。"},{"en":"As well as growing crops, the family kept goats.","zh":"除了種植作物外，這個家庭還養山羊。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that farmers have more than one source of food or income.","zh":"這個說法顯示農民有不止一個食物或收入來源。"},{"en":"Multiple activities can make farming life more secure but also more complicated.","zh":"多種活動可以令農業生活更穩定，但也更複雜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rear chickens","meaning":"飼養雞","examples":[{"en":"Small-scale farmers in the area rear chickens.","zh":"該地區的小規模農民飼養雞。"},{"en":"To rear chickens means to raise and care for chickens.","zh":"飼養雞是指養育和照顧雞。"},{"en":"Many families rear chickens for eggs, meat, and income.","zh":"許多家庭飼養雞以取得雞蛋、肉和收入。"},{"en":"Farmers who rear chickens must protect them from disease and predators.","zh":"飼養雞的農民必須保護牠們免受疾病和捕食者影響。"},{"en":"Chickens can be valuable because they provide regular food and money.","zh":"雞很有價值，因為牠們提供定期食物和收入。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an important source of income","meaning":"重要收入來源","examples":[{"en":"Chickens are an important source of income for farmers.","zh":"雞是農民的重要收入來源。"},{"en":"An important source of income is something that provides significant money to a person or family.","zh":"重要收入來源是為個人或家庭提供大量金錢的事物。"},{"en":"Selling eggs became an important source of income for the household.","zh":"售賣雞蛋成為該家庭的重要收入來源。"},{"en":"Losing chickens can damage an important source of income.","zh":"失去雞隻會損害一項重要收入來源。"},{"en":"Protecting income sources is essential for small-scale farmers.","zh":"保護收入來源對小規模農民至關重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an easy target for","meaning":"……的容易目標","examples":[{"en":"Chickens are an easy target for birds of prey.","zh":"雞是猛禽容易攻擊的目標。"},{"en":"An easy target for something is a person or animal that can be attacked or taken with little difficulty.","zh":"某事物的容易目標，是指容易被攻擊或捕捉的人或動物。"},{"en":"Young chicks are an easy target for predators.","zh":"小雞是捕食者容易攻擊的目標。"},{"en":"Animals left in open areas may become easy targets.","zh":"留在空曠地方的動物可能成為容易目標。"},{"en":"Providing shelter can make chickens less easy to attack.","zh":"提供遮蔽可以令雞較不容易被攻擊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"shoot these birds","meaning":"射殺這些鳥","examples":[{"en":"Farmers may shoot these birds to protect their chickens.","zh":"農民可能射殺這些鳥以保護自己的雞。"},{"en":"To shoot these birds means to kill or injure them with a gun.","zh":"射殺這些鳥，是指用槍殺死或傷害牠們。"},{"en":"Some farmers shoot birds of prey when they fear losing livestock.","zh":"有些農民害怕失去家禽時，會射殺猛禽。"},{"en":"Shooting protected birds may be illegal even if farmers feel desperate.","zh":"即使農民感到無奈，射殺受保護鳥類也可能是非法的。"},{"en":"Safer methods are needed so farmers do not shoot the birds.","zh":"需要更安全方法，讓農民不用射殺這些鳥。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"illegal but understandable","meaning":"非法但可以理解","examples":[{"en":"Shooting the birds is illegal but understandable.","zh":"射殺這些鳥是非法但可以理解的。"},{"en":"“Illegal but understandable” means an action breaks the law but the reason for it can be sympathised with.","zh":"「非法但可以理解」表示某行動違法，但其原因令人同情或理解。"},{"en":"Poisoning wildlife is illegal but may seem understandable to farmers who have lost animals.","zh":"毒殺野生動物是非法的，但對失去家禽的農民來說可能似乎可以理解。"},{"en":"The phrase separates legal judgement from human emotion.","zh":"這個說法把法律判斷與人的情感分開。"},{"en":"Understanding why people break a law can help create better solutions.","zh":"理解人們為何違法，可以幫助制定更好的解決方案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"poison the birds","meaning":"毒殺鳥類","examples":[{"en":"Some farmers may poison the birds.","zh":"有些農民可能毒殺鳥類。"},{"en":"To poison the birds means to kill or harm them using toxic substances.","zh":"毒殺鳥類是指使用有毒物質殺死或傷害牠們。"},{"en":"Poisoning birds of prey can also kill other animals that eat the poison.","zh":"毒殺猛禽也可能殺死其他吃到毒物的動物。"},{"en":"Poison is dangerous because it can spread through the ecosystem.","zh":"毒物很危險，因為它可能在生態系統中擴散。"},{"en":"Farmers need alternatives so they do not poison protected birds.","zh":"農民需要替代方法，才不會毒殺受保護鳥類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"negative effects on","meaning":"對……有負面影響","examples":[{"en":"Poisoning birds can have negative effects on the ecosystem.","zh":"毒殺鳥類可以對生態系統有負面影響。"},{"en":"Negative effects on something are harmful results that affect it.","zh":"對某事有負面影響，是指對它造成有害結果。"},{"en":"Chemicals can have negative effects on soil and water.","zh":"化學品可以對土壤和水造成負面影響。"},{"en":"Actions taken to protect chickens may have negative effects on wildlife.","zh":"為保護雞而採取的行動，可能對野生動物有負面影響。"},{"en":"Before choosing a method, farmers should consider its wider effects.","zh":"選擇方法前，農民應考慮其更廣泛影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the ecosystem","meaning":"生態系統","examples":[{"en":"Poison can have negative effects on the ecosystem.","zh":"毒物可以對生態系統有負面影響。"},{"en":"The ecosystem is the community of living things and their physical environment.","zh":"生態系統是生物群落及其物理環境的整體。"},{"en":"Birds, snakes, rodents, crops, and people are all part of the ecosystem.","zh":"鳥、蛇、囓齒動物、作物和人都是生態系統的一部分。"},{"en":"Removing one predator can change the balance of the ecosystem.","zh":"移除一種捕食者可以改變生態系統平衡。"},{"en":"A healthy ecosystem supports both wildlife and human communities.","zh":"健康生態系統支援野生動物和人類社區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"protect their chickens from","meaning":"保護雞免受……","examples":[{"en":"Farmers try to protect their chickens from birds of prey.","zh":"農民嘗試保護雞免受猛禽攻擊。"},{"en":"To protect chickens from something means to keep them safe from that danger.","zh":"保護雞免受某事影響，是指使牠們避開該危險。"},{"en":"Farmers build fences to protect chickens from predators.","zh":"農民建圍欄保護雞免受捕食者攻擊。"},{"en":"Protecting chickens is important because they provide food and income.","zh":"保護雞很重要，因為牠們提供食物和收入。"},{"en":"Protection methods should not create greater environmental harm.","zh":"保護方法不應造成更大的環境傷害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"prevent the predators from","meaning":"防止捕食者……","examples":[{"en":"Some people try to prevent the predators from settling nearby.","zh":"有些人嘗試防止捕食者在附近停留。"},{"en":"To prevent predators from doing something means to stop hunting animals from taking that action.","zh":"防止捕食者做某事，是指阻止捕食動物採取該行動。"},{"en":"Farmers try to prevent predators from entering the chicken area.","zh":"農民嘗試防止捕食者進入養雞區。"},{"en":"Preventing predators may require barriers, noise, or guard animals.","zh":"防止捕食者可能需要屏障、噪音或看守動物。"},{"en":"Good methods should stop predators without killing them.","zh":"好方法應阻止捕食者，而不殺死牠們。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"settle near","meaning":"停留在……附近","examples":[{"en":"Predators may settle near the area where chickens are kept.","zh":"捕食者可能停留在飼養雞的地方附近。"},{"en":"To settle near a place means to stay, rest, or establish oneself close to it.","zh":"停留在某地附近，是指在靠近該地的地方停留、休息或定居。"},{"en":"Birds of prey may settle near farms if food is easy to find.","zh":"如果食物容易找到，猛禽可能停留在農場附近。"},{"en":"Farmers may try to stop predators from settling near chicken shelters.","zh":"農民可能嘗試阻止捕食者停留在雞舍附近。"},{"en":"A predator that settles nearby may become a repeated threat.","zh":"停留在附近的捕食者可能成為反覆出現的威脅。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"keep this area free from vegetation","meaning":"令該區域沒有植被","examples":[{"en":"Some people keep the chicken area free from vegetation.","zh":"有些人令養雞區域沒有植被。"},{"en":"To keep an area free from vegetation means to remove plants, grass, or bushes from it.","zh":"令某區域沒有植被，是指移除該處的植物、草或灌木。"},{"en":"Farmers cleared the area to keep it free from vegetation.","zh":"農民清理該區，以令它沒有植被。"},{"en":"Removing vegetation may make predators easier to see.","zh":"移除植被可能令捕食者更容易被看見。"},{"en":"However, it can also remove cover that chickens need for protection.","zh":"然而，這也會移除雞需要用來保護自己的遮蔽物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"counter-productive","meaning":"適得其反","examples":[{"en":"Clearing vegetation is counter-productive.","zh":"清除植被是適得其反的。"},{"en":"Something counter-productive has the opposite effect from the one intended.","zh":"適得其反的事情，產生與原本目的相反的效果。"},{"en":"Removing bushes was counter-productive because the chickens lost hiding places.","zh":"移除灌木適得其反，因為雞失去了躲藏地方。"},{"en":"A method can seem sensible but be counter-productive in practice.","zh":"一種方法看似合理，但實際上可能適得其反。"},{"en":"Testing a solution helps people discover whether it is actually helpful.","zh":"測試解決方法可以幫助人們發現它是否真的有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cover to hide in","meaning":"可躲藏的遮蔽物","examples":[{"en":"Without vegetation, chickens have no cover to hide in.","zh":"沒有植被，雞就沒有可躲藏的遮蔽物。"},{"en":"Cover to hide in means shelter or objects that allow animals to avoid being seen.","zh":"可躲藏的遮蔽物是讓動物避免被看見的庇護物或物件。"},{"en":"Bushes give young chicks cover to hide in.","zh":"灌木給小雞提供可躲藏的遮蔽物。"},{"en":"Without cover, chickens are easier for predators to catch.","zh":"沒有遮蔽物，雞更容易被捕食者抓到。"},{"en":"Good farm design should provide safe cover without attracting too many predators.","zh":"良好農場設計應提供安全遮蔽物，同時避免吸引太多捕食者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"another possibility would be to","meaning":"另一個可能做法是","examples":[{"en":"Another possibility would be to keep the chickens indoors.","zh":"另一個可能做法是把雞留在室內。"},{"en":"“Another possibility would be to” introduces a different possible solution.","zh":"「另一個可能做法是」用來引入另一種可能解決方法。"},{"en":"Another possibility would be to use stronger chicken shelters.","zh":"另一個可能做法是使用更堅固的雞舍。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when comparing several options.","zh":"這個說法適合用於比較多個選項。"},{"en":"A possibility should be examined for cost, practicality, and effectiveness.","zh":"可能做法應從成本、實用性和效果方面評估。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"prevent the chickens from going outside","meaning":"防止雞到戶外","examples":[{"en":"Farmers could prevent the chickens from going outside.","zh":"農民可以防止雞到戶外。"},{"en":"To prevent chickens from going outside means to stop them leaving an indoor or enclosed area.","zh":"防止雞到戶外，是指阻止牠們離開室內或圍起來的地方。"},{"en":"A secure building can prevent chickens from going outside at night.","zh":"安全建築可以防止雞夜間到戶外。"},{"en":"Keeping chickens inside may reduce attacks from birds of prey.","zh":"把雞留在室內可以減少猛禽攻擊。"},{"en":"However, preventing chickens from going outside may cost money and require space.","zh":"然而，防止雞到戶外可能需要金錢和空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"keep them safe from predators","meaning":"保護牠們免受捕食者攻擊","examples":[{"en":"A building could keep the chickens safe from predators.","zh":"建築物可以保護雞免受捕食者攻擊。"},{"en":"To keep animals safe from predators means to protect them from being hunted or attacked.","zh":"保護動物免受捕食者攻擊，是指防止牠們被捕獵或攻擊。"},{"en":"A strong fence can keep chicks safe from predators.","zh":"堅固圍欄可以保護小雞免受捕食者攻擊。"},{"en":"Night shelters help keep chickens safe from owls and other hunters.","zh":"夜間雞舍有助保護雞免受貓頭鷹和其他捕食者攻擊。"},{"en":"Safety measures must be realistic for small-scale farmers.","zh":"安全措施對小規模農民來說必須實際可行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"inside a building","meaning":"在建築物內","examples":[{"en":"Chickens could be kept inside a building.","zh":"雞可以被飼養在建築物內。"},{"en":"Inside a building means within a structure with walls and a roof.","zh":"在建築物內，是指在有牆和屋頂的結構裏面。"},{"en":"Farmers may keep young chicks inside a building at night.","zh":"農民可能在夜間把小雞留在建築物內。"},{"en":"Keeping chickens inside a building can protect them but requires space and cleaning.","zh":"把雞留在建築物內可以保護牠們，但需要空間和清潔。"},{"en":"A building used for animals must have air, light, and safe flooring.","zh":"用來飼養動物的建築物必須有空氣、光線和安全地面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"far too much to be practical","meaning":"成本太高而不切實際","examples":[{"en":"Keeping chickens indoors would cost far too much to be practical.","zh":"把雞留在室內的成本太高而不切實際。"},{"en":"If something costs far too much to be practical, it is too expensive to be a realistic solution.","zh":"某事成本太高而不切實際，是指它太昂貴，不能成為現實方案。"},{"en":"Building large shelters for every farmer may cost far too much to be practical.","zh":"為每位農民建大型雞舍可能成本太高而不切實際。"},{"en":"A solution can be effective in theory but too costly in practice.","zh":"一個方案理論上有效，但實際上可能成本太高。"},{"en":"Practical solutions must match local budgets and resources.","zh":"實際方案必須配合本地預算和資源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a practical solution","meaning":"實際可行的解決方法","examples":[{"en":"Keeping chickens indoors is not a practical solution.","zh":"把雞留在室內並不是實際可行的解決方法。"},{"en":"A practical solution is a method that can realistically be used in real life.","zh":"實際可行的解決方法，是在現實生活中可真正使用的方法。"},{"en":"Using dogs may be a more practical solution for some farmers.","zh":"對有些農民來說，使用狗可能是更實際可行的解決方法。"},{"en":"A practical solution should be affordable, simple, and effective.","zh":"實際方案應價格可負擔、簡單而有效。"},{"en":"Researchers must consider whether a solution works for local people.","zh":"研究人員必須考慮方案是否適合本地人使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"spend time and effort","meaning":"花時間和精力","examples":[{"en":"Farmers spend time and effort trying to protect their chickens.","zh":"農民花時間和精力嘗試保護自己的雞。"},{"en":"To spend time and effort means to use one’s energy and hours to do something.","zh":"花時間和精力，是指用自己的時間和能量做某事。"},{"en":"Farmers spend time and effort building shelters and watching chicks.","zh":"農民花時間和精力建雞舍和看守小雞。"},{"en":"Protecting animals can require daily effort.","zh":"保護動物可能需要每天付出努力。"},{"en":"Time and effort are important costs, even when no money is spent.","zh":"即使沒有花錢，時間和精力也是重要成本。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"frighten off","meaning":"嚇走","examples":[{"en":"Farmers try to frighten off the birds of prey.","zh":"農民嘗試嚇走猛禽。"},{"en":"To frighten off an animal means to scare it so that it leaves.","zh":"嚇走動物是指把牠嚇到離開。"},{"en":"Loud noises can frighten off predators.","zh":"大聲噪音可以嚇走捕食者。"},{"en":"Farmers may frighten off birds without killing them.","zh":"農民可能在不殺死鳥類的情況下嚇走牠們。"},{"en":"Methods that frighten off wildlife are often safer than poison or shooting.","zh":"嚇走野生動物的方法通常比毒殺或射殺更安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"without actually harming them","meaning":"而不實際傷害牠們","examples":[{"en":"Farmers try to scare the birds without actually harming them.","zh":"農民嘗試嚇走鳥類，而不實際傷害牠們。"},{"en":"“Without actually harming them” means without really injuring or killing them.","zh":"「而不實際傷害牠們」表示不真正令牠們受傷或死亡。"},{"en":"Dogs can scare birds away without actually harming them.","zh":"狗可以嚇走鳥類，而不實際傷害牠們。"},{"en":"This approach protects chickens while respecting wildlife laws.","zh":"這種做法保護雞，同時尊重野生動物法例。"},{"en":"Non-harmful methods can reduce conflict between farmers and conservationists.","zh":"非傷害性方法可以減少農民與保育人士之間的衝突。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at least one dog","meaning":"至少一隻狗","examples":[{"en":"Most farmers had at least one dog.","zh":"大多數農民至少有一隻狗。"},{"en":"“At least one dog” means one dog or more.","zh":"「至少一隻狗」表示一隻或更多狗。"},{"en":"At least one dog stayed near the chickens during the day.","zh":"白天至少有一隻狗留在雞附近。"},{"en":"Having at least one dog can help farmers watch for predators.","zh":"至少有一隻狗可以幫助農民留意捕食者。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a minimum number, not an exact number.","zh":"這個說法設定最低數量，而不是精確數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a big help at","meaning":"對……很有幫助","examples":[{"en":"Dogs are a big help at scaring away predators.","zh":"狗對嚇走捕食者很有幫助。"},{"en":"To be a big help at something means to be very useful in doing it.","zh":"對某事很有幫助，是指在做該事方面非常有用。"},{"en":"Dogs are a big help at protecting chickens.","zh":"狗對保護雞很有幫助。"},{"en":"A simple tool can be a big help when resources are limited.","zh":"當資源有限時，簡單工具也可以很有幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal but clearly shows usefulness.","zh":"這個說法較口語，但清楚表示有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"scaring away the predators","meaning":"嚇走捕食者","examples":[{"en":"Dogs help farmers by scaring away the predators.","zh":"狗透過嚇走捕食者來幫助農民。"},{"en":"Scaring away the predators means frightening hunting animals so they leave the area.","zh":"嚇走捕食者，是指把捕獵動物嚇到離開該區域。"},{"en":"Noise and movement can help in scaring away predators.","zh":"噪音和動作可以幫助嚇走捕食者。"},{"en":"Scaring predators away is safer than killing them.","zh":"嚇走捕食者比殺死牠們更安全。"},{"en":"The method may need to be repeated because predators can return.","zh":"這種方法可能需要重複使用，因為捕食者可能回來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"during the breeding season","meaning":"在繁殖季節","examples":[{"en":"Chickens are particularly vulnerable during the breeding season.","zh":"雞在繁殖季節特別脆弱。"},{"en":"During the breeding season means in the period when animals reproduce and young are born or raised.","zh":"在繁殖季節，是指動物繁殖和幼崽出生或被照顧的時期。"},{"en":"Farmers watch chicks closely during the breeding season.","zh":"農民在繁殖季節密切看守小雞。"},{"en":"Predators may be more active when young animals are present.","zh":"當幼小動物出現時，捕食者可能更活躍。"},{"en":"The breeding season can require extra protection and monitoring.","zh":"繁殖季節可能需要額外保護和監察。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"particularly vulnerable","meaning":"特別脆弱","examples":[{"en":"Young chickens are particularly vulnerable to birds of prey.","zh":"小雞對猛禽來說特別脆弱。"},{"en":"Particularly vulnerable means especially likely to be harmed or attacked.","zh":"特別脆弱是指尤其容易受傷害或被攻擊。"},{"en":"Chicks are particularly vulnerable when they are outside without cover.","zh":"小雞在戶外且沒有遮蔽物時特別脆弱。"},{"en":"Vulnerable animals need more protection than adults.","zh":"脆弱動物比成年動物需要更多保護。"},{"en":"Identifying vulnerable periods helps farmers focus their efforts.","zh":"找出脆弱時期可以幫助農民集中精力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"watch over","meaning":"看守；照看","examples":[{"en":"Children watch over the chickens during the breeding season.","zh":"兒童在繁殖季節看守雞群。"},{"en":"To watch over someone or something means to guard, supervise, or look after them.","zh":"看守某人或某物，是指守護、監督或照顧他們。"},{"en":"The farmer asked his son to watch over the chicks.","zh":"農民叫兒子看守小雞。"},{"en":"Watching over animals can prevent attacks from predators.","zh":"看守動物可以防止捕食者攻擊。"},{"en":"This responsibility can take time away from school or other work.","zh":"這項責任可能佔用上學或其他工作的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hit pans with","meaning":"用……敲打鍋子","examples":[{"en":"Children hit pans with a metal spoon to make noise.","zh":"兒童用金屬湯匙敲打鍋子來製造噪音。"},{"en":"To hit pans with something means to strike cooking pots or pans using an object.","zh":"用某物敲打鍋子，是指用物件擊打煮食鍋具。"},{"en":"Children hit pans with sticks to scare birds away.","zh":"兒童用木棍敲打鍋子來嚇走鳥類。"},{"en":"Hitting metal pans can create a loud sound.","zh":"敲打金屬鍋子可以產生很大聲響。"},{"en":"Making noise is a simple method when farmers lack expensive equipment.","zh":"當農民缺乏昂貴設備時，製造噪音是一種簡單方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a metal spoon","meaning":"金屬湯匙","examples":[{"en":"Children use a metal spoon to hit pans.","zh":"兒童用金屬湯匙敲打鍋子。"},{"en":"A metal spoon is a spoon made from metal rather than wood or plastic.","zh":"金屬湯匙是由金屬而非木或塑膠製成的湯匙。"},{"en":"A metal spoon makes a loud sound when it hits a pan.","zh":"金屬湯匙敲到鍋子時會發出很大聲響。"},{"en":"Simple metal objects can be used to scare birds away.","zh":"簡單金屬物件可以用來嚇走鳥類。"},{"en":"The tool is cheap and easy for children to use.","zh":"這種工具便宜，而且兒童容易使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the resulting noise","meaning":"由此產生的噪音","examples":[{"en":"The resulting noise can drive away birds.","zh":"由此產生的噪音可以趕走鳥類。"},{"en":"The resulting noise is the sound produced by an action just mentioned.","zh":"由此產生的噪音，是剛才提到的行動所產生的聲音。"},{"en":"The children hit the pans, and the resulting noise frightened the birds.","zh":"兒童敲打鍋子，由此產生的噪音嚇走了鳥。"},{"en":"Loud noise can interrupt a predator’s attack.","zh":"大聲噪音可以打斷捕食者的攻擊。"},{"en":"Resulting noise may work temporarily but may not solve the problem completely.","zh":"由此產生的噪音可能暫時有效，但未必完全解決問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"succeed in driving away","meaning":"成功趕走","examples":[{"en":"The noise may succeed in driving away birds.","zh":"噪音可能成功趕走鳥類。"},{"en":"To succeed in driving away something means to manage to make it leave.","zh":"成功趕走某物，是指能令它離開。"},{"en":"The dogs succeeded in driving away the predators.","zh":"狗成功趕走了捕食者。"},{"en":"A method may succeed once but fail later if animals become used to it.","zh":"一種方法可能一次成功，但如果動物習慣了，之後可能失效。"},{"en":"Success should be measured by whether chickens remain safe.","zh":"是否成功應以雞是否保持安全來衡量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"seize the young chicks","meaning":"抓走小雞","examples":[{"en":"Birds may try to seize the young chicks.","zh":"鳥類可能嘗試抓走小雞。"},{"en":"To seize young chicks means to grab or snatch them quickly.","zh":"抓走小雞是指快速抓住或叼走牠們。"},{"en":"A hawk may swoop down and seize a young chick.","zh":"隼可能俯衝下來抓走小雞。"},{"en":"Young chicks are easier to seize because they are small and weak.","zh":"小雞體型小又脆弱，因此較容易被抓走。"},{"en":"Farmers try to prevent predators from seizing chicks during the breeding season.","zh":"農民在繁殖季節嘗試防止捕食者抓走小雞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a hundred per cent effective","meaning":"百分之百有效","examples":[{"en":"None of the methods was a hundred per cent effective.","zh":"沒有任何方法是百分之百有效的。"},{"en":"A hundred per cent effective means working perfectly every time.","zh":"百分之百有效是指每次都完全奏效。"},{"en":"No scare method is a hundred per cent effective against predators.","zh":"沒有任何驅嚇方法對捕食者百分之百有效。"},{"en":"A method can help even if it is not completely effective.","zh":"一種方法即使不是完全有效，也仍然可以有幫助。"},{"en":"When no method is perfect, people may combine several methods.","zh":"當沒有方法完美時，人們可能會結合幾種方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, villagers use more than one method.","zh":"因此，村民使用不止一種方法。"},{"en":"“As a result” introduces the effect or consequence of what was just said.","zh":"「因此」用來引入剛才所說事情的結果或後果。"},{"en":"No single method worked fully; as a result, farmers combined several methods.","zh":"沒有單一方法完全奏效；因此，農民結合多種方法。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly connects cause and effect.","zh":"這個說法清楚連接原因和結果。"},{"en":"It is useful in reports and explanations.","zh":"它適合用於報告和解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rather than just using one method","meaning":"而不是只使用一種方法","examples":[{"en":"Farmers use several methods rather than just using one method.","zh":"農民使用幾種方法，而不是只使用一種方法。"},{"en":"“Rather than just using one method” means choosing multiple approaches instead of relying on only one.","zh":"「而不是只使用一種方法」表示選擇多種做法，而非只依靠一種。"},{"en":"Farmers use dogs and noise rather than just using one method.","zh":"農民使用狗和噪音，而不是只使用一種方法。"},{"en":"Combining methods can reduce risk when each method has limits.","zh":"當每種方法都有局限，結合方法可以減少風險。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts a stronger approach with a weaker single approach.","zh":"這個說法把較強做法與較弱的單一做法作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be forced to use","meaning":"被迫使用","examples":[{"en":"The villagers are forced to use a combination of methods.","zh":"村民被迫使用多種方法的結合。"},{"en":"To be forced to use something means to have no real choice except to use it.","zh":"被迫使用某物，是指除了使用它之外幾乎沒有真正選擇。"},{"en":"Farmers were forced to use several methods because predators kept returning.","zh":"因為捕食者不斷回來，農民被迫使用幾種方法。"},{"en":"Economic pressure can force people to choose difficult solutions.","zh":"經濟壓力可以迫使人們選擇困難方案。"},{"en":"Being forced to use a method suggests that the situation is serious.","zh":"被迫使用某方法暗示情況嚴重。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a combination of methods","meaning":"多種方法的結合","examples":[{"en":"A combination of methods is usually needed.","zh":"通常需要多種方法的結合。"},{"en":"A combination of methods means two or more approaches used together.","zh":"多種方法的結合，是指同時使用兩種或以上做法。"},{"en":"Farmers used a combination of dogs, noise, and supervision.","zh":"農民使用狗、噪音和看守等多種方法的結合。"},{"en":"A combination of methods may work better than one method alone.","zh":"多種方法的結合可能比單一方法更有效。"},{"en":"The best combination depends on cost, risk, and local conditions.","zh":"最佳組合取決於成本、風險和本地環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have any effect","meaning":"有任何效果","examples":[{"en":"The methods need to be combined to have any effect.","zh":"這些方法需要結合起來才有任何效果。"},{"en":"To have any effect means to produce at least some result or influence.","zh":"有任何效果，是指至少產生一些結果或影響。"},{"en":"Noise alone did not have much effect after the birds became used to it.","zh":"鳥類習慣後，單靠噪音沒有太大效果。"},{"en":"A method may need to be repeated or combined to have an effect.","zh":"一種方法可能需要重複或結合其他方法才有效果。"},{"en":"If a solution has no effect, it wastes time and effort.","zh":"如果解決方法沒有任何效果，就會浪費時間和精力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"even so","meaning":"即使如此","examples":[{"en":"Even so, birds of prey remain a major threat.","zh":"即使如此，猛禽仍然是一大威脅。"},{"en":"“Even so” means despite what has just been said.","zh":"「即使如此」表示儘管剛才所說情況存在。"},{"en":"Farmers use several methods; even so, some chickens are still lost.","zh":"農民使用幾種方法；即使如此，仍有一些雞被抓走。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a remaining problem after efforts have been made.","zh":"這個說法在已經作出努力後，引出仍然存在的問題。"},{"en":"It helps show that a situation is difficult to solve completely.","zh":"它有助顯示情況很難完全解決。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"remain a major threat to","meaning":"仍然是對……的一大威脅","examples":[{"en":"Birds of prey remain a major threat to chickens’ survival.","zh":"猛禽仍然是對雞群生存的一大威脅。"},{"en":"To remain a major threat to something means to continue being a serious danger to it.","zh":"仍然是對某事的一大威脅，是指繼續對它構成嚴重危險。"},{"en":"Predators remain a major threat to young chicks.","zh":"捕食者仍然是小雞的一大威脅。"},{"en":"Even with protection, birds may remain a major threat if attacks continue.","zh":"即使有保護措施，如果攻擊持續，鳥類仍可能是一大威脅。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises that the danger has not disappeared.","zh":"這個說法強調危險並未消失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"chickens’ survival","meaning":"雞群的生存","examples":[{"en":"Birds of prey threaten chickens’ survival.","zh":"猛禽威脅雞群的生存。"},{"en":"Chickens’ survival means the ability of chickens to remain alive.","zh":"雞群的生存是指雞繼續存活的能力。"},{"en":"Farmers protect shelter areas to improve chickens’ survival.","zh":"農民保護雞舍區域，以改善雞群生存機會。"},{"en":"Young chicks’ survival is especially at risk during breeding season.","zh":"小雞在繁殖季節的生存尤其面臨風險。"},{"en":"Protecting chickens’ survival also protects farmers’ food and income.","zh":"保護雞群的生存，也是在保護農民的食物和收入。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"considerable economic loss","meaning":"相當大的經濟損失","examples":[{"en":"The birds cause considerable economic loss to farmers.","zh":"這些鳥令農民蒙受相當大的經濟損失。"},{"en":"Considerable economic loss is a large financial loss.","zh":"相當大的經濟損失是嚴重的金錢損失。"},{"en":"Losing many chickens can cause considerable economic loss for a small farm.","zh":"失去很多雞可以令小型農場蒙受相當大的經濟損失。"},{"en":"Economic loss may include lost food, lost sales, and lost breeding stock.","zh":"經濟損失可能包括失去食物、銷售收入和繁殖用雞。"},{"en":"Even a small number of attacks can be serious for poor farmers.","zh":"即使攻擊次數不多，對貧困農民來說也可能很嚴重。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"look at the possibility of","meaning":"研究……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"The researchers looked at the possibility of a longer-term solution.","zh":"研究人員研究較長遠解決方案的可能性。"},{"en":"To look at the possibility of something means to consider or investigate whether it could happen.","zh":"研究某事的可能性，是指考慮或調查它是否可以發生。"},{"en":"The team looked at the possibility of changing chicken shelters.","zh":"團隊研究改變雞舍的可能性。"},{"en":"Looking at possibilities helps researchers compare solutions.","zh":"研究不同可能性可以幫助研究人員比較解決方案。"},{"en":"A possibility should be tested before it is recommended.","zh":"一個可能方案應先測試，才被推薦。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a longer-term solution","meaning":"較長遠的解決方案","examples":[{"en":"The researchers considered a longer-term solution.","zh":"研究人員考慮較長遠的解決方案。"},{"en":"A longer-term solution is a plan that aims to solve a problem over a longer period.","zh":"較長遠的解決方案，是旨在較長時間內解決問題的計劃。"},{"en":"Training farmers may be a longer-term solution than simply scaring birds away.","zh":"培訓農民可能比單純嚇走鳥類更像較長遠的解決方案。"},{"en":"Longer-term solutions often require planning, trust, and resources.","zh":"長遠方案通常需要規劃、信任和資源。"},{"en":"A short-term method may reduce damage now, but a longer-term solution addresses the cause.","zh":"短期方法可以暫時減少損害，但長遠方案會處理成因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Research in the Area Around","meaning":"關於……周邊地區的研究","examples":[{"en":"The question section is about research in the area around the Chembe Bird Sanctuary.","zh":"問題部分是關於Chembe鳥類保護區周邊地區的研究。"},{"en":"“Research in the area around” means a study carried out in the surrounding region of a place.","zh":"「關於某地周邊地區的研究」是指在該地附近區域進行的研究。"},{"en":"Research in the area around the park included interviews with farmers.","zh":"關於公園周邊地區的研究包括訪問農民。"},{"en":"Studying the area around a sanctuary reveals how wildlife affects nearby residents.","zh":"研究保護區周邊地區，可以揭示野生動物如何影響附近居民。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used as a report or table heading.","zh":"這個說法常用作報告或表格標題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the importance of","meaning":"……的重要性","examples":[{"en":"The table describes the importance of birds of prey to local communities.","zh":"表格描述猛禽對本地社區的重要性。"},{"en":"The importance of something is the reason it matters or has value.","zh":"某事的重要性是指它為何重要或有價值。"},{"en":"The lecture explains the importance of predators in farming areas.","zh":"講座解釋捕食者在農業地區的重要性。"},{"en":"Understanding the importance of birds can reduce fear and misunderstanding.","zh":"了解鳥類的重要性可以減少恐懼和誤解。"},{"en":"Importance may be ecological, cultural, economic, or practical.","zh":"重要性可以是生態、文化、經濟或實際方面的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"local communities","meaning":"本地社區","examples":[{"en":"Birds of prey are important to local communities.","zh":"猛禽對本地社區很重要。"},{"en":"Local communities are people living in a particular area and sharing local resources or experiences.","zh":"本地社區是生活在特定地區並共享本地資源或經驗的人。"},{"en":"Local communities near the sanctuary know which birds appear in each season.","zh":"保護區附近的本地社區知道每個季節會出現哪些鳥。"},{"en":"Conservation works better when local communities are involved.","zh":"當本地社區參與其中，保育工作會更有效。"},{"en":"Local communities may value wildlife for culture, tourism, and practical benefits.","zh":"本地社區可能因文化、旅遊和實際好處而重視野生動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"help to prevent farmers from","meaning":"幫助防止農民……","examples":[{"en":"The birds help to prevent farmers from being bitten by snakes.","zh":"這些鳥幫助防止農民被蛇咬。"},{"en":"To help prevent someone from something means to reduce the chance that it will happen to them.","zh":"幫助防止某人遇到某事，是指減少該事發生在他們身上的機會。"},{"en":"Birds of prey help prevent farmers from facing too many snakes.","zh":"猛禽幫助防止農民面對過多蛇類。"},{"en":"Protective clothing can help prevent workers from being injured.","zh":"防護衣物可以幫助防止工人受傷。"},{"en":"Prevention is valuable because it reduces danger before harm occurs.","zh":"預防很有價值，因為它在傷害發生前減少危險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be bitten by","meaning":"被……咬","examples":[{"en":"Farmers may be bitten by snakes.","zh":"農民可能被蛇咬。"},{"en":"To be bitten by an animal means to be injured when the animal uses its teeth or fangs.","zh":"被動物咬，是指動物用牙齒或毒牙造成傷害。"},{"en":"A rural worker was bitten by a snake while walking through tall grass.","zh":"一名農村工作者穿過高草時被蛇咬。"},{"en":"Being bitten by a poisonous snake can be extremely dangerous.","zh":"被毒蛇咬可能極其危險。"},{"en":"Reducing snake numbers may lower the chance of workers being bitten.","zh":"減少蛇的數量可能降低工人被咬的機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"support the economy by","meaning":"透過……支持經濟","examples":[{"en":"The birds now support the economy by encouraging tourism.","zh":"這些鳥現在透過促進旅遊業支持經濟。"},{"en":"To support the economy by doing something means to help income, jobs, or business through that activity.","zh":"透過做某事支持經濟，是指透過該活動幫助收入、職位或生意。"},{"en":"The sanctuary supports the economy by attracting visitors.","zh":"保護區透過吸引遊客支持經濟。"},{"en":"Wildlife can support the local economy when tourists spend money nearby.","zh":"當遊客在附近消費，野生動物可以支持本地經濟。"},{"en":"Economic support from tourism can make conservation more valuable to residents.","zh":"旅遊業帶來的經濟支持可以令居民更重視保育。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"encourage tourism","meaning":"促進旅遊業","examples":[{"en":"The sanctuary encourages tourism in the area.","zh":"該保護區促進該地區的旅遊業。"},{"en":"To encourage tourism means to attract visitors and make travel to a place more likely.","zh":"促進旅遊業，是指吸引遊客並增加人們到訪某地的可能性。"},{"en":"Rare birds can encourage tourism by drawing birdwatchers.","zh":"稀有鳥類可以透過吸引觀鳥者來促進旅遊業。"},{"en":"Tourism can create jobs for guides, drivers, and guesthouse owners.","zh":"旅遊業可以為導遊、司機和旅館經營者創造職位。"},{"en":"Encouraging tourism should be balanced with protecting wildlife and local life.","zh":"促進旅遊業應與保護野生動物和本地生活取得平衡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"falling numbers of","meaning":"……數量下降","examples":[{"en":"The question focuses on falling numbers of birds of prey.","zh":"問題集中於猛禽數量下降。"},{"en":"Falling numbers of something means a decreasing population or quantity.","zh":"某物數量下降，是指種群或數量正在減少。"},{"en":"Falling numbers of owls worried conservationists.","zh":"貓頭鷹數量下降令保育人士擔心。"},{"en":"Falling numbers may show that threats are increasing.","zh":"數量下降可能顯示威脅正在增加。"},{"en":"Monitoring falling numbers helps scientists decide when action is urgent.","zh":"監察數量下降可以幫助科學家判斷何時需要緊急行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be accidentally killed","meaning":"被意外殺死","examples":[{"en":"The birds may be accidentally killed by traffic.","zh":"這些鳥可能被交通意外殺死。"},{"en":"To be accidentally killed means to die unintentionally because of an accident.","zh":"被意外殺死是指因意外而非故意死亡。"},{"en":"Birds can be accidentally killed when they land on roads.","zh":"鳥類降落在道路上時可能被意外殺死。"},{"en":"Accidental deaths may still be prevented with better awareness.","zh":"透過提高意識，意外死亡仍可能被預防。"},{"en":"A death can be accidental but still harmful to conservation efforts.","zh":"死亡即使是意外，仍會損害保育工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hunting or sleeping","meaning":"捕獵或睡覺時","examples":[{"en":"Birds may be killed while hunting or sleeping on roads.","zh":"鳥類可能在道路上捕獵或睡覺時被殺死。"},{"en":"Hunting or sleeping refers to two possible behaviours birds may perform on roads.","zh":"捕獵或睡覺是鳥類可能在道路上進行的兩種行為。"},{"en":"Birds are vulnerable while hunting or sleeping because they may not notice vehicles.","zh":"鳥類在捕獵或睡覺時很脆弱，因為牠們可能沒有注意到車輛。"},{"en":"Roads can attract birds during hunting or resting periods.","zh":"道路可能在鳥類捕獵或休息時吸引牠們。"},{"en":"Understanding when birds are hunting or sleeping can help reduce traffic deaths.","zh":"了解鳥類何時捕獵或睡覺，可以幫助減少交通死亡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"contact with power lines","meaning":"接觸電線","examples":[{"en":"Electrocution can result from contact with power lines.","zh":"觸電死亡可能由接觸電線造成。"},{"en":"Contact with power lines means touching or coming too close to electrical cables.","zh":"接觸電線是指碰到或過度接近電纜。"},{"en":"Large birds risk death through contact with power lines.","zh":"大型鳥類可能因接觸電線而死亡。"},{"en":"Contact with electrical equipment is especially dangerous in wet conditions.","zh":"在潮濕環境中，接觸電力設備尤其危險。"},{"en":"Insulating dangerous parts can reduce harmful contact.","zh":"為危險部分加上絕緣保護可以減少有害接觸。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"especially at times when","meaning":"尤其在……的時候","examples":[{"en":"The danger is greater especially at times when there is a lot of rain.","zh":"尤其在大量下雨的時候，危險更大。"},{"en":"“Especially at times when” highlights periods when something is particularly true.","zh":"「尤其在……的時候」突出某事特別成立的時段。"},{"en":"Roads are dangerous especially at times when visibility is poor.","zh":"尤其在能見度差的時候，道路很危險。"},{"en":"The phrase helps identify when a risk is highest.","zh":"這個說法有助指出風險最高的時候。"},{"en":"It is useful for explaining seasonal or temporary dangers.","zh":"它適合用來解釋季節性或暫時性危險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a lot of rain","meaning":"大量雨水","examples":[{"en":"Power lines are especially dangerous when there is a lot of rain.","zh":"當有大量雨水時，電線尤其危險。"},{"en":"A lot of rain means a large amount of rainfall.","zh":"大量雨水是指降雨量很大。"},{"en":"A lot of rain can make roads slippery and fields muddy.","zh":"大量雨水可以令道路濕滑、田地泥濘。"},{"en":"Electrical dangers may increase when there is a lot of rain.","zh":"當有大量雨水時，電力危險可能增加。"},{"en":"Farmers and drivers should take extra care during heavy rainfall.","zh":"在大雨期間，農民和司機應格外小心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ways of protecting","meaning":"保護……的方法","examples":[{"en":"The question table lists ways of protecting chickens.","zh":"問題表格列出保護雞的方法。"},{"en":"Ways of protecting something are methods used to keep it safe.","zh":"保護某物的方法，是用來保持其安全的做法。"},{"en":"Farmers discussed different ways of protecting young chicks.","zh":"農民討論保護小雞的不同方法。"},{"en":"Some ways of protecting chickens are cheap but not completely effective.","zh":"有些保護雞的方法便宜，但不完全有效。"},{"en":"A good protection plan often combines several methods.","zh":"良好的保護計劃通常會結合多種方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"clearing away vegetation","meaning":"清除植被","examples":[{"en":"Clearing away vegetation from the area is unhelpful.","zh":"從該區域清除植被沒有幫助。"},{"en":"Clearing away vegetation means removing plants, grass, or bushes from an area.","zh":"清除植被是指移除某地的植物、草或灌木。"},{"en":"Farmers cleared away vegetation to see predators more easily.","zh":"農民清除植被，以便更容易看見捕食者。"},{"en":"Clearing vegetation may remove hiding places for chickens.","zh":"清除植被可能移除雞的躲藏地方。"},{"en":"A method that looks protective may actually make animals more vulnerable.","zh":"看似保護性的做法，實際上可能令動物更脆弱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be unhelpful","meaning":"沒有幫助","examples":[{"en":"Clearing away vegetation is unhelpful.","zh":"清除植被沒有幫助。"},{"en":"If something is unhelpful, it does not improve the situation and may make it worse.","zh":"某事沒有幫助，是指它沒有改善情況，甚至可能令情況更差。"},{"en":"Removing all cover was unhelpful because chicks had nowhere to hide.","zh":"移除所有遮蔽物沒有幫助，因為小雞沒有地方躲藏。"},{"en":"An unhelpful solution wastes time and effort.","zh":"沒有幫助的方案會浪費時間和精力。"},{"en":"Evaluating results helps people stop using unhelpful methods.","zh":"評估結果可以幫助人們停止使用無效方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"providing a building for","meaning":"為……提供建築物","examples":[{"en":"Providing a building for chickens would be expensive.","zh":"為雞提供建築物會很昂貴。"},{"en":"Providing a building for animals means constructing or supplying an indoor space for them.","zh":"為動物提供建築物，是指建造或供應室內空間給牠們。"},{"en":"Providing a building for chickens could protect them from birds of prey.","zh":"為雞提供建築物可以保護牠們免受猛禽攻擊。"},{"en":"Buildings require money, materials, cleaning, and maintenance.","zh":"建築物需要金錢、材料、清潔和維修。"},{"en":"A solution may be safe but too expensive for small-scale farmers.","zh":"一個方案可能安全，但對小規模農民來說太昂貴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"frightening birds of prey by","meaning":"透過……嚇走猛禽","examples":[{"en":"Farmers try frightening birds of prey by using dogs and noise.","zh":"農民嘗試透過使用狗和噪音嚇走猛禽。"},{"en":"“Frightening birds of prey by” introduces the method used to scare the birds away.","zh":"「透過……嚇走猛禽」用來引入驅趕鳥類的方法。"},{"en":"Farmers frightened birds of prey by shouting and hitting pans.","zh":"農民透過叫喊和敲打鍋子嚇走猛禽。"},{"en":"Non-harmful frightening methods can reduce attacks without breaking wildlife laws.","zh":"非傷害性的驅嚇方法可以減少攻擊，而且不違反野生動物法例。"},{"en":"The method may need to change if birds become used to it.","zh":"如果鳥類習慣了，方法可能需要改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"making a noise","meaning":"發出噪音","examples":[{"en":"Children make a noise with metal objects to scare birds away.","zh":"兒童用金屬物件發出噪音來嚇走鳥類。"},{"en":"Making a noise means producing sound, often loudly.","zh":"發出噪音是指製造聲音，通常是較大的聲音。"},{"en":"Farmers tried making a noise to frighten the birds.","zh":"農民嘗試發出噪音來嚇走鳥類。"},{"en":"Loud noises can interrupt predators before they seize chicks.","zh":"大聲噪音可以在捕食者抓走小雞前打斷牠們。"},{"en":"Making noise is simple, but it may not work every time.","zh":"發出噪音很簡單，但未必每次有效。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"metal objects","meaning":"金屬物件","examples":[{"en":"Metal objects can be used to make a noise.","zh":"金屬物件可以用來發出噪音。"},{"en":"Metal objects are things made of metal, such as pans, spoons, or tins.","zh":"金屬物件是由金屬製成的東西，例如鍋子、湯匙或罐子。"},{"en":"Children hit metal objects together to scare birds away.","zh":"兒童把金屬物件互相敲打來嚇走鳥。"},{"en":"Metal objects often produce sharp, loud sounds.","zh":"金屬物件通常會發出尖銳而響亮的聲音。"},{"en":"Simple metal objects can be useful when farmers lack expensive tools.","zh":"當農民缺乏昂貴工具時，簡單金屬物件也很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"usually most effective","meaning":"通常最有效","examples":[{"en":"A combination of methods is usually most effective.","zh":"多種方法的結合通常最有效。"},{"en":"“Usually most effective” means generally works better than other options in most cases.","zh":"「通常最有效」表示在多數情況下一般比其他選項更有用。"},{"en":"Using dogs, noise, and supervision together is usually most effective.","zh":"同時使用狗、噪音和看守通常最有效。"},{"en":"A method may be most effective because it solves several parts of the problem at once.","zh":"一種方法可能因同時解決問題的幾個部分而最有效。"},{"en":"What is usually most effective should still be tested in local conditions.","zh":"通常最有效的做法仍應在本地環境中測試。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 4 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/listening/Practice 5/task-1":[{"front":"country park","meaning":"郊野公園","examples":[{"en":"Hinchingbrooke Country Park offers educational visits for schools.","zh":"Hinchingbrooke 郊野公園為學校提供教育參觀活動。"},{"en":"A country park is a large outdoor area where people can walk, learn about nature, and enjoy open space.","zh":"郊野公園是一大片戶外地方，人們可以散步、認識大自然和享受開放空間。"},{"en":"Families may visit a country park at the weekend to see trees, lakes, and wildlife.","zh":"家庭可能在週末到郊野公園看樹木、湖泊和野生生物。"},{"en":"A country park can protect habitats while also giving visitors places to explore.","zh":"郊野公園可以保護棲息地，同時讓遊客有地方探索。"},{"en":"Schools use country parks because children can learn outdoors in a real natural environment.","zh":"學校使用郊野公園，因為孩子可以在真實自然環境中進行戶外學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Sally speaking","meaning":"我是 Sally；Sally 接聽","examples":[{"en":"Good morning. Hinchingbrooke Country Park, Sally speaking.","zh":"早晨。Hinchingbrooke 郊野公園，我是 Sally。"},{"en":"Sally speaking is a phone greeting that means Sally is the person answering the call.","zh":"Sally speaking 是電話問候語，意思是 Sally 正在接聽電話。"},{"en":"A receptionist might say, “Good afternoon, school office, Mary speaking.”","zh":"接待員可能會說：「午安，學校辦公室，我是 Mary。」"},{"en":"Sally says this so the caller knows both the place and the person on the phone.","zh":"Sally 這樣說，讓來電者知道自己致電的地方和接聽者是誰。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in polite workplace phone calls.","zh":"這個短語常見於有禮貌的工作電話中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one of the rangers","meaning":"其中一名巡護員","examples":[{"en":"Sally is one of the rangers at Hinchingbrooke Country Park.","zh":"Sally 是 Hinchingbrooke 郊野公園其中一名巡護員。"},{"en":"One of the rangers means one member of the group of people who look after the park.","zh":"one of the rangers 意思是照顧公園的一群工作人員中的其中一位。"},{"en":"One of the rangers may guide visitors through the woodland.","zh":"其中一名巡護員可能會帶領遊客穿過林地。"},{"en":"Sally can answer John’s questions because rangers know the park well.","zh":"Sally 可以回答 John 的問題，因為巡護員很熟悉公園。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that Sally is part of a wider park staff team.","zh":"這個短語顯示 Sally 是公園員工團隊的一員。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"teaching assistant","meaning":"教學助理","examples":[{"en":"John Chapman is a teaching assistant at a local primary school.","zh":"John Chapman 是本地小學的一名教學助理。"},{"en":"A teaching assistant is a school worker who helps teachers and supports pupils in class.","zh":"教學助理是在學校幫助老師並支援學生上課的人員。"},{"en":"A teaching assistant may help children read, prepare materials, or join group activities.","zh":"教學助理可能幫孩子閱讀、準備教材或參與小組活動。"},{"en":"John arranges the visit because teaching assistants often help with school trips.","zh":"John 安排參觀，因為教學助理常協助學校旅行。"},{"en":"This role supports learning but is different from being the main class teacher.","zh":"這個角色支援學習，但不同於主要班主任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"local primary school","meaning":"本地小學","examples":[{"en":"John works at a local primary school.","zh":"John 在一間本地小學工作。"},{"en":"A local primary school is a nearby school for young children.","zh":"本地小學是附近給年幼孩子就讀的學校。"},{"en":"Parents often choose a local primary school because it is close to home.","zh":"家長常選擇本地小學，因為它靠近家。"},{"en":"John’s school wants to visit the park because it is in the same area.","zh":"John 的學校想參觀公園，因為公園也在同一地區。"},{"en":"This phrase tells us both the type of school and its connection to the community.","zh":"這個短語告訴我們學校類型，以及它與社區的關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"I’ve been asked to","meaning":"我被要求去……","examples":[{"en":"I’ve been asked to arrange a visit to the park for two of our classes.","zh":"我被要求為我們其中兩個班級安排到公園參觀。"},{"en":"I’ve been asked to means someone has requested or instructed me to do something.","zh":"I’ve been asked to 意思是有人請我或要求我做某事。"},{"en":"I’ve been asked to collect the forms before Friday.","zh":"我被要求在星期五前收集表格。"},{"en":"John uses this phrase because the school has given him the task of organising the visit.","zh":"John 使用這個短語，因為學校給了他安排參觀的任務。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the task comes from someone else.","zh":"這個短語顯示任務來自別人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"arrange a visit to","meaning":"安排參觀……","examples":[{"en":"John has been asked to arrange a visit to the park.","zh":"John 被要求安排參觀公園。"},{"en":"To arrange a visit to a place means to organise the date, details, and activities for going there.","zh":"arrange a visit to a place 意思是組織前往某地的日期、細節和活動。"},{"en":"A teacher may arrange a visit to a museum for history students.","zh":"老師可能為歷史學生安排參觀博物館。"},{"en":"John needs to ask about activities and costs before the school can visit.","zh":"John 需要先詢問活動和費用，學校才能前往參觀。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when planning educational trips or group outings.","zh":"這個短語適合用於計劃教育旅行或團體外出活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"two of our classes","meaning":"我們其中兩個班級","examples":[{"en":"John is arranging a visit for two of his school’s classes.","zh":"John 正為他學校其中兩個班級安排參觀。"},{"en":"Two of our classes means two classes from our school or organisation.","zh":"two of our classes 意思是我們學校或機構中的兩個班級。"},{"en":"Two of our classes will visit the science centre next month.","zh":"我們其中兩個班級下個月會參觀科學中心。"},{"en":"John needs details because bringing two classes means many children will attend.","zh":"John 需要細節，因為帶兩個班級代表會有很多孩子出席。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies part of a larger school group.","zh":"這個短語指出較大學校群體中的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"What would you like to know?","meaning":"你想知道甚麼？","examples":[{"en":"Sally asks John, “What would you like to know?”","zh":"Sally 問 John：「你想知道甚麼？」"},{"en":"What would you like to know? is a polite question asking what information someone needs.","zh":"What would you like to know? 是禮貌地問某人需要甚麼資料。"},{"en":"A librarian may ask, “What would you like to know?” when helping a student research.","zh":"圖書館主任幫學生做資料搜集時，可能會問：「你想知道甚麼？」"},{"en":"Sally asks this because John is planning a school visit and needs details.","zh":"Sally 這樣問，因為 John 正在計劃學校參觀，需要細節。"},{"en":"This phrase invites the other person to ask questions.","zh":"這個短語邀請對方提出問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"new to this area","meaning":"剛來這個地區","examples":[{"en":"John is new to this area, so he asks Sally about the park.","zh":"John 剛來這個地區，所以他向 Sally 詢問公園資料。"},{"en":"New to this area means someone has recently arrived and does not know the local place well.","zh":"new to this area 意思是某人最近才來到，對本地地方不太熟悉。"},{"en":"A family that is new to this area may ask neighbours where the supermarket is.","zh":"剛來這個地區的家庭可能會問鄰居超級市場在哪裏。"},{"en":"John needs Sally’s help because he is not familiar with the park or neighbourhood.","zh":"John 需要 Sally 幫忙，因為他不熟悉公園或附近地區。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why someone needs local information.","zh":"這個短語解釋為甚麼某人需要本地資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"perhaps you could tell me","meaning":"也許你可以告訴我","examples":[{"en":"Perhaps you could tell me something about the park first.","zh":"也許你可以先告訴我一些關於這個公園的資料。"},{"en":"Perhaps you could tell me is a polite way to ask someone for information.","zh":"Perhaps you could tell me 是禮貌地向某人詢問資料的方式。"},{"en":"Perhaps you could tell me how long the tour takes.","zh":"也許你可以告訴我導賞需時多久。"},{"en":"John uses this phrase because he wants basic information before asking detailed questions.","zh":"John 使用這個短語，因為他想先了解基本資料，再問詳細問題。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds more polite than simply saying “tell me.”","zh":"這個短語比直接說「告訴我」更有禮貌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"something about the park","meaning":"關於這個公園的一些資料","examples":[{"en":"John asks Sally to tell him something about the park.","zh":"John 請 Sally 告訴他關於這個公園的一些資料。"},{"en":"Something about the park means some general information about the park.","zh":"something about the park 意思是關於公園的一些基本資料。"},{"en":"A visitor may ask for something about the park before choosing a walking route.","zh":"遊客選擇步行路線前，可能會詢問關於公園的一些資料。"},{"en":"John wants to know the park’s size, habitats, and activities.","zh":"John 想知道公園的面積、棲息地和活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when someone wants a basic introduction.","zh":"這個短語用於某人想得到基本介紹時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"altogether","meaning":"總共；整體而言","examples":[{"en":"Altogether the park covers 170 acres.","zh":"這個公園總共佔地 170 英畝。"},{"en":"Altogether means in total or when everything is counted together.","zh":"altogether 意思是總共或把所有東西計算在一起。"},{"en":"Altogether, the trip will cost about fifty pounds per child.","zh":"總共來說，這次旅行每名孩子大約花費五十英鎊。"},{"en":"Sally uses this word before giving the full size of the park.","zh":"Sally 在說出公園總面積前使用這個字。"},{"en":"This word helps give a total amount clearly.","zh":"這個字幫助清楚說出總數。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"covers 170 acres","meaning":"佔地 170 英畝","examples":[{"en":"The park covers 170 acres.","zh":"這個公園佔地 170 英畝。"},{"en":"Covers 170 acres means has an area of 170 acres.","zh":"covers 170 acres 意思是面積達 170 英畝。"},{"en":"The farm covers fifty acres of land.","zh":"這個農場佔地五十英畝。"},{"en":"Because the park covers 170 acres, it has space for lakes, woods, and grassland.","zh":"因為公園佔地 170 英畝，所以有空間容納湖泊、林地和草地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the size of a piece of land.","zh":"這個短語描述一片土地的大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hectares","meaning":"公頃","examples":[{"en":"The park covers 69 hectares.","zh":"這個公園佔地 69 公頃。"},{"en":"Hectares are units used to measure large areas of land.","zh":"hectares 是用來量度大面積土地的單位。"},{"en":"A nature reserve may cover hundreds of hectares.","zh":"自然保護區可能佔地數百公頃。"},{"en":"Saying the park covers 69 hectares helps people understand its size in metric units.","zh":"說公園佔地 69 公頃，有助人們用公制單位理解它的大小。"},{"en":"This word is often used for parks, farms, forests, and land planning.","zh":"這個字常用於公園、農場、森林和土地規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"main types of habitat","meaning":"主要棲息地類型","examples":[{"en":"There are three main types of habitat in the park.","zh":"公園內有三種主要棲息地類型。"},{"en":"Main types of habitat means the most important kinds of natural places where plants and animals live.","zh":"main types of habitat 意思是植物和動物生活的最重要自然環境種類。"},{"en":"A nature reserve may have main types of habitat such as forest, marsh, and grassland.","zh":"自然保護區可能有森林、沼澤和草地等主要棲息地類型。"},{"en":"Knowing the habitats helps teachers plan science activities for children.","zh":"知道棲息地有助老師為孩子計劃科學活動。"},{"en":"This phrase groups natural environments by their features.","zh":"這個短語按特徵把自然環境分類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"wetland","meaning":"濕地","examples":[{"en":"Wetland is one of the main types of habitat in the park.","zh":"濕地是公園內其中一種主要棲息地。"},{"en":"A wetland is an area of land that is covered with water or has very wet soil.","zh":"濕地是被水覆蓋或泥土非常濕的土地區域。"},{"en":"Wetlands often support birds, insects, fish, and water plants.","zh":"濕地常支援鳥類、昆蟲、魚類和水生植物。"},{"en":"Children can study wetland life by looking at ponds, lakes, and streams.","zh":"孩子可以透過觀察池塘、湖泊和小溪來研究濕地生命。"},{"en":"Wetland habitats are important because many species depend on water.","zh":"濕地棲息地很重要，因為許多物種依賴水。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"grassland","meaning":"草地","examples":[{"en":"Grassland is one of the habitats in the park.","zh":"草地是公園內其中一種棲息地。"},{"en":"Grassland is open land mainly covered with grass.","zh":"草地是主要被草覆蓋的開放土地。"},{"en":"Rabbits, insects, and ground-nesting birds may live in grassland.","zh":"兔子、昆蟲和在地面築巢的鳥類可能生活在草地。"},{"en":"Children can compare grassland with woodland to see how different habitats support different life.","zh":"孩子可以比較草地和林地，看看不同棲息地如何支援不同生命。"},{"en":"Grassland is useful for outdoor learning because it is open and easy to observe.","zh":"草地適合戶外學習，因為它開闊而容易觀察。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"woodland","meaning":"林地","examples":[{"en":"Woodland is one of the main habitats in the park.","zh":"林地是公園內其中一種主要棲息地。"},{"en":"Woodland is an area of land covered with many trees.","zh":"林地是被許多樹木覆蓋的土地區域。"},{"en":"Birds may build nests in woodland, and insects may live under fallen leaves.","zh":"鳥類可能在林地築巢，昆蟲可能生活在落葉下。"},{"en":"The park’s woodland gives children a place to study trees and forest animals.","zh":"公園的林地給孩子一個研究樹木和森林動物的地方。"},{"en":"Woodland habitats are usually cooler and darker than open grassland.","zh":"林地棲息地通常比開放草地更涼和更陰暗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"well established","meaning":"發展成熟的","examples":[{"en":"The woods are well established and varied.","zh":"這些樹林發展成熟而且多樣化。"},{"en":"Well established means developed over a long time and now stable or strong.","zh":"well established 意思是經長時間發展，現在穩定或成熟。"},{"en":"A well-established garden has mature trees and healthy plants.","zh":"發展成熟的花園有成熟樹木和健康植物。"},{"en":"The woods are well established, so they provide good habitats for wildlife.","zh":"這些樹林發展成熟，所以為野生生物提供良好棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that something is not new or temporary.","zh":"這個短語暗示某物不是新的或暫時的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"varied","meaning":"多樣化的","examples":[{"en":"The woods and wetlands are varied.","zh":"樹林和濕地都很多樣化。"},{"en":"Varied means having many different types or forms.","zh":"varied 意思是有許多不同種類或形式。"},{"en":"A varied school lunch menu includes rice, noodles, fruit, and vegetables.","zh":"多樣化的學校午餐餐牌包括飯、麵、水果和蔬菜。"},{"en":"Varied habitats support more kinds of plants and animals.","zh":"多樣化的棲息地支援更多種類的植物和動物。"},{"en":"This word shows that something is not all the same.","zh":"這個字顯示某物並非全部一樣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"oak plantation","meaning":"橡樹種植林","examples":[{"en":"The woods include an oak plantation.","zh":"這些樹林包括一片橡樹種植林。"},{"en":"An oak plantation is an area where oak trees have been planted together.","zh":"oak plantation 是橡樹被一起種植的地方。"},{"en":"An oak plantation may provide acorns for birds and small mammals.","zh":"橡樹種植林可能為鳥類和小型哺乳動物提供橡果。"},{"en":"Children can visit the oak plantation to learn how planted woodland develops.","zh":"孩子可以參觀橡樹種植林，了解人工種植林地如何發展。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific type of tree area.","zh":"這個短語指出一種特定樹木區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mixed species","meaning":"混合物種；混合樹種","examples":[{"en":"Some areas of the woods contain mixed species.","zh":"樹林中有些區域包含混合樹種。"},{"en":"Mixed species means different kinds of plants or trees growing together.","zh":"mixed species 意思是不同種類的植物或樹木一起生長。"},{"en":"A mixed-species forest may include oak, birch, and pine trees.","zh":"混合樹種森林可能包括橡樹、樺樹和松樹。"},{"en":"Mixed species can make woodland healthier because different animals use different plants.","zh":"混合物種可以令林地更健康，因為不同動物會使用不同植物。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an area is not made up of only one kind of tree or organism.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個區域不是只由一種樹或生物組成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"original farmland","meaning":"原本的農地","examples":[{"en":"The original farmland was dug up around 40 years ago.","zh":"原本的農地大約 40 年前被挖開。"},{"en":"Original farmland means the land was first used for farming before it changed.","zh":"original farmland 意思是土地在改變前最初用於耕作。"},{"en":"A housing estate may be built on original farmland outside a town.","zh":"城鎮外的原本農地可能被建成屋苑。"},{"en":"The park’s lakes exist because the original farmland was later used for gravel extraction.","zh":"公園的湖泊存在，是因為原本的農地後來被用來開採礫石。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the earlier use of a piece of land.","zh":"這個短語指一片土地較早期的用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"dug up","meaning":"被挖開","examples":[{"en":"The original farmland was dug up to extract gravel.","zh":"原本的農地被挖開以開採礫石。"},{"en":"Dug up means broken open or removed by digging into the ground.","zh":"dug up 意思是土地被挖掘、打開或移走。"},{"en":"The road was dug up to repair underground pipes.","zh":"道路被挖開，以維修地下水管。"},{"en":"The farmland was dug up because workers needed to remove gravel from beneath it.","zh":"農地被挖開，因為工人需要移走地下的礫石。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes land that has been physically changed by digging.","zh":"這個短語常描述土地因挖掘而被實際改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"around 40 years ago","meaning":"大約 40 年前","examples":[{"en":"The farmland was dug up around 40 years ago.","zh":"那片農地大約 40 年前被挖開。"},{"en":"Around 40 years ago means about forty years in the past, not exactly forty.","zh":"around 40 years ago 意思是大約四十年前，不一定正好四十年。"},{"en":"The school building was opened around 40 years ago.","zh":"這座校舍大約 40 年前啟用。"},{"en":"Sally uses this phrase because the exact year is less important than the general time.","zh":"Sally 使用這個短語，因為確切年份不如大概時間重要。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate historical date.","zh":"這個短語提供大約的歷史時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"extract gravel","meaning":"開採礫石","examples":[{"en":"The farmland was dug up to extract gravel.","zh":"那片農地被挖開以開採礫石。"},{"en":"To extract gravel means to remove small stones from the ground for use in building or roads.","zh":"extract gravel 意思是從地下取出小石子，用於建築或道路。"},{"en":"Workers may extract gravel from old riverbeds.","zh":"工人可能從舊河床開採礫石。"},{"en":"The land changed because gravel extraction left deep pits behind.","zh":"土地因開採礫石而改變，因為採石後留下深坑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking a natural material out of the earth.","zh":"這個短語描述把天然材料從地中取出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"once this work was completed","meaning":"這項工程完成後","examples":[{"en":"Once this work was completed, the gravel pits filled with water.","zh":"這項工程完成後，礫石坑積滿了水。"},{"en":"Once this work was completed means after this job had been finished.","zh":"once this work was completed 意思是這項工作完成之後。"},{"en":"Once the road work was completed, buses could use the street again.","zh":"道路工程完成後，巴士可以再次使用那條街。"},{"en":"After gravel extraction ended, the empty pits began to fill naturally with water.","zh":"開採礫石結束後，空坑開始自然積水。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one event happened after another was finished.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事在另一件事完成後發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"gravel pits","meaning":"礫石坑","examples":[{"en":"The gravel pits filled with water and formed lakes.","zh":"礫石坑積滿水後形成湖泊。"},{"en":"Gravel pits are holes or open areas left after gravel has been dug out.","zh":"gravel pits 是礫石被挖走後留下的坑洞或開放區域。"},{"en":"Old gravel pits can sometimes become ponds or nature reserves.","zh":"舊礫石坑有時可以變成池塘或自然保護區。"},{"en":"In the park, the gravel pits became part of the wetland habitat.","zh":"在公園裏，礫石坑變成濕地棲息地的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes land shaped by mining or extraction.","zh":"這個短語描述因採礦或開採而形成的土地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"filled with water","meaning":"積滿水","examples":[{"en":"The gravel pits filled with water.","zh":"礫石坑積滿了水。"},{"en":"Filled with water means became full of water.","zh":"filled with water 意思是變得充滿水。"},{"en":"After heavy rain, the empty field filled with water.","zh":"大雨後，空地積滿了水。"},{"en":"The gravel pits filled with water and later became lakes for wildlife.","zh":"礫石坑積滿水後，後來成為野生生物使用的湖泊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a space becoming occupied by water.","zh":"這個短語描述一個空間被水填滿。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"forming the two large lakes","meaning":"形成兩個大湖","examples":[{"en":"The gravel pits filled with water, forming the two large lakes.","zh":"礫石坑積滿水，形成兩個大湖。"},{"en":"Forming the two large lakes means creating two big lakes as a result.","zh":"forming the two large lakes 意思是結果創造出兩個大湖。"},{"en":"Rainwater collected in the valley, forming a small lake.","zh":"雨水聚集在山谷中，形成一個小湖。"},{"en":"The old gravel pits changed into lakes when they filled with water.","zh":"舊礫石坑在積滿水後變成湖泊。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the result of a natural or physical process.","zh":"這個短語顯示自然或物理過程的結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ponds","meaning":"池塘","examples":[{"en":"The wetland includes lakes, ponds and a stream.","zh":"濕地包括湖泊、池塘和小溪。"},{"en":"Ponds are small areas of still water, usually smaller than lakes.","zh":"池塘是小片靜止水域，通常比湖泊細。"},{"en":"Frogs, insects, and water plants often live in ponds.","zh":"青蛙、昆蟲和水生植物常生活在池塘中。"},{"en":"Children can study pond life by carefully observing the water’s edge.","zh":"孩子可以透過小心觀察水邊來研究池塘生命。"},{"en":"Ponds are useful habitats because many small creatures depend on them.","zh":"池塘是有用棲息地，因為許多小生物依賴它們。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a stream","meaning":"小溪","examples":[{"en":"A stream flows through the park.","zh":"一條小溪流經公園。"},{"en":"A stream is a small narrow river.","zh":"小溪是一條細而窄的河流。"},{"en":"Children may follow a stream to learn how water moves through a landscape.","zh":"孩子可能沿著小溪走，學習水如何流經地貌。"},{"en":"The stream adds another wet habitat for plants and animals.","zh":"小溪為植物和動物增加另一種濕潤棲息地。"},{"en":"A stream can connect ponds, lakes, and other parts of a park.","zh":"小溪可以連接池塘、湖泊和公園其他部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"flows through","meaning":"流經……","examples":[{"en":"A stream flows through the park.","zh":"一條小溪流經公園。"},{"en":"Flows through means moves through a place as a liquid or stream.","zh":"flows through 意思是液體或溪流穿過某個地方。"},{"en":"A river flows through the centre of the city.","zh":"一條河流流經市中心。"},{"en":"The stream flows through the park and supports wetland wildlife.","zh":"小溪流經公園，支援濕地野生生物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement from one part of an area to another.","zh":"這個短語描述從一個區域的一部分流到另一部分的移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"different habitats","meaning":"不同棲息地","examples":[{"en":"The park has several different habitats.","zh":"公園有幾種不同棲息地。"},{"en":"Different habitats are different natural places where plants and animals live.","zh":"different habitats 是植物和動物生活的不同自然地方。"},{"en":"A beach, a forest, and a pond are different habitats.","zh":"海灘、森林和池塘都是不同棲息地。"},{"en":"The park’s different habitats allow children to compare wildlife in each area.","zh":"公園的不同棲息地讓孩子比較每個區域的野生生物。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain why a place can support many species.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋為何一個地方能支援很多物種。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"quite a variety of wildlife","meaning":"相當多種類的野生生物","examples":[{"en":"There is quite a variety of wildlife in the park.","zh":"公園裏有相當多種類的野生生物。"},{"en":"Quite a variety of wildlife means many different kinds of wild plants and animals.","zh":"quite a variety of wildlife 意思是有許多不同種類的野生植物和動物。"},{"en":"A large wetland may have quite a variety of wildlife, including birds and insects.","zh":"大型濕地可能有相當多種類的野生生物，包括鳥類和昆蟲。"},{"en":"The park has variety because it includes woodland, grassland, and wetland.","zh":"公園有多樣性，因為它包括林地、草地和濕地。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that visitors can see more than one kind of living thing.","zh":"這個短語顯示遊客可以看見不止一種生物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"different species of","meaning":"不同種類的……","examples":[{"en":"The park has many different species of birds and insects.","zh":"公園有許多不同種類的鳥類和昆蟲。"},{"en":"Different species of something means different biological types of that living thing.","zh":"different species of something 意思是某種生物的不同生物種類。"},{"en":"A garden can attract different species of butterflies.","zh":"花園可以吸引不同種類的蝴蝶。"},{"en":"The park’s habitats support different species because each animal needs a suitable place to live.","zh":"公園的棲息地支援不同物種，因為每種動物都需要合適地方生活。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when talking about biodiversity.","zh":"這個短語用於談論生物多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"birds and insects","meaning":"鳥類和昆蟲","examples":[{"en":"The park has many species of birds and insects.","zh":"公園有很多種類的鳥類和昆蟲。"},{"en":"Birds and insects are animals commonly found in parks, woods, and wetlands.","zh":"鳥類和昆蟲是常見於公園、樹林和濕地的動物。"},{"en":"Children may identify birds by their calls and insects by their body shapes.","zh":"孩子可以透過叫聲辨認鳥類，透過身體形狀辨認昆蟲。"},{"en":"Birds and insects can show whether a habitat is healthy.","zh":"鳥類和昆蟲可以顯示棲息地是否健康。"},{"en":"Studying birds and insects helps children observe small details in nature.","zh":"研究鳥類和昆蟲幫助孩子觀察大自然中的細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"animals like deer and rabbits","meaning":"像鹿和兔子這類動物","examples":[{"en":"The park has animals like deer and rabbits.","zh":"公園有像鹿和兔子這類動物。"},{"en":"Animals like deer and rabbits means animals such as deer and rabbits.","zh":"animals like deer and rabbits 意思是例如鹿和兔子這類動物。"},{"en":"In the countryside, visitors may see animals like sheep and horses.","zh":"在郊區，遊客可能看見像羊和馬這類動物。"},{"en":"Deer and rabbits live in the park because there is food, shelter, and open space.","zh":"鹿和兔子生活在公園裏，因為那裏有食物、庇護和開放空間。"},{"en":"This phrase gives familiar examples of the wildlife visitors may see.","zh":"這個短語給出遊客可能看見的熟悉野生動物例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"educational visits","meaning":"教育參觀活動","examples":[{"en":"The park organises educational visits for schools.","zh":"公園為學校組織教育參觀活動。"},{"en":"Educational visits are trips planned to help students learn outside normal lessons.","zh":"教育參觀活動是為幫助學生在普通課堂外學習而安排的旅行。"},{"en":"A museum may offer educational visits about history or science.","zh":"博物館可能提供關於歷史或科學的教育參觀活動。"},{"en":"The park’s educational visits let children study nature directly.","zh":"公園的教育參觀活動讓孩子直接研究大自然。"},{"en":"This phrase means the trip has a learning purpose, not just entertainment.","zh":"這個短語表示旅程有學習目的，而不只是娛樂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"school parties","meaning":"學校團體","examples":[{"en":"The park organises educational visits for school parties.","zh":"公園為學校團體組織教育參觀活動。"},{"en":"School parties are groups of students and adults visiting together from a school.","zh":"school parties 是由學校出發、一起參觀的學生和成人團體。"},{"en":"The museum entrance has a separate line for school parties.","zh":"博物館入口有一條給學校團體使用的隊伍。"},{"en":"Park staff prepare activities for school parties because children need guidance and supervision.","zh":"公園職員為學校團體準備活動，因為孩子需要指導和監督。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised school groups, not celebrations.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的學校團體，而不是慶祝派對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a wide range of activities","meaning":"各式各樣的活動","examples":[{"en":"The park can organise a wide range of activities.","zh":"公園可以組織各式各樣的活動。"},{"en":"A wide range of activities means many different kinds of activities.","zh":"a wide range of activities 意思是很多不同類型的活動。"},{"en":"A youth centre may offer a wide range of activities, from sports to art.","zh":"青少年中心可能提供各式各樣的活動，從運動到藝術都有。"},{"en":"The park can offer science, geography, history, and music activities.","zh":"公園可以提供科學、地理、歷史和音樂活動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that visitors have many choices.","zh":"這個短語顯示參觀者有很多選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"adapt them to suit","meaning":"調整至適合……","examples":[{"en":"The rangers can adapt the activities to suit all ages.","zh":"巡護員可以調整活動至適合所有年齡層。"},{"en":"To adapt them to suit someone means to change the activities so they fit that person or group.","zh":"adapt them to suit someone 意思是改變活動，讓它們適合某人或某群體。"},{"en":"A teacher can adapt a worksheet to suit younger pupils.","zh":"老師可以調整工作紙至適合較年幼學生。"},{"en":"Rangers may make activities simpler for small children and more detailed for older students.","zh":"巡護員可能把活動為小朋友簡化，為較年長學生加深細節。"},{"en":"This phrase shows flexible planning for different needs.","zh":"這個短語顯示按不同需要作靈活規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"all ages","meaning":"所有年齡層","examples":[{"en":"The activities can be adapted to suit all ages.","zh":"活動可以調整至適合所有年齡層。"},{"en":"All ages means people of every age group.","zh":"all ages 意思是每個年齡組別的人。"},{"en":"The festival has games for all ages, from toddlers to grandparents.","zh":"這個節日有適合所有年齡層的遊戲，從幼兒到祖父母都有。"},{"en":"The park can change activities so both young children and older pupils can learn.","zh":"公園可以改變活動，讓年幼孩子和較年長學生都能學習。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is not limited to one age group.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事不限於一個年齡層。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"give me some examples of","meaning":"給我一些……例子","examples":[{"en":"John asks Sally to give him some examples of the activities.","zh":"John 請 Sally 給他一些活動例子。"},{"en":"Give me some examples of means show or tell me a few specific cases.","zh":"give me some examples of 意思是向我展示或告訴我幾個具體例子。"},{"en":"Can you give me some examples of healthy snacks for children?","zh":"你可以給我一些適合孩子的健康小食例子嗎？"},{"en":"John asks for examples because general activity names are not enough for planning.","zh":"John 要例子，因為單是一般活動名稱不足以作計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase helps turn broad information into clear details.","zh":"這個短語幫助把廣泛資料變成清楚細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"one focus is on","meaning":"其中一個重點是","examples":[{"en":"One focus is on science.","zh":"其中一個重點是科學。"},{"en":"One focus is on means one main area of attention is a particular subject.","zh":"one focus is on 意思是其中一個主要注意範疇是某個主題。"},{"en":"One focus of the lesson is on teamwork.","zh":"這堂課其中一個重點是團隊合作。"},{"en":"The park’s science focus helps children study plants, trees, and insects.","zh":"公園的科學重點幫助孩子研究植物、樹木和昆蟲。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces one important topic among several.","zh":"這個短語在幾個主題中介紹其中一個重要主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"discover and study","meaning":"發現並研究","examples":[{"en":"Children discover and study plants, trees and insects.","zh":"孩子發現並研究植物、樹木和昆蟲。"},{"en":"To discover and study something means to find it and then examine it carefully.","zh":"discover and study something 意思是找到某物，然後仔細觀察和研究它。"},{"en":"Students discover and study shells during a beach science lesson.","zh":"學生在海灘科學課中發現並研究貝殼。"},{"en":"In the park, children learn by finding real living things and observing them.","zh":"在公園裏，孩子透過尋找真實生物並觀察它們來學習。"},{"en":"This phrase combines exploration with careful learning.","zh":"這個短語結合探索和仔細學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"plants, trees and insects","meaning":"植物、樹木和昆蟲","examples":[{"en":"Children study plants, trees and insects in the park.","zh":"孩子在公園裏研究植物、樹木和昆蟲。"},{"en":"Plants, trees and insects are living things children can observe in natural habitats.","zh":"植物、樹木和昆蟲是孩子可以在自然棲息地觀察的生物。"},{"en":"A science class may compare plants, trees and insects in different parts of a park.","zh":"科學班可能比較公園不同地方的植物、樹木和昆蟲。"},{"en":"Studying these living things helps children understand food chains and habitats.","zh":"研究這些生物幫助孩子理解食物鏈和棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase gives concrete examples of what children can study outdoors.","zh":"這個短語給出孩子可在戶外研究的具體例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"collect and analyse data","meaning":"收集並分析數據","examples":[{"en":"Children collect and analyse data about the things they see.","zh":"孩子收集並分析關於他們所見事物的數據。"},{"en":"To collect and analyse data means to gather information and study it to find meaning.","zh":"collect and analyse data 意思是收集資料並研究它，以找出意義。"},{"en":"Students collect and analyse data about how many birds visit the school garden.","zh":"學生收集並分析有多少鳥到訪學校花園的數據。"},{"en":"In the park, children may count insects and then compare numbers from different habitats.","zh":"在公園裏，孩子可能點算昆蟲，再比較不同棲息地的數量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important scientific process.","zh":"這個短語描述重要的科學過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"data about","meaning":"關於……的數據","examples":[{"en":"Children collect data about the things they see.","zh":"孩子收集關於他們所見事物的數據。"},{"en":"Data about something is information collected on that subject.","zh":"data about something 是就某個主題收集的資料。"},{"en":"A class may collect data about daily temperatures for a weather project.","zh":"一個班可能為天氣專題收集關於每日氣溫的數據。"},{"en":"Children collect data about plants and insects so they can compare habitats.","zh":"孩子收集關於植物和昆蟲的數據，以便比較棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase connects information with the subject being studied.","zh":"這個短語把資料與正在研究的主題連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"another focus is on","meaning":"另一個重點是","examples":[{"en":"Another focus is on geography.","zh":"另一個重點是地理。"},{"en":"Another focus is on means a different main area of attention is another subject.","zh":"another focus is on 意思是另一個主要注意範疇是另一個主題。"},{"en":"Another focus of the project is on local history.","zh":"這個項目的另一個重點是本地歷史。"},{"en":"Sally uses this phrase to move from science activities to geography activities.","zh":"Sally 使用這個短語，由科學活動轉到地理活動。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise several topics clearly.","zh":"這個短語幫助清楚組織幾個主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a great environment to","meaning":"適合……的好環境","examples":[{"en":"The park is a great environment to learn map-reading skills.","zh":"這個公園是學習閱讀地圖技巧的好環境。"},{"en":"A great environment to do something means a very suitable place for that activity.","zh":"a great environment to do something 意思是非常適合某活動的地方。"},{"en":"A quiet library is a great environment to study for exams.","zh":"安靜的圖書館是準備考試的好環境。"},{"en":"The park is suitable for map reading because children can connect the map with real paths.","zh":"公園適合閱讀地圖，因為孩子可以把地圖與真實小徑連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a place helps a certain kind of learning.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何一個地方有助某種學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"learn and practise","meaning":"學習和練習","examples":[{"en":"Children learn and practise reading a map.","zh":"孩子學習和練習閱讀地圖。"},{"en":"To learn and practise something means to understand it and then use it repeatedly.","zh":"learn and practise something 意思是先理解某事，再反覆使用它。"},{"en":"Students learn and practise new vocabulary by using it in sentences.","zh":"學生透過用新詞造句來學習和練習新詞彙。"},{"en":"Children learn map symbols first and then practise using them outdoors.","zh":"孩子先學習地圖符號，然後在戶外練習使用它們。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that learning improves through action.","zh":"這個短語顯示學習透過實踐而進步。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reading a map","meaning":"閱讀地圖","examples":[{"en":"Children practise reading a map in the park.","zh":"孩子在公園裏練習閱讀地圖。"},{"en":"Reading a map means understanding symbols, directions, and routes shown on a map.","zh":"reading a map 意思是理解地圖上的符號、方向和路線。"},{"en":"Hikers need to practise reading a map before walking in unfamiliar countryside.","zh":"遠足者在陌生郊區行走前需要練習閱讀地圖。"},{"en":"Children read the map to find paths, lakes, and woodland areas.","zh":"孩子閱讀地圖，以找出小徑、湖泊和林地區域。"},{"en":"This skill helps people know where they are and where to go.","zh":"這項技能幫助人知道自己在哪裏和應往哪裏走。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"using a compass","meaning":"使用指南針","examples":[{"en":"Children learn about using a compass.","zh":"孩子學習使用指南針。"},{"en":"Using a compass means using a tool that shows direction, especially north.","zh":"using a compass 意思是使用顯示方向，尤其是北方的工具。"},{"en":"Scouts learn about using a compass before going camping.","zh":"童軍在露營前學習使用指南針。"},{"en":"A compass helps children connect map directions with real-world directions.","zh":"指南針幫助孩子把地圖方向與真實世界方向連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical navigation skill.","zh":"這個短語描述實用的辨向技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"navigate around the park","meaning":"在公園內辨認方向","examples":[{"en":"Children use a compass to navigate around the park.","zh":"孩子使用指南針在公園內辨認方向。"},{"en":"To navigate around the park means to find your way through different parts of the park.","zh":"navigate around the park 意思是在公園不同部分中找路前進。"},{"en":"Visitors can navigate around the park by following signs and paths.","zh":"遊客可以透過跟隨指示牌和小徑在公園內辨認方向。"},{"en":"Children practise navigation by using maps, landmarks, and a compass.","zh":"孩子透過使用地圖、地標和指南針練習辨向。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on moving through a place without getting lost.","zh":"這個短語著重在某地方移動而不迷路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"connected with history","meaning":"與歷史有關","examples":[{"en":"John asks if the park offers anything connected with history.","zh":"John 問公園是否提供任何與歷史有關的內容。"},{"en":"Connected with history means related to past events, old land use, or earlier ways of life.","zh":"connected with history 意思是與過去事件、舊土地用途或早期生活方式有關。"},{"en":"A museum display about old village houses is connected with history.","zh":"關於舊村屋的博物館展覽與歷史有關。"},{"en":"John asks this because school visits may need to cover several subjects.","zh":"John 這樣問，因為學校參觀可能需要涵蓋幾個科目。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a link between an activity and historical learning.","zh":"這個短語顯示活動與歷史學習之間的連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"For instance, children can explore changes in land use.","zh":"例如，孩子可以探索土地用途的變化。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance 意思是例如。"},{"en":"Some outdoor activities teach science; for instance, children can study insects.","zh":"有些戶外活動教授科學；例如，孩子可以研究昆蟲。"},{"en":"Sally uses this phrase before giving a specific history activity.","zh":"Sally 在給出具體歷史活動前使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an example that makes the explanation clearer.","zh":"這個短語引入例子，使解釋更清楚。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"explore how","meaning":"探索……如何","examples":[{"en":"Children can explore how the use of the land has changed.","zh":"孩子可以探索土地用途如何改變。"},{"en":"To explore how something happens means to investigate or learn the way it happens.","zh":"explore how something happens 意思是調查或了解某事如何發生。"},{"en":"Students explore how plants grow by observing them each week.","zh":"學生透過每週觀察植物來探索植物如何生長。"},{"en":"Children explore how farmland became lakes and parkland.","zh":"孩子探索農地如何變成湖泊和公園土地。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active learning and questioning.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動學習和提問。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the use of the land","meaning":"土地用途","examples":[{"en":"Children learn how the use of the land has changed.","zh":"孩子學習土地用途如何改變。"},{"en":"The use of the land means what people do with a piece of land.","zh":"the use of the land 意思是人們如何使用一片土地。"},{"en":"The use of the land may change from farming to housing.","zh":"土地用途可能由耕作改為住宅。"},{"en":"In the park, land once used for farming and gravel extraction is now used for nature and education.","zh":"在公園裏，曾用於耕作和開採礫石的土地現在用於自然和教育。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect geography with history.","zh":"這個短語幫助把地理與歷史連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"changed over time","meaning":"隨時間改變","examples":[{"en":"The use of the land has changed over time.","zh":"土地用途隨時間改變。"},{"en":"Changed over time means became different gradually during a period.","zh":"changed over time 意思是在一段時間內逐漸變得不同。"},{"en":"The town’s buildings have changed over time as more people moved there.","zh":"隨着更多人搬到那裏，城鎮建築隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The park changed from farmland to gravel pits and then to lakes and habitats.","zh":"公園由農地變成礫石坑，再變成湖泊和棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase shows development across years, not a sudden moment only.","zh":"這個短語顯示多年來的發展，而不只是某一瞬間的改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"leisure and tourism","meaning":"休閒與旅遊","examples":[{"en":"The park also covers leisure and tourism.","zh":"公園也涵蓋休閒與旅遊。"},{"en":"Leisure and tourism means free-time activities and travel or visits for enjoyment.","zh":"leisure and tourism 意思是空閒活動，以及為享受而進行的旅行或參觀。"},{"en":"A seaside town may study leisure and tourism because many visitors go there on holiday.","zh":"海邊小鎮可能研究休閒與旅遊，因為很多遊客到那裏度假。"},{"en":"In the park, this subject looks at visitors and how they use the space.","zh":"在公園裏，這個主題研究遊客以及他們如何使用空間。"},{"en":"This phrase connects recreation, visitors, and place management.","zh":"這個短語連繫娛樂、遊客和地方管理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"集中於","examples":[{"en":"Leisure and tourism mostly focuses on the park’s visitors.","zh":"休閒與旅遊主要集中於公園遊客。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give main attention to it.","zh":"focus on something 意思是把主要注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"This lesson focuses on rivers and how they shape land.","zh":"這堂課集中於河流以及它們如何塑造土地。"},{"en":"The park’s leisure topic focuses on visitors because their behaviour affects the park.","zh":"公園的休閒主題集中於遊客，因為他們的行為會影響公園。"},{"en":"This phrase helps identify the main subject of study.","zh":"這個短語幫助指出主要研究主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"I would imagine","meaning":"我想；我估計","examples":[{"en":"That focuses on your visitors, I would imagine.","zh":"我想那是集中於你們的遊客。"},{"en":"I would imagine means I think this is probably true, though I am not completely sure.","zh":"I would imagine 意思是我認為這大概是真的，但不是完全肯定。"},{"en":"The activity will be outside, I would imagine, because it is about plants.","zh":"我想活動會在戶外進行，因為它是關於植物的。"},{"en":"John says this because he is guessing what leisure and tourism means in the park.","zh":"John 這樣說，因為他正在猜測公園中的休閒與旅遊是甚麼意思。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a careful guess.","zh":"這個短語表示謹慎猜測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"mostly","meaning":"主要地","examples":[{"en":"The leisure and tourism topic mostly focuses on visitors.","zh":"休閒與旅遊這個題目主要集中於遊客。"},{"en":"Mostly means mainly or for the most part.","zh":"mostly 意思是主要地或在大部分情況下。"},{"en":"The class is mostly about science, but it also includes some geography.","zh":"這堂課主要關於科學，但也包括一些地理。"},{"en":"The topic mostly focuses on visitors, although it may also include park management.","zh":"這個題目主要集中於遊客，雖然也可能包括公園管理。"},{"en":"This word shows the main part of something, not necessarily all of it.","zh":"這個字顯示某事的主要部分，但不一定是全部。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"find out about","meaning":"了解……","examples":[{"en":"The children find out about visitors and their requirements.","zh":"孩子了解遊客及他們的需求。"},{"en":"To find out about something means to learn information about it.","zh":"find out about something 意思是得知或了解某事的資料。"},{"en":"Students interview residents to find out about local transport problems.","zh":"學生訪問居民，以了解本地交通問題。"},{"en":"Children find out about visitors by asking questions and observing behaviour.","zh":"孩子透過提問和觀察行為來了解遊客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when learning through investigation.","zh":"這個短語適合用於透過調查學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"visitors’ requirements","meaning":"遊客的需求","examples":[{"en":"Children learn about visitors’ requirements.","zh":"孩子了解遊客的需求。"},{"en":"Visitors’ requirements are the things visitors need or expect when they come to a place.","zh":"visitors’ requirements 是遊客來到某地方時需要或期望的東西。"},{"en":"Visitors’ requirements may include toilets, signs, paths, and picnic areas.","zh":"遊客的需求可能包括洗手間、指示牌、小徑和野餐區。"},{"en":"Parks study visitors’ requirements so they can provide useful facilities.","zh":"公園研究遊客的需求，以便提供有用設施。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical needs from the visitor’s point of view.","zh":"這個短語從遊客角度著重實際需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"problems they may cause","meaning":"他們可能造成的問題","examples":[{"en":"Children consider the problems visitors may cause.","zh":"孩子思考遊客可能造成的問題。"},{"en":"Problems they may cause means difficulties that visitors might create.","zh":"problems they may cause 意思是遊客可能製造的困難。"},{"en":"Too many visitors may cause litter, noise, and damage to paths.","zh":"太多遊客可能造成垃圾、噪音和小徑損壞。"},{"en":"Children learn that visitors can enjoy a park but also create pressure on habitats.","zh":"孩子學會遊客可以享受公園，但也會對棲息地造成壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase helps students think about both benefits and impacts.","zh":"這個短語幫助學生同時思考好處和影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"manage these","meaning":"管理這些問題","examples":[{"en":"Children learn how the park manages these problems.","zh":"孩子學習公園如何管理這些問題。"},{"en":"To manage these means to control or deal with these problems.","zh":"manage these 意思是控制或處理這些問題。"},{"en":"A school manages noise by setting clear playground rules.","zh":"學校透過訂立清楚操場規則來管理噪音問題。"},{"en":"The park may manage visitor problems with signs, bins, paths, and staff guidance.","zh":"公園可能透過指示牌、垃圾桶、小徑和職員指引來管理遊客問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical ways to handle difficulties.","zh":"這個短語著重處理困難的實際方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"another subject we cover","meaning":"我們涵蓋的另一個主題","examples":[{"en":"Another subject the park covers is music.","zh":"公園涵蓋的另一個主題是音樂。"},{"en":"Another subject we cover means another topic included in the programme.","zh":"another subject we cover 意思是課程中包括的另一個題目。"},{"en":"Another subject we cover in the workshop is environmental protection.","zh":"我們在工作坊涵蓋的另一個主題是環境保護。"},{"en":"Sally says this to show that the park visits are not only about science and geography.","zh":"Sally 這樣說，是顯示公園參觀不只關於科學和地理。"},{"en":"This phrase helps introduce one more learning area.","zh":"這個短語幫助介紹另一個學習範疇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"experiment with","meaning":"嘗試使用；實驗","examples":[{"en":"Children experiment with natural materials.","zh":"孩子嘗試使用天然材料。"},{"en":"To experiment with something means to try using it in different ways to see what happens.","zh":"experiment with something 意思是用不同方法嘗試使用某物，看看會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Students experiment with magnets to learn how they attract metal.","zh":"學生用磁石做實驗，以學習它們如何吸引金屬。"},{"en":"Children experiment with sticks, leaves, and stones to create sounds.","zh":"孩子嘗試使用樹枝、葉子和石頭來創造聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests learning by trying, testing, and exploring.","zh":"這個短語暗示透過嘗試、測試和探索來學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"natural materials","meaning":"天然材料","examples":[{"en":"Children use natural materials to create sounds.","zh":"孩子使用天然材料來創造聲音。"},{"en":"Natural materials are things from nature, such as leaves, wood, stones, or shells.","zh":"natural materials 是來自大自然的東西，例如葉子、木頭、石頭或貝殼。"},{"en":"Art teachers may ask students to make pictures with natural materials.","zh":"美術老師可能請學生用天然材料製作圖畫。"},{"en":"In the park, natural materials help children connect music with the outdoor environment.","zh":"在公園裏，天然材料幫助孩子把音樂與戶外環境連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts nature-based materials with plastic or electronic tools.","zh":"這個短語把來自自然的材料與塑膠或電子工具作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"create sounds","meaning":"創造聲音","examples":[{"en":"Children create sounds with natural materials.","zh":"孩子用天然材料創造聲音。"},{"en":"To create sounds means to make noises, tones, or rhythms.","zh":"create sounds 意思是製造聲響、音調或節奏。"},{"en":"Children can create sounds by tapping sticks or shaking dry leaves.","zh":"孩子可以透過敲打樹枝或搖動乾葉來創造聲音。"},{"en":"The activity teaches music through the sounds found in nature.","zh":"這項活動透過大自然中的聲音教授音樂。"},{"en":"This phrase shows active making, not just listening.","zh":"這個短語顯示主動製作，而不只是聆聽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rhythm and tempo","meaning":"節奏與速度","examples":[{"en":"Children explore rhythm and tempo.","zh":"孩子探索節奏與速度。"},{"en":"Rhythm and tempo are parts of music: rhythm is the pattern of beats, and tempo is the speed.","zh":"rhythm and tempo 是音樂的一部分：rhythm 是拍子的模式，tempo 是速度。"},{"en":"Clapping games can teach children rhythm and tempo.","zh":"拍手遊戲可以教孩子節奏與速度。"},{"en":"Children may use sticks to make slow and fast beats outdoors.","zh":"孩子可能在戶外用樹枝敲出慢拍和快拍。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe basic musical features.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述基本音樂特徵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"That must be fun!","meaning":"那一定很有趣！","examples":[{"en":"John says, “That must be fun!”","zh":"John 說：「那一定很有趣！」"},{"en":"That must be fun! means the speaker thinks an activity is very likely enjoyable.","zh":"That must be fun! 意思是說話者認為某活動很可能令人享受。"},{"en":"Making music with leaves and sticks must be fun for young children.","zh":"用葉子和樹枝做音樂對年幼孩子來說一定很有趣。"},{"en":"John says this because the music activity sounds playful and creative.","zh":"John 這樣說，因為音樂活動聽起來好玩又有創意。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a strong guess based on what has just been described.","zh":"這個短語根據剛才描述的內容表達強烈推測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"really enjoy it","meaning":"非常喜歡它","examples":[{"en":"Most children really enjoy the music activities.","zh":"大部分孩子非常喜歡音樂活動。"},{"en":"Really enjoy it means like it very much.","zh":"really enjoy it 意思是非常喜歡它。"},{"en":"Children really enjoy it when science lessons include experiments.","zh":"當科學課包括實驗時，孩子非常喜歡它。"},{"en":"Most children enjoy the activity because they can make sounds themselves.","zh":"大部分孩子喜歡這項活動，因為他們可以自己創造聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong enjoyment, not just mild interest.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈喜愛，而不只是輕微興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"educational","meaning":"有教育意義的","examples":[{"en":"All the activities are educational.","zh":"所有活動都有教育意義。"},{"en":"Educational means designed to help people learn something.","zh":"educational 意思是設計來幫助人學習某事。"},{"en":"A game can be educational if it teaches vocabulary or problem-solving.","zh":"如果遊戲教授詞彙或解難，它可以有教育意義。"},{"en":"The park activities are educational because children learn science, geography, history, and music.","zh":"公園活動有教育意義，因為孩子學習科學、地理、歷史和音樂。"},{"en":"This word shows that an activity has a learning purpose.","zh":"這個字顯示活動有學習目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"learning outside the classroom","meaning":"課堂外學習","examples":[{"en":"Learning outside the classroom encourages children to be creative.","zh":"課堂外學習鼓勵孩子發揮創意。"},{"en":"Learning outside the classroom means learning in real places instead of only inside a school room.","zh":"learning outside the classroom 意思是在真實地方學習，而不只是坐在課室裏。"},{"en":"A farm visit is an example of learning outside the classroom.","zh":"農場參觀是課堂外學習的一個例子。"},{"en":"Outdoor learning lets children touch, see, and explore things directly.","zh":"戶外學習讓孩子直接觸摸、觀看和探索事物。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that learning can happen beyond desks and textbooks.","zh":"這個短語顯示學習可以發生在書桌和課本以外。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"encourage children to","meaning":"鼓勵孩子去……","examples":[{"en":"Outdoor learning encourages children to be creative.","zh":"戶外學習鼓勵孩子發揮創意。"},{"en":"To encourage children to do something means to help or motivate them to do it.","zh":"encourage children to do something 意思是幫助或推動孩子做某事。"},{"en":"Teachers encourage children to ask questions during science lessons.","zh":"老師在科學課鼓勵孩子提問。"},{"en":"Outdoor activities encourage children to explore because the environment feels open and real.","zh":"戶外活動鼓勵孩子探索，因為環境感覺開放而真實。"},{"en":"This phrase shows positive support for children’s actions.","zh":"這個短語顯示對孩子行動的正面支持。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be creative","meaning":"發揮創意","examples":[{"en":"Outdoor learning encourages children to be creative.","zh":"戶外學習鼓勵孩子發揮創意。"},{"en":"To be creative means to use imagination to make or think of new ideas.","zh":"be creative 意思是用想像力創造或想出新想法。"},{"en":"Children can be creative by making music from leaves and sticks.","zh":"孩子可以用葉子和樹枝製作音樂來發揮創意。"},{"en":"The park helps children be creative because they can use natural materials in new ways.","zh":"公園幫助孩子發揮創意，因為他們可以用新方法使用天然材料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes imaginative thinking and making.","zh":"這個短語描述有想像力的思考和創作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"explore and discover for themselves","meaning":"親自探索和發現","examples":[{"en":"Children can explore and discover for themselves.","zh":"孩子可以親自探索和發現。"},{"en":"To explore and discover for themselves means to learn by finding things through their own actions.","zh":"explore and discover for themselves 意思是透過自己的行動尋找事物來學習。"},{"en":"Children explore and discover for themselves when they examine insects under leaves.","zh":"當孩子檢查葉子下的昆蟲時，他們就是親自探索和發現。"},{"en":"Outdoor learning is powerful because pupils are not only listening to a teacher.","zh":"戶外學習很有力量，因為學生不只是聽老師講。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises independent, active learning.","zh":"這個短語強調自主而主動的學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get a sense of freedom","meaning":"得到一種自由感","examples":[{"en":"Children get a sense of freedom from learning outdoors.","zh":"孩子從戶外學習中得到一種自由感。"},{"en":"To get a sense of freedom means to feel more free than usual.","zh":"get a sense of freedom 意思是感到比平時更自由。"},{"en":"Children may get a sense of freedom when they run safely in open fields.","zh":"當孩子在開闊草地安全奔跑時，可能會得到一種自由感。"},{"en":"Outdoor lessons feel different because children can move, look around, and make choices.","zh":"戶外課感覺不同，因為孩子可以移動、四處觀察和作選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a feeling, not a physical object.","zh":"這個短語描述一種感覺，而不是實物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a normal part of their lives","meaning":"他們日常生活的一部分","examples":[{"en":"This sense of freedom might not be a normal part of their lives.","zh":"這種自由感可能不是他們日常生活的一部分。"},{"en":"A normal part of their lives means something they regularly experience in everyday life.","zh":"a normal part of their lives 意思是他們在日常生活中經常經歷的事情。"},{"en":"For some children, playing in open countryside is not a normal part of their lives.","zh":"對有些孩子來說，在開闊郊野玩耍不是他們日常生活的一部分。"},{"en":"The park visit may give children experiences they do not usually have.","zh":"公園參觀可能給孩子平時沒有的經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase compares outdoor learning with children’s usual daily routines.","zh":"這個短語把戶外學習與孩子平常日常生活作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"very often","meaning":"很多時候","examples":[{"en":"Very often, children discover that they can do new things.","zh":"很多時候，孩子發現自己能做到新事情。"},{"en":"Very often means frequently or in many cases.","zh":"very often 意思是經常或在很多情況下。"},{"en":"Very often, students learn better when they try tasks themselves.","zh":"很多時候，學生親自嘗試任務時會學得更好。"},{"en":"Sally uses this phrase because many children gain confidence during outdoor activities.","zh":"Sally 使用這個短語，因為很多孩子在戶外活動中建立自信。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something happens many times, not just once.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事發生很多次，而不只是一次。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"discover that they can","meaning":"發現自己能夠……","examples":[{"en":"Children discover that they can do things they did not know they could do.","zh":"孩子發現自己能做到以前不知道自己能做的事情。"},{"en":"To discover that they can means to realise they are able to do something.","zh":"discover that they can 意思是意識到自己有能力做某事。"},{"en":"A shy child may discover that they can speak confidently during a group activity.","zh":"害羞的孩子可能在小組活動中發現自己能夠自信地說話。"},{"en":"Outdoor tasks help children notice abilities they had not used before.","zh":"戶外任務幫助孩子注意到以前未曾使用的能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gaining self-knowledge through experience.","zh":"這個短語描述透過經驗獲得自我認識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"develop new skills","meaning":"發展新技能","examples":[{"en":"Children develop new skills during outdoor visits.","zh":"孩子在戶外參觀中發展新技能。"},{"en":"To develop new skills means to learn and improve abilities that were not strong before.","zh":"develop new skills 意思是學習並改善以前不強的能力。"},{"en":"Students develop new skills when they practise reading maps in real places.","zh":"學生在真實地方練習閱讀地圖時會發展新技能。"},{"en":"Park visits can help children develop observation, teamwork, and navigation skills.","zh":"公園參觀可以幫助孩子發展觀察、團隊合作和辨向技能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows learning through practice over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示透過練習逐漸學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"greater self-confidence","meaning":"更大的自信","examples":[{"en":"Learning new skills gives children greater self-confidence.","zh":"學習新技能給孩子更大的自信。"},{"en":"Greater self-confidence means a stronger belief in one’s own ability.","zh":"greater self-confidence 意思是對自己能力有更強信心。"},{"en":"A child may gain greater self-confidence after successfully leading a group activity.","zh":"孩子成功帶領小組活動後，可能會得到更大的自信。"},{"en":"Outdoor learning can build confidence because children see themselves solving real problems.","zh":"戶外學習可以建立自信，因為孩子看見自己正在解決真實問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase in personal belief and courage.","zh":"這個短語描述個人信念和勇氣的增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"practical side","meaning":"實際安排方面","examples":[{"en":"John asks about the practical side of the visit.","zh":"John 詢問參觀的實際安排方面。"},{"en":"The practical side means the real arrangements, such as cost, timing, transport, and supervision.","zh":"practical side 意思是實際安排，例如費用、時間、交通和監督。"},{"en":"Before a school trip, teachers must think about the practical side.","zh":"學校旅行前，老師必須考慮實際安排方面。"},{"en":"John asks about cost because he needs details before taking the idea to colleagues.","zh":"John 詢問費用，因為他需要細節才能向同事討論這個想法。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts practical arrangements with general ideas or benefits.","zh":"這個短語把實際安排與一般想法或好處作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"full-day visit","meaning":"全天參觀","examples":[{"en":"John asks about the cost of a full-day visit.","zh":"John 詢問全天參觀的費用。"},{"en":"A full-day visit is a visit that lasts for most or all of the school day.","zh":"full-day visit 是持續大部分或整個上課日的參觀。"},{"en":"A full-day visit to a museum may include a workshop and lunch break.","zh":"到博物館的全天參觀可能包括工作坊和午餐時間。"},{"en":"John needs the price because a full-day visit requires more planning than a short tour.","zh":"John 需要價格，因為全天參觀比短導賞需要更多計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the length of the visit.","zh":"這個短語描述參觀的長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"expect to bring","meaning":"預計帶同","examples":[{"en":"The school expects to bring between 30 and 40 children.","zh":"學校預計帶同 30 至 40 名孩子。"},{"en":"Expect to bring means plan or think you will bring a certain number of people or things.","zh":"expect to bring 意思是計劃或估計會帶同某個數量的人或物。"},{"en":"The club expects to bring twenty students to the competition.","zh":"學會預計帶同二十名學生參加比賽。"},{"en":"John gives an estimated number so Sally can explain the cost.","zh":"John 提供估計人數，讓 Sally 可以解釋費用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving a planned but not final number.","zh":"這個短語適合用於提供計劃中但未最終確定的數字。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"between 30 and 40 children","meaning":"30 至 40 名孩子之間","examples":[{"en":"The school expects to bring between 30 and 40 children.","zh":"學校預計帶同 30 至 40 名孩子。"},{"en":"Between 30 and 40 children means more than 30 or fewer than 40, or around that range.","zh":"between 30 and 40 children 意思是大約在 30 至 40 名孩子這個範圍內。"},{"en":"The summer camp usually has between 30 and 40 children each week.","zh":"夏令營每星期通常有 30 至 40 名孩子。"},{"en":"This number matters because the park’s price depends on group size.","zh":"這個人數很重要，因為公園價格取決於團體大小。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an estimated range rather than an exact number.","zh":"這個短語提供估計範圍，而不是準確數字。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"costs £4.95","meaning":"收費 4.95 英鎊","examples":[{"en":"If there are over 30 children, it costs £4.95 per child.","zh":"如果有超過 30 名孩子，每名孩子收費 4.95 英鎊。"},{"en":"Costs £4.95 means the price is four pounds and ninety-five pence.","zh":"costs £4.95 意思是價格為四英鎊九十五便士。"},{"en":"The museum workshop costs £4.95 for each pupil.","zh":"博物館工作坊每名學生收費 4.95 英鎊。"},{"en":"John needs this price so he can estimate the total cost for the school.","zh":"John 需要這個價格，這樣他可以估算學校總費用。"},{"en":"This phrase states the amount of money required.","zh":"這個短語說明所需金額。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"for each child","meaning":"每名孩子","examples":[{"en":"The park charges £4.95 for each child who attends.","zh":"公園向每名出席的孩子收取 4.95 英鎊。"},{"en":"For each child means for every individual child.","zh":"for each child 意思是按每一名孩子計算。"},{"en":"The zoo charges two pounds for each child in a school group.","zh":"動物園向學校團體每名孩子收取兩英鎊。"},{"en":"If 35 children attend, the school pays the child price 35 times.","zh":"如果 35 名孩子出席，學校就要把兒童價格乘以 35。"},{"en":"This phrase helps calculate the total cost from the number of children.","zh":"這個短語幫助根據孩子人數計算總費用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"attends on the day","meaning":"當日出席","examples":[{"en":"The school pays for each child who attends on the day.","zh":"學校為每名當日出席的孩子付款。"},{"en":"Attends on the day means actually comes to the visit on that day.","zh":"attends on the day 意思是在那一天真正出席。"},{"en":"The club only pays for students who attend on the day of the competition.","zh":"學會只為比賽當日出席的學生付款。"},{"en":"If a child is absent because of sickness, the school does not pay for that child.","zh":"如果孩子因病缺席，學校不用為那名孩子付款。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the payment depend on actual attendance.","zh":"這個短語使付款取決於實際出席情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"invoice you afterwards","meaning":"之後向你發出發票","examples":[{"en":"The park will invoice the school afterwards.","zh":"公園之後會向學校發出發票。"},{"en":"To invoice you afterwards means to send you a bill after the service or visit has happened.","zh":"invoice you afterwards 意思是在服務或參觀完成後向你發出帳單。"},{"en":"The repair company will invoice us afterwards, once the work is finished.","zh":"維修公司會在工作完成後向我們發出發票。"},{"en":"The park invoices the school later because the final number of children may change.","zh":"公園稍後向學校發票，因為最終孩子人數可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business and school payments.","zh":"這個短語常見於商業和學校付款情境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"because of sickness","meaning":"因病","examples":[{"en":"The school does not pay for children who cannot come because of sickness.","zh":"學校不用為因病不能出席的孩子付款。"},{"en":"Because of sickness means due to illness.","zh":"because of sickness 意思是由於生病。"},{"en":"The student missed the trip because of sickness.","zh":"那名學生因病錯過了旅行。"},{"en":"The park does not charge for absent children if they are ill on the day.","zh":"如果孩子當日生病缺席，公園不會收費。"},{"en":"This phrase gives illness as the reason something happens or does not happen.","zh":"這個短語以疾病作為某事發生或不發生的原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"no charge for","meaning":"……免費；不收費","examples":[{"en":"There is no charge for leaders and other adults.","zh":"領隊及其他成年人免費。"},{"en":"No charge for someone means that person does not need to pay.","zh":"no charge for someone 意思是某人不需要付款。"},{"en":"There is no charge for children under five at the museum.","zh":"博物館對五歲以下兒童免費。"},{"en":"The park does not charge adults who supervise the school group.","zh":"公園不向監督學校團體的成人收費。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly states who can join for free.","zh":"這個短語清楚說明誰可以免費參加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"leaders and other adults","meaning":"領隊及其他成年人","examples":[{"en":"There is no charge for leaders and other adults.","zh":"領隊及其他成年人不收費。"},{"en":"Leaders and other adults are the teachers, assistants, parents, or helpers who supervise children.","zh":"leaders and other adults 是監督孩子的老師、助教、家長或幫手。"},{"en":"A school trip needs leaders and other adults to keep children safe.","zh":"學校旅行需要領隊及其他成年人確保孩子安全。"},{"en":"The park lets these adults enter free because they are there to support the pupils.","zh":"公園讓這些成人免費入場，因為他們是來支援學生的。"},{"en":"This phrase separates supervising adults from the children attending.","zh":"這個短語把監督成人與出席的孩子區分開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as many as you want to bring","meaning":"想帶多少都可以","examples":[{"en":"The school can bring as many adults as it wants.","zh":"學校想帶多少成年人都可以。"},{"en":"As many as you want to bring means there is no limit on the number you may bring.","zh":"as many as you want to bring 意思是可以帶的人數沒有限制。"},{"en":"You can invite as many helpers as you want to bring for the school fair.","zh":"學校賣物會你想帶多少幫手都可以。"},{"en":"John can arrange enough adult supervision without worrying about extra adult fees.","zh":"John 可以安排足夠成人監督，而不用擔心額外成人費用。"},{"en":"This phrase gives freedom over quantity.","zh":"這個短語表示數量上的自由。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sounds very fair","meaning":"聽起來很合理","examples":[{"en":"John says the price sounds very fair.","zh":"John 說這個價格聽起來很合理。"},{"en":"Sounds very fair means seems reasonable and not unfair.","zh":"sounds very fair 意思是似乎合理而不不公平。"},{"en":"The museum’s group price sounds very fair because teachers enter free.","zh":"博物館團體價聽起來很合理，因為老師免費入場。"},{"en":"John thinks the cost is fair because the school pays only for children who attend.","zh":"John 覺得費用合理，因為學校只需為出席的孩子付款。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a positive judgement about price or rules.","zh":"這個短語對價格或規則作出正面判斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"thanks for all the information","meaning":"謝謝提供所有資料","examples":[{"en":"John thanks Sally for all the information.","zh":"John 感謝 Sally 提供所有資料。"},{"en":"Thanks for all the information means thank you for giving many useful details.","zh":"thanks for all the information 意思是感謝你提供許多有用細節。"},{"en":"Thanks for all the information about the course fees and timetable.","zh":"謝謝你提供所有關於課程費用和時間表的資料。"},{"en":"John says this because Sally has explained the park, activities, and cost.","zh":"John 這樣說，因為 Sally 已解釋公園、活動和費用。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and often used near the end of a helpful conversation.","zh":"這個短語很有禮貌，常用於有幫助的對話接近結束時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"discuss it with my colleagues","meaning":"和同事討論","examples":[{"en":"John needs to discuss the visit with his colleagues.","zh":"John 需要和同事討論這次參觀。"},{"en":"To discuss it with my colleagues means to talk about it with the people I work with.","zh":"discuss it with my colleagues 意思是和一起工作的人談論這件事。"},{"en":"I need to discuss the new timetable with my colleagues before agreeing.","zh":"我需要先和同事討論新時間表，然後才同意。"},{"en":"John must speak to other school staff before making the booking.","zh":"John 必須先與其他學校職員商量，才可以預訂。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a decision needs group agreement.","zh":"這個短語顯示決定需要團隊同意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"get back to you","meaning":"回覆你","examples":[{"en":"John hopes to get back to Sally soon.","zh":"John 希望很快回覆 Sally。"},{"en":"To get back to someone means to contact them later with an answer or update.","zh":"get back to someone 意思是稍後聯絡某人並給出答案或更新。"},{"en":"I will get back to you after I check the booking form.","zh":"我查看預訂表格後會回覆你。"},{"en":"John needs time to speak to colleagues before replying to Sally.","zh":"John 需要時間與同事商量，然後才回覆 Sally。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when you cannot give a final answer immediately.","zh":"當你不能立即給出最終答案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make a booking","meaning":"預訂","examples":[{"en":"John hopes to make a booking soon.","zh":"John 希望很快預訂。"},{"en":"To make a booking means to reserve a place, visit, room, or service.","zh":"make a booking 意思是預留位置、參觀、房間或服務。"},{"en":"The teacher made a booking for thirty students at the museum.","zh":"老師為三十名學生預訂了博物館參觀。"},{"en":"John will make a booking if his colleagues agree to the park visit.","zh":"如果同事同意公園參觀，John 就會預訂。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when arranging trips, restaurants, hotels, and activities.","zh":"這個短語常用於安排旅行、餐廳、酒店和活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"look forward to hearing from you","meaning":"期待收到你的消息","examples":[{"en":"Sally says she will look forward to hearing from John.","zh":"Sally 說她期待收到 John 的消息。"},{"en":"Look forward to hearing from you means I hope to receive your reply later.","zh":"look forward to hearing from you 意思是我希望稍後收到你的回覆。"},{"en":"After sending an enquiry, you might write, “I look forward to hearing from you.”","zh":"發出查詢後，你可能會寫：「我期待收到你的消息。」"},{"en":"Sally says this politely because John will contact her again after discussing the visit.","zh":"Sally 禮貌地這樣說，因為 John 討論參觀後會再次聯絡她。"},{"en":"This phrase is common at the end of formal or friendly conversations.","zh":"這個短語常用於正式或友善對話的結尾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"subjects studied","meaning":"學習的科目","examples":[{"en":"Subjects studied in educational visits include science and geography.","zh":"教育參觀中學習的科目包括科學和地理。"},{"en":"Subjects studied are the school topics or learning areas covered during an activity.","zh":"subjects studied 是活動中涵蓋的學校科目或學習範疇。"},{"en":"On a museum visit, subjects studied may include history, art, and design.","zh":"在博物館參觀中，學習的科目可能包括歷史、藝術和設計。"},{"en":"The park visit covers several subjects, so teachers can connect it to the curriculum.","zh":"公園參觀涵蓋幾個科目，所以老師可以把它連繫到課程。"},{"en":"This phrase summarises what pupils will learn about.","zh":"這個短語總結學生會學習甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"benefits of outdoor educational visits","meaning":"戶外教育參觀的好處","examples":[{"en":"The benefits of outdoor educational visits include freedom and self-confidence.","zh":"戶外教育參觀的好處包括自由感和自信。"},{"en":"Benefits of outdoor educational visits are the good results children gain from learning outside.","zh":"benefits of outdoor educational visits 是孩子從戶外學習中得到的好處。"},{"en":"Benefits may include better observation, teamwork, and enjoyment of nature.","zh":"好處可能包括更好的觀察力、團隊合作和享受大自然。"},{"en":"These visits help children learn actively instead of only sitting in class.","zh":"這些參觀幫助孩子主動學習，而不只是坐在課室裏。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on why outdoor school trips are useful.","zh":"這個短語著重戶外學校旅行為何有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"gain self-confidence","meaning":"增強自信","examples":[{"en":"Children learn new skills and gain self-confidence.","zh":"孩子學習新技能並增強自信。"},{"en":"To gain self-confidence means to become more confident in your own ability.","zh":"gain self-confidence 意思是對自己的能力變得更有信心。"},{"en":"A child may gain self-confidence after learning to read a map alone.","zh":"孩子學會獨自閱讀地圖後，可能會增強自信。"},{"en":"Outdoor activities help children see that they can solve problems and try new tasks.","zh":"戶外活動幫助孩子看見自己能解決問題並嘗試新任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive personal change.","zh":"這個短語描述正面的個人成長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"practical issues","meaning":"實際安排事項","examples":[{"en":"The practical issues include cost and adult supervision.","zh":"實際安排事項包括費用和成人監督。"},{"en":"Practical issues are real arrangements or problems that must be considered.","zh":"practical issues 是必須考慮的實際安排或問題。"},{"en":"For a school trip, practical issues include transport, lunch, safety, and payment.","zh":"對學校旅行來說，實際安排事項包括交通、午餐、安全和付款。"},{"en":"John asks about practical issues because the school must plan carefully.","zh":"John 詢問實際安排事項，因為學校必須仔細計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how an idea will work in real life.","zh":"這個短語著重一個想法在現實中如何運作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cost per child","meaning":"每名孩子的費用","examples":[{"en":"The cost per child depends on the number of children attending.","zh":"每名孩子的費用取決於出席孩子的人數。"},{"en":"Cost per child means the amount paid for each individual child.","zh":"cost per child 意思是每一名孩子需要支付的金額。"},{"en":"The cost per child for the workshop is lower when the group is larger.","zh":"當團體較大時，工作坊每名孩子的費用較低。"},{"en":"John needs the cost per child to calculate the total price for the school.","zh":"John 需要知道每名孩子的費用，以計算學校總價。"},{"en":"This phrase helps schools plan budgets for trips.","zh":"這個短語幫助學校為旅行計劃預算。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 5/task-2":[{"front":"members of the Twinning Association","meaning":"友好城鎮協會的成員","examples":[{"en":"It is great to see so many members of the Twinning Association here tonight.","zh":"今晚很高興見到這麼多友好城鎮協會的成員。"},{"en":"Members of the Twinning Association are people who belong to a group that supports friendship between two towns.","zh":"友好城鎮協會的成員，是屬於一個支持兩個城鎮友誼團體的人。"},{"en":"Members of the Twinning Association may help organise visits, meals, and cultural events.","zh":"友好城鎮協會的成員可能會幫忙組織探訪、聚餐和文化活動。"},{"en":"When many members attend a meeting, the Association can plan larger activities.","zh":"當很多成員出席會議時，協會可以策劃更大型活動。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the people who support the twinning relationship.","zh":"這個短語指出支持友好城鎮關係的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"It’s great to see","meaning":"很高興見到","examples":[{"en":"It’s great to see so many members here tonight.","zh":"今晚很高興見到這麼多成員。"},{"en":"It’s great to see means I am pleased or happy to see something or someone.","zh":"It’s great to see 的意思是我很高興或很愉快看見某人或某事。"},{"en":"It’s great to see so many students joining the charity event.","zh":"很高興見到這麼多學生參加慈善活動。"},{"en":"Speakers often use this phrase to welcome an audience warmly.","zh":"演講者常用這個短語熱情歡迎聽眾。"},{"en":"It shows positive feeling at the beginning of a speech or meeting.","zh":"它在演講或會議開始時表達正面感受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"twinning link","meaning":"友好城鎮關係","examples":[{"en":"The twinning link between the two towns was established many years ago.","zh":"兩個城鎮之間的友好城鎮關係在多年前已建立。"},{"en":"A twinning link is an official friendship relationship between two towns, often in different countries.","zh":"友好城鎮關係，是兩個城鎮之間的正式友誼關係，通常位於不同國家。"},{"en":"A twinning link may lead to school exchanges, cultural visits, and community events.","zh":"友好城鎮關係可能帶來學校交流、文化探訪和社區活動。"},{"en":"Towns use a twinning link to learn from each other and build friendship.","zh":"城鎮利用友好城鎮關係互相學習並建立友誼。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in local government and community relations.","zh":"這個短語常用於地方政府和社區關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be established","meaning":"建立；成立","examples":[{"en":"The twinning link between Stanthorpe and Malatte was established.","zh":"Stanthorpe 和 Malatte 之間的友好城鎮關係已建立。"},{"en":"To be established means to be officially created or started.","zh":"建立或成立，意思是正式創立或開始。"},{"en":"The school club was established ten years ago by a group of teachers.","zh":"這個學校學會由一群老師在十年前成立。"},{"en":"Once a partnership is established, both sides can start planning activities.","zh":"一旦合作關係建立，雙方就可以開始策劃活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when talking about organisations, relationships, and systems.","zh":"這個短語常用於談論組織、關係和制度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the relationship between","meaning":"……之間的關係","examples":[{"en":"The relationship between the towns has grown stronger.","zh":"兩個城鎮之間的關係變得更強。"},{"en":"The relationship between two people or places means the connection they have with each other.","zh":"兩個人或地方之間的關係，意思是它們彼此之間的連繫。"},{"en":"The relationship between a school and parents improves when communication is clear.","zh":"當溝通清楚時，學校與家長之間的關係會改善。"},{"en":"A strong relationship between two towns can lead to regular visits and cooperation.","zh":"兩個城鎮之間的良好關係可以帶來定期探訪和合作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how two sides are connected.","zh":"這個短語着重兩方如何連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"go from strength to strength","meaning":"越來越好；日益壯大","examples":[{"en":"The relationship between the towns has gone from strength to strength.","zh":"兩個城鎮之間的關係越來越好。"},{"en":"To go from strength to strength means to become more successful or stronger over time.","zh":"Go from strength to strength 的意思是隨時間變得更成功或更強大。"},{"en":"The school music club has gone from strength to strength since more students joined.","zh":"自從更多學生加入後，學校音樂學會越來越好。"},{"en":"A community project can go from strength to strength if volunteers keep supporting it.","zh":"如果義工持續支持，社區項目可以日益壯大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes steady improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述穩步改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"spend a weekend in","meaning":"在……度過一個週末","examples":[{"en":"Members from Stanthorpe spent a weekend in Malatte.","zh":"來自 Stanthorpe 的成員在 Malatte 度過了一個週末。"},{"en":"To spend a weekend in a place means to stay there for Saturday and Sunday, or for a short weekend visit.","zh":"在某地度過一個週末，意思是在那裏逗留星期六和星期日，或作短暫週末探訪。"},{"en":"My family spent a weekend in a small seaside town.","zh":"我家人在一個海邊小鎮度過了一個週末。"},{"en":"Spending a weekend in another town gives visitors time to meet people and see local life.","zh":"在另一個城鎮度過週末，讓訪客有時間認識人和看看本地生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a short visit.","zh":"這個短語描述短暫探訪。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"our hosts","meaning":"我們的接待方","examples":[{"en":"Our hosts had arranged a great programme.","zh":"我們的接待方安排了一個很好的活動。"},{"en":"Our hosts are the people who welcome and look after us during a visit.","zh":"我們的接待方，是在探訪期間歡迎並照顧我們的人。"},{"en":"Our hosts prepared dinner and showed us around the town.","zh":"我們的接待方準備了晚餐，並帶我們參觀城鎮。"},{"en":"Good hosts help visitors feel comfortable and included.","zh":"好的接待方會讓訪客感到舒服和被接納。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the people receiving guests.","zh":"這個短語指接待客人的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"arrange a programme","meaning":"安排活動","examples":[{"en":"The hosts arranged a great programme for the visitors.","zh":"接待方為訪客安排了一個很好的活動。"},{"en":"To arrange a programme means to plan a series of activities or events.","zh":"安排活動，意思是策劃一系列活動或項目。"},{"en":"The school arranged a programme of talks, games, and visits for exchange students.","zh":"學校為交流生安排了講座、遊戲和參觀活動。"},{"en":"A well-arranged programme helps visitors know what will happen each day.","zh":"安排得好的活動可以幫助訪客知道每天會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about organised visits.","zh":"這個短語適合用於談論有組織的探訪。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be produced in the region","meaning":"在該地區生產","examples":[{"en":"The group learned how cheese is produced in the region.","zh":"小組了解芝士如何在該地區生產。"},{"en":"To be produced in the region means to be made in that local area.","zh":"在該地區生產，意思是在那個本地區域製造。"},{"en":"Visitors learned how olive oil is produced in the region around the village.","zh":"訪客了解橄欖油如何在村莊周邊地區生產。"},{"en":"Products produced in the region often reflect local climate, skills, and traditions.","zh":"在該地區生產的產品通常反映本地氣候、技術和傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a product with its place of origin.","zh":"這個短語把產品與其來源地連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the region","meaning":"在該地區","examples":[{"en":"Cheese is produced in the region around Malatte.","zh":"芝士在 Malatte 周邊地區生產。"},{"en":"In the region means in that particular area or part of the country.","zh":"在該地區，意思是在那個特定地區或國家的一部分。"},{"en":"Apples grow well in the region because the climate is cool.","zh":"蘋果在該地區生長良好，因為氣候涼爽。"},{"en":"Local products in the region can attract visitors and support farmers.","zh":"該地區的本地產品可以吸引訪客並支持農民。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a geographical area.","zh":"這個短語描述地理區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have the chance to","meaning":"有機會","examples":[{"en":"The visitors had the chance to taste local products.","zh":"訪客有機會品嚐本地產品。"},{"en":"To have the chance to do something means to have the opportunity to do it.","zh":"有機會做某事，意思是有做該事的機會。"},{"en":"Students had the chance to speak with visitors from another country.","zh":"學生有機會與來自另一個國家的訪客交談。"},{"en":"Having the chance to try local food makes a visit more memorable.","zh":"有機會嘗試本地食物，會令探訪更難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on opportunity.","zh":"這個短語着重機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"taste the products","meaning":"品嚐產品","examples":[{"en":"The visitors tasted the products during the visit.","zh":"訪客在探訪期間品嚐了產品。"},{"en":"To taste the products means to try small amounts of food or drink to experience their flavour.","zh":"品嚐產品，意思是嘗試少量食物或飲品，以體驗其味道。"},{"en":"Visitors tasted the products at the farm shop before buying them.","zh":"訪客在農場商店購買前品嚐了產品。"},{"en":"Tasting local products helps people understand the region’s food culture.","zh":"品嚐本地產品有助人們了解該地區的飲食文化。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in visits to farms, markets, and factories.","zh":"這個短語常見於農場、市集和工廠參觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"theme park trip","meaning":"主題公園之旅","examples":[{"en":"The theme park trip had to be cancelled.","zh":"主題公園之旅不得不取消。"},{"en":"A theme park trip is a visit to an amusement park with rides and attractions.","zh":"主題公園之旅，是到有機動遊戲和景點的遊樂園參觀。"},{"en":"The school planned a theme park trip for the end of term.","zh":"學校計劃在學期末舉辦主題公園之旅。"},{"en":"A theme park trip may be cancelled if the weather is unsafe.","zh":"如果天氣不安全，主題公園之旅可能會取消。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an organised leisure visit.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的休閒探訪。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have to be cancelled","meaning":"不得不取消","examples":[{"en":"The theme park trip had to be cancelled.","zh":"主題公園之旅不得不取消。"},{"en":"To have to be cancelled means it must be stopped or not take place.","zh":"不得不取消，意思是必須停止或不能舉行。"},{"en":"The outdoor concert had to be cancelled because of heavy rain.","zh":"戶外音樂會因大雨不得不取消。"},{"en":"Events sometimes have to be cancelled for safety reasons.","zh":"活動有時因安全原因不得不取消。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that cancellation was necessary, not just a choice.","zh":"這個短語顯示取消是必要的，而不只是選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have a great time","meaning":"玩得很開心","examples":[{"en":"The visitors had a great time on the final boat trip.","zh":"訪客在最後的乘船遊河中玩得很開心。"},{"en":"To have a great time means to enjoy an experience very much.","zh":"玩得很開心，意思是非常享受某次經歷。"},{"en":"Children had a great time at the school fair.","zh":"孩子們在學校嘉年華玩得很開心。"},{"en":"If visitors have a great time, they may want to return next year.","zh":"如果訪客玩得很開心，他們可能明年想再來。"},{"en":"This phrase is friendly and common in informal speech.","zh":"這個短語友善而常見於口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the final boat trip","meaning":"最後的乘船遊河","examples":[{"en":"The final boat trip down the river was the highlight.","zh":"最後的沿河乘船遊河是亮點。"},{"en":"The final boat trip means the last organised journey by boat in a programme.","zh":"最後的乘船遊河，意思是活動安排中最後一次坐船旅程。"},{"en":"The final boat trip gave visitors a relaxing end to the weekend.","zh":"最後的乘船遊河為訪客的週末帶來輕鬆結尾。"},{"en":"A final activity can leave visitors with a strong memory.","zh":"最後一項活動可以給訪客留下深刻記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the last boat activity in a visit.","zh":"這個短語標示探訪中的最後一次乘船活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"down the river","meaning":"沿河而下","examples":[{"en":"The visitors enjoyed a boat trip down the river.","zh":"訪客享受了一次沿河而下的乘船遊河。"},{"en":"Down the river means along the river, usually following the direction of the water flow.","zh":"沿河而下，意思是沿着河流前進，通常順着水流方向。"},{"en":"We took a small boat down the river to see the old bridge.","zh":"我們乘小船沿河而下，去看舊橋。"},{"en":"A trip down the river can show visitors scenery from a different angle.","zh":"沿河而下的旅程可以讓訪客從不同角度欣賞景色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement along a river.","zh":"這個短語描述沿河移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the real highlight","meaning":"真正的亮點","examples":[{"en":"The boat trip was the real highlight of the weekend.","zh":"乘船遊河是週末真正的亮點。"},{"en":"The real highlight is the most enjoyable or memorable part of an event.","zh":"真正的亮點，是活動中最令人享受或最難忘的部分。"},{"en":"The real highlight of the school trip was meeting the artist.","zh":"學校旅行真正的亮點是見到那位藝術家。"},{"en":"Calling something the real highlight shows it stood out from everything else.","zh":"稱某事為真正的亮點，表示它比其他部分更突出。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to praise the best part of an experience.","zh":"這個短語用來讚賞一次經歷中最好的部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a special year for","meaning":"對……來說特別的一年","examples":[{"en":"This is a special year for the Association.","zh":"今年對協會來說是特別的一年。"},{"en":"A special year for someone or an organisation is a year with an important event or meaning.","zh":"對某人或組織來說特別的一年，是有重要事件或意義的一年。"},{"en":"This is a special year for the school because it is celebrating its 50th anniversary.","zh":"今年對學校來說是特別的一年，因為它正在慶祝 50 週年。"},{"en":"A special year often includes ceremonies, gifts, or community events.","zh":"特別的一年通常包括典禮、禮物或社區活動。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a year with a meaningful occasion.","zh":"這個短語把某一年與有意義的場合連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"25 years since","meaning":"自……以來 25 年","examples":[{"en":"It is 25 years since the Association was founded.","zh":"自協會成立以來已有 25 年。"},{"en":"25 years since means 25 years have passed after an event happened.","zh":"自……以來 25 年，意思是某事件發生後已過了 25 年。"},{"en":"It is 10 years since our school moved to this campus.","zh":"自我們學校搬到這個校園以來已有 10 年。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for anniversaries.","zh":"這個短語常用於週年紀念。"},{"en":"It connects the present with an important moment in the past.","zh":"它把現在與過去的重要時刻連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be founded","meaning":"成立","examples":[{"en":"The Twinning Association was founded 25 years ago.","zh":"友好城鎮協會在 25 年前成立。"},{"en":"To be founded means to be started or established as an organisation.","zh":"成立，意思是作為一個組織被創立或建立。"},{"en":"The charity was founded by local volunteers.","zh":"這個慈善機構由本地義工成立。"},{"en":"Knowing when an organisation was founded helps explain its history.","zh":"知道一個組織何時成立，有助解釋其歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in formal descriptions of groups and institutions.","zh":"這個短語常用於正式描述團體和機構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"mark this by doing something","meaning":"以做某事來紀念","examples":[{"en":"Malatte will mark this by building a footbridge.","zh":"Malatte 會以建造人行橋來紀念這件事。"},{"en":"To mark this by doing something means to celebrate or remember an event through an action.","zh":"以做某事來紀念，意思是透過某個行動慶祝或記住一件事。"},{"en":"The school marked its anniversary by planting trees.","zh":"學校以種樹來紀念週年。"},{"en":"Marking an event with a lasting object can help people remember it.","zh":"以持久物件紀念事件，可以幫助人們記住它。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a celebration with a symbolic action.","zh":"這個短語把慶祝與象徵性行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"build a footbridge","meaning":"建造人行橋","examples":[{"en":"They plan to build a footbridge in the municipal park.","zh":"他們計劃在市政公園建造人行橋。"},{"en":"To build a footbridge means to construct a small bridge for people to walk across.","zh":"建造人行橋，意思是建造一座供人步行通過的小橋。"},{"en":"The council built a footbridge over the stream so children could cross safely.","zh":"議會在溪流上建造人行橋，讓孩子安全通過。"},{"en":"A footbridge can improve access to a park or garden.","zh":"人行橋可以改善公園或花園的通行。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to building a bridge for pedestrians, not cars.","zh":"這個短語指建造供行人使用的橋，而不是汽車橋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"municipal park","meaning":"市政公園","examples":[{"en":"The footbridge will be built in the municipal park.","zh":"人行橋將建在市政公園內。"},{"en":"A municipal park is a public park managed by the town or city authority.","zh":"市政公園，是由城鎮或城市管理部門管理的公共公園。"},{"en":"Families often use a municipal park for walks, picnics, and sports.","zh":"家庭常在市政公園散步、野餐和做運動。"},{"en":"A new footbridge in a municipal park can benefit many residents.","zh":"市政公園內的新行人橋可以令許多居民受惠。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a public local-government park.","zh":"這個短語指由地方政府管理的公共公園。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"decide to do something","meaning":"決定做某事","examples":[{"en":"The Association decided to plant a poplar tree.","zh":"協會決定種一棵白楊樹。"},{"en":"To decide to do something means to choose a course of action after thinking about it.","zh":"決定做某事，意思是在思考後選擇一個行動。"},{"en":"The class decided to hold a charity sale.","zh":"班上決定舉辦慈善義賣。"},{"en":"A group decision can help everyone support the same plan.","zh":"小組決定可以幫助大家支持同一個計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an action was chosen deliberately.","zh":"這個短語顯示某行動是經過選擇而作出的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"plant a poplar tree","meaning":"種一棵白楊樹","examples":[{"en":"They will plant a poplar tree in the museum gardens.","zh":"他們會在博物館花園種一棵白楊樹。"},{"en":"To plant a poplar tree means to put a young poplar tree into the ground so it can grow.","zh":"種一棵白楊樹，意思是把一棵幼白楊樹種入泥土，讓它生長。"},{"en":"The town planted a poplar tree to celebrate the new partnership.","zh":"城鎮種了一棵白楊樹來慶祝新的夥伴關係。"},{"en":"Planting a tree can be a living symbol of friendship.","zh":"種樹可以成為友誼的有生命象徵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both a practical and symbolic action.","zh":"這個短語描述實際和象徵性的行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"museum gardens","meaning":"博物館花園","examples":[{"en":"The tree will be planted in the museum gardens.","zh":"這棵樹將種在博物館花園。"},{"en":"Museum gardens are outdoor garden areas belonging to or connected with a museum.","zh":"博物館花園，是屬於或連接博物館的戶外花園範圍。"},{"en":"Visitors may walk through the museum gardens after seeing the exhibition.","zh":"訪客參觀展覽後可能會在博物館花園散步。"},{"en":"A tree in museum gardens can become part of the site’s memory and beauty.","zh":"博物館花園中的樹可以成為該地記憶和美感的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the place where the tree will be planted.","zh":"這個短語指出樹將種植的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"consider doing something","meaning":"考慮做某事","examples":[{"en":"They considered buying a garden seat.","zh":"他們考慮購買一張花園長椅。"},{"en":"To consider doing something means to think about doing it before deciding.","zh":"考慮做某事，意思是在決定前思考是否做該事。"},{"en":"The committee considered holding the event outdoors.","zh":"委員會考慮在戶外舉辦活動。"},{"en":"Considering an idea does not mean the group will definitely do it.","zh":"考慮一個想法並不表示小組一定會做。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an option was discussed.","zh":"這個短語顯示某個選項曾被討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"garden seat","meaning":"花園長椅","examples":[{"en":"They considered buying a garden seat for the museum gardens.","zh":"他們曾考慮為博物館花園購買花園長椅。"},{"en":"A garden seat is a bench or chair placed outdoors for people to sit on.","zh":"花園長椅，是放在戶外供人坐下的長椅或椅子。"},{"en":"Visitors can rest on a garden seat after walking around the museum grounds.","zh":"訪客在博物館園區四處走後，可以坐在花園長椅上休息。"},{"en":"A garden seat may be useful, but it may not be suitable for every historic garden.","zh":"花園長椅可能有用，但未必適合每個歷史花園。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to outdoor seating.","zh":"這個短語指戶外座位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the authorities","meaning":"主管當局；有關部門","examples":[{"en":"The authorities were not happy with the idea.","zh":"有關部門不贊成這個想法。"},{"en":"The authorities are the official people or organisations with power to make decisions.","zh":"主管當局，是有權作決定的官方人士或組織。"},{"en":"The authorities may approve or reject changes in a public park.","zh":"有關部門可能批准或拒絕公共公園的改動。"},{"en":"If the authorities disagree with a plan, the group may need another idea.","zh":"如果有關部門不同意計劃，小組可能需要另一個想法。"},{"en":"This phrase often refers to official decision-makers.","zh":"這個短語常指官方決策者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be happy with an idea","meaning":"贊成某個想法","examples":[{"en":"The authorities were not happy with the idea of a garden seat.","zh":"有關部門不贊成花園長椅這個想法。"},{"en":"To be happy with an idea means to approve of it or feel satisfied with it.","zh":"贊成某個想法，意思是認可它或對它感到滿意。"},{"en":"The teacher was happy with the idea of a class exhibition.","zh":"老師贊成舉辦班級展覽這個想法。"},{"en":"If officials are not happy with an idea, they may ask for changes.","zh":"如果官員不贊成某個想法，他們可能會要求修改。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses approval or disapproval.","zh":"這個短語表達認可或不認可。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in terms of","meaning":"在……方面","examples":[{"en":"In terms of fundraising, the Association has done very well.","zh":"在籌款方面，協會做得很好。"},{"en":"In terms of means when considering a particular subject or area.","zh":"In terms of 的意思是從某個特定主題或方面來看。"},{"en":"In terms of cost, the bus trip is the best choice.","zh":"在成本方面，巴士旅行是最佳選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase helps focus discussion on one aspect of a topic.","zh":"這個短語有助把討論集中在某一方面。"},{"en":"It is common in formal speech and reports.","zh":"它常見於正式演講和報告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fundraising","meaning":"籌款","examples":[{"en":"The Association has done very well in fundraising.","zh":"協會在籌款方面做得很好。"},{"en":"Fundraising means collecting money to support an organisation, project, or cause.","zh":"籌款，意思是收集金錢以支持組織、項目或公益目的。"},{"en":"Students organised a cake sale for fundraising.","zh":"學生舉辦蛋糕義賣來籌款。"},{"en":"Successful fundraising can pay for events, travel, or community projects.","zh":"成功籌款可以支付活動、旅行或社區項目的費用。"},{"en":"This word describes the process of raising money.","zh":"這個詞描述籌集款項的過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"support our activities","meaning":"支持我們的活動","examples":[{"en":"The fundraising helps support the Association’s activities.","zh":"籌款有助支持協會的活動。"},{"en":"To support our activities means to provide money, help, or resources so our events can continue.","zh":"支持我們的活動，意思是提供金錢、幫助或資源，讓我們的活動能繼續。"},{"en":"Ticket sales help support our activities throughout the year.","zh":"門票收入有助全年支持我們的活動。"},{"en":"Without funds to support activities, a community group may have to cancel events.","zh":"如果沒有資金支持活動，社區團體可能不得不取消活動。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose of raising money.","zh":"這個短語解釋籌款的目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"do very well","meaning":"做得很好","examples":[{"en":"The Association has done very well in fundraising.","zh":"協會在籌款方面做得很好。"},{"en":"To do very well means to perform successfully or achieve good results.","zh":"做得很好，意思是表現成功或取得好結果。"},{"en":"The class did very well in the charity competition.","zh":"班級在慈善比賽中做得很好。"},{"en":"If an event does very well, the organisers may repeat it next year.","zh":"如果活動做得很好，主辦者可能明年再次舉辦。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a positive judgement about performance.","zh":"這個短語對表現給出正面評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pancake evening","meaning":"煎餅晚會","examples":[{"en":"The pancake evening was well attended.","zh":"煎餅晚會出席人數很多。"},{"en":"A pancake evening is an evening event where people eat pancakes, often to raise money or socialise.","zh":"煎餅晚會，是人們在晚上一起吃煎餅的活動，通常用於籌款或社交。"},{"en":"The school held a pancake evening to support the music club.","zh":"學校舉辦煎餅晚會來支持音樂學會。"},{"en":"A pancake evening can be simple, friendly, and good for fundraising.","zh":"煎餅晚會可以簡單、友善，而且適合籌款。"},{"en":"This phrase names a community food event.","zh":"這個短語命名一個社區食物活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be well attended","meaning":"出席人數很多","examples":[{"en":"The pancake evening was well attended.","zh":"煎餅晚會出席人數很多。"},{"en":"To be well attended means many people came to the event.","zh":"出席人數很多，意思是有很多人來參加活動。"},{"en":"The school concert was well attended by parents and students.","zh":"學校音樂會有很多家長和學生出席。"},{"en":"A well-attended event usually raises more money and feels more successful.","zh":"出席人數很多的活動通常能籌得更多款項，也感覺更成功。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong participation.","zh":"這個短語描述參與度高。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make record profits","meaning":"創下最高收益","examples":[{"en":"The pancake evening made record profits.","zh":"煎餅晚會創下最高收益。"},{"en":"To make record profits means to earn more profit than ever before.","zh":"創下最高收益，意思是賺取比以往任何時候都多的利潤。"},{"en":"The charity fair made record profits after hundreds of people attended.","zh":"數百人出席後，慈善市集創下最高收益。"},{"en":"Record profits show that an event was financially very successful.","zh":"最高收益顯示活動在財政上非常成功。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when comparing this year’s result with previous years.","zh":"這個短語常用於把今年結果與往年比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"demonstration of French cookery","meaning":"法式料理示範","examples":[{"en":"Everyone enjoyed the demonstration of French cookery.","zh":"大家都很享受法式料理示範。"},{"en":"A demonstration of French cookery is an event where someone shows how to cook French food.","zh":"法式料理示範，是有人展示如何烹調法國食物的活動。"},{"en":"A chef gave a demonstration of French cookery at the community hall.","zh":"一位廚師在社區禮堂進行法式料理示範。"},{"en":"Cookery demonstrations help people learn by watching each step.","zh":"烹飪示範幫助人們透過觀看每個步驟學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical food-learning event.","zh":"這個短語描述實用的飲食學習活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"French cookery","meaning":"法式烹飪","examples":[{"en":"The demonstration of French cookery was nearly as successful.","zh":"法式烹飪示範幾乎同樣成功。"},{"en":"French cookery means the style, methods, and dishes of French cooking.","zh":"法式烹飪，意思是法國料理的風格、方法和菜式。"},{"en":"French cookery may include sauces, pastries, soups, and regional dishes.","zh":"法式烹飪可能包括醬汁、糕點、湯和地區菜式。"},{"en":"A lesson in French cookery can introduce people to another culture.","zh":"法式烹飪課可以向人們介紹另一種文化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to cooking traditions from France.","zh":"這個短語指來自法國的烹飪傳統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"nearly as successful","meaning":"幾乎同樣成功","examples":[{"en":"The cookery demonstration was nearly as successful as the pancake evening.","zh":"烹飪示範幾乎與煎餅晚會同樣成功。"},{"en":"Nearly as successful means almost equally successful, but a little less.","zh":"幾乎同樣成功，意思是差不多一樣成功，但稍微少一點。"},{"en":"The second concert was nearly as successful as the first one.","zh":"第二場音樂會幾乎與第一場同樣成功。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two good results.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個好結果。"},{"en":"It suggests that one event did very well, though not quite as well as another.","zh":"它表示某活動做得很好，雖然不完全及得上另一個。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"film show","meaning":"電影放映活動","examples":[{"en":"Numbers for the film show were limited because of the venue.","zh":"電影放映活動的人數因場地而受限。"},{"en":"A film show is an event where people gather to watch a film.","zh":"電影放映活動，是人們聚在一起觀看電影的活動。"},{"en":"The Association organised a film show about French village life.","zh":"協會組織了一場關於法國鄉村生活的電影放映活動。"},{"en":"A film show needs enough seats, a screen, and sound equipment.","zh":"電影放映活動需要足夠座位、螢幕和音響設備。"},{"en":"This phrase names a public or community movie event.","zh":"這個短語命名公共或社區電影活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be limited because of","meaning":"因……而受限","examples":[{"en":"Numbers were limited because of the venue.","zh":"人數因場地而受限。"},{"en":"To be limited because of something means to be restricted by that reason.","zh":"因某事而受限，意思是因該原因受到限制。"},{"en":"The number of guests was limited because of the small room.","zh":"由於房間很小，嘉賓人數受到限制。"},{"en":"If an event is limited because of space, organisers may need a larger venue next time.","zh":"如果活動因空間而受限，主辦者下次可能需要較大場地。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the cause of a restriction.","zh":"這個短語解釋限制的原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the venue","meaning":"場地","examples":[{"en":"The venue was not large enough for the film show.","zh":"場地不夠大，容納不了電影放映活動。"},{"en":"The venue is the place where an event happens.","zh":"場地，是活動舉行的地方。"},{"en":"The school hall was chosen as the venue for the concert.","zh":"學校禮堂被選為音樂會場地。"},{"en":"A good venue should have enough space, seats, and equipment.","zh":"好場地應有足夠空間、座位和設備。"},{"en":"This word is useful when planning events.","zh":"這個詞在策劃活動時很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"look for somewhere bigger","meaning":"尋找更大的地方","examples":[{"en":"The Association is looking for somewhere bigger next year.","zh":"協會正在為明年尋找更大的地方。"},{"en":"To look for somewhere bigger means to search for a larger place.","zh":"尋找更大的地方，意思是搜尋較大的場所。"},{"en":"The club is looking for somewhere bigger because more students want to join.","zh":"學會正在尋找更大的地方，因為更多學生想加入。"},{"en":"If an event becomes popular, organisers may need to look for somewhere bigger.","zh":"如果活動變得受歡迎，主辦者可能需要尋找更大的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when a venue is too small.","zh":"當場地太小時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"look forward to welcoming","meaning":"期待迎接","examples":[{"en":"The Association is looking forward to welcoming its French visitors.","zh":"協會期待迎接法國訪客。"},{"en":"To look forward to welcoming someone means to feel happy and excited about receiving them.","zh":"期待迎接某人，意思是對接待他們感到高興和期待。"},{"en":"The school is looking forward to welcoming exchange students next month.","zh":"學校期待下月迎接交流生。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds polite and warm in speeches and letters.","zh":"這個短語在演講和信件中聽起來禮貌而親切。"},{"en":"It shows positive expectation before guests arrive.","zh":"它顯示客人到達前的正面期待。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"French visitors","meaning":"法國訪客","examples":[{"en":"The French visitors will arrive next week.","zh":"法國訪客將於下星期到達。"},{"en":"French visitors are guests from France.","zh":"法國訪客，是來自法國的客人。"},{"en":"The French visitors stayed with local families during the exchange.","zh":"法國訪客在交流期間住在本地家庭。"},{"en":"Welcoming French visitors can help people practise language and learn culture.","zh":"迎接法國訪客可以幫助人們練習語言和學習文化。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies visitors by nationality.","zh":"這個短語以國籍識別訪客。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"host individuals or families","meaning":"接待個人或家庭","examples":[{"en":"Many members will be hosting individuals or families.","zh":"許多成員將會接待個人或家庭。"},{"en":"To host individuals or families means to welcome single visitors or family groups into your home or community.","zh":"接待個人或家庭，意思是歡迎單獨訪客或家庭團體到家中或社區。"},{"en":"Local members hosted families from the twin town for the weekend.","zh":"本地成員在週末接待來自友好城鎮的家庭。"},{"en":"Hosting visitors includes providing food, conversation, and practical help.","zh":"接待訪客包括提供食物、交流和實際幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal hospitality.","zh":"這個短語描述個人款待。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the coach from France","meaning":"來自法國的旅遊巴士","examples":[{"en":"The coach from France will arrive at 5 pm on Friday.","zh":"來自法國的旅遊巴士會在星期五下午五點抵達。"},{"en":"The coach from France means the bus carrying visitors from France.","zh":"來自法國的旅遊巴士，意思是載着法國訪客的巴士。"},{"en":"Hosts waited near the hall for the coach from France.","zh":"接待家庭在禮堂附近等候來自法國的旅遊巴士。"},{"en":"Knowing when the coach arrives helps families prepare to meet their guests.","zh":"知道旅遊巴士何時抵達，有助家庭準備接待客人。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both the vehicle and where it comes from.","zh":"這個短語同時指出車輛和來源地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"arrive at","meaning":"在……抵達","examples":[{"en":"The coach from France will arrive at 5 pm.","zh":"來自法國的旅遊巴士會在下午五點抵達。"},{"en":"Arrive at a time means reach a place at that time.","zh":"在某時間抵達，意思是在該時間到達某地。"},{"en":"The train will arrive at 8:30 in the morning.","zh":"火車會在早上八點半抵達。"},{"en":"When guests arrive at a fixed time, hosts can plan meals and transport.","zh":"當客人在固定時間抵達時，接待方可以安排膳食和交通。"},{"en":"This phrase is commonly used with times and places.","zh":"這個短語常與時間和地點一起使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"try to do too much","meaning":"嘗試安排太多事情","examples":[{"en":"Hosts should not try to do too much on the first evening.","zh":"接待家庭不應在第一晚嘗試安排太多事情。"},{"en":"To try to do too much means to plan or attempt more than is sensible or comfortable.","zh":"嘗試做太多事情，意思是計劃或嘗試超過合理或舒服程度的事情。"},{"en":"After a long journey, visitors may feel tired if hosts try to do too much.","zh":"長途旅程後，如果接待方嘗試安排太多事情，訪客可能會感到疲倦。"},{"en":"Trying to do too much can make an evening stressful instead of enjoyable.","zh":"嘗試安排太多事情可以令晚上變得有壓力，而不是愉快。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against overplanning.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們不要過度計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"that first evening","meaning":"第一晚","examples":[{"en":"The visitors will be tired that first evening.","zh":"訪客第一晚會很疲倦。"},{"en":"That first evening means the evening when the visitors first arrive.","zh":"第一晚，意思是訪客剛到達的那個晚上。"},{"en":"On that first evening, the exchange students only wanted a quiet meal.","zh":"在第一晚，交流生只想吃一頓安靜的飯。"},{"en":"The first evening of a visit should usually be simple and relaxed.","zh":"探訪的第一晚通常應簡單而輕鬆。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a specific early moment in a visit.","zh":"這個短語指探訪初期的一個特定時刻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have dinner in the house or garden","meaning":"在屋內或花園吃晚飯","examples":[{"en":"Hosts should have dinner in the house or garden.","zh":"接待家庭應在屋內或花園吃晚飯。"},{"en":"To have dinner in the house or garden means to eat the evening meal at home, either indoors or outside.","zh":"在屋內或花園吃晚飯，意思是在家中吃晚餐，可以在室內或戶外。"},{"en":"Families may have dinner in the garden when the weather is warm.","zh":"天氣暖和時，家庭可能會在花園吃晚飯。"},{"en":"Having dinner at home can help visitors relax after travelling.","zh":"在家吃晚飯可以幫助訪客在旅程後放鬆。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a simple, welcoming first evening.","zh":"這個短語建議第一晚簡單而有歡迎感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Hosts should have dinner at home rather than eating out.","zh":"接待家庭應在家吃晚飯，而不是外出用餐。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of, and it shows a choice between two options.","zh":"Rather than 的意思是而不是，用來顯示兩個選項之間的選擇。"},{"en":"We walked to the park rather than taking the bus.","zh":"我們步行去公園，而不是乘巴士。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly shows which option is preferred.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示較被偏好的選項。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving advice or explaining a decision.","zh":"它適合用來給建議或解釋決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"eating out","meaning":"外出用餐","examples":[{"en":"The guide suggests eating at home instead of eating out.","zh":"指南建議在家吃飯，而不是外出用餐。"},{"en":"Eating out means eating a meal in a restaurant or café instead of at home.","zh":"外出用餐，意思是在餐廳或咖啡店吃飯，而不是在家。"},{"en":"Many families enjoy eating out on birthdays.","zh":"許多家庭喜歡在生日外出用餐。"},{"en":"After a long journey, eating out may feel tiring for guests.","zh":"長途旅程後，外出用餐對客人來說可能會很累。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common social activity.","zh":"這個短語描述常見社交活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"look as if","meaning":"看起來好像","examples":[{"en":"The weather looks as if it will be OK.","zh":"天氣看起來好像會不錯。"},{"en":"Look as if means seem likely, based on what we can see or know.","zh":"Look as if 的意思是根據我們看見或知道的情況，似乎可能如此。"},{"en":"The sky looks as if it will rain later.","zh":"天空看起來好像稍後會下雨。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when making a guess from signs or evidence.","zh":"這個短語用於根據跡象或證據作猜測。"},{"en":"It is less certain than saying something will definitely happen.","zh":"它比說某事一定會發生較不肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"plan a barbecue","meaning":"安排燒烤","examples":[{"en":"Hosts might like to plan a barbecue.","zh":"接待家庭可能想安排燒烤。"},{"en":"To plan a barbecue means to organise an outdoor meal where food is cooked on a grill.","zh":"安排燒烤，意思是組織一頓在戶外用烤爐烹調食物的餐。"},{"en":"The family planned a barbecue in the garden for their visitors.","zh":"這家人在花園為訪客安排燒烤。"},{"en":"Planning a barbecue requires food, equipment, good weather, and enough seats.","zh":"安排燒烤需要食物、設備、好天氣和足夠座位。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arranging a relaxed outdoor meal.","zh":"這個短語描述安排輕鬆的戶外餐。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"market day","meaning":"市集日","examples":[{"en":"The next morning is market day in town.","zh":"第二天早上是鎮上的市集日。"},{"en":"Market day is the day when stalls or sellers gather to sell goods in a town.","zh":"市集日，是小販或商戶聚集在城鎮出售貨品的日子。"},{"en":"On market day, people may buy fruit, cheese, bread, and handmade products.","zh":"在市集日，人們可能購買水果、芝士、麵包和手工產品。"},{"en":"Market day is a good chance for visitors to see local life.","zh":"市集日是訪客觀看本地生活的好機會。"},{"en":"This phrase names a regular community shopping event.","zh":"這個短語命名定期社區購物活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"stroll round","meaning":"四處散步逛逛","examples":[{"en":"The market is a good place to stroll round.","zh":"市集是四處散步逛逛的好地方。"},{"en":"To stroll round means to walk around slowly and casually, often for enjoyment.","zh":"四處散步逛逛，意思是慢慢而輕鬆地到處走，通常是為了享受。"},{"en":"Visitors strolled round the old streets after lunch.","zh":"訪客午飯後在舊街道四處散步。"},{"en":"Strolling round a market lets people look without rushing.","zh":"在市集四處逛逛，讓人們不用趕急也能觀看。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relaxed walking.","zh":"這個短語描述輕鬆步行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"meet up at","meaning":"在……集合","examples":[{"en":"Everyone will meet up at the football club on Saturday evening.","zh":"大家會在星期六晚上於足球會集合。"},{"en":"To meet up at a place means to gather there by arrangement.","zh":"在某地集合，意思是按安排在那裏聚集。"},{"en":"The students will meet up at the station before the trip.","zh":"學生會在旅行前於車站集合。"},{"en":"Giving a clear meeting place helps everyone arrive together.","zh":"給出清楚集合地點有助大家一起到達。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when organising group activities.","zh":"這個短語常用於組織小組活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"once again","meaning":"再次","examples":[{"en":"Once again, Toby Sharp and his band will perform.","zh":"Toby Sharp 和他的樂隊將再次演出。"},{"en":"Once again means one more time, especially after something happened before.","zh":"Once again 的意思是再一次，尤其是某事之前已發生過。"},{"en":"Once again, the school choir won first prize.","zh":"學校合唱團再次獲得一等獎。"},{"en":"This phrase shows repetition of an event or action.","zh":"這個短語顯示事件或行動重複發生。"},{"en":"It often suggests that something familiar is happening again.","zh":"它通常表示熟悉的事情再次發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"his band","meaning":"他的樂隊","examples":[{"en":"Toby Sharp and his band will perform country songs.","zh":"Toby Sharp 和他的樂隊將演唱鄉村歌曲。"},{"en":"His band means the group of musicians who perform with him.","zh":"他的樂隊，意思是與他一起演出的音樂人團體。"},{"en":"The singer arrived with his band before the concert.","zh":"歌手在音樂會前與他的樂隊一起到達。"},{"en":"A band usually includes singers and musicians playing instruments.","zh":"樂隊通常包括歌手和演奏樂器的音樂人。"},{"en":"This phrase connects the musical group with its leader or main performer.","zh":"這個短語把音樂團體與其領隊或主要表演者連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"perform country songs","meaning":"演唱鄉村歌曲","examples":[{"en":"The band will perform English and Scottish country songs.","zh":"樂隊將演唱英格蘭及蘇格蘭鄉村歌曲。"},{"en":"To perform country songs means to sing or play traditional or folk-style songs from the countryside or a country tradition.","zh":"演唱鄉村歌曲，意思是演唱或演奏來自鄉村或某國傳統的民間風格歌曲。"},{"en":"The school band performed country songs at the cultural evening.","zh":"學校樂隊在文化晚會演唱鄉村歌曲。"},{"en":"Performing country songs can introduce visitors to local musical traditions.","zh":"演唱鄉村歌曲可以向訪客介紹本地音樂傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a musical performance.","zh":"這個短語描述音樂表演。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"English and Scottish country songs","meaning":"英格蘭及蘇格蘭鄉村歌曲","examples":[{"en":"The band will perform English and Scottish country songs.","zh":"樂隊將演唱英格蘭及蘇格蘭鄉村歌曲。"},{"en":"English and Scottish country songs are traditional or folk-style songs from England and Scotland.","zh":"英格蘭及蘇格蘭鄉村歌曲，是來自英格蘭和蘇格蘭的傳統或民間風格歌曲。"},{"en":"English and Scottish country songs may be played at community dances or cultural events.","zh":"英格蘭及蘇格蘭鄉村歌曲可能在社區舞會或文化活動中演奏。"},{"en":"These songs can help visitors experience local heritage.","zh":"這些歌曲可以幫助訪客體驗本地文化遺產。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the cultural origin of the music.","zh":"這個短語指出音樂的文化來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be well known to","meaning":"為……所熟悉","examples":[{"en":"Toby Sharp will already be well known to many members.","zh":"Toby Sharp 已經為許多成員所熟悉。"},{"en":"To be well known to someone means to be familiar to that person or group.","zh":"為某人所熟悉，意思是被該人或群體認識。"},{"en":"The local singer is well known to families in the town.","zh":"這位本地歌手為鎮上的家庭所熟悉。"},{"en":"If a performer is well known to the audience, people may feel more excited to hear him.","zh":"如果表演者為觀眾所熟悉，人們可能會更期待聽他演出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes familiarity or recognition.","zh":"這個短語描述熟悉度或認識程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"organise a quiz night","meaning":"組織問答之夜","examples":[{"en":"Toby organised the special quiz night last year.","zh":"Toby 去年組織了特別問答之夜。"},{"en":"To organise a quiz night means to plan an evening event where teams answer questions.","zh":"組織問答之夜，意思是策劃一個晚上活動，讓隊伍回答問題。"},{"en":"The club organised a quiz night to raise money.","zh":"學會組織問答之夜來籌款。"},{"en":"A quiz night needs questions, teams, prizes, and a venue.","zh":"問答之夜需要題目、隊伍、獎品和場地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a social event based on general knowledge questions.","zh":"這個短語描述以常識問題為基礎的社交活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"present the prizes","meaning":"頒發獎品","examples":[{"en":"Toby presented the prizes at the quiz night.","zh":"Toby 在問答之夜頒發獎品。"},{"en":"To present the prizes means to give awards formally to the winners.","zh":"頒發獎品，意思是正式把獎項交給勝出者。"},{"en":"The principal presented the prizes after the sports competition.","zh":"校長在運動比賽後頒發獎品。"},{"en":"Presenting prizes recognises people’s effort and success.","zh":"頒發獎品表揚人們的努力和成功。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in ceremonies and competitions.","zh":"這個短語常見於典禮和比賽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take visitors to","meaning":"帶訪客去……","examples":[{"en":"The Association will take visitors to Farley House on Sunday.","zh":"協會會在星期日帶訪客去 Farley House。"},{"en":"To take visitors to a place means to bring or guide them there.","zh":"帶訪客去某地，意思是帶領或引導他們到那裏。"},{"en":"Hosts took visitors to the old market after breakfast.","zh":"接待家庭早餐後帶訪客去舊市集。"},{"en":"Taking visitors to local places helps them understand the town better.","zh":"帶訪客去本地地方有助他們更了解城鎮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes guiding guests to an attraction.","zh":"這個短語描述帶領客人前往景點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be familiar with","meaning":"熟悉","examples":[{"en":"Not everyone may be familiar with Farley House.","zh":"不是每個人都熟悉 Farley House。"},{"en":"To be familiar with something means to know it or have experience of it.","zh":"熟悉某事，意思是認識它或有相關經驗。"},{"en":"New students may not be familiar with the school building.","zh":"新生可能不熟悉學校大樓。"},{"en":"If visitors are not familiar with a place, a map can help them.","zh":"如果訪客不熟悉某地方，地圖可以幫助他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes knowledge through experience or information.","zh":"這個短語描述透過經驗或資料得到的認識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a map to help you","meaning":"一張幫助你的地圖","examples":[{"en":"The speaker gives the hosts a map to help them.","zh":"講者給接待家庭一張幫助他們的地圖。"},{"en":"A map to help you is a map provided so you can find places more easily.","zh":"一張幫助你的地圖，是提供給你以便更容易找到地方的地圖。"},{"en":"The museum gave visitors a map to help them find the exhibition rooms.","zh":"博物館給訪客一張地圖，幫助他們找到展覽室。"},{"en":"A map helps people avoid getting lost in a large site.","zh":"地圖幫助人們在大型場地避免迷路。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the practical purpose of the map.","zh":"這個短語解釋地圖的實際用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"car park","meaning":"停車場","examples":[{"en":"The car park is at the bottom of the map.","zh":"停車場在地圖底部。"},{"en":"A car park is an area where people leave their cars.","zh":"停車場，是人們停放汽車的地方。"},{"en":"Visitors should meet in the car park before the tour begins.","zh":"訪客應在導賞開始前於停車場集合。"},{"en":"A clearly marked car park helps drivers find the entrance.","zh":"清楚標示的停車場有助駕駛者找到入口。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in directions and maps.","zh":"這個短語常見於指路和地圖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at the bottom of the map","meaning":"在地圖底部","examples":[{"en":"The car park is at the bottom of the map.","zh":"停車場在地圖底部。"},{"en":"At the bottom of the map means in the lower part of the map.","zh":"在地圖底部，意思是在地圖的下方部分。"},{"en":"The entrance is shown at the bottom of the map.","zh":"入口顯示在地圖底部。"},{"en":"If something is at the bottom of the map, look near the lower edge.","zh":"如果某物在地圖底部，就看靠近下邊緣的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes map position.","zh":"這個短語描述地圖上的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"farm shop","meaning":"農場商店","examples":[{"en":"There is an excellent farm shop in the grounds.","zh":"園區內有一間很好的農場商店。"},{"en":"A farm shop is a shop that sells food or products from a farm or local area.","zh":"農場商店，是售賣農場或本地地區食品和產品的商店。"},{"en":"Visitors can buy cheese, jam, and vegetables at a farm shop.","zh":"訪客可以在農場商店購買芝士、果醬和蔬菜。"},{"en":"A farm shop helps local producers sell directly to customers.","zh":"農場商店幫助本地生產者直接向顧客銷售。"},{"en":"This phrase names a shop connected with farming and local produce.","zh":"這個短語命名與農業和本地農產品有關的商店。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the grounds","meaning":"在園區內","examples":[{"en":"The farm shop is in the grounds of Farley House.","zh":"農場商店位於 Farley House 的園區內。"},{"en":"In the grounds means within the land surrounding a large building.","zh":"在園區內，意思是在大型建築周圍所屬土地範圍內。"},{"en":"There is a café in the grounds of the museum.","zh":"博物館園區內有一間咖啡店。"},{"en":"Visitors can walk around the grounds before entering the house.","zh":"訪客可以在進入房子前於園區內散步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an outdoor area belonging to a property.","zh":"這個短語描述屬於某物業的戶外範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"local produce","meaning":"本地農產品","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can buy local produce at the farm shop.","zh":"訪客可以在農場商店購買本地農產品。"},{"en":"Local produce means food or goods grown or made in the nearby area.","zh":"本地農產品，意思是在附近地區種植或製造的食物或貨品。"},{"en":"Local produce may include fruit, vegetables, cheese, honey, and bread.","zh":"本地農產品可能包括水果、蔬菜、芝士、蜂蜜和麵包。"},{"en":"Buying local produce supports farmers and small businesses.","zh":"購買本地農產品支持農民和小企業。"},{"en":"This phrase connects products with their local origin.","zh":"這個短語把產品與其本地來源連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the old stables","meaning":"舊馬廄","examples":[{"en":"The farm shop is in the old stables.","zh":"農場商店位於舊馬廄內。"},{"en":"The old stables are former buildings where horses were kept.","zh":"舊馬廄，是以前用來飼養馬匹的建築。"},{"en":"Old stables can be converted into shops, cafés, or exhibition spaces.","zh":"舊馬廄可以改建成商店、咖啡店或展覽空間。"},{"en":"Using the old stables gives a historic building a new purpose.","zh":"使用舊馬廄可以給歷史建築新的用途。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a past use of the building.","zh":"這個短語指出建築物過去的用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the first building you come to","meaning":"你首先會見到的建築物","examples":[{"en":"The old stables are the first building you come to.","zh":"舊馬廄是你首先會見到的建築物。"},{"en":"The first building you come to means the first building you reach as you walk along a route.","zh":"你首先會見到的建築物，意思是你沿路走時第一座到達的建築。"},{"en":"After leaving the car park, the café is the first building you come to.","zh":"離開停車場後，咖啡店是你首先會見到的建築物。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people follow directions using landmarks.","zh":"這個短語幫助人們利用地標跟隨方向。"},{"en":"It tells visitors what they should see first.","zh":"它告訴訪客首先應看見甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be built round","meaning":"圍繞……而建","examples":[{"en":"The stables are built round a courtyard.","zh":"馬廄圍繞庭院而建。"},{"en":"To be built round something means to be arranged around it.","zh":"圍繞某物而建，意思是圍着它排列或建造。"},{"en":"The classrooms were built round a small garden.","zh":"課室圍繞一個小花園而建。"},{"en":"Buildings built round a courtyard often face inward toward the open space.","zh":"圍繞庭院而建的建築通常面向內部開放空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes architectural layout.","zh":"這個短語描述建築佈局。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"courtyard","meaning":"庭院","examples":[{"en":"The old stables are built round a courtyard.","zh":"舊馬廄圍繞庭院而建。"},{"en":"A courtyard is an open space surrounded by buildings or walls.","zh":"庭院，是被建築或牆圍繞的開放空間。"},{"en":"Students may sit in the courtyard during break time.","zh":"學生可能會在小息時坐在庭院。"},{"en":"A courtyard can bring light and air into a group of buildings.","zh":"庭院可以為一組建築帶來光線和空氣。"},{"en":"This word describes a central outdoor space.","zh":"這個詞描述中央戶外空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the far corner on the left","meaning":"左邊最遠的角落","examples":[{"en":"The shop is in the far corner on the left.","zh":"商店位於左邊最遠的角落。"},{"en":"The far corner on the left means the left-hand corner that is furthest from where you enter or stand.","zh":"左邊最遠的角落，意思是從你進入或站立位置看，最遠的左邊角落。"},{"en":"The information desk is in the far corner on the left of the hall.","zh":"資訊櫃檯在禮堂左邊最遠的角落。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise location inside a space.","zh":"這個短語在一個空間內給出準確位置。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving directions in a room or courtyard.","zh":"它適合用於在房間或庭院內指路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as you go in","meaning":"當你進去時","examples":[{"en":"There is a small café on the right as you go in.","zh":"當你進去時，右邊有一間小咖啡店。"},{"en":"As you go in means when you enter a place.","zh":"當你進去時，意思是當你進入某地時。"},{"en":"As you go in, you will see the ticket desk on your left.","zh":"當你進去時，你會在左邊看到售票處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what someone sees immediately after entering.","zh":"這個短語描述某人剛進入後會看到甚麼。"},{"en":"It is useful in directions.","zh":"它適合用於指路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not be all that mobile","meaning":"行動不太方便","examples":[{"en":"One or two visitors may not be all that mobile.","zh":"一兩位訪客可能行動不太方便。"},{"en":"Not be all that mobile means not able to move around easily.","zh":"行動不太方便，意思是不太容易四處走動。"},{"en":"Older visitors may not be all that mobile if there are many steps.","zh":"如果有很多台階，年長訪客可能行動不太方便。"},{"en":"If some guests are not very mobile, organisers should plan accessible routes.","zh":"如果有些客人行動不便，主辦者應安排無障礙路線。"},{"en":"This phrase politely describes limited physical movement.","zh":"這個短語有禮貌地描述行動能力有限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"main entrance","meaning":"正門","examples":[{"en":"The main entrance to the house has a lot of steps.","zh":"房子的正門有很多級台階。"},{"en":"The main entrance is the principal or most commonly used way into a building.","zh":"正門，是進入建築物的主要或最常用入口。"},{"en":"Visitors should meet at the main entrance before the tour begins.","zh":"訪客應在導賞開始前於正門集合。"},{"en":"If the main entrance has steps, some visitors may need another entrance.","zh":"如果正門有台階，一些訪客可能需要另一個入口。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the primary doorway or access point.","zh":"這個短語指出主要門口或進入點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have a lot of steps","meaning":"有很多級台階","examples":[{"en":"The main entrance has a lot of steps.","zh":"正門有很多級台階。"},{"en":"To have a lot of steps means there are many stairs to climb.","zh":"有很多級台階，意思是有很多樓梯級需要上落。"},{"en":"The old library has a lot of steps, so wheelchair users need another entrance.","zh":"舊圖書館有很多級台階，所以輪椅使用者需要另一個入口。"},{"en":"Buildings with a lot of steps can be difficult for visitors with mobility problems.","zh":"有很多級台階的建築，對行動不便的訪客來說可能困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an access difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述進出上的困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"disabled entry","meaning":"無障礙入口","examples":[{"en":"Visitors who cannot manage the steps can use the disabled entry.","zh":"不能應付台階的訪客可以使用無障礙入口。"},{"en":"Disabled entry means an entrance designed for people who have difficulty using standard steps or doors.","zh":"無障礙入口，是為難以使用普通台階或門口的人而設的入口。"},{"en":"The museum has disabled entry beside the main gate.","zh":"博物館在正門旁設有無障礙入口。"},{"en":"A disabled entry may include ramps, wider doors, or lifts.","zh":"無障礙入口可能包括斜道、較闊門口或升降機。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to accessible access for disabled visitors.","zh":"這個短語指方便殘疾訪客使用的入口。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on the far side of","meaning":"在……較遠的一側","examples":[{"en":"The disabled entry is on the far side of the house from the car park.","zh":"無障礙入口位於房子遠離停車場的一側。"},{"en":"On the far side of something means on the side that is further away from where you are or from a reference point.","zh":"在某物較遠的一側，意思是在離你或參照點較遠的那一邊。"},{"en":"The garden is on the far side of the building from the main road.","zh":"花園在建築物遠離大路的一側。"},{"en":"If an entrance is on the far side of a house, visitors may need clear directions.","zh":"如果入口在房子較遠的一側，訪客可能需要清楚指示。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relative position.","zh":"這個短語描述相對位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"adventure playground","meaning":"冒險遊樂場","examples":[{"en":"Children will probably be most interested in the adventure playground.","zh":"孩子們可能會對冒險遊樂場最感興趣。"},{"en":"An adventure playground is a play area with equipment for climbing, exploring, and active play.","zh":"冒險遊樂場，是有攀爬、探索和活躍遊玩設備的遊樂區。"},{"en":"The adventure playground has ropes, slides, bridges, and climbing frames.","zh":"冒險遊樂場有繩索、滑梯、橋和攀爬架。"},{"en":"Adventure playgrounds give children space to move and explore safely.","zh":"冒險遊樂場讓孩子有空間安全地活動和探索。"},{"en":"This phrase names a play area designed for excitement and activity.","zh":"這個短語命名為刺激和活動而設的遊樂區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be most interested in","meaning":"對……最感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Children will probably be most interested in the adventure playground.","zh":"孩子們可能會對冒險遊樂場最感興趣。"},{"en":"To be most interested in something means to find it more attractive than other options.","zh":"對某事最感興趣，意思是覺得它比其他選項更吸引。"},{"en":"Younger visitors may be most interested in the animals at the farm.","zh":"年幼訪客可能會對農場動物最感興趣。"},{"en":"Knowing what children are most interested in helps adults plan visits.","zh":"知道孩子最感興趣的是甚麼，有助成人策劃探訪。"},{"en":"This phrase compares levels of interest.","zh":"這個短語比較興趣程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the northern end of","meaning":"……的北端","examples":[{"en":"The adventure playground is at the northern end of the larger lake.","zh":"冒險遊樂場位於較大湖的北端。"},{"en":"The northern end of something means the end located toward the north.","zh":"某物的北端，意思是位於北方的那一端。"},{"en":"The café is at the northern end of the park.","zh":"咖啡店位於公園的北端。"},{"en":"Using “northern end” helps people find places on a map.","zh":"使用「北端」有助人們在地圖上找地方。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise directional location.","zh":"這個短語給出準確方向位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"larger lake","meaning":"較大的湖","examples":[{"en":"The adventure playground is near the larger lake.","zh":"冒險遊樂場靠近較大的湖。"},{"en":"The larger lake means the bigger one of two or more lakes.","zh":"較大的湖，意思是兩個或多個湖中較大的那一個。"},{"en":"The picnic area is beside the larger lake, not the smaller one.","zh":"野餐區在較大的湖旁邊，不是在較小的湖旁邊。"},{"en":"Comparing the larger lake with the smaller lake helps visitors follow the map.","zh":"把較大的湖與較小的湖比較，有助訪客跟隨地圖。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a lake by size.","zh":"這個短語以大小識別湖泊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in a bend on the path","meaning":"在小路轉彎處","examples":[{"en":"The playground is in a bend on the path that leads to the lake.","zh":"遊樂場位於通往湖的小路轉彎處。"},{"en":"In a bend on the path means at the curved part of a path.","zh":"在小路轉彎處，意思是在小路彎曲的部分。"},{"en":"The bench is in a bend on the path near the garden.","zh":"長椅位於花園附近的小路轉彎處。"},{"en":"A bend in the path can be a useful landmark.","zh":"小路轉彎處可以是一個有用地標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a location using the shape of the path.","zh":"這個短語利用小路形狀描述位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"通往","examples":[{"en":"The path leads to the lake.","zh":"這條小路通往湖。"},{"en":"To lead to a place means to go in the direction of that place and take people there.","zh":"通往某地，意思是朝那個地方延伸並帶人到那裏。"},{"en":"The narrow road leads to the village church.","zh":"這條窄路通往村莊教堂。"},{"en":"Paths and signs help visitors know where routes lead to.","zh":"小路和標誌幫助訪客知道路線通往哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the destination of a route.","zh":"這個短語描述路線的目的地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lots for children to do","meaning":"有很多適合孩子做的事情","examples":[{"en":"There is lots for children to do at the playground.","zh":"遊樂場有很多適合孩子做的事情。"},{"en":"Lots for children to do means many activities are available for children.","zh":"有很多適合孩子做的事情，意思是有許多活動可供孩子參與。"},{"en":"At the museum, there is lots for children to do, including games and workshops.","zh":"在博物館，有很多適合孩子做的事情，包括遊戲和工作坊。"},{"en":"If a place has lots for children to do, families may stay longer.","zh":"如果一個地方有很多適合孩子做的事情，家庭可能會停留更久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a child-friendly place.","zh":"這個短語描述適合孩子的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a number of","meaning":"一些；若干","examples":[{"en":"There are a number of lovely gardens near the house.","zh":"房子附近有若干美麗花園。"},{"en":"A number of means several.","zh":"A number of 的意思是一些或若干。"},{"en":"There are a number of cafés near the station.","zh":"車站附近有幾間咖啡店。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate amount without saying the exact number.","zh":"這個短語給出大約數量，而不說明確數字。"},{"en":"It is slightly more formal than “some.”","zh":"它比 “some” 稍為正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"near the house","meaning":"在房子附近","examples":[{"en":"The gardens are near the house.","zh":"花園在房子附近。"},{"en":"Near the house means close to the house, not far away.","zh":"在房子附近，意思是接近房子，不遠。"},{"en":"There is a small pond near the house.","zh":"房子附近有一個小池塘。"},{"en":"Gardens near the house are easy for visitors to reach.","zh":"房子附近的花園方便訪客到達。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location by distance from the house.","zh":"這個短語透過與房子的距離描述位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"kitchen gardens","meaning":"廚房花園；菜園","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen gardens are rectangular and surrounded by a wall.","zh":"菜園是長方形的，並被牆圍繞。"},{"en":"Kitchen gardens are gardens where fruit, vegetables, and herbs are grown for use in a kitchen.","zh":"廚房花園／菜園，是種植水果、蔬菜和香草供廚房使用的花園。"},{"en":"Old houses often had kitchen gardens to supply fresh food.","zh":"舊宅常有菜園來供應新鮮食物。"},{"en":"Kitchen gardens can show how people produced food for the household.","zh":"菜園可以顯示人們如何為家庭生產食物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical food-growing gardens, not decorative gardens only.","zh":"這個短語指實用的食物種植花園，而不只是裝飾花園。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be surrounded by","meaning":"被……圍繞","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen gardens are surrounded by a wall.","zh":"菜園被一道牆圍繞。"},{"en":"To be surrounded by something means to have it all around the outside.","zh":"被某物圍繞，意思是外面四周都有該物。"},{"en":"The school playground is surrounded by trees.","zh":"學校操場被樹木圍繞。"},{"en":"A garden surrounded by a wall may be protected from animals and wind.","zh":"被牆圍繞的花園可能受保護，免受動物和風影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what is around a place or object.","zh":"這個短語描述某地方或物件周圍有甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"to the north-east of","meaning":"在……的東北方","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen gardens are to the north-east of the house.","zh":"菜園在房子的東北方。"},{"en":"To the north-east of something means in the direction between north and east from it.","zh":"在某物的東北方，意思是從它看位於北方和東方之間的方向。"},{"en":"The lake is to the north-east of the car park.","zh":"湖在停車場的東北方。"},{"en":"Compass directions help visitors find places on a map.","zh":"羅盤方向幫助訪客在地圖上找地方。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise directional position.","zh":"這個短語給出準確方向位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"quite near","meaning":"離……相當近","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen gardens are quite near the smaller lake.","zh":"菜園離較小的湖相當近。"},{"en":"Quite near means fairly close, but not necessarily next to something.","zh":"相當近，意思是頗接近，但不一定就在旁邊。"},{"en":"The café is quite near the museum entrance.","zh":"咖啡店離博物館入口相當近。"},{"en":"If a garden is quite near a lake, visitors can walk between them easily.","zh":"如果花園離湖相當近，訪客可以輕鬆在兩者之間步行。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a moderate description of distance.","zh":"這個短語對距離作出中等程度描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"smaller lake","meaning":"較小的湖","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen gardens are near the smaller lake.","zh":"菜園靠近較小的湖。"},{"en":"The smaller lake means the lake that is less large than another lake nearby.","zh":"較小的湖，意思是比附近另一個湖更小的湖。"},{"en":"The children’s path goes around the smaller lake.","zh":"兒童小徑圍繞較小的湖而行。"},{"en":"Calling it the smaller lake helps visitors distinguish it from the larger lake.","zh":"稱它為較小的湖，有助訪客把它與較大的湖分開。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a lake by comparison.","zh":"這個短語透過比較識別湖泊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"still in use","meaning":"仍在使用","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen gardens are still in use.","zh":"菜園仍在使用。"},{"en":"Still in use means still being used now.","zh":"仍在使用，意思是現在仍然被使用。"},{"en":"The old bridge is still in use after two hundred years.","zh":"這座舊橋經過二百年後仍在使用。"},{"en":"If a historic garden is still in use, it remains part of daily life.","zh":"如果歷史花園仍在使用，它仍是日常生活的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something old has not only become a display.","zh":"這個短語顯示某件舊物不只是展品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a great collection of","meaning":"大量；豐富的……收藏／種類","examples":[{"en":"The gardens have a great collection of fruit and vegetables.","zh":"花園有大量水果和蔬菜。"},{"en":"A great collection of something means many good or interesting examples of it.","zh":"豐富的某物收藏或種類，意思是有很多好的或有趣的例子。"},{"en":"The library has a great collection of local history books.","zh":"圖書館有豐富的本地歷史書收藏。"},{"en":"A great collection of plants can make a garden educational and attractive.","zh":"豐富的植物種類可以令花園有教育意義又吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase praises both number and variety.","zh":"這個短語同時稱讚數量和多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fruit and vegetables","meaning":"水果和蔬菜","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen gardens contain fruit and vegetables.","zh":"菜園種有水果和蔬菜。"},{"en":"Fruit and vegetables are edible plants grown for food.","zh":"水果和蔬菜，是種植來作食物的可食用植物。"},{"en":"Apples, tomatoes, carrots, and beans are fruit and vegetables.","zh":"蘋果、番茄、甘筍和豆都是水果和蔬菜。"},{"en":"Growing fruit and vegetables in a garden can supply fresh food for a kitchen.","zh":"在花園種水果和蔬菜可以為廚房供應新鮮食物。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when talking about healthy food and gardening.","zh":"這個短語常用於談論健康食物和園藝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a bit more of a walk","meaning":"要多走一段路","examples":[{"en":"The Temple of the Four Winds is a bit more of a walk.","zh":"四風神殿要多走一段路。"},{"en":"A bit more of a walk means it is slightly farther away and takes more walking.","zh":"要多走一段路，意思是稍微遠一點，需要走更多路。"},{"en":"The viewpoint is a bit more of a walk, but the scenery is better.","zh":"觀景點要多走一段路，但景色更好。"},{"en":"This phrase warns visitors that a place is not very close.","zh":"這個短語提醒訪客某地方不是很近。"},{"en":"It sounds informal and gentle.","zh":"它聽起來口語而溫和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be worth it","meaning":"值得","examples":[{"en":"The walk to the temple is worth it.","zh":"走到神殿是值得的。"},{"en":"To be worth it means the effort, time, or cost is justified by the result.","zh":"值得，意思是結果足以證明花費的努力、時間或金錢有價值。"},{"en":"The climb is tiring, but the view is worth it.","zh":"攀登很累，但景色值得。"},{"en":"If an activity is worth it, people feel glad they made the effort.","zh":"如果一項活動值得，人們會慶幸自己付出了努力。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a positive reason to do something difficult.","zh":"這個短語給出做困難事情的正面理由。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take the path from","meaning":"從……沿路走","examples":[{"en":"Take the path from the car park.","zh":"從停車場沿路走。"},{"en":"To take the path from a place means to start walking along a path beginning there.","zh":"從某地沿路走，意思是由那個地方開始沿小路前進。"},{"en":"Take the path from the station to reach the old bridge.","zh":"從車站沿路走，便可到達舊橋。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the starting point of a walking route.","zh":"這個短語給出步行路線的起點。"},{"en":"It is common in map directions.","zh":"它常見於地圖指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"go past","meaning":"經過","examples":[{"en":"Go past the western sides of the stables and the house.","zh":"經過馬廄和房子的西側。"},{"en":"To go past something means to move by it without stopping there.","zh":"經過某物，意思是從它旁邊走過而不停留在那裏。"},{"en":"Go past the post office, and the school will be on your left.","zh":"經過郵局後，學校會在你左邊。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when giving directions with landmarks.","zh":"這個短語常用於帶有地標的指路。"},{"en":"It tells the listener which places they will pass.","zh":"它告訴聽者會經過哪些地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the western side of","meaning":"……的西側","examples":[{"en":"The path goes past the western side of the house.","zh":"小路經過房子的西側。"},{"en":"The western side of something is the side facing or located toward the west.","zh":"某物的西側，是面向或位於西方的一側。"},{"en":"The garden is on the western side of the museum.","zh":"花園在博物館的西側。"},{"en":"Compass directions help people find the correct side of a large building.","zh":"羅盤方向幫助人們找到大型建築的正確一側。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise directional location.","zh":"這個短語給出準確方向位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"when the path forks","meaning":"當小路分岔時","examples":[{"en":"When the path forks, take the right-hand path.","zh":"當小路分岔時，走右邊的小路。"},{"en":"When the path forks means when one path divides into two or more paths.","zh":"當小路分岔時，意思是一條小路分成兩條或更多小路時。"},{"en":"When the path forks near the trees, choose the left route.","zh":"當小路在樹旁分岔時，選左邊路線。"},{"en":"A fork in the path is an important point in directions.","zh":"小路分岔處是指路中的重要位置。"},{"en":"This phrase tells visitors what to do at a split in the route.","zh":"這個短語告訴訪客在分岔路口應怎樣做。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"right-hand path","meaning":"右邊的小路","examples":[{"en":"Take the right-hand path when the path forks.","zh":"小路分岔時，走右邊的小路。"},{"en":"The right-hand path is the path on the right side.","zh":"右邊的小路，是位於右側的路。"},{"en":"At the fork, the right-hand path leads to the viewpoint.","zh":"在分岔處，右邊的小路通往觀景點。"},{"en":"Saying “right-hand path” helps avoid confusion when there are two choices.","zh":"說「右邊的小路」有助避免在兩個選擇中混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in walking directions.","zh":"這個短語常見於步行指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"with the woods on your left","meaning":"樹林在你的左邊","examples":[{"en":"Go up the path with the woods on your left.","zh":"沿小路向上走，樹林在你的左邊。"},{"en":"With the woods on your left means the trees should be on your left side as you walk.","zh":"樹林在你的左邊，意思是你走路時樹木應在你的左側。"},{"en":"Walk along the path with the river on your right.","zh":"沿小路走，河流在你的右邊。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people check that they are going the correct way.","zh":"這個短語幫助人們確認自己走的方向正確。"},{"en":"It uses nearby features to guide movement.","zh":"它利用附近特徵引導行進。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"right at the end","meaning":"就在盡頭","examples":[{"en":"The temple is right at the end of the path.","zh":"神殿就在小路盡頭。"},{"en":"Right at the end means exactly at the final point.","zh":"就在盡頭，意思是正正在最後的位置。"},{"en":"The café is right at the end of the street.","zh":"咖啡店就在街道盡頭。"},{"en":"This phrase tells visitors they should keep going until the path finishes.","zh":"這個短語告訴訪客應一直走到小路結束。"},{"en":"It gives a precise final location.","zh":"它給出準確的最後位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"great views over","meaning":"俯瞰……的美景","examples":[{"en":"There are great views over the whole area.","zh":"那裏可以俯瞰整個區域的美景。"},{"en":"Great views over a place means excellent sights looking across or down over that place.","zh":"俯瞰某地的美景，意思是從高處或遠處看到該地的優美景色。"},{"en":"The hill has great views over the town and river.","zh":"山上可以俯瞰城鎮和河流的美景。"},{"en":"People may walk farther if the destination offers great views.","zh":"如果目的地有美景可看，人們可能願意多走一段路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an attractive viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語描述吸引人的觀景點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the whole area","meaning":"整個區域","examples":[{"en":"The temple has great views over the whole area.","zh":"神殿可以俯瞰整個區域的美景。"},{"en":"The whole area means all of the place being discussed, not just one part.","zh":"整個區域，意思是正在討論的整個地方，而不只是一部分。"},{"en":"From the tower, visitors can see the whole area of the park.","zh":"從塔上，訪客可以看見整個公園區域。"},{"en":"Seeing the whole area helps people understand the layout of a large site.","zh":"看見整個區域有助人們理解大型場地的佈局。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises completeness.","zh":"這個短語強調完整性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"During the visit to","meaning":"在到訪……期間","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what members enjoyed during the visit to Malatte.","zh":"問題問成員在到訪 Malatte 期間享受了甚麼。"},{"en":"During the visit to a place means while people were visiting that place.","zh":"在到訪某地期間，意思是在人們參觀該地方的時候。"},{"en":"During the visit to the museum, students saw old coins and maps.","zh":"在到訪博物館期間，學生看見了舊硬幣和地圖。"},{"en":"This phrase sets the time and place for an experience.","zh":"這個短語設定經歷發生的時間和地點。"},{"en":"It is useful in questions about trips or events.","zh":"它適合用於關於旅行或活動的問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"members especially enjoyed","meaning":"成員尤其享受","examples":[{"en":"Members especially enjoyed one activity during the visit.","zh":"成員在探訪期間尤其享受其中一項活動。"},{"en":"Members especially enjoyed something means they liked it more than the other activities.","zh":"成員尤其享受某事，意思是他們比其他活動更喜歡它。"},{"en":"Students especially enjoyed the boat ride during the school trip.","zh":"學生在學校旅行中尤其享受乘船。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the favourite part of an experience.","zh":"這個短語突出一次經歷中最受喜愛的部分。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing several activities.","zh":"它適合用於比較幾項活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"go to a theme park","meaning":"去主題公園","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions going to a theme park.","zh":"這個選項提到去主題公園。"},{"en":"To go to a theme park means to visit an amusement park with rides and attractions.","zh":"去主題公園，意思是參觀有機動遊戲和景點的遊樂園。"},{"en":"Families often go to a theme park during school holidays.","zh":"家庭常在學校假期去主題公園。"},{"en":"Going to a theme park can be exciting, but it depends on time and weather.","zh":"去主題公園可以很刺激，但取決於時間和天氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a leisure activity.","zh":"這個短語描述休閒活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"experience a river trip","meaning":"體驗乘船遊河","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions experiencing a river trip.","zh":"這個選項提到體驗乘船遊河。"},{"en":"To experience a river trip means to take part in a journey on a river, usually by boat.","zh":"體驗乘船遊河，意思是參與一次在河上的旅程，通常是坐船。"},{"en":"Visitors experienced a river trip and saw the town from the water.","zh":"訪客體驗乘船遊河，從水上看見城鎮。"},{"en":"Experiencing a river trip can be memorable because it offers different views.","zh":"體驗乘船遊河可以令人難忘，因為它提供不同景觀。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on taking part in the activity, not just hearing about it.","zh":"這個短語着重親身參與活動，而不只是聽說。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"visit a cheese factory","meaning":"參觀芝士工廠","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions visiting a cheese factory.","zh":"這個選項提到參觀芝士工廠。"},{"en":"To visit a cheese factory means to go to a place where cheese is made.","zh":"參觀芝士工廠，意思是前往製作芝士的地方。"},{"en":"Visitors may visit a cheese factory to learn how milk becomes cheese.","zh":"訪客可能會參觀芝士工廠，了解牛奶如何變成芝士。"},{"en":"Visiting a food factory can include watching production and tasting samples.","zh":"參觀食品工廠可以包括觀看生產過程和品嚐樣本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an educational food-related visit.","zh":"這個短語描述與食物有關的教育性參觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mark the 25th anniversary","meaning":"紀念 25 週年","examples":[{"en":"The town will do something to mark the 25th anniversary.","zh":"這個城鎮會做些事情來紀念 25 週年。"},{"en":"To mark the 25th anniversary means to celebrate or remember 25 years since an event began.","zh":"紀念 25 週年，意思是慶祝或記住某件事開始以來 25 年。"},{"en":"The school planted a tree to mark the 25th anniversary of its opening.","zh":"學校種了一棵樹來紀念開校 25 週年。"},{"en":"Marking an anniversary helps people remember shared history.","zh":"紀念週年有助人們記住共同歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a symbolic action with a special date.","zh":"這個短語把象徵性行動與特別日期連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the 25th anniversary","meaning":"25 週年","examples":[{"en":"This year is the 25th anniversary of the Association.","zh":"今年是協會的 25 週年。"},{"en":"The 25th anniversary is the date or year marking 25 years since something began.","zh":"25 週年，是某事開始以來滿 25 年的日期或年份。"},{"en":"The club held a dinner for its 25th anniversary.","zh":"學會為其 25 週年舉辦晚宴。"},{"en":"A 25th anniversary is often celebrated with speeches, gifts, or public events.","zh":"25 週年通常會以演講、禮物或公共活動慶祝。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a quarter-century milestone.","zh":"這個短語標示四分之一世紀的里程碑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"raise funds","meaning":"籌得款項","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which event raised most funds this year.","zh":"問題問今年哪項活動籌得最多款項。"},{"en":"To raise funds means to collect money for an organisation, project, or cause.","zh":"籌得款項，意思是為組織、項目或公益目的收集金錢。"},{"en":"Students sold cakes to raise funds for the school trip.","zh":"學生賣蛋糕為學校旅行籌款。"},{"en":"Raising funds can help pay for community activities.","zh":"籌得款項可以幫助支付社區活動費用。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in charity and club work.","zh":"這個短語常見於慈善和學會工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"most funds","meaning":"最多款項","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which event raised the most funds.","zh":"問題問哪項活動籌得最多款項。"},{"en":"Most funds means the largest amount of money compared with other events.","zh":"最多款項，意思是與其他活動相比籌得最大金額。"},{"en":"The concert raised the most funds for the charity.","zh":"音樂會為慈善機構籌得最多款項。"},{"en":"An event that raises the most funds may be repeated next year.","zh":"籌得最多款項的活動可能會在明年再次舉辦。"},{"en":"This phrase compares fundraising results.","zh":"這個短語比較籌款結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"host families","meaning":"接待家庭","examples":[{"en":"Host families are advised what to do on the first evening.","zh":"接待家庭獲建議第一晚應做甚麼。"},{"en":"Host families are families who welcome visitors into their homes during an exchange or visit.","zh":"接待家庭，是在交流或探訪期間歡迎訪客住進家中的家庭。"},{"en":"Host families may provide meals, conversation, and a place to sleep.","zh":"接待家庭可能提供膳食、交流和住宿地方。"},{"en":"Good host families help visitors feel safe and welcome.","zh":"好的接待家庭幫助訪客感到安全和受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in exchange programmes.","zh":"這個短語常見於交流計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be advised to","meaning":"獲建議","examples":[{"en":"Host families are advised to have a meal at home.","zh":"接待家庭獲建議在家用膳。"},{"en":"To be advised to do something means to be given a recommendation or guidance.","zh":"獲建議做某事，意思是得到建議或指引。"},{"en":"Visitors are advised to wear comfortable shoes.","zh":"訪客獲建議穿舒適鞋子。"},{"en":"Being advised to do something does not always mean it is a strict rule.","zh":"獲建議做某事不一定代表這是嚴格規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in instructions and guidance.","zh":"這個短語常見於指示和指引。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take someone for a walk round","meaning":"帶某人在……四處散步","examples":[{"en":"The option says hosts may take visitors for a walk round the town.","zh":"這個選項說接待方可以帶訪客在鎮上四處散步。"},{"en":"To take someone for a walk round a place means to guide them on a relaxed walk around it.","zh":"帶某人在某地四處散步，意思是引導他們輕鬆地在該地走走。"},{"en":"My cousin took me for a walk round the old market.","zh":"表親帶我在舊市集四處散步。"},{"en":"Taking visitors for a walk round town helps them see local streets and shops.","zh":"帶訪客在鎮上四處散步，有助他們看看本地街道和商店。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a friendly guided walk.","zh":"這個短語描述友善的導覽步行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a local restaurant","meaning":"本地餐廳","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions going to a local restaurant.","zh":"這個選項提到去本地餐廳。"},{"en":"A local restaurant is a restaurant in the nearby area, often serving local people or local food.","zh":"本地餐廳，是附近地區的餐廳，通常服務本地人或提供本地食物。"},{"en":"Visitors may enjoy a local restaurant if they want to try regional dishes.","zh":"如果訪客想嘗試地區菜式，可能會喜歡本地餐廳。"},{"en":"A local restaurant can be lively, but it may be tiring on the first evening.","zh":"本地餐廳可以很熱鬧，但第一晚去可能會很累。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a nearby eating place.","zh":"這個短語指出附近的用餐地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have a meal at home","meaning":"在家用膳","examples":[{"en":"Hosts are advised to have a meal at home.","zh":"接待家庭獲建議在家用膳。"},{"en":"To have a meal at home means to eat at one’s house instead of going out.","zh":"在家用膳，意思是在自己家中吃飯，而不是外出。"},{"en":"After a long journey, guests may prefer to have a meal at home.","zh":"長途旅程後，客人可能較喜歡在家用膳。"},{"en":"Having a meal at home can make conversation easier and more relaxed.","zh":"在家用膳可以令交談更容易和更放鬆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple domestic arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單的家庭安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"there will be the chance to","meaning":"將有機會","examples":[{"en":"On Saturday evening, there will be the chance to listen to music.","zh":"星期六晚上，大家將有機會聽音樂。"},{"en":"There will be the chance to means people will have an opportunity to do something.","zh":"There will be the chance to 的意思是人們將有機會做某事。"},{"en":"At the open day, there will be the chance to meet teachers.","zh":"在開放日，大家將有機會見老師。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when announcing activities in a programme.","zh":"這個短語適合用於宣布活動安排。"},{"en":"It highlights what visitors can do.","zh":"它突出訪客可以做甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"listen to a concert","meaning":"聽音樂會","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions listening to a concert.","zh":"這個選項提到聽音樂會。"},{"en":"To listen to a concert means to attend and hear a live music performance.","zh":"聽音樂會，意思是出席並聆聽現場音樂表演。"},{"en":"Families listened to a concert in the town hall.","zh":"家庭在市政廳聽音樂會。"},{"en":"Listening to a concert can be a relaxing evening activity for visitors.","zh":"聽音樂會可以是訪客輕鬆的晚間活動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on enjoying music as an audience member.","zh":"這個短語着重以觀眾身份享受音樂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"watch a match","meaning":"觀看比賽","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions watching a match.","zh":"這個選項提到觀看比賽。"},{"en":"To watch a match means to look at a sports game as a spectator.","zh":"觀看比賽，意思是以觀眾身份觀看體育賽事。"},{"en":"Visitors watched a football match at the local club.","zh":"訪客在本地球會觀看足球比賽。"},{"en":"Watching a match can help guests experience local sports culture.","zh":"觀看比賽可以幫助客人體驗本地體育文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes viewing a competition, not playing in it.","zh":"這個短語描述觀看競賽，而不是參與比賽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take part in a competition","meaning":"參加比賽","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions taking part in a competition.","zh":"這個選項提到參加比賽。"},{"en":"To take part in a competition means to join it as a competitor.","zh":"參加比賽，意思是以參賽者身份加入競賽。"},{"en":"Students took part in a cooking competition during the festival.","zh":"學生在節日期間參加烹飪比賽。"},{"en":"Taking part in a competition can be exciting, but it may require preparation.","zh":"參加比賽可以很刺激，但可能需要準備。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on active participation.","zh":"這個短語着重主動參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"label the map","meaning":"標示地圖","examples":[{"en":"Questions 16 to 20 ask listeners to label the map.","zh":"第 16 至 20 題要求聽者標示地圖。"},{"en":"To label the map means to write names, letters, or symbols on a map to identify places.","zh":"標示地圖，意思是在地圖上寫上名稱、字母或符號來識別地方。"},{"en":"Students labelled the map with the names of rivers and cities.","zh":"學生在地圖上標示河流和城市名稱。"},{"en":"Labelling a map shows that the listener understands the locations.","zh":"標示地圖顯示聽者理解位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in listening tests and geography tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於聆聽測驗和地理任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"write the correct letter","meaning":"寫上正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Listeners must write the correct letter next to each place.","zh":"聽者必須在每個地方旁寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"To write the correct letter means to choose and write the right letter answer.","zh":"寫上正確字母，意思是選擇並寫下正確的字母答案。"},{"en":"In the map task, students wrote the correct letter beside the library.","zh":"在地圖題中，學生在圖書館旁寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"This instruction is used when a map has labelled points such as A, B, and C.","zh":"當地圖有 A、B、C 等標示點時，會使用這個指示。"},{"en":"It checks whether listeners can match names with locations.","zh":"它檢查聽者是否能把名稱與位置配對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"next to","meaning":"在……旁邊","examples":[{"en":"Write the correct letter next to each question.","zh":"在每條問題旁邊寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"Next to means beside or immediately near something.","zh":"在……旁邊，意思是在某物旁邊或非常接近它。"},{"en":"Write your name next to your class number.","zh":"在你的班號旁邊寫上名字。"},{"en":"In a test, writing an answer next to the question makes it easy to check.","zh":"在測驗中把答案寫在問題旁邊，方便檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position on a page or in a place.","zh":"這個短語描述頁面或地方上的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Farm shop","meaning":"農場商店","examples":[{"en":"The farm shop sells local produce in the old stables.","zh":"農場商店在舊馬廄內售賣本地農產品。"},{"en":"A farm shop is a shop selling food or goods from farms or nearby producers.","zh":"農場商店，是售賣農場或附近生產者食品和貨品的商店。"},{"en":"Visitors may buy cheese, fruit, jam, and bread at the farm shop.","zh":"訪客可以在農場商店購買芝士、水果、果醬和麵包。"},{"en":"A farm shop helps visitors experience local food culture.","zh":"農場商店幫助訪客體驗本地飲食文化。"},{"en":"This phrase names a place where local produce is sold.","zh":"這個短語命名售賣本地農產品的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Disabled entry","meaning":"無障礙入口","examples":[{"en":"The disabled entry is useful for visitors who cannot use the steps.","zh":"無障礙入口對不能使用台階的訪客很有用。"},{"en":"Disabled entry is an accessible entrance for people with mobility difficulties.","zh":"無障礙入口，是為行動不便人士而設的易達入口。"},{"en":"The disabled entry may have a ramp instead of stairs.","zh":"無障礙入口可能有斜道而不是樓梯。"},{"en":"A clear disabled entry helps all visitors enter safely.","zh":"清楚的無障礙入口幫助所有訪客安全進入。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies an entrance designed for accessibility.","zh":"這個短語指出為無障礙而設的入口。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Adventure playground","meaning":"冒險遊樂場","examples":[{"en":"The adventure playground is likely to interest children.","zh":"冒險遊樂場很可能吸引孩子。"},{"en":"An adventure playground is an outdoor play area with exciting equipment for children.","zh":"冒險遊樂場，是有刺激設備供孩子玩耍的戶外遊樂區。"},{"en":"Children can climb, slide, swing, and explore in an adventure playground.","zh":"孩子可以在冒險遊樂場攀爬、滑梯、盪鞦韆和探索。"},{"en":"An adventure playground gives families a reason to spend more time at a site.","zh":"冒險遊樂場給家庭一個在場地停留更久的理由。"},{"en":"This phrase names an active play area for children.","zh":"這個短語命名給孩子使用的活躍遊樂區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Kitchen gardens","meaning":"廚房花園；菜園","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen gardens are still used for fruit and vegetables.","zh":"菜園仍用來種植水果和蔬菜。"},{"en":"Kitchen gardens are gardens where edible plants are grown for cooking.","zh":"廚房花園／菜園，是種植可食用植物供烹調使用的花園。"},{"en":"Kitchen gardens may grow herbs, carrots, beans, apples, and berries.","zh":"菜園可能種植香草、甘筍、豆、蘋果和莓果。"},{"en":"Historic kitchen gardens show how large houses once supplied fresh food.","zh":"歷史菜園顯示大型房屋過去如何供應新鮮食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical gardens connected with food.","zh":"這個短語描述與食物有關的實用花園。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"The Temple of the Four Winds","meaning":"四風神殿","examples":[{"en":"The Temple of the Four Winds has views over the whole area.","zh":"四風神殿可以俯瞰整個區域。"},{"en":"The Temple of the Four Winds is a named landmark or small temple-like building in the grounds.","zh":"四風神殿，是園區內一個有名稱的地標或小型神殿式建築。"},{"en":"Visitors may walk to the Temple of the Four Winds for the best views.","zh":"訪客可能會步行到四風神殿欣賞最佳景色。"},{"en":"A place like the Temple of the Four Winds can make a garden visit more memorable.","zh":"像四風神殿這樣的地方可以令花園參觀更難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific attraction on the map.","zh":"這個短語命名地圖上的特定景點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/listening/Practice 5/task-3":[{"front":"I haven’t seen you for a bit","meaning":"我有一陣子沒見到你了","examples":[{"en":"I haven’t seen you for a bit, Marie.","zh":"Marie，我有一陣子沒見到你了。"},{"en":"I haven’t seen you for a bit means I have not met or seen you for a short period of time.","zh":"我有一陣子沒見到你了，意思是我有一小段時間沒有見過你。"},{"en":"I haven’t seen you for a bit, so I wondered how your project was going.","zh":"我有一陣子沒見到你了，所以想知道你的專題進行得怎樣。"},{"en":"People say this when they meet someone again after some time.","zh":"人們隔了一段時間再見到某人時會這樣說。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds friendly and informal.","zh":"這個片語聽起來友善而口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be busy with","meaning":"忙於……","examples":[{"en":"Marie has been busy with her project.","zh":"Marie 一直忙於她的專題。"},{"en":"Be busy with something means spend a lot of time and effort on it.","zh":"忙於某事意思是花很多時間和精力在那件事上。"},{"en":"I have been busy with revision this week.","zh":"我這星期一直忙於溫習。"},{"en":"Students may be busy with a project before the deadline.","zh":"學生在截止日期前可能會忙於專題。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why someone has not had much free time.","zh":"這個片語解釋某人為何沒有太多空閒時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"project","meaning":"專題；項目","examples":[{"en":"Marie has been busy with her project on egg alternatives.","zh":"Marie 一直忙於她關於雞蛋替代品的專題。"},{"en":"A project is a piece of work that takes time, research, planning, or making.","zh":"專題或項目是需要時間、研究、計劃或製作的一項工作。"},{"en":"Our science project is about reducing food waste.","zh":"我們的科學專題是關於減少食物浪費。"},{"en":"A project often has a clear topic, aim, and final result.","zh":"專題通常有清晰題目、目標和最終成果。"},{"en":"Students do projects to investigate ideas more deeply.","zh":"學生做專題是為了更深入研究想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"vegan alternative to","meaning":"……的純素替代品","examples":[{"en":"Marie is making a vegan alternative to eggs.","zh":"Marie 正在製作雞蛋的純素替代品。"},{"en":"A vegan alternative to something is a plant-based replacement that does not use animal products.","zh":"某物的純素替代品是指不使用動物產品的植物性替代品。"},{"en":"Soy milk can be a vegan alternative to cow’s milk.","zh":"豆奶可以是牛奶的純素替代品。"},{"en":"A vegan alternative to eggs is useful for people who avoid animal foods.","zh":"雞蛋的純素替代品對避免動物食品的人有用。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on replacing an animal-based food with a vegan option.","zh":"這個片語集中於用純素選擇取代動物性食品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"animal products","meaning":"動物產品","examples":[{"en":"Marie is making something that does not use animal products.","zh":"Marie 正在製作不使用動物產品的東西。"},{"en":"Animal products are foods or materials that come from animals, such as eggs, milk, meat, or honey.","zh":"動物產品是來自動物的食物或材料，例如雞蛋、牛奶、肉類或蜂蜜。"},{"en":"A vegan cake does not contain animal products like butter or eggs.","zh":"純素蛋糕不含牛油或雞蛋等動物產品。"},{"en":"People may avoid animal products for health, ethical, or environmental reasons.","zh":"人們可能因健康、道德或環境原因避免動物產品。"},{"en":"The phrase is important when discussing vegan food.","zh":"這個片語在討論純素食品時很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"main aims","meaning":"主要目標","examples":[{"en":"Marie had two main aims when she started the project.","zh":"Marie 開始這個專題時有兩個主要目標。"},{"en":"Main aims are the most important goals someone wants to achieve.","zh":"主要目標是某人最想達成的重要目的。"},{"en":"The main aims of our project are to reduce waste and save money.","zh":"我們專題的主要目標是減少浪費和節省金錢。"},{"en":"Clear main aims help a project stay focused.","zh":"清晰的主要目標幫助專題保持焦點。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what a person is trying to do.","zh":"這個片語解釋某人正嘗試達成甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"start looking for","meaning":"開始尋找……","examples":[{"en":"Marie started looking for an alternative to eggs.","zh":"Marie 開始尋找雞蛋替代品。"},{"en":"Start looking for something means begin trying to find it.","zh":"開始尋找某物意思是開始嘗試找出它。"},{"en":"The students started looking for information in the library.","zh":"學生開始在圖書館尋找資料。"},{"en":"People start looking for a solution when they notice a problem.","zh":"人們注意到問題時，就會開始尋找解決方法。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the beginning of a search.","zh":"這個片語標示搜尋的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an alternative to eggs","meaning":"雞蛋替代品","examples":[{"en":"Marie is looking for an alternative to eggs.","zh":"Marie 正在尋找雞蛋替代品。"},{"en":"An alternative to eggs is another ingredient that can be used instead of eggs.","zh":"雞蛋替代品是可以代替雞蛋使用的另一種材料。"},{"en":"Mashed banana can be an alternative to eggs in some cakes.","zh":"在某些蛋糕中，香蕉泥可以是雞蛋替代品。"},{"en":"People may need an alternative to eggs if they are vegan or allergic to eggs.","zh":"如果人們是純素者或對雞蛋過敏，可能需要雞蛋替代品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a substitute for eggs.","zh":"這個片語描述雞蛋的替代材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have more advantages","meaning":"有更多優點","examples":[{"en":"Marie has found that chickpeas have more advantages.","zh":"Marie 發現鷹嘴豆有更多優點。"},{"en":"Have more advantages means offer more benefits than another option.","zh":"有更多優點意思是比另一個選擇提供更多好處。"},{"en":"Reusable bags have more advantages than plastic bags because they create less waste.","zh":"可重用袋比膠袋有更多優點，因為它們製造較少垃圾。"},{"en":"A food ingredient may have more advantages if it is cheap, healthy, and easy to find.","zh":"如果一種食材便宜、健康又容易找到，它可能有更多優點。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the benefits of different choices.","zh":"這個片語比較不同選擇的好處。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"project on reusing waste food","meaning":"關於廚餘再利用的專題","examples":[{"en":"Colin’s project is on reusing waste food.","zh":"Colin 的專題是關於廚餘再利用。"},{"en":"A project on reusing waste food studies how unwanted food can be used again instead of thrown away.","zh":"關於廚餘再利用的專題研究如何再次使用不需要的食物，而不是把它丟掉。"},{"en":"A school project on reusing waste food might turn old bread into snacks.","zh":"關於廚餘再利用的學校專題可能把舊麵包變成小食。"},{"en":"This kind of project can help reduce rubbish and save resources.","zh":"這類專題可以幫助減少垃圾和節省資源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a project focused on food waste solutions.","zh":"這個片語描述集中於食物浪費解決方法的專題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"reuse waste food","meaning":"再利用廚餘","examples":[{"en":"Colin is investigating ways to reuse waste food.","zh":"Colin 正在研究再利用廚餘的方法。"},{"en":"Reuse waste food means use food that might otherwise be thrown away for a new purpose.","zh":"再利用廚餘意思是把原本可能被丟掉的食物用於新用途。"},{"en":"Restaurants can reuse waste food by turning vegetable scraps into soup stock.","zh":"餐廳可以把蔬菜碎料做成湯底來再利用廚餘。"},{"en":"Reusing waste food helps reduce landfill waste.","zh":"再利用廚餘有助減少堆填垃圾。"},{"en":"The phrase is about giving unwanted food a second use.","zh":"這個片語是關於給不需要的食物第二個用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"look at bread","meaning":"研究麵包","examples":[{"en":"Colin was looking at bread in his waste food project.","zh":"Colin 在他的廚餘專題中研究麵包。"},{"en":"Look at bread means study or examine bread as the focus of research.","zh":"研究麵包意思是把麵包作為研究焦點來考察。"},{"en":"The students looked at bread to see how quickly it became stale.","zh":"學生研究麵包，看看它多久會變乾。"},{"en":"Looking at one food item can make a project more focused.","zh":"研究一種食物可以令專題更集中。"},{"en":"The phrase means investigate bread, not simply look at it with your eyes.","zh":"這個片語意思是調查麵包，而不只是用眼睛看。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hard work","meaning":"辛苦的工作","examples":[{"en":"The bread reuse project has been hard work.","zh":"麵包再利用專題一直是辛苦的工作。"},{"en":"Hard work means work that needs a lot of effort, time, or patience.","zh":"辛苦的工作意思是需要很多努力、時間或耐性的工作。"},{"en":"Testing the recipe again and again was hard work.","zh":"一次又一次測試食譜是辛苦的工作。"},{"en":"Hard work can feel tiring, but it may lead to a satisfying result.","zh":"辛苦的工作可能令人疲倦，但也可能帶來令人滿意的結果。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the project was not easy.","zh":"這個片語顯示專題並不容易。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the basic process","meaning":"基本流程","examples":[{"en":"The basic process was quite straightforward.","zh":"基本流程相當簡單直接。"},{"en":"The basic process means the main steps needed to do something.","zh":"基本流程意思是完成某事所需的主要步驟。"},{"en":"The basic process for making bread includes mixing, rising, and baking.","zh":"製作麵包的基本流程包括混合、發酵和烘焗。"},{"en":"Understanding the basic process helps people follow the method more easily.","zh":"理解基本流程可以幫助人更容易跟從方法。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the simple structure of a task.","zh":"這個片語集中於任務的簡單結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"quite straightforward","meaning":"相當簡單直接","examples":[{"en":"The basic process was quite straightforward.","zh":"基本流程相當簡單直接。"},{"en":"Quite straightforward means fairly simple and easy to understand.","zh":"相當簡單直接意思是頗簡單，而且容易明白。"},{"en":"The instructions were quite straightforward, so we finished quickly.","zh":"指示相當簡單直接，所以我們很快完成。"},{"en":"A process can be quite straightforward even if it still takes effort.","zh":"一個流程即使仍需要努力，也可以相當簡單直接。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests there were no complicated steps.","zh":"這個片語暗示沒有複雜步驟。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"break something down to","meaning":"把……分解成","examples":[{"en":"Colin broke the stale bread down to a paste.","zh":"Colin 把變乾的麵包分解成糊狀物。"},{"en":"Break something down to a form means reduce or process it until it becomes that form.","zh":"把某物分解成某種形態，意思是處理它直到它變成那種形態。"},{"en":"The machine broke the vegetables down to a smooth soup.","zh":"機器把蔬菜分解成順滑的湯。"},{"en":"Breaking bread down to paste makes it easier to reshape.","zh":"把麵包分解成糊狀物可以更容易重新塑形。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing the physical form of something.","zh":"這個片語描述改變某物的物理形態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stale bread","meaning":"變乾的麵包","examples":[{"en":"Colin used stale bread in his food reuse project.","zh":"Colin 在他的食物再利用專題中使用變乾的麵包。"},{"en":"Stale bread is bread that is no longer fresh and has become dry or hard.","zh":"變乾的麵包是不再新鮮、變乾或變硬的麵包。"},{"en":"Stale bread can still be used for breadcrumbs or pudding.","zh":"變乾的麵包仍可用來做麵包糠或布甸。"},{"en":"Reusing stale bread can prevent unnecessary food waste.","zh":"再利用變乾的麵包可以防止不必要的食物浪費。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bread that people might otherwise throw away.","zh":"這個片語描述人們原本可能會丟掉的麵包。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"paste","meaning":"糊狀物","examples":[{"en":"The stale bread was broken down to a paste.","zh":"變乾的麵包被分解成糊狀物。"},{"en":"Paste is a thick, soft, wet mixture.","zh":"糊狀物是濃稠、柔軟而濕潤的混合物。"},{"en":"The cook made a paste from beans, water, and spices.","zh":"廚師用豆、水和香料做成糊狀物。"},{"en":"A paste can be shaped more easily than dry pieces of bread.","zh":"糊狀物比乾麵包碎塊更容易塑形。"},{"en":"The word describes the texture of the reused bread mixture.","zh":"這個詞描述再利用麵包混合物的質感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reform it","meaning":"重新塑形","examples":[{"en":"Colin broke the bread down to a paste and then reformed it.","zh":"Colin 把麵包分解成糊狀物，然後重新塑形。"},{"en":"Reform it means shape it again into a new form.","zh":"重新塑形意思是把它再次塑造成新的形態。"},{"en":"The students melted old plastic and reformed it into a small tile.","zh":"學生把舊塑膠熔化，並重新塑形成小磚塊。"},{"en":"Reforming food can turn waste into something useful and attractive.","zh":"重新塑形食物可以把廢料變成有用和吸引的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the step after breaking the bread down.","zh":"這個片語顯示把麵包分解後的步驟。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"3-D printing","meaning":"3D 打印","examples":[{"en":"Colin used 3-D printing to make biscuits from the paste.","zh":"Colin 使用 3D 打印把糊狀物製成餅乾。"},{"en":"3-D printing is a process that builds objects layer by layer from a digital design.","zh":"3D 打印是一種根據數碼設計逐層製作物件的過程。"},{"en":"Some chefs experiment with 3-D printing to create unusual food shapes.","zh":"有些廚師嘗試用 3D 打印創造不尋常的食物形狀。"},{"en":"3-D printing can make patterns that are difficult to shape by hand.","zh":"3D 打印可以製作手工難以塑造的圖案。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the technology Colin used to form the biscuits.","zh":"這個片語描述 Colin 用來塑造餅乾的技術。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"make something into","meaning":"把……製成……","examples":[{"en":"Colin made the paste into biscuits.","zh":"Colin 把糊狀物製成餅乾。"},{"en":"Make something into something else means change it into a new form or product.","zh":"把某物製成另一物，意思是把它轉變成新的形態或產品。"},{"en":"The chef made leftover rice into rice cakes.","zh":"廚師把剩飯製成米餅。"},{"en":"Making waste food into snacks can reduce rubbish.","zh":"把廚餘製成小食可以減少垃圾。"},{"en":"The phrase shows transformation from one thing to another.","zh":"這個片語顯示從一種東西轉化成另一種東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"play around with","meaning":"嘗試；擺弄","examples":[{"en":"Colin had time to play around with different patterns.","zh":"Colin 有時間嘗試不同圖案。"},{"en":"Play around with something means try different ideas in a relaxed or experimental way.","zh":"嘗試或擺弄某物意思是以輕鬆或實驗方式嘗試不同想法。"},{"en":"The designer played around with colours before choosing the final poster.","zh":"設計師在選定最終海報前嘗試不同顏色。"},{"en":"Playing around with patterns can lead to creative results.","zh":"嘗試不同圖案可以帶來有創意的成果。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests experimenting, not working in a fixed way.","zh":"這個片語暗示實驗，而不是按固定方式工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"different patterns","meaning":"不同圖案","examples":[{"en":"Colin experimented with different patterns for the biscuits.","zh":"Colin 為餅乾嘗試不同圖案。"},{"en":"Different patterns are different repeated shapes, lines, colours, or designs.","zh":"不同圖案是不同的重複形狀、線條、顏色或設計。"},{"en":"The bakery tested different patterns on its biscuits to make them more attractive.","zh":"麵包店在餅乾上測試不同圖案，使它們更吸引。"},{"en":"Different patterns can make simple food look special.","zh":"不同圖案可以令簡單食物看起來特別。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visual variety in design.","zh":"這個片語描述設計上的視覺變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"add fruit and vegetables","meaning":"加入水果和蔬菜","examples":[{"en":"Colin added fruit and vegetables to the biscuit mixture.","zh":"Colin 在餅乾混合物中加入水果和蔬菜。"},{"en":"Add fruit and vegetables means put fruit and vegetables into a mixture or dish.","zh":"加入水果和蔬菜意思是把水果和蔬菜放進混合物或菜式中。"},{"en":"You can add fruit and vegetables to muffins for colour and nutrition.","zh":"你可以在鬆餅中加入水果和蔬菜，以增加顏色和營養。"},{"en":"Adding fruit and vegetables can improve taste, colour, and health value.","zh":"加入水果和蔬菜可以改善味道、顏色和健康價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding natural ingredients to food.","zh":"這個片語描述在食物中加入天然材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"an appetising colour","meaning":"令人有食慾的顏色","examples":[{"en":"Fruit and vegetables made the biscuits a more appetising colour.","zh":"水果和蔬菜令餅乾有更令人有食慾的顏色。"},{"en":"An appetising colour is a colour that makes food look pleasant and attractive to eat.","zh":"令人有食慾的顏色是令食物看起來美味和吸引人食用的顏色。"},{"en":"Golden brown is an appetising colour for freshly baked bread.","zh":"金啡色對新鮮焗好的麵包來說是令人有食慾的顏色。"},{"en":"Food with an appetising colour may make people more willing to try it.","zh":"有令人有食慾顏色的食物可能令人更願意嘗試。"},{"en":"The phrase connects appearance with appetite.","zh":"這個片語把外觀和食慾連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be pleased with","meaning":"對……感到滿意","examples":[{"en":"Colin was really pleased with what he managed to produce.","zh":"Colin 對自己成功製作出的東西非常滿意。"},{"en":"Be pleased with something means feel happy or satisfied about it.","zh":"對某事感到滿意意思是對它感到高興或滿足。"},{"en":"The teacher was pleased with the students’ careful research.","zh":"老師對學生仔細的研究感到滿意。"},{"en":"People are pleased with a result when it meets or exceeds their expectations.","zh":"當結果符合或超出期望時，人們會感到滿意。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses satisfaction.","zh":"這個片語表達滿足感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"manage to produce","meaning":"成功製作出","examples":[{"en":"Colin was pleased with what he managed to produce.","zh":"Colin 對自己成功製作出的東西感到滿意。"},{"en":"Manage to produce means succeed in making something, often after effort.","zh":"成功製作出意思是通常經過努力後成功做出某物。"},{"en":"After many tests, the team managed to produce a tasty snack.","zh":"經過多次測試後，團隊成功製作出一款美味小食。"},{"en":"Managing to produce a useful product can feel rewarding.","zh":"成功製作出有用產品會令人有成就感。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests success after work or difficulty.","zh":"這個片語暗示經過工作或困難後成功。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a great feeling","meaning":"很好的感覺","examples":[{"en":"It must have been a great feeling to make something appetising.","zh":"做出令人有食慾的東西一定是很好的感覺。"},{"en":"A great feeling means a very pleasant or satisfying emotion.","zh":"很好的感覺意思是非常愉快或令人滿足的情緒。"},{"en":"Finishing a difficult project on time is a great feeling.","zh":"準時完成困難專題是很好的感覺。"},{"en":"It can be a great feeling to turn waste into something useful.","zh":"把廢物變成有用東西可以是很好的感覺。"},{"en":"The phrase describes emotional satisfaction.","zh":"這個片語描述情感上的滿足。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make something appetising out of","meaning":"用……做出令人有食慾的東西","examples":[{"en":"Colin made something appetising out of bits of old bread.","zh":"Colin 用舊麵包碎塊做出令人有食慾的東西。"},{"en":"Make something appetising out of something means turn an unattractive ingredient into food that looks or tastes good.","zh":"用某物做出令人有食慾的東西，意思是把不吸引的食材變成看起來或吃起來好的食物。"},{"en":"The chef made an appetising soup out of leftover vegetables.","zh":"廚師用剩餘蔬菜做出令人有食慾的湯。"},{"en":"Making something appetising out of waste food can reduce rubbish and surprise people.","zh":"用廚餘做出令人有食慾的東西可以減少垃圾並令人驚喜。"},{"en":"The phrase shows creative reuse of ordinary or unwanted materials.","zh":"這個片語顯示創意地再利用普通或不需要的材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"bits of old bread","meaning":"舊麵包碎塊","examples":[{"en":"Colin reused bits of old bread that might have been thrown away.","zh":"Colin 再利用可能會被丟掉的舊麵包碎塊。"},{"en":"Bits of old bread are small pieces of bread that are no longer fresh.","zh":"舊麵包碎塊是不再新鮮的小塊麵包。"},{"en":"Bits of old bread can be made into crumbs for cooking.","zh":"舊麵包碎塊可以製成麵包糠來煮食。"},{"en":"Reusing bits of old bread is a simple way to prevent food waste.","zh":"再利用舊麵包碎塊是防止食物浪費的簡單方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes small leftover pieces of bread.","zh":"這個片語描述剩下的小塊舊麵包。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be thrown away","meaning":"被丟掉","examples":[{"en":"The old bread would have been thrown away otherwise.","zh":"否則，那些舊麵包會被丟掉。"},{"en":"Be thrown away means be put in the rubbish and not used.","zh":"被丟掉意思是被放進垃圾中，不再使用。"},{"en":"Fruit with small marks is often thrown away by shops.","zh":"有小瑕疵的水果常被商店丟掉。"},{"en":"Food that is thrown away wastes money, labour, and resources.","zh":"被丟掉的食物浪費金錢、勞力和資源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what happens to unwanted items.","zh":"這個片語描述不需要的物品會發生甚麼事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"otherwise","meaning":"否則","examples":[{"en":"The bread would have been thrown away otherwise.","zh":"否則，那些麵包會被丟掉。"},{"en":"Otherwise means if that had not happened, or in a different situation.","zh":"否則意思是如果那件事沒有發生，或在另一種情況下。"},{"en":"Take the leftovers home; otherwise, they will be wasted.","zh":"把剩菜帶回家；否則，它們會被浪費。"},{"en":"People use otherwise to show what would happen without a certain action.","zh":"人們用 otherwise 顯示如果沒有某個行動會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an action with the problem it prevents.","zh":"這個片語把行動和它防止的問題連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be interested in","meaning":"對……感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Colin hopes some restaurants will be interested in the biscuits.","zh":"Colin 希望一些餐廳會對這些餅乾感興趣。"},{"en":"Be interested in something means want to know more about it or possibly use it.","zh":"對某事感興趣意思是想了解更多，或可能想使用它。"},{"en":"The café was interested in selling the students’ recycled snacks.","zh":"那間咖啡店對售賣學生的再造小食感興趣。"},{"en":"If restaurants are interested in a product, they may ask for samples.","zh":"如果餐廳對產品感興趣，可能會要求樣品。"},{"en":"The phrase shows possible curiosity or business interest.","zh":"這個片語顯示可能的好奇或商業興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"restaurants in town","meaning":"鎮上的餐廳","examples":[{"en":"Colin hopes restaurants in town will be interested in his biscuits.","zh":"Colin 希望鎮上的餐廳會對他的餅乾感興趣。"},{"en":"Restaurants in town are eating places located in the local town area.","zh":"鎮上的餐廳是位於本地城鎮地區的食肆。"},{"en":"Restaurants in town often look for new snacks to attract customers.","zh":"鎮上的餐廳常尋找新小食來吸引顧客。"},{"en":"If restaurants in town support a project, it may reach more people.","zh":"如果鎮上的餐廳支持一個項目，它可能接觸到更多人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to local restaurants near the speaker.","zh":"這個片語指說話者附近的本地餐廳。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"send someone samples","meaning":"寄樣品給某人","examples":[{"en":"Colin is going to send restaurants some samples.","zh":"Colin 打算寄一些樣品給餐廳。"},{"en":"Send someone samples means give or mail small examples of a product for them to try.","zh":"寄樣品給某人意思是把產品的小份例子給或寄給對方試用。"},{"en":"The bakery sent cafés samples of its new biscuits.","zh":"麵包店寄了新餅乾樣品給咖啡店。"},{"en":"Samples help buyers decide whether they like a product.","zh":"樣品幫助買家決定是否喜歡產品。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in business and product testing.","zh":"這個片語常見於商業和產品測試。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"come across something","meaning":"偶然看到；偶然發現","examples":[{"en":"Marie came across something on the internet.","zh":"Marie 在網上偶然看到一些東西。"},{"en":"Come across something means find something by chance.","zh":"偶然看到或偶然發現某物意思是意外地找到某物。"},{"en":"I came across an article about food labels while searching online.","zh":"我在網上搜尋時偶然看到一篇關於食品標籤的文章。"},{"en":"People often come across useful ideas when researching another topic.","zh":"人們研究另一個題目時，常偶然發現有用想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an accidental discovery.","zh":"這個片語描述意外發現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on the internet","meaning":"在網上","examples":[{"en":"Marie came across a food-label idea on the internet.","zh":"Marie 在網上偶然看到一個食品標籤想法。"},{"en":"On the internet means online, through websites or digital platforms.","zh":"在網上意思是透過網站或數碼平台。"},{"en":"Students can find research articles on the internet.","zh":"學生可以在網上找到研究文章。"},{"en":"Information on the internet can be useful, but it should be checked carefully.","zh":"網上的資料可以有用，但應仔細核對。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where something was found.","zh":"這個片語指出某物在哪裏被找到。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"touch-sensitive sensors","meaning":"觸覺感應器","examples":[{"en":"A company has developed touch-sensitive sensors for food labels.","zh":"一間公司為食品標籤開發了觸覺感應器。"},{"en":"Touch-sensitive sensors are devices that react when someone touches them.","zh":"觸覺感應器是有人觸摸時會作出反應的裝置。"},{"en":"Touch-sensitive sensors on a label can change texture to give information.","zh":"標籤上的觸覺感應器可以改變質感來提供資訊。"},{"en":"These sensors may help people check food without reading small printed dates.","zh":"這些感應器可能幫助人不用閱讀細小印刷日期也能檢查食物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes technology that responds to touch.","zh":"這個片語描述會對觸摸作出反應的科技。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"food labels","meaning":"食品標籤","examples":[{"en":"The company developed sensors for food labels.","zh":"這間公司為食品標籤開發感應器。"},{"en":"Food labels are labels on food packages that give information about the food.","zh":"食品標籤是食品包裝上的標籤，提供關於食物的資料。"},{"en":"Food labels may show ingredients, dates, weight, and storage instructions.","zh":"食品標籤可能顯示成分、日期、重量和儲存指示。"},{"en":"Good food labels help people decide whether food is safe or suitable for them.","zh":"好的食品標籤幫助人決定食物是否安全或適合自己。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to information placed on food packaging.","zh":"這個片語指放在食品包裝上的資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"food package","meaning":"食品包裝","examples":[{"en":"The sensor is placed on the food package.","zh":"感應器放在食品包裝上。"},{"en":"A food package is the container or wrapping around food.","zh":"食品包裝是包住食物的容器或包裝物。"},{"en":"A food package may be made of plastic, paper, glass, or metal.","zh":"食品包裝可以由塑膠、紙、玻璃或金屬製成。"},{"en":"Information on a food package helps customers understand what they are buying.","zh":"食品包裝上的資訊幫助顧客了解自己購買的是甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase names the outside material that holds the food.","zh":"這個片語指出盛載食物的外層材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"when the label is smooth","meaning":"當標籤是光滑的時候","examples":[{"en":"When the label is smooth, the food is fresh.","zh":"當標籤是光滑的時候，食物就是新鮮的。"},{"en":"When the label is smooth means when the label feels flat and has no bumps.","zh":"當標籤是光滑的時候，意思是標籤摸起來平滑，沒有凸起。"},{"en":"If the label is smooth, customers know the milk has not gone bad.","zh":"如果標籤是光滑的，顧客就知道牛奶沒有變壞。"},{"en":"A smooth label gives a simple touch signal about freshness.","zh":"光滑標籤提供關於新鮮度的簡單觸覺信號。"},{"en":"The phrase explains one condition of the sensor.","zh":"這個片語解釋感應器的一種狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"feel bumps","meaning":"摸到凸起","examples":[{"en":"You can feel bumps on the label when the food has gone bad.","zh":"當食物變壞時，你可以在標籤上摸到凸起。"},{"en":"Feel bumps means notice raised areas by touching something.","zh":"摸到凸起意思是透過觸摸察覺隆起的地方。"},{"en":"A person can feel bumps on a textured label with their fingers.","zh":"人們可以用手指在有質感的標籤上摸到凸起。"},{"en":"Feeling bumps can give information without needing to read words.","zh":"摸到凸起可以不用閱讀文字也取得資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how users detect a change by touch.","zh":"這個片語描述用戶如何透過觸摸發現變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"go bad","meaning":"變壞；變質","examples":[{"en":"The bumps show that the food has gone bad.","zh":"凸起顯示食物已經變壞。"},{"en":"Go bad means become spoiled and no longer safe or pleasant to eat.","zh":"變壞或變質意思是食物腐壞，不再安全或適合食用。"},{"en":"Milk can go bad quickly if it is left outside the fridge.","zh":"牛奶如果放在雪櫃外，可能很快變壞。"},{"en":"Food that has gone bad may smell strange or change texture.","zh":"變壞的食物可能有奇怪氣味或質感改變。"},{"en":"The phrase is common when talking about food freshness.","zh":"這個片語常用於談論食物新鮮度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"start off as","meaning":"最初是","examples":[{"en":"The idea started off as a project for visually impaired people.","zh":"這個想法最初是為視障人士而設的專題。"},{"en":"Start off as something means begin as one thing before developing into something else.","zh":"最初是某物，意思是開始時是某樣東西，之後可能發展成其他東西。"},{"en":"The school garden started off as a small student project.","zh":"學校花園最初是一個小型學生項目。"},{"en":"An idea may start off as a simple solution and later become useful to many people.","zh":"一個想法可能最初是簡單解決方法，後來對很多人有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the original beginning of an idea.","zh":"這個片語描述想法的原本起點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"visually impaired people","meaning":"視障人士","examples":[{"en":"The project was designed to help visually impaired people.","zh":"這個專題是為了幫助視障人士而設計的。"},{"en":"Visually impaired people are people who have difficulty seeing or cannot see.","zh":"視障人士是指視力有困難或不能看見的人。"},{"en":"Touch-based labels can help visually impaired people check food more easily.","zh":"觸覺標籤可以幫助視障人士更容易檢查食物。"},{"en":"Public services should be designed so visually impaired people can use them safely.","zh":"公共服務應設計得讓視障人士能安全使用。"},{"en":"The phrase is a respectful way to describe people with sight difficulties.","zh":"這個片語是尊重地描述有視力困難人士的說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fit to eat","meaning":"適合食用","examples":[{"en":"The label helps people know whether food is fit to eat.","zh":"標籤幫助人知道食物是否適合食用。"},{"en":"Fit to eat means safe and suitable for eating.","zh":"適合食用意思是安全並適合吃。"},{"en":"Food that smells rotten is usually not fit to eat.","zh":"聞起來腐臭的食物通常不適合食用。"},{"en":"A clear label can help customers know whether milk is still fit to eat.","zh":"清晰標籤可以幫助顧客知道牛奶是否仍適合食用。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used when judging food safety.","zh":"這個片語常用於判斷食物安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"solid food","meaning":"固體食物","examples":[{"en":"Colin asks whether the label is only for solid food.","zh":"Colin 問標籤是否只用於固體食物。"},{"en":"Solid food is food that is firm, not liquid.","zh":"固體食物是有固定形態、不是液體的食物。"},{"en":"Bread, fruit, meat, and biscuits are examples of solid food.","zh":"麵包、水果、肉類和餅乾都是固體食物的例子。"},{"en":"Colin asks about solid food because he wants to know if the label also works for drinks.","zh":"Colin 問到固體食物，因為他想知道標籤是否也適用於飲品。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts food with liquids like milk or juice.","zh":"這個片語把食物與牛奶或果汁等液體作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"things like","meaning":"例如……之類的東西","examples":[{"en":"The label can be used for things like milk and juice.","zh":"這個標籤可以用於牛奶和果汁之類的東西。"},{"en":"Things like means examples such as these.","zh":"例如……之類的東西意思是像這些例子。"},{"en":"The shop sells healthy snacks, things like nuts, fruit bars, and yoghurt.","zh":"那間店售賣健康小食，例如堅果、水果棒和乳酪之類的東西。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when giving examples rather than a complete list.","zh":"人們舉例而不是列出完整清單時會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It makes speech sound natural and informal.","zh":"它令說話聽起來自然和口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"milk and juice","meaning":"牛奶和果汁","examples":[{"en":"The label can be used for drinks such as milk and juice.","zh":"這個標籤可以用於牛奶和果汁等飲品。"},{"en":"Milk and juice are common drinks that can spoil if stored badly or kept too long.","zh":"牛奶和果汁是常見飲品，如果儲存不當或放太久可能會變壞。"},{"en":"A freshness label on milk and juice could help people avoid drinking spoiled products.","zh":"牛奶和果汁上的新鮮度標籤可以幫助人避免飲用變壞產品。"},{"en":"Drinks like milk and juice need clear storage information.","zh":"牛奶和果汁等飲品需要清晰儲存資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase gives examples of liquid foods.","zh":"這個片語提供液態食品的例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"drug storage","meaning":"藥物儲存","examples":[{"en":"Marie thinks the sensors could be useful for drug storage.","zh":"Marie 認為這些感應器可能對藥物儲存有用。"},{"en":"Drug storage means keeping medicines in the right conditions so they remain safe and effective.","zh":"藥物儲存意思是把藥物保存在正確環境中，使其保持安全和有效。"},{"en":"Hospitals need careful drug storage because some medicines are damaged by heat.","zh":"醫院需要仔細的藥物儲存，因為有些藥物會受熱損壞。"},{"en":"Sensors could help staff know when drug storage conditions are unsafe.","zh":"感應器可以幫助職員知道藥物儲存環境何時不安全。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to storing medicine, not illegal drugs in this context.","zh":"在這個語境中，這個片語指儲存藥物，不是非法毒品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hospitals and pharmacies","meaning":"醫院和藥房","examples":[{"en":"The sensors could be used in hospitals and pharmacies.","zh":"這些感應器可以用於醫院和藥房。"},{"en":"Hospitals and pharmacies are places where medicines are used, stored, or supplied.","zh":"醫院和藥房是使用、儲存或供應藥物的地方。"},{"en":"Hospitals and pharmacies must check that medicines are safe for patients.","zh":"醫院和藥房必須檢查藥物對病人是否安全。"},{"en":"Sensors in hospitals and pharmacies could warn staff if products are no longer safe.","zh":"醫院和藥房中的感應器可以在產品不再安全時提醒職員。"},{"en":"The phrase names two medical settings.","zh":"這個片語指出兩種醫療場所。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come back to food","meaning":"回到食品方面","examples":[{"en":"Colin comes back to food after discussing drug storage.","zh":"Colin 在討論藥物儲存後回到食品方面。"},{"en":"Come back to food means return to the topic of food after talking about something else.","zh":"回到食品方面意思是在談過其他事情後，再回到食物這個話題。"},{"en":"After discussing packaging, let’s come back to food freshness.","zh":"討論完包裝後，讓我們回到食品新鮮度方面。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to guide a conversation back to the main topic.","zh":"人們用這個片語把對話帶回主要主題。"},{"en":"It signals a change back to an earlier subject.","zh":"它表示回到較早的話題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"besides freshness","meaning":"除了新鮮度之外","examples":[{"en":"The label might show information besides freshness.","zh":"標籤除了新鮮度之外，可能還會顯示其他資訊。"},{"en":"Besides freshness means in addition to information about how fresh the food is.","zh":"除了新鮮度之外，意思是在關於食物是否新鮮的資訊以外。"},{"en":"A label could show weight besides freshness.","zh":"標籤除了新鮮度之外，還可以顯示重量。"},{"en":"Food labels may become more useful if they show details besides freshness.","zh":"如果食品標籤除了新鮮度之外還顯示其他細節，可能會更有用。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another kind of information.","zh":"這個片語加入另一類資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a joint of meat","meaning":"一大塊肉","examples":[{"en":"The label might show how many kilograms a joint of meat is.","zh":"標籤可能顯示一大塊肉有多少公斤。"},{"en":"A joint of meat is a large piece of meat, often used for roasting.","zh":"一大塊肉是指一塊較大的肉，通常用來烤焗。"},{"en":"A butcher may weigh a joint of meat before selling it.","zh":"肉店可能在出售前稱一大塊肉的重量。"},{"en":"A label showing the weight of a joint of meat would help customers compare prices.","zh":"顯示一大塊肉重量的標籤可以幫助顧客比較價格。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to one large cut of meat.","zh":"這個片語指一大件切好的肉。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"all sorts of possibilities","meaning":"各種可能性","examples":[{"en":"Marie says there are all sorts of possibilities.","zh":"Marie 說有各種可能性。"},{"en":"All sorts of possibilities means many different possible uses, results, or ideas.","zh":"各種可能性意思是有許多不同的可能用途、結果或想法。"},{"en":"With smart labels, there are all sorts of possibilities for food safety.","zh":"有了智能標籤，食品安全方面有各種可能性。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when an idea could develop in many directions.","zh":"當一個想法可以向很多方向發展時，人們會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It suggests variety and future potential.","zh":"它暗示多樣性和未來潛力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"food trends","meaning":"食品趨勢","examples":[{"en":"Colin read an article about food trends.","zh":"Colin 讀了一篇關於食品趨勢的文章。"},{"en":"Food trends are popular changes in what people eat, buy, or care about in food.","zh":"食品趨勢是人們在飲食、購買或關注食品方面的流行變化。"},{"en":"Plant-based meals and local products are examples of food trends.","zh":"植物性餐點和本地產品都是食品趨勢的例子。"},{"en":"Food trends can affect shops, restaurants, farms, and consumers.","zh":"食品趨勢可以影響商店、餐廳、農場和消費者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing habits in the food world.","zh":"這個片語描述食品世界中的習慣變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"predict how","meaning":"預測……如何","examples":[{"en":"The article predicted how eating habits might change.","zh":"這篇文章預測飲食習慣可能如何改變。"},{"en":"Predict how means say what way something may change or happen in the future.","zh":"預測……如何意思是說明某事將來可能以甚麼方式改變或發生。"},{"en":"Experts try to predict how shopping habits will change next year.","zh":"專家嘗試預測明年購物習慣將如何改變。"},{"en":"Predictions are not certain, but they are based on evidence or patterns.","zh":"預測並不一定準確，但通常根據證據或模式。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a forecast about future change.","zh":"這個片語引出對未來變化的預測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"eating habits","meaning":"飲食習慣","examples":[{"en":"The article discussed how eating habits might change.","zh":"這篇文章討論飲食習慣可能如何改變。"},{"en":"Eating habits are the usual ways people choose, prepare, and eat food.","zh":"飲食習慣是人們選擇、準備和進食食物的慣常方式。"},{"en":"Eating habits may change when people become more concerned about health.","zh":"當人們更關注健康時，飲食習慣可能會改變。"},{"en":"Busy work schedules can affect people’s eating habits.","zh":"繁忙的工作時間可以影響人們的飲食習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to regular food choices and behaviours.","zh":"這個片語指規律的食物選擇和行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the next few years","meaning":"在未來幾年","examples":[{"en":"Eating habits may change in the next few years.","zh":"飲食習慣可能在未來幾年改變。"},{"en":"In the next few years means during the coming several years.","zh":"在未來幾年意思是在接下來數年之內。"},{"en":"Food packaging may become smarter in the next few years.","zh":"食品包裝可能在未來幾年變得更智能。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when talking about the near future.","zh":"人們談論較近的未來時會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It gives a time frame without naming exact dates.","zh":"它提供時間範圍，但不列出確切日期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"more focus on","meaning":"更重視……","examples":[{"en":"Marie mentions more focus on local products.","zh":"Marie 提到更重視本地產品。"},{"en":"More focus on something means greater attention or importance given to it.","zh":"更重視某事意思是給予它更多注意或重要性。"},{"en":"Schools are putting more focus on healthy lunches.","zh":"學校正更重視健康午餐。"},{"en":"More focus on local products could help reduce transport and packaging waste.","zh":"更重視本地產品可能有助減少運輸和包裝浪費。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shift in attention.","zh":"這個片語描述注意力的轉移。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"local products","meaning":"本地產品","examples":[{"en":"Shops may need to sell more local products.","zh":"商店可能需要售賣更多本地產品。"},{"en":"Local products are goods made or grown near the place where they are sold.","zh":"本地產品是在銷售地附近製造或種植的商品。"},{"en":"Local products can include vegetables, bread, sauces, or handmade snacks.","zh":"本地產品可以包括蔬菜、麵包、醬料或手工小食。"},{"en":"Buying local products can support nearby farmers and businesses.","zh":"購買本地產品可以支持附近農民和商戶。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts local goods with imported goods.","zh":"這個片語把本地商品與進口商品作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"seem so obvious","meaning":"看起來很明顯","examples":[{"en":"Buying local products seems so obvious to Marie.","zh":"購買本地產品對 Marie 來說看起來很明顯。"},{"en":"Seem so obvious means appear very clear, sensible, or easy to understand.","zh":"看起來很明顯意思是顯得非常清楚、合理或容易理解。"},{"en":"Reducing food waste seems so obvious, but many people still throw food away.","zh":"減少食物浪費看起來很明顯，但許多人仍然丟掉食物。"},{"en":"Something can seem obvious to one person but not be acted on by others.","zh":"某事對一個人來說可能很明顯，但其他人未必會行動。"},{"en":"The phrase shows surprise that an easy idea is not already common.","zh":"這個片語顯示說話者驚訝於一個簡單想法尚未普及。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be full of","meaning":"充滿……","examples":[{"en":"The shops are still full of imported foods.","zh":"商店仍然充滿進口食品。"},{"en":"Be full of something means contain a large amount of it.","zh":"充滿某物意思是含有大量某物。"},{"en":"The market was full of fresh fruit before the festival.","zh":"節日前，市場充滿新鮮水果。"},{"en":"If shops are full of imported foods, local products may be harder to find.","zh":"如果商店充滿進口食品，本地產品可能較難找到。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what is present in large quantities.","zh":"這個片語描述大量存在的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"imported foods","meaning":"進口食品","examples":[{"en":"Many shops are still full of imported foods.","zh":"許多商店仍然充滿進口食品。"},{"en":"Imported foods are foods brought in from other countries or regions.","zh":"進口食品是從其他國家或地區運來的食物。"},{"en":"Imported foods may include fruit, snacks, cheese, and frozen meals.","zh":"進口食品可能包括水果、小食、芝士和急凍餐。"},{"en":"Shops sell imported foods because customers like variety.","zh":"商店售賣進口食品，因為顧客喜歡多樣選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts food from elsewhere with local products.","zh":"這個片語把來自外地的食物與本地產品作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be more proactive","meaning":"更積極主動","examples":[{"en":"Shops need to be more proactive about local products.","zh":"商店需要在本地產品方面更積極主動。"},{"en":"Be more proactive means take action early instead of waiting for others to act.","zh":"更積極主動意思是提早採取行動，而不是等待別人行動。"},{"en":"Schools should be more proactive in teaching students about food waste.","zh":"學校應更積極主動地教學生認識食物浪費。"},{"en":"Retailers can be more proactive by clearly displaying local products.","zh":"零售商可以透過清楚展示本地產品來更積極主動。"},{"en":"The phrase praises active, planned action.","zh":"這個片語稱讚主動而有計劃的行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"address that","meaning":"處理那個問題","examples":[{"en":"Retailers need to be more proactive to address that.","zh":"零售商需要更積極主動來處理那個問題。"},{"en":"Address that means deal with that problem or issue.","zh":"處理那個問題意思是應對或解決那個問題。"},{"en":"If customers cannot find local food, shops should address that by changing displays.","zh":"如果顧客找不到本地食物，商店應透過改變陳列來處理那個問題。"},{"en":"People address a problem when they take steps to solve it.","zh":"人們採取步驟解決問題時，就是在處理問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to a problem already mentioned.","zh":"這個片語指回前面已提到的問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"motivate consumers to change","meaning":"推動消費者改變","examples":[{"en":"Retailers need to motivate consumers to change.","zh":"零售商需要推動消費者改變。"},{"en":"Motivate consumers to change means encourage shoppers to behave differently.","zh":"推動消費者改變意思是鼓勵購物者改變行為。"},{"en":"Discounts on local vegetables can motivate consumers to change their buying habits.","zh":"本地蔬菜折扣可以推動消費者改變購買習慣。"},{"en":"Clear information may motivate consumers to choose less wasteful products.","zh":"清楚資訊可能推動消費者選擇較少浪費的產品。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on encouraging customers to make new choices.","zh":"這個片語集中於鼓勵顧客作出新選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be aware of","meaning":"意識到","examples":[{"en":"Everyone is aware of the need to reduce unnecessary packaging.","zh":"每個人都意識到需要減少不必要的包裝。"},{"en":"Be aware of something means know that it exists or understand it.","zh":"意識到某事意思是知道它存在或理解它。"},{"en":"Many shoppers are aware of the problem of plastic waste.","zh":"許多購物者意識到塑膠垃圾問題。"},{"en":"Being aware of a problem is the first step toward solving it.","zh":"意識到問題是解決問題的第一步。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge or understanding.","zh":"這個片語描述認識或理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the need for","meaning":"對……的需要","examples":[{"en":"Everyone is aware of the need for a reduction in unnecessary packaging.","zh":"每個人都意識到對減少不必要包裝的需要。"},{"en":"The need for something means the importance or necessity of having or doing it.","zh":"對某事的需要意思是擁有或做某事的重要性或必要性。"},{"en":"There is a need for clearer food labels in supermarkets.","zh":"超市有對更清晰食品標籤的需要。"},{"en":"Recognising the need for change can lead to action.","zh":"認識到改變的需要可以帶來行動。"},{"en":"The phrase points to something that is necessary.","zh":"這個片語指出必要的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a reduction in","meaning":"……的減少","examples":[{"en":"There needs to be a reduction in unnecessary packaging.","zh":"不必要包裝需要減少。"},{"en":"A reduction in something means a decrease or lowering of its amount.","zh":"某物的減少意思是數量下降或降低。"},{"en":"A reduction in food waste would save money and resources.","zh":"食物浪費的減少可以節省金錢和資源。"},{"en":"Supermarkets can support a reduction in plastic by using refill stations.","zh":"超市可以透過使用補充站來支持塑膠的減少。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used when discussing environmental improvement.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論環境改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unnecessary packaging","meaning":"不必要的包裝","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets still use a lot of unnecessary packaging.","zh":"超市仍然使用很多不必要的包裝。"},{"en":"Unnecessary packaging is packaging that is not really needed to protect or carry a product.","zh":"不必要的包裝是指其實不需要用來保護或盛載產品的包裝。"},{"en":"A banana wrapped in plastic is often seen as unnecessary packaging.","zh":"用塑膠包着香蕉常被視為不必要的包裝。"},{"en":"Unnecessary packaging creates extra waste and uses more resources.","zh":"不必要的包裝製造額外垃圾並使用更多資源。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises packaging that could be avoided.","zh":"這個片語批評可以避免的包裝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"just about everything","meaning":"幾乎所有東西","examples":[{"en":"Just about everything in supermarkets is covered in plastic.","zh":"超市裏幾乎所有東西都被塑膠包住。"},{"en":"Just about everything means almost everything.","zh":"幾乎所有東西意思是差不多每一樣東西。"},{"en":"In that shop, just about everything comes in a plastic bag.","zh":"在那間店，幾乎所有東西都用膠袋包着。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to emphasise that something is very widespread.","zh":"人們用這個片語強調某事非常普遍。"},{"en":"It is informal and slightly stronger than “many things.”","zh":"它較口語，比「很多東西」語氣稍強。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be covered in plastic","meaning":"被塑膠包住","examples":[{"en":"Most supermarket products are still covered in plastic.","zh":"大多數超市產品仍然被塑膠包住。"},{"en":"Be covered in plastic means have plastic wrapping or packaging around something.","zh":"被塑膠包住意思是某物外面有塑膠包裝。"},{"en":"Many vegetables are covered in plastic even when they do not need it.","zh":"許多蔬菜即使不需要，也被塑膠包住。"},{"en":"Products covered in plastic create more waste after purchase.","zh":"被塑膠包住的產品在購買後會製造更多垃圾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common packaging problem.","zh":"這個片語描述常見包裝問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"do something about","meaning":"對……採取行動","examples":[{"en":"The government needs to do something about unnecessary packaging.","zh":"政府需要對不必要的包裝採取行動。"},{"en":"Do something about a problem means take action to improve or solve it.","zh":"對問題採取行動意思是採取措施改善或解決它。"},{"en":"The school should do something about the amount of food wasted at lunch.","zh":"學校應該對午餐浪費的食物量採取行動。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they think a problem should not be ignored.","zh":"當人們認為問題不應被忽視時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It calls for action rather than just discussion.","zh":"它要求行動，而不只是討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"It’s got to change","meaning":"這一定要改變","examples":[{"en":"Marie says unnecessary packaging has got to change.","zh":"Marie 說不必要的包裝一定要改變。"},{"en":"It’s got to change means it must change because the current situation is not acceptable.","zh":"這一定要改變意思是目前情況不能接受，所以必須改變。"},{"en":"The amount of plastic in shops has got to change.","zh":"商店中的塑膠數量一定要改變。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they feel strongly that action is needed.","zh":"當人們強烈認為需要行動時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It sounds firm and urgent.","zh":"它聽起來堅定而緊迫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"gluten-free food","meaning":"無麩質食品","examples":[{"en":"Colin asks whether there will be more interest in gluten-free food.","zh":"Colin 問人們是否會對無麩質食品更感興趣。"},{"en":"Gluten-free food is food that does not contain gluten, a protein found in wheat and some grains.","zh":"無麩質食品是不含麩質的食物；麩質是小麥和某些穀物中的蛋白質。"},{"en":"People with certain health conditions may need gluten-free food.","zh":"有某些健康狀況的人可能需要無麩質食品。"},{"en":"Gluten-free food can include bread, pasta, and cakes made with alternative flours.","zh":"無麩質食品可以包括用替代麵粉製成的麵包、意粉和蛋糕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes food made for people avoiding gluten.","zh":"這個片語描述為避免麩質的人製作的食品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lactose-free food","meaning":"無乳糖食品","examples":[{"en":"Colin asks whether there will be more interest in lactose-free food.","zh":"Colin 問人們是否會對無乳糖食品更感興趣。"},{"en":"Lactose-free food is food made without lactose, the natural sugar found in milk.","zh":"無乳糖食品是不含乳糖的食品；乳糖是牛奶中的天然糖分。"},{"en":"People who cannot digest milk well may choose lactose-free food.","zh":"不能很好消化牛奶的人可能會選擇無乳糖食品。"},{"en":"Lactose-free milk can help people enjoy dairy-style products without discomfort.","zh":"無乳糖牛奶可以幫助人享受類似乳製品，而不感到不適。"},{"en":"The phrase describes food for people avoiding lactose.","zh":"這個片語描述為避免乳糖的人而設的食品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"allergies","meaning":"過敏","examples":[{"en":"Gluten-free and lactose-free foods are useful for people with allergies.","zh":"無麩質和無乳糖食品對有過敏的人有用。"},{"en":"Allergies are health reactions caused by the body responding badly to certain foods or substances.","zh":"過敏是身體對某些食物或物質產生不良反應的健康狀況。"},{"en":"Nut allergies can be serious, so food labels must be clear.","zh":"堅果過敏可能很嚴重，所以食品標籤必須清楚。"},{"en":"People with allergies need to know exactly what is in their food.","zh":"有過敏的人需要確切知道食物裏有甚麼。"},{"en":"The word is often used when discussing special diets and safety.","zh":"這個詞常用於討論特殊飲食和安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"food intolerances","meaning":"食物不耐受","examples":[{"en":"Some people buy special foods because of food intolerances.","zh":"有些人因食物不耐受而購買特殊食品。"},{"en":"Food intolerances are problems digesting or reacting to certain foods, though they are not always allergies.","zh":"食物不耐受是指消化或身體反應某些食物時出現問題，但不一定是過敏。"},{"en":"Someone with lactose intolerance may feel sick after drinking normal milk.","zh":"有乳糖不耐受的人喝普通牛奶後可能會不舒服。"},{"en":"Food intolerances can affect what people buy and eat every day.","zh":"食物不耐受可以影響人們每天購買和進食的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase explains one reason for special food products.","zh":"這個片語解釋特殊食品產品出現的一個原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"that type of food","meaning":"那類食品","examples":[{"en":"Many people have been buying that type of food for years.","zh":"許多人已經購買那類食品很多年。"},{"en":"That type of food means that kind or category of food already mentioned.","zh":"那類食品意思是剛才提到的那種或那一類食物。"},{"en":"Gluten-free bread and lactose-free milk are examples of that type of food.","zh":"無麩質麵包和無乳糖牛奶都是那類食品的例子。"},{"en":"People may buy that type of food for health, comfort, or personal choice.","zh":"人們可能因健康、舒適或個人選擇而購買那類食品。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to a food category in the discussion.","zh":"這個片語指回討論中的某類食品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"for years now","meaning":"已經很多年","examples":[{"en":"Lots of people have been buying that food for years now.","zh":"許多人已經購買那類食品很多年。"},{"en":"For years now means for many years up to the present.","zh":"已經很多年意思是從很多年前一直到現在。"},{"en":"People have been using reusable bags for years now.","zh":"人們已經使用可重用袋很多年。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something is not new anymore.","zh":"這個片語暗示某事已經不新鮮。"},{"en":"It connects past behaviour with the present.","zh":"它把過去行為與現在連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be diagnosed with","meaning":"被診斷出","examples":[{"en":"Some people buy allergy foods even if they have not been diagnosed with an allergy.","zh":"有些人即使沒有被診斷出過敏，也會購買過敏食品。"},{"en":"Be diagnosed with a condition means be officially told by a medical professional that you have it.","zh":"被診斷出某種病症意思是由醫療專業人士正式告知你患有該病症。"},{"en":"She was diagnosed with a food allergy after several tests.","zh":"經過幾次測試後，她被診斷出食物過敏。"},{"en":"People should not assume they have a condition without proper diagnosis.","zh":"人們不應在沒有正式診斷下假設自己有某種病症。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in medical and health contexts.","zh":"這個片語用於醫療和健康語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"branded products","meaning":"品牌產品","examples":[{"en":"Marie has noticed more branded products related to celebrity chefs.","zh":"Marie 注意到更多與名廚有關的品牌產品。"},{"en":"Branded products are products sold under a particular name, label, or company identity.","zh":"品牌產品是以特定名稱、標籤或公司身份銷售的產品。"},{"en":"Supermarkets sell branded products as well as cheaper own-label products.","zh":"超市售賣品牌產品，也售賣較便宜的自家品牌產品。"},{"en":"A famous brand can make customers trust a product more quickly.","zh":"著名品牌可以令顧客更快信任產品。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on products identified by a brand name.","zh":"這個片語集中於以品牌名稱識別的產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"related to","meaning":"與……相關","examples":[{"en":"Some branded products are related to celebrity chefs.","zh":"有些品牌產品與名廚相關。"},{"en":"Related to means connected with or linked to something.","zh":"與某事相關意思是與某事有聯繫或關係。"},{"en":"This sauce is related to a famous cooking programme.","zh":"這款醬料與一個著名烹飪節目相關。"},{"en":"Products related to a celebrity chef may use the chef’s name or image.","zh":"與名廚相關的產品可能使用該廚師的名字或形象。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a connection between two things.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩件事之間的關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"celebrity chefs","meaning":"名人廚師；名廚","examples":[{"en":"Some products are sold with the names of celebrity chefs.","zh":"有些產品以名廚的名字銷售。"},{"en":"Celebrity chefs are famous cooks who are known through television, books, or social media.","zh":"名人廚師或名廚是透過電視、書籍或社交媒體為人熟知的著名廚師。"},{"en":"Celebrity chefs may sell sauces, spice mixes, or frozen meals.","zh":"名廚可能售賣醬料、混合香料或急凍食品。"},{"en":"Customers may buy products by celebrity chefs because they trust their cooking style.","zh":"顧客可能因信任名廚的烹飪風格而購買其產品。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to chefs who are public figures.","zh":"這個片語指身為公眾人物的廚師。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"watch someone cooking","meaning":"看某人下廚","examples":[{"en":"People watch celebrity chefs cooking on TV.","zh":"人們在電視上看名廚下廚。"},{"en":"Watch someone cooking means see a person prepare food.","zh":"看某人下廚意思是觀看一個人準備食物。"},{"en":"I watched my grandmother cooking soup and learned her method.","zh":"我看祖母下廚煮湯，學會了她的方法。"},{"en":"Watching someone cooking can help learners copy techniques.","zh":"看某人下廚可以幫助學習者模仿技巧。"},{"en":"The phrase describes observing a person while they cook.","zh":"這個片語描述觀察某人烹飪的過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"spice mixes","meaning":"混合香料","examples":[{"en":"People buy spice mixes with a chef’s name on them.","zh":"人們購買印有廚師名字的混合香料。"},{"en":"Spice mixes are blends of different spices used to flavour food.","zh":"混合香料是由不同香料混合而成，用來為食物調味。"},{"en":"A curry spice mix may contain cumin, turmeric, and chilli.","zh":"咖喱混合香料可能含有孜然、薑黃和辣椒。"},{"en":"Ready-made spice mixes make cooking quicker, but quality can vary.","zh":"現成混合香料令煮食更快，但質素可能不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes prepared seasoning blends.","zh":"這個片語描述預先調配好的調味香料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"frozen foods","meaning":"急凍食品","examples":[{"en":"Some frozen foods are sold under a celebrity chef’s name.","zh":"有些急凍食品以名廚名字銷售。"},{"en":"Frozen foods are foods kept very cold so they last longer.","zh":"急凍食品是被保持在很低溫度下以延長保存期的食物。"},{"en":"Frozen foods can include vegetables, pizzas, meals, and desserts.","zh":"急凍食品可以包括蔬菜、薄餅、餐點和甜品。"},{"en":"People buy frozen foods because they are convenient and easy to store.","zh":"人們購買急凍食品，因為它們方便又易儲存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes food preserved by freezing.","zh":"這個片語描述透過冷凍保存的食品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"with the chef’s name on","meaning":"印有廚師名字的","examples":[{"en":"People buy products with the chef’s name on them.","zh":"人們購買印有廚師名字的產品。"},{"en":"With the chef’s name on means having the chef’s name printed on the package or label.","zh":"印有廚師名字的意思是包裝或標籤上印有該廚師的名字。"},{"en":"A sauce bottle with the chef’s name on it may seem more trustworthy to fans.","zh":"印有廚師名字的醬料瓶可能令粉絲覺得更可信。"},{"en":"Products with a famous name can attract attention quickly.","zh":"印有名人名字的產品可以迅速吸引注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes branding on food packaging.","zh":"這個片語描述食品包裝上的品牌標示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ready-made spice mix","meaning":"現成混合香料","examples":[{"en":"Colin bought a ready-made spice mix for chicken.","zh":"Colin 買了一包雞肉用的現成混合香料。"},{"en":"A ready-made spice mix is a prepared blend of spices that can be used immediately.","zh":"現成混合香料是已預先調配、可以立即使用的香料混合物。"},{"en":"A ready-made spice mix saves time because the spices are already measured and mixed.","zh":"現成混合香料節省時間，因為香料已經量好並混合。"},{"en":"Some ready-made spice mixes taste strong, while others are disappointing.","zh":"有些現成混合香料味道濃，有些則令人失望。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a convenient cooking product.","zh":"這個片語描述方便的烹飪產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be supposed to be used by","meaning":"據說由……使用","examples":[{"en":"The spice mix was supposed to be used by a chef on television.","zh":"據說這款混合香料由電視上的一位廚師使用。"},{"en":"Be supposed to be used by someone means people are told or led to believe that the person uses it.","zh":"據說由某人使用，意思是人們被告知或被引導相信那人使用它。"},{"en":"This sauce is supposed to be used by a famous chef in his restaurant.","zh":"據說這款醬料由一位名廚在他的餐廳使用。"},{"en":"A product may sound better if it is supposed to be used by an expert.","zh":"如果產品據說由專家使用，它可能聽起來更好。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a claim that may need to be questioned.","zh":"這個片語暗示一個可能需要質疑的說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"taste of anything","meaning":"有任何味道","examples":[{"en":"The spice mix did not actually taste of anything.","zh":"這款混合香料其實沒有任何味道。"},{"en":"Taste of anything means have any noticeable flavour.","zh":"有任何味道意思是有明顯味道。"},{"en":"The soup looked good but did not taste of anything.","zh":"那碗湯看起來不錯，但沒有任何味道。"},{"en":"If a spice mix does not taste of anything, customers may feel cheated.","zh":"如果混合香料沒有任何味道，顧客可能覺得被騙。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to criticise food that is bland.","zh":"這個片語用來批評味道淡的食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ghost kitchens","meaning":"幽靈廚房","examples":[{"en":"Marie mentions ghost kitchens used to produce takeaway food.","zh":"Marie 提到用來製作外賣食品的幽靈廚房。"},{"en":"Ghost kitchens are kitchens that prepare food mainly for delivery and do not serve customers on site.","zh":"幽靈廚房是主要製作外送食品、但不在現場接待顧客的廚房。"},{"en":"A ghost kitchen may appear online as a restaurant brand.","zh":"幽靈廚房可能在網上以餐廳品牌出現。"},{"en":"Customers may not realise their meal came from a ghost kitchen.","zh":"顧客可能沒有意識到自己的餐點來自幽靈廚房。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a delivery-only food business model.","zh":"這個片語描述只做外送的食品商業模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"takeaway food","meaning":"外賣食品","examples":[{"en":"Ghost kitchens are used to produce takeaway food.","zh":"幽靈廚房用來製作外賣食品。"},{"en":"Takeaway food is food bought from a restaurant to eat somewhere else.","zh":"外賣食品是從餐廳購買、在其他地方食用的食物。"},{"en":"Many people order takeaway food when they are too busy to cook.","zh":"許多人太忙不能煮飯時會訂外賣食品。"},{"en":"Takeaway food can be delivered or collected by the customer.","zh":"外賣食品可以送上門，也可以由顧客自取。"},{"en":"The phrase describes food not eaten inside the restaurant.","zh":"這個片語描述不在餐廳內食用的食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have the name of","meaning":"掛着……的名字","examples":[{"en":"A ghost kitchen might have the name of a restaurant.","zh":"幽靈廚房可能掛着一間餐廳的名字。"},{"en":"Have the name of something means use that name or be labelled with it.","zh":"掛着某物的名字意思是使用那個名稱或以它作標籤。"},{"en":"A delivery brand may have the name of a well-known restaurant.","zh":"一個外送品牌可能掛着一間知名餐廳的名字。"},{"en":"If a kitchen has the name of a restaurant, customers may think the food comes from that restaurant.","zh":"如果一個廚房掛着餐廳名字，顧客可能以為食物來自那間餐廳。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how something is presented or labelled.","zh":"這個片語描述某物如何被呈現或標示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cooking facility","meaning":"烹調設施；廚房設施","examples":[{"en":"A ghost kitchen is a cooking facility for delivery meals.","zh":"幽靈廚房是用於外送餐點的烹調設施。"},{"en":"A cooking facility is a place equipped for preparing food.","zh":"烹調設施或廚房設施是配備用來準備食物的地方。"},{"en":"The school built a cooking facility for food technology lessons.","zh":"學校為食品科技課建了一個烹調設施。"},{"en":"A cooking facility for delivery meals may not have tables for customers.","zh":"用於外送餐點的廚房設施可能沒有給顧客用餐的桌子。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a practical food preparation space.","zh":"這個片語指實際準備食物的空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"just for delivery meals","meaning":"只用於外送餐點","examples":[{"en":"Ghost kitchens are just for delivery meals.","zh":"幽靈廚房只用於外送餐點。"},{"en":"Just for delivery meals means used only to prepare food that will be delivered.","zh":"只用於外送餐點意思是只用來準備會被送出的食物。"},{"en":"The kitchen has no dining area because it is just for delivery meals.","zh":"那個廚房沒有用餐區，因為它只用於外送餐點。"},{"en":"A business just for delivery meals can operate without a public restaurant space.","zh":"只做外送餐點的生意可以不用公開餐廳空間。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the limited purpose of the kitchen.","zh":"這個片語解釋廚房的有限用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the public","meaning":"一般市民","examples":[{"en":"The public do not ever go to ghost kitchens.","zh":"一般市民從來不會去幽靈廚房。"},{"en":"The public means ordinary people in general.","zh":"一般市民意思是普通大眾。"},{"en":"The public can order food from the brand but cannot eat inside the kitchen.","zh":"一般市民可以向該品牌訂餐，但不能在廚房內用餐。"},{"en":"If the public never visits a place, they may know little about how it works.","zh":"如果一般市民從不參觀某個地方，他們可能很少知道它如何運作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to general consumers or citizens.","zh":"這個片語指一般消費者或市民。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be aware of that","meaning":"知道那件事","examples":[{"en":"People are not aware of how ghost kitchens operate.","zh":"人們不知道幽靈廚房如何運作。"},{"en":"Be aware of that means know or understand that fact.","zh":"知道那件事意思是知道或理解那個事實。"},{"en":"Many customers are not aware of that when they order food online.","zh":"許多顧客在網上訂餐時不知道那件事。"},{"en":"If people are aware of how a system works, they can make better choices.","zh":"如果人們知道一個系統如何運作，就能作出更好選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase points to knowledge of a specific fact.","zh":"這個片語指對特定事實的認識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be kept very quiet","meaning":"保持低調；不公開","examples":[{"en":"The use of ghost kitchens is kept very quiet.","zh":"幽靈廚房的使用保持低調。"},{"en":"Be kept very quiet means not be openly discussed or publicised.","zh":"保持低調或不公開意思是不公開討論或宣傳。"},{"en":"The company kept the recipe change very quiet.","zh":"公司對食譜改動保持低調。"},{"en":"If something is kept very quiet, customers may not realise it is happening.","zh":"如果某事保持低調，顧客可能不會意識到它正在發生。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests secrecy or low publicity.","zh":"這個片語暗示保密或低調處理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"realise that","meaning":"意識到","examples":[{"en":"People do not realise that the food is not from the restaurant.","zh":"人們沒有意識到食物並不是來自那間餐廳。"},{"en":"Realise that means become aware or understand that something is true.","zh":"意識到意思是察覺或理解某事是真的。"},{"en":"Customers may not realise that two brands use the same kitchen.","zh":"顧客可能沒有意識到兩個品牌使用同一個廚房。"},{"en":"People often realise a fact only after someone explains it clearly.","zh":"人們常在有人清楚解釋後才意識到某個事實。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces new understanding.","zh":"這個片語引出新的理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"more and more people","meaning":"越來越多人","examples":[{"en":"More and more people are using different mushrooms for health reasons.","zh":"越來越多人因健康原因使用不同蘑菇。"},{"en":"More and more people means an increasing number of people.","zh":"越來越多人意思是人數正在增加。"},{"en":"More and more people are choosing plant-based meals.","zh":"越來越多人選擇植物性餐點。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a trend is growing.","zh":"這個片語顯示趨勢正在增長。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing changes in public behaviour.","zh":"它在討論公眾行為變化時很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"all sorts of different","meaning":"各種不同的","examples":[{"en":"People are using all sorts of different mushrooms.","zh":"人們使用各種不同的蘑菇。"},{"en":"All sorts of different means many different kinds of something.","zh":"各種不同的意思是許多不同種類的某物。"},{"en":"The shop sells all sorts of different teas.","zh":"那間店售賣各種不同的茶。"},{"en":"Using all sorts of different ingredients can be interesting but also confusing.","zh":"使用各種不同的食材可以很有趣，但也可能令人混亂。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises variety.","zh":"這個片語強調多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"treat health concerns","meaning":"處理健康問題","examples":[{"en":"Some people use mushrooms to treat health concerns.","zh":"有些人使用蘑菇來處理健康問題。"},{"en":"Treat health concerns means try to deal with health problems or worries.","zh":"處理健康問題意思是嘗試應對健康問題或憂慮。"},{"en":"Some people drink herbal tea to treat minor health concerns.","zh":"有些人喝草本茶來處理輕微健康問題。"},{"en":"Treating health concerns without proper advice can be risky.","zh":"沒有適當建議就處理健康問題可能有風險。"},{"en":"The phrase is about attempting to improve health issues.","zh":"這個片語是關於嘗試改善健康問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"heart problems","meaning":"心臟問題","examples":[{"en":"Some people use mushrooms for heart problems.","zh":"有些人為心臟問題使用蘑菇。"},{"en":"Heart problems are health conditions that affect the heart.","zh":"心臟問題是影響心臟的健康狀況。"},{"en":"People with heart problems should seek medical advice before trying unusual treatments.","zh":"有心臟問題的人在嘗試不尋常療法前應尋求醫療建議。"},{"en":"Heart problems can be serious and should not be treated casually.","zh":"心臟問題可能很嚴重，不應隨便處理。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to health issues involving the heart.","zh":"這個片語指涉及心臟的健康問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"take a big risk","meaning":"冒很大風險","examples":[{"en":"Marie thinks people might be taking a big risk.","zh":"Marie 認為人們可能正在冒很大風險。"},{"en":"Take a big risk means do something that could lead to serious harm or loss.","zh":"冒很大風險意思是做可能導致嚴重傷害或損失的事情。"},{"en":"Eating unknown mushrooms is taking a big risk.","zh":"食用不認識的蘑菇是在冒很大風險。"},{"en":"People take a big risk when they trust health claims without evidence.","zh":"人們在沒有證據下相信健康聲稱時，就是冒很大風險。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that an action may be dangerous.","zh":"這個片語提醒某個行動可能危險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"varieties","meaning":"品種","examples":[{"en":"It is hard to know which mushroom varieties are safe to eat.","zh":"很難知道哪些蘑菇品種可安全食用。"},{"en":"Varieties are different types of the same general thing.","zh":"品種是同一大類東西中的不同種類。"},{"en":"There are many varieties of apples, mushrooms, and rice.","zh":"蘋果、蘑菇和米都有許多品種。"},{"en":"Some mushroom varieties are safe, while others may be poisonous.","zh":"有些蘑菇品種安全，有些則可能有毒。"},{"en":"The word helps compare different kinds within one group.","zh":"這個詞幫助比較同一類別中的不同種類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"safe to eat","meaning":"可安全食用","examples":[{"en":"It is hard to know which mushrooms are safe to eat.","zh":"很難知道哪些蘑菇可安全食用。"},{"en":"Safe to eat means not harmful when eaten.","zh":"可安全食用意思是吃下去不會有害。"},{"en":"Food that smells bad may not be safe to eat.","zh":"聞起來不好的食物可能不可安全食用。"},{"en":"Mushrooms should only be eaten if you are sure they are safe to eat.","zh":"只有在確定蘑菇可安全食用時才應進食。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when judging food safety.","zh":"這個片語用於判斷食品安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"find most satisfying","meaning":"覺得最令人滿意","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which things Colin found most satisfying.","zh":"題目問 Colin 覺得哪些事情最令人滿意。"},{"en":"Find something most satisfying means feel that it gave the greatest sense of pleasure or achievement.","zh":"覺得某事最令人滿意，意思是感到它帶來最大的愉快或成就感。"},{"en":"Colin found the creative design part most satisfying.","zh":"Colin 覺得創意設計部分最令人滿意。"},{"en":"People find work satisfying when it produces a result they are proud of.","zh":"當工作產生令人自豪的結果時，人們會覺得它令人滿意。"},{"en":"The phrase asks about the part someone enjoyed most.","zh":"這個片語詢問某人最享受哪一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"bread reuse project","meaning":"麵包再利用專題","examples":[{"en":"Colin found several aspects of his bread reuse project satisfying.","zh":"Colin 覺得他的麵包再利用專題有幾方面令人滿意。"},{"en":"A bread reuse project is a project that finds ways to use old or unwanted bread again.","zh":"麵包再利用專題是尋找方法再次使用舊麵包或不需要麵包的專題。"},{"en":"A bread reuse project may turn stale bread into biscuits or breadcrumbs.","zh":"麵包再利用專題可能把變乾的麵包變成餅乾或麵包糠。"},{"en":"Such a project can reduce waste and create new food products.","zh":"這類專題可以減少浪費並創造新食品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes Colin’s specific food waste project.","zh":"這個片語描述 Colin 的特定食物浪費專題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"receive support from","meaning":"得到……支持","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions receiving support from local restaurants.","zh":"選項提到得到本地餐廳支持。"},{"en":"Receive support from someone means get help, encouragement, or backing from them.","zh":"得到某人支持意思是從他們那裏獲得幫助、鼓勵或支援。"},{"en":"The project received support from a local bakery.","zh":"這個專題得到本地麵包店支持。"},{"en":"Receiving support from restaurants could help a food idea become successful.","zh":"得到餐廳支持可以幫助食品想法成功。"},{"en":"The phrase describes help given by another person or group.","zh":"這個片語描述由另一個人或團體提供的幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"local restaurants","meaning":"本地餐廳","examples":[{"en":"Colin hopes local restaurants will be interested in his biscuits.","zh":"Colin 希望本地餐廳會對他的餅乾感興趣。"},{"en":"Local restaurants are restaurants in the nearby area or community.","zh":"本地餐廳是附近地區或社區中的餐廳。"},{"en":"Local restaurants may support projects that use local or recycled ingredients.","zh":"本地餐廳可能支持使用本地或再利用食材的項目。"},{"en":"Working with local restaurants can help students test a food product with real customers.","zh":"與本地餐廳合作可以幫助學生用真實顧客測試食品。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to nearby eating places.","zh":"這個片語指附近的食肆。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"prevent waste","meaning":"防止浪費","examples":[{"en":"Colin wanted to find a good way to prevent waste.","zh":"Colin 想找一個好方法防止浪費。"},{"en":"Prevent waste means stop useful materials or food from being thrown away unnecessarily.","zh":"防止浪費意思是阻止有用材料或食物被不必要地丟掉。"},{"en":"Planning meals carefully can prevent waste at home.","zh":"仔細計劃膳食可以在家中防止浪費。"},{"en":"Reusing stale bread is one way to prevent waste.","zh":"再利用變乾的麵包是防止浪費的一種方法。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on stopping waste before it happens.","zh":"這個片語集中於在浪費發生前阻止它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"overcome problems","meaning":"克服問題","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions overcoming problems in the process.","zh":"選項提到在過程中克服問題。"},{"en":"Overcome problems means successfully deal with difficulties.","zh":"克服問題意思是成功處理困難。"},{"en":"The team overcame problems with the recipe by testing it several times.","zh":"團隊透過多次測試食譜克服問題。"},{"en":"Overcoming problems can make a project more satisfying.","zh":"克服問題可以令專題更令人滿意。"},{"en":"The phrase shows progress despite difficulties.","zh":"這個片語顯示雖有困難仍取得進展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"basic process","meaning":"基本流程","examples":[{"en":"The basic process for reusing bread was straightforward.","zh":"再利用麵包的基本流程很簡單直接。"},{"en":"Basic process means the simple main steps of a method.","zh":"基本流程意思是一種方法的簡單主要步驟。"},{"en":"The basic process was to soften the bread, make a paste, and shape it again.","zh":"基本流程是把麵包軟化、做成糊狀物，再重新塑形。"},{"en":"A clear basic process helps other people repeat the experiment.","zh":"清晰的基本流程幫助其他人重複實驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the core method without extra details.","zh":"這個片語描述沒有額外細節的核心方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"experiment with designs and colours","meaning":"嘗試設計和顏色","examples":[{"en":"Colin enjoyed experimenting with designs and colours.","zh":"Colin 喜歡嘗試設計和顏色。"},{"en":"Experiment with designs and colours means try different visual styles and colour choices.","zh":"嘗試設計和顏色意思是測試不同視覺風格和顏色選擇。"},{"en":"The students experimented with designs and colours for their food packaging.","zh":"學生為食品包裝嘗試設計和顏色。"},{"en":"Experimenting with colours can make a product look more attractive.","zh":"嘗試顏色可以令產品看起來更吸引。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creative testing.","zh":"這個片語描述創意測試。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"apply 3-D printing","meaning":"應用 3D 打印","examples":[{"en":"Colin knew how to apply 3-D printing to food.","zh":"Colin 知道如何把 3D 打印應用於食物。"},{"en":"Apply 3-D printing means use 3-D printing technology for a particular purpose.","zh":"應用 3D 打印意思是把 3D 打印技術用於特定用途。"},{"en":"Designers can apply 3-D printing to make custom biscuit shapes.","zh":"設計師可以應用 3D 打印製作自訂餅乾形狀。"},{"en":"Applying 3-D printing to food requires the mixture to be the right texture.","zh":"把 3D 打印應用於食物，需要混合物有合適質感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using technology in a practical way.","zh":"這個片語描述以實際方式使用科技。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"agree that","meaning":"同意……","examples":[{"en":"The students agree that the sensors could be developed in future.","zh":"學生同意這些感應器將來可以被開發。"},{"en":"Agree that means share the same opinion about a statement.","zh":"同意某事意思是對某個說法有相同看法。"},{"en":"The group agreed that food labels should be clearer.","zh":"小組同意食品標籤應更清晰。"},{"en":"People agree that something is useful when they accept the same idea.","zh":"當人們接受同一想法時，就是同意某事有用。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a shared view.","zh":"這個片語引出共同觀點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be developed in future","meaning":"將來被開發","examples":[{"en":"The sensors could be developed in future for other uses.","zh":"這些感應器將來可以被開發作其他用途。"},{"en":"Be developed in future means be improved or expanded later.","zh":"將來被開發意思是之後被改良或擴展。"},{"en":"This label technology may be developed in future for medicines.","zh":"這種標籤技術將來可能被開發用於藥物。"},{"en":"An early idea can be developed in future into a useful product.","zh":"一個早期想法將來可以被開發成有用產品。"},{"en":"The phrase points to possible later improvement.","zh":"這個片語指向日後可能的改進。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"medical products","meaning":"醫療產品","examples":[{"en":"The sensors might be useful for medical products.","zh":"這些感應器可能對醫療產品有用。"},{"en":"Medical products are items used for health care, treatment, or medicine storage.","zh":"醫療產品是用於醫療護理、治療或藥物儲存的物品。"},{"en":"Medical products must be stored safely so they remain effective.","zh":"醫療產品必須安全儲存，以保持有效。"},{"en":"Sensors on medical products could warn users if conditions are unsafe.","zh":"醫療產品上的感應器可以在環境不安全時提醒使用者。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to products used in medical settings.","zh":"這個片語指醫療環境中使用的產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"no longer fit to eat","meaning":"不再適合食用","examples":[{"en":"The label can show that food is no longer fit to eat.","zh":"標籤可以顯示食物不再適合食用。"},{"en":"No longer fit to eat means not safe or suitable to eat anymore.","zh":"不再適合食用意思是已不再安全或不適合吃。"},{"en":"If milk smells sour, it may be no longer fit to eat or drink.","zh":"如果牛奶聞起來酸，它可能不再適合食用或飲用。"},{"en":"A warning label can prevent people from eating food that is no longer fit to eat.","zh":"警告標籤可以防止人們吃下不再適合食用的食物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes food that has become unsafe.","zh":"這個片語描述已變得不安全的食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"drinks as well as foods","meaning":"飲品以及食品","examples":[{"en":"The technology could be used with drinks as well as foods.","zh":"這項技術可以用於飲品以及食品。"},{"en":"Drinks as well as foods means both drinks and solid or other food products.","zh":"飲品以及食品意思是飲品和固體或其他食品都包括在內。"},{"en":"The label could work on juice bottles as well as food boxes.","zh":"這個標籤可以用於果汁瓶以及食品盒。"},{"en":"Using the technology for drinks as well as foods would make it more useful.","zh":"把技術用於飲品以及食品會令它更有用。"},{"en":"The phrase expands the range of possible uses.","zh":"這個片語擴大可能用途的範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"applications for blind people","meaning":"給失明人士使用的應用","examples":[{"en":"The sensors could provide applications for blind people.","zh":"這些感應器可以提供給失明人士使用的應用。"},{"en":"Applications for blind people are practical uses designed to help people who cannot see.","zh":"給失明人士使用的應用，是指為幫助不能看見的人而設的實際用途。"},{"en":"Touch-based labels have applications for blind people because they can be read by feeling.","zh":"觸覺標籤對失明人士有應用價值，因為可以用觸摸閱讀。"},{"en":"Technology with useful applications for blind people can improve independence.","zh":"對失明人士有用的科技可以提升獨立性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes helpful uses for a specific group.","zh":"這個片語描述為特定群體提供幫助的用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"indicate the weight of","meaning":"顯示……的重量","examples":[{"en":"The label might indicate the weight of certain foods.","zh":"標籤可能顯示某些食品的重量。"},{"en":"Indicate the weight of something means show how heavy it is.","zh":"顯示某物的重量意思是顯示它有多重。"},{"en":"A smart label could indicate the weight of a packet of meat.","zh":"智能標籤可以顯示一包肉的重量。"},{"en":"Showing weight helps customers compare prices and portion sizes.","zh":"顯示重量幫助顧客比較價格和份量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving weight information clearly.","zh":"這個片語描述清楚提供重量資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"certain foods","meaning":"某些食品","examples":[{"en":"The sensors might indicate the weight of certain foods.","zh":"感應器可能顯示某些食品的重量。"},{"en":"Certain foods means particular kinds of food, not all foods.","zh":"某些食品意思是特定種類的食物，而不是所有食物。"},{"en":"The label may work better for certain foods, such as meat or cheese.","zh":"標籤可能較適用於某些食品，例如肉類或芝士。"},{"en":"Some technologies are useful for certain foods but not for every product.","zh":"有些科技對某些食品有用，但未必適用於每種產品。"},{"en":"The phrase limits the meaning to specific food types.","zh":"這個片語把意思限制在特定食品種類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"opinion about","meaning":"對……的看法","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the students’ opinion about food trends.","zh":"題目詢問學生對食品趨勢的看法。"},{"en":"Opinion about something means what someone thinks or believes about it.","zh":"對某事的看法意思是某人對它的想法或信念。"},{"en":"The teacher asked for our opinion about reducing plastic packaging.","zh":"老師問我們對減少塑膠包裝的看法。"},{"en":"Different people may have different opinions about the same food trend.","zh":"不同人可能對同一食品趨勢有不同看法。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a personal view.","zh":"這個片語引出個人觀點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"only relevant to","meaning":"只與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The option says the trend is only relevant to young people.","zh":"選項說這個趨勢只與年輕人有關。"},{"en":"Only relevant to someone means important or connected only to that group.","zh":"只與某人有關意思是只對那個群體重要或有連繫。"},{"en":"This app is not only relevant to young people; older people can use it too.","zh":"這個應用程式不只與年輕人有關；長者也可以使用。"},{"en":"A trend may seem only relevant to one group but later affect everyone.","zh":"一個趨勢可能看似只與某群體有關，但後來影響所有人。"},{"en":"The phrase limits who something matters to.","zh":"這個片語限制某事與誰有關。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"young people","meaning":"年輕人","examples":[{"en":"The opinion suggests one trend may only be relevant to young people.","zh":"這個看法暗示一個趨勢可能只與年輕人有關。"},{"en":"Young people are children, teenagers, or adults in the earlier stage of life.","zh":"年輕人是指兒童、青少年或較年輕的成年人。"},{"en":"Young people often notice new food trends on social media.","zh":"年輕人常在社交媒體上注意到新的食品趨勢。"},{"en":"Food businesses may target young people because they try new products quickly.","zh":"食品企業可能以年輕人為目標，因為他們較快嘗試新產品。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a younger age group.","zh":"這個片語指較年輕的年齡群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have disappointing results","meaning":"結果令人失望","examples":[{"en":"A branded product may have disappointing results.","zh":"品牌產品可能有令人失望的結果。"},{"en":"Have disappointing results means produce outcomes that are worse than expected.","zh":"結果令人失望意思是產生比預期差的結果。"},{"en":"The celebrity chef’s spice mix had disappointing results because it tasted bland.","zh":"那款名廚混合香料結果令人失望，因為味道很淡。"},{"en":"People feel unhappy when an expensive product has disappointing results.","zh":"當昂貴產品結果令人失望時，人們會感到不滿。"},{"en":"The phrase describes poor performance compared with expectations.","zh":"這個片語描述表現低於期望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"already seem to be widespread","meaning":"似乎已經很普遍","examples":[{"en":"Some food trends already seem to be widespread.","zh":"有些食品趨勢似乎已經很普遍。"},{"en":"Already seem to be widespread means appear to be common in many places now.","zh":"似乎已經很普遍意思是現在看來在許多地方都常見。"},{"en":"Plant-based milk already seems to be widespread in many cafés.","zh":"植物奶在許多咖啡店似乎已經很普遍。"},{"en":"A trend that is widespread may no longer feel new.","zh":"已經很普遍的趨勢可能不再感覺新鮮。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that has become common.","zh":"這個片語描述已變得常見的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"retailers","meaning":"零售商","examples":[{"en":"Retailers should do more to encourage the use of local products.","zh":"零售商應做更多來鼓勵使用本地產品。"},{"en":"Retailers are businesses that sell goods directly to customers.","zh":"零售商是直接向顧客銷售商品的企業。"},{"en":"Supermarkets, shops, and online stores are retailers.","zh":"超市、商店和網店都是零售商。"},{"en":"Retailers can influence what consumers buy by changing displays and prices.","zh":"零售商可以透過改變陳列和價格影響消費者購買甚麼。"},{"en":"The word refers to sellers, not manufacturers.","zh":"這個詞指銷售者，不是製造商。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"encourage this","meaning":"鼓勵這件事","examples":[{"en":"Retailers should do more to encourage this trend.","zh":"零售商應做更多來鼓勵這個趨勢。"},{"en":"Encourage this means support or promote the thing just mentioned.","zh":"鼓勵這件事意思是支持或推動剛才提到的事情。"},{"en":"If customers want local food, shops should encourage this by giving it better shelf space.","zh":"如果顧客想買本地食品，商店應透過給予更好貨架位置來鼓勵這件事。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to refer back to a positive idea.","zh":"人們用這個片語指回一個正面想法。"},{"en":"It means help the trend grow.","zh":"它意思是幫助趨勢發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"financial support","meaning":"財政支持","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests more financial support is needed.","zh":"選項表示需要更多財政支持。"},{"en":"Financial support means money or funding given to help a person, project, or business.","zh":"財政支持是給予個人、項目或企業的金錢或資金幫助。"},{"en":"Small farms may need financial support to sell more local products.","zh":"小農場可能需要財政支持來銷售更多本地產品。"},{"en":"Financial support can help new food ideas become real products.","zh":"財政支持可以幫助新的食品想法變成真實產品。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on help in the form of money.","zh":"這個片語集中於金錢形式的幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"know little about","meaning":"對……所知甚少","examples":[{"en":"Most people know little about ghost kitchens.","zh":"大多數人對幽靈廚房所知甚少。"},{"en":"Know little about something means not know much information about it.","zh":"對某事所知甚少意思是不太了解它。"},{"en":"Many customers know little about where delivery meals are prepared.","zh":"許多顧客對外送餐點在哪裏準備所知甚少。"},{"en":"People may make different choices if they know more about ghost kitchens.","zh":"如果人們更了解幽靈廚房，可能會作出不同選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limited knowledge.","zh":"這個片語描述知識有限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"stricter regulations","meaning":"更嚴格的規管","examples":[{"en":"There should be stricter regulations about unnecessary packaging.","zh":"對不必要包裝應有更嚴格的規管。"},{"en":"Stricter regulations are stronger rules set by authorities.","zh":"更嚴格的規管是由當局制定的更強規則。"},{"en":"Stricter regulations could force supermarkets to reduce plastic packaging.","zh":"更嚴格的規管可以迫使超市減少塑膠包裝。"},{"en":"When voluntary change is too slow, stricter regulations may be needed.","zh":"當自願改變太慢時，可能需要更嚴格的規管。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to tougher official control.","zh":"這個片語指更嚴厲的官方控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"could be dangerous","meaning":"可能有危險","examples":[{"en":"Using mushrooms for health concerns could be dangerous.","zh":"使用蘑菇處理健康問題可能有危險。"},{"en":"Could be dangerous means might cause harm or risk.","zh":"可能有危險意思是可能造成傷害或風險。"},{"en":"Eating unknown mushrooms could be dangerous.","zh":"食用不認識的蘑菇可能有危險。"},{"en":"A natural product could be dangerous if people use it without expert advice.","zh":"如果人們沒有專家建議就使用天然產品，它可能有危險。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that something may not be safe.","zh":"這個片語提醒某事可能不安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":14}],"ielts/listening/Practice 5/task-4":[{"front":"for my presentation today","meaning":"在我今天的簡報中","examples":[{"en":"For my presentation today, I’m going to talk about the Céide Fields.","zh":"在我今天的簡報中，我會介紹 Céide Fields。"},{"en":"For my presentation today introduces the topic a speaker will discuss in that presentation.","zh":"for my presentation today 用來介紹說話者在該簡報中會討論的主題。"},{"en":"For my presentation today, I will explain how recycling works in our school.","zh":"在我今天的簡報中，我會解釋我們學校的回收如何運作。"},{"en":"Students often use this phrase at the beginning to tell the audience what to expect.","zh":"學生常在開頭使用這個短語，告訴觀眾接下來會聽到甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for starting a formal or classroom presentation clearly.","zh":"這個短語適合用來清楚開始正式或課堂簡報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"talk about","meaning":"談論；介紹","examples":[{"en":"The speaker is going to talk about the Céide Fields.","zh":"講者將會介紹 Céide Fields。"},{"en":"To talk about something means to discuss or give information about it.","zh":"talk about something 指討論某事或提供關於某事的資料。"},{"en":"The teacher will talk about climate change in tomorrow’s lesson.","zh":"老師明天課堂會談論氣候變化。"},{"en":"A museum guide may talk about old objects and explain why they matter.","zh":"博物館導賞員可能介紹舊物件，並解釋它們為何重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when introducing a topic in speaking or writing.","zh":"這個短語常用於在說話或寫作中介紹主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the northwest of Ireland","meaning":"愛爾蘭西北部","examples":[{"en":"The Céide Fields are in the northwest of Ireland.","zh":"Céide Fields 位於愛爾蘭西北部。"},{"en":"The northwest of Ireland means the northwestern part of the country of Ireland.","zh":"the northwest of Ireland 指愛爾蘭這個國家的西北部地區。"},{"en":"Many coastal landscapes can be found in the northwest of Ireland.","zh":"愛爾蘭西北部有許多海岸景觀。"},{"en":"A traveller visiting the northwest of Ireland may see cliffs, fields, and small villages.","zh":"到愛爾蘭西北部旅行的人可能看見懸崖、田野和小村莊。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the location of a place within Ireland.","zh":"這個短語指出某地在愛爾蘭境內的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one of the largest Neolithic sites","meaning":"最大的新石器時代遺址之一","examples":[{"en":"The Céide Fields are one of the largest Neolithic sites in the world.","zh":"Céide Fields 是世界上最大的新石器時代遺址之一。"},{"en":"One of the largest Neolithic sites means among the biggest known places from the Neolithic period.","zh":"one of the largest Neolithic sites 指已知新石器時代遺址中面積最大的其中之一。"},{"en":"A place can be one of the largest Neolithic sites if it covers a huge area of ancient remains.","zh":"如果一個地方覆蓋大量古代遺跡，它可以是最大的新石器時代遺址之一。"},{"en":"Archaeologists study one of the largest Neolithic sites to understand early farming communities.","zh":"考古學家研究最大的新石器時代遺址之一，以了解早期農耕社群。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the site is important because of its size and age.","zh":"這個短語顯示該遺址因其規模和年代而重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Neolithic site","meaning":"新石器時代遺址","examples":[{"en":"The Céide Fields are an important Neolithic site.","zh":"Céide Fields 是一個重要的新石器時代遺址。"},{"en":"A Neolithic site is a place with remains from the later Stone Age, when people began farming.","zh":"Neolithic site 指有新石器時代遺跡的地方，當時人們開始農耕。"},{"en":"A Neolithic site may contain old houses, tools, fields, or burial places.","zh":"新石器時代遺址可能包含古屋、工具、田地或墓地。"},{"en":"Archaeologists dig carefully at a Neolithic site to protect ancient evidence.","zh":"考古學家在新石器時代遺址小心挖掘，以保護古代證據。"},{"en":"Studying a Neolithic site helps us understand how early farmers lived.","zh":"研究新石器時代遺址有助我們了解早期農民如何生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the world","meaning":"世界上","examples":[{"en":"The Céide Fields are one of the largest Neolithic sites in the world.","zh":"Céide Fields 是世界上最大的新石器時代遺址之一。"},{"en":"In the world means across all countries or anywhere on Earth.","zh":"in the world 指在所有國家或地球任何地方之中。"},{"en":"This museum has one of the oldest maps in the world.","zh":"這間博物館有世界上最古老的地圖之一。"},{"en":"Some of the most famous archaeological sites in the world attract millions of visitors.","zh":"世界上一些最著名的考古遺址吸引數百萬遊客。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that something is important beyond one local area.","zh":"這個短語強調某事的重要性超越本地範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"observe the work","meaning":"觀察工作","examples":[{"en":"The speaker observed the work being done by archaeologists.","zh":"講者觀察了考古學家正在進行的工作。"},{"en":"To observe the work means to watch carefully as people carry out a task.","zh":"observe the work 指仔細觀看人們執行某項任務。"},{"en":"Students observed the work of museum staff cleaning an ancient pot.","zh":"學生觀察博物館職員清潔古代陶罐的工作。"},{"en":"A trainee may observe the work before trying the task alone.","zh":"實習生可能先觀察工作，然後才獨自嘗試任務。"},{"en":"Observing the work helps people learn methods, tools, and safety rules.","zh":"觀察工作有助人學習方法、工具和安全規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"currently being done","meaning":"目前正在進行的","examples":[{"en":"The work is currently being done by a team of archaeologists.","zh":"這項工作目前正由一支考古團隊進行。"},{"en":"Currently being done means happening or being carried out now.","zh":"currently being done 指現在正在發生或執行。"},{"en":"Repairs are currently being done on the school roof.","zh":"學校屋頂目前正在進行維修。"},{"en":"Research currently being done may change what we know about the site.","zh":"目前正在進行的研究可能改變我們對該遺址的認識。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the action is in progress at the present time.","zh":"這個短語顯示行動此刻正在進行中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a team of archaeologists","meaning":"考古團隊","examples":[{"en":"A team of archaeologists is working at the site.","zh":"一支考古團隊正在該遺址工作。"},{"en":"A team of archaeologists is a group of experts who study ancient human remains and objects.","zh":"a team of archaeologists 指研究古代人類遺跡和物件的一組專家。"},{"en":"A team of archaeologists carefully recorded each stone before moving it.","zh":"考古團隊在移動每塊石頭前都仔細記錄。"},{"en":"Large sites often need a team of archaeologists because the work is slow and detailed.","zh":"大型遺址通常需要考古團隊，因為工作緩慢而細緻。"},{"en":"A team of archaeologists can include diggers, surveyors, scientists, and students.","zh":"考古團隊可以包括挖掘人員、測量員、科學家和學生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"was first discovered","meaning":"最早被發現","examples":[{"en":"The site was first discovered in the 1930s.","zh":"該遺址最早在 1930 年代被發現。"},{"en":"Was first discovered means was found for the first known time.","zh":"was first discovered 指首次被人知道或發現。"},{"en":"The ancient tomb was first discovered by farmers digging a field.","zh":"那座古墓最早由正在挖田的農民發現。"},{"en":"A place may be first discovered by local people before experts study it.","zh":"一個地方可能先由本地人發現，之後才由專家研究。"},{"en":"This phrase tells us when or how people first became aware of something.","zh":"這個短語告訴我們人們何時或如何最初知道某事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the 1930s","meaning":"在 1930 年代","examples":[{"en":"The site was first discovered in the 1930s.","zh":"該遺址最早在 1930 年代被發現。"},{"en":"In the 1930s means during the years from 1930 to 1939.","zh":"in the 1930s 指在 1930 至 1939 年期間。"},{"en":"Many black-and-white photographs from the 1930s show daily village life.","zh":"許多 1930 年代的黑白相片展示村莊日常生活。"},{"en":"In the 1930s, archaeology used fewer modern scientific tools than it does today.","zh":"在 1930 年代，考古學使用的現代科學工具比今天少。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event in a specific decade.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在特定十年中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a local teacher","meaning":"本地教師","examples":[{"en":"A local teacher called Patrick Caulfield discovered the site.","zh":"一位名叫 Patrick Caulfield 的本地教師發現了該遺址。"},{"en":"A local teacher is a teacher who lives or works in the nearby area.","zh":"local teacher 指住在或任教於附近地區的教師。"},{"en":"A local teacher noticed old stones while walking near the village.","zh":"一位本地教師在村莊附近散步時注意到古老石頭。"},{"en":"Local teachers often know the history and stories of their communities.","zh":"本地教師常熟悉自己社區的歷史和故事。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an important discovery did not always begin with famous experts.","zh":"這個短語顯示重要發現不一定由著名專家開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"digging in the bog","meaning":"在沼澤中挖掘","examples":[{"en":"Local people were digging in the bog when they found rows of stones.","zh":"本地人在沼澤中挖掘時，發現了一排排石頭。"},{"en":"Digging in the bog means cutting or digging into wet peatland soil.","zh":"digging in the bog 指在潮濕泥炭地土壤中切割或挖掘。"},{"en":"People digging in the bog may uncover old wood, stones, or preserved objects.","zh":"在沼澤中挖掘的人可能發現古木、石頭或保存下來的物件。"},{"en":"Digging in the bog can be difficult because the ground is wet and heavy.","zh":"在沼澤中挖掘可能很困難，因為地面潮濕而沉重。"},{"en":"Archaeologists must be careful when digging in the bog because remains may be fragile.","zh":"考古學家在沼澤中挖掘時必須小心，因為遺跡可能很脆弱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"constantly hitting against","meaning":"不斷碰到","examples":[{"en":"They were constantly hitting against rows of stones.","zh":"他們不斷碰到一排排石頭。"},{"en":"Constantly hitting against something means repeatedly striking or bumping into it.","zh":"constantly hitting against something 指反覆撞到或碰到某物。"},{"en":"The workers were constantly hitting against hard rock while digging.","zh":"工人在挖掘時不斷碰到硬石。"},{"en":"If a shovel keeps hitting against stones, something may be buried below.","zh":"如果鏟子不停碰到石頭，下面可能埋着東西。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the problem happened again and again.","zh":"這個短語顯示問題一次又一次發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what seemed to be","meaning":"看似是……的東西","examples":[{"en":"They hit against what seemed to be rows of stones.","zh":"他們碰到看似是一排排石頭的東西。"},{"en":"What seemed to be means what appeared to be something, though people were not yet certain.","zh":"what seemed to be 指看起來像某物，但人們尚未完全確定。"},{"en":"The students found what seemed to be an old wall under the soil.","zh":"學生在泥土下發現看似是古牆的東西。"},{"en":"The object seemed to be a tool, but experts needed to check it.","zh":"那件物件看似是一件工具，但專家需要檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing an early guess before proof.","zh":"這個短語適合用來描述證實前的初步猜測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rows of stones","meaning":"一排排石頭","examples":[{"en":"Local people kept finding rows of stones in the bog.","zh":"本地人不斷在沼澤中發現一排排石頭。"},{"en":"Rows of stones are stones arranged in long lines.","zh":"rows of stones 指排列成長線的石頭。"},{"en":"Archaeologists found rows of stones that looked like ancient field walls.","zh":"考古學家發現一排排看似古代田界牆的石頭。"},{"en":"Rows of stones can show where old boundaries once existed.","zh":"一排排石頭可以顯示舊邊界曾經在哪裡。"},{"en":"When rows of stones appear underground, they may suggest human activity.","zh":"當地下出現一排排石頭，可能暗示有人類活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"realised that","meaning":"意識到","examples":[{"en":"Patrick Caulfield realised that the stones must be walls.","zh":"Patrick Caulfield 意識到那些石頭一定是牆。"},{"en":"Realised that means understood something after thinking, noticing, or learning more.","zh":"realised that 指在思考、注意或了解更多後明白某事。"},{"en":"She realised that the old map showed a forgotten road.","zh":"她意識到那張舊地圖顯示了一條被遺忘的道路。"},{"en":"The teacher realised that students were confused by the diagram.","zh":"老師意識到學生被圖表弄糊塗了。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a moment of understanding.","zh":"這個短語顯示理解的那一刻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"thousands of years old","meaning":"有數千年歷史","examples":[{"en":"The walls must be thousands of years old.","zh":"那些牆一定有數千年歷史。"},{"en":"Thousands of years old means having existed for many thousands of years.","zh":"thousands of years old 指已存在很多千年。"},{"en":"Archaeologists found tools that were thousands of years old.","zh":"考古學家發現有數千年歷史的工具。"},{"en":"A tree can be ancient, but stone walls may be thousands of years old.","zh":"樹可以很古老，但石牆可能有數千年歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the great age of an object or place.","zh":"這個短語強調物件或地方年代非常久遠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"predate the bog","meaning":"早於沼澤形成","examples":[{"en":"The walls must predate the bog that later grew over them.","zh":"這些牆一定早於後來覆蓋它們的沼澤形成。"},{"en":"To predate the bog means to exist before the bog formed.","zh":"predate the bog 指在沼澤形成之前已存在。"},{"en":"If stones predate the bog, they were placed there before the wetland covered them.","zh":"如果石頭早於沼澤形成，它們就是在濕地覆蓋前已被放置在那裡。"},{"en":"Archaeologists can study objects that predate the bog to understand earlier landscapes.","zh":"考古學家可以研究早於沼澤形成的物件，以了解早期地貌。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain the order of events in the site’s history.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋遺址歷史中的事件先後。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"subsequently grew over","meaning":"後來覆蓋於……之上","examples":[{"en":"The bog subsequently grew over the ancient walls.","zh":"沼澤後來覆蓋於古牆之上。"},{"en":"Subsequently grew over means later spread across and covered something.","zh":"subsequently grew over 指後來擴展並覆蓋某物。"},{"en":"Grass subsequently grew over the abandoned path.","zh":"草後來覆蓋於被棄用的小路之上。"},{"en":"Sand subsequently grew over the ruins after years of wind.","zh":"多年風沙後，沙土後來覆蓋於遺跡之上。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one natural process happened after an earlier human structure existed.","zh":"這個短語顯示某自然過程在人類結構存在之後發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"write to","meaning":"寫信給","examples":[{"en":"Patrick Caulfield wrote to the National Museum in Dublin.","zh":"Patrick Caulfield 寫信給都柏林的國家博物館。"},{"en":"To write to someone means to send them a letter, email, or formal message.","zh":"write to someone 指寄信、電郵或正式訊息給某人。"},{"en":"The student wrote to the museum to ask about the old coins.","zh":"學生寫信給博物館，詢問關於古錢幣的資料。"},{"en":"Residents wrote to the council about the damaged road.","zh":"居民寫信給議會，反映道路受損問題。"},{"en":"People write to organisations when they want advice, help, or investigation.","zh":"人們想要建議、幫助或調查時，會寫信給機構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the National Museum","meaning":"國家博物館","examples":[{"en":"He wrote to the National Museum in Dublin.","zh":"他寫信給都柏林的國家博物館。"},{"en":"The National Museum is a major museum that preserves and displays important objects from a country’s history.","zh":"National Museum 指保存並展示一個國家歷史重要物件的主要博物館。"},{"en":"The National Museum may keep ancient tools, artworks, and documents.","zh":"國家博物館可能收藏古代工具、藝術品和文件。"},{"en":"Archaeologists often contact the National Museum when they find important remains.","zh":"考古學家發現重要遺跡時，常聯絡國家博物館。"},{"en":"A National Museum helps the public learn about a country’s past.","zh":"國家博物館幫助公眾認識一個國家的過去。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ask someone to investigate","meaning":"要求某人調查","examples":[{"en":"He asked the museum to investigate the site.","zh":"他要求博物館調查該遺址。"},{"en":"To ask someone to investigate means to request that they examine something carefully.","zh":"ask someone to investigate 指要求某人仔細檢查某事。"},{"en":"The villagers asked experts to investigate the strange markings.","zh":"村民要求專家調查那些奇怪痕跡。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to investigate how plants grow in different soils.","zh":"老師可能要求學生調查植物如何在不同土壤中生長。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when someone wants a careful search for facts.","zh":"當某人想要仔細查明事實時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take someone seriously","meaning":"認真看待某人的話","examples":[{"en":"No one took Patrick Caulfield seriously at first.","zh":"起初沒有人認真看待 Patrick Caulfield 的話。"},{"en":"To take someone seriously means to believe their words deserve attention or respect.","zh":"take someone seriously 指相信某人的說話值得注意或尊重。"},{"en":"The doctor took the patient seriously and ordered more tests.","zh":"醫生認真看待病人的說話，並安排更多檢查。"},{"en":"Students feel encouraged when teachers take their ideas seriously.","zh":"當老師認真看待學生的想法，學生會感到受鼓勵。"},{"en":"If experts do not take someone seriously, important information may be ignored.","zh":"如果專家不認真看待某人的話，重要資料可能被忽視。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"It wasn’t until 40 years later that","meaning":"直到 40 年後才","examples":[{"en":"It wasn’t until 40 years later that Seamus Caulfield explored the site further.","zh":"直到 40 年後，Seamus Caulfield 才進一步探索該遺址。"},{"en":"It wasn’t until 40 years later that means something did not happen until forty years had passed.","zh":"It wasn’t until 40 years later that 指某事直到四十年過去後才發生。"},{"en":"It wasn’t until ten years later that the old letter was found.","zh":"直到十年後，那封舊信才被發現。"},{"en":"This structure emphasises a long delay before an important event.","zh":"這個結構強調重要事件發生前有很長延誤。"},{"en":"It wasn’t until many years later that people understood the discovery’s value.","zh":"直到多年後，人們才明白這項發現的價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"by then","meaning":"到那時","examples":[{"en":"Seamus had become an archaeologist by then.","zh":"到那時，Seamus 已成為一名考古學家。"},{"en":"By then means by that time in the past or future.","zh":"by then 指到過去或未來的某個時間點時。"},{"en":"The museum was closed by then, so we could not enter.","zh":"到那時，博物館已經關閉，所以我們不能進入。"},{"en":"By then, the student had already finished her project.","zh":"到那時，那名學生已經完成項目。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect an action with a later point in time.","zh":"這個短語幫助把行動與較後時間點連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"explore further","meaning":"進一步探索","examples":[{"en":"Seamus Caulfield began to explore the site further.","zh":"Seamus Caulfield 開始進一步探索該遺址。"},{"en":"To explore further means to investigate more deeply or in more detail.","zh":"explore further 指更深入或更仔細地調查。"},{"en":"The class decided to explore the topic further after watching the documentary.","zh":"全班看完紀錄片後決定進一步探索該課題。"},{"en":"Archaeologists explore further when early evidence seems important.","zh":"當初步證據看來重要時，考古學家會進一步探索。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the first look was not enough.","zh":"這個短語顯示初步觀察並不足夠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"insert probes into","meaning":"把探針插入……","examples":[{"en":"He inserted iron probes into the bog.","zh":"他把鐵探針插入沼澤。"},{"en":"To insert probes into something means to push long testing tools into it.","zh":"insert probes into something 指把長形測試工具推入某物中。"},{"en":"Scientists inserted probes into the soil to measure moisture.","zh":"科學家把探針插入土壤，以測量濕度。"},{"en":"Archaeologists inserted probes into the ground to find buried stones without digging everything up.","zh":"考古學家把探針插入地面，以在不全部挖開的情況下尋找埋藏石頭。"},{"en":"This method helps people discover what is hidden below the surface.","zh":"這種方法幫助人發現表面下隱藏的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"iron probes","meaning":"鐵探針","examples":[{"en":"Iron probes were used to locate the stones beneath the bog.","zh":"鐵探針被用來找出沼澤下方的石頭。"},{"en":"Iron probes are long metal tools used to feel or locate objects underground.","zh":"iron probes 指用來感測或定位地下物件的長金屬工具。"},{"en":"Farmers used iron probes to search for hard material below the soil.","zh":"農民使用鐵探針尋找土壤下的硬物。"},{"en":"Archaeologists can use iron probes before deciding where to dig.","zh":"考古學家可以在決定挖掘位置前使用鐵探針。"},{"en":"Iron probes help map hidden remains without immediately destroying the ground.","zh":"鐵探針幫助繪製隱藏遺跡，而不必立即破壞地面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"map the formation of","meaning":"繪製……的分布","examples":[{"en":"The probes helped map the formation of the stones.","zh":"探針幫助繪製石頭的分布。"},{"en":"To map the formation of something means to record its shape, pattern, or arrangement.","zh":"map the formation of something 指記錄某物的形狀、模式或排列。"},{"en":"Archaeologists mapped the formation of the buried walls.","zh":"考古學家繪製埋藏牆壁的分布。"},{"en":"Scientists map the formation of rocks to understand how the land changed.","zh":"科學家繪製岩石的分布，以了解土地如何改變。"},{"en":"Mapping the formation of hidden objects helps researchers see the larger pattern.","zh":"繪製隱藏物件的分布，有助研究人員看見較大的模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a traditional method","meaning":"傳統方法","examples":[{"en":"The technique was a traditional method used by local people.","zh":"這項技術是本地人使用的一種傳統方法。"},{"en":"A traditional method is a way of doing something passed down through local practice or history.","zh":"traditional method 指透過本地實踐或歷史流傳下來的做法。"},{"en":"Farmers used a traditional method to find water under the ground.","zh":"農民使用傳統方法尋找地下水。"},{"en":"A traditional method may still be useful even when modern tools exist.","zh":"即使有現代工具，傳統方法仍可能有用。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that knowledge can come from ordinary local experience.","zh":"這個短語顯示知識可以來自普通本地經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"local people","meaning":"本地人","examples":[{"en":"Local people had used the method for many years.","zh":"本地人已使用這種方法多年。"},{"en":"Local people are the people who live in or belong to a particular area.","zh":"local people 指住在或屬於某個地區的人。"},{"en":"Local people often know the land better than visitors.","zh":"本地人通常比訪客更熟悉土地。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may learn useful information from local people.","zh":"考古學家可能從本地人那裡學到有用資料。"},{"en":"Respecting local people is important when studying a historical site.","zh":"研究歷史遺址時，尊重本地人很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"finding fuel buried in","meaning":"尋找埋在……的燃料","examples":[{"en":"The method was used for finding fuel buried in the bog.","zh":"這種方法用於尋找埋在沼澤中的燃料。"},{"en":"Finding fuel buried in a place means locating material underground that can be burned for heat.","zh":"finding fuel buried in a place 指找出埋在地下、可燃燒取暖的材料。"},{"en":"Local families used probes for finding fuel buried in wet ground.","zh":"本地家庭使用探針尋找埋在濕地中的燃料。"},{"en":"In some areas, peat was fuel buried in the bog and used for fires.","zh":"在一些地區，泥炭是埋在沼澤中的燃料，可用來生火。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a practical reason for using the probing method.","zh":"這個短語解釋使用探測方法的實際原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"buried in the bog","meaning":"埋在沼澤中","examples":[{"en":"Fuel had been buried in the bog for thousands of years.","zh":"燃料已埋在沼澤中數千年。"},{"en":"Buried in the bog means covered and hidden under wet peatland.","zh":"buried in the bog 指被濕泥炭地覆蓋並隱藏起來。"},{"en":"Archaeologists found wooden tools buried in the bog.","zh":"考古學家發現埋在沼澤中的木製工具。"},{"en":"Objects buried in the bog may survive because the wet conditions slow decay.","zh":"埋在沼澤中的物件可能保存下來，因為潮濕環境減慢腐爛。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is hidden below the bog surface.","zh":"這個短語顯示某物隱藏在沼澤表面之下。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"carbon dating","meaning":"碳定年法","examples":[{"en":"Carbon dating proved that the site was over 5,000 years old.","zh":"碳定年法證明該遺址有 5,000 多年歷史。"},{"en":"Carbon dating is a scientific method used to estimate the age of old organic material.","zh":"carbon dating 是用來估算古老有機材料年代的科學方法。"},{"en":"Archaeologists use carbon dating on wood, bone, or charcoal from ancient sites.","zh":"考古學家會對古代遺址中的木材、骨頭或木炭使用碳定年法。"},{"en":"Carbon dating can help prove whether an object is hundreds or thousands of years old.","zh":"碳定年法可以幫助證明物件有數百年還是數千年歷史。"},{"en":"This method gives researchers evidence instead of guesses about age.","zh":"這種方法給研究人員關於年代的證據，而不只是猜測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"later proved that","meaning":"後來證明","examples":[{"en":"Carbon dating later proved that the site was Neolithic.","zh":"碳定年法後來證明該遺址屬於新石器時代。"},{"en":"Later proved that means showed something to be true after more time or evidence.","zh":"later proved that 指在更多時間或證據後顯示某事為真。"},{"en":"Tests later proved that the stone tool was ancient.","zh":"測試後來證明那件石器是古代物件。"},{"en":"A second investigation later proved that the first guess was correct.","zh":"第二次調查後來證明最初猜測是正確的。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how evidence can confirm an earlier idea.","zh":"這個短語顯示證據如何確認早前想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"over 5,000 years old","meaning":"有 5,000 多年歷史","examples":[{"en":"The site was over 5,000 years old.","zh":"該遺址有 5,000 多年歷史。"},{"en":"Over 5,000 years old means older than five thousand years.","zh":"over 5,000 years old 指超過五千年歷史。"},{"en":"The wooden remains were over 5,000 years old.","zh":"木製遺跡有 5,000 多年歷史。"},{"en":"An object over 5,000 years old can tell us about very early human life.","zh":"有 5,000 多年歷史的物件可以告訴我們非常早期的人類生活。"},{"en":"This phrase helps listeners understand the great age of the discovery.","zh":"這個短語幫助聽眾理解發現的年代非常久遠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"thanks to","meaning":"多虧","examples":[{"en":"Thanks to the bog, the remains are extremely well-preserved.","zh":"多虧沼澤，遺跡保存得極好。"},{"en":"Thanks to means because of something positive or helpful.","zh":"thanks to 指因為某件正面或有幫助的事。"},{"en":"Thanks to careful storage, the old letters survived.","zh":"多虧小心保存，舊信件保留下來。"},{"en":"Thanks to the rain, the dry fields began to recover.","zh":"多虧雨水，乾旱田地開始恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the cause of a good result.","zh":"這個短語顯示好結果的原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"covers the area","meaning":"覆蓋該地區","examples":[{"en":"The bog covers the area around the settlement.","zh":"沼澤覆蓋聚落周圍的地區。"},{"en":"Covers the area means spreads over or lies across that place.","zh":"covers the area 指鋪展或覆蓋在該地方之上。"},{"en":"Snow covers the area around the village in winter.","zh":"冬天，雪覆蓋村莊周圍的地區。"},{"en":"Thick forest covers the area where the old path once ran.","zh":"茂密森林覆蓋舊小路曾經經過的地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what lies on top of a place.","zh":"這個短語描述某地表面上覆蓋着甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the remains of the settlement","meaning":"聚落遺跡","examples":[{"en":"The remains of the settlement at Céide Fields are well-preserved.","zh":"Céide Fields 的聚落遺跡保存良好。"},{"en":"The remains of the settlement are the surviving parts of an old place where people lived.","zh":"remains of the settlement 指人們曾經居住地方中保存下來的部分。"},{"en":"Archaeologists found the remains of the settlement under layers of peat.","zh":"考古學家在層層泥炭下發現聚落遺跡。"},{"en":"The remains of the settlement may include walls, tools, and house foundations.","zh":"聚落遺跡可能包括牆壁、工具和房屋地基。"},{"en":"Studying the remains of the settlement helps explain how the community was organised.","zh":"研究聚落遺跡有助解釋該社群如何組織生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"extremely well-preserved","meaning":"保存得極好","examples":[{"en":"The remains are extremely well-preserved because of the bog.","zh":"由於沼澤，遺跡保存得極好。"},{"en":"Extremely well-preserved means kept in very good condition over a long time.","zh":"extremely well-preserved 指經過很長時間仍保持非常良好狀態。"},{"en":"The wooden bowl was extremely well-preserved in the wet soil.","zh":"那隻木碗在濕泥土中保存得極好。"},{"en":"An extremely well-preserved site gives archaeologists more evidence to study.","zh":"保存得極好的遺址給考古學家更多證據研究。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that time has not damaged something as much as expected.","zh":"這個短語顯示時間並沒有像預期般嚴重破壞某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"90 percent water","meaning":"百分之九十是水","examples":[{"en":"A bog is 90 percent water.","zh":"沼澤百分之九十是水。"},{"en":"90 percent water means water makes up almost all of the material.","zh":"90 percent water 指水分佔材料幾乎全部。"},{"en":"If soil is 90 percent water, it is extremely wet and soft.","zh":"如果土壤百分之九十是水，它會非常濕軟。"},{"en":"A bog that is 90 percent water can slow the decay of buried objects.","zh":"百分之九十是水的沼澤可以減慢埋藏物件腐爛。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear scientific detail about bog conditions.","zh":"這個短語給出關於沼澤環境的清楚科學細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"so saturated that","meaning":"飽和到……的程度","examples":[{"en":"The soil is so saturated that dead plants do not fully decay.","zh":"土壤飽和到枯死植物不會完全腐爛的程度。"},{"en":"So saturated that means so full of water that a particular result happens.","zh":"so saturated that 指充滿水分到導致某結果發生。"},{"en":"The ground was so saturated that our shoes sank into the mud.","zh":"地面飽和到我們的鞋子陷入泥中的程度。"},{"en":"The towel was so saturated that it could not absorb more water.","zh":"毛巾濕透到不能再吸水的程度。"},{"en":"This pattern shows a strong cause-and-effect relationship.","zh":"這個句式顯示強烈因果關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"grow on its surface","meaning":"在其表面生長","examples":[{"en":"Grasses and heathers grow on the surface of the bog.","zh":"草和石南在沼澤表面生長。"},{"en":"To grow on its surface means to live or develop on the top layer of something.","zh":"grow on its surface 指在某物的最上層生活或生長。"},{"en":"Moss can grow on the surface of old stones.","zh":"苔蘚可以在舊石頭表面生長。"},{"en":"Plants grow on the surface of wet peatland and later become part of the bog.","zh":"植物在濕泥炭地表面生長，之後成為沼澤的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe what can be seen above the ground.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述地面上可見的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fully decay","meaning":"完全腐爛","examples":[{"en":"The plants do not fully decay in the bog.","zh":"植物在沼澤中不會完全腐爛。"},{"en":"To fully decay means to break down completely after death.","zh":"fully decay 指死亡後完全分解。"},{"en":"Leaves usually fully decay in warm, dry soil.","zh":"樹葉通常會在溫暖乾爽的土壤中完全腐爛。"},{"en":"Wood may not fully decay if there is little oxygen.","zh":"如果氧氣很少，木材可能不會完全腐爛。"},{"en":"When plants do not fully decay, they can build up into peat.","zh":"當植物不完全腐爛，它們可以累積成泥炭。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"accumulate in layers","meaning":"層層堆積","examples":[{"en":"Dead plants accumulate in layers.","zh":"枯死植物會層層堆積。"},{"en":"To accumulate in layers means to build up gradually in separate levels.","zh":"accumulate in layers 指逐漸以一層一層的方式累積。"},{"en":"Snow can accumulate in layers during a long storm.","zh":"長時間暴風雪期間，積雪可以層層堆積。"},{"en":"Dead plants accumulate in layers and slowly form peat.","zh":"枯死植物層層堆積，慢慢形成泥炭。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a slow process of material building up over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示材料隨時間慢慢累積的過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"remain well preserved","meaning":"保存良好","examples":[{"en":"Objects remain well preserved in these conditions.","zh":"物件在這些條件下保存良好。"},{"en":"To remain well preserved means to stay in good condition over time.","zh":"remain well preserved 指隨時間仍保持良好狀態。"},{"en":"Ancient tools can remain well preserved in dry caves.","zh":"古代工具可以在乾燥洞穴中保存良好。"},{"en":"In wet bogs, wood may remain well preserved for thousands of years.","zh":"在潮濕沼澤中，木材可以保存良好數千年。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why old objects can still be studied today.","zh":"這個短語解釋為甚麼古物至今仍可被研究。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in these conditions","meaning":"在這些條件下","examples":[{"en":"Objects remain well preserved in these conditions.","zh":"物件在這些條件下保存良好。"},{"en":"In these conditions means under these particular physical or environmental circumstances.","zh":"in these conditions 指在這些特定身體、物理或環境情況下。"},{"en":"Plants grow slowly in these conditions because the soil is poor.","zh":"在這些條件下，植物因土壤貧瘠而生長緩慢。"},{"en":"In these conditions, metal may rust quickly.","zh":"在這些條件下，金屬可能迅速生鏽。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an environment with the result it creates.","zh":"這個短語把環境與其造成的結果連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the acidity of the peat","meaning":"泥炭的酸性","examples":[{"en":"Objects are preserved because of the acidity of the peat.","zh":"物件因泥炭的酸性而被保存。"},{"en":"The acidity of the peat means the acidic chemical condition of the partly decayed plant material.","zh":"acidity of the peat 指半腐爛植物材料中的酸性化學狀態。"},{"en":"The acidity of the peat can slow the breakdown of buried objects.","zh":"泥炭的酸性可以減慢埋藏物件的分解。"},{"en":"Scientists study the acidity of the peat to understand preservation conditions.","zh":"科學家研究泥炭的酸性，以了解保存條件。"},{"en":"This phrase explains one reason why bogs can protect ancient remains.","zh":"這個短語解釋沼澤能保護古代遺跡的其中一個原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"deficiency of oxygen","meaning":"缺乏氧氣","examples":[{"en":"The deficiency of oxygen helps preserve objects in the bog.","zh":"缺乏氧氣有助保存沼澤中的物件。"},{"en":"Deficiency of oxygen means a lack or shortage of oxygen.","zh":"deficiency of oxygen 指氧氣不足或缺乏。"},{"en":"A deficiency of oxygen slows the decay of organic materials.","zh":"缺乏氧氣會減慢有機材料腐爛。"},{"en":"In deep wet soil, a deficiency of oxygen can preserve wood and plants.","zh":"在深層濕泥土中，缺乏氧氣可以保存木材和植物。"},{"en":"This condition helps explain why objects survive in bogs for so long.","zh":"這種條件有助解釋為何物件能在沼澤中保存這麼久。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at least 175 days of rain","meaning":"至少 175 天降雨","examples":[{"en":"At least 175 days of rain a year are required for this to happen.","zh":"每年至少 175 天降雨才會出現這種情況。"},{"en":"At least 175 days of rain means no fewer than 175 rainy days.","zh":"at least 175 days of rain 指不少於 175 個下雨天。"},{"en":"A bog may need at least 175 days of rain each year to remain wet.","zh":"沼澤每年可能需要至少 175 天降雨才能保持潮濕。"},{"en":"Areas with at least 175 days of rain can develop very wet soil.","zh":"有至少 175 天降雨的地區可以形成非常潮濕的土壤。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a minimum rainfall condition.","zh":"這個短語給出最低降雨條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be required for","meaning":"……所需","examples":[{"en":"A high level of rainfall is required for a bog to form.","zh":"沼澤形成需要高降雨量。"},{"en":"To be required for something means to be necessary for it to happen.","zh":"be required for something 指某事發生所必需。"},{"en":"Careful planning is required for a safe school trip.","zh":"安全學校旅行需要周詳計劃。"},{"en":"Oxygen is required for many living things to survive.","zh":"許多生物生存需要氧氣。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a necessary condition.","zh":"這個短語解釋必要條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an average of","meaning":"平均","examples":[{"en":"This part of Ireland gets an average of 225 days of rain.","zh":"愛爾蘭這一部分平均有 225 天下雨。"},{"en":"An average of means the typical amount calculated from many examples or years.","zh":"an average of 指從多個例子或多年資料計算出的典型數量。"},{"en":"The class reads an average of two books a month.","zh":"全班平均每月閱讀兩本書。"},{"en":"The town receives an average of 100 rainy days each year.","zh":"這個城鎮每年平均有 100 個下雨天。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing normal or typical figures.","zh":"這個短語適合用來描述一般或典型數字。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"relative peace and stability","meaning":"相對和平與穩定","examples":[{"en":"The Neolithic farmers enjoyed relative peace and stability.","zh":"新石器時代農民享有相對和平與穩定。"},{"en":"Relative peace and stability means a period that was fairly calm and settled compared with other times.","zh":"relative peace and stability 指與其他時期相比較平靜和安定的時期。"},{"en":"A community can grow during relative peace and stability.","zh":"社群可以在相對和平與穩定中成長。"},{"en":"Farmers need relative peace and stability to build homes and care for animals.","zh":"農民需要相對和平與穩定來建屋和照顧動物。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean perfect peace, but a generally secure situation.","zh":"這個短語不是指完美和平，而是整體上安全穩定的情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"several centuries of","meaning":"數個世紀的……","examples":[{"en":"The farmers enjoyed several centuries of stability.","zh":"農民享有數個世紀的穩定。"},{"en":"Several centuries of something means a period lasting a few hundred years.","zh":"several centuries of something 指持續幾百年的時期。"},{"en":"The castle shows several centuries of local history.","zh":"那座城堡展示了數個世紀的本地歷史。"},{"en":"A farming system may continue for several centuries if conditions stay good.","zh":"如果環境保持良好，農耕制度可能延續數個世紀。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a long period of time.","zh":"這個短語突出一段很長時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Neolithic farmers","meaning":"新石器時代農民","examples":[{"en":"Neolithic farmers lived in permanent settlements.","zh":"新石器時代農民住在永久聚落中。"},{"en":"Neolithic farmers were people in the later Stone Age who grew crops and kept animals.","zh":"Neolithic farmers 指新石器時代種植農作物和飼養動物的人。"},{"en":"Neolithic farmers built fields, houses, and stone boundaries.","zh":"新石器時代農民建造田地、房屋和石邊界。"},{"en":"Unlike earlier hunters, Neolithic farmers often stayed in one place.","zh":"與較早期獵人不同，新石器時代農民常定居一地。"},{"en":"Studying Neolithic farmers helps us understand the beginnings of settled life.","zh":"研究新石器時代農民有助我們了解定居生活的開端。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"larger communities","meaning":"較大的社群","examples":[{"en":"Neolithic farmers lived in larger communities than their predecessors.","zh":"新石器時代農民住在比前人更大的社群中。"},{"en":"Larger communities are bigger groups of people living together or near one another.","zh":"larger communities 指一起或相近居住的人數較多的群體。"},{"en":"Farming allowed people to live in larger communities because food could be produced nearby.","zh":"農耕讓人們能生活在較大的社群中，因為食物可在附近生產。"},{"en":"Larger communities need rules, shared spaces, and cooperation.","zh":"較大的社群需要規則、共享空間和合作。"},{"en":"This phrase compares group size between different periods.","zh":"這個短語比較不同時期的群體大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"their predecessors","meaning":"他們的前人","examples":[{"en":"They lived in larger communities than their predecessors.","zh":"他們住在比前人更大的社群中。"},{"en":"Their predecessors are the people who came before them in time or role.","zh":"their predecessors 指在時間或角色上比他們更早出現的人。"},{"en":"Modern farmers use machines that their predecessors did not have.","zh":"現代農民使用他們的前人沒有的機器。"},{"en":"Neolithic farmers lived differently from their predecessors who moved around more often.","zh":"新石器時代農民的生活方式不同於較常遷徙的前人。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare one generation or group with an earlier one.","zh":"這個短語幫助把一代人或一個群體與更早的一代比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a number of houses","meaning":"多間房屋","examples":[{"en":"A number of houses were built around a community building.","zh":"多間房屋圍繞一座社區建築而建。"},{"en":"A number of houses means several houses, though the exact number may not be stated.","zh":"a number of houses 指有幾間房屋，但未必說明確實數目。"},{"en":"Archaeologists found a number of houses near the old field walls.","zh":"考古學家在古田界牆附近發現多間房屋。"},{"en":"A number of houses around a shared space suggests a settled community.","zh":"多間房屋圍繞共享空間，暗示有定居社群。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a general quantity without exact counting.","zh":"這個短語在不精確點算時表示大概數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"built around","meaning":"圍繞……而建","examples":[{"en":"The houses were built around a community building.","zh":"房屋圍繞一座社區建築而建。"},{"en":"Built around means constructed surrounding or centred on something.","zh":"built around 指在某物周圍或以某物為中心建造。"},{"en":"The village was built around a small market square.","zh":"村莊圍繞一個小市集廣場而建。"},{"en":"A school timetable can be built around students’ learning needs.","zh":"學校時間表可以圍繞學生的學習需要而設計。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe both physical arrangement and planning.","zh":"這個短語可以描述實體排列，也可以描述規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"community building","meaning":"社區建築","examples":[{"en":"The houses were built around a community building.","zh":"房屋圍繞一座社區建築而建。"},{"en":"A community building is a shared building used by people in a settlement or neighbourhood.","zh":"community building 指聚落或社區中的人共同使用的建築。"},{"en":"A community building may be used for meetings, storage, or ceremonies.","zh":"社區建築可能用於會議、儲存或儀式。"},{"en":"Finding a community building suggests that people organised group activities.","zh":"發現社區建築暗示人們曾組織群體活動。"},{"en":"Such a building can show how important cooperation was in a settlement.","zh":"這類建築可以顯示合作在聚落中有多重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"permanent settlements","meaning":"永久聚落","examples":[{"en":"Neolithic farmers lived in permanent settlements.","zh":"新石器時代農民住在永久聚落中。"},{"en":"Permanent settlements are places where people live for a long time instead of moving often.","zh":"permanent settlements 指人們長期居住，而不是經常遷移的地方。"},{"en":"Farming encouraged permanent settlements because crops and animals needed care.","zh":"農耕鼓勵永久聚落，因為農作物和動物需要照顧。"},{"en":"Permanent settlements may leave behind houses, fields, and tools.","zh":"永久聚落可能留下房屋、田地和工具。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts settled life with a nomadic way of life.","zh":"這個短語把定居生活與游牧生活作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as people often assume","meaning":"正如人們常以為的那樣","examples":[{"en":"The houses were not round, as people often assume.","zh":"房屋並不是圓形，並非正如人們常以為的那樣。"},{"en":"As people often assume means as many people commonly believe, sometimes wrongly.","zh":"as people often assume 指許多人通常相信某事，有時是錯誤的。"},{"en":"Ancient homes were not always simple huts, as people often assume.","zh":"古代房屋並不總是簡單小屋，並非正如人們常以為的那樣。"},{"en":"Older technology was not always less clever, as people often assume.","zh":"舊科技並不一定較不聰明，並非正如人們常以為的那樣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when correcting a common belief.","zh":"這個短語適合用來糾正常見看法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rectangular","meaning":"長方形的","examples":[{"en":"The houses were rectangular rather than round.","zh":"房屋是長方形的，而不是圓形的。"},{"en":"Rectangular means shaped like a rectangle, with four sides and four corners.","zh":"rectangular 指形狀像長方形，有四條邊和四個角。"},{"en":"The classroom tables are rectangular, so students can sit along both long sides.","zh":"課室桌子是長方形的，所以學生可以坐在兩條長邊旁。"},{"en":"Archaeologists found rectangular house foundations under the soil.","zh":"考古學家在泥土下發現長方形的房屋地基。"},{"en":"Describing a building as rectangular helps people imagine its shape.","zh":"描述建築物是長方形的，有助人想像其形狀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a hole in the roof","meaning":"屋頂上的洞","examples":[{"en":"The houses had a small hole in the roof.","zh":"房屋的屋頂上有一個小洞。"},{"en":"A hole in the roof is an opening at the top of a building.","zh":"hole in the roof 指建築物頂部的開口。"},{"en":"The hut had a hole in the roof to let smoke escape.","zh":"小屋屋頂上有一個洞，用來讓煙排出。"},{"en":"A hole in the roof can be useful if it is designed for ventilation.","zh":"如果為通風而設計，屋頂上的洞可以有用。"},{"en":"In an ancient house, a roof hole may show how people cooked indoors.","zh":"在古代房屋中，屋頂上的洞可能顯示人們如何在室內煮食。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"allow smoke to escape","meaning":"讓煙排出","examples":[{"en":"The hole in the roof allowed smoke to escape.","zh":"屋頂上的洞讓煙排出。"},{"en":"To allow smoke to escape means to let smoke leave a closed space.","zh":"allow smoke to escape 指讓煙離開封閉空間。"},{"en":"A chimney allows smoke to escape from a fireplace.","zh":"煙囪讓壁爐的煙排出。"},{"en":"Without a vent to allow smoke to escape, a room can become dangerous.","zh":"如果沒有通風口讓煙排出，房間可能變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the practical purpose of an opening.","zh":"這個短語解釋開口的實際用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"one of many innovations","meaning":"眾多創新之一","examples":[{"en":"Indoor cooking was one of many innovations.","zh":"室內烹飪是眾多創新之一。"},{"en":"One of many innovations means one new idea or invention among several others.","zh":"one of many innovations 指多項新想法或發明中的其中一項。"},{"en":"Irrigation was one of many innovations that helped early farming.","zh":"灌溉是幫助早期農耕的眾多創新之一。"},{"en":"The lift was one of many innovations that made buildings easier to use.","zh":"升降機是令建築物更易使用的眾多創新之一。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a change was part of a wider pattern of progress.","zh":"這個短語顯示某改變是更廣泛進步的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"indicate that","meaning":"表明","examples":[{"en":"The design indicates that the farmers cooked indoors.","zh":"這種設計表明農民在室內烹飪。"},{"en":"To indicate that means to show or suggest that something is true.","zh":"indicate that 指顯示或暗示某事是真的。"},{"en":"Smoke marks on the ceiling indicate that people used fire inside.","zh":"天花板上的煙痕表明人們曾在室內用火。"},{"en":"A worn path may indicate that many people walked there.","zh":"被磨損的小路可能表明很多人曾走過那裡。"},{"en":"This phrase connects evidence with a possible conclusion.","zh":"這個短語把證據與可能結論連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the first people to","meaning":"最早……的人","examples":[{"en":"Neolithic farmers were the first people to cook indoors.","zh":"新石器時代農民是最早在室內烹飪的人。"},{"en":"The first people to do something means the earliest known group who did it.","zh":"the first people to do something 指已知最早做某事的群體。"},{"en":"Early farmers may have been the first people to build permanent field walls.","zh":"早期農民可能是最早建造永久田界牆的人。"},{"en":"The first people to use pottery changed how food could be cooked and stored.","zh":"最早使用陶器的人改變了食物烹煮和儲存方式。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights an important early development in history.","zh":"這個短語突出歷史上的重要早期發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cook indoors","meaning":"在室內烹飪","examples":[{"en":"Neolithic farmers were the first people to cook indoors.","zh":"新石器時代農民是最早在室內烹飪的人。"},{"en":"To cook indoors means to prepare food inside a building rather than outside.","zh":"cook indoors 指在建築物內而不是戶外準備食物。"},{"en":"A hole in the roof made it safer to cook indoors because smoke could leave.","zh":"屋頂上的洞讓煙能排出，因此在室內烹飪較安全。"},{"en":"Cooking indoors helped people prepare food during bad weather.","zh":"在室內烹飪幫助人們在惡劣天氣中準備食物。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a change in how homes were used.","zh":"這個短語顯示房屋用途的改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"new technology","meaning":"新技術","examples":[{"en":"Pottery was a new technology brought to Ireland.","zh":"陶器是帶到愛爾蘭的新技術。"},{"en":"New technology means a new tool, method, or invention that changes how people do things.","zh":"new technology 指改變人們做事方式的新工具、方法或發明。"},{"en":"Writing was a new technology that helped people record information.","zh":"書寫是一項幫助人們記錄資料的新技術。"},{"en":"Pottery was new technology because it made cooking and storing food easier.","zh":"陶器是新技術，因為它令烹煮和儲存食物更容易。"},{"en":"New technology can change daily life, even in ancient communities.","zh":"新技術可以改變日常生活，即使在古代社群中也是如此。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Neolithic settlers","meaning":"新石器時代定居者","examples":[{"en":"Neolithic settlers brought pottery to Ireland.","zh":"新石器時代定居者把陶器帶到愛爾蘭。"},{"en":"Neolithic settlers were people from the later Stone Age who moved to live permanently in a place.","zh":"Neolithic settlers 指新石器時代遷往某地長期居住的人。"},{"en":"Neolithic settlers built homes and fields instead of moving constantly.","zh":"新石器時代定居者建造房屋和田地，而不是不斷遷移。"},{"en":"Neolithic settlers brought farming knowledge, animals, and tools with them.","zh":"新石器時代定居者帶來農耕知識、動物和工具。"},{"en":"Studying Neolithic settlers helps explain how new ways of life spread.","zh":"研究新石器時代定居者有助解釋新生活方式如何傳播。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"brought to Ireland","meaning":"帶到愛爾蘭","examples":[{"en":"Settlers brought pottery to Ireland.","zh":"定居者把陶器帶到愛爾蘭。"},{"en":"Brought to Ireland means carried, introduced, or transported into Ireland.","zh":"brought to Ireland 指被帶入、引入或運到愛爾蘭。"},{"en":"New farming methods were brought to Ireland by early settlers.","zh":"早期定居者把新農耕方法帶到愛爾蘭。"},{"en":"Objects brought to Ireland can show contact with other places.","zh":"帶到愛爾蘭的物件可以顯示與其他地方有接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how an idea or item entered Ireland.","zh":"這個短語解釋想法或物品如何進入愛爾蘭。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pottery","meaning":"陶器","examples":[{"en":"Pottery was an important Neolithic innovation.","zh":"陶器是重要的新石器時代創新。"},{"en":"Pottery means pots, bowls, or containers made from clay and hardened by heat.","zh":"pottery 指用黏土製成並經加熱變硬的罐、碗或容器。"},{"en":"Archaeologists study pottery to learn about cooking and storage.","zh":"考古學家研究陶器，以了解烹飪和儲存方式。"},{"en":"Broken pottery can still give useful evidence about ancient life.","zh":"破碎陶器仍能提供關於古代生活的有用證據。"},{"en":"Pottery allowed people to store food, carry liquids, and cook more effectively.","zh":"陶器讓人們能儲存食物、盛載液體和更有效烹煮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fragments of Neolithic pots","meaning":"新石器時代陶罐碎片","examples":[{"en":"Fragments of Neolithic pots have been found in Céide.","zh":"Céide 發現了新石器時代陶罐碎片。"},{"en":"Fragments of Neolithic pots are broken pieces of pottery from the Neolithic period.","zh":"fragments of Neolithic pots 指新石器時代陶器破碎後留下的碎片。"},{"en":"Archaeologists found fragments of Neolithic pots near an ancient house.","zh":"考古學家在古屋附近發現新石器時代陶罐碎片。"},{"en":"Small fragments of Neolithic pots can still show how pottery was made.","zh":"小小的新石器時代陶罐碎片仍能顯示陶器如何製作。"},{"en":"These fragments help researchers understand cooking, storage, and daily life.","zh":"這些碎片幫助研究人員了解烹飪、儲存和日常生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"elsewhere in Ireland","meaning":"愛爾蘭其他地方","examples":[{"en":"Fragments have been found in Céide and elsewhere in Ireland.","zh":"碎片在 Céide 和愛爾蘭其他地方都有發現。"},{"en":"Elsewhere in Ireland means in other places in Ireland.","zh":"elsewhere in Ireland 指在愛爾蘭的其他地方。"},{"en":"Similar tools were found at Céide and elsewhere in Ireland.","zh":"類似工具在 Céide 和愛爾蘭其他地方都有發現。"},{"en":"Evidence from elsewhere in Ireland helps archaeologists compare different sites.","zh":"來自愛爾蘭其他地方的證據幫助考古學家比較不同遺址。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a discovery is not limited to one location.","zh":"這個短語顯示發現不限於一個地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be used for many things","meaning":"有多種用途","examples":[{"en":"The pots were used for many things.","zh":"這些陶罐有多種用途。"},{"en":"To be used for many things means to have several different purposes.","zh":"be used for many things 指有幾種不同用途。"},{"en":"A bowl can be used for many things, such as mixing, serving, and storing food.","zh":"碗可以有多種用途，例如攪拌、盛載和儲存食物。"},{"en":"Ancient pots were used for many things in daily life.","zh":"古代陶罐在日常生活中有多種用途。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an object was practical and flexible.","zh":"這個短語顯示物件實用而靈活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as well as for storing food","meaning":"除了用於儲存食物外","examples":[{"en":"The pots were used as lamps as well as for storing food.","zh":"這些陶罐除了用於儲存食物外，也用作燈具。"},{"en":"As well as for storing food means in addition to being used to keep food.","zh":"as well as for storing food 指除了用來保存食物之外。"},{"en":"Clay pots were used for cooking as well as for storing food.","zh":"陶罐除了用於儲存食物外，也用於烹煮。"},{"en":"A container can be used for carrying water as well as for storing food.","zh":"容器除了用於儲存食物外，也可以用來盛水。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another use to an object’s main purpose.","zh":"這個短語為物件的主要用途再加入另一用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"storing food","meaning":"儲存食物","examples":[{"en":"Pots were used for storing food.","zh":"陶罐被用於儲存食物。"},{"en":"Storing food means keeping food safely for later use.","zh":"storing food 指安全保存食物以供之後使用。"},{"en":"Ancient farmers needed containers for storing food after harvest.","zh":"古代農民收成後需要容器來儲存食物。"},{"en":"Storing food well can prevent waste and hunger.","zh":"好好儲存食物可以防止浪費和飢餓。"},{"en":"Pottery changed daily life because it made storing food easier.","zh":"陶器改變日常生活，因為它令儲存食物更容易。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a small amount of","meaning":"少量的……","examples":[{"en":"The pots were filled with a small amount of fat.","zh":"這些陶罐裝有少量脂肪。"},{"en":"A small amount of something means a little quantity of it.","zh":"a small amount of something 指少量某物。"},{"en":"Add a small amount of oil before cooking the vegetables.","zh":"煮蔬菜前加入少量油。"},{"en":"A small amount of fat could burn long enough to provide light.","zh":"少量脂肪可以燃燒足夠久以提供光亮。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that only a limited quantity is needed.","zh":"這個短語顯示只需要有限數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"set alight","meaning":"被點燃","examples":[{"en":"The fat was set alight to create a lamp.","zh":"脂肪被點燃以製成燈。"},{"en":"To set something alight means to make it start burning.","zh":"set something alight 指使某物開始燃燒。"},{"en":"The campers set dry wood alight to make a fire.","zh":"露營者點燃乾木來生火。"},{"en":"In the pot, fat could be set alight to produce light.","zh":"在陶罐中，脂肪可以被點燃以產生光亮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes starting a controlled fire.","zh":"這個短語描述開始受控火焰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"serve as lamps","meaning":"用作燈具","examples":[{"en":"The pots served as lamps when the fat was set alight.","zh":"當脂肪被點燃時，陶罐用作燈具。"},{"en":"To serve as lamps means to function as lights.","zh":"serve as lamps 指發揮照明工具的功能。"},{"en":"Small oil bowls served as lamps in many ancient homes.","zh":"小油碗在許多古代家庭中用作燈具。"},{"en":"A container can serve as a lamp if it holds fuel safely.","zh":"如果容器能安全盛載燃料，它就可以用作燈具。"},{"en":"This phrase explains an object’s practical function.","zh":"這個短語解釋物件的實際功能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"It’s thought that","meaning":"人們認為","examples":[{"en":"It’s thought that the fields were used as paddocks.","zh":"人們認為這些田地被用作牲畜圍場。"},{"en":"It’s thought that means experts or people believe something is likely, though it may not be fully proven.","zh":"It’s thought that 指專家或人們相信某事很可能如此，但未必完全證實。"},{"en":"It’s thought that the stones formed part of an old wall.","zh":"人們認為這些石頭曾是古牆的一部分。"},{"en":"It’s thought that ancient farmers used these fields for animals.","zh":"人們認為古代農民用這些田地飼養動物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining a careful archaeological interpretation.","zh":"這個短語適合用來解釋謹慎的考古推斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"mainly used as","meaning":"主要用作","examples":[{"en":"The fields were mainly used as paddocks for animals.","zh":"這些田地主要用作動物的牲畜圍場。"},{"en":"Mainly used as means used mostly for one purpose.","zh":"mainly used as 指主要用於某一用途。"},{"en":"The room is mainly used as a study area.","zh":"這個房間主要用作溫習區。"},{"en":"Ancient pots may have been mainly used as food containers.","zh":"古代陶罐可能主要用作食物容器。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the primary function of a place or object.","zh":"這個短語指出地方或物件的主要功能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"paddocks","meaning":"牲畜圍場","examples":[{"en":"The Céide Fields were probably used as paddocks.","zh":"Céide Fields 很可能被用作牲畜圍場。"},{"en":"Paddocks are enclosed fields where animals can graze or be kept.","zh":"paddocks 指圍起來讓動物放牧或飼養的田地。"},{"en":"Farmers move cattle between paddocks to protect the grass.","zh":"農民把牛隻在不同牲畜圍場之間移動，以保護草地。"},{"en":"Stone walls may show where ancient paddocks were located.","zh":"石牆可能顯示古代牲畜圍場的位置。"},{"en":"Paddocks help control where animals feed and move.","zh":"牲畜圍場幫助控制動物在哪裡覓食和活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"graze in","meaning":"在……放牧","examples":[{"en":"The animals used the paddocks to graze in.","zh":"動物使用牲畜圍場在裡面放牧。"},{"en":"To graze in a place means for animals to feed on grass there.","zh":"graze in a place 指動物在某地吃草。"},{"en":"Sheep graze in the field during the day.","zh":"羊白天在田地裡放牧。"},{"en":"Cattle need enough land to graze in without damaging the plants.","zh":"牛隻需要足夠土地放牧，才不會破壞植物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how farm animals feed outdoors.","zh":"這個短語描述農場動物如何在戶外覓食。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"evidence suggests that","meaning":"證據顯示","examples":[{"en":"Evidence suggests that each plot could sustain an extended family.","zh":"證據顯示每塊土地可供養一個大家庭。"},{"en":"Evidence suggests that means facts or findings point toward a likely conclusion.","zh":"evidence suggests that 指事實或發現指向一個很可能的結論。"},{"en":"Evidence suggests that the building was used for storage.","zh":"證據顯示該建築曾用於儲存。"},{"en":"Soil marks and tools suggest that people farmed here long ago.","zh":"土壤痕跡和工具顯示很久以前有人在這裡耕作。"},{"en":"This phrase is careful because it presents a conclusion based on evidence.","zh":"這個短語較謹慎，因為它根據證據提出結論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"each plot of land","meaning":"每塊土地","examples":[{"en":"Each plot of land was large enough to support a family.","zh":"每塊土地都大到足以供養一個家庭。"},{"en":"Each plot of land means each separate piece or area of land.","zh":"each plot of land 指每一塊獨立的土地或區域。"},{"en":"Farmers divided the valley into each plot of land using stone walls.","zh":"農民用石牆把山谷分成每塊土地。"},{"en":"Each plot of land may have belonged to a different family group.","zh":"每塊土地可能屬於不同家庭群體。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe how land was divided and used.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述土地如何被分割和使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"of a suitable size to","meaning":"大小適合用來……","examples":[{"en":"Each plot was of a suitable size to sustain an extended family.","zh":"每塊土地大小適合用來供養一個大家庭。"},{"en":"Of a suitable size to means large or small enough for a particular purpose.","zh":"of a suitable size to 指大小足以或適合某個用途。"},{"en":"The classroom is of a suitable size to hold thirty students.","zh":"這間課室大小適合容納三十名學生。"},{"en":"A field must be of a suitable size to feed several animals.","zh":"田地大小必須適合用來餵養幾隻動物。"},{"en":"This phrase connects size with practical use.","zh":"這個短語把大小與實際用途連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sustain an extended family","meaning":"供養一個大家庭","examples":[{"en":"Each plot could sustain an extended family.","zh":"每塊土地都可以供養一個大家庭。"},{"en":"To sustain an extended family means to provide enough food and resources for a large family group.","zh":"sustain an extended family 指提供足夠食物和資源給一個大型家庭群體。"},{"en":"A productive farm can sustain an extended family for many years.","zh":"肥沃農場可以多年供養一個大家庭。"},{"en":"If soil becomes poor, it may no longer sustain an extended family.","zh":"如果土壤變差，它可能不再能供養一個大家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the link between land size and family survival.","zh":"這個短語顯示土地大小與家庭生存之間的關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"extended family","meaning":"大家庭","examples":[{"en":"The land could support an extended family.","zh":"這片土地可以供養一個大家庭。"},{"en":"An extended family includes relatives beyond parents and children, such as grandparents, uncles, aunts, and cousins.","zh":"extended family 指包括父母和子女以外親屬的家庭，例如祖父母、叔伯姨姑和表兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"An extended family may live together or share land and work.","zh":"大家庭可能一起居住，或共同分享土地和工作。"},{"en":"In farming communities, an extended family can help with planting, animals, and storage.","zh":"在農耕社群中，大家庭可以協助種植、照顧動物和儲存食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a larger family group, not just a small household.","zh":"這個短語描述較大的家庭群體，而不只是小家庭。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a system of rotational grazing","meaning":"輪流放牧制度","examples":[{"en":"The farmers may have used a system of rotational grazing.","zh":"農民可能使用輪流放牧制度。"},{"en":"A system of rotational grazing means moving animals between different fields so grass can recover.","zh":"system of rotational grazing 指把動物在不同田地之間移動，讓草地恢復的制度。"},{"en":"Farmers use a system of rotational grazing to avoid overusing one field.","zh":"農民使用輪流放牧制度，以避免過度使用同一片田地。"},{"en":"A system of rotational grazing can keep animals fed and land healthier.","zh":"輪流放牧制度可以讓動物有食物，同時令土地更健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an organised method of managing pasture.","zh":"這個短語描述管理牧場的有組織方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in order to prevent","meaning":"為了防止","examples":[{"en":"They used rotational grazing in order to prevent over-grazing.","zh":"他們使用輪流放牧制度，為了防止過度放牧。"},{"en":"In order to prevent means for the purpose of stopping something from happening.","zh":"in order to prevent 指為了阻止某事發生。"},{"en":"The school added handrails in order to prevent accidents.","zh":"學校加裝扶手，為了防止意外。"},{"en":"Farmers rotate crops in order to prevent soil exhaustion.","zh":"農民輪作農作物，為了防止土壤耗竭。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly explains the purpose of an action.","zh":"這個短語清楚解釋行動目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"over-grazing","meaning":"過度放牧","examples":[{"en":"Rotational grazing helped prevent over-grazing.","zh":"輪流放牧有助防止過度放牧。"},{"en":"Over-grazing happens when animals eat too much grass from the same land, damaging plant growth.","zh":"over-grazing 指動物在同一片土地吃掉太多草，破壞植物生長。"},{"en":"Over-grazing can leave soil bare and weak.","zh":"過度放牧會令土壤裸露和變弱。"},{"en":"Farmers move animals to new fields to reduce over-grazing.","zh":"農民把動物移到新田地，以減少過度放牧。"},{"en":"Preventing over-grazing helps land recover and stay productive.","zh":"防止過度放牧有助土地恢復並保持生產力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"allow for","meaning":"使……成為可能；顧及","examples":[{"en":"The system allowed for plant recovery and regrowth.","zh":"這個制度使植物恢復與再生成為可能。"},{"en":"To allow for something means to make it possible or take it into account.","zh":"allow for something 指使某事成為可能或把它考慮在內。"},{"en":"A good timetable allows for rest between lessons.","zh":"好時間表會顧及課堂之間的休息。"},{"en":"Rotational grazing allows for grass to grow back.","zh":"輪流放牧使草地再生成為可能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a system includes space or time for something important.","zh":"這個短語顯示制度為重要事情留出空間或時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"plant recovery and regrowth","meaning":"植物恢復與再生","examples":[{"en":"Rotational grazing allowed for plant recovery and regrowth.","zh":"輪流放牧讓植物恢復與再生成為可能。"},{"en":"Plant recovery and regrowth means plants becoming healthy again and growing back.","zh":"plant recovery and regrowth 指植物恢復健康並再次生長。"},{"en":"Fields need time for plant recovery and regrowth after animals graze there.","zh":"動物放牧後，田地需要時間讓植物恢復與再生。"},{"en":"Rain can help plant recovery and regrowth after a dry season.","zh":"旱季後，雨水可以幫助植物恢復與再生。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how land can become productive again.","zh":"這個短語解釋土地如何重新變得有生產力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"year-round activity","meaning":"全年活動","examples":[{"en":"Grazing must have been a year-round activity.","zh":"放牧一定是全年活動。"},{"en":"A year-round activity is something that happens throughout the whole year.","zh":"year-round activity 指全年都進行的活動。"},{"en":"In warm climates, outdoor farming can be a year-round activity.","zh":"在溫暖氣候中，戶外農耕可以是全年活動。"},{"en":"If grazing was a year-round activity, animals stayed outside in all seasons.","zh":"如果放牧是全年活動，動物全年各季都留在戶外。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the activity was not limited to summer or winter.","zh":"這個短語顯示活動不限於夏天或冬天。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"no structures have been found","meaning":"尚未發現任何建築","examples":[{"en":"No structures have been found for sheltering animals in winter.","zh":"尚未發現任何在冬季為動物提供庇護的建築。"},{"en":"No structures have been found means archaeologists have not discovered buildings or remains of buildings.","zh":"no structures have been found 指考古學家尚未發現建築或建築遺跡。"},{"en":"No structures have been found near the field walls so far.","zh":"到目前為止，田界牆附近尚未發現任何建築。"},{"en":"If no structures have been found, researchers must be careful about their conclusions.","zh":"如果尚未發現任何建築，研究人員必須謹慎下結論。"},{"en":"This phrase reports the absence of archaeological evidence.","zh":"這個短語報告缺乏考古證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"shelter animals","meaning":"為動物提供庇護","examples":[{"en":"No structures were found to shelter animals in winter.","zh":"沒有發現用來在冬季為動物提供庇護的建築。"},{"en":"To shelter animals means to protect them from weather, danger, or cold.","zh":"shelter animals 指保護動物免受天氣、危險或寒冷影響。"},{"en":"Farmers build barns to shelter animals during storms.","zh":"農民建造穀倉，在暴風雨期間為動物提供庇護。"},{"en":"Without buildings to shelter animals, cattle may stay outdoors all year.","zh":"如果沒有建築為動物提供庇護，牛隻可能全年留在戶外。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a practical use of farm buildings.","zh":"這個短語解釋農場建築的實際用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in the winter","meaning":"在冬季","examples":[{"en":"The animals probably stayed outside in the winter.","zh":"動物很可能在冬季留在戶外。"},{"en":"In the winter means during the coldest season of the year.","zh":"in the winter 指在一年中最寒冷的季節。"},{"en":"Farmers need extra food for animals in the winter.","zh":"農民在冬季需要為動物準備額外食物。"},{"en":"In the winter, wet ground can make outdoor farming difficult.","zh":"在冬季，濕地會令戶外耕作困難。"},{"en":"This phrase sets the season for a situation or activity.","zh":"這個短語設定某情況或活動發生的季節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"way of life","meaning":"生活方式","examples":[{"en":"This way of life at Céide ceased abruptly.","zh":"Céide 的這種生活方式突然終止。"},{"en":"A way of life is the usual pattern of living, working, eating, and organising society.","zh":"way of life 指生活、工作、飲食和組織社會的通常模式。"},{"en":"Farming became a way of life for many Neolithic communities.","zh":"農耕成為許多新石器時代社群的生活方式。"},{"en":"Climate change can force people to change their way of life.","zh":"氣候變化可能迫使人們改變生活方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes more than one habit; it describes a whole lifestyle.","zh":"這個短語描述的不只是一個習慣，而是整體生活方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cease abruptly","meaning":"突然終止","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists believe this way of life ceased abruptly.","zh":"考古學家相信這種生活方式突然終止。"},{"en":"To cease abruptly means to stop suddenly rather than slowly.","zh":"cease abruptly 指突然停止，而不是慢慢停止。"},{"en":"The village’s farming activity seems to have ceased abruptly after flooding.","zh":"水浸後，村莊的農耕活動似乎突然終止。"},{"en":"A sudden climate change can make a settlement cease abruptly.","zh":"突然的氣候變化可以令聚落突然終止。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a sharp and unexpected ending.","zh":"這個短語暗示急劇而意想不到的結束。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"several factors","meaning":"幾個因素","examples":[{"en":"Several factors may have contributed to the change.","zh":"幾個因素可能促成了這種變化。"},{"en":"Several factors means several causes or things that helped create a result.","zh":"several factors 指幾個造成結果的原因或事物。"},{"en":"Several factors affected the success of the harvest.","zh":"幾個因素影響了收成的成功。"},{"en":"Poor soil, heavy rain, and overuse were several factors in the decline.","zh":"土壤貧瘠、大雨和過度使用是衰落的幾個因素。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a problem may have more than one cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示問題可能不只一個原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"contribute to","meaning":"導致；促成","examples":[{"en":"Several factors may have contributed to the changing circumstances.","zh":"幾個因素可能促成了變化中的情況。"},{"en":"To contribute to something means to help cause or add to it.","zh":"contribute to something 指幫助造成或增加某事。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can contribute to soil erosion.","zh":"大雨可能導致土壤侵蝕。"},{"en":"Poor planning may contribute to the failure of a project.","zh":"計劃不周可能促成項目失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining one cause among several.","zh":"這個短語適合用來解釋多個原因中的一個。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"changing circumstances","meaning":"變化中的情況","examples":[{"en":"Several factors contributed to the changing circumstances.","zh":"幾個因素促成了變化中的情況。"},{"en":"Changing circumstances are situations or conditions that are becoming different over time.","zh":"changing circumstances 指隨時間變得不同的情況或條件。"},{"en":"Farmers must adapt to changing circumstances such as wetter weather.","zh":"農民必須適應更潮濕天氣等變化中的情況。"},{"en":"Changing circumstances can make an old way of life difficult to continue.","zh":"變化中的情況可能令舊生活方式難以延續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a situation that is not staying the same.","zh":"這個短語描述不是一成不變的情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"become less productive","meaning":"變得較不肥沃","examples":[{"en":"The soil became less productive over time.","zh":"土壤隨時間變得較不肥沃。"},{"en":"To become less productive means to produce less than before.","zh":"become less productive 指產出比以前少。"},{"en":"Land can become less productive if crops are grown too intensively.","zh":"如果農作物種植過於密集，土地可能變得較不肥沃。"},{"en":"A tired worker may become less productive after many hours without rest.","zh":"工人長時間沒有休息後可能變得較低效率。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a gradual fall in usefulness or output.","zh":"這個短語顯示用途或產出逐漸下降。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"Poor soil quality led to the abandonment of farming.","zh":"土壤質素差導致人們放棄農耕。"},{"en":"To lead to something means to cause it or result in it.","zh":"lead to something 指造成某事或導致某結果。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can lead to flooding in low fields.","zh":"大雨可能導致低窪田地水浸。"},{"en":"Poor planning may lead to delays in a project.","zh":"計劃不周可能導致項目延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly connects a cause with a result.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接原因和結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the abandonment of farming","meaning":"放棄農耕","examples":[{"en":"Less productive soil led to the abandonment of farming.","zh":"土壤較不肥沃導致人們放棄農耕。"},{"en":"The abandonment of farming means people stopped farming and left that activity behind.","zh":"abandonment of farming 指人們停止農耕並放棄這項活動。"},{"en":"Climate change may cause the abandonment of farming in some areas.","zh":"氣候變化可能導致某些地區放棄農耕。"},{"en":"The abandonment of farming can force communities to move elsewhere.","zh":"放棄農耕可能迫使社群遷往其他地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major change in a community’s way of life.","zh":"這個短語描述社群生活方式中的重大改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"crop rotation system","meaning":"輪作制度","examples":[{"en":"The crop rotation system was partly responsible for the decline.","zh":"輪作制度對衰落負有部分責任。"},{"en":"A crop rotation system is a method of growing different crops on the same land in a planned order.","zh":"crop rotation system 指按計劃順序在同一土地種植不同作物的方法。"},{"en":"Farmers use a crop rotation system to protect soil nutrients.","zh":"農民使用輪作制度來保護土壤養分。"},{"en":"If a crop rotation system is too intensive, the soil may still become tired.","zh":"如果輪作制度過於密集，土壤仍可能變得疲乏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an organised farming method.","zh":"這個短語描述一種有組織的農耕方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"partly responsible for","meaning":"對……負有部分責任","examples":[{"en":"The crop rotation system was partly responsible for the problem.","zh":"輪作制度對問題負有部分責任。"},{"en":"Partly responsible for something means one of the causes, but not the only cause.","zh":"partly responsible for something 指是其中一個原因，但不是唯一原因。"},{"en":"Poor weather was partly responsible for the failed harvest.","zh":"惡劣天氣對收成失敗負有部分責任。"},{"en":"Long working hours were partly responsible for the workers’ tiredness.","zh":"長工時對工人的疲勞負有部分責任。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that responsibility is shared among several factors.","zh":"這個短語顯示責任由幾個因素共同承擔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"very intensive","meaning":"非常密集的","examples":[{"en":"The farming system would have been very intensive.","zh":"這種農耕制度很可能非常密集。"},{"en":"Very intensive means using a lot of effort, land, labour, or resources in a concentrated way.","zh":"very intensive 指以集中方式使用大量努力、土地、勞力或資源。"},{"en":"Very intensive farming can produce more food at first but may damage soil later.","zh":"非常密集的農耕起初可能生產更多食物，但之後可能破壞土壤。"},{"en":"A very intensive study schedule can make students exhausted.","zh":"非常密集的溫習時間表可能令學生筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests heavy use rather than gentle or occasional use.","zh":"這個短語暗示大量使用，而不是溫和或偶爾使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not sustainable","meaning":"不可持續的","examples":[{"en":"The system was intensive and not sustainable.","zh":"這種制度很密集，而且不可持續。"},{"en":"Not sustainable means unable to continue for a long time without causing damage or running out of resources.","zh":"not sustainable 指無法長期持續而不造成破壞或耗盡資源。"},{"en":"Farming that damages soil is not sustainable.","zh":"會破壞土壤的農耕方式是不可持續的。"},{"en":"A work schedule with no rest is not sustainable for employees.","zh":"沒有休息的工作時間表對員工來說不可持續。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that something may fail if it continues unchanged.","zh":"這個短語警告某事若不改變，可能會失敗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"climatic pressures","meaning":"氣候壓力","examples":[{"en":"Climatic pressures also contributed to the decline.","zh":"氣候壓力也促成了衰落。"},{"en":"Climatic pressures are difficulties caused by changes in weather or climate.","zh":"climatic pressures 指由天氣或氣候變化造成的困難。"},{"en":"Drought and heavy rain are climatic pressures for farmers.","zh":"乾旱和大雨都是農民面對的氣候壓力。"},{"en":"Climatic pressures can force communities to change how they grow food.","zh":"氣候壓力可能迫使社群改變種植食物的方法。"},{"en":"This phrase explains environmental stress over time.","zh":"這個短語解釋長期環境壓力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"relatively dry period","meaning":"相對乾燥的時期","examples":[{"en":"The farmers enjoyed a relatively dry period.","zh":"農民享有一段相對乾燥的時期。"},{"en":"A relatively dry period is a time with less rain than other periods, though not necessarily completely dry.","zh":"relatively dry period 指比其他時期雨量較少的時間，但不一定完全乾旱。"},{"en":"Crops grew well during a relatively dry period.","zh":"在相對乾燥的時期，農作物生長良好。"},{"en":"A relatively dry period may allow people to farm land that later becomes too wet.","zh":"相對乾燥的時期可能讓人們耕種後來變得太濕的土地。"},{"en":"This phrase compares rainfall with wetter times before or after.","zh":"這個短語把降雨量與之前或之後較潮濕的時期比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"began to change","meaning":"開始改變","examples":[{"en":"The climate began to change.","zh":"氣候開始改變。"},{"en":"Began to change means started to become different.","zh":"began to change 指開始變得不同。"},{"en":"The weather began to change after many years of dryness.","zh":"多年乾燥後，天氣開始改變。"},{"en":"When the soil began to change, farming became more difficult.","zh":"當土壤開始改變，農耕變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the start of a process.","zh":"這個短語標示某過程的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"conditions became wetter","meaning":"環境變得更潮濕","examples":[{"en":"The conditions became wetter as rainfall increased.","zh":"隨着降雨增加，環境變得更潮濕。"},{"en":"Conditions became wetter means the environment had more water or rain than before.","zh":"conditions became wetter 指環境比以前有更多水分或雨水。"},{"en":"The fields became harder to farm when conditions became wetter.","zh":"當環境變得更潮濕，田地變得更難耕種。"},{"en":"If conditions become wetter, bogs may begin to form.","zh":"如果環境變得更潮濕，沼澤可能開始形成。"},{"en":"This phrase connects climate change with changes in the land.","zh":"這個短語把氣候變化與土地變化連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a lot more rain","meaning":"多得多的雨水","examples":[{"en":"The area began to receive a lot more rain.","zh":"該地區開始有多得多的雨水。"},{"en":"A lot more rain means much more rainfall than before.","zh":"a lot more rain 指比以前多很多的降雨。"},{"en":"Farmers had difficulty when the valley started getting a lot more rain.","zh":"當山谷開始有多得多的雨水，農民遇到困難。"},{"en":"A lot more rain can make soil too wet for crops.","zh":"多得多的雨水可以令土壤太濕，不適合作物生長。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a major increase in rainfall.","zh":"這個短語顯示降雨量大幅增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"encourage the bog to form","meaning":"促使沼澤形成","examples":[{"en":"The wetter conditions encouraged the bog to form.","zh":"更潮濕的環境促使沼澤形成。"},{"en":"To encourage the bog to form means to create conditions that help a bog develop.","zh":"encourage the bog to form 指創造有助沼澤發展的條件。"},{"en":"Heavy rainfall and poor drainage can encourage a bog to form.","zh":"大量降雨和排水不良可以促使沼澤形成。"},{"en":"Wetter soil encouraged the bog to form over the old fields.","zh":"更潮濕的土壤促使沼澤在舊田地上形成。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how climate helped change the landscape.","zh":"這個短語解釋氣候如何幫助改變地貌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"over the area","meaning":"覆蓋該地區","examples":[{"en":"The bog formed over the area.","zh":"沼澤覆蓋該地區形成。"},{"en":"Over the area means across or on top of that place.","zh":"over the area 指在該地方之上或遍及該地方。"},{"en":"Thick mist spread over the area in the morning.","zh":"早上濃霧覆蓋該地區。"},{"en":"Peat slowly formed over the area where people had once farmed.","zh":"泥炭慢慢覆蓋人們曾經耕作的地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something covering a place.","zh":"這個短語描述某物覆蓋某地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"survives today","meaning":"保存至今","examples":[{"en":"The bog that formed over the area survives today.","zh":"覆蓋該地區形成的沼澤保存至今。"},{"en":"Survives today means still exists now after a long time.","zh":"survives today 指經過很長時間後現在仍然存在。"},{"en":"The old stone wall survives today beneath the grass.","zh":"那道舊石牆至今仍保存在草地下。"},{"en":"A tradition that began centuries ago may still survive today.","zh":"數百年前開始的傳統可能仍保存至今。"},{"en":"This phrase shows continuity from the past to the present.","zh":"這個短語顯示從過去延續到現在。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"an important Neolithic archaeological site","meaning":"重要的新石器時代考古遺址","examples":[{"en":"The Céide Fields are an important Neolithic archaeological site.","zh":"Céide Fields 是一個重要的新石器時代考古遺址。"},{"en":"An important Neolithic archaeological site is a place from the Neolithic period that gives valuable evidence about ancient life.","zh":"important Neolithic archaeological site 指提供關於古代生活寶貴證據的新石器時代地方。"},{"en":"An important Neolithic archaeological site may show how early farmers lived and worked.","zh":"重要的新石器時代考古遺址可能顯示早期農民如何生活和工作。"},{"en":"Researchers protect an important Neolithic archaeological site so evidence is not damaged.","zh":"研究人員保護重要的新石器時代考古遺址，以免證據受損。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights both the age and research value of the place.","zh":"這個短語突出該地方的年代和研究價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"beneath the bog surface","meaning":"在沼澤表面之下","examples":[{"en":"The stones were found beneath the bog surface.","zh":"石頭在沼澤表面之下被發現。"},{"en":"Beneath the bog surface means under the top layer of the bog.","zh":"beneath the bog surface 指在沼澤最上層下面。"},{"en":"Archaeologists located walls beneath the bog surface using probes.","zh":"考古學家使用探針定位沼澤表面之下的牆壁。"},{"en":"Objects beneath the bog surface may remain hidden for thousands of years.","zh":"沼澤表面之下的物件可能隱藏數千年。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the hidden position of buried remains.","zh":"這個短語描述埋藏遺跡的隱藏位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"undertake an investigation","meaning":"展開調查","examples":[{"en":"Seamus Caulfield undertook an investigation of the site.","zh":"Seamus Caulfield 展開了對該遺址的調查。"},{"en":"To undertake an investigation means to begin and carry out a careful study or inquiry.","zh":"undertake an investigation 指開始並進行仔細研究或查問。"},{"en":"The museum undertook an investigation into the ancient bones.","zh":"博物館展開了對古代骨骼的調查。"},{"en":"Students undertook an investigation to find out why plants were dying.","zh":"學生展開調查，以找出植物死亡原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used for research or official study.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於研究或官方調查。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"used to identify","meaning":"用來辨認；用來找出","examples":[{"en":"The traditional method was used to identify where the stones were located.","zh":"這種傳統方法用來找出石頭所在的位置。"},{"en":"Used to identify means used to find, recognise, or confirm something.","zh":"used to identify 指用來找出、辨認或確認某事物。"},{"en":"Fingerprints are used to identify people.","zh":"指紋用來辨認人物身份。"},{"en":"Probes were used to identify hidden stones under the peat.","zh":"探針用來找出泥炭下隱藏的石頭。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose of a tool or method.","zh":"這個短語解釋工具或方法的用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"where stones were located","meaning":"石頭所在的位置","examples":[{"en":"The probes identified where the stones were located.","zh":"探針找出了石頭所在的位置。"},{"en":"Where stones were located means the exact places where the stones lay or were buried.","zh":"where stones were located 指石頭所在或埋藏的確切位置。"},{"en":"Archaeologists recorded where stones were located before drawing the map.","zh":"考古學家在繪製地圖前記錄石頭所在的位置。"},{"en":"Knowing where stones were located helped researchers understand the field walls.","zh":"知道石頭所在的位置幫助研究人員理解田界牆。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on position and arrangement.","zh":"這個短語聚焦位置和排列。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"items are well preserved","meaning":"物品保存良好","examples":[{"en":"Items are well preserved in the bog.","zh":"物品在沼澤中保存良好。"},{"en":"Items are well preserved means objects have stayed in good condition over time.","zh":"items are well preserved 指物件隨時間仍保持良好狀態。"},{"en":"Wooden items are well preserved when oxygen is limited.","zh":"當氧氣有限時，木製物品保存良好。"},{"en":"If items are well preserved, archaeologists can study them more easily.","zh":"如果物品保存良好，考古學家可以更容易研究它們。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why the site is valuable for research.","zh":"這個短語解釋該遺址為何具研究價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a lack of oxygen","meaning":"缺乏氧氣","examples":[{"en":"Items are preserved because of a lack of oxygen.","zh":"物品因缺乏氧氣而被保存。"},{"en":"A lack of oxygen means there is little or not enough oxygen.","zh":"lack of oxygen 指氧氣很少或不足。"},{"en":"A lack of oxygen slows the decay of plants and wood.","zh":"缺乏氧氣會減慢植物和木材腐爛。"},{"en":"In deep wet peat, a lack of oxygen can preserve ancient objects.","zh":"在深層濕泥炭中，缺乏氧氣可以保存古代物件。"},{"en":"This phrase names one condition that helps objects survive.","zh":"這個短語指出幫助物件保存的一種條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in shape","meaning":"在形狀上","examples":[{"en":"The houses were rectangular in shape.","zh":"房屋在形狀上是長方形的。"},{"en":"In shape describes the form or outline of something.","zh":"in shape 用來描述某物的形態或輪廓。"},{"en":"The old field was square in shape.","zh":"那片舊田地在形狀上是正方形的。"},{"en":"A table that is round in shape may suit group discussion.","zh":"在形狀上為圓形的桌子可能適合小組討論。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe what something looks like physically.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述某物的實際外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"used for storage","meaning":"用於儲存","examples":[{"en":"Pots were used for storage and lighting.","zh":"陶罐用於儲存和照明。"},{"en":"Used for storage means used to keep things safely for later use.","zh":"used for storage 指用來安全保存物品以供之後使用。"},{"en":"Ancient pots were used for storage of grain and dried food.","zh":"古代陶罐用於儲存穀物和乾糧。"},{"en":"A box used for storage should protect items from damage.","zh":"用於儲存的箱子應保護物品免受損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase explains one practical function of an object.","zh":"這個短語解釋物件的一個實際功能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"large enough to support","meaning":"大到足以供養","examples":[{"en":"Each field was large enough to support a big family.","zh":"每塊田地都大到足以供養一個大家庭。"},{"en":"Large enough to support means big or productive enough to provide what is needed.","zh":"large enough to support 指大小或產量足以提供所需。"},{"en":"The farm was large enough to support two families.","zh":"那個農場大到足以供養兩個家庭。"},{"en":"A small garden is not large enough to support a whole household.","zh":"小花園不夠大，無法供養整個家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase connects size with survival or practical use.","zh":"這個短語把大小與生存或實際用途連接起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"restrict the grazing of animals","meaning":"限制動物放牧","examples":[{"en":"The fields were probably used to restrict the grazing of animals.","zh":"這些田地很可能用來限制動物放牧。"},{"en":"To restrict the grazing of animals means to control where animals can feed on grass.","zh":"restrict the grazing of animals 指控制動物可在哪裡吃草。"},{"en":"Stone walls can restrict the grazing of animals to one field.","zh":"石牆可以把動物放牧限制在一塊田地內。"},{"en":"Farmers restrict grazing to prevent animals from damaging young plants.","zh":"農民限制放牧，以防動物破壞幼苗。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how field boundaries controlled animal movement.","zh":"這個短語解釋田界如何控制動物活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"evidence of structures","meaning":"建築物的證據","examples":[{"en":"There is no evidence of structures to house animals.","zh":"沒有安置動物的建築物證據。"},{"en":"Evidence of structures means signs or remains showing that buildings once existed.","zh":"evidence of structures 指顯示建築曾存在的跡象或遺跡。"},{"en":"Archaeologists looked for evidence of structures near the fields.","zh":"考古學家在田地附近尋找建築物的證據。"},{"en":"Stone foundations can be evidence of structures from an ancient settlement.","zh":"石地基可以是古代聚落建築物的證據。"},{"en":"Without evidence of structures, researchers may think animals stayed outdoors.","zh":"如果沒有建築物的證據，研究人員可能認為動物留在戶外。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"house animals","meaning":"安置動物","examples":[{"en":"No structures were found to house animals during winter.","zh":"沒有發現冬季用來安置動物的建築。"},{"en":"To house animals means to keep them inside a shelter or building.","zh":"house animals 指把動物安置在庇護所或建築物內。"},{"en":"Farmers use barns to house animals in cold weather.","zh":"農民在寒冷天氣使用穀倉安置動物。"},{"en":"If there are no buildings to house animals, they may graze outdoors all year.","zh":"如果沒有建築安置動物，牠們可能全年在戶外放牧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes providing animals with a place to stay.","zh":"這個短語描述為動物提供停留地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"reasons for the decline in","meaning":"……衰落的原因","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about reasons for the decline in farming.","zh":"這個問題問及農耕衰落的原因。"},{"en":"Reasons for the decline in something are causes that explain why it became weaker or less common.","zh":"reasons for the decline in something 指解釋某事變弱或減少的原因。"},{"en":"Researchers studied reasons for the decline in village populations.","zh":"研究人員研究村莊人口衰落的原因。"},{"en":"Poor soil was one reason for the decline in farming.","zh":"土壤貧瘠是農耕衰落的其中一個原因。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for causes behind a downward change.","zh":"這個短語要求說明下降變化背後的原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"soil quality","meaning":"土壤質素","examples":[{"en":"A decline in soil quality affected farming.","zh":"土壤質素下降影響了農耕。"},{"en":"Soil quality means how good soil is for growing plants.","zh":"soil quality 指土壤對植物生長有多適合。"},{"en":"Good soil quality helps crops grow strong and healthy.","zh":"良好土壤質素幫助農作物強壯健康地生長。"},{"en":"Too much farming can reduce soil quality over time.","zh":"過度耕作會隨時間降低土壤質素。"},{"en":"Farmers watch soil quality carefully because poor soil means smaller harvests.","zh":"農民仔細留意土壤質素，因為貧瘠土壤意味收成較少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"an increase in","meaning":"……的增加","examples":[{"en":"An increase in rain helped create the bog.","zh":"雨量的增加幫助形成沼澤。"},{"en":"An increase in something means a rise or growth in its amount, number, or level.","zh":"an increase in something 指某物的數量、數目或程度上升。"},{"en":"An increase in rainfall can make fields too wet for farming.","zh":"降雨量的增加可以令田地太濕而不適合耕作。"},{"en":"An increase in visitors may help a museum earn more money.","zh":"遊客數目的增加可能幫助博物館賺取更多收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an upward change.","zh":"這個短語描述向上的變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 5 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14}],"ielts/listening/Practice 6/task-1":[{"front":"I wanted to talk to you because","meaning":"我想跟你談談，因為……","examples":[{"en":"The woman wanted to talk to Colman because Josh had mentioned the guitar group.","zh":"那位女士想跟 Colman 談談，因為 Josh 提過吉他小組。"},{"en":"“I wanted to talk to you because...” introduces the reason for starting a conversation.","zh":"“I wanted to talk to you because...” 用來引出開始對話的原因。"},{"en":"A student may say, “I wanted to talk to you because I need help with the project.”","zh":"學生可能說：「我想跟你談談，因為我需要項目上的幫忙。」"},{"en":"Giving the reason first helps the listener understand why the conversation matters.","zh":"先給出原因有助聽者明白對話為何重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and useful when approaching someone with a purpose.","zh":"當你帶着目的接近某人時，這個短語有禮而實用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"join a guitar group","meaning":"加入吉他小組","examples":[{"en":"Colman joined a guitar group.","zh":"Colman 加入了一個吉他小組。"},{"en":"To join a guitar group means to become a member of a group that learns or plays guitar together.","zh":"join a guitar group 指成為一個一起學習或彈奏吉他的群組成員。"},{"en":"A beginner may join a guitar group to practise with other learners every week.","zh":"初學者可能加入吉他小組，每星期與其他學員一起練習。"},{"en":"Joining a group can make learning easier because people can encourage one another.","zh":"加入小組可以令學習更容易，因為大家可以互相鼓勵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking part in a music-learning community.","zh":"這個短語描述參與一個音樂學習社群。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sound really interesting","meaning":"聽起來很有趣","examples":[{"en":"The guitar group sounds really interesting.","zh":"這個吉他小組聽起來很有趣。"},{"en":"Sound really interesting means seem attractive or enjoyable based on what someone has heard.","zh":"sound really interesting 指根據聽到的資料，某事看似吸引或令人享受。"},{"en":"A cooking class may sound really interesting if students can make real dishes.","zh":"如果學生可以製作真正菜式，烹飪課可能聽起來很有趣。"},{"en":"When something sounds interesting, people may want to learn more or join it.","zh":"當某事聽起來有趣，人們可能想了解更多或參加。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a positive first reaction.","zh":"這個短語表達正面的第一反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"I’d really like to","meaning":"我真的很想……","examples":[{"en":"The woman says she would really like to learn guitar herself.","zh":"那位女士說她自己也真的很想學吉他。"},{"en":"“I’d really like to...” means I strongly want to do something.","zh":"“I’d really like to...” 指我強烈想做某事。"},{"en":"A student may say, “I’d really like to join the drama club this year.”","zh":"學生可能說：「我今年真的很想加入戲劇學會。」"},{"en":"The word “really” makes the wish sound stronger and more sincere.","zh":"“really” 令願望聽起來更強烈和真誠。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and natural when expressing interest.","zh":"表達興趣時，這個短語有禮而自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"learn myself","meaning":"我自己也學","examples":[{"en":"The woman would really like to learn guitar herself.","zh":"那位女士自己也真的很想學吉他。"},{"en":"Learn myself means learn personally, rather than only watching or hearing about someone else doing it.","zh":"learn myself 指親自學習，而不只是看或聽別人做。"},{"en":"A parent may watch a child swim and decide to learn swimming herself.","zh":"家長看見孩子游泳後，可能決定自己也學游泳。"},{"en":"Wanting to learn yourself shows personal interest and motivation.","zh":"想自己也學，顯示個人興趣和動機。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the speaker also wants to take part.","zh":"這個短語強調說話者也想參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"why don’t you...?","meaning":"你為甚麼不……？","examples":[{"en":"Colman asks, “Why don’t you come along?”","zh":"Colman 問：「你為甚麼不一起來？」"},{"en":"“Why don’t you...?” is a friendly way to make a suggestion.","zh":"“Why don’t you...?” 是友善地提出建議的方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “Why don’t you try writing the answer in simpler words?”","zh":"老師可能說：「你為甚麼不用較簡單的字寫答案？」"},{"en":"This phrase sounds softer than giving an order.","zh":"這個短語比直接命令聽起來更柔和。"},{"en":"It is useful when inviting someone to do something.","zh":"邀請某人做某事時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"come along","meaning":"一起來；一同參加","examples":[{"en":"Colman invites the woman to come along to the guitar group.","zh":"Colman 邀請那位女士一起來參加吉他小組。"},{"en":"To come along means to go somewhere with someone or join an activity.","zh":"come along 指與某人一起去某處，或參與某活動。"},{"en":"A student may ask a friend to come along to a school concert.","zh":"學生可能邀請朋友一起去學校音樂會。"},{"en":"Coming along can make a new activity feel less frightening.","zh":"一同參加可以令新活動感覺沒那麼可怕。"},{"en":"This phrase is friendly and informal.","zh":"這個短語友善而口語化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"there’s room for","meaning":"有空間容納……","examples":[{"en":"Colman is sure there is room for one more person.","zh":"Colman 確定還有空間容納多一個人。"},{"en":"There’s room for someone means there is enough space or capacity for that person to join.","zh":"there’s room for someone 指有足夠空間或名額讓那人加入。"},{"en":"A teacher may say there is room for two more students in the workshop.","zh":"老師可能說工作坊還有空間容納多兩名學生。"},{"en":"If there is room for one more person, joining is still possible.","zh":"如果還有空間容納多一個人，加入仍然可能。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to physical space or group capacity.","zh":"這個短語可以指實際空間，也可以指小組名額。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one more person","meaning":"多一個人","examples":[{"en":"The guitar group probably has room for one more person.","zh":"這個吉他小組大概還有空間容納多一個人。"},{"en":"One more person means one additional person beyond the people already included.","zh":"one more person 指在已有的人之外再多一個人。"},{"en":"A taxi may have space for one more person if only three passengers are inside.","zh":"如果的士內只有三名乘客，可能還可以坐多一個人。"},{"en":"Adding one more person can change group size, cost, or seating arrangements.","zh":"加多一個人會改變小組人數、成本或座位安排。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about limits or capacity.","zh":"討論限制或容量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"run the sessions","meaning":"負責課堂；主持活動","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks who runs the sessions.","zh":"那位女士問誰負責課堂。"},{"en":"To run the sessions means to organise and lead the classes or meetings.","zh":"run the sessions 指組織並帶領課堂或聚會。"},{"en":"A coach may run training sessions for a school football team.","zh":"教練可能為學校足球隊主持訓練活動。"},{"en":"The person who runs the sessions decides what activities happen and when.","zh":"負責活動的人決定進行甚麼活動和何時進行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes responsibility for leading regular activities.","zh":"這個短語描述帶領定期活動的責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"coordinator","meaning":"協調員","examples":[{"en":"Gary Mathieson is the coordinator of the guitar group.","zh":"Gary Mathieson 是吉他小組的協調員。"},{"en":"A coordinator is a person who organises people, times, places, and activities.","zh":"coordinator 指負責組織人員、時間、地點和活動的人。"},{"en":"A school trip coordinator checks transport, forms, and meeting points.","zh":"學校旅行協調員會檢查交通、表格和集合地點。"},{"en":"A good coordinator helps a group run smoothly.","zh":"好的協調員幫助小組順利運作。"},{"en":"This word describes an organising role, not necessarily the main teacher.","zh":"這個字描述組織角色，不一定是主要老師。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"let me write that down","meaning":"讓我記下來","examples":[{"en":"The woman says, “Let me write that down.”","zh":"那位女士說：「讓我記下來。」"},{"en":"Let me write that down means allow me to record the information so I do not forget it.","zh":"let me write that down 指讓我把資料寫下來，以免忘記。"},{"en":"A student may say this when a teacher gives an important website address.","zh":"老師給出重要網站地址時，學生可能這樣說。"},{"en":"Writing information down helps prevent mistakes in names, times, or places.","zh":"記下資料有助避免姓名、時間或地點出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone gives details worth remembering.","zh":"當別人提供值得記住的細節時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"spell his surname","meaning":"拼出他的姓氏","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks how to spell Gary’s surname.","zh":"那位女士問 Gary 的姓氏怎樣拼寫。"},{"en":"To spell his surname means to say the letters of his family name in order.","zh":"spell his surname 指按次序說出他的姓氏字母。"},{"en":"A receptionist may ask a visitor to spell his surname before checking an appointment.","zh":"接待員在查預約前，可能要求訪客拼出姓氏。"},{"en":"Spelling a surname prevents mistakes when names sound unfamiliar.","zh":"拼出姓氏可以避免不熟悉名字出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for names, forms, and contact details.","zh":"這個短語適合用於姓名、表格和聯絡資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be actually retired","meaning":"其實已經退休","examples":[{"en":"Gary is actually retired.","zh":"Gary 其實已經退休。"},{"en":"Be actually retired means in fact no longer working full-time because one has left regular employment.","zh":"be actually retired 指事實上已離開正式工作，不再全職工作。"},{"en":"A retired teacher may still help students in a community class.","zh":"退休老師仍可能在社區課程中幫助學生。"},{"en":"Someone can be retired but still active in hobbies, volunteering, or teaching.","zh":"一個人可以已退休，但仍活躍於嗜好、義工或教學。"},{"en":"The word “actually” corrects or adds surprising information.","zh":"“actually” 用來糾正或補充令人意外的資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"used to play in","meaning":"以前曾在……演奏","examples":[{"en":"Gary used to play in lots of bands.","zh":"Gary 以前曾在很多樂隊演奏。"},{"en":"Used to play in means regularly played as a member of something in the past but not necessarily now.","zh":"used to play in 指過去經常作為某組織成員演奏，但現在未必如此。"},{"en":"A musician may say he used to play in a school orchestra.","zh":"音樂人可能說自己以前曾在學校管弦樂團演奏。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a past habit or experience.","zh":"這個短語顯示過去習慣或經驗。"},{"en":"It helps explain why someone has musical knowledge now.","zh":"它幫助解釋某人現在為何有音樂知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lots of bands","meaning":"很多樂隊","examples":[{"en":"Gary used to play in lots of bands.","zh":"Gary 以前曾在很多樂隊演奏。"},{"en":"Lots of bands means many different music groups.","zh":"lots of bands 指許多不同音樂組合。"},{"en":"A guitarist who has played in lots of bands may know many musical styles.","zh":"曾在很多樂隊演奏的吉他手，可能認識許多音樂風格。"},{"en":"Playing in many bands can give someone confidence and performance experience.","zh":"在許多樂隊演奏可以給人信心和表演經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and means a large number of bands.","zh":"這個短語較口語，意思是大量樂隊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"how long have you been going?","meaning":"你去了多久？","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks Colman how long he has been going to the group.","zh":"那位女士問 Colman 他去了小組多久。"},{"en":"How long have you been going? asks about the length of time someone has attended an activity.","zh":"How long have you been going? 用來詢問某人參加某活動已有多久。"},{"en":"A student may ask, “How long have you been going to this piano class?”","zh":"學生可能問：「你上這個鋼琴班多久了？」"},{"en":"This question helps the speaker understand someone’s level of experience.","zh":"這個問題幫助說話者了解某人的經驗程度。"},{"en":"It is common when discussing clubs, courses, or regular meetings.","zh":"討論學會、課程或定期聚會時，這句很常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"about a month now","meaning":"現在大約一個月","examples":[{"en":"Colman has been going to the group for about a month now.","zh":"Colman 參加這個小組現在大約一個月了。"},{"en":"About a month now means roughly one month up to the present time.","zh":"about a month now 指到目前為止大約一個月。"},{"en":"A new worker may say she has been at the company for about a month now.","zh":"新員工可能說自己在公司工作現在大約一個月。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate time, not an exact number of days.","zh":"這個短語給出大約時間，而不是精確日數。"},{"en":"It is useful in casual conversation.","zh":"它適合日常對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"could you play anything?","meaning":"你以前會彈甚麼嗎？","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether Colman could play anything before he started.","zh":"那位女士問 Colman 開始前是否會彈甚麼。"},{"en":"Could you play anything? asks whether someone had any ability to play music before learning.","zh":"Could you play anything? 詢問某人在學習前是否已有任何演奏能力。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask a new student, “Could you play anything before this course?”","zh":"老師可能問新學生：「你上這課程前會彈甚麼嗎？」"},{"en":"The question helps judge whether someone is a complete beginner.","zh":"這個問題幫助判斷某人是否完全初學。"},{"en":"It is a natural question before joining a music class.","zh":"加入音樂課前，這是自然的問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"before you started","meaning":"在你開始之前","examples":[{"en":"Colman knew only a few chords before he started.","zh":"Colman 在開始之前只懂幾個和弦。"},{"en":"Before you started means before you began the activity or course.","zh":"before you started 指在你開始某活動或課程之前。"},{"en":"A student may know no French before she starts a beginner class.","zh":"學生在開始初級法文班前，可能完全不懂法文。"},{"en":"Comparing before and after helps show progress.","zh":"比較開始前和之後，有助顯示進步。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the time before learning begins.","zh":"這個短語標示學習開始前的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a few chords","meaning":"幾個和弦","examples":[{"en":"Colman knew a few chords before joining the group.","zh":"Colman 加入小組前懂幾個和弦。"},{"en":"A few chords means a small number of chord shapes or combinations of notes.","zh":"a few chords 指少量和弦指法或音符組合。"},{"en":"A beginner guitarist may learn a few chords before playing a simple song.","zh":"初學吉他者可能先學幾個和弦，再彈簡單歌曲。"},{"en":"Knowing a few chords gives a learner a small starting point.","zh":"懂幾個和弦給學習者一個小小起點。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests limited but useful musical knowledge.","zh":"這個短語暗示有限但有用的音樂知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"that was all","meaning":"僅此而已","examples":[{"en":"Colman knew a few chords, but that was all.","zh":"Colman 懂幾個和弦，但僅此而已。"},{"en":"That was all means there was nothing more beyond what was just mentioned.","zh":"that was all 指除了剛才提到的內容外，再沒有更多。"},{"en":"A student may say, “I knew the title of the book, but that was all.”","zh":"學生可能說：「我只知道那本書的書名，僅此而已。」"},{"en":"This phrase shows that someone’s knowledge or ability was limited.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人的知識或能力有限。"},{"en":"It often follows a small amount of information.","zh":"它常接在少量資料之後。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"better than me","meaning":"比我強","examples":[{"en":"The woman worries that everyone will be better than her.","zh":"那位女士擔心每個人都會比她強。"},{"en":"Better than me means having more skill or ability than I have.","zh":"better than me 指技能或能力比我更高。"},{"en":"A beginner may worry that everyone in the class will be better than him.","zh":"初學者可能擔心班中所有人都比自己強。"},{"en":"This worry can make people afraid to join a new activity.","zh":"這種擔心會令人害怕加入新活動。"},{"en":"The phrase compares one person’s ability with others.","zh":"這個短語把一個人的能力與別人比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"that’s what I thought too","meaning":"我當初也是這樣想","examples":[{"en":"Colman says that is what he thought too.","zh":"Colman 說他當初也是這樣想。"},{"en":"That’s what I thought too means I had the same idea or worry before.","zh":"that’s what I thought too 指我以前也有同樣想法或擔心。"},{"en":"A student may say this when a friend admits feeling nervous before a presentation.","zh":"朋友承認簡報前很緊張時，學生可能這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures someone that their feeling is normal.","zh":"這個短語讓對方放心，知道自己的感受很正常。"},{"en":"It creates connection through shared experience.","zh":"它透過共同經歷建立連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"first spoke to","meaning":"第一次與……交談","examples":[{"en":"Colman first spoke to Gary on the phone.","zh":"Colman 第一次與 Gary 交談是在電話中。"},{"en":"First spoke to someone means talked to that person for the first time.","zh":"first spoke to someone 指第一次與某人說話。"},{"en":"A student may first speak to a new tutor during a short phone call.","zh":"學生可能在一次短電話中第一次與新補習老師交談。"},{"en":"The first conversation can give someone confidence to join a course.","zh":"第一次對話可以給人信心去參加課程。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the beginning of communication.","zh":"這個短語指出溝通的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on the phone","meaning":"在電話中","examples":[{"en":"Colman spoke to Gary on the phone.","zh":"Colman 在電話中與 Gary 交談。"},{"en":"On the phone means by telephone, not face to face.","zh":"on the phone 指透過電話，而不是面對面。"},{"en":"A parent may discuss a school trip with a teacher on the phone.","zh":"家長可能在電話中與老師討論學校旅行。"},{"en":"Phone conversations help people ask questions before meeting in person.","zh":"電話對話幫助人在親身見面前先發問。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the communication method.","zh":"這個短語描述溝通方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a class for beginners","meaning":"初學者課程","examples":[{"en":"Gary said it was a class for beginners.","zh":"Gary 說那是初學者課程。"},{"en":"A class for beginners is a course designed for people with little or no experience.","zh":"class for beginners 指為幾乎沒有經驗或完全沒有經驗的人設計的課程。"},{"en":"A beginner swimming class teaches basic breathing and floating first.","zh":"初學游泳班會先教基本呼吸和漂浮。"},{"en":"Such classes move slowly so new learners do not feel lost.","zh":"這類課程進度較慢，讓新學員不會迷失。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures people who are worried about being behind.","zh":"這個短語能安慰擔心落後的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"worry that","meaning":"擔心……","examples":[{"en":"Colman worried that everyone would be better than him.","zh":"Colman 擔心每個人都會比他強。"},{"en":"Worry that means feel anxious about a possible situation.","zh":"worry that 指對某個可能情況感到焦慮。"},{"en":"A student may worry that she will forget her lines in a school play.","zh":"學生可能擔心自己在校劇中忘記台詞。"},{"en":"Worrying can stop people from trying something new.","zh":"擔心會阻止人嘗試新事物。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the thing someone is afraid may happen.","zh":"這個短語引出某人害怕可能發生的事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"equally hopeless","meaning":"一樣毫無基礎；一樣不濟","examples":[{"en":"Colman jokes that they are all equally hopeless.","zh":"Colman 開玩笑說他們全都一樣不濟。"},{"en":"Equally hopeless means everyone is bad at something to a similar degree.","zh":"equally hopeless 指每個人在某方面都差不多一樣差。"},{"en":"Three beginners may be equally hopeless at dancing on the first day.","zh":"三個初學者第一天跳舞時，可能一樣毫無基礎。"},{"en":"The phrase can make people feel less embarrassed because nobody is much better.","zh":"這個短語可以令人沒那麼尷尬，因為沒有人明顯更好。"},{"en":"It is often used humorously, not cruelly.","zh":"它常帶幽默意味，而不是刻薄。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"that’s reassuring","meaning":"那令人放心","examples":[{"en":"The woman says that Colman’s comment is reassuring.","zh":"那位女士說 Colman 的話令人放心。"},{"en":"That’s reassuring means that makes me feel less worried.","zh":"that’s reassuring 指那令我沒那麼擔心。"},{"en":"A student may say “That’s reassuring” when a teacher says the test will be simple.","zh":"老師說測驗會很簡單時，學生可能說「那令人放心」。"},{"en":"Reassuring information reduces fear before someone tries something new.","zh":"令人放心的資料會減少人在嘗試新事物前的恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase shows relief.","zh":"這個短語表達安心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"where do you meet?","meaning":"你們在哪裏聚會／上課？","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks where the guitar group meets.","zh":"那位女士問吉他小組在哪裏聚會。"},{"en":"Where do you meet? asks for the place where a group gathers regularly.","zh":"Where do you meet? 用來詢問小組定期集合的地方。"},{"en":"A student may ask a debate club, “Where do you meet after school?”","zh":"學生可能問辯論學會：「你們放學後在哪裏聚會？」"},{"en":"Knowing the meeting place helps someone decide whether joining is convenient.","zh":"知道聚會地點有助某人決定參加是否方便。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for clubs, classes, and activities.","zh":"這個短語適用於學會、課程和活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"when I joined the group","meaning":"我加入小組時","examples":[{"en":"When Colman joined the group, they were meeting at Gary’s house.","zh":"Colman 加入小組時，他們在 Gary 家裏聚會。"},{"en":"When I joined the group refers to the time when someone first became a member.","zh":"when I joined the group 指某人剛成為成員的時候。"},{"en":"When I joined the club, there were only six members.","zh":"我加入學會時，只有六名成員。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces how things were at the beginning.","zh":"這個短語常引出事情一開始的情況。"},{"en":"It helps compare the past situation with the present one.","zh":"它幫助比較過去情況與現在情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as the group got bigger","meaning":"隨着小組人數增加","examples":[{"en":"As the group got bigger, Gary booked a room at the college.","zh":"隨着小組人數增加，Gary 在學院預訂了一個房間。"},{"en":"As the group got bigger means while or because the number of members increased.","zh":"as the group got bigger 指隨着或因為成員人數增加。"},{"en":"As a study group gets bigger, students may need a larger classroom.","zh":"隨着學習小組人數增加，學生可能需要更大的課室。"},{"en":"Growth can create practical needs, such as more space or better organisation.","zh":"增長會帶來實際需要，例如更多空間或更好組織。"},{"en":"This phrase links increasing size with a change in arrangement.","zh":"這個短語把人數增加與安排改變連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"book a room","meaning":"預訂房間","examples":[{"en":"Gary decided to book a room at the college.","zh":"Gary 決定在學院預訂一個房間。"},{"en":"To book a room means to reserve it for a particular time and purpose.","zh":"book a room 指為特定時間和用途預留房間。"},{"en":"A teacher may book a room for an after-school drama rehearsal.","zh":"老師可能為放學後戲劇排練預訂房間。"},{"en":"Booking a room prevents other groups from using it at the same time.","zh":"預訂房間可以防止其他小組同時使用。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when organising meetings or classes.","zh":"組織會議或課堂時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at the college in town","meaning":"在鎮上的學院","examples":[{"en":"The guitar group now meets at the college in town.","zh":"吉他小組現在在鎮上的學院聚會。"},{"en":"At the college in town means at the local college located in the town area.","zh":"at the college in town 指在位於鎮中心或市鎮範圍內的本地學院。"},{"en":"A night class may be held at the college in town because it is easy to reach.","zh":"夜校課程可能在鎮上的學院舉行，因為交通方便。"},{"en":"A central location can make it easier for more people to attend.","zh":"中心地點可以令更多人較容易參加。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear public meeting place.","zh":"這個短語給出清楚的公共聚會地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"prefer going there","meaning":"比較喜歡去那裏","examples":[{"en":"Colman prefers going to the college.","zh":"Colman 比較喜歡去學院。"},{"en":"Prefer going there means like going to that place more than another place.","zh":"prefer going there 指比起其他地方，更喜歡去那裏。"},{"en":"A student may prefer going to the library because it is quieter than home.","zh":"學生可能比較喜歡去圖書館，因為那裏比家裏安靜。"},{"en":"People prefer places that are convenient, comfortable, or familiar.","zh":"人們會偏好方便、舒適或熟悉的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a choice between places.","zh":"這個短語表達地點之間的選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"I know that place","meaning":"我知道那個地方","examples":[{"en":"The woman says she knows that place.","zh":"那位女士說她知道那個地方。"},{"en":"I know that place means I am familiar with that location.","zh":"I know that place 指我熟悉那個地點。"},{"en":"Someone may say “I know that place” after hearing the name of an old café.","zh":"聽到一間舊咖啡店的名字後，有人可能說「我知道那個地方」。"},{"en":"Recognising a place can make directions easier to understand.","zh":"認得某地點可以令路線較容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase shows familiarity with a location.","zh":"這個短語顯示對某地點熟悉。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"used to go there for","meaning":"以前常去那裏上……","examples":[{"en":"The woman used to go there for tap dancing classes.","zh":"那位女士以前常去那裏上踢踏舞班。"},{"en":"Used to go there for something means regularly went there in the past for that activity.","zh":"used to go there for something 指過去經常去那裏參加某活動。"},{"en":"A student may say she used to go there for swimming lessons.","zh":"學生可能說她以前常去那裏上游泳課。"},{"en":"This phrase links a place with a past routine.","zh":"這個短語把地點與過去習慣連繫起來。"},{"en":"It shows that the activity happened before but may not happen now.","zh":"它顯示活動以前發生，但現在未必繼續。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tap dancing classes","meaning":"踢踏舞班","examples":[{"en":"The woman used to take tap dancing classes at the college.","zh":"那位女士以前在學院上踢踏舞班。"},{"en":"Tap dancing classes are lessons where students learn a dance style that makes rhythm with metal taps on shoes.","zh":"tap dancing classes 指學生學習用鞋底金屬片踏出節奏的舞蹈課。"},{"en":"Children may take tap dancing classes to improve rhythm and coordination.","zh":"孩子可能上踢踏舞班來改善節奏感和協調能力。"},{"en":"These classes often involve listening carefully to beats.","zh":"這些課堂通常需要仔細聆聽拍子。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific type of dance lesson.","zh":"這個短語指出一種特定舞蹈課。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"secondary school","meaning":"中學","examples":[{"en":"The woman went there when she was at secondary school.","zh":"那位女士在中學時曾去那裏。"},{"en":"Secondary school is the school stage for older children and teenagers after primary school.","zh":"secondary school 指小學之後，較年長兒童和青少年就讀的學校階段。"},{"en":"A student may join clubs and choose subjects at secondary school.","zh":"學生在中學可能加入學會並選擇科目。"},{"en":"Memories from secondary school can make an old place feel familiar.","zh":"中學時期的記憶可以令舊地方感覺熟悉。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a stage of education.","zh":"這個短語指出一個教育階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"I haven’t been there since then","meaning":"從那時起我就沒有去過那裏","examples":[{"en":"The woman has not been there since secondary school.","zh":"那位女士自中學以來就沒有去過那裏。"},{"en":"I haven’t been there since then means I have not visited that place from that past time until now.","zh":"I haven’t been there since then 指從過去那個時間到現在，我都沒有再去過那裏。"},{"en":"A person may say this about a park she last visited as a child.","zh":"一個人可能這樣說一個童年後就沒再去過的公園。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a long gap between visits.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩次到訪之間相隔很久。"},{"en":"It often carries a feeling of memory or nostalgia.","zh":"它常帶有回憶或懷舊感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"can’t remember what road it’s on","meaning":"記不起它在哪條路上","examples":[{"en":"The woman cannot remember what road the college is on.","zh":"那位女士記不起學院在哪條路上。"},{"en":"Can’t remember what road it’s on means cannot recall the street where a place is located.","zh":"can’t remember what road it’s on 指記不起某地點位於哪條街道。"},{"en":"A visitor may know a restaurant but cannot remember what road it is on.","zh":"訪客可能知道一間餐廳，但記不起它在哪條路上。"},{"en":"Forgetting the road can make directions unclear.","zh":"忘記街道名稱會令路線不清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when asking for location details.","zh":"詢問地點細節時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at the bottom of","meaning":"在……盡頭","examples":[{"en":"The college is at the bottom of New Street.","zh":"學院在 New Street 的盡頭。"},{"en":"At the bottom of a street means at the lower end or far end of that street.","zh":"at the bottom of a street 指在街道較低的一端或盡頭位置。"},{"en":"A shop may be at the bottom of a hill road near the bus stop.","zh":"商店可能在山路盡頭、巴士站附近。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people picture where a place is along a road.","zh":"這個短語幫助人想像某地在道路上的位置。"},{"en":"It is often used when giving directions.","zh":"它常用於指路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"city roundabout","meaning":"市區迴旋處","examples":[{"en":"The college is near the city roundabout.","zh":"學院在市區迴旋處附近。"},{"en":"A city roundabout is a circular road junction where traffic moves around a central island.","zh":"city roundabout 指市區內車輛圍繞中央圓島行駛的環形路口。"},{"en":"Drivers slow down when approaching a busy city roundabout.","zh":"司機接近繁忙市區迴旋處時會減速。"},{"en":"Roundabouts are useful landmarks when giving directions.","zh":"指路時，迴旋處是有用地標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a road feature in town.","zh":"這個短語描述鎮上的道路設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on the first floor","meaning":"在一樓","examples":[{"en":"The guitar group is on the first floor.","zh":"吉他小組在一樓。"},{"en":"On the first floor means located one level above the ground floor in British English.","zh":"on the first floor 在英式英語中通常指位於地下上一層。"},{"en":"A classroom on the first floor may require students to use stairs or a lift.","zh":"位於一樓的課室可能需要學生使用樓梯或升降機。"},{"en":"Giving the floor number helps visitors find the room more easily.","zh":"說出樓層號碼有助訪客更容易找到房間。"},{"en":"This phrase gives indoor location information.","zh":"這個短語提供室內位置資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"when do you meet?","meaning":"你們甚麼時候聚會／上課？","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks when the guitar group meets.","zh":"那位女士問吉他小組甚麼時候聚會。"},{"en":"When do you meet? asks for the time or day of a regular meeting.","zh":"When do you meet? 用來詢問定期聚會的時間或日子。"},{"en":"A student may ask a club, “When do you meet after school?”","zh":"學生可能問學會：「你們放學後甚麼時候聚會？」"},{"en":"Knowing the meeting time helps someone decide whether they can attend.","zh":"知道聚會時間有助某人決定是否能參加。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for arranging activities.","zh":"安排活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at the weekend","meaning":"在週末","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether the group meets at the weekend.","zh":"那位女士問小組是否在週末聚會。"},{"en":"At the weekend means on Saturday, Sunday, or both.","zh":"at the weekend 指在星期六、星期日或兩天。"},{"en":"Many students join sports activities at the weekend because they have no school.","zh":"許多學生在週末參加體育活動，因為不用上學。"},{"en":"Weekend meetings may be easier for people who work during the week.","zh":"對平日工作的人來說，週末聚會可能較方便。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the end of the week.","zh":"這個短語指一星期的尾段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"meet on Thursdays","meaning":"逢星期四聚會","examples":[{"en":"The guitar group meets on Thursdays.","zh":"吉他小組逢星期四聚會。"},{"en":"Meet on Thursdays means gather every Thursday or regularly on Thursday.","zh":"meet on Thursdays 指每逢星期四或定期在星期四聚會。"},{"en":"A reading club may meet on Thursdays after school.","zh":"閱讀學會可能逢星期四放學後聚會。"},{"en":"A fixed weekday makes it easier for members to plan ahead.","zh":"固定星期幾可以令成員更容易預先計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a regular schedule.","zh":"這個短語給出定期時間表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"it used to be at","meaning":"以前是在……","examples":[{"en":"The class used to be at 10:30.","zh":"課堂以前是在10時30分。"},{"en":"It used to be at a time means it was scheduled then in the past but has changed now.","zh":"it used to be at a time 指過去安排在某時間，但現在已改變。"},{"en":"The school bus used to be at 7:20, but now it comes earlier.","zh":"校巴以前是在7時20分，但現在更早來。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain a change in timetable.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋時間表的改變。"},{"en":"It compares the old arrangement with the current one.","zh":"它比較舊安排與現時安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"suit me really well","meaning":"非常適合我","examples":[{"en":"The 10:30 class suited Colman really well.","zh":"10時30分的課堂非常適合 Colman。"},{"en":"Suit me really well means be very convenient or appropriate for my needs.","zh":"suit me really well 指非常方便或很符合我的需要。"},{"en":"A morning lesson may suit a student really well if she studies best before lunch.","zh":"如果學生午飯前學習狀態最好，上午課可能非常適合她。"},{"en":"When a time suits someone well, they can attend without difficulty.","zh":"當某時間很適合某人，他就能較容易出席。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses personal convenience.","zh":"這個短語表達個人方便程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the class before us","meaning":"我們之前的一班","examples":[{"en":"The class before them asked to use the room longer.","zh":"他們之前的一班要求使用房間久一點。"},{"en":"The class before us means the group that uses the room immediately before our group.","zh":"the class before us 指在我們小組之前立即使用房間的那一班。"},{"en":"If the class before us finishes late, we may have to wait outside.","zh":"如果我們之前的一班遲下課，我們可能要在外面等。"},{"en":"The schedule of the previous class can affect the next class.","zh":"前一班的時間安排會影響下一班。"},{"en":"This phrase describes order in a timetable.","zh":"這個短語描述時間表中的先後次序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have the room for","meaning":"使用房間……","examples":[{"en":"The class before them wanted to have the room for an extra thirty minutes.","zh":"他們之前的一班想額外使用房間三十分鐘。"},{"en":"Have the room for a period means use or reserve the room for that length of time.","zh":"have the room for a period 指在某段時間內使用或預留該房間。"},{"en":"A drama club may have the hall for two hours before a performance.","zh":"戲劇學會可能在表演前使用禮堂兩小時。"},{"en":"If one group has the room longer, the next group may need to start later.","zh":"如果某小組使用房間久一點，下一組可能需要較遲開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes control or use of a space for a time.","zh":"這個短語描述在某段時間內使用空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an extra thirty minutes","meaning":"額外三十分鐘","examples":[{"en":"The class before them asked for an extra thirty minutes.","zh":"他們之前的一班要求額外三十分鐘。"},{"en":"An extra thirty minutes means thirty more minutes in addition to the original time.","zh":"extra thirty minutes 指在原本時間之外再多三十分鐘。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students an extra thirty minutes to finish a difficult test.","zh":"老師可能給學生額外三十分鐘完成困難測驗。"},{"en":"Extra time for one group can affect the schedule of another group.","zh":"給一組額外時間可能影響另一組的時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase describes added time.","zh":"這個短語描述增加的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"I’d love to come","meaning":"我很想來","examples":[{"en":"The woman says she would love to come.","zh":"那位女士說她很想來。"},{"en":"I’d love to come means I would be very happy to attend or join.","zh":"I’d love to come 指我很高興出席或參加。"},{"en":"A student may say, “I’d love to come to your music performance.”","zh":"學生可能說：「我很想來看你的音樂表演。」"},{"en":"This phrase shows stronger enthusiasm than simply saying yes.","zh":"這個短語比單純說 yes 更有熱情。"},{"en":"It is warm and polite when accepting an invitation.","zh":"接受邀請時，它溫暖而有禮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"second-hand","meaning":"二手的","examples":[{"en":"The woman can buy a second-hand guitar.","zh":"那位女士可以買一把二手吉他。"},{"en":"Second-hand means previously owned or used by someone else.","zh":"second-hand 指以前由別人擁有或使用過的。"},{"en":"A student may buy a second-hand textbook to save money.","zh":"學生可能買二手教科書來省錢。"},{"en":"Buying second-hand items can be cheaper than buying new ones.","zh":"買二手物品可以比買全新物品便宜。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in shopping and classified advertisements.","zh":"這個短語常見於購物和分類廣告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"all sorts of","meaning":"各種各樣的","examples":[{"en":"The website sells all sorts of musical instruments.","zh":"該網站售賣各種各樣的樂器。"},{"en":"All sorts of means many different kinds of something.","zh":"all sorts of 指許多不同種類的某物。"},{"en":"A school fair may sell all sorts of snacks, toys, and books.","zh":"學校賣物會可能售賣各種各樣的小食、玩具和書。"},{"en":"A website with all sorts of items gives buyers more choice.","zh":"有各種各樣物品的網站給買家更多選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and stresses variety.","zh":"這個短語較口語，強調多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"guitars, violins and so on","meaning":"吉他、小提琴等等","examples":[{"en":"The website sells guitars, violins and so on.","zh":"該網站售賣吉他、小提琴等等。"},{"en":"Guitars, violins and so on means guitars, violins, and other similar musical instruments.","zh":"guitars, violins and so on 指吉他、小提琴，以及其他類似樂器。"},{"en":"A music shop may sell pianos, drums, flutes and so on.","zh":"音樂店可能售賣鋼琴、鼓、長笛等等。"},{"en":"“And so on” shows the list continues without naming every item.","zh":"“and so on” 顯示清單仍有其他項目，但不逐一說出。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving examples from a larger group.","zh":"從較大類別中舉例時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"find something there","meaning":"在那裏找到合適的東西","examples":[{"en":"Colman is sure the woman will find something on the website.","zh":"Colman 確定那位女士會在網站上找到合適的東西。"},{"en":"Find something there means discover or choose a suitable item in that place or website.","zh":"find something there 指在某地方或網站發現或選到合適物品。"},{"en":"A student looking for a used calculator may find something there in an online marketplace.","zh":"尋找二手計算機的學生，可能在網上市集找到合適的東西。"},{"en":"Having many options makes it more likely that someone can find what they need.","zh":"選項多會令某人更可能找到所需物品。"},{"en":"This phrase gives encouragement about searching.","zh":"這個短語給搜尋者鼓勵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a typical lesson","meaning":"典型課堂","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks what a typical lesson with Gary is like.","zh":"那位女士問 Gary 的典型課堂是怎樣的。"},{"en":"A typical lesson is a normal or usual lesson, not a special one.","zh":"typical lesson 指正常或平常的課堂，而不是特別課。"},{"en":"A typical English lesson may include reading, vocabulary, speaking, and homework.","zh":"典型英文課可能包括閱讀、詞彙、說話和功課。"},{"en":"Knowing a typical lesson helps new students understand what to expect.","zh":"知道典型課堂內容，有助新學生了解會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the regular pattern of a class.","zh":"這個短語描述課堂的常規模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"what is something like?","meaning":"……是怎樣的？","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks what a typical lesson with Gary is like.","zh":"那位女士問 Gary 的典型課堂是怎樣的。"},{"en":"“What is something like?” asks someone to describe the nature, style, or experience of something.","zh":"“What is something like?” 用來請人描述某事的性質、風格或經驗。"},{"en":"A student may ask, “What is the interview like?” before applying for a school team.","zh":"學生申請校隊前可能問：「面試是怎樣的？」"},{"en":"This question invites explanation rather than a simple yes or no answer.","zh":"這個問題要求解釋，而不是簡單的是或否。"},{"en":"It is useful when you want to imagine an unfamiliar experience.","zh":"當你想想像不熟悉的經驗時，這句很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"start by","meaning":"由……開始","examples":[{"en":"Gary always starts by getting students to tune their guitars.","zh":"Gary 總是由叫學生為吉他調音開始。"},{"en":"Start by means begin a process with a particular first step.","zh":"start by 指以某個特定第一步開始一個過程。"},{"en":"A teacher may start by reviewing last week’s homework.","zh":"老師可能由檢討上星期功課開始。"},{"en":"Starting with preparation can make the main activity easier.","zh":"由準備工作開始，可以令主要活動更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain the order of actions.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋行動次序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get someone to","meaning":"叫某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Gary gets the students to tune their guitars.","zh":"Gary 叫學生為吉他調音。"},{"en":"Get someone to do something means ask, persuade, or make someone do it.","zh":"get someone to do something 指要求、說服或令某人做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may get students to work in pairs for speaking practice.","zh":"老師可能叫學生二人一組做口語練習。"},{"en":"Getting learners to do a task helps them practise actively.","zh":"叫學員做任務，可以幫助他們主動練習。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on causing another person to act.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於令另一人行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tune our guitars","meaning":"為吉他調音","examples":[{"en":"The students tune their guitars at the start of the lesson.","zh":"學生在課堂開始時為吉他調音。"},{"en":"To tune our guitars means adjust the strings so they produce the correct notes.","zh":"tune our guitars 指調整琴弦，使它們發出正確音高。"},{"en":"A guitarist tunes the guitar before playing a song on stage.","zh":"吉他手上台彈歌前會先為吉他調音。"},{"en":"If guitars are not tuned, the music may sound wrong even when the fingers are correct.","zh":"如果吉他沒有調音，即使手指按對，音樂也可能聽起來不對。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important preparation before playing.","zh":"這個短語描述演奏前的重要準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"that takes about","meaning":"那大約需要……","examples":[{"en":"Tuning the guitars takes about five minutes.","zh":"為吉他調音大約需要五分鐘。"},{"en":"That takes about means that activity needs approximately a certain amount of time.","zh":"that takes about 指某活動大約需要某段時間。"},{"en":"Walking from the station to school takes about ten minutes.","zh":"從車站走到學校大約需要十分鐘。"},{"en":"Saying how long something takes helps people plan their schedule.","zh":"說明某事需時多久，有助人規劃時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate duration.","zh":"這個短語給出大約時長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"do it by ear","meaning":"憑耳朵聽來做","examples":[{"en":"Some students tune their guitars by ear.","zh":"有些學生憑耳朵聽來為吉他調音。"},{"en":"To do it by ear means to judge sound without using written notes or a device.","zh":"do it by ear 指不用樂譜或裝置，而是靠聽覺判斷聲音。"},{"en":"A singer may learn a melody by ear after hearing it several times.","zh":"歌手可能聽幾次旋律後，憑耳朵學會它。"},{"en":"Doing music by ear requires careful listening.","zh":"憑耳朵做音樂需要仔細聆聽。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using hearing as the guide.","zh":"這個短語描述用聽覺作指引。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"go round","meaning":"四處走動","examples":[{"en":"Gary goes round and helps the students tune their guitars.","zh":"Gary 四處走動，幫學生為吉他調音。"},{"en":"To go round means to move from person to person or place to place in a group.","zh":"go round 指在小組中從一個人或一個地方走到另一個。"},{"en":"A teacher may go round the classroom checking students’ work.","zh":"老師可能在課室四處走動，檢查學生功課。"},{"en":"Going round allows the teacher to give individual help.","zh":"四處走動能讓老師給予個別幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving around within a space.","zh":"這個短語描述在空間內移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"what we’re going to do","meaning":"我們將會做甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Gary tells the students what they are going to do in the lesson.","zh":"Gary 告訴學生課堂中他們將會做甚麼。"},{"en":"What we’re going to do means the activities planned for the near future.","zh":"what we’re going to do 指接下來計劃進行的活動。"},{"en":"A teacher may tell students what they are going to do before starting a science experiment.","zh":"老師開始科學實驗前，可能告訴學生將會做甚麼。"},{"en":"Clear plans help learners feel prepared.","zh":"清楚計劃能幫助學員感到有準備。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the lesson agenda.","zh":"這個短語引入課堂流程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"spend about ten minutes doing","meaning":"花大約十分鐘做……","examples":[{"en":"The students usually spend about ten minutes doing strumming.","zh":"學生通常花大約十分鐘做掃弦練習。"},{"en":"Spend about ten minutes doing something means use roughly ten minutes on that activity.","zh":"spend about ten minutes doing something 指用大約十分鐘進行某活動。"},{"en":"Students may spend about ten minutes reviewing vocabulary before a test.","zh":"學生可能在測驗前花大約十分鐘重溫詞彙。"},{"en":"Setting a time limit helps a class move through different activities.","zh":"設定時間限制有助課堂進行不同活動。"},{"en":"This phrase combines time with an activity.","zh":"這個短語把時間與活動結合。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"strumming","meaning":"掃弦","examples":[{"en":"The students practise strumming at the start of the lesson.","zh":"學生在課堂開始時練習掃弦。"},{"en":"Strumming is brushing the fingers or thumb across guitar strings to make chords sound.","zh":"strumming 指用手指或拇指掃過吉他弦，使和弦發聲。"},{"en":"Beginners often practise strumming slowly before playing a song.","zh":"初學者常在彈歌前慢慢練習掃弦。"},{"en":"Good strumming helps a song keep rhythm.","zh":"好的掃弦幫助歌曲保持節奏。"},{"en":"This word describes a basic guitar-playing technique.","zh":"這個字描述基本吉他技巧。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"what are they called?","meaning":"那些叫甚麼？","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks, “What are they called?”","zh":"那位女士問：「那些叫甚麼？」"},{"en":"What are they called? asks for the name of something.","zh":"What are they called? 用來詢問某物的名稱。"},{"en":"A student may point to science tools and ask, “What are they called?”","zh":"學生可能指着科學工具問：「那些叫甚麼？」"},{"en":"This question is useful when someone recognises an object but does not know its name.","zh":"當某人認得物件但不知道名稱時，這問題很有用。"},{"en":"It helps learners build vocabulary.","zh":"它幫助學習者建立詞彙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"plectrums","meaning":"撥片","examples":[{"en":"The woman asks whether the students use plectrums.","zh":"那位女士問學生是否使用撥片。"},{"en":"Plectrums are small flat pieces used to pluck or strum guitar strings.","zh":"plectrums 指用來撥或掃吉他弦的小扁片。"},{"en":"A guitarist may hold a plectrum between the thumb and finger.","zh":"吉他手可能用拇指和手指夾着撥片。"},{"en":"Plectrums can make the sound sharper than using fingers alone.","zh":"撥片可以令聲音比單用手指更清脆。"},{"en":"This word names a common guitar accessory.","zh":"這個字指出常見吉他配件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"just use our thumbs","meaning":"只用拇指","examples":[{"en":"The students just use their thumbs for strumming.","zh":"學生掃弦時只用拇指。"},{"en":"Just use our thumbs means use only the thumbs, without a plectrum or other fingers.","zh":"just use our thumbs 指只使用拇指，不用撥片或其他手指。"},{"en":"A beginner may just use the thumb because it feels simpler.","zh":"初學者可能只用拇指，因為感覺較簡單。"},{"en":"Using thumbs can make strumming less technical at first.","zh":"用拇指可以令一開始的掃弦沒那麼技術化。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a simple method.","zh":"這個短語強調簡單方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"much easier","meaning":"容易得多","examples":[{"en":"The woman thinks using thumbs sounds much easier.","zh":"那位女士覺得用拇指聽起來容易得多。"},{"en":"Much easier means a lot less difficult.","zh":"much easier 指困難程度低很多。"},{"en":"Typing notes may be much easier than writing them by hand for some students.","zh":"對有些學生來說，打字記筆記可能比手寫容易得多。"},{"en":"If a method is much easier, beginners may feel more confident trying it.","zh":"如果方法容易得多，初學者可能更有信心嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase compares levels of difficulty.","zh":"這個短語比較難易程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"remind someone where to","meaning":"提醒某人在甚麼位置……","examples":[{"en":"Gary reminds the students where to put their fingers.","zh":"Gary 提醒學生應把手指放在哪裏。"},{"en":"To remind someone where to do something means to help them remember the correct place or position.","zh":"remind someone where to do something 指幫助某人記起正確位置。"},{"en":"A piano teacher may remind a child where to place her hands.","zh":"鋼琴老師可能提醒孩子把手放在哪裏。"},{"en":"Reminders are useful when learners forget steps during practice.","zh":"當學員在練習中忘記步驟時，提醒很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes guidance that corrects memory.","zh":"這個短語描述糾正記憶的指導。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"put our fingers","meaning":"放手指","examples":[{"en":"Gary reminds the students where to put their fingers for each chord.","zh":"Gary 提醒學生每個和弦應把手指放在哪裏。"},{"en":"Put our fingers means place the fingers in particular positions.","zh":"put our fingers 指把手指放在特定位置。"},{"en":"A guitarist must put the fingers on the correct strings to play a chord.","zh":"吉他手必須把手指放在正確琴弦上才能彈出和弦。"},{"en":"Wrong finger positions can make the note sound unclear or false.","zh":"錯誤手指位置會令音符聽起來不清楚或不準。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hand placement.","zh":"這個短語描述手部擺位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"for each chord","meaning":"每個和弦","examples":[{"en":"The students learn where to put their fingers for each chord.","zh":"學生學習每個和弦應把手指放在哪裏。"},{"en":"For each chord means for every different chord being played.","zh":"for each chord 指針對正在彈奏的每一個不同和弦。"},{"en":"A guitar chart may show finger positions for each chord in a song.","zh":"吉他圖表可能顯示歌曲中每個和弦的手指位置。"},{"en":"Different chords need different finger patterns.","zh":"不同和弦需要不同手指模式。"},{"en":"This phrase connects instructions to every item in a set.","zh":"這個短語把指示連繫到一組中的每一項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"play together","meaning":"一起彈奏","examples":[{"en":"The students play together after practising the chords.","zh":"學生練習和弦後一起彈奏。"},{"en":"To play together means to perform music at the same time as a group.","zh":"play together 指一群人同時演奏音樂。"},{"en":"Students in a band must listen carefully when they play together.","zh":"樂隊學生一起彈奏時，必須仔細聆聽。"},{"en":"Playing together can reveal timing problems quickly.","zh":"一起彈奏可以很快顯示節奏問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes group music-making.","zh":"這個短語描述小組音樂演奏。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"start laughing","meaning":"開始笑起來","examples":[{"en":"The students sometimes start laughing because their timing is bad.","zh":"學生有時因節奏很差而開始笑起來。"},{"en":"Start laughing means begin to laugh.","zh":"start laughing 指開始發笑。"},{"en":"Students may start laughing when everyone enters the song at the wrong time.","zh":"當所有人都在錯誤時間進入歌曲，學生可能開始笑起來。"},{"en":"Laughter can make mistakes feel less embarrassing.","zh":"笑聲可以令錯誤沒那麼尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of a reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述反應的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"timing is so bad","meaning":"節奏感很差","examples":[{"en":"The students laugh because their timing is so bad.","zh":"學生笑起來，因為他們的節奏感很差。"},{"en":"Timing is so bad means actions or sounds happen at the wrong moment.","zh":"timing is so bad 指動作或聲音在錯誤時間發生。"},{"en":"A singer’s timing is bad if she starts each line too early.","zh":"如果歌手每一句都太早開始，她的節奏感就很差。"},{"en":"Bad timing makes group music messy because people are not together.","zh":"節奏差會令小組音樂混亂，因為大家不同步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes poor rhythm or poor timing of action.","zh":"這個短語描述節奏或行動時間掌握不佳。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"start clapping","meaning":"開始拍手","examples":[{"en":"Gary starts clapping to help the students keep time.","zh":"Gary 開始拍手，幫助學生保持拍子。"},{"en":"Start clapping means begin hitting the hands together rhythmically.","zh":"start clapping 指開始有節奏地拍手。"},{"en":"A teacher may start clapping to help children follow the beat.","zh":"老師可能開始拍手，幫助孩子跟上拍子。"},{"en":"Clapping can give learners a clear rhythm to follow.","zh":"拍手可以給學員清楚節奏作跟隨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes beginning a sound-based guide.","zh":"這個短語描述開始用聲音作指引。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"help us","meaning":"幫助我們","examples":[{"en":"Gary claps to help the students with their timing.","zh":"Gary 拍手幫助學生掌握節奏。"},{"en":"Help us means make it easier for us to do something successfully.","zh":"help us 指令我們更容易成功做到某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may use diagrams to help students understand a difficult idea.","zh":"老師可能用圖表幫助學生理解困難概念。"},{"en":"Good help reduces confusion and improves performance.","zh":"好的幫助可以減少混亂並改善表現。"},{"en":"This phrase shows support given to learners.","zh":"這個短語顯示給學習者的支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"learn to play songs","meaning":"學習彈奏歌曲","examples":[{"en":"The students learn to play songs in the guitar group.","zh":"學生在吉他小組學習彈奏歌曲。"},{"en":"To learn to play songs means to practise until one can perform complete pieces of music.","zh":"learn to play songs 指練習到能演奏完整樂曲。"},{"en":"A beginner pianist may first learn to play simple children’s songs.","zh":"初學鋼琴者可能先學習彈奏簡單兒歌。"},{"en":"Learning songs helps students use chords and rhythm in a real context.","zh":"學習歌曲幫助學生在真實語境中使用和弦和節奏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical music-learning goal.","zh":"這個短語描述實用音樂學習目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at least one song","meaning":"至少一首歌","examples":[{"en":"The group usually does at least one song in each lesson.","zh":"小組通常每堂課至少練習一首歌。"},{"en":"At least one song means one song or more, but not zero.","zh":"at least one song 指一首或以上，不是零首。"},{"en":"A music class may practise at least one song before the concert.","zh":"音樂課可能在音樂會前至少練習一首歌。"},{"en":"Including at least one song gives students a clear achievement each lesson.","zh":"每堂包括至少一首歌，可以給學生清楚成就感。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a minimum number.","zh":"這個短語設定最低數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"words and chords","meaning":"歌詞和和弦","examples":[{"en":"The song sheet includes the words and chords.","zh":"歌紙包括歌詞和和弦。"},{"en":"Words and chords means the lyrics of the song and the guitar chords to play with them.","zh":"words and chords 指歌曲歌詞，以及配合歌詞彈奏的吉他和弦。"},{"en":"A beginner song sheet may show words above the chord names.","zh":"初學者歌紙可能在歌詞上方顯示和弦名稱。"},{"en":"Seeing words and chords together helps students sing and play at the same time.","zh":"同時看見歌詞和和弦，幫助學生邊唱邊彈。"},{"en":"This phrase describes basic information on a song sheet.","zh":"這個短語描述歌紙上的基本資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"harder than you’d think","meaning":"比你想像中更難","examples":[{"en":"Playing a song with words and chords is harder than you would think.","zh":"同時看着歌詞和和弦彈歌，比你想像中更難。"},{"en":"Harder than you’d think means more difficult than people usually expect.","zh":"harder than you’d think 指比人們通常預期更困難。"},{"en":"Keeping rhythm while singing can be harder than you’d think for beginners.","zh":"對初學者來說，一邊唱歌一邊保持節奏可能比你想像中更難。"},{"en":"Tasks that look simple may become difficult when several skills happen together.","zh":"看似簡單的任務，當幾種技能同時進行時可能變難。"},{"en":"This phrase warns people not to underestimate a task.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要低估任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"that part of the lesson","meaning":"課堂的那一部分","examples":[{"en":"That part of the lesson takes about fifteen minutes.","zh":"課堂的那一部分大約需要十五分鐘。"},{"en":"That part of the lesson means one section or stage within the whole class.","zh":"that part of the lesson 指整堂課中的其中一個部分或階段。"},{"en":"In a science lesson, the experiment part may take twenty minutes.","zh":"在科學課中，實驗部分可能需時二十分鐘。"},{"en":"Dividing a lesson into parts helps students know what is happening next.","zh":"把課堂分成不同部分，有助學生知道下一步做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one piece of a larger lesson.","zh":"這個短語指較大課堂中的一個部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bring a recording of","meaning":"帶來……的錄音","examples":[{"en":"Gary often brings a recording of a song.","zh":"Gary 常帶來一首歌的錄音。"},{"en":"To bring a recording of something means to take an audio or video version to a place for others to hear or watch.","zh":"bring a recording of something 指帶一段音訊或影片版本到某處，讓別人聽或看。"},{"en":"A teacher may bring a recording of a speech for students to analyse.","zh":"老師可能帶來一段演講錄音，讓學生分析。"},{"en":"A recording helps learners hear the correct speed, rhythm, and sound.","zh":"錄音幫助學員聽到正確速度、節奏和聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using recorded material in a lesson.","zh":"這個短語描述在課堂中使用錄製材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"play it to us first","meaning":"先播放給我們聽","examples":[{"en":"Gary plays the song to the students first.","zh":"Gary 先播放歌曲給學生聽。"},{"en":"Play it to us first means let us listen to the recording before we try it ourselves.","zh":"play it to us first 指在我們自己嘗試前，先讓我們聽錄音。"},{"en":"A music teacher may play a melody to students first so they know how it should sound.","zh":"音樂老師可能先播放旋律給學生聽，讓他們知道應該如何聽起來。"},{"en":"Hearing the piece first helps learners copy the rhythm and mood.","zh":"先聽樂曲有助學員模仿節奏和情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a listening step before practice.","zh":"這個短語描述練習前的聆聽步驟。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"give out","meaning":"派發","examples":[{"en":"Gary gives out the song sheet.","zh":"Gary 派發歌紙。"},{"en":"To give out something means to distribute it to several people.","zh":"give out something 指把某物分發給幾個人。"},{"en":"A teacher may give out worksheets at the start of class.","zh":"老師可能在課堂開始時派發工作紙。"},{"en":"Giving materials out ensures everyone has the same information.","zh":"派發材料能確保每個人都有同一份資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in classrooms and group activities.","zh":"這個短語常見於課室和小組活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"new chords","meaning":"新和弦","examples":[{"en":"The students practise any new chords first.","zh":"學生先練習任何新和弦。"},{"en":"New chords are chords students have not learned or used before.","zh":"new chords 指學生以前未學過或未用過的和弦。"},{"en":"A beginner may need extra time to practise new chords before playing a song.","zh":"初學者在彈歌前可能需要額外時間練習新和弦。"},{"en":"New chords can slow learners down because their fingers are not used to the shapes.","zh":"新和弦會令學員慢下來，因為手指未習慣那些形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unfamiliar musical patterns.","zh":"這個短語描述不熟悉的音樂模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"practise those first","meaning":"先練習那些","examples":[{"en":"If there are new chords, the students practise those first.","zh":"如果有新和弦，學生會先練習那些。"},{"en":"Practise those first means work on those items before doing the rest of the activity.","zh":"practise those first 指在做其餘活動前，先練習那些項目。"},{"en":"A student may practise difficult words first before reading the whole passage aloud.","zh":"學生朗讀整篇文章前，可能先練習困難詞語。"},{"en":"Practising hard parts first makes the full task easier later.","zh":"先練習困難部分，可以令之後完整任務更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a sensible learning order.","zh":"這個短語顯示合理學習次序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"play it together very slowly","meaning":"非常慢地一起彈","examples":[{"en":"The students play the song together very slowly.","zh":"學生非常慢地一起彈那首歌。"},{"en":"To play it together very slowly means the group performs the song at a slow speed so everyone can follow.","zh":"play it together very slowly 指小組以很慢速度演奏歌曲，好讓每個人跟得上。"},{"en":"A beginner orchestra may play a new piece very slowly before increasing speed.","zh":"初學管弦樂團可能先非常慢地演奏新樂曲，再加快速度。"},{"en":"Slow practice helps learners avoid mistakes and build confidence.","zh":"慢速練習幫助學員避免錯誤並建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful group practice.","zh":"這個短語描述小心的小組練習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"finger-picking","meaning":"指彈","examples":[{"en":"The students practise finger-picking at the end of the lesson.","zh":"學生在課堂結尾練習指彈。"},{"en":"Finger-picking is a guitar technique where players pluck individual strings with their fingers.","zh":"finger-picking 指吉他手用手指撥出單獨琴弦的技巧。"},{"en":"A guitarist may use finger-picking to make a song sound gentle and detailed.","zh":"吉他手可能用指彈令歌曲聽起來柔和而細緻。"},{"en":"Finger-picking requires concentration because each finger may play a different note.","zh":"指彈需要集中精神，因為每隻手指可能彈不同音符。"},{"en":"This word describes a more detailed way of playing guitar.","zh":"這個字描述較細緻的吉他演奏方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the last ten minutes","meaning":"最後十分鐘","examples":[{"en":"Finger-picking takes up the last ten minutes of the lesson.","zh":"指彈佔用課堂最後十分鐘。"},{"en":"The last ten minutes means the final ten-minute section before the lesson ends.","zh":"last ten minutes 指課堂結束前的最後十分鐘部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may use the last ten minutes to review homework.","zh":"老師可能用最後十分鐘檢討功課。"},{"en":"What happens in the last ten minutes often helps students remember the lesson.","zh":"最後十分鐘發生的事，常幫助學生記住課堂內容。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the closing part of a class.","zh":"這個短語標示課堂收結部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pick out individual notes","meaning":"彈出單獨音符","examples":[{"en":"The students pick out individual notes from a tune.","zh":"學生從旋律中彈出單獨音符。"},{"en":"To pick out individual notes means to play separate notes one by one rather than strum whole chords.","zh":"pick out individual notes 指逐一彈出分開的音符，而不是掃整個和弦。"},{"en":"A guitarist may pick out individual notes to play a simple melody.","zh":"吉他手可能彈出單獨音符來演奏簡單旋律。"},{"en":"Playing individual notes requires accuracy because each note can be heard clearly.","zh":"彈單獨音符需要準確，因為每個音都聽得清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful note-by-note playing.","zh":"這個短語描述逐音小心演奏。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"individual notes","meaning":"單獨音符","examples":[{"en":"Finger-picking involves playing individual notes.","zh":"指彈涉及彈奏單獨音符。"},{"en":"Individual notes are single musical sounds played separately.","zh":"individual notes 指分開彈出的單一音樂聲音。"},{"en":"A piano student may practise individual notes before playing both hands together.","zh":"鋼琴學生可能先練習單獨音符，再雙手一起彈。"},{"en":"Playing individual notes helps learners hear whether each sound is correct.","zh":"彈奏單獨音符幫助學員聽出每個聲音是否正確。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts single notes with full chords.","zh":"這個短語把單音與完整和弦作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a tune he’s made up","meaning":"他創作的一段旋律","examples":[{"en":"The students practise a tune that Gary has made up.","zh":"學生練習 Gary 創作的一段旋律。"},{"en":"A tune he’s made up means a short melody he created himself.","zh":"tune he’s made up 指他自己創作的一段短旋律。"},{"en":"A music teacher may make up a simple tune for beginners to practise new notes.","zh":"音樂老師可能為初學者創作簡單旋律來練習新音符。"},{"en":"A made-up tune can match the students’ level better than a famous song.","zh":"自創旋律可以比名曲更配合學生程度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an original melody created for practice.","zh":"這個短語描述為練習而創作的原創旋律。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make up a tune","meaning":"創作一段旋律","examples":[{"en":"Gary makes up simple tunes for the students to practise.","zh":"Gary 創作簡單旋律給學生練習。"},{"en":"To make up a tune means to create a melody, often without copying an existing song.","zh":"make up a tune 指創作一段旋律，通常不是抄現有歌曲。"},{"en":"A child may make up a tune while humming on the way home.","zh":"孩子回家途中哼歌時，可能創作一段旋律。"},{"en":"Making up simple tunes lets a teacher design practice for a specific skill.","zh":"創作簡單旋律讓老師能為特定技巧設計練習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes musical creation.","zh":"這個短語描述音樂創作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"that must be quite hard","meaning":"那一定相當難","examples":[{"en":"The woman says that finger-picking must be quite hard.","zh":"那位女士說指彈一定相當難。"},{"en":"That must be quite hard means I guess that activity is rather difficult.","zh":"that must be quite hard 指我估計那項活動頗困難。"},{"en":"A student may say, “That must be quite hard” after hearing someone practises violin daily.","zh":"學生聽到有人每天練小提琴後，可能說「那一定相當難」。"},{"en":"This phrase shows sympathy or respect for a difficult task.","zh":"這個短語顯示對困難任務的同情或尊重。"},{"en":"It is based on the speaker’s impression, not direct experience.","zh":"它基於說話者的印象，而不是直接經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"really have to concentrate","meaning":"真的必須集中精神","examples":[{"en":"Students like finger-picking because they really have to concentrate.","zh":"學生喜歡指彈，因為他們真的必須集中精神。"},{"en":"Really have to concentrate means must pay close attention and cannot be careless.","zh":"really have to concentrate 指必須高度專注，不能粗心。"},{"en":"A driver really has to concentrate in heavy rain.","zh":"大雨中駕駛的人真的必須集中精神。"},{"en":"Activities with many small steps require strong focus.","zh":"有很多小步驟的活動需要高度專注。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses mental effort.","zh":"這個短語強調精神上的努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sound quite impressive","meaning":"聽起來相當出色","examples":[{"en":"If everyone plays finger-picking well, it sounds quite impressive.","zh":"如果每個人都把指彈彈好，它聽起來相當出色。"},{"en":"Sound quite impressive means seem skilful or admirable when heard.","zh":"sound quite impressive 指聽起來有技巧或令人欣賞。"},{"en":"A beginner band can sound quite impressive when everyone keeps the rhythm together.","zh":"如果每個人都保持同一節奏，初學樂隊也可以聽起來相當出色。"},{"en":"Careful practice can make simple music sound better than expected.","zh":"仔細練習可以令簡單音樂聽起來比預期更好。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a positive judgement about sound.","zh":"這個短語對聲音作出正面評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the only trouble is that","meaning":"唯一問題是……","examples":[{"en":"The only trouble is that Gary sometimes makes students play alone.","zh":"唯一問題是 Gary 有時會叫學生獨自彈奏。"},{"en":"The only trouble is that introduces the one problem in an otherwise good situation.","zh":"the only trouble is that 用來引出整體不錯的情況中唯一的問題。"},{"en":"A student may say, “The only trouble is that the class starts too early.”","zh":"學生可能說：「唯一問題是課堂開始得太早。」"},{"en":"This phrase softens a complaint by showing most things are acceptable.","zh":"這個短語透過表示大部分事情可以接受，令投訴較柔和。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving a balanced opinion.","zh":"給出平衡意見時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get someone to play","meaning":"叫某人彈奏","examples":[{"en":"Gary sometimes gets the students to play one at a time.","zh":"Gary 有時叫學生一個接一個彈奏。"},{"en":"To get someone to play means to ask or make them perform music.","zh":"get someone to play 指要求或叫某人演奏音樂。"},{"en":"A piano teacher may get each student to play a short exercise.","zh":"鋼琴老師可能叫每個學生彈一段短練習。"},{"en":"Playing in front of others can help a teacher hear mistakes clearly.","zh":"在別人面前彈奏可以幫助老師清楚聽到錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes asking someone to perform.","zh":"這個短語描述要求某人演奏。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one at a time","meaning":"一個接一個","examples":[{"en":"Gary sometimes gets students to play one at a time.","zh":"Gary 有時叫學生一個接一個彈奏。"},{"en":"One at a time means individually, not all together.","zh":"one at a time 指逐個進行，而不是全部一起。"},{"en":"Students may enter the exam room one at a time.","zh":"學生可能一個接一個進入考試室。"},{"en":"Doing something one at a time allows each person to receive attention.","zh":"一個接一個地做事，可以讓每個人得到注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an orderly sequence.","zh":"這個短語描述有秩序的先後次序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"that sounds terrifying","meaning":"那聽起來很可怕","examples":[{"en":"The woman says playing alone sounds terrifying.","zh":"那位女士說獨自彈奏聽起來很可怕。"},{"en":"That sounds terrifying means that seems extremely frightening or stressful.","zh":"that sounds terrifying 指那看來極度可怕或很有壓力。"},{"en":"A shy student may say a solo speech sounds terrifying.","zh":"害羞學生可能說獨自演講聽起來很可怕。"},{"en":"This phrase shows fear before actually trying the activity.","zh":"這個短語顯示在真正嘗試前的恐懼。"},{"en":"It is stronger than saying “that sounds difficult.”","zh":"它比「那聽起來很難」更強烈。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be used to it","meaning":"習慣了","examples":[{"en":"Colman is used to playing alone now.","zh":"Colman 現在已習慣獨自彈奏。"},{"en":"Be used to it means be familiar with it and no longer find it strange or frightening.","zh":"be used to it 指熟悉某事，並不再覺得它奇怪或可怕。"},{"en":"A new student may be nervous at first but become used to speaking in class.","zh":"新學生起初可能緊張，但之後會習慣在課堂發言。"},{"en":"Repeated practice helps people get used to difficult tasks.","zh":"反覆練習幫助人習慣困難任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes comfort gained through experience.","zh":"這個短語描述透過經驗而得到的適應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"what to practise","meaning":"要練習甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Gary tells students what to practise for the next week.","zh":"Gary 告訴學生下星期要練習甚麼。"},{"en":"What to practise means which skills, songs, or exercises students should work on.","zh":"what to practise 指學生應練習哪些技巧、歌曲或練習。"},{"en":"A piano teacher may write down what to practise before the next lesson.","zh":"鋼琴老師可能在下堂課前寫下要練習甚麼。"},{"en":"Clear practice tasks help learners improve between classes.","zh":"清楚的練習任務幫助學員在課堂之間進步。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the focus of homework or preparation.","zh":"這個短語指出功課或準備的重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"for the next week","meaning":"為下星期","examples":[{"en":"Gary gives students practice work for the next week.","zh":"Gary 給學生下星期的練習功課。"},{"en":"For the next week means during the coming week before the next meeting or lesson.","zh":"for the next week 指在接下來的一星期，即下次聚會或課堂前。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to read one chapter for the next week.","zh":"老師可能要求學生為下星期讀一章書。"},{"en":"Weekly practice gives learners time to improve before returning to class.","zh":"每週練習讓學員在回到課堂前有時間進步。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a short future time period.","zh":"這個短語設定短期未來時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"go and look at","meaning":"去看看……","examples":[{"en":"The woman says she will go and look at the website.","zh":"那位女士說她會去看看那個網站。"},{"en":"To go and look at something means to check or examine it, often before deciding what to do.","zh":"go and look at something 指去查看或研究某物，通常是在作決定前。"},{"en":"A student may go and look at a university website before applying.","zh":"學生申請前可能去看看大學網站。"},{"en":"Looking at a website can provide prices, choices, and contact details.","zh":"查看網站可以取得價格、選擇和聯絡資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking the next step to gather information.","zh":"這個短語描述採取下一步去收集資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10}],"ielts/listening/Practice 6/task-2":[{"front":"never really planned to","meaning":"從來沒有真正計劃過","examples":[{"en":"I never really planned to be a lifeboat volunteer when I came to live in Northsea.","zh":"我搬來Northsea居住時，從來沒有真正計劃過成為救生艇義工。"},{"en":"To never really plan to do something means you did not seriously intend or expect to do it.","zh":"never really plan to do something意思是並沒有認真打算或預期去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may never really plan to join the drama club, but a friend’s invitation can change their mind.","zh":"學生可能從來沒有真正計劃過加入戲劇學會，但朋友邀請可以改變他的想法。"},{"en":"People sometimes enter meaningful work by chance rather than by careful planning.","zh":"人有時是偶然進入有意義的工作，而不是經過仔細規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the result was unexpected, not part of the original plan.","zh":"這個短語暗示結果是意料之外，而不是原本計劃的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lifeboat volunteer","meaning":"救生艇義工","examples":[{"en":"The speaker became a lifeboat volunteer after moving to Northsea.","zh":"說話者搬到Northsea後成為救生艇義工。"},{"en":"A lifeboat volunteer is someone who gives unpaid help to rescue people in trouble at sea.","zh":"lifeboat volunteer是義務協助拯救海上遇險人士的人。"},{"en":"A lifeboat volunteer may leave home at night when a boat is reported missing.","zh":"當有船隻報稱失蹤，救生艇義工可能在晚上離家出動。"},{"en":"Lifeboat volunteers need training because sea rescues can be dangerous and urgent.","zh":"救生艇義工需要訓練，因為海上救援可能危險而緊急。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rescue role done for service rather than salary.","zh":"這個短語描述一個以服務而非薪金為目的的救援角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"come to live in","meaning":"搬來……居住","examples":[{"en":"The speaker came to live in Northsea.","zh":"說話者搬來Northsea居住。"},{"en":"To come to live in a place means to move there and make it your home.","zh":"come to live in某地，意思是搬到那裡並把它當成家。"},{"en":"A family may come to live in a new town because the parents find work there.","zh":"家庭可能因父母在新市鎮找到工作而搬來那裡居住。"},{"en":"Moving to a new place can change a person’s hobbies, friends and daily routine.","zh":"搬到新地方可以改變一個人的嗜好、朋友和日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on settling in a place, not just visiting it.","zh":"這個短語著重定居某地，而不只是到訪。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"work as","meaning":"擔任……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker had been working in London as a website designer.","zh":"說話者之前在倫敦擔任網站設計師。"},{"en":"To work as something means to have that job or professional role.","zh":"work as某職位，意思是從事該工作或擔任該專業角色。"},{"en":"A university student may work as a tutor during the summer holidays.","zh":"大學生可能在暑假擔任補習老師。"},{"en":"Work experience in one role can later become useful in a different field.","zh":"在某角色中的工作經驗，日後可以在不同領域派上用場。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to identify someone’s job.","zh":"這個短語用來指出某人的工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"website designer","meaning":"網站設計師","examples":[{"en":"The speaker used to work as a website designer in London.","zh":"說話者以前在倫敦擔任網站設計師。"},{"en":"A website designer creates the look, layout and user experience of websites.","zh":"website designer負責創造網站的外觀、版面和用戶體驗。"},{"en":"A small shop may hire a website designer to make its online store easier to use.","zh":"小店可能聘請網站設計師，令網上商店更易使用。"},{"en":"Good website design can help visitors find information quickly and trust a business more.","zh":"良好網站設計可以幫助訪客快速找到資料，並更信任企業。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a creative and technical digital role.","zh":"這個短語指兼具創意和技術的數碼職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"although that was interesting","meaning":"雖然那很有趣","examples":[{"en":"Although that was interesting, the speaker did not like city life.","zh":"雖然那很有趣，說話者並不喜歡城市生活。"},{"en":"Although that was interesting introduces a contrast between something enjoyable and another problem.","zh":"although that was interesting用來引入某事有趣與另一個問題之間的對比。"},{"en":"Although the course was interesting, the long journey made it hard to attend every week.","zh":"雖然課程很有趣，漫長車程令每週出席變得困難。"},{"en":"People may leave a job even if the work is interesting when the lifestyle does not suit them.","zh":"即使工作內容有趣，如果生活方式不適合，人仍可能離職。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one positive point does not remove another concern.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個正面因素不能消除另一個憂慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"city life","meaning":"城市生活","examples":[{"en":"The speaker did not like city life.","zh":"說話者不喜歡城市生活。"},{"en":"City life is the way people live in a city, often with crowds, traffic and fast routines.","zh":"city life是人在城市中的生活方式，通常有擁擠人群、交通和快節奏日常。"},{"en":"A student used to village life may find city life noisy and stressful at first.","zh":"習慣鄉村生活的學生，起初可能覺得城市生活嘈吵而有壓力。"},{"en":"City life can offer jobs and entertainment, but it may also feel crowded and tiring.","zh":"城市生活可以提供工作和娛樂，但也可能令人感到擁擠和疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts urban living with quieter rural or seaside life.","zh":"這個短語把都市生活與較安靜的鄉郊或海邊生活作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be keen on","meaning":"熱衷於……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker had been really keen on boats as a teenager.","zh":"說話者十幾歲時非常熱衷於船隻。"},{"en":"To be keen on something means to be very interested in it or enthusiastic about it.","zh":"be keen on某事，意思是對它很感興趣或很有熱情。"},{"en":"A child who is keen on science may spend weekends building small experiments at home.","zh":"熱衷於科學的孩子可能週末在家做小實驗。"},{"en":"When people are keen on a hobby, they often look for chances to practise it.","zh":"當人們熱衷於某嗜好，通常會尋找機會練習。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English for describing strong interest.","zh":"這個短語常見於英式英語，用來描述強烈興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as a teenager","meaning":"十幾歲時","examples":[{"en":"The speaker was keen on boats as a teenager.","zh":"說話者十幾歲時熱衷於船隻。"},{"en":"As a teenager means during the period when someone was between thirteen and nineteen years old.","zh":"as a teenager意思是在某人十三至十九歲期間。"},{"en":"As a teenager, she loved drawing cartoons after school.","zh":"她十幾歲時喜歡放學後畫漫畫。"},{"en":"Interests formed as a teenager can influence later career or volunteer choices.","zh":"十幾歲時形成的興趣，可以影響後來的職業或義工選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase places a memory or habit in someone’s youth.","zh":"這個短語把記憶或習慣放在某人的青少年時期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"live by the sea","meaning":"住在海邊","examples":[{"en":"The speaker thought he could pursue his interest if he lived by the sea.","zh":"說話者認為如果住在海邊，就可以發展自己的興趣。"},{"en":"To live by the sea means to live near the coast or beside the ocean.","zh":"live by the sea意思是住在海岸附近或海邊。"},{"en":"A family may move to live by the sea because they enjoy swimming and quiet views.","zh":"一個家庭可能因喜歡游泳和寧靜景色而搬去住在海邊。"},{"en":"Living by the sea can make water sports, fishing or boating easier to enjoy.","zh":"住在海邊可以令人更容易享受水上運動、釣魚或划船。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location and lifestyle together.","zh":"這個短語同時描述地點和生活方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pursue that interest","meaning":"發展那個興趣","examples":[{"en":"The speaker wanted to pursue his interest in boats.","zh":"說話者想發展自己對船隻的興趣。"},{"en":"To pursue that interest means to actively spend time developing or enjoying that hobby or subject.","zh":"pursue that interest意思是主動花時間發展或享受那項嗜好或主題。"},{"en":"A student who loves music may pursue that interest by joining the school orchestra.","zh":"喜歡音樂的學生可能透過加入學校樂團來發展那個興趣。"},{"en":"People often pursue an interest more seriously when they find the right place or community.","zh":"當人們找到合適地方或社群，通常會更認真發展興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests action, not just casual liking.","zh":"這個短語暗示行動，而不只是隨便喜歡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in my free time","meaning":"在空閒時間","examples":[{"en":"The speaker hoped to pursue his interest in his free time.","zh":"說話者希望在空閒時間發展自己的興趣。"},{"en":"In my free time means during time when I am not working, studying or doing duties.","zh":"in my free time意思是在我沒有工作、學習或履行責任的時間。"},{"en":"In my free time, I like reading, walking and learning new songs.","zh":"在空閒時間，我喜歡閱讀、散步和學新歌。"},{"en":"People use free time differently depending on their interests and energy.","zh":"人們會因興趣和精力不同而以不同方式使用空閒時間。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to personal time for rest, hobbies or voluntary activities.","zh":"這個短語指用於休息、嗜好或義務活動的個人時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"find that","meaning":"發現……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker found that the Lifeboat Institution was looking for volunteers.","zh":"說話者發現救生艇機構正在招募義工。"},{"en":"To find that something is true means to discover or learn it.","zh":"find that某事屬實，意思是發現或得知它。"},{"en":"A student may find that the library stays open later during exam week.","zh":"學生可能發現圖書館在考試週開放至較晚。"},{"en":"New information can lead people to change their plans or try something new.","zh":"新資訊可以令人改變計劃或嘗試新事物。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a discovery.","zh":"這個短語引入一項發現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Lifeboat Institution","meaning":"救生艇機構","examples":[{"en":"The Lifeboat Institution was looking for volunteers.","zh":"救生艇機構正在招募義工。"},{"en":"The Lifeboat Institution is an organisation connected with lifeboat rescue services.","zh":"Lifeboat Institution是與救生艇救援服務有關的組織。"},{"en":"A lifeboat institution may train volunteers, maintain boats and respond to sea emergencies.","zh":"救生艇機構可能訓練義工、保養船隻並回應海上緊急情況。"},{"en":"Such institutions need reliable people because emergencies can happen at any time.","zh":"這類機構需要可靠的人，因為緊急情況可能隨時發生。"},{"en":"This phrase names an organisation that supports rescue work at sea.","zh":"這個短語命名一個支援海上救援工作的組織。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"look for volunteers","meaning":"招募義工","examples":[{"en":"The Lifeboat Institution was looking for volunteers.","zh":"救生艇機構正在招募義工。"},{"en":"To look for volunteers means to try to find people willing to help without being paid.","zh":"look for volunteers意思是嘗試尋找願意無償幫忙的人。"},{"en":"A school may look for volunteers to help at sports day.","zh":"學校可能招募義工協助運動會。"},{"en":"Organisations look for volunteers when the work is important but staff numbers are limited.","zh":"當工作重要但人手有限，機構就會招募義工。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recruitment for unpaid service.","zh":"這個短語描述為無薪服務招募人手。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"decide to apply","meaning":"決定申請","examples":[{"en":"The speaker decided to apply to become a volunteer.","zh":"說話者決定申請成為義工。"},{"en":"To decide to apply means to choose to submit an application for a role, course or opportunity.","zh":"decide to apply意思是選擇提交某角色、課程或機會的申請。"},{"en":"A student may decide to apply for a summer internship after hearing a teacher’s advice.","zh":"學生聽過老師建議後，可能決定申請暑期實習。"},{"en":"Deciding to apply is often the first step towards a new experience.","zh":"決定申請通常是邁向新經驗的第一步。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a choice followed by formal action.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個選擇之後接着正式行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hard to miss","meaning":"很顯眼；很難錯過","examples":[{"en":"The Lifeboat Institution building in Northsea is hard to miss.","zh":"Northsea的救生艇機構大樓很顯眼。"},{"en":"If something is hard to miss, it is very easy to notice because it is large, bright or obvious.","zh":"如果某物hard to miss，意思是它因巨大、鮮明或明顯而很容易被注意到。"},{"en":"A red bus outside the school gate is hard to miss in the morning.","zh":"早上校門外的一輛紅色巴士很難錯過。"},{"en":"Buildings are hard to miss when they are unusually big or placed in a central location.","zh":"當建築物異常巨大或位於中心地點，它就很顯眼。"},{"en":"This phrase means the thing is very noticeable.","zh":"這個短語意思是某物非常容易被看見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"one of the largest in the country","meaning":"全國最大之一","examples":[{"en":"The building is one of the largest lifeboat buildings in the country.","zh":"該建築是全國最大救生艇建築之一。"},{"en":"One of the largest in the country means among the biggest examples of that type nationwide.","zh":"one of the largest in the country意思是在全國同類之中屬最大之一。"},{"en":"A hospital may be one of the largest in the country if it has many wards and specialist centres.","zh":"如果醫院有很多病房和專科中心，它可能是全國最大之一。"},{"en":"Being one of the largest can show importance, capacity or public investment.","zh":"成為最大之一可以顯示重要性、容量或公共投入。"},{"en":"This phrase compares size within a whole country.","zh":"這個短語在整個國家範圍內比較大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be built with funds provided by","meaning":"由……提供的資金興建","examples":[{"en":"The building was built with funds provided by a generous local resident.","zh":"該建築由一名慷慨本地居民提供的資金興建。"},{"en":"To be built with funds provided by someone means the construction was paid for with money given by that person or group.","zh":"be built with funds provided by某人，意思是建築工程用該人或團體提供的金錢支付。"},{"en":"A school library may be built with funds provided by former students.","zh":"學校圖書館可能由舊生提供的資金興建。"},{"en":"Donations can make important community buildings possible when normal budgets are not enough.","zh":"當正常預算不足，捐款可以令重要社區建築得以興建。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the source of money used to build something.","zh":"這個短語解釋建築所用資金的來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"funds provided by","meaning":"由……提供的資金","examples":[{"en":"The project used funds provided by a generous member of the public.","zh":"該項目使用由一名慷慨公眾人士提供的資金。"},{"en":"Funds provided by someone are money given by that person or organisation for a purpose.","zh":"funds provided by某人，是由該人或機構為某目的提供的金錢。"},{"en":"A scholarship may use funds provided by a local business.","zh":"獎學金可能使用由本地企業提供的資金。"},{"en":"Projects can begin sooner when funds are provided by donors.","zh":"當捐助者提供資金，項目可以更早開始。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who paid for or supported something financially.","zh":"這個短語指出誰在財務上支付或支持某事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"generous member of the public","meaning":"慷慨的公眾人士","examples":[{"en":"A generous member of the public paid for the building.","zh":"一名慷慨的公眾人士支付了該建築的費用。"},{"en":"A generous member of the public is an ordinary citizen who willingly gives money, time or help to others.","zh":"generous member of the public是願意向他人捐出金錢、時間或幫助的普通市民。"},{"en":"A generous member of the public may donate books to a small school library.","zh":"慷慨的公眾人士可能向小型學校圖書館捐書。"},{"en":"Public generosity can support services that benefit the whole community.","zh":"公眾的慷慨可以支援惠及整個社區的服務。"},{"en":"This phrase praises kindness from someone outside an organisation.","zh":"這個短語讚賞機構以外人士的善意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"live here all one’s life","meaning":"一生都住在這裏","examples":[{"en":"The donor had lived in Northsea all her life.","zh":"捐款人一生都住在Northsea。"},{"en":"To live somewhere all one’s life means to spend one’s whole life living in that place.","zh":"live somewhere all one’s life意思是整個人生都住在該地方。"},{"en":"A shop owner who has lived in the same village all his life may know nearly every family there.","zh":"一生都住在同一村莊的店主，可能認識那裡幾乎每個家庭。"},{"en":"Living in one place for a lifetime can create deep local attachment.","zh":"一生住在同一地方可以建立深厚本地歸屬感。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long-term belonging to a place.","zh":"這個短語強調對地方的長期歸屬。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a charity that relies on","meaning":"依靠……的慈善機構","examples":[{"en":"The Lifeboat Institution is a charity that relies on donations.","zh":"救生艇機構是一個依靠捐款的慈善機構。"},{"en":"A charity that relies on something depends on that support to continue its work.","zh":"a charity that relies on某物，是依靠該支持來繼續工作的慈善機構。"},{"en":"A food bank may be a charity that relies on volunteers and donated food.","zh":"食物銀行可能是一個依靠義工和捐贈食物的慈善機構。"},{"en":"If donations fall, a charity that relies on them may have to reduce services.","zh":"如果捐款下降，依靠捐款的慈善機構可能要削減服務。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what keeps a charity operating.","zh":"這個短語解釋甚麼令慈善機構得以營運。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rely on donations","meaning":"依靠捐款","examples":[{"en":"The Lifeboat Institution relies on donations rather than government funding.","zh":"救生艇機構依靠捐款，而不是政府資金。"},{"en":"To rely on donations means to depend on money or support given voluntarily by others.","zh":"rely on donations意思是依賴他人自願提供的金錢或支援。"},{"en":"A small animal shelter may rely on donations to buy food and medicine.","zh":"小型動物收容所可能依靠捐款購買食物和藥物。"},{"en":"Organisations that rely on donations must keep public trust.","zh":"依靠捐款的機構必須保持公眾信任。"},{"en":"This phrase shows financial dependence on voluntary giving.","zh":"這個短語顯示財政上依賴自願捐助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The charity relies on donations rather than government funding.","zh":"該慈善機構依靠捐款，而不是政府資金。"},{"en":"Rather than shows a contrast and means instead of one thing, another thing is true.","zh":"rather than表示對比，意思是並非一件事，而是另一件事。"},{"en":"A student may choose to walk rather than take a taxi to save money.","zh":"學生可能選擇步行而不是坐的士，以節省金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate the real source, choice or cause from another possibility.","zh":"這個短語幫助把真正來源、選擇或原因與另一可能分開。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining what something is not.","zh":"它適合用於解釋某事不是甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"funding provided by the government","meaning":"由政府提供的資金","examples":[{"en":"The Lifeboat Institution does not depend mainly on funding provided by the government.","zh":"救生艇機構並不主要依賴由政府提供的資金。"},{"en":"Funding provided by the government is money given by public authorities to support a service or project.","zh":"funding provided by the government是由公共機關提供以支援服務或項目的金錢。"},{"en":"A museum may receive funding provided by the government to keep tickets affordable.","zh":"博物館可能接受由政府提供的資金，以保持票價可負擔。"},{"en":"Government funding can make services stable, but it may also come with rules and limits.","zh":"政府資金可以令服務穩定，但也可能伴隨規則和限制。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies public money as the source of support.","zh":"這個短語指出公共資金是支援來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a huge help to","meaning":"對……有很大幫助","examples":[{"en":"The donation was a huge help to the Lifeboat Institution.","zh":"這筆捐款對救生艇機構有很大幫助。"},{"en":"A huge help to someone means something gives them very important support.","zh":"a huge help to某人，意思是某事給予他們非常重要的支援。"},{"en":"A free bus service can be a huge help to elderly residents who cannot drive.","zh":"免費巴士服務對不會駕車的長者居民可以有很大幫助。"},{"en":"Extra money can be a huge help when an organisation needs equipment urgently.","zh":"當機構急需設備時，額外金錢可以有很大幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong practical value.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈實際價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have a health assessment","meaning":"接受健康評估","examples":[{"en":"The speaker had to have a health assessment when he applied.","zh":"說話者申請時必須接受健康評估。"},{"en":"To have a health assessment means to be checked by medical staff to see if you are fit and healthy enough.","zh":"have a health assessment意思是接受醫護人員檢查，以確認自己是否足夠健康和適合。"},{"en":"A new firefighter may have a health assessment before starting training.","zh":"新消防員開始訓練前可能要接受健康評估。"},{"en":"Health assessments protect both the worker and the people they may need to help.","zh":"健康評估保護工作者本身，也保護他們可能需要幫助的人。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when physical ability and safety matter.","zh":"當體能和安全很重要時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be particularly interested in","meaning":"特別關注……","examples":[{"en":"The doctors were particularly interested in the speaker’s vision.","zh":"醫生特別關注說話者的視力。"},{"en":"To be particularly interested in something means to pay special attention to it.","zh":"be particularly interested in某事，意思是特別注意它。"},{"en":"A teacher may be particularly interested in a student’s reading progress after a long absence.","zh":"學生長期缺席後，老師可能特別關注他的閱讀進度。"},{"en":"Doctors focus on certain details when those details are important for safety.","zh":"當某些細節對安全很重要，醫生會集中注意那些細節。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one issue matters more than others in that situation.","zh":"這個短語顯示在該情況中某問題比其他問題更重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"vision","meaning":"視力","examples":[{"en":"The doctors checked the speaker’s vision.","zh":"醫生檢查了說話者的視力。"},{"en":"Vision is a person’s ability to see.","zh":"vision是一個人看見東西的能力。"},{"en":"A driver needs good vision to notice signs, traffic lights and pedestrians.","zh":"司機需要良好視力來注意路牌、交通燈和行人。"},{"en":"Poor vision can make work dangerous if someone must read signals quickly.","zh":"如果某人必須快速讀取信號，視力差會令工作危險。"},{"en":"This word can mean eyesight in medical contexts.","zh":"這個詞在醫療語境中可指視力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"used to be short-sighted","meaning":"以前近視","examples":[{"en":"The speaker used to be short-sighted.","zh":"說話者以前近視。"},{"en":"Used to be short-sighted means someone had difficulty seeing distant objects clearly in the past.","zh":"used to be short-sighted意思是某人以前難以清楚看見遠處物件。"},{"en":"A student who used to be short-sighted may have needed to sit near the board.","zh":"以前近視的學生可能需要坐近黑板。"},{"en":"Eye surgery or glasses can change how a person deals with short-sightedness.","zh":"眼科手術或眼鏡可以改變人如何處理近視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a past eyesight condition that may no longer be true.","zh":"這個短語描述過去的視力情況，而現在可能不再如此。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"wear glasses","meaning":"戴眼鏡","examples":[{"en":"The speaker had to wear glasses before having eye surgery.","zh":"說話者接受眼科手術前必須戴眼鏡。"},{"en":"To wear glasses means to use glasses on your face to improve vision.","zh":"wear glasses意思是在臉上戴眼鏡以改善視力。"},{"en":"A child may wear glasses to read the board clearly at school.","zh":"孩子可能戴眼鏡，以便在學校清楚看見黑板。"},{"en":"People wear glasses when their eyes need help focusing properly.","zh":"當眼睛需要幫助才能正確聚焦，人們會戴眼鏡。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a common way of correcting eyesight.","zh":"這個短語指矯正視力的常見方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"laser eye surgery","meaning":"激光矯視手術","examples":[{"en":"The speaker had laser eye surgery two years earlier.","zh":"說話者兩年前接受了激光矯視手術。"},{"en":"Laser eye surgery is a medical operation that uses a laser to correct vision problems.","zh":"laser eye surgery是使用激光矯正視力問題的醫療手術。"},{"en":"An adult may choose laser eye surgery because they no longer want to depend on glasses.","zh":"成年人可能因不想再依賴眼鏡而選擇激光矯視手術。"},{"en":"After laser eye surgery, some people can see more clearly without lenses.","zh":"激光矯視手術後，有些人不用鏡片也能看得更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific kind of eye operation.","zh":"這個短語指特定眼科手術。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"two years earlier","meaning":"兩年前","examples":[{"en":"The speaker had laser eye surgery two years earlier.","zh":"說話者兩年前接受了激光矯視手術。"},{"en":"Two years earlier means two years before the time being discussed.","zh":"two years earlier意思是在所討論時間之前兩年。"},{"en":"She moved to the city in 2020; two years earlier, she had finished university.","zh":"她在2020年搬到城市；兩年前，她已完成大學。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers understand the order of past events.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者理解過去事件的先後次序。"},{"en":"It is useful when telling a story with more than one time point.","zh":"當故事有多個時間點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"test for colour blindness","meaning":"進行色盲測試","examples":[{"en":"The doctors gave the speaker tests for colour blindness.","zh":"醫生為說話者進行色盲測試。"},{"en":"To test for colour blindness means to check whether someone can distinguish colours correctly.","zh":"test for colour blindness意思是檢查某人是否能正確分辨顏色。"},{"en":"A pilot may be tested for colour blindness because signals use different colours.","zh":"機師可能需要接受色盲測試，因為信號使用不同顏色。"},{"en":"Colour tests help ensure people can recognise safety signs accurately.","zh":"顏色測試幫助確保人能準確辨認安全標誌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a medical or safety-related check.","zh":"這個短語描述醫療或安全相關檢查。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"colour blindness","meaning":"色盲","examples":[{"en":"The doctors tested the speaker for colour blindness.","zh":"醫生測試說話者是否有色盲。"},{"en":"Colour blindness is a condition in which a person has difficulty telling some colours apart.","zh":"colour blindness是一種難以分辨某些顏色的情況。"},{"en":"A student with colour blindness may confuse red and green on a chart.","zh":"有色盲的學生可能混淆圖表上的紅色和綠色。"},{"en":"Colour blindness can matter in jobs where coloured lights or signals are important.","zh":"在需要分辨彩色燈或信號的工作中，色盲可能很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a vision condition, not complete blindness.","zh":"這個短語描述一種視覺情況，而不是完全失明。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"it turned out","meaning":"結果證明","examples":[{"en":"It turned out that the speaker did not have a problem with colour blindness.","zh":"結果證明說話者沒有色盲問題。"},{"en":"It turned out means the result was discovered later.","zh":"it turned out意思是後來發現結果是怎樣。"},{"en":"The class worried the test would be hard, but it turned out to be quite fair.","zh":"全班擔心測驗會很難，但結果證明相當公平。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when the final result is different from what they expected or feared.","zh":"當最終結果與人們預期或擔心的不同時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the outcome after uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語在不確定後引入結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"coastguard","meaning":"海岸警衛隊","examples":[{"en":"The coastguard gets an alert and contacts the volunteers.","zh":"海岸警衛隊收到警報後聯絡義工。"},{"en":"The coastguard is an official service that helps protect people and boats near the coast.","zh":"coastguard是協助保護海岸附近人士和船隻的官方服務。"},{"en":"The coastguard may respond when a swimmer is missing or a boat is in trouble.","zh":"當游泳者失蹤或船隻遇險，海岸警衛隊可能作出回應。"},{"en":"Coastguards coordinate rescue work because they receive emergency information first.","zh":"海岸警衛隊協調救援工作，因為他們通常先收到緊急資訊。"},{"en":"This word refers to a sea-safety authority.","zh":"這個詞指海上安全機關。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get an alert","meaning":"收到警報","examples":[{"en":"When the coastguard gets an alert, the volunteers are contacted.","zh":"當海岸警衛隊收到警報，義工便會被聯絡。"},{"en":"To get an alert means to receive a warning or emergency message.","zh":"get an alert意思是收到警告或緊急訊息。"},{"en":"A teacher may get an alert if a fire alarm is triggered in the school.","zh":"如果學校火警鐘被觸發，老師可能收到警報。"},{"en":"Getting an alert allows people to act quickly before a situation gets worse.","zh":"收到警報讓人們在情況惡化前迅速行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in emergencies and safety systems.","zh":"這個短語常用於緊急情況和安全系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be contacted","meaning":"被聯絡","examples":[{"en":"All the volunteers are contacted when there is an alert.","zh":"當有警報時，所有義工都會被聯絡。"},{"en":"To be contacted means to be reached by phone, message, email or another method.","zh":"be contacted意思是透過電話、訊息、電郵或其他方式被聯絡到。"},{"en":"Parents may be contacted if a student becomes ill at school.","zh":"如果學生在校生病，家長可能會被聯絡。"},{"en":"Being contacted quickly is important when urgent action is needed.","zh":"當需要緊急行動，迅速被聯絡很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on receiving communication from someone.","zh":"這個短語著重收到他人的通訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rush to","meaning":"趕往……","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers rush to the lifeboat station after an alert.","zh":"義工在警報後趕往救生艇站。"},{"en":"To rush to a place means to go there very quickly because something is urgent.","zh":"rush to某地，意思是因事情緊急而很快前往那裡。"},{"en":"A nurse may rush to the ward when a patient suddenly needs help.","zh":"當病人突然需要幫助，護士可能趕往病房。"},{"en":"People rush when delay could make the situation worse.","zh":"當延誤可能令情況惡化，人們就會趕急行動。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests speed and urgency.","zh":"這個短語暗示速度和緊急性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lifeboat station","meaning":"救生艇站","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers rush to the lifeboat station.","zh":"義工趕往救生艇站。"},{"en":"A lifeboat station is a place where lifeboats, rescue equipment and crew are based.","zh":"lifeboat station是停放救生艇、救援設備和船員所在的地方。"},{"en":"A coastal town may have a lifeboat station near the harbour.","zh":"海邊小鎮可能在港口附近設有救生艇站。"},{"en":"Lifeboat stations must be easy to reach because emergencies require quick launches.","zh":"救生艇站必須容易到達，因為緊急情況需要快速出艇。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the operational base for sea rescue.","zh":"這個短語指海上救援的運作基地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"our target is to","meaning":"我們的目標是……","examples":[{"en":"The team’s target is to get to the lifeboat station in five minutes.","zh":"團隊的目標是在五分鐘內到達救生艇站。"},{"en":"Our target is to means our goal or aim is to do something.","zh":"our target is to意思是我們的目標或目的就是做某事。"},{"en":"Our target is to finish the school project before Friday afternoon.","zh":"我們的目標是在星期五下午前完成學校專題。"},{"en":"Clear targets help teams measure whether they are working fast enough.","zh":"清晰目標幫助團隊衡量工作速度是否足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a specific goal.","zh":"這個短語引入具體目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get there in five minutes","meaning":"在五分鐘內到達","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers try to get there in five minutes.","zh":"義工嘗試在五分鐘內到達那裡。"},{"en":"To get there in five minutes means to arrive at the place within five minutes.","zh":"get there in five minutes意思是在五分鐘內到達該地方。"},{"en":"A student may try to get to the classroom in five minutes after the bell rings.","zh":"鐘聲響起後，學生可能嘗試在五分鐘內到達課室。"},{"en":"Time limits matter in emergencies because every minute can affect the result.","zh":"時限在緊急情況中很重要，因為每分鐘都可能影響結果。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses fast arrival within a short deadline.","zh":"這個短語強調在短時間限制內迅速到達。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get the boat off the dock","meaning":"讓船離開碼頭","examples":[{"en":"The team tries to get the boat off the dock quickly.","zh":"團隊嘗試快速讓船離開碼頭。"},{"en":"To get the boat off the dock means to launch it away from the platform where it is kept.","zh":"get the boat off the dock意思是讓船離開停泊的平台並開始出動。"},{"en":"Sailors must untie ropes before they can get a boat off the dock.","zh":"水手必須先解開繩索，才能讓船離開碼頭。"},{"en":"In a rescue, getting the boat off the dock quickly saves valuable time.","zh":"在救援中，快速讓船離開碼頭可以節省寶貴時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first movement from harbour to water.","zh":"這個短語描述船由港口開始移動的第一步。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"out to sea","meaning":"出海","examples":[{"en":"The team gets the boat out to sea within a few minutes.","zh":"團隊在幾分鐘內讓船出海。"},{"en":"Out to sea means away from the shore and onto the sea.","zh":"out to sea意思是離開岸邊，前往海上。"},{"en":"Fishermen may go out to sea before sunrise to begin work early.","zh":"漁民可能在日出前出海，以便早些開始工作。"},{"en":"Rescue teams go out to sea when someone needs help beyond the coastline.","zh":"當有人在海岸以外需要幫助，救援隊就會出海。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the safety of land with being on open water.","zh":"這個短語把陸地安全與開放海面作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in another six to eight minutes","meaning":"再用六至八分鐘","examples":[{"en":"The team tries to launch the boat in another six to eight minutes.","zh":"團隊嘗試再用六至八分鐘出艇。"},{"en":"In another six to eight minutes means after an additional period of six to eight minutes.","zh":"in another six to eight minutes意思是在額外六至八分鐘後。"},{"en":"The bus may arrive in another six to eight minutes if traffic stays light.","zh":"如果交通仍暢順，巴士可能再用六至八分鐘到達。"},{"en":"Emergency teams use short time targets to keep every stage under control.","zh":"緊急隊伍使用短時間目標，讓每個階段保持受控。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate extra time needed.","zh":"這個短語給出大概仍需的額外時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be proud that","meaning":"為……感到自豪","examples":[{"en":"The team is proud that it usually achieves its target.","zh":"團隊為通常能達到目標而感到自豪。"},{"en":"To be proud that something happens means to feel pleased because of an achievement or quality.","zh":"be proud that某事發生，意思是因某項成就或品質而感到高興。"},{"en":"A teacher may be proud that her students helped one another during a difficult project.","zh":"老師可能為學生在困難項目中互相幫助而感到自豪。"},{"en":"Pride often comes when effort leads to a clear result.","zh":"當努力帶來清楚成果，自豪感通常會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses satisfaction with success.","zh":"這個短語表達對成功的滿意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"achieve that","meaning":"做到那一點","examples":[{"en":"The team usually achieves the launch-time target.","zh":"團隊通常做到出艇時間目標。"},{"en":"To achieve that means to succeed in doing or reaching the thing just mentioned.","zh":"achieve that意思是成功完成或達到剛提到的事情。"},{"en":"A student may aim to finish revision before dinner and achieve that by planning carefully.","zh":"學生可能目標是在晚飯前完成溫習，並透過仔細規劃做到那一點。"},{"en":"Teams achieve targets when they practise, communicate and know their roles.","zh":"當團隊練習、溝通並知道自己的角色，就能達成目標。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to successful completion of a goal.","zh":"這個短語指成功完成某目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"average time","meaning":"平均時間","examples":[{"en":"The average time across the country is eight and a half minutes.","zh":"全國平均時間是八分半鐘。"},{"en":"Average time is the typical time calculated from several examples or cases.","zh":"average time是由多個例子或個案計算出來的典型時間。"},{"en":"A school may record the average time students take to finish a reading test.","zh":"學校可能記錄學生完成閱讀測驗的平均時間。"},{"en":"Average time helps people compare one team’s performance with a wider standard.","zh":"平均時間幫助人把一隊表現與更廣泛標準比較。"},{"en":"This phrase uses numbers to show normal speed or duration.","zh":"這個短語用數字顯示正常速度或持續時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"across the country","meaning":"全國","examples":[{"en":"The average time across the country is eight and a half minutes.","zh":"全國平均時間是八分半鐘。"},{"en":"Across the country means throughout the whole country or in many places within it.","zh":"across the country意思是遍及整個國家或國內許多地方。"},{"en":"Schools across the country may close if a severe storm is expected.","zh":"如果預計有嚴重風暴，全國學校可能停課。"},{"en":"National comparisons show whether one local area is faster, slower or similar to others.","zh":"全國比較能顯示某本地區比其他地方更快、更慢還是相近。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a countrywide situation.","zh":"這個短語描述全國範圍的情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"eight and a half minutes","meaning":"八分半鐘","examples":[{"en":"The national average is eight and a half minutes.","zh":"全國平均時間是八分半鐘。"},{"en":"Eight and a half minutes means eight minutes and thirty seconds.","zh":"eight and a half minutes意思是八分鐘三十秒。"},{"en":"A student may need eight and a half minutes to walk from the bus stop to school.","zh":"學生可能需要八分半鐘由巴士站步行到學校。"},{"en":"In emergency work, eight and a half minutes can be a meaningful measure of speed.","zh":"在緊急工作中，八分半鐘可以是有意義的速度指標。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise time length.","zh":"這個短語給出精確時間長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"recently qualified as","meaning":"最近取得……資格","examples":[{"en":"The speaker has recently qualified as a helmsman.","zh":"說話者最近取得舵手資格。"},{"en":"To recently qualify as something means to have just gained the required training or certification for that role.","zh":"recently qualify as某職位，意思是剛取得該角色所需訓練或認證。"},{"en":"A nurse may recently qualify as a midwife after completing specialist training.","zh":"護士完成專科訓練後，可能最近取得助產士資格。"},{"en":"Becoming qualified can allow a volunteer or worker to take on greater responsibility.","zh":"取得資格可以讓義工或工作者承擔更大責任。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a new professional or trained status.","zh":"這個短語顯示新的專業或受訓身份。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"helmsman","meaning":"舵手","examples":[{"en":"A helmsman has ultimate responsibility for the lifeboat.","zh":"舵手對救生艇負有最終責任。"},{"en":"A helmsman is the person who steers a boat and takes responsibility for its safe operation.","zh":"helmsman是操控船隻方向並負責其安全運作的人。"},{"en":"On a rescue boat, the helmsman must judge waves, weather and crew safety.","zh":"在救援船上，舵手必須判斷海浪、天氣和船員安全。"},{"en":"If the helmsman makes a poor decision, everyone on the boat may be affected.","zh":"如果舵手作出錯誤決定，船上每個人都可能受影響。"},{"en":"This word describes a key leadership role on a boat.","zh":"這個詞描述船上的關鍵領導角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have the ultimate responsibility for","meaning":"對……負有最終責任","examples":[{"en":"The helmsman has the ultimate responsibility for the lifeboat.","zh":"舵手對救生艇負有最終責任。"},{"en":"To have the ultimate responsibility for something means to be the final person accountable for it.","zh":"have the ultimate responsibility for某事，意思是成為最終需要負責的人。"},{"en":"A principal has the ultimate responsibility for student safety during school hours.","zh":"校長在上課時間對學生安全負有最終責任。"},{"en":"When someone has ultimate responsibility, they must make difficult final decisions.","zh":"當某人負有最終責任，他必須作出困難的最終決定。"},{"en":"This phrase shows final authority and accountability.","zh":"這個短語顯示最終權力和責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"check that","meaning":"檢查……是否","examples":[{"en":"The speaker has to check that the equipment is in working order.","zh":"說話者必須檢查設備是否運作正常。"},{"en":"To check that something is true means to make sure it is correct, safe or ready.","zh":"check that某事屬實，意思是確認它正確、安全或準備好。"},{"en":"A teacher may check that all students have handed in their permission forms.","zh":"老師可能檢查所有學生是否已交回同意書。"},{"en":"Checking before action can prevent accidents, delays and mistakes.","zh":"行動前檢查可以防止意外、延誤和錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what must be confirmed.","zh":"這個短語引入必須確認的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"equipment","meaning":"設備","examples":[{"en":"The helmsman checks that the equipment is safe to use.","zh":"舵手檢查設備是否安全可用。"},{"en":"Equipment is the tools, machines or items needed for a particular activity or job.","zh":"equipment是進行特定活動或工作所需的工具、機器或物品。"},{"en":"A sports team needs equipment such as balls, nets and first-aid supplies.","zh":"運動隊需要球、球網和急救用品等設備。"},{"en":"Broken equipment can delay work or put people in danger.","zh":"損壞設備可以延誤工作或令人陷入危險。"},{"en":"This word refers to practical items used to do a task.","zh":"這個詞指用來完成任務的實用物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be in working order","meaning":"運作正常","examples":[{"en":"The equipment must be in working order.","zh":"設備必須運作正常。"},{"en":"If something is in working order, it functions properly and is safe or ready to use.","zh":"如果某物in working order，意思是它正常運作並安全或準備可用。"},{"en":"A printer is in working order when it prints clearly without jamming.","zh":"打印機能清楚列印而不卡紙，就是運作正常。"},{"en":"Rescue equipment must be checked often so it will work during emergencies.","zh":"救援設備必須經常檢查，才能在緊急情況中正常使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes proper operating condition.","zh":"這個短語描述正常操作狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the crew","meaning":"船員","examples":[{"en":"The crew wear special life jackets.","zh":"船員穿着特別救生衣。"},{"en":"The crew are the people who work together on a boat, plane or rescue vehicle.","zh":"the crew是在船、飛機或救援車輛上一起工作的人。"},{"en":"A lifeboat crew may include a helmsman and several trained volunteers.","zh":"救生艇船員可能包括一名舵手和幾名受訓義工。"},{"en":"Crews need clear communication because everyone’s safety depends on teamwork.","zh":"船員需要清晰溝通，因為每個人的安全都取決於合作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the working team on board.","zh":"這個短語指船上的工作團隊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"life jackets","meaning":"救生衣","examples":[{"en":"The crew have special life jackets.","zh":"船員有特別救生衣。"},{"en":"Life jackets are safety vests that help people float in water.","zh":"life jackets是幫助人在水中浮起的安全背心。"},{"en":"Children should wear life jackets when they ride in a small boat.","zh":"孩子乘坐小船時應穿救生衣。"},{"en":"Life jackets can save lives if someone falls into cold or rough water.","zh":"如果有人跌入寒冷或洶湧水中，救生衣可以救命。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to essential water-safety equipment.","zh":"這個短語指重要的水上安全設備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"support up to","meaning":"支撐最多……","examples":[{"en":"The life jackets can support up to four people in the water.","zh":"這些救生衣可在水中支撐最多四個人。"},{"en":"To support up to a number means to hold or help no more than that number of people or things.","zh":"support up to某數字，意思是支撐或幫助不超過該數量的人或物。"},{"en":"A small lift may support up to six people at one time.","zh":"小型升降機可能一次支撐最多六個人。"},{"en":"Capacity limits matter because exceeding them can make equipment unsafe.","zh":"容量限制很重要，因為超出限制會令設備不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the maximum amount something can handle.","zh":"這個短語給出某物可以承受的最高數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the water","meaning":"在水中","examples":[{"en":"The life jackets can support four people in the water.","zh":"這些救生衣可在水中支撐四個人。"},{"en":"In the water means physically in a lake, river, sea or pool.","zh":"in the water意思是身體在湖泊、河流、海洋或泳池中。"},{"en":"A swimmer in the water may need help if they become tired far from shore.","zh":"如果游泳者在離岸很遠的水中疲倦，可能需要協助。"},{"en":"Conditions in the water can become dangerous when waves, cold or currents are strong.","zh":"當海浪、寒冷或水流很強，水中情況會變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase places the action in a water environment.","zh":"這個短語把行動放在水中環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"it is ultimately my decision whether","meaning":"最終由我決定是否……","examples":[{"en":"It is ultimately the helmsman’s decision whether it is safe to launch the boat.","zh":"是否安全出艇最終由舵手決定。"},{"en":"It is ultimately my decision whether means I am the final person responsible for choosing if something should happen.","zh":"it is ultimately my decision whether意思是我最終負責決定某事是否應該發生。"},{"en":"It is ultimately the doctor’s decision whether a patient is fit enough to leave hospital.","zh":"病人是否適合出院，最終由醫生決定。"},{"en":"Final decisions are difficult when safety, time and pressure all matter.","zh":"當安全、時間和壓力都很重要，最終決定會很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase shows final authority after considering advice and conditions.","zh":"這個短語顯示在考慮建議和情況後的最終權力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"safe to launch the boat","meaning":"安全出艇","examples":[{"en":"The helmsman decides whether it is safe to launch the boat.","zh":"舵手決定是否安全出艇。"},{"en":"Safe to launch the boat means conditions are acceptable for sending the boat into the water.","zh":"safe to launch the boat意思是情況適合把船送入水中出動。"},{"en":"A team may check wind, waves and equipment before deciding it is safe to launch the boat.","zh":"團隊可能先檢查風、海浪和設備，才決定是否安全出艇。"},{"en":"Launching too early in unsafe conditions can put the crew at risk.","zh":"在不安全情況下太早出艇，可以令船員陷入危險。"},{"en":"This phrase combines safety judgement with action.","zh":"這個短語結合安全判斷與行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"launch the boat","meaning":"出艇","examples":[{"en":"The crew rarely decide not to launch the boat.","zh":"船員很少決定不出艇。"},{"en":"To launch the boat means to put the boat into the water or send it out for use.","zh":"launch the boat意思是把船放入水中或派出使用。"},{"en":"Fishermen launch the boat early when they want to start work before sunrise.","zh":"漁民想在日出前開始工作時，會很早出艇。"},{"en":"Rescue crews launch the boat quickly when lives may be at risk.","zh":"當生命可能有危險，救援船員會迅速出艇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the start of a boat’s journey or operation.","zh":"這個短語描述船隻旅程或行動的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"it is very rare not to","meaning":"很少不……","examples":[{"en":"It is very rare not to launch the lifeboat.","zh":"很少不派出救生艇。"},{"en":"It is very rare not to do something means that almost always the action is taken.","zh":"it is very rare not to do something意思是幾乎總是會採取該行動。"},{"en":"It is very rare not to cancel outdoor sports when a red rain warning is issued.","zh":"當紅色暴雨警告發出，很少不取消戶外運動。"},{"en":"If something is very rare, people treat it as an exception rather than the normal rule.","zh":"如果某事很罕見，人們會把它視為例外，而不是常規。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses how unusual the opposite action is.","zh":"這個短語強調相反行動非常少見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"even in the worst weather","meaning":"即使在最惡劣的天氣下","examples":[{"en":"The crew usually launch the boat even in the worst weather.","zh":"船員通常即使在最惡劣的天氣下也會出艇。"},{"en":"Even in the worst weather means despite extremely bad weather conditions.","zh":"even in the worst weather意思是儘管天氣情況極差。"},{"en":"Emergency workers may keep working even in the worst weather when people need help.","zh":"當人們需要幫助，緊急服務人員可能即使在最惡劣天氣下仍繼續工作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows determination because bad conditions do not stop the action.","zh":"這個短語顯示決心，因為惡劣條件沒有阻止行動。"},{"en":"It often describes courage, duty or necessity.","zh":"它常描述勇氣、職責或必要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"As well as going out on the lifeboat, the speaker does other work.","zh":"除了乘救生艇出海，說話者也做其他工作。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to something else.","zh":"as well as意思是除了某事之外。"},{"en":"As well as teaching English, she writes learning materials for her students.","zh":"除了教英語，她也為學生撰寫學習材料。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that someone has more than one duty or activity.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人有多於一項職責或活動。"},{"en":"It is useful when adding an extra role without making a new sentence.","zh":"當要加入額外角色而不另開新句時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go out on the lifeboat","meaning":"乘救生艇出海","examples":[{"en":"The speaker goes out on the lifeboat during emergencies.","zh":"說話者在緊急情況中乘救生艇出海。"},{"en":"To go out on the lifeboat means to travel on the lifeboat to respond to a rescue or sea incident.","zh":"go out on the lifeboat意思是乘救生艇前往處理救援或海上事故。"},{"en":"Volunteers may go out on the lifeboat when a small sailing boat loses power.","zh":"當小帆船失去動力，義工可能乘救生艇出海。"},{"en":"Going out on the lifeboat can be dangerous because sea conditions may be poor.","zh":"乘救生艇出海可能有危險，因為海況可能惡劣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active participation in a rescue mission.","zh":"這個短語描述積極參與救援任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"involve other things","meaning":"包括其他事情","examples":[{"en":"The speaker’s work involves other things too.","zh":"說話者的工作也包括其他事情。"},{"en":"To involve other things means to include additional duties or parts besides the obvious ones.","zh":"involve other things意思是除了明顯部分外，也包括額外職責或部分。"},{"en":"A teacher’s job involves other things besides teaching, such as marking and meeting parents.","zh":"老師工作除了教書，還包括批改和與家長見面等其他事情。"},{"en":"Jobs can be misunderstood when people only see the most dramatic part.","zh":"當人們只看見最戲劇性的部分，就可能誤解一份工作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a role is broader than it first appears.","zh":"這個短語顯示角色比起初看來更廣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"underestimate how quickly","meaning":"低估……有多快","examples":[{"en":"A lot of people underestimate how quickly conditions can change at sea.","zh":"很多人低估海上情況變化有多快。"},{"en":"To underestimate how quickly something happens means to think it happens more slowly than it really does.","zh":"underestimate how quickly某事發生，意思是以為它比實際發生得慢。"},{"en":"Students may underestimate how quickly exam time passes if they do not practise timed writing.","zh":"如果學生不練習限時寫作，可能低估考試時間過得有多快。"},{"en":"Underestimating speed can lead to poor preparation and risky decisions.","zh":"低估速度可以導致準備不足和危險決定。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that change can happen faster than expected.","zh":"這個短語提醒人變化可能比預期更快。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"conditions can change at sea","meaning":"海上情況會變化","examples":[{"en":"Conditions can change very quickly at sea.","zh":"海上情況可以變化得非常快。"},{"en":"Conditions can change at sea means weather, waves and safety levels may become different while people are on the water.","zh":"conditions can change at sea意思是人在水上時，天氣、海浪和安全程度可能改變。"},{"en":"A calm morning can become risky if wind and waves rise suddenly at sea.","zh":"如果海上風浪突然增強，平靜早上可以變得危險。"},{"en":"Sea conditions matter because boats and swimmers depend on stable weather.","zh":"海況很重要，因為船隻和游泳者依賴穩定天氣。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that the sea can be unpredictable.","zh":"這個短語提醒人海洋可以難以預測。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"speak to","meaning":"向……講解","examples":[{"en":"The speaker speaks to youth groups and sailing clubs.","zh":"說話者向青年團體和帆船會講解。"},{"en":"To speak to a group means to talk to them, often to explain, teach or inform.","zh":"speak to某群體，意思是向他們說話，通常是為了解釋、教導或提供資訊。"},{"en":"A nurse may speak to students about healthy eating during a school assembly.","zh":"護士可能在學校集會向學生講解健康飲食。"},{"en":"Speaking to community groups can spread important safety messages.","zh":"向社區團體講解可以傳播重要安全訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving information directly to an audience.","zh":"這個短語描述直接向受眾提供資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"youth groups","meaning":"青年團體","examples":[{"en":"The speaker gives safety talks to youth groups.","zh":"說話者向青年團體作安全講座。"},{"en":"Youth groups are organised groups of young people who meet for activities, learning or community service.","zh":"youth groups是年輕人為活動、學習或社區服務而組成的團體。"},{"en":"A youth group may organise hiking trips, volunteer work and leadership training.","zh":"青年團體可能組織行山、義工服務和領袖訓練。"},{"en":"Talking to youth groups can teach safety habits before young people face real risks.","zh":"向青年團體講解可以在年輕人面對真實風險前教導安全習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to community groups for young people.","zh":"這個短語指面向年輕人的社區團體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sailing clubs","meaning":"帆船會","examples":[{"en":"The speaker speaks to sailing clubs in the area.","zh":"說話者向區內帆船會講解。"},{"en":"Sailing clubs are groups or organisations for people who sail boats as a sport or hobby.","zh":"sailing clubs是讓人以運動或嗜好形式駕帆船的團體或組織。"},{"en":"A sailing club may teach beginners how to control a small boat safely.","zh":"帆船會可能教初學者如何安全控制小船。"},{"en":"Sailing clubs need safety talks because members spend time on the water.","zh":"帆船會需要安全講座，因為會員會花時間在水上。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to communities built around sailing.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞帆船活動建立的社群。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the area","meaning":"在區內","examples":[{"en":"The speaker talks to groups in the area.","zh":"說話者向區內團體講解。"},{"en":"In the area means in the local district or nearby region.","zh":"in the area意思是在本地區或附近地區。"},{"en":"A new clinic may serve families in the area.","zh":"新診所可能服務區內家庭。"},{"en":"Local talks are useful because they address risks people nearby may actually face.","zh":"本地講座很有用，因為它們處理附近人士可能真正面對的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a nearby community or location.","zh":"這個短語指附近社區或地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the sorts of problems that","meaning":"……那類問題","examples":[{"en":"The speaker explains the sorts of problems that sailors may face.","zh":"說話者解釋水手可能面對的那類問題。"},{"en":"The sorts of problems that means the kinds of difficulties that can happen in a situation.","zh":"the sorts of problems that意思是在某情況中可能出現的困難種類。"},{"en":"A careers talk may explain the sorts of problems that nurses face during night shifts.","zh":"職業講座可能解釋護士夜班時面對的那類問題。"},{"en":"Understanding possible problems helps people prepare before they happen.","zh":"理解可能問題有助人們在問題發生前作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples of likely difficulties.","zh":"這個短語引入可能困難的例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sailors and swimmers","meaning":"水手和游泳人士","examples":[{"en":"Sailors and swimmers can face problems when the weather gets bad.","zh":"當天氣變壞，水手和游泳人士可能面對問題。"},{"en":"Sailors and swimmers are people who use the sea for boating or swimming.","zh":"sailors and swimmers是使用海洋划船或游泳的人。"},{"en":"Sailors and swimmers should check weather warnings before going into open water.","zh":"水手和游泳人士進入開放水域前應查看天氣警告。"},{"en":"Bad weather can put both boat users and swimmers in danger.","zh":"惡劣天氣可以令船隻使用者和游泳者都陷入危險。"},{"en":"This phrase names two groups who may need sea-safety advice.","zh":"這個短語命名兩類可能需要海上安全建議的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"suddenly gets bad","meaning":"突然變壞","examples":[{"en":"The weather can suddenly get bad at sea.","zh":"海上天氣可以突然變壞。"},{"en":"Suddenly gets bad means changes quickly from acceptable to dangerous or unpleasant.","zh":"suddenly gets bad意思是迅速由可接受變成危險或令人不快。"},{"en":"A school picnic may end early if the weather suddenly gets bad.","zh":"如果天氣突然變壞，學校野餐可能提早結束。"},{"en":"Sudden changes are risky because people may not have time to prepare.","zh":"突然變化有風險，因為人們可能沒有時間準備。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses unexpected worsening.","zh":"這個短語強調意料之外的惡化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"organise activities","meaning":"組織活動","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers organise activities to raise money.","zh":"義工組織活動來籌款。"},{"en":"To organise activities means to plan and arrange events or tasks.","zh":"organise activities意思是規劃和安排活動或任務。"},{"en":"A class committee may organise activities for the school open day.","zh":"班會可能為學校開放日組織活動。"},{"en":"Well-organised activities attract more people and run more smoothly.","zh":"組織良好的活動會吸引更多人，並運作得更順暢。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on planning events, not just joining them.","zh":"這個短語著重規劃活動，而不只是參加活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"raise money for","meaning":"為……籌款","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers organise activities to raise money for the institution.","zh":"義工組織活動為該機構籌款。"},{"en":"To raise money for something means to collect donations or income to support it.","zh":"raise money for某事，意思是收集捐款或收入來支持它。"},{"en":"Students may sell cakes to raise money for a local animal shelter.","zh":"學生可能賣蛋糕為本地動物收容所籌款。"},{"en":"Fundraising helps organisations buy equipment, pay bills or continue services.","zh":"籌款幫助機構購買設備、支付帳單或維持服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collecting financial support for a cause.","zh":"這個短語描述為某個目標收集財政支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"could not manage without","meaning":"沒有……便無法運作","examples":[{"en":"The institution could not manage without its fundraising volunteers.","zh":"該機構沒有籌款義工便無法運作。"},{"en":"Could not manage without someone means could not operate successfully without that person’s help.","zh":"could not manage without某人，意思是沒有該人的幫助就無法成功運作。"},{"en":"A school fair could not manage without parents who help set up stalls.","zh":"學校賣物會沒有協助搭建攤位的家長便無法運作。"},{"en":"Organisations depend heavily on people who do essential but less visible work.","zh":"機構很依賴做重要但較不顯眼工作的人。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that someone’s contribution is necessary.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人的貢獻是必要的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the training we get","meaning":"我們接受的訓練","examples":[{"en":"The training the volunteers get is a continuous process.","zh":"義工接受的訓練是一個持續過程。"},{"en":"The training we get means the instruction and practice given to us to do a job or task well.","zh":"the training we get意思是我們為做好工作或任務而得到的指導和練習。"},{"en":"The training new teachers get helps them manage lessons and support students.","zh":"新老師接受的訓練幫助他們管理課堂和支援學生。"},{"en":"Good training reduces fear because people know what to do in difficult situations.","zh":"良好訓練能減少恐懼，因為人們知道困難情況中該怎樣做。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to preparation received from an organisation.","zh":"這個短語指從機構得到的準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"continuous process","meaning":"持續過程","examples":[{"en":"The training is a continuous process.","zh":"訓練是一個持續過程。"},{"en":"A continuous process is something that keeps going over time rather than happening once.","zh":"continuous process是隨時間持續進行，而不是只發生一次的事情。"},{"en":"Learning a language is a continuous process because students must practise regularly.","zh":"學習語言是一個持續過程，因為學生必須定期練習。"},{"en":"Safety training must be continuous when equipment and risks change.","zh":"當設備和風險改變，安全訓練必須持續進行。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses ongoing development.","zh":"這個短語強調持續發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"聚焦於……","examples":[{"en":"The training focuses on technical competence and safe handling techniques.","zh":"訓練聚焦於技術能力和安全操作技巧。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give most attention to it.","zh":"focus on某事，意思是把大部分注意力放在它上面。"},{"en":"A driving lesson may focus on parking before moving on to busy roads.","zh":"駕駛課可能先聚焦於泊車，再進入繁忙道路。"},{"en":"Training focuses on the most important skills when mistakes could be dangerous.","zh":"當錯誤可能危險，訓練會聚焦於最重要技能。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main learning point.","zh":"這個短語指出主要學習重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"technical competence","meaning":"技術能力","examples":[{"en":"The training develops technical competence.","zh":"訓練培養技術能力。"},{"en":"Technical competence is the ability to use specialist skills, tools or procedures correctly.","zh":"technical competence是正確使用專門技能、工具或程序的能力。"},{"en":"A laboratory assistant needs technical competence to handle chemicals safely.","zh":"實驗室助理需要技術能力來安全處理化學品。"},{"en":"Technical competence reduces mistakes because people know exactly how equipment works.","zh":"技術能力能減少錯誤，因為人們清楚知道設備如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical skill in a specialised task.","zh":"這個短語描述專門任務中的實際技能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"safe handling techniques","meaning":"安全操作技巧","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers learn safe handling techniques.","zh":"義工學習安全操作技巧。"},{"en":"Safe handling techniques are methods for using, lifting or managing equipment without causing harm.","zh":"safe handling techniques是安全使用、搬動或管理設備而不造成傷害的方法。"},{"en":"Warehouse workers learn safe handling techniques before moving heavy boxes.","zh":"倉庫員工在搬動重箱前會學習安全操作技巧。"},{"en":"Safe handling prevents injuries and protects equipment from damage.","zh":"安全操作可以防止受傷，並保護設備免受損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in practical and physical training.","zh":"這個短語常見於實務和體能訓練。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"give someone the confidence to","meaning":"給予某人信心去……","examples":[{"en":"The training gives the speaker the confidence to deal with emergencies.","zh":"訓練給予說話者信心去應對緊急情況。"},{"en":"To give someone the confidence to do something means to make them feel able and ready to do it.","zh":"give someone the confidence to do something意思是令某人覺得自己有能力並準備好做某事。"},{"en":"Practice interviews can give students the confidence to answer questions clearly.","zh":"模擬面試可以給學生信心去清楚回答問題。"},{"en":"Confidence grows when people understand the steps and have practised them before.","zh":"當人們理解步驟並曾經練習，信心就會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase connects preparation with courage.","zh":"這個短語把準備與勇氣連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"deal with extreme situations","meaning":"應對極端情況","examples":[{"en":"The speaker has the confidence to deal with extreme situations.","zh":"說話者有信心應對極端情況。"},{"en":"To deal with extreme situations means to manage very difficult, dangerous or unusual events.","zh":"deal with extreme situations意思是處理非常困難、危險或不尋常的事件。"},{"en":"Emergency doctors must deal with extreme situations when several injured patients arrive together.","zh":"當多名傷者同時到達，急症醫生必須應對極端情況。"},{"en":"Training helps people stay organised when pressure is high.","zh":"訓練幫助人在壓力很高時保持有條理。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests serious challenges that require calm action.","zh":"這個短語暗示需要冷靜行動的嚴重挑戰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"without panicking","meaning":"不驚慌地","examples":[{"en":"The training helps volunteers deal with emergencies without panicking.","zh":"訓練幫助義工不驚慌地應對緊急情況。"},{"en":"Without panicking means without becoming so frightened that you cannot think or act properly.","zh":"without panicking意思是沒有害怕到無法正常思考或行動。"},{"en":"A teacher should lead students out of a building without panicking during a fire drill.","zh":"火警演習期間，老師應不驚慌地帶領學生離開建築物。"},{"en":"Staying calm helps people follow procedures and make safer decisions.","zh":"保持冷靜幫助人遵循程序並作出更安全決定。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights calm behaviour under pressure.","zh":"這個短語突顯壓力下的冷靜行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"first aid course","meaning":"急救課程","examples":[{"en":"The speaker had done a first aid course before he started.","zh":"說話者開始前曾修讀急救課程。"},{"en":"A first aid course teaches basic help for injured or ill people before professional care arrives.","zh":"first aid course教授在專業醫護到達前，如何為受傷或生病人士提供基本幫助。"},{"en":"Students may take a first aid course to learn how to treat cuts and call for help.","zh":"學生可能修讀急救課程，學習如何處理割傷和求助。"},{"en":"First aid training can make ordinary people more useful in emergencies.","zh":"急救訓練可以令普通人在緊急情況中更有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical medical support training.","zh":"這個短語指實用醫療支援訓練。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a big help with","meaning":"對……很有幫助","examples":[{"en":"The first aid course was a big help with casualty care activities.","zh":"急救課程對傷者護理活動很有幫助。"},{"en":"A big help with something means very useful support for doing that task.","zh":"a big help with某事，意思是對完成該任務很有用的支援。"},{"en":"A checklist can be a big help with packing for a school camp.","zh":"清單對學校宿營收拾行李很有幫助。"},{"en":"Training is a big help when people must act quickly and correctly.","zh":"當人們必須快速而正確地行動，訓練很有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something makes a task easier.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事令任務更容易。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"casualty care","meaning":"傷者護理","examples":[{"en":"First aid is useful for casualty care activities.","zh":"急救對傷者護理活動很有用。"},{"en":"Casualty care is the care given to injured people, especially after an accident or emergency.","zh":"casualty care是給予受傷人士的護理，尤其在意外或緊急情況後。"},{"en":"A lifeguard may provide casualty care to a swimmer with a head injury.","zh":"救生員可能為頭部受傷的游泳者提供傷者護理。"},{"en":"Good casualty care can keep an injured person stable until medical help arrives.","zh":"良好傷者護理可以讓傷者在醫療支援到達前保持穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in emergency and first-aid contexts.","zh":"這個短語用於緊急和急救語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"deal with ropes","meaning":"處理繩索","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers learn how to deal with ropes.","zh":"義工學習如何處理繩索。"},{"en":"To deal with ropes means to handle, use and manage ropes correctly.","zh":"deal with ropes意思是正確處理、使用和管理繩索。"},{"en":"Camp leaders may teach students how to deal with ropes before setting up tents.","zh":"露營領袖可能在搭帳篷前教學生如何處理繩索。"},{"en":"Ropes can become dangerous if they are tangled, loose or tied badly.","zh":"如果繩索纏結、鬆脫或打結不當，就可能變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical handling of ropes.","zh":"這個短語描述繩索的實際處理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tie knots","meaning":"打結","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers learn how to tie knots.","zh":"義工學習如何打結。"},{"en":"To tie knots means to fasten rope by looping and pulling it into secure shapes.","zh":"tie knots意思是透過繞圈和拉緊繩索，把它固定成安全形狀。"},{"en":"Scouts learn to tie knots so they can build shelters and secure equipment.","zh":"童軍學習打結，以便搭建遮蔽物和固定設備。"},{"en":"A badly tied knot can come loose and create danger.","zh":"打得不好的結可能鬆脫並造成危險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a practical rope skill.","zh":"這個短語指實用繩索技巧。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"essential skill","meaning":"必要技能","examples":[{"en":"Tying knots is an essential skill for lifeboat volunteers.","zh":"打結是救生艇義工的必要技能。"},{"en":"An essential skill is a skill that is necessary for doing a job or activity properly.","zh":"essential skill是正確完成工作或活動所必需的技能。"},{"en":"Time management is an essential skill for students who balance study and part-time work.","zh":"對兼顧學業和兼職的學生來說，時間管理是必要技能。"},{"en":"Without essential skills, people may make mistakes even if they are enthusiastic.","zh":"沒有必要技能，即使人有熱情也可能犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights something that cannot be ignored.","zh":"這個短語突顯不可忽視的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one-week residential course","meaning":"一星期住宿課程","examples":[{"en":"The speaker did a one-week residential course after a year.","zh":"說話者一年後修讀了一星期住宿課程。"},{"en":"A one-week residential course is a course lasting one week where participants stay at the training place.","zh":"one-week residential course是為期一星期，參加者住在訓練地點的課程。"},{"en":"A school may send student leaders to a one-week residential course during summer.","zh":"學校可能在夏天派學生領袖參加一星期住宿課程。"},{"en":"Staying at the training centre allows learners to practise intensively each day.","zh":"住在訓練中心讓學習者每天密集練習。"},{"en":"This phrase combines duration with living on site.","zh":"這個短語結合課程長度和住宿安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"led by specialists","meaning":"由專家帶領","examples":[{"en":"The residential course was led by specialists.","zh":"該住宿課程由專家帶領。"},{"en":"Led by specialists means guided or taught by people with expert knowledge in the area.","zh":"led by specialists意思是由在該範疇有專業知識的人指導或教授。"},{"en":"A first-aid workshop led by specialists can teach students safer techniques.","zh":"由專家帶領的急救工作坊，可以教學生更安全技巧。"},{"en":"Specialist-led training is useful when mistakes could be serious.","zh":"當錯誤可能嚴重時，由專家帶領的訓練很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies expert leadership.","zh":"這個短語指出專家領導。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"wave-tank","meaning":"造浪池","examples":[{"en":"The training centre had a wave-tank.","zh":"訓練中心設有造浪池。"},{"en":"A wave-tank is a special pool or tank that can create waves for testing or training.","zh":"wave-tank是一種可以製造波浪作測試或訓練的特別水池或水槽。"},{"en":"Engineers may use a wave-tank to test how a small boat handles rough water.","zh":"工程師可能使用造浪池測試小船如何應對洶湧水面。"},{"en":"Wave-tanks let learners practise safely without going into dangerous real seas.","zh":"造浪池讓學習者在不進入真實危險海域的情況下安全練習。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to controlled water-training equipment.","zh":"這個短語指受控的水上訓練設備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"create extreme weather conditions","meaning":"製造極端天氣情況","examples":[{"en":"The wave-tank could create extreme weather conditions.","zh":"造浪池可以製造極端天氣情況。"},{"en":"To create extreme weather conditions means to produce very difficult weather-like situations for practice or testing.","zh":"create extreme weather conditions意思是製造非常困難、類似天氣的情況作練習或測試。"},{"en":"A training centre may create strong wind and rain so firefighters can practise rescue work.","zh":"訓練中心可能製造強風和大雨，讓消防員練習救援。"},{"en":"Simulated extreme conditions help people prepare without facing uncontrolled danger.","zh":"模擬極端情況幫助人們準備，而不用面對不可控制的危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes artificial practice conditions that imitate real danger.","zh":"這個短語描述模仿真實危險的人造練習環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get experience at","meaning":"取得……經驗","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers could get experience at dealing with capsized boats.","zh":"義工可以取得處理翻側船隻的經驗。"},{"en":"To get experience at doing something means to practise it and become more familiar with it.","zh":"get experience at doing something意思是透過練習熟悉某事。"},{"en":"A student can get experience at public speaking by joining debate competitions.","zh":"學生可以透過參加辯論比賽取得公開演說經驗。"},{"en":"Experience helps people feel calmer when the real situation happens.","zh":"經驗幫助人在真實情況發生時更冷靜。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses learning through practice.","zh":"這個短語強調透過實踐學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"what to do if","meaning":"如果……該怎樣做","examples":[{"en":"The course taught volunteers what to do if the boat turned over.","zh":"課程教義工如果船翻側該怎樣做。"},{"en":"What to do if means the correct action to take when a particular situation happens.","zh":"what to do if意思是當某特定情況發生時應採取的正確行動。"},{"en":"Students should know what to do if the fire alarm rings during class.","zh":"學生應知道如果上課時火警鐘響起該怎樣做。"},{"en":"Knowing what to do in advance reduces panic during emergencies.","zh":"預先知道該怎樣做能減少緊急情況中的恐慌。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a response plan for a possible problem.","zh":"這個短語引入對可能問題的應對計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"turn over","meaning":"翻側","examples":[{"en":"The boat might turn over in a storm.","zh":"船在暴風雨中可能翻側。"},{"en":"To turn over means to flip upside down or onto its side.","zh":"turn over意思是翻轉、倒轉或側翻。"},{"en":"A child’s toy car may turn over if it goes too fast around a corner.","zh":"孩子的玩具車如果轉彎太快，可能會翻側。"},{"en":"A boat turning over is dangerous because people may fall into the water.","zh":"船翻側很危險，因為人可能跌入水中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious change in position.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重的位置變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in a storm at night","meaning":"在夜間暴風雨中","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers practised what to do in a storm at night.","zh":"義工練習在夜間暴風雨中該怎樣做。"},{"en":"In a storm at night means during bad weather with wind or rain when it is dark.","zh":"in a storm at night意思是在有風雨的惡劣天氣中，而且天色黑暗。"},{"en":"Drivers must be extra careful in a storm at night because visibility is poor.","zh":"司機在夜間暴風雨中必須格外小心，因為能見度差。"},{"en":"Rescue work becomes harder at night because waves, wind and darkness all add danger.","zh":"夜間救援更困難，因為海浪、風和黑暗都增加危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a difficult and risky setting.","zh":"這個短語描述困難而有風險的環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"since I started","meaning":"自我開始以來","examples":[{"en":"Since the speaker started, he has dealt with many emergencies.","zh":"自說話者開始以來，他已處理過許多緊急情況。"},{"en":"Since I started means from the time I began doing something until now.","zh":"since I started意思是由我開始做某事那一刻直到現在。"},{"en":"Since I started learning English, I have become more confident speaking to tourists.","zh":"自我開始學英語以來，我與遊客說話更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase links a starting point with later experience or change.","zh":"這個短語把起點與後來經驗或變化連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing progress over time.","zh":"它適合描述隨時間累積的進展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a range of","meaning":"一系列","examples":[{"en":"The speaker has dealt with a range of emergency situations.","zh":"說話者已處理過一系列緊急情況。"},{"en":"A range of something means several different types of it.","zh":"a range of某事，意思是幾種不同類型的該事物。"},{"en":"A school library should offer a range of books for different ages and interests.","zh":"學校圖書館應提供一系列適合不同年齡和興趣的書。"},{"en":"Facing a range of cases helps people become more flexible and experienced.","zh":"面對一系列個案能幫助人變得更靈活和有經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety within a category.","zh":"這個短語強調同一類別中的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"emergency situations","meaning":"緊急情況","examples":[{"en":"Lifeboat volunteers deal with emergency situations at sea.","zh":"救生艇義工處理海上的緊急情況。"},{"en":"Emergency situations are sudden events that need quick action to protect life or safety.","zh":"emergency situations是需要迅速行動以保護生命或安全的突發事件。"},{"en":"A fire, serious injury or missing swimmer can be an emergency situation.","zh":"火警、嚴重受傷或游泳者失蹤都可以是緊急情況。"},{"en":"Emergency situations require calm communication and clear roles.","zh":"緊急情況需要冷靜溝通和清晰角色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes urgent problems that cannot wait.","zh":"這個短語描述不能等待的急切問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hugely motivating","meaning":"非常令人有動力","examples":[{"en":"The work is hugely motivating.","zh":"這份工作非常令人有動力。"},{"en":"Hugely motivating means very inspiring and able to make someone want to keep working hard.","zh":"hugely motivating意思是非常鼓舞人心，能令人想繼續努力。"},{"en":"Seeing students improve can be hugely motivating for a teacher.","zh":"看見學生進步，對老師來說可以非常令人有動力。"},{"en":"Meaningful results motivate people because they can see that their effort matters.","zh":"有意義的成果會激勵人，因為他們看見自己的努力有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong positive emotional drive.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈正面推動力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not just about","meaning":"不只是關於……","examples":[{"en":"The work is not just about saving lives.","zh":"這份工作不只是關於拯救生命。"},{"en":"Not just about something means the subject includes more than that one obvious part.","zh":"not just about某事，意思是該主題包括的不只那個明顯部分。"},{"en":"Teaching is not just about explaining grammar; it is also about confidence and support.","zh":"教學不只是關於解釋文法；它也關乎信心和支援。"},{"en":"This phrase expands a narrow idea into a broader understanding.","zh":"這個短語把狹窄想法擴展為更廣理解。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting an oversimplified view.","zh":"當要糾正過度簡化的看法時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"saving lives","meaning":"拯救生命","examples":[{"en":"Lifeboat volunteers are involved in saving lives.","zh":"救生艇義工參與拯救生命。"},{"en":"Saving lives means preventing people from dying, especially in dangerous situations.","zh":"saving lives意思是防止人死亡，尤其在危險情況中。"},{"en":"Doctors, firefighters and lifeguards all do work connected with saving lives.","zh":"醫生、消防員和救生員都從事與拯救生命有關的工作。"},{"en":"Quick action can be the difference between danger and safety when lives are at risk.","zh":"當生命有危險，迅速行動可以決定危險與安全之間的差別。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the most serious kind of help.","zh":"這個短語描述最嚴重也最重要的幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the technology involved","meaning":"相關技術","examples":[{"en":"The speaker has learned a lot about the technology involved.","zh":"說話者學到了很多相關技術。"},{"en":"The technology involved means the machines, systems or tools used in an activity.","zh":"the technology involved意思是某活動中使用的機器、系統或工具。"},{"en":"A student filming a school event may need to understand the technology involved in cameras and sound.","zh":"拍攝學校活動的學生可能需要理解相機和收音方面的相關技術。"},{"en":"Knowing the technology involved helps people solve problems when equipment fails.","zh":"了解相關技術能在人們設備故障時幫助解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the technical side of a task.","zh":"這個短語指任務中的技術層面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"background in IT","meaning":"資訊科技背景","examples":[{"en":"The speaker’s background in IT has been useful.","zh":"說話者的資訊科技背景一直很有用。"},{"en":"A background in IT means previous knowledge, study or work experience in information technology.","zh":"background in IT意思是以前在資訊科技方面的知識、學習或工作經驗。"},{"en":"A person with a background in IT may help a charity improve its website and databases.","zh":"有資訊科技背景的人可能幫助慈善機構改善網站和資料庫。"},{"en":"Past experience can become useful in unexpected new roles.","zh":"過去經驗可以在意想不到的新角色中變得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone’s earlier training or experience in technology.","zh":"這個短語描述某人在科技方面的早期訓練或經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"use my expertise to","meaning":"運用我的專業去……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker can use his expertise to help other volunteers.","zh":"說話者可以運用自己的專業去幫助其他義工。"},{"en":"To use my expertise to do something means to apply my specialist knowledge or skills for a purpose.","zh":"use my expertise to do something意思是運用我的專門知識或技能去達成某目的。"},{"en":"A nurse may use her expertise to teach families how to care for elderly relatives.","zh":"護士可能運用自己的專業去教家庭如何照顧年老親人。"},{"en":"Expertise becomes valuable when it helps others solve real problems.","zh":"當專業能幫助他人解決真實問題，它就變得有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase links professional skill with practical help.","zh":"這個短語把專業技能與實際幫助連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"help other volunteers","meaning":"幫助其他義工","examples":[{"en":"The speaker uses his IT expertise to help other volunteers.","zh":"說話者運用自己的資訊科技專業幫助其他義工。"},{"en":"To help other volunteers means to support people who are also giving their time without pay.","zh":"help other volunteers意思是支援同樣無償付出時間的人。"},{"en":"An experienced volunteer may help other volunteers learn how to welcome visitors.","zh":"有經驗的義工可能幫助其他義工學習如何接待訪客。"},{"en":"Volunteers work better when they share skills instead of working alone.","zh":"當義工分享技能而不是各自工作，團隊會運作得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cooperation within a volunteer team.","zh":"這個短語描述義工團隊內的合作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a great group","meaning":"很好的團隊","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers are a great group.","zh":"這些義工是一個很好的團隊。"},{"en":"A great group is a team of people who are supportive, capable and pleasant to work with.","zh":"a great group是由互相支持、有能力並令人樂於合作的人組成的團隊。"},{"en":"A class can become a great group when students listen to and encourage one another.","zh":"當學生互相聆聽和鼓勵，班級可以成為很好的團隊。"},{"en":"Good teamwork makes difficult work feel less lonely.","zh":"良好團隊合作令困難工作感覺不那麼孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase praises the people in a team.","zh":"這個短語讚賞團隊中的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"like a family","meaning":"像一家人","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers are like a family.","zh":"這些義工像一家人。"},{"en":"Like a family means very close, supportive and caring, even if people are not related by blood.","zh":"like a family意思是非常親近、互相支持和關心，即使沒有血緣關係。"},{"en":"A sports team may feel like a family after years of training and travelling together.","zh":"運動隊經過多年一起訓練和外出比賽後，可能感覺像一家人。"},{"en":"People become like a family when they trust one another during difficult moments.","zh":"當人們在困難時刻互相信任，他們就會像一家人。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses emotional closeness in a group.","zh":"這個短語表達群體中的情感親近。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"drag yourself out of bed","meaning":"勉強自己起床","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers sometimes drag themselves out of bed on stormy nights.","zh":"義工有時在暴風雨夜晚勉強自己起床。"},{"en":"To drag yourself out of bed means to force yourself to get up when you are tired or unwilling.","zh":"drag yourself out of bed意思是在疲倦或不願意時強迫自己起床。"},{"en":"A student may drag herself out of bed for an early exam after a sleepless night.","zh":"學生可能在失眠一夜後，為早上考試勉強自己起床。"},{"en":"People drag themselves out of bed when duty is stronger than comfort.","zh":"當責任大於舒適，人們會勉強自己起床。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests effort, tiredness and reluctance.","zh":"這個短語暗示努力、疲累和不情願。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cold stormy night","meaning":"寒冷暴風雨的夜晚","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers may be called out on a cold stormy night.","zh":"義工可能在寒冷暴風雨的夜晚被召喚出動。"},{"en":"A cold stormy night is a night with low temperature, strong wind, rain or rough weather.","zh":"cold stormy night是氣溫低、有強風、大雨或惡劣天氣的夜晚。"},{"en":"Few people want to leave home on a cold stormy night unless there is an urgent reason.","zh":"除非有緊急理由，很少人想在寒冷暴風雨的夜晚離家。"},{"en":"Bad weather makes rescue work harder because people are tired, wet and less able to see clearly.","zh":"惡劣天氣令救援工作更困難，因為人會疲倦、濕透和較難看清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a difficult and uncomfortable setting.","zh":"這個短語營造困難而不舒服的環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the colder months","meaning":"較寒冷的月份","examples":[{"en":"The colder months can be the most rewarding time.","zh":"較寒冷的月份可以是最有成就感的時候。"},{"en":"The colder months are the part of the year when the weather is colder.","zh":"the colder months是一年中天氣較冷的時段。"},{"en":"In the colder months, elderly people may need extra help with heating and health checks.","zh":"在較寒冷的月份，長者可能需要額外取暖和健康檢查協助。"},{"en":"For rescue workers, colder months can bring more serious incidents and more meaningful work.","zh":"對救援人員來說，較寒冷的月份可能帶來更嚴重事故和更有意義的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a seasonal period, often autumn and winter.","zh":"這個短語指季節性時段，通常是秋冬。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rewarding time","meaning":"有成就感的時候","examples":[{"en":"The colder months can be the most rewarding time for volunteers.","zh":"較寒冷的月份可以是義工最有成就感的時候。"},{"en":"A rewarding time is a period that feels meaningful because effort leads to valuable results.","zh":"rewarding time是因努力帶來有價值成果而令人感到有意義的時段。"},{"en":"Exam season can be a rewarding time for teachers when students finally improve.","zh":"當學生終於進步，考試季節對老師來說可以是有成就感的時候。"},{"en":"Work feels rewarding when people can see that their help matters.","zh":"當人們看見自己的幫助很重要，工作就令人有成就感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional satisfaction from useful effort.","zh":"這個短語描述有用努力帶來的情感滿足。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"incidents tend to be more serious","meaning":"事故往往較嚴重","examples":[{"en":"The incidents tend to be more serious in the colder months.","zh":"較寒冷月份的事故往往較嚴重。"},{"en":"Incidents tend to be more serious means accidents or problems are usually more severe.","zh":"incidents tend to be more serious意思是意外或問題通常較嚴重。"},{"en":"Road incidents tend to be more serious during heavy rain because drivers cannot see clearly.","zh":"大雨期間道路事故往往較嚴重，因為司機看不清楚。"},{"en":"When conditions are harsh, small mistakes can lead to bigger consequences.","zh":"當條件惡劣，小錯誤可以導致更大後果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a general pattern, not every single case.","zh":"這個短語描述一般模式，而不是每一宗個案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make a huge difference to","meaning":"對……產生重大影響","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers can make a huge difference to the outcome.","zh":"義工可以對結果產生重大影響。"},{"en":"To make a huge difference to something means to have a very strong effect on it.","zh":"make a huge difference to某事，意思是對它產生非常強烈影響。"},{"en":"A clear explanation can make a huge difference to a student’s confidence before an exam.","zh":"清晰解釋可以對學生考試前的信心產生重大影響。"},{"en":"Fast rescue action can change whether an incident ends safely or tragically.","zh":"快速救援行動可以改變事故是安全結束還是悲劇收場。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses powerful practical impact.","zh":"這個短語強調強大的實際影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the outcome","meaning":"結果","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers can make a huge difference to the outcome of an incident.","zh":"義工可以對事故結果產生重大影響。"},{"en":"The outcome is the final result of a situation or event.","zh":"the outcome是某情況或事件的最終結果。"},{"en":"In a school debate, preparation can affect the outcome of the competition.","zh":"在學校辯論中，準備可以影響比賽結果。"},{"en":"In emergencies, small decisions can change the outcome dramatically.","zh":"在緊急情況中，小決定可以大幅改變結果。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what finally happens.","zh":"這個短語著重最後發生的事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"if any of you are interested","meaning":"如果你們當中有人感興趣","examples":[{"en":"The speaker invites listeners to join if any of them are interested.","zh":"說話者邀請聽眾加入，如果他們當中有人感興趣。"},{"en":"If any of you are interested means if one or more people in the group want to know more or take part.","zh":"if any of you are interested意思是如果群體中有一個或多個人想知道更多或參與。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “If any of you are interested, I can recommend extra reading.”","zh":"老師可能說：「如果你們當中有人感興趣，我可以推薦額外閱讀。」"},{"en":"This phrase politely invites people without pressuring everyone to join.","zh":"這個短語有禮地邀請人，而不向所有人施壓。"},{"en":"It is useful at the end of talks, announcements and invitations.","zh":"它適合用於講座、公告和邀請的結尾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 6/task-3":[{"front":"get the copy of","meaning":"收到……的副本","examples":[{"en":"Don got the copy of the article on recycling footwear.","zh":"Don 收到了關於回收鞋類文章的副本。"},{"en":"To get a copy of something means to receive or obtain one version of a document, article, or file.","zh":"get a copy of something 指收到或取得某份文件、文章或檔案的一個版本。"},{"en":"A student may get a copy of the timetable from the school office.","zh":"學生可能從校務處收到時間表副本。"},{"en":"If everyone gets a copy of the notes, the group can discuss the same information.","zh":"如果每個人都收到筆記副本，小組就可以討論同一份資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about documents that can be shared.","zh":"這個短語適用於談論可以分享的文件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"article on","meaning":"關於……的文章","examples":[{"en":"Bella emailed Don an article on recycling footwear.","zh":"Bella 電郵給 Don 一篇關於回收鞋類的文章。"},{"en":"An article on a topic is a written text about that subject.","zh":"article on a topic 指關於某主題的文章。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students an article on healthy eating before a class discussion.","zh":"老師可能在課堂討論前給學生一篇關於健康飲食的文章。"},{"en":"If an article on a topic is clear, students can use it to prepare ideas.","zh":"如果關於某主題的文章清晰，學生可以用它準備想法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the subject of a written article.","zh":"這個短語引出文章的主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"recycling footwear","meaning":"回收鞋類","examples":[{"en":"The students are discussing an article on recycling footwear.","zh":"學生正在討論一篇關於回收鞋類的文章。"},{"en":"Recycling footwear means collecting old shoes and processing or reusing them instead of throwing them away.","zh":"recycling footwear 指收集舊鞋並處理或再用，而不是把它們丟掉。"},{"en":"A school may start a campaign on recycling footwear after students clean out their lockers.","zh":"學校可能在學生清理儲物櫃後發起回收鞋類活動。"},{"en":"Recycling footwear can reduce waste, but only if the shoes are still usable or properly sorted.","zh":"回收鞋類可以減少浪費，但前提是鞋仍可使用或經妥善分類。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an environmental process for old shoes.","zh":"這個短語描述舊鞋的環保處理流程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"email someone","meaning":"電郵給某人","examples":[{"en":"Bella emailed Don the article on recycling footwear.","zh":"Bella 把關於回收鞋類的文章電郵給 Don。"},{"en":"To email someone means to send a message or file to that person by email.","zh":"email someone 指透過電郵向某人發送訊息或檔案。"},{"en":"A student may email the teacher a homework file before the deadline.","zh":"學生可能在截止日期前把功課檔案電郵給老師。"},{"en":"If you email someone the wrong document, they may become confused.","zh":"如果你把錯誤文件電郵給某人，對方可能會困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sending information electronically.","zh":"這個短語描述以電子方式傳送資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have a look at","meaning":"看一看","examples":[{"en":"Don has had a look at the article.","zh":"Don 已經看過那篇文章。"},{"en":"To have a look at something means to read, check, or examine it briefly.","zh":"have a look at something 指簡略閱讀、查看或檢查某物。"},{"en":"A teacher may have a look at a student’s essay before giving detailed comments.","zh":"老師可能先看一看學生文章，再給詳細評語。"},{"en":"If you have a look at the notice early, you will know what to bring.","zh":"如果你早點看一看通告，就會知道要帶甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and means checking something without sounding too formal.","zh":"這個短語較口語，意思是查看某物而語氣不太正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a good topic for","meaning":"……的好題目","examples":[{"en":"Bella asks whether recycling footwear is a good topic for their presentation.","zh":"Bella 問回收鞋類是否是他們匯報的好題目。"},{"en":"A good topic for something is a subject that fits the purpose, audience, and length of the task.","zh":"a good topic for something 指符合任務目的、對象和長度的主題。"},{"en":"Healthy school lunches could be a good topic for a student survey.","zh":"健康學校午餐可以是學生調查的好題目。"},{"en":"If a topic has enough facts and examples, it may be good for a presentation.","zh":"如果一個題目有足夠事實和例子，它可能適合作匯報題目。"},{"en":"This phrase helps judge whether a subject is suitable.","zh":"這個短語幫助判斷主題是否合適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"presentation","meaning":"匯報；簡報","examples":[{"en":"The students are preparing a presentation on recycling footwear.","zh":"學生正在準備關於回收鞋類的匯報。"},{"en":"A presentation is a talk given to explain information, ideas, or research to an audience.","zh":"presentation 指向觀眾解釋資料、想法或研究的演講。"},{"en":"Students may prepare a presentation with slides, pictures, and short notes.","zh":"學生可能用簡報、圖片和短筆記準備匯報。"},{"en":"A clear presentation helps listeners understand the main points quickly.","zh":"清晰的匯報幫助聽眾快速理解重點。"},{"en":"This word is often used in school, university, and work settings.","zh":"這個字常用於學校、大學和工作場合。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"before I started reading","meaning":"在我開始閱讀之前","examples":[{"en":"Before Don started reading the article, he thought there might not be enough to say.","zh":"在 Don 開始閱讀文章之前，他以為可能沒有足夠內容可談。"},{"en":"Before I started reading means at the time before I began to read a text.","zh":"before I started reading 指在我開始閱讀某篇文字之前。"},{"en":"Before I started reading the report, I thought the problem was simple.","zh":"在我開始閱讀報告之前，我以為問題很簡單。"},{"en":"If your opinion changes after reading, it means the text gave you new information.","zh":"如果你的看法在閱讀後改變，代表文章給了你新資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for showing how your understanding changed.","zh":"這個短語適合用來展示理解如何改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"although","meaning":"雖然","examples":[{"en":"Although recycling footwear is interesting, Don first thought the topic was too limited.","zh":"雖然回收鞋類很有趣，Don 起初覺得這個題目太有限。"},{"en":"Although introduces a contrast between two ideas.","zh":"although 用來引出兩個想法之間的對比。"},{"en":"Although the lesson was difficult, the examples helped students understand it.","zh":"雖然課堂很難，但例子幫助學生理解。"},{"en":"If you use although, the second part of the sentence usually gives an unexpected contrast.","zh":"如果你使用 although，句子的另一部分通常會給出意料之外的對比。"},{"en":"This word helps connect opposite or surprising ideas smoothly.","zh":"這個字幫助順暢連接相反或令人意外的想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"quite interesting","meaning":"頗有趣","examples":[{"en":"Don thought recycling footwear was quite interesting.","zh":"Don 覺得回收鞋類頗有趣。"},{"en":"Quite interesting means fairly or rather interesting, but not extremely exciting.","zh":"quite interesting 指相當有趣，但不是極度令人興奮。"},{"en":"The museum talk was quite interesting because it used real objects from the past.","zh":"博物館講座頗有趣，因為它使用了真正的歷史物件。"},{"en":"If a topic is quite interesting, students may want to learn more about it.","zh":"如果題目頗有趣，學生可能想了解更多。"},{"en":"This phrase gives mild positive opinion.","zh":"這個短語表達溫和正面的看法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"enough to say about","meaning":"有足夠內容可談","examples":[{"en":"Don first thought there was not enough to say about recycling footwear.","zh":"Don 起初以為回收鞋類沒有足夠內容可談。"},{"en":"Enough to say about a topic means there is enough information, detail, or argument to discuss.","zh":"enough to say about a topic 指有足夠資料、細節或論點可以討論。"},{"en":"A student may worry there is not enough to say about a very narrow topic.","zh":"學生可能擔心一個很狹窄的題目沒有足夠內容可談。"},{"en":"If a topic has examples, causes, results, and opinions, there is usually enough to say about it.","zh":"如果一個題目有例子、原因、結果和意見，通常就有足夠內容可談。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when judging whether a topic is rich enough.","zh":"這個短語適合用於判斷題目是否夠豐富。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"put shoes in recycling bins","meaning":"將鞋放入回收箱","examples":[{"en":"People put shoes in recycling bins when they want to recycle them.","zh":"人們想回收鞋時，會將鞋放入回收箱。"},{"en":"To put shoes in recycling bins means to place old footwear in special containers for collection.","zh":"put shoes in recycling bins 指把舊鞋放入專門收集回收物的箱中。"},{"en":"A family may put shoes in recycling bins after cleaning out the shoe cabinet.","zh":"家庭清理鞋櫃後，可能將鞋放入回收箱。"},{"en":"If people put dirty or broken shoes in bins, some items may later be rejected.","zh":"如果人們把骯髒或破損鞋放入回收箱，有些物品之後可能被拒收。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first step in shoe recycling.","zh":"這個短語描述鞋類回收的第一步。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recycling bins","meaning":"回收箱","examples":[{"en":"Old shoes are often placed in recycling bins.","zh":"舊鞋常被放入回收箱。"},{"en":"Recycling bins are containers used to collect materials that can be reused or processed again.","zh":"recycling bins 指用來收集可再用或再處理材料的容器。"},{"en":"Schools may place recycling bins for paper, plastic bottles, and old uniforms.","zh":"學校可能設置回收箱，收集紙張、膠樽和舊校服。"},{"en":"If recycling bins are clearly labelled, people are less likely to put the wrong items inside.","zh":"如果回收箱標示清楚，人們較不容易放錯物品。"},{"en":"This phrase names the containers used for collecting recyclables.","zh":"這個短語指出用來收集回收物的容器。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go to charity shops","meaning":"送到慈善商店","examples":[{"en":"Some recycled shoes go to charity shops.","zh":"有些回收鞋會送到慈善商店。"},{"en":"If items go to charity shops, they are sent there to be sold or donated for a good cause.","zh":"如果物品 go to charity shops，即它們被送到慈善商店出售或捐出，以支持公益。"},{"en":"Old books may go to charity shops after a family clears out a cupboard.","zh":"家庭清理櫃子後，舊書可能送到慈善商店。"},{"en":"If donated shoes are clean and wearable, they may go to charity shops instead of landfill.","zh":"如果捐出的鞋乾淨且可穿，它們可能送到慈善商店，而不是堆填區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where donated goods may be sent.","zh":"這個短語描述捐贈物品可能被送往哪裡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"charity shops","meaning":"慈善商店","examples":[{"en":"Some donated shoes are sold in charity shops.","zh":"有些捐贈鞋會在慈善商店出售。"},{"en":"Charity shops are shops that sell donated goods to raise money for charitable causes.","zh":"charity shops 指售賣捐贈物品以為慈善目的籌款的商店。"},{"en":"People may buy second-hand clothes from charity shops at low prices.","zh":"人們可能在慈善商店以低價購買二手衣物。"},{"en":"If charity shops receive good-quality donations, they can raise more money.","zh":"如果慈善商店收到高質素捐贈品，就能籌得更多善款。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shops linked with donation and reuse.","zh":"這個短語描述與捐贈和再用有關的商店。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"that is about it","meaning":"大概就是這樣","examples":[{"en":"Don first thought shoes went to charity shops and that was about it.","zh":"Don 起初以為鞋會送到慈善商店，大概就是這樣。"},{"en":"That is about it means there is nothing much more to add.","zh":"that is about it 指沒有太多其他東西要補充。"},{"en":"I cleaned my desk, sent two emails, and that was about it for the morning.","zh":"我清理了書桌、發了兩封電郵，早上大概就是這樣。"},{"en":"If someone says that is about it, they think the explanation is almost complete.","zh":"如果某人說 that is about it，他認為解釋差不多完整。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests the matter is simple or limited.","zh":"這個短語常暗示事情很簡單或有限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"there is much more to it than that","meaning":"事情遠不止如此","examples":[{"en":"Bella says there is much more to recycling footwear than that.","zh":"Bella 說回收鞋類的事情遠不止如此。"},{"en":"There is much more to it than that means the situation is more complex than it first seems.","zh":"there is much more to it than that 指情況比一開始看起來更複雜。"},{"en":"A student may think cooking is just following a recipe, but there is much more to it than that.","zh":"學生可能以為煮食只是跟食譜做，但事情遠不止如此。"},{"en":"If a topic includes hidden processes and problems, there is much more to it than people expect.","zh":"如果一個題目包含隱藏流程和問題，事情就比人們預期複雜得多。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects an overly simple view.","zh":"這個短語用來糾正過於簡單的看法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"realise that now","meaning":"現在明白了","examples":[{"en":"Don realises now that recycling footwear is a richer topic.","zh":"Don 現在明白回收鞋類是一個更豐富的題目。"},{"en":"To realise that now means to understand something at this point, often after learning more.","zh":"realise that now 指到了現在才明白某事，通常是在學到更多之後。"},{"en":"I realise now that revision works better when I start early.","zh":"我現在明白，如果早點開始，溫習會更有效。"},{"en":"If someone realises something now, their earlier opinion may have changed.","zh":"如果某人現在明白某事，他早前的看法可能已改變。"},{"en":"This phrase shows new understanding.","zh":"這個短語顯示新的理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be keen to","meaning":"很想；熱衷於","examples":[{"en":"Don is keen to research the topic more.","zh":"Don 很想進一步研究這個題目。"},{"en":"To be keen to do something means to be eager or very interested in doing it.","zh":"be keen to do something 指很想或很有興趣做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be keen to join the debate team after watching a competition.","zh":"學生觀看比賽後，可能很想加入辯論隊。"},{"en":"If people are keen to learn, they usually ask more questions.","zh":"如果人們熱衷於學習，通常會問更多問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong interest and willingness.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈興趣和意願。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"research the topic","meaning":"研究這個題目","examples":[{"en":"The students want to research the topic of recycling footwear.","zh":"學生想研究回收鞋類這個題目。"},{"en":"To research the topic means to collect information and study a subject carefully.","zh":"research the topic 指收集資料並仔細研究某主題。"},{"en":"Students may research a topic by reading articles, watching interviews, and checking statistics.","zh":"學生可能透過閱讀文章、觀看訪問和查找統計數字來研究題目。"},{"en":"Good research helps a presentation become more accurate and convincing.","zh":"良好研究能令匯報更準確和有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious preparation before speaking or writing.","zh":"這個短語描述演講或寫作前的認真準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"one of the things","meaning":"其中一件事","examples":[{"en":"One of the things Don did not realise was how many trainers get recycled.","zh":"Don 沒有意識到的其中一件事，是有多少運動鞋被回收。"},{"en":"One of the things means one point, fact, or example among several.","zh":"one of the things 指幾個重點、事實或例子中的其中一個。"},{"en":"One of the things students worry about before exams is running out of time.","zh":"學生考試前擔心的其中一件事，是時間不夠。"},{"en":"If you say one of the things, listeners expect more than one point may exist.","zh":"如果你說 one of the things，聽眾會預期可能還有其他重點。"},{"en":"This phrase helps introduce one item from a larger group.","zh":"這個短語幫助引入較大群體中的一項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"did not realise until","meaning":"直到……才意識到","examples":[{"en":"Don did not realise the scale of trainer recycling until he read the article.","zh":"Don 直到讀了文章，才意識到運動鞋回收的規模。"},{"en":"Did not realise until means someone only understood something after a later event or moment.","zh":"did not realise until 指某人到較後事件或時刻才明白某事。"},{"en":"I did not realise how far the station was until I walked there.","zh":"我直到走過去，才意識到車站有多遠。"},{"en":"If people do not realise a problem until they read about it, the article has changed their understanding.","zh":"如果人們直到讀到相關資料才意識到問題，文章就改變了他們的理解。"},{"en":"This phrase shows delayed understanding.","zh":"這個短語顯示延遲理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pairs of trainers","meaning":"多雙運動鞋","examples":[{"en":"Many pairs of trainers are recycled each year.","zh":"每年有多雙運動鞋被回收。"},{"en":"Pairs of trainers means sets of two sports shoes worn together.","zh":"pairs of trainers 指成雙一起穿的運動鞋。"},{"en":"A sports shop may sell hundreds of pairs of trainers before a school running event.","zh":"學校跑步活動前，運動用品店可能售出數百雙運動鞋。"},{"en":"If many pairs of trainers are thrown away, recycling becomes more important.","zh":"如果許多雙運動鞋被丟棄，回收就變得更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase counts trainers as complete pairs, not single shoes.","zh":"這個短語把運動鞋以完整一雙來計算，而不是單隻鞋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get recycled","meaning":"被回收","examples":[{"en":"A large number of trainers get recycled.","zh":"大量運動鞋被回收。"},{"en":"To get recycled means to be collected and processed for reuse instead of being thrown away.","zh":"get recycled 指被收集並處理作再用，而不是被丟棄。"},{"en":"Plastic bottles get recycled when people put them in the correct bins.","zh":"膠樽被放進正確回收箱後，就會被回收。"},{"en":"If shoes get recycled properly, fewer of them end up in landfill.","zh":"如果鞋被妥善回收，較少鞋會進入堆填區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what happens to waste materials after collection.","zh":"這個短語描述廢物被收集後發生的事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"wear them all the time","meaning":"經常穿着它們","examples":[{"en":"Many young people wear trainers all the time.","zh":"許多年輕人經常穿運動鞋。"},{"en":"To wear them all the time means to use them very often or almost every day.","zh":"wear them all the time 指非常常用或幾乎每天穿着它們。"},{"en":"Some students wear hoodies all the time because they are comfortable.","zh":"有些學生經常穿連帽衫，因為很舒服。"},{"en":"If people wear the same shoes all the time, the soles may wear out quickly.","zh":"如果人們經常穿同一雙鞋，鞋底可能很快磨損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequent use.","zh":"這個短語描述頻繁使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"become more popular than","meaning":"變得比……更受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Trainers have become more popular than ordinary shoes.","zh":"運動鞋已變得比普通鞋更受歡迎。"},{"en":"To become more popular than something means to be liked or chosen by more people than that thing.","zh":"become more popular than something 指比某物更受人喜愛或更常被選擇。"},{"en":"Online payment has become more popular than cash in many shops.","zh":"在許多商店，電子支付已變得比現金更受歡迎。"},{"en":"If trainers become more popular than formal shoes, shops may stock more sports styles.","zh":"如果運動鞋變得比正式鞋更受歡迎，店舖可能上架更多運動款式。"},{"en":"This phrase compares changes in popularity.","zh":"這個短語比較受歡迎程度的變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ordinary shoes","meaning":"普通鞋","examples":[{"en":"Trainers are now more popular than ordinary shoes.","zh":"運動鞋現在比普通鞋更受歡迎。"},{"en":"Ordinary shoes are regular shoes for daily use, not special sports shoes or fashion items.","zh":"ordinary shoes 指日常穿着的一般鞋，不是專門運動鞋或時尚款式。"},{"en":"A student may wear ordinary shoes with school uniform on formal days.","zh":"學生在正式日子可能穿普通鞋配校服。"},{"en":"If people prefer trainers, ordinary shoes may be worn less often.","zh":"如果人們較喜歡運動鞋，普通鞋可能較少被穿。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts simple everyday footwear with more specialised shoes.","zh":"這個短語把簡單日常鞋與較專門的鞋作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"I guess","meaning":"我想；我估計","examples":[{"en":"Don says, “I guess they are very hard-wearing.”","zh":"Don 說：「我想它們很耐穿。」"},{"en":"I guess means I think so, but I am not completely certain.","zh":"I guess 指我認為如此，但不是完全肯定。"},{"en":"I guess the library is closed because all the lights are off.","zh":"我想圖書館已關門，因為所有燈都關了。"},{"en":"If someone says I guess, they are giving an opinion or assumption softly.","zh":"如果某人說 I guess，他是在較溫和地表達意見或推測。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a statement sound less forceful.","zh":"這個短語令陳述聽起來較不強硬。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hard-wearing","meaning":"耐穿","examples":[{"en":"Trainers are popular because they are hard-wearing.","zh":"運動鞋受歡迎，因為它們耐穿。"},{"en":"Hard-wearing means strong and able to last even with frequent use.","zh":"hard-wearing 指堅固，能在頻繁使用下維持很久。"},{"en":"A hard-wearing schoolbag can survive daily books, rain, and crowded buses.","zh":"耐用的書包可以承受每天裝書、下雨和擠巴士。"},{"en":"If shoes are hard-wearing, people can use them for sport, travel, and everyday walking.","zh":"如果鞋耐穿，人們可以用它們做運動、旅行和日常步行。"},{"en":"This word describes durability.","zh":"這個字描述耐用程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"look a bit casual","meaning":"看起來有點休閒","examples":[{"en":"Don thinks trainers look a bit casual for school uniform.","zh":"Don 覺得運動鞋配校服看起來有點休閒。"},{"en":"To look a bit casual means to appear slightly informal or not very smart.","zh":"look a bit casual 指看起來稍微不正式或不夠整齊。"},{"en":"Jeans may look a bit casual for a formal interview.","zh":"牛仔褲對正式面試來說可能看起來有點休閒。"},{"en":"If clothing looks too casual, a school or workplace may not allow it.","zh":"如果衣着看起來太休閒，學校或工作場所可能不容許。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a mild judgement about appearance.","zh":"這個短語對外觀作出溫和評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"school uniform","meaning":"校服","examples":[{"en":"Don does not think trainers are right for school uniform.","zh":"Don 不認為運動鞋適合校服。"},{"en":"A school uniform is a set of clothes students must wear to school.","zh":"school uniform 指學生上學必須穿着的一套服裝。"},{"en":"A school uniform may include a shirt, tie, skirt or trousers, and suitable shoes.","zh":"校服可能包括恤衫、領呔、裙或褲，以及合適鞋履。"},{"en":"If footwear does not match the school uniform, students may look less formal.","zh":"如果鞋履不配校服，學生可能看起來不夠正式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to standard clothing required by a school.","zh":"這個短語指學校要求的標準服裝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be right for","meaning":"適合……","examples":[{"en":"Don does not think trainers are right for school uniform.","zh":"Don 不認為運動鞋適合校服。"},{"en":"To be right for something means to be suitable or appropriate for it.","zh":"be right for something 指適合某事或某場合。"},{"en":"A quiet room is right for studying, but not right for a noisy party.","zh":"安靜房間適合溫習，但不適合嘈吵派對。"},{"en":"If shoes are not right for a formal event, the wearer may look out of place.","zh":"如果鞋不適合正式活動，穿着者可能顯得格格不入。"},{"en":"This phrase judges suitability.","zh":"這個短語用來判斷合適程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"look quite smart on","meaning":"穿在……身上看起來頗整齊","examples":[{"en":"Bella thinks some trainers look quite smart on pupils.","zh":"Bella 認為有些運動鞋穿在學生身上看起來頗整齊。"},{"en":"To look quite smart on someone means to look neat, tidy, and fairly formal when that person wears it.","zh":"look quite smart on someone 指某人穿上後看起來整潔、端正，而且頗正式。"},{"en":"A dark jacket can look quite smart on a student during a speech competition.","zh":"深色外套穿在學生身上參加演講比賽時，可能看起來頗整齊。"},{"en":"If trainers are clean and simple, they may look smart rather than messy.","zh":"如果運動鞋乾淨又簡約，它們可能看起來整齊，而不是邋遢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how clothing appears on a person.","zh":"這個短語描述衣物穿在人身上的外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pupils","meaning":"學生","examples":[{"en":"Some trainers look quite smart on pupils.","zh":"有些運動鞋穿在學生身上看起來頗整齊。"},{"en":"Pupils are children or young people who study at school.","zh":"pupils 指在學校讀書的兒童或年輕人。"},{"en":"Pupils often wear uniforms and follow school rules during lessons.","zh":"學生上課期間通常穿校服並遵守校規。"},{"en":"If pupils wear comfortable shoes, they may move around school more easily.","zh":"如果學生穿舒適鞋子，在校內走動可能更方便。"},{"en":"This word is common in British English for school students.","zh":"這個字在英式英語中常指中小學生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a scruffy old pair of shoes","meaning":"一雙殘舊邋遢的鞋","examples":[{"en":"Bella thinks smart trainers can look better than a scruffy old pair of shoes.","zh":"Bella 認為整齊的運動鞋可以比一雙殘舊邋遢的鞋更好看。"},{"en":"A scruffy old pair of shoes is a pair of shoes that looks dirty, worn, and untidy.","zh":"a scruffy old pair of shoes 指看起來骯髒、磨損又不整齊的一雙鞋。"},{"en":"A student should not wear a scruffy old pair of shoes to a graduation ceremony.","zh":"學生不應穿一雙殘舊邋遢的鞋出席畢業典禮。"},{"en":"If shoes become too scruffy, they may make the whole uniform look untidy.","zh":"如果鞋變得太邋遢，可能令整套校服看起來不整潔。"},{"en":"This phrase describes poor appearance caused by age and wear.","zh":"這個短語描述因老舊和磨損造成的不佳外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"keep shoes a long time","meaning":"把鞋保留很久","examples":[{"en":"Bella asks Don whether he keeps shoes a long time.","zh":"Bella 問 Don 是否把鞋保留很久。"},{"en":"To keep shoes a long time means to continue using or storing them for many months or years.","zh":"keep shoes a long time 指繼續使用或存放鞋很多月或多年。"},{"en":"Some people keep shoes a long time if they are comfortable and still look good.","zh":"如果鞋舒服而且仍好看，有些人會把鞋保留很久。"},{"en":"If you keep shoes a long time, you may repair them instead of buying new ones quickly.","zh":"如果你把鞋保留很久，你可能會修理它們，而不是很快買新鞋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-term use or ownership.","zh":"這個短語描述長期使用或擁有。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tend to","meaning":"往往；通常會","examples":[{"en":"Don tends to wear his old shoes for dirty jobs.","zh":"Don 通常會穿舊鞋做骯髒工作。"},{"en":"To tend to do something means to usually do it or be likely to do it.","zh":"tend to do something 指通常會做某事，或很可能做某事。"},{"en":"I tend to study better in the morning than late at night.","zh":"我通常早上比深夜溫習得更好。"},{"en":"If people tend to keep old shoes for chores, fewer shoes may be recycled immediately.","zh":"如果人們通常把舊鞋留來做雜務，較少鞋會立即被回收。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a usual habit or pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述慣常習慣或模式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"old pairs","meaning":"舊鞋","examples":[{"en":"Don uses his old pairs of shoes for cleaning his bike.","zh":"Don 用他的舊鞋來清潔單車。"},{"en":"Old pairs means pairs of items that have been used for a long time.","zh":"old pairs 指已使用很久的一雙雙物品。"},{"en":"A family may keep old pairs of gloves for gardening.","zh":"家庭可能保留舊手套來做園藝。"},{"en":"If old pairs of shoes are still useful, people may not throw them away.","zh":"如果舊鞋仍有用，人們可能不會丟掉它們。"},{"en":"This phrase often refers to old but still usable items.","zh":"這個短語常指舊但仍可用的物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dirty jobs","meaning":"骯髒工作","examples":[{"en":"Don wears old shoes for dirty jobs like cleaning his bike.","zh":"Don 穿舊鞋做清潔單車等骯髒工作。"},{"en":"Dirty jobs are tasks that make clothes, hands, or shoes dusty, muddy, or greasy.","zh":"dirty jobs 指會令衣服、雙手或鞋沾塵、沾泥或沾油的工作。"},{"en":"Gardening, painting, and washing a car can be dirty jobs.","zh":"園藝、油漆和洗車都可以是骯髒工作。"},{"en":"If a job is dirty, people often wear old clothes so good ones are not damaged.","zh":"如果工作很髒，人們通常穿舊衣服，以免好衣物受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical work that creates mess.","zh":"這個短語描述會弄髒東西的實際工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"I must admit","meaning":"我必須承認","examples":[{"en":"Bella says, “I must admit, I have recycled some perfectly good shoes.”","zh":"Bella 說：「我必須承認，我曾經回收一些完全沒問題的鞋。」"},{"en":"I must admit is used when someone honestly accepts something, often with slight embarrassment.","zh":"I must admit 用於某人誠實承認某事，常帶一點尷尬。"},{"en":"I must admit, I forgot to read the instructions before starting the homework.","zh":"我必須承認，我開始做功課前忘了看指示。"},{"en":"If someone says I must admit, they are preparing to confess or agree with something true.","zh":"如果某人說 I must admit，他正準備承認或同意某件真實的事。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds honest and slightly self-critical.","zh":"這個短語聽起來誠實而略帶自我批評。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"perfectly good shoes","meaning":"完全沒問題的鞋","examples":[{"en":"Bella has recycled some perfectly good shoes.","zh":"Bella 曾經回收一些完全沒問題的鞋。"},{"en":"Perfectly good shoes are shoes that are still usable, clean, and not damaged.","zh":"perfectly good shoes 指仍可使用、乾淨而沒有損壞的鞋。"},{"en":"It is wasteful to throw away perfectly good shoes just because the colour feels boring.","zh":"只因顏色覺得沉悶就丟掉完全沒問題的鞋，是浪費。"},{"en":"If perfectly good shoes are donated, someone else may be able to wear them.","zh":"如果完全沒問題的鞋被捐出，其他人可能可以穿。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the shoes did not really need to be discarded.","zh":"這個短語強調鞋其實不需要被丟棄。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"go out of fashion","meaning":"過時","examples":[{"en":"The shoes had not gone out of fashion.","zh":"那些鞋並沒有過時。"},{"en":"To go out of fashion means to stop being stylish or popular.","zh":"go out of fashion 指不再時髦或不再受歡迎。"},{"en":"A jacket may go out of fashion if people no longer like that colour or cut.","zh":"如果人們不再喜歡某種顏色或剪裁，一件外套可能會過時。"},{"en":"If shoes go out of fashion, some people stop wearing them even though they still fit.","zh":"如果鞋過時，有些人即使仍合穿也會停止穿。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing style trends.","zh":"這個短語描述時尚潮流的變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"still fit","meaning":"仍然合穿","examples":[{"en":"The shoes still fit Bella when she recycled them.","zh":"Bella 回收那些鞋時，它們仍然合穿。"},{"en":"Still fit means the size is still right and the item can still be worn comfortably.","zh":"still fit 指尺碼仍然合適，物品仍可舒適穿着。"},{"en":"A school blazer may still fit a student after summer if they have not grown much.","zh":"如果學生暑假後沒有長高很多，校褸可能仍然合穿。"},{"en":"If shoes still fit, throwing them away may be unnecessary.","zh":"如果鞋仍然合穿，丟掉它們可能沒有必要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continued suitability in size.","zh":"這個短語描述尺碼仍然適合。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"look great on","meaning":"穿在……身上好看","examples":[{"en":"Bella recycled the shoes because they did not look great on her anymore.","zh":"Bella 回收那些鞋，因為它們穿在她身上不再好看。"},{"en":"To look great on someone means to suit that person and make them look good.","zh":"look great on someone 指適合某人，並令那人看起來好看。"},{"en":"That dark blue dress looks great on her because it matches her style.","zh":"那條深藍色裙穿在她身上很好看，因為配合她的風格。"},{"en":"If clothes no longer look great on someone, they may stop wearing them even if they are still new.","zh":"如果衣物穿在某人身上不再好看，即使仍然很新，他也可能停止穿。"},{"en":"This phrase judges appearance on a specific person.","zh":"這個短語評價某物穿在特定人身上的外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"that is awful, is it not?","meaning":"那很糟糕，對吧？","examples":[{"en":"Bella thinks recycling perfectly good shoes for appearance is awful.","zh":"Bella 覺得只因外觀而回收完全沒問題的鞋很糟糕。"},{"en":"That is awful, is it not? is used to say something is bad and invite agreement.","zh":"That is awful, is it not? 用來表示某事很糟糕，並邀請對方同意。"},{"en":"Throwing away clean food is awful, is it not?","zh":"丟掉乾淨食物很糟糕，對吧？"},{"en":"If someone uses this question, they expect the listener to share their judgement.","zh":"如果某人使用這個問題，他預期聽者會同意他的判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase combines criticism with a tag question.","zh":"這個短語把批評與附加問句結合。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be common because","meaning":"因為……而常見","examples":[{"en":"Don thinks this behaviour is common because there is so much choice.","zh":"Don 認為這種行為很常見，因為選擇太多。"},{"en":"Be common because means happen often for a particular reason.","zh":"be common because 指因某個原因而經常發生。"},{"en":"Online shopping is common because people can compare prices quickly.","zh":"網上購物很常見，因為人們可以快速比較價格。"},{"en":"If wasteful behaviour is common because products are cheap, people may buy too much.","zh":"如果浪費行為因產品便宜而常見，人們可能買太多。"},{"en":"This phrase links frequency with cause.","zh":"這個短語把常見程度與原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"so much choice","meaning":"太多選擇","examples":[{"en":"People may discard shoes because there is so much choice.","zh":"人們可能因為選擇太多而丟棄鞋。"},{"en":"So much choice means there are many options available.","zh":"so much choice 指有很多選項可選。"},{"en":"A student may take a long time to choose lunch when there is so much choice in the canteen.","zh":"如果飯堂有太多選擇，學生可能花很久才選午餐。"},{"en":"If there is so much choice in shops, people may replace items before they are worn out.","zh":"如果店舖有太多選擇，人們可能在物品未用壞前就替換它們。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest freedom, but also waste or indecision.","zh":"這個短語可以表示自由，也可以暗示浪費或猶豫不決。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"recent sales of","meaning":"近年……的銷售","examples":[{"en":"The article says recent sales of footwear have increased enormously.","zh":"文章說近年鞋類銷售大幅增加。"},{"en":"Recent sales of something means the amount sold in the near past.","zh":"recent sales of something 指最近一段時間某物售出的數量。"},{"en":"Recent sales of school tablets rose after online lessons became common.","zh":"網課普及後，近年學校平板電腦的銷售上升。"},{"en":"If recent sales of a product increase, shops may order more stock.","zh":"如果某產品近年銷售增加，店舖可能訂購更多存貨。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about market trends.","zh":"這個短語適合用於談論市場趨勢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"footwear","meaning":"鞋類","examples":[{"en":"Sales of footwear have increased enormously.","zh":"鞋類銷售已大幅增加。"},{"en":"Footwear means items worn on the feet, such as shoes, boots, sandals, and trainers.","zh":"footwear 指穿在腳上的物品，例如鞋、靴、涼鞋和運動鞋。"},{"en":"A sports shop sells footwear for running, football, hiking, and everyday walking.","zh":"運動用品店售賣跑步、足球、遠足和日常步行用的鞋類。"},{"en":"If footwear sales rise, more old shoes may eventually enter recycling systems.","zh":"如果鞋類銷售上升，更多舊鞋最終可能進入回收系統。"},{"en":"This word is more formal and general than shoes.","zh":"這個字比 shoes 更正式和概括。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"increase enormously","meaning":"大幅增加","examples":[{"en":"Recent footwear sales have increased enormously.","zh":"近年鞋類銷售已大幅增加。"},{"en":"To increase enormously means to rise by a very large amount.","zh":"increase enormously 指以非常大的幅度上升。"},{"en":"The number of online lessons increased enormously when schools closed.","zh":"學校停課時，網上課堂數目大幅增加。"},{"en":"If sales increase enormously, factories may produce more goods quickly.","zh":"如果銷售大幅增加，工廠可能迅速生產更多貨品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very big rise.","zh":"這個短語描述非常大的上升。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"that did not surprise me","meaning":"那並不令我驚訝","examples":[{"en":"Bella says the rise in footwear sales did not surprise her.","zh":"Bella 說鞋類銷售上升並不令她驚訝。"},{"en":"That did not surprise me means I expected it or found it easy to believe.","zh":"that did not surprise me 指我早有預期，或覺得很容易相信。"},{"en":"The crowded library did not surprise me because exams were coming.","zh":"圖書館很擠並不令我驚訝，因為考試快到了。"},{"en":"If a result matches what you already thought, it may not surprise you.","zh":"如果結果符合你原本想法，它可能不會令你驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that information feels predictable.","zh":"這個短語表示資料令人覺得可預料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the amount of","meaning":"……的數量","examples":[{"en":"The amount of recycled footwear has fallen.","zh":"已回收鞋類的數量下降了。"},{"en":"The amount of something means the quantity or level of it.","zh":"the amount of something 指某物的數量或水平。"},{"en":"The amount of homework can affect how much time students have to rest.","zh":"功課的數量可以影響學生有多少時間休息。"},{"en":"If the amount of waste rises, recycling services may need more space and staff.","zh":"如果廢物數量上升，回收服務可能需要更多空間和人手。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for measuring how much there is.","zh":"這個短語用於量度有多少某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"recycled footwear","meaning":"已回收鞋類","examples":[{"en":"The amount of recycled footwear has fallen.","zh":"已回收鞋類的數量下降了。"},{"en":"Recycled footwear means shoes that have been collected for reuse, resale, or material processing.","zh":"recycled footwear 指已被收集作再用、再售或材料處理的鞋。"},{"en":"A charity may sort recycled footwear into shoes for sale and shoes for material recovery.","zh":"慈善機構可能把已回收鞋類分類為可出售鞋和可回收材料鞋。"},{"en":"If recycled footwear is dirty or damaged, it may not be accepted for resale.","zh":"如果已回收鞋類骯髒或損壞，可能不會被接受再售。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to shoes after they enter a recycling system.","zh":"這個短語指進入回收系統後的鞋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fall","meaning":"下降","examples":[{"en":"The amount of recycled footwear has fallen from a previous level.","zh":"已回收鞋類的數量已從之前水平下降。"},{"en":"To fall means to decrease or become lower.","zh":"fall 指減少或變低。"},{"en":"Temperatures fall at night, so hikers need warmer clothes.","zh":"夜晚氣溫下降，所以遠足者需要更保暖衣物。"},{"en":"If recycling rates fall, more waste may go to landfill.","zh":"如果回收率下降，更多廢物可能進入堆填區。"},{"en":"This word describes a downward change.","zh":"這個字描述向下變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"compared to","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"The recycling rate is now six percent compared to a previous level of eleven percent.","zh":"回收率現時是百分之六，與之前百分之十一的水平相比有所下降。"},{"en":"Compared to means measured or considered against another number, thing, or situation.","zh":"compared to 指與另一個數字、事物或情況作比較。"},{"en":"This month’s electricity bill is high compared to last month’s bill.","zh":"這個月的電費與上個月相比很高。"},{"en":"If six percent is compared to eleven percent, the drop becomes clear.","zh":"如果把百分之六與百分之十一相比，跌幅就變得清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show difference through comparison.","zh":"這個短語透過比較顯示差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"previous level of","meaning":"之前……的水平","examples":[{"en":"The previous level of recycled footwear was eleven percent.","zh":"之前已回收鞋類的水平是百分之十一。"},{"en":"Previous level of something means the earlier amount, rate, or standard before a change.","zh":"previous level of something 指改變前較早的數量、比率或標準。"},{"en":"A school’s current attendance is lower than the previous level of ninety-five percent.","zh":"學校現時出席率低於之前百分之九十五的水平。"},{"en":"If the previous level was higher, a fall may suggest a new problem.","zh":"如果之前水平較高，下降可能顯示新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase compares present data with earlier data.","zh":"這個短語把現時數據與較早數據作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not seem to make sense","meaning":"似乎說不通","examples":[{"en":"The fall in recycled footwear does not seem to make sense.","zh":"已回收鞋類數量下降似乎說不通。"},{"en":"If something does not seem to make sense, it appears confusing or illogical.","zh":"如果某事 does not seem to make sense，即它看起來令人困惑或不合邏輯。"},{"en":"The timetable does not seem to make sense because two exams are at the same time.","zh":"時間表似乎說不通，因為兩場考試在同一時間。"},{"en":"If sales rise but recycling falls, the situation may not seem to make sense at first.","zh":"如果銷售上升但回收下降，情況起初可能說不通。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that more explanation is needed.","zh":"這個短語表示需要更多解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"go through the recycling process","meaning":"經過回收流程","examples":[{"en":"Not all footwear goes through the recycling process.","zh":"並非所有鞋類都會經過回收流程。"},{"en":"To go through the recycling process means to pass through the steps of sorting, checking, and reuse or treatment.","zh":"go through the recycling process 指經過分類、檢查、再用或處理等步驟。"},{"en":"Plastic bottles go through the recycling process after being collected from bins.","zh":"膠樽從回收箱收集後會經過回收流程。"},{"en":"If shoes are too dirty, they may not go through the whole recycling process.","zh":"如果鞋太骯髒，可能無法經過整個回收流程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes completing a series of recycling steps.","zh":"這個短語描述完成一連串回收步驟。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"recycling process","meaning":"回收流程","examples":[{"en":"Some footwear is rejected before completing the recycling process.","zh":"有些鞋類在完成回收流程前被拒收。"},{"en":"A recycling process is a series of steps used to collect, sort, clean, reuse, or process materials.","zh":"recycling process 指用來收集、分類、清潔、再用或處理材料的一連串步驟。"},{"en":"The recycling process for paper may include collection, sorting, pulping, and remaking paper.","zh":"紙張回收流程可能包括收集、分類、打漿和重新造紙。"},{"en":"If the recycling process is strict, damaged items may be removed early.","zh":"如果回收流程嚴格，損壞物品可能早早被移除。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how recycling is organised.","zh":"這個短語描述回收如何被組織。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"good enough to resell","meaning":"好得足以再出售","examples":[{"en":"Some footwear is not good enough to resell.","zh":"有些鞋類狀況不夠好，不能再出售。"},{"en":"Good enough to resell means in suitable condition to be sold again to another person.","zh":"good enough to resell 指狀況適合再次賣給另一個人。"},{"en":"A second-hand phone is good enough to resell if the screen and battery still work well.","zh":"如果二手手機螢幕和電池仍運作良好，就好得足以再出售。"},{"en":"If shoes are stained, broken, or missing one shoe, they may not be good enough to resell.","zh":"如果鞋有污漬、破損或缺少一隻，可能不夠好，不能再出售。"},{"en":"This phrase judges whether used items can enter the second-hand market.","zh":"這個短語判斷二手物品能否進入二手市場。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for one reason or another","meaning":"因為各種原因","examples":[{"en":"Some footwear is rejected for one reason or another.","zh":"有些鞋類因為各種原因被拒收。"},{"en":"For one reason or another means for various possible reasons that are not all stated.","zh":"for one reason or another 指因不同可能原因，而未逐一說明。"},{"en":"Students may miss club meetings for one reason or another, such as illness or homework.","zh":"學生可能因病或功課等各種原因錯過學會會議。"},{"en":"If items fail checks for one reason or another, workers must decide what to do next.","zh":"如果物品因各種原因未能通過檢查，工人必須決定下一步。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids listing every exact reason.","zh":"這個短語避免列出每一個確切原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get rejected","meaning":"被拒收","examples":[{"en":"Some footwear gets rejected during recycling.","zh":"有些鞋類在回收過程中被拒收。"},{"en":"To get rejected means to be refused or not accepted.","zh":"get rejected 指被拒絕或不被接受。"},{"en":"A job application may get rejected if it is incomplete.","zh":"如果求職申請不完整，可能被拒絕。"},{"en":"If shoes get rejected by a recycling centre, they may be sent to landfill.","zh":"如果鞋被回收中心拒收，它們可能被送往堆填區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being turned away after checking.","zh":"這個短語描述經檢查後被拒絕。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"find examples of","meaning":"找出……的例子","examples":[{"en":"The students want to find examples of footwear rejected for recycling.","zh":"學生想找出鞋類被拒收回收的例子。"},{"en":"To find examples of something means to look for specific cases that show it clearly.","zh":"find examples of something 指尋找能清楚展示某事的具體個案。"},{"en":"A student may find examples of persuasive language in a newspaper article.","zh":"學生可能在報章文章中找出說服性語言的例子。"},{"en":"If you find good examples, your presentation becomes easier to understand.","zh":"如果你找到好例子，匯報會更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collecting evidence or illustrations.","zh":"這個短語描述收集證據或例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be rejected for","meaning":"因……而被拒收","examples":[{"en":"Some footwear was rejected for recycling.","zh":"有些鞋類因回收而被拒收。"},{"en":"To be rejected for something means to be refused for a particular purpose or process.","zh":"be rejected for something 指因某一用途或流程而被拒絕接受。"},{"en":"A passport photo may be rejected for an application if the background is wrong.","zh":"如果背景不合規格，護照相可能在申請中被拒收。"},{"en":"If shoes are rejected for recycling, they cannot continue through that process.","zh":"如果鞋在回收方面被拒收，就不能繼續該流程。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose for which something is refused.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物是因甚麼用途而被拒絕。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"interview with","meaning":"與……的訪問","examples":[{"en":"The article includes an interview with the recycling manager.","zh":"文章包括一段與回收經理的訪問。"},{"en":"An interview with someone is a conversation in which that person answers questions.","zh":"interview with someone 指某人回答問題的一段訪談。"},{"en":"A school magazine may publish an interview with the principal.","zh":"學校雜誌可能刊登與校長的訪問。"},{"en":"If an article includes an interview with an expert, readers can get first-hand explanations.","zh":"如果文章包括與專家的訪問，讀者可以得到第一手解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who was questioned.","zh":"這個短語指出受訪者是誰。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"recycling manager","meaning":"回收經理","examples":[{"en":"The recycling manager explains why some shoes are rejected.","zh":"回收經理解釋為甚麼有些鞋被拒收。"},{"en":"A recycling manager is a person who organises or supervises recycling work.","zh":"recycling manager 指組織或監督回收工作的人。"},{"en":"A recycling manager may check sorting rules, staff training, and waste collection records.","zh":"回收經理可能檢查分類規則、員工培訓和廢物收集紀錄。"},{"en":"If a recycling manager gives clear instructions, fewer unsuitable items enter the system.","zh":"如果回收經理給出清楚指示，較少不合適物品會進入系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a job role in recycling operations.","zh":"這個短語描述回收營運中的職位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"here it is","meaning":"就在這裏","examples":[{"en":"Don finds the relevant part and says, “Here it is.”","zh":"Don 找到相關部分並說：「就在這裏。」"},{"en":"Here it is means I have found or am showing the thing we were looking for.","zh":"here it is 指我找到了或正在展示我們尋找的東西。"},{"en":"A student may say “Here it is” after finding a missing paragraph in the textbook.","zh":"學生在課本中找到缺失段落後，可能說「就在這裏」。"},{"en":"If someone says “Here it is,” the next step is usually to read or examine the item.","zh":"如果某人說 “Here it is”，下一步通常是閱讀或檢查該物。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when locating something.","zh":"這個短語用於找到某物時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"start with","meaning":"先由……開始","examples":[{"en":"Bella suggests starting with the ladies’ high-heeled shoes.","zh":"Bella 建議先由女裝高跟鞋開始。"},{"en":"To start with something means to begin by discussing or doing that thing first.","zh":"start with something 指首先討論或做某事。"},{"en":"In a presentation, students may start with a surprising fact to attract attention.","zh":"在匯報中，學生可能先由一個驚人事實開始，以吸引注意。"},{"en":"If a topic has many parts, starting with a simple example can help listeners follow.","zh":"如果題目有很多部分，先由簡單例子開始可以幫助聽眾跟上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first step in an order.","zh":"這個短語描述次序中的第一步。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ladies’ high-heeled shoes","meaning":"女裝高跟鞋","examples":[{"en":"The first example is a pair of ladies’ high-heeled shoes.","zh":"第一個例子是一雙女裝高跟鞋。"},{"en":"Ladies’ high-heeled shoes are women’s shoes with raised heels.","zh":"ladies’ high-heeled shoes 指有高鞋跟的女裝鞋。"},{"en":"Someone may wear ladies’ high-heeled shoes to a dinner, office, or formal event.","zh":"有人可能穿女裝高跟鞋出席晚宴、上班或正式活動。"},{"en":"If high-heeled shoes are badly stained, they may not be suitable for resale.","zh":"如果高跟鞋污漬嚴重，可能不適合再出售。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific type of women’s footwear.","zh":"這個短語指出一種特定女裝鞋類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the material was suede","meaning":"物料是麂皮","examples":[{"en":"The material of the high-heeled shoes was suede.","zh":"這雙高跟鞋的物料是麂皮。"},{"en":"The material was suede means the shoes were made from a soft leather with a slightly rough surface.","zh":"the material was suede 指鞋由一種表面略粗、柔軟的皮革製成。"},{"en":"A suede jacket feels soft but can be difficult to clean after rain.","zh":"麂皮外套觸感柔軟，但下雨後可能很難清潔。"},{"en":"If the material is suede, mud and water stains may be hard to remove.","zh":"如果物料是麂皮，泥漬和水漬可能很難去除。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what something is made from.","zh":"這個短語指出某物由甚麼材料製成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"suede","meaning":"麂皮","examples":[{"en":"The rejected high-heeled shoes were made of suede.","zh":"那雙被拒收的高跟鞋由麂皮製成。"},{"en":"Suede is a soft type of leather with a slightly fuzzy surface.","zh":"suede 指表面略帶絨毛感的柔軟皮革。"},{"en":"A suede bag may look elegant but needs careful protection from rain.","zh":"麂皮袋可能看起來優雅，但需要小心避免淋雨。"},{"en":"If suede becomes stained, cleaning it can be harder than cleaning smooth leather.","zh":"如果麂皮染污，清潔它可能比清潔光面皮革更困難。"},{"en":"This word names a delicate material often used in shoes and bags.","zh":"這個字指出一種常用於鞋和袋的精細材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"beige in colour","meaning":"米色","examples":[{"en":"The high-heeled shoes were beige in colour.","zh":"那雙高跟鞋是米色的。"},{"en":"Beige in colour means having a pale brown or cream-like colour.","zh":"beige in colour 指呈淺啡色或奶油色。"},{"en":"A beige school cardigan may match many different uniforms.","zh":"米色學校外套可以配搭很多不同校服。"},{"en":"If beige shoes are stained with mud, the marks can be very easy to see.","zh":"如果米色鞋沾上泥漬，污跡可能非常明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes colour in a formal way.","zh":"這個短語以較正式方式描述顏色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"look like","meaning":"看起來像","examples":[{"en":"The shoes looked like someone had only worn them once.","zh":"那雙鞋看起來像有人只穿過一次。"},{"en":"To look like something means to appear similar to it or give that impression.","zh":"look like something 指外觀看似某事物或給人某種印象。"},{"en":"The classroom looked like nobody had cleaned it for weeks.","zh":"課室看起來像幾星期沒有人打掃。"},{"en":"If shoes look like they were worn only once, people may expect them to be in good condition.","zh":"如果鞋看起來像只穿過一次，人們可能預期它們狀況良好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes appearance or impression.","zh":"這個短語描述外觀或印象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"only worn them once","meaning":"只穿過一次","examples":[{"en":"Someone had probably only worn the shoes once.","zh":"有人很可能只穿過那雙鞋一次。"},{"en":"Only worn them once means used the shoes just one time.","zh":"only worn them once 指只使用那雙鞋一次。"},{"en":"A child may outgrow party shoes after only wearing them once.","zh":"孩子可能只穿過派對鞋一次就長大不合穿。"},{"en":"If shoes have only been worn once, they may still look almost new.","zh":"如果鞋只穿過一次，它們可能仍看起來幾乎全新。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very limited use.","zh":"這個短語描述使用次數非常少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"wet field","meaning":"潮濕的田地","examples":[{"en":"The shoes had been worn in a very wet field.","zh":"那雙鞋曾在非常潮濕的田地中穿着。"},{"en":"A wet field is an open area of land covered with damp soil, mud, or grass.","zh":"wet field 指覆蓋濕泥、泥濘或濕草的戶外土地。"},{"en":"Football players may leave muddy marks after playing on a wet field.","zh":"足球員在潮濕球場上踢球後，可能留下泥印。"},{"en":"If delicate shoes are worn in a wet field, they can easily become stained or damaged.","zh":"如果精細鞋履在潮濕田地中穿着，就容易弄污或受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a muddy outdoor setting.","zh":"這個短語描述泥濘的戶外環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"stained with mud and grass","meaning":"沾滿泥土和草漬","examples":[{"en":"The heels were too stained with mud and grass to resell.","zh":"鞋跟沾滿泥土和草漬，污得無法再出售。"},{"en":"Stained with mud and grass means marked or dirtied by soil and green plant material.","zh":"stained with mud and grass 指被泥土和綠色植物痕跡弄污。"},{"en":"After sports day, students’ socks may be stained with mud and grass.","zh":"運動會後，學生襪子可能沾滿泥土和草漬。"},{"en":"If light-coloured shoes are stained with mud and grass, cleaning them may be difficult.","zh":"如果淺色鞋沾滿泥土和草漬，可能很難清潔。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible outdoor dirt marks.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的戶外污跡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"too stained to resell","meaning":"污漬太重，無法再出售","examples":[{"en":"The heels were too stained to resell.","zh":"鞋跟污漬太重，無法再出售。"},{"en":"Too stained to resell means too dirty or marked to be sold again.","zh":"too stained to resell 指太骯髒或污痕太多，不能再次出售。"},{"en":"A white shirt may be too stained to resell after ink spills on it.","zh":"白恤衫如果被墨水灑到，可能污漬太重，無法再出售。"},{"en":"If an item is too stained to resell, a charity shop may reject it.","zh":"如果物品污漬太重不能再出售，慈善商店可能會拒收。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a second-hand item cannot be sold.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何二手物品不能售賣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"leather ankle boots","meaning":"皮革短靴","examples":[{"en":"The students discuss a pair of leather ankle boots.","zh":"學生討論一雙皮革短靴。"},{"en":"Leather ankle boots are short boots made of leather that cover the foot and ankle.","zh":"leather ankle boots 指由皮革製成、覆蓋腳和腳踝的短靴。"},{"en":"Someone may wear leather ankle boots with jeans in cool weather.","zh":"天氣涼時，有人可能穿皮革短靴配牛仔褲。"},{"en":"If one boot fades badly, the pair may no longer look suitable for resale.","zh":"如果其中一隻靴嚴重褪色，整雙可能不再適合再出售。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific type of footwear.","zh":"這個短語指出一種特定鞋類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"what was wrong with","meaning":"……有甚麼問題","examples":[{"en":"Bella asks what was wrong with the leather ankle boots.","zh":"Bella 問那雙皮革短靴有甚麼問題。"},{"en":"What was wrong with something asks what problem or fault it had.","zh":"what was wrong with something 用來問某物有甚麼問題或缺陷。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask what was wrong with a printer when it stops working.","zh":"打印機停止運作時，老師可能問它有甚麼問題。"},{"en":"If you ask what was wrong with an item, you expect an explanation of its defect.","zh":"如果你問某物有甚麼問題，你期望得到其缺陷解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to identify a problem.","zh":"這個短語用於找出問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"apparently","meaning":"顯然；看來","examples":[{"en":"Apparently, the heels were worn, but that was not the main problem.","zh":"看來鞋跟磨損了，但那不是主要問題。"},{"en":"Apparently means according to what seems true or according to the information available.","zh":"apparently 指根據看起來真實的情況或現有資料。"},{"en":"Apparently, the bus is late because there was an accident on the road.","zh":"看來巴士遲到是因為路上發生了意外。"},{"en":"If someone says apparently, they may not have seen the fact directly.","zh":"如果某人說 apparently，他可能不是親眼看見該事實。"},{"en":"This word introduces information that appears to be true.","zh":"這個字引出看來真實的資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"heels were worn","meaning":"鞋跟磨損","examples":[{"en":"The heels were worn on the leather ankle boots.","zh":"那雙皮革短靴的鞋跟磨損了。"},{"en":"Heels were worn means the back bottom parts of the shoes were damaged or thinned by use.","zh":"heels were worn 指鞋後底部因使用而損壞或變薄。"},{"en":"The heels of school shoes may become worn after months of walking.","zh":"校鞋鞋跟在走路數月後可能磨損。"},{"en":"If heels are worn, a repair shop may be able to replace them.","zh":"如果鞋跟磨損，修鞋店可能可以更換。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage from repeated use.","zh":"這個短語描述因反覆使用造成的損耗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not the problem","meaning":"不是問題所在","examples":[{"en":"The worn heels were not the problem.","zh":"磨損的鞋跟不是問題所在。"},{"en":"Not the problem means something is not the real or main issue.","zh":"not the problem 指某事不是真正或主要問題。"},{"en":"The printer’s ink was low, but that was not the problem; the cable was unplugged.","zh":"打印機墨水少了，但那不是問題所在；電線才是沒插好。"},{"en":"If people focus on what is not the problem, they may miss the real cause.","zh":"如果人們專注於不是問題所在的地方，可能會錯過真正原因。"},{"en":"This phrase separates a minor issue from the main issue.","zh":"這個短語把次要問題與主要問題分開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a much lighter shade than","meaning":"顏色比……淺得多","examples":[{"en":"One shoe was a much lighter shade than the other.","zh":"其中一隻鞋的顏色比另一隻淺得多。"},{"en":"A much lighter shade than means much paler in colour than something else.","zh":"a much lighter shade than 指顏色比另一物淡很多。"},{"en":"One curtain looked a much lighter shade than the other after months in the sun.","zh":"幾個月日曬後，其中一幅窗簾顏色比另一幅淺得多。"},{"en":"If two shoes are different shades, they may look mismatched as a pair.","zh":"如果兩隻鞋顏色深淺不同，整雙鞋可能看起來不成對。"},{"en":"This phrase compares colour intensity.","zh":"這個短語比較顏色深淺。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be left in the sun","meaning":"被放在陽光下","examples":[{"en":"One of the shoes had been left in the sun.","zh":"其中一隻鞋曾被放在陽光下。"},{"en":"To be left in the sun means to remain under direct sunlight for some time.","zh":"be left in the sun 指在陽光直接照射下放置一段時間。"},{"en":"A plastic bottle may become hot if it is left in the sun all afternoon.","zh":"膠樽如果整個下午被放在陽光下，可能會變熱。"},{"en":"If leather is left in the sun too long, its colour may fade.","zh":"如果皮革被放在陽光下太久，顏色可能褪色。"},{"en":"This phrase explains exposure to sunlight.","zh":"這個短語解釋暴露於陽光下。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"second-hand shoes","meaning":"二手鞋","examples":[{"en":"Even second-hand shoes should look the same.","zh":"即使是二手鞋，也應看起來一樣。"},{"en":"Second-hand shoes are shoes that have been owned or worn by someone before.","zh":"second-hand shoes 指以前由別人擁有或穿過的鞋。"},{"en":"Some people buy second-hand shoes online because they are cheaper than new ones.","zh":"有些人會在網上買二手鞋，因為比新鞋便宜。"},{"en":"If second-hand shoes are clean and matching, buyers may still accept them.","zh":"如果二手鞋乾淨且左右相配，買家仍可能接受。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to used shoes being sold or donated again.","zh":"這個短語指再次出售或捐贈的舊鞋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"look the same","meaning":"看起來一樣","examples":[{"en":"Both shoes in a pair should look the same.","zh":"一雙鞋中的兩隻應該看起來一樣。"},{"en":"To look the same means to have the same appearance, colour, size, or style.","zh":"look the same 指外觀、顏色、大小或風格相同。"},{"en":"Two socks should look the same if they are sold as a pair.","zh":"如果兩隻襪作為一雙出售，它們應該看起來一樣。"},{"en":"If the two shoes do not look the same, buyers may think one is damaged.","zh":"如果兩隻鞋看起來不一樣，買家可能認為其中一隻受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual matching.","zh":"這個短語描述外觀相配。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"red baby shoes","meaning":"紅色嬰兒鞋","examples":[{"en":"The red baby shoes were rejected because one shoe was missing.","zh":"那雙紅色嬰兒鞋因缺少一隻鞋而被拒收。"},{"en":"Red baby shoes are small red shoes made for babies.","zh":"red baby shoes 指給嬰兒穿的小紅鞋。"},{"en":"Parents may keep red baby shoes as a memory after a child grows up.","zh":"孩子長大後，父母可能保留紅色嬰兒鞋作紀念。"},{"en":"If one red baby shoe is missing, the pair cannot be sold or used properly.","zh":"如果紅色嬰兒鞋缺少其中一隻，整雙就不能正常出售或使用。"},{"en":"This phrase names a small children’s footwear item.","zh":"這個短語指出一種小童鞋類物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be told to","meaning":"被告知要……","examples":[{"en":"People are told to tie shoes together before recycling them.","zh":"人們被告知回收鞋前要把兩隻鞋綁在一起。"},{"en":"To be told to do something means to be instructed or advised to do it.","zh":"be told to do something 指被指示或建議做某事。"},{"en":"Students are told to write their names on every answer sheet.","zh":"學生被告知要在每張答題紙上寫上姓名。"},{"en":"If people are told to follow a rule but ignore it, problems can happen later.","zh":"如果人們被告知要遵守規則卻忽視它，之後可能出現問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving instructions.","zh":"這個短語描述接收指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tie shoes together","meaning":"將兩隻鞋綁在一起","examples":[{"en":"People should tie shoes together before putting them in a recycling bin.","zh":"人們在把鞋放入回收箱前，應將兩隻鞋綁在一起。"},{"en":"To tie shoes together means to join the two shoes in a pair using their laces or a string.","zh":"tie shoes together 指用鞋帶或繩把一雙鞋中的兩隻連在一起。"},{"en":"A parent may tie children’s shoes together before donating them.","zh":"家長捐鞋前可能把孩子的兩隻鞋綁在一起。"},{"en":"If shoes are tied together, workers are less likely to lose one of them.","zh":"如果鞋被綁在一起，工人較不容易弄失其中一隻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical way to keep a pair complete.","zh":"這個短語描述保持一雙鞋完整的實用方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"people often do not bother","meaning":"人們常常懶得做","examples":[{"en":"People are told to tie shoes together, but they often do not bother.","zh":"人們被告知要把兩隻鞋綁在一起，但常常懶得做。"},{"en":"People often do not bother means they often do not make the effort to do something.","zh":"people often do not bother 指人們常不願花力氣去做某事。"},{"en":"Students know they should check spelling, but they often do not bother when they are tired.","zh":"學生知道應檢查拼字，但疲倦時常懶得做。"},{"en":"If people do not bother to follow simple recycling rules, usable items may be wasted.","zh":"如果人們懶得遵守簡單回收規則，可用物品可能被浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests laziness or lack of effort.","zh":"這個短語暗示懶惰或不願付出努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"you would think","meaning":"你會以為","examples":[{"en":"You would think it would be easy to find the other shoe.","zh":"你會以為找到另一隻鞋很容易。"},{"en":"You would think means it seems reasonable to expect something, but the reality may be different.","zh":"you would think 指某事看來合理地會如此，但現實可能不同。"},{"en":"You would think a school notice would be easy to understand, but this one is confusing.","zh":"你會以為學校通告很容易明白，但這份卻很混亂。"},{"en":"If someone says you would think, they often introduce a surprising contrast.","zh":"如果某人說 you would think，通常會引出令人意外的對比。"},{"en":"This phrase points out that common expectation may be wrong.","zh":"這個短語指出一般預期可能是錯的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"find the other","meaning":"找到另一隻","examples":[{"en":"It was not easy to find the other red baby shoe.","zh":"找到另一隻紅色嬰兒鞋並不容易。"},{"en":"To find the other means to locate the missing second item in a pair or group.","zh":"find the other 指找到一雙或一組中缺失的另一件物品。"},{"en":"A child may find one sock quickly but struggle to find the other.","zh":"孩子可能很快找到一隻襪子，但很難找到另一隻。"},{"en":"If workers cannot find the other shoe, the pair cannot be resold.","zh":"如果工人找不到另一隻鞋，整雙鞋就不能再出售。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when one item of a pair is missing.","zh":"這個短語常用於一對物品中缺少一件時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"that was a shame","meaning":"那很可惜","examples":[{"en":"It was a shame because the red baby shoes were obviously new.","zh":"那很可惜，因為那雙紅色嬰兒鞋明顯是新的。"},{"en":"That was a shame means that was unfortunate or disappointing.","zh":"that was a shame 指那是不幸或令人失望的事。"},{"en":"The picnic was cancelled because of rain, and that was a shame.","zh":"野餐因下雨取消，那很可惜。"},{"en":"If new shoes are wasted because one is missing, that is a shame.","zh":"如果新鞋因缺少一隻而被浪費，那很可惜。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses mild regret.","zh":"這個短語表達輕微遺憾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"obviously new","meaning":"明顯是新的","examples":[{"en":"The red baby shoes were obviously new.","zh":"那雙紅色嬰兒鞋明顯是新的。"},{"en":"Obviously new means clearly unused or almost unused.","zh":"obviously new 指明顯未使用或幾乎未使用。"},{"en":"The notebook was obviously new because none of the pages had been written on.","zh":"那本筆記簿明顯是新的，因為沒有任何頁面被寫過。"},{"en":"If shoes are obviously new, rejecting them feels especially wasteful.","zh":"如果鞋明顯是新的，拒收它們會顯得特別浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that clearly looks unused.","zh":"這個短語描述看起來明顯未用過的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"look like they had been worn by","meaning":"看起來像曾被……穿過","examples":[{"en":"The trainers looked like they had been worn by a marathon runner.","zh":"那雙運動鞋看起來像曾被馬拉松跑手穿過。"},{"en":"To look like they had been worn by someone means to appear as if that person used them heavily.","zh":"look like they had been worn by someone 指看起來好像曾被某人頻繁使用。"},{"en":"The muddy boots looked like they had been worn by a farmer all week.","zh":"那雙泥靴看起來像曾被農夫穿了一整星期。"},{"en":"If shoes look like they have been worn by a runner, they may be badly worn out.","zh":"如果鞋看起來像曾被跑手穿過，可能已嚴重磨損。"},{"en":"This phrase uses appearance to suggest previous use.","zh":"這個短語用外觀暗示過往使用情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"marathon runner","meaning":"馬拉松跑手","examples":[{"en":"The trainers looked like they had been worn by a marathon runner.","zh":"那雙運動鞋看起來像曾被馬拉松跑手穿過。"},{"en":"A marathon runner is someone who runs long-distance races of about 42 kilometres.","zh":"marathon runner 指參加約42公里長跑比賽的人。"},{"en":"A marathon runner needs strong, comfortable shoes for long training sessions.","zh":"馬拉松跑手需要堅固舒適的鞋來進行長時間訓練。"},{"en":"If trainers are worn by a marathon runner, the soles may become thin quickly.","zh":"如果運動鞋被馬拉松跑手穿過，鞋底可能很快變薄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a person who does very long-distance running.","zh":"這個短語描述長距離跑步的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be split","meaning":"裂開","examples":[{"en":"Bella asks whether the trainers were split.","zh":"Bella 問那雙運動鞋是否裂開。"},{"en":"To be split means to be torn or divided open along a line.","zh":"be split 指沿某條線撕裂或裂開。"},{"en":"A schoolbag may be split at the side if it carries too many books.","zh":"如果書包裝太多書，側面可能裂開。"},{"en":"If shoes are split, water can enter and they may be unsafe to wear.","zh":"如果鞋裂開，水可能滲入，而且可能不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical tearing or opening.","zh":"這個短語描述實體撕裂或打開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not exactly","meaning":"不完全是","examples":[{"en":"Don says the trainers were not exactly split.","zh":"Don 說那雙運動鞋不完全是裂開。"},{"en":"Not exactly means not completely or not in that precise way.","zh":"not exactly 指不完全如此，或不是準確地那樣。"},{"en":"The answer was not exactly wrong, but it needed more detail.","zh":"答案不完全錯，但需要更多細節。"},{"en":"If someone says not exactly, they may be correcting a small misunderstanding.","zh":"如果某人說 not exactly，他可能正在糾正小誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a careful or partial correction.","zh":"這個短語作出謹慎或部分更正。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one of the soles","meaning":"其中一隻鞋底","examples":[{"en":"One of the soles was badly worn.","zh":"其中一隻鞋底嚴重磨損。"},{"en":"One of the soles means the bottom part of one shoe in a pair.","zh":"one of the soles 指一雙鞋中其中一隻鞋的底部。"},{"en":"One of the soles of my school shoes became thin after months of walking uphill.","zh":"我其中一隻校鞋鞋底在走了幾個月斜路後變薄。"},{"en":"If one sole is badly worn, the pair may feel uneven and uncomfortable.","zh":"如果其中一隻鞋底嚴重磨損，整雙鞋可能感覺不平衡又不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a specific bottom part of one shoe.","zh":"這個短語指出其中一隻鞋的特定底部。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"so worn that","meaning":"磨損得……以致","examples":[{"en":"One of the soles was so worn that you could put your finger through it.","zh":"其中一隻鞋底磨損得可以把手指穿過去。"},{"en":"So worn that means damaged by use to such a degree that a result happens.","zh":"so worn that 指因使用而損耗到某程度，以致產生某結果。"},{"en":"The old chair was so worn that the fabric had holes in it.","zh":"那張舊椅磨損得布料上有洞。"},{"en":"If a shoe sole is so worn that it has a hole, it is no longer safe for daily walking.","zh":"如果鞋底磨損得出現洞口，就不再適合日常步行。"},{"en":"This phrase links extreme wear with its consequence.","zh":"這個短語把嚴重磨損與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"under the foot","meaning":"在腳掌底下的位置","examples":[{"en":"The sole was badly worn under the foot.","zh":"鞋底在腳掌底下的位置嚴重磨損。"},{"en":"Under the foot means on the part directly below where the foot presses down.","zh":"under the foot 指位於腳掌直接向下施壓的位置。"},{"en":"Insoles provide soft support under the foot when people walk.","zh":"鞋墊在人們走路時，在腳掌底下提供柔軟支撐。"},{"en":"If a shoe is worn under the foot, the wearer may feel the ground more sharply.","zh":"如果鞋在腳掌底下磨損，穿着者可能更明顯感到地面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the lower contact area of footwear.","zh":"這個短語描述鞋履下方的接觸位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"put your finger through","meaning":"把手指穿過去","examples":[{"en":"The sole was so worn that you could put your finger through it.","zh":"鞋底磨損得你可以把手指穿過去。"},{"en":"To put your finger through something means a hole is large enough for a finger to pass through.","zh":"put your finger through something 指洞口大到手指可以穿過。"},{"en":"The paper bag was so torn that I could put my finger through it.","zh":"紙袋破得我可以把手指穿過去。"},{"en":"If you can put your finger through a shoe sole, the shoe is badly damaged.","zh":"如果你能把手指穿過鞋底，鞋已嚴重損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the size or seriousness of a hole.","zh":"這個短語顯示洞口大小或損壞嚴重程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"certainly use","meaning":"絕對可以使用","examples":[{"en":"The students could certainly use some of the examples in their presentation.","zh":"學生絕對可以在匯報中使用其中一些例子。"},{"en":"Certainly use means definitely make use of something.","zh":"certainly use 指肯定使用某物。"},{"en":"A student could certainly use clear statistics in a debate speech.","zh":"學生絕對可以在辯論演講中使用清晰統計數字。"},{"en":"If examples explain a problem well, they can certainly be used in a presentation.","zh":"如果例子能很好解釋問題，它們絕對可以用於匯報。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong confidence that something is useful.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈相信某物有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"explain why","meaning":"解釋為甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The examples help explain why many shoes end up in landfill.","zh":"這些例子幫助解釋為甚麼許多鞋最終進入堆填區。"},{"en":"To explain why means to give the reason for something.","zh":"explain why 指給出某事的原因。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain why an answer is wrong instead of just marking it with a cross.","zh":"老師可能解釋為甚麼答案錯，而不是只打一個叉。"},{"en":"If examples explain why a problem happens, listeners understand it more clearly.","zh":"如果例子解釋為甚麼問題發生，聽眾會理解得更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces reasons.","zh":"這個短語引出原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take something to","meaning":"將某物送到……","examples":[{"en":"People take shoes to recycling centres or bins.","zh":"人們將鞋送到回收中心或回收箱。"},{"en":"To take something to a place means to bring it there.","zh":"take something to a place 指把某物帶到某地方。"},{"en":"A student may take a broken laptop to the repair shop after school.","zh":"學生可能放學後把壞手提電腦送到維修店。"},{"en":"If people take old shoes to recycling centres, workers can sort them properly.","zh":"如果人們把舊鞋送到回收中心，工人就能妥善分類。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving an item to a destination.","zh":"這個短語描述把物品移到目的地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"recycling centres","meaning":"回收中心","examples":[{"en":"Many shoes are taken to recycling centres.","zh":"許多鞋被送到回收中心。"},{"en":"Recycling centres are places where recyclable items are collected, sorted, and sometimes processed.","zh":"recycling centres 指收集、分類，有時也處理可回收物品的地方。"},{"en":"A community recycling centre may accept paper, glass bottles, clothing, and small appliances.","zh":"社區回收中心可能接受紙張、玻璃樽、衣物和小型電器。"},{"en":"If recycling centres are easy to reach, more people may recycle properly.","zh":"如果回收中心容易到達，更多人可能會妥善回收。"},{"en":"This phrase names organised places for recycling.","zh":"這個短語指出有組織的回收地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get thrown into landfill","meaning":"被丟進堆填區","examples":[{"en":"Most rejected shoes get thrown into landfill.","zh":"大多數被拒收的鞋會被丟進堆填區。"},{"en":"To get thrown into landfill means to be disposed of in a waste burial site.","zh":"get thrown into landfill 指被棄置到垃圾堆填場。"},{"en":"Broken furniture may get thrown into landfill if no one can repair or reuse it.","zh":"如果沒有人能修理或再用，破家具可能被丟進堆填區。"},{"en":"If shoes are rejected by recyclers, they may get thrown into landfill instead of being reused.","zh":"如果鞋被回收者拒收，它們可能被丟進堆填區，而不是被再用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the final disposal of waste.","zh":"這個短語描述廢物的最終棄置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"landfill","meaning":"堆填區","examples":[{"en":"Many rejected shoes end up in landfill.","zh":"許多被拒收的鞋最終進入堆填區。"},{"en":"Landfill is a place where waste is buried in the ground.","zh":"landfill 指把垃圾埋在地下的地方。"},{"en":"Old mattresses, broken toys, and unusable shoes may be sent to landfill.","zh":"舊床褥、破玩具和不能使用的鞋可能被送到堆填區。"},{"en":"If too much waste goes to landfill, land is used up and environmental pressure increases.","zh":"如果太多廢物進入堆填區，土地會被耗用，環境壓力也會增加。"},{"en":"This word describes both the place and the waste-disposal method.","zh":"這個字同時描述地點和廢物處理方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"what did you think about","meaning":"你覺得……怎樣","examples":[{"en":"Bella asks what Don thought about the recycling project.","zh":"Bella 問 Don 覺得那個回收計劃怎樣。"},{"en":"What did you think about asks for someone’s opinion after they have read, seen, or experienced something.","zh":"what did you think about 用來詢問某人在閱讀、觀看或經歷某事後的意見。"},{"en":"After the film, a friend may ask, “What did you think about the ending?”","zh":"看完電影後，朋友可能問：「你覺得結局怎樣？」"},{"en":"If someone asks what you thought about a project, they want your judgement, not just facts.","zh":"如果有人問你覺得某項目怎樣，他想知道你的判斷，而不只是事實。"},{"en":"This phrase invites personal response.","zh":"這個短語邀請個人回應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"set up a project","meaning":"設立一個計劃","examples":[{"en":"The recycling team set up a project to make new shoes from old shoes.","zh":"回收團隊設立一個計劃，用舊鞋製作新鞋。"},{"en":"To set up a project means to organise and start a planned piece of work.","zh":"set up a project 指組織並開始一項有計劃的工作。"},{"en":"A school may set up a project to collect unused books for younger students.","zh":"學校可能設立計劃，為低年級學生收集不用的書。"},{"en":"If a project is set up well, it has clear goals, roles, and steps.","zh":"如果計劃設立得好，它會有清晰目標、角色和步驟。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating an organised activity.","zh":"這個短語描述創立有組織的活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"avoid this by","meaning":"透過……避免這情況","examples":[{"en":"The team tried to avoid landfill by making new shoes from old shoes.","zh":"團隊嘗試透過用舊鞋製作新鞋來避免進入堆填區。"},{"en":"To avoid this by doing something means to prevent a problem through a particular action.","zh":"avoid this by doing something 指透過某行動防止某問題發生。"},{"en":"Students can avoid late homework by starting assignments earlier.","zh":"學生可以透過早點開始功課來避免遲交。"},{"en":"If old shoes become new products, companies can avoid waste by reusing materials.","zh":"如果舊鞋變成新產品，公司就可以透過再用材料避免浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase links a problem with a way to prevent it.","zh":"這個短語把問題與防止方法連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make new shoes out of","meaning":"用……製作新鞋","examples":[{"en":"The team made new shoes out of the good parts of old shoes.","zh":"團隊用舊鞋中狀況好的部分製作新鞋。"},{"en":"To make new shoes out of old parts means to create new footwear using reused materials.","zh":"make new shoes out of old parts 指使用再用材料製作新鞋。"},{"en":"Artists sometimes make bags out of old jeans to reduce waste.","zh":"藝術家有時用舊牛仔褲製作袋，以減少浪費。"},{"en":"If new shoes are made out of old shoes, fewer materials need to be thrown away.","zh":"如果新鞋由舊鞋製成，需要丟棄的材料就會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating something new from used materials.","zh":"這個短語描述用舊材料創造新物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"good parts of old shoes","meaning":"舊鞋中狀況好的部分","examples":[{"en":"The project used the good parts of old shoes.","zh":"該計劃使用舊鞋中狀況好的部分。"},{"en":"Good parts of old shoes are the pieces that are still clean, strong, or usable.","zh":"good parts of old shoes 指仍乾淨、堅固或可使用的部分。"},{"en":"A repair shop may use the good parts of old shoes to fix another pair.","zh":"修鞋店可能用舊鞋中狀況好的部分來修理另一雙鞋。"},{"en":"If only the soles are damaged, the leather upper may still be a good part.","zh":"如果只是鞋底損壞，皮革鞋面可能仍是狀況好的部分。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on reusing what is still valuable.","zh":"這個短語重點在再用仍有價值的部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sound like a good idea","meaning":"聽起來是個好主意","examples":[{"en":"The project sounded like a good idea.","zh":"這個計劃聽起來是個好主意。"},{"en":"To sound like a good idea means to seem sensible or useful when first described.","zh":"sound like a good idea 指某想法剛被描述時聽起來合理或有用。"},{"en":"Starting a study group sounds like a good idea before exams.","zh":"考試前成立溫習小組聽起來是個好主意。"},{"en":"If an idea sounds good, people may still need to test whether it works in practice.","zh":"如果想法聽起來好，人們仍需要測試它實際上是否可行。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an early positive impression.","zh":"這個短語表達初步正面印象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"match parts","meaning":"配對部件","examples":[{"en":"The team received many shoes, so they should have been able to match parts.","zh":"團隊收到很多鞋，所以應該能夠配對部件。"},{"en":"To match parts means to find pieces that fit or look right together.","zh":"match parts 指找出能配合或看起來相配的零件。"},{"en":"A mechanic must match parts correctly when repairing a bicycle.","zh":"機械工修理單車時，必須正確配對部件。"},{"en":"If shoe parts do not match in colour or size, the finished pair may look strange.","zh":"如果鞋的部件在顏色或大小上不配，完成的一雙鞋可能看起來奇怪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pairing compatible pieces.","zh":"這個短語描述把相容部件配在一起。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be surprised that","meaning":"對……感到驚訝","examples":[{"en":"Don was not surprised that the project failed.","zh":"Don 對計劃失敗並不感到驚訝。"},{"en":"To be surprised that something happens means to feel it is unexpected.","zh":"be surprised that something happens 指覺得某事發生出乎意料。"},{"en":"I was surprised that the bus arrived early during heavy rain.","zh":"大雨中巴士竟然提早到達，令我感到驚訝。"},{"en":"If someone is not surprised that a plan fails, they probably expected problems.","zh":"如果某人對計劃失敗不感驚訝，他大概早已預期會有問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaction to a result.","zh":"這個短語描述對結果的反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"who wants to","meaning":"誰會想……","examples":[{"en":"Don asks who wants to buy second-hand shoes.","zh":"Don 問誰會想買二手鞋。"},{"en":"Who wants to asks which person would be willing or interested in doing something.","zh":"who wants to 用來問哪個人願意或有興趣做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask, “Who wants to read the first paragraph aloud?”","zh":"老師可能問：「誰想朗讀第一段？」"},{"en":"If someone asks who wants to buy a product, they may doubt there is enough demand.","zh":"如果有人問誰會想買某產品，他可能懷疑需求是否足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase can be a real question or a rhetorical doubt.","zh":"這個短語可以是真問題，也可以是反問式懷疑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"buy second-hand shoes","meaning":"買二手鞋","examples":[{"en":"Don doubts that people want to buy second-hand shoes.","zh":"Don 懷疑人們想買二手鞋。"},{"en":"To buy second-hand shoes means to purchase shoes that someone else has owned or worn before.","zh":"buy second-hand shoes 指購買以前由別人擁有或穿過的鞋。"},{"en":"Some shoppers buy second-hand shoes online if the price is low and the condition is good.","zh":"如果價格低而狀況好，有些購物者會在網上買二手鞋。"},{"en":"If buyers worry about hygiene, they may avoid second-hand shoes.","zh":"如果買家擔心衞生，他們可能避免買二手鞋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes purchasing used footwear.","zh":"這個短語描述購買舊鞋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"germs","meaning":"細菌","examples":[{"en":"Don worries about the germs that second-hand shoes may carry.","zh":"Don 擔心二手鞋可能帶有細菌。"},{"en":"Germs are tiny living things that can cause illness or infection.","zh":"germs 指可能導致疾病或感染的微小生物。"},{"en":"Washing hands before lunch helps reduce germs.","zh":"午飯前洗手有助減少細菌。"},{"en":"If shoes are not cleaned properly, germs may remain inside them.","zh":"如果鞋沒有妥善清潔，細菌可能留在裡面。"},{"en":"This word is often used when talking about hygiene and health.","zh":"這個字常用於談論衞生和健康。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"catch germs","meaning":"沾上細菌","examples":[{"en":"Don thinks people could catch germs from second-hand shoes.","zh":"Don 認為人們可能從二手鞋沾上細菌。"},{"en":"To catch germs means to pick up germs that may make you ill.","zh":"catch germs 指接觸並沾上可能令人患病的細菌。"},{"en":"Children can catch germs when they share dirty cups or towels.","zh":"孩子共用骯髒杯子或毛巾時，可能沾上細菌。"},{"en":"If people believe they may catch germs from used shoes, they may refuse to buy them.","zh":"如果人們相信可能從舊鞋沾上細菌，他們可能拒絕購買。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming exposed to harmful microbes.","zh":"這個短語描述接觸有害微生物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"refuse something for that reason","meaning":"因那個原因拒絕某物","examples":[{"en":"People did not refuse the shoes for that reason.","zh":"人們並不是因那個原因拒絕那些鞋。"},{"en":"To refuse something for that reason means to reject it because of the reason just mentioned.","zh":"refuse something for that reason 指因剛才提到的原因而拒絕某物。"},{"en":"A teacher may refuse late homework for that reason if the rule was clearly explained.","zh":"如果規則已清楚說明，老師可能因那個原因拒收遲交功課。"},{"en":"If buyers refuse a product for that reason, sellers must understand what really worries them.","zh":"如果買家因那個原因拒絕產品，賣家必須明白他們真正擔心甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase links rejection with a specific cause.","zh":"這個短語把拒絕與具體原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"identical","meaning":"完全相同","examples":[{"en":"People refused the shoes because the pairs were not identical.","zh":"人們拒絕那些鞋，因為每雙鞋並非完全相同。"},{"en":"Identical means exactly the same in appearance, size, or details.","zh":"identical 指外觀、大小或細節完全一樣。"},{"en":"Twins may look almost identical, though their personalities can be different.","zh":"雙胞胎可能看起來幾乎完全相同，但性格可以不同。"},{"en":"If two shoes in a pair are not identical, customers may think they do not belong together.","zh":"如果一雙鞋中的兩隻並非完全相同，顧客可能認為它們不是一對。"},{"en":"This word describes complete sameness.","zh":"這個字描述完全一致。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"manage to","meaning":"設法做到","examples":[{"en":"The team still managed to ship the shoes overseas.","zh":"團隊仍然設法把鞋運到海外。"},{"en":"To manage to do something means to succeed in doing it, often despite difficulty.","zh":"manage to do something 指成功做到某事，常是在有困難之下。"},{"en":"A student managed to finish the project even though the computer crashed.","zh":"即使電腦壞了，學生仍設法完成專題。"},{"en":"If a team manages to solve a problem, effort and planning probably helped.","zh":"如果團隊設法解決問題，努力和規劃大概起了作用。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests successful effort.","zh":"這個短語暗示努力後成功。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ship something overseas","meaning":"將某物運到海外","examples":[{"en":"The team shipped the shoes overseas.","zh":"團隊把鞋運到海外。"},{"en":"To ship something overseas means to send goods to another country or region by transport.","zh":"ship something overseas 指透過運輸把貨物送到另一個國家或地區。"},{"en":"A company may ship books overseas to customers who order online.","zh":"公司可能把書運到海外，送給網上訂購的顧客。"},{"en":"If shoes are shipped overseas, the cost and environmental impact may increase.","zh":"如果鞋被運到海外，成本和環境影響可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes international delivery of goods.","zh":"這個短語描述貨物的國際運送。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"another area to discuss","meaning":"另一個需要討論的範疇","examples":[{"en":"Shipping recycled shoes overseas is another area the students need to discuss.","zh":"把回收鞋運到海外是學生另一個需要討論的範疇。"},{"en":"Another area to discuss means another topic or part that should be talked about.","zh":"another area to discuss 指另一個應該談及的主題或部分。"},{"en":"After discussing school lunches, food waste is another area to discuss.","zh":"討論學校午餐後，食物浪費是另一個需要討論的範疇。"},{"en":"If a presentation has many areas to discuss, students should organise them clearly.","zh":"如果匯報有很多範疇要討論，學生應清楚組織它們。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an additional discussion point.","zh":"這個短語引入額外討論點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"used to consider","meaning":"過去常常從……角度看","examples":[{"en":"Don used to consider recycling only from his own perspective.","zh":"Don 過去常常只從自己的角度看回收。"},{"en":"Used to consider means thought about something in a certain way in the past.","zh":"used to consider 指過去以某種方式思考某事。"},{"en":"I used to consider homework a waste of time, but now I see how practice helps.","zh":"我過去常常覺得功課浪費時間，但現在明白練習有幫助。"},{"en":"If someone used to consider a problem narrowly, new information may broaden their view.","zh":"如果某人過去從狹窄角度看問題，新資料可能擴闊他的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a past way of thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述過去的思考方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"from my own perspective","meaning":"從我自己的角度","examples":[{"en":"Don used to consider recycling from his own perspective.","zh":"Don 過去常常從自己的角度看回收。"},{"en":"From my own perspective means from my personal point of view or experience.","zh":"from my own perspective 指從我個人的觀點或經驗出發。"},{"en":"From my own perspective, online lessons are useful when recordings are provided.","zh":"從我自己的角度看，如果有錄影，網課是有用的。"},{"en":"If people look only from their own perspective, they may miss other people’s needs.","zh":"如果人們只從自己的角度看，可能會忽略其他人的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a personal viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語引入個人觀點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"recycling behaviour","meaning":"回收行為","examples":[{"en":"Don used to think only about his own recycling behaviour.","zh":"Don 過去只思考自己的回收行為。"},{"en":"Recycling behaviour means the habits and actions people have when they recycle.","zh":"recycling behaviour 指人們回收時的習慣和行動。"},{"en":"Putting bottles into the correct bin is one kind of recycling behaviour.","zh":"把膠樽放入正確回收箱是一種回收行為。"},{"en":"If recycling behaviour is careless, good materials may become contaminated.","zh":"如果回收行為粗心，良好材料可能被污染。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what people actually do when recycling.","zh":"這個短語描述人們回收時實際做甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"without looking at","meaning":"沒有看……","examples":[{"en":"Don thought about his own behaviour without looking at the bigger picture.","zh":"Don 思考自己的行為時，沒有看更大的全局。"},{"en":"Without looking at something means not considering or examining it.","zh":"without looking at something 指沒有考慮或檢視某事。"},{"en":"A student may choose a subject without looking at the course requirements.","zh":"學生可能沒有看課程要求就選科。"},{"en":"If people make decisions without looking at all the facts, they may choose badly.","zh":"如果人們沒有看所有事實就作決定，可能會選錯。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an important view is missing.","zh":"這個短語顯示缺少重要視角。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the bigger picture","meaning":"更大的全局","examples":[{"en":"Don now wants to look at the bigger picture of footwear recycling.","zh":"Don 現在想看鞋類回收的更大全局。"},{"en":"The bigger picture means the wider situation, including causes, effects, and connections.","zh":"the bigger picture 指更廣泛的情況，包括原因、結果和關聯。"},{"en":"A student should look at the bigger picture before blaming one classmate for a group problem.","zh":"學生在責怪某個同學造成小組問題前，應先看更大的全局。"},{"en":"If people see the bigger picture, they understand how small actions affect a whole system.","zh":"如果人們看見更大的全局，就能理解小行動如何影響整個系統。"},{"en":"This phrase moves thinking beyond one narrow detail.","zh":"這個短語把思考帶離單一狹窄細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"so much happens once","meaning":"一旦……就會發生很多事","examples":[{"en":"So much happens once shoes leave the recycling area.","zh":"鞋一旦離開回收區，就會發生很多事。"},{"en":"So much happens once something occurs means many things begin after that point.","zh":"so much happens once something occurs 指某事一發生後，就開始有許多事情。"},{"en":"So much happens once students submit applications: interviews, checks, and waiting all follow.","zh":"學生一旦提交申請，就會發生很多事：面試、審核和等待都接着出現。"},{"en":"If many stages happen after collection, recycling is more complex than it seems.","zh":"如果收集後有很多階段，回收就比看起來更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a chain of later events.","zh":"這個短語引出後續一連串事件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"recycling area","meaning":"回收區","examples":[{"en":"Shoes go through many stages after leaving the recycling area.","zh":"鞋離開回收區後會經過很多階段。"},{"en":"A recycling area is a place where recyclable items are placed, collected, or sorted.","zh":"recycling area 指放置、收集或分類可回收物品的地方。"},{"en":"A school may set up a recycling area near the entrance for paper and bottles.","zh":"學校可能在入口附近設立回收區，收集紙張和膠樽。"},{"en":"If a recycling area is messy, useful items may be mixed with rubbish.","zh":"如果回收區混亂，可用物品可能與垃圾混在一起。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the starting place for recycling collection.","zh":"這個短語描述回收收集的起點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not as simple as","meaning":"不像……那麼簡單","examples":[{"en":"Footwear recycling is not as simple as Don first thought.","zh":"鞋類回收不像 Don 最初以為那麼簡單。"},{"en":"Not as simple as means more complicated than someone expected.","zh":"not as simple as 指比某人預期更複雜。"},{"en":"Planning a school trip is not as simple as booking a bus.","zh":"籌辦學校旅行不像預訂巴士那麼簡單。"},{"en":"If many rules, costs, and people are involved, a task is not as simple as it looks.","zh":"如果涉及許多規則、成本和人手，任務就不像看起來那麼簡單。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects an overly easy impression.","zh":"這個短語糾正過於簡單的印象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"first think","meaning":"最初以為","examples":[{"en":"The topic is not as simple as students may first think.","zh":"這個題目不像學生最初以為那麼簡單。"},{"en":"First think means initially believe before learning more.","zh":"first think 指在了解更多之前最初相信某事。"},{"en":"Students may first think a poem is only about love, but later notice political ideas.","zh":"學生可能最初以為一首詩只關於愛情，但後來注意到政治想法。"},{"en":"If people first think a problem is easy, research may reveal hidden complications.","zh":"如果人們最初以為問題容易，研究可能揭示隱藏複雜性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an early impression.","zh":"這個短語描述早期印象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"show that by","meaning":"透過……展示","examples":[{"en":"The students can show the complexity by taking a different approach.","zh":"學生可以透過採取不同方法展示其複雜性。"},{"en":"To show that by doing something means to prove or demonstrate a point through an action or method.","zh":"show that by doing something 指透過某行動或方法證明或展示某觀點。"},{"en":"A student can show confidence by speaking clearly and looking at the audience.","zh":"學生可以透過清楚說話和望向觀眾來展示信心。"},{"en":"If presenters show complexity by using real examples, listeners understand the issue better.","zh":"如果匯報者透過真實例子展示複雜性，聽眾會更理解議題。"},{"en":"This phrase links method with message.","zh":"這個短語把方法與訊息連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"take a different approach to","meaning":"對……採取不同方法","examples":[{"en":"The students can take a very different approach to the topic.","zh":"學生可以對這個題目採取非常不同的方法。"},{"en":"To take a different approach to something means to handle or think about it in another way.","zh":"take a different approach to something 指以另一種方式處理或思考某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may take a different approach to grammar by using games instead of worksheets.","zh":"老師可能透過遊戲而不是工作紙，對文法採取不同教法。"},{"en":"If one method is too narrow, taking a different approach can reveal new ideas.","zh":"如果一種方法太狹窄，採取不同方法可以揭示新想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing method or perspective.","zh":"這個短語描述改變方法或角度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"absolutely","meaning":"完全同意","examples":[{"en":"Don agrees completely and says, “Absolutely.”","zh":"Don 完全同意並說：「Absolutely。」"},{"en":"Absolutely means completely, definitely, or with full agreement.","zh":"absolutely 指完全、肯定，或表示完全同意。"},{"en":"If a friend asks whether clean water is important, you might answer, “Absolutely.”","zh":"如果朋友問清潔食水是否重要，你可能回答：「絕對重要。」"},{"en":"In conversation, absolutely can show strong support for another person’s idea.","zh":"在對話中，absolutely 可以表示強烈支持對方想法。"},{"en":"This word is more emphatic than simply saying yes.","zh":"這個字比單純說 yes 更有強調意味。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/listening/Practice 6/task-4":[{"front":"project on","meaning":"關於……的專題","examples":[{"en":"For my project on invertebrates, I chose to study tardigrades.","zh":"在我關於無脊椎動物的專題中，我選擇研究緩步動物。"},{"en":"A project on something is a piece of school or research work about that topic.","zh":"關於某事的專題是有關該主題的學校或研究作品。"},{"en":"A student may prepare a project on recycling by interviewing classmates about waste.","zh":"學生可以透過訪問同學對廢物的看法，準備關於回收的專題。"},{"en":"A good project on a science topic usually includes facts, examples and clear explanations.","zh":"一個好的科學專題通常包括事實、例子和清楚解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when naming the subject of a report or presentation.","zh":"這個短語適合用來說明報告或匯報的主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"invertebrates","meaning":"無脊椎動物","examples":[{"en":"For my project on invertebrates, I chose to study tardigrades.","zh":"在我關於無脊椎動物的專題中，我選擇研究緩步動物。"},{"en":"Invertebrates are animals that do not have a backbone.","zh":"無脊椎動物是沒有脊骨的動物。"},{"en":"Insects, worms and jellyfish are examples of invertebrates.","zh":"昆蟲、蠕蟲和水母都是無脊椎動物的例子。"},{"en":"Studying invertebrates helps students see how many animals do not look like mammals or birds.","zh":"研究無脊椎動物幫助學生明白許多動物並不像哺乳類或鳥類。"},{"en":"This word is often used in biology when classifying animals.","zh":"這個詞常用於生物學中的動物分類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"choose to study","meaning":"選擇研究","examples":[{"en":"I chose to study tardigrades for my project.","zh":"我選擇研究緩步動物作為我的專題。"},{"en":"To choose to study something means to decide to learn about or research that topic.","zh":"選擇研究某事意思是決定學習或研究該主題。"},{"en":"A student may choose to study whales after watching a documentary about the ocean.","zh":"學生看完關於海洋的紀錄片後，可能選擇研究鯨魚。"},{"en":"Choosing a topic carefully can make a project more interesting and easier to organise.","zh":"謹慎選擇主題可以令專題更有趣，也更容易組織。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a personal decision about learning.","zh":"這個短語重點是關於學習的個人決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tardigrades","meaning":"緩步動物","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades are tiny animals that belong to the phylum Tardigrada.","zh":"緩步動物是屬於緩步動物門的微小動物。"},{"en":"Tardigrades are very small animals known for surviving difficult conditions.","zh":"緩步動物是非常細小的動物，以能在艱難環境中存活而聞名。"},{"en":"A biology teacher may show students pictures of tardigrades under a microscope.","zh":"生物老師可能向學生展示顯微鏡下的緩步動物圖片。"},{"en":"Tardigrades interest scientists because they can survive in places where many animals cannot.","zh":"緩步動物令科學家感興趣，因為牠們能在許多動物不能生存的地方存活。"},{"en":"This word names a real group of tiny animals, not a fictional creature.","zh":"這個詞命名一個真實的微小動物群，而不是虛構生物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"microscopic","meaning":"微小至需用顯微鏡觀察的","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades are microscopic animals.","zh":"緩步動物是微小至需用顯微鏡觀察的動物。"},{"en":"Microscopic means so small that it is difficult or impossible to see clearly without a microscope.","zh":"微小至需用顯微鏡觀察的意思是太小，沒有顯微鏡便難以或無法清楚看見。"},{"en":"Bacteria are microscopic, so students usually need laboratory equipment to observe them.","zh":"細菌微小至需用顯微鏡觀察，所以學生通常需要實驗室設備才能觀察。"},{"en":"Microscopic organisms may be invisible to our eyes but still play important roles in nature.","zh":"微小生物可能肉眼看不見，但仍在自然界中發揮重要作用。"},{"en":"This word describes size, not importance.","zh":"這個詞描述大小，而不是重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"to be more precise","meaning":"更準確地說","examples":[{"en":"These are microscopic, or to be more precise, near-microscopic animals.","zh":"這些是微小至需用顯微鏡觀察的動物，或者更準確地說，是接近微觀大小的動物。"},{"en":"To be more precise is used when you want to correct or make a description more exact.","zh":"更準確地說用於想修正或令描述更精確時。"},{"en":"The meeting starts in the morning, or to be more precise, at 9:15 a.m.","zh":"會議在早上開始，或者更準確地說，是上午 9 時 15 分開始。"},{"en":"This phrase helps speakers avoid vague or slightly inaccurate statements.","zh":"這個短語幫助說話者避免含糊或略不準確的說法。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving measurements, definitions or careful explanations.","zh":"當提供量度、定義或仔細解釋時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"near-microscopic animals","meaning":"接近微觀大小的動物","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades are near-microscopic animals.","zh":"緩步動物是接近微觀大小的動物。"},{"en":"Near-microscopic animals are animals that are extremely small, almost requiring a microscope to see clearly.","zh":"接近微觀大小的動物是極其細小、幾乎需要顯微鏡才看得清楚的動物。"},{"en":"Some pond animals are near-microscopic and look like tiny dots in water.","zh":"有些池塘動物接近微觀大小，在水中看起來像小點。"},{"en":"Because near-microscopic animals are so small, they are easy to miss without careful observation.","zh":"因為接近微觀大小的動物十分細小，沒有仔細觀察很容易錯過。"},{"en":"This phrase describes animals close to microscopic size.","zh":"這個短語描述接近微觀尺寸的動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"well over","meaning":"遠超過","examples":[{"en":"There are well over a thousand known species of tardigrades.","zh":"緩步動物的已知物種遠超過一千種。"},{"en":"Well over means much more than a stated number or amount.","zh":"遠超過意思是比某個數字或數量多很多。"},{"en":"The school library has well over 10,000 books for students to borrow.","zh":"學校圖書館有遠超過一萬本書可供學生借閱。"},{"en":"If a charity receives well over its target amount, it can support more people.","zh":"如果慈善機構收到遠超過目標的款項，就可以支援更多人。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the number is clearly higher than expected.","zh":"這個短語強調數字明顯高於預期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"known species","meaning":"已知物種","examples":[{"en":"There are well over a thousand known species of these tiny animals.","zh":"這些微小動物的已知物種遠超過一千種。"},{"en":"Known species are species that scientists have identified and described.","zh":"已知物種是科學家已識別和描述的物種。"},{"en":"A museum display may show the number of known species of butterflies in a country.","zh":"博物館展覽可能展示某國蝴蝶的已知物種數量。"},{"en":"The number of known species can increase when scientists discover and classify new organisms.","zh":"當科學家發現並分類新生物，已知物種的數目可以增加。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to species already recorded by science.","zh":"這個短語指科學上已記錄的物種。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"belong to","meaning":"屬於……","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades belong to the phylum Tardigrada.","zh":"緩步動物屬於緩步動物門。"},{"en":"To belong to a group means to be a member or part of that group.","zh":"屬於某群體意思是成為該群體的成員或一部分。"},{"en":"A dolphin belongs to the group of mammals, even though it lives in water.","zh":"海豚屬於哺乳類，即使牠生活在水中。"},{"en":"Classification helps scientists explain which organisms belong to the same wider group.","zh":"分類幫助科學家解釋哪些生物屬於同一較大群體。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing membership or biological classification.","zh":"這個短語適合描述成員身份或生物分類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"phylum Tardigrada","meaning":"緩步動物門","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades belong to the phylum Tardigrada.","zh":"緩步動物屬於緩步動物門。"},{"en":"The phylum Tardigrada is the biological group that includes tardigrades.","zh":"緩步動物門是包括緩步動物在內的生物分類群。"},{"en":"In biology, a phylum is a major category used to classify living things.","zh":"在生物學中，「門」是用來分類生物的主要類別。"},{"en":"Knowing the phylum helps students understand where an organism fits in scientific classification.","zh":"知道所屬門類有助學生理解一種生物在科學分類中的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal scientific name.","zh":"這個短語是正式科學名稱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"range in length from...to","meaning":"長度介乎……至……","examples":[{"en":"Most tardigrades range in length from 0.05 to 1 millimetre.","zh":"大多數緩步動物長度介乎 0.05 至 1 毫米。"},{"en":"To range in length from one size to another means to vary between those two measurements.","zh":"長度介乎某尺寸至另一尺寸，意思是在兩個量度之間變化。"},{"en":"The pencils in the box range in length from five to fifteen centimetres.","zh":"盒中的鉛筆長度介乎五至十五厘米。"},{"en":"Giving a size range helps readers understand both the smallest and largest examples.","zh":"提供尺寸範圍有助讀者理解最小和最大的例子。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing measurements that are not all the same.","zh":"當描述不完全相同的量度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"millimetre","meaning":"毫米","examples":[{"en":"Most tardigrades are less than 1 millimetre long.","zh":"大多數緩步動物少於 1 毫米長。"},{"en":"A millimetre is a very small unit of length equal to one thousandth of a metre.","zh":"毫米是很小的長度單位，等於一米的一千分之一。"},{"en":"The thickness of a plastic card may be measured in millimetres.","zh":"膠卡的厚度可能以毫米量度。"},{"en":"Scientists use millimetres when measuring very small animals or objects.","zh":"科學家量度非常細小的動物或物件時會使用毫米。"},{"en":"This word is useful for precise small measurements.","zh":"這個詞適合用於精確的小尺寸量度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the largest species","meaning":"最大的物種","examples":[{"en":"The largest species can grow to be 1.2 millimetres in length.","zh":"最大的物種可以長到 1.2 毫米。"},{"en":"The largest species means the biggest type within a group of organisms.","zh":"最大的物種意思是某生物群中體型最大的種類。"},{"en":"The largest species of bird in a park may need more space than smaller birds.","zh":"公園中最大的鳥類物種可能比細小鳥類需要更多空間。"},{"en":"Identifying the largest species helps readers understand the upper limit of size in a group.","zh":"指出最大的物種有助讀者理解一個群體尺寸的上限。"},{"en":"This phrase compares different species within the same category.","zh":"這個短語比較同一類別中的不同物種。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"grow to be","meaning":"長到……","examples":[{"en":"The largest tardigrades can grow to be 1.2 millimetres in length.","zh":"最大的緩步動物可以長到 1.2 毫米。"},{"en":"To grow to be a certain size means to reach that size as it develops.","zh":"長到某尺寸意思是在發育過程中達到該大小。"},{"en":"A puppy may grow to be much larger than its owner expected.","zh":"小狗可能長到比主人預期大得多。"},{"en":"Plants grow to be taller when they receive enough sunlight, water and space.","zh":"植物獲得足夠陽光、水分和空間時，會長得更高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes final or possible size after growth.","zh":"這個短語描述成長後的最終或可能大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in length","meaning":"長度上","examples":[{"en":"The largest species can grow to be 1.2 millimetres in length.","zh":"最大的物種長度上可以長到 1.2 毫米。"},{"en":"In length means measured from one end to the other.","zh":"長度上意思是由一端到另一端量度。"},{"en":"The classroom table is two metres in length.","zh":"課室桌子長度上有兩米。"},{"en":"Saying “in length” makes clear that the measurement is about how long something is.","zh":"說 “in length” 可清楚表明該量度是關於某物有多長。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used with exact measurements.","zh":"這個短語常與精確量度一起使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be sometimes called","meaning":"有時被稱為","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades are also sometimes called water bears.","zh":"緩步動物有時也被稱為水熊。"},{"en":"To be sometimes called something means to have another name used by some people or in some situations.","zh":"有時被稱為某名意思是在某些人或情況中有另一個名稱。"},{"en":"Hong Kong is sometimes called a city of contrasts because old and new areas sit side by side.","zh":"香港有時被稱為對比之城，因為新舊地區並存。"},{"en":"Alternative names often describe how something looks, moves or behaves.","zh":"別名常描述某物的外貌、移動方式或行為。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a name that is not the only official name.","zh":"這個短語引入一個並非唯一正式名稱的名稱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"water bears","meaning":"水熊","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades are sometimes called water bears.","zh":"緩步動物有時被稱為水熊。"},{"en":"Water bears is an informal name for tardigrades, partly because of their shape and movement.","zh":"水熊是緩步動物的非正式名稱，部分原因是牠們的形狀和移動方式。"},{"en":"A science teacher may use the name water bears to help younger students remember tardigrades.","zh":"科學老師可能使用水熊這個名稱，幫助年幼學生記住緩步動物。"},{"en":"Informal names can make strange scientific animals feel easier to understand.","zh":"非正式名稱可以令陌生科學動物感覺較容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is a nickname, not a separate animal group.","zh":"這個短語是別名，而不是另一個動物群。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"thrive best","meaning":"生長得最好","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades thrive best in water.","zh":"緩步動物在水中生長得最好。"},{"en":"To thrive best means to grow, live or succeed most successfully in a particular condition.","zh":"生長得最好意思是在某種條件下最能成長、生活或成功。"},{"en":"Some classroom plants thrive best near a window with regular watering.","zh":"有些課室植物放在窗邊並定期澆水時生長得最好。"},{"en":"Animals thrive best when their environment provides food, shelter and suitable temperature.","zh":"當環境提供食物、庇護和合適溫度時，動物生長得最好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the conditions where something does especially well.","zh":"這個短語描述某物表現特別好的條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"because of the way","meaning":"因為……的方式","examples":[{"en":"They are called water bears because of the way they move.","zh":"牠們被稱為水熊，是因為牠們移動的方式。"},{"en":"Because of the way means due to the manner or method in which something happens.","zh":"因為某事的方式意思是由於某事發生的方法或樣子。"},{"en":"The road is dangerous because of the way cars turn the corner too quickly.","zh":"這條路很危險，因為車輛轉彎的方式太快。"},{"en":"People may remember a teacher because of the way she explains difficult ideas clearly.","zh":"人們可能記住一位老師，因為她清楚解釋困難概念的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase links a result with how something is done.","zh":"這個短語把結果與某事如何發生連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the way they move","meaning":"牠們移動的方式","examples":[{"en":"They are called bears because of the way they move.","zh":"牠們被稱為熊，是因為牠們移動的方式。"},{"en":"The way they move means the manner in which an animal or person travels or changes position.","zh":"牠們移動的方式意思是動物或人行進或改變位置的方式。"},{"en":"Penguins are easy to recognise because of the way they move on land.","zh":"企鵝在陸地上的移動方式令牠們容易被認出。"},{"en":"Movement can help scientists identify animals even when they are small or hard to see.","zh":"即使動物很小或難以看見，移動方式也能幫助科學家辨認牠們。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on motion and behaviour.","zh":"這個短語重點是動作和行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"moss piglet","meaning":"苔蘚小豬","examples":[{"en":"Moss piglet is another name for tardigrades.","zh":"苔蘚小豬是緩步動物的另一個名稱。"},{"en":"Moss piglet is an informal nickname for tardigrades, linked to their small shape and habitat.","zh":"苔蘚小豬是緩步動物的非正式別名，與牠們的小形狀和棲息地有關。"},{"en":"Children may remember the term moss piglet more easily than the scientific name.","zh":"孩子可能比起科學名稱更容易記住苔蘚小豬這個詞。"},{"en":"Nicknames like moss piglet make tiny organisms sound more familiar and memorable.","zh":"像苔蘚小豬這樣的別名，令微小生物聽起來更熟悉、更易記。"},{"en":"This phrase is playful rather than formal scientific language.","zh":"這個短語較有趣，不是正式科學語言。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"another name for","meaning":"……的另一個名稱","examples":[{"en":"Moss piglet is another name for tardigrades.","zh":"苔蘚小豬是緩步動物的另一個名稱。"},{"en":"Another name for something is a different word or phrase used to refer to the same thing.","zh":"某物的另一個名稱是用來指同一事物的不同詞語或短語。"},{"en":"“Bike” is another name for a bicycle in everyday speech.","zh":"在日常說話中，“bike” 是 bicycle 的另一個名稱。"},{"en":"Learning another name for a term can help students understand articles and videos more easily.","zh":"學習一個術語的另一個名稱，可以幫助學生更容易理解文章和影片。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an alternative name.","zh":"這個短語引入替代名稱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"viewed from the front","meaning":"從正面觀看時","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades look like tiny piglets when viewed from the front.","zh":"從正面觀看時，緩步動物看起來像細小豬仔。"},{"en":"Viewed from the front means seen from the side where the face or front part is visible.","zh":"從正面觀看時意思是從能看見面部或前方部分的一側觀察。"},{"en":"A building may look narrow when viewed from the front but much larger from the side.","zh":"建築物從正面觀看時可能看起來很窄，但從側面看大得多。"},{"en":"The appearance of an object can change depending on the angle from which it is viewed.","zh":"物件外貌會因觀看角度不同而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing appearance from a specific direction.","zh":"當從特定方向描述外貌時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"first discovered","meaning":"最早被發現","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades were first discovered in Germany in 1773.","zh":"緩步動物最早於 1773 年在德國被發現。"},{"en":"First discovered means found and recorded for the first time.","zh":"最早被發現意思是第一次被找到並記錄。"},{"en":"A new species may be first discovered in a forest during a scientific survey.","zh":"一個新物種可能在科學調查期間於森林中最早被發現。"},{"en":"When something is first discovered, scientists often study it again to understand it better.","zh":"當某物最早被發現後，科學家常會再次研究它以更好理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in science and history.","zh":"這個短語常用於科學和歷史。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"coin the name","meaning":"創造名稱","examples":[{"en":"Johann Goeze coined the name Tardigrada.","zh":"Johann Goeze 創造了 Tardigrada 這個名稱。"},{"en":"To coin the name means to invent or introduce a new name for something.","zh":"創造名稱意思是為某物發明或提出一個新名稱。"},{"en":"A scientist may coin the name of a new species after discovering it.","zh":"科學家發現新物種後，可能為它創造名稱。"},{"en":"A clear name helps people discuss a new discovery more easily.","zh":"清楚的名稱幫助人們更容易討論新發現。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when a term is created for the first time.","zh":"當一個術語首次被創造時，常會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as I say","meaning":"正如我所說","examples":[{"en":"As I say, there are many different species of tardigrade.","zh":"正如我所說，緩步動物有許多不同物種。"},{"en":"As I say means as I have already mentioned or explained.","zh":"正如我所說意思是正如我之前已提及或解釋。"},{"en":"As I say, this homework is difficult, so you should start early.","zh":"正如我所說，這份功課很難，所以你應早點開始。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase to remind listeners of an earlier point.","zh":"說話者使用這個短語提醒聽眾較早的重點。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in spoken explanations and presentations.","zh":"這個短語常見於口頭解釋和匯報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"too many to describe here","meaning":"太多而無法在此描述","examples":[{"en":"There are too many species of tardigrade to describe here.","zh":"緩步動物的物種太多，無法在此描述。"},{"en":"Too many to describe here means the number is so large that there is not enough time or space to explain all of them.","zh":"太多而無法在此描述，意思是數量太大，沒有足夠時間或篇幅全部解釋。"},{"en":"There are too many school clubs to describe here, so the website lists them separately.","zh":"學校學會太多而無法在此逐一描述，所以網站另行列出。"},{"en":"This phrase helps a speaker move on without giving every detail.","zh":"這個短語幫助說話者不用交代每個細節也能繼續說下去。"},{"en":"It is useful when a topic is broad but the explanation must stay short.","zh":"當主題很廣但解釋必須簡短時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"generally speaking","meaning":"一般來說","examples":[{"en":"Generally speaking, the different species share similar physical traits.","zh":"一般來說，不同物種具有相似的身體特徵。"},{"en":"Generally speaking means in most cases or as a broad statement.","zh":"一般來說意思是在大多數情況下，或作為廣泛說法。"},{"en":"Generally speaking, students learn better when examples are clear and practical.","zh":"一般來說，當例子清楚而實用時，學生學得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase allows exceptions while still giving a useful overall idea.","zh":"這個短語容許例外，同時仍提供有用的整體概念。"},{"en":"It is often used before a general explanation.","zh":"它常用於一般解釋之前。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"share similar physical traits","meaning":"具有相似的身體特徵","examples":[{"en":"Different species of tardigrade share similar physical traits.","zh":"不同緩步動物物種具有相似的身體特徵。"},{"en":"To share similar physical traits means to have body features that are alike.","zh":"具有相似的身體特徵意思是擁有相似的身體部位或外貌特點。"},{"en":"Many cats share similar physical traits, such as whiskers, claws and flexible bodies.","zh":"許多貓具有相似的身體特徵，例如鬍鬚、爪和柔軟身體。"},{"en":"Shared physical traits help scientists compare and group living things.","zh":"共同的身體特徵幫助科學家比較和歸類生物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing what different organisms have in common.","zh":"當描述不同生物有何共同點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"physical traits","meaning":"身體特徵","examples":[{"en":"The different species share similar physical traits.","zh":"不同物種具有相似的身體特徵。"},{"en":"Physical traits are visible body features such as shape, size, colour or body parts.","zh":"身體特徵是可見的身體特點，例如形狀、大小、顏色或身體部位。"},{"en":"Eye colour, height and hair texture are physical traits in humans.","zh":"眼睛顏色、身高和髮質都是人類的身體特徵。"},{"en":"Scientists study physical traits to identify species and understand how they live.","zh":"科學家研究身體特徵，以識別物種並了解牠們如何生活。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the body, not personality or behaviour.","zh":"這個短語重點是身體，而不是性格或行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a bit like","meaning":"有點像……","examples":[{"en":"The body is short and rounded, a bit like a barrel.","zh":"牠的身體短而圓，有點像桶。"},{"en":"A bit like means slightly similar to something else.","zh":"有點像某物意思是與另一事物略為相似。"},{"en":"The new library is a bit like a café because students can read and relax there.","zh":"新圖書館有點像咖啡店，因為學生可以在那裏閱讀和放鬆。"},{"en":"Comparing something to a familiar object helps listeners imagine it more easily.","zh":"把某物與熟悉物件比較，有助聽眾更容易想像。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and useful for simple descriptions.","zh":"這個短語較口語，適合用於簡單描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"barrel","meaning":"桶","examples":[{"en":"The tardigrade’s body is rounded, a bit like a barrel.","zh":"緩步動物的身體呈圓形，有點像桶。"},{"en":"A barrel is a large round container often used for storing liquid or goods.","zh":"桶是大型圓形容器，常用來儲存液體或貨物。"},{"en":"A water barrel in a garden can collect rainwater for plants.","zh":"花園中的水桶可以收集雨水給植物使用。"},{"en":"Saying something looks like a barrel suggests it is rounded and thick.","zh":"說某物看起來像桶，暗示它圓而厚實。"},{"en":"This word helps describe a short, rounded shape.","zh":"這個詞有助描述短而圓的形狀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"comprise four segments","meaning":"由四個節段組成","examples":[{"en":"The tardigrade’s body comprises four segments.","zh":"緩步動物的身體由四個節段組成。"},{"en":"To comprise four segments means to be made up of four separate sections.","zh":"由四個節段組成意思是由四個分開部分構成。"},{"en":"A simple report may comprise four sections: introduction, method, results and conclusion.","zh":"一份簡單報告可以由四個部分組成：引言、方法、結果和結論。"},{"en":"Dividing something into segments helps people describe its structure clearly.","zh":"把某物分成節段有助人們清楚描述其結構。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and useful in scientific description.","zh":"這個短語較正式，適合科學描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"segment","meaning":"節段","examples":[{"en":"Each segment has a pair of legs.","zh":"每個節段都有一對腿。"},{"en":"A segment is one part of something that has been divided into sections.","zh":"節段是某物被分成多部分後的其中一部分。"},{"en":"An orange has segments that can be separated and eaten one by one.","zh":"橙有一瓣瓣節段，可以逐一分開來吃。"},{"en":"In animals, body segments can help scientists describe where legs or organs are located.","zh":"在動物身上，身體節段可以幫助科學家描述腿或器官的位置。"},{"en":"This word is useful for describing parts of a larger whole.","zh":"這個詞適合用來描述整體中的部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a pair of","meaning":"一對……","examples":[{"en":"Each segment has a pair of legs.","zh":"每個節段都有一對腿。"},{"en":"A pair of something means two matching or connected items.","zh":"一對某物意思是兩件相配或相連的物件。"},{"en":"A pair of shoes includes one shoe for each foot.","zh":"一對鞋包括左右腳各一隻鞋。"},{"en":"In biology, a pair of legs means two legs found together on the same body section.","zh":"在生物學中，一對腿意思是在同一身體部分上一起出現的兩條腿。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when counting things that naturally come in twos.","zh":"當計算自然成雙的事物時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at the end of which","meaning":"在其末端","examples":[{"en":"Each segment has a pair of legs, at the end of which are sharp claws.","zh":"每個節段都有一對腿，而在其末端有尖銳的爪。"},{"en":"At the end of which means located at the final part of the thing just mentioned.","zh":"在其末端意思是位於剛提及事物的最後部分。"},{"en":"The pen has a small button, at the end of which is a rubber grip.","zh":"這枝筆有一個小按鈕，而在其末端有橡膠握位。"},{"en":"This phrase lets writers add extra information about a specific part clearly.","zh":"這個短語讓作者清楚補充某個特定部分的資料。"},{"en":"It is formal and often appears in careful descriptions.","zh":"它較正式，常出現在仔細描述中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sharp claws","meaning":"尖銳的爪","examples":[{"en":"Each leg may have between four and eight sharp claws.","zh":"每條腿可能有四至八隻尖銳的爪。"},{"en":"Sharp claws are pointed nails or hooks that can grip, scratch or hold onto surfaces.","zh":"尖銳的爪是能抓握、抓刮或附着表面的尖形指甲或鉤狀物。"},{"en":"A cat uses sharp claws to climb trees and catch toys.","zh":"貓用尖銳的爪爬樹和抓玩具。"},{"en":"Sharp claws help some animals hold food, climb or defend themselves.","zh":"尖銳的爪幫助一些動物抓住食物、攀爬或自衛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both shape and function.","zh":"這個短語同時描述形狀和功能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"I should also say that","meaning":"我也應該說明","examples":[{"en":"I should also say that some species do not have any claws.","zh":"我也應該說明，有些物種沒有任何爪。"},{"en":"I should also say that is used to add an important extra point.","zh":"我也應該說明用來加入一個重要補充點。"},{"en":"I should also say that the library closes early on Fridays.","zh":"我也應該說明，圖書館星期五會提早關門。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase when they realise another detail should be included.","zh":"說話者意識到應包括另一個細節時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds natural in presentations and spoken explanations.","zh":"這個短語在匯報和口頭解釋中聽起來自然。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"disc","meaning":"圓盤；吸盤狀構造","examples":[{"en":"Some species have discs instead of claws.","zh":"有些物種有圓盤，而不是爪。"},{"en":"A disc is a flat, round shape or structure.","zh":"圓盤是扁平而圓形的形狀或構造。"},{"en":"A suction cup looks like a small disc that can stick to glass.","zh":"吸盤看起來像一個可以黏在玻璃上的小圓盤。"},{"en":"In animals, disc-like structures may help them attach to surfaces.","zh":"在動物身上，圓盤狀構造可能幫助牠們附着在表面。"},{"en":"This word describes a round, flat form.","zh":"這個詞描述圓而扁平的形態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"by means of","meaning":"透過……方式","examples":[{"en":"These discs work by means of suction.","zh":"這些圓盤透過吸附作用運作。"},{"en":"By means of something means using that method or process.","zh":"透過某種方式意思是使用該方法或過程。"},{"en":"Students can share files by means of an online classroom platform.","zh":"學生可以透過網上課室平台分享檔案。"},{"en":"A lift moves people between floors by means of a motor and cables.","zh":"升降機透過摩打和鋼纜把人送到不同樓層。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and explains how something works.","zh":"這個短語較正式，用來解釋某物如何運作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"suction","meaning":"吸附作用","examples":[{"en":"The discs work by means of suction.","zh":"這些圓盤透過吸附作用運作。"},{"en":"Suction is the pulling force created when air or liquid pressure draws something inward or holds it in place.","zh":"吸附作用是由空氣或液體壓力把某物向內拉或固定在原位的力量。"},{"en":"A bathroom hook may stick to tiles by suction.","zh":"浴室掛鉤可能透過吸附作用黏在瓷磚上。"},{"en":"Suction helps some objects attach without glue or nails.","zh":"吸附作用幫助一些物件不用膠水或釘子也能附着。"},{"en":"This word is often used when describing how something sticks or draws liquid.","zh":"這個詞常用於描述某物如何黏住或吸取液體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"enable something to","meaning":"使……能夠","examples":[{"en":"The discs enable the tardigrade to cling on to surfaces.","zh":"這些圓盤使緩步動物能夠附着在表面上。"},{"en":"To enable something to do something means to make it possible for it to do that action.","zh":"使某物能夠做某事意思是令它可以完成該行動。"},{"en":"Good lighting enables students to read without straining their eyes.","zh":"良好燈光使學生能夠閱讀而不用勉強眼睛。"},{"en":"Strong internet access enables remote workers to join meetings from home.","zh":"穩定網絡使遙距工作者能夠在家參加會議。"},{"en":"This phrase links a feature with the action it makes possible.","zh":"這個短語把某特徵與其促成的行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cling on to","meaning":"附着在……上","examples":[{"en":"The discs enable the tardigrade to cling on to surfaces.","zh":"這些圓盤使緩步動物能夠附着在表面上。"},{"en":"To cling on to something means to hold onto it tightly.","zh":"附着在某物上意思是緊緊抓住或貼着它。"},{"en":"A child may cling on to a parent’s hand in a crowded station.","zh":"孩子可能在擠迫車站緊握父母的手。"},{"en":"Animals may cling on to rocks or leaves to avoid being washed away.","zh":"動物可能附着在岩石或葉片上，以免被沖走。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests strong attachment or holding.","zh":"這個短語暗示牢固附着或抓握。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"surfaces","meaning":"表面","examples":[{"en":"The tardigrade can cling on to surfaces.","zh":"緩步動物可以附着在表面上。"},{"en":"Surfaces are the outer or top layers of objects.","zh":"表面是物件的外層或上層。"},{"en":"Desks, walls and leaves all have surfaces that can be touched or seen.","zh":"書桌、牆壁和葉片都有可以觸摸或看見的表面。"},{"en":"Some animals have special body parts that help them stick to smooth or rough surfaces.","zh":"有些動物有特殊身體部位，幫助牠們黏附在光滑或粗糙表面。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing where something touches or attaches.","zh":"當描述某物接觸或附着的位置時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"grip its prey","meaning":"抓住獵物","examples":[{"en":"The claws or discs help the tardigrade grip its prey.","zh":"爪或圓盤幫助緩步動物抓住獵物。"},{"en":"To grip its prey means to hold the animal or organism it is hunting firmly.","zh":"抓住獵物意思是牢牢握住牠正在捕食的動物或生物。"},{"en":"A spider uses its legs and web to grip its prey before feeding.","zh":"蜘蛛進食前會用腿和網抓住獵物。"},{"en":"Strong gripping body parts help small animals catch food and stop it escaping.","zh":"強力抓握的身體部位幫助小動物捕捉食物並防止其逃走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes holding prey during feeding or hunting.","zh":"這個短語描述在進食或捕獵時抓住獵物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prey","meaning":"獵物","examples":[{"en":"The tardigrade can grip its prey.","zh":"緩步動物可以抓住牠的獵物。"},{"en":"Prey is an animal or organism that another animal hunts or eats.","zh":"獵物是被另一種動物捕捉或吃掉的動物或生物。"},{"en":"A mouse can be prey for an owl.","zh":"老鼠可以是貓頭鷹的獵物。"},{"en":"Predators need ways to find, catch and hold their prey.","zh":"捕食者需要方法尋找、捕捉和抓住獵物。"},{"en":"This word is used in food-chain and animal-behaviour discussions.","zh":"這個詞用於食物鏈和動物行為的討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"within the body","meaning":"在體內","examples":[{"en":"Within the body, there are no lungs.","zh":"在體內，沒有肺。"},{"en":"Within the body means inside the body.","zh":"在體內意思是在身體內部。"},{"en":"Blood moves within the body to carry oxygen and nutrients.","zh":"血液在體內流動，以運送氧氣和養分。"},{"en":"Scientists study what happens within the body to understand how animals survive.","zh":"科學家研究體內發生的事情，以理解動物如何生存。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing internal structures or processes.","zh":"當描述內部結構或過程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"organs for breathing","meaning":"呼吸器官","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades do not have any organs for breathing.","zh":"緩步動物沒有任何呼吸器官。"},{"en":"Organs for breathing are body parts that help an animal take in oxygen.","zh":"呼吸器官是幫助動物吸收氧氣的身體部位。"},{"en":"Human lungs are organs for breathing.","zh":"人類的肺是呼吸器官。"},{"en":"Animals without obvious breathing organs may exchange gases in other ways.","zh":"沒有明顯呼吸器官的動物可能用其他方式交換氣體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structures linked to respiration.","zh":"這個短語描述與呼吸有關的結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at all","meaning":"完全沒有","examples":[{"en":"There are no organs for breathing at all.","zh":"完全沒有呼吸器官。"},{"en":"At all is used to emphasise a negative statement completely.","zh":"At all 用來完全強調否定說法。"},{"en":"There was no milk at all in the fridge this morning.","zh":"今天早上雪櫃裏完全沒有牛奶。"},{"en":"Adding “at all” makes the meaning stronger and clearer.","zh":"加上 “at all” 會令意思更強、更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears after words like no, not or none.","zh":"這個短語常出現在 no、not 或 none 之後。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"instead","meaning":"相反","examples":[{"en":"Instead, oxygen and blood are transported in a fluid.","zh":"相反，氧氣和血液在液體中運送。"},{"en":"Instead means as an alternative to what was just mentioned.","zh":"相反或取而代之，意思是作為剛才提及事情的替代。"},{"en":"The train was cancelled, so we took a bus instead.","zh":"火車取消了，所以我們改乘巴士。"},{"en":"This word helps show a change from one method, choice or explanation to another.","zh":"這個詞有助顯示由一種方法、選擇或解釋轉為另一種。"},{"en":"It is useful when contrasting what does not happen with what happens.","zh":"當對比不發生的事與實際發生的事時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be transported in","meaning":"在……中運送","examples":[{"en":"Oxygen and blood are transported in a fluid.","zh":"氧氣和血液在液體中運送。"},{"en":"To be transported in something means to be carried or moved through that material or container.","zh":"在某物中運送意思是透過該材料或容器被帶走或移動。"},{"en":"Food may be transported in refrigerated trucks to keep it fresh.","zh":"食物可能在冷藏貨車中運送，以保持新鮮。"},{"en":"In the body, substances can be transported in blood or other fluids.","zh":"在體內，物質可以在血液或其他液體中運送。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the medium or vehicle used for movement.","zh":"這個短語描述用於移動的媒介或工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fluid","meaning":"液體","examples":[{"en":"Oxygen and blood are transported in a fluid.","zh":"氧氣和血液在液體中運送。"},{"en":"A fluid is a substance that can flow, such as a liquid or gas.","zh":"液體或流體是能流動的物質，例如液體或氣體。"},{"en":"Water, oil and air are examples of fluids.","zh":"水、油和空氣都是流體的例子。"},{"en":"Fluids can carry heat, oxygen or nutrients from one place to another.","zh":"流體可以把熱量、氧氣或養分從一處帶到另一處。"},{"en":"This word is common in science when discussing movement inside bodies or machines.","zh":"這個詞常見於科學中，用來討論身體或機器內的流動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fill the cavity of the body","meaning":"填滿體腔","examples":[{"en":"A fluid fills the cavity of the body.","zh":"液體填滿體腔。"},{"en":"To fill the cavity of the body means to occupy the open space inside the body.","zh":"填滿體腔意思是佔據身體內部的空間。"},{"en":"In some animals, internal fluid fills body spaces and helps transport substances.","zh":"在一些動物中，內部液體填滿身體空間並幫助運送物質。"},{"en":"When a space is filled with fluid, the fluid can support movement or internal exchange.","zh":"當空間被液體填滿，液體可以支持運動或內部交換。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where the fluid is located.","zh":"這個短語描述液體所在的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cavity of the body","meaning":"體腔","examples":[{"en":"Oxygen and blood are transported in a fluid that fills the cavity of the body.","zh":"氧氣和血液在填滿體腔的液體中運送。"},{"en":"The cavity of the body is an internal space inside an animal’s body.","zh":"體腔是動物身體內部的空間。"},{"en":"A doctor studies body cavities to understand where organs and fluids are located.","zh":"醫生研究體腔，以了解器官和液體的位置。"},{"en":"In small animals, a body cavity may help hold fluid that moves materials around.","zh":"在小型動物中，體腔可能幫助容納運送物質的液體。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and biological.","zh":"這個短語較正式，屬於生物學用語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as far as...is concerned","meaning":"至於……","examples":[{"en":"As far as the tardigrade’s head is concerned, it looks rather strange.","zh":"至於緩步動物的頭部，它看起來相當奇怪。"},{"en":"As far as something is concerned means regarding that particular topic or part.","zh":"至於某事意思是關於該特定主題或部分。"},{"en":"As far as homework is concerned, students must submit it by Friday.","zh":"至於功課，學生必須在星期五前提交。"},{"en":"This phrase helps narrow attention to one aspect of a larger subject.","zh":"這個短語幫助把注意力收窄到較大主題的一個方面。"},{"en":"It is useful in reports and spoken presentations.","zh":"它適合用於報告和口頭匯報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the best way I can describe","meaning":"我能作出的最佳描述是","examples":[{"en":"The best way I can describe the head is that it looks rather strange.","zh":"我能對牠頭部作出的最佳描述是，它看起來相當奇怪。"},{"en":"The best way I can describe means this is the clearest description I can give.","zh":"我能作出的最佳描述是，意思是這是我能給出的最清楚描述。"},{"en":"The best way I can describe the taste is that it is sweet but slightly smoky.","zh":"我能對這味道作出的最佳描述是，它甜但略帶煙燻味。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase when something is difficult to explain exactly.","zh":"當某事難以精確解釋時，說話者會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It helps introduce an approximate but useful description.","zh":"它有助引入近似但有用的描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rather strange","meaning":"相當奇怪","examples":[{"en":"The tardigrade’s head looks rather strange.","zh":"緩步動物的頭部看起來相當奇怪。"},{"en":"Rather strange means quite unusual or odd.","zh":"相當奇怪意思是頗不尋常或古怪。"},{"en":"The new school timetable looks rather strange because lunch is before the first lesson.","zh":"新學校時間表看起來相當奇怪，因為午飯在第一堂課之前。"},{"en":"Something may look strange when it is unfamiliar or different from what we expect.","zh":"當某事陌生或與預期不同，它可能看起來奇怪。"},{"en":"This phrase is softer than saying something is very strange.","zh":"這個短語比說非常奇怪語氣較柔和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a bit squashed","meaning":"有點扁","examples":[{"en":"The tardigrade’s head looks a bit squashed.","zh":"緩步動物的頭部看起來有點扁。"},{"en":"A bit squashed means slightly flattened or pressed out of shape.","zh":"有點扁意思是略為被壓平或壓得變形。"},{"en":"A sandwich may look a bit squashed after being kept at the bottom of a schoolbag.","zh":"三文治放在書包底部後，可能看起來有點扁。"},{"en":"Something becomes squashed when pressure pushes it flatter than usual.","zh":"當壓力把某物壓得比平常更平，它就會變扁。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and visual.","zh":"這個短語較口語，而且帶有視覺感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"websites I looked at","meaning":"我查看過的網站","examples":[{"en":"Many of the websites I looked at described the tardigrade as cute.","zh":"我查看過的許多網站都把緩步動物形容為可愛。"},{"en":"Websites I looked at means the online pages I visited or checked.","zh":"我查看過的網站意思是我瀏覽或查閱過的網頁。"},{"en":"The websites I looked at gave different advice about preparing for interviews.","zh":"我查看過的網站對準備面試給出不同建議。"},{"en":"When using websites for research, students should check whether the information is reliable.","zh":"學生使用網站做研究時，應檢查資料是否可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when explaining where information was found.","zh":"這個短語常用於解釋資料來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"describe its appearance as","meaning":"把其外貌形容為……","examples":[{"en":"Some websites describe its appearance as cute.","zh":"有些網站把牠的外貌形容為可愛。"},{"en":"To describe its appearance as something means to say what it looks like.","zh":"把其外貌形容為某樣子，意思是說它看起來如何。"},{"en":"A travel blog may describe a hotel’s appearance as modern and bright.","zh":"旅遊博客可能把酒店外貌形容為現代而明亮。"},{"en":"Descriptions of appearance can be subjective because people notice different features.","zh":"外貌描述可以很主觀，因為人們注意到不同特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how something looks.","zh":"這個短語重點是某物看起來如何。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not exactly very scientific","meaning":"不算十分科學","examples":[{"en":"Describing a tardigrade as cute is not exactly very scientific.","zh":"把緩步動物形容為可愛不算十分科學。"},{"en":"Not exactly very scientific means not based on precise scientific language or evidence.","zh":"不算十分科學意思是不是基於精確科學語言或證據。"},{"en":"Calling a medicine “magic” is not exactly very scientific, even if people like the result.","zh":"把藥物稱為「神奇」不算十分科學，即使人們喜歡其效果。"},{"en":"Scientific descriptions should use clear features rather than personal feelings alone.","zh":"科學描述應使用清楚特徵，而不是只靠個人感受。"},{"en":"This phrase gently criticises a statement as too informal or subjective.","zh":"這個短語溫和地批評某說法太口語或主觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a kind of tube","meaning":"一種管狀物","examples":[{"en":"The tardigrade’s mouth is a kind of tube.","zh":"緩步動物的口是一種管狀物。"},{"en":"A kind of tube means a structure shaped like a narrow hollow cylinder.","zh":"一種管狀物意思是形狀像狹窄中空圓柱的構造。"},{"en":"A straw is a kind of tube because liquid can pass through it.","zh":"飲管是一種管狀物，因為液體可以通過它。"},{"en":"Tube-like structures often help move liquid, air or food from one place to another.","zh":"管狀構造常幫助液體、空氣或食物從一處移到另一處。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a simple comparison to explain shape.","zh":"這個短語用簡單比較來解釋形狀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"open outwards","meaning":"向外張開","examples":[{"en":"The tardigrade’s mouth can open outwards.","zh":"緩步動物的口可以向外張開。"},{"en":"To open outwards means to open in a direction away from the centre or inside.","zh":"向外張開意思是朝離開中心或內部的方向打開。"},{"en":"Some shop doors open outwards onto the street.","zh":"有些店門會向外打開到街上。"},{"en":"A structure that opens outwards may reveal what is hidden inside.","zh":"向外張開的構造可能露出隱藏在內部的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the direction of opening.","zh":"這個短語描述張開的方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reveal","meaning":"露出；顯露","examples":[{"en":"The mouth can open outwards to reveal teeth-like structures.","zh":"口可以向外張開，露出牙齒狀構造。"},{"en":"To reveal something means to show something that was hidden or not clear before.","zh":"露出或顯露某物意思是展示之前隱藏或不清楚的東西。"},{"en":"Opening a gift box may reveal a handmade card inside.","zh":"打開禮物盒可能會露出裏面的手製卡。"},{"en":"A microscope can reveal details that cannot be seen with the naked eye.","zh":"顯微鏡可以顯露肉眼看不見的細節。"},{"en":"This verb is useful when something becomes visible or known.","zh":"當某物變得可見或被知道時，這個動詞很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"teeth-like structures","meaning":"牙齒狀構造","examples":[{"en":"The tardigrade has teeth-like structures known as stylets.","zh":"緩步動物有被稱為口針的牙齒狀構造。"},{"en":"Teeth-like structures are parts that look or work a little like teeth.","zh":"牙齒狀構造是外形或功能有點像牙齒的部分。"},{"en":"Some tools have teeth-like structures that help them grip or cut material.","zh":"有些工具有牙齒狀構造，幫助它們抓住或切割材料。"},{"en":"In animals, teeth-like structures may help pierce, scrape or hold food.","zh":"在動物身上，牙齒狀構造可能幫助刺穿、刮取或抓住食物。"},{"en":"This phrase compares unfamiliar body parts with teeth to make their function easier to imagine.","zh":"這個短語把陌生身體部位與牙齒作比較，令功能較易想像。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"known as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"These teeth-like structures are known as stylets.","zh":"這些牙齒狀構造被稱為口針。"},{"en":"Known as means called by a particular name.","zh":"被稱為意思是以某個特定名稱稱呼。"},{"en":"The city is known as a financial centre because many banks operate there.","zh":"這座城市被稱為金融中心，因為許多銀行在那裏營運。"},{"en":"In science, special structures are often known by precise technical names.","zh":"在科學中，特殊構造常以精確技術名稱稱呼。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the accepted name of something.","zh":"這個短語引入某物被接受的名稱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"stylets","meaning":"口針","examples":[{"en":"The tardigrade uses stylets to pierce plant or animal cells.","zh":"緩步動物使用口針刺穿植物或動物細胞。"},{"en":"Stylets are sharp, needle-like structures used by some tiny animals to pierce cells or tissues.","zh":"口針是一些微小動物用來刺穿細胞或組織的尖銳針狀構造。"},{"en":"A biology diagram may label the stylets near the tardigrade’s mouth.","zh":"生物圖可能會在緩步動物口部附近標示口針。"},{"en":"Stylets help the animal reach liquid food inside cells.","zh":"口針幫助動物取得細胞內的液體食物。"},{"en":"This word is a specialised biological term.","zh":"這個詞是專門的生物學術語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sharp enough to","meaning":"鋒利得足以……","examples":[{"en":"The stylets are sharp enough to pierce plant or animal cells.","zh":"口針鋒利得足以刺穿植物或動物細胞。"},{"en":"Sharp enough to do something means sufficiently sharp to complete that action.","zh":"鋒利得足以做某事意思是鋒利程度足夠完成該行動。"},{"en":"The knife is sharp enough to cut tomatoes without crushing them.","zh":"這把刀鋒利得足以切開番茄而不把它壓爛。"},{"en":"If a tool is not sharp enough, it may bend, slip or fail to cut properly.","zh":"如果工具不夠鋒利，它可能彎曲、滑開或無法正確切割。"},{"en":"This phrase links degree with ability.","zh":"這個短語把程度與能力連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pierce","meaning":"刺穿","examples":[{"en":"The stylets can pierce plant or animal cells.","zh":"口針可以刺穿植物或動物細胞。"},{"en":"To pierce something means to make a hole through it with a sharp point.","zh":"刺穿某物意思是用尖端穿過它並形成洞。"},{"en":"A needle can pierce fabric when someone is sewing a button.","zh":"縫鈕扣時，針可以刺穿布料。"},{"en":"Sharp structures pierce surfaces more easily than blunt ones.","zh":"尖銳構造比鈍的構造更容易刺穿表面。"},{"en":"This verb describes pushing through a surface.","zh":"這個動詞描述穿過表面的動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"plant or animal cells","meaning":"植物或動物細胞","examples":[{"en":"The stylets are sharp enough to pierce plant or animal cells.","zh":"口針鋒利得足以刺穿植物或動物細胞。"},{"en":"Plant or animal cells are the basic living units that make up plants and animals.","zh":"植物或動物細胞是構成植物和動物的基本生命單位。"},{"en":"Students may look at plant cells from an onion under a microscope.","zh":"學生可能在顯微鏡下觀察洋蔥的植物細胞。"},{"en":"Cells contain materials that some tiny animals can feed on.","zh":"細胞含有一些微小動物可以攝取的物質。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the living building blocks of plants and animals.","zh":"這個短語指植物和動物的生命基本單位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be found","meaning":"被發現於","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades are found in every part of the world.","zh":"緩步動物被發現於世界各地。"},{"en":"To be found somewhere means to exist or live in that place.","zh":"被發現於某地意思是存在或生活在該地方。"},{"en":"Mangrove trees are found along many warm coastal areas.","zh":"紅樹林被發現於許多溫暖沿海地區。"},{"en":"If a species is found in many places, it may be able to survive different conditions.","zh":"如果一個物種被發現於許多地方，它可能能在不同環境中生存。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when describing where living things occur.","zh":"當描述生物出現地點時，這個短語很常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"every part of the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades live in every part of the world.","zh":"緩步動物生活在世界各地。"},{"en":"Every part of the world means all regions or many different places across the planet.","zh":"世界各地意思是地球上所有地區或許多不同地方。"},{"en":"Plastic waste has become a problem in almost every part of the world.","zh":"塑膠廢物已成為世界各地幾乎都面對的問題。"},{"en":"A species found in every part of the world must be highly adaptable.","zh":"能在世界各地被發現的物種必定非常適應不同環境。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises extremely wide distribution.","zh":"這個短語強調分布極其廣泛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a variety of habitats","meaning":"各種棲息地","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades live in a variety of habitats.","zh":"緩步動物生活在各種棲息地。"},{"en":"A variety of habitats means many different natural environments where organisms can live.","zh":"各種棲息地意思是許多不同的自然生活環境。"},{"en":"Frogs may live in a variety of habitats, including ponds, forests and wetlands.","zh":"青蛙可能生活在各種棲息地，包括池塘、森林和濕地。"},{"en":"Species that use many habitats may survive better when one environment changes.","zh":"能使用多種棲息地的物種，在某一環境改變時可能更容易存活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ecological diversity.","zh":"這個短語描述生態上的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"most commonly","meaning":"最常見的是","examples":[{"en":"Most commonly, tardigrades are found on the bed of a lake.","zh":"最常見的是，緩步動物被發現於湖底。"},{"en":"Most commonly means most often or in the usual case.","zh":"最常見的是意思是最經常或在通常情況下。"},{"en":"Most commonly, students revise vocabulary by reading examples and repeating words.","zh":"最常見的是，學生透過閱讀例句和重複詞語來溫習詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers what usually happens, while allowing exceptions.","zh":"這個短語告訴讀者通常會發生甚麼，同時容許例外。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing a typical location, habit or pattern.","zh":"當描述典型地點、習慣或模式時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the bed of a lake","meaning":"湖底","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades may live on the bed of a lake.","zh":"緩步動物可能生活在湖底。"},{"en":"The bed of a lake is the bottom surface beneath the water.","zh":"湖底是水下的底部表面。"},{"en":"Mud, stones and plants can collect on the bed of a lake.","zh":"泥、石頭和植物可以積聚在湖底。"},{"en":"Small organisms may live on the lake bed because food and shelter can be found there.","zh":"小型生物可能生活在湖底，因為那裏可以找到食物和庇護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific underwater location.","zh":"這個短語描述一個特定的水下位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"wet environments","meaning":"潮濕環境","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades are often found in very wet environments.","zh":"緩步動物常被發現於非常潮濕的環境。"},{"en":"Wet environments are places with a lot of water or moisture.","zh":"潮濕環境是有很多水或濕氣的地方。"},{"en":"Ponds, damp soil and mossy rocks are wet environments for many small organisms.","zh":"池塘、濕泥土和長滿苔蘚的岩石，是許多小生物的潮濕環境。"},{"en":"Animals that need moisture may die or enter special states when wet environments dry out.","zh":"需要水分的動物在潮濕環境乾掉時，可能死亡或進入特殊狀態。"},{"en":"This phrase describes habitats where water is important.","zh":"這個短語描述水分很重要的棲息地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"research has found that","meaning":"研究發現","examples":[{"en":"Research has found that tardigrades can survive extreme conditions.","zh":"研究發現緩步動物能在極端環境中存活。"},{"en":"Research has found that means studies have shown evidence for a conclusion.","zh":"研究發現某事意思是研究已顯示支持某結論的證據。"},{"en":"Research has found that regular sleep helps students remember new information.","zh":"研究發現，規律睡眠有助學生記住新資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting a finding based on investigation rather than opinion.","zh":"當報告基於調查而非意見的發現時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It makes a statement sound evidence-based.","zh":"它令說法聽起來有證據支持。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be capable of","meaning":"有能力……","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades are capable of surviving radiation and very high pressure.","zh":"緩步動物有能力承受輻射和很高壓力而存活。"},{"en":"To be capable of something means to have the ability to do it.","zh":"有能力做某事意思是具有做該事的能力。"},{"en":"A well-trained nurse is capable of staying calm during an emergency.","zh":"受過良好訓練的護士有能力在緊急情況中保持冷靜。"},{"en":"Being capable of a difficult task does not mean it happens easily every time.","zh":"有能力完成困難任務，不代表每次都能輕鬆做到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability or potential.","zh":"這個短語描述能力或潛能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"survive radiation","meaning":"承受輻射而存活","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades can survive radiation.","zh":"緩步動物能承受輻射而存活。"},{"en":"To survive radiation means to stay alive after being exposed to harmful energy rays.","zh":"承受輻射而存活意思是在接觸有害能量射線後仍然活着。"},{"en":"Some medical treatments use radiation, so hospitals carefully protect staff and patients.","zh":"有些醫療治療會使用輻射，所以醫院會仔細保護職員和病人。"},{"en":"Radiation can damage living cells, so surviving it is unusual and scientifically interesting.","zh":"輻射可以損害活細胞，因此能承受輻射而存活是不尋常且具科學趣味的。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing extreme biological tolerance.","zh":"這個短語用於討論極端生物耐受力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"high pressure","meaning":"高壓","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades can survive very high pressure.","zh":"緩步動物能在很高壓力下存活。"},{"en":"High pressure means strong force pressing on something from outside or within.","zh":"高壓意思是來自外部或內部、壓在某物上的強大力量。"},{"en":"Deep-sea animals must survive high pressure because of the weight of water above them.","zh":"深海動物必須承受高壓，因為上方水體重量很大。"},{"en":"High pressure can crush objects that are not built to withstand it.","zh":"高壓可以壓碎沒有設計成能抵受壓力的物件。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe physical force or stressful situations, depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可描述物理壓力，也可視乎語境描述壓力情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be able to withstand","meaning":"能夠抵受……","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades are able to withstand extreme temperatures.","zh":"緩步動物能夠抵受極端溫度。"},{"en":"To be able to withstand something means to survive or resist it without being destroyed.","zh":"能夠抵受某事意思是在其中存活或抗住它而不被毀壞。"},{"en":"A strong umbrella can withstand heavy rain and wind.","zh":"堅固雨傘能夠抵受大雨和強風。"},{"en":"Buildings in earthquake zones must be able to withstand shaking.","zh":"地震區的建築必須能夠抵受震動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on resistance to difficult conditions.","zh":"這個短語重點是對困難環境的抵抗力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"temperatures as cold as","meaning":"低至……的溫度","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades can withstand temperatures as cold as minus 200 degrees centigrade.","zh":"緩步動物能抵受低至攝氏零下 200 度的溫度。"},{"en":"Temperatures as cold as a certain number means temperatures reaching that extremely low level.","zh":"低至某數值的溫度意思是溫度達到該極低水平。"},{"en":"Some freezers can reach temperatures as cold as minus 80 degrees centigrade for laboratory samples.","zh":"有些冷凍櫃可達低至攝氏零下 80 度的溫度，用於保存實驗室樣本。"},{"en":"Very cold temperatures can stop normal biological activity in most organisms.","zh":"極低溫會停止大多數生物的正常生命活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to emphasise extreme cold.","zh":"這個短語用來強調極端寒冷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"degrees centigrade","meaning":"攝氏度","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades can survive temperatures below minus 200 degrees centigrade.","zh":"緩步動物能在低於攝氏零下 200 度的溫度中存活。"},{"en":"Degrees centigrade are units used to measure temperature on the Celsius scale.","zh":"攝氏度是用攝氏溫標量度溫度的單位。"},{"en":"Water freezes at 0 degrees centigrade under normal conditions.","zh":"在正常情況下，水在攝氏 0 度結冰。"},{"en":"Weather reports in many countries use degrees centigrade to describe daily temperature.","zh":"許多國家的天氣報告使用攝氏度描述每日溫度。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to refer to Celsius degrees.","zh":"這個短語是指攝氏溫度的正式說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"highs of more than","meaning":"高於……的高溫","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades can also withstand highs of more than 148 degrees centigrade.","zh":"緩步動物也能抵受高於攝氏 148 度的高溫。"},{"en":"Highs of more than a number means temperatures or levels above that number.","zh":"高於某數值的高溫意思是溫度或水平超過該數字。"},{"en":"In summer, some desert areas can reach highs of more than 45 degrees centigrade.","zh":"夏天時，有些沙漠地區可達高於攝氏 45 度的高溫。"},{"en":"High temperatures can damage living tissues, so surviving extreme heat is remarkable.","zh":"高溫可以損害活組織，所以能在極端高溫中存活很不尋常。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when describing maximum temperatures.","zh":"這個短語常用於描述最高溫度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"it has been said that","meaning":"據說","examples":[{"en":"It has been said that tardigrades could survive long after humans disappear.","zh":"據說緩步動物在人類消失後仍可長期存活。"},{"en":"It has been said that means some people have claimed or suggested this, but the speaker may not be proving it directly.","zh":"據說某事意思是有人聲稱或提出這說法，但說話者未必直接證明它。"},{"en":"It has been said that breakfast is the most important meal of the day.","zh":"據說早餐是一天中最重要的一餐。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting a common claim carefully.","zh":"當謹慎轉述常見說法時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It sounds less certain than saying “research proves that”.","zh":"它聽起來不如「研究證明」那樣肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"survive long after","meaning":"在……之後仍長期存活","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades could survive long after human beings have been wiped out.","zh":"緩步動物可以在人類滅絕之後仍長期存活。"},{"en":"To survive long after something means to remain alive or continue existing for a long time following that event.","zh":"在某事之後仍長期存活意思是在該事件後長時間保持生命或繼續存在。"},{"en":"Some old traditions survive long after the original reason for them has been forgotten.","zh":"有些古老傳統在其原本原因被遺忘後仍長期存在。"},{"en":"A strong seed may survive long after the plant above it has died.","zh":"強壯的種子可能在地面上的植物死去後仍長期存活。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises continued existence after a major change.","zh":"這個短語強調重大變化後仍繼續存在。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"human beings","meaning":"人類","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades could outlive human beings.","zh":"緩步動物可能比人類存活更久。"},{"en":"Human beings are people, or members of the human species.","zh":"人類是指人，或人這個物種的成員。"},{"en":"Human beings depend on water, food and suitable living conditions.","zh":"人類依賴水、食物和合適生活環境。"},{"en":"Unlike many tiny organisms, human beings cannot survive extreme environments without protection.","zh":"與許多微小生物不同，人類沒有保護便不能在極端環境中存活。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than simply saying “people”.","zh":"這個短語比簡單說 “people” 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be wiped out","meaning":"被消滅；滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Human beings could be wiped out by an asteroid.","zh":"人類可能被小行星消滅。"},{"en":"To be wiped out means to be completely destroyed or killed.","zh":"被消滅或滅絕意思是被完全摧毀或殺死。"},{"en":"A disease can wipe out a crop if farmers cannot stop it quickly.","zh":"如果農民不能迅速阻止疾病，它可以摧毀整批農作物。"},{"en":"When a species is wiped out, it disappears forever.","zh":"當一個物種滅絕，它便永遠消失。"},{"en":"This phrase is strong and often used for disasters or extinction.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈，常用於災難或滅絕。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the event of","meaning":"萬一發生……","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades could survive even in the event of an asteroid hitting the earth.","zh":"萬一發生小行星撞擊地球，緩步動物甚至可能存活。"},{"en":"In the event of something means if that situation happens.","zh":"萬一發生某事意思是如果該情況發生。"},{"en":"In the event of a fire, students should leave the classroom calmly.","zh":"萬一發生火警，學生應冷靜離開課室。"},{"en":"Emergency plans explain what people should do in the event of danger.","zh":"應急計劃解釋萬一有危險時人們應做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used for possible serious events.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於可能發生的嚴重事件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"asteroid","meaning":"小行星","examples":[{"en":"An asteroid hitting the earth might not wipe out tardigrades.","zh":"小行星撞擊地球可能不會消滅緩步動物。"},{"en":"An asteroid is a rocky object that moves around the sun, smaller than a planet.","zh":"小行星是圍繞太陽運行、比行星小的岩石物體。"},{"en":"Scientists track asteroids to see whether any may pass close to Earth.","zh":"科學家追蹤小行星，以查看是否有任何小行星可能接近地球。"},{"en":"A large asteroid impact could cause serious damage to life on Earth.","zh":"大型小行星撞擊可能對地球生命造成嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"This word is often used in space science and disaster discussions.","zh":"這個詞常用於太空科學和災難討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hit the earth","meaning":"撞擊地球","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades might survive even if an asteroid hit the earth.","zh":"即使小行星撞擊地球，緩步動物也可能存活。"},{"en":"To hit the earth means to collide with or strike the planet.","zh":"撞擊地球意思是與地球碰撞或擊中地球。"},{"en":"Small space rocks often burn up before they hit the earth.","zh":"小型太空岩石通常在撞擊地球前已燃燒殆盡。"},{"en":"If a large object hit the earth, it could change the environment dramatically.","zh":"如果大型物體撞擊地球，可能會劇烈改變環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical impact with Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述與地球的物理撞擊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"conditions become too extreme","meaning":"環境變得過於極端","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades react when conditions become too extreme.","zh":"當環境變得過於極端時，緩步動物會作出反應。"},{"en":"Conditions become too extreme when the environment becomes too hot, cold, dry or dangerous for normal activity.","zh":"環境變得過於極端，是指環境太熱、太冷、太乾或太危險，以致不能正常活動。"},{"en":"Plants may die when conditions become too extreme during a long drought.","zh":"長期乾旱期間，當環境變得過於極端，植物可能死亡。"},{"en":"Animals often change behaviour when conditions become too extreme for ordinary survival.","zh":"當環境變得過於極端、不利於正常生存，動物常會改變行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the point when normal life becomes difficult.","zh":"這個短語描述正常生活變得困難的臨界點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at risk of","meaning":"有……的風險","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades enter cryptobiosis when they are at risk of drying out.","zh":"當緩步動物有乾枯的風險時，牠們會進入隱生狀態。"},{"en":"At risk of something means in danger of experiencing that problem.","zh":"有某事的風險意思是有可能遭遇該問題或危險。"},{"en":"A patient may be at risk of dehydration if they cannot drink enough water.","zh":"如果病人不能喝足夠水，可能有脫水的風險。"},{"en":"When people know they are at risk of harm, they can take protective action.","zh":"當人們知道自己有受害風險，便可以採取保護行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when warning about possible danger.","zh":"當提醒可能危險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dry out","meaning":"乾枯","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades may enter a special state if they are at risk of drying out.","zh":"如果緩步動物有乾枯風險，牠們可能進入特殊狀態。"},{"en":"To dry out means to lose moisture and become dry.","zh":"乾枯意思是失去水分並變乾。"},{"en":"Soil can dry out quickly during hot weather if plants are not watered.","zh":"炎熱天氣中，如果植物沒有澆水，泥土會很快乾枯。"},{"en":"Small organisms may need special ways to survive when their environment dries out.","zh":"當環境乾枯時，小型生物可能需要特殊方式生存。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing water loss.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論水分流失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"enter a state called","meaning":"進入一種稱為……的狀態","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades enter a state called cryptobiosis.","zh":"緩步動物進入一種稱為隱生的狀態。"},{"en":"To enter a state called something means to change into a condition with that name.","zh":"進入一種稱為某名的狀態，意思是轉變成具有該名稱的情況。"},{"en":"Some animals enter a state called hibernation during winter.","zh":"有些動物在冬天進入一種稱為冬眠的狀態。"},{"en":"Naming the state helps scientists describe what is happening clearly.","zh":"為該狀態命名，有助科學家清楚描述正在發生的事。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a technical term for a condition.","zh":"這個短語引入一個描述狀態的技術術語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cryptobiosis","meaning":"隱生","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades can survive extreme conditions through cryptobiosis.","zh":"緩步動物可以透過隱生在極端環境中存活。"},{"en":"Cryptobiosis is a state in which an organism’s life processes slow down greatly to survive harsh conditions.","zh":"隱生是一種生物生命過程大幅減慢，以在惡劣環境中存活的狀態。"},{"en":"A science lesson on cryptobiosis may explain how some tiny animals survive drying out.","zh":"關於隱生的科學課可能解釋一些微小動物如何在乾枯中存活。"},{"en":"Cryptobiosis helps organisms wait until water or better conditions return.","zh":"隱生幫助生物等待水分或較好環境回來。"},{"en":"This word is a specialised biological term.","zh":"這個詞是專門的生物學術語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"curl into a ball","meaning":"捲成一個球狀","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades curl into a ball when they become a tun.","zh":"緩步動物變成 tun 時會捲成一個球狀。"},{"en":"To curl into a ball means to bend the body into a small rounded shape.","zh":"捲成一個球狀意思是把身體彎曲成小而圓的形狀。"},{"en":"A hedgehog may curl into a ball when it feels threatened.","zh":"刺蝟感到受威脅時可能會捲成一個球狀。"},{"en":"Curling into a ball can protect soft body parts from danger or dryness.","zh":"捲成球狀可以保護柔軟身體部位免受危險或乾燥影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a body position.","zh":"這個短語描述一種身體姿勢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tun","meaning":"tun；隱生球狀體","examples":[{"en":"A tun is the ball-like state of a tardigrade during cryptobiosis.","zh":"tun 是緩步動物在隱生期間的球狀狀態。"},{"en":"A tun is a dried, curled-up form that a tardigrade can enter to survive extreme conditions.","zh":"tun 是緩步動物為了在極端環境中存活而進入的乾燥、捲曲形態。"},{"en":"In a biology diagram, a tun may look like a tiny rounded body with legs pulled in.","zh":"在生物圖中，tun 可能看起來像一個把腿縮起的小圓形身體。"},{"en":"Becoming a tun helps the animal reduce activity and wait for better conditions.","zh":"變成 tun 幫助動物降低活動並等待較好環境。"},{"en":"This word is a technical term for a special survival form.","zh":"這個詞是描述特殊生存形態的技術術語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"by retracting","meaning":"透過縮回……","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades form a tun by retracting their head and legs.","zh":"緩步動物透過縮回頭部和腿形成 tun。"},{"en":"By retracting means by pulling something back or inward.","zh":"透過縮回意思是透過把某物向後或向內拉回。"},{"en":"A turtle protects itself by retracting its head into its shell.","zh":"烏龜透過把頭縮回殼內來保護自己。"},{"en":"Retracting body parts can reduce exposure to danger or harsh conditions.","zh":"縮回身體部位可以減少暴露於危險或惡劣環境。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the action used to create a particular state.","zh":"這個短語解釋用來形成某狀態的動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"metabolism","meaning":"新陳代謝","examples":[{"en":"Their metabolism drops to less than one percent of normal levels.","zh":"牠們的新陳代謝下降至少於正常水平的百分之一。"},{"en":"Metabolism is the chemical activity in living things that uses energy and keeps them alive.","zh":"新陳代謝是生物體內使用能量並維持生命的化學活動。"},{"en":"Exercise can increase a person’s metabolism for a period of time.","zh":"運動可以在一段時間內提高人的新陳代謝。"},{"en":"When metabolism slows down greatly, an organism uses much less energy.","zh":"當新陳代謝大幅減慢，生物會使用少得多的能量。"},{"en":"This word is common in biology and health discussions.","zh":"這個詞常見於生物學和健康討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"drop to less than","meaning":"下降至少於……","examples":[{"en":"Their metabolism drops to less than one percent of normal levels.","zh":"牠們的新陳代謝下降至少於正常水平的百分之一。"},{"en":"To drop to less than a number means to decrease below that amount.","zh":"下降至少於某數值意思是減少到低於該數量。"},{"en":"The temperature may drop to less than 5 degrees at night in winter.","zh":"冬天晚上氣溫可能下降至少於 5 度。"},{"en":"When activity drops to less than usual levels, the body may save energy.","zh":"當活動下降至少於平常水平，身體可能會節省能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decrease below a stated limit.","zh":"這個短語描述下降到低於某個指定界線。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"normal levels","meaning":"正常水平","examples":[{"en":"Their metabolism falls far below normal levels.","zh":"牠們的新陳代謝遠低於正常水平。"},{"en":"Normal levels are the usual or expected amounts of something.","zh":"正常水平是某事物通常或預期的數量。"},{"en":"Doctors check whether a patient’s blood sugar is within normal levels.","zh":"醫生會檢查病人的血糖是否在正常水平內。"},{"en":"If levels fall far below normal, the body or system may not work properly.","zh":"如果水平遠低於正常，身體或系統可能無法正常運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when comparing measurements with what is typical.","zh":"當把量度與典型情況比較時，這個短語很常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"remain like this","meaning":"保持這種狀態","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades can remain like this until they are reintroduced to water.","zh":"緩步動物可以保持這種狀態，直到重新接觸水。"},{"en":"To remain like this means to stay in the same condition or state.","zh":"保持這種狀態意思是停留在同一情況或狀態中。"},{"en":"A classroom may remain like this until the repairs are finished.","zh":"課室可能會保持這種狀態，直到維修完成。"},{"en":"Some organisms can remain inactive until their environment improves.","zh":"有些生物可以保持不活躍，直到環境改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continued state over time.","zh":"這個短語描述狀態隨時間延續。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be reintroduced to","meaning":"重新接觸……","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades come back to life when they are reintroduced to water.","zh":"緩步動物重新接觸水時會恢復生命活動。"},{"en":"To be reintroduced to something means to be brought into contact with it again.","zh":"重新接觸某物意思是再次與它接觸。"},{"en":"A plant may recover when it is reintroduced to sunlight after days in darkness.","zh":"植物在黑暗中多日後重新接觸陽光時，可能會恢復。"},{"en":"Reintroducing water can restart activity in organisms that had dried out.","zh":"重新接觸水可以重新啟動已乾枯生物的活動。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises contact returning after an absence.","zh":"這個短語強調缺失後重新接觸。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"come back to life","meaning":"恢復生命活動","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades can come back to life after being reintroduced to water.","zh":"緩步動物重新接觸水後可以恢復生命活動。"},{"en":"To come back to life means to become active or alive again after seeming dead or inactive.","zh":"恢復生命活動意思是在看似死亡或不活躍後再次變得活躍或有生命力。"},{"en":"A dry plant may seem to come back to life after careful watering.","zh":"乾枯植物在仔細澆水後可能看似恢復生命活動。"},{"en":"In biology, coming back to life may mean activity restarts after dormancy.","zh":"在生物學中，恢復生命活動可能意思是在休眠後重新開始活動。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal or figurative, depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可作字面或比喻使用，視乎語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in a matter of","meaning":"在短短……之內","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades can come back to life in a matter of a few hours.","zh":"緩步動物可以在短短幾小時之內恢復生命活動。"},{"en":"In a matter of a period means within only that short amount of time.","zh":"在短短某段時間之內意思是只在那麼短的時間內。"},{"en":"A phone battery can charge enough for basic use in a matter of minutes.","zh":"手機電池可以在短短幾分鐘內充到足夠基本使用的電量。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that something happens quickly.","zh":"這個短語強調某事發生得很快。"},{"en":"It is often used with minutes, hours or days.","zh":"它常與分鐘、小時或日子一起使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"while in a state of","meaning":"處於……狀態時","examples":[{"en":"While in a state of cryptobiosis, tardigrades produce a protective protein.","zh":"處於隱生狀態時，緩步動物會產生保護性蛋白質。"},{"en":"While in a state of something means during the time when something is in that condition.","zh":"處於某種狀態時意思是在某物處於該情況期間。"},{"en":"While in a state of rest, the body still uses energy for basic functions.","zh":"處於休息狀態時，身體仍會為基本功能使用能量。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an action with the condition in which it happens.","zh":"這個短語把某行動與其發生時的狀態連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful in scientific and formal descriptions.","zh":"它適合用於科學和正式描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"produce a protein","meaning":"產生蛋白質","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades produce a protein that protects their DNA.","zh":"緩步動物會產生一種保護其 DNA 的蛋白質。"},{"en":"To produce a protein means for cells or organisms to make a particular protein.","zh":"產生蛋白質意思是細胞或生物製造某種蛋白質。"},{"en":"The body produces proteins to build tissue and support many functions.","zh":"身體產生蛋白質以建立組織並支援多種功能。"},{"en":"Producing a protective protein can help an organism survive stress or damage.","zh":"產生保護性蛋白質可以幫助生物在壓力或損害中存活。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in biology.","zh":"這個短語常見於生物學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"protect their DNA","meaning":"保護牠們的DNA","examples":[{"en":"The protein protects the tardigrades’ DNA.","zh":"該蛋白質保護緩步動物的 DNA。"},{"en":"To protect their DNA means to prevent damage to the genetic material inside their cells.","zh":"保護牠們的 DNA 意思是防止細胞內的遺傳物質受損。"},{"en":"Sunscreen helps protect human skin cells from some DNA damage caused by sunlight.","zh":"防曬霜幫助保護人類皮膚細胞，減少陽光造成的某些 DNA 損害。"},{"en":"If DNA is badly damaged, cells may not work properly.","zh":"如果 DNA 嚴重受損，細胞可能無法正常運作。"},{"en":"This phrase connects protection with genetic information.","zh":"這個短語把保護與遺傳資訊連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"revive","meaning":"使復活","examples":[{"en":"Scientists revived two tardigrades that had been tuns for more than 30 years.","zh":"科學家使兩隻已成為 tun 超過 30 年的緩步動物復活。"},{"en":"To revive something means to bring it back to life, activity or use.","zh":"使某物復活意思是使它恢復生命、活動或用途。"},{"en":"Doctors may try to revive a patient whose heart has stopped.","zh":"醫生可能嘗試使心臟停止的病人復甦。"},{"en":"Rain can revive dry grass after a long hot period.","zh":"長時間炎熱後，雨水可以使乾草恢復生機。"},{"en":"This verb can be used for living things, plans or traditions.","zh":"這個動詞可以用於生物、計劃或傳統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"for more than","meaning":"超過……","examples":[{"en":"Two tardigrades had been tuns for more than 30 years.","zh":"兩隻緩步動物已成為 tun 超過 30 年。"},{"en":"For more than a period means longer than that amount of time.","zh":"超過某段時間意思是長於該時間。"},{"en":"The library has served the neighbourhood for more than fifty years.","zh":"圖書館服務該社區已超過五十年。"},{"en":"When something lasts for more than expected, it may surprise people.","zh":"當某事持續超過預期時間，可能令人驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving a minimum length of time.","zh":"這個短語適合用於提供最少時間長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"there was a report that","meaning":"曾有報道指","examples":[{"en":"There was a report that a 120-year-old tun was revived.","zh":"曾有報道指，一個 120 年的 tun 被復活。"},{"en":"There was a report that means someone reported or claimed that something happened.","zh":"曾有報道指某事，意思是有人報道或聲稱某事發生。"},{"en":"There was a report that a rare bird had been seen near the harbour.","zh":"曾有報道指，一種稀有鳥類在海港附近被看見。"},{"en":"This phrase presents information carefully without saying it is definitely proven.","zh":"這個短語謹慎呈現資訊，而不是說它一定已被證實。"},{"en":"It is useful when a claim has been mentioned but not fully confirmed.","zh":"當一個說法被提及但未完全確認時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"120-year-old","meaning":"120年的","examples":[{"en":"A 120-year-old tun was reportedly revived in 1948.","zh":"據報一個 120 年的 tun 在 1948 年被復活。"},{"en":"120-year-old means having existed for 120 years.","zh":"120 年的意思是已經存在 120 年。"},{"en":"A 120-year-old building may need careful repairs to preserve its structure.","zh":"一座 120 年的建築可能需要仔細維修以保存結構。"},{"en":"Something that is 120 years old can carry historical or scientific interest.","zh":"120 年的東西可能具有歷史或科學價值。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the age of a person, object or state.","zh":"這個短語提供人、物件或狀態的年齡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"experiment","meaning":"實驗","examples":[{"en":"This experiment has never been repeated.","zh":"這個實驗從未被重複驗證。"},{"en":"An experiment is a planned test used to discover or check something.","zh":"實驗是用來發現或檢查某事的有計劃測試。"},{"en":"Students may do an experiment to test how light affects plant growth.","zh":"學生可能做實驗測試光線如何影響植物生長。"},{"en":"Experiments are stronger when other researchers can repeat them and get similar results.","zh":"當其他研究人員能重複實驗並得到相似結果，實驗會更有力。"},{"en":"This word is central to scientific investigation.","zh":"這個詞是科學調查的核心用語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have never been repeated","meaning":"從未被重複驗證","examples":[{"en":"The experiment has never been repeated.","zh":"這個實驗從未被重複驗證。"},{"en":"Have never been repeated means no one has successfully done the same test again.","zh":"從未被重複驗證意思是沒有人成功再次進行同樣測試。"},{"en":"A claim is weaker if the experiment behind it has never been repeated.","zh":"如果支持某說法的實驗從未被重複驗證，該說法會較弱。"},{"en":"Repeated experiments help scientists check whether a result is reliable.","zh":"重複實驗幫助科學家檢查結果是否可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests caution about accepting a result too quickly.","zh":"這個短語暗示接受結果時應保持謹慎。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"currently","meaning":"目前","examples":[{"en":"There are currently several tests taking place in space.","zh":"目前有幾項測試正在太空中進行。"},{"en":"Currently means at the present time.","zh":"目前意思是在現在這個時間。"},{"en":"The school is currently repairing the library roof.","zh":"學校目前正在維修圖書館屋頂。"},{"en":"Using currently makes clear that the situation may change later.","zh":"使用 currently 可清楚表示情況之後可能會改變。"},{"en":"This word is useful for describing what is happening now.","zh":"這個詞適合描述現在正在發生的事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"tests taking place","meaning":"正在進行的測試","examples":[{"en":"There are several tests taking place in space.","zh":"有幾項測試正在太空中進行。"},{"en":"Tests taking place are experiments or checks that are happening now.","zh":"正在進行的測試是現在正在發生的實驗或檢查。"},{"en":"There are safety tests taking place before the new bridge opens.","zh":"新橋啟用前，正有安全測試正在進行。"},{"en":"Tests taking place in a controlled setting can help researchers collect clear data.","zh":"在受控制環境中進行的測試，可以幫助研究人員收集清楚數據。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on tests currently in progress.","zh":"這個短語重點是目前正在進行的測試。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in space","meaning":"在太空中","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are testing how long tardigrades can survive in space.","zh":"科學家正在測試緩步動物能在太空中存活多久。"},{"en":"In space means outside Earth’s atmosphere, where conditions are very different from on Earth.","zh":"在太空中意思是在地球大氣層之外，那裏的環境與地球上非常不同。"},{"en":"Astronauts need special equipment to breathe and move safely in space.","zh":"太空人在太空中需要特殊設備才能呼吸和安全移動。"},{"en":"Experiments in space help scientists learn how living things react to extreme conditions.","zh":"太空中的實驗幫助科學家了解生物如何應對極端環境。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the environment beyond Earth.","zh":"這個短語指地球以外的環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"determine how long","meaning":"確定……多久","examples":[{"en":"The tests aim to determine how long tardigrades can survive in space.","zh":"這些測試旨在確定緩步動物能在太空中存活多久。"},{"en":"To determine how long something lasts means to find out its duration.","zh":"確定某事持續多久意思是找出其持續時間。"},{"en":"Doctors may run tests to determine how long a medicine stays active in the body.","zh":"醫生可能進行測試，以確定藥物在體內有效多久。"},{"en":"Measuring duration helps researchers understand limits and survival ability.","zh":"量度持續時間幫助研究人員了解限制和生存能力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when investigating time.","zh":"當研究時間長短時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"might be able to survive","meaning":"可能能夠存活","examples":[{"en":"The tests examine how long tardigrades might be able to survive in space.","zh":"這些測試研究緩步動物可能能夠在太空中存活多久。"},{"en":"Might be able to survive means may have the ability to stay alive.","zh":"可能能夠存活意思是也許有能力保持生命。"},{"en":"A plant might be able to survive a short drought if its roots are deep enough.","zh":"如果植物根部夠深，可能能夠在短暫乾旱中存活。"},{"en":"This phrase shows possibility, not certainty.","zh":"這個短語顯示可能性，而不是確定。"},{"en":"It is useful when scientists are still testing a claim.","zh":"當科學家仍在測試某說法時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"record so far","meaning":"目前的紀錄","examples":[{"en":"The record so far is 10 days.","zh":"目前的紀錄是 10 天。"},{"en":"The record so far means the best or highest result achieved up to the present time.","zh":"目前的紀錄意思是截至現在達到的最佳或最高結果。"},{"en":"The record so far for the class reading challenge is fifty books.","zh":"班級閱讀挑戰目前的紀錄是五十本書。"},{"en":"A record can change when someone achieves a better result later.","zh":"當之後有人取得更好結果，紀錄可以改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting current progress.","zh":"當報告目前進展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"moving on","meaning":"繼續說；轉到下一點","examples":[{"en":"Moving on, the speaker discusses the diet of tardigrades.","zh":"繼續說，講者討論緩步動物的飲食。"},{"en":"Moving on is used when a speaker shifts to the next topic.","zh":"Moving on 用於說話者轉到下一個主題時。"},{"en":"Moving on, let us look at the results of the survey.","zh":"轉到下一點，讓我們看看調查結果。"},{"en":"This phrase helps listeners follow the structure of a presentation.","zh":"這個短語幫助聽眾跟上匯報結構。"},{"en":"It is common in talks, lessons and reports.","zh":"它常見於演講、課堂和報告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in terms of","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"In terms of their diet, tardigrades consume liquids.","zh":"就牠們的飲食而言，緩步動物攝取液體。"},{"en":"In terms of something means considering that particular aspect.","zh":"就某方面而言意思是考慮該特定方面。"},{"en":"In terms of cost, taking the bus is usually cheaper than taking a taxi.","zh":"就成本而言，乘巴士通常比乘的士便宜。"},{"en":"This phrase helps narrow a discussion to one area.","zh":"這個短語有助把討論收窄到一個範疇。"},{"en":"It is useful when organising information by category.","zh":"當按類別組織資料時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"diet","meaning":"飲食","examples":[{"en":"The speaker explains the diet of tardigrades.","zh":"講者解釋緩步動物的飲食。"},{"en":"Diet means the food or drink that a person or animal usually consumes.","zh":"飲食意思是人或動物通常攝取的食物或飲品。"},{"en":"A panda’s diet mainly includes bamboo.","zh":"熊貓的飲食主要包括竹。"},{"en":"Understanding an animal’s diet helps scientists know where it can live.","zh":"了解動物的飲食幫助科學家知道牠可以在哪裏生活。"},{"en":"This word is used in biology, health and daily life.","zh":"這個詞用於生物學、健康和日常生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"consume liquids","meaning":"攝取液體","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades consume liquids in order to survive.","zh":"緩步動物攝取液體以維持生存。"},{"en":"To consume liquids means to take in liquid food or drink.","zh":"攝取液體意思是吸收液態食物或飲品。"},{"en":"Athletes consume liquids during exercise to avoid dehydration.","zh":"運動員在運動期間攝取液體，以避免脫水。"},{"en":"Animals that consume liquids may use special mouthparts to suck or draw in fluid.","zh":"攝取液體的動物可能使用特殊口部構造來吸取流體。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on taking in liquid rather than solid food.","zh":"這個短語重點是吸收液體，而不是固體食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in order to survive","meaning":"為了生存","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades consume liquids in order to survive.","zh":"緩步動物攝取液體是為了生存。"},{"en":"In order to survive means for the purpose of staying alive.","zh":"為了生存意思是以保持生命為目的。"},{"en":"Plants need sunlight and water in order to survive.","zh":"植物需要陽光和水是為了生存。"},{"en":"Animals change behaviour in order to survive when their environment becomes harsh.","zh":"當環境變得惡劣，動物會改變行為為了生存。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly explains purpose.","zh":"這個短語清楚解釋目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"use something for","meaning":"用……來","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades do not use their teeth for chewing.","zh":"緩步動物不會用牠們的牙齒來咀嚼。"},{"en":"To use something for a purpose means to employ it to do that action.","zh":"用某物來做某事意思是使用它完成該行動。"},{"en":"Students use notebooks for recording vocabulary and homework.","zh":"學生用筆記簿來記錄詞彙和功課。"},{"en":"A tool may be shaped differently depending on what people use it for.","zh":"工具的形狀可能因人們用它來做甚麼而不同。"},{"en":"This phrase links an object with its function.","zh":"這個短語把物件與其功能連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"chewing","meaning":"咀嚼","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades do not use their teeth for chewing.","zh":"緩步動物不會用牠們的牙齒來咀嚼。"},{"en":"Chewing is the action of breaking food into smaller pieces with the teeth.","zh":"咀嚼是用牙齒把食物咬成較小部分的動作。"},{"en":"People should chew food carefully before swallowing.","zh":"人們吞嚥前應仔細咀嚼食物。"},{"en":"Animals that do not chew may feed by sucking liquid or swallowing food whole.","zh":"不咀嚼的動物可能透過吸取液體或整個吞下食物來進食。"},{"en":"This word describes one way of eating solid food.","zh":"這個詞描述進食固體食物的一種方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"suck the juices from","meaning":"從……吸取汁液","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades suck the juices from moss.","zh":"緩步動物從苔蘚吸取汁液。"},{"en":"To suck the juices from something means to draw liquid out of it.","zh":"從某物吸取汁液意思是從它裏面抽取液體。"},{"en":"Some insects suck the juices from plant stems or leaves.","zh":"有些昆蟲從植物莖或葉吸取汁液。"},{"en":"Animals that suck juices need mouthparts that can pierce or draw in liquid.","zh":"吸取汁液的動物需要能刺穿或吸入液體的口部構造。"},{"en":"This phrase describes feeding on liquid inside another organism.","zh":"這個短語描述攝取另一生物內部液體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"moss","meaning":"苔蘚","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades suck the juices from moss.","zh":"緩步動物從苔蘚吸取汁液。"},{"en":"Moss is a small green plant-like organism that often grows in damp places.","zh":"苔蘚是一種細小綠色植物狀生物，常生長在潮濕地方。"},{"en":"Moss can grow on rocks, tree trunks and old walls after rain.","zh":"下雨後，苔蘚可以長在岩石、樹幹和舊牆上。"},{"en":"Damp moss can provide a habitat for tiny animals.","zh":"潮濕苔蘚可以為微小動物提供棲息地。"},{"en":"This word often appears when describing wet natural environments.","zh":"這個詞常出現在潮濕自然環境的描述中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"extract fluid from","meaning":"從……提取液體","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades extract fluid from seaweed.","zh":"緩步動物從海藻提取液體。"},{"en":"To extract fluid from something means to remove or draw liquid out of it.","zh":"從某物提取液體意思是從它裏面取出或抽出液體。"},{"en":"A juicer extracts fluid from fruit to make juice.","zh":"榨汁機從水果提取液體來製作果汁。"},{"en":"Extracting fluid allows an organism to feed without eating solid material.","zh":"提取液體讓生物不用吃固體材料也能進食。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking liquid from a source.","zh":"這個短語描述從來源取出液體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"seaweed","meaning":"海藻","examples":[{"en":"Some tardigrades extract fluid from seaweed.","zh":"有些緩步動物從海藻提取液體。"},{"en":"Seaweed is a plant-like organism that grows in the sea.","zh":"海藻是在海中生長的植物狀生物。"},{"en":"Seaweed can be used in soup, sushi and some snacks.","zh":"海藻可以用於湯、壽司和一些小食。"},{"en":"Small marine organisms may live around seaweed because it offers food and shelter.","zh":"小型海洋生物可能生活在海藻周圍，因為它提供食物和庇護。"},{"en":"This word is common in ocean and coastal biology.","zh":"這個詞常見於海洋和海岸生物學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prey on","meaning":"捕食……","examples":[{"en":"Some tardigrades prey on other tardigrades.","zh":"有些緩步動物捕食其他緩步動物。"},{"en":"To prey on something means to hunt and eat it.","zh":"捕食某物意思是獵捕並吃掉它。"},{"en":"Owls prey on mice at night.","zh":"貓頭鷹在夜間捕食老鼠。"},{"en":"Predators prey on other animals in order to get energy and survive.","zh":"捕食者捕食其他動物以獲得能量並生存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a feeding relationship.","zh":"這個短語描述一種進食關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"within their own species","meaning":"在同一物種內","examples":[{"en":"Some tardigrades prey on other tardigrades within their own species.","zh":"有些緩步動物在同一物種內捕食其他緩步動物。"},{"en":"Within their own species means among members of the same biological species.","zh":"在同一物種內意思是在同一生物物種的成員之間。"},{"en":"Competition within a species can happen when food or space is limited.","zh":"當食物或空間有限時，同一物種內可能出現競爭。"},{"en":"Behaviour within the same species can include cooperation, competition or conflict.","zh":"同一物種內的行為可以包括合作、競爭或衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on interactions among the same kind of organism.","zh":"這個短語重點是同類生物之間的互動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"I suppose this isn’t surprising","meaning":"我想這並不奇怪","examples":[{"en":"I suppose this isn’t surprising, given that tardigrades are mainly composed of liquid.","zh":"我想這並不奇怪，鑑於緩步動物主要由液體組成。"},{"en":"I suppose this isn’t surprising means the speaker thinks the fact is understandable after considering the reason.","zh":"我想這並不奇怪，意思是說話者考慮原因後認為該事可以理解。"},{"en":"I suppose this isn’t surprising, given that the shop lowered its prices and attracted more customers.","zh":"我想這並不奇怪，因為商店降價並吸引了更多顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase helps a speaker connect a result with a reasonable explanation.","zh":"這個短語幫助說話者把結果與合理解釋連繫起來。"},{"en":"It sounds conversational and reflective.","zh":"它聽起來口語而帶反思意味。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"given that","meaning":"鑑於；考慮到","examples":[{"en":"This is not surprising, given that tardigrades are mainly composed of liquid.","zh":"鑑於緩步動物主要由液體組成，這並不奇怪。"},{"en":"Given that means considering the fact that.","zh":"鑑於某事意思是考慮到該事實。"},{"en":"Given that the weather is bad, the school may cancel the outdoor activity.","zh":"鑑於天氣惡劣，學校可能取消戶外活動。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a reason that helps explain the main statement.","zh":"這個短語引入幫助解釋主要說法的理由。"},{"en":"It is common in formal and spoken explanation.","zh":"它常見於正式和口頭解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be composed of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades are mainly composed of liquid.","zh":"緩步動物主要由液體組成。"},{"en":"To be composed of something means to be made up of that material or those parts.","zh":"由某物組成意思是由該材料或那些部分構成。"},{"en":"A committee may be composed of teachers, parents and students.","zh":"委員會可能由老師、家長和學生組成。"},{"en":"Knowing what something is composed of helps explain how it works.","zh":"知道某物由甚麼組成，有助解釋它如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and useful in scientific writing.","zh":"這個短語較正式，適合科學寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be coated with","meaning":"覆蓋着……","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades are coated with a type of gel.","zh":"緩步動物覆蓋着一種凝膠。"},{"en":"To be coated with something means to be covered by a layer of it.","zh":"覆蓋着某物意思是被一層該物質包住。"},{"en":"A cake may be coated with chocolate before it is served.","zh":"蛋糕上桌前可能覆蓋着朱古力。"},{"en":"A coating can protect a surface or change how it feels.","zh":"覆蓋層可以保護表面或改變觸感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an outer covering.","zh":"這個短語描述外層覆蓋物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a type of gel","meaning":"一種凝膠","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades are coated with a type of gel.","zh":"緩步動物覆蓋着一種凝膠。"},{"en":"A type of gel is a soft, jelly-like substance.","zh":"一種凝膠是柔軟、像啫喱的物質。"},{"en":"Hair gel is a type of gel used to hold hair in place.","zh":"髮膠是一種用來固定頭髮的凝膠。"},{"en":"Gel-like coatings may help protect small organisms from drying out.","zh":"凝膠狀覆蓋物可能幫助小生物防止乾枯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a soft semi-solid material.","zh":"這個短語描述柔軟的半固體材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"I’d like to mention","meaning":"我想提及","examples":[{"en":"Finally, I’d like to mention the conservation status of tardigrades.","zh":"最後，我想提及緩步動物的保育狀況。"},{"en":"I’d like to mention is a polite way to introduce an additional point.","zh":"我想提及是有禮貌地引入補充重點的說法。"},{"en":"I’d like to mention that the library will be closed next Monday.","zh":"我想提及，圖書館下星期一會關閉。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase when adding information near the end of a talk.","zh":"說話者在演講接近尾聲時加入資料，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It sounds organised and courteous.","zh":"它聽起來有條理而有禮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"conservation status","meaning":"保育狀況","examples":[{"en":"The speaker mentions the conservation status of tardigrades.","zh":"講者提及緩步動物的保育狀況。"},{"en":"Conservation status describes how likely a species is to survive or become endangered.","zh":"保育狀況描述一個物種存活或變成瀕危的可能性。"},{"en":"The conservation status of an animal may change if its habitat is destroyed.","zh":"如果動物的棲息地被破壞，其保育狀況可能改變。"},{"en":"Knowing conservation status helps governments decide which species need protection.","zh":"了解保育狀況幫助政府決定哪些物種需要保護。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in environmental science.","zh":"這個短語常見於環境科學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"it is estimated that","meaning":"據估計","examples":[{"en":"It is estimated that tardigrades have existed for about half a billion years.","zh":"據估計，緩步動物已存在約五億年。"},{"en":"It is estimated that means experts believe a number or fact is approximately true based on evidence.","zh":"據估計某事意思是專家根據證據相信某數字或事實大約正確。"},{"en":"It is estimated that the repair work will take three weeks.","zh":"據估計，維修工程將需三星期。"},{"en":"Estimates are useful when exact numbers are difficult to know.","zh":"當準確數字難以知道時，估計很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is careful because it signals approximation.","zh":"這個短語較謹慎，因為它表示近似值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have been in existence","meaning":"已經存在","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades have been in existence for approximately half a billion years.","zh":"緩步動物已經存在大約五億年。"},{"en":"To have been in existence means to have existed over a period of time.","zh":"已經存在意思是在一段時間內一直存在。"},{"en":"The school has been in existence for more than one hundred years.","zh":"這所學校已經存在超過一百年。"},{"en":"Something that has been in existence for a long time may have survived many changes.","zh":"已經存在很長時間的事物，可能經歷了許多變化仍存續。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and focuses on duration.","zh":"這個短語較正式，重點是持續時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"approximately","meaning":"大約","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades have existed for approximately half a billion years.","zh":"緩步動物已存在大約五億年。"},{"en":"Approximately means about, or close to a number but not exact.","zh":"大約意思是接近某數字，但不是完全精確。"},{"en":"The journey takes approximately forty minutes by bus.","zh":"乘巴士車程大約四十分鐘。"},{"en":"Scientists use approximately when a figure is estimated rather than exact.","zh":"當數字是估計而非精確時，科學家會使用 approximately。"},{"en":"This word is useful for careful measurement and reporting.","zh":"這個詞適合用於謹慎量度和報告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"half a billion years","meaning":"五億年","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades have existed for approximately half a billion years.","zh":"緩步動物已存在大約五億年。"},{"en":"Half a billion years means five hundred million years.","zh":"五億年意思是五百萬乘以一百，即五百 million 年。"},{"en":"Half a billion years is far longer than the history of human civilisation.","zh":"五億年遠比人類文明史長得多。"},{"en":"A species that survives for half a billion years has endured huge environmental changes.","zh":"能存活五億年的物種經歷了巨大的環境變化。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses an extremely long period of time.","zh":"這個短語表達極其漫長的時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in that time","meaning":"在那段期間","examples":[{"en":"In that time, tardigrades have survived five mass extinctions.","zh":"在那段期間，緩步動物經歷了五次大滅絕仍存活。"},{"en":"In that time means during the period just mentioned.","zh":"在那段期間意思是在剛才提及的時間段內。"},{"en":"The shop has been open for ten years; in that time, it has served thousands of customers.","zh":"這間店開業十年；在那段期間，它服務了數以千計顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase links achievements or events to a previously stated time span.","zh":"這個短語把成就或事件連接到之前提到的時間跨度。"},{"en":"It helps avoid repeating the same time phrase.","zh":"它有助避免重複同一時間短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"mass extinctions","meaning":"大滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades have survived five mass extinctions.","zh":"緩步動物經歷了五次大滅絕仍存活。"},{"en":"Mass extinctions are events in which many species disappear from Earth in a relatively short geological period.","zh":"大滅絕是許多物種在相對短的地質時期內從地球上消失的事件。"},{"en":"Dinosaurs are often discussed when students learn about mass extinctions.","zh":"學生學習大滅絕時，常會討論恐龍。"},{"en":"Mass extinctions can be caused by major environmental changes, impacts or climate shifts.","zh":"大滅絕可能由重大環境變化、撞擊或氣候轉變造成。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to geology and evolutionary biology.","zh":"這個短語屬於地質學和演化生物學。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"come as no surprise","meaning":"並不令人驚訝","examples":[{"en":"It will probably come as no surprise that tardigrades are not on any endangered list.","zh":"緩步動物不在任何瀕危名單上，這大概並不令人驚訝。"},{"en":"To come as no surprise means to be expected or not shocking.","zh":"並不令人驚訝意思是符合預期或不令人震驚。"},{"en":"It came as no surprise that the student did well because she had practised for weeks.","zh":"那位學生表現好並不令人驚訝，因為她已練習數星期。"},{"en":"When evidence already points in one direction, the result may come as no surprise.","zh":"當證據已指向一個方向，結果可能並不令人驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase is used before giving an expected conclusion.","zh":"這個短語用於給出預期中的結論之前。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be evaluated by","meaning":"由……評估","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades have not been evaluated by the International Union for Conservation of Nature.","zh":"緩步動物尚未由國際自然保護聯盟評估。"},{"en":"To be evaluated by someone means to be assessed or judged by that person or organisation.","zh":"由某人評估意思是由該人或組織作出評估或判斷。"},{"en":"A school project may be evaluated by teachers using a marking rubric.","zh":"學校專題可能由老師使用評分準則評估。"},{"en":"Evaluation helps decide quality, risk or status.","zh":"評估有助判斷質素、風險或狀況。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in formal assessment.","zh":"這個短語常用於正式評審。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"International Union for Conservation of Nature","meaning":"國際自然保護聯盟","examples":[{"en":"The International Union for Conservation of Nature has not evaluated tardigrades.","zh":"國際自然保護聯盟尚未評估緩步動物。"},{"en":"The International Union for Conservation of Nature is an organisation connected with assessing conservation and species status.","zh":"國際自然保護聯盟是一個與評估保育和物種狀況有關的組織。"},{"en":"Students may see the organisation’s name when researching endangered animals.","zh":"學生研究瀕危動物時，可能會看到這個組織的名稱。"},{"en":"Conservation organisations help people understand which species may need protection.","zh":"保育組織幫助人們了解哪些物種可能需要保護。"},{"en":"This phrase is the formal name of an international conservation body.","zh":"這個短語是一個國際保育機構的正式名稱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"endangered list","meaning":"瀕危名單","examples":[{"en":"Tardigrades are not on any endangered list.","zh":"緩步動物不在任何瀕危名單上。"},{"en":"An endangered list is a list of species considered at risk of disappearing.","zh":"瀕危名單是列出被認為有消失風險的物種的清單。"},{"en":"A rare bird may be added to an endangered list if its population falls sharply.","zh":"如果某稀有鳥類數量急跌，牠可能被加入瀕危名單。"},{"en":"Species on endangered lists may receive more protection and public attention.","zh":"瀕危名單上的物種可能獲得更多保護和公眾關注。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in conservation discussions.","zh":"這個短語用於保育討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"describe something as","meaning":"把……形容為","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers have described tardigrades as thriving.","zh":"有些研究人員把緩步動物形容為繁盛生存。"},{"en":"To describe something as something means to say it has that quality or condition.","zh":"把某物形容為某種狀態，意思是說它具有該特質或情況。"},{"en":"A teacher may describe a student’s essay as clear and well organised.","zh":"老師可能把學生文章形容為清楚而有組織。"},{"en":"Descriptions can shape how readers understand a subject.","zh":"描述會塑造讀者如何理解某主題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting opinions or assessments.","zh":"當報告意見或評估時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"thriving","meaning":"繁盛生存","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers have described tardigrades as thriving.","zh":"有些研究人員把緩步動物形容為繁盛生存。"},{"en":"Thriving means growing, surviving or doing very well.","zh":"繁盛生存意思是生長、存活或發展得很好。"},{"en":"A school garden is thriving if the plants are healthy and new flowers keep appearing.","zh":"如果學校花園植物健康並不斷開出新花，就是繁盛生長。"},{"en":"A species may be described as thriving when it is not declining and can survive well.","zh":"當一個物種沒有衰退並能良好存活，它可能被形容為繁盛。"},{"en":"This word has a positive meaning of strong life or success.","zh":"這個詞有強大生命力或成功的正面意思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Does anyone have any questions they’d like to ask?","meaning":"有沒有人有問題想問？","examples":[{"en":"The speaker asks, “Does anyone have any questions they’d like to ask?”","zh":"講者問：「有沒有人有問題想問？」"},{"en":"“Does anyone have any questions they’d like to ask?” is a polite way to invite listeners to ask questions.","zh":"「有沒有人有問題想問？」是一種有禮貌地邀請聽眾提問的方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may say this after explaining a difficult grammar point.","zh":"老師解釋完困難文法點後，可能會這樣說。"},{"en":"Asking this question gives the audience a chance to clarify anything they did not understand.","zh":"問這個問題讓聽眾有機會澄清任何不明白的內容。"},{"en":"This sentence is common at the end of presentations, lessons and meetings.","zh":"這句話常見於匯報、課堂和會議結尾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 6 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"ielts/listening/Practice 7/task-1":[{"front":"settle into","meaning":"適應……；習慣……","examples":[{"en":"Shannon is settling into her new flat really well.","zh":"Shannon 很好地適應了她的新單位。"},{"en":"To settle into a place means to become comfortable and used to living or staying there.","zh":"settle into a place 指開始感到舒服，並習慣在某地方生活或逗留。"},{"en":"A new student may need a few weeks to settle into a different school.","zh":"新學生可能需要幾星期才能適應一間不同的學校。"},{"en":"People settle into a new home faster when they know the shops, transport, and neighbours nearby.","zh":"當人們熟悉附近商店、交通和鄰居，會更快適應新家。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests adjustment over time, not feeling comfortable immediately.","zh":"這個片語暗示需要時間適應，而不是立即感到自在。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"new flat","meaning":"新單位","examples":[{"en":"Shannon has recently moved into a new flat.","zh":"Shannon 最近搬進了一個新單位。"},{"en":"A new flat is a new apartment or living unit where someone has just started living.","zh":"new flat 指某人剛開始居住的新公寓或住宅單位。"},{"en":"A family may buy a new flat when they need more space for children.","zh":"家庭需要更多空間給孩子時，可能會買新單位。"},{"en":"Moving into a new flat can be exciting, but it also means arranging furniture, bills, and daily routines.","zh":"搬進新單位可以令人興奮，但也意味要安排家具、帳單和日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English; American English often uses “new apartment”.","zh":"這個片語常見於英式英語；美式英語常用 “new apartment”。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look like you’re going","meaning":"看起來像是要……","examples":[{"en":"Shannon looks like she is going shopping.","zh":"Shannon 看起來像是要去買東西。"},{"en":"Look like you’re going means someone appears to be about to go somewhere or do something.","zh":"look like you’re going 指某人看起來快要去某地或做某事。"},{"en":"You look like you’re going to the gym because you are carrying trainers and a towel.","zh":"你帶着運動鞋和毛巾，看起來像是要去健身室。"},{"en":"People guess what you are going to do by looking at your clothes, bags, or direction.","zh":"人們會透過你的衣着、袋子或方向猜測你接下來要做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when appearance gives clues about someone’s next action.","zh":"這個片語用於外表給出某人下一步行動線索時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"go shopping","meaning":"去買東西","examples":[{"en":"Shannon is going shopping because her cousins are coming to stay.","zh":"Shannon 要去買東西，因為她的表親要來暫住。"},{"en":"To go shopping means to go out to buy things such as food, clothes, or household items.","zh":"go shopping 指外出去購買食物、衣服或家居用品等東西。"},{"en":"Parents may go shopping on Saturday morning to buy food for the week.","zh":"父母可能在星期六早上去買東西，為一星期買食物。"},{"en":"If guests are coming, people often go shopping so they have enough food and drinks at home.","zh":"如果有客人來，人們常會去買東西，確保家中有足夠食物和飲品。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the activity of buying things, not simply walking around shops.","zh":"這個片語着重購買東西的活動，而不只是逛商店。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"come to stay","meaning":"來暫住","examples":[{"en":"Shannon’s cousins are coming to stay for a couple of days.","zh":"Shannon 的表親要來暫住幾天。"},{"en":"To come to stay means to visit someone and sleep at their home for a period of time.","zh":"come to stay 指到訪某人並在其家中住一段時間。"},{"en":"My aunt is coming to stay during the school holiday.","zh":"我姨姨會在學校假期來暫住。"},{"en":"When guests come to stay, the host may need to prepare bedding, food, and extra towels.","zh":"當客人來暫住，主人可能需要準備床鋪、食物和額外毛巾。"},{"en":"This phrase means a visit with overnight accommodation, not just a short afternoon visit.","zh":"這個片語指會過夜的探訪，而不只是短暫下午到訪。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for a couple of days","meaning":"幾天","examples":[{"en":"Her cousins are coming to stay for a couple of days.","zh":"她的表親要來暫住幾天。"},{"en":"For a couple of days means for two or a few days.","zh":"for a couple of days 指兩天或幾天。"},{"en":"A student may borrow a classmate’s notes for a couple of days before returning them.","zh":"學生可能向同學借筆記幾天，然後歸還。"},{"en":"If guests stay for a couple of days, the host needs enough food but not a whole week’s supply.","zh":"如果客人住幾天，主人需要足夠食物，但不需要準備一星期份量。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate short length of time.","zh":"這個片語表示大約較短的一段時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cook for","meaning":"為……煮飯","examples":[{"en":"Shannon has to cook for her cousins.","zh":"Shannon 要為她的表親煮飯。"},{"en":"To cook for someone means to prepare food for that person to eat.","zh":"cook for someone 指準備食物給某人吃。"},{"en":"A father may cook for the family when everyone comes home late.","zh":"當大家都很晚回家，父親可能為全家煮飯。"},{"en":"Cooking for guests requires planning because people may have different tastes or diets.","zh":"為客人煮飯需要規劃，因為人們可能有不同口味或飲食習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on preparing a meal for other people, not only cooking for yourself.","zh":"這個片語着重為他人準備餐點，而不只是為自己煮食。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"plenty of places to","meaning":"有很多地方可以……","examples":[{"en":"There are plenty of places to buy food in Kite Place.","zh":"Kite Place 有很多地方可以買食物。"},{"en":"Plenty of places to do something means many locations are available for that activity.","zh":"plenty of places to do something 指有許多地點可做某事。"},{"en":"There are plenty of places to study in the new library.","zh":"新圖書館有很多地方可以溫習。"},{"en":"If an area has plenty of places to eat, visitors can choose according to price and taste.","zh":"如果一個區有很多地方可以吃飯，訪客可以按價錢和口味選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that there is no shortage of options.","zh":"這個片語暗示選擇不缺乏。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"buy food","meaning":"買食物","examples":[{"en":"Kite Place has plenty of places to buy food.","zh":"Kite Place 有很多地方可以買食物。"},{"en":"To buy food means to purchase ingredients, snacks, or meals from shops, markets, or restaurants.","zh":"buy food 指從商店、市場或餐廳購買食材、小食或餐點。"},{"en":"Students may buy food near school when they forget to bring lunch.","zh":"學生忘記帶午餐時，可能在學校附近買食物。"},{"en":"People buy food before guests arrive so they can prepare meals without rushing.","zh":"人們在客人到達前買食物，這樣煮飯時就不用趕急。"},{"en":"This phrase includes buying raw ingredients as well as ready-to-eat items.","zh":"這個片語包括購買生食材和即食食品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the area by the harbour","meaning":"海港旁邊的區域","examples":[{"en":"Kite Place is the area by the harbour.","zh":"Kite Place 是海港旁邊的區域。"},{"en":"The area by the harbour means the part of town located beside the water where boats may be found.","zh":"the area by the harbour 指位於水邊、可能有船隻的城鎮部分。"},{"en":"Restaurants in the area by the harbour often sell fresh seafood.","zh":"海港旁邊區域的餐廳常售賣新鮮海鮮。"},{"en":"An area by the harbour may be busy because tourists, markets, and transport all meet there.","zh":"海港旁邊的區域可能很繁忙，因為旅客、市場和交通都聚集在那裡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location by the waterfront.","zh":"這個片語描述海濱位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"find something on the map","meaning":"在地圖上找到某處","examples":[{"en":"Shannon will find Kite Place on the map.","zh":"Shannon 會在地圖上找到 Kite Place。"},{"en":"To find something on the map means to locate a place by looking at a map.","zh":"find something on the map 指查看地圖並找出某地方的位置。"},{"en":"A tourist may find the nearest bus stop on the map before leaving the hotel.","zh":"旅客離開酒店前，可能在地圖上找到最近的巴士站。"},{"en":"Finding a place on the map helps people plan the route and avoid getting lost.","zh":"在地圖上找到地方有助人們規劃路線和避免迷路。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on identifying a location visually.","zh":"這個片語着重以視覺方式識別位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what sort of","meaning":"哪一類；甚麼種類","examples":[{"en":"Leon asks Shannon what sort of food she needs to get.","zh":"Leon 問 Shannon 需要買哪一類食物。"},{"en":"What sort of means what kind or type of something.","zh":"what sort of 指哪一類或甚麼種類。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask what sort of help a student needs before giving advice.","zh":"老師給建議前，可能問學生需要哪一類幫助。"},{"en":"Asking what sort of food someone wants helps avoid buying the wrong ingredients.","zh":"問別人想要哪一類食物，有助避免買錯食材。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when narrowing down a broad category.","zh":"這個片語適合用來收窄一個廣泛類別。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"need to get","meaning":"需要買；需要取得","examples":[{"en":"Shannon needs to get food for her cousins.","zh":"Shannon 需要為她的表親買食物。"},{"en":"To need to get something means to have to buy, collect, or obtain it.","zh":"need to get something 指需要購買、領取或取得某物。"},{"en":"A student may need to get a new notebook before the term starts.","zh":"學生可能在學期開始前需要買新筆記簿。"},{"en":"If guests are coming, you may need to get extra towels and snacks.","zh":"如果客人要來，你可能需要準備額外毛巾和小食。"},{"en":"This phrase is practical and often used when preparing for a task or event.","zh":"這個片語很實用，常用於為任務或活動作準備時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"neither of them","meaning":"他們兩個都不","examples":[{"en":"Neither of Shannon’s cousins eats meat.","zh":"Shannon 的兩位表親都不吃肉。"},{"en":"Neither of them means not one of the two people or things.","zh":"neither of them 指兩個人或兩件事中沒有任何一個。"},{"en":"Neither of the two students brought a calculator to the maths lesson.","zh":"兩名學生都沒有帶計數機上數學課。"},{"en":"If neither of the guests eats meat, the host should prepare fish, vegetables, or beans instead.","zh":"如果兩位客人都不吃肉，主人應準備魚、蔬菜或豆類。"},{"en":"This phrase is used only when talking about two people or two things.","zh":"這個片語只用於談及兩個人或兩件事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"eat meat","meaning":"吃肉","examples":[{"en":"Neither of Shannon’s cousins eats meat.","zh":"Shannon 的兩位表親都不吃肉。"},{"en":"To eat meat means to include meat such as beef, pork, chicken, or lamb in one’s diet.","zh":"eat meat 指飲食中包括牛肉、豬肉、雞肉或羊肉等肉類。"},{"en":"Some people do not eat meat for health, religious, or environmental reasons.","zh":"有些人因健康、宗教或環保原因不吃肉。"},{"en":"If someone does not eat meat, the cook should check whether fish, eggs, or dairy are acceptable.","zh":"如果某人不吃肉，廚師應確認魚、雞蛋或奶製品是否可接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dietary habit or choice.","zh":"這個片語描述飲食習慣或選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"both like","meaning":"兩者都喜歡","examples":[{"en":"Shannon’s cousins both like fish.","zh":"Shannon 的兩位表親都喜歡魚。"},{"en":"Both like means the two people share the same preference for something.","zh":"both like 指兩個人對某事有相同喜好。"},{"en":"My parents both like walking after dinner.","zh":"我的父母兩人都喜歡晚飯後散步。"},{"en":"If two guests both like fish, fish can be a safe main dish to prepare.","zh":"如果兩位客人都喜歡魚，魚可以是安全的主菜選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the preference is true for two people.","zh":"這個片語強調該喜好同時適用於兩個人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fish market","meaning":"魚市場","examples":[{"en":"There is a really good fish market in Kite Place.","zh":"Kite Place 有一個非常好的魚市場。"},{"en":"A fish market is a place where people buy fresh fish and seafood.","zh":"fish market 指人們購買新鮮魚類和海鮮的地方。"},{"en":"Chefs may visit the fish market early in the morning to choose the freshest catch.","zh":"廚師可能清晨到魚市場挑選最新鮮的漁獲。"},{"en":"Fish markets are often busy because seafood sells best when it is fresh.","zh":"魚市場通常很繁忙，因為海鮮越新鮮越好賣。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a market specialising in fish, not an ordinary supermarket shelf.","zh":"這個片語指專門售賣魚類的市場，而不是普通超市貨架。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"where exactly","meaning":"確切在哪裏","examples":[{"en":"Shannon asks Leon where the fish market is exactly.","zh":"Shannon 問 Leon 魚市場確切在哪裏。"},{"en":"Where exactly means the precise location, not just the general area.","zh":"where exactly 指準確位置，而不只是大概區域。"},{"en":"A visitor may ask where exactly the classroom is if the school has several buildings.","zh":"如果學校有幾棟建築物，訪客可能會問課室確切在哪裏。"},{"en":"Asking where exactly a shop is helps people avoid walking around in confusion.","zh":"詢問店舖確切在哪裏，有助避免四處亂走。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when someone needs clear directions.","zh":"這個片語用於某人需要清楚方向時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at the far end of","meaning":"在……的盡頭","examples":[{"en":"The fish market is at the far end of Kite Place.","zh":"魚市場在 Kite Place 的盡頭。"},{"en":"At the far end of a place means at the distant end, away from the entrance or starting point.","zh":"at the far end of a place 指在遠端，遠離入口或起點的位置。"},{"en":"The school office is at the far end of the corridor.","zh":"學校辦公室在走廊的盡頭。"},{"en":"If a market is at the far end of a street, visitors may need to walk past several shops first.","zh":"如果市場在街道盡頭，訪客可能要先經過幾間商店。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe location within a longer space.","zh":"這個片語有助描述較長空間中的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go over the bridge","meaning":"過橋","examples":[{"en":"Shannon has to go over the bridge to reach the fish market.","zh":"Shannon 要過橋才能到達魚市場。"},{"en":"To go over the bridge means to cross the bridge from one side to the other.","zh":"go over the bridge 指從橋的一邊走到另一邊。"},{"en":"Students go over the bridge every morning to get from the station to school.","zh":"學生每天早上過橋，從車站到學校。"},{"en":"If a shop is across the water, you may need to go over the bridge before turning right.","zh":"如果商店在水的另一邊，你可能需要先過橋再右轉。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear movement direction.","zh":"這個片語給出清楚的移動方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on the right","meaning":"在右邊","examples":[{"en":"After crossing the bridge, the fish market is on the right.","zh":"過橋後，魚市場在右邊。"},{"en":"On the right means on the right-hand side from the speaker’s or traveller’s direction.","zh":"on the right 指從說話者或行人方向看的右手邊。"},{"en":"The school gate is on the right after you pass the post office.","zh":"經過郵局後，學校大門在右邊。"},{"en":"Clear directions such as “on the right” help people find places without checking the map again.","zh":"“在右邊” 這類清楚方向有助人們不用再查地圖也找到地方。"},{"en":"This phrase depends on the direction you are facing or travelling.","zh":"這個片語取決於你面向或前進的方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"open all day","meaning":"全日營業","examples":[{"en":"Shannon asks whether the fish market is open all day.","zh":"Shannon 問魚市場是否全日營業。"},{"en":"Open all day means available to customers for the whole day, or most of normal daytime hours.","zh":"open all day 指整天或大部分正常日間營業時間都開放給顧客。"},{"en":"A convenience store near school may be open all day for snacks and drinks.","zh":"學校附近的便利店可能全日營業，售賣小食和飲品。"},{"en":"If a market is not open all day, shoppers must arrive before it closes.","zh":"如果市場不是全日營業，購物者必須在關門前到達。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when checking business hours.","zh":"這個片語用於查詢營業時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not close until","meaning":"直到……才關門","examples":[{"en":"The fish market does not close until four o’clock.","zh":"魚市場直到四時才關門。"},{"en":"Not close until a time means it remains open before that time and closes only then.","zh":"not close until a time 指在某時間之前仍然開放，到那時才關門。"},{"en":"The library does not close until nine, so students can study after dinner.","zh":"圖書館直到九時才關門，所以學生晚飯後仍可溫習。"},{"en":"If a shop does not close until late, customers have more time to buy what they need.","zh":"如果商店較晚才關門，顧客有更多時間買所需物品。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the closing time as later than expected.","zh":"這個片語強調關門時間比預期較晚。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"recommend going earlier","meaning":"建議早些去","examples":[{"en":"Leon recommends going earlier than four o’clock.","zh":"Leon 建議四時之前早些去。"},{"en":"To recommend going earlier means to suggest arriving before the latest possible time.","zh":"recommend going earlier 指建議在最後可能時間之前提早到達。"},{"en":"A teacher may recommend going earlier to an exam centre to avoid stress.","zh":"老師可能建議學生早些去考試中心，以避免壓力。"},{"en":"Going earlier can help shoppers get fresher food before popular items sell out.","zh":"早些去可以幫助購物者在熱門貨品賣完前買到更新鮮食物。"},{"en":"This phrase gives practical advice about timing.","zh":"這個片語給出關於時間安排的實用建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"run out of","meaning":"用完；賣完","examples":[{"en":"The fish market sometimes runs out of certain things.","zh":"魚市場有時會賣完某些東西。"},{"en":"To run out of something means to have none left because it has all been used or sold.","zh":"run out of something 指某物因被用完或賣完而沒有剩下。"},{"en":"A school canteen may run out of sandwiches before lunchtime ends.","zh":"學校飯堂可能在午餐時間結束前賣完三文治。"},{"en":"If a shop runs out of prawns, late customers must choose something else.","zh":"如果店舖賣完大蝦，遲來的顧客就必須選其他東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about limited supplies.","zh":"這個片語適合談及供應有限的情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"I don’t want that to happen","meaning":"我不想那樣的事發生","examples":[{"en":"Shannon says she does not want the fish to run out before she arrives.","zh":"Shannon 說她不想魚在她到達前賣完。"},{"en":"I don’t want that to happen means I want to prevent that unpleasant result.","zh":"I don’t want that to happen 指我想避免那個不愉快結果發生。"},{"en":"I will leave home early because I don’t want to miss the bus.","zh":"我會早點離家，因為我不想錯過巴士。"},{"en":"People plan ahead when they do not want a problem to happen later.","zh":"人們不想之後出問題時，就會提早計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a wish to avoid a bad or inconvenient situation.","zh":"這個片語表達想避免不好或不方便情況的願望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as long as","meaning":"只要……","examples":[{"en":"As long as Shannon gets there by 3.30, she should be fine.","zh":"只要 Shannon 在三時半前到達，她應該沒問題。"},{"en":"As long as means if a certain condition is met.","zh":"as long as 指如果某條件達成。"},{"en":"As long as you hand in the form today, your application will be accepted.","zh":"只要你今天交表，申請就會被接受。"},{"en":"A plan can work as long as people follow the timing carefully.","zh":"只要人們仔細遵守時間安排，計劃就能成功。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the condition needed for a good result.","zh":"這個片語引入取得好結果所需的條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get there by","meaning":"在……之前到達那裏","examples":[{"en":"Shannon should get there by 3.30.","zh":"Shannon 應在三時半之前到達那裏。"},{"en":"To get there by a time means to arrive at that place no later than that time.","zh":"get there by a time 指不遲於某個時間到達該地方。"},{"en":"Students should get there by 8:15 if the school trip leaves at 8:30.","zh":"如果學校旅行八時半出發，學生應在八時十五分前到達那裏。"},{"en":"Getting there by the suggested time helps avoid closed shops or sold-out items.","zh":"在建議時間前到達，有助避免店舖關門或貨品賣完。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on arriving before a deadline.","zh":"這個片語着重在限時前到達。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"you should be fine","meaning":"應該沒問題","examples":[{"en":"If Shannon arrives by 3.30, she should be fine.","zh":"如果 Shannon 三時半前到達，她應該沒問題。"},{"en":"You should be fine means there will probably be no problem if the condition is met.","zh":"you should be fine 指如果條件達成，大概不會有問題。"},{"en":"If you start revising today, you should be fine for Friday’s quiz.","zh":"如果你今天開始溫習，星期五的小測應該沒問題。"},{"en":"People say this to reassure someone who is worried about timing or preparation.","zh":"人們用這句話安慰擔心時間或準備的人。"},{"en":"This phrase gives mild confidence, not an absolute guarantee.","zh":"這個片語表示較溫和的信心，不是絕對保證。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"plenty of time","meaning":"時間很充裕","examples":[{"en":"It is only 11 o’clock, so Shannon has plenty of time.","zh":"現在才十一時，所以 Shannon 時間很充裕。"},{"en":"Plenty of time means more than enough time to do something without rushing.","zh":"plenty of time 指有超過足夠的時間做某事，不需要趕急。"},{"en":"If the train leaves at noon and it is only ten, we have plenty of time.","zh":"如果火車中午開出，而現在才十時，我們時間很充裕。"},{"en":"Having plenty of time reduces stress because people can travel, shop, or prepare calmly.","zh":"時間充裕可以減少壓力，因為人們可以冷靜地出行、購物或準備。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests there is no need to hurry.","zh":"這個片語暗示不需要趕。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"avoid","meaning":"避免","examples":[{"en":"Shannon wants to avoid plastic packaging in the supermarket.","zh":"Shannon 想在超市避免塑膠包裝。"},{"en":"To avoid something means to keep away from it or try not to use, do, or meet it.","zh":"avoid something 指遠離某事，或盡量不使用、不做或不遇到它。"},{"en":"Students should avoid leaving homework until the last minute.","zh":"學生應避免把功課留到最後一刻才做。"},{"en":"People avoid plastic packaging because it can create unnecessary waste.","zh":"人們避免塑膠包裝，因為它可能製造不必要的廢物。"},{"en":"This word often shows a deliberate choice to prevent a problem.","zh":"這個字常顯示為防止問題而作出的刻意選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"plastic packaging","meaning":"塑膠包裝","examples":[{"en":"Shannon wants to avoid plastic packaging when buying vegetables.","zh":"Shannon 買蔬菜時想避免塑膠包裝。"},{"en":"Plastic packaging is plastic material used to wrap, cover, or contain products.","zh":"plastic packaging 指用來包裹、覆蓋或盛載產品的塑膠材料。"},{"en":"Supermarkets often use plastic packaging for fruit, meat, snacks, and ready meals.","zh":"超市常用塑膠包裝盛載水果、肉類、小食和即食餐。"},{"en":"Plastic packaging can protect food, but too much of it increases waste.","zh":"塑膠包裝可以保護食物，但過多會增加廢物。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in discussions about shopping and the environment.","zh":"這個片語常用於購物和環保討論中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"organic shop","meaning":"有機食品店","examples":[{"en":"There is a really nice organic shop in Kite Place.","zh":"Kite Place 有一間很好的有機食品店。"},{"en":"An organic shop is a shop that sells food grown or made with fewer artificial chemicals.","zh":"organic shop 指售賣較少使用人工化學品種植或製作的食物的店舖。"},{"en":"Some families buy vegetables from an organic shop because they care about food quality.","zh":"有些家庭因重視食物質素而到有機食品店買蔬菜。"},{"en":"Organic shops may cost more, but customers often go there for freshness or environmental reasons.","zh":"有機食品店可能較貴，但顧客常因新鮮度或環保原因光顧。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a shop specialising in organic food and related products.","zh":"這個片語指專門售賣有機食物及相關產品的店舖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what’s it called?","meaning":"它叫甚麼名字？","examples":[{"en":"Leon tries to remember what the organic shop is called.","zh":"Leon 嘗試記起那間有機食品店叫甚麼名字。"},{"en":"What’s it called? is used when asking for the name of a person, place, or thing.","zh":"what’s it called? 用於詢問某人、某地方或某物的名稱。"},{"en":"If you forget the name of a restaurant, you may ask, “What’s it called?”","zh":"如果你忘記餐廳名稱，你可能會問：「它叫甚麼名字？」"},{"en":"People use this question when they know the thing but cannot remember its name.","zh":"人們知道某事物但記不起名稱時，會使用這個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and useful in everyday conversation.","zh":"這個片語較口語，在日常對話中很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the name of a flower","meaning":"一種花的名字","examples":[{"en":"The organic shop has the name of a flower.","zh":"那間有機食品店用了一種花的名字。"},{"en":"The name of a flower means a word used to identify a flower, such as rose, lily, or daisy.","zh":"the name of a flower 指用來識別花的詞語，例如玫瑰、百合或雛菊。"},{"en":"A café called Lily uses the name of a flower to sound soft and pleasant.","zh":"一間名為 Lily 的咖啡店使用花的名字，令它聽起來柔和舒服。"},{"en":"Remembering that a shop has the name of a flower can help someone recall its exact name later.","zh":"記得店名是一種花的名字，可以幫助人之後想起準確名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clue about a name rather than stating it directly.","zh":"這個片語給出名稱線索，而不是直接說出名稱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be called","meaning":"名為……","examples":[{"en":"The organic shop is called Rose.","zh":"那間有機食品店名為 Rose。"},{"en":"To be called something means to have that name.","zh":"be called something 指名稱是某個名字。"},{"en":"The new library café is called Chapter One.","zh":"新圖書館咖啡店名為 Chapter One。"},{"en":"Knowing what a place is called helps people search for it or ask for directions.","zh":"知道一個地方叫甚麼名字，有助人搜尋或問路。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when naming people, places, books, shops, or organisations.","zh":"這個片語用於命名人物、地方、書籍、商店或組織。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sell vegetables","meaning":"售賣蔬菜","examples":[{"en":"Rose sells vegetables and many other things.","zh":"Rose 售賣蔬菜和許多其他東西。"},{"en":"To sell vegetables means to offer vegetables for customers to buy.","zh":"sell vegetables 指提供蔬菜讓顧客購買。"},{"en":"A market stall may sell vegetables grown by local farmers.","zh":"市場攤檔可能售賣本地農夫種植的蔬菜。"},{"en":"If a shop sells fresh vegetables, families can buy ingredients for dinner there.","zh":"如果店舖售賣新鮮蔬菜，家庭可以在那裡買晚餐食材。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what a shop or seller provides.","zh":"這個片語描述店舖或賣家提供甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"quite a lot of other stuff","meaning":"很多其他東西","examples":[{"en":"The shop sells vegetables and quite a lot of other stuff.","zh":"這間店售賣蔬菜和很多其他東西。"},{"en":"Quite a lot of other stuff means many additional things besides the main item mentioned.","zh":"quite a lot of other stuff 指除了主要提到的物品外，還有許多其他東西。"},{"en":"The school shop sells notebooks and quite a lot of other stuff, such as pens and folders.","zh":"學校商店售賣筆記簿和很多其他東西，例如筆和文件夾。"},{"en":"If a shop sells a lot of extra items, customers may buy everything in one place.","zh":"如果店舖售賣很多額外物品，顧客可能在同一地方買齊所有東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suggests a useful variety.","zh":"這個片語較口語，暗示種類實用而豐富。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"as you reach","meaning":"當你到達……時","examples":[{"en":"As Shannon reaches the market, she will see a big grey building.","zh":"當 Shannon 到達市場時，她會看見一棟灰色大樓。"},{"en":"As you reach a place means when you arrive near or at that place.","zh":"as you reach a place 指當你接近或到達某地方時。"},{"en":"As you reach the station, you will see a bakery on your left.","zh":"當你到達車站時，你會在左邊看見一間麵包店。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in directions because it tells someone what they will notice at a certain point.","zh":"這個片語在指路時很有用，因為它告訴某人在某點會看見甚麼。"},{"en":"It connects movement with the next visible landmark.","zh":"它把移動與下一個可見地標連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on your left","meaning":"在你的左邊","examples":[{"en":"Shannon will see a big grey building on her left.","zh":"Shannon 會在她左邊看見一棟灰色大樓。"},{"en":"On your left means on the left-hand side from your direction of travel or view.","zh":"on your left 指從你前進或面向的方向看，在左手邊。"},{"en":"The classroom is on your left after you pass the lift.","zh":"經過升降機後，課室在你的左邊。"},{"en":"Giving left-right directions helps people find places without needing street names.","zh":"給出左右方向有助人們不用街名也找到地方。"},{"en":"This phrase depends on the direction the person is facing or walking.","zh":"這個片語取決於那人面向或步行的方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"used to be","meaning":"以前是……","examples":[{"en":"The big grey building used to be a warehouse.","zh":"那棟灰色大樓以前是一個倉庫。"},{"en":"Used to be means something was true in the past but is not true now.","zh":"used to be 指某事在過去是真的，但現在不是。"},{"en":"This café used to be a bookshop before it was renovated.","zh":"這間咖啡店翻新前以前是一間書店。"},{"en":"Knowing what a building used to be can help explain its size, shape, or history.","zh":"知道建築物以前是甚麼，可以幫助解釋它的大小、形狀或歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the past with the present.","zh":"這個片語把過去與現在作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"warehouse","meaning":"倉庫","examples":[{"en":"The grey building used to be a warehouse.","zh":"那棟灰色大樓以前是一個倉庫。"},{"en":"A warehouse is a large building used for storing goods before they are sold or moved.","zh":"warehouse 指用來儲存貨物、等候出售或運送的大型建築物。"},{"en":"A delivery company may keep boxes in a warehouse before sending them to customers.","zh":"送貨公司可能在把包裹送給顧客前，先把它們存放在倉庫。"},{"en":"Warehouses are often spacious, so old warehouses can be changed into shops or restaurants.","zh":"倉庫通常空間大，所以舊倉庫可以改成商店或餐廳。"},{"en":"This noun describes a storage building, not a normal home.","zh":"這個名詞描述儲物建築，而不是一般住宅。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"upstairs","meaning":"樓上","examples":[{"en":"There is now a restaurant upstairs in the grey building.","zh":"現在灰色大樓樓上有一間餐廳。"},{"en":"Upstairs means on a higher floor of a building.","zh":"upstairs 指在建築物較高樓層。"},{"en":"The music room is upstairs, above the school office.","zh":"音樂室在樓上，在學校辦公室之上。"},{"en":"If a restaurant is upstairs, visitors may need to find stairs, a lift, or an entrance inside the building.","zh":"如果餐廳在樓上，訪客可能需要找樓梯、升降機或大樓內的入口。"},{"en":"This word describes vertical location.","zh":"這個字描述垂直位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ground floor","meaning":"地下","examples":[{"en":"The ground floor has two shops beside the entrance.","zh":"地下入口旁邊有兩間商店。"},{"en":"The ground floor is the floor of a building at street level.","zh":"ground floor 指建築物與街道同一水平的樓層。"},{"en":"Many shops choose the ground floor because customers can enter easily from the street.","zh":"許多商店選擇地下，因為顧客可以容易從街上進入。"},{"en":"If a shop is on the ground floor, visitors do not need to climb stairs to reach it.","zh":"如果店舖在地下，訪客不用爬樓梯也能到達。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English; American English often uses “first floor”.","zh":"這個片語常見於英式英語；美式英語常用 “first floor”。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"either side of","meaning":"……兩邊","examples":[{"en":"There are two shops on either side of the entrance.","zh":"入口兩邊各有一間商店。"},{"en":"Either side of something means on both the left and right sides of it.","zh":"either side of something 指在某物左邊和右邊兩側。"},{"en":"Trees were planted on either side of the school path.","zh":"學校小路兩邊都種了樹。"},{"en":"If there are shops on either side of an entrance, visitors can use the entrance as a clear landmark.","zh":"如果入口兩邊有商店，訪客可以把入口當作清楚地標。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe balanced positions around a central point.","zh":"這個片語有助描述中心點兩側的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"entrance","meaning":"入口","examples":[{"en":"The organic shop is on the left side of the entrance.","zh":"那間有機食品店在入口左邊。"},{"en":"An entrance is the place where people go into a building, room, or area.","zh":"entrance 指人們進入建築物、房間或區域的地方。"},{"en":"Students should wait near the main entrance before the school tour begins.","zh":"學生應在學校參觀開始前於正門入口附近等候。"},{"en":"Clear entrances help visitors know where to go and avoid entering the wrong door.","zh":"清楚入口幫助訪客知道去哪裡，避免入錯門。"},{"en":"This word refers to the way in, not the whole building.","zh":"這個字指進入的地方，而不是整棟建築物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the one on the left","meaning":"左邊那一間","examples":[{"en":"Rose is the shop on the left of the entrance.","zh":"Rose 是入口左邊那一間商店。"},{"en":"The one on the left means the item or place located on the left side among choices.","zh":"the one on the left 指在幾個選項中位於左邊的那一個。"},{"en":"If there are two lifts, take the one on the left because it goes to the library.","zh":"如果有兩部升降機，乘左邊那一部，因為它通往圖書館。"},{"en":"This phrase helps someone choose correctly when there is more than one similar option.","zh":"當有多個相似選項時，這個片語幫助人正確選擇。"},{"en":"It is common in spoken directions.","zh":"它常見於口頭指路。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"easy enough","meaning":"相當容易；夠容易","examples":[{"en":"Shannon says the organic shop sounds easy enough to find.","zh":"Shannon 說那間有機食品店聽起來相當容易找到。"},{"en":"Easy enough means not too difficult and probably manageable.","zh":"easy enough 指不太困難，大概能做到。"},{"en":"The homework looks easy enough if students start before dinner.","zh":"如果學生晚飯前開始，這份功課看起來相當容易完成。"},{"en":"Clear landmarks can make a place easy enough to find even for a first-time visitor.","zh":"清楚地標可以令第一次到訪的人也相當容易找到某地方。"},{"en":"This phrase gives mild confidence rather than strong certainty.","zh":"這個片語表示溫和信心，而不是非常確定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"you can’t miss it","meaning":"你不會錯過的；很容易看見","examples":[{"en":"Leon says Shannon cannot miss the organic shop.","zh":"Leon 說 Shannon 不會錯過那間有機食品店。"},{"en":"You can’t miss it means it is very easy to see or find.","zh":"you can’t miss it 指某地方很容易看見或找到。"},{"en":"The school hall has a huge red door, so you can’t miss it.","zh":"學校禮堂有一扇巨大的紅門，所以你不會錯過。"},{"en":"People say this when a place has a clear sign, colour, or position.","zh":"當地方有清楚招牌、顏色或位置時，人們會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures someone that the directions are simple.","zh":"這個片語用來安慰別人方向很簡單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a big sign","meaning":"大招牌","examples":[{"en":"There is a big sign on the pavement outside the shop.","zh":"店外行人路上有一個大招牌。"},{"en":"A big sign is a large notice or board that gives information or attracts attention.","zh":"big sign 指提供資訊或吸引注意的大型告示或牌。"},{"en":"A big sign outside a library may show opening hours and special events.","zh":"圖書館外的大招牌可能顯示開放時間和特別活動。"},{"en":"Big signs help customers find shops quickly, especially in busy streets.","zh":"大招牌幫助顧客快速找到店舖，尤其是在繁忙街道上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visible marker used for information or advertising.","zh":"這個片語描述用於資訊或廣告的可見標記。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on the pavement","meaning":"在行人路上","examples":[{"en":"The sign is on the pavement outside the shop.","zh":"招牌在店外行人路上。"},{"en":"On the pavement means on the walking area beside the road.","zh":"on the pavement 指在道路旁供行人行走的地方。"},{"en":"Cafés sometimes place menu boards on the pavement to attract passers-by.","zh":"咖啡店有時會把餐牌板放在行人路上，以吸引路人。"},{"en":"A sign on the pavement is easier for pedestrians to notice than one hidden inside a shop.","zh":"放在行人路上的招牌，比藏在店內的招牌更容易被行人注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a location used by people walking along the street.","zh":"這個片語描述沿街步行的人使用的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"look for","meaning":"尋找；留意","examples":[{"en":"Shannon can look for the big sign on the pavement.","zh":"Shannon 可以留意行人路上的大招牌。"},{"en":"To look for something means to try to find it.","zh":"look for something 指嘗試尋找某物。"},{"en":"A student may look for a quiet seat in the library before starting homework.","zh":"學生開始做功課前，可能在圖書館尋找安靜座位。"},{"en":"Looking for a landmark can make directions easier to follow.","zh":"尋找地標可以令指路更容易跟隨。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on searching with intention.","zh":"這個片語着重有目的地搜尋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"if I need anything else","meaning":"如果我還需要其他東西","examples":[{"en":"Shannon may go to the supermarket if she needs anything else.","zh":"如果 Shannon 還需要其他東西，她可能會去超市。"},{"en":"If I need anything else means if there are extra things I still have to buy or get.","zh":"if I need anything else 指如果我仍有額外東西需要購買或取得。"},{"en":"I will visit the stationery shop if I need anything else for the project.","zh":"如果我還需要其他項目做專題，我會去文具店。"},{"en":"People keep another shop in mind in case the first shop does not have everything.","zh":"人們會把另一間店記在心中，以防第一間店不能買齊所有東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when planning for possible extra needs.","zh":"這個片語用於規劃可能出現的額外需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have to go to","meaning":"不得不去……","examples":[{"en":"Shannon may have to go to the supermarket.","zh":"Shannon 可能不得不去超市。"},{"en":"To have to go to a place means to need or be required to go there.","zh":"have to go to a place 指需要或必須去某地方。"},{"en":"A student may have to go to the office to collect a late pass.","zh":"學生可能不得不去校務處領遲到證。"},{"en":"If the market does not sell everything, Shannon may have to go to another shop.","zh":"如果市場沒有售賣所有東西，Shannon 可能不得不去另一間店。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests necessity, not just choice.","zh":"這個片語暗示必要性，而不只是選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"should be able to","meaning":"應該能夠……","examples":[{"en":"Shannon should be able to get everything she needs.","zh":"Shannon 應該能夠買到所需的一切。"},{"en":"Should be able to means will probably be able to do something.","zh":"should be able to 指很可能能夠做某事。"},{"en":"If the computer room is open, students should be able to print their essays.","zh":"如果電腦室開放，學生應該能夠列印文章。"},{"en":"A shop with many products should be able to meet most customers’ needs.","zh":"產品多的店舖應該能夠滿足大部分顧客需要。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses likely ability, not complete certainty.","zh":"這個片語表示可能做到，而不是完全確定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get everything you need","meaning":"買到所需的一切","examples":[{"en":"Shannon should be able to get everything she needs in Kite Place.","zh":"Shannon 應該能夠在 Kite Place 買到所需的一切。"},{"en":"To get everything you need means to obtain all the items required for a task or situation.","zh":"get everything you need 指取得某任務或情況所需的所有物品。"},{"en":"A parent may get everything needed for dinner from one supermarket.","zh":"家長可能在一間超市買齊晚餐所需的一切。"},{"en":"If an area has a market, bakery, and grocery shop, shoppers can save time by buying everything nearby.","zh":"如果一個區有市場、麵包店和雜貨店，購物者可以在附近買齊東西以節省時間。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests convenience and completeness.","zh":"這個片語暗示方便和齊全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"minibus","meaning":"小巴","examples":[{"en":"There is a minibus that goes to the supermarket.","zh":"有一輛前往超市的小巴。"},{"en":"A minibus is a small bus that carries fewer passengers than a full-sized bus.","zh":"minibus 指載客量少於大型巴士的小型巴士。"},{"en":"Students may take a minibus from the station to school when it is raining.","zh":"下雨時，學生可能從車站乘小巴到學校。"},{"en":"Minibuses are useful in areas where large buses do not run often.","zh":"在大型巴士不常行駛的地區，小巴很有用。"},{"en":"This word refers to a small public or private passenger vehicle.","zh":"這個字指小型公共或私人載客車輛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"go to the supermarket","meaning":"前往超市","examples":[{"en":"The purple minibus goes to the supermarket.","zh":"紫色小巴前往超市。"},{"en":"To go to the supermarket means to travel to a large shop that sells food and household items.","zh":"go to the supermarket 指前往售賣食物和家居用品的大型商店。"},{"en":"Families often go to the supermarket once a week to buy groceries.","zh":"家庭常每星期去一次超市買雜貨。"},{"en":"If local markets do not have everything, shoppers may go to the supermarket as a backup.","zh":"如果本地市場沒有所有東西，購物者可能把超市作為後備選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on travelling there, not only shopping inside.","zh":"這個片語着重前往該地，而不只是店內購物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the number is","meaning":"號碼是……","examples":[{"en":"The number of the purple minibus is 289.","zh":"紫色小巴的號碼是 289。"},{"en":"The number is means the route, label, or identifying number is a particular figure.","zh":"the number is 指路線、標籤或識別號碼是某個數字。"},{"en":"The number of the bus to the library is 12A.","zh":"前往圖書館的巴士號碼是 12A。"},{"en":"Knowing the number helps passengers choose the correct vehicle or service.","zh":"知道號碼有助乘客選擇正確車輛或服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when giving transport information.","zh":"這個片語常用於提供交通資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"need to get at","meaning":"需要在……買","examples":[{"en":"Leon asks what Shannon needs to get at the fish market.","zh":"Leon 問 Shannon 需要在魚市場買甚麼。"},{"en":"Need to get at a place means need to buy, collect, or obtain something there.","zh":"need to get at a place 指需要在某地方購買、領取或取得某物。"},{"en":"Before going to the stationery shop, a student should list what she needs to get there.","zh":"去文具店前，學生應列出需要在那裡買甚麼。"},{"en":"Asking what someone needs to get at a market helps plan the shopping route.","zh":"問某人需要在市場買甚麼，有助規劃購物路線。"},{"en":"This phrase connects the needed item with the place where it can be obtained.","zh":"這個片語把所需物品與可取得該物的地方連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"salmon","meaning":"三文魚","examples":[{"en":"The salmon at the fish market is always very good.","zh":"魚市場的三文魚一向很好。"},{"en":"Salmon is a pink-fleshed fish often eaten grilled, baked, smoked, or raw in sushi.","zh":"salmon 指一種粉紅色魚肉的魚，常用來烤、焗、煙燻或作壽司生食。"},{"en":"A restaurant may serve salmon with vegetables and rice for a healthy lunch set.","zh":"餐廳可能以三文魚配蔬菜和飯作健康午餐。"},{"en":"Fresh salmon sells quickly because many people like its rich taste and soft texture.","zh":"新鮮三文魚賣得快，因為很多人喜歡它濃郁味道和柔軟口感。"},{"en":"This word names a type of fish commonly bought for meals.","zh":"這個字命名一種常用於餐點的魚。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"shellfish","meaning":"貝類海鮮","examples":[{"en":"The shellfish at the fish market is also very good.","zh":"魚市場的貝類海鮮也很好。"},{"en":"Shellfish are sea animals with shells, such as prawns, crabs, clams, mussels, and oysters.","zh":"shellfish 指有殼的海產，例如大蝦、蟹、蜆、青口和蠔。"},{"en":"Some people avoid shellfish because they are allergic to it.","zh":"有些人因對貝類海鮮敏感而避免食用。"},{"en":"Fresh shellfish must be stored carefully because it can spoil quickly.","zh":"新鮮貝類海鮮必須小心儲存，因為它很快變壞。"},{"en":"This word refers to a group of seafood, not one single animal.","zh":"這個字指一類海鮮，而不是單一動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make a curry","meaning":"煮咖喱","examples":[{"en":"Shannon is going to make a curry for her cousins.","zh":"Shannon 打算為她的表親煮咖喱。"},{"en":"To make a curry means to cook a dish with spices, sauce, and ingredients such as meat, seafood, beans, or vegetables.","zh":"make a curry 指用香料、醬汁和肉類、海鮮、豆類或蔬菜等食材煮一道菜。"},{"en":"A family may make a curry on Sunday because it can feed many people.","zh":"家庭可能在星期日煮咖喱，因為它可以供很多人食用。"},{"en":"Making a curry requires choosing ingredients that absorb flavour well.","zh":"煮咖喱需要選擇能吸收味道的食材。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparing a spicy or richly flavoured dish.","zh":"這個片語描述準備辛香或味道濃郁的菜式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"need about","meaning":"需要大約……","examples":[{"en":"Shannon needs about twelve prawns for the curry.","zh":"Shannon 煮咖喱需要大約十二隻大蝦。"},{"en":"Need about means require approximately a certain amount, not an exact number.","zh":"need about 指需要大約某個數量，而不是完全精確數字。"},{"en":"We need about twenty chairs for the class meeting.","zh":"我們班會需要大約二十張椅子。"},{"en":"Giving an approximate number helps with planning when the exact amount is not critical.","zh":"當精確數量不是最重要時，提供大約數字有助規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for shopping, cooking, and organising events.","zh":"這個片語適合用於購物、煮食和籌辦活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"prawns","meaning":"大蝦","examples":[{"en":"Shannon needs about twelve prawns for the curry.","zh":"Shannon 煮咖喱需要大約十二隻大蝦。"},{"en":"Prawns are small shellfish with long bodies, often cooked in dishes such as curry, pasta, or noodles.","zh":"prawns 指身體較長的小型貝類海鮮，常用於咖喱、意粉或麵食。"},{"en":"A seafood shop may sell prawns fresh, frozen, or already peeled.","zh":"海鮮店可能售賣新鮮、急凍或已去殼大蝦。"},{"en":"Prawns cook quickly, so adding them too early can make them tough.","zh":"大蝦很快熟，所以太早加入可能令它們變硬。"},{"en":"This word is common in British English; American English often uses “shrimp”.","zh":"這個字常見於英式英語；美式英語常用 “shrimp”。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have plenty of","meaning":"有很多……","examples":[{"en":"The fish market will have plenty of prawns.","zh":"魚市場會有很多大蝦。"},{"en":"To have plenty of something means to have more than enough of it.","zh":"have plenty of something 指擁有超過足夠數量的某物。"},{"en":"The school library has plenty of seats during the morning.","zh":"學校圖書館早上有很多座位。"},{"en":"If a shop has plenty of stock, customers do not need to worry about items running out.","zh":"如果店舖有很多存貨，顧客就不用擔心貨品賣完。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests abundance and reassurance.","zh":"這個片語暗示數量充足，令人放心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have you ever tried","meaning":"你曾經試過……嗎？","examples":[{"en":"Leon asks Shannon whether she has ever tried samphire.","zh":"Leon 問 Shannon 是否曾經試過海蘆筍。"},{"en":"Have you ever tried asks whether someone has experienced eating, using, or doing something at any time before now.","zh":"have you ever tried 用來問某人到目前為止是否曾吃過、用過或做過某事。"},{"en":"Have you ever tried making soup with coconut milk?","zh":"你曾經試過用椰奶煮湯嗎？"},{"en":"People ask this question when suggesting something new or checking past experience.","zh":"人們建議新事物或確認過往經驗時，會問這個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for introducing unfamiliar food or activities.","zh":"這個片語適合用來引入不熟悉的食物或活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"samphire","meaning":"海蘆筍","examples":[{"en":"Leon suggests that Shannon try samphire.","zh":"Leon 建議 Shannon 試試海蘆筍。"},{"en":"Samphire is a salty green sea vegetable often served with fish or seafood.","zh":"samphire 指一種帶鹹味的綠色海邊蔬菜，常與魚或海鮮一起食用。"},{"en":"A cook may add samphire to a seafood dish because its salty taste matches the sea flavour.","zh":"廚師可能把海蘆筍加入海鮮菜式，因為它的鹹味配合海鮮味道。"},{"en":"Samphire can make a meal feel more unusual because many people have not tried it before.","zh":"海蘆筍可以令一餐飯感覺較特別，因為很多人以前沒有試過。"},{"en":"This word names a specific edible plant used in cooking.","zh":"這個字命名一種可食用並用於烹調的特定植物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a type of seaweed","meaning":"一種海藻","examples":[{"en":"Leon describes samphire as a type of seaweed.","zh":"Leon 把海蘆筍形容為一種海藻。"},{"en":"A type of seaweed means one kind of edible plant or plant-like food from the sea.","zh":"a type of seaweed 指一種來自海洋、可食用的植物或類似植物的食物。"},{"en":"Some soups use a type of seaweed to add a salty ocean flavour.","zh":"有些湯會使用一種海藻來加入鹹鮮海味。"},{"en":"Describing samphire as seaweed helps Shannon imagine that it goes well with seafood.","zh":"把海蘆筍形容為海藻，有助 Shannon 想像它適合配海鮮。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a simple category for an unfamiliar food.","zh":"這個片語為不熟悉的食物提供簡單分類。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ask for a handful","meaning":"要一把……","examples":[{"en":"Leon usually asks for a handful of samphire.","zh":"Leon 通常會要一把海蘆筍。"},{"en":"To ask for a handful means to request a small amount that could fit in one hand.","zh":"ask for a handful 指要求一小撮或一把，大約能放在一隻手中。"},{"en":"A customer may ask for a handful of fresh herbs to add to soup.","zh":"顧客可能要一把新鮮香草加進湯裡。"},{"en":"Asking for a handful is useful when the exact weight is not important.","zh":"當準確重量不重要時，要一把某物很實用。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when buying loose food at a market.","zh":"這個片語常用於在市場購買散裝食物時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fry it in butter","meaning":"用牛油煎","examples":[{"en":"Leon fries samphire in butter.","zh":"Leon 用牛油煎海蘆筍。"},{"en":"To fry something in butter means to cook it in hot butter in a pan.","zh":"fry something in butter 指在平底鑊中用熱牛油烹煮某物。"},{"en":"A cook may fry mushrooms in butter before adding them to pasta.","zh":"廚師可能先用牛油煎蘑菇，再把它們加入意粉。"},{"en":"Frying vegetables in butter can add a richer taste, but it also adds fat.","zh":"用牛油煎蔬菜可以增加濃郁味道，但也會增加脂肪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cooking method and the fat used.","zh":"這個片語描述烹調方法和所用油脂。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"how do you spell it?","meaning":"它怎樣串？","examples":[{"en":"Shannon asks Leon how to spell samphire.","zh":"Shannon 問 Leon samphire 怎樣串。"},{"en":"How do you spell it? asks someone to say the letters of a word in order.","zh":"how do you spell it? 是請別人按次序說出一個字的字母。"},{"en":"If a student hears a new word, they may ask, “How do you spell it?”","zh":"如果學生聽到新詞，可能會問：「它怎樣串？」"},{"en":"Asking for spelling helps people search for a word, write it correctly, or remember it later.","zh":"詢問串法有助人搜尋、正確寫下或日後記住該詞。"},{"en":"This question is common when a word sounds unfamiliar.","zh":"當一個字聽起來不熟悉時，這個問題很常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"spell","meaning":"串字","examples":[{"en":"Leon spells the word “samphire” for Shannon.","zh":"Leon 為 Shannon 串出 “samphire” 這個字。"},{"en":"To spell a word means to say or write its letters in the correct order.","zh":"spell a word 指按正確次序說出或寫出一個字的字母。"},{"en":"Teachers often ask students to spell difficult vocabulary before using it in a sentence.","zh":"老師常要求學生先串出困難詞彙，再用它造句。"},{"en":"Correct spelling matters because one wrong letter can make a word hard to recognise.","zh":"正確串字很重要，因為一個錯字母也可能令人難以辨認該字。"},{"en":"This verb focuses on letter order, not pronunciation alone.","zh":"這個動詞着重字母次序，而不只是發音。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"try something different","meaning":"嘗試不同的東西","examples":[{"en":"Shannon says it is always good to try something different.","zh":"Shannon 說嘗試不同的東西總是好的。"},{"en":"To try something different means to experience or choose something new instead of the usual option.","zh":"try something different 指體驗或選擇新事物，而不是平常選項。"},{"en":"A student may try something different by joining drama club instead of football club.","zh":"學生可以透過參加戲劇學會而不是足球會來嘗試不同的東西。"},{"en":"Trying different food can make shopping and cooking more interesting.","zh":"嘗試不同食物可以令購物和煮食更有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests openness to new experiences.","zh":"這個片語暗示願意接受新經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"see what they have","meaning":"看看他們有甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Shannon will see what beans they have in the organic shop.","zh":"Shannon 會看看有機食品店有甚麼豆類。"},{"en":"To see what they have means to check what items are available in a shop or place.","zh":"see what they have 指查看店舖或地方有甚麼可供選擇。"},{"en":"Before choosing lunch, students may see what the canteen has today.","zh":"選午餐前，學生可能看看飯堂今天有甚麼。"},{"en":"Checking what a shop has helps shoppers decide whether they can buy everything there.","zh":"查看店舖有甚麼，有助購物者決定是否能在那裡買齊所有東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and common in shopping situations.","zh":"這個片語較口語，常見於購物情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"beans","meaning":"豆類","examples":[{"en":"Shannon wants to see what beans the organic shop has.","zh":"Shannon 想看看有機食品店有甚麼豆類。"},{"en":"Beans are seeds from certain plants, often used in soups, curries, salads, and stews.","zh":"beans 指某些植物的種子，常用於湯、咖喱、沙律和燉菜。"},{"en":"Vegetarians may use beans as a source of protein instead of meat.","zh":"素食者可能用豆類作為蛋白質來源，而不是肉類。"},{"en":"Beans are useful for cooking because they are filling, affordable, and easy to store.","zh":"豆類很適合烹調，因為它們飽肚、價錢相宜並容易儲存。"},{"en":"This word can refer to many types, such as kidney beans, black beans, or chickpeas.","zh":"這個字可指許多種類，例如紅腰豆、黑豆或鷹嘴豆。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get something for dessert","meaning":"買些甜品","examples":[{"en":"Shannon wants to get something for dessert at the organic shop.","zh":"Shannon 想在有機食品店買些甜品。"},{"en":"To get something for dessert means to buy or prepare food to eat after the main meal.","zh":"get something for dessert 指購買或準備主餐後吃的食物。"},{"en":"A family may get fruit for dessert when they want something light.","zh":"家庭想吃清淡一點時，可能買水果作甜品。"},{"en":"Buying dessert in advance helps the host finish the meal without rushing back to the shops.","zh":"提前買甜品可以幫助主人完成一餐飯，而不用趕回店舖。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the sweet or final part of a meal.","zh":"這個片語着重一餐飯中甜的或最後部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"how about","meaning":"……怎麼樣？","examples":[{"en":"Leon suggests a mango by asking, “How about a mango?”","zh":"Leon 問：「芒果怎麼樣？」來建議買芒果。"},{"en":"How about is used to suggest an option or ask what someone thinks of it.","zh":"how about 用來提出一個選項或詢問對方對它的看法。"},{"en":"How about meeting at the library after school?","zh":"放學後在圖書館見面怎麼樣？"},{"en":"People use this phrase when offering an idea in a friendly way.","zh":"人們友善地提出想法時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It is softer than directly saying, “Choose this.”","zh":"它比直接說「選這個」更委婉。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"mango","meaning":"芒果","examples":[{"en":"Leon suggests buying a mango for dessert.","zh":"Leon 建議買一個芒果作甜品。"},{"en":"A mango is a sweet tropical fruit with soft orange flesh and a large seed inside.","zh":"mango 指一種甜的熱帶水果，果肉柔軟橙色，內有大核。"},{"en":"A shop may sell mangoes that are ripe, unripe, or ready to eat.","zh":"店舖可能售賣熟、未熟或即食芒果。"},{"en":"Mangoes are popular for dessert because they are sweet and refreshing.","zh":"芒果作甜品很受歡迎，因為它甜而清爽。"},{"en":"This word names a fruit often eaten fresh or used in drinks and puddings.","zh":"這個字命名一種常被新鮮食用或用於飲品和布甸的水果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"I’m not sure","meaning":"我不太肯定","examples":[{"en":"Shannon is not sure whether a mango is a good choice.","zh":"Shannon 不太肯定芒果是否好選擇。"},{"en":"I’m not sure means I do not know clearly or I have some doubt.","zh":"I’m not sure 指我不清楚知道，或有一些疑慮。"},{"en":"I’m not sure if the library is still open, so I will check online first.","zh":"我不太肯定圖書館是否仍然開放，所以我會先上網查看。"},{"en":"People say this when they need more information before deciding.","zh":"人們需要更多資料才作決定時，會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase shows uncertainty without strongly rejecting an idea.","zh":"這個片語顯示不確定，但不是強烈拒絕某想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not always ripe","meaning":"不一定熟","examples":[{"en":"Mangoes are not always ripe.","zh":"芒果不一定熟。"},{"en":"Not always ripe means sometimes the fruit is still hard or not ready to eat.","zh":"not always ripe 指水果有時仍然硬或未適合食用。"},{"en":"Bananas in supermarkets are not always ripe when customers buy them.","zh":"顧客在超市買香蕉時，香蕉不一定熟。"},{"en":"If fruit is not ripe, it may taste sour, hard, or less sweet.","zh":"如果水果未熟，味道可能偏酸、口感硬或不夠甜。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why someone may avoid choosing certain fruit for immediate dessert.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何某人可能避免選擇某種水果作即日甜品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"I’d prefer","meaning":"我比較想要","examples":[{"en":"Shannon says she would prefer a melon.","zh":"Shannon 說她比較想要蜜瓜。"},{"en":"I’d prefer means I would rather choose one thing instead of another.","zh":"I’d prefer 指我較想選擇一樣東西，而不是另一樣。"},{"en":"I’d prefer tea to coffee because coffee keeps me awake at night.","zh":"我比較想要茶而不是咖啡，因為咖啡令我晚上睡不着。"},{"en":"People use this phrase politely when they suggest a different choice.","zh":"人們禮貌地提出不同選擇時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It sounds softer than saying, “I don’t want that.”","zh":"它比說「我不想要那個」更委婉。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"melon","meaning":"蜜瓜","examples":[{"en":"Shannon would prefer a melon because it is bigger.","zh":"Shannon 比較想要蜜瓜，因為它較大。"},{"en":"A melon is a large, sweet fruit with juicy flesh, often eaten cold as dessert.","zh":"melon 指大型甜水果，果肉多汁，常冷食作甜品。"},{"en":"A family may buy a melon when several guests are sharing dessert.","zh":"家庭在幾位客人分享甜品時，可能會買一個蜜瓜。"},{"en":"Melons are useful for gatherings because one fruit can serve many people.","zh":"蜜瓜很適合聚會，因為一個水果可以供多人食用。"},{"en":"This word names a fruit, such as honeydew or cantaloupe.","zh":"這個字命名一種水果，例如蜜瓜或哈密瓜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"good idea","meaning":"好主意","examples":[{"en":"Leon thinks buying a melon is a good idea.","zh":"Leon 認為買蜜瓜是好主意。"},{"en":"A good idea is a sensible or useful suggestion.","zh":"good idea 指合理或有用的建議。"},{"en":"Bringing a reusable bag to the market is a good idea.","zh":"帶可重用袋去市場是好主意。"},{"en":"A good idea can save time, money, or trouble later.","zh":"好主意可以之後節省時間、金錢或麻煩。"},{"en":"This phrase shows approval of a suggestion.","zh":"這個片語表示認同某項建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sell a lot of spices","meaning":"售賣很多香料","examples":[{"en":"The owner sells a lot of spices that can go in a curry.","zh":"店主售賣很多可放進咖喱裏的香料。"},{"en":"To sell a lot of spices means to offer many kinds of flavouring ingredients for customers to buy.","zh":"sell a lot of spices 指提供多種調味食材讓顧客購買。"},{"en":"A market stall may sell a lot of spices, such as cumin, chilli, turmeric, and cinnamon.","zh":"市場攤檔可能售賣很多香料，例如孜然、辣椒、薑黃和肉桂。"},{"en":"Shops that sell many spices are useful for people cooking curries, soups, and stews.","zh":"售賣多種香料的店舖，對煮咖喱、湯和燉菜的人很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes variety and quantity in cooking ingredients.","zh":"這個片語描述烹調食材的種類和數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"spices","meaning":"香料","examples":[{"en":"Shannon may buy spices for the curry.","zh":"Shannon 可能買香料來煮咖喱。"},{"en":"Spices are strong-flavoured plant ingredients used to add taste, colour, or smell to food.","zh":"spices 指味道強烈的植物食材，用來為食物增加味道、顏色或香氣。"},{"en":"Pepper, chilli, cumin, and turmeric are common spices in many kitchens.","zh":"胡椒、辣椒、孜然和薑黃是許多廚房中的常見香料。"},{"en":"Using the right spices can make a simple dish taste richer and warmer.","zh":"使用合適香料可以令簡單菜式味道更濃郁溫暖。"},{"en":"This word refers to flavouring ingredients, not the main food itself.","zh":"這個字指調味食材，而不是食物主體本身。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"put in a curry","meaning":"放進咖喱裏","examples":[{"en":"The spices can be put in a curry.","zh":"這些香料可以放進咖喱裏。"},{"en":"To put something in a curry means to add it to the curry while cooking.","zh":"put something in a curry 指煮咖喱時把某物加入其中。"},{"en":"You can put beans in a curry to make it more filling.","zh":"你可以把豆類放進咖喱裏，令它更飽肚。"},{"en":"Ingredients put in a curry absorb sauce and flavour as they cook.","zh":"放進咖喱裏的食材會在烹煮時吸收醬汁和味道。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding food or seasoning to a curry dish.","zh":"這個片語描述把食物或調味料加入咖喱菜式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"things like","meaning":"例如……之類的東西","examples":[{"en":"The shop sells things like coconut.","zh":"這間店售賣椰子之類的東西。"},{"en":"Things like means examples of a wider group, not a complete list.","zh":"things like 指較大類別中的例子，而不是完整清單。"},{"en":"A school trip needs things like water, hats, and comfortable shoes.","zh":"學校旅行需要水、帽子和舒適鞋之類的東西。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when giving examples without naming every item.","zh":"人們給例子但不列出所有項目時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It suggests there are other similar things too.","zh":"它暗示還有其他相似東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"coconut","meaning":"椰子","examples":[{"en":"The organic shop sells things like coconut.","zh":"那間有機食品店售賣椰子之類的東西。"},{"en":"A coconut is a large tropical fruit with a hard shell, white flesh, and sweet liquid inside.","zh":"coconut 指一種大型熱帶水果，有硬殼、白色果肉和內裡甜液。"},{"en":"Coconut milk is often used in curries, desserts, and soups.","zh":"椰奶常用於咖喱、甜品和湯。"},{"en":"Adding coconut can make a curry taste richer and slightly sweet.","zh":"加入椰子可以令咖喱味道更濃郁並帶一點甜味。"},{"en":"This word can refer to the whole fruit, its flesh, water, or milk.","zh":"這個字可指整個水果、果肉、椰子水或椰奶。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have a look","meaning":"看一看","examples":[{"en":"Shannon says she will have a look at the spices.","zh":"Shannon 說她會看一看那些香料。"},{"en":"To have a look means to check or examine something briefly.","zh":"have a look 指簡短查看或檢視某物。"},{"en":"A teacher may have a look at a student’s draft before giving advice.","zh":"老師可能先看一看學生草稿，再給建議。"},{"en":"Having a look before buying helps shoppers compare prices and quality.","zh":"購買前看一看，有助購物者比較價格和質素。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and softer than “inspect”.","zh":"這個片語較口語，比 “inspect” 語氣柔和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"go with","meaning":"與……配搭","examples":[{"en":"Shannon knows that bread does not really go with curry.","zh":"Shannon 知道麵包與咖喱不太配。"},{"en":"To go with something means to match, suit, or taste good together with it.","zh":"go with something 指與某物配合、適合或一起吃起來好。"},{"en":"Rice goes well with curry because it absorbs the sauce.","zh":"飯很適合配咖喱，因為它能吸收醬汁。"},{"en":"If two foods do not go together, the meal may taste strange or unbalanced.","zh":"如果兩種食物不配，一餐飯可能味道奇怪或不平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for food, clothes, colours, and styles.","zh":"這個片語常用於食物、衣服、顏色和風格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in case","meaning":"以防萬一","examples":[{"en":"Shannon likes to have some bread in case it is needed.","zh":"Shannon 喜歡準備一些麵包，以防萬一需要。"},{"en":"In case means as preparation for a possible future situation.","zh":"in case 指為可能出現的未來情況作準備。"},{"en":"Bring a jacket in case the weather becomes cold.","zh":"帶件外套吧，以防萬一天氣變冷。"},{"en":"People buy extra food in case guests are hungrier than expected.","zh":"人們會多買食物，以防客人比預期更餓。"},{"en":"This phrase shows planning for something that may or may not happen.","zh":"這個片語顯示為可能發生或不發生的事情作準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as I said","meaning":"正如我所說","examples":[{"en":"Leon reminds Shannon that, as he said, all the bread is home-made.","zh":"Leon 提醒 Shannon，正如他所說，所有麵包都是自家製的。"},{"en":"As I said means as I mentioned earlier.","zh":"as I said 指正如我之前提過。"},{"en":"As I said, the library closes early on Sundays, so we should go now.","zh":"正如我所說，圖書館星期日較早關門，所以我們現在應該去。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to refer back to information they have already given.","zh":"人們用這個片語指回之前已提供的資料。"},{"en":"It can sound helpful, but if used sharply it may sound impatient.","zh":"它可以聽起來有幫助，但如果語氣強硬，也可能顯得不耐煩。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"home-made","meaning":"自家製的","examples":[{"en":"All the bread sold there is home-made.","zh":"那裡售賣的所有麵包都是自家製的。"},{"en":"Home-made means made at home or made in a small, personal way rather than factory-produced.","zh":"home-made 指在家中或以小規模、個人方式製作，而不是工廠生產。"},{"en":"A café may sell home-made soup to make customers feel the food is fresh and cared for.","zh":"咖啡店可能售賣自家製湯，令顧客覺得食物新鮮而用心。"},{"en":"Home-made food often feels special because someone prepared it by hand.","zh":"自家製食物常感覺特別，因為有人親手準備。"},{"en":"This word suggests care, freshness, and a less industrial style.","zh":"這個字暗示用心、新鮮和較少工業化的風格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lots of variety","meaning":"種類很多","examples":[{"en":"The organic shop has lots of variety in its bread.","zh":"那間有機食品店的麵包種類很多。"},{"en":"Lots of variety means many different types or choices.","zh":"lots of variety 指有許多不同種類或選擇。"},{"en":"A school canteen with lots of variety can serve students with different diets.","zh":"種類很多的學校飯堂可以服務有不同飲食需要的學生。"},{"en":"Variety helps customers choose something that matches their taste, budget, or health needs.","zh":"多樣選擇幫助顧客按口味、預算或健康需要選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a wide choice rather than only one or two options.","zh":"這個片語暗示選擇廣泛，而不只是有一兩種。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"brown bread","meaning":"全麥麵包","examples":[{"en":"Leon likes the brown bread himself.","zh":"Leon 自己喜歡全麥麵包。"},{"en":"Brown bread is bread made with wholemeal or darker flour, often considered healthier than white bread.","zh":"brown bread 指用全麥或較深色麵粉製成的麵包，常被視為比白麵包健康。"},{"en":"Some parents buy brown bread for breakfast because it feels more filling.","zh":"有些父母買全麥麵包作早餐，因為它感覺較飽肚。"},{"en":"Brown bread may suit people who want more fibre in their diet.","zh":"全麥麵包可能適合想在飲食中增加纖維的人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a type of bread, not bread that has simply been overcooked.","zh":"這個片語指一種麵包，而不是單純烤焦的麵包。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sounds good","meaning":"聽起來不錯","examples":[{"en":"Shannon thinks the bread sounds good.","zh":"Shannon 覺得那些麵包聽起來不錯。"},{"en":"Sounds good means the idea seems pleasant, useful, or worth trying.","zh":"sounds good 指某個想法聽起來令人喜歡、有用或值得一試。"},{"en":"A picnic in the park sounds good if the weather stays sunny.","zh":"如果天氣持續晴朗，在公園野餐聽起來不錯。"},{"en":"People say this when they approve of a suggestion based on what they have heard.","zh":"人們根據聽到的內容認同某項建議時，會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and positive.","zh":"這個片語較口語而正面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sell other things","meaning":"售賣其他東西","examples":[{"en":"The shop sells other things besides bread and vegetables.","zh":"那間店除了麵包和蔬菜外，也售賣其他東西。"},{"en":"To sell other things means to offer additional products apart from the ones already mentioned.","zh":"sell other things 指除了已提及的物品外，還提供額外產品。"},{"en":"A bookstore may sell other things such as stationery, bags, and greeting cards.","zh":"書店可能售賣其他東西，例如文具、袋和賀卡。"},{"en":"Shops that sell other useful things can save customers a second trip.","zh":"售賣其他實用物品的店舖可以讓顧客少跑一趟。"},{"en":"This phrase expands the list of what a shop provides.","zh":"這個片語擴展店舖提供的物品清單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"chocolate cake","meaning":"朱古力蛋糕","examples":[{"en":"Shannon says she loves chocolate cake.","zh":"Shannon 說她喜歡朱古力蛋糕。"},{"en":"Chocolate cake is a sweet cake made with chocolate or cocoa.","zh":"chocolate cake 指用朱古力或可可製成的甜蛋糕。"},{"en":"A family may buy chocolate cake for a birthday party.","zh":"家庭可能買朱古力蛋糕作生日派對甜品。"},{"en":"Chocolate cake is often chosen for dessert because it feels rich and celebratory.","zh":"朱古力蛋糕常被選作甜品，因為它感覺濃郁而有慶祝氣氛。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common sweet food, not a main meal.","zh":"這個片語命名一種常見甜食，而不是主餐。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a whole range of","meaning":"各式各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"The shop has a whole range of tarts.","zh":"這間店有各式各樣的撻。"},{"en":"A whole range of something means many different types of it.","zh":"a whole range of something 指有許多不同種類的某物。"},{"en":"The library offers a whole range of books for children, teenagers, and adults.","zh":"圖書館提供各式各樣的書籍給兒童、青少年和成人。"},{"en":"A whole range of choices helps customers find something suitable for different tastes.","zh":"各式各樣的選擇幫助顧客找到適合不同口味的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a complete or broad selection.","zh":"這個片語強調完整或廣泛選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tarts","meaning":"撻","examples":[{"en":"The shop sells a whole range of tarts.","zh":"這間店售賣各式各樣的撻。"},{"en":"Tarts are small or large pastries with a filling, often made with fruit, custard, or chocolate.","zh":"tarts 指有餡料的酥皮甜點，可大可小，常用水果、吉士或朱古力製成。"},{"en":"A bakery may sell egg tarts, fruit tarts, and chocolate tarts.","zh":"麵包店可能售賣蛋撻、水果撻和朱古力撻。"},{"en":"Tarts are popular for dessert because they are easy to share and look attractive.","zh":"撻作為甜品很受歡迎，因為它容易分享，而且外觀吸引。"},{"en":"This word refers to a type of pastry, not a full meal.","zh":"這個字指一種酥皮點心，而不是完整餐點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"strawberry ones","meaning":"士多啤梨味的那些","examples":[{"en":"The best tarts are the strawberry ones.","zh":"最好的撻是士多啤梨味的那些。"},{"en":"Strawberry ones means the items of that type which are made with or flavoured with strawberries.","zh":"strawberry ones 指同類物品中用士多啤梨製成或帶士多啤梨味的那些。"},{"en":"If the bakery has many cakes, I usually choose the strawberry ones.","zh":"如果麵包店有很多蛋糕，我通常選士多啤梨味的那些。"},{"en":"People use “ones” to avoid repeating the noun they have already mentioned.","zh":"人們使用 “ones” 來避免重複已提及的名詞。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare choices within the same group.","zh":"這個片語幫助比較同一組別中的選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hopefully","meaning":"希望","examples":[{"en":"Hopefully, Shannon will not have to go to the supermarket.","zh":"希望 Shannon 不需要去超市。"},{"en":"Hopefully means the speaker hopes that something will happen or be true.","zh":"hopefully 指說話者希望某事會發生或成真。"},{"en":"Hopefully, the rain will stop before the school trip begins.","zh":"希望學校旅行開始前雨會停。"},{"en":"People use this word when they want a good result but cannot fully control it.","zh":"當人們想有好結果但不能完全控制時，會使用這個字。"},{"en":"This word expresses hope, not certainty.","zh":"這個字表達希望，而不是確定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"won’t even have to","meaning":"甚至不用……","examples":[{"en":"Shannon hopes she will not even have to go to the supermarket.","zh":"Shannon 希望她甚至不用去超市。"},{"en":"Won’t even have to means will not need to do something at all, which is better or easier than expected.","zh":"won’t even have to 指完全不需要做某事，情況比預期更好或更輕鬆。"},{"en":"If we finish the project today, we won’t even have to meet on Saturday.","zh":"如果我們今天完成項目，就甚至不用星期六開會。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when avoiding an extra task feels like a relief.","zh":"當避免額外任務令人鬆一口氣時，人們會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It emphasises that the action may be unnecessary.","zh":"它強調該行動可能沒有必要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10}],"ielts/listening/Practice 7/task-2":[{"front":"children’s book festival","meaning":"兒童圖書節","examples":[{"en":"The children’s book festival is coming up again soon.","zh":"兒童圖書節很快又會舉行。"},{"en":"A children’s book festival is an event where children meet writers, enjoy stories, and join reading activities.","zh":"兒童圖書節是讓兒童見作家、享受故事和參加閱讀活動的活動。"},{"en":"A school may take pupils to a children’s book festival to help them discover new authors.","zh":"學校可能帶學生去兒童圖書節，幫助他們發現新作者。"},{"en":"A children’s book festival can encourage young readers because books feel lively and social there.","zh":"兒童圖書節可以鼓勵小讀者，因為書本在那裡變得生動而有社交感。"},{"en":"Parents may use a children’s book festival to find books that suit their child’s age and interests.","zh":"家長可能利用兒童圖書節，尋找適合孩子年齡和興趣的書。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"coming up again soon","meaning":"很快又會舉行","examples":[{"en":"The children’s book festival is coming up again soon.","zh":"兒童圖書節很快又會舉行。"},{"en":"If an event is coming up again soon, it will happen again in the near future.","zh":"如果一項活動 is coming up again soon，意思是它在不久後會再次發生。"},{"en":"The school picnic is coming up again soon, so parents should return the forms.","zh":"學校野餐很快又會舉行，所以家長應交回表格。"},{"en":"When an exam is coming up again soon, students usually start revising more seriously.","zh":"當考試很快又會舉行，學生通常會開始更認真溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for reminding people about a repeated event.","zh":"這個短語適合用來提醒人們一項再次舉行的活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"here to tell us all about","meaning":"來為我們詳細介紹……","examples":[{"en":"Jenny Morgan is here to tell us all about the festival.","zh":"Jenny Morgan 來為我們詳細介紹這個圖書節。"},{"en":"Someone is here to tell us all about something when they have come to explain it in detail.","zh":"someone is here to tell us all about something 的意思是某人來詳細解釋某事。"},{"en":"The coach is here to tell us all about the new training programme.","zh":"教練來為我們詳細介紹新的訓練計劃。"},{"en":"A speaker who tells us all about an event helps listeners know what to expect and how to join.","zh":"詳細介紹活動的講者能幫助聽眾知道可以期待甚麼以及如何參加。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used when introducing a guest on a radio show or stage.","zh":"這個短語常用於介紹電台節目或舞台上的嘉賓。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"festival organiser","meaning":"圖書節組織者","examples":[{"en":"Jenny Morgan is the festival organiser.","zh":"Jenny Morgan 是圖書節組織者。"},{"en":"A festival organiser is the person who plans, arranges, and manages a festival.","zh":"festival organiser 是負責計劃、安排和管理節日活動的人。"},{"en":"A festival organiser may book speakers, arrange rooms, and answer visitors’ questions.","zh":"圖書節組織者可能預約講者、安排場地和回答訪客問題。"},{"en":"If a festival organiser plans badly, events may start late or become confusing.","zh":"如果圖書節組織者計劃不周，活動可能遲開始或變得混亂。"},{"en":"A good festival organiser helps participants enjoy the event smoothly and safely.","zh":"好的圖書節組織者能幫助參加者順利而安全地享受活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what we can expect","meaning":"我們可以期待甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Jenny tells listeners what they can expect this year.","zh":"Jenny 告訴聽眾今年可以期待甚麼。"},{"en":"What we can expect means what is likely to happen or what will probably be provided.","zh":"what we can expect 的意思是可能會發生甚麼，或大概會提供甚麼。"},{"en":"Before a school trip, teachers explain what students can expect on the day.","zh":"學校旅行前，老師會解釋學生當天可以期待甚麼。"},{"en":"Knowing what we can expect reduces worry because people can prepare better.","zh":"知道我們可以期待甚麼能減少擔心，因為人們可以更好準備。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing plans, changes, or future events.","zh":"這個短語適合用於介紹計劃、改變或未來活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as usual","meaning":"和往年一樣","examples":[{"en":"As usual, the festival has five days of events for children.","zh":"和往年一樣，圖書節有五天兒童活動。"},{"en":"As usual means something happens in the normal or expected way.","zh":"as usual 的意思是某事按正常或預期方式發生。"},{"en":"As usual, the library opens at nine o’clock on weekdays.","zh":"和平常一樣，圖書館在平日上午九時開放。"},{"en":"When something happens as usual, people feel prepared because the routine has not changed.","zh":"當某事和平常一樣發生，人們會感到有準備，因為日常安排沒有改變。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows that an arrangement is familiar.","zh":"這個短語常表示安排是熟悉的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"five days of","meaning":"五天的……","examples":[{"en":"The festival has five days of exciting events for children.","zh":"圖書節有五天精彩的兒童活動。"},{"en":"Five days of something means the activity or programme lasts for five days.","zh":"five days of something 的意思是該活動或節目持續五天。"},{"en":"The camp offers five days of sports, games, and teamwork activities.","zh":"這個營地提供五天的運動、遊戲和團隊活動。"},{"en":"Five days of workshops can give children enough time to try different skills.","zh":"五天的工作坊可以給兒童足夠時間嘗試不同技能。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly tells readers the length of an event.","zh":"這個短語清楚告訴讀者活動長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"action-packed exciting events","meaning":"精彩豐富的活動","examples":[{"en":"The festival offers five days of action-packed exciting events.","zh":"圖書節提供五天精彩豐富的活動。"},{"en":"Action-packed exciting events are full of activities, energy, and things to do.","zh":"action-packed exciting events 是充滿活動、活力和不同事情可做的活動。"},{"en":"A school fun day with games, races, music, and shows can be action-packed.","zh":"有遊戲、比賽、音樂和表演的學校同樂日可以是精彩豐富的活動。"},{"en":"Action-packed events keep children interested because there is always something happening.","zh":"精彩豐富的活動能令兒童保持興趣，因為總有事情正在發生。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests the event will not be quiet, slow, or boring.","zh":"這個短語表示活動不會安靜、緩慢或沉悶。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"all over the country","meaning":"全國各地","examples":[{"en":"Writers are coming from all over the country.","zh":"作家會從全國各地前來。"},{"en":"All over the country means from many different places within the same country.","zh":"all over the country 的意思是來自同一國家內許多不同地方。"},{"en":"Students came from all over the country to join the national competition.","zh":"學生從全國各地前來參加全國比賽。"},{"en":"When guests come from all over the country, an event can feel more important and diverse.","zh":"當嘉賓從全國各地前來，活動會感覺更重要和更多元。"},{"en":"This phrase shows wide national participation.","zh":"這個短語顯示廣泛的全國參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get involved","meaning":"參與其中","examples":[{"en":"Writers from all over the country will get involved.","zh":"來自全國各地的作家會參與其中。"},{"en":"To get involved means to take part in an activity instead of just watching.","zh":"get involved 的意思是參加一項活動，而不是只旁觀。"},{"en":"Parents can get involved in school events by helping at booths or reading stories.","zh":"家長可以透過協助攤位或朗讀故事參與學校活動。"},{"en":"When more people get involved, an event usually has more energy and support.","zh":"當更多人參與其中，活動通常會有更多活力和支持。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to encourage participation.","zh":"這個短語常用於鼓勵人參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"just to give you an idea of","meaning":"只是為了讓你大概了解……","examples":[{"en":"Jenny introduces some workshops just to give listeners an idea of what is on offer.","zh":"Jenny 介紹一些工作坊，只是為了讓聽眾大概了解有哪些活動。"},{"en":"Just to give you an idea of something means to show a few examples so people can understand the general picture.","zh":"just to give you an idea of something 的意思是展示幾個例子，讓人理解大概情況。"},{"en":"A teacher may show one sample essay just to give students an idea of the expected style.","zh":"老師可能展示一篇範文，只是為了讓學生大概了解預期風格。"},{"en":"Giving people an idea of the options helps them decide what they want to join.","zh":"讓人了解選項的大概情況，有助他們決定想參加甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase usually introduces examples, not a complete list.","zh":"這個短語通常引出例子，而不是完整清單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what’s on offer","meaning":"提供甚麼活動；有哪些選擇","examples":[{"en":"Jenny explains what is on offer in the workshops.","zh":"Jenny 解釋工作坊提供甚麼活動。"},{"en":"What’s on offer means what activities, choices, services, or items are available.","zh":"what’s on offer 的意思是有哪些活動、選擇、服務或物品可供選擇。"},{"en":"Before choosing a summer course, parents may check what’s on offer at different centres.","zh":"選擇暑期課程前，家長可能查看不同中心有哪些選擇。"},{"en":"Knowing what’s on offer helps families compare prices, times, and activities.","zh":"知道有哪些選擇有助家庭比較價錢、時間和活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when talking about programmes, menus, and services.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論節目、餐牌和服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"first of all","meaning":"首先","examples":[{"en":"First of all, there is a very special event called Superheroes.","zh":"首先，有一個名為 Superheroes 的特別活動。"},{"en":"First of all is used to introduce the first point or item in a list.","zh":"first of all 用來引出清單中的第一點或第一項。"},{"en":"First of all, students should read the question carefully.","zh":"首先，學生應仔細閱讀題目。"},{"en":"Using first of all helps listeners follow the order of a speech or explanation.","zh":"使用 first of all 有助聽眾跟上演講或解釋的次序。"},{"en":"The phrase often signals that more points will come later.","zh":"這個短語常表示之後還會有更多要點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a very special event called","meaning":"一個名為……的特別活動","examples":[{"en":"There is a very special event called Superheroes.","zh":"有一個名為 Superheroes 的特別活動。"},{"en":"A very special event called something means an event with a particular name that is unusual or important.","zh":"a very special event called something 指一個有特定名稱、不同尋常或重要的活動。"},{"en":"The school is holding a very special event called Family Reading Night.","zh":"學校正在舉辦一個名為 Family Reading Night 的特別活動。"},{"en":"Giving an event a clear name helps people remember it and understand its theme.","zh":"給活動清楚名稱能幫助人記住它並理解其主題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a named activity.","zh":"這個短語適合用於介紹有名稱的活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a chance for someone to","meaning":"讓某人有機會……","examples":[{"en":"Superheroes is a chance for deaf children to share their reading experiences.","zh":"Superheroes 讓聽障兒童有機會分享閱讀經驗。"},{"en":"A chance for someone to do something is an opportunity for that person to do it.","zh":"a chance for someone to do something 是某人做某事的機會。"},{"en":"A class presentation gives shy students a chance to practise speaking.","zh":"課堂匯報讓害羞學生有機會練習說話。"},{"en":"When children get a chance to share ideas, they often feel more confident.","zh":"當兒童有機會分享想法，他們通常會更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights opportunity rather than obligation.","zh":"這個短語強調機會，而不是責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"deaf children","meaning":"聽障兒童","examples":[{"en":"Superheroes is a workshop for deaf children.","zh":"Superheroes 是一個為聽障兒童而設的工作坊。"},{"en":"Deaf children are children who cannot hear, or who have very limited hearing.","zh":"deaf children 是不能聽見或聽力非常有限的兒童。"},{"en":"Deaf children may use sign language, hearing aids, captions, or visual materials to learn.","zh":"聽障兒童可能使用手語、助聽器、字幕或視覺材料學習。"},{"en":"Inclusive workshops help deaf children join activities with confidence and dignity.","zh":"共融工作坊能幫助聽障兒童有信心、有尊嚴地參與活動。"},{"en":"The phrase should be used respectfully and with attention to access needs.","zh":"使用這個短語時應尊重，並注意無障礙需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"share their reading experiences with","meaning":"與……分享閱讀經驗","examples":[{"en":"Deaf children can share their reading experiences with Madeleine Gordon.","zh":"聽障兒童可以與 Madeleine Gordon 分享閱讀經驗。"},{"en":"To share reading experiences with someone means to talk about books, feelings, difficulties, and favourite parts with that person.","zh":"share reading experiences with someone 的意思是與某人談論書本、感受、困難和喜歡的部分。"},{"en":"Students may share their reading experiences with classmates after finishing a novel.","zh":"學生讀完小說後，可能與同學分享閱讀經驗。"},{"en":"Sharing reading experiences helps children realise that others may understand a story differently.","zh":"分享閱讀經驗能幫助兒童明白其他人可能以不同方式理解故事。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that reading can become a social activity.","zh":"這個短語顯示閱讀可以成為一種社交活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"author","meaning":"作者","examples":[{"en":"Madeleine Gordon is an author who is herself hearing impaired.","zh":"Madeleine Gordon 是一位本身有聽力障礙的作者。"},{"en":"An author is a person who writes books, stories, articles, or other written works.","zh":"author 是撰寫書籍、故事、文章或其他文字作品的人。"},{"en":"An author may visit a school to explain how a story was created.","zh":"作者可能到訪學校，解釋故事是如何創作的。"},{"en":"Meeting an author can encourage children because they see that real people write books.","zh":"見到作者可以鼓勵兒童，因為他們看見書本是由真人寫出來的。"},{"en":"The word usually focuses on the creator of a written text.","zh":"這個詞通常集中於文字作品的創作者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hearing impaired","meaning":"有聽力障礙的","examples":[{"en":"Madeleine Gordon is herself hearing impaired.","zh":"Madeleine Gordon 本身有聽力障礙。"},{"en":"Hearing impaired means having partial or total difficulty hearing sounds.","zh":"hearing impaired 的意思是部分或完全難以聽到聲音。"},{"en":"A hearing-impaired student may need captions, written instructions, or a seat near the teacher.","zh":"有聽力障礙的學生可能需要字幕、書面指示或坐近老師。"},{"en":"When venues support hearing-impaired visitors, more people can enjoy public events.","zh":"當場地支援有聽力障礙的訪客，更多人便能享受公共活動。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal, and many people also use “deaf” or “hard of hearing” depending on preference.","zh":"這個短語較正式，許多人也會視乎偏好使用 deaf 或 hard of hearing。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"practical workshop","meaning":"實作工作坊","examples":[{"en":"Just Do It is a practical workshop.","zh":"Just Do It 是一個實作工作坊。"},{"en":"A practical workshop is a session where people learn by doing activities, not only by listening.","zh":"practical workshop 是讓人透過做活動學習，而不只是聆聽的課節。"},{"en":"A cooking school may run a practical workshop where students prepare real dishes.","zh":"烹飪學校可能舉辦實作工作坊，讓學生準備真正菜式。"},{"en":"Practical workshops help learners remember skills because they use their hands and ideas.","zh":"實作工作坊能幫助學習者記住技能，因為他們會使用雙手和想法。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active participation.","zh":"這個短語表示主動參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"led by","meaning":"由……主持；由……帶領","examples":[{"en":"The workshop is led by the well-known illustrator Mark Keane.","zh":"這個工作坊由知名插畫家 Mark Keane 主持。"},{"en":"Led by someone means guided, taught, or managed by that person.","zh":"led by someone 的意思是由某人指導、教授或管理。"},{"en":"The school tour was led by two senior students.","zh":"學校導賞由兩名高年級學生帶領。"},{"en":"A workshop led by an expert can give participants clear advice and confidence.","zh":"由專家主持的工作坊可以給參加者清晰建議和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who is in charge of an activity.","zh":"這個短語指出誰負責一項活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"well-known illustrator","meaning":"知名插畫家","examples":[{"en":"Mark Keane is a well-known illustrator.","zh":"Mark Keane 是一位知名插畫家。"},{"en":"A well-known illustrator is an artist famous for creating pictures for books, magazines, or other texts.","zh":"well-known illustrator 是因為為書籍、雜誌或其他文字創作圖畫而出名的藝術家。"},{"en":"A well-known illustrator may be invited to teach children how pictures support stories.","zh":"知名插畫家可能獲邀教兒童圖畫如何支援故事。"},{"en":"When a well-known illustrator joins a workshop, more families may want to attend.","zh":"當知名插畫家參與工作坊，更多家庭可能想參加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both skill and public recognition.","zh":"這個短語同時描述技巧和公眾知名度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take participants on","meaning":"帶領參加者踏上……","examples":[{"en":"Mark Keane will take participants on a magical journey.","zh":"Mark Keane 會帶領參加者踏上一段奇幻旅程。"},{"en":"To take participants on a journey means to guide them through an experience, story, or activity.","zh":"take participants on a journey 的意思是引導參加者經歷一段體驗、故事或活動。"},{"en":"A museum guide can take visitors on a journey through the city’s history.","zh":"博物館導賞員可以帶領訪客踏上一段城市歷史之旅。"},{"en":"A good workshop takes participants on a clear journey from simple ideas to finished work.","zh":"好的工作坊會帶領參加者由簡單想法走向完成作品。"},{"en":"The phrase often sounds imaginative and engaging.","zh":"這個短語常帶有想像力和吸引力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a magical journey","meaning":"奇幻旅程","examples":[{"en":"The workshop takes participants on a magical journey to faraway lands.","zh":"這個工作坊帶領參加者踏上前往遙遠國度的奇幻旅程。"},{"en":"A magical journey is an imaginative experience that feels exciting, surprising, or full of wonder.","zh":"magical journey 是一種富想像力、令人興奮、驚喜或充滿奇妙感的體驗。"},{"en":"A story about dragons and hidden kingdoms can take children on a magical journey.","zh":"關於龍和隱藏王國的故事可以帶孩子踏上奇幻旅程。"},{"en":"Magical journeys encourage children to use imagination beyond ordinary daily life.","zh":"奇幻旅程鼓勵兒童運用超越日常生活的想像力。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used for stories, theatre, and creative workshops.","zh":"這個短語常用於故事、劇場和創意工作坊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"faraway lands","meaning":"遙遠國度","examples":[{"en":"Participants will imagine travelling to faraway lands.","zh":"參加者會想像前往遙遠國度。"},{"en":"Faraway lands are distant places, often imagined as exciting, strange, or adventurous.","zh":"faraway lands 是遙遠的地方，常被想像成令人興奮、陌生或充滿冒險。"},{"en":"Children may draw maps of faraway lands filled with castles, forests, and rivers.","zh":"兒童可能繪畫充滿城堡、森林和河流的遙遠國度地圖。"},{"en":"Stories about faraway lands can make young readers curious about the wider world.","zh":"關於遙遠國度的故事可以令小讀者對更廣闊世界感到好奇。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a sense of distance and adventure.","zh":"這個短語營造距離感和冒險感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"with an opportunity for","meaning":"並讓……有機會","examples":[{"en":"The workshop includes an opportunity for aspiring actors to do role play.","zh":"這個工作坊並讓有志成為演員的人有機會進行角色扮演。"},{"en":"With an opportunity for someone means giving that person a chance to do something useful or enjoyable.","zh":"with an opportunity for someone 的意思是給某人做有用或有趣事情的機會。"},{"en":"The summer camp includes an opportunity for children to try public speaking.","zh":"這個暑期營並讓兒童有機會嘗試公開演說。"},{"en":"Opportunities help learners build confidence because they practise in a real setting.","zh":"機會能幫助學習者建立信心，因為他們在真實情境中練習。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing what an activity offers.","zh":"這個短語適合用於描述活動提供甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"aspiring actors","meaning":"有志成為演員的人","examples":[{"en":"The workshop gives aspiring actors a chance to do role play.","zh":"這個工作坊讓有志成為演員的人有機會進行角色扮演。"},{"en":"Aspiring actors are people who hope to become actors in the future.","zh":"aspiring actors 是希望將來成為演員的人。"},{"en":"Aspiring actors may join drama clubs to practise voice, movement, and confidence.","zh":"有志成為演員的人可能參加戲劇學會，練習聲線、動作和自信。"},{"en":"Workshops help aspiring actors because they can try characters in a safe space.","zh":"工作坊能幫助有志成為演員的人，因為他們可以在安全空間嘗試角色。"},{"en":"The word aspiring shows ambition, not yet full professional status.","zh":"aspiring 這個詞表示志向，而不是已經完全成為專業人士。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"do some role play","meaning":"進行角色扮演","examples":[{"en":"Aspiring actors will have the opportunity to do some role play.","zh":"有志成為演員的人將有機會進行角色扮演。"},{"en":"To do some role play means to act as another person or character in a practice activity.","zh":"do some role play 的意思是在練習活動中扮演另一個人或角色。"},{"en":"Students may do some role play to practise ordering food in English.","zh":"學生可能進行角色扮演，以練習用英文點餐。"},{"en":"Role play helps learners prepare for real situations because they can make mistakes safely.","zh":"角色扮演幫助學習者準備真實情況，因為他們可以安全地犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in drama, language learning, and training.","zh":"這個短語常見於戲劇、語言學習和培訓。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"an inspiring and entertaining look at","meaning":"以鼓舞人心且有趣的方式探討……","examples":[{"en":"Count on Me is an inspiring and entertaining look at friendship.","zh":"Count on Me 以鼓舞人心且有趣的方式探討友誼。"},{"en":"An inspiring and entertaining look at a topic means a way of exploring it that encourages people and keeps them interested.","zh":"an inspiring and entertaining look at 某主題，指以令人受鼓舞並保持興趣的方式探索它。"},{"en":"A film can offer an inspiring and entertaining look at teamwork through a school sports story.","zh":"電影可以透過校園運動故事，以鼓舞人心且有趣的方式探討團隊合作。"},{"en":"When serious topics are presented in an inspiring and entertaining way, young people may listen more openly.","zh":"當嚴肅主題以鼓舞人心且有趣的方式呈現，年輕人可能更願意聆聽。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests both meaning and enjoyment.","zh":"這個短語表示內容既有意義又有趣味。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"issues of friendship","meaning":"友誼問題","examples":[{"en":"Count on Me looks at the issues of friendship for teenagers.","zh":"Count on Me 探討青少年的友誼問題。"},{"en":"Issues of friendship are problems or questions about trust, loyalty, conflict, and support between friends.","zh":"issues of friendship 是關於朋友之間信任、忠誠、衝突和支持的問題。"},{"en":"Teenagers may discuss issues of friendship when a friend feels left out.","zh":"當朋友感到被排斥，青少年可能討論友誼問題。"},{"en":"Understanding friendship issues can help young people solve arguments more kindly.","zh":"理解友誼問題可以幫助年輕人更友善地解決爭執。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that friendship can be complicated, not always easy.","zh":"這個短語顯示友誼可以很複雜，不總是容易。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"13–14-year-olds","meaning":"13至14歲青少年","examples":[{"en":"The workshop is designed for 13–14-year-olds.","zh":"這個工作坊是為13至14歲青少年設計的。"},{"en":"13–14-year-olds are young teenagers aged thirteen or fourteen.","zh":"13–14-year-olds 是十三或十四歲的年輕青少年。"},{"en":"Books for 13–14-year-olds often deal with friendship, identity, school, and growing up.","zh":"給13至14歲青少年的書常處理友誼、身份、學校和成長。"},{"en":"Activities designed for 13–14-year-olds should not feel too childish or too adult.","zh":"為13至14歲青少年設計的活動不應太幼稚，也不應太成人化。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific age group.","zh":"這個短語指出一個特定年齡組別。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"look at","meaning":"探討；審視","examples":[{"en":"The workshop looks at friendships described in popular books.","zh":"這個工作坊探討流行書籍中描寫的友誼。"},{"en":"To look at a topic means to examine, discuss, or think about it carefully.","zh":"look at 某主題的意思是仔細審視、討論或思考它。"},{"en":"A class may look at how advertisements influence children.","zh":"課堂可能探討廣告如何影響兒童。"},{"en":"Looking at a topic from different angles helps students understand it more deeply.","zh":"從不同角度審視一個主題，有助學生更深入理解它。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when introducing discussion topics.","zh":"這個短語常用於介紹討論題目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"described in","meaning":"在……中描寫的","examples":[{"en":"The workshop looks at friendships described in popular books.","zh":"這個工作坊探討流行書籍中描寫的友誼。"},{"en":"Described in a book or text means shown, explained, or presented there.","zh":"described in 書本或文本中，意思是在其中被展示、解釋或呈現。"},{"en":"The city described in the novel feels crowded, noisy, and exciting.","zh":"小說中描寫的城市感覺擁擠、嘈雜而令人興奮。"},{"en":"When a feeling is clearly described in a story, readers may recognise it in their own lives.","zh":"當故事清楚描寫一種感受，讀者可能在自己生活中認出它。"},{"en":"This phrase points to where information or images come from.","zh":"這個短語指出資訊或圖像來自哪裡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"popular books","meaning":"流行書籍","examples":[{"en":"The workshop discusses friendships in popular books.","zh":"這個工作坊討論流行書籍中的友誼。"},{"en":"Popular books are books that many people read, enjoy, or talk about.","zh":"popular books 是許多人閱讀、喜歡或討論的書。"},{"en":"Libraries often display popular books near the entrance to attract young readers.","zh":"圖書館常把流行書籍放在入口附近，以吸引小讀者。"},{"en":"Popular books can influence children because many classmates may discuss the same stories.","zh":"流行書籍可以影響兒童，因為許多同學可能討論同一故事。"},{"en":"A book can be popular because it is exciting, funny, moving, or easy to relate to.","zh":"一本書可以因刺激、搞笑、感人或容易有共鳴而流行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"compare these with","meaning":"將這些與……比較","examples":[{"en":"Participants compare these friendships with their own experiences.","zh":"參加者將這些友誼與他們自己的經驗比較。"},{"en":"To compare these with something means to look at similarities and differences between them.","zh":"compare these with something 的意思是查看這些事物與另一事物之間的相似和不同。"},{"en":"Students may compare stories in books with events in their own school lives.","zh":"學生可能將書中的故事與自己校園生活中的事件比較。"},{"en":"Comparing book friendships with real experiences can help teenagers think about their own choices.","zh":"將書本友誼與真實經驗比較，可以幫助青少年思考自己的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when connecting reading with personal reflection.","zh":"這個短語適合用於把閱讀與個人反思連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"their own experiences","meaning":"他們自己的經驗","examples":[{"en":"Participants compare book friendships with their own experiences.","zh":"參加者將書中的友誼與他們自己的經驗比較。"},{"en":"Their own experiences are the things people have personally seen, felt, or lived through.","zh":"their own experiences 是人們親自看見、感受或經歷過的事情。"},{"en":"Students write better reflections when they connect a story to their own experiences.","zh":"當學生把故事與他們自己的經驗連繫起來，反思會寫得更好。"},{"en":"Using their own experiences can make learning more meaningful and memorable.","zh":"使用他們自己的經驗可以令學習更有意義和更難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts personal life with examples from books or other people.","zh":"這個短語把個人生活與書本或他人的例子作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"part of a series of","meaning":"……系列的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Speak Up is part of a series of workshops on mental health.","zh":"Speak Up 是精神健康工作坊系列的一部分。"},{"en":"Part of a series of something means one item belongs to a connected group of events, lessons, or works.","zh":"part of a series of something 的意思是某一項屬於一組互相關連的活動、課堂或作品。"},{"en":"This lesson is part of a series of classes on public speaking.","zh":"這一課是公開演說課程系列的一部分。"},{"en":"Being part of a series helps learners build knowledge step by step.","zh":"作為系列的一部分，可以幫助學習者一步一步建立知識。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the activity is not alone but connected to others.","zh":"這個短語顯示活動不是獨立存在，而是與其他活動相連。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on the subject of","meaning":"以……為主題","examples":[{"en":"Speak Up is part of a series of workshops on the subject of mental health.","zh":"Speak Up 是以精神健康為主題的工作坊系列的一部分。"},{"en":"On the subject of something means about that topic.","zh":"on the subject of something 的意思是關於該主題。"},{"en":"The school invited a nurse to speak on the subject of healthy eating.","zh":"學校邀請護士就健康飲食這個主題演講。"},{"en":"When a workshop is on the subject of stress, students expect advice and examples about stress.","zh":"當工作坊以壓力為主題，學生會期待關於壓力的建議和例子。"},{"en":"This phrase is slightly formal and useful in announcements.","zh":"這個短語略正式，適合用於公告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mental health","meaning":"精神健康","examples":[{"en":"Speak Up is part of a series of workshops on mental health.","zh":"Speak Up 是精神健康工作坊系列的一部分。"},{"en":"Mental health is a person’s emotional and psychological well-being.","zh":"mental health 是一個人的情緒和心理健康狀態。"},{"en":"Schools support mental health by teaching students how to handle stress and ask for help.","zh":"學校透過教學生處理壓力和求助來支援精神健康。"},{"en":"Poor mental health can affect sleep, study, friendships, and confidence.","zh":"精神健康不佳可以影響睡眠、學習、友誼和信心。"},{"en":"Talking about mental health can reduce shame and help people seek support earlier.","zh":"討論精神健康可以減少羞恥感，並幫助人更早尋求支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"creative writing workshop","meaning":"創意寫作工作坊","examples":[{"en":"Speak Up is a creative writing workshop.","zh":"Speak Up 是一個創意寫作工作坊。"},{"en":"A creative writing workshop is a class where people practise writing stories, poems, or personal pieces.","zh":"creative writing workshop 是讓人練習寫故事、詩或個人作品的課堂。"},{"en":"Students may join a creative writing workshop to learn how to build characters and settings.","zh":"學生可能參加創意寫作工作坊，學習如何建立角色和背景。"},{"en":"Creative writing workshops help learners express feelings that may be hard to say directly.","zh":"創意寫作工作坊幫助學習者表達難以直接說出口的感受。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests imagination, practice, and feedback.","zh":"這個短語表示想像、練習和回饋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"encourage children to","meaning":"鼓勵兒童去……","examples":[{"en":"The workshop encourages children to describe loneliness.","zh":"這個工作坊鼓勵兒童去描述孤獨感。"},{"en":"To encourage children to do something means to support them so they feel willing or confident to do it.","zh":"encourage children to do something 的意思是支持兒童，讓他們願意或有信心去做某事。"},{"en":"Parents can encourage children to read by keeping interesting books at home.","zh":"家長可以透過在家中放置有趣書籍來鼓勵兒童閱讀。"},{"en":"Encouragement helps children try difficult tasks without feeling too afraid of mistakes.","zh":"鼓勵能幫助兒童嘗試困難任務，而不太害怕犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on gentle support, not force.","zh":"這個短語集中於溫和支持，而不是強迫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"situations where","meaning":"……的情況","examples":[{"en":"Children describe situations where young people experience loneliness.","zh":"兒童描述年輕人經歷孤獨感的情況。"},{"en":"Situations where something happens are cases or circumstances in which it occurs.","zh":"situations where something happens 是某事發生的案例或情境。"},{"en":"Teachers discuss situations where students may feel unsafe online.","zh":"老師討論學生可能在網上感到不安全的情況。"},{"en":"Naming situations where a problem appears helps people understand how to prevent it.","zh":"指出問題出現的情況，有助人們理解如何預防它。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an idea to real-life examples.","zh":"這個短語把概念與真實生活例子連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"experience loneliness","meaning":"經歷孤獨感","examples":[{"en":"Young people may experience loneliness in different situations.","zh":"年輕人可能在不同情況下經歷孤獨感。"},{"en":"To experience loneliness means to feel alone, disconnected, or not understood by others.","zh":"experience loneliness 的意思是感到孤單、與人疏離或不被理解。"},{"en":"A child may experience loneliness after moving to a new school.","zh":"小孩轉到新學校後可能經歷孤獨感。"},{"en":"Loneliness can affect confidence because young people may think nobody cares about them.","zh":"孤獨感可以影響信心，因為年輕人可能以為沒有人關心他們。"},{"en":"People can experience loneliness even when they are surrounded by others.","zh":"即使身邊有人，人也可以經歷孤獨感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"recent survey revealed that","meaning":"最近調查顯示","examples":[{"en":"A recent survey revealed that children can be lonely at home.","zh":"最近調查顯示，兒童在家中也可能感到孤單。"},{"en":"A recent survey revealed that means new research or questioning showed a particular result.","zh":"recent survey revealed that 的意思是新的研究或問卷顯示某個結果。"},{"en":"A recent survey revealed that many students sleep less before exams.","zh":"最近調查顯示，許多學生在考試前睡得較少。"},{"en":"Survey results can change public discussion because they show what people are actually experiencing.","zh":"調查結果可以改變公共討論，因為它們顯示人們實際經歷甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting findings.","zh":"這個短語適合用於報道調查發現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"even when","meaning":"即使在……的時候","examples":[{"en":"Children can be lonely even when they are at home with their families.","zh":"兒童即使與家人在家中，也可能感到孤單。"},{"en":"Even when means although a certain situation is true.","zh":"even when 的意思是即使某情況是真實的。"},{"en":"A student may feel nervous even when they have studied hard.","zh":"學生即使已努力溫習，也可能感到緊張。"},{"en":"Even when people look fine outside, they may still need support.","zh":"即使人們外表看起來沒事，他們仍可能需要支援。"},{"en":"This phrase shows contrast between what we expect and what actually happens.","zh":"這個短語顯示預期與實際情況之間的對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at home with their families","meaning":"與家人在家中","examples":[{"en":"Children may feel lonely even at home with their families.","zh":"兒童即使與家人在家中，也可能感到孤單。"},{"en":"At home with their families means being in the family home together with parents, siblings, or relatives.","zh":"at home with their families 的意思是與父母、兄弟姊妹或親人在家庭住所中。"},{"en":"A child can be physically at home with family but emotionally feel ignored.","zh":"小孩可以身體上與家人在家中，但情感上感到被忽視。"},{"en":"Spending time at home with family can reduce loneliness if people talk and listen to each other.","zh":"如果人們彼此交談和聆聽，與家人在家中共處可以減少孤獨感。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds us that being near people is not always the same as feeling connected.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，身邊有人不一定等於感到有連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as many of you will know","meaning":"很多人都知道","examples":[{"en":"As many of you will know, Jump for Joy is a best-selling story.","zh":"很多人都知道，《Jump for Joy》是一本暢銷故事書。"},{"en":"As many of you will know is used before saying something the audience probably already knows.","zh":"as many of you will know 用於說出聽眾可能已經知道的事情之前。"},{"en":"As many of you will know, our school library closes early on Fridays.","zh":"很多人都知道，我們學校圖書館逢星期五較早關門。"},{"en":"This phrase helps a speaker connect with listeners by recognising shared knowledge.","zh":"這個短語透過承認共同知識，幫助講者與聽眾連繫。"},{"en":"It is often used in talks, interviews, and announcements.","zh":"它常用於演講、訪問和公告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"heart-warming","meaning":"溫馨的","examples":[{"en":"Jump for Joy is a heart-warming story by Nina Karan.","zh":"《Jump for Joy》是 Nina Karan 寫的一個溫馨故事。"},{"en":"Heart-warming means making people feel happy, touched, or emotionally comforted.","zh":"heart-warming 的意思是令人感到開心、感動或情感上被安慰。"},{"en":"A heart-warming story about a lost dog returning home can make readers smile.","zh":"關於走失小狗回家的溫馨故事可以令讀者微笑。"},{"en":"Heart-warming books can comfort children because they show kindness and hope.","zh":"溫馨的書可以安慰兒童，因為它們展示善意和希望。"},{"en":"The word often describes stories that feel gentle and emotionally positive.","zh":"這個詞常描述感覺溫柔而情感正面的故事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"best-selling story","meaning":"暢銷故事","examples":[{"en":"Jump for Joy is a best-selling story by Nina Karan.","zh":"《Jump for Joy》是 Nina Karan 的暢銷故事。"},{"en":"A best-selling story is a story that has sold very many copies.","zh":"best-selling story 是銷量很高的故事。"},{"en":"A best-selling story may become popular because children recommend it to their friends.","zh":"暢銷故事可能因兒童推薦給朋友而變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"Strong sales can help a best-selling story reach libraries, schools, and bookshops.","zh":"強勁銷量可以幫助暢銷故事進入圖書館、學校和書店。"},{"en":"The phrase describes commercial success, not automatically literary quality.","zh":"這個短語描述商業成功，不自動等於文學質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a young girl’s trip to","meaning":"一名小女孩前往……的旅程","examples":[{"en":"The story is about a young girl’s trip to visit her relatives in India.","zh":"這個故事講述一名小女孩前往印度探望親戚的旅程。"},{"en":"A young girl’s trip to a place means a journey taken by a girl to that place.","zh":"a young girl’s trip to 某地，意思是一名小女孩前往該地的旅程。"},{"en":"A young girl’s trip to the countryside may become a story about family memories.","zh":"一名小女孩前往鄉郊的旅程，可能成為關於家庭回憶的故事。"},{"en":"Travel stories help children learn because the character discovers new places and people.","zh":"旅遊故事能幫助兒童學習，因為角色會發現新地方和新人物。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the main journey of a story.","zh":"這個短語引出故事的主要旅程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"visit her relatives","meaning":"探望她的親戚","examples":[{"en":"The girl takes a trip to visit her relatives in India.","zh":"這名女孩前往印度探望她的親戚。"},{"en":"To visit her relatives means to go and see members of her extended family.","zh":"visit her relatives 的意思是去見她的大家庭成員。"},{"en":"A child may visit her relatives during the summer holiday and learn family stories.","zh":"小孩可能在暑假探望親戚，並學到家庭故事。"},{"en":"Visiting relatives can strengthen family ties because people spend time together.","zh":"探望親戚可以加強家庭連繫，因為人們會一起相處。"},{"en":"This phrase often refers to grandparents, cousins, aunts, or uncles.","zh":"這個短語常指探望祖父母、表兄弟姊妹、姨母或叔伯等。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"received the gold medal","meaning":"獲得金獎","examples":[{"en":"The book recently received the gold medal at the Waterford Awards.","zh":"這本書最近在 Waterford Awards 獲得金獎。"},{"en":"Received the gold medal means won the highest award in a competition or ceremony.","zh":"received the gold medal 的意思是在比賽或頒獎禮中獲得最高獎項。"},{"en":"A student received the gold medal after winning the school swimming race.","zh":"一名學生贏得學校游泳比賽後獲得金獎。"},{"en":"Receiving the gold medal can bring attention to a book, athlete, or team.","zh":"獲得金獎可以為書本、運動員或團隊帶來關注。"},{"en":"The phrase shows achievement and recognition.","zh":"這個短語顯示成就和認可。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get children to","meaning":"讓兒童去……","examples":[{"en":"Nina will get children to celebrate the word joy.","zh":"Nina 會讓兒童去歌頌 joy 這個詞。"},{"en":"To get children to do something means to make, help, or encourage them to do it.","zh":"get children to do something 的意思是令、幫助或鼓勵兒童去做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may get children to act out a scene from a story.","zh":"老師可能讓兒童去演出故事中的一幕。"},{"en":"Getting children to join an activity works best when the task feels fun and clear.","zh":"當任務有趣而清晰，讓兒童參與活動效果最好。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes guiding children into action.","zh":"這個短語常描述引導兒童行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"celebrate the word","meaning":"歌頌這個詞","examples":[{"en":"Children will celebrate the word joy by writing a poem.","zh":"兒童會透過寫詩歌頌 joy 這個詞。"},{"en":"To celebrate a word means to explore, praise, and express the feeling or idea behind it.","zh":"celebrate a word 的意思是探索、讚美和表達這個詞背後的感覺或概念。"},{"en":"Students may celebrate the word kindness by writing notes to classmates.","zh":"學生可能透過寫便條給同學來歌頌 kindness 這個詞。"},{"en":"Celebrating a word helps children think about meaning, emotion, and personal examples.","zh":"歌頌一個詞能幫助兒童思考意思、情感和個人例子。"},{"en":"This phrase is creative and often used in writing activities.","zh":"這個短語富創意，常用於寫作活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"by writing a poem","meaning":"透過寫詩","examples":[{"en":"Children will celebrate joy by writing a poem.","zh":"兒童會透過寫詩歌頌快樂。"},{"en":"By writing a poem means through the act of creating a short piece of imaginative writing.","zh":"by writing a poem 的意思是透過創作一篇短小而富想像力的文字作品。"},{"en":"A child may express sadness by writing a poem about rain.","zh":"小孩可能透過寫一首關於雨的詩來表達悲傷。"},{"en":"Writing a poem can help children organise feelings into words and images.","zh":"寫詩可以幫助兒童把感受整理成文字和圖像。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the method used to achieve the activity’s goal.","zh":"這個短語顯示達成活動目標的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"beautifully illustrated picture book","meaning":"插圖精美的繪本","examples":[{"en":"Sticks and Stones is a beautifully illustrated picture book.","zh":"《Sticks and Stones》是一本插圖精美的繪本。"},{"en":"A beautifully illustrated picture book is a children’s book with attractive pictures that help tell the story.","zh":"beautifully illustrated picture book 是一本有吸引插圖並用圖畫幫助講故事的兒童書。"},{"en":"A beautifully illustrated picture book can help young readers understand the plot before they read every word.","zh":"插圖精美的繪本可以幫助小讀者在讀懂每個字前理解情節。"},{"en":"Strong illustrations make a picture book more memorable because children connect words with images.","zh":"出色插圖令繪本更難忘，因為兒童會把文字與圖像連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase praises both the artwork and the book format.","zh":"這個短語同時稱讚圖畫和書本形式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"young readers","meaning":"小讀者","examples":[{"en":"The picture book is written for young readers.","zh":"這本繪本是為小讀者而寫的。"},{"en":"Young readers are children who are learning to read or who are still developing reading skills.","zh":"young readers 是正在學習閱讀或仍在發展閱讀能力的兒童。"},{"en":"Books for young readers often use clear sentences, pictures, and familiar situations.","zh":"給小讀者的書通常使用清晰句子、圖畫和熟悉情境。"},{"en":"Supporting young readers early can build confidence and long-term reading habits.","zh":"早期支援小讀者可以建立信心和長期閱讀習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the intended age and reading level.","zh":"這個短語指出目標年齡和閱讀程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a community who organise","meaning":"一個舉辦……的社區","examples":[{"en":"The story is about a community who organise an African-Caribbean festival.","zh":"這個故事講述一個舉辦非洲加勒比節的社區。"},{"en":"A community who organise an event is a group of local people who plan and run it together.","zh":"a community who organise an event 指一群本地人一起計劃和舉辦活動。"},{"en":"A community who organise a street fair may ask neighbours to cook, decorate, and perform.","zh":"一個舉辦街坊市集的社區，可能請鄰居煮食、裝飾和表演。"},{"en":"When a community organises an event, people often feel more connected and proud.","zh":"當社區舉辦活動，人們通常會感到更有連繫和自豪。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights collective effort.","zh":"這個短語強調集體努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"African-Caribbean festival","meaning":"非洲加勒比節","examples":[{"en":"The community organise an African-Caribbean festival.","zh":"這個社區舉辦非洲加勒比節。"},{"en":"An African-Caribbean festival celebrates cultures connected to Africa and the Caribbean through music, food, dance, and stories.","zh":"African-Caribbean festival 是透過音樂、食物、舞蹈和故事慶祝與非洲及加勒比文化有關的節日。"},{"en":"Children may learn about history and identity at an African-Caribbean festival.","zh":"兒童可能在非洲加勒比節中了解歷史和身份。"},{"en":"Cultural festivals can strengthen pride because people see their heritage celebrated publicly.","zh":"文化節可以加強自豪感，因為人們看見自己的文化遺產被公開慶祝。"},{"en":"This phrase names a festival with a specific cultural focus.","zh":"這個短語命名一個有特定文化焦點的節日。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"local children","meaning":"本地兒童","examples":[{"en":"The festival helps local children learn about their Jamaican roots.","zh":"這個節日幫助本地兒童了解他們的牙買加根源。"},{"en":"Local children are children who live in the nearby area or community.","zh":"local children 是住在附近地區或社區的兒童。"},{"en":"A library may invite local children to join reading games after school.","zh":"圖書館可能邀請本地兒童放學後參加閱讀遊戲。"},{"en":"Activities for local children can build community because families meet one another.","zh":"為本地兒童而設的活動可以建立社區感，因為家庭會彼此認識。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on children from the surrounding neighbourhood.","zh":"這個短語集中於周邊社區的兒童。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"learn about","meaning":"了解……","examples":[{"en":"The festival helps children learn about their Jamaican roots.","zh":"這個節日幫助兒童了解他們的牙買加根源。"},{"en":"To learn about something means to gain knowledge or understanding of it.","zh":"learn about something 的意思是取得關於某事的知識或理解。"},{"en":"Students learn about recycling by visiting a waste centre.","zh":"學生透過參觀廢物處理中心了解回收。"},{"en":"Learning about family history can help children understand who they are.","zh":"了解家庭歷史可以幫助兒童明白自己是誰。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple and useful for education, culture, and daily life.","zh":"這個短語簡單，適用於教育、文化和日常生活。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Jamaican roots","meaning":"牙買加根源","examples":[{"en":"The children learn about their Jamaican roots.","zh":"兒童了解他們的牙買加根源。"},{"en":"Jamaican roots are a person’s family, cultural, or historical connections to Jamaica.","zh":"Jamaican roots 是一個人與牙買加在家庭、文化或歷史上的連繫。"},{"en":"A child may explore Jamaican roots through food, music, language, and family stories.","zh":"小孩可能透過食物、音樂、語言和家庭故事探索牙買加根源。"},{"en":"Learning about roots can help young people feel proud of where their family comes from.","zh":"了解根源可以幫助年輕人為自己家庭來源感到自豪。"},{"en":"The phrase connects identity with heritage.","zh":"這個短語把身份與文化傳承連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"musical event","meaning":"音樂活動","examples":[{"en":"This will be a musical event where children can play steel drums.","zh":"這會是一個音樂活動，兒童可以演奏鋼鼓。"},{"en":"A musical event is an activity centred on music, performance, singing, or instruments.","zh":"musical event 是以音樂、表演、歌唱或樂器為中心的活動。"},{"en":"A school musical event may include choir singing, drumming, and student performances.","zh":"學校音樂活動可能包括合唱、打鼓和學生表演。"},{"en":"Musical events can bring people together because rhythm and songs are easy to share.","zh":"音樂活動可以把人聚在一起，因為節奏和歌曲容易分享。"},{"en":"This phrase tells us that music is the main feature.","zh":"這個短語告訴我們音樂是主要特色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have the chance to","meaning":"有機會……","examples":[{"en":"Children will have the chance to play steel drums.","zh":"兒童將有機會演奏鋼鼓。"},{"en":"To have the chance to do something means to get an opportunity to do it.","zh":"have the chance to do something 的意思是得到做某事的機會。"},{"en":"Students may have the chance to meet an author at a book fair.","zh":"學生可能有機會在書展見到作者。"},{"en":"Having the chance to try something new can build confidence and curiosity.","zh":"有機會嘗試新事物可以建立信心和好奇心。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a positive opportunity.","zh":"這個短語表示正面的機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"play steel drums","meaning":"演奏鋼鼓","examples":[{"en":"Children will have the chance to play steel drums.","zh":"兒童將有機會演奏鋼鼓。"},{"en":"To play steel drums means to make music on metal percussion instruments often linked with Caribbean music.","zh":"play steel drums 的意思是在常與加勒比音樂有關的金屬敲擊樂器上演奏音樂。"},{"en":"Children may play steel drums in a workshop after learning simple rhythms.","zh":"兒童學習簡單節奏後，可能在工作坊中演奏鋼鼓。"},{"en":"Playing steel drums can help children feel rhythm physically and enjoy group music-making.","zh":"演奏鋼鼓可以幫助兒童用身體感受節奏，並享受集體音樂創作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes playing a specific musical instrument.","zh":"這個短語描述演奏一種特定樂器。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be bound to be","meaning":"一定會……","examples":[{"en":"This event is bound to be very popular.","zh":"這個活動一定會非常受歡迎。"},{"en":"If something is bound to be a certain way, it is almost certain to be that way.","zh":"如果某事 is bound to be 某種情況，意思是它幾乎肯定會那樣。"},{"en":"A free concert by a famous singer is bound to be crowded.","zh":"著名歌手的免費音樂會一定會很擠迫。"},{"en":"An event is bound to be popular when it is fun, free, and suitable for families.","zh":"當活動有趣、免費又適合家庭，它一定會受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong expectation.","zh":"這個短語表示強烈預期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"book as soon as possible","meaning":"盡快預訂","examples":[{"en":"Parents should book as soon as possible.","zh":"家長應盡快預訂。"},{"en":"To book as soon as possible means to reserve a place quickly before spaces run out.","zh":"book as soon as possible 的意思是在名額滿之前快速預留位置。"},{"en":"Families should book as soon as possible if a workshop has only twenty seats.","zh":"如果工作坊只有二十個座位，家庭應盡快預訂。"},{"en":"Booking early prevents disappointment because popular activities may fill up fast.","zh":"早點預訂可以避免失望，因為受歡迎活動可能很快爆滿。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in event announcements.","zh":"這個短語常用於活動公告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sounds really interesting","meaning":"聽起來很有趣","examples":[{"en":"The presenter says that all the events sound really interesting.","zh":"主持人說所有活動聽起來很有趣。"},{"en":"Sounds really interesting means something seems attractive or worth learning more about.","zh":"sounds really interesting 的意思是某事似乎吸引或值得了解更多。"},{"en":"A science workshop sounds really interesting if children can build their own robots.","zh":"如果兒童可以自己製作機械人，科學工作坊聽起來會很有趣。"},{"en":"When an activity sounds interesting, more people may ask questions or sign up.","zh":"當活動聽起來有趣，更多人可能會提問或報名。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a positive first reaction.","zh":"這個短語表達正面的第一反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"I’m just wondering if","meaning":"我只是想知道是否……","examples":[{"en":"The presenter is just wondering if Jenny has a favourite book to recommend.","zh":"主持人只是想知道 Jenny 是否有最喜歡的書可以推薦。"},{"en":"I’m just wondering if is a polite way to introduce a question or request.","zh":"I’m just wondering if 是禮貌地引出問題或請求的方法。"},{"en":"I’m just wondering if you could help me find this book.","zh":"我只是想知道你是否可以幫我找這本書。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a question sound softer and less direct.","zh":"這個短語令問題聽起來較柔和、不那麼直接。"},{"en":"It is useful in interviews, emails, and everyday conversations.","zh":"它適用於訪問、電郵和日常對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"favourite book","meaning":"最喜歡的書","examples":[{"en":"The presenter asks Jenny about her favourite book.","zh":"主持人問 Jenny 關於她最喜歡的書。"},{"en":"A favourite book is a book someone likes more than most others.","zh":"favourite book 是某人比大多數其他書更喜歡的書。"},{"en":"A child’s favourite book may be the one they ask to hear every night.","zh":"小孩最喜歡的書可能是他每晚都要求聽的那一本。"},{"en":"Favourite books can shape reading habits because people return to them again and again.","zh":"最喜歡的書可以塑造閱讀習慣，因為人們會一再回到它們。"},{"en":"The phrase is personal because different readers love different things.","zh":"這個短語很個人，因為不同讀者喜歡不同東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"recommend for","meaning":"推薦給……","examples":[{"en":"Jenny recommends a book for the listeners’ children.","zh":"Jenny 推薦一本書給聽眾的孩子。"},{"en":"To recommend something for someone means to suggest it because it suits that person’s needs or interests.","zh":"recommend something for someone 的意思是因某物適合某人的需要或興趣而建議它。"},{"en":"A librarian may recommend funny books for children who dislike serious stories.","zh":"圖書館員可能推薦搞笑書給不喜歡嚴肅故事的兒童。"},{"en":"Good recommendations save time because readers do not have to search blindly.","zh":"好推薦可以節省時間，因為讀者不用盲目尋找。"},{"en":"This phrase connects advice with a particular person or group.","zh":"這個短語把建議與特定人物或群體連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hard to choose","meaning":"很難選擇","examples":[{"en":"Jenny says it is hard to choose a favourite book.","zh":"Jenny 說很難選擇一本最喜歡的書。"},{"en":"Hard to choose means difficult to decide between several good options.","zh":"hard to choose 的意思是在幾個好選項之間很難決定。"},{"en":"It can be hard to choose a birthday gift when a child likes many things.","zh":"當小孩喜歡很多東西，生日禮物可能很難選擇。"},{"en":"Too many attractive choices can make it hard to choose quickly.","zh":"太多吸引選擇會令人很難快速選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when all options seem good.","zh":"當所有選項都看似不錯時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"definitely worth mentioning","meaning":"絕對值得一提","examples":[{"en":"Alive and Kicking is definitely worth mentioning.","zh":"《Alive and Kicking》絕對值得一提。"},{"en":"Definitely worth mentioning means clearly important or interesting enough to talk about.","zh":"definitely worth mentioning 的意思是明顯重要或有趣到值得談論。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement is definitely worth mentioning if they worked hard for months.","zh":"如果學生努力了幾個月，他的進步絕對值得一提。"},{"en":"Mentioning something worthwhile helps listeners notice what should not be overlooked.","zh":"提及值得一提的事物，可以幫助聽眾注意到不應忽略的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase gives strong positive emphasis.","zh":"這個短語帶有強烈正面強調。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"won’t have heard of","meaning":"可能未聽過","examples":[{"en":"Listeners probably will not have heard of the writer.","zh":"聽眾可能未聽過這位作家。"},{"en":"Won’t have heard of someone means probably do not know that person’s name or work.","zh":"won’t have heard of someone 的意思是可能不知道某人的名字或作品。"},{"en":"You may not have heard of a new author if her first book has just been published.","zh":"如果新作者的第一本書剛出版，你可能未聽過她。"},{"en":"When people have not heard of a writer, a recommendation can help them become curious.","zh":"當人們未聽過一位作家，推薦可以令他們產生好奇。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used before introducing someone less famous.","zh":"這個短語常用於介紹較不出名的人之前。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"first book","meaning":"第一本書","examples":[{"en":"Alive and Kicking is the writer’s first book.","zh":"《Alive and Kicking》是這位作家的第一本書。"},{"en":"A first book is the first work an author has published as a book.","zh":"first book 是作者第一次以書本形式出版的作品。"},{"en":"A writer’s first book may show fresh ideas even if the author is not famous yet.","zh":"作家的第一本書可能展現新鮮想法，即使作者仍未出名。"},{"en":"Publishing a first book can be impressive because the writer has completed a major project.","zh":"出版第一本書可以令人印象深刻，因為作者完成了一個重大項目。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the beginning of an author’s career.","zh":"這個短語突出了作者職業生涯的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"really impressive","meaning":"真的令人印象深刻","examples":[{"en":"The fact that this is her first book is really impressive.","zh":"這是她的第一本書這件事真的令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"Really impressive means very good, surprising, or worthy of admiration.","zh":"really impressive 的意思是非常好、令人驚訝或值得欣賞。"},{"en":"A child’s first speech in English can be really impressive if it is clear and confident.","zh":"如果小孩第一次用英文演講清晰又自信，真的會令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"Hard work makes an achievement more impressive because people see the effort behind it.","zh":"努力令成就更令人印象深刻，因為人們看見背後付出的努力。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong praise.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈讚賞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"teenage diary","meaning":"青少年日記","examples":[{"en":"The book is basically the teenage diary of a boy from Somalia.","zh":"這本書基本上是一名來自索馬里的男孩的青少年日記。"},{"en":"A teenage diary is a personal record written from the viewpoint of a teenager.","zh":"teenage diary 是從青少年角度寫下的個人記錄。"},{"en":"A teenage diary may describe school, friends, family worries, and private feelings.","zh":"青少年日記可能描述學校、朋友、家庭憂慮和私人感受。"},{"en":"Diaries can feel honest because readers see events through the writer’s own voice.","zh":"日記可以感覺真誠，因為讀者透過作者自己的聲音看見事件。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a personal and informal writing style.","zh":"這個短語表示個人化和非正式的寫作風格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"come to live in","meaning":"來……生活","examples":[{"en":"The boy comes to live in the UK.","zh":"這名男孩來英國生活。"},{"en":"To come to live in a place means to move there and make it one’s home.","zh":"come to live in 某地的意思是搬到那裡並把它當成家。"},{"en":"A family may come to live in a new country for work or safety.","zh":"一個家庭可能因工作或安全而來到新國家生活。"},{"en":"Coming to live in a new place can create challenges such as language, school, and friendship.","zh":"來新地方生活可以帶來語言、學校和友誼等挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on settling somewhere, not just visiting.","zh":"這個短語集中於在某地定居，而不只是探訪。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"deal with","meaning":"處理；探討","examples":[{"en":"The book deals with the serious issue of immigration.","zh":"這本書探討移民這個嚴肅議題。"},{"en":"To deal with a topic means to discuss, handle, or explore it.","zh":"deal with 某主題的意思是討論、處理或探索它。"},{"en":"A school talk may deal with bullying and how students can ask for help.","zh":"學校講座可能處理欺凌以及學生如何求助。"},{"en":"Books that deal with difficult topics can help readers understand real problems.","zh":"探討困難主題的書可以幫助讀者理解真實問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when describing what a book, film, or lesson is about.","zh":"這個短語常用於描述書、電影或課堂內容。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"serious issue of immigration","meaning":"移民這個嚴肅議題","examples":[{"en":"The book deals with the serious issue of immigration.","zh":"這本書探討移民這個嚴肅議題。"},{"en":"The serious issue of immigration means the important and difficult topic of people moving to live in another country.","zh":"serious issue of immigration 指人們搬到另一個國家生活這個重要而困難的題目。"},{"en":"A class may discuss the serious issue of immigration through stories about new students.","zh":"課堂可能透過新學生的故事討論移民這個嚴肅議題。"},{"en":"Immigration can be serious because it affects language, housing, jobs, identity, and belonging.","zh":"移民之所以嚴肅，是因為它影響語言、住屋、工作、身份和歸屬感。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the topic needs careful thought.","zh":"這個短語顯示該主題需要仔細思考。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"challenges someone has to face","meaning":"某人必須面對的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"The book describes the challenges the boy has to face.","zh":"這本書描述這名男孩必須面對的挑戰。"},{"en":"Challenges someone has to face are difficult situations or problems that person must deal with.","zh":"challenges someone has to face 是某人必須處理的困難情況或問題。"},{"en":"A new student may face challenges such as making friends and understanding school rules.","zh":"新學生可能面對交朋友和理解校規等挑戰。"},{"en":"Facing challenges can be stressful, but support from others can make them easier.","zh":"面對挑戰可能有壓力，但他人的支持可以令它們較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights difficulty and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語突出了困難和責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"language barrier","meaning":"語言障礙","examples":[{"en":"The boy has to deal with the language barrier at school.","zh":"這名男孩必須在學校處理語言障礙。"},{"en":"A language barrier is a difficulty in communication because people do not share the same language well enough.","zh":"language barrier 是因人們沒有足夠共同語言而產生的溝通困難。"},{"en":"A new student may face a language barrier when teachers speak too quickly.","zh":"當老師說話太快，新學生可能面對語言障礙。"},{"en":"Language barriers can make people feel lonely because they cannot explain themselves easily.","zh":"語言障礙可以令人感到孤單，因為他們不能容易地表達自己。"},{"en":"Pictures, translation tools, and patient classmates can reduce a language barrier.","zh":"圖片、翻譯工具和有耐性的同學可以減少語言障礙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cry with laughter","meaning":"笑到流淚","examples":[{"en":"The book made Jenny cry with laughter.","zh":"這本書令 Jenny 笑到流淚。"},{"en":"To cry with laughter means to laugh so much that tears come out.","zh":"cry with laughter 的意思是笑得太厲害，以致眼淚流出來。"},{"en":"A funny cartoon may make children cry with laughter.","zh":"搞笑漫畫可能令兒童笑到流淚。"},{"en":"Humour can make a serious story easier to read because readers cry with laughter as well as think deeply.","zh":"幽默可以令嚴肅故事較容易閱讀，因為讀者會笑到流淚，也會深入思考。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is extremely funny.","zh":"這個短語表示某事非常搞笑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on each page","meaning":"每一頁上","examples":[{"en":"On each page, there are black and white stick drawings.","zh":"每一頁上都有黑白火柴人畫。"},{"en":"On each page means on every page of a book or document.","zh":"on each page 的意思是在書本或文件的每一頁上。"},{"en":"A children’s dictionary may put a picture on each page to help young readers.","zh":"兒童字典可能在每一頁上放一幅圖，以幫助小讀者。"},{"en":"Repeated features on each page can make a book easier for children to follow.","zh":"每一頁上的重複特色可以令兒童更容易跟上書本內容。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where something appears throughout a book.","zh":"這個短語描述某物在整本書中出現的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"simple but hilarious","meaning":"簡單但非常搞笑","examples":[{"en":"The drawings are simple but hilarious.","zh":"這些圖畫簡單但非常搞笑。"},{"en":"Simple but hilarious means easy in style but extremely funny.","zh":"simple but hilarious 的意思是風格簡單，但非常有趣。"},{"en":"A quick cartoon face can be simple but hilarious if it captures a silly expression.","zh":"如果一張快速畫出的卡通臉捕捉到滑稽表情，它可以簡單但非常搞笑。"},{"en":"Simple humour works well for children because they understand it quickly.","zh":"簡單幽默對兒童很有效，因為他們能很快理解。"},{"en":"The phrase shows contrast between plain appearance and strong comic effect.","zh":"這個短語顯示樸素外表與強烈搞笑效果之間的對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"black and white","meaning":"黑白的","examples":[{"en":"The book has black and white drawings.","zh":"這本書有黑白圖畫。"},{"en":"Black and white drawings use only black, white, and shades of grey, not colour.","zh":"black and white drawings 使用黑、白和灰階，而不是彩色。"},{"en":"A comic can be powerful even with simple black and white pictures.","zh":"漫畫即使只有簡單黑白圖畫，也可以很有力量。"},{"en":"Black and white illustrations may make printing cheaper and the style clearer.","zh":"黑白插圖可能令印刷成本較低，也令風格更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺外觀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stick drawings","meaning":"火柴人畫","examples":[{"en":"The book contains stick drawings of the boy with his friends and teachers.","zh":"這本書包含這名男孩與朋友和老師的火柴人畫。"},{"en":"Stick drawings are simple pictures of people made with lines for bodies, arms, and legs.","zh":"stick drawings 是用線條畫身體、手臂和雙腿的簡單人物畫。"},{"en":"Children often use stick drawings when they first draw family members.","zh":"兒童最初畫家庭成員時，常使用火柴人畫。"},{"en":"Stick drawings can be funny because their simplicity leaves room for imagination.","zh":"火柴人畫可以很好笑，因為其簡單風格留下想像空間。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a very simple drawing style.","zh":"這個短語指一種非常簡單的繪畫風格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"diary entry","meaning":"日記篇章","examples":[{"en":"There are new English words at the end of each diary entry.","zh":"每篇日記篇章結尾都有新的英文字。"},{"en":"A diary entry is one piece of writing in a diary, usually about a particular day or event.","zh":"diary entry 是日記中的一篇文字，通常關於某一天或某件事。"},{"en":"A student may write a diary entry about their first day at a new school.","zh":"學生可能寫一篇關於新學校第一天的日記篇章。"},{"en":"Diary entries help readers understand a character’s private thoughts and feelings.","zh":"日記篇章幫助讀者理解角色的私人想法和感受。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in personal writing and school assignments.","zh":"這個短語常見於個人寫作和學校功課。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"develop children’s vocabulary","meaning":"擴展兒童詞彙量","examples":[{"en":"The new words may help develop children’s vocabulary.","zh":"這些新詞可能有助擴展兒童詞彙量。"},{"en":"To develop children’s vocabulary means to help children learn and use more words.","zh":"develop children’s vocabulary 的意思是幫助兒童學習和使用更多詞語。"},{"en":"Reading aloud can develop children’s vocabulary because they hear words beyond daily speech.","zh":"朗讀可以擴展兒童詞彙量，因為他們會聽到日常說話以外的詞語。"},{"en":"A wider vocabulary helps children understand books, lessons, and conversations more easily.","zh":"更廣的詞彙量能幫助兒童更容易理解書本、課堂和對話。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in education and language learning.","zh":"這個短語常用於教育和語言學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"advice for parents","meaning":"給父母的建議","examples":[{"en":"The presenter asks for advice for parents.","zh":"主持人請對方給父母一些建議。"},{"en":"Advice for parents is guidance that helps mothers, fathers, or carers support their children.","zh":"advice for parents 是幫助父母或照顧者支援孩子的指引。"},{"en":"A teacher may give advice for parents on how to build a reading routine.","zh":"老師可能給父母關於如何建立閱讀習慣的建議。"},{"en":"Good advice for parents can reduce confusion because families know what to try at home.","zh":"好的給父母的建議可以減少困惑，因為家庭知道在家可以嘗試甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in education, health, and childcare discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於教育、健康和育兒討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"encourage their children to read more","meaning":"鼓勵子女多閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Parents want to encourage their children to read more.","zh":"父母想鼓勵子女多閱讀。"},{"en":"To encourage children to read more means to help them build a stronger habit of reading.","zh":"encourage children to read more 的意思是幫助兒童建立更強的閱讀習慣。"},{"en":"Parents can encourage their children to read more by visiting libraries together.","zh":"父母可以透過一起去圖書館來鼓勵子女多閱讀。"},{"en":"Children read more when books feel enjoyable rather than like punishment.","zh":"當書本感覺有趣而不是懲罰，兒童會閱讀更多。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on support and motivation, not pressure.","zh":"這個短語集中於支持和動機，而不是壓力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get asked about","meaning":"經常被問及……","examples":[{"en":"Jenny gets asked about reading a lot.","zh":"Jenny 經常被問及閱讀。"},{"en":"To get asked about something means people often ask you questions on that topic.","zh":"get asked about something 的意思是人們常就某個題目問你問題。"},{"en":"A doctor may get asked about sleep by worried parents.","zh":"醫生可能經常被憂心的父母問及睡眠。"},{"en":"If someone gets asked about a topic often, they are probably seen as knowledgeable.","zh":"如果某人經常被問及一個題目，他很可能被視為有相關知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when describing repeated questions.","zh":"這個短語常用於描述反覆出現的問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"so many distractions","meaning":"太多令人分心的事物","examples":[{"en":"There are so many distractions for children these days.","zh":"現今兒童有太多令人分心的事物。"},{"en":"So many distractions means there are many things that take attention away from what someone should be doing.","zh":"so many distractions 的意思是有許多東西把人的注意力從應做的事情上拉走。"},{"en":"Phones, games, videos, and messages can be distractions during homework time.","zh":"電話、遊戲、影片和訊息都可以在做功課時成為令人分心的事物。"},{"en":"Too many distractions can make reading harder because children keep losing focus.","zh":"太多令人分心的事物可以令閱讀更困難，因為兒童會不斷失去專注。"},{"en":"This phrase often explains why concentration is difficult.","zh":"這個短語常解釋為何集中很困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"these days","meaning":"現今；如今","examples":[{"en":"Children have many distractions these days.","zh":"現今兒童有許多令人分心的事物。"},{"en":"These days means nowadays or in the present time.","zh":"these days 的意思是如今或現在這個時代。"},{"en":"These days, many students use tablets for homework.","zh":"現今，許多學生使用平板電腦做功課。"},{"en":"Saying these days often compares the present with the past.","zh":"說 these days 常是在把現在與過去作比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday speech.","zh":"這個短語常見於日常說話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hard to find time for","meaning":"很難抽時間做……","examples":[{"en":"It can be hard to find time for reading.","zh":"要抽時間閱讀可能很難。"},{"en":"Hard to find time for something means difficult to make space for it in a busy schedule.","zh":"hard to find time for something 的意思是在忙碌日程中很難騰出時間做某事。"},{"en":"Parents may find it hard to find time for exercise after work.","zh":"父母下班後可能很難抽時間做運動。"},{"en":"When life is busy, important habits may disappear unless people plan time for them.","zh":"當生活忙碌，重要習慣若沒有安排時間，可能會消失。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights lack of time, not lack of interest.","zh":"這個短語強調缺乏時間，而不是缺乏興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make time to","meaning":"抽時間去……","examples":[{"en":"Parents should make time to read with their children.","zh":"父母應抽時間與子女一起閱讀。"},{"en":"To make time to do something means to deliberately set aside time for it.","zh":"make time to do something 的意思是刻意留出時間做某事。"},{"en":"Students should make time to revise before the exam week begins.","zh":"學生應在考試週開始前抽時間溫習。"},{"en":"Making time for reading shows children that books are important in family life.","zh":"抽時間閱讀能向兒童顯示書本在家庭生活中很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active planning.","zh":"這個短語表示主動規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sit down with","meaning":"與……坐下來","examples":[{"en":"Parents should sit down with their children and share books.","zh":"父母應與子女坐下來，一起閱讀書籍。"},{"en":"To sit down with someone means to spend time together, usually to talk, read, or work on something.","zh":"sit down with someone 的意思是與某人一起花時間，通常是交談、閱讀或處理事情。"},{"en":"A parent may sit down with a child to help with difficult homework.","zh":"家長可能與孩子坐下來，幫助他完成困難功課。"},{"en":"Sitting down with children regularly can make them feel noticed and supported.","zh":"定期與孩子坐下來，可以令他們感到被看見和被支持。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests personal attention and shared time.","zh":"這個短語表示個人關注和共同時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"share books with","meaning":"與……一起閱讀書籍","examples":[{"en":"Parents should share books with their children.","zh":"父母應與子女一起閱讀書籍。"},{"en":"To share books with someone means to read, discuss, or enjoy books together.","zh":"share books with someone 的意思是與某人一起閱讀、討論或享受書本。"},{"en":"Older siblings can share books with younger children by reading aloud.","zh":"兄姊可以透過朗讀，與年幼孩子一起閱讀書籍。"},{"en":"Sharing books builds family bonds because stories create common memories.","zh":"一起閱讀書籍可以建立家庭連繫，因為故事會創造共同回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase makes reading sound social, not lonely.","zh":"這個短語令閱讀聽起來像社交活動，而不是孤單活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"give up reading aloud to","meaning":"放棄朗讀給……聽","examples":[{"en":"Many parents give up reading aloud to their children too soon.","zh":"許多父母太早放棄朗讀給子女聽。"},{"en":"To give up reading aloud to children means to stop reading books to them in spoken form.","zh":"give up reading aloud to children 的意思是停止以口頭形式讀書給兒童聽。"},{"en":"Some parents give up reading aloud once their child can read simple books alone.","zh":"有些父母在孩子能獨自讀簡單書後，就放棄朗讀給他們聽。"},{"en":"Giving up too soon may reduce children’s exposure to richer language.","zh":"太早放棄可能減少兒童接觸更豐富語言的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stopping a helpful habit.","zh":"這個短語描述停止一個有幫助的習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as soon as","meaning":"一……就……","examples":[{"en":"Some parents stop reading aloud as soon as their children can read independently.","zh":"有些父母在子女一能獨立閱讀，就停止朗讀給他們聽。"},{"en":"As soon as means immediately after something happens.","zh":"as soon as 的意思是某事一發生，另一事就立即發生。"},{"en":"Call me as soon as you arrive at the station.","zh":"你一到車站就打電話給我。"},{"en":"If parents stop reading aloud as soon as children can read, children may miss harder vocabulary.","zh":"如果父母在孩子一能閱讀就停止朗讀，孩子可能錯過較難詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one action follows another very quickly.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個行動很快跟隨另一個行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"read independently","meaning":"獨立閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Some children learn to read independently.","zh":"有些兒童學會獨立閱讀。"},{"en":"To read independently means to read without needing another person to help with every word.","zh":"read independently 的意思是不需要別人幫助每個字也能閱讀。"},{"en":"A child who reads independently can choose a book and follow the story alone.","zh":"能獨立閱讀的兒童可以自己選一本書並跟上故事。"},{"en":"Independent reading builds confidence because children feel they can handle books by themselves.","zh":"獨立閱讀能建立信心，因為兒童感到自己能處理書本。"},{"en":"Children can read independently and still enjoy being read to.","zh":"兒童可以獨立閱讀，同時仍享受別人朗讀給他們聽。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"this is a mistake","meaning":"這是一個錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Jenny says stopping reading aloud too early is a mistake.","zh":"Jenny 說太早停止朗讀是一個錯誤。"},{"en":"This is a mistake means this action or decision is wrong or unhelpful.","zh":"this is a mistake 的意思是這個行動或決定是錯誤或沒有幫助的。"},{"en":"It is a mistake to assume quiet students do not have ideas.","zh":"以為安靜學生沒有想法，這是一個錯誤。"},{"en":"Calling something a mistake warns people that it may cause problems later.","zh":"稱某事為錯誤，是在提醒人們它之後可能造成問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is direct and useful when giving advice.","zh":"這個短語直接，適合用於給建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"advanced books","meaning":"較進階的書","examples":[{"en":"Parents can read more advanced books to their children.","zh":"父母可以朗讀較進階的書給子女聽。"},{"en":"Advanced books are books with more difficult ideas, language, vocabulary, or structure.","zh":"advanced books 是概念、語言、詞彙或結構較困難的書。"},{"en":"A teacher may read advanced books aloud so children can enjoy stories above their reading level.","zh":"老師可能朗讀較進階的書，讓兒童享受超出自己閱讀程度的故事。"},{"en":"Advanced books can stretch children’s vocabulary and imagination.","zh":"較進階的書可以擴展兒童的詞彙和想像力。"},{"en":"This phrase does not always mean adult books; it means books beyond the child’s current level.","zh":"這個短語不一定指成人書，而是指超出孩子目前程度的書。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"develop their vocabulary","meaning":"擴展他們的詞彙量","examples":[{"en":"Reading advanced books helps children develop their vocabulary.","zh":"閱讀較進階的書幫助兒童擴展他們的詞彙量。"},{"en":"To develop their vocabulary means to help them learn, understand, and use more words.","zh":"develop their vocabulary 的意思是幫助他們學習、理解和使用更多詞語。"},{"en":"Children develop their vocabulary when adults explain new words during reading.","zh":"當成人在閱讀時解釋新詞，兒童就會擴展他們的詞彙量。"},{"en":"A larger vocabulary helps children understand lessons, stories, and instructions more easily.","zh":"更大的詞彙量幫助兒童更容易理解課堂、故事和指示。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in language learning and literacy education.","zh":"這個短語常見於語言學習和讀寫教育。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have time for this","meaning":"有時間做這件事","examples":[{"en":"Some parents do not have time for reading aloud.","zh":"有些父母沒有時間朗讀。"},{"en":"To have time for this means to have enough free time to do the activity being discussed.","zh":"have time for this 的意思是有足夠空閒時間做正在討論的活動。"},{"en":"Busy parents may not have time for this every night, but they can try weekends.","zh":"忙碌父母未必每晚都有時間做這件事，但可以嘗試週末。"},{"en":"If people do not make space in their schedule, they may feel they never have time for this.","zh":"如果人們不在日程中留出空間，他們可能覺得永遠沒有時間做這件事。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a practical time problem.","zh":"這個短語指出實際時間問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"listen to audio books","meaning":"聽有聲書","examples":[{"en":"Children can listen to audio books if parents are busy.","zh":"如果父母忙碌，兒童可以聽有聲書。"},{"en":"To listen to audio books means to hear recorded readings of books instead of reading the printed words yourself.","zh":"listen to audio books 的意思是聆聽錄製好的書本朗讀，而不是自己閱讀印刷文字。"},{"en":"Children may listen to audio books in the car or before bed.","zh":"兒童可能在車上或睡前聽有聲書。"},{"en":"Audio books can support reading because children hear pronunciation, rhythm, and storytelling.","zh":"有聲書可以支援閱讀，因為兒童會聽到發音、節奏和講故事方式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing alternatives to reading aloud.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論朗讀的替代方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"for themselves","meaning":"親自；自己","examples":[{"en":"Children often want to read books they have listened to for themselves.","zh":"兒童常想親自閱讀自己聽過的書。"},{"en":"For themselves means personally, independently, or without relying on another person.","zh":"for themselves 的意思是親自、獨立地，或不依賴別人。"},{"en":"After hearing a story, a child may want to read the ending for themselves.","zh":"聽完一個故事後，小孩可能想自己閱讀結局。"},{"en":"Doing something for themselves can build children’s confidence and independence.","zh":"親自做某事可以建立兒童的信心和獨立性。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows personal involvement.","zh":"這個短語常顯示個人參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make a mental note of","meaning":"在心裏記下","examples":[{"en":"Parents should make a mental note of the type of books their child is reading.","zh":"父母應在心裏記下孩子正在閱讀的書本類型。"},{"en":"To make a mental note of something means to remember it carefully without necessarily writing it down.","zh":"make a mental note of something 的意思是小心記住某事，不一定要寫下來。"},{"en":"A teacher may make a mental note of which students enjoy adventure stories.","zh":"老師可能在心裏記下哪些學生喜歡冒險故事。"},{"en":"Making a mental note helps parents recommend better books later.","zh":"在心裏記下這些資料，有助父母之後推薦更合適的書。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quiet observation and remembering.","zh":"這個短語描述安靜觀察和記住。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"type of books","meaning":"書本類型","examples":[{"en":"Parents should notice the type of books their child is reading.","zh":"父母應留意孩子正在閱讀的書本類型。"},{"en":"Type of books means the category or kind of books, such as fantasy, mystery, comics, or non-fiction.","zh":"type of books 指書本的類別或種類，例如奇幻、推理、漫畫或非小說。"},{"en":"A librarian may ask about the type of books a child enjoys before making suggestions.","zh":"圖書館員在推薦前，可能詢問小孩喜歡的書本類型。"},{"en":"Knowing the type of books children like helps adults introduce similar but slightly wider choices.","zh":"知道兒童喜歡的書本類型，有助成人介紹相似但更廣闊的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe reading interests.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述閱讀興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"read the same genre","meaning":"閱讀同一類型","examples":[{"en":"Children often read the same genre all the time.","zh":"兒童常一直閱讀同一類型的書。"},{"en":"To read the same genre means to keep choosing books from the same category or style.","zh":"read the same genre 的意思是不斷選擇同一類別或風格的書。"},{"en":"A child who loves mysteries may read the same genre every week.","zh":"喜歡推理故事的小孩可能每週都閱讀同一類型。"},{"en":"Reading the same genre can be comforting, but it may limit vocabulary and imagination.","zh":"閱讀同一類型可以令人安心，但也可能限制詞彙和想像力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing reading habits.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論閱讀習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"all the time","meaning":"一直；經常","examples":[{"en":"Children may read the same genre all the time.","zh":"兒童可能一直閱讀同一類型的書。"},{"en":"All the time means very often or continuously.","zh":"all the time 的意思是非常經常或持續不斷。"},{"en":"A child who reads comics all the time may not try other types of books.","zh":"一直看漫畫的小孩可能不會嘗試其他類型的書。"},{"en":"Doing the same thing all the time can become boring or limit learning.","zh":"一直做同一件事可能會變得沉悶或限制學習。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests repetition.","zh":"這個短語常表示重複。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"get a bit boring","meaning":"變得有點沉悶","examples":[{"en":"Reading the same genre all the time can get a bit boring.","zh":"一直閱讀同一類型的書可能會變得有點沉悶。"},{"en":"To get a bit boring means to become slightly dull or less interesting over time.","zh":"get a bit boring 的意思是隨時間變得有點乏味或不那麼有趣。"},{"en":"Eating the same lunch every day can get a bit boring.","zh":"每天吃同一款午餐可能會變得有點沉悶。"},{"en":"A habit gets boring when there is no variety or surprise.","zh":"當一個習慣沒有變化或驚喜，它就會變得沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase is gentle and less strong than “become very boring”.","zh":"這個短語語氣溫和，沒有 become very boring 那麼強烈。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"introduce new authors and genres","meaning":"介紹新的作者和類型","examples":[{"en":"Parents can introduce new authors and genres to their children.","zh":"父母可以向子女介紹新的作者和類型。"},{"en":"To introduce new authors and genres means to help children discover writers and book types they have not tried before.","zh":"introduce new authors and genres 的意思是幫助兒童發現以前未試過的作家和書本類型。"},{"en":"A librarian may introduce new authors and genres by setting up a display of different books.","zh":"圖書館員可能透過設置不同書本展示來介紹新的作者和類型。"},{"en":"Introducing variety can stop reading from becoming boring and expand children’s interests.","zh":"介紹多樣性可以避免閱讀變得沉悶，並擴展兒童興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on widening reading choices.","zh":"這個短語集中於擴闊閱讀選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be able to help with","meaning":"能夠在……方面幫忙","examples":[{"en":"Librarians should be able to help parents with book recommendations.","zh":"圖書館員應能夠在書本推薦方面幫助家長。"},{"en":"To be able to help with something means to have the knowledge or ability to give support in that area.","zh":"be able to help with something 的意思是在某方面有知識或能力提供支援。"},{"en":"A teacher may be able to help with grammar questions after class.","zh":"老師可能能夠在課後幫忙解答文法問題。"},{"en":"Getting help from someone knowledgeable can save time and reduce uncertainty.","zh":"向有知識的人求助可以節省時間並減少不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and practical when asking for support.","zh":"這個短語在請求支援時禮貌而實用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"really useful","meaning":"真的很有用","examples":[{"en":"The presenter says Jenny’s advice is really useful.","zh":"主持人說 Jenny 的建議真的很有用。"},{"en":"Really useful means very helpful in a practical way.","zh":"really useful 的意思是在實際方面非常有幫助。"},{"en":"A reading list is really useful when parents do not know which books to choose.","zh":"當家長不知道選哪些書，閱讀清單真的很有用。"},{"en":"Useful advice helps people take action instead of only understanding the problem.","zh":"有用的建議能幫助人採取行動，而不只是理解問題。"},{"en":"This phrase gives simple positive feedback.","zh":"這個短語給予簡單正面回饋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 7/task-3":[{"front":"get on with","meaning":"進展如何","examples":[{"en":"Clare asks Jake how he is getting on with the practical teaching.","zh":"Clare 問 Jake 實習教學進展如何。"},{"en":"To get on with something means to make progress with it or manage it.","zh":"get on with something 是指某事進展如何，或你如何應付它。"},{"en":"A student may ask a classmate how she is getting on with her history project.","zh":"學生可能會問同學歷史專題研習進展如何。"},{"en":"If you are getting on well with a task, you understand what to do and can continue smoothly.","zh":"如果你在一項任務上進展順利，你明白要做甚麼，也能順利繼續。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they want to know whether someone is coping or making progress.","zh":"人們想知道某人是否應付得來或有進展時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"practical teaching","meaning":"實習教學","examples":[{"en":"Jake is doing practical teaching as part of his training.","zh":"Jake 正在接受訓練，其中包括實習教學。"},{"en":"Practical teaching is real classroom teaching done to gain experience.","zh":"實習教學是在真實課室中教學，以獲得經驗。"},{"en":"A trainee teacher may do practical teaching before becoming fully qualified.","zh":"見習老師可能在正式取得資格前進行實習教學。"},{"en":"Practical teaching helps trainees learn how to explain ideas, manage students, and plan lessons.","zh":"實習教學幫助見習老師學習如何解釋概念、管理學生和規劃課堂。"},{"en":"It is different from simply studying education theory in a lecture room.","zh":"它不同於只在講課室學習教育理論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"harder than I expected","meaning":"比我預期中更難","examples":[{"en":"The practical teaching is harder than Jake expected.","zh":"實習教學比 Jake 預期中更難。"},{"en":"Harder than I expected means more difficult than I thought it would be.","zh":"harder than I expected 是指比我原本以為的更困難。"},{"en":"A student may say the exam was harder than she expected after seeing unfamiliar questions.","zh":"學生看到不熟悉的題目後，可能會說考試比她預期中更難。"},{"en":"A task can feel harder than expected when there are hidden problems or extra pressure.","zh":"當任務有隱藏問題或額外壓力時，可能會比預期中更難。"},{"en":"This phrase compares reality with what someone imagined before starting.","zh":"這個短語把實際情況與開始前的想像作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"how about you?","meaning":"你呢？","examples":[{"en":"Jake asks Clare, “How about you?”","zh":"Jake 問 Clare：「你呢？」"},{"en":"How about you? is used to ask the same question back to another person.","zh":"How about you? 用來把同一個問題反問另一個人。"},{"en":"If someone says, “I’m tired today. How about you?”, they are asking about your condition too.","zh":"如果有人說：「我今天很累。你呢？」他也在問你的情況。"},{"en":"This question keeps a conversation balanced because both people get a chance to answer.","zh":"這個問題令對話較平衡，因為雙方都有機會回答。"},{"en":"It is common in friendly conversations after one person has already shared something.","zh":"它常見於友善對話中，通常在一個人分享了事情之後使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"not brilliant","meaning":"不太好","examples":[{"en":"Clare says her practical teaching is not brilliant.","zh":"Clare 說她的實習教學不太好。"},{"en":"Not brilliant means not very good, but said in a mild or understated way.","zh":"not brilliant 是指不太好，但語氣較溫和或輕描淡寫。"},{"en":"A student may say her test result was not brilliant if she hoped for a higher mark.","zh":"如果學生本來希望取得更高分數，她可能會說測驗成績不太好。"},{"en":"People use not brilliant to admit a problem without sounding too dramatic.","zh":"人們用 not brilliant 來承認問題，但不想聽起來太誇張。"},{"en":"It is softer than saying something is terrible or a complete failure.","zh":"它比說某事很糟或完全失敗更委婉。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"struggle with","meaning":"在……方面很吃力","examples":[{"en":"Clare is struggling with her Year 12 science class.","zh":"Clare 在她的12年級科學班方面很吃力。"},{"en":"To struggle with something means to find it difficult to deal with or do well.","zh":"struggle with something 是指在處理或做好某事方面感到困難。"},{"en":"A student may struggle with essay writing if she cannot organise her ideas clearly.","zh":"如果學生無法清楚組織想法，她可能在寫文章方面很吃力。"},{"en":"People struggle with a task when it is confusing, stressful, or beyond their current skills.","zh":"當任務令人混亂、有壓力或超出目前能力時，人們會感到吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows difficulty, but it does not mean the person has completely given up.","zh":"這個短語表示困難，但不代表那個人已經完全放棄。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Year 12 science class","meaning":"12年級科學班","examples":[{"en":"Clare is teaching a Year 12 science class.","zh":"Clare 正在教一班12年級科學班。"},{"en":"A Year 12 science class is a senior secondary class studying science subjects.","zh":"12年級科學班是修讀科學科目的高中班級。"},{"en":"A Year 12 science class may learn biology, chemistry, physics, or general science.","zh":"12年級科學班可能學習生物、化學、物理或普通科學。"},{"en":"Teaching a Year 12 science class can be challenging because students may need exam preparation.","zh":"教12年級科學班可能具挑戰性，因為學生可能需要準備考試。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies both the students’ year level and the subject being taught.","zh":"這個短語同時指出學生年級和所教授的科目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hard to control","meaning":"難以管理","examples":[{"en":"Jake asks whether Clare’s students are hard to control.","zh":"Jake 問 Clare 的學生是否難以管理。"},{"en":"Hard to control means difficult to manage or keep calm and orderly.","zh":"hard to control 是指難以管理，或難以保持安靜和有秩序。"},{"en":"A large class may be hard to control if students keep talking over the teacher.","zh":"如果學生不停蓋過老師說話，大班課可能會難以管理。"},{"en":"A situation becomes hard to control when rules are unclear or people stop listening.","zh":"當規則不清楚或人們停止聆聽，情況便會變得難以控制。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used about groups, behaviour, crowds, or emotions.","zh":"這個短語常用於群體、行為、人群或情緒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"discipline problems","meaning":"紀律問題","examples":[{"en":"Clare does not have discipline problems as such.","zh":"Clare 嚴格來說沒有紀律問題。"},{"en":"Discipline problems are behaviour issues that break rules or disturb order.","zh":"discipline problems 是指違反規則或擾亂秩序的行為問題。"},{"en":"A class has discipline problems if students shout, refuse to work, or ignore instructions.","zh":"如果學生大叫、拒絕做事或不聽指示，班上就有紀律問題。"},{"en":"Discipline problems can waste lesson time because the teacher must keep stopping to manage behaviour.","zh":"紀律問題會浪費課堂時間，因為老師必須不斷停下來管理行為。"},{"en":"Not every quiet or bored class has discipline problems; sometimes the issue is lack of interest.","zh":"並非每個安靜或沉悶的班級都有紀律問題；有時問題是不感興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as such","meaning":"嚴格來說；本身而言","examples":[{"en":"Clare says she does not have discipline problems as such.","zh":"Clare 說她嚴格來說沒有紀律問題。"},{"en":"As such means strictly speaking or in the exact sense of the word.","zh":"as such 是指嚴格來說，或按該詞的準確意思而言。"},{"en":"The café is not a restaurant as such; it mainly sells drinks and small cakes.","zh":"這間咖啡店嚴格來說不是餐廳；它主要售賣飲品和小蛋糕。"},{"en":"People use as such when they want to correct or narrow the meaning of what was just said.","zh":"人們用 as such 來修正或收窄剛才所說的意思。"},{"en":"It helps show that something is similar to an idea but not exactly that idea.","zh":"它有助表示某事與某個概念相似，但不完全等同。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have anything to do with","meaning":"與……有任何關係","examples":[{"en":"The students do not think science has anything to do with their lives.","zh":"學生不認為科學與他們的生活有任何關係。"},{"en":"To have anything to do with something means to be connected or relevant to it.","zh":"have anything to do with something 是指與某事有聯繫或相關。"},{"en":"Some students think grammar has nothing to do with speaking, until they need clearer sentences.","zh":"有些學生認為文法與說話無關，直到他們需要更清楚的句子。"},{"en":"A subject feels boring when learners cannot see what it has to do with real life.","zh":"當學習者看不到一科與現實生活有何關係時，該科會顯得沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to question whether two things are related.","zh":"這個短語常用來質疑兩件事是否相關。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"their lives","meaning":"他們的生活","examples":[{"en":"The students do not see how science connects with their lives.","zh":"學生看不到科學如何與他們的生活連繫起來。"},{"en":"Their lives means the everyday experiences, needs, problems, and futures of those people.","zh":"their lives 是指那些人的日常經歷、需要、問題和未來。"},{"en":"Lessons feel more useful when students can connect them with their lives.","zh":"當學生能把課堂內容與他們的生活連繫起來，課堂會感覺更有用。"},{"en":"If young people see how budgeting affects their lives, they may take money lessons more seriously.","zh":"如果年輕人看到理財如何影響他們的生活，他們可能會更認真看待金錢課。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that learning becomes stronger when it links to real experience.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，學習與真實經驗連繫時會更有力量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"there’s no real engagement","meaning":"沒有真正投入","examples":[{"en":"The students listen, but there is no real engagement.","zh":"學生有聽課，但沒有真正投入。"},{"en":"There’s no real engagement means people are present but not truly interested or involved.","zh":"there’s no real engagement 是指人在場，但沒有真正感興趣或參與。"},{"en":"In a meeting, there is no real engagement if everyone stays silent and checks their phones.","zh":"在會議中，如果人人沉默並查看手機，就沒有真正投入。"},{"en":"Without real engagement, students may remember facts briefly but not think deeply about them.","zh":"沒有真正投入，學生可能只短暫記住資料，而不會深入思考。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lack of active attention, not simply bad behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏主動注意，而不只是行為差。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as part of","meaning":"作為……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Clare has to design an experiment as part of her teaching practice.","zh":"Clare 必須設計一個實驗，作為教學實習的一部分。"},{"en":"As part of means included within a larger activity, course, or plan.","zh":"as part of 是指包括在一個更大的活動、課程或計劃之內。"},{"en":"Students may give a presentation as part of their final assessment.","zh":"學生可能需要作匯報，作為期末評核的一部分。"},{"en":"A small task can feel more important when it is part of a larger project.","zh":"當一項小任務是一個較大項目的一部分時，它會顯得更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why an action is being done and what bigger thing it belongs to.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何要做某行動，以及它屬於哪個更大的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"teaching practice","meaning":"教學實習","examples":[{"en":"Clare must design an experiment for her teaching practice.","zh":"Clare 必須為她的教學實習設計一個實驗。"},{"en":"Teaching practice is a period when trainee teachers practise teaching real students.","zh":"teaching practice 是見習老師練習教真正學生的一段時期。"},{"en":"During teaching practice, a trainee may plan lessons, teach classes, and receive feedback.","zh":"在教學實習期間，見習老師可能要備課、授課和接受回饋。"},{"en":"Teaching practice helps future teachers discover what works in a real classroom.","zh":"教學實習幫助未來教師發現真實課室中甚麼方法有效。"},{"en":"It is important because teaching skills cannot be learned only from books.","zh":"它很重要，因為教學技巧不能只靠書本學會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"design an experiment","meaning":"設計一個實驗","examples":[{"en":"Clare has to design an experiment for her students to do.","zh":"Clare 必須設計一個實驗給學生做。"},{"en":"To design an experiment means to plan a fair test that can answer a question.","zh":"design an experiment 是指規劃一個公平測試，以回答某個問題。"},{"en":"A science teacher may design an experiment to test how light affects plant growth.","zh":"科學老師可能設計一個實驗，測試光線如何影響植物生長。"},{"en":"A good experiment needs clear steps, controlled variables, and reliable measurements.","zh":"好實驗需要清楚步驟、受控制的變項和可靠測量。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on planning the test before anyone carries it out.","zh":"這個短語著重在進行實驗前先作規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I was wondering about","meaning":"我在想是否可以……","examples":[{"en":"Clare was wondering about an experiment on children’s diets.","zh":"Clare 在想是否可以做一個關於兒童飲食的實驗。"},{"en":"I was wondering about means I was thinking about a possibility but have not decided yet.","zh":"I was wondering about 是指我在考慮一個可能性，但還未決定。"},{"en":"A student may say, “I was wondering about joining the debate team,” when she wants advice.","zh":"學生想尋求建議時，可能會說：「我在想是否可以加入辯論隊。」"},{"en":"People use this phrase to introduce an idea gently rather than directly announcing a decision.","zh":"人們用這個短語溫和地引入想法，而不是直接宣布決定。"},{"en":"It often invites the listener to comment, suggest, or question the idea.","zh":"它常邀請聽者評論、建議或質疑該想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"children’s diets","meaning":"兒童飲食","examples":[{"en":"Clare considers doing an experiment on children’s diets.","zh":"Clare 考慮做一個關於兒童飲食的實驗。"},{"en":"Children’s diets are the foods and drinks that children usually eat and drink.","zh":"children’s diets 是指兒童平時吃和喝的食物與飲品。"},{"en":"A school may study children’s diets to see whether pupils eat enough fruit and vegetables.","zh":"學校可能研究兒童飲食，看看學生是否吃足夠水果和蔬菜。"},{"en":"Poor children’s diets can affect energy, concentration, and long-term health.","zh":"不良兒童飲食可以影響精力、專注力和長遠健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is about eating patterns, not only one meal.","zh":"這個短語關於飲食模式，而不只是某一餐。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"record what they eat","meaning":"記錄他們吃了甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The children could record what they eat.","zh":"兒童可以記錄他們吃了甚麼。"},{"en":"To record what they eat means to write down or track all the food they consume.","zh":"record what they eat 是指寫下或追蹤他們吃過的所有食物。"},{"en":"A patient may record what she eats each day to understand stomach problems.","zh":"病人可能每天記錄自己吃了甚麼，以了解胃部問題。"},{"en":"Recording food can help people notice habits they would otherwise forget.","zh":"記錄食物可以幫助人注意到原本會忘記的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when data about diet is needed.","zh":"當需要飲食數據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"link something to","meaning":"把某事與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"Clare might link the children’s diets to their state of health.","zh":"Clare 可能會把兒童飲食與他們的健康狀況聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To link something to another thing means to connect them and suggest a relationship between them.","zh":"link something to another thing 是指把兩者連繫，並指出它們之間有關係。"},{"en":"Researchers may link poor sleep to lower exam performance.","zh":"研究人員可能把睡眠不足與較低考試表現聯繫起來。"},{"en":"If two things are linked, one may help explain or affect the other.","zh":"如果兩件事有聯繫，其中一件可能有助解釋或影響另一件。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing causes, effects, or relationships.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論原因、影響或關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"state of health","meaning":"健康狀況","examples":[{"en":"The experiment might connect diet with the children’s state of health.","zh":"這個實驗可能把飲食與兒童的健康狀況連繫起來。"},{"en":"A person’s state of health is their general physical condition.","zh":"一個人的 state of health 是指他的整體身體狀況。"},{"en":"A doctor may check a patient’s state of health before recommending exercise.","zh":"醫生可能在建議運動前檢查病人的健康狀況。"},{"en":"Diet, sleep, stress, and illness can all affect someone’s state of health.","zh":"飲食、睡眠、壓力和疾病都可以影響一個人的健康狀況。"},{"en":"This phrase is broader than one symptom; it refers to overall health.","zh":"這個短語比單一症狀更廣泛，指整體健康。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"methodology","meaning":"研究方法","examples":[{"en":"Jake says Clare’s methodology would involve children recording their food.","zh":"Jake 說 Clare 的研究方法會包括讓兒童記錄食物。"},{"en":"Methodology means the planned method or system used to carry out research.","zh":"methodology 是指進行研究所用的計劃方法或系統。"},{"en":"In a survey project, the methodology explains who will be asked and how answers will be collected.","zh":"在問卷研究中，研究方法會解釋會問誰，以及如何收集答案。"},{"en":"Weak methodology can lead to unreliable results because the data may not be fair or complete.","zh":"薄弱的研究方法可能導致不可靠結果，因為數據可能不公平或不完整。"},{"en":"This word is common in research, reports, and academic discussions.","zh":"這個詞常見於研究、報告和學術討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"involve someone doing","meaning":"包括某人做……","examples":[{"en":"The methodology would involve the children recording what they eat.","zh":"研究方法會包括兒童記錄他們吃了甚麼。"},{"en":"To involve someone doing something means to include that person in an activity or task.","zh":"involve someone doing something 是指包括某人參與一項活動或任務。"},{"en":"A school project may involve students interviewing local residents.","zh":"學校專題可能包括學生訪問本地居民。"},{"en":"If a plan involves people doing extra work, it may need clear instructions and permission.","zh":"如果計劃包括人們做額外工作，可能需要清楚指示和許可。"},{"en":"This phrase shows who must take part and what action they must do.","zh":"這個短語顯示誰必須參與，以及他們必須做甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have access to","meaning":"取得……的使用權；查閱……","examples":[{"en":"Clare would need to have access to the children’s medical records.","zh":"Clare 需要取得兒童醫療紀錄的查閱權。"},{"en":"To have access to something means to be allowed to see, use, or reach it.","zh":"have access to something 是指獲准查看、使用或接觸某物。"},{"en":"A teacher may have access to students’ attendance records but not their private medical files.","zh":"老師可能可以查閱學生出席紀錄，但不能查閱私人醫療文件。"},{"en":"Access to sensitive information can create privacy concerns if it is not controlled.","zh":"如果敏感資料的查閱權不受控制，可能會造成私隱問題。"},{"en":"This phrase often involves permission, rights, or availability.","zh":"這個短語常涉及許可、權限或可用性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"medical records","meaning":"醫療紀錄","examples":[{"en":"The experiment would require access to the children’s medical records.","zh":"這個實驗需要查閱兒童的醫療紀錄。"},{"en":"Medical records are documents that contain information about a person’s health and treatment.","zh":"medical records 是包含某人健康和治療資料的文件。"},{"en":"A hospital keeps medical records so doctors know a patient’s history.","zh":"醫院保存醫療紀錄，好讓醫生了解病人的病歷。"},{"en":"Medical records must be protected because they include private information.","zh":"醫療紀錄必須受到保護，因為它們包含私人資料。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to official health files, not casual notes about feeling unwell.","zh":"這個短語通常指正式健康檔案，而不是關於不舒服的隨意筆記。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be happy about","meaning":"對……感到樂意","examples":[{"en":"Jake does not think people would be happy about sharing medical records.","zh":"Jake 不認為人們會樂意分享醫療紀錄。"},{"en":"To be happy about something means to feel pleased or comfortable with it.","zh":"be happy about something 是指對某事感到高興、接受或放心。"},{"en":"Parents may not be happy about a school sharing children’s photos online.","zh":"學校在網上分享孩子照片，家長可能不會樂意。"},{"en":"People are less happy about a decision when it affects privacy or safety.","zh":"當決定影響私隱或安全時，人們通常較不樂意。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean real happiness, but often it simply means acceptance or comfort.","zh":"這個短語可以指真正高興，但常只是表示接受或感到放心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"confidentiality would be an issue","meaning":"保密會是一個問題","examples":[{"en":"Confidentiality would be an issue if Clare used medical records.","zh":"如果 Clare 使用醫療紀錄，保密會是一個問題。"},{"en":"Confidentiality would be an issue means keeping private information secret would be a problem or concern.","zh":"confidentiality would be an issue 是指保護私人資料不外泄會成為問題或憂慮。"},{"en":"If a school collects health data, confidentiality would be an issue for parents.","zh":"如果學校收集健康數據，保密會是家長關心的問題。"},{"en":"Confidentiality becomes an issue when personal details might be seen by the wrong people.","zh":"當個人資料可能被不應看見的人看到，保密便會成為問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when privacy must be protected carefully.","zh":"這個短語用於需要小心保護私隱時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get the right data","meaning":"取得正確數據","examples":[{"en":"The conclusions might be significant if Clare could get the right data.","zh":"如果 Clare 能取得正確數據，結論可能很有意義。"},{"en":"To get the right data means to collect the information needed to answer a question accurately.","zh":"get the right data 是指收集回答問題所需的準確資料。"},{"en":"A shop needs to get the right data before deciding which products customers like most.","zh":"商店在決定顧客最喜歡哪些產品前，需要取得正確數據。"},{"en":"If researchers collect the wrong data, their conclusions may be weak or misleading.","zh":"如果研究人員收集錯誤數據，結論可能薄弱或具誤導性。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that useful results depend on suitable information.","zh":"這個短語強調有用結果取決於合適資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"conclusions might be significant","meaning":"結論可能很有意義","examples":[{"en":"The conclusions might be significant if the data were available.","zh":"如果有數據，結論可能很有意義。"},{"en":"Conclusions might be significant means the findings could be important or meaningful.","zh":"conclusions might be significant 是指研究結果可能重要或有意義。"},{"en":"A study’s conclusions might be significant if they help schools improve student health.","zh":"如果一項研究能幫助學校改善學生健康，其結論可能很有意義。"},{"en":"Results become significant when they explain a problem or affect future decisions.","zh":"當結果能解釋問題或影響未來決定，它們便很有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean the conclusions are certain; it means they could matter.","zh":"這個短語不是說結論一定成立，而是說它們可能重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"I suspect","meaning":"我估計；我懷疑","examples":[{"en":"Jake suspects that getting the data will not be easy.","zh":"Jake 懷疑取得數據不會容易。"},{"en":"I suspect means I think something is probably true, often based on clues or experience.","zh":"I suspect 是指我認為某事很可能是真的，通常基於線索或經驗。"},{"en":"I suspect the bus will be late because traffic is already heavy.","zh":"我估計巴士會遲到，因為交通已經很擠塞。"},{"en":"People use I suspect when they are not completely certain but have a strong feeling.","zh":"人們在不完全肯定但有強烈感覺時，會使用 I suspect。"},{"en":"It sounds more careful than simply saying “I know”.","zh":"它比直接說「我知道」更謹慎。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"not going to be easy","meaning":"不會容易","examples":[{"en":"Getting the right medical data is not going to be easy.","zh":"取得正確醫療數據不會容易。"},{"en":"Not going to be easy means something will probably be difficult to do.","zh":"not going to be easy 是指某事很可能難以完成。"},{"en":"Finding a quiet flat in a busy city is not going to be easy.","zh":"在繁忙城市找一間安靜單位不會容易。"},{"en":"A task is not going to be easy when it needs time, permission, money, or special skills.","zh":"當任務需要時間、許可、金錢或特殊技能時，就不會容易。"},{"en":"This phrase prepares the listener for difficulty before the work begins.","zh":"這個短語在工作開始前讓聽者有心理準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"do an experiment using animals","meaning":"用動物做實驗","examples":[{"en":"Jake asks whether Clare has considered doing an experiment using animals.","zh":"Jake 問 Clare 是否考慮過用動物做實驗。"},{"en":"To do an experiment using animals means to carry out a scientific test with animals as subjects.","zh":"do an experiment using animals 是指以動物作為實驗對象進行科學測試。"},{"en":"A biology class may discuss whether it is ethical to do an experiment using animals.","zh":"生物課可能討論用動物做實驗是否合乎倫理。"},{"en":"Animal experiments need careful rules because the animals’ welfare must be protected.","zh":"動物實驗需要謹慎規則，因為必須保護動物福祉。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the type of experimental subject being used.","zh":"這個短語著重所使用的實驗對象類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be upsetting for","meaning":"令……難過","examples":[{"en":"Clare worries that using animals might be upsetting for the children.","zh":"Clare 擔心使用動物可能會令孩子難過。"},{"en":"To be upsetting for someone means to make that person feel sad, worried, or uncomfortable.","zh":"be upsetting for someone 是指令某人感到傷心、擔心或不舒服。"},{"en":"A frightening news story may be upsetting for young children.","zh":"可怕的新聞故事可能會令年幼兒童難過。"},{"en":"A lesson can be upsetting if students feel that animals or people are being treated unfairly.","zh":"如果學生覺得動物或人被不公平對待，課堂可能令人難過。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on emotional reaction, not physical danger.","zh":"這個短語著重情緒反應，而不是身體危險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be harmed in any way","meaning":"受到任何形式的傷害","examples":[{"en":"The animals do not have to be harmed in any way.","zh":"動物不需要受到任何形式的傷害。"},{"en":"To be harmed in any way means to be hurt physically, emotionally, or otherwise.","zh":"be harmed in any way 是指在身體、情緒或其他方面受到傷害。"},{"en":"School animals should not be harmed in any way during classroom activities.","zh":"課堂活動期間，學校飼養的動物不應受到任何形式的傷害。"},{"en":"A project is more acceptable when people can prove no living thing will be harmed.","zh":"如果人們能證明沒有生物會受到傷害，項目會較容易被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises that no kind of damage should happen.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調不應發生任何形式的損害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a certain diet","meaning":"某種特定飲食","examples":[{"en":"The animals could be given a certain diet.","zh":"可以給動物某種特定飲食。"},{"en":"A certain diet means a particular planned pattern of food.","zh":"a certain diet 是指某種經計劃的特定進食方式。"},{"en":"A doctor may recommend a certain diet for someone with high blood pressure.","zh":"醫生可能建議高血壓患者採用某種特定飲食。"},{"en":"Giving one group a certain diet helps researchers compare results fairly.","zh":"給其中一組某種特定飲食，有助研究人員公平比較結果。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to a controlled or chosen diet, not random eating.","zh":"這個短語通常指受控制或經選擇的飲食，而不是隨意進食。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"observe the effects","meaning":"觀察效果","examples":[{"en":"The effects of the diet could be observed.","zh":"可以觀察這種飲食的效果。"},{"en":"To observe the effects means to watch carefully and record what changes happen.","zh":"observe the effects 是指仔細觀察並記錄發生了甚麼變化。"},{"en":"A teacher may observe the effects of a new seating plan on class discussion.","zh":"老師可能會觀察新座位安排對課堂討論的效果。"},{"en":"Researchers observe effects over time because some changes do not appear immediately.","zh":"研究人員會隨時間觀察效果，因為有些變化不會即時出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in experiments where results must be noticed and measured.","zh":"這個短語常見於需要留意和測量結果的實驗中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get permission to","meaning":"取得許可去……","examples":[{"en":"Clare asks whether she would have to get permission to use animals.","zh":"Clare 問她是否需要取得許可去使用動物。"},{"en":"To get permission to do something means to receive approval before doing it.","zh":"get permission to do something 是指在做某事前獲得批准。"},{"en":"Students must get permission to leave school early.","zh":"學生必須取得許可才可提早離校。"},{"en":"Permission is needed when an action may affect safety, privacy, or other people’s rights.","zh":"當某行動可能影響安全、私隱或他人權利時，便需要許可。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that someone cannot simply do the action freely.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人不能隨意做該行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"submit an outline","meaning":"提交概要","examples":[{"en":"Clare would have to submit an outline of the experiment.","zh":"Clare 必須提交實驗概要。"},{"en":"To submit an outline means to hand in a short plan showing the main parts of a project.","zh":"submit an outline 是指交出一份簡短計劃，顯示項目的主要部分。"},{"en":"A student may submit an outline before writing a long research essay.","zh":"學生可能在寫長篇研究文章前提交概要。"},{"en":"An outline helps teachers check whether the plan is clear, safe, and possible.","zh":"概要幫助老師檢查計劃是否清楚、安全和可行。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used before a full project or report is approved.","zh":"這個短語常用於完整項目或報告獲批准之前。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fill in a form","meaning":"填寫表格","examples":[{"en":"Clare would have to fill in a form before using animals.","zh":"Clare 使用動物前必須填寫表格。"},{"en":"To fill in a form means to write the required information in the spaces provided.","zh":"fill in a form 是指在指定位置填上所需資料。"},{"en":"A parent may fill in a form before a child joins a school trip.","zh":"孩子參加學校旅行前，家長可能需要填寫表格。"},{"en":"Forms are used when organisations need clear records and official permission.","zh":"當機構需要清楚紀錄和正式許可時，便會使用表格。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in schools, offices, hospitals, and government services.","zh":"這個短語常見於學校、辦公室、醫院和政府服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"quite straightforward","meaning":"相當簡單直接","examples":[{"en":"The permission process is quite straightforward.","zh":"取得許可的程序相當簡單直接。"},{"en":"Quite straightforward means fairly simple, clear, and not difficult to understand.","zh":"quite straightforward 是指相當簡單、清楚，而且不難理解。"},{"en":"Setting up the new printer was quite straightforward after reading the instructions.","zh":"看過說明後，設定新打印機相當簡單直接。"},{"en":"A process feels straightforward when each step is clear and there are few complications.","zh":"當每個步驟清楚且少有複雜情況，程序便會顯得簡單直接。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures someone that a task is not as difficult as it may sound.","zh":"這個短語安撫別人，表示任務不像聽起來那麼難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"find out that","meaning":"發現……","examples":[{"en":"Clare asks what would happen if they found out that a diet affected animals.","zh":"Clare 問如果他們發現某種飲食影響動物，會怎樣。"},{"en":"To find out that something is true means to discover it through evidence or experience.","zh":"find out that something is true 是指透過證據或經驗發現某事屬實。"},{"en":"A teacher may find out that students learn better with visual examples.","zh":"老師可能發現學生配合視覺例子會學得更好。"},{"en":"Experiments help people find out whether an idea is supported by results.","zh":"實驗幫助人們發現一個想法是否獲結果支持。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on discovering information that was not known before.","zh":"這個短語著重發現以前不知道的資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"particular diet","meaning":"某種特定飲食","examples":[{"en":"A particular diet might affect the health of animals.","zh":"某種特定飲食可能會影響動物健康。"},{"en":"A particular diet is one specific eating plan or food pattern.","zh":"particular diet 是指某一種具體的飲食計劃或食物模式。"},{"en":"A doctor may test whether a particular diet helps patients with stomach pain.","zh":"醫生可能測試某種特定飲食是否幫助胃痛患者。"},{"en":"Studying one particular diet makes the experiment clearer than studying many diets at once.","zh":"研究某一種特定飲食，比同時研究多種飲食更清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the focus to a selected diet.","zh":"這個短語把焦點收窄到一種選定飲食。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"affect the health of","meaning":"影響……的健康","examples":[{"en":"The experiment might show that a diet affects the health of animals.","zh":"實驗可能顯示某種飲食會影響動物的健康。"},{"en":"To affect the health of someone or something means to change their physical condition.","zh":"affect the health of someone or something 是指改變其身體狀況。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can affect the health of students by lowering energy and concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足會降低精力和專注力，從而影響學生健康。"},{"en":"A diet high in sugar may affect health if it is eaten too often.","zh":"如果經常吃高糖飲食，可能會影響健康。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to good or bad effects, depending on the context.","zh":"這個短語可指好或壞的影響，視乎語境而定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not necessarily be true for","meaning":"不一定適用於……","examples":[{"en":"The same result would not necessarily be true for people.","zh":"同一結果不一定適用於人類。"},{"en":"Not necessarily be true for someone means something may not apply to that group or situation.","zh":"not necessarily be true for someone 是指某事不一定適用於該群體或情況。"},{"en":"A study about adults may not necessarily be true for children.","zh":"關於成年人的研究不一定適用於兒童。"},{"en":"Results from one school are useful, but they may not be true for every school.","zh":"一間學校的結果有用，但不一定適用於每間學校。"},{"en":"This phrase warns us not to overgeneralise from limited evidence.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們不要把有限證據過度推廣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"findings","meaning":"研究結果","examples":[{"en":"The findings for any experiment are going to be limited.","zh":"任何實驗的研究結果都會有局限。"},{"en":"Findings are the results or discoveries from research or an investigation.","zh":"findings 是指研究或調查所得的結果或發現。"},{"en":"A school survey’s findings may show that students want more quiet study spaces.","zh":"學校問卷的研究結果可能顯示學生想要更多安靜自修空間。"},{"en":"Findings matter because they help people decide what to do next.","zh":"研究結果很重要，因為它們幫助人決定下一步。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than simply saying results.","zh":"這個詞比單純說 results 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be limited","meaning":"有局限","examples":[{"en":"The findings of any experiment are going to be limited.","zh":"任何實驗的研究結果都會有局限。"},{"en":"To be limited means not to cover everything or not to be completely strong or general.","zh":"be limited 是指不能涵蓋所有情況，或並非完全有力或普遍。"},{"en":"A survey of twenty students is limited because it may not represent the whole school.","zh":"一項只訪問二十名學生的調查有局限，因為它未必代表全校。"},{"en":"Research can be limited by time, money, sample size, or available information.","zh":"研究可能受時間、金錢、樣本大小或可用資料限制。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us to be careful about how far we apply results.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們要小心判斷結果能應用到多遠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"it’s inevitable","meaning":"這是不可避免的","examples":[{"en":"Jake says that limited findings are inevitable.","zh":"Jake 說研究結果有局限是不可避免的。"},{"en":"It’s inevitable means it cannot be avoided and will almost certainly happen.","zh":"it’s inevitable 是指某事無法避免，而且幾乎一定會發生。"},{"en":"If a school has only one small hall, timetable clashes are almost inevitable.","zh":"如果學校只有一個小禮堂，時間表衝突幾乎不可避免。"},{"en":"Some mistakes are inevitable when people try something difficult for the first time.","zh":"人們第一次嘗試困難事情時，有些錯誤是不可避免的。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests acceptance rather than surprise.","zh":"這個短語表示接受，而不是驚訝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"investigate the effects of","meaning":"研究……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Clare wants to investigate the effects of diet.","zh":"Clare 想研究飲食的影響。"},{"en":"To investigate the effects of something means to study how it changes or influences something else.","zh":"investigate the effects of something 是指研究它如何改變或影響另一事物。"},{"en":"Scientists may investigate the effects of sleep on memory.","zh":"科學家可能研究睡眠對記憶的影響。"},{"en":"Teachers can investigate the effects of group work by comparing student participation before and after.","zh":"老師可以透過比較前後學生參與度，研究小組活動的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when describing the purpose of research.","zh":"這個短語常用於描述研究目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"experimental mice","meaning":"實驗小鼠","examples":[{"en":"Clare would need experimental mice for the experiment.","zh":"Clare 這個實驗需要實驗小鼠。"},{"en":"Experimental mice are mice used in scientific tests under controlled conditions.","zh":"experimental mice 是在受控制條件下用於科學測試的小鼠。"},{"en":"A laboratory may use experimental mice to study how a diet affects weight.","zh":"實驗室可能使用實驗小鼠研究飲食如何影響體重。"},{"en":"Experimental mice must be cared for properly because they are living animals.","zh":"實驗小鼠必須得到妥善照顧，因為牠們是活生生的動物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to mice used for research, not ordinary pet mice.","zh":"這個短語指用於研究的小鼠，而不是普通寵物鼠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be specially bred for","meaning":"專門為……培育","examples":[{"en":"Experimental mice are specially bred for experiments.","zh":"實驗小鼠是專門為實驗培育的。"},{"en":"To be specially bred for something means to be produced or raised for a particular purpose.","zh":"be specially bred for something 是指為某個特定目的而繁殖或培育。"},{"en":"Some guide dogs are specially bred for calmness and careful behaviour.","zh":"有些導盲犬是專門為沉着和細心行為而培育的。"},{"en":"Specially bred animals may give more reliable research results because their background is known.","zh":"專門培育的動物背景已知，因此研究結果可能較可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the animal or plant was not chosen randomly.","zh":"這個短語顯示該動物或植物不是隨機選來的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"what will your experiment be investigating?","meaning":"你的實驗會研究甚麼？","examples":[{"en":"Jake asks what Clare’s experiment will be investigating exactly.","zh":"Jake 問 Clare 的實驗究竟會研究甚麼。"},{"en":"What will your experiment be investigating? asks what question or effect the experiment will study.","zh":"What will your experiment be investigating? 是問實驗會研究哪個問題或影響。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask, “What will your experiment be investigating?” before approving a science project.","zh":"老師批准科學專題前，可能會問：「你的實驗會研究甚麼？」"},{"en":"If students cannot answer this question, their experiment may be too vague.","zh":"如果學生不能回答這個問題，他們的實驗可能太含糊。"},{"en":"This question helps define the exact focus of research.","zh":"這個問題有助界定研究的確切焦點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"something to do with","meaning":"與……有關的東西","examples":[{"en":"Clare wants to study something to do with nutrition.","zh":"Clare 想研究與營養有關的東西。"},{"en":"Something to do with means connected with a topic, though not yet stated exactly.","zh":"something to do with 是指與某個主題有關，但尚未準確說明。"},{"en":"A student may say her project is something to do with social media and teenagers.","zh":"學生可能說她的專題是與社交媒體和青少年有關的東西。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they have a general idea but have not narrowed it down.","zh":"人們有大概想法但尚未收窄時，會用這個短語。"},{"en":"It is useful for early discussion, but later the idea should become more specific.","zh":"它適合初步討論，但之後想法應變得更具體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"nutrition","meaning":"營養","examples":[{"en":"Clare wants the experiment to focus on nutrition.","zh":"Clare 想讓實驗集中於營養。"},{"en":"Nutrition is the way food gives the body energy and the materials it needs to stay healthy.","zh":"nutrition 是指食物如何為身體提供能量和維持健康所需的物質。"},{"en":"Schools teach nutrition so students understand why balanced meals matter.","zh":"學校教授營養知識，好讓學生明白均衡膳食為何重要。"},{"en":"Poor nutrition can affect growth, concentration, and resistance to illness.","zh":"營養不良可以影響成長、專注力和抵抗疾病能力。"},{"en":"This word is about the health value of food, not just taste.","zh":"這個詞關於食物的健康價值，而不只是味道。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"food supplements","meaning":"食品補充劑","examples":[{"en":"Clare considers studying food supplements.","zh":"Clare 考慮研究食品補充劑。"},{"en":"Food supplements are products added to a diet to provide extra nutrients.","zh":"food supplements 是加入飲食中、提供額外營養的產品。"},{"en":"Some people take food supplements such as vitamins when their diet lacks certain nutrients.","zh":"有些人在飲食缺乏某些營養時，會服用維他命等食品補充劑。"},{"en":"Food supplements can help in some cases, but they should not replace balanced meals.","zh":"食品補充劑在某些情況下有幫助，但不應取代均衡膳食。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to extra nutritional products, not ordinary snacks.","zh":"這個短語指額外營養產品，而不是普通零食。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"extra iron and extra protein","meaning":"額外鐵質和額外蛋白質","examples":[{"en":"Food supplements can include extra iron and extra protein.","zh":"食品補充劑可以包括額外鐵質和額外蛋白質。"},{"en":"Extra iron and extra protein are added nutrients beyond what is already in the normal diet.","zh":"extra iron and extra protein 是指在正常飲食已有營養之外額外添加的營養素。"},{"en":"A doctor may recommend extra iron if a patient’s blood test shows low iron levels.","zh":"如果病人驗血顯示鐵質偏低，醫生可能建議補充額外鐵質。"},{"en":"Extra protein may help people who need to rebuild muscle after illness or heavy exercise.","zh":"額外蛋白質可能幫助病後或大量運動後需要重建肌肉的人。"},{"en":"This phrase names two examples of nutrients that may be added to food or supplements.","zh":"這個短語列出可加入食物或補充劑的兩種營養素例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"impact on health","meaning":"對健康的影響","examples":[{"en":"Clare wants to study the impact of supplements on health.","zh":"Clare 想研究補充劑對健康的影響。"},{"en":"Impact on health means the effect something has on a person’s physical or mental condition.","zh":"impact on health 是指某事對一個人的身體或心理狀況造成的影響。"},{"en":"Regular exercise usually has a positive impact on health.","zh":"定期運動通常對健康有正面影響。"},{"en":"Too much sugar may have a negative impact on health over time.","zh":"長期攝取太多糖可能對健康有負面影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing whether something helps or harms the body.","zh":"這個短語適合用來討論某事對身體有幫助還是有害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rather broad","meaning":"相當廣泛","examples":[{"en":"Jake says Clare’s idea might be rather broad.","zh":"Jake 說 Clare 的想法可能相當廣泛。"},{"en":"Rather broad means too general or covering too many things at once.","zh":"rather broad 是指太籠統，或一次涵蓋太多事情。"},{"en":"A topic like “technology” is rather broad for a five-minute presentation.","zh":"「科技」這樣的題目對五分鐘匯報來說相當廣泛。"},{"en":"If an idea is rather broad, it may be hard to design a clear experiment or argument.","zh":"如果想法相當廣泛，就可能難以設計清楚實驗或論點。"},{"en":"This phrase politely suggests that the focus should be narrowed.","zh":"這個短語委婉地表示焦點應收窄。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"look at the effects of","meaning":"研究……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Jake suggests looking at the effects of one supplement.","zh":"Jake 建議研究一種補充劑的影響。"},{"en":"To look at the effects of something means to study what changes it causes.","zh":"look at the effects of something 是指研究它造成甚麼變化。"},{"en":"A school may look at the effects of later start times on student sleep.","zh":"學校可能研究延遲上課時間對學生睡眠的影響。"},{"en":"Looking at one effect at a time can make research clearer and fairer.","zh":"一次研究一個影響，可以令研究更清晰和公平。"},{"en":"This phrase is less formal than “investigate”, but the meaning is similar.","zh":"這個短語比 investigate 較不正式，但意思相近。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"focus on whether","meaning":"重點放在是否……","examples":[{"en":"Clare thinks the focus could be on whether mice can control their own diet.","zh":"Clare 認為重點可以放在小鼠是否能控制自己的飲食。"},{"en":"To focus on whether something is true means to make that question the main point.","zh":"focus on whether something is true 是指把該問題作為主要焦點。"},{"en":"A survey may focus on whether students feel safe travelling to school.","zh":"問卷可能重點放在學生上學途中是否感到安全。"},{"en":"Focusing on one clear question helps researchers collect the right evidence.","zh":"聚焦一個清楚問題，有助研究人員收集合適證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when narrowing a broad topic into a yes-or-no research question.","zh":"這個短語適合用於把廣泛題目收窄成是否式研究問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"control their own diet","meaning":"控制自己的飲食","examples":[{"en":"The experiment could examine whether mice can control their own diet.","zh":"這個實驗可以檢視小鼠能否控制自己的飲食。"},{"en":"To control their own diet means to choose or limit what they eat.","zh":"control their own diet 是指選擇或限制自己吃甚麼。"},{"en":"Some adults try to control their own diet by planning meals and avoiding too many snacks.","zh":"有些成年人透過規劃膳食和避免太多零食來控制自己的飲食。"},{"en":"If animals cannot control their diet, they may eat too much of food that tastes good but is unhealthy.","zh":"如果動物不能控制自己的飲食，可能會吃太多味道好但不健康的食物。"},{"en":"This phrase is about self-regulation in eating behaviour.","zh":"這個短語關於飲食行為上的自我調節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have access to","meaning":"可取得；可接觸到","examples":[{"en":"The mice may have access to more sugar than they need.","zh":"小鼠可能可取得比牠們需要更多的糖。"},{"en":"To have access to something means to be able to reach or use it.","zh":"have access to something 是指能夠接觸或使用某物。"},{"en":"Children with access to a library can borrow books after school.","zh":"可以使用圖書館的孩子放學後能借書。"},{"en":"If people have easy access to unhealthy snacks, they may eat them more often.","zh":"如果人們容易接觸到不健康零食，他們可能會更常吃。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on availability, not necessarily actual use.","zh":"這個短語著重可取得性，不一定代表實際使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"more sugar than they need","meaning":"比牠們需要更多的糖","examples":[{"en":"The mice may be given more sugar than they need.","zh":"小鼠可能會被給予比牠們需要更多的糖。"},{"en":"More sugar than they need means an amount of sugar greater than what is necessary or healthy.","zh":"more sugar than they need 是指糖的分量超過必要或健康所需。"},{"en":"A child may get more sugar than he needs if he drinks several sweet drinks every day.","zh":"如果孩子每天喝幾杯甜飲，他可能攝取比自己需要更多的糖。"},{"en":"Too much sugar can affect weight, teeth, and energy levels over time.","zh":"長期攝取太多糖可以影響體重、牙齒和能量水平。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly compares actual intake with what the body requires.","zh":"這個短語清楚比較實際攝取量與身體所需。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"decide to leave it","meaning":"決定不吃它；決定不要它","examples":[{"en":"The experiment asks whether the mice eat the sugar or decide to leave it.","zh":"這個實驗探問小鼠會吃糖，還是決定不吃它。"},{"en":"To decide to leave it means to choose not to take, eat, or use something.","zh":"decide to leave it 是指選擇不拿、不吃或不使用某物。"},{"en":"A student may see a free cake but decide to leave it because she is not hungry.","zh":"學生可能看到免費蛋糕，但因為不餓而決定不吃。"},{"en":"If animals leave extra food, it may show they can limit what they eat.","zh":"如果動物不吃額外食物，可能顯示牠們能限制自己進食。"},{"en":"This phrase shows choice and self-control rather than lack of access.","zh":"這個短語顯示選擇和自我控制，而不是無法取得。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"later on","meaning":"之後","examples":[{"en":"Later on, Clare could do a follow-up experiment.","zh":"之後，Clare 可以做一個後續實驗。"},{"en":"Later on means at a later time, after the present stage or first step.","zh":"later on 是指在稍後時間，在目前階段或第一步之後。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain the basic idea now and give harder exercises later on.","zh":"老師可能現在解釋基本概念，之後再給較難練習。"},{"en":"People use later on when something is not immediate but may happen afterwards.","zh":"人們用 later on 表示某事不是立即發生，但可能在之後發生。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise actions in time.","zh":"這個短語有助按時間組織行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"follow-up experiment","meaning":"後續實驗","examples":[{"en":"Jake suggests doing a follow-up experiment with another variable.","zh":"Jake 建議加入另一個變項做後續實驗。"},{"en":"A follow-up experiment is a later experiment that continues or extends an earlier one.","zh":"follow-up experiment 是在之後進行、延續或擴展較早實驗的實驗。"},{"en":"After testing sleep, researchers may do a follow-up experiment on diet and concentration.","zh":"測試睡眠後，研究人員可能做一個關於飲食和專注力的後續實驗。"},{"en":"Follow-up experiments help check whether the first results still hold under new conditions.","zh":"後續實驗有助檢查第一輪結果在新條件下是否仍然成立。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that research can happen in stages.","zh":"這個短語顯示研究可以分階段進行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"add another variable","meaning":"加入另一個變項","examples":[{"en":"The follow-up experiment could add another variable.","zh":"後續實驗可以加入另一個變項。"},{"en":"To add another variable means to include one more factor that may affect the result.","zh":"add another variable 是指加入另一個可能影響結果的因素。"},{"en":"A plant experiment may add another variable by changing both water and light.","zh":"植物實驗可以透過同時改變水分和光線來加入另一個變項。"},{"en":"Adding too many variables at once can make results harder to explain.","zh":"一次加入太多變項會令結果更難解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in experiments because variables must be controlled carefully.","zh":"這個短語在實驗中很重要，因為變項必須小心控制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"give someone the chance to","meaning":"給某人機會去……","examples":[{"en":"Clare could give some mice the chance to be more active.","zh":"Clare 可以給一些小鼠機會去更活躍。"},{"en":"To give someone the chance to do something means to provide an opportunity for that action.","zh":"give someone the chance to do something 是指提供機會讓某人做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may give quiet students the chance to speak in smaller groups.","zh":"老師可能給安靜的學生機會在較小組別中發言。"},{"en":"Giving people a chance can reveal abilities or choices that were not visible before.","zh":"給人機會可以顯示之前未被看見的能力或選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on opportunity, not forcing someone to act.","zh":"這個短語著重機會，而不是強迫某人行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be more active","meaning":"更活躍","examples":[{"en":"Some mice could be given the chance to be more active.","zh":"一些小鼠可以被給予機會去更活躍。"},{"en":"To be more active means to move around or do more physical activity.","zh":"be more active 是指四處活動或做更多體能活動。"},{"en":"Students can be more active by walking to school or joining sports clubs.","zh":"學生可以透過步行上學或參加運動社團變得更活躍。"},{"en":"Being more active can affect health, weight, mood, and energy levels.","zh":"更活躍可以影響健康、體重、心情和能量水平。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a higher level of activity with a quieter or less active state.","zh":"這個短語把較高活動量與較安靜或較不活躍的狀態作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"run on a wheel","meaning":"在滾輪上跑","examples":[{"en":"Some mice could run on a wheel in the experiment.","zh":"一些小鼠可以在實驗中在滾輪上跑。"},{"en":"To run on a wheel means for an animal to exercise on a small rotating wheel.","zh":"run on a wheel 是指動物在小型旋轉滾輪上運動。"},{"en":"Pet hamsters often run on a wheel at night because they are active animals.","zh":"寵物倉鼠常在晚上在滾輪上跑，因為牠們是活躍動物。"},{"en":"A wheel allows researchers to give animals exercise without needing a large space.","zh":"滾輪讓研究人員在不需要大空間的情況下給動物運動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a controlled form of activity in a cage.","zh":"這個短語描述籠子內受控制的活動方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sit around","meaning":"閒坐着","examples":[{"en":"The other mice could just sit around and do very little.","zh":"其他小鼠可以只是閒坐着，幾乎甚麼都不做。"},{"en":"To sit around means to spend time doing little or nothing active.","zh":"sit around 是指花時間坐着，很少或沒有活動。"},{"en":"Some teenagers sit around at home all weekend instead of going outside.","zh":"有些青少年整個週末在家閒坐着，而不是出外活動。"},{"en":"Sitting around for too long can reduce energy and physical fitness.","zh":"長時間閒坐可能降低精力和體能。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests inactivity or wasted time.","zh":"這個短語常暗示不活躍或浪費時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"repeat the experiment","meaning":"重複實驗","examples":[{"en":"Clare could repeat the experiment with a different type of food.","zh":"Clare 可以用不同種類的食物重複實驗。"},{"en":"To repeat the experiment means to do the same test again, often to check or compare results.","zh":"repeat the experiment 是指再次做同一測試，通常為了檢查或比較結果。"},{"en":"A student may repeat the experiment if the first measurements seem strange.","zh":"如果第一次測量結果看起來奇怪，學生可能會重複實驗。"},{"en":"Repeating an experiment helps researchers see whether the result is reliable.","zh":"重複實驗有助研究人員判斷結果是否可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that science often needs more than one trial.","zh":"這個短語顯示科學往往需要不止一次試驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"change the type of food","meaning":"改變食物種類","examples":[{"en":"Clare could change the type of food she provided.","zh":"Clare 可以改變她提供的食物種類。"},{"en":"To change the type of food means to use a different category or kind of food.","zh":"change the type of food 是指使用不同類別或種類的食物。"},{"en":"A parent may change the type of food in a lunchbox if a child keeps leaving it uneaten.","zh":"如果孩子經常不吃飯盒，父母可能會改變飯盒中的食物種類。"},{"en":"Changing food type in an experiment can show whether results depend on that food.","zh":"在實驗中改變食物種類，可以顯示結果是否取決於該食物。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on altering one part of a diet.","zh":"這個短語著重改變飲食中的一個部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"genetic structure","meaning":"基因結構","examples":[{"en":"Clare could use mice with a different genetic structure.","zh":"Clare 可以使用基因結構不同的小鼠。"},{"en":"Genetic structure means the inherited biological information that affects how a living thing develops.","zh":"genetic structure 是指影響生物如何發展的遺傳生物資料。"},{"en":"Two plant varieties may grow differently because they have different genetic structures.","zh":"兩個植物品種可能因基因結構不同而有不同生長情況。"},{"en":"Genetic structure can affect body size, disease risk, and response to diet.","zh":"基因結構可以影響體型、患病風險和對飲食的反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is scientific and refers to inherited biological makeup.","zh":"這個短語屬科學用語，指遺傳上的生物組成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"think about that some more","meaning":"再多考慮一下","examples":[{"en":"Clare might think about Jake’s idea some more.","zh":"Clare 可能會再多考慮一下 Jake 的想法。"},{"en":"To think about that some more means to consider an idea further before deciding.","zh":"think about that some more 是指在決定前進一步考慮某個想法。"},{"en":"A student may think about a subject choice some more before submitting the form.","zh":"學生提交表格前，可能會再多考慮一下選科。"},{"en":"People think about an idea more when it has advantages but also possible problems.","zh":"當一個想法有好處但也有潛在問題時，人們會再多考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the decision is not final yet.","zh":"這個短語顯示決定尚未最終落實。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"talk through","meaning":"逐步講解；仔細討論","examples":[{"en":"Clare wants to talk through a possible procedure.","zh":"Clare 想逐步講解一個可能的流程。"},{"en":"To talk through something means to discuss it step by step so it becomes clearer.","zh":"talk through something 是指逐步討論某事，使它變得更清楚。"},{"en":"A teacher may talk through an essay plan with a student before writing begins.","zh":"老師可能在學生開始寫作前，和學生逐步討論文章計劃。"},{"en":"Talking through a plan can reveal missing steps or possible problems.","zh":"仔細討論計劃可以揭示缺少的步驟或可能問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people need to understand a process carefully together.","zh":"當人們需要一起仔細理解一個流程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"possible procedure","meaning":"可能的流程","examples":[{"en":"Clare describes a possible procedure for the experiment.","zh":"Clare 描述一個實驗可能的流程。"},{"en":"A possible procedure is one set of steps that could be used to carry out a task.","zh":"possible procedure 是指一組可能用來完成任務的步驟。"},{"en":"A nurse may explain a possible procedure before a simple medical check.","zh":"護士可能在簡單身體檢查前解釋可能的流程。"},{"en":"A procedure must be clear so different people can follow the same steps.","zh":"流程必須清楚，這樣不同人才能跟隨相同步驟。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the plan is not final but can be discussed.","zh":"這個短語表示計劃尚未最終確定，仍可討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sugar supplement","meaning":"糖補充物","examples":[{"en":"The experiment involves giving mice a sugar supplement.","zh":"這個實驗包括給小鼠糖補充物。"},{"en":"A sugar supplement is extra sugar added to a diet.","zh":"sugar supplement 是加入飲食中的額外糖分。"},{"en":"An athlete’s drink may contain a sugar supplement to provide quick energy.","zh":"運動員飲品可能含有糖補充物，以提供快速能量。"},{"en":"In an experiment, a sugar supplement can help test how extra sugar affects weight or behaviour.","zh":"在實驗中，糖補充物可以幫助測試額外糖分如何影響體重或行為。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to added sugar, not sugar naturally present in all foods.","zh":"這個短語指額外添加的糖，而不是所有食物中天然存在的糖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"similar experiment","meaning":"類似實驗","examples":[{"en":"Jake did a similar experiment in college.","zh":"Jake 在大學時做過一個類似實驗。"},{"en":"A similar experiment is an experiment that is like another one in aim, method, or topic.","zh":"similar experiment 是指在目的、方法或主題上與另一個實驗相似的實驗。"},{"en":"A student may read about a similar experiment before designing her own project.","zh":"學生設計自己的專題前，可能會閱讀一個類似實驗。"},{"en":"Similar experiments can give useful guidance, but details may still need to change.","zh":"類似實驗可以提供有用指引，但細節仍可能需要改動。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect a new plan with previous experience.","zh":"這個短語有助把新計劃與過往經驗連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"how many mice would I need?","meaning":"我需要多少隻小鼠？","examples":[{"en":"Clare asks how many mice she would need.","zh":"Clare 問她需要多少隻小鼠。"},{"en":"How many mice would I need? asks about the number of mice required for an experiment.","zh":"How many mice would I need? 是問一個實驗需要多少隻小鼠。"},{"en":"A student planning a survey may ask, “How many people would I need?”","zh":"規劃問卷的學生可能會問：「我需要多少人？」"},{"en":"The number matters because too few subjects may make results unreliable.","zh":"數量很重要，因為研究對象太少可能令結果不可靠。"},{"en":"This question helps plan the size of a study or experiment.","zh":"這個問題有助規劃研究或實驗的規模。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"all young ones","meaning":"全部都是年輕的","examples":[{"en":"Jake says the mice should all be young ones.","zh":"Jake 說小鼠應該全部都是年輕的。"},{"en":"All young ones means every animal in the group should be young, not mixed with older ones.","zh":"all young ones 是指組內每隻動物都應該年輕，而不是混入年老的。"},{"en":"A pet shop may keep all young ones in a separate area because they need special care.","zh":"寵物店可能把所有幼小動物放在獨立區域，因為牠們需要特別照顧。"},{"en":"Using all young ones can make an experiment fairer because age affects growth and weight.","zh":"使用全部年輕的小鼠可以令實驗更公平，因為年齡會影響生長和體重。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the whole group should share the same age stage.","zh":"這個短語強調整組都應處於同一年齡階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a mixture of old and young","meaning":"老幼混合","examples":[{"en":"The experiment should not use a mixture of old and young mice.","zh":"實驗不應使用老幼混合的小鼠。"},{"en":"A mixture of old and young means a group containing both older and younger members.","zh":"a mixture of old and young 是指一組中同時有年老和年輕成員。"},{"en":"A sports class with a mixture of old and young participants may need different difficulty levels.","zh":"如果運動班老幼混合，可能需要不同難度級別。"},{"en":"In experiments, a mixture of old and young animals can make results harder to interpret.","zh":"在實驗中，老幼混合的動物會令結果更難解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights variation in age within one group.","zh":"這個短語突出同一組內的年齡差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"equal sizes","meaning":"相同大小","examples":[{"en":"Clare needs two groups of equal sizes.","zh":"Clare 需要兩組相同大小的小鼠。"},{"en":"Equal sizes means the groups contain the same number of members or items.","zh":"equal sizes 是指各組包含相同數量的成員或物件。"},{"en":"A teacher may divide a class into teams of equal sizes for a fair game.","zh":"老師可能把班級分成相同大小的小隊，以便公平比賽。"},{"en":"Groups of equal sizes make comparisons fairer because one group does not have more subjects than the other.","zh":"相同大小的組別令比較更公平，因為其中一組不會比另一組有更多研究對象。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in experiments, games, and planning.","zh":"這個短語常用於實驗、遊戲和規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in each group","meaning":"每組","examples":[{"en":"There would be six mice in each group.","zh":"每組會有六隻小鼠。"},{"en":"In each group means inside every group separately.","zh":"in each group 是指在每一組裏。"},{"en":"A teacher may put five students in each group for a discussion activity.","zh":"老師可能在討論活動中每組安排五名學生。"},{"en":"Keeping the same number in each group helps people compare results fairly.","zh":"每組保持相同人數，有助人們公平比較結果。"},{"en":"This phrase tells us how something is divided across groups.","zh":"這個短語告訴我們某物如何分配到各組。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tell them apart","meaning":"區分它們","examples":[{"en":"Clare needs a way to tell the two groups apart.","zh":"Clare 需要一個方法區分兩組小鼠。"},{"en":"To tell them apart means to recognise the difference between two similar people or things.","zh":"tell them apart 是指辨認兩個相似的人或物之間的差異。"},{"en":"Twins may look so similar that teachers need name tags to tell them apart.","zh":"雙胞胎可能看起來很相似，老師需要名牌才可區分他們。"},{"en":"If researchers cannot tell groups apart, they may record data incorrectly.","zh":"如果研究人員不能區分組別，可能會錯誤記錄數據。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on identification and avoiding confusion.","zh":"這個短語著重辨認和避免混淆。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"some sort of tag","meaning":"某種標籤","examples":[{"en":"Clare considers putting some sort of tag on one group.","zh":"Clare 考慮在其中一組身上放某種標籤。"},{"en":"Some sort of tag means some kind of label or marker used to identify something.","zh":"some sort of tag 是指用來識別某物的某種標籤或標記。"},{"en":"A suitcase may need some sort of tag so the owner can find it at the airport.","zh":"行李箱可能需要某種標籤，方便主人在機場找到。"},{"en":"A tag helps prevent confusion when several items look similar.","zh":"當幾件物品看起來相似時，標籤有助防止混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is vague because the exact type of tag has not been chosen yet.","zh":"這個短語較含糊，因為具體標籤類型尚未決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"mark them in some way","meaning":"以某種方式標記牠們","examples":[{"en":"Clare could mark the mice in some way.","zh":"Clare 可以以某種方式標記小鼠。"},{"en":"To mark them in some way means to put a sign or mark on them so they can be identified.","zh":"mark them in some way 是指在牠們身上做記號，以便辨認。"},{"en":"A teacher may mark students’ folders in some way to show different classes.","zh":"老師可能以某種方式標記學生文件夾，以顯示不同班別。"},{"en":"Marking similar items prevents mistakes when people need to sort or compare them.","zh":"標記相似物品可以防止人們在分類或比較時出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase leaves the exact method open.","zh":"這個短語沒有指定確切方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"food colouring","meaning":"食用色素","examples":[{"en":"Jake suggests using food colouring to mark the mice.","zh":"Jake 建議用食用色素標記小鼠。"},{"en":"Food colouring is a safe dye used to change the colour of food or mark something lightly.","zh":"food colouring 是用來改變食物顏色或輕微標記某物的安全染色劑。"},{"en":"Bakers use food colouring to make icing red, blue, or green.","zh":"麵包師會用食用色素把糖霜變成紅色、藍色或綠色。"},{"en":"In this experiment, food colouring would help identify groups without harming the mice.","zh":"在這個實驗中，食用色素可以幫助辨認組別而不傷害小鼠。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to colouring suitable for food, not ordinary paint.","zh":"這個短語指適合食物使用的色素，而不是普通油漆。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"wouldn’t hurt them","meaning":"不會傷害牠們","examples":[{"en":"Food colouring would not hurt the mice.","zh":"食用色素不會傷害小鼠。"},{"en":"Wouldn’t hurt them means would not cause them pain, injury, or harm.","zh":"wouldn’t hurt them 是指不會令牠們疼痛、受傷或受害。"},{"en":"A soft collar on a pet should not hurt it if it fits properly.","zh":"如果尺寸合適，寵物身上的柔軟頸圈不應傷害牠。"},{"en":"A method is more acceptable when it does not hurt the animals involved.","zh":"當一個方法不會傷害相關動物，它會較容易被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures the listener about safety or welfare.","zh":"這個短語用來安撫聽者，表示安全或動物福祉不受影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"go into a separate cage","meaning":"放進不同籠子","examples":[{"en":"Each group would go into a separate cage.","zh":"每組會放進不同籠子。"},{"en":"To go into a separate cage means to be placed in a different cage from another group.","zh":"go into a separate cage 是指被放進與另一組不同的籠子。"},{"en":"Sick animals may go into a separate cage so they can be cared for safely.","zh":"生病動物可能會放進不同籠子，以便安全照顧。"},{"en":"Separate cages prevent groups from mixing and confusing the results.","zh":"不同籠子可防止組別混在一起，令結果混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical separation for control or safety.","zh":"這個短語描述為控制或安全而作出的實體分隔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"control group","meaning":"對照組","examples":[{"en":"Group A would be the control group.","zh":"A組會是對照組。"},{"en":"A control group is the group in an experiment that does not receive the special treatment being tested.","zh":"control group 是實驗中沒有接受被測試特殊處理的組別。"},{"en":"In a study on a new drink, the control group may drink plain water.","zh":"在一項關於新飲品的研究中，對照組可能飲用普通清水。"},{"en":"A control group helps researchers see whether the treatment really causes a difference.","zh":"對照組幫助研究人員判斷處理是否真的造成差異。"},{"en":"Without a control group, it is harder to know what the results mean.","zh":"沒有對照組，就更難知道結果代表甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ordinary mouse food","meaning":"普通小鼠飼料","examples":[{"en":"The control group would have ordinary mouse food.","zh":"對照組會吃普通小鼠飼料。"},{"en":"Ordinary mouse food is the normal food usually given to mice.","zh":"ordinary mouse food 是通常給小鼠吃的正常飼料。"},{"en":"A pet shop sells ordinary mouse food for owners who keep mice at home.","zh":"寵物店售賣普通小鼠飼料給在家養小鼠的主人。"},{"en":"Using ordinary food for the control group helps compare normal diet with the special diet.","zh":"對照組使用普通飼料，有助比較正常飲食與特殊飲食。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts regular food with added or experimental food.","zh":"這個短語把一般食物與額外或實驗食物作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dry pellets","meaning":"乾顆粒","examples":[{"en":"Ordinary mouse food comes in dry pellets.","zh":"普通小鼠飼料是乾顆粒。"},{"en":"Dry pellets are small, hard pieces of dry food made for animals.","zh":"dry pellets 是給動物吃的小而硬的乾糧顆粒。"},{"en":"Many pet foods come as dry pellets because they are easy to store and measure.","zh":"許多寵物食品以乾顆粒形式出售，因為容易儲存和量度。"},{"en":"Dry pellets help researchers give each animal a consistent type of food.","zh":"乾顆粒幫助研究人員給每隻動物一致的食物種類。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the shape and texture of the food.","zh":"這個短語描述食物的形狀和質感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the same as","meaning":"與……相同","examples":[{"en":"The second group would have the same food as the first group.","zh":"第二組會吃與第一組相同的食物。"},{"en":"The same as means identical to or not different from something else.","zh":"the same as 是指與另一事物完全相同或沒有差異。"},{"en":"My timetable is the same as yours, so we finish school at the same time.","zh":"我的時間表與你的相同，所以我們同一時間放學。"},{"en":"In an experiment, keeping one thing the same helps isolate the factor being tested.","zh":"在實驗中，保持某一項相同有助隔離正在測試的因素。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when comparing two people, things, or situations.","zh":"這個短語用於比較兩個人、事物或情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"extra sugar","meaning":"額外的糖","examples":[{"en":"The second group would also have extra sugar.","zh":"第二組也會有額外的糖。"},{"en":"Extra sugar means additional sugar added beyond the normal amount.","zh":"extra sugar 是指在正常分量以外加入的糖。"},{"en":"A child may get extra sugar from sweets, soft drinks, and sweetened cereal.","zh":"孩子可能從糖果、汽水和加糖麥片中攝取額外的糖。"},{"en":"Extra sugar in a diet may affect weight, teeth, and energy levels.","zh":"飲食中的額外糖分可能影響體重、牙齒和能量水平。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights sugar added on top of the usual food.","zh":"這個短語突出在平常食物之外添加的糖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"straight sugar","meaning":"純糖；直接給糖","examples":[{"en":"Jake asks whether Clare would give the mice straight sugar.","zh":"Jake 問 Clare 是否會直接給小鼠純糖。"},{"en":"Straight sugar means pure sugar by itself, not mixed into another food.","zh":"straight sugar 是指單獨的純糖，而不是混入其他食物中的糖。"},{"en":"Eating straight sugar from a spoon would taste extremely sweet and offer little nutrition.","zh":"用匙羹直接吃純糖會非常甜，而且幾乎沒有營養。"},{"en":"In an experiment, straight sugar may be too unrealistic because animals rarely eat sugar that way.","zh":"在實驗中，純糖可能太不貼近現實，因為動物很少那樣吃糖。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts pure sugar with food that contains sugar.","zh":"這個短語把純糖與含糖食物作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"something like cereal","meaning":"像麥片之類的東西","examples":[{"en":"Clare thinks it might be better to give the mice something like cereal with the sugar.","zh":"Clare 認為給小鼠像麥片之類的東西配糖可能較好。"},{"en":"Something like cereal means a food similar to cereal, though not necessarily exactly cereal.","zh":"something like cereal 是指類似麥片的食物，但不一定完全是麥片。"},{"en":"A parent might give a child something like cereal for a quick breakfast.","zh":"父母可能給孩子像麥片之類的東西作快速早餐。"},{"en":"Giving sugar with food may be more natural than giving straight sugar alone.","zh":"把糖與食物一起給予，可能比單獨給純糖更自然。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate example rather than a precise item.","zh":"這個短語提供近似例子，而不是精確物件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"weigh the mice","meaning":"替小鼠稱重","examples":[{"en":"Clare would need to weigh the mice once a week.","zh":"Clare 需要每週替小鼠稱重一次。"},{"en":"To weigh the mice means to measure how heavy the mice are.","zh":"weigh the mice 是指量度小鼠有多重。"},{"en":"A vet may weigh a pet regularly to check whether it is growing properly.","zh":"獸醫可能定期替寵物稱重，以檢查牠是否正常成長。"},{"en":"Weighing the mice helps researchers track changes caused by diet or exercise.","zh":"替小鼠稱重有助研究人員追蹤飲食或運動造成的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a measurement step in an experiment.","zh":"這個短語描述實驗中的測量步驟。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"once a week","meaning":"每週一次","examples":[{"en":"The mice should be weighed once a week.","zh":"小鼠應每週稱重一次。"},{"en":"Once a week means one time every week.","zh":"once a week 是指每星期一次。"},{"en":"A student may meet her tutor once a week for speaking practice.","zh":"學生可能每週一次與導師練習口語。"},{"en":"Measuring something once a week gives regular data without checking every day.","zh":"每週測量一次可以提供定期數據，而不需要每天檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequency.","zh":"這個短語描述頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"electronic balance","meaning":"電子天平","examples":[{"en":"Clare would need an electronic balance.","zh":"Clare 需要一部電子天平。"},{"en":"An electronic balance is a digital device used to measure weight or mass accurately.","zh":"electronic balance 是用來準確量度重量或質量的數碼儀器。"},{"en":"Science labs use electronic balances to weigh chemicals before experiments.","zh":"科學實驗室使用電子天平在實驗前稱量化學品。"},{"en":"An electronic balance gives clearer readings than guessing by hand.","zh":"電子天平比用手估計提供更清楚的讀數。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to measuring equipment, not a balance of ideas.","zh":"這個短語指測量儀器，而不是想法上的平衡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hold them on the balance","meaning":"把牠們按在天平上","examples":[{"en":"Clare cannot hold the mice on the balance.","zh":"Clare 不能把小鼠按在天平上。"},{"en":"To hold them on the balance means to keep them in place by hand while they are being weighed.","zh":"hold them on the balance 是指稱重時用手把牠們固定在天平上。"},{"en":"A child should not hold a puppy on a scale if the hand changes the reading.","zh":"如果手會改變讀數，孩子就不應把小狗按在磅上。"},{"en":"Holding animals during weighing can make measurements inaccurate.","zh":"稱重時按住動物可能令測量不準確。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a method that may seem helpful but affects results.","zh":"這個短語解釋一種看似有用但會影響結果的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"affect the reading","meaning":"影響讀數","examples":[{"en":"Holding the mice would affect the reading on the balance.","zh":"按住小鼠會影響天平上的讀數。"},{"en":"To affect the reading means to change the number or result shown by a measuring device.","zh":"affect the reading 是指改變測量儀器顯示的數字或結果。"},{"en":"Leaning on a scale will affect the reading because extra force is added.","zh":"靠在磅上會影響讀數，因為加入了額外力量。"},{"en":"If a reading is affected, the data may no longer be reliable.","zh":"如果讀數受到影響，數據可能不再可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing measurement accuracy.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論測量準確度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"weighing chamber","meaning":"稱重室；稱重箱","examples":[{"en":"A weighing chamber can stop the mice from running away.","zh":"稱重室可以防止小鼠跑走。"},{"en":"A weighing chamber is a small container used to hold an animal safely while measuring its weight.","zh":"weighing chamber 是稱重時用來安全固定動物的小容器。"},{"en":"A lab may use a weighing chamber so a small animal can be weighed without being held by hand.","zh":"實驗室可能使用稱重箱，讓小動物不用被手按住也能稱重。"},{"en":"A weighing chamber improves accuracy because the animal stays in place on the balance.","zh":"稱重室提高準確度，因為動物會留在天平上。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to equipment that helps control movement during measurement.","zh":"這個短語指在測量期間幫助控制移動的設備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stop the mice from running away","meaning":"防止小鼠跑走","examples":[{"en":"The weighing chamber stops the mice from running away.","zh":"稱重室防止小鼠跑走。"},{"en":"To stop the mice from running away means to prevent them from escaping or moving off.","zh":"stop the mice from running away 是指防止小鼠逃走或離開。"},{"en":"A lid on a pet carrier can stop a hamster from running away during travel.","zh":"寵物運輸箱上的蓋子可以防止倉鼠在旅途中跑走。"},{"en":"If the mice run away, the experiment may become unsafe or disorganised.","zh":"如果小鼠跑走，實驗可能變得不安全或混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the practical purpose of using a container.","zh":"這個短語解釋使用容器的實際目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sound complicated","meaning":"聽起來很複雜","examples":[{"en":"The weighing chamber sounds complicated.","zh":"稱重室聽起來很複雜。"},{"en":"To sound complicated means to seem difficult or complex when described.","zh":"sound complicated 是指描述起來似乎困難或複雜。"},{"en":"A recipe may sound complicated before you see that it only has three steps.","zh":"食譜在你看到只有三個步驟前，可能聽起來很複雜。"},{"en":"Some tools sound complicated because their names are technical, even if they are simple.","zh":"有些工具因名稱技術性強而聽起來很複雜，即使其實很簡單。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a first impression, not necessarily the real difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述第一印象，不一定是真實難度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"plastic box with holes in the top","meaning":"頂部有洞的膠盒","examples":[{"en":"A weighing chamber can be a plastic box with holes in the top.","zh":"稱重室可以是一個頂部有洞的膠盒。"},{"en":"A plastic box with holes in the top is a simple container that lets air in while keeping something inside.","zh":"plastic box with holes in the top 是一個簡單容器，可以讓空氣進入，同時把東西留在裏面。"},{"en":"A child might keep insects briefly in a plastic box with holes in the top for observation.","zh":"孩子可能暫時把昆蟲放在頂部有洞的膠盒中觀察。"},{"en":"Holes in the top are important because living animals need air.","zh":"頂部有洞很重要，因為活的動物需要空氣。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear physical description of a simple piece of equipment.","zh":"這個短語清楚描述一件簡單設備的外形。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"measure the weight gain","meaning":"測量體重增加量","examples":[{"en":"Clare will measure the weight gain of each mouse.","zh":"Clare 會測量每隻小鼠的體重增加量。"},{"en":"To measure the weight gain means to record how much heavier something becomes over time.","zh":"measure the weight gain 是指記錄某物隨時間變重了多少。"},{"en":"A doctor may measure a baby’s weight gain to check healthy growth.","zh":"醫生可能測量嬰兒體重增加量，以檢查是否健康成長。"},{"en":"Measuring weight gain helps show whether diet or activity is affecting the body.","zh":"測量體重增加量有助顯示飲食或活動是否影響身體。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on change in weight, not just one weight reading.","zh":"這個短語著重體重變化，而不只是一次體重讀數。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"work out the average","meaning":"計算平均值","examples":[{"en":"The students can work out the average for each group.","zh":"學生可以計算每組的平均值。"},{"en":"To work out the average means to calculate the central value by adding numbers and dividing by how many there are.","zh":"work out the average 是指把數字加起來，再除以數字的數量，以計算中心數值。"},{"en":"Students work out the average test score by adding all scores and dividing by the number of students.","zh":"學生把所有分數加起來，再除以學生人數，便能計算平均測驗分。"},{"en":"Averages help compare groups, but they may hide individual differences.","zh":"平均值有助比較組別，但可能掩蓋個別差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is commonly used in maths, science, and everyday data.","zh":"這個短語常用於數學、科學和日常數據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"standard deviation","meaning":"標準差","examples":[{"en":"The students can calculate the average and the standard deviation.","zh":"學生可以計算平均值和標準差。"},{"en":"Standard deviation is a number that shows how spread out a set of data is.","zh":"standard deviation 是顯示一組數據分散程度的數字。"},{"en":"If test scores are close together, the standard deviation is small.","zh":"如果測驗分數彼此接近，標準差就小。"},{"en":"A large standard deviation means the results vary a lot from person to person or item to item.","zh":"標準差大代表結果在人與人或項目與項目之間差異很大。"},{"en":"This term helps students understand not only the average, but also the variation.","zh":"這個詞幫助學生不只理解平均值，也理解變異程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"see where we go from there","meaning":"再看看下一步怎樣做","examples":[{"en":"After analysing the results, the students can see where they go from there.","zh":"分析結果後，學生可以再看看下一步怎樣做。"},{"en":"To see where we go from there means to decide the next step after looking at what happens first.","zh":"see where we go from there 是指先看看發生甚麼，再決定下一步。"},{"en":"A team may try one advertising idea and then see where they go from there.","zh":"團隊可能先嘗試一個廣告想法，然後再看看下一步怎樣做。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the next decision depends on the first results.","zh":"當下一個決定取決於初步結果時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It suggests flexibility rather than a fixed plan from the beginning.","zh":"它表示保持彈性，而不是從一開始就固定所有計劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"that sounds cool","meaning":"那聽起來很不錯","examples":[{"en":"Clare thinks the experiment sounds cool.","zh":"Clare 覺得這個實驗聽起來很不錯。"},{"en":"That sounds cool means that idea seems interesting, enjoyable, or impressive.","zh":"that sounds cool 是指那個想法聽起來有趣、好玩或令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"A student may say, “That sounds cool,” when a friend describes a science club trip.","zh":"朋友描述科學社旅行時，學生可能會說：「那聽起來很不錯。」"},{"en":"People use this phrase to show positive reaction in an informal way.","zh":"人們用這個短語以非正式方式表達正面反應。"},{"en":"It is warmer and more casual than saying “That seems acceptable.”","zh":"它比說「那似乎可以接受」更溫暖、更口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the students will enjoy it","meaning":"學生會喜歡它","examples":[{"en":"Clare thinks the students will enjoy the experiment.","zh":"Clare 認為學生會喜歡這個實驗。"},{"en":"The students will enjoy it means the learners will find the activity interesting or pleasant.","zh":"the students will enjoy it 是指學習者會覺得這項活動有趣或愉快。"},{"en":"A teacher may choose a group game because she thinks the students will enjoy it.","zh":"老師可能選擇小組遊戲，因為她認為學生會喜歡它。"},{"en":"Students enjoy activities more when they are practical, clear, and connected to real questions.","zh":"當活動實用、清楚並與真實問題有關，學生會更喜歡。"},{"en":"This phrase predicts a positive reaction from the class.","zh":"這個短語預測班上會有正面反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 7/task-4":[{"front":"in today’s lecture","meaning":"在今天的講座中","examples":[{"en":"In today’s lecture, the speaker is going to talk about microplastics.","zh":"在今天的講座中，講者將會談論微塑膠。"},{"en":"In today’s lecture means during the lecture that is taking place today.","zh":"in today’s lecture意思是在今天進行的講座中。"},{"en":"In today’s lecture, the teacher will explain how plastic pollution enters rivers and oceans.","zh":"在今天的講座中，老師會解釋塑膠污染如何進入河流和海洋。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase at the beginning to tell listeners what topic will be covered.","zh":"講者在開始時使用這個短語，告訴聽眾將會涵蓋甚麼主題。"},{"en":"This phrase helps students know the time and setting of the talk.","zh":"這個短語幫助學生知道講座的時間和場合。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be talking about","meaning":"談論……","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer is going to be talking about microplastics.","zh":"講師將會談論微塑膠。"},{"en":"To be talking about something means to discuss or explain that topic.","zh":"be talking about某事，意思是討論或解釋該主題。"},{"en":"In the science lesson, students were talking about how rainwater carries waste into drains.","zh":"在科學課中，學生正在談論雨水如何把廢物帶入排水渠。"},{"en":"When a speaker says what they will be talking about, listeners can prepare for the main subject.","zh":"當講者說自己將會談論甚麼，聽眾就能為主題作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when introducing a topic in a lecture or conversation.","zh":"這個短語常用於介紹講座或對話中的主題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"microplastics","meaning":"微塑膠","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics are tiny pieces of plastic smaller than five millimetres.","zh":"微塑膠是小於五毫米的微小塑膠碎片。"},{"en":"Microplastics are very small plastic particles that can come from broken plastic waste or synthetic materials.","zh":"microplastics是非常細小的塑膠顆粒，可能來自碎裂塑膠廢物或合成物料。"},{"en":"Microplastics may enter water when clothes made from synthetic fibres are washed.","zh":"當合成纖維衣物被清洗時，微塑膠可能進入水中。"},{"en":"Because they are tiny, microplastics can be difficult to see, collect or remove.","zh":"因為微塑膠非常細小，所以可能難以看見、收集或移除。"},{"en":"This word is often used in discussions of pollution, food safety and ecosystems.","zh":"這個詞常用於污染、食物安全和生態系統的討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tiny pieces of plastic","meaning":"微小塑膠碎片","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics are tiny pieces of plastic.","zh":"微塑膠是微小塑膠碎片。"},{"en":"Tiny pieces of plastic are very small fragments of plastic material.","zh":"tiny pieces of plastic是非常細小的塑膠材料碎片。"},{"en":"A broken plastic bag can slowly become tiny pieces of plastic after sunlight and weather damage it.","zh":"破爛膠袋經陽光和天氣破壞後，可能慢慢變成微小塑膠碎片。"},{"en":"Tiny plastic pieces are concerning because animals may mistake them for food.","zh":"微小塑膠碎片令人擔心，因為動物可能把它們誤認為食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the size and material of microplastics in simple words.","zh":"這個短語用簡單語言描述微塑膠的大小和材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"smaller than","meaning":"小於……","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics are smaller than five millimetres in size.","zh":"微塑膠尺寸小於五毫米。"},{"en":"Smaller than means having a lower size, amount or measurement than something else.","zh":"smaller than意思是在尺寸、數量或量度上比另一物更小。"},{"en":"A grain of rice is smaller than a pencil, so it is easier to lose on the floor.","zh":"一粒米小於一支鉛筆，所以掉在地上較容易遺失。"},{"en":"If particles are smaller than a few millimetres, they can be hard to pick out by hand.","zh":"如果顆粒小於幾毫米，就可能難以用手挑出來。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to compare size clearly.","zh":"這個短語用來清楚比較大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"five millimetres in size","meaning":"尺寸為五毫米","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics are smaller than five millimetres in size.","zh":"微塑膠尺寸小於五毫米。"},{"en":"Five millimetres in size means measuring five millimetres across or in length.","zh":"five millimetres in size意思是闊度或長度量度為五毫米。"},{"en":"A small bead may be about five millimetres in size, so it can be hard to notice on a busy floor.","zh":"一粒小珠可能約五毫米大小，所以在繁忙地面上可能難以察覺。"},{"en":"Scientists use size limits to decide whether a plastic particle counts as a microplastic.","zh":"科學家使用尺寸限制來判斷塑膠顆粒是否屬於微塑膠。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise measurement.","zh":"這個短語給出精確量度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"greater awareness","meaning":"更高意識","examples":[{"en":"Recently there has been greater awareness of plastic waste in the environment.","zh":"近來，人們對環境中的塑膠廢物有更高意識。"},{"en":"Greater awareness means more people know about an issue and understand why it matters.","zh":"greater awareness意思是更多人知道某個議題並理解其重要性。"},{"en":"Schools can create greater awareness of recycling by showing students where rubbish goes after collection.","zh":"學校可以透過向學生展示垃圾收集後去了哪裡，提升他們對回收的意識。"},{"en":"Greater awareness can lead to changes in behaviour, laws and public pressure.","zh":"更高意識可以帶來行為、法律和公眾壓力上的改變。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that concern and knowledge have increased.","zh":"這個短語暗示關注和認識有所增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"large quantities of","meaning":"大量……","examples":[{"en":"There are large quantities of plastic waste in the environment.","zh":"環境中有大量塑膠廢物。"},{"en":"Large quantities of something means a great amount of it.","zh":"large quantities of某物，意思是大量該物。"},{"en":"A school canteen may produce large quantities of food packaging during lunch time.","zh":"學校飯堂在午飯時間可能產生大量食物包裝。"},{"en":"Large quantities of waste are harder to collect, sort and manage safely.","zh":"大量廢物較難安全地收集、分類和管理。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the amount is big enough to matter.","zh":"這個短語強調數量大到值得關注。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"plastic waste","meaning":"塑膠廢物","examples":[{"en":"Plastic waste can be found in the environment.","zh":"塑膠廢物可以在環境中被發現。"},{"en":"Plastic waste is used plastic material that has been thrown away or left unused.","zh":"plastic waste是被丟棄或不再使用的塑膠材料。"},{"en":"Empty drink bottles, food wrappers and broken containers can become plastic waste.","zh":"空飲品樽、食物包裝和破爛容器都可以變成塑膠廢物。"},{"en":"Plastic waste can remain in the environment for a long time and break into smaller pieces.","zh":"塑膠廢物可以在環境中停留很久，並分裂成更小碎片。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing pollution and waste management.","zh":"這個短語常用於污染和廢物管理討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the environment","meaning":"在環境中","examples":[{"en":"Large quantities of plastic waste are found in the environment.","zh":"大量塑膠廢物存在於環境中。"},{"en":"In the environment means in the natural world around us, including air, water, soil and living things.","zh":"in the environment意思是在我們周圍的自然世界中，包括空氣、水、土壤和生物。"},{"en":"Chemicals in the environment can affect plants, animals and human health.","zh":"環境中的化學物質可以影響植物、動物和人類健康。"},{"en":"Waste in the environment can move through rain, wind and rivers.","zh":"環境中的廢物可以透過雨水、風和河流移動。"},{"en":"This phrase places a problem outside controlled places like factories or bins.","zh":"這個短語把問題放在工廠或垃圾箱等受控地方以外。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the amount of","meaning":"……的數量","examples":[{"en":"The amount of plastic waste in the oceans has received widespread attention.","zh":"海洋中塑膠廢物的數量受到廣泛關注。"},{"en":"The amount of something means how much of it there is.","zh":"the amount of某物，意思是該物有多少。"},{"en":"The amount of homework can affect how much sleep students get.","zh":"功課的數量可以影響學生有多少睡眠。"},{"en":"When the amount of waste increases, the cost of managing it also rises.","zh":"當廢物數量增加，管理它的成本也會上升。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to discuss quantity.","zh":"這個短語用於討論數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"receive widespread attention","meaning":"受到廣泛關注","examples":[{"en":"Plastic waste in the oceans has received widespread attention.","zh":"海洋中的塑膠廢物已受到廣泛關注。"},{"en":"To receive widespread attention means to be noticed or discussed by many people.","zh":"receive widespread attention意思是被許多人注意或討論。"},{"en":"A safety problem at school may receive widespread attention if parents and newspapers discuss it.","zh":"如果家長和報紙討論校園安全問題，該問題可能受到廣泛關注。"},{"en":"Issues receive widespread attention when they affect many people or feel urgent.","zh":"當議題影響很多人或感覺迫切，它就會受到廣泛關注。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a topic has become publicly important.","zh":"這個短語顯示某主題已變得具公共重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"far less is known about","meaning":"人們對……了解少得多","examples":[{"en":"Far less is known about the effects of microplastics in soil.","zh":"人們對微塑膠在土壤中的影響了解少得多。"},{"en":"Far less is known about something means people have much less information or understanding about it.","zh":"far less is known about某事，意思是人們對它有少得多資料或理解。"},{"en":"Far less is known about a new illness when doctors have only seen a few cases.","zh":"當醫生只見過少數病例，人們對一種新疾病了解少得多。"},{"en":"When less is known, scientists need more studies before making firm conclusions.","zh":"當了解較少，科學家需要更多研究才可作出確定結論。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a knowledge gap.","zh":"這個短語突顯知識缺口。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the effects of","meaning":"……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are studying the effects of microplastics in freshwater and soil.","zh":"科學家正在研究微塑膠在淡水和土壤中的影響。"},{"en":"The effects of something are the changes or results it causes.","zh":"the effects of某事，是它造成的變化或結果。"},{"en":"Teachers may study the effects of sleep on students’ memory and attention.","zh":"老師可能研究睡眠對學生記憶和專注力的影響。"},{"en":"Understanding effects helps people decide whether something is harmful, helpful or neutral.","zh":"理解影響有助人判斷某事是有害、有益還是中性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing causes and results.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論原因和結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"freshwater","meaning":"淡水","examples":[{"en":"Far less is known about microplastics in freshwater.","zh":"人們對淡水中的微塑膠了解少得多。"},{"en":"Freshwater is water that is not salty, such as water in rivers, lakes and streams.","zh":"freshwater是不含鹽的水，例如河流、湖泊和溪流中的水。"},{"en":"Many communities depend on freshwater for drinking, farming and washing.","zh":"許多社區依賴淡水作飲用、農耕和清洗。"},{"en":"Pollution in freshwater can affect fish, plants and people who use it.","zh":"淡水污染可以影響魚類、植物和使用它的人。"},{"en":"This word contrasts with seawater or salt water.","zh":"這個詞與海水或鹽水形成對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"particularly in soil","meaning":"尤其是在土壤中","examples":[{"en":"The effects of microplastics are less understood, particularly in soil.","zh":"微塑膠的影響較少被理解，尤其是在土壤中。"},{"en":"Particularly in soil means especially in soil, more than in other places mentioned.","zh":"particularly in soil意思是尤其在土壤中，比提到的其他地方更值得注意。"},{"en":"Pollution is hard to remove from the environment, particularly in soil where particles can stay hidden.","zh":"污染很難從環境中移除，尤其是在顆粒可以隱藏的土壤中。"},{"en":"Soil matters because it supports plants, insects and farming.","zh":"土壤很重要，因為它支撐植物、昆蟲和農業。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows attention to soil as an important case.","zh":"這個短語把注意力收窄到土壤這個重要情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"enter the environment","meaning":"進入環境","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics can enter the environment through different sources.","zh":"微塑膠可以透過不同來源進入環境。"},{"en":"To enter the environment means to get into nature instead of staying inside controlled human systems.","zh":"enter the environment意思是進入自然界，而不是停留在人類可控制的系統中。"},{"en":"Oil can enter the environment if it leaks from a broken machine into a river.","zh":"如果破損機器漏油入河，油就會進入環境。"},{"en":"Once pollutants enter the environment, they may spread through water, air and soil.","zh":"污染物一旦進入環境，就可能透過水、空氣和土壤擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when explaining how pollution begins.","zh":"這個短語用於解釋污染如何開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"via a number of","meaning":"透過多個……","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics can enter the environment via a number of sources.","zh":"微塑膠可以透過多個來源進入環境。"},{"en":"Via a number of something means through several different routes, methods or sources.","zh":"via a number of某物，意思是透過幾個不同途徑、方法或來源。"},{"en":"Students can receive school notices via a number of channels, such as email, apps and paper letters.","zh":"學生可以透過多個渠道收到學校通知，例如電郵、應用程式和紙本信件。"},{"en":"When a problem enters via many sources, it becomes harder to control.","zh":"當問題透過多個來源進入，就會更難控制。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights multiple pathways.","zh":"這個短語突顯多重途徑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"different sources","meaning":"不同來源","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics come from a number of different sources.","zh":"微塑膠來自多個不同來源。"},{"en":"Different sources are several places, causes or origins from which something comes.","zh":"different sources是某物來自的幾個地方、原因或源頭。"},{"en":"A news report should use different sources to check whether information is reliable.","zh":"新聞報道應使用不同來源來查證資料是否可靠。"},{"en":"Pollution from different sources may require different solutions.","zh":"來自不同來源的污染可能需要不同解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that one problem may not have only one origin.","zh":"這個短語強調一個問題未必只有一個源頭。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"threads and microfibres","meaning":"線頭和微纖維","examples":[{"en":"Threads and microfibres detach from synthetic clothing.","zh":"線頭和微纖維會從合成纖維衣物脫落。"},{"en":"Threads and microfibres are very thin pieces of material that can come loose from fabric.","zh":"threads and microfibres是可以從布料鬆脫出來的非常幼細材料。"},{"en":"Tiny fibres may come off a fleece jacket when it is washed.","zh":"抓毛外套清洗時，可能會脫落微小纖維。"},{"en":"When many clothes shed fibres, small pieces can enter water systems.","zh":"當許多衣物脫落纖維，小碎片就可能進入水系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes small textile materials that can become pollution.","zh":"這個短語描述可能變成污染的細小紡織材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"detach from","meaning":"從……脫落","examples":[{"en":"Microfibres detach from synthetic clothing in the washing machine.","zh":"微纖維會在洗衣機中從合成纖維衣物脫落。"},{"en":"To detach from something means to come off or separate from it.","zh":"detach from某物，意思是從它上面脫落或分離。"},{"en":"A button may detach from a shirt if the thread becomes loose.","zh":"如果線變鬆，鈕扣可能從恤衫脫落。"},{"en":"When fibres detach from clothes, they can travel with wastewater.","zh":"當纖維從衣物脫落，它們可以隨污水流走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes separation from a larger object.","zh":"這個短語描述從較大物件分離。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"synthetic clothing","meaning":"合成纖維衣物","examples":[{"en":"Microfibres can come from synthetic clothing.","zh":"微纖維可以來自合成纖維衣物。"},{"en":"Synthetic clothing is clothing made from man-made materials such as polyester or nylon.","zh":"synthetic clothing是由人造物料如聚酯或尼龍製成的衣物。"},{"en":"Sports shirts and fleece jackets are often made from synthetic clothing materials.","zh":"運動衫和抓毛外套常由合成纖維衣物材料製成。"},{"en":"Synthetic fabrics can release tiny fibres when they are washed or worn.","zh":"合成纖維布料在清洗或穿着時可以釋放微小纖維。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts man-made fabrics with natural materials like cotton or wool.","zh":"這個短語把人造布料與棉或羊毛等天然材料作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"washing machine","meaning":"洗衣機","examples":[{"en":"Threads and microfibres detach when clothes are put in a washing machine.","zh":"衣物放入洗衣機時，線頭和微纖維會脫落。"},{"en":"A washing machine is a household machine used to wash clothes with water and detergent.","zh":"washing machine是用水和洗衣劑清洗衣物的家用機器。"},{"en":"Families often use a washing machine several times a week for uniforms and towels.","zh":"家庭常每星期多次使用洗衣機清洗校服和毛巾。"},{"en":"Washing can loosen fibres from clothing and carry them away in wastewater.","zh":"洗衣可以令衣物纖維鬆脫，並隨污水被帶走。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an everyday appliance linked here to microfibre pollution.","zh":"這個短語指日常家電，在此與微纖維污染相關。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"find their way into","meaning":"進入；流入","examples":[{"en":"Microfibres find their way into the water system.","zh":"微纖維會進入水系統。"},{"en":"To find their way into a place means to enter it, often gradually or indirectly.","zh":"find their way into某地，意思是逐漸或間接進入那裡。"},{"en":"Dust can find its way into a room even when the windows are closed.","zh":"即使窗戶關上，灰塵也可能進入房間。"},{"en":"Tiny fibres find their way into drains when wastewater leaves the washing machine.","zh":"當洗衣機排出污水，微小纖維會流入排水渠。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests movement into a place without being deliberately put there.","zh":"這個短語暗示某物並非被刻意放入，但仍進入某地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"water system","meaning":"水系統","examples":[{"en":"Microfibres from clothing can enter the water system.","zh":"來自衣物的微纖維可以進入水系統。"},{"en":"A water system is the network of pipes, drains, rivers or treatment facilities through which water moves.","zh":"water system是水流經的管道、排水渠、河流或處理設施網絡。"},{"en":"Dirty water from homes enters the water system through drains and sewers.","zh":"家居污水透過排水渠和污水渠進入水系統。"},{"en":"Pollution in the water system can spread beyond one house or street.","zh":"水系統中的污染可以擴散到一間屋或一條街以外。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the connected routes through which water travels.","zh":"這個短語指水流動的連接路線。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"big pieces of plastic waste","meaning":"大件塑膠廢物","examples":[{"en":"Big pieces of plastic waste can break down into smaller particles.","zh":"大件塑膠廢物可以分解成較小顆粒。"},{"en":"Big pieces of plastic waste are large discarded plastic items such as bottles, bags or containers.","zh":"big pieces of plastic waste是較大的被丟棄塑膠物品，例如膠樽、膠袋或容器。"},{"en":"A broken beach toy left in the sun can become a big piece of plastic waste.","zh":"留在陽光下的破爛沙灘玩具可以變成大件塑膠廢物。"},{"en":"Over time, large plastic waste can crack, fragment and create smaller particles.","zh":"隨着時間過去，大件塑膠廢物可以裂開、碎裂並產生較小顆粒。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts visible plastic rubbish with tiny microplastics.","zh":"這個短語把可見塑膠垃圾與微小微塑膠作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"already in the environment","meaning":"已存在於環境中","examples":[{"en":"Some plastic waste is already in the environment.","zh":"有些塑膠廢物已存在於環境中。"},{"en":"Already in the environment means it has entered nature and is no longer controlled or contained.","zh":"already in the environment意思是它已進入自然界，不再受控制或被妥善存放。"},{"en":"Old rubbish already in the environment may stay in rivers, soil or beaches for years.","zh":"已存在於環境中的舊垃圾，可能多年留在河流、土壤或海灘中。"},{"en":"Once waste is already in the environment, cleaning it up becomes more difficult.","zh":"廢物一旦已存在於環境中，清理就會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the pollution problem has already begun.","zh":"這個短語顯示污染問題已經開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"break down into","meaning":"分解成……","examples":[{"en":"Plastic waste can break down into microscopic particles.","zh":"塑膠廢物可以分解成微小顆粒。"},{"en":"To break down into something means to separate or decay into smaller parts.","zh":"break down into某物，意思是分裂或分解成較小部分。"},{"en":"A biscuit can break down into crumbs if it is crushed in a school bag.","zh":"餅乾如果在書包中被壓碎，可以碎成餅屑。"},{"en":"Plastic breaks down slowly, creating smaller pieces that may spread more easily.","zh":"塑膠慢慢分解，產生較小碎片，可能更容易擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change from larger material to smaller parts.","zh":"這個短語描述由較大材料變成較小部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"microscopic particles","meaning":"微小顆粒","examples":[{"en":"Plastic waste can break down into microscopic particles.","zh":"塑膠廢物可以分解成微小顆粒。"},{"en":"Microscopic particles are extremely small pieces that are difficult or impossible to see without special equipment.","zh":"microscopic particles是非常細小、沒有特殊設備就難以或無法看見的顆粒。"},{"en":"Dust in the air may contain microscopic particles that people cannot notice with their eyes.","zh":"空氣中的灰塵可能含有肉眼看不見的微小顆粒。"},{"en":"Because microscopic particles are so small, they can move through water, air and soil easily.","zh":"因為微小顆粒很細，它們可以容易地穿過水、空氣和土壤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes particles at a very tiny scale.","zh":"這個短語描述非常細微尺度的顆粒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"over a period of time","meaning":"經過一段時間","examples":[{"en":"Plastic waste breaks down over a period of time.","zh":"塑膠廢物經過一段時間會分解。"},{"en":"Over a period of time means gradually during a length of time, not immediately.","zh":"over a period of time意思是在一段時間內逐漸發生，而不是立即發生。"},{"en":"A student improves writing over a period of time by practising and receiving feedback.","zh":"學生透過練習和取得回饋，經過一段時間改善寫作。"},{"en":"Some changes happen slowly, so people may not notice them at first.","zh":"有些變化慢慢發生，所以人們起初可能不會注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses gradual development.","zh":"這個短語強調逐步發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on a larger scale","meaning":"從更大規模來看","examples":[{"en":"On a larger scale, factory waste is another route for microplastics.","zh":"從更大規模來看，工廠廢料是微塑膠的另一途徑。"},{"en":"On a larger scale means looking at a bigger level, amount or system.","zh":"on a larger scale意思是從更大的層面、數量或系統來看。"},{"en":"A class recycling plan works in one room; on a larger scale, the whole school needs bins and collection schedules.","zh":"班級回收計劃在一間課室可行；從更大規模來看，整間學校需要回收箱和收集時間表。"},{"en":"Problems can look different when they are considered beyond individual households.","zh":"當問題被放到個別家庭以外考慮，它可能顯得不同。"},{"en":"This phrase shifts attention from small examples to bigger systems.","zh":"這個短語把注意力由小例子轉向更大系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"factory waste","meaning":"工廠廢料","examples":[{"en":"Factory waste is another route by which microplastics enter the environment.","zh":"工廠廢料是微塑膠進入環境的另一途徑。"},{"en":"Factory waste is unwanted material or pollution produced by industrial production.","zh":"factory waste是工業生產所產生的不需要材料或污染物。"},{"en":"A factory may produce waste from packaging, chemicals, plastic pellets or leftover materials.","zh":"工廠可能產生包裝、化學品、塑膠粒或剩餘材料等廢料。"},{"en":"If factory waste is not controlled, it can enter rivers, soil or air.","zh":"如果工廠廢料沒有受控，它可以進入河流、土壤或空氣。"},{"en":"This phrase connects industrial activity with pollution.","zh":"這個短語把工業活動與污染連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"another route","meaning":"另一途徑","examples":[{"en":"Factory waste is another route for microplastics to enter the environment.","zh":"工廠廢料是微塑膠進入環境的另一途徑。"},{"en":"Another route means an additional way or pathway for something to happen.","zh":"another route意思是某事發生的另一種方法或途徑。"},{"en":"If the main road is closed, a bus driver may choose another route to reach the station.","zh":"如果主要道路封閉，巴士司機可能選擇另一途徑到達車站。"},{"en":"Pollution can spread through another route when one source is controlled but others remain.","zh":"當一個來源受控但其他來源仍存在，污染可以透過另一途徑擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that there is more than one pathway.","zh":"這個短語顯示不止一條路徑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"tyres","meaning":"車胎","examples":[{"en":"Tyres produce microplastics as they wear down on roads.","zh":"車胎在路上磨損時會產生微塑膠。"},{"en":"Tyres are the rubber outer parts of wheels on cars, lorries and bicycles.","zh":"tyres是汽車、貨車和單車車輪外層的橡膠部分。"},{"en":"Drivers need safe tyres because worn tyres can reduce control on wet roads.","zh":"司機需要安全車胎，因為磨損車胎會降低濕滑路面上的控制力。"},{"en":"As tyres rub against road surfaces, tiny particles can be released.","zh":"當車胎與路面摩擦，微小顆粒可以被釋放。"},{"en":"This word is important here because road transport can create microplastic pollution.","zh":"這個詞在此很重要，因為道路交通可以產生微塑膠污染。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"wear down","meaning":"磨損","examples":[{"en":"Tyres wear down as vehicles travel along road surfaces.","zh":"車輛沿着路面行駛時，車胎會磨損。"},{"en":"To wear down means to become thinner, weaker or damaged through repeated use or rubbing.","zh":"wear down意思是因反覆使用或摩擦而變薄、變弱或受損。"},{"en":"School shoes wear down quickly if a student walks long distances every day.","zh":"如果學生每天走很遠，校鞋會很快磨損。"},{"en":"When tyres wear down, small particles may be released onto roads.","zh":"當車胎磨損，細小顆粒可能被釋放到路面上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual damage from use.","zh":"這個短語描述因使用造成的逐漸損耗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lorries and so on","meaning":"貨車等等","examples":[{"en":"Cars, lorries and so on wear down tyres on road surfaces.","zh":"汽車、貨車等等會在路面上磨損車胎。"},{"en":"Lorries and so on means lorries and other similar vehicles.","zh":"lorries and so on意思是貨車和其他類似車輛。"},{"en":"Buses, vans, lorries and so on all add traffic to busy city roads.","zh":"巴士、客貨車、貨車等等都會增加繁忙城市道路的交通量。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids listing every example when the category is already clear.","zh":"當類別已經清楚，這個短語避免列出每個例子。"},{"en":"It is useful in spoken explanations and informal lists.","zh":"它適合用於口頭解釋和較非正式列表。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"travel along","meaning":"沿着……行駛","examples":[{"en":"Vehicles travel along road surfaces and wear down their tyres.","zh":"車輛沿着路面行駛並磨損車胎。"},{"en":"To travel along something means to move on or beside a route or surface.","zh":"travel along某物，意思是在一條路線或表面上移動。"},{"en":"Buses travel along the main road before turning into the school area.","zh":"巴士沿着主要道路行駛，然後轉入學校區域。"},{"en":"Repeated movement along a surface can create friction and wear.","zh":"反覆沿着表面移動可以產生摩擦和磨損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement following a path.","zh":"這個短語描述沿路徑移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"road surfaces","meaning":"路面","examples":[{"en":"Tyres wear down as vehicles move along road surfaces.","zh":"車輛沿路面行駛時，車胎會磨損。"},{"en":"Road surfaces are the top layers of roads that vehicles drive on.","zh":"road surfaces是車輛行駛的道路最上層。"},{"en":"Wet road surfaces can make braking more difficult for drivers.","zh":"濕滑路面可以令司機煞車更困難。"},{"en":"Tyres rub against road surfaces, which can release tiny particles.","zh":"車胎與路面摩擦，可能釋放細小顆粒。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the physical part of the road that touches the tyres.","zh":"這個短語指與車胎接觸的道路實體部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"understand some of the impacts of","meaning":"了解……的一些影響","examples":[{"en":"Scientists already understand some of the impacts of microplastics.","zh":"科學家已了解微塑膠的一些影響。"},{"en":"To understand some of the impacts of something means to know part of how it affects people, animals or systems.","zh":"understand some of the impacts of某事，意思是知道它如何影響人、動物或系統的一部分。"},{"en":"Doctors understand some of the impacts of poor sleep on memory and mood.","zh":"醫生了解睡眠不足對記憶和心情的一些影響。"},{"en":"Knowing only some impacts means more research may still be needed.","zh":"只知道一些影響，意思是仍可能需要更多研究。"},{"en":"This phrase shows partial knowledge, not complete certainty.","zh":"這個短語顯示部分知識，而不是完全確定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"studies involving","meaning":"涉及……的研究","examples":[{"en":"The impacts of microplastics are known from studies involving fish.","zh":"微塑膠的影響來自涉及魚類的研究。"},{"en":"Studies involving something are research projects that include that subject, group or material.","zh":"studies involving某物，是包括該主題、群體或材料的研究項目。"},{"en":"Studies involving children must be carefully designed to protect their safety and privacy.","zh":"涉及兒童的研究必須仔細設計，以保護他們的安全和私隱。"},{"en":"Research involving animals can help scientists observe effects that are hard to see directly in humans.","zh":"涉及動物的研究可以幫助科學家觀察在人類身上難以直接看見的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what or who is included in a study.","zh":"這個短語指出研究包括甚麼或哪些對象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"other animals","meaning":"其他動物","examples":[{"en":"Studies involving fish and other animals show some impacts of microplastics.","zh":"涉及魚類和其他動物的研究顯示微塑膠的一些影響。"},{"en":"Other animals means animals apart from the ones already mentioned.","zh":"other animals意思是除了已提及動物以外的動物。"},{"en":"A zoo may care for birds, reptiles and other animals in different areas.","zh":"動物園可能在不同區域照顧鳥類、爬蟲類和其他動物。"},{"en":"Studying different animals can show whether a problem affects only one species or many.","zh":"研究不同動物可以顯示問題只影響一個物種還是許多物種。"},{"en":"This phrase broadens the group beyond the first example.","zh":"這個短語把群體由第一個例子擴闊出去。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"there is evidence that","meaning":"有證據顯示……","examples":[{"en":"There is evidence that microplastics harm small creatures.","zh":"有證據顯示微塑膠會傷害小型生物。"},{"en":"There is evidence that means facts, observations or research support a claim.","zh":"there is evidence that意思是有事實、觀察或研究支持某聲稱。"},{"en":"There is evidence that regular reading improves vocabulary over time.","zh":"有證據顯示定期閱讀會隨時間改善詞彙。"},{"en":"Evidence makes a statement stronger than a guess or personal belief.","zh":"證據令陳述比猜測或個人信念更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase is careful because evidence may support a claim without proving every detail.","zh":"這個短語較謹慎，因為證據可能支持聲稱但未必證明每個細節。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"harm small creatures","meaning":"傷害小型生物","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics can harm small creatures in a variety of ways.","zh":"微塑膠可以以多種方式傷害小型生物。"},{"en":"To harm small creatures means to injure or damage tiny animals or living organisms.","zh":"harm small creatures意思是傷害或損害細小動物或生物。"},{"en":"Chemicals in a pond may harm small creatures such as insects, tadpoles and tiny fish.","zh":"池塘中的化學物質可能傷害昆蟲、蝌蚪和小魚等小型生物。"},{"en":"When small creatures are harmed, larger animals that eat them may also be affected.","zh":"當小型生物受害，捕食牠們的大型動物也可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase links pollution with damage to living things.","zh":"這個短語把污染與對生物的傷害連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in a variety of ways","meaning":"以多種方式","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics harm small creatures in a variety of ways.","zh":"微塑膠以多種方式傷害小型生物。"},{"en":"In a variety of ways means in several different ways.","zh":"in a variety of ways意思是以幾種不同方式。"},{"en":"Teachers can help students in a variety of ways, such as giving examples, feedback and practice.","zh":"老師可以以多種方式幫助學生，例如提供例子、回饋和練習。"},{"en":"A problem with many effects may need more than one solution.","zh":"有多種影響的問題可能需要多於一種解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the impact is not limited to one method.","zh":"這個短語顯示影響不限於一種方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"such as by","meaning":"例如透過……","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics can harm creatures, such as by damaging their mouths.","zh":"微塑膠可以傷害生物，例如透過損傷牠們的口部。"},{"en":"Such as by means for example, through this method or action.","zh":"such as by意思是例如透過這種方法或行動。"},{"en":"Schools can save energy, such as by turning off lights after class.","zh":"學校可以節省能源，例如透過下課後關燈。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a specific way in which something happens.","zh":"這個短語引入某事發生的一個具體方式。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining a general effect with a concrete example.","zh":"當用具體例子解釋一般影響時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"damage their mouths","meaning":"損傷牠們的口部","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics can damage the mouths of small creatures.","zh":"微塑膠可以損傷小型生物的口部。"},{"en":"To damage their mouths means to injure the parts they use for eating or taking in food.","zh":"damage their mouths意思是傷害牠們用來進食或攝取食物的部位。"},{"en":"Sharp rubbish in a pond can damage small animals’ mouths when they try to feed.","zh":"池塘中的尖銳垃圾可能在小動物嘗試進食時損傷牠們的口部。"},{"en":"If an animal’s mouth is damaged, it may struggle to eat enough food.","zh":"如果動物口部受損，牠可能難以吃到足夠食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical injury that can affect survival.","zh":"這個短語描述可能影響生存的身體傷害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"impair their ability to","meaning":"損害牠們……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics can impair animals’ ability to feed.","zh":"微塑膠可以損害動物進食的能力。"},{"en":"To impair someone’s ability to do something means to make it harder or less effective for them to do it.","zh":"impair someone’s ability to do something意思是令某人做某事變得更困難或較無效。"},{"en":"Poor eyesight can impair a driver’s ability to read road signs quickly.","zh":"視力差可以損害司機快速閱讀路牌的能力。"},{"en":"If pollution impairs an animal’s ability to feed, the animal may become weaker over time.","zh":"如果污染損害動物進食能力，動物可能隨時間變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage to function, not necessarily complete loss.","zh":"這個短語描述功能受損，而不一定是完全喪失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ability to feed","meaning":"進食能力","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics may impair small creatures’ ability to feed.","zh":"微塑膠可能損害小型生物的進食能力。"},{"en":"Ability to feed means the ability to find, take in and eat enough food.","zh":"ability to feed意思是尋找、攝取和吃到足夠食物的能力。"},{"en":"A bird with an injured beak may lose its ability to feed properly.","zh":"喙受傷的鳥可能失去正常進食能力。"},{"en":"If creatures cannot feed well, they may grow slowly or die.","zh":"如果生物不能好好進食，牠們可能生長緩慢或死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase is important because feeding is basic to survival.","zh":"這個短語很重要，因為進食是生存基礎。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"for example when","meaning":"例如當……時","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics may cause harm, for example when they get lodged in the digestive system.","zh":"微塑膠可能造成傷害，例如當它們卡在消化系統時。"},{"en":"For example when introduces a situation that shows how a general statement can happen.","zh":"for example when用來引入一個情況，展示一般說法如何發生。"},{"en":"A phone can disturb sleep, for example when messages arrive late at night.","zh":"手機可以打擾睡眠，例如當訊息在深夜到達時。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain an effect by giving a specific condition.","zh":"這個短語透過給出具體條件來解釋影響。"},{"en":"It is useful when a problem happens only in certain situations.","zh":"當問題只在某些情況發生時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get lodged in","meaning":"卡在……","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics can get lodged in an animal’s digestive system.","zh":"微塑膠可以卡在動物的消化系統中。"},{"en":"To get lodged in something means to become stuck inside it.","zh":"get lodged in某處，意思是卡在它裡面。"},{"en":"A fish bone may get lodged in someone’s throat if they swallow carelessly.","zh":"如果吞嚥不小心，魚骨可能卡在人的喉嚨。"},{"en":"If particles get lodged inside an animal, they may block normal body processes.","zh":"如果顆粒卡在動物體內，可能阻礙正常身體過程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being stuck in a place where removal is difficult.","zh":"這個短語描述卡在難以移除的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"digestive system","meaning":"消化系統","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics may get lodged in the digestive system.","zh":"微塑膠可能卡在消化系統中。"},{"en":"The digestive system is the body system that breaks down food and absorbs nutrients.","zh":"digestive system是分解食物並吸收養分的身體系統。"},{"en":"The stomach and intestines are important parts of the digestive system.","zh":"胃和腸道是消化系統的重要部分。"},{"en":"If something blocks the digestive system, an animal may not get enough nutrition.","zh":"如果某物阻塞消化系統，動物可能得不到足夠營養。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in biology and health contexts.","zh":"這個短語用於生物和健康語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"surprisingly perhaps","meaning":"或許令人驚訝的是","examples":[{"en":"Surprisingly perhaps, humans are likely to consume microplastics.","zh":"或許令人驚訝的是，人類很可能會攝入微塑膠。"},{"en":"Surprisingly perhaps means the information may be unexpected or surprising to listeners.","zh":"surprisingly perhaps意思是這項資訊對聽眾可能出乎意料或令人驚訝。"},{"en":"Surprisingly perhaps, indoor air can sometimes contain more dust than outdoor air.","zh":"或許令人驚訝的是，室內空氣有時可能比室外空氣含有更多灰塵。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase when they expect listeners to be surprised by the next point.","zh":"當講者預期聽眾會對下一點感到驚訝，就會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase softens the surprise while still drawing attention.","zh":"這個短語柔化驚訝語氣，同時仍吸引注意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"it is likely that","meaning":"很可能……","examples":[{"en":"It is likely that humans consume microplastics.","zh":"人類很可能會攝入微塑膠。"},{"en":"It is likely that means something is probably true or probably happens.","zh":"it is likely that意思是某事很可能屬實或發生。"},{"en":"It is likely that students will remember examples better than definitions alone.","zh":"學生很可能比起單靠定義，更容易記住例子。"},{"en":"This phrase is careful because it suggests probability rather than certainty.","zh":"這個短語較謹慎，因為它表示可能性而不是確定性。"},{"en":"It is useful when evidence points in one direction but the speaker avoids overclaiming.","zh":"當證據指向某方向但講者避免過度聲稱時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"consume microplastics","meaning":"攝入微塑膠","examples":[{"en":"Humans may consume microplastics through food and drink.","zh":"人類可能透過食物和飲品攝入微塑膠。"},{"en":"To consume microplastics means to take tiny plastic particles into the body by eating or drinking.","zh":"consume microplastics意思是透過飲食把微小塑膠顆粒帶入身體。"},{"en":"People may consume microplastics if particles are present in bottled water or seafood.","zh":"如果微粒存在於樽裝水或海鮮中，人們可能攝入微塑膠。"},{"en":"Consuming tiny particles can be difficult to avoid when they are found in common products.","zh":"當微小顆粒存在於常見產品中，攝入它們可能難以避免。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intake through the mouth, not just contact with plastic.","zh":"這個短語描述經口攝入，而不只是接觸塑膠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be detected in","meaning":"在……中被檢測到","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics have been detected in a wide range of food and drink products.","zh":"微塑膠已在各式各樣的食物和飲品中被檢測到。"},{"en":"To be detected in something means to be found there through testing or observation.","zh":"be detected in某物，意思是透過測試或觀察在其中發現。"},{"en":"Chemicals may be detected in river water after a factory leak.","zh":"工廠洩漏後，化學物質可能在河水中被檢測到。"},{"en":"Detection does not always prove harm, but it shows that a substance is present.","zh":"檢測到並不一定證明有害，但顯示某物質存在。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in science and health reports.","zh":"這個短語常見於科學和健康報告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a wide range of","meaning":"各式各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics have been found in a wide range of products.","zh":"微塑膠已在各式各樣的產品中被發現。"},{"en":"A wide range of something means many different kinds or examples of it.","zh":"a wide range of某物，意思是許多不同種類或例子。"},{"en":"A library should offer a wide range of books for different ages and interests.","zh":"圖書館應提供各式各樣適合不同年齡和興趣的書。"},{"en":"When a substance appears in a wide range of products, exposure may be common.","zh":"當某物質出現在各式各樣的產品中，接觸它可能很普遍。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety and breadth.","zh":"這個短語強調種類多和範圍廣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"food and drink products","meaning":"食物及飲品","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics have been detected in food and drink products.","zh":"微塑膠已在食物及飲品中被檢測到。"},{"en":"Food and drink products are items people eat or drink, often bought from shops.","zh":"food and drink products是人們食用或飲用、常從商店購買的產品。"},{"en":"Bread, bottled water, juice and canned soup are food and drink products.","zh":"麵包、樽裝水、果汁和罐頭湯都是食物及飲品。"},{"en":"If contaminants are found in food and drink products, many consumers may be affected.","zh":"如果污染物在食物及飲品中被發現，許多消費者可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to everyday consumer goods for eating and drinking.","zh":"這個短語指日常用來吃和喝的消費品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bottled water","meaning":"樽裝水","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics have been detected in bottled water.","zh":"微塑膠已在樽裝水中被檢測到。"},{"en":"Bottled water is drinking water sold in plastic or glass bottles.","zh":"bottled water是以膠樽或玻璃樽出售的飲用水。"},{"en":"Students may buy bottled water when the school water fountain is not nearby.","zh":"當學校飲水機不在附近，學生可能購買樽裝水。"},{"en":"Bottled water creates packaging waste if bottles are used once and thrown away.","zh":"如果樽只用一次便丟棄，樽裝水會產生包裝廢物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a common drink product.","zh":"這個短語指一種常見飲品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"以及","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics have been found in bottled water as well as tap water.","zh":"微塑膠已在樽裝水以及自來水中被發現。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to another thing.","zh":"as well as意思是除了另一事物之外，也包括某物。"},{"en":"Students need sleep as well as revision before an exam.","zh":"學生考試前需要溫習以及睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two or more things are included.","zh":"這個短語顯示包括兩件或以上事情。"},{"en":"It is useful when adding another example without changing the main point.","zh":"它適合在不改變主旨下加入另一例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"water that comes direct from the tap","meaning":"直接來自水龍頭的水","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics have been found in water that comes direct from the tap.","zh":"微塑膠已在直接來自水龍頭的水中被發現。"},{"en":"Water that comes direct from the tap is tap water taken straight from a household or public water supply.","zh":"water that comes direct from the tap是直接從家居或公共供水系統水龍頭取得的自來水。"},{"en":"A student may fill a bottle with water that comes direct from the tap before leaving home.","zh":"學生離家前可能把直接來自水龍頭的水裝進水樽。"},{"en":"If particles are found in tap water, people may be exposed even without buying bottled drinks.","zh":"如果顆粒在自來水中被發現，人們即使不買樽裝飲品也可能接觸到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordinary drinking water from a tap.","zh":"這個短語描述來自水龍頭的普通飲用水。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"what’s more","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"What’s more, salt and many kinds of seafood contain microplastics.","zh":"此外，鹽和多種海鮮含有微塑膠。"},{"en":"What’s more introduces an extra point that strengthens or adds to what was just said.","zh":"what’s more用來引入額外重點，加強或補充剛才說法。"},{"en":"The bus is late; what’s more, it is raining heavily.","zh":"巴士遲到；此外，還下着大雨。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when the next fact makes the argument stronger.","zh":"當下一個事實令論點更有力，作者會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase is slightly conversational and useful in explanations.","zh":"這個短語略帶口語感，適合用於解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"many kinds of seafood","meaning":"多種海鮮","examples":[{"en":"Many kinds of seafood have been found to contain microplastics.","zh":"多種海鮮被發現含有微塑膠。"},{"en":"Many kinds of seafood means several types of food from the sea, such as fish, shellfish and shrimp.","zh":"many kinds of seafood意思是幾種來自海洋的食物，例如魚、貝類和蝦。"},{"en":"A restaurant menu may include many kinds of seafood for customers who like fish and shellfish.","zh":"餐廳餐牌可能包括多種海鮮，供喜歡魚和貝類的顧客選擇。"},{"en":"If many kinds of seafood contain a pollutant, people who eat seafood often may be more exposed.","zh":"如果多種海鮮含有污染物，經常吃海鮮的人可能接觸更多。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to variety within sea-based food.","zh":"這個短語指海產食物中的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be found to contain","meaning":"被發現含有……","examples":[{"en":"Salt and seafood have been found to contain microplastics.","zh":"鹽和海鮮被發現含有微塑膠。"},{"en":"To be found to contain something means testing or research shows that it has that substance inside it.","zh":"be found to contain某物，意思是測試或研究顯示其中含有該物質。"},{"en":"A drink may be found to contain too much sugar after laboratory testing.","zh":"飲品經實驗室測試後，可能被發現含有過多糖分。"},{"en":"When products are found to contain unwanted substances, consumers may become worried.","zh":"當產品被發現含有不想要的物質，消費者可能會擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in scientific and consumer safety reports.","zh":"這個短語常見於科學和消費者安全報告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"underline that","meaning":"強調……","examples":[{"en":"It is important to underline that there is not yet conclusive proof.","zh":"重要的是要強調，目前仍未有確鑿證據。"},{"en":"To underline that means to emphasise or make a point especially clear.","zh":"underline that意思是強調或特別清楚表明某一點。"},{"en":"A teacher may underline that copying homework is dishonest even if the answers are correct.","zh":"老師可能強調，即使答案正確，抄功課仍是不誠實。"},{"en":"Speakers underline important points when listeners may misunderstand or overreact.","zh":"當聽眾可能誤解或反應過度，講者會強調重要重點。"},{"en":"This phrase means stressing a key idea, not literally drawing a line.","zh":"這個短語指強調關鍵想法，而不是字面畫線。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"conclusive proof","meaning":"確鑿證據","examples":[{"en":"There is not yet conclusive proof that microplastics harm people.","zh":"目前仍未有確鑿證據顯示微塑膠會傷害人類。"},{"en":"Conclusive proof is evidence strong enough to settle a question clearly.","zh":"conclusive proof是強到足以清楚解決問題的證據。"},{"en":"A court needs conclusive proof before declaring someone guilty.","zh":"法庭需要確鑿證據才可裁定某人有罪。"},{"en":"Without conclusive proof, researchers may describe a risk carefully rather than making a final claim.","zh":"沒有確鑿證據時，研究人員可能會謹慎描述風險，而不是作最終聲稱。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that evidence must be strong and decisive.","zh":"這個短語顯示證據必須強而有決定性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"significant harm","meaning":"重大傷害","examples":[{"en":"There is not yet proof that microplastics cause significant harm to people.","zh":"目前仍未有證據證明微塑膠會對人造成重大傷害。"},{"en":"Significant harm means serious or important damage.","zh":"significant harm意思是嚴重或重要的傷害。"},{"en":"A small paper cut is minor, but a deep wound can cause significant harm.","zh":"小紙割傷是輕微的，但深傷口可以造成重大傷害。"},{"en":"Scientists look for significant harm before deciding how serious a risk is.","zh":"科學家會尋找重大傷害，才判斷風險有多嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to meaningful damage, not tiny or uncertain effects.","zh":"這個短語指有意義的損害，而不是微小或不確定影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"legislation","meaning":"法例","examples":[{"en":"Many countries have legislation controlling plastic microbeads.","zh":"許多國家有控制塑膠微珠的法例。"},{"en":"Legislation means laws made by a government or law-making body.","zh":"legislation意思是由政府或立法機關制定的法律。"},{"en":"Legislation can require shops to charge for plastic bags.","zh":"法例可以要求商店收取膠袋費。"},{"en":"Strong legislation can change what companies are allowed to sell or produce.","zh":"強而有力的法例可以改變公司獲准銷售或生產的東西。"},{"en":"This word is common in discussions of law and public policy.","zh":"這個詞常見於法律和公共政策討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prevent manufacturers from","meaning":"阻止製造商……","examples":[{"en":"Legislation prevents manufacturers from adding plastic microbeads to products.","zh":"法例阻止製造商在產品中加入塑膠微珠。"},{"en":"To prevent manufacturers from doing something means to stop companies that make products from doing it.","zh":"prevent manufacturers from doing something意思是阻止製造產品的公司做某事。"},{"en":"Safety rules may prevent manufacturers from using dangerous chemicals in children’s toys.","zh":"安全規則可能阻止製造商在兒童玩具中使用危險化學品。"},{"en":"Laws can prevent harmful practices by making them illegal or punishable.","zh":"法律可以透過把有害做法定為非法或可懲罰來阻止它們。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how rules stop producers from taking a certain action.","zh":"這個短語顯示規則如何阻止生產者採取某行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"manufacturers","meaning":"製造商","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers are not allowed to add plastic microbeads to some products.","zh":"製造商不獲准在某些產品中加入塑膠微珠。"},{"en":"Manufacturers are companies or people that make goods in factories or workshops.","zh":"manufacturers是在工廠或工場製造貨品的公司或人士。"},{"en":"A toy manufacturer makes toys that shops later sell to families.","zh":"玩具製造商製作玩具，之後由商店賣給家庭。"},{"en":"Manufacturers must follow safety rules because their products may affect many users.","zh":"製造商必須遵守安全規則，因為他們的產品可能影響許多用家。"},{"en":"This word identifies the makers of products.","zh":"這個詞指出產品的製作者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"plastic microbeads","meaning":"塑膠微珠","examples":[{"en":"Plastic microbeads are banned in some shower gels and facial cleansers.","zh":"塑膠微珠在某些沐浴露和潔面乳中被禁止。"},{"en":"Plastic microbeads are tiny plastic beads sometimes added to personal care products for scrubbing.","zh":"plastic microbeads是有時加入個人護理產品作磨砂用途的微小塑膠珠。"},{"en":"A face wash with plastic microbeads may feel rough because the beads rub the skin.","zh":"含塑膠微珠的洗面產品可能感覺粗糙，因為微珠會摩擦皮膚。"},{"en":"Microbeads can enter drains after use and may reach rivers or oceans.","zh":"微珠使用後可以進入排水渠，並可能到達河流或海洋。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific type of small plastic particle in products.","zh":"這個短語指產品中的一種特定細小塑膠顆粒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"shower gels","meaning":"沐浴露","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers cannot add plastic microbeads to shower gels.","zh":"製造商不能在沐浴露中加入塑膠微珠。"},{"en":"Shower gels are liquid soap products used for washing the body.","zh":"shower gels是用來清洗身體的液體皂類產品。"},{"en":"Many people use shower gels every morning instead of bar soap.","zh":"許多人每天早上使用沐浴露，而不是肥皂。"},{"en":"Ingredients in shower gels can enter wastewater after people rinse them off.","zh":"沐浴露中的成分在人們沖洗後可以進入污水。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a common personal care product.","zh":"這個短語指常見個人護理產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"facial cleansers","meaning":"潔面乳","examples":[{"en":"Plastic microbeads are banned in facial cleansers.","zh":"塑膠微珠在潔面乳中被禁止。"},{"en":"Facial cleansers are products used to clean the skin on the face.","zh":"facial cleansers是用來清潔面部皮膚的產品。"},{"en":"A teenager may use a facial cleanser at night to remove oil and dirt.","zh":"青少年可能晚上使用潔面乳去除油脂和污垢。"},{"en":"If facial cleansers contain harmful particles, those particles can be washed into drains.","zh":"如果潔面乳含有有害顆粒，這些顆粒可以被沖入排水渠。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to skincare products for the face.","zh":"這個短語指面部護膚清潔產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"toothpaste","meaning":"牙膏","examples":[{"en":"Some legislation prevents plastic microbeads from being added to toothpaste.","zh":"一些法例阻止塑膠微珠被加入牙膏中。"},{"en":"Toothpaste is a paste used with a toothbrush to clean teeth.","zh":"toothpaste是配合牙刷清潔牙齒的膏狀物。"},{"en":"Children learn to use toothpaste every morning and night to prevent tooth decay.","zh":"孩子學習每天早晚使用牙膏，以防蛀牙。"},{"en":"Ingredients in toothpaste are washed down the drain after brushing.","zh":"牙膏中的成分在刷牙後會被沖入排水渠。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an everyday dental care product.","zh":"這個短語指日常牙齒護理產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"accurately estimate","meaning":"準確估計","examples":[{"en":"It is very difficult to accurately estimate the amount of microplastics in soil.","zh":"準確估計土壤中微塑膠的數量非常困難。"},{"en":"To accurately estimate something means to calculate or judge it closely to the real amount.","zh":"accurately estimate某事，意思是計算或判斷得接近真實數量。"},{"en":"A teacher may accurately estimate how long a test will take after seeing students practise it.","zh":"老師看過學生練習後，可能準確估計測驗需要多長時間。"},{"en":"Accurate estimates are difficult when the thing being measured is tiny, hidden or unevenly spread.","zh":"當被量度的東西細小、隱藏或分布不均，準確估計會很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase combines careful judgement with measurement.","zh":"這個短語結合仔細判斷與量度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"total amount of","meaning":"……的總量","examples":[{"en":"It is hard to estimate the total amount of microplastic particles in the soil.","zh":"很難估計土壤中微塑膠顆粒的總量。"},{"en":"The total amount of something is the full quantity when all parts are added together.","zh":"the total amount of某物，是把所有部分加起來後的完整數量。"},{"en":"A family may calculate the total amount of money spent on transport each month.","zh":"家庭可能計算每月交通開支的總量。"},{"en":"Knowing the total amount helps people understand the full size of a problem.","zh":"知道總量幫助人理解問題的完整規模。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on complete quantity, not just one sample.","zh":"這個短語著重完整數量，而不只是單一樣本。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"microplastic particles","meaning":"微塑膠顆粒","examples":[{"en":"Microplastic particles can be hard to detect in soil.","zh":"微塑膠顆粒在土壤中可能難以檢測。"},{"en":"Microplastic particles are tiny pieces of plastic small enough to mix with soil, water or food.","zh":"microplastic particles是細小到可與土壤、水或食物混合的塑膠碎片。"},{"en":"Scientists may need special tools to find microplastic particles in a soil sample.","zh":"科學家可能需要特殊工具，才可在土壤樣本中找到微塑膠顆粒。"},{"en":"Because the particles are so small, they can be swallowed by small organisms.","zh":"因為這些顆粒很小，它們可以被小型生物吞下。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to individual tiny pieces of microplastic.","zh":"這個短語指一粒粒細小微塑膠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be hard to detect","meaning":"難以檢測","examples":[{"en":"Microplastic particles can be hard to detect.","zh":"微塑膠顆粒可能難以檢測。"},{"en":"To be hard to detect means to be difficult to find, notice or measure.","zh":"be hard to detect意思是難以發現、注意或量度。"},{"en":"A small crack in a water pipe can be hard to detect until the floor becomes wet.","zh":"水管中的細小裂縫可能難以檢測，直到地板變濕才發現。"},{"en":"Tiny pollutants are hard to detect without special equipment or careful testing.","zh":"沒有特殊設備或仔細測試，微小污染物很難檢測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something hidden or difficult to identify.","zh":"這個短語描述隱藏或難以辨認的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be carried in the air","meaning":"在空氣中傳播","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics are carried in the air.","zh":"微塑膠會在空氣中傳播。"},{"en":"To be carried in the air means to move through the air, often by wind or currents.","zh":"be carried in the air意思是在空氣中移動，通常由風或氣流帶動。"},{"en":"Pollen can be carried in the air and make people sneeze in spring.","zh":"花粉可以在空氣中傳播，令人在春天打噴嚏。"},{"en":"If particles are carried in the air, they can travel away from their original source.","zh":"如果顆粒在空氣中傳播，它們可以離開原本來源。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how tiny materials can spread without flowing water.","zh":"這個短語解釋微小物料如何不靠流水也能擴散。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be deposited in","meaning":"沉積於……","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics are deposited in the soil by rain.","zh":"微塑膠由雨水帶入並沉積於土壤中。"},{"en":"To be deposited in a place means to be placed, dropped or left there after being carried.","zh":"be deposited in某地，意思是在被帶走後被放下、掉落或留在那裡。"},{"en":"Dust can be deposited on windowsills after a windy day.","zh":"大風天後，灰塵可以沉積於窗台上。"},{"en":"Particles carried in air may be deposited in soil when rain brings them down.","zh":"空氣中的顆粒可能在雨水把它們帶下時沉積於土壤中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where material finally settles.","zh":"這個短語描述材料最終停留的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"by rain","meaning":"由雨水帶入","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics can be deposited in soil by rain.","zh":"微塑膠可以由雨水帶入並沉積於土壤中。"},{"en":"By rain means through the action of rainwater.","zh":"by rain意思是透過雨水的作用。"},{"en":"Soil on a hillside can be carried downhill by rain during a storm.","zh":"暴風雨期間，山坡上的泥土可以由雨水帶到坡下。"},{"en":"Rain can move particles from the air or ground into rivers, drains and soil.","zh":"雨水可以把空氣中或地面上的顆粒帶入河流、排水渠和土壤。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies rain as the method or cause.","zh":"這個短語指出雨水是方法或原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fertilisers","meaning":"肥料","examples":[{"en":"Many fertilisers used by farmers and gardeners contain microplastics.","zh":"許多農民和園丁使用的肥料含有微塑膠。"},{"en":"Fertilisers are substances added to soil to help plants grow.","zh":"fertilisers是加入土壤中以幫助植物生長的物質。"},{"en":"Farmers may use fertilisers to give crops nutrients such as nitrogen and phosphorus.","zh":"農民可能使用肥料，為農作物提供氮和磷等養分。"},{"en":"If fertilisers contain unwanted particles, those particles can enter farmland soil.","zh":"如果肥料含有不想要的顆粒，這些顆粒可以進入農田土壤。"},{"en":"This word is common in farming, gardening and soil discussions.","zh":"這個詞常見於農業、園藝和土壤討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"farmers and gardeners","meaning":"農民和園丁","examples":[{"en":"Farmers and gardeners may use fertilisers that contain microplastics.","zh":"農民和園丁可能使用含有微塑膠的肥料。"},{"en":"Farmers and gardeners are people who grow crops, plants, flowers or vegetables.","zh":"farmers and gardeners是種植農作物、植物、花或蔬菜的人。"},{"en":"Farmers grow food on a larger scale, while gardeners may care for plants at home or in parks.","zh":"農民較大規模地種植食物，而園丁可能照顧家中或公園植物。"},{"en":"Their choices affect soil because they add water, fertilisers and other materials to it.","zh":"他們的選擇會影響土壤，因為他們會向土壤加入水、肥料和其他材料。"},{"en":"This phrase names two groups who work directly with soil.","zh":"這個短語命名兩類直接與土壤工作的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"carry out a study of","meaning":"進行一項關於……的研究","examples":[{"en":"A team from Anglia Ruskin University carried out a study of microplastics.","zh":"來自Anglia Ruskin University的團隊進行了一項關於微塑膠的研究。"},{"en":"To carry out a study of something means to conduct research into that topic.","zh":"carry out a study of某事，意思是對該主題進行研究。"},{"en":"A school may carry out a study of students’ reading habits before changing library rules.","zh":"學校在改變圖書館規則前，可能進行一項關於學生閱讀習慣的研究。"},{"en":"Researchers carry out studies to gather evidence instead of relying on guesses.","zh":"研究人員進行研究是為了收集證據，而不是依賴猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in academic writing.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常見於學術寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"effects of microplastics on","meaning":"微塑膠對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The study examined the effects of microplastics on earthworms.","zh":"該研究檢視微塑膠對蚯蚓的影響。"},{"en":"The effects of microplastics on something are the changes or harm microplastics cause to that thing.","zh":"effects of microplastics on某物，是微塑膠對該物造成的變化或傷害。"},{"en":"Scientists may study the effects of microplastics on fish to see whether they affect feeding.","zh":"科學家可能研究微塑膠對魚類的影響，以了解它們是否影響進食。"},{"en":"Studying effects on one organism can reveal wider risks to an ecosystem.","zh":"研究對一種生物的影響，可以揭示對生態系統的更廣泛風險。"},{"en":"This phrase connects microplastics with the living thing or system affected.","zh":"這個短語把微塑膠與受影響的生物或系統連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"digestive tracts","meaning":"消化道","examples":[{"en":"The study looked at the digestive tracts of earthworms.","zh":"該研究觀察蚯蚓的消化道。"},{"en":"Digestive tracts are the parts of the body through which food passes and is digested.","zh":"digestive tracts是食物通過並被消化的身體部位。"},{"en":"Doctors may examine digestive tracts when patients have stomach or bowel problems.","zh":"當病人有胃部或腸道問題，醫生可能檢查消化道。"},{"en":"If particles enter digestive tracts, they may affect feeding and nutrient absorption.","zh":"如果顆粒進入消化道，可能影響進食和養分吸收。"},{"en":"This phrase is a biological term related to digestion.","zh":"這個短語是與消化有關的生物學術語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"earthworms","meaning":"蚯蚓","examples":[{"en":"Earthworms are an essential component of the agricultural system.","zh":"蚯蚓是農業系統的重要組成部分。"},{"en":"Earthworms are long, soft-bodied worms that live in soil.","zh":"earthworms是生活在土壤中的長而柔軟的蠕蟲。"},{"en":"Children may find earthworms in the garden after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，孩子可能在花園中找到蚯蚓。"},{"en":"Earthworms help soil by moving through it and mixing organic matter.","zh":"蚯蚓透過在土壤中移動並混合有機物來幫助土壤。"},{"en":"This word names a small animal important to soil health.","zh":"這個詞命名一種對土壤健康重要的小動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"live in topsoil","meaning":"生活於表土中","examples":[{"en":"Earthworms live in topsoil.","zh":"蚯蚓生活於表土中。"},{"en":"To live in topsoil means to make the upper layer of soil one’s habitat.","zh":"live in topsoil意思是以上層土壤作為棲息地。"},{"en":"Many insects and roots live in topsoil because it contains air, water and nutrients.","zh":"許多昆蟲和根部生活於表土中，因為那裡含有空氣、水和養分。"},{"en":"If topsoil is damaged, creatures that live there may lose food and shelter.","zh":"如果表土受損，生活在那裡的生物可能失去食物和庇護。"},{"en":"This phrase links an organism with the soil layer where it is found.","zh":"這個短語把生物與其所在土壤層連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"topsoil","meaning":"表土","examples":[{"en":"Earthworms that live in topsoil help make soil fertile.","zh":"生活於表土中的蚯蚓幫助令土壤肥沃。"},{"en":"Topsoil is the upper layer of soil where many roots, organisms and nutrients are found.","zh":"topsoil是土壤上層，當中有許多根部、生物和養分。"},{"en":"Gardeners protect topsoil because plants depend on it for growth.","zh":"園丁會保護表土，因為植物生長依賴它。"},{"en":"If topsoil is washed away by heavy rain, farming becomes more difficult.","zh":"如果表土被大雨沖走，耕作會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This word refers to the most active and fertile soil layer.","zh":"這個詞指最活躍和肥沃的土壤層。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"essential component of","meaning":"……的重要組成部分","examples":[{"en":"Earthworms are an essential component of our agricultural system.","zh":"蚯蚓是我們農業系統的重要組成部分。"},{"en":"An essential component of something is a necessary part of a larger system.","zh":"essential component of某事，是較大系統中必要的一部分。"},{"en":"Teachers are an essential component of a school because learning depends on their guidance.","zh":"老師是學校的重要組成部分，因為學習依賴他們的引導。"},{"en":"If an essential component is damaged, the whole system may work less well.","zh":"如果重要組成部分受損，整個系統可能運作得較差。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a part that is necessary, not optional.","zh":"這個短語突顯必要而非可有可無的部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"agricultural system","meaning":"農業系統","examples":[{"en":"Earthworms play an important role in the agricultural system.","zh":"蚯蚓在農業系統中發揮重要作用。"},{"en":"An agricultural system is the connected process of growing food, managing soil, using water and raising crops or animals.","zh":"agricultural system是種植食物、管理土壤、使用水和飼養作物或動物的連接過程。"},{"en":"Farmers, soil, weather, tools and markets are all parts of an agricultural system.","zh":"農民、土壤、天氣、工具和市場都是農業系統的一部分。"},{"en":"If soil quality falls, the agricultural system may produce less food.","zh":"如果土壤質素下降，農業系統可能生產較少食物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the whole network behind farming.","zh":"這個短語指農業背後的整個網絡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"feed on","meaning":"以……為食","examples":[{"en":"Earthworms feed on soil and mix nutrients into it.","zh":"蚯蚓以土壤為食，並把養分混入其中。"},{"en":"To feed on something means to eat it or use it as food.","zh":"feed on某物，意思是吃它或把它用作食物。"},{"en":"Caterpillars feed on leaves before they become butterflies.","zh":"毛蟲在變成蝴蝶前以葉子為食。"},{"en":"What an animal feeds on affects its body and the environment around it.","zh":"動物以甚麼為食會影響牠的身體和周圍環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the food source of a living thing.","zh":"這個短語描述生物的食物來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"mix nutrients into","meaning":"將養分混入……","examples":[{"en":"Earthworms mix nutrients into the soil.","zh":"蚯蚓將養分混入土壤。"},{"en":"To mix nutrients into something means to blend useful substances into it.","zh":"mix nutrients into某物，意思是把有用物質混合到其中。"},{"en":"A gardener may mix nutrients into soil before planting vegetables.","zh":"園丁可能在種植蔬菜前將養分混入土壤。"},{"en":"Nutrients in soil help plants grow stronger roots and leaves.","zh":"土壤中的養分幫助植物長出更強壯的根和葉。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how a material becomes richer or more useful.","zh":"這個短語顯示某材料如何變得更豐富或更有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"thereby making it more fertile","meaning":"從而令其更加肥沃","examples":[{"en":"Earthworms mix nutrients into the soil, thereby making it more fertile.","zh":"蚯蚓將養分混入土壤，從而令其更加肥沃。"},{"en":"Thereby making it more fertile means as a result, making it better for plants to grow.","zh":"thereby making it more fertile意思是結果令它更適合植物生長。"},{"en":"Compost adds organic matter to garden soil, thereby making it more fertile.","zh":"堆肥把有機物加入花園土壤，從而令其更加肥沃。"},{"en":"When soil becomes more fertile, crops can grow more strongly.","zh":"當土壤變得更肥沃，農作物可以更強壯地生長。"},{"en":"This phrase connects one action with its direct result.","zh":"這個短語把一個行動與其直接結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fertile","meaning":"肥沃的","examples":[{"en":"Earthworms help make the soil more fertile.","zh":"蚯蚓幫助令土壤更加肥沃。"},{"en":"Fertile soil is soil that has enough nutrients and good conditions for plants to grow well.","zh":"fertile soil是有足夠養分和良好條件讓植物生長良好的土壤。"},{"en":"Farmers prefer fertile fields because crops grow better there.","zh":"農民較喜歡肥沃的田地，因為農作物在那裡長得更好。"},{"en":"Soil can become less fertile if nutrients are removed and not replaced.","zh":"如果養分被帶走而沒有補充，土壤可以變得不再肥沃。"},{"en":"This word is often used when discussing farming, gardening and plant growth.","zh":"這個詞常用於討論農業、園藝和植物生長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"set out to discover","meaning":"着手探究","examples":[{"en":"The researchers set out to discover whether microplastics affected soil quality.","zh":"研究人員着手探究微塑膠是否影響土壤質素。"},{"en":"To set out to discover something means to begin a study or task with the aim of finding it out.","zh":"set out to discover某事，意思是開始一項研究或任務，目的是找出它。"},{"en":"A student may set out to discover why classmates prefer online homework to paper worksheets.","zh":"學生可能着手探究為何同學較喜歡網上功課而不是紙本工作紙。"},{"en":"Researchers set clear questions before collecting data so their work has direction.","zh":"研究人員在收集數據前設定清晰問題，使研究有方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the starting aim of an investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述調查開始時的目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the introduction of","meaning":"……的引入","examples":[{"en":"The study examined the introduction of microplastics into the soil.","zh":"該研究檢視微塑膠被引入土壤的情況。"},{"en":"The introduction of something means the act of bringing it into a place, system or situation.","zh":"the introduction of某事，意思是把它帶入某地方、系統或情況的行動。"},{"en":"The introduction of tablets into classrooms changed how students completed exercises.","zh":"平板電腦引入課室改變了學生完成練習的方式。"},{"en":"Introducing a new material into soil can change the organisms and chemistry there.","zh":"把新物質引入土壤可以改變當中的生物和化學狀況。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the point when something enters a system.","zh":"這個短語著重某物進入系統的一刻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"subsequent ingestion","meaning":"隨後攝入","examples":[{"en":"The researchers studied the subsequent ingestion of microplastics by earthworms.","zh":"研究人員研究蚯蚓隨後攝入微塑膠的情況。"},{"en":"Subsequent ingestion means eating or taking in something after an earlier event has happened.","zh":"subsequent ingestion意思是在較早事件發生後吃下或攝入某物。"},{"en":"If medicine is left on a table, subsequent ingestion by a child can be dangerous.","zh":"如果藥物被放在桌上，孩子隨後攝入可能很危險。"},{"en":"In the study, microplastics were first introduced into soil, and ingestion happened afterwards.","zh":"在該研究中，微塑膠先被引入土壤，攝入則在之後發生。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a later act of eating with what happened before.","zh":"這個短語把後來的進食行為與之前發生的事連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ingestion","meaning":"攝入","examples":[{"en":"The ingestion of microplastics by earthworms may affect soil quality.","zh":"蚯蚓攝入微塑膠可能影響土壤質素。"},{"en":"Ingestion means taking something into the body by eating or swallowing it.","zh":"ingestion意思是透過進食或吞嚥把某物帶入身體。"},{"en":"Accidental ingestion of small toy parts can be dangerous for young children.","zh":"幼兒意外攝入小玩具零件可能很危險。"},{"en":"Ingestion matters because substances inside the body may affect health or behaviour.","zh":"攝入很重要，因為進入體內的物質可能影響健康或行為。"},{"en":"This word is common in scientific and medical contexts.","zh":"這個詞常見於科學和醫療語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"impact soil quality","meaning":"影響土壤質素","examples":[{"en":"The researchers asked whether microplastics would impact soil quality.","zh":"研究人員詢問微塑膠會否影響土壤質素。"},{"en":"To impact soil quality means to affect how healthy, fertile or useful the soil is.","zh":"impact soil quality意思是影響土壤有多健康、肥沃或有用。"},{"en":"Too much chemical fertiliser can impact soil quality if it changes the soil balance.","zh":"如果過量化學肥料改變土壤平衡，就可能影響土壤質素。"},{"en":"Poor soil quality can reduce plant growth and make farming less productive.","zh":"土壤質素差可以減少植物生長，並令農業生產力下降。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with changes in soil condition.","zh":"這個短語把原因與土壤狀況變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"soil quality","meaning":"土壤質素","examples":[{"en":"The study examined whether microplastics would affect soil quality.","zh":"該研究檢視微塑膠是否會影響土壤質素。"},{"en":"Soil quality is how healthy and suitable soil is for supporting plants and organisms.","zh":"soil quality是土壤有多健康和適合支援植物及生物。"},{"en":"Farmers check soil quality before deciding which crops to grow.","zh":"農民在決定種植哪種作物前會檢查土壤質素。"},{"en":"Good soil quality helps seeds germinate, roots spread and plants absorb nutrients.","zh":"良好土壤質素幫助種子發芽、根部伸展和植物吸收養分。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to farming, gardening and environmental science.","zh":"這個短語是農業、園藝和環境科學的核心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ultimately inhibit","meaning":"最終抑制……","examples":[{"en":"Microplastics may ultimately inhibit plant growth.","zh":"微塑膠可能最終抑制植物生長。"},{"en":"To ultimately inhibit something means to finally slow, block or reduce it after a process.","zh":"ultimately inhibit某事，意思是經過一個過程後最終減慢、阻礙或減少它。"},{"en":"Constant stress may ultimately inhibit a student’s ability to concentrate.","zh":"持續壓力可能最終抑制學生的專注能力。"},{"en":"If soil organisms are harmed, plant growth may ultimately be reduced.","zh":"如果土壤生物受害，植物生長最終可能被減弱。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a later negative result.","zh":"這個短語顯示後來出現的負面結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"plant growth","meaning":"植物生長","examples":[{"en":"The study considered whether microplastics would inhibit plant growth.","zh":"該研究考慮微塑膠會否抑制植物生長。"},{"en":"Plant growth is the process by which plants develop roots, stems, leaves, flowers or fruit.","zh":"plant growth是植物發展根、莖、葉、花或果實的過程。"},{"en":"Sunlight, water and good soil all support plant growth.","zh":"陽光、水和良好土壤都支持植物生長。"},{"en":"If seeds fail to germinate, plant growth cannot begin properly.","zh":"如果種子未能發芽，植物生長就不能正常開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in biology, farming and gardening.","zh":"這個短語用於生物、農業和園藝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the short answer was","meaning":"簡單答案是……","examples":[{"en":"The short answer was that microplastics did affect soil quality.","zh":"簡單答案是微塑膠確實影響了土壤質素。"},{"en":"The short answer was means the simple or direct answer to a question was this.","zh":"the short answer was意思是某問題的簡單或直接答案是這樣。"},{"en":"The short answer was that the trip had to be cancelled because the storm was too strong.","zh":"簡單答案是旅行必須取消，因為風暴太強。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase before giving a simple answer to a complicated question.","zh":"講者在回答複雜問題前，會用這個短語給出簡單答案。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that more detailed explanation may follow.","zh":"這個短語表示之後可能會有更詳細解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"different types of","meaning":"不同種類的……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers placed three different types of microplastic particles into the soil.","zh":"研究人員將三種不同種類的微塑膠顆粒放入土壤。"},{"en":"Different types of something means several kinds within the same general category.","zh":"different types of某物，意思是同一大類中的幾種種類。"},{"en":"A school library has different types of books, such as novels, biographies and reference books.","zh":"學校圖書館有不同種類的書，例如小說、自傳和參考書。"},{"en":"Testing different types helps researchers see whether results are the same or different.","zh":"測試不同種類有助研究人員了解結果是否相同或不同。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety within one group.","zh":"這個短語強調同一群體中的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"place something into","meaning":"將某物放入……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers placed microplastic particles into the soil.","zh":"研究人員將微塑膠顆粒放入土壤。"},{"en":"To place something into somewhere means to put it carefully or deliberately there.","zh":"place something into某處，意思是小心或有意地把某物放進那裡。"},{"en":"A teacher may place seeds into small pots for a class experiment.","zh":"老師可能將種子放入小盆中作課堂實驗。"},{"en":"In research, placing materials into a sample helps test their effect under controlled conditions.","zh":"在研究中，將材料放入樣本有助在受控條件下測試其影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a deliberate action of putting something inside.","zh":"這個短語描述有意把某物放進去的行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"perennial rye grass","meaning":"多年生黑麥草","examples":[{"en":"The researchers planted perennial rye grass in the treated soil.","zh":"研究人員在處理過的土壤中種植多年生黑麥草。"},{"en":"Perennial rye grass is a type of grass that can live and grow for more than one year.","zh":"perennial rye grass是一種可以生長超過一年的草。"},{"en":"Parks and sports fields may use perennial rye grass because it can grow thick and green.","zh":"公園和運動場可能使用多年生黑麥草，因為它可以長得濃密和翠綠。"},{"en":"Researchers may use grass seeds to test whether soil supports plant growth.","zh":"研究人員可能使用草種測試土壤是否支持植物生長。"},{"en":"This phrase names the plant used in the experiment.","zh":"這個短語命名實驗中使用的植物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"biodegradable PLA","meaning":"可生物降解 PLA","examples":[{"en":"The particles included biodegradable PLA.","zh":"這些顆粒包括可生物降解PLA。"},{"en":"Biodegradable PLA is a type of plastic designed to break down under certain conditions.","zh":"biodegradable PLA是一種設計成在特定條件下分解的塑膠。"},{"en":"Some disposable cups or food containers may be made from biodegradable PLA.","zh":"一些即棄杯或食物容器可能由可生物降解PLA製成。"},{"en":"“Biodegradable” does not always mean the material disappears quickly in every environment.","zh":"「可生物降解」不一定表示該材料在每種環境中都會快速消失。"},{"en":"This phrase names one type of microplastic particle in the study.","zh":"這個短語命名研究中的一種微塑膠顆粒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"conventional high-density polyethylene","meaning":"傳統高密度聚乙烯","examples":[{"en":"The study included conventional high-density polyethylene.","zh":"該研究包括傳統高密度聚乙烯。"},{"en":"Conventional high-density polyethylene is a common strong plastic often used in containers, pipes and packaging.","zh":"conventional high-density polyethylene是一種常見而堅固的塑膠，常用於容器、管道和包裝。"},{"en":"Milk bottles and cleaning product bottles may be made from high-density polyethylene.","zh":"牛奶樽和清潔產品樽可能由高密度聚乙烯製成。"},{"en":"If this plastic breaks into tiny particles, it can become part of the microplastic problem.","zh":"如果這種塑膠碎成微小顆粒，就可能成為微塑膠問題的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the full technical name of HDPE.","zh":"這個短語給出HDPE的完整技術名稱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"HDPE","meaning":"高密度聚乙烯","examples":[{"en":"HDPE is a type of conventional high-density polyethylene.","zh":"HDPE是一種傳統高密度聚乙烯。"},{"en":"HDPE is short for high-density polyethylene, a strong and widely used plastic.","zh":"HDPE是high-density polyethylene的縮寫，是一種堅固而廣泛使用的塑膠。"},{"en":"Many household bottles are made from HDPE because it is tough and lightweight.","zh":"許多家居瓶子由HDPE製成，因為它堅韌而輕。"},{"en":"When HDPE breaks down, tiny pieces may remain in soil or water.","zh":"當HDPE分解，微小碎片可能留在土壤或水中。"},{"en":"This abbreviation is common in plastics and recycling discussions.","zh":"這個縮寫常見於塑膠和回收討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be ingested by","meaning":"被……攝入","examples":[{"en":"The particles were ingested by the earthworms.","zh":"這些顆粒被蚯蚓攝入。"},{"en":"To be ingested by an animal means to be taken into its body by eating or swallowing.","zh":"be ingested by某動物，意思是被牠透過進食或吞嚥帶入體內。"},{"en":"Small pieces of litter may be ingested by fish if they look like food.","zh":"如果小塊垃圾看起來像食物，可能被魚類攝入。"},{"en":"When unwanted particles are ingested, they can affect digestion or health.","zh":"當不想要的顆粒被攝入，它們可能影響消化或健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in scientific descriptions of feeding and pollution.","zh":"這個短語常用於關於進食和污染的科學描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lose weight rapidly","meaning":"體重迅速下降","examples":[{"en":"The worms lost weight rapidly after ingesting microplastics.","zh":"蚯蚓攝入微塑膠後體重迅速下降。"},{"en":"To lose weight rapidly means to become lighter very quickly.","zh":"lose weight rapidly意思是體重非常快速地變輕。"},{"en":"A sick pet may lose weight rapidly if it cannot eat properly.","zh":"如果生病寵物不能正常進食，牠可能體重迅速下降。"},{"en":"Rapid weight loss can be a sign that an animal is stressed or unhealthy.","zh":"迅速體重下降可以是動物受壓或不健康的跡象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fast physical change.","zh":"這個短語描述快速身體變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a lower percentage than normal","meaning":"低於正常比例","examples":[{"en":"A lower percentage than normal of the rye grass seeds germinated.","zh":"黑麥草種子發芽的比例低於正常比例。"},{"en":"A lower percentage than normal means a smaller proportion than usually expected.","zh":"a lower percentage than normal意思是比通常預期較小的比例。"},{"en":"A lower percentage than normal of students passed the test when the instructions were unclear.","zh":"當指示不清，通過測驗的學生比例可能低於正常比例。"},{"en":"Lower percentages can signal that conditions are worse than usual.","zh":"較低比例可以表示條件比平常更差。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a result with the expected normal level.","zh":"這個短語把結果與預期正常水平作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rye grass seeds","meaning":"黑麥草種子","examples":[{"en":"Fewer rye grass seeds germinated in the experiment.","zh":"實驗中較少黑麥草種子發芽。"},{"en":"Rye grass seeds are the seeds of rye grass, a grass often used in lawns, fields and research.","zh":"rye grass seeds是黑麥草的種子，黑麥草常用於草坪、田地和研究。"},{"en":"Gardeners may plant rye grass seeds to cover bare soil quickly.","zh":"園丁可能種植黑麥草種子，以快速覆蓋裸露土壤。"},{"en":"Seeds are useful in experiments because germination shows whether soil supports new plant life.","zh":"種子在實驗中有用，因為發芽情況顯示土壤是否支持新植物生命。"},{"en":"This phrase names the plant seeds tested in the study.","zh":"這個短語命名研究中測試的植物種子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"germinate","meaning":"發芽","examples":[{"en":"A lower percentage of the rye grass seeds germinated.","zh":"較低比例的黑麥草種子發芽。"},{"en":"To germinate means for a seed to begin growing into a plant.","zh":"germinate意思是種子開始長成植物。"},{"en":"Bean seeds germinate when they receive enough water, warmth and air.","zh":"豆種子在得到足夠水分、溫暖和空氣時會發芽。"},{"en":"If soil is unhealthy, fewer seeds may germinate successfully.","zh":"如果土壤不健康，較少種子能成功發芽。"},{"en":"This verb describes the first stage of plant growth from a seed.","zh":"這個動詞描述種子長成植物的第一階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"conclude that","meaning":"得出結論認為……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers concluded that the result was caused by the earthworms’ condition.","zh":"研究人員得出結論，認為該結果是由蚯蚓的狀況造成。"},{"en":"To conclude that something is true means to decide it after considering evidence.","zh":"conclude that某事屬實，意思是在考慮證據後作出判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher may conclude that students need more practice after marking many weak essays.","zh":"老師批改許多薄弱文章後，可能得出結論認為學生需要更多練習。"},{"en":"Researchers should conclude carefully so they do not claim more than the evidence supports.","zh":"研究人員應謹慎下結論，以免聲稱超出證據支持範圍。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a reasoned judgement.","zh":"這個短語引入有理由支持的判斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a direct result of","meaning":"……的直接結果","examples":[{"en":"The lower germination rate was a direct result of earthworms failing to fulfil their role.","zh":"較低發芽率是蚯蚓未能發揮作用的直接結果。"},{"en":"A direct result of something is an outcome caused clearly by that thing.","zh":"a direct result of某事，是由該事清楚造成的結果。"},{"en":"A late bus may be a direct result of a traffic accident on the main road.","zh":"巴士遲到可能是主要道路交通意外的直接結果。"},{"en":"When causes are direct, the link between action and outcome is easier to see.","zh":"當原因直接，行動與結果之間的關係較容易看見。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a result closely to its cause.","zh":"這個短語把結果與其原因緊密連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be unable to","meaning":"無法……","examples":[{"en":"The earthworms were unable to fulfil their normal role.","zh":"蚯蚓無法發揮正常作用。"},{"en":"To be unable to do something means to not be able to do it.","zh":"be unable to do something意思是不能夠做某事。"},{"en":"A student with a broken arm may be unable to write quickly during an exam.","zh":"手臂骨折的學生可能無法在考試中快速書寫。"},{"en":"When organisms are unable to do their normal work, the system around them may suffer.","zh":"當生物無法做其正常工作，周圍系統可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lack of ability, often because of a problem or limitation.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏能力，通常因問題或限制造成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fulfil their normal role","meaning":"發揮正常作用","examples":[{"en":"The earthworms could not fulfil their normal role in making soil fertile.","zh":"蚯蚓無法發揮令土壤肥沃的正常作用。"},{"en":"To fulfil their normal role means to do the usual job or function expected of them.","zh":"fulfil their normal role意思是完成或發揮通常被期望的工作或功能。"},{"en":"Teachers fulfil their normal role when they explain, guide and support students’ learning.","zh":"老師在解釋、引導和支援學生學習時，就是發揮正常作用。"},{"en":"If earthworms cannot fulfil their role, soil may lose nutrients and structure.","zh":"如果蚯蚓不能發揮其作用，土壤可能失去養分和結構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes carrying out an expected function.","zh":"這個短語描述履行預期功能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"increase in the amount of","meaning":"……的數量增加","examples":[{"en":"The team discovered an increase in the amount of acid in the soil.","zh":"團隊發現土壤中的酸含量增加。"},{"en":"An increase in the amount of something means there is more of it than before.","zh":"increase in the amount of某物，意思是該物比以前更多。"},{"en":"A school may notice an increase in the amount of paper used during exam season.","zh":"學校可能注意到考試季節用紙量增加。"},{"en":"When the amount of acid increases in soil, plant growth may be affected.","zh":"當土壤中的酸含量增加，植物生長可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rise in quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述數量上升。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"acid found in the soil","meaning":"土壤中的酸","examples":[{"en":"The researchers found more acid in the soil.","zh":"研究人員發現土壤中的酸增加。"},{"en":"Acid found in the soil refers to acidic substances present in soil samples.","zh":"acid found in the soil指土壤樣本中存在的酸性物質。"},{"en":"Farmers may test acid in the soil before choosing crops or adding treatment.","zh":"農民在選擇作物或加入處理物前，可能測試土壤中的酸。"},{"en":"Too much acid in soil can make it harder for some plants to grow.","zh":"土壤中酸太多，可以令某些植物較難生長。"},{"en":"This phrase links soil chemistry with plant health.","zh":"這個短語把土壤化學與植物健康連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be attributed mainly to","meaning":"主要歸因於……","examples":[{"en":"The increase in acid was attributed mainly to particles from HDPE plastic.","zh":"酸含量增加主要歸因於來自HDPE塑膠的顆粒。"},{"en":"To be attributed mainly to something means to be explained mostly as being caused by it.","zh":"be attributed mainly to某事，意思是主要被解釋為由它造成。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be attributed mainly to regular practice rather than luck.","zh":"學生的進步可能主要歸因於定期練習，而不是運氣。"},{"en":"When a result is attributed mainly to one cause, that cause is seen as the most important.","zh":"當結果主要歸因於一個原因，該原因被視為最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research explanations.","zh":"這個短語常見於研究解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"conventional HDPE plastic","meaning":"傳統 HDPE 塑膠","examples":[{"en":"The acid increase was linked to conventional HDPE plastic.","zh":"酸含量增加與傳統HDPE塑膠有關。"},{"en":"Conventional HDPE plastic is ordinary high-density polyethylene, a common strong plastic material.","zh":"conventional HDPE plastic是普通高密度聚乙烯，一種常見而堅固的塑膠材料。"},{"en":"Cleaning bottles and milk containers may be made from conventional HDPE plastic.","zh":"清潔劑瓶和牛奶容器可能由傳統HDPE塑膠製成。"},{"en":"If HDPE particles affect soil chemistry, their presence may matter even when they are tiny.","zh":"如果HDPE顆粒影響土壤化學，即使它們很細小，其存在也可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase names a standard type of plastic used in the experiment.","zh":"這個短語命名實驗中使用的一種標準塑膠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"conclusions of the study","meaning":"研究結論","examples":[{"en":"The conclusions of the study make for interesting reading.","zh":"研究結論讀起來很有意思。"},{"en":"The conclusions of the study are the final findings or judgements reached after the research.","zh":"conclusions of the study是研究後得出的最終發現或判斷。"},{"en":"Students should read the conclusions of a study to understand what the evidence suggests.","zh":"學生應閱讀研究結論，以理解證據顯示甚麼。"},{"en":"Conclusions are useful only when they are supported by clear methods and data.","zh":"結論只有在由清晰方法和數據支持時才有用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the end-point of research reasoning.","zh":"這個短語指研究推理的終點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make for interesting reading","meaning":"讀起來很有意思","examples":[{"en":"The conclusions of the study make for very interesting reading.","zh":"研究結論讀起來非常有意思。"},{"en":"To make for interesting reading means to be interesting to read because the information is surprising or important.","zh":"make for interesting reading意思是因資訊令人驚訝或重要而讀起來有趣。"},{"en":"A report on students’ real sleep habits may make for interesting reading for parents.","zh":"關於學生真實睡眠習慣的報告，對家長來說可能讀起來很有意思。"},{"en":"Research makes for interesting reading when it changes how people see a familiar issue.","zh":"當研究改變人們對熟悉議題的看法，它就讀起來有意思。"},{"en":"This phrase comments on how engaging a text or finding is.","zh":"這個短語評論文本或發現的吸引程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"include the reference","meaning":"附上參考資料","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer included the reference in the notes.","zh":"講師在筆記中附上參考資料。"},{"en":"To include the reference means to add the source details so readers can find the original material.","zh":"include the reference意思是加入來源資料，讓讀者能找到原本材料。"},{"en":"A student should include the reference when using a fact from a website in an essay.","zh":"學生在文章中使用網站資料時，應附上參考資料。"},{"en":"References help readers check information and avoid plagiarism.","zh":"參考資料幫助讀者查證資訊並避免抄襲。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic notes and research writing.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術筆記和研究寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at the end of this session","meaning":"在本節課結束時","examples":[{"en":"The notes will be given at the end of this session.","zh":"筆記會在本節課結束時派發。"},{"en":"At the end of this session means when this lesson, meeting or talk finishes.","zh":"at the end of this session意思是在這節課、會議或講座完結時。"},{"en":"A teacher may collect worksheets at the end of this session before students leave.","zh":"老師可能在本節課結束時收回工作紙，然後讓學生離開。"},{"en":"Giving notes at the end helps students listen first and review later.","zh":"在結束時派筆記幫助學生先聆聽，之後再複習。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the finishing point of a class or event.","zh":"這個短語指出課堂或活動的結束時間點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"to summarise","meaning":"總括而言","examples":[{"en":"To summarise, the authors proposed a new way to regard soil.","zh":"總括而言，作者提出了一種看待土壤的新方式。"},{"en":"To summarise means to state the main points briefly.","zh":"to summarise意思是簡短說出主要重點。"},{"en":"To summarise, the school trip was safe, useful and well organised.","zh":"總括而言，學校旅行安全、有用且組織良好。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase near the end to help listeners remember the key idea.","zh":"講者在結尾附近使用這個短語，幫助聽眾記住核心想法。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that details will be reduced to the main message.","zh":"這個短語表示細節會被濃縮成主要訊息。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"propose the idea that","meaning":"提出……的想法","examples":[{"en":"The authors proposed the idea that soil should be treated like other natural processes.","zh":"作者提出土壤應像其他自然過程一樣被看待的想法。"},{"en":"To propose the idea that means to suggest a way of thinking for others to consider.","zh":"propose the idea that意思是提出一種思考方式供他人考慮。"},{"en":"A teacher may propose the idea that mistakes are useful evidence for learning.","zh":"老師可能提出錯誤是學習有用證據的想法。"},{"en":"New ideas are proposed when people want others to change how they understand a topic.","zh":"當人們希望他人改變對某主題的理解，就會提出新想法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an argument or viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語引入論點或觀點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"regard soil as","meaning":"將土壤視為……","examples":[{"en":"We need to regard soil as we would regard any other process in nature.","zh":"我們需要將土壤視為如同自然界中任何其他過程一樣。"},{"en":"To regard soil as something means to think of soil in that way.","zh":"regard soil as某物，意思是以那種方式看待土壤。"},{"en":"Farmers may regard soil as a living resource, not just dirt under their feet.","zh":"農民可能將土壤視為活的資源，而不只是腳下泥土。"},{"en":"How people regard soil affects whether they protect it or misuse it.","zh":"人們如何看待土壤，會影響他們是保護它還是濫用它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a way of understanding or valuing soil.","zh":"這個短語顯示理解或重視土壤的一種方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"process in nature","meaning":"自然界中的過程","examples":[{"en":"Soil should be regarded as a process in nature.","zh":"土壤應被視為自然界中的過程。"},{"en":"A process in nature is a natural series of changes or actions that happen over time.","zh":"process in nature是隨時間發生的一系列自然變化或行動。"},{"en":"The water cycle is a process in nature because water moves through air, land and sea.","zh":"水循環是自然界中的過程，因為水在空氣、陸地和海洋之間移動。"},{"en":"Seeing soil as a process helps people understand that it depends on decay and living organisms.","zh":"把土壤視為過程，幫助人理解它依賴分解和生物。"},{"en":"This phrase treats nature as active and changing.","zh":"這個短語把自然視為活躍且不斷變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"accept the implications of","meaning":"接受……所帶來的含意","examples":[{"en":"We should accept the implications of soil being dependent on decay.","zh":"我們應接受土壤依賴分解所帶來的含意。"},{"en":"To accept the implications of something means to recognise the consequences or meanings that follow from it.","zh":"accept the implications of某事，意思是承認由它帶來的後果或意義。"},{"en":"If a student accepts the implications of poor sleep, they may change their study schedule.","zh":"如果學生接受睡眠不足所帶來的含意，可能會改變溫習時間表。"},{"en":"Accepting implications can be uncomfortable because it may require action or responsibility.","zh":"接受含意可能令人不舒服，因為它可能要求行動或責任。"},{"en":"This phrase means understanding what an idea really leads to.","zh":"這個短語意思是理解一個想法真正導向甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be dependent on","meaning":"依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Soil is dependent on decaying and dead matter.","zh":"土壤依賴腐爛及死亡物質。"},{"en":"To be dependent on something means to need it in order to exist, work or succeed.","zh":"be dependent on某事，意思是需要它才能存在、運作或成功。"},{"en":"A baby is dependent on adults for food, safety and care.","zh":"嬰兒依賴成人提供食物、安全和照顧。"},{"en":"If a system is dependent on one part, damage to that part can affect the whole system.","zh":"如果一個系統依賴某一部分，該部分受損會影響整個系統。"},{"en":"This phrase shows reliance.","zh":"這個短語顯示依靠關係。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"decaying and dead matter","meaning":"腐爛及死亡物質","examples":[{"en":"Soil depends on decaying and dead matter.","zh":"土壤依賴腐爛及死亡物質。"},{"en":"Decaying and dead matter is organic material from once-living things that is breaking down.","zh":"decaying and dead matter是來自曾經活着的東西、正在分解的有機材料。"},{"en":"Fallen leaves, dead roots and old plant stems can become decaying matter in soil.","zh":"落葉、死亡根部和舊植物莖可以成為土壤中的腐爛物質。"},{"en":"As this matter breaks down, it can return nutrients to the soil.","zh":"當這些物質分解，它們可以把養分送回土壤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the natural material that helps create fertile soil.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助形成肥沃土壤的天然材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be passed through","meaning":"通過……","examples":[{"en":"Dead matter is passed through the bodies of earthworms.","zh":"死亡物質會通過蚯蚓的身體。"},{"en":"To be passed through something means to move through it from one part to another.","zh":"be passed through某物，意思是由一部分移動穿過它到另一部分。"},{"en":"Food is passed through the digestive system before nutrients are absorbed.","zh":"食物會通過消化系統，然後養分被吸收。"},{"en":"When organic matter passes through earthworms, it can become part of healthier soil.","zh":"當有機物通過蚯蚓身體，它可以成為更健康土壤的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement through a body, system or space.","zh":"這個短語描述通過身體、系統或空間的移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bodies of earthworms","meaning":"蚯蚓的身體","examples":[{"en":"Soil depends on matter passing through the bodies of earthworms.","zh":"土壤依賴物質通過蚯蚓的身體。"},{"en":"Bodies of earthworms refers to the physical bodies of earthworms, especially their digestive systems in this context.","zh":"bodies of earthworms指蚯蚓的身體，在此尤其指牠們的消化系統。"},{"en":"Organic matter passes through the bodies of earthworms as they feed in soil.","zh":"當蚯蚓在土壤中進食，有機物會通過蚯蚓的身體。"},{"en":"This process helps break down material and return nutrients to the soil.","zh":"這個過程幫助分解物質並把養分送回土壤。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that small organisms can play a large role in soil health.","zh":"這個短語顯示小生物可以在土壤健康中發揮大作用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"that is","meaning":"也就是說","examples":[{"en":"That is, microplastics in soil can affect ecosystems and society.","zh":"也就是說，土壤中的微塑膠可以影響生態系統和社會。"},{"en":"That is means in other words, and it introduces a clearer explanation of the previous idea.","zh":"that is意思是換言之，並引入對前一想法更清楚的解釋。"},{"en":"The school wants better attendance; that is, students should come on time every day.","zh":"學校希望改善出席率；也就是說，學生應每天準時到校。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when they want to restate an idea more directly.","zh":"作者想更直接地重述想法時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase helps make a complex point easier to understand.","zh":"這個短語幫助令複雜重點更容易理解。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"become impoverished by","meaning":"因……而變得貧瘠","examples":[{"en":"Soil becomes impoverished by the presence of microplastics.","zh":"土壤因微塑膠的存在而變得貧瘠。"},{"en":"To become impoverished by something means to become poorer, weaker or less healthy because of it.","zh":"become impoverished by某事，意思是因它而變得更貧乏、更弱或較不健康。"},{"en":"A garden can become impoverished by repeated planting without adding nutrients back to the soil.","zh":"如果反覆種植卻不補充養分，花園土壤可以因此變得貧瘠。"},{"en":"When soil becomes impoverished, plants may grow less strongly.","zh":"當土壤變得貧瘠，植物可能長得較弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes loss of richness or quality.","zh":"這個短語描述豐富程度或質素的喪失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"presence of microplastics","meaning":"微塑膠的存在","examples":[{"en":"The presence of microplastics can impoverish soil.","zh":"微塑膠的存在可以令土壤變得貧瘠。"},{"en":"The presence of microplastics means that microplastics exist or are found in a place.","zh":"presence of microplastics意思是微塑膠存在或被發現於某地方。"},{"en":"The presence of smoke in a room may show that something is burning nearby.","zh":"房間中煙霧的存在可能顯示附近有東西在燃燒。"},{"en":"If microplastics are present in soil, they may affect organisms living there.","zh":"如果微塑膠存在於土壤中，它們可能影響生活在那裡的生物。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on existence in a location, not necessarily visible amount.","zh":"這個短語著重某地存在某物，而不一定是可見數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"not only ecosystems but also","meaning":"不但生態系統，而且……","examples":[{"en":"Not only ecosystems but also the whole of society are negatively impacted.","zh":"不但生態系統，而且整個社會都受到負面影響。"},{"en":"Not only ecosystems but also means both ecosystems and another wider group are affected.","zh":"not only ecosystems but also意思是不但生態系統，還有另一個更廣泛群體都受影響。"},{"en":"Poor air quality harms not only students’ health but also their concentration in class.","zh":"空氣質素差不但傷害學生健康，而且影響他們上課專注力。"},{"en":"This structure adds a second, often more surprising or broader, affected area.","zh":"這個結構加入第二個、通常更令人意外或更廣泛的受影響範圍。"},{"en":"It helps show that a problem has more than one level of impact.","zh":"它幫助顯示一個問題有多於一個層面的影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the whole of society","meaning":"整個社會","examples":[{"en":"The whole of society can be affected by poor soil.","zh":"整個社會都可以受到貧瘠土壤影響。"},{"en":"The whole of society means all people and social systems, not just one small group.","zh":"the whole of society意思是所有人和社會系統，而不只是某一小群體。"},{"en":"A serious food shortage can affect the whole of society, from families to businesses.","zh":"嚴重食物短缺可以影響整個社會，由家庭到企業都受影響。"},{"en":"When soil quality falls, farmers, consumers and communities may all be affected.","zh":"當土壤質素下降，農民、消費者和社區都可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a broad social impact.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛社會影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be negatively impacted","meaning":"受到負面影響","examples":[{"en":"Ecosystems and society are negatively impacted by microplastics in soil.","zh":"生態系統和社會受到土壤中微塑膠的負面影響。"},{"en":"To be negatively impacted means to be harmed, weakened or affected in a bad way.","zh":"be negatively impacted意思是受到傷害、削弱或不良影響。"},{"en":"Students’ learning can be negatively impacted by noise, hunger and lack of sleep.","zh":"噪音、飢餓和睡眠不足可以對學生學習造成負面影響。"},{"en":"If farming is negatively impacted, food supply and prices may also be affected.","zh":"如果農業受到負面影響，食物供應和價格也可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unfavourable effect on people, systems or conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述對人、系統或情況的不利影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 7 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/listening/Practice 8/task-1":[{"front":"one of the supervisors","meaning":"其中一位主管","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden is one of the supervisors at the supermarket.","zh":"Kaeden 是超級市場其中一位主管。"},{"en":"One of the supervisors means one person in a group of people who manage or guide workers.","zh":"one of the supervisors 指負責管理或指導員工的一群人之中的其中一人。"},{"en":"One of the supervisors checks the staff timetable before the shop opens.","zh":"其中一位主管會在店舖開門前檢查員工時間表。"},{"en":"If there is a problem at work, one of the supervisors can give instructions.","zh":"如果工作上有問題，其中一位主管可以給予指示。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a manager without saying he is the only manager.","zh":"這個短語指出某人是主管之一，而不是唯一主管。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"welcome to the team","meaning":"歡迎加入團隊","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden welcomes Charlotte to the team.","zh":"Kaeden 歡迎 Charlotte 加入團隊。"},{"en":"To welcome someone to the team means to greet a new member and make them feel included.","zh":"welcome someone to the team 指迎接新成員，並令對方覺得被接納。"},{"en":"A manager may welcome a new cashier to the team on her first day.","zh":"經理可能在新收銀員第一天上班時歡迎她加入團隊。"},{"en":"If new workers feel welcomed to the team, they may become confident more quickly.","zh":"如果新員工感到被歡迎加入團隊，他們可能更快建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase is friendly and often used at the start of a job.","zh":"這個短語語氣友善，常用於開始新工作時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get my name wrong","meaning":"把我的名字弄錯","examples":[{"en":"People often get Kaeden’s name wrong.","zh":"人們常常把 Kaeden 的名字弄錯。"},{"en":"To get someone’s name wrong means to say, write, or remember the name incorrectly.","zh":"get someone’s name wrong 指把某人的名字說錯、寫錯或記錯。"},{"en":"A teacher may get a new student’s name wrong during the first lesson.","zh":"老師在第一堂課可能把新學生的名字弄錯。"},{"en":"If people get your name wrong often, spelling it clearly can help.","zh":"如果人們常把你的名字弄錯，清楚拼寫可以有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mistake with someone’s name.","zh":"這個短語描述關於名字的錯誤。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"know how to spell it","meaning":"知道如何拼寫","examples":[{"en":"People often do not know how to spell Kaeden’s name.","zh":"人們常常不知道如何拼寫 Kaeden 的名字。"},{"en":"To know how to spell it means to know the correct letters in a word or name.","zh":"know how to spell it 指知道某個字或名字的正確字母。"},{"en":"A receptionist needs to know how to spell a customer’s name before printing a badge.","zh":"接待員在列印名牌前，需要知道如何拼寫顧客姓名。"},{"en":"If people do not know how to spell a name, records may contain mistakes.","zh":"如果人們不知道如何拼寫名字，紀錄可能出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when accuracy in writing matters.","zh":"這個短語適用於需要書寫準確的情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in case","meaning":"以防","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden spells his name in case Charlotte ever needs to write it.","zh":"Kaeden 拼出自己的名字，以防 Charlotte 日後需要寫下它。"},{"en":"In case means because something might happen later and you want to be prepared.","zh":"in case 指因為某事日後可能發生，所以先作準備。"},{"en":"Take an umbrella in case it rains after school.","zh":"帶傘吧，以防放學後下雨。"},{"en":"If you save a phone number in case you need help, you can act quickly later.","zh":"如果你先儲存電話號碼以防需要幫忙，之後就能快速行動。"},{"en":"This phrase explains preparation for a possible situation.","zh":"這個短語解釋為可能情況作準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"try and remember","meaning":"努力記住","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte says she will try and remember Kaeden’s name.","zh":"Charlotte 說她會努力記住 Kaeden 的名字。"},{"en":"To try and remember something means to make an effort not to forget it.","zh":"try and remember something 指努力不忘記某事。"},{"en":"A student may try and remember a new teacher’s email address.","zh":"學生可能努力記住新老師的電郵地址。"},{"en":"If a name is unusual, repeating it quietly can help you try and remember it.","zh":"如果名字較少見，輕聲重複它可以幫助你努力記住。"},{"en":"This phrase shows effort, not certainty.","zh":"這個短語表示努力，而不是肯定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"practical things","meaning":"實際事項","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte has a few practical things to sort out in the morning.","zh":"Charlotte 早上有幾件實際事項要處理。"},{"en":"Practical things are necessary everyday matters that must be arranged before work can run smoothly.","zh":"practical things 指工作順利進行前必須安排好的日常必要事項。"},{"en":"On the first school day, practical things include getting a timetable and finding classrooms.","zh":"開學第一天，實際事項包括拿時間表和找課室。"},{"en":"If practical things are not sorted out, a new worker may not know where to go.","zh":"如果實際事項沒有安排好，新員工可能不知道去哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to useful arrangements, not theory.","zh":"這個短語指實用安排，而不是理論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sort out","meaning":"處理；安排好","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte needs to sort out a few practical things.","zh":"Charlotte 需要處理幾件實際事項。"},{"en":"To sort out something means to deal with it, organise it, or fix it.","zh":"sort out something 指處理、整理或解決某事。"},{"en":"A student must sort out his login details before using the school computer.","zh":"學生使用學校電腦前，必須先處理登入資料。"},{"en":"If a manager sorts out a problem early, the team can work without delay.","zh":"如果經理及早處理問題，團隊就能不受延誤地工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes handling something until it is in order.","zh":"這個短語描述把事情處理妥當。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"show someone what to do","meaning":"告訴某人要做甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden will show Charlotte what she is going to do today.","zh":"Kaeden 會告訴 Charlotte 今天要做甚麼。"},{"en":"To show someone what to do means to explain or demonstrate the task they need to perform.","zh":"show someone what to do 指解釋或示範某人需要完成的工作。"},{"en":"A senior student may show a new club member what to do at registration.","zh":"高年級學生可能在登記時告訴新學會成員要做甚麼。"},{"en":"If no one shows new workers what to do, they may make simple mistakes.","zh":"如果沒有人告訴新員工要做甚麼，他們可能犯簡單錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in training or first-day instructions.","zh":"這個短語常用於培訓或第一天工作指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"front desk","meaning":"前台","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte has to go to the front desk first.","zh":"Charlotte 必須先去前台。"},{"en":"The front desk is the reception area where visitors or staff first ask for help or information.","zh":"front desk 指訪客或員工首先尋求幫助或資料的接待處。"},{"en":"Hotel guests usually check in at the front desk.","zh":"酒店住客通常在前台辦理入住。"},{"en":"If a workplace has security rules, new staff may need to report to the front desk first.","zh":"如果工作場所有保安規則，新員工可能要先到前台報到。"},{"en":"This phrase names the main reception point.","zh":"這個短語指出主要接待點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"letter of appointment","meaning":"聘用信；任命信","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte needs to show her letter of appointment at the front desk.","zh":"Charlotte 需要在前台出示她的聘用信。"},{"en":"A letter of appointment is an official letter confirming someone’s job or role.","zh":"letter of appointment 指確認某人職位或角色的正式信件。"},{"en":"A new teacher may bring a letter of appointment on the first day of school.","zh":"新老師可能在開工第一天帶同聘用信。"},{"en":"If staff check the letter of appointment, they can confirm the person should be there.","zh":"如果職員檢查聘用信，就能確認該人應在場。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal proof of employment or appointment.","zh":"這個短語指聘用或任命的正式證明。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pick up my badge","meaning":"領取我的職員證","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte has to pick up her badge at the front desk.","zh":"Charlotte 必須在前台領取她的職員證。"},{"en":"To pick up my badge means to collect my staff or visitor identification card.","zh":"pick up my badge 指領取我的職員或訪客身份證明牌。"},{"en":"A volunteer may pick up her badge before entering the event hall.","zh":"義工進入活動禮堂前，可能要領取職員證。"},{"en":"If you do not pick up your badge, security may not let you enter staff-only areas.","zh":"如果你沒有領取職員證，保安可能不讓你進入員工專用區域。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collecting an ID item.","zh":"這個短語描述領取身份證明物件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"staffroom","meaning":"職員休息室","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte needs her badge to enter the staffroom.","zh":"Charlotte 需要職員證才能進入職員休息室。"},{"en":"A staffroom is a room where employees can rest, store things, or take breaks.","zh":"staffroom 指員工休息、存放物品或小休的房間。"},{"en":"Teachers may eat lunch and prepare lessons in the staffroom.","zh":"老師可能在職員休息室吃午餐和備課。"},{"en":"If a staffroom is locked, workers may need a badge or key to enter.","zh":"如果職員休息室上鎖，員工可能需要職員證或鑰匙才能進入。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an employee-only rest area.","zh":"這個短語指員工專用休息區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"shoppers are not allowed","meaning":"顧客不得進入","examples":[{"en":"There are areas of the supermarket where shoppers are not allowed.","zh":"超級市場有些區域顧客不得進入。"},{"en":"Shoppers are not allowed means customers do not have permission to enter or do something.","zh":"shoppers are not allowed 指顧客沒有許可進入某處或做某事。"},{"en":"Shoppers are not allowed inside the stockroom because heavy boxes may fall.","zh":"顧客不得進入貨倉，因為重箱可能掉下來。"},{"en":"If shoppers enter staff-only areas, it can create safety and security problems.","zh":"如果顧客進入員工專用區域，可能造成安全和保安問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rule limiting customer access.","zh":"這個短語描述限制顧客進入的規則。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"after you have finished","meaning":"在你完成之後","examples":[{"en":"After Charlotte has finished at the front desk, Kaeden will take her to the staffroom.","zh":"Charlotte 在前台完成手續後，Kaeden 會帶她去職員休息室。"},{"en":"After you have finished means when you have completed the task you are doing.","zh":"after you have finished 指當你完成正在做的任務後。"},{"en":"After you have finished the form, give it to the school office.","zh":"在你填完表格之後，把它交給校務處。"},{"en":"If one step must be completed first, instructions often begin with after you have finished.","zh":"如果某一步必須先完成，指示常會用 after you have finished 開始。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the order of actions.","zh":"這個短語顯示行動次序。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"take someone to","meaning":"帶某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden will take Charlotte to the staffroom.","zh":"Kaeden 會帶 Charlotte 去職員休息室。"},{"en":"To take someone to a place means to lead, guide, or bring that person there.","zh":"take someone to a place 指帶領、引導或陪某人到某地方。"},{"en":"A receptionist may take a visitor to the meeting room.","zh":"接待員可能帶訪客去會議室。"},{"en":"If a new worker does not know the building, someone should take them to the right place.","zh":"如果新員工不熟悉大樓，應有人帶他到正確地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes guiding a person to a destination.","zh":"這個短語描述帶某人前往目的地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rucksack","meaning":"背囊","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte can put her coat and rucksack in a locker.","zh":"Charlotte 可以把外套和背囊放進儲物櫃。"},{"en":"A rucksack is a bag carried on the back, often used for books, clothes, or daily items.","zh":"rucksack 指背在背上的袋，常用來放書、衣物或日常用品。"},{"en":"A student may carry a rucksack with textbooks, lunch, and a water bottle.","zh":"學生可能用背囊裝課本、午餐和水樽。"},{"en":"If a rucksack is left on the shop floor, it may block customers or create a safety risk.","zh":"如果背囊留在店舖地上，可能阻礙顧客或造成安全風險。"},{"en":"This word is common in British English for backpack.","zh":"這個字在英式英語中常指背包。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lockers","meaning":"儲物櫃","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte can use one of the lockers in the staffroom.","zh":"Charlotte 可以使用職員休息室其中一個儲物櫃。"},{"en":"Lockers are small lockable cupboards used for storing personal belongings.","zh":"lockers 指可上鎖的小櫃，用來存放個人物品。"},{"en":"Students may keep sports clothes and textbooks in school lockers.","zh":"學生可能把運動服和課本放在學校儲物櫃。"},{"en":"If staff use lockers, bags and coats will not be left in work areas.","zh":"如果員工使用儲物櫃，袋和外套就不會留在工作區域。"},{"en":"This word refers to secure storage spaces.","zh":"這個字指安全存放空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"whichever one is free","meaning":"哪一個空着就用哪一個","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte can take whichever locker is free.","zh":"Charlotte 可以哪個儲物櫃空着就用哪一個。"},{"en":"Whichever one is free means any one that is not being used or occupied.","zh":"whichever one is free 指任何一個未被使用或佔用的。"},{"en":"In the library, students can sit at whichever desk is free.","zh":"在圖書館，學生可以哪張書桌空着就坐哪張。"},{"en":"If lockers are shared, workers should choose whichever one is free and return the key later.","zh":"如果儲物櫃是共用的，員工應哪個空着就用哪個，之後歸還鑰匙。"},{"en":"This phrase gives flexible choice among available options.","zh":"這個短語表示可在現有選項中靈活選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"try not to","meaning":"盡量不要","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte should try not to lose the locker key.","zh":"Charlotte 應盡量不要弄失儲物櫃鑰匙。"},{"en":"To try not to do something means to make an effort to avoid doing it.","zh":"try not to do something 指努力避免做某事。"},{"en":"Try not to forget your homework folder before leaving home.","zh":"離家前盡量不要忘記功課文件夾。"},{"en":"If you try not to lose a key, you may keep it in the same pocket each time.","zh":"如果你盡量不弄失鑰匙，可以每次把它放在同一個口袋。"},{"en":"This phrase gives gentle advice or warning.","zh":"這個短語給出溫和建議或提醒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at the end of the day","meaning":"在一天結束時","examples":[{"en":"At the end of the day, Charlotte should leave the key in the locker door.","zh":"在一天結束時，Charlotte 應把鑰匙留在儲物櫃門上。"},{"en":"At the end of the day means when the working day or activity is finished.","zh":"at the end of the day 指工作日或活動完成時。"},{"en":"At the end of the day, students must tidy the classroom before leaving.","zh":"在一天結束時，學生必須離開前整理課室。"},{"en":"If staff return keys at the end of the day, the next shift can use them.","zh":"如果員工在一天結束時歸還鑰匙，下一班人就能使用。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the final part of a day or task.","zh":"這個短語標示一天或任務的最後部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"leave it in the door","meaning":"把它留在門上","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte should leave the key in the door for the next person.","zh":"Charlotte 應把鑰匙留在門上，給下一個人使用。"},{"en":"To leave it in the door means to keep the key placed in the lock instead of taking it away.","zh":"leave it in the door 指把鑰匙留在鎖上，而不是帶走。"},{"en":"A cleaner may leave the cupboard key in the door after finishing the job.","zh":"清潔工完成工作後，可能把櫃門鑰匙留在門上。"},{"en":"If shared keys are left in the door, the next user can find them easily.","zh":"如果共用鑰匙留在門上，下一位使用者就容易找到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes leaving a key where others can use it.","zh":"這個短語描述把鑰匙留在可供他人使用的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"for the next person to use","meaning":"讓下一個人使用","examples":[{"en":"The key should be left in the door for the next person to use.","zh":"鑰匙應留在門上，讓下一個人使用。"},{"en":"For the next person to use means so that the following user can use it later.","zh":"for the next person to use 指讓之後的使用者稍後可以使用。"},{"en":"Please leave the classroom clean for the next class to use.","zh":"請把課室保持清潔，讓下一班使用。"},{"en":"If shared equipment is prepared for the next person to use, work runs more smoothly.","zh":"如果共用設備已準備好讓下一個人使用，工作會更順利。"},{"en":"This phrase explains consideration for the following user.","zh":"這個短語解釋對下一位使用者的體貼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Will do","meaning":"好的；會照做","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte says, “Will do,” when Kaeden tells her what to do with the key.","zh":"Kaeden 告訴 Charlotte 如何處理鑰匙時，她說：「好的，會照做。」"},{"en":"Will do means I will do that or I will follow the instruction.","zh":"Will do 指我會做那件事，或我會按照指示做。"},{"en":"If a teacher says, “Please send me the file tonight,” a student may reply, “Will do.”","zh":"如果老師說：「今晚請把檔案寄給我」，學生可能回答：「好的，會照做。」"},{"en":"This phrase is short, polite, and shows agreement to an instruction.","zh":"這個短語簡短、有禮，並表示同意指示。"},{"en":"It is often used in spoken English or informal messages.","zh":"它常用於英語口語或非正式訊息。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"HR department","meaning":"人力資源部","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte also needs to go to the HR department.","zh":"Charlotte 也需要去人力資源部。"},{"en":"The HR department is the part of a company that deals with staff records, hiring, training, and workplace issues.","zh":"HR department 指公司中負責員工紀錄、招聘、培訓和工作場所問題的部門。"},{"en":"New employees may visit the HR department to complete forms on their first day.","zh":"新員工可能在第一天到人力資源部填表。"},{"en":"If HR records are wrong, pay, contracts, or staff benefits may be affected.","zh":"如果人力資源紀錄有錯，薪金、合約或員工福利可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the human resources office.","zh":"這個短語指人力資源辦公室。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"really helpful","meaning":"很樂意幫忙","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden says Tiffany is really helpful.","zh":"Kaeden 說 Tiffany 很樂意幫忙。"},{"en":"Really helpful means very willing and able to assist people.","zh":"really helpful 指非常願意而且能夠協助別人。"},{"en":"A really helpful librarian can show students how to find the right books quickly.","zh":"很樂意幫忙的圖書館員可以教學生快速找到合適書籍。"},{"en":"If a colleague is really helpful, new staff feel less nervous when asking questions.","zh":"如果同事很樂意幫忙，新員工提問時會較不緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase gives strong praise for someone’s support.","zh":"這個短語強烈稱讚某人的支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be told to","meaning":"被告知要……","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte was told to bring her passport.","zh":"Charlotte 被告知要帶護照。"},{"en":"To be told to do something means to receive an instruction to do it.","zh":"be told to do something 指收到做某事的指示。"},{"en":"Students are told to arrive ten minutes before the exam begins.","zh":"學生被告知要在考試開始前十分鐘到達。"},{"en":"If staff are told to bring documents, they should prepare them before coming to work.","zh":"如果員工被告知要帶文件，就應在上班前準備好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being given a clear instruction.","zh":"這個短語描述收到清楚指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"bring something with me","meaning":"隨身帶備某物","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte was told to bring her passport with her.","zh":"Charlotte 被告知要隨身帶備護照。"},{"en":"To bring something with me means to carry or take it when I go somewhere.","zh":"bring something with me 指去某地方時帶同某物。"},{"en":"I need to bring my student card with me to enter the library.","zh":"我需要隨身帶備學生證，才能進入圖書館。"},{"en":"If you forget to bring important documents with you, registration may take longer.","zh":"如果你忘記隨身帶備重要文件，登記可能需時更久。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses taking an item along.","zh":"這個短語強調帶同某件物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take a note of","meaning":"記下","examples":[{"en":"HR needs to take a note of the number in Charlotte’s passport.","zh":"人力資源部需要記下 Charlotte 護照上的號碼。"},{"en":"To take a note of something means to write it down or record it for later use.","zh":"take a note of something 指把某事寫下或記錄下來，以供日後使用。"},{"en":"A teacher may take a note of students who are absent.","zh":"老師可能記下缺席學生的名字。"},{"en":"If HR takes a note of a passport number, the company can keep accurate records.","zh":"如果人力資源部記下護照號碼，公司就能保存準確紀錄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recording information carefully.","zh":"這個短語描述小心記錄資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ID card","meaning":"身份證","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte can show her ID card instead of her passport.","zh":"Charlotte 可以出示身份證代替護照。"},{"en":"An ID card is an official card that proves a person’s identity.","zh":"ID card 指證明個人身份的官方卡片。"},{"en":"Students may need an ID card to borrow books or sit public exams.","zh":"學生可能需要身份證來借書或參加公開考試。"},{"en":"If a passport is not available, an ID card may still confirm who the person is.","zh":"如果沒有護照，身份證仍可確認該人的身份。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to identity proof.","zh":"這個短語指身份證明。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give someone a uniform","meaning":"給某人制服","examples":[{"en":"Tiffany will give Charlotte a uniform.","zh":"Tiffany 會給 Charlotte 一套制服。"},{"en":"To give someone a uniform means to provide work or school clothing that the person must wear.","zh":"give someone a uniform 指提供某人工作或學校要求穿着的服裝。"},{"en":"A restaurant manager may give new waiters a uniform before their first shift.","zh":"餐廳經理可能在新侍應第一班前給他們制服。"},{"en":"If staff wear uniforms, customers can identify them more easily.","zh":"如果員工穿制服，顧客就更容易認出他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes providing required clothing.","zh":"這個短語描述提供指定服裝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in different sizes","meaning":"有不同尺碼","examples":[{"en":"The uniforms come in different sizes.","zh":"制服有不同尺碼。"},{"en":"In different sizes means available in more than one size so people can choose the right fit.","zh":"in different sizes 指有多於一種尺碼可供選擇，讓人挑選合身大小。"},{"en":"School shirts come in different sizes because students have different body shapes.","zh":"校服恤衫有不同尺碼，因為學生身形不同。"},{"en":"If uniforms come in different sizes, workers can move more comfortably.","zh":"如果制服有不同尺碼，員工活動會更舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase describes size options.","zh":"這個短語描述尺碼選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"tell someone what you need","meaning":"告訴某人你需要甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte should tell Tiffany what size she needs.","zh":"Charlotte 應告訴 Tiffany 她需要甚麼尺碼。"},{"en":"To tell someone what you need means to clearly say what is required or suitable for you.","zh":"tell someone what you need 指清楚說出你需要或適合的是甚麼。"},{"en":"A patient should tell the nurse what medicine he needs.","zh":"病人應告訴護士自己需要甚麼藥。"},{"en":"If you do not tell staff what you need, they may give you the wrong item.","zh":"如果你不告訴職員你需要甚麼，他們可能給你錯誤物品。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses clear communication.","zh":"這個短語強調清楚溝通。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"come with you","meaning":"和你一起去","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden will not come with Charlotte to HR.","zh":"Kaeden 不會和 Charlotte 一起去人力資源部。"},{"en":"To come with you means to go together with you to a place.","zh":"come with you 指與你一起去某地方。"},{"en":"A friend may come with you to the clinic if you feel nervous.","zh":"如果你感到緊張，朋友可能和你一起去診所。"},{"en":"If no one comes with a new worker, clear directions become more important.","zh":"如果沒有人陪新員工一起去，清晰方向就更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accompanying someone.","zh":"這個短語描述陪同某人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sort something else out","meaning":"處理另一件事","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden has to go and sort something else out.","zh":"Kaeden 必須去處理另一件事。"},{"en":"To sort something else out means to deal with another problem or task.","zh":"sort something else out 指處理另一個問題或任務。"},{"en":"A teacher may leave the classroom briefly to sort something else out in the office.","zh":"老師可能短暫離開課室，到辦公室處理另一件事。"},{"en":"If a supervisor has to sort something else out, another worker may need to wait.","zh":"如果主管要處理另一件事，另一位員工可能需要等候。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that attention must move to another matter.","zh":"這個短語顯示注意力要轉到另一件事上。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"bread slicer","meaning":"麵包切片機","examples":[{"en":"There is a problem with a bread slicer.","zh":"有一部麵包切片機出了問題。"},{"en":"A bread slicer is a machine used to cut loaves of bread into slices.","zh":"bread slicer 指用來把麵包切成片的機器。"},{"en":"A bakery uses a bread slicer so customers can buy evenly sliced bread.","zh":"麵包店使用麵包切片機，讓顧客買到切得均勻的麵包。"},{"en":"If a bread slicer is not working properly, staff may stop using it for safety reasons.","zh":"如果麵包切片機運作不正常，員工可能因安全理由停止使用。"},{"en":"This phrase names a bakery machine.","zh":"這個短語指出一種麵包部機器。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"near the staffroom","meaning":"在職員休息室附近","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte asks whether the HR office is near the staffroom.","zh":"Charlotte 問人力資源部辦公室是否在職員休息室附近。"},{"en":"Near the staffroom means close to the room used by staff for breaks or storage.","zh":"near the staffroom 指接近員工休息或存放物品的房間。"},{"en":"The toilets are near the staffroom, so new workers can find them easily.","zh":"洗手間在職員休息室附近，所以新員工容易找到。"},{"en":"If HR is near the staffroom, Charlotte will not need complicated directions.","zh":"如果人力資源部在職員休息室附近，Charlotte 就不需要複雜指示。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location in relation to the staffroom.","zh":"這個短語描述相對於職員休息室的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"first floor","meaning":"一樓","examples":[{"en":"The staffroom is on the first floor.","zh":"職員休息室在一樓。"},{"en":"The first floor is the level of a building called the first floor in that location’s system.","zh":"first floor 指按當地樓層系統稱為一樓的樓層。"},{"en":"A school office may be on the first floor near the main entrance.","zh":"學校辦公室可能在一樓近正門位置。"},{"en":"If a room is on the first floor, visitors should check whether stairs or a lift are needed.","zh":"如果房間在一樓，訪客應確認是否需要行樓梯或搭升降機。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a building level.","zh":"這個短語提供建築物樓層。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a couple of floors above","meaning":"上面幾層","examples":[{"en":"The HR office is a couple of floors above the staffroom.","zh":"人力資源部辦公室在職員休息室上面幾層。"},{"en":"A couple of floors above means two or a few levels higher in the same building.","zh":"a couple of floors above 指在同一建築物中高兩層或幾層。"},{"en":"The music room is a couple of floors above the library.","zh":"音樂室在圖書館上面幾層。"},{"en":"If an office is a couple of floors above, staff may need the stairs or lift.","zh":"如果辦公室在上面幾層，員工可能需要行樓梯或搭升降機。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate vertical location.","zh":"這個短語提供大約的垂直位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"third floor","meaning":"三樓","examples":[{"en":"The HR office is on the third floor.","zh":"人力資源部辦公室在三樓。"},{"en":"The third floor is the building level called the third floor.","zh":"third floor 指被稱為三樓的建築物樓層。"},{"en":"A dentist’s clinic may be on the third floor of a shopping centre.","zh":"牙科診所可能在商場三樓。"},{"en":"If a room is on the third floor, signs should help visitors find the right staircase or lift.","zh":"如果房間在三樓，標示應幫助訪客找到正確樓梯或升降機。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific floor.","zh":"這個短語指出特定樓層。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"staircase","meaning":"樓梯","examples":[{"en":"There is a staircase outside the staffroom.","zh":"職員休息室外面有樓梯。"},{"en":"A staircase is a set of stairs connecting different floors of a building.","zh":"staircase 指連接建築物不同樓層的一組樓梯。"},{"en":"Students use the staircase when the school lift is crowded.","zh":"當學校升降機擠迫時，學生會使用樓梯。"},{"en":"If a staircase is outside the staffroom, staff can go upstairs without crossing the shop floor.","zh":"如果樓梯在職員休息室外，員工可以不用穿過店面就上樓。"},{"en":"This word refers to the stairs as a structure.","zh":"這個字指作為建築結構的樓梯。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"come and find me","meaning":"來找我","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte should come and find Kaeden in the bakery section.","zh":"Charlotte 應到麵包部來找 Kaeden。"},{"en":"Come and find me means come to where I am and look for me there.","zh":"come and find me 指到我所在的地方找我。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “Come and find me after class if you need help.”","zh":"老師可能說：「如果你需要幫忙，下課後來找我。」"},{"en":"If a new worker gets lost, being told where to come and find someone is reassuring.","zh":"如果新員工迷路，知道可以到哪裡找人會令人安心。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear way to get help later.","zh":"這個短語提供日後尋求幫助的清楚方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"bakery section","meaning":"麵包部；烘焙區","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden will be in the bakery section of the shop.","zh":"Kaeden 會在店舖的麵包部。"},{"en":"The bakery section is the part of a shop where bread, cakes, and baked goods are sold or prepared.","zh":"bakery section 指店內售賣或準備麵包、蛋糕和烘焙食品的區域。"},{"en":"Customers may smell fresh bread when they walk past the bakery section.","zh":"顧客走過麵包部時，可能聞到新鮮麵包香味。"},{"en":"If the bakery section is busy, staff must keep shelves full and labels clear.","zh":"如果麵包部繁忙，員工必須保持貨架充足和標籤清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase names a supermarket department.","zh":"這個短語指出超級市場的一個部門。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"look forward to getting started","meaning":"期待開始","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte is looking forward to getting started.","zh":"Charlotte 期待開始工作。"},{"en":"To look forward to getting started means to feel excited about beginning a new task or job.","zh":"look forward to getting started 指對開始新任務或新工作感到興奮。"},{"en":"A student may look forward to getting started on a drama project with friends.","zh":"學生可能期待與朋友開始戲劇專題。"},{"en":"If someone looks forward to starting work, they probably feel positive and motivated.","zh":"如果某人期待開始工作，他大概感到正面和有動力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows eager anticipation.","zh":"這個短語表示熱切期待。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"give someone my phone number","meaning":"給某人我的電話號碼","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden gives Charlotte his phone number.","zh":"Kaeden 把自己的電話號碼給 Charlotte。"},{"en":"To give someone my phone number means to share my contact number with that person.","zh":"give someone my phone number 指把我的聯絡電話分享給某人。"},{"en":"A tutor may give a student her phone number for urgent lesson changes.","zh":"導師可能把電話號碼給學生，以便緊急更改課堂。"},{"en":"If a supervisor gives a new worker his phone number, the worker can ask for help quickly.","zh":"如果主管把電話號碼給新員工，新員工就能快速求助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sharing contact information.","zh":"這個短語描述分享聯絡資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in case you cannot find me","meaning":"以防你找不到我","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden gives Charlotte his number in case she cannot find him.","zh":"Kaeden 把電話號碼給 Charlotte，以防她找不到他。"},{"en":"In case you cannot find me means because it is possible you may not know where I am later.","zh":"in case you cannot find me 指因為你之後可能不知道我在哪裡。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students her office room number in case they cannot find her after school.","zh":"老師可能把辦公室房號給學生，以防他們放學後找不到她。"},{"en":"If a workplace is large, contact details help in case someone cannot find a supervisor.","zh":"如果工作場所很大，聯絡資料能在某人找不到主管時提供幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase prepares for a possible difficulty.","zh":"這個短語為可能出現的困難作準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Have you got your phone there?","meaning":"你手機在身邊嗎？","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden asks Charlotte whether she has her phone there.","zh":"Kaeden 問 Charlotte 她手機是否在身邊。"},{"en":"Have you got your phone there? means do you have your phone with you right now?","zh":"Have you got your phone there? 指你現在有沒有把手機帶在身邊。"},{"en":"A parent may ask, “Have you got your phone there?” before sending an address.","zh":"家長傳地址前可能問：「你手機在身邊嗎？」"},{"en":"If someone has their phone there, they can save a number immediately.","zh":"如果某人手機在身邊，就可以立即儲存電話號碼。"},{"en":"This question checks whether the listener can use the phone at that moment.","zh":"這個問題確認聽者當下能否使用手機。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"double-six","meaning":"兩個六","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden says “double-six” when giving his phone number.","zh":"Kaeden 讀電話號碼時說「兩個六」。"},{"en":"Double-six means two sixes together in a number.","zh":"double-six 指一個號碼中連續兩個六。"},{"en":"In a phone number, 6602 may be read as “double-six zero two.”","zh":"在電話號碼中，6602 可以讀作「兩個六、零、二」。"},{"en":"Saying double-six can make a long number easier to hear and remember.","zh":"說 double-six 可以令長號碼更容易聽清和記住。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when reading numbers aloud.","zh":"這個短語用於朗讀數字。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tasks today","meaning":"今天的工作","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte’s tasks today are in several sections of the supermarket.","zh":"Charlotte 今天的工作分布在超級市場幾個部門。"},{"en":"Tasks today are the jobs or duties someone needs to do on that day.","zh":"tasks today 指某人在當天需要完成的工作或職責。"},{"en":"A teacher may write the class’s tasks today on the board.","zh":"老師可能把全班今天的工作寫在黑板上。"},{"en":"If tasks today are clear, workers can move from one job to the next smoothly.","zh":"如果今天的工作清楚，員工就能順利從一項工作轉到下一項。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the day’s work list.","zh":"這個短語指當天工作清單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sushi counter","meaning":"壽司櫃位","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte will work on the sushi counter.","zh":"Charlotte 會在壽司櫃位工作。"},{"en":"A sushi counter is the shop area where sushi is prepared, displayed, or sold.","zh":"sushi counter 指準備、展示或售賣壽司的店內區域。"},{"en":"Customers may choose lunch boxes from the sushi counter during the lunch rush.","zh":"顧客可能在午飯繁忙時間從壽司櫃位選購飯盒。"},{"en":"If the sushi counter is busy, staff must keep food fresh and the area clean.","zh":"如果壽司櫃位很忙，員工必須保持食物新鮮和地方清潔。"},{"en":"This phrase names a food counter selling sushi.","zh":"這個短語指出售賣壽司的食品櫃位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"meat and fish counters","meaning":"肉類及魚類櫃位","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte will also work on the meat and fish counters.","zh":"Charlotte 也會在肉類及魚類櫃位工作。"},{"en":"Meat and fish counters are shop areas where fresh meat and fish are displayed and sold.","zh":"meat and fish counters 指展示和售賣新鮮肉類及魚類的店內區域。"},{"en":"A customer may ask staff at the meat and fish counters to weigh a piece of salmon.","zh":"顧客可能請肉類及魚類櫃位的職員稱一塊三文魚。"},{"en":"If meat and fish counters are not cleaned properly, hygiene risks can increase.","zh":"如果肉類及魚類櫃位沒有妥善清潔，衞生風險可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to fresh food service areas.","zh":"這個短語指新鮮食品服務區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"check sell-by dates","meaning":"檢查最後銷售日期","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte’s first job is to check sell-by dates on bread and cakes.","zh":"Charlotte 的第一項工作是檢查麵包和蛋糕的最後銷售日期。"},{"en":"To check sell-by dates means to look at the final date by which products should be sold.","zh":"check sell-by dates 指查看產品應在何日前售出的最後日期。"},{"en":"Supermarket staff check sell-by dates so customers do not buy items that are too old.","zh":"超市職員檢查最後銷售日期，以免顧客買到太舊的貨品。"},{"en":"If sell-by dates are near, staff may reduce the price or remove the product.","zh":"如果最後銷售日期臨近，員工可能減價或移走產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important stock-checking task.","zh":"這個短語描述重要的存貨檢查工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bread and cakes","meaning":"麵包和蛋糕","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte has to check the sell-by dates on bread and cakes.","zh":"Charlotte 必須檢查麵包和蛋糕的最後銷售日期。"},{"en":"Bread and cakes are baked foods that can become stale or unsafe after some time.","zh":"bread and cakes 指烘焙食品，過一段時間可能變乾或不安全。"},{"en":"A bakery shelf may contain bread and cakes with different sell-by dates.","zh":"麵包店貨架可能有不同最後銷售日期的麵包和蛋糕。"},{"en":"If bread and cakes are close to their sell-by dates, shops may put discount labels on them.","zh":"如果麵包和蛋糕接近最後銷售日期，店舖可能貼上減價標籤。"},{"en":"This phrase names common bakery products.","zh":"這個短語指出常見烘焙產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"put a new price label on","meaning":"貼上新的價錢標籤","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte should put a new price label on the packaging.","zh":"Charlotte 應在包裝上貼上新的價錢標籤。"},{"en":"To put a new price label on something means to stick a new label showing the price onto it.","zh":"put a new price label on something 指在某物上貼上顯示價格的新標籤。"},{"en":"A shop assistant may put a new price label on a discounted lunch box.","zh":"店員可能在減價飯盒上貼上新的價錢標籤。"},{"en":"If the label is placed clearly, customers can see the new price before paying.","zh":"如果標籤貼得清楚，顧客付款前就能看到新價格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes updating product price information.","zh":"這個短語描述更新產品價格資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"price label","meaning":"價錢標籤","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte needs to put a yellow price label on some products.","zh":"Charlotte 需要在一些產品上貼黃色價錢標籤。"},{"en":"A price label is a small sticker or tag that shows how much something costs.","zh":"price label 指顯示某物售價的小貼紙或標籤。"},{"en":"A customer checks the price label before deciding whether to buy a cake.","zh":"顧客決定是否買蛋糕前會查看價錢標籤。"},{"en":"If the price label is wrong, customers may be charged the wrong amount.","zh":"如果價錢標籤錯誤，顧客可能被收取錯誤金額。"},{"en":"This phrase names the label that shows price information.","zh":"這個短語指出顯示價格資料的標籤。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"packaging","meaning":"包裝","examples":[{"en":"The new price label should be put on the packaging.","zh":"新價錢標籤應貼在包裝上。"},{"en":"Packaging is the material around a product, such as a box, bag, wrapper, or container.","zh":"packaging 指包住產品的材料，例如盒、袋、包裝紙或容器。"},{"en":"A sandwich may have clear packaging so customers can see what is inside.","zh":"三文治可能有透明包裝，讓顧客看到裡面有甚麼。"},{"en":"If packaging is damaged, the product may look unattractive or unsafe.","zh":"如果包裝損壞，產品可能看起來不吸引或不安全。"},{"en":"This word refers to the covering used to protect or present goods.","zh":"這個字指用來保護或展示貨品的外層。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"yesterday’s dates","meaning":"昨天的日期","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte asks what to do with labels showing yesterday’s dates.","zh":"Charlotte 問標籤上顯示昨天的日期時該怎樣做。"},{"en":"Yesterday’s dates means dates from the day before today.","zh":"yesterday’s dates 指今天前一天的日期。"},{"en":"A notice with yesterday’s date may no longer be useful if it announced a one-day event.","zh":"如果通告日期是昨天，而它宣布的是一日活動，就可能已不再有用。"},{"en":"If food labels show yesterday’s dates, staff must check whether the products should be removed.","zh":"如果食物標籤顯示昨天的日期，員工必須檢查產品是否應被移走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dates that may already be past.","zh":"這個短語描述可能已過去的日期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"throw those items away","meaning":"把那些貨品丟掉","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte asks whether she should throw those items away.","zh":"Charlotte 問她是否應把那些貨品丟掉。"},{"en":"To throw those items away means to put those things in the rubbish because they cannot be used or sold.","zh":"throw those items away 指因那些物品不能使用或出售而把它們丟進垃圾。"},{"en":"A shop may throw damaged fruit away if it is unsafe to eat.","zh":"如果水果損壞並不安全食用，店舖可能把它丟掉。"},{"en":"If items are thrown away too early, the shop may waste food and money.","zh":"如果貨品太早被丟掉，店舖可能浪費食物和金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disposal of unwanted goods.","zh":"這個短語描述棄置不需要的貨品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"that should not happen","meaning":"那應該不會發生","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden says that expired labels should not happen.","zh":"Kaeden 說過期標籤應該不會出現。"},{"en":"That should not happen means the situation is not expected or should be prevented.","zh":"that should not happen 指某情況不應出現或應被防止。"},{"en":"A school door should not be left unlocked after closing time.","zh":"學校關門後，門不應該沒上鎖。"},{"en":"If checks are done properly, old price labels should not happen on shelves.","zh":"如果檢查做得妥當，貨架上不應出現舊價錢標籤。"},{"en":"This phrase points out that something is wrong or unlikely.","zh":"這個短語指出某事是錯誤或不太可能的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"check the stock","meaning":"檢查存貨","examples":[{"en":"The supermarket checks the stock every day.","zh":"超級市場每天檢查存貨。"},{"en":"To check the stock means to examine the goods available in a shop or storage area.","zh":"check the stock 指檢查店舖或儲物區現有貨品。"},{"en":"A bookshop checks the stock before ordering more popular textbooks.","zh":"書店訂購更多熱門教科書前會檢查存貨。"},{"en":"If staff check the stock daily, expired or missing items can be noticed quickly.","zh":"如果員工每天檢查存貨，過期或缺貨項目就能很快被發現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes monitoring available goods.","zh":"這個短語描述監察現有貨品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"every day","meaning":"每天","examples":[{"en":"The staff check the stock every day.","zh":"員工每天檢查存貨。"},{"en":"Every day means each day, without skipping days.","zh":"every day 指每日都做，沒有隔天。"},{"en":"Students should read a little English every day to build vocabulary.","zh":"學生應每天讀一點英文，以建立詞彙。"},{"en":"If stock is checked every day, problems are less likely to build up.","zh":"如果每天檢查存貨，問題較不容易累積。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regular daily action.","zh":"這個短語描述每日定期行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"when something needs","meaning":"當某物需要……時","examples":[{"en":"When something needs a new price label, Charlotte should put a yellow one on it.","zh":"當某貨品需要新的價錢標籤時，Charlotte 應貼上黃色標籤。"},{"en":"When something needs something means at the time when that thing requires it.","zh":"when something needs something 指當某物需要某東西的時候。"},{"en":"When a plant needs water, its leaves may begin to droop.","zh":"當植物需要水時，葉子可能開始下垂。"},{"en":"If a product needs a new label, staff should not leave the old information visible.","zh":"如果產品需要新標籤，員工不應讓舊資料仍清晰可見。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the condition for an action.","zh":"這個短語引出行動的條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"next to","meaning":"在……旁邊","examples":[{"en":"The yellow label should be placed next to the original price.","zh":"黃色標籤應貼在原價旁邊。"},{"en":"Next to means beside or immediately close to something.","zh":"next to 指在某物旁邊或非常接近。"},{"en":"A student may sit next to a friend during lunch.","zh":"學生午飯時可能坐在朋友旁邊。"},{"en":"If the discount label is next to the original price, customers can compare them easily.","zh":"如果減價標籤在原價旁邊，顧客可以容易比較。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position.","zh":"這個短語描述位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"original price","meaning":"原價","examples":[{"en":"The new label should be placed next to the original price.","zh":"新標籤應貼在原價旁邊。"},{"en":"The original price is the price before a discount or change.","zh":"original price 指折扣或改價前的價格。"},{"en":"A shop may show the original price beside the sale price during a promotion.","zh":"店舖促銷期間可能在特價旁邊顯示原價。"},{"en":"If customers see the original price, they can understand how much money they save.","zh":"如果顧客看到原價，就能明白自己省下多少錢。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the first price with the new price.","zh":"這個短語把最初價格與新價格作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sushi takeaway counter","meaning":"壽司外賣櫃位","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte will go to the sushi takeaway counter after checking bread and cakes.","zh":"Charlotte 檢查完麵包和蛋糕後，會去壽司外賣櫃位。"},{"en":"A sushi takeaway counter is a place where customers buy sushi to eat elsewhere.","zh":"sushi takeaway counter 指顧客購買壽司後帶走食用的櫃位。"},{"en":"Office workers may visit the sushi takeaway counter for a quick lunch.","zh":"上班族可能到壽司外賣櫃位買快捷午餐。"},{"en":"If takeaway boxes run out, the sushi counter cannot serve customers efficiently.","zh":"如果外賣盒用完，壽司櫃位就不能有效服務顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a counter selling sushi for takeaway.","zh":"這個短語指售賣外賣壽司的櫃位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"prepare boxes of food","meaning":"準備盒裝食物","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte asks whether she will be preparing boxes of food.","zh":"Charlotte 問她是否會準備盒裝食物。"},{"en":"To prepare boxes of food means to put food into containers ready for sale or serving.","zh":"prepare boxes of food 指把食物放入容器中，準備出售或供應。"},{"en":"Staff may prepare boxes of salad before the lunch rush begins.","zh":"員工可能在午飯繁忙時間前準備盒裝沙律。"},{"en":"If boxes of food are prepared early, customers can buy them quickly.","zh":"如果盒裝食物提早準備好，顧客就能快速購買。"},{"en":"This phrase describes packing food for customers.","zh":"這個短語描述為顧客包裝食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for today","meaning":"今天暫時","examples":[{"en":"For today, Charlotte will just help the staff.","zh":"今天暫時，Charlotte 只會協助職員。"},{"en":"For today means only for this day or during today’s work period.","zh":"for today 指只限今天或今天的工作時段。"},{"en":"For today, students will practise speaking instead of writing essays.","zh":"今天暫時，學生會練習口語，而不是寫文章。"},{"en":"If a rule applies only for today, it may change tomorrow or later.","zh":"如果規則只適用於今天，明天或之後可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase limits an instruction to the present day.","zh":"這個短語把指示限制在當天。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"help the staff","meaning":"協助職員","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte will help the staff at the sushi counter.","zh":"Charlotte 會協助壽司櫃位的職員。"},{"en":"To help the staff means to assist the workers with their tasks.","zh":"help the staff 指協助員工完成工作。"},{"en":"A volunteer may help the staff hand out forms at a school event.","zh":"義工可能在學校活動中協助職員派發表格。"},{"en":"If new workers help the staff first, they can learn routines safely before doing harder jobs.","zh":"如果新員工先協助職員，就能在做較難工作前安全學習流程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes supporting employees.","zh":"這個短語描述支援員工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"flat cardboard boxes","meaning":"平放的紙盒","examples":[{"en":"There are flat cardboard boxes at one end of the counter.","zh":"櫃位一端有平放的紙盒。"},{"en":"Flat cardboard boxes are folded or unassembled paper-based boxes that lie flat before use.","zh":"flat cardboard boxes 指使用前平放、摺疊或未組裝的紙質盒子。"},{"en":"A pizza shop may keep flat cardboard boxes near the packing area.","zh":"薄餅店可能把平放紙盒放在包裝區附近。"},{"en":"If flat cardboard boxes are stored neatly, staff can assemble them quickly when needed.","zh":"如果平放紙盒存放整齊，員工需要時就能快速組裝。"},{"en":"This phrase describes packaging before it is opened into box shape.","zh":"這個短語描述打開成盒形之前的包裝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at one end of","meaning":"在……的一端","examples":[{"en":"The flat cardboard boxes are at one end of the counter.","zh":"平放的紙盒在櫃位的一端。"},{"en":"At one end of something means at one side or extreme point of a long object or area.","zh":"at one end of something 指在一個較長物件或區域的一邊或盡頭。"},{"en":"The printer is at one end of the classroom near the teacher’s desk.","zh":"打印機在課室靠近老師桌子的一端。"},{"en":"If supplies are kept at one end of the counter, staff know where to find them.","zh":"如果用品放在櫃位一端，員工就知道去哪裡找。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a specific position.","zh":"這個短語提供具體位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"beneath those","meaning":"在那些下面","examples":[{"en":"The plastic boxes are kept beneath the cardboard boxes.","zh":"膠盒放在那些紙盒下面。"},{"en":"Beneath those means under the things just mentioned.","zh":"beneath those 指在剛才提到的那些東西下面。"},{"en":"The spare notebooks are on the shelf, and the coloured paper is beneath those.","zh":"備用筆記簿在架上，而彩色紙就在那些下面。"},{"en":"If supplies are kept beneath other items, new staff may need to be told where to look.","zh":"如果用品放在其他物件下面，新員工可能需要被告知去哪裡找。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lower position in relation to something already named.","zh":"這個短語描述相對於已提及物件的較低位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"plastic boxes","meaning":"膠盒","examples":[{"en":"The sushi counter uses plastic boxes for takeaway food.","zh":"壽司櫃位使用膠盒盛載外賣食物。"},{"en":"Plastic boxes are containers made of plastic, often used to hold food or small items.","zh":"plastic boxes 指由塑膠製成的容器，常用來盛載食物或小物件。"},{"en":"A supermarket may pack salads and fruit in clear plastic boxes.","zh":"超級市場可能用透明膠盒包裝沙律和水果。"},{"en":"If plastic boxes run out, staff cannot pack takeaway food properly.","zh":"如果膠盒用完，員工就不能妥善包裝外賣食物。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common food container.","zh":"這個短語指出常見食物容器。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"run out of","meaning":"用完","examples":[{"en":"The staff run out of plastic boxes really quickly.","zh":"職員很快用完膠盒。"},{"en":"To run out of something means to use all of it so there is none left.","zh":"run out of something 指把某物全部用完，沒有剩下。"},{"en":"A class may run out of paper during a big art project.","zh":"班上進行大型美術活動時，可能用完紙張。"},{"en":"If a shop runs out of takeaway boxes, customers may have to wait.","zh":"如果店舖用完外賣盒，顧客可能需要等候。"},{"en":"This phrase describes supplies becoming used up.","zh":"這個短語描述用品被耗盡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"really quickly","meaning":"很快","examples":[{"en":"The plastic boxes run out really quickly.","zh":"膠盒很快就用完。"},{"en":"Really quickly means very fast or in a short time.","zh":"really quickly 指非常快或在短時間內。"},{"en":"Tickets for the school concert sold out really quickly.","zh":"學校音樂會門票很快售罄。"},{"en":"If a supply runs out really quickly, staff may need to bring more before it is gone.","zh":"如果用品很快用完，員工可能要在耗盡前多拿一些來。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses speed.","zh":"這個短語強調速度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"bring more from","meaning":"從……多拿一些來","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte should bring more plastic boxes from the storeroom.","zh":"Charlotte 應從儲物室多拿一些膠盒來。"},{"en":"To bring more from a place means to go there and carry additional items back.","zh":"bring more from a place 指到某地方拿更多物品回來。"},{"en":"A waiter may bring more plates from the kitchen during a busy dinner service.","zh":"晚市繁忙時，侍應可能從廚房多拿一些碟來。"},{"en":"If a counter is running out of supplies, someone must bring more from storage.","zh":"如果櫃位用品快用完，就必須有人從儲物處多拿一些來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes restocking from another place.","zh":"這個短語描述從另一地方補充用品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"storeroom","meaning":"儲物室","examples":[{"en":"The plastic boxes are kept in the storeroom.","zh":"膠盒存放在儲物室。"},{"en":"A storeroom is a room where supplies, stock, or equipment are kept.","zh":"storeroom 指存放用品、存貨或設備的房間。"},{"en":"A school storeroom may contain paper, sports equipment, and cleaning tools.","zh":"學校儲物室可能有紙張、運動器材和清潔工具。"},{"en":"If the storeroom is organised, staff can find supplies quickly.","zh":"如果儲物室整理得好，員工就能快速找到用品。"},{"en":"This word refers to a storage area.","zh":"這個字指存放物品的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"only task","meaning":"唯一工作","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte asks whether bringing plastic boxes is her only task on the sushi counter.","zh":"Charlotte 問多拿膠盒是否她在壽司櫃位的唯一工作。"},{"en":"Only task means the one job someone has to do, with no other duties included.","zh":"only task 指某人要做的唯一一項工作，不包括其他職責。"},{"en":"During the event, my only task was to check tickets at the door.","zh":"活動期間，我的唯一工作是在門口查票。"},{"en":"If bringing boxes is not the only task, Charlotte must learn other duties too.","zh":"如果多拿盒子不是唯一工作，Charlotte 也必須學習其他職責。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether there is just one responsibility.","zh":"這個短語詢問是否只有一項責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prepare the dishes","meaning":"準備食物","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte needs to clean the area where the staff prepare the dishes.","zh":"Charlotte 需要清潔職員準備食物的區域。"},{"en":"To prepare the dishes means to make, arrange, or get food ready for serving or sale.","zh":"prepare the dishes 指製作、擺放或準備食物供應或出售。"},{"en":"Restaurant staff prepare the dishes before customers arrive for lunch.","zh":"餐廳員工會在顧客午飯前準備食物。"},{"en":"If the preparation area is dirty, dishes may become unsafe to eat.","zh":"如果準備食物的區域骯髒，食物可能變得不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes getting food ready.","zh":"這個短語描述把食物準備好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cloths","meaning":"抹布","examples":[{"en":"There are cloths by the sink.","zh":"洗手盆旁邊有抹布。"},{"en":"Cloths are pieces of fabric used for wiping, cleaning, or drying surfaces.","zh":"cloths 指用來擦拭、清潔或抹乾表面的布。"},{"en":"A cleaner may use separate cloths for tables and sinks.","zh":"清潔工可能分開使用抹桌子的抹布和抹洗手盆的抹布。"},{"en":"If cloths are dirty, they can spread germs instead of removing them.","zh":"如果抹布骯髒，它們可能傳播細菌，而不是清除細菌。"},{"en":"This word names a basic cleaning item.","zh":"這個字指出基本清潔用品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bottles of spray","meaning":"噴霧瓶","examples":[{"en":"There are bottles of spray by the sink.","zh":"洗手盆旁邊有噴霧瓶。"},{"en":"Bottles of spray are containers that release cleaning liquid in a fine mist.","zh":"bottles of spray 指能以細霧形式噴出清潔液的容器。"},{"en":"Staff may use bottles of spray to clean tables between customers.","zh":"員工可能用噴霧瓶在顧客之間清潔桌面。"},{"en":"If bottles of spray are empty, cleaning will take longer or be less effective.","zh":"如果噴霧瓶空了，清潔會更慢或效果較差。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to spray bottles used for cleaning.","zh":"這個短語指用於清潔的噴瓶。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"by the sink","meaning":"在洗手盆旁邊","examples":[{"en":"The cloths and bottles of spray are by the sink.","zh":"抹布和噴霧瓶在洗手盆旁邊。"},{"en":"By the sink means next to or near the basin used for washing hands, dishes, or equipment.","zh":"by the sink 指在用來洗手、洗碗或洗設備的盆旁邊或附近。"},{"en":"The soap is by the sink so students can wash their hands easily.","zh":"肥皂在洗手盆旁邊，讓學生容易洗手。"},{"en":"If cleaning supplies are by the sink, staff can clean surfaces without searching for them.","zh":"如果清潔用品在洗手盆旁邊，員工就不用到處找也能清潔表面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical nearby location.","zh":"這個短語描述實用的附近位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden asks Charlotte to make sure she cleans the sink too.","zh":"Kaeden 要 Charlotte 確保也清潔洗手盆。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check or do something carefully so that it definitely happens.","zh":"make sure 指仔細檢查或做某事，以確保它一定發生。"},{"en":"Make sure you lock the classroom door before leaving.","zh":"離開前要確保鎖好課室門。"},{"en":"If staff make sure the sink is clean, food preparation becomes safer.","zh":"如果員工確保洗手盆清潔，食物準備會更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strong reminder.","zh":"這個短語給出強烈提醒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"clean that too","meaning":"也清潔那個","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte must clean the sink too.","zh":"Charlotte 也必須清潔洗手盆。"},{"en":"Clean that too means also clean the thing just mentioned.","zh":"clean that too 指也要清潔剛才提到的那樣東西。"},{"en":"After wiping the table, clean the chair too because food may have fallen on it.","zh":"擦完桌子後，也清潔椅子，因為食物可能掉在上面。"},{"en":"If staff clean the counter but not the sink, germs may still remain nearby.","zh":"如果員工只清潔櫃位而不清潔洗手盆，附近仍可能有細菌。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another item to a cleaning task.","zh":"這個短語把另一個項目加入清潔任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"absolutely","meaning":"絕對是","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden says that cleaning the food preparation area is absolutely important.","zh":"Kaeden 說清潔食物準備區絕對重要。"},{"en":"Absolutely means completely or definitely, often used for emphasis.","zh":"absolutely 指完全或肯定，常用來加強語氣。"},{"en":"Wearing a seat belt is absolutely necessary in a car.","zh":"坐車時繫安全帶絕對必要。"},{"en":"If hygiene is absolutely important, staff must follow cleaning rules carefully.","zh":"如果衞生絕對重要，員工就必須仔細遵守清潔規則。"},{"en":"This word makes the statement stronger.","zh":"這個字令陳述更有力度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"wash up knives","meaning":"清洗刀具","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte must not wash up knives.","zh":"Charlotte 不可以清洗刀具。"},{"en":"To wash up knives means to clean knives after they have been used.","zh":"wash up knives 指在刀具使用後清洗它們。"},{"en":"In a kitchen, trained staff wash up knives carefully to avoid cuts.","zh":"在廚房中，受過訓練的員工會小心清洗刀具，以免割傷。"},{"en":"If an untrained worker washes up knives, they may hurt themselves.","zh":"如果未受訓員工清洗刀具，可能弄傷自己。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cleaning sharp kitchen tools.","zh":"這個短語描述清潔尖銳廚具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"do some training","meaning":"接受一些訓練","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte has to do some training before touching sharp objects.","zh":"Charlotte 在接觸尖銳物件前必須接受一些訓練。"},{"en":"To do some training means to receive instruction and practise how to do a task safely or correctly.","zh":"do some training 指接受指導並練習如何安全或正確完成任務。"},{"en":"New lifeguards do training before they work at the swimming pool.","zh":"新救生員在泳池工作前會接受訓練。"},{"en":"If staff do training before using equipment, accidents are less likely.","zh":"如果員工在使用設備前接受訓練，意外就較不容易發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning before doing a job.","zh":"這個短語描述工作前的學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be allowed to","meaning":"被允許","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte is not allowed to touch sharp objects before training.","zh":"Charlotte 在接受訓練前不被允許接觸尖銳物件。"},{"en":"To be allowed to do something means to have permission to do it.","zh":"be allowed to do something 指有許可做某事。"},{"en":"Students are allowed to use the library computers after they log in.","zh":"學生登入後被允許使用圖書館電腦。"},{"en":"If workers are not allowed to use equipment, they should ask trained staff for help.","zh":"如果員工不被允許使用設備，就應請受訓員工幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes permission.","zh":"這個短語描述許可。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"touch sharp objects","meaning":"接觸尖銳物件","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte needs training before she can touch sharp objects.","zh":"Charlotte 需要訓練後才可以接觸尖銳物件。"},{"en":"To touch sharp objects means to handle items that can cut or injure you.","zh":"touch sharp objects 指處理可能割傷或傷害你的物品。"},{"en":"Children should not touch sharp objects such as knives or broken glass.","zh":"孩子不應接觸刀具或破玻璃等尖銳物件。"},{"en":"If staff touch sharp objects without training, injuries can happen quickly.","zh":"如果員工未經訓練就接觸尖銳物件，意外可能很快發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes handling dangerous pointed or cutting items.","zh":"這個短語描述處理危險的尖銳或切割物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sharp objects","meaning":"尖銳物件","examples":[{"en":"Knives are sharp objects that Charlotte must not handle yet.","zh":"刀具是 Charlotte 暫時不可處理的尖銳物件。"},{"en":"Sharp objects are items with edges or points that can cut or pierce skin.","zh":"sharp objects 指有邊緣或尖端、可割傷或刺穿皮膚的物品。"},{"en":"Scissors, needles, and broken glass are sharp objects.","zh":"剪刀、針和破玻璃都是尖銳物件。"},{"en":"If sharp objects are left carelessly on a counter, someone may get hurt.","zh":"如果尖銳物件隨便放在櫃面上，可能有人受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase names objects that require careful handling.","zh":"這個短語指出需要小心處理的物件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ask someone to","meaning":"請某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte should ask someone to put knives in the dishwasher.","zh":"Charlotte 應請某人把刀具放進洗碗碟機。"},{"en":"To ask someone to do something means to request that person to do it.","zh":"ask someone to do something 指請求某人做某事。"},{"en":"A student may ask a classmate to explain the homework instructions.","zh":"學生可能請同學解釋功課指示。"},{"en":"If a task is unsafe for you, you should ask someone trained to do it.","zh":"如果某工作對你不安全，你應請受過訓練的人去做。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a request.","zh":"這個短語描述提出請求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dishwasher","meaning":"洗碗碟機","examples":[{"en":"Knives should be put in the dishwasher by trained staff.","zh":"刀具應由受訓員工放進洗碗碟機。"},{"en":"A dishwasher is a machine that washes plates, cups, cutlery, and kitchen tools.","zh":"dishwasher 指清洗碟、杯、餐具和廚房工具的機器。"},{"en":"Restaurant staff load the dishwasher after customers finish eating.","zh":"餐廳員工在顧客用餐後會把餐具放入洗碗碟機。"},{"en":"If sharp knives are placed in the dishwasher incorrectly, someone may be injured.","zh":"如果尖刀放進洗碗碟機的位置不正確，可能有人受傷。"},{"en":"This word names a kitchen cleaning machine.","zh":"這個字指出廚房清潔機器。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get anything wrong","meaning":"做錯任何事","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte does not want to get anything wrong.","zh":"Charlotte 不想做錯任何事。"},{"en":"To get anything wrong means to make any mistake in what you do or say.","zh":"get anything wrong 指在做事或說話時犯任何錯誤。"},{"en":"A student may check the exam number twice because she does not want to get anything wrong.","zh":"學生可能檢查考生編號兩次，因為她不想做錯任何事。"},{"en":"If a new worker worries about getting things wrong, clear instructions can help.","zh":"如果新員工擔心做錯事，清楚指示可以幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase shows concern about making mistakes.","zh":"這個短語顯示對犯錯的擔心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"you will be fine","meaning":"你會沒事；你會應付到","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden tells Charlotte that she will be fine.","zh":"Kaeden 告訴 Charlotte 她會應付到。"},{"en":"You will be fine means you will manage the situation successfully and should not worry too much.","zh":"you will be fine 指你會成功處理情況，不需要太擔心。"},{"en":"A teacher may tell a nervous student, “You will be fine,” before a short speech.","zh":"老師可能在學生短講前對緊張的學生說：「你會沒事的。」"},{"en":"If someone receives guidance and support, they are more likely to be fine in a new job.","zh":"如果某人得到指導和支援，在新工作中就較可能應付到。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to reassure someone.","zh":"這個短語用來安慰某人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be around to help","meaning":"在附近幫忙","examples":[{"en":"Kaeden will be around to help Charlotte.","zh":"Kaeden 會在附近幫 Charlotte。"},{"en":"To be around to help means to be nearby and available if someone needs assistance.","zh":"be around to help 指在附近並可在某人需要時提供協助。"},{"en":"During a school fair, teachers are around to help students at the stalls.","zh":"學校嘉年華期間，老師會在附近幫忙學生照顧攤位。"},{"en":"If a supervisor is around to help, new workers can ask questions immediately.","zh":"如果主管在附近幫忙，新員工就能立即提問。"},{"en":"This phrase describes nearby support.","zh":"這個短語描述附近支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"finally","meaning":"最後","examples":[{"en":"Finally, Kaeden explains the tasks at the meat and fish counters.","zh":"最後，Kaeden 解釋肉類及魚類櫃位的工作。"},{"en":"Finally means at the last point in a sequence or after earlier steps.","zh":"finally 指在一連串事情中的最後一點，或較早步驟之後。"},{"en":"First we cleaned the desks, then we moved the chairs, and finally we locked the classroom.","zh":"我們先清潔書桌，然後搬椅子，最後鎖好課室。"},{"en":"If someone says finally, listeners know the last part is coming.","zh":"如果某人說 finally，聽者就知道最後部分即將出現。"},{"en":"This word helps organise instructions or stories.","zh":"這個字幫助組織指示或故事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"serve customers","meaning":"服務顧客","examples":[{"en":"Staff serve customers at the meat and fish counters.","zh":"員工在肉類及魚類櫃位服務顧客。"},{"en":"To serve customers means to help customers buy goods, answer questions, or provide a service.","zh":"serve customers 指幫助顧客購買貨品、回答問題或提供服務。"},{"en":"A café worker serves customers by taking orders and bringing drinks.","zh":"咖啡店員工透過接單和送飲品來服務顧客。"},{"en":"If staff serve customers politely, shoppers are more likely to return.","zh":"如果員工有禮地服務顧客，顧客較可能再次光顧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct customer service work.","zh":"這個短語描述直接顧客服務工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"including","meaning":"包括","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte has to clean the area, including the weighing scales.","zh":"Charlotte 必須清潔該區域，包括電子磅。"},{"en":"Including introduces something that is part of a larger group or task.","zh":"including 用來引出較大群體或任務中的其中一部分。"},{"en":"Students must bring stationery, including a pen, pencil, and ruler.","zh":"學生必須帶文具，包括原子筆、鉛筆和間尺。"},{"en":"If instructions say including the scales, staff must not forget that item.","zh":"如果指示說包括磅秤，員工就不可忘記該物件。"},{"en":"This word shows that an item is part of the list.","zh":"這個字表示某項目是清單的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"wipe the weighing scales","meaning":"擦拭電子磅","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte needs to wipe the weighing scales.","zh":"Charlotte 需要擦拭電子磅。"},{"en":"To wipe the weighing scales means to clean the scales by rubbing them with a cloth.","zh":"wipe the weighing scales 指用布擦拭磅秤以清潔它們。"},{"en":"Staff should wipe the weighing scales after weighing raw fish.","zh":"員工在稱量生魚後應擦拭電子磅。"},{"en":"If the weighing scales are not wiped, food residue may remain on the surface.","zh":"如果電子磅沒有被擦拭，食物殘留可能留在表面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a hygiene task.","zh":"這個短語描述衞生工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"weighing scales","meaning":"電子磅；磅秤","examples":[{"en":"The weighing scales must be cleaned at the meat and fish counters.","zh":"肉類及魚類櫃位的電子磅必須被清潔。"},{"en":"Weighing scales are devices used to measure how heavy something is.","zh":"weighing scales 指用來量度物件重量的設備。"},{"en":"A market stall uses weighing scales to price fruit by weight.","zh":"街市攤檔使用磅秤按重量為水果定價。"},{"en":"If weighing scales are dirty or inaccurate, customers may lose trust.","zh":"如果電子磅骯髒或不準確，顧客可能失去信任。"},{"en":"This phrase names equipment used for measuring weight.","zh":"這個短語指出量度重量的設備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be laid on ice","meaning":"放在冰上","examples":[{"en":"The fish is laid on ice at the counter.","zh":"魚在櫃位上被放在冰上。"},{"en":"To be laid on ice means to be placed on ice to keep it cold and fresh.","zh":"be laid on ice 指被放在冰上，以保持低溫和新鮮。"},{"en":"Seafood in a market is often laid on ice during the day.","zh":"街市海鮮白天常被放在冰上。"},{"en":"If fish is not laid on ice, it may spoil faster.","zh":"如果魚沒有放在冰上，可能更快變壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a way to keep food cold.","zh":"這個短語描述保持食物低溫的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"start to melt","meaning":"開始融化","examples":[{"en":"When the ice starts to melt, Charlotte needs to get more.","zh":"當冰開始融化時，Charlotte 需要拿更多冰。"},{"en":"To start to melt means to begin changing from solid into liquid because of heat.","zh":"start to melt 指因熱力而開始由固體變成液體。"},{"en":"Ice cream starts to melt if it is left outside the freezer.","zh":"雪糕如果離開冰箱，就會開始融化。"},{"en":"If the ice starts to melt around fish, staff need to replace it to keep the food cold.","zh":"如果魚旁邊的冰開始融化，員工需要更換冰以保持食物低溫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of melting.","zh":"這個短語描述融化的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cold-room","meaning":"冷藏室","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte needs to get more ice from the cold-room.","zh":"Charlotte 需要從冷藏室拿更多冰。"},{"en":"A cold-room is a refrigerated storage room used to keep food or supplies very cold.","zh":"cold-room 指用來把食物或用品保持低溫的冷藏儲物室。"},{"en":"Restaurants keep meat, fish, and dairy products in a cold-room.","zh":"餐廳把肉、魚和奶製品存放在冷藏室。"},{"en":"If staff enter a cold-room without proper gloves, they may be hurt by the low temperature.","zh":"如果員工沒有合適手套就進入冷藏室，可能因低溫受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase names a very cold storage area.","zh":"這個短語指出非常寒冷的儲物區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"food counters","meaning":"食品櫃位","examples":[{"en":"The staff on the food counters wear hats.","zh":"食品櫃位的員工會戴帽。"},{"en":"Food counters are service areas where food is displayed, prepared, or sold.","zh":"food counters 指展示、準備或售賣食物的服務區域。"},{"en":"A supermarket may have food counters for sushi, meat, fish, and cheese.","zh":"超級市場可能有壽司、肉類、魚類和芝士食品櫃位。"},{"en":"If staff work on food counters, hygiene rules are especially important.","zh":"如果員工在食品櫃位工作，衞生規則尤其重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to customer-facing food areas.","zh":"這個短語指面向顧客的食品區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"wear a hat","meaning":"戴帽","examples":[{"en":"Staff on the food counters wear a hat.","zh":"食品櫃位的員工會戴帽。"},{"en":"To wear a hat means to put a hat on your head as part of clothing or safety rules.","zh":"wear a hat 指把帽戴在頭上，作為服裝或安全規則的一部分。"},{"en":"Kitchen staff wear hats to keep hair away from food.","zh":"廚房員工戴帽，以免頭髮掉進食物。"},{"en":"If workers wear a hat at food counters, customers may trust the hygiene standard more.","zh":"如果食品櫃位員工戴帽，顧客可能更信任衞生標準。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wearing head covering.","zh":"這個短語描述佩戴頭部覆蓋物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be the same for me","meaning":"我也一樣嗎？","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte asks whether the hat rule will be the same for her.","zh":"Charlotte 問戴帽規則是否對她也一樣。"},{"en":"Be the same for me means apply to me in the same way as it applies to others.","zh":"be the same for me 指像適用於其他人一樣適用於我。"},{"en":"A new student may ask whether the homework rule is the same for her.","zh":"新學生可能問功課規則是否對她也一樣。"},{"en":"If a rule is the same for everyone, staff know what is expected.","zh":"如果規則對每個人都一樣，員工就知道期望是甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether a rule also applies to the speaker.","zh":"這個短語詢問某規則是否也適用於說話者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"serve customers directly","meaning":"直接服務顧客","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte will not be serving customers directly.","zh":"Charlotte 不會直接服務顧客。"},{"en":"To serve customers directly means to deal with customers face to face and help them buy things.","zh":"serve customers directly 指面對面處理顧客需要並協助他們購物。"},{"en":"A cashier serves customers directly by scanning goods and taking payment.","zh":"收銀員透過掃描貨品和收款直接服務顧客。"},{"en":"If a trainee is not serving customers directly, she can learn behind-the-scenes tasks first.","zh":"如果實習員工不直接服務顧客，她可以先學習幕後工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frontline customer service.","zh":"這個短語描述前線顧客服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make sure you put on","meaning":"確保戴上","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte must make sure she puts on thermal gloves.","zh":"Charlotte 必須確保戴上保暖手套。"},{"en":"Make sure you put on something means remember to wear it before doing the task.","zh":"make sure you put on something 指做任務前記得穿戴某物。"},{"en":"Make sure you put on a helmet before riding a bike.","zh":"騎單車前，確保戴上頭盔。"},{"en":"If workers make sure they put on safety gear, injuries are less likely.","zh":"如果員工確保戴上安全裝備，受傷機會會較低。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an important safety reminder.","zh":"這個短語給出重要安全提醒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"thermal gloves","meaning":"保暖手套","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte must wear thermal gloves in the cold-room.","zh":"Charlotte 在冷藏室必須戴保暖手套。"},{"en":"Thermal gloves are warm protective gloves designed to protect hands from very cold temperatures.","zh":"thermal gloves 指保暖保護手套，用來保護雙手免受極低溫傷害。"},{"en":"Workers in a freezer warehouse wear thermal gloves when moving frozen food.","zh":"冷凍倉庫工人搬冷凍食品時會戴保暖手套。"},{"en":"If someone touches very cold items without thermal gloves, their skin may be injured.","zh":"如果某人沒有戴保暖手套就觸碰極冷物件，皮膚可能受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase names protective cold-weather handwear.","zh":"這個短語指出防寒保護手套。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take anything out of","meaning":"從……拿出任何東西","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte must wear thermal gloves when taking anything out of the cold-room.","zh":"Charlotte 從冷藏室拿出任何東西時，都必須戴保暖手套。"},{"en":"To take anything out of a place means to remove any item from that place.","zh":"take anything out of a place 指從某地方移走任何物品。"},{"en":"Students should ask before taking anything out of the science cupboard.","zh":"學生從科學櫃拿出任何東西前應先詢問。"},{"en":"If workers take frozen items out of a cold-room, they need protection from the cold.","zh":"如果員工從冷藏室拿出冷凍物品，就需要防寒保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes removing items from a storage place.","zh":"這個短語描述從儲物地方取出物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"low enough to","meaning":"低得足以……","examples":[{"en":"The temperature is low enough to cause frostbite.","zh":"溫度低得足以造成凍傷。"},{"en":"Low enough to do something means sufficiently low to produce a particular result.","zh":"low enough to do something 指低到足以產生某個結果。"},{"en":"The shelf is low enough for young children to reach the books safely.","zh":"書架低得足以讓幼童安全拿到書。"},{"en":"If a temperature is low enough to injure skin, workers must use protective equipment.","zh":"如果溫度低得足以傷害皮膚，員工必須使用保護裝備。"},{"en":"This phrase links degree with result.","zh":"這個短語把程度與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get frostbite","meaning":"凍傷","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte could get frostbite from touching things in the cold-room.","zh":"Charlotte 在冷藏室觸碰物件可能會凍傷。"},{"en":"To get frostbite means to have skin or body tissue damaged by extreme cold.","zh":"get frostbite 指皮膚或身體組織因極冷而受損。"},{"en":"Hikers can get frostbite if they walk in snow without warm gloves.","zh":"遠足者如果在雪地中沒有戴暖手套行走，可能會凍傷。"},{"en":"If staff touch frozen metal for too long, they may get frostbite.","zh":"如果員工觸碰冷凍金屬太久，可能會凍傷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cold-related injury.","zh":"這個短語描述與寒冷有關的傷害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"from touching things","meaning":"因觸碰物件而","examples":[{"en":"The cold-room is cold enough to cause frostbite from touching things.","zh":"冷藏室冷得足以因觸碰物件而造成凍傷。"},{"en":"From touching things means as a result of putting your hands on objects or surfaces.","zh":"from touching things 指因用手接觸物件或表面而產生某結果。"},{"en":"A child may get paint on his fingers from touching things in the art room.","zh":"孩子可能因觸碰美術室物件而手指沾上顏料。"},{"en":"If objects are extremely cold, injury can happen from touching them without gloves.","zh":"如果物件極冷，沒有戴手套觸碰就可能受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the action that causes the result.","zh":"這個短語解釋導致結果的動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"understood","meaning":"明白","examples":[{"en":"Charlotte says “Understood” after hearing the safety instruction.","zh":"Charlotte 聽完安全指示後說：「明白。」"},{"en":"Understood means I have heard, understood, and will follow the instruction.","zh":"understood 指我已聽到、明白，並會遵守指示。"},{"en":"A worker may say “Understood” after a supervisor explains a new safety rule.","zh":"主管解釋新的安全規則後，員工可能說：「明白。」"},{"en":"If someone says understood, the speaker knows the message has been received clearly.","zh":"如果某人說 understood，說話者就知道訊息已被清楚接收。"},{"en":"This word is a short formal way to show comprehension and agreement.","zh":"這個字是表示理解和同意的簡短正式說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 8/task-2":[{"front":"running coach","meaning":"跑步教練","examples":[{"en":"Liz Fuller is a running coach with Compton Park Runners Club.","zh":"Liz Fuller 是 Compton Park Runners Club 的跑步教練。"},{"en":"A running coach is a person who trains runners and gives advice on technique, fitness and training plans.","zh":"跑步教練是訓練跑手並就技巧、體能和訓練計劃提供建議的人。"},{"en":"A school may invite a running coach to help students prepare for a charity race.","zh":"學校可能邀請跑步教練幫助學生準備慈善跑。"},{"en":"A good running coach can prevent injuries by teaching beginners how to build up slowly.","zh":"好的跑步教練可以透過教新手如何逐步提升來預防受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to someone who guides running practice, not just someone who enjoys running.","zh":"這個短語指指導跑步訓練的人，而不只是喜歡跑步的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"take up running","meaning":"開始跑步","examples":[{"en":"Liz helps people who are thinking about taking up running.","zh":"Liz 幫助正在考慮開始跑步的人。"},{"en":"To take up running means to start running as a new activity or hobby.","zh":"開始跑步意思是把跑步作為新的活動或興趣。"},{"en":"A busy office worker may take up running to improve fitness after work.","zh":"忙碌的辦公室員工可能下班後開始跑步以改善體能。"},{"en":"People often take up running slowly so their bodies have time to adapt.","zh":"人們通常會慢慢開始跑步，讓身體有時間適應。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when someone begins an activity they did not do regularly before.","zh":"當某人開始一項以前沒有定期做的活動時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be here to help","meaning":"在這裏提供幫助","examples":[{"en":"If you are thinking about taking up running, Liz is here to help.","zh":"如果你正在考慮開始跑步，Liz 在這裏提供幫助。"},{"en":"To be here to help means to be available and ready to give support or advice.","zh":"在這裏提供幫助意思是可以並準備好提供支援或建議。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “I am here to help,” when students feel worried about exams.","zh":"當學生擔心考試時，老師可能會說：「我在這裏提供幫助。」"},{"en":"Knowing someone is here to help can make beginners feel less nervous.","zh":"知道有人在這裏提供幫助，可以令新手較不緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds friendly and reassuring.","zh":"這個短語聽起來友善而令人安心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"training programmes","meaning":"訓練計劃","examples":[{"en":"There are many training programmes available online.","zh":"網上有很多訓練計劃。"},{"en":"Training programmes are planned sets of exercises or lessons designed to improve ability over time.","zh":"訓練計劃是有計劃的一套練習或課程，旨在隨時間提升能力。"},{"en":"A beginner runner may follow a training programme that starts with short runs and rest days.","zh":"跑步新手可能跟從由短跑和休息日開始的訓練計劃。"},{"en":"Good training programmes reduce confusion because people know what to do each week.","zh":"良好訓練計劃可以減少混亂，因為人們知道每星期要做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in sport, work, education and health contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於運動、工作、教育和健康語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"available online","meaning":"網上有提供","examples":[{"en":"Many running programmes are available online.","zh":"很多跑步計劃網上有提供。"},{"en":"Available online means people can find or use something on the internet.","zh":"網上有提供意思是人們可以在互聯網上找到或使用某物。"},{"en":"School forms are available online, so parents do not need to collect paper copies.","zh":"學校表格網上有提供，所以家長不用領取紙本。"},{"en":"When advice is available online, more people can access it quickly.","zh":"當建議網上有提供，更多人可以快速取得。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information, services or products that can be reached through the internet.","zh":"這個短語描述可透過互聯網取得的資訊、服務或產品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"aim to","meaning":"旨在；目的是","examples":[{"en":"The programmes aim to help people build up to running five kilometres.","zh":"這些計劃旨在幫助人們逐步達到跑五公里。"},{"en":"To aim to do something means to have that purpose or goal.","zh":"旨在做某事意思是有該目的或目標。"},{"en":"A school campaign may aim to reduce plastic waste by encouraging reusable bottles.","zh":"學校活動可能旨在透過鼓勵使用可重用水樽來減少塑膠廢物。"},{"en":"Clear aims help people understand why an activity is being done.","zh":"清楚目標有助人們明白為何要進行某活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the purpose of a plan, course or project.","zh":"當解釋計劃、課程或項目的目的時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"build up to","meaning":"逐步達到……","examples":[{"en":"The programmes help people build up to running five kilometres.","zh":"這些計劃幫助人們逐步達到跑五公里。"},{"en":"To build up to something means to improve gradually until you can do it.","zh":"逐步達到某事意思是逐漸進步直到能做到。"},{"en":"A student may build up to reading a full English novel by starting with short stories.","zh":"學生可以先讀短篇故事，再逐步達到閱讀整本英文小說。"},{"en":"Building up slowly helps prevent frustration and injury.","zh":"慢慢逐步提升有助防止挫折和受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests steady progress rather than sudden achievement.","zh":"這個短語暗示穩定進展，而不是突然達成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"five kilometres","meaning":"五公里","examples":[{"en":"Many beginners train until they can run five kilometres.","zh":"許多新手訓練直到能跑五公里。"},{"en":"Five kilometres is a distance equal to 5,000 metres.","zh":"五公里是等於 5,000 米的距離。"},{"en":"A five-kilometre run is short enough for beginners but still gives them a clear challenge.","zh":"五公里跑對新手來說距離不算太長，但仍提供清楚挑戰。"},{"en":"Training for five kilometres can help new runners build confidence and stamina.","zh":"為五公里訓練可以幫助跑步新手建立信心和耐力。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for beginner-friendly running events.","zh":"這個短語常用於適合新手的跑步活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"thousands of people","meaning":"數以千計的人","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of people of all ages take part in five-kilometre races.","zh":"數以千計各個年齡層的人參加五公里賽。"},{"en":"Thousands of people means a very large number of people.","zh":"數以千計的人意思是非常大量的人。"},{"en":"Thousands of people may join a city fun run to raise money for charity.","zh":"數以千計的人可能參加城市慈善歡樂跑以籌款。"},{"en":"When thousands of people take part, an event can feel exciting and supportive.","zh":"當數以千計的人參與，活動可以感覺熱鬧而有支持感。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises large participation.","zh":"這個短語強調大量參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"of all ages","meaning":"各個年齡層的","examples":[{"en":"People of all ages take part in five-kilometre races.","zh":"各個年齡層的人都參加五公里賽。"},{"en":"Of all ages means including children, adults and older people.","zh":"各個年齡層的意思是包括兒童、成年人和長者。"},{"en":"A community festival can welcome visitors of all ages with games, music and food.","zh":"社區節日可以透過遊戲、音樂和食物歡迎各個年齡層的訪客。"},{"en":"Activities for people of all ages help families join together.","zh":"適合各個年齡層的活動有助家庭一起參與。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is not limited to one age group.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事不限於某個年齡群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"take part in","meaning":"參加","examples":[{"en":"Many runners take part in five-kilometre races.","zh":"許多跑手參加五公里賽。"},{"en":"To take part in something means to join an activity or event.","zh":"參加某事意思是加入一項活動或事件。"},{"en":"Students can take part in a school clean-up by collecting litter after class.","zh":"學生可以放學後撿垃圾，參加學校清潔活動。"},{"en":"Taking part in group activities helps people feel involved and motivated.","zh":"參加集體活動有助人們感到投入和有動力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on participation.","zh":"這個短語重點是參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"across the country","meaning":"全國各地","examples":[{"en":"People are taking part in races across the country.","zh":"人們正在全國各地參加比賽。"},{"en":"Across the country means in many places throughout a nation.","zh":"全國各地意思是在一個國家的許多地方。"},{"en":"Schools across the country may join the same reading campaign.","zh":"全國各地的學校可能參與同一閱讀活動。"},{"en":"When an activity spreads across the country, many communities can take part.","zh":"當活動傳遍全國各地，許多社區都可以參與。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wide national reach.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛的全國範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"More people are entering five-kilometre races as a result.","zh":"因此，更多人報名參加五公里賽。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what has just happened or been mentioned.","zh":"因此意思是因為剛才發生或提及的事情。"},{"en":"The school added more sports clubs; as a result, more students exercised after class.","zh":"學校增設更多運動學會；因此，更多學生放學後做運動。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with its consequence.","zh":"這個短語把原因與後果連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful in explanations, reports and essays.","zh":"它適合用於解釋、報告和文章。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"easy to follow","meaning":"容易遵循","examples":[{"en":"People like the programmes because they are easy to follow.","zh":"人們喜歡這些計劃，因為它們容易遵循。"},{"en":"Easy to follow means simple to understand and do step by step.","zh":"容易遵循意思是容易理解並一步一步去做。"},{"en":"A recipe is easy to follow if it uses clear instructions and common ingredients.","zh":"如果食譜使用清楚指示和常見材料，它就容易遵循。"},{"en":"Beginners are more likely to continue when a plan is easy to follow.","zh":"當計劃容易遵循，新手更可能繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes instructions, plans or explanations that are clear.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚的指示、計劃或解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"push someone too hard","meaning":"把某人逼得太緊","examples":[{"en":"The programmes do not push beginners too hard.","zh":"這些計劃不會把新手逼得太緊。"},{"en":"To push someone too hard means to demand more effort than they are ready for.","zh":"把某人逼得太緊意思是要求他們付出超出準備程度的努力。"},{"en":"A teacher should not push new students too hard before they understand the basics.","zh":"老師不應在新學生明白基礎前把他們逼得太緊。"},{"en":"Pushing beginners too hard can cause stress, injury or loss of motivation.","zh":"把新手逼得太緊可能造成壓力、受傷或失去動力。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against excessive pressure.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要施加過度壓力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"work for everyone","meaning":"適合所有人","examples":[{"en":"Online training programmes do not work for everyone.","zh":"網上訓練計劃並不適合所有人。"},{"en":"If something works for everyone, it suits all people and their needs.","zh":"如果某事適合所有人，意思是它符合所有人的需要。"},{"en":"One study method may help some students, but it does not work for everyone.","zh":"一種學習方法可能幫到一些學生，但不適合所有人。"},{"en":"Programmes fail to work for everyone because people have different bodies, schedules and goals.","zh":"計劃未必適合所有人，因為人們有不同身體、日程和目標。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining limits or exceptions.","zh":"當解釋限制或例外時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"suffer from","meaning":"患有……","examples":[{"en":"Some people suffer from a heart condition or asthma.","zh":"有些人患有心臟問題或哮喘。"},{"en":"To suffer from an illness or condition means to have it and be affected by it.","zh":"患有疾病或情況意思是有該問題並受其影響。"},{"en":"A student who suffers from migraines may need rest in a quiet room.","zh":"患有偏頭痛的學生可能需要在安靜房間休息。"},{"en":"People who suffer from health problems may need specialist advice before exercising.","zh":"患有健康問題的人在運動前可能需要專業建議。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing medical conditions.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論醫療狀況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"heart condition","meaning":"心臟問題","examples":[{"en":"A heart condition may make general running programmes unsuitable.","zh":"心臟問題可能令一般跑步計劃不合適。"},{"en":"A heart condition is a medical problem that affects how the heart works.","zh":"心臟問題是影響心臟如何運作的醫療問題。"},{"en":"Someone with a heart condition should ask a doctor before starting intense exercise.","zh":"有心臟問題的人在開始劇烈運動前應詢問醫生。"},{"en":"A heart condition can make training riskier if the plan is too demanding.","zh":"如果訓練計劃要求太高，心臟問題可能令訓練風險更大。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to health problems related to the heart.","zh":"這個短語指與心臟有關的健康問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"asthma","meaning":"哮喘","examples":[{"en":"People with asthma may need more specific running advice.","zh":"有哮喘的人可能需要更具體的跑步建議。"},{"en":"Asthma is a condition that can make breathing difficult, especially during exercise or illness.","zh":"哮喘是一種可令呼吸困難的狀況，尤其是在運動或生病期間。"},{"en":"A runner with asthma may carry an inhaler during training.","zh":"有哮喘的跑手訓練時可能攜帶吸入器。"},{"en":"Cold air, dust or hard exercise can sometimes trigger asthma symptoms.","zh":"冷空氣、塵埃或劇烈運動有時會引發哮喘症狀。"},{"en":"This word names a breathing condition that needs care during sport.","zh":"這個詞指一種在運動時需要小心處理的呼吸狀況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be aimed at","meaning":"針對……","examples":[{"en":"Most online programmes are aimed at people with average fitness.","zh":"大多數網上計劃是針對一般體能的人。"},{"en":"To be aimed at a group means to be designed for that group.","zh":"針對某群體意思是為該群體而設計。"},{"en":"A beginner grammar course is aimed at students who need basic sentence practice.","zh":"初級文法課程是針對需要基本句子練習的學生。"},{"en":"If a programme is aimed at the wrong audience, users may find it too hard or too easy.","zh":"如果計劃針對錯誤對象，使用者可能覺得太難或太易。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the intended users of a plan, product or activity.","zh":"這個短語解釋計劃、產品或活動的目標使用者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"average fitness","meaning":"一般體能","examples":[{"en":"The programmes are aimed at people with average fitness.","zh":"這些計劃是針對一般體能的人。"},{"en":"Average fitness means a normal level of physical ability, neither very fit nor very unfit.","zh":"一般體能意思是普通的身體能力水平，既不是非常健壯，也不是非常缺乏體能。"},{"en":"A person with average fitness may walk comfortably but struggle with long runs.","zh":"有一般體能的人可能能舒服地步行，但長跑會吃力。"},{"en":"Programmes for average fitness may not suit people with medical conditions or advanced athletes.","zh":"針對一般體能的計劃未必適合有醫療狀況的人或進階運動員。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a middle level of physical condition.","zh":"這個短語描述中等身體狀況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"running ability","meaning":"跑步能力","examples":[{"en":"The programmes are designed for people with average running ability.","zh":"這些計劃是為一般跑步能力的人設計的。"},{"en":"Running ability means how well someone can run, including speed, stamina and control.","zh":"跑步能力意思是某人跑步的能力，包括速度、耐力和控制。"},{"en":"A beginner’s running ability may improve after several weeks of regular training.","zh":"新手經過幾星期定期訓練後，跑步能力可能會提升。"},{"en":"Matching training to running ability helps people improve without injury.","zh":"把訓練配合跑步能力有助人們進步而不受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on skill and fitness specifically related to running.","zh":"這個短語重點是與跑步特別相關的技巧和體能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"specific questions","meaning":"具體問題","examples":[{"en":"Some beginners have specific questions related to their needs.","zh":"有些新手有與自己需要相關的具體問題。"},{"en":"Specific questions are detailed questions about a particular situation or problem.","zh":"具體問題是關於特定情況或問題的詳細提問。"},{"en":"A new runner may ask specific questions about knee pain, shoes or breathing.","zh":"跑步新手可能提出關於膝痛、跑鞋或呼吸的具體問題。"},{"en":"Specific questions often need personal advice rather than general information.","zh":"具體問題通常需要個人化建議，而不是一般資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts detailed concerns with broad questions.","zh":"這個短語把詳細關注與廣泛問題作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"related to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Some questions are related to a runner’s personal needs.","zh":"有些問題與跑手的個人需要有關。"},{"en":"Related to something means connected with it.","zh":"與某事有關意思是與它有聯繫。"},{"en":"A student’s poor sleep may be related to heavy homework and late phone use.","zh":"學生睡眠差可能與功課繁重和晚上使用手機有關。"},{"en":"When advice is related to someone’s needs, it is more useful and practical.","zh":"當建議與某人的需要有關，它會更有用和實際。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to show connection between two things.","zh":"這個短語用來顯示兩件事之間的聯繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"provide answers","meaning":"提供答案","examples":[{"en":"Online programmes may not provide answers to specific questions.","zh":"網上計劃未必能為具體問題提供答案。"},{"en":"To provide answers means to give information that solves questions or problems.","zh":"提供答案意思是給出能解決問題或疑問的資訊。"},{"en":"A teacher can provide answers after students try the exercise themselves.","zh":"老師可以在學生自己嘗試練習後提供答案。"},{"en":"General websites may not provide answers for unusual personal situations.","zh":"一般網站未必能為不尋常的個人情況提供答案。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on giving useful explanations or solutions.","zh":"這個短語重點是給出有用解釋或方案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a couple of","meaning":"幾個；兩三個","examples":[{"en":"Liz has a couple of simple tips for new runners.","zh":"Liz 有幾個給跑步新手的簡單建議。"},{"en":"A couple of means two or a few.","zh":"幾個或兩三個意思是兩個或少數幾個。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students a couple of minutes to check their answers.","zh":"老師可能給學生幾分鐘檢查答案。"},{"en":"Saying “a couple of” makes the number sound small and manageable.","zh":"說 “a couple of” 會令數量聽起來少而容易處理。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday spoken English.","zh":"這個短語常見於日常口語英文。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"simple tips","meaning":"簡單建議","examples":[{"en":"Liz gives simple tips to new runners.","zh":"Liz 給跑步新手簡單建議。"},{"en":"Simple tips are easy pieces of advice that people can understand and use quickly.","zh":"簡單建議是容易理解並能快速使用的建議。"},{"en":"A doctor may give simple tips for better sleep, such as avoiding coffee at night.","zh":"醫生可能給改善睡眠的簡單建議，例如晚上避免喝咖啡。"},{"en":"Simple tips help beginners because they do not feel overloaded with information.","zh":"簡單建議能幫助新手，因為他們不會覺得資訊過多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical advice that is not complicated.","zh":"這個短語描述不複雜的實用建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"new runners","meaning":"跑步新手","examples":[{"en":"New runners often need practical advice.","zh":"跑步新手常需要實用建議。"},{"en":"New runners are people who have recently started running.","zh":"跑步新手是最近開始跑步的人。"},{"en":"New runners may begin with short runs and walking breaks.","zh":"跑步新手可能由短跑和步行休息開始。"},{"en":"Without guidance, new runners may run too fast and become tired or injured.","zh":"沒有指導時，跑步新手可能跑得太快並感到疲倦或受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to beginners in running.","zh":"這個短語指跑步方面的初學者。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"I expect","meaning":"我估計；我想","examples":[{"en":"Liz says, “I expect you have been told to run slowly.”","zh":"Liz 說：「我想你曾被告知要慢慢跑。」"},{"en":"I expect means I think something is likely or probably true.","zh":"我估計或我想意思是我認為某事很可能是真的。"},{"en":"I expect many students feel nervous before their first oral exam.","zh":"我想許多學生在第一次口試前都會緊張。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase when making a reasonable guess.","zh":"說話者在作出合理猜測時會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It sounds softer than saying “I know”.","zh":"它比說 “I know” 語氣較柔和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be told to","meaning":"被告知要……","examples":[{"en":"Beginners are often told to run very slowly.","zh":"新手常被告知要跑得很慢。"},{"en":"To be told to do something means to receive an instruction or piece of advice to do it.","zh":"被告知要做某事意思是收到做該事的指示或建議。"},{"en":"Students are told to write their names at the top of the answer sheet.","zh":"學生被告知要在答題紙頂部寫上名字。"},{"en":"Being told to do something does not always mean the advice suits every person.","zh":"被告知要做某事，不一定代表該建議適合每個人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on instructions given by others.","zh":"這個短語重點是別人給出的指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"run very slowly","meaning":"跑得很慢","examples":[{"en":"Many beginners are told to run very slowly at first.","zh":"許多新手一開始被告知要跑得很慢。"},{"en":"To run very slowly means to move at a low running speed.","zh":"跑得很慢意思是以較低跑步速度移動。"},{"en":"A runner recovering from injury may run very slowly to avoid putting too much pressure on the body.","zh":"正從傷患恢復的跑手可能跑得很慢，以避免給身體太大壓力。"},{"en":"Running very slowly can help beginners start safely, but it may limit progress if done all the time.","zh":"跑得很慢可以幫助新手安全開始，但如果一直如此，可能限制進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pace, not effort alone.","zh":"這個短語描述速度，而不只是努力程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"until your fitness increases","meaning":"直到體能提升","examples":[{"en":"Some people tell beginners to run slowly until their fitness increases.","zh":"有些人告訴新手要慢慢跑，直到體能提升。"},{"en":"Until your fitness increases means up to the point when your physical ability improves.","zh":"直到體能提升意思是直到身體能力改善的那一刻。"},{"en":"A new runner may use walking breaks until their fitness increases enough for continuous running.","zh":"跑步新手可能使用步行休息，直到體能提升到足以連續跑步。"},{"en":"Training becomes easier when fitness increases because the body handles effort better.","zh":"當體能提升，訓練會變得較容易，因為身體更能應付努力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an action is temporary while improvement develops.","zh":"這個短語顯示某行動在進步形成期間是暫時的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prevent progress","meaning":"阻礙進步","examples":[{"en":"Running too slowly can prevent progress.","zh":"跑得太慢可以阻礙進步。"},{"en":"To prevent progress means to stop improvement from happening.","zh":"阻礙進步意思是阻止改善發生。"},{"en":"Studying only easy questions can prevent progress because students never practise harder skills.","zh":"只做簡單題目會阻礙進步，因為學生從不練習較難技能。"},{"en":"A training plan that is too gentle may prevent progress if the body is never challenged.","zh":"如果身體從未受到挑戰，過於輕鬆的訓練計劃可能阻礙進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that blocks development.","zh":"這個短語描述阻擋發展的事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"run at a speed","meaning":"以……速度跑","examples":[{"en":"You should run at a speed that feels comfortable.","zh":"你應以感到舒服的速度跑。"},{"en":"To run at a speed means to move while running at a particular pace.","zh":"以某速度跑意思是以特定步速跑步移動。"},{"en":"A beginner should run at a speed that still allows them to speak short sentences.","zh":"新手應以仍能說短句的速度跑。"},{"en":"Running at the right speed helps people train without becoming exhausted too quickly.","zh":"以合適速度跑有助人訓練而不會太快筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on choosing a suitable pace.","zh":"這個短語重點是選擇合適步速。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"feel comfortable","meaning":"感到舒服","examples":[{"en":"Beginners should run at a speed that feels comfortable.","zh":"新手應以感到舒服的速度跑。"},{"en":"To feel comfortable means to feel physically or emotionally at ease.","zh":"感到舒服意思是身體或情緒上感到自在。"},{"en":"A student speaks better when they feel comfortable in the classroom.","zh":"學生在課室感到舒服時，說話會更好。"},{"en":"If a running pace feels comfortable, beginners are more likely to continue training.","zh":"如果跑步速度令人感到舒服，新手更可能繼續訓練。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a level that is manageable and not stressful.","zh":"這個短語描述可應付而不緊張的程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"time yourself","meaning":"為自己計時","examples":[{"en":"You should time yourself when you run.","zh":"你跑步時應為自己計時。"},{"en":"To time yourself means to measure how long you take to do something.","zh":"為自己計時意思是量度自己完成某事需要多久。"},{"en":"A student may time themselves while practising a reading paper.","zh":"學生練習閱讀卷時可能為自己計時。"},{"en":"Timing yourself helps you see whether you are improving or slowing down.","zh":"為自己計時有助你看見自己是在進步還是變慢。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for training, exams and any task with a time goal.","zh":"這個短語適合用於訓練、考試和任何有時間目標的任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a bit faster each time","meaning":"每次快一點","examples":[{"en":"Beginners should try to run a bit faster each time.","zh":"新手應嘗試每次跑快一點。"},{"en":"A bit faster each time means slightly increasing speed on each attempt.","zh":"每次快一點意思是每次嘗試都稍微提高速度。"},{"en":"A student practising typing may try to type a bit faster each time without losing accuracy.","zh":"練習打字的學生可能嘗試每次打快一點，同時不失準確度。"},{"en":"Small increases in speed can build confidence without overwhelming beginners.","zh":"小幅提高速度可以建立信心，而不會壓垮新手。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests gradual improvement.","zh":"這個短語暗示逐步改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take your mind off things","meaning":"轉移注意力","examples":[{"en":"Listening to music can take your mind off things.","zh":"聽音樂可以轉移你的注意力。"},{"en":"To take your mind off things means to distract you from worries, pain or tiredness.","zh":"轉移注意力意思是令你暫時不再想着憂慮、疼痛或疲倦。"},{"en":"A walk after school can take your mind off exam stress for a while.","zh":"放學後散步可以暫時轉移你對考試壓力的注意。"},{"en":"Music can take your mind off discomfort during exercise and make time pass faster.","zh":"音樂可以在運動期間轉移你對不適的注意，並令時間過得更快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes helpful distraction.","zh":"這個短語描述有幫助的分心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get into a rhythm","meaning":"進入節奏","examples":[{"en":"Music can help your body get into a rhythm.","zh":"音樂可以幫助你的身體進入節奏。"},{"en":"To get into a rhythm means to settle into a steady repeated pattern of movement or work.","zh":"進入節奏意思是進入穩定重複的動作或工作模式。"},{"en":"A student may get into a rhythm after writing several practice essays.","zh":"學生寫了幾篇練習文章後，可能會進入節奏。"},{"en":"When runners get into a rhythm, their breathing and steps may feel smoother.","zh":"當跑手進入節奏，呼吸和步伐可能感覺更順。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding a steady flow.","zh":"這個短語描述找到穩定流暢感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"running with a friend","meaning":"和朋友一起跑步","examples":[{"en":"Listening to music may be better than running with a friend.","zh":"聽音樂可能比和朋友一起跑步更好。"},{"en":"Running with a friend means going for a run together with someone you know.","zh":"和朋友一起跑步意思是與認識的人一起去跑步。"},{"en":"Running with a friend can make exercise more social and less lonely.","zh":"和朋友一起跑步可以令運動更有社交感，也較不孤單。"},{"en":"However, running with a friend may make beginners run too fast if they try to keep up.","zh":"然而，如果新手嘗試跟上朋友，和朋友一起跑步可能令他們跑得太快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shared running activity.","zh":"這個短語描述共同跑步活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"competitive","meaning":"有競爭心的","examples":[{"en":"Many people are competitive when they run with others.","zh":"很多人和別人一起跑步時會有競爭心。"},{"en":"Competitive means wanting to win or do better than other people.","zh":"有競爭心的意思是想勝出或做得比別人好。"},{"en":"A competitive student may try to get the highest score in every test.","zh":"有競爭心的學生可能每次測驗都想拿最高分。"},{"en":"Being too competitive can make friendly activities feel stressful.","zh":"太有競爭心會令友善活動變得有壓力。"},{"en":"This word can be positive in sport, but it may be unhelpful for beginners.","zh":"這個詞在運動中可以是正面的，但對新手未必有幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"just starting","meaning":"剛開始","examples":[{"en":"Competition is not what you want when you are just starting.","zh":"當你剛開始時，競爭不是你想要的東西。"},{"en":"Just starting means beginning an activity and still being new to it.","zh":"剛開始意思是正在開始一項活動，並且仍然是新手。"},{"en":"A student who is just starting piano lessons should not compare themselves with advanced players.","zh":"剛開始學鋼琴的學生不應把自己與進階演奏者比較。"},{"en":"When people are just starting, encouragement is often more useful than pressure.","zh":"當人們剛開始時，鼓勵通常比壓力更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the early beginner stage.","zh":"這個短語突顯早期新手階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the time of day","meaning":"一天中的時間","examples":[{"en":"Liz does not think the time of day is especially important.","zh":"Liz 不認為一天中的時間特別重要。"},{"en":"The time of day means whether something happens in the morning, afternoon, evening or night.","zh":"一天中的時間意思是某事發生在早上、下午、傍晚還是晚上。"},{"en":"Some students study better at a different time of day from their friends.","zh":"有些學生適合在與朋友不同的一天中的時間溫習。"},{"en":"The best time of day for exercise depends on energy, schedule and safety.","zh":"最適合運動的一天中的時間取決於精力、日程和安全。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on when during the day an activity happens.","zh":"這個短語重點是活動在一天中甚麼時候發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"especially important","meaning":"特別重要","examples":[{"en":"The time of day is not especially important for running.","zh":"一天中的時間對跑步來說並非特別重要。"},{"en":"Especially important means more important than usual or particularly significant.","zh":"特別重要意思是比平常更重要或尤其有意義。"},{"en":"Drinking enough water is especially important during hot weather.","zh":"在炎熱天氣中，喝足夠水特別重要。"},{"en":"A detail becomes especially important when ignoring it could cause problems.","zh":"當忽略某細節可能造成問題時，它就變得特別重要。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a stronger level of importance.","zh":"這個短語突顯較高程度的重要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"morning people","meaning":"適合早上活動的人","examples":[{"en":"Some runners are morning people.","zh":"有些跑手是適合早上活動的人。"},{"en":"Morning people are people who feel more energetic and productive early in the day.","zh":"適合早上活動的人是在一天較早時間感到更有精神和更有效率的人。"},{"en":"A morning person may prefer to exercise before work or school.","zh":"適合早上活動的人可能較喜歡上班或上學前運動。"},{"en":"Morning people may find evening training harder because they feel tired by then.","zh":"適合早上活動的人可能覺得晚上訓練較難，因為到那時已感疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a natural preference for mornings.","zh":"這個短語描述對早上的自然偏好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be consistent","meaning":"保持規律","examples":[{"en":"New runners need to be consistent.","zh":"跑步新手需要保持規律。"},{"en":"To be consistent means to keep doing something regularly and steadily.","zh":"保持規律意思是定期而穩定地繼續做某事。"},{"en":"A student improves writing by being consistent with weekly practice.","zh":"學生透過每週規律練習來改善寫作。"},{"en":"Consistency helps runners build fitness because the body adapts over time.","zh":"規律性幫助跑手建立體能，因為身體會隨時間適應。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses regular effort rather than occasional hard work.","zh":"這個短語強調定期努力，而不是偶爾拼命。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"aim to","meaning":"目標是……","examples":[{"en":"Beginners should aim to train regularly.","zh":"新手應以定期訓練為目標。"},{"en":"To aim to do something means to make it your goal.","zh":"目標是做某事意思是把它定為自己的目標。"},{"en":"Students should aim to review vocabulary a little every day.","zh":"學生應以每天溫習一點詞彙為目標。"},{"en":"Clear goals help people stay focused and measure progress.","zh":"清楚目標幫助人們保持專注並量度進步。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving practical advice.","zh":"這個短語適合用於提供實用建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"train regularly","meaning":"定期訓練","examples":[{"en":"New runners should train regularly.","zh":"跑步新手應定期訓練。"},{"en":"To train regularly means to practise according to a steady routine.","zh":"定期訓練意思是按照穩定常規練習。"},{"en":"A student preparing for a speech contest may train regularly by reading aloud every evening.","zh":"準備演講比賽的學生可能每晚朗讀來定期訓練。"},{"en":"Regular training builds skill and confidence more safely than sudden intense effort.","zh":"定期訓練比突然劇烈努力更安全地建立技能和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated practice over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間重複練習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"twice a week","meaning":"每星期兩次","examples":[{"en":"Twice a week is enough to begin with.","zh":"一開始每星期兩次已經足夠。"},{"en":"Twice a week means two times each week.","zh":"每星期兩次意思是每週兩次。"},{"en":"A student may attend English lessons twice a week before an exam.","zh":"學生可能在考試前每星期上兩次英文課。"},{"en":"Training twice a week can help beginners improve while still leaving time to rest.","zh":"每星期訓練兩次可以幫助新手進步，同時仍有時間休息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequency.","zh":"這個短語描述頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"to begin with","meaning":"一開始","examples":[{"en":"Twice a week is enough to begin with.","zh":"一開始每星期兩次已經足夠。"},{"en":"To begin with means at the start or in the early stage.","zh":"一開始意思是在開始或早期階段。"},{"en":"To begin with, students should learn simple sentence patterns before writing long essays.","zh":"一開始，學生應先學簡單句式，再寫長文章。"},{"en":"Starting gently can help people continue instead of giving up quickly.","zh":"溫和地開始可以幫助人繼續，而不是很快放棄。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces what is suitable at the beginning.","zh":"這個短語常引入開始時適合的做法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be put off","meaning":"對……卻步；不想做……","examples":[{"en":"New members are often put off running by a lack of confidence.","zh":"新會員常因缺乏信心而對跑步卻步。"},{"en":"To be put off something means to feel discouraged and no longer want to do it.","zh":"對某事卻步意思是感到氣餒，因而不再想做。"},{"en":"A student may be put off reading if the first book is far too difficult.","zh":"如果第一本書太難，學生可能會對閱讀卻步。"},{"en":"Lack of confidence can put people off trying activities they might enjoy.","zh":"缺乏信心可以令人不想嘗試自己可能會喜歡的活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes losing interest because something feels worrying or unpleasant.","zh":"這個短語描述因某事令人擔心或不愉快而失去興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lack confidence","meaning":"缺乏信心","examples":[{"en":"Some new runners lack confidence.","zh":"有些跑步新手缺乏信心。"},{"en":"To lack confidence means to not feel sure about your ability to do something.","zh":"缺乏信心意思是對自己做某事的能力沒有把握。"},{"en":"A student may lack confidence when speaking English in front of classmates.","zh":"學生在同學面前說英文時可能缺乏信心。"},{"en":"People who lack confidence may avoid activities even when they are capable of doing them.","zh":"缺乏信心的人即使有能力，也可能避開某些活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes self-doubt.","zh":"這個短語描述自我懷疑。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have time","meaning":"有時間","examples":[{"en":"Some people think they do not have time to run.","zh":"有些人認為自己沒有時間跑步。"},{"en":"To have time means to have enough free time available to do something.","zh":"有時間意思是有足夠空閒時間做某事。"},{"en":"A parent may not have time to cook a long meal after work.","zh":"家長下班後可能沒有時間煮一頓很長的飯。"},{"en":"People are more likely to exercise if they can find a time that fits their routine.","zh":"如果人們能找到配合日常安排的時間，就更可能運動。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing busy schedules.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論繁忙日程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dislike running","meaning":"不喜歡跑步","examples":[{"en":"Some people think they dislike running before they try it.","zh":"有些人在嘗試之前便認為自己不喜歡跑步。"},{"en":"To dislike running means to not enjoy running or to feel negative about it.","zh":"不喜歡跑步意思是不能享受跑步或對它有負面感覺。"},{"en":"A student may dislike running because school races once made them feel embarrassed.","zh":"學生可能因學校賽跑曾令他尷尬而不喜歡跑步。"},{"en":"People sometimes dislike an activity less after they try it in a supportive setting.","zh":"人們在有支持的環境中嘗試後，有時會較少討厭某活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a negative feeling toward running.","zh":"這個短語描述對跑步的負面感覺。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"join the club","meaning":"加入俱樂部","examples":[{"en":"Ceri joined the club two years ago.","zh":"Ceri 兩年前加入俱樂部。"},{"en":"To join the club means to become a member of a club or group.","zh":"加入俱樂部意思是成為一個俱樂部或團體的成員。"},{"en":"A student may join the chess club to meet people with the same interest.","zh":"學生可能加入棋藝學會，以認識有相同興趣的人。"},{"en":"Joining a club can make a new activity easier because support is available.","zh":"加入俱樂部可以令新活動較容易，因為有人提供支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming part of an organised group.","zh":"這個短語描述成為有組織團體的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at the age of","meaning":"在……歲時","examples":[{"en":"Ceri joined the club at the age of 40.","zh":"Ceri 在 40 歲時加入俱樂部。"},{"en":"At the age of means when someone was that many years old.","zh":"在某歲時意思是某人那個年齡的時候。"},{"en":"My aunt learned to swim at the age of 55.","zh":"我阿姨在 55 歲時學會游泳。"},{"en":"Starting something at a later age can still lead to real progress.","zh":"在較大年紀開始某事仍可以帶來真正進步。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the age when an event happened.","zh":"這個短語提供事件發生時的年齡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"enjoy running at school","meaning":"上學時喜歡跑步","examples":[{"en":"Ceri had always enjoyed running at school.","zh":"Ceri 一直上學時喜歡跑步。"},{"en":"To enjoy running at school means to like running during school years or school activities.","zh":"上學時喜歡跑步意思是在讀書年代或學校活動中喜歡跑步。"},{"en":"Some adults return to sports they enjoyed at school after many years away.","zh":"有些成年人多年後會重新開始自己上學時喜歡的運動。"},{"en":"Enjoying a sport at school can make it easier to restart later in life.","zh":"上學時喜歡某項運動，可以令日後重新開始較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a present interest with a childhood or teenage experience.","zh":"這個短語把現在的興趣與童年或青少年經歷連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be sure if","meaning":"確定是否……","examples":[{"en":"Ceri was not sure if she would be able to run again.","zh":"Ceri 不確定自己是否能再次跑步。"},{"en":"To be sure if something will happen means to know or feel certain about it.","zh":"確定是否某事會發生，意思是知道或肯定它會否發生。"},{"en":"A student may not be sure if they can finish the essay before the deadline.","zh":"學生可能不確定自己是否能在限期前完成文章。"},{"en":"People often need encouragement when they are not sure if they can succeed.","zh":"當人們不確定自己是否能成功時，通常需要鼓勵。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses uncertainty about a possibility.","zh":"這個短語表達對可能性的疑慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be able to","meaning":"能夠……","examples":[{"en":"Ceri was not sure if she would be able to do it.","zh":"Ceri 不確定自己是否能夠做到。"},{"en":"To be able to do something means to have the ability or opportunity to do it.","zh":"能夠做某事意思是有能力或機會做該事。"},{"en":"A beginner may be able to run for one minute before needing to walk.","zh":"新手可能能夠跑一分鐘，然後需要步行。"},{"en":"People become able to do harder tasks when they practise gradually.","zh":"當人們逐步練習，就會能夠完成更難任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability, possibility or permission.","zh":"這個短語描述能力、可能性或許可。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be worried about","meaning":"擔心……","examples":[{"en":"Ceri was worried about being left behind.","zh":"Ceri 擔心被拋離。"},{"en":"To be worried about something means to feel anxious or concerned about it.","zh":"擔心某事意思是對它感到焦慮或憂慮。"},{"en":"A student may be worried about speaking in front of the class.","zh":"學生可能擔心在全班面前說話。"},{"en":"Worries can stop people from trying something new.","zh":"憂慮可以阻止人嘗試新事物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes anxiety about a possible problem.","zh":"這個短語描述對可能問題的焦慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be left behind","meaning":"落後；被拋離","examples":[{"en":"Ceri was worried about being left behind.","zh":"Ceri 擔心落後。"},{"en":"To be left behind means to fall behind others or be unable to keep up.","zh":"落後或被拋離意思是落在別人後面或跟不上。"},{"en":"A student may feel left behind if the class moves on before they understand the topic.","zh":"如果班級在學生明白主題前繼續前進，學生可能覺得被拋離。"},{"en":"In running, fear of being left behind can make beginners nervous about joining a group.","zh":"在跑步中，害怕被拋離會令新手對加入群體感到緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe physical distance or progress.","zh":"這個短語可以描述實際距離或進度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the slowest runner","meaning":"跑得最慢的人","examples":[{"en":"Ceri was worried about being the slowest runner.","zh":"Ceri 擔心自己是跑得最慢的人。"},{"en":"The slowest runner is the person who runs at the lowest speed in a group.","zh":"跑得最慢的人是在一群人中跑步速度最低的人。"},{"en":"A beginner may fear being the slowest runner during their first club session.","zh":"新手可能害怕在第一次俱樂部訓練中成為跑得最慢的人。"},{"en":"Supportive groups make the slowest runner feel welcome instead of embarrassed.","zh":"有支持的團體會令跑得最慢的人感到受歡迎，而不是尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase compares speed within a group.","zh":"這個短語比較一個群體中的速度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be made to feel welcome","meaning":"被人熱情接待；感到受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Ceri was made to feel very welcome at the club.","zh":"Ceri 在俱樂部感到非常受歡迎。"},{"en":"To be made to feel welcome means to be treated kindly so that you feel accepted.","zh":"感到受歡迎意思是受到友善對待，因而覺得被接納。"},{"en":"New students are made to feel welcome when classmates show them around the school.","zh":"當同學帶新生參觀學校，新生會感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"Feeling welcome can reduce fear and help people continue with a new activity.","zh":"感到受歡迎可以減少恐懼，並幫助人繼續新活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the effect of friendly treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述友善對待造成的效果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"forget all about","meaning":"完全忘記……","examples":[{"en":"Ceri soon forgot all about her worries.","zh":"Ceri 很快完全忘記自己的憂慮。"},{"en":"To forget all about something means to stop thinking about it completely.","zh":"完全忘記某事意思是完全不再想起它。"},{"en":"A child may forget all about their nervousness once the birthday party begins.","zh":"生日會開始後，孩子可能完全忘記自己的緊張。"},{"en":"Friendly support can make people forget all about fears they had before trying something.","zh":"友善支持可以令人完全忘記嘗試某事前的恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests worries disappear from someone’s mind.","zh":"這個短語暗示憂慮從某人腦中消失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hate the idea of","meaning":"討厭……這個想法","examples":[{"en":"James had always hated the idea of running.","zh":"James 一直討厭跑步這個想法。"},{"en":"To hate the idea of something means to strongly dislike even thinking about doing it.","zh":"討厭某事這個想法意思是甚至想到要做它也非常不喜歡。"},{"en":"A student may hate the idea of public speaking before trying a supportive class activity.","zh":"學生在嘗試有支持的課堂活動前，可能討厭公開演說這個想法。"},{"en":"People sometimes hate the idea of an activity because they expect it to be painful or embarrassing.","zh":"人們有時討厭某活動的想法，因為他們預期它會痛苦或尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong resistance before actual experience.","zh":"這個短語描述實際經驗前的強烈抗拒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"encourage someone to","meaning":"鼓勵某人……","examples":[{"en":"A friend encouraged James to come along for a taster session.","zh":"一位朋友鼓勵 James 來參加體驗課。"},{"en":"To encourage someone to do something means to support or persuade them to try it.","zh":"鼓勵某人做某事意思是支持或說服他們嘗試。"},{"en":"A teacher may encourage a shy student to join a debate team.","zh":"老師可能鼓勵害羞學生加入辯論隊。"},{"en":"Encouragement can help people try activities they would avoid alone.","zh":"鼓勵可以幫助人們嘗試自己一個人會避開的活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes positive support rather than force.","zh":"這個短語描述正面支持，而不是強迫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come along","meaning":"一同前來；來參加","examples":[{"en":"James was encouraged to come along for a taster session.","zh":"James 被鼓勵來參加體驗課。"},{"en":"To come along means to go with someone or attend an event.","zh":"一同前來或來參加意思是跟某人一起去或出席一項活動。"},{"en":"A friend may ask you to come along to a school concert.","zh":"朋友可能請你一同前來學校音樂會。"},{"en":"People are more likely to come along when they know the event is friendly and informal.","zh":"當人們知道活動友善而輕鬆，就更可能來參加。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and often used in invitations.","zh":"這個短語較隨意，常用於邀請。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"taster session","meaning":"體驗課","examples":[{"en":"James came along for a taster session.","zh":"James 來參加了一節體驗課。"},{"en":"A taster session is a short introductory session that lets people try an activity before committing.","zh":"體驗課是讓人們在承諾參加前先試一試活動的簡短入門課。"},{"en":"A language school may offer a taster session so students can meet the teacher first.","zh":"語言學校可能提供體驗課，讓學生先見老師。"},{"en":"Taster sessions reduce pressure because people can try something without joining permanently.","zh":"體驗課可以減少壓力，因為人們可以在不永久加入下先嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in clubs, courses and hobbies.","zh":"這個短語常見於俱樂部、課程和興趣活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"haven’t looked back","meaning":"從此沒有回頭；一直堅持下去","examples":[{"en":"James tried running and has not looked back.","zh":"James 嘗試跑步後便一直堅持下去。"},{"en":"To have not looked back means to continue successfully after starting something and not regret it.","zh":"從此沒有回頭意思是開始某事後成功持續下去，並不後悔。"},{"en":"After joining the drama club, she has not looked back and now performs every term.","zh":"她加入戲劇學會後便一直堅持下去，現在每學期都表演。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when a first step leads to lasting enthusiasm or progress.","zh":"當第一步帶來持久熱情或進步時，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It suggests a positive change that continues.","zh":"它暗示一個持續的正面改變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"miss a training session","meaning":"缺席訓練課","examples":[{"en":"James never misses a training session.","zh":"James 從不缺席訓練課。"},{"en":"To miss a training session means to be absent from a scheduled practice.","zh":"缺席訓練課意思是沒有出席已安排的練習。"},{"en":"A swimmer may miss a training session if they are ill.","zh":"游泳運動員生病時可能缺席訓練課。"},{"en":"Missing too many training sessions can slow progress because practice becomes irregular.","zh":"缺席太多訓練課會拖慢進步，因為練習變得不規律。"},{"en":"This phrase describes not attending a planned training time.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有出席已計劃的訓練時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"despite having","meaning":"儘管有……","examples":[{"en":"James never misses training despite having a demanding job.","zh":"儘管有一份要求很高的工作，James 從不缺席訓練。"},{"en":"Despite having something means even though someone has that situation or difficulty.","zh":"儘管有某事意思是即使某人有該情況或困難。"},{"en":"A student finished the project despite having a busy week of tests.","zh":"學生儘管有一個充滿測驗的繁忙星期，仍完成了專題。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights effort because the person continues in spite of an obstacle.","zh":"這個短語突顯努力，因為某人儘管有障礙仍繼續。"},{"en":"It is useful when contrasting difficulty with action.","zh":"當對比困難與行動時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"demanding job","meaning":"要求很高的工作","examples":[{"en":"James has a really demanding job.","zh":"James 有一份要求很高的工作。"},{"en":"A demanding job is a job that requires a lot of time, energy, skill or responsibility.","zh":"要求很高的工作是需要大量時間、精力、技能或責任的工作。"},{"en":"A nurse may have a demanding job because shifts are long and patients need constant care.","zh":"護士的工作可能要求很高，因為輪班時間長而病人需要持續照顧。"},{"en":"Demanding jobs can make hobbies harder to maintain because workers feel tired after work.","zh":"要求很高的工作會令興趣較難維持，因為員工下班後感到疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work that takes serious effort.","zh":"這個短語描述需要大量努力的工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"commit himself to","meaning":"承諾投入……","examples":[{"en":"Leo was worried about having to commit himself to weekly training.","zh":"Leo 擔心自己必須承諾投入每週訓練。"},{"en":"To commit himself to something means to promise or seriously agree to spend time and effort on it.","zh":"承諾投入某事意思是承諾或認真同意為它花時間和努力。"},{"en":"A student may commit himself to practising piano for thirty minutes every day.","zh":"學生可能承諾每天練習鋼琴三十分鐘。"},{"en":"Commitment can feel difficult when someone already has many responsibilities.","zh":"當某人已有許多責任時，承諾投入可能感覺困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious personal dedication.","zh":"這個短語描述認真的個人投入。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"training sessions","meaning":"訓練課","examples":[{"en":"Leo was worried about attending training sessions every week.","zh":"Leo 擔心每星期出席訓練課。"},{"en":"Training sessions are organised periods of practice or instruction.","zh":"訓練課是有組織的練習或教學時段。"},{"en":"A football team may hold training sessions after school twice a week.","zh":"足球隊可能每星期放學後舉行兩次訓練課。"},{"en":"Regular training sessions help people improve because practice happens on a schedule.","zh":"定期訓練課幫助人進步，因為練習按時間表進行。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in sports, work and skill development.","zh":"這個短語用於運動、工作和技能發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fit training into","meaning":"把訓練安排進……","examples":[{"en":"Leo was not sure he could fit training into his busy schedule.","zh":"Leo 不確定自己能否把訓練安排進繁忙日程。"},{"en":"To fit training into a schedule means to find time for training among other commitments.","zh":"把訓練安排進日程意思是在其他責任之間找時間訓練。"},{"en":"A parent may fit exercise into the morning before taking children to school.","zh":"家長可能把運動安排在早上送孩子上學前。"},{"en":"People need realistic plans if they want to fit training into busy lives.","zh":"如果人們想把訓練安排進繁忙生活，就需要實際可行的計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arranging time for an activity.","zh":"這個短語描述為某活動安排時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"busy schedule","meaning":"繁忙日程","examples":[{"en":"Leo wondered if running could fit into his busy schedule.","zh":"Leo 想知道跑步能否安排進他的繁忙日程。"},{"en":"A busy schedule is a timetable full of work, tasks or commitments.","zh":"繁忙日程是充滿工作、任務或承諾的時間表。"},{"en":"A student with a busy schedule may need to plan study time carefully.","zh":"日程繁忙的學生可能需要仔細計劃溫習時間。"},{"en":"Busy schedules can make exercise harder unless people choose realistic times.","zh":"繁忙日程會令運動更難，除非人們選擇實際可行的時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited free time because many things are planned.","zh":"這個短語描述因安排很多事情而空閒時間有限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"experience stress at work","meaning":"在工作上承受壓力","examples":[{"en":"Leo experienced a lot of stress at work.","zh":"Leo 在工作上承受很大壓力。"},{"en":"To experience stress at work means to feel pressure, worry or tension because of one’s job.","zh":"在工作上承受壓力意思是因工作而感到壓力、擔憂或緊張。"},{"en":"A teacher may experience stress at work during exam season.","zh":"老師在考試季節可能在工作上承受壓力。"},{"en":"Work stress can affect sleep, mood and health if it continues too long.","zh":"如果工作壓力持續太久，可能影響睡眠、心情和健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pressure linked to the workplace.","zh":"這個短語描述與工作場所有關的壓力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"give it a go","meaning":"試一試","examples":[{"en":"Leo came along to the club and gave running a go.","zh":"Leo 來到俱樂部並試一試跑步。"},{"en":"To give something a go means to try it, especially when you are not sure you will like it or succeed.","zh":"試一試某事意思是嘗試它，尤其是在不確定自己會否喜歡或成功時。"},{"en":"A student may give public speaking a go after a friend encourages them.","zh":"朋友鼓勵後，學生可能試一試公開演說。"},{"en":"Trying something once can reduce fear because the activity becomes less unknown.","zh":"嘗試一次可以減少恐懼，因為活動變得較不陌生。"},{"en":"This phrase is friendly and informal.","zh":"這個短語友善而口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"feel more relaxed","meaning":"感到更放鬆","examples":[{"en":"Leo now feels much more relaxed.","zh":"Leo 現在感到放鬆得多。"},{"en":"To feel more relaxed means to feel calmer and less tense than before.","zh":"感到更放鬆意思是比以前更平靜和不那麼緊張。"},{"en":"A student may feel more relaxed after revising with a clear plan.","zh":"學生按照清楚計劃溫習後，可能感到更放鬆。"},{"en":"Exercise can help people feel more relaxed by reducing stress and clearing the mind.","zh":"運動可以透過減少壓力和清理思緒，幫助人感到更放鬆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an improvement in mood or tension.","zh":"這個短語描述心情或緊張程度的改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"look forward to","meaning":"期待……","examples":[{"en":"Leo looks forward to his weekly run.","zh":"Leo 期待每星期一次的跑步。"},{"en":"To look forward to something means to feel happy or excited about something that will happen.","zh":"期待某事意思是對將會發生的事感到高興或興奮。"},{"en":"Students may look forward to a school trip after weeks of exams.","zh":"經過幾星期考試後，學生可能期待學校旅行。"},{"en":"Looking forward to an activity can make it easier to keep doing it regularly.","zh":"期待某項活動可以令人更容易定期持續做它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes positive expectation.","zh":"這個短語描述正面的期待。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"weekly run","meaning":"每星期一次的跑步","examples":[{"en":"Leo looks forward to his weekly run.","zh":"Leo 期待每星期一次的跑步。"},{"en":"A weekly run is a run that happens once every week.","zh":"每星期一次的跑步是每週發生一次的跑步活動。"},{"en":"A family may plan a weekly run together every Sunday morning.","zh":"家庭可能計劃每星期日早上一起跑步一次。"},{"en":"Weekly runs help create routine because people know when they will exercise.","zh":"每週跑步有助建立常規，因為人們知道何時會運動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regular running frequency.","zh":"這個短語描述規律跑步頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be typical of","meaning":"是……的典型","examples":[{"en":"Mark is quite typical of the club’s new members.","zh":"Mark 相當是俱樂部新會員的典型。"},{"en":"To be typical of a group means to be a usual or representative example of that group.","zh":"是某群體的典型意思是該群體中常見或具代表性的例子。"},{"en":"Feeling nervous is typical of many students before their first presentation.","zh":"第一次匯報前感到緊張，是許多學生的典型情況。"},{"en":"A typical example helps people understand what a larger group is often like.","zh":"典型例子幫助人們理解較大群體通常是怎樣的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something common or representative.","zh":"這個短語描述常見或具代表性的事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"consider himself to be","meaning":"認為自己是……","examples":[{"en":"Mark has never considered himself to be a sporty person.","zh":"Mark 從未認為自己是愛運動的人。"},{"en":"To consider himself to be something means to think of himself in that way.","zh":"認為自己是某類人意思是以那種方式看待自己。"},{"en":"A student may not consider herself to be artistic until a teacher praises her drawing.","zh":"學生可能直到老師稱讚她的畫，才認為自己有藝術天分。"},{"en":"How people consider themselves can affect what activities they are willing to try.","zh":"人們如何看待自己，會影響他們願意嘗試甚麼活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes self-image or self-judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述自我形象或自我判斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sporty person","meaning":"愛運動的人","examples":[{"en":"Mark never considered himself to be a sporty person.","zh":"Mark 從未認為自己是愛運動的人。"},{"en":"A sporty person is someone who enjoys sport or is active in physical activities.","zh":"愛運動的人是喜歡運動或積極參與體能活動的人。"},{"en":"A sporty person may join football, swimming or running clubs.","zh":"愛運動的人可能加入足球、游泳或跑步俱樂部。"},{"en":"People who are not sporty can still become active if they find a suitable activity.","zh":"不愛運動的人如果找到合適活動，也仍可以變得活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interest and habit, not only natural talent.","zh":"這個短語描述興趣和習慣，而不只是天生才能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"it was only when","meaning":"直到……才","examples":[{"en":"It was only when Mark retired that he took up running.","zh":"Mark 直到退休才開始跑步。"},{"en":"It was only when something happened that something else happened means the second event did not happen until the first event occurred.","zh":"直到某事發生才有另一事發生，意思是第二件事在第一件事發生前沒有出現。"},{"en":"It was only when the exam was near that the student began to revise seriously.","zh":"學生直到考試臨近才開始認真溫習。"},{"en":"This structure emphasises the turning point that caused a change.","zh":"這個結構強調造成改變的轉折點。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing delayed action.","zh":"當展示延遲行動時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"retire","meaning":"退休","examples":[{"en":"Mark decided to take up running when he retired.","zh":"Mark 退休時決定開始跑步。"},{"en":"To retire means to stop working, usually because of age or after a long career.","zh":"退休意思是停止工作，通常因年齡或長期職業生涯後如此。"},{"en":"A teacher may retire after many years of working at the same school.","zh":"老師可能在同一所學校工作多年後退休。"},{"en":"Retirement can give people more time to try hobbies they delayed before.","zh":"退休可以給人更多時間嘗試以前延遲的興趣。"},{"en":"This verb describes leaving regular paid work permanently or semi-permanently.","zh":"這個動詞描述永久或半永久離開定期受薪工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"take up the challenge of","meaning":"接受……的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Mark took up the challenge of trying to run five kilometres.","zh":"Mark 接受嘗試跑五公里的挑戰。"},{"en":"To take up the challenge of doing something means to accept a difficult task and try to do it.","zh":"接受做某事的挑戰意思是接受一項困難任務並嘗試完成。"},{"en":"A student may take up the challenge of reading one English book every month.","zh":"學生可能接受每月讀一本英文書的挑戰。"},{"en":"Accepting a challenge can build confidence because progress becomes visible.","zh":"接受挑戰可以建立信心，因為進步會變得可見。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests courage and willingness to try.","zh":"這個短語暗示勇氣和願意嘗試。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"find the courage to","meaning":"鼓起勇氣去……","examples":[{"en":"It took Mark months to find the courage to contact the club.","zh":"Mark 花了幾個月才鼓起勇氣聯絡俱樂部。"},{"en":"To find the courage to do something means to become brave enough to do it.","zh":"鼓起勇氣做某事意思是變得足夠勇敢去做它。"},{"en":"A shy student may take weeks to find the courage to ask a question in class.","zh":"害羞學生可能花幾星期才鼓起勇氣在課堂發問。"},{"en":"People often need time and reassurance before they find the courage to try something new.","zh":"人們通常需要時間和安慰，才會鼓起勇氣嘗試新事物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes overcoming fear.","zh":"這個短語描述克服恐懼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"feel reassured","meaning":"感到放心","examples":[{"en":"Mark felt reassured immediately.","zh":"Mark 立即感到放心。"},{"en":"To feel reassured means to feel calmer because worries have been reduced.","zh":"感到放心意思是因憂慮減少而感到較平靜。"},{"en":"A patient may feel reassured after a doctor explains that the test results are normal.","zh":"醫生解釋檢查結果正常後，病人可能感到放心。"},{"en":"Friendly information can make beginners feel reassured before joining an activity.","zh":"友善資訊可以令新手在參加活動前感到放心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes comfort after uncertainty or fear.","zh":"這個短語描述不確定或恐懼後的安心感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"people his age","meaning":"和他年紀相若的人","examples":[{"en":"There were other people his age taking up running.","zh":"有其他和他年紀相若的人正在開始跑步。"},{"en":"People his age means people who are about the same age as him.","zh":"和他年紀相若的人意思是與他年齡大約相同的人。"},{"en":"A retired man may feel more comfortable joining a class with people his age.","zh":"退休男士可能更願意加入有同齡人的課程。"},{"en":"Seeing people your age doing an activity can make it feel more possible.","zh":"看見和自己年紀相若的人做某活動，可以令人覺得自己也做得到。"},{"en":"This phrase compares age with another person or group.","zh":"這個短語把年齡與另一人或群體作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"only just","meaning":"才剛剛","examples":[{"en":"Some people his age were only just taking up running.","zh":"有些和他年紀相若的人才剛剛開始跑步。"},{"en":"Only just means very recently or barely at the beginning of something.","zh":"才剛剛意思是最近才開始，或只是剛在初期。"},{"en":"A student who only just started learning English may need very simple reading tasks.","zh":"才剛剛開始學英文的學生可能需要很簡單的閱讀任務。"},{"en":"When people have only just begun, they should not expect perfect performance.","zh":"當人們才剛剛開始時，不應期待完美表現。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that something has just started.","zh":"這個短語強調某事剛開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for the first time","meaning":"第一次","examples":[{"en":"Some members were taking up running for the first time.","zh":"有些會員是第一次開始跑步。"},{"en":"For the first time means doing something that one has never done before.","zh":"第一次意思是做一件以前從未做過的事。"},{"en":"A child may ride a bicycle without help for the first time.","zh":"孩子可能第一次不用幫助踩單車。"},{"en":"Doing something for the first time can feel exciting and frightening at the same time.","zh":"第一次做某事可以同時令人興奮和害怕。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a new experience.","zh":"這個短語突顯新經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"my own journey","meaning":"我自己的歷程","examples":[{"en":"Liz says her own journey has not been easy.","zh":"Liz 說她自己的歷程並不容易。"},{"en":"My own journey means my personal experience of progress, struggle or change.","zh":"我自己的歷程意思是我個人在進步、掙扎或改變中的經驗。"},{"en":"A teacher may share her own journey of learning English to encourage students.","zh":"老師可能分享自己學英文的歷程來鼓勵學生。"},{"en":"Personal journeys often include setbacks, practice and turning points.","zh":"個人歷程通常包括挫折、練習和轉折點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a life or learning process, not only physical travel.","zh":"這個短語描述人生或學習過程，而不只是實際旅行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"marathon","meaning":"馬拉松","examples":[{"en":"Liz did her first marathon when she was 37.","zh":"Liz 在 37 歲時完成了第一次馬拉松。"},{"en":"A marathon is a long-distance race of about 42.2 kilometres.","zh":"馬拉松是約 42.2 公里的長跑比賽。"},{"en":"A runner usually trains for months before attempting a marathon.","zh":"跑手通常在嘗試馬拉松前訓練數月。"},{"en":"Marathons require stamina, planning and mental strength.","zh":"馬拉松需要耐力、計劃和心理力量。"},{"en":"This word refers to a very demanding running event.","zh":"這個詞指非常具挑戰性的跑步賽事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"after having had","meaning":"在已經有……之後","examples":[{"en":"Liz did her first marathon after having had two children.","zh":"Liz 在已經有兩個孩子之後完成了第一次馬拉松。"},{"en":"After having had something means after someone has already experienced or gone through that situation.","zh":"在已經有某經歷之後，意思是在某人已經經歷或經過某情況後。"},{"en":"A parent may return to study after having had several years away from school.","zh":"家長可能在離開學校幾年後重返學習。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an achievement happened after an important life experience.","zh":"這個短語顯示某項成就是在重要人生經歷之後發生的。"},{"en":"It is useful when linking past experience with later action.","zh":"當把過往經驗與之後行動連繫起來時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"run marathons for years","meaning":"多年來一直跑馬拉松","examples":[{"en":"Liz’s husband had been running marathons for years.","zh":"Liz 的丈夫多年來一直跑馬拉松。"},{"en":"To run marathons for years means to take part in marathon races over a long period.","zh":"多年來一直跑馬拉松意思是在很長時間內參加馬拉松比賽。"},{"en":"A teacher who has run marathons for years may give useful advice about training and rest.","zh":"多年來一直跑馬拉松的老師，可能能就訓練和休息提供有用建議。"},{"en":"Long experience can make runners more confident about handling difficult races.","zh":"長期經驗可以令跑手更有信心應付困難賽事。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises repeated marathon running over time.","zh":"這個短語強調隨時間重複跑馬拉松。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"never dream","meaning":"從沒想過","examples":[{"en":"Liz never dreamed she would run a marathon with her husband.","zh":"Liz 從沒想過自己會和丈夫一起跑馬拉松。"},{"en":"To never dream something would happen means to never imagine it was possible.","zh":"從沒想過某事會發生，意思是從未想像它有可能。"},{"en":"A shy student may never dream they could win a public speaking prize.","zh":"害羞學生可能從沒想過自己能贏得演講獎。"},{"en":"People sometimes achieve things they never dreamed of when they receive support and keep practising.","zh":"當人們得到支持並持續練習，有時會達成自己從沒想過的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses surprise at an unexpected achievement.","zh":"這個短語表達對意外成就的驚訝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"manage to complete","meaning":"成功完成","examples":[{"en":"Liz managed to complete her first marathon in four hours.","zh":"Liz 成功在四小時內完成她第一次馬拉松。"},{"en":"To manage to complete something means to succeed in finishing it, especially when it is difficult.","zh":"成功完成某事意思是成功做完它，尤其是在它很困難時。"},{"en":"A student managed to complete the essay despite having only one evening left.","zh":"學生即使只剩一個晚上，仍成功完成文章。"},{"en":"Finishing a hard task can build confidence because it proves effort worked.","zh":"完成艱難任務可以建立信心，因為它證明努力有效。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights successful completion after challenge.","zh":"這個短語突顯挑戰後的成功完成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"feel like giving up","meaning":"想放棄","examples":[{"en":"Liz felt like giving up halfway through the marathon.","zh":"Liz 在馬拉松到一半時想放棄。"},{"en":"To feel like giving up means to want to stop because something feels too hard.","zh":"想放棄意思是因某事感覺太難而想停止。"},{"en":"A student may feel like giving up when a maths problem remains unsolved for a long time.","zh":"當一道數學題長時間解不到，學生可能想放棄。"},{"en":"Support from others can help people continue when they feel like giving up.","zh":"當人們想放棄時，別人的支持可以幫助他們繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a moment of discouragement.","zh":"這個短語描述灰心的一刻。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"halfway through","meaning":"到一半時","examples":[{"en":"Liz felt like giving up halfway through the marathon.","zh":"Liz 在馬拉松到一半時想放棄。"},{"en":"Halfway through something means at the middle point of an activity or period.","zh":"到一半時意思是在一項活動或時間段的中間點。"},{"en":"Halfway through the lesson, the teacher asked students to discuss in pairs.","zh":"課堂到一半時，老師要求學生二人一組討論。"},{"en":"People may feel tired halfway through a long task, even if they started with energy.","zh":"人們在長任務到一半時可能感到疲倦，即使一開始很有精神。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a time or progress point in the middle.","zh":"這個短語提供中段的時間或進度點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"support of the spectators","meaning":"觀眾的支持","examples":[{"en":"The support of the spectators kept Liz going.","zh":"觀眾的支持令 Liz 堅持下去。"},{"en":"The support of the spectators means encouragement from people watching an event.","zh":"觀眾的支持意思是觀看活動的人給予的鼓勵。"},{"en":"In a school sports day, the support of classmates can help runners finish strongly.","zh":"在學校運動會中，同學的支持可以幫助跑手強勢完成。"},{"en":"Spectator support can give tired athletes energy when they are close to stopping.","zh":"當疲倦運動員快要停下時，觀眾支持可以給他們力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes encouragement from the audience.","zh":"這個短語描述來自觀眾的鼓勵。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"keep someone going","meaning":"令某人堅持下去","examples":[{"en":"The spectators’ support kept Liz going.","zh":"觀眾的支持令 Liz 堅持下去。"},{"en":"To keep someone going means to help them continue when they are tired or discouraged.","zh":"令某人堅持下去意思是在他們疲倦或灰心時幫助他們繼續。"},{"en":"A kind message from a teacher can keep a student going during exam revision.","zh":"老師的一則善意訊息可以令學生在考試溫習期間堅持下去。"},{"en":"Encouragement keeps people going because it reminds them that their effort matters.","zh":"鼓勵令人堅持下去，因為它提醒人們自己的努力有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes support that prevents someone from stopping.","zh":"這個短語描述防止某人停下的支持。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sign up for","meaning":"報名參加","examples":[{"en":"Signing up for a race can be motivating.","zh":"報名參加比賽可以有激勵作用。"},{"en":"To sign up for something means to register or put your name down to join it.","zh":"報名參加某事意思是登記或寫下名字以加入它。"},{"en":"Students may sign up for an English workshop before the deadline.","zh":"學生可能在限期前報名參加英文工作坊。"},{"en":"Signing up can make a goal feel real because there is now a clear event ahead.","zh":"報名可以令目標感覺真實，因為前方已有清楚活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for classes, clubs, races and events.","zh":"這個短語用於課程、俱樂部、比賽和活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"of whatever length","meaning":"不論長短","examples":[{"en":"A race of whatever length can be motivating.","zh":"不論長短，任何比賽都可以有激勵作用。"},{"en":"Of whatever length means no matter how long or short it is.","zh":"不論長短意思是不管它多長或多短。"},{"en":"A writing task of whatever length still needs a clear beginning and ending.","zh":"不論長短，寫作任務仍需要清楚開首和結尾。"},{"en":"Any race, of whatever length, can give runners a goal to work towards.","zh":"任何比賽不論長短，都可以給跑手一個努力目標。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the exact size or distance is not the main point.","zh":"這個短語顯示確切大小或距離不是重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be motivating","meaning":"有激勵作用","examples":[{"en":"Signing up for a race is motivating.","zh":"報名參加比賽有激勵作用。"},{"en":"To be motivating means to make someone want to work harder or continue.","zh":"有激勵作用意思是令人想更努力或繼續做下去。"},{"en":"A clear progress chart can be motivating for students learning vocabulary.","zh":"清楚進度表可以對學習詞彙的學生有激勵作用。"},{"en":"Motivation helps people keep practising even when progress feels slow.","zh":"動力幫助人們即使覺得進步緩慢也繼續練習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that encourages action.","zh":"這個短語描述鼓勵行動的事物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"work towards","meaning":"為……努力","examples":[{"en":"A race gives runners something to work towards.","zh":"比賽給跑手一個可以為之努力的目標。"},{"en":"To work towards something means to make effort over time to reach a goal.","zh":"為某事努力意思是隨時間付出努力以達到目標。"},{"en":"A student may work towards a higher writing score by practising every week.","zh":"學生可以透過每週練習，為更高寫作分數努力。"},{"en":"Having a goal to work towards can make daily practice feel more meaningful.","zh":"有一個可以為之努力的目標，會令日常練習感覺更有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes steady effort directed at a target.","zh":"這個短語描述朝目標持續努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sense of achievement","meaning":"成就感","examples":[{"en":"Finishing a race gives runners a sense of achievement.","zh":"完成比賽會給跑手成就感。"},{"en":"A sense of achievement is the proud feeling that comes after completing something difficult or meaningful.","zh":"成就感是在完成困難或有意義的事情後產生的自豪感。"},{"en":"A student may feel a sense of achievement after reading their first full English book.","zh":"學生讀完第一本完整英文書後，可能感到成就感。"},{"en":"A sense of achievement can encourage people to set another goal.","zh":"成就感可以鼓勵人們設定另一個目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional reward after effort.","zh":"這個短語描述努力後的情緒回報。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"certainly very challenging","meaning":"確實非常有挑戰性","examples":[{"en":"Liz’s first 10K was certainly very challenging.","zh":"Liz 的第一次 10 公里跑確實非常有挑戰性。"},{"en":"Certainly very challenging means definitely difficult and requiring serious effort.","zh":"確實非常有挑戰性意思是肯定很困難並需要大量努力。"},{"en":"Writing a full essay in a new language can be certainly very challenging for beginners.","zh":"對新手來說，用新語言寫完整文章確實非常有挑戰性。"},{"en":"A challenging task can still be useful if it is difficult but achievable.","zh":"有挑戰性的任務如果困難但可達成，仍可以有用。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises difficulty.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調困難程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"necessarily recommend","meaning":"不一定推薦","examples":[{"en":"Liz would not necessarily recommend doing a 10K so early.","zh":"Liz 不一定推薦這麼早就跑 10 公里。"},{"en":"Would not necessarily recommend means would not say it is always a good idea for everyone.","zh":"不一定推薦意思是不是說這對每個人都一定是好主意。"},{"en":"A teacher would not necessarily recommend learning advanced grammar before mastering basic sentences.","zh":"老師不一定推薦學生在掌握基本句子前學高階文法。"},{"en":"This phrase gives careful advice because people’s situations differ.","zh":"這個短語提供謹慎建議，因為每個人的情況不同。"},{"en":"It softens a warning without completely forbidding something.","zh":"它柔化警告，而不是完全禁止某事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"after only six months","meaning":"只過了六個月後","examples":[{"en":"Liz did her first 10K after only six months.","zh":"Liz 只過了六個月後便完成第一次 10 公里跑。"},{"en":"After only six months means just six months later, which may feel like a short time.","zh":"只過了六個月後意思是僅僅六個月之後，可能感覺時間很短。"},{"en":"A student may speak more confidently after only six months of regular practice.","zh":"學生定期練習只過了六個月後，可能說話更有信心。"},{"en":"Saying “only” emphasises that the progress happened faster than expected.","zh":"使用 “only” 強調進步比預期快。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a short period before an achievement.","zh":"這個短語突顯成就前的短時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"train for a few weeks","meaning":"訓練幾星期","examples":[{"en":"After you have trained for a few weeks, you can consider a 5K race.","zh":"當你訓練幾星期後，可以考慮參加 5 公里賽。"},{"en":"To train for a few weeks means to practise regularly over several weeks.","zh":"訓練幾星期意思是在數星期內定期練習。"},{"en":"A beginner may train for a few weeks before joining a short charity run.","zh":"新手可能先訓練幾星期，然後參加短途慈善跑。"},{"en":"A few weeks of training can help the body adapt before a race.","zh":"幾星期訓練可以幫助身體在比賽前適應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a short preparation period.","zh":"這個短語描述短期準備時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"it’s worth","meaning":"值得……","examples":[{"en":"It is worth putting your name down for a 5K.","zh":"報名參加 5 公里賽是值得的。"},{"en":"It is worth doing something means it is a good idea because the benefit is enough.","zh":"值得做某事意思是這是好主意，因為好處足夠。"},{"en":"It is worth checking your essay twice before submitting it.","zh":"提交文章前檢查兩次是值得的。"},{"en":"Something is worth doing when the effort brings useful results.","zh":"當付出的努力帶來有用結果，某事就是值得做的。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to recommend an action gently.","zh":"這個短語用來溫和地推薦一項行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"put your name down for","meaning":"報名參加","examples":[{"en":"Beginners can put their name down for a 5K race.","zh":"新手可以報名參加 5 公里賽。"},{"en":"To put your name down for something means to register or sign up for it.","zh":"報名參加某事意思是登記或報名加入它。"},{"en":"A student may put their name down for the school talent show.","zh":"學生可能報名參加學校才藝表演。"},{"en":"Putting your name down can make a plan feel official and harder to ignore.","zh":"報名可以令計劃感覺正式，並較難忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English for joining events or lists.","zh":"這個短語在英式英語中常用於參加活動或加入名單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"practice runs","meaning":"練跑","examples":[{"en":"Some people only need a few practice runs before a race.","zh":"有些人在比賽前只需要幾次練跑。"},{"en":"Practice runs are runs done before a race to prepare and build confidence.","zh":"練跑是在比賽前為準備和建立信心而進行的跑步。"},{"en":"A beginner may do practice runs in the park before joining a public event.","zh":"新手可能在參加公開活動前先在公園練跑。"},{"en":"Practice runs help runners test their pace, shoes and breathing before race day.","zh":"練跑幫助跑手在比賽日前測試速度、跑鞋和呼吸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparation through repeated trial.","zh":"這個短語描述透過重複嘗試來準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"take part in a race","meaning":"參加比賽","examples":[{"en":"Some beginners take part in a race after a few practice runs.","zh":"有些新手練跑幾次後便參加比賽。"},{"en":"To take part in a race means to join a running competition or organised running event.","zh":"參加比賽意思是加入跑步競賽或有組織的跑步活動。"},{"en":"A student may take part in a race during school sports day.","zh":"學生可能在學校運動會參加比賽。"},{"en":"Taking part in a race can give beginners a clear goal and a sense of excitement.","zh":"參加比賽可以給新手清楚目標和興奮感。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on participating, not necessarily winning.","zh":"這個短語重點是參與，而不一定是勝出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"give yourself","meaning":"給自己……","examples":[{"en":"Liz suggests giving yourself at least a couple of months.","zh":"Liz 建議給自己至少幾個月時間。"},{"en":"To give yourself time means to allow yourself enough time to prepare, learn or recover.","zh":"給自己時間意思是讓自己有足夠時間準備、學習或恢復。"},{"en":"A student should give themselves a week to plan and write a careful essay.","zh":"學生應給自己一星期時間來規劃並寫好文章。"},{"en":"Giving yourself enough time reduces pressure and helps you avoid rushing.","zh":"給自己足夠時間可以減少壓力並避免趕工。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in advice about preparation.","zh":"這個短語常用於關於準備的建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a couple of months at least","meaning":"至少幾個月","examples":[{"en":"Beginners should give themselves a couple of months at least.","zh":"新手應給自己至少幾個月時間。"},{"en":"A couple of months at least means no less than about two months, and possibly more.","zh":"至少幾個月意思是不少於大約兩個月，甚至可能更多。"},{"en":"A student preparing for a major exam should give themselves a couple of months at least.","zh":"準備大型考試的學生應給自己至少幾個月時間。"},{"en":"Allowing at least a couple of months helps beginners build habits slowly and safely.","zh":"預留至少幾個月可以幫助新手慢慢而安全地建立習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a minimum preparation time.","zh":"這個短語設定最低準備時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 8/task-3":[{"front":"be off to","meaning":"即將前往……","examples":[{"en":"Jane will be off to Denmark soon to do her work placement.","zh":"Jane 很快就會前往丹麥做工作實習。"},{"en":"To be off to a place means to be going there soon.","zh":"be off to a place 指很快將要前往某地。"},{"en":"My brother is off to university next week, so he is packing his clothes tonight.","zh":"我哥哥下星期即將前往大學，所以今晚正在收拾衣服。"},{"en":"When someone is off to another country, they may need to arrange visas, housing, and travel.","zh":"當某人即將前往另一個國家，可能需要安排簽證、住宿和交通。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds casual and is often used when someone is leaving for a trip, study, or work.","zh":"這個片語語氣較輕鬆，常用於某人因旅行、升學或工作而出發時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"work placement","meaning":"工作實習","examples":[{"en":"Jane is going to Denmark to do her work placement.","zh":"Jane 要去丹麥做工作實習。"},{"en":"A work placement is a period of practical work experience, often arranged as part of a course.","zh":"work placement 指一段實際工作經驗，通常是課程的一部分。"},{"en":"A nursing student may do a work placement in a hospital to learn from real patients.","zh":"護理學生可能在醫院做工作實習，向真實病人學習。"},{"en":"Work placements help students connect classroom knowledge with workplace skills.","zh":"工作實習幫助學生把課堂知識與職場技能連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to temporary training, not a permanent full-time job.","zh":"這個片語通常指暫時培訓，而不是永久全職工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look forward to","meaning":"期待……","examples":[{"en":"Jane is really looking forward to her work placement.","zh":"Jane 非常期待她的工作實習。"},{"en":"To look forward to something means to feel happy and excited about something that will happen.","zh":"look forward to something 指對即將發生的事情感到開心和興奮。"},{"en":"Students may look forward to the summer holiday after a long exam period.","zh":"經過漫長考試期後，學生可能期待暑假。"},{"en":"Looking forward to an event can make preparation feel less stressful.","zh":"期待某活動可以令準備過程感覺沒那麼有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is followed by a noun or an -ing form, such as “looking forward to meeting you”.","zh":"這個片語後面接名詞或 -ing 形式，例如 “looking forward to meeting you”。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"start packing up","meaning":"開始把……打包","examples":[{"en":"Jane has just started packing up all her books.","zh":"Jane 剛開始把她所有書本打包。"},{"en":"To start packing up means to begin putting things into boxes, bags, or containers.","zh":"start packing up 指開始把東西放進箱、袋或容器中。"},{"en":"A family may start packing up before moving to a new flat.","zh":"家庭搬到新單位前，可能會開始把東西打包。"},{"en":"Starting early helps people avoid rushing and forgetting important items.","zh":"早點開始有助人們避免趕急和忘記重要物品。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests preparation for moving, storing, or leaving a place.","zh":"這個片語常暗示為搬遷、存放或離開某地作準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"put something in storage","meaning":"把某物存放起來","examples":[{"en":"Jane is packing up her books to put them in storage.","zh":"Jane 正在把書打包，以便把它們存放起來。"},{"en":"To put something in storage means to keep it in a safe place for later use.","zh":"put something in storage 指把某物放在安全地方，以便日後使用。"},{"en":"A student studying abroad may put winter clothes in storage until she returns.","zh":"出國讀書的學生可能把冬天衣服存放起來，直到回來。"},{"en":"Putting things in storage protects them when there is not enough space at home.","zh":"當家中空間不足，把東西存放起來可以保護它們。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests temporary keeping, not throwing things away.","zh":"這個片語暗示暫時保存，而不是丟掉東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get spoilt","meaning":"被弄壞","examples":[{"en":"Kieran hopes Jane’s books do not get spoilt in storage.","zh":"Kieran 希望 Jane 的書不會在存放期間被弄壞。"},{"en":"To get spoilt means to become damaged or ruined.","zh":"get spoilt 指變得受損或被破壞。"},{"en":"Food can get spoilt if it is left outside the fridge for too long.","zh":"如果食物放在雪櫃外太久，可能會變壞。"},{"en":"Books may get spoilt in a damp room because moisture can damage the pages.","zh":"書本放在潮濕房間可能會被弄壞，因為濕氣會損害書頁。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when something loses its good condition.","zh":"這個片語常用於某物失去良好狀態時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"work in a bookshop","meaning":"在書店工作","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather works in a bookshop.","zh":"Jane 的祖父在書店工作。"},{"en":"To work in a bookshop means to have a job selling, organising, or recommending books.","zh":"work in a bookshop 指從事售賣、整理或推薦書籍的工作。"},{"en":"Someone who works in a bookshop may help customers find novels, textbooks, or children’s books.","zh":"在書店工作的人可能幫顧客尋找小說、課本或兒童書。"},{"en":"Working in a bookshop can teach a person how to handle, store, and display books properly.","zh":"在書店工作可以教人如何正確拿取、存放和展示書本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a job location and type of work.","zh":"這個片語描述工作地點和工作類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tell someone how to","meaning":"告訴某人如何……","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather told her how to pack the books.","zh":"Jane 的祖父告訴她如何打包書本。"},{"en":"To tell someone how to do something means to explain the steps or method.","zh":"tell someone how to do something 指向某人解釋步驟或方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may tell students how to write a formal letter before they begin.","zh":"老師可能在學生開始前告訴他們如何寫正式信件。"},{"en":"Clear instructions help people avoid mistakes when they are doing something new.","zh":"清楚指示能幫助人們在做新事情時避免錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone gives practical guidance.","zh":"這個片語適合用於某人提供實用指導時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"support the spine","meaning":"支撐書脊","examples":[{"en":"You have to support the spine when packing books.","zh":"打包書本時，你必須支撐書脊。"},{"en":"To support the spine means to protect the part of the book that holds the pages together.","zh":"support the spine 指保護把書頁固定在一起的書脊部分。"},{"en":"When carrying a heavy dictionary, hold it firmly so you support the spine.","zh":"拿厚重字典時，要穩穩握住，以支撐書脊。"},{"en":"If the spine is not supported, the pages may loosen or the cover may break.","zh":"如果書脊沒有被支撐，書頁可能鬆脫，封面也可能裂開。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when handling books carefully.","zh":"這個片語在小心處理書本時很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"otherwise","meaning":"否則","examples":[{"en":"You have to support the spine; otherwise, the pages may come away from the cover.","zh":"你必須支撐書脊，否則書頁可能會從封面脫落。"},{"en":"Otherwise means if not, or if the previous action is not done.","zh":"otherwise 指如果不是這樣，或如果之前的行動沒有做。"},{"en":"Put your name on the answer sheet; otherwise, the teacher may not know whose work it is.","zh":"在答題紙上寫上名字，否則老師可能不知道那是誰的作品。"},{"en":"This word warns about a bad result that may happen if advice is ignored.","zh":"這個字提醒如果忽視建議，可能會出現不良結果。"},{"en":"It is often used to connect an instruction with a consequence.","zh":"它常用來把指示與後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"come away from","meaning":"從……脫落","examples":[{"en":"The paper can come away from the cover if the spine is not supported.","zh":"如果書脊沒有支撐，紙張可能會從封面脫落。"},{"en":"To come away from something means to become detached or separated from it.","zh":"come away from something 指從某物上分離或脫落。"},{"en":"The label may come away from the bottle if it gets wet.","zh":"如果瓶子弄濕，標籤可能會從瓶身脫落。"},{"en":"If pages come away from a book cover, the book becomes harder to read and repair.","zh":"如果書頁從封面脫落，那本書會更難閱讀和修補。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something loosening from the thing it was attached to.","zh":"這個片語描述某物從原本附着的東西鬆開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pack them flat","meaning":"把它們平放打包","examples":[{"en":"Jane was told to pack the books flat in the box.","zh":"Jane 被告知要把書平放在箱內打包。"},{"en":"To pack books flat means to lay them horizontally rather than standing or leaning them.","zh":"pack books flat 指把書水平放置，而不是直立或斜放。"},{"en":"When storing heavy books, pack them flat so their covers do not bend.","zh":"存放厚重書本時，把它們平放打包，封面才不會彎曲。"},{"en":"Packing books flat can protect the spine and keep the pages even.","zh":"平放打包書本可以保護書脊並保持書頁平整。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a careful method of placing books in a box.","zh":"這個片語描述把書放進箱中的小心方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on their side","meaning":"側放","examples":[{"en":"Books should not be packed on their side.","zh":"書本不應側放打包。"},{"en":"On their side means resting sideways rather than lying flat or standing upright.","zh":"on their side 指側着放，而不是平放或直立。"},{"en":"If plates are stored on their side without support, they may slide and break.","zh":"如果碟子沒有支撐地側放，可能會滑落並破裂。"},{"en":"Books left on their side for a long time may bend under their own weight.","zh":"書本長時間側放，可能會因自身重量而彎曲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position and is often used when explaining storage.","zh":"這個片語描述位置，常用於解釋存放方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"leave them like that","meaning":"讓它們保持那樣","examples":[{"en":"If you leave books like that for a year, they may stay bent.","zh":"如果你讓書本保持那樣一年，它們可能會一直彎曲。"},{"en":"To leave them like that means to keep things in the same position or condition without changing them.","zh":"leave them like that 指不改變位置或狀態，讓東西保持原樣。"},{"en":"If you leave wet clothes like that overnight, they may smell bad.","zh":"如果你讓濕衣服那樣放一晚，它們可能會有異味。"},{"en":"Leaving books in a bad position for too long can cause lasting damage.","zh":"讓書本長時間保持不良位置，可能造成持久損害。"},{"en":"This phrase often warns that doing nothing may create a problem.","zh":"這個片語常提醒甚麼也不做可能造成問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"get something back to","meaning":"令某物恢復到……","examples":[{"en":"It is hard to get bent books back to their normal shape.","zh":"要令彎曲的書本恢復到原本形狀很困難。"},{"en":"To get something back to a state means to make it return to that condition.","zh":"get something back to a state 指令某物回復到某種狀態。"},{"en":"After a long illness, it may take weeks to get your energy back to normal.","zh":"長病後，可能需要幾星期才能令精力恢復正常。"},{"en":"Once paper is badly bent, it can be difficult to get it back to its original form.","zh":"紙張一旦嚴重彎曲，可能很難恢復原狀。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on restoring something after damage or change.","zh":"這個片語着重在受損或改變後恢復某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"normal shape","meaning":"原本形狀","examples":[{"en":"Books may not return to their normal shape after being bent for a long time.","zh":"書本長時間彎曲後，可能無法回復原本形狀。"},{"en":"Normal shape means the usual or original form something should have.","zh":"normal shape 指某物應有的平常或原本形態。"},{"en":"A plastic bottle may lose its normal shape if it is crushed in a schoolbag.","zh":"膠樽如果在書包中被壓扁，可能會失去原本形狀。"},{"en":"When books lose their normal shape, they may not close properly.","zh":"當書本失去原本形狀，它們可能無法正常合上。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing a damaged item with its original condition.","zh":"這個片語適合把受損物品與原本狀態作比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"it’s pretty clear that","meaning":"很明顯……","examples":[{"en":"It is pretty clear that poor storage can ruin books.","zh":"很明顯，存放不當可以把書弄壞。"},{"en":"It’s pretty clear that means it is quite obvious or easy to understand that something is true.","zh":"it’s pretty clear that 指某事相當明顯或容易理解為真。"},{"en":"It is pretty clear that the class needs more time because many students have not finished.","zh":"很明顯，這班需要更多時間，因為許多學生還未完成。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when the evidence strongly points to one conclusion.","zh":"當證據強烈指向一個結論時，人們會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It is less formal than “it is evident that” but still clear and confident.","zh":"它比 “it is evident that” 沒那麼正式，但仍清楚而有信心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ruin books","meaning":"把書弄壞","examples":[{"en":"Bending books for a long time can ruin them.","zh":"長時間把書弄彎可以把書弄壞。"},{"en":"To ruin books means to damage them so badly that they lose their good condition or usefulness.","zh":"ruin books 指嚴重損害書本，使其失去良好狀態或用途。"},{"en":"Leaving books in the rain can ruin them within minutes.","zh":"把書放在雨中，幾分鐘內就可以把它們弄壞。"},{"en":"Rough handling can ruin books by tearing pages, breaking spines, or staining covers.","zh":"粗暴處理會撕破書頁、弄斷書脊或弄污封面，從而把書弄壞。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that careless treatment can cause lasting harm.","zh":"這個片語提醒粗心對待會造成持久傷害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"can’t be bothered to","meaning":"懶得……","examples":[{"en":"Many people cannot be bothered to protect their books properly.","zh":"很多人懶得妥善保護自己的書。"},{"en":"Can’t be bothered to do something means being too lazy or unwilling to make the effort.","zh":"can’t be bothered to do something 指因懶惰或不願花力氣而不做某事。"},{"en":"Some students cannot be bothered to check their spelling before handing in homework.","zh":"有些學生懶得在交功課前檢查串字。"},{"en":"If people cannot be bothered to clean their room, small problems can quickly build up.","zh":"如果人們懶得清潔房間，小問題很快會累積。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often sounds critical.","zh":"這個片語較口語，通常帶批評意味。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"protect their books","meaning":"保護自己的書","examples":[{"en":"Some people cannot be bothered to protect their books.","zh":"有些人懶得保護自己的書。"},{"en":"To protect their books means to keep books safe from damage, dirt, moisture, or bending.","zh":"protect their books 指保護書本免受損壞、污漬、濕氣或彎曲。"},{"en":"Students can protect their books by using covers and keeping drinks away from them.","zh":"學生可以用書套並讓飲品遠離書本，以保護自己的書。"},{"en":"Protecting books helps them last longer and remain pleasant to read.","zh":"保護書本有助它們保存更久，並保持閱讀時舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on careful care rather than simply owning books.","zh":"這個片語着重小心保養，而不只是擁有書本。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"it’s such a shame that","meaning":"……真可惜","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather says it is such a shame that publishers do not use better paper.","zh":"Jane 的祖父說出版商不用更好的紙張真可惜。"},{"en":"It’s such a shame that means it is very unfortunate or disappointing that something happens.","zh":"it’s such a shame that 指某事發生非常可惜或令人失望。"},{"en":"It is such a shame that the library closes early when many students want to study.","zh":"很多學生想溫習，但圖書館很早關門，真可惜。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they feel a situation could have been better.","zh":"當人們覺得情況本來可以更好時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses regret or disappointment, not anger alone.","zh":"這個片語表達遺憾或失望，而不只是憤怒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"publishers","meaning":"出版商","examples":[{"en":"Some publishers do not use high-quality paper.","zh":"有些出版商不使用高質素紙張。"},{"en":"Publishers are companies or people who produce and sell books, magazines, or other written materials.","zh":"publishers 指製作並售賣書籍、雜誌或其他文字材料的公司或人士。"},{"en":"A publisher may work with writers, editors, designers, and printers to create a book.","zh":"出版商可能與作家、編輯、設計師和印刷商合作製作一本書。"},{"en":"Publishers choose paper, covers, fonts, and prices, so their decisions affect book quality.","zh":"出版商選擇紙張、封面、字體和價格，所以他們的決定影響書本質素。"},{"en":"This word refers to the people or organisations behind printed or digital publications.","zh":"這個字指印刷或數碼出版物背後的人或組織。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"better-quality paper","meaning":"較高質素的紙張","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather wishes publishers used better-quality paper.","zh":"Jane 的祖父希望出版商使用較高質素的紙張。"},{"en":"Better-quality paper is stronger, longer-lasting, and less likely to turn yellow or break.","zh":"better-quality paper 指更堅固、更耐用，並較不容易變黃或破裂的紙張。"},{"en":"Important certificates are often printed on better-quality paper so they can be kept for years.","zh":"重要證書常印在較高質素的紙張上，以便保存多年。"},{"en":"Books made with better paper may cost more, but they usually survive longer.","zh":"用較好紙張製作的書可能較貴，但通常保存更久。"},{"en":"This phrase compares paper by durability and appearance, not just thickness.","zh":"這個片語以耐用度和外觀比較紙張，而不只是厚度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the acid in the paper","meaning":"紙張中的酸性物質","examples":[{"en":"The acid in the paper causes old books to go yellow.","zh":"紙張中的酸性物質令舊書變黃。"},{"en":"The acid in the paper means chemical substances in paper that can slowly damage it over time.","zh":"the acid in the paper 指紙張中會隨時間慢慢損害紙張的化學物質。"},{"en":"Old newspapers often turn yellow because of acid in the paper.","zh":"舊報紙常因紙張中的酸性物質而變黃。"},{"en":"If paper contains too much acid, it may become brittle and break more easily.","zh":"如果紙張含太多酸性物質，它可能變脆並更容易破裂。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a hidden chemical reason for ageing paper.","zh":"這個片語解釋紙張老化背後隱藏的化學原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cause the problem","meaning":"造成問題","examples":[{"en":"The acid in the paper causes the problem.","zh":"紙張中的酸性物質造成這個問題。"},{"en":"To cause the problem means to be the reason why the problem happens.","zh":"cause the problem 指成為問題發生的原因。"},{"en":"In a classroom, poor ventilation can cause the problem of students feeling sleepy.","zh":"在課室中，通風差可能造成學生昏昏欲睡的問題。"},{"en":"Finding what causes a problem helps people choose the right solution.","zh":"找出造成問題的原因，有助人們選擇正確解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase links a difficulty to its source.","zh":"這個片語把困難與其來源連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"go yellow","meaning":"變黃","examples":[{"en":"Old books often go yellow because of the acid in the paper.","zh":"舊書常因紙張中的酸性物質而變黃。"},{"en":"To go yellow means to become yellow in colour over time.","zh":"go yellow 指隨時間變成黃色。"},{"en":"White shirts may go yellow if they are stored badly for many years.","zh":"白恤衫如果多年存放不當，可能會變黃。"},{"en":"Paper goes yellow when age, light, or chemicals change its colour.","zh":"紙張會因年歲、光線或化學物質而變黃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gradual change in appearance.","zh":"這個片語描述外觀上的逐漸變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"some of the books","meaning":"其中一些書","examples":[{"en":"Some of the books Jane’s grandfather gave her are already yellow.","zh":"Jane 的祖父給她的其中一些書已經變黃。"},{"en":"Some of the books means a portion of the books, not all of them.","zh":"some of the books 指部分書本，而不是全部。"},{"en":"Some of the books in the classroom library are new, but others are very old.","zh":"課室圖書館其中一些書是新的，但另一些很舊。"},{"en":"Saying “some of the books” helps show that only part of the collection has a problem.","zh":"說 “some of the books” 有助顯示只有部分藏書有問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about a group without including every item.","zh":"這個片語適合談及一組物品但不包括每一件時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"dump them","meaning":"把它們扔掉","examples":[{"en":"Jane thinks she should dump the books if they are going to deteriorate further.","zh":"Jane 覺得如果那些書會進一步變壞，她應該把它們扔掉。"},{"en":"To dump something means to throw it away, often carelessly or because it seems useless.","zh":"dump something 指把某物丟掉，通常較隨便或因覺得無用。"},{"en":"A student should not dump old textbooks if another student can still use them.","zh":"如果舊課本仍可給另一名學生使用，學生不應把它們扔掉。"},{"en":"Dumping books may save space, but it can feel wasteful if they have sentimental value.","zh":"扔掉書本可以節省空間，但如果它們有情感價值，就可能顯得浪費。"},{"en":"This word is informal and can sound a little harsh.","zh":"這個字較口語，聽起來可以有點粗魯。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"deteriorate further","meaning":"進一步變壞","examples":[{"en":"The old books may deteriorate further over time.","zh":"舊書可能隨時間進一步變壞。"},{"en":"To deteriorate further means to become even worse in condition.","zh":"deteriorate further 指狀態變得更差。"},{"en":"A damp wall will deteriorate further if no one repairs the leak.","zh":"如果沒有人修理漏水，潮濕牆壁會進一步變壞。"},{"en":"If old paper keeps breaking, the book may become impossible to read.","zh":"如果舊紙張一直碎裂，書本可能變得無法閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes worsening damage or quality.","zh":"這個片語描述損壞或質素惡化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"feel bad","meaning":"感到難過；感到內疚","examples":[{"en":"Jane would feel bad if she threw away her grandfather’s books.","zh":"如果 Jane 扔掉祖父的書，她會感到難過。"},{"en":"To feel bad means to feel guilty, sad, or uncomfortable about something.","zh":"feel bad 指對某事感到內疚、傷心或不舒服。"},{"en":"A student may feel bad after forgetting a friend’s birthday.","zh":"學生忘記朋友生日後，可能會感到內疚。"},{"en":"People feel bad when an action seems practical but emotionally wrong.","zh":"當某行動看似實際但情感上不對，人們會感到難過。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes guilt or regret in everyday situations.","zh":"這個片語常描述日常情況中的內疚或遺憾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"remind me of","meaning":"令我想起……","examples":[{"en":"The books will always remind Jane of her grandfather.","zh":"這些書永遠會令 Jane 想起她的祖父。"},{"en":"To remind someone of someone or something means to make them think about that person or thing.","zh":"remind someone of someone or something 指令某人想起某人或某事。"},{"en":"The smell of soup may remind a person of childhood dinners at home.","zh":"湯的氣味可能令一個人想起童年在家的晚餐。"},{"en":"Objects remind people of loved ones because they carry memories and emotions.","zh":"物件會令人想起摯愛的人，因為它們承載記憶和情感。"},{"en":"This phrase links a present thing with a memory.","zh":"這個片語把眼前事物與回憶連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"quite a collector","meaning":"很愛收藏的人","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather is quite a collector.","zh":"Jane 的祖父很愛收藏。"},{"en":"Quite a collector means someone who collects many things seriously or enthusiastically.","zh":"quite a collector 指認真或熱衷收藏許多物品的人。"},{"en":"My uncle is quite a collector of old coins and keeps them in careful albums.","zh":"我叔叔很愛收藏舊硬幣，並把它們小心放在收藏冊中。"},{"en":"A collector may spend years looking for rare items and protecting them properly.","zh":"收藏家可能花多年尋找罕有物品並妥善保護它們。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests admiration for someone’s strong collecting habit.","zh":"這個片語常暗示對某人強烈收藏習慣的欣賞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be important to","meaning":"對……很重要","examples":[{"en":"The books are important to Jane because they remind her of her grandfather.","zh":"這些書對 Jane 很重要，因為它們令她想起祖父。"},{"en":"To be important to someone means to have value, meaning, or emotional significance for that person.","zh":"be important to someone 指對某人有價值、意義或情感重要性。"},{"en":"A family photo may be important to a child who misses a parent.","zh":"對思念父母的孩子來說，家庭照片可能很重要。"},{"en":"Something can be important even if it is not expensive.","zh":"某物即使不昂貴，也可以很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase explains personal value rather than market value.","zh":"這個片語解釋個人價值，而不是市場價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"regret doing something","meaning":"後悔做某事","examples":[{"en":"Jane would regret throwing the books away.","zh":"Jane 會後悔扔掉那些書。"},{"en":"To regret doing something means to feel sorry later because you wish you had not done it.","zh":"regret doing something 指之後感到懊悔，因為希望自己沒有做某事。"},{"en":"A student may regret skipping revision when the exam is harder than expected.","zh":"如果考試比預期困難，學生可能後悔沒有溫習。"},{"en":"People often regret throwing away sentimental items after the memories become more important.","zh":"人們在回憶變得更重要後，常會後悔扔掉有情感價值的物品。"},{"en":"This phrase looks back at an action with sadness or guilt.","zh":"這個片語帶着傷心或內疚回望某行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"throw something away","meaning":"把某物丟掉","examples":[{"en":"Jane would regret throwing away the old books.","zh":"Jane 會後悔把那些舊書丟掉。"},{"en":"To throw something away means to put it in the rubbish or get rid of it.","zh":"throw something away 指把某物放進垃圾或處理掉。"},{"en":"Do not throw old notebooks away if the blank pages can still be used.","zh":"如果舊筆記簿仍有空白頁，不要把它們丟掉。"},{"en":"Throwing things away creates waste, so people may donate or recycle them instead.","zh":"丟掉東西會製造廢物，所以人們可能改為捐贈或回收。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on disposal, not storage or repair.","zh":"這個片語着重棄置，而不是存放或修補。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be taught to","meaning":"被教導要……","examples":[{"en":"Kieran was taught to treasure books.","zh":"Kieran 被教導要珍惜書本。"},{"en":"To be taught to do something means to be trained or guided to behave in that way.","zh":"be taught to do something 指被訓練或引導以某種方式行事。"},{"en":"Children are taught to say thank you when someone helps them.","zh":"孩子被教導在有人幫忙時要說謝謝。"},{"en":"What people are taught when young can shape their habits as adults.","zh":"人們年幼時被教導的事情可以塑造成年後的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on learning through guidance, not natural instinct alone.","zh":"這個片語着重透過指導學習，而不只是天生本能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"treasure books","meaning":"珍惜書本","examples":[{"en":"Kieran was taught to treasure books from a young age.","zh":"Kieran 從小就被教導要珍惜書本。"},{"en":"To treasure books means to value them highly and take good care of them.","zh":"treasure books 指高度重視書本並妥善照顧它們。"},{"en":"A reader who treasures books may avoid folding pages or writing carelessly in them.","zh":"珍惜書本的讀者可能避免摺頁或隨便在書上寫字。"},{"en":"When people treasure books, they are more likely to store and handle them properly.","zh":"當人們珍惜書本，他們更可能妥善存放和拿取它們。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests emotional respect as well as practical care.","zh":"這個片語暗示情感上的尊重和實際照顧。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hate seeing someone do something","meaning":"討厭看到某人做某事","examples":[{"en":"Kieran hates seeing students force open the pages of paperbacks.","zh":"Kieran 討厭看到學生用力撐開平裝書書頁。"},{"en":"To hate seeing someone do something means to feel upset or annoyed when watching that action.","zh":"hate seeing someone do something 指看到某人做某事時感到不快或惱怒。"},{"en":"A teacher may hate seeing students waste food after lunch.","zh":"老師可能討厭看到學生午餐後浪費食物。"},{"en":"People hate seeing careless behaviour when it damages something they value.","zh":"當粗心行為損害人們重視的東西，他們會討厭看到這種行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong negative reaction to another person’s action.","zh":"這個片語描述對他人行動的強烈負面反應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"force open","meaning":"用力撐開","examples":[{"en":"Some students force open the pages of paperbacks.","zh":"有些學生用力撐開平裝書的書頁。"},{"en":"To force something open means to open it with too much pressure or strength.","zh":"force something open 指用過大壓力或力量打開某物。"},{"en":"A child may force open a stuck drawer and break the handle.","zh":"孩子可能用力拉開卡住的抽屜，結果弄斷把手。"},{"en":"Forcing open a book can damage the spine and loosen the pages.","zh":"用力撐開書本會損害書脊並令書頁鬆脫。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests rough action rather than careful handling.","zh":"這個片語暗示粗暴行動，而不是小心處理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"paperbacks","meaning":"平裝書","examples":[{"en":"Paperbacks are not designed to last a long time.","zh":"平裝書並不是設計來長久保存的。"},{"en":"Paperbacks are books with soft paper covers rather than hard covers.","zh":"paperbacks 指封面較軟的書，而不是硬封面書。"},{"en":"Students often buy paperbacks because they are cheaper and lighter than hardbacks.","zh":"學生常買平裝書，因為它們比精裝書便宜和輕。"},{"en":"Paperbacks may bend or tear more easily if they are carried loosely in a bag.","zh":"如果平裝書在袋中隨便放置，可能更容易彎曲或撕裂。"},{"en":"This word names a type of book binding.","zh":"這個字命名一種書本裝訂形式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"press so hard that","meaning":"按得太用力以致……","examples":[{"en":"Some students press so hard that they break the spine.","zh":"有些學生按得太用力，以致弄斷書脊。"},{"en":"Press so hard that means apply so much pressure that a result happens.","zh":"press so hard that 指施加很大壓力，以致某結果發生。"},{"en":"A child may press so hard on a pencil that the tip breaks.","zh":"孩子可能按鉛筆按得太用力，以致筆尖斷掉。"},{"en":"Pressing too hard on a book can cause damage that cannot be repaired easily.","zh":"太用力按書本會造成不容易修復的損壞。"},{"en":"This structure links strong pressure with its consequence.","zh":"這個結構把強大壓力與其後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"end up doing something","meaning":"最後做了某事","examples":[{"en":"Students may end up breaking the spine of the book.","zh":"學生最後可能會弄斷書本的書脊。"},{"en":"To end up doing something means to finally do it, often unintentionally or after a series of actions.","zh":"end up doing something 指最後做了某事，通常不是本意或是在一連串行動後發生。"},{"en":"If you leave homework until midnight, you may end up making careless mistakes.","zh":"如果你把功課留到午夜才做，最後可能會犯粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"People may end up damaging books when they rush or handle them roughly.","zh":"人們趕急或粗暴處理書本時，最後可能會損壞它們。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes an unwanted final result.","zh":"這個片語常描述不想要的最終結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"break the spine","meaning":"弄斷書脊","examples":[{"en":"Pressing too hard can break the spine of a paperback.","zh":"按得太用力會弄斷平裝書的書脊。"},{"en":"To break the spine of a book means to damage the binding that holds the pages together.","zh":"break the spine of a book 指損壞固定書頁的裝訂部分。"},{"en":"A thick workbook may break its spine if students fold it backwards every day.","zh":"如果學生每天把厚工作簿向後摺，它可能會斷書脊。"},{"en":"Once the spine is broken, pages may begin to fall out.","zh":"書脊一旦斷裂，書頁可能開始掉出來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious damage to a book’s structure.","zh":"這個片語描述對書本結構的嚴重損害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"unfortunately","meaning":"不幸的是","examples":[{"en":"Unfortunately, paperbacks are not designed to last a long time.","zh":"不幸的是，平裝書並不是設計來長久保存的。"},{"en":"Unfortunately means sadly or regrettably.","zh":"unfortunately 指可惜地或令人遺憾地。"},{"en":"Unfortunately, the library is closed today because of a water leak.","zh":"不幸的是，圖書館今天因漏水而關閉。"},{"en":"Writers use this word before giving bad news or a disappointing fact.","zh":"作者在給出壞消息或令人失望的事實前會使用這個字。"},{"en":"This word helps soften a negative statement while still making it clear.","zh":"這個字有助柔化負面陳述，同時仍然清楚表達。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be designed to","meaning":"被設計來……","examples":[{"en":"Paperbacks are not designed to last a long time.","zh":"平裝書並不是設計來長久保存的。"},{"en":"To be designed to do something means to be made for that purpose.","zh":"be designed to do something 指為某用途而製造或設計。"},{"en":"A school bag is designed to carry books, not heavy tools.","zh":"書包是設計來裝書，而不是裝重工具。"},{"en":"If something is not designed for long use, it may wear out quickly.","zh":"如果某物不是設計來長期使用，它可能很快磨損。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the intended function of an object or system.","zh":"這個片語解釋物件或系統的原定功能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"last a long time","meaning":"持久保存","examples":[{"en":"Paperbacks are not designed to last a long time.","zh":"平裝書並不是設計來持久保存的。"},{"en":"To last a long time means to remain usable or in good condition for many years.","zh":"last a long time 指多年後仍然可用或保持良好狀態。"},{"en":"A good school desk should last a long time even if students use it every day.","zh":"好的學校書桌即使每天被學生使用，也應能持久使用。"},{"en":"Things last longer when they are made with stronger materials and handled carefully.","zh":"物品若用更堅固材料製成並小心處理，便能保存更久。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on durability.","zh":"這個片語着重耐用程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hardbacks","meaning":"精裝書","examples":[{"en":"Hardbacks are not quite as weak as paperbacks.","zh":"精裝書沒有平裝書那麼脆弱。"},{"en":"Hardbacks are books with stiff, hard covers that protect the pages better.","zh":"hardbacks 指有堅硬封面的書，能更好地保護書頁。"},{"en":"Libraries often buy hardbacks because they can survive repeated borrowing.","zh":"圖書館常買精裝書，因為它們能承受反覆借閱。"},{"en":"Hardbacks usually cost more, but they may last longer than paperbacks.","zh":"精裝書通常較貴，但可能比平裝書更耐用。"},{"en":"This word names a type of book binding with a stronger cover.","zh":"這個字命名一種有較堅固封面的書本裝訂形式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not quite as weak","meaning":"沒有那麼脆弱","examples":[{"en":"Hardbacks are not quite as weak as paperbacks.","zh":"精裝書沒有平裝書那麼脆弱。"},{"en":"Not quite as weak means a little stronger or less fragile than something else.","zh":"not quite as weak 指比另一物稍強或較不易壞。"},{"en":"A metal lunchbox is not quite as weak as a paper bag.","zh":"金屬飯盒沒有紙袋那麼脆弱。"},{"en":"If an object is not as weak, it may still need care but can survive more use.","zh":"如果物品沒有那麼脆弱，它仍需要小心處理，但能承受更多使用。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a careful comparison rather than saying something is very strong.","zh":"這個片語作出謹慎比較，而不是說某物非常堅固。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"I suppose","meaning":"我想；我覺得","examples":[{"en":"Hardbacks are different, I suppose.","zh":"我想，精裝書是不同的。"},{"en":"I suppose means I think so, though I am not completely certain or strongly committed.","zh":"I suppose 指我認為如此，但不完全肯定或語氣不太強。"},{"en":"I suppose we could study in the library if the classroom is too noisy.","zh":"如果課室太嘈，我想我們可以在圖書館溫習。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when giving a mild opinion or accepting a point.","zh":"人們提出溫和意見或接受某點時會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It makes a statement sound softer and less forceful.","zh":"它令陳述聽起來較柔和，沒那麼強硬。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"value something like they used to","meaning":"像以前那樣重視……","examples":[{"en":"People do not value hardbacks like they used to.","zh":"人們不再像以前那樣重視精裝書。"},{"en":"To value something like they used to means to appreciate or respect it as much as people did in the past.","zh":"value something like they used to 指像過去那樣欣賞或重視某物。"},{"en":"Some people do not value handwritten letters like they used to because messages are now instant.","zh":"由於現在訊息即時傳送，有些人不再像以前那樣重視手寫信。"},{"en":"When habits change, objects once admired may seem less important.","zh":"當習慣改變，曾經受重視的物品可能顯得沒那麼重要。"},{"en":"This phrase compares present attitudes with past attitudes.","zh":"這個片語比較現在與過去的態度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"decorative","meaning":"有裝飾性的","examples":[{"en":"Hardbacks are not as decorative as some other objects.","zh":"精裝書不如某些其他物品有裝飾性。"},{"en":"Decorative means attractive and used to make a place look nicer.","zh":"decorative 指外觀吸引，並用來令地方更好看。"},{"en":"A vase can be decorative even if it is not used every day.","zh":"花瓶即使不是每天使用，也可以有裝飾性。"},{"en":"If books are seen as decorative, people may display them on shelves instead of hiding them away.","zh":"如果書被視為有裝飾性，人們可能會把它們放在書架上展示，而不是收起來。"},{"en":"This word describes appearance and visual value.","zh":"這個字描述外觀和視覺價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"other objects","meaning":"其他物品","examples":[{"en":"Books are not always seen as decorative like other objects.","zh":"書本不一定像其他物品那樣被視為有裝飾性。"},{"en":"Other objects means different things apart from the one already mentioned.","zh":"other objects 指除了已提及物品外的不同東西。"},{"en":"A shelf may hold books, photos, plants, and other objects.","zh":"書架上可能有書、照片、植物和其他物品。"},{"en":"Comparing books with other objects helps show how people use them in the home.","zh":"把書與其他物品比較，有助顯示人們如何在家中使用它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is general and depends on the context.","zh":"這個片語較籠統，意思取決於語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"plus","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"Plus, people do not keep books out on shelves as much as they used to.","zh":"此外，人們不再像以前那樣多把書擺放在書架上展示。"},{"en":"Plus means also or in addition.","zh":"plus 指此外或另外。"},{"en":"The library is quiet; plus, it has comfortable chairs and free Wi-Fi.","zh":"圖書館很安靜；此外，它有舒適椅子和免費 Wi-Fi。"},{"en":"People use “plus” to add another reason in a casual way.","zh":"人們用 “plus” 以較口語方式加入另一個理由。"},{"en":"This word is common in spoken explanations and informal writing.","zh":"這個字常見於口頭解釋和非正式寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"keep books out on shelves","meaning":"把書擺放在書架上展示","examples":[{"en":"People do not keep hardbacks out on shelves as much as before.","zh":"人們不再像以前那樣多把精裝書擺放在書架上展示。"},{"en":"To keep books out on shelves means to leave books visible and displayed on shelves.","zh":"keep books out on shelves 指把書留在書架上可見地展示。"},{"en":"A family may keep favourite books out on shelves so guests can see and borrow them.","zh":"家庭可能把最喜愛的書擺放在書架上展示，讓客人看見和借閱。"},{"en":"Books kept out on shelves can make a room feel warm, thoughtful, and lived-in.","zh":"擺放在書架上的書可以令房間感覺溫暖、有思想和有生活感。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts display with storing books away in boxes or cupboards.","zh":"這個片語把展示與把書收進箱子或櫃子作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as much as they used to","meaning":"像以前那樣多","examples":[{"en":"People do not display books as much as they used to.","zh":"人們不再像以前那樣多展示書本。"},{"en":"As much as they used to means to the same degree or frequency as in the past.","zh":"as much as they used to 指與過去相同程度或頻率。"},{"en":"Many children do not write letters as much as they used to because they send messages online.","zh":"許多兒童不再像以前那樣多寫信，因為他們在網上傳訊息。"},{"en":"When lifestyles change, old habits may happen less often than before.","zh":"當生活方式改變，舊習慣可能比以前少出現。"},{"en":"This phrase compares present behaviour with past behaviour.","zh":"這個片語比較現在與過去的行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"that’s such a pity","meaning":"那真可惜","examples":[{"en":"Kieran thinks it is such a pity that people display fewer books now.","zh":"Kieran 覺得現在人們展示較少書本真可惜。"},{"en":"That’s such a pity means that is very unfortunate or disappointing.","zh":"that’s such a pity 指那非常可惜或令人失望。"},{"en":"It is such a pity that the school garden is closed during spring.","zh":"學校花園春天關閉真可惜。"},{"en":"People say this when they feel something valuable has been lost or reduced.","zh":"當人們覺得有價值的東西已失去或減少，會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses regret in a gentle way.","zh":"這個片語以溫和方式表達遺憾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be drawn to","meaning":"被……吸引","examples":[{"en":"Kieran is drawn to a colourful book when he visits someone’s home.","zh":"Kieran 到訪別人家時，會被色彩繽紛的書吸引。"},{"en":"To be drawn to something means to feel attracted to it.","zh":"be drawn to something 指被某物吸引。"},{"en":"A child may be drawn to a bright picture book in the library.","zh":"孩子可能會被圖書館中一本鮮艷圖畫書吸引。"},{"en":"People are often drawn to objects that look beautiful, unusual, or personally meaningful.","zh":"人們常被美麗、特別或有個人意義的物件吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attraction that feels natural or immediate.","zh":"這個片語描述自然或即時產生的吸引力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"book covers","meaning":"書封","examples":[{"en":"Book covers can be a work of art in themselves.","zh":"書封本身可以是一件藝術品。"},{"en":"Book covers are the outer parts of books that protect the pages and show the title or design.","zh":"book covers 指書本外部保護書頁並顯示書名或設計的部分。"},{"en":"A colourful book cover can make a child pick up a book before reading the first page.","zh":"色彩繽紛的書封可以令孩子在讀第一頁前先拿起一本書。"},{"en":"Good book covers help readers guess the mood, topic, or style of a book.","zh":"好書封幫助讀者猜測書本的氣氛、主題或風格。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to both protection and visual design.","zh":"這個片語同時指保護和視覺設計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a work of art in itself","meaning":"本身就是一件藝術品","examples":[{"en":"A beautiful book cover can be a work of art in itself.","zh":"美麗的書封本身可以是一件藝術品。"},{"en":"A work of art in itself means something is beautiful or creative enough to be valued on its own.","zh":"a work of art in itself 指某物本身已足夠美麗或有創意，值得被欣賞。"},{"en":"A well-designed school poster can be a work of art in itself.","zh":"設計精美的學校海報本身也可以是一件藝術品。"},{"en":"When a cover is a work of art, people may admire it even before reading the book.","zh":"當封面本身是藝術品，人們可能在閱讀前已欣賞它。"},{"en":"This phrase praises the object’s independent artistic value.","zh":"這個片語讚賞物件本身獨立的藝術價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"eye-catching","meaning":"搶眼的；吸引目光的","examples":[{"en":"Some book covers are really eye-catching.","zh":"有些書封真的很搶眼。"},{"en":"Eye-catching means visually attractive and easy to notice.","zh":"eye-catching 指視覺上吸引，而且容易被注意到。"},{"en":"An eye-catching poster can make students stop and read about a school event.","zh":"搶眼的海報可以令學生停下來閱讀學校活動資料。"},{"en":"Bright colours, bold pictures, and unusual designs can make something eye-catching.","zh":"鮮艷顏色、大膽圖片和特別設計可以令某物吸引目光。"},{"en":"This word is often used for designs, adverts, clothes, and displays.","zh":"這個字常用於設計、廣告、衣服和展示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"handle books carefully","meaning":"小心拿書","examples":[{"en":"Kieran has always been taught to handle books carefully.","zh":"Kieran 一直被教導要小心拿書。"},{"en":"To handle books carefully means to touch, hold, open, and move books without damaging them.","zh":"handle books carefully 指以不損壞書本的方式觸摸、握住、翻開和移動書本。"},{"en":"Students should handle library books carefully because many people will borrow them later.","zh":"學生應小心拿圖書館書，因為之後還有很多人會借閱。"},{"en":"Careful handling can prevent torn pages, broken spines, and dirty covers.","zh":"小心處理可以防止書頁撕裂、書脊斷裂和封面變髒。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on respectful physical treatment of books.","zh":"這個片語着重對書本的尊重式實體處理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take a book off a shelf","meaning":"從書架上取書","examples":[{"en":"Many people take a book off a shelf in the wrong way.","zh":"很多人用錯方法從書架上取書。"},{"en":"To take a book off a shelf means to remove a book from where it is standing or lying on a shelf.","zh":"take a book off a shelf 指把書從書架上直立或平放的位置取下。"},{"en":"A librarian may show children how to take a book off a shelf without pulling the top of the spine.","zh":"圖書館員可能示範如何不拉書脊頂部而從書架上取書。"},{"en":"Taking books off shelves roughly can damage both the book and nearby books.","zh":"粗暴地從書架上取書會損壞該書和旁邊的書。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common action that can be done carefully or carelessly.","zh":"這個片語描述一個可以小心或粗心完成的常見動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"do it wrong","meaning":"做錯；用錯方法","examples":[{"en":"People often do it wrong when taking books off a shelf.","zh":"人們從書架上取書時常用錯方法。"},{"en":"To do it wrong means to perform an action in an incorrect or unsuitable way.","zh":"do it wrong 指以不正確或不合適方式做某事。"},{"en":"Students may do the experiment wrong if they skip the instructions.","zh":"如果學生跳過指示，可能會做錯實驗。"},{"en":"Doing something wrong can create damage even when the task seems simple.","zh":"即使任務看似簡單，用錯方法也可能造成損害。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and direct.","zh":"這個片語較口語而直接。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put your hand over","meaning":"把手放在……上方","examples":[{"en":"You should put your hand over the top of the book.","zh":"你應把手放在書本上方。"},{"en":"To put your hand over something means to place your hand above or across it.","zh":"put your hand over something 指把手放在某物上方或覆蓋其上。"},{"en":"A teacher may put her hand over a child’s hand to guide the correct pencil movement.","zh":"老師可能把手放在孩子手上，引導正確握筆動作。"},{"en":"Putting your hand over the top of a book helps you hold it more securely.","zh":"把手放在書本上方有助你更穩固地握住它。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a physical instruction about hand position.","zh":"這個片語給出關於手部位置的實體指示。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"right over the top of","meaning":"正正放在……上方","examples":[{"en":"You should put your hand right over the top of the book.","zh":"你應把手正正放在書本上方。"},{"en":"Right over the top of means directly above or covering the upper part of something.","zh":"right over the top of 指正正在某物上方或覆蓋其上部。"},{"en":"Put the label right over the top of the box so people can read it easily.","zh":"把標籤正正貼在盒子上方，讓人容易閱讀。"},{"en":"Placing your hand right over the top gives better control when pulling a book out.","zh":"把手正正放在書本上方，可以在抽出書本時有更好控制。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the position more exact than simply saying “over”.","zh":"這個片語比單純說 “over” 更準確描述位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pull the other books aside","meaning":"把其他書拉到一旁","examples":[{"en":"You can pull the other books aside to hold the whole cover.","zh":"你可以把其他書拉到一旁，以握住整個封面。"},{"en":"To pull the other books aside means to move nearby books slightly away to make space.","zh":"pull the other books aside 指把旁邊的書稍微移開，騰出空間。"},{"en":"A student may pull other folders aside to reach the notebook at the back of a shelf.","zh":"學生可能把其他文件夾拉到一旁，以拿到書架後面的筆記本。"},{"en":"Moving other books aside prevents you from dragging one book out by its spine.","zh":"把其他書移開可以防止你拉着書脊把一本書拖出來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a careful action before removing a book.","zh":"這個片語描述取書前的小心動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hold the whole cover","meaning":"握住整個封面","examples":[{"en":"You should hold the whole cover when taking a book off a shelf.","zh":"從書架上取書時，你應握住整個封面。"},{"en":"To hold the whole cover means to grip the front and back cover firmly rather than pulling one small part.","zh":"hold the whole cover 指穩固握住前後封面，而不是只拉一小部分。"},{"en":"When taking a heavy atlas down, hold the whole cover so the binding is supported.","zh":"取下厚重地圖集時，要握住整個封面，讓裝訂部分有支撐。"},{"en":"Holding the whole cover spreads the pressure and reduces damage to the spine.","zh":"握住整個封面可以分散壓力並減少對書脊的損害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a careful way to handle books.","zh":"這個片語描述小心處理書本的方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"learn all this","meaning":"學會這一切","examples":[{"en":"Kieran asks Jane when she learned all this about handling books.","zh":"Kieran 問 Jane 何時學會這一切關於拿書的方法。"},{"en":"To learn all this means to acquire all the information or skills just mentioned.","zh":"learn all this 指學到剛才提及的所有資料或技能。"},{"en":"A student may ask a classmate where she learned all this about essay writing.","zh":"學生可能問同學在哪裡學會這一切關於寫文章的方法。"},{"en":"People often learn careful habits after making a mistake or being taught by someone experienced.","zh":"人們常在犯錯後或由有經驗的人教導後學會小心習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a set of knowledge, not one isolated fact.","zh":"這個片語指回一整套知識，而不是單一事實。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pull a heavy book off the shelf","meaning":"從書架上拉下一本厚重的書","examples":[{"en":"Jane once pulled a heavy book off the shelf when she was small.","zh":"Jane 小時候曾從書架上拉下一本厚重的書。"},{"en":"To pull a heavy book off the shelf means to remove a large or weighty book by pulling it from the shelf.","zh":"pull a heavy book off the shelf 指把一本大型或沉重的書從書架上拉下。"},{"en":"A child should ask for help before pulling a heavy book off a high shelf.","zh":"孩子從高書架上拉下厚重書本前，應請人幫忙。"},{"en":"Pulling a heavy book too quickly can make it fall and hurt someone.","zh":"太快拉下厚重書本，可能令它跌下並弄傷人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical action that needs care.","zh":"這個片語描述需要小心的實體動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fall on the floor","meaning":"掉到地上","examples":[{"en":"The heavy book fell on the floor and broke apart.","zh":"那本厚重的書掉到地上並散開了。"},{"en":"To fall on the floor means to drop from a higher place onto the ground indoors.","zh":"fall on the floor 指從較高位置掉到室內地面上。"},{"en":"A glass may fall on the floor if it is placed too close to the edge of a desk.","zh":"如果玻璃杯放得太近桌邊，可能會掉到地上。"},{"en":"Heavy objects can be damaged or cause injury when they fall on the floor.","zh":"厚重物件掉到地上時可能受損或令人受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where something lands after falling.","zh":"這個片語描述某物跌落後落在哪裡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"break apart","meaning":"散開；裂開","examples":[{"en":"The heavy book broke apart when it fell on the floor.","zh":"那本厚重的書掉到地上時散開了。"},{"en":"To break apart means to separate into pieces or sections because of damage.","zh":"break apart 指因損壞而分成幾部分或裂開。"},{"en":"An old toy may break apart if a child pulls it too hard.","zh":"如果孩子太用力拉舊玩具，它可能會散開。"},{"en":"When a book breaks apart, the cover, spine, and pages may separate.","zh":"當一本書散開，封面、書脊和書頁可能會分離。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious physical damage.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重實體損壞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"oh dear","meaning":"天啊；哎呀","examples":[{"en":"Kieran says “Oh dear” when he hears about the damaged book.","zh":"Kieran 聽到那本書被損壞時說：「哎呀。」"},{"en":"Oh dear is an expression used when something unfortunate, worrying, or disappointing happens.","zh":"oh dear 是在不幸、令人擔心或令人失望的事情發生時使用的表達。"},{"en":"“Oh dear,” the teacher said when the projector stopped working.","zh":"投影機停止運作時，老師說：「哎呀。」"},{"en":"People use this phrase to show concern without sounding too dramatic.","zh":"人們用這個片語表達關心，但不會聽起來太誇張。"},{"en":"It is gentle and often used in British English.","zh":"它語氣溫和，常見於英式英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"I can still remember it","meaning":"我到現在還記得","examples":[{"en":"Jane can still remember the accident with the heavy book.","zh":"Jane 到現在還記得那次厚重書本的意外。"},{"en":"I can still remember it means the memory remains clear even after time has passed.","zh":"I can still remember it 指即使時間過去，記憶仍然清楚。"},{"en":"I can still remember my first day at school because I was so nervous.","zh":"我到現在還記得上學第一天，因為當時很緊張。"},{"en":"Strong emotions or surprising events often make memories last longer.","zh":"強烈情緒或令人驚訝的事件常令記憶維持更久。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that something was memorable.","zh":"這個片語強調某事令人難忘。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the smell of new books","meaning":"新書的氣味","examples":[{"en":"Kieran really likes the smell of new books.","zh":"Kieran 很喜歡新書的氣味。"},{"en":"The smell of new books means the fresh paper, ink, and binding smell that new books have.","zh":"the smell of new books 指新書帶有的新鮮紙張、油墨和裝訂氣味。"},{"en":"Some readers enjoy the smell of new books when they walk into a bookshop.","zh":"有些讀者走進書店時，喜歡聞到新書的氣味。"},{"en":"Smells can create strong memories because they are linked to places and experiences.","zh":"氣味可以製造強烈記憶，因為它們與地方和經歷相連。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sensory pleasure connected with reading.","zh":"這個片語描述與閱讀相關的感官樂趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"me too","meaning":"我也是","examples":[{"en":"Jane says she likes the smell of new books too.","zh":"Jane 說她也喜歡新書的氣味。"},{"en":"Me too means I feel the same way or the same thing is true for me.","zh":"me too 指我也有同樣感受，或同樣事情也適用於我。"},{"en":"“I love reading in quiet cafés.” “Me too.”","zh":"「我喜歡在安靜咖啡店閱讀。」「我也是。」"},{"en":"People use this phrase to show agreement or shared feeling.","zh":"人們用這個片語表示同意或共同感受。"},{"en":"It is short, casual, and very common in conversation.","zh":"它簡短、口語，而且在對話中非常常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"used to laugh at me","meaning":"以前常常取笑我","examples":[{"en":"Kieran’s parents used to laugh at him when he was a child.","zh":"Kieran 小時候，他的父母以前常常取笑他。"},{"en":"Used to laugh at me means people often laughed at me in the past.","zh":"used to laugh at me 指人們過去經常取笑我。"},{"en":"My classmates used to laugh at me for carrying too many books.","zh":"我的同學以前常常取笑我帶太多書。"},{"en":"People may laugh at unusual habits before understanding why they matter.","zh":"人們可能在理解某習慣的重要性前，先取笑它不尋常。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated past action that no longer happens in the same way.","zh":"這個片語描述過去重複發生、現在不再同樣發生的行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"when I was a kid","meaning":"我小時候","examples":[{"en":"Kieran loved smelling books when he was a kid.","zh":"Kieran 小時候很喜歡聞書。"},{"en":"When I was a kid means during the time when I was a child.","zh":"when I was a kid 指我還是小孩的時候。"},{"en":"When I was a kid, I borrowed picture books from the library every week.","zh":"我小時候每星期都從圖書館借圖畫書。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to introduce childhood memories or habits.","zh":"人們用這個片語引入童年回憶或習慣。"},{"en":"It is more casual than “when I was a child”.","zh":"它比 “when I was a child” 更口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"put books up to my nose","meaning":"把書拿到鼻子前","examples":[{"en":"Kieran loved putting books up to his nose.","zh":"Kieran 很喜歡把書拿到鼻子前。"},{"en":"To put books up to my nose means to lift books close to my nose, usually to smell them.","zh":"put books up to my nose 指把書拿近鼻子，通常是為了聞它們。"},{"en":"A child may put a flower up to her nose to smell it more clearly.","zh":"孩子可能把花拿到鼻子前，以更清楚聞到香味。"},{"en":"People bring objects close to their nose when the smell is part of the enjoyment.","zh":"當氣味是享受的一部分，人們會把物件拿近鼻子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical action linked to scent.","zh":"這個片語描述與氣味相關的實體動作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"almost as much as","meaning":"幾乎和……一樣多","examples":[{"en":"Kieran liked smelling books almost as much as reading them.","zh":"Kieran 喜歡聞書，幾乎和喜歡讀書一樣多。"},{"en":"Almost as much as means nearly the same amount or degree as something else.","zh":"almost as much as 指數量或程度幾乎與另一事物相同。"},{"en":"Some children enjoy choosing books almost as much as reading them.","zh":"有些孩子喜歡選書，幾乎和喜歡閱讀一樣多。"},{"en":"If someone likes one activity almost as much as another, both are important to them.","zh":"如果某人喜歡一項活動幾乎和另一項一樣多，兩者對他都很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two pleasures or amounts that are very close.","zh":"這個片語比較兩種非常接近的樂趣或數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"aren’t cheap","meaning":"並不便宜","examples":[{"en":"New books are not cheap.","zh":"新書並不便宜。"},{"en":"Aren’t cheap means cost a lot of money or are not inexpensive.","zh":"aren’t cheap 指價錢高或不算便宜。"},{"en":"University textbooks are not cheap, so students often buy second-hand copies.","zh":"大學課本並不便宜，所以學生常買二手本。"},{"en":"When books are expensive, people may borrow them from libraries instead of buying them.","zh":"當書本昂貴，人們可能從圖書館借閱，而不是購買。"},{"en":"This phrase is a simple way to say something is costly.","zh":"這個片語是表達某物昂貴的簡單說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"I guess we’re lucky","meaning":"我想我們很幸運","examples":[{"en":"Kieran thinks they are lucky because they can buy new books.","zh":"Kieran 覺得他們很幸運，因為他們可以買新書。"},{"en":"I guess we’re lucky means I think we should feel grateful because our situation is better than some people’s.","zh":"I guess we’re lucky 指我想我們應該感恩，因為我們的情況比某些人好。"},{"en":"I guess we’re lucky to have a library near home.","zh":"我想我們很幸運，家附近有圖書館。"},{"en":"People say this when they realise something normal to them may not be available to everyone.","zh":"當人們意識到自己覺得平常的東西未必人人都有時，會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses mild gratitude and reflection.","zh":"這個片語表達溫和的感恩和反思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stock second-hand books","meaning":"備有二手書","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather stocks second-hand books as well as new ones.","zh":"Jane 的祖父備有二手書，也有新書。"},{"en":"To stock second-hand books means to keep used books in a shop for customers to buy.","zh":"stock second-hand books 指店舖備有舊書供顧客購買。"},{"en":"A small bookshop may stock second-hand books to help students save money.","zh":"小書店可能備有二手書，以幫助學生省錢。"},{"en":"Stocking used books can attract readers who want rare, cheaper, or out-of-print titles.","zh":"備有舊書可以吸引想找罕有、較便宜或絕版書的讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what a shop keeps for sale.","zh":"這個片語描述店舖備有甚麼出售。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"以及；也","examples":[{"en":"The bookshop stocks second-hand books as well as new ones.","zh":"這間書店備有二手書以及新書。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to or also.","zh":"as well as 指除了……之外，也包括……。"},{"en":"The school library has magazines as well as novels.","zh":"學校圖書館有雜誌，也有小說。"},{"en":"Offering old books as well as new books gives customers more choice.","zh":"同時提供舊書和新書，可以給顧客更多選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another item without replacing the first one.","zh":"這個片語加入另一項目，而不是取代第一項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"second-hand books","meaning":"二手書","examples":[{"en":"Second-hand books do not smell quite as good as new books.","zh":"二手書的氣味不如新書那麼好。"},{"en":"Second-hand books are books that have been owned or used by someone before.","zh":"second-hand books 指之前已被別人擁有或使用過的書。"},{"en":"Students often buy second-hand books because they are cheaper than new copies.","zh":"學生常買二手書，因為它們比新書便宜。"},{"en":"Second-hand books may contain notes, marks, or signs of past readers.","zh":"二手書可能有筆記、標記或過往讀者留下的痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to used books, not fake or damaged books necessarily.","zh":"這個片語指舊書，不一定是假書或損壞書。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not quite as good","meaning":"沒有那麼好","examples":[{"en":"Second-hand books do not smell quite as good as new books.","zh":"二手書聞起來沒有新書那麼好。"},{"en":"Not quite as good means a little less good than something else.","zh":"not quite as good 指比另一樣東西稍為差一點。"},{"en":"The school lunch is not quite as good as home cooking, but it is convenient.","zh":"學校午餐沒有家中煮食那麼好，但很方便。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when making a gentle comparison rather than harsh criticism.","zh":"人們作溫和比較而非嚴厲批評時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It suggests the thing is acceptable, but not at the same level.","zh":"它暗示某物可以接受，但不在同一水平。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"I’d love to","meaning":"我很想……","examples":[{"en":"Kieran would love to have a bookshop like Jane’s grandfather.","zh":"Kieran 很想擁有像 Jane 祖父那樣的書店。"},{"en":"I’d love to means I would really like to do or have something.","zh":"I’d love to 指我真的很想做某事或擁有某物。"},{"en":"I’d love to visit that old library during the holiday.","zh":"我很想在假期參觀那間舊圖書館。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to express strong interest or desire politely.","zh":"人們用這個片語有禮地表達強烈興趣或願望。"},{"en":"It sounds warmer than simply saying “I want to”.","zh":"它比單純說 “I want to” 更溫暖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"what’s it like?","meaning":"它是怎樣的？","examples":[{"en":"Kieran asks Jane what her grandfather’s bookshop is like.","zh":"Kieran 問 Jane 她祖父的書店是怎樣的。"},{"en":"What’s it like? asks someone to describe the character, appearance, or feeling of something.","zh":"what’s it like? 用來請某人描述某物的特色、外觀或感覺。"},{"en":"If a friend studies abroad, you may ask, “What’s it like living there?”","zh":"如果朋友在海外讀書，你可能問：「住在那裡是怎樣的？」"},{"en":"This question invites description rather than a yes-or-no answer.","zh":"這個問題邀請對方描述，而不是回答是或不是。"},{"en":"It is useful when you want to imagine a place or experience.","zh":"當你想想像某地方或經歷時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"two floors and an attic","meaning":"兩層樓和一個閣樓","examples":[{"en":"The bookshop has two floors and an attic.","zh":"這間書店有兩層樓和一個閣樓。"},{"en":"Two floors and an attic means the building has two main levels plus a small space under the roof.","zh":"two floors and an attic 指建築物有兩個主要樓層，另有屋頂下的小空間。"},{"en":"A house with two floors and an attic may have bedrooms upstairs and storage above.","zh":"有兩層樓和一個閣樓的房子，樓上可能有睡房，頂部則用作儲物。"},{"en":"Extra space such as an attic can help a shop store more books.","zh":"閣樓等額外空間可以幫助店舖存放更多書。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical structure of a building.","zh":"這個片語描述建築物的實體結構。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stock all kinds of","meaning":"備有各式各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather stocks all kinds of books.","zh":"Jane 的祖父備有各式各樣的書。"},{"en":"To stock all kinds of something means to keep many different types available for customers.","zh":"stock all kinds of something 指備有許多不同種類供顧客選擇。"},{"en":"A stationery shop may stock all kinds of pens, notebooks, and folders.","zh":"文具店可能備有各式各樣的筆、筆記簿和文件夾。"},{"en":"Stocking many types of books helps a bookshop serve children, students, collectors, and casual readers.","zh":"備有多種書籍有助書店服務兒童、學生、收藏家和普通讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises variety.","zh":"這個片語強調多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"first editions","meaning":"初版書","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather treasures first editions and other rare books.","zh":"Jane 的祖父珍惜初版書和其他珍本書。"},{"en":"First editions are the first printed versions of a book when it is originally published.","zh":"first editions 指一本書最初出版時的第一批印刷版本。"},{"en":"Collectors may pay more for first editions because they are historically important.","zh":"收藏家可能為初版書付更多錢，因為它們有歷史價值。"},{"en":"A first edition can become valuable if the author later becomes famous.","zh":"如果作者後來成名，初版書可能變得有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in book collecting and publishing.","zh":"這個片語常見於藏書和出版語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rare books","meaning":"珍本書；罕有書籍","examples":[{"en":"The bookshop has first editions and other rare books.","zh":"這間書店有初版書和其他珍本書。"},{"en":"Rare books are books that are hard to find because they are old, limited, special, or valuable.","zh":"rare books 指因年代久遠、數量有限、特別或有價值而難以找到的書。"},{"en":"A library may keep rare books in a special room to protect them from damage.","zh":"圖書館可能把珍本書放在特別房間，以保護它們免受損壞。"},{"en":"Rare books can attract collectors who are looking for unusual editions.","zh":"珍本書可以吸引尋找特別版本的收藏家。"},{"en":"This phrase describes books that are not commonly available.","zh":"這個片語描述不常見的書籍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"you might think","meaning":"你可能會以為……","examples":[{"en":"You might think he would keep the rare books in the attic.","zh":"你可能會以為他會把珍本書放在閣樓。"},{"en":"You might think means it may seem reasonable to believe something at first.","zh":"you might think 指一開始相信某事似乎合理。"},{"en":"You might think the cheapest bag is the best choice, but it may break quickly.","zh":"你可能會以為最便宜的袋是最佳選擇，但它可能很快破裂。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase before correcting an assumption.","zh":"作者在修正一個假設前會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It prepares the reader for a contrast or surprise.","zh":"它為讀者準備一個對比或驚喜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"keep something in the attic","meaning":"把某物放在閣樓","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather does not keep the rare books hidden in the attic.","zh":"Jane 的祖父沒有把珍本書藏在閣樓。"},{"en":"To keep something in the attic means to store it in the space under the roof.","zh":"keep something in the attic 指把某物存放在屋頂下方的空間。"},{"en":"Families often keep old toys and suitcases in the attic.","zh":"家庭常把舊玩具和行李箱放在閣樓。"},{"en":"Keeping valuable books in an attic may be risky if the space is hot, dusty, or damp.","zh":"如果閣樓炎熱、滿佈塵埃或潮濕，把珍貴書籍放在那裡可能有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a storage location.","zh":"這個片語描述存放位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be hidden","meaning":"被藏起來","examples":[{"en":"Kieran thinks the rare books might be hidden in the attic.","zh":"Kieran 以為珍本書可能被藏在閣樓。"},{"en":"To be hidden means to be kept where people cannot easily see or find something.","zh":"be hidden 指被放在別人不容易看見或找到的地方。"},{"en":"The spare keys are hidden inside a small box near the door.","zh":"備用鑰匙被藏在門旁的小盒子裡。"},{"en":"Valuable items may be hidden to protect them from theft.","zh":"有價值物品可能被藏起來，以防被盜。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on being out of sight.","zh":"這個片語着重不被看見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"like people to know that","meaning":"喜歡讓別人知道……","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather likes people to know that he has rare books.","zh":"Jane 的祖父喜歡讓別人知道他有珍本書。"},{"en":"To like people to know that means to want others to be aware of a fact.","zh":"like people to know that 指希望其他人知道某個事實。"},{"en":"A school may like parents to know that it has a new library.","zh":"學校可能喜歡讓家長知道它有新圖書館。"},{"en":"If customers know a shop has rare books, collectors may visit more often.","zh":"如果顧客知道店舖有珍本書，收藏家可能更常到訪。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a wish to make information visible rather than secret.","zh":"這個片語顯示希望資訊被看見，而不是保密。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"put them out in the shop","meaning":"把它們放在店內展示","examples":[{"en":"He puts the rare books out in the shop.","zh":"他把珍本書放在店內展示。"},{"en":"To put items out in a shop means to display them where customers can see them.","zh":"put items out in a shop 指把商品放在顧客可看見的地方展示。"},{"en":"A bakery puts fresh bread out in the shop every morning.","zh":"麵包店每天早上把新鮮麵包放在店內展示。"},{"en":"Putting rare books out can attract attention, but it also requires protection.","zh":"把珍本書展示出來可以吸引注意，但也需要保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes displaying goods rather than keeping them in storage.","zh":"這個片語描述展示貨品，而不是把它們存放起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"He makes sure customers need a ladder to reach the rare books.","zh":"他確保顧客需要梯子才可以拿到珍本書。"},{"en":"To make sure means to take action so that something definitely happens.","zh":"make sure 指採取行動，確保某事一定發生。"},{"en":"Students should make sure their names are on the answer sheet before handing it in.","zh":"學生交卷前應確保答題紙上有自己的名字。"},{"en":"A shop owner may make sure expensive items are not easy to steal.","zh":"店主可能會確保昂貴物品不容易被偷。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on careful control or checking.","zh":"這個片語着重小心控制或檢查。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"need a ladder to","meaning":"需要梯子才可以……","examples":[{"en":"Customers need a ladder to get the rare books.","zh":"顧客需要梯子才可以拿到珍本書。"},{"en":"To need a ladder to do something means the object is too high to reach without one.","zh":"need a ladder to do something 指物件太高，沒有梯子便不能做到某事。"},{"en":"A cleaner may need a ladder to change a light near the ceiling.","zh":"清潔工可能需要梯子才可以更換天花附近的燈。"},{"en":"If rare books require a ladder, casual customers cannot take them down easily.","zh":"如果珍本書需要梯子才拿到，普通顧客就不能輕易取下它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical height-related need.","zh":"這個片語描述與高度有關的實際需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prevent thefts","meaning":"防止盜竊","examples":[{"en":"Placing the rare books high up would prevent thefts.","zh":"把珍本書放在高處可以防止盜竊。"},{"en":"To prevent thefts means to stop people from stealing things.","zh":"prevent thefts 指阻止人們偷竊物品。"},{"en":"Shops use cameras and locked cabinets to prevent thefts.","zh":"商店使用閉路電視和鎖櫃來防止盜竊。"},{"en":"Keeping valuable books out of easy reach can reduce the chance of stealing.","zh":"把珍貴書籍放在不易拿到的地方，可以減少偷竊機會。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on stopping crime before it happens.","zh":"這個片語着重在罪案發生前阻止它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stock books for children","meaning":"備有兒童書","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather stocks books for children.","zh":"Jane 的祖父備有兒童書。"},{"en":"To stock books for children means to keep children’s books available for sale or use.","zh":"stock books for children 指備有兒童書供出售或使用。"},{"en":"A library stocks books for children on low shelves so young readers can reach them.","zh":"圖書館把兒童書放在矮書架上，讓年幼讀者可以拿到。"},{"en":"Stocking children’s books can encourage families to visit a shop more often.","zh":"備有兒童書可以鼓勵家庭更常到訪店舖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes providing books for a specific age group.","zh":"這個片語描述為特定年齡群體提供書籍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"particularly like to","meaning":"特別喜歡……","examples":[{"en":"He particularly likes to encourage children to read.","zh":"他特別喜歡鼓勵小朋友閱讀。"},{"en":"To particularly like to do something means to especially enjoy or care about doing it.","zh":"particularly like to do something 指特別享受或重視做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may particularly like to help shy students speak with confidence.","zh":"老師可能特別喜歡幫助害羞學生有信心說話。"},{"en":"People spend more effort on activities they particularly care about.","zh":"人們會在自己特別重視的活動上花更多心力。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a special preference or priority.","zh":"這個片語突出特別喜好或優先事項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"encourage kids to read","meaning":"鼓勵小朋友閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather likes to encourage kids to read.","zh":"Jane 的祖父喜歡鼓勵小朋友閱讀。"},{"en":"To encourage kids to read means to make children more willing and excited to read books.","zh":"encourage kids to read 指令兒童更願意和更有興趣閱讀書本。"},{"en":"Parents can encourage kids to read by keeping colourful books at home.","zh":"父母可以透過在家中放色彩繽紛的書來鼓勵小朋友閱讀。"},{"en":"Children read more when adults praise their effort and help them choose suitable books.","zh":"當成年人讚賞孩子的努力並幫助他們選合適書籍，孩子會讀得更多。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on building a reading habit, not forcing children.","zh":"這個片語着重建立閱讀習慣，而不是強迫兒童。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sit under the stairs","meaning":"坐在樓梯底下","examples":[{"en":"He used to sit under the stairs with a pile of books.","zh":"他以前常坐在樓梯底下，身邊有一疊書。"},{"en":"To sit under the stairs means to sit in the small space below a staircase.","zh":"sit under the stairs 指坐在樓梯下方的小空間。"},{"en":"A child may sit under the stairs to read quietly away from the noise of the living room.","zh":"孩子可能坐在樓梯底下閱讀，避開客廳的噪音。"},{"en":"Small hidden spaces can feel cosy and private for children who love books.","zh":"小而隱蔽的空間對愛書的孩子來說可以感覺舒適和私密。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both a position and a childhood image.","zh":"這個片語同時描述位置和童年畫面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as a child","meaning":"小時候","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather loved reading as a child.","zh":"Jane 的祖父小時候很喜歡閱讀。"},{"en":"As a child means when someone was young.","zh":"as a child 指某人年幼時。"},{"en":"As a child, my sister borrowed fairy tales from the library every week.","zh":"我姐姐小時候每星期從圖書館借童話故事。"},{"en":"Childhood habits often influence adult interests and values.","zh":"童年習慣常影響成年後的興趣和價值觀。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces information about someone’s early life.","zh":"這個片語引入某人早年生活的資料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a pile of books","meaning":"一疊書","examples":[{"en":"He used to sit under the stairs with a pile of books.","zh":"他以前常坐在樓梯底下，身邊有一疊書。"},{"en":"A pile of books is a group of books stacked or placed together.","zh":"a pile of books 指堆疊或放在一起的一組書。"},{"en":"A student may have a pile of books on the desk before exams.","zh":"考試前，學生書桌上可能有一疊書。"},{"en":"A pile of books can show that someone is studying, reading, or sorting materials.","zh":"一疊書可以顯示某人正在學習、閱讀或整理材料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visible quantity of books gathered in one place.","zh":"這個片語描述聚集在一處、可見數量的書。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not exactly","meaning":"不完全是","examples":[{"en":"The children’s books are not exactly kept under the stairs.","zh":"兒童書不完全是放在樓梯底下。"},{"en":"Not exactly means not completely or not in the precise way just suggested.","zh":"not exactly 指不完全是，或不是剛才所說的精確方式。"},{"en":"The café is not exactly beside the station; it is two streets away.","zh":"那間咖啡店不完全是在車站旁邊；它在兩條街外。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to correct an idea gently without rejecting it completely.","zh":"人們用這個片語溫和地修正想法，而不是完全否定。"},{"en":"It often introduces a more accurate explanation.","zh":"它常引入更準確的解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a dedicated area","meaning":"專門區域","examples":[{"en":"The bookshop has a dedicated area for young children.","zh":"這間書店有一個給年幼兒童的專門區域。"},{"en":"A dedicated area is a space set aside for a specific purpose or group of people.","zh":"dedicated area 指為特定用途或群體預留的空間。"},{"en":"A library may have a dedicated area for quiet study.","zh":"圖書館可能有專門區域供人安靜自修。"},{"en":"Dedicated areas help users know where to go and what the space is for.","zh":"專門區域幫助使用者知道該去哪裡，以及該空間用途是甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful planning and clear use.","zh":"這個片語暗示有仔細規劃和清晰用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on the ground floor","meaning":"在地下","examples":[{"en":"The children’s area is on the ground floor.","zh":"兒童區在地下。"},{"en":"On the ground floor means on the floor at street level.","zh":"on the ground floor 指在與街道同一水平的樓層。"},{"en":"Shops on the ground floor are easier for parents with pushchairs to enter.","zh":"在地下的商店較方便推嬰兒車的家長進入。"},{"en":"Putting children’s areas on the ground floor can make them safer and more accessible.","zh":"把兒童區設在地下，可以令它更安全和更容易到達。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a building location.","zh":"這個片語描述建築物內的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"with cushions","meaning":"有坐墊","examples":[{"en":"The children’s area has cushions for parents and toddlers.","zh":"兒童區有坐墊給家長和幼兒使用。"},{"en":"With cushions means having soft pads for people to sit or lean on.","zh":"with cushions 指有柔軟墊子供人坐或靠着。"},{"en":"A reading corner with cushions can make children feel comfortable and relaxed.","zh":"有坐墊的閱讀角可以令孩子感到舒服和放鬆。"},{"en":"Cushions help families stay longer because sitting on the floor becomes easier.","zh":"坐墊令坐在地上更容易，幫助家庭逗留更久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a feature that makes a space more comfortable.","zh":"這個片語描述令空間更舒適的設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"toddlers","meaning":"幼兒","examples":[{"en":"Parents can enter the area with their toddlers.","zh":"家長可以帶幼兒進入該區域。"},{"en":"Toddlers are very young children who are learning to walk, usually around one to three years old.","zh":"toddlers 指正在學走路的幼小兒童，通常約一至三歲。"},{"en":"Toddlers may enjoy picture books with bright colours and simple words.","zh":"幼兒可能喜歡色彩鮮艷、文字簡單的圖畫書。"},{"en":"Spaces for toddlers need to be safe because they move around and touch things often.","zh":"給幼兒使用的空間需要安全，因為他們常四處走動和觸摸東西。"},{"en":"This word refers to children younger than typical school-age children.","zh":"這個字指比一般學齡兒童更年幼的孩子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"spend some time doing something","meaning":"花時間做某事","examples":[{"en":"Parents can spend some time reading to their toddlers.","zh":"家長可以花時間讀書給幼兒聽。"},{"en":"To spend some time doing something means to use a period of time for that activity.","zh":"spend some time doing something 指用一段時間做某活動。"},{"en":"Students should spend some time reviewing notes before starting homework.","zh":"學生開始做功課前應花時間溫習筆記。"},{"en":"Spending time reading with children can build language skills and warm memories.","zh":"花時間與孩子閱讀可以建立語言能力和溫暖回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on deliberately giving time to an activity.","zh":"這個片語着重有意識地把時間給某活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"read to someone","meaning":"讀書給某人聽","examples":[{"en":"Parents can spend time reading to their children.","zh":"家長可以花時間讀書給孩子聽。"},{"en":"To read to someone means to read words aloud so that person can listen.","zh":"read to someone 指朗讀文字，讓某人聆聽。"},{"en":"A teacher may read to the class when introducing a new story.","zh":"老師介紹新故事時，可能讀書給全班聽。"},{"en":"Reading to young children helps them hear pronunciation, rhythm, and new words.","zh":"讀書給幼童聽有助他們聽到發音、節奏和新詞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reading aloud for another person, not silent reading.","zh":"這個片語描述為他人朗讀，而不是默讀。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a place for pushchairs","meaning":"放嬰兒車的地方","examples":[{"en":"There is a place for pushchairs by the front door.","zh":"前門旁邊有放嬰兒車的地方。"},{"en":"A place for pushchairs is a space where parents can leave baby strollers safely.","zh":"a place for pushchairs 指家長可以安全放置嬰兒車的空間。"},{"en":"A café with a place for pushchairs is easier for families with young children to use.","zh":"有地方放嬰兒車的咖啡店較方便有幼兒的家庭使用。"},{"en":"Providing this space prevents pushchairs from blocking aisles or entrances.","zh":"提供這個空間可防止嬰兒車阻塞通道或入口。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical family-friendly facility.","zh":"這個片語描述實用的家庭友善設施。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"by the front door","meaning":"在前門旁邊","examples":[{"en":"The place for pushchairs is by the front door.","zh":"放嬰兒車的地方在前門旁邊。"},{"en":"By the front door means next to or very near the main entrance.","zh":"by the front door 指在主要入口旁邊或非常接近它。"},{"en":"A shop may keep umbrellas by the front door on rainy days.","zh":"雨天時，商店可能把雨傘放在前門旁邊。"},{"en":"Placing pushchairs by the front door makes it easier for parents to collect them when leaving.","zh":"把嬰兒車放在前門旁邊，方便家長離開時取回。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a location close to the main way in and out.","zh":"這個片語描述接近主要出入口的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"refreshments","meaning":"茶點；飲品小食","examples":[{"en":"There is a café if anyone needs refreshments.","zh":"如果有人需要茶點，那裡有一間咖啡店。"},{"en":"Refreshments are light drinks and snacks served during a visit, break, meeting, or event.","zh":"refreshments 指到訪、休息、會議或活動期間提供的輕便飲品和小食。"},{"en":"A school open day may provide refreshments for parents after the talk.","zh":"學校開放日可能在講座後為家長提供茶點。"},{"en":"Refreshments help visitors rest, stay longer, and continue their activity comfortably.","zh":"茶點幫助訪客休息、逗留更久，並舒適地繼續活動。"},{"en":"This word usually refers to light food and drinks, not a full meal.","zh":"這個字通常指輕食和飲品，而不是完整餐點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"good to know","meaning":"知道這點很好","examples":[{"en":"Kieran says it is good to know that the bookshop has a café.","zh":"Kieran 說知道那間書店有咖啡店很好。"},{"en":"Good to know means the information is useful or reassuring.","zh":"good to know 指該資訊有用或令人安心。"},{"en":"It is good to know that the library has lockers for students’ bags.","zh":"知道圖書館有儲物櫃給學生放書包很好。"},{"en":"People say this when new information helps them plan or feel more comfortable.","zh":"當新資訊幫助人們計劃或感到更安心時，人們會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase is friendly and common in conversation.","zh":"這個片語友善，常見於對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as I said","meaning":"正如我所說","examples":[{"en":"Jane says, “As I said, it is a big shop.”","zh":"Jane 說：「正如我所說，這是一間大店。」"},{"en":"As I said means as I mentioned earlier.","zh":"as I said 指正如我之前提過。"},{"en":"As I said, the meeting starts at nine, so please arrive early.","zh":"正如我所說，會議九時開始，所以請早點到達。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to refer back to something they have already explained.","zh":"人們用這個片語指回自己已經解釋過的內容。"},{"en":"It can sound helpful or slightly impatient depending on tone.","zh":"它可以聽起來有幫助，也可能因語氣而顯得有點不耐煩。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"storage area","meaning":"儲物區","examples":[{"en":"There is a storage area out the back.","zh":"後面有一個儲物區。"},{"en":"A storage area is a space used for keeping items that are not currently on display or in use.","zh":"storage area 指用來存放暫時不展示或不使用物品的空間。"},{"en":"A school library may have a storage area for old magazines and extra chairs.","zh":"學校圖書館可能有儲物區存放舊雜誌和額外椅子。"},{"en":"Storage areas help shops keep the main customer space tidy.","zh":"儲物區幫助店舖保持主要顧客空間整潔。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical space for keeping goods or equipment.","zh":"這個片語描述用來存放貨品或設備的實用空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"out the back","meaning":"在後面","examples":[{"en":"The bookshop has a storage area out the back.","zh":"這間書店後面有一個儲物區。"},{"en":"Out the back means at the rear part of a building or behind the main area.","zh":"out the back 指在建築物後方或主要區域後面。"},{"en":"The café keeps extra tables out the back.","zh":"咖啡店把額外桌子放在後面。"},{"en":"Shops often store boxes out the back so customers do not trip over them.","zh":"商店常把箱子存放在後面，讓顧客不會絆倒。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and common in British English.","zh":"這個片語較口語，常見於英式英語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hardly ever","meaning":"幾乎從不","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather hardly ever throws anything away.","zh":"Jane 的祖父幾乎從不丟掉任何東西。"},{"en":"Hardly ever means almost never.","zh":"hardly ever 指幾乎從不。"},{"en":"My teacher hardly ever gives homework on Fridays.","zh":"我的老師星期五幾乎從不派功課。"},{"en":"Someone who hardly ever throws things away may keep old items for future use.","zh":"幾乎從不丟東西的人，可能會把舊物留作日後使用。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something happens very rarely.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事極少發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"throw anything away","meaning":"丟掉任何東西","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather hardly ever throws anything away.","zh":"Jane 的祖父幾乎從不丟掉任何東西。"},{"en":"To throw anything away means to discard things or put them in the rubbish.","zh":"throw anything away 指丟棄物品或把它們放進垃圾。"},{"en":"Some families do not throw anything away until they check whether it can be reused.","zh":"有些家庭在確認物品能否重用前，不會丟掉任何東西。"},{"en":"Not throwing things away can reduce waste, but it can also create clutter.","zh":"不丟掉東西可以減少浪費，但也可能造成雜亂。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on getting rid of items.","zh":"這個片語着重處理掉物品。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"unwanted books","meaning":"沒有人要的書","examples":[{"en":"He leaves unwanted books by the front door for customers to take.","zh":"他把沒有人要的書放在前門旁邊，讓顧客拿走。"},{"en":"Unwanted books are books that the owner no longer needs, wants, or can sell easily.","zh":"unwanted books 指擁有者不再需要、不想要或不容易出售的書。"},{"en":"A school may collect unwanted books and give them to younger students.","zh":"學校可能收集沒有人要的書，送給低年級學生。"},{"en":"Unwanted books can still be valuable to someone else.","zh":"沒有人要的書對其他人仍可能有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes books no longer wanted by one person, not books with no value.","zh":"這個片語描述某人不再想要的書，而不是沒有價值的書。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"leave something by","meaning":"把某物放在……旁邊","examples":[{"en":"He leaves unwanted books by the front door.","zh":"他把沒有人要的書放在前門旁邊。"},{"en":"To leave something by a place means to put it next to or near that place.","zh":"leave something by a place 指把某物放在某地方旁邊或附近。"},{"en":"Please leave your shoes by the classroom door before entering.","zh":"進課室前，請把鞋放在課室門旁邊。"},{"en":"Leaving books by the front door makes them easy for customers to notice.","zh":"把書放在前門旁邊，讓顧客容易注意到它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where someone places something.","zh":"這個片語描述某人把東西放在哪裡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"for customers to take","meaning":"讓顧客拿走","examples":[{"en":"The unwanted books are left for customers to take.","zh":"沒有人要的書被放在那裡，讓顧客拿走。"},{"en":"For customers to take means customers are allowed to pick them up and keep them.","zh":"for customers to take 指顧客獲准拿起並保留它們。"},{"en":"A café may leave free magazines near the door for customers to take.","zh":"咖啡店可能把免費雜誌放在門旁，讓顧客拿走。"},{"en":"If items are clearly left for customers to take, people do not need to ask permission.","zh":"如果物品清楚是讓顧客拿走，人們就不用問准。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose of placing items in a public spot.","zh":"這個片語解釋把物品放在公共位置的目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"institutions","meaning":"機構","examples":[{"en":"Some books have been requested by people or institutions.","zh":"有些書是由個人或機構要求提供的。"},{"en":"Institutions are organisations such as schools, libraries, universities, hospitals, or charities.","zh":"institutions 指學校、圖書館、大學、醫院或慈善團體等組織。"},{"en":"A museum may donate old books to educational institutions.","zh":"博物館可能把舊書捐給教育機構。"},{"en":"Institutions often request books for teaching, research, or community use.","zh":"機構常為教學、研究或社區用途要求書籍。"},{"en":"This word refers to organised bodies, not individual people.","zh":"這個字指有組織的團體，而不是個人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"request books","meaning":"預訂；要求提供書籍","examples":[{"en":"People and institutions sometimes request books from the shop.","zh":"個人和機構有時會向書店要求提供書籍。"},{"en":"To request books means to ask a shop or library to provide particular books.","zh":"request books 指請書店或圖書館提供特定書籍。"},{"en":"A teacher may request books about local history for a class project.","zh":"老師可能為班級專題要求提供本地歷史書籍。"},{"en":"When customers request books, shops can order or reserve them in advance.","zh":"當顧客預訂書籍，店舖可以提前訂購或預留。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than simply saying “ask for books”.","zh":"這個片語比單純說 “ask for books” 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"go at the far end","meaning":"放在最遠端","examples":[{"en":"Requested books go at the far end of the storage area.","zh":"預訂書籍會放在儲物區最遠端。"},{"en":"To go at the far end means to be placed at the most distant part of a space.","zh":"go at the far end 指被放在某空間最遠的部分。"},{"en":"Extra chairs go at the far end of the hall after the event.","zh":"活動後，額外椅子會放在禮堂最遠端。"},{"en":"Putting reserved items at the far end can keep them separate from regular stock.","zh":"把預留物品放在最遠端，可以令它們與一般存貨分開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where something is placed.","zh":"這個片語描述某物被放置的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"keep something out of","meaning":"把某物放在……之外","examples":[{"en":"He keeps boxed new books out of the main shopping area.","zh":"他把已入箱的新書放在主要購物區之外。"},{"en":"To keep something out of a place means to prevent it from being in that area.","zh":"keep something out of a place 指不讓某物出現在某區域內。"},{"en":"Schools keep bicycles out of corridors to prevent accidents.","zh":"學校把單車放在走廊之外，以防意外。"},{"en":"Keeping boxes out of the shopping area makes the shop safer and less crowded.","zh":"把箱子放在購物區之外，可以令店舖更安全和沒那麼擠迫。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on separation from a particular space.","zh":"這個片語着重與某特定空間分隔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the main shopping area","meaning":"主要購物區","examples":[{"en":"Requested books are kept out of the main shopping area.","zh":"預訂書籍被放在主要購物區之外。"},{"en":"The main shopping area is the part of a shop where customers usually browse and buy goods.","zh":"main shopping area 指店內顧客通常瀏覽和購買貨品的部分。"},{"en":"A supermarket keeps special displays in the main shopping area to attract customers.","zh":"超市把特別展示放在主要購物區，以吸引顧客。"},{"en":"If storage boxes fill the main shopping area, customers may find it difficult to move around.","zh":"如果儲物箱佔滿主要購物區，顧客可能難以走動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the central public area of a shop.","zh":"這個片語描述店舖中主要的公眾區域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"boxed and new","meaning":"已入箱而且全新","examples":[{"en":"The requested books are boxed and new.","zh":"預訂書籍已入箱而且全新。"},{"en":"Boxed and new means the items are new and still packed in boxes.","zh":"boxed and new 指物品是新的，而且仍放在箱內。"},{"en":"A school may receive boxed and new computers before setting up a computer room.","zh":"學校在設置電腦室前，可能收到已入箱而且全新的電腦。"},{"en":"Boxed new books are often kept separate so they stay clean and undamaged.","zh":"已入箱的新書常被分開存放，以保持乾淨和不受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both condition and packaging.","zh":"這個片語同時描述狀態和包裝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"coursebooks","meaning":"課本","examples":[{"en":"Jane got her coursebooks from her grandfather’s shop.","zh":"Jane 從祖父的書店取得她的課本。"},{"en":"Coursebooks are textbooks or study books used for a particular course.","zh":"coursebooks 指某課程使用的教科書或學習用書。"},{"en":"University students often buy coursebooks before the first week of term.","zh":"大學生常在學期第一週前購買課本。"},{"en":"Having the right coursebooks helps students follow lessons and complete assignments.","zh":"有合適課本有助學生跟上課堂並完成作業。"},{"en":"This word refers to books required for study, not general reading books.","zh":"這個字指學習所需書本，而不是一般閱讀書。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"naturally","meaning":"當然","examples":[{"en":"Jane says that she naturally got her coursebooks from her grandfather.","zh":"Jane 說她當然從祖父那裡買課本。"},{"en":"Naturally means as expected or of course, because the situation makes sense.","zh":"naturally 指如預期那樣或當然，因為情況合理。"},{"en":"Naturally, students went to the library when they needed quiet study space.","zh":"學生需要安靜自修空間時，當然會去圖書館。"},{"en":"People use this word when an action seems obvious in the circumstances.","zh":"當某行動在情況中看來很自然明顯時，人們會使用這個字。"},{"en":"This word can also mean “in a natural way”, but here it means “of course”.","zh":"這個字也可指「自然地」，但在這裡意思是「當然」。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"stock books for","meaning":"為……備有書籍","examples":[{"en":"Jane’s grandfather stocks books for many colleges.","zh":"Jane 的祖父為許多學院備有書籍。"},{"en":"To stock books for a group means to keep books that group needs or buys.","zh":"stock books for a group 指備有某群體需要或會購買的書籍。"},{"en":"A bookshop near a campus may stock books for university students.","zh":"校園附近的書店可能為大學生備有書籍。"},{"en":"Stocking books for colleges helps students get required materials more easily.","zh":"為學院備有書籍可以幫助學生更容易取得指定材料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes supplying books for a particular audience.","zh":"這個片語描述為特定讀者群提供書本。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"on the first floor","meaning":"在一樓","examples":[{"en":"He used to keep the coursebooks on the first floor.","zh":"他以前把課本放在一樓。"},{"en":"On the first floor means on the level above the ground floor in British English.","zh":"on the first floor 在英式英語中指地下上一層。"},{"en":"The language classroom is on the first floor, above the school office.","zh":"語言課室在一樓，在校務處上方。"},{"en":"If coursebooks are on the first floor, students must go upstairs to find them.","zh":"如果課本在一樓，學生必須上樓尋找。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a building level and can differ between British and American English.","zh":"這個片語描述建築物樓層，在英式與美式英語中可能不同。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hometown","meaning":"家鄉","examples":[{"en":"There is now a new university in Jane’s hometown.","zh":"Jane 的家鄉現在有一所新大學。"},{"en":"A hometown is the town or city where someone comes from or grew up.","zh":"hometown 指某人來自或長大的城鎮或城市。"},{"en":"Many students return to their hometown during long holidays.","zh":"許多學生在長假期回到家鄉。"},{"en":"When a hometown gains a new university, local shops may attract more students.","zh":"當家鄉有新大學，本地商店可能吸引更多學生。"},{"en":"This word carries a personal connection, not just a location.","zh":"這個字帶有個人連繫，而不只是地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"move them downstairs","meaning":"把它們搬到樓下","examples":[{"en":"He has moved the coursebooks downstairs to attract students.","zh":"他已把課本搬到樓下，以吸引學生。"},{"en":"To move them downstairs means to take them to a lower floor.","zh":"move them downstairs 指把它們帶到較低樓層。"},{"en":"A shop may move popular items downstairs so customers can find them more easily.","zh":"商店可能把熱門商品搬到樓下，讓顧客更容易找到。"},{"en":"Moving coursebooks downstairs can increase sales because students notice them quickly.","zh":"把課本搬到樓下可以增加銷售，因為學生更快注意到它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing the location of items within a building.","zh":"這個片語描述改變物品在建築物內的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"attract the students","meaning":"吸引學生","examples":[{"en":"The coursebooks were moved downstairs to attract the students.","zh":"課本被搬到樓下，以吸引學生。"},{"en":"To attract the students means to make students notice something and want to come or buy.","zh":"attract the students 指令學生注意某事並想前來或購買。"},{"en":"A café may offer study tables to attract students after class.","zh":"咖啡店可能提供自修桌，以吸引學生放學後光顧。"},{"en":"Shops attract students by placing useful and affordable items where they can see them.","zh":"商店把實用和價錢相宜的物品放在學生看得見的位置，以吸引學生。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on gaining students’ attention and interest.","zh":"這個片語着重取得學生注意和興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"part of the coffee shop","meaning":"屬於咖啡店區域的一部分","examples":[{"en":"The coursebooks are actually part of the coffee-shop area.","zh":"課本其實屬於咖啡店區域的一部分。"},{"en":"Part of the coffee shop means included within the space or area used by the café.","zh":"part of the coffee shop 指包含在咖啡店使用的空間或區域之內。"},{"en":"A reading corner can be part of the coffee shop if customers sit there with drinks.","zh":"如果顧客拿着飲品坐在閱讀角，閱讀角可以是咖啡店的一部分。"},{"en":"Placing books in a café area can make students notice them while they relax.","zh":"把書放在咖啡店區域，可以令學生放鬆時注意到它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how one section belongs within a larger space.","zh":"這個片語描述某部分如何屬於較大空間之內。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"low shelves","meaning":"矮書架","examples":[{"en":"The coursebooks are kept on low shelves around the coffee shop.","zh":"課本放在咖啡店四周的矮書架上。"},{"en":"Low shelves are shelves that are close to the ground and easy to reach.","zh":"low shelves 指接近地面、容易拿取的書架。"},{"en":"Children’s books are often placed on low shelves so young readers can choose them by themselves.","zh":"兒童書常放在矮書架上，讓年幼讀者可以自己選。"},{"en":"Low shelves make books more visible and accessible to customers sitting nearby.","zh":"矮書架令附近坐着的顧客更容易看見和拿取書籍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shelf height and convenience.","zh":"這個片語描述書架高度和便利性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"all around it","meaning":"圍繞着它四周","examples":[{"en":"The low shelves are placed all around the coffee shop.","zh":"矮書架放在咖啡店四周。"},{"en":"All around it means on every side or in many places surrounding it.","zh":"all around it 指在它每一邊或周圍許多地方。"},{"en":"Plants were placed all around the reading corner to make it feel calm.","zh":"植物被放在閱讀角四周，令那裡感覺平靜。"},{"en":"Shelves all around a café can turn the whole space into a browsing area.","zh":"咖啡店四周都有書架，可以把整個空間變成瀏覽區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something surrounding a central place.","zh":"這個片語描述某物圍繞一個中心地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pretty central","meaning":"位置相當中心","examples":[{"en":"Kieran says the coursebooks are in a pretty central location.","zh":"Kieran 說課本的位置相當中心。"},{"en":"Pretty central means quite near the middle or easy to notice and reach.","zh":"pretty central 指相當接近中心，或容易被注意和到達。"},{"en":"The school noticeboard is in a pretty central place near the entrance.","zh":"學校告示板在入口附近，位置相當中心。"},{"en":"Items in a central location attract more attention because people pass them often.","zh":"位於中心位置的物品會吸引更多注意，因為人們經常經過。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and means the location is fairly important or convenient.","zh":"這個片語較口語，意思是位置頗重要或方便。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"take me there some time","meaning":"改天帶我去那裏","examples":[{"en":"Kieran asks Jane to take him to the bookshop some time.","zh":"Kieran 請 Jane 改天帶他去那間書店。"},{"en":"Take me there some time means bring me to that place on a future occasion.","zh":"take me there some time 指將來某個時候帶我去那個地方。"},{"en":"If your favourite café is that good, take me there some time after class.","zh":"如果你最喜歡的咖啡店那麼好，放學後改天帶我去那裡。"},{"en":"People say this when they are interested in visiting a place but have not fixed a date yet.","zh":"當人們有興趣到訪某地但尚未定日期時，會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and friendly.","zh":"這個片語語氣輕鬆而友善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/listening/Practice 8/task-4":[{"front":"tree planting","meaning":"植樹","examples":[{"en":"Tree planting now dominates political and popular agendas.","zh":"植樹現在主導政治及大眾議程。"},{"en":"Tree planting means putting young trees into the ground so they can grow into a forest, park, or green space.","zh":"tree planting 的意思是把幼樹種入泥土，讓它們長成森林、公園或綠化空間。"},{"en":"A school may organise tree planting to teach students about nature and responsibility.","zh":"學校可能組織植樹活動，教學生認識自然和責任。"},{"en":"Tree planting can cool neighbourhoods, improve air quality, and create habitats for wildlife.","zh":"植樹可以令社區降溫、改善空氣質素，並為野生動物創造棲息地。"},{"en":"Tree planting helps only when the right trees are planted in the right places.","zh":"只有在正確地方種下正確樹種，植樹才真正有幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dominates political and popular agendas","meaning":"主導政治及大眾議程","examples":[{"en":"Tree planting now dominates political and popular agendas.","zh":"植樹現在主導政治及大眾議程。"},{"en":"If an issue dominates political and popular agendas, it receives major attention from governments, media, and ordinary people.","zh":"如果一個議題 dominates political and popular agendas，意思是它受到政府、媒體和普通人的重大關注。"},{"en":"Housing prices may dominate political and popular agendas when many families cannot afford homes.","zh":"當許多家庭買不起樓，樓價可能主導政治及大眾議程。"},{"en":"An issue can dominate agendas because people see it as urgent, emotional, or closely connected to daily life.","zh":"一個議題可以因為被視為迫切、具情感性或與日常生活密切相關，而主導議程。"},{"en":"When one topic dominates agendas, other important issues may receive less attention.","zh":"當一個題目主導議程，其他重要議題可能得到較少關注。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be presented as","meaning":"被呈現為","examples":[{"en":"Tree planting is often presented as an easy answer to the climate crisis.","zh":"植樹常被呈現為應對氣候危機的簡單方法。"},{"en":"To be presented as something means to be described or shown in a particular way.","zh":"be presented as something 的意思是被描述或展示成某種樣子。"},{"en":"A new app may be presented as a solution to poor time management.","zh":"一個新應用程式可能被呈現為解決時間管理差的方法。"},{"en":"When a complex issue is presented as simple, people may ignore important details.","zh":"當複雜議題被呈現為簡單，人們可能忽略重要細節。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how something is framed, not whether the description is fully true.","zh":"這個短語集中於某事如何被包裝，而不一定代表描述完全真實。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an easy answer to","meaning":"應對……的簡單方法","examples":[{"en":"Tree planting is often presented as an easy answer to the climate crisis.","zh":"植樹常被呈現為應對氣候危機的簡單方法。"},{"en":"An easy answer to a problem is a solution that seems simple and convenient.","zh":"an easy answer to a problem 是看似簡單方便的解決方法。"},{"en":"Extra homework is sometimes presented as an easy answer to poor exam results.","zh":"額外功課有時被呈現為應對考試成績差的簡單方法。"},{"en":"An easy answer may attract attention because it sounds quick, but it may not solve deeper causes.","zh":"簡單方法可能因聽起來快速而吸引注意，但未必能解決深層原因。"},{"en":"Complex problems rarely have one easy answer.","zh":"複雜問題很少只有一個簡單方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"climate crisis","meaning":"氣候危機","examples":[{"en":"Tree planting is often presented as an easy answer to the climate crisis.","zh":"植樹常被呈現為應對氣候危機的簡單方法。"},{"en":"The climate crisis refers to serious climate change problems, such as rising temperatures, extreme weather, and damage to ecosystems.","zh":"climate crisis 指嚴重的氣候變化問題，例如氣溫上升、極端天氣和生態系統受損。"},{"en":"Schools may teach students about the climate crisis through lessons on heatwaves and flooding.","zh":"學校可能透過關於熱浪和洪水的課堂，教學生認識氣候危機。"},{"en":"The climate crisis affects food, water, health, housing, and wildlife.","zh":"氣候危機影響食物、水、健康、住屋和野生動物。"},{"en":"Responding to the climate crisis requires many actions, not just one solution.","zh":"應對氣候危機需要許多行動，而不只是一個解決方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"以及","examples":[{"en":"Tree planting is seen as a climate solution, as well as a way to offset emissions.","zh":"植樹被視為氣候解決方案，以及抵銷排放的方法。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to something else.","zh":"as well as 的意思是除了某事之外，也包括另一事。"},{"en":"The library offers storybooks as well as homework support.","zh":"圖書館提供故事書以及功課支援。"},{"en":"A good park provides exercise space as well as shade and cleaner air.","zh":"好公園提供運動空間，以及樹蔭和較潔淨空氣。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another function, benefit, or example.","zh":"這個短語加入另一個功能、好處或例子。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"business corporations","meaning":"商業企業","examples":[{"en":"Business corporations use tree planting to offset their carbon emissions.","zh":"商業企業利用植樹來抵銷碳排放。"},{"en":"Business corporations are large companies that operate to sell goods or services and make profit.","zh":"business corporations 是銷售商品或服務並追求利潤的大型公司。"},{"en":"Business corporations may publish environmental reports to show how they reduce pollution.","zh":"商業企業可能發布環境報告，展示它們如何減少污染。"},{"en":"When business corporations make climate promises, people often ask whether the actions are real or only publicity.","zh":"當商業企業作出氣候承諾，人們常會問這些行動是真實還是只為宣傳。"},{"en":"The phrase is more formal than simply saying “companies”.","zh":"這個短語比單純說 companies 更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"offset carbon emissions","meaning":"抵銷碳排放","examples":[{"en":"Some corporations plant trees to offset their carbon emissions.","zh":"有些企業植樹來抵銷碳排放。"},{"en":"To offset carbon emissions means to balance pollution released into the air by supporting actions that remove or reduce carbon elsewhere.","zh":"offset carbon emissions 的意思是透過支持在其他地方移除或減少碳的行動，來平衡釋放到空氣中的污染。"},{"en":"An airline may pay for forest projects to offset carbon emissions from flights.","zh":"航空公司可能支付森林項目費用，以抵銷航班產生的碳排放。"},{"en":"Offsetting carbon emissions can help, but it should not replace cutting pollution at the source.","zh":"抵銷碳排放可以有幫助，但不應取代從源頭減少污染。"},{"en":"A company should measure emissions honestly before claiming to offset them.","zh":"公司在聲稱抵銷碳排放前，應誠實量度排放量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"unfortunately","meaning":"不幸的是","examples":[{"en":"Unfortunately, tree planting is not as straightforward as some people think.","zh":"不幸的是，植樹並非像有些人想的那麼簡單。"},{"en":"Unfortunately is used to introduce bad, disappointing, or inconvenient information.","zh":"unfortunately 用來引出不好、令人失望或不方便的資訊。"},{"en":"Unfortunately, the workshop is full, so new applicants must join a waiting list.","zh":"不幸的是，工作坊已滿，新申請者必須加入輪候名單。"},{"en":"People use unfortunately when they want to sound polite while giving unwelcome news.","zh":"人們在給出不受歡迎的消息時，使用 unfortunately 令語氣較禮貌。"},{"en":"The word prepares the listener for a problem or limitation.","zh":"這個詞讓聽者準備面對問題或限制。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"not as straightforward as","meaning":"並非像……那麼簡單","examples":[{"en":"Tree planting is not as straightforward as some people think.","zh":"植樹並非像有些人想的那麼簡單。"},{"en":"Not as straightforward as means more complicated than it first appears.","zh":"not as straightforward as 的意思是比表面看起來更複雜。"},{"en":"Choosing a school is not as straightforward as picking the nearest one.","zh":"選學校並非像選最近的一間那麼簡單。"},{"en":"A task may not be straightforward because it involves money, people, rules, and long-term effects.","zh":"一項任務可能並不簡單，因為它涉及金錢、人、規則和長遠影響。"},{"en":"This phrase warns readers not to assume something is simple.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者不要假設某事很簡單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"wrong trees are planted in the wrong place","meaning":"在錯誤地方種下錯誤樹種","examples":[{"en":"Problems arise when the wrong trees are planted in the wrong place.","zh":"當在錯誤地方種下錯誤樹種，問題就會出現。"},{"en":"The wrong trees are planted in the wrong place when species are chosen without considering the local ecosystem.","zh":"wrong trees are planted in the wrong place 指在沒有考慮本地生態系統下選擇樹種。"},{"en":"A city may create problems if fast-growing trees are planted where roots damage pavements and pipes.","zh":"如果城市在樹根會破壞行人路和水管的地方種下快生樹種，就可能製造問題。"},{"en":"Planting the wrong trees in the wrong place can waste money and harm wildlife.","zh":"在錯誤地方種下錯誤樹種，可能浪費金錢並傷害野生動物。"},{"en":"Good tree planting begins with matching tree species to location.","zh":"好的植樹始於把樹種與地點配合。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"considerably more damage than good","meaning":"弊遠大於利","examples":[{"en":"Planting the wrong trees can do considerably more damage than good.","zh":"種錯樹可能弊遠大於利。"},{"en":"Considerably more damage than good means the harm is much greater than the benefit.","zh":"considerably more damage than good 的意思是傷害遠大於好處。"},{"en":"A poorly planned road may do considerably more damage than good if it destroys homes and saves little time.","zh":"如果一條規劃不良的道路破壞住屋卻節省不了多少時間，它可能弊遠大於利。"},{"en":"A policy can do more damage than good when it solves one problem but creates several larger ones.","zh":"當一項政策解決一個問題卻製造幾個更大問題，它可能弊遠大於利。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly warns that a good intention can still produce bad results.","zh":"這個短語強烈提醒人們，好意仍可能帶來壞結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"do damage","meaning":"造成損害","examples":[{"en":"Tree planting can do damage if it is poorly planned.","zh":"如果規劃不良，植樹可以造成損害。"},{"en":"To do damage means to cause harm to people, places, systems, or relationships.","zh":"do damage 的意思是對人、地方、系統或關係造成傷害。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can do damage to roads if drains are blocked.","zh":"如果排水渠堵塞，大雨可以對道路造成損害。"},{"en":"Careless comments can do damage to trust between friends.","zh":"粗心說話可以對朋友之間的信任造成損害。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on harmful results, not intentions.","zh":"這個短語集中於有害結果，而不是意圖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"failing to help either A or B","meaning":"既未能幫助A，也未能幫助B","examples":[{"en":"Poor tree planting may fail to help either people or the environment.","zh":"糟糕的植樹可能既未能幫助人，也未能幫助環境。"},{"en":"Failing to help either A or B means not benefiting either of two important groups or goals.","zh":"failing to help either A or B 的意思是對兩個重要群體或目標都沒有好處。"},{"en":"A badly designed school rule may fail to help either teachers or students.","zh":"設計差劣的校規可能既未能幫助老師，也未能幫助學生。"},{"en":"A project that ignores local needs may fail to help either the community or nature.","zh":"忽視本地需要的項目，可能既未能幫助社區，也未能幫助自然。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an action can miss both targets.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個行動可以兩個目標都達不到。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reforestation projects","meaning":"再造林計劃","examples":[{"en":"Reforestation projects are currently being undertaken in many countries.","zh":"再造林計劃目前正在許多國家進行。"},{"en":"Reforestation projects are organised efforts to plant trees or restore forests in areas where forests have been lost or damaged.","zh":"reforestation projects 是在森林消失或受損地區種樹或恢復森林的有組織工作。"},{"en":"A town may start reforestation projects after hillsides are damaged by fire.","zh":"山坡被火災破壞後，城鎮可能展開再造林計劃。"},{"en":"Reforestation projects can protect soil, restore habitats, and support local communities.","zh":"再造林計劃可以保護土壤、恢復棲息地，並支援本地社區。"},{"en":"Such projects need careful planning because forests take many years to grow.","zh":"這類計劃需要仔細規劃，因為森林需要多年才能長成。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"currently being undertaken","meaning":"目前正在進行","examples":[{"en":"Reforestation projects are currently being undertaken on a huge scale.","zh":"再造林計劃目前正在大規模進行。"},{"en":"Currently being undertaken means happening or being carried out now.","zh":"currently being undertaken 的意思是現在正在發生或正在執行。"},{"en":"Road repairs are currently being undertaken, so drivers should use another route.","zh":"道路維修目前正在進行，所以駕駛者應使用其他路線。"},{"en":"If a study is currently being undertaken, its final results may not be ready yet.","zh":"如果一項研究目前正在進行，其最終結果可能尚未準備好。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in reports.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於報告。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on a huge scale","meaning":"大規模地","examples":[{"en":"Reforestation projects are being undertaken on a huge scale in many countries.","zh":"再造林計劃正在許多國家大規模地進行。"},{"en":"On a huge scale means involving very large numbers, areas, or resources.","zh":"on a huge scale 的意思是涉及非常大的數量、面積或資源。"},{"en":"A vaccination programme may be organised on a huge scale during a public health emergency.","zh":"在公共健康緊急情況中，疫苗接種計劃可能大規模地組織。"},{"en":"Work done on a huge scale can bring big benefits, but mistakes can also become very costly.","zh":"大規模進行的工作可以帶來重大好處，但錯誤也可能變得非常昂貴。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises size and reach.","zh":"這個短語強調規模和影響範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"it is crucial that","meaning":"……是至關重要的","examples":[{"en":"It is crucial that the right trees are selected.","zh":"選擇正確樹種是至關重要的。"},{"en":"It is crucial that means something is extremely important and must not be ignored.","zh":"it is crucial that 的意思是某事極其重要，不能被忽視。"},{"en":"It is crucial that students read the instructions before answering exam questions.","zh":"學生在回答考試題目前閱讀指示是至關重要的。"},{"en":"It is crucial that hospitals keep emergency exits clear because delays can cost lives.","zh":"醫院保持緊急出口暢通是至關重要的，因為延誤可能造成生命損失。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply saying something is useful.","zh":"這個短語比單純說某事有用更強烈。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the right trees are selected","meaning":"選擇正確樹種","examples":[{"en":"It is crucial that the right trees are selected for reforestation projects.","zh":"再造林計劃選擇正確樹種是至關重要的。"},{"en":"The right trees are selected when species are chosen because they suit the local climate, soil, and ecosystem.","zh":"the right trees are selected 指因樹種適合本地氣候、土壤和生態系統而被選中。"},{"en":"A park project succeeds more easily when the right trees are selected for shade, safety, and maintenance.","zh":"當公園項目因應樹蔭、安全和維護選擇正確樹種，它會較容易成功。"},{"en":"If the wrong species are chosen, the project may harm native plants or waste resources.","zh":"如果選錯物種，項目可能傷害本土植物或浪費資源。"},{"en":"Selecting the right trees requires ecological knowledge, not just good intentions.","zh":"選擇正確樹種需要生態知識，而不只是好意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a mix of species","meaning":"多種物種組合","examples":[{"en":"A mix of species should always be planted.","zh":"應該一直種植多種物種組合。"},{"en":"A mix of species means several different kinds of plants, animals, or organisms together.","zh":"a mix of species 指幾種不同植物、動物或生物一起存在。"},{"en":"A garden with a mix of species can attract bees, butterflies, and birds.","zh":"有多種物種組合的花園可以吸引蜜蜂、蝴蝶和雀鳥。"},{"en":"Planting a mix of species reduces risk because one disease is less likely to destroy everything.","zh":"種植多種物種組合可以降低風險，因為一種疾病較不容易摧毀一切。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights diversity rather than sameness.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣性，而不是單一性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"typical of","meaning":"……的典型","examples":[{"en":"The trees should be typical of the local natural forest ecosystem.","zh":"這些樹應該是本地天然森林生態系統的典型樹種。"},{"en":"Typical of something means usual, normal, or characteristic of that thing.","zh":"typical of something 的意思是某事物通常、正常或具代表性的特徵。"},{"en":"Hot, humid weather is typical of summer in many coastal cities.","zh":"炎熱潮濕的天氣是許多沿海城市夏天的典型特徵。"},{"en":"Trees typical of a local forest are more likely to support local insects, birds, and soil life.","zh":"本地森林的典型樹種更可能支援本地昆蟲、雀鳥和土壤生命。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe what naturally belongs in a place or situation.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述某地或某情況中自然屬於它的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"local natural forest ecosystem","meaning":"本地天然森林生態系統","examples":[{"en":"The species should be typical of the local natural forest ecosystem.","zh":"這些物種應該是本地天然森林生態系統的典型物種。"},{"en":"A local natural forest ecosystem is the original forest community of plants, animals, fungi, soil, water, and climate in an area.","zh":"local natural forest ecosystem 是某地原有的森林群落，包括植物、動物、真菌、土壤、水和氣候。"},{"en":"Scientists study the local natural forest ecosystem before choosing trees for restoration.","zh":"科學家在選擇復育樹種前，會研究本地天然森林生態系統。"},{"en":"Protecting the local natural forest ecosystem helps native species survive together.","zh":"保護本地天然森林生態系統有助本土物種共同存活。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that a forest is a living system, not just a group of trees.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，森林是活的系統，而不只是一群樹。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rare and endangered species","meaning":"稀有及瀕危物種","examples":[{"en":"Reforestation should include rare and endangered species.","zh":"再造林應包括稀有及瀕危物種。"},{"en":"Rare and endangered species are species that are uncommon and at risk of disappearing.","zh":"rare and endangered species 是不常見並面臨消失風險的物種。"},{"en":"A conservation garden may protect rare and endangered species by growing them carefully.","zh":"保育花園可能透過細心種植來保護稀有及瀕危物種。"},{"en":"Including rare and endangered species can help rebuild a damaged ecosystem.","zh":"包括稀有及瀕危物種可以幫助重建受損生態系統。"},{"en":"These species need protection because losing them may reduce biodiversity permanently.","zh":"這些物種需要保護，因為失去它們可能永久減少生物多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了","examples":[{"en":"Different species should be planted in order to create a rich ecosystem.","zh":"應種植不同物種，為了建立豐富的生態系統。"},{"en":"In order to means for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"in order to 的意思是為了達到某個目的。"},{"en":"Students revise past papers in order to understand exam question styles.","zh":"學生操練歷屆試題，為了理解考試題型。"},{"en":"A city may plant more trees in order to reduce heat and improve public spaces.","zh":"城市可能種植更多樹木，為了減少炎熱並改善公共空間。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly connects an action with its purpose.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接行動與目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"create a rich ecosystem","meaning":"建立豐富的生態系統","examples":[{"en":"A mix of species can help create a rich ecosystem.","zh":"多種物種組合可以幫助建立豐富的生態系統。"},{"en":"To create a rich ecosystem means to build an environment with many living things that support one another.","zh":"create a rich ecosystem 的意思是建立一個有許多生物互相支持的環境。"},{"en":"A school pond can create a rich ecosystem if it attracts plants, insects, frogs, and birds.","zh":"如果學校池塘吸引植物、昆蟲、青蛙和雀鳥，它可以建立豐富的生態系統。"},{"en":"Rich ecosystems are stronger because different species perform different roles.","zh":"豐富的生態系統更強韌，因為不同物種發揮不同角色。"},{"en":"A rich ecosystem takes time, planning, and protection to develop.","zh":"豐富的生態系統需要時間、規劃和保護才能發展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"avoid non-native species","meaning":"避免外來物種","examples":[{"en":"It is important to avoid non-native species that could become invasive.","zh":"避免可能變成入侵性的外來物種很重要。"},{"en":"To avoid non-native species means to choose not to introduce species that do not naturally belong in the area.","zh":"avoid non-native species 的意思是選擇不引入不自然屬於該地區的物種。"},{"en":"A gardener may avoid non-native species if they spread too quickly and crowd out local plants.","zh":"如果外來植物蔓延太快並擠走本地植物，園丁可能會避免外來物種。"},{"en":"Avoiding risky species can protect native wildlife and reduce future control costs.","zh":"避免有風險的物種可以保護本土野生動物，並減少未來控制成本。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in conservation because one wrong species can change an ecosystem.","zh":"這個短語在保育中很重要，因為一個錯誤物種可以改變生態系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"non-native species","meaning":"外來物種","examples":[{"en":"Non-native species may become invasive.","zh":"外來物種可能變成入侵性。"},{"en":"Non-native species are plants, animals, or organisms introduced to an area where they do not naturally occur.","zh":"non-native species 是被引入到並非自然出現地區的植物、動物或生物。"},{"en":"A pond fish from another country may be a non-native species in a local river.","zh":"來自另一國家的池塘魚，在本地河流中可能是外來物種。"},{"en":"Some non-native species are harmless, but others spread quickly and harm local ecosystems.","zh":"有些外來物種無害，但另一些會快速蔓延並傷害本地生態系統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes origin, not automatically danger.","zh":"這個短語描述來源，而不一定代表危險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"become invasive","meaning":"變成入侵性","examples":[{"en":"Some non-native species could become invasive.","zh":"有些外來物種可能變成入侵性。"},{"en":"To become invasive means to spread aggressively and harm native species or ecosystems.","zh":"become invasive 的意思是猛烈擴散，並傷害本土物種或生態系統。"},{"en":"A garden plant can become invasive if its seeds spread into nearby countryside.","zh":"如果園藝植物的種子散播到附近郊野，它可能變成入侵性。"},{"en":"When a species becomes invasive, it may be expensive and difficult to control.","zh":"當一個物種變成入侵性，它可能昂貴且難以控制。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a species can change from harmless-looking to harmful.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們，一個物種可以由看似無害變成有害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"invasive species","meaning":"入侵物種","examples":[{"en":"Invasive species are a significant contributor to the biodiversity crisis.","zh":"入侵物種是生物多樣性危機的重要成因。"},{"en":"Invasive species are non-native species that spread and harm local plants, animals, or habitats.","zh":"invasive species 是會擴散並傷害本地植物、動物或棲息地的外來物種。"},{"en":"Invasive plants may cover riverbanks and stop native flowers from growing.","zh":"入侵植物可能覆蓋河岸，阻止本土花朵生長。"},{"en":"Invasive species can reduce biodiversity because native species lose food, space, or light.","zh":"入侵物種可以減少生物多樣性，因為本土物種失去食物、空間或光線。"},{"en":"Preventing invasive species is usually easier than removing them later.","zh":"預防入侵物種通常比日後移除它們更容易。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a significant contributor to","meaning":"……的重要成因","examples":[{"en":"Invasive species are a significant contributor to the global biodiversity crisis.","zh":"入侵物種是全球生物多樣性危機的重要成因。"},{"en":"A significant contributor to a problem is an important cause of that problem.","zh":"a significant contributor to a problem 是某問題的重要成因。"},{"en":"Poor diet can be a significant contributor to health problems.","zh":"不良飲食可以是健康問題的重要成因。"},{"en":"Traffic emissions are a significant contributor to air pollution in many cities.","zh":"交通排放是許多城市空氣污染的重要成因。"},{"en":"This phrase helps identify one major cause among several causes.","zh":"這個短語幫助在多個原因中指出一個主要原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"global biodiversity crisis","meaning":"全球生物多樣性危機","examples":[{"en":"Invasive species contribute to the current global biodiversity crisis.","zh":"入侵物種導致當前的全球生物多樣性危機。"},{"en":"The global biodiversity crisis is the worldwide loss of plants, animals, habitats, and genetic variety.","zh":"global biodiversity crisis 是全球植物、動物、棲息地和遺傳多樣性的喪失。"},{"en":"Schools may explain the global biodiversity crisis through examples of disappearing insects and forests.","zh":"學校可能透過昆蟲和森林消失的例子解釋全球生物多樣性危機。"},{"en":"The crisis matters because food, clean water, medicine, and stable ecosystems depend on biodiversity.","zh":"這場危機重要，因為食物、潔淨食水、藥物和穩定生態系統都依賴生物多樣性。"},{"en":"It cannot be solved by protecting one famous animal only.","zh":"它不能只靠保護一種著名動物來解決。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in competition with","meaning":"與……競爭","examples":[{"en":"Invasive species are often in competition with native species.","zh":"入侵物種常與本土物種競爭。"},{"en":"To be in competition with something means to fight for the same resources, space, or advantage.","zh":"be in competition with something 的意思是爭奪相同資源、空間或優勢。"},{"en":"Small shops are in competition with supermarkets for customers.","zh":"小店與超級市場競爭顧客。"},{"en":"Plants in competition with one another may struggle for sunlight, water, and soil nutrients.","zh":"彼此競爭的植物可能爭奪陽光、水和土壤養分。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two sides cannot easily get everything they need at the same time.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩方不能同時輕易得到所有需要的東西。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"native species","meaning":"本土物種","examples":[{"en":"Invasive species may threaten the survival of native species.","zh":"入侵物種可能威脅本土物種的生存。"},{"en":"Native species are plants, animals, or organisms that naturally live in a particular area.","zh":"native species 是自然生活在特定地區的植物、動物或生物。"},{"en":"Native species often support local food chains because other animals depend on them.","zh":"本土物種常支援本地食物鏈，因為其他動物依賴它們。"},{"en":"When native species disappear, the balance of an ecosystem may change.","zh":"當本土物種消失，生態系統的平衡可能改變。"},{"en":"Planting native species usually helps restoration projects fit the local environment.","zh":"種植本土物種通常有助復育計劃配合本地環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"long-term survival","meaning":"長遠生存","examples":[{"en":"Invasive species may threaten the long-term survival of native species.","zh":"入侵物種可能威脅本土物種的長遠生存。"},{"en":"Long-term survival means continuing to live or exist far into the future.","zh":"long-term survival 的意思是在很長的未來仍能繼續生活或存在。"},{"en":"A business needs loyal customers for long-term survival.","zh":"企業需要忠實顧客才能長遠生存。"},{"en":"A species needs enough food, habitat, and genetic diversity for long-term survival.","zh":"物種需要足夠食物、棲息地和遺傳多樣性才能長遠生存。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on lasting success, not only short-term protection.","zh":"這個短語集中於持久成功，而不只是短期保護。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"restoring biodiversity","meaning":"恢復生物多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Restoring biodiversity is key when reforesting an area.","zh":"為某地區再造林時，恢復生物多樣性是關鍵。"},{"en":"Restoring biodiversity means bringing back many different plants, animals, and living systems to a damaged place.","zh":"restoring biodiversity 的意思是把多種植物、動物和生命系統帶回受損地方。"},{"en":"A pond project may restore biodiversity by adding native plants and protecting insects and frogs.","zh":"池塘項目可能透過加入本土植物並保護昆蟲和青蛙來恢復生物多樣性。"},{"en":"Restoring biodiversity makes ecosystems stronger because many species support one another.","zh":"恢復生物多樣性能令生態系統更強韌，因為許多物種互相支持。"},{"en":"This goal is broader than simply planting trees.","zh":"這個目標比單純植樹更廣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"maximise carbon capture","meaning":"最大化碳捕捉","examples":[{"en":"Restoring biodiversity can help maximise carbon capture.","zh":"恢復生物多樣性可以幫助最大化碳捕捉。"},{"en":"To maximise carbon capture means to increase the amount of carbon stored by trees, soil, and ecosystems as much as possible.","zh":"maximise carbon capture 的意思是盡可能增加樹木、土壤和生態系統儲存的碳量。"},{"en":"Healthy forests can maximise carbon capture when trees grow well and soil is protected.","zh":"當樹木生長良好、土壤受保護，健康森林可以最大化碳捕捉。"},{"en":"Biodiverse ecosystems may capture carbon more reliably because they are less likely to collapse.","zh":"生物多樣性高的生態系統可能更可靠地捕捉碳，因為它們較不容易崩潰。"},{"en":"This phrase connects climate action with ecosystem health.","zh":"這個短語把氣候行動與生態系統健康連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"is key when","meaning":"在……時是關鍵","examples":[{"en":"Restoring biodiversity is key when reforesting an area.","zh":"為某地區再造林時，恢復生物多樣性是關鍵。"},{"en":"If something is key when doing an activity, it is very important for success at that time.","zh":"如果某事 is key when 做某活動，意思是它在該時候對成功非常重要。"},{"en":"Clear communication is key when organising a school trip.","zh":"組織學校旅行時，清晰溝通是關鍵。"},{"en":"Clean equipment is key when doctors carry out surgery.","zh":"醫生進行手術時，乾淨設備是關鍵。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the most important condition for a successful action.","zh":"這個短語突出了成功行動中最重要的條件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reforest an area","meaning":"為某地區再造林","examples":[{"en":"Restoring biodiversity is key when reforesting an area.","zh":"為某地區再造林時，恢復生物多樣性是關鍵。"},{"en":"To reforest an area means to plant trees or help forest return to land where it has been lost.","zh":"reforest an area 的意思是在森林消失的土地上種樹或幫助森林回復。"},{"en":"Volunteers may reforest an area after a wildfire destroys a hillside.","zh":"山火摧毀山坡後，義工可能為該地區再造林。"},{"en":"Reforesting an area can reduce erosion, support wildlife, and store carbon.","zh":"為某地區再造林可以減少侵蝕、支援野生動物並儲存碳。"},{"en":"A successful project should reforest an area without harming local people or existing ecosystems.","zh":"成功項目應在不傷害本地人或現有生態系統下為地區再造林。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ideally","meaning":"理想情況下","examples":[{"en":"Ideally, any reforestation project should have several goals.","zh":"理想情況下，任何再造林計劃都應有多個目標。"},{"en":"Ideally means in the best possible situation or according to the best plan.","zh":"ideally 的意思是在最佳情況下或根據最佳計劃。"},{"en":"Ideally, students should start revising before they feel stressed.","zh":"理想情況下，學生應在感到壓力前開始溫習。"},{"en":"Ideally, a park should provide shade, safety, exercise space, and wildlife habitat.","zh":"理想情況下，公園應提供樹蔭、安全、運動空間和野生動物棲息地。"},{"en":"This word shows what should happen, even if reality may be harder.","zh":"這個詞顯示應該發生甚麼，即使現實可能較困難。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have several goals","meaning":"有多個目標","examples":[{"en":"Any reforestation project should ideally have several goals.","zh":"任何再造林計劃理想情況下都應有多個目標。"},{"en":"To have several goals means to aim for more than one result.","zh":"have several goals 的意思是追求多於一個結果。"},{"en":"A school sports day may have several goals: exercise, teamwork, confidence, and fun.","zh":"學校運動日可能有多個目標：運動、團隊合作、信心和樂趣。"},{"en":"Projects with several goals can create broader benefits, but they need careful planning.","zh":"有多個目標的項目可以創造更廣泛好處，但需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that one purpose is not enough.","zh":"這個短語表示一個目的並不足夠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"contribute to wildlife conservation","meaning":"有助於野生動物保育","examples":[{"en":"Trees can contribute to wildlife conservation.","zh":"樹木可以有助於野生動物保育。"},{"en":"To contribute to wildlife conservation means to help protect wild animals and their habitats.","zh":"contribute to wildlife conservation 的意思是幫助保護野生動物及其棲息地。"},{"en":"A city park with native trees can contribute to wildlife conservation by giving birds places to nest.","zh":"有本土樹木的城市公園可以透過給鳥類築巢地方而有助於野生動物保育。"},{"en":"Protecting habitats contributes to conservation because animals need food, shelter, and breeding spaces.","zh":"保護棲息地有助保育，因為動物需要食物、庇護和繁殖空間。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how one action supports a larger environmental goal.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個行動如何支持更大的環境目標。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"wildlife conservation","meaning":"野生動物保育","examples":[{"en":"Tree selection can support wildlife conservation.","zh":"樹種選擇可以支援野生動物保育。"},{"en":"Wildlife conservation means protecting wild animals, plants, and the places they need to survive.","zh":"wildlife conservation 的意思是保護野生動物、植物和它們生存所需的地方。"},{"en":"Wildlife conservation may involve protecting forests, stopping illegal hunting, and restoring rivers.","zh":"野生動物保育可能涉及保護森林、阻止非法狩獵和復育河流。"},{"en":"Good conservation helps future generations see living species, not just pictures of extinct ones.","zh":"良好保育能幫助下一代看見活生生的物種，而不只是已滅絕物種的圖片。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on protecting nature from decline or disappearance.","zh":"這個短語集中於保護自然免於衰退或消失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"improve the availability of food","meaning":"改善食物供應","examples":[{"en":"Trees can improve the availability of food for the local community.","zh":"樹木可以改善本地社區的食物供應。"},{"en":"To improve the availability of food means to make food easier to find, grow, buy, or access.","zh":"improve the availability of food 的意思是令食物更容易找到、種植、購買或取得。"},{"en":"Community gardens can improve the availability of fresh vegetables in poor neighbourhoods.","zh":"社區花園可以改善貧困社區的新鮮蔬菜供應。"},{"en":"Fruit trees can improve food availability by providing seasonal produce close to homes.","zh":"果樹可以透過在住家附近提供季節性農產來改善食物供應。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on access to food, not only the amount grown.","zh":"這個短語集中於取得食物，而不只是食物產量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"local community","meaning":"本地社區","examples":[{"en":"Reforestation can benefit the local community.","zh":"再造林可以令本地社區受益。"},{"en":"A local community is the group of people who live in a particular area.","zh":"local community 是住在特定地區的一群人。"},{"en":"A local community may use a restored forest for shade, food, jobs, and recreation.","zh":"本地社區可能使用復育森林作為樹蔭、食物、工作和康樂空間來源。"},{"en":"Projects work better when the local community is consulted before decisions are made.","zh":"在作出決定前諮詢本地社區，項目通常會運作得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on people directly affected by a place or project.","zh":"這個短語集中於直接受一個地方或項目影響的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"maintain the stability of","meaning":"維持……的穩定","examples":[{"en":"Trees can help maintain the stability of soil systems.","zh":"樹木可以幫助維持土壤系統的穩定。"},{"en":"To maintain the stability of something means to keep it steady, balanced, and less likely to collapse or fail.","zh":"maintain the stability of something 的意思是保持某物穩定、平衡，並較不容易崩潰或失效。"},{"en":"Good sleep helps maintain the stability of a student’s mood and attention.","zh":"良好睡眠幫助維持學生情緒和注意力的穩定。"},{"en":"Tree roots maintain soil stability by holding the ground together during heavy rain.","zh":"樹根透過在大雨中固定土地來維持土壤穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase shows protection against sudden breakdown or damage.","zh":"這個短語顯示對突然崩潰或損害的保護。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"soil systems","meaning":"土壤系統","examples":[{"en":"Tree roots can help maintain the stability of soil systems.","zh":"樹根可以幫助維持土壤系統的穩定。"},{"en":"Soil systems are the living and physical structures in soil, including minerals, water, roots, fungi, insects, and microorganisms.","zh":"soil systems 是土壤中的生命和物理結構，包括礦物、水、根、真菌、昆蟲和微生物。"},{"en":"Farmers protect soil systems by avoiding too much chemical use and erosion.","zh":"農夫透過避免過度使用化學品和防止侵蝕來保護土壤系統。"},{"en":"Healthy soil systems help plants grow and store water more effectively.","zh":"健康土壤系統幫助植物更有效生長和儲水。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that soil is active and alive, not just dirt.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，土壤是活躍而有生命的，不只是泥土。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as many of these goals as possible","meaning":"盡可能多地達成這些目標","examples":[{"en":"A good project should meet as many of these goals as possible.","zh":"好項目應盡可能多地達成這些目標。"},{"en":"As many of these goals as possible means the largest number of listed aims that can realistically be achieved.","zh":"as many of these goals as possible 的意思是在現實可行下達成已列目標中的最大數量。"},{"en":"A school event should meet as many goals as possible, such as learning, safety, fun, and inclusion.","zh":"學校活動應盡可能多地達成目標，例如學習、安全、樂趣和共融。"},{"en":"Meeting several goals makes a project more valuable because different needs are served.","zh":"達成多個目標令項目更有價值，因為它服務不同需要。"},{"en":"This phrase accepts that achieving every goal may be difficult, but more is better.","zh":"這個短語承認達成每個目標可能困難，但達成越多越好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"whilst doing no harm to","meaning":"同時不傷害……","examples":[{"en":"Projects should meet goals whilst doing no harm to local communities.","zh":"項目應達成目標，同時不傷害本地社區。"},{"en":"Whilst doing no harm to someone or something means achieving an aim without damaging them.","zh":"whilst doing no harm to someone or something 的意思是在達成目標時不損害他們。"},{"en":"A school should improve exam results whilst doing no harm to students’ mental health.","zh":"學校應提高考試成績，同時不傷害學生的精神健康。"},{"en":"A development project should create jobs whilst doing no harm to rivers and farmland.","zh":"發展項目應創造就業，同時不傷害河流和農田。"},{"en":"This phrase balances progress with protection.","zh":"這個短語平衡進步與保護。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"native ecosystems","meaning":"本土生態系統","examples":[{"en":"Tree planting should do no harm to native ecosystems.","zh":"植樹不應傷害本土生態系統。"},{"en":"Native ecosystems are natural local systems of plants, animals, soil, water, and climate that belong to an area.","zh":"native ecosystems 是自然屬於某地的本地植物、動物、土壤、水和氣候系統。"},{"en":"A wetland is a native ecosystem if it naturally supports local birds, fish, and plants.","zh":"如果濕地自然支援本地鳥類、魚類和植物，它就是本土生態系統。"},{"en":"Damaging native ecosystems can reduce biodiversity even if trees are planted elsewhere.","zh":"即使在其他地方植樹，傷害本土生態系統仍會減少生物多樣性。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whole living systems, not just individual species.","zh":"這個短語集中於整個生命系統，而不只是個別物種。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"vulnerable species","meaning":"脆弱物種","examples":[{"en":"Tree planting should protect vulnerable species.","zh":"植樹應保護脆弱物種。"},{"en":"Vulnerable species are species that are at risk because their numbers, habitats, or survival conditions are weak.","zh":"vulnerable species 是因數量、棲息地或生存條件薄弱而面臨風險的物種。"},{"en":"A vulnerable species may need protected breeding areas to survive.","zh":"脆弱物種可能需要受保護的繁殖地才能生存。"},{"en":"If a project destroys the habitat of vulnerable species, it may harm biodiversity despite good intentions.","zh":"如果項目破壞脆弱物種的棲息地，即使出於好意，也可能傷害生物多樣性。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights species that need extra care.","zh":"這個短語突出了需要額外照顧的物種。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the sign of","meaning":"……的標誌","examples":[{"en":"Meeting these goals is the sign of a successful tree-planting scheme.","zh":"達成這些目標是成功植樹計劃的標誌。"},{"en":"The sign of something is evidence that shows it is present or true.","zh":"the sign of something 是顯示某事存在或真實的證據。"},{"en":"Students asking thoughtful questions can be the sign of real understanding.","zh":"學生提出有思想的問題，可以是真正理解的標誌。"},{"en":"A clean river with returning fish may be the sign of successful restoration.","zh":"有魚類回歸的清潔河流，可能是成功復育的標誌。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a visible clue or proof.","zh":"這個短語指出可見線索或證明。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"highly successful","meaning":"非常成功的","examples":[{"en":"Meeting multiple goals is the sign of a highly successful scheme.","zh":"達成多個目標是非常成功的計劃的標誌。"},{"en":"Highly successful means very effective and producing strong results.","zh":"highly successful 的意思是非常有效並產生強大成果。"},{"en":"A highly successful reading programme may improve skills and make students enjoy books.","zh":"非常成功的閱讀計劃可能提升能力，並令學生享受書本。"},{"en":"Projects become highly successful when they solve real problems and continue working over time.","zh":"當項目解決真實問題並能長期持續，就會變得非常成功。"},{"en":"The phrase gives stronger praise than simply saying “successful”.","zh":"這個短語比單純說 successful 有更強讚賞意味。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tree-planting scheme","meaning":"植樹計劃","examples":[{"en":"A successful tree-planting scheme should not harm local ecosystems.","zh":"成功的植樹計劃不應傷害本地生態系統。"},{"en":"A tree-planting scheme is a planned project to plant trees for environmental, social, or economic purposes.","zh":"tree-planting scheme 是為環境、社會或經濟目的而規劃的植樹項目。"},{"en":"A town may start a tree-planting scheme to shade streets and improve public spaces.","zh":"城鎮可能展開植樹計劃，為街道提供樹蔭並改善公共空間。"},{"en":"A tree-planting scheme can fail if it ignores water supply, species choice, or local needs.","zh":"如果植樹計劃忽視供水、樹種選擇或本地需要，它可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests organised planning, not random planting.","zh":"這個短語表示有組織的規劃，而不是隨意種植。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ensure the survival and resilience of","meaning":"確保……的存活及韌性","examples":[{"en":"Genetic diversity helps ensure the survival and resilience of a planted forest.","zh":"遺傳多樣性有助確保人工種植森林的存活及韌性。"},{"en":"To ensure the survival and resilience of something means to help it stay alive and recover from stress or damage.","zh":"ensure the survival and resilience of something 的意思是幫助某物存活，並能從壓力或損害中恢復。"},{"en":"Vaccination can help ensure the survival and resilience of vulnerable communities during disease outbreaks.","zh":"接種疫苗可以在疾病爆發期間幫助確保脆弱社區的存活及韌性。"},{"en":"A forest with many genetic types can better survive droughts, pests, and climate shifts.","zh":"有多種遺傳類型的森林，能更好地抵禦乾旱、害蟲和氣候轉變。"},{"en":"This phrase links protection with the ability to recover.","zh":"這個短語把保護與恢復能力連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"survival and resilience","meaning":"存活及韌性","examples":[{"en":"Tree seeds should support the survival and resilience of the forest.","zh":"樹種子應支援森林的存活及韌性。"},{"en":"Survival and resilience mean staying alive and being able to recover after difficulties.","zh":"survival and resilience 指保持存活，並能在困難後恢復。"},{"en":"A community’s survival and resilience may depend on clean water, strong relationships, and emergency plans.","zh":"社區的存活及韌性可能取決於潔淨食水、強大關係和緊急計劃。"},{"en":"Forest survival and resilience improve when trees can resist disease and adapt to weather changes.","zh":"當樹木能抵抗疾病並適應天氣變化，森林的存活及韌性會提高。"},{"en":"This phrase combines endurance with recovery.","zh":"這個短語結合了持續承受與恢復能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"planted forest","meaning":"人工種植森林","examples":[{"en":"A planted forest needs genetic diversity to survive.","zh":"人工種植森林需要遺傳多樣性才能存活。"},{"en":"A planted forest is a forest created by people planting trees, rather than one that grew naturally without direct human planting.","zh":"planted forest 是由人類種樹創造的森林，而不是沒有直接人為種植而自然生長的森林。"},{"en":"A planted forest may be used for restoration, timber, shade, or carbon storage.","zh":"人工種植森林可能用於復育、木材、遮蔭或碳儲存。"},{"en":"If a planted forest contains only one species, it may be vulnerable to pests and disease.","zh":"如果人工種植森林只包含一種物種，它可能容易受害蟲和疾病影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how the forest began, not whether it is healthy.","zh":"這個短語描述森林如何開始，而不是它是否健康。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"it is vital to","meaning":"……是極為重要的","examples":[{"en":"It is vital to use tree seeds with genetic diversity.","zh":"使用具遺傳多樣性的樹種子是極為重要的。"},{"en":"It is vital to do something means it is extremely important and necessary.","zh":"it is vital to do something 的意思是做某事極其重要且必要。"},{"en":"It is vital to wash hands before preparing food.","zh":"準備食物前洗手是極為重要的。"},{"en":"It is vital to save important files before updating a computer system.","zh":"更新電腦系統前儲存重要檔案是極為重要的。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when ignoring the action could cause serious problems.","zh":"當忽略某行動可能造成嚴重問題時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"appropriate levels of","meaning":"適當程度的……","examples":[{"en":"Tree seeds should have appropriate levels of genetic diversity.","zh":"樹種子應有適當程度的遺傳多樣性。"},{"en":"Appropriate levels of something means the right amount for a particular purpose or situation.","zh":"appropriate levels of something 的意思是符合特定目的或情況的適當數量。"},{"en":"Children need appropriate levels of sleep for their age.","zh":"兒童需要適合其年齡的適當睡眠時間。"},{"en":"A classroom needs appropriate levels of noise: too much is distracting, but total silence may feel tense.","zh":"課室需要適當程度的聲音：太多會令人分心，但完全安靜可能令人緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests balance, not simply more or less.","zh":"這個短語表示平衡，而不只是越多或越少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"genetic diversity","meaning":"遺傳多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Genetic diversity is essential for the survival of a species.","zh":"遺傳多樣性對一個物種的生存至關重要。"},{"en":"Genetic diversity means variation in genes within a species or population.","zh":"genetic diversity 指一個物種或族群內基因上的差異。"},{"en":"A crop with high genetic diversity may better survive disease or drought.","zh":"遺傳多樣性高的農作物可能更能抵抗疾病或乾旱。"},{"en":"Low genetic diversity can make a population weaker because many individuals share the same weaknesses.","zh":"低遺傳多樣性會令族群較脆弱，因為許多个體共有相同弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in conservation, farming, and medicine.","zh":"這個短語在保育、農業和醫學中都很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"genetic variation","meaning":"遺傳變異","examples":[{"en":"Genetic diversity refers to the amount of genetic variation within a species.","zh":"遺傳多樣性指一個物種內遺傳變異的多少。"},{"en":"Genetic variation means differences in genes among individuals in the same species.","zh":"genetic variation 指同一物種個體之間基因上的差異。"},{"en":"Genetic variation can explain why some plants tolerate heat better than others.","zh":"遺傳變異可以解釋為何有些植物比其他植物更耐熱。"},{"en":"More genetic variation can help a species adapt when conditions change.","zh":"更多遺傳變異可以幫助物種在環境改變時適應。"},{"en":"Without enough genetic variation, a disease may affect many individuals in the same way.","zh":"如果沒有足夠遺傳變異，疾病可能以同樣方式影響許多个體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"within a species","meaning":"在一個物種內","examples":[{"en":"Genetic variation within a species is essential for survival.","zh":"在一個物種內的遺傳變異對生存至關重要。"},{"en":"Within a species means inside one biological group whose members can reproduce with one another.","zh":"within a species 的意思是在同一個能互相繁殖的生物群體內。"},{"en":"There can be colour, size, or disease-resistance differences within a species.","zh":"在一個物種內，可以有顏色、大小或抗病能力上的差異。"},{"en":"Variation within a species helps populations respond to changes in climate or disease.","zh":"物種內的變異幫助族群回應氣候或疾病變化。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on differences inside one species, not between different species.","zh":"這個短語集中於同一物種內的差異，而不是不同物種之間的差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"essential for","meaning":"對……至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Genetic variation is essential for the survival of a species.","zh":"遺傳變異對一個物種的生存至關重要。"},{"en":"Essential for something means absolutely necessary for it to happen or continue.","zh":"essential for something 的意思是對某事發生或延續絕對必要。"},{"en":"Clean water is essential for human health.","zh":"潔淨食水對人類健康至關重要。"},{"en":"Trust is essential for teamwork because people must depend on one another.","zh":"信任對團隊合作至關重要，因為人們必須依靠彼此。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “helpful” because without it, the result may fail.","zh":"這個短語比 helpful 更強，因為沒有它，結果可能失敗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"low genetic diversity","meaning":"低遺傳多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Using seeds with low genetic diversity lowers forest resilience.","zh":"使用低遺傳多樣性的種子會降低森林韌性。"},{"en":"Low genetic diversity means there is little genetic difference among individuals in a population.","zh":"low genetic diversity 的意思是一個族群中的個體在基因上差異很少。"},{"en":"A crop with low genetic diversity may be destroyed quickly if one disease spreads.","zh":"低遺傳多樣性的農作物若遇上一種疾病蔓延，可能很快被摧毀。"},{"en":"Low genetic diversity makes adaptation harder because fewer useful traits are available.","zh":"低遺傳多樣性令適應更困難，因為可用的有利特徵較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a biological weakness that may not be visible at first.","zh":"這個短語描述一種起初未必可見的生物弱點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lowers the resilience of","meaning":"降低……的韌性","examples":[{"en":"Low genetic diversity lowers the resilience of restored forests.","zh":"低遺傳多樣性會降低復育森林的韌性。"},{"en":"To lower the resilience of something means to reduce its ability to recover from stress, disease, or damage.","zh":"lower the resilience of something 的意思是降低某物從壓力、疾病或損害中恢復的能力。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep lowers the resilience of students when they face exam pressure.","zh":"睡眠不足會在學生面對考試壓力時降低他們的韌性。"},{"en":"Poor soil lowers the resilience of plants during drought.","zh":"貧瘠土壤會在乾旱期間降低植物的韌性。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something becomes weaker when facing future problems.","zh":"這個短語顯示某物在面對未來問題時變得較弱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"restored forests","meaning":"復育森林","examples":[{"en":"Restored forests can become vulnerable if their genetic diversity is low.","zh":"如果遺傳多樣性低，復育森林可能變得脆弱。"},{"en":"Restored forests are damaged or lost forests that have been brought back through planting, protection, or natural recovery.","zh":"restored forests 是透過種植、保護或自然恢復而重新出現的受損或消失森林。"},{"en":"Restored forests may take many years before they support birds, insects, and mammals again.","zh":"復育森林可能需要多年才能再次支援鳥類、昆蟲和哺乳動物。"},{"en":"A restored forest is healthier when it contains many native species and strong soil systems.","zh":"當復育森林包含多種本土物種和強健土壤系統，它會更健康。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to forests after recovery work has begun or succeeded.","zh":"這個短語指恢復工作已開始或成功後的森林。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"vulnerable to disease","meaning":"容易受疾病侵害","examples":[{"en":"Forests with low genetic diversity can be vulnerable to disease.","zh":"遺傳多樣性低的森林可能容易受疾病侵害。"},{"en":"Vulnerable to disease means more likely to become sick or damaged by disease.","zh":"vulnerable to disease 的意思是更容易因疾病而生病或受損。"},{"en":"Children may be more vulnerable to disease if they lack clean water and good nutrition.","zh":"如果兒童缺乏潔淨食水和良好營養，他們可能更容易受疾病侵害。"},{"en":"A forest becomes vulnerable to disease when many trees share the same weakness.","zh":"當許多樹木共有同一弱點，森林就會容易受疾病侵害。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a higher risk, not a certainty.","zh":"這個短語顯示較高風險，而不是必然結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"adapt to climate change","meaning":"適應氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"Forests with low genetic diversity may be unable to adapt to climate change.","zh":"遺傳多樣性低的森林可能無法適應氣候變化。"},{"en":"To adapt to climate change means to adjust to changing temperatures, rainfall, storms, and other climate conditions.","zh":"adapt to climate change 的意思是調整以面對氣溫、降雨、風暴和其他氣候條件的變化。"},{"en":"Farmers may adapt to climate change by growing crops that need less water.","zh":"農夫可能透過種植較少需水的作物來適應氣候變化。"},{"en":"Species with more variation may adapt better because some individuals can survive new conditions.","zh":"有更多變異的物種可能更能適應，因為有些個體能在新條件下存活。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on survival through adjustment.","zh":"這個短語集中於透過調整而生存。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the right location for","meaning":"適合……的地點","examples":[{"en":"Choosing the right location for reforestation projects is very important.","zh":"選擇適合再造林計劃的地點非常重要。"},{"en":"The right location for something is the place that best suits its purpose, needs, and risks.","zh":"the right location for something 是最適合其目的、需要和風險的地方。"},{"en":"The right location for a playground should be safe, easy to reach, and away from heavy traffic.","zh":"適合遊樂場的地點應該安全、容易到達，並遠離繁忙交通。"},{"en":"Choosing the wrong location can make even a good project fail.","zh":"選錯地點可以令一個好項目也失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that place matters as much as the action itself.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，地點與行動本身同樣重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as important as","meaning":"與……一樣重要","examples":[{"en":"Choosing the right location is as important as choosing the right trees.","zh":"選擇正確地點與選擇正確樹種一樣重要。"},{"en":"As important as means equally important.","zh":"as important as 的意思是同樣重要。"},{"en":"Sleep is as important as revision before an exam.","zh":"考試前，睡眠與溫習一樣重要。"},{"en":"In a hospital, clear communication is as important as modern equipment.","zh":"在醫院中，清晰溝通與現代設備一樣重要。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two things and shows neither should be ignored.","zh":"這個短語比較兩件事，並顯示兩者都不應被忽視。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ultimately","meaning":"歸根究底","examples":[{"en":"Ultimately, the best planting areas are formerly forested areas in poor condition.","zh":"歸根究底，最佳植樹地區是狀況欠佳的曾經是森林的地區。"},{"en":"Ultimately means in the end, after considering the most important points.","zh":"ultimately 的意思是在考慮最重要因素後，最終或歸根究底。"},{"en":"Ultimately, students learn best when they understand mistakes and keep practising.","zh":"歸根究底，學生在理解錯誤並持續練習時學得最好。"},{"en":"A project may have many details, but ultimately it must solve the real problem.","zh":"一個項目可能有許多細節，但歸根究底必須解決真正問題。"},{"en":"This word introduces a final or most important conclusion.","zh":"這個詞引出最終或最重要的結論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"formerly forested areas","meaning":"曾經是森林的地區","examples":[{"en":"The best areas for planting are formerly forested areas.","zh":"最適合植樹的地區是曾經是森林的地區。"},{"en":"Formerly forested areas are places that used to have forests but no longer do, or where the forest is badly reduced.","zh":"formerly forested areas 是過去有森林但現在沒有，或森林大幅減少的地方。"},{"en":"A hillside cleared for mining may become a formerly forested area suitable for restoration.","zh":"被採礦清理過的山坡，可能成為適合復育的曾經是森林的地區。"},{"en":"Replanting formerly forested areas can help rebuild ecosystems that naturally belonged there.","zh":"重新種植曾經是森林的地區，可以幫助重建原本自然屬於那裡的生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase points to land with a forest history.","zh":"這個短語指出有森林歷史的土地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in poor condition","meaning":"狀況欠佳","examples":[{"en":"The best planting areas are formerly forested areas that are in poor condition.","zh":"最佳植樹地區是狀況欠佳的曾經是森林的地區。"},{"en":"In poor condition means damaged, unhealthy, weak, or not working well.","zh":"in poor condition 的意思是受損、不健康、薄弱或運作不佳。"},{"en":"A playground in poor condition may have broken equipment and unsafe ground.","zh":"狀況欠佳的遊樂場可能有損壞設備和不安全地面。"},{"en":"Land in poor condition may need soil repair before trees can grow well.","zh":"狀況欠佳的土地在樹木能良好生長前，可能需要修復土壤。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something needs improvement or restoration.","zh":"這個短語顯示某物需要改善或復育。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"non-forested landscapes","meaning":"非森林地貌","examples":[{"en":"It is better to avoid non-forested landscapes.","zh":"避免非森林地貌較好。"},{"en":"Non-forested landscapes are natural areas that are not forests, such as grasslands, savannas, or wetlands.","zh":"non-forested landscapes 是並非森林的自然地區，例如草地、稀樹草原或濕地。"},{"en":"A natural grassland is a non-forested landscape even if it has few trees.","zh":"天然草地即使有少量樹木，也屬於非森林地貌。"},{"en":"Planting trees in non-forested landscapes can harm species that need open habitats.","zh":"在非森林地貌植樹可能傷害需要開闊棲息地的物種。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that not every treeless place should become a forest.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，並非每個沒有樹的地方都應變成森林。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"natural grasslands","meaning":"天然草地","examples":[{"en":"Natural grasslands already contribute greatly to carbon capture.","zh":"天然草地已對碳捕捉有很大貢獻。"},{"en":"Natural grasslands are open ecosystems where grasses are the main plants and trees are naturally few or absent.","zh":"natural grasslands 是以草為主要植物、樹木自然很少或不存在的開闊生態系統。"},{"en":"Natural grasslands can support insects, grazing animals, birds, and deep soil carbon.","zh":"天然草地可以支援昆蟲、吃草動物、鳥類和深層土壤碳。"},{"en":"Turning natural grasslands into forests may damage the species that depend on open space.","zh":"把天然草地變成森林可能傷害依賴開闊空間的物種。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a valuable ecosystem, not empty land.","zh":"這個短語描述有價值的生態系統，而不是空地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"savannas","meaning":"稀樹草原","examples":[{"en":"Savannas should generally be avoided in reforestation projects.","zh":"再造林計劃一般應避免稀樹草原。"},{"en":"Savannas are open grassland ecosystems with scattered trees, often found in warm regions.","zh":"savannas 是有零散樹木的開闊草地生態系統，常見於溫暖地區。"},{"en":"Savannas can support large animals, grasses, insects, and fire-adapted plants.","zh":"稀樹草原可以支援大型動物、草、昆蟲和適應火的植物。"},{"en":"Planting dense forests in savannas may damage the natural balance of that ecosystem.","zh":"在稀樹草原種植茂密森林，可能破壞該生態系統的自然平衡。"},{"en":"This word describes a natural landscape, not failed forest.","zh":"這個詞描述自然地貌，而不是失敗的森林。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"wetlands","meaning":"濕地","examples":[{"en":"Wetlands already contribute greatly to capturing carbon.","zh":"濕地已對捕捉碳有很大貢獻。"},{"en":"Wetlands are areas where land is covered or saturated with water, such as marshes, swamps, and mangroves.","zh":"wetlands 是被水覆蓋或浸潤的土地，例如沼澤、濕沼和紅樹林。"},{"en":"Wetlands can store carbon, filter water, and provide homes for fish and birds.","zh":"濕地可以儲存碳、過濾水，並為魚類和鳥類提供棲息地。"},{"en":"Destroying wetlands can increase flooding and release stored carbon.","zh":"破壞濕地可以增加洪水風險，並釋放已儲存的碳。"},{"en":"Wetlands are valuable ecosystems, even though they may not look like forests.","zh":"濕地是有價值的生態系統，即使它們看起來不像森林。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"contribute greatly to","meaning":"對……有很大貢獻","examples":[{"en":"Wetlands contribute greatly to capturing carbon.","zh":"濕地對捕捉碳有很大貢獻。"},{"en":"To contribute greatly to something means to help it in a major or important way.","zh":"contribute greatly to something 的意思是以重大或重要方式幫助某事。"},{"en":"Good public transport contributes greatly to reducing traffic congestion.","zh":"良好公共交通對減少交通擠塞有很大貢獻。"},{"en":"Parents who read with children contribute greatly to early language development.","zh":"與孩子一起閱讀的父母，對早期語言發展有很大貢獻。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a strong positive effect.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈正面影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"capturing carbon","meaning":"捕捉碳","examples":[{"en":"Grasslands, savannas and wetlands help with capturing carbon.","zh":"草地、稀樹草原和濕地有助捕捉碳。"},{"en":"Capturing carbon means taking carbon dioxide from the air or storing carbon in plants, soil, or ecosystems.","zh":"capturing carbon 的意思是從空氣中吸收二氧化碳，或把碳儲存在植物、土壤或生態系統中。"},{"en":"Healthy soil can help with capturing carbon by storing organic matter underground.","zh":"健康土壤可以透過在地下儲存有機物來幫助捕捉碳。"},{"en":"Capturing carbon can slow climate change, but it does not replace cutting emissions.","zh":"捕捉碳可以減慢氣候變化，但不能取代減少排放。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in climate and environmental discussions.","zh":"這個短語常用於氣候和環境討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"it would be advantageous to","meaning":"選擇……會有好處","examples":[{"en":"It would be advantageous to choose an area where trees provide other benefits.","zh":"選擇一個樹木能提供其他好處的地區會有好處。"},{"en":"It would be advantageous to do something means doing it would be useful or beneficial.","zh":"it would be advantageous to do something 的意思是做某事會有用或有利。"},{"en":"It would be advantageous to arrive early for an interview because you can settle down first.","zh":"面試時提早到達會有好處，因為你可以先安定下來。"},{"en":"It would be advantageous to plant trees near schools if they provide shade and learning spaces.","zh":"如果樹木能提供樹蔭和學習空間，選擇在學校附近植樹會有好處。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and careful.","zh":"這個短語聽起來正式而審慎。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"provide other benefits","meaning":"提供其他好處","examples":[{"en":"Trees can provide other benefits, such as recreational spaces.","zh":"樹木可以提供其他好處，例如康樂空間。"},{"en":"To provide other benefits means to offer extra advantages beyond the main purpose.","zh":"provide other benefits 的意思是除了主要目的外，還提供額外好處。"},{"en":"A library can provide other benefits besides books, such as quiet study space and community events.","zh":"圖書館除了書本外，可以提供其他好處，例如安靜自修空間和社區活動。"},{"en":"A project is stronger when it provides several benefits to different groups.","zh":"當項目為不同群體提供多種好處，它會更有力量。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers to look beyond one simple outcome.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者不要只看一個簡單結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"recreational spaces","meaning":"康樂空間","examples":[{"en":"Trees can provide recreational spaces for the community.","zh":"樹木可以為社區提供康樂空間。"},{"en":"Recreational spaces are places where people can relax, play, exercise, or spend free time.","zh":"recreational spaces 是讓人放鬆、玩樂、運動或度過空閒時間的地方。"},{"en":"Parks, playgrounds, walking paths, and sports fields are recreational spaces.","zh":"公園、遊樂場、步行徑和運動場都是康樂空間。"},{"en":"Recreational spaces improve health because people have safe places to move and rest.","zh":"康樂空間能改善健康，因為人們有安全地方活動和休息。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on public enjoyment and well-being.","zh":"這個短語集中於公共享受和福祉。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"exploited for agriculture","meaning":"被用作農業用途","examples":[{"en":"Areas currently exploited for agriculture should be avoided.","zh":"目前被用作農業用途的地區應該避免。"},{"en":"Exploited for agriculture means used for farming, growing crops, or raising animals.","zh":"exploited for agriculture 的意思是被用於耕種、種植農作物或飼養動物。"},{"en":"Land exploited for agriculture may provide food and income for local families.","zh":"被用作農業用途的土地可能為本地家庭提供食物和收入。"},{"en":"Reforesting farmland without planning can harm food supply or push farming into other forests.","zh":"沒有規劃地把農地再造林，可能傷害食物供應或把農業推向其他森林。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how land is being used.","zh":"這個短語集中於土地正如何被使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"leads to","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"Reforesting farmland often leads to other areas being deforested.","zh":"為農地再造林常導致其他地區被砍伐森林。"},{"en":"Leads to means causes or results in something.","zh":"leads to 的意思是造成或帶來某事。"},{"en":"Poor sleep often leads to weak concentration the next day.","zh":"睡眠不足常導致翌日專注力差。"},{"en":"A lack of affordable housing can lead to longer journeys and family stress.","zh":"缺乏可負擔住屋可以導致更長通勤和家庭壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase connects cause and result.","zh":"這個短語連接原因與結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"other areas being deforested","meaning":"其他地區被砍伐森林","examples":[{"en":"Reforesting agricultural land may lead to other areas being deforested.","zh":"為農地再造林可能導致其他地區被砍伐森林。"},{"en":"Other areas being deforested means forests elsewhere are cut down or cleared as a result.","zh":"other areas being deforested 的意思是其他地方的森林因此被砍倒或清除。"},{"en":"If farms are moved from one valley, other areas may be deforested to replace the lost land.","zh":"如果農場從一個山谷遷走，其他地區可能被砍伐森林來替代失去的土地。"},{"en":"Protecting one place can still harm nature if it causes forests somewhere else to be cleared.","zh":"保護一個地方仍可能傷害自然，如果它導致其他地方森林被清除。"},{"en":"This phrase warns about shifting damage from one location to another.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們，損害可能從一地轉移到另一地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"large-scale reforestation projects","meaning":"大規模再造林計劃","examples":[{"en":"Large-scale reforestation projects require careful planning.","zh":"大規模再造林計劃需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"Large-scale reforestation projects are major forest restoration efforts covering big areas or involving many trees.","zh":"large-scale reforestation projects 是覆蓋大面積或涉及大量樹木的重大森林復育工作。"},{"en":"A government may fund large-scale reforestation projects after years of forest loss.","zh":"政府可能在多年森林流失後資助大規模再造林計劃。"},{"en":"Large-scale projects can bring major benefits, but mistakes can also affect many people and ecosystems.","zh":"大規模計劃可以帶來重大好處，但錯誤也可以影響許多人和生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises both size and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語同時強調規模和責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"require careful planning","meaning":"需要仔細規劃","examples":[{"en":"Large-scale reforestation projects require careful planning.","zh":"大規模再造林計劃需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"To require careful planning means to need detailed preparation before action begins.","zh":"require careful planning 的意思是在行動開始前需要詳細準備。"},{"en":"A school trip requires careful planning because transport, food, safety, and timing all matter.","zh":"學校旅行需要仔細規劃，因為交通、食物、安全和時間都很重要。"},{"en":"Careful planning reduces mistakes, waste, and harm.","zh":"仔細規劃能減少錯誤、浪費和傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when a task is complicated or risky.","zh":"這個短語常用於複雜或有風險的任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"making the right decisions about","meaning":"就……作出正確決定","examples":[{"en":"Making the right decisions about where to plant trees depends on good information.","zh":"就在哪裡植樹作出正確決定取決於良好資訊。"},{"en":"Making the right decisions about something means choosing wisely after considering evidence, needs, and risks.","zh":"making the right decisions about something 的意思是在考慮證據、需要和風險後明智選擇。"},{"en":"Parents need good school information when making the right decisions about their child’s education.","zh":"父母在就孩子教育作出正確決定時，需要良好學校資訊。"},{"en":"Without accurate facts, people may make decisions that seem sensible but cause problems later.","zh":"沒有準確事實，人們可能作出看似合理但之後造成問題的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase connects judgement with preparation.","zh":"這個短語把判斷與準備連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"depends on","meaning":"取決於","examples":[{"en":"Making the right decisions depends on having the right information.","zh":"作出正確決定取決於擁有正確資訊。"},{"en":"Depends on means is controlled or affected by something else.","zh":"depends on 的意思是受另一件事控制或影響。"},{"en":"Whether a picnic succeeds depends on the weather, food, and transport.","zh":"野餐是否成功取決於天氣、食物和交通。"},{"en":"Good decisions depend on reliable information rather than guesswork.","zh":"好決定取決於可靠資訊，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one thing cannot be judged alone.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事不能單獨判斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"detailed and up-to-date maps","meaning":"詳細且最新的地圖","examples":[{"en":"Detailed and up-to-date maps are essential for planning.","zh":"詳細且最新的地圖對規劃是必要的。"},{"en":"Detailed and up-to-date maps show accurate, recent information about roads, land, forests, water, and settlements.","zh":"detailed and up-to-date maps 顯示關於道路、土地、森林、水源和聚居地的準確近期資訊。"},{"en":"Emergency teams need detailed and up-to-date maps to reach people quickly after floods.","zh":"緊急隊伍需要詳細且最新的地圖，在洪水後快速到達居民。"},{"en":"Old or vague maps can lead to wrong decisions because land conditions may have changed.","zh":"舊或模糊的地圖可能導致錯誤決定，因為土地情況可能已改變。"},{"en":"This phrase combines accuracy with freshness of information.","zh":"這個短語結合了準確性和資訊的新近程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"identify high-priority areas","meaning":"識別高優先次序地區","examples":[{"en":"Maps can identify high-priority areas for intervention.","zh":"地圖可以識別需要介入的高優先次序地區。"},{"en":"To identify high-priority areas means to find the places that need action most urgently.","zh":"identify high-priority areas 的意思是找出最迫切需要行動的地方。"},{"en":"A hospital map can identify high-priority areas where elderly patients need easier access.","zh":"醫院地圖可以識別長者病人需要更方便出入的高優先次序地區。"},{"en":"Identifying priority areas helps organisations use limited money and workers wisely.","zh":"識別優先地區幫助機構明智使用有限金錢和人手。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on choosing where action should come first.","zh":"這個短語集中於選擇哪裡應最先行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"high-priority areas","meaning":"高優先次序地區","examples":[{"en":"Reforestation planners need to identify high-priority areas.","zh":"再造林規劃者需要識別高優先次序地區。"},{"en":"High-priority areas are places that should receive attention first because their needs are urgent or important.","zh":"high-priority areas 是因需要迫切或重要而應首先獲得關注的地方。"},{"en":"After a storm, high-priority areas may include hospitals, damaged roads, and flooded homes.","zh":"風暴後，高優先次序地區可能包括醫院、受損道路和水浸房屋。"},{"en":"In restoration, high-priority areas may be places where forest loss causes severe erosion or biodiversity decline.","zh":"在復育中，高優先次序地區可能是森林流失造成嚴重侵蝕或生物多樣性下降的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase helps rank needs when resources are limited.","zh":"這個短語在資源有限時幫助排列需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"intervention","meaning":"介入；干預","examples":[{"en":"Maps help identify high-priority areas for intervention.","zh":"地圖幫助識別需要介入的高優先次序地區。"},{"en":"Intervention is action taken to improve a problem or stop it from getting worse.","zh":"intervention 是為改善問題或阻止其惡化而採取的行動。"},{"en":"Early intervention can help a child with reading difficulties before they fall far behind.","zh":"早期介入可以在孩子閱讀困難嚴重落後前幫助他們。"},{"en":"In conservation, intervention may include planting, protection, monitoring, or removing invasive species.","zh":"在保育中，介入可能包括種植、保護、監察或移除入侵物種。"},{"en":"This word suggests purposeful action, not passive observation.","zh":"這個詞表示有目的的行動，而不是被動觀察。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"is essential","meaning":"是必要的","examples":[{"en":"Having up-to-date maps is essential.","zh":"擁有最新地圖是必要的。"},{"en":"Is essential means is necessary and very important.","zh":"is essential 的意思是必要且非常重要。"},{"en":"Clean water is essential in every home and school.","zh":"潔淨食水在每個家庭和學校都是必要的。"},{"en":"Accurate information is essential because wrong facts can lead to wrong decisions.","zh":"準確資訊是必要的，因為錯誤事實可以導致錯誤決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than saying something is useful or nice to have.","zh":"這個短語比說某事有用或有會更好更強烈。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"drone technology","meaning":"無人機技術","examples":[{"en":"Drone technology is a useful tool for forest restoration.","zh":"無人機技術是森林復育的實用工具。"},{"en":"Drone technology uses small unmanned flying devices to collect images, data, or carry out tasks from the air.","zh":"drone technology 使用小型無人飛行裝置從空中收集圖像、數據或執行任務。"},{"en":"Farmers may use drone technology to check crop health without walking across every field.","zh":"農夫可能使用無人機技術檢查作物健康，而不用走遍每塊田。"},{"en":"Drone technology can save time because it reaches places that are difficult or dangerous for people.","zh":"無人機技術可以節省時間，因為它能到達人類難以或危險前往的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in modern mapping, farming, safety, and environmental work.","zh":"這個短語常出現在現代測繪、農業、安全和環境工作中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a useful tool in helping to","meaning":"有助於……的實用工具","examples":[{"en":"Drone technology is a useful tool in helping to monitor degraded forests.","zh":"無人機技術是有助於監察退化森林的實用工具。"},{"en":"A useful tool in helping to do something is something that supports or makes the task easier.","zh":"a useful tool in helping to do something 是支援某項任務或令它更容易的工具。"},{"en":"A checklist is a useful tool in helping to prepare for exams.","zh":"清單是有助於準備考試的實用工具。"},{"en":"Translation apps can be useful tools in helping tourists communicate in simple situations.","zh":"翻譯應用程式可以是有助於旅客在簡單情況中溝通的實用工具。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the tool assists the work but may not solve everything alone.","zh":"這個短語顯示工具能協助工作，但未必單靠它就能解決一切。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"prioritise and monitor","meaning":"排定優先次序並監察","examples":[{"en":"Drones can help prioritise and monitor areas of degraded forest.","zh":"無人機可以幫助排定退化森林地區的優先次序並監察它們。"},{"en":"To prioritise and monitor means to decide what needs attention first and then keep checking its condition.","zh":"prioritise and monitor 的意思是決定甚麼最需要優先關注，然後持續檢查其情況。"},{"en":"Teachers prioritise and monitor students who need extra help before exams.","zh":"老師在考試前會為需要額外幫助的學生排定優先次序並監察。"},{"en":"Health workers prioritise and monitor high-risk patients so problems are found early.","zh":"醫護人員會為高風險病人排定優先次序並監察，讓問題及早被發現。"},{"en":"This phrase combines decision-making with ongoing observation.","zh":"這個短語結合決策和持續觀察。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"degraded forest","meaning":"退化森林","examples":[{"en":"Drones can monitor areas of degraded forest for restoration.","zh":"無人機可以監察需要復育的退化森林地區。"},{"en":"Degraded forest is forest that has been damaged and no longer functions as healthily as before.","zh":"degraded forest 是已受損且不再像以前一樣健康運作的森林。"},{"en":"A degraded forest may have fewer trees, poorer soil, and fewer animals than a healthy forest.","zh":"退化森林可能比健康森林有較少樹木、較差土壤和較少動物。"},{"en":"Degraded forests need restoration because they may lose their ability to store carbon and support wildlife.","zh":"退化森林需要復育，因為它們可能失去儲存碳和支援野生動物的能力。"},{"en":"This phrase means damaged forest, not necessarily land with no trees at all.","zh":"這個短語指受損森林，不一定是完全沒有樹的土地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"restoration","meaning":"復育；恢復","examples":[{"en":"Drone technology can support forest restoration.","zh":"無人機技術可以支援森林復育。"},{"en":"Restoration means bringing something damaged back to a healthier or better condition.","zh":"restoration 的意思是把受損的東西帶回較健康或較好的狀態。"},{"en":"A community may work on river restoration by removing rubbish and planting native plants.","zh":"社區可能透過清除垃圾和種植本土植物來進行河流復育。"},{"en":"Restoration can take years because natural systems recover slowly.","zh":"復育可能需要多年，因為自然系統恢復緩慢。"},{"en":"This word is used for buildings, ecosystems, health, and communities.","zh":"這個詞可用於建築、生態系統、健康和社區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"identify and quantify","meaning":"識別並量化","examples":[{"en":"Drones are used to identify and quantify damage in the Amazon.","zh":"無人機被用來識別並量化亞馬遜的破壞。"},{"en":"To identify and quantify something means to find it and measure how much of it there is.","zh":"identify and quantify something 的意思是找出某事，並量度它有多少。"},{"en":"A school may identify and quantify absenteeism by counting how many students miss lessons.","zh":"學校可能透過計算缺課學生人數來識別並量化缺勤問題。"},{"en":"Scientists identify and quantify forest damage so they can decide where help is most needed.","zh":"科學家識別並量化森林破壞，從而決定哪裡最需要幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase combines recognition with measurement.","zh":"這個短語結合辨認和量度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"parts of the Amazon","meaning":"亞馬遜部分地區","examples":[{"en":"Drones identify how parts of the Amazon are being damaged.","zh":"無人機識別亞馬遜部分地區如何受到破壞。"},{"en":"Parts of the Amazon means particular areas within the Amazon rainforest or region.","zh":"parts of the Amazon 指亞馬遜雨林或地區中的特定區域。"},{"en":"Some parts of the Amazon are remote and difficult for researchers to reach on foot.","zh":"亞馬遜部分地區偏遠，研究人員難以步行到達。"},{"en":"Damage in parts of the Amazon can affect wildlife, local people, and global climate systems.","zh":"亞馬遜部分地區的破壞可以影響野生動物、本地人和全球氣候系統。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to sections of a vast region, not the whole Amazon at once.","zh":"這個短語指廣闊地區中的部分，而不是整個亞馬遜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be devastated by","meaning":"受到……嚴重破壞","examples":[{"en":"Parts of the Amazon are being devastated by human activities.","zh":"亞馬遜部分地區正受到人類活動嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"To be devastated by something means to be severely damaged or destroyed by it.","zh":"be devastated by something 的意思是受到某事嚴重損害或摧毀。"},{"en":"A coastal town may be devastated by a powerful storm.","zh":"沿岸小鎮可能受到強烈風暴嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"Forests can be devastated by illegal logging, fire, or mining.","zh":"森林可以受到非法伐木、火災或採礦嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “affected” because the damage is serious.","zh":"這個短語比 affected 更強，因為損害很嚴重。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"human activities","meaning":"人類活動","examples":[{"en":"Human activities such as cattle rearing and illegal logging damage forests.","zh":"飼養牛隻和非法伐木等人類活動會破壞森林。"},{"en":"Human activities are things people do that affect the environment, economy, or society.","zh":"human activities 是人類所做並影響環境、經濟或社會的事情。"},{"en":"Building roads, farming land, and burning fuel are human activities that can change ecosystems.","zh":"修路、耕種土地和燃燒燃料都是可以改變生態系統的人類活動。"},{"en":"Some human activities damage nature, while others can restore and protect it.","zh":"有些人類活動傷害自然，另一些則可以復育和保護自然。"},{"en":"This phrase is broad and depends on context.","zh":"這個短語很廣泛，意思取決於語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rearing cattle","meaning":"飼養牛隻","examples":[{"en":"Rearing cattle can contribute to forest destruction.","zh":"飼養牛隻可以導致森林破壞。"},{"en":"Rearing cattle means raising cows or bulls for meat, milk, leather, or farming work.","zh":"rearing cattle 的意思是飼養牛，用於肉類、牛奶、皮革或農務。"},{"en":"Farmers rearing cattle need land for grazing, water, and animal care.","zh":"飼養牛隻的農夫需要放牧土地、水和動物照料。"},{"en":"If forests are cleared for cattle pasture, rearing cattle can drive deforestation.","zh":"如果森林被清除作為牛隻牧場，飼養牛隻可以推動砍伐森林。"},{"en":"This phrase describes animal farming, not simply owning pets.","zh":"這個短語描述畜牧，而不是單純養寵物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"illegal logging","meaning":"非法伐木","examples":[{"en":"Illegal logging is one cause of forest devastation.","zh":"非法伐木是森林嚴重破壞的原因之一。"},{"en":"Illegal logging means cutting down trees without legal permission or against forest protection rules.","zh":"illegal logging 的意思是在沒有法律許可或違反森林保護規則下砍樹。"},{"en":"Illegal logging may happen at night in remote forests to avoid officials.","zh":"非法伐木可能在偏遠森林的夜間發生，以避開官員。"},{"en":"Illegal logging damages ecosystems and can steal resources from local communities.","zh":"非法伐木會破壞生態系統，並可能奪走本地社區資源。"},{"en":"This phrase is connected to law, profit, and environmental harm.","zh":"這個短語與法律、利潤和環境損害有關。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a good example of where","meaning":"一個……的好例子","examples":[{"en":"Lampang Province is a good example of where the right trees were picked.","zh":"南邦府是一個選對樹種的好例子。"},{"en":"A good example of where something happened is a place or case that clearly shows a successful or important point.","zh":"a good example of where something happened 是清楚展示成功或重要觀點的地方或案例。"},{"en":"This school is a good example of where reading programmes improved student confidence.","zh":"這間學校是一個閱讀計劃改善學生信心的好例子。"},{"en":"Examples help readers understand an idea because they show it in a real situation.","zh":"例子幫助讀者理解想法，因為它在真實情況中展示該想法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence through a specific place or case.","zh":"這個短語透過特定地方或案例引入證據。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the right trees were picked","meaning":"選對樹種","examples":[{"en":"The right trees were picked to restore the forest in Lampang Province.","zh":"為復育南邦府的森林，團隊選對樹種。"},{"en":"The right trees were picked means suitable tree species were chosen for the local environment and goals.","zh":"the right trees were picked 的意思是為本地環境和目標選擇合適樹種。"},{"en":"For a school garden, the right trees are picked when they provide shade without unsafe roots.","zh":"對學校花園而言，若樹木能提供樹蔭而沒有危險樹根，就是選對樹種。"},{"en":"Picking the right trees can help wildlife return and reduce maintenance problems.","zh":"選對樹種可以幫助野生動物回歸，並減少維護問題。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises correct species choice.","zh":"這個短語強調正確的物種選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"achieve a restored forest","meaning":"成功復育森林","examples":[{"en":"The project picked the right trees to achieve a restored forest.","zh":"這個項目選對樹種，以成功復育森林。"},{"en":"To achieve a restored forest means to successfully bring damaged forest land back to a healthier forest condition.","zh":"achieve a restored forest 的意思是成功把受損森林土地帶回較健康的森林狀態。"},{"en":"A community may achieve a restored forest by planting native species and protecting young trees.","zh":"社區可能透過種植本土物種和保護幼樹來成功復育森林。"},{"en":"Achieving a restored forest takes time because animals, soil, and plant diversity must return.","zh":"成功復育森林需要時間，因為動物、土壤和植物多樣性都必須回來。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the final restoration result.","zh":"這個短語集中於最終復育成果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"previously forested site","meaning":"曾經是森林的地點","examples":[{"en":"The project took place on a previously forested site.","zh":"這個項目在曾經是森林的地點進行。"},{"en":"A previously forested site is land that used to be covered by forest.","zh":"previously forested site 是過去曾被森林覆蓋的土地。"},{"en":"A mining area can be a previously forested site if trees were removed before excavation.","zh":"如果挖掘前樹木被移除，採礦區可以是曾經是森林的地點。"},{"en":"Restoring a previously forested site often makes ecological sense because forest once naturally grew there.","zh":"復育曾經是森林的地點通常有生態意義，因為森林曾自然在那裡生長。"},{"en":"This phrase gives historical information about the land.","zh":"這個短語提供土地的歷史資訊。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"degraded through mining","meaning":"因採礦而退化","examples":[{"en":"The site had been degraded through mining.","zh":"該地點因採礦而退化。"},{"en":"Degraded through mining means damaged because minerals, stone, or other materials were removed from the land.","zh":"degraded through mining 的意思是因從土地中移除礦物、石材或其他材料而受損。"},{"en":"Land degraded through mining may have poor soil, little vegetation, and polluted water.","zh":"因採礦而退化的土地可能有貧瘠土壤、少量植被和受污染水源。"},{"en":"Mining can degrade land by removing topsoil and changing drainage patterns.","zh":"採礦可以透過移除表土和改變排水模式令土地退化。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the cause of environmental damage.","zh":"這個短語解釋環境損害的原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be reforested by","meaning":"由……進行再造林","examples":[{"en":"The site was reforested by a cement company and Chiang Mai University.","zh":"該地點由一間水泥公司和清邁大學進行再造林。"},{"en":"To be reforested by someone means the forest was restored through that person or organisation’s work.","zh":"be reforested by someone 的意思是森林透過某人或某機構的工作而恢復。"},{"en":"A damaged hillside may be reforested by volunteers and local schools.","zh":"受損山坡可能由義工和本地學校進行再造林。"},{"en":"When land is reforested by experts and local people together, the project may be more sustainable.","zh":"當土地由專家和本地人一起進行再造林，項目可能更可持續。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who carried out the reforestation.","zh":"這個短語指出誰執行再造林工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"together with","meaning":"與……一起","examples":[{"en":"A cement company worked together with Chiang Mai University.","zh":"一間水泥公司與清邁大學一起合作。"},{"en":"Together with means in cooperation with or along with someone or something else.","zh":"together with 的意思是與某人或某事合作或一同進行。"},{"en":"A school may work together with parents to improve students’ reading habits.","zh":"學校可能與家長一起改善學生的閱讀習慣。"},{"en":"Projects often work better when experts work together with local communities.","zh":"當專家與本地社區一起工作，項目通常會更好。"},{"en":"This phrase shows partnership or combination.","zh":"這個短語顯示合作或結合。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"spread topsoil","meaning":"鋪上表土","examples":[{"en":"The team spread 60 cm of topsoil before planting trees.","zh":"團隊在植樹前鋪上60厘米表土。"},{"en":"To spread topsoil means to lay the upper, fertile layer of soil over an area.","zh":"spread topsoil 的意思是在某地鋪上上層肥沃土壤。"},{"en":"Gardeners spread topsoil before planting grass so roots can grow better.","zh":"園丁在種草前鋪上表土，讓根部能更好生長。"},{"en":"Spreading topsoil can improve poor land because young plants need nutrients and structure.","zh":"鋪上表土可以改善貧瘠土地，因為幼苗需要養分和結構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical preparation step before planting.","zh":"這個短語描述種植前的實際準備步驟。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"native tree species","meaning":"本土樹種","examples":[{"en":"The team planted 14 different native tree species.","zh":"團隊種植了14種不同本土樹種。"},{"en":"Native tree species are tree species that naturally belong to a particular area.","zh":"native tree species 是自然屬於特定地區的樹木物種。"},{"en":"A park may use native tree species because local birds and insects already depend on them.","zh":"公園可能使用本土樹種，因為本地鳥類和昆蟲已依賴它們。"},{"en":"Native tree species often need less artificial care because they suit the local climate and soil.","zh":"本土樹種通常需要較少人工照料，因為它們適合本地氣候和土壤。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when planning ecological restoration.","zh":"這個短語在規劃生態復育時很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"several species of","meaning":"幾種……","examples":[{"en":"The project included several species of fig.","zh":"這個項目包括幾種無花果樹。"},{"en":"Several species of something means more than two different kinds within the same general group.","zh":"several species of something 的意思是在同一大類中有多於兩種不同物種。"},{"en":"A garden may contain several species of butterfly if it has many flowering plants.","zh":"如果花園有許多開花植物，它可能有幾種蝴蝶。"},{"en":"Including several species can increase resilience because each species may respond differently to stress.","zh":"包括幾種物種可以增加韌性，因為每個物種可能對壓力有不同反應。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights diversity within one category.","zh":"這個短語強調同一類別中的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"keystone species","meaning":"關鍵物種","examples":[{"en":"Figs are a keystone species in tropical forests.","zh":"無花果樹是熱帶森林中的關鍵物種。"},{"en":"A keystone species is a species that plays an especially important role in keeping an ecosystem healthy.","zh":"keystone species 是在維持生態系統健康方面發揮特別重要作用的物種。"},{"en":"Bees can act like a keystone species where many plants depend on their pollination.","zh":"在許多植物依賴蜜蜂授粉的地方，蜜蜂可以像關鍵物種一樣發揮作用。"},{"en":"If a keystone species disappears, many other species may suffer.","zh":"如果關鍵物種消失，許多其他物種可能受害。"},{"en":"The phrase comes from the idea that one key part can hold a whole structure together.","zh":"這個短語來自一個關鍵部分能支撐整個結構的概念。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"critical role","meaning":"關鍵作用","examples":[{"en":"Figs play a critical role in maintaining wildlife populations.","zh":"無花果樹在維持野生動物族群方面發揮關鍵作用。"},{"en":"A critical role is an extremely important function in making something work or continue.","zh":"critical role 是令某事運作或延續的極其重要功能。"},{"en":"Nurses play a critical role in patient care because they monitor changes closely.","zh":"護士在病人護理中發揮關鍵作用，因為他們密切監察變化。"},{"en":"In forests, food trees can play a critical role by supporting animals during difficult seasons.","zh":"在森林中，食物樹可以透過在困難季節支援動物而發揮關鍵作用。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises importance and necessity.","zh":"這個短語強調重要性和必要性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"play a role in","meaning":"在……中發揮作用","examples":[{"en":"Figs play a critical role in maintaining wildlife populations.","zh":"無花果樹在維持野生動物族群方面發揮關鍵作用。"},{"en":"To play a role in something means to have a part or function in causing, supporting, or shaping it.","zh":"play a role in something 的意思是在造成、支援或塑造某事方面有部分功能。"},{"en":"Parents play a role in children’s reading habits by keeping books at home.","zh":"父母透過在家中放置書本，在孩子閱讀習慣中發揮作用。"},{"en":"Exercise plays a role in health because it affects sleep, mood, and strength.","zh":"運動在健康中發揮作用，因為它影響睡眠、心情和體力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows contribution, not always full responsibility.","zh":"這個短語顯示貢獻，而不一定是全部責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"maintaining wildlife populations","meaning":"維持野生動物族群","examples":[{"en":"Figs help maintain wildlife populations.","zh":"無花果樹幫助維持野生動物族群。"},{"en":"Maintaining wildlife populations means keeping wild animal groups healthy and numerous enough to survive.","zh":"maintaining wildlife populations 的意思是保持野生動物群體健康並有足夠數量生存。"},{"en":"Protected wetlands help maintain bird populations by providing food and nesting sites.","zh":"受保護濕地透過提供食物和築巢地點來維持鳥類族群。"},{"en":"If food sources disappear, maintaining wildlife populations becomes much harder.","zh":"如果食物來源消失，維持野生動物族群會困難得多。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on long-term support for wild animals.","zh":"這個短語集中於對野生動物的長期支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be central to","meaning":"是……的核心","examples":[{"en":"Figs are central to tropical reforestation projects.","zh":"無花果樹是熱帶再造林計劃的核心。"},{"en":"To be central to something means to be very important at the heart of it.","zh":"be central to something 的意思是在某事中非常重要，處於核心位置。"},{"en":"Clear communication is central to successful teamwork.","zh":"清晰溝通是成功團隊合作的核心。"},{"en":"Native species are central to restoration because they help rebuild natural relationships.","zh":"本土物種是復育的核心，因為它們幫助重建自然關係。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is not minor but essential.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事不是次要，而是必不可少。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tropical reforestation projects","meaning":"熱帶再造林計劃","examples":[{"en":"Figs are important in tropical reforestation projects.","zh":"無花果樹在熱帶再造林計劃中很重要。"},{"en":"Tropical reforestation projects are forest restoration efforts in hot, humid regions near the tropics.","zh":"tropical reforestation projects 是在接近熱帶的炎熱潮濕地區進行的森林復育工作。"},{"en":"Tropical reforestation projects often need species that can grow quickly and support wildlife.","zh":"熱帶再造林計劃常需要能快速生長並支援野生動物的物種。"},{"en":"These projects can protect biodiversity because tropical forests contain many species.","zh":"這些計劃可以保護生物多樣性，因為熱帶森林包含許多物種。"},{"en":"This phrase combines location, climate, and restoration purpose.","zh":"這個短語結合地點、氣候和復育目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"accelerate the speed of","meaning":"加快……的速度","examples":[{"en":"Figs accelerate the speed of the recovery process.","zh":"無花果樹加快復育過程的速度。"},{"en":"To accelerate the speed of something means to make it happen faster.","zh":"accelerate the speed of something 的意思是令某事發生得更快。"},{"en":"Extra reading practice can accelerate the speed of language improvement.","zh":"額外閱讀練習可以加快語言進步的速度。"},{"en":"Good soil preparation can accelerate the speed of plant growth.","zh":"良好土壤準備可以加快植物生長的速度。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on making a process quicker.","zh":"這個短語集中於令一個過程更快。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"recovery process","meaning":"復育過程","examples":[{"en":"Figs help accelerate the recovery process.","zh":"無花果樹幫助加快復育過程。"},{"en":"A recovery process is the series of steps through which something damaged returns to a healthier condition.","zh":"recovery process 是受損事物回到較健康狀態的一連串步驟。"},{"en":"After an injury, the recovery process may include rest, exercise, and medical checks.","zh":"受傷後，恢復過程可能包括休息、運動和醫療檢查。"},{"en":"In a forest, the recovery process includes soil improvement, plant growth, and wildlife return.","zh":"在森林中，復育過程包括土壤改善、植物生長和野生動物回歸。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that healing or restoration happens gradually.","zh":"這個短語顯示治癒或復育是逐步發生的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"attract animals and birds","meaning":"吸引動物和雀鳥","examples":[{"en":"Figs attract animals and birds to restored forests.","zh":"無花果樹吸引動物和雀鳥到復育森林。"},{"en":"To attract animals and birds means to bring them to a place by providing food, shelter, or suitable habitat.","zh":"attract animals and birds 的意思是透過提供食物、庇護或合適棲息地，把動物和鳥類帶到一個地方。"},{"en":"A garden with berries and water can attract animals and birds.","zh":"有漿果和水的花園可以吸引動物和雀鳥。"},{"en":"Attracting animals and birds helps a restored forest because they spread seeds and support food chains.","zh":"吸引動物和雀鳥有助復育森林，因為牠們會散播種子並支援食物鏈。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how plants can invite wildlife back.","zh":"這個短語顯示植物如何邀請野生動物回來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"act as","meaning":"充當；作為","examples":[{"en":"Animals and birds act as natural seed dispersers.","zh":"動物和雀鳥充當天然種子傳播者。"},{"en":"To act as something means to serve a particular function or role.","zh":"act as something 的意思是發揮某種功能或角色。"},{"en":"A library can act as a quiet study space after school.","zh":"圖書館可以作為放學後的安靜自修空間。"},{"en":"Trees can act as natural air filters by trapping dust and absorbing gases.","zh":"樹木可以透過阻隔灰塵和吸收氣體充當天然空氣過濾器。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what role something plays.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物發揮甚麼角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"natural seed dispersers","meaning":"天然種子傳播者","examples":[{"en":"Birds and animals can act as natural seed dispersers.","zh":"雀鳥和動物可以充當天然種子傳播者。"},{"en":"Natural seed dispersers are animals or natural forces that move seeds away from the parent plant.","zh":"natural seed dispersers 是把種子從母株帶到其他地方的動物或自然力量。"},{"en":"Birds become natural seed dispersers when they eat fruit and drop seeds elsewhere.","zh":"當雀鳥吃水果並在其他地方留下種子，牠們就成為天然種子傳播者。"},{"en":"Seed dispersers help forests spread and recover because young plants can grow in new places.","zh":"種子傳播者幫助森林擴展和恢復，因為幼苗可以在新地方生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a natural way plants reproduce and spread.","zh":"這個短語描述植物繁殖和擴散的自然方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"promote diversity","meaning":"促進多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Natural seed dispersers help promote diversity.","zh":"天然種子傳播者有助促進多樣性。"},{"en":"To promote diversity means to encourage a wider variety of species, people, ideas, or choices.","zh":"promote diversity 的意思是鼓勵更多不同物種、人、想法或選擇。"},{"en":"A school library can promote diversity by offering books from many cultures.","zh":"學校圖書館可以透過提供來自多種文化的書本來促進多樣性。"},{"en":"In forests, seed dispersal promotes diversity because many different plants can regrow.","zh":"在森林中，種子散播促進多樣性，因為許多不同植物可以再生。"},{"en":"This phrase shows support for variety rather than sameness.","zh":"這個短語顯示支持多樣，而不是單一。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"healthy regrowth","meaning":"健康再生","examples":[{"en":"Seed dispersal supports the healthy regrowth of plant species.","zh":"種子散播支援植物物種健康再生。"},{"en":"Healthy regrowth means new plants grow back strongly after damage or clearing.","zh":"healthy regrowth 的意思是植物在受損或被清除後強健地重新生長。"},{"en":"After a fire, healthy regrowth may appear when native plants return naturally.","zh":"火災後，當本土植物自然回來，可能會出現健康再生。"},{"en":"Healthy regrowth depends on good soil, enough water, and protection from further damage.","zh":"健康再生取決於良好土壤、足夠水分和避免再次受損。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on recovery that is strong and natural.","zh":"這個短語集中於強健而自然的恢復。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a wide range of","meaning":"各式各樣的","examples":[{"en":"A wide range of plant species can regrow in restored forests.","zh":"各式各樣的植物物種可以在復育森林中再生。"},{"en":"A wide range of something means many different kinds of it.","zh":"a wide range of something 的意思是許多不同種類的某物。"},{"en":"A good library offers a wide range of books for different ages and interests.","zh":"好圖書館為不同年齡和興趣提供各式各樣的書本。"},{"en":"A wide range of species makes an ecosystem richer and more resilient.","zh":"各式各樣的物種令生態系統更豐富和更有韌性。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises variety and breadth.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣和廣度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"plant species","meaning":"植物物種","examples":[{"en":"Healthy regrowth can include a wide range of plant species.","zh":"健康再生可以包括各式各樣的植物物種。"},{"en":"Plant species are different kinds of plants, such as trees, grasses, flowers, or shrubs.","zh":"plant species 是不同種類的植物，例如樹木、草、花或灌木。"},{"en":"A rainforest contains thousands of plant species, many of which support animals and insects.","zh":"雨林包含數以千計的植物物種，其中許多支援動物和昆蟲。"},{"en":"Losing plant species can damage food chains because many animals depend on specific plants.","zh":"失去植物物種可以破壞食物鏈，因為許多動物依賴特定植物。"},{"en":"This phrase is a scientific way to talk about kinds of plants.","zh":"這個短語是談論植物種類的科學說法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"unlike the majority of","meaning":"與大多數……不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike the majority of fruit trees, figs bear fruit all year round.","zh":"與大多數果樹不同，無花果樹全年結果。"},{"en":"Unlike the majority of something means different from most members of that group.","zh":"unlike the majority of something 的意思是與該群體中大多數成員不同。"},{"en":"Unlike the majority of students, she enjoys studying very early in the morning.","zh":"與大多數學生不同，她喜歡在清晨很早溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights an important difference from what is usual.","zh":"這個短語突出了與通常情況不同的重要差異。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why one example is special.","zh":"當解釋為何某個例子特別時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bear fruit all year round","meaning":"全年結果","examples":[{"en":"Figs bear fruit all year round.","zh":"無花果樹全年結果。"},{"en":"To bear fruit all year round means to produce fruit throughout the whole year.","zh":"bear fruit all year round 的意思是全年都產生果實。"},{"en":"A tree that bears fruit all year round can provide steady food for animals.","zh":"全年結果的樹可以為動物提供穩定食物。"},{"en":"If a community has fruit trees that bear fruit all year round, food supply may become more reliable.","zh":"如果社區有全年結果的果樹，食物供應可能變得更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase can also metaphorically mean producing results continuously, but here it is literal.","zh":"這個短語也可比喻持續產生成果，但在這裡是字面意思。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"reliable food source","meaning":"穩定食物來源","examples":[{"en":"Figs provide a reliable food source for many species.","zh":"無花果樹為許多物種提供穩定食物來源。"},{"en":"A reliable food source is food that can be found regularly and depended on.","zh":"reliable food source 是可以定期找到並可依賴的食物。"},{"en":"A school canteen is a reliable food source for students who do not bring lunch.","zh":"學校飯堂是沒有帶午餐學生的穩定食物來源。"},{"en":"In forests, reliable food sources help animals survive seasons when other food is scarce.","zh":"在森林中，穩定食物來源幫助動物度過其他食物稀少的季節。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises steadiness and dependability.","zh":"這個短語強調穩定和可靠。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rainy seasons","meaning":"雨季","examples":[{"en":"Monkeys returned after only three rainy seasons.","zh":"猴子只經過三個雨季後就回來了。"},{"en":"Rainy seasons are periods of the year when a region receives much more rain than usual.","zh":"rainy seasons 是一年中某地降雨比平常多得多的時期。"},{"en":"Farmers may plant crops at the beginning of the rainy season.","zh":"農夫可能在雨季開始時種植農作物。"},{"en":"In restoration projects, rainy seasons can help young trees grow because water is more available.","zh":"在復育項目中，雨季可以幫助幼樹生長，因為水分較充足。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in tropical and subtropical climate descriptions.","zh":"這個短語常見於熱帶和亞熱帶氣候描述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"naturally dispersing seeds","meaning":"自然散播種子","examples":[{"en":"Monkeys helped by naturally dispersing seeds.","zh":"猴子透過自然散播種子提供幫助。"},{"en":"Naturally dispersing seeds means spreading seeds through normal natural processes, such as eating fruit and moving around.","zh":"naturally dispersing seeds 的意思是透過正常自然過程散播種子，例如吃果實和四處移動。"},{"en":"Birds naturally disperse seeds when they eat berries and later drop seeds in new places.","zh":"雀鳥吃漿果並之後在新地方留下種子時，就自然散播種子。"},{"en":"Natural seed dispersal helps forests recover without people planting every tree by hand.","zh":"自然種子散播幫助森林恢復，而不用人手種下每一棵樹。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how animals support plant regrowth.","zh":"這個短語顯示動物如何支援植物再生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"through defecation","meaning":"透過排便","examples":[{"en":"Monkeys dispersed seeds through defecation.","zh":"猴子透過排便散播種子。"},{"en":"Through defecation means by passing waste from the body after eating.","zh":"through defecation 的意思是在進食後透過排出身體廢物。"},{"en":"Animals can spread seeds through defecation after eating fruit.","zh":"動物吃水果後，可以透過排便散播種子。"},{"en":"Seeds spread through defecation may grow far from the parent tree.","zh":"透過排便散播的種子可能在遠離母樹的地方生長。"},{"en":"This phrase is biological and direct, so it is used mainly in scientific explanation.","zh":"這個短語是生物學用語，較直接，主要用於科學解釋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"aim to make sure that","meaning":"旨在確保","examples":[{"en":"Reforestation projects should aim to make sure that communities are consulted.","zh":"再造林計劃應旨在確保社區得到諮詢。"},{"en":"To aim to make sure that something happens means to set it as a clear goal and take steps to achieve it.","zh":"aim to make sure that something happens 的意思是把某事定為清晰目標，並採取步驟達成它。"},{"en":"Schools should aim to make sure that every student understands the safety rules.","zh":"學校應旨在確保每位學生都理解安全規則。"},{"en":"A project that aims to make sure people are consulted is more likely to earn trust.","zh":"旨在確保人們得到諮詢的項目，更可能獲得信任。"},{"en":"This phrase combines intention with responsibility.","zh":"這個短語結合意圖與責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"local communities are consulted","meaning":"諮詢本地社區","examples":[{"en":"Local communities should be consulted in reforestation projects.","zh":"再造林計劃應諮詢本地社區。"},{"en":"Local communities are consulted when people living in the area are asked for their views before decisions are made.","zh":"local communities are consulted 指在作出決定前，詢問居於該區人士的看法。"},{"en":"Residents should be consulted before a new road changes their neighbourhood.","zh":"在新道路改變社區前，應諮詢居民。"},{"en":"Consulting local communities can prevent conflict because people feel heard and respected.","zh":"諮詢本地社區可以避免衝突，因為人們感到被聆聽和尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses participation before action.","zh":"這個短語強調行動前的參與。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"involved in","meaning":"參與……","examples":[{"en":"Local communities should be involved in the decision-making process.","zh":"本地社區應參與決策過程。"},{"en":"To be involved in something means to take part in it or have a role in it.","zh":"be involved in something 的意思是參與某事或在其中有角色。"},{"en":"Parents may be involved in school planning through meetings and surveys.","zh":"家長可能透過會議和問卷參與學校規劃。"},{"en":"People support projects more when they are involved in decisions that affect them.","zh":"當人們參與影響自己的決定，他們更會支持項目。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests participation, not just being informed afterwards.","zh":"這個短語表示參與，而不是事後才被告知。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"decision-making process","meaning":"決策過程","examples":[{"en":"Local communities should be involved in the decision-making process.","zh":"本地社區應參與決策過程。"},{"en":"The decision-making process is the series of steps used to choose what should be done.","zh":"decision-making process 是用來選擇應該做甚麼的一連串步驟。"},{"en":"A family’s decision-making process may include discussing costs, needs, and timing.","zh":"家庭的決策過程可能包括討論成本、需要和時間。"},{"en":"A fair decision-making process helps people trust the final result, even if they disagree.","zh":"公平的決策過程幫助人們信任最終結果，即使他們不同意。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how decisions are made, not only the decision itself.","zh":"這個短語集中於決定如何作出，而不只是決定本身。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"restoration of mangrove forests","meaning":"紅樹林復育","examples":[{"en":"The restoration of mangrove forests in Madagascar benefited the community.","zh":"馬達加斯加的紅樹林復育令社區受益。"},{"en":"The restoration of mangrove forests means bringing damaged mangrove areas back to a healthy condition.","zh":"restoration of mangrove forests 的意思是把受損紅樹林地區帶回健康狀態。"},{"en":"Coastal villages may support restoration of mangrove forests because mangroves protect homes and fish habitats.","zh":"沿岸村落可能支持紅樹林復育，因為紅樹林保護家園和魚類棲息地。"},{"en":"Restoring mangroves can improve biodiversity, reduce flooding, and support local jobs.","zh":"復育紅樹林可以改善生物多樣性、減少洪水，並支援本地就業。"},{"en":"This phrase connects ecological recovery with coastal protection.","zh":"這個短語把生態恢復與海岸保護連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"mangrove forests","meaning":"紅樹林","examples":[{"en":"Mangrove forests can protect coastal communities.","zh":"紅樹林可以保護沿岸社區。"},{"en":"Mangrove forests are coastal forests made up of salt-tolerant trees growing in muddy or tidal areas.","zh":"mangrove forests 是由耐鹽樹木組成、長於泥灘或潮汐區的沿岸森林。"},{"en":"Mangrove forests provide shelter for young fish, crabs, birds, and other wildlife.","zh":"紅樹林為幼魚、蟹、鳥類和其他野生動物提供庇護。"},{"en":"When mangrove forests are destroyed, coastlines may become more exposed to storms and erosion.","zh":"當紅樹林被破壞，海岸線可能更容易受到風暴和侵蝕影響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a special forest ecosystem between land and sea.","zh":"這個短語指介乎陸地與海洋之間的特殊森林生態系統。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"succeeded in creating","meaning":"成功創造","examples":[{"en":"The project succeeded in creating real benefits for the community.","zh":"這個項目成功為社區創造實際好處。"},{"en":"Succeeded in creating means managed to produce or bring about something successfully.","zh":"succeeded in creating 的意思是成功產生或帶來某事物。"},{"en":"The school succeeded in creating a calmer classroom by setting clear routines.","zh":"學校透過建立清晰常規，成功創造更安靜的課室。"},{"en":"A project succeeds in creating change when people can see practical improvements in daily life.","zh":"當人們能在日常生活中看見實際改善，項目就成功創造改變。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a successful result.","zh":"這個短語集中於成功結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"real benefits","meaning":"實際好處","examples":[{"en":"The project created real benefits for the local community.","zh":"這個項目為本地社區創造實際好處。"},{"en":"Real benefits are practical advantages that people can actually feel or use.","zh":"real benefits 是人們能真正感受到或使用的實際優勢。"},{"en":"A new bus route brings real benefits if workers can get home faster and cheaper.","zh":"如果新巴士路線令員工更快、更便宜回家，它就帶來實際好處。"},{"en":"Environmental projects bring real benefits when they improve health, income, safety, or daily life.","zh":"當環境項目改善健康、收入、安全或日常生活，它就帶來實際好處。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts genuine improvement with empty promises.","zh":"這個短語把真正改善與空洞承諾作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"destruction of","meaning":"對……的破壞","examples":[{"en":"The destruction of the mangrove forests harmed wildlife and local people.","zh":"對紅樹林的破壞傷害了野生動物和本地人。"},{"en":"The destruction of something means severe damage to it or the complete loss of it.","zh":"destruction of something 的意思是對某物造成嚴重損害或使其完全消失。"},{"en":"The destruction of a playground can leave children without a safe place to play.","zh":"對遊樂場的破壞可以令兒童失去安全玩耍地方。"},{"en":"Destruction of forests harms more than trees because animals and people depend on them.","zh":"對森林的破壞傷害的不只是樹木，因為動物和人都依賴森林。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights serious loss or damage.","zh":"這個短語突出了嚴重損失或損害。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"have a terrible impact on","meaning":"對……造成嚴重影響","examples":[{"en":"The destruction had a terrible impact on plant and animal life.","zh":"這種破壞對動植物生命造成嚴重影響。"},{"en":"To have a terrible impact on something means to affect it very badly.","zh":"have a terrible impact on something 的意思是非常嚴重地影響某事。"},{"en":"Long-term bullying can have a terrible impact on a child’s confidence.","zh":"長期欺凌可以對孩子的信心造成嚴重影響。"},{"en":"Pollution can have a terrible impact on rivers by killing fish and plants.","zh":"污染可以透過殺死魚類和植物，對河流造成嚴重影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is strong and negative.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈而負面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"plant and animal life","meaning":"動植物生命","examples":[{"en":"The destruction of mangroves harmed plant and animal life.","zh":"對紅樹林的破壞傷害了動植物生命。"},{"en":"Plant and animal life means the plants and animals living in a particular place.","zh":"plant and animal life 指生活在特定地方的植物和動物。"},{"en":"A healthy pond supports plant and animal life such as reeds, fish, frogs, and insects.","zh":"健康池塘支援蘆葦、魚、青蛙和昆蟲等動植物生命。"},{"en":"When habitats are destroyed, plant and animal life may decline quickly.","zh":"當棲息地被破壞，動植物生命可能快速減少。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple but broad, covering many living things.","zh":"這個短語簡單但廣泛，涵蓋許多生命。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"badly affected","meaning":"嚴重影響","examples":[{"en":"The destruction of mangroves badly affected the fishing industry.","zh":"紅樹林被破壞嚴重影響漁業。"},{"en":"Badly affected means seriously harmed or strongly influenced in a negative way.","zh":"badly affected 的意思是受到嚴重傷害或強烈負面影響。"},{"en":"Shops were badly affected when the road was closed for repairs.","zh":"道路關閉維修時，商店受到嚴重影響。"},{"en":"Students can be badly affected by noise if they have no quiet place to study.","zh":"如果學生沒有安靜地方溫習，他們可能受到噪音嚴重影響。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the effect is serious, not minor.","zh":"這個短語顯示影響嚴重，而不是輕微。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fishing industry","meaning":"漁業","examples":[{"en":"The fishing industry was a major source of employment for local people.","zh":"漁業是本地人的主要就業來源。"},{"en":"The fishing industry includes the people and businesses that catch, process, sell, or transport fish and seafood.","zh":"fishing industry 包括捕魚、加工、銷售或運送魚類和海鮮的人與企業。"},{"en":"A coastal town may depend on the fishing industry for jobs and food.","zh":"沿岸小鎮可能依賴漁業提供工作和食物。"},{"en":"If fish habitats are destroyed, the fishing industry may lose income and workers may suffer.","zh":"如果魚類棲息地被破壞，漁業可能失去收入，工人也可能受苦。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an economic sector linked to the sea or rivers.","zh":"這個短語指與海洋或河流有關的經濟行業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"major source of employment","meaning":"主要就業來源","examples":[{"en":"The fishing industry was a major source of employment in coastal areas.","zh":"漁業是沿岸地區的主要就業來源。"},{"en":"A major source of employment is an important provider of jobs for many people.","zh":"major source of employment 是為許多人提供工作的主要來源。"},{"en":"Tourism can be a major source of employment in towns with beaches and hotels.","zh":"在有海灘和酒店的城鎮，旅遊業可以是主要就業來源。"},{"en":"If a major source of employment disappears, families may lose income and young people may leave.","zh":"如果主要就業來源消失，家庭可能失去收入，年輕人可能離開。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an industry with jobs and livelihoods.","zh":"這個短語把行業與工作和生計連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"local people living in coastal areas","meaning":"居於沿岸地區的本地居民","examples":[{"en":"The fishing industry supported local people living in coastal areas.","zh":"漁業支援居於沿岸地區的本地居民。"},{"en":"Local people living in coastal areas are residents whose homes and livelihoods are near the sea or coast.","zh":"local people living in coastal areas 是家園和生計靠近海洋或海岸的居民。"},{"en":"Local people living in coastal areas may depend on fishing, tourism, and sea transport.","zh":"居於沿岸地區的本地居民可能依賴捕魚、旅遊和海上運輸。"},{"en":"Coastal people can be vulnerable to storms, flooding, and changes in marine ecosystems.","zh":"沿岸居民可能容易受到風暴、洪水和海洋生態系統變化影響。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the community most directly affected by coastal changes.","zh":"這個短語指出最直接受沿岸變化影響的社區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"involve hiring","meaning":"涉及聘請","examples":[{"en":"The project involved hiring local people to plant mangroves.","zh":"這個項目涉及聘請本地人種植紅樹林。"},{"en":"To involve hiring people means to include employing them as part of the project or activity.","zh":"involve hiring people 的意思是在項目或活動中包括僱用他們。"},{"en":"A school renovation project may involve hiring local builders and electricians.","zh":"學校翻新項目可能涉及聘請本地建築工人和電工。"},{"en":"Hiring local people can create income and increase support for a project.","zh":"聘請本地人可以創造收入並增加對項目的支持。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that employment is part of the plan.","zh":"這個短語顯示就業是計劃的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"care for","meaning":"照料","examples":[{"en":"Local people were hired to plant and care for the new mangrove trees.","zh":"本地人獲聘種植並照料新的紅樹林樹木。"},{"en":"To care for something means to look after it and keep it healthy or safe.","zh":"care for something 的意思是照顧某物，使其保持健康或安全。"},{"en":"Students may care for a class plant by watering it and checking its leaves.","zh":"學生可能透過澆水和檢查葉子照料班房植物。"},{"en":"Young trees need care because they may die without water, protection, or monitoring.","zh":"幼樹需要照料，因為沒有水、保護或監察，它們可能死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests ongoing responsibility, not just one action.","zh":"這個短語表示持續責任，而不只是一次行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"resulted in","meaning":"導致；帶來","examples":[{"en":"Planting mangroves resulted in the return of a healthy aquatic ecosystem.","zh":"種植紅樹林帶來健康水生生態系統的回復。"},{"en":"Resulted in means caused something to happen as an outcome.","zh":"resulted in 的意思是造成某結果發生。"},{"en":"Regular practice resulted in better pronunciation and more confidence.","zh":"規律練習帶來更好發音和更多信心。"},{"en":"Heavy rain resulted in flooding because the drains were blocked.","zh":"大雨因排水渠堵塞而導致水浸。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an action or event with its result.","zh":"這個短語把行動或事件與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the return of","meaning":"……的回復","examples":[{"en":"The project resulted in the return of a healthy aquatic ecosystem.","zh":"這個項目帶來健康水生生態系統的回復。"},{"en":"The return of something means something comes back after being absent or damaged.","zh":"the return of something 的意思是某物在消失或受損後回來。"},{"en":"The return of birds to a park may show that the habitat is improving.","zh":"鳥類回到公園可能顯示棲息地正在改善。"},{"en":"The return of customers after a renovation can show that a shop has regained trust.","zh":"翻新後顧客回流可以顯示店舖重新獲得信任。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights recovery or reappearance.","zh":"這個短語突出了恢復或重新出現。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"healthy aquatic ecosystem","meaning":"健康水生生態系統","examples":[{"en":"The mangrove project restored a healthy aquatic ecosystem.","zh":"紅樹林項目恢復了健康水生生態系統。"},{"en":"A healthy aquatic ecosystem is a balanced water-based environment where plants, animals, and microorganisms can live well.","zh":"healthy aquatic ecosystem 是一個平衡的水域環境，當中植物、動物和微生物能良好生活。"},{"en":"A clean river with fish, insects, plants, and clear water may be a healthy aquatic ecosystem.","zh":"有魚、昆蟲、植物和清水的清潔河流，可能是健康水生生態系統。"},{"en":"Pollution can damage aquatic ecosystems by reducing oxygen and killing species.","zh":"污染可以透過減少氧氣和殺死物種來破壞水生生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to life in water, not on land.","zh":"這個短語指水中的生命，而不是陸地上的生命。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"act as a defence against","meaning":"作為抵禦……的屏障","examples":[{"en":"Mangroves act as a defence against flooding.","zh":"紅樹林作為抵禦洪水的屏障。"},{"en":"To act as a defence against something means to protect against it or reduce its damage.","zh":"act as a defence against something 的意思是保護免受某事影響或減少其損害。"},{"en":"A strong password acts as a defence against online theft.","zh":"強密碼作為抵禦網上盜竊的屏障。"},{"en":"Trees can act as a defence against landslides by holding soil in place.","zh":"樹木可以透過固定土壤，作為抵禦山泥傾瀉的屏障。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a protective function.","zh":"這個短語描述保護功能。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"increased threat of flooding","meaning":"洪水威脅增加","examples":[{"en":"Mangroves protect against the increased threat of flooding.","zh":"紅樹林保護人們免受洪水威脅增加的影響。"},{"en":"The increased threat of flooding means a higher risk that water will overflow and damage land, homes, or communities.","zh":"increased threat of flooding 的意思是水溢出並破壞土地、房屋或社區的風險增加。"},{"en":"Low-lying towns face an increased threat of flooding during stronger storms.","zh":"低窪城鎮在更強風暴期間面對洪水威脅增加。"},{"en":"Climate change can increase flood threats by raising sea levels and intensifying rainfall.","zh":"氣候變化可以透過海平面上升和降雨加劇來增加洪水威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on risk becoming greater.","zh":"這個短語集中於風險變得更大。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"caused by climate change","meaning":"由氣候變化造成","examples":[{"en":"The increased threat of flooding is caused by climate change.","zh":"洪水威脅增加是由氣候變化造成。"},{"en":"Caused by climate change means produced or made worse by long-term changes in temperature, weather patterns, and sea levels.","zh":"caused by climate change 的意思是由氣溫、天氣模式和海平面長期變化所產生或加劇。"},{"en":"Some heatwaves are becoming more intense because of climate change.","zh":"有些熱浪因氣候變化而變得更強烈。"},{"en":"Flood risks caused by climate change can force communities to improve drainage and coastal protection.","zh":"由氣候變化造成的洪水風險，可以迫使社區改善排水和海岸保護。"},{"en":"This phrase links a problem to changes in the climate system.","zh":"這個短語把問題與氣候系統變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"what’s more","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"What’s more, the local economy is more stable.","zh":"此外，本地經濟更加穩定。"},{"en":"What’s more is used to add another point, often one that strengthens the previous idea.","zh":"what’s more 用來加入另一點，通常是加強前一個想法。"},{"en":"The park is beautiful; what’s more, it gives children a safe place to play.","zh":"這個公園很漂亮；此外，它給兒童安全玩耍的地方。"},{"en":"A plan becomes more persuasive when the speaker adds useful points with “what’s more”.","zh":"當講者用 what’s more 加入有用觀點，計劃會更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in speech and informal writing.","zh":"這個短語常見於說話和非正式寫作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"local economy","meaning":"本地經濟","examples":[{"en":"The local economy became more stable after mangrove restoration.","zh":"紅樹林復育後，本地經濟變得更穩定。"},{"en":"The local economy is the system of jobs, businesses, income, and trade in a particular area.","zh":"local economy 是特定地區中的工作、企業、收入和貿易系統。"},{"en":"A new market can support the local economy by helping small shops sell goods.","zh":"新市場可以透過幫助小店售賣商品來支援本地經濟。"},{"en":"If the local economy depends on one industry only, families may suffer when that industry declines.","zh":"如果本地經濟只依賴一個行業，該行業衰退時家庭可能受苦。"},{"en":"This phrase connects community life with money and work.","zh":"這個短語把社區生活與金錢和工作連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"more stable","meaning":"更穩定","examples":[{"en":"The local economy is now more stable.","zh":"本地經濟現在更穩定。"},{"en":"More stable means steadier, less likely to collapse, and better able to handle change.","zh":"more stable 的意思是更平穩、較不容易崩潰，並更能應對變化。"},{"en":"A family budget becomes more stable when income is regular and debts are controlled.","zh":"當收入穩定且債務受控，家庭預算會變得更穩定。"},{"en":"A more stable ecosystem can recover better after storms or disease.","zh":"更穩定的生態系統在風暴或疾病後能更好恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a better condition with a less steady one.","zh":"這個短語把較好狀態與較不穩定狀態比較。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"send their children to school","meaning":"送子女上學","examples":[{"en":"Thousands more Madagascans can now send their children to school.","zh":"現在多了數以千計的馬達加斯加人能送子女上學。"},{"en":"To send their children to school means to make it possible for children to attend school regularly.","zh":"send their children to school 的意思是讓子女能定期上學。"},{"en":"Parents may struggle to send their children to school if transport and fees are too expensive.","zh":"如果交通和費用太昂貴，父母可能難以送子女上學。"},{"en":"Better local income helps families send children to school instead of keeping them at work.","zh":"更好的本地收入幫助家庭送子女上學，而不是讓他們工作。"},{"en":"This phrase connects education with family resources and opportunity.","zh":"這個短語把教育與家庭資源和機會連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"important point to consider","meaning":"需要考慮的重要一點","examples":[{"en":"One other important point to consider is how local communities benefit.","zh":"另一個需要考慮的重要一點是本地社區如何受益。"},{"en":"An important point to consider is a key idea that should be thought about before making a decision.","zh":"important point to consider 是作出決定前應思考的關鍵想法。"},{"en":"When choosing a school, an important point to consider is how long the journey will take.","zh":"選擇學校時，需要考慮的重要一點是路程需時多久。"},{"en":"Considering key points early helps people avoid mistakes later.","zh":"及早考慮重點有助人們避免日後犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when adding a factor that should not be ignored.","zh":"這個短語適合用於加入不應忽視的因素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 8 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"ielts/listening/Practice 9/task-1":[{"front":"excuse me","meaning":"不好意思；打擾一下","examples":[{"en":"The man says “Excuse me” before asking Sadie some survey questions.","zh":"那名男子在問 Sadie 一些調查問題前說：「不好意思。」"},{"en":"Excuse me is a polite phrase used to get someone’s attention or apologise for interrupting.","zh":"Excuse me 是用來引起別人注意或為打擾別人道歉的禮貌用語。"},{"en":"A passenger may say “Excuse me” before asking someone to move their bag from a seat.","zh":"乘客可能會先說「不好意思」，再請別人把袋從座位上拿開。"},{"en":"Using “Excuse me” makes a request sound less rude because it shows respect.","zh":"使用 Excuse me 會令請求聽起來較不無禮，因為它顯示尊重。"},{"en":"People often say “Excuse me” before asking a stranger for help or information.","zh":"人們在向陌生人求助或詢問資料前，常說 Excuse me。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"would you mind if","meaning":"你介意我……嗎？","examples":[{"en":"The man asks, “Would you mind if I asked you some questions?”","zh":"那名男子問：「你介意我問你幾個問題嗎？」"},{"en":"Would you mind if is a polite way to ask whether someone is willing to let you do something.","zh":"Would you mind if 是禮貌地詢問對方是否願意讓你做某事。"},{"en":"A student may ask, “Would you mind if I sat here?” before taking an empty seat.","zh":"學生坐下空位前，可能會問：「你介意我坐這裏嗎？」"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the action may interrupt or trouble another person.","zh":"當某行動可能打擾或麻煩別人時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It sounds more polite than simply saying, “Can I do this?”","zh":"它比直接說「我可以這樣做嗎？」更有禮貌。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ask you some questions","meaning":"問你幾個問題","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks Sadie some questions about transport.","zh":"訪問員問 Sadie 幾個關於交通的問題。"},{"en":"To ask you some questions means to get information from you by asking several things.","zh":"ask you some questions 是指透過問幾件事向你取得資料。"},{"en":"A doctor may ask you some questions before deciding what treatment you need.","zh":"醫生決定你需要甚麼治療前，可能會問你幾個問題。"},{"en":"Interviewers ask questions so they can understand people’s experiences or opinions.","zh":"訪問員問問題，是為了了解人們的經驗或意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in surveys, interviews, appointments, and school discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於調查、訪問、約診和課堂討論中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"do a survey on","meaning":"做一項關於……的調查","examples":[{"en":"They are doing a survey on transport.","zh":"他們正在做一項關於交通的調查。"},{"en":"To do a survey on something means to ask people questions in order to collect information about that topic.","zh":"do a survey on something 是指向人們提問，以收集關於該主題的資料。"},{"en":"A school may do a survey on lunch choices before changing the canteen menu.","zh":"學校改變飯堂餐牌前，可能會做一項關於午餐選擇的調查。"},{"en":"Doing a survey can help organisations make decisions based on real opinions.","zh":"做調查可以幫助機構根據真實意見作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research involves asking many people the same questions.","zh":"當研究涉及向許多人問相同問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"first of all","meaning":"首先","examples":[{"en":"First of all, the man asks for Sadie’s name.","zh":"首先，那名男子詢問 Sadie 的姓名。"},{"en":"First of all is used to introduce the first point, question, or action in a sequence.","zh":"First of all 用來引入一連串內容中的第一點、第一個問題或第一個行動。"},{"en":"First of all, a teacher may check attendance before starting the lesson.","zh":"首先，老師可能會點名，然後才開始上課。"},{"en":"This phrase helps listeners follow the order of information clearly.","zh":"這個短語幫助聽者清楚跟上資料次序。"},{"en":"It is often used at the beginning of explanations, interviews, and instructions.","zh":"它常用於解釋、訪問和指示的開頭。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"take your name","meaning":"記下你的姓名","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks if he can take Sadie’s name.","zh":"訪問員問是否可以記下 Sadie 的姓名。"},{"en":"To take your name means to write down or record your name.","zh":"take your name 是指寫下或記錄你的姓名。"},{"en":"A receptionist may take your name before you see the doctor.","zh":"接待員可能在你看醫生前記下你的姓名。"},{"en":"Taking someone’s name helps staff identify the person later.","zh":"記下某人的姓名有助職員之後辨認該人。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in surveys, bookings, appointments, and official records.","zh":"這個短語常見於調查、預約、約診和正式紀錄中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"date of birth","meaning":"出生日期","examples":[{"en":"The man asks for Sadie’s date of birth.","zh":"那名男子詢問 Sadie 的出生日期。"},{"en":"A date of birth is the day, month, and year when a person was born.","zh":"date of birth 是指一個人出生的日、月、年。"},{"en":"You may need to write your date of birth on a school form or medical form.","zh":"你可能需要在學校表格或醫療表格上填寫出生日期。"},{"en":"Organisations ask for a date of birth to confirm age or identity.","zh":"機構詢問出生日期，是為了確認年齡或身份。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to birth information, not today’s date.","zh":"這個短語指出生資料，而不是今天的日期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"just the year will do","meaning":"只要年份就可以","examples":[{"en":"For the date of birth, just the year will do.","zh":"出生日期方面，只要年份就可以。"},{"en":"Just the year will do means only the year is enough; the full date is not needed.","zh":"just the year will do 是指只提供年份已足夠，不需要完整日期。"},{"en":"If a form only needs your age group, just the year will do.","zh":"如果表格只需要你的年齡組別，只要年份就可以。"},{"en":"This phrase reduces the amount of information someone has to give.","zh":"這個短語減少對方需要提供的資料量。"},{"en":"People use it when a simpler answer is acceptable.","zh":"當較簡單答案可以接受時，人們會使用這句話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"actually","meaning":"其實","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer says that just the year will do, actually.","zh":"訪問員說，其實只要年份就可以。"},{"en":"Actually is used to correct, clarify, or add a more accurate detail.","zh":"actually 用來修正、澄清或補充更準確的細節。"},{"en":"I thought the meeting was at ten, but actually it starts at half past ten.","zh":"我以為會議在十點開始，但其實是十點半開始。"},{"en":"People use actually when they want to adjust what was just said.","zh":"人們想調整剛才所說的內容時，會使用 actually。"},{"en":"It can make a correction sound softer in conversation.","zh":"它可以令對話中的修正聽起來較柔和。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"is that all right?","meaning":"這樣可以嗎？","examples":[{"en":"The man asks whether giving just the year is all right.","zh":"那名男子問只提供年份是否可以。"},{"en":"Is that all right? is used to check whether someone accepts or agrees with something.","zh":"Is that all right? 用來確認對方是否接受或同意某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “I’ll move your presentation to Friday. Is that all right?”","zh":"老師可能會說：「我把你的匯報改到星期五，這樣可以嗎？」"},{"en":"This question gives the listener a chance to object or agree.","zh":"這個問題給聽者機會反對或同意。"},{"en":"It sounds polite because it does not assume the other person is comfortable.","zh":"它聽起來有禮貌，因為它沒有假設對方一定接受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"that’s fine","meaning":"這樣可以；沒問題","examples":[{"en":"Sadie says giving the year is fine.","zh":"Sadie 說提供年份沒問題。"},{"en":"That’s fine means that something is acceptable or not a problem.","zh":"that’s fine 是指某事可以接受或沒有問題。"},{"en":"If a friend is five minutes late, you may say, “That’s fine,” to reassure them.","zh":"如果朋友遲到五分鐘，你可能會說「沒問題」來安撫他。"},{"en":"People say this when they agree to a small change or request.","zh":"人們同意小改動或小請求時，會說這句話。"},{"en":"It is a simple, polite way to show acceptance.","zh":"這是一個簡單而有禮貌的接受方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"postcode","meaning":"郵政編碼","examples":[{"en":"The man asks Sadie for her postcode.","zh":"那名男子向 Sadie 詢問她的郵政編碼。"},{"en":"A postcode is a group of letters and numbers used to identify an address area for mail and records.","zh":"postcode 是一組字母和數字，用來識別郵寄和紀錄中的地址區域。"},{"en":"Online shops often ask for your postcode before calculating delivery options.","zh":"網店在計算送貨選項前，常要求你提供郵政編碼。"},{"en":"Postcodes help services know roughly where a person lives.","zh":"郵政編碼幫助服務機構大概知道一個人住在哪裏。"},{"en":"This word is especially common in British English.","zh":"這個詞在英式英語中特別常見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"is that in...?","meaning":"那是在……嗎？","examples":[{"en":"The man asks whether Sadie’s postcode is in Wells.","zh":"那名男子問 Sadie 的郵政編碼是否在 Wells。"},{"en":"Is that in...? is used to check whether a place belongs to a particular area.","zh":"Is that in...? 用來確認某地是否屬於某個區域。"},{"en":"If someone says they live in KT2, you may ask, “Is that in Kingston?”","zh":"如果有人說自己住在 KT2，你可能會問：「那是在 Kingston 嗎？」"},{"en":"This question helps the speaker confirm location rather than guess wrongly.","zh":"這個問題幫助說話者確認位置，而不是胡亂猜測。"},{"en":"It is useful when a place name, postcode, or district is unfamiliar.","zh":"當地名、郵政編碼或區域不熟悉時，這句很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"it’s actually in","meaning":"其實是在……","examples":[{"en":"Sadie says her postcode is actually in Harborne.","zh":"Sadie 說她的郵政編碼其實是在 Harborne。"},{"en":"It’s actually in is used to correct someone’s idea about where a place is.","zh":"it’s actually in 用來修正別人對某地位置的理解。"},{"en":"The school is actually in Kowloon Tong, not Mong Kok.","zh":"那間學校其實是在九龍塘，不是在旺角。"},{"en":"This phrase is helpful when two areas are close and easy to confuse.","zh":"當兩個地區相近而容易混淆時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"The word actually makes the correction sound conversational rather than harsh.","zh":"actually 令修正聽起來較自然，不那麼生硬。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not far from","meaning":"離……不遠","examples":[{"en":"Wells is not far from Harborne.","zh":"Wells 離 Harborne 不遠。"},{"en":"Not far from means close to a place or only a short distance away.","zh":"not far from 是指接近某地或距離不遠。"},{"en":"My school is not far from the bus stop, so I can walk there easily.","zh":"我的學校離巴士站不遠，所以我可以輕鬆走過去。"},{"en":"Living not far from work can save time and transport costs.","zh":"住得離工作地點不遠可以節省時間和交通費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distance in a simple, everyday way.","zh":"這個短語用簡單日常方式描述距離。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"that area","meaning":"那一區","examples":[{"en":"The man really likes that area.","zh":"那名男子很喜歡那一區。"},{"en":"That area means the place or district that has just been mentioned.","zh":"that area 是指剛才提及的地方或區域。"},{"en":"If someone talks about Sai Kung, you might say, “I like that area because it is quiet.”","zh":"如果有人談到西貢，你可能會說：「我喜歡那一區，因為那裏安靜。」"},{"en":"People use that area when the location is already clear from the conversation.","zh":"當對話中地點已清楚時，人們會用 that area。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the full place name again.","zh":"這個短語避免再次重複完整地名。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"when I was a kid","meaning":"我小時候","examples":[{"en":"The man’s grandmother lived there when he was a kid.","zh":"那名男子小時候，他的祖母住在那裏。"},{"en":"When I was a kid means during the time when I was a child.","zh":"when I was a kid 是指我還是小孩子的時候。"},{"en":"When I was a kid, I walked to school with my neighbours every morning.","zh":"我小時候，每天早上都和鄰居一起走路上學。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when telling memories from childhood.","zh":"人們講述童年回憶時會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It often gives a personal or nostalgic feeling to a story.","zh":"它常為故事加入個人或懷舊感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"how you travelled here today","meaning":"你今天怎樣來這裏","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks Sadie how she travelled here today.","zh":"訪問員問 Sadie 今天怎樣來這裏。"},{"en":"How you travelled here today asks what transport method you used to reach this place today.","zh":"how you travelled here today 是問你今天使用甚麼交通方式到達這裏。"},{"en":"A receptionist may ask how you travelled here today to understand parking or transport needs.","zh":"接待員可能會問你今天怎樣來這裏，以了解泊車或交通需要。"},{"en":"This question helps survey workers collect information about people’s real journeys.","zh":"這個問題幫助調查人員收集人們真實行程的資料。"},{"en":"It focuses on today’s journey, not the person’s usual habits in general.","zh":"它集中於今天的行程，而不是一般習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"use public transport","meaning":"使用公共交通","examples":[{"en":"Sadie used public transport to travel into the city centre.","zh":"Sadie 使用公共交通前往市中心。"},{"en":"To use public transport means to travel by services such as buses, trains, trams, or the underground.","zh":"use public transport 是指乘搭巴士、火車、電車或地下鐵等交通服務。"},{"en":"Many students use public transport because they do not drive.","zh":"許多學生使用公共交通，因為他們不駕車。"},{"en":"Using public transport can reduce traffic if fewer people drive private cars.","zh":"如果較少人駕駛私家車，使用公共交通可以減少交通擠塞。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts shared transport with travelling by private vehicle.","zh":"這個短語把共用交通與乘坐私人交通工具作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"come by bus","meaning":"乘巴士來","examples":[{"en":"Sadie came by bus.","zh":"Sadie 乘巴士來。"},{"en":"To come by bus means to travel to a place on a bus.","zh":"come by bus 是指乘坐巴士到某地。"},{"en":"A visitor may come by bus if there is no parking near the school.","zh":"如果學校附近沒有泊車位，訪客可能會乘巴士來。"},{"en":"Coming by bus can be cheaper than taking a taxi.","zh":"乘巴士來可能比乘的士便宜。"},{"en":"This phrase tells us the transport method used to arrive somewhere.","zh":"這個短語告訴我們到達某地所用的交通方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the reason for","meaning":"……的原因","examples":[{"en":"The man asks about the reason for Sadie’s trip.","zh":"那名男子詢問 Sadie 這次行程的原因。"},{"en":"The reason for something is the cause or purpose behind it.","zh":"the reason for something 是指某事背後的原因或目的。"},{"en":"The reason for a student’s absence may be illness or a family matter.","zh":"學生缺席的原因可能是生病或家庭事務。"},{"en":"Knowing the reason for a journey helps survey workers understand travel patterns.","zh":"了解行程的原因有助調查人員理解出行模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when asking why something happened or why someone did something.","zh":"當詢問某事為何發生或某人為何做某事時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"your trip today","meaning":"你今天的行程","examples":[{"en":"The survey asks about Sadie’s trip today.","zh":"這項調查詢問 Sadie 今天的行程。"},{"en":"Your trip today means the journey or outing you made on this particular day.","zh":"your trip today 是指你在今天這一天所作的行程或外出。"},{"en":"A travel survey may ask about your trip today, including where it began and why you travelled.","zh":"交通調查可能會詢問你今天的行程，包括從哪裏開始和為何出行。"},{"en":"Details about today’s trip can be different from someone’s normal weekly routine.","zh":"今天行程的細節可能與某人平常每週習慣不同。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on one specific journey, not all travel habits.","zh":"這個短語集中於一個特定行程，而不是所有出行習慣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I can see","meaning":"我看得出","examples":[{"en":"The man can see that Sadie has some shopping with her.","zh":"那名男子看得出 Sadie 帶着一些買來的東西。"},{"en":"I can see is used when you notice something from what is visible or obvious.","zh":"I can see 用於表示你從可見或明顯的情況注意到某事。"},{"en":"I can see you are tired, so we can finish the meeting early.","zh":"我看得出你很累，所以我們可以提早結束會議。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to show that their next comment is based on observation.","zh":"人們用這個短語表示接下來的評論基於觀察。"},{"en":"It can make a question feel more natural because it connects to what is in front of them.","zh":"它可以令問題更自然，因為它連接到眼前所見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have some shopping with you","meaning":"帶着買來的東西","examples":[{"en":"Sadie has some shopping with her.","zh":"Sadie 帶着一些買來的東西。"},{"en":"To have some shopping with you means to be carrying things you have bought.","zh":"have some shopping with you 是指隨身帶着已購買的物品。"},{"en":"A passenger with several bags may have some shopping with her after visiting the market.","zh":"乘客去完街市後帶着幾個袋，可能就是帶着買來的東西。"},{"en":"Having shopping with you can show that shopping was part of your trip.","zh":"帶着買來的東西可以顯示購物是行程的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to bought items, not the activity of shopping itself.","zh":"這個短語指買來的物品，而不是購物這個活動本身。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"do some shopping","meaning":"買些東西","examples":[{"en":"Sadie did some shopping during her trip.","zh":"Sadie 在行程中買了些東西。"},{"en":"To do some shopping means to buy things, usually from shops or a market.","zh":"do some shopping 是指在商店或市場買東西。"},{"en":"A family may do some shopping on Saturday morning for food and household items.","zh":"一家人可能在星期六早上買些食物和家居用品。"},{"en":"People often do some shopping when they are already in town for another reason.","zh":"人們已經因其他原因進城時，常會順便買些東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is general; it does not specify exactly what was bought.","zh":"這個短語很籠統，沒有指出具體買了甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the main reason","meaning":"主要原因","examples":[{"en":"The main reason Sadie came was to go to the dentist.","zh":"Sadie 來的主要原因是去看牙醫。"},{"en":"The main reason is the most important cause or purpose.","zh":"the main reason 是指最重要的原因或目的。"},{"en":"The main reason I chose this course was to improve my speaking confidence.","zh":"我選這門課的主要原因是提升說話信心。"},{"en":"A trip may have several purposes, but the main reason explains why it really happened.","zh":"一次行程可能有幾個目的，但主要原因解釋它真正發生的原因。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate the most important reason from smaller extra reasons.","zh":"這個短語有助把最重要原因與較小的附加原因分開。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"go to the dentist","meaning":"去看牙醫","examples":[{"en":"Sadie came into town to go to the dentist.","zh":"Sadie 進城是為了去看牙醫。"},{"en":"To go to the dentist means to visit a dental professional for tooth or mouth care.","zh":"go to the dentist 是指去見牙科專業人士，接受牙齒或口腔護理。"},{"en":"A child may go to the dentist if a tooth hurts or needs checking.","zh":"如果孩子牙痛或需要檢查，可能會去看牙醫。"},{"en":"Regularly going to the dentist can help find problems before they become serious.","zh":"定期去看牙醫可以幫助在問題變嚴重前發現它。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to treatment, a check-up, or dental advice.","zh":"這個短語可指治療、例行檢查或牙科建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"not much fun","meaning":"不太有趣；不太好受","examples":[{"en":"The man says going to the dentist is not much fun.","zh":"那名男子說去看牙醫不太好受。"},{"en":"Not much fun means not very enjoyable or pleasant.","zh":"not much fun 是指不太令人享受或舒服。"},{"en":"Waiting in a long queue in the rain is not much fun.","zh":"下雨時排長隊不太好受。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to talk about something unpleasant in a light way.","zh":"人們用這個短語以輕鬆方式談論不愉快的事情。"},{"en":"It is softer and more conversational than saying something is terrible.","zh":"它比說某事很糟糕更柔和、更口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hope it was nothing serious","meaning":"希望不是甚麼嚴重問題","examples":[{"en":"The man hopes that Sadie’s dental visit was nothing serious.","zh":"那名男子希望 Sadie 的牙科檢查不是甚麼嚴重問題。"},{"en":"Hope it was nothing serious means I hope the problem was not dangerous, severe, or worrying.","zh":"hope it was nothing serious 是指希望問題不危險、不嚴重或不令人擔心。"},{"en":"If a friend went to hospital, you might say, “I hope it was nothing serious.”","zh":"如果朋友去了醫院，你可能會說：「希望不是甚麼嚴重問題。」"},{"en":"This phrase shows concern while avoiding too many personal questions.","zh":"這個短語顯示關心，同時避免問太多私人問題。"},{"en":"It is often used after hearing that someone had a medical appointment or accident.","zh":"它常用於聽到某人曾有醫療預約或意外之後。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"just a check-up","meaning":"只是例行檢查","examples":[{"en":"Sadie says it was just a check-up.","zh":"Sadie 說那只是例行檢查。"},{"en":"Just a check-up means only a routine examination, not treatment for a serious problem.","zh":"just a check-up 是指只是常規檢查，而不是治療嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A patient may visit the clinic for just a check-up even when feeling healthy.","zh":"即使身體健康，病人也可能到診所只是做例行檢查。"},{"en":"Check-ups can find small problems before they become more serious.","zh":"例行檢查可以在小問題變嚴重前發現它們。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures others that there was probably no major issue.","zh":"這個短語安撫別人，表示大概沒有重大問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"normally travel by bus","meaning":"平常乘巴士出行","examples":[{"en":"Sadie normally travels by bus into the city centre.","zh":"Sadie 平常乘巴士進市中心。"},{"en":"To normally travel by bus means to usually use the bus for journeys.","zh":"normally travel by bus 是指通常乘巴士出行。"},{"en":"A student may normally travel by bus to school because it stops near her home.","zh":"學生可能平常乘巴士上學，因為巴士站在她家附近。"},{"en":"People normally use the transport option that is cheapest, quickest, or most convenient for them.","zh":"人們通常會使用對自己最便宜、最快或最方便的交通選項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a usual habit, not just one journey today.","zh":"這個短語描述日常習慣，而不只是今天的一次行程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"into the city centre","meaning":"進市中心","examples":[{"en":"Sadie usually travels by bus into the city centre.","zh":"Sadie 通常乘巴士進市中心。"},{"en":"Into the city centre means towards the central part of a town or city.","zh":"into the city centre 是指朝城鎮或城市的中心地帶前往。"},{"en":"Many office workers travel into the city centre every morning.","zh":"許多上班族每天早上進市中心。"},{"en":"Travelling into the city centre may take longer during rush hour.","zh":"在繁忙時間進市中心可能需要更長時間。"},{"en":"This phrase shows direction from outside or another area towards the centre.","zh":"這個短語顯示從外圍或其他地區向中心移動的方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stop driving in","meaning":"不再駕車進城","examples":[{"en":"Sadie stopped driving into the city centre ages ago.","zh":"Sadie 很久以前已不再駕車進市中心。"},{"en":"To stop driving in means to no longer use a car to travel into a town or city centre.","zh":"stop driving in 是指不再駕車進入城鎮或市中心。"},{"en":"A worker may stop driving in after parking fees become too expensive.","zh":"當泊車費變得太貴，上班族可能會不再駕車進城。"},{"en":"People stop driving in when public transport becomes easier or traffic becomes too stressful.","zh":"當公共交通更方便或交通太令人有壓力，人們會不再駕車進城。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests a change from car travel to another transport method.","zh":"這個短語常表示從駕車改用另一種交通方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ages ago","meaning":"很久以前","examples":[{"en":"Sadie stopped driving into town ages ago.","zh":"Sadie 很久以前已不再駕車進城。"},{"en":"Ages ago means a long time ago.","zh":"ages ago 是指很久以前。"},{"en":"I bought this jacket ages ago, but I still wear it every winter.","zh":"我很久以前買了這件外套，但每個冬天仍然穿。"},{"en":"People use ages ago in casual speech when the exact date is not important.","zh":"當確切日期不重要時，人們在口語中會用 ages ago。"},{"en":"It sounds more conversational than saying “a long time previously”.","zh":"它比說 a long time previously 更口語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"parking was difficult to find","meaning":"泊車位很難找","examples":[{"en":"Sadie stopped driving because parking was difficult to find.","zh":"Sadie 不再駕車，是因為泊車位很難找。"},{"en":"Parking was difficult to find means there were not many available places to leave a car.","zh":"parking was difficult to find 是指可泊車的位置不多。"},{"en":"Near a busy hospital, parking can be difficult to find in the morning.","zh":"在繁忙醫院附近，早上泊車位可能很難找。"},{"en":"If parking is difficult to find, drivers may waste time circling the streets.","zh":"如果泊車位很難找，司機可能會浪費時間在街上兜圈。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why people may choose public transport instead of driving.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何人們可能選擇公共交通而不是駕車。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cost so much","meaning":"費用很高","examples":[{"en":"Parking in the city centre costs so much.","zh":"市中心泊車費用很高。"},{"en":"Cost so much means be very expensive.","zh":"cost so much 是指非常昂貴。"},{"en":"Eating out every day can cost so much that students run out of money quickly.","zh":"每天外出吃飯可能費用很高，令學生很快用完錢。"},{"en":"When something costs so much, people may look for cheaper alternatives.","zh":"當某事費用很高，人們可能會尋找較便宜的替代選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often shows frustration about price.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常表達對價格的不滿。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"much more convenient","meaning":"方便得多","examples":[{"en":"The bus is much more convenient than driving.","zh":"乘巴士比駕車方便得多。"},{"en":"Much more convenient means far easier, simpler, or more suitable to use.","zh":"much more convenient 是指容易、簡單或合用得多。"},{"en":"Paying by phone is much more convenient than carrying coins for every machine.","zh":"用手機付款比每次為機器帶硬幣方便得多。"},{"en":"A transport option becomes more convenient when it saves time, effort, or stress.","zh":"當交通選項能節省時間、力氣或壓力，它就更方便。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly compares two choices and says one is easier.","zh":"這個短語清楚比較兩個選擇，指出其中一個較方便。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"only take about","meaning":"只需大約……","examples":[{"en":"The bus only takes about 30 minutes.","zh":"巴士只需大約三十分鐘。"},{"en":"Only take about means need approximately a small or reasonable amount of time.","zh":"only take about 是指大約只需要一段不長或合理的時間。"},{"en":"The walk to school only takes about ten minutes if the traffic lights are quick.","zh":"如果交通燈轉得快，步行到學校只需大約十分鐘。"},{"en":"People may choose a route if it only takes about the same time as driving.","zh":"如果一條路線只需大約與駕車相同時間，人們可能會選擇它。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate time and often suggests the journey is manageable.","zh":"這個短語提供約略時間，並常暗示行程可接受。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"start your journey","meaning":"開始行程","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks where Sadie started her journey.","zh":"訪問員問 Sadie 從哪裏開始行程。"},{"en":"To start your journey means to begin travelling from a particular place.","zh":"start your journey 是指從某個特定地方開始出行。"},{"en":"A travel app may ask where you start your journey before suggesting a route.","zh":"交通應用程式可能在建議路線前問你從哪裏開始行程。"},{"en":"Knowing the starting point helps calculate distance, time, and transport choices.","zh":"知道起點有助計算距離、時間和交通選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the beginning of a trip.","zh":"這個短語著重行程的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"bus stop","meaning":"巴士站","examples":[{"en":"Sadie started her journey at the bus stop on Claxby Street.","zh":"Sadie 在 Claxby Street 的巴士站開始行程。"},{"en":"A bus stop is a place where buses stop so passengers can get on or off.","zh":"bus stop 是巴士停下讓乘客上落車的地方。"},{"en":"Students often wait at the bus stop before going to school.","zh":"學生上學前常在巴士站等車。"},{"en":"A bus stop near your home makes public transport easier to use.","zh":"家附近有巴士站會令公共交通更易使用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the stopping place, not the bus itself.","zh":"這個短語指停車地點，而不是巴士本身。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"spell a street name","meaning":"拼出街名","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer checks how to spell Claxby Street.","zh":"訪問員確認 Claxby Street 這個街名怎樣拼寫。"},{"en":"To spell a street name means to say or write the letters of the street name correctly.","zh":"spell a street name 是指正確說出或寫出街名的字母。"},{"en":"A receptionist may ask you to spell a street name if it is unusual.","zh":"如果街名不常見，接待員可能會請你拼出街名。"},{"en":"Spelling a street name correctly prevents mistakes in addresses and records.","zh":"正確拼出街名可以防止地址和紀錄出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when names sound similar or are hard to hear.","zh":"當名稱發音相似或難以聽清時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"that’s right","meaning":"沒錯","examples":[{"en":"Sadie confirms the spelling by saying, “That’s right.”","zh":"Sadie 說「沒錯」來確認拼寫。"},{"en":"That’s right means what you said or wrote is correct.","zh":"that’s right 是指你所說或所寫的是正確的。"},{"en":"If a teacher reads your answer and says “That’s right,” it means you are correct.","zh":"如果老師看了你的答案後說「沒錯」，意思是你答對了。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to confirm information clearly and quickly.","zh":"人們用這個短語清楚而快速地確認資料。"},{"en":"It is common in conversations when checking names, numbers, addresses, or spellings.","zh":"它常見於核對姓名、數字、地址或拼寫的對話中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be satisfied with","meaning":"對……感到滿意","examples":[{"en":"The man asks how satisfied Sadie is with the bus service.","zh":"那名男子問 Sadie 對巴士服務有多滿意。"},{"en":"To be satisfied with something means to feel that it is good enough or meets your needs.","zh":"be satisfied with something 是指覺得某事足夠好或符合需要。"},{"en":"A customer may be satisfied with a meal if the food is fresh and the service is polite.","zh":"如果食物新鮮、服務有禮，顧客可能會對一餐飯感到滿意。"},{"en":"People are more satisfied with public transport when it is reliable, clean, and affordable.","zh":"當公共交通可靠、清潔和負擔得起時，人們會更滿意。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in surveys about services and experiences.","zh":"這個短語常用於關於服務和體驗的調查。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the service","meaning":"服務","examples":[{"en":"Sadie comments on the bus service.","zh":"Sadie 評論巴士服務。"},{"en":"The service means the help, transport, or system provided to customers or users.","zh":"the service 是指提供給顧客或使用者的協助、交通或系統。"},{"en":"A bank customer may complain if the service is slow and unfriendly.","zh":"如果服務緩慢又不友善，銀行顧客可能會投訴。"},{"en":"Good service makes people more likely to use the same company again.","zh":"良好服務會令人更可能再次使用同一間公司。"},{"en":"In this context, the service refers to how well the buses operate for passengers.","zh":"在這個語境中，the service 指巴士對乘客而言運作得如何。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have any complaints","meaning":"有任何不滿","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks whether Sadie has any complaints.","zh":"訪問員問 Sadie 是否有任何不滿。"},{"en":"To have any complaints means to have problems or dissatisfaction that you want to mention.","zh":"have any complaints 是指有想提出的問題或不滿。"},{"en":"A hotel guest may have complaints if the room is noisy or dirty.","zh":"如果房間嘈雜或骯髒，酒店住客可能有不滿。"},{"en":"Complaints help organisations see what needs improvement.","zh":"投訴幫助機構知道哪些地方需要改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used politely in surveys or customer service conversations.","zh":"這個短語常禮貌地用於調查或客戶服務對話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as I said","meaning":"正如我所說","examples":[{"en":"Sadie says, “As I said, it’s very convenient.”","zh":"Sadie 說：「正如我所說，它非常方便。」"},{"en":"As I said is used to repeat or refer back to something you mentioned earlier.","zh":"as I said 用來重複或回指你較早提過的內容。"},{"en":"As I said, the meeting will start at nine, so please arrive early.","zh":"正如我所說，會議會在九點開始，所以請早到。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect a new comment to an earlier point.","zh":"這個短語幫助把新評論連接到較早觀點。"},{"en":"It can sound firm if the speaker feels they have already explained something.","zh":"如果說話者覺得自己已解釋過，它可能聽起來較堅定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on time","meaning":"準時","examples":[{"en":"The bus is convenient and quick when it is on time.","zh":"巴士準時時，既方便又快捷。"},{"en":"On time means arriving or happening at the planned or expected time.","zh":"on time 是指在計劃或預期時間到達或發生。"},{"en":"Students should arrive on time so the lesson can start smoothly.","zh":"學生應準時到達，這樣課堂才能順利開始。"},{"en":"If buses are on time, passengers can plan their journeys more confidently.","zh":"如果巴士準時，乘客可以更有信心地規劃行程。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with being late or delayed.","zh":"這個短語與遲到或延誤相對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be late","meaning":"遲到；晚點","examples":[{"en":"The bus was late this morning.","zh":"巴士今天早上晚點了。"},{"en":"To be late means to arrive or happen after the expected or planned time.","zh":"be late 是指在預期或計劃時間之後才到達或發生。"},{"en":"A student may be late for class if the train breaks down.","zh":"如果火車故障，學生可能會上課遲到。"},{"en":"When buses are late, passengers may miss appointments or connections.","zh":"當巴士晚點，乘客可能會錯過預約或轉車。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for people, vehicles, events, and deadlines.","zh":"這個短語可用於人、交通工具、活動和截止日期。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"but still","meaning":"但始終；但還是","examples":[{"en":"The bus was only about ten minutes late, but still, it was annoying.","zh":"巴士只遲了大約十分鐘，但還是令人煩厭。"},{"en":"But still is used to say that something remains true or important despite another point.","zh":"but still 用來表示即使有另一點，某事仍然真實或重要。"},{"en":"The mistake was small, but still, it delayed the whole group.","zh":"錯誤很小，但始終拖延了整組人。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the speaker accepts one fact but keeps their feeling or opinion.","zh":"這個短語顯示說話者接受一個事實，但仍保留自己的感受或意見。"},{"en":"It often adds mild frustration or emphasis.","zh":"它常加入輕微不滿或強調。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"I understand that’s annoying","meaning":"我明白那令人煩厭","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer understands that the delay was annoying.","zh":"訪問員明白那次延誤令人煩厭。"},{"en":"I understand that’s annoying means I recognise that the situation is frustrating for you.","zh":"I understand that’s annoying 是指我明白這情況令你感到沮喪或煩躁。"},{"en":"A customer service worker may say, “I understand that’s annoying,” when a delivery is late.","zh":"當送貨遲到，客戶服務職員可能會說：「我明白那令人煩厭。」"},{"en":"This phrase shows empathy before asking more questions or offering help.","zh":"這個短語在繼續提問或提供協助前表達同理心。"},{"en":"It is useful when someone has experienced a small but irritating problem.","zh":"當某人經歷小但惱人的問題時，這句很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"what about","meaning":"那……方面呢？","examples":[{"en":"The man asks, “What about the timetable?”","zh":"那名男子問：「那時刻表方面呢？」"},{"en":"What about is used to introduce another topic, option, or person for discussion.","zh":"what about 用來引入另一個要討論的主題、選項或人物。"},{"en":"We have talked about the price; what about the delivery time?","zh":"我們已談過價格；那送貨時間方面呢？"},{"en":"This phrase helps move a conversation to a related point.","zh":"這個短語幫助把對話轉到相關的另一點。"},{"en":"It is common in interviews, planning, and everyday discussions.","zh":"它常見於訪問、規劃和日常討論中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"timetable","meaning":"時刻表","examples":[{"en":"Sadie comments on the bus timetable.","zh":"Sadie 評論巴士時刻表。"},{"en":"A timetable is a schedule showing when buses, trains, classes, or events happen.","zh":"timetable 是顯示巴士、火車、課堂或活動何時發生的時間表。"},{"en":"Students check the timetable to know when each lesson starts.","zh":"學生查看時間表，以知道每節課何時開始。"},{"en":"A clear timetable helps people plan and avoid waiting too long.","zh":"清楚的時刻表幫助人們規劃，避免等候太久。"},{"en":"This word is often used for transport and school schedules.","zh":"這個詞常用於交通和學校時間安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"comments about","meaning":"關於……的意見","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks whether Sadie has any comments about the timetable.","zh":"訪問員問 Sadie 是否有關於時刻表的意見。"},{"en":"Comments about something are opinions, remarks, or feedback on that topic.","zh":"comments about something 是指對該主題的看法、評論或回饋。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students for comments about a new homework system.","zh":"老師可能詢問學生對新功課制度的意見。"},{"en":"Comments help people understand what works well and what needs change.","zh":"意見幫助人們了解甚麼做得好，以及甚麼需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when asking for views without requiring a formal complaint.","zh":"這個短語適合用來詢問看法，而不一定要求正式投訴。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mainly use","meaning":"主要使用","examples":[{"en":"Sadie mainly uses the bus during the day.","zh":"Sadie 主要在日間使用巴士。"},{"en":"To mainly use something means to use it most often or for the largest part of the time.","zh":"mainly use something 是指最常或大部分時間使用某物。"},{"en":"A student may mainly use a tablet for reading notes, not watching videos.","zh":"學生可能主要使用平板電腦閱讀筆記，而不是看影片。"},{"en":"Knowing what people mainly use helps planners understand their habits.","zh":"知道人們主要使用甚麼，有助規劃者了解他們的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the usual or most common use, not every single use.","zh":"這個短語顯示通常或最常見的用途，而不是每一次用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"during the day","meaning":"在日間","examples":[{"en":"Sadie mainly uses the bus during the day.","zh":"Sadie 主要在日間使用巴士。"},{"en":"During the day means in the daytime, not at night.","zh":"during the day 是指在白天，而不是晚上。"},{"en":"Shops are usually busier during the day than late at night.","zh":"商店在日間通常比深夜更繁忙。"},{"en":"Public transport may run more often during the day because more people travel then.","zh":"公共交通在日間可能班次更頻密，因為那時較多人出行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the time period between morning and evening.","zh":"這個短語描述早上至傍晚之間的時段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"any time I’ve been","meaning":"每次我曾經……","examples":[{"en":"Any time Sadie has been in town in the evening, she has waited a long time for a bus.","zh":"Sadie 每次晚上在城裏，都要等很久才有巴士。"},{"en":"Any time I’ve been means every occasion when I have gone or been somewhere.","zh":"any time I’ve been 是指我每一次去過或身處某地時。"},{"en":"Any time I’ve been to that clinic, the staff have been polite and helpful.","zh":"我每次去那間診所，職員都很有禮貌和幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase uses repeated personal experience to support an opinion.","zh":"這個短語用重複的個人經驗支持意見。"},{"en":"It suggests the situation has happened more than once.","zh":"它表示該情況發生過不止一次。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in town","meaning":"在城裏；在市中心","examples":[{"en":"Sadie sometimes goes into town for dinner or the cinema.","zh":"Sadie 有時會進城吃晚飯或看電影。"},{"en":"In town means in the central or main part of a town or city.","zh":"in town 是指在城鎮或城市的中心或主要地區。"},{"en":"I will be in town this afternoon, so I can collect the tickets.","zh":"我今天下午會在市中心，所以可以取票。"},{"en":"People go into town for shopping, appointments, meals, or entertainment.","zh":"人們會進城購物、赴約、吃飯或娛樂。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and usually refers to a familiar local centre.","zh":"這個短語較口語，通常指熟悉的本地中心區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the evening","meaning":"在晚上","examples":[{"en":"Sadie notices fewer buses in the evening.","zh":"Sadie 注意到晚上巴士較少。"},{"en":"In the evening means during the later part of the day, after afternoon and before night.","zh":"in the evening 是指下午之後、夜晚之前的一天較後時段。"},{"en":"Many families eat dinner together in the evening.","zh":"許多家庭在晚上一起吃晚飯。"},{"en":"Transport services may be less frequent in the evening if fewer passengers travel.","zh":"如果較少乘客出行，交通服務在晚上可能班次較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a time period, not a specific hour.","zh":"這個短語描述一段時間，而不是某個確切小時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for dinner","meaning":"去吃晚飯","examples":[{"en":"Sadie sometimes goes into town for dinner.","zh":"Sadie 有時會進城去吃晚飯。"},{"en":"For dinner means for the purpose of eating an evening meal.","zh":"for dinner 是指以吃晚飯為目的。"},{"en":"Friends may meet in town for dinner after work.","zh":"朋友可能下班後在市中心見面吃晚飯。"},{"en":"People often travel for dinner when there are better restaurants in another area.","zh":"當另一區有更好的餐廳，人們常會為了晚飯而出行。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose of going somewhere.","zh":"這個短語解釋去某地的目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at the cinema","meaning":"在戲院","examples":[{"en":"Sadie sometimes goes into town to watch a film at the cinema.","zh":"Sadie 有時會進城在戲院看電影。"},{"en":"At the cinema means in a movie theatre where films are shown to an audience.","zh":"at the cinema 是指在向觀眾放映電影的戲院裏。"},{"en":"A family may watch an animated film at the cinema during the weekend.","zh":"一家人可能在週末到戲院看動畫電影。"},{"en":"Watching a film at the cinema can feel different from watching it at home because of the big screen and sound.","zh":"在戲院看電影與在家看不同，因為有大銀幕和音響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the place where the film is watched.","zh":"這個短語指觀看電影的地點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"wait a long time for","meaning":"等……很久","examples":[{"en":"Sadie has to wait a long time for a bus in the evening.","zh":"Sadie 晚上要等巴士很久。"},{"en":"To wait a long time for something means to spend a lot of time before it arrives or happens.","zh":"wait a long time for something 是指花很多時間等某物到來或某事發生。"},{"en":"Patients may wait a long time for an appointment at a busy clinic.","zh":"病人可能要等繁忙診所的預約很久。"},{"en":"Long waiting times can make a service feel unreliable or inconvenient.","zh":"等候時間長會令服務感覺不可靠或不方便。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests frustration or wasted time.","zh":"這個短語常暗示不滿或浪費時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"there aren’t that many","meaning":"數量不多","examples":[{"en":"There are not that many buses in the evening.","zh":"晚上的巴士數量不多。"},{"en":"There aren’t that many means the number is fairly small or fewer than expected.","zh":"there aren’t that many 是指數量相當少，或比預期少。"},{"en":"There aren’t that many seats left, so we should book quickly.","zh":"剩下的座位數量不多，所以我們應該快點預訂。"},{"en":"If there aren’t that many buses, passengers may need to wait longer.","zh":"如果巴士數量不多，乘客可能需要等更久。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to explain shortage or limited choice.","zh":"這個短語常用來解釋短缺或選擇有限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"car use","meaning":"用車情況","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks Sadie about her car use.","zh":"訪問員詢問 Sadie 的用車情況。"},{"en":"Car use means how often and for what purposes someone uses a car.","zh":"car use 是指某人使用汽車的頻率和目的。"},{"en":"A transport survey may study car use to understand traffic and parking demand.","zh":"交通調查可能研究用車情況，以了解交通和泊車需求。"},{"en":"High car use can lead to more congestion and pollution in busy areas.","zh":"用車頻繁可能在繁忙地區造成更多擠塞和污染。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on habits of using a car, not simply owning one.","zh":"這個短語著重使用汽車的習慣，而不只是擁有汽車。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"I have got","meaning":"我有……","examples":[{"en":"Sadie has got a car, but she does not use it often.","zh":"Sadie 有一部車，但她不常使用。"},{"en":"I have got means I have or I own something, especially in British English.","zh":"I have got 是指我有或我擁有某物，尤其常見於英式英語。"},{"en":"I have got a monthly bus pass, so I do not need to buy tickets every day.","zh":"我有一張月票，所以不需要每天買車票。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to talk about possessions, responsibilities, or arrangements.","zh":"人們用這個短語談論擁有物、責任或安排。"},{"en":"It is common in everyday spoken English.","zh":"它常見於日常口語英文。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not use it that often","meaning":"不太經常使用它","examples":[{"en":"Sadie has a car but does not use it that often.","zh":"Sadie 有一部車，但不太經常使用它。"},{"en":"Not use it that often means not use it very frequently.","zh":"not use it that often 是指不太頻繁使用它。"},{"en":"A person may own a printer but not use it that often because most documents are online.","zh":"一個人可能有打印機，但因為大部分文件都在線上，所以不太經常使用它。"},{"en":"If someone does not use a car often, keeping it may still be expensive.","zh":"如果某人不常用車，保養它仍可能很昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase softens the idea of rarely using something.","zh":"這個短語較柔和地表達很少使用某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"mainly just to","meaning":"主要只是為了……","examples":[{"en":"Sadie mainly uses the car just to go to the supermarket.","zh":"Sadie 使用汽車主要只是為了去超級市場。"},{"en":"Mainly just to means mostly for only one simple purpose.","zh":"mainly just to 是指主要只為一個簡單目的。"},{"en":"I mainly use my laptop just to write essays and check emails.","zh":"我使用手提電腦主要只是為了寫文章和查看電郵。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the use is limited and not very varied.","zh":"這個短語顯示用途有限，而且不太多樣。"},{"en":"It often suggests that something is owned but used only for a narrow reason.","zh":"它常暗示某物雖然擁有，但只因很狹窄的原因而使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"go to the supermarket","meaning":"去超級市場","examples":[{"en":"Sadie mainly uses her car to go to the supermarket.","zh":"Sadie 主要用車去超級市場。"},{"en":"To go to the supermarket means to visit a large food and household goods shop.","zh":"go to the supermarket 是指前往大型食品和家居用品商店。"},{"en":"A family may go to the supermarket once a week to buy groceries.","zh":"一家人可能每週去超級市場一次買日用品和食物。"},{"en":"People often drive to the supermarket when they need to carry heavy bags.","zh":"當人們需要拿很重的購物袋時，常會駕車去超級市場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common everyday errand.","zh":"這個短語描述常見的日常差事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"that’s about it","meaning":"基本上就是這樣","examples":[{"en":"Sadie mainly uses the car for shopping, and that is about it.","zh":"Sadie 主要用車購物，基本上就是這樣。"},{"en":"That’s about it means there is nothing much more to add.","zh":"that’s about it 是指沒有甚麼更多要補充。"},{"en":"I only use the tablet for reading notes and checking messages; that’s about it.","zh":"我只用平板電腦看筆記和查看訊息，基本上就是這樣。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to show that a list or explanation is basically complete.","zh":"人們用這個短語表示清單或解釋大致完成。"},{"en":"It sounds casual and often suggests the situation is simple.","zh":"它聽起來較口語，常暗示情況很簡單。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at the weekends","meaning":"在週末","examples":[{"en":"Sadie’s husband uses the car at the weekends.","zh":"Sadie 的丈夫在週末使用汽車。"},{"en":"At the weekends means on Saturdays and Sundays.","zh":"at the weekends 是指在星期六和星期日。"},{"en":"Many families visit relatives at the weekends because they are free from work or school.","zh":"許多家庭在週末探望親戚，因為不用上班或上學。"},{"en":"Transport habits can change at the weekends because people travel for leisure rather than work.","zh":"週末的交通習慣可能改變，因為人們為休閒而不是工作出行。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English; American English often says “on the weekends”.","zh":"這個短語常見於英式英語；美式英語常說 on the weekends。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"golf club","meaning":"高爾夫球會","examples":[{"en":"Sadie’s husband drives to the golf club at the weekends.","zh":"Sadie 的丈夫週末駕車去高爾夫球會。"},{"en":"A golf club is a place where people play golf and may also socialise.","zh":"golf club 是人們打高爾夫球，也可能社交的地方。"},{"en":"Members of a golf club may book times to play on the course.","zh":"高爾夫球會會員可能會預訂球場時間。"},{"en":"People often drive to a golf club because it may be outside the town centre.","zh":"人們常駕車去高爾夫球會，因為它可能位於市中心以外。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean both the organisation and the place where golf is played.","zh":"這個短語既可指組織，也可指打高爾夫球的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"what about a bicycle?","meaning":"那單車呢？","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks Sadie about using a bicycle.","zh":"訪問員問 Sadie 使用單車方面的情況。"},{"en":"What about a bicycle? asks whether cycling is another possible transport option.","zh":"What about a bicycle? 是問踩單車是否另一個可能的交通選項。"},{"en":"After discussing buses and cars, a survey worker may ask, “What about a bicycle?”","zh":"討論完巴士和汽車後，調查員可能會問：「那單車呢？」"},{"en":"This question introduces a new but related topic in the conversation.","zh":"這個問題在對話中引入新的相關主題。"},{"en":"It is a short way to ask for someone’s opinion or experience with bikes.","zh":"它是詢問某人對單車的看法或經驗的簡短方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at the moment","meaning":"目前","examples":[{"en":"Sadie does not have a bicycle at the moment.","zh":"Sadie 目前沒有單車。"},{"en":"At the moment means right now or at the present time.","zh":"at the moment 是指現在或目前這個時候。"},{"en":"I am not taking any extra classes at the moment because I am busy with exams.","zh":"我目前沒有上額外課程，因為正忙於考試。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest that the situation may change later.","zh":"這個短語可以暗示情況之後可能會改變。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing a current condition rather than a permanent fact.","zh":"它適合用來描述目前狀況，而不是永久事實。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"city bikes","meaning":"城市租用單車","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks about the city bikes people can rent.","zh":"訪問員詢問人們可以租用的城市租用單車。"},{"en":"City bikes are shared bicycles that people can rent for short journeys in a city.","zh":"city bikes 是人們可在城市中租用作短途行程的共享單車。"},{"en":"Tourists may use city bikes to travel between museums, parks, and cafés.","zh":"遊客可能使用城市租用單車往返博物館、公園和咖啡店。"},{"en":"City bikes can reduce short car trips if they are cheap and easy to find.","zh":"如果價格便宜又容易找到，城市租用單車可以減少短途汽車旅程。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a public bike-rental system, not someone’s personal bicycle.","zh":"這個短語指公共單車租用系統，而不是某人的私人單車。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rent","meaning":"租用","examples":[{"en":"People can rent city bikes.","zh":"人們可以租用城市單車。"},{"en":"To rent something means to pay to use it for a limited time without owning it.","zh":"rent something 是指付費在有限時間內使用某物，但不擁有它。"},{"en":"A family may rent a car for a holiday instead of buying one.","zh":"一家人可能為假期租用汽車，而不是購買一部。"},{"en":"Renting is useful when you need something temporarily.","zh":"當你暫時需要某物時，租用很有用。"},{"en":"This word contrasts with buying, because the item must usually be returned.","zh":"這個詞與購買相對，因為物品通常必須歸還。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"do you ever use those?","meaning":"你有用過那些嗎？","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks whether Sadie ever uses the city bikes.","zh":"訪問員問 Sadie 是否有用過那些城市單車。"},{"en":"Do you ever use those? asks whether someone uses those things at any time.","zh":"Do you ever use those? 是問某人是否曾經在任何時候使用那些東西。"},{"en":"If a friend points to exercise machines, she may ask, “Do you ever use those?”","zh":"如果朋友指着健身器械，她可能會問：「你有用過那些嗎？」"},{"en":"This question is useful when the speaker wants to know about occasional habits, not regular ones only.","zh":"當說話者想知道偶爾習慣，而不只是定期習慣時，這個問題很有用。"},{"en":"Ever makes the question include even rare use.","zh":"ever 令問題包括即使很少發生的使用情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not keen on","meaning":"不太喜歡；不太想","examples":[{"en":"Sadie is not keen on cycling in the city.","zh":"Sadie 不太喜歡在城裏踩單車。"},{"en":"Not keen on something means not very interested in it or not liking it much.","zh":"not keen on something 是指對某事不太感興趣或不太喜歡。"},{"en":"A student may be not keen on group work if she prefers studying alone.","zh":"如果學生較喜歡獨自溫習，她可能不太喜歡小組活動。"},{"en":"People may not be keen on an activity because it feels unsafe, difficult, or unpleasant.","zh":"人們可能因某活動感覺不安全、困難或不舒服而不太想做。"},{"en":"This phrase is softer than saying “I hate it”.","zh":"這個短語比說 “I hate it” 更委婉。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cycling","meaning":"踩單車","examples":[{"en":"Sadie is not keen on cycling there because of the pollution.","zh":"Sadie 因為污染而不太喜歡在那裏踩單車。"},{"en":"Cycling means riding a bicycle.","zh":"cycling 是指踩單車。"},{"en":"Many people enjoy cycling to work because it gives them exercise.","zh":"許多人喜歡踩單車上班，因為這能讓他們運動。"},{"en":"Cycling can be less attractive when roads are busy or air quality is poor.","zh":"當道路繁忙或空氣質素差，踩單車可能變得較不吸引。"},{"en":"This word refers to the activity of using a bike, often for transport or exercise.","zh":"這個詞指使用單車的活動，通常作交通或運動用途。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"because of","meaning":"因為……","examples":[{"en":"Sadie avoids cycling because of all the pollution.","zh":"Sadie 因為嚴重污染而避免踩單車。"},{"en":"Because of introduces the reason for something.","zh":"because of 用來引入某事的原因。"},{"en":"The match was cancelled because of heavy rain.","zh":"比賽因為大雨而取消。"},{"en":"People may change travel plans because of cost, weather, or safety concerns.","zh":"人們可能因為費用、天氣或安全問題而改變出行計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is followed by a noun phrase, not a full clause.","zh":"這個短語後面接名詞短語，而不是完整子句。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"all the pollution","meaning":"嚴重污染","examples":[{"en":"Sadie does not want to cycle in the city because of all the pollution.","zh":"Sadie 不想在城裏踩單車，因為污染嚴重。"},{"en":"All the pollution means the large amount of dirty air, noise, or harmful substances in an area.","zh":"all the pollution 是指某地大量骯髒空氣、噪音或有害物質。"},{"en":"People may avoid walking beside busy roads because of all the pollution.","zh":"人們可能因為污染嚴重而避免在繁忙馬路旁步行。"},{"en":"Pollution can make outdoor exercise less healthy and less pleasant.","zh":"污染會令戶外運動較不健康，也較不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds conversational and emphasises that there is a lot of pollution.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並強調污染很多。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"get a bike","meaning":"買一部單車","examples":[{"en":"Sadie would like to get a bike.","zh":"Sadie 想買一部單車。"},{"en":"To get a bike means to buy, obtain, or start having a bicycle.","zh":"get a bike 是指買、取得或開始擁有一部單車。"},{"en":"A student may get a bike to travel to school more quickly.","zh":"學生可能會買一部單車，以更快上學。"},{"en":"Getting a bike can save transport money if there is a safe place to ride and store it.","zh":"如果有安全路線和存放地方，買單車可以節省交通費。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and does not specify whether the bike is bought new or second-hand.","zh":"這個短語較口語，沒有說明單車是新買還是二手。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"get to work","meaning":"上班；前往工作地點","examples":[{"en":"A bike would be good for getting to work.","zh":"單車對上班會很有用。"},{"en":"To get to work means to travel to the place where you do your job.","zh":"get to work 是指前往你工作的地方。"},{"en":"Some people get to work by train, while others walk or cycle.","zh":"有些人乘火車上班，另一些人步行或踩單車。"},{"en":"A reliable way to get to work is important because being late can affect your job.","zh":"可靠的上班方式很重要，因為遲到可能影響工作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the journey to the workplace.","zh":"這個短語著重前往工作地點的行程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"live in a flat","meaning":"住在單位","examples":[{"en":"Sadie lives in a flat on the second floor.","zh":"Sadie 住在二樓的一個單位。"},{"en":"To live in a flat means to live in an apartment within a building.","zh":"live in a flat 是指住在大廈中的一個住宅單位。"},{"en":"Many people in cities live in flats because land is limited.","zh":"許多城市人住在單位裏，因為土地有限。"},{"en":"Living in a flat can make storing large items difficult if there is little space.","zh":"如果空間少，住在單位裏可能令存放大型物品變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone’s type of home.","zh":"這個短語描述某人的居住類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on the second floor","meaning":"在二樓","examples":[{"en":"Sadie lives on the second floor.","zh":"Sadie 住在二樓。"},{"en":"On the second floor means on the level of a building above the first floor.","zh":"on the second floor 是指在建築物一樓以上的第二層。"},{"en":"A classroom on the second floor may require students to use the stairs or lift.","zh":"在二樓的課室可能需要學生使用樓梯或升降機。"},{"en":"Carrying a heavy bicycle to the second floor can be tiring.","zh":"把沉重單車搬到二樓可能很累。"},{"en":"This phrase tells us the level or storey of a building.","zh":"這個短語告訴我們建築物的樓層。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"storage space","meaning":"儲物空間","examples":[{"en":"Sadie’s flat does not have any storage space.","zh":"Sadie 的單位沒有任何儲物空間。"},{"en":"Storage space is space used for keeping things when they are not being used.","zh":"storage space 是用來存放暫時不用物品的空間。"},{"en":"A small flat may not have enough storage space for suitcases, sports equipment, or bicycles.","zh":"小單位可能沒有足夠儲物空間放行李箱、運動器材或單車。"},{"en":"Lack of storage space can stop people from buying large items.","zh":"缺乏儲物空間可能令人不買大型物品。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical space for keeping belongings.","zh":"這個短語指用來存放物品的實用空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"leave it in the hall","meaning":"把它放在走廊","examples":[{"en":"Sadie would have to leave the bike in the hall outside the flat.","zh":"Sadie 必須把單車放在單位外面的走廊。"},{"en":"To leave it in the hall means to put it in the corridor or entrance area and keep it there.","zh":"leave it in the hall 是指把它放在走廊或入口區域並留在那裏。"},{"en":"A tenant may leave an umbrella in the hall to dry after heavy rain.","zh":"租客可能在大雨後把雨傘放在走廊晾乾。"},{"en":"Leaving a bike in the hall may block neighbours or create a safety problem.","zh":"把單車放在走廊可能阻礙鄰居或造成安全問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes storing something in a shared indoor space.","zh":"這個短語描述把某物存放在共用室內空間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"outside the flat","meaning":"在單位外面","examples":[{"en":"The bike would have to be left outside the flat.","zh":"單車必須放在單位外面。"},{"en":"Outside the flat means not inside the apartment, usually in the hallway or nearby shared area.","zh":"outside the flat 是指不在住宅單位裏面，通常在走廊或附近共用區域。"},{"en":"Shoes left outside the flat may annoy neighbours if they block the corridor.","zh":"放在單位外面的鞋若阻塞走廊，可能令鄰居不滿。"},{"en":"Keeping valuable items outside the flat can increase the risk of theft or damage.","zh":"把貴重物品放在單位外面，可能增加被盜或損壞風險。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with storing something inside the home.","zh":"這個短語與把某物放在家裏面相對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"I think that’s all","meaning":"我想問題就到這裏","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer says, “I think that’s all,” at the end of the survey.","zh":"訪問員在調查結束時說：「我想問題就到這裏。」"},{"en":"I think that’s all means I believe there is nothing more to ask, say, or do.","zh":"I think that’s all 是指我認為沒有更多要問、要說或要做的事。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “I think that’s all,” after answering the final question.","zh":"老師回答最後一個問題後，可能會說：「我想就到這裏。」"},{"en":"This phrase signals that a conversation, meeting, or task is ending.","zh":"這個短語表示對話、會議或任務即將結束。"},{"en":"It sounds polite because it gently closes the interaction.","zh":"它聽起來有禮貌，因為它溫和地結束互動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 1.pdf","sourcePage":8}],"ielts/listening/Practice 9/task-2":[{"front":"let me start by","meaning":"讓我先……","examples":[{"en":"Let me start by welcoming you all to this talk.","zh":"讓我先歡迎大家來到這個講座。"},{"en":"“Let me start by...” is used when a speaker wants to begin with a particular first point or action.","zh":"“Let me start by...” 用於說話者想以某個第一點或第一個行動開始。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “Let me start by explaining today’s lesson aims.”","zh":"老師可能說：「讓我先解釋今天的課堂目標。」"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise a speech because it tells listeners what will come first.","zh":"這個短語有助組織演講，因為它告訴聽眾接下來首先會做甚麼。"},{"en":"It is polite and common at the beginning of talks, meetings, and presentations.","zh":"它有禮，常見於講座、會議和簡報開頭。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"welcome you all to","meaning":"歡迎大家來到……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker welcomes everyone to the talk.","zh":"講者歡迎大家來到這個講座。"},{"en":"To welcome you all to an event means to greet everyone politely at the beginning.","zh":"welcome you all to an event 指在活動開始時有禮地問候所有人。"},{"en":"A principal may welcome parents to a school open day.","zh":"校長可能歡迎家長來到學校開放日。"},{"en":"Welcoming people helps create a friendly atmosphere before the main message begins.","zh":"歡迎大家可以在主要內容開始前營造友善氣氛。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and useful for public speaking.","zh":"這個短語較正式，適合公開演說。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"thank you for taking the time to","meaning":"感謝你抽時間去……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker thanks them for taking the time to consider joining ACE.","zh":"講者感謝他們抽時間考慮加入 ACE。"},{"en":"Thank you for taking the time to do something means thank you for spending your time on it.","zh":"thank you for taking the time to do something 指感謝你花時間做某事。"},{"en":"A manager may say, “Thank you for taking the time to attend this interview.”","zh":"經理可能說：「感謝你抽時間參加這次面試。」"},{"en":"This phrase shows respect because it recognises that the listener’s time is valuable.","zh":"這個短語顯示尊重，因為它承認聽者的時間有價值。"},{"en":"It is common in formal talks, emails, and meetings.","zh":"它常見於正式講話、電郵和會議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"consider joining","meaning":"考慮加入……","examples":[{"en":"The audience are considering joining ACE voluntary organisation.","zh":"聽眾正在考慮加入 ACE 義工組織。"},{"en":"To consider joining means to think carefully about becoming a member of a group.","zh":"consider joining 指仔細思考是否成為某組織的成員。"},{"en":"A student may consider joining a drama club after watching a school performance.","zh":"學生看完學校表演後，可能考慮加入戲劇學會。"},{"en":"People often consider joining when they want to know the time, duties, and benefits first.","zh":"人們通常想先了解時間、職責和好處，才考慮加入。"},{"en":"This phrase shows interest, but not a final decision yet.","zh":"這個短語顯示有興趣，但尚未作最終決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"voluntary organisation","meaning":"義工組織","examples":[{"en":"ACE is a voluntary organisation.","zh":"ACE 是一個義工組織。"},{"en":"A voluntary organisation is a group that helps people or the community, often using unpaid volunteers.","zh":"voluntary organisation 指幫助人或社區的組織，通常依靠無薪義工。"},{"en":"A voluntary organisation may run food drives, visit elderly people, or support disabled children.","zh":"義工組織可能舉辦食物捐贈、探訪長者或支援殘疾兒童。"},{"en":"Such organisations depend on people giving time, skills, and energy.","zh":"這類組織依靠人們付出時間、技能和精力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a group created to serve others rather than make profit.","zh":"這個短語描述為服務他人而成立，而不是為牟利而成立的組織。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"offer support to","meaning":"為……提供支援","examples":[{"en":"ACE offers support to people and services in the local area.","zh":"ACE 為本區居民和服務項目提供支援。"},{"en":"To offer support to someone means to give help, advice, time, money, or practical assistance.","zh":"offer support to someone 指給予幫助、建議、時間、金錢或實際協助。"},{"en":"A school may offer support to students who are struggling with exams.","zh":"學校可能為考試吃力的學生提供支援。"},{"en":"Offering support can reduce pressure and help people continue difficult work.","zh":"提供支援可以減輕壓力，並幫助人繼續困難工作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on giving help where it is needed.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於在有需要的地方給予幫助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"people and services","meaning":"居民和服務項目","examples":[{"en":"ACE offers support to people and services in the local area.","zh":"ACE 為本區居民和服務項目提供支援。"},{"en":"People and services means individuals in the community and organised help such as clubs, centres, or care programmes.","zh":"people and services 指社區中的個人，以及學會、中心或照顧計劃等有組織支援。"},{"en":"A charity may support people and services by helping both families and local youth centres.","zh":"慈善機構可以透過幫助家庭和本地青年中心來支援居民和服務項目。"},{"en":"Helping services can indirectly help many people who use them.","zh":"幫助服務項目可以間接幫助許多使用服務的人。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that support can go to individuals and organisations.","zh":"這個短語顯示支援可以給個人，也可以給組織。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"local area","meaning":"本區；當地","examples":[{"en":"ACE works with people and services in the local area.","zh":"ACE 與本區居民和服務項目合作。"},{"en":"The local area is the nearby community, district, or neighbourhood.","zh":"local area 指附近的社區、地區或鄰里。"},{"en":"A volunteer group may clean parks and visit care homes in the local area.","zh":"義工小組可能在本區清潔公園和探訪護老院。"},{"en":"Focusing on the local area helps an organisation understand real community needs.","zh":"聚焦本區有助組織了解真正的社區需要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the place close to where people live or work.","zh":"這個短語指人們居住或工作的附近地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look for more volunteers","meaning":"尋找更多義工","examples":[{"en":"ACE is looking for more volunteers.","zh":"ACE 正在尋找更多義工。"},{"en":"To look for more volunteers means to try to find additional people willing to help without pay.","zh":"look for more volunteers 指嘗試尋找額外願意無薪幫忙的人。"},{"en":"A school fair may look for more volunteers to run game stalls.","zh":"學校賣物會可能尋找更多義工來負責遊戲攤位。"},{"en":"When there are not enough helpers, an organisation needs to look for more volunteers.","zh":"當人手不足，組織就需要尋找更多義工。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when extra human help is needed.","zh":"這個短語用於需要額外人手幫忙時。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"help us do this","meaning":"幫助我們做這件事","examples":[{"en":"More volunteers are needed to help ACE support the local area.","zh":"ACE 需要更多義工幫助它支援本區。"},{"en":"Help us do this means assist us in carrying out the task just mentioned.","zh":"help us do this 指協助我們完成剛才提到的任務。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “Please help us do this by returning the forms on time.”","zh":"老師可能說：「請準時交回表格，幫助我們做這件事。」"},{"en":"This phrase connects listeners to a shared action or goal.","zh":"這個短語把聽者與共同的行動或目標連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when asking people to take part in a community effort.","zh":"邀請人參與社區工作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"by the way","meaning":"順帶一提","examples":[{"en":"By the way, the speaker hopes everyone is comfortable.","zh":"順帶一提，講者希望大家感到舒適。"},{"en":"By the way is used to add a related or extra comment to the conversation.","zh":"by the way 用來在對話中加入相關或額外補充。"},{"en":"A student may say, “By the way, the meeting room has changed.”","zh":"學生可能說：「順帶一提，會議室改了。」"},{"en":"This phrase signals a small change of topic without ending the main discussion.","zh":"這個短語表示話題稍微轉變，但不會結束主要討論。"},{"en":"It is common in casual and semi-formal speech.","zh":"它常見於日常和半正式說話。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be comfortable","meaning":"坐得舒服；感到舒適","examples":[{"en":"The speaker hopes that everyone is comfortable.","zh":"講者希望大家感到舒適。"},{"en":"Be comfortable means feel physically relaxed, not too hot, crowded, tired, or awkward.","zh":"be comfortable 指身體上放鬆，不太熱、不太擠、不太累或不尷尬。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask whether students are comfortable before a long exam briefing.","zh":"老師在長時間考試簡介前，可能問學生是否坐得舒服。"},{"en":"If people are comfortable, they can listen and participate more easily.","zh":"如果人們感到舒適，就能更容易聆聽和參與。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe physical ease or emotional ease.","zh":"這個短語可以描述身體舒適，也可以描述情緒自在。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"bring in extra seats","meaning":"加設額外座位","examples":[{"en":"ACE has brought in extra seats for the talk.","zh":"ACE 為這個講座加設了額外座位。"},{"en":"To bring in extra seats means to add more chairs because the original number is not enough.","zh":"bring in extra seats 指因原本座位不足而增加更多椅子。"},{"en":"A school hall may bring in extra seats when more parents arrive than expected.","zh":"當到場家長比預期多，學校禮堂可能加設額外座位。"},{"en":"Extra seats help prevent people from standing during an event.","zh":"額外座位有助避免人們在活動中站着。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical arrangement for a larger audience.","zh":"這個短語描述為較多觀眾作出的實際安排。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"so that no one has to","meaning":"以便沒有人需要……","examples":[{"en":"Extra seats were brought in so that no one has to stand.","zh":"加設額外座位，以便沒有人需要站着。"},{"en":"So that no one has to means in order to prevent anyone from needing to do something.","zh":"so that no one has to 指為了避免任何人需要做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may print extra worksheets so that no one has to share.","zh":"老師可能多印工作紙，以便沒有人需要共用。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose of an action.","zh":"這個短語解釋行動的目的。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing how planning avoids inconvenience.","zh":"說明計劃如何避免不便時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stand","meaning":"站着","examples":[{"en":"No one has to stand during the talk.","zh":"講座期間沒有人需要站着。"},{"en":"To stand means to be on your feet rather than sitting.","zh":"stand 指以雙腳支撐身體，而不是坐下。"},{"en":"Passengers may have to stand on a crowded bus when all seats are taken.","zh":"當座位全滿時，乘客可能需要在擠迫巴士上站着。"},{"en":"Standing for a long time can make people tired and less able to focus.","zh":"長時間站着會令人疲倦，較難集中精神。"},{"en":"This word describes a basic body position.","zh":"這個字描述基本身體姿勢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"it does mean that","meaning":"這確實意味著……","examples":[{"en":"It does mean that the people at the back may be a bit squashed.","zh":"這確實意味著房間後方的人可能會有點擠迫。"},{"en":"It does mean that is used to point out a real consequence, often after giving good news.","zh":"it does mean that 用來指出一個真實後果，常在說出好消息後補充。"},{"en":"We have enough chairs, but it does mean that the aisle will be narrow.","zh":"我們有足夠椅子，但這確實意味著通道會較窄。"},{"en":"This phrase helps the speaker be honest about a small disadvantage.","zh":"這個短語幫助說話者誠實說出小缺點。"},{"en":"It usually introduces something listeners should accept or notice.","zh":"它通常引出聽者應接受或留意的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at the back of the room","meaning":"在房間後方","examples":[{"en":"The people at the back of the room may be a bit squashed.","zh":"在房間後方的人可能會有點擠迫。"},{"en":"At the back of the room means in the area farthest from the front or speaker.","zh":"at the back of the room 指在離前方或講者最遠的位置。"},{"en":"Students at the back of the room may find it harder to see the board.","zh":"坐在房間後方的學生可能較難看見白板。"},{"en":"People at the back may need louder sound or clearer slides.","zh":"後方的人可能需要更大的聲音或更清晰的投影片。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position inside a room.","zh":"這個短語描述房間內的位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a bit squashed","meaning":"有點擠迫","examples":[{"en":"The people at the back may be a bit squashed.","zh":"後方的人可能有點擠迫。"},{"en":"A bit squashed means slightly crowded, with not much space to move.","zh":"a bit squashed 指有點擁擠，沒有太多活動空間。"},{"en":"Students may feel a bit squashed when too many desks are placed in one classroom.","zh":"當太多書桌放在同一間課室，學生可能感到有點擠迫。"},{"en":"Being squashed can make people uncomfortable, but “a bit” makes the complaint milder.","zh":"擠迫會令人不舒服，但 “a bit” 令投訴語氣較溫和。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mild physical crowding.","zh":"這個短語描述輕微身體擠迫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"for about half an hour","meaning":"大約半小時","examples":[{"en":"The talk will last for about half an hour.","zh":"講座會持續大約半小時。"},{"en":"For about half an hour means for roughly thirty minutes.","zh":"for about half an hour 指大約三十分鐘。"},{"en":"A school assembly may last for about half an hour before lessons begin.","zh":"學校早會可能在上課前持續大約半小時。"},{"en":"Giving an approximate length helps listeners know how long they need to stay focused.","zh":"提供大約時長有助聽眾知道需要集中多久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an estimated duration.","zh":"這個短語描述估計時間長度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hopefully","meaning":"希望","examples":[{"en":"Hopefully, the crowded seating is acceptable.","zh":"希望擠迫的座位安排可以接受。"},{"en":"Hopefully means the speaker hopes something will happen or be true.","zh":"hopefully 指說話者希望某事會發生或是真的。"},{"en":"Hopefully, the rain will stop before the school picnic begins.","zh":"希望在學校野餐開始前雨會停。"},{"en":"This word shows optimism, but not certainty.","zh":"這個字顯示樂觀，但不是肯定。"},{"en":"It is often used when the speaker cannot fully control the result.","zh":"當說話者不能完全控制結果時，常會使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"one of the first questions","meaning":"最先被問到的問題之一","examples":[{"en":"One of the first questions often asked is about age.","zh":"最先被問到的問題之一通常是關於年齡。"},{"en":"One of the first questions means one question people usually ask near the beginning.","zh":"one of the first questions 指人們通常在一開始附近提出的其中一個問題。"},{"en":"One of the first questions about a new course is often how much it costs.","zh":"關於新課程，最先被問到的問題之一通常是費用多少。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights an early and common concern.","zh":"這個短語突出早期而常見的關注點。"},{"en":"It is useful when introducing frequently asked questions.","zh":"介紹常見問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be often asked","meaning":"經常被問到","examples":[{"en":"The organisation is often asked how old volunteers need to be.","zh":"該組織經常被問到義工需要幾歲。"},{"en":"Be often asked means people ask this question many times.","zh":"be often asked 指人們多次提出這個問題。"},{"en":"A teacher is often asked whether the test will include writing.","zh":"老師經常被問到測驗是否包括寫作。"},{"en":"If a question is often asked, it may need a clear answer in advance.","zh":"如果某問題經常被問到，可能需要預先清楚回答。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated question.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆出現的問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"how old you need to be","meaning":"你需要幾歲","examples":[{"en":"People often ask how old they need to be to volunteer.","zh":"人們常問做義工需要幾歲。"},{"en":"How old you need to be means the minimum or suitable age required for an activity.","zh":"how old you need to be 指參加某活動所需的最低或合適年齡。"},{"en":"Students may ask how old they need to be to join a first-aid course.","zh":"學生可能問參加急救課程需要幾歲。"},{"en":"Age requirements help protect younger people and match them with suitable tasks.","zh":"年齡要求有助保護較年輕的人，並把他們配對到合適任務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when checking eligibility.","zh":"查詢資格時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"volunteer","meaning":"做義工","examples":[{"en":"People can volunteer for ACE from the age of 16.","zh":"人們由16歲起可以為 ACE 做義工。"},{"en":"To volunteer means to offer time and effort to help without being paid.","zh":"volunteer 指自願付出時間和努力幫忙，而不收取薪酬。"},{"en":"A student may volunteer at a charity shop on Saturday mornings.","zh":"學生可能逢星期六早上在慈善商店做義工。"},{"en":"Volunteering can help others while giving the volunteer experience and confidence.","zh":"做義工可以幫助別人，同時給義工經驗和信心。"},{"en":"This verb describes choosing to help willingly.","zh":"這個動詞描述自願選擇幫忙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as young as","meaning":"年輕至……","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers can be as young as 16.","zh":"義工可以年輕至16歲。"},{"en":"As young as 16 means 16 is the lowest or surprisingly young age allowed.","zh":"as young as 16 指16歲是容許的最低或令人覺得年輕的年齡。"},{"en":"Some music classes accept children as young as five.","zh":"有些音樂班接受年輕至五歲的孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase draws attention to how young someone can be and still qualify.","zh":"這個短語突出某人可以多麼年輕而仍符合資格。"},{"en":"It is often used when a low age is notable.","zh":"當低年齡值得注意時，常會使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"60 or over","meaning":"60歲或以上","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers can also be 60 or over.","zh":"義工也可以是60歲或以上。"},{"en":"60 or over means aged 60 or older.","zh":"60 or over 指年齡為60歲或更高。"},{"en":"People who are 60 or over may join community classes after retirement.","zh":"60歲或以上的人退休後可能參加社區課程。"},{"en":"Including people 60 or over shows that older adults can still contribute actively.","zh":"包括60歲或以上的人，顯示年長成年人仍可積極貢獻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an age group beginning at 60.","zh":"這個短語描述由60歲開始的年齡群組。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it all depends on","meaning":"這完全取決於……","examples":[{"en":"It all depends on what type of voluntary work they want to do.","zh":"這完全取決於他們想做哪種類型的義務工作。"},{"en":"It all depends on means the answer changes according to a particular factor.","zh":"it all depends on 指答案會按照某個特定因素而改變。"},{"en":"Whether a student needs extra tuition all depends on her goals and current level.","zh":"學生是否需要額外補習，完全取決於她的目標和目前程度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when there is no single simple answer.","zh":"當沒有單一簡單答案時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It tells listeners which condition matters most.","zh":"它告訴聽者最重要的條件是甚麼。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"type of voluntary work","meaning":"義務工作的類型","examples":[{"en":"The age requirement depends on the type of voluntary work.","zh":"年齡要求取決於義務工作的類型。"},{"en":"Type of voluntary work means the particular kind of unpaid helping role.","zh":"type of voluntary work 指無薪幫忙角色的特定種類。"},{"en":"Reading stories to children and collecting litter are different types of voluntary work.","zh":"為孩子講故事和清理垃圾是不同類型的義務工作。"},{"en":"Different work types need different ages, skills, and levels of responsibility.","zh":"不同工作類型需要不同年齡、技能和責任程度。"},{"en":"This phrase helps match volunteers with suitable roles.","zh":"這個短語有助把義工配對到合適角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"other considerations","meaning":"其他考慮因素","examples":[{"en":"Other considerations are crucial in voluntary work.","zh":"其他考慮因素在義務工作中非常重要。"},{"en":"Other considerations are additional things that must be thought about before deciding.","zh":"other considerations 指決定前必須思考的額外事項。"},{"en":"When choosing a school trip, other considerations include safety, cost, and travel time.","zh":"選擇學校旅行時，其他考慮因素包括安全、費用和交通時間。"},{"en":"Considering more than one factor helps people avoid poor decisions.","zh":"考慮多於一個因素有助人避免差劣決定。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the first issue is not the only important one.","zh":"這個短語顯示第一個問題不是唯一重要的事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reliability","meaning":"可靠性","examples":[{"en":"Reliability is crucial in voluntary work.","zh":"可靠性在義務工作中非常重要。"},{"en":"Reliability means being dependable, keeping promises, and turning up when expected.","zh":"reliability 指值得信賴、守承諾，並在預期時間出現。"},{"en":"A reliable student arrives on time for every group meeting.","zh":"可靠的學生會準時出席每次小組會議。"},{"en":"If volunteers lack reliability, services may be cancelled or clients may be disappointed.","zh":"如果義工缺乏可靠性，服務可能取消，服務使用者也可能失望。"},{"en":"This word describes whether people can be trusted to do what they said.","zh":"這個字描述人們是否可信地做到自己答應的事。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be crucial in","meaning":"在……中非常重要","examples":[{"en":"Reliability is crucial in voluntary work.","zh":"可靠性在義務工作中非常重要。"},{"en":"Be crucial in something means be extremely important in that situation or activity.","zh":"be crucial in something 指在某情況或活動中極其重要。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are crucial in a science experiment.","zh":"清晰指示在科學實驗中非常重要。"},{"en":"If something is crucial, problems may occur when it is missing.","zh":"如果某事非常重要，一旦缺少它就可能出問題。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a key factor.","zh":"這個短語突出關鍵因素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Age is not related to reliability.","zh":"年齡與可靠性無關。"},{"en":"Be related to something means have a connection with it.","zh":"be related to something 指與某事有連繫。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is often related to weak concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足常與課堂專注力弱有關。"},{"en":"If two things are not related, one does not clearly affect or explain the other.","zh":"如果兩件事無關，其中一件就不能清楚影響或解釋另一件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes connection between ideas, facts, or causes.","zh":"這個短語描述想法、事實或原因之間的連繫。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in our experience","meaning":"根據我們的經驗","examples":[{"en":"In ACE’s experience, age is not related to reliability.","zh":"根據 ACE 的經驗，年齡與可靠性無關。"},{"en":"In our experience means based on what we have seen or done before.","zh":"in our experience 指根據我們以前看過或做過的事情。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “In our experience, students improve faster with regular practice.”","zh":"老師可能說：「根據我們的經驗，學生定期練習會進步得更快。」"},{"en":"This phrase gives an opinion more weight because it comes from real experience.","zh":"這個短語令意見更有分量，因為它來自真實經驗。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining a practical judgement.","zh":"解釋實際判斷時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"relate to training","meaning":"與培訓有關","examples":[{"en":"Another question relates to training.","zh":"另一個問題與培訓有關。"},{"en":"Relate to training means be connected with the training that people receive.","zh":"relate to training 指與人們接受的培訓有連繫。"},{"en":"A new employee’s question may relate to training if she asks how to use the company system.","zh":"如果新員工問如何使用公司系統，她的問題可能與培訓有關。"},{"en":"Questions about training often appear before people agree to join a role.","zh":"人們同意加入某角色前，常會提出關於培訓的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a topic connected to learning preparation.","zh":"這個短語引入與學習準備有關的話題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"plenty of","meaning":"大量……","examples":[{"en":"There is plenty of training for volunteers.","zh":"義工有大量培訓。"},{"en":"Plenty of means a large amount or enough of something.","zh":"plenty of 指大量或足夠的某物。"},{"en":"There is plenty of food at the school picnic, so no one should go hungry.","zh":"學校野餐有大量食物，所以沒有人應該會餓。"},{"en":"Having plenty of training can make new volunteers feel prepared.","zh":"有大量培訓可以令新義工感到準備充足。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures people that there is no shortage.","zh":"這個短語讓人放心，表示沒有短缺。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"face-to-face","meaning":"面對面","examples":[{"en":"All the training is face-to-face.","zh":"所有培訓都是面對面的。"},{"en":"Face-to-face means happening in person, with people physically meeting each other.","zh":"face-to-face 指親身進行，人們實際見面。"},{"en":"A face-to-face interview happens in the same room, not by video call.","zh":"面對面面試是在同一房間進行，而不是視像通話。"},{"en":"Face-to-face training allows people to ask questions and practise directly.","zh":"面對面培訓讓人可以直接發問和練習。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with online or remote contact.","zh":"這個短語與網上或遙距接觸形成對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"what’s more","meaning":"而且","examples":[{"en":"What’s more, training does not end when volunteers start working.","zh":"而且，義工開始工作時，培訓並不會結束。"},{"en":"What’s more means in addition, especially when adding another important point.","zh":"what’s more 指此外，尤其用來加入另一個重要觀點。"},{"en":"The course is free; what’s more, all materials are provided.","zh":"課程免費；而且，所有材料都會提供。"},{"en":"This phrase helps strengthen a point by adding extra information.","zh":"這個短語透過加入額外資料來加強觀點。"},{"en":"It is useful when listing advantages or reasons.","zh":"列出好處或理由時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"start working for us","meaning":"開始為我們工作","examples":[{"en":"Training does not end when volunteers start working for ACE.","zh":"義工開始為 ACE 工作時，培訓並不會結束。"},{"en":"Start working for us means begin doing work for our organisation.","zh":"start working for us 指開始為我們的組織做工作。"},{"en":"New staff may receive support after they start working for a company.","zh":"新員工開始為公司工作後，可能仍會獲得支援。"},{"en":"When people start working, they often still need guidance and practice.","zh":"當人們開始工作，他們通常仍需要指導和練習。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the beginning of service or employment with a group.","zh":"這個短語標示開始為某組織服務或受僱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take place before, during and after","meaning":"在……之前、期間和之後進行","examples":[{"en":"Training takes place before, during and after periods of work.","zh":"培訓在工作時段之前、期間和之後進行。"},{"en":"Take place before, during and after means happen at all three stages: earlier, at the same time, and later.","zh":"take place before, during and after 指在三個階段都發生：之前、同時和之後。"},{"en":"Safety checks may take place before, during and after a school trip.","zh":"安全檢查可能在學校旅行之前、期間和之後進行。"},{"en":"Doing something across all stages helps prevent problems and improve performance.","zh":"在所有階段都做某事，有助防止問題並改善表現。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses continuous support, not a single event.","zh":"這個短語強調持續支援，而不是單一事件。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"periods of work","meaning":"工作時段","examples":[{"en":"Training continues before, during and after periods of work.","zh":"培訓在工作時段之前、期間和之後繼續。"},{"en":"Periods of work are blocks of time when people are doing their duties.","zh":"periods of work 指人們履行職責的時間段。"},{"en":"A volunteer may have two periods of work each week at a community centre.","zh":"義工每星期可能在社區中心有兩個工作時段。"},{"en":"Planning around work periods helps trainers give support at the right time.","zh":"圍繞工作時段規劃，有助培訓者在合適時間提供支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes scheduled working times.","zh":"這個短語描述安排好的工作時間。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be run by","meaning":"由……負責","examples":[{"en":"Training is often run by experienced volunteers.","zh":"培訓通常由有經驗的義工負責。"},{"en":"Be run by someone means be organised, led, or managed by that person or group.","zh":"be run by someone 指由某人或某群體組織、帶領或管理。"},{"en":"A school club may be run by senior students with a teacher’s support.","zh":"學校學會可能由高年級學生在老師支援下負責。"},{"en":"Who runs an activity affects its style, quality, and organisation.","zh":"誰負責一項活動，會影響其風格、質素和組織。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the people responsible for managing something.","zh":"這個短語指出負責管理某事的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"experienced volunteers","meaning":"有經驗的義工","examples":[{"en":"Experienced volunteers often run the training.","zh":"有經驗的義工通常負責培訓。"},{"en":"Experienced volunteers are volunteers who have done the work before and understand what is needed.","zh":"experienced volunteers 指以前做過相關工作並明白需要甚麼的義工。"},{"en":"An experienced volunteer can show new helpers how to speak to elderly residents politely.","zh":"有經驗的義工可以示範新助手如何有禮地與長者交談。"},{"en":"Experience helps volunteers explain real problems that beginners may not expect.","zh":"經驗幫助義工解釋初學者可能意想不到的真實問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes volunteers with practical knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述有實務知識的義工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tend to prefer to","meaning":"通常較喜歡……","examples":[{"en":"Managers tend to prefer to get on with other things.","zh":"經理通常較喜歡繼續處理其他事情。"},{"en":"Tend to prefer to means usually like to do one thing more than another.","zh":"tend to prefer to 指通常較喜歡做某事多於另一事。"},{"en":"Some students tend to prefer to study in the morning rather than late at night.","zh":"有些學生通常較喜歡早上溫習，而不是深夜溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a general habit, not an absolute rule.","zh":"這個短語描述一般習慣，而不是絕對規則。"},{"en":"It is useful when speaking carefully about people’s usual choices.","zh":"謹慎描述人們通常的選擇時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get on with","meaning":"繼續處理……","examples":[{"en":"Managers prefer to get on with other things.","zh":"經理較喜歡繼續處理其他事情。"},{"en":"To get on with something means to continue doing it or start dealing with it without delay.","zh":"get on with something 指繼續做某事，或不拖延地開始處理它。"},{"en":"A student should get on with homework instead of checking messages again.","zh":"學生應該繼續做功課，而不是再次查看訊息。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they want to move past interruption and continue work.","zh":"當人們想越過打擾並繼續工作時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It suggests practical action and progress.","zh":"它暗示實際行動和進展。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"consider a couple of","meaning":"考慮幾個……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker asks applicants to consider a couple of important issues.","zh":"講者要求申請者考慮幾個重要問題。"},{"en":"To consider a couple of things means to think about two or a small number of things carefully.","zh":"consider a couple of things 指仔細思考兩個或少數幾個事項。"},{"en":"Before joining a club, students should consider a couple of questions about time and cost.","zh":"加入學會前，學生應考慮幾個關於時間和費用的問題。"},{"en":"Considering a few key issues can prevent regret later.","zh":"考慮幾個關鍵問題可以防止日後後悔。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a short list of things to think about.","zh":"這個短語引出一小串需要思考的事項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"important issues","meaning":"重要問題","examples":[{"en":"Applicants should consider a couple of important issues.","zh":"申請者應考慮幾個重要問題。"},{"en":"Important issues are matters that need serious attention because they affect the decision.","zh":"important issues 指因會影響決定而需要認真注意的事情。"},{"en":"When choosing a university, important issues include fees, location, and course quality.","zh":"選擇大學時，重要問題包括學費、地點和課程質素。"},{"en":"Ignoring important issues can lead to stress or poor choices later.","zh":"忽視重要問題會導致日後壓力或錯誤選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to key points that should not be overlooked.","zh":"這個短語指不應忽略的關鍵事項。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"decide to apply for","meaning":"決定申請……","examples":[{"en":"People should think carefully before they decide to apply for voluntary work.","zh":"人們在決定申請義務工作前應仔細思考。"},{"en":"Decide to apply for something means make up your mind to formally request a place, job, or role.","zh":"decide to apply for something 指下定決心正式申請名額、工作或角色。"},{"en":"A student may decide to apply for a scholarship after checking the requirements.","zh":"學生查看要求後，可能決定申請獎學金。"},{"en":"Deciding to apply should come after understanding the responsibilities involved.","zh":"決定申請前應先了解當中的責任。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the step before submitting an application.","zh":"這個短語標示提交申請前的一步。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"apply for voluntary work","meaning":"申請義務工作","examples":[{"en":"People can apply for voluntary work with ACE.","zh":"人們可以申請 ACE 的義務工作。"},{"en":"To apply for voluntary work means to formally ask to become a volunteer.","zh":"apply for voluntary work 指正式申請成為義工。"},{"en":"A student may apply for voluntary work at a library during the summer holiday.","zh":"學生可能在暑假申請到圖書館做義務工作。"},{"en":"Applications help organisations match people with suitable roles.","zh":"申請有助組織把人配對到合適角色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of becoming a volunteer.","zh":"這個短語描述成為義工的過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"worry about why","meaning":"擔心……的原因","examples":[{"en":"ACE does not worry about why people want to volunteer.","zh":"ACE 不擔心人們想做義工的原因。"},{"en":"Worry about why means be concerned about the reason behind someone’s action.","zh":"worry about why 指關心某人行動背後的原因。"},{"en":"A teacher may not worry about why students join a reading club as long as they read seriously.","zh":"只要學生認真閱讀，老師未必擔心他們加入閱讀學會的原因。"},{"en":"Sometimes the reason matters less than the person’s commitment and behaviour.","zh":"有時原因不及一個人的投入和行為重要。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on concern about motivation.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於對動機的憂慮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"many different reasons","meaning":"各種不同原因","examples":[{"en":"People have many different reasons for volunteering.","zh":"人們做義工有各種不同原因。"},{"en":"Many different reasons means there are several possible motivations, not just one.","zh":"many different reasons 指有幾種可能動機，而不只是單一原因。"},{"en":"Students may join a club for many different reasons, such as friendship, interest, or experience.","zh":"學生加入學會可能有各種不同原因，例如友誼、興趣或經驗。"},{"en":"Understanding different reasons helps organisers support people better.","zh":"理解不同原因有助組織者更好地支援人們。"},{"en":"This phrase shows variety in people’s motivations.","zh":"這個短語顯示人們動機的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"range from…to…","meaning":"從……到……不等","examples":[{"en":"Reasons for volunteering range from getting work experience to doing something enjoyable.","zh":"做義工的原因從獲取工作經驗到做一直想做的事不等。"},{"en":"Range from A to B means include many possibilities between two examples.","zh":"range from A to B 指包括兩個例子之間的許多可能性。"},{"en":"School activities range from sports to music and community service.","zh":"學校活動從運動到音樂和社區服務不等。"},{"en":"This structure shows that the list is broad rather than limited to one type.","zh":"這個結構顯示清單很廣，而不是限於一種類型。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing variety.","zh":"描述多樣性時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get work experience","meaning":"獲取工作經驗","examples":[{"en":"Some people volunteer to get work experience.","zh":"有些人做義工是為了獲取工作經驗。"},{"en":"To get work experience means to gain practical knowledge of working in a real setting.","zh":"get work experience 指在真實工作環境中取得實際工作知識。"},{"en":"A student may help in an office to get work experience before applying for jobs.","zh":"學生可能在辦公室幫忙，以便申請工作前獲取工作經驗。"},{"en":"Work experience can help people understand responsibilities, teamwork, and workplace behaviour.","zh":"工作經驗可以幫助人了解責任、團隊合作和職場行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing career preparation.","zh":"這個短語常見於事業準備討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"do something they have always wanted to do","meaning":"做一直想做的事","examples":[{"en":"Some people volunteer to do something they have always wanted to do.","zh":"有些人做義工是為了做一直想做的事。"},{"en":"To do something you have always wanted to do means finally take part in an activity you have long wished for.","zh":"do something you have always wanted to do 指終於參與自己長久以來希望做的活動。"},{"en":"A retired person may volunteer at a theatre to do something she has always wanted to do.","zh":"退休人士可能在劇院做義工，做一直想做的事。"},{"en":"Volunteering can give people a chance to explore old interests.","zh":"做義工可以給人機會探索舊有興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase connects volunteering with personal dreams.","zh":"這個短語把義工服務與個人夢想連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"it is critical that","meaning":"關鍵是……","examples":[{"en":"It is critical that volunteers have enough time for the role.","zh":"關鍵是義工有足夠時間擔任該角色。"},{"en":"It is critical that means it is extremely important that something happens or is true.","zh":"it is critical that 指某事發生或成立是極其重要的。"},{"en":"It is critical that students read the question carefully before answering.","zh":"關鍵是學生在作答前仔細閱讀題目。"},{"en":"If something is critical, ignoring it may cause serious problems.","zh":"如果某事是關鍵，忽視它可能造成嚴重問題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a key requirement.","zh":"這個短語引出關鍵要求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have enough hours in the day","meaning":"每天有足夠時間","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers must have enough hours in the day for their role.","zh":"義工每天必須有足夠時間擔任自己的角色。"},{"en":"Have enough hours in the day means have enough time available in daily life.","zh":"have enough hours in the day 指日常生活中有足夠可用時間。"},{"en":"A student with school, homework, and a part-time job may not have enough hours in the day for another club.","zh":"有上學、功課和兼職的學生，可能每天沒有足夠時間再參加另一個學會。"},{"en":"If people lack time, even meaningful work can become stressful.","zh":"如果人們缺乏時間，即使有意義的工作也會變得有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical time capacity.","zh":"這個短語描述實際時間容量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"whatever role","meaning":"任何角色；所負責的角色","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers need enough time for whatever role is suitable for them.","zh":"義工需要有足夠時間擔任任何適合自己的角色。"},{"en":"Whatever role means any role that is chosen or agreed later.","zh":"whatever role 指之後選定或同意的任何角色。"},{"en":"A school may train students for whatever role they receive on sports day.","zh":"學校可能為學生運動會當天分配到的任何角色提供訓練。"},{"en":"This phrase keeps the statement open because the exact role is not yet fixed.","zh":"這個短語令說法保持開放，因為確切角色尚未固定。"},{"en":"It is useful when several possible positions exist.","zh":"當有幾個可能職位時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"agree is suitable for","meaning":"同意……適合","examples":[{"en":"ACE and the volunteer agree which role is suitable for them.","zh":"ACE 和義工同意哪個角色適合該義工。"},{"en":"Agree is suitable for means both sides decide that something fits a person’s needs, skills, and situation.","zh":"agree is suitable for 指雙方都認為某事符合一個人的需要、技能和情況。"},{"en":"A teacher and student may agree that a reading club is suitable for a shy learner.","zh":"老師和學生可能同意閱讀學會適合害羞學習者。"},{"en":"Agreement matters because a role should work for both the organisation and the person.","zh":"達成共識很重要，因為角色應同時適合組織和個人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shared decision about fit.","zh":"這個短語描述關於合適程度的共同決定。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"suitable for","meaning":"適合……","examples":[{"en":"The role must be suitable for the volunteer.","zh":"該角色必須適合義工。"},{"en":"Suitable for someone means fitting that person’s ability, needs, age, time, or situation.","zh":"suitable for someone 指符合某人的能力、需要、年齡、時間或情況。"},{"en":"A quiet library role may be suitable for a volunteer who dislikes noisy crowds.","zh":"安靜的圖書館角色可能適合不喜歡嘈雜人群的義工。"},{"en":"If a role is unsuitable, the volunteer may feel stressed or perform poorly.","zh":"如果角色不合適，義工可能感到壓力或表現不佳。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a good match.","zh":"這個短語描述良好配對。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"become stressful","meaning":"變得有壓力","examples":[{"en":"If being a volunteer becomes stressful, it may not be suitable.","zh":"如果做義工變得有壓力，它可能並不合適。"},{"en":"Become stressful means start to cause pressure, worry, or emotional difficulty.","zh":"become stressful 指開始造成壓力、擔憂或情緒困難。"},{"en":"A school project can become stressful if the deadline is too close.","zh":"如果截止日期太近，學校項目可以變得有壓力。"},{"en":"When volunteering becomes stressful, the person may lose motivation or make mistakes.","zh":"當義工工作變得有壓力，人可能會失去動力或犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change from manageable to difficult.","zh":"這個短語描述由可處理變成困難的轉變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"best not to do it at all","meaning":"最好完全不要做","examples":[{"en":"If volunteering becomes stressful, it is best not to do it at all.","zh":"如果做義工變得有壓力，最好完全不要做。"},{"en":"Best not to do it at all means the wisest choice is to avoid doing it completely.","zh":"best not to do it at all 指最明智的選擇是完全避免做某事。"},{"en":"If a student is too ill, it is best not to join the race at all.","zh":"如果學生病得太重，最好完全不要參加比賽。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when doing something may cause more harm than benefit.","zh":"當做某事可能弊多於利時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It gives strong but practical advice.","zh":"它給出強烈但實際的建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"it is up to you to decide","meaning":"由你自己決定","examples":[{"en":"It is up to volunteers to decide if they can work without earning money.","zh":"義工是否能夠無薪工作，由他們自己決定。"},{"en":"It is up to you to decide means you are responsible for making the decision.","zh":"it is up to you to decide 指由你負責作出決定。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “It is up to you to decide whether to enter the competition.”","zh":"老師可能說：「是否參加比賽，由你自己決定。」"},{"en":"This phrase gives freedom but also responsibility.","zh":"這個短語給予自由，但也給予責任。"},{"en":"It is useful when the speaker cannot decide for another person.","zh":"當說話者不能替另一人決定時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"work without earning money","meaning":"無薪工作","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers need to decide whether they can work without earning money.","zh":"義工需要決定自己是否能夠無薪工作。"},{"en":"Work without earning money means spend time and effort on a role without receiving pay.","zh":"work without earning money 指花時間和努力做一個角色，但不收取薪酬。"},{"en":"A student may work without earning money at a charity event to gain experience.","zh":"學生可能在慈善活動中無薪工作，以獲取經驗。"},{"en":"Doing unpaid work requires enough time, motivation, and financial stability.","zh":"做無薪工作需要足夠時間、動機和財政穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the practical reality of volunteering.","zh":"這個短語描述義工服務的實際情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"what we value is","meaning":"我們重視的是……","examples":[{"en":"What ACE values is dedication.","zh":"ACE 重視的是投入。"},{"en":"What we value is introduces the quality or thing an organisation considers most important.","zh":"what we value is 用來引出某組織認為最重要的品質或事物。"},{"en":"A school may say, “What we value is effort, not only high marks.”","zh":"學校可能說：「我們重視的是努力，而不只是高分。」"},{"en":"This phrase helps make priorities clear.","zh":"這個短語有助清楚說明優先事項。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining standards or expectations.","zh":"解釋標準或期望時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dedication","meaning":"投入；奉獻","examples":[{"en":"ACE values dedication in its volunteers.","zh":"ACE 重視義工的投入。"},{"en":"Dedication means strong commitment, effort, and loyalty to a task or cause.","zh":"dedication 指對任務或目標有強烈承諾、努力和忠誠。"},{"en":"A dedicated student practises every day even when progress is slow.","zh":"投入的學生即使進步緩慢，也每天練習。"},{"en":"Dedication helps volunteers continue when the work is tiring or unpaid.","zh":"奉獻精神幫助義工在工作疲累或無薪時仍繼續。"},{"en":"This word describes serious and steady commitment.","zh":"這個字描述認真而穩定的承諾。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"loyal volunteers","meaning":"忠誠的義工","examples":[{"en":"Some of ACE’s most loyal volunteers earn very little.","zh":"ACE 一些最忠誠的義工本身收入很少。"},{"en":"Loyal volunteers are volunteers who keep helping an organisation steadily over time.","zh":"loyal volunteers 指長時間穩定地幫助某組織的義工。"},{"en":"A loyal volunteer may return every Saturday for years to help at a food bank.","zh":"忠誠的義工可能多年來每星期六都回到食物銀行幫忙。"},{"en":"Loyalty is valuable because organisations can depend on people who continue to support them.","zh":"忠誠很有價值，因為組織可以依靠持續支持它們的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-term commitment, not just one-time help.","zh":"這個短語描述長期承諾，而不是一次性幫忙。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"earn very little","meaning":"收入很少","examples":[{"en":"Some loyal volunteers earn very little themselves.","zh":"有些忠誠義工本身收入很少。"},{"en":"Earn very little means receive only a small amount of money from work.","zh":"earn very little 指從工作中只得到少量金錢。"},{"en":"A part-time worker may earn very little but still help at a community kitchen.","zh":"兼職員工可能收入很少，但仍在社區廚房幫忙。"},{"en":"People who earn very little may still give generously through time and effort.","zh":"收入很少的人仍可能透過時間和努力慷慨付出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low income.","zh":"這個短語描述低收入。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"give their full energy to","meaning":"全心投入……","examples":[{"en":"ACE’s loyal volunteers give their full energy to the work.","zh":"ACE 的忠誠義工全心投入工作。"},{"en":"To give your full energy to something means to put all your effort and attention into it.","zh":"give your full energy to something 指把全部努力和注意力投放在某事上。"},{"en":"A student gives her full energy to a debate competition when she prepares every evening.","zh":"學生每晚準備辯論比賽，就是全心投入比賽。"},{"en":"Giving full energy helps people do demanding work well.","zh":"全心投入有助人做好要求高的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows wholehearted effort.","zh":"這個短語顯示全心全意的努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the work they do","meaning":"他們所做的工作","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers give their full energy to the work they do with ACE.","zh":"義工全心投入他們在 ACE 所做的工作。"},{"en":"The work they do means the tasks, duties, or services they carry out.","zh":"the work they do 指他們執行的任務、職責或服務。"},{"en":"The work teachers do includes planning lessons, marking, and supporting students.","zh":"老師所做的工作包括備課、批改和支援學生。"},{"en":"Understanding the work people do helps others respect their contribution.","zh":"了解人們所做的工作，有助他人尊重他們的貢獻。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to real actions, not just titles.","zh":"這個短語指實際行動，而不只是職銜。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take a look at","meaning":"看一看……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker asks the audience to take a look at some work areas.","zh":"講者請聽眾看一看一些工作範疇。"},{"en":"To take a look at something means to examine or consider it briefly.","zh":"take a look at something 指簡略查看或考慮某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to take a look at the timetable before choosing activities.","zh":"老師可能請學生在選活動前看一看時間表。"},{"en":"Looking at options helps people decide what suits them.","zh":"查看選項有助人決定甚麼適合自己。"},{"en":"This phrase is friendly and less formal than “examine”.","zh":"這個短語友善，比 “examine” 較不正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"work areas","meaning":"工作範疇","examples":[{"en":"ACE needs volunteers for several work areas.","zh":"ACE 在幾個工作範疇都需要義工。"},{"en":"Work areas are different categories or sections of work within an organisation.","zh":"work areas 指組織內不同工作類別或部分。"},{"en":"A school event may have work areas such as ticketing, decoration, and first aid.","zh":"學校活動可能有售票、裝飾和急救等工作範疇。"},{"en":"Dividing work into areas helps volunteers choose suitable tasks.","zh":"把工作分成不同範疇，有助義工選擇合適任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised types of work.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的工作類型。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the sort of things that","meaning":"……那類事情","examples":[{"en":"The speaker explains the sort of things that would help in each work area.","zh":"講者解釋在每個工作範疇中會有幫助的那類事情。"},{"en":"The sort of things that means the kinds of skills, qualities, or actions that are useful.","zh":"the sort of things that 指有用的技能、品質或行動種類。"},{"en":"A coach may explain the sort of things that help players improve, such as practice and teamwork.","zh":"教練可能解釋幫助球員進步的那類事情，例如練習和團隊合作。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples without making a strict list.","zh":"這個短語引入例子，但不是給出嚴格清單。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing helpful qualities in a general way.","zh":"一般描述有用特質時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"help you in those","meaning":"在那些工作中幫到你","examples":[{"en":"Certain skills would help volunteers in those work areas.","zh":"某些技能會在那些工作範疇中幫到義工。"},{"en":"Help you in those means make it easier for you to succeed in those particular situations or roles.","zh":"help you in those 指令你在那些特定情況或角色中更容易成功。"},{"en":"Clear speaking skills can help you in roles that involve children.","zh":"清楚說話的能力可以在涉及兒童的角色中幫到你。"},{"en":"The right skill can make a difficult task safer, easier, or more effective.","zh":"合適技能可以令困難任務更安全、更容易或更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase connects skills with specific areas of work.","zh":"這個短語把技能與特定工作範疇連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"wish simply to","meaning":"只是想……","examples":[{"en":"Some people may wish simply to help raise money.","zh":"有些人可能只是想幫忙籌款。"},{"en":"Wish simply to means only want to do one particular thing, without a more complicated aim.","zh":"wish simply to 指只想做某一件事，沒有更複雜目的。"},{"en":"A visitor may wish simply to donate old books rather than join a committee.","zh":"訪客可能只是想捐舊書，而不是加入委員會。"},{"en":"This phrase makes someone’s intention sound modest and straightforward.","zh":"這個短語令某人的意圖聽起來謙遜而直接。"},{"en":"It is useful when people want a simple way to help.","zh":"當人們想以簡單方式幫忙時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"raise money","meaning":"籌款","examples":[{"en":"Some volunteers help ACE raise money.","zh":"有些義工幫助 ACE 籌款。"},{"en":"To raise money means to collect funds for a cause, organisation, or project.","zh":"raise money 指為某個目標、組織或項目籌集資金。"},{"en":"Students may raise money for a charity by selling homemade cakes.","zh":"學生可能透過售賣自製蛋糕為慈善機構籌款。"},{"en":"Money raised can pay for equipment, services, or support for people in need.","zh":"籌得的金錢可以支付設備、服務或對有需要人士的支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collecting financial support.","zh":"這個短語描述籌集財政支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have the creativity to","meaning":"有創意去……","examples":[{"en":"ACE welcomes people who have the creativity to design new fundraising ideas.","zh":"ACE 歡迎有創意去設計新籌款點子的人。"},{"en":"Have the creativity to do something means have the imagination and skill to think of new ideas.","zh":"have the creativity to do something 指有想像力和能力去想出新點子。"},{"en":"A student may have the creativity to turn old bottles into art decorations.","zh":"學生可能有創意把舊瓶子變成藝術裝飾。"},{"en":"Creative people can make ordinary tasks more interesting and effective.","zh":"有創意的人可以令普通任務更有趣和有效。"},{"en":"This phrase praises the ability to invent fresh solutions.","zh":"這個短語稱讚發明新解決方法的能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"come up with","meaning":"想出","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers may come up with a novel way of fundraising.","zh":"義工可能想出一種新穎的籌款方法。"},{"en":"To come up with something means to think of or create an idea, plan, or solution.","zh":"come up with something 指想出或創造一個點子、計劃或解決方法。"},{"en":"A student may come up with a new poster design for a school event.","zh":"學生可能為學校活動想出新的海報設計。"},{"en":"Good ideas often come up when people understand the problem clearly.","zh":"當人們清楚理解問題，好點子通常更容易出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述產生想法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"imaginative or novel way","meaning":"有想像力或新穎的方法","examples":[{"en":"ACE welcomes an imaginative or novel way of fundraising.","zh":"ACE 歡迎有想像力或新穎的籌款方法。"},{"en":"An imaginative or novel way is a creative or new method that is not ordinary.","zh":"imaginative or novel way 指有創意或新的方法，而不是普通做法。"},{"en":"A class may use an imaginative way to raise money, such as a sponsored silent reading hour.","zh":"班級可能使用有想像力的方式籌款，例如贊助式靜默閱讀一小時。"},{"en":"New methods can attract attention when old methods feel boring.","zh":"當舊方法令人覺得沉悶，新方法可以吸引注意。"},{"en":"This phrase praises originality and fresh thinking.","zh":"這個短語稱讚原創性和新思維。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fundraising","meaning":"籌款","examples":[{"en":"Standing with a collection box is a common form of fundraising.","zh":"拿着捐款箱站着是常見的籌款形式。"},{"en":"Fundraising is the activity of collecting money for a cause, group, or project.","zh":"fundraising 指為某個目標、團體或項目籌集金錢的活動。"},{"en":"A charity run is a popular fundraising event in many schools.","zh":"慈善跑是許多學校常見的籌款活動。"},{"en":"Fundraising helps organisations pay for services they could not otherwise provide.","zh":"籌款幫助組織支付原本未必能提供的服務。"},{"en":"This word describes organised money-raising work.","zh":"這個字描述有組織的籌款工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"we would be delighted","meaning":"我們會非常高興","examples":[{"en":"ACE would be delighted if volunteers had creative fundraising ideas.","zh":"如果義工有創意籌款點子，ACE 會非常高興。"},{"en":"We would be delighted means we would be very pleased or happy.","zh":"we would be delighted 指我們會非常愉快或高興。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “We would be delighted if parents joined the reading day.”","zh":"老師可能說：「如果家長參加閱讀日，我們會非常高興。」"},{"en":"This phrase sounds polite, positive, and encouraging.","zh":"這個短語聽起來有禮、正面和鼓勵。"},{"en":"It is often used when inviting help or welcoming an idea.","zh":"邀請幫忙或歡迎想法時，常會使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stand in local streets","meaning":"站在本地街道","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers may stand in local streets with a collection box.","zh":"義工可能拿着捐款箱站在本地街道。"},{"en":"To stand in local streets means to be physically present on nearby public roads or pavements.","zh":"stand in local streets 指親身站在附近公共道路或行人路上。"},{"en":"Charity workers may stand in local streets to speak to passers-by.","zh":"慈善工作者可能站在本地街道上與路人交談。"},{"en":"Street fundraising reaches people who may not visit the organisation directly.","zh":"街頭籌款能接觸到未必會直接到訪組織的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a public outdoor activity.","zh":"這個短語描述公開戶外活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"collection box","meaning":"捐款箱","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers sometimes use a collection box to raise money.","zh":"義工有時使用捐款箱籌款。"},{"en":"A collection box is a container used to collect donations from the public.","zh":"collection box 指用來收集公眾捐款的容器。"},{"en":"A charity may place a collection box beside a shop counter.","zh":"慈善機構可能把捐款箱放在商店櫃枱旁。"},{"en":"A visible collection box reminds people that even small coins can help.","zh":"明顯的捐款箱提醒人即使小硬幣也能幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase names a simple fundraising tool.","zh":"這個短語指出簡單的籌款工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rather boring","meaning":"頗沉悶","examples":[{"en":"Standing with a collection box can be rather boring.","zh":"拿着捐款箱站着可能頗沉悶。"},{"en":"Rather boring means quite dull or not very interesting.","zh":"rather boring 指相當乏味或不太有趣。"},{"en":"Waiting at a bus stop for an hour can be rather boring.","zh":"在巴士站等一小時可能頗沉悶。"},{"en":"If a task is boring, volunteers may need patience to continue.","zh":"如果任務沉悶，義工可能需要耐性才能繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds mild, not extremely negative.","zh":"這個短語語氣溫和，不是極度負面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"outdoor activity","meaning":"戶外活動","examples":[{"en":"Litter collection is one outdoor activity that needs volunteers.","zh":"清理垃圾是一項需要義工的戶外活動。"},{"en":"An outdoor activity is something done outside rather than inside a building.","zh":"outdoor activity 指在建築物外，而不是室內進行的活動。"},{"en":"Hiking, planting trees, and beach cleaning are outdoor activities.","zh":"遠足、植樹和清潔海灘都是戶外活動。"},{"en":"Outdoor activities may require suitable clothes, water, and good weather planning.","zh":"戶外活動可能需要合適衣物、水和天氣安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes activities in open air.","zh":"這個短語描述露天活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"litter collection","meaning":"清理垃圾","examples":[{"en":"ACE needs volunteers for litter collection.","zh":"ACE 需要義工參與清理垃圾。"},{"en":"Litter collection is the activity of picking up rubbish from public places.","zh":"litter collection 指在公共地方拾起垃圾的活動。"},{"en":"Students may join litter collection in a park after a school picnic.","zh":"學校野餐後，學生可能在公園參與清理垃圾。"},{"en":"Litter collection makes streets cleaner and protects animals from waste.","zh":"清理垃圾令街道更乾淨，並保護動物免受廢物傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical environmental work.","zh":"這個短語描述實際環保工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"it is useful if","meaning":"如果……會有用","examples":[{"en":"It is useful if litter-collection volunteers can walk for long periods.","zh":"如果清理垃圾的義工能長時間步行，會很有用。"},{"en":"It is useful if means something is helpful, though not always absolutely required.","zh":"it is useful if 指某事有幫助，雖然未必絕對必要。"},{"en":"It is useful if a class monitor can speak clearly during announcements.","zh":"如果班長能在宣布事項時清楚說話，會很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a helpful quality or skill.","zh":"這個短語引出有幫助的品質或技能。"},{"en":"It sounds less strict than saying “you must”.","zh":"它比說 “you must” 語氣較不嚴格。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"walk for long periods","meaning":"長時間步行","examples":[{"en":"Litter-collection volunteers need to walk for long periods.","zh":"清理垃圾的義工需要長時間步行。"},{"en":"To walk for long periods means to walk for a long time without much rest.","zh":"walk for long periods 指長時間走路，期間休息不多。"},{"en":"Tour guides often walk for long periods while leading visitors around a city.","zh":"導遊帶領遊客遊覽城市時，常需要長時間步行。"},{"en":"People who cannot walk long may need a different volunteer role.","zh":"不能長時間步行的人可能需要不同義工角色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical stamina.","zh":"這個短語描述體能耐力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"uphill","meaning":"上斜；上坡","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers may sometimes need to walk uphill.","zh":"義工有時可能需要上坡步行。"},{"en":"Uphill means moving up a slope or hill.","zh":"uphill 指向斜坡或山上移動。"},{"en":"Walking uphill to school can make students tired before lessons begin.","zh":"上坡走路返學會令學生上課前已感到疲倦。"},{"en":"Uphill walking requires more effort than walking on flat ground.","zh":"上坡步行比在平地步行需要更多力氣。"},{"en":"This word describes direction and physical difficulty.","zh":"這個字描述方向和身體難度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"regular collectors","meaning":"固定清理垃圾的義工","examples":[{"en":"Some regular collectors are elderly but active.","zh":"有些固定清理垃圾的義工年紀頗大但很活躍。"},{"en":"Regular collectors are people who collect litter or donations repeatedly, not just once.","zh":"regular collectors 指反覆清理垃圾或收集捐款的人，而不是只做一次。"},{"en":"A regular collector may help clean the same park every Sunday.","zh":"固定清理垃圾的義工可能每星期日幫忙清潔同一個公園。"},{"en":"Regular helpers give organisations steady support over time.","zh":"固定幫手能隨時間給組織穩定支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people who do a collecting task consistently.","zh":"這個短語描述持續做收集或清理任務的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"quite elderly","meaning":"年紀頗大","examples":[{"en":"Some of the regular collectors are quite elderly.","zh":"有些固定清理垃圾的義工年紀頗大。"},{"en":"Quite elderly means fairly old, usually old enough to be considered senior.","zh":"quite elderly 指相當年長，通常已屬長者。"},{"en":"A quite elderly volunteer may still be strong enough to help at community events.","zh":"年紀頗大的義工仍可能有足夠體力在社區活動中幫忙。"},{"en":"Age alone does not show whether someone can do active work.","zh":"年齡本身不能顯示某人是否能做活躍工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes age in a polite and mild way.","zh":"這個短語以禮貌和溫和方式描述年齡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"very active","meaning":"非常活躍","examples":[{"en":"The elderly collectors are very active.","zh":"年長清理垃圾義工非常活躍。"},{"en":"Very active means physically energetic and often involved in activities.","zh":"very active 指身體有活力，並經常參與活動。"},{"en":"A retired person may be very active if she swims, volunteers, and walks daily.","zh":"如果退休人士游泳、做義工並每天散步，她可能非常活躍。"},{"en":"Active people can often handle outdoor tasks better than expected.","zh":"活躍的人通常比預期更能應付戶外任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes energy and participation.","zh":"這個短語描述精力和參與度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"keen to protect","meaning":"熱心保護……","examples":[{"en":"The collectors are keen to protect the environment.","zh":"清理垃圾義工熱心保護環境。"},{"en":"Keen to protect means strongly interested in keeping something safe from harm.","zh":"keen to protect 指強烈希望保護某物免受傷害。"},{"en":"Students may be keen to protect animals after visiting a wildlife centre.","zh":"學生參觀野生動物中心後，可能熱心保護動物。"},{"en":"When people are keen to protect something, they are more willing to take action.","zh":"當人們熱心保護某事物，就更願意採取行動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong positive motivation.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈正面動機。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"protect the environment","meaning":"保護環境","examples":[{"en":"The regular collectors are keen to protect the environment.","zh":"固定清理垃圾的義工熱心保護環境。"},{"en":"To protect the environment means to help keep air, water, land, plants, and animals safe and healthy.","zh":"protect the environment 指幫助保持空氣、水、土地、植物和動物安全健康。"},{"en":"A family can protect the environment by recycling and reducing waste.","zh":"家庭可以透過回收和減少浪費來保護環境。"},{"en":"Protecting the environment prevents pollution and preserves places for future generations.","zh":"保護環境可以防止污染，並為下一代保存地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes care for the natural world.","zh":"這個短語描述對自然世界的照顧。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"enjoy working with children","meaning":"喜歡與小朋友相處","examples":[{"en":"People who enjoy working with children may become playmates.","zh":"喜歡與小朋友相處的人可以成為玩伴義工。"},{"en":"Enjoy working with children means like spending time with children and helping them learn or play.","zh":"enjoy working with children 指喜歡花時間陪伴小朋友，並幫助他們學習或玩耍。"},{"en":"A volunteer who enjoys working with children may help at a reading club.","zh":"喜歡與小朋友相處的義工可能在閱讀會幫忙。"},{"en":"Enjoyment matters because children often need patience, warmth, and clear guidance.","zh":"喜歡很重要，因為小朋友常需要耐性、溫暖和清晰指導。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a personal preference for child-focused work.","zh":"這個短語描述對兒童相關工作的個人偏好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"vacancies for","meaning":"……的空缺","examples":[{"en":"ACE has three vacancies for playmates.","zh":"ACE 有三個玩伴義工的空缺。"},{"en":"Vacancies for a role are open positions that need people to fill them.","zh":"vacancies for a role 指需要有人填補的空缺職位。"},{"en":"A school may have vacancies for library helpers after several students leave the team.","zh":"幾名學生離開團隊後，學校可能有圖書館助手空缺。"},{"en":"When there are vacancies, suitable people can apply or volunteer.","zh":"當有空缺，合適的人就可以申請或自願加入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes available roles.","zh":"這個短語描述可供申請的角色。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"what are called","meaning":"所謂的……","examples":[{"en":"ACE has vacancies for what are called “playmates”.","zh":"ACE 有所謂「玩伴義工」的空缺。"},{"en":"What are called is used to introduce the name or label people use for something.","zh":"what are called 用來引入人們給某事物使用的名稱或標籤。"},{"en":"A school may have helpers for what are called peer mentors.","zh":"學校可能有所謂朋輩導師的助手。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the term may be new to listeners.","zh":"當術語對聽者可能較陌生時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It signals that a special name is about to be explained.","zh":"它表示接下來會解釋一個特別名稱。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"playmates","meaning":"玩伴義工","examples":[{"en":"Playmates help children learn about staying healthy.","zh":"玩伴義工幫助小朋友學習保持健康。"},{"en":"Playmates are volunteers who spend time with children through play and activities.","zh":"playmates 指透過遊戲和活動陪伴小朋友的義工。"},{"en":"A playmate may lead games that teach children about food, exercise, or safety.","zh":"玩伴義工可能帶領遊戲，教小朋友認識食物、運動或安全。"},{"en":"Children often learn better when lessons feel like play.","zh":"當課堂感覺像遊戲，小朋友通常學得更好。"},{"en":"This word describes a friendly helper for children.","zh":"這個字描述兒童的友善助手。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"help children learn about","meaning":"幫助小朋友學習……","examples":[{"en":"Playmates help children learn about staying healthy.","zh":"玩伴義工幫助小朋友學習保持健康。"},{"en":"Help children learn about something means guide children so they understand a topic.","zh":"help children learn about something 指引導小朋友理解某個題目。"},{"en":"Parents can help children learn about money by giving them a small budget.","zh":"父母可以透過給孩子小預算，幫助小朋友學習金錢概念。"},{"en":"Children learn better when explanations are simple and connected to daily life.","zh":"當解釋簡單並連繫日常生活，小朋友學得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes educational support for young learners.","zh":"這個短語描述對年幼學習者的教育支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"staying healthy","meaning":"保持健康","examples":[{"en":"Children learn about staying healthy through activities.","zh":"小朋友透過活動學習保持健康。"},{"en":"Staying healthy means keeping the body and mind in good condition.","zh":"staying healthy 指保持身體和心理狀況良好。"},{"en":"Students stay healthy by eating well, sleeping enough, and exercising regularly.","zh":"學生透過飲食得宜、睡眠充足和定期運動來保持健康。"},{"en":"Learning about health early can help children build good habits.","zh":"及早學習健康知識可以幫助小朋友建立好習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes everyday choices that support wellbeing.","zh":"這個短語描述支持身心健康的日常選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"through a range of","meaning":"透過一系列……","examples":[{"en":"Children learn through a range of out-of-school activities.","zh":"小朋友透過一系列課外活動學習。"},{"en":"Through a range of means by using several different kinds of something.","zh":"through a range of 指透過幾種不同類型的某物。"},{"en":"Students can learn history through a range of activities, including visits, videos, and projects.","zh":"學生可以透過參觀、影片和項目等一系列活動學習歷史。"},{"en":"Using a range of methods helps different learners understand better.","zh":"使用多種方法有助不同學習者更好理解。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety in approach.","zh":"這個短語強調方法上的多樣性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"out-of-school activities","meaning":"課外活動","examples":[{"en":"Playmates help children through out-of-school activities.","zh":"玩伴義工透過課外活動幫助小朋友。"},{"en":"Out-of-school activities are activities that happen outside normal school lessons.","zh":"out-of-school activities 指在正常學校課堂以外發生的活動。"},{"en":"Sports clubs, museum visits, and weekend workshops are out-of-school activities.","zh":"運動學會、博物館參觀和週末工作坊都是課外活動。"},{"en":"These activities can teach children skills that ordinary lessons may not cover.","zh":"這些活動可以教導普通課堂未必涵蓋的技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning beyond the classroom.","zh":"這個短語描述課室以外的學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"don’t need to have children yourself","meaning":"自己不需要有小朋友","examples":[{"en":"Applicants do not need to have children themselves.","zh":"申請者自己不需要有小朋友。"},{"en":"Don’t need to have children yourself means being a parent is not required for the role.","zh":"don’t need to have children yourself 指擔任該角色並不要求你是父母。"},{"en":"A volunteer can work well with children even if she has no children of her own.","zh":"即使義工自己沒有孩子，也可以很好地與小朋友合作。"},{"en":"This phrase removes a possible worry for applicants.","zh":"這個短語消除申請者可能有的擔心。"},{"en":"It shows that interest, patience, and training may matter more than parenthood.","zh":"它顯示興趣、耐性和培訓可能比為人父母更重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"know something about","meaning":"對……有一些認識","examples":[{"en":"It is useful if playmates know something about nutrition.","zh":"如果玩伴義工對營養有一些認識，會很有用。"},{"en":"Know something about a subject means have some basic understanding of it.","zh":"know something about a subject 指對某題目有基本理解。"},{"en":"A sports volunteer should know something about first aid in case someone falls.","zh":"運動義工應對急救有一些認識，以防有人跌倒。"},{"en":"Basic knowledge helps volunteers answer simple questions and avoid mistakes.","zh":"基本知識幫助義工回答簡單問題並避免錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean expert knowledge.","zh":"這個短語不代表專家知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"nutrition","meaning":"營養","examples":[{"en":"Playmates should ideally know something about nutrition.","zh":"玩伴義工理想上應對營養有一些認識。"},{"en":"Nutrition is the study or practice of getting the right food for health and growth.","zh":"nutrition 指為健康和成長攝取合適食物的知識或做法。"},{"en":"Children learn nutrition when they understand why fruit, vegetables, and water matter.","zh":"當小朋友明白水果、蔬菜和水的重要性時，就是學習營養。"},{"en":"Good nutrition supports energy, concentration, and long-term health.","zh":"良好營養支持精力、專注力和長遠健康。"},{"en":"This word is closely connected with healthy eating.","zh":"這個字與健康飲食密切相關。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"give clear instructions","meaning":"給予清晰指示","examples":[{"en":"Playmates should be able to give clear instructions.","zh":"玩伴義工應能給予清晰指示。"},{"en":"To give clear instructions means to explain exactly what people should do in a way they can understand.","zh":"give clear instructions 指以別人能理解的方式，準確解釋應該做甚麼。"},{"en":"A teacher gives clear instructions when she says where to sit, what to write, and when to stop.","zh":"老師說明坐在哪裏、寫甚麼和何時停止，就是給予清晰指示。"},{"en":"Clear instructions reduce confusion and keep activities safe.","zh":"清晰指示可以減少混亂並保持活動安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when working with children or groups.","zh":"與小朋友或小組合作時，這個短語很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"appeal to","meaning":"吸引……","examples":[{"en":"If working with children does not appeal to someone, they may help at the story club.","zh":"如果與小朋友相處不吸引某人，他們可以在故事會幫忙。"},{"en":"Appeal to someone means attract or interest that person.","zh":"appeal to someone 指吸引某人或令某人感興趣。"},{"en":"A quiet library role may appeal to volunteers who enjoy reading.","zh":"安靜的圖書館角色可能吸引喜歡閱讀的義工。"},{"en":"If a role does not appeal to someone, they may do better in a different role.","zh":"如果某角色不吸引某人，他可能在另一個角色中做得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal attraction or interest.","zh":"這個短語描述個人吸引力或興趣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be interested in helping out","meaning":"有興趣幫忙","examples":[{"en":"Some volunteers may be interested in helping out at the story club.","zh":"有些義工可能有興趣在故事會幫忙。"},{"en":"Be interested in helping out means want to assist or take part in a helpful way.","zh":"be interested in helping out 指想以有幫助的方式協助或參與。"},{"en":"A student may be interested in helping out at a school open day.","zh":"學生可能有興趣在學校開放日幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase shows willingness before a definite commitment is made.","zh":"這個短語在作出確定承諾前顯示意願。"},{"en":"It is friendly and suitable for volunteer contexts.","zh":"它友善，適合義工語境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"story club","meaning":"故事會","examples":[{"en":"ACE runs a story club for disabled children.","zh":"ACE 為殘疾兒童營辦故事會。"},{"en":"A story club is a group where children listen to, read, discuss, or perform stories.","zh":"story club 指小朋友聆聽、閱讀、討論或表演故事的小組。"},{"en":"A school library may run a story club after lessons on Fridays.","zh":"學校圖書館可能在星期五放學後舉辦故事會。"},{"en":"Story clubs can help children build language, imagination, and confidence.","zh":"故事會可以幫助小朋友建立語言、想像力和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an activity group built around stories.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞故事而設的活動小組。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"disabled children","meaning":"殘疾兒童","examples":[{"en":"The story club is for disabled children.","zh":"故事會是為殘疾兒童而設的。"},{"en":"Disabled children are children who have physical, sensory, learning, or developmental difficulties that may require support.","zh":"disabled children 指有身體、感官、學習或發展困難，並可能需要支援的兒童。"},{"en":"A disabled child may need wheelchair access, clearer instructions, or extra time.","zh":"殘疾兒童可能需要輪椅通道、更清晰指示或額外時間。"},{"en":"Suitable activities can help disabled children participate more fully.","zh":"合適活動可以幫助殘疾兒童更充分參與。"},{"en":"This phrase should be used respectfully and with attention to support needs.","zh":"這個短語應以尊重方式使用，並留意支援需要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"especially if","meaning":"尤其是如果……","examples":[{"en":"The story club may suit volunteers, especially if they have done some acting.","zh":"故事會可能適合義工，尤其是如果他們有表演經驗。"},{"en":"Especially if means particularly in the case where a certain condition is true.","zh":"especially if 指特別是在某條件成立的情況下。"},{"en":"A drama club may appeal to students, especially if they enjoy performing.","zh":"戲劇學會可能吸引學生，尤其是如果他們喜歡表演。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a condition that makes something more suitable.","zh":"這個短語突出令某事更合適的條件。"},{"en":"It helps explain when advice applies most strongly.","zh":"它幫助解釋建議在甚麼情況下最適用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have done some acting","meaning":"有表演經驗","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers with acting experience may help at the story club.","zh":"有表演經驗的義工可以在故事會幫忙。"},{"en":"Have done some acting means have performed in plays, drama activities, videos, or similar performances before.","zh":"have done some acting 指以前曾參與戲劇、劇場活動、影片或類似表演。"},{"en":"A student who joined school plays has done some acting.","zh":"曾參加校劇的學生就是有一些表演經驗。"},{"en":"Acting experience can help volunteers read stories with expression and confidence.","zh":"表演經驗可以幫助義工有表情和信心地朗讀故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes previous performance experience.","zh":"這個短語描述過往表演經驗。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"put on performances","meaning":"演出","examples":[{"en":"The story club puts on three performances a year.","zh":"故事會每年演出三場。"},{"en":"To put on performances means to organise and present shows for an audience.","zh":"put on performances 指組織並向觀眾呈現表演。"},{"en":"A school drama club may put on performances at Christmas and graduation.","zh":"學校戲劇學會可能在聖誕節和畢業禮演出。"},{"en":"Performances require planning, practice, costumes, and people to help backstage.","zh":"演出需要規劃、練習、服裝和後台幫手。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing a public show.","zh":"這個短語描述製作公開表演。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"three performances a year","meaning":"每年三場演出","examples":[{"en":"The story club puts on three performances a year.","zh":"故事會每年演出三場。"},{"en":"Three performances a year means three shows are presented every year.","zh":"three performances a year 指每年呈現三場表演。"},{"en":"A choir may give three performances a year: one in spring, one in summer, and one at Christmas.","zh":"合唱團每年可能有三場演出：春季一場、夏季一場和聖誕一場。"},{"en":"Knowing the number of performances helps volunteers judge the time commitment.","zh":"知道演出場數有助義工判斷時間承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the annual frequency of events.","zh":"這個短語給出活動每年的頻率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"based on","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"The performances are based on books the children have read.","zh":"演出根據孩子讀過的書改編。"},{"en":"Based on means developed from or using something as the source.","zh":"based on 指由某物發展而來，或以某物作來源。"},{"en":"A film may be based on a famous novel.","zh":"電影可能根據一本著名小說改編。"},{"en":"When a performance is based on a book, the story, characters, or ideas come from that book.","zh":"當演出根據一本書而成，故事、角色或想法來自那本書。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the source material behind a new work.","zh":"這個短語顯示新作品背後的來源材料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be always looking for","meaning":"一直尋找……","examples":[{"en":"ACE is always looking for support with the theatrical side of the story club.","zh":"ACE 一直尋找故事會戲劇方面的支援。"},{"en":"Be always looking for means continually need or try to find something.","zh":"be always looking for 指持續需要或嘗試尋找某物。"},{"en":"A school is always looking for parents to help with reading activities.","zh":"學校一直尋找家長幫忙閱讀活動。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an ongoing need, not a one-time request.","zh":"這個短語暗示持續需要，而不是一次性請求。"},{"en":"It is useful when an organisation regularly needs help.","zh":"當組織定期需要幫忙時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"support with","meaning":"在……方面的支援","examples":[{"en":"ACE needs support with the theatrical side of the performances.","zh":"ACE 需要在演出戲劇方面的支援。"},{"en":"Support with something means help in a particular area or task.","zh":"support with something 指在某個特定範疇或任務上提供幫助。"},{"en":"A student may need support with maths homework before an exam.","zh":"學生考試前可能需要數學功課方面的支援。"},{"en":"Asking for support with a specific area makes the need clearer.","zh":"要求特定範疇的支援，會令需要更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses help on one part of a larger activity.","zh":"這個短語把幫助集中在較大活動中的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"theatrical side","meaning":"戲劇方面","examples":[{"en":"The story club needs help with the theatrical side of its work.","zh":"故事會需要在其工作中的戲劇方面得到幫助。"},{"en":"The theatrical side means the performance-related part, such as acting, staging, costumes, voice, and movement.","zh":"theatrical side 指與表演有關的部分，例如演技、舞台安排、服裝、聲線和動作。"},{"en":"A school play needs help with the theatrical side as well as ticket sales.","zh":"學校話劇除了售票，也需要戲劇方面的幫助。"},{"en":"Strong theatrical support can make a story more exciting for children.","zh":"強大的戲劇支援可以令故事對小朋友更精彩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the drama and performance aspect of an activity.","zh":"這個短語描述活動中的戲劇和表演面向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the last area I’ll mention","meaning":"我會提到的最後一個範疇","examples":[{"en":"The last area the speaker mentions is first aid.","zh":"講者提到的最後一個範疇是急救。"},{"en":"The last area I’ll mention means the final topic or category I will talk about.","zh":"the last area I’ll mention 指我會談及的最後一個題目或類別。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “The last area I’ll mention is exam timing.”","zh":"老師可能說：「我會提到的最後一個範疇是考試時間安排。」"},{"en":"This phrase helps listeners know the talk is moving toward its end.","zh":"這個短語幫助聽眾知道講話正走向結尾。"},{"en":"It is useful for organising a speech clearly.","zh":"它有助清楚組織演講。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"first aid","meaning":"急救","examples":[{"en":"ACE needs volunteers for first aid work.","zh":"ACE 需要急救工作的義工。"},{"en":"First aid is basic help given to an injured or ill person before professional medical care arrives.","zh":"first aid 指在專業醫療到達前，給受傷或不適人士的基本協助。"},{"en":"A first-aid volunteer may clean a small cut or help someone who feels faint.","zh":"急救義工可能清潔小傷口，或幫助感到暈眩的人。"},{"en":"First aid can reduce harm and keep a person safe while waiting for further help.","zh":"急救可以減少傷害，並在等待進一步協助時保持病人安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes immediate practical health support.","zh":"這個短語描述即時而實際的健康支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"join this group","meaning":"加入這個小組","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers who join this group may teach others.","zh":"加入這個小組的義工可能會教導他人。"},{"en":"Join this group means become a member of this particular team or activity area.","zh":"join this group 指成為這個特定團隊或活動範疇的成員。"},{"en":"A student who likes gardening may join the school garden group.","zh":"喜歡園藝的學生可能加入學校園藝小組。"},{"en":"Joining a group gives people shared duties and training.","zh":"加入小組會讓人有共同職責和培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to becoming part of a specific group.","zh":"這個短語指成為某特定小組的一部分。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"end up teaching","meaning":"最終會教導","examples":[{"en":"First-aid volunteers can end up teaching others.","zh":"急救義工最終可能會教導他人。"},{"en":"End up teaching means eventually teach, even if that was not the first thing expected.","zh":"end up teaching 指最終會教導，即使一開始未必預期如此。"},{"en":"A student who joins a computer club may end up teaching younger students basic coding.","zh":"加入電腦學會的學生，可能最終會教導較年輕學生基本編程。"},{"en":"People can end up teaching when they gain enough knowledge and confidence.","zh":"當人們取得足夠知識和信心，就可能最終會教導別人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unexpected or later result.","zh":"這個短語描述意想不到或較後出現的結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"vulnerable groups","meaning":"弱勢群體","examples":[{"en":"First-aid volunteers may teach people in vulnerable groups.","zh":"急救義工可能教導弱勢群體中的人士。"},{"en":"Vulnerable groups are people who may need extra protection because they face higher risk or difficulty.","zh":"vulnerable groups 指因面對較高風險或困難而可能需要額外保護的人。"},{"en":"Elderly people, disabled children, and people with serious illnesses can be vulnerable groups.","zh":"長者、殘疾兒童和患嚴重疾病的人都可以是弱勢群體。"},{"en":"Support for vulnerable groups helps reduce harm and inequality.","zh":"支援弱勢群體有助減少傷害和不平等。"},{"en":"This phrase is used respectfully in social care and public health.","zh":"這個短語在社會照顧和公共健康中以尊重方式使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be at risk of injury","meaning":"有受傷風險","examples":[{"en":"Vulnerable groups may be at risk of injury.","zh":"弱勢群體可能有受傷風險。"},{"en":"Be at risk of injury means be more likely to get hurt.","zh":"be at risk of injury 指較有可能受傷。"},{"en":"Children running near a wet floor are at risk of injury.","zh":"在濕地板附近跑動的小朋友有受傷風險。"},{"en":"People at risk of injury may need safer surroundings and clear guidance.","zh":"有受傷風險的人可能需要更安全環境和清晰指導。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a danger that has not necessarily happened yet.","zh":"這個短語描述尚未必發生的危險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"initially","meaning":"起初","examples":[{"en":"Initially, first-aid volunteers need to absorb a lot of information.","zh":"起初，急救義工需要吸收大量資料。"},{"en":"Initially means at the beginning or in the first stage.","zh":"initially 指在開始時或第一階段。"},{"en":"Initially, a new student may feel nervous in a large class.","zh":"起初，新學生在大班中可能感到緊張。"},{"en":"This word helps separate the early stage from what happens later.","zh":"這個字幫助區分早期階段和之後發生的事。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining a process over time.","zh":"解釋隨時間發展的過程時，它很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"your priority will be to","meaning":"你的首要任務是……","examples":[{"en":"Your priority will be to take in a lot of information.","zh":"你的首要任務是吸收大量資料。"},{"en":"Your priority will be to means the most important thing for you to do will be something.","zh":"your priority will be to 指你最重要要做的事情會是某事。"},{"en":"On the first day of a new job, your priority may be to learn safety rules.","zh":"新工作第一天，你的首要任務可能是學習安全規則。"},{"en":"Setting a priority helps people focus on what matters most.","zh":"設定首要任務有助人專注於最重要的事。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the main task.","zh":"這個短語引出主要任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take in a lot of information","meaning":"吸收大量資料","examples":[{"en":"First-aid volunteers need to take in a lot of information.","zh":"急救義工需要吸收大量資料。"},{"en":"To take in a lot of information means to understand, remember, and process many details.","zh":"take in a lot of information 指理解、記住並處理許多細節。"},{"en":"Students must take in a lot of information before a final exam.","zh":"學生在期末考試前必須吸收大量資料。"},{"en":"When there is too much information, people may need notes, practice, and review.","zh":"當資料太多，人們可能需要筆記、練習和重溫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental effort in learning.","zh":"這個短語描述學習中的心智能力付出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"important steps or details","meaning":"重要步驟或細節","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers must not forget any important steps or details.","zh":"義工不可忘記任何重要步驟或細節。"},{"en":"Important steps or details are actions or pieces of information that must be remembered for the task to be done correctly.","zh":"important steps or details 指為了正確完成任務而必須記住的行動或資料。"},{"en":"In first aid, important steps may include checking breathing and calling for help.","zh":"在急救中，重要步驟可能包括檢查呼吸和求助。"},{"en":"Forgetting a key detail can make a task unsafe or ineffective.","zh":"忘記關鍵細節可能令任務不安全或無效。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses careful attention to procedure.","zh":"這個短語強調對流程的仔細注意。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"does anyone have any questions","meaning":"有沒有人有問題","examples":[{"en":"The speaker ends by asking whether anyone has any questions.","zh":"講者最後詢問有沒有人有問題。"},{"en":"“Does anyone have any questions?” invites listeners to ask about anything unclear.","zh":"“Does anyone have any questions?” 邀請聽眾詢問任何不清楚的地方。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask this after explaining a homework task.","zh":"老師解釋功課後，可能問這句。"},{"en":"This question gives people a chance to check details before leaving.","zh":"這個問題給人機會在離開前確認細節。"},{"en":"It is a common closing line in talks, lessons, and meetings.","zh":"它是講座、課堂和會議中常見的結尾語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 2.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/listening/Practice 9/task-3":[{"front":"what did you think of","meaning":"你覺得……怎樣","examples":[{"en":"Hugo asks Chantal what she thought of the talk.","zh":"Hugo問Chantal覺得那場講座怎樣。"},{"en":"What did you think of something means asking someone for their opinion about it.","zh":"what did you think of某事，意思是詢問某人對它的看法。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask, “What did you think of the film?” after a class screening.","zh":"老師可能在班級觀影後問：「你覺得那部電影怎樣？」"},{"en":"This question invites evaluation, not just a yes-or-no answer.","zh":"這個問題邀請人作出評價，而不只是回答是或不是。"},{"en":"People often use this phrase after a talk, lesson, performance or event.","zh":"人們常在講座、課堂、表演或活動後使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"once I had moved seats","meaning":"在我換了座位之後","examples":[{"en":"Chantal thought the talk was good once she had moved seats.","zh":"Chantal在換了座位之後覺得講座很好。"},{"en":"Once I had moved seats means after I changed to a different seat.","zh":"once I had moved seats意思是在我換到另一個座位之後。"},{"en":"A student could see the board clearly once she had moved seats to the front row.","zh":"學生換到前排座位之後，就能清楚看見黑板。"},{"en":"Changing seats can solve a problem if someone is blocking the view or making noise.","zh":"如果有人擋住視線或發出噪音，換座位可以解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one action happened before the situation improved.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個行動發生後，情況才有所改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"chatting or something","meaning":"聊天之類的","examples":[{"en":"Hugo asks whether the people beside Chantal were chatting or something.","zh":"Hugo問Chantal旁邊的人是否在聊天之類的。"},{"en":"Chatting or something means talking casually or doing some similar distracting thing.","zh":"chatting or something意思是閒聊或做類似令人分心的事情。"},{"en":"During a film, people behind you may be chatting or something and make it hard to concentrate.","zh":"看電影時，後面的人可能在聊天之類的，令你難以集中。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds informal because the speaker is guessing, not giving a definite reason.","zh":"這個短語較口語，因為說話者是在猜測，而不是給出確定原因。"},{"en":"It is often used when someone is unsure exactly what happened.","zh":"當某人不確定到底發生甚麼時，常會使用它。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it was not that","meaning":"不是那樣","examples":[{"en":"Chantal says it was not that when Hugo asks about people chatting.","zh":"當Hugo問是否有人聊天時，Chantal說不是那樣。"},{"en":"It was not that means that was not the real reason or problem.","zh":"it was not that意思是那並不是真正原因或問題。"},{"en":"If a student leaves class early, it may not be that they are bored; they may feel sick.","zh":"如果學生早退，不一定是因為覺得無聊；他可能身體不適。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects another person’s guess.","zh":"這個短語用來糾正別人的猜測。"},{"en":"It helps the speaker explain the true cause after rejecting the first idea.","zh":"它幫助說話者否定第一個想法後，解釋真正原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"so that","meaning":"以便","examples":[{"en":"Chantal went early so that she would get a seat.","zh":"Chantal早到，以便找到座位。"},{"en":"So that means in order that, and it introduces the purpose of an action.","zh":"so that意思是為了、以便，用來引入行動的目的。"},{"en":"Students arrived early so that they could sit near the front.","zh":"學生早到，以便可以坐近前排。"},{"en":"People often plan ahead so that they can avoid problems later.","zh":"人們常提前計劃，以便日後避免問題。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an action with the result someone wants.","zh":"這個短語把行動與某人想要的結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get a seat","meaning":"找到座位","examples":[{"en":"Chantal went early to get a seat.","zh":"Chantal早到以找到座位。"},{"en":"To get a seat means to find or obtain a place to sit.","zh":"get a seat意思是找到或取得一個可坐的位置。"},{"en":"People line up early for a popular lecture to get a seat near the stage.","zh":"人們為熱門講座提早排隊，以便找到靠近舞台的座位。"},{"en":"If you do not get a seat on a crowded bus, you may have to stand.","zh":"如果你在擁擠巴士上找不到座位，就可能要站着。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when seating is limited or important.","zh":"當座位有限或座位很重要時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"not have to stand","meaning":"不用站着","examples":[{"en":"Chantal wanted to get a seat and not have to stand.","zh":"Chantal想找到座位，不用站着。"},{"en":"Not have to stand means not being required to remain on your feet.","zh":"not have to stand意思是不需要一直站立。"},{"en":"Elderly passengers are grateful when they get a seat and do not have to stand.","zh":"長者乘客找到座位不用站着時，通常會很感激。"},{"en":"Standing for a long talk can make people tired and less able to listen.","zh":"長時間站着聽講座可以令人疲倦，並較難聆聽。"},{"en":"This phrase shows relief from an uncomfortable situation.","zh":"這個短語顯示擺脫不舒服情況的放鬆感。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"right in front of","meaning":"就在……正前方","examples":[{"en":"A very tall man sat right in front of Chantal.","zh":"一名很高的男子坐在Chantal正前方。"},{"en":"Right in front of someone means directly before them, with almost no space or obstruction between.","zh":"right in front of某人，意思是就在某人正前面，幾乎沒有距離或遮隔。"},{"en":"A student cannot see the screen if a poster is placed right in front of her desk.","zh":"如果海報放在學生桌子正前方，她就看不到屏幕。"},{"en":"Something right in front of you can block your view or demand your attention.","zh":"就在你正前方的東西可以擋住視線或吸引你的注意。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses exact position.","zh":"這個短語強調確切位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hard to see through","meaning":"很難透過……看","examples":[{"en":"It is hard to see through people’s heads.","zh":"很難透過別人的頭看東西。"},{"en":"Hard to see through something means difficult to look past or look through it clearly.","zh":"hard to see through某物，意思是很難清楚透過或越過它看見。"},{"en":"It is hard to see through a dirty classroom window after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，很難透過骯髒的課室窗戶看出去。"},{"en":"If something blocks your view, it becomes hard to see through or around it.","zh":"如果某物擋住視線，就很難透過或繞過它看見。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a person may need to move seats.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某人可能需要換座位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"to answer your question","meaning":"回答你的問題","examples":[{"en":"Chantal says, “To answer your question, I thought it was really interesting.”","zh":"Chantal說：「回答你的問題，我覺得它真的很有趣。」"},{"en":"To answer your question means I am now responding directly to what you asked.","zh":"to answer your question意思是我現在直接回應你剛才問的問題。"},{"en":"To answer your question, the meeting will start at nine, not half past nine.","zh":"回答你的問題，會議九點開始，不是九點半。"},{"en":"This phrase helps a speaker return to the original question after some explanation.","zh":"這個短語幫助說話者在解釋後回到原本問題。"},{"en":"It sounds organised and polite in conversation.","zh":"它在對話中聽起來有條理而有禮。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"really interesting","meaning":"非常有趣","examples":[{"en":"Chantal thought the talk was really interesting.","zh":"Chantal覺得那場講座非常有趣。"},{"en":"Really interesting means very engaging, informative or worth listening to.","zh":"really interesting意思是非常吸引人、有資訊量或值得聆聽。"},{"en":"A lesson becomes really interesting when the teacher uses real examples and stories.","zh":"當老師使用真實例子和故事，課堂會變得非常有趣。"},{"en":"If a talk is really interesting, listeners may keep thinking about it afterwards.","zh":"如果講座非常有趣，聽眾之後可能會一直思考它。"},{"en":"This phrase gives strong positive feedback.","zh":"這個短語給出強烈正面評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"especially what","meaning":"尤其是……","examples":[{"en":"Chantal was especially interested in what the speaker said about the job market.","zh":"Chantal尤其對講者談到就業市場的內容感興趣。"},{"en":"Especially what means particularly the part or information that follows.","zh":"especially what意思是尤其是後面提到的部分或資訊。"},{"en":"I liked the workshop, especially what the trainer said about interview confidence.","zh":"我喜歡那個工作坊，尤其是導師談到面試信心的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows attention to the most interesting or important part.","zh":"這個短語把注意力收窄到最有趣或最重要的部分。"},{"en":"It is useful when one detail stands out from a larger event.","zh":"當某個細節在較大事件中特別突出時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the speaker said about","meaning":"講者談到……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker said something important about the job market.","zh":"講者談到就業市場時說了一些重要內容。"},{"en":"The speaker said about something means the speaker gave information or opinions on that topic.","zh":"the speaker said about某事，意思是講者就該主題提供資料或意見。"},{"en":"Students wrote notes on what the speaker said about choosing university courses.","zh":"學生記下講者談到選擇大學課程的內容。"},{"en":"What a speaker says about a topic can influence how listeners think about it.","zh":"講者就某主題所說的話，可以影響聽眾如何思考它。"},{"en":"This phrase links a person’s comments with a subject.","zh":"這個短語把某人的評論與一個主題連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"job market","meaning":"就業市場","examples":[{"en":"The speaker talked about the job market in the fashion industry.","zh":"講者談到時裝業的就業市場。"},{"en":"The job market is the situation in which people look for jobs and employers look for workers.","zh":"job market是人們求職和僱主招聘員工的情況。"},{"en":"Graduates study the job market to see which skills companies want.","zh":"畢業生研究就業市場，以了解公司想要哪些技能。"},{"en":"A weak job market can make it harder for young people to find work.","zh":"疲弱的就業市場會令年輕人更難找到工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing careers and employment.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論事業和就業。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go into","meaning":"進入","examples":[{"en":"The students know they are going into a competitive field.","zh":"學生知道自己將進入一個競爭激烈的領域。"},{"en":"To go into a field means to enter a particular career, subject or industry.","zh":"go into某領域，意思是進入某個職業、學科或行業。"},{"en":"A student who loves animals may decide to go into veterinary nursing.","zh":"喜歡動物的學生可能決定進入獸醫護理行業。"},{"en":"People should learn about a field before they go into it.","zh":"人們在進入某領域前應先了解它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing a future direction.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇未來方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"competitive field","meaning":"競爭激烈的領域","examples":[{"en":"Fashion is a very competitive field.","zh":"時裝是一個競爭非常激烈的領域。"},{"en":"A competitive field is an area of work where many people compete for limited opportunities.","zh":"competitive field是很多人爭奪有限機會的工作範疇。"},{"en":"Acting is a competitive field because many talented people want the same few roles.","zh":"演藝是競爭激烈的領域，因為許多有才華的人想得到同樣少數角色。"},{"en":"In a competitive field, experience and contacts can matter as much as qualifications.","zh":"在競爭激烈的領域中，經驗和人脈可能與資歷同樣重要。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that success may require persistence.","zh":"這個短語提醒人成功可能需要堅持。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"it is obvious that","meaning":"很明顯","examples":[{"en":"It is obvious that the students may struggle to get work.","zh":"很明顯，學生可能很難找到工作。"},{"en":"It is obvious that means it is easy to see or understand that something is true.","zh":"it is obvious that意思是某事很容易看出或理解為真。"},{"en":"It is obvious that a tired student will find a three-hour exam harder.","zh":"很明顯，疲倦學生會覺得三小時考試更困難。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when the evidence seems clear.","zh":"當證據看來清楚時，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It can sound direct, so it should be used carefully in polite discussion.","zh":"它可能聽起來直接，所以在有禮討論中應小心使用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"struggle to get work","meaning":"很難找到工作","examples":[{"en":"Fashion students may struggle to get work after graduation.","zh":"時裝學生畢業後可能很難找到工作。"},{"en":"To struggle to get work means to find it difficult to find a job.","zh":"struggle to get work意思是很難找到工作。"},{"en":"New graduates may struggle to get work if they have no experience or portfolio.","zh":"如果新畢業生沒有經驗或作品集，可能很難找到工作。"},{"en":"A difficult job market can make even capable people struggle to get work.","zh":"困難的就業市場可以令有能力的人也難以找到工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a hard job-search situation.","zh":"這個短語描述艱難的求職情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"dream job","meaning":"夢想工作","examples":[{"en":"Not every student can have a dream job in the industry.","zh":"不是每個學生都能在行業中擁有夢想工作。"},{"en":"A dream job is the job someone most wants because it matches their interests and hopes.","zh":"dream job是某人最想要、因為符合興趣和期望的工作。"},{"en":"For one student, a dream job might be designing clothes for stage performers.","zh":"對某學生來說，夢想工作可能是為舞台表演者設計服裝。"},{"en":"Dream jobs are attractive, but they may require years of preparation and rejection.","zh":"夢想工作很吸引，但可能需要多年準備和面對拒絕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an ideal career, not just any job.","zh":"這個短語描述理想職業，而不只是任何工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a whole range of","meaning":"一整個範圍的……","examples":[{"en":"There is a whole range of areas of work in the fashion industry.","zh":"時裝業有一整個範圍的工作範疇。"},{"en":"A whole range of something means many different kinds or options.","zh":"a whole range of某物，意思是很多不同種類或選項。"},{"en":"A university fair may introduce a whole range of courses, from nursing to engineering.","zh":"大學展覽可能介紹一整個範圍的課程，由護理到工程都有。"},{"en":"Seeing a whole range of options can help students avoid choosing too quickly.","zh":"看見一整個範圍的選項，可以幫助學生避免太快作選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety and breadth.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣性和廣泛範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"areas of work","meaning":"工作範疇","examples":[{"en":"The talk introduced different areas of work in fashion.","zh":"講座介紹了時裝中的不同工作範疇。"},{"en":"Areas of work are different job types or professional sections within an industry.","zh":"areas of work是一個行業中的不同工作類型或專業部分。"},{"en":"In healthcare, areas of work include nursing, pharmacy, administration and therapy.","zh":"在醫療行業中，工作範疇包括護理、藥劑、行政和治療。"},{"en":"Learning about different areas of work helps students match jobs with their skills.","zh":"了解不同工作範疇幫助學生把工作與自身技能配對。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an industry contains many career paths.","zh":"當一個行業包含多種職業路徑時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"had not even thought of","meaning":"甚至沒有想過","examples":[{"en":"The students had not even thought of areas like fashion journalism.","zh":"學生甚至沒有想過時尚新聞等範疇。"},{"en":"Had not even thought of means had never considered it at all.","zh":"had not even thought of意思是完全沒有考慮過。"},{"en":"A student may not have even thought of working in publishing until a teacher mentions it.","zh":"學生可能直到老師提起，才發現自己甚至沒有想過出版工作。"},{"en":"Career talks can reveal options students have not even thought of before.","zh":"職業講座可以揭示學生之前甚至沒有想過的選項。"},{"en":"This phrase shows surprise at a new possibility.","zh":"這個短語顯示對新可能性的驚訝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fashion journalism","meaning":"時尚新聞","examples":[{"en":"Fashion journalism is one possible career option.","zh":"時尚新聞是一個可能的職業選擇。"},{"en":"Fashion journalism is writing, reporting or commenting on fashion for magazines, websites or media.","zh":"fashion journalism是為雜誌、網站或媒體撰寫、報道或評論時裝。"},{"en":"A fashion journalist may review a designer’s new collection after a show.","zh":"時尚新聞工作者可能在時裝秀後評論設計師的新系列。"},{"en":"This field requires writing skill, industry knowledge and a sense of style.","zh":"這個領域需要寫作能力、行業知識和風格觸覺。"},{"en":"This phrase names a media-related job area within fashion.","zh":"這個短語命名時裝業中與媒體相關的工作範疇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"Hugo mentions fashion journalism, for instance.","zh":"Hugo提到時尚新聞，例如。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance意思是例如。"},{"en":"Students can build experience through small projects, for instance by writing for a school magazine.","zh":"學生可以透過小型項目累積經驗，例如為校刊撰文。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain a general point with a specific case.","zh":"這個短語幫助用具體個案解釋一般重點。"},{"en":"It is common in speech, essays and discussions.","zh":"它常見於說話、文章和討論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"expect so many","meaning":"預料到這麼多……","examples":[{"en":"Chantal was not expecting so many career options.","zh":"Chantal沒有預料到有這麼多職業選擇。"},{"en":"To expect so many means to think there would be such a large number.","zh":"expect so many意思是預計會有這麼大的數量。"},{"en":"A visitor may not expect so many students to attend a lunchtime careers talk.","zh":"訪客可能沒有預料到這麼多學生參加午餐時間的職業講座。"},{"en":"When people discover more options than expected, they may rethink their plans.","zh":"當人們發現選項比預期更多，就可能重新思考計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase shows surprise about quantity.","zh":"這個短語顯示對數量感到驚訝。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"career options","meaning":"職業選擇","examples":[{"en":"The talk introduced many career options.","zh":"講座介紹了許多職業選擇。"},{"en":"Career options are possible jobs or career paths someone can choose.","zh":"career options是某人可以選擇的可能工作或職業路徑。"},{"en":"A school counsellor may help students compare career options after graduation.","zh":"學校輔導員可能幫助學生比較畢業後的職業選擇。"},{"en":"More career options can reduce pressure because students do not feel limited to one path.","zh":"更多職業選擇可以減少壓力，因為學生不會覺得只限於一條路。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in education and job planning.","zh":"這個短語常見於教育和職業規劃。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"overall","meaning":"整體而言","examples":[{"en":"Overall, the speaker had quite a strong message.","zh":"整體而言，講者傳達了相當強烈的訊息。"},{"en":"Overall means considering everything together.","zh":"overall意思是把所有事情一起考慮。"},{"en":"Overall, the project was successful even though the presentation started late.","zh":"整體而言，項目是成功的，雖然匯報開始得較遲。"},{"en":"This word helps summarise a general opinion after discussing details.","zh":"這個詞幫助在討論細節後概括整體看法。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving a balanced conclusion.","zh":"它適合用於給出平衡結論。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"strong message","meaning":"強烈訊息","examples":[{"en":"The speaker had quite a strong message for the students.","zh":"講者向學生傳達了相當強烈的訊息。"},{"en":"A strong message is a clear and forceful idea that the speaker wants people to remember.","zh":"strong message是講者希望人們記住的清晰而有力的想法。"},{"en":"A safety talk may have a strong message about never swimming alone.","zh":"安全講座可能有一個強烈訊息，就是絕不要獨自游泳。"},{"en":"Strong messages can influence listeners because they sound urgent and important.","zh":"強烈訊息可以影響聽眾，因為它聽起來迫切而重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main point of a speech or talk.","zh":"這個短語描述演講或講座的主要重點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"keep saying","meaning":"不斷說","examples":[{"en":"The speaker kept saying things that challenged the students’ assumptions.","zh":"講者不斷說一些挑戰學生假設的事情。"},{"en":"To keep saying something means to repeat it several times.","zh":"keep saying某事，意思是多次重複說它。"},{"en":"A coach may keep saying “slow down” if students rush and make mistakes.","zh":"如果學生太急而犯錯，教練可能不斷說「慢下來」。"},{"en":"Repetition can show that the speaker thinks the point is important.","zh":"重複可以顯示講者認為該重點很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase can sometimes suggest annoyance if something is repeated too often.","zh":"如果某事被重複太多，這個短語有時可暗示煩厭。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"how it really is","meaning":"實際情況是怎樣","examples":[{"en":"The speaker told the students how the industry really is.","zh":"講者告訴學生這個行業實際情況是怎樣。"},{"en":"How it really is means the true situation, not the ideal or imagined version.","zh":"how it really is意思是真實情況，而不是理想化或想像中的版本。"},{"en":"An experienced nurse can tell students how hospital work really is during night shifts.","zh":"有經驗的護士可以告訴學生醫院夜班工作實際情況是怎樣。"},{"en":"Learning how something really is can prevent unrealistic expectations.","zh":"了解某事實際情況可以防止不切實際期望。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts reality with fantasy.","zh":"這個短語把現實與幻想作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"narrow-minded about","meaning":"對……看法狹隘","examples":[{"en":"Hugo thinks the speaker may see students as narrow-minded about the industry.","zh":"Hugo認為講者可能覺得學生對行業看法狹隘。"},{"en":"To be narrow-minded about something means to have a limited view and reject wider possibilities.","zh":"narrow-minded about某事，意思是對它看法有限，並拒絕更廣泛可能。"},{"en":"A student is narrow-minded about careers if they think success means only one famous job.","zh":"如果學生認為成功只等於一份有名工作，就是對職業看法狹隘。"},{"en":"Being narrow-minded can stop people from noticing useful opportunities.","zh":"看法狹隘會阻止人注意到有用機會。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises a limited way of thinking.","zh":"這個短語批評有限的思考方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the industry","meaning":"行業","examples":[{"en":"The students are learning about the fashion industry.","zh":"學生正在學習時裝行業。"},{"en":"The industry means a particular area of business or work.","zh":"the industry意思是某個特定商業或工作範疇。"},{"en":"The film industry includes actors, directors, cinemas, editors and producers.","zh":"電影行業包括演員、導演、戲院、剪接師和監製。"},{"en":"Knowing the industry helps students understand its jobs, rules and expectations.","zh":"了解行業幫助學生理解其工作、規則和期望。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to a professional field already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語通常指前文已提及的專業領域。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a bit harsh","meaning":"有點嚴厲","examples":[{"en":"Chantal thought the speaker’s comments were a bit harsh.","zh":"Chantal覺得講者的評論有點嚴厲。"},{"en":"A bit harsh means slightly too severe, critical or unkind.","zh":"a bit harsh意思是稍微過於嚴厲、批判或不友善。"},{"en":"A teacher’s comment may feel a bit harsh if it points out mistakes without encouragement.","zh":"如果老師只指出錯誤而沒有鼓勵，評論可能感覺有點嚴厲。"},{"en":"Harsh criticism can make people defensive instead of reflective.","zh":"嚴厲批評可以令人防衛，而不是反思。"},{"en":"This phrase softens criticism by using “a bit”.","zh":"這個短語用a bit來柔化批評。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"tough industry","meaning":"艱難的行業","examples":[{"en":"The students already know that fashion is a tough industry.","zh":"學生已經知道時裝是艱難的行業。"},{"en":"A tough industry is an industry where success is difficult because of pressure, competition or unstable work.","zh":"tough industry是因壓力、競爭或工作不穩而難以成功的行業。"},{"en":"Journalism can be a tough industry because deadlines are tight and jobs are limited.","zh":"新聞業可以是艱難的行業，因為截稿時間緊而職位有限。"},{"en":"People in tough industries often need resilience and strong networks.","zh":"艱難行業中的人通常需要韌性和強大人脈。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that the work will not be easy.","zh":"這個短語提醒人工作不會容易。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"first years","meaning":"一年級學生","examples":[{"en":"The students are only first years.","zh":"學生只是第一年學生。"},{"en":"First years are students in their first year of a course, school or university programme.","zh":"first years是在課程、學校或大學項目第一年的學生。"},{"en":"First years may still be learning how lectures, assignments and deadlines work.","zh":"一年級學生可能仍在學習講座、功課和期限如何運作。"},{"en":"Because first years are new, they may need guidance before making career decisions.","zh":"因為一年級學生仍是新手，他們在作職業決定前可能需要指導。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies students at an early stage.","zh":"這個短語指出學生處於早期階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"after all","meaning":"畢竟","examples":[{"en":"The students are only first years, after all.","zh":"畢竟，學生只是第一年學生。"},{"en":"After all is used to remind someone of an important reason or fact.","zh":"after all用來提醒某人一個重要理由或事實。"},{"en":"We should not expect perfect essays yet; the class has only just started, after all.","zh":"我們不應期望現在就有完美文章；畢竟課程才剛開始。"},{"en":"This phrase often softens judgement by adding context.","zh":"這個短語常透過加入背景來柔化判斷。"},{"en":"It helps explain why a situation should be viewed more fairly.","zh":"它幫助解釋為何應更公平地看待情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have a lot to learn","meaning":"有很多要學","examples":[{"en":"The students have a lot to learn about the fashion industry.","zh":"學生對時裝業還有很多要學。"},{"en":"To have a lot to learn means to still need much knowledge, skill or experience.","zh":"have a lot to learn意思是仍需要很多知識、技能或經驗。"},{"en":"A new employee has a lot to learn about office systems and customer expectations.","zh":"新員工對辦公室系統和顧客期望有很多要學。"},{"en":"People who have a lot to learn should ask questions and accept feedback.","zh":"有很多要學的人應提問並接受回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase shows someone is still developing.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人仍在發展中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"secondary-school education","meaning":"中學教育","examples":[{"en":"Chantal asks whether their secondary-school education should have been more career-focused.","zh":"Chantal問他們的中學教育是否本應更以職業規劃為重點。"},{"en":"Secondary-school education is the education students receive after primary school and before higher education.","zh":"secondary-school education是學生在小學後、高等教育前接受的教育。"},{"en":"Secondary-school education may include academic subjects, activities and career guidance.","zh":"中學教育可能包括學術科目、活動和職業指導。"},{"en":"Good secondary-school education can help students understand both exams and future choices.","zh":"良好中學教育可以幫助學生理解考試和未來選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the school stage for teenagers.","zh":"這個短語指青少年的學校階段。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"career-focused","meaning":"以職業規劃為重點的","examples":[{"en":"Chantal wonders whether school education should have been more career-focused.","zh":"Chantal想知道學校教育是否本應更以職業規劃為重點。"},{"en":"Career-focused means designed to help people think about jobs, skills and future work.","zh":"career-focused意思是設計來幫助人思考工作、技能和未來職業。"},{"en":"A career-focused workshop may teach students how to build a portfolio and write a CV.","zh":"以職業規劃為重點的工作坊可能教學生如何建立作品集和寫履歷。"},{"en":"Career-focused education can make school feel more connected to real life.","zh":"以職業規劃為重點的教育可以令學校更連接現實生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning that points towards future employment.","zh":"這個短語描述指向未來就業的學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"numerous talks on","meaning":"許多關於……的講座","examples":[{"en":"Hugo had numerous talks on careers at secondary school.","zh":"Hugo在中學時聽過許多關於職業的講座。"},{"en":"Numerous talks on something means many presentations or discussions about that topic.","zh":"numerous talks on某事，意思是關於該主題的許多演講或討論。"},{"en":"Students may attend numerous talks on university applications before finalising their choices.","zh":"學生在最終選擇前，可能參加許多關於大學申請的講座。"},{"en":"Many talks can become useful only if they are practical and relevant.","zh":"許多講座只有在實用和相關時才變得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses quantity, not necessarily quality.","zh":"這個短語強調數量，而不一定是質素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"careers","meaning":"職業","examples":[{"en":"The students had talks on careers at school.","zh":"學生在學校聽過關於職業的講座。"},{"en":"Careers are long-term paths of work, training and professional development.","zh":"careers是工作、培訓和專業發展的長期路徑。"},{"en":"A student interested in animals may consider careers in veterinary care, conservation or research.","zh":"對動物感興趣的學生可能考慮獸醫護理、保育或研究等職業。"},{"en":"Careers develop through study, experience, choices and sometimes unexpected opportunities.","zh":"職業透過學習、經驗、選擇，有時也透過意外機會而發展。"},{"en":"This word is broader than one single job.","zh":"這個詞比單一工作更廣泛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"very inspiring","meaning":"很有啟發性的","examples":[{"en":"The careers talks were not very inspiring.","zh":"那些職業講座不是很有啟發性。"},{"en":"Very inspiring means strongly encouraging people to think, act or feel hopeful.","zh":"very inspiring意思是非常能鼓勵人思考、行動或感到有希望。"},{"en":"A speaker can be very inspiring if she tells honest stories about failure and recovery.","zh":"如果講者講述關於失敗和重新振作的真實故事，她可以很有啟發性。"},{"en":"Talks that are not inspiring may give information but fail to motivate students.","zh":"不具啟發性的講座可能提供資料，但未能激勵學生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional and motivational impact.","zh":"這個短語描述情感和動機上的影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"could have asked","meaning":"本可以請","examples":[{"en":"The school could have asked more people like today’s speaker to talk to students.","zh":"學校本可以請更多像今天講者那樣的人與學生談話。"},{"en":"Could have asked means had the chance to invite or request someone, but did not do so.","zh":"could have asked意思是本有機會邀請或請求某人，但沒有這樣做。"},{"en":"The club could have asked alumni to share interview advice before the job fair.","zh":"社團本可以在招聘會前請校友分享面試建議。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests a missed opportunity.","zh":"這個短語常暗示錯失機會。"},{"en":"It is used when looking back and imagining a better choice.","zh":"它用於回顧過去並想像更好選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"talk to us","meaning":"跟我們談","examples":[{"en":"The school could have invited experts to talk to the students.","zh":"學校本可以邀請專家跟學生談。"},{"en":"To talk to us means to speak with us directly, often to explain or share experience.","zh":"talk to us意思是直接與我們說話，通常是解釋或分享經驗。"},{"en":"Students appreciate it when professionals talk to them honestly about real working life.","zh":"當專業人士坦誠地跟學生談真實工作生活，學生會很欣賞。"},{"en":"Direct talks can make career advice feel personal and believable.","zh":"直接談話可以令職業建議感覺個人化和可信。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communication between a speaker and a group.","zh":"這個短語描述講者與群體之間的溝通。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"just when we needed to be","meaning":"正正在我們需要的時候","examples":[{"en":"The students were told about careers just when they needed to be.","zh":"學生正正在需要的時候獲告知職業資訊。"},{"en":"Just when we needed to be means exactly at the time when it was necessary or useful for us.","zh":"just when we needed to be意思是正正在我們需要或覺得有用的時候。"},{"en":"Students need career advice just when they are choosing subjects for senior school.","zh":"學生在選擇高中科目時，正正需要職業建議。"},{"en":"Good timing can make advice more useful because people are ready to act on it.","zh":"良好時機可以令建議更有用，因為人們準備好採取行動。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the timing was appropriate.","zh":"這個短語強調時機合適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"experts who really know stuff","meaning":"真正懂行的專家","examples":[{"en":"The students wanted to hear from experts who really know stuff.","zh":"學生想聽真正懂行的專家分享。"},{"en":"Experts who really know stuff are people with real knowledge and experience in a field.","zh":"experts who really know stuff是在某領域有真知識和經驗的人。"},{"en":"Fashion students may prefer hearing from designers who have worked with actual clients.","zh":"時裝學生可能較想聽曾與真實客戶合作的設計師分享。"},{"en":"Advice from real experts feels more useful because it comes from practice, not theory alone.","zh":"真正專家的建議感覺更有用，因為它來自實踐，而不只是理論。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and praises practical expertise.","zh":"這個短語較口語，讚賞實用專業知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"influence your thoughts on","meaning":"影響你對……的想法","examples":[{"en":"Hugo asks whether the talk influenced Chantal’s thoughts on her future career.","zh":"Hugo問那場講座是否影響Chantal對未來職業的想法。"},{"en":"To influence your thoughts on something means to affect how you think about it.","zh":"influence your thoughts on某事，意思是影響你如何思考它。"},{"en":"A hospital visit may influence a student’s thoughts on becoming a nurse.","zh":"一次醫院探訪可能影響學生對成為護士的想法。"},{"en":"New information can influence someone’s thoughts by showing risks or possibilities they had not considered.","zh":"新資訊可以透過展示未曾考慮的風險或可能性，影響某人的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase connects experience with changing opinions.","zh":"這個短語把經驗與想法改變連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take up","meaning":"從事","examples":[{"en":"Chantal has not yet decided what career she would like to take up.","zh":"Chantal尚未決定想從事甚麼職業。"},{"en":"To take up a career means to begin doing that kind of work.","zh":"take up某職業，意思是開始做那類工作。"},{"en":"A graduate may take up teaching after discovering that she enjoys helping younger students.","zh":"畢業生發現自己喜歡幫助年幼學生後，可能從事教學。"},{"en":"Choosing what to take up can be difficult when there are many possible paths.","zh":"當有許多可能路徑時，選擇從事甚麼會很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for starting work, study or hobbies.","zh":"這個短語常用於開始工作、學習或嗜好。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the future","meaning":"將來","examples":[{"en":"The students are thinking about careers they may take up in the future.","zh":"學生正在思考將來可能從事的職業。"},{"en":"In the future means at a later time, not now.","zh":"in the future意思是在較後時間，而不是現在。"},{"en":"Students may need digital skills in the future even if their current courses are creative.","zh":"即使學生現在讀創意課程，將來也可能需要數碼技能。"},{"en":"Thinking about the future helps people make better choices today.","zh":"思考將來幫助人今天作出更好選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase points to plans, possibilities or expectations ahead.","zh":"這個短語指向未來的計劃、可能性或期望。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"promise myself that","meaning":"向自己承諾","examples":[{"en":"Chantal promised herself that she would keep an open mind.","zh":"Chantal向自己承諾會保持開放心態。"},{"en":"To promise myself that means to make a private commitment to do something.","zh":"promise myself that意思是私下承諾自己會做某事。"},{"en":"A student may promise herself that she will revise a little every day.","zh":"學生可能向自己承諾每天溫習一點。"},{"en":"Private promises can guide behaviour even when no one else is checking.","zh":"即使沒有人檢查，私人承諾也可以引導行為。"},{"en":"This phrase shows personal determination.","zh":"這個短語顯示個人決心。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"go through this course","meaning":"完成這個課程","examples":[{"en":"Chantal wants to go through the course before choosing a career path.","zh":"Chantal想先完成這個課程，再選擇職業道路。"},{"en":"To go through a course means to complete or experience the course from beginning to end.","zh":"go through a course意思是由開始到結束完成或經歷該課程。"},{"en":"Students should go through the course before judging which module they like most.","zh":"學生應先完成課程，再判斷自己最喜歡哪個單元。"},{"en":"Completing a course gives learners more evidence before making big decisions.","zh":"完成課程能讓學習者在作重大決定前有更多依據。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests learning by experiencing the whole programme.","zh":"這個短語暗示透過經歷整個課程來學習。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"keep an open mind","meaning":"保持開放心態","examples":[{"en":"Chantal wants to keep an open mind until the end of the course.","zh":"Chantal想在課程結束前保持開放心態。"},{"en":"To keep an open mind means to stay willing to consider different ideas or options.","zh":"keep an open mind意思是願意考慮不同想法或選項。"},{"en":"A student should keep an open mind when trying new subjects in the first year.","zh":"一年級學生嘗試新科目時，應保持開放心態。"},{"en":"Keeping an open mind can prevent people from rejecting opportunities too early.","zh":"保持開放心態可以防止人太早拒絕機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes flexible thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述靈活思考。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"till the end","meaning":"直到最後","examples":[{"en":"Chantal will keep an open mind till the end of the course.","zh":"Chantal會保持開放心態直到課程最後。"},{"en":"Till the end means until something finishes.","zh":"till the end意思是直到某事結束。"},{"en":"Students should listen till the end of a talk before judging the speaker’s argument.","zh":"學生應聽完整場講座直到最後，才判斷講者的論點。"},{"en":"Waiting till the end can give people the full picture.","zh":"等到最後可以讓人看到完整圖像。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses completion before final judgement.","zh":"這個短語強調在作最終判斷前完成整個過程。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pick an area of","meaning":"選定……的一個範疇","examples":[{"en":"Hugo thinks students should pick an area of the industry early.","zh":"Hugo認為學生應及早選定行業中的一個範疇。"},{"en":"To pick an area of something means to choose one part or section to focus on.","zh":"pick an area of某事，意思是選擇其中一個部分或範疇來專注。"},{"en":"A business student may pick an area of finance, such as investment or accounting.","zh":"商科學生可能選定金融中的一個範疇，例如投資或會計。"},{"en":"Picking an area early can help people build specific skills.","zh":"及早選定範疇可以幫助人建立特定技能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a field has many specialisms.","zh":"當一個領域有很多專門方向時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"aim to","meaning":"以……為目標","examples":[{"en":"Hugo wants to aim to get better and better at one area.","zh":"Hugo想以在一個範疇越來越好為目標。"},{"en":"To aim to do something means to set it as a goal.","zh":"aim to do something意思是把做某事定為目標。"},{"en":"A student may aim to finish a portfolio before the summer break.","zh":"學生可能以暑假前完成作品集為目標。"},{"en":"Clear aims help people decide what to practise and what to ignore.","zh":"清晰目標幫助人決定要練習甚麼和忽略甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase shows intention and direction.","zh":"這個短語顯示意圖和方向。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get better and better at","meaning":"在……方面越來越好","examples":[{"en":"Hugo thinks students should get better and better at one area.","zh":"Hugo認為學生應在一個範疇越來越好。"},{"en":"To get better and better at something means to improve gradually and continuously.","zh":"get better and better at某事，意思是逐漸並持續進步。"},{"en":"A writer gets better and better at dialogue by reading, practising and receiving feedback.","zh":"作家透過閱讀、練習和取得回饋，在寫對白方面越來越好。"},{"en":"Repeated practice helps people become more skilled over time.","zh":"反覆練習幫助人隨時間變得更熟練。"},{"en":"This phrase describes steady progress.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定進步。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"differ on that issue","meaning":"在那個問題上意見不同","examples":[{"en":"Chantal thinks she and Hugo will have to differ on that issue.","zh":"Chantal認為她和Hugo在那個問題上只好意見不同。"},{"en":"To differ on that issue means to have different opinions about that particular matter.","zh":"differ on that issue意思是對該特定事情有不同意見。"},{"en":"Two students may differ on whether it is better to specialise early or explore widely.","zh":"兩名學生可能在應及早專門發展還是廣泛探索上意見不同。"},{"en":"People can differ on an issue without becoming enemies.","zh":"人們可以在一個問題上意見不同，而不變成敵人。"},{"en":"This phrase is a polite way to show disagreement.","zh":"這個短語是表示不同意的有禮方式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"one thing is for certain","meaning":"有一件事是肯定的","examples":[{"en":"Hugo says one thing is for certain.","zh":"Hugo說有一件事是肯定的。"},{"en":"One thing is for certain means at least one point is definitely true.","zh":"one thing is for certain意思是至少有一點絕對屬實。"},{"en":"One thing is for certain: students need a strong portfolio in a creative industry.","zh":"有一件事是肯定的：學生在創意行業需要強大的作品集。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when other details are uncertain but one fact is clear.","zh":"當其他細節不確定但有一項事實清楚時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It helps introduce a confident statement.","zh":"它幫助引入有把握的陳述。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"from what she said","meaning":"根據她所說","examples":[{"en":"From what the speaker said, students may work unpaid for a long time.","zh":"根據講者所說，學生可能會長時間無薪工作。"},{"en":"From what she said means based on the information or impression she gave.","zh":"from what she said意思是根據她提供的資訊或印象。"},{"en":"From what the doctor said, the patient needs more rest before returning to work.","zh":"根據醫生所說，病人需要更多休息才可復工。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the speaker is drawing a conclusion from someone else’s words.","zh":"這個短語顯示說話者正從別人的話中得出結論。"},{"en":"It is useful when summarising or interpreting another person’s comments.","zh":"當概括或解讀他人評論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"unpaid assistants","meaning":"無薪助理","examples":[{"en":"The students may become unpaid assistants in the industry.","zh":"學生可能成為行業中的無薪助理。"},{"en":"Unpaid assistants are helpers who work without receiving wages.","zh":"unpaid assistants是沒有工資的助手。"},{"en":"A fashion studio may use unpaid assistants to organise clothes before a show.","zh":"時裝工作室可能使用無薪助理在時裝秀前整理服裝。"},{"en":"Unpaid work can give experience, but it can also be unfair if it continues too long.","zh":"無薪工作可以帶來經驗，但如果持續太久也可能不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase raises questions about opportunity and exploitation.","zh":"這個短語引出關於機會和剝削的問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for quite a long time","meaning":"相當長時間","examples":[{"en":"Hugo expects to be an unpaid assistant for quite a long time.","zh":"Hugo預計自己會做相當長時間的無薪助理。"},{"en":"For quite a long time means for a fairly long period.","zh":"for quite a long time意思是持續一段頗長時間。"},{"en":"A new graduate may work in junior roles for quite a long time before being promoted.","zh":"新畢業生可能在初級職位工作相當長時間，才獲晉升。"},{"en":"When something lasts for quite a long time, it can test patience and finances.","zh":"當某事持續相當長時間，它可以考驗耐性和財政。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the period is longer than someone might wish.","zh":"這個短語暗示時間比某人希望的更長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be prepared for","meaning":"為……做好準備","examples":[{"en":"Hugo is prepared for unpaid work in the industry.","zh":"Hugo已為行業中的無薪工作做好準備。"},{"en":"To be prepared for something means to be ready to face or handle it.","zh":"be prepared for某事，意思是準備好面對或處理它。"},{"en":"Students should be prepared for criticism when they present creative work.","zh":"學生展示創意作品時，應為批評做好準備。"},{"en":"Preparation reduces shock because people know what difficulties may come.","zh":"準備能減少震驚，因為人們知道可能會有甚麼困難。"},{"en":"This phrase shows readiness for a possible challenge.","zh":"這個短語顯示對可能挑戰已有準備。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"accept that view","meaning":"接受那種看法","examples":[{"en":"Chantal is not going to accept that view.","zh":"Chantal不會接受那種看法。"},{"en":"To accept that view means to agree with that opinion or believe it is correct.","zh":"accept that view意思是同意那個意見或相信它正確。"},{"en":"A student may refuse to accept the view that only rich people can enter creative industries.","zh":"學生可能拒絕接受只有富人才能進入創意行業的看法。"},{"en":"People reject a view when it feels unfair, too negative or unsupported by evidence.","zh":"當看法感覺不公平、太負面或缺乏證據，人們會拒絕它。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on agreeing with an opinion.","zh":"這個短語著重同意某個意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"it is the case","meaning":"情況就是如此","examples":[{"en":"Hugo says the speaker knows it is the case.","zh":"Hugo說講者知道情況就是如此。"},{"en":"It is the case means it is true or it is the real situation.","zh":"it is the case意思是某事屬實或真實情況就是這樣。"},{"en":"If many graduates work unpaid at first, it may be the case that the industry relies on free labour.","zh":"如果許多畢業生起初無薪工作，情況可能就是該行業依賴免費勞動。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and is often used in arguments.","zh":"這個短語聽起來較正式，常用於論證。"},{"en":"It presents something as fact rather than opinion.","zh":"它把某事呈現為事實，而不是意見。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"everyone else says the same","meaning":"其他人也這樣說","examples":[{"en":"Hugo says everyone else says the same about unpaid work.","zh":"Hugo說其他人也這樣談無薪工作。"},{"en":"Everyone else says the same means many other people express the same opinion or information.","zh":"everyone else says the same意思是許多其他人表達同樣意見或資訊。"},{"en":"If every graduate says the internship is unpaid, students may start to believe it is common.","zh":"如果每個畢業生都說實習無薪，學生可能開始相信這很常見。"},{"en":"Repeated comments from many people can make a claim seem more credible.","zh":"許多人反覆說同一件事，可以令聲稱看似更可信。"},{"en":"This phrase uses social agreement as support.","zh":"這個短語以社會共識作支持。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have to be true for me","meaning":"對我來說必然如此","examples":[{"en":"Chantal says it does not have to be true for her.","zh":"Chantal說這不一定對她來說必然如此。"},{"en":"Have to be true for me means must apply to my own situation.","zh":"have to be true for me意思是必須適用於我自己的情況。"},{"en":"Just because most people follow one career path does not mean it has to be true for me.","zh":"只因大多數人走同一條職業路，並不代表它對我來說必然如此。"},{"en":"This phrase separates a general pattern from one person’s future.","zh":"這個短語把一般模式與個人的未來分開。"},{"en":"It shows personal hope or resistance against a common expectation.","zh":"它顯示對常見期望的個人希望或抗拒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"I hope you are right","meaning":"希望你是對的","examples":[{"en":"Hugo hopes Chantal is right about her future.","zh":"Hugo希望Chantal對自己的未來判斷是對的。"},{"en":"I hope you are right means I want your opinion or prediction to be true.","zh":"I hope you are right意思是我希望你的意見或預測屬實。"},{"en":"If a friend says the exam will be fair, you may reply, “I hope you are right.”","zh":"如果朋友說考試會公平，你可能回答：「希望你是對的。」"},{"en":"This phrase can express support while still showing uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語可以表達支持，同時仍顯示不確定。"},{"en":"It is often used when the speaker wants a positive outcome.","zh":"它常用於說話者希望有正面結果的情況。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"account of","meaning":"對……的敘述","examples":[{"en":"Chantal found the speaker’s account of her first job fascinating.","zh":"Chantal覺得講者對第一份工作的敘述非常吸引。"},{"en":"An account of something is a description or story about what happened.","zh":"account of某事，是關於發生了甚麼的描述或故事。"},{"en":"A nurse gave students an honest account of working in an emergency ward.","zh":"護士向學生講述在急症病房工作的真實經歷。"},{"en":"Personal accounts help listeners understand real experience, not just theory.","zh":"個人敘述幫助聽眾理解真實經驗，而不只是理論。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone tells a detailed story.","zh":"當某人講述詳細故事時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"first job","meaning":"第一份工作","examples":[{"en":"The speaker told the students about her first job.","zh":"講者向學生講述她的第一份工作。"},{"en":"A first job is the first paid or professional role someone has.","zh":"first job是某人第一份有薪或專業角色。"},{"en":"A student’s first job may be serving customers in a café during the summer.","zh":"學生第一份工作可能是在夏天於咖啡店服務顧客。"},{"en":"First jobs often teach practical lessons about responsibility and workplace behaviour.","zh":"第一份工作通常教人關於責任和職場行為的實用課。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an early step in a person’s working life.","zh":"這個短語指一個人工作人生中的早期一步。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fascinating","meaning":"非常吸引人的","examples":[{"en":"The speaker’s account of her first job was fascinating.","zh":"講者對第一份工作的敘述非常吸引人。"},{"en":"Fascinating means extremely interesting and able to hold people’s attention.","zh":"fascinating意思是極有趣並能吸引人的注意。"},{"en":"A true story about how a designer lost and rebuilt a career can be fascinating.","zh":"關於設計師如何失去事業又重新建立的真實故事，可以非常吸引人。"},{"en":"People find stories fascinating when they reveal details they did not expect.","zh":"當故事揭示意想不到的細節，人們會覺得它非常吸引人。"},{"en":"This word gives stronger praise than simply “interesting”.","zh":"這個詞比單純說interesting有更強讚賞意味。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"admit that","meaning":"承認","examples":[{"en":"The speaker admitted that she was lucky to get the job.","zh":"講者承認自己很幸運能得到那份工作。"},{"en":"To admit that something is true means to say it honestly, even if it is not easy to say.","zh":"admit that某事屬實，意思是誠實說出它，即使不容易開口。"},{"en":"A student may admit that he did not prepare enough for the interview.","zh":"學生可能承認自己沒有為面試準備足夠。"},{"en":"Admitting the truth can make a speaker sound honest and reflective.","zh":"承認事實可以令講者聽起來誠實並懂得反思。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces a confession or honest acknowledgement.","zh":"這個短語常引入坦白承認或誠實承認。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be lucky to","meaning":"很幸運能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker was lucky to get work as a personal dresser.","zh":"講者很幸運能找到私人造型師工作。"},{"en":"To be lucky to do something means to have a good opportunity partly because of chance.","zh":"be lucky to do something意思是因部分靠機會而得到好機遇。"},{"en":"A graduate may be lucky to meet a helpful mentor at their first internship.","zh":"畢業生可能很幸運在第一份實習中遇到樂於幫助的導師。"},{"en":"Luck can open a door, but people still need skill to keep the opportunity.","zh":"運氣可以打開機會之門，但人仍需要能力去保住機會。"},{"en":"This phrase recognises fortune rather than pure effort.","zh":"這個短語承認幸運，而不只是努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get work","meaning":"找到工作","examples":[{"en":"The speaker was lucky to get work as a personal dresser.","zh":"講者很幸運能找到私人造型師工作。"},{"en":"To get work means to find employment or paid work.","zh":"get work意思是找到受僱或有薪工作。"},{"en":"New designers may get work by showing a strong portfolio to small studios.","zh":"新設計師可能透過向小型工作室展示強大作品集而找到工作。"},{"en":"Getting work can be difficult when many people want the same job.","zh":"當很多人想要同一份工作，找工作會很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on finding a job rather than doing the job itself.","zh":"這個短語著重找到工作，而不是工作本身。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"personal dresser","meaning":"私人造型師","examples":[{"en":"The speaker worked as a personal dresser for a musician.","zh":"講者曾為一名音樂人擔任私人造型師。"},{"en":"A personal dresser helps choose, prepare or manage clothes for one particular client.","zh":"personal dresser是幫某一位客戶挑選、準備或管理服裝的人。"},{"en":"A singer may hire a personal dresser before concerts, interviews and photo shoots.","zh":"歌手可能在演唱會、訪問和拍攝前聘請私人造型師。"},{"en":"Personal dressers need to understand the client’s image, not only their own taste.","zh":"私人造型師需要理解客戶形象，而不只是自己的品味。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a styling job focused on one person.","zh":"這個短語描述專注於一人的造型工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"apply for the job","meaning":"申請那份工作","examples":[{"en":"The speaker did not even apply for the job.","zh":"講者甚至沒有申請那份工作。"},{"en":"To apply for the job means to formally ask to be considered for that position.","zh":"apply for the job意思是正式要求被考慮擔任該職位。"},{"en":"A student may apply for a summer job by sending a CV and cover letter.","zh":"學生可能透過提交履歷和求職信申請暑期工。"},{"en":"If you do not apply, employers usually do not know you want the role.","zh":"如果你不申請，僱主通常不知道你想得到該角色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the formal first step in getting a job.","zh":"這個短語描述求職的正式第一步。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get paid to","meaning":"收錢去……","examples":[{"en":"The speaker got paid to choose a musician’s clothes.","zh":"講者收錢為一名音樂人挑選衣服。"},{"en":"To get paid to do something means to receive money for doing that work.","zh":"get paid to do something意思是因做該工作而收取金錢。"},{"en":"A student may get paid to design posters for a school event.","zh":"學生可能收錢為學校活動設計海報。"},{"en":"When people get paid for a skill, the skill becomes part of their work.","zh":"當人因某技能而收錢，該技能就成為工作的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase links an activity with payment.","zh":"這個短語把活動與報酬連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"choose all his clothes","meaning":"挑選他的所有服裝","examples":[{"en":"The speaker was paid to choose all the musician’s clothes.","zh":"講者收錢挑選那名音樂人的所有服裝。"},{"en":"To choose all his clothes means to select every outfit or item of clothing for him.","zh":"choose all his clothes意思是為他選擇每套衣服或每件衣物。"},{"en":"A stylist may choose all a performer’s clothes for a tour so the image stays consistent.","zh":"造型師可能為表演者巡演挑選所有服裝，令形象保持一致。"},{"en":"Choosing someone’s clothes requires understanding their body, taste, schedule and public image.","zh":"挑選某人的服裝需要理解其身形、品味、日程和公眾形象。"},{"en":"This phrase shows full responsibility for a person’s wardrobe choices.","zh":"這個短語顯示對一個人衣櫥選擇的全面責任。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"must have felt","meaning":"一定感覺……","examples":[{"en":"Chantal says it must have felt amazing to get that job.","zh":"Chantal說得到那份工作一定感覺很棒。"},{"en":"Must have felt means the speaker strongly guesses how someone felt in the past.","zh":"must have felt意思是說話者強烈推測某人過去的感受。"},{"en":"Winning a scholarship must have felt wonderful after months of hard work.","zh":"經過數月努力後獲得獎學金，一定感覺很美好。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when we infer emotions from a situation.","zh":"當我們根據情況推斷情緒時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It expresses a confident guess, not direct knowledge.","zh":"它表達有信心的推測，而不是直接知道。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"all she was looking for","meaning":"她當時所追求的只是","examples":[{"en":"All the speaker was looking for back then was experience.","zh":"講者當時所追求的只是經驗。"},{"en":"All she was looking for means the only thing she wanted or hoped to get.","zh":"all she was looking for意思是她唯一想要或希望得到的東西。"},{"en":"At her first internship, all she was looking for was a chance to learn.","zh":"在第一份實習中，她所追求的可能只是學習機會。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows someone’s aim to one main thing.","zh":"這個短語把某人的目標收窄到一件主要事情。"},{"en":"It often contrasts one goal with other possible rewards.","zh":"它常把一個目標與其他可能回報作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"back then","meaning":"當時","examples":[{"en":"Back then, the speaker was looking for experience rather than money.","zh":"當時，講者追求的是經驗，而不是金錢。"},{"en":"Back then means at that earlier time in the past.","zh":"back then意思是在過去那個較早時候。"},{"en":"Back then, students used paper portfolios instead of online profiles.","zh":"當時，學生使用紙本作品集，而不是網上個人檔案。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when comparing the past with the present.","zh":"這個短語常用於比較過去與現在。"},{"en":"It gives a conversational, memory-based tone.","zh":"它帶有口語化和回憶式語氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"financial reward","meaning":"金錢回報","examples":[{"en":"The speaker wanted experience, not financial reward.","zh":"講者想要的是經驗，而不是金錢回報。"},{"en":"Financial reward means money or payment received for work or effort.","zh":"financial reward意思是因工作或努力而得到的金錢或報酬。"},{"en":"Some volunteers choose community service for learning and meaning rather than financial reward.","zh":"有些義工選擇社區服務，是為了學習和意義，而不是金錢回報。"},{"en":"Financial reward matters, but it is not the only reason people take opportunities.","zh":"金錢回報很重要，但不是人們接受機會的唯一原因。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts money with other benefits such as experience.","zh":"這個短語把金錢與經驗等其他好處作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be mean","meaning":"刻薄","examples":[{"en":"The musician was mean when he criticised the speaker.","zh":"那名音樂人批評講者時很刻薄。"},{"en":"To be mean means to be unkind, hurtful or unfair in what one says or does.","zh":"be mean意思是說話或行為不友善、傷人或不公平。"},{"en":"A classmate is mean if she laughs at someone’s mistake instead of helping.","zh":"如果同學嘲笑別人的錯誤而不是幫忙，她就是刻薄。"},{"en":"Mean comments can damage confidence even when they contain some truth.","zh":"刻薄評論即使包含一些事實，也可以傷害信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes behaviour that feels cruel or ungenerous.","zh":"這個短語描述感覺殘酷或不大方的行為。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"more interested in","meaning":"對……更感興趣","examples":[{"en":"The musician said she was more interested in her own appearance than his.","zh":"那名音樂人說她對自己的外表比對他的外表更感興趣。"},{"en":"More interested in something means caring about it more than another thing.","zh":"more interested in某事，意思是比起另一事更關心它。"},{"en":"A designer should not be more interested in showing off than solving the client’s problem.","zh":"設計師不應比起解決客戶問題，更感興趣於炫耀自己。"},{"en":"If someone focuses on the wrong priority, their work may suffer.","zh":"如果某人專注錯誤優先次序，其工作可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase compares levels of attention or concern.","zh":"這個短語比較關注或在意的程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one’s own appearance","meaning":"自己的外表","examples":[{"en":"The speaker was criticised for caring too much about her own appearance.","zh":"講者被批評太在意自己的外表。"},{"en":"One’s own appearance means how one personally looks, including clothes, hair and style.","zh":"one’s own appearance意思是某人自己的外觀，包括衣着、髮型和風格。"},{"en":"A student may worry about her own appearance before an interview.","zh":"學生在面試前可能擔心自己的外表。"},{"en":"Caring about appearance is normal, but it can become a problem if it distracts from the task.","zh":"關心外表是正常的，但如果分散對任務的注意，就會成為問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on personal looks rather than another person’s image.","zh":"這個短語著重個人外觀，而不是另一個人的形象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"realise someone was right","meaning":"意識到某人是對的","examples":[{"en":"The speaker realised the musician was right about her mistake.","zh":"講者意識到那名音樂人對她的錯誤看法是對的。"},{"en":"To realise someone was right means to understand later that their opinion or criticism was correct.","zh":"realise someone was right意思是後來明白某人的意見或批評是正確的。"},{"en":"A student may realise a teacher was right after poor planning leads to a rushed essay.","zh":"當規劃不足導致文章趕急完成，學生可能意識到老師是對的。"},{"en":"Realising someone was right can be uncomfortable but useful for improvement.","zh":"意識到某人是對的可能不舒服，但對改進有用。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a change in understanding.","zh":"這個短語顯示理解上的轉變。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make me think","meaning":"令我思考","examples":[{"en":"The speaker’s story really made Chantal think.","zh":"講者的故事真的令Chantal思考。"},{"en":"To make me think means to cause me to reflect seriously on something.","zh":"make me think意思是令我認真反思某事。"},{"en":"A documentary about waste may make students think about their shopping habits.","zh":"關於浪費的紀錄片可能令學生思考自己的購物習慣。"},{"en":"Stories make people think when they connect ideas with real experience.","zh":"當故事把想法與真實經驗連繫起來，就會令人思考。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something has mental or emotional impact.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事有思想或情感影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"consider my own clothes","meaning":"考慮自己的衣着","examples":[{"en":"Chantal is always considering her own clothes.","zh":"Chantal總是在考慮自己的衣着。"},{"en":"To consider my own clothes means to think carefully about what I wear and how I look.","zh":"consider my own clothes意思是仔細思考自己穿甚麼和看起來如何。"},{"en":"A fashion student may consider her own clothes before attending a design interview.","zh":"時裝學生可能在設計面試前考慮自己的衣着。"},{"en":"Thinking too much about personal clothing can distract someone from a client’s needs.","zh":"太多思考個人衣着可以令人分心，忽略客戶需要。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on personal style decisions.","zh":"這個短語著重個人風格選擇。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"focus on your client","meaning":"專注於你的客戶","examples":[{"en":"A personal dresser should focus on the client.","zh":"私人造型師應專注於客戶。"},{"en":"To focus on your client means to put the client’s needs, image and goals first.","zh":"focus on your client意思是把客戶需要、形象和目標放在首位。"},{"en":"A designer should focus on the client before choosing colours or materials.","zh":"設計師在選擇顏色或材料前，應先專注於客戶。"},{"en":"If professionals focus only on themselves, the service may fail.","zh":"如果專業人士只專注自己，服務可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in service and creative work.","zh":"這個短語在服務和創意工作中很重要。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"obviously regretted","meaning":"顯然後悔","examples":[{"en":"The speaker obviously regretted losing the job.","zh":"講者顯然後悔失去那份工作。"},{"en":"Obviously regretted means clearly felt sorry or disappointed about something in the past.","zh":"obviously regretted意思是明顯對過去某事感到後悔或失望。"},{"en":"A student obviously regretted missing the deadline when she saw the mark penalty.","zh":"學生看到扣分後，顯然後悔錯過期限。"},{"en":"Regret often appears when people realise what they should have done differently.","zh":"當人們意識到自己本應不同做法，後悔常會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the feeling is easy to notice.","zh":"這個短語顯示該感受很容易看出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lose the job","meaning":"失去那份工作","examples":[{"en":"The speaker regretted losing her first job.","zh":"講者後悔失去第一份工作。"},{"en":"To lose the job means to no longer have that job, often because the employer ends it.","zh":"lose the job意思是不再擁有該工作，通常因僱主終止它。"},{"en":"A worker may lose the job if they repeatedly arrive late and ignore warnings.","zh":"如果員工反覆遲到並忽視警告，可能失去那份工作。"},{"en":"Losing a job can be upsetting but may also teach important lessons.","zh":"失去工作可以令人難過，但也可能教會人重要教訓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unwanted end to employment.","zh":"這個短語描述僱用關係不想要的結束。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as she said","meaning":"正如她所說","examples":[{"en":"As the speaker said, she should have hidden her negative feelings.","zh":"正如講者所說，她本應隱藏自己的負面感受。"},{"en":"As she said means according to what she herself stated earlier.","zh":"as she said意思是根據她自己早前所說。"},{"en":"As the teacher said, revision is more useful when students practise questions.","zh":"正如老師所說，學生練習題目時溫習更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to someone’s own words for support.","zh":"這個短語引用某人自己的說話作支持。"},{"en":"It helps connect a comment with a previous statement.","zh":"它幫助把評論與之前陳述連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"should have hidden","meaning":"本應隱藏","examples":[{"en":"The speaker should have hidden her negative feelings about the musician.","zh":"講者本應隱藏她對那名音樂人的負面感受。"},{"en":"Should have hidden means it would have been better to keep something from being shown.","zh":"should have hidden意思是本來最好不要讓某事表露出來。"},{"en":"A student should have hidden her disappointment during an interview and stayed polite.","zh":"學生在面試中本應隱藏失望，並保持有禮。"},{"en":"In professional settings, showing negative feelings too openly can damage trust.","zh":"在專業場合中，太公開表露負面感受可以損害信任。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses regret about a past action.","zh":"這個短語表達對過去行動的後悔。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"negative feelings about","meaning":"對……的負面感受","examples":[{"en":"The speaker failed to hide her negative feelings about the musician.","zh":"講者未能隱藏她對那名音樂人的負面感受。"},{"en":"Negative feelings about someone are unpleasant emotions such as dislike, anger or irritation towards that person.","zh":"negative feelings about某人，是對該人的不快情緒，例如不喜歡、憤怒或煩厭。"},{"en":"A team member may have negative feelings about a manager who never listens.","zh":"如果經理從不聆聽，團隊成員可能對他有負面感受。"},{"en":"If negative feelings are shown too strongly, relationships at work can suffer.","zh":"如果負面感受表現得太強烈，職場關係可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unfavourable emotions towards a person or situation.","zh":"這個短語描述對某人或某情況的不利情緒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pick oneself up","meaning":"重新振作","examples":[{"en":"The speaker picked herself up after losing the job.","zh":"講者失去那份工作後重新振作。"},{"en":"To pick oneself up means to recover emotionally and continue after a failure or setback.","zh":"pick oneself up意思是在失敗或挫折後情緒上恢復並繼續前進。"},{"en":"A student who fails a test can pick herself up by asking for feedback and practising again.","zh":"測驗不合格的學生可以透過尋求回饋和再次練習來重新振作。"},{"en":"People need resilience to pick themselves up after disappointment.","zh":"人們在失望後重新振作需要韌性。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests recovery and renewed effort.","zh":"這個短語暗示恢復和重新努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take a job in retail","meaning":"接受零售工作","examples":[{"en":"The speaker took a job in retail after losing her first job.","zh":"講者失去第一份工作後接受零售工作。"},{"en":"To take a job in retail means to accept work in shops or selling goods to customers.","zh":"take a job in retail意思是接受在店舖或向顧客銷售貨品的工作。"},{"en":"A fashion student may take a job in retail to understand what customers actually buy.","zh":"時裝學生可能接受零售工作，以了解顧客實際購買甚麼。"},{"en":"Retail jobs can teach communication, patience and customer awareness.","zh":"零售工作可以教人溝通、耐性和顧客意識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes entering shop-based work.","zh":"這個短語描述進入店舖銷售相關工作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fancy working in","meaning":"竟然去……工作","examples":[{"en":"Hugo says, “Fancy working in a shop after that!”","zh":"Hugo說：「之後竟然去店舖工作！」"},{"en":"Fancy working in something expresses surprise at the idea of working there.","zh":"fancy working in某地，表達對在那裡工作這件事感到驚訝。"},{"en":"Fancy working in a tiny café after managing a large restaurant!","zh":"管理過大型餐廳後，竟然去小咖啡店工作！"},{"en":"This phrase can sound informal and slightly humorous or critical.","zh":"這個短語較口語，可能帶有輕微幽默或批評。"},{"en":"It often suggests the situation is unexpected after what came before.","zh":"它常暗示在之前情況之後，這件事出乎意料。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"recommend someone do something","meaning":"建議某人做某事","examples":[{"en":"The speaker recommended that the students work in retail at some point.","zh":"講者建議學生在某個階段從事零售工作。"},{"en":"To recommend someone do something means to advise them to do it because it may help them.","zh":"recommend someone do something意思是建議某人做某事，因為它可能對他有幫助。"},{"en":"A careers adviser may recommend students build a portfolio before applying for design jobs.","zh":"職業顧問可能建議學生在申請設計工作前建立作品集。"},{"en":"Recommendations are useful when they come from experience.","zh":"來自經驗的建議很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces practical advice.","zh":"這個短語引入實用建議。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at some point","meaning":"在某個階段","examples":[{"en":"The speaker recommended working in retail at some point.","zh":"講者建議在某個階段從事零售工作。"},{"en":"At some point means at an unspecified time in the future or during a period.","zh":"at some point意思是在未來或某段期間中未指明的某個時間。"},{"en":"Students should practise interview skills at some point before graduation.","zh":"學生應在畢業前某個階段練習面試技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the exact time is not important.","zh":"當確切時間不重要時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It suggests something should happen eventually.","zh":"它暗示某事最終應該發生。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as a designer","meaning":"作為設計師","examples":[{"en":"Chantal thinks retail experience may help someone as a designer.","zh":"Chantal認為零售經驗可能幫助某人作為設計師。"},{"en":"As a designer means in the role or position of a designer.","zh":"as a designer意思是以設計師的角色或身份。"},{"en":"As a designer, you need to understand both beauty and practical use.","zh":"作為設計師，你需要理解美感和實際用途。"},{"en":"Experience with real customers can help someone work better as a designer.","zh":"與真實顧客接觸的經驗，可以幫助某人更好地作為設計師工作。"},{"en":"This phrase links an action or skill with a professional role.","zh":"這個短語把行動或技能與專業角色連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get to find out","meaning":"有機會了解","examples":[{"en":"Retail work helps designers get to find out useful information.","zh":"零售工作幫助設計師有機會了解有用資料。"},{"en":"To get to find out something means to have the chance to discover or learn it.","zh":"get to find out某事，意思是有機會發現或了解它。"},{"en":"A shop assistant gets to find out which colours customers avoid.","zh":"店員有機會了解顧客避開哪些顏色。"},{"en":"Direct contact with customers helps workers find out things reports may not show.","zh":"直接接觸顧客幫助工作者了解報告未必顯示的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests access to useful knowledge.","zh":"這個短語暗示能接觸到有用知識。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"useful information","meaning":"有用資料","examples":[{"en":"Retail work can give designers useful information about shoppers.","zh":"零售工作可以給設計師關於顧客的有用資料。"},{"en":"Useful information is knowledge that helps someone make better decisions or solve problems.","zh":"useful information是幫助人作出更好決定或解決問題的知識。"},{"en":"Customer comments can give a designer useful information about comfort and size.","zh":"顧客意見可以給設計師關於舒適度和尺寸的有用資料。"},{"en":"Information becomes useful when it changes what people do next.","zh":"當資料改變人下一步做法，它就變得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses practical value.","zh":"這個短語強調實用價值。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"average shopper","meaning":"一般顧客","examples":[{"en":"A designer may learn how big or small the average shopper is.","zh":"設計師可能了解一般顧客的身形大小。"},{"en":"The average shopper means the typical customer who buys from a shop or market.","zh":"average shopper意思是在商店或市場購物的典型顧客。"},{"en":"A shoe shop studies the average shopper to decide which sizes to stock.","zh":"鞋店研究一般顧客，以決定入貨哪些尺碼。"},{"en":"Understanding average shoppers helps businesses avoid designing only for unusual cases.","zh":"了解一般顧客幫助企業避免只為特殊個案設計。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a typical consumer, not one exact person.","zh":"這個短語描述典型消費者，而不是某一個人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an issue for","meaning":"……要處理的問題","examples":[{"en":"Hugo thinks shopper size is an issue for manufacturers.","zh":"Hugo認為顧客尺碼是製造商要處理的問題。"},{"en":"An issue for someone means a matter that person or group needs to deal with.","zh":"an issue for某人，意思是該人或群體需要處理的事情。"},{"en":"Storage space is an issue for small shops that receive many deliveries.","zh":"對收取大量貨物的小店來說，儲存空間是要處理的問題。"},{"en":"A problem can be an issue for one group but less relevant to another.","zh":"一個問題可以是某群體要處理的問題，但對另一群體較不相關。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who is responsible for or affected by a problem.","zh":"這個短語指出誰負責或受某問題影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"manufacturers","meaning":"製造商","examples":[{"en":"Hugo thinks clothing sizes are more relevant to manufacturers than designers.","zh":"Hugo認為服裝尺碼對製造商比對設計師更相關。"},{"en":"Manufacturers are companies or people that make products in large quantities.","zh":"manufacturers是大量製造產品的公司或人士。"},{"en":"Clothing manufacturers turn designers’ ideas into garments that can be sold in shops.","zh":"服裝製造商把設計師的想法變成可在店舖出售的衣服。"},{"en":"Manufacturers need accurate measurements because mistakes can waste material and money.","zh":"製造商需要準確量度，因為錯誤會浪費材料和金錢。"},{"en":"This word refers to product makers, not usually shop staff.","zh":"這個詞指產品製作者，通常不是店員。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a gap in the market","meaning":"市場缺口","examples":[{"en":"Retail work can help designers notice a gap in the market.","zh":"零售工作可以幫助設計師注意到市場缺口。"},{"en":"A gap in the market is an unmet customer need that businesses are not yet serving well.","zh":"a gap in the market是企業尚未好好滿足的顧客需要。"},{"en":"A shop may find a gap in the market for stylish clothes in larger sizes.","zh":"店舖可能發現市場上缺少大碼而時尚的衣服。"},{"en":"Finding a market gap can lead to a new product or business idea.","zh":"找到市場缺口可以帶來新產品或商業構想。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business and product design.","zh":"這個短語常見於商業和產品設計。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"no one is stocking","meaning":"沒有人入貨","examples":[{"en":"A gap exists when no one is stocking an item consumers want.","zh":"當沒有人入貨消費者想要的物品時，就存在市場缺口。"},{"en":"No one is stocking something means no shop is keeping or selling that product.","zh":"no one is stocking某物，意思是沒有店舖存貨或售賣該產品。"},{"en":"Customers may ask for a certain school bag, but no local shop is stocking it.","zh":"顧客可能詢問某款書包，但本地沒有店舖入貨。"},{"en":"If no one stocks a product people want, a business opportunity may exist.","zh":"如果沒有人入貨人們想要的產品，就可能存在商機。"},{"en":"This phrase connects supply with customer demand.","zh":"這個短語把供應與顧客需求連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"consumers are looking for","meaning":"消費者正在尋找","examples":[{"en":"A gap in the market may involve an item consumers are looking for.","zh":"市場缺口可能涉及消費者正在尋找的物品。"},{"en":"Consumers are looking for something means buyers want it and are trying to find it.","zh":"consumers are looking for某物，意思是買家想要並正在嘗試找到它。"},{"en":"Parents may be looking for affordable school shoes that last more than one term.","zh":"家長可能正在尋找可負擔而能穿超過一個學期的校鞋。"},{"en":"When many consumers look for the same missing product, businesses may create it.","zh":"當許多消費者尋找同一種缺失產品，企業可能會創造它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active customer demand.","zh":"這個短語描述積極的顧客需求。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"give up searching","meaning":"放棄尋找","examples":[{"en":"Chantal says consumers do not give up searching for what they want.","zh":"Chantal說消費者不會放棄尋找自己想要的東西。"},{"en":"To give up searching means to stop trying to find something.","zh":"give up searching意思是停止嘗試尋找某物。"},{"en":"A student may give up searching for a book if every library copy is already borrowed.","zh":"如果每本圖書館藏書都已借出，學生可能放棄尋找那本書。"},{"en":"If customers do not give up searching, it shows strong demand.","zh":"如果顧客不放棄尋找，就顯示需求強烈。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stopping an effort to find something.","zh":"這個短語描述停止尋找的努力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take things back to","meaning":"將東西退回……","examples":[{"en":"Consumers take things back to the store if they are not right.","zh":"如果東西不合適，消費者會將它們退回商店。"},{"en":"To take things back to a store means to return bought items there.","zh":"take things back to a store意思是把已購買物品退回那裡。"},{"en":"A customer may take shoes back to the shop if the size is wrong.","zh":"如果鞋子尺碼不對，顧客可能把鞋退回店舖。"},{"en":"Frequent returns can show that a product has quality or fit problems.","zh":"頻繁退貨可以顯示產品有質素或合身問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in shopping situations.","zh":"這個短語常見於購物情境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"expensive shop","meaning":"高級商店","examples":[{"en":"Hugo imagines working in an expensive shop.","zh":"Hugo想像在高級商店工作。"},{"en":"An expensive shop is a shop that sells high-priced goods.","zh":"expensive shop是出售高價商品的店舖。"},{"en":"An expensive shop may offer designer clothes, luxury bags or personal service.","zh":"高級商店可能售賣設計師服裝、奢侈手袋或提供個人化服務。"},{"en":"Customers in expensive shops often expect high quality and careful attention.","zh":"高級商店的顧客通常期望高質素和細心服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both price level and shop image.","zh":"這個短語同時描述價格水平和店舖形象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"find out","meaning":"發現；查明","examples":[{"en":"A retail worker may find out why garments are being returned.","zh":"零售員可能查明衣服為何被退回。"},{"en":"To find out means to discover information by asking, checking or observing.","zh":"find out意思是透過提問、檢查或觀察發現資訊。"},{"en":"A teacher may find out why students are confused by looking at their answers.","zh":"老師可能透過查看學生答案，查明他們為何困惑。"},{"en":"Finding out the cause of a problem helps people fix it properly.","zh":"查明問題原因有助人正確解決它。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on discovering the truth.","zh":"這個短語著重發現真相。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"garments","meaning":"衣服","examples":[{"en":"The garments sold in the shop were being returned.","zh":"店內售賣的衣服正在被退回。"},{"en":"Garments are pieces of clothing, especially when spoken about in a business or fashion context.","zh":"garments是衣物，尤其在商業或時裝語境中使用。"},{"en":"A designer checks each garment before it is sent to the shop.","zh":"設計師會在每件衣服送到店舖前檢查。"},{"en":"Poorly made garments may tear, shrink or lose shape after washing.","zh":"製作差劣的衣服洗後可能撕裂、縮水或變形。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “clothes”.","zh":"這個詞比clothes更正式。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be returned","meaning":"被退回","examples":[{"en":"The garments were being returned because they fell apart in the wash.","zh":"那些衣服因洗完後散開而被退回。"},{"en":"To be returned means to be taken or sent back to the place where it was bought or received.","zh":"be returned意思是被帶回或送回購買或收到的地方。"},{"en":"A faulty phone may be returned to the shop for a refund.","zh":"有問題的手機可能被退回商店退款。"},{"en":"Products are often returned when they do not work, fit or match expectations.","zh":"當產品不能運作、不合身或不符合期望時，通常會被退回。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in shopping and customer service.","zh":"這個短語常見於購物和客戶服務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fall apart in the wash","meaning":"洗完後散開；洗壞","examples":[{"en":"The garments fell apart in the wash.","zh":"那些衣服洗完後散開。"},{"en":"To fall apart in the wash means to break, tear or lose shape after being washed.","zh":"fall apart in the wash意思是洗完後破裂、撕開或變形。"},{"en":"A cheap T-shirt may fall apart in the wash if the stitching is weak.","zh":"如果縫線脆弱，便宜T恤可能洗完後散開。"},{"en":"Clothes that fall apart after washing suggest poor quality or wrong materials.","zh":"洗後散開的衣服顯示質素差或材料不合適。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical clothing problem customers notice quickly.","zh":"這個短語描述顧客很快會注意到的實際衣物問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"that kind of thing","meaning":"那類事情","examples":[{"en":"Chantal agrees that it would be useful to know that kind of thing.","zh":"Chantal同意知道那類事情會很有用。"},{"en":"That kind of thing means information, examples or situations similar to what has just been mentioned.","zh":"that kind of thing意思是與剛提到內容相似的資訊、例子或情況。"},{"en":"A designer should know why customers return clothes, complain about sizes and avoid certain fabrics, that kind of thing.","zh":"設計師應知道顧客為何退貨、投訴尺碼和避開某些布料，那類事情。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and avoids listing every detail.","zh":"這個短語較口語，避免列出每個細節。"},{"en":"It is useful when the listener already understands the general category.","zh":"當聽者已理解大致類別時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 3.pdf","sourcePage":11}],"ielts/listening/Practice 9/task-4":[{"front":"presentation","meaning":"簡報；匯報","examples":[{"en":"The student gives a presentation about how groups of elephants are moved.","zh":"這名學生就大象群如何被遷移作簡報。"},{"en":"A presentation is a talk that explains information, research, or ideas to an audience.","zh":"presentation 指向觀眾解釋資料、研究或想法的演講。"},{"en":"Students may give a presentation with photos, maps, and short notes.","zh":"學生可能用照片、地圖和簡短筆記作匯報。"},{"en":"A clear presentation helps listeners understand a difficult process step by step.","zh":"清晰的簡報能幫助聽眾逐步理解複雜過程。"},{"en":"This word is often used in school, university, and workplace tasks.","zh":"這個字常用於學校、大學和工作任務。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"groups of elephants","meaning":"大象群","examples":[{"en":"The presentation explains how groups of elephants have been moved.","zh":"這個簡報解釋大象群如何被遷移。"},{"en":"Groups of elephants are several elephants living, travelling, or being managed together.","zh":"groups of elephants 指一起生活、移動或被管理的多隻大象。"},{"en":"A wildlife guide may show tourists groups of elephants near a waterhole.","zh":"野生動物導遊可能帶遊客看水塘附近的大象群。"},{"en":"If groups of elephants are moved together, family bonds can be protected.","zh":"如果大象群一起被遷移，牠們的家庭連繫可以受到保護。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to elephants as social units, not isolated animals.","zh":"這個短語指作為社群單位的大象，而不是單獨動物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be moved and settled in","meaning":"被遷移並安置於……","examples":[{"en":"Groups of elephants have been moved and settled in new reserves.","zh":"大象群已被遷移並安置於新的保護區。"},{"en":"To be moved and settled in a place means to be taken there and helped to live there safely.","zh":"be moved and settled in a place 指被帶到某地，並被協助在那裡安全生活。"},{"en":"Families displaced by floods may be moved and settled in temporary housing.","zh":"因水災流離失所的家庭可能被遷移並安置於臨時房屋。"},{"en":"If animals are moved but not settled in properly, they may become stressed or leave the area.","zh":"如果動物只被遷移而沒有妥善安置，牠們可能受壓或離開該地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both relocation and adjustment after arrival.","zh":"這個短語同時描述遷移和抵達後的適應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"new reserves","meaning":"新保護區","examples":[{"en":"The elephants were settled in new reserves.","zh":"大象被安置於新的保護區。"},{"en":"New reserves are newly chosen or prepared protected areas for wildlife.","zh":"new reserves 指新選定或新準備好的野生動物保護區。"},{"en":"A government may create new reserves to protect birds, forests, or endangered animals.","zh":"政府可能建立新保護區來保護鳥類、森林或瀕危動物。"},{"en":"If new reserves have enough food and water, animals can live there more safely.","zh":"如果新保護區有足夠食物和水，動物就能更安全生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protected places prepared for conservation.","zh":"這個短語描述為保育而準備的受保護地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be known as","meaning":"被稱為……","examples":[{"en":"This process is known as translocation.","zh":"這個過程被稱為遷地轉移。"},{"en":"To be known as something means to be called or recognised by that name.","zh":"be known as something 指被稱作或被認識為某個名稱。"},{"en":"Hong Kong is known as a city with a busy harbour and tall buildings.","zh":"香港被稱為一個有繁忙海港和高樓大廈的城市。"},{"en":"If a process is known as a technical term, students may need a simple explanation of it.","zh":"如果某過程被稱為專業術語，學生可能需要簡單解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a name or label.","zh":"這個短語引出名稱或標籤。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"translocation","meaning":"遷地轉移","examples":[{"en":"Translocation has been carried out in Malawi in recent years.","zh":"近年來，馬拉維進行了遷地轉移。"},{"en":"Translocation is the process of moving animals or plants from one place to another for conservation.","zh":"translocation 指為了保育而把動物或植物從一個地方遷到另一個地方的過程。"},{"en":"Scientists may use translocation when a species has too many animals in one area and too few in another.","zh":"當某物種在一個地區太多、另一個地區太少時，科學家可能使用遷地轉移。"},{"en":"If translocation is planned badly, animals may suffer stress or fail to adapt.","zh":"如果遷地轉移規劃不當，動物可能受壓或未能適應。"},{"en":"This word describes a managed conservation move.","zh":"這個字描述受管理的保育遷移。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be carried out","meaning":"被進行；被實施","examples":[{"en":"Elephant translocation has been carried out in Malawi.","zh":"大象遷地轉移已在馬拉維被實施。"},{"en":"To be carried out means to be done, performed, or put into action.","zh":"be carried out 指某事被完成、執行或付諸實行。"},{"en":"A safety inspection is carried out before a school trip begins.","zh":"學校旅行開始前會進行安全檢查。"},{"en":"If a plan is carried out carefully, problems can be reduced.","zh":"如果計劃被仔細執行，問題可以減少。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for official work, research, and projects.","zh":"這個短語常用於官方工作、研究和項目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in recent years","meaning":"近年來","examples":[{"en":"Translocation has been carried out in Malawi in recent years.","zh":"近年來，馬拉維進行了遷地轉移。"},{"en":"In recent years means during the last few years, not long ago.","zh":"in recent years 指在過去幾年，即不久以前的一段時間。"},{"en":"In recent years, many schools have used more online learning tools.","zh":"近年來，許多學校使用更多網上學習工具。"},{"en":"If a problem has grown in recent years, people may need new solutions.","zh":"如果問題近年來加劇，人們可能需要新解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event in the near past.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在較近的過去。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"overpopulation","meaning":"數量過多；過度繁殖","examples":[{"en":"Overpopulation of elephants caused problems in some areas.","zh":"大象數量過多在一些地區造成問題。"},{"en":"Overpopulation happens when there are too many living things in one place for the available space or resources.","zh":"overpopulation 指某地方的生物數量超過可用空間或資源所能承受。"},{"en":"A classroom can feel overcrowded if too many students are put into one room.","zh":"如果太多學生被安排在同一課室，課室會顯得過分擠迫。"},{"en":"Overpopulation can lead to food shortages, stress, and damage to the environment.","zh":"數量過多可以導致食物短缺、壓力和環境破壞。"},{"en":"This word describes a number that has become too high for an area to support.","zh":"這個字描述某地區承受不了的過高數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a good problem to have","meaning":"好問題；值得高興的問題","examples":[{"en":"Overpopulation is a good problem to have.","zh":"大象數量過多是一個值得高興的問題。"},{"en":"A good problem to have is still a problem, but it comes from success rather than failure.","zh":"a good problem to have 指雖然仍是問題，但它源於成功而不是失敗。"},{"en":"A school having too many students applying is a good problem to have because it shows popularity.","zh":"學校收到太多學生申請是一個好問題，因為這顯示它受歡迎。"},{"en":"If a charity receives too many donations to store, it has a good problem to have.","zh":"如果慈善機構收到太多捐贈而無處存放，它就是遇上一個好問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the situation is difficult but also positive.","zh":"這個短語暗示情況有困難，但同時正面。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tend to hear about","meaning":"往往會聽到","examples":[{"en":"Overpopulation of elephants is not something we tend to hear about very often.","zh":"大象數量過多並不是我們很常聽到的事情。"},{"en":"To tend to hear about something means to usually or commonly hear people mention it.","zh":"tend to hear about something 指通常或經常聽到人們提及某事。"},{"en":"We tend to hear about traffic jams more than quiet, well-run bus services.","zh":"我們往往較常聽到交通擠塞，而不是安靜又運作良好的巴士服務。"},{"en":"If people do not tend to hear about a problem, it may surprise them when they learn about it.","zh":"如果人們不常聽到某問題，了解它時可能會感到意外。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what is commonly discussed.","zh":"這個短語描述通常被討論的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"elephant population","meaning":"大象族群","examples":[{"en":"The elephant population in Majete National Park had been wiped out.","zh":"Majete National Park 的大象族群曾被消滅。"},{"en":"Elephant population means the number or group of elephants living in a particular area.","zh":"elephant population 指生活在特定地區的大象數量或群體。"},{"en":"Scientists count the elephant population to see whether conservation is working.","zh":"科學家點算大象族群，以了解保育是否有效。"},{"en":"If the elephant population grows too fast, food and space may become limited.","zh":"如果大象族群增長太快，食物和空間可能變得有限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes elephants as a living group in one place.","zh":"這個短語把大象描述為一個地方中的生物群體。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be wiped out by","meaning":"被……消滅","examples":[{"en":"The elephant population had been wiped out by poachers.","zh":"大象族群曾被偷獵者消滅。"},{"en":"To be wiped out by someone or something means to be completely destroyed or removed by them.","zh":"be wiped out by someone or something 指被某人或某事完全摧毀或清除。"},{"en":"A small shop may be wiped out by rising rent and falling sales.","zh":"小店可能被租金上升和銷售下跌摧毀。"},{"en":"If a disease wipes out crops, farmers may lose their income.","zh":"如果疾病摧毀農作物，農民可能失去收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe or complete loss caused by a force.","zh":"這個短語描述由某種力量造成的嚴重或完全損失。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"poachers","meaning":"偷獵者","examples":[{"en":"Poachers killed the elephants for their ivory.","zh":"偷獵者為了象牙而殺害大象。"},{"en":"Poachers are people who illegally hunt or capture wild animals.","zh":"poachers 指非法獵捕野生動物的人。"},{"en":"Park rangers may patrol at night to stop poachers from entering a reserve.","zh":"公園巡護員可能在夜間巡邏，以阻止偷獵者進入保護區。"},{"en":"Poachers can damage wildlife populations and threaten endangered species.","zh":"偷獵者可以破壞野生動物族群，並威脅瀕危物種。"},{"en":"This word describes illegal hunters, not legal wildlife managers.","zh":"這個字描述非法獵人，而不是合法野生動物管理人員。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ivory","meaning":"象牙","examples":[{"en":"Poachers killed elephants for their ivory.","zh":"偷獵者為了象牙而殺害大象。"},{"en":"Ivory is the hard white material from elephant tusks.","zh":"ivory 指來自大象象牙的堅硬白色材料。"},{"en":"Some old ornaments were made from ivory, but trading it can harm elephants.","zh":"有些舊擺設由象牙製成，但象牙貿易可能傷害大象。"},{"en":"If demand for ivory rises, elephants may face a greater risk of being killed.","zh":"如果象牙需求上升，大象被殺害的風險可能增加。"},{"en":"This word is strongly connected with wildlife crime and conservation.","zh":"這個字與野生動物罪案和保育密切相關。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be restocked","meaning":"重新引入動物","examples":[{"en":"The park was restocked with elephants in 2003.","zh":"這個公園在2003年重新引入大象。"},{"en":"To be restocked with animals means to have animals brought back into an area where they had disappeared or declined.","zh":"be restocked with animals 指把動物重新帶回牠們曾消失或數量下降的地方。"},{"en":"A fish pond may be restocked after pollution kills many fish.","zh":"如果污染殺死很多魚，魚塘可能重新投放魚苗。"},{"en":"If a reserve is restocked carefully, the animal population can recover.","zh":"如果保護區被小心重新引入動物，動物族群可以恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rebuilding a population by adding animals.","zh":"這個短語描述透過加入動物來重建族群。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"effective law enforcement","meaning":"有效執法","examples":[{"en":"Effective law enforcement was introduced in the park.","zh":"公園引入了有效執法。"},{"en":"Effective law enforcement means laws are actively and successfully used to stop illegal behaviour.","zh":"effective law enforcement 指法律被積極而成功地執行，以阻止非法行為。"},{"en":"Effective law enforcement can reduce speeding if police check dangerous roads regularly.","zh":"如果警方定期檢查危險道路，有效執法可以減少超速。"},{"en":"In a wildlife park, effective law enforcement can stop poachers and protect animals.","zh":"在野生動物公園中，有效執法可以阻止偷獵者並保護動物。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that rules must be enforced, not just written.","zh":"這個短語強調規則不只是寫下來，還必須被執行。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be introduced","meaning":"被引入；被實施","examples":[{"en":"Effective law enforcement was introduced in 2003.","zh":"有效執法在2003年被引入。"},{"en":"To be introduced means to be brought in or started for the first time.","zh":"be introduced 指某制度、規則或做法被首次帶入或開始。"},{"en":"A new school lunch system was introduced after students complained about long queues.","zh":"學生投訴排隊太久後，學校引入了新的午餐制度。"},{"en":"If a safety rule is introduced, staff need to learn how to follow it.","zh":"如果安全規則被引入，員工需要學會如何遵守。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the start of a new system, rule, or practice.","zh":"這個短語描述新制度、規則或做法的開始。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not a single","meaning":"連一個也沒有","examples":[{"en":"Since then, not a single elephant has been poached.","zh":"自那時起，連一隻大象也沒有被偷獵。"},{"en":"Not a single means not even one.","zh":"not a single 指連一個也沒有。"},{"en":"Not a single student arrived late after the school changed the bus schedule.","zh":"學校更改巴士時間表後，連一名學生也沒有遲到。"},{"en":"If not a single case happens after new rules begin, the rules may be working well.","zh":"如果新規則開始後連一宗個案也沒有發生，規則可能很有效。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises zero.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調零。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be poached","meaning":"被偷獵","examples":[{"en":"Not a single elephant has been poached since then.","zh":"自那時起，沒有一隻大象被偷獵。"},{"en":"To be poached means to be illegally hunted or killed, usually for valuable body parts.","zh":"be poached 指被非法獵捕或殺害，通常是為了有價值的身體部位。"},{"en":"Rhinos may be poached for their horns if law enforcement is weak.","zh":"如果執法薄弱，犀牛可能因犀牛角而被偷獵。"},{"en":"If animals are poached, their population can fall quickly.","zh":"如果動物被偷獵，其族群數量可能迅速下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes illegal hunting, not normal wildlife management.","zh":"這個短語描述非法獵殺，而不是正常野生動物管理。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"safe environment","meaning":"安全環境","examples":[{"en":"The elephant population boomed in this safe environment.","zh":"大象族群在這個安全環境中迅速增加。"},{"en":"A safe environment is a place where people or animals are protected from serious danger.","zh":"safe environment 指人或動物受到保護、免受嚴重危險的地方。"},{"en":"Children learn better in a safe environment where they are not afraid to ask questions.","zh":"孩子在不害怕提問的安全環境中學得更好。"},{"en":"If animals live in a safe environment, they may breed and grow in number.","zh":"如果動物生活在安全環境中，牠們可能繁殖並增加數量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes surroundings that support survival and confidence.","zh":"這個短語描述有助生存和建立信心的環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"boom","meaning":"迅速增加；急速增長","examples":[{"en":"In this safe environment, the elephant population boomed.","zh":"在這個安全環境中，大象族群迅速增加。"},{"en":"To boom means to grow or increase very quickly.","zh":"boom 指快速增長或增加。"},{"en":"Online shopping boomed when many people stayed at home.","zh":"當很多人留在家中時，網上購物急速增長。"},{"en":"If a population booms, food, space, and planning may become important issues.","zh":"如果族群迅速增加，食物、空間和規劃可能成為重要問題。"},{"en":"This word describes rapid growth.","zh":"這個字描述快速增長。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"breeding went well","meaning":"繁殖情況良好","examples":[{"en":"Breeding went so well that the park could not support all the elephants.","zh":"繁殖情況非常好，以致公園無法供養所有大象。"},{"en":"Breeding went well means animals reproduced successfully and produced many young.","zh":"breeding went well 指動物繁殖成功，產下很多幼崽。"},{"en":"A farm may say breeding went well if many healthy calves are born.","zh":"如果許多健康小牛出生，農場可能說繁殖情況良好。"},{"en":"If breeding goes too well in a limited area, the population may become too large.","zh":"如果有限地區內繁殖太成功，族群數量可能變得過大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes successful reproduction.","zh":"這個短語描述成功繁殖。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"more...than...could support","meaning":"多於……能承受的數量","examples":[{"en":"There were more elephants than the park could support.","zh":"大象數量多於公園能承受的數量。"},{"en":"More...than...could support means the number was greater than the resources or space available.","zh":"more...than...could support 指數量超過可用資源或空間所能承受。"},{"en":"A small classroom may have more students than it can support comfortably.","zh":"小課室的學生可能多於它能舒適容納的數量。"},{"en":"If a town has more cars than its roads can support, traffic jams become common.","zh":"如果城鎮汽車數量多於道路能承受，交通擠塞會變得常見。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that demand is beyond capacity.","zh":"這個短語顯示需求超出承載能力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致；帶來","examples":[{"en":"This led to a number of problems.","zh":"這導致了一些問題。"},{"en":"To lead to something means to cause it or make it happen.","zh":"lead to something 指導致某事或令某事發生。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can lead to weak concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致上課專注力差。"},{"en":"If a park has too many animals, it can lead to food shortages.","zh":"如果公園有太多動物，可能導致食物短缺。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with a result.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a number of problems","meaning":"一些問題","examples":[{"en":"The growing elephant population led to a number of problems.","zh":"不斷增長的大象族群帶來了一些問題。"},{"en":"A number of problems means several difficulties or issues.","zh":"a number of problems 指幾個困難或議題。"},{"en":"A school trip can face a number of problems if transport and food are not planned well.","zh":"如果交通和食物沒有計劃好，學校旅行可能面對一些問題。"},{"en":"If several problems happen together, managers need to decide which one is most urgent.","zh":"如果幾個問題同時出現，管理者需要決定哪一個最緊急。"},{"en":"This phrase describes more than one problem.","zh":"這個短語描述不止一個問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"competition for food","meaning":"食物競爭","examples":[{"en":"There was more competition for food among the elephants.","zh":"大象之間出現更多食物競爭。"},{"en":"Competition for food happens when many animals or people need the same limited food supply.","zh":"competition for food 指許多動物或人需要同一有限食物供應。"},{"en":"In a crowded canteen, students may face competition for the last few lunch sets.","zh":"在擠迫飯堂中，學生可能為最後幾份午餐而競爭。"},{"en":"If competition for food increases, weaker animals may suffer first.","zh":"如果食物競爭加劇，較弱的動物可能最先受苦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pressure caused by limited food.","zh":"這個短語描述由食物有限造成的壓力。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"suffer from hunger","meaning":"捱餓；受飢餓之苦","examples":[{"en":"Some elephants were suffering from hunger.","zh":"有些大象正受飢餓之苦。"},{"en":"To suffer from hunger means to experience pain, weakness, or poor health because there is not enough food.","zh":"suffer from hunger 指因食物不足而感到痛苦、虛弱或健康變差。"},{"en":"Families may suffer from hunger when food prices rise and incomes fall.","zh":"當食物價格上升而收入下降，家庭可能捱餓。"},{"en":"If animals suffer from hunger, they may search for food outside safe areas.","zh":"如果動物受飢餓之苦，牠們可能到安全區域外尋找食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the harmful result of not having enough to eat.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有足夠食物的有害結果。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a limit to","meaning":"……的限制","examples":[{"en":"There was a limit to the amount of food in the national park.","zh":"國家公園內的食物數量有限制。"},{"en":"A limit to something means there is only a certain amount or level available.","zh":"a limit to something 指某事只有一定數量或程度可用。"},{"en":"There is a limit to how many books a student can borrow at one time.","zh":"學生一次可借的書本數量有限制。"},{"en":"If there is a limit to food, a growing population may face shortages.","zh":"如果食物有限，增長中的族群可能面對短缺。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is not unlimited.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事並非無限。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the amount of food","meaning":"食物數量","examples":[{"en":"The amount of food in the national park was limited.","zh":"國家公園內的食物數量有限。"},{"en":"The amount of food means the quantity of food available.","zh":"the amount of food 指可用食物的數量。"},{"en":"A family checks the amount of food in the fridge before going shopping.","zh":"家庭去購物前會查看雪櫃裡的食物數量。"},{"en":"If the amount of food is too small for a group, some people or animals may go hungry.","zh":"如果食物數量對一個群體來說太少，有些人或動物可能會捱餓。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how much food there is.","zh":"這個短語重點在有多少食物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"national park","meaning":"國家公園","examples":[{"en":"Majete National Park had more elephants than it could support.","zh":"Majete National Park 的大象數量多於它能承受的數量。"},{"en":"A national park is a protected natural area managed for wildlife, scenery, and public enjoyment.","zh":"national park 指為保護野生動物、景色和公眾欣賞而管理的自然保護區。"},{"en":"Families may visit a national park to hike, watch birds, or learn about nature.","zh":"家庭可能到國家公園遠足、觀鳥或學習自然知識。"},{"en":"If a national park is well managed, it can protect animals and attract visitors.","zh":"如果國家公園管理良好，它可以保護動物並吸引訪客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a protected area of national importance.","zh":"這個短語描述具國家重要性的受保護地區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"look further afield","meaning":"到更遠地方尋找","examples":[{"en":"Some elephants began looking further afield for food.","zh":"有些大象開始到更遠地方尋找食物。"},{"en":"To look further afield means to search in places farther away from the usual area.","zh":"look further afield 指到比平常範圍更遠的地方尋找。"},{"en":"If a student cannot find a book in the school library, she may look further afield in public libraries.","zh":"如果學生在學校圖書館找不到書，她可能到公共圖書館等更遠地方尋找。"},{"en":"When local jobs are limited, workers may look further afield for better opportunities.","zh":"當本地工作有限，工人可能到更遠地方尋找更好機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes searching beyond the nearby area.","zh":"這個短語描述超出附近範圍的搜尋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"routinely","meaning":"經常地；例行地","examples":[{"en":"Elephants were routinely knocking down fences around the park.","zh":"大象經常撞倒公園周圍的圍欄。"},{"en":"Routinely means regularly or as part of a repeated pattern.","zh":"routinely 指定期地，或作為重複模式的一部分。"},{"en":"Nurses routinely check patients’ temperature in the morning.","zh":"護士早上會例行檢查病人體溫。"},{"en":"If a problem happens routinely, it is not a one-off accident.","zh":"如果問題經常發生，它就不是一次性意外。"},{"en":"This word describes something that happens again and again.","zh":"這個字描述一再發生的事情。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"knock down fences","meaning":"撞倒圍欄","examples":[{"en":"Elephants were knocking down fences around the park.","zh":"大象正在撞倒公園周圍的圍欄。"},{"en":"To knock down fences means to push or break fences so that they fall.","zh":"knock down fences 指推倒或撞壞圍欄，使它們倒下。"},{"en":"A strong storm can knock down fences in a village.","zh":"強烈風暴可以吹倒村裡的圍欄。"},{"en":"If animals knock down fences, they may leave protected areas and enter farms.","zh":"如果動物撞倒圍欄，牠們可能離開保護區並進入農地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical damage to barriers.","zh":"這個短語描述對屏障的實體破壞。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"around the park","meaning":"在公園周圍","examples":[{"en":"The fences around the park had to be repaired.","zh":"公園周圍的圍欄必須被修復。"},{"en":"Around the park means surrounding or located along the edges of the park.","zh":"around the park 指圍繞公園或位於公園邊界一帶。"},{"en":"Signs around the park tell visitors where they can walk safely.","zh":"公園周圍的標誌告訴訪客哪裡可以安全步行。"},{"en":"If fences around a park are broken, animals may move in or out freely.","zh":"如果公園周圍的圍欄破損，動物可能自由進出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the area surrounding a park.","zh":"這個短語描述公園周邊範圍。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be repaired","meaning":"被修復","examples":[{"en":"The fences had to be repaired at a significant cost.","zh":"這些圍欄必須以高昂成本被修復。"},{"en":"To be repaired means to be fixed after being damaged or broken.","zh":"be repaired 指在受損或壞掉後被修理。"},{"en":"A school gate must be repaired if it no longer closes properly.","zh":"如果學校大門不能正常關上，就必須被修復。"},{"en":"If equipment is repaired quickly, work can continue with less delay.","zh":"如果設備很快被修復，工作就能少受延誤地繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes restoring something to working condition.","zh":"這個短語描述把某物恢復到可用狀態。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at a significant cost","meaning":"以高昂成本","examples":[{"en":"The fences had to be repaired at a significant cost.","zh":"這些圍欄必須以高昂成本修復。"},{"en":"At a significant cost means with a large amount of money, effort, or loss involved.","zh":"at a significant cost 指涉及大量金錢、努力或損失。"},{"en":"A school may repair an old roof at a significant cost after years of leaks.","zh":"學校可能在多年漏水後，以高昂成本修理舊屋頂。"},{"en":"If damage happens repeatedly, repairs at a significant cost can strain a budget.","zh":"如果損壞反覆發生，高昂維修成本可能令預算受壓。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the price is not small.","zh":"這個短語強調代價不小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"to solve this problem","meaning":"為了解決這個問題","examples":[{"en":"To solve this problem, the decision was made to move dozens of elephants.","zh":"為了解決這個問題，人們決定遷移數十隻大象。"},{"en":"To solve this problem means in order to fix or reduce the difficulty just mentioned.","zh":"to solve this problem 指為了修正或減少剛提到的困難。"},{"en":"To solve this problem, the school added another lunch queue.","zh":"為了解決這個問題，學校增設了一條午餐隊伍。"},{"en":"If a solution addresses the real cause, it is more likely to solve the problem.","zh":"如果解決方法處理真正原因，就較可能解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the purpose of an action.","zh":"這個短語引出行動目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the decision was made to","meaning":"人們決定……","examples":[{"en":"The decision was made to move elephants to Nkhotakota Wildlife Park.","zh":"人們決定把大象遷到 Nkhotakota Wildlife Park。"},{"en":"The decision was made to do something means people officially decided to do it.","zh":"the decision was made to do something 指人們正式決定做某事。"},{"en":"After many complaints, the decision was made to change the school bus route.","zh":"在收到許多投訴後，人們決定更改校巴路線。"},{"en":"If the decision is made after careful study, people may trust it more.","zh":"如果決定是在仔細研究後作出，人們可能更信任它。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and is often used in reports.","zh":"這個短語語氣正式，常用於報告中。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dozens of","meaning":"數十……","examples":[{"en":"Dozens of elephants were moved from Majete National Park.","zh":"數十隻大象從 Majete National Park 被遷走。"},{"en":"Dozens of means many, usually several groups of twelve or roughly twenty-four or more.","zh":"dozens of 指許多，通常是幾組十二個，或約二十四個以上。"},{"en":"Dozens of students joined the school clean-up after the typhoon.","zh":"颱風後，數十名學生參加學校清潔活動。"},{"en":"If dozens of animals are moved, planning and transport become complicated.","zh":"如果數十隻動物被遷移，規劃和運輸會變得複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large but not exact number.","zh":"這個短語描述大量但不精確的數目。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"wildlife park","meaning":"野生動物公園","examples":[{"en":"The elephants were moved to Nkhotakota Wildlife Park.","zh":"大象被遷移到 Nkhotakota Wildlife Park。"},{"en":"A wildlife park is a protected area where wild animals live and are managed.","zh":"wildlife park 指野生動物生活並受管理的保護區。"},{"en":"Families may visit a wildlife park to see animals in a more natural setting than a zoo.","zh":"家庭可能到野生動物公園，在比動物園更自然的環境中看動物。"},{"en":"If a wildlife park is well protected, animals can breed safely there.","zh":"如果野生動物公園受到良好保護，動物可以在那裡安全繁殖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place for wildlife conservation and public education.","zh":"這個短語描述用於野生動物保育和公眾教育的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"attempt to","meaning":"嘗試……","examples":[{"en":"The team attempted to move many elephants to a new home.","zh":"團隊嘗試把許多大象遷到新家園。"},{"en":"To attempt to do something means to try to do it, especially when it is difficult.","zh":"attempt to do something 指嘗試做某事，尤其是困難的事。"},{"en":"A student may attempt to solve a hard maths question before asking the teacher.","zh":"學生可能先嘗試解一道困難數學題，再問老師。"},{"en":"If a team attempts a risky project, it needs careful preparation.","zh":"如果團隊嘗試高風險項目，就需要仔細準備。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses effort rather than guaranteed success.","zh":"這個短語強調努力，而不是保證成功。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"significant numbers of","meaning":"大量的……","examples":[{"en":"Moving significant numbers of elephants was a major challenge.","zh":"遷移大量大象是一項重大挑戰。"},{"en":"Significant numbers of something means many enough to matter or create an effect.","zh":"significant numbers of something 指數量多到重要或會造成影響。"},{"en":"Significant numbers of students were absent when flu spread through the school.","zh":"當流感在學校傳播時，大量學生缺席。"},{"en":"If significant numbers of workers leave, a company may struggle to operate.","zh":"如果大量員工離職，公司可能難以運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large and important quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述龐大而重要的數量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a new home","meaning":"新家園；新棲地","examples":[{"en":"The elephants were moved to a new home 300 kilometres away.","zh":"大象被遷移到300公里外的新家園。"},{"en":"A new home is a new place where people or animals can live.","zh":"a new home 指人或動物可以生活的新地方。"},{"en":"A rescued dog may need time to feel safe in a new home.","zh":"獲救的狗可能需要時間在新家感到安全。"},{"en":"If animals are moved to a new home, they must find food, water, and safe routes.","zh":"如果動物被遷到新棲地，牠們必須找到食物、水源和安全路線。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe a new living place, not only a house.","zh":"這個短語可以描述新的生活地方，不只是房屋。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"quite a challenge","meaning":"相當大的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Moving elephants 300 kilometres away is quite a challenge.","zh":"把大象遷到300公里外是相當大的挑戰。"},{"en":"Quite a challenge means a fairly difficult task that needs effort and planning.","zh":"quite a challenge 指相當困難、需要努力和規劃的任務。"},{"en":"Organising a school concert with hundreds of students is quite a challenge.","zh":"組織有數百名學生參與的學校音樂會是相當大的挑戰。"},{"en":"If a task involves safety, transport, and timing, it can be quite a challenge.","zh":"如果任務涉及安全、運輸和時間安排，它可以是相當大的挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is not easy.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事並不容易。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"process work in practice","meaning":"過程實際上如何運作","examples":[{"en":"The speaker explains how the translocation process worked in practice.","zh":"講者解釋遷地轉移過程實際上如何運作。"},{"en":"How a process works in practice means how it actually happens in real life.","zh":"how a process works in practice 指一個過程在現實中實際如何發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain how exam marking works in practice by showing sample answers.","zh":"老師可能透過展示樣本答案，解釋考試評分實際上如何運作。"},{"en":"If a plan sounds simple on paper, seeing how it works in practice may reveal difficulties.","zh":"如果計劃在紙上看似簡單，了解它實際如何運作可能會揭示困難。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real operation with theory.","zh":"這個短語把實際運作與理論作對比。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in groups of between...and...","meaning":"以……至……為一組","examples":[{"en":"Elephants were moved in groups of between eight and twenty.","zh":"大象以八至二十隻為一組被遷移。"},{"en":"In groups of between eight and twenty means each group had at least eight and at most twenty members.","zh":"in groups of between eight and twenty 指每組最少八個、最多二十個成員。"},{"en":"Students may work in groups of between three and five for a class project.","zh":"學生做課堂專題時，可能以三至五人為一組。"},{"en":"If animals are moved in groups of a suitable size, they may feel safer and easier to manage.","zh":"如果動物以合適大小的組別遷移，牠們可能較安全，也較易管理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes group size within a range.","zh":"這個短語描述某範圍內的組別大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"belong to","meaning":"屬於……","examples":[{"en":"The elephants in each group all belonged to one family.","zh":"每組大象都屬於同一個家庭。"},{"en":"To belong to a group means to be a member or part of that group.","zh":"belong to a group 指是某群體的成員或一部分。"},{"en":"A student may belong to the school orchestra and the debate club.","zh":"學生可能屬於學校管弦樂團和辯論學會。"},{"en":"If animals belong to the same family, separating them may cause stress.","zh":"如果動物屬於同一家族，分開牠們可能造成壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows connection or membership.","zh":"這個短語顯示連繫或成員身份。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同時","examples":[{"en":"Related elephants had to be moved at the same time.","zh":"有親屬關係的大象必須同時被遷移。"},{"en":"At the same time means during the same period or together.","zh":"at the same time 指在同一時間或一起進行。"},{"en":"A student cannot listen carefully and text friends at the same time.","zh":"學生不能一邊認真聆聽，一邊同時傳訊息給朋友。"},{"en":"If family animals are moved at the same time, they may stay calmer.","zh":"如果同一家族的動物同時被遷移，牠們可能較平靜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes simultaneous action.","zh":"這個短語描述同步行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"team of vets","meaning":"獸醫團隊","examples":[{"en":"A team of vets helped move the elephants.","zh":"一支獸醫團隊協助遷移大象。"},{"en":"A team of vets is a group of animal doctors working together.","zh":"team of vets 指一組一起工作的動物醫生。"},{"en":"A zoo may call a team of vets when several animals need health checks.","zh":"當幾隻動物需要健康檢查時，動物園可能請獸醫團隊協助。"},{"en":"If large animals are moved, a team of vets is needed to manage medicine and safety.","zh":"如果大型動物被遷移，就需要獸醫團隊管理藥物和安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes professional animal medical support.","zh":"這個短語描述專業動物醫療支援。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"park rangers","meaning":"公園巡護員","examples":[{"en":"Park rangers flew over the park in helicopters.","zh":"公園巡護員乘直升機飛越公園。"},{"en":"Park rangers are workers who protect parks, wildlife, visitors, and natural resources.","zh":"park rangers 指保護公園、野生動物、訪客和自然資源的工作人員。"},{"en":"Park rangers may guide hikers, check trails, and stop illegal hunting.","zh":"公園巡護員可能引導遠足者、檢查山徑和阻止非法狩獵。"},{"en":"If park rangers patrol regularly, wildlife areas become safer.","zh":"如果公園巡護員定期巡邏，野生動物區會更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes staff who manage and protect parks.","zh":"這個短語描述管理和保護公園的員工。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fly over","meaning":"飛越……","examples":[{"en":"The team flew over the park in helicopters.","zh":"團隊乘直升機飛越公園。"},{"en":"To fly over a place means to travel above it by aircraft.","zh":"fly over a place 指乘飛機或直升機在某地上空飛行。"},{"en":"News helicopters may fly over a city after a major storm.","zh":"大風暴後，新聞直升機可能飛越城市。"},{"en":"If researchers fly over a forest, they can see animal groups from above.","zh":"如果研究人員飛越森林，就能從空中看到動物群。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement through the air above a place.","zh":"這個短語描述在某地上空的空中移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in helicopters","meaning":"乘坐直升機","examples":[{"en":"The vets and park rangers flew over the park in helicopters.","zh":"獸醫和公園巡護員乘坐直升機飛越公園。"},{"en":"In helicopters means using helicopters as the form of transport.","zh":"in helicopters 指以直升機作為交通工具。"},{"en":"Rescue workers may arrive in helicopters when roads are blocked.","zh":"當道路受阻時，救援人員可能乘坐直升機到達。"},{"en":"If teams travel in helicopters, they can reach remote areas more quickly.","zh":"如果團隊乘直升機出行，就能更快到達偏遠地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how people travel by air.","zh":"這個短語描述人們如何空中移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"target a group","meaning":"鎖定一組","examples":[{"en":"The team targeted a group of elephants.","zh":"團隊鎖定一組大象。"},{"en":"To target a group means to choose a particular group for action or attention.","zh":"target a group 指為某行動或關注選定特定群體。"},{"en":"A teacher may target a group of students who need extra reading support.","zh":"老師可能鎖定一組需要額外閱讀支援的學生。"},{"en":"If conservation workers target the wrong animal group, family units may be separated.","zh":"如果保育人員鎖定錯誤動物群，家庭單位可能被拆散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes selecting a group for a specific purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為特定目的選出一組。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be rounded up","meaning":"被圍攏起來","examples":[{"en":"The elephants were rounded up and directed to an open plain.","zh":"大象被圍攏起來，並被引導到開闊平原。"},{"en":"To be rounded up means to be gathered together, often by guiding or surrounding.","zh":"be rounded up 指被聚集起來，通常透過引導或包圍。"},{"en":"Farmers rounded up the sheep before moving them to another field.","zh":"農民把羊群圍攏起來，再把牠們移到另一塊田。"},{"en":"If animals are rounded up too roughly, they may panic or injure themselves.","zh":"如果動物被太粗暴地圍攏，牠們可能驚慌或受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing scattered animals into one group.","zh":"這個短語描述把分散動物集合成一群。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be directed to","meaning":"被引導到……","examples":[{"en":"The elephants were directed to a designated open plain.","zh":"大象被引導到指定的開闊平原。"},{"en":"To be directed to a place means to be guided or told to go there.","zh":"be directed to a place 指被引導或被指示去某地方。"},{"en":"New students were directed to the school hall for registration.","zh":"新生被引導到學校禮堂登記。"},{"en":"If people are directed clearly, they are less likely to get lost.","zh":"如果人們被清楚引導，就較不容易迷路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes guided movement toward a place.","zh":"這個短語描述朝某地的受引導移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"designated open plain","meaning":"指定的開闊平原","examples":[{"en":"The elephants were moved to a designated open plain.","zh":"大象被移到指定的開闊平原。"},{"en":"A designated open plain is a wide flat area officially chosen for a particular purpose.","zh":"designated open plain 指被正式選定作特定用途的寬闊平坦地帶。"},{"en":"During sports day, students gather in a designated open area before races begin.","zh":"運動會期間，學生在比賽開始前聚集在指定開闊區域。"},{"en":"If elephants are guided to an open plain, the team can work more safely and clearly.","zh":"如果大象被引導到開闊平原，團隊可以更安全清楚地工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a planned open working area.","zh":"這個短語描述經規劃的開闊工作區。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"use darts to","meaning":"使用飛鏢去……","examples":[{"en":"The vets used darts to immobilise the elephants.","zh":"獸醫使用飛鏢使大象失去行動能力。"},{"en":"To use darts to do something means to fire small pointed devices containing medicine or chemicals for that purpose.","zh":"use darts to do something 指為某目的發射裝有藥物或化學物的小型尖頭裝置。"},{"en":"Wildlife vets may use darts to give medicine to an animal that cannot be approached safely.","zh":"野生動物獸醫可能使用飛鏢，為不能安全接近的動物注射藥物。"},{"en":"If darts are used correctly, animals can be treated without close physical contact at first.","zh":"如果飛鏢使用得當，動物起初可在沒有近距離接觸下接受處理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a controlled method of giving medicine from a distance.","zh":"這個短語描述從遠距離施藥的受控方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"immobilise","meaning":"使……失去行動能力","examples":[{"en":"The vets used darts to immobilise the elephants.","zh":"獸醫使用飛鏢使大象失去行動能力。"},{"en":"To immobilise an animal means to make it unable to move for a short time, usually for treatment or transport.","zh":"immobilise an animal 指令動物暫時不能移動，通常為了治療或運輸。"},{"en":"Doctors may immobilise a broken arm with a cast so it can heal properly.","zh":"醫生可能用石膏固定斷臂，讓它好好癒合。"},{"en":"If a large animal is immobilised safely, vets can examine it without being harmed.","zh":"如果大型動物被安全地制動，獸醫就能檢查牠而不受傷。"},{"en":"This word describes stopping movement for safety or medical reasons.","zh":"這個字描述因安全或醫療理由而停止移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tricky manoeuvre","meaning":"棘手的操作","examples":[{"en":"Darting the elephants was a tricky manoeuvre.","zh":"用飛鏢射中大象是一項棘手的操作。"},{"en":"A tricky manoeuvre is a difficult action that requires skill, timing, and care.","zh":"tricky manoeuvre 指需要技巧、時機和小心的困難動作。"},{"en":"Parking a large bus in a narrow space can be a tricky manoeuvre.","zh":"把大型巴士泊進狹窄位置可以是棘手操作。"},{"en":"If a manoeuvre is tricky, a small mistake can cause danger or delay.","zh":"如果操作棘手，小錯誤也可能造成危險或延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a difficult practical operation.","zh":"這個短語描述困難的實際操作。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not only...but...","meaning":"不但……而且……","examples":[{"en":"The vets not only selected the right dose but also darted moving elephants.","zh":"獸醫不但要選擇合適劑量，而且要射中移動中的大象。"},{"en":"Not only...but... connects two points and emphasises that both are true.","zh":"not only...but... 連接兩個重點，並強調兩者都成立。"},{"en":"A good class monitor not only collects homework but also helps classmates understand notices.","zh":"好班長不但收功課，而且幫同學理解通告。"},{"en":"If a task requires not only skill but also speed, it becomes more demanding.","zh":"如果任務不但需要技巧，而且需要速度，它就變得更高要求。"},{"en":"This structure adds emphasis by showing two important parts together.","zh":"這個結構透過同時展示兩個重要部分來加強語氣。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"select the right dose","meaning":"選擇合適劑量","examples":[{"en":"The vets had to select the right dose of tranquiliser.","zh":"獸醫必須選擇合適的鎮靜劑劑量。"},{"en":"To select the right dose means to choose the correct amount of medicine.","zh":"select the right dose 指選擇正確的藥物分量。"},{"en":"A doctor selects the right dose of medicine based on a patient’s age and weight.","zh":"醫生會根據病人的年齡和體重選擇合適藥物劑量。"},{"en":"If the dose is too low, it may not work; if it is too high, it may be dangerous.","zh":"如果劑量太低，可能無效；如果太高，可能危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful medical judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述謹慎的醫療判斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dose of tranquiliser","meaning":"鎮靜劑劑量","examples":[{"en":"The right dose of tranquiliser depended on the elephant’s size.","zh":"合適的鎮靜劑劑量取決於大象體型。"},{"en":"A dose of tranquiliser is an amount of calming medicine used to make an animal or person less active.","zh":"dose of tranquiliser 指用來令動物或人減少活動的鎮靜藥物分量。"},{"en":"Vets calculate a dose of tranquiliser carefully before treating a large animal.","zh":"獸醫在處理大型動物前，會仔細計算鎮靜劑劑量。"},{"en":"If the dose of tranquiliser is wrong, the animal may stay awake or become unsafe.","zh":"如果鎮靜劑劑量錯誤，動物可能仍然清醒或變得不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a measured amount of sedating medicine.","zh":"這個短語指經量度的鎮靜藥物分量。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"different-sized elephants","meaning":"不同體型的大象","examples":[{"en":"The vets treated different-sized elephants with different doses.","zh":"獸醫用不同劑量處理不同體型的大象。"},{"en":"Different-sized elephants are elephants of different body sizes or weights.","zh":"different-sized elephants 指身體大小或體重不同的大象。"},{"en":"In a class, different-sized desks may be needed for younger and older students.","zh":"在課室中，較年幼和較年長學生可能需要不同大小的書桌。"},{"en":"If elephants are different-sized, medicine doses cannot be exactly the same.","zh":"如果大象體型不同，藥物劑量就不能完全相同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes variation in physical size.","zh":"這個短語描述體型上的差異。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"run around","meaning":"四處奔跑","examples":[{"en":"The elephants were running around when the vets darted them.","zh":"獸醫射飛鏢時，大象正在四處奔跑。"},{"en":"To run around means to move quickly in different directions, often without staying still.","zh":"run around 指快速向不同方向移動，通常沒有停定。"},{"en":"Children may run around the playground during lunch break.","zh":"孩子可能在午膳時間在操場四處奔跑。"},{"en":"If animals run around during treatment, it becomes harder and more dangerous to help them.","zh":"如果動物在治療期間四處奔跑，協助牠們會更困難和危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active, uncontrolled movement.","zh":"這個短語描述活躍、不受控的移動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as quickly as possible","meaning":"盡快","examples":[{"en":"The darting had to be done as quickly as possible.","zh":"射飛鏢必須盡快完成。"},{"en":"As quickly as possible means as fast as one can safely or reasonably do it.","zh":"as quickly as possible 指在安全或合理情況下盡量快。"},{"en":"Students should leave the building as quickly as possible during a fire drill.","zh":"火警演習期間，學生應盡快離開大樓。"},{"en":"If a medical task must be done quickly, delay can increase risk.","zh":"如果醫療任務必須快速完成，延誤會增加風險。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses speed and urgency.","zh":"這個短語強調速度和緊急性。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"so as to","meaning":"以便；為了","examples":[{"en":"The team worked quickly so as to minimise stress.","zh":"團隊快速工作，以便盡量減少壓力。"},{"en":"So as to means in order to or for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"so as to 指為了或以便做某事。"},{"en":"Students whisper in the library so as to avoid disturbing others.","zh":"學生在圖書館輕聲說話，以免打擾別人。"},{"en":"If workers plan carefully so as to reduce mistakes, the project becomes safer.","zh":"如果工人仔細計劃以減少錯誤，項目就會更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces purpose in a formal way.","zh":"這個短語以較正式方式引出目的。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"minimise the stress caused","meaning":"盡量減少造成的壓力","examples":[{"en":"The team worked quickly to minimise the stress caused.","zh":"團隊快速工作，以盡量減少造成的壓力。"},{"en":"To minimise the stress caused means to reduce the pressure, fear, or discomfort created by an event.","zh":"minimise the stress caused 指減少某事件造成的壓力、恐懼或不適。"},{"en":"A teacher can minimise the stress caused by exams by explaining the format early.","zh":"老師可以透過早點解釋考試格式，盡量減少考試造成的壓力。"},{"en":"If animal handlers work calmly, they can minimise the stress caused by transport.","zh":"如果動物處理人員冷靜工作，就能盡量減少運輸造成的壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing harm or discomfort.","zh":"這個短語描述減少傷害或不適。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as soon as","meaning":"一……就……","examples":[{"en":"As soon as the elephants began to fall, the team moved in.","zh":"大象一開始倒下，團隊就靠近。"},{"en":"As soon as means immediately after something happens.","zh":"as soon as 指某事一發生就立即。"},{"en":"As soon as the bell rings, students leave the classroom.","zh":"鐘聲一響，學生就離開課室。"},{"en":"If help arrives as soon as a problem begins, danger can be reduced.","zh":"如果問題一開始就有人幫忙，危險可以減少。"},{"en":"This phrase shows quick action after a trigger.","zh":"這個短語表示觸發事件後的快速行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"flop onto the ground","meaning":"重重倒在地上","examples":[{"en":"The elephants began to flop onto the ground.","zh":"大象開始重重倒在地上。"},{"en":"To flop onto the ground means to fall heavily and loosely onto the ground.","zh":"flop onto the ground 指沉重而鬆散地倒在地上。"},{"en":"After sports practice, a tired student may flop onto the grass.","zh":"運動訓練後，疲倦的學生可能重重倒在草地上。"},{"en":"If a large animal flops onto the ground, people nearby must move carefully.","zh":"如果大型動物重重倒地，附近的人必須小心移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a heavy, uncontrolled fall.","zh":"這個短語描述沉重而不受控的倒下。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"move in","meaning":"靠近；進場","examples":[{"en":"The team moved in to take care of the elephants.","zh":"團隊靠近去照料大象。"},{"en":"To move in means to approach or enter an area to take action.","zh":"move in 指靠近或進入某區域採取行動。"},{"en":"Paramedics moved in after the road was cleared.","zh":"道路清理後，救護人員進場。"},{"en":"If a team moves in too early, it may be unsafe; if too late, help may be delayed.","zh":"如果團隊太早進場，可能不安全；如果太遲，協助可能延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes going closer to act.","zh":"這個短語描述靠近以採取行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take care of","meaning":"照料","examples":[{"en":"The team moved in to take care of the elephants.","zh":"團隊進場照料大象。"},{"en":"To take care of someone or something means to look after them and make sure they are safe or well.","zh":"take care of someone or something 指照顧某人或某物，確保其安全或狀況良好。"},{"en":"Parents take care of young children when they are sick.","zh":"父母在幼童生病時照料他們。"},{"en":"If workers take care of animals properly, injuries and stress can be reduced.","zh":"如果工作人員妥善照料動物，受傷和壓力可以減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes looking after needs and safety.","zh":"這個短語描述照顧需要和安全。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"avoid the risk of","meaning":"避免……的風險","examples":[{"en":"The team worked carefully to avoid the risk of suffocation.","zh":"團隊小心工作，以避免窒息風險。"},{"en":"To avoid the risk of something means to prevent the chance of that dangerous thing happening.","zh":"avoid the risk of something 指防止某種危險事情發生的可能性。"},{"en":"Cyclists wear helmets to avoid the risk of serious head injury.","zh":"騎單車者戴頭盔，以避免嚴重頭部受傷風險。"},{"en":"If workers identify risks early, they can take steps to avoid them.","zh":"如果工人及早識別風險，就可以採取措施避免它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preventing possible danger.","zh":"這個短語描述防止潛在危險。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"suffocation","meaning":"窒息","examples":[{"en":"The elephants had to be positioned correctly to avoid suffocation.","zh":"大象必須被正確放置，以避免窒息。"},{"en":"Suffocation is the condition of being unable to breathe properly.","zh":"suffocation 指無法正常呼吸的狀況。"},{"en":"A plastic bag should be kept away from babies because it can cause suffocation.","zh":"膠袋應遠離嬰兒，因為它可能造成窒息。"},{"en":"If a heavy body presses on the chest, suffocation can happen.","zh":"如果沉重身體壓住胸部，就可能發生窒息。"},{"en":"This word describes a dangerous breathing problem.","zh":"這個字描述危險的呼吸問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"The team had to make sure no elephants were lying on their chests.","zh":"團隊必須確保沒有大象趴在胸部上。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check carefully so that something definitely is or is not the case.","zh":"make sure 指仔細檢查，以確保某事確實如此或不會發生。"},{"en":"Make sure the classroom windows are closed before you leave.","zh":"離開前要確保課室窗戶已關好。"},{"en":"If staff make sure safety rules are followed, accidents become less likely.","zh":"如果員工確保安全規則被遵守，意外就較不容易發生。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strong reminder to check.","zh":"這個短語給出強烈檢查提醒。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lie on their chests","meaning":"趴在胸部上","examples":[{"en":"The elephants could not be allowed to lie on their chests.","zh":"大象不能被容許趴在胸部上。"},{"en":"To lie on their chests means to rest with the front part of the body facing down.","zh":"lie on their chests 指身體前方朝下躺着。"},{"en":"A patient may be told not to lie on his chest after surgery.","zh":"病人手術後可能被告知不要趴在胸部上。"},{"en":"If heavy animals lie on their chests while sedated, breathing can become dangerous.","zh":"如果大型動物在鎮靜後趴在胸部上，呼吸可能變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a body position that may cause pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述可能造成壓力的身體姿勢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lungs","meaning":"肺","examples":[{"en":"Their lungs could be crushed in that position.","zh":"在那個姿勢下，牠們的肺可能被壓傷。"},{"en":"Lungs are the organs in the chest that help people and animals breathe.","zh":"lungs 指胸腔內幫助人和動物呼吸的器官。"},{"en":"Doctors may listen to a patient’s lungs when checking a cough.","zh":"醫生檢查咳嗽時，可能會聽病人的肺部聲音。"},{"en":"If the lungs cannot expand properly, breathing becomes difficult.","zh":"如果肺不能正常擴張，呼吸就會變困難。"},{"en":"This word names a vital breathing organ.","zh":"這個字指出重要呼吸器官。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be crushed","meaning":"被壓傷","examples":[{"en":"The elephants’ lungs could be crushed if they lay on their chests.","zh":"如果大象趴在胸部上，牠們的肺可能被壓傷。"},{"en":"To be crushed means to be pressed so hard that damage happens.","zh":"be crushed 指被重力或壓力壓到受損。"},{"en":"A cardboard box may be crushed if heavy books are placed on top of it.","zh":"如果厚重書本放在紙箱上，紙箱可能被壓扁。"},{"en":"If a person’s chest is crushed, breathing can become an emergency.","zh":"如果人的胸部被壓傷，呼吸可能變成緊急情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage from heavy pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述由沉重壓力造成的損傷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in this position","meaning":"在這個姿勢下","examples":[{"en":"The elephants’ lungs could be crushed in this position.","zh":"在這個姿勢下，大象的肺可能被壓傷。"},{"en":"In this position means while the body or object is placed in this particular way.","zh":"in this position 指身體或物件以這種特定方式放置時。"},{"en":"A baby should not sleep in this position if it makes breathing difficult.","zh":"如果某個睡姿令呼吸困難，嬰兒不應以這個姿勢睡覺。"},{"en":"If furniture is left in this position, it may block the doorway.","zh":"如果家具保持在這個位置，可能會阻塞門口。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific arrangement or posture.","zh":"這個短語指特定安排或姿勢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be placed on their sides","meaning":"被放成側躺","examples":[{"en":"All the elephants had to be placed on their sides.","zh":"所有大象都必須被放成側躺。"},{"en":"To be placed on their sides means to be positioned with the body lying sideways.","zh":"be placed on their sides 指身體被安排成側身躺着。"},{"en":"A patient may be placed on his side so he can breathe more easily.","zh":"病人可能被放成側躺，以便更容易呼吸。"},{"en":"If sedated animals are placed on their sides, pressure on the chest can be reduced.","zh":"如果鎮靜後的動物被放成側躺，胸部壓力可以減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a safer body position.","zh":"這個短語描述較安全的身體姿勢。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stay with","meaning":"陪在……旁邊","examples":[{"en":"One person stayed with each elephant.","zh":"每隻大象都有一個人陪在旁邊。"},{"en":"To stay with someone or something means to remain beside them for support, safety, or observation.","zh":"stay with someone or something 指留在某人或某物旁邊，以提供支援、安全或觀察。"},{"en":"A nurse may stay with a patient after an operation.","zh":"手術後，護士可能陪在病人旁邊。"},{"en":"If someone stays with a sleeping animal, they can notice problems quickly.","zh":"如果有人陪在沉睡動物旁邊，就能迅速注意到問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes remaining nearby and watching over someone or something.","zh":"這個短語描述留在附近並照看某人或某物。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"do checks","meaning":"進行檢查","examples":[{"en":"The vets did checks on the elephants.","zh":"獸醫對大象進行檢查。"},{"en":"To do checks means to examine something to make sure it is safe, correct, or healthy.","zh":"do checks 指檢查某事物，以確保它安全、正確或健康。"},{"en":"Teachers do checks on classroom equipment before a science lesson.","zh":"老師在科學課前會檢查課室設備。"},{"en":"If vets do checks regularly, they can notice breathing or injury problems early.","zh":"如果獸醫定期進行檢查，就能及早注意呼吸或受傷問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful inspection.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細檢查。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"keep an eye on","meaning":"密切留意","examples":[{"en":"It was important to keep an eye on the elephants’ breathing.","zh":"密切留意大象的呼吸很重要。"},{"en":"To keep an eye on something means to watch it carefully.","zh":"keep an eye on something 指小心觀察某事物。"},{"en":"A parent may keep an eye on a child playing near the road.","zh":"家長可能密切留意在馬路附近玩耍的孩子。"},{"en":"If staff keep an eye on a machine, they can stop it before a fault becomes serious.","zh":"如果員工密切留意機器，就能在故障變嚴重前停止它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful monitoring.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細監察。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"breathing","meaning":"呼吸","examples":[{"en":"The team had to keep an eye on the elephants’ breathing.","zh":"團隊必須密切留意大象的呼吸。"},{"en":"Breathing is the act of taking air into the lungs and letting it out again.","zh":"breathing 指把空氣吸入肺部再呼出的動作。"},{"en":"Doctors check breathing when a patient feels dizzy or weak.","zh":"當病人感到頭暈或虛弱時，醫生會檢查呼吸。"},{"en":"If breathing becomes too slow, urgent medical help may be needed.","zh":"如果呼吸變得太慢，可能需要緊急醫療協助。"},{"en":"This word refers to a basic sign of life and health.","zh":"這個字指生命和健康的基本跡象。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"breaths per minute","meaning":"每分鐘呼吸次數","examples":[{"en":"An elephant needed urgent help if it took fewer than six breaths per minute.","zh":"如果大象每分鐘呼吸少於六次，就需要緊急協助。"},{"en":"Breaths per minute means the number of times someone or an animal breathes in one minute.","zh":"breaths per minute 指人或動物在一分鐘內呼吸的次數。"},{"en":"A nurse may count a patient’s breaths per minute during a health check.","zh":"護士可能在健康檢查中計算病人的每分鐘呼吸次數。"},{"en":"If breaths per minute fall too low, the body may not get enough oxygen.","zh":"如果每分鐘呼吸次數太低，身體可能得不到足夠氧氣。"},{"en":"This phrase measures breathing rate.","zh":"這個短語量度呼吸速率。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"urgent medical attention","meaning":"緊急醫療處理","examples":[{"en":"The elephant would need urgent medical attention.","zh":"這隻大象需要緊急醫療處理。"},{"en":"Urgent medical attention means immediate care from trained medical staff.","zh":"urgent medical attention 指由受訓醫療人員立即提供的照護。"},{"en":"A student with serious breathing difficulty needs urgent medical attention.","zh":"有嚴重呼吸困難的學生需要緊急醫療處理。"},{"en":"If medical attention is delayed in an emergency, the condition may become worse.","zh":"如果緊急情況下醫療處理被延誤，情況可能惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quick medical help for a serious situation.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重情況下的快速醫療協助。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"collars were fitted to","meaning":"項圈被戴在……身上","examples":[{"en":"Collars were fitted to the matriarch in each group.","zh":"每組的母象首領都被戴上項圈。"},{"en":"Collars were fitted to animals means tracking or identification collars were put around their necks.","zh":"collars were fitted to animals 指把追蹤或識別用項圈戴在動物頸上。"},{"en":"A rescue centre may fit collars to dogs so staff can identify them.","zh":"救援中心可能給狗戴上項圈，讓職員能識別牠們。"},{"en":"If tracking collars are fitted to wild animals, researchers can monitor where they go.","zh":"如果野生動物被戴上追蹤項圈，研究人員就能監察牠們去向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attaching collars for management or tracking.","zh":"這個短語描述為管理或追蹤而戴上項圈。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"matriarch","meaning":"母象首領","examples":[{"en":"The matriarch in each elephant group wore a collar.","zh":"每個大象群中的母象首領都戴着項圈。"},{"en":"A matriarch is the older female leader of a family or animal group.","zh":"matriarch 指家庭或動物群中年長的女性領袖。"},{"en":"In some families, the grandmother acts as the matriarch who keeps everyone connected.","zh":"在一些家庭中，祖母擔任把大家連繫起來的女性長輩領袖。"},{"en":"If an elephant matriarch moves calmly, the rest of the group may follow her.","zh":"如果母象首領冷靜移動，其餘成員可能會跟隨牠。"},{"en":"This word describes female leadership within a group.","zh":"這個字描述群體中的女性領導。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"movements could be tracked","meaning":"活動可被追蹤","examples":[{"en":"The elephants’ movements could be tracked in their new home.","zh":"大象在新家園中的活動可被追蹤。"},{"en":"If movements can be tracked, people can follow where someone or something goes.","zh":"movements could be tracked 指人們可以跟進某人或某物去了哪裡。"},{"en":"Parents may track a school bus’s movements through an app.","zh":"家長可能透過應用程式追蹤校巴的行蹤。"},{"en":"If wildlife movements are tracked, researchers can learn whether animals are settling safely.","zh":"如果野生動物的活動可被追蹤，研究人員就能知道牠們是否安全適應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes monitoring location over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間監察位置。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take measurements of","meaning":"測量……","examples":[{"en":"The team took measurements of each elephant’s tusks and feet.","zh":"團隊測量每隻大象的象牙和腳。"},{"en":"To take measurements of something means to measure its size, length, width, or other physical details.","zh":"take measurements of something 指量度某物的大小、長度、闊度或其他身體細節。"},{"en":"A tailor takes measurements of a customer before making a suit.","zh":"裁縫製作西裝前會為顧客量度尺寸。"},{"en":"If scientists take accurate measurements, they can compare changes over time.","zh":"如果科學家取得準確測量數據，就能比較隨時間出現的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recording physical dimensions.","zh":"這個短語描述記錄實體尺寸。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tusks","meaning":"象牙","examples":[{"en":"Measurements were taken of each elephant’s tusks.","zh":"每隻大象的象牙都被量度。"},{"en":"Tusks are the long curved teeth that grow from an elephant’s mouth.","zh":"tusks 指從大象口中長出的長而彎曲的牙。"},{"en":"Wildlife officers may record tusks to identify individual elephants.","zh":"野生動物人員可能記錄象牙特徵，以識別個別大象。"},{"en":"If elephants have large tusks, they may be more attractive to poachers.","zh":"如果大象有大型象牙，牠們可能更吸引偷獵者。"},{"en":"This word names an elephant body part connected with ivory.","zh":"這個字指出與象牙材料有關的大象身體部位。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at greater risk from","meaning":"面對更大……風險","examples":[{"en":"Elephants with large tusks were at greater risk from poachers.","zh":"有大型象牙的大象面對更大的偷獵者風險。"},{"en":"To be at greater risk from something means to face a higher chance of being harmed by it.","zh":"be at greater risk from something 指面對某事造成傷害的機會較高。"},{"en":"Elderly people may be at greater risk from extreme heat during summer.","zh":"長者在夏季極端高溫下可能面對更大風險。"},{"en":"If animals have valuable body parts, they may be at greater risk from illegal hunters.","zh":"如果動物有有價值的身體部位，牠們可能面對更大非法獵人風險。"},{"en":"This phrase compares levels of danger.","zh":"這個短語比較危險程度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"recovery area","meaning":"恢復區","examples":[{"en":"The elephants were taken to a recovery area before transport.","zh":"大象在運輸前被帶到恢復區。"},{"en":"A recovery area is a place where people or animals rest and are monitored after treatment or sedation.","zh":"recovery area 指人或動物在治療或鎮靜後休息並受監察的地方。"},{"en":"After surgery, patients may stay in a recovery area until they wake up fully.","zh":"手術後，病人可能留在恢復區，直到完全醒來。"},{"en":"If animals recover in a safe area, vets can check them before moving them again.","zh":"如果動物在安全區域恢復，獸醫可以在再次移動牠們前檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place for controlled rest after medical care.","zh":"這個短語描述醫療處理後受控休息的地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be loaded onto","meaning":"被裝上……","examples":[{"en":"The elephants were loaded onto trucks.","zh":"大象被裝上貨車。"},{"en":"To be loaded onto something means to be placed onto a vehicle or container for transport.","zh":"be loaded onto something 指被放上車輛或容器以便運輸。"},{"en":"Boxes of school books were loaded onto a van before delivery.","zh":"一箱箱學校書本在送貨前被裝上客貨車。"},{"en":"If heavy animals are loaded onto trucks, special equipment and careful timing are needed.","zh":"如果大型動物被裝上貨車，就需要特殊設備和小心時間安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes putting something onto transport.","zh":"這個短語描述把某物放上交通工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"trucks","meaning":"貨車","examples":[{"en":"The elephants were loaded onto trucks and transported to their new home.","zh":"大象被裝上貨車，並被運送到新家園。"},{"en":"Trucks are large road vehicles used to carry heavy goods, equipment, or animals.","zh":"trucks 指用來運載重貨、設備或動物的大型道路車輛。"},{"en":"A supermarket uses trucks to deliver food from warehouses to shops.","zh":"超級市場使用貨車把食物從倉庫送到店舖。"},{"en":"If trucks carry heavy loads, drivers must plan safe routes and stops.","zh":"如果貨車運載重物，司機必須規劃安全路線和停靠點。"},{"en":"This word names a vehicle used for transport.","zh":"這個字指出用於運輸的車輛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be transported to","meaning":"被運送到……","examples":[{"en":"The elephants were transported to their new home.","zh":"大象被運送到新家園。"},{"en":"To be transported to a place means to be moved or carried there by a vehicle or system.","zh":"be transported to a place 指透過車輛或系統被移送到某地。"},{"en":"Patients may be transported to hospital by ambulance.","zh":"病人可能由救護車運送到醫院。"},{"en":"If animals are transported over a long distance, they need careful monitoring.","zh":"如果動物被長途運送，牠們需要仔細監察。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being moved from one place to another.","zh":"這個短語描述從一地移到另一地。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"settle in","meaning":"適應新環境","examples":[{"en":"The elephants translocated to Nkhotakota settled in very well.","zh":"遷移到 Nkhotakota 的大象非常適應新環境。"},{"en":"To settle in means to become comfortable and used to a new place.","zh":"settle in 指變得習慣並適應一個新地方。"},{"en":"A new student may need a few weeks to settle in at school.","zh":"新學生可能需要幾星期適應新學校。"},{"en":"If animals settle in well, they eat, move, and behave normally in the new area.","zh":"如果動物適應良好，牠們會在新地方正常進食、移動和活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes successful adjustment after a move.","zh":"這個短語描述搬遷後成功適應。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be accepted to have been","meaning":"普遍被認為已經……","examples":[{"en":"The project has generally been accepted to have been a huge success.","zh":"這個項目普遍被認為已經取得巨大成功。"},{"en":"To be accepted to have been something means people generally agree that it was that thing.","zh":"be accepted to have been something 指人們普遍同意某事曾經是某種情況。"},{"en":"The school concert was accepted to have been a success after parents and teachers praised it.","zh":"家長和老師稱讚後，學校音樂會被認為已經成功。"},{"en":"If a project is accepted to have been successful, future projects may copy its methods.","zh":"如果項目被認為已經成功，未來項目可能借鑑其方法。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and describes general judgement after an event.","zh":"這個短語語氣正式，描述事件後的普遍判斷。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a huge success","meaning":"巨大成功","examples":[{"en":"The elephant translocation project was a huge success.","zh":"大象遷地轉移項目取得巨大成功。"},{"en":"A huge success is something that works extremely well and achieves important results.","zh":"a huge success 指非常成功並取得重要成果的事情。"},{"en":"The charity sale was a huge success because it raised more money than expected.","zh":"慈善義賣籌得比預期更多善款，因此取得巨大成功。"},{"en":"If a project is a huge success, people may want to repeat it elsewhere.","zh":"如果項目取得巨大成功，人們可能想在其他地方重複它。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong positive judgement.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈正面評價。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not just for","meaning":"不只是對……而言","examples":[{"en":"The project was a success not just for the elephants.","zh":"這個項目不只是對大象而言成功。"},{"en":"Not just for means not only benefiting or involving one group, but also others.","zh":"not just for 指不只是惠及或涉及一個群體，也包括其他群體。"},{"en":"A new library is useful not just for students but also for parents and neighbours.","zh":"新圖書館不只是對學生有用，也對家長和鄰居有用。"},{"en":"If a conservation project helps both animals and people, its value is wider.","zh":"如果保育項目同時幫助動物和人，其價值就更廣。"},{"en":"This phrase expands the focus beyond one group.","zh":"這個短語把焦點擴展到一個群體之外。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"employment prospects","meaning":"就業前景","examples":[{"en":"Employment prospects have improved enormously.","zh":"就業前景已大幅改善。"},{"en":"Employment prospects are people’s chances of finding stable or better work.","zh":"employment prospects 指人們找到穩定或更好工作的機會。"},{"en":"Vocational training can improve young people’s employment prospects.","zh":"職業培訓可以改善年輕人的就業前景。"},{"en":"If tourism grows, local employment prospects may improve because more guides and hotel workers are needed.","zh":"如果旅遊業增長，本地就業前景可能改善，因為需要更多導遊和酒店員工。"},{"en":"This phrase describes future job opportunities.","zh":"這個短語描述未來工作機會。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"improve enormously","meaning":"大幅改善","examples":[{"en":"Employment prospects have improved enormously.","zh":"就業前景已大幅改善。"},{"en":"To improve enormously means to become much better by a large degree.","zh":"improve enormously 指以很大程度變得更好。"},{"en":"A student’s speaking can improve enormously after months of regular practice.","zh":"學生經過數月定期練習後，口語可以大幅改善。"},{"en":"If transport improves enormously, people can reach work and school more easily.","zh":"如果交通大幅改善，人們上班和上學會更方便。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very big improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述非常大的改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"contribute to","meaning":"促成；有助於……","examples":[{"en":"The project contributed to rising living standards.","zh":"這個項目有助於生活水平提高。"},{"en":"To contribute to something means to help cause it or add to it.","zh":"contribute to something 指幫助造成某事或增加某事。"},{"en":"Regular exercise can contribute to better health.","zh":"定期運動有助於改善健康。"},{"en":"If a new business creates jobs, it can contribute to a stronger local economy.","zh":"如果新企業創造職位，它可以有助於本地經濟變強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one factor helping a result happen.","zh":"這個短語描述促成結果的其中一個因素。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rising living standards","meaning":"不斷提高的生活水平","examples":[{"en":"The project contributed to rising living standards for the whole community.","zh":"這個項目有助於整個社區生活水平不斷提高。"},{"en":"Rising living standards mean people’s quality of life is improving.","zh":"rising living standards 指人們的生活質素正在改善。"},{"en":"Rising living standards may include better jobs, safer homes, and improved healthcare.","zh":"生活水平提高可以包括更好工作、更安全住所和改善醫療。"},{"en":"If more families earn reliable income, living standards can rise over time.","zh":"如果更多家庭獲得穩定收入，生活水平可以隨時間提高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement in daily life conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述日常生活條件的改善。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the whole community","meaning":"整個社區","examples":[{"en":"The project benefited the whole community.","zh":"這個項目令整個社區受益。"},{"en":"The whole community means all the people living or working in a local area.","zh":"the whole community 指生活或工作於某本地區域的所有人。"},{"en":"A new clinic can help the whole community, not just one family.","zh":"新診所可以幫助整個社區，而不只是一個家庭。"},{"en":"If a project creates jobs and safer surroundings, the whole community may benefit.","zh":"如果項目創造職位和更安全環境，整個社區都可能受益。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the benefit is broad.","zh":"這個短語強調受益範圍廣泛。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"no longer an issue","meaning":"不再是問題","examples":[{"en":"Poaching is no longer an issue.","zh":"偷獵不再是問題。"},{"en":"No longer an issue means something is no longer a problem or concern.","zh":"no longer an issue 指某事不再是問題或憂慮。"},{"en":"After the school added more buses, lateness was no longer an issue.","zh":"學校增設巴士後，遲到不再是問題。"},{"en":"If poaching is no longer an issue, animals can live with less danger.","zh":"如果偷獵不再是問題，動物就能在較少危險下生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a problem that has been solved or reduced.","zh":"這個短語描述已被解決或減少的問題。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"former poachers","meaning":"前偷獵者","examples":[{"en":"Former poachers are now able to find reliable income.","zh":"前偷獵者現在能找到可靠收入。"},{"en":"Former poachers are people who used to hunt wildlife illegally but no longer do so.","zh":"former poachers 指以前非法獵捕野生動物但現在不再這樣做的人。"},{"en":"Former poachers may become park guides if they know the land well.","zh":"如果前偷獵者熟悉土地，他們可能成為公園導遊。"},{"en":"If former poachers can earn money legally, they have less reason to return to hunting.","zh":"如果前偷獵者能合法賺錢，他們就較少理由重返偷獵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people who have left illegal hunting behind.","zh":"這個短語描述已離開非法狩獵的人。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reliable sources of income","meaning":"可靠收入來源","examples":[{"en":"Former poachers found more reliable sources of income.","zh":"前偷獵者找到更可靠的收入來源。"},{"en":"Reliable sources of income are steady ways to earn money that people can depend on.","zh":"reliable sources of income 指人們可以依靠的穩定賺錢方式。"},{"en":"A full-time job can be a reliable source of income for a family.","zh":"全職工作可以是一個家庭的可靠收入來源。"},{"en":"If people lack reliable income, they may take risky or illegal work.","zh":"如果人們缺乏可靠收入，可能會做高風險或非法工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dependable money for daily life.","zh":"這個短語描述日常生活可依靠的金錢來源。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"volunteer to","meaning":"主動提出……","examples":[{"en":"Many former poachers volunteered to give up their weapons.","zh":"許多前偷獵者主動提出交出武器。"},{"en":"To volunteer to do something means to offer to do it willingly, without being forced.","zh":"volunteer to do something 指自願提出做某事，而不是被迫。"},{"en":"Students may volunteer to clean the classroom after a school event.","zh":"學生可能在學校活動後主動提出清潔課室。"},{"en":"If people volunteer to help, a project can gain trust and support.","zh":"如果人們主動提出幫忙，項目就能得到信任和支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a willing offer of action.","zh":"這個短語描述自願提出行動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"give up their weapons","meaning":"交出武器","examples":[{"en":"Former poachers gave up their weapons.","zh":"前偷獵者交出武器。"},{"en":"To give up weapons means to hand them over or stop using them.","zh":"give up weapons 指交出武器或停止使用它們。"},{"en":"A security officer may ask visitors to give up sharp tools before entering a building.","zh":"保安員可能要求訪客進入大樓前交出尖銳工具。"},{"en":"If former hunters give up weapons, they show they are leaving illegal hunting behind.","zh":"如果前獵人交出武器，就表示他們正在離開非法狩獵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes surrendering dangerous tools.","zh":"這個短語描述交出危險工具。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"no longer of any use to","meaning":"對……再沒有用處","examples":[{"en":"The weapons were no longer of any use to the former poachers.","zh":"這些武器對前偷獵者再沒有用處。"},{"en":"No longer of any use to someone means something is not useful to that person anymore.","zh":"no longer of any use to someone 指某物對某人不再有用。"},{"en":"An old student card is no longer of any use after graduation.","zh":"畢業後，舊學生證再沒有用處。"},{"en":"If workers change jobs, some old tools may no longer be of any use to them.","zh":"如果工人轉工，一些舊工具可能對他們再沒有用處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes usefulness ending.","zh":"這個短語描述用途結束。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"more than two dozen","meaning":"二十多個","examples":[{"en":"More than two dozen elephants have been born at Nkhotakota.","zh":"Nkhotakota 已有二十多隻大象出生。"},{"en":"More than two dozen means more than twenty-four.","zh":"more than two dozen 指多於二十四個。"},{"en":"More than two dozen students signed up for the hiking club.","zh":"二十多名學生報名參加遠足學會。"},{"en":"If more than two dozen animals are born, the population is clearly growing.","zh":"如果有二十多隻動物出生，族群明顯正在增長。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate number above twenty-four.","zh":"這個短語提供超過二十四的約數。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"since relocation","meaning":"自遷移以來","examples":[{"en":"More than two dozen elephants have been born since relocation.","zh":"自遷移以來，已有二十多隻大象出生。"},{"en":"Since relocation means from the time the move happened until now.","zh":"since relocation 指從遷移發生時起直到現在。"},{"en":"Since relocation to the new campus, the school has opened three new laboratories.","zh":"自遷往新校舍以來，學校已開設三個新實驗室。"},{"en":"If many young animals are born since relocation, the new home may be suitable.","zh":"如果自遷移以來有很多幼崽出生，新棲地可能合適。"},{"en":"This phrase measures change after a move.","zh":"這個短語量度搬遷後的變化。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"with an area of","meaning":"面積達……","examples":[{"en":"Nkhotakota has an area of more than 1,800 square kilometres.","zh":"Nkhotakota 面積達1,800多平方公里。"},{"en":"With an area of means covering a total size of a particular amount.","zh":"with an area of 指覆蓋某個總面積。"},{"en":"A park with an area of ten hectares can include gardens, paths, and sports fields.","zh":"面積達十公頃的公園可以包括花園、小徑和運動場。"},{"en":"If a reserve has a large area, animals have more room to move and feed.","zh":"如果保護區面積大，動物就有更多空間活動和覓食。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical size.","zh":"這個短語描述實際面積。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"square kilometres","meaning":"平方公里","examples":[{"en":"The park covers more than 1,800 square kilometres.","zh":"這個公園覆蓋1,800多平方公里。"},{"en":"Square kilometres are units used to measure large areas of land.","zh":"square kilometres 是用來量度大片土地面積的單位。"},{"en":"A city’s size may be described in square kilometres.","zh":"城市大小可能以平方公里描述。"},{"en":"If a wildlife park covers many square kilometres, patrols and transport become important.","zh":"如果野生動物公園覆蓋許多平方公里，巡邏和交通就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a measurement of area.","zh":"這個短語提供面積量度。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"plenty of space","meaning":"充足空間","examples":[{"en":"There is plenty of space for the elephant population to grow.","zh":"那裡有充足空間讓大象族群增長。"},{"en":"Plenty of space means more than enough room for people, animals, or activities.","zh":"plenty of space 指有超過足夠的地方供人、動物或活動使用。"},{"en":"A classroom with plenty of space lets students move around safely.","zh":"有充足空間的課室讓學生可以安全走動。"},{"en":"If animals have plenty of space, they may compete less for food and shelter.","zh":"如果動物有充足空間，牠們可能較少爭奪食物和棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes enough room for growth or movement.","zh":"這個短語描述有足夠空間供成長或活動。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"continue to grow","meaning":"繼續增長","examples":[{"en":"The elephant population can continue to grow.","zh":"大象族群可以繼續增長。"},{"en":"To continue to grow means to keep increasing over time.","zh":"continue to grow 指隨時間持續增加。"},{"en":"A school club may continue to grow if more students join each year.","zh":"如果每年有更多學生加入，學校學會可能繼續增長。"},{"en":"If a population continues to grow, planners must make sure resources remain enough.","zh":"如果族群繼續增長，規劃者必須確保資源仍然足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing increase.","zh":"這個短語描述持續增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"their presence","meaning":"牠們的存在","examples":[{"en":"The elephants’ presence is helping to rebalance the ecosystem.","zh":"大象的存在正幫助重新平衡生態系統。"},{"en":"Their presence means the fact that they are there.","zh":"their presence 指牠們在場或存在這件事。"},{"en":"A teacher’s presence in the classroom can make students behave more calmly.","zh":"老師在課室中的存在可以令學生行為更冷靜。"},{"en":"If elephants are present in an ecosystem, they can change vegetation and animal movement.","zh":"如果大象存在於生態系統中，牠們可以改變植被和動物活動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the effect of being in a place.","zh":"這個短語重點在身處某地所帶來的影響。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rebalance","meaning":"重新平衡","examples":[{"en":"The elephants are helping to rebalance the damaged ecosystem.","zh":"大象正幫助重新平衡受損的生態系統。"},{"en":"To rebalance something means to bring it back to a healthier or fairer balance.","zh":"rebalance something 指令某事恢復較健康或較公平的平衡。"},{"en":"A student may rebalance her timetable by adding more rest and less late-night study.","zh":"學生可能透過增加休息、減少深夜溫習來重新平衡時間表。"},{"en":"If one species disappears, reintroducing it may help rebalance the ecosystem.","zh":"如果一個物種消失，重新引入它可能幫助生態系統重新平衡。"},{"en":"This word describes restoring balance after disruption.","zh":"這個字描述在受擾亂後恢復平衡。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"damaged ecosystem","meaning":"受損的生態系統","examples":[{"en":"Nkhotakota has a damaged ecosystem that elephants can help restore.","zh":"Nkhotakota 有一個大象可以幫助恢復的受損生態系統。"},{"en":"A damaged ecosystem is a natural system harmed by hunting, pollution, habitat loss, or imbalance.","zh":"damaged ecosystem 指因狩獵、污染、棲息地流失或失衡而受害的自然系統。"},{"en":"A river with few fish and polluted water is part of a damaged ecosystem.","zh":"魚類稀少又受污染的河流，是受損生態系統的一部分。"},{"en":"If a damaged ecosystem is not restored, many plants and animals may struggle to survive.","zh":"如果受損生態系統沒有被恢復，許多植物和動物可能難以生存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes nature that has been seriously disturbed.","zh":"這個短語描述已被嚴重擾亂的自然環境。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sustainable conservation model","meaning":"可持續保育模式","examples":[{"en":"The project provides a sustainable conservation model.","zh":"這個項目提供了一個可持續保育模式。"},{"en":"A sustainable conservation model is a way to protect nature that can continue over time without causing new harm.","zh":"sustainable conservation model 指一種可以長期持續且不造成新傷害的自然保護方法。"},{"en":"A community forest project can be a sustainable conservation model if local people earn income from protecting trees.","zh":"如果本地人能從保護樹木中獲得收入，社區森林項目可以是可持續保育模式。"},{"en":"If conservation depends only on outside money, it may not be sustainable.","zh":"如果保育只依賴外來資金，它可能不可持續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a conservation method that can last.","zh":"這個短語描述可以長久維持的保育方法。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be replicated in","meaning":"在……被複製；被借鑑","examples":[{"en":"The conservation model could be replicated in other parks.","zh":"這個保育模式可以在其他公園被借鑑。"},{"en":"To be replicated in another place means to be copied or used there in a similar way.","zh":"be replicated in another place 指在另一地方以相似方式複製或使用。"},{"en":"A successful school reading programme can be replicated in other schools.","zh":"成功的學校閱讀計劃可以在其他學校被複製。"},{"en":"If a project is replicated without considering local needs, it may fail.","zh":"如果項目在沒有考慮本地需要下被複製，可能會失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes applying a successful model elsewhere.","zh":"這個短語描述把成功模式應用到其他地方。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a big draw for tourism","meaning":"對旅遊業的一大吸引力","examples":[{"en":"The elephant project has been a big draw for tourism.","zh":"這個大象項目一直是旅遊業的一大吸引力。"},{"en":"A big draw for tourism is something that attracts many visitors to a place.","zh":"a big draw for tourism 指吸引許多遊客到訪某地的事物。"},{"en":"A famous night market can be a big draw for tourism in a city.","zh":"著名夜市可以是城市旅遊業的一大吸引力。"},{"en":"If wildlife becomes a big draw for tourism, local hotels and guides may earn more income.","zh":"如果野生動物成為旅遊業的一大吸引力，本地酒店和導遊可能賺取更多收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major tourist attraction.","zh":"這個短語描述主要旅遊吸引點。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"contribute five times more than","meaning":"貢獻是……的五倍","examples":[{"en":"Tourism contributes five times more than the illegal wildlife trade to GDP.","zh":"旅遊業對本地生產總值的貢獻是非法野生動物貿易的五倍。"},{"en":"To contribute five times more than something means to add five times the amount that another thing adds.","zh":"contribute five times more than something 指貢獻量是另一事物的五倍。"},{"en":"One fundraiser may contribute five times more money than another if many more people support it.","zh":"如果更多人支持，一項籌款活動的貢獻可能是另一項的五倍。"},{"en":"If legal tourism contributes more than illegal trade, protecting wildlife can make economic sense.","zh":"如果合法旅遊業貢獻高於非法貿易，保護野生動物在經濟上也合理。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the size of two contributions.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種貢獻的大小。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"illegal wildlife trade","meaning":"非法野生動物貿易","examples":[{"en":"Tourism contributes more to GDP than the illegal wildlife trade.","zh":"旅遊業對本地生產總值的貢獻比非法野生動物貿易更多。"},{"en":"Illegal wildlife trade is the buying and selling of protected animals or animal parts against the law.","zh":"illegal wildlife trade 指違法買賣受保護動物或動物部位。"},{"en":"Selling ivory or rare animal skins can be part of illegal wildlife trade.","zh":"販賣象牙或稀有動物皮毛可以屬於非法野生動物貿易。"},{"en":"If illegal wildlife trade grows, endangered species may decline quickly.","zh":"如果非法野生動物貿易增長，瀕危物種可能迅速減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wildlife crime linked to money and markets.","zh":"這個短語描述與金錢和市場有關的野生動物罪案。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"GDP","meaning":"本地生產總值","examples":[{"en":"Tourism contributes significantly to GDP.","zh":"旅遊業對本地生產總值有重大貢獻。"},{"en":"GDP is the total value of goods and services produced by a country or region in a period.","zh":"GDP 指一個國家或地區在某段時間內生產的貨品和服務總值。"},{"en":"Economists use GDP to compare the size of different economies.","zh":"經濟學家使用本地生產總值比較不同經濟體的規模。"},{"en":"If tourism increases GDP, the government may invest more in visitor facilities.","zh":"如果旅遊業提高本地生產總值，政府可能投資更多遊客設施。"},{"en":"This term is used to measure economic output.","zh":"這個術語用來量度經濟產出。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"mainly because of","meaning":"主要因為……","examples":[{"en":"The rise in tourism is mainly because of the elephants.","zh":"旅遊業上升主要因為大象。"},{"en":"Mainly because of means mostly as a result of one reason.","zh":"mainly because of 指主要由於某一原因。"},{"en":"The café became popular mainly because of its friendly staff and cheap lunch sets.","zh":"那間咖啡店變得受歡迎，主要因為員工友善和午餐便宜。"},{"en":"If tourism rises mainly because of wildlife, protecting animals becomes economically important.","zh":"如果旅遊業主要因野生動物而上升，保護動物就變得有經濟重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main cause.","zh":"這個短語指出主要原因。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a dramatic rise in interest","meaning":"興趣大幅上升","examples":[{"en":"There has been a dramatic rise in interest in the elephant project.","zh":"人們對大象項目的興趣大幅上升。"},{"en":"A dramatic rise in interest means many more people have become interested in something, and the change is large and noticeable.","zh":"a dramatic rise in interest 指更多人對某事產生興趣，而且變化明顯而巨大。"},{"en":"A school may see a dramatic rise in interest in coding after students build useful apps.","zh":"學生製作有用應用程式後，學校可能看見學生對編程的興趣大幅上升。"},{"en":"If interest rises dramatically, more visitors, donations, or media attention may follow.","zh":"如果興趣大幅上升，可能會帶來更多訪客、捐款或媒體關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sharp increase in public attention.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾關注急劇增加。"}],"source":"IELTS Listening > Practice 9 > Task 4.pdf","sourcePage":12}]};
